  }
  // The morning after: the Moths have the Joke, the Warden has a clerk, and the Reader has a hat.
  Rule bd_ludd_resigns when bd_ludd_exposed(party) and not bd_ludd_gone(party) and hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 20 once
    says "By the second bell the Moths are doing the Joke at the door in the wings, with a pail for the door. Master Orlick comes in under the proscenium, hears himself said by a boy of nineteen, goes quite still, and then, with great dignity, lays his red pencils on the prompt-corner shelf in a row, takes the Crow's domino off its nail and puts it in his pocket. 'The Warden will want a letter,' he says, and goes out by the stage door. Nobody laughs after that. It is the worst silence the Wet Stage has ever kept." { Assert bd_ludd_gone(party). }

  // ── The leak in the flies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The poet cannot write because the page will not stay dry; the manager will say yes to a dry stage sooner than to a
  // good argument. Mended by hand (mending) or paid for (four coin to a rigger who drinks at the Weights quay).
  Action bd_patch_flies(actor: group, site: place) "Patch the leak in the flies with a lashed square of tarred sailcloth" {
    Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, stage_flies) and not bd_flies_dry().
    Resolve check(actor, mending, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bd_flies_mended_rel(stage_flies). Increase bd_orme_warm(actor) by 1. }
    Result "It takes an hour, a ladder and a good deal of bad language to the barge, which has heard worse. You cut the cloth to the seam, tar it, lash it, and stand back. The long grey thread stops. Under the deck, for the first time in nine winters, the flies are dry. Nobody tells Madame Orme. By morning she has moved a bucket.".
    Otherwise "You lash the cloth over the seam, and it holds until the first long gust, and then the barge settles a quarter-inch, and the thread of water comes back in a different place, as if it had been consulted.".
  }
  Action bd_patch_pay(actor: group, site: place) "Hire the rigger from the Weights quay to patch the leak in the flies, four coin" {
    Time 12.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, stage_flies) and not bd_flies_dry() and quantity(actor, gold) >= 4.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Assert bd_flies_mended_rel(stage_flies). Increase bd_orme_warm(actor) by 1. }
    Result "The rigger comes in two hours with a ladder and a bucket of tar, and does it in an hour with an air of having done it in every playhouse in the Delta. 'Leaks are cheap,' he says. 'It is the buckets people can't give up.' You pay him; he spits on the coin, which is, you gather, the quay's receipt. By morning Madame Orme has moved a bucket.".
  }

  // ── Pantaloon Tarrow ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Wet Stage's clown: thirty-eight years the man who gets hit. He teaches the craft of a joke to a player and the
  // fall to a bard; he wants, once more, to hear the house forget itself. He keeps everything in his hat.
  Relation bd_quist_beats(group). Relation bd_quist_happy(group). Relation bd_scraps_got(group). Relation bd_pratfall_given(group).
  Topic bd_quist_cold with bd_quist "Speak to him" when not masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "The old clown sees your face and, with enormous courtesy, falls down. He gets up. He does not look at you. It was not for you.".
  }
  Topic bd_quist_customer with bd_quist "Ask him what he does" when masked(actor) and not wears(actor, face_moth) and publicHours() {
    Says "'Falls,' says the old man, and lifts the paper nose to be heard. 'Pantaloon: the man who gets hit. The Codicil allows a Pantaloon three blows of the slapstick in any scene, no more, and the Reader counts them. There were years I would have taken twenty.' He considers the stairs. 'Three is a very fine number. It is the number of a joke.'".
  }
  Topic bd_quist_beats_topic with bd_quist "Ask him how a joke is made" when wears(actor, face_moth) and publicHours() and not bd_quist_beats(actor) once {
    Says "'Three beats,' says Tarrow. 'The set-up, which is true. The doubt, which is where the house leans in and the amateur runs on. And the knife.' He pulls the paper nose down over his own. 'Nobody laughs at the knife. They laugh at the doubt, once the knife is in. Don't rush the doubt, and don't lie in the set-up, because you can lie in the knife but not before it.' He thinks. 'A good lie is only a truth that has been given a better coat.'".
    On discuss { Assert bd_quist_beats(actor). Increase bd_craft(actor) by 1. }
  }
  Topic bd_quist_night with bd_quist "Sit with him in the green room, in the dark" when not masked(actor) and privateHours() and at(bd_quist, stage_green_room) once {
    Says "He has taken the nose off, and without it he is only an old man with a large face that has been told what to do for a very long time. 'Thirty-eight years,' he says. 'I fall, I get up, they clap. Since the Dark Year they clap. They do not laugh; they clap, like people at a funeral for somebody they didn't know. I should like.' He looks at the stove. 'I should like to hear the house forget itself once more, before I can't get up. Only once. I know the Walnut. I have the Walnut. I haven't a house.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bd_quist_name). }
  }
  Action bd_quist_audience(actor: group, site: place) "Be his house for an hour, in the dark, while he does the Walnut" {
    Speaker bd_quist. Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_quist, site) and not masked(actor) and privateHours() and knows(actor, bd_quist_name) and not bd_quist_happy(actor).
    On success { Assert bd_quist_happy(actor). Assert knows(actor, bd_stock_known). }
    Result "The Walnut is the oldest thing the Wet Stage does: a walnut, a table, and a man who will crack it. He tries his hand, his shoe, a mallet, the Warden's Key from the prop-box, a very small sermon. The walnut is not cracked. It is never cracked. In the end he sits on it. It is nothing. It is an old man and a nut in the dark; and at the end of it you are laughing so that you have to hold the bench, and he is standing on the boards in the one lamp with his large face gone quite still. 'There,' says Pantaloon Tarrow. 'I'd forgotten it did that.'".
  }
  Discovery bd_stock_known "Tarrow's Walnut, the oldest thing the Wet Stage does, is a joke about a man who will try everything but the obvious; a house will forget itself for it, and has not in twelve years." { Known by bd_quist. }
  Action bd_quist_lesson(actor: group, learner: member, site: place) "Have him teach {learner} to fall" {
    Speaker bd_quist. Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_quist, site) and memberOf(learner, actor) and awake(learner) and bd_quist_happy(actor) and not bd_pratfall_given(actor).
    Resolve endow(learner, dexterity, by_one).
    On success { Assert bd_pratfall_given(actor). }
    Result "He teaches you the one thing a clown knows that a warrior does not: that you do not fall down, you fall toward something. 'Go down as the blow comes. It lands on nothing, and you are up again behind it.' He shows you forty times. You learn it in about a dozen, and the bruises last a week.".
  }
  Topic bd_quist_scraps with bd_quist "Ask him about the paper in his hat" when knows(actor, bd_finch_block) and not bd_scraps_got(actor) once {
    Says "He takes off the hat, which is a Pantaloon's and has a lining like a magpie's nest, and tips it. 'He threw it in the bucket, a year ago, in forty pieces,' says Tarrow. 'In the middle of the night, with the water coming down. A clown is a man who is used to having things thrown at him. I fished them out.' He tips out a tangle of foolscap, damp and curling, covered in a fine hand. 'Don't give them back. Give him something to put them to.'".
    On discuss { Assert bd_scraps_got(actor). Give bd_scraps to actor. }
  }

  // ── Ambrose Finch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The elegy he wrote a year ago for the six hundred of the Cullet Reach, where his mother and his sister were, and
  // which the Reader struck (it named the Serene of that year, by implication, as the one who stood in the gallery and
  // said nothing). He tore it in forty pieces, and has not written since. He is moved by being read: his own first
  // stanza, put together from Tarrow's hat and given back to him; or left on his table, an hour, by someone who goes.
  // What he writes then is the bard's to choose the ending of: the Serene (which is cruelty), the girl who was Treasurer
  // (which is truth, and costs the dead), or the water (which is kind, and says nothing).
  Relation bd_scraps_fit(group). Relation bd_finch_moved(group). Relation bd_finch_alone(group). Relation bd_elegy_ended(group).
  Relation bd_elegy_serene(group). Relation bd_elegy_girl(group). Relation bd_elegy_water(group).
  Discovery bd_finch_block "Ambrose Finch has not written a line in a year, since the Reader struck the elegy he wrote for the six hundred of Cullet Reach, where his mother and sister drowned; he tore it into forty pieces and Tarrow kept them." { Known by bd_finch, bd_quist. }
  Topic bd_finch_cold with bd_finch "Speak to him" when not masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "Finch does not look round. 'Nobody here,' he says, mildly, to the ceiling, 'is at home.'".
  }
  Topic bd_finch_customer with bd_finch "Ask him what he is doing in the flies" when masked(actor) and not wears(actor, face_moth) and publicHours() {
    Says "'I am in residence,' says the thin man. 'By the bequest of the late Abelard Tenn, forty coin a year and a bed in the flies, that a poet may be in residence. It has been read to mean that I must be seen to be in it, between the Third Bell and the Ninth, on pain of forfeit; and so I am seen. By the buckets, mostly.' The half-mask smiles for him. 'It is a very fine poem, that bequest. It is the only one I have been able to finish.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bd_finch_name). }
  }
  Topic bd_finch_moth with bd_finch "Ask him what he is writing" when wears(actor, face_moth) and publicHours() and not knows(actor, bd_finch_block) {
    Says "'Nothing,' says Finch. 'I do not mean badly; I mean nothing. The page and I have not been introduced for a year.' He turns the white foolscap a quarter turn, as if it might look better from the side. 'Come at night, if you want a poet. By day I am only residence.'".
  }
  Topic bd_finch_reach with bd_finch "Ask him what happened a year ago" when not masked(actor) and privateHours() and not knows(actor, bd_finch_block) once {
    Says "'The Rain-Wives asked me for something for the thirtieth year of the Sluice. I wrote it in a month. It was the only thing I have written that was true.' He turns a page that has nothing on it. 'The Reader struck it under the second head. It named the Serene of that year, by implication, as the one who stood in the gallery in white and gold and said nothing. That is the only thing it says about anyone: that he said nothing.' He stops. 'My mother was at Cullet Reach. My sister. So I tore it into forty pieces, and found that there was no reason to write anything else.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bd_finch_block). }
  }
  Action bd_fit_scraps(actor: group, site: place) "Lay Tarrow's forty scraps out on the table and fit them together" {
    Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, stage_flies) and bd_scraps_got(actor) and not bd_scraps_fit(actor) and carries(actor, bd_scraps).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bd_scraps_fit(actor). Assert knows(actor, bd_stanza_known). }
    Result "You lay them out on the dry foolscap like a game. It is a matter of the grain of the paper and the lie of a hand, and of verse, which is a kind of grain too. At the end of the hour you have the first stanza whole: 'They said the water would be kind to us / for the first time, as to the others. / The lamps were lit in the low islands / and the mothers counted the lamps.' Nothing after. The rest is the part he would have to write.".
    Otherwise "The pieces will not agree. You get four lines that scan, and three that do not, and a word that appears to be his own name, and the foolscap curls.".
  }
  Discovery bd_stanza_known "The first stanza of Finch's elegy, pieced from the scraps: 'They said the water would be kind to us / for the first time, as to the others. / The lamps were lit in the low islands / and the mothers counted the lamps.'".
  Kind bd_scraps_kind "a tangle of damp foolscap" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "Forty scraps of foolscap, damp and curled, covered in a fine small hand: a year old and kept in a clown's hat.".
  Item bd_scraps "Finch's forty scraps" is bd_scraps_kind at offstage.
  Action bd_finch_read(actor: group, site: place) "Read him his own first stanza, aloud, in the dry flies" {
    Speaker bd_finch. Time 20 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_finch, site) and not masked(actor) and privateHours() and knows(actor, bd_stanza_known) and not bd_finch_moved(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bd_finch_moved(actor). }
    Result "You read it the way it was written, which is to say as if nothing were being asked of the listener, and the water coming down into the bucket keeps time. When you come to 'counted the lamps' Finch has his hand over his mouth. 'Who gave you that,' he says; and then, because he knows, 'Of course he did. He fishes. He fishes everything.' He takes the pen out of the bucket where it has lived for a year and looks at it, and wipes it on his sleeve. 'Go away,' he says, kindly. 'It's coming.'".
    Otherwise "You read it too well, which is to say as a performance, and he sits through it with his chin on his chest, politely, like a man at his own recital. 'Yes,' he says. 'That's it. That's what it was.' But it has been a performance, and he cannot write to a performance.".
  }
  // For a company that cannot read a hand: the scraps, laid out on a dry table, an hour left alone with them.
  Action bd_finch_scraps_leave(actor: group, site: place) "Lay Tarrow's scraps on his dry table, as they are, and leave him an hour with them" {
    Speaker bd_finch. Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_finch, site) and not masked(actor) and privateHours() and carries(actor, bd_scraps) and bd_flies_dry() and not bd_finch_moved(actor).
    On success { Assert bd_finch_moved(actor). Assert bd_finch_alone(actor). Spend bd_scraps from actor. }
    Result "You tip the forty pieces out on the dry foolscap in the lamplight, face up, unmatched, and sit down against the cot. He looks at them as at a dead animal, and does not touch. Then, with one finger, he turns a piece over, and another, and does not say anything. You wait. At the end of the hour he is on his knees at the table, fitting them like a man at a puzzle, with the pen in his teeth. He does not look up. You let yourself out by the ladder, and you hear him begin to read aloud, under his breath, a line at a time.".
  }
  Action bd_finch_leave(actor: group, site: place) "Pin the stanza over his table, leave the dry foolscap beside it, and go" {
    Speaker bd_finch. Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_finch, site) and not masked(actor) and privateHours() and knows(actor, bd_stanza_known) and bd_flies_dry() and not bd_finch_moved(actor).
    On success { Assert bd_finch_moved(actor). Assert bd_finch_alone(actor). }
    Result "You pin the first stanza over the table, and put the clean foolscap where the drip used to fall, and the pen by it. You sit with him for an hour, saying nothing, as he does not look at the page. At the end of the hour you stand, and go, and at the ladder you hear the pen go down on the paper like a foot on a stair. He does not say thank you. He is not thinking about you at all, which is the best that could have been done for him.".
  }
  Action bd_elegy_serene_end(actor: group, site: place) "Let the elegy end on the Serene who stood in the gallery and said nothing" {
    Speaker bd_finch. Time 20 minutes.
    Grave "It is a true line, and a cruel one. The man it names is alive.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_finch, site) and bd_finch_moved(actor) and not bd_elegy_ended(actor).
    On success { Assert bd_elegy_ended(actor). Assert bd_elegy_serene(actor). Assert knows(actor, bd_elegy_made). }
    Result "'It ends as it began,' says Finch. 'With a man who stood in a gallery.' He writes it down and reads it back, and you both hear that it is a good last line, and that there is a person at the end of it. It is the best poem he has ever written. It will hurt someone.".
  }
  Action bd_elegy_girl_end(actor: group, site: place) "Tell him who the Treasurer was, and let the elegy end on a girl of nineteen" {
    Speaker bd_finch. Time 20 minutes.
    Grave "It is the truth, and it is of a woman who is dead, and who spent thirty-one years paying for it. It cannot be unsaid.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_finch, site) and bd_finch_moved(actor) and not bd_elegy_ended(actor) and knows(actor, marrick_was_treasurer).
    On success { Assert bd_elegy_ended(actor). Assert bd_elegy_girl(actor). Assert knows(actor, bd_elegy_made). }
    Result "He listens with the pen not moving. 'A girl,' he says. 'A lamp-trimmer's daughter, nineteen, with a key she could not carry.' He puts his face in his hands, and takes it out again. 'It was the Urn. It was the lot. It was nobody's fault and everybody's, and I have been hating a man in a gallery for thirty years.' He writes. It is a different poem, much slower, and when he reads it back the last line is addressed to nobody at all, and is the most terrible thing you have heard in the flies.".
  }
  Action bd_elegy_water_end(actor: group, site: place) "Let the elegy end on the water, and name no one" {
    Speaker bd_finch. Time 20 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_finch, site) and bd_finch_moved(actor) and not bd_elegy_ended(actor).
    On success { Assert bd_elegy_ended(actor). Assert bd_elegy_water(actor). Assert knows(actor, bd_elegy_made). }
    Result "'The water,' says Finch. 'Only the water. It would not be a lie, exactly. It would be an elegy for weather.' He writes it, and the last stanza lets the six hundred go, one lamp at a time, without blame and without explaining anything, and it is very beautiful, and it excuses everybody. 'I shall not be able to read it to anyone who knew,' he says. 'But it will make them cry in the right place.'".
  }
  Discovery bd_elegy_made "Finch has written the elegy of Cullet Reach, and is willing to see it played.".
  Topic bd_finch_candid with bd_finch "Ask him what the Candid's Reading-room is saying" when bd_finch_moved(actor) and not knows(actor, bd_candid_known) once {
    Says "'They push the tracts under the flies door, between the Third Bell and the Ninth. It is the only post I get.' He reads one aloud with great gravity. '“A Citizen has the right to know whose hand is on the lock. A Citizen who is not told is a Subject; a Subject who is told is a Citizen. Therefore all Subjects must be told. Therefore the hand on the lock of the Reading-room, which is the Candid's own, is a hand to be told of. It is not told. The door is locked, for the safety of the truth.”' He lowers the tract. 'It is the best satire in the Delta, and she does not know she has written it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bd_candid_known). }
  }
  Discovery bd_candid_known "The Candid's tracts demand that every hand on every lock be told, and are pushed under the door of the Wet Stage's flies; the door of the Candid's own Reading-room is locked, for the safety of the truth." { Known by bd_finch. }

  // ── Tobiah Venable ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The mimic who can do the Warden's walk, and has not done the Assessor's in twelve years. His father took the blame
  // for a line that was not his; whether he is told is the bard's.
  Relation bd_cast_moths(group). Relation bd_crake_knows(group). Relation bd_echo_given(group).
  Topic bd_crake_cold with bd_crake "Speak to him" when not masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "Venable's walk takes him in a wide curve round the place where you stand, as round a puddle.".
  }
  Topic bd_crake_customer with bd_crake "Ask him to do the Warden's walk" when masked(actor) and not wears(actor, face_moth) and publicHours() {
    Says "'The Office,' says Venable, 'not the man. There is a difference of about eleven degrees at the left hip, and the Codicil rests on it.' He does the Office, a gait of such general and spacious proprietorship that three people in the pit look at their pockets. 'See? Nobody.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bd_crake_name). }
  }
  Topic bd_crake_father with bd_crake "Ask him why he does the Warden's walk and not the Assessor's" when wears(actor, face_moth) and publicHours() and not knows(actor, bd_crake_dad) once {
    Says "'My father did the Assessor.' Venable says it to the boards. 'He did him in the farce that shut us, and he did the walk, and a woman in the third row said the man's name, and that was the Dark Year, and my father went to the Drip and did not come back from it.' He lets the walk go out of him. 'He said it was his walk. He said it so often I believe it. I have never done an Assessor since. I do the Warden's, because the Warden does not walk like anybody I love.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bd_crake_dad). }
  }
  Discovery bd_crake_dad "Venable's father played the Assessor in the farce that shut the Wet Stage, said it was his walk that did it, and died in the Drip; Venable has never done an Assessor since." { Known by bd_crake, orme. }
  Action bd_tell_crake(actor: group, site: place) "Tell him whose line it was that named the Assessor" {
    Speaker bd_crake. Time 20 minutes.
    Grave "It cannot be untold. It may cost Madame Orme her house, or her Moth, or both.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_crake, site) and publicHours() and knows(actor, bd_line_known) and knows(actor, bd_crake_dad) and not bd_crake_knows(actor).
    On success { Assert bd_crake_knows(actor). }
    Result "He listens with his big hands hanging, and when you have finished he does not say anything for so long that the drip in the aisle counts it. 'A line,' says Venable. 'Hers. In the wings.' He turns his head, slowly, towards the green-room door. 'He knew,' he says. 'That is the thing. He knew, and he said it was the walk, and he let me think it, so that I should not have to hate her, because there was nowhere else for us to be.' He stands very still. 'Don't tell me she's sorry. I should rather not be told.'".
  }
  Action bd_cast_moths_free(actor: group, site: place) "Ask him if the Moths will carry the Lampoon, on the manager's word" {
    Speaker bd_crake. Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_crake, site) and publicHours() and bd_commissioned(actor) and not bd_cast_moths(actor) and bd_open().
    On success { Assert bd_cast_moths(actor). Increase bd_craft(actor) by 1. }
    Result "'Her word?' says Venable. 'Then it is a play. Then it is mine to be frightened about, not hers.' He claps his hands once, and in the wings twelve Moths straighten, as flowers do when the water comes.".
  }
  Action bd_cast_moths_ask(actor: group, site: place) "Ask him if the Moths will carry a satire, without Madame Orme's word" {
    Speaker bd_crake. Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_crake, site) and publicHours() and not bd_commissioned(actor) and not bd_cast_moths(actor) and bd_open() and bd_admitted(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bd_cast_moths(actor). Increase bd_craft(actor) by 1. }
    Result "'Without her?' says Venable. He looks at the wings, where the Moths are pretending not to listen. 'The Dark Year,' he says. 'You know what you are asking.' And then, because they have been waiting twelve years to be asked: 'We carry it. On our own heads. It is a thing we owe a house.'".
    Otherwise "'Not without her,' says Venable. 'Not after the last time. Bring me her word and I will bring you the Moths.' He is polite about it, and so are the Moths, who are not looking at you.".
  }
  // What the Moths know that the Codicil does not license: a likeness made of lamp, sheet and lamp-black, in the air
  // above the boards. Given to the company that made them laugh, once, at a Warden. (The shared catalog's reward
  // spells are too few to teach it as a spell: friction, see the note.)
  Kind bd_likeness_kind "the Moths' likeness-kit" is gear worth 0 weighing 1 granting deception described "A pot of lamp-black, a sheet gone grey with use and a dark-lantern with a tin hood cut to a shape: all that is wanted to stand a man in the air above the boards who is not there. Whoever carries it learns to wear someone else's bearing for as long as a lie requires, and not a moment longer.".
  Item bd_likeness "the Moths' likeness-kit" is bd_likeness_kind at offstage.
  Action bd_echo_lesson(actor: group, site: place) "Ask him for the Moths' likeness-kit, and the trick of it" {
    Speaker bd_crake. Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_crake, site) and bd_farce_great(actor) and not bd_echo_given(actor).
    On success { Assert bd_echo_given(actor). Give bd_likeness to actor. }
    Result "'It is a thing I do and cannot teach,' says Venable, and teaches it, in an hour, with a lamp, a sheet and a pot of black. You do not mimic; you make the air stand up in a shape, and hold it there while somebody looks. 'That is the Warden's walk,' he says, at the end, as the sheet sways between you with nobody in it. 'It is also how you win an argument. I would use it sparingly. It is unkind.' He gives you the kit, which was his father's.".
  }

  // ── The Lampoon: what it is made of ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The bard composes from the city's small stories. Each tale the company has learned may be set down on a leaf of the
  // prompt-book (five leaves, no more) and brings a measure of laughter, of grief and of anger. What the Lampoon is
  // *for* is decided leaf by leaf: a tale may be sharpened with a line that cannot be proved (more laughter, and a lie),
  // softened (less anger, more grief, and someone is let off), or used with or without its keeper's leave. Then a target
  // is chosen, and a form, and a cast, and the Moths rehearse it, and it is played: on the Wet Stage in the last three
  // nights of the season if the house is open, or at the Drawing, to the Hall.
  Kind bd_tale. Kind bd_mark. Kind bd_shape.
  Entity bd_t_tax: bd_tale "the Warden's Lock-tax".
  Entity bd_t_unfaced: bd_tale "the Warden's call on the dying Registrar".
  Entity bd_t_pound: bd_tale "the Short Pound".
  Entity bd_t_ferry: bd_tale "Rill's boat, sinking by inches".
  Entity bd_t_sluice: bd_tale "the year of the Sluice".
  Entity bd_t_girl: bd_tale "the girl who was drawn Treasurer".
  Entity bd_t_lovers: bd_tale "the Heron and the Lamp".
  Entity bd_t_dusting: bd_tale "the retainer dusting for no one".
  Entity bd_t_stair: bd_tale "the stair nobody has used in three hundred years".
  Entity bd_t_tally: bd_tale "the Rain-Wives' tally".
  Entity bd_t_hollow: bd_tale "the empty Urn".
  Entity bd_t_cuts: bd_tale "the Reader's chest of cut jokes".
  Entity bd_t_cutscene: bd_tale "the Reader and the Joke at his door".
  Entity bd_t_stock: bd_tale "Tarrow's Walnut".
  Entity bd_t_candid: bd_tale "the Candid's tracts".
  Entity bd_t_dark: bd_tale "the Dark Year of the Wet Stage".
  Entity bd_t_elegy_s: bd_tale "Finch's elegy of Cullet Reach, ending on the Serene".
  Entity bd_t_elegy_g: bd_tale "Finch's elegy of Cullet Reach, ending on the girl".
  Entity bd_t_elegy_w: bd_tale "Finch's elegy of Cullet Reach, ending on the water".
  Entity bd_m_lacke: bd_mark "the Warden of Locks".
  Entity bd_m_candid: bd_mark "the Candid".
  Entity bd_m_contessa: bd_mark "the Contessa and the Old Names".
  Entity bd_m_urn: bd_mark "the Urn".
  Entity bd_f_farce: bd_shape "a farce".
  Entity bd_f_elegy: bd_shape "an elegy".
  Entity bd_f_ballad: bd_shape "a ballad".

  // What each tale is worth: laughter, grief, anger.
  Measure bd_funny(bd_tale). Measure bd_grief(bd_tale). Measure bd_anger(bd_tale).
  Initially Set bd_funny(bd_t_tax) to 2. Initially Set bd_anger(bd_t_tax) to 2.
  Initially Set bd_grief(bd_t_unfaced) to 2. Initially Set bd_anger(bd_t_unfaced) to 2.
  Initially Set bd_funny(bd_t_pound) to 3. Initially Set bd_anger(bd_t_pound) to 1.
  Initially Set bd_funny(bd_t_ferry) to 1. Initially Set bd_grief(bd_t_ferry) to 2.
  Initially Set bd_grief(bd_t_sluice) to 3. Initially Set bd_anger(bd_t_sluice) to 2.
  Initially Set bd_grief(bd_t_girl) to 2. Initially Set bd_anger(bd_t_girl) to 1.
  Initially Set bd_funny(bd_t_lovers) to 2. Initially Set bd_grief(bd_t_lovers) to 1.
  Initially Set bd_funny(bd_t_dusting) to 1. Initially Set bd_grief(bd_t_dusting) to 3.
  Initially Set bd_funny(bd_t_stair) to 2. Initially Set bd_anger(bd_t_stair) to 1.
  Initially Set bd_funny(bd_t_tally) to 2. Initially Set bd_anger(bd_t_tally) to 1.
  Initially Set bd_funny(bd_t_hollow) to 3. Initially Set bd_grief(bd_t_hollow) to 1. Initially Set bd_anger(bd_t_hollow) to 3.
  Initially Set bd_funny(bd_t_cuts) to 3.
  Initially Set bd_funny(bd_t_cutscene) to 2. Initially Set bd_grief(bd_t_cutscene) to 2.
  Initially Set bd_funny(bd_t_stock) to 2.
  Initially Set bd_funny(bd_t_candid) to 3.
  Initially Set bd_grief(bd_t_dark) to 2. Initially Set bd_anger(bd_t_dark) to 1.
  Initially Set bd_grief(bd_t_elegy_s) to 2. Initially Set bd_anger(bd_t_elegy_s) to 3.
  Initially Set bd_grief(bd_t_elegy_g) to 3. Initially Set bd_anger(bd_t_elegy_g) to 1.
  Initially Set bd_grief(bd_t_elegy_w) to 3.

  // The tales the company has learned, from the city's own facts and rounds and from the Stage's people.
  Relation bd_has(bd_tale). Relation bd_set(bd_tale). Relation bd_sharp(bd_tale). Relation bd_soft(bd_tale). Relation bd_leave(bd_tale).
  Rule bd_has_tax when knows(party, lacke_taxed) and not bd_has(bd_t_tax) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_tax). }
  Rule bd_has_unfaced when knows(party, lacke_unfaced) and not bd_has(bd_t_unfaced) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_unfaced). }
  Rule bd_has_pound when roundDone(party, r_pound) and not bd_has(bd_t_pound) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_pound). }
  Rule bd_has_ferry when roundDone(party, r_ferry) and not bd_has(bd_t_ferry) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_ferry). }
  Rule bd_has_sluice when knows(party, sluice_known) and not bd_has(bd_t_sluice) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_sluice). }
  Rule bd_has_girl when knows(party, marrick_was_treasurer) and not bd_has(bd_t_girl) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_girl). }
  Rule bd_has_lovers when loversMet(party) and not bd_has(bd_t_lovers) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_lovers). }
  Rule bd_has_dusting when roundDone(party, r_gaspar) and not bd_has(bd_t_dusting) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_dusting). }
  Rule bd_has_stair when knows(party, private_stair_known) and not bd_has(bd_t_stair) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_stair). }
  Rule bd_has_tally when knows(party, lie_tally) and not bd_has(bd_t_tally) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_tally). }
  Rule bd_has_hollow when knows(party, urn_hollow) and not bd_has(bd_t_hollow) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_hollow). }
  Rule bd_has_cuts when knows(party, bd_cuts_known) and not bd_has(bd_t_cuts) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_cuts). }
  Rule bd_has_cutscene when knows(party, bd_ludd_scene) and not bd_has(bd_t_cutscene) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_cutscene). }
  Rule bd_has_stock when knows(party, bd_stock_known) and not bd_has(bd_t_stock) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_stock). }
  Rule bd_has_candid when knows(party, bd_candid_known) and not bd_has(bd_t_candid) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_candid). }
  Rule bd_has_dark when knows(party, bd_dark_year) and not bd_has(bd_t_dark) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_dark). }
  Rule bd_has_elegy_s when bd_elegy_serene(party) and not bd_has(bd_t_elegy_s) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_elegy_s). }
  Rule bd_has_elegy_g when bd_elegy_girl(party) and not bd_has(bd_t_elegy_g) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_elegy_g). }
  Rule bd_has_elegy_w when bd_elegy_water(party) and not bd_has(bd_t_elegy_w) { Assert bd_has(bd_t_elegy_w). }

  // Which targets a Lampoon can be aimed at: one must have something set down about it.
  Relation bd_apt(bd_mark).
  Rule bd_apt_lacke when (bd_set(bd_t_tax) or bd_set(bd_t_unfaced)) and not bd_apt(bd_m_lacke) { Assert bd_apt(bd_m_lacke). }
  Rule bd_apt_candid when bd_set(bd_t_candid) and not bd_apt(bd_m_candid) { Assert bd_apt(bd_m_candid). }
  Rule bd_apt_contessa when (bd_set(bd_t_dusting) or bd_set(bd_t_stair)) and not bd_apt(bd_m_contessa) { Assert bd_apt(bd_m_contessa). }
  Rule bd_apt_urn when (bd_set(bd_t_sluice) or bd_set(bd_t_hollow) or bd_set(bd_t_tally) or bd_set(bd_t_girl) or bd_set(bd_t_elegy_s) or bd_set(bd_t_elegy_g) or bd_set(bd_t_elegy_w)) and not bd_apt(bd_m_urn) { Assert bd_apt(bd_m_urn). }

  // The prompt-book itself: Madame Orme's black oilcloth one, or (if she is not asked) a blank quarto from Finch.
  Kind bd_book_kind "the Wet Stage's prompt-book" is gear worth 0 weighing 1 described "A prompt-book bound in black oilcloth gone green at the corners, with a blue tape. The pages are ruled in two columns; the left is for the play. The right is the margin, and the margin is full, in a very small hand, of other people's jokes.".
  Item bd_prompt_book "the prompt-book" is bd_book_kind at offstage.
  Relation bd_desk(place).
  Initially Assert bd_desk(stage_green_room). Initially Assert bd_desk(bd_prompt). Initially Assert bd_desk(stage_flies).
  Measure bd_jest(group). Measure bd_sorrow(group). Measure bd_ire(group). Measure bd_craft(group). Measure bd_lies(group). Measure bd_leaves(group). Measure bd_rehearsed(group).
  Topic bd_finch_book with bd_finch "Ask him if he has a book you could write in" when not masked(actor) and privateHours() and not carries(actor, bd_prompt_book) and not bd_commissioned(actor) and not bd_book_given(actor) once {
    Says "'A book.' He looks at the white foolscap and then at you. 'I have a quarto. It was bound for the elegy; I had it done at the Weights quay by a man who could not read. It is quite empty. I do not think it minds.' He gives it you out of the bottom of the table, with its blue tape still on. 'Don't put anything in it that you could not stand to see struck. Orlick strikes the true ones first.'".
    On discuss { Assert bd_book_given(actor). Give bd_prompt_book to actor. }
  }
  Relation bd_book_given(group).

  Action bd_set_down(actor: group, tale: bd_tale, site: place) "Set down {tale} in the prompt-book" {
    Time 20 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and bd_desk(site) and carries(actor, bd_prompt_book) and bd_has(tale) and not bd_set(tale) and bd_leaves(actor) < 5.
    On success { Assert bd_set(tale). Increase bd_leaves(actor) by 1. Increase bd_jest(actor) by bd_funny(tale). Increase bd_sorrow(actor) by bd_grief(tale). Increase bd_ire(actor) by bd_anger(tale). }
    Result "You turn to a clean leaf and set it down: the beats, the turn, the line at which a house will lean in. It is not a thing yet, only a shape in the left-hand column. In the margin, in somebody else's very small hand, there is already a note about how it might be cut.".
  }
  Action bd_sharpen(actor: group, tale: bd_tale, site: place) "Sharpen {tale} with a line you cannot prove" {
    Time 10 minutes.
    Grave "The line will get the laugh. It will not be true. A thing said on a stage about a person who is not there is believed.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and bd_desk(site) and carries(actor, bd_prompt_book) and bd_set(tale) and not bd_sharp(tale) and not bd_soft(tale).
    On success { Assert bd_sharp(tale). Increase bd_jest(actor) by 2. Increase bd_lies(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You write the line. It is a good line. It is the kind of thing that would have been true if the world had had a little more taste. You read it back in your head in three voices and it gets a laugh in each, and you leave it in, and do not look at it again.".
  }
  Action bd_soften(actor: group, tale: bd_tale, site: place) "Leave out of {tale} the person it would hurt" {
    Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and bd_desk(site) and carries(actor, bd_prompt_book) and bd_set(tale) and not bd_sharp(tale) and not bd_soft(tale) and bd_anger(tale) >= 1.
    On success { Assert bd_soft(tale). Decrease bd_ire(actor) by 1 or to nothing. Increase bd_sorrow(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You strike the name, and then the shape of the name, and then the pause after where the name would have gone. It is a gentler thing. It is also, you notice, a little more sad, as a room is when someone has stopped being angry in it.".
  }
  Observe bd_book_empty at stage_green_room when carries(party, bd_prompt_book) and bd_leaves(party) == 0 "The prompt-book lies open on your knee at a clean leaf. A year of other men's margins looks over its edge.".
  Observe bd_book_jest at stage_green_room when carries(party, bd_prompt_book) and bd_leaves(party) >= 2 and bd_jest(party) > bd_sorrow(party) + bd_ire(party) "The prompt-book, as it stands, is a funny one. It is all turns and doors; you can hear where the house would go off.".
  Observe bd_book_grief at stage_green_room when carries(party, bd_prompt_book) and bd_leaves(party) >= 2 and bd_sorrow(party) > bd_jest(party) and bd_sorrow(party) >= bd_ire(party) "The prompt-book, as it stands, is a quiet one. It wants a very still house, and a single lamp.".
  Observe bd_book_ire at stage_green_room when carries(party, bd_prompt_book) and bd_leaves(party) >= 2 and bd_ire(party) > bd_sorrow(party) and bd_ire(party) >= bd_jest(party) "The prompt-book, as it stands, is an angry one. It is going to want a tune.".
  Observe bd_book_full at stage_green_room when carries(party, bd_prompt_book) and bd_leaves(party) >= 5 "Every leaf is written. A sixth thing could go in only by putting a fifth out, and a play is a poor sort of thing that has not already left something out.".

  // The keepers of a tale: a thing used with leave is a thing lent; used without, a thing taken.
  Action bd_leave_peck(actor: group, site: place) "Ask him for leave to sing the year of the Sluice" {
    Speaker peck. Time 20 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(peck, site) and bd_has(bd_t_sluice) and not bd_leave(bd_t_sluice).
    On success { Assert bd_leave(bd_t_sluice). }
    Result "Absalom Peck is a long time answering, and when he does it is to the cup in his hands. 'Sing it,' he says. 'I have been the only verse of it for thirty years, and I never cared for the tune.' He looks up. 'Sing it so they know the water had a name too. I should be obliged to be a verse in the right company.'".
  }
  Action bd_leave_rill(actor: group, site: place) "Ask her if her boat may go into the Lampoon" {
    Speaker rill. Time 20 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(rill, site) and bd_has(bd_t_ferry) and not bd_leave(bd_t_ferry).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bd_leave(bd_t_ferry). }
    Result "'My boat,' says Rill Ketch, and looks along the gunwale she has been bailing for nine years. 'In a play.' She thinks it over like a woman pricing a fare. 'Put her in. She has been in worse company. But she is not to be funnier than she is, and she is not to sink. I will not have her drowned for a laugh.'".
    Otherwise "'No,' says Rill. 'She is not a story. She is a boat.' She puts her back to you and the bailing-can goes down, over and over, as a drum would.".
  }

  // ── What the Lampoon is for: target, form and cast ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation bd_target(group, bd_mark) exclusive. Relation bd_form(group, bd_shape) exclusive. Relation bd_aimed(group). Relation bd_shaped(group).
  Action bd_aim(actor: group, mark: bd_mark, site: place) "Aim the Lampoon at {mark}" {
    Time 10 minutes.
    Grave "Once the Moths have blocked it, it is aimed. You cannot turn a play on a new man in the wings.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and bd_desk(site) and carries(actor, bd_prompt_book) and bd_apt(mark) and not bd_aimed(actor).
    On success { Assert bd_target(actor, mark). Assert bd_aimed(actor). }
    Result "You write the name at the head of the first leaf, and under it, in the margin, an old hand has already written Under the first head.".
  }
  Action bd_shape(actor: group, form: bd_shape, site: place) "Cast the Lampoon as {form}" {
    Time 10 minutes.
    Grave "A farce cannot be turned into an elegy in the wings. It is the form you will rehearse, and the form the house will hear.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and bd_desk(site) and carries(actor, bd_prompt_book) and bd_aimed(actor) and not bd_shaped(actor).
    On success { Assert bd_form(actor, form). Assert bd_shaped(actor). }
    Result "You write the form at the head of the page and it is, at once, a little more like a play and a little less like what you meant. Forms do that.".
  }
  Relation bd_cast_orme(group). Relation bd_cast_quist(group). Relation bd_cast_self(group).
  Action bd_cast_orme_act(actor: group, site: place) "Ask her to play the principal part" {
    Speaker orme. Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(orme, site) and bd_orme_plays(actor) and not bd_cast_orme(actor) and bd_open().
    On success { Assert bd_cast_orme(actor). Increase bd_craft(actor) by 2. }
    Result "'The pearls come off,' says Madame Orme. 'The mask stays on. I shall be a woman in a half-mask, and a half-mask is a thing nobody has ever been able to name.' She holds out her hand for the book. 'I shall want my own cue. I shall want a pail.'".
  }
  Action bd_cast_quist_act(actor: group, site: place) "Ask him to play the Pantaloon" {
    Speaker bd_quist. Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_quist, site) and bd_quist_happy(actor) and not bd_cast_quist(actor).
    On success { Assert bd_cast_quist(actor). Increase bd_craft(actor) by 1. }
    Result "'Three blows,' says Tarrow, 'no more,' and puts the paper nose down over his own, which is the answer.".
  }
  Action bd_cast_self_act(actor: group, site: place) "Take the principal part yourself" {
    Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and bd_desk(site) and carries(actor, bd_prompt_book) and not bd_cast_self(actor).
    On success { Assert bd_cast_self(actor). Increase bd_craft(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You write your own name against the principal part, in pencil, which is how players have always done it, so that it may be crossed out.".
  }
  Query bd_cast_any() means bd_cast_moths(party) or bd_cast_orme(party) or bd_cast_quist(party) or bd_cast_self(party).

  // ── The Reader's pencil, and rehearsal ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A Lampoon goes past the Reader whole, or it is cut. A Reader who is the company's friend, or its fool, or in its
  // pocket, or gone, does not cut it; one who is none of these takes two off its craft; and one who is passed the sides
  // under another name does not know what he has passed.
  Relation bd_passed(group). Relation bd_freed_paid(group). Relation bd_g_trust(group). Relation bd_g_read(group). Relation bd_g_gone(group).
  Query bd_freed() means bd_ludd_trusts(party) or bd_written_in(party) or bd_ludd_leashed(party) or bd_ludd_gone(party) or bd_passed(party).
  Rule bd_free_gain when bd_freed() and not bd_freed_paid(party) { Increase bd_craft(party) by 2. Assert bd_freed_paid(party). }
  Rule bd_trust_gain when bd_ludd_trusts(party) and not bd_g_trust(party) { Increase bd_craft(party) by 1. Assert bd_g_trust(party). }
  Rule bd_read_gain when bd_written_in(party) and not bd_g_read(party) { Increase bd_craft(party) by 2. Assert bd_g_read(party). }
  Rule bd_gone_gain when bd_ludd_gone(party) and not bd_g_gone(party) { Increase bd_craft(party) by 1. Assert bd_g_gone(party). }
  Relation bd_reh_a(group). Relation bd_reh_b(group). Relation bd_reh_c(group).
  Action bd_reh_block(actor: group, site: place) "Block the Lampoon on the boards with Venable and the Moths" {
    Speaker bd_crake. Time 12.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_crake, site) and bd_shaped(actor) and bd_cast_moths(actor) and not bd_reh_a(actor) and publicHours() and bd_open().
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bd_reh_a(actor). Increase bd_rehearsed(actor) by 1. Increase bd_craft(actor) by 1. }
    Result "Two hours with twelve Moths, a chair for the Warden's box and a mop for the Urn. You block the entrances so that nobody falls over anybody, you find the one turn in the second scene where the house will want to breathe, and when the Moths have gone to their dinner it is, for the first time, a thing that can be played.".
    Otherwise "Two hours, and the chase runs into the chair, and the Moths are patient with you in the way of people who have watched a lot of directors. It will do; it will not do well.".
  }
  Action bd_reh_form(actor: group, site: place) "Put the Lampoon in the old form with him, as the Codicil licenses it" {
    Speaker bd_quist. Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bd_quist, site) and bd_shaped(actor) and not bd_reh_b(actor) and publicHours() and bd_open().
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bd_reh_b(actor). Increase bd_rehearsed(actor) by 1. Increase bd_craft(actor) by 1. }
    Result "The Codicil licenses three forms and says what each one must have: the farce its Five Turns, the elegy its Three Silences, the ballad its Burden at every fourth verse. Tarrow knows them as a man knows his own stairs. You lay the Lampoon on the old frame, and where it was loose it tightens, and where it was clever it is made to wait.".
    Otherwise "You have the forms wrong in a way Tarrow is too polite to correct, and the Lampoon comes out on the frame like a coat on the wrong peg.".
  }
  Action bd_reh_cut(actor: group, site: place) "Hand him the Lampoon's sides under the name of Master Dibble" {
    Speaker ludd. Time 20 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ludd, site) and bd_shaped(actor) and masked(actor) and publicHours() and not bd_reh_c(actor) and not bd_freed() and not wears(actor, face_moth).
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert bd_reh_c(actor). Assert bd_passed(actor). Increase bd_rehearsed(actor) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert bd_reh_c(actor). Assert bd_ludd_sour(actor). }
    Result "You hand him the sides with the title page turned: THE WEIGHTS AND MEASURES OF MASTER DIBBLE, a second act. He reads it as he reads everything, with his mouth a little open. He cuts a comma. He cuts a second comma. He gives it back with the Reader's oval on it and a note in the margin: Rather better than the first. Do not let them improvise.".
    Otherwise "He reads the first leaf, and the second, and looks at you with great sadness. 'Master Dibble,' he says, 'has never in his life been a man who might be known by his hip.' He strikes it, whole, in three long red strokes. It will not be possible to unstrike it. It will have to be done from memory.".
  }

  // ── The Lampoon: ready, played, received ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Ready when three leaves are written, aimed and cast, and rehearsed once. Played once on the Wet Stage on the last
  // three nights of the season (days six to eight, between the sixth bell and the eighth) if the house is open, or at
  // the Drawing, in the Hall, before the Urn: and a Lampoon that flopped on the Stage may be played again at the Drawing.
  // The house takes it by what it is (a farce, an elegy, a ballad), what it is aimed at, and how well it was made.
  Relation bd_lampoon_ready(group). Relation bd_played(group). Relation bd_reacted(group). Relation bd_flopped(group). Relation bd_venue_told(group).
  Relation bd_great_night(group). Relation bd_farce_great(group). Relation bd_drip_sings(group). Relation bd_flagged(group). Relation bd_morning_told(group).
  Measure bd_venue(group). Measure bd_mood(group). Measure bd_when(group).
  Rule bd_ready when bd_leaves(party) >= 3 and bd_aimed(party) and bd_shaped(party) and bd_cast_any() and bd_rehearsed(party) >= 1 and not bd_lampoon_ready(party)
    says "It is a play now. Not a good one yet, or a bad one, but a thing with a first scene and a last, in somebody's hand, with a cast who know their entrances and a Reader who has not yet been asked. It could be put on a stage tomorrow, or in the Hall of the Urn on the ninth night. Nothing is left to settle except how, and nothing has ever been settled until the lamps go down." {
    Assert bd_lampoon_ready(party). Assert handReady(party, hand_lampoon). Assert arcBegun(party, hand_lampoon). }
  Query bd_stage_night() means day(clock) >= 6 and day(clock) <= 8 and hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 20.
  Query bd_fair() means (bd_form(party, bd_f_farce) and bd_jest(party) + bd_craft(party) >= 14) or (bd_form(party, bd_f_elegy) and bd_sorrow(party) + bd_craft(party) >= 13)
    or (bd_form(party, bd_f_ballad) and bd_ire(party) + bd_sorrow(party) + bd_craft(party) >= 18).
  Query bd_great() means (bd_form(party, bd_f_farce) and bd_jest(party) + bd_craft(party) >= 20) or (bd_form(party, bd_f_elegy) and bd_sorrow(party) + bd_craft(party) >= 19)
    or (bd_form(party, bd_f_ballad) and bd_ire(party) + bd_sorrow(party) + bd_craft(party) >= 24).

  Action bd_play_stage(actor: group, site: place) "Go on: play the Lampoon to the house" {
    Time 6.
    Grave "It is played once on this stage. Whatever the house makes of it, it has made of it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, bd_stage) and bd_lampoon_ready(actor) and not bd_played(actor) and bd_open() and bd_stage_night() and not bd_cast_self(actor).
    On success { Assert bd_played(actor). Set bd_venue(actor) to 1. Set bd_when(actor) to watch(clock). }
    Result "The lamps go down, a lamp at a time, and the Moths go on.".
  }
  Action bd_play_stage_self(actor: group, site: place) "Go on yourself, in the principal part, and play the Lampoon to the house" {
    Time 6.
    Grave "It is played once on this stage. Whatever the house makes of it, it has made of it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, bd_stage) and bd_lampoon_ready(actor) and not bd_played(actor) and bd_open() and bd_stage_night() and bd_cast_self(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bd_played(actor). Set bd_venue(actor) to 1. Set bd_when(actor) to watch(clock). Increase bd_craft(actor) by 2. Assert bd_nerve_good(actor). }
    On failure { Assert bd_played(actor). Set bd_venue(actor) to 1. Set bd_when(actor) to watch(clock). Decrease bd_craft(actor) by 2 or to nothing. Assert bd_nerve_bad(actor). }
    Result "You tie the half-mask on, and the lamps go down.".
    Otherwise "You tie the half-mask on, and the lamps go down.".
  }
  Action bd_play_hall(actor: group, site: place) "Play the Lampoon to the Hall, before the Urn" {
    Time 6.
    Grave "The Hall is the whole city, and it will not be asked twice.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and bd_lampoon_ready(actor) and (not bd_played(actor) or bd_flopped(actor)) and not bd_cast_self(actor).
    On success { Assert bd_played(actor). Set bd_venue(actor) to 2. Set bd_when(actor) to watch(clock). Retract bd_reacted(actor). Retract bd_flopped(actor). Retract bd_venue_told(actor). Assert handPlayed(party, hand_lampoon). Increase heat(actor) by 1. }
    Result "A Moth sets a lantern on the floor in front of the bronze jar, and the Hall, which was talking, finds that it has stopped.".
  }
  Action bd_play_hall_self(actor: group, site: place) "Go on yourself before the Urn, and play the Lampoon to the Hall" {
    Time 6.
    Grave "The Hall is the whole city, and it will not be asked twice.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and bd_lampoon_ready(actor) and (not bd_played(actor) or bd_flopped(actor)) and bd_cast_self(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert bd_played(actor). Set bd_venue(actor) to 2. Set bd_when(actor) to watch(clock). Retract bd_reacted(actor). Retract bd_flopped(actor). Retract bd_venue_told(actor). Retract bd_nerve_told(actor). Retract bd_nerve_bad(actor).
      Assert handPlayed(party, hand_lampoon). Increase heat(actor) by 1. Increase bd_craft(actor) by 2. Assert bd_nerve_good(actor). }
    On failure { Assert bd_played(actor). Set bd_venue(actor) to 2. Set bd_when(actor) to watch(clock). Retract bd_reacted(actor). Retract bd_flopped(actor). Retract bd_venue_told(actor). Retract bd_nerve_told(actor). Retract bd_nerve_good(actor).
      Assert handPlayed(party, hand_lampoon). Increase heat(actor) by 1. Decrease bd_craft(actor) by 2 or to nothing. Assert bd_nerve_bad(actor). }
    Result "You step into the chalk line with the Hall at your back and the jar at your front, and the lantern is set down at your feet.".
    Otherwise "You step into the chalk line with the Hall at your back and the jar at your front, and the lantern is set down at your feet.".
  }
  Relation bd_nerve_good(group). Relation bd_nerve_bad(group). Relation bd_nerve_told(group).

  Rule bd_venue_stage when bd_played(party) and bd_venue(party) == 1 and not bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_ludd_gone(party) and not bd_written_in(party)
    says "The house is full to the sailcloth. In the Warden's box, in his master's chair with the carved key, sits the Reader in his Crow, a pencil in each hand and the third behind his ear. Below him, in the wings, Madame Orme is a grey shape with a prompt-book against her chest. The lamps go down, a lamp at a time, and the Cuff takes up its half-beat under the floor. And the Moths go on." { Assert bd_venue_told(party). }
  Rule bd_venue_stage_read when bd_played(party) and bd_venue(party) == 1 and not bd_venue_told(party) and bd_written_in(party)
    says "The house is full to the sailcloth. In the Warden's box, in his master's chair, sits the Reader in his Crow with the prompt-book shut on his knee and his lips moving. Below him, in the wings, Madame Orme is a grey shape with her fist at her throat. The lamps go down, a lamp at a time. The Moths go on, and somewhere in the second scene a man in the Warden's box begins to say a part under his breath, and stops, and is very still." { Assert bd_venue_told(party). }
  Rule bd_venue_stage_gone when bd_played(party) and bd_venue(party) == 1 and not bd_venue_told(party) and bd_ludd_gone(party) and not bd_written_in(party)
    says "The house is full to the sailcloth, and the Warden's box has in it a new man with a notebook and no pencil, who looks about him in the manner of someone who has been sent to read a thing he has not been taught to. Below him, in the wings, Madame Orme is a grey shape with a prompt-book against her chest. The lamps go down. The Moths go on." { Assert bd_venue_told(party). }
  Rule bd_venue_hall when bd_played(party) and bd_venue(party) == 2 and not bd_venue_told(party)
    says "It is the biggest house the Moths have ever played, and it is not a house at all: it is a city standing in its wet wool between nineteen chairs. They have cleared a space before the bronze jar. It is thirty feet, a chalk line, and no proscenium. The Moths go on in the light of a single lantern, and the Hall, which has come to see a Drawing, is made to wait." { Assert bd_venue_told(party). }

  // How the player's own turn goes is told after the house has been, as a house is told by the one on the boards.
  Rule bd_nerve_good_says when bd_venue_told(party) and bd_nerve_good(party) and not bd_nerve_told(party)
    says "And you go on. The part is a coat that fits. You stop being afraid at about the second line, which is the only place anyone ever does." { Assert bd_nerve_told(party). }
  Rule bd_nerve_bad_says when bd_venue_told(party) and bd_nerve_bad(party) and not bd_nerve_told(party)
    says "And you go on, and for the first minute you are somebody else's idea of a player, and the house is kind about it. You find the part by the second scene. The first is gone." { Assert bd_nerve_told(party). }

  // A Lampoon that is not good enough does not offend anybody. It is only a play.
  Rule bd_flop_farce when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_form(party, bd_f_farce) and not bd_fair()
    says "The first laugh does not come. The Moths hold for it, as players do, with that faint nasal brightness, and it arrives at last from a Cockle in the third row, alone, and dies of loneliness. The second act goes by like a cart in a quiet street. It is not a disgrace. It is only a play. In the lobby, afterwards, nobody says anything, in a number of masks." { Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_flopped(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 0. }
  Rule bd_flop_elegy when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_form(party, bd_f_elegy) and not bd_fair()
    says "The elegy asks for silence and receives it, which is a different thing from being heard. The house sits through it as a house sits through a sermon on a subject it has already agreed with. Somebody coughs. Somebody laughs, at the wrong place, helplessly, and is hushed. It is not bad. It is only that nothing in it is yet true enough to hurt." { Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_flopped(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 0. }
  Rule bd_flop_ballad when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_form(party, bd_f_ballad) and not bd_fair()
    says "The ballad has too many verses and a tune nobody can sing. The Gulls try; the Magpies try; the house, sportingly, hums. By the ninth verse the Moths are singing to themselves, and the Cuff is singing under them in the piles, a little flat, and kinder." { Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_flopped(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 0. }

  // Twelve ways it can be received, by what it is aimed at and what it is. Fair or great.
  Rule bd_lacke_farce when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_fair() and bd_target(party, bd_m_lacke) and bd_form(party, bd_f_farce)
    says "The Moths give the Warden of Locks a key for every door and a door for none, and by the second act he is locked out of his own house by a cat. The tallymen's clerks in the Magpie dominoes know exactly what a Lock-tax is, and they are the first to go: the laughter starts there and goes through the room like a draught through a lit church. Nobody says a name. A great deal of the evening is spent not saying it, loudly." {
    Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_lacke_stung(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 1. Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 1. }
  Rule bd_lacke_elegy when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_fair() and bd_target(party, bd_m_lacke) and bd_form(party, bd_f_elegy)
    says "It is an elegy for a man still living: for the Warden of Locks, who counted every key in Ombra and was never once asked to dinner. The Moths play it slowly, in the grey light of a single lamp, and the room does what rooms never do for a Warden: it listens. At the last line, about a man who locked up a city and could not remember, at the end, what he had been afraid of, someone in the dark says 'Ah,' as if a bone had been set." {
    Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_lacke_spent(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 2. Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 2. }
  Rule bd_lacke_ballad when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_fair() and bd_target(party, bd_m_lacke) and bd_form(party, bd_f_ballad)
    says "A ballad of the Lock-tax, to a ferrymen's tune any child in the Drip can sing, in sixteen verses, each ending on the price of a door. By the fourth verse the Gulls at the end of the benches have it, and by the eighth the whole room is singing the price of a door in the Warden's own voice, which is a bad tune to be sung to a man, and a worse one to sing in a crowd. When they have done, nobody goes home." {
    Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_lacke_stung(party). Assert bd_room_angry(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 3. Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 3. }
  Rule bd_candid_farce when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_fair() and bd_target(party, bd_m_candid) and bd_form(party, bd_f_farce)
    says "The Candid enters, in a mask of no mask, and announces that everything shall be known. The Moths pass her a locked door, which she informs, at some length, ought to be open; she explains this to the door. It goes on; it has the grace of something that is true. The Reading-room's regulars laugh hardest, and a little late, as people do who have just found the pamphlet in their own pocket." {
    Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_candid_weak(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 1. Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 1. }
  Rule bd_candid_elegy when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_fair() and bd_target(party, bd_m_candid) and bd_form(party, bd_f_elegy)
    says "A lament for the Book of Faces, which is not here: played as a loss, in a bare light, by Moths with their half-masks off one after another, not saying who they are. It is not a satire. It is the Candid's own cause told to her as grief, and the room, which had come to jeer, remembers what it was to have a name. Somebody at the back begins to cry, and does not stop." {
    Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_candid_strong(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 2. Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 2. }
  Rule bd_candid_ballad when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_fair() and bd_target(party, bd_m_candid) and bd_form(party, bd_f_ballad)
    says "A ballad of the Open Book, fifty verses, every one of them beginning 'Who wore the Key?' The Moths sing it as a march. It is the Candid's own song, given back with the tune put right, and the room, which was at best amused by her, has it by the third verse and is tramping on the benches by the sixth. It is a very good song. It is very much the song she would have wanted, and not at all the one she would have written." {
    Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_candid_strong(party). Assert bd_room_angry(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 3. Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 3. }
  Rule bd_contessa_farce when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_fair() and bd_target(party, bd_m_contessa) and bd_form(party, bd_f_farce)
    says "A great house of nine hundred rooms and one servant, who is dusting. The Moths play the Fourteen Palaces as fourteen very old people sitting down to a dinner for forty, each politely waiting for the others to die. The Hill's retainers in the back rows laugh until they have to hold the benches, and then look about to see whether anyone saw." {
    Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_hill_stung(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 1. Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 1. }
  Rule bd_contessa_elegy when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_fair() and bd_target(party, bd_m_contessa) and bd_form(party, bd_f_elegy)
    says "An old servant with a feather duster goes through an empty palace room by room, dusting for a family that has gone to live in the Drip and sew hems. He dusts a portrait, and a chair, and a place laid at table for forty. When it is over a number of the Hill's retainers, in the good Magpie dominoes they have brought for the occasion, sit very still and do not applaud. It is the greatest compliment the Stage has ever been paid." {
    Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_hill_moved(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 2. Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 2. }
  Rule bd_contessa_ballad when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_fair() and bd_target(party, bd_m_contessa) and bd_form(party, bd_f_ballad)
    says "'The Song of the Fourteen' is a rousing thing, and an unkind one: a catalogue of palaces, each with its debt, its duel and its portrait, to the tune of a funeral march that speeds up. The Drip knows the tune. By the end the room is stamping, and the Hill's few retainers in the boxes are very upright, as men are who are listening to a hundred years go out through a door." {
    Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_hill_stung(party). Assert bd_room_angry(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 3. Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 3. }
  Rule bd_urn_farce when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_fair() and bd_target(party, bd_m_urn) and bd_form(party, bd_f_farce)
    says "The Urn is played by Tarrow, if there is a Tarrow, or else by a Moth in a barrel with a slot. Every year a man puts a tessera into the slot. Every year somebody draws out a name. The joke is in the draw: the Pantaloon, with a face of enormous gravity, reaches into himself and brings out the name of whoever is in the best coat. It is the funniest thing the Wet Stage has done in twelve years. Several people in the room have stopped laughing, one at a time, and are looking at their neighbours." {
    Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_urn_laughed(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 1. Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 1. }
  Rule bd_urn_elegy when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_fair() and bd_target(party, bd_m_urn) and bd_form(party, bd_f_elegy)
    says "An elegy for the Urn: a requiem in two voices for a jar that has been shaken in public every year for three hundred years and has given the city, every year, exactly the people it needed. The Moths play it without irony, which is the most dangerous way. The room hears, under the grief, something worse than grief: the sound of a thing being forgiven in advance." {
    Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_urn_mourned(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 2. Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 2. }
  Rule bd_urn_ballad when bd_venue_told(party) and not bd_reacted(party) and bd_fair() and bd_target(party, bd_m_urn) and bd_form(party, bd_f_ballad)
    says "A ballad of the Sluice, to the lamp-trimmers' tune. It is about water, and six hundred, and a man in a gallery who said nothing; and about a jar at the end with a slot in it, into which the singer drops, one at a time, the names of the dead. The room does not like it. The room has not been asked to like it. By the last verse it is on its feet, and very angry, and it is not entirely clear at whom." {
    Assert bd_reacted(party). Assert bd_urn_angry(party). Assert bd_room_angry(party). Set bd_mood(party) to 3. Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 3. }
  Relation bd_lacke_laughed(group). Relation bd_lacke_stung(group). Relation bd_lacke_spent(group). Relation bd_lacke_mobbed(group). Relation bd_candid_weak(group). Relation bd_candid_strong(group).
  Relation bd_hill_stung(group). Relation bd_hill_moved(group). Relation bd_urn_laughed(group). Relation bd_urn_mourned(group). Relation bd_urn_angry(group). Relation bd_urn_told(group). Relation bd_room_angry(group).

  // When the Urn is known to be empty and the Lampoon is aimed at it, somebody says so, in the middle, without any
  // change of voice.
  Rule bd_reveal when bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and bd_target(party, bd_m_urn) and bd_set(bd_t_hollow) and not bd_urn_told(party)
    says "And somewhere in the second movement, without any change of voice, the Pantaloon says that the Urn is empty. It goes into the room like a stone into a well, and the room does not make a sound for the whole time it takes to land. Then, in the third row, a Cockle laughs once, very loud, as a person does who has been afraid for some time of exactly that, and the room goes on from there." { Assert bd_urn_told(party). }

  // The great night: it does not stop when the lamps come up. And what it does to the man it was aimed at.
  Rule bd_great_farce when bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and bd_form(party, bd_f_farce) and bd_great() and not bd_great_night(party)
    says "It is the sort of night the Stage dreams of: the laugh that does not stop at the end of the line but goes on after it, going round the room by itself, as water finds its level. When the Moths take their call the pit is on its feet. A man in the Magpie dominoes has to be helped out. They will have the best of it by heart in the Row by morning." { Assert bd_great_night(party). Assert bd_farce_great(party). }
  Rule bd_great_elegy when bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and bd_form(party, bd_f_elegy) and bd_great() and not bd_great_night(party)
    says "At the end there is no applause, and it is not that kind of silence. Nobody moves. A Gull in the front row is holding the hand of a person she has not met. The lamps are brought up a lamp at a time, and in the whole house nobody wants to be the first to be seen." { Assert bd_great_night(party). }
  Rule bd_great_ballad when bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and bd_form(party, bd_f_ballad) and bd_great() and not bd_great_night(party)
    says "The Burden comes round for the fourth time and the whole house has it, from the Gulls at the back to the Magpies in the boxes, in a rough ragged chorus like the sea coming in. When the Moths stop, the house does not. They sing it out of the door and across the Mask bridge, and the sound of it goes on down Maskers' Lane for an hour, getting smaller, like a boat going out." { Assert bd_great_night(party). Assert bd_drip_sings(party). }
  Rule bd_ballad_drip when bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and bd_form(party, bd_f_ballad) and not bd_drip_sings(party) { Assert bd_drip_sings(party). }
  Rule bd_topple when bd_great_night(party) and bd_farce_great(party) and bd_target(party, bd_m_lacke) and not bd_lacke_laughed(party)
    says "By morning the Row has it. In the Tally Coffee-house a man in a Magpie domino says the word 'cat', and four tallymen put their cups down." { Assert bd_lacke_laughed(party). }
  Rule bd_mobbed when bd_great_night(party) and bd_form(party, bd_f_ballad) and bd_target(party, bd_m_lacke) and not bd_lacke_mobbed(party)
    says "In the small hours a crowd goes down the Row singing the price of a door, and stops outside the Warden's house. Nobody breaks anything. A great many people, in a great many wet coats, stand in the street and sing at a lit window until it goes out." { Assert bd_lacke_mobbed(party). Increase heat(party) by 1. }
  Rule bd_morning_after_song when bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and not bd_morning_told(party) and bd_mood(party) == 3 and watch(clock) >= bd_when(party) + 50 and hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 20
    says "By the morning the Lampoon is in the streets. Nobody has written it down, and everybody has it. In the Masked Hours, where nothing is said, a woman in a Cockle is humming the Burden under her breath at the baker's, and the baker, in his own Cockle, is humming it back." { Assert bd_morning_told(party). }
  Rule bd_morning_after when bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and not bd_morning_told(party) and watch(clock) >= bd_when(party) + 50 and hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 20
    says "The Wet Stage has been talked about. Not in the Masked Hours, where nothing is, but in the voice a city uses for what it has said and cannot take back." { Assert bd_morning_told(party). }
  Observe bd_prompt_heard at bd_prompt when bd_ludd_heard(party) "The slit in the canvas, through which you watched a man play a joke to the dark, looks smaller by day, and a good deal more like a thing that was not meant to be looked through.".

  // ── What the Stage gives the company that played it ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind bd_tongue_kind "the Moth's tongue" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 granting performance described "A thin silver tongue no longer than a finger-joint, pierced for a ribbon: the Moth's tongue, which every player of the Wet Stage is given the night she is first applauded, and which she wears behind the half-mask, against the teeth. It is said to put a word where the next one ought to be. It is certainly very cold.".
  Item bd_tongue "the Moth's tongue" is bd_tongue_kind at offstage.
  Relation bd_tongue_given(group). Relation bd_lesson_taken(group).
  Topic bd_orme_after with orme "Ask her how the house took it" when bd_reacted(actor) and not bd_flopped(actor) and not bd_tongue_given(actor) once {
    Says "'How it took it,' says Madame Orme. She is in the wings still, in the half-mask, with the prompt-book against her chest; she has not taken off the choker. 'They took it as they take rain. They stood in it.' She goes to the shelf over the stove and comes back with a thing in her palm. 'Every Moth has one on the night she is first applauded. I was given mine at nineteen, and pawned it at thirty, and bought it back at forty-three. It is nothing. It is a little cold. Put it behind your teeth and say a line.'".
    On discuss { Assert bd_tongue_given(actor). Give bd_tongue to actor. }
  }
  Topic bd_orme_after_flop with orme "Ask her how the house took it" when bd_reacted(actor) and bd_flopped(actor) and not bd_orme_after_told(actor) once {
    Says "'They took it as a play,' says Madame Orme. 'That is no insult. A play is a thing that can be played again.' She does not look at you; she looks at the stage, which she has looked at every night for thirty-seven years. 'You wanted it to be a stone, and it was a pebble. There are nights for stones. This was not one.'".
    On discuss { Assert bd_orme_after_told(actor). }
  }
  Relation bd_orme_after_told(group).
  Action bd_orme_lesson(actor: group, reader: member, site: place) "Sit for her lesson in how to hold a room" {
    Speaker orme. Time 12.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(orme, site) and memberOf(reader, actor) and awake(reader) and bd_reacted(actor) and not bd_flopped(actor) and not bd_lesson_taken(actor).
    Resolve endow(reader, charisma, by_one).
    On success { Assert bd_lesson_taken(actor). }
    Result "She gives it you without a gesture, in the empty pit, standing at the back with her hands behind her: how to arrive in a room as if the room had been waiting; how to wait for the doubt; how to stop. 'You do not hold a house,' says Madame Orme. 'You let it hold you, and then you do not drop it.' It takes two hours. It is the best two hours of teaching you have had, and she does not once say that it is.".
  }

  // A mask that did a mask's kind of good is remembered on the mask.
  Relation bd_gw_paid(group).
  Rule bd_goodwill_moth when bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and wears(party, face_moth) and not bd_gw_paid(party) { Increase goodwill(face_moth) by 1. Assert bd_gw_paid(party). }
  // How the company comes to the Wet Stage at all: the Annex rents the players' mask, and Moll has seen who wears it.
  Discovery bd_stage_hint "The Wardrobe Annex rents the Moth, the players' half-mask, to anyone with three coin; the Wet Stage in Maskers' Lane takes whoever wears it for one of its own, for as long as the face lasts, and its manager is short of players." { Known by moll. }
  Topic bd_moll_moth with moll "Ask which face a person wears to be taken for a player" when not knows(actor, bd_stage_hint) once {
    Says "Moll considers the pegs. 'The Moth,' he says. 'Grey, with the wings. They rent it to the Wet Stage by the dozen when theirs are wet, which is always, and the Wet Stage's manager looks at any Moth who walks in and wonders whether it can say a line.' A pause. 'It generally cannot. But she looks. Maskers' Lane, past the Mask bridge, the barge with a roof like a bad tooth.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bd_stage_hint). }
  }

  // The song the Drip sings, and who hums it.
  Observe bd_drip_ballad at bread_market when bd_drip_sings(party) and bd_form(party, bd_f_ballad) "From somewhere in the bread-market comes a man's voice, humming the tune of the Lampoon, and a baker's boy, correcting him, has the second verse. They are not a very good duet. It is, you suppose, what it is for.".
  Observe bd_drip_other at bread_market when bd_drip_sings(party) and not bd_form(party, bd_f_ballad) "In the bread-market somebody is telling the best of the Wet Stage's night to somebody who was not there, doing the voices; and the somebody who was not there is laughing, with the face of a person who will be able to say, afterwards, that he knew it.".
  Observe bd_moll_hums near moll when bd_drip_sings(party) "Ferris Moll, who does not look up, is humming something under his breath as he writes your coin in the book: three bars of it, and again. He does not seem to know he is doing it.".

  // ── Milestones ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Query bd_ludd_done() means bd_written_in(party) or bd_ludd_trusts(party) or bd_ludd_leashed(party) or bd_ludd_gone(party) or bd_codicil(wet_stage) or bd_passed(party) or bd_sealed(wet_stage).
  Milestone bd_ms_licence "The Wet Stage keeps its licence" worth 25 when bd_kept(wet_stage) or bd_restored(wet_stage).
  Milestone bd_ms_ludd "The Reader is dealt with" worth 50 when bd_ludd_done().
  Milestone bd_ms_finch "Finch writes again" worth 25 when bd_finch_moved(party).
  Milestone bd_ms_orme "Madame Orme gives you her book" worth 25 when bd_commissioned(party) or bd_orme_plays(party).
  Milestone bd_ms_quist "Tarrow's house forgets itself" worth 25 when bd_quist_happy(party).
  Milestone bd_ms_lampoon "The Lampoon is played" worth 75 when bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party).
  Milestone bd_ms_great "The house forgets itself" worth 50 when bd_great_night(party).
  Milestone bd_ms_drip "A song the Drip sings" worth 25 when bd_drip_sings(party).

  // ── The Lampoon at the Drawing, when it has been played already ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A Lampoon that went well on the Wet Stage has been talked of; at the Drawing it is carried into the Hall by whoever
  // heard it, and counts as played without the Moths going on again.
  Rule bd_echo_farce when drawingNight() and at(party, urn_hall) and bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and bd_venue(party) == 1 and not handPlayed(party, hand_lampoon) and bd_form(party, bd_f_farce)
    says "In the Hall of the Urn, among the nineteen chairs, somebody at the back says a word softly to somebody else, and by the time it has been passed to the front there is a laugh in it. The Wet Stage got here before the Moths." { Assert handPlayed(party, hand_lampoon). Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 1. }
  Rule bd_echo_elegy when drawingNight() and at(party, urn_hall) and bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and bd_venue(party) == 1 and not handPlayed(party, hand_lampoon) and bd_form(party, bd_f_elegy)
    says "Somebody in the Hall is humming, very low, the burden of the elegy, and the Drip around her is going quiet in the way people do when they find that they are all holding the same hand." { Assert handPlayed(party, hand_lampoon). Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 2. }
  Rule bd_echo_ballad when drawingNight() and at(party, urn_hall) and bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and bd_venue(party) == 1 and not handPlayed(party, hand_lampoon) and bd_form(party, bd_f_ballad)
    says "From the back of the Hall, from the Drip's benches, a voice begins the Burden; and by the second line it is the Hall's." { Assert handPlayed(party, hand_lampoon). Set handWay(hand_lampoon) to 3. }

  // ── Fates: what became of the Wet Stage and its people ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Told in the last hour before the book closes. The Lampoon's own account comes last.
  Relation bd_fate_done(group). Relation bd_fate_stage(place). Relation bd_fate_lampoon(group).
  Rule bd_fate_orme_played when newsHour() and bd_cast_orme(party) and bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and not bd_fate_done(orme) once
    says "Of Madame Orme: She played the principal part of the Lampoon in a half-mask and without the pearls, and nobody in the third row said a name that night, or any night. In the spring the choker came back from the pawnshop at the Weights quay, a pearl at a time, in the order they had gone. She wears it with every fourth pearl paste, to remember which." { Assert bd_fate_done(orme). }
  Rule bd_fate_orme_crake when newsHour() and bd_crake_knows(party) and not bd_fate_done(orme) once
    says "Of Madame Orme: Tobiah Venable told her, on the morning after, that he had always known whose line it was; she sat down on a hamper and did not speak. A week later, in the empty pit, they did the Pump together, the Assessor's year inside the Pump's three minutes. The Moths who watched say that nobody has ever been so exactly said, or so forgiven." { Assert bd_fate_done(orme). }
  Rule bd_fate_orme_dark when newsHour() and bd_revoked(wet_stage) and not bd_restored(wet_stage) and not bd_fate_done(orme) once
    says "Of Madame Orme: The Wet Stage was dark for the rest of the Novena, and she sat in the green room with the accounts and the pearls and played the Pump to the bucket. On the tenth morning, whoever the Warden then was, his clerk came for the licence. She asked him to wait, and finished the figures." { Assert bd_fate_done(orme). }
  Rule bd_fate_orme_flop when newsHour() and bd_played(party) and bd_flopped(party) and not bd_fate_done(orme) once
    says "Of Madame Orme: She kept your prompt-book on the shelf over the stove, with the blue tape on it, next to her own. 'A play,' she says, to anyone who asks. 'It is a play that has not been played properly yet. There is a great deal to be said for being a play that has not been played.'" { Assert bd_fate_done(orme). }
  Rule bd_fate_orme_watched when newsHour() and bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and not bd_fate_done(orme) once
    says "Of Madame Orme: She watched the Lampoon from the wings with the prompt-book against her chest, and did not once look at the stage; she watched the house. 'There,' she said, at the end, in the dark. 'That is what it was like.' She has not said what it was like. Master Dibble has come off the board, and the Pump is on it for the spring." { Assert bd_fate_done(orme). }
  Rule bd_fate_orme_default when newsHour() and not bd_fate_done(orme) once
    says "Of Madame Orme: The Wet Stage played Master Dibble to the end of its season, to a house that clapped, and she kept the pearl choker on and the accounts in the heap. On wet nights she is said to be heard in the empty pit giving the Pump, both parts, to the drip." { Assert bd_fate_done(orme). }

  Rule bd_fate_ludd_read when newsHour() and bd_written_in(party) and not bd_fate_done(ludd) once
    says "Of Master Orlick: He sat in the Warden's box on the last night with the prompt-book shut on his knee, and when the Joke came on he said the Reader's lines under his breath along with the Moth, a half-beat late, like the house. His report to the Warden was one line: A revival of Master Dibble. Passed. He plays one cut joke a night now, from the chest, before the farce, and calls it the Reader's Cue." { Assert bd_fate_done(ludd). }
  Rule bd_fate_ludd_friend when newsHour() and bd_ludd_trusts(party) and not bd_fate_done(ludd) once
    says "Of Master Orlick: He sealed the season and went on sealing it, and cut rather less than he had. The chest is under the prompt-corner shelf still, and somebody has been adding to it in a hand that is not his: one slip a night, folded once." { Assert bd_fate_done(ludd). }
  Rule bd_fate_ludd_leash when newsHour() and bd_ludd_leashed(party) and not bd_fate_done(ludd) once
    says "Of Master Orlick: He passed what he was given and did not look up, and gave notice on the tenth morning, in a very neat letter. He sits in the pit of the Wet Stage on the nights it plays, in the third row, in the Crow, alone, with a pencil in his hand, striking nothing." { Assert bd_fate_done(ludd). }
  Rule bd_fate_ludd_gone when newsHour() and bd_ludd_gone(party) and not bd_fate_done(ludd) once
    says "Of Master Orlick: He was dismissed by the Warden's clerk on the morning after the Moths found his plays. They have the Joke at the door by heart, and nobody says it where he can hear. He walks the aisles of the Wet Stage at night, unmasked, and the Moths leave the stage door on the latch." { Assert bd_fate_done(ludd). }
  Rule bd_fate_ludd_sour when newsHour() and (bd_codicil(wet_stage) or bd_ludd_sour(party)) and not bd_fate_done(ludd) once
    says "Of Master Orlick: He is the Reader still. His note is in the margin of the licence in his own hand, signed, and it is the thing of his life he is proudest of and does not forgive you for. He cuts, now, with a certain exactness; and the reasons, in the margins, are shorter." { Assert bd_fate_done(ludd). }
  Rule bd_fate_ludd_default when newsHour() and not bd_fate_done(ludd) once
    says "Of Master Orlick: He reads the plays of the Wet Stage for the Warden, and cuts them, and keeps what he cuts. The chest is under the prompt-corner shelf, and by now it is a good deal larger than the repertory." { Assert bd_fate_done(ludd). }

  Rule bd_fate_quist_cast when newsHour() and bd_cast_quist(party) and bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and not bd_fate_done(bd_quist) once
    says "Of Pantaloon Tarrow: He played the Pantaloon in the Lampoon, and took his three blows of the slapstick, and fell down his two stairs for the forty-thousand-and-first time; and the house forgot itself. He got up. He says it is the last time. He says it every night." { Assert bd_fate_done(bd_quist). }
  Rule bd_fate_quist_happy when newsHour() and bd_quist_happy(party) and not bd_fate_done(bd_quist) once
    says "Of Pantaloon Tarrow: He did the Walnut, once, for a house of one, in the dark, and it is the best house he has ever had. He tells it to the Moths with the voices. They have learned to say that they remember it." { Assert bd_fate_done(bd_quist). }
  Rule bd_fate_quist_default when newsHour() and not bd_fate_done(bd_quist) once
    says "Of Pantaloon Tarrow: He falls down his two stairs, and the house claps. He has stopped looking up to see who saw." { Assert bd_fate_done(bd_quist). }

  Rule bd_fate_finch_serene when newsHour() and bd_elegy_serene(party) and not bd_fate_done(bd_finch) once
    says "Of Ambrose Finch: He finished the elegy of Cullet Reach, and it ends on a man in a gallery who said nothing. It is the best poem in the Delta and it has a living man in it. It was cried in the Drip in a week, and in a month an old man in the Hospice was seen to put his hands over his ears." { Assert bd_fate_done(bd_finch). }
  Rule bd_fate_finch_girl when newsHour() and bd_elegy_girl(party) and not bd_fate_done(bd_finch) once
    says "Of Ambrose Finch: He finished the elegy of Cullet Reach, and it ends on a girl of nineteen with a key she could not carry. It was read at the Reach on the thirty-first year, in the rain, to the families of the low islands. Many wept. None, so far as is known, was angry. One old woman said a name, and was told to hush, and did." { Assert bd_fate_done(bd_finch). }
  Rule bd_fate_finch_water when newsHour() and bd_elegy_water(party) and not bd_fate_done(bd_finch) once
    says "Of Ambrose Finch: He finished the elegy of Cullet Reach, and it ends on the water and blames nobody. It makes people cry in the right place and go home. He is not sure whether it was a kindness, and sits with that in the flies, with a dry foolscap and a new pen." { Assert bd_fate_done(bd_finch). }
  Rule bd_fate_finch_alone when newsHour() and bd_finch_alone(party) and not bd_fate_done(bd_finch) once
    says "Of Ambrose Finch: He wrote, in the end, because somebody pinned a stanza over his table and went away, and he does not know who; he has asked Tarrow, who says it was the drip. He writes every day now, and tears up about half of it, which he says is the proper proportion." { Assert bd_fate_done(bd_finch). }
  Rule bd_fate_finch_moved when newsHour() and bd_finch_moved(party) and not bd_fate_done(bd_finch) once
    says "Of Ambrose Finch: He writes every day now, and tears up about half of it, which he says is the proper proportion." { Assert bd_fate_done(bd_finch). }
  Rule bd_fate_finch_default when newsHour() and not bd_fate_done(bd_finch) once
    says "Of Ambrose Finch: He is in residence, by the bequest of the late Abelard Tenn, and is seen to be. The foolscap is white. It has been looked at for another season." { Assert bd_fate_done(bd_finch). }

  Rule bd_fate_stage_dark when newsHour() and bd_revoked(wet_stage) and not bd_restored(wet_stage) and not bd_fate_stage(wet_stage) once
    says "Of the Wet Stage: It was a salt-barge with a bucket in it from the fourth day, and the Moths sang for coin in the Drip, in half-masks, on the landings. When the book closed, nobody knew what would become of the house. The nail in the door has the Warden's notice on it still, and, under it, in chalk, somebody has written: INTERVAL." { Assert bd_fate_stage(wet_stage). }
  Rule bd_fate_stage_shut when newsHour() and bd_played(party) and bd_venue(party) == 1 and bd_target(party, bd_m_lacke) and not bd_written_in(party) and not bd_ludd_trusts(party) and not bd_fate_stage(wet_stage) once
    says "Of the Wet Stage: The Warden of Locks, as the Lampoon had him, signed the closing of the house on the morning after, in the hand he had left; it was the last paper he signed with the Key on. The Moths are in the Drip for the winter, singing it for coin. The house is a hull with a bucket in it. It is very much talked of." { Assert bd_fate_stage(wet_stage). }
  Rule bd_fate_stage_played when newsHour() and bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and not bd_fate_stage(wet_stage) once
    says "Of the Wet Stage: It is the busiest house in the Delta. The benches are full of people who have heard of it, and the Moths have found that a play, once it has been talked about, can be played every night and not run out. Madame Orme has bought a tarpaulin for the flies, and would like it known that she did not need to." { Assert bd_fate_stage(wet_stage). }
  Rule bd_fate_stage_default when newsHour() and not bd_fate_stage(wet_stage) once
    says "Of the Wet Stage: It plays Master Dibble to a house that claps. The licence is renewed each quarter on the day, and nobody can remember whether anything was ever to be said in it." { Assert bd_fate_stage(wet_stage). }

  Rule bd_fate_lampoon_lie when newsHour() and bd_lies(party) >= 1 and bd_lacke_laughed(party) and not bd_fate_lampoon(party) once
    says "Of the Lampoon: The Warden of Locks was unseated by a joke that was not true. He was guilty of everything else; but it was not for that they laughed." { Assert bd_fate_lampoon(party). }
  Rule bd_fate_lampoon_urn when newsHour() and bd_urn_told(party) and not bd_fate_lampoon(party) once
    says "Of the Lampoon: The city knows that the Urn is empty because a clown said so, in the middle of a farce, and cannot make up its mind whether to believe a clown." { Assert bd_fate_lampoon(party). }
  Rule bd_fate_lampoon_lie_other when newsHour() and bd_lies(party) >= 1 and bd_reacted(party) and not bd_fate_lampoon(party) once
    says "Of the Lampoon: In the Row they quote the line you made up as if it were history. It is on a ballad-sheet now, with a name in it; it will be there when the facts are not." { Assert bd_fate_lampoon(party). }
  Rule bd_fate_lampoon_stung when newsHour() and bd_lacke_stung(party) and not bd_lacke_laughed(party) and not bd_fate_lampoon(party) once
    says "Of the Lampoon: The Warden of Locks heard it, or was told, and laughed it off in the Tally Coffee-house where it could be seen to be laughed. He has been seen, since, to try each of his doors twice." { Assert bd_fate_lampoon(party). }
  Rule bd_fate_lampoon_urn_funny when newsHour() and bd_urn_laughed(party) and not bd_fate_lampoon(party) once
    says "Of the Lampoon: They laughed at the Urn. It is a harder thing to do again with a straight face, in the Masked Hours, on the Chapel steps; the Chaplain has remarked on it, mildly, to the damp." { Assert bd_fate_lampoon(party). }
  Rule bd_fate_lampoon_urn_angry when newsHour() and bd_urn_angry(party) and not bd_fate_lampoon(party) once
    says "Of the Lampoon: The ballad of the Sluice is sung in the Drip now, at weddings, which is not what it was for; the last verse is said to be the one that makes the old men leave the table." { Assert bd_fate_lampoon(party). }
  Rule bd_fate_lampoon_candid when newsHour() and bd_candid_weak(party) and not bd_fate_lampoon(party) once
    says "Of the Lampoon: It was a farce of the Candid, and it was true, and it was funny, and a good many people who had been going to the Reading-room stopped. She was right about nearly everything. It is a thing to have made funnier than her." { Assert bd_fate_lampoon(party). }
  Rule bd_fate_lampoon_hill when newsHour() and bd_hill_stung(party) and not bd_fate_lampoon(party) once
    says "Of the Lampoon: The Hill has not forgiven it. The shutters on the Terrace stay down; a Second in a good Magpie domino was heard, in the Row, to ask whether it were true that servants dusted, and was answered by a laugh, and went home early." { Assert bd_fate_lampoon(party). }
  Rule bd_fate_lampoon_angry when newsHour() and bd_room_angry(party) and bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and not bd_fate_lampoon(party) once
    says "Of the Lampoon: It was a song, and the room that sang it did not go home. For a week there was a crowd in one square or another, singing a verse at a lit window; and the Watch, which was told to stop it, asked what, precisely, the offence was, and was told it was the tune." { Assert bd_fate_lampoon(party). }
  Rule bd_fate_lampoon_kind when newsHour() and bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and (bd_lacke_spent(party) or bd_hill_moved(party) or bd_urn_mourned(party) or bd_candid_strong(party)) and not bd_fate_lampoon(party) once
    says "Of the Lampoon: It was a kind thing, and it was well done, and it is remembered as one: as the night the Wet Stage did not hurt anybody. Nobody has yet worked out what, if anything, it cost the people it spared." { Assert bd_fate_lampoon(party). }
  Rule bd_fate_lampoon_played when newsHour() and bd_reacted(party) and not bd_flopped(party) and not bd_fate_lampoon(party) once
    says "Of the Lampoon: It was played, and the house took it, and the tune or the line of it is in the city now, with the weather and the price of eels." { Assert bd_fate_lampoon(party). }
  Rule bd_fate_lampoon_unplayed when newsHour() and bd_lampoon_ready(party) and not bd_played(party) and not bd_fate_lampoon(party) once
    says "Of the Lampoon: It lies in a prompt-book on a shelf over a stove, ready, with a blue tape on it. It was never played. There is a good deal to be said for a joke that has not been told; and nothing, Tarrow says, that it can be said for." { Assert bd_fate_lampoon(party). }

  // @@END
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/body.kyr:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The Registrar's body ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // She lies in the bier-room in the white mask of her office. The Warrant lets a Bare lift it, which is the whole reason
  // the Warrant exists; and what the face and the mask say, once lifted, is the first real evidence of the book: that she
  // died of her heart, in her sleep as it were, with her hands folded by someone else; that her mask was put back on
  // by a frightened person who knew what it was; and that under the white mask the skin carries the pale band of an
  // older Office than hers.
  Observe bier_scene at bier_room when true "A cold small room off the lamp-room with a stone bier in it and a white sheet to the chin. A candle burns at the head and another at the foot, and between them, on the face, is the white mask of the Registrar: a plain bare oval with two slits and no mouth. The mask has been wiped. There is no other mark of the building on her at all.".
  Observe bier_night at bier_room when privateHours() "At night the candles are the only thing in the bier-room that moves, and they move very little. The rain on the lamp-room roof is next door, and rather far.".
  Thing bier "the Registrar's body" at bier_room {
    State masked "The Registrar lies in her white mask on the bier.".
    State bared "The Registrar lies on the bier with her white mask lifted and set beside her.".
    Change lift "Lift the Registrar's white mask, by the Warrant" from masked to bared.
  }
  Relation maskLifted(group).
  Rule lifted_by_warrant when state(bier, bared) and warrantHeld(party) and not maskLifted(party) says "You lift it by the rim, as the Warrant says you may, and set it down beside her. The face under it is a small, old, composed face with the look people have when they have stopped being interrupted. A narrow face, a lamp-trimmer's daughter's. It is exactly as if nothing had ever happened to it, and you notice you are holding your own breath, as one is meant not to." { Assert maskLifted(party). }

  Discovery marrick_natural "The Registrar died of her heart, quietly, without a mark on her; her hands were folded afterwards by someone else.".
  Discovery mask_reset "The white mask was put back on the Registrar after her death, by a frightened hand that knew what it was and wanted it straight: the tie is knotted twice, and the left slit is a fraction high.".
  Discovery old_band "Under the pale band the white mask leaves, there is another, older and fainter: the mark of a different Office worn once for a year, a long time ago, and a different shape.".
  Action examine_death(actor: group, site: place) "Examine the Registrar's body for the manner of her death" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and maskLifted(actor) and not knows(actor, marrick_natural).
    Time 20.
    Resolve check(actor, mending, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, marrick_natural). }
    Result "Nothing is broken, nothing is cut, nothing is in the lips. The nails are clean; the colour is the colour of a heart that gave out quite politely. The hands, which someone has folded, are folded by someone who had not folded a dead woman's hands before. She was not killed, so far as a body can say. That is going to be very awkward for the people who say she was.".
    Otherwise "You look for an hour at a small old woman and learn only that you do not know what you are looking for.".
  }
  Action examine_mask(actor: group, site: place) "Look at how the white mask was put on" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and maskLifted(actor) and not knows(actor, mask_reset).
    Time 10.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, mask_reset). }
    Result "You turn it over. The knot of the tie is a clerk's knot, tied twice, the way a person ties a thing they are afraid will come off. The left slit sits a fraction high on the face, as if the hand that put it there was shaking. Whoever did it stopped halfway, and began again.".
    Otherwise "It is a mask, and it has been tied on. You cannot make it tell you more.".
  }
  Action examine_bands(actor: group, site: place) "Look at the marks a mask leaves on the Registrar's face" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and maskLifted(actor) and not knows(actor, old_band).
    Time 10.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, old_band). }
    Result "A mask worn a year leaves a band of pale skin the width of its rim, and a mask worn thirty years leaves a different one. Over the white mask's there is another, fainter, a hand's breadth wider at the temple, that has all but healed: an Office she held once, long ago, for exactly one year. A broad Office. A heavy one. It sat low on her cheeks, the way the Treasurer's does.".
    Otherwise "A band of pale skin. You have a notion there is another, and you have no notion what a Fitter would see.".
  }
  // The same is found by anyone who simply sits with her, no skill: it takes the night.
  Action sit_with_body(actor: group, site: place) "Sit with the Registrar until the candle burns down" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and maskLifted(actor) and privateHours() and not knows(actor, mask_reset) and not sat_vigil(actor).
    Time 60.
    On success { Assert sat_vigil(actor). Assert knows(actor, mask_reset). }
    Result "You sit as you would sit with anybody. Near the end of the hour you notice that the tie of the mask is knotted twice and the left slit sits a little high; and that whoever put it back did not do it quickly. It is the only thing in the room that is not quiet.".
  }
  Relation sat_vigil(group).
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/chapel.kyr:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── Chapel Island ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Chapel of the Bare Face is the one house in Ombra whose door is knocked masked and answered bare. Its rooms
  // here are the steps, the nave, the lamp-room where the Registrar died, the vestry and the confessionals; the
  // bier-room, the Registry and the Urn Hall are the integrator's, the cloister the monk's. Three threads are told
  // here: the lamp-room (what the evidence of an evening says, and how a quick reading is wrong), the stranger on
  // the steps (a Bare nobody may bury), and the children who forget the Assessor of Weights. The cleric's hearing is
  // cleric.kyr's, but it sits on Father Ansel and the lamp-room: what the cleric learns under the seal can be proved
  // here without it.
  //
  // Ids of mine that other files may read: the persons `chaplain`, `ch_verger`, `ch_corrow`, `ch_choir`; the thing
  // `lamp_table`; the facts `ch_evening` (the lamp-room fully read), `ch_stranger_name`; the relations
  // `ch_buried(party)`, `ch_name_cried(party)`, `ch_choir_ready(party)`, `ch_ansel_trusts(party)`.

  // ── The steps ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe ch_steps_public at chapel_steps when publicHours() "Nine broad steps climb out of the Cuff to the Chapel of the Bare Face, black with wet, and on every one a cluster of masked people waits out the rain under oiled paper without looking at one another. The Chapel bridge comes in on one side and the Candle bridge on the other, and between them the water stairs go down into the Cuff, where the ferrymen tie up to leave the dead. The door is open. Over it, worn nearly smooth by three hundred winters of hands, someone has cut HERE NOBODY IS ASKED.".
  Observe ch_steps_private at chapel_steps when privateHours() "After the Ninth Bell the steps empty. The door is shut, with a wicket cut in it at the height of a hand, for knocking; a lamp in a glass burns above it, and the rain walks through the light in long diagonals. Across the water the Hill is dark. In the cloister a single window shows, and goes out.".
  Observe ch_steps_cloister at chapel_steps when true "A lane of wet paving runs off round the Chapel's flank to the cloister door of the Bare Brothers, who go about it with their faces uncovered and are not looked at.".

  Observe ch_nave_public at nave when publicHours() "The nave is long and bare, whitewashed to the height of a hand and then left to the damp. There are no statues. Along both walls, where saints would stand, hang rows of plain oval masks of unpainted wood, each with a ribbon, each a gift from a person who is not named, and under the rain on the high windows they look like a congregation that has come in and kept quiet. The lamp-room door is on the east side, the vestry on the west; the confessionals are in the north-west corner; the Registry doors, bronze, are at the far end and shut.".
  Observe ch_nave_private at nave when privateHours() "The nave at night is a long dark hall with the lamps of the Novena burning at the east end, one for each night that has been, and by the ninth night, you think, it will have got very bright. The wooden masks on the walls have turned their faces to the lamps. Your footsteps come back from the Registry doors a moment late, as if they had been let in and asked their business.".
  Observe ch_nave_lamps at nave when day(clock) >= 2 and day(clock) < 9 "The verger keeps the Novena lamps, and says that a lamp that goes out before its night is over is a thing one does not mention.".

  Observe ch_vestry_scene at vestry when true "A small room with a smell of old linen and bay. Presses of grey vestments, a table with a ledger and a sand-tray, a hearth where a fire is never quite lit, and a stool worn to the shape of someone who sits with his head in his hands. On the wall a plain oval of wood, no mask at all, hangs where a crucifix would hang in another city. A door in the north wall has been papered over and painted, and a draught comes round its edge.".
  Observe ch_vestry_stair at vestry when knows(party, private_stair_known) "The papered door in the north wall has a thin edge of old dust along its foot, as if a very long time ago a stair went up behind it.".
  Observe ch_confessionals_public at confessionals when publicHours() "Two boxes of black oak stand side by side against the north wall, each with a curtain and a door and between them a grille of lead no wider than a hand: the Hearer's side, and the penitent's. By day nobody kneels here; a penitent masked in the Masked Hours is no penitent, the Chapel says, only a face confessing for a trade. A tin saucer of tallow stubs stands on the ledge.".
  Observe ch_confessionals_private at confessionals when privateHours() "A taper burns in the penitent's box, on the ledge under the grille, and the curtain is drawn. The Hearer's side has a chair, a cushion and a candle in a tin shade. At night the confessionals are the one place in Ombra where a masked person walks up to a bare one on purpose, and kneels.".

  // ── The people of the Chapel ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Father Ansel keeps the Chapel and has heard its confessions for forty years behind a veil. Two days before she died
  // the Registrar confessed to him, and he cannot say what it was; and an hour before she died he stood in the nave
  // and heard a man in the lamp-room say her name aloud. He has said nothing since. He is kind, and afraid, and ashamed of both.
  Person chaplain "Father Ansel" at nave {
    Role "the Hearer of the Chapel of the Bare Face". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "A tall stooped man of sixty-four in a grey coat looks up, with the tilt of the head of someone who has spent his life listening through a grille and has not learned to stop. He has hands like a boatman's, and the ink-stain of the Chapel's ledger up the side of one. 'The Chapel is open,' says Father Ansel. 'It is always open. I am sorry that it has not much to give, this week.'".
    Greets again "Father Ansel looks up from the lamps, and then at the place where your face is, and then at a point slightly to the left of it, out of kindness.".
  }
  Person ch_verger "Jonas Heddle" at nave {
    Role "the Chapel's verger". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "A broad man in a brown apron stands on a stool with a taper, pushing a wick up into a lamp with the care of someone forcing a cork. He does not look round. 'Mind the floor by the lamp-room door,' says Jonas Heddle. 'Father says leave it. I've swept round it nine days and I don't know what I'm sweeping round.'".
    Greets again "Jonas Heddle, on his stool, says to the lamp, 'Mind the floor.'".
  }
  Person ch_corrow "Mistress Odell" at nave {
    Role "the choir-mistress, who rehearses the Nineteen Offices". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "A thin woman with a tuning-fork and a voice like a drawn nail stands in front of nine children in grey smocks, and does not turn. 'From the Locks,' she says to them. 'Again. From the Locks.' To you, over her shoulder, with no change of tone: 'If you are going to stand there, stand there quietly.'".
    Greets again "'From the Locks,' says Mistress Odell, to the children, and then to you, 'Quietly.'".
  }
  Person ch_choir "the children of the choir" at nave {
    Role "the nine children of the Chapel's choir, in grey smocks". Ancestry human. Numbers 9. Peaceable. Pronouns they. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "Nine children in grey smocks stand in a row facing the Registry doors and sing, in the flat voice of children who have been told that the melody is not the point, the Nineteen Offices of Ombra. They sing the Treasurer and the Warden of Locks, the Master of Measures; and then there is a gap in the row of faces as wide as a door, and they go on, bravely, with the Physician-General.".
    Greets again "The children look at you sideways without moving their heads.".
  }

  // The day and the night of the Chapel. Father Ansel is in the nave through the Masked Hours, in his vestry from the
  // Ninth Bell until midnight, in his cell after; on the ninth night he is where the Drawing is. The verger keeps the
  // lamps lit until the last of them is trimmed, and the choir sings in the afternoon, which is the only time children
  // can be got to be quiet.
  Rule ch_ansel_nave when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 20 and not drawingNight() and not at(chaplain, nave) { Assert at(chaplain, nave). }
  Rule ch_ansel_vestry when hour(clock) >= 20 and not drawingNight() and not at(chaplain, vestry) { Assert at(chaplain, vestry). }
  Rule ch_ansel_cell when hour(clock) < 8 and not at(chaplain, offstage) { Assert at(chaplain, offstage). }
  Rule ch_ansel_drawing when drawingNight() and not at(chaplain, urn_hall) { Assert at(chaplain, urn_hall). }
  Rule ch_verger_nave when hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 21 and not at(ch_verger, nave) { Assert at(ch_verger, nave). }
  Rule ch_verger_home when (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 7) and not at(ch_verger, offstage) { Assert at(ch_verger, offstage). }
  Rule ch_choir_sings when hour(clock) >= 14 and hour(clock) < 17 and not drawingNight() and not at(ch_choir, nave) { Assert at(ch_choir, nave). Assert at(ch_corrow, nave). }
  Rule ch_choir_home when (hour(clock) >= 17 or hour(clock) < 14) and not at(ch_choir, offstage) { Assert at(ch_choir, offstage). Assert at(ch_corrow, offstage). }
  Observe ch_ansel_veil at nave when publicHours() and at(chaplain, nave) "Father Ansel stands among the lamps in a Hearer's veil, a square of plain grey linen hung from the brow and tied behind, which hides nothing and is understood to hide everything; he wears it as other men wear a limp.".
  Observe ch_ansel_bare at vestry when privateHours() and at(chaplain, vestry) "Father Ansel sits on the worn stool with his veil in his lap, folded in four, and his bare face is older than his voice.".

  // A Hearer met by day by someone with no face of their own says one cold thing: the Chapel is not unkind, only exact.
  Topic ch_ansel_cold with chaplain "Speak to Father Ansel" when not masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "The veil turns a little toward the place beside your head, and stays there. 'The Chapel is open to every face,' says Father Ansel, gently, as to a draught. 'I am not able to hear one that has none. After the Ninth Bell, in the vestry, I am only a man in a room. Forgive me.'".
  }
  Topic ch_jonas_cold with ch_verger "Speak to the verger" when not masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "'Not paid to see you,' says Jonas Heddle, to the lamp, and gives the wick a push that settles the matter.".
  }
  Topic ch_corrow_cold with ch_corrow "Speak to the choir-mistress" when not masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "'Nobody is here,' says Mistress Odell, and strikes her fork on the pulpit, and nine children begin again.".
  }

  // By day, to a face: the Chapel answers as the face is met. An Owl is the lamp-trimmers' own; a Gull is the
  // ferrymen's, who carry what is left on the water stairs.
  Topic ch_ansel_chapel with chaplain "Ask Father Ansel about the Chapel of the Bare Face" when masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "'The oldest house in Ombra that no one owns.' He smiles under the veil. 'The Concord made a law that no one shall be known, and then had to put somewhere the people who were wounded by it. So: a house where a person may kneel as a person. The Hearer sits bare behind the grille and the penitent kneels masked and says what the mask cannot, and not even I know whose face it is. Forty years, and I have never once asked. It is the only mercy I have ever been any good at.'".
  }
  Topic ch_ansel_dead with chaplain "Ask Father Ansel who lies in the bier-room" when masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "'A person of the Chapel is not well.' He says it as one lays a plate down. 'No one may lawfully say who, or whether, or that there is a place that needs filling.' His hands, which have been folded, come apart. 'I should like to say it to someone. It is a thing I should like very much to be allowed to do. Go to the Gate, to the Sergeant. She holds a paper that lets me.' He looks at the lamp-room door. 'I was her Hearer. Two days before. You will not ask me what she brought, and I should be grateful if you did not think that she brought anything.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ch_her_hearer). }
  }
  Discovery ch_her_hearer "Father Ansel was the Registrar's own Hearer, and she confessed to him two days before she died; he cannot say what she told him.".
  Topic ch_ansel_seal with chaplain "Ask Father Ansel what the Registrar confessed to him" when masked(actor) and publicHours() and knows(actor, ch_her_hearer) and not hearer(actor) {
    Says "The veil does not move. 'No,' says Father Ansel, quite gently, and nothing else, and goes on standing there so that you will have to be the one who leaves.".
  }
  Topic ch_ansel_seal_hearer with chaplain "Ask Father Ansel what the Registrar confessed to him" when masked(actor) and publicHours() and knows(actor, ch_her_hearer) and hearer(actor) {
    Says "You have your question halfway out and you hear it for what it is, and so does he; the stillness in the veil is the stillness of someone watching a colleague about to step off a quay. 'You are a Hearer,' he says. 'So you know that I could not tell you if I wished, and I do not wish it, and that if I did you would think less of me.' He lets out his breath. 'Thank you for not having asked. I should like it noted that you did not.'".
    On discuss { Assert ch_ansel_trusts(actor). }
  }
  Relation ch_ansel_trusts(group).
  // By night, in the vestry, to a bare face: he is only a man in a room, and says what he may not say in the nave.
  Topic ch_ansel_night with chaplain "Ask Father Ansel how he is" when privateHours() and not masked(actor) and at(chaplain, vestry) once {
    Says "He is glad to be asked, and it is clear that nobody has. 'I have not slept since,' says Father Ansel, 'and I do not mean it as a figure of speech. I lie there and I hear the lamp-room door. It makes a sound like a man clearing his throat to say something that will end a conversation.' He laughs, not well. 'You are Bare. I may say that to you. A man who says it to a Bare says it to a wall that happens to be listening. It is the one comfort the Concord ever thought of that I approve of without reservation.'".
  }
  Topic ch_ansel_night_dead with chaplain "Ask Father Ansel who is dead" when privateHours() and not masked(actor) and at(chaplain, vestry) once {
    Says "'Ysolde,' he says; and stops, and puts his hand over his mouth, and takes it away. 'No. There. It is said, in a vestry, at midnight, to a stranger. If the Concord wishes to Name me for it, I am sixty-four and I should like to see it try.' His eyes are wet. 'The Registrar. Lying in the bier-room in the mask. I was her Hearer; two days before, she knelt where you will kneel, and what she brought me I carry, and I will not set it down, not for the Sergeant and not for you.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, marrick_dead). Assert knows(actor, ch_her_hearer). }
  }
  Topic ch_ansel_gull with chaplain "Ask Father Ansel about the stranger on the steps" when wears(actor, face_gull) and publicHours() and not ch_buried(actor) and ch_body_here(actor) once {
    Says "'You are the Gull. Then you will have seen what the Hospice left on my step in a sheet.' His voice goes very quiet. 'The Concord does not allow me to bury him. He is a Bare; he was nobody in life; I am not able to make him anybody in death. He has a number. Nine. Nine of them have gone into the Cuff since the Novena began, and nobody has said a word over any, because nobody was there to be said over.' He looks at the sheet. 'He has a boot,' he says. 'I did not look in it. I could not bear to be the one who knew.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ch_boot_hint). }
  }
  Discovery ch_boot_hint "A dead Bare lies in a Hospice sheet on the Chapel steps; the Concord will not let the Chaplain bury him, and Father Ansel has not been able to bear looking in his boot.".
  Topic ch_ansel_owl with chaplain "Ask Father Ansel about the Chapel's lamps" when wears(actor, face_owl) and publicHours() once {
    Says "'The Owls,' he says, with relief; it is a trade he can talk to. 'The Chapel's wicks are trimmed by a lamp-boy, one of your steward's, of an evening. A little thing, very quick, who will not look at the Hearer; I believe he thinks I am a ghost. He has not come since the night the Registrar,' and he stops, and starts again, 'since the night of the Hearing's postponement. Treen. A good name for a trimmer. If you see his mother, tell her the lamps are all right.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ch_boy_known). }
  }
  Discovery ch_boy_known "Pip Treen, a lamp-boy of the Owls' steward, trimmed the Chapel's wicks of an evening and has not been seen here since the night the Registrar died; his mother thinks he went down with the lamp-boys.".

  // The verger has been told to leave the floor and so knows what is on it. He tells a face that does a little work.
  Topic ch_jonas_floor with ch_verger "Ask Jonas Heddle why Father said to leave the floor" when masked(actor) and publicHours() once {
    Says "'Because of what's on it.' He climbs down off the stool, slowly, as if a lamp might hear. 'I came back from the Row at nine, the night it was. The Registrar had sent me with a note. Father was standing at that door with his hand on the latch and he did not open it, and he did not take his hand away. I said, Father. He said, Jonas, leave it as it is.' He rubs his thumb along his apron. 'Nine nights. I'd have swept it the first morning. I have a pan of what was on the floor, because I am a verger, and I took it.' He looks at you. 'I have not told Father I took it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ch_jonas_pan). }
  }
  Discovery ch_jonas_pan "Jonas Heddle, the verger, swept up what lay on the floor of the lamp-room doorway on the night the Registrar died, against orders, and has kept it in a pan; he has not told Father Ansel.".
  Topic ch_jonas_floor_night with ch_verger "Ask Jonas Heddle why Father said to leave the floor" when privateHours() and not masked(actor) and at(ch_verger, nave) once {
    Says "He is putting out the last of the lamps with a snuffer on a pole, and does not look round. 'After the Ninth Bell a bare face is only a face,' says Jonas Heddle, 'and I'll say to it what I wouldn't say to a mask. There's a thing in a pan in the lamp-cupboard that Father told me to leave on the floor. I didn't. A verger can't. I swept up what the broom could reach and I have it still.' He puts out a lamp. 'Come by in the day with a face on, and help me trim, and I'll give it you. I can't be seen giving it to a Bare. That is not the Concord; that is Mistress Odell.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ch_jonas_pan). }
  }
  Relation ch_jonas_helped(group).
  Action ch_help_jonas(actor: group, site: place) "Help Jonas Heddle trim the Novena lamps, an hour" {
    Speaker ch_verger.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ch_verger, site) and at(actor, nave) and masked(actor) and publicHours() and knows(actor, ch_jonas_pan) and not ch_jonas_helped(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert ch_jonas_helped(actor). Assert knows(actor, ch_cooper). Assert knows(actor, ch_boy_known). Give ch_curls to actor. }
    Result "You hold the ladder and pass up the wicks, and by the fourth lamp he has stopped explaining what he is doing and started explaining why. At the end of the hour he takes a pan out of the lamp-cupboard, with a tin lid on it, and puts it in your hands without a word. Oak curls, pale and sweet, and with them a smell that is not the Chapel's at all: brine, and a fire made of shavings. 'And the Treen boy, that trims for the Owls,' he says, to the ladder. 'He's not been in since the night. His mother says he's gone down with the lamp-boys. I should not like to be the one to say it was for something he saw.'".
  }
  Kind ch_curls_kind "a pan of oak shavings" is gear worth 0 weighing 1 described "Curls of white oak, an inch across and as fine as lace, with a smell of brine and charred wood. Someone has been shaving staves, and has done it for years: each curl is cut to the same bevel.".
  Item ch_curls "a pan of oak shavings" is ch_curls_kind at offstage.

  // ── The Lamp-Room ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Where Ysolde Marrick died, at her lamp-table, between one office and the next. Father Ansel has had it left as it
  // was. The evening is in the room: three visitors, each of whom lit a taper at her candle, as the Chapel's courtesy
  // asks of anyone who comes to the Registrar, and put it out in their own way. What each of the seven readings finds
  // is true; none of them finds all of it. Looking closely at the three stubs and nothing else gives a story that
  // reads cleanly and is wrong in a useful way: that the last to leave, who arranged her, is the one who killed her.
  Observe ch_lamp_public at lamp_room when publicHours() "A narrow room under the north windows, smelling of lamp-oil, cold wax and, very faintly, of a candle that was put out in a hurry. Lamps without chimneys hang from the beams on hooks, like fruit on a wall, and wicks in boxes line one shelf. A door on the east side goes through to the bier-room, and is shut. Everything here has been left exactly as it was found, and the room knows it.".
  Observe ch_lamp_private at lamp_room when privateHours() "At night the lamp-room has only the light you bring. The lamps hang unlit in the dark above the table and give back nothing. The rain is louder here than in the nave, because the roof is lower and the window is cracked along one pane, and somebody has pushed a rag into the crack.".
  Observe ch_lamp_death at lamp_room when true "This is where the Registrar of Ombra died: the lamp-room of the Chapel of the Bare Face, where she sat on the nights she was not walking the streets." teaches marrick_dead.

  Thing lamp_table "the lamp-table" at lamp_room {
    State as_found "A long table of black oak for trimming wicks, scarred with the rings of cups, with a high-backed chair at its head and a plain visitor's chair pulled out in front of it, square, as for someone who was expected. Wax has run over the table's edge in long falls and set, layer on layer, like candlework on a cake.".
  }
  Thing ch_tapers "three candle-stubs in the visitors' holders" at lamp_room {
    State as_found "Three iron holders stand in a row on the table's end, and in each the stub of a taper: one burned very low, one hardly at all, one halfway.".
  }
  Thing ch_hooks "the mask-hooks by the door" at lamp_room {
    State as_found "Two iron hooks by the bier-room door, where a visitor might hang a mask who had been asked to be received bare. One is worn bright. On the other, a thread hangs.".
  }
  Thing ch_floor "the floor by the door" at lamp_room {
    State as_found "The boards by the door are cleaner than the rest of the floor. Somebody has swept here, once, and then been stopped.".
  }
  Thing ch_under "the dark under the lamp-table" at lamp_room {
    State as_found "Under the table, where the wax has run down the leg in a long fall and pooled on the boards, the dark is thicker than it need be.".
  }
  Thing ch_cord "a cut end of white silk cord" at lamp_room {
    State as_found "At the foot of the high-backed chair lies a short end of white silk cord, cut clean, with a flat black knot at one end.".
  }

  Observe ch_tapers_quick at lamp_room when tried(ch_tapers, looking) and not knows(party, ch_quick_reading) and not knows(party, ch_order) "You count them again, because the number is the point. Three visitors, then, and the burn-lengths to say how long each stayed: one for an hour, one for a breath, one for the time it takes to do something with your hands. The last of them put out his light with a clean pinch and went on after the others, to judge by the wax; and on the table beside the high chair, where the Registrar sat, lies the cut end of a cord. It reads like a page: two men quarrelling at her table, a third who comes after, ties her mask straight, and goes out with the Book. Whoever came last, you think, is the man who killed her, or the man who most wanted it hid." teaches ch_quick_reading.
  Discovery ch_quick_reading "The lamp-room's three candle-stubs say three visitors came the Registrar's last evening, and the last to leave straightened her mask and took the Book: the clerk, then, whom the others only quarrelled with, is the one to look for.".
  Observe ch_hooks_look at lamp_room when tried(ch_hooks, looking) and not knows(party, serene_saw) "The thread on the second hook is red-gold, silk, the thickness of a hair, and looks like something torn from the edge of a ribbon. It has nothing to say that you can find.".
  Observe ch_floor_look at lamp_room when tried(ch_floor, looking) and not knows(party, ch_cooper) "Between two boards, where the broom did not go, there is a little pale grit: wood, or what was once wood.".
  Observe ch_under_look at lamp_room when tried(ch_under, looking) and not knows(party, ch_child) "Wax lies in a flat white pool on the boards beneath the table, and in its skin there is a mark you take at first for a dropped glove.".
  Observe ch_table_look at lamp_room when tried(lamp_table, looking) and not knows(party, ch_glove) "Along the table's edge at the head, in the layers of old wax, there is a scratch: four small points in a row, each cut deep, close as the teeth of a comb.".
  Observe ch_cord_look at lamp_room when tried(ch_cord, looking) and not knows(party, ch_knot) "A silk cord with a flat black clerk's tape tied round one end. It might be nothing; it is the sort of thing a room has.".

  // Seven readings, each by a different skill, each needing the thing to have been looked at first. Wrong or failed, a
  // reading is only a reading that has not come yet: it costs half an hour and may be tried again.
  Action ch_read_tapers(actor: group, site: place) "Read the candle-stubs, and where each visitor stood" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lamp_room) and tried(ch_tapers, looking) and not knows(actor, ch_order).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ch_order). }
    Result "You stand in the room as each of them stood. The wax says it: the first fall lies thickest on the floor in front of the table, in a long line, and the man who made it paced; he could not keep still for an hour, and she did not once get up. The second visitor never came past the door-sill; his taper has hardly burned, and it was blown, not pinched, in the breath of someone who could not wait to be out. The third sat, in the visitor's chair, and the taper he lit is burned to the middle: he stayed to do something, and did it carefully. And at the head of the table, the Registrar's own candle, which she would have trimmed every quarter-hour of her life, has burned down untrimmed into its own pool from the hour the first visitor went: no hand touched it after him.".
    Otherwise "You read the room as you would read a face and it gives you what it gives anyone: three candles, three visitors, a sense of weight. You cannot make it say which came when.".
  }
  Discovery ch_order "Three people came to the Registrar's lamp-room that evening, one after another: the first paced the floor for an hour while she sat; the second never came past the threshold and blew out his taper and fled; the third sat in the visitor's chair and stayed to do something with care.".
  Action ch_read_glove(actor: group, site: place) "Read the scratch in the wax at the head of the table" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lamp_room) and tried(lamp_table, looking) and not knows(actor, ch_glove).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, trapwork, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ch_glove). }
    Result "Four points in a row at a finger's span: you have seen this scratch before, or its kind, on every lock in a strongroom. It is the stud-plate of a ward-glove, the old Office pattern cut with pins to turn the wards of a lock without a key. Nobody wears it but a Warden of Locks in his Office. He laid his hand on the table, hard, at the head, where the Registrar's own hand would lie, and leaned.".
    Otherwise "A scratch in wax. You turn your head to it from each side and it is a scratch in wax.".
  }
  Discovery ch_glove "A Warden of Locks' ward-glove, with a stud-plate of four pins, scored the lamp-table's edge at the head, where the Registrar's own hand would lie: the Warden of Locks stood over her and leaned on her table.".
  Action ch_read_flake(actor: group, site: place) "Read the thread on the second mask-hook" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lamp_room) and tried(ch_hooks, looking) and not knows(actor, serene_saw).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, serene_saw). }
    Result "Red-gold silk, a hair thick, with a fleck of gilt at the end of it like a scale: leaf-gold laid on lacquer, which breaks off when a mask is knocked against a post. Only one mask in Ombra is gilded, because only one is made to be looked at from across a square. The Serene's cord snapped on this hook; the Serene came into the Registrar's lamp-room that night, and did not stay to mend it.".
    Otherwise "A thread. It is very pretty, red and gold. You know that it is from a mask, and you do not know which.".
  }
  Action ch_read_shavings(actor: group, site: place) "Read what the broom did not reach by the door" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lamp_room) and tried(ch_floor, looking) and not knows(actor, ch_cooper).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ch_cooper). }
    Result "White oak, shaved fine, seasoned in brine and fire: the curls of a cooper's drawknife, carried on a cuff. The Chapel is not made of oak and no one in the Chapel works it. A man who makes barrels for a living stood at this door in his work-coat and did not go in.".
    Otherwise "Wood, you decide, and then, very sure of it, that it is a different wood from the floor's; and no more.".
  }
  Discovery ch_cooper "White oak shavings, seasoned in brine, lay at the lamp-room door: a cooper stood there in his work-coat, and did not go in.".
  Action ch_read_hand(actor: group, site: place) "Read the mark in the wax under the table" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lamp_room) and tried(ch_under, looking) and not knows(actor, ch_child).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, mending, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ch_child). }
    Result "Not a glove. A hand, the right, pressed flat into the wax while it was soft and then held there until it cooled; the print goes down to the whorls. A child's, nine or ten years: the thumb is bitten to the quick, the palm has the small hard places a boy gets from wick-snips, and a rim of lamp-oil shines along the fingers still. Whoever it was lay under the table through all three visits, and put the hand down to keep it from shaking, and did not dare to lift it. The small bare feet went out last, toward the lamp-stair, running.".
    Otherwise "You cannot make it more than a smear. It is warm in the room, and you are tired, and a thing under a table is only a thing under a table.".
  }
  Discovery ch_child "A child of nine or ten, with the hands of a wick-trimmer, lay under the lamp-table through all three visits with a hand pressed into the wax to keep it still, and ran out by the lamp-stair afterward.".
  Action ch_read_cord(actor: group, site: place) "Read the knot on the cut cord" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lamp_room) and tried(ch_cord, looking) and not knows(actor, ch_knot).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, mending, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ch_knot). }
    Result "The white silk was the cord of a mask. It was cut with a small sharp blade, close to the lacing, to take the mask off a face that was past helping; and then it was tied again with a clerk's tape, in a flat knot that will lie under a pillow, in the order a man ties a thing he cannot bear to hurt. He retied her mask, and left the cut end because he could not bring himself to burn it. He did it after she was past help. The knot has no hurry in it at all.".
    Otherwise "A cord and a knot. A knot is a knot to you, and this one says nothing yet.".
  }
  Discovery ch_knot "The Registrar's mask-cord was cut and then retied with a clerk's tape in a flat, careful knot, after she was past help, by someone who did not want her seen and did not hurry.".

  // The evening, assembled: what the room says when all of it is read. It replaces the quick reading: the last visitor
  // was not a murderer but a clerk who covered a woman's face.
  Rule ch_evening_read when knows(party, ch_order) and knows(party, ch_glove) and knows(party, serene_saw) and knows(party, ch_cooper) and knows(party, ch_child) and knows(party, ch_knot) and not knows(party, ch_evening)
    says "You lay them in a row as you would lay out the stitches of a hem, and the evening gets up and walks. The Registrar sat in her lamp-room with the Novena three days off. The Warden of Locks came first, in his ward-glove, and for an hour he paced and she sat, and he said what he had come to say; she did not rise. The cooper came second, in the Serene's mask, and stood at the door and saw her face, and ran, and blew his taper out in terror. A child lay under the table through all of it. The clerk came last, sat in the visitor's chair, cut her mask free and retied it as kindly as a man can, and took the Book; he did not kill her; she was dead before he came. Nobody killed her. Three people were each, for an hour, the worst thing that happened to her night." teaches ch_evening { }
  Discovery ch_evening "The Registrar's last evening, read from the lamp-room: the Warden of Locks came first and paced an hour in a ward-glove over her; the cooper in the Serene's mask came second and fled; a boy lay under the table; and the clerk came last, retied her mask with a clerk's tape and took the Book; she had been dead since the Warden went.".
  Observe ch_evening_known at lamp_room when knows(party, ch_evening) "You know the room now. The visitor's chair is a clerk's chair, the table a Warden's, the doorway a cooper's, and the dark under the table a child's, and you cannot look at any of them without seeing the person who was there.".

  // What the room proves, and what it needs to be put with: the glove and Father Ansel's ear through the door; the child
  // and a name for the child. Neither the room nor the confessional alone makes either, but both can be had without the seal.
  Topic ch_ansel_heard with chaplain "Ask Father Ansel what he heard through the lamp-room door" when privateHours() and not masked(actor) and at(chaplain, vestry) and (ch_ansel_trusts(actor) or knows(actor, ch_evening) or ch_buried(actor)) and not knows(actor, ch_threat) once {
    Says "He is silent so long that you think he has gone to sleep. 'A Warden's voice,' he says. 'I know the cant: by the Key and by the Lock. I did not see him. I did not leave the nave. He said a name aloud.' He covers his mouth with his hand. 'I will not say it either, do you understand. In the Chapel. I heard him say a woman's name, slowly, like reading a price, and say that he would say it again in the Row at noon, unless the Rounds were called off. She said: Say it. And he said it again, louder, and again, and after that I did not hear her answer, and I told myself that was the rain.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ch_threat). }
  }
  Discovery ch_threat "Father Ansel heard a Warden of Locks, through the lamp-room door, say a woman's name aloud three times and threaten to cry it in the Row at noon unless the Registrar's Rounds were called off; she answered, Say it.".
  Action ch_press_ansel(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Father Ansel, with your whole attention, what he has not been able to say" {
    Speaker chaplain.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(chaplain, site) and at(actor, vestry) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and not knows(actor, ch_threat) and not ch_pressed(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ch_threat). Assert ch_ansel_trusts(actor). Assert ch_pressed(actor). }
    On failure { Assert ch_pressed(actor). }
    Result "You do not push. You sit on the other stool and look at the fire that is not lit, and you see what is wrong with the silence: it has the shape of something he heard, and is not the shape of something he did. 'I was in the nave,' he says. 'I was not asked to hear it. I heard it. There is no seal on what a man hears with his ears,' and he tells you, with his hand over his mouth.".
    Otherwise "He lets you wait, and takes it kindly, and says the Chapel is a quiet house and he is a quiet man. You have the sense of having stood before a door that was already ajar and pushed it shut.".
  }
  Relation ch_pressed(group).
  Rule ch_warden_proved when knows(party, ch_glove) and knows(party, ch_threat) and not knows(party, lacke_unfaced)
    says "The glove and the voice agree. The Warden of Locks stood over the Registrar in her lamp-room, in his ward-glove, and said her name aloud; the Chaplain heard it through the door. You did not hear it from anyone under a seal, and you may say it to anyone." teaches lacke_unfaced { }
  Rule ch_boy_named when knows(party, ch_child) and (knows(party, rounds_known) or knows(party, ch_boy_known)) and not knows(party, pip_saw)
    says "A boy of nine under the table, with a trimmer's calluses; a lamp-boy of the Owls' steward who has not been to the Chapel since; a ledger with a P. T. and a word, cisterns, beside it. It is the same child. He lay under the table, and saw all three, and has hidden since in the cisterns under the Drip." teaches pip_saw { }

  // ── The stranger on the steps ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A Bare died at the Hospice on the fifth night of nobody's attention, and by the Concord's usage the Hospice leaves its
  // dead on the Chapel steps in a sheet to be carried to the water. The Chapel may not bury him, for he is nobody. He
  // has a boot. If nobody does anything, the porter tips him into the Cuff on the fourth morning and nobody says a word.
  Kind ch_body_kind "the dead stranger, in a Hospice sheet" is gear worth 0 weighing 6 described "A man of fifty or so in a grey Hospice sheet, tied at the feet and the neck with tape, a tag sewn to the corner: NINE. He is lighter than he looks, which is a thing the living do not like to learn.".
  Item ch_body "the dead stranger" is ch_body_kind at chapel_steps.
  Observe ch_body_laid at chapel_steps when at(ch_body, chapel_steps) and publicHours() "Under the lee of the third step, where the water stairs begin, a long shape lies in a grey Hospice sheet, tagged NINE, with the rain running off it in lines. The masked people on the steps have arranged themselves so that none of them is standing within a yard of it.".
  Observe ch_body_night at chapel_steps when at(ch_body, chapel_steps) and privateHours() "Someone has put a saucer with a stub of tallow on the step by the sheet, and the rain has put it out.".
  Observe ch_body_gone at chapel_steps when ch_buried(party) and not at(ch_body, chapel_steps) "The lowest step is clean, and a darker patch where the sheet lay is already going pale.".
  Relation ch_buried(group). Relation ch_cuffed(group). Measure ch_burial_way(group).
  // The stranger is still to be buried: on the steps, or in the company's arms.
  Query ch_body_here(c: group) means at(ch_body, chapel_steps) or carries(c, ch_body).
  Rule ch_porter when day(clock) == 4 and hour(clock) >= 6 and at(ch_body, chapel_steps) and not ch_buried(party) and not ch_cuffed(party)
    says "At first light a Hospice porter in a cape comes down the Chapel steps with a hand-barrow and does what the Concord's usage asks: he tips the stranger off the bottom step into the Cuff, tag and all, as one empties a bucket, and walks away. No one on the steps looks up. Father Ansel stands in the Chapel door in his veil, and does not move, and does not speak." {
    Retract at(ch_body, chapel_steps). Assert ch_cuffed(party). }
  Action ch_open_boot(actor: group, site: place) "Look in the dead stranger's boot" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ch_body, site) and not knows(actor, ch_stranger_name).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ch_stranger_name). }
    Result "Folded small in the left boot, under the insole, in a waxed paper: a card, in a hand that wrote as it was taught to, and then more slowly. EDRIC SALT, CHANDLER, OF WENNICK. I WAS NINE DAYS IN THIS CITY AND NOBODY SAID MY NAME. IF I DIE HERE, CRY IT ONCE, ALOUD, IN A SQUARE, AS IF I WERE SOMEBODY. IT IS ALL I ASK. THE REST YOU MAY DO AS YOU LIKE.".
  }
  Discovery ch_stranger_name "The dead Bare on the Chapel steps was Edric Salt, a chandler of Wennick, who left in his boot a card asking that his name be cried once, aloud, in a square, as if he were somebody; the rest of him they might do as they liked.".

  // First way: by rite. Father Ansel will lend the stole to a Hearer who asks for it, though he cannot be seen to use it.
  Topic ch_ansel_stole with chaplain "Ask Father Ansel for the burial stole" when hearer(actor) and knows(actor, ch_stranger_name) and at(ch_body, chapel_steps) and not ch_stole(actor) once {
    Says "He does not ask what for. He goes to the press in the vestry, and comes back with a narrow band of grey wool, worn shiny, and holds it a moment before he gives it over. 'I may not be seen to lend it,' he says. 'There is a bench at the foot of the water stairs. The Concord has nothing to say about what a stranger may do on a bench.' He puts the stole into your hands, and closes his over them. 'I shall be at my prayers. I shall be at my prayers with my back to the steps, as is my custom.'".
    On discuss { Assert ch_stole(actor). }
  }
  Relation ch_stole(group).
  Action ch_bury_rite(actor: group, site: place) "Read the office over the stranger, in Father Ansel's stole, and let him down into the water" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ch_body, site) and at(actor, chapel_steps) and ch_stole(actor) and knows(actor, ch_stranger_name) and not ch_buried(actor).
    Grave "A Bare is given to the Cuff; it takes him, and he is not seen again. You will have said his name over him, once, quietly, and the rite is the only thing of yours that will go down with him.".
    Time 6.
    Resolve check(actor, rites, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert ch_buried(actor). Retract at(ch_body, site). Set ch_burial_way(actor) to 1. Assert ch_ansel_trusts(actor). }
    Result "You say it at the foot of the water stairs with the stole round your neck and the rain on the page you do not need: the office for the dead who are not to be mourned, the shortest in the book, and you lengthen it with his name, Edric Salt, chandler, of Wennick, said low, once, in the voice you would use for something that might still wake. The masked people on the steps look away with their whole bodies. Behind you, in the Chapel, a Hearer is at his prayers with his back to the steps. You let him down into the Cuff, and it takes him as it takes everything, without comment.".
    Otherwise "The words will not come in their order. The rain gets into the book, and your voice, which you wanted to be level, comes out as a clerk's reading a will. You stop before the end, because to go on would be to do it badly, and he deserves better than that, and so, God help you, does the Concord.".
  }

  // Second way: by night, in the reeds. The Chaplain looks away; the ground is the question.
  Topic ch_ansel_prayers with chaplain "Tell Father Ansel that you mean to take the stranger to the reeds tonight" when privateHours() and not masked(actor) and at(chaplain, vestry) and knows(actor, ch_stranger_name) and ch_body_here(actor) and not ch_leave(actor) once {
    Says "'I did not hear that.' He puts his veil over his face, as if it were a handkerchief, and takes it away again. 'I pray until the Fourth Bell, with my back to the steps, and the door is not locked, because there is nothing in this Chapel worth the locking. The reeds,' he says, 'hold nothing in the Rains. If you must go, go where a heron stands. A heron does not stand where the ground is going to go.'".
    On discuss { Assert ch_leave(actor). Assert knows(actor, ch_heron_ground). }
  }
  Relation ch_leave(group).
  Discovery ch_heron_ground "Father Ansel says the Heronry's reeds hold nothing in the Rains, and that a grave should be dug where a heron stands, since a heron does not stand where the ground will go.".
  Relation ch_firm(group). Relation ch_floated(group).
  Action ch_sound_ground(actor: group, site: place) "Find the firm ground in the reeds, where a heron would stand" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, reed_path) and not ch_firm(actor).
    Time 6.
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert ch_firm(actor). }
    Result "You follow the herons. Not the birds: their places, a slope of tussock a hand above the water where six or seven reeds have stood for a hundred years, and the mud under them takes the pole and holds it. It will hold the Rains. It will hold, you think, the rest of the century.".
    Otherwise "Every tussock looks as firm as another, and each gives under the pole a little differently, and the water comes up in the hole you dig to try it. You cannot tell the ground that will hold from the ground that will not.".
  }
  Action ch_bury_reeds(actor: group, site: place) "Bury the stranger in the reeds by night, and say nothing about it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, reed_path) and carries(actor, ch_body) and ch_leave(actor) and knows(actor, ch_stranger_name) and privateHours() and not ch_buried(actor).
    Grave "A Bare in the reeds is in the Heronry's ground, and the Heronry is under a writ; whatever the reeds do with him, they will have been the ones to do it.".
    Time 12.
    Resolve check(actor, digging, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert ch_buried(actor). Spend ch_body from actor. Set ch_burial_way(actor) to 2. }
    Result "You carry him the last quarter-mile on your back, because the reed path will take no barrow, and the lantern you did not bring is a thing you are glad of. The hole takes an hour and a half. He goes in on his side with the card in his boot and the sheet over his face, and you lay the turf back as you found it and pat it, which is a foolish thing to do and which you do twice. A heron somewhere in the dark lifts one foot, and puts it down.".
    Otherwise "The spade goes down a foot and finds water, and the water comes up to meet it. By the second hole you are knee-deep and the stranger is lying on the path in his sheet with the rain on his face; and you say a thing you will not be repeating in a Chapel.".
  }
  Rule ch_reeds_float when day(clock) >= 6 and ch_burial_way(party) == 2 and not ch_firm(party) and not ch_floated(party)
    says "On the sixth day, in the Flood, a reed-cutter finds a grey sheet at the edge of the Heronry, tagged NINE, as clean as a pebble, and without a word fetches it back to the Hospice by the water-gate, on a hurdle. The Hospice porter will tip him in the Cuff tomorrow. It is not your fault, and it is." {
    Assert ch_floated(party). }

  // Third way: a ferryman carries what is left on the water stairs, for the name, and will not carry what has none.
  Topic ch_rill_body with rill "Ask Rill to carry the stranger out on the Cuff, as a ferryman's cargo" when wears(actor, face_gull) and publicHours() and carries(actor, ch_body) and knows(actor, ch_stranger_name) and not ch_buried(actor) once {
    Says "Rill Ketch looks at the sheet in your arms and at the Gull on your face, and at the Gull on her own, and then not at anything. 'A Gull carries what is left on the water, and doesn't say.' She is already moving the boat-hook. 'What's the name?' You tell her. 'Edric Salt,' she says, to the water, not loud. 'Wennick. There's a Wennick on the bank where the delta goes out, a stone and a post. I take them past the bar on the ebb.' She puts out a hand, not for coin. 'Give him here. And don't thank me. I'm not doing it for you. I'm doing it for the Gull.'".
    On discuss { Assert ch_buried(actor). Spend ch_body from actor. Set ch_burial_way(actor) to 3. Increase goodwill(face_gull) by 1. Assert ch_rill_carried(actor). }
  }
  Relation ch_rill_carried(group).
  Topic ch_tibb_cellar with tibb "Ask Mother Tibb to keep the dead man in the Hospice cellar until he can be buried" when knows(actor, ch_boot_hint) and not ch_buried(actor) and ch_body_here(actor) once {
    Says "'A sheet is not a bed.' She does not raise her voice; she has never needed to. 'The Hospice has nine beds and eleven Strangers and a rule, and the rule says the dead go to the Chapel steps by the third bell after, so that the beds may be turned. If I keep him I must turn a living man out, and I will not have a living man in the rain for a dead one. He has had his bed.' A pause. 'He had it nine nights. It was the best I had.'".
  }

  // The name cried: the request in the boot, and the thing the city fears done kindly. A Bare may Name, so it costs the
  // company nothing if it comes as nobody; a masked company that names a name aloud is Named, and the Watch counts it,
  // since it cannot tell a dead man's name from a living one's.
  Relation ch_name_cried(group).
  Action ch_cry_name(actor: group, site: place) "Cry the stranger's name aloud on the Chapel steps, as he asked" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapel_steps) and publicHours() and knows(actor, ch_stranger_name) and not ch_name_cried(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert ch_name_cried(actor). Assert ch_ansel_trusts(actor). }
    Result "You go up three steps, to where you can be seen, and say it as loud as you can: EDRIC SALT, CHANDLER, OF WENNICK. It goes out over the steps like a coin dropped in a well and every masked head turns, because every one of them has been told since birth what is done to a name in a square, and has just heard one cried for nothing. A woman in a Cockle's domino puts her hand to her mouth. A Heron-cowled clerk sits down on the step where he is. Nobody does anything. After a moment the verger, inside, rings the one small bell he rings for the Novena, once. Then everyone goes on.".
  }
  Rule ch_cry_heat when ch_name_cried(party) and masked(party) and not ch_heat_noted(party) says "A domino of the Watch has come up the steps, and stands looking at you, and writes something, and goes away. A name said aloud by a masked face is a name said aloud, and the Watch has no way to tell a stranger's from a neighbour's. It will count it." {
    Increase heat(party) by 1. Assert ch_heat_noted(party). }
  Relation ch_heat_noted(group).
  Observe ch_candle_steps at chapel_steps when ch_name_cried(party) and privateHours() "On the lowest step, in a saucer, a taper burns for Edric Salt; and another has been lit from it beside it. Nobody is there. The rain has not got them out.".
  Observe ch_candle_nave at nave when ch_name_cried(party) and publicHours() "Someone has hung a plain oval of unpainted wood on the wall of the nave, among the rest, with a ribbon on it, and written nothing on it at all.".

  // ── The Offices the children forget ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Chapel's choir rehearses the Nineteen Offices for the ninth night. Every child forgets the Assessor of Weights,
  // whose Office is the Pound and is addressed by it, and so has no line of its own; the litany goes from the Key to
  // the Measures in a gap like a missing tooth. Mistress Odell has tried everything except noticing.
  Observe ch_choir_rehearsal at nave when at(ch_choir, nave) and not ch_choir_ready(party) "The children sing the Offices in the flat voice of a drill: the Treasurer, the Warden of Locks, the Key, the Master of Measures; and in the place between the Key and the Measures, where the Assessor of Weights should be, there is a rest of exactly the length of a held breath. The smallest of them moves her lips on it, hopefully, and gives up.".
  Observe ch_choir_ready_scene at nave when at(ch_choir, nave) and ch_choir_ready(party) "The children sing the Offices from the Treasurer to the Registrar, all nineteen, and the Pound comes in its place between the Key and the Measures, short, a quarter-beat, and the smallest of them takes it on the nose. Mistress Odell does not look up from her fork.".
  Relation ch_choir_ready(group). Relation ch_corrow_asked(group).
  Topic ch_corrow_gap with ch_corrow "Ask Mistress Odell why the children skip a line of the litany" when masked(actor) and publicHours() and at(ch_corrow, nave) and not ch_corrow_asked(actor) once {
    Says "'They don't skip it.' She strikes the fork on the pulpit. 'They have never been taught it. The Assessor of Weights is the Pound. The Offices are addressed by their masks, and the Pound is a thing a child can hold in her hand and has never seen. They are asked to sing a Pound.' She stops. 'Nobody has been able to tell me what it sounds like, and I am not a woman to guess. The Drawing is in nine days. The Offices sing to the Urn; an Office that is not sung is not, I am told, strictly drawn.'".
    On discuss { Assert ch_corrow_asked(actor). Assert knows(actor, ch_litany_gap). }
  }
  Discovery ch_litany_gap "The Chapel's children cannot sing the Assessor of Weights in the litany of the Nineteen Offices, because the Office is the Pound, addressed by its mask, and no one has told them what a Pound sounds like.".
  Action ch_teach_pound(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the children what a Pound is: an ounce short, and everyone knows it" {
    Speaker ch_corrow.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ch_corrow, site) and ch_corrow_asked(actor) and not ch_choir_ready(actor).
    Time 6.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert ch_choir_ready(actor). Assert knows(actor, ch_pound_sung). }
    Result "You tell them what the Pound is: that it is a lump of brass in a locked room, and has been wrong, to anyone who has weighed against it, since before their grandmothers. That the bakers curse it, and love it, and it is short by a very little. 'So the Pound is a short beat,' says the smallest one, at once. 'A quarter.' Mistress Odell strikes the fork on the pulpit, and it does not make a noise she approves of, and the children sing the whole of the Offices from the Treasurer to the Registrar without a gap, and she says nothing for a long moment. 'A quarter,' she says, as though it had been her own idea.".
    Otherwise "You explain it, and it is an explanation: weights, and measures, and a standard. The children listen with the faces of children being told how much their dinner cost. The smallest of them says, 'Is it big?', and Mistress Odell says 'From the Locks,' and they sing the gap again.".
  }
  Action ch_sweeten_choir(actor: group, site: place) "Promise the children honeyed almonds from the Row, if they get through the Offices once without a gap" {
    Speaker ch_corrow.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ch_corrow, site) and ch_corrow_asked(actor) and not ch_choir_ready(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 2.
    Time 3.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Assert ch_choir_ready(actor). Assert knows(actor, ch_pound_sung). }
    Result "Nine faces turn to you with a unanimity the Offices have never got from them. 'Anyone who does it without a gap,' says Mistress Odell, without waiting, 'may name what is in the bag.' They do it on the third try, with the Assessor sung as a gasp, and the smallest, who has been shown the Pound as a thing you gasp at, gasps it so hard she is sick in the font. It is not what she meant. It is correct.".
  }
  Discovery ch_pound_sung "The Chapel's children sing the Assessor of Weights, the Pound, as a quarter-beat short, between the Key and the Measures.".

  // ── Later effects ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What the Chapel does for a company that has been kind in it, and what it learns of one that has not.
  Observe ch_ansel_warm at nave when publicHours() and at(chaplain, nave) and ch_ansel_trusts(party) "Father Ansel, when he sees you come in under the arch, inclines his veil to you, which is an honour: he does it to the lamps.".
  Topic ch_ansel_thanks with chaplain "Thank Father Ansel for the stole" when masked(actor) and publicHours() and ch_burial_way(actor) == 1 once {
    Says "'There is nothing to thank.' He lowers his voice below the nave's. 'I should like it entered somewhere, in a hand that is not mine, that for one hour on the ninth day of the Novena a man called Edric Salt was buried with an office read over him by someone who knew his name. The ledger is for the Chapel's own. I shall put it in the margin, in pencil. A margin is a thing the Concord does not regulate.'".
  }

  // ── Milestones ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Milestone ch_m_lamp "read the Registrar's last evening from the lamp-room" worth 50 when knows(party, ch_evening).
  Milestone ch_m_burial "saw a stranger buried who would have gone into the Cuff unnamed" worth 50 when ch_buried(party).
  Milestone ch_m_name "cried a dead stranger's name on the Chapel steps" worth 25 when ch_name_cried(party).
  Milestone ch_m_choir "taught the Chapel's choir the Pound" worth 25 when ch_choir_ready(party).

  // ── What became of them ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule ch_fate_stranger_rite when newsHour() and ch_burial_way(party) == 1 once says "Of Edric Salt, a chandler of Wennick: he is in the Cuff off the Chapel steps, with an office read over him by someone who had his name, and the Chaplain has written it in pencil in the margin of the Chapel's ledger, where the Concord does not look." { }
  Rule ch_fate_stranger_reeds when newsHour() and ch_burial_way(party) == 2 and not ch_floated(party) once says "Of Edric Salt, a chandler of Wennick: he lies in the Heronry on the ground a heron stands on, with a card in his boot. The reeds have come over him. The herons stand there for no reason that anyone can give." { }
  Rule ch_fate_stranger_floated when newsHour() and ch_floated(party) once says "Of Edric Salt, a chandler of Wennick: the reeds gave him up in the Flood, and the Hospice porter tipped him into the Cuff on the seventh morning, as the usage required. Somebody had dug him a grave; and it is true that he was not nobody for a little while." { }
  Rule ch_fate_stranger_ferry when newsHour() and ch_rill_carried(party) and ch_burial_way(party) == 3 once says "Of Edric Salt, a chandler of Wennick: Rill Ketch took him past the bar on the ebb, and the ferrymen are said to have cried his name from the Gull's stern as the boat went out, in turn, quietly. She has told nobody that she did, and the Gulls have not forgotten." { }
  Rule ch_fate_stranger_cuffed when newsHour() and ch_cuffed(party) once says "Of the dead stranger on the Chapel steps, called Nine: the porter tipped him into the Cuff on the fourth morning, and the Chapel's door stayed open on the nave, and nobody ever learned what was in his boot." { }
  Rule ch_fate_name when newsHour() and ch_name_cried(party) once says "Of the name cried on the Chapel steps: it is said in the Drip, by people who were not there, that on the ninth day a name was shouted in the open and nobody was Named for it, and that this is the only time anyone in Ombra has heard it." { }
  Rule ch_fate_choir_sung when newsHour() and ch_choir_ready(party) once says "Of the children of the Chapel's choir: they sang the Nineteen Offices at the Drawing without a gap. The Pound came in a quarter-beat short, as it should, and the Assessor's mask, in the front row, was seen to flinch, and then to nod. Mistress Odell has been told by someone that it was the best she has ever done, and has said it was adequate." { }
  Rule ch_fate_choir_gap when newsHour() and not ch_choir_ready(party) once says "Of the children of the Chapel's choir: they sang the Nineteen Offices at the Drawing with a gap between the Key and the Measures the width of a door, and the city, which had not been told, assumed it was part of the form." { }
  Rule ch_fate_jonas when newsHour() and ch_jonas_helped(party) once says "Of Jonas Heddle, the Chapel's verger: he has swept the lamp-room floor, at last. Father Ansel stood in the door while he did it and did not say a word, and when he had finished said only, 'Thank you, Jonas.'" { }
  Rule ch_fate_ansel_warm when newsHour() and ch_ansel_trusts(party) and not cl_seal_broken(party) once says "Of Father Ansel, Hearer of the Chapel of the Bare Face: he went into the Drawing in his veil and came out of it without, and is said to be hearing again, from the bare side of the grille, in the evening, with the door open." { }
  Rule ch_fate_ansel_cold when newsHour() and not ch_ansel_trusts(party) and not cl_seal_broken(party) once says "Of Father Ansel, Hearer of the Chapel of the Bare Face: he is hearing again, behind the veil. The Novena lamps were kept lit by the verger, and the Chaplain lit nine candles of his own, one for each of the days, and said no prayer over them, for the first time in forty years." { }
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/cisterns.k:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The cisterns under the Drip ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The lamp-oil and rain-water of the poor islands are kept in a drowned brick cathedral that older engineers than
  // Ombra's built and Ombra's lamp-trimmers filled. Under the cistern the Brewers' Drain, which the Drip calls the
  // Ninefold for its turnings, goes down by five reaches to an Aenean pump and, below the pump, to the cellar under
  // the Urn Hall. It is passable for the first five days of the Novena, hard from the third, and shut for good by the
  // Flood on the sixth: the rains fill it from the top. Three lamp-boys hide in the den above it, and the youngest has
  // seen what no one may. Everything that is here is the Drip's own, and its masks are old and few: the dark is the
  // one place in Ombra where nobody has to be anybody. (Prefix ci_; the people are pip, ci_nell, ci_tobit.)

  // ── The Drain's rooms and ways ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The spine gives the foot of the steps, the oil-cistern, the den, the drain's mouth, the pump-chamber and the
  // cellar; the five reaches between the mouth and the pump are ours. (The spine's own stair from mouth to pump is shut
  // by a sump until the pump has run: the long way is the only way the first time.)
  Place ci_weir "the weir" is room within cisterns at 2, 1 underground.
  Place ci_slick "the oil gallery" is room within cisterns at 3, 1 underground.
  Place ci_eelrun "the eel-run" is room within cisterns at 3, 2 underground.
  Place ci_chimney "the Brewers' chimney" is room within cisterns at 2, 2 underground.
  Place ci_aenean "the Aenean stair-head" is room within pump_level at 0, 2 underground.
  Initially Assert unlit(cistern_head). Initially Assert unlit(cistern_hall). Initially Assert unlit(drain_mouth).
  Initially Assert unlit(ci_weir). Initially Assert unlit(ci_slick). Initially Assert unlit(ci_eelrun). Initially Assert unlit(ci_chimney).
  Initially Assert unlit(ci_aenean). Initially Assert unlit(pump_chamber). Initially Assert unlit(urn_cellar).
  Passage ci_weir_steps "the weir steps" is steps between drain_mouth and ci_weir taking 6 minutes.
  Passage ci_gallery_arch "the gallery arch" is arch between ci_weir and ci_slick.
  Passage ci_run_way "the run" is culvert between ci_slick and ci_eelrun taking 8 minutes.
  // Two ways on from the eel-run: through the water, which the eel keeps; and over it, by the ledge and the chimney.
  Passage ci_siphon_way "the Siphon" is crawl between ci_eelrun and ci_aenean taking 10 minutes.
  Passage ci_ledge_way "the ledge over the run" is passage between ci_eelrun and ci_chimney needing climbing or rope taking 8 minutes.
  Passage ci_chimney_way "the Brewers' chimney" is shaft between ci_chimney and ci_aenean needing climbing or rope.
  Passage ci_door_way "the Aenean door" is door between ci_aenean and pump_chamber.

  // ── The water ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Days one and two: the Drain runs knee-deep and the Siphon has an air-gap you can crawl. From the Deepening the rain
  // fills the Siphon to the roof, so that it is crossed under water (and hurts) unless the Aenean pump is working.
  // The sixth morning's Flood drowns the foot of the steps, and the Drain with it, for good.
  Hazard ci_undertow "the Drain's water, running" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless strength save against (12).".
  Hazard ci_drowning "the Siphon, under water" means "Deal (1d8) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (12).".
  Thing ci_water "the water in the Siphon" on ci_siphon_way is scenery {
    State ci_low "The Siphon is a low black arch with a hand's breadth of air under it and water to the wrists: it can be crawled.".
    State ci_high dangerous "The Siphon is full to the roof: whoever goes through goes through under water, by feel, holding what breath they have.".
    Hurts with ci_drowning when ci_high then ci_high.
  }
  Rule ci_siphon_fills when day(clock) >= 3 and hour(clock) >= 6 and state(ci_water, ci_low) and not state(ci_pump, ci_running)
    says "Somewhere below, in the dark, the water finds the roof of the Siphon and takes it, with a sound like a long swallow." { Assert state(ci_water, ci_high). }
  Rule ci_siphon_ebbs when state(ci_pump, ci_running) and state(ci_water, ci_high)
    says "Under the floor something thumps, slowly, and the water in the Drain goes down the walls in long sighs." { Assert state(ci_water, ci_low). }
  // The Flood. From the sixth morning the foot of the cistern steps is under, and what was below is a cistern full
  // to the arch. The boys have gone to higher ground before it comes; whoever is below is thrown out of it.
  Thing ci_flood "the water on the cistern steps" on cistern_down is scenery {
    State ci_shallow "The cistern steps go down into the dark between wet walls.".
    State ci_drowned blocking dangerous "Grey water stands in the stairwell to the fourth step from the top, with the Drip's rain falling into it in rings. Nothing goes down here for a week.".
  }
  Rule ci_flood_comes when day(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) >= 6 and state(ci_flood, ci_shallow) { Assert state(ci_flood, ci_drowned). }
  Rule ci_washed_out when state(ci_flood, ci_drowned) and within(party, cisterns) and not state(ci_hatch, ci_open)
    says "The note of the dripping changes. Then it is not dripping but pouring, and the dark is full of cold, and every wall you have been touching is moving. The Flood takes you off your feet and puts you down again a long way up, on your hands and knees on the cistern steps, coughing lamp-oil, with the Drip's rain coming down on your back like a blessing." {
    Assert strikes(ci_undertow, party). Assert at(party, cistern_steps). }
  // Above the hatch, in the Urn Hall, is somewhere the Flood does not take the company out of: it is a dry place for as
  // long as the hatch is shut.
  Rule ci_washed_up when state(ci_flood, ci_drowned) and within(party, cisterns) and state(ci_hatch, ci_open) and not at(party, urn_hall)
    says "The Flood comes up the Drain behind you with a noise like a crowd. You go up the hatch ladder with the water at your heels, and out, onto the floor of the Urn Hall, and it follows you." {
    Assert at(party, urn_hall). }
  // A hatch left open takes the Flood into the Urn Hall whoever is there to see it.
  Rule ci_hall_floods at urn_hall when state(ci_flood, ci_drowned) and state(ci_hatch, ci_open) and not ci_hall_wet(party)
    says "Water comes up through the cellar hatch in the Hall's floor, slowly, in a black skin, and spreads. It smells of lamp-oil and the Drain. The Hall will be held in it." { Assert ci_hall_wet(party). }
  Relation ci_hall_wet(group).

  // ── The foot of the steps, the oil-cistern, the den ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe ci_head_scene at cistern_head when true "The steps end in a landing of black brick, and the rain that follows you down the stairwell goes on past you in a thin steady rope, into a drain, into the dark, with a noise like somebody counting. The air is cold and sweet: tallow, wet stone, and lamp-oil laid up in the dark like wine. East, a low arch, and over its keystone a tally cut by someone's thumbnail, in nines.".
  Observe ci_head_deep at cistern_head as weather when day(clock) >= 3 and day(clock) < 6 "Somebody has laid planks over the two lowest steps, and the water has been up to them in the night and gone down again, leaving a tide-line of oil that shines like a bruise.".
  Observe ci_head_bell at cistern_head as ambience when privateHours() "Far above, through the grating, the Ninth Bell has rung, and in the dripping something has changed; it has the patience of a house that has taken its face off.".
  Observe ci_hall_scene at cistern_hall when true "A brick cathedral gone under: aisles of pillars standing in black oil and water, each aisle a lane of dark with its end lost, and the vaulting over it all sweating with the Drip's whole rain. The lamp-oil is kept in the nave, in a long still lake with a skin on it like a plum, and it breathes. The lamp-boys have run a ledge of planks along the pillars, and on one of them someone has cut TRIM, and under it, smaller, a boy's name that has been scratched out. A crawl goes off east under a low arch, and the Drain's mouth is south, through an iron gate somebody has propped open with a brick.".
  Observe ci_den_scene at lamp_boys_den when true "A low brick room off the oil-cistern's flank, dry, which is the whole of its virtue: a drift of sacking and sail in one corner, a row of wick-ends laid out on a plank like a rank of tiny soldiers, a rat's skull strung from a nail, a cracked tin kettle, and chalk on the brick, in three hands, counting something. At the far end the sacking has been drawn across in a way that looks careless, and is not. Somebody is breathing behind it, in the careful way of someone who has been told to.".
  Observe ci_den_lit at lamp_boys_den when knows(party, ci_boys_found) "A candle-stub burns on the kettle's lid, the only light in the cisterns that has not been brought down by a stranger. Three small shadows lie against the wall and do not move until they are spoken to.".
  Observe ci_mouth_scene at drain_mouth when true "The Drain begins as a square brick throat in the cistern's south wall, with an iron sluice-door hung from it by one hinge, and goes away into the dark with the water going the same way, a little faster than you want it to. Over the door, cut by hands that could count and had no use for names, a row of nine notches, and under the ninth the word REACH in a script that was old when the Brewers were young. The draught off the water is cold and smells of lamp-oil, and of something else that is much older.".
  Observe ci_mouth_low at drain_mouth as weather when state(ci_water, ci_low) "The Drain runs knee-deep and slow, brown with the Drip's silt, with a skin of oil on it that takes the light and gives it back in a rainbow nobody wanted.".
  Observe ci_mouth_deep at drain_mouth as weather when state(ci_water, ci_high) "The Drain runs thigh-deep and quick, and what it carries has stopped being silt and become the Drip's whole rain, going down to the lagoon in a hurry, as if it had remembered an appointment.".

  // ── The weir, with the lamp-rats ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Brewers left a coil of rope on the weir's rail for whoever came after, stiff with oil and sound: the way down
  // the Drain is not for the climber alone.
  Item ci_old_rope "a coil of the Brewers' rope" is rope at ci_weir.
  Observe ci_weir_scene at ci_weir when true "The first of the nine turnings: the Drain steps down over a weir of old brick with an iron rail along it worn bright by every hand that has needed it, and the water goes over in a brown glassy lip. The walls are honeycombed with holes the size of a fist, and in every hole something is awake. There is a smell of rat and, from the arch ahead, of something sweeter and more dangerous: lamp-oil, standing in the air.".
  Observe ci_weir_smell at ci_weir as feature when state(ci_fumes, ci_heavy) "The sweet smell from the gallery is strong enough to taste. A boy's chalk on the arch has been rubbed half out, and what is left says NO LITE, and a drawing of a flame with a line through it, and a drawing of a boy.".

  // ── The oil gallery ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Lamp-oil from the cistern's leak has run down the Drain's old overflow for years and lies on the gallery's low
  // water in a skin, and its fumes lie on the skin. A lit light carried into it goes off like a bell. Dark is safe; so
  // is no leak; so is a flame set to it from the weir, at a distance, which costs the Drip its oil.
  Hazard ci_flash "the fumes of the oil gallery, taking" means "Deal (2d6) fire damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  Thing ci_fumes "the fumes in the oil gallery" at ci_slick is scenery {
    State ci_heavy "The air in the gallery is thick with lamp-oil, sweet and cold, standing in layers.".
    State ci_clear "The air in the gallery is only damp. The smell has gone off it, and the skin on the water has broken into islands.".
    State ci_burnt "The gallery is black along its roof, and bitter with smoke, and the oil that lay on its water is gone. The water is only water.".
  }
  Relation ci_oil_burnt(group). Relation ci_slipped(group). Relation ci_sealed_at(group).
  Rule ci_flash_rule when at(party, ci_slick) and state(ci_fumes, ci_heavy) and capable(party, light)
    says "The light you are carrying leans, in your hand, toward something it has smelled, and the gallery lights from end to end: a sheet of blue and then yellow, silent, and then all the sound there has ever been." {
    Assert strikes(ci_flash, party). Assert state(ci_fumes, ci_burnt). Assert ci_oil_burnt(party). }
  Rule ci_slip_rule when at(party, ci_slick) and state(ci_fumes, ci_heavy) and not capable(party, light) and not capable(party, wayfinding)
    and not knows(party, ci_oil_line) and not ci_slipped(party)
    says "You go along the gallery's wall by feel, and the floor under the oil is a floor of old brick with a lip every few paces, and one of the lips finds your heel. You go down on your back in the oil, and lie there for a moment with your heart going, in the dark, smelling like a chapel." {
    Assert ci_slipped(party). Assert strikes(ci_fall, party). }
  Hazard ci_fall "a fall on the oil" means "Deal (1d4) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (11).".
  Observe ci_slick_scene at ci_slick when true "A long gallery with a floor of brick under a hand's depth of water, and on the water, everywhere, a skin of oil that does not break when you walk through it. The walls shine with it. At the far end the gallery bends away left; at the near end is the weir. Along the right-hand wall, at the height of a boy's hand, a line of knots in a bit of old fishing-cord has been pegged along the brick for the whole length, and the cord is worn dark and smooth by touching.".
  Observe ci_slick_after at ci_slick when state(ci_fumes, ci_burnt) "The ceiling is black. Pegged along the right-hand wall are the burnt ends of a cord, where the lamp-boys' knotted line was, and the pegs are still in the brick.".
  Action ci_burn_off(actor: group, site: place) "Touch a flame to the gallery's fumes from the weir, and stand back" {
    Description "It costs the Drip the oil that has been running down the Drain. It does not cost you anything else.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, ci_weir) and state(ci_fumes, ci_heavy) and capable(actor, flame).
    Grave "The oil on the gallery's water belongs to the Drip, which has little enough of it. It will not come back.".
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert state(ci_fumes, ci_burnt). Assert ci_oil_burnt(actor). }
    Result "You hold the torch out at the full stretch of your arm, to the arch, and the dark takes it. A hush. Then the whole gallery draws breath and lets it go in one long blue gasp that you feel on your face from ten paces; the rats are in the walls before it has finished; and when you look again the arch is a mouth with an orange tongue in it, which sinks and goes out. There is a smell of smoke and sweet burnt oil, and somewhere over your head, a long way, the Drip's lamp-oil has stopped being the Drip's.".
  }

  // ── The leak that feeds it ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Thing ci_leak "the leak at the third pillar" at cistern_hall {
    State ci_seeping "Oil seeps out of the opened mortar at the foot of the third pillar, a bead at a time.".
    State ci_sealed "The leak at the third pillar is stopped with a plug of clay.".
    Change ci_plug "Stop the leak with pitched rag and clay" from ci_seeping to ci_sealed needing mending.
    Change ci_dig_plug "Dig clay from the floor of the aisle and pack the leak with it" from ci_seeping to ci_sealed needing digging.
    Change ci_drive "Drive a wooden bung into the opened mortar" from ci_seeping to ci_sealed needing brawn.
  }
  Observe ci_leak_looked near ci_leak when tried(ci_leak, looking) and state(ci_leak, ci_seeping) "The brick has opened along a mortar-line the thickness of a finger and a boy's arm long. The oil that comes out of it does not go to the cistern's drains but into a groove the Brewers cut for water, and the groove goes south, to the Drain, to the gallery, to the dark. It has been going for years. Whatever lies along the gallery's water, that is where it came from." teaches ci_leak_known.
  Discovery ci_leak_known "The oil that lies in skins on the Drain's gallery comes from a leak in the oil-cistern at the third pillar, along a groove the Brewers cut for water; stop the leak and the gallery clears.".
  Rule ci_leak_stopped when state(ci_leak, ci_sealed) and state(ci_fumes, ci_heavy) and not ci_sealed_at(party)
    says "The smell of lamp-oil in the cistern's air has thinned, as if somebody had opened a window in a very old house." { Assert ci_sealed_at(party). Set ci_sealed_when(party) to watch(clock). }
  Measure ci_sealed_when(group).
  Rule ci_gallery_clears when ci_sealed_at(party) and state(ci_fumes, ci_heavy) and watch(clock) >= ci_sealed_when(party) + 36 { Assert state(ci_fumes, ci_clear). }

  // The Drip's oil is free to draw to anybody who has a flask and a reason; the trimmers will not notice a flask.
  Item ci_oil_stock "a flask of lamp oil" is lamp_oil at offstage.
  Action ci_draw_oil(actor: group, site: place) "Fill a flask at the oil-cistern's tap" {
    Description "It is the Drip's oil, and a flask of it will not be missed.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, cistern_hall) and not holding(actor, lamp_oil) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Give ci_oil_stock to actor. }
    Result "The tap is a brass cock on the cistern's flank, green with the damp, and the oil comes out of it slow and golden and smelling of a thousand evening streets. You fill the flask to the neck and stop it.".
  }

  // ── The eel-run ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Eight feet of black water between two ledges, and the eel that lives in it. It keeps the Siphon. It can be fed
  // (the lamp-boys do, and have for years), slipped, climbed over by those who can climb, or fought.
  Species ci_eel_kind "a cistern eel" like great_pike temperament territorial described "An eel the length of a ladder and as thick as a thigh, the colour of the dark it lives in, with a head like a shut fist and eyes that have given up. The lamp-boys call her the Warden, because she has never let anyone past without a toll.".
  Person ci_eel "the cistern eel" at ci_eelrun {
    Role "an eel as long as a ladder, in the run". Species ci_eel_kind. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Pronouns she.
    Lair ci_eelrun.
    State ci_watching blocking "The Siphon is the eel's: she lies in the run with her head to its lip, still as a stone in a well, and whoever crosses it crosses over her.".
    Guards ci_siphon_way.
    Warns "The water at the foot of the Siphon bellies up, and the eel's head comes out of it to the level of your knee, and stays there, with the whole slow weight of her behind it. She is not in a hurry. She has not been in a hurry for forty years.".
    Comes "The Warden comes up out of the run in one long dark piece, with her mouth open.".
  }
  Relation ci_eel_fed(group).
  Rule ci_eel_gone when (dead(ci_eel) or routed(ci_eel)) and not ci_eel_fed(party) { Assert ci_eel_fed(party). }
  Kind ci_heads_kind "a bucket of fish-heads" is gear worth 0 weighing 1 described "A bucket of eel-pond heads, gone high, kept by the lamp-boys for the Warden's toll. It is the best thing in the cisterns to be carrying and the worst to be carrying near anyone.".
  Item ci_heads "a bucket of fish-heads" is ci_heads_kind at lamp_boys_den hidden until ci_eel_toll.
  Action ci_feed_eel(actor: group, site: place) "Throw the Warden her toll" {
    Description "Fish-heads from the lamp-boys' shelf, or a ration, thrown to the far side of the run.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, ci_eelrun) and at(ci_eel, site) and able(ci_eel) and not tolerates(ci_eel, actor)
      and (holding(actor, ci_heads_kind) or quantity(actor, rations) >= 1).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert tolerates(ci_eel, actor). Assert ci_eel_fed(party). }
    Result "You throw it as far as the far ledge, underhand, and the run goes still and then very loud. The Warden takes it in one long heave and goes back down with it, and the water closes over the place with no more fuss than a hand closing on a coin. She will not come up again for a while.".
  }

  // ── The chimney and the Siphon, to the stair-head ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe ci_eelrun_scene at ci_eelrun when true "The Drain widens into a long cold room with a pool in it, a ledge on either side a hand wide, and the pool black and dead level, as if poured. On the far side a low arch lets the pool go on into the dark: the Siphon. High on the right a second way goes up by a hand-cut ledge to a dark shaft in the roof. Something in the pool is looking at you, from under the water, with all the time in the world.".
  Observe ci_chimney_scene at ci_chimney when true "A square shaft, going up out of sight and down into the dark, with iron staples let into one wall at a spacing that suited somebody with longer arms than yours. The Brewers built it to draw the Drain's air; it draws it still, and the draught that goes up past you smells of nothing at all. Far over your head, very small and very square, there is something that is not dark: a gleam of light, a slot of grey, a grating at the Drip's street-level a very long way off. A child's voice, once, would carry down it.".
  Observe ci_aenean_scene at ci_aenean when true "The Drain ends here, and something older begins. The brick gives way to black stone fitted without mortar, plain and square and cut with a precision that hurts the eye (the Aeneans' lettering over the door is cut into it afterward, as a notice is nailed to a door someone else hung), and in the floor of the stair-head, before a door of the same black stone, there is a single paving-slab that is not quite the colour of the others. Water runs down the walls in lines.".
  Hazard ci_stone "the Aenean counterweight, falling" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13).".
  Discovery ci_plate_known "The paving-slab before the Aenean door is a pressure-plate: stood on, it lets a counterweight fall from the lintel.".
  Thing ci_plate "the slab before the Aenean door" on ci_door_way {
    State ci_primed dangerous "In the floor at the Aenean door one slab is a shade paler than the rest, and the joints around it are clean.".
    State ci_sprung "The Aenean door's slab has been trodden down into the floor, and the counterweight lies split in the doorway, with the dust still settling.".
    State ci_safe "The Aenean door's slab has been made safe, its chain wedged.".
    Change ci_wedge "Wedge the counterweight's chain, and stand on the slab" from ci_primed to ci_safe needing trapwork after learning ci_plate_known.
    Hurts with ci_stone when ci_primed then ci_sprung.
    Tries prodding.
  }
  Observe ci_plate_read beside ci_door_way of ci_plate when tried(ci_plate, looking) and state(ci_plate, ci_primed) "The joints round the slab are clean of silt and the others are not, and the slab sits a hair lower on its seat, as if it had been leaned on. Over the lintel, in the black stone, there is a slot the width of a shut door, and a gleam of chain." teaches ci_plate_known.
  Rule ci_plate_poled when tried(ci_plate, prodding) and state(ci_plate, ci_primed)
    says "You lean out and lay the pole's iron shoe on the slab, and press. The slab goes down with a click you feel in your teeth. Overhead, a block of black stone as big as a door comes out of the lintel with a long grinding noise and falls on the place where you would have been, and splits, and lies there, and the dust comes down on you like flour." {
    Assert state(ci_plate, ci_sprung). }
  Rule ci_plate_stepped when knows(party, ci_plate_step) and state(ci_plate, ci_primed) and at(party, ci_aenean)
    says "You step over the pale slab, as you were told, on the left-hand black one beside it, and the door opens to your hand." { Assert state(ci_plate, ci_safe). }
  Discovery ci_plate_step "The lamp-boys cross the Aenean door's stair-head on the left-hand black slab, and never on the pale one.".
  Discovery ci_oil_line "The lamp-boys have pegged a knotted cord along the right-hand wall of the oil gallery, and cross it in the dark by touch, a knot at a stride, because a light in there goes off like a bell.".
  Discovery ci_eel_toll "The lamp-boys pay the eel in the Drain a toll of fish-heads, which they keep in a bucket on the shelf of their den, and she lets them by.".

  // ── The Aenean pump ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Older than the Drain: a wheel and a piston in a hall of black stone, which the Aeneans found and learned to start, and used to keep this end of
  // their city dry, and wrote their plaque beside, and left. It was kept going by the Brewers, and then not. Three things are wrong with it, and it
  // can be put right by each of three crafts. When it runs it holds the Siphon low (and so keeps the Drain open on the
  // third to fifth days) and drains the Drain's water to wherever its valve is set: the lagoon, through the Heronry,
  // which it has done since the Aeneans and which the Heronry has never asked for; or to the Weighhouse Yard on the
  // Row, which is a sunk yard the Exchange has coveted for years.
  Observe ci_pump_scene at pump_chamber when true "A round hall of black stone under a low dome, and in the middle of it, in a pit, a wheel: twice a man's height, black metal, spokes like the ribs of something, a piston standing up beside it in a jacket of green bronze. A plaque in the wall is cut in letters you half know. Round the wheel's pit, the floor is silted, and in the silt the print of a boy's bare foot goes in a circle and does not go on. A valve-wheel as big as a cartwheel stands on a pillar by the door, with an arrow cut on its rim.".
  Observe ci_pump_running at pump_chamber as sound when state(ci_pump, ci_running) "The great wheel turns, a quarter-turn to the minute, with the long wet knock of the piston going up and down inside its jacket, and the whole hall hums with it like a bell that has been struck and not stopped.".
  Thing ci_pump "the Aenean pump" at pump_chamber {
    State ci_silted "The wheel stands in its pit, locked in silt to the hub, with its piston down.".
    State ci_cleared "The silt is out of the wheel's pit. The wheel turns a hand's breadth when pushed, and stops, and is dry as a bone.".
    State ci_primed "The wheel's bearings shine with lamp-oil, and the piston's jacket is wet to the top.".
    State ci_running "The wheel turns in its pit, slowly, and the piston goes up and down in its jacket.".
    State ci_drowned "The pump stands in a hall full of black water, and does not turn.".
    Change ci_clear_silt "Clear the silt out of the wheel's pit" from ci_silted to ci_cleared needing digging or brawn.
    Change ci_clear_bind "Free the wheel's pawl and work the silt out of its bearings" from ci_silted to ci_cleared needing mending.
    Change ci_prime "Prime the bearings and the piston's jacket with lamp-oil" from ci_cleared to ci_primed consuming lamp_oil.
    Change ci_start_wheel "Put your shoulder to the spokes and start the wheel" from ci_primed to ci_running needing brawn.
    Change ci_start_pawl "Lift the pawl, and let the wheel take the weight of the stair" from ci_primed to ci_running needing lockwork or mending.
  }
  Rule ci_pump_drowns when state(ci_flood, ci_drowned) and state(ci_pump, ci_running) { Assert state(ci_pump, ci_drowned). }
  Observe ci_pump_looked near ci_pump when tried(ci_pump, looking) and state(ci_pump, ci_silted) "The wheel is locked by silt, but silt does not do this alone: the bearings are dry, black, and the oil-ports on the piston's jacket have been put out of the way of the rain by somebody who knew what they were for. A pump like this wants clearing, and oiling, and starting; and the plaque beside it will tell you in what order." teaches ci_pump_known.
  Discovery ci_pump_known "The Aenean pump in the pump-chamber wants three things: its pit cleared of silt, its bearings primed with lamp-oil, and its wheel started; running, it holds the Drain's Siphon low.".
  Discovery ci_valve_known "The Aenean pump's valve-wheel sets where it throws what it pumps: to the lagoon, through the Heronry's reeds, as the Aeneans had it; or by the Brewers' old cut to the Weighhouse Yard on the Row.".
  Thing ci_valve "the pump's valve-wheel" at pump_chamber {
    State ci_lagoon "The valve-wheel's arrow points to a drawing of a reed-bed: the lagoon, and the Heronry's reeds on the way to it.".
    State ci_cut "The valve-wheel's arrow points to a drawing of a square: the Brewers' cut, and the Weighhouse Yard on the Row.".
    Change ci_to_cut "Turn the valve-wheel to the Brewers' cut" from ci_lagoon to ci_cut needing brawn.
    Change ci_to_lagoon "Turn the valve-wheel to the lagoon" from ci_cut to ci_lagoon needing brawn.
  }
  Observe ci_valve_read near ci_valve when tried(ci_valve, looking) "The rim of the wheel is cut with two drawings and an arrow, and under the drawings, in Aenean, the two words that mean WHERE IT GOES. The drawing of the reed-bed has been worn bright by the hand that last set it, in a world that had reeds in it already. The other is a square, with a line through it, like a yard." teaches ci_valve_known.
  Thing ci_plaque "the plaque in the wall" at pump_chamber {
    State ci_cut "The plaque is cut in the black stone, four lines of square Aenean, with a drawing at the foot of a wheel and a drop.".
  }
  Observe ci_plaque_read near ci_plaque when tried(ci_plaque, looking) and capable(party, lore) "You read it as you would read a receipt, left to right and without hope. THE WHEEL WANTS: ITS HOUSE CLEARED; ITS OIL; ITS HAND. IT THROWS WHERE THE VALVE IS TURNED. KEEP IT, AND THE WATER IS YOURS. And under it, a line added in the Brewers' blunter script: IT BELONGS TO THE HERONS' WATER, WHICH WE NEVER ASKED." teaches ci_pump_known.
  Rule ci_pump_known_valve when knows(party, ci_pump_known) and not knows(party, ci_valve_known) and capable(party, lore) and at(party, pump_chamber)
    says "The plaque's last four words you had taken for decoration; they are a note about the valve." teaches ci_valve_known { }
  // The spine's own stair, from mouth to pump, is shut by the sump until the pump has run.
  Thing ci_sump "the sump on the pump stair" on pump_way {
    State ci_flooded blocking dangerous "The stair from the Drain's mouth goes down into black water to the roof, and stays there. It has been this way since the Brewers.".
    State ci_drained "The stair from the Drain's mouth down to the pump is dry, and slimed, and shines.".
  }
  Rule ci_sump_drains when state(ci_pump, ci_running) and state(ci_sump, ci_flooded)
    says "Under your feet the pump takes its first slow breath, and somewhere beyond the wall the sump on the stair drops away with a gurgle like the end of a bath." { Assert state(ci_sump, ci_drained). }
  Measure ci_pump_since(group).
  Rule ci_pump_stamp when state(ci_pump, ci_running) and ci_pump_since(party) < 1 { Set ci_pump_since(party) to watch(clock). }
  Rule ci_pump_throws_lagoon when state(ci_pump, ci_running) and state(ci_valve, ci_lagoon) and ci_pump_since(party) >= 1 and watch(clock) >= ci_pump_since(party) + 36 and not ci_reeds_drawn(party)
    says "Far to the north-west, under the lagoon's mist, the reeds of the Heronry begin to lose their water by a hand's breadth a day. Nobody in the Drip will see it for some time." { Assert ci_reeds_drawn(party). }
  Rule ci_pump_throws_cut when state(ci_pump, ci_running) and state(ci_valve, ci_cut) and ci_pump_since(party) >= 1 and watch(clock) >= ci_pump_since(party) + 36 and not ci_yard_dry(party) { Assert ci_yard_dry(party). }
  Relation ci_reeds_drawn(group). Relation ci_yard_dry(group).

  // ── The shaft to the cellar, and the cellar below the Urn ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Thing ci_shaft "the shaft to the cellar" on cellar_way {
    State ci_sheer blocking "The shaft goes down from the pump-chamber's floor into the dark, and the iron ladder in it has rusted to stumps. There is not a handhold below the first.".
    State ci_rigged "A rope hangs down the shaft, tied off round the pump's pillar, with a knot every arm's length.".
    Change ci_rig "Tie a rope off round the pillar and let it down the shaft" from ci_sheer to ci_rigged needing rope.
    Change ci_free_climb "Go down the shaft by the rust-stumps, without a rope" from ci_sheer to ci_rigged needing climbing.
  }
  Observe ci_cellar_scene at urn_cellar when true "A cellar of black stone, square, dry, and very quiet, with the shaft in one wall and in the other a ladder of iron staples going up into a round trapdoor. Over your head, in the middle of the ceiling, a bronze plate the size of a cartwheel is let into the stone, green with the damp, with a slot in its middle like a mouth. Under it, on the floor, a shallow bronze bowl on three feet, and nothing in it but a fur of dust, undisturbed, as even as a mould.".
  Observe ci_cellar_dust at urn_cellar as feature when not knows(party, lie_urn) "The dust in the bowl has not been touched in a very long time. It has no marks in it at all, no tessera-edge, no print of a hand.".
  Action ci_rap_plate(actor: group, site: place) "Rap on the bronze plate in the ceiling, and listen" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_cellar) and not knows(actor, lie_urn) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, lie_urn). }
    Result "You stand on the bowl's rim and rap on the plate with the butt of your pole, or your knuckle, or the heel of your hand, and it rings. It rings like a bell that has nothing to say, a long clean note that goes up through the Hall above and comes back down the shaft of the slot: the note of a bronze jar with nothing in it. A jar of three hundred thousand lots would have said nothing. In the bowl under the slot, where the Aeneans caught what the Urn let fall, there is not a mark in the dust.".
  }
  Hazard ci_hatch_blow "the hatch coming down" means "Deal (1d6) physical damage to ally unless strength save against (11).".
  Thing ci_hatch "the cellar hatch" on cellar_hatch {
    State ci_bolted blocking "The trapdoor over the ladder is bolted on the far side: you can see the line of the bolt through the seam, and a thread of light, which is the Urn Hall.".
    State ci_open "The cellar hatch stands open on the Urn Hall, and the ladder goes up into light.".
    State ci_seated "The hatch lies down on its seat, unbolted, with a gasket of old pitch round it, and keeps the water out.".
    Change ci_work_bolt "Work the bolt back with a blade through the seam" from ci_bolted to ci_open needing lockwork.
    Change ci_heave_hatch "Heave the hatch against its bolt, until the bolt gives" from ci_bolted to ci_open needing brawn.
    Change ci_lift_pins "Lift the hatch off its hinge-pins with the bar" from ci_bolted to ci_open needing crowbar.
    Change ci_seat_down "Let the hatch down on its seat, and tread it home" from ci_open to ci_seated.
    Change ci_raise_again "Lift the hatch on its seat" from ci_seated to ci_open.
  }
  Observe ci_hatch_wet at urn_hall when state(ci_hatch, ci_open) and state(ci_flood, ci_drowned) "Water stands on the Urn Hall's floor in a black skin, coming up round the cellar hatch in slow rings, and the Hall smells of the Drain.".
  Observe ci_hatch_hole at urn_hall when state(ci_hatch, ci_open) and state(ci_flood, ci_shallow) "In the floor of the Hall a round hatch stands open on the dark, with a ladder going down.".

  // ── The lamp-rats ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Four of them at the weir, big as terriers, who have eaten the boys' leavings for as long as the boys have been
  // down here and have no great love of a stranger's boots. A light drives them back into the walls; without one they
  // hold the weir, and are fought.
  Species ci_rat_kind "a lamp-rat" like rat temperament defensive described "A rat the size of a terrier and the colour of the oil it lives on, wet, quick, with a tail like a length of wick and no idea that it is meant to be afraid of you.".
  Person ci_rats "the lamp-rats" at ci_weir {
    Role "four lamp-rats at the weir, big as terriers". Species ci_rat_kind. Level 1. Numbers 4. Pronouns they.
    Temperament defensive.
    Lair ci_weir. Refuge cistern_hall. Fears flame.
    Warns "The holes in the walls are full of eyes, and the eyes have all come forward. A long thin noise starts somewhere low in the brick, like a lot of small wet wheels, and the nearest rat sits up on the rail and shows you exactly how many teeth a rat has.".
    Comes "The rats pour off the weir at you.".
    Flinches "The rats are gone off the weir in a long brown ripple, back into the walls, with the light in their eyes.".
  }

  // ── The lamp-boys ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Three of them, and one is the book's whole heart. The boys are the Owls' (the lamp-trimmers'): they trim the Drip's
  // lamps and the Chapel's wicks and are counted for their candle-ends at the end of every night. Pip, who is nine,
  // was trimming under the lamp-table when the Registrar died. He saw her bare face, which in his religion is the end
  // of him; he saw the clerk, the cooper and the Warden come and go; and he has been in the cisterns since, with a stub
  // of candle he took from the table, which he will not put down. Pip is not moved by evidence, which he has had
  // plenty of; he is moved by being asked what he wants. By day, in the Masked Hours, he wears his Owl and speaks
  // as the Owl, to an Owl, or not at all; by night, or to a bare knock at his own den, he is nine.
  Discovery ci_boys_found "Three lamp-boys hide behind the drawn sacking at the end of the den off the oil-cistern: Nell, who is eleven and speaks for the others; Tobit, who is six; and the smallest, who holds a candle-stub in both hands and will not put it down.".
  Discovery ci_pip_named "The smallest of the lamp-boys in the cisterns is Pip Treen, nine, a lamp-trimmer's boy: the P. T. of the Registrar's ledger.".
  Discovery ci_pip_fear "Pip is not afraid of the Watch. He believes that to see the Registrar's bare face is what killed her, and that her face, now, is looking for him.".
  Discovery ci_pip_wish "Pip wants a candle: a whole one, that no steward has counted, that is his to keep.".
  Discovery ci_pip_clerk "The Registrar's clerk found Pip under the lamp-table, told him he had seen nothing, and left him there in the dark with her until morning.".
  Discovery ci_pip_hers "The Registrar knew the lamp-boy's name, and the south wick he was always late with; she said she was sorry, and he does not know for what.".
  // The catalog's candle is known to the module by an item of its kind, set where nobody reaches it, so that what a company
  // carries can be asked for by its kind.
  Item ci_candle_stock "a tallow candle" is candle at offstage.
  Measure ci_trust(group). Measure ci_closed_until(group).
  Relation ci_asked(group). Relation ci_candle(group). Relation ci_told_saw(group). Relation ci_told_others(group). Relation ci_may_tell(group).
  Relation ci_told_warden(group). Relation ci_pell_message(group). Relation ci_pell_knows(group). Relation ci_pip_forgave(group).
  Relation ci_spooked(group). Relation ci_bribed(group). Relation ci_clowned(group). Relation ci_where_asked(group).
  Relation ci_pip_settled(group). Relation ci_pip_stays(group). Relation ci_pip_garrity(group). Relation ci_pip_taken(group).
  Query ci_found(a: group) means knows(a, ci_boys_found).
  Query ci_heard(a: group) means privateHours() or wears(a, face_owl).
  Query ci_open_now() means watch(clock) >= ci_closed_until(pip).

  Person pip "Pip Treen" at lamp_boys_den {
    Role "a lamp-boy, nine, with a candle-stub in both hands". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Known as "a small figure in a cut-down Owl" when not knows(party, ci_pip_named).
    Seen when knows(viewer, ci_boys_found).
    Greets "The smallest of them comes forward on his knees as far as the end of the sacking and no further. His Owl is a man's, cut down with a pair of shears and tied on with bootlace, the eyeholes too big, so that he looks out of the corners of them like something in a hedge. In both hands, against his chest, the way you would hold a wren, he has a candle-stub no longer than a thumb. 'Bares don't come down here,' he says. 'Bares don't go nowhere. You're lost.'".
    Greets again "The boy in the cut-down Owl watches you from the end of the sacking with the stub held against his chest.".
    Joins "Pip tucks the stub into his hat, takes hold of the back of your coat in his fist, and does not look up at the Drip's rain.".
    Leaves "Pip lets go of your coat and does not say anything.".
  }
  Person ci_nell "Nell" at lamp_boys_den {
    Role "a lamp-boy's sister, eleven, who has appointed herself the rest". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Seen when knows(viewer, ci_boys_found).
    Greets "A girl of eleven in a man's coat to her ankles gets between you and the smallest without appearing to move. She has a boy's trimming-knife and the look of someone who has been left in charge of a thing too large for her and has decided to do it anyway. 'No,' says Nell.".
    Greets again "'Still no,' says Nell, with less conviction.".
  }
  Person ci_tobit "Tobit" at lamp_boys_den {
    Role "a lamp-boy, six, who does not speak". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Seen when knows(viewer, ci_boys_found).
    Greets "The smallest of all sits on the sail-cloth with his knees up, regarding you gravely, and says nothing, and goes on saying it.".
    Greets again "Tobit looks at you for a while longer.".
  }

  // ── Finding the boys ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // By tracking (woodcraft, a check; failed, it sends them to ground for the half-day), by food and patience (a ration, an
  // hour, no check), by sitting out their fear in the dark (no light, no coin, no craft; only at night), by paying
  // (they take it and go), or by telling the Watch, which is the cruellest and the quickest.
  Action ci_read_den(actor: group, site: place) "Read the den's floor and walls for where the boys have gone" {
    Description "Wet bare feet; soot at a hand's height; the draught under the sacking. A tracker reads an alley as a woodsman reads a wood.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lamp_boys_den) and not knows(actor, ci_boys_found) and not ci_spooked(actor) and not benighted(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ci_boys_found). }
    On failure { Assert ci_spooked(actor). Set ci_spook_end(actor) to watch(clock) + 72. }
    Result "It is all there, as it is on any ground, if you can bear to read it as a story and not as a mess: three sets of bare prints, a man's size and a girl's and a smaller than either, going in and out at the sacking's edge in the order of a game that has rules; soot at the height of a hand on a child; a trodden place on the floor where somebody has sat for a long time facing the wall. The draught under the sacking is warm. You lift the end of it, and three faces look back.".
    Otherwise "You read the floor wrong, or too loud: a stone turns under your heel in the dark, and behind the sacking a whole small household draws one breath and is gone, with a skitter, into the crawl at the back of the den that you had not seen. You hear them go a long way. They will not be back for half a day.".
  }
  Measure ci_spook_end(group).
  Rule ci_unspook when ci_spooked(party) and watch(clock) >= ci_spook_end(party) { Retract ci_spooked(party). }
  Action ci_leave_food(actor: group, site: place) "Leave a ration at the sacking's edge, and sit well back for an hour" {
    Description "Nobody has been kind to a lamp-boy by accident in the history of the Drip.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lamp_boys_den) and not knows(actor, ci_boys_found) and not ci_spooked(actor) and quantity(actor, rations) >= 1.
    Time 6.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, rations) by 1. Assert knows(actor, ci_boys_found). Increase ci_trust(pip) by 1. }
    Result "You lay it where the sacking meets the floor, and move to the far wall, and sit with your hands where they can be seen, and do not look. It is a long hour. Water drips somewhere. At the end of it the ration has gone and a hand has come out for it three times, a different size each time, and the sacking has been drawn back the width of a face; and the face, which is smaller than you expected, says nothing, and neither do you.".
  }
  Action ci_wait_dark(actor: group, site: place) "Put out your light, sit in the dark, and wait for the Ninth Bell to have rung" {
    Description "Nobody comes out to a stranger. They come out, a little, once a stranger has stopped being there.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lamp_boys_den) and not knows(actor, ci_boys_found) and privateHours().
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ci_boys_found). }
    Result "You put your light out and sit down on the cold brick with your back to the wall, and make yourself as little as you can. After a time you cannot count, you become aware of breathing that is not yours; after another, of the faint smell of tallow and wet wool that is children; and then, at the edge of hearing, a whisper in three voices, one very small, arguing about whether you have gone. The sacking moves. You have the sense, not of being looked at, but of being tried, like a plank over water.".
  }
  Action ci_hold_out_coin(actor: group, site: place) "Hold out three coin into the dark, and call that it is for the boy with the candle" {
    Description "He will take it. He is nine, and it is three coin.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lamp_boys_den) and not knows(actor, ci_boys_found) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3.
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Assert ci_bribed(actor). Assert knows(actor, ci_boys_found). Assert knows(actor, ci_pip_named). Assert knows(actor, pip_saw).
      Assert at(pip, loft_roof). Assert at(ci_nell, loft_roof). Assert at(ci_tobit, loft_roof). Retract at(pip, lamp_boys_den). Retract at(ci_nell, lamp_boys_den). Retract at(ci_tobit, lamp_boys_den). }
    Result "A hand comes out of the sacking, quick as a wren's beak, and the coin is gone from your palm; and a voice says, very fast and without drawing breath, that it was him, it was Pip, he was under the table, he saw her face and the clerk and a man and he never saw nothing else and that is all, and that is three coin's worth, and the sacking whips shut, and the den is empty, and from the crawl at the back you hear them going, all three, a long way up and away, a handful of bare feet in the dark. They will have gone to the highest and driest place in the Sleeve, which is the pigeon-loft at the Post.".
  }

  // ── The wrong way to find a child, and the quick one ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic ci_betray_boy with vail "Tell Sergeant Vail that the lamp-boy is hiding in the cisterns under the Drip" when knows(actor, ci_boys_found) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) and not ci_pip_settled(actor) once {
    Grave "A boy who has been told a Watch cannot Face him will be Faced by it: a witness is a person in Ombra, and a witness has a face given him.".
    Says "Vail does not write it down. She has a good memory for what she is told by a Bare, and she gives you the look of a woman putting a fact in a drawer she has not decided whether to lock. 'The Warrant is a good deal more than a pass to ask questions,' she says. 'A child who saw a Registrar die. He will not be hurt. He will be fed, and given a bed, and a face, a small one, with a ribbon, so that he can be spoken to, and three questions will be asked him by a clerk with a sheet.' She stops, and finds, for a moment, that she cannot say the rest. 'It is what we are for,' she says.".
    On discuss { Assert ci_pip_taken(actor). Assert knows(actor, pip_saw). Assert knows(actor, serene_saw). Assert knows(actor, lacke_unfaced). Assert knows(actor, ci_pip_named). }
  }
  Rule ci_pip_to_gate when ci_pip_taken(party) and at(pip, ?p) and distinct(?p, gate_hall) { Retract at(pip, ?p). Assert at(pip, gate_hall). }
  Rule ci_nell_to_gate when ci_pip_taken(party) and at(ci_nell, ?p) and distinct(?p, gate_hall) { Retract at(ci_nell, ?p). Assert at(ci_nell, gate_hall). }
  Rule ci_tobit_to_gate when ci_pip_taken(party) and at(ci_tobit, ?p) and distinct(?p, gate_hall) { Retract at(ci_tobit, ?p). Assert at(ci_tobit, gate_hall). }
  Topic ci_pip_in_watch with pip "Speak to the boy in the Watch's keeping" when ci_pip_taken(actor) {
    Says "They have given him a small white domino, with a ribbon. He has not put it on; it lies in his lap, face-up, and he looks at it. He has the stub in his hands, still, but it has been snuffed, and his thumb goes over the wick and over the wick. 'I'm nobody,' he tells you, politely, the way one tells a stranger a street's name. He does not look up, and does not say whose face he is hoping it will not be.".
  }
  Topic ci_nell_in_watch with ci_nell "Speak to the girl in the Watch's keeping" when ci_pip_taken(actor) {
    Says "'You,' says Nell, and that is all she says, and she says it with her whole body, and after a moment she turns her back, so that you will have the trouble of knowing she has done it on purpose.".
  }

  // ── Pip, by day and by night ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic ci_pip_cold_bare with pip "Speak to the boy behind the sacking" when publicHours() and not masked(actor) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) {
    Says "'I'm at my work,' says the Owl, to the sacking, in a small flat voice that has been told what to say. 'I'm nobody. You're nobody. That's two nobodies and no business.' The stub does not move.".
  }
  Topic ci_pip_cold_mask with pip "Speak to the boy behind the sacking" when publicHours() and masked(actor) and not wears(actor, face_owl) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) {
    Says "'Don't know that face,' says the Owl, politely, from behind the sacking. 'I'm at my work, whoever you are. Go on.' It is the voice of a boy being very good in front of a stranger, who has been told what happens to the other kind.".
  }
  Topic ci_pip_who with pip "Ask the boy his name" when ci_heard(actor) and ci_found(actor) and not knows(actor, ci_pip_named) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) once {
    Says "'Nobody,' he says, and then, because he is nine, and a boy in the dark will tell a name to anything that does not scare him: 'Pip, if you've to call me something. Pip Treen. It's only what they call me. It ain't mine, it's the Owls'. The steward's got it in a book.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ci_pip_named). }
  }
  Action ci_read_fear(actor: group, site: place) "Watch his hands, and say aloud what he is afraid of" {
    Speaker pip.
    Description "It is not the Watch. A child hiding from the Watch holds his candle away from his body; this one holds it like a wound.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pip, site) and ci_heard(actor) and ci_found(actor) and not knows(actor, ci_pip_fear) and not ci_told_saw(actor) and ci_open_now() and not ci_pip_taken(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ci_pip_fear). Increase ci_trust(pip) by 1. }
    On failure { Set ci_closed_until(pip) to watch(clock) + 6. }
    Result "'You're not afraid of the Watch,' you say, and the boy goes quite still. 'You're afraid of her. You think it was looking at her that did it. You think her face is somewhere now, looking for you.' Nobody has told him that anyone can see this. He does not answer, and he does not run. His thumb goes over the stub's wick, once, like a man testing whether a knife is sharp, and the whole room waits.".
    Otherwise "'The Watch,' you say; and it is so wrong, and so plainly the guess of a grown person, that he draws the sacking shut with a snap. 'I ain't afraid of the Watch.' It is an hour, at least, before he will say anything to anyone.".
  }
  Topic ci_pip_evidence with pip "Tell him it cannot have been seeing her that killed her" when ci_heard(actor) and knows(actor, ci_pip_fear) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) once {
    Says "'You weren't there,' says Pip. He says it kindly, and it is the kindness of a child with a better case than yours. 'Everybody says it. Nell says it. The cooper's lad down the Drip says his da says. Said it's her heart.' He turns the stub over. 'It ain't a *reason*, though, is it? It's only what you say when it's already happened.'".
  }
  Topic ci_pip_ask_want with pip "Ask him what he wants" when ci_heard(actor) and ci_found(actor) and not ci_asked(actor) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) once {
    Says "He does not answer at once. You see him go through the things people have said to him, the things he has been told he must do, the Watch, the steward, the Chapel, and then back to the question, which is not in that list and which he turns over like a coin he cannot place. 'Nobody asked,' says Pip, slowly. 'Nobody asked me that. Not ever.' The stub comes down against his knee. 'A candle. A whole one. Not a stub. That nobody's counted, that the steward don't have in his book. That's mine to keep.' He seems astonished to have said it, and then to be unable to stop. 'That's all. That's all I want.'".
    On discuss { Assert ci_asked(actor). Increase ci_trust(pip) by 2. Assert knows(actor, ci_pip_wish). }
  }
  Action ci_clown(actor: group, site: place) "Do the Assessor of the Pound addressing the Hall of Weights: pompously, to the pigeons" {
    Speaker pip.
    Description "It is a rule followed to its humane absurd end: the Assessor must be addressed as the Pound. It is, to a boy of nine in the dark, the funniest thing in Ombra.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pip, site) and ci_heard(actor) and ci_found(actor) and not ci_clowned(actor) and not ci_pip_settled(actor) and ci_open_now() and not ci_pip_taken(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert ci_clowned(actor). Increase ci_trust(pip) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert ci_clowned(actor). Set ci_closed_until(pip) to watch(clock) + 6. }
    Result "You draw yourself up and address a pillar, in the voice of a man who has never been wrong, as the Pound; and the pillar, you inform the room, is two ounces light. From behind the sacking comes a small damp snort, and then a larger one, and then the sound of somebody trying with all his strength not to laugh and being defeated by it: a high, helpless, gasping child's laugh that goes up the oil-cistern's arches and comes back down. Nell says, in a furious whisper, 'Shut up,' and does not mean it. Tobit, at last, smiles.".
    Otherwise "You do it, and it is dreadful. The silence afterwards is the particular silence of three children being tactful to an adult. 'That was a joke,' Pip tells you gently, 'was it?'".
  }
  Topic ci_pip_route with pip "Ask how the boys get under the Drain" when ci_heard(actor) and ci_found(actor) and ci_trust(pip) >= 1 and not ci_pip_taken(actor) once {
    Says "'We don't,' says Pip, which is a lie, and then, because it is a poor lie and he knows it, 'we don't *go*. We go to the weir for the rats. Nell's got a line in the gallery, in the dark, you do it by the knots, you can't have a light, it goes up, I saw it go. The eel's called the Warden. She wants her heads, from that bucket, and she's civil. And the door at the end's got a black slab, a left one, you stand on that and not the pale one, because the pale one's a liar.' He stops. 'That's nothing. That's not a route. That's just where we put our feet.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ci_oil_line). Assert knows(actor, ci_eel_toll). Assert knows(actor, ci_plate_step). }
  }
  Topic ci_pip_saw_t with pip "Ask what he saw, that night, under the lamp-table" when ci_heard(actor) and ci_found(actor) and ci_trust(pip) >= 2 and not ci_told_saw(actor) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) once {
    Says "'I was trimming the south wick,' says Pip. 'I'm always late with the south one. And she come in.' He is looking at the stub. 'She'd her mask on. And then she sat down, and she took it off, like you'd take off a hat, and set it on the table next to my knee, and I seen her face. She was only a woman. That's the thing. She wasn't big or nothing. She had a cold.' A silence. 'She said, *Oh, there you are. South wick.* And then, *I am sorry.* And I don't know what for.'".
    On discuss { Assert ci_told_saw(actor). Assert knows(actor, pip_saw). Assert knows(actor, ci_pip_hers). Increase ci_trust(pip) by 1. }
  }
  Topic ci_pip_others_t with pip "Ask who else came, after she had sat down" when ci_heard(actor) and ci_found(actor) and ci_told_saw(actor) and not ci_told_others(actor) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) once {
    Says "'A big man in a leather apron,' says Pip, 'that smelled of birch and hot tar, and he stood in the door with his hands hanging, and he said, *Oh God, oh no.* And he ran. Fast, for a big one.' He swallows. 'Then a thin man, with ink on his thumbs. He cried. He put her mask on her, careful, the way you would a baby's cap. And he saw me. He *saw* me. And he said, *You saw nothing. You saw nothing, do you hear?* And he took a book off the lectern, and he went, and he left me in the dark. With her.'".
    On discuss { Assert ci_told_others(actor). Assert knows(actor, serene_saw). Assert knows(actor, ci_pip_clerk). }
  }
  Action ci_give_candle(actor: group, site: place) "Give him a candle of your own, a whole one, that nobody has counted" {
    Speaker pip.
    Description "Tallow, a wick, and nobody's book.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pip, site) and ci_asked(actor) and not ci_candle(actor) and holding(actor, candle) and not ci_pip_taken(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Spend candle from actor. Assert ci_candle(actor). Increase ci_trust(pip) by 1. Assert restful(lamp_boys_den). }
    Result "You hold it out across the gap in the sacking, the whole length of it, white and straight and tall as a boy's forearm. For a long moment nothing happens. Then Pip reaches out with one hand, and takes hold of the middle of it, the way you take the arm of someone about to fall; and lights it from the stub, very carefully, with his tongue between his teeth; and pinches the stub out between a finger and thumb that do not flinch, and puts the stub in his hat. 'Nobody's counted that,' he says, in a whisper. 'Have they?' The flame stands straight up in the dark, with nothing in the whole cistern to trouble it.".
  }
  Action ci_roll_candle(actor: group, site: place) "Ask for the stub, and roll him a whole candle from it and the wax-ends of the den" {
    Speaker pip.
    Description "He will have to let go of the stub to let you. It is the first thing he has not let go of since the night she died.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pip, site) and ci_asked(actor) and not ci_candle(actor) and not holding(actor, candle) and ci_open_now() and not ci_pip_taken(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, mending, dc_fair).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert ci_candle(actor). Increase ci_trust(pip) by 1. Assert restful(lamp_boys_den). }
    On failure { Set ci_closed_until(pip) to watch(clock) + 6. }
    Result "He gives it to you with both hands, as one gives up a bird. You melt it in the kettle's lid with the wax-ends from the plank, a hundred small soldiers, and stir in a twist of the sail-cloth's thread for a wick, and roll the lot between your palms on the slate until it is whole and long and your hands are burning, and set it to stand. It is lopsided. It is the finest candle in the cisterns. Pip stands it in front of him and holds his hand round the flame, to keep off a draught that is not there. 'That's mine,' he says. 'Out of mine.'".
    Otherwise "The wick drowns in its own wax and the whole thing guts and slumps, and there is nothing in the kettle but a grey sticky smear where the stub was. Pip looks at it. 'That was a good stub,' he says, in a very small voice, and goes behind the sacking, and does not say another word for an hour.".
  }
  Action ci_tell_nobody(actor: group, site: place) "Tell him a Bare is no one, and what is told to no one has not been Said" {
    Speaker pip.
    Description "The Concord's cruellest law has one hole in it, and you are standing in it. A Bare cannot Name, and cannot be Named; and a Bare is not a person.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pip, site) and ci_heard(actor) and ci_told_others(actor) and ci_trust(pip) >= 3 and not ci_may_tell(actor) and ci_open_now() and not ci_pip_taken(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert ci_may_tell(actor). }
    On failure { Set ci_closed_until(pip) to watch(clock) + 6. }
    Result "'There's a thing about a Bare,' you tell him. 'A Bare's nobody. Nobody can name you to a Bare, because a Bare isn't anybody the Concord has got. If you tell me a name, you haven't Said it; you've told a wall. And walls aren't Named.' You say it slowly, as it is true. Pip thinks about it for a while, with the lit candle in front of his face. 'A wall,' he says. 'Like the oil-cistern's.' He has a look you recognise, of a child who has found a hole in a fence and is trying to decide whether it is a hole or a trap. 'All right,' he says. 'But you're a wall.'".
    Otherwise "'But you're *somebody*,' says Pip. 'You've got a face. You've got a mouth.' It is perfectly unanswerable, and you do not answer it.".
  }
  Action ci_sit_with(actor: group, site: place) "Sit by his candle and say nothing, for as long as it takes" {
    Speaker pip.
    Description "There is a kind of telling that is done by someone else's silence, and takes an hour, and needs nothing but a candle and no questions.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pip, site) and ci_heard(actor) and ci_told_others(actor) and ci_candle(actor) and not ci_may_tell(actor) and not ci_pip_taken(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert ci_may_tell(actor). Increase ci_trust(pip) by 1. }
    Result "You sit down on the cold brick, with your back to a pillar, and do not look at him. The candle burns. Nell, who has been standing guard for three nights without sleeping, sits down too, in the end, with the knife across her knees. Tobit puts his head in her lap. For an hour nothing is said at all, and in the dark the drip counts. When it is over Pip says, in the voice of someone speaking to the flame, 'There was another one. After.'".
  }
  Topic ci_pip_warden_t with pip "Ask about the other one, who came after" when ci_heard(actor) and ci_found(actor) and ci_may_tell(actor) and not ci_told_warden(actor) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) once {
    Says "'A man with keys,' says Pip. 'On his belt, the big iron ones. In a green coat. He didn't see me. He came to *shout*. At her. He said she'd to stop, stop the walking about, or he'd tell. He said she was a, he said, I ain't going to say what he said.' The flame shivers. 'He said her *name*. Out loud. In the Chapel. And I know it now, and it won't come out of my head, and I ain't going to say it, not to you, not to a wall, don't make me.' He is shaking. 'He said it twice.'".
    On discuss { Assert ci_told_warden(actor). Assert knows(actor, lacke_unfaced). Increase ci_trust(pip) by 1. }
  }

  // ── Forgiving the clerk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Pip is angry at one person, and it is not the Warden: it is the clerk who told him he had seen nothing and left him
  // in the dark with a dead woman. The clerk has a reason, and he has been carrying it for a week, and has never been
  // able to say it to the one person it is owed to. The company can carry it down. (post.kyr reads ci_pip_forgave.)
  Topic ci_pell_pip with pell "Tell Tomas Pell that the boy under the lamp-table is alive, and has been asking after no one" when knows(actor, ci_pip_clerk) and not (publicHours() and not masked(actor)) and not ci_pell_knows(actor) once {
    Says "Pell has been standing quite still for some time. 'Alive,' he says, and sits down, quite suddenly, on whatever there is. 'I thought. I did not know what I thought. I left a child in the dark with her. I have known it every hour of seven days.' He covers his mouth. 'I said it so that, if he was asked, he could say it truly. *I saw nothing.* A child who has seen a bare Registrar, and is asked, and says he has, is Faced. A child who says he has seen nothing is a child. It was all that I could think of.' He looks up. 'Tell him. Tell him I am sorry I was too frightened to stay. Tell him it was the only gift I could give and I gave it badly.'".
    On discuss { Assert ci_pell_knows(actor). Assert ci_pell_message(actor). }
  }
  Topic ci_pip_forgives with pip "Carry Tomas Pell's words to Pip, as he said them" when ci_heard(actor) and ci_found(actor) and ci_pell_message(actor) and ci_trust(pip) >= 2 and not ci_pip_forgave(actor) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) once {
    Says "You say it as he said it, word for word, and the lamp-boy listens with his eyes fixed on the flame. For a while there is no answer. 'He said I'd seen nothing,' says Pip, at last. 'Because he thought, if I said it true. If somebody asked. I wouldn't be.' He is working it out aloud, as children do, with a good deal of pausing. 'Nell says he's a coward.' A long breath. 'He *cried*. He put her mask on straight.' The candle burns. 'Tell him he can have it back, the nothing. I'll not say.' He looks up, finally, at you. 'No. Tell him *I saw it*, and I'm all right, and he needn't have. Tell him that.'".
    On discuss { Assert ci_pip_forgave(actor). Increase ci_trust(pip) by 1. }
  }

  // ── Nell, and Tobit ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic ci_nell_cold with ci_nell "Speak to the girl in the man's coat" when publicHours() and not masked(actor) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) {
    Says "'No,' says Nell. It is not an answer to anything you said. It is the whole of her policy, said once.".
  }
  Topic ci_nell_hint with ci_nell "Ask Nell how the boy might be got to talk" when ci_found(actor) and not ci_asked(actor) and (privateHours() or wears(actor, face_owl) or masked(actor)) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) once {
    Says "Nell does not get up; she turns her knife over on her knees, point and then handle. 'Everybody tells him,' she says. 'The Watch told him. The steward told him. The Chaplain told him on the steps, I saw. Told him he's to come in, told him he's to be good, told him he's safe.' She spits, neatly, into the oil. 'I tell him. I'm worse than any of them. *Nobody asks him.* Nobody's ever asked him a thing in his life, that wasn't what's he done. If you want him out, ask him something. That's all I know.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ci_pip_named). }
  }
  Topic ci_nell_heads with ci_nell "Ask Nell what the boys feed the eel" when ci_found(actor) and (privateHours() or masked(actor)) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) once {
    Says "'The heads,' says Nell. 'Off the eel-pond, when they're going. She's not hard to keep; she wants the same thing every night, and she's *polite* about it. You can put your hand in a bucket on the shelf there and not be sorry.' She considers you. 'Or a ration. She'll eat a ration. She's not proud.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ci_eel_toll). }
  }
  Topic ci_tobit_t with ci_tobit "Ask Tobit what his name is" when ci_found(actor) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) once {
    Says "Tobit regards you with the grave attention of the very small. He holds out, for inspection, with perfect solemnity, a lamp-rat's tail, dried hard as a bootlace. Whether it is a gift, a toll, or his name, he does not say, and Nell, who knows, plainly does not intend to either.".
  }

  // ── Where he goes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Once he has told it, and has his candle, the choice of what he becomes is his to be asked about, not the company's to
  // give. He stays among the boys (the guild's steward, paid, will stop counting his candle-ends); or he goes up to
  // the pigeon-loft, where the old master is deaf in one ear and has a loft that needs a boy with good ones. Left to
  // himself the Flood sends him to the loft anyway, but not as somebody's.
  Topic ci_pip_where with pip "Ask him where he would be, if he might be anywhere" when ci_heard(actor) and ci_found(actor) and ci_asked(actor) and ci_candle(actor) and ci_told_others(actor) and ci_trust(pip) >= 3 and not ci_where_asked(actor) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) once {
    Says "'Anywhere?' He has not thought it was a thing one was allowed. 'Here, with Nell and Tobit. Only they'd not have me counted.' He thinks. 'Or the birds. There's a man at the Post has birds, white tumblers, and the white tumblers sit on his head. He's got one ear, the other's no good, I've heard him shout. I give them crusts through the grating, on the sly. If there was a place where somebody wanted a boy for the other ear.' A pause. 'It wouldn't be a lamp. But it'd be a whole candle, kind of.'".
    On discuss { Assert ci_where_asked(actor). }
  }
  Action ci_pip_stays_a(actor: group, site: place) "Tell him he may stay with the boys, and that you will see he is not counted" {
    Speaker pip.
    Description "It costs six coin, paid to the steward of the Owls for the boys' keep, and it buys what a boy of nine most wants: to stay where he knows the dark.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pip, site) and ci_where_asked(actor) and ci_candle(actor) and not ci_pip_settled(actor) and not ci_pip_taken(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 6.
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Increase quantity(steward, gold) by 6. Assert ci_pip_settled(actor). Assert ci_pip_stays(actor). Assert roundDone(actor, r_pip). }
    Result "You put six coin on the kettle's lid, for the steward, with a message that the three boys in the cistern are a charge on the Owls' account and are not to be counted in anything at all. Pip looks at it, and at you, and at his candle. 'You can't do that,' he says. 'There ain't a way.' And then, to the candle, wonderingly, 'There's a *way*.' Nell says nothing, and comes and stands by his shoulder, and for the first time since you came down, puts the knife away.".
  }
  Action ci_pip_goes(actor: group, site: place) "Ask him if he would come up to the pigeon-loft at the Post, to Old Gorrell" {
    Speaker pip.
    Description "He is nine, and has not been in the daylight since the night she died. By day the Drip is masked, and he has a cut-down Owl to go in. The loft is on the far side of the city.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pip, site) and ci_where_asked(actor) and ci_candle(actor) and not ci_pip_settled(actor) and not following(pip, actor) and not ci_pip_taken(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert following(pip, actor). }
    Result "He gets up, quite slowly, with the candle in one hand and the other held out, a little, to nobody; and Nell, without a word, takes hold of it, and holds it for a moment, and lets go. 'Bring him back,' she says, 'if it's no good.' Pip puts his hat on, with the stub in it, and the leather Owl over his eyes, and takes hold of the back of your coat in his fist. 'I'll be nobody,' he tells you, as one telling the time. 'Up there. Only I'll be nobody *with a candle*.'".
  }
  Topic ci_pip_stayed with pip "Ask Pip how the boys are, now they are not counted" when ci_pip_stays(actor) and (privateHours() or wears(actor, face_owl)) {
    Says "'We had a whole row of candles last night,' says Pip. 'Nell made us count them. Not for the steward. For *us*.' He laughs. He doesn't often. 'Tobit blew one out. First thing he ever did on purpose.'".
  }

  Topic ci_pip_loft_t with pip "Ask Pip how he finds the loft" when ci_pip_garrity(actor) and (privateHours() or masked(actor)) {
    Says "'They sit on me,' says Pip, with dignity. 'The white ones. Gorrell says it's a sign of respect, and I say it's because I've bread in my hat.' He considers. 'He talks all the time. He never asks me nothing. He just says *which one*, and I *say*.' He is rather pink. 'I've still got the candle. He put it on the shelf by the corn. It's not counted. I checked.'".
  }

  // ── The Flood sends the boys up, if nobody has ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // On the sixth morning the den is a fathom under; the boys have gone to the highest, driest place they know, which
  // is the roof of the pigeon-loft at the Post, where a deaf man with six dozen birds has not yet counted them.
  Rule ci_boys_flee when state(ci_flood, ci_drowned) and at(pip, lamp_boys_den) { Retract at(pip, lamp_boys_den). Assert at(pip, loft_roof). }
  Rule ci_nell_flees when state(ci_flood, ci_drowned) and at(ci_nell, lamp_boys_den) { Retract at(ci_nell, lamp_boys_den). Assert at(ci_nell, loft_roof). }
  Rule ci_tobit_flees when state(ci_flood, ci_drowned) and at(ci_tobit, lamp_boys_den) { Retract at(ci_tobit, lamp_boys_den). Assert at(ci_tobit, loft_roof). }

  // ── Milestones ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Milestone ci_m_found "found the lamp-boys hiding under the Drip" worth 25 when knows(party, ci_boys_found).
  Milestone ci_m_asked "asked a lamp-boy what he wanted, and was answered" worth 25 when ci_asked(party).
  Milestone ci_m_pip "brought Pip Treen's story to an end he could live with" worth 50 when roundDone(party, r_pip).
  Milestone ci_m_forgave "carried a clerk's apology down to the child it was owed to" worth 50 when ci_pip_forgave(party).
  Milestone ci_m_cellar "went under the Drip and the Cuff by the Ninefold Drain, and stood in the cellar below the Urn" worth 75 when at(party, urn_cellar).
  Milestone ci_m_pump "set the Aenean pump going, after some centuries" worth 25 when state(ci_pump, ci_running).
  Milestone ci_m_urn "heard the Urn ring hollow, from below" worth 25 when knows(party, lie_urn).

  // ── What became of them ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule ci_fate_pip_stays when newsHour() and ci_pip_stays(party) once says "Of Pip Treen: the Owls' steward did, in the end, strike three names from his candle-book, and did not say why, and has not been asked. The boy trims the Drip's lamps still, and walks the Drip in a cut-down Owl, by day. By night, in the cisterns, with Nell and Tobit, he keeps a whole candle burning on the lid of a kettle, which nobody counts. He is, on the Drip's own account, the happiest boy in it, and nobody has ever once asked him if he is." { }
  Rule ci_fate_pip_garrity when newsHour() and ci_pip_garrity(party) once says "Of Pip Treen: he sits on the left of an old man in a pigeon-loft on the Wet Post, at the ear that does not hear, and says *there* when a bird comes in. The white tumblers sit on his head. The Owls have lost a boy, and nobody has come to the loft to say so. He has been given a bed, and a candle, and a name that is the loft's, and he has not been Faced; he wears a feather in his hat instead, which the Post says is his own." { }
  Rule ci_fate_pip_taken when newsHour() and ci_pip_taken(party) once says "Of Pip Treen: a witness in the keeping of the Masked Watch, in a small white domino with a ribbon, which he has not been seen to put on. He answers when he is spoken to, politely, that he is nobody. The Watch is kind to him. It does not know that this is the worst of it." { }
  Rule ci_fate_pip_left when newsHour() and not ci_pip_settled(party) and not ci_pip_taken(party) and not ci_bribed(party) once says "Of Pip Treen: the Flood put him on the roof of the pigeon-loft at the Post, with Nell and Tobit, three small wet nobodies among the white birds. An old man who is deaf on the left side found them in the morning, and did not tell anybody, and did not send them away. They are there still. Nobody has asked the boy what he wants. The pigeons, it is said, have been told." { }
  Rule ci_fate_pip_bribed when newsHour() and ci_bribed(party) and not ci_pip_settled(party) once says "Of Pip Treen: he took the money, and went, as a boy would, and was found at the loft, where the pigeons are, by an old man who is deaf in one ear. He keeps the three coin in a boot. He told you the little that three coin buys, and nobody has ever told him that it was not enough." { }
  Rule ci_fate_pell_forgiven when newsHour() and ci_pip_forgave(party) once says "Of Tomas Pell: he has had a message, by a stranger, from a nine-year-old, which said that he need not have. He has not been able to say what he made of it. He has kept the Book's keys in the same pocket as the candle-end a boy sent him, and in the Dead Letter Office they say he has not been heard to mutter since." { }
  Rule ci_fate_oil when newsHour() and ci_oil_burnt(party) once says "Of the Drip's lamp-oil: the gallery of the Drain burned, one blue evening, and the lamp-trimmers found the cistern's oil a hand lower than it was and accounted for it, in the Owls' book, as rats. The steward, who knows better, has said nothing, and counts the candle-ends twice. The Drip's lamps were lit on the ninth night, in the end, a little yellower than their custom, which the Drip put down to the Flood." { }
  Rule ci_fate_eel when newsHour() and ci_eel_fed(party) once says "Of the Warden of the Drain: she was fed, or she was fought, or she was passed in the dark; the eel in the eel-run has, in any case, the whole Drain to herself, to the arch, and the Flood has put the sea in it. She will have been astonished." { }
  Rule ci_fate_hall_wet when newsHour() and ci_hall_wet(party) once says "Of the Urn Hall: the Drawing was held, as the Concord says it must be, in four inches of the Drain, which came up through a hatch that somebody forgot to shut; the Urn stood in it as it had stood for ninety years, and did not rattle; and the Assessor of Weights, who had to read the lots, did so in galoshes." { }
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/cleric.kyr:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The Confessional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The cleric's arc. In a city where nobody answers a bare face, the Chapel keeps one box where a masked person kneels
  // to a bare one on purpose. Father Ansel has heard it behind a veil for forty years; since the Registrar's death
  // he cannot, and lets whoever has the rites sit the grille. Three penitents come on the third, fifth and seventh
  // nights, each in turn: a cooper in the Serene's mask who ran, a Warden of Locks who performs, a clerk who has
  // hidden the Book. Each tells a little more each night, to someone who is trusted, and less to someone who is not.
  //
  // Three decisions fix what kind of Hearer the company took itself for. (1) Absolve, or set a penance: absolution
  // costs the penitent nothing and changes nothing; a penance costs them something and may change them. (2) The seal:
  // what is said in the box cannot be used. The Warden's confession exposes the one crime the Concord can prosecute;
  // the company keeps the seal and proves it another way (the lamp-room, chapel.kyr), lets him report himself, or
  // breaks the seal and carries the confession to the Watch, which costs it the grille. (3) At the Drawing Father
  // Ansel asks the Hearer to bless the Draw, knowing what the Urn holds.
  //
  // Ids of mine that other files may read: `hearer(party)`; relations `cl_assigned`, `cl_seal_broken`,
  // `cl_pell_penitent` (Pell has been heard at least once), `cl_pell_released` (Pell has agreed to put the Book down),
  // `cl_hobb_unburdened`, `cl_lacke_spent`, `cl_lacke_reporting`, `cl_blessed_lie`, `cl_refused`, `cl_blessed_true` (and
  // `handWay(hand_blessing)` 1 = lie blessed, 2 = refused, 3 = the people blessed); the item `cl_chit` that Pell gives.

  Query hearer(c: group) means memberOf(?m, c) and brings(?m, rites).

  Relation cl_assigned(group). Relation cl_seal_broken(group). Relation cl_pell_penitent(group). Relation cl_pell_released(group).
  Relation cl_hobb_unburdened(group). Relation cl_hobb_eased(group). Relation cl_lacke_spent(group). Relation cl_lacke_reporting(group).
  Relation cl_blessed_lie(group). Relation cl_refused(group). Relation cl_blessed_true(group). Relation cl_asked(group).
  Measure cl_stage(group). Measure cl_trust(group). Measure cl_lastnight(group). Measure cl_waitnight(group). Measure cl_closed(group).
  Relation cl_open(group). Relation cl_absolved(group). Relation cl_sealed(fact).
  // What is learned in the box is sealed; the page and the journal say so, and the company's own acts decide what it does with it.
  Initially Assert cl_sealed(cl_hobb_1). Initially Assert cl_sealed(cl_hobb_2). Initially Assert cl_sealed(cl_hobb_urn).
  Initially Assert cl_sealed(cl_lacke_1). Initially Assert cl_sealed(cl_lacke_2). Initially Assert cl_sealed(cl_lacke_said).
  Initially Assert cl_sealed(cl_clerk_1). Initially Assert cl_sealed(cl_clerk_2). Initially Assert cl_sealed(cl_pell_said).

  // ── Father Ansel gives up the grille ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The seal is a law of the Chapel older than the Concord: what is said in the box is said to nobody, and is not to
  // be repeated, or used to the speaker's harm, by the Hearer who heard it; one who does so is not let sit the grille again.
  Topic cl_ansel_assign with chaplain "Tell Father Ansel that you will sit the grille, if he cannot" when hearer(actor) and day(clock) >= 2 and day(clock) < 8 and not cl_assigned(actor) and ((masked(actor) and publicHours()) or (not masked(actor) and privateHours())) once {
    Says "He puts a hand over his eyes. 'It is not that I cannot,' says Father Ansel, 'it is that I have begun to hear the wrong thing. Forty years. I listen through the grille, and what comes through is a voice, and under the voice is her voice, saying a thing I am not allowed to say. I cannot hear them any more. And they will come. They came to me because nobody would answer them in the street. They will come on the third night, and the fifth, and the seventh, because they have already begun.' He lowers the hand. 'Sit bare. A mask on the Hearer is a penitent. Hear them in the order they come. And, my dear. What is said in the box is said to nobody. If you carry it out, the grille is closed to you, and to the next, and to me.'".
    On discuss { Assert cl_assigned(actor). Assert arcBegun(actor, hand_blessing). Assert knows(actor, cl_the_seal). }
  }
  Discovery cl_the_seal "The Chapel's seal: what a penitent says in the confessional is said to nobody; the Hearer may not repeat it or use it to the penitent's harm, and one who does is not let sit the grille again. A Hearer sits bare, at night, and hears the penitents in the order they come: the third night, the fifth and the seventh.".

  // The penitents: voices behind a grille, who come masked to a bare Hearer, by schedule. A penitent is not identified
  // by anything said to the Hearer: by what the Hearer already knows of the evening (the oak, the glove, the tape), or by
  // what the Hearer has the wit to read, and a name is not to be said.
  Query hearingNight() means (day(clock) == 3 or day(clock) == 5 or day(clock) == 7) and hour(clock) >= 20.
  Query hearingOn() means hearingNight() and cl_assigned(party) and not cl_seal_broken(party).
  // A masked Hearer is a penitent: with a face on, nobody kneels.
  Query penitentsCome() means hearingOn() and not masked(party).
  Person cl_cooper "the first penitent" at offstage {
    Role "a cooper, who is the Serene". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Known as "a masked penitent, smelling of brine and burnt oak" when not knows(party, cl_hobb_1) and not knows(party, ch_cooper).
    Greets "A big man kneels on the penitent's side, a darkness the width of two shoulders on the other side of a hand's breadth of lead. You smell oak, and brine, and a fire made of shavings. He kneels as if he were holding something up.".
    Greets again "The big man kneels again on the penitent's side. The smell of brine and shavings comes through the grille ahead of him.".
  }
  Person cl_warden "the second penitent" at offstage {
    Role "a Warden of Locks, who is wearing the Key". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Known as "a masked penitent in grey leather gloves" when not knows(party, cl_lacke_1) and not knows(party, ch_glove).
    Greets "Someone kneels on the penitent's side with a great deal of rustle, and settles his coat, and lays one hand on the ledge under the grille, gloved in grey leather. He has a lovely voice, which he knows. 'Do begin when you like,' he says, as if he were the one being heard.".
    Greets again "The gloved hand comes down on the ledge under the grille. 'Hearer,' says the lovely voice, 'again.'".
  }
  Person cl_clerk "the third penitent" at offstage {
    Role "a clerk of the Registry, who keeps what he took". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
    Known as "a masked penitent smelling of ink" when not knows(party, cl_clerk_1) and not knows(party, ch_knot).
    Greets "A narrow man kneels on the penitent's side and does not touch the ledge. Ink, and tallow smoke, and a sweet note of old paper. He wipes his right thumb against his forefinger, over and over, as a man does who is trying to take something off it.".
    Greets again "The narrow man kneels again. His thumb is at work against his forefinger before he is settled.".
  }
  Rule cl_cooper_arrives when penitentsCome() and cl_stage(cl_cooper) < 3 and cl_lastnight(cl_cooper) != day(clock) and not at(cl_cooper, confessionals) { Assert at(cl_cooper, confessionals). }
  Rule cl_warden_arrives when penitentsCome() and cl_stage(cl_warden) < 3 and cl_lastnight(cl_warden) != day(clock) and (hour(clock) >= 21 or cl_lastnight(cl_cooper) == day(clock) or cl_stage(cl_cooper) >= 3) and not at(cl_warden, confessionals) { Assert at(cl_warden, confessionals). }
  Rule cl_clerk_arrives when penitentsCome() and cl_stage(cl_clerk) < 3 and cl_lastnight(cl_clerk) != day(clock) and (hour(clock) >= 22 or cl_lastnight(cl_warden) == day(clock) or cl_stage(cl_warden) >= 3) and not at(cl_clerk, confessionals) { Assert at(cl_clerk, confessionals). }
  Rule cl_cooper_leaves when at(cl_cooper, confessionals) and (not penitentsCome() or cl_lastnight(cl_cooper) == day(clock) or cl_stage(cl_cooper) >= 3) { Assert at(cl_cooper, offstage). }
