  Topic dr_pallet_after_march with rainmother "Speak to Goody Pallet" when dr_marchers(party) and masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "'We are at the Chapel,' says Goody Pallet, at the Chapel steps, where she is not; it is the hall, and her chair, and her stitching, and the cloth is gone. 'The Wives carried it. I stayed. Somebody has to keep the hall, and I am old enough to be forgiven for not being brave.' She counts. 'Thirty-eight. Thirty-nine. They are very slow, the old ones. They went by the long way, to be seen.'".
  }
  Topic dr_wives_pot with rainmother "Ask whether the Rain-Wives could take on the Saint's pot, as the Wives' washing-penny" when dr_petition_answered(party) and not dr_wives_lied(party) and not dr_pallet_cool(party) and not dr_pot_secured(party) and not dr_kitchen_shut(party) and not dr_pot_by_wives(party) and masked(actor) and publicHours() once {
    Says "'Forty women, a penny a week,' says Goody Pallet, thinking. 'Three hundred bowls a day. It is not charity; a Wife who eats the Saint's soup has the right to say who fills the pot. That is a thing we can do.' She puts her needle in the cloth like a pennant. 'We have done it before, for the lamp-boys. It was never in the cloth. I do not know why that is, for a thing that has been done.'".
    On discuss { Assert dr_pot_by_wives(party). Increase dr_supply(party) by 4. }
  }
  Milestone dr_m_cloth "read the Rain-Wives' Tally-cloth" worth 25 when dr_cloth_read(party).
  Milestone dr_m_petition "answered the Rain-Wives' Petition, truly or kindly or by a delay" worth 50 when dr_petition_answered(party).

  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // THREAD 4: THE LAMP-TRIMMERS' STRIKE. The Owls are owed sixty coin of arrears, drawn from the Hall of Weights on the
  // quarter-day and carried to the lamp-house in a wage-box by Hal Dunne, the steward's brother, who put twenty-two of it
  // on an eel and has the rest in an oil-cask. The Hall says it paid. Jory has sworn on his key-ring to the Owls that the
  // wage would be in the box by the eighth day, and will not unswear it for a stranger's money: an Owl's wage is hands.
  // What he trusts is hands: a lamp lit in order, a box handed back, a day stood in the yard. On the eighth day the Owls
  // walk out unless it is settled; no lamps on the ninth night means a dark city (dr_dark(party), which the integrator
  // reads). Ways: pay (coin, once he trusts you); find the box (Hal, by insight and persuasion, or the cask by lockwork or
  // stealth) and bring it back whole; break the strike (the Hospice's Bare lodgers lighting the lamps in the Owl's domino;
  // the Owls will not forgive it); or join the walk (the Owls make you one; the city goes dark).
  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Discovery dr_arrears_known "The lamp-trimmers are owed sixty coin of arrears drawn from the Hall of Weights on the quarter-day; the steward has sworn the wage will be in the box by the eighth day, and the Owls will walk out on the eighth day if it is not.".
  Discovery dr_box_taken "The Owls' wage-box went missing on the road from the Hall of Weights in the hands of the steward's brother Hal, who is drinking in the lamp-house corner; there is a key missing from his peg.".
  Discovery dr_cask_known "Hal Dunne has what is left of the wage-box in a locked oil-cask at the back of the lamp-house, thirty-eight of the sixty coin; the rest went on an eel.".
  Measure dr_arrears(group). Relation dr_jory_trusts(group). Relation dr_box_returned(group). Relation dr_hal_will(group). 

  Topic dr_jory_cold with steward "Speak to {steward}" when not masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "{steward} looks at your bare face, and then at your hands, and decides about both. 'The lamps are for the Owls,' he says, to nobody in particular, to the yard. 'The dry may look at them. They may not touch them. It is not personal. It has never been personal.'".
  }
  Topic dr_jory_burglar with steward "Speak to {steward}" when masked(actor) and privateHours() {
    Says "The yard goes quiet. 'A face at night,' says {steward}, and his hand is on the key-ring in a way you do not like. 'Take it off in the lamp-house where we can see it, or take it away down the Drip. There is a man here who has not slept since the quarter-day.'".
  }
  Topic dr_jory_customer with steward "Ask {steward} about the lamps of the Drip" when masked(actor) and not wears(actor, face_owl) and publicHours() and not dr_strike_on(party) once {
    Says "'Ninety-one,' says {steward}. 'Lit at the Eighth Bell, trimmed at the Third, filled on Thursdays. Only an Owl touches a street lamp: the Articles of the Lamp, which is older than the Concord and a good deal more sensible.' He watches the rain come down on his poles. 'We have not been paid since the quarter-day. Sixty coin of arrears, in a wage-box, from the Hall of Weights. I have sworn on my key-ring that it will be in the lamp-house by the Eighth Day. After the Eighth, the Owls walk.' A pause. 'It is not a threat. A threat is when you hope it works.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, dr_arrears_known). Assert knows(actor, dr_jory_name). }
  }
  Topic dr_jory_owl with steward "Speak to {steward} as one Owl to another" when wears(actor, face_owl) and publicHours() and not dr_strike_on(party) once {
    Says "'An Owl.' {steward} looks at the domino and, for a moment, at your face under it, where he has not been invited. 'Then you will know what an unpaid week is. The box went to the Hall of Weights on the quarter-day and came back on the road with my half-brother Hal, who says he never saw it. Sixty coin. I believe him: he is the best of us.' He does not sound as if he were quite certain what he believed. 'He has not been well. I am the steward, and I swore the wage by the Eighth.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, dr_arrears_known). Assert knows(actor, dr_jory_name). Assert knows(actor, dr_hal_name). }
  }
  Topic dr_jory_boys with steward "Ask {steward} about the empty bench" when masked(actor) and publicHours() and not dr_strike_on(party) once {
    Says "{steward}'s face, under the domino, does something. 'The lamp-boys,' he says. 'Three of them went down the cistern steps on the first night and did not come up. Nell, and Tobit, and the Treen child. They are not in trouble. They have seen a thing, the way a child sees a thing, and they are afraid of the daylight.' He folds his arms. 'We leave a heel of bread and a cup of milk on the second step, and it is gone by morning. I would not have anybody go down after them who frightens easy. They have a candle, and they have each other.'".
  }

  // The brother, by night, in the lamp-house corner.
  Topic dr_hal_cold with dr_hal "Speak to the young man in the corner" when masked(actor) and privateHours() {
    Says "He looks at the mask, and puts down the jug quite carefully, and it is not a gesture of friendship. 'No,' says Hal Dunne, in an altered voice, 'I have nothing for the Watch. I do not know a thing. Ask my brother.'".
  }
  Topic dr_hal_sit with dr_hal "Sit down by Hal Dunne, bare, and share the jug" when privateHours() and not masked(actor) and at(dr_hal, lamp_yard) once {
    Says "'Sit! Sit.' Hal Dunne moves the jug to make room, and then moves it back, and then pours you a cup you did not ask for with a hand that is not quite steady. 'A stranger. You are bare, so you are a stranger, and strangers are the only people I can bear. My brother is the steward. He is a good man. I am a runner for the Hall of Weights. Did I say that? I run.' He laughs, and it falls over. 'It is quite all right. I shall be all right by the Eighth Day.'".
  }
  Action dr_hal_read(actor: group, site: place) "Watch Hal Dunne's hands, and the peg with the missing key, and say what you see" {
    Speaker dr_hal.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(dr_hal, site) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and not knows(actor, dr_box_taken) and not dr_jory_cool(party).
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, dr_box_taken). Assert knows(actor, dr_hal_name). }
    Otherwise "He is a young man with a jug, and a brother, and a hard week, and any one of them might be all of it. He catches you looking and offers you the jug again.".
    On failure { Assert dr_jory_cool(party). }
    Result "He has a key on a string round his neck that he keeps touching, in the way a man touches a tooth. It is not the lamp-house key; it is a small one, brass, for a cask. The peg above his name on the board has been empty since the quarter-day. He has not been drinking to forget. He has been drinking to be where the key is. You do not say it. He sees you looking at the string, and the cup shakes in his hand, and he says, quietly, 'Oh. Oh, you are good at this.'".
  }
  Rule dr_jory_warm when hour(clock) == 6 and dr_jory_cool(party) { Retract dr_jory_cool(party). }
  Action dr_hal_coax(actor: group, site: place) "Say to Hal, as one who has done worse, that the box may go back and nobody have to know" {
    Speaker dr_hal.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(dr_hal, site) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and knows(actor, dr_box_taken) and not dr_box_found(party) and not dr_jory_cool(party).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert dr_box_found(party). Assert dr_hal_shielded(party). Assert knows(actor, dr_cask_known). }
    Otherwise "'No,' says Hal Dunne. He says it with great politeness. 'I think you had better go. I think I will be sick.' He is, a little, into the jug. It is not a refusal, you think, so much as an inability. You may try another night.".
    On failure { Assert dr_jory_cool(party). }
    Result "You do not argue. You say what you did once, which was less than this and a good deal worse, and nobody found out, and it was a long time before you could look at your own hands. He listens as a drowning man listens to a rope. At the end he takes the key from his neck without a word, and goes to the cask at the back of the lamp-house, and comes back with a canvas bag that clinks, and puts it in your lap. 'Thirty-eight,' he says. 'I lost twenty-two on an eel. I could not tell him. Take it to Jory. Do not say me.'".
  }
  Action dr_find_cask(actor: group, site: place) "While Hal sleeps it off, find the cask and what is in it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(dr_hal, site) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and knows(actor, dr_box_taken) and not dr_box_found(party).
    Resolve check(actor, lockwork, dc_fair).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert dr_box_found(party). Assert knows(actor, dr_cask_known). }
    Otherwise "The little brass lock will not give, and the cask is as dumb as a drum, and Hal Dunne has begun to stir in the corner. You are on the other side of the room with a jug in your hand and nothing in your face when he opens his eyes.".
    On failure { Assert dr_jory_cool(party). }
    Result "It is the third cask along: an oil-cask with a brass lock the size of a thumbnail, put in an oil-cask because nobody checks them for money. The lock gives with a noise like a held breath. Inside, under the rag, is a canvas bag, and in the bag, thirty-eight coin. Hal Dunne is asleep with his cheek on the wall, and in his sleep he is saying 'twenty-two' over and over, in a small ashamed voice.".
  }
  Action dr_return_box(actor: group, site: place) "Put the canvas bag of thirty-eight coin in {steward}'s hands" {
    Speaker steward.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(steward, site) and dr_box_found(party) and not dr_box_returned(party) and not dr_strike_settled(party).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert dr_box_returned(party). Increase dr_arrears(party) by 38. Assert dr_jory_trusts(party). }
    Result "{steward} takes the bag, and weighs it, and does not open it. He looks at the peg on the lamp-house door, and then at you, and then away. 'Thirty-eight,' he says. 'It is short.' He does not ask where it was found, or whom from. It is possible he does not need to. 'An Owl does not take a stranger's coin,' he says. 'But a lamp-trimmer may take his own wage from whoever found it in the yard.' He puts it inside his shirt, where the keys are. It is, you gather, the nearest a man of his sort comes to an embrace.".
  }
  Topic dr_tell_jory_hal with steward "Tell {steward} that it was his brother Hal who took the wage-box" when knows(actor, dr_box_taken) and not dr_hal_told(party) and not dr_hal_shielded(party) once {
    Grave "A thing said to a brother about a brother is said. It will not be unsaid.".
    Says "{steward} does not move. For quite a time he does not move. 'Hal,' he says. 'Hal ran the box.' He goes to the lamp-house door and stands in it, in the rain, with his keys, and comes back. 'I knew,' he says, 'on the first night, and I thought if I did not say it I would not have been told it. That is the whole of being a steward.' He takes the ring from his belt and holds it. 'You have done a hard thing, and I do not thank you for it. I will have it out of him before the Eighth Day, and out of me, and the Owls will have their wage.'".
    On discuss { Assert dr_hal_told(party). Assert dr_jory_trusts(party). }
  }
  Action dr_pay_arrears(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the Owls what is still owing them, in the box, to the steward's hand" {
    Speaker steward.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(steward, site) and dr_jory_trusts(party) and not dr_strike_settled(party) and not dr_strike_broken(party)
      and quantity(actor, gold) >= 60 - dr_arrears(party).
    Time 3.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 60 - dr_arrears(party). Set dr_arrears(party) to 60. Assert dr_arrears_paid(party). Assert dr_strike_settled(party). }
    Result "{steward} counts it twice into the box, and shuts the lid, and says to the yard, in a voice that carries, 'The wage is in.' It does not sound like a victory. It sounds like a man putting down a very heavy thing that is still his. The Owls look at one another, and then, one by one, at the poles, and the grumble comes back into the yard like a tide.".
  }
  Topic dr_jory_no_money with steward "Offer to pay the Owls' arrears yourself" when masked(actor) and publicHours() and not dr_jory_trusts(party) and knows(actor, dr_arrears_known) and not dr_strike_settled(party) {
    Says "'No.' {steward} does not raise his voice. 'Sixty coin out of a stranger's purse is a bribe, and the Owls have never been bribed; they have been robbed, which is different, and it is honest. I will not have the wage in the box and have it be somebody's kindness.' He looks at your hands again. 'Light a lamp. Stand in the yard. Bring me back something that was ours. Then I will know whose hands you have.'".
  }
  Rule dr_strike_begins when day(clock) == 8 and hour(clock) >= 6 and not dr_strike_settled(party) and not dr_strike_broken(party) and not dr_strike_on(party) says "The sound of a great many people not doing something: at the Eighth Bell the Drip's street-lamps are not lit. They stand all along the lanes in their cages with their wicks unlit, ninety-one of them, and a board nailed up at the lamp-yard says in chalk: NO OIL, NO WAGE, NO LIGHT." {
    Assert dr_strike_on(party). }
  Rule dr_strike_goes_dark when day(clock) == 9 and hour(clock) >= 6 and dr_strike_on(party) and not dr_strike_settled(party) and not dr_strike_broken(party) and not dr_dark(party) says "The Owls have not gone back, and nobody has. By the Ninth Bell the Drip will be as dark as the Cuff, and so, you gather from the way people are talking, will the rest of the city: the lamp-trimmers keep all of Ombra's lamps and have an understanding with the lamp-trimmers of the other islands." {
    Assert dr_dark(party). }
  Rule dr_strike_over when (dr_strike_settled(party) or dr_strike_broken(party)) and dr_strike_on(party) { Retract dr_strike_on(party). }
  Rule dr_strike_ends_dark when (dr_strike_settled(party) or dr_strike_broken(party)) and dr_dark(party) { Retract dr_dark(party). }

  // Breaking it: the Hospice's Bare light the lamps in the Owl's domino. Only an Owl may touch a street lamp.
  Topic dr_tibb_lodgers with tibb "Ask Mother Tibb whether any of the Hospice's lodgers could be lent, for an evening, to light a street of lamps" when knows(actor, dr_arrears_known) and (dr_strike_on(party) or day(clock) >= 7) and not dr_lodgers_lent(party) and not dr_strike_settled(party) once {
    Says "'Eleven strangers and nine beds,' says Mother Tibb, as one reading a figure off a wall. 'Two of them I would be glad to see go out for an evening and I need not enter where.' She taps the ledger once, on the page that is not open. 'The Owls will not like it. A Bare lighting an Owl's lamp is a Bare touching what is not his, and he does it in a domino that is not his either. You will be wanting the Owl on your face, and the Owls will want your head.' She writes something in the margin of the sheet. 'I should not do it, if I were you. I should do it at the last possible hour.'".
    On discuss { Assert dr_lodgers_lent(party). }
  }
  Action dr_light_with_lodgers(actor: group, site: place) "Light the Drip's lamps in the Owl, with the Hospice's lodgers, while the Owls stand in the yard" {
    Speaker steward.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and dr_strike_on(party) and dr_lodgers_lent(party) and wears(actor, face_owl) and hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 20
      and not dr_strike_broken(party) and not dr_strike_settled(party).
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_fair).
    Time 12.
    Grave "Only an Owl may touch a street lamp. Lit by strangers in a borrowed domino, the Drip's lamps burn, and the Owls will not forgive it, and will not let the Owl's face stay on anybody who did it.".
    On success { Assert dr_strike_broken(party). Decrease goodwill(face_owl) by 3 or to nothing. }
    Otherwise "You get as far as the first post. A heavy-shouldered man in a round-eyed domino takes the pole out of your hands, quite gently, as a man takes a knife from a child, and a ring of Owls closes round the two Bare lodgers, who have been standing about with the look of those who would like to be back in bed. Nobody strikes anybody. You are walked to the end of the lane. It is worse than being struck.".
    On failure { Assert dr_jory_cool(party). Decrease goodwill(face_owl) by 1 or to nothing. }
    Result "The lodgers carry the ladder, and you carry the pole, in the Owl's round-eyed domino, and for an hour the Drip's lamps are lit by a woman from Strand Street and a man from the road who has not been indoors since February, and nobody can say, in the rain and the dusk, whose faces are under the dominoes. Ninety-one lamps. The Owls stand in the yard, and the glow comes up over the wall; and then somebody in the yard begins to say, 'Who--', and somebody else says, 'Hush,' and then nobody says anything. It is a very cold sort of silence.".
  }
  Rule dr_owls_take_back when dr_strike_broken(party) and holdsFace(party, face_owl) and not rented(party, face_owl) { Retract holdsFace(party, face_owl). Retract wears(party, face_owl). Retract masked(party). }
  Rule dr_owls_rent_back when dr_strike_broken(party) and rented(party, face_owl) and wears(party, face_owl) { Retract wears(party, face_owl). Retract masked(party). }

  // Joining it: the Owls make you one. The city goes dark.
  Action dr_join_walk(actor: group) "Stand in the yard with the Owls in the Owl's domino, and do not work" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, lamp_yard) and dr_strike_on(party) and wears(actor, face_owl) and publicHours() and not dr_strike_joined(party) and not dr_strike_broken(party).
    Time 36.
    On success { Assert dr_strike_joined(party). Assert dr_jory_trusts(party). Increase goodwill(face_owl) by 2. }
    Result "You stand in the yard from the Third Bell to the Ninth in a round-eyed domino with your hands in your sleeves, not working, and it is harder than any work you have done in Ombra. The rain runs off the poles. Nobody tells you what to think. At dusk the steward comes down the line, and at the end of it he stops in front of you, and takes the brass key from his own belt-ring, and gives it you: the key to the yard's gate. 'We make you one,' says {steward}. It is not a thanks. It is the thing that comes after one.".
  }
  Rule dr_joined_dark when dr_strike_joined(party) and day(clock) >= 9 and dr_strike_on(party) and not dr_dark(party) { Assert dr_dark(party). }
  Milestone dr_m_strike "settled the Lamp-Trimmers' arrears, and kept the city lit" worth 75 when dr_strike_settled(party).
  Milestone dr_m_strike_broke "broke the Lamp-Trimmers' strike with the Hospice's lodgers" worth 25 when dr_strike_broken(party).
  Milestone dr_m_strike_joined "stood a day with the Owls" worth 25 when dr_strike_joined(party).

  // ── Later effects that cross the threads ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Rill's morning bakers' leavings, to the Saint, by the Patience, once she trusts the company's hands.
  Topic dr_rill_leavings with rill "Ask {rill} whether the Row bakers' leavings could come across on the Patience for the Saint's pot" when roundDone(party, r_ferry) and not dr_pot_secured(party) and not dr_kitchen_shut(party) and not dr_pot_by_rill(party) and publicHours() and masked(actor) once {
    Says "'The ends,' says {rill}. 'The Cockles on the Row throw out forty loaves a day, the crusts and the ends and the ones that burned. Cosimo's lot, the clerks, have them for the pigeons.' She spits over the side, with precision. 'They can have them for the Saint's pot. It costs me nothing to carry. It is not a kindness; it is a cargo.' The cup goes in. 'I will have it in the Account, and the Account will say Saint, and she will never know whom to thank. That is the right way round.'".
    On discuss { Assert dr_pot_by_rill(party). Increase dr_supply(party) by 3. }
  }
  Topic dr_rill_davit with rill "Ask {rill} what Davit did when he came to the end of the count" when roundDone(party, r_ferry) and dr_rill_bailed(party) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) once {
    Says "{rill} turns the cup in her hands, a long time. 'He started again,' she says. 'That is all it is. You get to the end of the strokes, and you start again from one. I said it was a stupid way to live, and he said it was the only way he had found, and then he was in the Cuff on the fourth of the Deepening, and I was in the boat.' She puts a penny in the tin, and the tin says what it says. 'I have been counting since. Not strokes. Years. It is a good deal easier when somebody is bailing.'".
  }
  Topic dr_rill_about_wives with rill "Ask {rill} what the Drip says about the Rain-Wives' cloth" when masked(actor) and publicHours() and dr_petition_asked(party) and not dr_petition_answered(party) once {
    Says "'The Drip says the Wives have found something and are too frightened to say what, and that the Wives are never frightened, and that therefore it must be something to do with the water.' {rill} bails. 'My mother was in that cloth, I think. One of the black stitches. I have never asked which.'".
  }

  // ── The closing account: what became of the people of the Drip ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule dr_fate_rill_custom when newsHour() and dr_boat_how_custom(party) and not dr_boat_how_bought(party) and roundDone(party, r_ferry) once says "Of Rill Ketch: the Patience rides dry, and she has put a line in the Account that she shows nobody: *one boat's planking, sold to a Gull, one penny, paid*. She does not say what it cost her to take it. She takes a Row fare in the morning and a Drip fare at night, and on the first of the month, they say, she puts a coin in the tin for no reason at all, and does not look to see who sees." { }
  Rule dr_fate_rill_resold when newsHour() and dr_boat_how_bought(party) and dr_boat_how_custom(party) and roundDone(party, r_ferry) once says "Of Rill Ketch: you bought the Patience, and she called you master for two days at both ends of every sentence, and then you sold her back for a penny, and she put the penny in the tin with a noise like a small bell. She has not forgiven the forty coin. She has put it in the Account in a column of its own, headed *Owed to the Bare*, and every Gull on the landing knows she means to pay it, and nobody knows how." { }
  Rule dr_fate_rill_guild when newsHour() and dr_boat_how_guild(party) and dr_rill_indebted(party) and roundDone(party, r_ferry) once says "Of Rill Ketch: she signed for the Guild's planks with her chin out, and owes a farthing in the penny till Michaelmas, and has never loved a boat as well as one she owes for. She will pay it off a week early. She will tell the steward so, and the steward will write it in the ledger as the Guild's good fortune, which it is." { }
  Rule dr_fate_rill_right when newsHour() and dr_boat_how_right(party) and roundDone(party, r_ferry) and not named(dr_ley) once says "Of Rill Ketch: the Guild was very sorry, in writing, and she has had the surveyor's berth-money for the year, which she calls her due and nothing else. The Patience is sound, and her hull is the only one on the landing that has had its own Articles read over it. She is, for a Gull, almost talkative about it." { }
  Rule dr_fate_rill_named_ley when newsHour() and dr_boat_how_right(party) and named(dr_ley) once says "Of Rill Ketch: the Patience is sound, and the man who laid her green was Named in the landing's hearing, and every grudge he ever escaped came home to roost on him by sundown. She does not say she is sorry. She stands at the stage with her cup and watches the water where his name went, for a good while, with the expression of one who has been given a thing she did not ask for, and has had to pay for it, and is not sure to whom." { }
  Rule dr_fate_rill_hired when newsHour() and dr_rill_hired(party) once says "Of Rill Ketch: she is your hired Gull, and says 'Master' to you at both ends of every sentence, with a precision of diction that could cut glass. The Patience is sound, and in your name. She is, by every account, the best servant the Drip has ever had, and has not once looked at you since the day of the sale." { }
  Rule dr_fate_rill_sold when newsHour() and dr_berth_sold(party) and not dr_boat_sound(party) once says "Of Rill Ketch: the Patience was condemned on the seventh day by a surveyor's mallet and her berth let to his brother-in-law; she hires a Gull's oar on another woman's boat now, and has been seen on the landing at night with a tin and a cup and nothing to bail, bailing it." { }
  Rule dr_fate_rill_insulted when newsHour() and dr_rill_insulted(party) once says "Of Rill Ketch: the Patience is sound, and has been since a night in the Novena when somebody she did not ask mended her in the dark. She has said nothing to that person, then or since. She keeps the silence like a good tool, oiled and in its place; and every day, with a bad conscience, she looks at her new strakes." { }

  Rule dr_fate_nobody_named when newsHour() and named(nobody) once says "Of Sister Nobody: she lives in the Hospice now, bare, in a bed that is the tenth of nine, and was Named in a square. She does not go out. Mother Tibb has given her the bed by the stove and a task, which is counting the linen. She counts it every hour, with two fingers on each fold, as one counts a pulse." { }
  Rule dr_fate_nobody_shut when newsHour() and dr_kitchen_shut(party) and not named(nobody) once says "Of Sister Nobody: the kitchen shut at noon on the sixth day. Nobody was fed in the soup-room for three days, and the Drip went to the Rain-Wives' copper and the Gulls' rations and Mother Gammon's back door, and said nothing about it, which is how the Drip says what it thinks of a thing. She sits in the cold room with her mask on. She has been seen to sit." { }
  Rule dr_fate_nobody_seated when newsHour() and dr_pot_secured(party) and dr_nobody_seated(party) once says "Of Sister Nobody: the pot is full to the Drawing and past it, and on the ninth night, for the first time in twelve years, she sat down at her own table and ate the supper somebody else had brought. She takes the grey cloth off in the evenings now and leaves it on its nail. She is the Saint by day, and by night an old woman in a good chair with a bowl, and she says that she prefers it. She has not smiled. She has been observed to be about to." { }
  Rule dr_fate_nobody_laughed when newsHour() and dr_pot_secured(party) and dr_nobody_laughed(party) once says "Of Sister Nobody: the pot is full to the Drawing and past it, and every so often, in the middle of a queue, over the copper, she says to nobody 'The Pound has dropped a Pound', and stops, and says 'Next,' with her shoulders shaking. The Drip thinks it is a cough, and has begun to say so in the street. She has not smiled. That is not what a laugh is for." { }
  Rule dr_fate_nobody_plain when newsHour() and dr_pot_secured(party) and not dr_nobody_moved(party) and not dr_pot_by_coin(party) and not named(nobody) and not dr_nobody_unhooded(party) once says "Of Sister Nobody: the pot is full to the Drawing and past it, and she does not know why, and will not ask. She ladles. A bowl, and a bowl, and a bowl. She does not know whom to thank, and has made that the whole of her thanks. It is the Saint." { }
  Rule dr_fate_nobody_coin when newsHour() and dr_pot_by_coin(party) and not dr_nobody_moved(party) and not named(nobody) and not dr_nobody_unhooded(party) once says "Of Sister Nobody: the pot is full to the Drawing and past it, on thirty coin that came into her tin box one night with a noise like a cough, bare-handed and not by a face. She does not know whom to thank, and has made that the whole of her thanks. She ladles. She is, you are told, ladling rather more slowly; as a woman does who has begun to count how many days there are." { }
  Rule dr_fate_nobody_unhooded when newsHour() and dr_nobody_unhooded(party) and not named(nobody) once says "Of Sister Nobody: somebody lifted her mask, in the queue, in the rain, with leave or without it. She tied it on again with a surgeon's care and has said to that person nothing but Next. She goes on, because three hundred of the Drip must be fed whoever has seen her face." { }

  Rule dr_fate_tansy when newsHour() and dr_cloth_counting(party) once says "Of Tansy Ruddock: she has the sum on the hall floor in chalk, and has not scrubbed it. Four hundred and two of five hundred and eighty-nine. She stands on it in the evenings with her domino on her forehead like a pair of spectacles and says, to anybody, that she should have liked to be wrong. Nobody, in the Drip, has ever seen her so happy." { }
  Rule dr_fate_pallet_chance when newsHour() and dr_marchers(party) and dr_wives_chance(party) once says "Of Goody Pallet: the Rain-Wives stood at the foot of the Chapel steps with the Tally-cloth between them for a jar, and the banner, in a hand that has had a good deal of practice at keeping quiet, said so. She stayed in the hall and stitched, and when the news came to her she stitched one more pink knot, at the end of the thirty-first foot, in the place where the Drawing was to be. 'A jar,' she says, to the cloth. 'Whatever it holds.'" { }
  Rule dr_fate_pallet_deferred when newsHour() and dr_marchers(party) and (dr_deferred(party) or dr_wives_waiting(party)) and not dr_wives_chance(party) once says "Of Goody Pallet: she held the Wives for two days, as she said she would, and on the Eighth Day she was at the head of them, because she had said she would be, an old woman of seventy in a grey domino with the strings in a bow, at a pace she set herself. Nobody came out of the Chapel to say whose the wash was. They are still, they say, waiting." { }
  Rule dr_fate_pallet_marched when newsHour() and dr_marchers(party) and not dr_wives_chance(party) and not dr_deferred(party) and not dr_wives_waiting(party) once says "Of Goody Pallet: the Rain-Wives marched on the Sixth Day with forty damp sleeves and no reason that could be written down, and stood at the foot of the Chapel steps till the Ninth Bell. She says it was not nothing. She says a thing that is stood before is a thing that has been answered, even by silence. She is not sure she is right. She keeps a space on the cloth." { }
  Rule dr_fate_pallet_kept when newsHour() and dr_wives_keep(party) and not dr_marchers(party) once says "Of Goody Pallet: she put out the lamp with two fingers and told the street the Wives had read the cloth and found it good. She has not stitched since. She sits at the end of it with the needle in the linen, and does not draw it through; and sometimes at night, in her own face, she says to the Wives, 'It was a good girl they picked,' and nobody asks who." { }
  Rule dr_fate_pallet_lied when newsHour() and dr_wives_lied(party) and not dr_marchers(party) and not dr_wives_keep(party) once says "Of Goody Pallet: the lamp went out on the Fourth Day on the word of a Bare, and the Wives have been very kind to one another since. She counts steps. She counts forty-one from the door to the cloth, and she has begun to count a second number, under her breath, that she has told nobody. It is the number of the years since the cloth was last wrong." { }

  Rule dr_fate_jory_returned when newsHour() and dr_strike_settled(party) and dr_box_returned(party) and not dr_hal_told(party) once says "Of Jory Wickham: the box was in the lamp-house on the Eighth Day, thirty-eight and twenty-two. He swore on his key-ring that he did not ask where the thirty-eight was found, and he has kept it. He and his brother go home at night down the same lane, not speaking, and on the ninth night they lit the lamps of the Drip side by side, each on his own pole, and the Owls say it is the best they have ever burned." { }
  Rule dr_fate_jory_told when newsHour() and dr_strike_settled(party) and dr_hal_told(party) once says "Of Jory Wickham: the box was in the lamp-house, and Hal Dunne went down the delta road on the Ninth Day with a purse his brother had made up out of his own pocket, and a letter to a cousin in the Marsh, and a lamp. Jory trimmed the Drip's lamps that night alone, in his own face, and did not say who he was trimming them for." { }
  Rule dr_fate_jory_paid when newsHour() and dr_arrears_paid(party) and not dr_box_returned(party) and not dr_hal_told(party) once says "Of Jory Wickham: the wage was in the box on the Eighth Day, from a stranger's purse that he took for the Owls and not for himself, and he said so, in the yard, in front of everybody. The Weights have still not said where the other box went. Hal sits in the corner with the jug and a face like a letter nobody has answered." { }
  Rule dr_fate_jory_broken when newsHour() and dr_strike_broken(party) once says "Of Jory Wickham: the lamps of the Drip were lit by strangers in an Owl's domino, and the Owls did not forgive it. He stands in the yard with the key-ring in his hands, and when somebody asks him who it was he says the Hospice, and that is all he says. He has not struck anybody. He has not been asked. The Owls who stayed do not look at the lamp-house door, where the chalk was rubbed off with a sleeve." { }
  Rule dr_fate_jory_joined when newsHour() and dr_dark(party) and dr_strike_joined(party) once says "Of Jory Wickham: the Owls stood in the yard on the Ninth Day with a stranger among them in a round-eyed domino, and the Drip was dark. He says it was the longest night of his life. It is also, he says, the one he is proudest of. He gave the stranger the yard's gate-key, and has not asked for it back." { }
  Rule dr_fate_jory_dark when newsHour() and dr_dark(party) and not dr_strike_joined(party) once says "Of Jory Wickham: the Owls did not go back, and nobody made them, and the city was dark on the ninth night. He stood at the gate in the rain with the poles racked behind him, and when the Drawing began, a mile away, he took off his domino and held it in his hands and watched the black water, and was not ashamed. He will say the strike was just. He will not say it was wise." { }

  // ── More of the Drip's people, in their two registers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Jory by night, bare, in the lamp-house: the oath, and the brother.
  Topic dr_jory_night with steward "Knock at the lamp-house door, bare, and ask to sit by the stove" when privateHours() and not masked(actor) and not dr_strike_on(party) once {
    Says "The lamp-house is one room, hot as an oven, and eleven men in their shirts round a stove with their boots off and their dominoes hung on pegs. Nobody in it is an owl. {steward} sits at the head of them with the key-ring in his lap, turning it, and he does not get up. 'Bare,' he says, quite mildly. 'Then you may sit. It is not often a stranger comes to the Owls at night.' A man passes you a tin cup of something hot. 'We are owed sixty coin, since the quarter-day, and I swore on this ring to the yard that it would be in the box by the Eighth.' He looks at the ring. 'I do not know where it is. That is a thing I should not say in the day.' In the corner at the back, a young man laughs too loudly at nothing.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, dr_arrears_known). Assert knows(actor, dr_jory_name). Assert knows(actor, dr_hal_name). }
  }
  Topic dr_gammon_cold with dr_gammon "Speak to the bread-woman" when not masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "Mother Gammon looks over your bare face at the awning, and says to it, 'Loaves are a penny. Not to the dry. Not because I am hard. Because I have forty customers in the wet, and every one of them has a face, and I have only the one pair of hands.'".
  }
  Topic dr_gammon_pound with dr_gammon "Ask the bread-woman about the brass pound on her board" when masked(actor) and publicHours() once {
    Says "'The pound.' She lays one flat hand on it. It is worn to a pale gold at the middle, as a doorstep is. 'My mother weighed with it and her mother. It is the market's pound, and a pound is what it says, and nobody has ever asked it for its papers.' She weighs a loaf on it, quite slowly, and looks at the pan. 'The Weights come down once in a long while and look at it. Then they go back up the Row. It is a very good pound. It is a very old one. I have never known a loaf go short on it.' The loaf goes in the bag. 'Have you?'".
  }
  Observe dr_wives_at_steps at chapel_steps when dr_marchers(party) and day(clock) >= dr_march_day(party) and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 20 "At the foot of the steps, in the rain, forty women in grey linen stand with a long strip of embroidered cloth laid out flat on the stones in front of them, and do not say anything to anybody who goes up.".
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/endings.ky:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── When the book closes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At midnight on the ninth night, or when the Concord's offer of a face has been answered after a Drawing has been held.
  // The first whose condition holds wins, in the order written. What became of each of the city's people is told in the
  // hour before (aftermath.kyr). In a world that goes on, Ombra goes on after it.
  Rule drawing_over when closing() and not drawingOver(ombra_delta) { Assert drawingOver(ombra_delta). }

  // The Concord's offer: the last act. A face, or the road home with the Concord's thanks.
  Kind white_domino_kind "the Warrant's white domino" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 granting insight described "A plain white half-mask of the kind a Registrar wears, with the bare oval of the Concord stamped on the inside of the brow, and no name on it anywhere. A Fitter has cut it to your face from a cast you never sat for, and it fits like a thing you were born holding. By day in Ombra it is answered as a person. It gives away nothing at all, which is its whole use.".
  Item white_domino "the Warrant's white domino" is white_domino_kind at offstage.
  Kind countersigned_warrant_kind "the Stranger's Warrant, countersigned" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 granting persuasion described "The grey slip you were given on the first morning, with a second oval stamped over the first in the Chaplain's violet and a line in a small round hand: THE CONCORD THANKS THE BARE, AND DOES NOT ASK THEM TO STAY. Anywhere the Concord's name is known, it is a passport; and anywhere it is not, a very well-bred piece of paper.".
  Item countersigned_warrant "the Stranger's Warrant, countersigned" is countersigned_warrant_kind at offstage.
  Action accept_face(actor: group, who: member, site: place) "Accept the face the Concord offers, and let {who} wear it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingHeld(actor) and warrantHeld(actor) and not faceTaken(actor) and not faceDeclined(actor) and awake(who) and memberOf(who, actor).
    Time 5.
    Resolve endow(who, wisdom, by_one).
    On success { Assert faceTaken(actor). Assert holdsFace(actor, face_white). Give white_domino to actor. }
    Result "Sergeant Vail finds you at the foot of the dais. She has the grey slip in her glove. 'A face,' she says. 'Your own. A trade, a place in the next Urn, a name nobody may say, and nobody will.' There is a question in how she is standing. You take it. She puts into your hands a white half-mask the plain size of a person; it fits, and the whole room, which has not been able to look at you for nine days, looks at you as at one of itself. You will be, in Ombra, from now on, a person. You find you did not know until this minute how much you wanted it, or what it would cost.".
  }
  Action decline_face(actor: group, who: member, site: place) "Decline the face, and go home Bare" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingHeld(actor) and warrantHeld(actor) and not faceTaken(actor) and not faceDeclined(actor) and awake(who) and memberOf(who, actor).
    Time 5.
    Resolve endow(who, charisma, by_one).
    On success { Assert faceDeclined(actor). Give countersigned_warrant to actor. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 100. }
    Result "'Bare,' says the Watch, and then, after a time, in a voice she has not used all week, 'You are the second to refuse it in sixty-two years.' She does not seem surprised. She hands you the Warrant, stamped a second time, and a purse of a hundred coin in the Concord's grey leather, and says the thing the Concord says to its Bare, and which you are fairly sure she has just made up: 'The city thanks you, and does not ask you to stay.' Then she puts her mask straight and, more quietly: 'I should have asked.'".
  }
  Action vail_joins(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Sergeant Vail whether she would walk out of Ombra with you, some day" {
    Speaker vail.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(vail, site) and vailTrust(actor) >= 3 and (faceTaken(actor) or faceDeclined(actor)) and not vailWilling(actor).
    Time 5.
    On success { Assert vailWilling(actor). Assert willing(vail, actor). Set hire(vail) to 0. }
    Result "'I have been a hound for nineteen years,' says Ottoline Vail. She takes the black domino off and looks at it in her hand, in the Urn Hall, in front of the Watch. 'I find that I am prepared to be a person for a little while, on the road, where nobody is anybody and it is allowed.' She hangs it on the Urn's wax. 'Ask me again when I have got used to it. I will say yes.'".
  }
  Relation vailWilling(group).

  // Each ending is the Drawing's way, said as the city has it in the morning.
  Ending end_put_out "Put Out at the Gate" when gateShut(party) "By the sixth mark the Watch has stopped being patient and started being procedure. The Warrant is struck through with a line of white wax and the Gate of Strangers is closed on you with a very small, very civil sound, like a ledger shutting. Behind you the Novena goes on in its rain. You do not hear who is drawn. You hear, from a long way down the delta road, on the ninth night, a crowd breathing out, and cannot tell if it is relief.".
  Ending end_quiet_hand "The Quiet Hand" when closing() and wayQuiet(party) "Ombra goes to bed on the ninth night as it has done every year for thirty-one, and wakes to a city with nineteen new faces in it, none of whom knows how they came there. The Urn is sealed again. The Book is back on its lectern. A woman in a white mask is read the lots at the next Drawing, and the next; she has your handwriting, and goes about the streets by night in the Registrar's mask, mending. It is, by every measure that Ombra has, a very well-governed city. Only you know why. On the ninth night you walk out along the delta road with the grey Warrant folded in your sleeve, and nobody asks for it back.".
  Ending end_open_book_consent "The Consenting Book" over end_open_book when closing() and wayOpenBook(party) and openBookConsent(party) "Fifty-one stood up. In the days after, a great many more, in doorways, in the bread-market, on the Chapel steps, a mask in their hand, saying: it was I. Orsolya Hart has stopped saying her own name as a crime and begun saying it as an introduction. The Spent begin to be spoken to. There are two duels and a marriage. The city, which had thought of the Concord as the thing that protected it from itself, finds it was the thing that stopped it from being brave. It does not become good. It becomes a little less safe, and a little more known; and nobody, for the moment, is Named who did not ask.".
  Ending end_open_book "The Open Book" when closing() and wayOpenBook(party) "By morning the names are in every square. The Treasurer of the Year of the Sluice is a lamp-trimmer's daughter, dead, and the city does not know whether to curse her or to bury her; it does both, in a quarrel that lasts nine days. The Candid hold the Chapel, and the Registry, and the Book, and a register of names on a board outside it, which is for the first time a thing in Ombra that can be asked for. By the end of the week, in the Drip, two old feuds have been restarted over the dead. There is a debt, in the Exchange, that has found its man. Absalom Peck, if he is living, is cheered in the street, which kills him faster than the Naming did.".
  Ending end_honest_urn "The Honest Urn" when closing() and wayHonest(party) "The first Office goes to a girl of seventeen who had come in out of the rain; the second, to a man who immediately sells it, which is not allowed, and is overturned at the Hearing. The Treasurer is a drunk. The Warden of Locks is a woman who has never locked a door. The Physician-General, by a margin of nine tesserae, is a person who is in every other respect a physician. It is, for a year, the worst-governed city on the delta, and the most alive, and in the Rains the Cullet Sluice holds, by an accident of chance, in the hands of a ferryman's son who has no idea what a sluice is and asks, and is told.".
  Ending end_qualified "The Qualified Draw" when closing() and wayQualified(party) "It is a civic compromise, and is called one by every faction, and satisfies none. The Offices go by lot out of those whom the city has already said it trusts. Anybody may put a name on the list. By the first Novena a ferrywoman is Treasurer, protesting; the Candid have nailed the list to the Chapel door and are correcting its spelling; and in the Drip they have started a column for it on the Tally-cloth, in chalk, with odds. It is a worse lottery than the Urn's, and a better government than the Registrar's, and neither the Candid nor the Old Names nor the Chapel have been able to find the principle on which to attack it, since it is, at bottom, what the Rounds were.".
  Ending end_nobody "The Year of Nobody" when closing() and wayNobody(party) "For a year there is no Treasurer, no Warden and no Serene in Ombra, and everybody knows who they are. The sluices are kept by the people who live below them; the Weights are kept by whoever happens to be holding the scale; the lamps are lit by the Owls and the bread weighed by the Cockles and the Watch walks about with its mask in its hand, asking for directions. It is chaos, in the sense that nobody is sure who is in charge, and a festival, in the sense that nobody minds. At the next Novena the Urn is brought out and there is a great deal of discussion as to whether to put anything in it. It is put to a show of hands. The hands do not agree.".
  Ending end_old_names "The Old Names Come Down" when closing() and wayOldNames(party) "The Fourteen come down from Quiet Hill in the morning, in daylight, in silk, with their shutters open. The Contessa Tarn is the first Registrar in three hundred years to read the Offices in her own name. It is not a tyranny. It is, if anything, a very stylish and exacting regime of the elderly, who have a great many opinions on the lamps and the weights. The Feud does not restart, because nobody is quite sure who would be the other side. The Seconds' Guild is paid. In the Drip they begin, after a month, to call their children after the Houses, which is how you know it has worked.".
  Ending end_stranger "The Stranger's Face" when closing() and wayStranger(party) "You are the Serene of Ombra, for a year, in white and gold, and nobody can say so. It is quiet in the Mask. There are things the Serene may not say and things the Serene may not hear, and in between a great deal of weather. At the end of the year there is a Drawing. You are drawn out of the Urn; you stand there, bare, in the Urn Hall, and they say, 'We do not know who you are,' which is, you find, a very great relief. A woman in a lamp-trimmer's grey says she will see you home. You are not at all sure that she is not the Registrar, and you do not ask.".
  Ending end_interregnum "The Interregnum" when closing() and not drawingHeld(party) "At the stroke of midnight the Concord's own text takes effect: all nineteen Offices dissolve, being only masks. There is a long silence in the Urn Hall in which everybody present looks at the faces next to them, and finds them to be a stranger's. Then the sluice-keepers go home, and the Watch lays down its hounds, and in the Drip somebody lights a lamp that nobody has told them to. For some days it is a city without a government. A ferryman is seen to ask a Watch domino the time, and to be told. By the Novena's end the Old Names have a hold on the Hill, the Candid on the Row and the Rain-Wives on the Drip, and the three of them are discussing, with a seriousness neither of them had planned for, the matter of a Concord.".
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/faces.kyr:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── Wearing a face ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // By day nobody in Ombra answers a bare face, and everybody answers a masked one as the mask. A trade's face may be
  // rented at the Wardrobe Annex for the Masked Hours; an Office's is borrowed, stolen, or made to fit. Whoever wears
  // a face is that face's person to the city: its goodwill, its heat and its manners are theirs.
  Relation rentable(face).
  Initially Assert rentable(face_gull). Initially Assert rentable(face_owl). Initially Assert rentable(face_cockle).
  Initially Assert rentable(face_heron). Initially Assert rentable(face_magpie). Initially Assert rentable(face_moth).
  Initially Assert rentable(face_crow).

  Person moll "Ferris Moll" at annex_counter {
    Role "the Wardrobe Annex's clerk, behind a counter of pegs". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "A long young man with ink on his cuffs stands among ten thousand pegs, and on each peg a domino, and he does not look up. 'Faces by the day,' he says to the counter, in the tone of someone who has been told that he should look at people and finds it hard. 'Three coin, back at the Ninth Bell. Not the Offices; the Offices are not rented. A face of one's own is another matter and not mine.' Now he looks up, briefly, at the place where your mask would be. 'You are Bare. Sorry. It is only that I have to say it.'".
    Greets again "'Faces by the day,' says Ferris Moll, to the pegs.".
  }
  Action rent_face(actor: group, mask: face, site: place) "Rent {mask} from the Annex, three coin" {
    Speaker moll.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(moll, site) and rentable(mask) and not holdsFace(actor, mask)
      and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3.
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Increase quantity(moll, gold) by 3. Assert holdsFace(actor, mask). Assert rented(actor, mask).
      Set rentEnds(actor) to watch(clock) + 72. }
    Result "Moll takes it down off its peg without looking at it, and writes your three coin in a book, and under it, in a smaller hand, a description of how you hold your head. The face is yours until the Ninth Bell.".
  }
  Action don_face(actor: group, mask: face, site: place) "Put on {mask}" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and holdsFace(actor, mask) and not wears(actor, mask).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert wears(actor, mask). Assert masked(actor). }
    Result "You tie it on. The rain on your cheeks stops, and with it the sense of being looked through.".
  }
  Action doff_face(actor: group, site: place) "Take your face off" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and masked(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract masked(actor). }
    Result "You take it off. The air on your face is cold, and the street, for a moment, has no idea who you are.".
  }
  Rule face_off when not masked(party) and wears(party, ?f) { Retract wears(party, ?f). }
  // A rented face goes back at the Ninth Bell, wherever the company is.
  Rule face_returned when rented(party, ?f) and rentEnds(party) >= 1 and watch(clock) >= rentEnds(party) {
    Retract rented(party, ?f). Retract holdsFace(party, ?f). Retract wears(party, ?f). Retract masked(party). Set rentEnds(party) to 0. }

  // ── The Watch's count ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Naming a masked person aloud, lifting a mask, a burglary seen: each is heat, the Masked Watch's patience with a
  // Bare. It cools by one each morning. At three the Warrant is suspended; at six the Gate shuts.
  Measure heatDay(group).
  Rule heat_cools when hour(clock) >= 6 and heatDay(party) < day(clock) { Set heatDay(party) to day(clock). Decrease heat(party) by 1 or to nothing. }
  Rule gate_shuts when heat(party) >= 6 and not gateShut(party) { Assert gateShut(party). }

  // Unfacing: who a masked person is can be learned by lifting the mask, with or without the Warrant's leave, or said
  // aloud, which is Naming. A person's file says what lifting their mask teaches (unmaskTeaches) and what being
  // Named does to them.
  Relation unmaskTeaches(group, fact). Relation lifted(group).
  Action lift_mask_warranted(actor: group, who: group, truth: fact, site: place) "Lift {who}'s mask, by the Warrant" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(who, site) and unmaskTeaches(who, truth) and warrantLive()
      and not lifted(who) and not knows(actor, truth).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert lifted(who). Assert knows(actor, truth). Increase heat(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You put two fingers under the edge of the mask, as the Warrant allows, and lift. It is not nearly as dramatic as it sounds. It is a face. The face knows what it has just been; it does not forgive you.".
  }
  Action lift_mask_bold(actor: group, who: group, truth: fact, site: place) "Lift {who}'s mask, with no leave" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(who, site) and unmaskTeaches(who, truth) and not warrantLive()
      and not lifted(who) and not knows(actor, truth).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert lifted(who). Assert knows(actor, truth). Increase heat(actor) by 3. }
    Result "You lift it. Somebody in the street has seen you do it, and in the way of the city has seen nothing, and will say so to the first Watch domino they meet.".
  }
  Action name_aloud(actor: group, who: group, truth: fact, site: place) "Name {who} aloud, in the street" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(who, site) and unmaskTeaches(who, truth) and knows(actor, truth)
      and publicHours() and not named(who).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert named(who). Increase heat(actor) by 2. }
    Result "You say it. The name goes out across the square like a coin dropped into a well, and every masked head in the square turns, and every one of them is somebody who has heard it. By dusk it will be in every Sleeve.".
  }
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/gate.kyr:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The Gate of Strangers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The landward end of the city, and the one place in it that has to say what it is: a stair, a square, a Hospice with
  // nine beds for eleven Strangers, and a shop of pegs. Everything here teaches a rule of the city by doing it to the
  // company: nobody answers a bare face before the Ninth Bell, except the people whose office it is to; a mask is not
  // lodged; after the Ninth Bell a bare knock is received. The Gatehouse hall is the Warrant's (warrant.kyr).

  // ── The road and the Steps and the Square, by day and by night ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe road_end_scene at road_end when publicHours() "The delta road comes to an end all at once, as if it had been Named: a last flat stone, a lamp-post with its lamp unlit, and a board nailed to the post that reads BARE ARE REQUESTED TO PROCEED TO THE CUSTOMS STEPS, in a hand that has been requesting it for a long time. Past the board the silt gives way to water, and across the water, in the rain, Ombra: roofs, bridges, bell-towers and not one face.".
  Observe road_end_night at road_end when privateHours() "The delta road ends at a lamp-post whose lamp somebody has lit, for once, and left to the rain. Across the water the whole city has put its windows on, one at a time, and behind each window, you understand, somebody is sitting with their face in their lap. The board on the post says BARE ARE REQUESTED TO PROCEED TO THE CUSTOMS STEPS. After dark, it is not a request.".
  Observe steps_scene at customs_steps when publicHours() "Forty wet steps go up from the water to the Gate, and all along them people are putting their faces on. A woman in a gull-domino ties her strings with her teeth. Two men in the same cowl hold each other's lanterns while they do up the buckles at the back. Every head turns a little away from you as you pass, politely, the way a street turns from a drunk, and you see that this is not rudeness but the whole of the law: there is nobody here to speak to you.".
  Observe steps_night at customs_steps when privateHours() "The Customs Steps after the Ninth Bell are bare, wet, and nearly empty. A lantern burns in a bracket, and beside the Gate's low door a bell-pull has been labelled, in neat black paint, KNOCK BARE. Someone has hung a domino on the lantern-bracket and left it for the rain to have.".
  Observe square_scene at gate_square when publicHours() "Strangers' Square is the only place in Ombra with a name that admits what it is: a paved yard in the rain with the Gatehouse on one side, the Hospice on another, and on the third the Wardrobe Annex with its pegs in the window like a crowd that has just looked away. Over the Hospice door, in plain black on plain white, one word: BARE. Across the square the city goes to work in disguise: porters in the Cockle's cream domino, a Heron-clerk with his cowl pulled forward against the wet, and a pair of grey Watch dominoes who look neither left nor right and see everything.".
  Observe square_night at gate_square when privateHours() "The square after the Ninth Bell: shutters closed, lamps lit, the masks gone indoors with the people who wore them. One Watch domino stands under the Gatehouse lamp in the rain, being nobody at a steady pace. Over the Hospice door a lamp is lit, and the white of the door is the whitest thing in the quarter.".
  // The first lesson, given before anyone has said a word: a good morning, unheard.
  Discovery gt_unheard "By day nobody in Ombra answers a bare face: not rudeness, but law. Whoever is spoken to by day is spoken to as the face they wear.".
  Rule gt_first_bare at customs_steps when at(party, customs_steps) and publicHours() and not masked(party) once says "You say good morning to the nearest ferryman. He does not hear it, in the way a wall does not hear it, and the woman beside him has begun, with great attention, to read the rain. A small boy in a cockle-domino looks at you, and is turned round by the collar, gently, by someone who has not looked down. Nothing has been done to you. A woman with a basket steps round you, saying 'Mind' to the air at your elbow, and does not look to see whether it minded. Nobody has been anything but kind. It is a very thorough way of being nobody." teaches gt_unheard { }

  Observe hall_scene at hospice_hall when publicHours() "The Hospice hall is the loudest room in Ombra, and it takes a moment to see why: everyone in it is bare. Benches, a stove that smokes according to the wind, a long table with a ledger and a hand-bell on it, and thirty feet of damp strangers all talking at once, in the voices of people who were silent in the street an hour ago and are making it up. It is the one room in the city where, by day, a face is spoken to.".
  Observe hall_night at hospice_hall when privateHours() "The Hospice hall at night: the stove banked, the benches pushed to the walls, a lamp on the long table beside the ledger and the bell. The talk is down to a mutter from the dormitory. On a nail by the dormitory door hangs a string, a yard of it, grey with handling, with a knot in it for every one of the Bare who has died under this roof.".
  Observe dorm_scene at hospice_dorm when publicHours() "Nine cots in two rows under a long window, each with a number painted on the headboard and a folded sheet stamped with the same number. Two men sleep on the floor between them by an arrangement that has been agreed and is never discussed. By day the dormitory is empty but for whoever is sleeping off something, and the rain on the window is the only conversation.".
  Observe dorm_night at hospice_dorm when privateHours() "Nine cots and eleven sleepers, and the breathing of all of them, in several keys. The window has a lamp in it. Somebody has put a candle-stub on the sill by the cot at the end, and not lit it, as one keeps a place at table.".
  Observe annex_scene at annex_counter when publicHours() "A shop of pegs. Thousands of them: the domino and cowl of every trade in Ombra hung by their strings from rails to the ceiling, so that the room seems full of a crowd that has that moment looked away. Behind a counter the width of a coffin a long young man writes in a book, and does not look up. Over the counter, a card: FACES BY THE DAY. THE OFFICES ARE NOT RENTED.".
  Observe annex_night at annex_counter when privateHours() "The Annex shuttered, the pegs hung up in the lamplight, strings straight down, and every domino turns a quarter-inch when the stove ticks, and back. A single lamp burns on the counter, and by it, with something across his knees, the clerk sits up.".

  // ── What the Hospice teaches: the Almanack of Usages, and a sheet ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Three rules, one joke and one threat, on one folded page; the Hospice has printed it for ninety years and nobody has
  // read it. A bed needs a sheet, a sheet needs the Three Questions, and the Questions are procedure followed to its
  // end: the Hospice is the first place the company learns the city's manners by having them done to it.
  Kind gt_almanack_kind "the Almanack of Usages" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "One sheet, folded in eight, printed both sides in a type that has printed it for ninety years and is now mostly ink. FIRST USAGE: Between the Third Bell and the Ninth the city is masked, and answers the mask. A bare face is not impolite; it is not there. SECOND USAGE: A masked person who names another aloud is Named, and cried in every square by sundown with every debt he escaped. A Bare may name whom he likes. The Watch counts. THIRD USAGE: After the Ninth Bell the city is at home and bare, and knocks are received bare. A masked knock is a burglar. The Hospice keeps nine beds. It has never been known to keep eleven strangers, and it has never been known to be wrong. A Bare who outstays nine days is a Resident, and the Hospice has no beds for Residents.".
  Item gt_almanack "the Almanack of Usages" is gt_almanack_kind at offstage.
  Kind gt_sheet_kind "a Hospice sheet" is gear worth 0 weighing 1 described "A grey linen sheet, stamped in blue with a number, and under the number the Hospice's single word. The number on yours is the cot under the window that has never been dry. It is, in the Hospice's view, a bed.".
  Item gt_sheet_item "a Hospice sheet" is gt_sheet_kind at offstage.
  Relation gt_almanack_given(group). Relation gt_sheet(group). Relation gt_asked(group). Measure gt_tibb_retry(group). Relation gt_reason(group).
  Relation gt_q2_done(group). Relation gt_q3_done(group). Relation gt_kin_named(group). Relation gt_kin_none(group). Relation gt_summoned(group).
  Discovery gt_usages "The Hospice's Almanack of Usages: by day the city is masked and answers the mask; to name a masked person aloud is to be cried in every square; after the Ninth Bell the city is at home and bare, and a masked knock is a burglar.".
  Discovery gt_string_known "Mother Tibb ties a knot in a string for each Bare who dies under her roof, since the Bare have no names that can be written down: there are forty-one, and the Tuesdays are mostly the old.".
  Discovery gt_peck_name "Absalom Peck, the old man by the Hospice stove with a bottle between his boots, was the Serene in the Year of the Cullet Sluice, and was Named for it, and has been Bare for thirty-one years.".

  Person tibb "Mother Tibb" at hospice_hall {
    Role "the keeper of the Hospice of the Bare". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
    Offers lodging "a bed under a numbered sheet" for 0 coin.
    Greets "A square woman in a grey half-mask sits behind a long table on which are a ledger, a hand-bell and a folded sheet, and writes. The mask is the Hospice's own, and she wears it as other women wear spectacles, pushed up and forgotten. 'Face or no face?' she says, without looking up. 'It changes what I am permitted to say.'".
    Greets again "'Face or no face,' says Mother Tibb, to the ledger.".
  }
  // A mask is not lodged: the Hospice is the one room that speaks to the bare by day, and the one that will not speak to a face.
  Topic gt_tibb_masked with tibb "Speak to Mother Tibb" when masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "Mother Tibb looks at the mask in the way a custodian looks at a coat left on a bench. 'The Hospice is for the Bare,' she says, to the domino, not to whoever is in it. 'A mask in this hall is a burglar who has not yet made up his mind. Take it off at the door or go through it.' She goes back to her ledger. It is, you notice, more than anyone has said to you all day, and it was not said to you.".
  }
  Topic gt_tibb_almanack with tibb "Ask Mother Tibb for the Almanack of Usages" when not masked(actor) and not gt_almanack_given(actor) once {
    Says "'Everybody wants one and nobody has read it.' She does not look up; she slides it across the table with two fingers, as one passes a plate to a man one is not sure of. 'Three usages, one joke and one threat. The joke is the one about beds. I should read the threat first, if I were you; it is at the bottom, in the smaller type.' She has begun to write again. 'Do not give it to a mask. The mask will believe it.'".
    On discuss { Give gt_almanack to actor. Assert gt_almanack_given(actor). Assert knows(actor, gt_usages). }
  }
  Topic gt_tibb_bed with tibb "Ask Mother Tibb for a bed" when not masked(actor) and not gt_sheet(actor) and not gt_asked(actor) once {
    Says "'A bed,' she says, and uncaps the ink with the air of a woman who has uncapped it eleven thousand times. 'A bed needs a sheet. A sheet needs three answers. I do not make the law, I only have the ledger.' She turns it round so that you can read it upside down: NINE REASONS FOR A BARE. Sickness. Pilgrimage. Trade. Summons. Grief. The law. Weather. Curiosity, disfavoured. None, at the Mother's discretion. 'First. Why are you in Ombra? Everyone has chosen weather. I should choose weather.'".
    On discuss { Assert gt_asked(actor). }
  }
  Topic gt_a1_true with tibb "Tell her the truth: you came to see the city" answering gt_tibb_bed when not warrantHeld(actor) and not gt_reason(actor) {
    Says "'Curiosity.' She writes it, and then, in a smaller hand, the word disfavoured, as if sorry to have to. 'Column eight. You will be last to the stove. It is the truest of the nine and it has never helped anybody.' She dips the pen. 'Second.'".
    On discuss { Assert gt_reason(actor). }
  }
  Topic gt_a1_summons with tibb "Tell her the truth: the Watch has sent for you" answering gt_tibb_bed when warrantHeld(actor) and not gt_reason(actor) {
    Says "The pen stops. 'Summons.' She looks up at last, as far as your collar. 'The Watch does not send, the Watch summons; it is a different column and a better one, and it has not been written in this ledger for sixty-two years.' She writes it, slowly, and the pen is not quite steady. 'Then it is you,' she says. 'Well. Second.'".
    On discuss { Assert gt_reason(actor). Assert gt_summoned(actor). }
  }
  Action gt_a1_grief(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Mother Tibb you have come in grief, and look it" {
    Speaker tibb.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(tibb, site) and gt_asked(actor) and not gt_reason(actor) and not masked(actor) and watch(clock) >= gt_tibb_retry(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert gt_reason(actor). }
    On failure { Set gt_tibb_retry(actor) to watch(clock) + 6. }
    Result "'Grief.' She writes it in column five without a flicker, and blots it. 'Everyone is, a little, who comes by the delta road. Second.' You are not at all sure she has been taken in. You are quite sure she has been paid the compliment of being lied to well.".
    Otherwise "'Grief,' says Mother Tibb, and does not write it. 'For whom?' You find that you have not decided. 'Think about weather,' she says, kindly, and turns a page. She does not look up again for an hour.".
  }
  Action gt_a1_discretion(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Mother Tibb to use the Mother's discretion, and write none" {
    Speaker tibb.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(tibb, site) and gt_asked(actor) and not gt_reason(actor) and not masked(actor) and watch(clock) >= gt_tibb_retry(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert gt_reason(actor). }
    On failure { Set gt_tibb_retry(actor) to watch(clock) + 6. }
    Result "She considers you for the first time as a thing with an inside. 'None,' she says. 'At the Mother's discretion. I have used it four times in twenty-six years, and I have been right three.' She writes it very small. 'Second.'".
    Otherwise "'The discretion is mine,' says Mother Tibb, 'and I have not been moved to it. Choose again.' She does not look up again for an hour.".
  }
  Topic gt_tibb_q2 with tibb "Say you are ready for the second question" when gt_reason(actor) and not gt_q2_done(actor) once {
    Says "'Second.' She does not look up. 'How long do you propose to stay? The law gives the Bare nine days from the first Bell, and then the Hospice has no beds for Residents. I have to ask. I have asked it of a woman who was ninety.'".
  }
  Topic gt_a2_drawing with tibb "Say you will stay until the Drawing" answering gt_tibb_q2 when not gt_q2_done(actor) {
    Says "'Until the ninth night.' She writes it with something like relief. 'Everyone who is sensible says that. Nine days, and then you are somebody's problem.' She blots it. 'Third. It is the one people mind.'".
    On discuss { Assert gt_q2_done(actor). }
  }
  Topic gt_a2_unsure with tibb "Say you had not planned to leave" answering gt_tibb_q2 when not gt_q2_done(actor) {
    Says "'Undecided.' She writes it, and a second word beside it which you cannot read upside down, and it looks to be a longer word. 'It is not a column. I have made it a column. Third.'".
    On discuss { Assert gt_q2_done(actor). }
  }
  Topic gt_tibb_q3 with tibb "Say you are ready for the third question" when gt_q2_done(actor) and not gt_q3_done(actor) once {
    Says "'Third.' The pen is quite still. 'If you die under this roof, and some do, whom am I to write to?' She looks up, and the grey half-mask is the colour of the room. 'I do not ask it to be unkind. I ask it because there is a space in the ledger and I do not like to leave a space.'".
  }
  Topic gt_a3_name with tibb "Give her a name to write to" answering gt_tibb_q3 when not gt_q3_done(actor) {
    Says "She writes it with a clerk's care, and you see that she has done this many times and that a good half of the names she has been given have not been true. 'There,' she says. 'You are the kind that has someone. It is a great comfort to the ledger.' She stamps a grey sheet and pushes it across. 'Number seven. The cot under the window, which has never been dry. Do not take it up with the window.'".
    On discuss { Assert gt_q3_done(actor). Assert gt_sheet(actor). Assert gt_kin_named(actor). Give gt_sheet_item to actor. }
  }
  Topic gt_a3_none with tibb "Say there is no one" answering gt_tibb_q3 when not gt_q3_done(actor) {
    Says "She writes nothing. She puts the pen down, and takes a grey string from her apron and, with one practised movement, ties a knot in it, and hangs it on a nail behind her. 'That is yours,' she says. 'It saves time. I have never yet had to move one.' She stamps a sheet. 'Number seven. The cot under the window, which has never been dry.' She does not say it unkindly. That is the dreadful part of it.".
    On discuss { Assert gt_q3_done(actor). Assert gt_sheet(actor). Assert gt_kin_none(actor). Give gt_sheet_item to actor. }
  }
  // Without a sheet the Hospice does not make a bed up; with one, and bare, it does, for nothing, as the law says.
  Rule gt_hospice_refuses when company(?c) and (not gt_sheet(?c) or masked(?c)) and not refusesService(tibb, ?c) { Assert refusesService(tibb, ?c). }
  Rule gt_hospice_accepts when company(?c) and gt_sheet(?c) and not masked(?c) and refusesService(tibb, ?c) { Retract refusesService(tibb, ?c). }
  Rule gt_tibb_post when hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 21 and not at(tibb, hospice_hall) { Assert at(tibb, hospice_hall). }
  Rule gt_tibb_watch when (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 7) and not at(tibb, hospice_dorm) { Assert at(tibb, hospice_dorm). }

  // ── Absalom Peck (Round 3) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Thirty-one years ago he was the Serene, who stands in the public gallery in gold and white and says nothing. In the
  // Year of the Cullet Sluice he said nothing as he was bound to, and six hundred drowned, and the mob needed a face and
  // the Serene's was the one that could be named. He has been Bare ever since: drunk by day (it is tea), old at night, and
  // the one man in Ombra who knows who the Treasurer of that year became. She came to his bed every first night of the
  // Novena for thirty-one years, in the white, and sat for the length of a candle, and could not speak, since a
  // Registrar may not say a Named man's name. What he wants is that: his name, said kindly, once. What he holds is
  // the Sluice year and her name. He is moved by neither proof nor pressure; he is moved by being spoken to as a
  // person, in the dark, by someone who wants nothing of him; and he dies on the seventh night if no one does.
  Initially Assert named(peck).
  Person peck "Absalom Peck" at hospice_hall {
    Role "the oldest of the Hospice's Bare". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "In the best place by the stove, in a chair that everyone has the tact to leave to him, an old man sits with a bottle between his boots and the gravity of a bishop. His coat was good once; you can see the ghost of gold-and-white braid where it was picked off, thread by thread, by somebody patient. 'A new one,' he says, with great courtesy. 'Sit, sit; you are the weather's guest. I should rise, but I have given it up. Peck. Absalom Peck, since you will have it from the Mother in any case; do not trouble to look as if it meant anything. It used to.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says the old man, and lifts a hand an inch, as a hat.".
    Joins "The old man gets up, which takes some time, and takes his stick from where it leans, and his hat. 'A walk,' he says, to nobody. 'I have not had one with somebody since the Sluice.'".
    Leaves "The old man lowers himself, with great care, as one lowers something hot.".
  }
  Relation gt_peck_met(group). Relation gt_peck_seen(group). Relation gt_peck_wounded(group). Relation gt_peck_easy(group). Relation gt_peck_gone(group).
  Relation gt_peck_given(group). Relation gt_peck_wish(group). Relation gt_peck_candle(group).
  Relation gt_told_lady(group). Relation gt_told_treasurer(group). Relation gt_told_sluice(group).
  Relation gt_via_name(group). Relation gt_via_vigil(group). Relation gt_via_cast(group). Relation gt_via_chapel(group). Relation gt_via_confession(group).
  Relation gt_peck_sealed(group). Measure gt_peck_retry(group).
  Discovery gt_peck_wish "Absalom Peck would like, once, to hear his own name said kindly: not cried, as it was cried in every square, but said to him as to a person.".
  Discovery gt_peck_sober "Absalom Peck is a sober man playing a drunk: the bottle by his boot is tea, and has been for eleven years. A drunk is not asked questions; a drunk is handed things.".
  Discovery gt_peck_treasurer "The Treasurer of the Sluice year was a lamp-trimmer's daughter of nineteen, drawn honestly by the Urn and bad at it: nobody had told her the keepers' wages went by her seal.".
  Discovery gt_peck_lady "A woman in a white mask sat by Absalom Peck's bed for the length of a candle on the first night of every Novena for thirty-one years, and never spoke; this year she did not come.".
  Discovery gt_serene_knot "The Serene's Mask is tied with the gallery knot, which the wearer can undo with one pull of the left string; Peck was shown it on his first day, and no Serene has been shown it since.".
  Query gt_peck_open(a: group) means gt_peck_met(a) and not gt_peck_wounded(peck) and not gt_peck_given(peck) and not gt_peck_easy(peck) and not gt_peck_gone(peck).
  Query gt_peck_ready(a: group) means not masked(a) and gt_peck_open(a).
  // Where he sits: by the stove by day, in the end cot at night; in the cot all day once he is too ill to leave it.
  Rule gt_peck_stove when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 20 and day(clock) < 6 and not gt_peck_gone(peck) and not following(peck, party) and not at(peck, hospice_hall) { Assert at(peck, hospice_hall). }
  Rule gt_peck_cot_day when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 20 and day(clock) >= 6 and not gt_peck_easy(peck) and not gt_peck_gone(peck) and not following(peck, party) and not at(peck, hospice_dorm) { Assert at(peck, hospice_dorm). }
  Rule gt_peck_stove_easy when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 20 and day(clock) >= 6 and gt_peck_easy(peck) and not gt_peck_gone(peck) and not following(peck, party) and not at(peck, hospice_hall) { Assert at(peck, hospice_hall). }
  Rule gt_peck_cot_night when (hour(clock) >= 20 or hour(clock) < 8) and not gt_peck_gone(peck) and not following(peck, party) and not at(peck, hospice_dorm) { Assert at(peck, hospice_dorm). }
  // Brought out on the company's arm he is taken home again by evening on the seventh day: he will not die in a street.
  Rule gt_peck_home when day(clock) == 7 and hour(clock) >= 20 and following(peck, party) and not gt_peck_gone(peck) says "The old man stops at the next lamp and looks at it for some time. 'Home,' he says. 'Now, I think. Not for any reason.' He has already turned. Whatever he is going to do not to be dying in a street, he does it, and goes back up the road to the Hospice with his stick, alone." { Retract following(peck, party). Retract acceptsEscort(peck, party). Assert at(peck, hospice_dorm). }
  // Days of his decline, told to whoever is in the room.
  Observe peck_hall_cough at hospice_hall when at(peck, hospice_hall) and day(clock) >= 4 and day(clock) < 6 and not gt_peck_easy(peck) "By the stove the old man's cough has got into the hall's general noise, and the hall has made a space for it.".
  Observe peck_hall_easy at hospice_hall when at(peck, hospice_hall) and gt_peck_easy(peck) "The old man by the stove has a blanket over his knees that Mother Tibb is pretending she did not knit, and the bottle by his boot has gone. He sits as a man sits who is waiting for a ferry and is in no hurry for it.".
  Observe peck_hall_betrayed at hospice_hall when at(peck, hospice_hall) and gt_peck_given(peck) and not gt_peck_gone(peck) "The old man has turned his chair to face the wall. It is the first time anyone has seen him do it. The Hospice has understood that something has been said to somebody, and it is being polite about it in the loud, practised way of a room that has been betrayed before.".
  Observe peck_dorm_cot at hospice_dorm when at(peck, hospice_dorm) and day(clock) >= 6 and not gt_peck_easy(peck) and not gt_peck_gone(peck) "In the end cot, the old man lies propped on three pillows with his eyes open, breathing like a man carrying water up a stair. The candle-stub on the sill beside him has been trimmed, and is not lit.".
  Observe peck_dorm_empty at hospice_dorm when gt_peck_gone(peck) "The end cot has been stripped to its ticking, and the sheet folded on it, number nine, with its corners to the corners. On the sill a candle-stub has been lit, and burned down to the saucer, and nobody has taken the saucer away.".
  Observe peck_hall_gone at hospice_hall when gt_peck_gone(peck) "The best chair by the stove stands empty, and nobody has sat in it, and nobody will before the Novena is out. On the nail by the dormitory door the string has a fresh knot in it, tied tight by someone who did not want to tie it.".

  // The first day: a stranger by the stove, the name, the Urn, and a rule about the Bare's courtesy.
  Topic gt_peck_whoami with peck "Ask Absalom Peck what his name used to mean" when not masked(actor) and not knows(actor, gt_peck_name) once {
    Says "'It was read aloud a good deal; you must have heard it, in a manner of speaking, and not known it was a name.' He tips the bottle to his mouth with great grace, and sets it down. 'I was the Serene. I stood in the gallery in the gold-and-white and I said nothing, which is the whole of the Office, and I was very good at it.' He smiles at the stove. 'Then the Sluice. Then I was a great many things. Now I am by the stove. It is better.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, gt_peck_name). Assert gt_peck_met(actor). }
  }
  Topic gt_peck_sit with peck "Sit by the old man a while, and let him talk" when not masked(actor) and publicHours() and not gt_peck_wounded(peck) and not gt_peck_given(peck) once {
    Says "He talks as a man pours who has had practice: a long unbroken arc, not a drop lost. The Concord, the Urn, the winter the pigeons voted (they did not); the gallery, where one stands in gold and white and is a pillar; the inside of a mask, which smells, he says, of the last man. And in the middle of a sentence about eels: 'The girl was drawn honest. I watched the Urn give her up with my own eyes. Honest as rain. And after her it was never the same, the Urn. Never.' He looks at the bottle as if it had spoken. 'Ask the Mother about the weather,' he says.".
    On discuss { Assert gt_peck_met(actor). Assert knows(actor, lie_peck). }
  }
  // A mask is not spoken to by a Bare, and the Bare know it: Peck's courtesy is a bow, and nothing else.
  Topic gt_peck_bow with peck "Speak to the old man by the stove" when masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "The old man looks at the mask, and gets to his feet, which costs him, and bows from the hips as to a person of rank, and does not say a word. When you do not move on he bows again, slightly lower. It is the exact courtesy of the Bare to a face. He has no right to speak to you, and you, he is too well-bred to remark, have no right to be speaking to him. He sits down again with the care of a man lowering something hot.".
  }
  Topic gt_tibb_peck with tibb "Ask Mother Tibb about Absalom Peck" when not masked(actor) and not knows(actor, gt_peck_name) once {
    Says "'Peck.' She says it to the ledger. 'Absalom. I say it because he is Bare, and a Bare's name is only a noise, and he has had it said to him more than any man alive, and nobody ever meant it well.' She dips the pen. 'He was somebody, once, and it was the wrong somebody. He is in nine, at the end. He has been in nine for eleven years. I give him the bottle by day because he thinks I think it is gin.' She does not look up. 'Do not tell him that I know.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, gt_peck_name). }
  }

  // The same man at night: Tibb has taken the bottle, and he is simply old. He asks what you want, since everyone wants
  // something after dark; the answers are the first fork.
  Topic gt_peck_night with peck "Sit on the end of the old man's cot, after the lamp is turned down" when not masked(actor) and privateHours() and not gt_peck_given(peck) and not gt_peck_gone(peck) once {
    Says "He does not look drunk at all. He looks as if he had put on, for the night, his own face, and found it a little large. 'The Mother takes the bottle at the Ninth Bell. It is only tea, you know; she thinks I think it is gin.' He moves his feet to make room for you with great politeness. 'By day I am a drunk, which is a trade, like another, and the Bare have not many. At night I am merely old. What do you want of me? Everyone wants something, after dark.'".
    On discuss { Assert gt_peck_met(actor). }
  }
  Topic gt_pa_sluice with peck "Tell him you want to hear about the Sluice year" answering gt_peck_night when not gt_peck_wish(actor) {
    Says "'Ah.' He is not offended; he is only tired. 'Everyone does. They want the six hundred, and a face to put on them, and I have been that face and it was a good fit.' He folds his hands. 'I will tell it to nobody who wants it. I have decided. It is the one thing in my life I have decided. You may try; they have.'".
  }
  Topic gt_pa_nothing with peck "Tell him you want nothing of him" answering gt_peck_night when not gt_peck_wish(actor) {
    Says "He laughs, a short bark that turns into the cough and is a long time getting out of it. 'The first lie anyone has told me in a year, and a good one.' He wipes his mouth. 'If I were to ask for something, you understand, I am not asking, it would be this. Just to hear it said once. My name. By somebody who did not want a thing: not cried. I have been called it by forty thousand and none of them meant it as a name.' He looks away. 'It is nothing. It is an old man's whim.'".
    On discuss { Assert gt_peck_wish(actor). Assert knows(actor, gt_peck_wish). }
  }
  Topic gt_pa_sit with peck "Tell him you came only to sit" answering gt_peck_night when not gt_peck_wish(actor) {
    Says "'To sit.' He considers it, as a man considers an unfamiliar coin. 'Nobody has come to sit in the Hospice since the winter the pigeons voted.' He settles back against the three pillows. 'Then sit. I will not say a thing, and you will not say a thing, and it will be, I think, the best conversation I have had.' After a while he adds, in the dark, without turning his head: 'Not the Sluice. Never the Sluice. But a name said kindly would not come amiss, if a man were choosing.'".
    On discuss { Assert gt_peck_wish(actor). Assert knows(actor, gt_peck_wish). }
  }
  Topic gt_tibb_wish with tibb "Ask Mother Tibb what the old man wants" when privateHours() and not masked(actor) and gt_peck_met(actor) and not knows(actor, gt_peck_wish) once {
    Says "'He asked me once.' She is knotting a spare piece of string, which she does when she is not saying something. 'Eleven years ago, drunk, or being drunk. He said, say it to me, Mother, once, so I know it still works. And I could not, because I am the Hospice, and the Hospice has a mask on, and a masked woman who says a Named man's name is a masked woman who has said a name. So I said, go to bed, Mr Peck.' The string goes round her finger. 'It is a thing a stranger could do. Strangers are not Named for it. That is the only use of them.'".
    On discuss { Assert gt_peck_wish(actor). Assert knows(actor, gt_peck_wish). }
  }
  Topic gt_tibb_lady with tibb "Ask Mother Tibb who sits with Peck at the Novena" when privateHours() and not masked(actor) and knows(actor, gt_peck_name) and not knows(actor, gt_peck_lady) once {
    Says "She stops the string. 'Who told you that?' Nobody has. She tightens the knot she was tying until it must hurt her finger, and takes up the string again. 'A woman in a white mask,' she says. 'First night of every Novena, after the Ninth Bell, by the street door with her own key, which no one has ever asked her about. She sits by nine with a candle he has put out for her. She does not speak. She is gone before the candle is. Thirty-one years.' The knot tightens. 'I took her for one of the Chaplain's. I did not ask. You do not ask a white mask where it has been.' She glances at the end cot. 'She did not come this year.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, gt_peck_lady). }
  }

  // ── What the company may try with him, and what each costs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Four checks, four different things: reading a man (insight), knowing a sluice (lore), leaning on him (intimidation: it
  // works, and costs), and asking him straight (persuasion). None of them gets her name. That is given only to the
  // kindnesses below, because it is the one thing he has chosen not to say.
  Action gt_peck_read(actor: group, site: place) "Watch the old man's hands while he talks" {
    Speaker peck.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(peck, site) and gt_peck_ready(actor) and not gt_peck_seen(actor) and watch(clock) >= gt_peck_retry(actor).
    Time 3 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert gt_peck_seen(actor). Assert knows(actor, gt_peck_sober). }
    On failure { Set gt_peck_retry(actor) to watch(clock) + 36. }
    Result "You stop listening to what he says and watch what he does. The bottle goes to his mouth and he wets his lip; he does not drink. His hands are the steadiest in the room. He catches you at it, and after a moment inclines his head, as a fencer does. 'Tea,' he says, quite softly. 'Eleven years. The Mother thinks it is gin. A drunk is not asked questions; a drunk is handed things. It is a good trade, and you are the first to look at the hands.'".
    Otherwise "He is exactly as drunk as he appears, you decide, and then you are not sure, and then he has begun upon the pigeons again and the thought is gone. He settles his chin on his chest, and appears, for some hours, to be asleep.".
  }
  Action gt_peck_sluice(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the old man how the Cullet Sluice worked, as a thing that works" {
    Speaker peck.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(peck, site) and gt_peck_ready(actor) and not knows(actor, sluice_known) and watch(clock) >= gt_peck_retry(actor).
    Time 6.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, sluice_known). }
    On failure { Set gt_peck_retry(actor) to watch(clock) + 36. }
    Result "'On the Cullet there is a rack and a pawl,' you say, 'and the pawl is dogged by a seal, and a sluice-keeper is paid by the dogging.' Peck sets the bottle down. 'Nobody has asked me about the pawl in thirty-one years,' he says. 'They ask who. They have never once asked how.' And he tells it as a wright would: the keepers unpaid because the wages went by the Treasurer's seal and the Treasurer did not know they were hers to give; the keepers walking; the pawl left undogged in the Rains; the Cuff coming up the low islands in a night. Six hundred. 'I stood in the gallery,' he says. 'I said nothing. It was the whole of my Office. They cried my name by sunset.' He will not say whose seal. You do not ask.".
    Otherwise "You say pawl and rack and get the order wrong, and he looks at you with real kindness, which is the worst of it. 'No,' he says. 'No. It is not like that. Nobody knows what it is like.' He settles his chin on his chest, and appears, for some hours, to be asleep.".
  }
  Action gt_peck_press(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the old man the Watch will have it out of him, if you do not" {
    Speaker peck.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(peck, site) and gt_peck_ready(actor) and not knows(actor, gt_peck_treasurer) and watch(clock) >= gt_peck_retry(actor).
    Time 3 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, gt_peck_treasurer). Assert knows(actor, sluice_known). Assert gt_peck_wounded(peck). }
    On failure { Set gt_peck_retry(actor) to watch(clock) + 36. }
    Result "You say it as if you had the right. The old man's face does not change; it merely goes elsewhere, and what is left behind it answers, in a clear sober voice, like a clerk's. A girl of nineteen. A lamp-trimmer's daughter, drawn by the Urn, honest as rain. The keepers' wages went by her seal and nobody told her. Six hundred. 'There,' he says. 'There is your Sluice. You will want to wash your hands.' He turns his face to the stove. He does not speak to you again that day, and he will not look.".
    Otherwise "'I have been Named by forty thousand,' says the old man, mildly, 'and you are not as frightening as that.' He lifts the bottle. 'Try again when you have been cried in a square. It is a great teacher.' He settles his chin on his chest, and appears, for some hours, to be asleep.".
  }
  Action gt_peck_ask_plain(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the old man, plainly and without a threat, who the Treasurer was" {
    Speaker peck.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(peck, site) and gt_peck_ready(actor) and not knows(actor, gt_peck_treasurer) and watch(clock) >= gt_peck_retry(actor).
    Time 6.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, gt_peck_treasurer). }
    On failure { Set gt_peck_retry(actor) to watch(clock) + 36. }
    Result "He is silent so long that the stove ticks twice. 'Of the year,' he says at last. 'Not of the name. A girl of nineteen, a lamp-trimmer's daughter, drawn by the Urn as honest as rain, who was bad at the Treasury, as a girl of nineteen would be, and nobody had told her the keepers' wages went by her seal.' He shuts his mouth on the rest of it like a purse. 'That is all of that I can say, and I have said more than I said to the Chaplain.'".
    Otherwise "'Not today,' says the old man, pleasantly, 'and not in the hall, and not in that voice.' You have been, you realise, very nearly asked to leave by a drunk in a chair. He settles his chin on his chest, and appears, for some hours, to be asleep.".
  }
  Action gt_peck_apologise(actor: group, site: place) "Sit by the old man and say you are sorry" {
    Speaker peck.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(peck, site) and not masked(actor) and gt_peck_wounded(peck) and not gt_peck_gone(peck).
    Time 6.
    On success { Retract gt_peck_wounded(peck). }
    Result "He does not look at you for most of an hour. The Hospice goes on being loud around the two of you. Then, without turning, he passes you the bottle, and you drink the tea. 'You were frightened,' he says. 'Of an old man in a blanket.' He takes the bottle back. 'Go on, then, I forgive you. It is no trouble. I have had the practice.'".
  }

  // ── The kindnesses: each one is a way of saying his name that is not crying it ──────────────────────────────────────────
  // The name, said at night, bare, with nothing wanted: costs nothing but the knowing; the vigil costs a night; a cast of
  // his face costs Madame Pavane's price; the Chapel costs a walk; a confession costs a cleric and the seal. Each ends with
  // him at ease and the Round done, and each opens the telling in its own way. None can be done as a face: a mask is not
  // addressed by a Bare, and does not address one.
  Action gt_peck_namekind(actor: group, site: place) "Say the old man's name to him, softly, as you would to a friend" {
    Speaker peck.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(peck, site) and gt_peck_ready(actor) and knows(actor, gt_peck_name) and knows(actor, gt_peck_wish) and privateHours().
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert gt_peck_easy(peck). Assert gt_via_name(peck). }
    Result "You wait until the lamp is turned down and the dormitory has settled into its several keys. Then you say it: not Peck, not the Serene, not the thing it was cried as across every square by people who wanted somebody. You say it as one says it across a table, to a man one is glad has come. 'Absalom Peck.' For a time nothing happens at all. The old man looks at the ceiling. His mouth works once, as if the name were a coin he had been looking for the pocket of. 'Again,' he says. 'No. Don't. Once is what I asked for.' He lays the back of his wrist across his eyes, and neither of you looks at where the bottle goes.".
  }
  Action gt_peck_vigil(actor: group, site: place) "Sit up with the old man through the evening, and say nothing" {
    Speaker peck.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(peck, site) and gt_peck_ready(actor) and privateHours() and (hour(clock) >= 20 or hour(clock) < 3).
    Time 18.
    On success { Assert gt_peck_easy(peck). Assert gt_via_vigil(peck). }
    Result "You do not speak. He does not speak. The stove ticks, and the dormitory breathes, and about the second hour he stops arranging his face. At the third he puts out his hand and lays it, quite lightly, on your sleeve, as one touches a thing to be sure it is there; and leaves it. Nobody in thirty-one years has stayed in a room with him for no reason.".
  }
  Action gt_peck_confess(actor: group) "Hear the old man's confession, under the seal" {
    Speaker peck.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, confessionals) and at(peck, confessionals) and following(peck, actor) and gt_peck_ready(actor) and capable(actor, rites).
    Time 12.
    On success { Assert gt_peck_easy(peck). Assert gt_via_confession(peck). Assert gt_peck_sealed(actor). }
    Result "The confessional is the one place on the Island where a masked face and a bare one may speak as persons, and it has been unused by him for thirty-one years. He kneels, with difficulty, the stick across his knees, and says it into the grille in a small flat voice. Not the Sluice, which is the world's. The three seconds in the gallery when anyone might have spoken. He counts them aloud: one, two, three. 'And I did not.' The seal is on it. At the words of release he stays down so long that the lay-brother coughs; when he gets up he has left the stick on the floor, and has to be handed it.".
  }
  Action gt_peck_chapel(actor: group) "Stand with the old man at the Chapel's lamps while he lights one for the six hundred" {
    Speaker peck.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, nave) and at(peck, nave) and following(peck, actor) and gt_peck_ready(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert gt_peck_easy(peck). Assert gt_via_chapel(peck). }
    Result "The lamps for the dead burn in a rack by the nave door, each for a name that cannot be said; the Chaplain's boy keeps them trimmed. The old man stands in front of them with his hat in his hand until the boy has trimmed two wicks that did not need it. Then he takes a taper, and lights one, and does not say whose it is. He has not been through this door since the Sluice. Nobody stops him. Nobody notices; the Chapel is good at that, for the Bare. His hand is steady on the taper, and it is the first thing today that has not been a performance.".
  }
  Topic gt_peck_invite with peck "Ask the old man whether he would walk to the Chapel with you, for company" when gt_peck_ready(actor) and gt_peck_wish(actor) and not acceptsEscort(peck, actor) once {
    Says "He looks at you with a long, level look, and you see him decide whether to be insulted. 'The Chapel of the Bare Face,' he says. 'I have not been through that door since the Sluice.' He turns his hat in his hands. 'If you ask me to be carried I shall refuse; I am too old. If you ask me to be led I shall refuse; I am too proud.' The hat stops. 'You said company. It is the only word that was not an insult. Give me a minute to find my stick.'".
    On discuss { Assert acceptsEscort(peck, actor). }
  }
  // The Cast: a life-cast of his face for the Wall, which has had no Peck on it for thirty-one years (the Named are taken
  // down); Madame Pavane's price in coin, or asked for as a favour, for its own sake.
  Relation gt_cast_asked(group).
  Action gt_peck_cast_paid(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Madame Pavane six coin to take a cast of the old man's face, and no mask to go with it" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, site) and at(peck, site) and following(peck, actor) and gt_peck_open(actor) and masked(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 6.
    Time 12.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Increase quantity(pavane, gold) by 6. Assert gt_peck_easy(peck). Assert gt_via_cast(peck). }
    Result "He sits for the plaster with the gravity of a bishop at his own consecration, with a straw in each nostril and a smear of grease on his brows, and for the three-quarters of an hour that it takes to set he does not move a hair. When it is lifted off he asks, in a small voice, whether it came out; and Madame Pavane turns it over, and he looks at his own face in reverse, thirty years younger in the hollow than in the glass, and says nothing at all.".
  }
  Action gt_peck_cast_asked(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Madame Pavane to cast the old man's face for its own sake, with no mask to go with it" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, site) and at(peck, site) and following(peck, actor) and gt_peck_open(actor) and masked(actor).
    Time 12.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert gt_peck_easy(peck). Assert gt_via_cast(peck). }
    Result "She looks at the old man, and then at you, with the face of a craftsman whose client wants something that is not in the book. 'There is no fee for a face that nobody is going to wear,' she says at last. 'I should have to charge for the mask. Sit.' He sits for the plaster with a straw in each nostril and his hat on his knee, because nobody has told him to take it off. When it comes off he asks to hold it, and holds it a long while, hollow side up, like a bowl, and for once his mouth is not guarding anything.".
    Otherwise "'I cut faces for a reason,' says Madame Pavane, and goes back to her bench. 'Tell me what it is for, and I will cut it. Tell me it is for itself and I am a busy woman.'".
  }

  // The telling: what he says once he is at ease, in the order it comes. Each rule is one beat of it.
  Rule gt_tell_lady when gt_via_name(peck) and not gt_told_lady(peck) once says "'She came every first night of the Novena,' he says, to the ceiling, 'thirty-one years, in the white, by the street door with her own key. She sat where you are, for the length of a candle. She did not speak, because she could not: a Registrar may not say a Named man's name. I put the stub out for her myself, so she should have the light to sit by.' The wrist stays where it is. 'This year the stub went out and nobody came. I knew then. Nobody may say it, and I do not. I only say that I knew.'" teaches gt_peck_lady { Assert gt_told_lady(peck). }
  Rule gt_tell_treasurer when gt_peck_easy(peck) and not gt_told_treasurer(peck) and (not gt_via_name(peck) or gt_told_lady(peck)) once says "He tells it then, in the order it comes. 'Ysolde Marrick. A lamp-trimmer's girl of nineteen, drawn by the Urn as honest as rain, and bad at the Treasury, God keep her, as I should have been. She knew about wicks and nothing about seals. I could have told her; it was not the Serene's place to speak. And she knew my name, and did not say it, for thirty-one years, and I did not say hers.' He turns his head a little, toward nothing in particular. 'She became the Registrar. That is who sat by my bed. Do you see? It was the only way she had to say it.'" teaches marrick_was_treasurer { Assert gt_told_treasurer(peck). }
  Rule gt_tell_sluice when gt_told_treasurer(peck) and not gt_told_sluice(peck) and not knows(party, sluice_known) once says "'And the Sluice,' he says, 'for the tally. The keepers walked because the wages went by her seal. The pawl was left undogged in the Rains. The Cuff came up the low islands in the night, and six hundred drowned, and by sunset somebody had to have done it; and the Serene is the one whose name may be cried.' He shrugs, a small old man's shrug. 'It is not an injustice. It is only a city. It had to be somebody.'" teaches sluice_known { Assert gt_told_sluice(peck). }
  Rule gt_tell_knot when gt_told_treasurer(peck) and not knows(party, gt_serene_knot) once says "As he is settling, he says, as an afterthought: 'There is one thing in my gift, for what it is worth. The Serene's Mask is tied with the gallery knot. It comes off with one pull of the left string. They show it you on your first day, in the vestry, and no one shows the next. If the Serene who wears it now has forgotten, or was never shown, he may think he cannot take it off.' He closes his eyes. 'It would be an unkind thing to leave a man in a mask for want of a string.'" teaches gt_serene_knot { }
  Rule gt_peck_round when gt_peck_easy(peck) and not roundDone(party, r_peck) { Assert roundDone(party, r_peck). }
  Rule gt_peck_dies at hospice_dorm when nightCount(clock) == 7 and hour(clock) >= 3 and hour(clock) < 6 and not gt_peck_easy(peck) and not gt_peck_gone(peck) says "Some time after the Third Bell of the morning the breathing at the end of the dormitory changes its key, and goes on in the lower one for a little, and stops as a clock stops that no one was watching. Mother Tibb is at the cot before you have understood it. She does not speak. She stands for a moment with the back of her hand against her grey half-mask. Then she takes the string from its nail." { Assert gt_peck_gone(peck). Assert at(peck, offstage). Retract following(peck, party). }

  // Betraying him: the Watch will take his statement; and the Hospice will take it that you did.
  Topic gt_vail_peck with vail "Tell the Sergeant where the Serene of the Sluice year is to be found" when knows(actor, gt_peck_name) and not gt_peck_given(peck) and not gt_peck_easy(peck) and not gt_peck_gone(peck) once {
    Says "'Peck,' says Sergeant Vail. 'Absalom.' She writes it in her book at once, and underlines it, and you see that she has known where he was for thirty-one years and has been waiting, with the whole patience of the Watch, for somebody to tell her officially. 'A witness to the Sluice. The Hearing will want him.' She looks at you, and something almost like approval crosses a domino. 'The Watch is obliged. You have been a help, and your count shall be the lighter by one.' It is exactly as simple as that. You look for what it has cost, and find nothing, and go on looking.".
    On discuss { Assert gt_peck_given(peck). Decrease heat(actor) by 1 or to nothing. Retract acceptsEscort(peck, actor). }
  }
  Rule gt_peck_given_word when gt_peck_given(peck) and not gt_peck_gone(peck) and at(party, hospice_hall) once says "A Watch domino has been to the Hospice, and gone, and left behind it a card in the ledger in Mother Tibb's hand: ATTEND. The old man has read it, and has read it again. He says nothing. It is not what he has been waiting for, and he knows who it was that told them." { }
  Topic gt_tibb_cold with tibb "Ask Mother Tibb for your bed" when gt_sheet(actor) and not masked(actor) and (gt_peck_wounded(peck) or gt_peck_given(peck)) {
    Says "'There is no bed.' She does not look up. 'There are nine. There is one with a sheet of yours on it, and I am not able to find it.' The pen goes on. 'I do not ask what is said in my hall. I ask only that it should not be said to an old man who has been very kind to the Hospice for eleven years and has never once asked it for anything.' She turns a page. 'The old man's door is the end cot. I should say so, if I were you, to the old man.'".
  }
