  // ── Cosimo ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule lc_fate_cosimo_laugh when newsHour() and loversTogether(party) and lcByLaugh(party) once says "Of Cosimo Dray: he was married in the spring, by the Chaplain, in a Heron's cowl that he removed at the door of the Chapel as the Concord allows. His wife, who rows the Row ferry, took the oars the next morning. He pays two, and she charges two, for one umbrella and two persons: it is, they say on the Row, the only fare in Ombra that was ever settled by a laugh. He has entered the sound of it, once, in the Hall's margin, in a column that has no heading. Nobody has been able to make the figure balance." { }
  Rule lc_fate_cosimo_light when newsHour() and loversTogether(party) and not lcByLaugh(party) once says "Of Cosimo Dray: he has not entered the crossing in any book. He keeps the tin box on the table with the lock turned for the first time, for it is empty, and he takes a Penhallow's umbrella to the ferry every morning, and holds it, by the Twelfth, over two. The Hall's Standard Room has a clerk who now says, of the third desk, that it is the only one in the building that is more than it weighs." { }
  Rule lc_fate_cosimo_civil when newsHour() and lcCivil(party) once says "Of Cosimo Dray: he quarrels with the ferrywoman at eight and at six about whether an open umbrella is a passenger, and loses, and pays. At night in his room he writes to the Lamp that he is a better man by post. She writes him that he is no such thing, and that she will have the fare. He considers it, on the whole, the best arrangement of his life, and has been heard to say so, once, to a Heron who will not repeat it." { }
  Rule lc_fate_cosimo_dark when newsHour() and lcMetDark(party) once says "Of Cosimo Dray: he crossed the Cuff in the Swap with a stranger who said the best thing he has ever heard anyone say in a boat, and never knew who. He thinks of it at night. He writes to the Lamp that he met a person, once, a little like her. She writes back that she, too, once crossed with a man whose sentences were a little like his. Neither says what is plain to the Crow in the arcade, who sets both letters down, and says nothing." { }
  Rule lc_fate_cosimo_estranged when newsHour() and lcEstranged(party) once says "Of Cosimo Dray: he rides the ferry with his umbrella furled, and pays a fare that is not asked, and has stopped writing. He is a very good third clerk, and is spoken of at the Hall as a man who has found his figures at last. The tin box is under the bed. It is locked." { }
  Rule lc_fate_cosimo_unmet when newsHour() and not lcOutcome(party) and not lcEstranged(party) once says "Of Cosimo Dray: he went to the Row quay on the Swap with a spare in his handkerchief, and gave it to a stranger who was kind, and crossed, and came home, and entered nothing. He writes to the Lamp on Thursday. He does not know that on the eight o'clock ferry he is paying her fare. It is, the Crow in the arcade has decided, still a great deal." { }

  // ── Rill ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule lc_fate_rill_together when newsHour() and loversTogether(party) once says "Of Rill Ketch: she dictates no more letters. She says what she has to say to a clerk in a Heron's cowl, in the boat, on the Cuff, and he says what he has to say to her, and neither has needed a Crow since. She laughs, now, in public. The Cuff, which has been listening for years for the sound of a sheet being torn, is said to have grown fond of it." { }
  Rule lc_fate_rill_civil when newsHour() and lcCivil(party) once says "Of Rill Ketch: she charges the Heron for his umbrella every morning, and he pays. She writes him on Tuesdays, in the Crow's hand, in a style she has begun to claim, in the face of all the evidence, as her own. She has a good deal of the evidence. She is, the Drip says, perfectly insufferable about it." { }
  Rule lc_fate_rill_dark when newsHour() and lcMetDark(party) once says "Of Rill Ketch: she rowed a stranger across the Cuff in the Swap, and has told nobody what he said. She writes to the Heron that she met a man, once, a little like him; she signs it with a lamp. She has not changed her fare." { }
  Rule lc_fate_rill_estranged when newsHour() and lcEstranged(party) once says "Of Rill Ketch: she goes on rowing the Row ferry. She goes on taking his coin, which is the fare, and not a farthing over, and does not look at his hands. The lantern in the stern burns every night; she does not write by it." { }
  Rule lc_fate_rill_unmet when newsHour() and not lcOutcome(party) and not lcEstranged(party) once says "Of Rill Ketch: she crossed the Swap as the Usage requires, in a stranger's spare, and gave it back to the stranger, and has gone on. She writes by the lantern on Tuesdays. She tells the Crow what to say, and the Crow puts it right. Every morning at eight a clerk with an umbrella pays her his fare, and every morning she says four." { }

  // ── Hester Lyle ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule lc_fate_lamb_gone_half when newsHour() and lcSurrendered(party) and lcWarnedHalf(party) once says "Of Hester Lyle: she gave the Book of Hands to the Warden's man at the Ninth Bell on the sixth day, with half its pages cut away by clients who had been warned in the night; and he read what was left, and found, among the baker's brothers and the widow's hats, a good deal that he could not use. Her board is turned to the wall. She writes, now, only for those who come to the booth after dark. It is, she says, a smaller trade, and an honester." { }
  Rule lc_fate_lamb_gone when newsHour() and lcSurrendered(party) and not lcWarnedHalf(party) once says "Of Hester Lyle: she gave the Book of Hands to the Warden's man at the Ninth Bell on the sixth day, and her board is turned to the wall. The stool is gone in. Four hundred people read, that week, in the Warden's house, by a man who was not trained to understand them; and four hundred did not come to her again. She writes nothing. In the arcade it is thought that a Crow who has been read is a Crow who has been unfaced." { }
  Rule lc_fate_lamb_burned when newsHour() and lcBurned(party) once says "Of Hester Lyle: she burned the Book of Hands in her own stove, and keeps what was in it by heart, and writes on at the last stall under the awning, one letter at a time, with no ledger at all, as the first of the Crows did. The man in the key-grey called twice, and went away twice. 'It is a worse place for them,' she says, 'and a safer.' She has taken, it is said, a prentice, a girl who cannot spell, to whom she is teaching nothing in the world but what a letter is for." { }
  Rule lc_fate_lamb_sealed_read when newsHour() and lcSealed(party) and lcRead(party) once says "Of Hester Lyle: she got the Book of Hands back, and knew at once, by the way the sailcloth lay, that it had been read. She did not say so. She put it on the shelf behind the baskets. She writes on, in the last stall, with a certain reserve; and has been seen, at night, in her booth, to turn it, now and then, face to the wall." { }
  Rule lc_fate_lamb_sealed when newsHour() and lcSealed(party) and not lcRead(party) once says "Of Hester Lyle: she got the Book of Hands back across her own stall, sealed as it had left her, and put it on the shelf behind the baskets, and did not open it to see. The man in the key-grey, who had no writ to bring to a Warrant, was recalled to the Key. The Warden has taken it as the greatest insult of his year, and has made it, in a long and quiet way, her fault." { }
  Rule lc_fate_lamb_warned when newsHour() and lcWarned(party) and not lcSealed(party) and not lcBurned(party) and not lcSurrendered(party) once says "Of Hester Lyle: four hundred people, who had been told by a bare face in the night that the Warden wanted their secrets, cut the pages out of her book with their own knives, and her ledger went to the Warden's man on the sixth day thin as a prayer-book. She has had, since, a great many callers. They say nothing; they stand a while in the arcade; they order a letter, and when it is written, tell her the whole of the thing again, as if it had never been said." { }
  Rule lc_fate_lamb_decoy when newsHour() and lcDecoyPassed(party) and not lcSealed(party) and not lcBurned(party) and not lcSurrendered(party) and not lcWarned(party) once says "Of Hester Lyle: she did not know until the Chapel's last bell that the Warden's man had been given a book of landladies and hats, by a hand that was not hers. She has since been seen to look at the spine of every book in her stall with a thoughtful eye, and to say of one, aloud, to nobody, that there is a place in it where the sand does not come out." { }
  Rule lc_fate_lamb_index when newsHour() and lcIndexGiven(party) and not lcSealed(party) and not lcBurned(party) and not lcSurrendered(party) and not lcWarned(party) and not lcDecoyPassed(party) once says "Of Hester Lyle: she gave the Warden's man her index, the names without the words, and kept her book. Four hundred doors were knocked at in the Row that week by the Key's clerks, who were met, at every one of them, by a person with nothing to say. She says she did not betray a secret. She does not say that four hundred people learned that their names were in the Warden's pocket, and several have stopped coming." { }

  // ── The umbrella-makers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule lc_fate_row_merged when newsHour() and lcMerged(party) once says "Of Maud Orrell and Silas Haskew: they have cut a door through the wall between the shops, and sold, since the Deepening, four thousand umbrellas under a single board. They agree on nothing; they have agreed on this, and on very little else, with great vehemence, over a tray of oilcloth. It is said that when the bell rings for the Row's Trial they sit on the judge's stool together, bare, and the stool holds." { }
  Rule lc_fate_row_wed when newsHour() and lcWedded(party) once says "Of Maud Orrell and Silas Haskew: they will be, in the spring, a mother of the bride and a father of the groom, and have been heard to say so, without ceasing, in the same breath, to every person on the Row. The board over each shop still says THE FIRST. Under both of them, in a fresh hand, somebody has added a pair of initials joined by a stitch." { }
  Rule lc_fate_row_patent_o when newsHour() and lcPatentO(party) once says "Of Maud Orrell and Silas Haskew: Ostler's has the ribbon, and the queue; Penhallow's has the shutters half down and a boy sweeping nothing. Maud Orrell does not mention it. She has taken to walking past her rival's door at six in the evening with her umbrella furled, as one walks past a house in which there has been a death." { }
  Rule lc_fate_row_patent_p when newsHour() and lcPatentP(party) once says "Of Maud Orrell and Silas Haskew: Penhallow's has the ribbon, and the queue; Ostler's has the shutters half down and a girl in the door with her arms folded over her apron. Silas Haskew has entered the judgement in his register, in full, in a hand that does not shake, and drawn a line under it. He has not drawn the other line." { }
  Rule lc_fate_row_funeral when newsHour() and lcFuneral(party) once says "Of Maud Orrell and Silas Haskew: Ned Orrell was buried from the Drip chapel in the rain, with an umbrella over his coffin from each shop, which nobody remarked on, because nobody on the Row had the heart. The Concord ended the Feud three hundred years ago. It has not ended on Umbrella Row, which has just discovered that it was not as long ago as it had thought." { }
  Rule lc_fate_row_hurt when newsHour() and lcDuelled(party) and not lcFuneral(party) and not lcWarOver() once says "Of Maud Orrell and Silas Haskew: Ned Orrell carries his arm in a sling to this day, and Kit Haskew has a scar on the side of his head like a mask he did not choose. Neither shop sells to anyone who has been in the other. The boards still say THE FIRST. The Row, which has been waiting forty years to see what a duel would be like, has seen one, and does not, on the whole, wish to again." { }
  Rule lc_fate_row_quiet when newsHour() and lcQuiet(party) and not lcDuelled(party) and not lcWarOver() once says "Of Maud Orrell and Silas Haskew: the cousins were paid off and went home. The boards still say THE FIRST, and the two shops are still eleven paces apart, door to door; but there is, since the Deepening, a stool under the Usages, bare, and a rule that on the Third Day somebody sits on it. It is generally held that a quarrel which has a stool is half a quarrel." { }
  Rule lc_fate_children_wed when newsHour() and lcWedded(party) once says "Of Wyn Orrell and Tam Haskew: they will marry at the Chapel in the spring. Each has taken off the Cockle in the lane, in the dark, at the Ninth Bell, and looked at a face she or he had known since they could walk and had never looked at. They say it is the only time in their lives they have been introduced." { }
  Rule lc_fate_children_met when newsHour() and lcChildrenMet(party) and not lcWedded(party) once says "Of Wyn Orrell and Tam Haskew: they know, now, whose children they are, and have gone on meeting at the pond. They stand a good deal nearer. They have said nothing at home, and each is waiting for the other's family to be the first to see sense, which, by the habit of both families, may take some time." { }
  Rule lc_fate_children_unknown when newsHour() and not lcChildrenMet(party) and not lcWedded(party) once says "Of Wyn Orrell and Tam Haskew: they go on meeting at the eel-pond at six, in their Cockles, a yard apart, looking at an old eel in the sixth flume. Neither has asked the other's name. It will be, the Drip has decided, a long courtship, and a short one if anybody has the sense to cough." { }

  // ── Barnaby Sweet and Old Gudge ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule lc_fate_sweet_saved when newsHour() and lcSweetBack(party) and lcSweetSaved(party) once says "Of Barnaby Sweet: he did not lose his face. He does not entirely know why; he has been told that a Bare read a Usage, and has put it down to an unusual form of luck. He tallies at the Coffee-house in his Magpie, and pays his twelve coin, in installments, and has been seen to stop at the eel-pond on the way home, and take his hand from his cheek, and look at his reflection a while." { }
  Rule lc_fate_sweet_won when newsHour() and lcSweetBack(party) and lcGudgeBeaten(party) and not lcSweetSaved(party) once says "Of Barnaby Sweet: his silver won the race, and is on the Coffee-house's bill of fare, on Fridays, with a mark in the margin that nobody has ever explained. He is a Magpie of the Exchange, and a legend on the Row, and he says, to anyone who will listen, that it was the best bet of his life, and that he would not do it again for a kingdom." { }
  Rule lc_fate_sweet_redeemed when newsHour() and lcSweetBack(party) and not lcSweetSaved(party) and not lcGudgeBeaten(party) once says "Of Barnaby Sweet: he has his face back, from the wall of the shed, with the tag still on the string; he keeps the tag. It is the only face in the Drip that has been lost and returned, and he wears it with a kind of attention, as a man wears a coat that has been mended. He tallies to a hair, and is very rarely heard to laugh." { }
  Rule lc_fate_sweet_new when newsHour() and lcSweetNew(party) and not lcSweetBack(party) once says "Of Barnaby Sweet: he tallies at the Coffee-house in a Magpie that nobody has seen before. It sits an inch high, and is wearing in. The Exchange has been very decent about it, and has, in the manner of the Exchange, not mentioned it once. He still has his hand at his cheek, a little, as if to see where the old one went." { }
  Rule lc_fate_sweet_slate when newsHour() and lcSweetSlate(party) and not lcSweetBack(party) and not lcSweetNew(party) once says "Of Barnaby Sweet: the slate outside the Tally Coffee-house is the Exchange's most consulted instrument. A bare man stands beside it, answering nobody, and the Bare of the Hospice queue at his elbow with their purses, and the Magpies, who have always been jealous of an honest sum, say that he is the only tallyman in the Row who has ever been trusted by a stranger. There is talk of letting it become a custom." { }
  Rule lc_fate_sweet_tallied when newsHour() and lcSweetTallied(party) and not lcSweetBack(party) and not lcSweetNew(party) and not lcSweetSlate(party) once says "Of Barnaby Sweet: his debt was paid, by a Bare, from the Coffee-house's own coin; he has no face, and nine days at the Hospice, and nothing in the world he knows how to do. Mother Tibb has given him a bed and a list of reasons, and he has been seen on the Hospice steps, counting the Bare as they come in, under his breath, by the head, for something to count." { }
  Rule lc_fate_sweet_lost when newsHour() and lcSweetLost(party) and not lcSweetBack(party) and not lcSweetNew(party) and not lcSweetSlate(party) and not lcSweetTallied(party) once says "Of Barnaby Sweet: he went to the Hospice on the fourth day, as a man must who has no face, and out at the Gate on the thirteenth. Nobody is sure where. There is a tallyman, they say, in a river town to the south, who does sums for nothing, bare, in a market, and is, apparently, never wrong." { }
  Rule lc_fate_gudge_beaten when newsHour() and lcGudgeBeaten(party) once says "Of Old Gudge: he took the first defeat of his life on the tub with the net across his knees, and has since hung a new tag on the wall of the shed, which says, in the spidery hand, in place of the weight of an eel, WON. The pond is, he says, exact. He has been heard, once, to add that it is a good thing to be reminded." { }
  Rule lc_fate_gudge_kept when newsHour() and lcGudgeKept(party) and not lcSweetBack(party) once says "Of Old Gudge: he hung the thirty-second face on the wall of the shed, with the weight of its eel written under it, and sits under it, at night, with a lantern. The pond is exact. There is, he says, nothing to be said against exactness, except that it makes a very quiet house." { }
  Rule lc_fate_gudge_returned when newsHour() and lcGudgeKept(party) and lcSweetBack(party) and not lcGudgeBeaten(party) once says "Of Old Gudge: there is a space on the wall of the shed where the thirty-second face used to hang, and he has not filled it. People say it is the Drip's single oddest monument. He says nothing of it. He has been known to look at the space for a long time, at night, in the light of a lantern, and then take the net down off its nail and go out to the pond, and stand a while, in the rain, with the eels." { }
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/mage.kyr:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The Fit ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The mage's research: of Likeness, a spell for making a face hold. Four stages: (1) Dr Thole's failing theory in the
  // Collegium of Measures; (2) three sources, each a different understanding (Form at Madame Pavane's casts, Measure at
  // the Standard Pound, Cost at the drowned mask or at the Warden of Locks' night table); (3) the synthesis, a lead
  // chosen, and a Master who must be made to change his mind; (4) the casting at the Urn on the ninth night.
  // The reward is a lesson from Thole (the shared `train_member` in belongings.kyr, which wants a student who can be
  // taught it and twenty experience) plus a book that raises Intelligence. Only a mage can be taught; anyone with lore
  // can assist, and reads the treatise for its margins.
  // What a level-1 mage can actually learn and prepare was measured in play (see notes-counting.md): a first-level
  // spell is prepared at once; a second-level one is learned and waits for third-level slots, which a company that
  // ends the book on 1000 experience does not reach. So each lead teaches one of each.

  // ── The Master of Measures ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery mg_theory "Dr Thole's treatise On the Held Shape says a face is a shape held by bone, muscle and nerve, and that a mask cut to its measure must hold; the Fitting-frame measures to a sixty-fourth of an inch, and every mask it cuts falls off; Thole says the frame is warped.".
  Discovery mg_failure "The Collegium has a hundred and four masks cut by the Fitting-frame, and not one stays on a face; Thole has begun to wonder, in private, whether it is the rule that forbids masks over a measuring instrument, or the frame.".
  Discovery mg_clue_form "Dr Thole's rival, Madame Pavane, casts every citizen at sixteen in plaster by the feel of her thumbs, with no measurement at all; and her masks fit.".
  Discovery mg_clue_measure "The Standard Pound in the Hall of Weights fits every beam on the Row and has never been measured to a sixty-fourth; Thole would like to know why a pound fits.".
  Discovery mg_clue_cost "A mask in the Drip fits nobody and its maker is ashamed of it; and the Warden of Locks says the mask of his Office has cost him more than it should: two places where a face is paid for.".
  Relation mg_audience(group). Relation mg_engine_seen(group). Relation mg_thole_agrees(group). Relation mg_taught(group). Relation mg_studied(group). Relation mg_margin_given(group).
  Person thole "Dr Aurelian Thole" at collegium_study {
    Role "the Master of Measures".
    Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Greets "In the middle of the workroom, in a chair on wheels with a rug over its knees, sits a very old man in a gown the colour of ink, with an ear-trumpet as long as a child's trombone laid across his lap like a sleeping pet. This is Aurelian Thole, eighty, Master of Measures, who has been deaf for twenty years and has told nobody, on the grounds that nobody has asked. From the arm of the chair hangs a slate on a string, and on the slate, in a hand that has not wavered since the Third Bell of 1241: STATE UNITS.".
    Greets again "Dr Thole looks at your lips, and then at his slate, and sighs, and taps the word UNITS.".
  }
  Rule mg_thole_hours when not at(thole, collegium_study) { Assert at(thole, collegium_study). }
  Observe mg_thole_nod near thole when privateHours() and at(thole, collegium_study) "He is awake, and has been for some hours, and is trying to look as if he were not; a man whose arithmetic goes on in the dark, where nobody can mark it.".
  // Getting his ear. He is deaf and proud; the Collegium has a form for everything, and the form for a question is the slate.
  // Either you can put a question in the units the Collegium asks for, or you can speak the old recitative into the trumpet.
  Action mg_slate(actor: group, site: place) "Write your question on his slate, with its units" {
    Speaker thole.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(thole, site) and not mg_audience(actor).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert mg_audience(actor). }
    Result "You write: HOW LONG HAS THE FRAME BEEN IN ERROR; and, because the slate says STATE UNITS, you add, in years. Thole reads it, and reads the unit, and his whole face opens like a man handed a lit lamp in a cellar. 'Years!' he says aloud, in a voice meant for a lecture-hall. 'Someone has put the years! In eleven years of correspondence nobody has put the years.' He pushes the trumpet off his knee. You are, it appears, in.".
    Otherwise "You write: A LONG TIME. He reads it with the patience of a very large tortoise, and writes under it HOW LONG? and hands the slate back. You spend the better part of an hour pacing out the workroom, because he has found it necessary, in the first instance, to know how big it is.".
  }
  Action mg_trumpet(actor: group, site: place) "Speak into the ear-trumpet in the Collegium's old recitative" {
    Speaker thole.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(thole, site) and not mg_audience(actor).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert mg_audience(actor). }
    Result "You put your mouth to the brass and say it, not as speech but as the Collegium taught its students to say a figure across the Quad: on a note, in measures, each number held a beat longer than the last. Thole's head comes up like a dog's. He has heard it. It goes into him not as a word but as a bar of weather. 'Nobody has done that,' he says, 'since Tollemache,' and then does not say anything for some time, and wipes his eye with the cuff of the gown, as if it had got there by mistake.".
    Otherwise "The trumpet takes your voice and does something to it that you cannot account for. He winces, and leans away, and writes on the slate, in the manner of a man correcting a pupil's gait: PLEASE.".
  }
  Topic mg_thole_treatise with thole "Ask him for the treatise, On the Held Shape" when mg_audience(actor) once {
    Says "'The Held Shape.' He is already pulling a leather roll from under the rug, though you have not asked him in any form that he could have read. 'A face is a shape that is held. Held, you see, by the structure: bone, muscle, the long habit of the nerve. A mask cut to that shape must hold on it as a cork holds in a bottle. The Frame takes the measure of the shape to a sixty-fourth of an inch, and the mask cut by it must hold.' He taps the roll. 'It does not hold. The Frame is warped. It has been warped since 1269, and will be corrected when the Bursar sends the brass.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mg_theory). }
  }
  Topic mg_thole_wall with thole "Ask him about the masks on the walls" when mg_audience(actor) and knows(actor, mg_theory) once {
    Says "'A hundred and four,' says Thole. 'Perfect. Perfect. They are perfectly, perfectly, perfectly in error.' He pats the nearest; it swings on its ear-hole, empty. 'One for every Collegiate head since the Frame was made. Not one has stayed on. It is a rule of the house that nobody shall do arithmetic in a mask, and I have begun, lately, to wonder, at night, whether the rule is in the habit of the house, or in the Frame.' He looks, quickly, at your face, and away. 'You did not hear that. I said it to the slate.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mg_failure). }
  }
  Topic mg_thole_pavane with thole "Ask who else has tried to cut a mask that holds" when mg_audience(actor) and knows(actor, mg_theory) once {
    Says "'Pavane,' says Thole, with such violence that the trumpet slides off his knee. 'Madame Pavane. In Maskers' Lane. She casts. In plaster, from the living, at sixteen: every citizen of Ombra, I understand, in a cellar. Not one measurement among them. It is done by the feel of a woman's thumbs.' He retrieves the trumpet. 'And her masks fit.' He looks at the wall of his own. 'I should not like it to be thumbs.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mg_clue_form). }
  }
  Topic mg_thole_pound with thole "Ask whether anything in Ombra has ever been made to fit anything" when mg_audience(actor) and knows(actor, mg_theory) once {
    Says "He considers the question at some length, in a great stillness. 'The Standard Pound,' he says at last, like a man naming a rival. 'In the Hall of Weights, in a case. It fits every beam on the Row, and the Drip's, and the Hill's. It has never been measured to the sixty-fourth. Nobody has dared; the Hall would take it as an insult.' He rubs the trumpet. 'A pound fits and a face does not. I have never been able to say why it is not the same thing.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mg_clue_measure). }
  }
  Topic mg_thole_price with thole "Ask what he would give for a mask that held" when mg_audience(actor) and knows(actor, mg_theory) once {
    Says "'Give.' He seems to take the word out and look at it. 'I am eighty. I have given forty years, to a frame.' A long pause. 'There is a story in the Drip of a mask that fits nobody, and the boy who cut it; I have not been told it. And the Warden of Locks, whose clocks I mend, tells me that the mask of his Office has cost him a great deal more than it should, and will not say what. I do not follow the Row.' He smooths the rug. 'But I notice where a man pays for a thing. That is all arithmetic is.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mg_clue_cost). }
  }
  // The frame at work: a hundred and fourth mask, cut in front of the company, falls off before anyone has finished
  // looking at it.
  Action mg_engine(actor: group, site: place) "Ask him to run the Fitting-frame on a plaster face" {
    Speaker thole.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(thole, site) and mg_audience(actor) and knows(actor, mg_theory) and not mg_engine_seen(actor).
    Time 4.
    On success { Assert mg_engine_seen(actor). Assert arcBegun(actor, hand_likeness). }
    Result "A hundred feelers come down on the plaster, delicately, each on its jewel; a bell rings; a brass arm pares a sheet of lacquered leather; and a mask comes out of the frame, a thing of such flawless correspondence that it makes the plaster look approximate. Thole fits it to the plaster, where it sits like a lid. Then he fits it to the face of his own student, who has come in to hold the lamp, and it holds for about as long as a held breath, and slides off, and rolls across the floor, and stops with its hollow upward. 'You see,' says Thole, not unkindly, to the slate.".
  }

  // ── Stage two: three sources ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Each gives a different understanding of why a mask fits. The company may take them in any order; each has a second
  // way in, in a different place and at a different cost, and a deeper reading for those who have done other work in the
  // city first.
  Discovery mg_form "A face is a shape that something is holding; a cast keeps the shape and loses the holder, so every cast is of a face at rest, and nobody has one.".
  Discovery mg_form_deep "On the Wall of Faces the casts taken at sixteen keep, in the lines about the mouth, the very habit of holding the face had: a mask cut from them is cut from a person, and not from a shape.".
  Discovery mg_measure "A pound is not the bronze; it is a promise two strangers keep about it, and a thing fits when both sides are held to the same measure.".
  Discovery mg_measure_custom "A measure that is wrong by the same amount every time is not false but fitted: a custom is an error that everyone has agreed to keep.".
  Discovery mg_cost "A mask that fits is a face somebody has given up: the Key costs its wearer his name, the drowned mask the one who would have claimed it. The price of a fit is whoever the face was cut from.".
  // Form, at the casts of the living (Pavane's cellar) or the dead (the plaster Masters of the Collegium's hall).
  Action mg_read_casts(actor: group, site: place) "Read the casts on the Wall of Faces for what they keep" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, cast_cellar) and knows(actor, mg_theory) and not knows(actor, mg_form) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, mg_form). Assert knows(actor, mg_form_deep). }
    Result "Hundreds of faces on shelves: all sixteen, all with their eyes shut and their mouths a little closed, as a face is when someone has asked it, very nicely, to hold still. You stop looking at the shape, and look at the lines about the mouth. In every one, faint as the memory of a hand on a banister, there is the habit of the person: the corner that went down when they were afraid, the lip that was bitten. The plaster has kept not the shape of a face but what the face was doing to hold itself. Pavane's masks fit because they are cut from the holding.".
    Otherwise "You walk the shelves with the lamp until your eyes are full of plaster. Every face is perfect, and every face is a stranger's, and you carry nothing up the stair but the sense that you were told something by someone speaking in another room.".
  }
  Action mg_read_masters(actor: group, site: place) "Read the plaster Masters of the Collegium for what they keep" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, collegium_hall) and knows(actor, mg_theory) and not knows(actor, mg_form).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, mg_form). }
    Result "They are death-masks: each Master of Measures, cast the day he died, mouth shut and eyes closed, in a line along the wall like the beads of a very long sum. You look at one for an hour. It has nothing in it. It is exactly the shape of a man who has stopped. A face, you see, is what a person does with a shape; and a cast keeps the shape, and cannot keep the doing. Every cast ever taken is of a face at rest, and nobody has one.".
    Otherwise "You stand before the Masters until you can feel their expressions, and cannot say what it is that you feel. There is a student, behind you, who has been waiting to be asked to leave for some time.".
  }
  // Measure, at the Standard Pound: either what a pound is, or what a short one teaches.
  Action mg_measure_true(actor: group, site: place) "Stand before the Standard Pound and ask what makes a pound a pound" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, standard_room) and not at(assessor, standard_room) and knows(actor, mg_theory) and not knows(actor, mg_measure).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, mg_measure). }
    Result "You stand before it in its case a good while, as the Hall's visitors do: a drum of bronze the colour of strong tea. Nothing about it is exact. It has a thumbprint in its patina and a chip on its ring; its weight is, you will find, what the Hall's own Second says it is, and the Second is what the Standard says. They hold each other up. A pound is not the metal. It is the promise that the Hall will keep to it and the Drip will keep to the Hall, and a thing that is held to by both sides fits, whatever its shape.".
    Otherwise "You look at it for an hour and it is a pound. You were hoping for something less like a pound.".
  }
  Action mg_measure_short(actor: group, site: place) "Set the market's short pound against the Standard, and study the ounce" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, standard_room) and not at(assessor, standard_room) and knows(actor, mg_theory) and holding(actor, ct_pound_kind) and not knows(actor, mg_measure).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, mg_measure). Assert knows(actor, mg_measure_custom). }
    Result "The short pound rises in the pan, an ounce, no more, and what you cannot stop looking at is that it rises by an ounce *every time*. The Drip's bakers, the Row's brokers, the loaf in a woman's hand: everyone in the Sleeve has fitted to it, and been fitted, as a coat is to a stoop. It is not that it is false. It is that it is false by a fixed amount, and so reliable; and a measure that is wrong the same way every time is a measure two people can agree on. A fit is an agreement; and a custom is an error that has been agreed to be kept.".
  }
  // Cost, from the drowned mask and the boy who cut it, or from the Warden of Locks at his night-table.
  Action mg_cost_dov(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Dov to put the drowned mask in your hands, and tell you what it cost him to cut" {
    Speaker dov.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(dov, site) and knows(actor, mg_theory) and not knows(actor, mg_cost) and (holdsFace(actor, mk_face_drowned) or mk_dov_trusts(actor)).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, mg_cost). }
    Result "He puts it in your hands as he might put down a thing that had been in the family, and tells you without any of the usual pretences. It was cut from a man pulled out of the lagoon in the Sluice year; nobody claimed him. 'It fits whoever has nobody,' says Dov Ashe. 'That is all it is: I cut it from a face and it gives the face back to the next one who needs it. That is what a mask is meant to do. Only he was somebody's. Every time it sits on somebody, that is him not being claimed.' He wipes his hands on his apron. 'A fit is something somebody paid for. I do not think it is ever free.'".
    Otherwise "He holds it out and does not let go. 'It's only a mask,' says Dov, and you cannot tell if he is lying to you or to himself, and you leave with the sense of a door that was meant to be opened and was not, by either of you.".
  }
  Action mg_cost_lacke(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Warden what the Key has cost him, as one who has had it" {
    Speaker lacke.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(lacke, site) and ctNight(actor) and ct_lacke_warm(lacke) and knows(actor, mg_theory) and not knows(actor, mg_cost).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, mg_cost). }
    Result "'It costs you the one who was under it,' says Corvin Lacke. He has not been asked; he has been waiting eleven months to be asked. 'A year ago I was a man with an opinion about clocks. The Key does not hold opinions. In the beginning one wears it, and in the middle it wears one, and I do not recall a morning at which the one became the other.' He looks at the shelf where it rests. 'A mask that fits has been paid for, sir, by whoever it fitted before.'".
    Otherwise "'The Key has cost me,' says Lacke, and examines the sentence, and does not finish it. 'I think we shall not go into that.' He winds a clock to hide in.".
  }
  Rule mg_sources when knows(party, mg_form) and knows(party, mg_measure) and knows(party, mg_cost) and not mg_sources_known(party) says "You lay them side by side as you would three witnesses to a crime they each saw from the other side of a wall. A face is a shape that is held, and what holds it is the person; a fit is a promise two sides keep to a measure; and a fit has been paid for, by whoever the face was cut from. They are not one thing. They are three, and each, followed far enough, is the whole of it. In the Collegium's workroom there is a table, and a pen, and a choice about which of the three to follow." { Assert mg_sources_known(party). }
  Relation mg_sources_known(group).

  // ── Stage three: the lead ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The research can follow only one understanding; the other two become footnotes. The kind chosen is the spell's kind:
  // Form, the Likeness that sees; Measure, the Likeness that fits; Cost, the Likeness that gives.
  Relation mg_led(group). Relation mg_led_form(group). Relation mg_led_measure(group). Relation mg_led_cost(group).
  Discovery mg_lead_form "The research follows Form: a likeness is a face's holding, taken and shown; the Urn can be made to show what it holds.".
  Discovery mg_lead_measure "The research follows Measure: a likeness is a promise kept to a measure; a mask can be made to fit, and an Office to fail to.".
  Discovery mg_lead_cost "The research follows Cost: a likeness is a face given; its price can be paid by one, or shared among many.".
  Action mg_lead_form(actor: group, site: place) "Follow Form: a likeness is a holding, taken and shown" {
    Grave "A research has one lead. The other two understandings become footnotes, and the footnotes will not be cast.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, collegium_study) and mg_sources_known(actor) and not mg_led(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert mg_led(actor). Assert mg_led_form(actor). Assert knows(actor, mg_lead_form). }
    Result "You write it up by the study lamp: a likeness is not a shape but a holding, and the spell, if there is a spell, is an act of seeing what holds a face. A fine, cold, exact clarity comes over the page. It is the kind of understanding that has no use for anything it can see, and is at its best on lies.".
  }
  Action mg_lead_measure(actor: group, site: place) "Follow Measure: a likeness is a promise kept to a measure" {
    Grave "A research has one lead. The other two understandings become footnotes, and the footnotes will not be cast.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, collegium_study) and mg_sources_known(actor) and not mg_led(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert mg_led(actor). Assert mg_led_measure(actor). Assert knows(actor, mg_lead_measure). }
    Result "You write it up by the study lamp: a likeness is a promise, and the spell, if there is a spell, is the keeping of one: a face made to fit by being held to a measure by both sides, or made not to, by one side letting go. The page has a quiet, fair, civic quality. It is the kind of understanding that rules the Row and cannot, for the life of it, be moved to feel anything.".
  }
  Action mg_lead_cost(actor: group, site: place) "Follow Cost: a likeness is a face given" {
    Grave "A research has one lead. The other two understandings become footnotes, and the footnotes will not be cast.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, collegium_study) and mg_sources_known(actor) and not mg_led(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert mg_led(actor). Assert mg_led_cost(actor). Assert knows(actor, mg_lead_cost). }
    Result "You write it up by the study lamp, and stop twice. A likeness is not a thing taken but a thing given up; and the spell, if there is a spell, is the paying of a price: your own face, or somebody's, or shared out among a great many so that none of it is heavy. You are aware of having written a sentence that you would not like to have to say aloud to the man under the mask.".
  }

  // Dr Thole must be made to change his mind. He holds that the frame is warped; the truth is that it measures the shape
  // and leaves out the hand that holds it. Three ways to bring him to it, none of them evidence: he has had evidence
  // for forty years.
  Discovery mg_held_by_whom "Dr Thole has changed his mind: the frame is not warped; it measures the shape of a face and leaves out whoever is holding it; a face is a shape held, and the Master of Measures had not once in forty years asked by whom.".
  Action mg_thole_bare(actor: group, site: place) "Ask him to explain what a face is to someone who has none" {
    Speaker thole.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(thole, site) and mg_led(actor) and mg_audience(actor) and not masked(actor) and not mg_thole_agrees(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert mg_thole_agrees(actor). Assert knows(actor, mg_held_by_whom). }
    Result "You do not ask him to look at the research. You ask him, plainly, as one who has never worn a face, to explain it. He starts the recitation he has given a thousand times, at the speed of a man who knows it by heart: a face is a shape that is held. He gets to the word held. For the first time in forty years the sentence has to be finished for someone who does not already know what it means. 'Held,' says Thole, and stops. 'By what?' You wait. 'By its owner,' he says, slowly. 'By the one who has it. The Frame measured the shape, all of it, to a sixty-fourth, and left out the hand.' He puts down the trumpet. 'It is not warped.' He writes on the slate, enormous, HELD BY WHOM? and underlines it twice, and looks like a man who has been forgiven by a creditor he did not know he had.".
  }
  Action mg_thole_lend(actor: group, site: place) "Ask him to hold your mask on his own face, for the length of one sentence" {
    Speaker thole.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(thole, site) and mg_led(actor) and mg_audience(actor) and masked(actor) and not mg_thole_agrees(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert mg_thole_agrees(actor). Assert knows(actor, mg_held_by_whom). }
    Result "You wait for the moment when he has the pen down and nothing to correct, and ask him, in the plainest units, to put your mask on. 'In the Collegium,' he says, and then does not finish the sentence. He puts it on. It is the wrong size; it should slip. It does not. He sits quite still in the chair on wheels with a stranger's face on his face. 'It holds,' he says in a very small voice. 'It is held. I am holding it.' A long while. He takes it off, and the gown has gone damp at the collar. 'Forty years,' says Thole. 'The frame cuts the shape and I have never once thought to hold it.' He writes HELD BY WHOM? on the slate and looks at it as one looks at a name.".
    Otherwise "You ask a half-second late, over the top of a sentence of his, and the moment goes by like a ferry you were slow for. 'Not in the Collegium,' says Thole, from far away, and hands the mask back by one edge, as one hands back an unfinished remark.".
  }
  Action mg_thole_argue(actor: group, site: place) "Tell him, to his face, that the frame is not warped" {
    Speaker thole.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(thole, site) and mg_led(actor) and mg_audience(actor) and not mg_thole_agrees(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert mg_thole_agrees(actor). Assert knows(actor, mg_held_by_whom). }
    Result "You write it on the slate in the largest hand you have: THE FRAME IS NOT WARPED. IT MEASURES THE SHAPE AND LEAVES OUT THE HAND. He reads it three times, the third time aloud, with a face like a man being told, in a public place, that his house has been on fire for some time. Then he argues, for a quarter of an hour, with himself, in three voices, and loses all three. 'Held,' he says. 'By whom. By whom.' And begins, with the tip of his pen, to put a question mark after a sentence he published in 1269.".
    Otherwise "He reads it, and a great calm comes over his face, the calm of a man who has met the argument before and defeated it in committee. 'Warped,' says Thole, and begins to explain the Bursar's brass. You nod for an hour. At the end of it he is quite sure that you agree with him.".
  }
  Rule mg_thole_lessons_form when mg_thole_agrees(party) and mg_led_form(party) and not teaches(thole, magic_missile) once says "At the study table the Master of Measures draws a line under the page and signs it. 'I shall teach it,' he says to the slate. 'Both parts. It is the first thing I have taught in thirty years that I did not already know.'" { Assert teaches(thole, magic_missile). Assert teaches(thole, acid_arrow). Assert teaches(thole, augury). Assert arcBegun(party, hand_likeness). }
  Rule mg_thole_lessons_measure when mg_thole_agrees(party) and mg_led_measure(party) and not teaches(thole, armor) once says "At the study table the Master of Measures draws a line under the page and signs it. 'I shall teach it,' he says to the slate. 'Both parts. It is the first thing I have taught in thirty years that I did not already know.'" { Assert teaches(thole, armor). Assert teaches(thole, blur). Assert teaches(thole, mirror_image). Assert arcBegun(party, hand_likeness). }
  Rule mg_thole_lessons_cost when mg_thole_agrees(party) and mg_led_cost(party) and not teaches(thole, hex) once says "At the study table the Master of Measures draws a line under the page and signs it. 'I shall teach it,' he says to the slate. 'Both parts. It is the first thing I have taught in thirty years that I did not already know.'" { Assert teaches(thole, hex). Assert teaches(thole, charm). Assert teaches(thole, mind_blank). Assert arcBegun(party, hand_likeness). }
  // His fee is the Collegium's: three coin to the Bursar. That a lesson has been paid for is how the rest of the module
  // knows a mage, and not a bystander, has been taught.
  Initially Set lessonFee(thole) to 3.
  Initially Set quantity(thole, gold) to 0.
  Rule mg_lesson_given when quantity(thole, gold) >= 3 and not mg_taught(party) says "Thole watches the spell go in, as one watches a pupil take the first step on a stair: not with pride, with a sort of terrified accuracy. 'There,' he says. 'It holds.' He sounds, for a moment, surprised that it does." { Assert mg_taught(party). Assert handReady(party, hand_likeness). }
  // The margin of the treatise, for all who helped: the Master's corrections, in a second ink. It sharpens the reader.
  Topic mg_thole_copy with thole "Ask him for a copy of the treatise, with his corrections" when mg_thole_agrees(actor) and not mg_margin_given(actor) once {
    Says "He is already writing. For an hour the pen goes, in the second ink, in the margin, and it is not a margin any more but the whole of the page: the original, entire, with the correction of every line beside it. HELD BY WHOM?, on the first, and on the last, and between them forty years' worth of the Frame, and where it was right. He sands it, and gives it to you. 'It is not the work of a man who was wrong,' says Thole. 'It is the work of a man who was exact about the wrong thing.'".
    On discuss { Give mg_treatise to actor. Assert mg_margin_given(actor). }
  }
  Kind mg_treatise_kind "Thole's marginal treatise" is gear worth 0 weighing 1 granting lore described "A copy of Dr Thole's On the Held Shape in his own hand, with a margin as wide as the text and the margin in a second ink: the corrections of a man who has been wrong for forty years, in detail, and has enjoyed it.".
  Item mg_treatise "Thole's marginal treatise" is mg_treatise_kind at offstage.
  Action mg_study_margin(actor: group, reader: member, site: place) "Have {reader} read Thole's corrections through, and be corrected" {
    Requires able(actor) and memberOf(reader, actor) and awake(reader) and holding(actor, mg_treatise_kind) and not mg_studied(actor) and at(actor, site) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 12.
    Resolve endow(reader, intelligence, by_one).
    On success { Assert mg_studied(actor). }
    Result "{reader} reads it through, the original and its corrections in turn, twice, and the second time begins to see where the margin is wrong; and then where it is right in a way the margin did not know. By the end the page is a conversation, and {reader} has been in it.".
  }

  // ── Stage four: the casting at the Urn ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // On the ninth night, in the Urn Hall, the company casts the Likeness it followed. drawing.kyr reads handPlayed and
  // these three relations.
  Relation mg_urn_shown(group). Relation mg_fit_false(group). Relation mg_burden_shared(group). Relation mg_unremembered(group).
  Action mg_cast_form(actor: group, site: place) "Cast the Likeness of Form on the Urn" {
    Grave "A likeness cast at the Urn cannot be called back. The room will see what you have seen.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and handReady(actor, hand_likeness) and mg_led_form(actor) and not handPlayed(actor, hand_likeness).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_likeness). Assert mg_urn_shown(actor). Assert arcDone(actor, hand_likeness). }
    Result "You lay the spell on the Urn as you would lay a hand on a brow, and see what holds it. The bronze jar, which the city has believed in for thirty-one years, is not holding anything. There is no shape in it: no tessera, no lot, no luck, no chance; only the metal, and the weight of the metal, and above it, very faintly, the shape of a hand that has been in and out of its slot a great many times. You let the room see it. Nobody speaks. In the Urn Hall, at the ninth hour, a hundred masks turn toward a jar.".
  }
  Action mg_cast_measure(actor: group, site: place) "Cast the Likeness of Measure on the Offices" {
    Grave "A likeness cast at the Urn cannot be called back. The Offices will not sit as they did.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and handReady(actor, hand_likeness) and mg_led_measure(actor) and not handPlayed(actor, hand_likeness).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_likeness). Assert mg_fit_false(actor). Assert arcDone(actor, hand_likeness). }
    Result "You do not cast it at the Urn. You cast it at the nineteen Offices' masks laid out in their case: a fine, civic, even spell, a promise withdrawn. The Key, the Pound, the Serene: each, in turn, sits on its cushion and ceases, for a moment, to be held to its measure by the face it was cut for. Whoever claims an Office tonight will find that the mask does not fit them as it should, and that the city can see it. Nobody will say why. The mask will merely fall off.".
  }
  Action mg_cast_cost(actor: group, site: place) "Cast the Likeness of Cost, and share the lie out" {
    Grave "The price is paid in faces: yours, and then everyone's who stands in the Hall. You will not be remembered by what you wore.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and handReady(actor, hand_likeness) and mg_led_cost(actor) and not handPlayed(actor, hand_likeness).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_likeness). Assert mg_burden_shared(actor). Assert mg_unremembered(actor). Assert arcDone(actor, hand_likeness). Retract masked(actor). }
    Result "You give it away. Not the lie, which is not yours, but the weight of it, spread among everyone in the Hall at the same moment, an ounce each, like a short pound: a little of the thirty-one years laid on every mask in the room, so that nobody has to carry the whole. And your own face, which you spend as the first payment, goes out of the memory of every person you have spoken to in Ombra, by degrees, like a coin spent where nobody counts. For a moment you are a person nobody has ever met. It is, you find, extremely restful.".
  }

  // ── Milestones and fates ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Milestone mg_m_theory "had the Master of Measures explain his failing theory" worth 25 when knows(party, mg_theory).
  Milestone mg_m_sources "found three understandings of a fit" worth 50 when mg_sources_known(party).
  Milestone mg_m_agrees "made Dr Thole ask by whom" worth 50 when mg_thole_agrees(party).
  Milestone mg_m_taught "was taught the Likeness" worth 50 when mg_taught(party).
  Milestone mg_m_cast "cast the Likeness at the Urn" worth 100 when handPlayed(party, hand_likeness).

  Rule mg_fate_form when newsHour() and mg_urn_shown(party) once says "Of Dr Thole: he was in the Urn Hall, in his chair on wheels, and did not hear it, and was told afterwards by a student on the slate, in units; and the whole of the Collegium watched the Master of Measures read it and take, very carefully, his mask off the peg by the door, and put it on, and go down the steps in the rain with it." { }
  Rule mg_fate_measure when newsHour() and mg_fit_false(party) once says "Of Dr Thole: the Offices, drawn on the ninth night, would not sit; the masks fell off the faces they had been cut for, one after another, in front of the Hall, and nobody could say why, and the Master of Measures, on the slate, in the Collegium, wrote 'by agreement' and underlined it twice." { }
  Rule mg_fate_cost when newsHour() and mg_burden_shared(party) and mg_unremembered(party) once says "Of Dr Thole: the Collegium found, on the tenth morning, that it had mislaid the name of the Bare who had been its guest at night; Thole, who had it in a margin, did not tell them. 'A fit is paid for,' he is reported to have said, to the frame. 'By whoever it fitted before.'" { }
  Rule mg_fate_agrees when newsHour() and mg_thole_agrees(party) and not handPlayed(party, hand_likeness) once says "Of Dr Thole: he has revised On the Held Shape; the new edition has three words on its title-page and a hundred and four masks in an appendix; the Frame has been fitted with a hook for a hand, and is not warped. He is said to be happier, and to hear less." { }
  Rule mg_fate_failed when newsHour() and mg_audience(party) and not mg_thole_agrees(party) once says "Of Dr Thole: the Bursar has sent the brass, and the Frame has been corrected, and a hundred and five masks hang on the wall of the workroom, perfect, each by its ear-holes; and the Master of Measures is waiting, with the patience of eighty years, for someone to put a unit on the question." { }
  Rule mg_fate_unmet when newsHour() and not mg_audience(party) once says "Of Dr Thole: he went on measuring, in the cold, until the ninth night, as he had every night for forty years, and did not hear the bells." { }
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/maskers.ky:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── Maskers' Lane ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Guild of Maskers: workshops with their shutters hooked back to the rain, the Wet Stage (bard.kyr's), the
  // Cockle and Heron mask-shop that cuts the Annex's faces by the gross, and Madame Pavane's house, which has under it
  // the Wall of Faces: a life-cast of every citizen taken at sixteen, because a mask must fit. Three threads live here:
  // the Wall itself and the woman who keeps it (this file); an apprentice's made face that fits nobody (this file); and
  // the Cast-Room, the thief's own heist on the Wall (thief.kyr, which uses what is declared here).
  //
  // Facts this file may teach: lie_wall (the Menders' shelf, seen from the cellar) and marrick_was_treasurer (the
  // Registrar's veiled cast). Declared here for others to read: mk_dov_trusts(party), mk_face_drowned, castTaken (the
  // spine's), fitted (the spine's), mk_maule_has(party), mk_crude_fit(party, face), mk_cast_pavane(party).

  // ── The lane, the rooms ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe mk_lane_day at maskers_lane when publicHours() "Maskers' Lane is a lane of faces being made. Every second door is a workshop with its shutters hooked back to the rain, and in each a figure in a trade's half-mask bends over a block, so that the whole street seems to be nodding. Lacquer, hot glue and wet plaster cross the air in layers, and the gutters run white. Over the Fitter's door a brass oval, polished by thumbs, says PAVANE, and under it, smaller: BY APPOINTMENT OF THE FACE.".
  Observe mk_lane_night at maskers_lane when privateHours() "At night the lane is a row of shut faces. The workshops have their shutters up and their stoves banked, and the rain goes down the gutters white with plaster to the Cuff. A lamp burns on the sill of the Fitter's fitting-room, as it does every night, so that a late customer may know where to knock.".
  Observe mk_lane_roof at maskers_lane when privateHours() and at(dov, maskers_roof) "Somewhere above the Fitter's eaves, on the slates, something is sitting very still in the rain. It is larger than a cat. It has a little light, the size of a thumbnail, that it shades with its hand.".
  Observe mk_lane_hawker at maskers_lane when at(th_slee, maskers_lane) "At the mouth of the lane a barrow stands under an oilcloth, and on it, among a heap of second-hand faces with their ribbons knotted, a brass scale with two pans.".

  Observe mk_fitting_day at fitting_room when publicHours() "Madame Pavane's fitting-room is the one tidy room in the Lane. A single chair stands on a dais under a skylight of ground glass, with an iron headrest and a bowl of drinking-straws; round the walls, on pegs, hang a hundred plaster brows with no faces under them, the Fitter's working blocks, and the light from the skylight is the grey of an oyster. Nothing here is for sale. A bell by the parlour door has a card: WAIT.".
  Observe mk_fitting_night at fitting_room when privateHours() "By night the fitting-room has put a sheet over its hundred brows, and they stand in rows like the foreheads of the drowned. The chair keeps its dais and its straws. The lamp on the sill burns for any late face that needs finding, and the parlour door stands an inch open, with light in the crack.".
  Observe mk_parlour_day at pavane_parlour when publicHours() "Behind the fitting-room is the working half of the house: a stove, a long table dusted white, racks of knives and spoons and little saws, and on every shelf the stock of a trade that makes one thing four thousand ways. By the window an unfinished mask stands on an iron stand with a cloth over its face. A narrow door in the corner says CELLAR, and the lock on it says it twice.".
  Observe mk_parlour_night at pavane_parlour when privateHours() "The parlour at night is the warmest room in the lane. The stove is up, a kettle ticks on it, and the long table has been cleared of plaster and laid with a cloth and two cups, as though somebody had been told to expect somebody. The unfinished mask on its stand has had its cloth taken off: it has a brow and a mouth and nothing between them, and by lamplight it looks like a face thinking of something else.".
  Observe mk_parlour_blank at pavane_parlour when publicHours() and not knows(party, mk_blank_known) "On the iron stand by the window the half-made mask is a different grey from the rest, older and more handled. It is not for the Offices and it is not for the trades; there is no peg or ticket on it.".

  Observe mk_cellar_scene at cast_cellar when true "The Wall of Faces. The cellar is long, low, vaulted and dry, lit by a single hooded lamp on a hook at the stair foot that, by the smell of its oil, has not gone out in forty years. Every wall is shelving, and on every shelf, close as cobbles, stand faces: plaster faces, life-size, eyes shut, from the brow to the chin, each with a little chalk plate beneath it. There are forty thousand, give or take. They are not frightening, which you notice with relief and then do not trust. Each has the slight set of a face holding still for someone, and none of them is holding still for you.".
  Observe mk_cellar_trades at cast_cellar when true "The shelves are labelled by trade in a hand that has copied the same words for forty years: MAKERS. KEEPERS. CARRIERS. FERRYMEN. BAKERS. LAMPS. MENDERS.".
  Observe mk_cellar_menders at cast_cellar when true "The shelf of MENDERS is one of the smaller ones, and the best kept. Under each of its faces the plate gives a street and a trade in the Fitter's code and, under a good many, a second line in a different chalk: a letter and a year. You read down the second lines. K, P, T, S, W: the same nineteen letters, year after year after year, thirty years of them, each a face from this shelf and from no other." teaches lie_wall.
  Observe mk_cellar_drowned at cast_cellar when true "The shelf marked DROWNED is lower than the rest and set closer, and the faces on it have a dampness about the mouth that plaster should not keep. There are six hundred of them, taken from the dead for the box, because the Concord buries nobody faceless. Each has a name chalked under it and a line through the name where it was claimed. The last has no name: the plate says only a question mark, and a tally of nine, and nine, and nine, one for each nine days that nobody came.".
  Observe mk_cellar_niche at cast_cellar when true "In the middle of the long wall, at the height of a face, there is a niche with a lampblacked bracket and nothing in it. The plate under it has been rubbed out and rewritten so often that the slate has gone thin; it says THE FITTER. It is the one empty place on forty thousand shelves." teaches mk_empty_niche.
  Observe mk_cellar_veil at cast_cellar when not knows(party, marrick_was_treasurer) "On the shelf of LAMPS, near the end, one face has a cloth over it, a square of black wool pinned at the brow, the way a house covers its mirrors. Whatever the plate under it says, the cloth hides.".
  Observe mk_cellar_veil_up at cast_cellar when knows(party, marrick_was_treasurer) "On the shelf of LAMPS the black cloth is folded back from the last face: a girl's, young and plain, with a lamp-trimmer's jaw. The plate says Y. MARRICK, and under it, in the other chalk, T for the year of the Sluice, and then R. It is the only face on either shelf that has an Office chalked against it from before the Menders began. She does not look as if she knew what was going to be done to her.".

  Observe mk_shop_day at mask_shop_floor when publicHours() "The Cockle and Heron sells faces by the gross. Domino on domino hangs from the beams on loops of tape, bakers' Cockles and clerks' Herons, each pair of eyeholes at a slightly different height, so that the whole shop appears to be looking at a point just past you. A bell on the counter has a card: RING ONCE. THE MASTER IS AT THE LAST ONE.".
  Observe mk_shop_night at mask_shop_floor when privateHours() "The mask-shop is shut up and smells of size. The faces hang in the dark in their hundreds with the rain behind them, and a ladder-stair goes up through a hatch in the ceiling to the drying-loft, where, if you look, there is a lamp.".
  Observe mk_loft_day at mk_loft when publicHours() "The drying-loft: a long low room under the tiles, where damp masks hang from lines like washing, by the thousand, drying their glue. It smells of size and wet card and the inside of other people's faces. Nobody is here but the faces, and the rain ticking on the tiles over their heads.".
  Observe mk_loft_night at mk_loft when privateHours() "The drying-loft by night: a long low room under the tiles with a single lamp turned down on a crate, and the masks hanging from the lines in their thousands, turning very slightly in the draught. Those nearest the lamp have dried to the colour of tea; the far ones are still the white of a boiled egg.".

  Observe mk_roof_day at maskers_roof when publicHours() "The Maskers' roofs are a country of wet slate and tile, cut by gutters and chimney-stacks. Over the Fitter's fitting-room a skylight of ground glass; over the parlour, set into the pitch, a smaller one on a hinge, with a bolt on the inside. The rain falls here with nothing to apologise for.".
  Observe mk_roof_free at maskers_roof when privateHours() and mk_dov_free(party) and at(dov, maskers_roof) "Dov is on the ridge, with his hood back, in the rain, doing nothing in particular. His hands are open on his knees.".
  Observe mk_roof_night at maskers_roof when privateHours() "At night the roofs are very dark and very loud: every slate has a voice, and the gutters run like a crowd of people all being told the same thing. Below you the lane is a strip of weak tea, the Fitter's lamp on its sill; beyond, across the Cuff, the lamps of the Drip stand in the rain like a drowned town.".

  // The drying-loft above the mask-shop is Slee's counting-house by night (thief.kyr); the stair is ours.
  Place mk_attic "the attic of the mask-shop" is level within mask_shop.
  Place mk_loft "the drying-loft over the mask-shop" is room within mk_attic at 2, 0 indoors.
  Passage mk_loft_stair "the drying-loft stair" is stair between mask_shop_floor and mk_loft.

  // ── Madame Pavane ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Sixty-one, vain of her craft, cold, and wanting only to be seen as an artist. She came down the delta road
  // Bare thirty-nine years ago, was offered a face, took it, and has cut every Office's mask since; her own face is
  // the one place on her Wall that has never been filled. She has always known the Offices go to Menders, because she
  // sees whom she fits; she thinks it is the best thing the city does, and has kept it for thirty-one years.
  Person pavane "Madame Pavane" at fitting_room {
    Role "the Fitter of the Maskers' Guild". Ancestry human. Pronouns she. Manner proud.
    Known as "a woman of sixty in a Fitter's grey half-mask and a plaster-dusted apron" when publicHours() and not knows(party, mk_pavane_name).
    Known as "a grey-haired woman in a quilted gown with plaster under her nails" when privateHours() and not knows(party, mk_pavane_name).
    Greets "A tall woman with plaster to the elbow and a long, mobile, unsculpted hand does not turn from her work, but she has measured the width of your face, brow to chin, before you are through the door; you feel it as you feel a draught. 'Do not apologise,' she says to the plaster. 'You are wondering whether your face is as ordinary as it feels. It is. They all are. It is the great comfort of my trade.'".
    Greets again "'Face,' says Madame Pavane, as another woman says good morning, and goes on with her knife.".
  }
  Initially Assert unmaskTeaches(pavane, mk_pavane_name).
  Discovery mk_pavane_name "Under the Fitter's grey half-mask is a woman called Sabine Orrell, from the far side of the delta road; Pavane is the name of the house, and Orrell is the name she has not said aloud in Ombra for thirty-nine years.".
  Discovery mk_wall_known "Under Madame Pavane's house, in a cellar, is the Wall of Faces: a plaster cast of every citizen's face taken at sixteen, because a mask must fit, shelved by trade.".
  Discovery mk_blank_known "On a stand in the Fitter's parlour is a half-made mask that is for nobody: she begins one every winter, she says, and has never finished one.".
  Discovery mk_empty_niche "On the Wall of Faces there is one empty niche, in the middle of the long wall, with a plate that says THE FITTER: the Fitter has never been cast.".
  Discovery mk_pavane_was_bare "Madame Pavane came down the delta road Bare, was offered a face by the Concord and took it, and was never cast, since the Wall takes faces at sixteen and she came at twenty-two.".
  Discovery mk_pavane_knows_lie "Madame Pavane has known for thirty-one years that every Office goes to a face from the Menders' shelf; she cut each mask and saw whose face it was, and thought it the best thing the city did.".

  Relation mk_guiding(group). Relation mk_pavane_trust(group). Relation mk_commissioned(group). Relation mk_waited(group).
  Relation mk_warranted(group). Relation mk_pavane_seen(group). Relation mk_pavane_moved(group). Relation mk_wall_refused(group).
  Relation mk_veil_refused(group). Relation mk_cast_pavane(group). Relation mk_pavane_cold(group). Relation mk_free_fit(group).
  Relation mk_pavane_told(group). Relation mk_sitting_known(group).

  // Her day, by the hour: the chair by day, the parlour by night, abed from one. A guided visit holds her wherever she is
  // leading; a Naming shuts her in the parlour with the door locked.
  Rule mk_pavane_chair when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 20 and not named(pavane) and not mk_guiding(pavane) and not at(pavane, fitting_room) { Assert at(pavane, fitting_room). }
  Rule mk_pavane_evening when (hour(clock) >= 20 or hour(clock) < 1 or (hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 8)) and not mk_guiding(pavane) and not at(pavane, pavane_parlour) { Assert at(pavane, pavane_parlour). }
  Rule mk_pavane_abed when hour(clock) >= 1 and hour(clock) < 7 and not mk_guiding(pavane) and not at(pavane, offstage) { Assert at(pavane, offstage). }
  Rule mk_pavane_shut when named(pavane) and hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 20 and not mk_guiding(pavane) and not at(pavane, pavane_parlour) { Assert at(pavane, pavane_parlour). }
  Rule mk_guide_ends when mk_guiding(pavane) and not at(party, cast_cellar) { Retract mk_guiding(pavane). }

  // The cellar door. Locked unless the Fitter has led the company down; she locks it again behind them.
  Thing mk_cellar_lock "the cellar door" on cellar_stair {
    State locked blocking "The cellar door in the corner of the parlour is shut, and the lock on it is a good one, with a plate of brass so clean that it shows your thumb.".
    State open "The cellar door stands open on a stair going down into lamplight.".
  }
  Rule mk_relock when state(mk_cellar_lock, open) and not at(party, cast_cellar) and not mk_picked_open(party) { Retract state(mk_cellar_lock, open). Assert state(mk_cellar_lock, locked). }
  Relation mk_picked_open(group).

  // ── The Fitter by day: the chair, the study, the Fit ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // By day she answers a face. A bare one gets one cold sentence and a hint of the one place in Ombra the Concord does
  // not reach: the chair, where a face is cast bare, because plaster does not take a mask.
  Topic mk_p_cold with pavane "Say good day to the Fitter" when not masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "'We are not at home to the Bare,' says the Fitter to her plaster, in the voice she keeps for people who do not matter. Then, as if it were a rule of the trade that came out by itself: 'If it is a face you want, the chair is there. It is the one thing in Ombra that does not mind what is in it.' She does not look round.".
  }
  Topic mk_p_named_topic with pavane "Speak to the Fitter, whose name has been cried" when named(pavane) {
    Says "She does not turn from the shuttered window. 'You have ruined a woman,' says Sabine Orrell, in the voice of someone reading an inscription. 'It was not my name in your mouth. It was the name of a girl who stood nine days at a gate with her hands in her sleeves. I have not the strength to be angry; I shall have to be it in the morning.' She waits, perfectly still, until you have gone.".
  }
  Topic mk_p_trade with pavane "Ask the Fitter what a Fit is" when masked(actor) and publicHours() once {
    Says "'A mask is a promise made of paste,' says Madame Pavane. 'The Gull's is a promise to the ferry. I cut it by the dozen and it goes on any face, and the face keeps the promise. An Office's is a promise to the city, and it is cut to one face. It sits on that face like a hand. On any other face it sits like a hand on the wrong arm, and any Fitter can tell you the tell.' She does not tell you the tell. 'It is the one thing in Ombra that cannot be forged, and I am tired of being its only witness.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mk_fit_told). }
  }
  Discovery mk_fit_told "Madame Pavane says an Office's mask is cut to one face only and sits on no other like a hand on the wrong arm: every Fit has a tell that a Fitter can see.".
  Topic mk_p_appraise with pavane "Ask the Fitter what she makes of the face you are wearing" when masked(actor) and publicHours() and not wears(actor, face_moth) once {
    Says "She takes your chin in two plaster fingers and turns your head to the grey light, quite without ceremony, and looks at the mask and not at you. 'An Annex face. Maule's, by the gross. It fits you well enough to be wrong.' She lets go. 'Come to me by night with your own face on, and I will show you the difference. It is not a thing one does by day. By day I am a pair of hands.'".
  }
  Topic mk_p_moth with pavane "Show the Fitter that you wear the Moth" when wears(actor, face_moth) and publicHours() once {
    Says "'The Moth.' She says it as she might say the name of a disease. 'Players. You want your faces by the dozen and your Fits by Friday, and you wear them out in a night and call it art.' Then, because she cannot help it: 'The lacquer on the Wet Stage's Lamp is mine. Whoever cut its eyes cut them an eighth too wide. Tell him I know.'".
  }
  Topic mk_p_burglar with pavane "Say you have come to talk" when masked(actor) and privateHours() {
    Says "'Faces off,' says Madame Pavane, without looking up, in the voice of a woman who has found that the shortest way with a burglar is to treat him as a guest. 'This house is received bare after the Ninth Bell. I make no exception for the Gull.' She has not moved her hand from the drawer where the knives are.".
  }

  // The chair: six coin, forty minutes, bare. Her price for a look at her Wall is a face of one's own on it.
  Action mk_p_sit(actor: group, site: place) "Sit in the Fitter's chair to be cast, six coin" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, site) and publicHours() and not masked(actor) and not castTaken(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 6.
    Time 40 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Increase quantity(pavane, gold) by 6. Assert castTaken(actor). Assert knows(actor, mk_wall_known). }
    Result "Straws in the nostrils, oiled cloth at the hairline, and then the plaster, which is warm, and heavier than a face has any right to be. You breathe through the straws and count, and the Fitter works in total silence with her hands on your cheekbones, and once, near the end, you feel her stop and simply look. It sets. It comes away with a small wet sound, and she holds it up to the grey light and says, to no one, 'There you are.' It will go on the Wall, she says; and the sitter may look at the shelf that is theirs.".
  }
  Action mk_p_commission(actor: group, site: place) "Commission a Fitter's study of your face, ten coin" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, site) and publicHours() and masked(actor) and not mk_commissioned(actor) and not castTaken(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 10.
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Increase quantity(pavane, gold) by 10. Assert mk_commissioned(actor). Assert knows(actor, mk_wall_known). }
    Result "'A study,' says Madame Pavane, and the word changes her, as a word will change a priest: she straightens, and the half-mask seems for an instant the least of her. 'A study begins from the Wall. The customer is taken down to see the faces his own has come from, and chooses.' She names a figure. It is not a figure for a mask; it is a figure for a look. Whatever the study is, she is not going to make it, and both of you know it, and the coin is a fair price for being let down.".
  }
  Action mk_p_guide(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Madame Pavane to take you down to the Wall" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, site) and not named(pavane) and (mk_commissioned(actor) or castTaken(actor) or mk_pavane_trust(actor) or mk_warranted(actor)) and not mk_guiding(pavane).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert at(actor, cast_cellar). Assert at(pavane, cast_cellar). Assert mk_guiding(pavane). Retract state(mk_cellar_lock, locked). Assert state(mk_cellar_lock, open). Assert knows(actor, mk_wall_known). }
    Result "She takes the key from the chain at her neck and goes before you down the stair, and at the foot of it she takes off her mask and hangs it on a hook, among a great many hooks, with the air of a woman leaving a hat at a church. 'Nobody wears one down here,' she says. 'They find it rude.'".
  }

  // ── The Fitter by night ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A bare knock is received. What she says by night she would not say by day, and she says it to the only kind of person
  // who cannot be made to answer for it: a Bare is not bound by the Concord, and so may Name, and she knows it.
  Topic mk_p_night with pavane "Sit at the Fitter's stove, bare, and say you came to talk" when not masked(actor) and privateHours() once {
    Says "She looks at your bare face for a long moment, as a farmer looks at a field he has been told is his. 'Sit. Not the chair; the chair is for work.' She pours something from the kettle that is not tea. 'It is the rule of the house that at night we are two people and not two faces. I am Pavane. It is the house's. The woman who lives in it is not to be asked.' Her hand, round the cup, is not quite steady, and she is pleased with you for not noticing.".
  }
  Topic mk_p_wall_ask with pavane "Ask Madame Pavane about the Wall under her house" when not masked(actor) and privateHours() and knows(actor, mk_wall_known) and not mk_wall_refused(actor) and not mk_pavane_trust(actor) and not mk_commissioned(actor) and not castTaken(actor) once {
    Says "'The Wall is the Guild's, and the Guild's is the city's, and the city has never once asked to see it. That is why it has stayed so tidy.' She turns her cup a quarter turn on the cloth. 'It is shown to the sitter, and the sitter is shown the shelf that is his, and nobody else. Ask me again in the morning. I shall have forgotten the question; I am sixty-one.'".
    On discuss { Assert mk_wall_refused(actor). }
  }
  Topic mk_p_blank with pavane "Ask about the unfinished mask on the stand" when not masked(actor) and privateHours() and not knows(actor, mk_blank_known) once {
    Says "'Nobody's.' She looks at it, not at you. 'The one thing in this house that is not cut to measure. I begin one every winter. They are in the cellar, under the stair; there are thirty-nine. I have never finished one: a face wants somebody to be wrong for, and I have never been able to think of whom.' She says it as a joke, and does not smile at it, and goes on looking at the mask as if it had said something.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mk_blank_known). }
  }
  Measure mk_blank_tries(group). Measure mk_cut_try(group).
  Action mk_p_see_blank(actor: group, site: place) "Tell her what you see in the mask that is for nobody" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, site) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and knows(actor, mk_blank_known) and not mk_pavane_seen(actor) and mk_blank_tries(actor) < 2.
    Time 20 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert mk_pavane_seen(actor). }
    On failure { Increase mk_blank_tries(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You do not say that it is well made. You say that it is the only thing in the room that is looking at something, and that you think the empty place between the brow and the mouth is the whole point of it, and that nobody making a face for a person would have left it so. The kettle ticks. Madame Pavane sets down her cup very precisely, as though it were the thing most likely to fall. 'No one has said that,' she says. 'In thirty-nine years, no one has said anything. They say it is very fine.'".
    Otherwise "You say something about the line of the brow, which is true, and about the craftsmanship, which is true, and she thanks you for your interest in her work in exactly the voice she uses to the Watch. The kettle ticks. It has been a good evening and nothing has happened in it.".
  }
  Action mk_p_ask_cut(actor: group, site: place) "Ask her to finish the mask for nobody, and sit by while she does" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, site) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and mk_pavane_seen(actor) and not mk_pavane_moved(actor) and mk_cut_try(actor) < day(clock).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert mk_pavane_moved(actor). Assert mk_pavane_trust(actor). Set mk_cut_try(actor) to day(clock). }
    On failure { Set mk_cut_try(actor) to day(clock). }
    Result "You sit where she puts you, and you do not pose; you hold still and let your face be the thing it is when nobody has asked it to be anything, which is a good deal harder, and takes the whole of your attention. She works for two hours with the knife and the little saw and does not speak. Toward the end she stops, and holds the mask at arm's length, and for the first time in thirty-nine winters it is a face: not yours, not anyone's, the face of someone who has just stopped waiting. She puts it down on the table between you. 'Finished,' she says, in an odd voice, and then, 'Well.'".
    Otherwise "You sit, and you hold a face, and you can feel yourself doing it: the little managing muscles at the corners of the mouth, that want to be liked. She sees it, as she sees everything of that kind. She works ten minutes and puts the knife down, and says that it is late, and that she is a woman of sixty-one, and that she will think about it.".
  }
  Action mk_p_press(actor: group, site: place) "Tell her the Warrant covers what masks may not see, and the Wall is one" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, site) and warrantLive() and not mk_warranted(actor) and not mk_pavane_trust(actor) and not mk_guiding(pavane) and not named(pavane).
    Time 5 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert mk_warranted(actor). Assert mk_pavane_cold(actor). Increase heat(actor) by 1. Assert knows(actor, mk_wall_known). }
    On failure { Increase heat(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You say the seventy-first article, as Vail said it to you, and she listens to the end with her eyes on your forehead, like a woman weighing a block of clay she did not order. 'The law of the Concord says that the Wall is the Guild's,' she says. 'The law of the Stranger's Warrant says I am to show you what the Concord forbids. I have never in my life been so glad that it is somebody else's decision.' Not a word more will you get from her that is not about plaster, and a note will go to the Watch in the morning, and it will be polite.".
    Otherwise "She hears the article out, and corrects your citation of it, and says that in sixty-two years the Warrant has been shown to her once, and it was in better handwriting. She rings the bell by the parlour door. A boy is sent to the Watch-house with a note, and you are left to find your own way out of a very civil silence.".
  }
  Action mk_p_wait(actor: group, site: place) "Stand in the rain before Madame Pavane's door until she comes down" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, maskers_lane) and privateHours() and hour(clock) >= 20 and hour(clock) < 23 and not masked(actor) and not mk_waited(actor) and not mk_pavane_trust(actor) and not named(pavane).
    Time 60 minutes.
    On success { Assert mk_waited(actor). Assert mk_pavane_trust(actor). Assert knows(actor, mk_wall_known). }
    Result "You do not knock. You stand on the step with the rain running off your hair into your collar, in the lamp from the sill, and the hour goes by as an hour does when it is being watched: the Chapel strikes it, a long way off, across water. The door opens the width of a face. 'People who knock three times are the Watch, or in love,' says Madame Pavane. 'People who stand are neither. Come in, before you ruin my step.' In the parlour she gives you a towel without comment and the cup by the stove without being asked, and says, in a different voice, that the Wall may be shown to people who have been rained on.".
  }

  // ── What she tells the company she trusts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic mk_p_niche with pavane "Ask her why there is nothing on the Wall where THE FITTER should be" when not masked(actor) and (mk_pavane_moved(actor) or mk_drowned_pavane(actor)) and knows(actor, mk_empty_niche) and not knows(actor, mk_pavane_was_bare) once {
    Says "'Because I came down the delta road at twenty-two,' says Madame Pavane. 'The Wall takes a face at sixteen. I was sixteen in another country, where nobody had thought of it.' She turns the empty cup. 'I stood at the Gate of Strangers nine days with my hands in my sleeves. On the ninth the Concord offered me a face, and I took it, and was a Fitter's girl by the spring. I have cut every Office's mask since. I have never been cast. I never asked. Who would I have asked?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mk_pavane_was_bare). }
  }
  Topic mk_p_name with pavane "Ask Madame Pavane what she wants you to do with what she has said" when not masked(actor) and knows(actor, mk_pavane_was_bare) and not knows(actor, mk_pavane_name) once {
    Says "She looks at your bare face with an exactness that is almost tenderness. 'My name is Sabine Orrell. If you say it in a square you have ruined a woman; I am not asking you not to. I am telling you because you are the one person I know who is not bound to hold your tongue, and I should like, once, to be a person to someone who might.' She picks up the cup, and finds it empty, and holds it anyway. 'That is all. It is a great deal more than I meant to give.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mk_pavane_name). Assert mk_pavane_told(actor). }
  }
  Topic mk_p_told with pavane "Ask Madame Pavane how she is, now that she has said what she has said" when not masked(actor) and privateHours() and mk_pavane_told(actor) once {
    Says "'Lighter,' she says. She weighs it in the hand that is not holding the cup. 'And frightened. That is new.' She pours. 'I wore it so long I forgot there was weather. You will not forget you know. I want you to know I know it.'".
  }
  Topic mk_p_knew with pavane "Ask the Fitter whether she has ever noticed whose faces the Offices are cut to" when not masked(actor) and privateHours() and mk_pavane_moved(actor) and not knows(actor, mk_pavane_knows_lie) once {
    Says "'Noticed.' She laughs, shortly. 'I cut the Treasurer's mask each spring to a face from the Menders' shelf. And the Warden's, and the Assessor's, and the Serene's: thirty-one years of them. I am a Fitter, Bare; I know every face in this city better than its mother does. I have never once cut an Office to a gambler or a thief or a fool.' She looks at the stove. 'I thought it was the best thing the city did. I still think so. Do not tell me otherwise tonight. I have been polite for a very long time.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mk_pavane_knows_lie). }
  }
  Action mk_p_cast_her(actor: group, site: place) "Offer to take the Fitter's own cast, for the empty niche on her Wall" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, site) and not masked(actor) and knows(actor, mk_pavane_was_bare) and not mk_cast_pavane(actor) and not named(pavane).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, mending, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert mk_cast_pavane(actor). Assert mk_pavane_trust(actor). Assert mk_free_fit(actor). Give mk_fitters_picks to actor. }
    Result "She sits in her own chair, which she has not done in thirty-nine years, with the straws in her nose and the oiled cloth at her hairline, and says in a small voice that it is the oddest thing, to be on the other side of one's own hands. Yours are not hers. But you have watched; you rub the plaster up to the right warmth, and lay it as lightly as breath, and you wait. It comes away with a small wet sound. She holds her own face up to the lamp, and says nothing for so long that the stove ticks twice. Then she takes a ring of little steel picks from her apron, and puts it in your hand, and shuts your fingers on it. 'I shall want it back,' she says, 'when you have stopped being a stranger.' She will put it on the Wall tomorrow. Tonight she wants it here.".
    Otherwise "The plaster goes on too warm and sets crooked, and when you lift it, it takes a tuft of her hair and half her eyebrow with it. She says nothing at all, with great dignity, until you are both laughing, which is a thing neither of you expected to do tonight. 'Again,' she says. 'Not tonight. I have no more eyebrow.'".
  }
  Action mk_p_veil(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Madame Pavane to lift the black cloth from the last face on the shelf of Lamps" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cast_cellar) and at(pavane, cast_cellar) and at(actor, site) and not knows(actor, marrick_was_treasurer) and not mk_veil_refused(actor) and not mk_cast_pavane(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, marrick_was_treasurer). Assert mk_pavane_told(actor). }
    On failure { Assert mk_veil_refused(actor). }
    Result "She is a long time at it, with the cloth between finger and thumb. 'Nineteen,' she says. 'Lamps. My master cut her Treasurer on a morning like this one, in the second week of the Rains, and I held the bowl, and she cried through the whole of the fitting, and I, God forgive me, told her to hold still.' She folds the cloth, and lays it on the shelf, and the plate under it says T for the Sluice year, and then, in the same hand, R. 'The Registrar is dead. I know it as a Fitter knows it: the cloth goes on when a mask comes back to me with nobody in it. I have not said so to a living soul, because it is not mine to say.' She looks at you. 'Do not make me sorry.'".
    Otherwise "'No.' She does not raise her voice. 'There are cloths on a Fitter's Wall that are not to be lifted by a stranger, and that one is the first of them.' She stands between you and the shelf, and the lamp swings very slightly on its hook, as though something had passed.".
  }
  Action mk_p_veil_free(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Madame Pavane, whose face you have cast, to lift the black cloth" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cast_cellar) and at(pavane, cast_cellar) and at(actor, site) and not knows(actor, marrick_was_treasurer) and mk_cast_pavane(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, marrick_was_treasurer). Assert mk_pavane_told(actor). }
    Result "She lifts it before you have finished asking. 'Nineteen,' she says. 'Lamps. My master cut her Treasurer on a morning like this one, in the second week of the Rains, and I held the bowl, and she cried through the whole of it, and I told her to hold still.' She lays the cloth on the shelf. The plate under it says T for the Sluice year, and then R. 'I have been wanting to say that to someone for nine days,' says Madame Pavane. 'There was no one it was safe to say it to.'".
  }
  // Lifted by hand, with or without her leave: with the Fitter by it is a rudeness she remembers; alone it costs nothing.
  Action mk_lift_veil(actor: group, site: place) "Lift the black cloth from the last face on the shelf of Lamps" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cast_cellar) and at(actor, site) and not knows(actor, marrick_was_treasurer) and not at(pavane, cast_cellar).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, marrick_was_treasurer). }
    Result "The wool comes away in your fingers with a faint pull of the pin. Under it is a girl's face in plaster, plain, a lamp-trimmer's jaw, and the plate says Y. MARRICK, and the second chalk says T for the year of the Sluice, and under that R. It is the same R as on the Registrar's seal. The cloth is the kind a house puts over its mirrors when somebody has died.".
  }
  Action mk_lift_veil_rude(actor: group, site: place) "Lift the black cloth yourself, with the Fitter standing by" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cast_cellar) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, cast_cellar) and mk_veil_refused(actor) and not knows(actor, marrick_was_treasurer).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, marrick_was_treasurer). Retract mk_pavane_trust(actor). Assert mk_pavane_cold(actor). Increase heat(actor) by 1. Assert at(actor, pavane_parlour). Retract mk_guiding(pavane). Assert at(pavane, pavane_parlour). }
    Result "You lift it. She does not stop you; she watches you do it, with an expression you will remember: not anger, but the look of a woman who has been right about a person. Under the wool is a girl's face, and the plate, and T, and R. Then she takes you by the elbow, perfectly politely, up the stair and out of her parlour, and the cellar door shuts behind you with a very small sound, and a note will go to the Watch in the morning.".
  }

  // The Fit. A sitter whose Office mask is in hand may have it cut to their face; the Fitter's are good fits with no tell.
  Action mk_p_fit(actor: group, mask: face, site: place) "Ask the Fitter to Fit {mask} to your face, twenty-five coin" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, site) and castTaken(actor) and holdsFace(actor, mask) and not rentable(mask) and distinct(mask, face_white) and not fitted(actor, mask) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 25 and not named(pavane).
    Time 90 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 25. Increase quantity(pavane, gold) by 25. Assert fitted(actor, mask). }
    Result "She works with the mask on her knee and your cast on the table beside it, and shaves a hair from here and a hair from there, and bends the eyeholes a thought toward the face that is going to have to look out of them, and does not say what she is doing, or whose face it was cut for, or what she thinks of someone who would come to her with this. When it goes on, it sits like a hand. 'There,' she says. 'It has no tell. That is the other thing I am for.'".
  }
  Action mk_p_fit_free(actor: group, mask: face, site: place) "Ask the Fitter, whose face you cast, to Fit {mask} to you for nothing" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, site) and castTaken(actor) and mk_free_fit(actor) and holdsFace(actor, mask) and not rentable(mask) and distinct(mask, face_white) and not fitted(actor, mask) and not named(pavane).
    Time 90 minutes.
    On success { Retract mk_free_fit(actor). Assert fitted(actor, mask). }
    Result "She does not take a coin. She works with her lip between her teeth and the mask on her knee, and when it goes on and sits like a hand she says, without looking up, 'There. Do not tell anyone I did it for nothing. They will think I have gone soft, and the Guild will want to charge more.'".
  }

  // ── Dov Ashe, and the mask that fits nobody ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Sixteen, brilliant, ashamed. His journeyman's piece is judged by the Guild on the ninth afternoon: a mask cut from a
  // cast of the Fitter's choosing, which must fit the face it was cut for. She told him to take a face nobody would miss;
  // he took the last on the shelf of the Drowned, a man pulled from the Cuff in the Sluice year and never claimed, and
  // not on the Wall's other shelves, because he was a stranger. The mask is the best Dov has made. It falls off every
  // face in Ombra, and sits on the Bare: a face for somebody who has no one to claim him.
  Person dov "Dov Ashe" at fitting_room {
    Role "the Fitter's apprentice". Ancestry human. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Known as "a boy in an apprentice's half-mask, with a broom" when publicHours() and not knows(party, mk_dov_name).
    Known as "a boy in an oilcloth cape with plaster in his hair" when privateHours() and not knows(party, mk_dov_name).
    Greets "A boy of sixteen starts like a hare and puts both hands behind him, though there is nothing in them but a broom. 'I wasn't,' he says. 'I'm not meant to — I sweep.' He holds the broom across himself the way a Second holds a sword, and looks at you with the particular dread of the very young who have done one thing wrong and think it is written on them.".
    Greets again "Dov looks up, and down again, and goes on sweeping a patch of floor that is already clean.".
  }
  Initially Assert unmaskTeaches(dov, mk_dov_name).
  Discovery mk_dov_name "The Fitter's apprentice is Dov Ashe, sixteen, a lamp-trimmer's son from the Drip, whose mother takes in sheets for the Guild and owes the Rain-Wives' burial club for his father.".
  Discovery mk_dov_hiding "On the Maskers' roofs after the Ninth Bell the Fitter's apprentice sits in the rain with something wrapped in oilcloth in his arms, which he holds as one holds a child.".
  Discovery mk_dov_story "Dov Ashe's journeyman's piece, to be judged by the Guild on the ninth afternoon, is a mask cut from the last nameless face on the Wall's shelf of the Drowned: a stranger pulled from the Cuff in the Sluice year and never claimed. It is the best mask he has made, and it falls off every face he has tried.".
  Discovery mk_mask_fits_bare "Dov's mask, cut from a drowned stranger who had nobody, falls off every face in Ombra and sits on yours: it fits only someone who has no one to claim them, a Bare.".
  Discovery mk_maule_makes "The Annex's faces are cut by the gross by Maule of the Cockle and Heron in Maskers' Lane; the Offices' faces are the Fitter's, and she does not say how she cuts them.".
  Discovery mk_maule_offer "Maule, the rival maskmaker, would take on Dov Ashe if the Fitter turned him out.".

  Relation mk_dov_holds(group). Relation mk_dov_showed(group). Relation mk_dov_trusts(group). Relation mk_dov_proud(group).
