    Greets "A round man with his sleeves rolled to the elbow looks out of the hatch with a ladle held like a sceptre. 'Soup,' he says. It is the only word in the room. 'I may speak, you see, because a kitchen that cannot say hot is a kitchen that scalds. The Rule is very clear on it, and I have never once been sorry. Soup.'".
    Greets again "'Soup,' says Brother Dunstan, comfortably.".
  }
  Rule mo_dunstan_day when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 21 and not at(mo_dunstan, refectory) { Assert at(mo_dunstan, refectory). }
  Rule mo_dunstan_night when (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 8) and not at(mo_dunstan, brothers_cells) { Assert at(mo_dunstan, brothers_cells). }
  Topic mo_dunstan_soup with mo_dunstan "Ask Brother Dunstan what the Brothers think of the Silence" when not masked(actor) once {
    Says "He wipes the ladle on his sleeve, which does not improve either. 'The Silence is very fine for those who are good at it. I have been excused it for twenty years, and I will tell you what I have learned, which is that a man who may speak and does not is very different from a man who may not.' He lowers his voice, which is not much lower. 'They are all in there arguing. Not aloud. You can taste it in the soup. It is salty with it.'".
  }
  Person mo_wick "Brother Wick" at cloister_garth {
    Role "a young Brother, with a bundle". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "A boy of nineteen in a Brother's wool is scrubbing the well-head with a brush, hard, as if it had offended him. He looks up, and then very quickly down. 'Wick,' he says. 'I am not allowed to say more than that to a guest, and I am not a very good Brother, so you must please say nothing about it.' He scrubs. 'It is only that there is so much of the day.'".
    Greets again "Brother Wick scrubs the well-head and does not look up.".
  }
  Rule mo_wick_garth when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 21 and not mo_wick_gone(party) and not at(mo_wick, cloister_garth) { Assert at(mo_wick, cloister_garth). }
  Rule mo_wick_cell when (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 8) and not mo_wick_gone(party) and not at(mo_wick, brothers_cells) { Assert at(mo_wick, brothers_cells). }
  Topic mo_wick_day with mo_wick "Ask Brother Wick what there is so much of" when not masked(actor) and publicHours() once {
    Says "'The day.' He sits back on his heels. 'The Rule says there are nine hours of the Silence and nine of work and nine of sleep, and it does not say what there is when you have done all three and are still nineteen.' He looks, quickly, at the garth door and the gate beyond it. 'At the Swap, you know, the Bare may take a face from any citizen who offers one. For a night. It is the only night we could.' He scrubs. 'I only wonder what it is like to be asked for something.'".
  }

  // ── Taking the cord: three ways in, and what each leaves ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // He will not teach the Quiets: they are happened to. The company is taken in as a guest by being heard (persuasion),
  // by being seen (insight: no one has looked at his hands in thirty years), or by freeing the bell (a rope, a ladder,
  // two arms: no charm at all). Each way leaves him thinking something different of the guest.
  Kind mo_cord_kind "a guest-cord of the Bare Brothers" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "A length of undyed rope the width of a finger, knotted nine times: one knot for each of the Quiets, tied loose, to be tightened by whoever has kept it. It is warm from a man's hand. It is the only thing the Brothers own that they were willing to give away.".
  Item mo_cord "a guest-cord of the Bare Brothers" is mo_cord_kind at offstage.
  Topic mo_amery_masked with amery "Speak to Brother Amery" when masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "The Brother turns, and looks at the mask, and then very carefully at the wall behind it. 'The Brothers do not speak to masks,' he says, to the wall, 'and masks do not speak to the Brothers. It is the single article on which the Order and the city have agreed in three hundred years.' He goes back to the broom. 'I should take it as a kindness, if you would take it off before you come again. I do not say it to be answered.'".
  }
  Topic mo_ask_in with amery "Ask Brother Amery to take you in as a guest of the Brothers" when not masked(actor) and not mo_vow(actor) and not mo_asked(actor) once {
    Says "'Take,' says Brother Amery. 'The Brothers do not take; we are found, like the weather. What is it you want of us? Everybody wants something of the Bare Brothers, it is the whole of our usefulness: a quiet corner, a burial, a bell.' He leans on the broom. 'Nine days. It will be nine days of being set exercises. It will not be pleasant, and at the end of it I will not be able to tell you that you passed. Convince me you are not here to be Bare in a better coat.' He does not look at the bell in the corner, which hangs fouled, and has hung so since the morning.".
    On discuss { Assert mo_asked(actor). }
  }
  Action mo_plead(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Brother Amery you have come for the Quiets and will not be turned away" {
    Speaker amery.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(amery, site) and mo_asked(actor) and not mo_vow(actor) and not masked(actor).
    Time 6.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert mo_vow(actor). Assert mo_vow_pleaded(actor). Assert arcBegun(actor, hand_door). Give mo_cord to actor. Assert knows(actor, mo_quiets_known). }
    Result "You say it as you would say it to a magistrate, and then, because he is not one, you say it again as you would say it to a friend. He listens to the second one. 'You have a good voice,' says Brother Amery. 'It will be the first thing the Quiets take.' He goes to the well, and draws a cup, and gives it to you, which is, you gather, the rite. A length of rope with nine loose knots is in your hand, and he is sweeping again. 'Mouth, Name, Hand, Back, Step, Hoard, Tongue, Face, Crown,' he says, to the flagstone. 'In that order, one a day. Do not look for them. Do not say I told you.'".
    Otherwise "He listens with great attention, as a man listens to rain that has begun to find a way in. 'I have heard that before,' says Brother Amery. 'It is a good voice. I have heard it from the pulpit, and it has not yet once been answered by a silence.' He sweeps.".
  }
  Action mo_read(actor: group, site: place) "Look at Brother Amery's hands, and not at his face, and ask what he is afraid of" {
    Speaker amery.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(amery, site) and mo_asked(actor) and not mo_vow(actor) and not masked(actor).
    Time 6.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert mo_vow(actor). Assert mo_vow_read(actor). Assert mo_afraid(actor). Assert knows(actor, mo_amery_afraid). Assert arcBegun(actor, hand_door). Give mo_cord to actor. Assert knows(actor, mo_quiets_known). }
    Result "You watch his hands, as you were not asked to. The broom goes on, but the left hand in his sleeve is working at something: a cord, with knots in it, nine of them; and each time the Door is named, the thumb goes down the cord and stops at the ninth. 'You are afraid,' you say. 'Not of the crowd.' The broom stops. 'In thirty years,' says Brother Amery, 'nobody has looked at my hands.' He does not look at them himself. Then he takes the cord out of his sleeve, and cuts a length of it with a knife, and gives it you. 'Mouth, Name, Hand, Back, Step, Hoard, Tongue, Face, Crown,' he says. 'One a day. Do not look for them.'".
    Otherwise "You look at his hands, and they are a sweeper's hands, and they sweep. If there is something in them it keeps its own counsel, and the Brother lets you look, with the courtesy of a man who has nothing to hide, or who is very good at it.".
  }
  // The bell: a rope fouled over the beam, which any strong back, or good hands, or a head for a ladder, can clear.
  Thing mo_bell "the cloister bell" at cloister_garth {
    State fouled "In the corner of the garth, under its own small roof, the Brothers' bell hangs from a beam with its rope fouled round the headstock; the clapper cannot swing, and the Brother whose duty it is has been standing under it since dawn, looking up.".
    State hung "The Brothers' bell hangs clear in its corner of the garth, with a tarred rope as thick as a wrist, and its voice, when it comes, is a plain brown one.".
    Change clear "Climb the beam and clear the bell-rope" from fouled to hung needing climbing.
    Change splice "Splice the frayed rope from the ground, and haul it free" from fouled to hung needing mending.
    Change heave "Heave the bell-rope free, hand over hand" from fouled to hung needing brawn.
  }
  Rule mo_bell_taken when state(mo_bell, hung) and changedBy(mo_bell, party) and not mo_vow(party) says "The bell speaks once, clean, and the Brother who stood under it all day sits down on the well-head and puts his face in his hands. Brother Amery has put down the broom. 'That bell,' he says, 'has been fouled since the morning of the Novena, and four of us have been up it. I cannot say no to a man who has mended my bell.' He takes a length of knotted rope from his sleeve, and puts it in your hand. 'Mouth, Name, Hand, Back, Step, Hoard, Tongue, Face, Crown. One a day. Do not look for them.'" teaches mo_quiets_known { Assert mo_vow(party). Assert mo_vow_bell(party). Assert arcBegun(party, hand_door). Give mo_cord to party. }

  // ── Brother Amery by night: the Door, and what he is afraid of ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // By day he speaks in the Order's formulae; after the Ninth Bell, in the refectory, he reads aloud to the dead, and speaks
  // like a man. The Reading is a register of the Bare buried in the garth: a day, a weather, no name. Sitting through
  // it is the one thing nobody has done in forty years, and it is what changes his mind.
  Topic mo_amery_door with amery "Ask Brother Amery, at the table after the Bell, about the Door" when privateHours() and not masked(actor) and mo_vow(actor) once {
    Says "'The Door,' he says, and sets down the pencil. 'Ninety years the Brothers have stood in the Chapel's door on the night of the Drawing and done nothing. The crowd goes round us like water round a post. It is the one useful thing we do.' His left hand is in his sleeve. 'This year the Registrar is dead, and nobody may say who the Drawing is for, and nobody knows if the Urn is anything but a jar. I have told the Order that the Brothers will not stand.' He looks at the ledger. 'I should be obliged if you did not ask me why.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mo_amery_door_known). }
  }
  Discovery mo_amery_door_known "Brother Amery has told the Bare Brothers they will not stand in the Chapel's door at the Drawing this year, and will not say why.".
  Action mo_amery_lore(actor: group, site: place) "Quote Brother Amery the Rule of the Door, as one who has read it" {
    Speaker amery.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(amery, site) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and mo_vow(actor) and knows(actor, mo_amery_door_known) and not knows(actor, mo_alder).
    Time 6.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, mo_alder). Assert mo_rule(actor). }
    Result "'The Brother at the Door does not stand against the crowd,' you say. 'He stands as a post stands, and the crowd, being water, goes round.' Brother Amery does not move. 'You have read the footnote,' he says. 'No one reads the footnote.' The footnote is one line: that the Rule has been broken once. He closes the ledger on the pencil. 'Alder,' he says. 'Nineteen, a good hand with a sick animal. Last year I told him to stand, for the Rule, and the crowd did not go round, for it was a bad year and they were frightened; and it went over him. They buried him by the well. I have not told the Order that I think the Rule is a lie. I have only told them we shall not stand.'".
    Otherwise "You say what the Rule says, as you remember it, and Brother Amery listens with courtesy and corrects it in four places. 'No,' he says. 'You are thinking of the Rule of the Silence. It is not the same. It is a great deal worse.'".
  }
  Action mo_sit_reading(actor: group) "Sit with Brother Amery through the Reading of the Weather, and say nothing" {
    Speaker amery.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, refectory) and at(amery, refectory) and not masked(actor) and mo_vow(actor) and not mo_reading(actor) and hour(clock) >= 20 and hour(clock) < 22.
    Time 12.
    On success { Assert mo_reading(actor). Set conviction(amery, mo_refusal) to 1. }
    Result "He reads. It is the register of the Bare who are buried in the garth, a line for each and no name: Tuesday. Rain. Wind from the south-west. Thursday. Fog. Thursday. Rain. He reads forty-one of them, in the voice of one reading to the dead because they cannot say it is dull. You do not speak. Somewhere in the third year he stops looking at the ledger, and by the fortieth he is reading it to you. At the end he does not say anything. He shuts the ledger. 'In forty years,' says Brother Amery, 'nobody has sat the Reading. I thought it was for me.'".
  }
  Entity mo_refusal: claim "Stillness is refusal: the Brothers do nothing because the city should be left to what it has made".
  Initially Assert believes(amery, mo_refusal). Initially Set conviction(amery, mo_refusal) to 2.
  Measure moMercy(group). Measure moAnswered(group). Measure moPresence(group).
  Action mo_confess(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Brother Amery what you did, and why, and that you were wrong to" {
    Speaker amery.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(amery, site) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and mo_vow(actor) and moMercy(actor) >= 1.
    Time 6.
    On success { Decrease moMercy(actor) by 1. Increase moAnswered(actor) by 1. Increase moKept(actor) by 1. Set conviction(amery, mo_refusal) to 1. }
    Result "You tell it badly, since it is a thing to be done well or not at all: the Quiet, the hour, what you did instead, and who it was for. He listens with his head down. 'You are telling me,' he says, 'that you broke it for another, and know that you broke it, and have not come to be told you were right.' He turns the pencil over. 'Then it is not broken. It was answered. The Rule has no word for it; I have always thought that a defect in the Rule.' He lays his hand, briefly and quite lightly, on your sleeve. 'I should be very sorry to be that sure of myself again.'".
  }
  Rule mo_amery_lets_go when mo_reading(party) and (moAnswered(party) >= 1 or moPresence(party) >= 3) and not mo_brothers_stand(party) and at(party, cloister_garth) and hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 20 once says "Brother Amery is sitting in the cloister garth at dawn, with the broom across his knees, and he does not get up as you come. 'I have been wrong about it,' he says, and it is quite quietly said. 'Not about Alder. About the Door. A post is not what they need. I thought stillness was a wall. It is a thing one gives, like a hand, and it was never meant to be given alone.' The cord in his sleeve has been cut in two. 'The Brothers will stand. All of us. You will not stand alone.'" { Assert mo_brothers_stand(party). Set conviction(amery, mo_refusal) to 0. }
  Rule mo_amery_lets_go_word when mo_reading(party) and (moAnswered(party) >= 1 or moPresence(party) >= 3) and not mo_brothers_stand(party) and not at(party, cloister_garth) and hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 20 once says "A Brother in undyed wool has come across the water after you, bare-headed, in the rain, to say what he was sent to say, and he says it like a man reading a register: that Brother Amery sat up all night over the book, and has changed his mind about the Door; that the Brothers will stand, all of them, nine abreast; and that you are not to stand alone." { Assert mo_brothers_stand(party). Set conviction(amery, mo_refusal) to 0. }

  Topic mo_amery_quiets with amery "Ask Brother Amery what the Quiets are for" when not masked(actor) and mo_vow(actor) and not knows(actor, mo_amery_for) once {
    Says "'For?' He sweeps. 'If I were to answer you I should have to be right.' A long pause, and the broom goes round the well-head. 'The Order says: that a man who can keep silent in the face of every provocation is a man nobody can use. It is a very good answer. It is the answer I was given at your age, and I gave it to Alder.' He looks at the flagstone as if it had spoken. 'I think I should like to be wrong about it. I should be wrong in a more interesting way than most.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mo_amery_for). }
  }
  Discovery mo_amery_for "The Order teaches that a man who can keep silent in the face of every provocation is a man nobody can use. Brother Amery gave that answer to Alder, and would like, he says, to be wrong about it.".
  Observe mo_amery_cut at cloister_garth when mo_brothers_stand(party) and at(amery, cloister_garth) "Brother Amery's broom leans against the well-head, where it has not leaned before, and the cord he kept in his sleeve has been cut through and tied to the bell-rope, in two ends, as one ties up a thing that has been let go.".

  // ── The Nine Quiets: the machinery ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A Quiet opens on its day, for a guest who has taken the cord, at a place in the city, between two hours; it closes
  // when it is met or when the window does. It is kept, or broken, or missed. Missing is neither: the thing happened and
  // the guest was not there for it, and absence is not keeping. A Quiet broken for another's sake may be told to the Quiet
  // by night and counted kept (answered); a Quiet kept by staying with someone is presence, and presence is what the Order
  // did not know it was for. moQuiet(party, q) holds for a Quiet kept (or answered); moBroke for one broken; moKept is the
  // count kept, moBroken the count broken; moPresence how many were kept by staying and not only by silence.
  Kind mo_quiet.
  Entity mo_q1: mo_quiet "the Quiet of the Mouth". Entity mo_q2: mo_quiet "the Quiet of the Name". Entity mo_q3: mo_quiet "the Quiet of the Hand".
  Entity mo_q4: mo_quiet "the Quiet of the Back". Entity mo_q5: mo_quiet "the Quiet of the Step". Entity mo_q6: mo_quiet "the Quiet of the Hoard".
  Entity mo_q7: mo_quiet "the Quiet of the Tongue". Entity mo_q8: mo_quiet "the Quiet of the Face". Entity mo_q9: mo_quiet "the Quiet of the Crown".
  Relation moQuiet(group, mo_quiet). Relation moBroke(group, mo_quiet). Relation mo_done(group, mo_quiet). Relation mo_missed(group, mo_quiet).
  Relation mo_open(mo_quiet). Relation mo_shut(mo_quiet). Relation mo_counted(mo_quiet). Relation mo_counted_broke(mo_quiet).
  Measure mo_day(mo_quiet). Measure mo_to(mo_quiet). Measure moKept(group). Measure moBroken(group).
  Initially Set mo_day(mo_q1) to 1. Initially Set mo_day(mo_q2) to 2. Initially Set mo_day(mo_q3) to 3. Initially Set mo_day(mo_q4) to 4. Initially Set mo_day(mo_q5) to 5.
  Initially Set mo_day(mo_q6) to 6. Initially Set mo_day(mo_q7) to 7. Initially Set mo_day(mo_q8) to 8. Initially Set mo_day(mo_q9) to 9.
  Initially Set mo_to(mo_q1) to 20. Initially Set mo_to(mo_q2) to 20. Initially Set mo_to(mo_q3) to 20. Initially Set mo_to(mo_q4) to 20. Initially Set mo_to(mo_q5) to 23.
  Initially Set mo_to(mo_q6) to 20. Initially Set mo_to(mo_q7) to 23. Initially Set mo_to(mo_q8) to 20. Initially Set mo_to(mo_q9) to 23.
  Rule mo_count_kept when moQuiet(party, ?q) and not mo_counted(?q) { Assert mo_counted(?q). Increase moKept(party) by 1. }
  Rule mo_count_broke when moBroke(party, ?q) and not mo_counted_broke(?q) { Assert mo_counted_broke(?q). Increase moBroken(party) by 1. }
  Rule mo_missed_rule when mo_open(?q) and not mo_done(party, ?q) and hour(clock) >= mo_to(?q) says "The hour of {?q} has gone by, and nothing was kept or broken in it. The thing happened, as things in the city do, with nobody of yours there to see it. The Brothers will not say you failed. They will only say that it was not kept." { Assert mo_missed(party, ?q). Assert mo_done(party, ?q). }
  Rule mo_closes when mo_open(?q) and (mo_done(party, ?q) or day(clock) != mo_day(?q) or hour(clock) >= mo_to(?q)) { Retract mo_open(?q). Assert mo_shut(?q). }
  // Each Quiet opens at its own place and hour for a company that has the cord, and says where to look.
  Rule mo_open_q1 when mo_vow(party) and day(clock) == 1 and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 20 and not mo_open(mo_q1) and not mo_shut(mo_q1) says "The cord in your sleeve is a little warmer than it was. Across the water, at the Gate, something has begun in the square that you would be a fool not to look at." { Assert mo_open(mo_q1). }
  Rule mo_open_q2 when mo_vow(party) and day(clock) == 2 and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 20 and not mo_open(mo_q2) and not mo_shut(mo_q2) says "The second knot has begun to itch. It is something at the Wardrobe Annex, you think, and you do not know why you think it." { Assert mo_open(mo_q2). }
  Rule mo_open_q3 when mo_vow(party) and day(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 20 and not mo_open(mo_q3) and not mo_shut(mo_q3) says "A sudden quiet comes across the square from the Hospice, such as you have not heard in that room, and you know it for a thing you are meant to go to." { Assert mo_open(mo_q3). }
  Rule mo_open_q4 when mo_vow(party) and day(clock) == 4 and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 20 and not mo_open(mo_q4) and not mo_shut(mo_q4) says "It has begun to rain harder on the Customs Steps. You do not know how you know that." { Assert mo_open(mo_q4). }
  Rule mo_open_q5 when mo_vow(party) and day(clock) == 5 and hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 23 and not mo_open(mo_q5) and not mo_shut(mo_q5) says "Dusk, and the Swap. In the cloister garth a Brother has been standing by the door for an hour with a bundle, and has not yet moved." { Assert mo_open(mo_q5). }
  Rule mo_open_q6 when mo_vow(party) and day(clock) == 6 and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 20 and not mo_open(mo_q6) and not mo_shut(mo_q6) says "The Flood has sent the low islands up to Chapel Island, and a queue has begun at the Brothers' refectory door that goes out of the cloister and round the corner of the wall." { Assert mo_open(mo_q6). }
  Rule mo_open_q7 when mo_vow(party) and day(clock) == 7 and hour(clock) >= 20 and hour(clock) < 23 and not mo_open(mo_q7) and not mo_shut(mo_q7) says "After the Ninth Bell the seventh knot is warm. In the Hospice, a woman is sitting up with a string." { Assert mo_open(mo_q7). }
  Rule mo_open_q8 when mo_vow(party) and day(clock) == 8 and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 20 and not mo_open(mo_q8) and not mo_shut(mo_q8) says "Crowds are gathering on the steps of the Chapel, the first of the Drawing's: and for the first time in the Novena a good many of them are looking, with interest, at the Bare." { Assert mo_open(mo_q8). }

  // ── 1. The Mouth: a child struck in the square ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // To speak. The alternatives: speak (a face is heard; a bare mouth is only counted), or kneel and gather the pies. The
  // first costs heat if you are bare, and teaches the Standing in the plainest way there is: said to nobody, and charged.
  Observe mo_q1_scene at gate_square when mo_open(mo_q1) "By the Annex window a big man in a cockle-domino has a child by the collar, with a tray-boy's tray at his feet and eel-pies all over the wet paving. The child is perhaps seven and has the look of one who has been struck before and waits, with a kind of professional interest, to see where. The square goes round them as water goes round a stone; a porter studies the sky. Nobody has said anything. It is nobody's business. That is the Concord.".
  Relation mo_spoke1(group).
  Action mo_q1_gather(actor: group) "Kneel in the wet and gather up the child's pies, saying nothing" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, gate_square) and mo_open(mo_q1) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q1).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q1). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q1). Increase moPresence(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You get down on the stones, which is not easy in the clothes you are wearing, and begin to pick up eel-pies one at a time. The man stands over you, waiting to be answered, with his hand still out; and nobody answers him, and there is nothing to hit; and after a while the hand finds out what it is doing, and goes into his coat. He goes. The boy takes the last pie out of your hand and looks at you, directly, which no one else in the square has done, and goes after his tray. Your own hands are shaking. That, you suppose, is the Quiet.".
  }
  Action mo_q1_speak(actor: group) "Tell the man to stop" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, gate_square) and mo_open(mo_q1) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q1) and publicHours().
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q1). Assert moBroke(actor, mo_q1). Increase moMercy(actor) by 1. Assert mo_spoke1(actor). }
    Result "'Stop,' you say, aloud, in the square, in daylight, to a man in a mask.".
  }
  Rule mo_q1_heard when mo_spoke1(party) and masked(party) once says "He turns, and finds a face to answer, which is what he has been trained for. One mask to another: he lets go of the collar, and says in the trade's form that he did not see your hand in the matter, and is very sorry. The boy is gone before the word is done. The man goes with some dignity, as one who has been corrected by a colleague. It has worked entirely, and for a wrong reason: nothing was said to him. It was said to your face." { }
  Rule mo_q1_unheard when mo_spoke1(party) and not masked(party) once says "The man does not hear it. He goes on not hearing it with a thoroughness you can only admire, and in the pause the blow he had begun lands anyway, on the child, and the child cries. Three masked heads in the square have turned, as heads turn at a smell, and one grey Watch domino has stopped walking. You said a word to nobody, and have been counted for it." { Increase heat(party) by 1. }

  // ── 2. The Name: the Inspector of Rented Faces ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // To name. A Bare may Name whom he likes: it is the only weapon the city lets him. The alternatives: Name him in the
  // Annex (the generic name_aloud: heat, and a man ruined by sundown); whisper the name to him, which is the Concord's
  // loophole and a quiet cruelty of its own; or stand there, and be thanked for not saying it.
  Person mo_inspector "Orrin Gadd" at offstage {
    Role "the Inspector of Rented Faces". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Known as "the Inspector of Rented Faces, in a Heron's cowl" when not knows(party, mo_pask_known).
    Greets "A Heron's cowl turns a quarter toward you, and away, as a man turns from a draught.".
  }
  Discovery mo_pask_known "The Inspector of Rented Faces, who fines Moll a coin for every face returned a minute after the Ninth Bell by a clock a quarter of an hour fast, is Orrin Gadd.".
  Initially Assert unmaskTeaches(mo_inspector, mo_pask_known).
  Rule mo_inspector_comes when mo_open(mo_q2) and not at(mo_inspector, annex_counter) { Assert at(mo_inspector, annex_counter). }
  Rule mo_inspector_goes when not mo_open(mo_q2) and at(mo_inspector, annex_counter) { Assert at(mo_inspector, offstage). }
  Observe mo_q2_scene at annex_counter when mo_open(mo_q2) "A Heron's cowl stands at the counter with a ledger of its own, and before it, hands flat on the wood, Moll is counting coins out of his own purse: the Inspector of Rented Faces, fining the Annex a coin for each face returned a minute after the Ninth Bell, by a clock that is, Moll would tell you if he could, a quarter of an hour fast. By the Inspector's glove lies a chit signed in the neat hand of a man paid to be understood: O. GADD. It is the third such morning." teaches mo_pask_known.
  Rule mo_q2_named when named(mo_inspector) and not mo_done(party, mo_q2) and not moBroke(party, mo_q2) says "The name goes across the Annex like a dropped tray, and out of the door, and across the square: Gadd. By dusk the whole Gate will have it, and every grudge that has not yet been told it: his creditors, his tailor, his wife's sister. The cowl stands quite still. Moll has gone the colour of the pegs. Nobody is fined. It is the first quiet hour the Annex has had in three mornings, and you have bought it with a man." { Assert mo_done(party, mo_q2). Assert moBroke(party, mo_q2). }
  Action mo_q2_whisper(actor: group) "Lean across the counter and say the Inspector's name to him, very low" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, annex_counter) and mo_open(mo_q2) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q2) and knows(actor, mo_pask_known).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q2). Assert moBroke(actor, mo_q2). Increase moMercy(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You say it so low that Moll, a yard away, does not hear it; so low it is hardly a word. 'Gadd.' The Inspector's glove stops on the counter. For a long moment the cowl does not turn, and then he lays down on the wood, one at a time, the coins he has taken, and two more for the morning, and goes out. He does not look at you. Nobody has been Named; the square has heard nothing. Behind you Moll lets out a breath he has been keeping since the Novena began.".
  }
  Action mo_q2_stand(actor: group) "Stand at the end of the counter and say nothing, while Moll is fined" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, annex_counter) and mo_open(mo_q2) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q2).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q2). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q2). }
    Result "You stand where a man could see you. The Inspector does not; the Bare are not there. He counts out the fine, and Moll counts it in, and the Annex clock, which is fast, strikes the quarter. When the cowl has gone Moll puts his hand on the counter beside yours, not touching, as a man rests a hand near a dog he does not know. 'Thank you for not saying anything,' he says. 'It is very rare.' He does not say what it cost him to be so thanked, and you do not ask. It cost him three coin.".
  }

  // ── 3. The Hand: a mask in the Hospice ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // To strike. The alternatives: hit him (heat, and a wet glad roar); stand between, saying nothing (the body as a wall);
  // or ring Tibb's bell, and let the Hospice's own usage make him a burglar by daylight. The third is the Gate's lesson
  // in miniature: the city's rules are weapons that nobody uses.
  Observe mo_q3_scene at hospice_hall when mo_open(mo_q3) "A man in the Cockle's cream domino has come in off the square, which a mask may not do, and stands in the middle of the Hospice hall with Master Voss by the collar and a baker's bill in his fist. The loud room has gone quiet in a way that can be heard. The cartographer holds his drawing-board to his chest like a shield, and does not look up: he cannot, you remember, look at a face. At the long table Mother Tibb has lifted her pen, and is waiting, with the air of a woman who has been waiting nine years, to be asked.".
  Action mo_q3_bell(actor: group) "Take up Mother Tibb's hand-bell and ring it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, hospice_hall) and mo_open(mo_q3) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q3) and not masked(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q3). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q3). }
    Result "You take the bell off the table and ring it. The effect is out of all proportion. Mother Tibb lowers the pen. 'A mask,' she says, in the Hospice voice, 'in the hall after the bell. By the Usages, a burglar.' Every bare face in the room turns to look at him at once, thirty damp faces, with nothing between them and him; and the man in the cockle-domino, who has never in his life been looked at by so many faces together, lets go of the collar as if it were hot, and goes backward through the door, bill and all. 'There,' says Mother Tibb. 'It is a very good rule. I do not think it has been used in nine years.'".
  }
  Action mo_q3_stand(actor: group) "Stand between the man and the cartographer, and say nothing" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, hospice_hall) and mo_open(mo_q3) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q3) and not masked(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q3). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q3). Increase moPresence(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You get up and stand between them, close, with your hands where he can see them. It is, in a city of masks, the single most alarming thing a Bare can do, since he cannot tell whom he is being stood in front of. He tries to go round you. You stand. After a time he lets go the collar to wave you off, and finds he has said the bill aloud, and that thirty people have heard what it was, which was four coin; and he puts it in his coat, and goes. Master Voss does not look up. His hand on the board has stopped shaking.".
  }
  Action mo_q3_strike(actor: group) "Strike the man" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, hospice_hall) and mo_open(mo_q3) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q3) and not masked(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q3). Assert moBroke(actor, mo_q3). Increase heat(actor) by 2. }
    Result "You hit him. It is not a good blow, but he is not expecting any; he sits down on the floor with his domino askew and the bill still in his fist, and for a moment you see the edge of a face under it: a plain frightened one, with a moustache. The hall roars, a great wet glad bare roar. He gets up and goes, and you have been, in front of thirty of the Bare and one window of the Watch, a Bare who struck a mask. Mother Tibb writes in her ledger, quite slowly. You do not know what.".
  }

  // ── 4. The Back: a woman on the Steps ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // To turn away. The Quiet is kept by staying; what the Order did not teach is that a coin is the most courteous way of
  // going. The alternatives all break it: walk on, or pay and walk on. The one that keeps it costs three hours in the rain
  // and gives her nothing at all.
  Observe mo_q4_scene at customs_steps when mo_open(mo_q4) "On the sixth step up from the water a Bare woman sits in the rain with a child's shoe in one hand and no sheet. She has been put out of the Hospice, by the nine-day rule or the eleven-in-nine one, and has not yet found anywhere else to be. People go up and down past her with their heads a little turned. She is not asking for anything. That, you see, is what makes it difficult.".
  Action mo_q4_sit(actor: group) "Sit down on the wet step beside her, and stay" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, customs_steps) and mo_open(mo_q4) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q4).
    Time 18.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q4). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q4). Increase moPresence(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You sit. The stone is wet through at once. She does not look at you. After an hour she begins to talk, not to you, to the water: about a girl, and a boat that went to the Drip with a lamp and did not come back, and the shoe. You do not answer. At the end of the third hour, when the Ninth Bell is near, she says 'Thank you' to the steps, and gets up, and goes up them to find the Brothers, who will bury, if they cannot house. You have given her nothing. You stand with a numb leg and the damp sense of having been, for three hours, less alone than you had arranged to be.".
  }
  Action mo_q4_coin(actor: group) "Give her four coin, and go on up" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, customs_steps) and mo_open(mo_q4) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q4) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 4.
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q4). Assert moBroke(actor, mo_q4). }
    Result "She takes it, and says thank you, and means it, and you go up the steps lighter by four coin and the whole of your intention. It was the right amount. It was exactly the sum that lets a person be left. Behind you on the sixth step a woman with a shoe holds a coin in her other hand and has not looked up. The step is just as wet.".
  }
  Action mo_q4_on(actor: group) "Go on up the steps" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, customs_steps) and mo_open(mo_q4) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q4).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q4). Assert moBroke(actor, mo_q4). }
    Result "You go on up the steps. It is perfectly easy; it is what the Bare do; the whole of Ombra goes up and down past her. You are nearly at the top when you notice that your own head has turned a little to one side, as the others' do. You are not aware of having turned it.".
  }

  // ── 5. The Step: Brother Wick and the Swap ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // To intervene. The Brother is going, tonight, as a Bare may at the Swap, if a stranger will give him a face. The
  // alternatives: argue him out of it (it may work, and it is not yours to do), carry his lantern while he goes (presence:
  // the Quiet kept by taking part), or let him go alone (kept, and cold).
  Observe mo_q5_scene at cloister_garth when mo_open(mo_q5) "Brother Wick stands by the garth door with a bundle in a cloth, and has stood there an hour, watching the rain. Tonight is the Swap, and a Bare may take a face for the night from anyone who will give it. He has not said he is going. He has not said anything. It is the Rule.".
  Action mo_q5_lantern(actor: group) "Carry Brother Wick's lantern to the Square, and wait while he is asked" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cloister_garth) and at(mo_wick, cloister_garth) and mo_open(mo_q5) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q5).
    Time 12.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q5). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q5). Increase moPresence(actor) by 1. Assert mo_wick_gone(actor). Assert at(mo_wick, offstage). }
    Result "You carry the lantern. He says nothing and neither do you. In Strangers' Square, in the dusk, he stands on the paving with the bundle at his feet while the whole city goes by in its spare faces, offering them about, laughing, as at a fair; and nobody offers him anything for a long time. He stands very straight. Then a woman in a pierrot-white half-mask, who has been watching him, puts it into his hands without a word, and he takes it, and holds it, and does not put it on. He looks at you. 'It is only for the night,' he says. Then he puts it on, and is somebody, and goes into the crowd as a boy goes into a river. You are left holding the lantern. It is still lit.".
  }
  Action mo_q5_argue(actor: group) "Tell Brother Wick that he is a Brother and should not go" {
    Speaker mo_wick.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cloister_garth) and at(mo_wick, cloister_garth) and mo_open(mo_q5) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q5) and not masked(actor).
    Time 6.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q5). Assert moBroke(actor, mo_q5). Assert mo_wick_stays(actor). }
    On failure { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q5). Assert moBroke(actor, mo_q5). Assert mo_wick_gone(actor). Assert at(mo_wick, offstage). }
    Result "He listens with the bundle in both hands. It is a good argument; you hear, as you make it, that it is nearly all your own. 'You are right,' says Brother Wick at last, in a small voice, and puts the bundle down by the well, and picks up the brush; and does not look at you again for the rest of the day.".
    Otherwise "He hears you out with a face of stone, nineteen and obstinate, and thanks you for it, and picks up the bundle. 'You mean it well,' he says, 'and you are the second today who has.' He goes out through the garth door, quite politely, with his hood back, into the rain.".
  }
  Action mo_q5_letgo(actor: group) "Let him go without a word" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cloister_garth) and at(mo_wick, cloister_garth) and mo_open(mo_q5) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q5).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q5). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q5). Assert mo_wick_gone(actor). Assert at(mo_wick, offstage). }
    Result "You say nothing. He looks at you for a moment, in case. Then he picks up the bundle and goes out through the garth door with his hood back, into the rain, and the door is a long time swinging after him. Somewhere in the cloister a Brother who saw him go has begun, very softly, to sweep. It is a thing the Rule is for, you suppose. You do not feel that it was for him.".
  }
  Rule mo_wick_unmet when day(clock) == 5 and hour(clock) >= 23 and not mo_wick_gone(party) and not mo_wick_stays(party) says "At some hour after the Swap has begun, somebody in the cloister goes out of the garth door with a bundle, bare-headed, without being asked, and the door is a long time swinging." { Assert mo_wick_gone(party). Assert at(mo_wick, offstage). }

  // ── 6. The Hoard: the Flood, and the Order's last sacks ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // To hoard. The Flood sends the low islands up the hill to the cloister; the Order's last store is for the ninth night,
  // when the Brothers feed the Chapel's crowd. Giving what is yours keeps the Quiet and costs a little; opening the store
  // keeps it and costs the Drawing a supper; holding back everything for the ninth night breaks it, for the best of reasons.
  Relation mo_stores_given(group). Relation mo_stores_kept(group).
  Observe mo_q6_scene at refectory when mo_open(mo_q6) "The queue for the Brothers' hatch goes out of the refectory door, round the corner of the cloister wall and into the rain: mothers with children inside their coats, a man with a clock he saved from the water, an old woman carrying a hen. Brother Dunstan is ladling as fast as a ladle will go, and the soup is thinning. In the store behind the hatch, you have been told, are the Order's last sacks: they are for the ninth night, when the Brothers feed the Chapel's crowd.".
  Action mo_q6_give(actor: group) "Give what food and coin you can spare to the queue" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, refectory) and mo_open(mo_q6) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q6) and (quantity(actor, rations) >= 1 or quantity(actor, gold) >= 1).
    Time 6.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, rations) by 3 or to nothing. Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 4 or to nothing. Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q6). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q6). }
    Result "You put what you have in the cook's hands, which is not much, and he ladles it into the pot without comment, as a man puts a coin in a well. It feeds eleven. You watch eleven people who had nothing eat what you had, and go; and then you look at the queue, which has not noticeably shortened. It is a very clean feeling. It is also, you notice, far too small.".
  }
  Action mo_q6_ladle(actor: group) "Take a ladle beside Brother Dunstan, and serve until the soup runs out" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, refectory) and mo_open(mo_q6) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q6).
    Time 18.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q6). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q6). Increase moPresence(actor) by 1. }
    Result "He does not say a word, which for Brother Dunstan is a remark. You stand beside him in the steam and ladle, and the faces come up to the hatch one after another, wet and polite and hungry, and each of them looks at the soup and not at you, and you find you have learned the trick of it: to hand the bowl across so that the hand is steady and the eyes are somewhere kind. After three hours the pot scrapes. 'There,' says Brother Dunstan. It is the longest speech you have heard from him. 'There. That is the Silence, if you want to know. It is for the soup.'".
  }
  Action mo_q6_store(actor: group) "Ask Brother Dunstan to open the Order's store for the queue" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, refectory) and mo_open(mo_q6) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q6).
    Time 12.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q6). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q6). Assert mo_stores_given(actor). }
    Result "He holds the ladle still over the pot, and the soup runs off it in a thread. 'It is for the ninth,' says Brother Dunstan. 'Yes,' you say. He says something under his breath that would be a prayer in anyone wearing a face. Then he unlocks the store. By dusk the queue has eaten the Order's whole reserve and gone away warm. Nobody thanks you; they do not know who you are. On the ninth night, you think, there will have to be a miracle; and you find you do not much mind.".
  }
  Action mo_q6_hold(actor: group) "Keep your rations, and keep the store shut for the ninth night" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, refectory) and mo_open(mo_q6) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q6).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q6). Assert moBroke(actor, mo_q6). Increase moMercy(actor) by 1. Assert mo_stores_kept(actor). }
    Result "You tell Brother Dunstan that the ninth night will want its soup, and that tomorrow will not be less hungry than today. He nods slowly, with the face of a man who has made the same arithmetic. It is true. Every word of it is true; and at the hatch, as you say it, a woman with a hen turns and goes out of the queue with her face quite empty. You have done something which, tomorrow, will be right.".
  }

  // ── 7. The Tongue: Mother Tibb and the eleven ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // To comfort falsely. Tibb asks to be told that the eleven she sent out of the Gate were all right. The company knows no
  // such thing. The alternatives: lie, which she will see through and accept; say it does not know and sit with her; or
  // say nothing and let her go on knotting.
  Observe mo_q7_scene near tibb when mo_open(mo_q7) "Mother Tibb sits with the string in her lap, and has not knotted anything for a quarter of an hour. She has taken off the grey half-mask, and looks, without it, as anyone does. 'You have been out in the city,' she says, to the string. 'You will have seen the Gate. Tell me about the eleven I sent out of it. You will have seen them. Tell me they were all right.'".
  Action mo_q7_truth(actor: group, site: place) "Tell her that you do not know, and sit with her" {
    Speaker tibb.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(tibb, site) and mo_open(mo_q7) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q7) and not masked(actor).
    Time 12.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q7). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q7). Increase moPresence(actor) by 1. }
    Result "'I do not know,' you say. 'I have never seen them. I will sit.' She breathes out through her nose, nearly a laugh, and moves the string over so that you may hold the other end. You sit. She ties a knot that she has been putting off; it is for nobody yet; it is for the space in the ledger, and she will not say whose. At the end she says: 'It is the first true thing anyone has said to me since the Novena began, and it was no use at all.' She does not let go of her end of the string.".
  }
  Action mo_q7_lie(actor: group, site: place) "Tell her that they were all right" {
    Speaker tibb.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(tibb, site) and mo_open(mo_q7) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q7) and not masked(actor).
    Time 3 minutes.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q7). Assert moBroke(actor, mo_q7). Increase moMercy(actor) by 1. }
    Result "'They were all right,' you say. 'I saw them. They were well.' It is easy. It is the kindest thing you have said in nine days. Mother Tibb looks at you with an expression you cannot read, and then she nods, slowly, and thanks you; and you see that she knows precisely what you have done, and that she is going to let you have done it. 'That is very good of you,' she says. 'You will not be offended if I do not believe a word.' She goes back to the string. It is, you realise, the exact kindness she gives Peck, with the tea, and it has been returned.".
  }
  Action mo_q7_still(actor: group, site: place) "Say nothing, and let her go on with the string" {
    Speaker tibb.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(tibb, site) and mo_open(mo_q7) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q7) and not masked(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q7). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q7). }
    Result "You say nothing. She goes on knotting, and does not need you to do otherwise. After a time you understand that you were not asked to answer; it was only that she wished it said into the room. When she has finished she says, 'Good night, Bare,' and means it a little more than she did this morning.".
  }

  // ── 8. The Face: the Exchange offers a white domino ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // To be seen. For the Drawing the Guilds have decided to look at the Brother of the Door, and to give him a face of
  // honour. A face makes a person, and a person can be pushed: the Door holds only as a post holds, because it is nobody.
  Relation mo_honoured(group).
  Observe mo_q8_scene at chapel_steps when mo_open(mo_q8) "A knot of masks at the foot of the Chapel steps has been watching the cloister door, and now a delegation comes across: three Heron-cowls and a Cockle, with a white domino of fine linen on a cushion. 'Brother,' says the eldest, to you, which nobody has said to a Bare since the Novena began, 'the Exchange and the Guilds, who do not generally see you, have for the Drawing decided that they do. It is proposed that the Brother of the Door should stand as somebody. A face of honour; white; nobody's. You would be the first Bare in three hundred years the city has been so good as to look at.'".
  Action mo_q8_take(actor: group) "Take the white domino of honour, and put it on" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, chapel_steps) and mo_open(mo_q8) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q8).
    Time 3 minutes.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q8). Assert moBroke(actor, mo_q8). Assert mo_honoured(actor). }
    Result "It is very fine linen, and it fits. They say so: three Heron-cowls and a Cockle, in a small murmur, a thing nobody has said of you in this city. For the first time since you came down the delta road the rain on your face stops. Heads turn, as to a person. A woman nods. You are looked at, and you find that it is a good deal like being warm. It is only afterwards, in the cloister, that you take it off and find the strings have printed on your cheeks, in red, the exact shape of what you wanted.".
  }
  Action mo_q8_refuse(actor: group) "Decline the domino, and say nothing" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, chapel_steps) and mo_open(mo_q8) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q8).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q8). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q8). }
    Result "You do not take it. You look at it on its cushion, and at them, and you shake your head a very little, and the eldest Heron lowers the cushion with the air of a man who has been refused a thing he did not understand he was offering. 'As you like,' he says; and then, to the others, in the voice masks use among themselves, 'Of course. They would.' You hear in it a great relief, and a little contempt; and you cannot tell which of the two is meant for you.".
  }
  Action mo_q8_bow(actor: group) "Bow to them, take nothing, and go on being looked at" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, chapel_steps) and mo_open(mo_q8) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q8).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q8). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q8). Increase moPresence(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You bow, which no Bare has done to a face in three hundred years without being asked, and you do not take the domino, and you do not go. You let them look. It is a long, odd, steady minute: the Heron-cowls, the Cockle, a child on her father's shoulders, all of them looking at a man with a bare face and nothing to give them, and being, for once, not looked away from. The eldest clears his throat. 'Well,' he says, rather helplessly. 'Well. There you are.' It is, you think, as near as the city has come to saying it.".
  }

  // ── 9. The Crown: the Door ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // To be proud. On the ninth night the Chapel's door is held, as it has been held for ninety years, by a man standing in
  // it and doing nothing. It is available to a company that has kept five of the Quiets. What the crowd does depends on
  // how many were kept, whether the Brothers stand with you, and whether you stand as nobody. The alternative to standing is
  // to speak, from the top step, what you know; and that is for the Drawing, and for the integrator, to answer.
  Relation mo_door_stood(group). Relation mo_door_spoke(group). Relation mo_door_told(group). Measure moDoor(group).
  Observe mo_q9_scene at chapel_steps when mo_open(mo_q9) and mo_vow(party) "The crowd of the Drawing has come over the Chapel bridge, and is still coming: all of Ombra in its Sunday faces, in the rain, with its lanterns, and the great doors of the Chapel standing open on a dark that smells of wax. They are not an angry crowd. They are only a very large one, and very tired, and nine days in the rain, and in every mouth a name that nobody has been allowed to say; and the doors are open, and at the far end of the nave, under the Urn Hall's arch, a stair goes down.".
  Rule mo_open_q9 when mo_vow(party) and day(clock) == 9 and hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 23 and not mo_open(mo_q9) and not mo_shut(mo_q9) says "The ninth knot is warm. At the Chapel steps the crowd has begun to gather, and you know what you are for." { Assert mo_open(mo_q9). }
  Rule mo_door_ready when mo_vow(party) and moKept(party) >= 5 and drawingNight() and not handReady(party, hand_door) says "You have kept the five that are needed, and the cord in your sleeve is knotted tight where they were. The Door is open for you to stand in, if you choose to." { Assert handReady(party, hand_door). }
  Action mo_door_stand(actor: group) "Stand in the Chapel's door, and do nothing" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, chapel_steps) and mo_open(mo_q9) and handReady(actor, hand_door) and not handPlayed(actor, hand_door) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q9).
    Time 18.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q9). Assert moQuiet(actor, mo_q9). Assert mo_door_stood(actor). Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_door). Assert arcDone(actor, hand_door). }
    Result "You stand in the door. You do not draw anything, or say anything, or lift a hand. You stand as a post stands, with the rain going down your neck, and the whole of Ombra, who have never in their lives been looked through so patiently, come up the steps.".
  }
  Action mo_door_speak(actor: group) "Go up on the top step and tell the crowd what you know of the Urn" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, chapel_steps) and mo_open(mo_q9) and handReady(actor, hand_door) and knows(actor, urn_hollow) and not handPlayed(actor, hand_door) and not mo_done(actor, mo_q9).
    Time 3 minutes.
    On success { Assert mo_done(actor, mo_q9). Assert moBroke(actor, mo_q9). Assert mo_door_spoke(actor). Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_door). Assert arcDone(actor, hand_door). }
    Result "You go up on the top step, with the door at your back, and open your mouth: and a Bare Brother speaking, in the rain, at the Drawing, is a thing that stops a crowd as a bell stops it. You tell them. You tell them in a plain, carrying, unpractised voice what you have seen of the Urn. It is quiet for as long as a held breath. And then the whole of the square is turning its head to see who has done this, and seeing a man with no face, and the thing you have said is no longer in your hands.".
  }
  Rule mo_door_honoured when mo_door_stood(party) and mo_honoured(party) and not mo_door_told(party) once says "They see a face. A white domino of honour in the Chapel door, somebody, and the crowd does what a crowd does with a somebody: it takes hold. You hold. You hold with the whole of your body for a long, wet, shoving hour, as a person holds, and not as a post; and there are bruises that will last, and there is a moment near the end when the door gives a hand's breadth and you give it back. It is held. It is a near thing. You are not sure it was the Quiet that held it." { Assert mo_door_told(party). Set moDoor(party) to 1. }
  Rule mo_door_calm when mo_door_stood(party) and mo_brothers_stand(party) and moKept(party) >= 7 and not mo_door_told(party) once says "The crowd comes up the steps, and finds a man standing in the door, and on either side of him, in the rain, in undyed wool, with their hoods back and their hands in their sleeves, the Bare Brothers: all of them, nine abreast, with Brother Amery at the end. There is a moment when the whole front of the crowd wavers like a held note. Then, somewhere at the back, someone sits down on the wet steps; and then another; and by the time the lamps are lit for the Drawing there are four thousand people sitting down in the rain, very quietly, as though they had been asked, and nobody has asked." { Assert mo_door_told(party). Set moDoor(party) to 3. }
  Rule mo_door_goes_round when mo_door_stood(party) and (moKept(party) >= 7 or mo_brothers_stand(party)) and not mo_door_told(party) once says "The crowd comes up the steps, and finds a man in the door who does not move, and goes round him like water round a post. It takes a long time, and there is a good deal of shoving, and one man spits; but the water finds its way, and after the first quarter-hour it has forgotten you are there. You are not alone, you notice, in the doorway of the Chapel of the Bare Face: there are others standing, at the edge of the steps, with their hoods back, watching. It was always meant to be done like this." { Assert mo_door_told(party). Set moDoor(party) to 2. }
  Rule mo_door_breaks when mo_door_stood(party) and not mo_door_told(party) once says "The crowd comes up the steps, and finds a man in the door who does not move, and does not go round him. It breaks on you: it spills at the edges, it shoves, it presses a lantern into your ribs; and for a long, wet, bruising hour you stand there with the rain going down your neck, and nothing in the world but your own feet. The door is held. At the end of it, the front of the crowd has learned, from its own weight, that there is something in front of it that is not going to give; and it goes, a little ashamed, to find another way in." { Assert mo_door_told(party). Set moDoor(party) to 1. }
  Rule mo_door_spoken when mo_door_spoke(party) and not mo_door_told(party) once says "The silence breaks at the back, first as a murmur and then as a shout; and a Brother has spoken in the open air, and whatever it was that the speech was for, it is a crowd's now, and has gone off with it into the rain, and there is nothing left in the doorway but a man with no face who has said what he knew." { Assert mo_door_told(party). Set moDoor(party) to 0. }

  // ── What the guest is given ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind mo_mantle_kind "the Bare Brothers' mantle" like old_glossary granting insight worth 0 weighing 1 described "A grey woollen mantle, undyed, with a hood to put back. It is the colour of the cloister walls, and warmer than it looks. A Brother in the street, in this, is not seen: not because he is hidden, but because the eye of the city slides off a thing that does not want to be looked at.".
  Item mo_mantle "the Bare Brothers' mantle" is mo_mantle_kind at offstage.
  Relation mo_mantled(group). Relation mo_endowed(group).
  Topic mo_amery_mantle with amery "Ask Brother Amery whether the Order has anything for a guest who has kept five" when not masked(actor) and mo_vow(actor) and moKept(actor) >= 5 and not mo_mantled(actor) once {
    Says "He puts down the broom, and goes into the walk, and comes out with a folded grey thing over his arm. 'It was Alder's,' says Brother Amery. 'It has been waiting.' He does not hold it out; he lays it across your arm, as one lays down something that is still warm. 'It does not make you invisible. The city does that by itself. What it does is let you look at a thing for as long as it takes, and nobody asks why.' He takes his hand away. 'He would have liked you,' he says, 'and I should not have let him.'".
    On discuss { Give mo_mantle to actor. Assert mo_mantled(actor). }
  }
  Action mo_endow(actor: group, reader: member) "Have {reader} take up the last knot of the cord, and tighten it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and memberOf(reader, actor) and at(actor, cloister_garth) and moKept(actor) >= 5 and not mo_endowed(actor).
    Time 12. Resolve endow(reader, wisdom, by_one).
    On success { Assert mo_endowed(actor). }
    Result "You sit in the garth by the well, in the rain, and work the last of the loose knots tight with your thumbs, and the nine days come down into the cord and stay there. It is a plain thing to do and takes an hour. When you are finished you find you are looking at the bell, and at the rain, and at the Brother with the broom, as if for the first time, and without wanting anything of them.".
  }

  // ── Milestones ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Milestone mo_m_vow "was taken in by the Bare Brothers, and given the cord" worth 25 when mo_vow(party).
  Milestone mo_m_five "kept five of the Nine Quiets" worth 75 when moKept(party) >= 5.
  Milestone mo_m_mind "changed Brother Amery's mind about the Door" worth 50 when mo_brothers_stand(party).
  Milestone mo_m_door "stood in the Chapel's door at the Drawing, and did nothing" worth 100 when mo_door_stood(party).

  // ── What became of them ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule mo_fate_amery_stood when newsHour() and mo_door_stood(party) and mo_brothers_stand(party) once says "Of Brother Amery: he stood at the end of the line of nine in the Chapel's door with his hands in his sleeves, and when it was over he sat down on the top step, in the rain, and laughed, which the Brothers say they had not heard in forty years, and is not in the Rule. He says that he was wrong about the Rule and right about the Door, and that the first is more use. He has had the Alder stone recut, with a name." { }
  Rule mo_fate_amery_alone when newsHour() and mo_door_stood(party) and not mo_brothers_stand(party) once says "Of Brother Amery: he did not stand. He watched from the cloister wall, with a broom in his hands, while the company held the door alone, and at the end of the night he put the broom down, and said, to the wall, that he had been wrong about the Order's silence, and had not had the courage to be wrong in time. He has gone about since with the cord in his sleeve cut through." { }
  Rule mo_fate_amery_unmet when newsHour() and mo_vow(party) and not mo_door_stood(party) once says "Of Brother Amery: the Chapel's door stood open on the night of the Drawing, and nobody stood in it, and the crowd went in as water goes into a house. Nobody was hurt. It was, the Brothers say, the first year in ninety that the Door was only a door, and Brother Amery has been seen, in the garth, looking at it as though it had come out wrong." { }
  Rule mo_fate_amery_novow when newsHour() and not mo_vow(party) once says "Of Brother Amery: the Brothers did not stand in the Chapel's door at the Drawing, for the Quiet had said they would not, and the crowd went in as water goes into a house. He swept the garth the whole of the night. It is not known whom he was sweeping it for." { }
  Rule mo_fate_wick_stays when newsHour() and mo_wick_stays(party) once says "Of Brother Wick: he is still in the cloister, scrubbing the well-head, harder than anyone has ever scrubbed a well-head. He says it is only that there is so much of the day. He has been seen, once, at the garth door, at dusk, looking at the Square; and then at you, if you were there, with a face that had decided something unfair." { }
  Rule mo_fate_wick_gone when newsHour() and mo_wick_gone(party) once says "Of Brother Wick: a boy in a pierrot half-mask was seen in the crowd at the Drawing, bare-headed in his heart, laughing; he has taken a trade, they say, in the Drip, and a face for it, and not once in his life since has he been asked for what he was." { }
  Rule mo_fate_dunstan_given when newsHour() and mo_stores_given(party) once says "Of Brother Dunstan: on the ninth night the Brothers had no soup for the crowd, and the crowd, which had been told for ninety years that the Bare Brothers fed the Drawing, made a sound at the hatch that was not anger. A woman with a hen went up to the Chapel's well and drew water, and the Brothers served it, hot, in the soup-bowls, and said it was soup, and Brother Dunstan has not once since been sorry." { }
  Rule mo_fate_dunstan_kept when newsHour() and mo_stores_kept(party) once says "Of Brother Dunstan: on the ninth night the Brothers fed the Drawing's crowd, as they had for ninety years, from the store he had held shut. A great many of the crowd were fed who had been refused on the sixth. He serves them with a face that has not forgiven itself, and says the soup is very good this year, and that he does not know why." { }
  Rule mo_fate_quiets_all when newsHour() and moKept(party) >= 9 once says "Of the Nine Quiets: all nine were kept, which the Order does not count as a success, since there is no word in the Rule for the one who keeps them all. The cord in the cloister is knotted tight. The Brothers have hung it by the bell, where it will be seen, and where no one will ever read what it is." { }
  Rule mo_fate_quiets_most when newsHour() and moKept(party) >= 7 and moKept(party) < 9 once says "Of the Nine Quiets: most were kept, and the two that were not are in the cloister's register as broken and answered, in a hand that has begun to be less certain which is which. The cord hangs by the bell. One knot has been left loose, on purpose, by a man who says the Order has always wanted one." { }
  Rule mo_fate_quiets_some when newsHour() and moKept(party) >= 5 and moKept(party) < 7 once says "Of the Nine Quiets: five or six were kept, which is the number, and the rest were not; the cord hangs by the bell with its loose knots like a rope of weather. Brother Amery says that is the right number, since it is the number that can say it was wrong." { }
  Rule mo_fate_quiets_few when newsHour() and mo_vow(party) and moKept(party) < 5 and moBroken(party) >= 3 once says "Of the Nine Quiets: more were broken than kept, and the Brothers say so without reproach. The cord hangs by the bell with its knots loose, and Brother Amery says that is the rope's honest condition, and that the Order, with its nine knots all tight, has been dishonest for ninety years." { }
  Rule mo_fate_door_calm when newsHour() and moDoor(party) >= 3 once says "Of the Chapel's door: four thousand people sat down in the rain on the Chapel steps on the night of the Drawing, and nobody has been able to explain it. The Chaplain calls it a miracle, the Watch calls it weather, and the Brothers do not call it anything." { }
  Rule mo_fate_woman_kept when newsHour() and moQuiet(party, mo_q4) once says "Of the woman on the Customs Steps: the Brothers have put her in the cell by the garth door, with a blanket and a bowl and the shoe, where she has been for five days, speaking to nobody, and no longer, they say, alone." { }
  Rule mo_fate_woman_not when newsHour() and moBroke(party, mo_q4) once says "Of the woman on the Customs Steps: she has not been seen since the ninth morning. The sixth step has been mopped. The Brothers have a line in their register for a Bare found at the foot of the steps at dawn, and it is the line for a Tuesday." { }
  Topic mo_amery_after with amery "Ask Brother Amery what he will do about the Door now" when mo_rule(actor) and not mo_brothers_stand(actor) once {
    Says "'I do not know.' He does not sweep; the broom has been put against the wall. 'I have been thinking that a post is a very bad thing to be, when the thing that goes round is a boy of nineteen. I have been thinking that I was told a Rule, and that it was a lie, and that it was a lie told to me by a man who believed it. That is the worst kind.' He looks at his hand. 'I will tell you at the Drawing. If I tell you now I shall have to be sure.'".
  }
  Observe mo_amery_pleaded at cloister_garth when mo_vow_pleaded(party) and at(amery, cloister_garth) and day(clock) >= 2 "Brother Amery sweeps with his back to you, in the manner of a man who is listening for a voice he is not at all sure he wishes to hear again.".
  Observe mo_amery_read at cloister_garth when mo_vow_read(party) and at(amery, cloister_garth) and day(clock) >= 2 "Brother Amery keeps his left hand in his sleeve, and when you come near he takes it out, quite slowly, and begins to sweep with both, so that you may see them.".
  Observe mo_amery_bell at cloister_garth when mo_vow_bell(party) and at(amery, cloister_garth) and day(clock) >= 2 "The bell speaks the hours in a plain brown voice, and each time Brother Amery looks up at it, and then at you, as at the face of a thing that does not need to be thanked.".
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/placed.kyr:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // A province of a generated world's first country: the company that comes down the delta road is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  // What the country's towns say of Ombra (a notice of the Novena, nailed up where travellers are kept): once the
  // Drawing is over, one way or another, it is old news there.
  Entity word: fact "What is said of Ombra and its Drawing in the towns of the country.".
  Rule word_old when drawingOver(ombra_delta) and not stale(word) { Assert stale(word). }
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/ranger.kyr:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The ranger: the Heronry ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Ombra has no wild but the reed-garden at the lagoon's edge and what the rats and the pigeons have made of the rest,
  // and a ranger in it is a tracker without a wood. The arc is three things. A craft: tracking a child who does not
  // want to be found through a city that rains on its own tracks, by what the rain does not wash (soot at a hand's
  // height, the crumbs on a grating, the runs the rats make to a scrap): three small readings, each a check, and a last
  // that costs nothing, which lets a company that has read the city walk into the den downwind and still. A question:
  // what a ranger is for, to keep the wild out of the city or to mend it so the city can live beside it (the Writ is the
  // whole argument in one reed-bed; Withy asks it, and what the company answers is the arc's creed). And a finale at
  // the Drawing, two ways, in the Hall: the old heron loosed in the light-well over the Urn, a sign the crowd takes for
  // the Registrar's soul; or a child brought up to speak. Anyone may play either; a ranger has the craft, the question,
  // a feather, a vigil, a lesson and a bird. (Prefix rg_; reads cisterns.kyr and heronry.kyr.)

  Query rg_ranger(a: group) means capable(a, woodcraft) or craft(a, craft_wild).

  // ── The craft: three readings of a city ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Rain washes a track in an hour and a Concord does not wash a habit. A lamp-boy goes by walls, not ground: he puts his
  // hand on the brick, so there is soot at a hand's height; he feeds pigeons, so there are crumbs on a lip; he leaves
  // scraps, so the rats make runs. A ranger who has read the three has read the boy.
  Discovery rg_sign_soot "Under the Chapel's porch, at a small child's hand-height on the dry stone, there is a soot-smudge of a lamp-boy's palm, and a snipped wick-end. He went out by the Candle bridge, at dawn, bare-faced and running.".
  Discovery rg_sign_grating "At the cistern steps' grating, the bars are polished at a boy's reach, and a line of crumbs is laid along the lip of it, every day, in a row: someone feeds the pigeons, patiently, and does not come up.".
  Discovery rg_sign_runs "In the oil-cistern the rats' runs on the pillars' ledge all lead to one place: a low crawl on the east side, where something is fed, regularly, by someone who does not mean to be seen.".
  Action rg_read_porch(actor: group, site: place) "Read the Chapel steps and the porch's undersides for what the rain has not washed" {
    Description "A track in this city lasts the length of a shower. A habit lasts as long as the boy.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapel_steps) and not knows(actor, rg_sign_soot) and not rg_blind_porch(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, rg_sign_soot). Assert arcBegun(actor, hand_heron). }
    On failure { Assert rg_blind_porch(actor). Set rg_porch_end(actor) to watch(clock) + 36. }
    Result "The steps themselves tell you nothing: a hundred masked feet have been over them since. You get down on your knees in the wet and look up under the porch's lip, where nobody looks, and there, on the dry stone, at the height of a child's hand, is a smudge of soot the shape of a palm, and under it a snipped wick-end, dropped by someone who could not bear to waste it and could not bear to keep it. The smudge points toward the Candle bridge.".
    Otherwise "A great deal of the Chapel's steps is wet, and the rest is somebody's boots. You see nothing that a clerk would not see, and a Masked Watch domino on the steps looks at you with the courteous contempt reserved for a Bare who has got on his knees to the stonework.".
  }
  Relation rg_blind_porch(group). Measure rg_porch_end(group).
  Rule rg_porch_clears when rg_blind_porch(party) and watch(clock) >= rg_porch_end(party) { Retract rg_blind_porch(party). }
  Action rg_read_grating(actor: group, site: place) "Read the grating at the cistern steps, where the pigeons gather" {
    Description "A pigeon is a good witness: it goes where it is fed, and tells nobody.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, cistern_steps) and not knows(actor, rg_sign_grating) and not rg_blind_grating(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, rg_sign_grating). Assert arcBegun(actor, hand_heron). }
    On failure { Assert rg_blind_grating(actor). Set rg_grating_end(actor) to watch(clock) + 36. }
    Result "You wait, which is the whole of the craft, and the Drip's pigeons come back: a dozen, then forty, in the rain, to the iron grating by the head of the steps, and sit along the bars with their feathers up. The lip of the grating has a row of crumbs laid along it, neat, equal, nine to the foot, such as no pigeon and no grown person would lay, and the bars at the height of a boy's reach have been rubbed bright. Somebody comes here every day with his pockets full and does not come up. The row points, as a finger would, at the head of the cistern steps.".
    Otherwise "You stand in the rain among forty pigeons, who are not interested in you, and go away.".
  }
  Relation rg_blind_grating(group). Measure rg_grating_end(group).
  Rule rg_grating_clears when rg_blind_grating(party) and watch(clock) >= rg_grating_end(party) { Retract rg_blind_grating(party). }
  Action rg_read_runs(actor: group, site: place) "Read the rats' runs on the oil-cistern's ledge" {
    Description "Rats go where the food is, and the food is where the boys are.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, cistern_hall) and not knows(actor, rg_sign_runs) and not benighted(actor) and not rg_blind_runs(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, rg_sign_runs). Assert arcBegun(actor, hand_heron). }
    On failure { Assert rg_blind_runs(actor). Set rg_runs_end(actor) to watch(clock) + 36. }
    Result "The ledge along the pillars is greasy, and the rats have worn it into a lane: a lane with an end, which is not the Drain, nor the gate, but the low crawl on the east side. You stand at the mouth of it and watch for a time. A rat comes out with a crumb, and another, and a long way in there, through the brick, quite distinctly, someone coughs, and is hushed.".
    Otherwise "You find a great many rats, and no sense in their coming and going.".
  }
  Relation rg_blind_runs(group). Measure rg_runs_end(group).
  Rule rg_runs_clears when rg_blind_runs(party) and watch(clock) >= rg_runs_end(party) { Retract rg_blind_runs(party). }
  // The last reading is a method and not a skill: the company that has read all three walks into the den downwind and
  // still, and the sacking opens. There is no check, and so no way to frighten them.
  Action rg_come_in_still(actor: group, site: place) "Go in to the den downwind and still, as the three signs say" {
    Description "You have read the Chapel's porch, the grating and the rats' lane: you know what he does with his hands, and how long he waits. It is the only approach that cannot go wrong.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lamp_boys_den) and knows(actor, rg_sign_soot) and knows(actor, rg_sign_grating) and knows(actor, rg_sign_runs) and not knows(actor, ci_boys_found).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ci_boys_found). Increase ci_trust(pip) by 1. }
    Result "You come in as the signs say: with the draught in your face, your hands where they can be seen, your pace the pace of the dripping. You do not look at the sacking. You sit down with your back to a pillar, at the distance a child's courtesy requires, and take out nothing at all. After a while the sacking moves a hand's breadth, and a face looks out at you that has been looking, you think, for some time. 'You read us,' says the smallest, not as an accusation. 'You read it off the *wall*.'".
  }

  // ── The question: what is a ranger for? ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Mistress Withy does not ask it of anyone else. She asks it of a ranger because her husband was one, of a kind, and
  // had two answers, and never settled which was his.
  Relation rg_creed_wild(group). Relation rg_creed_tended(group). Relation rg_creed_asked(group).
  Topic rg_reed_asks with withy "Show Mistress Withy what you are: a ranger of the wild" when rg_ranger(actor) and hr_reed_trust(actor) and not rg_creed_asked(actor) and not (publicHours() and masked(actor)) once {
    Says "She looks at your hands, and your boots, and where your eyes go when a bird calls. 'A ranger,' says Mistress Withy. 'They told me you were all dead.' She sits on her bucket. 'My husband said he was one, when he was a ratcatcher, because the Drip hadn't a word for it. He had two answers to what it's *for*, and he never made up his mind. Keep it out, he'd say: the wild's the wild, and the city's the city, and the herons are better for not knowing us. Or tend it: they've lived beside us seven hundred years on our mud and our eels, and what's wild here has always been half ours.' Her voice is perfectly flat. 'Which are you?'".
    On discuss { Assert rg_creed_asked(actor). }
  }
  Topic rg_creed_keep with withy "Say that the wild must be kept out of the city: it is a thing apart" answering rg_reed_asks when true {
    Says "'That's his,' says Withy, quietly. 'He was a hard man with a rat and a soft one with a bird, and it is the soft thing in him he said that for.' She looks at the pool. 'Then you'll hold the Writ. I'll have no one tell me otherwise.'".
    On discuss { Assert rg_creed_wild(actor). }
  }
  Topic rg_creed_tend with withy "Say that the wild is mended best by the people who live beside it" answering rg_reed_asks when true {
    Says "'That's mine,' says Withy, 'and I've never said it aloud, not to him, not to the Board, not to myself. Seven hundred years of eels and mud and nets.' She is staring. 'Then I'll hear what the Exchange man's got to say, if it comes to it. I'll *listen*.'".
    On discuss { Assert rg_creed_tended(actor). }
  }
  // What the company did in the reeds, whatever it said: kept, or tended. The closing account reads both.
  Relation rg_wild(group). Relation rg_tended(group). Relation rg_lone(group).
  Rule rg_wild_set when rg_ranger(party) and hr_reeds_kept(party) and not hr_garden_deal(party) and not rg_wild(party) { Assert rg_wild(party). }
  Rule rg_tended_set when rg_ranger(party) and hr_garden_deal(party) and not rg_tended(party) { Assert rg_tended(party). }
  Rule rg_lone_set when rg_ranger(party) and hr_reeds_sunk(party) and not hr_garden_deal(party) and not rg_lone(party) { Assert rg_lone(party). }

  // ── The feather ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // When the old heron has stood, she drops a feather on the pool's rim: a long white scapular, the best thing in the
  // Heronry to carry. It may be taken, which is a theft from a bird that is not a person; or left, which costs the
  // company the charm, and which Mistress Withy notices.
  Kind rg_feather_kind "the old heron's feather" is gear worth 8 weighing 0 granting stealth described "A scapular feather of a white heron, as long as a forearm, quite perfect, with a spine like a bird's own bone. You are better at being still while you carry it, and a good deal more at being nobody.".
  Item rg_feather "the old heron's feather" is rg_feather_kind at heron_pool hidden until rg_feather_seen.
  Discovery rg_feather_seen "When the old heron has stood in the pool, a long white feather lies on the water at the pool's rim.".
  Observe rg_feather_scene at heron_pool when state(heron, hr_standing) and not rg_feather_gone(party) "At the pool's rim, where the old heron has trodden the mud flat, one long white feather lies on the water, quite perfect, turning a little in the rain." teaches rg_feather_seen.
  Relation rg_feather_taken(group). Relation rg_feather_gone(group). Relation rg_feather_given(group).
  Rule rg_feather_taken_rule when carries(party, rg_feather) and not rg_feather_taken(party)
    says "It comes up out of the water into your hand as if it had been waiting to, and for a moment, across the pool, the old heron lifts her head and looks at you with one round yellow eye, and puts it back on her shoulder." { Assert rg_feather_taken(party). Assert rg_feather_gone(party). }
  Topic rg_reed_feather with withy "Ask Mistress Withy about the feather on the water" when knows(actor, rg_feather_seen) and not rg_feather_taken(actor) and not rg_feather_given(actor) and hr_decided(actor) once {
    Says "'You've left it.' It is not a question. 'Eleven years ago a young man took one off the rim, a clerk with a bird-book, and he had it a month, and the old fellow wouldn't stand for him again. He knows who's taken.' She opens the tin on her belt, the one she keeps the Writ's copy in, and takes out, wrapped in a bit of oiled paper, a long white feather gone cream at the barb. 'Mine,' she says. 'Twenty-two years. He gave it me. I'd like you to have it, if you're the sort that leaves one.'".
    On discuss { Give rg_gift_feather to actor. Assert rg_feather_given(actor). }
  }
  Kind rg_gift_kind "a heron's feather, given" is gear worth 12 weighing 0 granting woodcraft described "A heron's scapular, cream at the barb with twenty-two years in Mistress Withy's tin, wrapped in oiled paper. It was given. It makes you better at reading what is not there to be read, and at waiting for it.".
  Item rg_gift_feather "a heron's feather, given" is rg_gift_kind at offstage.
  Topic rg_reed_taken with withy "Tell Mistress Withy about the feather you took" when rg_feather_taken(actor) and hr_decided(actor) once {
    Says "Mistress Withy does not look at the feather. 'He'll not come to you, now,' she says, without anger. 'Not for a long while. He'd have given it you, if you'd waited. That's all.' She turns the bucket over. 'It's not a thing I'd say to a person twice.'".
  }

  // ── Withy's lesson, and the vigil ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A heron's stillness is the one technique in the Heronry, and Withy has been watching it for thirty years. It is the
  // ranger's own at the third level; to a ranger who has not come to it, it is the old heron's gift.
  Rule rg_reed_teaches when state(heron, hr_standing) and rg_ranger(party) and not rg_taught(party) { Assert teaches(withy, hide). Assert rg_taught(party). }
  Relation rg_taught(group). Relation rg_vigil_kept(group).
  Action rg_vigil(actor: group, reader: member, site: place) "Have {reader} keep the heron's vigil at the pool until the Ninth Bell" {
    Description "Six hours, standing, in the reeds' edge, without moving or speaking, as a heron does. It is the nearest thing in Ombra to prayer that is not asked for a name.".
    Requires at(actor, site) and memberOf(reader, actor) and awake(reader) and at(actor, heron_pool) and state(heron, hr_standing) and not hr_decided(actor) and rg_ranger(actor) and not rg_vigil_kept(actor) and hour(clock) >= 14 and hour(clock) < 20.
    Time 36. Resolve endow(reader, wisdom, by_one).
    On success { Assert rg_vigil_kept(actor). Assert arcBegun(actor, hand_heron). }
    Result "You stand where the reeds meet the water, on the one dry hummock, and do nothing, and then do nothing better, as the afternoon goes by on the pool like a slow barge. The heron does not look at you. At some point {reader} stops waiting for something to happen, and is, simply, in the light on the water, and a good deal later is surprised to find that the Ninth Bell has gone, and that Mistress Withy, on the hummock behind, has not said a word in six hours, and is nodding.".
  }

  // ── Gorrell's bird ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind rg_pigeon_kind "Tally, a homing pigeon of the Post" is gear worth 4 weighing 0 described "A grey Post pigeon, ringed on the left leg, with an eye like a drop of tea. Gorrell says she has never in her life flown to the wrong roof, which is the same as saying she has never been told one.".
  Item rg_pigeon "Tally, a homing pigeon of the Post" is rg_pigeon_kind at offstage.
  Relation rg_pigeon_given(group). Relation rg_pigeon_sent(group).
  Topic rg_garrity_bird with garrity "Take the grey pigeon Old Gorrell offers you, for the road" when hr_birds_fly(actor) and rg_ranger(actor) and not rg_pigeon_given(actor) and (privateHours() or masked(actor)) once {
    Says "'You've the look,' says Gorrell, to the point six inches to your right. 'Of a person who's got a dozen places to be and nobody to tell them.' He reaches into the nearest box, with the unerring delicacy of long habit, and comes out with a grey bird, which sits on his wrist as one who knows her duty. 'Tally. Never wrong. You put a word on her leg, you let her go, and she'll be at the Post before you've shut the door.' He puts her in your hands. 'Don't send her anywhere near a falcon. Not that there's one. Eh? What?'".
    On discuss { Give rg_pigeon to actor. Assert rg_pigeon_given(actor). }
  }
  Action rg_send_bird(actor: group, site: place) "Send Tally to the Gate with a word for the Watch" {
    Description "She goes to the Post, and a Post clerk takes the word to Sergeant Vail's desk, who has been wondering, for two days, whether a Bare is still about the Warrant's business.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and carries(actor, rg_pigeon) and not rg_pigeon_sent(actor) and heat(actor) >= 1 and not (publicHours() and not masked(actor)).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Spend rg_pigeon from actor. Assert rg_pigeon_sent(actor). Decrease heat(actor) by 1 or to nothing. }
    Result "You write on a scrap of the pigeon's own wrapping, in as few words as will say a Bare is still working: *Warrant in hand. Business ongoing. Nothing lifted since.* She goes up off your wrist in the rain, a grey fleck, straight as a plumb-line, over the Drip's roofs toward the Post, and is gone before you have finished watching. By the time you reach the Gate, the Watch is of the view that you are, on the whole, a considerate Stranger.".
  }

  // ── The finale: two ways at the Drawing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // handReady when either piece is in hand: the old heron, standing, and not given offence; or the child, forgiving and
  // trusting. They are separate acts, at the Urn Hall on the ninth night, and a company may do either or both.
  Relation rg_heron_carried(group). Relation rg_heron_flown(group). Relation rg_pip_asked(group). Relation rg_pip_spoke(group).
  Rule rg_ready_heron when state(heron, hr_standing) and not rg_feather_taken(party) and not handReady(party, hand_heron)
    says "The old bird stands in the pool like a sheet drawn off a face, and it comes to you, quite quietly, what a crowd would take her for." { Assert handReady(party, hand_heron). }
  Rule rg_ready_pip when ci_asked(party) and ci_candle(party) and ci_told_warden(party) and ci_trust(pip) >= 3 and not handReady(party, hand_heron)
    says "It comes to you that what a nine-year-old has told you, in the dark of the den, is a sentence that could be said in a hall, aloud, to everyone, by him, if he were asked." { Assert handReady(party, hand_heron). }
  Action rg_carry_heron(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the old heron to come, in Withy's basket, to the city, on the ninth day" {
    Description "She will not be hurried; she will sit in a basket on your knee, with her eye on the Drip, and she will be a long way from her water for a night.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heron_pool) and at(heron, site) and state(heron, hr_standing) and not rg_feather_taken(actor) and not rg_heron_carried(actor) and drawingDay() and hr_decided(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert rg_heron_carried(actor). Assert following(heron, actor). }
    Result "Mistress Withy brings the basket, a long one, of plaited reed, with a lid like a hat, and puts it in the shallows. The old heron looks at it, and at you, and at the reeds. Then she steps over its rim, with a dignity such as is not often spared a basket, and folds in, a long white fold of neck and leg, with her eye turned up at you through the weave. 'Bring her back,' says Withy. 'At the Ninth Bell on the tenth, if the book's still open, and the day after if it isn't.'".
  }
  Action rg_release_heron(actor: group, site: place) "Loose the old heron from her basket in the Urn Hall's light-well" {
    Description "A shaft of grey light comes down the Hall's well from the Chapel's roof. A white bird going up it, in the lamplight, in front of the whole city, will be taken for something.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and rg_heron_carried(actor) and following(heron, actor) and not rg_heron_flown(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert rg_heron_flown(actor). Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_heron). Assert arcDone(actor, hand_heron). Retract following(heron, actor). Set handWay(hand_heron) to 1. }
    Result "You take the lid off the basket in the light of the Hall's well, in front of the nineteen Offices and the whole of the Ninth Bell's crowd, and the old heron stands up. She looks at them. She looks, for rather a long time, at the Urn. Then she opens her wings, which are a great deal larger than anyone had been told, and goes up the shaft, slowly, white as a sheet drawn off a face, into the dark of the Chapel roof, and out. Nobody speaks. Somebody, in the gallery, says *her*; and it goes round the Hall like a breath, as a name goes round a room that is not allowed to say it, and nobody is Named.".
  }
  Action rg_ask_pip_to_speak(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Pip if he will say, in the Hall, what he saw: the Warden said her name" {
    Speaker pip.
    Description "He is nine. It is the Concord's whole gallery, and the whole crowd, and the Warden of Locks in his green coat. He is not to say the name. He is to say that it was said.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pip, site) and ci_asked(actor) and ci_candle(actor) and ci_told_warden(actor) and ci_trust(pip) >= 3 and not rg_pip_asked(actor) and not following(pip, actor) and not ci_pip_taken(actor).
    Grave "A child who says a thing in public in Ombra is a person afterwards, whether he wishes it or not.".
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert rg_pip_asked(actor). Assert following(pip, actor). }
    Result "He thinks about it, with the whole of his face, for a long time. Nell does not say a word, which costs her. 'Will they say my name?' he asks. 'No.' 'Will I be Faced?' 'Not by me.' A pause. 'And I'll not have to say hers.' 'No.' Pip looks at his candle. 'Then I'll say it,' he says. 'That the man with the keys said it. That it was said, and I heard. I'll say it to everyone.' His hand finds your coat. 'You'll stand by me?'".
  }
  Action rg_pip_speaks(actor: group, site: place) "Stand beside Pip while he says what he heard" {
    Speaker pip.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and following(pip, actor) and rg_pip_asked(actor) and not rg_pip_spoke(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert rg_pip_spoke(actor). Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_heron). Assert arcDone(actor, hand_heron). Retract following(pip, actor). Assert at(pip, urn_hall). Set handWay(hand_heron) to 2. }
    Result "There is a stir in the Hall as the boy steps up, because nobody has told it that anyone would. He is very small in the lamp-light, in his cut-down Owl, with a whole candle in his fist. He does not take the mask off. He says, to the gallery, in a clear high voice that does not shake until the end, that he was under the lamp-table, and he saw her bare, and it was not a terrible thing; and that a man in a green coat with the Warden's keys came, that night, and said her name aloud, twice, in the Chapel, and that is all. He sits down on the step with the candle. Behind you the Warden's seat has gone very quiet. The Hall, which cannot say what it has heard, has heard it.".
  }

  // ── Milestones ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Milestone rg_m_signs "read a lamp-boy's habits off a city the rain had washed" worth 25 when knows(party, rg_sign_soot) and knows(party, rg_sign_grating) and knows(party, rg_sign_runs).
  Milestone rg_m_creed "said aloud what a ranger is for, to a woman who needed to hear it" worth 25 when rg_creed_asked(party) and (rg_creed_wild(party) or rg_creed_tended(party)).
  Milestone rg_m_vigil "kept the heron's vigil until the Ninth Bell" worth 25 when rg_vigil_kept(party).
  Milestone rg_m_given "left the feather on the water, and was given one" worth 25 when rg_feather_given(party).
  Milestone rg_m_flown "loosed a heron in the light-well over the Urn Hall" worth 100 when rg_heron_flown(party).
  Milestone rg_m_spoke "stood by a nine-year-old while he said what he had heard" worth 100 when rg_pip_spoke(party).

  // ── What became of them ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule rg_fate_flown when newsHour() and rg_heron_flown(party) once says "Of the old heron: she went up through the Chapel roof on the ninth night and was seen at dawn on the Candle bridge, on one leg, looking at the water, like something that had been asked a question and was considering it. The Drip says it was the Registrar. The Post says it was a heron. She is in the pool by the Ninth Bell on the tenth, as a matter of fact, standing, to the knee, with her head on her shoulder, and Mistress Withy rings the bell." { }
  Rule rg_fate_spoke when newsHour() and rg_pip_spoke(party) once says "Of Pip Treen, at the Drawing: he said it, in the Urn Hall, aloud, at nine years old, before the nineteen Offices, and then sat on a step with a candle. He is not Named. He is not Faced. The Concord has not decided what to do with a child who has said a thing in public, and so, for the present, has done nothing at all, which in Ombra is the greatest kindness it has." { }
  Rule rg_fate_wild when newsHour() and rg_wild(party) once says "Of the ranger of the Heronry: in the reeds the company told Mistress Withy to hold the Writ, and the Writ held, and the reeds are the herons' to this day; and the six hundred of the Drip are somewhere else, which is a thing a keeper of the wild must learn to bear, and finds, in the evenings, that she cannot." { }
  Rule rg_fate_tended when newsHour() and rg_tended(party) once says "Of the ranger of the Heronry: in the reeds the company told Mistress Withy that the wild is mended best by those who live beside it, and the west reeds are a street, and the east reeds a pond, and the old heron stands in it, in sight of a good many windows. It is not the wild. It is, in the Drip's view, a good deal better than that." { }
  Rule rg_fate_lone when newsHour() and rg_lone(party) once says "Of the ranger of the Heronry: the reeds went to the Exchange, in the end, to the stake and the chain, and the ranger who had read a whole city off its walls could not read the one thing that would have kept them. Mistress Withy has not asked her what she is for again." { }
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/registry.k:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The Registry and the Urn Hall ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Off the nave, behind a door the Doorward keeps, the Registry: a lectern where the Book of Faces stood, shelves of
  // ninety years of Books before it, and a stair down to the Urn Hall, where the Drawing is held. Five ways in. The
  // Warrant's (the Hearing opens it by right, hearing.kyr); the Face (a mask the Doorward must take for the Office it is);
  // the Cisterns (the cellar under the Urn Hall, cisterns.kyr); the Stair (the Contessa's key, once her private stair is
  // lent); and the lock itself, which a thief can pick, and which rings a bell in the vestry when it is.
  Observe nave_door_note at nave when not registryOpened(party) "On the east wall of the nave a plain oak door has a bare oval carved in it at the height of a face, and under the oval a lock of the old square kind. A lay-brother's stool stands beside it, empty at the moment, with a rush mat and a flask.".
  Observe registry_scene at registry when true "A high narrow room all of paper. Ninety years of Books of Faces stand on the walls in white vellum, spine after spine, each with a year in black on it and no name anywhere. In the middle, on a lectern with a brass rail, there is a clean oblong in the dust where the current Book lay, with the sheen of a hand on the wood beside it. At the far end a stair goes down.".
  Observe urn_hall_scene at urn_hall when not drawingNight() "A long vault with a barrel ceiling, under the Chapel, lit by oil in niches. Nine rows of benches face a dais, and on the dais, alone, on a stone plinth the height of a man's waist, stands the Urn: a bronze jar as wide as a cart-wheel, green at the seams, sealed with a bare oval of white wax. Everything in the hall is arranged to look at it. The benches are empty. The Urn is not.".
  Observe urn_hall_drawing at urn_hall when drawingNight() "The Urn Hall is full. A thousand people sit on nine rows of benches in their faces, in the oil-light, and not one of them is speaking. Somewhere behind you the doors have been left open on the rain. On the dais the Urn waits on its plinth with the white wax on its seams, and in front of it is an empty chair.".

  // ── The door ──
  Person doorward "Brother Alder" at nave {
    Role "the Chapel's Doorward, an old lay-brother in a grey cowl with a ring of keys".
    Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
    Greets "A very old man in a grey cowl is sitting on the stool by the oak door with his hands on his knees, doing nothing, in the way of a person who has been doing it for sixty years. 'The Registry is shut,' he says, before you have said anything. 'The Registrar's dead. It is shut till there is a Registrar. If you are an Office, I will know you by the Fit; if you are not, I will know you by the rest of you.'".
    Greets again "'Shut,' says Brother Alder, and moves a hand on his knee to say it is not personal.".
  }
  Relation officeFace(face).
  Initially Assert officeFace(face_key). Initially Assert officeFace(face_pound). Initially Assert officeFace(face_serene).
  Relation registryOpened(group). Relation registryAlarmed(group). Relation registryKeyed(group). Relation registryByFace(group).
  Thing registry_lock "the Registry's lock" on registry_door {
    State barred blocking "The Registry door is locked, and the Doorward sits beside it.".
    State open "The Registry door stands open on a room of white spines.".
    Change pick "Pick the Registry's lock" from barred to open needing lockwork.
    Change unlock "Unlock the Registry door with the Contessa's old key" from barred to open needing registry_key_kind.
  }
  Kind registry_key_kind "the Contessa's old key" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "A black iron key as long as a hand, with a bare oval for a bow. The Contessa Tarn's family has kept it for three hundred years against the day it was wanted, and it is cold, as old keys are.".
  Item registry_key "the Contessa's old key" is registry_key_kind at offstage.
  Rule registry_by_right when registryOpened(party) and state(registry_lock, barred) { Assert state(registry_lock, open). }
  // At the Ninth Bell of the ninth night the Chapel opens the Registry and the Urn Hall to the city, as it always has: the
  // ways above are for those who must be there before.
  Rule registry_opens_for_drawing when drawingNight() and state(registry_lock, barred) { Assert state(registry_lock, open). }
  // A lock picked is heard in the vestry; the Warrant is not made for it.
  Rule lock_alarm when state(registry_lock, open) and not drawingNight() and not registryOpened(party) and not registryByFace(party) and not registryKeyed(party) and not registryAlarmed(party) says "Somewhere on the other side of the nave a small bell begins, once, and a lay-brother's voice says, mildly, 'Brother Alder?'" {
    Assert registryAlarmed(party). Increase heat(party) by 2. }

  // The Face: an Office is shown to the Doorward, who judges the Fit.
  Action show_fitted_face(actor: group, mask: face, site: place) "Show Brother Alder {mask}, which was cut for you" {
    Speaker doorward.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(doorward, site) and officeFace(mask) and wears(actor, mask) and fitted(actor, mask) and publicHours() and not registryByFace(actor) and state(registry_lock, barred).
    Time 5.
    On success { Assert registryByFace(actor). Assert state(registry_lock, open). }
    Result "The old man looks at the mask for a long time, as at a coat he has brushed for sixty years. 'It sits,' he says at last. 'It is a very good Fit.' He gets up, which takes some time, and takes a key from the ring, and says to the door, 'The Office goes in. The Office will be quick.' Two lay-brothers by the font find the roof extremely interesting.".
  }
  Action show_unfitted_face(actor: group, mask: face, site: place) "Show Brother Alder {mask}, and hope the Fit will be forgiven" {
    Speaker doorward.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(doorward, site) and officeFace(mask) and wears(actor, mask) and not fitted(actor, mask) and publicHours() and not registryByFace(actor) and state(registry_lock, barred).
    Time 5.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert registryByFace(actor). Assert state(registry_lock, open). }
    On failure { Increase heat(actor) by 1. }
    Result "He turns it a quarter-turn on your face with two old fingers, and you hold still, and he turns it back. 'It does not sit,' he says. 'But it has been a very wet nine days and everybody's face is a little wrong.' He gets up and takes the key.".
    Otherwise "'That is not a Fit,' says Brother Alder, with no unkindness. 'That is a mask on a person.' He sits down. A little later a hound-domino passes the end of the nave, and does not look, and you understand you have been entered in a book.".
  }
  // The Stair's way: the Contessa lends the key when her private stair is yours (hill.kyr's price).
  Action tarn_gives_key(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Contessa for the old key to the Registry" {
    Speaker tarn.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(tarn, site) and privateStairOpen(actor) and not registryKeyed(actor).
    Time 5.
    On success { Assert registryKeyed(actor). Give registry_key to actor. }
    Result "'It has not been used since my great-grandmother's time,' says the Contessa, and takes it off a hook in the wall behind a very old shawl. 'She said it would be wanted by someone who could not be trusted with it.' She hands it over by the bow, not the shaft. 'I find I am not at all sure which of us she meant.'".
  }

  // ── The lectern and the Book ──
  Discovery book_columns "In the Book of Faces, in the Registrar's hand for the last thirty-one years, beside every name drawn there is a second column headed WALKED, with a street, a date and one word: MENDS, MENDS, MENDS. The Offices were not drawn; they were chosen, and she walked every street to choose them.".
  Action read_book(actor: group, site: place) "Read the Book of Faces at the lectern" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, registry) or at(actor, candid_room)) and carries(actor, book_of_faces) and not bookRead(actor).
    Time 60.
    On success { Assert bookRead(actor). Assert knows(actor, book_columns). Assert knows(actor, urn_hollow). Assert knows(actor, marrick_was_treasurer). }
    Result "Ninety years of one hand after another, and then, the last thirty-one, hers. Beside each name a street, a date and the word MENDS. Nineteen Offices a year, and every one of them somebody a street had been glad of. You turn back and back, and in the Year of the Cullet Sluice, in a hand that is nineteen years old and cannot spell Treasurer, a lamp-trimmer's daughter wrote her own name in the column headed DRAWN. The next year there is no column of that name at all.".
  }
  // The Urn: shaken, it does not rattle.
  Thing urn "the Urn" at urn_hall {
    State sealed "The Urn stands on its plinth, sealed with a bare oval of white wax.".
    State filled "The Urn stands on its plinth, its wax broken, filled to the throat with clay tesserae.".
    Change fill "Fill the Urn with tesserae from the Registry's shelves" from sealed to filled at urn_hall.
  }
  Action shake_urn(actor: group, site: place) "Take the Urn by its handles and shake it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and state(urn, sealed) and not knows(actor, lie_urn).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, lie_urn). Increase heat(actor) by 1. }
    Result "It does not rattle. It does not shift. It is a bronze jar the weight of a bronze jar, and a very old stillness comes up through your wrists. Forty thousand tesserae, the Concord says: one for every citizen. There is not one of them in it.".
  }
  Action fill_urn(actor: group, site: place) "Carry tesserae from the Registry's shelves to the Urn, and fill it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and knows(actor, urn_hollow) and state(urn, sealed) and drawingDay().
    Time 120.
    On success { Assert state(urn, filled). Assert urnFilled(actor). }
    Result "Forty thousand clay tesserae are kept in sacks in the Registry's lowest shelf, each pressed with a name, and have been since the Concord, against the day they were wanted. It takes two hours and a barrow. When it is done the Urn is as heavy as it has always pretended to be.".
  }
  Relation urnFilled(group).
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/revision.k:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The Pound's first page (the broad pass, doc/imbar/adventures/book-of-faces.md) ─────────────────────────────────
  // The Account, in Ombra: the count is the Standard Pound; its keeper is the Collegium of Measures (which WEIGHS: assay and
  // standards) and, under it, an office of eleven Assayers and a twelfth hook left empty; its first page is missing (the
  // Collegium has always said the Pound is a measure, and the Standard Room's own card says it is a promise); the price of
  // reading it is that a standard which was kept becomes a standard which is owed. Prefix rv_. Reads counting.kyr, mage.kyr.
  //
  // Added here: the Bursar of the Collegium; a stair behind the Fitting-frame to the assay cellar, guarded by a Counterpoise
  // (a fight is possible and costly; the chit, a short loaf and Thole's recitative are the ways round); a case with a second
  // lock which only a thief of the company sees; a company quarrel with a consequence; the companions' voices across the
  // city; three small pieces of the Row's own history; links outward by item and by world event.

  // ── Places ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place rv_cellars "the Collegium's cellars" is level within collegium.
  Place rv_landing "the foot of the assay stair" is room within rv_cellars at 0, 0 underground.
  Place rv_assay "the assay cellar" is room within rv_cellars at 1, 0 underground.
  Passage rv_stair_way "the assay stair behind the Frame" is steps between collegium_study and rv_landing taking 3 minutes.
  Passage rv_pound_door "the Pound's door" is door between rv_landing and rv_assay.

  Observe rv_hooks_scene at collegium_hall when true "By the door, over the pegs of wooden hands, a rail of twelve brass hooks, each with a brass tag. Eleven tags are engraved with a name and a number, and the hooks under them are polished by thumbs; the twelfth hook is bare, has no tag, and is the only thing in the hall that somebody has oiled. The hall smells of iron-gall ink, wet wool and the tallow of a hundred slates being wiped. Every student, going out, presses a wet thumb to the slate by the door. A Moth of about nine, asked, says it is so the slate will know you again. It is wiped every hour.".
  Observe rv_row_plates at row_street when publicHours() "Passing the brass plates on the Row, almost everyone touches the lowest corner of one, a flick of two fingers, without looking, as a sailor touches a rail. The corners have worn bright and thin.".
  Observe rv_landing_scene at rv_landing when true "A square brick landing under the workroom, dry, with iron-gall in the air and a lamp-niche with a stub of tallow in it. Against the far wall stands the Counterpoise, a bronze figure twice the height of a man whose arms end in two flat pans, one empty, the other holding a single grey pebble. The pans are exactly level. A door of black oak is let into the wall behind it.".
  Observe rv_assay_scene at rv_assay when publicHours() "A vault of dressed stone with a drain in the middle of the floor and a table of black stone beside it, older than the vault. On the table, in a glass-fronted case, stands a drum of bronze the colour of strong tea: not the Standard Pound, the Pound's mould. Above the door, cut into the lintel, a row of names and numbers, the last ISAURA HEXHAM, ASSAYER.".
  Observe rv_assay_night at rv_assay when privateHours() "A tallow lamp in a wall-bracket, trimmed this quarter by somebody. The bronze in the case gives back the light in a slow brown pulse.".

  // ── The Bursar ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Perpetua Gaunt keeps the Collegium's purse, its rail of hooks and its door. WANTS the quarter's assay of the Pound to
  // come out even. FEARS that it will not, by a grain, and that she is the only one who has weighed it honestly. Her LIE
  // is that a measure has no opinion. Pressed, she SURPRISES: she is the twelfth, the only Assayer alive, and has been
  // keeping a hook oiled for a successor she is not allowed to appoint.
  Person rv_bursar "Bursar Perpetua Gaunt" at collegium_hall {
    Role "the Bursar of the Collegium of Measures". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "A woman in an ink-coloured gown sits at a counting-table inside the door with a ledger open, a pen in one hand and the other hand flat on the page as if the page might leave. She does not look up until the column has been added twice. 'Fees are by the Collegium's schedule,' she says to the ledger. 'Visitors are owed courtesy. Which are you?'".
    Greets again "'Bare,' says the Bursar, and moves her hand a finger's breadth from the column. It is as close as she comes to a welcome.".
  }
  Relation rv_met(group). Relation rv_twelfth_asked(group). Relation rv_chit_given(group). Relation rv_stair_told(group).
  Discovery rv_owed_kept "The Collegium of Measures says everything is OWED: a weight is owed to the buyer, a pound to the city. The old writs, the Bursar admits, say KEPT, and the Collegium is no longer sure that there is a difference.".
  Discovery rv_hook_twelfth "The Collegium of Measures has twelve Assayers' hooks by its door, eleven tagged and polished and one oiled and bare. The Bursar does not say who the twelfth is.".
  Discovery rv_stair_known "There is an assay stair behind the Fitting-frame, down to a vault under the Collegium that is not on any plan; a Counterpoise stands at its foot.".
  Topic rv_b_work with rv_bursar "Ask what the Collegium of Measures does" when true once {
    Says "'We weigh,' says the Bursar. 'Not for money: for the city. A cheese, a coin, a sluice-gate, a claim. The Hall of Weights keeps the Pound, and we keep the Hall.' She says it flat, as learnt by heart, and then, because you are still standing there: 'Veyra teaches. Corran collects. We say what a thing comes to. The mother-house is at Sennet; I have never seen it.' She turns a page. 'Two hundred and eleven years ago we sued the Hall over a cheese. Neither of us has been sure who won. We still send the cheese a card at midwinter.'".
    On discuss { Assert rv_met(actor). }
  }
  Topic rv_b_owed with rv_bursar "Ask why she says everything is owed" when rv_met(actor) and not rv_mould_broken(actor) once {
    Says "'Because it is,' says the Bursar. 'A weight is owed. A fee is owed. A pound is owed to the city by whoever holds it.' She stops. 'There is a writ in the cellar-press, an old one, from the Marches, that says KEPT. Keeping, not owing. The Collegium has never been able to decide whether that is a difference or only a way of speaking.' She puts the pen down. 'A measure has no opinion, Bare. That is its whole use. I would be obliged if you did not put one in it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, rv_owed_kept). }
  }
  Topic rv_b_letter with rv_bursar "Show her the letter of the Collegium of Lesser Instruments" when holding(actor, collegium_letter) and rv_met(actor) and not rv_chit_given(actor) once {
    Says "She reads it with her lips moving, and then reads it again, and her face does three things in a row, the last of which is delight. 'Collects,' she says. 'They collect. They have a letter-head with a spanner on it.' A sound escapes her, a short dry bark that might be a laugh, and she covers her mouth with the ledger. 'Corran sends us a letter every ten years to ask whether we will lend them a standard. We write back to say a standard is not lent but kept, and they write again.' She wipes an eye with the back of a wrist. 'Here. A chit of assay, signed. It opens the stair for any Collegium friend, and you are plainly one of Corran's, which is the next best.'".
    On discuss { Give rv_chit to actor. Assert rv_chit_given(actor). }
  }
  Kind rv_chit_kind "the Bursar's chit of assay" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "A slip of grey card with the Collegium's scale stamped in blue and a signature in a small, hard hand: BEARER MAY GO DOWN. It is not a key. It is a statement that somebody who has the right to refuse has chosen not to.".
  Item rv_chit "the Bursar's chit of assay" is rv_chit_kind at offstage.
  Action rv_b_fee(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the Bursar the three-coin fee for a chit of assay" {
    Speaker rv_bursar.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(rv_bursar, site) and rv_met(actor) and not rv_chit_given(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3.
    Time 5.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Give rv_chit to actor. Assert rv_chit_given(actor). }
    Result "She counts the coin on the table with the tip of her pen, then writes the chit with her other hand, never looking at either. 'Three, by the schedule,' she says. 'Not a favour, and not owed. A fee.' She blows on the ink. 'The Counterpoise has been given no instructions in my time except to keep the cellar level. It will read this as an instruction. I would be careful what you ask it to weigh.'".
  }
  Topic rv_b_twelfth with rv_bursar "Ask about the eleven hooks and the twelfth, bare and oiled" when rv_met(actor) and not rv_twelfth_asked(actor) and not rv_cp_broken(actor) and not rv_mould_broken(actor) once {
    Says "Her hand comes off the page. For the first time she looks at you and not at the column, and the look is that of a woman who has been waiting for someone to ask and hoped, until this moment, that no one would. 'Eleven Assayers of the Pound, since the Pound was fixed,' she says. 'Each appointed by the one before, each at the end of a quarter, in the cellar, with no other present. The eleventh was Isaura Hexham, who was my teacher.' She lays the pen straight. 'A twelfth is appointed by the eleventh. I was. I am the only one living who has weighed it, and it comes out light by a grain, and I am forbidden by the form of my office to say so to anyone I have not appointed.' She breathes out. 'There.'".
    On discuss { Assert rv_twelfth_asked(actor). Assert knows(actor, rv_hook_twelfth). }
  }

  // ── The stair and the Counterpoise: a danger with three ways round ───────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Thole knows the stair is there, and has not gone down it in thirty years. The Counterpoise is a Weight of the old
  // Collegium: it stands at the Pound's door and keeps the cellar level. It does not hate; it is exact. A fight is
  // possible, and costly: it is bronze, and it is not hurried. Without a fight the way is by the Bursar's chit (an
  // instruction it reads), by a short loaf of the Drip (it weighs it, and is satisfied), or by the Master's recitative
  // (a witness it still obeys). Of level 4 since a species grows by its level (main's QTC-21): of 6, it killed a company
  // of four before the second blow; of 4, the warrior stands alone at the end of it.
  Species rv_counterpoise_kind "a Counterpoise" like bronze_construct temperament territorial described "A bronze figure twice the height of a man, whose arms end in two flat pans and whose face is a pointer on a scale that has not moved in living memory. It does not strike so much as set down.".
  Person rv_counterpoise "the Counterpoise" at rv_landing {
    Role "a bronze Weight at the Pound's door". Species rv_counterpoise_kind. Level 4. Temperament territorial. Pronouns it.
    Lair rv_landing.
    State rv_cp_watching blocking "The Counterpoise stands before the black door with its pans held level, and nothing goes by it that has not been weighed.".
    Guards rv_pound_door.
    Warns "The pointer in the Counterpoise's face swings to you and stops. Both pans tilt, very slightly, toward the nearest of you, and the grey pebble in the left one rolls to the edge and does not fall.".
    Comes "The Counterpoise steps off its mark. The sound is that of a very heavy thing being exact.".
  }
  // A fight is a way down, and it is paid for in the Collegium's coin: the Weight broken, the Bursar will not speak of the
  // hook, the chit is waste, and the vigil is not to be sat with a Weight in pieces on the floor.
  Relation rv_cp_broken(group).
  Rule rv_cp_down when (dead(rv_counterpoise) or routed(rv_counterpoise)) and not rv_cp_broken(party) says "The Counterpoise goes down in pieces, pan after pan, and the grey pebble rolls out across the landing and stops against a boot. The note of a cracked bell goes up the stair and does not come down. Somewhere above, in the hall, a woman has stopped writing." {
    Assert rv_cp_broken(party).
  }
  Topic rv_thole_stair with thole "Ask what is down the stair behind the Frame" when mg_audience(actor) and not rv_stair_told(actor) once {
    Says "He does not write a word for a time, and then writes, in a hand that is slightly less steady than usual: THE CELLAR. NOT ENTERED SINCE TOLLEMACHE. 'A Weight,' he says aloud, forgetting the volume, 'a Counterpoise. Set to keep the level. It listens, it is said, for the recitative, though I do not know that I remember the part that it listens for.' He looks at his own hands. 'It would be in the older measures. I should be glad to try.'".
    On discuss { Assert rv_stair_told(actor). Assert knows(actor, rv_stair_known). }
  }
  Action rv_thole_calls(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Dr Thole to call down the stair in the old recitative" {
    Speaker thole.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(thole, site) and at(actor, collegium_study) and rv_stair_told(actor) and not tolerates(rv_counterpoise, actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert tolerates(rv_counterpoise, actor). }
    Result "Thole goes to the head of the stair on your arm and takes a breath that costs him something, and says it down into the dark, not in speech but in the old figures, on a note, each number held a beat longer than the last. Far below, something sets down a very small weight and picks it up again. He listens, as the deaf do, with the whole of his face. 'It has heard,' he says, in a voice quite unlike a lecturer's. 'It says: let them go down, and let them be weighed.' He sits back, a little grey, and he is smiling.".
  }
  Action rv_show_chit(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Counterpoise the Bursar's chit of assay" {
    Description "It will read the card as an instruction. Whether it will like what it reads is another matter.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rv_landing) and at(rv_counterpoise, site) and holding(actor, rv_chit_kind) and not tolerates(rv_counterpoise, actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert tolerates(rv_counterpoise, actor). }
    Result "The pointer in its face turns, and turns back. It takes the card in the left pan, where the pebble was, and the pebble goes into the right one; both pans level, and the card lies there, weightless, a statement. It hands it back. It steps one pace to the left, which is, you gather, the first time it has stepped in a very long while.".
  }
  Action rv_offer_loaf(actor: group, site: place) "Set a penny-loaf of the Drip on the Counterpoise's pan" {
    Description "The Counterpoise weighs. It has had nothing to weigh for a long time but a pebble.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rv_landing) and at(rv_counterpoise, site) and holding(actor, ct_loaf_kind) and not tolerates(rv_counterpoise, actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert tolerates(rv_counterpoise, actor). Spend ct_loaf_kind from actor. }
    Result "It takes the loaf as if it had been waiting for it. The right pan sinks, rocks, settles. It tilts its pointer to the fifteenth ounce, and holds it there, and you have the clear impression, for the first time, that something in the Collegium of Measures is pleased. 'Light,' it says, in a voice like a spoon in a bowl, 'by the exact amount the Hall allows.' It sets the loaf in the niche behind its pans, where a lamp might go, and steps aside as if a great weight had been taken off it. It had.".
  }

  // ── The case with the second lock: a thief's, and a thief's only ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Pound's mould stands in its case with one plain lock, which is open, and nothing in the case but the mould.
  // The leaf is under the pan of the case's floor, behind a lock that has no keyhole on the face and is felt from below.
  Kind rv_page_kind "the first leaf of the Pound's book" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 granting lore described "A single leaf of rag paper, folded in four and dry as bone, in the hand of the first Assayer: a list of seven weights and a drawing of a drum, and under it, in a larger hand: THIS IS NOT A WEIGHT. IT IS KEPT. WHOEVER HOLDS IT KEEPS IT FOR THE REST, AND IS NOT ITS OWNER. The Collegium has never copied it; it would have had to say who was keeping.".
  Item rv_page "the first leaf of the Pound's book" is rv_page_kind at offstage.
  Relation rv_page_taken(group). Relation rv_page_returned(group). Relation rv_page_kept(group). Relation rv_quarrelled(group).
  Discovery rv_first_page "The first page of the Pound's book says: THIS IS NOT A WEIGHT. IT IS KEPT. WHOEVER HOLDS IT KEEPS IT FOR THE REST, AND IS NOT ITS OWNER.".
  Action rv_search_case(actor: group, site: place) "Look the Pound's case over for another way in" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rv_assay) and not rv_page_taken(actor).
    Time 6.
    Result "It is a good plain case with one lock, which is open, and there is nothing in it but the print of a drum. You tap the base, the glass, the table: all honest, all what they seem. If there is a second thing here, you have not the eye for it. You have only the weight of a bar and a good arm, and the table's black flank, where a drawer would be, has no seam you can find and one you could make.".
  }
  Action rv_open_case(actor: group, who: member, site: place) "Have {who} feel under the pan of the Pound's case for a lock without a keyhole" {
    Description "A case with one open lock is an invitation to look no further. A thief does not accept invitations.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rv_assay) and memberOf(who, actor) and awake(who) and hasCalling(who, calling_thief) and not rv_page_taken(actor).
    Time 12.
    On success { Assert rv_page_taken(actor). Assert knows(actor, rv_first_page). Give rv_page to actor. }
    Result "{who} lies on the cold floor with an ear against the plinth, and runs a thumb along the underside of the table until it finds a seam in the black stone that is too clean to be wear. A second lock, felt from below, with a pin no thicker than a hair. It takes the better part of the hour and a piece of wire from {who}'s boot; the tumblers are old and civil, and give, one by one, as if they had been waiting to be asked in order. A drawer the width of a hand slides out. In it is one leaf, folded in four.".
  }
  // The company has two minds, and each is right: the thief took what was never anyone's, and the cleric knows that
  // something kept is not something taken.
  Rule rv_page_quarrel at rv_assay when at(party, rv_assay) and memberOf(?t, party) and hasCalling(?t, calling_thief) and awake(?t) and memberOf(?c, party) and hasCalling(?c, calling_cleric) and awake(?c) and rv_page_taken(party) and not rv_quarrelled(party) and not rv_page_returned(party) and not rv_page_kept(party)
    says "{?t} unfolds the leaf and reads it aloud, once, in the lamp. {?c} has gone very still. 'It says kept,' says {?c}, quietly. 'It says whoever holds it is not its owner.' {?t} turns the leaf over; the back is blank. 'Then whoever holds it keeps it for the rest,' says {?t}. 'And the rest are upstairs, being told it is owed.' Neither is wrong, and both are looking at you." {
    Assert rv_quarrelled(party).
  }
  Action rv_side_thief(actor: group, t: member, c: member, site: place) "Tell {c} that {t} is right, and keep the leaf for the rest" {
    Description "Take the leaf out of the cellar. The Bursar will not forgive it. The city may.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rv_assay) and rv_quarrelled(actor) and not rv_page_kept(actor) and not rv_page_returned(actor) and memberOf(t, actor) and hasCalling(t, calling_thief) and memberOf(c, actor) and hasCalling(c, calling_cleric).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert rv_page_kept(actor). }
    Result "{c} looks at the lintel a long time, and then helps {t} close the drawer so that it will not be seen to have been opened. 'I will not say a word against it,' {c} says, 'but I will remember that I did not.' The leaf goes inside {t}'s coat.".
  }
  Action rv_side_cleric(actor: group, t: member, c: member, site: place) "Tell {t} that {c} is right, and return the leaf to the drawer" {
    Description "Put it back, and tell the Bursar where it is. She will know what to do with the fact of it, which is more than the leaf could.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rv_assay) and rv_quarrelled(actor) and not rv_page_kept(actor) and not rv_page_returned(actor) and memberOf(t, actor) and hasCalling(t, calling_thief) and memberOf(c, actor) and hasCalling(c, calling_cleric) and holding(actor, rv_page_kind).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert rv_page_returned(actor). Spend rv_page_kind from actor. }
    Result "{t} says nothing, folds the leaf along its old creases and lays it back in the drawer, and slides the stone shut until the seam is gone. {c} puts a hand briefly on the glass, as on a font. 'It is kept,' {c} says, to the room. 'That is what it said.' {t}'s mouth is a flat line, and then it is not. 'I knew what it said,' {t} says. 'I wanted someone else to say it.'".
  }
  // The lone company's way (a warrior cannot feel a lock; a warrior can break one). The leaf comes out whole, the Pound's mould
  // does not go back whole, and the Bursar, who keeps the Collegium's door, will not speak of the hooks or the writ again.
  // The thief's way remains the best: no one is told, nothing is cracked, and the company may quarrel over it.
  Relation rv_mould_broken(group).
  Action rv_force_case(actor: group, who: member, site: place) "Have {who} force the Pound's case with a bar" {
    Description "A case, a table and a drawer that must be somewhere. It can be found by a hand that is gentle or by a bar that is not.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rv_assay) and memberOf(who, actor) and awake(who) and hasCalling(who, calling_warrior) and not rv_page_taken(actor).
    Time 8.
    On success { Assert rv_page_taken(actor). Assert rv_mould_broken(actor). Assert knows(actor, rv_first_page). Give rv_page to actor. }
    Result "{who} sets the bar under the lip of the black table and leans. The stone does not break. The mould does: the glass goes, the bronze drum rolls off its plinth and strikes the drain with a flat, a ruined note, and where it struck there is a split down its flank you could lay a finger in. The drawer, which was behind it all the time, comes out in two pieces. In it is one leaf, folded in four. Overhead, faintly, in the hall, a pen stops.".
  }
  Rule rv_bursar_cold at collegium_hall when at(party, collegium_hall) and rv_mould_broken(party) once says "The Bursar does not look up. 'The Counterpoise is level,' she says to the ledger. 'I heard something fall.' She turns a page. 'The Collegium has nothing to tell you, Bare.'" {
  }
  Rule rv_news_forced when newsHour() and rv_mould_broken(party) once says "Of the Collegium of Measures: the Pound's mould is found cracked in its case, and the Bursar has entered it in the quarter's book as OWED, in a hand not quite her own. The twelfth hook has been taken down." { }

  Action rv_tell_bursar(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Bursar where the leaf is, and that it is kept" {
    Speaker rv_bursar.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(rv_bursar, site) and rv_page_returned(actor) and rv_twelfth_asked(actor) and not rv_told_bursar(actor).
    Time 4.
    On success { Assert rv_told_bursar(actor). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 8. }
    Result "She does not ask how you know. She goes white, then red, then sits down on the bench by the door with the ledger in her lap. 'The first leaf,' she says. 'Hexham said it was there. I never could find where.' She is silent for a time. 'I shall enter that the Pound is kept,' she says. 'Not owed. I shall enter it in my own hand and sign it, and let them make what they like of it.' She presses eight coin into your hand from the Collegium's purse, which is not allowed, and does not look at it. 'It is not a fee.'".
  }
  Relation rv_told_bursar(group).

  // ── The Master's mask ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The leaf is the Measure source of the mage's research made plain: a pound fits because it is not a measure, it is a
  // promise held by whoever carries it. Thole WANTS a mask that stays on; FEARS it is the rule, not the Frame; LIES that
  // the Frame is warped. Shown the leaf he does arithmetic in a mask, which the Collegium forbids.
  Topic rv_thole_leaf with thole "Show Dr Thole the first leaf of the Pound's book" when mg_audience(actor) and holding(actor, rv_page_kind) and not rv_thole_masked(actor) once {
    Says "He reads it with his lips, then with his fingers, then holds it up to the lamp and reads the water-mark. When he has done he lays it very gently on the rug and takes one of the hundred and four masks from its hook on the wall, with the carefulness of a man picking up something sleeping, and puts it on. It sits as if the face had been waiting for it. 'KEPT,' he says, in the big voice, 'not measured. A shape that is held is held by someone. The Frame was never in error. We were asking it the wrong question.' He puts his hands on his knees and begins, under the mask, in the dark of the workroom, to do a sum. It is the first arithmetic he has done in a mask in sixty years, and it comes out.".
    On discuss { Assert rv_thole_masked(actor). }
  }
  Relation rv_thole_masked(group).
  Observe rv_thole_masked_scene near thole when rv_thole_masked(party) and at(thole, collegium_study) "The Master of Measures sits in a mask with a pen in his hand and nobody has told him to take it off. The pen goes steadily. The slate on its string says, in new chalk: HELD BY WHOM.".

  // ── A grave scene: the vigil of the Counterpoise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // After a city of masks and a satire of Offices, a still room. The Counterpoise has weighed nothing for two hundred
  // years but a pebble; one night's company changes the pebble.
  Relation rv_vigil(group).
  Action rv_sit_vigil(actor: group, site: place) "Sit the night watch in the assay cellar, as the Assayers did" {
    Description "Each Assayer sat here on the last night of a quarter.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rv_assay) and privateHours() and tolerates(rv_counterpoise, actor) and not rv_vigil(actor) and not rv_mould_broken(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert rv_vigil(actor). Assert knows(actor, rv_vigil_known). }
    Result "You sit on the cold floor with your backs against the black table. Nobody speaks. The bronze gives back the lamp. The Counterpoise comes in from the landing, stands by the door and sets its pebble down in the dust, which it has not done before. At the end of the hour the lamp is as it was. On the way up it holds the door.".
  }
  Discovery rv_vigil_known "The assay cellar's Assayers sat a night's vigil at the end of each quarter, and the twelfth hook is oiled against the day someone sits it again.".

  // ── What the others in the company see ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Said once, by whoever the company has of the calling; a company without the calling has nobody to notice it.
  Relation heardNave(group). Relation heardLocks(group). Relation heardDrip(group). Relation heardStair(group).
  Relation heardStage(group). Relation heardFrame(group). Relation heardCellar(group).
  Rule rv_voice_nave at nave when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, nave) and not heardNave(party)
    says "{?m} stands at the foot of the bier-room door and does not go in. 'They have not said her name,' {?m} says. 'So no office has been read. A funeral without a name is a tally with the number scratched out. She is dead and nothing in this place has been told so.' {?m} touches the lintel. 'Somebody ought to.'" {
    Assert heardNave(party).
  }
  Rule rv_voice_locks at locks_office when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, locks_office) and not heardLocks(party)
    says "{?m} walks once round the room and stops at the door they came in by. 'No handle on the outside,' {?m} says. 'The hinges are on the inside too. That is not a door, that is a wall with an opinion.' {?m} glances at the strongroom. 'The joke of this house is that it has no lock. The lock is that you were let in.'" {
    Assert heardLocks(party).
  }
  Rule rv_voice_drip at drip_landing when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and awake(?m) and at(party, drip_landing) and not heardDrip(party)
    says "{?m} crouches by the nearest piling and runs a thumb along a line of green on the timber, a hand above the water. 'Rain does not wash this,' {?m} says. 'This is the Flood of nine years ago, and there is another, higher, and a third higher than that. They are measuring the sluice by the damp.' {?m} stands. 'You could read the Drip's whole history from the pilings, if you could stand to.'" {
    Assert heardDrip(party).
  }
  Rule rv_voice_stair at hill_foot when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_warrior) and awake(?m) and at(party, hill_foot) and not heardStair(party)
    says "{?m} looks up the Duelling Stair and then down at the bottom step. 'Worn on the left,' {?m} says. 'Every one of them led with the same foot. A hundred years of Seconds, and not one has thought to change.' {?m} rolls a shoulder. 'Whoever has the left foot at the top has the stair. It is not a fight, it is a habit in armour.'" {
    Assert heardStair(party).
  }
  Rule rv_voice_stage at stage_pit when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, stage_pit) and not heardStage(party)
    says "{?m} stands with a head cocked at the boards. 'The Cuff slaps under the stage on every beat,' {?m} says, 'and the Moths time their laughs to it. They do not know they do.' {?m} grins. 'Give me a month under this floor and I could make them laugh at anything by leaving a gap where the water goes.'" {
    Assert heardStage(party).
  }
  Rule rv_voice_frame at collegium_study when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_mage) and awake(?m) and at(party, collegium_study) and not heardFrame(party)
    says "{?m} holds a hand over the sheeted Frame and takes it away again. 'It is warm,' {?m} says. 'Not from the lamp. From the arithmetic. Something has been going on in here for sixty years and has not stopped for the sheet.' {?m} looks at the back wall, where a dark stair goes down behind the crab, and says nothing more about it at all." {
    Assert heardFrame(party).
  }
  Rule rv_voice_cellar at rv_assay when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, rv_assay) and not heardCellar(party) and not rv_page_taken(party)
    says "{?m} walks round the black table slowly, and stops, and looks at its underside and then at its legs. 'One lock on the case,' {?m} says. 'Open. A thing this old and this careful does not have one lock.' {?m} gets down on one knee. 'I will be a moment.'" {
    Assert heardCellar(party).
  }

  // ── The others who are pressed ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Vail WANTS to be a person for a little while. FEARS she is only the hound. LIES that she is procedure. Pressed, she
  // takes the domino off in the Gatehouse for the length of a kettle.
  Relation rv_vail_kettle(group).
  Topic rv_vail_kettle_t with vail "Ask her what she does with the Gatehouse kettle at night" when warrantHeld(actor) and not rv_vail_kettle(actor) once {
    Says "'It is procedure,' says the Watch, and then, as you wait, with the patience of a stranger who has no mask to hide it, 'It is a kettle. I put it on at the third hour and stand by it, and it boils, and I take off the domino.' She does it, now, with one hand, and the face under it is a plain tired woman of forty, not unlike a baker. 'Nobody is in the Gatehouse. It is the only place in Ombra where I am not looked at by a hound.' She puts the domino back on, quite deliberately. 'You may tell no one,' she says.".
    On discuss { Assert rv_vail_kettle(actor). Increase vailTrust(actor) by 1. }
  }
  // Hart WANTS a name on a lock. FEARS the Book's names are small. LIES that she wants the city to be less safe, not hurt.
  // Pressed with the Pound's first leaf she asks not to be given it.
  Topic rv_vane_leaf with vane "Show Orsolya Hart the first leaf of the Pound's book" when holding(actor, rv_page_kind) and not rv_vane_leaf_t(actor) once {
    Says "She reads it standing, and then sits. 'KEPT,' she says. 'Not owned.' She turns it over to the blank back, as every reader does. When she looks up, her long furious face is the face of someone who has been offered, for the first time in eleven years, a thing she wanted and found she could not use. 'Do not give it to me,' she says. 'I shall print it. Everybody will have it. And then it will be owed, by the third edition, because a thing in a pamphlet is a thing the city must have.' She folds the leaf and gives it back. 'Keep it,' she says. 'Hand it on. It is the only thing I have ever been shown that is made to be handed on and not read out.'".
    On discuss { Assert rv_vane_leaf_t(actor). }
  }
  Relation rv_vane_leaf_t(group).

  // ── Links outward ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // By item: a keeper's tally from the Marches is read at the Tally Coffee-house; the Corran letter opens the Bursar
  // (above). By world event: the coffee-house's board changes when the Rose of the Winds is made whole, wherever that
  // was: Ombra sees only that a price has moved. A visitor from elsewhere would come to Ombra by the Watch's notice in
  // any town, for the Drawing, or with a standard to be sealed against the Pound.
  Topic rv_tally_read with ct_tally "Show the tallyman the rubbing of a keeper's tally" when holding(actor, tally_rubbing) and not rv_tally_read_t(actor) once {
    Says "He takes the rubbing, wipes his slate, and reads it as a man reads a menu he used to know. 'Stroke for a ship, strokes beneath for the dead on her,' he says. 'This long one at the head, then three, then a flame. And here, the oldest, a hand I cannot read, though the notation is a tally, not a letter.' He taps the margin. 'The Row keeps its tallies in three notations. We have lost the oldest. I should be glad of the loan of your bench.' It is the first time in your hearing that a Magpie has said I.".
    On discuss { Assert rv_tally_read_t(actor). }
  }
  Relation rv_tally_read_t(group).
  Observe rv_board_rose at coffee_room when befell(rose_made_whole) and publicHours() "On the long blackboard a new price has been chalked, in an unfamiliar hand, for a commodity nobody can name. Under it a boy has written, in a child's capitals: CARRIED BY SEA. The Magpies are being careful not to be seen to look at it.".

  // ── What the Row says, the hour before ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule rv_news_kept when newsHour() and rv_told_bursar(party) once says "Of the Collegium of Measures: the Bursar entered in her own hand, in the quarter's book and signed, that the Pound is KEPT. The Hall of Weights has not replied. The twelfth hook has been seen to have a tag on it, with a name that is not yet engraved." { }
  Rule rv_news_leaf_taken when newsHour() and rv_page_kept(party) once says "Of the Pound: the Bursar has found the drawer in the Pound's table empty, and the seam in the stone as clean as it was, and has said nothing to anyone. She has sat the quarter's vigil with the Counterpoise, and when she came up the pebble in its pan was in the other pan." { }
  Rule rv_news_broken when newsHour() and rv_cp_broken(party) once says "Of the Collegium of Measures: a Counterpoise was found in the cellar in pieces, and the Bursar has entered it in the book as OWED, and has not said to whom. The twelfth hook is polished, and has been seen to have a tag on it with nothing engraved." { }
  Rule rv_news_thole_masked when newsHour() and rv_thole_masked(party) once says "Of Dr Thole: he does his arithmetic in a mask now, and has been seen to correct a student's slate in one. The Collegium is said to be considering a rule." { }
  Rule rv_news_vigil when newsHour() and rv_vigil(party) once says "Of the assay cellar: the Counterpoise, was seen on the ninth morning holding the cellar door, and on being asked what it weighed, said it weighed the night." { }
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/rounds.kyr:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The Rounds ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Registrar's own ledger: nine entries, initials and a street each, left in the Watch's keeping for whoever took
  // the Warrant. Each entry names the opening of a small story; the Round is done when that story ends in a way its
  // person can live with (state.kyr counts the Marks). Behind the last page, a sealed letter.
  Kind rounds_kind "the Registrar's Rounds" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "A narrow ledger bound in black oilcloth, the corners soft with handling and the spine mended with lamp-wick. Nine pages, each headed with the initials of a person and the name of a street; under each, one line in a small upright hand. On the last page there is no entry, only a flap of wax.".
  Item rounds_ledger "the Registrar's Rounds" is rounds_kind at offstage.
  Kind marrick_letter_kind "the Registrar's sealed letter" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "A single sheet folded in three and sealed with a bare oval in white wax. Across the fold, in the small upright hand of the ledger: NOT BEFORE THE NINTH DAY. ON THE NINTH, AT NOON, OPEN IT IN THE CHAPEL, AND DO NOT HURRY.".
  Item marrick_letter "the Registrar's sealed letter" is marrick_letter_kind at offstage.
  Relation ledgerHeld(group).

  Discovery round_ferry_known "Round 1 in the Registrar's ledger: R. K., the Gull, on the Drip ferry. 'Boat sinking by inches. Will not take a gift. Find the way she will.'".
  Discovery round_lovers_known "Round 2: C. D., the Heron, at the Weights. 'Writes every night to a Lamp. The Lamp writes back. Neither has asked who the other is. Leave it, or end it kindly; I could not decide.'".
  Discovery round_peck_known "Round 3: A. P., at the Hospice. 'A bed that is not the Hospice's. His name said once, not cried. He is dying and has been for some time. He will not ask.'".
  Discovery round_soup_known "Round 4: Sister N., the Anonymous Saint's kitchen. 'I have kept the pot. I shall not be able to. Someone must. She must not be told the donor.'".
  Discovery round_pound_known "Round 5: the short pound, at the bread-market. 'An ounce light, for ten years, and nobody has asked the Assessor. She cannot say a name. Someone must weigh it for her.'".
  Discovery round_lacke_known "Round 6: C. L., Counting Row. 'The Lock-tax. I have the arithmetic. I have not the nerve, or rather I have the nerve and not the years.'".
  Discovery round_pip_known "Round 7: P. T., in the cisterns. 'A lamp-boy. I saw him go down the steps and did not follow. I should have followed. He is nine.'".
  Discovery round_heronry_known "Round 8: the Heronry. 'The writ says a heron. The surveyors say the writ is old. Both are right, and the reeds are older than either.'".
  Discovery round_gaspar_known "Round 9: Gaspar, on Quiet Hill. 'He has been dusting a house for twenty-six years for a family that does not know it exists. I found her. I did not tell either. It was not mine to.'".
  Action read_ledger(actor: group, site: place) "Read the Registrar's Rounds" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and ledgerHeld(actor) and not knows(actor, rounds_known).
    Time 20.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, rounds_known). Assert knows(actor, round_ferry_known). Assert knows(actor, round_lovers_known). Assert knows(actor, round_peck_known).
      Assert knows(actor, round_soup_known). Assert knows(actor, round_pound_known). Assert knows(actor, round_lacke_known). Assert knows(actor, round_pip_known).
      Assert knows(actor, round_heronry_known). Assert knows(actor, round_gaspar_known). }
    Result "Nine pages in one small upright hand, each a person and a street and a line: not a list of offences or of debts but of things that wanted mending. At the end the oilcloth has been rubbed paler by a thumb. She read this a great deal. Whoever she was, she did not think of it as a duty; she thought of it, you suspect, as the only reading she liked.".
  }
  // After two Rounds are done the ledger reads differently: they are a selection.
  Rule rounds_selection when knows(party, rounds_known) and marks(party) >= 2 and not knows(party, lie_rounds) says "You take out the ledger again, with two of its pages done, and read the initials as you would read a roll: a ferrywoman, a clerk, a lamp-boy, a cook. Every one of them has something mended and is trusted by a street. They are not a list of the city's troubles. They are a list of the city's best." teaches lie_rounds { }

  // The sealed letter. Opened early, it is the secret told; kept till the ninth noon, it is a dead woman's patience.
  Discovery letter_read "The Registrar's sealed letter says, in her own hand: that she was Treasurer in the Year of the Cullet Sluice and six hundred drowned of it; that she has chosen the Offices by hand for thirty-one years, and the Urn is empty; that she means to leave the choice of what comes next to a Bare, since a Bare is the only person in Ombra she is allowed to tell; and that she is sorry about the Rounds, which she left in such a hurry.".
  Action break_seal(actor: group, site: place) "Break the Registrar's seal before the Ninth Day" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and holding(actor, marrick_letter_kind) and not knows(actor, letter_read) and not (day(clock) == 9 and hour(clock) >= 12).
    Time 5.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, letter_read). Assert knows(actor, urn_hollow). Assert knows(actor, marrick_was_treasurer). Assert sealBroken(actor). }
    Result "The wax is a bare oval and it comes away clean, which is a very polite thing for wax to do. You read it standing up, in the wet, with the ink beginning to run from your own thumbs, and when you have done you read it again, slower, and then you fold it as it was and put it away; and the city, when you look up, has a different shape.".
  }
  Relation sealBroken(group).
  Action open_seal_at_noon(actor: group, site: place) "Open the Registrar's letter, as she asked, in the Chapel on the Ninth Day at noon" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and within(actor, chapel) and holding(actor, marrick_letter_kind) and not knows(actor, letter_read) and day(clock) == 9 and hour(clock) >= 12.
    Time 10.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, letter_read). Assert knows(actor, urn_hollow). Assert knows(actor, marrick_was_treasurer). Assert sealWaited(actor). }
    Result "You open it in the nave at noon, with the rain on the Chapel's roof like a very large audience clearing its throat, and read it at the pace she asked. It is shorter than you feared. It does not accuse anyone, and it does not apologise for the one thing it should; and at the foot of it, in smaller writing, it says: I have kept the pot.".
  }
  Relation sealWaited(group).
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/serene.kyr:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── Hobb, the Serene ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // This year's Serene is a cooper named Hobb, whom the Registrar chose for his dullness. The night she died he went to
  // the lamp-room to beg to be let off the Mask, and saw her, and ran home to his cooperage in the Drip, where he has
  // sat in the white-and-gold for nine days, making barrels, unable to take it off for fear that without it he would be
  // asked what he saw. He is needed at the Drawing, because the Serene calls the Urn. He is moved neither by proof nor by
  // argument but by seeing someone sit bare in front of him and be all right.
  Observe cooperage_scene at cooperage_floor when publicHours() "A long low shed of staves and shavings, smelling of oak and boiled water and, very faintly, of something that is nearly fear. Hoops are stacked to the roof on one side and, on the other, barrels in the middle of becoming barrels. At a bench under the one window a broad man in a white-and-gold mask sits adzing a stave, and does not stop when you come in.".
  Observe cooperage_night at cooperage_floor when privateHours() "The cooperage at night is oak-dark and rain-loud. A single lamp burns on the bench. The man in the white-and-gold mask has not taken it off.".
  Person hobb "the Serene" at cooperage_floor {
    Role "a cooper in the white-and-gold mask of the Serene, sitting very still" when not knows(party, hobb_name).
    Role "Hobb the cooper, in the Serene's mask" when knows(party, hobb_name).
    Known as "a broad man in a white-and-gold mask" when not knows(party, hobb_name).
    Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "The man at the bench says, without looking up, in a voice that has been rehearsed in a mirror, 'The Serene hears.' The adze goes on. It is a very good voice and it is not the voice of the hand on the adze, which is shaking.".
    Greets again "'The Serene hears,' says the cooper, to the stave.".
  }
  Discovery hobb_name "The Serene Mask is worn this year by a cooper named Hobb, in the Drip, who has not taken it off since the Registrar died.".
  Relation hobbOpen(group). Relation hobbMoved(group). Relation hobbComes(group). Relation hobbGaveMask(group). Relation hobbHelped(group).
  // Public register: the Serene speaks as an Office. A bare company is told nothing at all.
  Topic hobb_bare_cold with hobb "Speak to the cooper" when publicHours() and not masked(actor) and not hobbOpen(actor) once {
    Says "'The Serene hears,' says the cooper, and the adze goes on, and goes on, and does not at any point stop for you. After a while you understand that you are being heard in the way a wall hears a draught.".
  }
  Topic hobb_masked with hobb "Speak to the cooper as a face" when publicHours() and masked(actor) and not hobbOpen(actor) once {
    Says "'The Serene hears every trade in Ombra,' says the cooper. 'The Serene has heard the Gulls, and the Cockles, and the Owls. The Serene has nothing to say to any of them that is not in the Concord.' He adzes. 'The Serene is not accepting petitions.' He has said it so often that you realise he has been waiting for somebody to say something that is not a petition.".
  }
  // The night knock: a bare knock is let in.
  Topic hobb_knock with hobb "Knock at the cooperage and say you are Bare" when privateHours() and not masked(actor) and not hobbOpen(actor) once {
    Says "The adze stops. It stops with a small hard sound, like a decision. 'Come in,' says the Serene's voice, and then a very different voice, lower, from the same throat: 'There is no one else. Close the door.' He has not turned. His shoulders under the white-and-gold are the shoulders of a man who has been holding up a ceiling. 'You are not from the Watch. The Watch sends a hound. You are not a Warden.' A pause. 'Are you a Bare?'".
    On discuss { Assert hobbOpen(actor). Assert knows(actor, hobb_name). }
  }
  Action read_hobb(actor: group, site: place) "Look at how he sits in the mask, and what he is not doing" {
    Speaker hobb.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hobb, site) and hobbOpen(actor) and not knows(actor, hobb_afraid).
    Time 5.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, hobb_afraid). }
    Result "He has not turned his head for the whole of the time you have been in the room: not to look at the door, not at the lamp, not at you. A man who will not turn his head is a man who knows precisely what he would see.".
    Otherwise "He is a broad man in a mask and he is very quiet. You do not know what the quiet is made of.".
  }
  Discovery hobb_afraid "The Serene is afraid, not of the Warden or the Watch, but of the face under the mask: he saw the Registrar in the lamp-room, and fears that without the Mask on he will be asked what he saw.".
  // Three ways in, and one needs no tongue at all: help him at the bench.
  Action help_cooper(actor: group, site: place) "Take the other end of the stave and help him bend the hoop" {
    Speaker hobb.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hobb, site) and hobbOpen(actor) and not hobbHelped(actor).
    Time 120.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert hobbHelped(actor). Assert knows(actor, serene_saw). }
    On failure { Assert hobbHelped(actor). }
    Result "A cask is one of the few things in the world that does not mind a stranger. You hold the hoop and he drives it, and neither of you speaks, and after the third barrel he says, to the stave, in the low voice: 'I came in the first night to ask her to take me off. I thought she might say no and that I would be able to bear it. She was at the table. She was not saying anything, and I knew before I got to the door she was not going to.' The adze rests. 'I ran. I never ran in my life.'".
    Otherwise "You hold the hoop and he drives it and it springs off the stave and cuts your hand. He looks at the blood and, for the first time, at you, and says nothing, and wraps it in a clean shaving. You learn nothing; but he has looked at you.".
  }
  Action coax_hobb(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Serene that the city needs him at the Drawing, and that he is allowed to be afraid" {
    Speaker hobb.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hobb, site) and hobbOpen(actor) and knows(actor, hobb_afraid) and not hobbMoved(actor).
    Time 10.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert hobbMoved(actor). }
    Result "'Allowed,' says the cooper, as if it were a word in a foreign tongue. He is silent for the length of a barrel-stave. 'No one has ever said that to the Serene. It is not in the Concord.' He turns a little in his seat, which is a very great deal. 'Ask me again when I am not in it.'".
    Otherwise "'The Serene cannot be afraid,' says the cooper. 'It is a rule.' His shoulders say it is not a rule that holds.".
  }
  // The thing that moves him: someone sitting bare, who is all right.
  Action sit_bare(actor: group, site: place) "Sit down on a barrel across from him, bare-faced, and say nothing" {
    Speaker hobb.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hobb, site) and hobbOpen(actor) and not masked(actor) and privateHours() and not hobbMoved(actor).
    Time 60.
    On success { Assert hobbMoved(actor). }
    Result "You sit. The rain talks on the roof. The lamp makes the shavings gold. He sees, in the course of an hour, that you have no mask, and no Office, and no name the city can say, and that you are eating a ship's biscuit with an expression of mild interest; that nobody has come, and nothing has happened to you. About the end of the hour he says, 'May I?' and puts his hands up. 'I have not had it off in nine days.'".
  }
  Topic hobb_off with hobb "Ask him what he will do with the Mask" when hobbMoved(actor) and not hobbComes(actor) and not hobbGaveMask(actor) once {
    Says "The Serene's mask is on the bench, white-and-gold, and under it is a big, tired, entirely ordinary face with the red line of the rim across the forehead. He looks at the Mask, and at you, and at the Mask. 'There is nobody inside it,' he says, and laughs, and it is a terrible laugh. 'I thought there would have to be. I thought it was somebody.' He wipes his face. 'I can put it on and go and call the Urn, and be the Serene till midnight, and be a cooper again. Or you can have it. It is the only Office in Ombra that does not ask for a name. I shall not mind.' He breathes. 'I should like to be told which.'".
  }
  Action hobb_goes(actor: group, site: place) "Tell him to wear it to the Drawing, and call the Urn himself" {
    Speaker hobb.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hobb, site) and hobbMoved(actor) and not hobbComes(actor) and not hobbGaveMask(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert hobbComes(actor). Assert knows(actor, hobb_name). }
    Result "'Right,' says the cooper. He puts it on, slowly, as you would put on an old coat that has become heavier. 'I shall be at the Urn Hall at the Ninth Bell. I shall be very much afraid.' He takes up the adze. 'I should like that on record.'".
  }
  Action hobb_gives(actor: group, site: place) "Take the Serene's mask from him, for the Drawing" {
    Speaker hobb.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hobb, site) and hobbMoved(actor) and not hobbComes(actor) and not hobbGaveMask(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert hobbGaveMask(actor). Assert holdsFace(actor, face_serene). Assert knows(actor, hobb_name). }
    Result "It is heavier than it looks, as a great many things in this city are. He puts it into your two hands with a visible effort not to put it on again, and flexes his face, and says, 'I have always wanted to be a cooper in a quiet street.' You hold the Serene Mask. It has the faint animal warmth of a face and, inside the rim, a ring of the man's sweat and a thumbprint of the Registrar's white wax.".
  }
  // If nobody comes, he does not go, and the Drawing has no one to call it.
  Rule hobb_urn when hobbComes(party) and drawingNight() and hour(clock) >= 20 and not at(hobb, urn_hall) { Assert at(hobb, urn_hall). }
  Rule hobb_home when not (drawingNight() and hour(clock) >= 20) and not at(hobb, cooperage_floor) { Assert at(hobb, cooperage_floor). }
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/state.kyr:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── What every part of the city reads ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Warrant, the face the company wears, the Watch's patience (heat), what the city thinks of each mask
  // (goodwill), the Registrar's Rounds and the Marks they leave, and the Book of Faces itself.

  // The Warrant (warrant.kyr). Held from the first morning by a company that took it; suspended while heat is three
  // or more; withdrawn when the Gate shuts.
  Relation warrantHeld(group). Relation faceOffered(group). Relation faceTaken(group). Relation faceDeclined(group). Relation gateShut(group).
  // The Watch's patience: heat on the company, up to six (see faces.kyr). Three suspends the Warrant, six shuts the Gate.
  Measure heat(group) at most 6.
  Query warrantLive() means warrantHeld(party) and heat(party) < 3 and not gateShut(party).

  // ── Faces ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A face is a trade's mask or an Office's. The company is Bare, or wears one face (wears(party, f)); a face it may
  // wear it holds (holdsFace), by rent, gift, theft or right. What a mask has earned is goodwill on the mask and not on
  // whoever wore it; what it has done is heat on the mask as well.
  Kind face.
  Entity face_gull: face "the Gull, the ferrymen's domino".
  Entity face_owl: face "the Owl, the lamp-trimmers' domino".
  Entity face_cockle: face "the Cockle, the bakers' and chandlers' domino".
  Entity face_heron: face "the Heron, the Weights clerks' cowl".
  Entity face_magpie: face "the Magpie, the tallymen's domino".
  Entity face_moth: face "the Moth, the players' half-mask".
  Entity face_crow: face "the Crow, the letter-writers' and post-clerks' domino".
  Entity face_key: face "the Key, the Warden of Locks' Office-mask".
  Entity face_pound: face "the Pound, the Assessor of Weights' Office-mask".
  Entity face_serene: face "the Serene Mask".
  Entity face_white: face "the White Face, the Registrar's".
  Relation holdsFace(group, face). Relation wears(group, face) exclusive. Relation masked(group).
  Relation rented(group, face). Measure rentEnds(group).
  Measure goodwill(face). Measure faceHeat(face).
  // A face is fitted to someone, or to no one: a mask sits properly only on the face it was cut for (faces.kyr).
  Relation fitted(group, face).

  // ── Rounds and Marks ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Registrar's ledger has nine errands. A Round is done when its story is brought to an end its person can live
  // with; each one done leaves a Mark, and the Marks are the franchise of the Qualified Draw.
  Kind round.
  Entity r_ferry: round "Round 1: R. K., the Gull".
  Entity r_lovers: round "Round 2: C. D., the Heron".
  Entity r_peck: round "Round 3: A. P., at the Hospice".
  Entity r_soup: round "Round 4: Sister N.".
  Entity r_pound: round "Round 5: the short pound".
  Entity r_lacke: round "Round 6: Weights Row, C. L.".
  Entity r_pip: round "Round 7: P. T., in the cisterns".
  Entity r_heronry: round "Round 8: the heron-writ".
  Entity r_gaspar: round "Round 9: Gaspar".
  Relation roundDone(group, round). Relation marked(round). Measure marks(group).
  Rule round_marked when roundDone(party, ?r) and not marked(?r) { Assert marked(?r). Increase marks(party) by 1. }

  // ── The case ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The four hands on the Registrar's last evening and what the city is made of. Every file may teach these.
  Discovery marrick_dead "The Registrar of Ombra lay dead in the Chapel's lamp-room on the eve of the Novena, in the white mask of her office, and the Book of Faces is gone from its lectern.".
  Discovery rounds_known "The Registrar kept a ledger of nine Rounds for the nine nights: initials and a street each, errands of the kind she had been doing by night in the white mask.".
  Discovery pell_hid_book "Tomas Pell, the Registrar's Clerk of the Book, found her dead, put her mask straight, and posted the Book to Nobody at the Dead Letter Office, which burns its Nobodies at noon on the ninth day.".
  Discovery serene_saw "The Serene came to the Registrar's lamp-room the night she died, and ran; he has not taken the Mask off since.".
  Discovery lacke_unfaced "Ser Corvin Lacke, the Warden of Locks, called on the Registrar in the Chapel an hour before she died, threatened her, and said her name aloud: Unfacing, the one crime the Concord can prosecute in the case.".
  Discovery lacke_taxed "The Warden of Locks has been skimming the Lock-tax for years; the Registrar's Rounds were closing on him.".
  Discovery pip_saw "A lamp-boy named Pip Treen, nine, was under the lamp-table and saw the Registrar bare, and saw the clerk, the cooper and the Warden come and go; he is hiding in the cisterns under the Drip.".
  Discovery marrick_was_treasurer "The Registrar, Ysolde Marrick, was drawn Treasurer at nineteen in the Year of the Cullet Sluice, in which the Sluice failed and six hundred drowned; the Serene of that year took the blame.".
  Discovery sluice_known "In the Year of the Cullet Sluice the Sluice failed in the Rains and six hundred in the low islands drowned. The Serene of that year, Absalom Peck, was Named for it and has lived Bare since.".
  // The Lie: the Urn is a sealed bronze jar with nothing in it, and for thirty-one years the Registrars have chosen the
  // Offices by hand. Five places show it; any three give it away (the Drawing Table).
  Discovery lie_tally "The Rain-Wives' tally of thirty years of draws: the Offices go, year after year, to the best bakers, ferrymen and clerks in the city, with a regularity no lot would give.".
  Discovery lie_wall "On the Wall of Faces the nineteen Offices of the last thirty years stand on the shelf of Menders: those whom their streets trust.".
  Discovery lie_peck "Absalom Peck says the Treasurer of the Sluice year was drawn by the Urn at nineteen; and that after it, the drawing was never the same.".
  Discovery lie_urn "The Urn in the Urn Hall does not rattle when shaken: it is a sealed bronze jar with a slot, and the weight in it is its own.".
  Discovery lie_rounds "The Registrar's Rounds are a selection: errands in streets, each a person tried.".
  Discovery urn_hollow "The Urn is empty. For thirty-one years, since the Sluice, the Registrars of Ombra have chosen the Offices by hand and read them from a palm-card, and let the city believe in chance.".
  Measure lieClues(group).
  Relation counted(fact).
  Rule count_tally when knows(party, lie_tally) and not counted(lie_tally) { Assert counted(lie_tally). Increase lieClues(party) by 1. }
  Rule count_wall when knows(party, lie_wall) and not counted(lie_wall) { Assert counted(lie_wall). Increase lieClues(party) by 1. }
  Rule count_peck when knows(party, lie_peck) and not counted(lie_peck) { Assert counted(lie_peck). Increase lieClues(party) by 1. }
  Rule count_urn when knows(party, lie_urn) and not counted(lie_urn) { Assert counted(lie_urn). Increase lieClues(party) by 1. }
  Rule count_rounds when knows(party, lie_rounds) and not counted(lie_rounds) { Assert counted(lie_rounds). Increase lieClues(party) by 1. }
  Rule urn_deduced when lieClues(party) >= 3 and not knows(party, urn_hollow) says "You lay three of them side by side, as you would lay out stitches: the tally, the shelf, the jar that does not rattle, the street each errand was in. They make one shape. The Urn does not draw. Somebody has been drawing for it, by hand, for thirty years, and has been good at it." teaches urn_hollow {
    Assert deduced(party). }
  Relation deduced(group).

  // ── The Book of Faces ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Book is a thing the company may hold (post.kyr hides it in the Dead Letter Office); what it says is read at
  // the Registry (registry.kyr).
  Kind book_of_faces_kind "the Book of Faces" is gear worth 0 weighing 2 described "A ledger bound in white vellum gone grey at the corners, clasped with a brass lock that has been forced, and under the lock the seal of the Registrar, a bare oval with nothing in it. Inside, in ninety years of one hand after another, the names that wore the masks.".
  Item book_of_faces "the Book of Faces" is book_of_faces_kind at offstage.
  Relation bookRead(group). Relation drawingOver(place). Relation drawingHeld(group).

  // ── Hands at the Drawing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Each calling's arc ends in an act the company may do on the ninth night (drawing.kyr reads these).
  Kind hand.
  Entity hand_stair: hand "the Stair held".
  Entity hand_likeness: hand "the Likeness cast".
  Entity hand_cast: hand "the casts of the Wall".
  Entity hand_blessing: hand "the Draw blessed, or refused".
  Entity hand_lampoon: hand "the Lampoon played".
  Entity hand_heron: hand "the heron flown".
  Entity hand_door: hand "the Door held".
  Entity hand_procession: hand "the Trades' procession".
  // An arc asserts handReady when its finale is available and handPlayed when the company has used it at the Drawing,
  // with a handWay saying how (each arc's own entities: its relations are its own).
  Relation handReady(group, hand). Relation handPlayed(group, hand). Measure handWay(hand).
  // How the arcs are doing, for the closing news.
  Relation arcBegun(group, hand). Relation arcDone(group, hand).

  // ── Other things the city shares ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation privateStairOpen(group). Discovery private_stair_known "The Palazzo Tarn keeps a private stair from the Contessa's study to the Chapel's vestry, shut three hundred years.".
  // The lovers (post.kyr, drip.kyr): the Heron and the Lamp.
  Relation loversMet(group). Relation loversRevealed(group). Relation loversTogether(group).
  // Who has been Named, in a square, aloud.
  Relation named(group).
  // The Wall of Faces has a cast of the company's own face.
  Relation castTaken(group).
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/thief.kyr:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The Cast-Room ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The thief's own: a heist in five stages on the Wall of Faces under Madame Pavane's house (maskers.kyr). Anyone may
  // do it; a company with lockwork, stealth and climbing does it cheaply; a company with none may do it by the apprentice
  // (a favour taken from a boy), by the Many Hands (a price in coin and in squeezes), or as the Fitter's guest (a trust
  // taken from a woman). The stages: (1) casing, (2) a crew, (3) a way in, (4) the take, (5) the fence; and at the Drawing
  // the hand_cast, in the Urn Hall. A thief takes what is owed, what is valuable, or what is hidden:
  //   owed      Absalom Peck's cast, turned to the wall among the Named, and one's own cast, if one sat for it;
  //   valuable  the Offices' casts, the faces the Offices are cut to (th_keys);
  //   hidden    the Menders' row and the Registrar's cast, the proof of the Lie (th_proof).
  // What it leaves: heat, the Fitter, a boy who is turned out unless the company goes back, the Hands' squeezes.
  //
  // For the other files: handReady/handPlayed (hand_cast) and arcBegun; th_cast_vane, th_cast_lacke, th_cast_broken,
  // th_cast_back (what became of the casts: relations on the party); th_proof_*, th_keys_* the same per kind.

  // ── Obadiah Slee, of the Many Hands ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Many Hands are the pickpockets' guild; they have worn the Magpie's domino four hundred years and been taken for
  // tallymen. Slee is their fence, and sells silence by weight: a secret is priced at what it would cost the person it
  // is kept from, and weighed on a brass scale with a sworn weight in the other pan. He wants one thing of the cellar,
  // which is a squeeze of the Warden of Locks' face, because the Warden taxes their locks.
  Person th_slee "Obadiah Slee" at maskers_lane {
    Role "the fence of the Many Hands". Ancestry halfling. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Known as "a small man in a Magpie's domino beside a barrow and a brass scale" when publicHours() and not knows(party, th_slee_name).
    Known as "a small man in his shirtsleeves with a brass scale at his knee" when privateHours() and not knows(party, th_slee_name).
    Greets "A small man with very clean hands has not looked up from the scale since you came near, and it has told him, you suspect, everything he needs. 'Weight of a coat,' he says, to nobody. 'Weight of a cough. Weight of a thing you'd as soon was not said.' He sets a brass weight on one pan and watches the other rise. 'Good day to you. I sell faces, nearly. Sometimes I sell the other thing.'".
    Greets again "'Weight of the day,' says Slee, and does not look up.".
  }
  Discovery th_slee_name "The Many Hands' fence is Obadiah Slee, who sells silence by weight from a barrow in Maskers' Lane by day and from the drying-loft over the Cockle and Heron by night.".
  Discovery th_slee_terms "Slee of the Many Hands will give a company a roof and a muffled bell-line and weigh the silence afterward, for fourteen coin and a cut: the Hands take a squeeze of whatever comes out of the Wall.".
  Discovery th_slee_wants "What Slee wants of the Wall is not coin: it is a squeeze of the Warden of Locks' face, since the Warden taxes the Hands' locks, and a Key-mask that fitted would open every one of the Warden's doors.".
  Rule th_slee_barrow when hour(clock) >= 11 and hour(clock) < 17 and not at(th_slee, maskers_lane) { Assert at(th_slee, maskers_lane). }
  Rule th_slee_loft when (hour(clock) >= 20 or hour(clock) < 3) and not at(th_slee, mk_loft) { Assert at(th_slee, mk_loft). }
  Rule th_slee_bed when ((hour(clock) >= 3 and hour(clock) < 11) or (hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 20)) and not at(th_slee, offstage) { Assert at(th_slee, offstage). }
  Observe th_slee_loft_scene at mk_loft when at(th_slee, mk_loft) "At the end of the loft, among the masks on their lines, a man sits on a crate in his shirtsleeves with a brass scale between his feet. Beside it, in a row, are the weights: little brass things, in sizes, each with a word stamped on it in a language that is only letters.".

  Topic th_slee_cold with th_slee "Say good day to the man with the scale" when not masked(actor) and publicHours() {
    Says "The scale does not move. 'Not at home to the Bare, by day,' says Slee, pleasantly. 'By day I am a Magpie with a barrow. At night I am at home to everyone with nothing to lose.' His eyes, which are very mild, go once up and down you like a thumb along a blade. 'It is an hour after the Ninth Bell. Mind the ladder; the Heron drips.'".
  }
  Topic th_slee_day with th_slee "Ask the hawker what he is weighing" when masked(actor) and publicHours() once {
    Says "'Faces,' says Slee. 'Second-hand ones, mostly; the best faces have been worn.' He sets a Gull on one pan and a brass weight on the other, and the Gull goes up. 'I weigh other things, if the face is right: a thing you would rather not have said, say, or not have seen. Silence is sold by weight in this lane. A pound of it costs about what the thing costs.' Under the Magpie's domino his eyes weigh you without the scale. 'Come when the Lane has gone home, if you have such a thing.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, th_slee_name). }
  }
  Topic th_slee_hello with th_slee "Climb the ladder to the loft, bare, and say you were told to come" when not masked(actor) and privateHours() and at(th_slee, mk_loft) once {
    Says "'Faces off at the stair,' says Slee. 'You've done that. Good. A masked man in my loft at night is a burglar, and I am a respectable house of crime.' He taps the scale. 'Obadiah Slee, of the Hands. You have a thing in the Fitter's cellar, I think. You look it. Everyone who comes up that ladder after dark has a thing in somebody's cellar.' He moves a weight a quarter inch. 'Sit. Mind the Heron on your left. He drips.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, th_slee_name). }
  }
  Topic th_slee_terms_ask with th_slee "Ask what the Hands would do for a share" when not masked(actor) and privateHours() and knows(actor, th_slee_name) and at(th_slee, mk_loft) once {
    Says "'A hand on the roof, a muffle for the bell-line, a silence afterward, weighed honest.' He ticks them off without raising his hands. 'The roof is on me; the bells are a child called Tick, who is eleven and could go through a keyhole; the silence is by weight, and I weigh fair. Fourteen coin, the lot. And a cut. The Hands take a squeeze of anything that comes out of that cellar. It is not mine to waive; I am a clerk of it.' He does not smile. 'You can say no. They generally come back.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, th_slee_terms). }
  }
  Measure th_fee(group).
  Initially Set th_fee(party) to 14.
  Relation th_read_slee(group). Relation th_haggled(group). Relation th_bluffed(group). Relation th_waive_tried(group). Relation th_cut_waived(group).
  Relation th_slee_paid(group). Relation th_parcel_done(group). Relation th_slee_secret_given(group).
  // First check: a man who sells silence by weight tells you what he wants by what he leaves on the scale.
  Action th_slee_read(actor: group, site: place) "Watch what Slee does with his hands when you say the word cellar, and say what you think he wants" {
    Speaker th_slee.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(th_slee, site) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and knows(actor, th_slee_terms) and not th_read_slee(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert th_read_slee(actor). Assert knows(actor, th_slee_wants). }
    On failure { Assert th_read_slee(actor). }
    Result "When you say the word cellar his left hand goes still on the scale, and his right goes on moving the weights: that is the hand that does not care. You say it is not the casts. You say it is one cast; you say it is a man who taxes locks. For a very long moment Slee looks at the scale as at a witness. 'The Warden of Locks,' he says. 'Corvin. Two coin on every lock the Hands have ever opened, and a Key-mask that fitted would open every door he owns. Yes.' He weighs it, and finds that he does not mind that you know. 'I like to be read. It happens so seldom.'".
    Otherwise "You say you think he wants coin, and a great deal of it, and he agrees with you gently, in the manner of a man agreeing that it is raining. His left hand did something when you said cellar. You did not see what.".
  }
  // Second: the price. One try. A failed haggle is a dearer bargain.
  Action th_slee_haggle(actor: group, site: place) "Haggle with Slee over the fourteen coin" {
    Speaker th_slee.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(th_slee, site) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and knows(actor, th_slee_terms) and not th_haggled(actor) and not th_slee_paid(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert th_haggled(actor). Decrease th_fee(actor) by 5 or to nothing. }
    On failure { Assert th_haggled(actor). Increase th_fee(actor) by 2. }
    Result "You do not argue the price; you argue the weight, which is the Hands' only philosophy: that a silence kept for a child of eleven, over a roof, in the rain, is lighter than a silence kept in a room with a stove. He weighs it. He is a man who loves to be beaten fairly. 'Nine,' he says. 'And I shall tell the Hands I was robbed.'".
    Otherwise "He lets you talk. When you have finished he puts a very small brass weight on the pan, and the pan does not move. 'Sixteen,' says Slee, with immense regret. 'The silence has got heavier while you were speaking. That is how it is with silence.'".
  }
  // Third: the Hands' own name, borrowed. A lie told to a man whose trade is lies has to be a particular kind of lie.
  Action th_slee_bluff(actor: group, site: place) "Let Slee think that a Magpie of the Hands gave you the way up the ladder" {
    Speaker th_slee.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(th_slee, site) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and knows(actor, th_slee_terms) and not th_bluffed(actor) and not th_slee_paid(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert th_bluffed(actor). Decrease th_fee(actor) by 4 or to nothing. }
    On failure { Assert th_bluffed(actor). Increase th_fee(actor) by 4. }
    Result "You say that a woman in a Magpie's domino at the Row quay, with one boot, told you. You do not say her name; you say her boot. It is the right detail: there is a Magpie with one boot, and Slee's face does a small, brief thing around the eyes, and he says that Wick has a mouth like a drain and a heart like a church. 'Ten,' he says. 'For a friend of Wick's. Do not tell her I said friend.'".
    Otherwise "'There is no Magpie with one boot,' says Slee, kindly, putting down a weight. 'There is a Magpie with two, and he has not told anyone the way up my ladder, because he does not know it.' He looks at you a while. 'Eighteen. For the lie. It was a good lie; it just was not true.'".
  }
  // Fourth: to be let off the cut. Slee will not, for argument; for something he wants more than he wants squeezes, perhaps.
  Action th_slee_waive(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Slee to let the Hands forgo their squeeze" {
    Speaker th_slee.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(th_slee, site) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and knows(actor, th_slee_terms) and not th_cut_waived(actor) and not th_waive_tried(actor) and not th_slee_paid(actor) and not th_read_slee(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert th_waive_tried(actor). Assert th_cut_waived(actor). }
    On failure { Assert th_waive_tried(actor). }
    Result "You say that a squeeze is a Hand in the Wall's pocket for as long as there are Walls, and that the thing you want is for the Wall to have no pockets. You say it as if it were a principle. It is, a little. Slee looks at you for a while with his head on one side. 'The Hands do not have principles,' he says, 'but we are famously fond of people who have.' He moves a weight off the scale. 'No cut. I shall tell them I was moved. They will say I am growing soft. I am.'".
    Otherwise "'A squeeze is a squeeze,' says Slee, and the voice is the voice of a man reading from a book of rules, which he is. 'It is not a thing I can waive. It is a thing I can be sorry about.' He is, a little.".
  }
  Action th_slee_waive_read(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Slee to let the Hands forgo their squeeze, for the sake of what he wants" {
    Speaker th_slee.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(th_slee, site) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and knows(actor, th_slee_wants) and not th_cut_waived(actor) and not th_waive_tried(actor) and not th_slee_paid(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert th_waive_tried(actor). Assert th_cut_waived(actor). }
    On failure { Assert th_waive_tried(actor). }
    Result "You say you will bring him the Warden's face, or the next best thing, if the Hands forgo the rest. It is a promise only of a kind, and he knows it. 'A man who taxes locks,' says Slee, slowly, 'and a Key-mask that would not fit.' He puts a hand flat over the scale, which is the Hands' way of closing a matter. 'No cut. Bring me the Warden, and we are paid.'".
    Otherwise "He listens with the whole of his face, and shakes his head, and the voice in which he says no is a wistful one. 'I should like to,' says Slee. 'I should like it very much. But the cut is the Hands'. It is only the Warden that is mine.'".
  }
  // Fifth: a thing carried, which asks neither wit nor skill: an errand the Hands cannot send their own on.
  Kind th_parcel_kind "Slee's parcel" is gear worth 0 weighing 1 described "A parcel in greasy sacking the size of two fists, tied with a bit of ribbon that has been tied and untied a great many times. It is heavy for its size, and it ticks, very faintly, as a clock does that has not been told it is not wanted.".
  Item th_parcel "Slee's parcel" is th_parcel_kind at offstage.
  Topic th_slee_parcel with th_slee "Ask what the Hands would have you carry, in place of coin" when not masked(actor) and privateHours() and knows(actor, th_slee_terms) and not th_parcel_done(actor) and not carries(actor, th_parcel) and not th_slee_paid(actor) once {
    Says "'Carry.' He looks, for the first time, quite pleased. 'There is a parcel. It goes to the end of the Row quay, where a boy with one boot will take it. You do not open it and you do not ask. If the Watch stops you, it is an eel. I should hold it a little away from you.' He puts it on the crate between you. 'Four off the fee. And my good opinion, which is not for sale, so you may as well have it for nothing.'".
    On discuss { Give th_parcel to actor. }
  }
  Action th_deliver_parcel(actor: group, site: place) "Leave the parcel at the end of the Row quay for the boy with one boot" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, row_quay) and carries(actor, th_parcel).
    Time 15 minutes.
    On success { Spend th_parcel from actor. Assert th_parcel_done(actor). Decrease th_fee(actor) by 4 or to nothing. }
    Result "The boy with one boot is there, in the rain, at the end of the quay, as if he had been put there by the quay. He takes the parcel in both hands, does not say a word, and weighs it with his arms; then he is gone along the edge of the water faster than a boy with one boot should be. It stopped ticking when he took it. You will never know what it was.".
  }
  // Sixth: a secret for a secret. What the Hands were never able to prove about the Warden of Locks is worth more than coin.
  Action th_slee_secret(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Slee, as a thing weighed, that the Warden of Locks has been skimming the Lock-tax" {
    Speaker th_slee.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(th_slee, site) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and knows(actor, th_slee_terms) and knows(actor, lacke_taxed) and not th_slee_secret_given(actor) and not th_slee_paid(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert th_slee_secret_given(actor). Assert th_cut_waived(actor). Set th_fee(actor) to 0. }
    Result "He does not write it down. A man who writes down what he is told ends in the Cuff. He puts a brass weight on the pan, a heavy one, and looks at it for a time without breathing. 'Skimming,' says Slee. 'For years. And I have been paying him the tax.' The look on his face is the look of a man whose scale has at last been used. 'This is worth more than fourteen coin. It is worth more than the cut. Go up the roof, and I shall see that the bell is muffled, and nothing is owed. You have given me a thing I can weigh. It is the only currency I trust.'".
  }
  Action th_slee_deal(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the bargain with Slee: a roof, a muffled bell-line, a weighed silence" {
    Speaker th_slee.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(th_slee, site) and privateHours() and hour(clock) >= 20 and hour(clock) < 23 and not masked(actor) and knows(actor, th_slee_terms) and not th_slee_paid(actor) and not th_crew_dov(actor) and not th_crew_alone(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= th_fee(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by th_fee(actor). Increase quantity(th_slee, gold) by th_fee(actor). Assert th_slee_paid(actor). Assert th_crew_slee(actor). Assert th_bells_off(actor). Assert knows(actor, th_routine). Assert knows(actor, th_bells). Assert knows(actor, th_roof_way). }
    Result "You put the coin on the crate, and he does not count it; he weighs it, on the scale, against a word. 'Tonight, at eleven, the skylight bolt is off, and a child called Tick has been along the roof with a plank,' he says. 'The Fitter is at her stove until one, and abed after, with the cellar key on a chain at her neck, and a line of tin bells from her bed to the stair-head. Tick will be at the bell. You go in after one. You go down. You come out. You come back to me, with what you have, and I weigh it.' He puts a finger on the scale. 'Not before one. She is a light sleeper until one.'".
  }
  // The Hands' silence, afterward, by weight: a coin for each thing taken, and six beyond the lot.
  Measure th_loot(group).
  Action th_slee_silence(actor: group, site: place) "Have Slee weigh the silence over what has come out of the cellar" {
    Speaker th_slee.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(th_slee, site) and th_crew_slee(actor) and th_took_any(actor) and not th_silenced(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= th_loot(actor) * 4 + 6.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by th_loot(actor) * 4 + 6. Increase quantity(th_slee, gold) by th_loot(actor) * 4 + 6. Assert th_silenced(actor). }
    Result "He weighs what you took, on the scale, in his hands, with his eyes shut, as a priest weighs a sin; then the price of the silence, in coin, against a word you cannot read. 'Heavy,' he says. 'Plaster is. It is a pound of plaster for a pound of trouble.' He takes the coin, and the lane's gossip of tomorrow will not have your shape in it. Whoever speaks of the cellar will be wrong in a way that is useful.".
  }
  Relation th_silenced(group).
  Action th_slee_squeezes(actor: group, site: place) "Buy back the Hands' squeezes of the casts you took, thirty coin" {
    Speaker th_slee.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(th_slee, site) and th_hands_squeezed(actor) and not th_squeezes_back(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 30.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 30. Increase quantity(th_slee, gold) by 30. Assert th_squeezes_back(actor). }
    Result "'Thirty,' says Slee, with the sorrow of a man selling a favourite horse, and takes a flat parcel out of the lining of the crate, and a second, and a third; and the plaster faces on them are very fine, and very thin, and look like what they are, which is a coat the Hands had been going to wear. 'I should say they were burnt. But I do not lie to people who have paid.' He gives them to you. 'You will want to burn them. Not in my stove.'".
  }
  Relation th_squeezes_back(group). Relation th_hands_squeezed(group).
  Action th_slee_hand_name(actor: group, site: place) "Show Slee what you carried out of the Fitter's house, and ask whether it is a name" {
    Speaker th_slee.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(th_slee, site) and th_took_any(actor) and not th_hands_name(actor) and not th_seen(actor) and (th_crew_slee(actor) or th_crew_alone(actor)).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert th_hands_name(actor). }
    Result "He looks at what you have, and at you, and for the first time he takes his hand off the scale. 'In by the roof, down by the wall, out by the same, and not a bell,' says Slee. 'In forty years I've had it done twice.' He gets up, which he does not do, and puts out a very clean hand. 'You are a Hand,' he says. 'The name is Pale Sparrow, and it is yours, and you may say it in any pocket in Ombra, and it will be known. You may not say it to the Watch.' It is the first time anyone in Ombra has given you a name that is not a mask.".
  }
  Relation th_hands_name(group).
  Action th_slee_lesson(actor: group, who: member, site: place) "Have {who} shown the Hands' third trick by Slee" {
    Speaker th_slee.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(th_slee, site) and memberOf(who, actor) and th_hands_name(actor) and not th_lesson_given(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve endow(who, dexterity, by_one).
    On success { Assert th_lesson_given(actor). }
    Result "It is a trick with the thumb and the third finger and a coin that is not there. He shows it eleven times, slowly, then once at the speed of a thought, and you cannot see where the coin went; and then the Pale Sparrow takes it out of your own sleeve. 'It is not for the Fitter's lock,' he says. 'It is for the day somebody asks to see your hands.'".
  }
  Relation th_lesson_given(group).

  // ── Stage one: casing ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Fitter's night, the bell-line, the roof, the key. Three ways to learn it: watch, ask the boy, buy it from Slee.
  Discovery th_routine "Madame Pavane is at her stove until one in the morning and abed after, with the cellar key on a chain about her neck; a Fitter's house keeps no dog, only habit.".
  Discovery th_bells "A line of tin bells runs from the Fitter's bed to the head of the cellar stair, strung a hand above the third step; whoever goes down must step along the wall or cut the cord.".
  Discovery th_dov_key "Dov Ashe sweeps the Wall and keeps a copy of the cellar key on a cord inside his shirt.".
  Discovery th_roof_way "The slates over the Fitter's parlour are loose at the north end and the skylight's bolt is a thin hook on the inside, which a blade slid between frame and sash will lift.".
  Query th_cased(a: group) means knows(a, th_routine) and knows(a, th_bells).
  Relation th_alerted(group). Relation th_watched(group).
  Action th_watch_house(actor: group, site: place) "Watch Madame Pavane's house from the lane, through a night, for the way it keeps itself" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, maskers_lane) and privateHours() and hour(clock) >= 20 and hour(clock) < 23 and not masked(actor) and not th_cased(actor) and not th_watched(actor).
    Time 6.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert th_watched(actor). Assert knows(actor, th_routine). Assert knows(actor, th_bells). Assert knows(actor, th_roof_way). }
    On failure { Assert th_watched(actor). Assert th_alerted(actor). Increase heat(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You find the doorway of the shut mask-shop opposite, and you wait in it, and the lane goes by you in its night: the Fitter's lamp, the Fitter's shadow on the ground glass, the boy going up the roof ladder with a bundle at eight and coming down again at midnight. At one the lamp goes out. A second light, small, moves through the house and stops at the head of a stair and a window you cannot see; and then there is a line of little notes in the air, like a spoon on a glass, as if somebody were testing something. A string of tin bells. At one in the morning the Fitter goes to bed with her key about her neck. The slates over the parlour are a different grey at the north end, where a tile is out.".
    Otherwise "You find the doorway opposite, and wait in it, and it is a very long and very wet hour. Somebody at the Cockle and Heron's shutter sees a shape where there should not be one, and says so, loudly, in the way the Lane says things: to nobody, at the top of its voice. A lamp comes on at the Fitter's. You go home, and the Fitter, in her dressing-gown, comes out on the step to look at the rain for a good while.".
  }
  Topic th_dov_idle with dov "Ask Dov, idly, how the Fitter's house keeps itself at night" when not masked(actor) and at(dov, maskers_roof) and mk_dov_trusts(actor) and not th_dov_asked(actor) once {
    Says "'Keeps itself?' He laughs, being sixteen and fond of being asked anything. 'She goes to bed at one. Always. There's a bell-line from her bed to the cellar stair, since the year somebody lifted a Mender's cast; you go along the wall, on the left, and it does not ring. The roof bolt's a hook. I'm the only one who knows.' He pats his shirt. 'And the key, the spare, I had made, so as not to wake her for the sweeping. Why?' He looks at you, and the laugh goes out, and does not quite leave. 'Why do you want to know?'".
    On discuss { Assert th_dov_asked(actor). Assert knows(actor, th_routine). Assert knows(actor, th_bells). Assert knows(actor, th_dov_key). Assert knows(actor, th_roof_way). }
  }
  Relation th_dov_asked(group).

  // ── Stage two: a crew ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Alone; the apprentice (the inside man, and what it costs him); the Hands (coin, and a cut). One only.
  Relation th_crew_alone(group). Relation th_crew_dov(group). Relation th_crew_slee(group).
  Action th_decide_alone(actor: group, site: place) "Resolve to do it with nobody's help and nobody's name" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and th_cased(actor) and not th_crew_alone(actor) and not th_crew_dov(actor) and not th_crew_slee(actor).
    Time 0.
    On success { Assert th_crew_alone(actor). }
    Result "You will do it alone: the roof, the bolt, the key, the line of bells, the dark, and afterward nobody to say it was you. It is the most expensive way, and the only one with nobody to blame.".
  }
  Promise th_dov_promise "to keep Dov Ashe out of it" to dov
    kept at the close when th_crew_dov(party) and not th_dov_failed(party) "Dov Ashe was kept out of it, as you said."
    broken when th_dov_failed(party) "The Fitter has put Dov Ashe out of her house for a key that was used, and you said he would not be blamed." { }.
  Relation th_dov_failed(group).
  Action th_dov_recruit(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Dov, as you would ask a journeyman, to be your inside man" {
    Speaker dov.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(dov, site) and at(dov, maskers_roof) and not masked(actor) and mk_dov_trusts(actor) and th_dov_asked(actor) and not th_crew_dov(actor) and not th_crew_alone(actor) and not th_crew_slee(actor) and not th_dov_refused(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert th_crew_dov(actor). Assert th_have_key(actor). Assert th_bells_off(actor). Assert promiseMade(th_dov_promise). }
    On failure { Assert th_dov_refused(actor). Assert th_alerted(actor). }
    Result "You ask him as you would ask a journeyman, and he has never been asked: you can see it arrive, like a coin dropped down a well. 'It's the Wall,' he says. 'It's the faces. Not her. The faces.' He takes the cord from inside his shirt, with the little key on it, and holds it a while, and does not give it. 'If she finds it,' he says, 'it'll be me. It's only me that has one.' You say it will not be him. You say it in so many words. He gives you the key as one gives away the last of something. 'Go along the wall on the left,' he says. 'Not the right. Not ever the right.'".
    Otherwise "He goes quite still, and then he is up and has put the width of the ridge between you. 'No,' he says. 'No. It's the Wall.' He is too frightened to be angry, and it makes him sound like his mother. 'I'll not say. I'll not say anything. But I shall have to tell her somebody was asking after the cellar, because they were.' He is gone down the ladder, and the lamp in the Fitter's window goes on.".
  }
  Relation th_dov_refused(group).
  // The same key, by the other way: not asked of him but taken from a gratitude. It costs nothing to the company, and costs him.
  Topic th_dov_favour with dov "Ask Dov for the spare key, as the favour he owes you" when not masked(actor) and at(dov, maskers_roof) and mk_dov_trusts(actor) and mk_dov_free(actor) and th_dov_asked(actor) and not th_crew_dov(actor) and not th_crew_alone(actor) and not th_crew_slee(actor) once {
    Says "He gives it as if you had asked him for a glass of water. 'Of course,' says Dov, and takes the cord off over his head, and puts it in your hand, and does not ask what it is for, because you are the person who sat on a wet roof with him for an hour and asked him nothing. 'Along the wall on the left,' he says. 'The right rings.'".
    On discuss { Assert th_crew_dov(actor). Assert th_have_key(actor). Assert th_bells_off(actor). Assert promiseMade(th_dov_promise). Assert th_dov_used(actor). }
  }
  Relation th_dov_used(group).

  // ── Stage three: the way in ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The roof, by the parlour skylight; the front, as a customer who does not leave; the guest, who is received.
  Relation th_was_guest(group). Relation th_on_slates(group). Relation th_have_key(group). Relation th_bells_off(group). Relation th_intruder(group). Relation th_via_guest(group).
  Relation th_seen(group). Relation th_heat_paid(group). Relation th_hidden(group).
  Thing th_skylight "the parlour skylight" on roof_parlour {
    State bolted blocking "The parlour skylight is a small hinged window set in the pitch, bolted on the inside; through the glass, far below, a stove-glow and the edge of a table.".
    State unbolted blocking "The skylight stands unbolted, a hand's breadth ajar, and the warm air coming up through it smells of plaster and kettle. The drop is the height of a tall man.".
  }
  Rule th_skylight_crewed when (th_crew_dov(party) or th_crew_slee(party)) and state(th_skylight, bolted) and (hour(clock) >= 23 or hour(clock) < 5) { Retract state(th_skylight, bolted). Assert state(th_skylight, unbolted). Assert th_on_slates(party). }
  Rule th_rebolt when state(th_skylight, unbolted) and hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 12 and not at(party, pavane_parlour) { Retract state(th_skylight, unbolted). Assert state(th_skylight, bolted). Retract th_on_slates(party). }
  Rule th_guest_ends when th_via_guest(party) and hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 12 { Retract th_via_guest(party). }
  Action th_cross_slates(actor: group, site: place) "Cross the wet slates to the Fitter's skylight, by the north end" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, maskers_roof) and privateHours() and not masked(actor) and knows(actor, th_roof_way) and not th_on_slates(actor) and not th_crew_dov(actor) and not th_crew_slee(actor).
    Time 20 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, climbing, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert th_on_slates(actor). }
    On failure { Assert th_seen(actor). Assert th_alerted(actor). }
    Result "The slates are slick and the gutters are loud, and at the north end of the pitch, where the tile is out, you go on your belly like a lizard, and the whole of the Lane is under you, all its shutters, all its faces, going on being nobody. You do not look down. You reach the skylight with your cheek against the wet glass and the stove-glow in it, and you lie there, listening, and nothing in the house has heard.".
    Otherwise "A tile goes. You hear it go the way you hear a word you cannot take back: down the pitch, over the gutter, in a long singing fall to the lane. It lands in the lamp from the Fitter's sill in a spray of white. Somewhere, a shutter. A man shouts, in the manner of the Lane, at nobody. You are lying quite flat on a roof, and every light in the lane has come on.".
  }
  Action th_lift_bolt(actor: group, site: place) "Slide a blade between sash and frame and lift the bolt-hook" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, maskers_roof) and th_on_slates(actor) and state(th_skylight, bolted).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, lockwork, dc_fair).
    On success { Retract state(th_skylight, bolted). Assert state(th_skylight, unbolted). }
    On failure { Assert th_seen(actor). Assert th_alerted(actor). }
    Result "It is not a lock; it is an idea of a lock, a hook in an eye, and the blade lifts it with the sound of a sigh. The skylight comes up a hand's breadth on its own weight. The room under it is warm.".
    Otherwise "The blade skids, and rings on the hook, once. It is a very small sound in a very large rain. You lie with the knife in your hand and count; at fifty, a window in the house below opens, and a head looks out, at the sky, and shuts it.".
  }
  Action th_drop_in(actor: group, site: place) "Let yourself down through the skylight into the Fitter's parlour" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, maskers_roof) and state(th_skylight, unbolted) and not masked(actor).
    Time 3 minutes.
    On success { Assert at(actor, pavane_parlour). Assert th_intruder(actor). }
    Result "You hang by your hands from the frame and drop. The table takes your hip. The stove is a coal in the dark, and the unfinished mask on its stand has no face to look at you with. The cellar door is in the corner, with its good lock.".
  }
  // The front: the customer who stays. Faces leave a trail: the mask worn to the booking is remembered.
  Action th_stay_behind(actor: group, mask: face, site: place) "Stay behind in the fitting-room's cupboard of blocks when the Fitter shuts for the day" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, fitting_room) and wears(actor, mask) and masked(actor) and publicHours() and hour(clock) >= 17 and knows(actor, th_routine) and not th_hidden(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 6.
    Time 20 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert th_hidden(actor). Assert th_intruder(actor). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Increase faceHeat(mask) by 2. }
    On failure { Assert th_alerted(actor). Increase faceHeat(mask) by 2. Assert at(actor, maskers_lane). }
    Result "You pay six coin for a fitting you will not attend, and say you will wait in the cupboard where the blocks are, to see which suits. She says that is irregular. She says it is, in thirty-nine years, the first time anyone has asked to wait among the faces. You stand behind a hundred plaster brows in the dark, with one of them against your cheek, and when the Fitter has put the sheet over them and put out the lamp and gone through to her stove, you are in the house, and you were never there.".
    Otherwise "She finds you in the cupboard in a minute and a half, as one finds a coat in a closet, and does not say anything at all; she puts a finger on your brow, the way one puts a finger on a place in a book, and walks you to the door. The mask you wore is, you notice, being looked at very closely. 'A rented face,' she says. 'Hask's pegs. The Annex keeps a ledger.'".
  }
  // The guest: received, bare, at her stove; and the thing taken is the thing she has given.
  Action th_guest_wait(actor: group, site: place) "Stay at the Fitter's stove past midnight, and keep her cup full" {
    Speaker pavane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, site) and at(pavane, pavane_parlour) and privateHours() and hour(clock) >= 21 and hour(clock) < 23 and not masked(actor) and mk_pavane_trust(actor) and knows(actor, th_routine) and not th_via_guest(actor).
    Time 120 minutes.
    On success { Assert th_via_guest(actor). Assert th_was_guest(actor). Assert th_bells_off(actor). }
    Result "She talks, tonight, as she has not in a long while: about her master, who cut the first Treasurer's mask she ever saw; about the winter she nearly went home. You put more in her cup than she asks. By midnight her words have slowed, and her head goes down by degrees onto her hand, as a lamp goes down when the oil is low. She is asleep in her chair with the stove ticking and the kettle on the hob. It is a quarter past twelve. There is a chain about her neck, and something small and brass on it, and her breathing is the breathing of a woman who trusts the room.".
  }
  Action th_lift_key(actor: group, site: place) "Lift the cellar key from the chain about her sleeping neck" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pavane, site) and th_via_guest(actor) and not th_have_key(actor).
    Time 3 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert th_have_key(actor). }
    On failure { Retract mk_pavane_trust(actor). Assert mk_pavane_cold(actor). Increase heat(actor) by 1. Assert th_alerted(actor). Retract th_via_guest(actor). }
    Result "The clasp is a hook and an eye, made by someone who did not expect to be robbed in her own chair. You lift the chain with two fingers, a link at a time, over her cheek; she stirs, and murmurs a word in a language you do not know. Then the key is in your palm, warm from her throat. You do not feel clever. You feel like a person who has taken something out of a hand that was open.".
    Otherwise "Her eyes are open. She has not moved, and her hand is on the chain, over yours. She looks at you for what seems like a long time, with no anger at all. 'Go home,' says Madame Pavane. 'You may let yourself out. I do not think I shall be at home to you again, and I should rather not be told why.' Her voice is perfectly even. The cup beside her has been drunk, and it was not drugged, and neither of you says that this is the worst of it.".
  }
  // Inside, the lock, and the bells.
  Action th_open_cellar_key(actor: group, site: place) "Unlock the cellar door with the key" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, pavane_parlour) and th_have_key(actor) and state(mk_cellar_lock, locked) and not mk_guiding(pavane).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Retract state(mk_cellar_lock, locked). Assert state(mk_cellar_lock, open). Assert mk_picked_open(actor). }
    Result "It turns without a sound, the oil of thirty-nine years of Dov's care in it, and the door swings in on a stair going down into a dim and level lamplight.".
  }
  Action th_pick_cellar(actor: group, site: place) "Pick the cellar door's lock" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, pavane_parlour) and not th_have_key(actor) and state(mk_cellar_lock, locked) and not mk_guiding(pavane) and not th_alerted(actor).
    Time 15 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, lockwork, dc_fair).
    On success { Retract state(mk_cellar_lock, locked). Assert state(mk_cellar_lock, open). Assert mk_picked_open(actor). }
    On failure { Assert th_seen(actor). }
    Result "A Fitter's lock is a Fitter's trade: dull, handsome, and good. It takes you a quarter of an hour, with the stove ticking at your back and the unfinished mask watching over your shoulder, and then the last pin gives and the bolt goes back, and a cold air comes up out of the dark smelling of plaster, and oil, and a great many faces.".
    Otherwise "The pin sets, and slips, and the pick rings in the lock. In the house, somewhere above you, a board moves. A voice that is perfectly awake and perfectly calm says, 'I should be much obliged if you would go away.' You go. You do not go quickly enough to be unseen.".
  }
  Action th_pick_cellar_hard(actor: group, site: place) "Pick the cellar door's lock, which has been changed since you were watched" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, pavane_parlour) and not th_have_key(actor) and state(mk_cellar_lock, locked) and not mk_guiding(pavane) and th_alerted(actor).
    Time 20 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, lockwork, dc_hard).
    On success { Retract state(mk_cellar_lock, locked). Assert state(mk_cellar_lock, open). Assert mk_picked_open(actor). }
    On failure { Assert th_seen(actor). }
    Result "She has put a second pin in it, since the night of the tile. You find the new one by feel, like a stone in a pear. The bolt goes back with a groan of a good lock that has been woken.".
