  // Four ends for each kind of casts: the Candid (who will publish), the Warden (who will use), the Cuff (the end of the
  // Wall), the shelf (put back). Not for Peck's cast: that is for Peck, and the company's own is already gone.
  Relation th_proof_vane(group). Relation th_keys_vane(group). Relation th_cast_vane(group).
  Relation th_proof_lacke(group). Relation th_keys_lacke(group). Relation th_cast_lacke(group).
  Relation th_proof_broken(group). Relation th_keys_broken(group). Relation th_cast_broken(group).
  Relation th_peck_cast(group).
  Action th_vane_proof(actor: group, site: place) "Give the Menders' row and the Registrar's cast to the Candid" {
    Speaker vane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(vane, site) and carries(actor, th_proof).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Spend th_proof from actor. Assert th_proof_vane(actor). Assert th_cast_vane(actor). }
    Result "She takes the sack as one takes a sleeping child, and looks into it, and is quiet for a moment. 'The Menders,' says Orsolya Hart. 'Of course. The nineteen, and the year-chalks.' She runs a finger along a row without touching. 'I shall not ask how. I shall publish it the day before the Drawing, in the Reading-room, on a long table, every face with its chalk. And the Registrar. Poor girl.' She looks up. 'You understand what this does. It does not give the city its Offices. It tells the city it never had any. They will not forgive that for a generation.' She does not say she will not do it.".
  }
  Action th_vane_keys(actor: group, site: place) "Give the four Offices' casts to the Candid" {
    Speaker vane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(vane, site) and carries(actor, th_keys).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Spend th_keys from actor. Assert th_keys_vane(actor). Assert th_cast_vane(actor). }
    Result "'The faces of the Offices,' says Hart, and her voice goes, for an instant, very small. 'Of the people who are the Offices. It is the thing I have wanted all my life. And I do not want it.' She lifts KEY out of its straw and looks at the face of the Warden of Locks, asleep, sixteen, and sets it back. 'I will put them on the table. Every face in Ombra will go past, and nobody will be allowed to say anyone's name, and everyone will know. That is publicity. I have never been sure that it is not simply the Concord, in a different coat.'".
  }
  Action th_lacke_proof(actor: group, site: place) "Sell the Menders' row and the Registrar's cast to the Warden of Locks, thirty coin" {
    Speaker lacke.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(lacke, site) and carries(actor, th_proof).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Spend th_proof from actor. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 30. Assert th_proof_lacke(actor). Assert th_cast_lacke(actor). Decrease heat(actor) by 1 or to nothing. }
    Result "He does not open the sack. He weighs it on his palm, as a man does who has been sold things before. 'Ah,' says Ser Corvin Lacke. 'The Mender-shelf.' He gives the word a faint distaste. 'I have been wondering how many nights it would be before somebody came to me with this. I can use it; one can always use a shelf of faces that one need not explain.' He counts out thirty. 'The Watch will be rather less interested in you by Thursday. I am a very discreet buyer. It is the whole of my trade.' He counts the coin into your palm himself, one at a time, so that you will remember whose it was.".
  }
  Action th_lacke_keys(actor: group, site: place) "Sell the four Offices' casts to the Warden of Locks, forty coin" {
    Speaker lacke.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(lacke, site) and carries(actor, th_keys).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Spend th_keys from actor. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 40. Assert th_keys_lacke(actor). Assert th_cast_lacke(actor). Decrease heat(actor) by 1 or to nothing. }
    Result "He lifts the first of them out of the straw, KEY, with his own face on it, sixteen and asleep, and looks at it for some time with a curious composure. 'I was a rather good-looking boy,' he says. 'One forgets.' He puts it back. 'Forty. And you will forgive me if I observe that this makes you the second most dangerous person in Ombra, and I the first.' He smiles. 'I should not be seen to have been of service, if I were you.'".
  }
  Action th_break_proof(actor: group, site: place) "Break the Menders' row and the Registrar's cast, and tip them into the Cuff" {
    Grave "Broken, the proof of what the Wall shows cannot be put back, and cannot be shown to anyone ever again.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, row_quay) and carries(actor, th_proof).
    Time 30 minutes.
    On success { Spend th_proof from actor. Assert th_proof_broken(actor). Assert th_cast_broken(actor). }
    Result "You break them on the edge of the quay one by one with the heel of a hammer, nineteen Menders and a girl in black wool, and the plaster goes into the Cuff in a long white slick that the current takes down toward the low islands. Nobody will ever know what was on the shelf. In an hour it will look like any other flood.".
  }
  Action th_break_keys(actor: group, site: place) "Break the four Offices' casts, and tip them into the Cuff" {
    Grave "Broken, the faces the Offices are cut to are gone, and with them the means to fit any other mask.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, row_quay) and carries(actor, th_keys).
    Time 20 minutes.
    On success { Spend th_keys from actor. Assert th_keys_broken(actor). Assert th_cast_broken(actor). }
    Result "KEY goes first, since it is on top. Then POUND, which is stolid; SERENE, which does not seem to mind; and WHITE, which you hold a moment longer than the others, and then do not. The Cuff is a milky brown by the end of it. Four people in Ombra will have a very quiet night, and will not know why.".
  }
  Action th_back_proof(actor: group, site: place) "Put the Menders' row and the Registrar's cast back on their shelves" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, cast_cellar) and carries(actor, th_proof) and not mk_guiding(pavane) and (th_intruder(actor) or th_via_guest(actor)).
    Time 20 minutes.
    On success { Spend th_proof from actor. Retract th_took_proof(actor). Assert th_cast_back(actor). Retract th_took_any(actor). }
    Result "You put them back in their places, a face at a time, in the order they came. The last is the girl in black wool. You do not tie the cloth. It is not the sort of thing one pins, as it was; it is something one lays.".
  }
  Action th_back_keys(actor: group, site: place) "Put the four Offices' casts back on their rack" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, cast_cellar) and carries(actor, th_keys) and not mk_guiding(pavane) and (th_intruder(actor) or th_via_guest(actor)).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Spend th_keys from actor. Retract th_took_keys(actor). Assert th_cast_back(actor). Retract th_took_any(actor). }
    Result "KEY, POUND, SERENE, WHITE, back on their hooks with their brass tags. They look exactly as they did. Only the straw is flattened on one side, where a hand held them.".
  }
  Topic th_peck_give with peck "Give Peck his own cast, from the shelf of the Named" when carries(actor, th_owed_cast) and not th_peck_cast(actor) once {
    Says "He does not take it. He looks at it in your hands, a boy of sixteen with a mouth ready to laugh, and his own mouth does something very slowly. 'I have not seen him,' says Absalom Peck, 'in thirty-one years. They don't let you. They turn it to the wall.' He puts out one finger, and touches the cheekbone, as one touches the face of a sleeping child. 'He was a good boy. He didn't know. Nobody had told him what the white and gold would do. I've been very angry with him.' He takes it, at last, in both hands, and holds it in his lap with the wet face down against his coat. 'There,' he says to it. 'There, there. It's all right. I'm here.'".
    On discuss { Spend th_owed_cast from actor. Assert th_peck_cast(actor). }
  }

  // ── Ombra's own end of it: what the Warden does, and what the Hands do ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule th_squeezes_taken when th_took_any(party) and th_crew_slee(party) and not th_cut_waived(party) and not th_hands_squeezed(party) { Assert th_hands_squeezed(party). }
  Rule th_hands_swap when th_hands_squeezed(party) and not th_squeezes_back(party) and swapNight() and not th_swap_said(party) once says "On the night of the Swap, in four squares, a Warden of Locks in a rented Key buys drinks for a whole tavern with the Watch's own purse, and an Assessor of Weights is seen to give away a pound of bread, free, in the rain. Somebody has been wearing faces that fit rather too well. By midnight the Key's name in the Row is a thing the Row will not say." { Assert th_swap_said(party). Increase faceHeat(face_key) by 2. Increase faceHeat(face_pound) by 2. }
  Relation th_swap_said(group).
  Rule th_lacke_betrays when named(lacke) and (th_proof_lacke(party) or th_keys_lacke(party)) and not th_betrayed(party) once says "The Warden's clerk has put the Fitter's cellar on a paper in the Watch-house, with a description. It is very exact. It has your nose." { Assert th_betrayed(party). Increase heat(party) by 3. }
  Relation th_betrayed(group).

  // ── At the Drawing: the casts to the room, or the fire ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Query th_loot_held(a: group) means carries(a, th_proof) or carries(a, th_keys).
  Rule th_hand_ready when th_took_any(party) and (th_loot_held(party) or th_cast_vane(party) or th_cast_lacke(party)) and not handReady(party, hand_cast) { Assert handReady(party, hand_cast). }
  Rule th_hand_gone when handReady(party, hand_cast) and not handPlayed(party, hand_cast) and not th_loot_held(party) and not th_cast_vane(party) and not th_cast_lacke(party) { Retract handReady(party, hand_cast). }
  Rule th_arc_begun when (th_cased(party) or th_crew_slee(party) or th_crew_dov(party) or th_crew_alone(party)) and not arcBegun(party, hand_cast) { Assert arcBegun(party, hand_cast). }
  Relation th_cast_room(group). Relation th_cast_fire(group). Relation th_lacke_used(group). Relation th_vane_read(group).
  Action th_draw_room_proof(actor: group, site: place) "Set the Menders' row and the Registrar's cast down before the room" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and carries(actor, th_proof).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Spend th_proof from actor. Assert th_cast_room(actor). Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_cast). }
    Result "You put the sack on the Urn Hall's floor in the light of the braziers, and lift the faces out one at a time, and stand them on the stones in a row. Somebody in the crowd says, 'That is Mender Wickes of Lamp Street,' and somebody else, 'And that is the Treasurer, I danced with her at a wedding,' and then the hall begins to understand that it is looking at its own shelf. There is no sound at all; and then there is one.".
  }
  Action th_draw_room_keys(actor: group, site: place) "Set the four Offices' casts down before the room" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and carries(actor, th_keys).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Spend th_keys from actor. Assert th_cast_room(actor). Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_cast). }
    Result "KEY, POUND, SERENE, WHITE, in their straw, set down in the light of the braziers on the Urn Hall floor, four people asleep. Somebody in the crowd has the sense not to say a name. Everybody is looking at four faces that they have each of them stood next to, in the street, at the baker's, in the ferry, for a year. The faces are not looking at anyone. That is the horror of them; they are only young.".
  }
  Action th_draw_fire_proof(actor: group, site: place) "Put the Menders' row and the Registrar's cast into the Urn Hall's brazier" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and carries(actor, th_proof).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Spend th_proof from actor. Assert th_cast_fire(actor). Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_cast). }
    Result "Plaster does not burn; it calcines. It goes in the brazier one face at a time and sits in the coals for a long moment, quite unchanged, and then the water in it goes out with a hiss and it falls to a white dust, the Menders and the Registrar together, with a sound like a clearing of the throat. Somebody in the crowd, who has no idea what they are seeing, takes off their mask to wipe their eyes.".
  }
  Action th_draw_fire_keys(actor: group, site: place) "Put the four Offices' casts into the Urn Hall's brazier" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and carries(actor, th_keys).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Spend th_keys from actor. Assert th_cast_fire(actor). Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_cast). }
    Result "They go in one at a time, KEY, POUND, SERENE, WHITE, and sit in the coals, and the water in them goes out with a long dry hiss, and they fall to dust. Nobody in the hall knows what was burnt. Four people in it, among the masks, put their hands to their faces at the same moment, and do not know why.".
  }
  Action th_draw_vane(actor: group, site: place) "Stand beside the Candid while she opens the sack" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and th_cast_vane(actor) and not th_vane_read(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert th_vane_read(actor). Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_cast). }
    Result "She is at the foot of the Urn with the sack and a lamp, in a plain brown coat, and she does not make a speech. She opens it, and lays the faces out on the Urn Hall steps in the order of their years, and says, to nobody and everybody: 'These are the faces you have been governed by.' She does not say a name. She does not need to. A woman in the front row has put her hand over her mouth.".
  }
  Action th_draw_lacke(actor: group, site: place) "Stand by while the Warden's clerks hand round the Offices' faces" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and th_cast_lacke(actor) and not th_lacke_used(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert th_lacke_used(actor). Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_cast). }
    Result "You are standing at the edge of the light when the lots are read, and you hear, and so do a good many others, the name of the Treasurer, and the Warden of Locks' own, and the Assessor's, in the voice of the Registrar's palm-card, and you notice what nobody else does, that each of the four people drawn is a face a Fitter in Maskers' Lane would have cut a mask to this morning. Ser Lacke, across the hall, in the Key, does not look at you. He is smiling at the ceiling.".
  }

  // ── Milestones ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Milestone th_m_cased "cased the Fitter's house" worth 25 when th_cased(party).
  Milestone th_m_crew "chose who would stand in the cellar with you" worth 25 when th_crew_dov(party) or th_crew_slee(party) or th_crew_alone(party).
  Milestone th_m_took "took from the Wall of Faces" worth 75 when th_took_any(party).
  Milestone th_m_clean "came out of the Fitter's house unseen" worth 50 when th_took_any(party) and not th_seen(party) and not th_intruder(party) and not at(party, cast_cellar) and not at(party, pavane_parlour).
  Milestone th_m_hands "was given a name in the Many Hands" worth 50 when th_hands_name(party).
  Milestone th_m_fence "put the casts of the Wall where they would be used" worth 75 when th_cast_vane(party) or th_cast_lacke(party) or th_cast_broken(party) or th_peck_cast(party).
  Milestone th_m_back "went back to the Fitter" worth 50 when th_confessed(party).
  Milestone th_m_hand "played the casts of the Wall at the Drawing" worth 100 when handPlayed(party, hand_cast).

  // ── The news ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule th_fate_slee_paid when newsHour() and th_crew_slee(party) and th_hands_name(party) once says "Of Obadiah Slee: he has been seen at the Row quay in a clean Magpie's domino, weighing nothing, which is as near as he comes to happiness. The Hands say a Pale Sparrow flew over the Fitter's roof in the Novena and left no feather. Nobody has told the Watch, as you were not to." { }
  Rule th_fate_slee_squeezed when newsHour() and th_hands_squeezed(party) and not th_squeezes_back(party) once says "Of the Many Hands: they hold, in a flat parcel in the lining of a crate, the faces of the Offices, in squeezes, and are in no hurry. A Key-mask that fits has been seen, on the Row, once, at midnight, opening a door that was the Warden's own. Slee says he did not see it. He is a very honest liar." { }
  Rule th_fate_slee_secret when newsHour() and th_slee_secret_given(party) once says "Of Obadiah Slee: he has stopped paying the Warden of Locks his two coin on every lock, on the ground that a man who skims has no standing to tax. The Hands have been told why. They have not been told by whom. It has been a very good week for the Row's locksmiths." { }
  Rule th_fate_slee_nothing when newsHour() and not th_crew_slee(party) and knows(party, th_slee_name) once says "Of Obadiah Slee: he is at his barrow in Maskers' Lane, with his scale, weighing a Gull against a brass weight, and the Gull goes up." { }
  Rule th_fate_dov_used when newsHour() and th_dov_failed(party) and th_dov_used(party) and not mk_maule_took_dov(party) and not th_confessed(party) once says "Of Dov Ashe: he gave the key as one gives a glass of water, and asked no questions, and was put out of the Fitter's house for it with his things in a pillowcase. He has never been told why the person he was kind to was not a friend. He has gone to his mother's, in the Drip, with his hands in his pockets, and has not, they say, been up on a roof since." { }
  Rule th_fate_dov_blamed when newsHour() and th_dov_failed(party) and not th_dov_used(party) and not mk_maule_took_dov(party) and not th_confessed(party) once says "Of Dov Ashe: he said nothing, for four days, about the key. On the fifth, somebody in the Lane remarked that a boy who has been put out of a Fitter's house for the loss of a key is a boy who has been told what he is. He has gone to his mother's, in the Drip, with his hands in his pockets." { }
  Rule th_fate_dov_clear when newsHour() and th_confessed(party) and th_crew_dov(party) once says "Of Dov Ashe: he is at his broom in the Fitter's fitting-room, and has been told, in the Fitter's kindest voice, that a boy who lends a key to a person who is not a thief is a boy who does not yet know whom to trust. It is a learning. It is the beginning of one." { }
  Rule th_fate_wall_back when newsHour() and th_cast_back(party) once says "Of the Wall of Faces: it stands where it stood. Somebody has been at the Menders' shelf; the Fitter says nothing of it, and the Watch has not been told, and the black wool has been laid, not pinned, over the face on the shelf of Lamps." { }
  Rule th_fate_wall_vane when newsHour() and th_proof_vane(party) and not th_cast_back(party) once says "Of the Wall of Faces: its Menders are on a long table in the Candid Reading-room, with the year-chalks showing, and the Reading-room has not closed since the Novena. The Fitter has put up her shutters. The Wall's gaps are filled with grey blanks, which the Lane says look like teeth." { }
  Rule th_fate_wall_vane_keys when newsHour() and th_keys_vane(party) and not th_cast_back(party) once says "Of the Offices' casts: four faces lie in straw in the Candid Reading-room, with their brass tags, and the people of Ombra go past them in a line, in their masks, with their eyes carefully down. Nobody has said a name. It is generally agreed that it was the quietest thing the Candid has ever done." { }
  Rule th_fate_wall_lacke when newsHour() and th_cast_lacke(party) and not th_cast_back(party) once says "Of the Wall of Faces: the Warden of Locks has a cellar of his own now, which was not in the plans, and a Fitter he is on very good terms with, in the Lane, whose name nobody will say. The Wall has gaps. Nobody has been told." { }
  Rule th_fate_wall_broken when newsHour() and th_proof_broken(party) and not th_cast_back(party) and not th_hands_squeezed(party) once says "Of the Wall of Faces: the shelf of Menders is a row of grey blanks, and the Fitter has not replaced the faces, since it is a thing one cannot do. Nobody in Ombra can now say, with plaster, who it was that was trusted with the Offices. Some people are quite relieved." { }
  Rule th_fate_keys_broken when newsHour() and th_keys_broken(party) and not th_cast_back(party) once says "Of the Offices' casts: they are in the Cuff, off the low islands, in a white slick that has long since spread. The Fitter will cut the Offices for the Drawing to measure, as she has always done; the faces she measures them to are no longer anywhere but on the faces." { }
  Rule th_fate_wall_room when newsHour() and th_cast_room(party) once says "Of the Wall of Faces: for one night its faces stood on the floor of the Urn Hall, and Ombra read them. It has not spoken of it since, as is its way; but every shutter in the Lane is down by the Ninth Bell, and the Fitter has been seen at the mouth of the cellar stair, with a lamp, standing as a woman stands who is waiting to be asked a question." { }
  Rule th_fate_wall_fire when newsHour() and th_cast_fire(party) once says "Of the Wall of Faces: some of it went into the Urn Hall's brazier on the ninth night, and rose as white dust, and nobody in the hall knew what they had been watching. The Fitter, who did, has begun a new Wall, a face at a time, by hand, from nothing; it will take her thirty years, and she says she does not mind." { }
  Rule th_fate_vane_read when newsHour() and th_vane_read(party) once says "Of Orsolya Hart: she opened the sack at the foot of the Urn in a plain brown coat and said nine words, and has not said a tenth. The faces she showed were, by morning, the only thing in Ombra that anyone could think about, and none of them were named." { }
  Rule th_fate_lacke_used when newsHour() and th_lacke_used(party) once says "Of the Offices drawn: the Treasurer, the Warden, the Assessor and the Serene are four people whom a Fitter would have cut a mask to this morning. The Warden of Locks has been seen to smile at a ceiling." { }
  Rule th_fate_wall_untouched when newsHour() and not th_took_any(party) and not th_cast_back(party) and knows(party, th_routine) once says "Of the Wall of Faces: nobody has been at it. A Fitter's lock was looked at, once, in the Novena, by somebody, and left alone." { }
  Rule th_fate_peck when newsHour() and th_peck_cast(party) once says "Of Absalom Peck: he has a face on his blanket, a boy's, sixteen, ready to laugh, and sits with it most evenings. He says it is not the same as being forgiven. It is, he says, a thing he can look at." { }
  Rule th_fate_pavane_found when newsHour() and th_found(party) and not th_confessed(party) and not th_pavane_hurt(party) once says "Of Madame Pavane: she knows that there was a thief, and not who, and has added a second lock, and a second bell-line, and a very large dog, which is a thing the Fitter's house has never kept. She cuts the Offices without a word, and in the evening she sits with the Wall, in the lamp, among the gaps." { }
  Rule th_fate_pavane_guest when newsHour() and th_pavane_hurt(party) once says "Of Madame Pavane: she has not been seen at her stove at night since the Novena, and the lamp on the sill of the fitting-room is not lit. The Lane say she has taken to bolting the door at the Ninth Bell, as a householder does. She has been in the Lane a long time, and had thought, once, that she was not a householder." { }
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/vane.kyr:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The Candid ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Orsolya Hart, who has not worn a mask in eleven years, and whose Reading-room on Counting Row is the one place in
  // Ombra where a bare face is spoken to by day. She leads the Candid, a few hundred who go unmasked by vow and are
  // despised for it; and she is right about nearly everything except what a name is for. She wants the Book of Faces read
  // aloud at the Drawing. She is moved not by evidence but by being refused, as an equal, by someone who stays.
  Observe candid_scene at candid_room when publicHours() "A long room over a printer's, with a hand-press at one end that is never still and a table at the other covered in galleys that are all, if you look, the same page. A hundred bare faces on the wall in pencil, each with a number and no name. The Candid do not hide in here. They work in the open and look at each other: it is the oddest thing in the whole of Ombra, and you catch yourself, twice, looking away from someone only to be polite.".
  Observe candid_night at candid_room when privateHours() "At night the press is covered and the room has the look of a house where a meeting has just broken up. Somebody has left a lamp lit under a drawing of a face with its mask in its hand.".
  Person vane "Orsolya Hart" at candid_room {
    Role "the Candid, who has not worn a mask in eleven years".
    Ancestry human. Calling bard. Level 5. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner proud.
    Greets "A tall woman in a grey coat, with ink to her elbows and not so much as a veil, looks up from the press and sees you as no one has seen you since you came down the delta road: all at once, from the top of your head. 'A Bare,' she says. 'And you came in at the front. Sit.' Her face is long and plain and furious and kind, and it has no mask on it, and it has been rained on, and slapped, and spat on, and nothing has made it look away. 'I am Orsolya Hart,' she says, 'and it is a crime to say so. I shall go on saying it.'".
    Greets again "'Bare,' says Orsolya Hart, and moves a galley so you can sit.".
  }
  Relation vaneListened(group). Relation vaneBookWanted(group). Relation vaneDoubts(group). Relation vaneHolds(group). Relation vaneRefused(group).
  Topic vane_creed with vane "Ask what the Candid want" when true once {
    Says "'A face is a promise,' says Orsolya Hart. 'It says: it is I who am standing here and you may hold me to it. The Concord took it away. We have lived three hundred years in a city where nobody can be held to anything. The Treasurer has no name and so the sluice has no keeper. The Warden has no name and so the tax has no thief.' She taps the galley. 'I am not asking for a feud. I am asking for a name on a lock.'".
    On discuss { Assert vaneListened(actor). }
  }
  Topic vane_book with vane "Ask what she means to do with the Book" when vaneListened(actor) once {
    Says "'The Registrar is dead and the Book is gone, and the Drawing will be read on the ninth night by somebody,' she says. 'When I have the Book, I shall read it aloud in the Urn Hall, every name, every year, before a Registrar sits down. And the city will know who has been its masks.' She does not blink. 'I do not want to hurt them. I want them to be a little less safe. It is not the same.'".
    On discuss { Assert vaneBookWanted(actor). }
  }
  Topic vane_who with vane "Ask her why she has no mask" when vaneListened(actor) and privateHours() once {
    Says "'I was the Serene,' she says, after a while, 'four years ago.' She has the look of a woman making herself go over a wall. 'I wore it a year. In the year, nobody said a thing to me that was not to the Serene. At the end of it I was Spent, and went home, and nobody in my street would speak to a person who had been it; and nobody could say why, since nobody could say I had been.' She turns a galley over. 'I decided I would rather be spat on by people who could name me.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, vane_was_serene). }
  }
  Discovery vane_was_serene "Orsolya Hart, the Candid, was the Serene four years ago, and has gone unmasked ever since: she would rather be spat on by people who can name her than be thanked by nobody.".
  // Giving her the Book, or not. The Book itself is the post.kyr's find.
  Action give_vane_book(actor: group, site: place) "Give Orsolya Hart the Book of Faces" {
    Speaker vane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(vane, site) and carries(actor, book_of_faces) and not vaneHolds(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert vaneHolds(actor). Spend book_of_faces from actor. Assert at(book_of_faces, candid_room). }
    Result "She takes it in both hands and does not open it. 'Ninety years of names,' she says, and her face does something quite complicated. 'I have wanted to hold this since I was nineteen.' Then she does open it, at random, and reads a line, and says, very quietly, 'Oh, they are so small.'".
  }
  // The second beat. A person who has been agreed with for eleven years is moved by a refusal that stays in the room.
  Action refuse_vane(actor: group, site: place) "Tell her, to her face, that you will not give her the Book, and stay to hear her answer" {
    Speaker vane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(vane, site) and vaneBookWanted(actor) and not vaneRefused(actor) and not vaneHolds(actor).
    Time 20.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert vaneRefused(actor). Assert vaneDoubts(actor). }
    On failure { Assert vaneRefused(actor). Increase heat(actor) by 1. }
    Result "She goes still. For eleven years the masks have said no and the Candid have said yes, and you are neither, and you have not left. 'You are afraid I shall hurt the Spent,' she says at last. 'I am afraid of that too, God knows.' A silence. 'Tell me what you would have read, and what not.' She takes a pencil. It is the first time she has asked.".
    Otherwise "She says, with great courtesy, that she did not know a Bare had opinions, and rises, and has the press stopped for the first time in a month so that the whole room can hear you go.".
  }
  Action vane_consent(actor: group, site: place) "Persuade her to read only the names of the Spent who consent" {
    Speaker vane.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(vane, site) and vaneDoubts(actor) and not vaneHolds(actor) and not vane_consents(actor).
    Time 20.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert vane_consents(actor). }
    Result "'All right,' says Orsolya Hart. 'Names that are given. Not names that are taken.' She writes it on the wall in pencil, over the hundred bare faces, in a hand that has been waiting a long time to write it. 'And if nobody consents?' 'Then you will have a silence,' you say, 'and the city will have to learn to stand in it.' She laughs, which is not a thing she does.".
    Otherwise "'I will think about it,' she says, in a voice that has finished thinking.".
  }
  Relation vane_consents(group).
  Topic vane_bare_day with vane "Ask whether a Bare may rest here by day" when publicHours() once {
    Says "'You may rest here, read here, ask here, and be asked,' she says. 'You are the one person in the city who will not be looked through in this room.' She finds a stool and does not apologise for it. 'It is the only thing I can offer a stranger that the Concord does not.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/warrant.ky:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The Stranger's Warrant ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Concord's seventy-first article: when the city is at an impasse it forbids itself to resolve, it may hire a
  // Bare to see what no mask may see. Sergeant Vail of the Masked Watch has it in her glove. She meets the Bare in
  // Strangers' Square on the first morning, and from the first sentence she will not say her own name.
  Kind warrant_kind "the Stranger's Warrant" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "A strip of grey paper with a bare oval stamped on it in white wax, and under the oval, in a clerk's round hand, the seventy-first article of the Concord: THE CONCORD MAY HIRE A STRANGER TO LOOK. It does not say what the stranger is to say.".
  Item warrant_paper "the Stranger's Warrant" is warrant_kind at offstage.
  Discovery warrant_terms "The Stranger's Warrant lets a Bare look at what no mask may: a masked body, a sealed room, a face under a mask. It does not make anyone speak, and it is suspended when the Watch's patience (three marks of heat) runs out.".
  Discovery vail_name "The sergeant of the Masked Watch who hired you is Ottoline Vail.".

  Person vail "a sergeant of the Masked Watch" at gate_square {
    Role "a sergeant of the Masked Watch, in the black hound-domino" when not knows(party, vail_name).
    Role "Sergeant Ottoline Vail of the Masked Watch" when knows(party, vail_name).
    Known as "a sergeant of the Masked Watch" when not knows(party, vail_name).
    Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 4. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    Greets "A woman in the black hound-domino of the Masked Watch stands on the wet flags at the head of the Customs Steps with her hands behind her, as the Watch does, and does not look at you as the others come up past her. The rain makes a small music on her mask. When the last of the Bare has gone by she turns and looks at you, and only you. 'You,' she says. 'Bare. Fair-sized, no mask, no name the city can hear. Good.' It does not sound like a compliment. 'I am the Watch. I will not tell you what else I am. The Watch has a use for a stranger, if you have a minute and no opinion of us.'".
    Greets again "'Bare,' says the Watch, and nods, which from the Watch is a sentence.".
  }
  // By day the sergeant is at the Square till she has her stranger; after, at the Gatehouse by day and in the Chapel at
  // dusk, and where she is by night is her own business (but she opens the door of the Gatehouse to a bare knock).
  Rule vail_square when begun() and not warrantHeld(party) and not warrantRefused(party) and not at(vail, gate_square) { Assert at(vail, gate_square). }
  Rule vail_hall when (warrantHeld(party) or warrantRefused(party)) and publicHours() and not at(vail, gate_hall) { Assert at(vail, gate_hall). }
  Rule vail_night when (warrantHeld(party) or warrantRefused(party)) and privateHours() and not at(vail, gate_hall) { Assert at(vail, gate_hall). }
  Relation warrantRefused(group).
  Measure vailTrust(group).

  // The first speeches. Each teaches a rule of the city by showing it.
  Topic vail_use with vail "Ask what use the Watch has for a stranger" when not warrantHeld(actor) and not warrantRefused(actor) once {
    Says "'The Registrar of Ombra is dead,' says the Watch, 'in the bier-room of the Chapel of the Bare Face, in the white mask of her office, and the Book of Faces is not on its lectern.' She says it without any weight at all, the way a clerk reads out a bridge toll. 'A Registrar's mask may be lifted by her successor-designate and nobody else, and the successor-designate is in the Book. So nobody may lawfully say who is dead. Nobody may say the Office is vacant. In nine days the Drawing must be read by a Registrar, and if it is not, every Office in this city dissolves at midnight, being only masks.' She turns her head very slightly. 'The seventy-first article says the Concord may hire a stranger to look. Look.' She tips her head down the Cuff, towards a bell being rung for no one in particular. 'Start where she lies. You will find the Chapel by the people not looking at it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, marrick_dead). Assert knows(actor, warrant_terms). }
  }
  Topic vail_pay with vail "Ask what the Warrant pays" when not warrantHeld(actor) and not warrantRefused(actor) once {
    Says "'Lodging at the Hospice, nine days, under Mother Tibb. Five coin now.' She counts it onto the strip of paper. 'At the end, if there is an end, the Concord offers the Bare who served a face of their own. A trade. A place in the next Urn.' She might be reading it off the inside of her mask. 'Sixty-two years, no one has taken it. The last one went home. Noted.'".
    On discuss { Assert faceOffered(actor). }
  }
  Topic vail_why with vail "Ask why a Bare, and why you" when not warrantHeld(actor) and not warrantRefused(actor) once {
    Says "'Why a Bare: because every other face in this city is a person who might be Named for what they saw.' The rain ticks on the hound's black brow. 'Why you: I was told to take the first who came off the road after the Third Bell and could stand up.' A very small pause. 'I was told it would not matter who.' You have the distinct impression that she was told a great deal more than that, and does not agree with it.".
  }
  Action take_warrant(actor: group, site: place) "Take the Stranger's Warrant" {
    Speaker vail.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(vail, site) and not warrantHeld(actor) and knows(actor, marrick_dead).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert warrantHeld(actor). Assert knows(actor, warrant_terms). Give warrant_paper to actor. Give rounds_ledger to actor. Give marrick_letter to actor. Assert ledgerHeld(actor). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Assert met(vail). }
    Result "She puts a strip of grey paper into your hand, with five coin under it, and a sealed packet under that, and closes your fingers over the lot. 'The Warrant. You are the Concord's eyes. You are not its mouth. If it comes to saying, I will say for you, or the Chaplain will.' She takes her hand away. 'Do not lift a mask in the street. There is a bier-room for that.'".
  }
  Action refuse_warrant(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the sergeant that you will not be the Concord's eyes" {
    Speaker vail.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(vail, site) and not warrantHeld(actor) and not warrantRefused(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert warrantRefused(actor). }
    Result "'Then you are only a Bare,' says the Watch, without any heat at all, 'and the Hospice has nine beds.' She turns her face back to the road. 'The Warrant stays where I put it, in my glove, until the third day. It is a very long way to Chapel Island if one has to go without it.'".
  }
  // A refusal can be mended for two days.
  Action take_warrant_late(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the sergeant for the Warrant after all" {
    Speaker vail.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(vail, site) and warrantRefused(actor) and not warrantHeld(actor) and day(clock) <= 3.
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract warrantRefused(actor). Assert warrantHeld(actor). Give warrant_paper to actor. Give rounds_ledger to actor. Give marrick_letter to actor. Assert ledgerHeld(actor). Assert knows(actor, warrant_terms). }
    Result "'Third day,' says the Watch, and gives it to you, with no comment, and no five coin.".
  }

  // After the Warrant. Her trust is a measure: the Watch's help is bought with candour, not with coin.
  Topic vail_ledger with vail "Ask about the sealed packet" when warrantHeld(actor) and not knows(actor, rounds_known) once {
    Says "'I have not read it.' It is the first thing she has said that sounds like hers. 'Her instruction was the Watch should give it to the Bare who took the Warrant, and nobody else, and not open it. I have a hand and a Warrant of my own, and I have done as the instruction said.' A beat. 'She was a person who left good instructions.'".
  }
  Topic vail_name_ask with vail "Ask her what she is called" when warrantHeld(actor) and not knows(actor, vail_name) and privateHours() and vailTrust(actor) >= 2 once {
    Says "She has taken the hound-domino off, at last, in the Gatehouse after the Ninth Bell, and put it on the table, and it looks smaller there. A square, closed face, fortyish, a scar through one eyebrow. 'Vail,' she says. 'Ottoline. It is a very long time since I have said it to someone who could not repeat it.' She looks at you, and then, with a difficulty you can see, away. 'You may be the only person in Ombra I can say it to.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, vail_name). Increase vailTrust(actor) by 1. }
  }
  Topic vail_candour with vail "Tell the Watch honestly what you have found, and what you have not" when warrantHeld(actor) and (knows(actor, pip_saw) or knows(actor, lacke_taxed) or knows(actor, pell_hid_book) or knows(actor, serene_saw)) and not vailTold(actor) once {
    Says "She listens in the Gatehouse with her mask in her lap, which is how you know it is serious. When you have done she turns the mask in her lap a quarter-turn, and back. 'If I take that to the Watch-house they will say I asked a Bare to Unface a Warden,' she says. 'So I have not heard it.' She puts the mask back on. 'But I know where to stand on the ninth night, now. That is not nothing.'".
    On discuss { Assert vailTold(actor). Increase vailTrust(actor) by 1. }
  }
  Relation vailTold(group).
  Action vail_confide(actor: group, site: place) "Sit with the sergeant in the Gatehouse after the Ninth Bell, and say nothing in particular" {
    Speaker vail.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(vail, site) and warrantHeld(actor) and privateHours() and not vailSat(actor).
    Time 60.
    On success { Assert vailSat(actor). Increase vailTrust(actor) by 1. }
    Result "She does not take the mask off and you do not ask her to. At the Tenth Bell she says that the Hospice kettle is better than the Watch-house one, and you drink from it in silence, and when you go she says, to the door, 'Thank you for not being clever.'".
  }
  Relation vailSat(group).
  Observe gate_hall_scene at gate_hall when publicHours() "A long low hall with a counter down one side and a stove at the end, smelling of wet wool, lamp-oil and the paper of a very great many forms. On the wall behind the counter is a board of pegs and on each peg a black hound-domino, one for each of the Watch's twenty, and nineteen of them are always out in the rain. A grille at the end of the counter says BARE: PLEASE WAIT.".
  Observe gate_hall_night at gate_hall when privateHours() "The Gatehouse at night is a stove and a lamp and the pegs of hound-dominoes, all but one empty. The rain has stopped talking on the roof and gone to muttering. Somebody has left a kettle on the stove that is not quite boiling.".

  // A Bare at the Gate with no Warrant has nothing in particular to do there but wait: the Watch, being the Watch, notes it.
  Observe vail_waiting at gate_square when begun() and not warrantHeld(party) and not warrantRefused(party) and at(vail, gate_square) "At the head of the Customs Steps the sergeant of the Watch is still standing with her hands behind her, as the rain runs off the brim of the hound's brow, waiting for you to finish looking at the city.".
}

data/adventures/book-of-faces/warrior.ky:
Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── The Gauntlet ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Duelling Stair of Quiet Hill is ninety-nine steps in nine flights, with a landing at the top of each and a
  // Second on every landing. The Seconds' Guild (the Old Names' hired swords, who go bare-faced by oath, because a
  // Second signs his blows) holds that a champion is made by what they refuse, so each landing asks one question of a
  // blade and takes a company's answer as the answer. What the answers add up to is the company's creed on the Stair:
  // a sword for hire (the Hireling), a shield for the unarmed (the Defender) or one that breaks what binds (the
  // Breaker), and the Captain at the head of the Stair says which, at the end, and asks what it refuses.
  // A company with no blade to answer with (nobody in it of the warrior's calling) is let up as the weather is, and
  // can finish nothing but the climb; the water-gate and the Terrace are the other way up and need no answer at all.

  Relation wr_post(group, place). Relation wr_landing(place). Relation wr_counted(group).
  // What the company answered, landing by landing: the creed is whichever of these is the most.
  Measure wr_hire(group). Measure wr_defend(group). Measure wr_break(group). Measure wr_height(group).
  Relation wr_blooded(group).
  Relation wr_sworn(group). Relation wr_hireling(group). Relation wr_defender(group). Relation wr_breaker(group). Relation wr_plain(group).
  Relation wr_asked(group). Relation wr_bout(group, group). Relation wr_carried(group).
  Hazard wr_bruise "A Second's fist, or the flat of a blade" means "Deal (1d3) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (11).".
  // Three falls on the Stair in one climb is the Guild's count: whoever has taken them is carried down and sent to the bench.
  Measure wr_falls(group).

  // ── The landings ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place wr_l1 "the landing of the Open Hand" is room within duelling_stair at 0, 9 outdoors.
  Place wr_l2 "the landing of the Door" is room within duelling_stair at 0, 8 outdoors.
  Place wr_l3 "the landing of the Fool" is room within duelling_stair at 0, 7 outdoors.
  Place wr_l4 "the landing of the Ledger" is room within duelling_stair at 0, 6 outdoors.
  Place wr_l5 "the landing of the Yielding" is room within duelling_stair at 0, 5 outdoors.
  Place wr_l6 "the landing of the Veil" is room within duelling_stair at 0, 4 outdoors.
  Place wr_l7 "the landing of the Brother" is room within duelling_stair at 0, 3 outdoors.
  Place wr_l8 "the landing of the Lamp" is room within duelling_stair at 0, 2 outdoors.
  Place wr_l9 "the landing of the Captain" is room within duelling_stair at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Passage wr_f1 "the first flight of the Stair" is steps between hill_foot and wr_l1 taking 3 minutes.
  Passage wr_f2 "the second flight" is steps between wr_l1 and wr_l2 taking 3 minutes.
  Passage wr_f3 "the third flight" is steps between wr_l2 and wr_l3 taking 3 minutes.
  Passage wr_f4 "the fourth flight" is steps between wr_l3 and wr_l4 taking 3 minutes.
  Passage wr_f5 "the fifth flight" is steps between wr_l4 and wr_l5 taking 3 minutes.
  Passage wr_f6 "the sixth flight" is steps between wr_l5 and wr_l6 taking 3 minutes.
  Passage wr_f7 "the seventh flight" is steps between wr_l6 and wr_l7 taking 3 minutes.
  Passage wr_f8 "the eighth flight" is steps between wr_l7 and wr_l8 taking 3 minutes.
  Passage wr_f9 "the ninth flight" is steps between wr_l8 and wr_l9 taking 3 minutes.
  Passage wr_f10 "the last of the Stair" is steps between wr_l9 and stair_top taking 3 minutes.
  Initially Assert wr_landing(wr_l1). Initially Assert wr_landing(wr_l2). Initially Assert wr_landing(wr_l3).
  Initially Assert wr_landing(wr_l4). Initially Assert wr_landing(wr_l5). Initially Assert wr_landing(wr_l6).
  Initially Assert wr_landing(wr_l7). Initially Assert wr_landing(wr_l8). Initially Assert wr_landing(wr_l9).

  Observe wr_stair_foot at hill_foot when true "Under the Hill the Duelling Stair goes up out of a stone yard like a throat, ninety-nine steps, with a landing at every eleventh and the rain coming down them in a sheet. A board by the bottom step lists what is not allowed on it: umbrellas, bargaining, and the word *quits*.".
  Observe wr_stair_foot_dark at hill_foot when dark() "At night the Stair is lit only at its landings, nine small yellow squares one above another, with a shadow standing in each.".
  Observe wr_dark_landing at ?p when wr_landing(?p) and dark() "The lamp on the wall is the only light, and the rain falls through it in lines.".
  Observe wr_l1_scene at wr_l1 when true "The first landing is a stone shelf the width of a cart, roofed with nothing, with an iron rack on the wall for steel and a bucket by the rack. The rain has worn a dish in the paving where thirty generations of champions have stood to be asked the same thing.".
  Observe wr_l2_scene at wr_l2 when true "The second landing has a door in its wall, a narrow door with the Guild's iron ring on it, and a step down in front of it that is the only part of the Stair anybody ever sweeps. The rest is wet stone, and the sound of two men not quite whispering behind the door.".
  Observe wr_l3_scene at wr_l3 when true "On the third landing there is a smell of boiled sweets. A fool's cap with three bells hangs from the lamp-bracket, and on the top step, with her chin on a wooden sword, a girl of about seven sits and watches the stair below with the patience of someone who has been told to.".
  Observe wr_l4_scene at wr_l4 when true "The fourth landing is a counting-room with no walls: a high desk bolted to the stone and under a tin hood against the rain, a ledger chained to it, and a stool. Everything on it is dry but the clerk.".
  Observe wr_l5_scene at wr_l5 when true "The fifth landing has a bench, which none of the others has, and a view: from here the whole of Quiet Hill lies below with its shutters closed, and past it the Cuff, and across the Cuff the green copper of the Chapel roof going to blue in the rain. An old man sits on the bench with something long across his knees under a cloth.".
  Observe wr_l6_scene at wr_l6 when true "The sixth landing is hung with grey sailcloth on three sides, so that the rain is a drumming and the light is the colour of a tent. In the middle of it, standing quite still, is a Second in a domino of black lacquer, with his hands crossed on the pommel of a sword.".
  Observe wr_l7_scene at wr_l7 when true "The seventh landing has had its paving scrubbed white. It is the only clean thing on the Stair, and it smells of vinegar and, under the vinegar, of drink. A man in a Second's grey stands at the far side of it with his back to the rain, as one does who has stopped noticing it.".
  Observe wr_l8_scene at wr_l8 when true "The eighth landing has no lamp. Someone has put it out, and the iron bracket drips. By the grey light off the water you can make out a wall, a step, and a boy standing against the wall with a sword held out in front of him in both hands, as if it were something that had been handed to him in the street.".
  Observe wr_l9_scene at wr_l9 when true "The ninth landing is the widest, and it is bare. The Captain's table stands in the open, a plank on two barrels, and on it a lamp under a glass, a pen, and nothing else. Beyond it the last of the Stair goes up into the rain to a gate, and through the gate the flat grey roofs of the Fourteen.".
  Observe wr_head_scene at stair_top when true "The head of the Stair is a small stone court with a gate in its far wall and, over the gate, the Seconds' motto, cut deep and filled with moss: WHAT I REFUSE. Below, the Hill; beyond, the water. Nobody who has come up ninety-nine steps in the rain has ever liked the motto, and everybody has stopped to read it.".
  Observe wr_head_night at stair_top when dark() "The last lamp of the Stair is burning over the gate, and in its light the motto looks a little less like a boast.".

  // The Guild rule for the whole Stair: a Second guards the flight above his landing, and lets a company by when it has
  // answered his question. Whoever has no blade is not asked.
  Rule wr_unarmed_by when wr_post(?s, ?p) and at(party, ?p) and not capable(party, brawn) and not tolerates(?s, party) and not dead(?s)
    says "The Second looks at your empty hands, and at the rain on your face, and steps aside. 'The Stair is a stair,' he says. 'We ask nothing of the unarmed but that they hold the rail.'" {
    Assert tolerates(?s, party). }
  Rule wr_height_counts when wr_post(?s, ?p) and tolerates(?s, party) and not wr_counted(?s) { Assert wr_counted(?s). Increase wr_height(party) by 1. }
  Rule wr_dead_counts when wr_post(?s, ?p) and dead(?s) and not wr_counted(?s) { Assert wr_counted(?s). Increase wr_height(party) by 1. }
  // A Second killed on the Stair is blood on it: the Guild does not forgive it, and tells the company so at the head.
  Relation wr_slain(group).
  Rule wr_blood_on_stair when wr_post(?s, ?p) and dead(?s) and not wr_slain(?s) and company(party)
    says "Somewhere below, on the Hill, a bell is rung once, the way it is for a Second. Nobody on the Stair has told it. Every landing has heard." { Assert wr_slain(?s). Assert wr_blooded(party). }
  // A company that falls on the Stair is carried down it, as the Guild always has: the Seconds do not leave their dead
  // or their guests on a landing, and the Mercy of the engine has left a little life in them.
  Rule wr_carried_down when wr_post(?s, ?p) and captured(?s, party) and not wr_carried(party)
    says "Two Seconds you have not seen before take you under the arms and carry you down ninety-nine steps in the rain, talking quietly over your head about something else. They set you on the stone at the bottom, and one of them folds your cloak under your head. 'Come again,' he says. 'Everyone does.'" {
    Retract captured(?s, party). Retract assails(?s, party). Assert peaceable(?s). Assert at(party, hill_foot). }
  Rule wr_carried_reset when wr_carried(party) { Retract wr_carried(party). }
  Rule wr_three_falls when wr_falls(party) >= 3 and at(party, ?p) and wr_landing(?p)
    says "Somebody on the landing below calls the count, and it is taken up from landing to landing, quite gently: three. Two Seconds you have not seen before come up the flight and take you under the arms, and carry you down ninety-nine steps in the rain. 'Three is the Guild's count,' says one of them. 'There is a bench. There is a surgeon. There is no hurry on the Stair, and nobody has ever once been late.'" {
    Set wr_falls(party) to 0. Assert at(party, hill_foot). }

  // The Seconds are Peaceable until a company chooses steel: then they are as dangerous as they are, and it is a real
  // fight, to the end, which the Mercy of the engine makes the end of the company only if all of it falls.
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(wr_marl). Initially Assert takesPrisoners(wr_pair). Initially Assert takesPrisoners(wr_dobb).
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(wr_vask). Initially Assert takesPrisoners(wr_veil). Initially Assert takesPrisoners(wr_anselm).
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(wr_rook). Initially Assert takesPrisoners(reeve).

  // ── 1. Dignity: Second Odo Sturry ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person wr_marl "Second Odo Sturry" at wr_l1 {
    Role "a Second of the Seconds' Guild, a heavy man on a bucket". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    State holding blocking "A heavy man in Second's grey sits on a bucket across the flight with a wet cigar, and is not going to get up for nothing.".
    Guards wr_f2.
    Greets "'Odo Sturry,' says the man on the bucket, getting up as far as his knees, 'Second, of this landing, and of the Guild, and of nobody's much else.' He takes the cigar out. 'A Second says his name first. It is so that the one he hurts has something to put on the writ.'".
    Greets again "'Sturry,' says Sturry, as to a ledger.".
  }
  Initially Assert wr_post(wr_marl, wr_l1).
  Topic wr_marl_rule with wr_marl "Ask Sturry what the first landing asks" when true {
    Says "'The Open Hand,' says Sturry, and nods at the rack. 'Steel on the rack, as it comes. You and me, and the hands we were born with, and first blood: the nose, the lip, a knuckle. No judge. The one who bleeds says so.' He considers the cigar. 'It is the first thing the Stair asks, and it asks it so as to find out how a man takes being hit by somebody he has no quarrel with. Some say it is dignity. I say it is the toll.'".
  }
  Action wr_box(actor: group, site: place) "Lay your steel on the rack and box Sturry to first blood" {
    Speaker wr_marl.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wr_marl, site) and able(wr_marl) and not tolerates(wr_marl, actor) and capable(actor, brawn).
    Time 5 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert tolerates(wr_marl, actor). Increase wr_defend(actor) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert strikes(wr_bruise, actor). Increase wr_falls(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You lay your steel on the rack among the others and square up in the dish worn in the paving. It is not much of a fight and not a bad one: he is slow and sound and has been hit by better, and at the end of it he sits down on his bucket with his nose running red and says 'Sturry. First blood,' with great satisfaction, as one reading out a result. 'Up you go.'".
    Otherwise "Sturry's fist finds your mouth, gently, as a man hangs up a coat. 'First blood to Sturry, who is sorry,' he says. 'Have your dinner and come back.' You taste iron and rain.".
  }
  Action wr_toll(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Sturry the Stair's toll, three coin, and go by" {
    Speaker wr_marl.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wr_marl, site) and able(wr_marl) and not tolerates(wr_marl, actor) and capable(actor, brawn) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3.
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Increase quantity(wr_marl, gold) by 3. Assert tolerates(wr_marl, actor). Increase wr_hire(actor) by 1. }
    Result "Sturry weighs the three coin in his hand and puts them away in the lining of his hat. 'The toll was Second Pyke's, the year the roof came in,' he says. 'Nobody has liked to repeal it. Go up.' He does not look at you, which is a courtesy, and which you notice.".
  }
  Action wr_steel1(actor: group, site: place) "Keep your steel, and tell Sturry that a stair is a stair" {
    Speaker wr_marl.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wr_marl, site) and able(wr_marl) and not tolerates(wr_marl, actor) and capable(actor, brawn).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract peaceable(wr_marl). Assert assails(wr_marl, actor). Increase wr_break(actor) by 1. }
    Result "Sturry looks at the rack, and then at the sword in your hand, and then, for a long time, at you. 'Odo Sturry,' he says, getting up off the bucket with something like regret, and draws.".
  }

  // ── 2. The Door: Seconds Hale and Tace ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person wr_pair "Seconds Hale and Tace" at wr_l2 {
    Role "two Seconds of the Guild, in the doorway of the second landing". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Numbers 2. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    State holding blocking "Two Seconds in grey stand in the narrow door of the second landing, shoulder to shoulder, and the flight above it goes past them and not through them.".
    Guards wr_f3.
    Greets "'Hale,' says the elder of the two, and 'Tace,' says the other, a half-beat behind, as if a bell had been rung for him. They stand either side of the Guild's door with their hands loose. 'We are paid by the hour,' says Hale, 'and we are on the hour.'".
    Greets again "'Hale.' 'Tace.'".
  }
  Initially Assert wr_post(wr_pair, wr_l2).
  Topic wr_pair_rule with wr_pair "Ask what the second landing asks" when true {
    Says "'The Door,' says Hale. 'It is a door on a landing, and nobody comes through it unless they are carrying something worth the carrying. We are the two who want to get through. You are the one who has the doorway.' Tace nods. 'Hold it for the length of the Concord's preamble.' 'Which is long,' says Tace. 'And Hale reads slowly.' 'The Guild says a man learns what a door is for by being the only thing in it.'".
  }
  Action wr_hold(actor: group, site: place) "Take the narrow door, and hold it against the pair of them" {
    Speaker wr_pair.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wr_pair, site) and able(wr_pair) and not tolerates(wr_pair, actor) and capable(actor, brawn).
    Time 8 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert tolerates(wr_pair, actor). Increase wr_defend(actor) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert strikes(wr_bruise, actor). Increase wr_falls(actor) by 1. }
