    Result "The stone is scrubbed because there was something on it. The vinegar is to cover another smell. And the sword is held low and a little away from the body, the way one carries a full cup across a crowded room, and the hand that holds it, under the glove, is not quite still. Nobody on the Hill has told you why. He sees you look and does not move it. 'Winter,' he says, as if you had asked. 'A boy. He was seventeen, and he did not yield, and I did not stop.' Then, in the manner of one who has said it a good many times to a wall: 'I am quite good enough. Come on.'".
    Otherwise "He is better than you, and he is waiting, and nothing in him that you can read is any different from what it was.".
  }
  Action wr_disarm(actor: group, site: place) "Take the sword out of his hand" {
    Speaker wr_anselm.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wr_anselm, site) and able(wr_anselm) and not tolerates(wr_anselm, actor) and capable(actor, brawn).
    Time 8 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert tolerates(wr_anselm, actor). Increase wr_hire(actor) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert strikes(wr_bruise, actor). Increase wr_falls(actor) by 1. }
    Result "He is very, very good, and you are lucky; in the end the sword goes out of his hand and skitters across the clean paving and over the edge of the landing, and you hear it ring on the rock below for a long time. He does not look at it. 'Well done,' says Anselm Reeve, to the wall. 'My sister will be very pleased,' and then, in a very different voice, 'Will she be told?'".
    Otherwise "He puts the flat of his blade across your wrist and the strength goes out of your arm, and your own sword rings on the paving. 'Not yet,' he says. It is a courtesy, and his voice is not quite steady on it, and it is the courtesy that you remember.".
  }
  Action wr_let_touch(actor: group, site: place) "Drop your point, and let him touch you, and say that he has won" {
    Speaker wr_anselm.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wr_anselm, site) and able(wr_anselm) and not tolerates(wr_anselm, actor) and capable(actor, brawn) and knows(actor, wr_brother_shakes).
    Time 4 minutes.
    On success { Assert tolerates(wr_anselm, actor). Increase wr_defend(actor) by 1. Assert strikes(wr_bruise, actor). Assert wr_brother_spared(actor). }
    Result "You lower your point, and say, aloud, so that the Seconds on the landing below will hear it, that the seventh landing is his, and take his blade along your forearm, not deeply, because he is very good, and at the last he is not quite good enough to stop it. 'No,' says Anselm Reeve, white to the lips. 'No, you did not need to do that.' He looks at his hand, which is steady. 'Go up. Tell her I held. Tell her I held,' and he sits down on the clean stone, all at once, like someone whose strings have been let go.".
  }
  Relation wr_brother_spared(group).
  Action wr_steel7(actor: group, site: place) "Fight the Captain's brother, with steel, to the end" {
    Speaker wr_anselm.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wr_anselm, site) and able(wr_anselm) and not tolerates(wr_anselm, actor) and capable(actor, brawn).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract peaceable(wr_anselm). Assert assails(wr_anselm, actor). Increase wr_break(actor) by 1. }
    Result "'Anselm Reeve,' he says, and his sword comes up out of its low guard as if the thing had been waiting all winter to hear it.".
  }

  // ── 8. Fear: Second Hesk ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person wr_rook "Second Pen Hesk" at wr_l8 {
    Role "a boy of sixteen, sworn to the Guild last week, with a lamp put out". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    State holding blocking "A boy is standing against the wall of the eighth landing with a sword held out in front of him in both hands, and the sword is shaking, and so is the rest of him, and he is between you and the flight above.".
    Guards wr_f9.
    Greets "'Hesk,' says the boy, and swallows, and starts again. 'Pen Hesk. Second. Of the Guild. A Second says his name before he strikes.' His voice breaks on 'strikes'. 'I am to ask you,' he says, with great care, as if reading it off the inside of his skull, 'whether you are afraid. And then I am to fight you. That is the eighth landing. I am very sorry about the lamp.'".
    Greets again "'Hesk,' says the boy, and the blade ticks against the wall.".
  }
  Initially Assert wr_post(wr_rook, wr_l8).
  Topic wr_rook_rule with wr_rook "Ask what the eighth landing asks" when true {
    Says "'Fear,' says Hesk. 'It is a person who is afraid. It is never anybody else, you see. The Guild puts one on every landing, but the eighth is the one that is always the newest, and it is the one nobody has ever had to put a name to.' His teeth chatter and he shuts them. 'I am meant to be what you will have to go past. They did not say it would be me.'".
  }
  Action wr_stare(actor: group, site: place) "Stare the boy down, and walk past him" {
    Speaker wr_rook.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wr_rook, site) and able(wr_rook) and not tolerates(wr_rook, actor) and capable(actor, brawn).
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert tolerates(wr_rook, actor). Increase wr_hire(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You walk toward him as if he were furniture, and he has nowhere to go but flat against the wall, where he lets his sword drop, and you go by with the rain on your back. Behind you he is quietly sick over the edge. It was perfectly effective.".
    Otherwise "He shuts his eyes and holds the sword out, as stiffly as a curtain-rail, and sets his jaw, and does not move. It is more frightening than you expected, and more difficult to go past.".
  }
  Action wr_wait_rook(actor: group, site: place) "Sit on the step across from him and wait until his hand stops" {
    Speaker wr_rook.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wr_rook, site) and able(wr_rook) and not tolerates(wr_rook, actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert tolerates(wr_rook, actor). Increase wr_defend(actor) by 1. Assert wr_rook_waited(actor). }
    Result "You put your own sword across your knees where he can see it, and sit down on the wet step, and say nothing. It takes most of an hour. The rain keeps up and the boy keeps the sword out, and at some point he is not holding it as a rail but as a weight, and at some point the point has come down, and then he sits too, with his back to the wall, and says, to the lampless bracket, 'I did not know it was allowed to sit.' Then: 'Hesk. I mean, you may go by, Pen Hesk, Second, I am sorry.' It is not clear which of you has been got past.".
  }
  Relation wr_rook_waited(group).
  Action wr_steel8(actor: group, site: place) "Cut him down before he can swing" {
    Speaker wr_rook.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wr_rook, site) and able(wr_rook) and not tolerates(wr_rook, actor) and capable(actor, brawn).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract peaceable(wr_rook). Assert assails(wr_rook, actor). Increase wr_break(actor) by 1. }
    Result "'Hesk,' says the boy, in a thread of a voice. 'Pen Hesk,' and he swings, because he was told to, with his eyes shut.".
  }

  // ── 9. The Captain: Brannoch Reeve ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person reeve "Captain Brannoch Reeve" at wr_l9 {
    Role "Captain of the Seconds' Guild, at her table in the rain" when not at(reeve, urn_hall).
    Role "Captain of the Seconds' Guild, with forty Seconds in grey at her back" when at(reeve, urn_hall).
    Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 4. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    State holding blocking "A woman in Captain's grey sits at a plank table on the ninth landing with a lamp, a pen, and her hands folded, and the last of the Stair goes up behind her. She has watched you come up the whole way.".
    Guards wr_f10.
    Greets "'Reeve,' says the Captain of Seconds, not rising. She is fifty and square and looks as if she had been cut from the same stone as the Stair and rained on for as long. 'I will not give you my first name. It is the one thing on the Hill I have kept.' She turns her pen over once. 'You have come a long way up in the wet, and I have watched you the whole of it, which is not a courtesy, it is the post. Sit.'".
    Greets again "'Reeve,' says the Captain, and moves the lamp a hand's breadth to see you better.".
  }
  Initially Assert wr_post(reeve, wr_l9).
  Topic wr_reeve_unarmed with reeve "Ask the Captain what is at the head of the Stair" when not capable(actor, brawn) {
    Says "'The Hill,' says Reeve, 'and a gate, and a motto, which you may read.' She does not look at your hands, as the Seconds below did not. 'The Guild's oath is for those who carry. You are not asked it, and I should not think any the less of you. Go up, and see what the Old Names have shut their shutters on. It is not much.'".
  }
  Topic wr_reeve_rule with reeve "Ask the Captain what she asks at the top" when wr_bladed_up() {
    Says "'Nothing,' says Reeve. 'Eight asked, and you answered, and the book has it. I only read it back.' She opens the ledger on the table. It is another ledger, the Captain's, with a column for each landing, and in the column for each landing, in a different hand for each, a line. 'A champion is made by what they refuse. I do not ask what you will do. I know it: I have a Second at every landing. I ask what you *refuse*.'".
  }
  Query wr_bladed_up() means capable(party, brawn) and wr_height(party) >= 8.
  // The Captain's question, put once; the three answers are the three creeds, each available to a company that has
  // earned it by what it did on the landings (twice, at the least).
  Topic wr_reeve_asks with reeve "Tell the Captain you will answer her question" when wr_bladed_up() and not wr_blooded(party) once {
    Says "She turns the ledger round so that you can read it. 'The first,' says Reeve, 'laid his steel on the rack, or took your coin, or drew. The second held a door or fought two. The third was a clown with a daughter. The fourth was paid to fall to you, and was, or was not. The fifth held out a sword. The sixth wore a mask. The seventh is my brother.' Her voice does not change on it. 'The eighth was a child. And I have a column of what you did. Say what it is that you refuse.'".
  }
  Topic wr_say_hire with reeve "Say that you refuse nothing that is fairly paid for" answering wr_reeve_asks when wr_hire(party) >= 2 {
    Says "'A sword for rent,' says Reeve, and does not make it sound like an insult, which is a gift. 'The Guild is mostly that. It is honest work. The buyer is told the price; the sword does what it is paid for and no more.' She taps the rack. 'If that is what you are, say it. Do not let anyone call it shame.'".
    On discuss { Assert wr_hireling(party). Assert wr_asked(party). }
  }
  Topic wr_say_defend with reeve "Say that you refuse to see the unarmed hurt" answering wr_reeve_asks when wr_defend(party) >= 2 {
    Says "'A shield,' says Reeve. Her eyes go to the lamp. 'It is the rarest, and nobody has thanked it, ever, and it is the one the Guild is for, on paper. A Second who refuses to let the unarmed be hurt is a Second who gets in the way of the people who pay Seconds. You will not be rich. You will, I should think, be the last person on the Stair that they are afraid of, and the only one they come to when it is over.'".
    On discuss { Assert wr_defender(party). Assert wr_asked(party). }
  }
  Topic wr_say_break with reeve "Say that you refuse a rule that makes you do it" answering wr_reeve_asks when wr_break(party) >= 2 {
    Says "'A breaker,' says Reeve, and for the first time sits back. 'It is what the Hill is afraid of, and what it is secretly for. Someone has to be the person to whom it can be said, *and the rule?* and who answers, *what rule*.' She almost smiles. 'The Guild has had four in three hundred years. We did not swear them in. We keep their names in the book, in the back, in a hand nobody else can read. You will be in it.'".
    On discuss { Assert wr_breaker(party). Assert wr_asked(party). }
  }
  Topic wr_say_plain with reeve "Say that you do not know what you refuse" answering wr_reeve_asks when wr_hire(party) < 2 and wr_defend(party) < 2 and wr_break(party) < 2 {
    Says "'That is the commonest answer,' says Reeve, 'and the one I like best. It is the truthful one.' She makes a note. 'You have climbed nine landings and answered nine ways, and not one of them twice, and I shall put you down as plain. You are not a hireling or a shield or a breaker. You are a Second, which is all that is on the oath; the rest is what you find out.'".
    On discuss { Assert wr_plain(party). Assert wr_asked(party). }
  }
  // What the Captain says of the blood on the Stair, to a company that has left some.
  Topic wr_reeve_blood with reeve "Ask the Captain what she will say of the Stair" when wr_blooded(party) and capable(actor, brawn) {
    Says "'You have killed on my Stair,' says Reeve. 'Seconds I have trained, who signed their blows. The Guild's oath is not for those who bring blood up it, and you know that it is not, or you would not have drawn on a man who was paid to be hit.' She does not stand. 'You may go up. It is a public stair. I will not swear you, and you will not be a Second, and I will tell you which of mine I buried, since you did not ask.' She names them. It does not take long.".
  }
  Topic wr_reeve_ledger with reeve "Ask the Captain about the forty coin in the fourth landing's book" when knows(actor, wr_paid_to_lose) {
    Says "'Mine,' says Reeve at once. She does not make it a confession. 'Forty coin from my purse, in my hand, signed R., and every Second on the Stair has a column and a custom, and the fourth landing's is to see what a champion does with a gift. I put the purse in. I wanted to see what you did.' She turns the pen once. 'It is a mean little test and I am the Captain. Do not take it personally. You were next.'".
  }
  Action wr_swear(actor: group, site: place) "Kneel on the wet stone, and take the Seconds' oath" {
    Speaker reeve.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(reeve, site) and wr_asked(actor) and not wr_blooded(actor) and not wr_sworn(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert wr_sworn(actor). Give wr_seconds_blade to actor. Assert handReady(actor, hand_stair). Assert arcBegun(actor, hand_stair).
      Assert tolerates(reeve, actor). }
    Result "You kneel on the paving in the rain and say the oath, which is shorter than you were afraid of: to sign what you strike; to refuse what is to be refused; to come when the Stair calls. The Captain stands, which she does for nobody, and gives you, hilt first, a plain grey blade with the Guild's ring pommel, and says, in the voice of someone reading a column: 'Second.' Then, as the Seconds on every landing below you lift their hands, each as it hears it, one after another, nine times down the rain: 'Welcome up.'".
  }
  // The Captain lets a company that has not been sworn up and out: it is a public stair. What she will not do is let it
  // go by her unasked while it carries a blade.
  Rule wr_reeve_lets_by when reeve_lets(party) and not tolerates(reeve, party) { Assert tolerates(reeve, party). }
  Relation reeve_lets(group).
  Rule wr_reeve_lets_blood when wr_blooded(party) and wr_height(party) >= 8 and at(party, wr_l9) and not reeve_lets(party) { Assert reeve_lets(party). }
  Rule wr_reeve_lets_plain when wr_asked(party) and not wr_sworn(party) and not reeve_lets(party) { Assert reeve_lets(party). }
  Kind wr_seconds_blade_kind "a Second's blade" is gear worth 40 weighing 3 granting brawn described "A plain grey sword with a ring for a pommel, and the Guild's mark cut into the ricasso: a hand, open, held up. It has no name, which is the point. A Second signs his blows; the blade does not have to.".
  Item wr_seconds_blade "a Second's blade" is wr_seconds_blade_kind at offstage.

  // What the oath leaves with a company: the Guild's own creed, said at the head of the Stair, the standing invitation
  // into the Guild's yard (its infirmary, its practice ring) and, once, an hour's drill with the Captain.
  Relation wr_drilled(group).
  Action wr_drill(actor: group, who: member, site: place) "Drill an hour in the Guild's yard with the Captain, and be put through it" {
    Speaker reeve.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(reeve, site) and memberOf(who, actor) and wr_sworn(actor) and not wr_drilled(actor) and capable(actor, brawn).
    Time 6.
    Resolve endow(who, strength, by_one).
    On success { Assert wr_drilled(actor). }
    Result "She works you in the yard for an hour in the rain until you can no longer lift the sword and then makes you lift it. It is not kindness and it is not cruelty, only the Guild's own sums. At the end of it she looks at you. 'You are stronger,' says Reeve. 'It is not that I taught you. It is that nobody else made you do it past the point of wanting to.'".
  }
  // The standing invitation: the Guild's surgeon sees to its own for nothing, and does not ask what was done on the Stair.
  Action wr_yard_care(actor: group, site: place) "Be seen to on the surgeon's bench, as one of the Guild" {
    Speaker hl_surgeon.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hl_surgeon, site) and wr_sworn(actor).
    Time 6.
    Resolve recover(actor).
    Result "'A Second,' says Goodwife Ream, without looking up, and moves along the bench. She does not ask what it was, and she does not take a coin. By the end of the hour you are stitched, strapped, and so thoroughly fed that you have to be told when to stop.".
  }
  Milestone wr_m_five "climbed the Duelling Stair to the fifth landing" worth 25 when wr_height(party) >= 5.
  Milestone wr_m_top "answered every landing of the Duelling Stair, and the Captain's question" worth 50 when wr_asked(party).
  Milestone wr_m_sworn "was sworn a Second of the Seconds' Guild" worth 75 when wr_sworn(party).

  // ── The Contessa's killing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At the top of the Stair the Contessa wants a Second for a killing: Lord Dacre Ullin has put a child in her
  // goddaughter, Elinor Sarum, and will not own it, and on the Hill what the Houses will not own is washed by a Second.
  // The truth is that they were married by lamplight in the Chapel, by someone now dead, and that the Houses will not
  // hear it, because Ullin sits at the eleventh place and Sarum at the fourteenth, and a spoon does not marry down.
  // Three ways: do it (a hireling's), refuse it, or stand for Elinor in the yard on the Guild's own Rule.
  Relation wr_commissioned(group). Relation wr_hired(group). Relation wr_refused(group).
  Relation wr_ullin_dead(group). Relation wr_ullin_bound(group). Relation wr_ullin_taken(group). Relation wr_other_second(group).
  Query wr_ullin_settled() means wr_ullin_dead(party) or wr_ullin_bound(party) or wr_other_second(party).
  Person wr_elinor "Elinor Sarum" at offstage {
    Role "the Contessa's goddaughter, of House Sarum, with her hand on a window-seat" when at(wr_elinor, tarn_hall).
    Role "the Contessa's goddaughter, of House Sarum" when not at(wr_elinor, tarn_hall).
    Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "A young woman sits in the window of the hall of the Palazzo Tarn with a book she is not reading, and a hand laid very lightly on her gown below the waist, in the manner of a person who does not yet know she is doing it. 'I am Elinor Sarum,' she says. 'I am the Contessa's goddaughter, and you are the Bare, and I am not to be spoken to; she is quite firm about it. She is very kind.'".
    Greets again "'You are not to speak to me,' says Elinor Sarum, and makes room on the seat.".
  }
  Person wr_ullin "Lord Dacre Ullin" at offstage {
    Role "of House Ullin, who practises alone in the Guild's yard by lamplight" when not wr_other_second(party).
    Role "of House Ullin, who is not at the Guild's yard any more" when wr_other_second(party).
    Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Greets "The young man in the practice ring lowers his sword and does not take it for a courtesy. 'Ullin,' he says. 'Dacre, if you must. The eleventh spoon.' He wipes his face with his sleeve. 'You are somebody's Second. They are always somebody's Second, at this hour. I wish you would say whose, and let me get on with it.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Lord Ullin, and does not lift the sword.".
  }
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(wr_ullin).
  Rule wr_elinor_hall when publicHours() and not hl_dining_hours() and not at(wr_elinor, tarn_hall) { Assert at(wr_elinor, tarn_hall). }
  Rule wr_elinor_bed when privateHours() and not at(wr_elinor, offstage) and not wr_ullin_bound(party) { Assert at(wr_elinor, offstage). }
  Rule wr_ullin_yard when hour(clock) >= 18 and not wr_ullin_dead(party) and not wr_other_second(party) and not at(wr_ullin, seconds_yard) { Assert at(wr_ullin, seconds_yard). }
  Rule wr_ullin_home when (hour(clock) < 18 or wr_other_second(party)) and not wr_ullin_dead(party) and not at(wr_ullin, offstage) { Assert at(wr_ullin, offstage). }
  Discovery wr_elinor_story "Elinor Sarum is with child by Lord Dacre Ullin, and they were married by lamplight in the Chapel by someone who is now dead; the Houses will not own it, because Ullin's spoon is the eleventh and Sarum's the fourteenth, and the Contessa calls it a dishonour that only a Second's blade can wash.".
  Topic wr_elinor_tells with wr_elinor "Ask Elinor why she is not to be spoken to" when true once {
    Says "She laughs, and it is not a laugh. 'Because I am a dishonour.' She is very composed. 'I was married in the Chapel, in October, at night, by somebody who did not ask what the Houses thought, because she did not need to; she was to be dead in a week, and I believe she knew. Dacre knelt in the vestry. I wore my second-best gown.' Her hand does not move. 'The Houses say a Sarum does not marry an Ullin, because of the eleventh spoon and the fourteenth. I have told them that I have, and that there is a child, and they say that a dishonour is not a marriage, and the Contessa has said that she knows how a dishonour is washed.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, wr_elinor_story). }
  }
  Topic wr_elinor_ask with wr_elinor "Ask what she would have a Second do" when knows(actor, wr_elinor_story) once {
    Says "'Nothing.' It comes very fast. 'Nothing. I should like very much not to have anyone's death on the child.' She looks at her hands. 'If there were a way that he might say it, in front of the Fourteen, that it was true, I think the Contessa would not be able to say that it was a dishonour. She cannot bear to be disproved. She bears a good deal else. I do not know of any way, and I do not know a Second. But I should be quite, quite glad, if somebody found one.'".
  }
  Topic wr_ullin_story with wr_ullin "Ask him whether he knows what the Contessa means to do" when knows(actor, wr_elinor_story) once {
    Says "'Of course I know.' He puts the sword in the rack, as a man puts away something that has been a comfort. 'It was a Second who told me, last week, as a kindness. I am to be killed by the Contessa's Second before the ninth, in a yard, in the dark, and I am to have the privilege of not seeing it coming, which I do not, since I have been in this yard every night.' A short laugh. 'I should marry her in the street. I should marry her in the Terrace and have it cried, if they would hear it. It is not a question of what I will say. It is a question of whether anybody on the Hill is *listening*.'".
  }
  Topic wr_tarn_asks with tarn "Tell the Contessa that you are sworn" when wr_sworn(actor) and not wr_commissioned(actor) and (not masked(actor) or publicHours()) once {
    Says "'A Second.' She puts down the spoon. 'The Captain sent me word by the water-gate, which is quicker than the Stair, and I have been looking forward to you.' She is not unkind, and she is not asking. 'There is a man, Dacre Ullin, of the Ullins, the eleventh spoon. He has dishonoured a daughter of this house, my goddaughter, Elinor, and he will not own what he has done. In the Houses a thing of that kind is washed by a Second, in a yard, with the Guild's leave, and the Guild's leave I have. Sixty coin. On or before the eighth night. He practises alone.' She regards you. 'You may think it over. You may not think it over for long.'".
    On discuss { Assert wr_commissioned(actor). Assert knows(actor, wr_commission_known). }
  }
  Discovery wr_commission_known "The Contessa has commissioned a sworn Second to kill Lord Dacre Ullin of the eleventh spoon, in the Guild's yard, by the eighth night, for sixty coin, for dishonouring her goddaughter Elinor Sarum.".
  Action wr_take_commission(actor: group, site: place) "Take the Contessa's sixty coin, and the commission" {
    Speaker tarn.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(tarn, site) and wr_commissioned(actor) and not wr_hired(actor) and not wr_refused(actor) and not wr_ullin_settled().
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert wr_hired(actor). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 60. Decrease quantity(tarn, gold) by 60 or to nothing. }
    Result "'Good.' She counts it out herself, into your hand, sixty small gold coins out of a purse that has been kept for the purpose, and does not once look at your face. 'I have always found,' says the Contessa Tarn, 'that it is the ones who take the money who finish. The ones who refuse it do not finish; they merely feel.'".
  }
  Action wr_refuse_commission(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Contessa that you will not do it" {
    Speaker tarn.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(tarn, site) and wr_commissioned(actor) and not wr_hired(actor) and not wr_refused(actor) and not wr_ullin_settled().
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert wr_refused(actor). Decrease hl_trust(actor) by 1 or to nothing. }
    Result "'No,' says the Contessa, as one who has been told that it will rain. She regards you for some time. 'It is, I suppose, what a Second is for, in the end. You are the only one in the Guild who will say it to my face, and I am not sure I shall forgive you.' She picks up the spoon. 'Somebody else will. They are cheaper than the other kind.'".
  }
  Action wr_kill_ullin(actor: group, site: place) "Take the Contessa's commission, in the yard, with steel" {
    Speaker wr_ullin.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wr_ullin, site) and able(wr_ullin) and wr_hired(actor) and not wr_ullin_settled().
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract peaceable(wr_ullin). Assert assails(wr_ullin, actor). }
    Result "'Ah,' says Lord Ullin, very quietly. 'It is you.' He lifts the sword out of the rack. 'Dacre Ullin,' says Lord Ullin, which is the Guild's way, and the practice ring is suddenly a good deal smaller.".
  }
  Rule wr_ullin_falls when dead(wr_ullin) and wr_hired(party) and not wr_ullin_dead(party)
    says "He falls in the lamplight, with the practice-sword still in his hand, and says one word that you do not catch. It is not an oath. It is, you think, a name." { Assert wr_ullin_dead(party). Increase wr_hire(party) by 1. }
  Action wr_champion(actor: group, site: place) "Stand for Elinor Sarum, as her Second, and call the Rule of Acknowledgement against him" {
    Speaker wr_ullin.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wr_ullin, site) and able(wr_ullin) and wr_sworn(actor) and knows(actor, wr_elinor_story) and not wr_ullin_settled().
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert wr_ullin_bound(actor). Increase wr_defend(actor) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert strikes(wr_bruise, actor). Increase wr_falls(actor) by 1. }
    Result "'On the Rule of Acknowledgement, to first blood,' you say, 'for the Lady Elinor Sarum, who is his wife.' He stares at you. Then he laughs, and lifts the sword, and for a time the yard rings. At the end of it he is on his knee on the cobbles, with a cut on his wrist, and when he looks up he is quite white. 'I acknowledge it,' says Lord Ullin, to the whole of the Guild's yard, which is empty, and then, louder, to the dark, 'I acknowledge her, and the child, and the marriage, before the Seconds' Guild, and any of the Fourteen who like to ask.' He is crying. 'I have been waiting so long for somebody to make me.'".
    Otherwise "He is far better than you hoped, and perhaps a little better than he cares to be: the Rule is called, and he fights it with the whole of his heart, and puts you down, not unkindly, on the cobbles. 'First blood to Ullin,' he says, breathless. 'And, you know, if I could be made to say it by a blade, I should have been made by now.'".
  }
  Action wr_talk_ullin(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Ullin that the Houses will listen, if he says it before the Fourteen at the Contessa's table" {
    Speaker wr_ullin.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wr_ullin, site) and able(wr_ullin) and knows(actor, wr_elinor_story) and not wr_ullin_settled() and not wr_ullin_talked(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert wr_ullin_bound(actor). Assert wr_ullin_talked(actor). }
    On failure { Assert wr_ullin_talked(actor). }
    Result "'Not in a yard,' you say. 'Not in the street, either, where it can be said that you were made to. At the dinner, at the Contessa's table, with all fourteen of the spoons in the room. She cannot call it a dishonour in front of the Houses if the Ullin says it to her face and in his own voice.' He is silent so long that the lamp gutters. 'It would be the end of the eleventh spoon,' says Dacre Ullin. 'I should be an Ullin that married a Sarum. I should be, I think, extremely happy.'".
    Otherwise "He listens to it all, courteously, and at the end he says, with great weariness, that it is exactly what he would say himself, to somebody else, and that he would not, in the end, either believe it or do it. 'Come back with a better reason, or a better sword.'".
  }
  Relation wr_ullin_talked(group).
  // Left alone, the Contessa finds a cheaper Second, in the dark of the eighth night.
  Rule wr_ullin_taken_by_other when day(clock) == 8 and hour(clock) >= 23 and not wr_ullin_settled() and not wr_ullin_taken(party)
    says "In the small hours of the eighth night a Second whose name is not in the Guild's book goes into the practice ring of the yard by lamplight, and a young man with a sword is found in it in the morning." { Assert wr_ullin_taken(party). Assert wr_other_second(party). Assert at(wr_ullin, offstage). }
  Milestone wr_m_ullin "settled the Ullin matter without a death" worth 50 when wr_ullin_bound(party).
  Milestone wr_m_killed "did the Contessa's killing" worth 25 when wr_ullin_dead(party).

  // ── The Stair held ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // On the ninth night the Seconds keep the crowd off the Urn Hall's stair. The Captain brings forty of them across the
  // Cuff at dusk, and what they do is the sworn company's to say; drawing.kyr reads handPlayed(hand_stair) and handWay:
  // 1 the Stair held with shields (nobody hurt), 2 held with steel (the crowd bled), 3 the line opened (nobody held).
  Rule wr_reeve_marches when drawingNight() and wr_sworn(party) and not at(reeve, urn_hall) { Assert at(reeve, urn_hall). }
  Relation wr_held(group).
  Action wr_hold_shields(actor: group, site: place) "Have the Seconds close their shields across the Urn Hall stair, and hold" {
    Speaker reeve.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(reeve, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and handReady(actor, hand_stair) and not handPlayed(actor, hand_stair).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_stair). Assert arcDone(actor, hand_stair). Set handWay(hand_stair) to 1. Assert wr_held(actor). }
    Result "Forty Seconds in grey come down the Urn Hall stair in the lamplight and close their shields across the foot of it, a wall of plain painted wood, two ranks deep, in total silence, and the crowd, which has come to the Chapel with every sort of grievance, finds that it is looking at a line of faces that say *no* so politely. They do not draw. They do not need to. At each end of the line a Second says his name, quietly, to the people in front of him, and by the third repeating it has begun to sound like an apology.".
  }
  Action wr_hold_steel(actor: group, site: place) "Order the Seconds to clear the stair with steel" {
    Speaker reeve.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(reeve, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and handReady(actor, hand_stair) and not handPlayed(actor, hand_stair) and not wr_defender(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_stair). Assert arcDone(actor, hand_stair). Set handWay(hand_stair) to 2. Assert wr_held(actor). Assert wr_crowd_bled(actor). }
    Result "'On your word,' says the Captain, and the Seconds go down the stair with their swords drawn, saying their names, and what follows is quick and not at all like the Stair: a crowd is not a Second, and does not yield when it is bloodied. The Urn Hall's stair is held. It is held, you see afterwards, over eleven people lying on it, and the Captain does not look at you for the rest of the night, and is, throughout, entirely correct.".
  }
  Relation wr_crowd_bled(group).
  Action wr_open_line(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Seconds to stand aside, and let the crowd through" {
    Speaker reeve.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(reeve, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingNight() and handReady(actor, hand_stair) and not handPlayed(actor, hand_stair) and wr_breaker(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert handPlayed(actor, hand_stair). Assert arcDone(actor, hand_stair). Set handWay(hand_stair) to 3. Assert wr_line_opened(actor). }
    Result "'A breaker,' says Reeve, very softly, and looks along the line of her Seconds, and gives a signal that is not in the Guild's book. They step apart, forty of them, each a pace to the side, all at once, as men do who have been waiting to be told, and the crowd, which had braced for a wall, goes down the stair of the Urn Hall in a rush that is almost embarrassed. 'It is the first time in three hundred years,' says the Captain, 'that the Stair has refused to hold.'".
  }
  Relation wr_line_opened(group).
  Milestone wr_m_held "held the Stair at the Drawing" worth 75 when wr_held(party).
  Milestone wr_m_opened "opened the Seconds' line at the Drawing" worth 75 when wr_line_opened(party).

  // ── What came of them ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule wr_fate_reeve_hireling when newsHour() and wr_hireling(party) once says "Of Captain Reeve: she has written your name in the front of the Guild's book, with a price against it, and the Seconds have taken to quoting a rate for each landing, as you did, and calling it the Hireling's courtesy." { }
  Rule wr_fate_reeve_defender when newsHour() and wr_defender(party) once says "Of Captain Reeve: she has put your name in the front of the Guild's book with nothing against it. The Seconds say that when a company of the unarmed is in trouble on the Hill, there is now one door in the Guild they know to knock at." { }
  Rule wr_fate_reeve_breaker when newsHour() and wr_breaker(party) once says "Of Captain Reeve: she has written your name in the back of the Guild's book, in the hand that nobody else can read, and under it a single line: *The rule, and?*" { }
  Rule wr_fate_reeve_plain when newsHour() and wr_plain(party) once says "Of Captain Reeve: you are down in the book as plain, which is the commonest entry and the one she likes best. She has been seen to read it, on the ninth landing, in the rain." { }
  Rule wr_fate_reeve_blooded when newsHour() and wr_blooded(party) and not wr_sworn(party) once says "Of Captain Reeve: she has buried the Seconds she trained that you killed, with the Guild's honours, on the Hill, and has not said your name aloud, which on the Hill is the worst that can be done to anybody." { }
  Rule wr_fate_reeve_never when newsHour() and not wr_sworn(party) and not wr_blooded(party) once says "Of Captain Reeve: she keeps the ninth landing as she always has, and has been seen, at the hour when somebody might come up it, to lift her head." { }
  Rule wr_fate_hesk when newsHour() and wr_rook_waited(party) once says "Of Pen Hesk: the lamp on the eighth landing is lit again, and he sits by it with his sword across his knees, and has told nobody on the Stair that it was allowed to sit." { }
  Rule wr_fate_bled when newsHour() and wr_crowd_bled(party) once says "Of the Seconds' line at the Chapel: eleven of the crowd were carried across the Cuff by the Guild before dawn, and the Captain has had every name written down, in the Guild's own book, and read them aloud in the yard." { }
  Rule wr_fate_promised when newsHour() and wr_promised(party) and not wr_ullin_settled() once says "Of the Contessa's Second: she is still waiting, with the lamp on the third step of her private stair unlit, for somebody who said they would come." { }
  Rule wr_fate_anselm when newsHour() and wr_brother_spared(party) once says "Of Anselm Reeve: he has put down the vinegar, and holds the seventh landing steady, and says that he held. His sister has not told him that she knows." { }
  Rule wr_fate_dobb_dead when newsHour() and wr_orphan(wr_dobb) once says "Of Dilly, the Fool's daughter: she sits on the third landing's top step on the Third Bell days, with the wooden sword across her knees, and watches the stair below, and when a champion bows, she does not clap." { }
  Rule wr_fate_dobb_fooled when newsHour() and wr_fooled(party) and not wr_orphan(wr_dobb) once says "Of Fenwick Dobb: the Fool of the Stair has a new joke, and does it badly, on purpose, in your honour, to a child who has never in her life laughed at anything as hard." { }
  Rule wr_fate_vask when newsHour() and wr_vask_honest(party) once says "Of Corin Vask: the Ledger of the fourth landing records that he lost to a champion who would not be given the win, and that the loss was fair, in his own hand. He has framed the page." { }
  Rule wr_fate_wend_blade when newsHour() and wr_blade_taken(party) once says "Of Aldous Wend: on the Third Bell of the Drawing a boy comes up the Stair to ask whether the sword is still kept, and is told that it is, by somebody who does not tell him that it was a gift." { }
  Rule wr_fate_wend_broken when newsHour() and wr_blade_broken(party) once says "Of Aldous Wend: nine families on the Hill have been told that the sword is refused, and not broken, and nobody has disputed it, and he has been seen on his bench laughing, with his hands over his face." { }
  Rule wr_fate_wend_helped when newsHour() and wr_wend_helped(party) once says "Of Aldous Wend: somebody has put his water jar by his hand on the fifth landing every morning since the day somebody carried it down for him." { }
  Rule wr_fate_veil_named when newsHour() and named(wr_veil) once says "Of Tobias Vesper: he is no longer a Second of no name. He has gone from Quiet Hill by the water-gate, in the rain, with a trunk, and the Palazzo Vesper has taken the black domino down from the wall of the Guild's yard and burned it." { }
  Rule wr_fate_veil_spared when newsHour() and wr_veil_spared(party) once says "Of Tobias Vesper: he still stands on the sixth landing in a black domino, and says his no-name to the sailcloth, and has told nobody on the Hill what somebody said to him there." { }
  Rule wr_fate_ullin_bound when newsHour() and wr_ullin_bound(party) once says "Of Elinor Sarum and Dacre Ullin: she is the Lady Ullin, by the Rule, before the Seconds' Guild, and the eleventh spoon has been seen at the table with the fourteenth next to it. The Contessa said she was not at all sure it was permitted, and ate her soup." { }
  Rule wr_fate_ullin_dead when newsHour() and wr_ullin_dead(party) once says "Of Elinor Sarum: she has gone into the Bare Brothers' cloister, with her hand on her gown, and the child that was born, or will be, is to be a Sarum. The Contessa has had the sixty coin returned to her purse, and counted it twice." { }
  Rule wr_fate_ullin_other when newsHour() and wr_other_second(party) once says "Of Elinor Sarum: Lord Ullin was found in the practice ring of the Guild's yard on the ninth morning, and a Second whose name is not in the book has been paid. Elinor has gone into the cloister, and the Contessa has said that it was a thing that had to be done, in a voice that nobody on the Hill has heard her use before." { }
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/act1.kyr:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── Act I: The Marchants' Men ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Comedy of errors. The King's Name-Day is in four days and the Chancellor has hired a company of masquers who are
  // stuck behind a flooded ford. Gosse's Company comes in at the River Gate and is taken for them. A page at the Rotunda
  // is the Chancellor's missing daughter in boy's clothes. Kit Arden, the boy who plays the girls, is the image of her.
  // Her twin brother is a lieutenant of the Watch. The Chamberlain is keeping a book. By the fourth day there are two
  // companies of masquers, two Oriels and one King, who would like to be amused.
  Relation posing(group). Relation gateTruth(group). Relation gateHonest(group).
  Relation kitTaken(group). Relation kitProved(group). Relation kitLied(group).
  Relation orielSworn(group). Relation orielToldFather(group). Relation orielHelped(group). Relation twinsMet(group).
  Relation masqueChosen(group). Relation masqueGhost(group). Relation masqueMiser(group). Relation masqueFarce(group).
  Relation realMasquers(place). Relation auditioned(place). Relation provisional(place).
  Measure auditionScore(place).
  Chapter ch_arrive "The Marchants' Men" when royalCall(pentrice) and not auditioned(rierdan) "The King's Road ends at a customs arch with a kettle under it. The sergeant has been expecting you, and has got the wrong you.".

  // The gate: the sergeant puts one question, and the answer is a life.
  Topic gate_ask with tallis "Say who you are, since the sergeant has not asked" when not gateTruth(party) and not posing(party) and not gateHonest(party) once {
    Says "'Marchant's men,' says Sergeant Peverell, making a tick. 'Now. I have eight and a bear on my list and the Chancellor's steward has told me twice that the one with the voices is to be treated as if he were a bishop.' He looks you over with the flat patience of a customs shed. 'You're the masquers. Aren't you.'".
  }
  Topic gate_masquers with tallis "We are. The Marchants' masquers, and we are late" answering gate_ask when true {
    Says "He ticks and does not look up. 'Then the steward will be pleased,' he says, 'and I'll be spared his face.' The ledger takes your name as Marchant's, which is not the first time a book has lied for you, and is the first time it has done it so promptly.".
    On discuss { Assert posing(actor). }
  }
  Topic gate_truth with tallis "We are Gosse's Company, with the King's own writ" answering gate_ask when holding(actor, writ_kind) {
    Says "'The King's,' says Peverell, and takes the writ, and reads it the wrong way up, and then the right way, and goes pink. 'It's real,' he says. 'Mallam!' A young clerk in the Household's blue, a lanky cheerful twenty-two, comes at a run. 'It's real. They're the King's. The King's what, I couldn't say, but it's real.' You are walked up the Gate Street by two men who are afraid of you and one who is only curious.".
    On discuss { Assert gateTruth(actor). Increase favour(rierdan) by 1. }
  }
  Topic gate_nobody with tallis "Nobody's. We want a bed and the price of one" answering gate_ask when true {
    Says "'A bed,' says Peverell, and puts down the pen with regret. 'You've come to the right city. We have one of every kind of bed. You want the Brazen Sparrow, on the Row, where the players lodge.' He writes something. 'I'd say the Chancellor's steward will be along. I shouldn't say it to him.'".
    On discuss { Assert gateHonest(actor). }
  }
  Kind writ_kind "the King's writ" is document described "A writ sealed in blue wax with a crowned tower: COME TO DUN RIERDAN BY THE KING'S ROAD, BEING FOUND SUFFICIENT, AND PLAY. In a different hand: BRING THE BEAR.".
  Rule writ_given when writHeld(party) and not has_writ(party) { Give writ_kind to party. Assert has_writ(party). }
  Relation has_writ(group).

  // The Marchants' house: Kit Arden is brought, and is received.
  Action bring_kit(actor: group, site: place) "Take Kit Arden along to the Marchants' house" {
    Speaker kit.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(kit, site) and royalCall(pentrice) and not following(kit, actor).
    Time 0.
    On success { Assert following(kit, actor). }
    Result "Kit looks at the Row, the towers and the pie stall in one glance, and takes hold of your sleeve.".
  }
  Rule kit_received at marchant_hall when at(party, marchant_hall) and following(kit, party) and not kitTaken(party) and not kitProved(party)
    says "The steward drops a tray. It is a large tray, and the noise goes up the stair. 'My lady,' says Beadle Simm, in a voice that has not been used since the Chancellor's wife died. 'My lady Oriel.' He is on his knees on the tiles. Kit has gone the colour of whey. 'Beadle Simm,' Kit says. 'I am Kit. Kit Arden. I play the girls.' From the stair a short stout man in a robe of office is saying, gently, 'My daughter,' and coming down." {
    Assert kitTaken(party). }
  Topic marchant_ask with marchant "Answer the Chancellor, who has put a hand on Kit's shoulder" when kitTaken(party) and not kitProved(party) and not kitLied(party) once {
    Says "'Six weeks,' says Lord Marchant. 'I have had the Watch turn over the city for six weeks. I was told you were dead, and I was told you were in a convent, and I was told by your brother that you were happy. I had not been told you had taken to the stage.' He looks round at you. 'This person is my daughter. I ask you, since you appear to be her friends. Is she not?'".
  }
  Topic marchant_yes with marchant "She is, my lord, and she is a good deal improved by it" answering marchant_ask when true {
    Says "'There,' says Lord Marchant, with immense satisfaction. 'Beadle. A room. A proper room. A gown.' Kit looks at you with the eyes of a hare at the end of a field. 'I am Kit,' Kit says again, faintly, to nobody. They have taken him upstairs. It will be necessary, you think, to get him back.".
    On discuss { Assert kitLied(actor). Retract following(kit, actor). Assert at(kit, marchant_hall). }
  }
  Topic marchant_no with marchant "No, my lord. He is a boy called Kit Arden, and he plays the girls" answering marchant_ask when true {
    Says "'A boy,' says Lord Marchant. 'A boy who plays the girls.' He lifts Kit's chin with a finger. 'A good likeness, then. I congratulate the profession.' He is not convinced; you can see it. A man who has lost a daughter for six weeks does not want to find a boy. 'Prove it,' he says.".
  }
  Relation kitDoubted(group).
  Rule kit_released when auditioned(rierdan) and kitDoubted(party) and at(kit, marchant_hall) { Assert at(kit, sparrow_loft). }
  Action prove_kit(actor: group, site: place) "Prove Kit is a boy, with Kit's help and some dignity" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, marchant_hall) and kitTaken(party) and not kitProved(party) and not kitDoubted(party).
    Time 30.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert kitProved(actor). Increase favour(rierdan) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert kitDoubted(actor). Retract following(kit, party). Assert at(kit, marchant_hall). }
    Result "It takes a minute of Kit's best baritone, the recital of the Fool's catalogue from The Miser's Wedding, and, in the end, the Chancellor's own barber, fetched in a hurry, who looks at Kit's jaw and says: 'Mine, my lord, I have been shaving that chin since it was a hope.' Lord Marchant sits down on the stair. 'Then where,' he says, in a different voice, 'is my daughter?'".
    Otherwise "Lord Marchant, who is a lawyer, hears the proof and remarks that it proves what a good actor Kit is.".
  }
  Rule kit_freed when kitProved(party) and kitLied(party) { Retract kitLied(party). }

  // The twin.
  Topic cyprian_talk with cyprian "Tell Lieutenant Marchant what the Chancellor believes" when kitTaken(party) and not twinsMet(party) once {
    Says "Cyprian listens, white. 'He believes it is Oriel,' he says. 'He believes his daughter has come back as a boy who plays girls.' He passes a hand over his face. 'It was always going to be some such thing. We look alike. We have looked alike since the cradle. I have never in my life wished I looked less like her than I did when I was twelve and wanted to join the Watch, and she wanted to go on the stage, and our father wanted neither.' He lowers his hand. 'Where is she?'".
  }
  Topic oriel_ask with oriel "Ask the page Orrin why a Rotunda boy has such a look" when not knows(party, oriel_unmasked) once {
    Says "The page puts the prompt-copy behind his back, a thing real pages never do. 'Look at what?' says Orrin, in the carrying clear voice of someone who has been rehearsing to be someone else. 'I'm Orrin. I run errands for Master Fallow. I have done nothing wrong.' He looks at you. 'If I told you I was running away from a marriage,' he says, much lower, 'would you tell my father?'".
  }
  Topic oriel_sworn with oriel "No. Not a word, on my word" answering oriel_ask when true {
    Says "Something lets go in her shoulders. 'I am Oriel,' she says, and takes off the page's cap, and a quantity of dark hair comes down which was plainly not a page's. 'The Chancellor's. I have been in the wings six weeks. I have never been so happy in my life, and I have never been so hungry.' She puts the cap on again. 'Thank you.'".
    On discuss { Assert orielSworn(actor). Assert knows(actor, oriel_unmasked). }
  }
  Topic oriel_father with oriel "Yes. He has the right to know where his daughter is" answering oriel_ask when true {
    Says "'Then it was kind of you to ask first,' says Orrin, with a dreadful composure, and takes off the cap. 'I am Oriel Marchant. I'll go with you. I should like it to be known that I think you wrong.' She does not weep. She picks up the prompt-copy. 'But I'll not be taken. I'll go in my own time, and I'll go as myself.'".
    On discuss { Assert orielToldFather(actor). Assert knows(actor, oriel_unmasked). Retract at(oriel, rot_wings). Assert at(oriel, marchant_hall). }
  }
  Topic oriel_help with oriel "I'd help you if I could. What do you want?" answering oriel_ask when true {
    Says "She looks you up and down with all the shrewdness the stage has given her. 'I want to play,' she says. 'Not in a box, not at a window, not at the end of a corridor with a husband at the other end. I want to play a part that is a person.' She takes off the cap. 'I am Oriel Marchant. I should like it very much if you helped me.'".
    On discuss { Assert orielHelped(actor). Assert knows(actor, oriel_unmasked). }
  }
  Action unmask_oriel(actor: group, site: place) "Look hard at the page, and then at Kit, and then at the page" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rot_wings) and at(oriel, rot_wings) and kitTaken(party) and not knows(actor, oriel_unmasked).
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, oriel_unmasked). Assert orielHelped(actor). }
    Result "You do the sum a child could. The page's chin, the Chancellor's boy-girl, and the resemblance. 'Lady Oriel,' you say. The page stands still. Then, with an air of weary relief, takes off the cap.".
    Otherwise "The page looks back at you with the guileless eyes of a Rotunda page, and the question goes by.".
  }
  Action reunite_twins(actor: group, site: place) "Bring Oriel and Cyprian into the same room" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, marchant_hall) and knows(actor, oriel_unmasked) and at(cyprian, marchant_hall) and not twinsMet(actor) and (travelsWith(oriel, actor) or at(oriel, marchant_hall)).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert twinsMet(actor). Increase favour(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "They stop on either side of a pillar and look at each other for a long second, like a pair of mirrors. Then, at the same moment, in the same voice, they say 'You utter fool', and are in each other's arms, and the steward sits down hard on the stair. Lord Marchant says nothing at all, but he holds out a handkerchief to both of them, from the same pocket.".
  }
  Topic oriel_join with oriel "Ask Oriel to come with the company, as herself" when (orielSworn(actor) or orielHelped(actor)) and not orielToldFather(actor) and not travelsWith(oriel, actor) once {
    Says "'Yes,' says Oriel at once, and then, more carefully, 'if I may be paid. I do not want to be a Marchant at a table. I want to be a person at a salary.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(oriel, actor). Set hire(oriel) to 0. }
  }

  // The play: Hepzibah asks which one it will be.
  Topic hepzibah_play with hepzibah "Ask Hepzibah what the company will give the King" when royalCall(pentrice) and not masqueChosen(party) once {
    Says "Hepzibah takes the pencil out of her hair and puts it behind the other ear. 'There are three things we can give,' she says, 'and I'll tell you what each costs. I do not do this for everyone. Which would you choose?'".
  }
  Topic hepzibah_ghost with hepzibah "The Alderman's Ghost, as it was written" answering hepzibah_play when ghostPlay(pentrice) {
    Says "'Dangerous,' says Hepzibah. 'It is the best thing we have, and it is a play about a dead man who will not stay buried, in front of a King of eighty-one.' She writes something in the book. 'I do not mind. I like danger in a play. I do not like it in a man who can have us hanged.'".
    On discuss { Assert masqueChosen(actor). Assert masqueGhost(actor). }
  }
  Topic hepzibah_miser with hepzibah "The Miser's Wedding, the old one" answering hepzibah_play when true {
    Says "'Safe,' says Hepzibah. 'Safe is what Gosse has been telling the old kings since before I could read. It will not offend a soul.' She taps the book. 'It will also not be remembered.'".
    On discuss { Assert masqueChosen(actor). Assert masqueMiser(actor). }
  }
  Topic hepzibah_farce with hepzibah "A farce, tonight, made of the mistakes of this week" answering hepzibah_play when true {
    Says "Hepzibah looks at you over her spectacles until the pencil has finished a line. 'You mean,' she says, 'The Marchants' Men. The one that is happening to us.' She opens the book at a clean page. 'I have been waiting thirty-four years for someone to ask me to write a play that hasn't been finished yet. I'll need a Chancellor, a boy who plays girls, and a page.' She smiles. It is a small, rare, dangerous smile. 'Which we have.'".
    On discuss { Assert masqueChosen(actor). Assert masqueFarce(actor). }
  }

  // The real masquers arrive, which is the farce's turn.
  Rule real_masquers_come when royalCall(pentrice) and day(clock) >= arrivedR(rierdan) + 2 and not realMasquers(rierdan) and not auditioned(rierdan) and at(party, concourse)
    says "A wagon comes into the Concourse, hung with bunting, on which eight people in half-made costumes are shouting at each other over the head of a man in a mask who is plainly the actor-manager. 'The ford!' he is crying. 'The ford was a lake! We have come through a lake!' It is the Marchants' masquers. They are three days late and they are going to be extremely difficult to explain." {
    Assert realMasquers(rierdan). }

  // The audition: the Audience Chamber, and the King.
  Action audition_ghost(actor: group, site: place) "Play the King The Alderman's Ghost, the best scene, on the rug" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, audience) and masqueGhost(actor) and not gosseHam(actor) and not auditioned(rierdan).
    Time 30.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert auditioned(rierdan). Increase favour(rierdan) by 3. Assert provisional(rierdan). Set auditionScore(rierdan) to 3. }
    On failure { Assert auditioned(rierdan). Increase favour(rierdan) by 1. Set auditionScore(rierdan) to 1. }
    Result "The King sits upright through the whole of it. At the line where the Alderman insists he is not dead he laughs, once, with surprise, and the Chamberlain writes it down. At the end the old man is on his feet, and he says in his thin clear voice: 'I should like that again, with a better ending.' It is not clear whether this is praise. It is the best the Household has had in three years.".
    Otherwise "The scene goes up on the rug with perfect craft, and the King sleeps through the best of it. At the end he opens his eyes and says: 'Was it a comedy? I thought I heard a ghost.'".
  }
  Action audition_ghost_ham(actor: group, site: place) "Play the King The Alderman's Ghost, with Gosse in crimson, as he has asked" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, audience) and masqueGhost(actor) and gosseHam(actor) and not auditioned(rierdan).
    Time 30.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_formidable).
    On success { Assert auditioned(rierdan). Increase favour(rierdan) by 2. Assert provisional(rierdan). Set auditionScore(rierdan) to 2. }
    On failure { Assert auditioned(rierdan). Set auditionScore(rierdan) to 0. }
    Result "Gosse plays the Alderman as a king, and the King, who knows kings, sits still. It is the wrong size for the part, and enormous, and at the line where the Alderman insists he is not dead the old man says, aloud, 'I should hope not,' and the Chamberlain, who does not know whether to write that down, writes it down.".
    Otherwise "Gosse plays the Alderman in crimson, for the back of a hall that is not there. The King says, kindly, that he had understood the Alderman to be a smaller man.".
  }
  Action audition_miser_honest(actor: group, site: place) "Play the King The Miser's Wedding, with Gosse as he is" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, audience) and masqueMiser(actor) and gosseHonest2(actor) and not auditioned(rierdan).
    Time 30.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert auditioned(rierdan). Increase favour(rierdan) by 3. Assert provisional(rierdan). Set auditionScore(rierdan) to 3. }
    On failure { Assert auditioned(rierdan). Increase favour(rierdan) by 1. Set auditionScore(rierdan) to 1. }
    Result "Gosse plays the Miser as an old man would, tired and clever, counting his money with care. The King leans forward on his stick. He does not say the lines before Swale this time. He lets them come.".
    Otherwise "An old man plays an old miser quietly to an old King, and nobody in the room knows what to do with their hands.".
  }
  Action audition_miser(actor: group, site: place) "Play the King The Miser's Wedding, as his grandfather had it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, audience) and masqueMiser(actor) and not gosseHonest2(actor) and not auditioned(rierdan).
    Time 30.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert auditioned(rierdan). Increase favour(rierdan) by 2. Assert provisional(rierdan). Set auditionScore(rierdan) to 2. }
    On failure { Assert auditioned(rierdan). Set auditionScore(rierdan) to 0. }
    Result "The King knows the play. He says the Miser's lines a beat before Swale does, and then stops, mortified, and says, 'Go on.' It is the most nearly human thing the court has seen him do in a year.".
    Otherwise "The King recites every line before Swale can, and then remarks to the Chamberlain, audibly, that the company is old-fashioned.".
  }
  Action audition_farce(actor: group, site: place) "Play the King The Marchants' Men, with the two companies and the two Oriels" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, audience) and masqueFarce(actor) and realMasquers(rierdan) and (kitTaken(actor) or kitProved(actor)) and (twinsMet(actor) or orielSworn(actor)) and not auditioned(rierdan).
    Time 30.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert auditioned(rierdan). Increase favour(rierdan) by 4. Assert provisional(rierdan). Set auditionScore(rierdan) to 4. }
    On failure { Assert auditioned(rierdan). Set auditionScore(rierdan) to 1. }
    Result "It is performed by two sets of players at once, in two different costumes, in front of a Chancellor who is also in it, by accident, and three Oriels. The King does not stop laughing. At the end he is wiping his eyes with the Chamberlain's book. 'That,' he says, 'is the first time since the Siege of Thrall that I have understood a joke before the end.'".
    Otherwise "The farce is a collision. Everyone talks at once. At the end the King says, kindly, that it was a great deal of play for one afternoon.".
  }
  // The fiasco: whatever was played, the Audience Chamber ends full of the wrong people, and the Chamberlain, who has two
  // lists open and one pencil, ticks the wrong company. The title is the players' by a clerk's slip.
  Relation titleByAccident(place).
  Rule slip_of_the_pencil at audience when auditioned(rierdan) and at(party, audience) and not titleByAccident(rierdan)
    says "In the pause after the laughter the Chamberlain turns two pages at once. 'The King's Players,' says Sir Ferrand Pyke, writing it down in the harder pencil, in a voice of great relief, 'are to be the company from the Rotunda's green-room, the Pentrice people, and not the masquers.' He has ticked the wrong column. He does not know it yet. Behind him Osbert Mallam has seen, and is deciding whether to be a good clerk or a happy one." {
    Assert titleByAccident(rierdan). Assert provisional(rierdan). }
  Observe king_verdict near casimir when auditioned(rierdan) and masqueFarce(party) "The King has had a stool brought to the foot of the rug and sits on it, with his chin on his stick, looking at the wreck of the Audience Chamber, the two companies, the Marchants, a bear and a Chancellor under the throne, looking pleased, and then suspicious of being pleased. 'Do it again tomorrow,' he says. 'Somebody write that down.'".
  Observe king_verdict_plain near casimir when auditioned(rierdan) and not masqueFarce(party) "The King has had a stool brought to the foot of the rug and sits on it, with his chin on his stick, looking at the empty rug and the company that played on it, and a bear in the doorway who has not been announced. 'Again,' he says. 'Somebody write that down.' It is a tidy audience, and a tidy audition, and the Chamberlain is oddly disappointed.".
  Relation masquersMet(place).
  Rule masquers_meet when realMasquers(rierdan) and posing(party) and not masquersMet(rierdan) and at(party, concourse)
    says "The wagon of the real masquers is drawn up in the Concourse with its bunting down. A man in a mask looks at you, and at the Wick's playbill under your arm, and at the Marchants' crest on a servant's sleeve. 'We have been the Marchants' masquers for eleven years,' he says, not unkindly. 'So who are you?' The Concourse turns to see. You say what you have been saying, and it is thinner than it was." { Assert masquersMet(rierdan). }
  Topic gosse_audition with gosse "Ask Gosse how he wants the King to see him" when royalCall(pentrice) and not gosseSeen(party) once {
    Says "Gosse is standing at the window of the Sparrow's loft with his back to the room and his head a little on one side. 'Forty-one years,' he says. 'I have played for innkeepers, for bishops, for a duke who was drunk and a duchess who was not, and never for a King.' He does not turn. 'I have never learned his lines,' he says. 'I have only learned where he stands.' He turns, and he is an old man with a good face. 'Tell me how I should seem. As what I am, or as what I was?'".
  }
  Relation gosseSeen(group). Relation gosseHam(group). Relation gosseHonest2(group).
  Topic gosse_was with gosse "As what you were. The King wants a king" answering gosse_audition when true {
    Says "'Good,' says Gosse, and puts back his shoulders, and is forty years younger, and his coat is crimson. 'I shall not let him down.' You are not sure whether you have given him a gift or a trap.".
    On discuss { Assert gosseSeen(actor). Assert gosseHam(actor). }
  }
  Topic gosse_is with gosse "As what you are. He's old too" answering gosse_audition when true {
    Says "Gosse looks at you for a good while. 'That,' he says, 'is a harder part,' and sits down on the hamper, and takes his hat off, and holds it in both hands as if waiting to be called. 'I shall try.'".
    On discuss { Assert gosseSeen(actor). Assert gosseHonest2(actor). }
  }

  Milestone m_gate "went in at the River Gate under a name that was not theirs" worth 80 when posing(party) or gateTruth(party) or gateHonest(party).
  Milestone m_twins "brought the twins into one room" worth 200 when twinsMet(party).
  Milestone m_audition "played for the King" worth 250 when auditioned(rierdan).
  Milestone m_provisional "was appointed, for the season, provisionally" worth 250 when provisional(rierdan).
  Observe audition_score near casimir when auditionScore(rierdan) >= 3 "The King has had the ghost scene played a second time in his head and is trying not to laugh at it again.".
  Observe marchant_note at sparrow_loft when posing(party) and not kitTaken(party) and not kitProved(party) "A note in the Marchants' crest has been pushed under the loft door: HIS LORDSHIP THE CHANCELLOR WILL RECEIVE THE MASQUERS ON LAMP HILL, AND DESIRES TO SEE THE BOY WHO PLAYS THE GIRLS. Hepzibah has underlined the last six words twice, in the hard pencil.".
  Observe farce_hint at audience when masqueFarce(party) and not auditioned(rierdan) and not ((kitTaken(party) or kitProved(party)) and (twinsMet(party) or orielSworn(party))) "The Audience Chamber is the Audience Chamber, with a King in it who has been told a farce and sees one person on a rug. Hepzibah, at your elbow, murmurs that a farce wants its Kit and its Oriel: the Chancellor's hall on Lamp Hill, and the Rotunda's wings. Or you can change the bill.".
  Action change_the_bill(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Hepzibah to change the bill, since the farce has no cast" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, audience) and masqueFarce(actor) and not auditioned(rierdan) and not ((kitTaken(actor) or kitProved(actor)) and (twinsMet(actor) or orielSworn(actor))).
    Time 2.
    On success { Retract masqueFarce(actor). Assert masqueMiser(actor). }
    Result "'The Miser,' says Hepzibah, with the sigh of a woman who has told them. 'The old one. He will know every word.'".
  }
  Relation nameDayPassed(place).
  Rule name_day when royalCall(pentrice) and not auditioned(rierdan) and not nameDayPassed(rierdan) and day(clock) >= arrivedR(rierdan) + 4 and hour(clock) >= 9 { Assert nameDayPassed(rierdan). Set favour(rierdan) to 0. }
  Observe name_day_note at sparrow_loft when nameDayPassed(rierdan) and not auditioned(rierdan) "The King's Name-Day has come and gone without them. A servant of the Household has left a note under the loft door: the King is graciously informed that the players have been delayed, and is graciously willing to see them still, since nobody else has been engaged. Whatever favour the company had earned has gone with the Name-Day, like a bill the Household has not paid.".
  Observe name_day_warning at sparrow_loft when royalCall(pentrice) and not auditioned(rierdan) and not nameDayPassed(rierdan) and day(clock) >= arrivedR(rierdan) + 2 "Hepzibah has chalked on the loft door: THE NAME-DAY IS THE FOURTH DAY. THE KING WILL NOT ASK TWICE. Under it, in her hard pencil: Whatever we have earned with the Chancellor by then is all we have; after, it is forgotten.".
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/act2.kyr:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── Act II: The Mousetrap ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Suspense, and in places horror. The King's brother, Duke Aldous Orvane, fell from the roof of the Tower of Lamps
  // last winter. His grandnephew the Prince has seen him on the roof, and wants a play that will make the man who
  // pushed him show his face. The Duke has his own opinion about waiting. He walks, once the play is promised, one
  // hour at a time from the roof of the Lamps toward the Rotunda, and he is not particular about who he passes.
  // The night is the act. Success may be simply surviving it.
  Relation mousetrapAsked(place). Relation nightOn(place). Relation ghostBound(place). Relation salted(place).
  Relation tarnExposed(place). Relation tarnFallen(place). Relation lotharWounded(place). Relation flyGuard(place).
  Relation decoyBox(place). Relation modePoint(place). Relation modeVague(place). Relation modeCancel(place).
  Relation saltGiven(group). Relation bellRemember(group). Relation bellAvenge(group). Relation bellLeave(group).
  Relation gloveFound(group). Relation playDone(place). Relation lothalTrust(group). Relation lothalDoubt(group).
  Relation nightOver(place). Relation tarnByGhost(place). Relation tarnByFall(place). Relation tarnByArrest(place).
  Measure nightDay(place). Measure ghostHour(place). Measure ghostScore(place).
  Hazard ghost_chill "The Duke's hand" means "Deal (2d6) necrotic damage to ally unless constitution save against (14).".
  Hazard crossbow_bolt "A bolt from the flies" means "Deal (3d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (15).".
  Chapter ch_mousetrap "The Mousetrap" when mousetrapAsked(rierdan) and not nightOver(rierdan) "The Prince has seen his great-uncle on the roof of the Lamps, and the Marshal of the Watch has been kind to him since. The King's Players are to give a play on the second evening.".

  // The Prince on the terrace: he puts the question to the one who answers.
  Topic lothar_ghost with lothar "Go out on the terrace and stand where the Prince can say it" when auditioned(rierdan) and not mousetrapAsked(rierdan) once {
    Says "'You are the players,' says Prince Lothar again, as if you had not said it back. 'You can lie in public. It is the only honest trade in this city.' He looks at the Lamps. 'My great-uncle fell off that roof in the winter. There is a new rail. I have seen him on it, at night, with his cap in his hand, looking down at the Concourse, and I do not see things.' He turns round. 'Do you believe in ghosts?'".
  }
  Topic lothar_yes with lothar "Yes. I've met two" answering lothar_ghost when true {
    Says "'Then I am not mad,' says Lothar, and sits suddenly on the parapet. 'Or you are, which is not the same.' He gives you the Duke's signet ring on a bootlace from round his neck. 'He was pushed. I do not know by whom. I want a play. A play with a man in it who pushes another man, and a ghost, and a king watching, in the Rotunda, in front of the whole court, so that whoever did it cannot keep his face still.' He puts the ring in your palm. 'A ghost knows its murderer. Let it see him.'".
    On discuss { Assert mousetrapAsked(rierdan). Assert lothalTrust(actor). Set nightDay(rierdan) to day(clock) + 1. Give signet_kind to actor. }
  }
  Topic lothar_no with lothar "No. But I'll stage one" answering lothar_ghost when true {
    Says "'A professional,' says Lothar, with bitterness. 'Good.' He looks at you from head to foot. 'I need you to pretend. Do it properly. If you do it half-way the man will know it is a play, and so will the ghost.' He tells you what he wants. It takes until the lamps are lit, and at the end you realise he has not once asked whether the thing on the roof is real.".
    On discuss { Assert mousetrapAsked(rierdan). Assert lothalDoubt(actor). Set nightDay(rierdan) to day(clock) + 1. }
  }
  Topic lothar_play with lothar "I play them. Ghosts are my trade" answering lothar_ghost when true {
    Says "Lothar laughs, once, like a hinge. 'Then you will know where to stand.' He tells you quickly what the play must be and when. 'Tomorrow night. The Rotunda. The Marshal of the Watch will be in the box with the King, and the Warden, and me.' He stops. 'The Marshal has been kind to me,' he says. 'I find I do not like it.'".
    On discuss { Assert mousetrapAsked(rierdan). Assert lothalTrust(actor). Set nightDay(rierdan) to day(clock) + 1. }
  }
  Kind signet_kind "Duke Aldous's signet" is gear described "A gold ring with a tower on it, worn smooth on the inside where a thumb pressed.".

  // The afternoon: three things to be got, and what they cost.
  // 1. Salt, from the guild-wives. The eldest asks a question and the answer decides.
  Topic salt_ask with salt_wives "Ask the Salt-Wives what keeps a dead thing out of a house" when mousetrapAsked(rierdan) and not saltGiven(party) once {
    Says "The three look at each other and the kettle sings. 'Salt,' says the eldest. 'Iron. And a name said right.' She turns the scale over, and the grain falls out. 'But we do not give salt to people who will use it badly. What does a player fear most in a house?'".
  }
  Topic salt_silence with salt_wives "Silence. When they stop listening" answering salt_ask when true {
    Says "'Ah,' says the eldest, and puts a hand in her apron and brings out three little pouches of grey salt, tied with red wool. 'Then you know what the dead fear. They are not afraid of fire. They are afraid of being passed in the street.' She drops them in your hand. 'Put it on a sill. It stops them. It does not stop them forever.' The third wife, who has not spoken, says to the fire: 'And hail to the Marshal that shall be Warden.' Nobody looks at her.".
    On discuss { Assert saltGiven(actor). Give salt_kind to actor. Give salt_kind to actor. Give salt_kind to actor. Assert knows(actor, prophecy_known). }
  }
  Topic salt_applause with salt_wives "Applause. The wrong kind" answering salt_ask when true {
    Says "'Foolish,' says the eldest, not unkindly. 'You'd be afraid of the living.' She gives you a single pouch, as a gift to the young. 'One. Do not waste it.' The third wife says, softly, 'Hail to the Marshal that shall be Warden, and to the Warden that shall be King,' and the others hush her. You have heard it.".
    On discuss { Assert saltGiven(actor). Give salt_kind to actor. Assert knows(actor, prophecy_known). }
  }
  Topic salt_forgot with salt_wives "Being forgotten. Nothing is worse" answering salt_ask when true {
    Says "The eldest closes her eyes. 'Then you will be kind to the dead,' she says. 'That is the whole of it.' She does not give you salt. She tells you the Duke's name, the thing he was called at nine, the name no one else in the city knows. 'Say it to him,' she says. 'Salt keeps a thing out. A name brings it in. You must choose.'".
    On discuss { Assert saltGiven(actor). Assert knows(actor, duke_name_known). Assert knows(actor, prophecy_known). }
  }
  Kind salt_kind "a pouch of the Salt-Wives' grey salt" is gear described "A pouch of grey salt tied with red wool. It is cold in the hand.".
  Discovery prophecy_known "The youngest Salt-Wife has said, to the fire, in the Marshal's hearing last winter and again to you: Hail to the Marshal that shall be Warden, and to the Warden that shall be King.".
  Discovery duke_name_known "The Duke was called Aldie when he was nine. Said to him by the right voice, it brings him in.".
  Action salt_threshold(actor: group, site: place) "Lay a line of grey salt across the threshold" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and holding(actor, salt_kind) and not salted(site).
    Time 0.
    On success { Spend salt_kind from actor. Assert salted(site). }
    Result "You lay it end to end, a finger wide, and the room has a cold edge to it that was not there before.".
  }

  // 2. The bell: Brother Ambros asks what the dead want.
  Topic ambros_dead with ambros "Ask Brother Ambros how to stop a walking dead man" when mousetrapAsked(rierdan) and not bellRemember(party) and not bellAvenge(party) and not bellLeave(party) once {
    Says "'You do not stop him,' says Ambros. 'You answer him.' His hand is on the rope, feeling the tower. 'What do the dead want from a play, if they come to one?'".
  }
  Topic ambros_remember with ambros "To be remembered. His name, said aloud" answering ambros_dead when true {
    Says "'Yes,' says Ambros. He leans down, takes a small hand-bell from beside the stool, and rings it once in the dark of the loft. The note goes into your chest. 'Ring it and say the name and he will stand and listen to the end of it. An hour, perhaps. No more. You will have to mean it.'".
    On discuss { Assert bellRemember(actor). Give handbell_kind to actor. }
  }
  Topic ambros_avenge with ambros "To be avenged. To see the man who did it" answering ambros_dead when true {
    Says "'That is what the living want for them,' says Ambros, but he gives you the bell, and rings it so that you will know its note. 'Ring it at the man you mean and say what he did. The Duke will go to him. I do not say where it ends.' He turns his dead eyes to the roof. 'I never liked the Marshal. He rings his own bell when he comes in. It is the only bell in the city I cannot hear.'".
    On discuss { Assert bellAvenge(actor). Give handbell_kind to actor. }
  }
  Topic ambros_leave with ambros "To be left alone. To be let go" answering ambros_dead when true {
    Says "He is quiet for so long you think he is asleep. 'Then you are one of the rare ones,' he says. 'I will tell you the other way. Salt the doors, and ring the great bell at midnight, three, and he will go up and not come down.' He does not give you the hand-bell. He gives you the right to ring the Bells at midnight, which is a thing no one has been given in forty years. 'Be careful,' he says. 'Some of them are only waiting to be let go.'".
    On discuss { Assert bellLeave(actor). }
  }
  Kind handbell_kind "Brother Ambros's hand-bell" is gear described "A small bronze bell with a worn leather grip, the note of which goes into the chest.".

  // 3. The roof: what the new rail hides.
  Action search_rail(actor: group, site: place) "Look at the new rail, the old wall and the place the Duke stood" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lamp_roof) and not gloveFound(actor).
    Time 10.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert gloveFound(actor). Give glove_kind to actor. Assert knows(actor, glove_known). }
    Result "The old rail was cut, not broken. In the angle of the wall where the iron meets the stone a glove has been jammed, left, soft, lined with squirrel, and darned at the thumb with a stitch you would know in a thousand. On the inside of the cuff, in ink gone brown: E.M.".
    Otherwise "A wind comes up out of the Concourse and takes the whole roof in its teeth. You see rail, wall, and a great deal of sky.".
  }
  Kind glove_kind "a squirrel-lined left glove, E.M." is gear described "A man's left glove, soft with wear, darned at the thumb, with E.M. inked inside the cuff.".
  Discovery glove_known "A left glove marked E.M., lined with squirrel and darned at the thumb, was jammed into the angle of the Lamp roof where the Duke's rail was cut.".

  // The night itself.
  Rule night_begins when mousetrapAsked(rierdan) and not nightOn(rierdan) and not nightOver(rierdan) and day(clock) >= nightDay(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 18 {
    Assert nightOn(rierdan). Assert holdingAct(rierdan). Set ghostHour(rierdan) to watch(clock). Set ghostScore(rierdan) to 0.
    Assert at(duke_ghost, lamp_roof).
    Assert at(gosse, rot_wings). Assert at(hepzibah, rot_wings). Assert at(swale, rot_stage). Assert at(dorcas, rot_stage).
    Assert at(pudding, rot_flies). Assert at(kit, rot_wings). Assert at(tam, rot_wings).
    Assert at(tarn, rot_box). Assert at(lothar, rot_box). Assert at(casimir, rot_box). }
    Person duke_ghost "the Duke's ghost" nowhere {
    Role "a tall old man in a nightcap and a fur-lined gown, with the front of his head missing". Species wraith. Level 3. Numbers 1. Temperament savage.
    Warns "The old man at the rail turns round with his cap in his hand. There is nothing wrong with his face from the side. From the front it is not there.".
    Comes "The Duke comes across the iron at you, silently, with his hand out, and the cold comes first.".
    Flinches "The Duke steps back, once, and looks at his own hand.".
    Pleads "The Duke stands still and looks at you with the side of his face that is there.".
    Fears flame.
  }
  Observe ghost_at_roof at lamp_roof when at(duke_ghost, lamp_roof) and nightOn(rierdan) "At the rail an old man in a nightcap stands with his cap in his hand, looking down at the Concourse. The wind does not move his gown.".
  // One hour a step: roof, hill, Concourse, Row, the Rotunda's front, the stage. Salt on the threshold stops him.
  Relation ghostNext(place, place).
  Initially Assert ghostNext(lamp_roof, lamp_hill). Initially Assert ghostNext(lamp_hill, concourse).
  Initially Assert ghostNext(concourse, playhouse_row). Initially Assert ghostNext(playhouse_row, rot_front).
  Initially Assert ghostNext(rot_front, rot_stage).
  Rule ghost_steps when nightOn(rierdan) and not ghostBound(rierdan) and at(duke_ghost, ?a) and ghostNext(?a, ?b) and not salted(?b) and watch(clock) >= ghostHour(rierdan) + 6 {
    Retract at(duke_ghost, ?a). Assert at(duke_ghost, ?b). Set ghostHour(rierdan) to watch(clock). Increase ghostScore(rierdan) by 1. }
  Observe ghost_near_hill at lamp_hill as sound when nightOn(rierdan) and at(duke_ghost, lamp_roof) "Overhead on the iron, slow, a step, and a pause, and a step, like someone going down a stair in the dark in carpet slippers.".
  Observe ghost_in_concourse at concourse when nightOn(rierdan) and at(duke_ghost, concourse) "The lamps in the Concourse go down one at a time round the ring, as if a hand were passing along them. At the far end, beside the dead fountain, an old man in a gown stands with his cap in his hand.".
  Observe ghost_in_row at playhouse_row when nightOn(rierdan) and at(duke_ghost, playhouse_row) "Every shutter on Playhouse Row bangs shut at once, from the Rotunda to the Wick. In the sudden dark a pie stall goes over on its own. Something cold has stopped outside the Rotunda's doors and is considering them.".
  Observe ghost_in_front at rot_front when nightOn(rierdan) and at(duke_ghost, rot_front) "The marble foyer has a frost on it that was not there a minute ago. Corin Fallow's portraits have all turned a little on their nails to look at the door.".
  Observe ghost_salted at playhouse_row when nightOn(rierdan) and salted(rot_front) and at(duke_ghost, playhouse_row) "At the Rotunda's door the cold comes up against something and stops, like a hand against glass. It stays there. It is waiting for the salt to be lifted.".
  Rule ghost_hurts when nightOn(rierdan) and at(duke_ghost, ?a) and at(party, ?a) and not tolerates(duke_ghost, party) and not ghostBound(rierdan) and not hurtOnce(party) {
    Assert strikes(ghost_chill, party). Assert hurtOnce(party). }
  Relation hurtOnce(group).
  Rule hurt_clears when hurtOnce(party) and not at(duke_ghost, ?a) { Retract hurtOnce(party). }
  // What the ghost can be given. Ringing the bell at the right moment is a thing a person must mean.
  Action ring_remembering(actor: group, site: place) "Ring Ambros's bell, and say the Duke's name, to his face" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and holding(actor, handbell_kind) and nightOn(rierdan) and at(duke_ghost, site) and bellRemember(actor).
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert tolerates(duke_ghost, actor). }
    Result "You ring it and say it: Aldous Orvane. The old man's head comes round. He listens to his own name as if it were a letter in someone else's hand. It takes the whole of a minute. When it is over he is standing at your elbow, looking where you look, as a guest does.".
    Otherwise "The note rings true and your voice does not. The Duke leans in and hears what you meant to mean, and it is not enough.".
  }
  Action ring_avenging(actor: group, site: place) "Ring Ambros's bell at the man you mean, and say what he did" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and holding(actor, handbell_kind) and nightOn(rierdan) and at(duke_ghost, site) and bellAvenge(actor) and at(tarn, site).
    Time 0.
    On success { Assert tarnByGhost(rierdan). Assert tarnExposed(rierdan). Assert ghostBound(rierdan). Assert at(duke_ghost, site). }
    Result "You ring it at the Marshal, in front of everyone, and say it: Aldous Orvane, from the Lamp roof, at midnight, by a man's hand. The Duke goes past you, not through you, and across the floor to the Marshal. Nobody sees what he does. The Marshal sits still, and then not at all.".
  }
  Action ring_midnight(actor: group, site: place) "Ring the great bell three times, at midnight, to send him up" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, bell_nave) and nightOn(rierdan) and bellLeave(actor) and hour(clock) >= 0 and hour(clock) < 2.
    Time 0.
    On success { Assert ghostBound(rierdan). Assert ghostSatisfied(rierdan). Assert at(duke_ghost, lamp_roof). }
    Result "You put your weight on the rope. The bell goes out over the whole city, once, twice, three times. Somewhere on a roof an old man puts on his cap. The cold goes up the Tower of Lamps like smoke, and the iron baskets flare, all at once, and burn down to embers.".
  }
  Relation ghostSatisfied(place).

  // The play: the Mousetrap. Hepzibah asks whose name goes in the poison scene.
  Topic hepzibah_trap with hepzibah "Ask Hepzibah to prompt the Mousetrap" when nightOn(rierdan) and at(party, rot_wings) and not playDone(rierdan) once {
    Says "Hepzibah has the book open on her knee and the pencil in her hand. 'I have been prompting thirty-four years,' she says, 'and I do not put a living man's name in a villain's mouth. It gets people killed. It is not a rule. It is an observation.' She looks at you. 'Whose name goes in the poison scene?'".
  }
  Topic trap_point with hepzibah "The Marshal's. Plainly" answering hepzibah_trap when true {
    Says "She writes it. She writes a good deal more. When she has finished she has not so much written a speech as aimed it. 'Very well,' she says. 'May the Bells have mercy on whoever speaks it.'".
    On discuss { Assert modePoint(rierdan). }
  }
  Topic trap_vague with hepzibah "A name like his. Near enough for him to wince" answering hepzibah_trap when true {
    Says "'That,' says Hepzibah, 'is what I would have chosen.' She writes. The villain is called Marshal Tarsus of Ashmere, which is not at all like anything. 'He will know. The others will not. Everyone is safer except the person who matters.'".
    On discuss { Assert modeVague(rierdan). }
  }
  Topic trap_cancel with hepzibah "No name. Cancel the trap. Play something else" answering hepzibah_trap when true {
    Says "She shuts the book. 'There is a time,' she says, 'to put the pencil down. It is when you are asked to write someone's death for someone else's conscience.' She nods. 'I think that is now. I will tell the Prince.' She does not look sorry. She looks like someone who has put down something heavy.".
    On discuss { Assert modeCancel(rierdan). Assert playDone(rierdan). }
  }
  Action stage_mousetrap(actor: group, site: place) "Give the signal for the curtain, and the play" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, rot_wings) or at(actor, rot_flies)) and nightOn(rierdan) and not playDone(rierdan) and modePoint(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 21.
    Time 20.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert playDone(rierdan). Assert tarnExposed(rierdan). Assert tarnByArrest(rierdan). }
    On failure { Assert playDone(rierdan). }
    Result "The curtain goes up on the Duke of Ashmere at his supper, and the Rotunda is quiet in the way a house is quiet when it knows it is being watched. In the box the Marshal's hand goes to his collar. Then the ghost comes on, played by Swale, in the nightcap, with a face of white flour, and says the Duke's last words as the Prince gave them. In the third row a woman screams. The Marshal gets up. He looks past the stage. He looks at the Prince.".
    Otherwise "It is a competent play. The house is moved. The Marshal watches with every sign of a clear conscience, and applauds in the right places. The Prince, in the box, sits with his hand over his mouth.".
  }
  Action stage_mousetrap_vague(actor: group, site: place) "Give the signal for the curtain, and the play with the villain who is not anyone" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, rot_wings) or at(actor, rot_flies)) and nightOn(rierdan) and not playDone(rierdan) and modeVague(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 21.
    Time 20.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert playDone(rierdan). Assert tarnShaken(rierdan). }
    On failure { Assert playDone(rierdan). }
    Result "The curtain goes up on Marshal Tarsus of Ashmere, and the Rotunda is a house at a play. In the box the Marshal of the Watch sits with a still face. When Tarsus is exposed at the supper he does not rise; he turns his glove over and looks into it. The Prince has seen him do it. The Prince does not understand what he has seen.".
    Otherwise "It is a decent play about an unknown Tarsus, and the house enjoys it. The Marshal applauds in the right places and does not turn his head.".
  }
  Relation tarnShaken(place).
  // The assassin: Tarn, once seen, goes for the Prince in the interval, from the flies.
  Rule tarn_strikes when nightOn(rierdan) and playDone(rierdan) and (modePoint(rierdan) or modeVague(rierdan)) and not tarnByArrest(rierdan) and not lotharWounded(rierdan) and not flyGuard(rierdan) and not decoyBox(rierdan) and not tarnFallen(rierdan) and not ghostBound(rierdan) and (hour(clock) >= 22 or hour(clock) < 5) and at(party, rot_wings)
    says "In the dark of the interval something goes up the fly ladder two rungs at a time. A string twangs. A bolt comes down out of the loft and goes into the back of the royal chair, through the velvet. The Prince is on the floor of the box with his arm held in the other hand and a face of astonished fury." {
    Assert lotharWounded(rierdan). Assert tarnByFall(rierdan). }
  Rule guard_lapses when flyGuard(rierdan) and nightOn(rierdan) and not at(party, rot_flies) { Retract flyGuard(rierdan). }
  Rule tarn_strikes_unseen when nightOn(rierdan) and playDone(rierdan) and (modePoint(rierdan) or modeVague(rierdan)) and not tarnByArrest(rierdan) and not lotharWounded(rierdan) and not decoyBox(rierdan) and not tarnFallen(rierdan) and not ghostBound(rierdan) and (hour(clock) >= 22 or hour(clock) < 5) and not at(party, rot_wings) and not at(party, rot_flies) {
    Assert lotharWounded(rierdan). Assert tarnByFall(rierdan). }
  Action guard_flies(actor: group, site: place) "Take up Pudding's place in the fly-loft with a sandbag and a cold stare" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rot_flies) and nightOn(rierdan) and not flyGuard(rierdan).
    Time 0.
    On success { Assert flyGuard(rierdan). }
    Result "You settle behind the cloud with the sandbag across your knees. Anyone coming up that ladder will find you in the way.".
  }
  Action decoy_the_prince(actor: group, site: place) "Put Kit in the Prince's cloak in the royal chair, and the Prince in the pit" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rot_box) and nightOn(rierdan) and not decoyBox(rierdan) and (kitProved(actor) or kitTaken(actor) or following(kit, actor) or at(kit, rot_wings)).
    Time 0.
    On success { Assert decoyBox(rierdan). }
    Result "Kit goes into the Prince's black cloak with a great deal of dignity and a hat pulled down. In the half-light of the box he is exactly a Prince of nineteen who has not slept. Lothar looks at him and says: 'Is that how I stand?' and is moved to the pit, to the left, behind a pillar, where a bolt cannot get him.".
  }
  Rule tarn_falls when nightOn(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) < 12 and day(clock) > nightDay(rierdan) and not nightOver(rierdan) and (tarnExposed(rierdan) or lotharWounded(rierdan) or tarnByGhost(rierdan) or tarnShaken(rierdan) or gloveFound(party)) {
    Assert nightOver(rierdan). Retract nightOn(rierdan). Retract holdingAct(rierdan). Assert tarnFallen(rierdan). Assert bodyLies(pentrice).
    Assert at(duke_ghost, lamp_roof). Retract flyGuard(rierdan). }
  // Nothing laid at his door: the Marshal lives, the night is only a night, and there is no body for the Edict.
  Relation marshalLives(place).
  Rule night_ends_quiet when nightOn(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) < 12 and day(clock) > nightDay(rierdan) and not nightOver(rierdan) and not tarnExposed(rierdan) and not lotharWounded(rierdan) and not tarnByGhost(rierdan) and not tarnShaken(rierdan) and not gloveFound(party) {
    Assert nightOver(rierdan). Retract nightOn(rierdan). Retract holdingAct(rierdan). Retract flyGuard(rierdan). Assert marshalLives(rierdan). Assert actIIIDone(rierdan). Assert at(duke_ghost, lamp_roof). }
  Observe marshal_lives_note at concourse when marshalLives(rierdan) "Marshal Edric Marrick rides up Lamp Hill at nine with his scarred hand on the rein, and tips his hat to a player. He has no idea what he did not do. Clemency Orde, in the Wick, is writing a long angry letter to nobody: 'No body, no fifth act.'".
  Rule by_default when nightOver(rierdan) and not tarnByGhost(rierdan) and not tarnByArrest(rierdan) and not tarnByFall(rierdan) { Assert tarnByFall(rierdan). }
  Observe morning_news at concourse when nightOver(rierdan) and tarnByGhost(rierdan) "The city has found the Marshal of the Watch in the royal box of the Rotunda, in his chair, dead and unmarked, with an expression of the deepest civility. The Watch will say nothing. The Salt-Wives have said, to anyone who asks, that it rained on Thursday.".
  Observe morning_news2 at concourse when nightOver(rierdan) and tarnByArrest(rierdan) and not tarnByGhost(rierdan) "At first light the Watch comes down the Lamp Hill road with its Marshal between two halberdiers, in his shirt, with a glove missing. The Warden has not slept. The King has said only: Take him to the Tower of Dust. It is done before the bells ring nones, in the yard of the Dust, by men who do not look at his face; and by evening he is a body on a plank, and the Edict is being lettered.".
  Observe morning_sling at concourse when nightOver(rierdan) and lotharWounded(rierdan) "The Prince is about the Concourse with his arm in a sling, and a face of astonished fury, and has asked to see the Marshal. He was told it would not be proper.".
  Observe glove_fits at lamp_roof when gloveFound(party) and nightOver(rierdan) "The glove you took off the roof is a man's glove, left-handed, with a scorch at the thumb where a fuse is lit. The Marshal's left hand, when they laid him out, had the scorch. Nobody asked you for the glove. It is the only proof the Duke's murder will ever have, and the Duke is not in a position to ask for it.".
  Rule glove_names_him when gloveFound(party) and nightOver(rierdan) and not tarnExposed(rierdan) { Assert tarnExposed(rierdan). }
  Observe morning_news3 at concourse when nightOver(rierdan) and tarnByFall(rierdan) and not tarnByGhost(rierdan) and not tarnByArrest(rierdan) "They found the Marshal at dawn in the Concourse, at the foot of the Tower of Lamps. He had gone up to the roof in the night and did not come down by the stair. The new rail is gone.".
  Observe morning_still at concourse when nightOver(rierdan) and ghostSatisfied(rierdan) and tarnByFall(rierdan) "At dawn the Marshal of the Watch went up the Tower of Lamps alone, and stood a while at the new rail. He did not say why. The bells of the Seven are all ringing the same hour, for once.".
  Milestone m_signet "was given the Duke's ring" worth 100 when holding(party, signet_kind).
  Milestone m_salt "had salt from the Wives" worth 100 when saltGiven(party).
  Milestone m_night "lived through the night of the Mousetrap" worth 350 when nightOver(rierdan).
  Observe ghost_reached at concourse when nightOver(rierdan) and ghostScore(rierdan) >= 5 "A crowd stands in front of the Rotunda in the grey light looking at the doors. The frost on the front step has not melted. The Duke walked the whole way, they say, and has gone in.".
  Relation courtHome(place).
  Rule court_home when nightOver(rierdan) and not courtHome(rierdan) { Assert courtHome(rierdan). Assert at(casimir, audience). Assert at(lothar, terrace). }
  Rule marshal_home when marshalLives(rierdan) and at(tarn, ?x) and distinct(?x, lamp_hill) { Retract at(tarn, ?x). Assert at(tarn, lamp_hill). }
  Rule marshal_gone when tarnFallen(rierdan) and at(tarn, ?x) { Retract at(tarn, ?x). }
  Observe lothar_yes_note near lothar when lothalTrust(party) and not nightOver(rierdan) "Prince Lothar has not let the signet out of his sight. He looks at you now and then, as if you were the only thing left that he had not yet doubted.".
  Observe lothar_no_note near lothar when lothalDoubt(party) and not nightOver(rierdan) "Prince Lothar looks at you the way one looks at a rope he is going to have to trust.".
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/act3.kyr:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── Act III: The Unburied ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Tragedy. The Marshal of the Watch is dead and a traitor by the Warden's reckoning, and the law of the Tower of Dust
  // is that a traitor lies in the Field of Exposure three days under the sky, unmourned, and then goes to the river.
  // His daughter is an acolyte of the Bells, whose first rule is that no dead thing lies unwept. The Warden who made
  // the edict is a just man. His son loves the daughter. A blind man in the bell-tower has a prophecy nobody wants.
  // Loss is possible and nothing forces it: there are six ways through the three nights and they cost different things.
  // There is no hearing. It is a field, a spade and a night.
  Relation edictOn(place). Relation prophecyHeard(group). Relation verrallSoftened(group). Relation lucanPleaded(group).
  Relation ysoltAsked(group). Relation ysoltBury(group). Relation clemAsked(group).
  Relation buriedNight(place). Relation ysoltSealed(place). Relation ysoltFree(place). Relation lucanDead(place).
  Relation lucanLives(place). Relation verrallResigned(place). Relation verrallStays(place). Relation actIIIDone(place).
  Relation bodyTaken(place). Relation bodyStaged(place). Relation pardoned(place).
  Relation clemFurious(place). Relation clemSatisfied(place). Relation lucanLoved(group). Relation lucanFled(place).
  Measure exposeDay(place). Measure ysoltTrust(group).
  Hazard sexton_blow "A sexton's mattock" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13).".
  Chapter ch_unburied "The Unburied" when bodyLies(pentrice) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) "The Field of Exposure has one who on it, under the sky, with a sexton at each corner. The birds have not come down yet.".

  Rule edict_issued when bodyLies(pentrice) and not edictOn(rierdan) {
    Assert edictOn(rierdan). Set exposeDay(rierdan) to day(clock). Assert at(tarn_body, field). }
  Thing tarn_body "the Marshal's body" at field {
    State lying "A big man lies on his back on the mown grass in his shirt, with his hands at his sides and a square of grey cloth over the face. Four sextons stand at the corners of the Field. It is quiet. The birds sit in a row on the wall.".
    State buried "The grass is lifted at one end of the Field in a long strip, and put back. There is nothing to be seen but a rectangle of dark earth.".
    State taken "The grey cloth lies folded on the grass. The Field is empty.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(tarn_body, lying).
  Person sextons "the sextons" at field {
    Role "four grey-robed sextons, one at each corner of the Field". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Numbers 4. Peaceable.
    Greets "The nearest sexton lowers his mattock from his shoulder. 'The Field is the Warden's three days,' he says. 'You will stand back to the wall.' They do not strike a visitor. They strike whoever puts a hand to the turf, and they wait, at the corners, for the one sort of thing the Edict allows them to hear: a verdict.".
    Warns "The nearest sexton lowers his mattock from his shoulder. 'The Field is the Warden's three days,' he says. 'You will stand back to the wall.'".
    Comes "The sextons come in from the corners with their mattocks level, in step.".
  }
  Observe sexton_roll at sexton_hall when edictOn(rierdan) "The Sextons' roll hangs by the stove, a long column of names on grey paper. The newest, at the foot, in a fresh hand, is EDRIC MARRICK, LATE MARSHAL, with a line ruled under it and the days of his exposure ticked off in pencil. Under it a sexton has written, for his own use, in a smaller hand: 'Wardens decide. We hear.'".
  Observe edict_posted at concourse when edictOn(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) "The Edict is nailed to the dead fountain in the Warden's hand: ON THE TRAITOR EDRIC MARRICK LATE MARSHAL OF THE WATCH. THREE DAYS UNDER THE SKY, UNWEPT, UNBURIED, AND THEN THE RIVER. WHOEVER COVERS HIM, OR MOURNS HIM IN PUBLIC, IS SEALED IN THE DUST. By order, C. VERRALL, WARDEN. Below it someone has pasted a ballad about the Marshal. Below that, someone has torn it down.".

  // The Warden. The Prince has told him. He is sorry. He will not move.
  Topic verrall_ask with dray "Ask the Warden whether it must be the whole three days" when edictOn(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) once {
    Says "Lord Warden Verrall does not look up from the paper in front of him. 'Edric Marrick was my friend for thirty years,' he says. 'He taught my son to ride. The Watch says he was the Prince's enemy and the Duke's murderer, and I am the Warden of the Realm: what the Watch says, I am bound to treat as so. If I unwrite the Edict for a friend, I have written a law for friends, and the Seven Seats are a hundred and forty years of men saying that the law is not for friends.' He lifts his eyes. 'You are going to ask me something. Ask it as someone who would have to live in a city where I said yes.' He pauses. 'Would you?'".
  }
  Topic verrall_yes with dray "Yes. I'd live in it" answering verrall_ask when true {
    Says "'Then you are not a Warden,' says Verrall, without heat. 'Good.' He goes back to the paper. 'I shall not do it.' He has heard you. It has cost him something to hear you. You can tell.".
    On discuss { Assert verrallSoftened(actor). }
  }
  Topic verrall_no with dray "No. A city where the Warden bends is a city of bent men" answering verrall_ask when true {
    Says "Verrall nods, by degrees. 'Yes,' he says. 'Yes.' It is not the answer he wanted, but it is the one he has been given by everyone, and he takes it up like a coat. 'The Field is three days.' He looks past you again.".
    On discuss { Assert verrallHardened(actor). }
  }
  Topic verrall_son with dray "Ask where his son is, and does he know" when edictOn(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) once {
    Says "'My son is on duty at the Dust Gate,' says Verrall. 'He asked me last night, in the same voice you are using now, whether I would hear the girl. I said I would hear anyone who came by the door of the Seats.' He puts the pen down. 'She has not come by the door of the Seats. She is in the Bells. She is on her knees. I understand she has been there since the Edict.' He covers his eyes with one hand. 'I wish she would come by the door.'".
  }

  // The acolyte. She asks one thing, and means it.
  Topic ysolt_ask with ysolt "Speak to the acolyte of the Bells, who is on her knees" when edictOn(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) once {
    Says "Ysolt Marrick does not look round. 'They tell me it is wrong,' she says, to the rope. 'To weep. They tell me the dead may not be wept for in public, and I have not wept in public. I have wept in the Bells, which is not public, because nobody comes.' Her voice is steady. 'He was my father. He was also a murderer, I think, and I think he was a good father. I do not need anyone to tell me those can be true together.' She turns. 'I am going to bury him. You may help me, or you may watch, or you may stop me. Which would you do?'".
  }
  Topic ysolt_help with ysolt "Help you, if I can" answering ysolt_ask when true {
    Says "She looks at you for a long moment. 'Be careful what you offer,' she says. 'They will seal whoever covers him. I would not like it to be someone I had asked.' But her hands have stopped shaking. 'The second night. There are two sextons at the east corner who share a flask.'".
    On discuss { Assert ysoltBury(actor). Assert ysoltAsked(actor). Increase ysoltTrust(actor) by 1. }
  }
  Topic ysolt_watch with ysolt "Watch. It is yours to do" answering ysolt_ask when true {
    Says "'Thank you,' says Ysolt, and means it, and you can see it is the first kindness she has had since the Edict. 'It is a mercy to be left alone with a thing.' She makes the sign of the Bells. 'The second night.'".
    On discuss { Assert ysoltAsked(actor). }
  }
  Topic ysolt_stop with ysolt "Stop you. I don't think you've counted the cost" answering ysolt_ask when true {
    Says "Her face shuts like a book. 'I have counted it,' she says. 'It is the only thing I have been counting since the Edict.' She turns back to the rope. 'You can tell the Warden. Lucan will not.' She has said his name without thinking, and then she stops.".
    On discuss { Assert ysoltAsked(actor). Assert stopTried(actor). }
  }
  Relation stopTried(group). Relation ysoltDefiant(place). Relation ysoltBroken(place).
  Action hold_ysolt(actor: group, site: place) "Keep Ysolt from the Field, by whatever can be said to her face" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, bell_nave) and edictOn(rierdan) and stopTried(actor) and not ysoltStopped(actor) and not ysoltDefiant(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan).
    Time 10.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_formidable).
    On success { Assert ysoltStopped(actor). Assert ysoltBroken(rierdan). }
    On failure { Assert ysoltDefiant(rierdan). }
    Result "You tell her what the sextons will do, and what the Warden will do, and what her brother will do, and you tell her the truth, which is that her father would not have wanted her sealed. It works. Something in her goes out like a lamp. She nods. She takes off the acolyte's cord and lays it on the rope. 'I am not going,' she says. She does not say it to you.".
    Otherwise "She listens to all of it and says, 'You are very kind,' and that is the end of it. You have told her you mean to stop her. She will now be careful to be where you are not.".
  }


  // The blind ringer: a prophecy given only to someone who answers what he is owed.
  Topic ambros_edict with ambros "Ask Brother Ambros what the bells say of the Edict" when edictOn(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) once {
    Says "'The Bells say nothing,' says Ambros. 'The Bells ring the hours. The hours say the dead are owed.' He turns his dead face to you. 'I am old, and I am blind, and the Wardens have never believed in anything I say, so I may as well say it. Whom do the dead belong to? The city that fed them? The god that took them? The people who weep?'".
  }
  Topic ambros_city with ambros "The city. They were fed by it, and they owe it a clean death" answering ambros_edict when true {
    Says "'A fair answer,' says Ambros sadly. 'I have heard it from Wardens since I was a boy. It is the answer that buries cities.' He holds her tongue else. The tower hums.".
    On discuss { Assert ambrosGrieves(actor). }
  }
  Topic ambros_weep with ambros "The ones who weep. They are the only ones the dead have" answering ambros_edict when true {
    Says "He is silent so long the bells shift a little in their cradles. 'Then you will hear it,' he says. 'Tell the Warden: the day the Edict is carried out, the Warden's own house will have a body in it that is not buried, and a daughter in the Dust, and a son in the wall. I do not say it to be cruel. I say it as I would say there is rain by Thursday.' His hand goes to the rope. 'He will not like it from me. He may like it from you.'".
    On discuss { Assert prophecyHeard(actor). }
  }
  Topic ambros_god with ambros "The god. And the god does not take orders from Wardens" answering ambros_edict when true {
    Says "Ambros smiles for the first time. It changes his face a great deal. 'That is the thing the nuns say, and then do what the Wardens say,' he says. 'If you mean it, you will find the tower is on your side. I cannot make the bells ring for a traitor. I can make them ring for a man.' He takes his hand from the rope. 'I have not decided which he is.'".
    On discuss { Assert prophecyHeard(actor). Assert bellsOffered(actor). }
  }
  Relation bellsOffered(group). Relation verrallRefused(place). Relation outTried(place). Relation wardenFact(group).
  // The harder fact: the Warden will not bend for an old man's prophecy and a son's tears. He will for a hole in his own law.
  Topic verrall_law with dray "Show the Warden the Edict's own words: UNWEPT, UNBURIED, and who is to carry out its third clause" when edictOn(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) and (tarnExposed(rierdan) or gloveFound(party)) and not wardenFact(party) once {
    Says "Verrall takes the Edict and reads it as if he had not written it. 'Whoever covers him, or mourns, shall be sealed.' He puts his thumb on a line. 'And the river afterward.' He stops. 'The Edict says the Warden carries out the third day. It does not say what the Warden does if the man was named before the city by a court of the Realm, as he was. It says nothing of one whose guilt is already in the Chamberlain's book.' He sets it down. 'I wrote it for a traitor. I wrote it to be read by men who would not ask whether he was named.' A pause. 'He was named.' That is the fact. He does not look glad.".
    On discuss { Assert wardenFact(actor). }
  }

  // The Warden's son, who asks something of the player that nobody should have to be asked.
  Topic lucan_ask with lucan "Speak to Lucan Verrall at the Dust Gate" when edictOn(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) once {
    Says "Lucan is on the gate and has been two nights, and has not slept, and has stopped pretending he has. 'He gave me this post himself,' he says. 'Himself! I think he thought it was a kindness.' He kicks the pillar. 'She'll come. She'll come over that wall at midnight with a spade, and I'll have to put my hand on her, and I swear to you I can feel it already.' He wipes his face with his sleeve. 'You. You're not anybody. What would you do?'".
  }
  Topic lucan_stop with lucan "Yes. And you'd have to live with it" answering lucan_ask when true {
    Says "'Yes,' says Lucan, in a small voice. 'That is what my father would say.' He puts a hand on the pommel of his sword, and takes it off again. 'I'll be here.'".
    On discuss { Assert lucanHeldGate(actor). }
  }
  Topic lucan_look with lucan "No. Look the other way. Nobody will thank you for the other thing" answering lucan_ask when true {
    Says "Lucan stares. 'You are telling me to break my oath,' he says. Then: 'I have been wanting to be told that for two days.' He turns his back, in a manner that is almost military, on the road to the Field. 'I am looking at the wall.'".
    On discuss { Assert lucanLoved(actor). }
  }
  Topic lucan_plead with lucan "Go to your father yourself. Tell him what he's done" answering lucan_ask when true {
    Says "'I have,' says Lucan. 'He heard me.' A pause. 'He heard me,' he says again, in a voice that has been keeping the price. 'I do not know what else there is. If you can think of what else there is, I will do it.'".
    On discuss { Assert lucanPleaded(actor). }
  }

  // ── The six ways through ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // 1. Help her bury him on the second night (the tragic path, if no one else acts: she is caught, and sealed).
  Action help_bury(actor: group, site: place) "Take a spade and help Ysolt Marrick lift the turf" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, field) and edictOn(rierdan) and not buriedNight(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 23 and day(clock) >= exposeDay(rierdan) + 1 and ysoltBury(actor) and ysoltTrust(actor) >= 1 and not actIIIDone(rierdan).
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert buriedNight(rierdan). Assert state(tarn_body, buried). Assert buriedUnseen(rierdan). Assert actIIIDone(rierdan). Assert lucanLives(rierdan). Assert verrallStays(rierdan). }
    On failure { Assert strikes(sexton_blow, actor). Assert buriedNight(rierdan). Assert state(tarn_body, buried). Assert caughtBurying(rierdan). }
    Result "The two sextons at the east corner are passing a flask. It is a clear night. You lift the turf in long strips, as she shows you, with a spade each, and lay it on a cloth, and dig, and the earth is loose and sweet. At the bottom she kneels and says the words of the Bells in a whisper. You cover him. Neither of you speaks, and when you lay the turf back in its strips you could not tell where it had been.".
    Otherwise "A boot scrapes. A sexton's lantern swings and a voice says, calmly: 'Who is it?'".
  }
  Relation caughtBurying(place). Relation buriedUnseen(place). Relation ysoltExiled(place). Relation verrallShamed(place). Relation gosseBanned(place).
  Relation ysoltStopped(group). Relation lucanHeldGate(group). Relation verrallHardened(group). Relation ambrosGrieves(group). Relation bodyRiver(place).
  // 2. Persuade the Warden himself, on the second night, at the Dust Gate. Needs the prophecy and a plea.
  Action beg_verrall(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Warden what the blind man said, and what his son said, at the Dust Gate" {
    Speaker dray.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, dust_gate) and at(dray, dust_gate) and edictOn(rierdan) and (prophecyHeard(actor) or bellsOffered(actor)) and (lucanPleaded(actor) or lucanLoved(actor) or ysoltBury(actor)) and wardenFact(actor) and not verrallSoftened(actor) and not verrallHardened(actor) and not verrallRefused(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan).
    Time 5.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_formidable).
    On failure { Assert verrallRefused(rierdan). Retract at(lucan, dust_gate). Assert at(lucan, king_court). }
    On success { Assert pardoned(rierdan). Assert verrallResigned(rierdan). Assert ysoltFree(rierdan). Assert lucanLives(rierdan). Assert actIIIDone(rierdan). Assert state(tarn_body, taken). Assert clemFurious(rierdan). }
    Result "Verrall hears it to the end, standing, in the lamp of the Gate. When you have finished he is silent for so long that Lucan, behind him, takes a step. 'I wrote it,' the Warden says. 'I wrote it as a just man.' He puts his hand into his coat and takes out the seal of the Warden of the Realm, and looks at it, and gives it to his son. 'You will take it to the King in the morning,' he says. 'And you will tell him I am an old man who has found the limit of what he can do. And then you will go and tell that girl she may bury her father.' He does not wait for an answer. He goes down the Dust Road, past the sextons, who stand aside, and sits on the wall of the Field in the dark with his back to the body, like a guard, until morning.".
    Otherwise "The Warden listens with his head bowed. 'I know,' he says. 'I know what it will cost. I would rather it cost my house than my word.' He sends Lucan off the Gate that night to the King's Court, under guard of a pretext. It is the first thing the refusal costs; there will be others.".
  }
  Action beg_verrall_heard(actor: group, site: place) "Remind the Warden what he heard you say, and tell him what the blind man said, at the Dust Gate" {
    Speaker dray.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, dust_gate) and at(dray, dust_gate) and edictOn(rierdan) and (prophecyHeard(actor) or bellsOffered(actor)) and (lucanPleaded(actor) or lucanLoved(actor) or ysoltBury(actor)) and wardenFact(actor) and verrallSoftened(actor) and not verrallRefused(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan).
    Time 5.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_formidable).
    On failure { Assert verrallRefused(rierdan). Retract at(lucan, dust_gate). Assert at(lucan, king_court). }
    On success { Assert pardoned(rierdan). Assert verrallResigned(rierdan). Assert ysoltFree(rierdan). Assert lucanLives(rierdan). Assert actIIIDone(rierdan). Assert state(tarn_body, taken). Assert clemFurious(rierdan). }
    Result "Verrall hears it to the end, standing, in the lamp of the Gate. When you have finished he is silent for so long that Lucan, behind him, takes a step. 'I wrote it,' the Warden says. 'I wrote it as a just man.' He puts his hand into his coat and takes out the seal of the Warden of the Realm, and looks at it, and gives it to his son. 'You will take it to the King in the morning,' he says. 'And you will tell him I am an old man who has found the limit of what he can do. And then you will go and tell that girl she may bury her father.' He does not wait for an answer. He goes down the Dust Road, past the sextons, who stand aside, and sits on the wall of the Field in the dark with his back to the body, like a guard, until morning.".
    Otherwise "The Warden listens with his head bowed. 'I know,' he says. 'I know what it will cost. I would rather it cost my house than my word.' He goes into the dark.".
  }
  // 3. Go over his head: the King, through the Prince.
  Action ask_the_king(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the King for the Marshal's burial, in his own audience" {
    Speaker casimir.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, audience) and edictOn(rierdan) and lothalTrust(actor) and (favour(rierdan) >= 2 or holding(actor, signet_kind)) and not actIIIDone(rierdan).
    Time 10.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert pardoned(rierdan). Assert ysoltFree(rierdan). Assert lucanLives(rierdan). Assert actIIIDone(rierdan). Assert verrallStays(rierdan). Assert verrallShamed(rierdan). Assert state(tarn_body, taken). Assert clemFurious(rierdan). }
    Result "The King listens to you, which he does not always do, and then to the Chamberlain, which he does. 'Edric taught the boy to ride,' he says. 'Bury him.' The Chamberlain writes it down. It will be done by noon. In the doorway, with the seal of the Realm in his hand, stands the Lord Warden, who has been sent for and told, in front of the Household, that his law has been overruled. He looks past you. Lucan, behind him, looks at his father's back. The Warden will keep his office, and every man in the Seven Seats will know what it was worth on this one day.".
    Otherwise "The King hears you out, and turns to the Chamberlain, who says that the Warden of the Realm has His Majesty's entire confidence in the matter of the Edict. The King says: 'Yes.' The Chamberlain writes it in the book.".
  }
  Action ask_the_king_doubtful(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the King for the Marshal's burial, though the Prince has not trusted you" {
    Speaker casimir.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, audience) and edictOn(rierdan) and lothalDoubt(actor) and favour(rierdan) >= 3 and not actIIIDone(rierdan).
    Time 10.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_formidable).
    On success { Assert pardoned(rierdan). Assert ysoltFree(rierdan). Assert lucanLives(rierdan). Assert actIIIDone(rierdan). Assert verrallStays(rierdan). Assert verrallShamed(rierdan). Assert state(tarn_body, taken). Assert clemFurious(rierdan). }
    Result "The King listens, and the Prince, who has stood at the back with his arms folded, says in a stiff voice that he will not oppose it. It is the first thing he has said all day that he did not mean. 'Bury him,' says the King. The Warden is sent for in front of the Household.".
    Otherwise "The Prince does not speak for you and the King does not remember who you are. The Chamberlain writes it in the book.".
  }
  // 4. Take the body in the night and give it to the water: the Salt-Wives' boat.
  Action steal_body(actor: group, site: place) "Take the body from the Field in the Salt-Wives' handcart under the cloth, to the river" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, field) and edictOn(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 23 and (saltGiven(actor) or holding(actor, herring_kind)) and day(clock) >= exposeDay(rierdan) + 1.
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert bodyTaken(rierdan). Assert state(tarn_body, taken). Assert ysoltFree(rierdan). Assert ysoltExiled(rierdan). Assert lucanLives(rierdan). Assert actIIIDone(rierdan). Assert verrallStays(rierdan). Assert clemFurious(rierdan). }
    On failure { Assert strikes(sexton_blow, actor). }
    Result "The Wives' handcart comes down the Dust Road under a load of herring-barrels, with a blue apron on every one of you. The sextons hold their lanterns up and smell it and wave you through. At the Field you lay the Marshal under the barrels and go out by the same gate. At the Salt Quay the three old women are waiting with a boat, a lamp and a sack of salt. 'For the sea,' says the eldest. 'The Bells will call it a wake. The Dust will call it the river. Neither of them is wrong.' Ysolt Marrick, who has come down to the Quay in her grey, goes into the boat with him, because there is nothing left in Dun Rierdan that will not be asked where he is. She looks past the city. She does not say goodbye to anyone, and you are one of them.".
    Otherwise "A sexton lifts the cloth. He looks at the barrels until the lantern gutters, and then at your aprons, and then at your boots. 'Wrong boots,' he says, and the mattocks come round.".
  }
  // 5. Stage the exposure: Clemency's play on the Field, for the Marshal, in the name the Dust demands.
  Topic clem_play with clemency "Ask Clemency Orde what she is writing" when edictOn(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) and not clemAsked(party) once {
    Says "Clemency Orde does not put down the pen. She has been installed in the Wick's wardrobe for six days, in the dead king's cloak, with a candle, three inkwells and a sleep that she takes in the hamper with the lid on. 'The Unburied,' she says. 'A play. A daughter buries her father against the law of the city and is sealed in the vault, and her betrothed follows her, and the city learns something.' She looks up. 'It is going to be the best thing I have written. It is only missing a third act, which is happening at the moment in the Field of Exposure. I should like you to leave it exactly as it is.' She does not smile. 'My father was Lord Mayor of Pentrice, and Gosse made a fool of him, and every sentence he spoke afterward was true and none was kind. I am writing the other sort.'".
  }
  Topic clem_nobody with clemency "Nobody. Write it so nobody dies" answering clem_play when true {
    Says "Clemency lays the pen across the inkwell. 'That is not a tragedy,' she says. 'That is a pageant.' She picks the pen up again. 'I'll write it your way. I'll hate it.' It is a promise made with the eyes of a woman who has been told her house is to be demolished.".
    On discuss { Assert clemAsked(actor). Assert clemSoft(actor). }
  }
  Topic clem_ysolt with clemency "The girl. It is what the story wants" answering clem_play when true {
    Says "'Exactly,' says Clemency, with great gentleness, as one speaks to a student who has at last said the right thing. 'Thank you.' She writes. She does not say that it is a girl. She does not need to.".
    On discuss { Assert clemAsked(actor). Assert clemHard(actor). }
  }
  Topic clem_you with clemency "Whoever the city decides. You write what happens; don't make it happen" answering clem_play when true {
    Says "Clemency's pen stops. She is silent for a time. 'That,' she says, 'is an impertinent thing to say to a dramatist,' and puts the pen down, and looks at it as if she had not seen it before. 'Go away. I need to think about it.'".
    On discuss { Assert clemAsked(actor). }
  }
  Relation clemSoft(group). Relation clemHard(group).
  Action stage_unburied(actor: group, site: place) "Play the Marshal's tragedy at the Field of Exposure, over the body, and name him" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, field) and edictOn(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) and clemAsked(actor) and not clemHard(actor) and hour(clock) >= 19.
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert bodyStaged(rierdan). Assert ysoltFree(rierdan). Assert lucanLives(rierdan). Assert actIIIDone(rierdan). Assert verrallStays(rierdan). Assert gosseBanned(rierdan). Assert state(tarn_body, taken). Assert clemSatisfied(rierdan). }
    On failure { Assert strikes(sexton_blow, actor). }
    Result "Gosse stands at the head of the Field in the Marshal's own cloak as the Chorus and tells the city what it is looking at. Swale is the Warden. Dorcas, who has agreed to it with her eyes shut, is the daughter. At the end of the second scene the sextons lower their mattocks, because the Edict says that a man is exposed until he is named aloud before the city by one with a right, and Gosse, in that great voice, has named him eleven times. Verrall stands at the wall of the Field and does not give the order. In the third act the sextons put down their lanterns and bring the Marshal in on a bier, as the play requires. By the fifth, the dust of the Field has been dug for a grave by men who think they are acting. Clemency, in the dark, with a wet face, has written nothing for an hour.".
    Otherwise "Gosse's voice is carried off by the wind. The sextons wait politely until the end, and then re-form their square.".
  }
  // 6. Take the Marshal's daughter and son out of the city that night, and let the Field be.
  Action get_them_out(actor: group, site: place) "Get Ysolt and Lucan out of the city by the River Gate before the Field is closed" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, river_gate) and edictOn(rierdan) and lucanLoved(actor) and ysoltAsked(actor) and not outTried(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan).
    Time 10.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_hard).
    On failure { Assert outTried(rierdan). }
    On success { Assert ysoltFree(rierdan). Assert ysoltExiled(rierdan). Assert lucanFled(rierdan). Assert actIIIDone(rierdan). Assert verrallStays(rierdan). Assert clemSatisfied(rierdan). }
    Result "Peverell, who is a man of simple loyalties, lifts the bar for the Captain of the Household and a nun, and does not ask where two people are going at midnight with a cart. 'Mind the ford,' he says, as one who has been told nothing and is pleased. They go out into the dark. Behind them in the Field the Marshal lies under the sky with the birds waiting. In the morning the Warden has no son, and no daughter-to-be, and a Field to keep.".
    Otherwise "The sergeant looks at the nun and the Captain. 'In the morning,' he says, kindly. 'Everyone leaves in the morning.'".
  }

  // The default: no one acts. The tragedy keeps its own appointments.
  Rule night_comes when edictOn(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) and not buriedNight(rierdan) and not ysoltStopped(party) and day(clock) >= exposeDay(rierdan) + 2 and hour(clock) >= 3 and hour(clock) < 10 {
    Assert buriedNight(rierdan). Assert caughtBurying(rierdan). Assert state(tarn_body, buried). }
  Rule caught_sealed when caughtBurying(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) and not ysoltFree(rierdan) {
    Assert ysoltSealed(rierdan). Assert actIIIDone(rierdan). Assert clemSatisfied(rierdan). }
  Rule edict_runs_out when edictOn(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) and ysoltStopped(party) and not ysoltBury(party) and day(clock) >= exposeDay(rierdan) + 3 and hour(clock) >= 6 {
    Assert bodyRiver(rierdan). Assert actIIIDone(rierdan). Assert lucanLives(rierdan). Assert verrallStays(rierdan). Assert state(tarn_body, taken). Assert clemSatisfied(rierdan). }
  Observe river_morning at concourse when bodyRiver(rierdan) "On the third morning the sextons lift the Marshal on a bier and carry him down the Dust Road, and nobody follows. The river has him by noon. Ysolt Marrick is not in the Bells. The acolyte's cord hangs on the rope, and the Bells say she has gone to her mother's people on the coast; she did not say goodbye to anyone, and the one who stopped her is on the list of people she will not name. Lucan holds the Gate and has not been told why.".
  Rule lucan_follows when ysoltSealed(rierdan) and not lucanLives(rierdan) and not lucanDead(rierdan) {
    Assert lucanDead(rierdan). }
  Observe sealed_morning at concourse when ysoltSealed(rierdan) "At first light the Warden walks down the Dust Road in his formal robe, alone, with a ring of keys. The sextons stand in two lines. At the door of the Vault a nun in grey goes in on her own feet, and does not look back. The Warden closes the door himself. Afterwards he leans on it, the way one leans on a wall in the dark. Nobody speaks to him.".
  Observe lucan_gone at dust_gate when lucanDead(rierdan) "The Captain of the Household did not go back to his post. They found him at dawn at the Door of the Vault, sitting with his back against it and his sword across his knees, dead, of nothing anyone can name. The Warden has put a cloak over him. He is sitting beside him.".
  Observe lucan_held near lucan when lucanHeldGate(party) and ysoltSealed(rierdan) "Lucan Verrall stood at the Gate for four nights as he said he would. It was his hand on her arm in the end, and the whole of the Household watched it be gentle.".
  Observe verrall_hard near dray when verrallHardened(party) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) "Lord Warden Verrall has been told by one more person that a Warden who bends is a Warden who is not needed, and has taken it, like a coat, and put it on.".
  Observe ambros_grieves at ringers_loft when ambrosGrieves(party) "Brother Ambros rings the hours a little late. Nobody has said anything to him about it.".
  Observe exile_note at salt_quay when ysoltExiled(rierdan) "The Salt-Wives are mending nets on the slip. One of them has a grey wool shawl across her knees that nobody has asked about.".
  Observe shamed_note at king_court when verrallShamed(rierdan) "The Lord Warden Verrall crosses the King's Court at noon with the Household watching him do it. He walks as upright as he did on the day before, and the Household has decided to be busy.".
  Observe banned_note at dust_gate when gosseBanned(rierdan) "A board is nailed to the gate-post of the Dust: NO PLAYER OF THE WICK TO COME WITHIN THE GATE. The sextons say, if asked, that they did not make the rule and they would not have unmade it either.".
  Observe clem_pleased near clemency when ysoltSealed(rierdan) "Clemency Orde has put the pen down. She has the last page in front of her and does not touch it. 'I did not want it to be true,' she says, to nobody. 'I wanted it to be good.'".
  Observe clem_chain near clemency when verrallResigned(rierdan) "Clemency Orde has the Warden's resignation copied out fair. 'He took off the chain,' she says. 'It is a good scene. A man gives up the one thing he is.' She turns the page. 'It is not the scene I was waiting for. You gave me his office instead of his child. I shall have to be grateful.'".
  Observe clem_shamed near clemency when verrallShamed(rierdan) "Clemency Orde is writing furiously and crossing it out. 'A King,' she says. 'A King! Who does not know what he has signed. You made the Crown do the thing the Warden could not, and he will know it every morning, and I have no ending for that.' She underlines a word. 'It is the cruellest thing in the book and nobody dies.'".
  Observe clem_sea near clemency when bodyTaken(rierdan) "Clemency Orde has not spoken of the boat. When she is asked she says, 'Put into the sea. By women. In an apron.' She looks at the pen. 'I would have written that better if I had been there. I would have written it worse if I had been asked.'".
  Observe clem_staged near clemency when bodyStaged(rierdan) "Clemency Orde has her play in the drawer with the last page written and played. 'It was my play,' she says, 'in a field, in front of the Dust, in Gosse's voice.' She cannot look at the drawer.".
  Observe clem_exile near clemency when lucanFled(rierdan) "Clemency Orde has crossed out the word she would have put at the end. 'Past the ford,' she says. 'There is nothing after the ford. You cannot end a play with a ford.'".
  Observe clem_river near clemency when bodyRiver(rierdan) "Clemency Orde has taken the tragedy out of its drawer and put it back. 'The river,' she says. 'Nobody's hands in it. Nobody to blame. I cannot use any of it.'".
  Observe verrall_resigned near dray when verrallResigned(rierdan) "The Lord Warden Verrall has taken off the chain of office and put it on the table. He is looking at a window, as if he had stopped being a wall.".
  Observe tarn_buried_field at field when state(tarn_body, buried) "The turf has been laid back in long strips, with care. There is no sign of the grave but a single white pebble, set on the grass, which is not a thing that grows there.".
  Observe pebble_warden near dray when buriedUnseen(rierdan) "The Lord Warden Verrall comes back from the Field at first light with one white pebble in his gloved hand. He has seen the turf. He looks at the pebble for a time, and then at you, and puts the pebble in his pocket. 'The sextons report the body undisturbed,' he says, each word set down by itself, so that he cannot be misquoted. 'I have inspected it.' He does not say anything else. He will know, for the rest of his life, what he did not see; and so, now, will you.".
  Rule clem_comes when nightOver(rierdan) and not clemInWick(rierdan) { Assert clemInWick(rierdan). Assert at(clemency, lant_ward). }
  Relation clemInWick(place).
  Observe clem_soft_note near clemency when clemSoft(party) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) "Clemency has crossed out a great deal. The margin is a battlefield. She looks up and says, without being asked: 'I have given her a window. It is a small window.'".
  Observe clem_hard_note near clemency when clemHard(party) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) "Clemency has a clean sheet on the desk headed ACT FIVE, and a line under it, and nothing else. She has been looking at it for an hour with the fixed brightness of someone who is waiting to be told what to write.".
  Milestone m_edict "stood in the Field of Exposure" worth 150 when edictOn(rierdan) and been(party, field).
  Milestone m_actiii "came to the end of the three nights" worth 400 when actIIIDone(rierdan).
  Observe bell_for_tarn near ambros when bellsOffered(party) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) "Brother Ambros has put a black ribbon on the knotted rope. He will not say what it is for. He says only that the bells are on your side if they are rung.".
  Observe body_taken_quay at salt_quay when bodyTaken(rierdan) "On the slip at the end of the Quay a handcart stands upturned with a few herring-scales in the bed. The Wives say it blew over in the night.".
  Observe pardoned_court at king_court when pardoned(rierdan) "The petitioners' benches are full of whispering. The Warden of the Realm is on the end of one, in a plain coat, with his hands between his knees, waiting to be sent for.".
  Observe lucan_fled_gate at river_gate when lucanFled(rierdan) "Sergeant Peverell has taken to polishing the bar of the gate that nobody has lifted since. He looks at the road a good deal.".
  Observe verrall_stays_note at concourse when verrallStays(rierdan) and not verrallResigned(rierdan) and actIIIDone(rierdan) "The Warden of the Realm walks across the Concourse at noon as he has for twenty years, upright, alone, with his hand on the Edict he no longer has to read.".
  Observe edict_exposed at concourse when edictOn(rierdan) and tarnExposed(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) "Somebody has written under the Edict, in chalk: HE WAS NAMED BEFORE THE CITY. The sextons have rubbed it out twice.".
  Rule warden_keeps_watch when edictOn(rierdan) and not actIIIDone(rierdan) and day(clock) >= exposeDay(rierdan) + 1 and hour(clock) >= 21 and not at(dray, dust_gate) { Assert at(dray, dust_gate). }
  Rule warden_goes_home when edictOn(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 20 and at(dray, dust_gate) { Assert at(dray, king_court). }
  Observe ysolt_broken_nave at bell_nave when ysoltBroken(rierdan) "The acolyte's cord hangs on the great rope where she left it. The worn place on the floor is bare, and the nuns step round it, as round a grave.".
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/act4.kyr:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── Act IV: The Note ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A caper. The Crown has given the company the Wick, dark for nine years, on a lease that voids if "any instrument of
  // the Players is found false". Master Mauger of the Tower of Coin has lent three hundred crowns for the fit-out and
  // holds, besides, a note for eighty in Absalom Gosse's name, which Ambrose Swale wrote to settle a debt of his own. It
  // is a good forgery. He means to be paid, in a private performance at his daughter's wedding and a speaking part for
  // himself. The note is in the strong-box in his counting-room. The Wick opens on a Saturday, and Master Mauger
  // will be in Lord Rask's box from seven till nine. Nobody is to be hanged, imprisoned or reformed.
  // Whoever takes it back has taken it back, and nothing civic changes: the Tower of Coin will go on lending.
  Relation wickGranted(place). Relation swaleOwned(group). Relation swaleHidden(group). Relation gosseTold(group).
  Relation planPudding(group). Relation planDorcas(group). Relation planTam(group). Relation planOriel(group).
  Relation disguiseHad(group). Relation keyCopied(group). Relation clerkLured(place).
  Relation boxOpened(group). Relation noteTaken(group). Relation noteBurned(group). Relation noteReturned(group).
  Relation caughtInCounting(group). Relation heistOver(place). Relation raskCharmed(group).
  Relation openingNight(place). Relation pomfretBack(place). Relation pomfretArrived(place).
  Measure openingDay(place). Measure alarm(place).
  Chapter ch_note "The Note" when wickGranted(rierdan) and not heistOver(rierdan) "The Wick has a roof, a stage and a lease, and the lease has a clause. It opens on the third evening after the grant, at seven; Master Mauger sits in Lord Rask's box until nine; at ten the doors shut and whatever the company has done, or not done, is done. Master Mauger is fond of the company. He sends flowers.".

  Rule wick_given when actIIIDone(rierdan) and not wickGranted(rierdan) {
    Assert wickGranted(rierdan). Set openingDay(rierdan) to day(clock) + 3. Assert houseGranted(rierdan).
    Assert at(pomfret_clerk, crake_room). }
  Person pomfret_clerk "Corbin Ashplant" nowhere {
    Role "Master Mauger's chief clerk, a long grey man". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "The chief clerk looks at you over a pair of spectacles and does not offer to take your name. 'Master Mauger is at the Exchange,' he says. 'He is always at the Exchange. I am here.'".
  }
  Topic pomfret_terms with crake "Ask Master Mauger about the lease on the Wick" when wickGranted(rierdan) and not heistOver(rierdan) once {
    Says "Master Mauger opens a book and shows you a page of beautiful copperplate. 'Three hundred for the fit-out,' he says. 'At a most generous five in the hundred by the month. And a small matter of eighty crowns, upon a note of hand in Mr Gosse's name, which Mr Swale was good enough to bring me in the spring.' He closes the book. 'I would not dream of troubling the Chamberlain with it. The lease, I am told, is particular about false instruments. I think we understand one another.' He smiles. 'The Wick opens on the third evening, at seven, and I'll be in Lord Rask's box until nine, which I mention only so that you may be easy. My daughter marries at Haysel-tide. I have always thought a private performance would be so nice.'".
  }

  // Swale owns it, or doesn't; Gosse is told, or isn't.
  Topic swale_ask with swale "Ask Swale why he cannot meet your eye" when wickGranted(rierdan) and troupe(swale) and not swaleOwned(party) and not swaleHidden(party) once {
    Says "Ambrose Swale rises, magnificently, and sits again. 'There is a paper,' he says. 'In Isidore Mauger's strong-box. It has Gosse's name on it, and Gosse did not write it. I did.' He looks at his hands. 'I was owed a part. I was owed the Hamlet in Pentrice, and Gosse gave it to the boy. I thought: a trifle. Eighty crowns, to settle a tailor, and a man of my gifts being sat on by a tailor.' He closes his eyes. 'Gosse has never raised his voice to me in nineteen years. I cannot bear to tell him. What would you do?'".
  }
  Topic swale_tell with swale "Tell Gosse yourself, tonight, before Mauger does" answering swale_ask when true {
    Says "'Yes,' says Swale, in the voice he uses for the last act of Lear. 'Yes! I shall go now, to Absalom, and I shall throw myself on his mercy, and he shall do with me as he pleases!' He gets his coat on the wrong arm and has to start again. 'Where is he? Is he in the loft? Has anybody got a handkerchief?'".
    On discuss { Assert swaleOwned(actor). Assert gosseTold(actor). }
  }
  Topic swale_hide with swale "Say nothing. We'll get the paper back and he need never know" answering swale_ask when true {
    Says "Swale's relief is so great that for a moment he cannot speak. 'Thank you,' he says, and takes your hand in both of his, which are damp. 'I shall never forget it.' He will. But he will be useful tonight. A man with a secret is a good accomplice.".
    On discuss { Assert swaleHidden(actor). }
  }
  Topic swale_blame with swale "Let it be a company debt. We'll all say we agreed it" answering swale_ask when true {
    Says "Swale stares. 'You'd lie,' he says. 'For me.' 'For the company,' you say, and he accepts that, because it lets him. 'Gosse will know,' he says, 'whatever we say.' 'Then he'll know,' you say. It is the kindest and least honest thing you have ever said, and Swale has not stopped looking at the door.".
    On discuss { Assert swaleHidden(actor). Assert swaleOwned(actor). }
  }

  // Four plans; the company will not agree. Hepzibah asks the player to choose the one that goes.
  Topic hepzibah_plan with hepzibah "Ask Hepzibah to gather the company about the note" when wickGranted(rierdan) and not planPudding(party) and not planDorcas(party) and not planTam(party) and not planOriel(party) once {
    Says "The company is in the Wick's wardrobe among the hampers. Four people begin speaking at once and Hepzibah rings the prompt-bell, which is how you tell it is serious. 'Jem has a plan,' she says. 'Dorcas has a plan. Tam has a plan. The Marchant girl has a plan, and so far hers is the only one with a seal in it. I have put them in order. I should like you to choose, because if I do I'll be blamed for the result.'".
  }
  Topic plan_pudding with hepzibah "Jem's: a false clerk, a false summons, and a good coat" answering hepzibah_plan when true {
    Says "Jem Pudding stands on a hamper, in the dim, in one of Mauger's own clerk's coats that has been taken in by Pardew. 'I have juggled for clerks,' he says. 'Eleven years of them, in every town in Imbar. They are the worst house there is; they never once look at the stage.' He bows. 'I know exactly what they do not look at. I'll be perfectly dull.'".
    On discuss { Assert planPudding(actor). }
  }
  Topic plan_dorcas with hepzibah "Dorcas's: she keeps Master Mauger in the box, and Lord Rask looks the other way" answering hepzibah_plan when troupe(dorcas) {
    Says "Dorcas is sitting on a hamper with her chin up. 'I'm forty-eight,' she says. 'A girl of twenty can't do what I can do to an old man's attention.' She looks past anyone. 'Lord Rask has a large box and a small mind. I'll keep Isidore Mauger in it till nine.'".
    On discuss { Assert planDorcas(actor). }
  }
  Topic plan_tam with hepzibah "Tam's: over the roof of the Tower of Coin, through the skylight" answering hepzibah_plan when true {
    Says "Tam Hautboy has drawn the Tower of Coin on the floor in chalk, with the skylight and the downpipe and the drop. 'Forty feet,' he says. 'A rope, and a hook, and somebody who has built a great many scaffolds.' He looks at the others. 'I'd want somebody on the street to cough.'".
    On discuss { Assert planTam(actor). }
  }
  Topic plan_oriel with hepzibah "Oriel's: a summons from the Chamberlain, sealed, to take the clerk away" answering hepzibah_plan when orielHelped(party) or orielSworn(party) {
    Says "Oriel Marchant has the Chamberlain's seal in a clay impression as big as a coin, and a stiff piece of the Household's paper. 'I know his hand,' she says. 'I copied it for my father a hundred times. The clerk will go. They always go for the Household.' She hesitates. 'I should be using my father's name, I think. I should like to. A little.'".
    On discuss { Assert planOriel(actor). }
  }

  // The draper's: disguise, a key, and a price. Mistress Pardew knows who everybody is, and sells it.
  Topic pardew_deal with pardew "Ask Mistress Pardew whether she dressed a clerk" when wickGranted(rierdan) and not disguiseHad(party) once {
    Says "Mistress Pardew does not answer. She measures you with her eyes. 'I have dressed every clerk in the Tower of Coin for twenty years,' she says. 'I know the coat, I know the collar, I know where the left cuff is darned. What I do not know is why a company of players should want one.' She takes a pin from her mouth. 'I'll find out in a week. Four crowns, and an alteration. And tell me one true thing you were not going to tell me.'".
  }
  Topic pardew_true with pardew "The note's a forgery. We mean to take it back" answering pardew_deal when true {
    Says "Mistress Pardew sits down on her counter, which she never does. 'Eighty crowns,' she says. 'He bought my husband's debt in the autumn and my husband died of it.' She tears the price-ticket off the coat. 'Take it. Take the key-mould too, I have a copy of the clerk's. It was a thing I did when I was angry.' She puts it in your hand. 'Bring me the paper, when you have it, and I'll burn it myself.'".
    On discuss { Assert disguiseHad(actor). Assert keyCopied(actor). Give clerk_coat to actor. Give key_kind to actor. Assert pardewOwed(actor). }
  }
  Topic pardew_lie with pardew "Costumes for a play about a clerk" answering pardew_deal when true {
    Says "Mistress Pardew looks at you for a long moment. 'Four crowns. An alteration. And you will be telling that to someone else tomorrow.' The coat is a good coat. The key she keeps in her pocket; she says, with her eyes on the pins, that she sells it to the truthful, or to the rich.".
    On discuss { Assert disguiseHad(actor). Give clerk_coat to actor. Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 4 or to nothing. }
  }
  Topic pardew_key with pardew "Ask Mistress Pardew whether the key-mould is still for sale" when disguiseHad(party) and not keyCopied(party) once {
    Says "Mistress Pardew considers the question with a pin between her lips. 'Twelve crowns,' she says. 'Or the true thing you did not tell me, which is cheaper. I am not particular which you pay in. I only take one.'".
  }
  Topic pardew_key_pay with pardew "Twelve crowns. I would rather you did not know" answering pardew_key when true {
    Says "She weighs the coin on her palm and gives you a wax mould wrapped in a bit of cloth. 'You will tell me when you have it done,' she says, 'or not.' It is exactly the right amount of kindness.".
    On discuss { Assert keyCopied(actor). Give key_kind to actor. Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 12 or to nothing. }
  }
  Topic pardew_key_true with pardew "The note's a forgery, and we mean to take it back" answering pardew_key when true {
    Says "Mistress Pardew sits on her counter, which she never does. 'Eighty crowns,' she says. 'He bought my husband's debt in the autumn and my husband died in the debtors' yard.' She gives you the mould. 'Bring me the paper, when you have it. I'll burn it myself, and I'll remember who did not.'".
    On discuss { Assert keyCopied(actor). Give key_kind to actor. Assert pardewOwed(actor). }
  }
  Relation pardewOwed(group). Relation coatSeen(place). Relation roofOut(place). Relation forgeryClue(group). Relation sealUsed(place).
  Rule pardew_betrayed when heistOver(rierdan) and pardewOwed(party) and noteGone(rierdan) and not noteReturned(party) and not pardewSoured(rierdan) { Assert pardewSoured(rierdan). }
  Relation pardewSoured(place).
  Observe pardew_soured_note at draper when pardewSoured(rierdan) "Mistress Pardew's shutters are up in the daytime. A boy at the door says she has gone to her sister's, and will be back at Haysel-tide, and will not be wanting players.".
  Kind clerk_coat "a clerk's coat of the Tower of Coin" is gear described "A grey wool coat with a black collar, smelling of ink and tallow. The left cuff is darned.".
  Kind key_kind "a wax mould of the counting-room key" is gear described "A cake of wax with the key's teeth pressed into it, wrapped in a bit of cloth.".

  // The night. The Wick opens at seven; Mauger is in the box till nine.
  Rule opening_begins when wickGranted(rierdan) and day(clock) >= openingDay(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 19 and not openingNight(rierdan) and not heistOver(rierdan) {
    Assert openingNight(rierdan). Assert holdingAct(rierdan). Set alarm(rierdan) to 0.
    Assert at(crake, wick_box). Assert at(rask, wick_box). Assert at(gosse, lant_stage). Assert at(swale, lant_stage). Assert at(hepzibah, lant_ward).
    Assert at(dorcas, lant_stage). Assert at(kit, lant_ward). Assert at(pudding, lant_ward). Assert at(tam, lant_ward). }
  Place wick_box "Lord Rask's box" is room within lantern at 1, 1.
  Passage wick_box_door "the box stair" is steps between lant_stage and wick_box.
  Observe wick_box_scene at wick_box when true "Lord Rask's box at the Wick is a velvet cupboard over the stage left, with three chairs, a bottle and a good view. Master Mauger has the best chair and the whole of Rask's attention. Below, the house is full. The ghost-light has been put out for the first time in nine years, and somebody has remarked on it.".
  Rule opening_ends when openingNight(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 22 and not heistOver(rierdan) {
    Retract openingNight(rierdan). Retract holdingAct(rierdan). Assert heistOver(rierdan). }
  // The Wick opens even if no one steals anything. Dorcas keeps Mauger in the box, or doesn't.
  Action charm_pomfret(actor: group, site: place) "Take Lord Rask's box for the evening, and a bottle, and Master Mauger's whole attention" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wick_box) and openingNight(rierdan) and not pomfretLocked(rierdan) and not pomfretBack(rierdan).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert pomfretLocked(rierdan). Assert raskCharmed(actor). }
    On failure { Assert pomfretBack(rierdan). Increase alarm(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "Dorcas, in the second act's interval, in a gown not entirely hers, takes the third chair and the bottle and begins to tell Master Mauger, in her best contralto, about her first Cordelia. Lord Rask hangs on every word that is not for him. Mauger has the look of a man being flattered by an expert. You will have until nine.".
    Otherwise "Mauger, who has been flattered by experts, says that he must see to a small matter at the Exchange before the third act. He is up out of the chair. You will have rather less than you thought.".
  }
  Relation pomfretLocked(place).
  Action present_the_summons(actor: group, site: place) "Present the Chamberlain's sealed summons at the counting-room door, and send the chief clerk to the King's Court" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, exchange) and openingNight(rierdan) and planOriel(actor) and not inCounting(actor) and not clerkLured(rierdan).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert clerkLured(rierdan). Assert inCounting(actor). Assert sealUsed(rierdan). Assert at(pomfret_clerk, king_court). Assert at(party, crake_room). }
    On failure { Increase alarm(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "Corbin Ashplant reads the summons through his spectacles. He reads the seal. He gets up, with cold fury, because he knows precisely what he is looking at and cannot refuse it. 'The Household,' he says. 'At this hour.' He goes out past you with his hat. The door is not locked behind him, and he has left the strong-box on the latch, as one who does who means to be back in a quarter of an hour.".
    Otherwise "The clerk reads it twice. 'A good seal,' he says. 'A bad hand.' He looks at you. 'I'll go and ask.' He does not go. He sits down at his desk where he can see you.".
  }
  Action slip_in_while_dorcas_has_him(actor: group, site: place) "Slip in at the counting-room door while Dorcas has Master Mauger in the box, as the gentleman who is expected" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, exchange) and openingNight(rierdan) and planDorcas(actor) and raskCharmed(actor) and not pomfretBack(rierdan) and not inCounting(actor).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert inCounting(actor). Assert at(party, crake_room). }
    On failure { Increase alarm(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "The night porter has been told that Master Mauger expects a gentleman from the Wick about a private performance. You are the gentleman. He lights you up the stair himself and goes down again to the street door, whistling, and the chief clerk, at his desk, has been given a bottle by somebody and is not at all himself.".
    Otherwise "The porter asks which gentleman, and from where, and on whose word. You say the wrong theatre.".
  }
  Action enter_by_roof(actor: group, site: place) "Go over the roof of the Tower of Coin on Tam's rope and in by the skylight" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, exchange) and openingNight(rierdan) and planTam(actor) and not inCounting(actor).
    Time 10.
    Resolve check(actor, climbing, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert inCounting(actor). Assert roofOut(rierdan). Assert at(party, crake_room). }
    On failure { Increase alarm(rierdan) by 2. Assert strikes(roof_fall, actor). }
    Result "Tam throws the hook on the third try. You go up the downpipe like a cat and across the leads on your belly, and the skylight is a pane out of a frame that Tam has had a week to oil. You let yourself down on the rope into the counting-room, which is lit by one candle and smells of Mauger. Tam, on the roof, coughs, twice, to say it is clear.".
    Otherwise "The rope is too short, or you are. You come down the last ten feet by an arrangement of gutters and let go.".
  }
  Hazard roof_fall "The Tower of Coin's gutters" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13).".
  Relation inCounting(group).
  Action walk_in_as_clerk(actor: group, site: place) "Walk in at the counting-room door in the clerk's coat, as if you worked there" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, exchange) and openingNight(rierdan) and planPudding(actor) and disguiseHad(actor) and not inCounting(actor).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert inCounting(actor). Assert coatSeen(rierdan). Assert at(party, crake_room). }
    On failure { Increase alarm(rierdan) by 2. }
    Result "You go in as Jem would, with a pen behind the ear and the expression of a man owed his supper. The night porter says, 'Evening, Mr Dunstable,' and you say, 'Evening,' in a voice that has nothing in it at all.".
    Otherwise "The porter looks at the darn in the cuff, and at your face, and makes a small interrogative noise.".
  }
  Action open_the_box(actor: group, site: place) "Open Master Mauger's strong-box, with a key or without" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, crake_room) and inCounting(actor) and openingNight(rierdan) and not boxOpened(actor) and (holding(actor, key_kind) or capable(actor, lockwork) or clerkLured(rierdan) or forgeryClue(actor)).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, lockwork, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert boxOpened(actor). Assert noteTaken(actor). Give forged_note to actor. }
    On failure { Increase alarm(rierdan) by 2. }
    Result "The box opens with a sound like a small cough. Under a velvet bag of crowns and a miniature of Mauger's late wife there is a single sheet, folded in three, in a hand you have seen on a hundred bills. A. GOSSE. The letters are wonderful. You take it, and shut the box, and the velvet bag is where it was.".
    Otherwise "The tumbler turns and sticks. Somewhere in the Tower a floor creaks.".
  }
  Kind forged_note "the note for eighty crowns, in Gosse's hand" is document described "A note of hand for eighty crowns, in a beautiful, shaky copy of Absalom Gosse's signature. The forger has given the G a flourish Gosse never used.".
  Action leave_unseen(actor: group, site: place) "Go out by the way you came, with the paper, before the third act ends" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, crake_room) and noteTaken(actor) and openingNight(rierdan) and ((alarm(rierdan) < 3) or (roofOut(rierdan) and alarm(rierdan) < 5)).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert at(party, exchange). }
    Result "The porter says 'Goodnight, Mr Dunstable.' You say it back. The Exchange is empty under the lamps. A beggar on a stool counts three piles of coin and does not look up. The Wick's third-act bell is going down the Row, and you are in the pit, in your own coat, before the Alderman has finished dying.".
  }
  Rule alarm_rings when openingNight(rierdan) and ((alarm(rierdan) >= 3 and not roofOut(rierdan)) or alarm(rierdan) >= 5) and at(party, crake_room) and not caughtInCounting(party)
    says "A bell begins to go in the Tower of Coin, a small, bright, officious bell. The night porter says, in a different voice, 'Mr Dunstable is in the Wick.' Boots on the stairs." {
    Assert caughtInCounting(party). }
  // The three endings of the night, and not one of them is a verdict.
  Action burn_the_note(actor: group, site: place) "Burn the note in the Wick's ghost-light" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lant_stage) and holding(actor, forged_note) and not noteBurned(actor).
    Time 0.
    On success { Spend forged_note from actor. Assert noteBurned(actor). Assert noteGone(rierdan). }
    Result "The ghost-light has been out all evening. Gosse relights it himself, at the end, for tradition, and you hold the paper to the flame. It curls round the beautiful G. 'A wonderful forgery,' says Swale, behind you, hoarse. 'I thought so,' says Hepzibah.".
  }
  Action return_note_to_pardew(actor: group, site: place) "Take the note to Mistress Pardew, as promised" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, draper) and holding(actor, forged_note) and disguiseHad(actor) and not noteReturned(actor) and keyCopied(actor).
    Time 0.
    On success { Spend forged_note from actor. Assert noteReturned(actor). Assert noteGone(rierdan). }
    Result "Mistress Pardew holds it over her candle with a pair of sugar-tongs and watches until the last of the G goes. Then she sweeps the ashes into her palm and puts them in the pocket where she keeps the pins. 'Thank you,' she says. It is the only time you will hear her say it.".
  }
  Relation noteGone(place).
  Observe pomfret_next near crake when heistOver(rierdan) and noteGone(rierdan) "Master Mauger has opened his strong-box, looked at the empty place under the velvet bag, closed it, and sat with his hands on his knees. He cannot prove a thing. 'Nine years that theatre was dark,' he says, to the miniature, pleasantly. 'I do hope they will be happy in it.' The Tower of Coin goes on lending. It is not a story that has an end.".
  Observe pomfret_prevails near crake when heistOver(rierdan) and not noteGone(rierdan) "Master Mauger has come down from Lord Rask's box, and has the note out on his desk and a pen beside it, and a diary open at Haysel-tide. 'Not a large wedding,' he says. 'Forty guests. A little speech, in the second act. I have written it myself.' He beams. He has the Chamberlain's ear and Lord Rask's, and nobody to whom he need justify himself.".
  Observe caught_net near pomfret_clerk when caughtInCounting(party) "The chief clerk has locked the door of the counting-room with you inside it and gone for the Watch. It is, he says through the keyhole, a serious thing. He will be perhaps an hour. It is not clear what he thinks you will do in the meantime.".
  // The Seats sit on the Wick's business, and the debtors' yard keeps Mistress Pardew's husband.
  Observe seats_docket at seats when wickGranted(rierdan) "On the Seats' docket for the week, between a dispute over a bridge and a goose, stands MAUGER v. A TRAVELLING COMPANY, on a lease with a clause. It is called, and adjourned, and called again. The clerk of the court is a Coin man, and he is patient.".
  Observe debt_yard_pardew at debt_yard when wickGranted(rierdan) "A cell in the yard has a name scratched over the door: PARDEW, T., DRAPER, FOR EIGHTY CROWNS AND COSTS. It is the one the draper's husband died in. The warder says the Coin Tower bought the debt in the autumn, as it buys the autumn's debts, and that Mistress Pardew comes on Sundays with a clean shirt for a dead man's peg.".
  Milestone m_plan "chose a plan" worth 100 when planPudding(party) or planDorcas(party) or planTam(party) or planOriel(party).
  Milestone m_note "got the note back" worth 400 when noteTaken(party).
  Milestone m_noted "had the note gone, and nothing to show for it" worth 150 when noteGone(rierdan).
  Rule pomfret_walks when openingNight(rierdan) and not pomfretBack(rierdan) and (hour(clock) >= 21 or (not pomfretLocked(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 20)) { Assert pomfretBack(rierdan). }
  Rule pomfret_arrives when openingNight(rierdan) and pomfretBack(rierdan) and not pomfretArrived(rierdan) and at(party, crake_room)
    says "Footsteps on the counting-room stair, unhurried, the footsteps of the owner of the house. A voice says, to somebody, 'I do hope nobody has been at my papers.'" { Assert pomfretArrived(rierdan). Increase alarm(rierdan) by 2. }
  Observe dorcas_plan_note near dorcas when planDorcas(party) and openingNight(rierdan) "Dorcas has the gown on. She has the look of a woman who has been told she is the only plan, and has agreed to be.".
  Observe wick_clock at lant_ward when wickGranted(rierdan) and not openingNight(rierdan) and not heistOver(rierdan) "Hepzibah has chalked it on the wardrobe door, in the hard pencil's capitals: OPENING THE THIRD EVENING, AT SEVEN. MAUGER IN RASK'S BOX TILL NINE. DOORS SHUT AT TEN. Under it, smaller: Whoever is in the counting-room at nine is a burglar.".
  Observe box_hint at crake_room when inCounting(party) and not boxOpened(party) and not holding(party, key_kind) and not clerkLured(rierdan) "The strong-box is a good one, with a lock as big as a fist. It wants a key, or hands that know locks. Mistress Pardew, they say, keeps a mould for the truthful.".
  Action try_the_box(actor: group, site: place) "Try the strong-box with what you have" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, crake_room) and inCounting(actor) and not boxOpened(actor) and openingNight(rierdan) and not (holding(actor, key_kind) or capable(actor, lockwork) or clerkLured(rierdan) or forgeryClue(actor)).
    Time 1.
    On success { Increase alarm(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "It does not open. It is a Coin-tower box with a lock the size of a man's fist, and you have neither Pardew's wax key nor the hands for it nor the clerk's own forgetfulness. The tumbler does not even turn. A floor creaks somewhere overhead, in the way of a house that has heard a lock tried.".
  }
  Rule coat_seen_costs when coatSeen(rierdan) and openingNight(rierdan) and at(party, crake_room) and not coatPaid(rierdan)
    says "The night porter has been looking at you through the glass of his box, and at the left cuff of your coat. He goes up the street door's three steps, and down, and up again." { Assert coatPaid(rierdan). Increase alarm(rierdan) by 1. }
  Relation coatPaid(place).
  Rule light_favour when openingNight(rierdan) and lightLit(rierdan) and not lightLeft(rierdan) and not lightPaid(rierdan) { Assert lightPaid(rierdan). Decrease alarm(rierdan) by 1 or to nothing. }
  Rule light_cost when openingNight(rierdan) and lightLeft(rierdan) and not lightPaid(rierdan) { Assert lightPaid(rierdan). Increase alarm(rierdan) by 1. }
  Relation lightPaid(place).
  Rule printer_clue when printerHired(rierdan) and wickGranted(rierdan) and not forgeryClue(party) { Assert forgeryClue(party). }
  Observe printer_clue_note at print_row when printerHired(rierdan) and wickGranted(rierdan) "Gadsby has been told what the Wick wants with a good lock, and does not ask. He has a thin steel hook in his waistcoat and a printer's contempt for anything that has to be opened by force. It is yours, for the price of a title-page, and you have already paid.".
  Observe light_good_note at lant_stage when openingNight(rierdan) and lightLit(rierdan) and not lightLeft(rierdan) "The ghost-light burns white. A stagehand in the flies has put a rope across the street door of the Wick, for the night, with the care of someone who wants you out of the house in good time.".
  Observe light_out_note at lant_stage when lightOut(rierdan) "The Wick has no ghost-light. The stage is a stage, and the flats stand up when they are told, and nobody in the flies is on anyone's side.".
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/act5.kyr:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── Act V: The Mirrors ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The command performance. Clemency Orde has written a play for the King in which a company of players, a ghost, a
  // daughter, a note and a pair of twins are all, at the last, in one room. Everything the company has done in Dun
  // Rierdan arrives on the Wick's stage on the same evening, and most of it has not been told it is in the play.
  // Scene by scene a complication comes in, and the company can head it off or let it run; what is let run is chaos, and
  // chaos is the whole of the evening. The ending is whatever room it ends in.
  Relation commandOn(place). Relation commandDone(place). Relation bookCorrected(group).
  Relation s1Done(place). Relation s2Done(place). Relation s3Done(place). Relation s4Done(place).
  Relation s5Done(place). Relation s6Done(place).
  Relation fallowSeen(group). Relation maskersSeen(group). Relation duneSeen(group). Relation pomfretStood(group).
  Relation twinsSorted(group). Relation dorcasStays(group). Relation dorcasLeaves(group).
  Relation hepzibahSpoke(group). Relation hepzibahSilent(group). Relation kitStays(group). Relation kitLeaves(group).

  Measure chaos(place). Measure commandDay(place). Measure repertoire(place).
  Chapter ch_command "The Mirrors" when commandOn(rierdan) and not commandDone(rierdan) "The Wick is lit for the first time in nine years. The King is in the box. The company has a play, six hours' sleep between it, and a bear.".

  // The clerk's question, back in the first act, answered here.
  Topic mallam_book with mallam "Ask Osbert Mallam whether he means to correct the Chamberlain's book" when titleByAccident(rierdan) and not bookCorrected(party) and not mallamKept(party) once {
    Says "Osbert Mallam looks at the door to be sure it is shut. 'It was a slip,' he says. 'He ticked the wrong column. Sir Ferrand has a good heart and no sense of which hand is which.' He turns the book so that you can see. 'I have until the Name-Day to put it right. I do not want to be the clerk who saw it and did not say. I do not want to be the clerk who said it, either.' He looks at you. 'What would you do?'".
  }
  Topic mallam_correct with mallam "Put it right. You'll sleep better" answering mallam_book when true {
    Says "'Yes,' says Mallam, miserably. 'That is how I sleep.' He takes up his pencil. The Players are, in the Household's book, a company that has been ticked and un-ticked within a week. You will have to earn it twice.".
    On discuss { Assert bookCorrected(actor). Retract titleByAccident(rierdan). Retract provisional(rierdan). }
  }
  Topic mallam_keep with mallam "Leave it. A slip is a slip, and the King is happy" answering mallam_book when true {
    Says "'I thought you would say that,' says Mallam, with a slow grin; he has been waiting all week for leave to be happy. 'I'll keep it quiet.' He closes the book. It is the only time you will see him close it.".
    On discuss { Assert mallamKept(actor). }
  }
  Relation mallamKept(group).

  // The repertoire grows with what was played.
  Rule rep_miser when masqueMiser(party) and auditioned(rierdan) and not rep1(rierdan) { Assert rep1(rierdan). Increase repertoire(rierdan) by 1. }
  Rule rep_ghost when masqueGhost(party) and auditioned(rierdan) and not rep2(rierdan) { Assert rep2(rierdan). Increase repertoire(rierdan) by 1. }
  Rule rep_farce when masqueFarce(party) and auditioned(rierdan) and not rep3(rierdan) { Assert rep3(rierdan). Increase repertoire(rierdan) by 1. }
  Rule rep_trap when playDone(rierdan) and not cancelled(rierdan) and not rep4(rierdan) { Assert rep4(rierdan). Increase repertoire(rierdan) by 1. }
  Rule rep_unburied when bodyStaged(rierdan) and not rep5(rierdan) { Assert rep5(rierdan). Increase repertoire(rierdan) by 1. }
  Relation rep1(place). Relation rep2(place). Relation rep3(place). Relation rep4(place). Relation rep5(place). Relation cancelled(place).
  Rule cancelled_rule when modeCancel(rierdan) and not cancelled(rierdan) { Assert cancelled(rierdan). }
  Observe board at lant_stage when repertoire(rierdan) >= 1 "On the Wick's board by the stage-door, in Hepzibah's hand, the company's repertoire stands in a column, newest at the top. It is longer than it was.".
  Observe board_miser at lant_stage when rep1(rierdan) "THE MISER'S WEDDING. Safe. Played for a King who knew every line.".
  Observe board_ghost at lant_stage when rep2(rierdan) "THE ALDERMAN'S GHOST. Dangerous. Played in a room that had a ghost of its own.".
  Observe board_farce at lant_stage when rep3(rierdan) "THE MARCHANTS' MEN. Not yet finished. Played in the wrong order, by the wrong people, correctly.".
  Observe board_trap at lant_stage when rep4(rierdan) "THE FALL OF ASHMERE. Played once, at night, in front of a dead man's brother. Not to be played again.".
  Observe board_unburied at lant_stage when rep5(rierdan) "THE UNBURIED. Played in a field. The text is not in the book; it was the city.".

  // The evening opens three days after the Wick's, with a chaos counter and seven scenes.
  Rule command_set when heistOver(rierdan) and not commandOn(rierdan) { Assert commandOn(rierdan). Set commandDay(rierdan) to day(clock) + 3. Set chaos(rierdan) to 0. }
  Rule command_begins when commandOn(rierdan) and not holdingCommand(rierdan) and not commandDone(rierdan) and day(clock) >= commandDay(rierdan) and hour(clock) >= 19 {
    Assert holdingCommand(rierdan). Assert holdingAct(rierdan). Assert at(party, lant_stage). Assert at(fallow, lant_stage). Assert at(casimir, lant_stage). }
  Relation holdingCommand(place).
  Action next_scene(actor: group, site: place) "Give Hepzibah the nod for the next scene" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lant_stage) and holdingCommand(rierdan) and not commandDone(rierdan) and sceneV(rierdan) < 7.
    Time 10.
    On success { Increase sceneV(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "Hepzibah rings the prompt-bell and the stage-hands change the flats. The house waits in the dark.".
  }
  Measure sceneV(place).

  // Scene 1: the entrance. Fallow in a hat. Always.
  Observe s1 at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 1 and holdingCommand(rierdan) "The King is brought in. At the same moment, through the other door, comes Corin Fallow, who has not been asked, in a hat with a plume that goes up four feet and sways. Every head in the house follows the plume. The King has stopped looking at the stage.".
  Action stop_fallow(actor: group, site: place) "Take Corin Fallow by the arm and walk him to a seat in the second row" {
    Speaker fallow.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lant_stage) and sceneV(rierdan) == 1 and not s1Done(rierdan).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert s1Done(rierdan). Assert fallowSeen(actor). }
    On failure { Assert s1Done(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "'Corin,' you say, 'the King is looking.' He is. The plume goes down. He sits in the second row with the dignity of one who has agreed to be someone else's audience.".
    Otherwise "'I'm on the bill,' he says, in the voice of somebody who is not on any bill. The plume is in the King's eyeline for most of the first scene.".
  }
  // Scene 2: the real masquers, if they were ever posed against.
  Observe s2 at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 2 and posing(party) "Through the back of the house come eight people in half-made costumes and a man in a mask. 'We are the Marchants' masquers!' cries the man. 'We are three days late and we have been paid!' The King, who has never seen the end of a play, leans forward with hope.".
  Action quiet_masquers(actor: group, site: place) "Seat the Marchants' masquers in the pit, and promise them the afterpiece" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lant_stage) and sceneV(rierdan) == 2 and not s2Done(rierdan).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert s2Done(rierdan). Assert maskersSeen(actor). }
    On failure { Assert s2Done(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "The man in the mask turns out to be an entirely reasonable fellow called Spandrel who wishes only to be given a part. He is given the Chancellor, and does it very well.".
    Otherwise "Spandrel shouts that he has been defrauded by a bear. The audience is delighted.".
  }
  Rule s2_skip when sceneV(rierdan) == 3 and not s2Done(rierdan) and not posing(party) { Assert s2Done(rierdan). }
  // Scene 3: the light. If the Duke was never put to rest, he takes the box.
  Observe s3 at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 3 and not ghostSatisfied(rierdan) and not tarnByGhost(rierdan) "The ghost-light is lit at the centre of the stage. The flame leans toward the royal box. A cold air goes down the aisle, and in the third chair, between Lord Rask and the Chamberlain, an old man in a nightcap has taken a seat and is looking at the stage with polite attention. Nobody has noticed but the King.".
  Action seat_the_duke(actor: group, site: place) "Ring the Duke's bell, say his name, and give him a better seat" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lant_stage) and sceneV(rierdan) == 3 and not s3Done(rierdan) and (holding(actor, handbell_kind) or knows(actor, duke_name_known)).
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert s3Done(rierdan). Assert duneSeen(actor). }
    On failure { Assert s3Done(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "The note goes down the aisle and the old man turns his head. 'Aldie,' you say, to the third chair. A long look; a settling. The King raises two fingers in a salute. The Duke lifts his cap, and stays for the rest of the play, where the Chamberlain's draught cannot reach him.".
    Otherwise "The note is a note and the name is the wrong one. The old man lifts his cap, perplexed, and walks through the stage.".
  }
  Rule s3_skip when sceneV(rierdan) == 4 and not s3Done(rierdan) and (ghostSatisfied(rierdan) or tarnByGhost(rierdan)) { Assert s3Done(rierdan). }
  // Scene 4: the note, if it is not burned.
  Observe s4 at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 4 and not noteGone(rierdan) "Master Mauger has stood up in the second tier with a paper held high in one hand. 'A note of hand,' he is saying, in the kindly voice of a man at a font, 'in the name of Mr Absalom Gosse, for eighty crowns, which I regret to say I find has not been honoured, and which I should perhaps mention in the presence of the Chamberlain.'".
  Action shout_pomfret_down(actor: group, site: place) "Play the Alderman at the top of your voice until he sits" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lant_stage) and sceneV(rierdan) == 4 and not noteGone(rierdan) and not s4Done(rierdan).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert s4Done(rierdan). Assert pomfretStood(actor). }
    On failure { Assert s4Done(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 2. }
    Result "Gosse, with the whole of his lungs, begins The Alderman's Ghost from the middle. Swale joins in. The Chamberlain, who has been reading the playbill, thinks it is the next scene. Master Mauger sits down by degrees with the paper still in his hand, and the King says, loudly, 'He is not a good actor, that one.'".
    Otherwise "Mauger reads the note out in full. He has an excellent voice. It is the best reading of the evening.".
  }
  Rule s4_skip when sceneV(rierdan) == 5 and not s4Done(rierdan) and noteGone(rierdan) { Assert s4Done(rierdan). }
  // Scene 5: the twins, and Kit.
  Observe s5 at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 5 and (twinsMet(party) or kitTaken(party)) "Oriel, who was not to go on, is on. Cyprian, in the Watch's grey, who was not to be in the house, is in the wings with his mouth open. Kit, in the part of Oriel, is on the other side. The audience sees two Oriels and a lieutenant who is the first. The Chancellor, in the second tier, has put on his spectacles.".
  Action sort_the_twins(actor: group, site: place) "Send the twins on from opposite wings, in the right order, in front of the Chancellor" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lant_stage) and sceneV(rierdan) == 5 and not s5Done(rierdan).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert s5Done(rierdan). Assert twinsSorted(actor). }
    On failure { Assert s5Done(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "Cyprian takes Kit by the shoulder, and Oriel takes Cyprian by the other. For a moment all three of them stand in a line at the footlights. 'My lord Chancellor,' says Oriel, in her own voice, 'this is my brother, and this is the person who plays me, and I am going to be an actress.' There is a pause. Lord Marchant says, from the second tier, distinctly, 'I have never in my life been so bewildered. Go on.'".
    Otherwise "Cyprian takes Kit for Oriel and Oriel for the prompter, and the Chancellor, on his feet, shouts a fond name. Three people answer it.".
  }
  Rule s5_skip when sceneV(rierdan) == 6 and not s5Done(rierdan) and not twinsMet(party) and not kitTaken(party) { Assert s5Done(rierdan). }
  // Scene 6: the grave. What the evening is for, if she is in the vault.
  Observe s6_grave at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 6 and ysoltSealed(rierdan) "The scene of The Unburied is in Clemency's draft for the fifth act. Gosse is to speak the Chorus alone. There is a place in the third row where a girl in grey was to sit. The seat is empty and nobody has put anything on it. Gosse sees it. He stops. The house waits for the company to decide whether to go on.".
  Observe s6_saved at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 6 and ysoltFree(rierdan) "The scene of The Unburied is in Clemency's draft for the fifth act. Gosse is to speak the Chorus alone. In the third row a girl in grey is sitting next to a captain of the Household with his sword in his lap. They are not looking at the stage. They are looking at each other. In the wings, Clemency is white to the lips and cannot be spoken to.".
  Action play_the_chorus(actor: group, site: place) "Give Gosse the Chorus, and let him say it as it is written" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lant_stage) and sceneV(rierdan) == 6 and not s6Done(rierdan).
    Time 5.
    On success { Assert s6Done(rierdan). Assert chorusPlayed(rierdan). }
    Result "Gosse says it. He does not play it. He says every line of it to the third row in his great voice, as simply as one who giving directions, and the house is as still as the Field. At the end he bows to the empty seat, or the full one, as the case may be. Nobody applauds for a good while. Then everybody does.".
  }
  Action cut_the_chorus(actor: group, site: place) "Cut the scene, and go on to the bear" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lant_stage) and sceneV(rierdan) == 6 and not s6Done(rierdan).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert s6Done(rierdan). Assert chorusCut(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 1. }
    Result "'It's a long scene,' says Hepzibah, in a low voice, 'and the King is tired.' You cut it. It is the right thing for the evening. You will remember it.".
  }
  // Scene 7: Patience takes the bow. Always. The romances come to their points in the wings.
  Observe s7 at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 7 and holdingCommand(rierdan) "The scenes are played. The house is in the state of a house that has seen more than it paid for. Out of the wings, unannounced, comes the old bear, Patience, with her collar on and no teeth, and walks to the centre of the stage and sits down. The King stands. He is the first on his feet. After a moment the whole house is on its feet. The King says: 'That is the best actor of the evening.'".
  Relation chorusPlayed(place). Relation chorusCut(place). Relation bowCompany(place). Relation bowBear(place).
  Action bear_alone(actor: group, site: place) "Send Patience out to the call alone, and keep the company in the wings" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lant_stage) and sceneV(rierdan) >= 7 and not commandDone(rierdan).
    Time 5.
    On success { Assert commandDone(rierdan). Assert bowBear(rierdan). Retract holdingCommand(rierdan). Retract holdingAct(rierdan). }
    Result "You do not take them down. You open the prompt-side door and Patience walks out into the light by herself, with her collar on, and sits. The King is on his feet. The company watches from the wings, Gosse with his hand over his mouth, Hepzibah with the book against her chest, and nobody is looking at them at all. It is the first call in thirty years the company has not been in.".
  }
  Action take_the_bow(actor: group, site: place) "Take the company down for the call, in front of the bear" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lant_stage) and sceneV(rierdan) >= 7 and not commandDone(rierdan).
    Time 5.
    On success { Assert commandDone(rierdan). Assert bowCompany(rierdan). Retract holdingCommand(rierdan). Retract holdingAct(rierdan). }
    Result "You go down in a line with your hands joined, Gosse at the centre, Hepzibah at the end with the prompt-book under her arm, which is not done. The bear bows. The King throws his handkerchief. The Wick has not sounded like this for nine years.".
  }
  // A scene the company lets pass unmanaged costs the evening a point of chaos; the skips above cover the scenes that
  // never arose (no masquers posed against, a Duke already laid, a note already burned, no twins).
  Rule s1_ignored when sceneV(rierdan) == 2 and not s1Done(rierdan) { Assert s1Done(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 1. }
  Rule s2_ignored when sceneV(rierdan) == 3 and not s2Done(rierdan) and posing(party) { Assert s2Done(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 1. }
  Rule s3_ignored when sceneV(rierdan) == 4 and not s3Done(rierdan) and not ghostSatisfied(rierdan) and not tarnByGhost(rierdan) { Assert s3Done(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 1. }
  Rule s4_ignored when sceneV(rierdan) == 5 and not s4Done(rierdan) and not noteGone(rierdan) { Assert s4Done(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 2. }
  Rule s5_ignored when sceneV(rierdan) == 6 and not s5Done(rierdan) and (twinsMet(party) or kitTaken(party)) { Assert s5Done(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 1. }

  // The hearts: three private matters, none of which is a hearing.
  Topic dorcas_rask with dorcas "Ask Dorcas what Lord Rask said in the box" when raskCharmed(party) and not dorcasStays(party) and not dorcasLeaves(party) once {
    Says "Dorcas is sitting on the floor of the wardrobe with her shoes off. 'He asked me to marry him,' she says, without turning. 'Anselm. In the interval, with Mauger listening, in front of the Row. He is thirty and stupid and entirely sincere, and he says he will give up the box.' She picks at the heel. 'I'm forty-eight, and I have never once in my life been asked in front of other people. What would you do?'".
  }
  Topic dorcas_stay with dorcas "Stay. You'd never forgive the house for the loss of you" answering dorcas_rask when true {
    Says "'Of course I'd stay,' says Dorcas, and it is not a lie. She puts on her shoes. But she looks, as she stands, at the door, and does not stop looking till someone speaks to her. She will tell Anselm in the morning. He will take it, you think, very well. That is what is wrong with him.".
    On discuss { Assert dorcasStays(actor). }
  }
  Topic dorcas_go with dorcas "Go. It is the only time anyone will ask like that" answering dorcas_rask when true {
    Says "Dorcas rises from the hamper in the great manner, with one hand to her throat. 'Go! Yes! My dear, you have said what the part required, and I shall play it to the end.' Her contralto does not shake; it was trained not to. 'I'll be Lady Rask by Haysel-tide, with a box and a bottle and a bad conscience, and nobody in the house will see me play.' She blows out the candle with a flourish and sits a good while in the dark.".
    On discuss { Assert dorcasLeaves(actor). }
  }
  Topic hepzibah_heart with hepzibah "Ask Hepzibah whether she has ever told Gosse" when royalCall(pentrice) and not proposed(gosse) and not emptyWing(gosse) and not hepzibahSpoke(party) and not hepzibahSilent(party) once {
    Says "Hepzibah does not move her pencil. 'No,' she says. 'Thirty-four years.' She does not need to say what. 'He is going deaf. He is going to go on until he cannot, and then he will stop in the middle of a speech, and I'll prompt him.' She puts the pencil down. 'It is not necessary to say. Is it?'".
  }
  Topic hepzibah_wife with hepzibah "Ask Hepzibah how she likes being Mrs Gosse" when royalCall(pentrice) and (proposed(gosse) or emptyWing(gosse)) and not hepzibahSpoke(party) and not hepzibahSilent(party) once {
    Says "Hepzibah does not move her pencil. 'He says it to the King's face now,' she says. 'Mrs Gosse. As if it were a part.' She turns a page. 'He is going deaf. He will go on until he cannot, and then he will stop in the middle of a speech, and I'll prompt him, and nobody will know it is not the line.' The pencil goes down the margin. 'Is it enough, do you think, to have been asked?'".
  }
  Topic hepw_enough with hepzibah "It is enough. It is more than most are given" answering hepzibah_wife when true {
    Says "'Noted,' says Hepzibah, and writes it down, which is how she accepts anything. 'Enough. Yes. I did not think I should be told.' She turns the page. The line she writes in the margin is not in the book.".
    On discuss { Assert hepzibahSpoke(actor). }
  }
  Topic hepw_more with hepzibah "No. Say it out loud, once, before the King" answering hepzibah_wife when true {
    Says "'I should die,' says Hepzibah. She considers it. 'I should die happily.' She picks up the book and holds it against her chest, like a woman at a window.".
    On discuss { Assert hepzibahSilent(actor). }
  }
  Topic hep_say with hepzibah "Tell him. A man ought to know" answering hepzibah_heart when true {
    Says "Hepzibah takes her time with the pencil. 'You will tell me I am a fool,' she says, 'and I'll write that down also.' She goes to the loft window where Gosse is standing with his head on one side. You do not hear what is said. You see him turn round. He takes her hand and puts it in the crook of his elbow, as for a bishop, and they look at the Rotunda's roof for some time.".
    On discuss { Assert hepzibahSpoke(actor). }
  }
  Topic hep_silent with hepzibah "No. It would only make it harder" answering hepzibah_heart when true {
    Says "'Yes,' she says. 'It would.' She opens the book at the next scene. 'Thirty-four years,' she says, 'is a great many years to be prompter to a man's life. I should hate to start giving my own lines.' Her pencil goes down the margin. It does not shake.".
    On discuss { Assert hepzibahSilent(actor). }
  }
  Topic kit_oriel with kit "Ask Kit about Oriel Marchant" when twinsMet(party) and not kitStays(party) and not kitLeaves(party) once {
    Says "Kit goes the colour of a beetroot, then white. 'She's the first person who ever looked at me and saw a boy,' he says, 'and the second who didn't mind it. My voice is going. I can feel it. I'll be a baritone by Haysel-tide and no good to anyone as a girl.' He looks at his hands. 'She says I should go to her father's house and learn the law. She says an actor with a profession is a free man.' A pause. 'I think I want to do it. I don't think I want to be asked.'".
  }
  Topic kit_stay with kit "Stay with the company. You're a player" answering kit_oriel when true {
    Says "'Right,' says Kit, and straightens. 'A player.' He goes out to the yard to practise a man's walk, with his hands in his coat and his chin down, and does it badly. You are not sure that you have done him a kindness.".
    On discuss { Assert kitStays(actor). }
  }
  Topic kit_go with kit "Go with her. A trade is a trade, and love is rarer" answering kit_oriel when true {
    Says "He stares at you. Then he laughs, a short cracked laugh with a man in it. 'Oh,' he says. 'You'd say that.' He takes his coat off its nail. 'Tell Gosse I'm obliged,' he says. 'Tell him I shall be at the Seven Seats if he wants a clerk.' He goes out without looking round. The yard is quiet.".
    On discuss { Assert kitLeaves(actor). }
  }

  // Endings: whichever room the evening ends in. None of them is a settlement.
  // The Act III outcome decides which ending; Acts IV and V speak in the coda that is played over it. None is a settlement.
  Ending grave "A Grave in the Dust" when commandDone(rierdan) and ysoltSealed(rierdan) and chorusPlayed(rierdan) and not wardenFact(party) "They played the King's play and the King applauded, and the Warden did not come. The seat in the third row stayed empty. Clemency Orde wrote the fifth act that week, as it had happened, and burned it. Lucan Verrall is in the wall of the Dust. Gosse does not play the Chorus any more. At the Wick on Saturdays he stands at the head of the stage and holds her tongue, and the house stands up.".
  Ending door "The Door of the Vault" when commandDone(rierdan) and ysoltSealed(rierdan) and chorusPlayed(rierdan) and wardenFact(party) "The Warden came to the third row. He had read the Edict's own words in the Seats and found a man named before the city, and in the Wick he heard the Chorus say it again, in Gosse's great voice, to the empty seat. He did not sit. In the morning he went down the Dust Road with a ring of keys, alone, and opened the door of the Vault from the outside. Ysolt Marrick came out on her own feet. Lucan Verrall did not need to follow. It cost the Warden nothing but his reputation for being right, which he had lost already. Clemency Orde says it is the least tragic thing that ever happened to her and she resents every word of it.".
  Ending quiet "The Marshal Rides By" when commandDone(rierdan) and marshalLives(rierdan) "Nobody was exposed that night, and nobody fell. Marshal Edric Marrick still rides up Lamp Hill at nine with his scarred hand on the rein, and tips his hat to the players, and has no idea what he did not do. There is no Edict and no grave and no fifth act; Clemency Orde wrote the scene of the Duke at the rail eleven times and tore it up, and keeps the carbon. The King's Players have the Wick, a bear and a repertoire. The ghost of the old Duke is still on the roof of the Tower of Lamps, and the company plays under it on Saturdays with a salt-line at the door.".
  Ending seat "The Seat in the Third Row" when commandDone(rierdan) and ysoltSealed(rierdan) and not chorusPlayed(rierdan) "They cut the Chorus, or the evening ran past it, and nobody in the house knew what had been cut. The seat in the third row was empty and was not looked at. Ysolt Marrick is in the vault, and Lucan Verrall with her; the Warden has not been seen in the Concourse since. Clemency Orde wrote the fifth act that week from the transcript of what was not said, and does not speak of it. Gosse does not ask what was cut. Hepzibah knows, and the prompt-book has a pencilled bracket where it was.".
  Ending pebble "The White Pebble" when commandDone(rierdan) and buriedUnseen(rierdan) "Ysolt Marrick put a spade in the Field one night, with your help, and a Warden found a pebble in the morning and pocketed it, and has been exact in his reports ever since. The Marshal has a grave nobody has seen. The girl is a nun in the Bells; the Captain of the Household is her friend, not her husband, and the Warden watches the two of them in the Concourse as one who watches a clock. The Wick has a lease and a company. Gosse does not know. Hepzibah does, and has not told him.".
  Ending chain "The Chain on the Table" when commandDone(rierdan) and pardoned(rierdan) and verrallResigned(rierdan) "Lord Verrall gave up the chain, and Lucan carried the seal to the King, and Edric Marrick was buried by his daughter in the Bells' ground with the Warden sitting on the wall of the Field in the dark. The Seven Seats have a new Warden, who is sensible. The old one keeps bees. Clemency Orde has written a scene about it, which is good, and which she will not call a tragedy; she sits in the Wick's second row on Saturdays with her arms folded and her pen put away. The King's Players play on.".
  Ending shamed "The Warden Overruled" when commandDone(rierdan) and pardoned(rierdan) and verrallShamed(rierdan) "The King said bury him, and the Marshal was buried by noon, and the Lord Warden Verrall kept his office. He keeps it exactly. He never speaks to the Players, and signs their licence each quarter in a hand with no flourish in it. Lucan is married to Ysolt Marrick in the Bells, and the Warden did not come. Clemency Orde says the King has ruined a perfectly good Warden. The Wick is full, and it is not the Warden's wish.".
  Ending sea "The Boat at the Quay" when commandDone(rierdan) and bodyTaken(rierdan) "The Salt-Wives put the Marshal into the sea, and a girl in grey went with him as far as the first island and did not come back. Lucan Verrall is a Captain in the Household who does not speak of it. The Bells call it a wake and the Dust calls it the river, and the sextons wrote EXPOSED, THEN RIVER in the roll, in pencil, and nobody has inked it. Clemency Orde never forgave the herring-cart. The Wick's company has the Wives' blue apron in a hamper, for the Saturday the Salt Quay needs a favour.".
  Ending staged "The Play in the Field" when commandDone(rierdan) and bodyStaged(rierdan) "Gosse named the Marshal eleven times before the city, and the sextons put down their lanterns and buried him as the play required. The Dust has not forgiven it. A board on the gate-post bars the Wick's company, and the Warden, who let it happen, enforces the board with scrupulous courtesy. Ysolt Marrick is alive and a nun, and Lucan Verrall is her friend. Clemency Orde has her play in a drawer, with its last page written and played, and finds that she cannot read it.".
  Ending exile "The Ford" when commandDone(rierdan) and lucanFled(rierdan) "Sergeant Peverell lifted the bar for a Captain of the Household and a nun, and both of them are somewhere past the ford with different names. Lord Verrall has no son and a Field to keep, and keeps it, and the Marshal went to the river on the third morning. The Warden does not mention it. The Chamberlain writes in the book that the Captain is on leave. Clemency Orde says it is the only honest ending of the lot and she cannot bear it. The Players play the Wick on a Saturday with a rope-trick.".
  Ending river "The River Has Him" when commandDone(rierdan) and bodyRiver(rierdan) "The Edict ran its three days. Nobody covered the Marshal, because the girl who would have was talked out of it, by you or by someone who loved her, and the river had him on the third morning. Ysolt Marrick weeps in the Bells and answers no one. Lucan Verrall is on the Dust Gate, alive and ashamed. The Warden has been right. Clemency Orde says it is a much better tragedy than the one she had planned, and goes out. The Wick is full on Saturday.".
  // The coda, over whichever ending: what the evening itself came to.
  Relation coda(place).
  Rule coda_fiasco when commandDone(rierdan) and chaos(rierdan) >= standingR(rierdan) + 4 and not coda(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "It was not the play. Things were said that were not in it, and a bear sat down, and the King laughed until he had to be carried to the terrace; and in the morning he said he had not understood a word and wanted it again. The Chamberlain wrote it in the book, in the wrong column." { Assert coda(rierdan). }
  Rule coda_unproved when commandDone(rierdan) and chaos(rierdan) < standingR(rierdan) + 4 and noteGone(rierdan) and not coda(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "The play went as played. Master Mauger never found the note and could not say it was gone; he sends flowers to the Wick every opening, and a draper on the Quay has a pocket of ashes." { Assert coda(rierdan). }
  Rule coda_owed when commandDone(rierdan) and chaos(rierdan) < standingR(rierdan) + 4 and not noteGone(rierdan) and not coda(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "The play went well, and the note did not go with it. Master Mauger has a speech for his daughter's wedding in the second act, and a lease clause for every quarter after." { Assert coda(rierdan). }
  Rule king_home when commandDone(rierdan) and at(casimir, lant_stage) { Retract at(casimir, lant_stage). Assert at(casimir, audience). }
  Observe king_wreck near casimir when commandDone(rierdan) and chaos(rierdan) >= 4 "The King has to be helped to the terrace. He is crying with laughter and cannot say why. 'The bear,' he says. 'The bear, and the other bear.' There was only the one bear.".
  Observe king_smooth near casimir when commandDone(rierdan) and chaos(rierdan) < 2 "The King applauds with his stick and the Chamberlain notes that it was a good evening. Sir Ferrand looks, for the first time, a little uneasy. He distrusts evenings that go as planned.".
  Observe duke_box at lant_stage when duneSeen(party) "A cap has been left on the third chair of Lord Rask's box, a nightcap with a tassel. The Chamberlain, who sees it, writes it down and does not ask.".
  Observe fallow_gracious at rot_front when fallowSeen(party) "Corin Fallow's portraits are all looking at the door again. He has been talked into the second row and has taken it with grace, and told everyone on the Row that it was his idea.".
  Observe spandrel_chancellor at lant_stage when maskersSeen(party) "Spandrel, in the Chancellor's robe borrowed from the real one, is playing the Chancellor in the Wick's afterpiece, and the real Chancellor is in the second tier, mouthing the lines.".
  Observe twins_after near oriel when twinsSorted(party) and commandDone(rierdan) "Oriel and Cyprian stand together on the Wick's stage after the call with their arms linked, a matched pair, and the house is saying their names in the wrong order.".
  Observe pomfret_sat near crake when pomfretStood(party) and commandDone(rierdan) "Master Mauger sits through the afterpiece with the note in his hand and the smile of someone who knows he has been outplayed but not by whom.".

  // ── What the arcs were for ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Each answer given in the wings or the wardrobe is paid out in the command performance, once, by something that reads it.
  Relation payTam(place). Relation payPudding(place). Relation swaleStood(place). Relation swaleBlurted(place). Relation cyprianSorted(place).
  Rule tam_pays when holdingCommand(rierdan) and sceneV(rierdan) == 1 and not payTam(rierdan) and (tamBack(party) or tamStood(party)) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "Tam has seen to the flats. They are up, or they are not, according to whether the carpenters were paid, and the stage-hands whisper it between scenes." {
    Assert payTam(rierdan). }
  Rule tam_back_holds when payTam(rierdan) and tamBack(party) and not tamPaid(rierdan) { Assert tamPaid(rierdan). Decrease chaos(rierdan) by 1 or to nothing. }
  Rule tam_strike_costs when payTam(rierdan) and tamStood(party) and not tamPaid(rierdan) { Assert tamPaid(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 1. }
  Relation tamPaid(place).
  Rule pudding_pays when holdingCommand(rierdan) and sceneV(rierdan) == 1 and not payPudding(rierdan) and (puddingBrave(party) or puddingFool(party)) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "Pudding is in the wings, where he is always, with an onion in each hand; and you do not know whether he is going to throw them." {
    Assert payPudding(rierdan). }
  Rule pudding_brave_holds when payPudding(rierdan) and puddingBrave(party) and not puddingPaid(rierdan) { Assert puddingPaid(rierdan). Decrease chaos(rierdan) by 1 or to nothing. }
  Rule pudding_fool_costs when payPudding(rierdan) and puddingFool(party) and not puddingPaid(rierdan) { Assert puddingPaid(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 1. }
  Relation puddingPaid(place).
  Rule swale_blurts when holdingCommand(rierdan) and sceneV(rierdan) == 4 and swaleHidden(party) and not gosseTold(party) and not noteGone(rierdan) and not swaleBlurted(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "Swale is on his feet in the third row before Mauger has finished the sentence. 'It is not Gosse's hand!' he cries, in the voice of the Ghost. 'It is mine! I wrote it! Eighty crowns! A tailor!' The house, which has not been told what the play is, applauds." {
    Assert swaleBlurted(rierdan). Assert s4Done(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 2. }
  Rule swale_stands when holdingCommand(rierdan) and sceneV(rierdan) == 4 and swaleOwned(party) and gosseTold(party) and not noteGone(rierdan) and not swaleStood(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "Swale rises in the stalls before Mauger has finished, and says in a good plain voice that the hand on the note is his, that Mr Gosse has known since the spring, and that Mr Gosse has forgiven it. He sits. Gosse, on the stage, does not turn his head. 'I did,' he says, to the house, in the voice that fills the Wick. 'Go on.'" {
    Assert swaleStood(rierdan). Assert s4Done(rierdan). }
  Rule cyprian_sorts when holdingCommand(rierdan) and sceneV(rierdan) == 5 and cyprianWith(party) and not s5Done(rierdan) and not cyprianSorted(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "Cyprian does not wait to be sent for. He walks onto the stage in the Watch's grey, takes his sister by the elbow, and presents her, with Kit at her other side, to their father in the second tier as one who presents a surprise party he is not certain is wanted. 'Sir,' he says. 'We should like to be forgiven in the interval.'" {
    Assert cyprianSorted(rierdan). Assert s5Done(rierdan). Assert twinsSorted(party). }
  Rule kit_goes when kitLeaves(party) and troupe(kit) { Retract troupe(kit). Assert at(kit, marchant_hall). }
  Observe s5_kitgone at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 5 and kitLeaves(party) and (twinsMet(party) or kitTaken(party)) "Oriel is on, who was not to go on. Cyprian is in the wings in the Watch's grey with his mouth open. On the other side, where Kit should be, there is a gap the width of a sixteen-year-old; he has gone to the Marchants' house, and sits in the second tier next to the Chancellor in a blue coat that does not fit, looking at his hands.".
  Observe s7_dorcas_gone at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 7 and dorcasLeaves(party) "The line comes down for the call and there is a gap in it where a woman of forty-eight should be. Lord Rask is in his box with a woman in a gown on his arm who looks past the stage.".
  Observe s7_dorcas_stays at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 7 and dorcasStays(party) "Dorcas is in the line in a gown that is not all hers, and takes Gosse's hand without looking at him, and Lord Rask, in his box, claps once, and is the only man in the house who knows why she is crying.".
  Observe s7_hep_spoke at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 7 and hepzibahSpoke(party) "At the end of the line Gosse puts out his arm without looking, and Hepzibah, with the prompt-book under her other arm, takes it.".
  Observe s7_hep_silent at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 7 and hepzibahSilent(party) "At the end of the line Hepzibah stands with the prompt-book against her chest, apart, and watches the back of Gosse's head. He bows. He does not turn round.".
  Observe s7_book_kept at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 7 and mallamKept(party) "The Chamberlain's book lies open on the royal arm with the title in the wrong column, and Osbert Mallam, who put it there, applauds with his whole face.".
  Observe s7_book_mended at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 7 and bookCorrected(party) "Osbert Mallam is in the second tier with the Chamberlain's book in his lap, corrected, and as the bear sits down he crosses out a word and writes it in again, a little larger, and is red.".

  // The repertoire is the Crown's patience. Every two plays in it forgive one point of chaos in the command evening, and
  // what the court says of the company follows what it has seen.
  Relation stA(place). Relation stB(place).
  Rule standing_a when repertoire(rierdan) >= 2 and not stA(rierdan) { Assert stA(rierdan). Increase standingR(rierdan) by 1. }
  Rule standing_b when repertoire(rierdan) >= 4 and not stB(rierdan) { Assert stB(rierdan). Increase standingR(rierdan) by 1. }
  Observe court_rep_0 at king_court when royalCall(pentrice) and repertoire(rierdan) == 0 "The Household has not made up its mind about the company. The King's Players is a name still in pencil.".
  Observe court_rep_1 at king_court when repertoire(rierdan) >= 1 and repertoire(rierdan) < 3 "The Chamberlain's clerks have begun to say 'the King's Players' without checking the book first. The Household is deciding to be amused.".
  Observe court_rep_3 at king_court when repertoire(rierdan) >= 3 and repertoire(rierdan) < 5 "In the King's Court they ask the company for a play by name, and are annoyed to be told it is not in the book. Lord Rask has begun to bring friends.".
  Observe court_rep_5 at king_court when repertoire(rierdan) >= 5 "In the King's Court the Players are discussed the way people discuss weather: with proprietary despair. A petition has been laid before the Chamberlain asking that they be kept in the city by law.".
  Observe s7_clem_furious at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 7 and clemFurious(rierdan) "Clemency Orde sits in the second row with her arms folded, and does not stand for the bear. She has the look of a woman who has been rescued from a good ending.".
  Observe s7_clem_satisfied at lant_stage when sceneV(rierdan) == 7 and clemSatisfied(rierdan) "Clemency Orde stands at the back of the house, in grey, with her hand over her mouth, and does not applaud. She has what she came for, and it was dear.".
  Relation stF(place).
  Rule standing_f when favour(rierdan) >= 6 and not stF(rierdan) { Assert stF(rierdan). Increase standingR(rierdan) by 1. }
  Rule book_mended_pays when holdingCommand(rierdan) and bookCorrected(party) and not mendPaid(rierdan) { Assert mendPaid(rierdan). Increase standingR(rierdan) by 2. }
  Relation mendPaid(place). Relation slipFound(place).
  Rule slip_found when holdingCommand(rierdan) and sceneV(rierdan) == 3 and mallamKept(party) and not bookCorrected(party) and not slipFound(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "Sir Ferrand Pyke, who has been reading the column of the Book all through the second scene, stops, and goes back a page, and a page again. 'The Pentrice company,' he says, to the second tier, 'is entered as the King's Players. And the masquers, who are the King's Players, are entered as absent.' He looks up. He looks at Mallam. The Chamberlain does not say what he does next, but Mallam is out of the house in a minute and the company is, for a scene, under suspicion." { Assert slipFound(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 2. }
  Relation codaChoice(place).
  Rule coda_chorus when commandDone(rierdan) and chorusPlayed(rierdan) and not codaChoice(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "Gosse said the Chorus as it was written, and the house heard what it was for. It is the speech they will ask for." { Assert codaChoice(rierdan). }
  Rule coda_cut when commandDone(rierdan) and chorusCut(rierdan) and not codaChoice(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "The Chorus was cut for the King's tiredness. Gosse says the company was right to. Hepzibah says nothing, in a way that is written down." { Assert codaChoice(rierdan). }
  Rule coda_bear when commandDone(rierdan) and bowBear(rierdan) and not codaBear(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "The King's Players did not take the call. The King sent for the bear in the morning, and for the company three days after." { Assert codaBear(rierdan). }
  Relation codaBear(place).
  Relation codaCompany(place).
  Rule coda_company when commandDone(rierdan) and bowCompany(rierdan) and not codaCompany(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "The company took the call together, in a line, with the bear in front, and the Wick has not sounded like that for nine years. They will be asked to do it every Saturday." { Assert codaCompany(rierdan). }
  Relation casualty(place).
  Rule disaster_costs when commandDone(rierdan) and chaos(rierdan) >= standingR(rierdan) + 7 and not casualty(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage) and troupe(swale)
    says "It was a disaster of the sort that is written down. Swale, who forged the note or knew who did, who has been called a ghost in four plays and a drunk in two, walks out of the Wick by the stage-door into the Row and does not come back. Gosse says he will play the Ghost himself. Hepzibah says that nobody can." { Assert casualty(rierdan). Retract troupe(swale). Assert swaleGone(swale). }
  Rule seal_found_out when holdingCommand(rierdan) and sceneV(rierdan) == 5 and sealUsed(rierdan) and not sealPaid(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "In the second tier the Chancellor of the Realm has been handed a letter, by a clerk of the Household, about a sealed summons presented at the Tower of Coin on the night the Wick opened. He reads it. He looks at his daughter. He does not speak, which is worse." { Assert sealPaid(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 1. }
  Relation sealPaid(place).
  Relation presPaid(place). Relation mumPaid(place).
  Rule press_smashed_costs when holdingCommand(rierdan) and sceneV(rierdan) == 1 and printerSmashed(rierdan) and not presPaid(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "A boy in the pit is selling a sheet printed in Hog Lane that morning: THE KING'S PLAYERS UNMASKED, or THE PLAYERS AND THE PRESS. The House has been reading it through the first scene. There is a woman in the third row whose name is in it." { Assert presPaid(rierdan). Increase chaos(rierdan) by 1. }
  Rule press_bought_pays when holdingCommand(rierdan) and sceneV(rierdan) == 1 and printerBought(rierdan) and not presPaid(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "The playbills in the house are Gadsby's best, and in the right type, and the bill says what the play is. The King has read it twice and is smiling at the right line before it comes." { Assert presPaid(rierdan). Increase standingR(rierdan) by 1. }
  Rule mummers_pay when holdingCommand(rierdan) and sceneV(rierdan) == 2 and mummersLicensed(rierdan) and not s2Done(rierdan) and not mumPaid(rierdan) and at(party, lant_stage)
    says "The horse from the Gate Street, in his ribbon, comes onto the stage with the masquers' wagon and turns out to be the best-received thing so far. Spandrel hands the man in the mask his own cue, and the masquers sit down in the pit as people who have been licensed." { Assert mumPaid(rierdan). Assert s2Done(rierdan). Assert maskersSeen(party). }
  Observe light_dukes_clue at lant_stage when lightLit(rierdan) and not lightLeft(rierdan) and sceneV(rierdan) == 3 and not ghostSatisfied(rierdan) "The ghost-light stands up straight and white at the centre of the stage, and the old man in the third chair, who has been looking at the stage with polite attention, looks at the light instead and, after a moment, nods to it, as to a colleague.".
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/bench.kyr:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── The Bench ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Four critics, named by the Guildhall, the Gullet, the Close and the Owl. Three votes give the Patent. Each has a
  // regard for Gosse's Company that what the company does, and what it plays, moves; each holds a different idea of
  // what a play is for, which can be learned by asking them, or by watching them watch.
  // What pleases a critic, and what does not: a vote is won by the one outweighing the other.
  Measure regard(group). Measure slight(group). Relation critic(group).
  Initially Assert critic(clay). Initially Assert critic(gammage). Initially Assert critic(mallory). Initially Assert critic(callow).
  Initially Set regard(gammage) to 1. Initially Set regard(callow) to 1.
  Discovery taste_clay "Ormsby Clay, the Guildhall's critic, wants order of a play: verse spoken as verse, decorum, every person brought to their proper end; he cannot abide clowns, bears or words that are not in the book." { Known by clay. }
  Discovery taste_gammage "Dame Thalia Gammage, the Gullet's critic, wants joy of a play: laughter, spectacle, a good cry and home; she hates pomp and long speeches, and has hated Ambrose Swale in print for fifteen years." { Known by gammage. }
  Discovery taste_mallory "Canon Mallory, the Close's critic, wants a play to leave its house better than it found it: a moral, and nobody the worse; he will not have indecency, nor the dead mocked." { Known by mallory. }
  Discovery taste_callow "Nym Carrow, the Owl's critic, wants a play to tell the truth to power, and despises anything the Office would license." { Known by callow. }
