    says "Abel Tunstall lays the sticks on the cloth in a row, very carefully, as his father must have laid out wicks." teaches lamplighter_known { }
  Rule c6_open_known at orde_parlour when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 6 and not courseOpen(course_six) and knows(party, lamplighter_known)
    says "URANIA: Abel. The sticks. Abel Tunstall comes to the table with the night's tally in its bundle and reads it out, as he has every Trial for twenty years, in a voice like a ruler: so many notches, at a crown a notch. Carrow gets to his feet. CALLOW: There it is. Forty years of a muzzle with a motto. A City that fines a crown for every true word— CLEMENCY (turning from the window): The Office was not made because a mayor was laughed at, Mr Carrow. Urania Orde looks across the table at you. 'You know why it was made, I think,' she says. 'Tell him.' And because she is looking at you, you tell it: the ladder, the singing, the boy taken into the Office; and when you have finished Carrow sits down, and so does Tunstall, for the first time in twenty years." { Assert courseOpen(course_six). }
  Action c6_both(actor: group, site: place) "Say that it was funny, and that a man died of it, and that both are true" {
    Time 0.
    Requires speaking(actor) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 6 and at(actor, site) and not spoke(course_six).
    On success { Assert spoke(course_six). Increase regard(mallory) by 1. Increase regard(clay) by 1. Increase regard(callow) by 1. }
    Result "'It was funny,' you say, 'and a man died of it, and both of those are true; and the play knows it, or there would not be a ghost in it.' Carrow opens his mouth and shuts it again. Clay nods once, slowly, as at a sum correctly done. The Canon says 'Amen' without meaning to, and then means it.".
  }
  Action c6_liberty(actor: group, site: place) "Defend the liberty of the Soke: what is said at the Wheel is the Soke's to say" {
    Time 0.
    Requires speaking(actor) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 6 and at(actor, site) and not spoke(course_six).
    On success { Assert spoke(course_six). Increase regard(callow) by 2. Increase slight(mallory) by 1. Increase slight(clay) by 1. }
    Result "Carrow bangs the table so that the claret jumps. 'Hear him!' he says, and is so pleased to have an ally that he forgets to say allegory. The Canon looks at the lamplighter's son by the door, and says nothing, and that is worse than anything he could have said.".
  }
  Action c6_stone(actor: group, site: place) "Tell them what is cut on the old stone step under the Wheel's stage" {
    Time 0.
    Requires speaking(actor) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 6 and at(actor, site) and not spoke(course_six) and knows(actor, stone_read).
    On success { Assert spoke(course_six). Increase regard(clay) by 2. Increase regard(callow) by 1. Increase regard(gammage) by 1. }
    Result "'WHO SPEAKS HERE IN THE MASK IS NOT ANSWERED FOR,' you say. Clay sits up as if stung. 'Aenean,' he says. 'You read it? Under the Wheel? Then the Liberty is older than the charter, older than the City—' and he is off, happily, for five minutes, about masks, and the old stone theatres of the coast, and Aulus Fenne, who it now appears never wrote anything without stealing it from a step; and Carrow writes all of it down; and Dame Gammage says she always knew the yard was holy, it smelt like it.".
  }
  Action c6_stick(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Bench why your tally stick has no notches on it" {
    Time 0.
    Requires speaking(actor) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 6 and at(actor, site) and not spoke(course_six) and stickStill(actor).
    On success { Assert spoke(course_six). Increase regard(callow) by 2. Increase regard(gammage) by 1. }
    Result "'I didn't count,' you say. 'I watched.' Tunstall, at the table, does not look up from his sticks; but he says, 'That is true. I took the stick myself,' and Carrow claps, alone, and Urania Orde lets him.".
  }
  Rule c6_close when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 6 and courseDone() { Set supperBeat(pentrice) to 7. Set supperAt(pentrice) to watch(clock). }

  // ── VII. What you would vote ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule c7_open at orde_parlour when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 7 and not courseOpen(course_seven)
    says "URANIA: Now. Not the vote: the Bench votes at ten at the Guildhall, as the charter says, and not in my parlour. But what you would vote, if it were now. Ormsby. And they tell her, each in turn, as the candles burn down." { Assert courseOpen(course_seven). }
  Observe c7_clay_for at orde_parlour when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 7 and midCourse() and clayWon() "CLAY: For it. Against every rule I hold. I shall write a very severe notice and vote for it, and I do not expect to be understood.".
  Observe c7_clay_against at orde_parlour when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 7 and midCourse() and not clayWon() "CLAY: Against. It is a fine thing broken into pieces, and a Patent should go to a whole thing. I am sorry for it. I am often sorry; it is my profession.".
  Observe c7_gammage_for at orde_parlour when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 7 and midCourse() and gammageWon() "GAMMAGE: For. Of course for. It made me laugh till I hurt and then it made me cry, which is all I have ever asked of a play, and I have been asking for forty years.".
  Observe c7_gammage_against at orde_parlour when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 7 and midCourse() and not gammageWon() "GAMMAGE: Against, God help me. I wanted to love it, and it wouldn't let me. It kept stopping to be clever.".
  Observe c7_mallory_for at orde_parlour when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 7 and midCourse() and malloryWon() "MALLORY: For. I shall have to preach on it, which I dislike. For.".
  Observe c7_mallory_against at orde_parlour when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 7 and midCourse() and not malloryWon() "MALLORY: Against. Not for the verb. For Ezra. Forgive me, Urania. URANIA: Nothing to forgive, Hugh. You were always wrong about him.".
  Observe c7_callow_for at orde_parlour when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 7 and midCourse() and callowWon() "CALLOW: For. Obviously. It's— (he stops, and for once does not say it) —it is very good.".
  Observe c7_callow_against at orde_parlour when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 7 and midCourse() and not callowWon() "CALLOW: Against. It lost its nerve. A satire that loves its target is a sermon with a bear in it.".
  Relation appealMade(place). Relation triedAppeal(group).
  Action c7_appeal(actor: group, site: place) "Make the company's case to the Bench, once, for all of them" {
    Time 0.
    Requires speaking(actor) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 7 and at(actor, site) and not spoke(course_seven) and not triedAppeal(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert spoke(course_seven). Assert appealMade(pentrice). }
    On failure { Assert triedAppeal(actor). }
    Result "You make it. Afterward you cannot remember exactly what you said: something about forty-one years under the sky, and a prompter in a wing, and a ghost who could not lie down until somebody said the true thing aloud. When you stop nobody says anything at all; and then Urania Orde says, 'Well,' and pours you more claret than you can drink.".
    Otherwise "You make it, and it comes out like a playbill, and the Bench is very kind about it, which is worse.".
  }
  Action c7_epilogue(actor: group, site: place) "Stand up and give the Bench the Epilogue, as Gosse gave it" {
    Time 0.
    Requires speaking(actor) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 7 and at(actor, site) and not spoke(course_seven) and craft(actor, craft_stage).
    On success { Assert spoke(course_seven). Assert appealMade(pentrice). }
    Result "You stand up at the Ordes' table among the pie and the candles and give them the Epilogue as Gosse gave it, word for word, as one of the profession can: 'So ends our town, sirs, which was never yours...' And at 'and first, as dead men may,' Urania Orde puts her hand over her eyes, and keeps it there until you have finished.".
  }
  // The case made: each judge not yet won is moved a little toward it.
  Rule appeal_clay when appealMade(pentrice) and not clayWon() and not appealTook(clay) { Assert appealTook(clay). Increase regard(clay) by 1. }
  Rule appeal_gammage when appealMade(pentrice) and not gammageWon() and not appealTook(gammage) { Assert appealTook(gammage). Increase regard(gammage) by 1. }
  Rule appeal_mallory when appealMade(pentrice) and not malloryWon() and not appealTook(mallory) { Assert appealTook(mallory). Increase regard(mallory) by 1. }
  Rule appeal_callow when appealMade(pentrice) and not callowWon() and not appealTook(callow) { Assert appealTook(callow). Increase regard(callow) by 1. }
  Relation appealTook(group).
  // Whoever said one true thing at the start, Urania remembers at the end.
  Rule true_remembered at orde_parlour when trueSaid(party) and supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 7 and courseDone() and not trueTold(pentrice)
    says "Urania Orde, before she lets them go, turns to the Canon. 'Hugh. The waiter, or the guest, or whatever this one is, said a true thing at the start. Everybody in it was laughing at somebody they loved. Ezra would have said so. Think about it on your way home.'" { Assert trueTold(pentrice). Increase regard(mallory) by 1. }
  Relation trueTold(place).
  Rule c7_close when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 7 and courseDone() { Set supperBeat(pentrice) to 8. Set supperAt(pentrice) to watch(clock). }

  // ── VIII. A comedy of this supper ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule c8_open at orde_parlour when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 8 and not courseOpen(course_eight)
    says "It is past one. The candles are down to the last inch, Carrow is asleep with his cheek on his notebook, and Dame Gammage is eating the last of the pie with her fingers. URANIA: Somebody should make a comedy of this evening. CLAY: Nobody would license it. CLEMENCY (turning from the window at last; and for a moment, in the low light, she is very like her mother): Somebody might. Urania looks at her daughter for a long while and says nothing whatever, which from her is a speech. SUKEY (at the door): The carriages, Mistress. And the Bench gets up, and finds its hats, and goes out into Hill Street in a row, in no order at all." { Assert courseOpen(course_eight). }
  Observe c8_farewell at orde_parlour when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 8 and midCourse() and (guest(party) or servant(party)) "At the door Urania Orde takes your hand. 'Come again when there isn't a play,' she says. 'We don't have anything to say then, and it is very restful.'".
  Rule c8_close when supperOn(pentrice) and supperBeat(pentrice) == 8 and courseDone() { Assert supperOver(pentrice). Retract supperOn(pentrice). }
  Milestone ms_supper "sat at the Bench's supper and spoke for the play" worth 300 when supperOver(pentrice) and (guest(party) or servant(party)) and (spoke(course_two) or spoke(course_three) or spoke(course_six)).
}

data/adventures/gosses-company/town.kyr:
Module pentrice "Gosse's Company" {
  // ── Corin Fallow, manager of the Lord Mayor's Servants ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // He has held the Patent eleven years. He thinks Gosse's kind of theatre is over, says so kindly, and acts on it:
  // a pension for Gosse and a place for Dorcas on the first morning; the heckler on the third; the watermen at dusk on
  // the third, to strike on the fourth; and the Office, if a pirated copy of an unlicensed play comes his way.
  Person fallow "Corin Fallow" at mayors_hall {
    Role "who manages the Lord Mayor's Servants". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "Corin Fallow is a handsome grey-haired man in a beautiful plain coat, with the easy manner of somebody whose rent has always been paid. 'You're with Gosse,' he says, not unkindly. 'Sit down. I'm very fond of Absalom. Everyone is. That's the trouble.'".
  }
  Relation fallowGrateful(group). Relation fallowVisited(group).
  Rule fallow_comes when tday(pentrice) >= 1 and hour(clock) >= 10 and not fallowVisited(fallow) and not pensionTaken(gosse) {
    Assert fallowVisited(fallow). Assert fallowOffered(gosse). Assert fallowOffered(dorcas). }
  Rule fallow_seen at moon_loft when at(party, moon_loft) and fallowVisited(fallow) and tday(pentrice) == 1 and daytime() and not spread(fallow_visit_known)
    says "Corin Fallow comes up the loft stair in his beautiful plain coat with his hat in his hand, and is very civil to everyone, and asks for a word with Absalom, and then a word with Dorcas, and goes away again. Gosse stands at the window afterward, watching him cross the yard, and says nothing for nearly a minute, which is a record." { Assert spread(fallow_visit_known). }
  Rule fallow_heard at moon_loft when at(party, moon_loft) and fallowVisited(fallow) and not (tday(pentrice) == 1 and daytime()) and not spread(fallow_visit_known)
    says "They tell you in the loft that Corin Fallow came up the stair on the first morning in his beautiful plain coat, with his hat in his hand, and was very civil to everyone, and asked for a word with Absalom and a word with Dorcas; and that Gosse stood at the window afterward and said nothing for nearly a minute, which is a record." { Assert spread(fallow_visit_known). }
  Discovery fallow_visit_known "Corin Fallow came to the Moon on the first morning with offers for Gosse and for Dorcas Quaile.".
  Topic fallow_trial with fallow "Ask Fallow about the Trial" when not royalCall(pentrice) once {
    Says "'The Siege of Arle,' says Fallow, 'on the second night. You've seen it. Everyone has; it's eleven years old. It is handsome, it is safe, it is licensed to the last comma, and the Guildhall and the Close vote for it every year because it is what a city's play should be.' He shrugs. 'I don't pretend it's art. It's a roof. My people have had a roof since the Siege. Absalom's have had the sky.'".
  }
  Topic fallow_gosse with fallow "Ask Fallow about Gosse" when not royalCall(pentrice) once {
    Says "'He was the best fool I ever saw,' says Fallow. 'Forty years ago. I was in the pit the night of the riot, a prentice of sixteen, and I'd have followed him into the river.' He turns his hat in his hands. 'He's sixty-three, and deaf, and his company sleeps on straw, and his leading lady is forty-eight playing girls of nineteen. Somebody has to tell him it's over, and nobody will, because everybody loves him.' He looks at you. 'I offered him thirty crowns a year to stop. It's the kindest thing anyone will ever do for him, and he'll hate me for it.'".
  }
  // Fallow on his own campaign, once there is something of it to put to him.
  Topic fallow_campaign with fallow "Ask Fallow what he thinks he is doing to Gosse's Company" when not royalCall(pentrice) and (garlickHired(garlick) or watermenPaid(ferriby) or informed(fallow) or dorcasGone(dorcas)) once {
    Says "Fallow does not pretend not to understand. 'Winning,' he says. 'I have won eleven Trials, and not one of them by luck. A heckler is a cost of business; so is a boatman; so is a wardrobe-mistress.' He looks at you quite kindly. 'Absalom would do the same, if he had ever had a shilling at the right moment. He never has. That is the whole difference between us, and it is the only one he will not forgive.' He opens the door for you. 'Come and see the Siege. It is very good. It is always very good.'".
  }
  Action watch_fallow(actor: group, site: place) "Watch Fallow's face while he talks of what he has offered Dorcas Quaile" {
    Speaker fallow. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(fallow, site) and fallowOffered(dorcas) and not knows(actor, fallow_wardrobe)
      and not triedWatch(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, fallow_wardrobe). }
    On failure { Assert triedWatch(actor). }
    Result "'A place,' says Fallow, 'in the Servants,' and his eyes go, for half a second, to the wardrobe-room door at the side of the hall, where a pile of unsewn costumes is spilling off a chair. You remember that no woman may speak on a licensed stage within the walls. Corin Fallow is not offering Dorcas Quaile a part. He is offering her a needle.".
    Otherwise "'A place,' says Fallow, 'in the Servants,' and smiles, and you cannot read him at all.".
  }
  Relation triedWatch(group).

  // ── Patience in the Gullet ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // On the first afternoon she gets out of her stall and goes to the honey. Bowle, the bear-ward of the Soke, comes for
  // her at three, and takes her over the river if nobody has her by then.
  Relation fed(group). Relation bearLoose(group). Relation bearTaken(group). Relation bearHome(group).
  Initially Assert home(the_bear, moon_yard).
  Rule bear_out when tday(pentrice) >= 1 and hour(clock) >= 14 and at(the_bear, moon_yard) and not fed(the_bear) and not bearLoose(the_bear) and not bearHome(the_bear) {
    Retract at(the_bear, moon_yard). Assert at(the_bear, gullet). Assert bearLoose(the_bear). }
  // Whoever is in the Gullet when she gets there sees it for themselves.
  Rule bear_out_seen when bearLoose(the_bear) and at(the_bear, gullet) and at(party, gullet) and not spread(bear_loose_known) { Assert spread(bear_loose_known). }
  Rule bear_out_told when bearLoose(the_bear) and at(the_bear, gullet) and not spread(bear_loose_known) and inCity() and not at(party, gullet)
    says "The Moon's pot-boy comes running, scarlet, shouting before he has got his breath: 'Patience is out! She's in the Gullet, at the honey! The fishwives have got knives and a man from the bear-garden's coming!'" { Assert spread(bear_loose_known). }
  Discovery bear_loose_known "Patience has got out of her stall at the Moon and gone to the honey stall in the Gullet; the bear-ward of the Soke is coming for her.".
  Observe bear_in_gullet at gullet when at(the_bear, gullet) and not following(the_bear, party) "In the middle of the Gullet, sitting on her haunches with her nose in Ma Tolly's honey-pots and bees all over her face, is Patience. The fishwives stand round her at a distance with gutting knives, shouting. Patience is ignoring them, with a honey-pot on one paw, like a woman at a funeral who has found the cake.".
  Action honey_bear(actor: group, site: place) "Hold out a pot of honey to Patience, and walk backward toward home" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(the_bear, site) and quantity(actor, honey) >= 1 and not following(the_bear, actor)
      and not bearTaken(the_bear) and bearLoose(the_bear) and not bearHome(the_bear).
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, honey) by 1. Assert acceptsEscort(the_bear, actor). Assert following(the_bear, actor). Assert fed(the_bear). }
    Result "Patience lifts her head out of Ma Tolly's pots and looks at the honey in your hand with the deepest interest. You walk backward. She comes, on all fours, with the patience of her name, and the fishwives part for her like water.".
  }
  Action calm_bear(actor: group, site: place) "Talk low to Patience, get a hand on her collar, and lead her" {
    Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(the_bear, site) and not following(the_bear, actor) and not bearTaken(the_bear)
      and bearLoose(the_bear) and not bearHome(the_bear) and not triedBear(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert acceptsEscort(the_bear, actor). Assert following(the_bear, actor). }
    On failure { Assert triedBear(actor). }
    Result "You go up to her slowly from the side, talking the whole time, nonsense, the kind of thing you say to a horse, and she lets you put your hand on her collar, and leans her great warm head against your hip as if to say she had been waiting for someone sensible. She comes.".
    Otherwise "Patience looks at your hand on her collar, and then at you, and sits down harder, and goes on eating honey.".
  }
  Relation triedBear(group).
  Topic pudding_bear with pudding "Tell Pudding that Patience is loose in the Gullet" when bearLoose(the_bear) and at(the_bear, gullet) and not following(the_bear, party) once {
    Says "Pudding is up and running before you have finished, and you hear him down the stair: 'Fishwives! Do not touch that duchess!'".
    On discuss { Assert puddingFetches(the_bear). Set fetchAt(the_bear) to watch(clock). }
  }
  Relation puddingFetches(group). Relation puddingLed(group).
  Measure fetchAt(group).
  // He runs down, and leads her home, in the one moment: whoever is in the Gullet sees him come and go.
  Rule pudding_leads when puddingFetches(the_bear) and at(pudding, ?q) and at(the_bear, gullet) and watch(clock) >= fetchAt(the_bear) + 1 {
    Retract at(the_bear, gullet). Assert at(the_bear, moon_yard). Retract at(pudding, ?q). Assert at(pudding, moon_loft). Retract puddingFetches(the_bear). Assert bearHome(the_bear). Assert puddingLed(the_bear). }
  Rule pudding_leads_told at gullet when puddingLed(the_bear) and at(party, gullet) and not spread(pudding_led) says "Pudding comes down Fish Lane at a run, and stops, and hums a tune, and Patience gets up off her haunches and dances, slowly, turning, with a honey-pot stuck on one paw. The fishwives put their knives away. Then Pudding walks off up Fish Lane still humming, and Patience follows him on all fours, home." { Assert spread(pudding_led). }
  Discovery pudding_led "Pudding led Patience home from the Gullet, humming.".
  Rule bear_home when at(the_bear, moon_yard) and bearLoose(the_bear) and not bearHome(the_bear) { Assert bearHome(the_bear). }
  Rule bear_settled when bearHome(the_bear) and following(the_bear, ?c) and at(the_bear, moon_yard) { Retract following(the_bear, ?c). }
  Rule bear_stays when at(the_bear, moon_yard) and acceptsEscort(the_bear, ?c) and not following(the_bear, ?c) { Retract acceptsEscort(the_bear, ?c). }

  Person bowle "Simeon Bowle" at bear_pen {
    Role "the bear-ward of the Soke". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
    Greets "Simeon Bowle is a short broad man with a leather apron and scarred forearms and a face that has been bitten by something. Behind him, in the pens, the mastiffs go mad at the sight of you.".
  }
  Rule bowle_comes when bearLoose(the_bear) and at(the_bear, gullet) and not following(the_bear, party) and not puddingFetches(the_bear) and tday(pentrice) >= 1 and hour(clock) >= 15 and not bearTaken(the_bear) {
    Retract at(the_bear, gullet). Assert at(the_bear, bear_pen). Assert bearTaken(the_bear). }
  Rule bowle_comes_told when bearTaken(the_bear) and not spread(bear_taken_known) and inCity()
    says "Word comes up from the Gullet: Simeon Bowle the bear-ward came over from the Soke with two men and a chain, and took Gosse's bear across the river to the bear-garden, and says she is his now by the Liberty's law of strays." { Assert spread(bear_taken_known). }
  Discovery bear_taken_known "Simeon Bowle, the bear-ward of the Soke, has taken Patience to the bear-garden as a stray.".
  Thing bear_pen_gate "the bear's pen" at bear_pen {
    State penned "In a pen at the end, apart from the dogs, an old brown bear lies with her chin on her paws. The pen has a padlock on it.".
    State open "The bear's pen at the end of the bear-garden stands open and empty.".
    Change pick "Pick the padlock on Patience's pen" from penned to open needing lockwork.
  }
  Observe bear_pen_patience at bear_pen when at(the_bear, bear_pen) and state(bear_pen_gate, penned) "Patience, in the end pen, has heard your voice, and is standing up on her hind legs with her paws on the bars.".
  Rule pen_opened when state(bear_pen_gate, open) and at(the_bear, bear_pen) and not following(the_bear, party) { Assert acceptsEscort(the_bear, party). Assert following(the_bear, party). Retract bearTaken(the_bear). }
  Topic bowle_bear with bowle "Ask Bowle about the bear" when at(the_bear, bear_pen) once {
    Says "'Stray,' says Bowle. 'Found loose in the City, brought over the water, mine by the law of the Liberty.' He jerks his head at the dogs. 'She's too old to bait. Too old to be worth the dogs' time. I'll have her dance on Sundays.' He looks at the end pen. 'Twelve coin and she's yours again. I'm not a hard man. I've just got a lot of dogs.'".
  }
  Topic bowle_past with bowle "Ask Bowle where he learned to handle bears" when at(the_bear, bear_pen) and not bowleTold(bowle) once {
    Says "Bowle is quiet a while. 'On the road,' he says. 'With a company. I led a bear for Tom Fyfe's players thirty years back, before Fyfe drank himself into the Arle. Old she-bear called Maud.' He looks at the end pen, at Patience with her paws on the bars, and something in his bitten face changes. 'Maud had a cub, the last winter. Fyfe sold it to some players going west.' A long pause. 'Brown, with a white nick in her ear.' Patience has a white nick in her ear.".
    On discuss { Assert bowleTold(bowle). }
  }
  Relation bowleTold(group).
  Action ask_bowle(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Bowle to let Maud's cub go home, for Maud's sake" {
    Speaker bowle. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bowle, site) and bowleTold(bowle) and at(the_bear, bear_pen) and state(bear_pen_gate, penned).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert bowleLet(bowle). Assert state(bear_pen_gate, open). }
    Result "Bowle doesn't answer. He goes down to the end pen with his keys and unlocks it and stands back, and Patience comes out and puts her nose against his apron, and he puts his scarred hand on her head, just for a moment. 'Go on, then,' he says, to her, not you. 'Go on home.'".
    Otherwise "'Maud's dead,' says Bowle. 'Twelve coin.'".
  }
  Action buy_bear(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Bowle twelve coin for Patience" {
    Speaker bowle. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bowle, site) and at(the_bear, bear_pen) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 12
      and state(bear_pen_gate, penned).
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 12. Increase quantity(bowle, gold) by 12. Assert bowleLet(bowle). Assert state(bear_pen_gate, open). }
    Result "Bowle counts it twice and goes and unlocks the end pen without a word.".
  }
