    Result "Sir Gervase looks at you over the sword for a long moment. Then at the door. 'Nobody,' he says. 'I sit up for nobody. It's warmer by the fire.' But the point of the sword has gone down, and he goes back to his chair, and sits facing the door again, as if you were furniture. 'You can stay,' he says, 'if you don't open anything.'".
    Otherwise "'That's my business,' says Sir Gervase Carth, and the sword comes up.".
