  Observe mopsa_on_beacon at beacon when at(mopsa, beacon) "Mopsa Gedge is walking on the Beacon by herself, fast, with her bonnet in her hand, as if she had somewhere to be and the somewhere were not here.".
  // The Season's round, from the one person in the household paid to know where everybody is.
  Topic mopsa_round with mopsa "Ask Mopsa how a day of the Season goes" when legs(actor) once {
    Says "Mopsa does not even close her book. 'Eight, the Pump Room: everybody, a glass of the waters, and Mrs Scrope, who drinks nothing and hears everything. Ten till noon, the baths. Noon, the Beacon, in pairs, slowly; Ismay walks out to the Sham Castle by herself and thinks nobody knows. Three, dinner. Seven, the Rooms, till eleven, when Mr Twiss stops the band in the middle of a bar. The chairmen are on Stall Street all day and at the Two Poles all night.' She turns a page. 'Sunday at eleven, the banns. Monday at ten, the wedding; Monday at seven, the Ball. Tuesday at noon the coaches go, and it's over.' Another page. 'And at two every morning somebody knocks at the house at the end of the Crescent. Nobody in Hessel will tell you who, because nobody in Hessel has asked.'".
  }
  Topic mopsa_household with mopsa "Ask Mopsa what she makes of the household" when true once {
    Says "'The household.' Mopsa closes her book on her finger. 'Mrs Cherrett is the best woman in Hessel and has been told she is the vulgarest so often she's started to collect it, like china. Ismay is the cleverest and has been taught to be quiet about it. Rob is the kindest and has been taught nothing at all. I'm the companion.' She opens the book again. 'Companions don't make anything of anything. We're paid not to.'".
    On discuss { Increase mopsaRegard(mopsa) by 1. }
  }
  Discovery twiss_form "To make an apology to Mr Twiss that he will accept: it must be made in his own parlour, between ten and six, by somebody of the household, in so many words, with the Rule that was broken named and the word 'regret' in it, not 'sorry'. Mr Twiss holds that 'sorry' is for servants and dogs.".
  Topic mopsa_twiss with mopsa "Ask Mopsa how one apologises to Mr Twiss" when true once {
    Says "'In his parlour,' says Mopsa at once. 'Between ten and six. By one of the household, in so many words. You name the Rule. You use the word regret. Never sorry. Mr Twiss holds that sorry is for servants and dogs.' She turns a page. 'She'll never do it. She laughed at the Countess of Arne's minuet because the Countess of Arne was dancing it like a heron with gout, and she'll die before she says she regrets it.' A pause. 'Which is soon, so we must hurry.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, twiss_form). }
  }
  Discovery navvy_story "Mrs Cherrett's father meant her to marry a chandler with a shop. She ran off at nineteen with Josiah Cherrett, a navvy with a shovel and nothing else, and cooked for his gangs on the cuts for twenty years before there was any money at all.".
  Topic mopsa_navvy with mopsa "Ask Mopsa how Mrs Cherrett came to marry" when mopsaRegard(mopsa) >= 1 once {
    Says "Mopsa looks at you with something like approval. 'Now that's a good question. Nobody asks it, because they think they know: money married money.' She lowers her voice, not much. 'Her father kept a public on the Wem road and meant her for a chandler with a wooden leg and a shop. At nineteen she went out of the window to Josiah Cherrett, who was a navvy digging the Wem cut, with a shovel and a laugh and nothing else in the world. He carried her into Wem church over his shoulder with her father's dogs in the porch, and set her down at the rail, and she cooked for his gang in a hut for twenty years before there was a penny.' She smiles, which is rare and alarming. 'She'll tell you she was a fool. Ask her if she'd do it again.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, navvy_story). Increase mopsaRegard(mopsa) by 1. }
  }
  Topic mopsa_ismay with mopsa "Ask Mopsa whom Ismay loves" when mopsaRegard(mopsa) >= 2 and not knows(actor, ismay_loves_kit) once {
    Says "Mopsa looks at you for so long that you think she will not answer. 'If I tell you,' she says, 'you'll go and do something about it. People like you always do.' She shuts her book. 'The young chairman. Danby. The one who reads. She's loved him for a year and she'll marry Rupert Wenlock on Monday and keep the Wenlock accounts until she dies, and never say a word about it, because nobody has ever told Ismay she's allowed to want anything.' She opens the book again, at the wrong page. 'Don't make it worse.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ismay_loves_kit). }
  }
  Discovery mopsa_wants "Mopsa Gedge wants the lease of Number Four, Quay Lane, a lodging-house in the Old Town, to be her own mistress in it: forty coin down to the agent, Mr Gilmour, and a character from someone he respects.".
  Topic mopsa_want with mopsa "Ask Mopsa what she wants" when mopsaRegard(mopsa) >= 1 once {
    Says "'Nobody,' says Mopsa, 'has ever asked me that in Hessel. In Hessel I'm a piece of furniture that reads aloud.' She considers you. 'A house. Number Four, Quay Lane, in the Old Town. Six rooms, a copper, a yard, a view of the laundries. To let, forty down to Mr Gilmour and a character from somebody he thinks is somebody. I'd take in lodgers. Invalids' maids and chairmen's widows and the curate. I would answer the door to nobody I didn't like.' She looks at the window. 'Mrs Cherrett means to marry me to a widower in Bath with five children. She means it kindly. Everybody means it kindly.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mopsa_wants). Increase mopsaRegard(mopsa) by 1. }
  }
  Topic mopsa_hartopp with mopsa "Ask Mopsa about Dr Hartopp" when true once {
    Says "'Dr Hartopp.' Mopsa smiles thinly. 'Dr Hartopp attended Mrs Cherrett's heart in March and attended me on the back stairs in April, by surprise, from behind, at night. I happened to be carrying the warming-pan up to her bed.' She turns a page. 'It was a good heavy brass one. He wore his hat lower for a fortnight.' She looks up. 'He's doubled her drops since she put him in her will. I can't prove it and I'm the companion and nobody would listen if I could. There.'".
    On discuss { Assert mopsaToldHartopp(mopsa). }
  }
  Relation mopsaToldHartopp(group).
  Topic mopsa_laugh with mopsa "Laugh, about the warming-pan" when mopsaToldHartopp(mopsa) and not laughedWith(party) and not shockedAt(party) once {
    Says "You laugh, and after a moment so does she, properly, with her head back, a laugh that nobody in the Circus has ever heard out of Mrs Cherrett's companion. 'Nobody's laughed,' she says, wiping her eyes. 'They've been shocked, or sorry for me, or they've asked if I gave him encouragement. You're the first that laughed.'".
    On discuss { Assert laughedWith(party). Increase mopsaRegard(mopsa) by 1. }
  }
  Topic mopsa_shocked with mopsa "Ask her whether she gave him any encouragement" when mopsaToldHartopp(mopsa) and not laughedWith(party) and not shockedAt(party) once {
    Says "Mopsa looks at you with no expression whatever. 'Yes,' she says. 'I said, good evening, Dr Hartopp, on the stairs. It was very forward of me.' She goes back to her book, and does not look up again while you are there.".
    On discuss { Assert shockedAt(party). Set mopsaRegard(mopsa) to 0. }
  }
  Relation laughedWith(group). Relation shockedAt(group).
  Topic mopsa_drops_ask with mopsa "Ask Mopsa to beg Mrs Cherrett to stop the drops" when knows(actor, drops_doubled) and dosed(cherrett) and not gone(cherrett) and not mopsaPromised(mopsa) once {
    Says "'Me?' Mopsa puts her book down. 'I'm the companion. If I tell her her physician's killing her she'll turn me off by dinner for impertinence, and be dead by Tuesday all the same, and I'll be in the street with no character.' She looks at you hard. 'If you'll stand by me after. If she turns me off. If you'll see I'm not in the street.' She waits. 'Then I'll do it.'".
    On discuss { Assert mopsaAskedTerms(mopsa). }
  }
  Relation mopsaAskedTerms(group). Relation mopsaPromised(group).
  Topic mopsa_promise with mopsa "Promise Mopsa you will see she is not put in the street" when mopsaAskedTerms(mopsa) and not mopsaPromised(mopsa) and not gone(cherrett) once {
    Says "Mopsa nods once, the way a man nods who has shaken on a horse. Then she gets up and goes across the room to Mrs Cherrett's chair and says, quite loudly, 'Ma'am. Dr Hartopp has doubled your drops since you put him in your will, and I think he means you to die of them, and I would rather you didn't.' The room is very quiet. Mrs Cherrett looks at her companion. 'Impudence,' she says. 'You're dismissed.' Then: 'Is it true?' 'Yes, ma'am.' A long silence. 'Then you're not dismissed,' says Mrs Cherrett. 'Give me that bottle. No; throw it on the fire. Dr Hartopp can whistle for his hundred pounds.' And to you, low, as Mopsa goes out of the room very fast: 'Did you put her up to that?' You say yes. 'Good,' says Mrs Cherrett.".
    On discuss { Assert mopsaPromised(mopsa). Assert stoppedBy(cherrett, mopsa). Increase mopsaRegard(mopsa) by 2. Increase softened(cherrett) by 1. }
  }
}

data/adventures/hessel/clock.kyr:
Module hessel "The Banns at Hessel" {
  // ── The four days and a morning ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Hessel's days are counted from the company's coming, at each six o'clock after the first hour it is here: the day
  // it comes is the first. The Season ends at noon on the fifth, when the coaches go. Nothing here names a month: the
  // Season is Hessel's own, whatever the calendar of the country round it says.
  Measure dayN(place). Relation dawned(place).
  Initially Set dayN(hessel_town) to 1.
  Rule dawn_counts when hour(clock) == 6 and not dawned(hessel_town) and watch(clock) >= 6 { Increase dayN(hessel_town) by 1. Assert dawned(hessel_town). }
  Rule dawn_passes when hour(clock) != 6 and dawned(hessel_town) { Retract dawned(hessel_town). }
  Query firstDay() means dayN(hessel_town) == 1.
  Query secondDay() means dayN(hessel_town) == 2.
  Query thirdDay() means dayN(hessel_town) == 3.
  Query fourthDay() means dayN(hessel_town) == 4.
  Query fifthDay() means dayN(hessel_town) >= 5.
  Query daytime() means hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 21.
  Query morning() means hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 12.
  Query pumpHour() means hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 10.
  Query noonHour() means hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 15.
  Query evening() means hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 23.
  Query smallHours() means hour(clock) >= 0 and hour(clock) < 5.
  // The night is the night of the day just gone until six: the second night is the one after the second day.
  Query nightOf(n: place) means smallHours() and dayN(hessel_town) == dayN(n) + 1.
  // The Season's end: the coaches go at noon on the fifth day.
  Query seasonOver() means fifthDay() and hour(clock) >= 12 or dayN(hessel_town) >= 6.

  // ── The chapters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Each of the Season's days opens on the first page after six on which the company is in the valley: what the town is
  // doing, what it remembers, and what the day is for.
  Rule chapter_two when secondDay() and hour(clock) >= 6 and cameToHessel(party) and (inHessel() or onOrmRoad()) and not spread(chapter_two)
    says "SATURDAY. The bells of Saint Ebba's ring six over the steam. They have rung it since the abbey was a sty: Ebba was a swineherd's daughter, the story goes, whose lame pigs wandered up the hill and came back whole and steaming, and she followed them to the hot spring; the pigs are carved among the angels on the west front, if you know where to look. Below the bridge the water-carts are filling from the river, because nobody in Hessel drinks the waters who can help it. Up on the Circus a maid is beating a carpet out of a window, and the sound comes down the hill a moment late." { Assert spread(chapter_two). }
  Rule chapter_three when thirdDay() and hour(clock) >= 6 and cameToHessel(party) and (inHessel() or onOrmRoad()) and not spread(chapter_three)
    says "SUNDAY: the third time of asking. Saint Ebba's rings all eight bells for an hour before service, a peal the ringers of Orm have called wrong in the fourth change for two hundred years. The Season comes out in its second-best, keeping the best for the Ball, and the Pump Room is shut, so it has nowhere to look at itself but in church. At eleven Mr Pyne will read the banns for the last time, and come to the place where he asks if any of you know cause, and pause, as he always does, because he is young and dreads it." { Assert spread(chapter_three). }
  Rule chapter_four when fourthDay() and hour(clock) >= 6 and cameToHessel(party) and (inHessel() or onOrmRoad()) and not spread(chapter_four)
    says "MONDAY, the last day of the Season. At first light the Rooms' five chandeliers are let down on their chains, and men on ladders fit eight hundred and forty new candles, the number the Rooms' accounts have recorded for every Closing Ball since the old King came for his gout and could not dance at it. Every milliner in Quay Lane has her shutters down by six. At ten, if nobody has spoken, there is a wedding at Saint Ebba's; at seven, the Ball; at eleven, Mr Twiss will lift his hand." { Assert spread(chapter_four). }
  Rule chapter_five when fifthDay() and hour(clock) >= 6 and not seasonOver() and cameToHessel(party) and (inHessel() or onOrmRoad()) and not spread(chapter_five)
    says "TUESDAY, the morning the Season ends. Before it is light the coaches are brought round into the Abbey Yard nose to tail, and the horses stand in the cold with their breath going up like the Baths. Trunks come down the Parade on the chairmen's backs. Up at the Circus, at eight, Mopsa Gedge will take in Mrs Cherrett's chocolate, as she does every morning, and knock, and go in." { Assert spread(chapter_five). }
  Entity chapter_two: fact "Saturday". Entity chapter_three: fact "Sunday". Entity chapter_four: fact "Monday". Entity chapter_five: fact "Tuesday".

  // ── Where the company is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A company that has come into Hessel at all: every ending and every fate asks it, so that a Season that ended
  // while the company was elsewhere does not close a book it was never in.
  Relation cameToHessel(group).
  // The rooms of the town (city.kyr marks each), and of the road to Orm.
  Relation townRoom(place). Relation roadRoom(place).
  Rule came_in when at(party, ?p) and townRoom(?p) and not cameToHessel(party) { Assert cameToHessel(party). }
  Query inHessel() means at(party, ?p) and townRoom(?p).
  Query onOrmRoad() means at(party, ?p) and roadRoom(?p).
  // A place the company has left and come back to is told shortly.
  Relation visitedNow(place). Relation visitedBefore(place).
  Rule arrives_at when at(party, ?p) and not visitedNow(?p) { Assert visitedNow(?p). }
  Rule leaves_from when visitedNow(?p) and not at(party, ?p) { Retract visitedNow(?p). Assert visitedBefore(?p). }
  // What a place shows the company the first time, it shows until the company has learned it and gone away; then the
  // place says it plainly. (A line held only until it is known would be gone before the page that shows it is drawn.)
  Relation teachesAt(entity, place). Relation teachesNear(entity, group). Relation seenOnce(entity).
  Rule seen_once_at when knows(party, ?f) and teachesAt(?f, ?p) and not at(party, ?p) and not seenOnce(?f) { Assert seenOnce(?f). }
  Rule seen_once_near when knows(party, ?f) and teachesNear(?f, ?g) and at(?g, ?p) and not at(party, ?p) and not seenOnce(?f) { Assert seenOnce(?f). }
  Initially Assert teachesAt(celia_book, carth_drawing).
  Initially Assert teachesAt(celia_candle, crescent).
  Initially Assert teachesAt(celia_hand, crescent).
  Initially Assert teachesAt(ismay_watches, cherrett_parlour).
  Initially Assert teachesAt(tryst_seen, sham_castle).
  Initially Assert teachesAt(rupert_married, hetty_shop).
  Initially Assert teachesNear(rupert_public, scrope).
  Initially Assert teachesNear(kit_public, scrope).
  Initially Assert teachesNear(drops_public, scrope).
  Initially Assert teachesNear(nan_public, scrope).
  Initially Assert teachesNear(window_public, scrope).
  Initially Assert teachesNear(ruin_public, scrope).
  // Whoever is going along with the company keeps up with it, however it goes (in a chair, on a carrier's cart).
  Rule keep_up when following(?x, party) and at(party, ?p) and not at(?x, ?p) { Assert at(?x, ?p). }
  // News already told, so it is not told twice.
  Relation spread(fact).
}

data/adventures/hessel/company.kyr:
Module hessel "The Banns at Hessel" {
  // The campaign played alone: a stranger coming up the south road into Hessel at nine in the morning, on the first of
  // the Season's last four days, with a little money and no letters of introduction. (placed.kyr is the world's own
  // company, come over the march by the same road.)
  Company party "You" of 1 to 3 at south_road.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 12. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 2.
}

data/adventures/hessel/endings.kyr:
Module hessel "The Banns at Hessel" {
  // ── The morning after the Ball ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At nine on the fifth morning Mrs Cherrett, if she woke, sends for her legs; if she did not, her will does. Either
  // way the company is paid. What it is given is Josiah Cherrett's compass, which found him the line of three canals.
  Kind cherrett_compass "Josiah Cherrett's pocket compass" like old_glossary granting wayfinding worth 5 weighing 0 described "A brass pocket compass in a case worn smooth by a navvy's thumb, with J.C. scratched inside the lid and, under it, smaller, A. He found the line of three canals with it.".
  Item compass "Josiah Cherrett's pocket compass" is cherrett_compass at limbo.
  Relation thanked(group).
  Rule thanks_living at cherrett_lodging when fifthDay() and hour(clock) >= 9 and not gone(cherrett) and legs(party) and not thanked(party) and (at(party, cherrett_parlour) or at(party, cherrett_bedroom))
    says "Mrs Cherrett is up, and dressed, and packing, which is to say that she is sitting in the middle of the parlour telling three maids how to pack. She sees you and stops. 'There you are,' she says. 'My legs.' She counts twenty coins into your hand out of the pudding-cloth purse, and then, after a moment, takes something out of her bodice on a ribbon and gives you that too: a brass pocket compass, worn smooth. 'Josiah's,' she says. 'He found the line of three canals with it, and the fourth's on my wall in red, where he stopped. He'd want it to go somewhere that isn't a wall.' She looks at you. 'You did well, mostly. You did some things I'd have had your hide for, a week ago.' She waves her stick. 'Go on. Go and see the coaches off. I'm not crying, it's the dropsy.'" {
    Assert thanked(party). Increase quantity(party, gold) by 20. Assert at(compass, cherrett_parlour). }
  Rule thanks_will at cherrett_lodging when fifthDay() and hour(clock) >= 9 and gone(cherrett) and legs(party) and not thanked(party) and (at(party, cherrett_parlour) or at(party, circus))
    says "Mopsa meets you at the door with a paper in her hand. 'She wrote it on Saturday,' she says. 'A codicil. Her lawyer's going to have a fit.' She reads it out, in Mrs Cherrett's words, which are not a lawyer's: To my legs, who caught me, or tried to, twenty pound and Josiah's compass, as I've nobody else would know what it was for. Mopsa gives you the compass, on its ribbon, still warm from where it lay on the dressing-table. 'She'd have liked the funeral,' says Mopsa. 'She'd have laughed all through it.'" {
    Assert thanked(party). Increase quantity(party, gold) by 20. Assert at(compass, cherrett_parlour). }
  // Kit, if he is to marry an heiress, will not stay on the poles; he gives his to whoever helped.
  Kind chair_pole "an ash chair-pole, nine feet, polished by twenty years of hands" like quarterstaff worth 3 weighing 3.
  Item kit_pole "Kit Danby's chair-pole" is chair_pole at limbo.
  Relation poleGiven(group).
  Rule kit_gives_pole at stall_street when (kitEngaged(kit) or cherrettBlessesKit(cherrett)) and fifthDay() and hour(clock) >= 8 and not poleGiven(kit) and at(party, stall_street)
    says "Kit Danby is on Stall Street in his Sunday coat, not his blue one, and he holds out one of his poles to you, the near-side one, ash, polished black by twenty years of other men's hands before his. 'I'll not be carrying,' he says. 'Not for a while. Lanyon says it's a sin to sell a pole, so I'm giving it.' He puts it in your hands. 'It's a good weight for a staff. I've seen a man stop a runaway horse with one.' He grins, for the first time you have ever seen. 'Or a bath-chair.'" {
    Assert poleGiven(kit). Assert at(kit_pole, stall_street). }
  // Mopsa, engaged and without a house to keep, will go on the road with the company; Ottery, if he came home.
  Rule mopsa_willing when mopsaYes(party) and not mopsaHouse(mopsa) and not willing(mopsa, party) and not travelsWith(mopsa, party) { Assert willing(mopsa, party). }
  Initially Set hire(mopsa) to 0.

  // ── The Season's end ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At noon on the fifth day the coaches go, and the book closes on an account: each strand's morning after, told
  // plainly, and then one ending, by whether Mrs Cherrett woke. No custom, no ever-after; the morning, and stop.
  Query accounting() means seasonOver() and cameToHessel(party).
  Rule fate_ismay_wed when accounting() and married(couple_kit) and not spread(fate_ismay) says "Ismay Cherrett was married to Christopher Danby, chairman, at nine o'clock on a weekday at Saint Ebba's, by a licence with the names filled in afterwards, and the Season, getting into its coaches, could talk of nothing else. She keeps the books of the Stall Street stand now. They have never balanced so well." { Assert spread(fate_ismay). }
  Rule fate_ismay_engaged when accounting() and (kitEngaged(kit) or cherrettBlessesKit(cherrett)) and not married(couple_kit) and not spread(fate_ismay) says "Ismay Cherrett and Kit Danby are to be married at home in the autumn, by banns, read three times, with nobody pausing; Kit has given up the poles, and Mrs Cherrett has given him a canal to look after, which he says is just a very long chair." { Assert spread(fate_ismay). }
  Rule fate_ismay_hartopp when accounting() and hartoppClaims(ismay) and not hartoppRuined(hartopp) and not spread(fate_ismay) says "Ismay Cherrett goes home engaged to Dr Hartopp, because he stood up with her twice running at the Closing Ball and nobody stopped him, and in Hessel that is the same thing as a promise. She keeps her own accounts still. In the margin of the household book, against his name, she has written a small exact sum." { Assert spread(fate_ismay). }
  Rule fate_ismay_jilted when accounting() and ismayJilted(ismay) and not spread(fate_ismay) says "Ismay Cherrett goes home unmarried, jilted at the altar, the Season says, though it was not her that was left. She sits in the coach with her ledger on her knee and looks out of the window at Stall Street as it goes by, at the chairmen's bench, and does not turn a page." { Assert spread(fate_ismay). }
  Rule fate_ismay_free when accounting() and not spread(fate_ismay) says "Ismay Cherrett goes home unmarried, with her ledger, which is more than she came with." { Assert spread(fate_ismay). }
  Entity fate_ismay: fact "Ismay".
  Rule fate_rupert_family when accounting() and grandmother(lady_wenlock) and not spread(fate_rupert) says "Lady Wenlock has taken the lease of a house in Quay Lane for the winter, three doors from a milliner's, and is said to be learning to make bonnets, very badly. The Honourable Rupert Wenlock and his wife walk on the Beacon at noon with their son between them, in a pair, the way the Season walks it." { Assert spread(fate_rupert). }
  Rule fate_rupert_spoke when accounting() and rupertSpoke(rupert) and not grandmother(lady_wenlock) and not spread(fate_rupert) says "Rupert Wenlock stood up in Saint Ebba's and said it himself, and his mother has not spoken to him since, and he has gone home to Quay Lane with his hat on the peg, and is the happiest man in Hessel, and the poorest." { Assert spread(fate_rupert). }
  Rule fate_rupert_scandal when accounting() and scandal(wenlock) and not grandmother(lady_wenlock) and not spread(fate_rupert) says "The Wenlocks left Hessel by the first coach after the scandal, Lady Wenlock in one and her son, his wife and child in another, going different ways. Mrs Scrope has told the story so often she has begun to improve it." { Assert spread(fate_rupert). }
  Rule fate_rupert_quiet when accounting() and not spread(fate_rupert) and withdrawnByCherrett(ebbas) says "The Wenlock match was broken off by Mrs Cherrett, with regret expressed, and Lady Wenlock took it as a great insult and went home; and Rupert went down to Quay Lane every noon to the end of the Season, as before, with his secret, and nobody in Hessel any the wiser." { Assert spread(fate_rupert). }
  Rule fate_rupert_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_rupert) says "The Honourable Rupert Wenlock goes home with his mother, and his secret, and his beetle." { Assert spread(fate_rupert). }
  Entity fate_rupert: fact "Rupert".
  Rule fate_rob_wed when accounting() and married(couple_rob) and not spread(fate_rob) says "Rob Cherrett married Celia Carth at nine in the morning at Saint Ebba's, by licence, with the names filled in; she wore no fur cap. He has written a poem since that is very nearly good." { Assert spread(fate_rob). }
  Rule fate_rob_celia when accounting() and robCeliaSpoke(rob) and celiaOut(celia) and not married(couple_rob) and not spread(fate_rob) says "Rob Cherrett is not engaged to Miss Pinnock, or to anybody, yet. He is staying on in Hessel after the Season, lodging in the Crescent, three doors from Carth House, where a girl reads Ovid in the window with the shutter open." { Assert spread(fate_rob). }
  Rule fate_rob_window when accounting() and celiaHasPoem(celia) and not celiaOut(celia) and not spread(fate_rob) says "Rob Cherrett goes home with his aunt, and writes, and does not show anyone what he writes. In the end house of the Crescent a girl in a fur cap keeps a poem in her Ovid, to mark the place." { Assert spread(fate_rob). }
  Rule fate_rob_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_rob) says "Rob Cherrett goes home unengaged, with eleven bad poems, and looks back at the Crescent from the coach until it is gone." { Assert spread(fate_rob). }
  Entity fate_rob: fact "Rob".
  Rule fate_carth_open when accounting() and carthReunited(carth) and not spread(fate_carth) says "The shutters of Carth House stand open the whole length of the house, and its fires are out, and its clocks are going, all of them wrong. Lady Carth does not go back to the laundries, but she goes down on Thursdays, with Brannagh, and stands at the coppers with her sleeves up, talking, and nobody stops her." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_child when accounting() and carthReunited(carth) and knows(party, snow_child) and spread(fate_carth) and not spread(fate_snow_child) says "On the Sunday after the Season, at the end of morning service, Sir Gervase Carth takes down the white marble tablet under the west window of Saint Ebba's himself, with a crowbar, in front of the town, which has stayed to watch. The slate one beside it he does not touch. Lady Carth has asked for a name to be cut on it, at last, and they are waiting for the man who does gateposts." { Assert spread(fate_snow_child). }
  Entity fate_snow_child: fact "the snow child".
  Rule fate_carth_door when accounting() and doorOpenedByOther(carth) and not spread(fate_carth) says "Nobody knocks at Carth House at two in the morning any more. Sir Gervase still sits up in the hall, in his greatcoat, facing the door, with the bolts drawn, now, and the door on the latch, and nobody comes." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_fled when accounting() and nanFled(nan) and not doorOpenedByOther(carth) and not spread(fate_carth) says "Nan Bellamy left the laundries the day the town came down to look at her, and nobody knows where she went. At Carth House the fires burn and the clocks say two." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_celia when accounting() and celiaTaken(celia) and not carthReunited(carth) and not spread(fate_carth) says "Celia Carth is out, and does not go back. Sir Gervase sits in his hall with the fires burning and the clocks at two, and the knock still comes at two, and now there is nobody upstairs either." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_carth) says "At the end of the Crescent the shutters of Carth House are closed and its chimneys smoke, and tonight at two someone will come up the Parade in a grey cloak and knock once." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Entity fate_carth: fact "the Carths".
  Rule fate_ottery_road when accounting() and travelsWith(ottery, party) and not spread(fate_ottery) says "Dr Ottery is on the road with you, with his bag, arguing." { Assert spread(fate_ottery). }
  Rule fate_ottery_licensed when accounting() and otteryLicensed(ottery) and not spread(fate_ottery) says "There is a new brass plate on Doctors' Walk, very small and badly polished: J. OTTERY, PHYSICIAN, WHO WILL TELL YOU. He has more patients than he wants, and charges the rich double so as to see the poor for nothing." { Assert spread(fate_ottery). }
  Rule fate_ottery_gone when accounting() and otteryGone(ottery) and not spread(fate_ottery) says "Dr Ottery went north from the gate of Orm, and the Hospital of the Waters has a new physician, recommended by Dr Hartopp, who is very pleasant." { Assert spread(fate_ottery). }
  Rule fate_ottery_struck when accounting() and otteryStruck(ottery) and not spread(fate_ottery) says "Dr Ottery is struck off the College's roll, and physicks the Old Town without a licence for a shilling a time, or a pie, and the College at Orm has decided not to know." { Assert spread(fate_ottery). }
  Rule fate_ottery_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_ottery) says "Dr Ottery packed his bag and went, and nobody in Hessel asked where." { Assert spread(fate_ottery). }
  Entity fate_ottery: fact "Ottery".
  Rule fate_mopsa_wed when accounting() and married(couple_mopsa) and not spread(fate_mopsa) says "Mopsa Gedge married you at nine o'clock at Saint Ebba's by a licence with the names filled in afterwards, and did not change her name, and laughed in the vestry until Mr Pyne had to sit down." { Assert spread(fate_mopsa). }
  Rule fate_mopsa_both when accounting() and mopsaYes(party) and mopsaHouse(mopsa) and not married(couple_mopsa) and not spread(fate_mopsa) says "Mopsa Gedge has a house in Quay Lane and an understanding with you, on her terms, both of which she mentions to everyone, in that order." { Assert spread(fate_mopsa). }
  Rule fate_mopsa_house when accounting() and mopsaHouse(mopsa) and not spread(fate_mopsa) says "Mopsa Gedge has the lease of Number Four, Quay Lane, and a card in the window: ROOMS, RESPECTABLE, NO PHYSICIANS. Her first lodger is a chairman's widow; her second, Mr Pyne." { Assert spread(fate_mopsa). }
  Rule fate_mopsa_yes when accounting() and mopsaYes(party) and not spread(fate_mopsa) says "Mopsa Gedge has said yes to you, on her terms, and has said nothing else about it to anybody, which is how you know she means it." { Assert spread(fate_mopsa). }
  Rule fate_mopsa_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_mopsa) says "Mopsa Gedge goes home in the second coach with her book and Mrs Cherrett's shawl, a companion still, and looks out of the window at Quay Lane as it goes by." { Assert spread(fate_mopsa). }
  Entity fate_mopsa: fact "Mopsa".
  Rule fate_chairmen when accounting() and faresRestored(chairmen) and not spread(fate_chairs) says "The fares stand at ninepence the Parade, and Mr Twiss's speech to the Corporation is printed as a broadside and sold on Stall Street at a penny, to the chairmen, who frame it." { Assert spread(fate_chairs). }
  Rule fate_chairmen_struck when accounting() and stoodWith(party) and not faresRestored(chairmen) and not spread(fate_chairs) says "The chairmen kept the poles crossways to the end of the Season, and the Season walked; and the Corporation, which had to walk too, restored the fares in a week." { Assert spread(fate_chairs). }
  Rule fate_chairmen_scab when accounting() and scab(party) and not spread(fate_chairs) says "On Stall Street nobody in a blue coat will say your name." { Assert spread(fate_chairs). }
  Entity fate_chairs: fact "the chairmen".
  Rule fate_hartopp_ruined when accounting() and (hartoppRuined(hartopp) or hartoppBarred(hartopp) and hartoppDismissed(hartopp)) and not spread(fate_hartopp) says "Dr Hartopp has taken his plate down from Doctors' Walk and gone to practise in a town where the waters are colder and the patients do not talk to each other." { Assert spread(fate_hartopp). }
  Rule fate_hartopp_barred when accounting() and (hartoppBarred(hartopp) or hartoppCooled(hartopp)) and not spread(fate_hartopp) says "Dr Hartopp is not seen at the Rooms, and his practice has fallen away by half, and he is very pleasant to everyone who is left." { Assert spread(fate_hartopp). }
  Rule fate_hartopp_dismissed when accounting() and hartoppDismissed(hartopp) and not spread(fate_hartopp) says "Dr Hartopp has been dismissed by Mrs Cherrett, and struck out of her will with a pen that went through the paper, and by nobody else; he has eleven new patients for next Season, and prescribes hope, which he never charges for." { Assert spread(fate_hartopp). }
  Rule fate_hartopp_well when accounting() and not spread(fate_hartopp) says "Dr Hartopp has eleven new patients for next Season and a hundred pounds in prospect, and prescribes hope, which he never charges for." { Assert spread(fate_hartopp). }
  Entity fate_hartopp: fact "Hartopp".

  // ── The endings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Ending turned_away "Turned Away" when accounting() and legsLost(party) "The coaches go at noon from the Abbey Yard, and you watch them from the Pump Room colonnade, where nobody looks at you. Mrs Cherrett's goes past with the blinds half down. In the second, Mopsa Gedge sees you, and looks at you, and does not wave. The steam stands up off the Baths, and the bells of Saint Ebba's ring for nothing in particular, and the Season is over, and you were in it, and it was not yours.".
  Rule fate_prayed when accounting() and prayedFor(cherrett) and not spread(fate_prayed_told) says "They took her home with the prayers said over her by a stranger in a rented room, which the vicar at home thought very irregular, and Mopsa told him so." { Assert spread(fate_prayed_told). }
  Entity fate_prayed_told: fact "the prayers".
  Ending seasons_end "The Season's End" when accounting() and gone(cherrett) "Mrs Cherrett did not wake on the last morning of the Season, and the coaches went without her at noon from the Abbey Yard, and her own went last, empty but for Mopsa, Ismay and Rob, and her stick, which nobody could bring themselves to put in the boot. They bury her at home, by Josiah, under a stone she wrote herself: ABIGAIL CHERRETT, WHO COOKED FOR THE DELVE CUT. It says nothing about the forty thousand pounds. Everybody who was at the Rooms that Season remembers the laugh, and nobody remembers why she was barred.".
  Ending last_dance "The Last Dance" when accounting() and cherrettDanced(cherrett) "At noon the coaches go from the Abbey Yard, and the last of them is Mrs Cherrett's, with her in it, wide awake, in purple, with her stick across her knees, and the blinds up so that she can see everything. Mr Twiss is on the Pump Room steps in his dove-grey, and as the coach goes by he takes off his hat and bows the bow that is several bows, and she laughs out of the window at him so that the whole Abbey Yard hears it. She will not see another Season, and she knows it, and she is not, at this moment, minding at all.".
  Ending morning_after "The Morning After" when accounting() and legs(party) "At noon the coaches go from the Abbey Yard, one after another, down Stall Street and over Lim Bridge, and the Season goes with them: the colonels and the bishops' nieces and the widows in lavender. Mrs Cherrett's goes last, with the blinds up, and her in it, awake and cross and hungry, waving her stick at you from the window as if you were a canal gang that had stopped for its dinner. Then the Abbey Yard is empty, and the pumper is putting the chairs up on the tables, and Hessel is a town on a hill with hot water in it, until next year.".
  Ending passing_through "Passing Through" when accounting() and not legs(party) and not legsLost(party) "At noon the coaches go from the Abbey Yard, and the Season goes with them, and you watch it go from the colonnade like everybody else who was never quite in it. A very large old woman in purple goes by with the blinds up, and looks at you as if she might once have bought you, and then she is gone. The pumper puts the chairs up on the tables.".
}

data/adventures/hessel/lore.kyr:
Module hessel "The Banns at Hessel" {
  Description "Links outward from the Lim valley: a rumour of raiders on the coast, a letter-carrying commission, and the almanack woman's visit.".

  // ── An entry point: raiders, and a Tolleth packet delayed ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_raiders_rumour "It is said in the Pump Room that raiders have been taking salt-boats off the western coast, and that the Tolleth packet, the Dorothea, is a week behind and her owners are not saying why.".
  Topic lore_scrope_raiders with scrope "Ask Mrs Scrope what is said of the coast beyond the valley" when true once {
    Says "'The coast,' says Mrs Scrope, with a delighted shudder. 'Raiders. Salt-boats taken off the Orsett shore, and not a soul hanged, which is what makes it so shocking. I have it from a lady whose son writes the manifests at Tolleth. The packet, the Dorothea, with a Captain Bascom, a woman, imagine, is a week behind. They say the Orsett factors have put a man aboard to count her oil.' She leans forward. 'Anyone with a good strong back and no engagements might take a passage. I should never. The sea is so very damp.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_raiders_rumour). }
  }

  // ── The almanack woman ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_cattermole_hessel "Jessamy Cattermole sold Mrs Scrope the Season's only almanack that gives the moon right, and says the fourth change of Saint Ebba's peal is the same tune a ferryman hums at a town on the Wray.".
  Topic lore_scrope_cattermole with scrope "Ask Mrs Scrope about the woman with the almanacks" when true once {
    Says "'Mrs Cattermole!' Mrs Scrope claps her hands. 'Such a person. Six calendars and no two of them the same year, and she said, my dear, the year is a local arrangement, like a dialect. I bought the one that has the moon right. She told me the fourth change of the Sunday peal is wrong and always was wrong, and that a ferryman at a river town she calls the Wray hums it on his stage as a thing he was taught, and has no notion why.' She sits back. 'Imagine anyone humming anything on purpose. She has gone on to the Wray for the Third Night, she said. People do like a bridge-penny.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_cattermole_hessel). }
  }
}

data/adventures/hessel/oldtown.kyr:
Module hessel "The Banns at Hessel" {
  // ── The chairmen ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Thirty men in blue coats who carry the Season up and down its hill, two to a chair, by a fare-table the Corporation
  // sets. They see everyone; they carry everyone; nobody of quality ever looks at them, which is how they see
  // everything. The Corporation has cut the fares for the Season's end. If nothing is done, on the third morning they
  // lay their poles crossways, and on the night of the Ball nobody in silk slippers gets up the hill.
  Entity chairmen: group "the chairmen of Hessel".
  Measure goodwill(group).
  Relation strike(group). Relation faresRestored(group). Relation stoodWith(group). Relation scab(group).
  Rule chairmen_strike when dayN(hessel_town) >= 3 and hour(clock) >= 6 and not faresRestored(chairmen) and not strike(chairmen) and not strikeOver(chairmen)
    says "In the Abbey Yard and on Stall Street and at the foot of the Parade, the chairmen are laying their poles crossways on their chairs. In Hessel that means no." { Assert strike(chairmen). }
  Rule strike_ends when strike(chairmen) and (faresRestored(chairmen) or dayN(hessel_town) >= 5) { Retract strike(chairmen). Assert strikeOver(chairmen). }
  Relation strikeOver(group).
  Person lanyon "Big Lanyon" at stall_street {
    Role "the chairmen's spokesman, a huge mild man with a voice like a bell under water". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "The biggest of the chairmen looks at you a long time, as if weighing you for the fare-table. 'Afternoon,' he says, whatever the hour.".
    Greets again "Big Lanyon nods.".
  }
  Rule lanyon_stand when hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 19 and not at(lanyon, stall_street) { Assert at(lanyon, stall_street). }
  Rule lanyon_poles when (hour(clock) >= 19 or hour(clock) < 1) and not at(lanyon, two_poles) { Assert at(lanyon, two_poles). }
  Rule lanyon_bed when hour(clock) >= 1 and hour(clock) < 7 and not at(lanyon, limbo) { Assert at(lanyon, limbo). }
  Discovery fares_cut "The Corporation has cut the chairmen's fares for the Season's end. Unless they are restored, the chairmen will lay their poles crossways from the third morning: no chairs, and so nobody of quality up the hill to Mr Twiss's Ball.".
  Topic lanyon_fares with lanyon "Ask Big Lanyon what the chairmen are grumbling about" when not faresRestored(chairmen) once {
    Says "'Fares,' says Big Lanyon. 'The Corporation's cut them. Sixpence the Parade, was ninepence. Says the Season's ending and the town must be generous to the departing.' He considers his enormous hands. 'Generous with our legs. Well. Day after tomorrow we lay the poles crossways. Nobody goes up that hill in a chair, nor down it. Ball night and all.' He smiles, slowly. 'Let them walk the Parade in their dancing-slippers. Let them see what it is.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, fares_cut). }
  }
  Topic twiss_chairs with twiss "Tell Mr Twiss that the chairmen mean to strike, and there will be no chairs on the night of the Ball" when knows(actor, fares_cut) and not faresRestored(chairmen) and dayN(hessel_town) <= 4 once {
    Says "Mr Twiss puts down his pen. 'No chairs,' he says. 'On the night of the Closing Ball. Seventy ladies of quality, walking the Parade in satin.' He stands up. 'The Corporation dines at four. I shall be at the Corporation's dinner. I shall be at the Corporation's dinner if I have to be carried there by the chairmen themselves.' He goes out without his hat. In the evening the word comes down the hill: the fares are restored, ninepence the Parade, and Mr Twiss has made a speech that the Mayor will not repeat.".
    On discuss { Assert faresRestored(chairmen). Increase goodwill(chairmen) by 1. Increase twissFavour(twiss) by 1. }
  }
  Topic lanyon_stand_with with lanyon "Tell Big Lanyon you are with the chairmen, poles and all" when knows(actor, fares_cut) and not stoodWith(actor) and not scab(actor) once {
    Says "Big Lanyon looks at you, and at the rest of them on the bench, and something goes along the bench like a wind through barley. 'Are you, now,' he says. 'A stranger. Well.' He looks up the Parade, at the Circus roofs. 'Everybody in this town is carried by somebody. Mostly they don't look down to see who.' He puts out a hand like a spade and you shake it. 'Then here's what we'll do, for you and nobody else. If the poles are down on Ball night, and your old lady wants to go up to the Rooms, we'll carry her. For you. Nobody else in this town, but her.'".
    On discuss { Assert stoodWith(actor). Increase goodwill(chairmen) by 2. }
  }
  Action break_strike(actor: group, site: place) "Take up a pair of poles and carry a lady up the Parade for the strike-breakers' rate, five coin" {
    Description "The gentry pay well to be carried while the chairmen sit. The chairmen will see you do it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, abbey_yard) and strike(chairmen) and not scab(actor) and not stoodWith(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_fair).
    On success { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Assert scab(actor). Set goodwill(chairmen) to 0. }
    On failure { Assert scab(actor). Set goodwill(chairmen) to 0. }
    Result "You carry a doctor's widow from the foot of the Parade to the top, with a hired man from the Two Poles who will not meet your eye, and she pays five coin and says you were very smooth. On Stall Street, as you come down, every chairman on the bench turns his head and looks at you, and none of them says anything at all.".
    Otherwise "Halfway up the Parade the doctor's widow is screaming and the chair is tipping and you have to set it down in the gutter. She pays you nothing and tells everybody. On Stall Street every chairman on the bench looks at you, and none of them says a word.".
  }
  // A chair up the hill or down it, two coin, while the chairmen carry.
  Action chair_up(actor: group, site: place) "Take a chair up the Parade to the Circus, two coin" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, abbey_yard) or at(actor, stall_street)) and not strike(chairmen)
      and daytimeOrEvening() and quantity(actor, gold) >= 2 and not scabbed(actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Retract at(actor, site). Assert at(actor, circus). }
    Result "Two chairmen in blue lift you as if you were a basket of eggs, and up the Parade you go, swaying, past the ridges and the people walking, and are set down on the Circus lawn as gently as if you were going to hatch.".
  }
  Action chair_down(actor: group, site: place) "Take a chair down the Parade to the Abbey Yard, two coin" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, circus) and not strike(chairmen)
      and daytimeOrEvening() and quantity(actor, gold) >= 2 and not scabbed(actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Retract at(actor, site). Assert at(actor, abbey_yard). }
    Result "Down the Parade in a chair, which is faster than walking and much more frightening, with the front man calling 'By your leave!' and everybody's leave being given.".
  }
  Query daytimeOrEvening() means hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 23.
  Query scabbed(a: group) means scab(a) and goodwill(chairmen) < 2.
  // The chairmen carry everybody and see everybody: Lanyon will tell a friend who goes up the hill at two in the morning.
  Topic lanyon_knocker with lanyon "Ask Big Lanyon if he knows who knocks at Carth House at two in the morning" when goodwill(chairmen) >= 2 and knows(actor, knocker_seen) and not knows(actor, nan_knocks) once {
    Says "Big Lanyon waits until the bench has gone quiet. 'We see her,' he says at last. 'Coming down the Parade, nights, after two, in her grey cloak. Nine years. Nan Bellamy, from the laundries.' He looks at you. 'Nobody ever asked her why. You don't. A woman goes up a hill at two in the morning and comes down again; that's hers.' He lowers his voice to a rumble. 'There's some on this bench say she was a lady once. I say she's a laundress, and a good one, and leave her be.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, nan_knocks). }
  }
  Topic lanyon_hartopp with lanyon "Tell Big Lanyon what Dr Hartopp has been giving Mrs Cherrett" when knows(actor, drops_doubled) and goodwill(chairmen) >= 3 and not chairmenRefuseHartopp(chairmen) once {
    Says "Big Lanyon listens without moving a muscle of his face. Then he turns his head and says, not loudly, down the bench, 'Hartopp,' and the word goes along it from man to man like a ball down a skittle-alley. 'Dr Hartopp,' he says to you, 'will find he's walking. Anywhere he likes. Up the Parade, down the Parade. In his silk stockings.' He folds his arms. 'Nobody in a blue coat in this town will carry that man again.'".
    On discuss { Assert chairmenRefuseHartopp(chairmen). }
  }
  Topic lanyon_davy with lanyon "Tell Big Lanyon about the boys at the gibbet, and the one in a blue coat, and the gentleman who smelt of cloves" when knows(actor, hartopp_paid_pads) and not chairmenRefuseHartopp(chairmen) once {
    Says "Big Lanyon hears it out with his hands on his knees. 'Davy,' he says. 'My sister's boy. In his father's coat.' He is quiet for long enough that the bench goes quiet with him. 'There's men in this town would pay a boy to stand in the road,' he says, 'and there's boys would take it, the fares being what they are. I know that.' He stands up, and he is taller than you remembered. 'Cloves,' he says. 'There's one man in Hessel smells of cloves, and we've carried him up that hill every evening for six years. But not in that coat. And not that man.' The word goes down the bench. 'Dr Hartopp walks,' says Big Lanyon. 'From today. Anywhere he likes.'".
    On discuss { Assert chairmenRefuseHartopp(chairmen). Increase goodwill(chairmen) by 1. }
  }
  Relation chairmenRefuseHartopp(group).
  Observe hartopp_walking at abbey_yard when chairmenRefuseHartopp(chairmen) and at(hartopp, circus) and hour(clock) == 17 and not hartoppWalked(hartopp) "Dr Hartopp is walking up the Parade. He is not used to it. He stops every twenty yards with his hand on the railings, in his plum-coloured coat, and behind him, all down Stall Street, thirty chairmen sit on their poles and watch him go.".
  Rule hartopp_walks when chairmenRefuseHartopp(chairmen) and hour(clock) >= 17 and not hartoppWalked(hartopp) { Assert hartoppWalked(hartopp). }

  // ── The Two Poles ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The chairmen's house, and the cheapest beds in Hessel; the Season does not sleep here, its servants' servants do.
  Person gully "Mrs Gully" at two_poles {
    Role "who keeps the Two Poles, a little round woman with a big voice". Ancestry human. Profession innkeeper. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner jovial.
    Greets "Mrs Gully looks up from the barrel she is tapping. 'Bed or beer? The beds are clean and the beer's honest, which is more than you'll get up the hill for twice the money.'".
    Greets again "Mrs Gully nods you to the fire.".
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 8.
  }

  // ── Kit Danby ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person kit "Kit Danby" at stall_street {
    Role "a young chairman in a blue coat, with a book in his pocket" when not kitEngaged(kit).
    Role "a young chairman in his Sunday coat, with a look on him" when kitEngaged(kit).
    Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "The young chairman stands up when you come, which none of the others do, and takes his hat off, and waits to be told what you want.".
    Greets again "Kit Danby nods to you, and closes his book on his finger.".
    Wants ismay_note.
  }
  Measure kitTrust(group).
  // Mornings on the Circus with Mrs Cherrett's chair (unless he is turned off, or the poles are down); afternoons at the
  // stand; evenings at the Two Poles.
  Relation kitAway(group).
  Rule kit_circus when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 12 and not at(kit, circus) and not kitDismissed(kit) and not strike(chairmen) and not kitAway(kit) and not chairLoose(cherrett) and not following(kit, party) and not travelsWith(kit, party) { Assert at(kit, circus). }
  Rule kit_stand when (hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 19 or hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 12 and (kitDismissed(kit) or strike(chairmen))) and not at(kit, stall_street) and not kitAway(kit) and not chairLoose(cherrett) and not following(kit, party) and not travelsWith(kit, party) { Assert at(kit, stall_street). }
  Rule kit_evening when hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 23 and not at(kit, two_poles) and not kitAway(kit) and not following(kit, party) and not travelsWith(kit, party) { Assert at(kit, two_poles). }
  Rule kit_night when (hour(clock) >= 23 or hour(clock) < 8) and not at(kit, limbo) and not kitAway(kit) and not following(kit, party) and not travelsWith(kit, party) { Assert at(kit, limbo). }
  Observe kit_reading at circus when at(kit, circus) and not kitEngaged(kit) "On the Circus lawn the chairmen sit on the poles of Mrs Cherrett's chair waiting for her to want it. The young one is reading a book with his back to her windows, and every so often, without lifting his head, he looks up at them.".
  Discovery kit_looked "Kit Danby let go of Mrs Cherrett's chair at the top of the Parade because he looked up at something; he will not say what.".
  Topic kit_how with kit "Ask the young chairman how the chair got away from him" when chairRan(cherrett) once {
    Says "He goes red to the ears. 'I looked up,' he says. 'At the top of the Parade. I looked up and I let go the strap.' He turns his hat round in his hands. 'I've carried for nine years and never let go a strap. I looked up.' He does not say at what, and you can see that he will not.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, kit_looked). }
  }
  Discovery kit_violet "Kit Danby keeps a pressed violet in the book he reads on the poles: Ismay Cherrett's, dropped on the Parade in the spring. She told him to keep it.".
  Topic kit_book with kit "Ask Kit what he is reading" when true once {
    Says "He shows you: a book of essays, old, coming apart, bought off a barrow. 'The man in it says,' he begins, and stops, because when he opened it to show you something fell out of the pages into the grass, and he has gone down on one knee after it as if it were a sovereign. It is a violet, pressed flat and brown. He puts it back between the pages very carefully. 'It's nothing,' he says, and puts the book inside his coat.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, kit_violet). Increase kitTrust(kit) by 1. }
  }
  Relation kitHopes(group). Relation kitPushed(group). Relation kitHasNote(group). Relation kitTryst(group). Relation kitEngaged(group).
  Topic kit_she_watches with kit "Tell Kit that Ismay stands at the window every morning while his chair is on the Circus, and does not turn a page" when knows(actor, ismay_watches) and not kitHopes(kit) once {
    Says "Kit Danby goes quite still, the way a man does who has heard his name called in a crowd. 'She does the accounts,' he says. 'At the window. For the light.' He looks at you, and away, and up at the windows, and away. 'Don't,' he says. 'Don't say things like that to a man on the poles. It isn't kind.' But he does not open his book again.".
    On discuss { Assert kitHopes(kit). Increase kitTrust(kit) by 1. }
  }
  Topic kit_push with kit "Tell Kit that if he says nothing, she will marry Rupert Wenlock on Monday, and keep the Wenlock books until she dies" when knows(actor, ismay_loves_kit) and not kitPushed(kit) and not kitEngaged(kit) once {
    Says "Kit hears you out with his jaw set. 'And if I say something,' he says, 'what then? I've a bench and two poles and nine shillings. She's got forty thousand pounds. They'd say I was after it. They'd be right to.' He is very angry, and not with you. 'You think I don't know what Monday is? I've known since the first banns. I carried her to church for them.'".
    On discuss { Assert kitPushed(kit). }
  }
  // Ismay's note: where she walks at noon. Given to Kit, and with hope in him, he goes to the Sham Castle the next noon.
  Measure trystDay(group).
  Event kit_reads near kit when keeps(kit, ismays_note) and not kitHasNote(kit) and (kitHopes(kit) or kitPushed(kit)) "Kit reads it standing up, and then sits down on the bench, and reads it again. 'The Sham Castle,' he says. 'Noon.' He puts it in his book, beside the violet. 'I'll go,' he says, to the book. 'God help me, I'll go.'" then {
    Assert kitHasNote(kit). Assert kitTryst(kit). Set trystDay(kit) to dayN(hessel_town) + 1. }
  Event kit_reads_proud near kit when keeps(kit, ismays_note) and not kitHasNote(kit) and not kitHopes(kit) and not kitPushed(kit) "Kit reads it, and folds it, and puts it in his book beside the violet. 'Thank you,' he says, very formally. 'Tell Miss Cherrett I had it.' He goes back to his reading. He is not reading." then {
    Assert kitHasNote(kit). }
  // A note kept without hope can still be acted on once he has some.
  Rule kit_hopes_late when kitHasNote(kit) and not kitTryst(kit) and (kitHopes(kit) or kitPushed(kit)) and not kitEngaged(kit) { Assert kitTryst(kit). Set trystDay(kit) to dayN(hessel_town) + 1. }
  Rule tryst_kept when kitTryst(kit) and dayN(hessel_town) >= trystDay(kit) and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 13 and not kitEngaged(kit) and not ismayAway(ismay) and not gone(cherrett) {
    Assert kitEngaged(kit). Assert at(kit, sham_castle). Assert at(ismay, sham_castle). Assert ismayOut(ismay). Assert kitAway(kit). }
  Observe tryst_seen at sham_castle when kitEngaged(kit) and at(kit, sham_castle) and at(ismay, sham_castle) and not seenOnce(tryst_seen) "Behind the Sham Castle, in the shade of the wall that is a castle from the Crescent and a wall from here, Ismay Cherrett and Kit Danby are standing a yard apart and not touching, as if the yard were the whole of the Season. She is talking very fast, about something; he is not listening to a word of it. Then he says something, and she stops. You go away again, quietly, round the end of the wall, and the sheep look at you." teaches tryst_seen.
  Discovery tryst_seen "Ismay Cherrett and Kit Danby met behind the Sham Castle at noon, and said what they had not said for a year.".
  Rule tryst_over when kitEngaged(kit) and hour(clock) >= 13 and (kitAway(kit) or ismayOut(ismay)) and not atBall(ismay) { Retract kitAway(kit). Retract ismayOut(ismay). }
  // Mrs Cherrett's blessing: she must be told, and reminded who she was; and Ismay must not deny it.
  Relation cherrettBlessesKit(group). Relation cherrettToldKit(group).
  Topic cherrett_told_kit with cherrett "Tell Mrs Cherrett that Ismay loves Kit Danby, the chairman" when knows(actor, ismay_loves_kit) and not cherrettToldKit(cherrett) and not gone(cherrett) and not cherrettBlessesKit(cherrett) once {
    Says "'A chairman!' Mrs Cherrett's stick hits the floor so hard the pike rattles in its case. 'A chairman! My granddaughter, that I've brought up to be a lady, that I've had taught French and the harp! A man that carries people for ninepence!' She is scarlet. 'Ismay! Is it true?'".
    On discuss { Assert cherrettToldKit(cherrett). }
  }
  Topic remind_navvy with cherrett "Remind Mrs Cherrett that at nineteen she went out of a window to a navvy with a shovel" when cherrettToldKit(cherrett) and knows(actor, navvy_story) and not cherrettBlessesKit(cherrett) and ismayStoodBy(ismay) and not gone(cherrett) once {
    Says "There is a terrible silence. Mrs Cherrett looks at you; at the stuffed pike, as if for a second opinion; at Ismay, who has come and stood by your side with her ledger held against her chest like a shield. 'Is it true, girl?' says Mrs Cherrett again, quite quietly. 'Yes, Grandmother.' The old woman's face works. Then she begins to laugh: the laugh, the coal-scuttle laugh, the one that got her barred from the Rooms; it goes on and on, and she wipes her eyes with the pudding-cloth purse. 'A window,' she says. 'It was a ground-floor window. Josiah held the ladder anyway, the great fool, and carried me up the aisle at Wem like a sack of meal, with Father's dogs in the porch.' She holds out her hand to Ismay. 'Send for the boy,' she says. 'Send for him. And somebody write to that Wenlock woman and tell her I'm very sorry. No. Tell her I regret it.'".
    On discuss { Assert cherrettBlessesKit(cherrett). Retract kitDismissed(kit). Assert bannsWithdrawn(ebbas). Assert withdrawnByCherrett(ebbas). Increase softened(cherrett) by 1. }
  }
  Relation withdrawnByCherrett(place).
  Topic remind_navvy_alone with cherrett "Remind Mrs Cherrett that at nineteen she went out of a window to a navvy with a shovel" when cherrettToldKit(cherrett) and knows(actor, navvy_story) and not cherrettBlessesKit(cherrett) and not ismayStoodBy(ismay) and not gone(cherrett) once {
    Says "Mrs Cherrett's mouth opens and shuts. She looks at Ismay. 'Well? Is it true, girl?' And Ismay, who has said yes, Grandmother, to every question her grandmother has asked her for twenty-one years, says, white to the lips, 'No, Grandmother.' Mrs Cherrett sits back. 'There,' she says to you. 'Navvies. Windows. Mind your own business.'".
    On discuss { Assert ismayDenied(ismay). }
  }
  Relation ismayDenied(group).
  // Denied once, she can still say it: once someone has stood by her, she goes back of her own accord.
  Rule ismay_unsays when ismayDenied(ismay) and ismayStoodBy(ismay) and cherrettToldKit(cherrett) and not cherrettBlessesKit(cherrett) and at(ismay, cherrett_parlour) and at(cherrett, cherrett_parlour) and at(party, cherrett_parlour) and knows(party, navvy_story)
    says "Ismay puts down her ledger. 'Grandmother,' she says. 'I said no. It was yes. It's always been yes.' Mrs Cherrett looks at her. Then, slowly, she begins to laugh, the coal-scuttle laugh that got her barred from the Rooms. 'A window,' she says. 'Mine was a ground-floor window. Send for the boy.'" {
    Assert cherrettBlessesKit(cherrett). Retract kitDismissed(kit). Assert bannsWithdrawn(ebbas). Assert withdrawnByCherrett(ebbas). Retract ismayDenied(ismay). }

  // ── Hetty Quiney ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person hetty "Hetty Quiney" at hetty_shop {
    Role "a milliner with pins in her mouth and a baby on her hip". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "The milliner takes the pins out of her mouth one at a time to speak to you. 'Bonnets, is it? Or ribbons? Or are you looking for him?' She looks at you sharp. 'No. You're not anybody's. What can I do for you?'".
    Greets again "Hetty Quiney shifts the baby to the other hip.".
  }
  Relation hettyAway(group). Relation hettyWilling(group). Relation hettyAtChurch(group).
  Rule hetty_shop_hours when not at(hetty, hetty_shop) and not hettyAway(hetty) and not following(hetty, party) { Assert at(hetty, hetty_shop). }
  Observe hetty_scene at hetty_shop when not visitedBefore(hetty_shop) "Hetty Quiney's shop: three bonnets on wooden heads, a counter, ribbons in drawers labelled in a round hand, and a cradle under the counter.".
  Observe hetty_again at hetty_shop when visitedBefore(hetty_shop) "Hetty Quiney's shop: the bonnets, the ribbon drawers, the cradle under the counter.".
  Thing hat_peg "the gentleman's hat on the peg" at hetty_shop {
    Tries looking.
    State hung "A gentleman's beaver hat, good, a little worn, on the peg by the back door.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(hat_peg, hung).
  Discovery hat_initials "Inside the crown of the gentleman's hat at Hetty Quiney's are the initials R. W. and, pinned to the lining, a dried beetle.".
  Observe hat_looked near hat_peg when tried(hat_peg, looking) and not knows(party, hat_initials) "Inside the crown, in gilt on the leather, R. W.; and pinned to the lining, very carefully, a little dried beetle with a green back." teaches hat_initials.
  Observe rupert_at_hetty at hetty_shop when at(rupert, hetty_shop) and not seenOnce(rupert_married) "The Honourable Rupert Wenlock is sitting behind Hetty Quiney's counter in his shirt-sleeves, with a fat baby on his knee, making a beetle walk across the counter for it. The baby is shrieking with joy. Rupert looks up and sees you, and every drop of colour goes out of his face, and he does not stop the beetle." teaches rupert_married.
  Observe rupert_at_hetty_again at hetty_shop when at(rupert, hetty_shop) and seenOnce(rupert_married) and not rupertAway(rupert) "Rupert Wenlock is behind Hetty's counter in his shirt-sleeves with his son on his knee, as if he belonged there, which he does between noon and two.".
  Topic hetty_hat with hetty "Ask Hetty whose hat that is on the peg" when knows(actor, hat_initials) and not knows(actor, rupert_married) once {
    Says "Hetty looks at the hat, and at you, and takes the last pin out of her mouth. 'My husband's,' she says. 'He leaves it when he goes up the hill. He's a gentleman up the hill and a husband down it, and I'm about tired of it.' She puts the baby in the cradle. 'You'll have guessed. Everybody'll guess on Monday, when he marries a girl with forty thousand pounds at Saint Ebba's and I'm stood at the door with his son.' She looks at you. 'Unless he stands up on Sunday. He swears every week he will.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, rupert_married). }
  }
  Topic hetty_ultimatum with hetty "Ask Hetty what she will do" when knows(actor, rupert_married) and not hettyWilling(hetty) and not bannsWithdrawn(ebbas) once {
    Says "'Do?' Hetty threads a needle at the first try. 'I'll do what I've done for two years. Wait for him to be brave.' She bites the thread. 'And on Monday at ten, if he hasn't been, I'll be on the steps of Saint Ebba's with Jack. Not to make a scene. Just so he has to walk past us.'".
  }
  Topic hetty_come with hetty "Tell Hetty that Rupert means to tell his mother, and wants her and Jack there" when rupertBrave(rupert) and not hettyWilling(hetty) and not bannsWithdrawn(ebbas) once {
    Says "Hetty sits down on her own counter. 'He said that?' She is laughing and crying at once, and wipes her face on a ribbon. 'Two years. Two years I've said, bring me up the hill, let her see Jack, let her see me. She can only say no.' She gets up, and puts on a bonnet, the best one, from the window. 'Come on, then,' she says. 'Before he thinks better of it.'".
    On discuss { Assert hettyWilling(hetty). Assert acceptsEscort(hetty, actor). Assert acceptsEscort(rupert, actor). }
  }
  // The Old Town's way: not into Lady Wenlock's drawing room, but up the aisle of Saint Ebba's on Sunday, with the
  // chairmen standing at the back of the church.
  Topic hetty_church with hetty "Ask Hetty to come up to Saint Ebba's on Sunday morning and say it herself, with the chairmen at the back" when knows(actor, rupert_married) and (stoodWith(actor) or goodwill(chairmen) >= 3) and not hettyWilling(hetty) and not hettyChurch(hetty) and not bannsWithdrawn(ebbas) once {
    Says "'In church?' Hetty stops sewing. 'Stand up in Saint Ebba's in front of the Season and say he's mine?' She looks at the cradle, and at the hat on the peg. 'I said Monday, on the steps. I said I'd not make a scene.' Then: 'Lanyon'd be there? At the back?' You say the chairmen will be at the back, all of them, in their blue coats. Hetty puts down the bonnet. 'Then I'll come,' she says. 'Sunday. Come for me at half past ten. If I've thought better of it, carry me.'".
    On discuss { Assert hettyChurch(hetty). }
  }
  Relation hettyChurch(group).
  Rule hetty_ready when hettyChurch(hetty) and thirdDay() and hour(clock) == 10 and not acceptsEscort(hetty, party) { Assert acceptsEscort(hetty, party). }
  Observe hetty_dressed at hetty_shop when hettyChurch(hetty) and thirdDay() and hour(clock) == 10 "Hetty Quiney is ready in her best bonnet with Jack in his christening gown, sitting very upright on the counter, waiting to be fetched.".
  Relation grandsonShown(group).
  Action family_scene(actor: group, site: place) "Stand beside Rupert while he tells his mother, and Hetty puts the baby in her arms" {
    Description "You will be in the room.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wenlock_room) and at(lady_wenlock, wenlock_room)
      and (at(rupert, wenlock_room) or following(rupert, actor)) and (at(hetty, wenlock_room) or following(hetty, actor))
      and rupertBrave(rupert) and hettyWilling(hetty) and not bannsWithdrawn(ebbas).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert grandmother(lady_wenlock). Assert bannsWithdrawn(ebbas). Assert grandsonShown(lady_wenlock).
      Retract following(hetty, actor). Retract following(rupert, actor). Assert at(hetty, wenlock_room). Assert at(rupert, wenlock_room). Assert hettyAway(hetty). Assert rupertAway(rupert). }
    Result "Rupert says it standing up, with his hat in his hands, all of it, in one breath, Bristol and the milliner and the two years and the banns, and when he has finished he sits down on one of the hard chairs as if his legs had been cut. Lady Wenlock does not speak. She looks at Hetty Quiney in her best bonnet, and at you, and at her son. Then Hetty, without asking anybody, goes across the room and puts Jack into Lady Wenlock's arms. Jack looks at Lady Wenlock. Lady Wenlock looks at Jack. Jack takes hold of the glass on its stick, and pulls it, and laughs. 'He has the Wenlock nose,' says Lady Wenlock, in a voice nobody in the room has heard her use. 'God help him.' She does not give him back. 'Rupert,' she says, without looking up, 'send to Saint Ebba's. Tell Mr Pyne there will be no third reading. And ring for tea. Four cups.' A pause. 'Five.'".
  }
  Rule family_home when grandsonShown(lady_wenlock) and hour(clock) >= 18 and hettyAway(hetty) and not atBall(hetty) { Retract hettyAway(hetty). Retract rupertAway(rupert). }

  // ── Jem Mallender, the apothecary's boy ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person jem "Jem Mallender" at apothecary {
    Role "the apothecary's boy, with stained fingers and a careful face". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "The boy behind the counter looks up from his scales. 'Master's out,' he says. 'I can do you anything that's written down.'".
    Greets again "Jem Mallender wipes his fingers on his apron.".
  }
  Rule jem_hours when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 20 and not at(jem, apothecary) { Assert at(jem, apothecary). }
  Rule jem_home when (hour(clock) >= 20 or hour(clock) < 8) and not at(jem, limbo) { Assert at(jem, limbo). }
  Topic jem_drops with jem "Ask Jem about Mrs Cherrett's drops" when not knows(actor, drops_doubled) and goodwill(chairmen) < 2 once {
    Says "Jem Mallender's careful face gets more careful. 'Physicians' prescriptions are confidential,' he says, as if reading it off a card. He looks at the row of little brown bottles waiting to go up the hill. 'I can't say what's in another person's physic. Not for nothing.'".
    On discuss { Assert jemAsked(jem). }
  }
  Relation jemAsked(group).
  Action pay_jem(actor: group, site: place) "Put two coin on the counter for Jem Mallender's trouble" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(jem, site) and jemAsked(jem) and not knows(actor, drops_doubled) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 2.
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Increase quantity(jem, gold) by 2. Assert knows(actor, drops_doubled). }
    Result "The coins go into the till, not his pocket, which says something about Jem. 'Twenty at night, she had,' he says quietly, to the scales. 'Laudanum and cardamom. A month ago Dr Hartopp came in and wrote forty. Himself. I said, forty, sir? He said, she sleeps badly. I said, she'll sleep.' He looks up. 'She's a big woman. Forty won't kill her in a night. It'll kill her in a week.'".
  }
  Topic jem_drops_cousin with jem "Ask Jem about Mrs Cherrett's drops, as a friend of the chairmen" when not knows(actor, drops_doubled) and goodwill(chairmen) >= 2 once {
    Says "'Lanyon's my uncle,' says Jem, 'and he says you're all right.' He looks at the row of brown bottles. 'Twenty at night, she had. Laudanum and cardamom. A month ago Dr Hartopp came in and wrote forty, himself. I said, forty, sir? He said, she sleeps badly. I said, she'll sleep.' He looks up. 'Forty won't kill her in a night. It'll kill her in a week.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, drops_doubled). }
  }

  // ── Mr Gilmour and Number Four ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person gilmour "Mr Gilmour" at no_four {
    Role "the agent for Number Four, a dry man with a ring of keys". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "The agent jingles his keys. 'Number Four. Six rooms, copper, yard. Forty down and a character. The view of the laundries is extra,' he says, 'in the sense that you can't avoid it.'".
  }
  Rule gilmour_hours when hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 18 and not at(gilmour, no_four) and not mopsaHouse(mopsa) { Assert at(gilmour, no_four). }
  Rule gilmour_home when (hour(clock) >= 18 or hour(clock) < 9 or mopsaHouse(mopsa)) and not at(gilmour, limbo) { Assert at(gilmour, limbo). }
  Observe no_four_scene at no_four when not mopsaHouse(mopsa) "Number Four, Quay Lane: six empty rooms smelling of whitewash, a copper in the scullery, a yard with a pear tree in it, and a window over the laundries, which are steaming.".
  Observe no_four_hers at no_four when mopsaHouse(mopsa) "Number Four, Quay Lane: Mopsa's. There are already books on a plank across two bricks, a kettle, a card in the window saying ROOMS, RESPECTABLE, NO PHYSICIANS, and Mopsa.".
  Relation mopsaCharacter(group). Relation mopsaFunded(group). Relation mopsaPartner(group).
  Topic twiss_character with twiss "Ask Mr Twiss to give Mopsa Gedge a character, for the lease of a house" when knows(actor, mopsa_wants) and twissFavour(twiss) >= 2 and not mopsaCharacter(mopsa) once {
    Says "'Miss Gedge.' Mr Twiss writes before you have finished. 'Mrs Cherrett's companion. She has sat at the back of my Rooms in grey for three Seasons and has never once been bored in public, which is a greater accomplishment than the minuet.' He sands it and folds it. 'Give her that with my compliments. Tell her I regret she does not dance.'".
    On discuss { Assert mopsaCharacter(mopsa). }
  }
  Topic lanyon_character with lanyon "Ask Big Lanyon whether the chairmen know Mr Gilmour, the agent" when knows(actor, mopsa_wants) and goodwill(chairmen) >= 2 and not mopsaCharacter(mopsa) once {
    Says "'Gilmour?' Big Lanyon laughs, a sound like a cart going over a bridge. 'He's my wife's cousin. He'll take a character from the bench, if the bench gives it.' He calls down the bench. 'Miss Gedge, that hit the doctor with the warming-pan. For a house in Quay Lane.' There is a sort of cheer. 'There's your character,' says Big Lanyon. 'Thirty of us.'".
    On discuss { Assert mopsaCharacter(mopsa). }
  }
  Topic wenlock_character with lady_wenlock "Ask Lady Wenlock to give Mopsa Gedge a character" when knows(actor, mopsa_wants) and grandmother(lady_wenlock) and not mopsaCharacter(mopsa) once {
    Says "Lady Wenlock is holding Jack and does not put him down to write, so Hetty holds the paper. 'A character,' she says. 'For the woman who hit Dr Hartopp with a warming-pan. I wish I'd seen it.' She signs with a flourish over Jack's head.".
    On discuss { Assert mopsaCharacter(mopsa). }
  }
  Topic cherrett_settle with cherrett "Ask Mrs Cherrett to settle something on Mopsa" when knows(actor, mopsa_wants) and not mopsaFunded(mopsa) and not dosed(cherrett) and softened(cherrett) >= 1 and not gone(cherrett) once {
    Says "'Settle something on Mopsa?' Mrs Cherrett looks across the room at her companion, who is reading with her back very straight and has heard every word. 'I meant to settle a husband on her.' She considers. 'A house, is it? In the Old Town. On her own.' A long pause. 'I had a hut on the Delve cut, on my own, all one winter while Josiah was up the line,' she says. 'Best winter of my life.' She gets out the pudding-cloth purse, and then thinks better of it, and writes a note to her banker instead. 'Forty. Not a word, Mopsa. Not a word or I'll take it back.' Mopsa does not say a word. She cannot.".
    On discuss { Assert mopsaFunded(mopsa). Increase mopsaRegard(mopsa) by 1. }
  }
  Topic mopsa_see_house with mopsa "Ask Mopsa to come down and look at Number Four with you" when knows(actor, mopsa_wants) and mopsaRegard(mopsa) >= 2 and not mopsaHouse(mopsa) and not sawHouse(party) and daytime() once {
    Says "Mopsa looks at Mrs Cherrett, and at the clock, and at you. 'Look at it,' she says. 'I've looked at it from the end of the lane every Sunday for three weeks. I've never been in.' She gets her bonnet. 'Half an hour. If she wakes, I was at church.'".
    On discuss { Assert acceptsEscort(mopsa, actor). Assert following(mopsa, actor). Assert mopsaAway(mopsa). }
  }
  Relation sawHouse(group).
  Event mopsa_in_house at no_four when following(mopsa, party) and not sawHouse(party) "Mopsa goes through the six rooms of Number Four without a word, touching things: the copper, the window-catch, the mantelpiece, the pear tree in the yard. In the empty front room she stands in the middle of the floor and turns round once, slowly, like a child. 'Mine,' she says, trying it. Then, to you, sharp: 'Don't look at me like that.'" then {
    Assert sawHouse(party). Increase courtship(mopsa) by 1. }
  Action take_lease(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Mr Gilmour forty coin down on Number Four, for Mopsa Gedge" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, no_four) and at(gilmour, no_four) and mopsaCharacter(mopsa)
      and (at(mopsa, no_four) or following(mopsa, actor)) and not mopsaHouse(mopsa) and not mopsaFunded(mopsa) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 40.
    Time 3.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 40. Increase quantity(gilmour, gold) by 40. Assert mopsaHouse(mopsa). Assert mopsaGiven(mopsa). }
    Result "Mr Gilmour counts the forty twice, reads the character twice, and gives Mopsa the keys. Mopsa looks at the keys, and then at you. 'That's a great deal of money,' she says. 'I shall pay you back. I shall pay you back at four in the hundred, quarterly, and I shall hate every penny of it.'".
  }
  Relation mopsaGiven(group).
  Action take_lease_halves(actor: group, site: place) "Put twenty coin to Mopsa's twenty, and take Number Four as her partner" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, no_four) and at(gilmour, no_four) and mopsaCharacter(mopsa)
      and (at(mopsa, no_four) or following(mopsa, actor)) and not mopsaHouse(mopsa) and not mopsaFunded(mopsa) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 20.
    Time 3.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 20. Increase quantity(gilmour, gold) by 40. Assert mopsaHouse(mopsa). Assert mopsaPartner(mopsa). Increase courtship(mopsa) by 1. }
    Result "Mopsa takes twenty coin out of the lining of her stays, where they have been for six years, and puts them beside yours on Mr Gilmour's ledger. 'Halves,' she says. 'Partners. You'll have a room here whenever you're in Hessel, and you'll pay for your coals like anybody.' Mr Gilmour gives her the keys. She gives you one.".
  }
  Action take_lease_funded(actor: group, site: place) "Take Mopsa down to Mr Gilmour with Mrs Cherrett's forty and a character" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, no_four) and at(gilmour, no_four) and mopsaCharacter(mopsa)
      and (at(mopsa, no_four) or following(mopsa, actor)) and not mopsaHouse(mopsa) and mopsaFunded(mopsa).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert mopsaHouse(mopsa). }
    Result "Mr Gilmour reads Mrs Cherrett's note to her banker, and the character, and gives Mopsa the keys. Mopsa holds them so tight her knuckles go white. 'She cried,' she says, on the way out. 'Mrs Cherrett. When I thanked her. She said it was the dropsy.'".
  }
  Rule mopsa_settles when mopsaHouse(mopsa) and following(mopsa, party) { Retract following(mopsa, party). Retract mopsaAway(mopsa). Assert at(mopsa, no_four). }
  Rule mopsa_back when mopsaAway(mopsa) and not following(mopsa, party) and not mopsaHouse(mopsa) { Retract mopsaAway(mopsa). }

  // ── Courting Mopsa ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Not a meter: things done together, each remembered, read by her words. Rescuing her, arranging her or lying to the
  // town spoil it; she will be anyone's partner and nobody's charity.
  Measure courtship(group).
  Relation walkedWith(group). Relation triedRescue(group). Relation mopsaYes(group). Relation mopsaNo(group).
  Rule laughed_counts when laughedWith(party) and not counted(laughed_mark) { Increase courtship(mopsa) by 1. Assert counted(laughed_mark). }
  Rule stood_counts when mopsaPromised(mopsa) and not counted(stood_mark) { Increase courtship(mopsa) by 1. Assert counted(stood_mark). }
  Relation counted(fact). Entity laughed_mark: fact "laughed". Entity stood_mark: fact "stood by".
  // What happened at nineteen: Mrs Cherrett went out of a window; Mopsa went into service.
  Topic mopsa_nineteen with mopsa "Ask Mopsa what happened when she was nineteen" when walkedWith(actor) once {
    Says "'Nineteen.' Mopsa walks on a few steps. 'My father died owing money to a wine merchant, a tailor and the Bishop of Orm, and I went to be companion to a lady at Upper Haddow who did not care for conversation. Eight years. She left me a garnet brooch and the advice to keep my opinions in a drawer.' She touches the brooch at her throat. 'At nineteen Mrs Cherrett went out of a window. At nineteen I went into a drawer.' She laughs, short. 'I've been thinking, lately, that I'd like the window.'".
  }
  Action walk_beacon(actor: group, site: place) "Walk the Beacon with Mopsa, the way the Season walks it, slowly, in pairs" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, beacon) and at(mopsa, beacon) and mopsaRegard(mopsa) >= 1 and not walkedWith(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert walkedWith(actor). Increase courtship(mopsa) by 1. Increase mopsaRegard(mopsa) by 1. }
    Result "You walk the Beacon with Mopsa, slowly, in a pair, the way the Season walks it, and the Season, which walks behind you, looks at the companion and the stranger and whispers. Mopsa does not care. She talks the whole way round, about the sheep, and the Sham Castle, and the people in the Crescent who own telescopes, and a book she read once about a woman who went to sea dressed as a man, and at the end of the walk she says, 'That's the longest I've talked to anybody since I was nineteen,' and looks annoyed about it.".
  }
  Topic mopsa_rescue with mopsa "Offer to marry Mopsa, so that she need never be anybody's companion again" when not mopsaHouse(mopsa) and not triedRescue(party) and not mopsaYes(party) and mopsaRegard(mopsa) >= 1 once {
    Says "Mopsa looks at you with an expression of the most profound disappointment. 'Oh,' she says. 'Oh, no. You too.' She shuts her book. 'I have been offered marriage four times, always out of kindness, by men who thought it would be a fine thing to save a poor companion from being one. I said no to the curate and the widower and the half-pay major and I'll say no to you. I don't want to be saved. I want a house.' She opens the book. 'Ask me again when you've stopped feeling sorry for me. If you ever do.'".
    On discuss { Assert triedRescue(party). }
  }
  Query mopsaWillHave() means courtship(mopsa) >= 3 and not shockedAt(party) and not liedPublicly(party) and not triedRescue(party).
  Topic mopsa_ask with mopsa "Ask Mopsa to marry you" when mopsaWillHave() and not mopsaYes(party) and not mopsaNo(party) and dayN(hessel_town) >= 3 once {
    Says "Mopsa does not answer at once. She looks at you as she looks at a page she means to read twice. 'Not to save me,' she says. 'Not because I'm poor, or plain, or the companion, or because it would be a fine thing.' It is not a question, so you do not answer it. 'Because you'd like it,' she says. 'Because you'd find it interesting.' She puts her book down open on its face, which she never does, it breaks the spine. 'Yes. On my terms. My house, my name on the lease, my own money, and you're to laugh at me when I'm absurd, which is often.' She holds out her hand, not to be kissed: to be shaken.".
    On discuss { Assert mopsaYes(party). }
  }
  Topic mopsa_ask_early with mopsa "Ask Mopsa to marry you" when not mopsaWillHave() and not mopsaYes(party) and not mopsaNo(party) and not triedRescue(party) and mopsaRegard(mopsa) >= 2 and dayN(hessel_town) >= 3 once {
    Says "Mopsa looks at you kindly, which is worse than anything. 'No,' she says. 'Not no for ever. No for now. I don't know you. I know you're kind, and you can carry things, and you've been in Hessel four days.' She picks up her book. 'People get married in Hessel in four days. That's what's wrong with Hessel.'".
    On discuss { Assert mopsaNo(party). }
  }
}

data/adventures/hessel/orm.kyr:
Module hessel "The Banns at Hessel" {
  // ── Dr Ottery ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Sixty, irascible, badly dressed, the best physician in Hessel. Turned off the Hospital of the Waters last month at
  // Dr Hartopp's instance "for frightening the patients", which is to say for telling Mrs Cherrett she was dying when
  // she asked him. Summoned before the College of Physicians at Orm at noon on the second day, for practising without
  // its licence; he needs a witness of good character to stand with him, and nobody in Hessel will be seen to.
  // His question is the work's: is it kinder to tell the truth, or to let people hope? He thinks he knows.
  Person ottery "Dr Jonas Ottery" at hospital {
    Role "an untidy old physician in a coat that has been slept in". Ancestry human. Calling monk. Trait compassion. Level 4. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "The old man in the slept-in coat looks up from the bag he is packing. 'If you're ill, go to Doctors' Walk; there are eleven of them and they're all very pleasant. If you're dying, sit down. I'm the only one in this town who'll tell you so.'".
    Greets again "Ottery grunts at you, which is warmer than it sounds.".
    Joins "'Lead on,' says Ottery, picking up his bag. 'Somebody had better come along and keep you alive. You've a gift for walking into things.'".
  }
  Relation witnessPromised(group). Relation otteryOnRoad(group). Relation otteryWalkedAlone(group).
  Relation otteryLicensed(group). Relation otteryStruck(group). Relation otteryGone(group). Relation otteryFugitive(group).
  Relation otteryHome(group). Relation otteryDecided(group).
  Query otteryInHessel() means otteryHome(ottery) and not otteryGone(ottery) and not travelsWith(ottery, party).
  Initially Assert otteryHome(ottery).
  Query otteryLeaving() means secondDay() and hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 8 and not otteryDecided(ottery).
  Rule ottery_hospital when otteryInHessel() and not otteryLeaving() and not at(ottery, hospital) and not following(ottery, party) and not otteryOnRoad(ottery) and not otteryAway(ottery) { Assert at(ottery, hospital). }
  Relation otteryAway(group).
  Discovery ottery_summons "Dr Ottery is summoned before the College of Physicians at Orm at noon tomorrow, for practising without its licence. He needs a witness of good character to stand with him, and nobody in Hessel will be seen to. He sets out from the Beacon at seven.".
  Topic ottery_why with ottery "Ask Dr Ottery why he is packing" when dayN(hessel_town) <= 2 and not otteryDecided(ottery) once {
    Says "'Because I'm turned off.' Ottery stuffs a roll of lint into the bag as if it had insulted him. 'Twenty years I've physicked the poor of three counties on this ward for nothing, and last month the governors turned me off for frightening the patients.' He snorts. 'Mrs Cherrett asked me, in the Pump Room, in front of everybody, was she dying. I said yes, madam, of dropsy, by the end of the Season, and you'd do well to stop drinking that muck. Dr Hartopp is a governor.' He shuts the bag. 'And now the College at Orm wants me tomorrow noon, for practising without its licence, which I never needed while I was the Hospital's. I need a witness of good character. There's not a soul in Hessel would be seen walking up the Orm road with me.' He looks at you. 'Seven o'clock, the Beacon. If anybody wanted to know.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ottery_summons). }
  }
  Topic ottery_promise with ottery "Tell Dr Ottery you will be at the Beacon at seven, and walk to Orm with him" when knows(actor, ottery_summons) and not witnessPromised(actor) and dayN(hessel_town) == 1 once {
    Says "Ottery looks at you over his spectacles. 'You,' he says. 'A stranger. Of good character.' He considers it. 'Well, nobody knows you're not. Seven. Don't be late. The College hangs about for nobody, and it'll strike me off for the pleasure of not having to read my letters.'".
    On discuss { Assert witnessPromised(actor). }
  }
  // The one truth he has kept back, for nine years, at someone else's asking.
  Topic ottery_tablet with ottery "Ask Dr Ottery about the slate tablet in Saint Ebba's that says HE CAME TOO LATE" when knows(actor, tablets_read) and not knows(actor, snow_child) once {
    Says "Ottery takes his spectacles off, which he does when he does not want to see what he is saying. 'That's mine,' he says. 'Paid for it. Cut by a man who does gateposts.' He polishes the spectacles on his slept-in coat. 'Every patient I have, I tell the truth. You know that; it's why I'm going to Orm.' He puts them back on. 'That one I promised I'd never tell, and I never have, and I'll not start for you.' But he looks at you over them, a long look, as if you might be the kind of person who goes down to the laundries and asks. 'Some promises are worse than lies,' he says. 'They last longer.'".
  }
  Topic ottery_drops with ottery "Tell Dr Ottery what Hartopp has been giving Mrs Cherrett" when knows(actor, drops_doubled) and otteryInHessel() and dosed(cherrett) and not gone(cherrett) and not otteryToldDrops(ottery) once {
    Says "'Forty,' says Ottery. 'Forty a night.' He sits down on the end of a bed. 'That's not a physic, that's a verdict.' He is quiet. 'She asked me in the Pump Room, was she dying, and I told her, and she laughed in my face and went on with the drops. That's her right.' He looks at you. 'But she has the right to know he's doubled it, too. What she does then is hers.'".
    On discuss { Assert otteryToldDrops(ottery). }
  }
  Relation otteryToldDrops(group). Relation halved(group).
  // He goes up the hill and tells her. What he tells her, and what she does, turns on what the company told him on the
  // road: one who said comfort is kinder has made him less sure, and he halves the dose instead of stopping it.
  Action ottery_to_cherrett(actor: group, site: place) "Take Dr Ottery up to the Circus to see Mrs Cherrett" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, cherrett_parlour) and at(cherrett, cherrett_parlour) and (at(ottery, cherrett_parlour) or following(ottery, actor))
      and otteryToldDrops(ottery) and dosed(cherrett) and not gone(cherrett) and not saidComfort(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert stoppedBy(cherrett, ottery). }
    Result "Ottery stands in front of Mrs Cherrett's chair with his hat on, because he has forgotten it, and tells her: forty drops, doubled a month since, laudanum, enough to stop a heart like hers inside a week. Mrs Cherrett listens without interrupting, which nobody has ever seen. 'You told me I was dying,' she says. 'In the Pump Room. Everybody laughed.' 'So you are.' 'Not of Hartopp, though.' 'Not if you can help it.' She looks at him. 'I'd like to die awake,' she says. 'I'd like to see how it comes out. Throw that bottle in the fire, Jonas Ottery, and come to dinner.'".
  }
  Action ottery_halves(actor: group, site: place) "Take Dr Ottery up to the Circus to see Mrs Cherrett" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, cherrett_parlour) and at(cherrett, cherrett_parlour) and (at(ottery, cherrett_parlour) or following(ottery, actor))
      and otteryToldDrops(ottery) and dosed(cherrett) and doubled(cherrett) and not gone(cherrett) and saidComfort(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Retract doubled(cherrett). Assert halved(cherrett). }
    Result "Ottery looks at Mrs Cherrett asleep in her chair with her mouth open, for a long time. Then he takes the bottle from the dressing-table, and pours half of it out of the window, and fills it up from the jug. 'Twenty,' he says, low. 'As it was.' He looks at you. 'You told me on the down that hope's a physic. Well. She's an old woman, and her nights are bad, and she'll sleep.' He puts the bottle back. 'I'll tell her about Hartopp in the morning. Or I won't. I find I'm not as sure as I was.'".
  }

  // The ward without its physician: a company with a nurse's hands can keep it for a morning, which the Old Town remembers.
  Relation wardKept(group).
  Action keep_ward(actor: group, site: place) "Keep the Hospital ward for a morning while its physician is away" {
    Description "Dressings, physic, water, a hand held.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hospital) and not at(ottery, hospital) and capable(actor, mending)
      and not wardKept(actor) and daytime().
    Time 18.
    On success { Assert wardKept(actor). Increase goodwill(chairmen) by 1. }
    Result "Three hours of it: dressings changed, a fever sponged, a boy's arm reset that the Season's physicians would have sent for a guinea, an old woman listened to. Twenty beds, and at the end of the morning a chairman's wife comes in with a basket for her father and finds you with your sleeves up, and goes out again, and by the evening every man on Stall Street has heard it.".
  }
