    Description "The chairmen look after their own, and their own know it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, crossways) and at(footpads, crossways) and warned(footpads, actor)
      and (stoodWith(actor) or goodwill(chairmen) >= 2) and not padsShamed(footpads).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Retract warned(footpads, actor). Assert tolerates(footpads, actor). Assert padsShamed(footpads). Assert knows(actor, hartopp_paid_pads). Assert at(footpads, limbo). }
    Result "The smallest one takes his mask off. He is about sixteen, with Lanyon's ears. 'He don't,' he says. 'And you'll not tell him.' The tall one says, 'Shut up, Davy,' and Davy does not. It comes out all together, with the other two trying to stop it: a gentleman, in a plum coat, at the back door of the Two Poles last night; a purse; three coin a head to stop an old man in a slept-in coat getting to Orm before noon, and not to hurt him much. 'He smelt of cloves,' says Davy. 'Like a pudding.' Then all three go off down the drove road at a trot, and Ottery, who has heard every word, sits down on the step of the gibbet and laughs until he has to wipe his eyes.".
  }
  Relation padsShamed(group).
  Discovery hartopp_paid_pads "The boys at the gibbet were paid to keep Ottery from Orm, by a gentleman who smelt of cloves.".
  // Fought down in front of a physician, the footpads are a physician's business.
  Event footpads_tended at crossways when at(party, crossways) and not able(footpads) and following(ottery, party) "Ottery is down on his knees in the heather beside the two men in crape before you have got your breath, with his bag open. He takes their masks off: two boys from the Old Town, one of them with a chairman's blue coat under his smock. 'You'll live,' he tells them, binding a head, 'which is more than you deserve and less than you'll thank me for.' He does not look at you while he does it. The youngest, with his head bound up, tells Ottery who paid them, because Ottery asks him in the voice he uses on the ward: a gentleman in a plum coat, at the back of the Two Poles, who smelt of cloves. Ottery finishes the knot before he says anything. 'Well,' he says. 'He's a governor. He'd want it done properly.'" teaches hartopp_paid_pads then { Assert tendedFootpads(ottery). }
