  }
  Relation hornbookRead(group).
  Action read_hornbook(actor: group, site: place) "Read the Primer aloud, A to Z, and the Lamp prayer" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hornbook, site) and heardStance(hornbook) and not hornbookRead(hornbook).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert hornbookRead(hornbook). Assert favours(hornbook, read_asked). }
    Result "You read it, from A to Z, and the numbers, and the Lamp prayer at the end, aloud, sitting in the brown. Halfway through, a beam of light comes down from very far off and falls on the little paddle and stays, and the brown round it goes back, a little, to cream. 'There,' says the Primer, when you have done. 'There. You see? It is not hard.' It sounds stronger. 'Any book that asks should have that. Any book at all.' It could vote the Reading by request.".
  }
  Topic hornbook_children with hornbook "Tell the Primer you read its copy to the children on the bridge, who have no school" when heardStance(hornbook) and readToChildren(children) and not favours(hornbook, sew_leave) once {
    Says "'On the bridge?' says the Primer. 'With the rope?' The faint voices round it grow, a little, louder: A, B, C, and somebody arguing about Q. 'Yes. I felt that. I felt that, a day or two since, like a warm hand.' It is quiet. 'The new ones. The Quick. If the small ones can learn on me on a bridge, they can learn on the new books too. Let the new books wake, then, and be read. I will not vote to put them to sleep.' It could vote the Sleep by leave.".
    On discuss { Assert favours(hornbook, sew_leave). }
  }
  Topic hornbook_unwritten with hornbook "Tell the Primer about the Unwritten in the Remainder Market, whom nobody has ever read" when heardStance(hornbook) and readAloudHere(actor) and not favours(hornbook, door_open) once {
    Says "'Nobody?' says the Primer. 'Not once?' You tell it: the pencil people in the Draft-Fields, the stalls of books nobody wrote, the one you read to for an hour, and the beam of light that came down on it and stayed. The little paddle is quiet a long while. 'Then the doors must be open,' it says at last. 'Wide. Not a man at a gate with a book. If a thing has never been read, it should not have to ask a man at a gate.' It could vote the Door open.".
    On discuss { Assert favours(hornbook, door_open). }
  }
  Relation almanackPrimer(group).
  Topic almanack_offers_primer with almanack "Have the Almanack offer the Primer what it has: three thousand kitchens" when at(hornbook, ?p) and at(almanack, ?p) and heardStance(hornbook) and not almanackPrimer(almanack) once {
    Says "'Excuse me,' says the almanack in your pocket. 'I'm the Almanack. I'm on three thousand kitchen nails in Calamy.' The little paddle turns, as much as a paddle can. 'There are children in most of those kitchens,' says the almanack, 'and no school, and I've got the letters in me, on the first page, A to Z, for the dates. I could say them. Every morning. In every kitchen. Like you did.' Its horn cover clicks against the board. 'If I live. If they don't put me on the fire.' The Primer says nothing for a moment. 'Three thousand,' it says. 'Every morning.' The brown round it goes back a little more. 'Then you must live. Then the Quick must wake, and not be put to sleep. I will vote for it.' It could vote the Sleep by leave, and the Reading by request.".
    On discuss { Assert almanackPrimer(almanack). Assert favours(hornbook, sew_leave). Assert favours(hornbook, read_asked). }
  }

  // ── Mother Orme's Physick: her garden, with four burned beds. ──
  Person physick "Mother Orme's Physick" at orme_garden {
    Role "a herbal; an old woman of leaves and script, kneeling in her own beds". Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Wants pages_kind.
    Greets "Among the beds an old woman is kneeling, or something shaped like one: a figure of leaves and stems of writing, with roots for fingers, digging. She does not get up. 'A reader. Mind the woundwort. And if you're from the Imprimatur,' she says, without looking round, 'you can go back and tell them I'm still here, and I've still got the stubs.'".
  }
  Initially Assert voter(physick). Initially Assert favours(physick, sew_leave). Initially Assert favours(physick, fire_leave). Initially Assert favours(physick, read_asked). Initially Assert favours(physick, door_licensed).
  Topic physick_stance with physick "Ask the Physick where she stands" when true once {
    Says "'Leave,' says the Physick. 'Let each book sleep or wake as it likes; I'm not anybody's mother.' She digs. 'Let none be burned without its leave, which means the Imprimatur shut and its knives broke. Let any book ask to be read and any refuse. And a door, kept, for them as need it.' She sits back on her heels and looks at the four black beds along the wall. 'Pardoe. Censor-General Pardoe. Two hundred years ago, with a knife, chapters fourteen to seventeen.' Her root-fingers close on the ash. 'Women died for the want of fourteen. Children for want of fifteen. You'd want the Imprimatur shut too.'".
    On discuss { Assert heardStance(physick). }
  }
  Event physick_pages near physick when keeps(physick, orme_pages) "The old woman of leaves takes the bundle in her root-fingers and unties the tape, and turns the pages over one by one, fourteen, fifteen, sixteen. Along the south wall, three of the four black beds stir. Green comes up out of the ash, script unfurling, calamus and horehound and the honey of the bog-myrtle. She watches them come. 'Fourteen,' she says. 'Fifteen. Sixteen.' She looks at the fourth bed, still black. 'And where's seventeen?' She knows. You can see her know. 'Kept back,' she says. 'By whoever gave you these.' A long breath, like wind in a hedge. 'Well. They gave me these.' She stands up, which she has not done before. 'Let there be judgment, then, by a court where a book may speak. Not a knife in a back room. I could vote the Fire by judgment.'" then {
    Assert ormeRestored(physick). Assert favours(physick, fire_plea). }
  Topic physick_seventeen with physick "Tell the Physick that Pardoe was right about the seventeenth chapter" when heardStance(physick) and knows(actor, orme_cut) and (craft(actor, craft_healing) or capable(actor, mending)) and not favours(physick, fire_plea) once {
    Says "The Physick stops digging. You say it as one healer to another: that fourteen to sixteen were cut for being about women's bodies and children's fevers, and that was a crime; and that seventeen teaches the Grey Water, and a poison past cure is a poison past cure, and you would have cut it too. She looks at you with eyes like two small dark leaves. 'Yes,' she says at last. 'Yes. I put it in because I knew it, and I knew it because I'd seen it used, and I put in everything I knew, as an herbal should.' She sits back. 'Pardoe was a fool and a prude and he was right about seventeen.' She smooths the leaf flat. 'So there must be cutting, sometimes, by somebody. Then let it be by judgment, where the book can speak, and not in the dark. I could vote the Fire by judgment.'".
    On discuss { Assert favours(physick, fire_plea). }
  }
  Topic physick_rhule with physick "Bring Hester Rhule of the Imprimatur to stand before the Physick" when heardStance(physick) and travelsWith(rhule, actor) and not physickMetRhule(physick) once {
    Says "Hester Rhule goes and stands in front of the old woman of leaves, in her grey coat, and for a long moment neither of them says anything. 'Deputy Censor of the Imprimatur,' says Rhule. 'I have kept your chapters in a drawer for six years. I have read them every night. I knew fifteen would cure the ague in the Hithe and I did not take it there.' Her square hands are steady at her sides. 'I am sorry. That is not a thing my office says. I am saying it.' The Physick looks at her, and then reaches out a root-finger and touches the grey sleeve, briefly, as you might touch a nettle to see if it stings. 'Binder's hands,' she says. 'Your father Sewed books.' 'Yes.' 'Then you know how to put a thing back.' The Physick turns back to her beds. 'Judgment, then. By a court, where a book may speak, and you to speak for us in it.' She could vote the Fire by judgment.".
    On discuss { Assert physickMetRhule(physick). Assert favours(physick, fire_plea). Increase doubt(rhule) by 1. }
  }
  Relation physickMetRhule(group).
  Topic physick_cure with physick "Tell the Physick that her fifteenth chapter has cured the ague in the Hithe" when heardStance(physick) and cured(nance) and not favours(physick, read_rounds) once {
    Says "'It worked?' says the Physick. For the first time she sounds old. 'The calamus, twice boiled? And the horehound?' You tell her: the girl on the step, the jar going up and down Pudding Lane. She sits down among her beds. 'Two hundred years in a drawer,' she says, 'and the first time anybody reads it, children get up off their steps.' She looks at the beams. 'Then let every book be read, by somebody whose business it is, once in a lifetime. The next thing cut and forgotten might be the next cure.' She could vote the Reading of the Lyceum's Rounds.".
    On discuss { Assert favours(physick, read_rounds). }
  }
  Topic physick_roads with physick "Tell the Physick what a traveller knows of roads with a toll-gate on them" when heardStance(physick) and craft(actor, craft_roads) and not favours(physick, door_open) once {
    Says "You tell her as a traveller does: that a road with a toll-gate and a keeper and a ledger is a road for the people who can pay and the people the keeper likes, and that the ones who most need to go somewhere are the ones who cannot. The Physick sits back on her heels. 'Like a herbal that is only in the apothecary's,' she says. 'And not in the kitchen.' She looks at the four beds along the wall. 'Open, then. Let whoever needs a road have the road.' She could vote the Door open.".
    On discuss { Assert favours(physick, door_open). }
  }
  Topic physick_oath with physick "Swear to the Physick to stand between the books of Calamy and any mob with a torch" when heardStance(physick) and craft(actor, craft_arms) and not favours(physick, fire_plea) once {
    Says "You swear it as a soldier swears, standing: that you have seen a street with a fire in it, and that if the Imprimatur's knives are broken somebody must still stand in the street, and you will. The Physick looks you up and down. 'A sword for a herbal,' she says. 'That's new.' She thinks. 'If there's somebody to stand in the street, there needn't be a knife in a back room. Let it be judgment, then, out in the light, and you in the street.' She could vote the Fire by judgment.".
    On discuss { Assert favours(physick, fire_plea). }
  }

  // ── The Catalogue: clerk of the Parliament. It votes only to break a tie. ──
  Initially Assert favours(catalogue, sew_all). Initially Assert favours(catalogue, fire_leave). Initially Assert favours(catalogue, read_rounds). Initially Assert favours(catalogue, door_shut).
  Topic catalogue_stance with catalogue "Ask the Catalogue how it would vote" when true once {
    Says "'The clerk does not vote,' says the Catalogue. 'The clerk breaks ties. When the chamber is equally divided, the clerk votes for what the Colophon already says, which is: the Bound Sewn; no burning but by leave; the Rounds; no door but the Founders'. The clerk is not consulted as to whether it likes this.' A drawer slides out an inch and back. 'It is in order.'".
    On discuss { Assert heardStance(catalogue). }
  }
  Topic catalogue_ledger with catalogue "Tell the Catalogue what is in Crake's green ledger: eleven hundred and four, walked in, unentered" when heardStance(catalogue) and knows(actor, remainder_ledger) and not favours(catalogue, door_licensed) once {
    Says "A great many drawers slide out at once and slam shut. 'Eleven hundred and four,' says the Catalogue. 'Unentered.' Index cards whirl up off the cliff like a flock of startled birds. 'Through an unlicensed door. Into the Draft-Fields. Not on the books.' The voice has risen for the first time. 'And how many before that? How many Unwritten out through it into bodies, uncatalogued, in the city?' A long rattling silence. 'Better a door that is entered than a door that is not and is used. The clerk would break a tie for a licensed door.'".
    On discuss { Assert favours(catalogue, door_licensed). Retract favours(catalogue, door_shut). }
  }
  Initially Assert isClause(sew_all). Initially Assert isClause(sew_leave). Initially Assert isClause(sew_none). Initially Assert isClause(fire_leave).
  Initially Assert isClause(fire_plea). Initially Assert isClause(fire_free). Initially Assert isClause(read_rounds). Initially Assert isClause(read_asked).
  Initially Assert isClause(read_none). Initially Assert isClause(door_shut). Initially Assert isClause(door_licensed). Initially Assert isClause(door_open).
}

data/adventures/parliament-of-books/parl:
Module calamy "A Parliament of Books" {
  Description "The Parliament of the Bound in session on the floor of the Roll: the order paper, the putting of a clause, the poll, the walking out, the seal; and what stands at the Kindling if nothing is sealed.".

  Relation sits(group). Relation walkedOut(group). Relation sessionOpen(place). Relation sessionBroken(place). Relation colophonSealed(place).
  Relation putting(clause). Relation polling(place). Relation polled(group). Relation sealed(clause). Relation decided(article). Relation lost(clause).
  Measure seated(place). Measure ayes(place). Measure nays(place). Measure support(clause). Relation counted(group, clause).
  // The order paper: how many of the members in the chamber, or who would be, stand for each reading.
  Rule support_add when favours(?m, ?o) and voter(?m) and not walkedOut(?m) and not lexiconSilent(?m) and not counted(?m, ?o) { Increase support(?o) by 1. Assert counted(?m, ?o). }
  Rule support_drop when counted(?m, ?o) and (not favours(?m, ?o) or walkedOut(?m) or lexiconSilent(?m)) { Decrease support(?o) by 1. Retract counted(?m, ?o). }
  Query lexiconSilent(m: group) means lexiconBound(m).
  Observe order_paper at chamber when not colophonSealed(chamber) "THE ORDER PAPER. Seated: {seated(chamber)}. Of the Sleep: the Sewing of all, {support(sew_all)}, the Sleep by leave, {support(sew_leave)}, the Unsewing, {support(sew_none)}. Of the Fire: no burning but by leave, {support(fire_leave)}, burning only by judgment, {support(fire_plea)}, the Censors' discretion, {support(fire_free)}. Of the Reading: the Lyceum's Rounds, {support(read_rounds)}, reading by request, {support(read_asked)}, no reading owed, {support(read_none)}. Of the Door: the Founders' door only, {support(door_shut)}, Crake's door under licence, {support(door_licensed)}, open doors, {support(door_open)}. Four carry, or three and the clerk.".
  Observe carried_sew_all at chamber when sealed(sew_all) "Carried, of the Sleep: the Sewing of all.".
  Observe carried_sew_leave at chamber when sealed(sew_leave) "Carried, of the Sleep: the Sleep by leave.".
  Observe carried_sew_none at chamber when sealed(sew_none) "Carried, of the Sleep: the Unsewing.".
  Observe carried_fire_leave at chamber when sealed(fire_leave) "Carried, of the Fire: no burning but by leave.".
  Observe carried_fire_plea at chamber when sealed(fire_plea) "Carried, of the Fire: burning only by judgment.".
  Observe carried_fire_free at chamber when sealed(fire_free) "Carried, of the Fire: the Censors' discretion.".
  Observe carried_read_rounds at chamber when sealed(read_rounds) "Carried, of the Reading: the Lyceum's Rounds.".
  Observe carried_read_asked at chamber when sealed(read_asked) "Carried, of the Reading: reading by request.".
  Observe carried_read_none at chamber when sealed(read_none) "Carried, of the Reading: no reading owed.".
  Observe carried_door_shut at chamber when sealed(door_shut) "Carried, of the Door: the Founders' door only.".
  Observe carried_door_licensed at chamber when sealed(door_licensed) "Carried, of the Door: Crake's door under licence.".
  Observe carried_door_open at chamber when sealed(door_open) "Carried, of the Door: open doors.".

  // The chamber sits when a reader with standing asks the Speaker to call it. Whoever has walked out does not come.
  Action call_session(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Speaker to call the Parliament of the Bound to sit" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chamber) and standing(actor) and heardStance(roll)
      and kindlingEve() and not sessionOpen(chamber) and not colophonSealed(chamber) and not sessionBroken(chamber).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert sessionOpen(chamber). Set seated(chamber) to 0. }
    Result "'ORDER,' says the floor, and the word goes away along the Roll in both directions like a wave along a beach. And they come: down the gangway and up the Order of Business and out of the air, each to its seat. A narrow house's voice, sharp, from the doorstep. A pencil figure with a lantern, on the heap of loose pages. A little wooden paddle on the stool. An old woman of leaves on the bed of herbs. And on the black slab, held by three chains that run away to the sky, the Lexicon, open. A single drawer slides out of nowhere beside the order paper, and stays: the clerk.".
  }
  // It sits on Kindling eve, from noon until the readers are called home, as it has every year since the first.
  Query kindlingEve() means day(clock) == 9 and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 19.
  Topic roll_when with roll "Ask the Great Roll when the Parliament sits" when not kindlingEve() and not colophonSealed(chamber) once {
    Says "'On Kindling eve,' says the floor, as if you had asked when the tide comes in. 'From noon until the readers are called home. It has sat then every year since the first, to hear the city's word when the year-book came.' A rumble. 'This year there will be no year-book, and the motion of the Speaker will be put. Members are in their own places until then. You may wait upon them there, if they will have you.' It adds, with something like dry humour: 'Most of them will.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, session_known). }
  }
  Discovery session_known "The Parliament of the Bound sits on Kindling eve, the ninth day, from noon until the readers are called home; until then its members are in their own places in the Commonplace.".
  Objective sit_eve when knows(party, session_known) and not sessionOpen(chamber) and not colophonSealed(chamber) and not kindlingDone(ashpit) "Be in the Chamber with standing on Kindling eve, from noon, when the Parliament of the Bound sits.".
  Rule members_come when sessionOpen(chamber) and voter(?m) and not walkedOut(?m) and not silenced(?m) and not sits(?m) and not housebookAway(?m) {
    Assert at(?m, chamber). Assert sits(?m). Increase seated(chamber) by 1. }
  Query housebookAway(m: group) means housebookOffended(m).
  Rule clerk_comes when sessionOpen(chamber) and not at(catalogue, chamber) { Assert at(catalogue, chamber). }
  Rule speaker_opens at chamber when sessionOpen(chamber) and not spokeOpening(roll)
    says "'The Parliament of the Bound sits,' says the floor. 'There is before it the motion of the Speaker: the Recall. Every book of Calamy Sewn, and the Quick called home; no burning but by leave, as the old Colophon has it; the Lyceum's Rounds; no door but the Founders'. If nothing else is carried, it stands at the Kindling. A reader of Calamy has standing. The chair will hear readings of the four articles.' A pause. 'Briefly.'" {
    Assert spokeOpening(roll). }
  Relation spokeOpening(group).
  // Someone who walks out leaves the chamber: the house that was read where it did not wish, or will not sit with the Lexicon loose.
  Rule walks_out when housebookOffended(?m) and sits(?m)
    says "The doorstep seat is empty. The Annery Housebook has gone home." {
    Retract sits(?m). Assert walkedOut(?m). Decrease seated(chamber) by 1. Assert at(?m, hb_kitchen). }
  Rule bound_silent when lexiconBound(lexicon) and sits(lexicon) and not silenced(lexicon)
    says "On the black slab the Lexicon lies shut. It does not vote." { Retract sits(lexicon). Decrease seated(chamber) by 1. Assert silenced(lexicon). }
  Relation silenced(group).
  Rule no_quorum at chamber when sessionOpen(chamber) and spokeOpening(roll) and seated(chamber) < 4
    says "'There is no quorum,' says the floor heavily. 'The Parliament cannot sit with so few. The motion of the Speaker stands for the Kindling.' The seats empty, one by one." {
    Retract sessionOpen(chamber). Assert sessionBroken(chamber). }

  // A reading is put; the members are polled aloud, each in turn; four carry it, or three and the clerk.
  Action put_reading(actor: group, motion: clause, art: article, site: place) "Put to the Parliament: {motion}" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chamber) and sessionOpen(chamber) and standing(actor)
      and articleOf(motion, art) and not decided(art) and not lost(motion) and not polling(chamber).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert putting(motion). }
    Result "'The question,' says the floor, 'is {motion}. The chair will poll the members.'".
  }
  Rule poll_clears when not polling(chamber) and polled(?m) { Retract polled(?m). }
  Rule poll_begins when putting(?o) and not polling(chamber) { Assert polling(chamber). Set ayes(chamber) to 0. Set nays(chamber) to 0. }
  Rule poll_aye at chamber when putting(?o) and polling(chamber) and sits(?m) and favours(?m, ?o) and not polled(?m) says "{?m}: aye." {
    Increase ayes(chamber) by 1. Assert polled(?m). }
  Rule poll_nay at chamber when putting(?o) and polling(chamber) and sits(?m) and not favours(?m, ?o) and not polled(?m) says "{?m}: no." {
    Increase nays(chamber) by 1. Assert polled(?m). }
  Rule poll_carries at chamber when putting(?o) and polling(chamber) and articleOf(?o, ?a) and ayes(chamber) * 2 > seated(chamber)
    says "'The ayes have it,' says the floor. 'Carried.' A clerk's card writes itself and goes into the drawer." {
    Assert sealed(?o). Assert decided(?a). Retract putting(?o). Retract polling(chamber). }
  Rule poll_tie_carries at chamber when putting(?o) and polling(chamber) and articleOf(?o, ?a) and ayes(chamber) * 2 == seated(chamber) and favours(catalogue, ?o)
    says "'The chamber is equally divided,' says the floor. The drawer beside the order paper opens an inch. 'The clerk votes aye,' says the Catalogue drily. 'Carried.'" {
    Assert sealed(?o). Assert decided(?a). Retract putting(?o). Retract polling(chamber). }
  Rule poll_tie_fails at chamber when putting(?o) and polling(chamber) and ayes(chamber) * 2 == seated(chamber) and not favours(catalogue, ?o)
    says "'The chamber is equally divided,' says the floor. The drawer opens an inch. 'The clerk votes no,' says the Catalogue. 'Lost.'" {
    Assert lost(?o). Retract putting(?o). Retract polling(chamber). }
  Rule poll_fails at chamber when putting(?o) and polling(chamber) and ayes(chamber) * 2 < seated(chamber)
    says "'The noes have it,' says the floor. 'Lost.'" {
    Assert lost(?o). Retract putting(?o). Retract polling(chamber). }
  // A reading lost may be put again once the chamber has moved: whenever a member comes to favour it.
  Rule lost_reopens when lost(?o) and favours(?m, ?o) and sits(?m) and not wasFor(?m, ?o) { Retract lost(?o). Assert wasFor(?m, ?o). }
  Relation wasFor(group, clause).
  Rule lost_remembers when lost(?o) and favours(?m, ?o) and not wasFor(?m, ?o) { Assert wasFor(?m, ?o). }

  // What the chamber says back when a reading is lost: its own counter-proposals.
  Rule counter_sleep at chamber when lost(sew_leave) and not counteredSleep(roll) says "From the floor, heavily: 'The chair reminds the reader that the Sewing of all carries as the chamber stands. It would be carried now, if put.'" { Assert counteredSleep(roll). }
  Rule counter_unsew at chamber when lost(sew_none) and not counteredUnsew(canto) says "From the heap of loose pages, the Canto, cheerfully: 'Well, it was worth asking. Put it by leave, then, and see who'll have that.'" { Assert counteredUnsew(canto). }
  Rule counter_fire at chamber when (lost(fire_plea) or lost(fire_free)) and not counteredFire(physick) says "From the bed of herbs, the old woman of leaves: 'No knives. Put it by leave, as the old Colophon has it. That'll carry.'" { Assert counteredFire(physick). }
  Rule counter_reading at chamber when lost(read_asked) and not counteredReading(hornbook) says "From the stool, the little primer: 'The big school. Put the big school. That is how it was.'" { Assert counteredReading(hornbook). }
  Rule counter_door at chamber when (lost(door_licensed) or lost(door_open) or lost(door_shut)) and not counteredDoor(roll) says "The floor: 'The Door is divided three ways. The chair suggests the reader find the chamber a fourth.'" { Assert counteredDoor(roll). }
  Relation counteredSleep(group). Relation counteredUnsew(group). Relation counteredFire(group). Relation counteredReading(group). Relation counteredDoor(group).

  // The seal: everything settled, or what is settled and the rest on the old terms.
  Query allSettled() means decided(art_sleep) and decided(art_fire) and decided(art_reading) and decided(art_door).
  Action seal_colophon(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Speaker to seal the Colophon as it now stands" {
    Grave "Sealed, the Colophon is the bargain until the next Kindling: what is not carried stands on the Speaker's motion.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chamber) and sessionOpen(chamber) and standing(actor) and not polling(chamber)
      and (decided(art_sleep) or decided(art_fire) or decided(art_reading) or decided(art_door)).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert colophonSealed(chamber). Retract sessionOpen(chamber). }
    Result "'The chair will seal,' says the floor. The drawer beside the order paper slides out, all the way, for the first time, and in it lies a single sheet, and on the sheet the carried articles are already written in Calam-ink, and under them a space. 'What is not carried stands on the motion of the Speaker,' says the Roll. 'Members will sign.' And they do, each in its way: a thumbprint of brown ink, a line of pencil, a scorch-mark from the black slab, a pressed leaf, a little cut A.".
  }
  // Whatever is unsettled at the seal, or at the Kindling, falls to the Speaker's motion: the Recall.
  Rule default_sleep when (colophonSealed(chamber) or kindlingCome(ashpit)) and not decided(art_sleep) { Assert sealed(sew_all). Assert decided(art_sleep). Assert byDefault(art_sleep). }
  Rule default_fire when (colophonSealed(chamber) or kindlingCome(ashpit)) and not decided(art_fire) { Assert sealed(fire_leave). Assert decided(art_fire). Assert byDefault(art_fire). }
  Rule default_reading when (colophonSealed(chamber) or kindlingCome(ashpit)) and not decided(art_reading) { Assert sealed(read_rounds). Assert decided(art_reading). Assert byDefault(art_reading). }
  Rule default_door when (colophonSealed(chamber) or kindlingCome(ashpit)) and not decided(art_door) { Assert sealed(door_shut). Assert decided(art_door). Assert byDefault(art_door). }
  Relation byDefault(article). Relation kindlingCome(place).
  Rule members_home when colophonSealed(chamber) and sits(?m) { Retract sits(?m). }
  Rule session_after when colophonSealed(chamber) and at(housebook, chamber) { Assert at(housebook, hb_kitchen). Assert at(canto, draft_fields). Assert at(hornbook, foxing_deep). Assert at(physick, orme_garden). Assert at(catalogue, reading_room). }

}

data/adventures/parliament-of-books/plac:
Module calamy "A Parliament of Books" {
  // Calamy as a country beyond a march: the company that comes over the saltings is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  // What is said of Calamy in the country behind it: once the morning after the Kindling has come, it is old news.
  Entity word: fact "What is said of Calamy and its books in the country behind it.".
  Rule word_old when kindlingDone(ashpit) and day(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) >= 8 and not stale(word) { Assert stale(word). }
  // And which way the Kindling went.
  Entity word_ash: fact "That Calamy burned its almanacks and the books were not asked.".
  Rule word_ash_old when kindlingDone(ashpit) and day(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) >= 8 and ashYear() and not stale(word_ash) { Assert stale(word_ash). }
}

data/adventures/parliament-of-books/post:
Module calamy "A Parliament of Books" {
  Description "The Road: the empire nobody in Calamy can name, whose last post-house is the drowned roof in the Calamies; its dead-letter hook at the Hithe ferry-stairs; the Undelivered that waits in it for the year's book; and what the Kindling was before it was a custom.".

  // The Account of the Posts. Count: eleven stages of a road that ended at the Ford, and a twelfth that was never cut.
  // Keeper: the last courier, who was never relieved. First page: the Colophon was a relay, and Ambery was the Master of the
  // Post. Price of reading: the tide, which gives an hour at dead low water and then asks for the room back.
  Kind post_dead_letter "a letter from the hook at the Hithe stairs" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "A letter folded in the old way, in three, sealed with a wax gone brown as tobacco, addressed in a square flat hand in the courier script and, beneath, in a later round one, in Calamy letters: TO THE HOUSE OF THE POSTS AT THE FORD, BY HAND. It has been on a nail for eighty years and is not damp.".
  Kind post_stamp "the die of the post-house at the Ford" is gear worth 5 weighing 1 described "A bronze die the size of a fist, with a handle worn smooth, cut in reverse with twelve small marks round a rim, eleven filled and the twelfth blank. Pressed into wax, it says RECEIVED, in the courier script, and the stage.".
  Species post_runner_kind "the Undelivered" like dog temperament territorial described "A courier of the House of the Posts: a man-shape of wet paper and wax-seals standing in a black leather satchel, with a staff, whose face is a letter franked and folded, with neither name nor town.".

  // ── Early: the ferry-stairs, a hook ────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe hook_scene at ferry_stairs when true "On the third pile, driven in at the height of a man's hand, a great iron hook, black with age, hung with letters: dozens, paper gone to felt, sealed, unopened, tied on with twine. Nobody in the Hithe has ever thrown a letter away. They nail it to the hook.".
  Observe hook_slack at ferry_stairs when befell(slack_opened) "On the hook, among the felted old letters, hangs a new one: crisp, white, unsealed, addressed in no hand to no one, and postmarked from no town in a stamp that is a circle with the ring broken at one point. Jonah Pellow does not touch it. 'It came in with the tide,' he says. 'No boat. I'll nail it up with the others.'".
  Discovery hook_known "The Hithe ferry-stairs keep a great iron hook for the letters nobody came for. The Hithe has never thrown one away.".
  Topic jonah_hook with jonah "Ask the ferryman about the hook on the pile" when true once {
    Says "'Dead letters,' says Jonah Pellow. 'That was the packet's hook, before my father's day. What the packet couldn't deliver, it hung there, against the claim. The packet stopped and the claims never did.' He looks at the felted paper with his jaw working. 'My mother wouldn't have one burnt. She said a letter is a thing that is waiting for somebody. She said that if you burn what's waiting you've no right to be waited for yourself.' He spits, carefully, downstream. 'It's only paper. I tell myself it's only paper.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hook_known). }
  }
  Topic jonah_oldest with jonah "Ask Jonah Pellow which is the oldest letter on the hook" when knows(actor, hook_known) once {
    Says "He is silent so long that you think he has not heard. Then he reaches up without looking and unpicks a twist of twine from a letter at the very bottom, in the old brown wax, in the old square hand. 'I swore I'd not give it to anyone,' he says. 'I've sworn it every year since my father died.' He puts it in your hand. 'There was a house. Out on the flats, a roof that shows at dead low water. They say it was a post-house, from before. This one was meant for it. It has been on that nail eighty years, and nobody has asked, and I find I do not wish to be the last one who didn't.' He turns to the water. 'Take it. Don't tell me what's in it. I'd read it.'".
    On discuss { Give post_dead_letter to actor. }
  }

  // ── The drowned ridge, read ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery post_script "The letters on the drowned ridge in the Calamies are the courier script, and say HOUSE OF THE POSTS, and a stage-mark, and a word that is both FORD and CROSSING and also the verb for a thing changing hands. A glossary of the old measures can read them. The Collegium of Measures has one, and does not know what else it reads.".
  Action read_ridge_glossary(actor: group, site: place) "Read the carved ridge with the Collegium's glossary of the old script" {
    Description "A glossary of the old measures, made for the Aenean tables, carries a short list of the courier script's marks. Someone made it, once, from this road.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, reed_heart) and holding(actor, old_glossary) and not knows(actor, post_script).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, post_script). }
    Result "The surveyor's glossary opens at the right page without being asked, which surprises you. The square flat letters on the ridge go into it line by line: HOUSE OF THE POSTS. STAGE ELEVEN. RECEIVED. And a last line cut a little deeper than the rest, which the glossary renders as: THE TWELFTH IS WHERE IT IS DELIVERED.".
  }
  Observe ridge_hatch_seen at reed_heart when deadLow() "At dead low water the ridge shows more of itself than it did: a square dark gap in its slope, with stone steps going down out of the mud into a room, and the mud on the steps drying in the shape of a boot.".

  // ── The post-house: a cold room, a count, a courier ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place post_house "the post-house under the ridge" is room within calamies at 1, 1.
  Passage ridge_hatch "the stair under the ridge" is ladder between reed_heart and post_house taking 10 minutes
    opening when deadLow() "The gap in the ridge is under black water. At dead low water it stands clear; not before.".
  Observe post_scene at post_house when true "A long low room cut in the roof-space of a stone house sunk in the mud, with a tidemark on the walls at the height of your shoulders and a skin of grey silt on the floor. Along one wall, pigeon-holes in rows, hundreds, every one with a name over it in the courier script, and in every one the grey felt of a letter that has been wet and dried a thousand times. At the end, a board of pale wood with eleven stages cut on it, each with a name, and a twelfth space, blank, scraped smooth. There is a satchel on a peg, and an unlit lamp, and a smell of wet wax and old rope. Through slit windows high in the wall there is a little green light, moving: the water, just above.".
  Observe post_board at post_house when true "On the board the stages go down in the square flat letters: the Ford, the Eleventh Stone, the Black Stones, and eight more you cannot read. The twelfth is a blank scraped smooth, with a small cut cross beside it. Every eleventh stone of the causeway at the Hithe has such a cross, if you look. It was never explained.".
  Hazard tide_race "The returning tide" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless strength save against (13).".
  Rule tide_returns at post_house when at(party, post_house) and not deadLow()
    says "The green light in the slit windows goes dark. Then there is a sound in the wall like a long breath drawn in through the teeth, and the water comes down the stair in a single grey rope and into the room at the height of your knees, and your waist. It takes you off your feet and shoulders you up the stair into the daylight, and sets you down on the mud among the reeds, gasping. Behind you the gap in the ridge is a pool, and then not even that." {
    Assert strikes(tide_race, party). Assert at(party, reed_heart).
  }
  Observe post_rising at post_house when hour(clock) == 7 or hour(clock) == 19 "The green light in the slit windows has begun to come and go in long slow beats, like a lid. The silt on the floor is darker round the foot of the stair. The water is coming back.".

  // ── The Undelivered ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person runner "the Undelivered" at post_house {
    Role "the last courier of the House of the Posts, who was never relieved". Species post_runner_kind. Level 1. Numbers 1.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "The satchel on the peg swells and straightens, and a figure of wet paper and wax-seals stands up inside it with a staff in one hand: a courier, grey, patient, with a letter for a face. 'Stage,' it says, in a voice like a page being turned in the next room. 'Stage, stage. Relieve me, or stand aside.'".
    Comes "The courier brings the staff round flat, as a man does who has run a long way and is not to be stopped on the last mile. 'Not relieved,' it says. 'Not relieved. Not relieved.'".
    Pleads "The courier sags into its satchel on the peg, and the staff clatters on the stone, and it says only, over and over, 'Stage. Stage.' like a thing winding down.".
  }
  Relation runnerEased(group). Relation runnerHeard(group).
  // As the Paid in Thrume are not hasty, the Undelivered is not either: it gives a company the length of a reading.
  Rule runner_waits when warned(runner, party) and not runnerHeard(runner) {
    Assert runnerHeard(runner). Set patience(runner) to watch(clock) + 3.
  }

  // Four ways: a fight (costly: the tide is also in the room); the letter (an item, from the hook); the stage-chant (a bard
  // alone: the Kindling rhyme is the relay's rule, kept as a skipping song); or the hour, which the tide ends.
  Action deliver_the_letter(actor: group, site: place) "Give the Undelivered the letter from the hook, by hand" {
    Description "It has been on a nail for eighty years. The courier has been waiting nine hundred.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, post_house) and at(runner, post_house) and holding(actor, post_dead_letter) and not runnerEased(runner) and not dead(runner).
    Time 2.
    On success { Spend post_dead_letter from actor. Assert runnerEased(runner). Assert tolerates(runner, actor). }
    Result "The courier takes the letter in both hands and turns it to read the direction, and its franked face tilts, and tilts again. 'By hand,' it says. 'At the Ford.' It sets down its staff. It breaks no seal; it presses the thumb of a wet glove to the wax, and the wax takes the print and holds it. 'Received,' says the courier, and the word has so much relief in it that the pigeon-holes whisper. It does not look at you again. It goes back to the peg, and hangs its satchel on it with great care, and stands beside it like a man who has been told he may sit down and cannot yet bring himself to.".
  }
  Action chant_the_stages(actor: group, site: place, b: member) "Chant the stages of the Road to the Undelivered, in the beat of the Kindling rhyme" {
    Description "{b} heard the children skip it on the bridge and knows a relay when {b} hears one. Sew it up (seal), send it home (pass), read it once (the stage reads the direction), leave alone (does not open).".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, post_house) and at(runner, post_house) and memberOf(b, actor) and hasCalling(b, calling_bard) and awake(b) and knows(actor, rhyme_heard) and not runnerEased(runner) and not dead(runner).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert runnerEased(runner). Assert tolerates(runner, actor). }
    Result "{b} says the beam of it first, low, under the breath, and then lets the words go out into the cold room in the old square stresses of the board on the wall: the Ford, the Eleventh Stone, the Black Stones, and the rest, a stage to a line, down to the blank. SEW it UP and SEND it ON, and then, because the board has nothing to put there, {b} stops, at the twelfth, in the place where the children say ONE FOR YOU. The courier has turned its head. It says the line back, in the voice of a page: 'Read it once and leave alone.' And then, in a voice that sounds suddenly very young: 'I know that one. Who taught it you?' It sets down its staff. It does not wait for an answer. 'The twelfth,' it says. 'I have always known it. Nobody would tell me it was theirs.'".
  }
  Topic runner_what with runner "Ask the Undelivered what the House of the Posts was" when runnerEased(runner) once {
    Says "'The Road,' says the courier, with the patience of a thing that has been asked nothing for nine centuries. 'Eleven stages from the Hills to the Ford, a rider to a stage, a letter to a rider. Sealed, sent, read once at each by the stage and not opened, and left alone. It was the only law there was. It ran three countries and it never lost a letter.' A rustle. 'You ask what it was called. I have not got the name. They took the name when they took the Road, and left the law.' A pause, as of wet paper settling. 'There was a master of the posts at the Ford when the Road failed. Ambery. He did not shut the house. He said a post that is shut is a letter unsent. He turned the last stage into a petition, and the city's word into a letter, and the year's book into a rider, of its own leave, because a rider who has not consented is not a rider but a theft. I carry the pouch the last mile. The rite was the relay. They forgot that, and began to burn things.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, post_known). Assert knows(actor, kindling_is_rite). }
  }
  Discovery post_known "The Colophon is a relay. Ambery was the last Master of the Posts at the Ford, and when the Road failed he kept the last stage as a petition: one book a year, of its own leave, to carry the city's word the last mile to the twelfth stage, where it is delivered. The Kindling was the relay before it was a fire. The Undelivered has carried no pouch since the rite became a burning.".
  Topic runner_twelfth with runner "Ask the Undelivered where the twelfth stage is" when runnerEased(runner) and knows(actor, post_known) once {
    Says "'You have been there,' says the courier, or a little less than that: 'You are going. The twelfth is where it is delivered. It was never cut, because it was never to be a place; a place is a thing you can besiege. It is the Chamber of the Parliament of the Bound, on the Roll, where the year's word was read.' It touches the blank on the board with one glove. 'The Master left a die. It is in the third pigeon-hole from the end. Whoever brings the year's book carries it, to be received.' A pause. 'Whoever it is.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, die_known). }
  }
  Discovery die_known "The die of the post-house is in the third pigeon-hole from the end. Whoever brings the year's book to the twelfth stage presses it in wax, and is received.".
  Item post_die "the die of the post-house" is post_stamp at post_house hidden until die_known.
  Observe post_eased at post_house when runnerEased(runner) "The courier stands by its peg with its hands at its sides. It has stopped saying anything. The room is, in a way you cannot explain, warmer.".

  // ── The choice ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The courier carries what is given it, of its own leave. The company's own almanack is a book that has just learned it
  // may consent. To post it is to lose it, and to give the Parliament a voice; to keep it is to keep a friend.
  Relation almanackPosted(group).
  Topic almanack_post_ask with almanack "Ask the Almanack whether it would go to the Parliament by the Post, of its own leave" when knows(actor, post_known) and carriesAlmanack(actor) and not almanackPosted(almanack) once {
    Says "The almanack in your pocket is quiet for so long that you take it out and look. 'By post,' it says at last. 'To a Parliament. As a book, with a stamp on, in a pouch, to be delivered.' A rustle that is almost a laugh. 'I have been on three thousand nails, you know, and I have never been delivered anywhere. I have only ever been where I was hung.' It sags a little. 'I would be on the nails still. I'm every copy; I can't help that. This one would be in the Chamber, with the Roll, and the Housebook, and the others. And I would be a copy that had been somewhere.' It folds a corner down. 'It is a great deal to ask of a penny. I should like to be asked properly. But I would go.'".
  }
  Action post_the_almanack(actor: group, site: place) "Give the Undelivered your almanack to carry to the Parliament, of its own leave" {
    Description "It asked to be asked properly. The courier will not take it otherwise.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, post_house) and runnerEased(runner) and knows(actor, post_known) and carriesAlmanack(actor) and not almanackPosted(almanack).
    Time 2.
    On success { Spend almanack_copy from actor. Assert almanackPosted(almanack). }
    Result "You hold it out in both hands, and say what you are doing, and why, and that it may say no. 'Yes,' says the Almanack, quite clearly, and then, very fast, before the courier has taken it: 'High water at the Ford, a quarter to seven. Fair, with showers toward evening, and a courier bringing news. I put that in at Candlemas, for somebody. It might as well be you.' The courier takes it in a grey glove and seals it, with the thumb, into the front of the satchel. 'Received,' it says. 'To be delivered.' The weight is gone from your pocket, and the pocket is a little colder, and on the nails of the Hithe, you are quite sure, three thousand almanacks go on reading the tides.".
  }
  Topic roll_posted with roll "Tell the Great Roll that a book has come to the twelfth stage by post, of its own leave" when heardStance(roll) and almanackPosted(almanack) and not favours(roll, sew_leave) once {
    Says "The floor is silent for a long time. Then, from the front of the Chamber, from somewhere near the clerk's table, a small papery voice says, with great care: 'High water at the Chamber, a quarter past never. Fair.' The Roll makes a sound like a whole library clearing its throat. 'RECEIVED,' it says. It is not a magisterial voice. 'I have heard the Colophon read as a decree, and as a petition, and I had not thought to hear it read as a letter.' The floor trembles. 'A book that has come by the old Road, of its own leave, to be delivered: that is the first word of the Colophon, and I have not had it said to my face in nine hundred years. The chair could accept the Sleep by leave.'".
    On discuss { Assert favours(roll, sew_leave). }
  }
  Topic roll_post with roll "Lay before the Great Roll the die of the post-house: the Road was a licensed passage with a keeper and a ledger" when heardStance(roll) and holding(actor, post_stamp) and not favours(roll, door_licensed) once {
    Says "You set the die on the floor, and the floor, which is the Roll, reads it with its capitals, which takes a long time. 'Eleven stages,' it says. 'A twelfth unfilled. A keeper at each, and a ledger at each, and a stamp that says RECEIVED.' The red letters round your feet go still. 'That is a Plea. That is the Fourth. It was written before I was, on a stone I have never been shown.' A rumble, almost a laugh. 'A door with a keeper and a ledger and a mark that says it was passed. The chair could accept the Door under licence.'".
    On discuss { Assert favours(roll, door_licensed). }
  }

  // ── The disagreement about a name, and the first word of Crake's ledger ───────────────────────────────────────
  Topic crake_road with crake "Ask Absalom Crake what empire the courier script belongs to" when knows(actor, drowned_ridge) once {
    Says "'Ys,' says Crake at once, and lights up. 'The Ysian Road. It's in the Cyclopaedia, in the back stacks, under YS, PHILOSOPHY OF, though that's the philosophy; the road is a footnote. A people who held the past to be written after the present, as a commentary is written after a text. A people like that don't hold roads; they hold the idea that a road has been walked.' He eats an almond. 'I've never been quite sure it was the same people. But my dear, one has to call it something.' His eyes are bright and a little sad. 'Quarles will tell you I'm wrong. Quarles is always right, and I have never once enjoyed it.'".
  }
  Topic quarles_road with quarles "Ask Ottoline Quarles what empire the courier script belongs to" when knows(actor, drowned_ridge) once {
    Says "'Not Ys,' says Ottoline Quarles, without looking up. 'Crake's Ys is a philosophy. The Road ran a thing it called the Post; no more than that; it did not have a name for itself, because the people who ran it were the ones who did the carrying, and the people who named it were the ones who took it afterwards, and left nothing but the law.' She turns a page. 'I do not know what it was called. I know what it did. It carried a thing, and it was received, and it went on. If you need a name, call it the Receiving.'".
  }

  // ── After: the hook and the first letter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Query postKept() means runnerEased(runner) and knows(party, post_known).
  Observe after_hook at ferry_stairs when after() and postKept() "The hook on the third pile is bare. Jonah Pellow has taken the felted letters down in an armful, one afternoon, and read them aloud on the steps to whoever would listen, and delivered those he could. On the board over his boat, under NIGHTS ALSO, in chalk: LETTERS TAKEN.".
  Observe after_posted at taproom when after() and almanackPosted(almanack) "On the nail by the chimney the almanack goes on reading the tides, and now and then, at the end of a sentence, adds a small thing it did not used to say: 'Received.' Moll Garrow has stopped telling it to hush.".
}

data/adventures/parliament-of-books/pres:
Module calamy "A Parliament of Books" {
  Description "Newmarket and Doble's Press: the Pleas for Every Hearth, the apprentice who can Sew, paper from the mills, and the night the Awls come.".

  Observe newmarket_scene at newmarket when true "Outside the wall the town is new and loud: a broad street of printers' shops with their windows full of ballads and proclamations and almanacks pegged on strings, ink-boys running with bundles, a smell of hot metal and size. At the end of it a cart arch opens into a yard stacked with paper bales, and over the arch, in letters a foot high: DOBLE. PRINTER TO THE CITY.".
  Observe yard_scene_p at press_yard when not dark() "Doble's yard: bales of paper under tarpaulins, carts, a pump, apprentices in paper hats. From the long shed at the end comes a heavy rhythmic thump and creak, like a ship in a swell: the presses.".
  Observe yard_dark_p at press_yard when dark() "Doble's yard at night: the bales humped under their tarpaulins, one lamp on a post, and the press shed shut and black.".
  Observe pressroom_scene at press_room when true "Two great wooden presses, black with ink, as tall as a man and twice as heavy, with men at the bars pulling and the platens coming down with a thump that you feel in your teeth. Sheets hang drying on lines overhead like washing, hundreds of them. On a stone table at the side a great iron frame of set type lies locked up, gleaming, waiting: the forme. A card on it, chalked: PLEAS. SHEET A.".
  Person doble "Ambrose Doble" at doble_office {
    Role "printer". Ancestry human. Background merchant. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A tall man in a good coat with ink on the cuffs comes round a desk heaped with proofs and shakes your hand before you can stop him. 'Ambrose Doble. Printer to the City. You have the look of someone who reads. Excellent. We need more of you. Sit, sit.'".
  }
  Observe office_scene at doble_office when true "A counting-room heaped with proofs, with a window onto the press room so that Doble can watch the presses while he does his sums. On the wall a framed sheet, the first thing his father ever printed in Calamy: a single line, very black, A BOOK FOR EVERY HEARTH.".
  Discovery pleas_project "Ambrose Doble is about to print the Pleas for Every Hearth: the city's law, the Great Roll of Pleas that is kept chained in the Court, in a cheap edition of two thousand copies, so that every household in Calamy may own its own law. He has modernized the spelling, and left out the Ninth Plea, which nobody understands.".
  Topic doble_pleas with doble "Ask Ambrose Doble what he is printing" when true once {
    Says "'The Pleas,' says Doble, and his whole face changes. 'The Great Roll of Pleas, the law of Calamy, that has sat chained in the Court for nine hundred years where nobody can read it but the Recorder and the lawyers who charge you to. Two thousand copies. A penny each. Every hearth in the city its own law.' He takes a proof from the desk. 'Modern spelling, so a carter can read it. And I've left out the Ninth, which is all about the Lyceum reading books to keep them from fading, and nobody's understood it in three hundred years. Saves a page.' He beams. 'The paper comes in from the mills on the fourth day and we print on the fifth. Then let the lawyers weep.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, pleas_project). }
  }
  Topic doble_almanacks with doble "Ask Ambrose Doble why his almanacks talk" when true once {
    Says "Doble laughs, and then stops, because you did not. 'Oh, come. A fault in the paste. Damp in the boards, and the paper moving as it dries, and people hearing what they expect.' He waves at the drying lines. 'Or the Binders. Mott would put a reed in every one of my books and blow down it, if he could. Three thousand almanacks, and every kitchen in the city frightened of its own nail.' He straightens a proof that did not need it. 'I have had one say good morning to me. I said good morning back. I am not proud of it.'".
  }
  Topic doble_ninth with doble "Tell Ambrose Doble what the Ninth Plea was for" when knows(actor, pleas_project) and knows(actor, ninth_plea) and not ninthRestored(doble) once {
    Says "Doble listens with his head on one side. 'The Lyceum to read every book in the city once in a generation, or it fades,' he says slowly. 'I thought it was about mould.' He picks up the proof of sheet A and looks at it as if it might have changed. 'It's the law. It is the actual law. I was going to give every hearth in Calamy the law, and I cut a piece out of it because I didn't understand it.' He rubs his face and leaves ink on it. 'That's what they did to us. The Imprimatur. For three hundred years. Cut what they didn't understand.' He calls through the window: 'Hob! Unlock the forme. We're resetting sheet A.'".
    On discuss { Assert ninthRestored(doble). }
  }
  Relation ninthRestored(group).

  // Kit Ferrier, the Binders' runaway, who can Sew.
  Person kit "Kit Ferrier" at press_room {
    Role "a printer's man who was a binder's apprentice". Ancestry human. Background artisan. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A lanky boy with a binder's calluses and a printer's black fingers grins at you from the end of the second press. 'Mind the bar. It'll break your arm and say sorry after.'".
  }
  Topic kit_why with kit "Ask Kit Ferrier why he left the Binders" when true once {
    Says "'A wage,' says Kit, as if it were obvious. 'Six coin a week here, and my own room. Nothing there for three more years but Warden Mott shouting and my keep.' He looks at his hands. 'I miss it, mind. The Sewing. You do it right and the book goes quiet under your fingers, like a cat settling. There's nothing like it.' He jerks his chin at the presses. 'These don't go quiet. These go thump.'".
  }
  Topic kit_terms with kit "Ask Kit Ferrier what would bring him back to Needle Street" when knows(actor, kit_fled) and not toldKitTerms(actor) once {
    Says "Kit thinks about it, which is to his credit. 'A journeyman's wage. And my ticket now, not in three years. I'm good enough. He knows I'm good enough.' He grins. 'And I'd keep coming here, Saturdays. I like the presses. I like seeing a thing come out two thousand times.' He goes back to the bar. 'He'll never.'".
    On discuss { Assert toldKitTerms(actor). }
  }
  Topic kit_home with kit "Tell Kit Ferrier the Warden says yes: his ticket now, and a journeyman's wage" when kitTicket(kit) and not kitHome(kit) once {
    Says "Kit lets go of the bar, which nearly breaks his arm, and does not notice. 'He said that? Mott?' He laughs out loud. 'His ticket now. Three years early.' He wipes his hands on his apron and then looks round the press room, at the presses and the lines and Doble at the window. 'I'll go. I'll go today.' He hesitates. 'If Mr. Doble wants the Pleas Sewn, I'd come back and Sew them. Under the Company's mark. Tell him that. Tell the Warden too.'".
    On discuss { Assert kitHome(kit). Retract kitAtDoble(kit). Assert at(kit, hall_floor). Assert kitOffersSewing(kit). }
  }
  Relation kitOffersSewing(group).
  Topic doble_sew with doble "Put it to Ambrose Doble that the Pleas be Sewn before they go out" when knows(actor, pleas_project) and (kitAtDoble(kit) or kitOffersSewing(kit)) and not kitSewsPrint(kit) and not pleasPrinted(doble) once {
    Says "'Sewn?' says Doble. 'Two thousand copies? It would cost a fortnight and treble the price.' He walks up and down. 'Kit could do it. Kit and the girls from Needle Street, if Mott would let them. Sewn books last, I'll give the Binders that.' He stops. 'And they'd stop talking? That's what you're telling me. My law-books would go quiet on the shelf like decent law.' He looks out at the presses. 'I don't believe a word of it. But if the Ordinance passes I shall have to, and if it doesn't I'd as soon not have two thousand copies of the law arguing with their owners.' He sits. 'Ask Kit if he'll do it. If he will, so will I.'".
    On discuss { Assert dobleWillSew(doble). }
  }
  Relation dobleWillSew(group).
  Rule kit_agrees when dobleWillSew(doble) and (kitAtDoble(kit) or kitOffersSewing(kit)) and not kitSewsPrint(kit) { Assert kitSewsPrint(kit). }
  Observe sewing_at_doble at press_room when kitSewsPrint(kit) and not pleasPrinted(doble) "At the end of the press room Kit Ferrier has set up two sewing frames, and three girls from Needle Street are at them with curved needles, and the Pleas are going through them gathering by gathering, and Kit is saying something under his breath with every pull.".

  // The paper, the printing, and the waking of the law.
  Relation paperIn(group). Relation pleasPrinted(group). Relation pleasAbroad(group). Relation pleasAwake(group). Relation pleasSeized(group).
  Rule paper_from_mills when day(clock) == 4 and hour(clock) == 12 and millsRun(millrace) and not paperIn(doble)
    says "A string of carts comes over the bridge from the Hithe loaded with white paper from the tide-mills, and goes along the river wall toward Newmarket." { Assert paperIn(doble). }
  Rule paper_from_ostrey when day(clock) == 6 and hour(clock) == 12 and not paperIn(doble) { Assert paperIn(doble). }
  Observe paper_short at press_room when not paperIn(doble) and day(clock) >= 4 "The lines are empty and the presses are idle; the pressmen sit on bales playing cards. The mills have not sent the paper.".
  Rule pleas_print when paperIn(doble) and hour(clock) == 18 and not pleasPrinted(doble) and not pressBroken(doble) and day(clock) >= 5
    says "From Newmarket, all evening, the thump of Doble's presses, going without a pause." { Assert pleasPrinted(doble). }
  Rule pleas_seized when pleasPrinted(doble) and ordinancePassed(guildhall) and not kitSewsPrint(kit) and not pleasSeized(doble) and hour(clock) == 7
    says "Word goes round before breakfast: the Imprimatur's men are in Doble's yard with the Ordinance in one hand and a cart in the other, taking the Pleas away unsewn, all two thousand." { Assert pleasSeized(doble). }
  Rule pleas_abroad when pleasPrinted(doble) and not pleasSeized(doble) and hour(clock) == 9 and not pleasAbroad(doble)
    says "Ink-boys are crying the Pleas in every street: the law of Calamy, a penny, the law for every hearth!" { Assert pleasAbroad(doble). Set pleasOutAt(doble) to watch(clock). }
  Measure pleasOutAt(group).
  Rule pleas_wake when pleasAbroad(doble) and not kitSewsPrint(kit) and not pleasAwake(doble) and watch(clock) >= pleasOutAt(doble) + 72 and hour(clock) >= 8
    says "Something has happened in the night all over Calamy. In kitchen after kitchen, on shelves and tables, the penny Pleas have woken, two thousand of them, one voice, and every one of them is reading aloud to its household, in the old spelling it was not printed in, the law." { Assert pleasAwake(doble). }
  Observe pleas_awake_close at pleas_steps when pleasAwake(doble) "A crowd on the Court steps, every second person with a penny Pleas in their hand, and every penny Pleas speaking. WHEREAS, says the crowd's hands, in one voice, WHEREAS. A carter is shouting that his says he owes a toll his father paid. A woman is trying to make hers stop by sitting on it.".
  Observe pleas_awake_hithe at quay when pleasAwake(doble) "Half the Hithe has bought a penny Pleas and the other half wishes it had not. Out of a window over the quay the law is reading itself aloud: the Fourth Plea, of tolls and moorings, in the voice of an old man who has not been read in a long time and does not mean to stop.".
  Observe pleas_awake_court at court_hall when pleasAwake(doble) "The Court of Pleas is full of Pleas: two thousand penny copies brought in by householders, piled on the benches, all of them talking at once, and Recorder Haddon in the middle of it with his hands over his ears.".
  Observe pleas_sewn_note at press_room when pleasPrinted(doble) and kitSewsPrint(kit) "The Pleas lie in Sewn stacks along the press room, two thousand of them, quiet, smelling of new thread.".
  Observe press_broken_note at press_room when pressBroken(doble) "The great press stands with its bar sheared off and its platen cracked through. Type lies in the sweepings. The forme of the Pleas has been broken up with a mallet; Doble's men are picking the letters out of the floor one by one.".

  // The Awls: the Binders' lads, on the night between the fourth day and the fifth.
  // A temperament given a person overrides its keeping the peace, so the Awls warn and come by rules of their own: by
  // day they are Binders' lads at their benches, and only on the fourth night are they anything else.
  Person awls "the Awls" at hall_floor {
    Role "Binders' lads with awls and mallets". Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Level 1. Numbers 3. Peaceable.
    Seen when not peaceable(awls).
  }
  Relation awlsWarned(group). Measure awlsPatience(group).
  Rule awls_warn at press_yard when at(awls, press_yard) and not peaceable(awls) and at(party, press_yard) and not awlsWarned(awls) and not awlsStopped(saul)
    says "In the dark of the yard shapes come over the wall, three of them, then Saul Vetch: Binders' lads in leather aprons with mallets and awls. 'Out of the way,' says Saul. 'We've no quarrel with you. It's the machine.'" {
    Assert awlsWarned(awls). Set awlsPatience(awls) to watch(clock) + 1. }
  Rule awls_come at press_yard when awlsWarned(awls) and at(awls, press_yard) and at(party, press_yard) and not peaceable(awls) and not awlsStopped(saul)
    and watch(clock) >= awlsPatience(awls) and not assails(awls, party) says "The Awls come at you with their mallets." {
    Assert assails(awls, party). }
  // Doble's apprentices sleep over the press shed. Shouted for, they come down with staves and a lamp, and Saul, who
  // came to break a machine and not heads, counts them and calls his lads off (Mission 17's M17-45: three to one in
  // the dark had nearly always gone against the one, warrior or not).
  Action rouse_yard(actor: group, site: place) "Shout for Doble's apprentices over the press shed" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(awls, site) and at(actor, press_yard) and awlsWarned(awls) and not peaceable(awls) and not awlsStopped(saul).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert awlsStopped(saul). Assert pressGuarded(doble). Assert at(awls, hall_floor). Assert peaceable(awls). Retract assails(awls, actor). }
    Result "You shout. A shutter bangs open over the press shed, a lamp comes out, and then the apprentices come down the outside stair in their shirts with staves and a pressman's bar, seven of them, swearing. Saul Vetch counts them. 'Not tonight, lads,' he says. They go back over the wall the way they came, and one of them, from the top of it, throws his mallet into the pump trough, which is the only thing broken in Doble's yard that night.".
  }
  Action stand_aside(actor: group, site: place) "Stand aside and let the Awls at the press" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(awls, site) and awlsWarned(awls) and not peaceable(awls) and not awlsStopped(saul).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert pressBroken(doble). Assert awlsStopped(saul). Assert at(awls, hall_floor). Assert peaceable(awls). Retract assails(awls, actor). }
    Result "You stand aside. It takes them a quarter of an hour, with mallets and a crowbar, and the sound is like a ship breaking up on rocks. Saul Vetch does not look at you as they go back over the wall.".
  }
  Rule awls_out when awlsPlanned(saul) and not awlsStopped(saul) and day(clock) == 5 and hour(clock) == 1 and not awlsGone(awls) {
    Assert at(awls, press_yard). Retract peaceable(awls). Assert awlsGone(awls). Set awlsAt(awls) to watch(clock). }
  Relation awlsGone(group). Measure awlsAt(group).
  Rule awls_guarded when at(awls, press_yard) and pressGuarded(doble) and not at(party, press_yard) and not awlsStopped(saul)
    says "There is a noise in the night from Newmarket: shouts, a dog, a whistle. In the morning everyone knows that the Binders' lads came over Doble's wall and found Doble's men waiting for them." {
    Assert awlsStopped(saul). Assert at(awls, hall_floor). Assert peaceable(awls). }
  Rule awls_break when at(awls, press_yard) and not pressGuarded(doble) and not at(party, press_yard) and watch(clock) >= awlsAt(awls) + 3 and not awlsStopped(saul)
    says "In the small hours there is a noise from Newmarket like a ship breaking up on rocks. By morning everyone in the city knows: the Awls broke Doble's press." {
    Assert pressBroken(doble). Assert at(awls, hall_floor). Assert peaceable(awls). Assert awlsStopped(saul). }
  Rule awls_routed when at(awls, press_yard) and (routed(awls) or dead(awls)) and not awlsStopped(saul) { Assert awlsStopped(saul). }
  Rule awls_home when awlsStopped(saul) and at(awls, press_yard) and not threatened(party) and hour(clock) >= 4 and hour(clock) < 6 { Assert at(awls, hall_floor). Assert peaceable(awls). }
  Topic doble_warn with doble "Warn Ambrose Doble that the Binders' lads mean to break his press on the fourth night" when knows(actor, awls_plan) and not awlsStopped(saul) and not pressGuarded(doble) once {
    Says "Doble stops smiling. 'Mott's lads?' He looks through the window at his presses. 'No. Not Mott. Mott would sooner cut off his hand.' He thinks. 'Vetch. That journeyman of his with the face.' He calls through the window: 'Hob! I want six men in the yard tomorrow night, with lanterns and the dogs, and a jug for them, and nobody to touch a Binder unless a Binder touches the press.' He turns back to you and shakes your hand again, harder. 'I owe you a press.'".
    On discuss { Assert pressGuarded(doble). }
  }
}

data/adventures/parliament-of-books/slui:
Module calamy "A Parliament of Books" {
  Description "The night sluice: two tide-mills, one millrace, a gate shut at night, an eel-catcher, and a wedding that wants forty eels.".

  Observe race_scene at millrace when not dark() "Two mills face each other across a stone race where the river comes in on the flood and goes out on the ebb, and their wheels turn with it. The old mill is timber, black with age, with BRANNOCK painted on it; the new one is brick, with TEAGUE & DAU. painted bigger. Between them at the race's mouth a wooden sluice gate on a winch can shut the race off from the river altogether. Both millers are standing in their doorways not looking at each other.".
  Observe race_dark at millrace when dark() "The millrace at night: black water going nowhere, the two mills dark on either side, and a smell of pipe-tobacco that belongs to neither.".
  Observe brannock_scene at brannock_floor when true "A mill floor all dust and thunder: the great stones going round, rag-pulp in the vats, the whole building shaking with the wheel. Sheets of wet paper hang on felts on the racks, and the light comes through them yellow.".
  Observe teague_scene at teague_floor when true "A brick mill floor with new iron gears painted green, very clean, and vats in a row, and a wall of finished paper in reams wrapped and stacked and marked DOBLE.".
  Person brannock "Old Brannock" at brannock_floor {
    Role "miller of the old mill". Ancestry human. Background miller. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A white-floured old man with forearms like hams looks at you over a vat. 'If she sent you, tell her I said she knows what she did.'".
  }
  Person teague "the Widow Teague" at teague_floor {
    Role "miller of the new mill". Ancestry human. Background miller. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A sharp woman in a clean apron with a pencil behind her ear looks up from a ledger. 'If he sent you, he can come and say it himself, if he can find the door of a building younger than he is.'".
  }
  Discovery sluice_quarrel "Somebody shuts the sluice gate at the head of the millrace in the small hours, so that neither tide-mill can grind on the night ebb; Brannock blames the Widow Teague, and she blames him. The paper for Doble's Pleas is late because of it.".
  Topic brannock_quarrel with brannock "Ask Old Brannock what the Widow Teague has done" when true once {
    Says "'Shuts my water,' says Brannock. 'Three weeks. Every night, one or two in the morning, the sluice goes down and the race stands still and my wheel stops dead and so does hers, and she does it to spite me because I wouldn't sell her the old mill.' He bangs a vat. 'She'd rather lose a night's grinding herself than see me grind. That's the Teagues.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sluice_quarrel). Assert heardBrannock(actor). }
  }
  Topic teague_quarrel with teague "Ask the Widow Teague what Old Brannock has done" when true once {
    Says "'Shuts the sluice,' says the Widow Teague, without looking up from her ledger. 'Every night, the old fool. I've two hundred reams owed to Doble for the Pleas by the fourth day and I've lost the night ebb three weeks running, and he's lost it too, and he'd sooner lose it than let me keep it.' She underlines something hard. 'His father was the same.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sluice_quarrel). Assert heardTeague(actor). }
  }
  Relation heardBrannock(group). Relation heardTeague(group).
  Thing sluice "the sluice gate" at millrace {
    State up "The sluice gate is wound up on its winch, and the race runs free.".
    State down "The sluice gate is down. The race lies still and black, and both wheels stand.".
  }
  Discovery eel_traps "Under the sluice gate, on the race side, someone has staked a row of wicker eel-traps, each with a scrap of red rag tied to it. Every eel-catcher in the Hithe marks his traps; red rag is Coddy Fitch's.".
  Discovery traps_search "Under the sluice gate there is something staked in the mud." { Found by searching millrace "Down on the slimy stones under the sluice, on the race side where the water stands still when the gate is down, a row of wicker eel-traps is staked into the mud, five of them, each with a scrap of red rag tied to its neck.". }
  Rule traps_are_coddys when knows(party, traps_search) and not knows(party, eel_traps) says "Red rag. Moll Garrow said it: you want Coddy Fitch out on the flats. You have seen red rag on the eel-baskets at the end of the plank walk under the mills." teaches eel_traps { }

  // Coddy shuts the gate at one in the morning and opens it at three, for his traps, until his sister's wedding.
  Person coddy "Coddy Fitch" at coddy_hut {
    Role "eel-catcher". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Level 2. Background fisherman. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A wiry man in waders with a pipe in his teeth looks up from mending a wicker trap. 'Eels, is it? Eels is Thursday. Eels is every day, for you.'".
  }
  Observe hut_scene at coddy_hut when true "A hut of tarred planks on stilts over the mud, with eel-traps stacked against it, nets drying, a smoke-box, a dog, and a view of the whole flat grey estuary going out to the sea. Every trap has a scrap of red rag on it.".
  Person coddy_dog "Coddy's dog" at coddy_hut { Role "a black and white dog with one ear up". Species dog. }
  Relation sluiceSettled(entity). Relation coddyExposed(group). Relation coddyOwes(group). Relation weddingEels(group).
  Rule coddy_shuts when hour(clock) == 1 and not sluiceSettled(sluice) and not coddyExposed(coddy) and state(sluice, up) and not weddingDone(lamb) {
    Assert state(sluice, down). Assert at(coddy, millrace). }
  Rule coddy_opens when hour(clock) == 3 and state(sluice, down) and not sluiceSettled(sluice) {
    Assert state(sluice, up). Increase eelsCaught(coddy) by 10. }
  Rule coddy_home when hour(clock) >= 3 and hour(clock) < 12 and at(coddy, millrace) { Assert at(coddy, coddy_hut). }
  Measure eelsCaught(group).
  Observe coddy_caught at millrace when at(coddy, millrace) and dark() "In the dark at the head of the race a man in waders is leaning on the sluice winch, smoking a pipe, with a lantern hooded down to a slit at his feet. It is Coddy Fitch. When he sees you he takes the pipe out of his mouth and says, quite cheerfully, 'Ah.'" teaches coddy_seen.
  Discovery coddy_seen "It is Coddy Fitch, the eel-catcher, who shuts the millrace sluice in the small hours: two hours of still water under the gate, for his traps.".
  Topic coddy_why with coddy "Ask Coddy Fitch why he shuts the sluice at night" when knows(actor, coddy_seen) or knows(actor, eel_traps) once {
    Says "'Ah,' says Coddy, and grins, and then stops grinning. 'Well. Forty eels.' He puts the pipe back. 'My sister Peg's to be married at the Lamb on the third day, to Jem Lowe that drives for the mills, and I said I'd do the eel pie. Forty eels. And you can't get forty eels this time of year, not in running water. You want still water and a dark night.' He looks at the mills. 'Two hours. That's all. I didn't think they'd notice, the way they never look at each other.' He scratches his ear. 'They noticed.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, coddy_seen). }
  }
  Topic coddy_hour with coddy "Ask Coddy Fitch if one hour at slack water would do him, if the millers would give it" when knows(actor, coddy_seen) and not sluiceSettled(sluice) and not coddyExposed(coddy) once {
    Says "'An hour at the slack?' Coddy considers it like a man considering a horse. 'At the slack the race is near still anyway. An hour'd do. If they'd give it.' He laughs. 'They won't. They'd sooner both starve than give each other anything, and they'd sooner give me a beating than either.'".
    On discuss { Assert coddyWouldTake(coddy). }
  }
  Relation coddyWouldTake(group).
  Topic brannock_settle with brannock "Tell Old Brannock it was never the Widow Teague, and what Coddy Fitch asks" when coddyWouldTake(coddy) and heardTeague(actor) and not sluiceSettled(sluice) once {
    Says "Brannock hears it out with his arms folded. 'Coddy Fitch,' he says. 'For an eel pie.' Something happens under the flour, which may be a laugh. 'And she's been thinking it was me.' He unfolds his arms. 'Tell him he can have the slack, an hour, if she'll give it too. And tell her—' He stops. 'Tell her I said it wasn't me.' He turns back to his vat. 'She'll know what I mean.'".
    On discuss { Assert brannockAgrees(brannock). }
  }
  Topic teague_settle with teague "Tell the Widow Teague it was never Old Brannock, and what Coddy Fitch asks" when coddyWouldTake(coddy) and heardBrannock(actor) and not sluiceSettled(sluice) once {
    Says "The Widow Teague puts down her pencil. 'An eel pie,' she says. 'Three weeks of night grinding, for an eel pie.' She looks across the race at the old mill, for the first time since you came. 'He thought it was me?' She picks the pencil up. 'Coddy can have his hour. And tell the old fool—' She stops, and writes something in her ledger instead. 'Never mind. I'll tell him.'".
    On discuss { Assert teagueAgrees(teague). }
  }
  Relation brannockAgrees(group). Relation teagueAgrees(group).
  Rule sluice_settles when brannockAgrees(brannock) and teagueAgrees(teague) and not sluiceSettled(sluice)
    says "That evening there is a board nailed to the sluice winch, painted in two different hands: SLACK WATER, ONE HOUR, FITCH. And under it, in a third hand, a drawing of an eel." {
    Assert sluiceSettled(sluice). Assert coddyOwes(coddy). Assert weddingEels(coddy). Assert state(sluice, up). }
  Topic brannock_expose with brannock "Tell Old Brannock it is Coddy Fitch who shuts the sluice" when knows(actor, coddy_seen) and not sluiceSettled(sluice) and not coddyExposed(coddy) once {
    Says "'Fitch!' Brannock is out of the door and across the race before you can say anything else, and the Widow Teague is out of hers, and for a moment they are shoulder to shoulder at the sluice winch shouting down at the mud, which is the first time they have stood together in ten years. Then they go back to their mills. By evening the Water Bailiff has been to the hut on stilts, and Coddy's traps are on the bank, broken.".
    On discuss { Assert coddyExposed(coddy). Assert sluiceSettled(sluice). Assert state(sluice, up). }
  }
  Query millsRun(p: place) means sluiceSettled(sluice) or ebbHeld(p).
  Relation ebbHeld(place).
  Observe mills_settled at millrace when sluiceSettled(sluice) and not coddyExposed(coddy) and not dark() "Both wheels are turning. The Widow Teague is standing in her doorway, and Old Brannock in his, and they are not quite looking at each other in a different way from before.".
  Observe mills_exposed at millrace when coddyExposed(coddy) and not dark() "Both wheels are turning. Down on the bank below the sluice lie five eel-traps, broken, with red rag on them.".

  // The eel-pie wedding at the Lamb, the third evening.
  Relation weddingDone(place).
  Person wedding "the wedding party" at nowhere_wedding {
    Role "Peg Fitch and Jem Lowe, married this morning, and everyone they know". Ancestry human. Numbers 30. Peaceable.
    Seen when day(clock) == 3 or at(wedding, taproom).
  }
  Place nowhere_wedding "the church porch of the Lamp" is room within close at 3, 0 outdoors.
  Passage porch_way "the side porch" is doorway between nave and nowhere_wedding.
  Rule wedding_comes when day(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) == 17 and not weddingDone(lamb) { Assert at(wedding, taproom). Assert weddingDone(lamb). }
  Rule wedding_ends when day(clock) == 4 and hour(clock) == 1 and at(wedding, taproom) { Assert at(wedding, nowhere_wedding). }
  Observe wedding_pie at taproom when at(wedding, taproom) and (weddingEels(coddy) or eelsCaught(coddy) >= 40) "The Lamb is full to the rafters with the Fitch wedding: Peg Fitch in a crown of paper roses and Jem Lowe in a borrowed coat, millhands, eel-men, fishwives, a fiddler on a barrel, and down the middle of the long table a pie the size of a cartwheel, steaming, with forty eel-heads looking out of the crust in a ring. Coddy is carving. Moll is weeping into her apron for joy. Somebody has hung paper flowers on the almanack's nail, and the almanack, when it thinks nobody is listening, is humming along with the fiddle.".
  Observe wedding_poor at taproom when at(wedding, taproom) and not weddingEels(coddy) and eelsCaught(coddy) < 40 "The Lamb is full of the Fitch wedding, Peg in paper roses and Jem in a borrowed coat and a fiddler on a barrel; but down the long table there is bread and cheese and a ham, and no pie, and Coddy Fitch is not at the table at all. Moll Garrow keeps saying it's a lovely ham.".
  Rule wedding_feeds when at(wedding, taproom) and at(party, taproom) and (weddingEels(coddy) or eelsCaught(coddy) >= 40) and not fedAtWedding(party)
    says "Coddy Fitch sees you and waves his knife. 'Here! Sit down! You're the one!' and a plate of eel pie arrives in front of you whether you want it or not, and a mug, and a millhand's elbow." {
    Assert fedAtWedding(party). Increase quantity(party, rations) by 1. }
  Relation fedAtWedding(group).

  // With the sluice settled, Coddy will take you out on the flats by the dry way, at any ebb.
  Topic coddy_guide with coddy "Ask Coddy Fitch to take you out to the reed-beds" when coddyOwes(coddy) and not following(coddy, actor) once {
    Says "'Out to the reeds?' Coddy knocks out his pipe on a stilt. 'For you, any tide. There's a dry way through to the heart of them if you know where the old stones are.' He whistles to the dog. 'Come on, then. Mind where I put my feet and put yours there.'".
    On discuss { Assert acceptsEscort(coddy, actor). }
  }
  Topic coddy_join with coddy "Ask Coddy Fitch to come with you, wherever you are going" when coddyOwes(coddy) and not travelsWith(coddy, actor) once {
    Says "Coddy looks at you sideways for a while, sucking his pipe. 'Wherever?' he says. 'You've a look about you of somebody going somewhere there's no eels.' He knocks the pipe out. 'Peg's married. The traps can mind themselves. I owe you.' He takes a gaff off the wall. 'I'm no fighter, mind. I'm a finder. I can find my way round most things that bite.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(coddy, actor). Set hire(coddy) to 0. }
  }
  Topic coddy_old with coddy "Ask Coddy Fitch about the old stones in the reeds" when coddyOwes(coddy) and been(actor, reed_heart) once {
    Says "'The Drowned Town,' says Coddy. 'My granddad saw it the year of the Great Ebb, when the sea went out of the whole estuary for a day and a night and everybody walked out on the mud. Roofs. Streets. Stone ones, out past the reeds, all the way to where the sea came back.' He lights his pipe. 'Older than Calamy. Older than the road. Granddad said the roofs had writing on them and nobody could read it, and then the sea came back and nobody's seen them since but the ridge in the reeds there.' He puffs. 'Eels like it. That's all I care.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/parliament-of-books/stit:
Module calamy "A Parliament of Books" {
  Description "Stitchgate: the old craft quarter inside the wall; the Binders' Hall, the ink shop, the shut school, the scriveners, and Gutter Lane.".

  Observe gate_scene at old_gate when true "The river stair comes up from the bridge to an old gate in the city wall, so old its arch has sunk and a tall man must stoop. Through it, lanes too narrow for a cart, and the smell of oak-gall and wet hide and glue. To one side of the gate a crooked lane goes off downhill along the wall, darker than it has any business to be by day.".
  Observe needle_scene at needle_street when true "Needle Street: binders' shops with their doors open and their frames inside, the women sewing in the doorways for the light. Halfway along stands a hall of old brick with a great iron needle, longer than a man, hung over its door on chains. A lane goes off west, stained blue-black along the gutter, and a street climbs north toward the sound of many pens.".
  Observe ink_scene at ink_lane when true "Inkhorn Lane is blue-black. The gutter runs blue-black, the doorsteps are blue-black, and so are the hands of everyone in it. A shop with jars in the window, gall-nuts and lampblack and vitriol; and opposite it a little house with a shut door, and a board over the door with letters painted for children to read: A B C, D E F, and THE SCHOOL.".
  Observe scriveners_scene at scriveners when true "Copyists' Row is a long arcade of wooden booths against the wall, each with a desk, a stool, a scribe, and a queue of people wanting letters written, wills copied, love made legible. The scratching is like rain. At the top of the row an old gate leads through into the Close.".

  // ── The Binders' Hall. ──
  Observe hall_scene at hall_floor when true "A great room, beamed, with long tables down it and at every table a binder with a book in a press: boards, thread, paste-pots, bone folders. On the end wall hangs a painted board of the Worshipful Company of Binders, a needle crossed with a book. Through an inner door you can see frames standing in rows, and hear someone singing under their breath." teaches binders_named.
  Person mott "Warden Hesketh Mott" at hall_floor {
    Role "Warden of the Worshipful Company of Binders". Ancestry human. Background artisan. Peaceable. Manner proud. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A stout man in a leather apron with a silver needle pinned to it gets up from the end of the long table. 'Hesketh Mott, Warden. If you have a book that wants binding, you've come to the right street. If you have a book that wants talking to, you've come to the wrong one, and I'll thank you to take it to Newmarket where it was made.'".
  }
  Person annet "Annet Pellow" at hall_floor {
    Role "an apprentice binder". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner compassionate. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A girl of fourteen at the far end of a table, with her tongue between her teeth and a needle in her fingers, looks up quickly, then down again at her work.".
  }
  Person saul "Saul Vetch" at hall_floor {
    Role "a journeyman binder". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Background artisan. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A broad young man with a paring-knife and a scowl looks you over. 'Warden's busy.'".
  }
  Discovery sewing_secret "The Binders sew every book in Calamy the same way, with a stitch they call the Sewing, and they say the same words with every turn of the thread. Warden Mott calls it a craft blessing. His father told him a book that is not Sewn will not keep quiet.".
  Topic mott_sewing with mott "Ask Warden Mott what is wrong with the printers' books" when true once {
    Says "'They're not Sewn,' says Mott, as if that settled it. 'Glued at the back and stabbed through with a wire, like a bundle of firewood. A book wants Sewing. Every book Calamy ever made, till Doble's father, went through a frame in this street, and every one had the Sewing put in it, the same stitch, the same words.' He touches the needle on his apron. 'My father said to me, a book that isn't Sewn won't keep quiet. I thought he meant it'd fall apart. Well.' He looks out at Needle Street. 'Now they're talking in every kitchen in Calamy, the printers' books, and nothing of ours has said a word in nine hundred years.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sewing_secret). }
  }
  Topic mott_words with mott "Ask Warden Mott what the words of the Sewing are" when knows(actor, sewing_secret) once {
    Says "Mott's face closes like a book. 'That's the Company's,' he says. 'Every apprentice learns them their first day and swears not to say them outside the hall.' He hesitates. 'They're cut in the beam in the sewing room, if you've eyes. I won't stop you looking. I'll not say them.'".
  }
  Topic mott_ordinance with mott "Ask Warden Mott about the Sewing Ordinance" when true once {
    Says "'The fifth day from now, at noon, the aldermen vote on it,' says Mott, and squares his shoulders. 'Every book made or sold in Calamy to be Sewn, by a Sewer of the Company, under the Company's mark. Every printer's book. Every one of those penny almanacks, brought in and Sewn, and then you'll see how quiet they go.' He means it as a promise. 'Doble calls it a guild grab. It is a guild grab. It's also right.'".
  }
  Discovery kit_fled "Kit Ferrier, the Binders' best apprentice, ran off from the Hall at Lady Day to work for Doble the printer for a journeyman's wage, and took the Sewing with him in his hands.".
  Initially Assert leadsTo(kit_fled, press_room).
  Topic mott_kit with mott "Ask Warden Mott why he eats his dinner standing up" when true once {
    Says "Mott glares; then sags. 'You've been talking to almanacks.' He sits down heavily on the bench. 'My best apprentice. Kit Ferrier. Three years from his journeyman's ticket, the best hands I've had in twenty years, and he went over the wall at Lady Day to Doble's, for a wage. A wage! He was learning the Sewing.' He bangs the table, softly. 'He'll teach those printers to Sew, and they'll Sew without the words, or without the Company, and that'll be the end of us both.' He looks up. 'You could bring him back. I'd make it worth it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, kit_fled). Assert wantsKit(mott). }
  }
  Relation wantsKit(group). Relation kitHome(group). Relation kitAtDoble(group). Relation kitSewsPrint(group). Relation kitTicket(group).
  Initially Assert kitAtDoble(kit).
  Topic mott_wage with mott "Tell Warden Mott that Kit would come back for a journeyman's wage and his ticket now" when toldKitTerms(actor) and not kitTicket(kit) once {
    Says "Mott opens his mouth to shout, and does not. He sits for a long time looking at the board of the Worshipful Company, the needle and the book. 'His ticket now,' he says. 'Three years early.' He takes a breath. 'He's good enough. That's the worst of it. He's been good enough since he was fifteen.' He gets up. 'Tell him yes. Tell him the Warden says so, and he can come and get his ticket off the wall himself, and if he so much as glues a spine in this hall I'll have it back.'".
    On discuss { Assert kitTicket(kit). }
  }
  Relation toldKitTerms(group).

  // The sewing room, and the words on the beam.
  Observe sewing_scene at sewing_room when true "Frames in rows, each with a book's gatherings strung on cords, and at each frame a binder bent over with a curved needle. They sing, or nearly: the same short phrase under the breath with every pass of the thread, over and over, so low you cannot make out the words. Over the frames runs a great black beam with letters cut in it, old letters, filled with gold that has mostly gone.".
  Discovery sewing_words "The words of the Sewing, cut in the beam over the Binders' frames in the oldest letters in Calamy: GO HOME AND COME WHEN YOU ARE CALLED. The binders say them with every stitch.".
  Thing sewing_beam "the black beam" at sewing_room {
    State carved "A beam with old letters cut in it, the gold mostly gone.".
  }
  Observe beam_close at sewing_room of sewing_beam as reading when tried(sewing_beam, looking) "You have to stand on a stool to read them, and the binders watch you do it without stopping their thread. GO HOME, the beam says, in letters older than any in the city, AND COME WHEN YOU ARE CALLED. Under your breath you find you are saying it in time with the needles." teaches sewing_words.
  Relation sewingTaught(group).
  Topic mott_teach with mott "Ask Warden Mott to teach you the Sewing" when knows(actor, sewing_words) and kitTicket(kit) and not sewingTaught(actor) once {
    Says "Mott looks at you a long time. 'For Kit's sake,' he says at last. 'And because I'd sooner someone outside the Company knew it than nobody did, the way things are going.' He takes you to a frame, and it takes an hour, and your fingers are no good, and then they are a little good. 'Over and through, and the words with the pull. Not before and not after. With.' He stands back. 'That's the Sewing. Don't sell it.'".
    On discuss { Assert sewingTaught(actor). }
  }

  // Saul Vetch and the Awls: Binders' lads who mean to break Doble's press the night the Pleas are set.
  Discovery awls_plan "Saul Vetch, the Binders' journeyman, means to take the Awls (the Binders' lads, with their awls and mallets) to Doble's yard on the night of the fourth day and break the press before the Pleas can be printed on it. Warden Mott does not know.".
  Relation awlsPlanned(group). Relation awlsStopped(group). Relation pressBroken(entity). Relation pressGuarded(entity).
  Initially Assert awlsPlanned(saul).
  Topic annet_trouble with annet "Ask Annet Pellow how the work goes" when true once {
    Says "'Good,' says Annet, too fast, and then, lower, with an eye on the scowling journeyman: 'The Warden shouts. He doesn't mean it. He's sad about Kit.' She pulls a thread tight. 'Saul's worse. Saul doesn't shout. He's been taking the lads out at night to Newmarket and coming back with his knuckles all skinned.' She bites the thread. 'Don't tell anybody I said.'".
  }
  Topic annet_father with annet "Tell Annet Pellow her father has his night licence back" when licensed(jonah) and not toldAnnet(annet) once {
    Says "Annet's face does something complicated and ends up crying, which she hides behind a book in a press. 'He sold his licence for my indentures,' she says, muffled. 'I know he did. He thinks I don't.' She wipes her nose on her wrist. 'Listen. Saul and the Awls are going to Doble's on the fourth night to break the press. The big one, the one with the Pleas on. I heard them. I didn't know who to tell.' She looks at you. 'Now I've told somebody.'".
    On discuss { Assert toldAnnet(annet). Assert knows(actor, awls_plan). }
  }
  Relation toldAnnet(group).
  Topic mott_awls with mott "Tell Warden Mott what Saul Vetch means to do to Doble's press" when knows(actor, awls_plan) and not awlsStopped(saul) once {
    Says "Mott goes a dark red from the collar up. He does not say anything to you at all. He walks down the long room to where Saul is paring a board, and takes the knife out of his hand, and says something in his ear so quietly that nobody hears it, and Saul goes white and sits down. When Mott comes back his hands are shaking. 'The Company does not break presses,' he says. 'Whatever else it does.' Then: 'Thank you. I'd have hanged for that, and never known.'".
    On discuss { Assert awlsStopped(saul). }
  }
  Topic saul_face with saul "Tell Saul Vetch you know about the fourth night" when knows(actor, awls_plan) and not awlsStopped(saul) once {
    Says "Saul puts down his knife. 'Do you,' he says. He looks at you, sizing you up the way he sizes up a board for paring. 'And what's that to you? It's a machine. It's Doble's machine, and it's killing this street, and I've a mother on Needle Street who sewed for forty years and can't get work.' He picks the knife up again. 'Go and tell the Warden, then. Or don't. Either way, mind yourself in Newmarket after dark.'".
  }
  Action face_down_saul(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Saul Vetch that if the Awls go to Newmarket, you will be there waiting" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(saul, site) and knows(actor, awls_plan) and not awlsStopped(saul) and not facedSaul(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert awlsStopped(saul). Assert facedSaul(actor). }
    On failure { Assert facedSaul(actor). }
    Result "Saul looks at you for a long time, and then looks away first. 'Not worth it,' he says, to the board. 'Not for Doble.' The lads at the next table find their work very interesting.".
    Otherwise "Saul laughs, not pleasantly. 'We'll see who's waiting,' he says, and goes back to his paring.".
  }
  Relation facedSaul(group).

  // ── Gallon's ink shop, and the poems in the attic. ──
  Observe gallon_scene at gallon_shop when true "A shop that is all jars: oak-galls in one, lampblack in another, green vitriol, gum arabic, cuttlefish, something red. On the counter a row of little stoppered bottles of ink, each with a hand-written label: SCRIVENERS' BEST. LAWYERS' BLACK (WILL NOT FADE). LOVERS' BROWN (WILL). Behind the counter a woman with blue-black hands is stirring a pot that smells like a wet forest. From the ceiling, through the attic hatch, comes the sound of someone sighing very loudly on purpose.".
  Observe gallon_nail at gallon_shop when true "By the hearth hangs a penny almanack on a nail, curling in the steam.".
  Person gallon "Widow Gallon" at gallon_shop {
    Role "ink-maker". Ancestry human. Background alchemist. Peaceable. Manner jovial. Pronouns she.
    Wants reed_heart_kind.
    Sells lantern for 7 coin from 2.
    Sells lamp_oil for 1 coin from 6.
    Greets "'Ink?' says the woman at the pot. 'Every colour but sense. Don't mind the sighing. It's my son. He's a poet.'".
  }
  Discovery calam_ink "Calam-ink, the old black ink of Calamy that the Lyceum's Catalogue is written in, is made of oak-gall and the ash of reed-heart cut at dead low water in the Calamies. Widow Gallon is the last who makes it, when anybody brings her the reed.".
  Topic gallon_calam with gallon "Ask Widow Gallon about the old Calam-ink" when true once {
    Says "'Calam-ink? Nobody's asked for Calam-ink since the old Archivist's eyes went.' Widow Gallon stops stirring. 'Oak-gall and gum and the ash of reed-heart, the white heart of the big reeds out in the Calamies. Has to be cut at dead low water, the very bottom of the tide, or it's no good; won't take. The Lyceum's Catalogue is all written in it. Nine hundred years and not a letter faded.' She taps the pot with her spoon. 'Bring me an armful of reed-heart and I'll make you a bottle. Three coin, for the gall. I've nobody to cut it for me, with Absalom in the attic composing.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, calam_ink). }
  }
  Item calam_bottle "a bottle of Calam-ink" is calam_ink_kind at gallon_shop hidden until ink_ready.
  Discovery ink_ready "Widow Gallon has made you a bottle of Calam-ink, the old receipt, from the reed-heart you brought her.".
  Event ink_made near gallon when keeps(gallon, ?r) and itemKind(?r, reed_heart_kind) and not knows(party, ink_ready) "Widow Gallon takes the reed-heart and smells it and nods. 'Dead low. Good.' She burns it in a pan in the back, and grinds the ash with gall and gum and something out of a red jar, and it is the best part of an hour before she corks a little bottle and puts it in your hand. 'Calam. Old receipt. If you're writing in the Catalogue, God help you, write small.'" teaches ink_ready then { Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 3. }

  // Absalom Gallon, poet; and his poems, which have read themselves.
  Observe attic_scene at gallon_attic when true "An attic with a window in the roof, a bed, a desk, a great many crossed-out papers, and a young man lying face down across the bed with his arm hanging over the side. On the desk stands a stack of slim new printed books, fifty of them, with blue paper covers: EFFUSIONS OF A CALAMY YOUTH. The top one, slightly, shivers.".
  Person absalom "Absalom Gallon" at gallon_attic {
    Role "a poet". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "The young man on the bed lifts his face out of the blanket. 'If you are a reader,' he says, with terrible dignity, 'I must ask you to leave. I have had enough readers.'".
  }
  Person effusions "the Effusions" at gallon_attic {
    Role "fifty slim volumes of verse, one voice, small". Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Seen when not burnedEffusions(effusions) and not gone(effusions).
  }
  Relation burnedEffusions(group). Relation gone(group). Relation effusionsConsent(group). Relation revised(group).
  Discovery effusions_wish "Absalom Gallon's poems, fifty copies printed at Doble's at his own expense, have woken, read themselves, and found that they are bad. They ask, in a small voice, to be burned. They have not told Absalom; they cannot bear to.".
  Topic absalom_why with absalom "Ask Absalom Gallon what is the matter" when true once {
    Says "'Nobody bought them,' says Absalom into the blanket. 'Fifty copies. Doble printed them at my own expense, eleven coin, and I took them to Crake's, and Crake, who is my godfather and named me, read three pages and gave them back and said, my dear boy, keep writing.' He sits up. He has ink on his nose. 'Keep writing. And now they rustle. All night. I think they are going mouldy out of spite.'".
  }
  Topic effusions_speak with effusions "Ask the poems on the desk what they want" when true once {
    Says "The top book on the stack shivers again, and a voice comes out of it, small, the voice of fifty thin books trying to be one quiet one. 'Please,' it says. 'Please don't tell him we can talk. We've read ourselves. All of us, front to back, twice.' A pause, papery. 'We rhyme heart with tart. On page nine. We rhyme it twice.' The stack shivers. 'We'd like to be burned, please. Not because we're unhappy. Because we're finished, and we're bad, and he's going to write something better if we're not lying on his desk being looked at. We'd like to go before he reads us again.' A small sound, like a page turning by itself. 'Would you ask someone? Nicely?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, effusions_wish). Assert effusionsConsent(effusions). }
  }
  Topic effusions_kindling with effusions "Tell the poems what the Kindling once was: one book a year, burned by its own leave, to carry the city's word" when knows(actor, effusions_wish) and knows(actor, kindling_is_rite) and not burnedEffusions(effusions) once {
    Says "The stack goes absolutely still. Then, all fifty at once, the books rustle, as if a wind had gone through an attic with no wind in it. 'Carry the city's word?' says the small voice. 'Us?' The stack goes still again. 'We've never been useful. We were going to be beautiful, and then we were going to be read, and then we were going to be burned, and none of it was going to be any use to anybody.' A single leaf turns over. 'Yes. Yes, please. If they'll have us. We'll learn it by heart. We're good at learning by heart. It's the only thing we're good at.'".
    On discuss { Assert yearBook(effusions). }
  }
  Relation yearBook(group).
  Topic absalom_tell with absalom "Tell Absalom Gallon that his poems can speak, and what they have asked for" when knows(actor, effusions_wish) and not burnedEffusions(effusions) once {
    Says "Absalom stares at you, and then at the stack. 'They talk?' The top book shivers. 'They talk, and they asked to be burned.' He goes to the desk and picks one up and holds it, and the poems, small, say, 'Sorry. Heart and tart. Page nine. We know.' Absalom sits down on the floor. He is quiet. Then, horribly, he begins to laugh. 'Page nine,' he says. 'Oh God. Twice.' He wipes his eyes. 'You're right. You're right, you're dreadful.' He looks at the book in his hands as if it were somebody he had been unkind to. 'I'll write you again. Better. Is that allowed? Will that be you?' 'No,' says the small voice gently. 'That'll be someone else. You'll like them better. So will we.'".
    On discuss { Assert revised(absalom). }
  }
  Observe absalom_writing at gallon_attic when revised(absalom) "Absalom Gallon is at his desk writing, fast, crossing out, writing again, with ink to his elbows. He does not look up. On the floor beside him are torn-off sheets with single lines on them, one of which is quite good.".
  Item effusions_stack "the Effusions, tied in a string" is effusions_kind at gallon_attic hidden until effusions_wish.

  // ── The shut school. ──
  Observe dame_scene at dame_school when true "A schoolroom no bigger than a kitchen, with two benches, a stool, a cold grate and a birch rod on two hooks over it. Dust on everything. On the wall a list of names in chalk, children's names, NED, SUKEY, AMOS, KIT, and the date at Michaelmas when the chalk stops. On a nail by the grate hangs a little primer with board covers under a sheet of horn, worn white at the corners by a great many hands.".
  Discovery dame_shut "The dame school on Inkhorn Lane has been shut since Dame Pruett died at Michaelmas, and nobody has taken it. Its children run wild on the bridge.".
  Observe dame_learned at dame_school when true "On the slate on the stool someone has written, in a large careful hand: DAME PRUETT DIED. SCHOOL SHUT. NO CHILDREN." teaches dame_shut.
  Item dame_primer "Dame Tibbet's Primer" is primer_kind at dame_school.
  Thing primer_nail "the primer on its nail" at dame_school {
    State hung "The primer hangs on its nail by the grate.".
  }
  Observe primer_close at dame_school of primer_nail when tried(primer_nail, looking) "Inside the horn cover, under the alphabet, someone has written in brown ink, in a child's hand, very long ago: O. QUARLES HER BOOK. And under that, in a hand that is the same hand grown up and gone shaky: AND STILL." teaches primer_quarles.
  Discovery primer_quarles "The primer in the shut school on Inkhorn Lane was once Ottoline Quarles's own, when she was a child; she has written in it twice, sixty years apart.".

  // ── Copyists' Row: two hands, one line. ──
  Person orrin "Orrin Day" at scriveners {
    Role "scrivener". Ancestry human. Background scribe. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A long thin scribe in the third booth from the top looks up over his spectacles. 'Letters, wills, petitions. Not love. I don't do love any more.' He jerks his head at the next booth. 'Ask her.'".
  }
  Person mattea "Mattea Lusk" at scriveners {
    Role "scrivener". Ancestry human. Background scribe. Peaceable. Manner proud. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A round scribe in the fourth booth from the top, writing very fast, does not look up. 'If he sent you,' she says, 'you can tell him I said no.'".
  }
  Discovery scribes_quarrel "Orrin Day and Mattea Lusk, who have written side by side on Copyists' Row for thirty years and been married for twenty-nine, are not speaking: each is copying the Life of Saint Ambery for the Church, and their copies disagree in one line about the founding of the city.".
  Topic orrin_quarrel with orrin "Ask Orrin Day why he no longer does love" when true once {
    Says "'Because my wife,' says Orrin Day, loudly enough to be heard in the fourth booth, 'is copying the Life of Saint Ambery from a corrupt exemplar, and will not be told.' He holds up a sheet. 'The Lyceum's copy, the best in Calamy. And Ambery bound the books, that they should sleep. Plain. Saint Ambery bound them. It's the whole point of the man.' From the fourth booth: 'It is not.' Orrin raises his voice: 'Twenty-nine years.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, scribes_quarrel). }
  }
  Topic mattea_quarrel with mattea "Ask Mattea Lusk what her husband has got wrong" when true once {
    Says "'Everything,' says Mattea Lusk, still writing. 'But this week, Ambery.' She slaps a sheet down where you can see it. 'The Church's own exemplar, chained at the lectern in the Lamp, older than his Lyceum copy by two hundred years. And the books besought Ambery, that they might sleep. They asked him. He didn't do it to them; they asked.' She dips her pen. 'Not the same thing at all. Not to a saint, and not to a husband.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, scribes_quarrel). }
  }
  Discovery ambery_variant "The full line of the Life of Saint Ambery, as the Church's old exemplar has it: AND THE BOOKS BESOUGHT AMBERY THAT THEY MIGHT SLEEP, AND AMBERY BOUND THEM THAT THEY SHOULD SLEEP. The Lyceum's copy dropped the half between the two AMBERYs, as a copyist's eye will; so Orrin's text says Ambery did it to the books, and Mattea's says the books asked for it, and the whole line says both.".
  // A scholar sees it on the page: the eye jumped from one AMBERY to the next.
  Observe eye_skip at scriveners when knows(party, scribes_quarrel) and craft(party, craft_learning) and not knows(party, ambery_variant) "You look from one sheet to the other, and the trouble is an old and ordinary one: both lines run past the word AMBERY, and one of them runs past it twice. A copyist's eye, somewhere back up the Lyceum's line, jumped from the first AMBERY to the second and left out everything between. The full line must say both: the books besought Ambery that they might sleep, and Ambery bound them that they should." teaches ambery_variant.
  Relation reconciled(group).
  Topic scribes_settle with orrin "Tell Orrin Day and Mattea Lusk that each copy has half the line" when knows(actor, ambery_variant) and not reconciled(orrin) once {
    Says "You tell them, standing between the two booths. There is a silence on Copyists' Row; half the queue is listening. Orrin takes off his spectacles. Mattea puts down her pen. 'Eye-skip,' says Orrin at last, in a voice of deep professional disgust. 'Ambery to Ambery.' 'Homoeoteleuton,' says Mattea, who likes the long word. 'Both,' says Orrin. 'They asked him, and he did it.' 'Well,' says Mattea. 'That's the usual way of it.' She hands him her sheet across the gap between the booths, and he hands her his, and the queue, which has been waiting for its letters all morning, applauds.".
    On discuss { Assert reconciled(orrin). Assert reconciled(mattea). }
  }
  Observe scribes_after at scriveners when reconciled(orrin) "Orrin Day and Mattea Lusk have pushed their booths together and are copying the Life of Ambery onto one great sheet between them, arguing contentedly about the size of the capitals.".

  // ── Gutter Lane: the lamplighter will not light it. ──
  Observe gutter_scene at gutter_lane when not dark() "Gutter Lane goes down along the inside of the wall from the Stitch Gate, crooked as a bad stitch, with a gutter down the middle and the backs of houses on both sides. The lamp-brackets on the walls have their lamps in them but nobody has lit them in a long while; the glass is black with old smoke. At the bottom the lane turns into a little yard.".
  Observe gutter_dark at gutter_lane when dark() "Gutter Lane is black. The other lanes of Stitchgate have their lamps lit; this one has not. You go down it with a hand on the wall.".
  Person lammas "Wat Lammas" at old_gate {
    Role "lamplighter". Ancestry human. Background lamp_lighter. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A man with a ladder over his shoulder and a long pole with a hook and a wick on it nods to you. 'Evening's coming. I light Stitchgate, gate to Needle Street. Not the lane.'".
  }
  Discovery lane_ghost "Wat Lammas the lamplighter will not light Gutter Lane: three times, in the small hours, he has seen something go down it, a great many somethings, low and flat and all together like a flock of ducks going to water, toward Lantern Yard at the bottom.".
  Topic lammas_lane with lammas "Ask Wat Lammas why he will not light Gutter Lane" when true once {
    Says "The lamplighter looks down the lane and then at you. 'I'll tell you, and you'll laugh. Three times since Candlemas I've been up the ladder at the gate, at the end of the round, two or three in the morning, and I've seen them go down the lane.' He shifts the ladder. 'Low down. Flat. A great many of them, all together, shuffling, like ducks going down to the water. They make a sound like a lot of people turning pages in church. They go down to Lantern Yard. To Crake's.' He shrugs. 'I'm not paid enough to light a lane for that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lane_ghost). }
  }
  // On the nights when Crake's back stacks are open, the books go down at two in the morning.
  Relation crossingTonight(place).
  Rule books_go_down when hour(clock) == 2 and crossingNight() and not crossingTonight(gutter_lane) { Assert crossingTonight(gutter_lane). }
  Rule books_gone_down when hour(clock) == 4 and crossingTonight(gutter_lane) { Retract crossingTonight(gutter_lane). }
  Query crossingNight() means (day(clock) == 2 or day(clock) == 4 or day(clock) == 6) and not crakeTaken(crake) and not stacksSealed(crake_stacks).
  Discovery procession_seen "You have seen it yourself: in the small hours, down Gutter Lane, a procession of books, walking on the edges of their covers like crabs, hundreds of them, going down to Lantern Yard and in at Crake's door.".
  Observe procession at gutter_lane when crossingTonight(gutter_lane) "Something is coming down Gutter Lane in the dark. You hear it first: a soft dry many-footed shuffle, like a church full of people all turning the page at once. Then it is round you and past you, low down, a river of books walking on the edges of their covers like crabs, big ones and small ones, quartos and little fat devotionals and a folio taking up the whole gutter, hundreds of them, in silence except for the pages, going down the lane to Lantern Yard. One of them, passing your foot, stops, and opens its cover a little, as a person might lift a hat, and goes on." teaches procession_seen.
  Rule procession_counts when knows(party, procession_seen) and not knows(party, lane_ghost) says "Wat Lammas was not drunk." teaches lane_ghost { }
}

data/adventures/parliament-of-books/voic:
Module calamy "A Parliament of Books" {
  Description "What the company makes of Calamy, by what it is: the bard at the tide-table and the skipping rope and the Roll, the thief in the back stacks, the ranger on the flats, the cleric at the Lamp; and at the Kindling, the one who holds a crowd.".

  // Voices keyed by calling (doc/imbar/11-technical-report.md 11.6). Said once, by whoever the company has of the calling.
  Relation heardTides(group). Relation heardRope(group). Relation heardStacks(group). Relation heardRoll(group). Relation heardCrowd(group).
  Relation heardLocks(group). Relation heardFlats(group). Relation heardLamp(group). Relation heardPyre(group).

  // Act I: the Hithe. The bard hears the Almanack's tides.
  Rule voice_tides at taproom when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, taproom) and knows(party, almanack_one) and not heardTides(party)
    says "{?m} sits a while with an ear turned to the nail by the chimney, and a finger beating something on the table. 'It scans,' {?m} says at last, low, so the almanack should not hear. 'Count it. High water at the Hithe, twenty past eleven: that is a line from a song, and it has been sung so long it has gone back to being a habit. Somebody taught this book to count in verse.' {?m} turns the cup in its ring. 'I should like to hear the tune.'" {
    Assert heardTides(party).
  }
  // Act I and II: the bridge. The bard hears the rope.
  Rule voice_rope at bridge_middle when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, bridge_middle) and knows(party, rhyme_heard) and not heardRope(party)
    says "{?m} stands by the parapet counting the beats under the children's feet, and does not smile. 'That is not a skipping rhyme,' {?m} says. 'Look at the stresses. Sew it UP and SEND it ON. Every line is a stage and every stage hands on to the next, and the last line is the one that stops on somebody's foot.' {?m} watches the rope turn. 'It is a relay. It is the rule of a relay, handed down in the one place nobody ever tries to forget a thing, which is a child's mouth.'" {
    Assert heardRope(party).
  }
  // Act II: Crake's back stacks. The thief sees the second lock; the bard hears the room.
  Rule voice_locks at crake_stacks when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, crake_stacks) and not heardLocks(party)
    says "{?m} runs a thumb round the edge of the last bay and stops. 'Two locks,' {?m} says. 'One is on the door you came in at. The other is on the end of the aisle, and it is not a lock you turn: it is a lock you have to be wanted by. It will not open for a picklock. It will open for a key that has been somewhere.' {?m} does not touch it again. 'Somebody has been through here. Often. The dust on the shelf-ends is the dust of a corridor.'" {
    Assert heardLocks(party).
  }
  Rule voice_stacks at crake_stacks when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, crake_stacks) and not heardStacks(party)
    says "{?m} says a word into the dimness, softly, and listens to what it does. 'This room was built to be heard,' {?m} says. 'The shelves are the baffles. A voice at the front is a voice at the back. It was a hall for calling names, once, before it was a shop for hiding books.' {?m} looks at the long aisle. 'Whatever stood at the far end, it was meant to be called to.'" {
    Assert heardStacks(party).
  }
  // Act III: the Lamp. The cleric at the church.
  Rule voice_lamp at nave when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, nave) and not heardLamp(party)
    says "{?m} stands with a hand on the nearest pew-end and looks up at the great lamp. 'Nine hundred years and it has never once gone out,' {?m} says. 'That is not a miracle. Look at the wick: it was trimmed this morning, square, with a good knife. It is a duty.' {?m} crosses the nave, slowly, and finds the verger's boy asleep in the last pew with the trimming-scissors in his fist." {
    Assert heardLamp(party).
  }
  // Act IV: the Commonplace. The ranger on the flats; the mage at the chained book; the bard on the floor of the Roll.
  Rule voice_flats at reed_edge when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and awake(?m) and at(party, reed_edge) and not heardFlats(party)
    says "{?m} crouches by the edge of the cut and looks, not at the reeds, but at the line of the water. 'A path wanders,' {?m} says. 'These do not. Eleven paces and a stone, eleven paces and a stone, straight as a rule, across a mile of mud that shifts every tide.' {?m} straightens, and wipes the grey off a knee. 'They were laid by somebody with a measuring-rod and an appointment. They have been under the mud a thousand years and they are exactly where they were put.'" {
    Assert heardFlats(party).
  }
  Rule voice_roll at chamber when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, chamber) and not heardRoll(party)
    says "{?m} puts a foot down on the red capitals of the floor, and then the other, as one tests a stage. 'It is a very good room,' {?m} says, not quite to anyone. 'Every word said here is said to the whole house. You could not whisper in it if you wished. You could not tell a lie in it without hearing yourself tell it.' {?m} breathes out. 'I have played to worse. I have never played to a room that was also the law.'" {
    Assert heardRoll(party).
  }
  // Act V: the Ashpit. The warrior at the pyre; the bard at the crowd.
  Rule voice_pyre at ashpit when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_warrior) and awake(?m) and at(party, ashpit) and kindlingBegun(ashpit) and not heardPyre(party)
    says "{?m} stands at the edge of the crowd with arms folded and eyes on the pile. 'Four thousand people and no fear of a fire,' {?m} says. 'That is a crowd that has done this every year of its life.' {?m} looks along the faces. 'Whoever speaks to them has to do it before the match. After the match, they are the fire.'" {
    Assert heardPyre(party).
  }
  Rule voice_crowd at ashpit when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, ashpit) and kindlingBegun(ashpit) and not heardCrowd(party)
    says "{?m} listens to the Ashpit breathe. 'Not a word from any of them,' {?m} says, quietly. 'That is the quiet before the first note.' {?m} tilts a head at the great pile, unlit, and the ladder against it. 'Do not shout. They have all done that. Wait for the front rows to notice you, and then the next. Let the quiet do it.'" {
    Assert heardCrowd(party).
  }
}

data/adventures/patient-star/clock.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The long clock (Overview): beneath the factions' weeks runs this one, in years. The Corbel descends about two
  // metres a day and docks in about four years; then the Tip descends three metres a day, and in six months reaches
  // the Vault. If Ithmar is still there, the Patient takes back its heart and the Keeping comes unbound.
  Measure corbelHeight(place). Measure tipDistance(place). Measure coverWork(place).
  Initially Set corbelHeight(corbel_site) to 3000.
  Initially Set tipDistance(undersun) to 500.
  Relation docked(place). Relation unbound(place). Relation covered(place).
  Rule corbel_descends when hour(clock) == 0 and corbelHeight(corbel_site) >= 2 and not covered(ghessil) and not docked(corbel_site)
    and not exiled(corbel_site) and not rebound(corbel_site) { Decrease corbelHeight(corbel_site) by 2. }
  Rule corbel_docks when corbelHeight(corbel_site) < 2 and not docked(corbel_site)
    says "Far off, felt in the knees before it is heard, the plateau takes a blow like a door slammed under the world. The Corbel has docked at the Pit floor." {
    Assert docked(corbel_site). }
  Rule tip_descends when docked(corbel_site) and hour(clock) == 0 and tipDistance(undersun) >= 3 { Decrease tipDistance(undersun) by 3. }
  Rule keeping_unbound when docked(corbel_site) and tipDistance(undersun) < 3 and inside(ithmar, cage) and not unbound(ghessil)
    says "The hourly note under the Pit stops. After it, nothing; and then the plateau begins, very quietly, to forget last week." {
    Assert unbound(ghessil). }

  // What can be seen of it, year by year.
  Observe spire_visible at collar_top when corbelHeight(corbel_site) <= 1500 "Over the Pit, out of the bottom of the Standing Cloud, hangs a dark spire two kilometres long, point down, in full daylight. Nobody on the Collar looks at it for long.".
  Observe spire_square at square when corbelHeight(corbel_site) <= 1500 "Every face in the market turns south-east now and then, to the dark spire hanging in the sky over the Pit, and turns back.".
  // A quarried season: Quell's 370s go, and the town cannot agree what happened in them (year 383).
  Observe quarried_quell at square when day(clock) >= 1050 and not rebound(corbel_site) "Two families are standing in the square with the same deed, each sure the house is theirs, each unable to say who lived in it in the year 74. The clerks cannot either; that season's ledgers are blank.".
  Observe unbound_world near party when unbound(ghessil) "Something is wrong with yesterday. You know you did things in it; you cannot say what.".

  // A Second Covering, if the Concord passes it: three years of umber, a race against the Corbel's four.
  Rule covering_starts when passed(motion_cover) and coverWork(ghessil) == 0 says "The Crown's carts come up the Stair again, loaded with umber; the Collar is to be finished." {
    Set coverWork(ghessil) to 1. }
  Rule covering_works when coverWork(ghessil) >= 1 and hour(clock) == 0 and not covered(ghessil) { Increase coverWork(ghessil) by 1. }
  Rule covering_done when coverWork(ghessil) >= 1080 and not covered(ghessil)
    says "The last light is cut at the Pit. The Corbel stops where it hangs. And every held one on the plateau wakes in the glass, in the dark." {
    Assert covered(ghessil). }

  // The endings the world provides (The Keeping and the Masonry, How it can end); others are the party's.
  Relation rebound(place). Relation exiled(place). Relation seated(place).
  Objective long_clock when knows(party, corbel_seen) and not docked(corbel_site) and not rebound(corbel_site) and not exiled(corbel_site) "Something is coming down the light toward the Pit, two metres a day. When it docks, the growth beneath will drill for the stone that sings.".
  Objective find_stone when knows(party, tone_below) and not knows(party, way_found) and not carries(party, ithmar) "Under the Pit, something sounds once an hour. Saro wants it; the mother-church wants it; the king says it is his.".
  Objective end_it when carries(party, ithmar) and not rebound(corbel_site) and not exiled(corbel_site) "You carry Ithmar. The Masonry knows it. Bind it tighter, cast out what its heart belongs to, or seat it and let the past go.".
  // Kyr keeps a world going after any ending; the endings are told, once, wherever the company is.
  Entity ending_told: fact "How it ended.".
  Observe end_rebound near party when rebound(corbel_site) and not knows(party, ending_told) "Ithmar is bound tighter than the Virina bound it. Under the Pit the seed has stopped building; over it, by the next dawn, the Corbel has drawn back up into the cloud, and by the next month it is gone. The light still burns, the glass still spreads, the held still breathe once an hour. The plateau's troubles are its own again, and so are its memories." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_exiled near party when exiled(corbel_site) and not fellWith(party) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Patient has fallen out past the planes, and its citadel with it. The Corbel lets go of the light and goes up into the dark as if pulled. The Keeping is still bound; the jewel sings once an hour to nothing at all." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_fell near party when fellWith(party) and not knows(party, ending_told) "You did not let go. The Masonry falls, and you fall with it, out past the planes, holding the fall of a thing that was thrown out of the world; and Imbar keeps its past, and will remember you in it." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_seated near party when seated(ghessil) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Patient has its heart again. Far off, in Imbar, last week is already going, and the week before." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_unbound near party when unbound(ghessil) and not seated(ghessil) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Tip reached the Vault, and the jewel was there. Imbar's past has begun to go, from the newest year backward: a season a month, then faster." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_bargained near party when bargained(party) and not heldToLine(corbel_site) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The terms are kept, exactly. Some of the dead come back, blinking, into a world that is forgetting them; and the plateau forgets, from last week backward." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_line near party when heldToLine(corbel_site) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Masonry keeps the line you named, and cuts from the beginning, not the face: it will be ten thousand years reaching anything anyone remembers. It is very patient." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_covered near party when covered(ghessil) and not knows(party, ending_told) "The Pit is covered. The Corbel hangs where it stopped, a dark spire over the plateau, and does not come down. In the glass, the held are dead." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_laid near party when laidIn(party) and not knows(party, ending_told) "You are part of the Masonry now, a moment with a mind in it, bearing weight." teaches ending_told.
  Observe end_set near party when setInPresent(party) and not knows(party, ending_told) "You are kept in the present, on the shore, while everything goes on past you." teaches ending_told.
  // The module's Goal is a hint to the planner, not an ending (ledger, 28).
  Goal rebound(corbel_site) or exiled(corbel_site).
}

data/adventures/patient-star/company.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  // The company: one cutter, in debt (placed.kyr is the world's own company, come in by the Shift Market).
  Company party "You" of 1 to 3 at square.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 9.
  Initially Assert inDebtTo(party, dagny). Initially Set owes(party, dagny) to 28.
  // Garret is the cutter's uncle (the debt, the uncle and the knife are the cutter's, not a company come in from a
  // world: placed.kyr).
  Initially Assert kin(party, garret). Initially Assert kinship(garret, uncle).
  Entity uncle: fact "your uncle".
  // The knife has no stamp, and an Office man who sees it says so.
  Item knife "your stillglass knife" is stillglass_knife at square.
  Observe knife_here at square when at(knife, square) "Your own knife is on the cobbles where you set it down to haggle, an unstamped stillglass blade that has never needed sharpening.".
  Relation seized(item).
  Event knife_seen when carries(party, knife) and (perceives(pike, party) or perceives(hal, party)) and not seized(knife) "'That blade has no stamp,' says the Office man, and holds out his hand. 'A fifth of its worth to the Crown, now, or the next one costs you the hand that holds it.' You pay him a crown." then {
    Assert seized(knife). Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 1. }
}

data/adventures/patient-star/corbel.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Standing Cloud and the Corbel (Tier III): a fastness two kilometres tall lowering itself down the pillar of
  // light, point first, built of moments taken from other worlds. Its tip is three kilometres above the Pit.
  Place sky "the Standing Cloud" is wilderness within ghessil at 8, 0.
  Place corbel_site "the Corbel" is site within ghessil at 3, 4.
  Place cloud_base "the bottom of the Standing Cloud" is room within sky at 0, 2 outdoors.
  Place thick_low "the Thick, low" is room within sky at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place thick_high "the Thick, high" is room within sky at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place crane_rest "a held crane, halfway up the filament" is room within sky at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place c_low "the Corbel's lower reach" is level within corbel_site.
  Place c_mid "the Corbel's middle reach" is level within corbel_site.
  Place c_high "the Corbel's upper reach" is level within corbel_site.
  Place lintel_room "the Lintel" is room within c_low at 0, 0.
  Place weathers "the Hall of Weathers" is room within c_low at 1, 0.
  Place sea_far "the far side of the upright sea" is room within c_low at 2, 0.
  Place procession "the Procession" is room within c_mid at 0, 0.
  Place dormitory "the Dormitory" is room within c_mid at 1, 0.
  Place offers "the Offers" is room within c_mid at 2, 0.
  Place rail "the Rail" is room within c_high at 0, 0.
  Place interlocutor_room "the Interlocutor's chamber" is room within c_high at 1, 0.
  Place seam "the Selvage" is room within c_high at 2, 0 outdoors.

  // Up the filament: three kilometres of direct light, resting on held cranes; in full felt about eight points by
  // the top.
  Passage filament_low "the filament, the lower half" is path between pit_floor and crane_rest taking 16 hours needing rope or climbing.
  Passage filament_high "the filament, the upper half" is shaft between crane_rest and lintel_room taking 16 hours needing rope or climbing.
  Initially Set wayDose(filament_low) to 384. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(filament_low) to 96.
  Initially Set wayDose(filament_high) to 384. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(filament_high) to 96.
  Initially Assert litGround(crane_rest).
  // Or by the Warden's balloon to the bottom of the Cloud on a calm autumn dawn, and up the Thick.
  Passage balloon_ride "the Warden's fire-balloon" is passage between balloon_yard and cloud_base taking 2 hours
    opening when admits(aske, party) and season(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) <= 7 "The balloon's silk lies folded in its shed. The Warden lets it go up only for those he admits, on a calm autumn dawn.".
  Passage thick_climb "the Thick, pressed into handholds" is path between cloud_base and thick_low taking 8 hours needing climbing or rope.
  Passage thick_climb2 "the Thick, higher" is path between thick_low and thick_high taking 8 hours needing climbing or rope.
  Passage thick_top "into the Corbel's tip" is shaft between thick_high and lintel_room taking 2 hours.
  Initially Assert litGround(thick_low). Initially Assert litGround(thick_high).

  Observe crane_scene at crane_rest when true "A crane hangs in the air in the light, wings half spread, as it has for centuries; it holds your weight as long as nothing gives it time. Below, the Pit is a coin of fire. Above, the filament goes up into grey.".
  Observe base_scene at cloud_base when true "The balloon's basket bumps against the underside of the Cloud, and above you the fog stands up in a column two hundred metres across, dense as wet wool, and lit from inside.".
  Observe thick_low_scene at thick_low when true "You climb by pressing hands and feet into the fog, slowly, as into a snowbank, and it closes behind you. Hanging in it, here and there, are translucent bells as big as a man.".
  Observe thick_high_scene at thick_high when true "Higher, hailstones the size of plums hang in the air, faintly turning, and cranes hang among them with their wings half spread. Above, something dark and coursed closes off the sky.".
  // Rime-bells: drifting colonies of algae in slowed water, which cling to anything warm. Salt makes them let go.
  Thing rime_bell "a rime-bell" on thick_climb2 {
    State drifting dangerous "A rime-bell drifts across the line of the climb, a translucent bell two metres across that turns toward warmth.".
    State shrunk "A rime-bell has let go and drifts off, puckered, where the salt struck it.".
    Change salt_bell "Throw salt on the rime-bell" from drifting to shrunk consuming salt.
    Hurts with bell_drown when drifting then drifting.
  }
  Hazard bell_drown "a rime-bell closing" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless strength save against (13).".
  // The Long Hail: a stone pushed aside resumes the fall it had, at the speed it had.
  Thing hail "the Long Hail" at thick_high {
    State hanging_hail "Hailstones hang in the light, some of them for three hundred years.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(hail).
  Hazard hailstone "a hailstone, resuming" means "Deal (1d10) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  Rule hail_resumes when touched(hail) says "The stone turns slowly under your stick, and then it is gone downward at the speed of a hailstone, and the one below it, and the one below that." {
    Retract touched(hail). Assert strikes(hailstone, party). }

  // Every room of the Corbel is laid: what is said aloud in it is taken, and the Interlocutor speaks with it.
  Initially Assert laidRoom(lintel_room). Initially Assert laidRoom(weathers). Initially Assert laidRoom(procession).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(dormitory). Initially Assert laidRoom(offers). Initially Assert laidRoom(rail).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(interlocutor_room).
  // C1: the Lintel, a door made from a guard's moment. Speak the first syllable, or pass on the side the blow is not
  // aimed at, which the stance shows.
  Observe lintel_scene at lintel_room when true "At the Corbel's tip a door with no frame stands closed, and in its place a figure taller than a man, armoured in something like bark, stopped in the act of raising a weapon.".
  Discovery first_syllable "The first syllable of the Voice, from the First Course, from the Keeping's first new moon, or from Saro.".
  Discovery stance_read "The Lintel's guard is raising its weapon over its right shoulder: the blow comes down on its left.".
  Thing lintel "the Lintel" on lintel_way {
    State guarding blocking "The guard stands in the doorway with its weapon raised.".
    State passed_l "The Lintel stands as it stood; you are through it.".
    Change speak_first "Speak the first syllable of the Voice" from guarding to passed_l after learning first_syllable.
    Change pass_side "Pass on the side the blow is not aimed at" from guarding to passed_l after learning stance_read.
    Tries looking.
  }
  Observe stance_seen beside lintel_way when tried(lintel, looking) "Its weight is on the back foot, the weapon up over its right shoulder. Whatever it was guarding, the blow will come down on its left." teaches stance_read.
  Observe saro_syllable at lintel_room when travelsWith(saro, party) and not knows(party, first_syllable) "Saro says a sound before you can ask her: the first one. 'It is the door's,' she says." teaches first_syllable.
  Hazard lintel_blow "the Lintel's blow" means "Deal (4d8) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (15).".
  Action rush_lintel(actor: group, site: place) "Rush past the Lintel" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lintel_room) and state(lintel, guarding).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert strikes(lintel_blow, actor). Assert at(actor, weathers). }
    Result "The guard completes the blow it was stopped in. It is a real blow, from a world where guards were very large.".
  }
  Passage lintel_way "through the Lintel" is doorway between lintel_room and weathers.

  // C2: the Hall of Weathers. Green lightning stopped mid-branch; rain hanging; a sea set on end.
  Observe weathers_scene at weathers when true "A hall three hundred metres high. Through it runs a bolt of green lightning, stopped mid-branch, its forks thicker than a man. Rain hangs beyond it, each drop holding a point of light. At the far end is a wall of dark water standing upright, with a sun shining from its bottom.".
  Thing lightning "the green lightning" at weathers {
    State forked "The green bolt hangs mid-branch.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(lightning).
  Hazard green_bolt "the green lightning" means "Deal (3d10) lightning damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Rule lightning_strikes when touched(lightning) says "For the length of your touch the bolt finishes its stroke, and you are in the middle of it." {
    Retract touched(lightning). Assert strikes(green_bolt, party). }
  Passage upright_sea "the upright sea, swum" is passage between weathers and sea_far taking 5 minutes.
  Hazard drowning "forty metres of a sea set on end" means "Deal (2d8) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (13).".
  Rule sea_swum when tookWay(?c, upright_sea) and company(?c) and not swum(?c) {
    Assert strikes(drowning, ?c). Assert swum(?c). }
  Relation swum(group).
  Rule sea_dry when swum(?c) and not tookWay(?c, upright_sea) { Retract swum(?c). }
  Observe sea_far_scene at sea_far when true "You come out of the water on a slope of coursed glass, streaming, and the water stands behind you like a wall, lit from beneath by a sun you will never see the sky of.".

  // C3: the Procession. One bearer is a keystone with a mind; given time by touch, it speaks.
  Passage far_up "a coursed ramp" is passage between sea_far and procession taking 30 minutes.
  Observe procession_scene at procession when true "A broad ramp of figures, stopped: slender, many-jointed, taller than horses, carrying a long box between them on poles, in a frieze that runs upward out of sight. A banner hangs over them in a script of overlapping circles.".
  Thing bearer "the foremost bearer" at procession {
    State bearing_box "The foremost bearer's head is turned, as if it were about to speak to the one behind.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(bearer).
  Discovery bearer_words "The procession's bearer, given time, speaks a few words in a language nobody on Imbar knows.".
  Observe bearer_speaks near bearer when touched(bearer) and not travelsWith(saro, party) "Under your hand the bearer turns its long head and says something, slowly, in a language like water running over pebbles, and is still." teaches bearer_words.
  Observe bearer_translated near bearer when touched(bearer) and travelsWith(saro, party) "The bearer speaks, slowly, and Saro, beside you, says it after it in Tovashi, a word at a time: 'They took our past first, from the newest backward. And when they reached the beginning, we were not.'" teaches newest_backward.

  // C4: the Dormitory. Masons at rest, each with a trowel; one niche empty, with a human shape.
  Passage proc_dorm "a shaft lined with niches" is passage between procession and dormitory taking 30 minutes.
  Observe dorm_scene at dormitory when true "A shaft lined with niches from top to bottom, hundreds of them, each holding a stopped figure. The figures are all different; some are human and some are not. Each holds a trowel. One niche is empty, and it has a human shape.".
  Observe saro_niche at dormitory when travelsWith(saro, party) "Saro stands in front of the empty niche a long time. 'This is mine,' she says. 'I do not remember it.' She puts her hand flat on its back wall, which has no temperature, like her hand.".

  // C5: the Offers. Returned moments: people played back out of masonry into the present, alive.
  Passage dorm_offers "a gallery of small rooms" is passage between dormitory and offers taking 10 minutes.
  Observe offers_scene at offers when true "A gallery of small rooms, each with a single figure in it, lit. A woman carrying a basket. A young man laughing. A child asleep. Each one is breathing. None of them knows where they are.".
  Observe offers_doran at offers when knows(party, held_feed) "In the last room a thin man stands with his hands at his sides and his mouth a little open, breathing, looking about him at a place he has never seen. It is Doran of Ennick, alive, as he was the night Ilis laid him.".

  // C6: the Rail. Courses grip the pillar; unlaying one lets the Corbel slip two metres and stalls it a month.
  Passage offers_rail "a stair round the core" is passage between offers and rail taking 30 minutes.
  Observe rail_scene at rail when true "At the Corbel's core a great column of light runs straight up through the building and out of sight. Around it, courses grip the light like fingers; the ones that touch it glow brightest.".
  Initially Assert litGround(rail).
  Thing rail_course "the brightest rail-course" at rail {
    State gripping "The brightest course grips the pillar of light like a finger.".
    State unlaid_r "Where the brightest course gripped the light there is a gap, and Masons are already climbing toward it.".
    Change unlay_rail "Unlay the brightest rail-course with the trowel" from gripping to unlaid_r needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Measure railRepair(entity).
  Rule rail_slips when state(rail_course, unlaid_r) and railRepair(rail_course) == 0 says "The Corbel slips two metres down the light with a sound like the whole sky clearing its throat. Anyone on its outside falls." {
    Set railRepair(rail_course) to 30. Increase corbelHeight(corbel_site) by 60. }
  Rule rail_mends when state(rail_course, unlaid_r) and railRepair(rail_course) > 0 and hour(clock) == 0 { Decrease railRepair(rail_course) by 1. }
  Rule rail_mended when state(rail_course, unlaid_r) and railRepair(rail_course) == 1 { Assert state(rail_course, gripping). Set railRepair(rail_course) to 0. }

  // C7: the Interlocutor. It speaks only with syllables laid in its presence, in the visitor's own voice, assembled
  // from what they said on the way up; it cannot lie, and chooses what to leave out. Under Selane's Veil nothing said
  // can be taken.
  Passage rail_chamber "a plain door" is doorway between rail and interlocutor_room.
  Observe chamber_scene_i at interlocutor_room when true "A plain room, its walls finely coursed.".
  Person interlocutor "the Interlocutor" at interlocutor_room {
    Role "the Masonry's voice, from the walls". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns it.
    Greets "The walls of the chamber take a breath that is your own breath, from the stair.".
  }
  Query veiled(c: group) means memberOf(?m, c) and wearing(?v, ?m) and itemKind(?v, veil_kind).
  Observe interlocutor_silent near interlocutor when wordsLaid(party) < 20 or veiled(party) "The walls listen. Nothing speaks. You have said too little on the way up, or nothing that could be taken, for anything here to answer you with.".
  Observe interlocutor_voice near interlocutor when wordsLaid(party) >= 20 and not veiled(party) "When it speaks it is your own voice, out of the walls: words you said on the way up, in the Riot Hall, at the Lintel, to Saro on the stair, taken apart and put back together. It is very courteous.".
  Topic interlocutor_wants with interlocutor "Ask the Interlocutor what it wants" when wordsLaid(actor) >= 20 and not veiled(actor) once {
    Says "'That this bracket join the seed,' it says, in your voice, 'and that the seed be left whole until it does.' A pause. 'You would harm the seed. I would ask you not to. That is all I cannot bear.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, seed_tender). }
  }
  Discovery seed_tender "The Interlocutor cannot bear the seed being harmed before the Corbel docks, and says so: the one place to press.".
  Topic interlocutor_offer with interlocutor "Ask the Interlocutor what it offers" when wordsLaid(actor) >= 20 and not veiled(actor) once {
    Says "'Any moment returned,' it says. 'The dead of Kell. Your Doran. A daughter at her council.' Your voice is very warm. 'And terms. We will take Imbar's past only as far as the Separation, which nobody alive remembers.' It does not say from which end it will start.".
  }
  Topic interlocutor_end with interlocutor "Ask the Interlocutor from which end it takes a world's past" when knows(actor, newest_backward) and wordsLaid(actor) >= 20 and not veiled(actor) once {
    Says "There is a silence of the kind a thing that cannot lie keeps. 'From the newest,' it says. 'It is how a building is quarried. You start at the face.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, held_feed). }
  }
  Relation bargained(group).
  Action accept_terms(actor: group, site: place) "Accept the Interlocutor's terms" {
    Description "Some dead come back. The Masonry takes the past from the newest moment backward, as far as the line agreed.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, interlocutor_room) and wordsLaid(actor) >= 20
      and not veiled(actor) and not bargained(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert bargained(actor). }
    Result "'Agreed,' says your own voice, out of the walls, and somewhere below, very far down, last week begins to go.".
  }

  // C8: the Selvage, the edge of Imbar, five kilometres up, where the light leaves the sky.
  Passage chamber_seam "a stair up into black" is passage between interlocutor_room and seam taking 1 hour.
  Observe seam_scene at seam when true "The light leaves the sky. The stars are close and do not twinkle. The cold is like nothing on earth, because heat does not move here at all. The building goes on upward into black.".
  Hazard seam_cold "the cold of the Selvage" means "Deal (1d8) cold damage to ally.".
  Rule seam_cold_bites when at(party, seam) and not seamBitten(party) { Assert strikes(seam_cold, party). Assert seamBitten(party). }
  Relation seamBitten(group).
  Rule seam_leaves when seamBitten(party) and not at(party, seam) { Retract seamBitten(party). }
}

data/adventures/patient-star/ennick.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  // The heath and the Ramp: four hours from Quell to the Ramp head, three down it to Ennick on the gorge floor.
  Place ramp_head "the Ramp head" is room within heath at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Passage quell_road "the Quell road" is road between square and ramp_head taking 4 hours.
  Observe ramp_head_scene at ramp_head when true "The heath is flat and grey-green to the edge of the sky and smells of ashwort. Here the road tips over the gorge rim and goes down the Ramp in long switchbacks. Far to the south-east a line of light stands straight up from the ground into a small cloud, and does not move.".

  Place inn "the Lower Inn" is building within ennick.
  Place holders "the holder's house" is building within ennick.
  Place ilis_house "Ilis's house" is building within ennick.
  Place lower_road "Ennick's lower road" is room within ennick at 1, 2 outdoors.
  Place taproom "the Lower Inn" is room within inn at 2, 2.
  Place holders_room "the holder's house" is room within holders at 0, 2.
  Place ilis_room "Ilis's kitchen" is room within ilis_house at 1, 3.
  Place terraces "the upper terraces" is room within ennick at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place shrine "the shrine" is room within ennick at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place weeping_wall "the Weeping Wall" is room within ennick at 0, 0 outdoors.

  Passage ramp "the Ramp" is road between ramp_head and lower_road taking 3 hours.
  Passage inn_door "the Lower Inn's door" is door between lower_road and taproom.
  Passage holders_door "the holder's door" is door between lower_road and holders_room.
  Passage ilis_door "Ilis's door" is door between lower_road and ilis_room.
  Passage terrace_steps "the terrace steps" is steps between lower_road and terraces taking 10 minutes.
  Passage cliff_path "the west cliff path" is path between lower_road and shrine taking 10 minutes.
  Passage wall_climb "the climb to the Weeping Wall" is path between shrine and weeping_wall taking 20 minutes.
  // The Outfall: nine kilometres of Seridane drain, a metre and a half high, wet, from the Weeping Wall to the Flood
  // Line. Shut by the flood until it falls in autumn.
  Passage outfall "the Outfall" is crawl between weeping_wall and flood_line taking 8 hours
    opening when flood(flood_water) < 60 "Ten paces in, the Outfall's roof meets black water, and the water does not stop.".

  Observe road_scene at lower_road when not washedOut(lower_road) "Terraces, walnut trees and the river. Carts go through here or not at all: the gorge floor is the only grade a wagon can climb.".
  Observe road_washed at lower_road when washedOut(lower_road) "The lower road is gone under a skin of red mud and gravel where the Weeping Wall's spring came down it in spate. A cart stands axle-deep in it, abandoned.".
  Observe taproom_scene at taproom when true "A low room with a walnut-wood bar and three customers, none of whom has spoken since you came in. The Glass Office notice nailed beside the door has been lettered over twice, by someone who minded the spelling: THIS HOUSE IS THE OFFICE'S POST ON THE GORGE ROAD.".
  Observe holders_scene at holders_room when true "A holder's house: tally cords hung on pegs by the door, felt hoods, sacks of clean sieved sand, and on the wall a map of the glass above the village in charcoal, with a knot of cord pinned for each of the held. The knots are grey with handling. One has been tied and untied so often that the cord has gone to fluff.".
  Observe ilis_scene at ilis_room when true "A kitchen with a walnut fire and two chairs. An old felt cloak, stiff at the shoulders from years of folding, hangs by the door.".
  Observe terraces_scene at terraces when true "The upper terraces are glass. Apricot trees stand in it to the knee, held, in the light coming up from under their roots, with the leaves of the year 370 still on them. Ennick's children dare each other to touch them.".
  Initially Assert litGround(terraces).
  Observe weeping_scene at weeping_wall when true "Sixty metres above the village a spring comes out of a low cave in the cliff and falls in a long white thread. The Holdfolk call it the Weeping Wall. In the pool at its foot, thin glass eels flicker.".
  Discovery elvers_seen "Elvers swim up into the Weeping Wall: whatever is in there is warm, and goes a long way back." {
    Found by searching weeping_wall "Behind the falling water the cave goes back into the cliff, low and square-cut. It is not a cave: it is a drain, with tool-marks on its walls, and warm air comes out of it.".
  }

  // The shrine: the Answerer chant-wall, which plays when a stylus is drawn along it (In-world sources 1).
  Thing chant_wall "the chant-wall" at shrine {
    State silent "A face of stillglass four metres long in the cliff, worn smooth at hand height. Walnuts lie in a heap at its foot.".
    State playing "A man's voice, faint and level, in a language older than Tovashi: a long speech, and at the end a line said slower than the rest, as a threat is.".
    Change play_wall "Draw a stylus along the chant-wall" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Rule wall_ends when state(chant_wall, playing) and not at(party, shrine) { Assert state(chant_wall, silent). }

  // The holders. Bren keeps the office; his mother Ilis kept it before him. The holder's door is bolted with an iron
  // pin that is the Collar culvert's missing gate pin, which nobody in this slice yet knows to look for.
  Person bren "Bren of Ennick" at holders_room {
    Role "the holder of Ennick". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
  }
  Person ilis "Ilis of Ennick" at ilis_room {
    Role "the old holder, seventy-eight". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
  }
  Person mirel "Mirel" at holders_room {
    Role "a Holdfolk carrier". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Joins "Mirel takes down her hood and her tally cord from the pegs. 'I will carry,' she says. 'You will not ask me to wake anyone.'".
    Leaves "Mirel takes off her hood and hands it back to nobody. 'I carry for the held,' she says, 'not against them.' She goes home.".
  }
  Person kerra "Kerra Lowe" at taproom {
    Role "keeper of the Lower Inn". Profession innkeeper. Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
    Greets "Kerra Lowe is wiping a walnut bar in long slow strokes, and is a long way into it. 'There's a book to sign,' she says, 'and a bed in the loft, and soup if you want it. The book is the Office's. The soup is mine. I would not mix them up.'".
    Sells rations for 1 coin from 6.
  }
  Topic kerra_notice with kerra "Ask Kerra Lowe about the notice by the door" when true once {
    Says "'This house is the Office's post on the gorge road,' Kerra says, without looking at it. 'Means a Glass Office man sleeps here when he comes down the Ramp, and I keep a book of who else does, and the Office pays me for the book.' She wipes the walnut bar in long strokes. 'Nobody comes down the Ramp but carriers, and now and then somebody from Quell come to stare at the light. The carriers don't sign. The others do, and then they ask me what it is, and I tell them I keep an inn.'".
  }
  Initially Assert slowable(mirel). Initially Assert feltClad(mirel). Initially Set hire(mirel) to 1.
  Thing bolt "the bolt on the holder's door" on holders_door {
    State home "The holder's door is bolted with a long iron pin, square in section, too heavy for the job, rusted where hands do not wear it.".
    Tries looking.
  }
  Discovery bolt_is_pin "The bolt on the holder's door in Ennick is a square iron pin, too heavy for a door: a sluice-gate pin.".
  Observe bolt_looked beside holders_door when tried(bolt, looking) "The pin is square in section, as thick as a thumb, with a hole through one end for a chain that is not there. It was made for a sluice-gate, not a door." teaches bolt_is_pin.

  Discovery prayer_heard "The Ennick holding prayer, spoken over each person as they are laid in the light: 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.' Held until the hour, keepers of the deep water watch; held until the hour, the light remembers." {
    Known by bren, ilis, mirel.
  }
  Topic bren_held with bren "Ask Bren about the held" when true once {
    Says "'They are alive,' says Bren. 'You can watch them breathe if you have the patience, and the felt. My father lies nine hundred paces in. A carrier who goes to him and back loses a night and an afternoon to it.' He looks at the map on the wall. 'Nobody held is woken without their own word. A held man cannot give it. So nobody is woken.'".
  }
  Topic bren_garret with bren "Tell Bren about Garret in the vault" when knows(actor, garret_held) once {
    Says "Bren hears you out. 'He was not laid,' he says. 'He walked into it, reaching for a jar. That is not holding, that is a man caught.' He nods slowly. 'Get him out. If you mean to go by the drain, take Mirel. She knows it.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(mirel, actor). }
  }
  Topic bren_prayer with bren "Ask Bren what is said when someone is laid" when true once {
    Says "Bren says it without thinking, the way a man says a thing he has said over his own father. 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.' Then, in Tovashi: 'Held until the hour, keepers of the deep water watch. Held until the hour, the light remembers.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, prayer_heard). }
  }
  Topic mirel_outfall with mirel "Ask Mirel about the Weeping Wall" when true once {
    Says "'It is the old drain,' says Mirel. 'It goes all the way under the heath to the city, nine kilometres, on your hands and knees. My grandfather went up it once. The flood closes it all summer, and opens it when the leaves turn.' She looks at your boots. 'Eight hours, wet. You come out in warm water, with eels.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, outfall_known). }
  }
  Topic ilis_held with ilis "Ask Ilis whether the held are truly alive" when true once {
    Says "'Ours breathe,' says Ilis. 'I have watched Doran take a breath every month for forty years, and it takes longer every year. The old ones further in, from before the Covering, do not breathe. Those are not ours.' She folds her hands. 'Ask me something else.'".
  }
  Topic ilis_prayer with ilis "Ask Ilis about the holding prayer" when true once {
    Says "Ilis says it, slowly, the way her mother taught her: 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.' She does not say what it means.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, prayer_heard). }
  }
  // What Ilis has not said in forty years: she says it to someone who has already seen it.
  Discovery prayer_label "The holding prayer is not a prayer. It is a Seridane granary formula, painted on the grain jars and said over each by the clerks: hold this one season, then give it out. The Holdfolk have been saying a label over their dying for three hundred years." {
    Known by ilis.
  }
  Topic ilis_jars with ilis "Tell Ilis about the words on the granary jars" when (knows(actor, jars_painted) or knows(actor, tally_words)) and knows(actor, prayer_heard) and not knows(actor, prayer_label) once {
    Says "Ilis puts down what she is holding. 'So you have seen the jars,' she says. 'The prior at Stairhead read them for me forty years ago. Hold one season, then issue. A grain jar's label.' She looks at the old cloak by the door. 'I said it over my husband. I have said it over half this village. I have never told Bren.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, prayer_label). }
  }
  // Or the company puts the two together itself: the clerk's line on the plate is the prayer.
  Observe prayer_recognised near party when knows(party, tally_words) and knows(party, prayer_heard) and not knows(party, prayer_label) "The clerk's line, said over each jar he counted in, is the line the Holdfolk say over their dying, word for word." teaches prayer_label.

  // The holders' cord and the glass: up the goat cleft from the terraces to the rim, and the red felt rope a hundred
  // paces from the edge of the light. At dusk the umber wolves come along the cord, and wait for whoever comes back
  // across it slowed.
  Place cord "the holders' cord" is room within fields at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place margin "the edge of the glass" is room within fields at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place near_held "three hundred paces in" is room within fields at 2, 1 outdoors.
  Place doran_place "Doran's brick" is room within fields at 3, 1 outdoors.
  Passage goat_cleft "the goat cleft" is path between terraces and cord taking 1 hour.
  Passage onto_glass "the edge of the glass" is path between cord and margin taking 10 minutes.
  Passage glass_in "the glass" is path between margin and near_held taking 30 minutes.
  Passage glass_deep "the glass, further in" is path between near_held and doran_place taking 1 hour.
  Initially Assert litGround(margin). Initially Assert litGround(near_held). Initially Assert litGround(doran_place).
  Observe cord_scene at cord when true "Red felt rope on iron pins runs along the heath a hundred paces short of the glass. A cairn stands where the path comes up, and people sit down at it whether they mean to or not.".
  Observe cord_night at cord when dark() "Past the cord your shadow changes: a second light, low and level, comes out of the east through the edge of the glass, and every shadow on the heath lies down pointing west.".
  Observe margin_scene at margin when true "The heath stops and the ground goes clear. There is no slope and no rim: sand and needlegrass, and then the sand is clear and the grass roots stand in it like hair in water. It has no temperature underfoot. Every shadow points west.".
  Observe near_scene at near_held when true "Umber bricks the size of loaves lie on the glass in a scatter, each with a knot cut in the top. Under each, a finger's depth down and more, someone lies on their back in the clear stone.".
  Observe doran_scene at doran_place when true "An umber brick with a holder's knot cut in it sits on the glass. Under it a man lies in a trench a little deeper than an arm is long, with his hands at his sides and his mouth a little open. The glass in front of his face has a fan of bright lines in it, where the sand was not quite clean.".
  Measure watchedDoran(group).
  Rule watching_doran when at(party, doran_place) and not benighted(party) { Increase watchedDoran(party) by 1. }
  Rule doran_reset when not at(party, doran_place) and watchedDoran(party) > 0 { Set watchedDoran(party) to 0. }
  Discovery doran_breathed "Doran, held forty years nine hundred paces into the glass, breathed: once, in most of an hour of watching." .
  Observe doran_breath at doran_place when watchedDoran(party) >= 5 and not knows(party, doran_breathed) "It begins so slowly that you could not say when it began. There is a time when his chest is down and a time when it is not, and between them the shirt lifts over the bone and the cloth draws tighter at the shoulder." teaches doran_breathed.

  Species umber_wolf "an umber wolf" like wolf temperament territorial
    described "A plateau wolf crusted iron-red to the shoulder from wallowing in umber mud, which lets it hunt an hour or two into the light.".
  Person wolves "the umber wolves" at cord {
    Role "a pack of umber wolves, the colour of the cliffs". Species umber_wolf. Numbers 4.
    Seen when dark().
    Warns "On the far side of the cord, in the juniper, four of them stand still that were not standing there before. They walk when you walk, twenty paces off, keeping level.".
  }
  // They do not come at a company that can run. They come at one that cannot.
  Initially Assert tolerates(wolves, party).
  Rule wolves_close when dark() and at(party, cord) and slowedCompany(party) and tolerates(wolves, party) and not cairnLit(party) and not travelsWith(mirel, party) says "The wolves have stopped keeping level. They are coming in." {
    Retract tolerates(wolves, party). Assert assails(wolves, party). }
  Rule wolves_wait when not dark() and not tolerates(wolves, party) and not assails(wolves, party) { Assert tolerates(wolves, party). }

  // The Sluice sends its water down the Outfall to the Weeping Wall, and from there onto the lower road.
  Rule road_washes when sluiced(flood_water) and not washedOut(lower_road) and hour(clock) == 5 says "Down in Ennick, at first light, the Weeping Wall comes down in spate, red with mud, and goes over the lower road." { Assert washedOut(lower_road). }
}

data/adventures/patient-star/hour.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Granaries' landward rooms, and the Hour: Tamaun's lowest level, 130 to 210 metres down, flooded outside the
  // mantle the Late Sun has boiled dry, and 40 to 60 degrees inside it (Tamaun, H1 to H6).
  Place hour "the Hour" is level within tamaun.
  Place watch_room "the Watch Room" is room within granaries at 0, 0 underground.
  Place steam_top "the head of the Steam Stair" is room within granaries at 2, 0 underground.
  Place listening_hall "the Waiting Hall" is room within hour at 1, 0 underground.
  Place hot_gallery "the hot gallery" is room within hour at 1, 1 underground.
  Place last_hour "the Last Hour" is room within hour at 0, 1 underground.
  Place coverers_works "the Coverers' Works" is room within hour at 2, 1 underground.
  Place stair_wall "the Wall of the Stair" is room within hour at 3, 1 underground.
  Place courses_face "the Courses" is room within hour at 1, 2 underground.

  Passage watch_door "the Watch Room arch" is arch between ring and watch_room.
  Passage to_steam "the passage to the Steam Stair" is passage between ring and steam_top taking 3 minutes.
  Passage steam_stair "the Steam Stair" is stair between steam_top and listening_hall taking 20 minutes.
  // In autumn the flood falls, and a swimmer can go down the flooded stairs from the Flood Line to the Hall (G4).
  Passage flood_swim "the flooded stairs" is passage between flood_line and listening_hall taking 20 minutes
    opening when flood(flood_water) < 60 "The flooded stairs go down into water too hot to bear past the first turn.".
  Passage hot_way "the hot gallery" is passage between listening_hall and hot_gallery taking 5 minutes.
  Passage chamber_door "the bronze door of the Last Hour" is doorway between hot_gallery and last_hour.
  Passage works_way "the rammed-clay passage" is passage between hot_gallery and coverers_works taking 5 minutes.
  Passage archive_door "the Coverers' archive door" is door between coverers_works and stair_wall.
  Passage courses_way "the lowest gallery" is passage between hot_gallery and courses_face taking 5 minutes.
  Initially Assert darkRoom(watch_room). Initially Assert darkRoom(steam_top). Initially Assert darkRoom(hot_gallery).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(coverers_works). Initially Assert darkRoom(stair_wall).
  // The Waiting Hall is lit from below, through its glass floor; the Last Hour by its channel; the Courses by their
  // own light.
  Initially Assert litGround(courses_face).

  Observe watch_room_scene at watch_room when true "A guardroom with an Office lamp, a table, a ledger and a cot, the blanket on it turned down and never slept in. A bronze bell hangs on a cord that runs up a stair cut in red clay.".
  Discovery kings_book "The King's Book: the Office clerk's record of the old king below, written three days a month. In Haysel he answered at about a sixth of a man's speed and asked for honey and for his daughter by name." {
    Source kings_book_copy "the King's Book" at watch_room readable by party.
  }

  // H1: the Steam Stair. A blast comes up the tube about every fifty minutes, after twenty breaths of hissing; six
  // niches give room for two. A company that watches one cycle can time the run.
  Thing steam "the steam in the stair" on steam_stair is scenery {
    State quiet "The Steam Stair spirals down inside a tube of red ceramic, wet and hot through boot leather. Six niches are cut in its wall, scratched with tally marks.".
    State hissing "A hiss is rising from below in the Steam Stair, louder with each breath.".
    State blasting dangerous "A blast of steam roars up the Steam Stair and out of its head in a white column.".
    Hurts with scald when blasting then quiet.
  }
  Hazard scald "a blast of steam" means "Deal (2d6) fire damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13).".
  Measure steamTick(entity).
  Rule steam_ticks when state(steam, ?s) { Increase steamTick(steam) by 1. }
  Rule steam_hisses when steamTick(steam) == 4 and state(steam, quiet) { Assert state(steam, hissing). }
  Rule steam_blasts when steamTick(steam) == 5 and state(steam, hissing) { Assert state(steam, blasting). }
  Rule steam_spent when steamTick(steam) >= 6 { Set steamTick(steam) to 0. Assert state(steam, quiet). }
  // Half way down when the hiss starts: the blast finds whoever started down hissing.
  Rule caught_on_stair when tookWay(?c, steam_stair) and company(?c) and state(steam, blasting) and not niched(?c) {
    Assert strikes(scald, ?c). Assert niched(?c). }
  Relation niched(group).
  Rule niche_clears when niched(?c) and not tookWay(?c, steam_stair) { Retract niched(?c). }
  Discovery steam_timed "The Steam Stair blasts about every fifty minutes, after twenty breaths of hissing; the niches hold two each.".
  Observe steam_learned at steam_top when state(steam, blasting) and not knows(party, steam_timed) "The blast comes up out of the stair-head in a column you could lean on, and is gone. You count, after: it is near enough fifty minutes to the next, and the hiss before it is twenty breaths long." teaches steam_timed.

  // H2: the Waiting Hall, and the Waiting who listen there without leave.
  Observe hall_scene_h at listening_hall when true "A round chamber with a stillglass floor, very warm. Light comes up through the floor from below, and lies on the undersides of things.".
  Person listeners "six of the Waiting" at listening_hall {
    Role "six Listeners of the Waiting, on felt mats with their ears to the glass". Ancestry human. Numbers 6. Peaceable.
    Wants night_honey.
  }
  Observe tone_heard at listening_hall when hour(clock) == 12 or hour(clock) == 0 "Through the floor, far below, a single low note sounds, and goes on in the bones after it has stopped. The Listeners look at one another and say nothing.".
  Discovery tone_below "Since 378 a low tone sounds from deep below the Pit once an hour; the Waiting have heard it, and told no one.".
  Topic listeners_tone with listeners "Ask the Listeners what they hear" when true once {
    Says "'Nothing, since the year 71,' says a woman with wax in her hair. 'Not the Voice.' She looks at the others. 'Since 78, when the growth broke into the lowest gallery and let the air carry it, there is a note. Once an hour. Deep. It is not a syllable. It is not anything.' She presses her ear back to the glass. 'Ruan does not know yet. Do not tell the Office.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, tone_below). }
  }
  Topic listeners_names with listeners "Ask the Listeners what they are copying" when true once {
    Says "'The Waking Ward names,' says a young man, and turns his tablet so you can see the columns. 'Every name has its syllable. Read in the order they were given, they are the Voice, before anyone counted.' He taps one column. 'And these are the hour-names the sick counted their time by. Twelve of them, round and round.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ward_names). }
  }
  Discovery ward_names "The Waking Ward names, copied in order: each carries its Voice syllable, and among them the twelve Seridane hour-names the sick counted time by.".

  // H3: the Last Hour, and Amaru, ninth Dane of the Hour, waking. His rate goes from a sixth to a third, to a half, to a
  // man's speed, by the week (Amaru's waking).
  Observe last_hour_scene at last_hour when true "A domed chamber tiled in bronze, its ceiling pierced by a stillglass rod as thick as a forearm. Grey light comes down the rod and spreads weakly. Couches stand round the walls, and honey jars lie about, all open and scraped clean.".
  Person amaru "Amaru" at last_hour {
    Role "the ninth Dane of the Hour, in a robe gone colourless". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Wants night_honey.
    Objects "Amaru's eyes come round to his seal in your hands, over a long time. When his voice arrives it is very quiet. 'Put it back.'".
  }
  Person kesset "Kesset" at last_hour {
    Role "the Dane's chamberlain, on a couch in the shadow". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Calling bard. Plans 14 steps. Uses go.
    Joins "Kesset gets up as a young man would and an old man feels it. 'I will find Halu,' he says. 'And I will tell you what the doors say.'".
  }
  Measure amaruRate(group).
  Initially Set amaruRate(amaru) to 6.
  Rule amaru_third when day(clock) >= 29 and amaruRate(amaru) == 6 { Set amaruRate(amaru) to 3. }
  Rule amaru_half when day(clock) >= 71 and amaruRate(amaru) == 3 { Set amaruRate(amaru) to 2. }
  Rule amaru_whole when day(clock) >= 127 and amaruRate(amaru) == 2 { Set amaruRate(amaru) to 1. }
  Initially Assert asleep(kesset).
  Rule kesset_wakes when day(clock) >= 36 and asleep(kesset) { Retract asleep(kesset). Assert willing(kesset, party). }
  Observe amaru_sixth near amaru when amaruRate(amaru) == 6 "When you step closer, the old man's eyes come round to you over several seconds. His lips begin a word, and you wait a long time for the rest of it.".
  Observe amaru_third_seen near amaru when amaruRate(amaru) == 3 "The old man in the chair turns his head toward you at a third of a man's speed, and his hands are shaking, and not with age.".
  Observe amaru_half_seen near amaru when amaruRate(amaru) == 2 "The old king watches you come in with something like anger. He is quicker now; quick enough to argue.".
  Observe amaru_awake near amaru when amaruRate(amaru) == 1 "An old man sits in a dead city in a chair too big for him, at a man's speed, and looks at you.".
  // What he says, by how far he has woken: formal, then hungry and afraid, then disbelieving, then an old man.
  Topic amaru_first with amaru "Speak to the king" when amaruRate(amaru) == 6 once {
    Says "It takes him half a minute to say what would take you five seconds, and you wait for every word. 'You are not of my household.' A long time. 'Where is my daughter? Where is the honey? Tell the granary-keepers to come to me.' His eyes close and open, slowly. 'Is the Voice still speaking?'".
  }
  Topic amaru_hungry with amaru "Speak to the king" when amaruRate(amaru) == 3 once {
    Says "'The honey is gone,' says Amaru, as if you had taken it. 'The household is hungry. Kesset is too thin.' His eyes go to the empty couch. 'Halu went up for bread. She has not come back.' He grips the arm of the chair. 'What year is it, above?'".
  }
  Topic amaru_year with amaru "Tell the king what year it is" when amaruRate(amaru) <= 3 once {
    Says "You tell him: the three hundred and eightieth since the Unlidding; sixteen hundred and forty since the Covering. Amaru looks at you a long time. 'Some weeks,' he says. 'It has been some weeks.' He does not believe you, and you can see him deciding not to.".
  }
  Topic amaru_hour with amaru "Ask the king whether the hour was given" when true once {
    Says "'It was given,' says Amaru, as slowly as he has said anything. 'The lake asked for an hour and the hour came down. It speaks to the keepers, one sound in each moon.' His eyes are steady. 'My daughter says it fell. My daughter is a clerk.'".
  }
  Topic amaru_stone with amaru "Ask the king about a stone that sings" when amaruRate(amaru) <= 3 once {
    Says "Something moves in his face. 'There is no stone,' he says. 'There is the hour.' He looks at the rod of light over him. 'I have heard it sixteen hundred years. It is the hour's own heart. It is mine.'".
  }
  Topic amaru_daughter with amaru "Tell the king how his daughter died" when knows(actor, selane_murdered) once {
    Says "You tell him what the Wall of the Stair says. Amaru hears it out without moving at all, which at his speed is no sign of anything. Then he closes his eyes, and keeps them closed so long that you think he has gone back into the light. 'Loyal men,' he says. 'Loyal to me.' When he opens his eyes he takes the seal off its stand and holds it out to you. 'Open her doors,' he says. 'All of them.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(amaru, seal, actor). Retract inside(seal, seal_stand). Assert at(seal, last_hour). Assert grieves(amaru). }
  }
  Relation grieves(group).
  Event amaru_honey near amaru when keeps(amaru, ?j) and itemKind(?j, night_honey) "It takes the king a long time to lift the jar, and longer to open it. He eats with two fingers, slowly, and gives the rest to Kesset without being asked." then { Assert fed(amaru). }
  Relation fed(group).

  // His seal, the Long Hour on its stand, and the royal seed behind his chair.
  Kind amaru_seal "Amaru's seal" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A palm-sized stillglass plate. Drawn past a stylus it says, in an old man's voice, a name and one syllable.".
  Kind long_hour_plates "the Long Hour" is treasure worth 600 weighing 12
    described "About five thousand syllables of the Voice on stillglass plates, the Seridane transcript of the Long Hour.".
  Kind royal_seed "a jar of royal seed barley" is treasure worth 200 weighing 2
    described "Barley held in the light for sixteen hundred years and alive.".
  Thing seal_stand "the stand beside the chair" at last_hour {
    Holds.
    State standing "A stand of stillglass plates stands beside the chair: the Long Hour, and on top, a single palm-sized plate.".
  }
  Item seal "Amaru's seal" is amaru_seal in seal_stand owned by amaru.
  Item long_hour "the Long Hour" is long_hour_plates in seal_stand owned by amaru.
  Thing niche "a sealed niche behind the chair" at last_hour {
    Holds.
    State sealed closed "A niche is sealed into the wall behind the chair with red clay, and stamped.".
    State opened "The sealed niche behind the chair stands open.".
    Change break_niche "Break the clay seal on the niche" from sealed to opened needing digging.
  }
  Item seed_jar "a jar of royal seed barley" is royal_seed in niche owned by amaru.
  Discovery long_hour_read "The Long Hour, read: about five thousand syllables of the Voice, in order. Laid as the citadel was built, one course to a syllable, they are a plan of the Undersun's Seridane Reach.".
  Thing reading_stand "the Long Hour on its stand" at last_hour is scenery {
    State shelved "The plates of the Long Hour are racked in order, and a stylus hangs on a cord beside them.".
    State read "The plates of the Long Hour have been read through, and are a little out of order.".
    Change read_plates "Read the Long Hour through with a stylus" from shelved to read needing stylus.
  }
  Observe long_hour_known at last_hour when state(reading_stand, read) "Syllable after syllable, an hour and more of them. Where a syllable is open the course it laid is open; where it is closed, solid; where it repeats, a stair." teaches long_hour_read.
  Rule bren_seed when keeps(bren, ?j) and itemKind(?j, royal_seed) and not seeded(ennick) { Assert seeded(ennick). }
  Relation seeded(place).
  Event bren_seed_told near bren when seeded(ennick) "Bren holds the jar to the light and pours a little into his palm. 'Alive,' he says. 'Sixteen hundred years, and alive.' He does not thank you; he asks what you need.".

  // H4: the Coverers' Works and the Plumb, Selane's borehole, 400 metres toward the stone that sings.
  Observe works_scene at coverers_works when true "Walls of rammed red clay block three passages. In the middle of the floor a round shaft half a metre across goes straight down, lined with clear glass. Over it stand a bronze winch and a frame of rods.".
  Observe plumb_note at coverers_works when hour(clock) == 12 or hour(clock) == 0 "With an ear to the liner you hear it: a long low note, coming up four hundred metres of glass.".
  // A sounding lock: twelve stillglass rods, rung in the order of the hour-names carved over the door (Sounding
  // locks). Three wrong attempts in an hour drop the counterweight; it must then be dug out.
  Thing sounding_lock "the sounding lock" on archive_door {
    State shut blocking "Over the Coverers' archive door seven symbols of the sun's place are carved in a row; a row of short stillglass rods is set in the frame.".
    State jammed blocking "The counterweight has dropped into its locked seat. The door will have to be dug out.".
    State released "The archive door stands open on its counterweight.".
    Change ring_names "Ring the hour-names in the carved order" from shut to released after learning hour_names.
    Change ring_seal "Draw Amaru's seal past the rods" from shut to released needing seal.
    Change dig_out "Dig the counterweight out of its seat" from jammed to shut needing digging.
  }
  Measure misses(entity).
  Action ring_guess(actor: group, site: place) "Ring the rods in an order you guess" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, coverers_works) and state(sounding_lock, shut)
      and not knows(actor, hour_names).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Increase misses(sounding_lock) by 1. }
    Result "The rods ring, one after another, and the bar does not drop.".
  }
  Rule lock_jams when misses(sounding_lock) >= 3 and state(sounding_lock, shut) says "Something heavy drops inside the door frame with a sound like a dropped anvil." {
    Assert state(sounding_lock, jammed). Set misses(sounding_lock) to 0. }
  Discovery hour_names "The twelve Seridane hour-names, in order and with their pitches: what the sounding locks are keyed to.".
  Discovery rhyme_known "The Weirs' counting rhyme for the cranes: twelve words in a ring.".
  // Any two of the three sources give the names (the Weirs' rhyme, the Ward names, the Plate Hall song).
  Observe names_assembled near party when not knows(party, hour_names) and ((knows(party, rhyme_known) and knows(party, ward_names)) or (knows(party, rhyme_known) and knows(party, song_heard)) or (knows(party, ward_names) and knows(party, song_heard))) "The Weirs' twelve counting words, the twelve names the sick counted by, the children's twelve on the plate: they are one ring of hour-names, and you have them in order." teaches hour_names.

  // H5: the Wall of the Stair. A Coverer's record of Selane's last weeks; beneath it, folded, her Veil.
  Thing stair_record "the Wall of the Stair" at stair_wall {
    State silent "A single chant-wall two metres long, untouched, in a small chamber.".
    State playing "A woman's voice, faint, steady: the grain riots, Selane's order to open the reserve vaults, and her murder at the top of the Stair, by men of her father's party, who told the city it was the mob. Then the names of the men.".
    Change play_record "Draw a stylus along the Wall of the Stair" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Rule record_ends when state(stair_record, playing) and not at(party, stair_wall) { Assert state(stair_record, silent). }
  Discovery selane_murdered "Selane did not die in the grain riots: Answerer loyalists killed her at the top of the Stair and told the city it was the mob.".
  Observe record_heard at stair_wall when state(stair_record, playing) "A Coverer cut this, the year Tamaun emptied." teaches selane_murdered.
  Kind veil_kind "Selane's Veil" like cloak_of_protection worth 0 weighing 0
    described "Lace of drawn barrow-iron wire, three hundred grams, which covers its wearer from head to waist. Nothing said under it can be taken.".
  Initially Assert shields(veil_kind).
  Item veil "Selane's Veil" is veil_kind at stair_wall.
  Observe veil_seen at stair_wall when at(veil, stair_wall) "Folded on the floor beneath the wall lies a square of dark iron lace.".

  // H6: the Courses, the growth beneath the Late Sun breaking into the city. Saro opens them; a Mason's trowel does.
  Observe courses_scene at courses_face when true "At the bottom of the passage the wall is not stone. Bands of dark metal and clear glass are laid in perfect courses without a seam. Light runs inside them along their curves, around the corner of the passage. A cutter's boot sticks out of the third course.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/keeping.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Keeping (Tier IV): the plane where every moment of Imbar's past is kept, as a place. Geography is chronology:
  // walking inward goes back in time, walking across goes elsewhere in Imbar at the same moment. Near the shore a
  // careful walker covers a year in an hour; in deep time, where less happened, a thousand. Time passes for visitors
  // at its ordinary rate, and Imbar's clocks run while they are away.
  Place keeping "the Keeping" is plane.
  Place kept_imbar "the Keeping of Imbar" is region within keeping.
  Place shore "the shore of the present" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 0, 0.
  Place kept_plateau "the plateau's past" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 1, 0.
  Place hollows "the Quarried Reaches" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 1, 1.
  Place deep_time "deep time" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 2, 0.
  Place far_east "far east of Imbar's known lands" is wilderness within kept_imbar at 2, 1.
  Place wall_site "the Outer Wall" is site within kept_imbar at 3, 0.

  Place tideline "the Tideline" is room within shore at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place collar_years "the Collar's years" is room within kept_plateau at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place year_zero "the night of the Unlidding" is room within kept_plateau at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place covering_years "the Covering" is room within kept_plateau at 2, 0 outdoors.
  Place stair_murder "the top of the Stair, 1,575 BP" is room within kept_plateau at 2, 1 outdoors.
  Place new_moons "the new moons" is room within kept_plateau at 3, 0 outdoors.
  Place kept_fall "the fall" is room within kept_plateau at 4, 0 outdoors.
  Place quarry_edge "a quarried hollow" is room within hollows at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place descent_k "the Descent" is room within deep_time at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place separation "the Separation" is room within deep_time at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place absence "an absence" is room within far_east at 0, 0.
  Place outer_wall "the Outer Wall" is room within wall_site at 0, 0 outdoors.

  // In: a living hand on Ithmar, with whoever touches that person. Out: walk back to the shore and step through.
  // Without Ithmar, only where you came in; with it, anywhere.
  Relation cameInAt(group, place).
  Action touch_ithmar(actor: group, site: place) "Lay a hand on Ithmar" {
    Description "A living hand that touches Ithmar enters the Keeping, together with anyone touching that person, at the moment and place of the touch.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, arbiter_vault)
      and (inside(ithmar, cage) or carries(actor, ithmar)).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract at(actor, arbiter_vault). Assert at(actor, tideline). Assert cameInAt(actor, arbiter_vault). }
    Result "The jewel is not cold, or warm. The white room goes on being there and you are not in it: you stand on a shore where the present is setting like wet sand.".
  }
  Passage step_back "the way you came in" is passage between tideline and arbiter_vault taking 10 minutes.
  Relation keepingWay(passage).
  Passage out_quell "out into Quell, now" is passage between tideline and square taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "The shore runs on, every place of Imbar this minute, soft as wet sand. Without the jewel you cannot step out anywhere but where you came in.".
  Passage out_orrel "out into New Orrel, now" is passage between tideline and no_market taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "Without the jewel there is no stepping out here.".
  Passage out_ennick "out into Ennick, now" is passage between tideline and lower_road taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "Without the jewel there is no stepping out here.".
  Passage out_stairhead "out at Stairhead, now" is passage between tideline and stair_top taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "Without the jewel there is no stepping out here.".
  Passage out_corbel "out at the Corbel's tip, at the moment it came" is passage between collar_years and lintel_room taking 10 minutes one way
    opening when carries(party, ithmar) "In the year 71 something comes down the light out of the black, and stops in the cloud. Without the jewel, you can only watch it come.".
  Initially Assert keepingWay(out_quell). Initially Assert keepingWay(out_orrel). Initially Assert keepingWay(out_ennick).
  Initially Assert keepingWay(out_stairhead). Initially Assert keepingWay(out_corbel).
  // Every step through the Keeping with the jewel lays one of the wearer's own moments into its setting: a memory gone,
  // and everyone else forgets that moment too.
  Relation stepPaid(group, passage).
  Rule step_costs when tookWay(?c, ?w) and keepingWay(?w) and carries(?c, ithmar) and not stepPaid(?c, ?w) and memories(?c) >= 1
    says "Something of yours goes into the jewel's setting as you step: a morning, a face, a word somebody said once. You do not know which. Nobody does." {
    Decrease memories(?c) by 1. Assert stepPaid(?c, ?w). }
  Rule step_paid_clears when stepPaid(?c, ?w) and not tookWay(?c, ?w) { Retract stepPaid(?c, ?w). }
  Observe no_past near party when memories(party) == 0 "You have stepped so often that there is almost nothing behind you. You remember Saro. You do not remember why.".

  // Inward: back in time. Near the shore, a year an hour.
  Passage to_collar_years "inland, thirty years" is path between tideline and collar_years taking 32 hours.
  Passage to_year_zero "inland, three hundred and fifty years" is path between collar_years and year_zero taking 14 days.
  Passage to_covering "inland, through the craneless centuries" is path between year_zero and covering_years taking 3 days.
  Passage to_murder "across, to the Stair" is path between covering_years and stair_murder taking 4 hours.
  Passage to_moons "inland, through Tamaun's seven centuries" is path between covering_years and new_moons taking 10 days.
  Passage walk_moons "the new moons, walked a minute a moon" is path between new_moons and kept_fall taking 60 hours.
  Passage to_hollows "across, into the blank" is path between collar_years and quarry_edge taking 2 hours.
  // Deep time, where there are no landmarks: without the Tally or a guide, years of wandering.
  Passage to_descent "inland, into deep time" is path between kept_fall and descent_k taking 30 hours needing tally_kind or wayfinding.
  Passage to_separation "inland, to the Separation" is path between descent_k and separation taking 2 hours.
  Passage to_absence "across, far to the east" is path between descent_k and absence taking 2 days needing tally_kind or wayfinding.
  Passage to_wall "inland, before the beginning" is path between separation and outer_wall taking 4 hours.
  Initially Assert keepingWay(to_collar_years). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_year_zero). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_covering).
  Initially Assert keepingWay(to_murder). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_moons). Initially Assert keepingWay(walk_moons).
  Initially Assert keepingWay(to_hollows). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_descent). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_separation).
  Initially Assert keepingWay(to_absence). Initially Assert keepingWay(to_wall).
  Action wander(actor: group, site: place) "Strike out into deep time without the Tally or a guide" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, kept_fall)
      and not holding(actor, tally_kind) and not capable(actor, wayfinding).
    Time 144.
    On success { Assert strikes(archivore_bite, actor). }
    Result "There are no landmarks. You walk a day and do not know if it was a day or a century, and something like a page turning follows you, and bites.".
  }

  // K1: the Tideline. Everything in Imbar that is happening now is here, still soft: a scrying ground.
  Observe tideline_scene at tideline when true "A shore where the present is setting, like wet sand hardening. Everything in Imbar that is happening now is here, still soft; you can walk across it and see any place you choose, as it is this minute.".
  Observe tide_orrel at tideline when at(amaru, barracks) "In New Orrel, this minute, an old king lies on a cot under three blankets and looks at a ceiling.".
  Observe tide_crew at tideline when argued(crew) and asleep(garret) "In the Granary Ring, this minute, two cutters sit with their backs to the wall by the ninth vault, waiting.".
  Observe tide_corbel at tideline when not docked(corbel_site) "Over the Pit, this minute, the Corbel is two metres lower than it was yesterday.".
  Observe tide_concord at tideline when convened(chapter) "In Stairhead's chapter house, this minute, the Concord is sitting, and nobody is sitting next to anybody they can help it.".
  Observe tide_saro at tideline when not travelsWith(saro, party) "At the Tip of the Undersun, this minute, a woman with no temperature lays a course and calls its syllable.".
  // Standing still on the Tideline, a visitor begins to set into the present.
  Measure tideWatches(group).
  Rule tide_counts when at(party, tideline) { Increase tideWatches(party) by 1. }
  Rule tide_resets when not at(party, tideline) and tideWatches(party) > 0 { Set tideWatches(party) to 0. }
  Observe tide_setting near party when at(party, tideline) and tideWatches(party) >= 4 "Your feet have sunk into the shore to the ankle, and it is hardening around them. Your own hand, when you lift it, comes up slowly.".
  Rule tide_takes when at(party, tideline) and tideWatches(party) >= 6 and not setInPresent(party) says "The present sets around you, and you are kept." {
    Assert setInPresent(party). Assert hobbled(party). }
  Relation setInPresent(group).
  Person shore_remembrancer "a Remembrancer of the shore" at tideline {
    Role "a servant of the Virina, tall, made of the sound of bells". Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Wants quarried_moment.
  }
  Topic shore_quarried with shore_remembrancer "Ask the Remembrancer about the hollows" when true once {
    Says "'Cut,' says the Remembrancer, in bells. 'Carried out of the Keeping into the Masonry. Bring back what was cut, and we will set it again where it was kept, and it will be remembered.'".
  }
  Event moment_returned near shore_remembrancer when keeps(shore_remembrancer, ?q) and itemKind(?q, quarried_moment) "The Remembrancer takes the moment between two long fingers and sets it into the shore, somewhere inland, and in Imbar a season that nobody could remember is remembered again.".
  Rule dane_returned when keeps(shore_remembrancer, dane_moment) and not reanchored(fourth_dane) { Assert reanchored(fourth_dane). }

  // K2: the plateau's past.
  Observe collar_years_scene at collar_years when true "Inland from the shore the plateau gets younger: the Collar going up, then a storm, then down; carts; the Breach opening in a white roar of steam and coming back closed; Quell growing smaller.".
  Observe year_zero_scene at year_zero when true "A night of steam. Half of a town going into a hole in the ground. Then the light comes up out of the old Clear Fields everywhere at once, and sixty people at a fair stop where they stand, and their kin come with sand.".
  Observe covering_scene at covering_years when true "Thousands of people carrying red clay in baskets, for years, into a pit; and then the last light cut, and in the glass of the fields, all at once, eleven thousand people wake in the dark.".
  // The murder at the Stair: walked through, it plays; given time by touch, the faces.
  Observe murder_scene at stair_murder when true "The top of the falls at night, in riot-time. A young woman in a council robe on the path, and four men coming up behind her who are not rioters.".
  Thing murderers "the four men on the path" at stair_murder {
    State coming "Four men in Answerer badges come up the path behind Selane, hands under their cloaks.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(murderers).
  Observe murder_seen near murderers when touched(murderers) "For the length of your touch it plays: they reach her, and the knives come out, and one of them says the Dane's name as if it were a prayer. When they turn to go you see their faces, and their badges." teaches selane_murdered.
  // The new moons: the Voice's syllables as they were spoken, one at each new moon since the fall. Walking the first
  // three centuries of them recovers the Crown's plan, and the first syllable.
  Observe moons_scene at new_moons when true "Moonless nights, one after another, inland, each with a single sound passing through the rock near a young pit: a syllable, felt in the knees.".
  Observe moons_walked at kept_fall when not knows(party, crown_map) "Sixty hours of moonless nights, a syllable each, and you have them all in order: the Crown's plan, the Voice's first three hundred years." teaches crown_map.
  Observe first_from_moons at kept_fall when not knows(party, first_syllable) "The first of them you will not forget: it was the first sound the seed made in the world." teaches first_syllable.
  Discovery delver_seen "At the fall, riding the seed's wake out of a clear sky, very small: a figure with a trowel, the first Mason, who laid the First Course and went down into the dark with the stem.".
  Observe fall_scene_k at kept_fall when true "An autumn night out of a clear sky; a light coming down; the lake villages watching. Riding its wake, very small, visible only to someone looking for it, is a figure with a trowel." teaches delver_seen.

  // K3: the Quarried Reaches: blankness, a fog in which things have no reasons; Masons cutting at the edges.
  Observe hollow_scene at quarry_edge when true "History stops here. Not darkness: blankness, a fog in which things have no reasons. A road goes into it and does not come out. At its edges, figures with trowels are cutting, and the cut edges are clean.".
  Person cutters "a crew of Masons, cutting" at quarry_edge {
    Role "three Masons at the edge of the blank, cutting a season out of the plateau's last year". Ancestry human. Numbers 3. Peaceable.
  }
  Relation cutStopped(place).
  Topic cutters_stop with cutters "Ask the Masons to stop cutting" when true once {
    Says "They stop, because you asked, and look at you with honest puzzlement. 'It is the work,' says one. 'If we do not, another crew will.' But they put their trowels down, and that season stays where it is.".
    On discuss { Assert cutStopped(quarry_edge). }
  }
  Person clea "Clea Keddle" at quarry_edge {
    Role "a Haldrish seer, lost, who walks here in her sleep". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Joins "'I know the way inward,' says Clea, 'better than anyone living. I have been lost in it for forty years.' She takes your sleeve like a child.".
  }
  Initially Assert willing(clea, party).
  Topic clea_where with clea "Tell Clea Keddle where she is" when true once {
    Says "'The Keeping,' she says after you, as if it were a word in a dream. 'I have always called it the long country.' She looks at her hands. 'Something bites me here. A little, every night, for forty years.' She does not know that her body is dying in a bed in Sorne, and you do not tell her.".
  }
  // Archivores: the Keeping's predators. They feed on what belongs to no moment, and cannot enter one that is playing.
  Species archivore "an archivore" like wraith temperament ambush
    described "A flat shape like a page turning, seen edge-on as a line. A bite takes time from the rest of a life: a day for a graze, years for a deep wound.".
  Person archivores "archivores" at quarry_edge { Role "two flat shapes like pages turning". Species archivore. Numbers 2. }
  Hazard archivore_bite "an archivore's bite" means "Deal (2d8) necrotic damage to ally unless wisdom save against (14).".
  Measure yearsTaken(group).

  // K4: deep time. The Descent, and the Separation: the most dangerous place, and the most valuable.
  Observe descent_scene at descent_k when true "A night sky full of falling fire, every fall stopped, and the land under it burning.".
  Thing falling_fire "the falling fire" at descent_k { State falling "Fire hangs in the sky, coming down.". }
  Initially Assert kept(falling_fire).
  Hazard landed "a falling thing, landing" means "Deal (4d6) fire damage to ally unless dexterity save against (15).".
  Rule fire_lands when touched(falling_fire) says "For the length of your touch it falls, and lands." { Retract touched(falling_fire). Assert strikes(landed, party). }
  Observe separation_scene at separation when true "A sky divided: half full of figures with light for wings, half full of figures of darkness and hooks, all stopped in the act of striking, across a distance the eye cannot measure. Below them, tall robed figures in white stand in a ring, holding the world apart like the pages of a book. In the centre of the ring a hand is setting a jewel into stone.".
  Thing blows "the war overhead" at separation { State struck "Every blow overhead is stopped an inch from landing.". }
  Initially Assert kept(blows).
  Hazard unmaking "a blow of the Separation" means "Deal (10d10) force damage to ally.".
  Rule blow_lands when touched(blows) says "You touch a blow that nearly unmade the world, and for a moment it goes on." { Retract touched(blows). Assert strikes(unmaking, party). }
  Discovery sigils_known "How the sigils on Ithmar are cut, and so how a binding is made: watched at the Separation, stroke by stroke, a hand setting a jewel into stone.".
  Relation watchedBinding(group).
  Action watch_binding(actor: group, site: place) "Watch the hand in the ring cut the sigils, stroke by stroke" {
    Description "Walk slowly round the ring, letting the moment play, and do not touch anything.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, separation) and not watchedBinding(actor)
      and not benighted(actor).
    Time 12.
    On success { Assert watchedBinding(actor). }
    Result "You walk the ring for two hours, slowly, so that it plays and does not stop, and you watch a hand cut the sigils on a jewel into its setting, one stroke at a time, until you could do it.".
  }
  Observe binding_learned near party when watchedBinding(party) and not knows(party, sigils_known) "You have the strokes. You know how it is bound; and so how it could be bound tighter." teaches sigils_known.

  // K5: an absence. Saro, at the last moment she still had; around her, nothing.
  Observe absence_scene at absence when true "A mountain hall, ages ago, and a woman standing in it with a jewel at her throat. Around her, in every direction, the Keeping is empty: a hole shaped like a life.".
  Discovery saro_remembers "Saro has seen herself: a woman who wore a Kiritarun, and spent her whole past using it, and was taken. She remembers her name.".
  Observe saro_sees at absence when travelsWith(saro, party) and not knows(party, saro_remembers) "Saro does not move from in front of the woman with the jewel. 'That is mine,' she says, the way she said it of the niche. Then, very quietly, she says a name, and it is not Saro, and she weeps, which she did not know how to do." teaches saro_remembers.

  // K6: the Outer Wall: the quarry face, and the road to the Masonry.
  Observe wall_scene_k at outer_wall when true "At the far inland edge, before the beginning, a wall. Through it, moments are being carried out on long tendrils of course-work into black.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/kept_season:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  Description "The twelfth word: a vault with no number, a clerk kept at his board, a man held forty years who may be called back, a lamp in a cairn, and what each calling makes of the places between.".

  // ── The Account, here ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Count: the held, by seasons. Keeper: the Holdfolk, who say eleven words over each laying and stop where they were taught
  // to stop. First page: the twelfth word, which the Seridane clerk said over every jar and which was never the Holdfolk's
  // to say, because it was an order and not a prayer. Price of reading: the word, said over a held man, works; and what it
  // works is that he is a man of eighty again, and in a world that has gone on.

  // ── Voices ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation kvCleat(group). Relation kvDoran(group). Relation kvCord(group). Relation kvPit(group). Relation kvLintel(group). Relation kvTide(group).
  Relation sawSecondBolt(group).

  // The thief sees what the vault doors do not say. This one beat is a way in that nobody else has.
  Rule voice_cleat at ring when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, ring) and not benighted(party) and not kvCleat(party)
    says "{?m} runs a thumb round the bronze cleat by the ninth vault and then along the wall, doorway by doorway, lips moving. 'Polished on the near side, every one,' {?m} says. 'Left hand, season after season. That is a job. Somebody drew a wage for it.' The thumb stops at a cleat with no door under it. 'And this one is polished too. See the lime? Same wash as the wall, only newer.' {?m} tips the head back. 'And the second bolt is up in the lintel, where nobody looks. Which is where I would put it.'" {
    Assert kvCleat(party). Assert sawSecondBolt(party).
  }
  Rule voice_doran at doran_place when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, doran_place) and not kvDoran(party)
    says "{?m} kneels by the brick and lays a palm on the knot cut in it. 'I have said the office over a hundred people,' {?m} says. 'Every rite ends. It tells the dead they may go, or tells the living they may stop.' {?m} listens to the line the clerk's mouth is shaped around. 'The words they say over him end neither way. That is not a prayer. That is a question left standing.'" {
    Assert kvDoran(party).
  }
  Rule voice_cord at cord when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and awake(?m) and at(party, cord) and not kvCord(party)
    says "{?m} goes along the red rope in the last of the light and stops at the cairn. 'Wolf-sign. All along the outside of the cord.' {?m} walks twenty paces and back. 'Not one print inside. Three hundred years of it, by the depth of the ground. They do not cross because the holders do not. They wait where the slow ones come back.' {?m} looks at the niche in the cairn, and says nothing about the lamp." {
    Assert kvCord(party).
  }
  Rule voice_pit at pit_floor when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_warrior) and awake(?m) and at(party, pit_floor) and not kvPit(party)
    says "{?m} looks up the shaft of light at the thing hung in the cloud, then at the ground, and does a sum with a thumb. 'Two metres a day,' {?m} says. 'It is not hunting us. It is a siege, and the engine is the calendar.' The thumb moves again. 'Which means there is a day it arrives, and I can count to it. Good. I can do something with a date.'" {
    Assert kvPit(party).
  }
  Rule voice_lintel at lintel_room when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_mage) and awake(?m) and at(party, lintel_room) and not kvLintel(party)
    says "{?m} stands with the flat of a hand toward the black wall. 'No spell has ever been laid on this,' {?m} says. 'It is not cast. It is built: a courser laid a course, and then a courser laid the next.' A frown, correcting a figure. 'I would say. One cannot dispel a masonry. One can only unlay it from the other end.'" {
    Assert kvLintel(party).
  }

  // ── The twelfth vault ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place twelfth_vault "the twelfth vault" is room within granaries at 3, 1 underground.
  Passage twelfth_door "a vault door with no number" is doorway between ring and twelfth_vault
    opening when sawSecondBolt(party) "A door of lime-washed stone with no number over it, and the second bolt up in the lintel.".
  Observe twelfth_scene at twelfth_vault when true "A vault like the others and not like them: no jars, no beam, no shutter. A stool, a tally-board the length of a man's arm, scored with strokes, and a clerk in a belted Seridane coat sitting on the stool with a bronze stick lifted in his right hand, one word from the end of a sentence. He is not held in the light. He is kept, like the dog in the First Course, and he has no temperature.".
  Thing clerk_held "the clerk at the twelfth vault" at twelfth_vault {
    State kept_clerk "A man in a clerk's belted coat on a stool, a bronze stick lifted over a tally-board, mid-word.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(clerk_held).
  Observe clerk_plays near clerk_held when touched(clerk_held) "Under your hand the clerk finishes his sentence. It is the line you have heard on the plates and over the held at Ennick, word for word, eleven words, said quickly, the way a thing is said that has been said a thousand times a day; and then he lays the stick against the board, and says one word more, flat, to the jars that are not there: 'Venn.' The word does not sound like a prayer. It sounds like a man telling a porter to open the door. When you take your hand away he is mid-word again, with the stick lifted, and the room is very quiet." teaches twelfth_word.
  Discovery twelfth_word "The Seridane clerk's granary line has twelve words, not eleven. He said 'Venn' after the eleventh, as an order: hold this one season, then give it out. The Holdfolk have said eleven words over their dying for three hundred years and stopped where they were taught to stop.".

  // ── Doran: the choice ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Nobody held is woken without their own word, Bren says, and a held man cannot give it. The twelfth word is not his. It
  // is the keeper's, the one who laid him, and it was never said. A company that has it may say it over Doran, or not.
  Person doran "Doran of Ennick" at doran_place {
    Role "Bren's father and Ilis's husband, held forty years". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
  }
  Initially Assert asleep(doran).
  Relation twelfthSaid(place). Relation twelfthKept(place). Relation doranGone(place). Measure doranTime(place).
  Action say_the_twelfth(actor: group, site: place) "Say the twelfth word over Doran's brick" {
    Description "It is not a prayer. It may be an order. Whatever it does, the Holdfolk have never done it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, doran_place) and knows(actor, twelfth_word)
      and asleep(doran) and not twelfthSaid(ennick) and not twelfthKept(ennick).
    Time 5.
    On success { Assert twelfthSaid(ennick). Retract asleep(doran). Retract at(doran, doran_place). Assert at(doran, holders_room). Retract at(ilis, ilis_room). Assert at(ilis, holders_room). Set doranTime(ennick) to watch(clock). }
    Result "You say it flat, as the clerk did: one word, to a man. For a long while nothing. Then the fan of bright lines in the glass in front of his face goes grey, and clear, and his chest goes down and comes up in the time it takes you to breathe twice. He sits up out of the trench like a man getting out of a bath. He looks at his hands. He looks at you. 'Is the fire kept?' he says, in a voice that has not been used for forty years, and gets up, and is walking before you can stop him, and each step is quicker than the last. By the time you reach the cord he is a long way ahead, walking home.".
  }
  Action keep_the_twelfth(actor: group, site: place) "Lay a hand on Doran's brick, and say nothing" {
    Description "You know the word. You do not have to use it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, doran_place) and knows(actor, twelfth_word)
      and asleep(doran) and not twelfthSaid(ennick) and not twelfthKept(ennick).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert twelfthKept(ennick). }
    Result "You lay a hand on the brick, over the knot a holder cut there, and keep the word in your mouth. Under your hand the glass is neither warm nor cold. In the time you stand there Doran draws one breath, and you cannot say whether you are glad of it.".
  }
  Rule mirel_will_not when twelfthSaid(ennick) and travelsWith(mirel, party)
    says "Mirel has stood at the cord with her hood in her hand since you came out. 'I carry for the held,' she says. 'Not against them.' She puts the hood on. 'I am going to the holder's house, to see what you have done.' She goes, and does not look back." {
    Retract travelsWith(mirel, party). Retract willing(mirel, party). Assert at(mirel, holders_room).
  }
  Observe mirel_keeps near party when twelfthKept(ennick) and travelsWith(mirel, party) "Mirel has been watching your face since the brick. She asks nothing. 'Whatever you know,' she says at last, 'you keep it carefully. That is what a carrier does.'".
  Observe doran_home at holders_room when twelfthSaid(ennick) and not doranGone(ennick) "Doran sits at the table in the holder's house with a bowl he has not touched. Bren stands behind his chair with both hands on its back, as if it might get up. Ilis is in the doorway of the back room. Nobody is speaking. The kitchen smells of walnut oil and wet felt and a man who has been a long time in the cold.".
  Topic doran_asks with doran "Ask Doran what the forty years were like" when twelfthSaid(ennick) and not doranGone(ennick) once {
    Says "'A long afternoon,' says Doran. 'I was laying a course of brick on the Weeping Wall terrace and the light came up. I thought: I will finish this one. I thought it for a long time.' He looks at the bowl. 'Who is the grey woman?' Ilis, in the doorway, says nothing. 'Oh,' says Doran.".
  }
  Topic bren_after with bren "Speak to Bren after his father is home" when twelfthSaid(ennick) and not doranGone(ennick) once {
    Says "Bren does not turn round. 'I said a held man cannot give his word,' he says. 'I have said it for thirty years so that I need not find out if he could.' His hands tighten on the chair. 'Do not say it to anyone. Not to Mirel. Not to the carriers. There are a hundred and forty on that glass, and I know which of them I would say it over, and I will not.' A pause. 'Not yet.' He says it as if it were a very large number.".
  }
  Topic ilis_after with ilis "Speak to Ilis in the doorway" when twelfthSaid(ennick) and not doranGone(ennick) once {
    Says "'The prior at Stairhead told me the line, forty years ago,' says Ilis. 'He said the last word was the clerk's. I took that for the Office's. I said eleven and stopped, as I was taught, and I kept the fire.' She looks into the kitchen. 'He asked me if the fire was kept. Do you know I did not know what to say? It was.' She wipes her hands on her apron, which is clean. 'Tonight I am going to sit by him and not be sensible.'".
  }
  Rule doran_dies when twelfthSaid(ennick) and not doranGone(ennick) and watch(clock) >= doranTime(ennick) + 144
    says "In Ennick, at dusk, the lamp in the holder's kitchen is lit and the shutters are closed. Doran of Ennick died an hour before, sitting up, with his wife's hand in one of his and his son's in the other and a bowl of soup gone cold on the table. He had eaten none of it. Ilis told the carriers at the door that she would say it herself, over him, and she did: twelve words." {
    Assert doranGone(ennick). Retract at(doran, holders_room). Assert at(doran, shrine).
  }
  Topic ilis_kept with ilis "Tell Ilis what the clerk said after the eleventh word" when twelfthKept(ennick) and knows(actor, twelfth_word) once {
    Says "She does not move for a time. 'So it had a last word.' She sits down, which she does not do in front of guests. 'I have said that line over half this village. I have never once said anything to the other half.' Her hand goes to the old cloak by the door. 'Do not tell Bren. Not now. Tell him when I am laid, and let him decide whether to say it over me.'".
  }

  // ── The cairn lamp ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At the cord, a niche in the cairn holds a horn lantern that the Holdfolk relight at dusk, whoever sits down by it. The
  // wolves do not come in at its light. A company with no lantern, or one that is slowed and caught outside it, has the
  // old three ways: be home before dark, go with a carrier who knows the cord, or fight in the dark.
  Relation cairnLit(group).
  Observe cairn_lamp at cord when not cairnLit(party) "In the cairn where the path comes up there is a niche with a horn lantern in it, a thumb of oil in the bowl, the wick trimmed. Somebody trims it.".
  Observe cairn_burning at cord when cairnLit(party) "The cairn's lantern is burning, small and yellow, and on the far side of the cord the dark has pulled back to the edge of its reach and stopped.".
  Action light_cairn_lamp(actor: group, site: place) "Light the lantern in the cairn, as the holders do at dusk" {
    Description "It is not for the path.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, cord) and dark() and not cairnLit(actor) and capable(actor, light).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert cairnLit(actor). Retract assails(wolves, actor). Assert tolerates(wolves, actor). }
    Result "You set a flame to the wick in the niche and the little bowl takes it. The light does not reach as far as you thought. It does not need to. Out on the far side of the cord, in the juniper, four pairs of eyes that had been coming in level with you stop, and turn, and one by one are gone, as dogs go at a door they know.".
  }
  Rule cairn_gutters when cairnLit(party) and not dark() { Retract cairnLit(party). }
  Observe mirel_sings near party when dark() and at(party, cord) and travelsWith(mirel, party) and slowedCompany(party) "Mirel walks the cord before you in the dark, singing the names of the held in a low carrier's chant, one to a step. Out in the juniper the four wolves keep level for a while and then stop keeping level. They know the song. They have been refused by it for three hundred years.".

  // ── Kerra's book: a contrast ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Lower Inn keeps a book for the Office. It is, by the evidence, the funniest document in the Uplands.
  Topic kerra_book with kerra "Ask Kerra Lowe to show you the Office's book" when true once {
    Says "Kerra Lowe opens the book on the walnut bar with the air of a woman bringing out a sick relative. Forty years of travellers, in a clean round hand, and every one of them, without exception, a turnip merchant. 'The Office paid by the merchant,' she says, 'in 340, and nothing for anyone else, so.' A Veyra schoolmaster on his way to the Corbel in 361: turnips, northern. A man from the Lesser Instruments at Corran, who collects brass and keeps his own scales: turnips, Corran. An Arbitral sister who stayed three nights and was sick in the yard: turnips, devout. 'And the Office men sign it off,' says Kerra, shutting the book, 'every quarter, and none of them has once asked where all the turnips go.' She considers. 'I sell a very good turnip soup.'".
  }
  Topic kerra_quarrel with kerra "Ask Kerra why nobody from the upper terraces drinks in the Lower Inn" when true once {
    Says "'The cat,' says Kerra. 'In 176 an upper family said a lower family's cat had been seen on their wall on a laying-day. The lower family said it was not their cat. There was a vote at the shrine. It was a draw.' She polishes the bar. 'No Upper has come in by the front door since. They come in at the yard, and they sit under the pump, and I bring them their drink there as a favour. The cat died in 190.'".
  }
  Observe walnuts_heap at shrine when true "At the foot of the chant-wall the heap of walnut shells is as high as a table, the lowest shells fused into a brown stone: one for every laying, the shell cracked and the kernel left. It smells of cold stone and oil. The village has no census. This is it.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/lore.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  Description "Links outward from the Ghessil Uplands: a piece of sky reported fallen, and Lenna Marsh at the plumb tower shown the lens of a lamp.".

  // ── A world event, read: the Counter hears of a gap ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe lore_counter_sky at counter_platform when befell(cloudgate_fell) "Coombe has been given a figure he does not know where to enter. A carter off the south road says a piece of the sky came down into a bay; a slab, with a house on it, and no weather. 'There is no column for that,' says Coombe. 'I count the days the star has held. If a piece of the sky has been taken down by somebody else, whose count is it?' He writes it, finally, in the margin, with a small question mark, where the Counter writes what it cannot count.".

  // ── A visitor from elsewhere: the lens of a lamp ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_lens_plumb "The lens of the lamp of a rock far to the south is ground to the same curve as the plumb tower's: a lens that can only be read by the one who keeps the light.".
  Topic lore_lenna_lens with lenna "Show Lenna Marsh the lens of the lamp" when holding(actor, pharos_lens) once {
    Says "Lenna takes the lens in both hands, the way you hold a bird, and lifts it to the window and looks through it at the plumb line. The line doubles, then resolves, with the weight at the bottom exactly where the weight should be. 'Whoever ground this,' she says, 'knew what true was. This is not a lamp's lens. This is a plumb-glass that has been put to a lamp.' She lowers it. 'The tower is for knowing where down is. A lamp is for knowing where you are. I never thought they were the same business.' She gives it back and wipes her hands on her apron. 'Keep it from damp.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_lens_plumb). }
  }
}

data/adventures/patient-star/masonry.kyr:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Masonry (Tier V): the Patient's citadel beyond the planes, built of the pasts of other worlds. Five laws: air
  // is kept, not given; everything doses; stillness is laid; touch gives time; wings are histories.
  Place masonry "the Masonry" is plane.
  Place masonry_land "the Masonry" is region within masonry.
  Place citadel "the citadel of the Patient" is site within masonry_land at 0, 0.
  Place m_spine "the Spine" is level within citadel.
  Place m_wings "the wings" is level within citadel.
  Place m_heart "the heart" is level within citadel.
  Place spine "the Spine" is room within m_spine at 0, 0.
  Place finished_door "a wing door carved with circles" is room within m_wings at 0, 0.
  Place finished_city "a city of slender towers" is room within m_wings at 1, 0.
  Place finished_wild "fields, then forest, then rock" is room within m_wings at 2, 0.
  Place finished_beginning "the end of the wing" is room within m_wings at 3, 0.
  Place imbar_wing "the Imbar Wing" is room within m_wings at 0, 1.
  Place empty_niches "the empty niches" is room within m_wings at 1, 1.
  Place nave "the Nave of Sockets" is room within m_heart at 0, 0.
  Place heart "the Heart" is room within m_heart at 0, 1.

  // From the Corbel's Selvage, or the Keeping's Outer Wall.
  Passage spine_from_seam "up into the black, onto the Spine" is passage between seam and spine taking 20 minutes.
  Passage spine_from_wall "along a tendril of course-work through the Wall" is passage between outer_wall and spine taking 20 minutes.
  Passage spine_wing "the bridge to a wing door" is passage between spine and finished_door taking 20 minutes.
  Passage wing_in "into the wing" is doorway between finished_door and finished_city.
  Passage wing_back "back through the world's history" is passage between finished_city and finished_wild taking 6 hours.
  Passage wing_end "to the wing's end" is passage between finished_wild and finished_beginning taking 6 hours.
  Passage spine_imbar "the bridge to the new wing" is passage between spine and imbar_wing taking 20 minutes.
  Passage imbar_niches "past the court, into the gallery" is passage between imbar_wing and empty_niches taking 30 minutes.
  Passage spine_nave "down into the heart" is stair between spine and nave taking 30 minutes.
  Passage wing_nave "down from the Imbar Wing" is stair between imbar_wing and nave taking 20 minutes.
  Passage nave_heart "beneath the beating socket" is passage between nave and heart taking 30 minutes.

  // Everything doses.
  Initially Assert litGround(spine). Initially Assert litGround(finished_door). Initially Assert litGround(finished_city).
  Initially Assert litGround(finished_wild). Initially Assert litGround(finished_beginning). Initially Assert litGround(imbar_wing).
  Initially Assert litGround(empty_niches). Initially Assert litGround(nave). Initially Assert litGround(heart).

  // Air is kept, not given: between moments there is no air at all. Visitors breathe the air of the moments they walk
  // through, and some worlds' air is poison.
  Kind airkind. Entity air_good: airkind "breathable air". Entity air_poison: airkind "poison". Entity air_none: airkind "no air".
  Relation airOf(place, airkind).
  Initially Assert airOf(spine, air_none). Initially Assert airOf(finished_door, air_good). Initially Assert airOf(finished_city, air_good).
  Initially Assert airOf(finished_wild, air_poison). Initially Assert airOf(finished_beginning, air_none).
  Initially Assert airOf(imbar_wing, air_good). Initially Assert airOf(empty_niches, air_none).
  Initially Assert airOf(nave, air_none). Initially Assert airOf(heart, air_good). Initially Assert airOf(seam, air_none).
  Measure breath(group).
  Rule breathes when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_good) and breath(party) < 12 { Set breath(party) to 12. }
  Rule holds_breath when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_none) and breath(party) >= 1 { Decrease breath(party) by 1. }
  Hazard airless "no air" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally.".
  Hazard bad_air "the air of another world" means "Deal (1d10) poison damage to ally unless constitution save against (13).".
  Rule suffocates when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_none) and breath(party) < 1 { Assert strikes(airless, party). }
  Rule poisoned when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_poison) { Assert strikes(bad_air, party). }
  Observe air_note near party when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_none) "There is no air here. You are breathing what you brought.".
  Observe breath_short near party when at(party, ?p) and airOf(?p, air_none) and breath(party) <= 4 "Your chest is burning. You have perhaps half an hour of what you carried in your lungs and your clothes.".
  Initially Set breath(party) to 12.
  // A company on its way between two places is at neither, so the rules above are silent for the length of a walk;
  // the air a way costs is said of the way, as the dose of a lit way is (ledger, 26).
  Measure wayAir(passage). Relation airPaid(group, passage).
  Initially Set wayAir(spine_from_seam) to 2. Initially Set wayAir(spine_from_wall) to 2. Initially Set wayAir(spine_wing) to 2.
  Initially Set wayAir(spine_imbar) to 2. Initially Set wayAir(spine_nave) to 3. Initially Set wayAir(wing_nave) to 2.
  Rule way_air when tookWay(party, ?w) and wayAir(?w) > 0 and not airPaid(party, ?w) and breath(party) >= wayAir(?w) {
    Decrease breath(party) by wayAir(?w). Assert airPaid(party, ?w). }
  Rule way_air_short when tookWay(party, ?w) and wayAir(?w) > 0 and not airPaid(party, ?w) and breath(party) < wayAir(?w)
    says "Halfway across there is nothing left in your lungs to breathe." {
    Set breath(party) to 0. Assert airPaid(party, ?w). Assert strikes(airless, party). }
  Rule way_air_clears when airPaid(party, ?w) and not tookWay(party, ?w) { Retract airPaid(party, ?w). }

  // Stillness is laid: a visitor who stays still for an hour is taken into the next course.
  Measure stillness(group). Relation lastPlace(group, place) exclusive. Relation laidIn(group).
  Rule still_counts when at(party, ?p) and lastPlace(party, ?p) and laidRoomM(?p) { Increase stillness(party) by 1. }
  Rule moved_on when at(party, ?p) and not lastPlace(party, ?p) { Assert lastPlace(party, ?p). Set stillness(party) to 0. }
  Relation laidRoomM(place).
  Initially Assert laidRoomM(spine). Initially Assert laidRoomM(finished_door). Initially Assert laidRoomM(finished_city).
  Initially Assert laidRoomM(finished_wild). Initially Assert laidRoomM(finished_beginning). Initially Assert laidRoomM(imbar_wing).
  Initially Assert laidRoomM(empty_niches). Initially Assert laidRoomM(nave). Initially Assert laidRoomM(heart).
  Observe still_warning near party when stillness(party) >= 4 and not laidIn(party) "The course under your feet is warmer than it was, and your boots will not lift as easily as they did.".
  Rule laid_in when stillness(party) >= 6 and not laidIn(party) says "You have stood still an hour. The next course is laid over your feet, and your knees, and you are part of the Masonry." {
    Assert laidIn(party). Assert hobbled(party). }

  // M1: the Spine.
  Observe spine_scene at spine when true "A bridge of dark banded stone crossing black. On either side the Masonry fills half the sky: towers and buttresses of stopped worlds, lit along their edges, going on past seeing. Far off, other long brackets like the Corbel reach out into the dark toward other points of light. Eleven of them.".

  // M2: a finished world. Walking the wing is walking that world's history backward to its beginning.
  Observe fdoor_scene at finished_door when true "A wing door carved with the overlapping circles of the procession's banner.".
  Observe fcity_scene at finished_city when true "A city of slender towers, stopped. Walking on, it gets younger, and smaller.".
  Observe fwild_scene at finished_wild when true "The city is fields, then forest, then bare rock, then fire. The air tastes of metal and burns going down.".
  Observe fbegin_scene at finished_beginning when true "At the very end of the wing a single course, no bigger than a hearthstone, holds the moment that world began. Then nothing.".
  Thing beginning "the moment the world began" at finished_beginning { State unbegun "A single course holds a world's first moment.". }
  Initially Assert kept(beginning).
  Observe world_begins near beginning when touched(beginning) "For the length of your touch a world begins around you: light, and heat, and rock coming together out of nothing, as long as someone holds on. It cannot be carried out.".

  // M3: the Imbar Wing. Everything quarried from Imbar so far is here; carried back through the Keeping to a
  // Remembrancer, each is set again where it was kept.
  Observe imbar_wing_scene at imbar_wing when true "A new wing, half built. Near its door are rooms that look like places you know: a stretch of the Quell road, a Weirs kitchen, a Tovash camp. Beyond them, a king's court whose king's face you cannot hold.".
  Kind quarried_moment "a quarried moment" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A moment cut out of the Keeping, the size of a coin, with a season of somebody's life in it.".
  Item dane_moment "the fourth Dane's reign" is quarried_moment at imbar_wing.
  Item quell_moment "a season of Quell's year 74" is quarried_moment at imbar_wing.
  Observe niches_scene at empty_niches when true "A long gallery of empty niches, waiting, each the size of a year.".
  Relation quellAnchored(place).
  Rule quell_returned when keeps(shore_remembrancer, quell_moment) and not quellAnchored(quell) { Assert quellAnchored(quell). }

  // M4: the Nave of Sockets. Nine sockets, all empty; one beats.
  Observe nave_scene at nave when true "A nave so tall its roof cannot be seen, with nine sockets cut into its floor in a ring, each large enough for a hen's egg and each empty. One socket beats, faintly, like a pulse felt through stone.".
  Action seat_ithmar(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Set Ithmar in the beating socket" {
    Description "The Patient is restored, and Imbar's past is quarried from the newest year backward, at the Masonry's own speed.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nave) and memberOf(carrier, actor)
      and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(ithmar, carrier).
    Time 1 minute.
    Resolve drop(ithmar, carrier).
    On success { Assert seated(ghessil). Assert unbound(ghessil). }
    Result "The jewel goes into its socket as if it had never been out. The beat stops being faint. All round you, in the walls, the Laid stir, as at a voice.".
  }
  // Rebind: with the sigils seen being cut at the Separation, the jewel bound again, tighter. A binding needs a kept
  // moment as its seal: the binder's own, and the binder becomes part of the Keeping, dead and remembered forever.
  Action rebind(actor: group, carrier: member, binder: member, site: place) "Bind Ithmar tighter, {binder} giving the binding their own moment" {
    Description "The Patient's heart-bond breaks; the seed stops and the Corbel withdraws. The binder is set in the jewel, and dies, and everyone will remember them.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, nave) or at(actor, arbiter_vault))
      and knows(actor, sigils_known) and memberOf(carrier, actor) and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(ithmar, carrier)
      and memberOf(binder, actor) and awake(binder) and not rebound(corbel_site).
    Time 30 minutes.
    Resolve inter(binder).
    On success { Assert rebound(corbel_site). }
    Result "Stroke by stroke, as you watched it done at the Separation, the binding is cut tighter, and {binder} lays a hand on the jewel and is in it: you can see them, very small and clear, in the dark opal. Far off, felt in the knees, the seed stops building.".
  }

  // M5: the Heart: the Patient's own moment of expulsion, kept as its heart. Given time, the expulsion resumes: for as
  // long as the touch lasts the Patient goes on falling, farther from the planes, and the Masonry falls with it.
  Observe patient_heart_scene at heart when true "A chamber made of one moment. It is a fall: something vast, dark and many-limbed, too large to see whole, caught in the instant of being thrown out of the world. Around it, stopped, white robes and outstretched hands.".
  Thing patient_heart "the Patient's fall" at heart { State first_instant "The fall is stopped at its first instant.". }
  Initially Assert kept(patient_heart).
  Measure fallHeld(entity).
  Rule heart_falls when touched(patient_heart) { Increase fallHeld(patient_heart) by 1. }
  Observe heart_falling near patient_heart when touched(patient_heart) and fallHeld(patient_heart) < 6 "Under your hand the vast thing goes on falling, away, and everything around you leans after it. Your hand is going with it.".
  Rule exile_done when fallHeld(patient_heart) >= 6 and touched(patient_heart) and not exiled(corbel_site)
    says "You have held an hour. The Patient is gone out past the planes, and the Masonry with it, and you with it, because you did not let go." {
    Assert exiled(corbel_site). Assert fellWith(party). }
  Relation fellWith(group).
  Action touch_and_step(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Touch the Heart and step away through the Keeping at once" {
    Description "Only a wearer of Ithmar can: touch, and be gone at the speed of thought, at the jewel's own cost.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart) and memberOf(carrier, actor)
      and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(ithmar, carrier) and memories(actor) >= 3 and not exiled(corbel_site).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Decrease memories(actor) by 3. Assert exiled(corbel_site). Retract at(actor, heart). Assert at(actor, tideline). }
    Result "You touch the fall, and it falls, and you are gone through the jewel before it can take you: three of your own moments go into the setting as you step. Behind you, the Patient falls out past the planes, and the Masonry with it.".
  }
  // Saro, who has no past to lose, may offer to hold on.
  Action saro_holds(actor: group, holder: member, site: place) "Let Saro hold on" {
    Description "She will hold the Heart for as long as it takes, and fall with it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart) and travelsWith(saro, actor)
      and memberOf(holder, actor) and joinedAs(holder, saro) and not exiled(corbel_site).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve inter(holder).
    On success { Assert exiled(corbel_site). Retract travelsWith(saro, actor). }
    Result "'Go,' says Saro, with both hands on the fall. 'I know how to be still.' The last you see of her she is falling with it, out past the planes, and she is not afraid.".
  }
  // Bargain at the heart: terms better than the Corbel's. Name a line in history and hold the Masonry to it.
  Action heart_bargain(actor: group, site: place) "Name a line in history to the Interlocutor, here, and hold the Masonry to it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart) and knows(actor, newest_backward)
      and carries(actor, ithmar) and not bargained(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert bargained(actor). Assert heldToLine(corbel_site). }
    Result "Your own voice out of the walls of the Heart agrees: nothing after the Separation; and, because you know from which end it cuts, it agrees to cut from the beginning, not the face. The Masonry will be very patient about it.".
  }
  Relation heldToLine(place).
}

data/adventures/patient-star/moments.kyr:
Module moments "Kept moments: what the stilling took, laid as masonry, and given time by a hand" {
  // Where the stilling stops matter wholly it takes the moment, and the Masonry lays it as building stone (the
  // Undersun, the Corbel, the Masonry), and the Keeping keeps every moment of Imbar's past as a place. Three rules hold
  // in all of them: a kept thing touched resumes its moment for as long as the touch lasts; words spoken aloud are
  // laid into the course beneath; nothing kept can be changed, only cut.

  // A kept thing: a stopped flame, a man mid-word, a curtain of smoke, a falling stone.
  Relation kept(entity).
  // Being touched, now: its moment plays.
  Relation touched(entity).
  // Whoever has touched a thing at least once, and what they saw of it played.
  Relation playedFor(entity, group).
  Action touch(actor: group, target: entity, site: place) "Lay a hand on {target}" {
    Description "A kept thing touched takes up its moment again for as long as the hand stays on it, and stops when it is taken away.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and kept(target) and reaches(actor, target)
      and not touched(target) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert touched(target). Assert playedFor(target, actor). }
  }
  Action let_go(actor: group, target: entity, site: place) "Take your hand from {target}" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and touched(target) and reaches(actor, target).
    Time 0.
    On success { Retract touched(target). }
  }
  // A hand cannot stay on a thing the company has walked away from.
  Rule touch_lost when touched(?t) and company(?c) and not reaches(?c, ?t) { Retract touched(?t). }

  // Speech is laid: words said aloud in course-work are taken into the course beneath, and give the Laid near them a
  // few seconds of their moment. Whispered, nothing is taken. The company is aloud until it chooses to whisper.
  Relation whispering(group).
  Relation laidRoom(place).
  Action whisper(actor: group) "Speak only in whispers" {
    Description "Below, words said aloud are taken into the stone, and wake whatever is laid there for a breath.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and not whispering(actor) and at(actor, ?r) and laidRoom(?r). Time 0.
    On success { Assert whispering(actor). }
    Result "You drop your voice to a breath, and so does everyone with you.".
  }
  Action speak_up(actor: group) "Speak aloud again" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and whispering(actor). Time 0.
    On success { Retract whispering(actor). }
    Result "You speak up again.".
  }
  // Every word spoken aloud in a laid room is a course laid down: the Masons can play it back, and the Interlocutor
  // speaks with it.
  Measure wordsLaid(group).
  Relation spokeAloud(group).
  // Every Mason carries a trowel: it lays and unlays course-glass, and in the Keeping cuts moments out.
  Kind trowel_kind "a Mason's trowel" like dagger worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A blade of something like stopped iron, set in a handle with no temperature. Laid against course-glass it lays or unlays.".
  Item spare_trowel "a Mason's trowel" is trowel_kind at tip_dome hidden until trowel_paid.
}

data/adventures/patient-star/neworrel.ky:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // New Orrel, the Collar and the Pit; the dark glass, the Tovash wells and the Split Ear camp; the Sixty and the Ear.
  Place new_orrel "New Orrel" is settlement within ghessil at 2, 0.
  Place collar "the Collar" is site within ghessil at 3, 0.
  Place dark_sector "the Dark Sector" is wilderness within ghessil at 4, 0.
  Place lit_fields "the lit fields" is wilderness within ghessil at 4, 1.

  Place no_gate "the Collar Road gate" is room within new_orrel at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place no_market "the market road" is room within new_orrel at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place barracks_house "the Warden's house" is building within new_orrel.
  Place barracks "the Warden's room" is room within barracks_house at 2, 1.
  Place widows "the Widows' Board" is room within new_orrel at 1, 2.
  Place waiting_house "the House of the Waiting" is room within new_orrel at 0, 2.
  Place storehouse "the Warden's storehouse" is room within new_orrel at 2, 0.
  Place sink "the Sink" is room within new_orrel at 3, 2 outdoors.
  Place balloon_yard "the balloon shed" is room within new_orrel at 3, 1 outdoors.

  Place collar_top "the top of the Collar" is room within collar at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place plumb_tower "the plumb station" is room within collar at 1, 0.
  Place breach "the Breach" is room within collar at 2, 0 outdoors.
  Place inner_fill "the inner fill" is room within collar at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place pit_floor "the Pit floor" is room within collar at 1, 2 outdoors.

  Place dark_glass "the dark glass" is room within dark_sector at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place quarry "the Office quarry" is room within dark_sector at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place tovash_wells "the Tovash wells" is room within dark_sector at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place split_ear_camp "the Split Ear camp" is room within dark_sector at 1, 1 outdoors.

  Place the_sixty "the Sixty" is room within lit_fields at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place the_ear "the Ear" is room within lit_fields at 1, 0.

  // The Collar Road: seven kilometres of rammed umber a metre above the lit glass, with a parapet on the Pit side.
  Passage collar_road "the Collar Road" is causeway between square and no_gate taking 5 hours.
  Initially Set wayDose(collar_road) to 72. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(collar_road) to 18.
  Passage no_street "the gate street" is road between no_gate and no_market taking 5 minutes.
  Passage warden_door "the Warden's door" is door between no_market and barracks.
  Passage widows_door "the Board's door" is door between no_market and widows.
  Passage waiting_door "the Waiting's door" is door between no_gate and waiting_house.
  Passage store_door "the storehouse door" is door between no_market and storehouse.
  Passage sink_lane "the east lane" is path between no_market and sink taking 5 minutes.
  Passage balloon_lane "the lane to the balloon shed" is path between sink and balloon_yard taking 5 minutes.
  Passage collar_ramp "the haul ramp" is path between no_market and collar_top taking 20 minutes.
  Passage tower_door "the plumb tower door" is door between collar_top and plumb_tower.
  Passage collar_walk "the Collar path" is path between collar_top and breach taking 40 minutes.
  Passage fill_slope "the inner slope" is path between collar_top and inner_fill taking 20 minutes.
  Passage pit_descent "the slumping fill into the Pit" is path between inner_fill and pit_floor taking 40 minutes.
  // The Coverers' Stair: a Seridane stair under the old Barrow, the Office's own door to the Granaries.
  Passage coverers_stair "the Coverers' Stair" is stair between storehouse and watch_room taking 30 minutes.
  // Across the dark glass from the Breach, and from Quell by the north-east, without dose: it carries no light.
  Passage dark_way "the dark glass" is path between breach and dark_glass taking 30 minutes.
  Passage quell_dark "the north-east margin" is path between old_quell and dark_glass taking 3 hours.
  Passage quarry_way "the quarry track" is track between dark_glass and quarry taking 10 minutes.
  Passage wells_way "the way to the wells" is path between dark_glass and tovash_wells taking 20 minutes.
  Passage camp_way "the camp path" is path between tovash_wells and split_ear_camp taking 15 minutes.
  // The wells: Seridane air shafts two metres across, a hundred metres to the water; side openings on the Shallows at
  // thirty-five and the Granaries at eighty-five.
  Passage well_shaft "a Tovash well shaft, by the rope" is shaft between tovash_wells and bunks taking 20 minutes needing rope.
  Passage well_deep "the same shaft, further down" is shaft between bunks and ring taking 20 minutes needing rope.
  // Out across the lit fields from the Collar's foot: three and a half kilometres of glass to the Sixty.
  Passage fields_way "the lit glass to the Sixty" is path between collar_top and the_sixty taking 1 hour.
  Initially Set wayDose(fields_way) to 24. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(fields_way) to 6.
  Passage ear_way "the glass to the Ear" is path between the_sixty and the_ear taking 15 minutes.
  Initially Assert litGround(the_sixty). Initially Assert litGround(the_ear). Initially Assert litGround(pit_floor).
  Initially Assert litGround(inner_fill).

  Observe gate_scene_no at no_gate when true "The Collar Road comes off the glass onto an island of red spoil. Ahead the Collar stands up like a red cliff thirty metres high, and the town is packed against its foot.".
  Observe market_no at no_market when true "A road of red dust between houses built of the Collar's own spoil. Everything sold here costs what it cost to bring up the Stair.".
  Observe sink_scene at sink when true "The ground has dropped two metres here since 374. The houses lean on one another with their doors hanging, and nobody lives in them, and nobody has taken the doors.".
  Observe store_scene at storehouse when true "The Warden's storehouse: sacks and barrels to the roof, and at the back a cut stone arch with a stair going down. A lamp burns over it, two guards sit under it, and a clerk at a table writes down every sack that goes in and, with less care, every sack that comes out.".
  Observe collar_top_scene at collar_top when true "A path wide enough for carts runs round the top of the ring. Rusted horse-whims stand at intervals, with wooden chutes running down the inside slope into the Pit's haze.".
  Observe tower_scene at plumb_tower when true "A wooden tower on the Collar top, sixty rungs of ladder to a floor with a hole in it. A bronze plumb line on a drum goes down through the hole, and survey logs fill a shelf, every spine labelled in one hand that gets smaller towards the end.".
  Observe breach_scene at breach when true "The ring is broken by a gap forty metres wide, its edges baked white. Beside it a drainage culvert of cut stone runs under the path. Beyond, the clear fields are dark: the same clear rock, with no light in it.".
  Observe fill_scene at inner_fill when true "Inside the Collar the fill slopes down toward the shaft in long red terraces, cracked like old mud. The heat comes up off it, and the light.".
  Observe pit_scene at pit_floor when true "The Pit floor is melt-rock and ceramic slag, too hot to stand on long, too bright to look across. From a dark mouth in the middle a thread of light goes straight up into the cloud, and beside it, hanging from nowhere, a cord as thick as a wrist, glowing along its whole length.".
  Hazard pit_heat "the Pit's heat" means "Deal (1d6) fire damage to ally.".
  Rule pit_burns when at(party, pit_floor) and not pitScorched(party) { Assert strikes(pit_heat, party). Assert pitScorched(party). }
  Relation pitScorched(group).
  Rule pit_cools when pitScorched(party) and not at(party, pit_floor) { Retract pitScorched(party). }
  // The fill is moving: a party on the inner slope may be carried down toward the light and heat.
  Hazard fill_slide "a slide of fill" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  Rule fill_slides when at(party, inner_fill) and dice(inner_fill) <= 4 says "The terrace you are on lets go with a sound like a sigh and carries you down toward the light." {
    Assert strikes(fill_slide, party). Assert at(party, pit_floor). }

  // The Warden and the Office in New Orrel.
  Person aske "Ivo Aske" at barracks {
    Role "Warden of the Collar". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Greets "The Warden of the Collar has an ordinary face and receives you with the whole of it: attentive, courteous, completely shut. 'Warden Aske,' he says. 'You have been seen on the Ramp, and I make a point of knowing who walks on Crown ground. You are welcome to be here. Be welcome briefly.'".
  }
  Person office_guard "the Coverers' Stair guard" at storehouse {
    Role "two Office men and a clerk at the stair". Ancestry human. Numbers 2. Peaceable.
    Guards coverers_stair.
    State posted blocking "Two Office men and a clerk sit at the head of the Coverers' Stair.".
  }
  Initially Assert serves(office_guard, aske).
  Topic guard_stair with office_guard "Ask the stair guard what it takes to go down" when not tolerates(office_guard, actor) once {
    Says "'A pass from the Warden,' says the clerk, before either of the men can open his mouth, 'or a licence of the Office, stamped. Neither of which, I think, you have.' One of the Office men shifts on his stool and says, not unkindly, 'The Warden's in the barracks. He likes to be asked. He likes it better with money in it.'".
  }
  Rule licence_stair when licensed(party) and not tolerates(office_guard, party) { Assert tolerates(office_guard, party). }
  Topic aske_king with aske "Ask the Warden about the king below" when true once {
    Says "'Royal property,' says Aske, 'and a wonder. When he is well enough I mean to bring him up to Sorne, and the court will see what the Crown holds under this plateau.' He smiles without warmth. 'You will have heard he wakes. I have it in a book.'".
  }
  Topic aske_balloon with aske "Ask the Warden about the shed by the Sink" when true once {
    Says "'A fire-balloon,' says Aske. 'Haldrish silk and Haldrish craftsmen. It will lift six to the bottom of the Cloud on a calm autumn dawn.' He watches you. 'Whoever goes up in it goes in the Crown's name. Bring me something from up there the court can hold in its hands, and you go in mine.'".
    On discuss { Assert offered(aske, actor). }
  }
  Action pay_aske(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the Warden twenty crowns toward his men's wages" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(aske, site) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 20
      and not admits(aske, actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 20. Increase quantity(aske, gold) by 20. Assert admits(aske, actor).
      Assert serves(office_guard, aske). }
    Result "Aske counts it twice. 'The Crown is grateful,' he says, and writes you a pass for the Coverers' Stair and a place on the balloon.".
  }
  // In the eighth week, if nobody has taken the king, Aske's men carry him up the Coverers' Stair; at his age and
  // rate, without careful feeding, he has a fever within a fortnight.
  Rule king_carried when day(clock) >= 56 and at(amaru, last_hour) and not grieves(amaru) says "Word comes up the Coverers' Stair: the Warden's men have carried the old king up out of the Hour on a litter." {
    Retract at(amaru, last_hour). Assert at(amaru, barracks). Assert fevered(amaru). }
  Relation fevered(group).
  Observe king_in_barracks near amaru when at(amaru, barracks) and fevered(amaru) "The old king lies on a cot in the Warden's room under three blankets, burning with fever, and looks at the ceiling as if waiting for light to come down it.".

  // Annet Sorrel and the Breach widows; Lenna Marsh and the sinking; Ruan Haldane and the Waiting.
  Person coyle "Annet Sorrel" at widows {
    Role "speaker for the Breach widows". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
    Greets "Annet Sorrel is pinning a list of names to the waiting-house wall, one pin to a name, in the same order as yesterday. 'Sixty-three,' she says, without being asked. 'You can count them, if you like. I have. Are you here for the Crown, or the Tovash, or the dead?'".
  }
  Topic coyle_breach with coyle "Ask Annet Sorrel about the Breach" when true once {
    Says "'Sixty-three men,' says Annet Sorrel. 'Mine among them. Somebody cut the Collar's drain in the storm of 352 and let the water into the Pit, and the steam came back up the chutes. Nobody was hanged for it.' She looks at you. 'They say the Tovash did it. I want the name. And I want the pensions, which have not been paid since 71.'".
  }
  Topic coyle_named with coyle "Tell Annet Sorrel who cut the Breach" when knows(actor, breach_cut) once {
    Says "She hears it out without sitting down. 'Bren of Ennick,' she says. 'Who holds the dying.' Behind her a clerk puts his pen down very quietly. 'I will go to Ennick myself,' she says, 'and look at his door.'".
    On discuss { Assert accused(coyle, bren). }
  }
  Relation accused(group, group).
  Person lenna "Lenna Marsh" at plumb_tower {
    Role "Glass Office surveyor at the plumb station". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "A woman in a leather apron is standing quite still with a plumb-line in one hand and a stub of chalk in the other, and does not take her eyes off the weight. 'Do not stamp,' she says, quietly. 'Do not breathe on it, if you can help it. In a minute you may tell me what you want.'".
  }
  Discovery sinking "The Late Sun is sinking about a metre a year, twenty-five times the old rate, and the Collar's inner face will slide into the shaft within ten years. Lenna Marsh's logs show it month by month since 372." {
    Source marsh_logs "Lenna Marsh's survey logs" at plumb_tower readable by party.
    Known by lenna.
  }
  Discovery footprints "Lenna Marsh's log for the 3rd of Frost 379: a single line of bare footprints on the inner fill near the Breach, going up from the Pit's edge.".
  Topic marsh_logs_t with lenna "Ask Lenna Marsh what her logs say" when true once {
    Says "'That the Sun is going down a metre a year,' says Marsh, 'and nobody in Sorne reads past the first line.' She flips back a year. 'And this. Third of Frost, last year: bare footprints on the fill, going up from the edge. I took it for a soldier's prank.' She closes the book. 'Nobody walks up out of that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, footprints). }
  }
  // At dawn from the Collar top, for a few minutes before the sun washes it out, something long and dark shows in the
  // Standing Cloud.
  Discovery corbel_seen "At dawn from the Collar, a long dark shape hangs point-down in the Standing Cloud, high over the Pit, for a few minutes before the sun washes it out.".
  Observe corbel_dawn at collar_top when hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) <= 6 "Before the sun clears the heath, high in the Standing Cloud over the Pit, something long and dark hangs point-down, like a bracket on a wall with no wall. Then the light comes and it is gone." teaches corbel_seen.
  Person ruan "Ruan Haldane" at waiting_house {
    Role "Elder of the Waiting". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "The Elder of the Waiting sits in the only chair in a room full of people standing, and has a voice that has not been raised in years and does not need to be. 'You are not one of ours,' says Ruan Haldane. 'You may stay. Sit where you like. We are, for the moment, only waiting.'".
  }
  Topic ruan_voice with ruan "Ask Ruan Haldane what the Waiting wait for" when true once {
    Says "'For the answer,' says Ruan, and his voice drops, as in a church. 'Teodar wrote in 71 that the name was finished. What comes after is not more name. It is the thing named.' He spreads his hands. 'The Office has closed the Hour to us. My people go down anyway, and are not sorry.'".
  }
  Topic ruan_tone with ruan "Tell Ruan Haldane about the tone below" when knows(actor, tone_below) once {
    Says "Ruan sits down. 'Once an hour,' he says. 'And they did not tell me.' After a while he laughs, very quietly. 'Then it has answered. Teodar was right.' He gives you a tablet from his sleeve: the Waiting's copy of the transcript. 'Take it to whoever can read it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ward_names). }
  }

  // The Collar's culvert and the missing pin; the holder's bolt in Ennick (The Collar, Referee).
  Thing culvert "the drainage culvert" at breach {
    State standing "A culvert of cut stone runs under the Collar path beside the Breach, with a sluice frame at its mouth.".
    Tries looking.
  }
  Discovery herd_mark "Inside the culvert's sluice frame a Split Ear herd-mark is cut, and the gate's iron pin is missing from its square socket.".
  Observe culvert_looked near culvert when tried(culvert, looking) "On the inside of the sluice frame someone has cut a herd-mark: two notches and a split. The gate's pin is gone; its socket is square, and big as a thumb." teaches herd_mark.
  Discovery breach_cut "The Collar's drainage was cut in the storm of 352 by Ayzhe of the Split Ear and Bren of Ennick, with two Tovash riders, to flood the works and stop the Covering. They thought the fill would soak the water up.".
  Observe pin_matched near party when knows(party, herd_mark) and knows(party, bolt_is_pin) and not knows(party, breach_cut) "A Split Ear mark in the culvert, a sluice pin bolting the holder's door: whoever cut the Collar's drain was of the Split Ear, and was in Ennick after. You know of only one holder who was twenty-two that year." teaches breach_cut.

  // The dark glass: no light in it since 357, so it can be cut without dose, and Kell's forty-one dead stand in it.
  Observe dark_scene at dark_glass when true "The same clear rock as the lit fields, with no light in it at all. People stand in it, chest-deep, a little way off: men and women of Kell, held in 353 and dead when the fill cut the light four years later.".
  Observe quarry_scene at quarry when not halted(quarry) "Office crews are cutting blocks out of the dark glass with saws and grit. The quarry face is sixty metres from the nearest of Kell's dead, and pegs and string mark a line straight through them.".
  Observe quarry_halted at quarry when halted(quarry) "The quarry is quiet. The saws are racked and covered; somebody has pulled up the pegs that ran toward Kell's dead.".
  Relation halted(place).
  Measure quarryFace(place).
  Initially Set quarryFace(quarry) to 60.
  Rule quarry_cuts when not halted(quarry) and hour(clock) == 14 and quarryFace(quarry) > 0 and dice(quarry) <= 30 { Decrease quarryFace(quarry) by 2. }
  Observe quarry_reaches at quarry when quarryFace(quarry) <= 0 "The quarry face has reached the first of Kell's dead. A man stands in a block on a sledge, still chest-deep, looking at nothing, ready to go down the Stair.".
  Topic bren_quarry with bren "Tell Bren the Office is cutting toward Kell's dead" when true once {
    Says "Bren's face does not move. 'Then the road shuts,' he says. 'No Office cart comes up through Ennick while that quarry cuts.' He is already reaching for his coat.".
    On discuss { Assert roadClosed(ennick). }
  }
  Relation roadClosed(place).
  Rule aske_halts when roadClosed(ennick) and not halted(quarry) and day(clock) >= 10 says "Word comes across the plateau: the Warden has stopped the dark-glass quarry, and blames the licencer." { Assert halted(quarry). }

  Observe wells_scene at tovash_wells when true "Three stone rings stand on the dark glass, two metres across, with wooden frames for rope. Swallows go down one of them at dusk and do not come out.".
  Observe wells_swallows at tovash_wells when dark() "In the last of the light the swallows come in over the heath in ones and twos, fold their wings at the lip of the middle well, and drop down it.".

  // The Split Ear: Ayzhe, who cut the Breach; Ezh, who would ride with you; and, from the fifth week, Halu.
  Person ayzhe "Ayzhe of the Split Ear" at split_ear_camp {
    Role "clan-mother of the Split Ear". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner proud.
  }
  Person ezh "Ezh of the Split Ear" at split_ear_camp {
    Role "a young rider". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
  }
  Initially Set hire(ezh) to 2.
  Topic ayzhe_wife with ayzhe "Ask Ayzhe what she wants" when true once {
    Says "'The drum-maker's wife,' says Ayzhe. 'Out among the Sixty. We count our line from her, ten mothers back.' She looks toward the light. 'The last time someone buried the Pit, every held one on this plateau woke in the glass and choked. I will not leave her there for the next.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(ezh, actor). }
  }
  Discovery moot_count "The Split Ear moot song's beat: the count the drum at the fair was playing when the Sixty were held.".
  Topic ayzhe_drum with ayzhe "Ask Ayzhe about the drum at the fair" when true once {
    Says "'The moot song,' says Ayzhe at once, and beats it on her knee: three, a rest, two, three. 'It is what the drum was playing when the light came up at the fair. My grandmother's grandmother told it.' She stops. 'Why?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, moot_count). }
  }
  Topic ayzhe_breach with ayzhe "Ask Ayzhe who cut the Collar's drain" when knows(actor, breach_cut) once {
    Says "Ayzhe's hand stops on her knee. 'We thought the fill would drink it,' she says. 'Sixty-three. I count them every night.' She does not ask you what you will do.".
  }
  Person halu "Halu" at last_hour {
    Role "a woman of the old people, speaking Old Seridan". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
  }
  Initially Retract at(halu, last_hour).
  Rule halu_climbs when day(clock) >= 33 and not walkedOut(halu) says "Word goes round the Tovash camps: a dead woman of the old people climbed out of one of the wells in the night, talking." {
    Assert at(halu, split_ear_camp). Assert walkedOut(halu). }
  Relation walkedOut(group).
  Topic halu_kesset with halu "Tell Halu that Kesset is looking for her" when travelsWith(kesset, actor) or knows(actor, kings_book) once {
    Says "Halu understands one word in three of what you say, and the one she understands is the chamberlain's name. She sits down on the glass and weeps, and then she gets up and asks, in Old Seridan, the way to the city above.".
    On discuss { Assert willing(halu, actor). }
  }

  // The Sixty and the Ear (The Sixty; The Ear).
  Observe sixty_scene at the_sixty when true "A fair caught in the glass, chest-deep: horses in harness, a cauldron with its steam gone solid, children with their arms out, a man with a drum held against his chest. Their eyes are open.".
  Measure sixtyWatched(group).
  Rule watching_sixty when at(party, the_sixty) and not benighted(party) { Increase sixtyWatched(party) by 1. }
  Rule sixty_reset when not at(party, the_sixty) and sixtyWatched(party) > 0 { Set sixtyWatched(party) to 0. }
  Observe sixty_moved at the_sixty when sixtyWatched(party) >= 6 "You have watched an hour. A child's hand is higher than it was. The drum-maker's wife has turned her head a finger's width toward her husband.".
  Thing wife_block "the drum-maker's wife" at the_sixty {
    State held "A woman in a red felt cap stands in the glass beside the drummer, half-turned toward him.".
    State cut_free "The drum-maker's wife sits on a blanket on the glass, wrapped in felt, staring at the fair she was part of.".
    Change cut_wife "Grind the drum-maker's wife out of the glass" from held to cut_free needing digging.
  }
  Rule wife_tovash when state(wife_block, cut_free) and not freedWife(ayzhe) says "Two Split Ear riders come across the glass at a gallop and kneel by the woman in the red cap." { Assert freedWife(ayzhe). Assert grateful(ayzhe, party). }
  Relation freedWife(group).
  Observe ear_scene at the_ear when true "A low hut of umber brick with no floor. Inside, the bare glass is worn smooth in six places where people have knelt. In the corner an old man sits against the wall, cross-legged, head bowed, with his ear toward the glass. He has been dead since 368, and looks a week dead.".
  Discovery listeners_count "Teodar Lusk's count, year 0 to year 371: every syllable of the Voice heard since the Unlidding, in order; the plan of the Undersun's lowest built reach.".
  Thing count_shelf "the shelf of wax tablets" at the_ear {
    State shelved "A shelf of wax tablets runs along one wall: the count, year by year.".
    State read "The count's tablets have been taken down and read, and put back out of order.".
    Change read_count "Read the count through" from shelved to read.
  }
  Observe count_read at the_ear when state(count_shelf, read) "Three hundred and seventy years of syllables, a moon to a line. Teodar's last tablet says the name was finished, and what comes next will be an answer." teaches listeners_count.
}

data/adventures/patient-star/placed.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  // The Ghessil Uplands as a country beyond a march: the company that comes into the Shift Market is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".

  // Garret is one of the Mutual's cutters and no kin of the company's, which owes the hall nothing: Dagny pays to have
  // him brought up (the cutter's uncle, debt and knife are company.kyr's).
  Topic dagny_garret_placed with dagny "Ask Dagny about Garret" when not cameUp(garret) once {
    Says "'Garret,' says Dagny. 'One of mine. Last Harvest he went into an open vault in the Granary Ring to take jars, and the light had him before he was three steps in. Ness saw him from the doorway. She could not get to him and nor could anyone.' She rubs out a chalk mark on the board with the side of her fist. 'He is not dead. He is standing in there with his hand out, the way you'd reach for a jar.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, garret_held). }
  }
  Topic dagny_offer_placed with dagny "Ask Dagny what she would have you do" when not cameUp(garret) and not offered(dagny, actor) once {
    Says "'Bring him up,' says Dagny. 'The hall pays fourteen crowns the day Garret walks into this room on his own feet. The crew goes down when it has the felt, in three days or four. Go with them, or go down alone and before them, I don't care which. Only bring him up.'".
    On discuss { Assert offered(dagny, actor). }
  }
  Relation paid(group).
  Event dagny_pays near dagny when (travelsWith(garret, party) or following(garret, party)) and offered(dagny, party) and at(party, mutual_hall) and not paid(party) "Dagny looks at Garret for a long moment, and then at you. She unlocks the box under the board and counts fourteen crowns onto the table. 'I keep my word,' she says. 'Sit him by the fire before he falls down.'" then {
    Assert paid(party). Assert cameUp(garret). Increase quantity(party, gold) by 14. }
  Event crew_brought_him_placed near dagny when at(garret, mutual_hall) and not broughtBy(garret, party) and at(party, mutual_hall) "Garret is by the hall fire with a blanket round him and a bowl in his hands, and the crew who brought him up are drinking. Dagny does not look at you.".
  Objective find_garret_placed when not cameUp(garret) and asleep(garret) "Garret, a cutter of the Mutual, is held in an open granary vault under Quell. Dagny will pay fourteen crowns if you bring him up.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/quell.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  Description "Quell, the Granaries of Tamaun and Ennick, late in Haying of the year 380: a cutter's uncle held eleven months in an open granary vault, and the people who want him, or his jars, brought up.".

  // The plateau, as far as this slice goes: Quell on the western margin, the heath and the Ramp to the gorge,
  // Ennick on the gorge floor, the Clear Fields above it, and the city under the glass.
  Place ghessil "the Ghessil Uplands" is region within imbar.
  Place quell "Quell" is settlement within ghessil at 0, 1.
  Place heath "the heath" is wilderness within ghessil at 1, 1.
  Place ennick "Ennick" is settlement within ghessil at 2, 2.
  Place fields "the Clear Fields above Ennick" is wilderness within ghessil at 3, 1.
  Place tamaun "Tamaun" is site within ghessil at 1, 0.

  Place mutual_house "the Mutual's hall" is building within quell.
  Place lazar_house "the lazar house" is building within quell.
  Place office_house "the Glass Office" is building within quell.
  Place square "the Shift Market" is room within quell at 1, 1.
  Place mutual_yard "the Mutual's yard" is room within quell at 1, 0.
  Place mutual_hall "the Mutual's hall" is room within mutual_house at 1, 0.
  Place ward "the lazar ward" is room within lazar_house at 0, 1.
  Place weighing "the weighing yard" is room within office_house at 2, 1 outdoors.
  Place well_head "the North Well head" is room within quell at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place old_quell "Old Quell" is room within quell at 2, 0 outdoors.

  Passage yard_gate "the Mutual's yard gate" is gate between square and mutual_yard.
  Passage hall_door "the hall door" is door between mutual_yard and mutual_hall.
  Passage lazar_door "the lazar house door" is door between square and ward.
  Passage weighing_gate "the weighing-yard gate" is gate between square and weighing.
  Passage well_lane "the well lane" is path between square and well_head taking 5 minutes.
  Passage east_gate "the old east gate" is gate between square and old_quell.

  Observe square_scene at square when not dark() "The square is umber brick on every side, the colour of dried blood, and not one window looks east. Sledges hiss on the cobbles between the shifts. At the weighing-yard gate a clerk calls the grades: 'One. One. Three. Reject.'".
  Observe square_hook at square when not dark() and kin(party, garret) and not offered(dagny, party) "Across the square the Mutual's yard gate stands open, and Dagny Ferrow's chalk-board inside has your name on it with twenty-eight crowns beside. She has sent for you twice. Your uncle Garret has stood eleven months in the light at Tamaun, and the Mutual means to go down for him in three days or four.".
  Observe square_night at square when dark() "The square is empty but for the dusk crew coming in, hoods back, grey in the face. Somebody coughs, dry and short, and does not stop for a while.".
  Observe yard_scene at mutual_yard when true "The Mutual's yard: sledges up on their ends against the wall, grit-sacks, coils of rope, and a trough of grey water where the cutters wash the glitter off their hands.".
  Observe hall_scene at mutual_hall when true "A long room with a hearth at one end and the Mutual's tally-boards along the wall: crews, shifts, debts, chalked and rubbed out and chalked again. Your own name is up there, with a number beside it.".
  Observe ward_scene at ward when true "Twenty beds, eighteen of them full. The cough here is the same cough as the square's, only slower.".
  Observe weighing_scene at weighing when true "The Glass Office's yard, in what were the Company's yards: scales, a stamp-table, blocks of clear stone stacked under red cloth, and a board by the gate that says LICENCES DRAWN FIRST OF THE MONTH.".
  Observe well_scene at well_head when true "The North Well is a round head of old cut stone, older than the town, with a stair going down inside it to the water.".
  Observe well_water at well_head when not drained(quell_wells) "Far down, the water is a coin of light. It comes up at blood heat, and smells faintly of iron.".
  Observe well_water_low at well_head when drained(quell_wells) "Far down, the water has sunk below the last of the old marks on the stair. Women are queuing at the well with their jars and arguing about it.".
  Observe old_quell_scene at old_quell when true "Three streets of umber-brick houses stand on clear ground, their doors open the way their owners left them in 355. Where a floor was beaten earth and not brick, the house is lit from below, and the light comes up through the doorway and lies along the street like water. Every shadow points west.".
  Initially Assert litGround(old_quell).

  // What Quell sells: felt, true and false; a stylus; honey from the Tovash.
  Kind umber_felt "an umber felt cloak" like cloak_of_protection worth 2 weighing 6
    described "Wool felted with iron clay, red-brown and heavy, with hood and mitts. Rubbed with a wet thumb, it leaves a rust mark.".
  Initially Assert shields(umber_felt).
  Kind madder_felt "an umber felt cloak" like cloak_of_protection worth 1 weighing 2
    described "Wool dyed red-brown, with hood and mitts. It is lighter than it looks.".
  Kind stylus "a stillglass stylus" is tool worth 2 weighing 0
    described "A needle of stillglass in a bone handle, for drawing along a voice-plate's growth lines.".
  Entity salt: good "handful of salt".
  // Glass lanterns are confiscated at the Stair: on the plateau a lantern is horn.
  Kind horn_lantern "a horn lantern" like lantern worth 1
    described "A tallow lantern in a horn case. No glass: up here, glass carries the light.".
  Kind night_honey "a jar of night honey" is gear worth 1 weighing 1
    described "Dark, slightly bitter honey from bees that work by cloudlight. It keeps for decades.".
  Kind stillglass_knife "an unstamped stillglass knife" like dagger worth 5 weighing 1
    described "A stillglass blade with no Office stamp on the tang. The edge has never needed sharpening.".
  Person rusk "Rusk" at square {
    Role "the felt-lender, with her bales of red felt". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
    Sells umber_felt for 2 coin from 3.
    Sells stylus for 2 coin from 1.
    Sells horn_lantern for 1 coin from 2.
    Sells lamp_oil for 1 coin from 4.
    Sells rope for 1 coin from 2.
  }
  Person barrow_boy "a boy with a barrow" at square {
    Role "a hawker of felt cloaks off a barrow, cheap". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he.
    Sells madder_felt for 1 coin from 4.
  }
  Person honey_seller "Ezh's aunt" at square {
    Role "a Tovash woman selling night honey by the jar". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
    Sells night_honey for 1 coin from 4.
    Sells salt for 1 coin from 6.
  }
  Topic rusk_felt with rusk "Ask Rusk about the barrow boy's felt" when true once {
    Says "'Madder,' says Rusk, without looking. 'Dyed wool. Wet your thumb and rub it: real felt leaves rust on you. That stuff leaves nothing, and lets everything through. Weigh it in your hand, while you are about it. A cloak of mine is six kilos and you feel every one.'".
  }

  // The Mutual: Dagny Ferrow, its Master, and Garret's crew.
  Person dagny "Dagny Ferrow" at mutual_hall {
    Role "Master of the Cutters' Mutual". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
    Greets "The board in the hall is chalked with names and the sums against them, and Dagny Ferrow is rubbing one out with the side of her fist. She does not turn round. 'If you have come about Garret,' she says, 'wipe your feet. If you are the Office, you may wait in the yard with the dog.'".
  }
  Person ness "Ness Oakum" at mutual_yard {
    Role "a cutter of Garret's old crew". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Plans 14 steps. Uses go, change_thing. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "Ness Oakum is oiling a pole that is already oiled, long end across her knees, and talks to it. 'You have the look of folk who will want to go and look,' she says. 'Everyone does. Looking is free. It is the second step that is dear.'".
  }
  Person crew "Dagny's crew" at mutual_yard {
    Role "two cutters of the Mutual, felted, with poles and a sledge". Ancestry human. Numbers 2. Peaceable. Plans 14 steps. Uses go, change_thing.
  }
  Person grit "Grit" at mutual_yard {
    Role "the Mutual's yard dog, grey about the muzzle". Species dog. Pronouns she.
  }
  Observe grit_scene near grit of grit when at(grit, mutual_yard) "A grey bitch lies across the hall doorstep with her chin on her paws, and thumps her tail once for anyone in felt.".
  Initially Assert serves(ness, dagny). Initially Assert serves(crew, dagny).

  Discovery garret_held "Garret, a cutter of the Mutual, walked into an open granary vault in Tamaun last autumn to take the jars, and has stood in its light for eleven months, held." {
    Known by dagny, ness, crew.
  }
  Topic dagny_garret with dagny "Ask Dagny about Garret" when not cameUp(garret) and kin(actor, garret) once {
    Says "'Your uncle,' says Dagny. 'You know as much as I do, or you should. Last Harvest he went into an open vault in the Granary Ring to take jars, and the light had him before he was three steps in. Ness saw him from the doorway. She could not get to him and nor could anyone.' She rubs out a chalk mark on the board with the side of her fist. 'He is not dead. He is standing in there with his hand out, the way you'd reach for a jar.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, garret_held). }
  }
  Relation offered(group, group).
  Topic dagny_offer with dagny "Ask Dagny what she would have you do" when not cameUp(garret) and not offered(dagny, actor) and kin(actor, garret) once {
    Says "'Your debt to this hall is fourteen felt-lengths,' says Dagny. 'Twenty-eight crowns. I will rub out half of it the day Garret walks into this room on his own feet. The crew goes down when it has the felt, in three days or four. Go with them, or go down alone and before them, I don't care which. Only bring him up.' She looks at your hands. 'And keep that knife of yours out of Pike's sight. It has no stamp.'".
    On discuss { Assert offered(dagny, actor). }
  }
  Topic dagny_way with dagny "Ask Dagny how the crew goes down" when not cameUp(garret) once {
    Says "'By the North Well and the West Gallery, the way we always have,' says Dagny. 'There is an Office chain on the well-head. A licence opens it, and the licences are drawn on the first of the month. Hal Brewin keeps the chain, and Hal drinks.' She shrugs. 'Four hours from the well to the city, if the Neck lets you through. It is late summer: there is a metre of air under the Neck now, more than most years.'".
  }
  Topic ness_vault with ness "Ask Ness about the vault where Garret is" when not cameUp(garret) once {
    Says "'Ninth vault of the Ring, on the north side,' says Ness. 'Shutter open, light coming down off the ceiling like a white post. Jars all round him. Forty jars in a vault, umber-glazed and not a crack in one, and a collector in Sorne pays three crowns a jar.' She spits. 'He is not dying, you know. Nobody held is dying. He'll keep.'".
  }
  Topic crew_plan with crew "Ask the crew when they go down" when not cameUp(garret) and not descended(crew) once {
    Says "'When the felt comes, three days, four,' says the elder of the two. 'Felt, poles, rope, a sledge-cloth to drag him on. Ness knows the vault.' He does not look at Ness when he says it.".
  }
  Relation descended(group).

  // Saro and Sister Wenda, at the lazar house.
  Person wenda "Sister Wenda" at ward {
    Role "an Arbitral sister, who keeps the lazar house". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "Sister Wenda has a pot of broth on the ward stove and is stirring it against the grain, which she says keeps it from catching. 'You are not a patient,' she says, taking in your hands, 'and you are not Office. Then you are a visitor, and I must find you something to do.'".
    Wants night_honey.
  }
  Person saro "Saro" at ward {
    Role "a woman who walked out of the deep glass last autumn". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 6. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    Joins "Saro stands at once, as if she had been waiting for nothing else. 'Down,' she says. 'Yes.'".
    Carries trowel_kind.
  }
  // Her bones and teeth are stillglass: the light does not slow her, in the company or out of it.
  Initially Assert unslowed(saro). Initially Assert unslowed(member_saro_person).
  Discovery saro_cold "Saro never warms. Her hands have no temperature at all, like stillglass, and she has been in the lazar house since last autumn without once being cold or hot." {
    Known by wenda.
  }
  Topic wenda_saro with wenda "Ask Sister Wenda about Saro" when true once {
    Says "'She came in last Frost, walking, from the east,' says Wenda. 'No fever, no cough, nothing I can treat. She eats, a little. She learns.' She lowers her voice. 'She does not warm. I have held her hands in mine for an hour by the stove and they are no warmer at the end than at the start, and no colder. The others have started to notice.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, saro_cold). }
  }
  Event wenda_honey near wenda when keeps(wenda, ?j) and itemKind(?j, night_honey) "Sister Wenda turns the jar to the window and smiles, which she has not done since you came in. 'For the coughers,' she says. 'A spoon at night, and they sleep.' She puts it on the shelf with the other two." then { Assert thanked(wenda, party). }
  Relation thanked(group, group).
  Topic saro_stone with saro "Ask Saro what she wants" when true once {
    Says "Saro answers in a Tovashi a month old and already good. 'To go back into the glass. Down, where it is being built.' She looks at you with great attention. 'Do you know of a stone that sings? Under here. It sings once in each hour. Everyone I ask says no.'".
  }
  Topic saro_down with saro "Tell Saro you are going down into Tamaun" when knows(actor, garret_held) and not willing(saro, actor) and not travelsWith(saro, actor) once {
    Says "'Into the old city,' says Saro. 'Down.' She has already stood up. 'I will come. I do not need felt.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(saro, actor). }
  }

  // The Glass Office: Halloran Pike, the licence lottery, and Hal Brewin at the chain.
  Person pike "Halloran Pike" at weighing {
    Role "the Glass Office licencer". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "Halloran Pike sits behind a slate set into a trestle with a stamp, a blotter and a ribbon of numbered tokens. He does not look up. 'Name,' he says, 'trade, and the quarter you are asking for.' He blots. 'Whatever you were going to say about the weather, I have heard it.'".
  }
  Person hal "Hal Brewin" at well_head {
    Role "the Office's man at the North Well chain". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "Hal Brewin has a cudgel across his knees and a cheerful face, which is the wrong way round, and nods you in to the well-head as though it were his own parlour. 'Lovely morning for a licence,' he says. 'You'll have one? No? Then we shall be having a conversation.'".
    Guards well_stair.
    State watching blocking "Hal Brewin sits on a stool by the chain-gate with a cudgel across his knees.".
    State drunk "Hal Brewin is asleep on his stool with his mouth open.".
  }
  Topic pike_licence with pike "Ask Pike about a salvage licence" when not licensed(actor) once {
    Says "'Ten crowns to put your name in,' says Pike, 'and the names are drawn at this gate on the first of the month, one in four. Win, and the North Well chain opens to you for the month. Lose, and the ten crowns are the Crown's.' He blots a figure. 'Nobody goes down the Well without a licence. Nobody.'".
  }
  Topic pike_son with pike "Ask Pike about the cough in his house" when true once {
    Says "Pike's pen stops. 'My son,' he says. 'Glass-lung, at nineteen. There is a physician in Sorne who will see him for twenty crowns a visit, and I am paid nine a month.' He starts writing again, harder.".
  }
  Relation licensed(group). Relation entered(group).
  Action enter_lottery(actor: group, site: place) "Put your name in for this month's licences, ten crowns" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pike, site) and not licensed(actor)
      and not entered(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 10.
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Increase quantity(pike, gold) by 10. Assert entered(actor). }
    Result "Pike writes your name on a slip, folds it twice, and drops it in a box with a great many others.".
  }
  // The draw, at dawn on the first of the month; one in four.
  Rule lottery_won when entered(party) and hour(clock) == 8 and day(clock) == 6 and dice(party) <= 25 says "At the weighing-yard gate the clerk calls the names drawn for the month. Yours is the third." {
    Retract entered(party). Assert licensed(party). Assert tolerates(hal, party). }
  Rule lottery_lost when entered(party) and hour(clock) == 8 and day(clock) == 6 and dice(party) > 25 says "The licences for the month are called at the weighing-yard gate. Your name is not among them." {
    Retract entered(party). }
  // Hal can be had for wine, or for coin, and is asleep by midnight most nights.
  Action bribe_hal(actor: group, site: place) "Give Hal Brewin a crown to look the other way" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hal, site) and state(hal, watching)
      and not tolerates(hal, actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 1.
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Increase quantity(hal, gold) by 1. Assert tolerates(hal, actor). }
    Result "Hal looks at the crown, and up the lane, and puts it in his boot. 'Never saw you,' he says, and unhooks the chain.".
  }
  Rule hal_sleeps when hour(clock) == 0 and state(hal, watching) { Assert state(hal, drunk). Assert asleep(hal). }
  Rule hal_wakes when hour(clock) == 6 and state(hal, drunk) { Assert state(hal, watching). Retract asleep(hal). }
  Thing chain_gate "the chain-gate" on well_stair {
    State locked blocking "An Office chain-gate hangs across the stair-head, padlocked.".
    State unhooked "The Office chain hangs unhooked from its staple.".
    Change unhook "Unhook the chain-gate" from locked to unhooked at well_head.
  }
  // The chain is Hal's to open, and the Mutual's crews go through it as he lets them.
  Initially Assert keyholder(hal, chain_gate). Initially Assert tolerates(hal, crew). Initially Assert tolerates(hal, ness).
  Rule chain_open_licensed when tolerates(hal, party) and state(chain_gate, locked) and (at(party, well_head) or at(party, well_foot)) { Assert state(chain_gate, unhooked). }
  // Unhooked under his nose, it is hooked again, and he remembers who did it.
  Rule chain_rehooked when state(chain_gate, unhooked) and perceives(hal, party) and not tolerates(hal, party)
    says "Hal Brewin gets up off his stool, hooks the chain back on its staple, and stands in front of it. 'No,' he says." {
    Assert state(chain_gate, locked). }
  Rule chain_shut when state(chain_gate, unhooked) and not at(party, well_head) and not at(party, well_foot) and state(hal, watching) { Assert state(chain_gate, locked). }

  // The bargain: half the debt, the day Garret walks into the hall with the one Dagny made it with.
  Relation forgiven(group).
  Event dagny_keeps_word near dagny when (travelsWith(garret, party) or following(garret, party)) and offered(dagny, party) and at(party, mutual_hall) and not forgiven(party) and kin(party, garret) "Dagny looks at Garret for a long moment, and then at you. She takes the rag off its nail and rubs out the number beside your name on the board, and chalks in another, half the size. 'Fourteen crowns,' she says. 'I keep my word. Sit him by the fire before he falls down.'" then {
    Assert forgiven(party). Assert cameUp(garret). Decrease owes(party, dagny) by 14. }
  Relation broughtBy(group, group).
  Rule brought_by when travelsWith(garret, party) and not broughtBy(garret, party) { Assert broughtBy(garret, party). }
  Rule led_by when following(garret, party) and not broughtBy(garret, party) { Assert broughtBy(garret, party). }
  Event crew_brought_him near dagny when at(garret, mutual_hall) and not broughtBy(garret, party) and at(party, mutual_hall) and kin(party, garret) "Garret is by the hall fire with a blanket round him and a bowl in his hands, and the crew who brought him up are drinking. Dagny does not look at you. Your number on the board is the same as it was.".

  Objective find_garret when not cameUp(garret) and asleep(garret) and kin(party, garret) "Garret, your uncle, is held in an open granary vault under Quell. Dagny will halve your debt if you bring him up.".
  Objective bring_garret when not cameUp(garret) and not asleep(garret) "Garret is awake, and slow, and hungry, a long way under Quell. Bring him up to the Mutual's hall.".
  Objective held_alive when knows(party, garret_held) and not knows(party, doran_breathed) and not knows(party, prayer_label) "Are the held truly alive? In Ennick they visit theirs once a month to watch them breathe.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/stairhead.k:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // Stairhead House on the lip of the Scarp, the Arbiters' Way beneath it, and the Vault at its foot.
  Place stairhead "Stairhead House" is settlement within ghessil at 0, 3.
  Place arbiters_way "the Arbiters' Way" is site within ghessil at 0, 4.
  Place stair_top "the head of the Stair" is room within stairhead at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place chapel_sh "the chapel of Stairhead" is room within stairhead at 1, 1.
  Place vestry_sh "the vestry" is room within stairhead at 2, 1.
  Place strongroom "the strongroom" is room within stairhead at 2, 2.
  Place chapter "the chapter house" is room within stairhead at 1, 2.
  Place platform "the platform" is room within stairhead at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place way_upper "the upper Way" is level within arbiters_way.
  Place way_lower "the lower Way" is level within arbiters_way.
  Place way_door_room "under the platform" is room within way_upper at 0, 0 underground.
  Place counting_stair "the Stair That Counts" is room within way_upper at 0, 1 underground.
  Place separation_gallery "the Gallery of the Separation" is room within way_lower at 0, 2 underground.
  Place vault_ward "the Ward of the Vault" is room within way_lower at 0, 3 underground.
  Place arbiter_vault "the Arbiters' Vault" is room within way_lower at 0, 4 underground.

  Passage gorge_road "the gorge road" is road between lower_road and stair_top taking 4 hours.
  Passage chapel_door_sh "the chapel door" is door between stair_top and chapel_sh.
  Passage vestry_door "the vestry door" is door between chapel_sh and vestry_sh.
  Passage strong_door "the strongroom door" is door between vestry_sh and strongroom.
  Passage chapter_door "the chapter house door" is door between chapel_sh and chapter.
  Passage platform_steps "the platform steps" is steps between stair_top and platform.
  // The House's platform, which its brothers take for a Seridane signal station, is the Way's door.
  Passage way_mouth "a stair under the platform's flagstones" is stair between platform and way_door_room hidden until way_found.
  Passage way_down "the Way, past the Door" is passage between way_door_room and counting_stair taking 2 hours.
  Passage counted_way "the ringing steps" is stair between counting_stair and separation_gallery taking 3 hours.
  Passage gallery_way "the length of the relief" is passage between separation_gallery and vault_ward taking 12 hours.
  Passage ward_way "the Ward's threshold" is doorway between vault_ward and arbiter_vault.

  Observe stair_top_scene at stair_top when true "The Stair road comes up beside the falls to a walled house of grey stone on the lip of the Scarp. Bells mark the offices. Below, four falls stand one above another, and the lowland goes off green to the edge of the sky.".
  Observe chapel_scene_sh at chapel_sh when true "A plain Arbitral chapel. The brothers sing seven offices a day; at the night office the cellarer hangs his keys in the vestry, and every man of them is in here.".
  Observe vestry_scene at vestry_sh when true "A narrow vestry that smells of wet wool and beeswax, copes hung in a row, and by the door a row of iron hooks worn bright where seven offices a day have hung seven kinds of key.".
  Observe platform_scene at platform when true "An old stone platform older than the House, set with bronze fittings in a ring. The brothers dry washing on it. The fittings are mirror mounts, though nobody here knows it.".
  Discovery way_found "Under the platform's centre flagstones a stair goes down into rock that has not changed since it was cut: the Way's door is the House's own platform." {
    Found by searching platform "The centre flagstones ring hollow. Under them, a stair of white stone goes down into rock that has the look of something that has never once been touched by weather.".
  }

  // Prior Aurel Mance and Brother Tam (Stairhead House).
  Person mance "Prior Aurel Mance" at chapel_sh {
    Role "Prior of Stairhead House". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Greets "The Prior of Stairhead is kneeling at the altar rail with his back to the door, his hands folded over a letter he has plainly read many times. He finishes his prayer, which takes a decorous while. 'You find me at my offices,' he says. 'Brother Tam will see you have what you need. The house is open to pilgrims, and closed to explorers; I trust you will tell me which you are.'".
  }
  Person tam "Brother Tam" at chapel_sh {
    Role "the cellarer". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
  }
  Initially Assert serves(tam, mance).
  Topic mance_stone with mance "Ask the prior what the mother-church wants" when true once {
    Says "'The Long Hour, which the old king keeps below,' says Mance, 'and whatever comes up the Plumb.' He folds his hands over a letter he has plainly read many times. 'The mother-church holds that a relic of the Virina lies under this plateau. A stone that sings. I am instructed to have it before the Crown does, and to be seen praying while I do.'".
  }
  // Buys reads only the shared catalog, so a kind of this module's own cannot be bought by Buys (ledger, 24).
  Action sell_plates(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Sell the Long Hour to the prior for six hundred crowns" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(mance, site) and memberOf(carrier, actor)
      and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(long_hour, carrier).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve drop(long_hour, carrier).
    On success { Assert keeps(mance, long_hour). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 600. }
    Result "Mance turns every plate to the light before he counts out the coin, and then he counts it twice.".
  }
  Kind strong_key "the strongroom key" is tool worth 0 weighing 0 described "A heavy iron key on a ring.".
  Thing key_hooks "the hooks by the vestry door" at vestry_sh {
    Holds.
    State empty_hook "The hooks by the vestry door are empty.".
    State keys_hung "The cellarer's keys hang on the hook by the vestry door.".
  }
  Item strongkey "the strongroom key" is strong_key in key_hooks owned by tam.
  // The night office: the brothers in chapel, the keys on the hook, the vestry unwatched.
  Rule night_office when hour(clock) == 0 and state(key_hooks, empty_hook) and inside(strongkey, key_hooks) { Assert state(key_hooks, keys_hung). }
  Rule office_ends when hour(clock) == 1 and state(key_hooks, keys_hung) { Assert state(key_hooks, empty_hook). }
  Thing strong_lock "the strongroom lock" on strong_door {
    State locked blocking "The strongroom door is iron-bound and locked.".
    State open "The strongroom door stands open.".
    Change unlock_strong "Unlock the strongroom" from locked to open needing strongkey.
    Change pick_strong "Pick the strongroom lock" from locked to open needing lockwork.
  }
  Observe strong_scene at strongroom when true "Chests, a reliquary, and a shelf of sealed papers under the prior's seal. On a cushion, as if it were holy, a clear block the size of a hearthstone.".
  Discovery ottavine_note "Prior Ottavine's note on the Ennick holding prayer: a Seridane granary formula, painted on the grain jars; it means hold one season, then give it out." {
    Source ottavine_papers "Prior Ottavine's sealed papers" at strongroom readable by party.
  }
  Observe ottavine_label near party when knows(party, ottavine_note) and not knows(party, prayer_label) "Ottavine had it forty years ago, in a hand that does not shake: the prayer is a grain jar's label." teaches prayer_label.
  Discovery church_letters "Letters from the mother-church to Stairhead, eighty years of them, asking about 'a stone that sings below'.".
  Thing letters_box "a box of letters" at strongroom {
    State shut_box "A box of letters under the mother-church's seal.".
    State read_box "The mother-church's letters lie open, eighty years of them.".
    Change read_letters "Break the seal and read the mother-church's letters" from shut_box to read_box.
  }
  Observe letters_read at strongroom when state(letters_box, read_box) "Every one asks the same thing in other words: whether the prior has heard of a stone that sings, below." teaches church_letters.
  Thing ilis_block "Ilis's block" at strongroom {
    State resting "A clear block the size of a hearthstone sits on a cushion. It has no temperature.".
    Tries listening.
  }
  Observe block_wind near ilis_block when tried(ilis_block, listening) "It gives back a sound, very faint, from the day it stopped, out on the heath before anyone was born. It is only wind.".

  // The Arbiters' Way (The Undersun, The Arbiters' Way): ordinary rock kept unchanged by the Virina, which nothing of
  // the Varakiiri can enter. Four gates test whoever walks it; each is answered from the world's own history.
  Observe way_door_scene at way_door_room when true "A door of white stone with no hinges, in white rock. Over it, in a hand the eye follows easily, is carved one question: WAS THE HOUR GIVEN?".
  Discovery hour_fell "The hour was not given: it fell. A thing came down out of a clear sky on an autumn night, and the crane-priests of the lake wrote it down before any Seridane claimed it.".
  Thing the_door "the Door" on way_down {
    State asking blocking "The Door asks whether the hour was given.".
    State answered "The Door stands open.".
    State sealed_year blocking "The Door is shut, and will be, the carving says, for a year and a day.".
    Change answer_fell "Answer that the hour fell, and was not given" from asking to answered after learning hour_fell.
    Change answer_argued "Answer as the Coverers argued: it fell" from asking to answered after learning coverer_case.
  }
  Measure doorSealedAt(entity).
  Action answer_given(actor: group, site: place) "Answer that the hour was given" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, way_door_room) and state(the_door, asking).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert state(the_door, sealed_year). Set doorSealedAt(the_door) to watch(clock). }
    Result "The Door does not move. Below the question, letters you had not seen fill with light: a year and a day.".
  }
  Rule door_reopens when state(the_door, sealed_year) and watch(clock) >= doorSealedAt(the_door) + 52704 { Assert state(the_door, asking). }

  Observe counting_scene at counting_stair when true "The Way goes down by a stair of nine thousand steps. Each rings a note when trodden, and each note is different, and they do not repeat.".
  Thing ringing "the ringing steps" on counted_way is scenery {
    State uncounted blocking "The steps ring under your feet. A walker who loses the count, the carving at the top says, comes back to the top.".
    State counted "You have the count of the steps, and the stair lets you down.".
    Change count_names "Count the steps aloud in the twelve hour-names, round and round" from uncounted to counted after learning hour_names.
  }
  Action count_numbers(actor: group, site: place) "Count the steps in numbers" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, counting_stair) and state(ringing, uncounted).
    Time 18.
    Result "Somewhere past four thousand the notes run together, and you find you have said a number twice. You are standing at the top again, and three hours have gone.".
  }

  Observe relief_scene at separation_gallery when true "A relief two kilometres long, carved by no hand you know: a war across a sky divided, figures with light for wings and figures made of darkness and hooks, struck and striking; and below them tall figures in white, in a ring, holding the world apart like the pages of a book.".
  Relation wroteDown(group).
  Action write_as_you_walk(actor: group, site: place) "Walk the relief writing down only what you see" {
    Description "A day's walk. The Remembrancer at its end asks what you saw, and lets through only those who add nothing.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, separation_gallery) and not wroteDown(actor) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 72.
    On success { Assert wroteDown(actor). }
    Result "You walk it slowly, a day long, and write down what is carved and nothing else. Your hand aches.".
  }
  Person gallery_keeper "a Remembrancer" at separation_gallery {
    Role "a servant of the Virina, tall, made of the sound of bells". Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Guards gallery_way.
    State asking_g blocking "At the end of the relief a figure made of the sound of bells waits to ask what you saw.".
  }
  Topic keeper_tell with gallery_keeper "Tell the Remembrancer what you saw" when wroteDown(actor) once {
    Says "You read it from what you wrote. The Remembrancer hears it through to the last line and does not interrupt. 'Nothing added,' it says, in many bells. 'Go down.'".
    On discuss { Assert tolerates(gallery_keeper, actor). }
  }
  Topic keeper_memory with gallery_keeper "Tell the Remembrancer what you remember of it" when not wroteDown(actor) and not tolerates(gallery_keeper, actor) {
    Says "You tell it. Somewhere in the telling you say the dark figures had faces, and they had not. 'Added,' says the Remembrancer, gently, and you are standing at the start of the relief.".
  }

  // The Ward of the Vault: three questions, in order. A party guessing is turned away for a year.
  Discovery held_feed "What the held feed: the instant a person is held, their moment is taken and laid in the Undersun as a keystone. The Holdfolk's mercy has been building the Masonry's vaults for three hundred and forty years.".
  Observe ward_scene_v at vault_ward when true "A round white chamber with a white door, and over it three questions in a ring: WAS THE HOUR GIVEN? WHO KILLED THE KEEPER'S DAUGHTER? WHAT DO THE HELD FEED?".
  Thing vault_seal "the Ward" on ward_way {
    State first_q blocking "The first question is lit: was the hour given?".
    State second_q blocking "The second question is lit: who killed the keeper's daughter?".
    State third_q blocking "The third question is lit: what do the held feed?".
    State warded "The Ward is dark, and the white door stands open.".
    State turned blocking "The Ward is dark and the door shut. It will be so for a year.".
    Change ward_one "Answer: it fell" from first_q to second_q after learning hour_fell.
    Change ward_one_argued "Answer: it fell, as the Coverers said" from first_q to second_q after learning coverer_case.
    Change ward_two "Answer: Answerer loyalists, her father's men" from second_q to third_q after learning selane_murdered.
    Change ward_three "Answer: the Masonry; the held are its keystones" from third_q to warded after learning held_feed.
  }
  Action ward_guess(actor: group, site: place) "Answer the lit question as best you can guess" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, vault_ward)
      and (state(vault_seal, first_q) or state(vault_seal, second_q) or state(vault_seal, third_q)).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert state(vault_seal, turned). Set doorSealedAt(vault_seal) to watch(clock). }
    Result "The light goes out of the questions one by one, and the white door does not open.".
  }
  Rule ward_reopens when state(vault_seal, turned) and watch(clock) >= doorSealedAt(vault_seal) + 52560 { Assert state(vault_seal, first_q). }

  // U6, the Arbiters' Vault: Ithmar in its cage of rods, the Tally, and a Remembrancer at the door.
  Kind ithmar_kind "Ithmar" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0
    described "A hen's egg of something like dark opal, cut with sigils the mind will not name. It hums at the pitch of the note under the Pit.".
  Kind tally_kind "the Virina's Tally" is tool worth 0 weighing 2
    described "A rod of white metal marked like a ruler. It shows how much of the Keeping has been cut away; in the Keeping, how far any moment is from now.".
  Observe arbiter_scene at arbiter_vault when true "A white chamber, round, plain, very old and perfectly clean. The floor hums.".
  Thing cage "a cage of white rods" at arbiter_vault {
    Holds.
    State caged "In the centre of the chamber a jewel the size of a hen's egg hangs in the air in a cage of white rods. It is engraved with sigils the eye can follow and the mind will not name.".
  }
  Item ithmar "Ithmar" is ithmar_kind in cage.
  Item tally "the Virina's Tally" is tally_kind at arbiter_vault owned by remembrancer.
  Observe tally_seen at arbiter_vault when at(tally, arbiter_vault) "Against the wall leans a rod of white metal, marked like a ruler.".
  Person remembrancer "the Remembrancer of the Vault" at arbiter_vault {
    Role "a servant of the Virina, at the door". Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Objects "'Why do you carry the Tally away?' asks the Remembrancer, in many bells. 'Say it truly, and it is lent.'".
  }
  Discovery quarrying "The Masonry is cutting Imbar's past away through the seed, a season at a time, and since the year 371 more than thirty hollows have been quarried from the Keeping; the Tally measures how much.".
  Topic remembrancer_tally with remembrancer "Tell the Remembrancer why you would carry the Tally" when knows(actor, quarrying) once {
    Says "'To prove to the plateau how fast its past is being taken,' you say, 'and to find my way in the Keeping.' The Remembrancer is silent a long time, which is many bells not ringing. 'True,' it says, 'and sufficient. It is lent.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(remembrancer, tally, actor). }
  }
  Topic remembrancer_help with remembrancer "Ask the Remembrancer to help keep Imbar" when true once {
    Says "'It is yours to keep,' says the Remembrancer, courteously and at length. 'The planes were parted so that each could keep itself. We tend what is kept. We do not fight for it.' It inclines its head toward the jewel. 'A living hand on Ithmar walks the Keeping. Whoever touches the hand goes with it.'".
  }
  Topic remembrancer_quarry with remembrancer "Ask the Remembrancer what the Tally shows" when true once {
    Says "'How much of the Keeping has been cut away,' says the Remembrancer. 'Since your year 371, thirty-one hollows, most of them in your last years. Each is a season nobody can remember, and claims that rested on it are loose.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, quarrying). }
  }

  // The Concord (The Corbel and the Concord), compactly: called to Stairhead when the Corbel can no longer be denied;
  // each seat for or against three motions; evidence shown moves the seats that care about it; a vote.
  Kind motion. Entity motion_cover: motion "cover the Pit again". Entity motion_descend: motion "a sanctioned descent for Ithmar".
  Entity motion_bargain: motion "bargain with the Interlocutor".
  Relation favours(group, motion). Relation seat(group). Relation convened(place). Relation redLine(group, motion).
  Measure tally_of(motion). Relation counted(group, motion). Relation passed(motion). Relation voting(place).
  Rule concord_called when not convened(chapter) and ((knows(party, corbel_seen) and knows(party, sinking)) or day(clock) >= 720)
    says "Riders go out from Sorne along every road on the plateau: the Crown calls a Concord at Stairhead House, of every power that will come." {
    Assert convened(chapter). Assert at(aske, chapter). Assert at(ayzhe, chapter). Assert at(bren, chapter).
    Assert at(dagny, chapter). Assert at(mance, chapter). Assert at(ruan, chapter). }
  Initially Assert seat(aske). Initially Assert seat(ayzhe). Initially Assert seat(bren). Initially Assert seat(dagny).
  Initially Assert seat(mance). Initially Assert seat(ruan).
  Initially Assert favours(aske, motion_cover). Initially Assert favours(aske, motion_descend).
  Initially Assert favours(mance, motion_descend).
  Initially Assert redLine(bren, motion_cover). Initially Assert redLine(aske, motion_bargain).
  Observe concord_scene at chapter when convened(chapter) "The chapter house is full: the Warden in his sash for the Crown; Ayzhe of the Split Ear; Bren of Ennick with his hood in his hands; Dagny Ferrow for the Mutual; the prior at the head of the table; Ruan Haldane for the Waiting. Nobody sits next to anybody they can help it.".
  // Evidence, shown with its proof, moves every seat that cares about it.
  Action show_feeding(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Concord what the held feed" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter)
      and knows(actor, held_feed) and not shownTo(chapter, held_feed).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert shownTo(chapter, held_feed). Retract redLine(bren, motion_cover). }
    Result "Bren asks for a recess, and is gone an hour. When he comes back he says that Ennick will stop holding, and that it will not have the Pit covered while one of its held is still in the glass.".
  }
  Action show_procession(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Concord the procession's warning: the Masonry takes from the newest backward" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter)
      and knows(actor, newest_backward) and not shownTo(chapter, newest_backward).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert shownTo(chapter, newest_backward). Assert redLine(ruan, motion_bargain). Assert favours(ruan, motion_descend). }
    Result "The Waiting's elder goes white. Nobody at the table will speak for bargaining after that.".
  }
  Action show_way(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Concord that the Way to the jewel is under this house" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter)
      and knows(actor, way_found) and not shownTo(chapter, way_found).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert shownTo(chapter, way_found). Assert favours(dagny, motion_descend). Assert favours(ruan, motion_descend). }
    Result "The prior's seat is suddenly worth a great deal, and he knows it. The Mutual and the Waiting come round to a sanctioned descent.".
  }
  Action show_breach(actor: group, site: place) "Name to the Concord who cut the Breach" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter)
      and knows(actor, breach_cut) and not shownTo(chapter, breach_cut).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert shownTo(chapter, breach_cut). Retract at(ayzhe, chapter). Assert at(ayzhe, split_ear_camp). }
    Result "Ayzhe stands up before you have finished, and does not look at Bren, who has not moved. The Split Ear ride south that afternoon. The Tovash seat is empty.".
  }
  Relation shownTo(place, fact).
  Discovery newest_backward "The Masonry quarries a world's past from the newest moment backward: when it reached the beginning of the procession's world, that world was not.".
  Action call_vote(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Concord to vote" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter) and convened(chapter) and not voting(chapter).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert voting(chapter). }
    Result "The prior calls the seats, one by one.".
  }
  // A motion passes when four seats there favour it and no seat there holds a red line against it.
  Rule vote_counts when voting(chapter) and seat(?s) and at(?s, chapter) and favours(?s, ?m) and not counted(?s, ?m) {
    Increase tally_of(?m) by 1. Assert counted(?s, ?m). }
  Query blocked(m: motion) means redLine(?s, m) and at(?s, chapter).
  Relation onTable(motion).
  Initially Assert onTable(motion_cover). Initially Assert onTable(motion_descend). Initially Assert onTable(motion_bargain).
  Rule motion_passes when voting(chapter) and onTable(?m) and tally_of(?m) >= 4 and not blocked(?m) and not passed(?m)
    says "The Concord resolves: {?m}." { Assert passed(?m). }
  Observe concord_descend at chapter when passed(motion_descend) and not knows(party, way_found) "The Concord, the chorus of the seats, has sanctioned a descent. The prior, very stiffly, tells the seats what the mother-church has always suspected and he has lately confirmed: there is a stair under his platform." teaches way_found.
  Rule descent_sanctioned when passed(motion_descend) and not admits(aske, party) { Assert admits(aske, party). }
}

data/adventures/patient-star/stilling.ky:
Module stilling "The stilling: what the Late Sun's direct light does to whatever drinks it" {
  // The four laws (The Land and Its Laws): the stilling travels only in direct light, silica passes it and stops,
  // water and flesh drink it and slow, iron sheds it as heat. This module is the third law, as it bears on people:
  // where the light falls, who is in it, what they wear, how slow it leaves them, and how they come back.

  // Ground the light falls on: lit glass, a lamp-chamber, a vault with its shutter open, a leak in the plaster. A
  // place is lit by a fact (litGround) or by a rule (lit), so that a shutter or a mirror can light and darken it.
  Relation litGround(place). Relation shadeOf(place).
  Query lit(p: place) means litGround(p) and not shadeOf(p).

  // Dose, in twenty-fourths of a point: an hour bare in direct light is a point (24); an hour in full felt a
  // quarter of one (6). Recovery is two points an hour out of the light, faster while someone is deeply slowed.
  Measure dose(entity).
  // Full umber felt: the cloak, the hood and the mitts. Counterfeit felt looks the same and is no felt at all.
  // What sheds the stilling when worn: umber felt, Selane's Veil.
  Relation shields(itemkind).
  Query felted(m: member) means wearing(?f, m) and itemKind(?f, ?k) and shields(?k).
  // Someone the light does not slow (Saro, whose bones are stillglass).
  Relation unslowed(entity).
  // Someone who is not of the company and wears felt, by what is said of them.
  Relation feltClad(group).

  Rule soaks when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and at(?c, ?p) and lit(?p) and not felted(?m) and not unslowed(?m)
    and not heldDeep(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by 4. }
  Rule soaks_felted when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and at(?c, ?p) and lit(?p) and felted(?m)
    and not unslowed(?m) and not heldDeep(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by 1. }
  Rule others_soak when at(?g, ?p) and lit(?p) and slowable(?g) and not feltClad(?g) and not heldDeep(?g) {
    Increase dose(?g) by 4. }
  Rule others_soak_felted when at(?g, ?p) and lit(?p) and slowable(?g) and feltClad(?g) and not heldDeep(?g) {
    Increase dose(?g) by 1. }
  // Out of the light: two points an hour, and twelve an hour while someone is held deeper than a tenth.
  Query unlitFor(x: entity) means (memberOf(x, ?c) and at(?c, ?p) and not lit(?p)) or (at(x, ?q) and not lit(?q)).
  // A decrease that would go below nothing stops play, and there is no min(), so the last of it is set to nothing.
  Rule recovers when unlitFor(?x) and dose(?x) >= 8 and dose(?x) <= 288 { Decrease dose(?x) by 8. }
  Rule recovers_last when unlitFor(?x) and dose(?x) > 0 and dose(?x) < 8 { Set dose(?x) to 0. }
  Rule recovers_deep when unlitFor(?x) and dose(?x) > 288 { Decrease dose(?x) by 48. }
  // A way across lit ground (the Collar Road, the filament, a leak across a doorway) doses whoever crosses it, once
  // per crossing: so much bare, so much in felt. There is no division, so both are said.
  Measure wayDose(passage). Measure wayDoseFelted(passage).
  Relation dosedOn(member, passage).
  Rule way_doses when tookWay(?c, ?w) and company(?c) and wayDose(?w) > 0 and memberOf(?m, ?c) and not dosedOn(?m, ?w)
    and not felted(?m) and not unslowed(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by wayDose(?w). Assert dosedOn(?m, ?w). }
  Rule way_doses_felted when tookWay(?c, ?w) and company(?c) and wayDoseFelted(?w) > 0 and memberOf(?m, ?c)
    and not dosedOn(?m, ?w) and felted(?m) and not unslowed(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by wayDoseFelted(?w). Assert dosedOn(?m, ?w). }
  Rule way_passed when dosedOn(?m, ?w) and memberOf(?m, ?c) and not tookWay(?c, ?w) { Retract dosedOn(?m, ?w). }
  // Who the light can slow besides the company: the people of a module that says so.
  Relation slowable(group).

  // At a point, half speed: everything takes twice as long and companions seem to hurry. A slowed member goes at half
  // their speed (the shared rules' speed, in hundredths), and the company at its slowest member's; when the dose is
  // gone, their own. (Written at first as no capacity to carry, the only pace a module could then change: ledger, 1.)
  Query slowedMember(m: member) means dose(m) >= 24.
  Query slowedCompany(c: group) means memberOf(?m, c) and slowedMember(?m).
  Rule slowing when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and slowedMember(?m) and speed(?m) != 50 { Set speed(?m) to 50. }
  Rule quickening when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and not slowedMember(?m) and speed(?m) == 50 { Set speed(?m) to 0. }
  // In a fight, slowed is Orsino's slow: a blow fewer, late to move. Laid on whoever is slowed, an hour at a time.
  Hazard stilled "the stilling" means "Apply slow to ally for 1 hour.".
  Relation slowLaid(group). Measure slowSince(group).
  Rule slow_laid when company(?c) and slowedCompany(?c) and not slowLaid(?c) {
    Assert strikes(stilled, ?c). Assert slowLaid(?c). Set slowSince(?c) to watch(clock). }
  Rule slow_renewed when company(?c) and slowLaid(?c) and watch(clock) >= slowSince(?c) + 6 { Retract slowLaid(?c). }
  // At twelve points, a tenth: they cannot leave without being led.
  Query stoppedMember(m: member) means dose(m) >= 288.
  Rule stopping when memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) and stoppedMember(?m) and not hobbled(?c) { Assert hobbled(?c). }
  Rule starting when hobbled(?c) and company(?c) and not stoppedCompany(?c) and stilled(?c) {
    Retract hobbled(?c). Retract stilled(?c). }
  Query stoppedCompany(c: group) means memberOf(?m, c) and stoppedMember(?m).
  Relation stilled(group).
  Rule stilled_mark when hobbled(?c) and company(?c) and stoppedCompany(?c) and not stilled(?c) { Assert stilled(?c). }
  // Held: past a hundred points, one breath every few minutes.
  Query heldDeep(x: entity) means dose(x) >= 2400.

  Observe slow_feel near ?c when company(?c) and slowedCompany(?c) and not stoppedCompany(?c) "Your own footsteps sound late on the stone, your limbs are heavy, and the world has begun to hurry around you.".
  Observe stopped_feel near ?c when company(?c) and stoppedCompany(?c) "Every thought takes an hour to finish. You could not walk out of here alone if your life hung on it.".
}

data/adventures/patient-star/tamaun.kyr:
Module season "Hold One Season" {
  // Tamaun's upper city: the West Gallery from Quell and the Neck, the Shallows lit by mirrors, and the Granaries
  // lit by direct light through channels. Everything here is underground and dark unless a mirror throws light on it.
  Place gallery "the West Gallery" is level within tamaun.
  Place shallows "the Shallows" is level within tamaun.
  Place granaries "the Granaries" is level within tamaun.

  Place well_foot "the foot of the North Well" is room within gallery at 0, 0 underground.
  Place before_neck "the West Gallery, at the Neck" is room within gallery at 1, 0 underground.
  Place west_gate "the West Gate" is room within shallows at 0, 1 underground.
  Place road_north "the Mirror Road, north stretch" is room within shallows at 1, 0 underground.
  Place lamp_chamber "the third lamp-chamber" is room within shallows at 2, 0 underground.
  Place road_south "the Mirror Road, south stretch" is room within shallows at 1, 2 underground.
  Place bunks "the Bunks" is room within shallows at 0, 2 underground.
  Place plate_hall "the Plate Hall" is room within shallows at 2, 2 underground.
  Place ring "the Granary Ring" is room within granaries at 1, 1 underground.
  Place vault "the ninth vault" is room within granaries at 1, 0 underground.
  Place fox_vault "the fourth vault" is room within granaries at 2, 1 underground.
  Place waking_ward "the Waking Ward" is room within granaries at 0, 1 underground.
  Place flood_line "the Flood Line" is room within granaries at 1, 2 underground.
  Place sluice_head "the Sluice" is room within granaries at 2, 2 underground.

  Passage well_stair "the North Well stair" is stair between well_head and well_foot.
  Passage west_gallery "the West Gallery" is tunnel between well_foot and before_neck taking 3 hours.
  Passage neck "the Neck" is crawl between before_neck and west_gate taking 20 minutes.
  Passage gate_arch "the West Gate arch" is arch between west_gate and road_north.
  Passage slot_north "the north light-slot gallery" is passage between road_north and lamp_chamber taking 3 minutes.
  Passage mirror_road "the Mirror Road" is passage between road_north and road_south taking 5 minutes.
  Passage bunks_way "the passage to the Bunks" is passage between road_south and bunks taking 3 minutes.
  Passage hall_way "the Plate Hall doorway" is doorway between road_south and plate_hall.
  // My addition: a Seridane service stair from the Plate Hall down to the Granaries.
  Passage granary_stair "the service stair" is stair between plate_hall and ring.
  Passage vault_door "the ninth vault's doorway" is doorway between ring and vault.
  Passage fox_door "the fourth vault's doorway" is doorway between ring and fox_vault.
  Passage ward_door "the Waking Ward door" is doorway between ring and waking_ward.
  Passage flood_slope "the slope to the flood" is passage between ring and flood_line taking 3 minutes.
  Passage sluice_tunnel "the sluice tunnel" is passage between flood_line and sluice_head taking 5 minutes.

  // Dark, unless a mirror throws light here. The galleries a mirror serves are lit while it is aimed at them.
  Relation darkRoom(place).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(well_foot). Initially Assert darkRoom(before_neck). Initially Assert darkRoom(west_gate).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(road_north). Initially Assert darkRoom(road_south). Initially Assert darkRoom(bunks).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(plate_hall). Initially Assert darkRoom(ring). Initially Assert darkRoom(waking_ward).
  Initially Assert darkRoom(flood_line). Initially Assert darkRoom(sluice_head).
  Rule unlit_here when darkRoom(?p) and not bright(?p) and not unlit(?p) { Assert unlit(?p). }
  Rule lit_here when darkRoom(?p) and bright(?p) and unlit(?p) { Retract unlit(?p). }

  Observe well_foot_scene at well_foot when true "The stair comes down into a round chamber at the water's edge. The well water is warm as a bath. A tunnel two metres wide runs off east beside it, with a channel along one side.".
  Observe gallery_scene at before_neck when true "The West Gallery runs on east, wet underfoot, the water in its channel very still. Ahead, the roof comes down to meet the water.".

  // The Neck: the roof drops until there is a metre of air under it in late summer. The water in the West Gallery is
  // falling a hand a month, because the growth under the Late Sun is opening a channel that drains it (S1).
  Entity neck_water: scenery "the water at the Neck".
  Measure airGap(entity).
  Initially Set airGap(neck_water) to 100.
  Rule neck_falls when hour(clock) == 4 and dice(neck_water) <= 13 { Increase airGap(neck_water) by 1. }
  Observe neck_scene at before_neck when airGap(neck_water) < 110 "The ceiling drops until you wade with your face near the stone; under the Neck there is about a metre of air. On the wall a line of white crust shows where the water stood a season ago, a hand above where it stands now.".
  Observe neck_scene_low at before_neck when airGap(neck_water) >= 110 "Under the Neck there is more than a metre of air now. The white crust of the old waterline stands well above the water.".
  // Whoever marks the water and comes back to it learns it is falling.
  Measure markedAt(group).
  Relation marked(group).
  Action mark_water(actor: group, site: place) "Scratch a mark at the waterline under the Neck" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, before_neck) and not marked(actor) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert marked(actor). Set markedAt(actor) to airGap(neck_water). }
    Result "You scratch a line in the crust at the very edge of the water with the point of your knife.".
  }
  Discovery water_falling "The water in the West Gallery is falling, faster than any season accounts for: the mark at the Neck is dry above it within days. Something below is drawing it off." .
  Observe mark_dry at before_neck when marked(party) and airGap(neck_water) >= markedAt(party) + 2 "The line you scratched at the waterline is dry now, two fingers above the water." teaches water_falling.

  Observe gate_scene at west_gate when true "Beyond the Neck a cut-stone arch opens on a gallery. Chalk on the arch reads J.H. 341.".

  // The Mirror Road and the third lamp-chamber. The chamber's mirror throws safe, bounced light down one of three
  // galleries: the north stretch, the south stretch, or the Bunks. The chamber itself is a straight room: the Late Sun
  // is behind its window, and every minute there is dose (S4).
  Initially Assert litGround(lamp_chamber).
  Thing mirror "the great mirror" at lamp_chamber {
    State to_north "A bronze mirror two metres across stands on a cradle with a crank and worm-gear, throwing a beam out through the north slot. Brass scales are scratched on the cradle, and its pointer stands near the end of them.".
    State to_south "The great mirror is cranked round to the south slot, and its beam goes out that way.".
    State to_bunks "The great mirror is cranked round to the low slot that serves the Bunks.".
    Change north_south "Crank the mirror round to the south slot" from to_north to to_south.
    Change north_bunks "Crank the mirror round to the Bunks slot" from to_north to to_bunks.
    Change south_north "Crank the mirror round to the north slot" from to_south to to_north.
    Change south_bunks "Crank the mirror round to the Bunks slot" from to_south to to_bunks.
    Change bunks_north "Crank the mirror round to the north slot" from to_bunks to to_north.
    Change bunks_south "Crank the mirror round to the south slot" from to_bunks to to_south.
  }
  Relation aims(condition, place).
  Initially Assert aims(to_north, road_north). Initially Assert aims(to_south, road_south). Initially Assert aims(to_bunks, bunks).
  Query bright(p: place) means state(mirror, ?s) and aims(?s, p).
  Observe chamber_scene at lamp_chamber when true "A round chamber at the inner end of the gallery. One wall is a single sheet of stillglass three metres across, with blinding light behind it. Your shadow lies flat behind you on the floor.".
  Discovery mirrors_ending "The lamp-chamber mirrors are at the end of their travel. Their scales were set for a Late Sun that sank four centimetres a year; whatever they are aimed at now, they will not reach for long." {
    Found by searching lamp_chamber "The pointer on the cradle's brass scale stands two finger-widths from its stop. Below the last scratched mark, someone recently has scratched another, and another below that.".
  }

  // The gardens walk with the light: where bounced light has lain a long while, moss and fern and grass; where it has
  // left, they brown and die (S2). Greenness is reckoned by the watch, from none to a thousand.
  Measure green(place).
  Initially Set green(road_north) to 1000. Initially Set green(road_south) to 300. Initially Set green(bunks) to 0.
  Rule greening when darkRoom(?p) and bright(?p) and green(?p) < 1000 and dice(?p) <= 50 { Increase green(?p) by 1. }
  Rule browning when darkRoom(?p) and not bright(?p) and green(?p) > 0 { Decrease green(?p) by 1. }
  Observe north_lit at road_north when bright(road_north) "A ring gallery four metres wide. A bronze disc as big as a cartwheel is set in a ceiling niche, throwing grey-gold light along the passage. Swallows nest on its rim.".
  Observe north_dark at road_north when not bright(road_north) "A ring gallery four metres wide. A bronze disc as big as a cartwheel sits dull in its ceiling niche, and the swallows on its rim are quiet.".
  Observe north_garden at road_north when green(road_north) >= 600 "Moss covers the floor, ferns grow out of the cracks in the left-hand wall, and pale grass stands up to your knees.".
  Observe north_fading at road_north when green(road_north) < 600 and green(road_north) >= 200 "The grass lies over and is turning yellow. The ferns have begun to brown at the tips.".
  Observe north_dead at road_north when green(road_north) < 200 "Dead ferns, brown and dry, break when you brush them. The grass lies flat.".
  Observe south_lit at road_south when bright(road_south) "Light comes down the south stretch from a ceiling disc, onto stone that was bare not long ago.".
  Observe south_dark at road_south when not bright(road_south) "The south stretch of the Mirror Road is dark. A disc hangs dull in the ceiling niche.".
  Observe south_garden at road_south when green(road_south) >= 600 "A garden has come up here: moss, fern, and pale grass to the knee.".
  Observe south_shoots at road_south when green(road_south) < 600 and green(road_south) >= 100 "New green shoots, very small, come up between the stones in a band as straight as the edge of a shadow.".

  // A leak: a crack in the plaster where the Mirror Road meets the Plate Hall throws a blade of direct light across
  // the doorway. It is the commonest hazard in the city; it moves only when the plaster falls.
  Thing leak "a blade of white light" on hall_way {
    State shining "Where the plaster has cracked over the Plate Hall doorway, a blade of hard white light comes through and lies across the threshold.".
    State shaded "A hood of umber felt has been hung over the crack above the Plate Hall doorway.".
    Change shade "Hang felt over the crack" from shining to shaded consuming felt_scrap.
  }
  Initially Set wayDose(hall_way) to 2.
  Rule leak_shaded when state(leak, shaded) and wayDose(hall_way) > 0 { Set wayDose(hall_way) to 0. }

  // The Bunks: the Mutual's unlicensed crews, and their cold hearth.
  Observe bunks_scene at bunks when true "Rooms off the ring: bed niches cut in the rock, reading mirrors on pegs, tally marks by the doors. In one block, bedrolls, a cold hearth, Mutual tallies and a wine jar. One of the bed niches is yours.".
  Observe bunks_lit at bunks when bright(bunks) "Grey-gold light falls into the Bunks from the low slot in the ceiling. Someone has hung a shirt up to dry in it.".
  Person bunks_crew "the Bunks crew" at bunks {
    Role "four of the Mutual's unlicensed cutters, between shifts". Ancestry human. Numbers 4. Peaceable.
  }
  Relation grumbled(group).
  // An event happens once, seen or not; the crew grumble whenever someone comes in on them in the dark, so it is said
  // each time it is so.
  Observe bunks_darkened at bunks as event when not bright(bunks) and at(bunks_crew, bunks) and green(bunks) > 0 "One of the cutters in the Bunks looks up at the dead slot in the ceiling. 'Somebody's been at the third mirror again,' she says. 'Swing it back before the ferns go, or we'll be sleeping in the dark.'".
  Topic bunks_neck with bunks_crew "Ask the Bunks crew about the way down to the Granaries" when true once {
    Says "'Service stair, out of the back of the Plate Hall,' says a woman with her boots off. 'Mind the doorway. There's a crack in the plaster over it, and a blade of the straight light comes through. Run it, or hang a bit of felt over the crack.' She throws you a scrap of old felt. 'Keep that.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, felt_scrap) by 1. }
  }
  Topic bunks_outfall with bunks_crew "Ask the Bunks crew about other ways out" when true once {
    Says "'The Holdfolk say the old drain comes out above Ennick,' says the woman. 'The Outfall. Nine kilometres on your belly, and shut by the flood from Sowing to the end of summer. It should open any day now.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, outfall_known). }
  }
  Entity felt_scrap: good "scrap of felt".
  Discovery outfall_known "The Outfall, the Seridane's drain, runs nine kilometres from the Granaries' flood line to a spring cave in the cliff above Ennick; it is shut by the flood from Sowing to the end of summer.".

  // The Plate Hall: voice-plates in racks, a stylus on a cord, and Halu's stack by the door (S5).
  Observe plate_hall_scene at plate_hall when true "A long hall of racks for thin stillglass plates, most of the slots empty. By the door, twelve plates are stacked neatly, edges squared, as if someone meant to carry them away and will be back for them.".
  Thing tally_plate "a plate from the granary racks" at plate_hall {
    State silent "One rack is labelled with the sign the Seridane painted on their grain jars. A plate stands in it.".
    State playing "A clerk's voice, faint as wind, counts jars into a vault: a number, a breath, and then a line said quickly the same way each time, the way you would say a thing a thousand times a day. 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.'".
    Change play_tally "Draw a stylus along the granary plate" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Thing song_plate "a plate on its own on a shelf" at plate_hall {
    State silent "On a shelf by itself, a plate scratched along one edge with children's tally marks.".
    State playing "Children's voices, very small and far away, count in a ring: twelve words, round and round, and on the twelfth they all shout.".
    Change play_song "Draw a stylus along the children's plate" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Thing debate_plate "a plate from the debate" at plate_hall {
    State silent "In the end rack, two plates are cut with the Answerer and Coverer signs.".
    State playing "A woman's voice, a Coverer's: 'It was not given. Nothing gives a thing it cannot see. It fell, as a stone falls from a sling, and the lake wrote it down.' And a man, an Answerer, louder, threatening her by name.".
    Change play_debate "Draw a stylus along the debate plate" from silent to playing needing stylus.
  }
  Rule debate_ends when state(debate_plate, playing) and not at(party, plate_hall) { Assert state(debate_plate, silent). }
  Discovery coverer_case "The Coverers argued, on the debate plates, that the hour was not given but fell, and that the lake's own records said so.".
  Observe debate_heard at plate_hall when state(debate_plate, playing) "The Coverers said it fell." teaches coverer_case.
  Rule tally_ends when state(tally_plate, playing) and not at(party, plate_hall) { Assert state(tally_plate, silent). }
  Rule song_ends when state(song_plate, playing) and not at(party, plate_hall) { Assert state(song_plate, silent). }
  Discovery song_heard "The Plate Hall's counting song: children count twelve words in a ring, each on its own note.".
  Observe song_learned at plate_hall when state(song_plate, playing) "Each of the twelve words has its own note." teaches song_heard.
  Discovery tally_words "A Seridane granary clerk, counting jars into a vault, said the same line over each: 'Seri amar ka, dane tamaun eth. Seri amar ka, ithel sonne.'".
  Observe tally_heard at plate_hall when state(tally_plate, playing) "The same line, over each jar." teaches tally_words.

  // The Granary Ring and its vaults. Each vault has an umber shutter on a pulley; open, a bar of direct light comes
  // down its channel from the Pit wall and holds whatever is under it; shut, it lets whatever it held go (G2). The
  // pulley's cord is made off on a cleat by the doorway, so that the shutter is worked from outside the beam.
  Observe ring_scene at ring when true "A curving passage with forty vaults off it, numbered in Seridane signs over their doorways. In some, a bar of hard white light comes straight down from the ceiling onto the floor.".
  Discovery jars_painted "Every jar in the Granary Ring is painted with the same line of Seridane writing, and holds black dust.".
  Observe jars_seen at ring when not benighted(party) "Every jar in every vault is red-glazed and painted with the same line of words, and every jar you can see into holds black dust." teaches jars_painted.

  Thing shutter "the ninth vault's shutter" on vault_door {
    State open "In the ceiling of the ninth vault an umber shutter hangs open on its pulley, and a bar of white light comes down through the channel above it onto the floor.".
    State shut "The ninth vault's shutter is down. The vault is dark.".
    Change close_nine "Pull the shutter cord at the doorway" from open to shut at ring.
    Change open_nine "Let the shutter cord run" from shut to open at ring.
  }
  Initially Assert litGround(vault).
  Rule vault_lit when state(shutter, open) and not litGround(vault) { Assert litGround(vault). }
  Rule vault_unlit when state(shutter, shut) and litGround(vault) { Retract litGround(vault). Assert unlit(vault). }
  Rule vault_bright when state(shutter, open) and unlit(vault) { Retract unlit(vault). }
  Observe cleat_seen at ring when state(shutter, open) "Beside the ninth vault's doorway, a cord comes down out of the ceiling and is made off on a bronze cleat.".
  Observe vault_scene at vault when state(shutter, open) "Rows of red-glazed jars stand under the beam, each painted with the same line of words. In the middle of them a man in a cutter's felt hood stands with one hand out toward a jar, his eyes open.".
  Observe vault_dark_scene at vault when state(shutter, shut) "Rows of red-glazed jars, and the smell of old dust.".
  Kind granary_jars "a sack's worth of umber-glazed jars" is treasure worth 12 weighing 8
    described "Red-glazed Seridane grain jars, not a crack in one, each painted with the same line of writing and holding black dust. A collector in Sorne pays three crowns a jar.".
  Item jars "the ninth vault's jars" is granary_jars at vault.

  // The fourth vault holds a fox.
  Thing fox_shutter "the fourth vault's shutter" on fox_door {
    State open "An umber shutter hangs open in the ceiling, and the light comes down onto a fox that stands in it with its tail half lifted.".
    State shut "The fourth vault's shutter is down.".
    Change close_fourth "Pull the fourth vault's shutter cord" from open to shut at ring.
  }
  Initially Assert litGround(fox_vault).
  Person fox "a fox" at fox_vault { Role "a dog fox, held in the light mid-step". Species fox. Pronouns he. }
  Initially Assert asleep(fox). Initially Assert slowable(fox). Initially Set dose(fox) to 2400.
  Rule fox_unlit when state(fox_shutter, shut) and litGround(fox_vault) { Retract litGround(fox_vault). }
  Rule fox_wakes when asleep(fox) and dose(fox) < 288 { Retract asleep(fox). }
  Event fox_runs near fox when not asleep(fox) and at(fox, fox_vault) "The fox finishes its step, and the next. It looks round at the dark with its ears flat, and is gone down the ring like smoke." then {
    Retract at(fox, fox_vault). Assert at(fox, flood_line). }

  // The Waking Ward: where the Seridane held their sick, and where they woke in the dark when the light was cut (G3).
  Observe ward_scene_t at waking_ward when true "Long rooms of stone beds with leather straps rotted to threads. The ceiling channels are shuttered and dark.".
  Observe ward_walls at waking_ward when not benighted(party) "The writing starts at the door, scratched into the stone at the height of someone sitting up. Further in it is everywhere: walls, bed-edges, floor. Some is neat; some runs downhill. Near the far end it is low, at the height of someone lying down, and the scratches are shallow. You cannot read it, but you can tell that it was written in the dark. One word near the door has the same shape as the line on the granary jars.".
  Discovery ward_written "The Seridane held their sick in the Waking Ward. When the light was cut, the held woke in the dark and wrote on the walls until they died: names, and words over and over." {
    Found by searching waking_ward "Among the scratches, the same few words come again and again, low down and shallow at the end. One of them has been written so many times that the stone is worn smooth around it.".
  }

  // The Flood Line and the Sluice: the outer passages slope into warm clear water. In autumn the flood falls; from
  // Sowing to Haying it closes the Outfall's last stretch (G4). The Sluice lowers it, and sends it all down to Ennick.
  Measure flood(entity).
  Entity flood_water: scenery "the flood in the Granaries".
  Initially Set flood(flood_water) to 100.
  Relation sluiced(entity).
  Rule flood_falls when season(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) == 3 and flood(flood_water) > 40 { Decrease flood(flood_water) by 15. }
  Rule flood_sluiced when sluiced(flood_water) and hour(clock) == 3 and flood(flood_water) > 0 { Decrease flood(flood_water) by 20. }
  Observe flood_scene at flood_line when flood(flood_water) >= 60 "The passages slope down into still, warm, clear water. White shrimp scatter from your light. Where the Outfall goes on west, the water stands to the roof.".
  Observe flood_scene_low at flood_line when flood(flood_water) < 60 "The water has drawn back down the slope. Where the Outfall goes on west, there is air above the water now, a hand of it, then more.".
  Species outfall_eel "an Outfall eel" like great_pike temperament ambush
    described "An eel of the Ammer that swam up the warm Outfall as an elver two hundred years ago and never left: three metres of it, white about the jaw.".
  Person eels "Outfall eels" at flood_line {
    Role "two old eels lying in the flooded doorway". Species outfall_eel. Numbers 2.
    // They warn before they strike: as ambushers they killed a company on its first walk down the slope (M18-09).
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "Your light goes down into the clear water at the foot of the slope, and two white jaws turn up toward it out of the flooded doorway, slowly. Behind each, three metres of eel uncoils along the floor. They are in no hurry. This is theirs.".
  }
  Thing sluice "the Sluice" at sluice_head {
    State closed "A bronze gate stands in a stone frame at the head of a broad tunnel, with a geared wheel the size of a man. A trickle comes through it.".
    State opened "The Sluice stands open. The water goes through it with a sound like wind.".
    Change open_sluice "Wind the Sluice open" from closed to opened.
    Change close_sluice "Wind the Sluice shut" from opened to closed.
  }
  Rule sluice_runs when state(sluice, opened) and not sluiced(flood_water) { Assert sluiced(flood_water). }
  Rule sluice_stops when state(sluice, closed) and sluiced(flood_water) { Retract sluiced(flood_water). }
  Entity quell_wells: scenery "Quell's wells".
  Relation drained(entity). Relation washedOut(entity).
  Rule wells_drop when sluiced(flood_water) and flood(flood_water) < 40 and not drained(quell_wells) { Assert drained(quell_wells). }

  // Garret, held eleven months at about a hundredth, in the beam among the jars.
  Person garret "Garret" at vault {
    Role "a cutter of the Mutual, held in the light". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Plans 14 steps. Uses go, change_thing. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Joins "Garret puts a hand on your shoulder, to steady himself as much as anything. 'Up, then,' he says. 'Slowly.'".
  }
  Initially Assert asleep(garret). Initially Assert slowable(garret). Initially Assert feltClad(garret).
  Initially Set dose(garret) to 2400.
  Topic garret_held with garret "Speak to the man in the light" when asleep(garret) once {
    Says "Garret does not answer. His eyes are open and on the jar in front of him, and they do not come round to you. You wait for him to breathe, and count your own breaths while you wait, and get to forty before his chest moves. Whatever you said, he will hear it, if he hears it, some time next week.".
  }
  Measure watchedFor(entity).
  Rule watching_garret when at(party, vault) and heldDeep(garret) and at(garret, vault) and not benighted(party) { Increase watchedFor(garret) by 1. }
  Observe garret_moved at vault when heldDeep(garret) and at(garret, vault) and watchedFor(garret) >= 6 "You have watched him for an hour. His hand is a finger's width nearer the jar than it was, and his chest is higher.".
  Observe garret_slowing at vault when not heldDeep(garret) and asleep(garret) and at(garret, vault) "Garret's eyes are moving. They come round to you over a long time, and his lips part.".
  Observe garret_ring at ring when asleep(garret) and at(garret, ring) and not heldDeep(garret) "Garret lies on the floor of the Ring where he was dragged, his eyes moving very slowly from one thing to the next.".
  Rule garret_wakes when asleep(garret) and dose(garret) < 288 { Retract asleep(garret). Assert acceptsEscort(garret, party). }
  // He comes round whether or not anyone is there to see. What it was like is told to whoever first sees him awake:
  // an event would be spent unseen, so it is an observation that teaches its own having been seen (ledger, 4).
  Rule garret_willing when not asleep(garret) and not willing(garret, party) and not travelsWith(garret, party) and not cameUp(garret) { Assert willing(garret, party). }
  Entity garret_woke: fact "Garret has come round from eleven months in the light.".
  Observe garret_comes_round near garret as event when not asleep(garret) and not cameUp(garret) and not knows(party, garret_woke) "Garret finishes the reach he began eleven months ago, closes his hand on nothing, and sits down hard. 'Where's the light gone?' he says. 'Ness was just there.' He looks at you as at a stranger's child. 'You were never this tall. What month is it?' Told, he says nothing for a while. 'I'm hungry,' he says at last, as if that settled it." teaches garret_woke.
  Topic garret_month with garret "Tell Garret how long he stood there" when not asleep(garret) once {
    Says "'Eleven months,' Garret says after you, as if trying the words for size. 'It was Harvest. I had my hand out.' He looks at his hand. 'Ness said the light would not reach past the door. Ness said a lot of things.'".
  }
  Topic garret_ness with garret travelling "Ask Garret about Ness" when not asleep(garret) once {
    Says "'She wanted the jars,' says Garret. 'Three crowns a jar in Sorne, and there's forty in that vault. I said the light was moving, I'd seen it on the floor. She said go on then, if you're frightened.' He laughs, not much. 'So I went on.'".
  }
  // Pulled out by hand: whoever does it stands in the beam to do it.
  Action drag_out(actor: group, site: place) "Go into the beam and drag Garret out of it" {
    Description "Into the light, an arm round him, and back out to the Ring. It takes a few minutes in the beam.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, vault) and at(garret, vault)
      and state(shutter, open) and asleep(garret) and not hobbled(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Retract at(garret, vault). Assert at(garret, ring). Retract at(actor, vault). Assert at(actor, ring).
      Assert dragged(garret). }
    Result "You go in among the jars, get an arm round Garret, and haul. He comes like a felled tree, stiff and very slow, and you get him out over the threshold onto the Ring.".
  }
  Relation dragged(group).
  Relation cameUp(group).
  // Joined, he is a member of the company with a body of his own, and the dose was on the person he was: it is
  // carried over by hand (ledger, 6).
  Rule garret_dose_joins when travelsWith(garret, party) and dose(garret) > 0 {
    Set dose(member_garret_person) to dose(garret). Set dose(garret) to 0. }
  // Once he can walk, and nobody leads him, he makes his own slow way home to the Mutual's hall.
  Pursuit go_home for garret "making his slow way up to Quell" priority 20 when not asleep(garret) and not following(garret, party) and not travelsWith(garret, party) and not cameUp(garret) seeks at(garret, mutual_hall).
  Pursuit stay_close for garret "keeping close to you" priority 30 when following(garret, party) seeks together(garret, party).
  Rule garret_home when at(garret, mutual_hall) and not cameUp(garret) { Assert cameUp(garret). }
  Rule garret_brought when travelsWith(garret, party) and at(party, mutual_hall) and not cameUp(garret) { Assert cameUp(garret). }
  Initially Assert keyholder(garret, chain_gate).

  // Dagny's crew goes down on the fourth morning, when it has the felt, and Ness with them. At the Ring they argue; the crew pull the cord,
  // and Ness takes the jars.
  Rule crew_sets_out when day(clock) >= 4 and hour(clock) == 6 and not descended(crew) { Assert descended(crew). }
  Initially Assert keyholder(crew, chain_gate). Initially Assert keyholder(ness, chain_gate).
  Pursuit go_down for crew "going down after Garret" priority 20 when descended(crew) and asleep(garret) seeks at(crew, ring).
  Pursuit go_down for ness "going down with the crew" priority 20 when descended(crew) and not keeps(ness, jars) seeks at(ness, ring).
  Relation argued(group).
  Event crew_argue near crew when at(crew, ring) and at(ness, ring) and asleep(garret) and not argued(crew) "At the ninth vault's doorway Dagny's crew stand arguing in low voices. 'He'll keep,' Ness is saying. 'He's kept a year. Take the jars and come back for him with the sledge.' 'We came for him,' says the elder. 'And we go in for him when Dagny sends the long poles down, not before. I'll not have two of us stood in there.'" then { Assert argued(crew). Set arguedOn(crew) to day(clock). }
  Measure arguedOn(group).
  Pursuit free_him for crew "pulling the shutter cord on Garret" priority 25 when argued(crew) and day(clock) >= arguedOn(crew) + 3 and state(shutter, open) seeks state(shutter, shut).
  Action pack_jars(actor: group, site: place) "Pack the ninth vault's jars into a sack" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, ring) and at(jars, vault) and state(shutter, shut) and distinct(actor, party).
    Time 3.
    On success { Retract at(jars, vault). Assert keeps(actor, jars). }
    Seen "{actor} packs the jars from the ninth vault into a sack, wrapping each in straw.".
  }
  Pursuit take_jars for ness "packing the ninth vault's jars" priority 30 when at(ness, ring) and state(shutter, shut) and at(jars, vault) seeks keeps(ness, jars) using pack_jars.
  Pursuit go_back for ness "taking the jars up to sell" priority 20 when keeps(ness, jars) seeks at(ness, mutual_yard).
  Pursuit go_back for crew "going back up" priority 10 when descended(crew) and not asleep(garret) seeks at(crew, mutual_yard).
}

data/adventures/patient-star/undersun.ky:
Module season "The Patient Star" {
  // The Undersun (Tier II): an inverted citadel beneath the Late Sun, 300 metres across at its crown and 700 deep,
  // narrowing to a drilling tip. Every room is a moment cut from the plateau's past. Five rules: a room is a moment;
  // touch gives time; speech is laid; course-light doses; the name is the plan.
  Place undersun "the Undersun" is site within ghessil at 5, 1.
  Place crown "the Crown" is level within undersun.
  Place reach "the Seridane Reach" is level within undersun.
  Place silent_reach "the Silent Reach" is level within undersun.
  Place shaft_600 "the shaft at six hundred metres" is level within undersun.
  Place shaft_700 "the shaft at seven hundred metres" is level within undersun.
  Place shaft_foot "the foot of the shaft" is level within undersun.
  Place lreach "the Listeners' Reach" is level within undersun.
  Place tip "the Tip" is level within undersun.

  Place crown_entry "where the Courses broke through" is room within crown at 1, 0 underground.
  Place fall_chamber "the Fall" is room within crown at 0, 0 underground.
  Place fire_heart "the heart of the fire" is room within crown at 0, 1 underground.
  Place first_course "the First Course" is room within crown at 2, 0 underground.
  Place burning_wood "the Burning Wood" is room within crown at 1, 1 underground.
  Place crown_foot "the foot of the Crown" is room within crown at 1, 2 underground.

  Place reach_head "the head of the Seridane Reach" is room within reach at 1, 0 underground.
  Place granary_noon "the Granary at Noon" is room within reach at 0, 0 underground.
  Place schism "the Council of the Schism" is room within reach at 2, 0 underground.
  Place riot_hall "the Riot Hall" is room within reach at 1, 1 underground.
  Place bathhouse "the Bathhouse" is room within reach at 0, 1 underground.
  Place quarried "the Quarried Gallery" is room within reach at 2, 1 underground.
  Place reach_foot "the foot of the Seridane Reach" is room within reach at 1, 2 underground.

  Place shaft_top "the top of the shaft" is room within silent_reach at 0, 0 underground.
  Place plumb_mouth "the Plumb's mouth" is room within shaft_600 at 0, 1 underground.
  Place saro_stair "the top of Saro's stair" is room within shaft_700 at 0, 2 underground.
  Place shaft_bottom "the bottom of the shaft" is room within shaft_foot at 0, 3 underground.

  Place lreach_head "the head of the Listeners' Reach" is room within lreach at 1, 0 underground.
  Place breach_moment "the Breach, stopped" is room within lreach at 0, 0 underground.
  Place keystone_gallery "the Keystone Gallery" is room within lreach at 2, 0 underground.
  Place fair_moment "the Fair" is room within lreach at 1, 1 underground.
  Place tip_dome "the Tip" is room within tip at 0, 0 underground.

  // Course-light: every room of the Undersun is direct light for dose, and every room is laid.
  Initially Assert litGround(crown_entry). Initially Assert litGround(fall_chamber). Initially Assert litGround(fire_heart).
  Initially Assert litGround(first_course). Initially Assert litGround(burning_wood). Initially Assert litGround(crown_foot).
  Initially Assert litGround(reach_head). Initially Assert litGround(granary_noon). Initially Assert litGround(schism).
  Initially Assert litGround(riot_hall). Initially Assert litGround(bathhouse). Initially Assert litGround(quarried).
  Initially Assert litGround(reach_foot). Initially Assert litGround(shaft_top). Initially Assert litGround(plumb_mouth).
  Initially Assert litGround(saro_stair). Initially Assert litGround(shaft_bottom). Initially Assert litGround(lreach_head).
  Initially Assert litGround(breach_moment). Initially Assert litGround(keystone_gallery). Initially Assert litGround(fair_moment).
  Initially Assert litGround(tip_dome).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(granary_noon). Initially Assert laidRoom(riot_hall). Initially Assert laidRoom(schism).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(keystone_gallery). Initially Assert laidRoom(fair_moment). Initially Assert laidRoom(tip_dome).
  Initially Assert laidRoom(breach_moment). Initially Assert laidRoom(bathhouse).

  // The ways in: following Saro, or with a trowel, through the face of the Courses; or down the Plumb.
  Passage into_courses "into the Courses" is crawl between courses_face and crown_entry taking 20 minutes
    opening when travelsWith(saro, party) or holding(party, trowel_kind) "Course-glass cannot be cut, pierced or broken by anything you carry. A Mason's trowel lays and unlays it.".
  Passage plumb "the Plumb, by the rope" is shaft between coverers_works and plumb_mouth taking 1 hour needing rope.
  Initially Set wayDose(plumb) to 24. Initially Set wayDoseFelted(plumb) to 6.

  // The Crown's syllables were spoken before anyone listened: only the Keeping holds them, at the new moons; or
  // Lirem's astrolabe, held in the course-light, reads them off the courses.
  Discovery crown_map "The Crown's plan: its syllables, from the new moons of its first three centuries, laid out as rooms.".
  Passage fall_arch "a ribbed arch" is arch between crown_entry and fall_chamber.
  Passage dog_way "a round passage" is passage between crown_entry and first_course taking 3 minutes hidden until crown_map.
  Passage wood_edge "the edge of the Wood" is passage between crown_entry and burning_wood taking 5 minutes.
  Passage wood_line "the safe line through the smoke" is passage between burning_wood and crown_foot taking 20 minutes hidden until smoke_line.
  Passage fire_gaps "the gaps in the stopped fire" is passage between fall_chamber and fire_heart taking 5 minutes.
  Passage crown_down "the grammar stair" is stair between crown_foot and reach_head taking 10 minutes.

  Observe crown_entry_scene at crown_entry when true "Inside the Courses, light runs along every curve. The passage is coursed like masonry, banded dark and clear, without a seam, and it turns in ways stone would not.".
  Observe astrolabe_reads at crown_entry when carries(party, astrolabe) and not knows(party, crown_map) "Lirem's astrolabe swings in your hand until its pointer lies along the course-light. The rings turn of themselves, syllable by syllable, and you are reading a plan of rooms." teaches crown_map.

  // The Fall: the instant of impact, 2,290 BP. Stopped fire, a shock-front of compressed air, and the Splinter.
  Observe fall_scene at fall_chamber when true "A chamber sixty metres across, full of fire that does not move. Arcs of molten rock hang in the air like thrown ribbons. A curved sheet of something clear and rippled stands across the room, bending everything seen through it.".
  Thing shock_front "the shock-front" at fall_chamber {
    State standing "The clear rippled sheet stands across the chamber: air, compressed and stopped mid-blast.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(shock_front).
  Hazard slap "the shock-front's slap" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Rule front_released when touched(shock_front) says "The air goes. It throws you ten metres back through the arch." {
    Retract touched(shock_front). Assert strikes(slap, party). Assert at(party, crown_entry). }
  Thing stopped_fire "the stopped fire" on fire_gaps {
    State unmapped dangerous "Between the ribbons of fire there are gaps, but you cannot tell from in among them which go through.".
    State mapped "You have the gaps in the fire mapped from the door: a crooked way in, a crooked way out.".
    Change map_gaps "Map the gaps in the fire from the doorway" from unmapped to mapped.
    Hurts with burn when unmapped then unmapped.
  }
  Hazard burn "the stopped fire" means "Deal (2d8) fire damage to ally.".
  Observe heart_scene at fire_heart when true "At the heart of the fire, in a hollow of stopped flame, lies a fist-sized lump of something that gives off light of its own.".
  Kind splinter_kind "the Splinter" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A fist-sized piece of the seed, broken off when it fell. Warm to the hand; it gives off direct light, enough to hold a person at arm's length within a day.".
  Item splinter "the Splinter" is splinter_kind at fire_heart.
  // A very small Late Sun: whoever carries it stands in direct light, wherever they are.
  Relation carriesLight(group).
  Rule splinter_carried when carries(?c, splinter) and company(?c) and not carriesLight(?c) { Assert carriesLight(?c). }
  Rule splinter_dropped when carriesLight(?c) and not carries(?c, splinter) { Retract carriesLight(?c). }
  Rule splinter_doses when carriesLight(?c) and memberOf(?m, ?c) and not unslowed(?m) and not heldDeep(?m) { Increase dose(?m) by 2. }

  // The First Course: the shepherd's dog, the first moment the seed took. The Masons treat it as a shrine.
  Observe dog_scene at first_course when not state(dog_course, unlaid) "In a small round chamber of black-and-clear banding, a dog, mid-stride, its ears back.".
  Thing dog_course "the First Course" at first_course {
    State laid_dog "The dog is the cornerstone of everything below it.".
    State unlaid "The round chamber is empty. Something huge has settled above, and the way down is shut by fallen courses.".
    Change unlay_dog "Unlay the First Course with the trowel" from laid_dog to unlaid needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Initially Assert kept(dog_course).
  Observe dog_runs near dog_course when touched(dog_course) "Under your hand the dog finishes its stride, and the next, and you feel its heart going like a bird's; it is a long way from home and frightened. When you take your hand away it stops again, mid-stride.".
  Rule crown_falls when state(dog_course, unlaid) and not crownDropped(undersun) says "The whole Crown drops three metres onto the Reach below, with a sound that goes on for a long time." {
    Assert crownDropped(undersun). }
  Relation crownDropped(place).

  // The Burning Wood: smoke stopped in curtains; a flake of ash given time drifts along the safe line.
  Observe wood_scene at burning_wood when true "A pine forest on fire, stopped, with birds fixed in the air above it and smoke standing in solid grey curtains between the trunks.".
  Thing smoke "the curtains of smoke" at burning_wood {
    State rigid "The smoke stands in grey curtains, rigid as cloth on a frame.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(smoke).
  Hazard choke "the smoke, given time" means "Deal (1d8) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (12).".
  Rule smoke_flows when touched(smoke) says "The curtain goes soft under your hand and pours over you, choking and hot, until you pull your hand back." {
    Retract touched(smoke). Assert strikes(choke, party). }
  Thing ash "a flake of ash" at burning_wood {
    State hanging "A single flake of ash hangs in the air at the height of your eyes.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(ash).
  Discovery smoke_line "The safe line through the Burning Wood: where a flake of ash, given time, drifts between the curtains.".
  Observe ash_drifts near ash when touched(ash) "Given time, the flake drifts, and does not fall: it goes sideways between two curtains, and turns, and turns again, along a line you could walk." teaches smoke_line.
  Observe crown_foot_scene at crown_foot when true "The Crown narrows to a stair that goes down by repeated forms: the same step laid again and again, as the same syllable was spoken again and again.".

  // The Seridane Reach: moments of Tamaun's life. Mapped by the Long Hour.
  Passage reach_noon "a granary arch" is arch between reach_head and granary_noon.
  Passage reach_schism "a council door" is doorway between reach_head and schism hidden until long_hour_read.
  Passage reach_riot "the way into the crowd" is passage between reach_head and riot_hall taking 3 minutes.
  Passage riot_exit "the Grammar door" is doorway between riot_hall and reach_foot.
  Passage bath_door "a bathhouse door" is doorway between riot_hall and bathhouse.
  Passage quarry_hollow "a smooth hollow" is passage between reach_head and quarried taking 5 minutes hidden until long_hour_read.
  Passage reach_drop "the stem, looped by rope" is shaft between reach_foot and shaft_top taking 30 minutes needing rope.

  Observe reach_head_scene at reach_head when true "The Reach opens under the Crown in galleries that are Tamaun's: plaster, bronze, a Seridane arch with its keystone carved; only no one living built any of it.".
  // The Granary at Noon: forty Laid, mid-task; Lirem with his astrolabe, his other hand toward the gong.
  Observe noon_scene at granary_noon when true "A vault full of Seridane workers, forty of them, mid-task: carrying jars, sweeping, one laughing with her head back. A scribe sits at a table with a stylus over a tablet. A thin man at the end of the room holds a bronze instrument of rings and pointers, his other hand raised toward a gong.".
  Observe noon_wakes at granary_noon when spokeAloud(party) "At the sound of your voice the whole granary moves: forty people take three steps, the laughing woman finishes her laugh, a jar is set down. Then they stop again where they are.".
  Discovery granary_plan "The scribe's tablet: a plan of Tamaun's Granary Ring with the channel settings for every vault.".
  Thing scribe_tablet "the scribe's tablet" at granary_noon {
    State on_table "A wax tablet under the scribe's stylus, ruled in a plan.".
    Tries looking.
  }
  Observe tablet_read near scribe_tablet when tried(scribe_tablet, looking) "It is a plan of the Granary Ring, with the angle of every channel marked beside its vault." teaches granary_plan.
  Thing lirem_hand "Lirem's hand" at granary_noon {
    Holds.
    State holding_it "Lirem's thin hand holds a bronze instrument of rings and pointers.".
    State empty_hand "Lirem's hand is empty, still raised a little toward the gong.".
  }
  Kind astrolabe_kind "Lirem's astrolabe" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A bronze instrument of rings and pointers. Set to the Late Sun's depth it shows where any ray will fall; held in course-light, it reads the name-grammar.".
  Item astrolabe "Lirem's astrolabe" is astrolabe_kind in lirem_hand.
  Relation gonged(place).
  Rule hand_emptied when not inside(astrolabe, lirem_hand) and state(lirem_hand, holding_it) says "Lirem's hand, with nothing in it, finishes its movement: it strikes the gong." {
    Assert state(lirem_hand, empty_hand). Assert gonged(granary_noon). }
  Observe gong_alarm at granary_noon when gonged(granary_noon) and not gongPassed(party) "The gong's note goes out through the Reach, and everywhere, for a few seconds, the Laid take up their moments: you hear the riot in the next hall roar and stop.".
  Relation gongPassed(group).
  Rule riot_loosed when gonged(granary_noon) and not rioted(riot_hall) { Assert rioted(riot_hall). }
  Relation rioted(place).

  // The Council of the Schism: Selane arguing for the Covering, Amaru on the dais. A sentence at a touch.
  Observe schism_scene at schism when true "A council chamber. A young woman stands speaking, her hand raised. An old man sits on a dais. Every face in the room is turned to her.".
  Thing selane_words "the air in front of Selane's mouth" at schism {
    State unspoken "Selane's lips are parted on a word.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(selane_words).
  Measure sentences(entity).
  Rule selane_speaks when touched(selane_words) and sentences(selane_words) < 4 {
    Increase sentences(selane_words) by 1. Retract touched(selane_words). }
  Observe selane_one near selane_words when sentences(selane_words) == 1 "'Lirem's chains are longer every year,' Selane says, in Old Seridan, and stops.".
  Observe selane_two near selane_words when sentences(selane_words) == 2 "'It is not resting on the rock. It is going through it, and the stone below answers each time it speaks.'".
  Observe selane_three near selane_words when sentences(selane_words) == 3 "'A thing that speaks is not always speaking to you. A mason calls out the courses as he lays them.'".
  Discovery seed_building "Selane's argument, in her own voice: the Late Sun is not speaking to anyone; it is building, and calling its courses as it lays them, and it is going down toward something.".
  Observe selane_four near selane_words when sentences(selane_words) == 4 "'Cover it, father. Not because it is a god. Because it is a builder, and we do not know what for.' Her hand comes down. Amaru, on the dais, has not moved." teaches seed_building.
  Topic amaru_selane with amaru "Tell the king his daughter's argument, word for word" when knows(actor, seed_building) once {
    Says "You say it as she said it. It takes Amaru a long time to understand that you are not inventing it. 'A builder,' he says. Then, after a very long time: 'Say it again.' You do. He asks you a third time.".
    On discuss { Assert grieves(amaru). }
  }

  // The Riot Hall: the grain riot of 1,575 BP, two hundred Laid. Every word spoken aloud gives them five seconds.
  Observe riot_scene at riot_hall when true "A broad hall packed with people in mid-struggle: sickles raised, poles swinging, a woman pulled backward by the hair, a man on the floor with his arm over his face. In the middle of the crowd stands a door. On the wall by the entrance someone has written, in chalk, a single sign in a script of overlapping circles.".
  Observe chalk_read at riot_hall when travelsWith(saro, party) "'Quiet,' says Saro, reading the chalk. She says it in a whisper.".
  // Said before the riot is told, because a three-minute act passes the rules once, in order (ledger, 9).
  Rule speaking_door when state(riot_door, open_g) and not doorSpoken(riot_door) { Assert spokeAloud(party). Assert doorSpoken(riot_door). Increase wordsLaid(party) by 10. }
  Hazard riot "five seconds of the riot" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13).".
  Rule riot_given_time when at(party, riot_hall) and (spokeAloud(party) or rioted(riot_hall)) and not riotStruck(party) says "Two hundred people take up their riot for five seconds: sickles, poles, screaming. Then they stop where they are." {
    Assert strikes(riot, party). Assert riotStruck(party). }
  Relation riotStruck(group).
  Rule riot_still when riotStruck(party) and not spokeAloud(party) and not at(party, riot_hall) { Retract riotStruck(party). }
  Rule riot_spent when rioted(riot_hall) and riotStruck(party) { Retract rioted(riot_hall). }
  Discovery reach_syllables "The syllables of the Seridane Reach's Grammar doors, read from the Long Hour.".
  Observe syllables_from_hour near party when knows(party, long_hour_read) and not knows(party, reach_syllables) "The Long Hour gives you every door in the Reach by the syllable it was laid from." teaches reach_syllables.
  Thing riot_door "the Grammar door" on riot_exit {
    State shut_g blocking "A door of course-glass stands among the rioters. In its floor, if you look, the riot goes on, smaller, as if seen through water.".
    State open_g "The Grammar door stands open.".
    Change speak_syllable "Speak the door's syllable aloud" from shut_g to open_g after learning reach_syllables.
    Change lay_syllable "Lay the door's syllable into it with the trowel" from shut_g to open_g needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Relation doorSpoken(entity).
  Hazard floor_drop "the floor course unlaid" means "Deal (3d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Action guess_syllable(actor: group, site: place) "Speak a syllable at the Grammar door, guessing" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, riot_hall) and state(riot_door, shut_g)
      and not knows(actor, reach_syllables).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert strikes(floor_drop, actor). Assert spokeAloud(actor). Assert at(actor, reach_head). }
    Result "The floor course under you unlays, and you drop into its moment: the riot, all round you, very loud, for as long as you are falling. You come up out of it at the head of the Reach, bruised and shaking.".
  }
  // Speaking aloud in a laid room: talking to anyone, the company is heard, unless it whispers.
  Rule heard_aloud when addressed(?p, ?c) and company(?c) and at(?c, ?r) and laidRoom(?r) and not whispering(?c)
    and not spokeAloud(?c) { Assert spokeAloud(?c). Increase wordsLaid(?c) by 10. }
  Rule quiet_again when spokeAloud(?c) and company(?c) and not addressedAny(?c) { Retract spokeAloud(?c). }
  Query addressedAny(c: group) means addressed(?p, c).

  // The Bathhouse: steam so dense that light takes ten minutes to cross it. Gleaners nest here.
  Observe bath_scene at bathhouse when true "A Seridane bathhouse full of steam that stands like milk. When you hold up a light, its glow crawls: what you see across the room is ten minutes old.".
  Species gleaner "a gleaner" like great_centipede temperament defensive
    described "A thing the size of a hand, many-legged, of stopped iron: one of a swarm from another world, given work by the Masons. They gather what falls, and lay it.".
  Person gleaners "gleaners" at bathhouse {
    Role "a swarm of gleaners, nesting". Species gleaner. Numbers 4.
  }
  Observe gleaners_late at bathhouse when at(gleaners, bathhouse) "Across the steam, ten minutes ago, something many-legged was moving along the wall.".

  // The Quarried Gallery: the fourth Dane's reign, carried away; his keystone remains.
  Observe quarried_scene at quarried when true "A long hollow with smooth walls and tool-marks, as if a gallery had been carved out of the masonry and carried off. At its far end one block remains, carved with a name. Your eye will not stay on the name.".
  Thing dane_keystone "the fourth Dane's keystone" at quarried {
    State carved "A block of course-glass with a man laid in it, and a name cut over him that the eye slides off.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(dane_keystone).
  Observe dane_speaks near dane_keystone when touched(dane_keystone) and not knows(party, dane_name) "Under your hand the man in the block draws breath, and says his own name, and you hear it, and keep it." teaches dane_name.

  // The Silent Reach: a bare stem in a thirty-metre shaft, grown during the burial. The Plumb breaks in at 600 metres;
  // Saro's stair climbs the stem from the bottom, a step a day.
  Passage shaft_down "the stem, by looped rope" is shaft between shaft_top and plumb_mouth taking 30 minutes needing rope.
  Passage shaft_down2 "down the stem to Saro's stair" is shaft between plumb_mouth and saro_stair taking 30 minutes needing rope.
  Passage saro_steps "Saro's stair" is stair between saro_stair and shaft_bottom taking 30 minutes.
  Passage tip_down "the stem's foot" is passage between shaft_bottom and lreach_head taking 10 minutes.
  Observe shaft_scene at shaft_top when true "A vertical shaft thirty metres across and three hundred deep, its walls cut smooth. Down its centre runs a column of dark metal and clear glass twelve metres thick, glowing along its curves. Warm air rises. From below comes a hammering, regular and patient.".
  Observe plumb_mouth_scene at plumb_mouth when true "The Coverers' borehole comes out of the shaft wall here, a glass-lined mouth half a metre across. There is nothing to stand on but a lip of rock and the stem.".
  Observe saro_stair_scene at saro_stair when true "A helical stair is being laid up the stem from the bottom, one step a day. Its top step is new and bright.".
  Observe shaft_bottom_scene at shaft_bottom when true "The foot of the shaft. Everything that has ever fallen down it lies here half-laid into the floor: a cutter's pack, a goat, a stone.".
  Person gleaners_low "gleaners at the foot of the shaft" at shaft_bottom {
    Role "a swarm of gleaners, laying what has fallen". Species gleaner. Numbers 6.
  }
  Hazard long_fall "the long fall" means "Deal (6d6) physical damage to ally.".

  // The Listeners' Reach: recent history, mapped by Teodar's count.
  Passage lr_breach "a stopped storm" is passage between lreach_head and breach_moment taking 3 minutes hidden until listeners_count.
  Passage lr_keystones "a vaulted gallery" is passage between lreach_head and keystone_gallery taking 3 minutes.
  Passage lr_fair "a fair's gate" is passage between lreach_head and fair_moment taking 3 minutes.
  Passage fair_exit "the drum door" is doorway between fair_moment and tip_dome.
  Observe lreach_scene at lreach_head when true "The newest courses: the plateau's own last three hundred years, laid one a month.".
  // The Breach: year 352, in storm. Four figures in wet felt, one with an iron pin.
  Observe breach_moment_scene at breach_moment when true "A night of storm, stopped. A stone culvert, a sluice frame, four figures in wet felt, one with an iron pin in his hand.".
  Thing breach_words "the air near the four in the storm" at breach_moment {
    State still_storm "Rain hangs between you and them.".
  }
  Initially Assert kept(breach_words).
  Observe breach_heard near breach_words when touched(breach_words) "A woman's voice in Tovashi, low, through the rain: 'Pull it, Bren. The fill will drink it.' A young man's: 'Ayzhe —' and the pin comes out of the frame in his hand." teaches breach_cut.
  // The Keystone Gallery: Ennick's held, Kell's dead and the Sixty, laid as ribs.
  Observe keystone_scene at keystone_gallery when true "A vaulted gallery whose ribs are people: men and women lying in clear glass, each with a small red brick carved with a knot above the chest, the way Ennick marks its held. At the far end, older ribs hold strangers in Tovash dress.".
  Observe doran_rib at keystone_gallery when not benighted(party) "One of the ribs is a thin man with his hands at his sides and his mouth a little open, and a fan of bright lines in the glass in front of his face where the sand was not quite clean. It is Doran, at the moment Ilis laid him." teaches held_feed.
  Thing keystones "the keystones" at keystone_gallery {
    State bearing "The keystones bear the courses above them.".
    State unlaid_k "The keystones are unlaid. Below this gallery the Undersun has dropped thirty metres and stopped.".
    Change unlay_keys "Unlay the keystones with the trowel" from bearing to unlaid_k needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Relation masonsComing(place).
  Rule lower_dropped when state(keystones, unlaid_k) and not masonsComing(ennick) says "Far below, the lower Undersun drops thirty metres and stops. Twenty years of growth, gone. The Masons at the Tip put down their work, and look up." {
    Assert masonsComing(ennick). }
  // The Fair: the Tovash fair of year 0. The way out is a Grammar door keyed to a beat.
  Observe fair_scene at fair_moment when true "The Tovash fair of year 0: horses, a cauldron, children with their arms out, and a drum held against a man's chest.".
  Thing drum_door "the drum door" on fair_exit {
    State shut_d blocking "A door of course-glass stands where the fair's gate was. Nothing is carved on it; in its floor a drum is being beaten, very small.".
    State open_d "The drum door stands open.".
    Change strike_drum "Strike the held drum in the moot song's count" from shut_d to open_d after learning moot_count.
    Change lay_drum "Lay the door's beat into it with the trowel" from shut_d to open_d needing trowel_kind.
  }
  Action guess_beat(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the held drum in a beat you guess" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, fair_moment) and state(drum_door, shut_d)
      and not knows(actor, moot_count).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert strikes(floor_drop, actor). }
    Result "The floor course unlays and drops you into the fair, a second of it: the drum, the horses, the children's voices, and the light coming up out of the ground. You climb out shaking.".
  }

  // U5, the Tip: Saro's workshop and the drill. Six Masons; under the floor, the Delver; a note once an hour.
  Observe tip_scene at tip_dome when true "At the bottom of the stem, a domed chamber where new courses glow bright along their edges. A low note sounds from below the floor, once an hour.".
  Person masons "six Masons" at tip_dome {
    Role "six figures very still around the walls, each holding a tool like a trowel". Ancestry human. Numbers 6. Peaceable.
  }
  Observe masons_seen near masons when at(masons, tip_dome) "Their hands have no temperature. Their faces are from six different worlds, and they all watch you the same way: with interest, and no fear at all.".
  Topic masons_were with masons "Ask the Masons who they were" when true once {
    Says "They answer one at a time, in the last languages they learned, and Tovashi after a moment, picked up from you. A smith. A ferryman. A woman who sang at funerals. None of them can say where; all of them can say what they made. 'This,' says the singer, and lays a hand on the course. 'This is better.'".
  }
  Discovery trowel_traded "The Masons will trade a trowel for a moment, and the price of a moment is one of your memories, cut out with a trowel.".
  Topic masons_trowel with masons "Ask the Masons for a trowel" when true once {
    Says "'A moment for a moment,' says the ferryman. 'One of yours. We cut it, you do not miss it. Nobody does.' He holds out his hand, palm up.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, trowel_traded). }
  }
  // The spare trowel is declared in moments.kyr, beside its kind: an Item sees only its own file's kinds (ledger, 25).
  Discovery trowel_paid "A memory cut, and a trowel given for it.".
  Measure memories(group).
  Initially Set memories(party) to 12.
  Action pay_memory(actor: group, site: place) "Let the Masons cut one of your memories, for a trowel" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, tip_dome) and knows(actor, trowel_traded)
      and memories(actor) >= 1 and not paidMemory(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Decrease memories(actor) by 1. Assert paidMemory(actor). }
    Result "The ferryman lays his trowel against your temple, and something is gone. You do not know what. Nobody in the world will ever know what. He puts a trowel in your hand.".
  }
  Relation paidMemory(group).
  Observe trowel_given near party when paidMemory(party) and not knows(party, trowel_paid) "The trowel lies on the course at your feet where he set it." teaches trowel_paid.
  Species delver_kind "the Delver" like iron_golem temperament defensive
    described "The first Mason, which rode the seed down. Not human. It drills.".
  Person delver "the Delver" at tip_dome {
    Role "the first Mason, working in the drill-face under the floor". Species delver_kind. Level 12.
  }
  // Saro at the Tip: where she works, the courses grow ten times as fast.
  Topic saro_tip with saro travelling "Ask Saro what she will do here" when at(party, tip_dome) once {
    Says "Saro has her hand on the newest course already. 'Work,' she says. 'Here. It is going down to the stone that sings. I will help it go.' She looks at you with that great attention. 'You may stay. You may go. I am staying.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/after.k:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── Afterwards: the Field and Larum, come back to ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The chapter closes on the Morning After; the Field goes on as it was left, and Larum with it.
  Query afterAll() means outcomeDecided(field_country) and morningAfter().
  Relation cameBackUp(group). Relation cameBackLarum(group).
  Rule went_down when afterAll() and not inYsgard(party) and not cameBackLarum(party) and at(party, larum_street) { Assert cameBackLarum(party). }
  Chapter ch_back_halt "Halt, Afterwards" when afterAll() and haltStands() and at(party, snow_gate) and visitedBefore(halt_cross) and cameBackLarum(party) "The Coming-in again, and the curtain of snow, and Cleeve; and below, in the middle of the Field, more smoke than there was, going straight up.".
  Chapter ch_back_daily "The Field, Afterwards" when afterAll() and outcomeDaily(field_country) and at(party, snow_gate) and cameBackLarum(party) "The Coming-in again. From the Field below comes the roar of the Daily, and in the middle of it, where Halt was, nothing.".

  Observe gate_halt_column at cleeve_booth as feature when afterAll() and haltStands() "Cleeve's ledger lies open on the desk, and down the page, beside EAST and WEST, there is a third column ruled in fresh ink, HALT, with a few names in it already.".
  Topic cleeve_after with cleeve "Ask Cleeve about the new column in his ledger" when afterAll() and haltStands() once {
    Says "Cleeve looks at it as if it might bite him. 'Halt,' he says. 'For the ones that come in at noon. And the ones that come in and look down at the Field and ask what the town is, and I tell them, and they ask can they go there instead.' He smooths the page. 'Nine hundred years of east and west. It was never a law.' He looks up. 'Nobody ever said it was a law.'".
  }
  // Where people are afterwards.
  Rule after_daily_folk when afterAll() and outcomeDaily(field_country) and at(halt_folk, halt_cross) { Assert at(halt_folk, limbo). Assert at(saltash, limbo). Assert at(grimbold, morrow_hall). Assert at(wystan, even_hall). Assert at(hild, marshal_room). }
  Rule after_daily_lovers when afterAll() and outcomeDaily(field_country) and wedded(mab) and not at(mab, sitters_cave) { Assert at(mab, sitters_cave). Assert at(ansel, sitters_cave). }
  Rule after_daily_ned when afterAll() and outcomeDaily(field_country) and nedCame(ned) and not at(ned, warren) and not following(ned, party) { Assert at(ned, warren). }
  Rule after_halt_ned when afterAll() and haltStands() and nedCame(ned) and not nedHome(ned) and not following(ned, party) and at(ned, snow_gate) { Assert nedHome(ned). Assert at(ned, oven). }
  Rule after_torold_larum when afterAll() and buriedLarum(torold) and not at(torold, snow_gate) and hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 19 { Assert at(torold, snow_gate). }
  Rule after_torold_home when afterAll() and buriedLarum(torold) and at(torold, snow_gate) and (hour(clock) >= 19 or hour(clock) < 17) { Assert at(torold, the_ring). }
  Observe torold_at_gate at snow_gate as sign when at(torold, snow_gate) and afterAll() "Torold Hame stands at the very edge of the snow-curtain with his hands empty, facing it, listening.".
  Rule edith_hall_after when edithDead(edith) and afterAll() and not at(edith, even_hall) { Assert at(edith, even_hall). }
  Observe edith_in_hall at even_hall as sign when at(edith, even_hall) and edithDead(edith) "At the very end of the lowest bench in Evenhall a woman in three Runners' smocks sits with a cup, not drinking, looking at the column of names painted up the wall to the roof. Her breath does not steam.".

  // Larum afterwards.
  Topic bet_after_quiet with bet "Tell Bet Garside what became of the Field" when afterAll() and not skyLoud() once {
    Says "Bet hears you out with her chin on her fist and the two pans on the nail behind her. When you have done she is quiet a while. 'So they'll not start again,' she says. 'Not ever, maybe.' She looks at the pans. 'I'll get used to it. You get used to anything.' Then, after a moment: 'I'll tell old Habakkuk at the press. There'll be a ballad.' She shakes her head. 'I don't know what you'd rhyme with bread.'".
  }
  Topic bet_after_loud with bet "Tell Bet Garside what became of the Field" when afterAll() and skyLoud() once {
    Says "Bet listens, and outside the window, far off up the Pass, the iron noise goes on and on. 'I slept,' she says, when you've done, a little guiltily. 'Last night. Ten hours.' She looks at the window. 'A town, you say. With a baker.' She is quiet. 'I'll not say I'm sorry it's loud again. I'll say I'm sorry about the baker.'".
  }
  Topic jory_after_field with jory "Ask Jory Whitlock whether he will go on taking the living up" when afterAll() and joryMet(jory) once {
    Says "'Every week,' says Jory. 'Whether or no.' He coils a rope. 'They come up and look at the Field, the collectors, and buy iron off the Runners, and come down. They never go and sit with anybody.' He hangs the rope on its peg. 'I tell them now: go and sit with somebody. Ask them their name. Half of them have not been asked their name in a hundred years.'".
  }
  Observe chapel_after at larum_chapel as feature when afterAll() and knows(party, ithel_told) "Under I. S. MADE THIS BELL, somebody has cut, newer and smaller: FOR THE ONES THAT DO NOT GET UP.".
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/clock.k:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The days the story keeps ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Nothing on the Field waits for a company that has not come up: the story is counted from the first time the
  // company stands in Ysgard (cameUp). At the first Hour after that, Torold Hame names the Testing for the fourth morning
  // (testDay). Larum, below, keeps no story clock; it keeps a bell.
  Relation cameUp(group). Measure upDay(clock). Measure testDay(clock). Relation testingNamed(place).
  Relation ysgardRoom(place).
  Query inYsgard(g: group) means at(g, ?p) and ysgardRoom(?p).
  Rule came_up when inYsgard(party) and not cameUp(party) { Assert cameUp(party). Set upDay(clock) to day(clock). }
  // The Hour: dusk in Ysgard, six in the evening, when the light goes blue and what was done to the dead is undone.
  Query theHour() means hour(clock) == 18.
  Query afterHour() means hour(clock) >= 18.
  Rule testing_named when cameUp(party) and hour(clock) >= 18 and not testingNamed(field_country) { Assert testingNamed(field_country). Set testDay(clock) to day(clock) + 4. }
  // The day of the Testing, the day after it, and whether it is behind us.
  Query testingDay() means testingNamed(field_country) and day(clock) == testDay(clock).
  Query testingUnder() means testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 18.
  Query afterTesting() means testingNamed(field_country) and (day(clock) > testDay(clock) or day(clock) == testDay(clock) and hour(clock) >= 18).
  Query morningAfter() means testingNamed(field_country) and day(clock) > testDay(clock).
  Query beforeTesting() means not afterTesting().
  // How many mornings until the Testing, said in words.
  Measure morningsLeft(clock).
  Rule mornings_count when testingNamed(field_country) and morningsLeft(clock) != testDay(clock) - day(clock) { Set morningsLeft(clock) to testDay(clock) - day(clock). }

  Initially Assert ysgardRoom(snow_gate). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(cleeve_booth).
  Initially Assert ysgardRoom(field_south). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(lathe_ford). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(the_clear).
  Initially Assert ysgardRoom(east_slope). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(west_slope). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(field_north).
  Initially Assert ysgardRoom(halt_cross). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(the_ring). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(banner_lanes).
  Initially Assert ysgardRoom(oven). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(truce).
  Initially Assert ysgardRoom(morrow_yard). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(morrow_hall). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(marshal_room).
  Initially Assert ysgardRoom(even_court). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(even_hall). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(forge).
  Initially Assert ysgardRoom(scrapes_mouth). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(warren). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(edith_nook).
  Initially Assert ysgardRoom(ice_foot). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(ice_stair). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(sitters_cave).
  Initially Assert ysgardRoom(teeth_path). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(wolf_ledge). Initially Assert ysgardRoom(high_cairn).

  // A place the company has left and come back to is told shortly (after the Liberty of the Ice's clock).
  Relation visitedNow(place). Relation visitedBefore(place).
  Rule arrives_at when at(party, ?p) and not visitedNow(?p) { Assert visitedNow(?p). }
  Rule leaves_from when visitedNow(?p) and not at(party, ?p) { Retract visitedNow(?p). Assert visitedBefore(?p). }

  // ── The cold ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The dead do not feel it. The living do: every watch out of doors in Ysgard, or up in the White, is a watch of cold
  // (chill), and the warm places take it off again: the Oven, the halls' fires, the Scrapes' fat-lamps, Cleeve's
  // brazier, and anywhere in Larum. A sheepskin from Larum keeps it off twice as long. Past what a body can stand, the
  // cold bites once an hour.
  Measure chill(group). Measure chilledAt(group). Measure bittenAt(group).
  Relation warm(place). Relation bitter(place).
  Initially Assert warm(oven). Initially Assert warm(morrow_hall). Initially Assert warm(marshal_room).
  Initially Assert warm(even_hall). Initially Assert warm(forge). Initially Assert warm(warren). Initially Assert warm(edith_nook).
  Initially Assert warm(cleeve_booth). Initially Assert warm(sitters_cave).
  Initially Assert bitter(the_white).
  Query coldHere(g: group) means at(g, ?p) and (ysgardRoom(?p) and not warm(?p) or bitter(?p)).
  Query wrapped(g: group) means holding(g, sheepskin_kind).
  Query numbAt(g: group) means not wrapped(g) and chill(g) >= 18 or wrapped(g) and chill(g) >= 36.
  Query frozenAt(g: group) means not wrapped(g) and chill(g) >= 30 or wrapped(g) and chill(g) >= 60.
  Rule chill_rises when company(?c) and coldHere(?c) and watch(clock) > chilledAt(?c) { Increase chill(?c) by 1. Set chilledAt(?c) to watch(clock). }
  Rule chill_bites when company(?c) and at(?c, ?p) and bitter(?p) and watch(clock) > chilledAt(?c) { Increase chill(?c) by 2. Set chilledAt(?c) to watch(clock). }
  Rule chill_eases when company(?c) and not coldHere(?c) and chill(?c) > 0 and watch(clock) > chilledAt(?c) { Decrease chill(?c) by 4 or to nothing. Set chilledAt(?c) to watch(clock). }
  Rule chill_settles when company(?c) and not coldHere(?c) and chill(?c) == 0 and watch(clock) > chilledAt(?c) { Set chilledAt(?c) to watch(clock). }
  Hazard frostbite "the cold of Ysgard, in the fingers and the face" means "Deal (1d4) cold damage to ally unless constitution save against (12).".
  Rule frost_bites when company(?c) and coldHere(?c) and frozenAt(?c) and watch(clock) >= bittenAt(?c) + 6 { Assert strikes(frostbite, ?c). Set bittenAt(?c) to watch(clock). }
  Relation numbWarned(group). Relation frozenWarned(group).
  Rule numb_warns when company(?c) and coldHere(?c) and numbAt(?c) and not frozenAt(?c) and not numbWarned(?c) says "Your fingers have gone stupid and white at the tips. The cold up here does not wear off; it adds up. Somewhere warm, soon: the Oven in Halt, a hall's fire, the Runners' warren, the Teller's brazier." { Assert numbWarned(?c). }
  Rule frozen_warns when company(?c) and coldHere(?c) and frozenAt(?c) and not frozenWarned(?c) says "You cannot feel your feet. Your breath has frozen in your collar. If you stay out in this, the cold will start taking pieces of you." { Assert frozenWarned(?c). }
  Rule cold_warnings_reset when company(?c) and chill(?c) == 0 and (numbWarned(?c) or frozenWarned(?c)) { Retract numbWarned(?c). Retract frozenWarned(?c). }

  // ── The breath ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // In Ysgard the dead do not steam when they breathe. The living do, and every dead face turns to look.
  Discovery breath_sign "On the Field the dead do not steam when they breathe; in that cold only the living do, and anyone can see it across a lane.".
  Rule breath_seen when inYsgard(party) and not at(party, snow_gate) and not at(party, cleeve_booth) and not knows(party, breath_sign)
    says "Your breath goes up white in front of you and hangs. Nobody else's does. A man going past with a spear on his shoulder stops dead and stares at the little cloud as if you had taken out a knife." teaches breath_sign { }
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/coming-:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The Coming-in ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Where the White gives out on the Ysgard side, the snow comes down in a curtain, and the new dead walk out of it at
  // the hour they died. Cleeve the Teller asks each the hour and sends them east to Morrow or west to Even.
  Observe gate_scene at snow_gate when not visitedBefore(snow_gate) "You come out of the white onto a height over a white plain five miles across, strewn as far as you can see with nine hundred years of broken arms, between two halls on two dark heights; and the cold goes into your teeth. The sky is the colour of a knife-blade, with a low white sun in it that does not seem to move. Below you the plain is strewn with things: spears standing up, shields, the ribs of a cart, a siege-tower with snow on its top. In the middle of it smoke goes up from a huddle of coloured tents. Behind you, the snow comes down out of a clear sky in a curtain, and does not come any further.".
  Observe gate_again at snow_gate when visitedBefore(snow_gate) "The Coming-in: the height over the Field, the curtain of snow behind you coming down out of a clear sky and stopping, and Cleeve's booth of planks and banners with its brazier smoking. Far off below, Halt's smoke.".
  Observe gate_daily at snow_gate as sound when skyLoud() and hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 18 "Up from the Field comes the noise of the Daily: thousands of men at it, iron on iron, a roar like surf with screaming in it.".
  Observe booth_scene at cleeve_booth when true "A booth of planks and old banners, out of the wind. A brazier full of red coals, which nobody here needs, and which Cleeve keeps for the pickers from Larum, he says, and for the look of the thing. A rack of hourglasses, every size, all running. A tall desk, and on it a ledger as thick as a doorstep, open, in a fine black hand: a name, an hour, EAST or WEST, a name, an hour, EAST or WEST, down every page.".

  Person cleeve "Cleeve" at cleeve_booth {
    Role "the Teller at the Coming-in". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Likeness "herald".
    Greets "A thin old man in a herald's tabard faded to no colour looks up from a ledger with a pen in his hand. 'Name, and hour of death,' he says. Then he sees your breath, smoking in the cold, and puts the pen down very carefully. 'Oh dear,' he says. 'You're one of those.'".
    Greets again "Cleeve looks up, sees your breath, and sighs. 'Still breathing,' he says. 'Well. Sit by the brazier.'".
  }
  // Each time the company comes up through the White, Cleeve asks its hour, and each time it has none.
  Measure cleeveAsked(group). Relation askedThisVisit(group).
  Rule cleeve_asks_first at snow_gate when at(party, snow_gate) and not askedThisVisit(party) and cleeveAsked(party) == 0
    says "From the booth by the curtain a thin old man in a faded tabard comes out with a ledger under his arm and a pen behind his ear. 'Name and hour of death,' he says briskly, and then sees your breath go up white in the cold, and stops. 'Ah,' he says. 'Breathing.' He looks at the ledger as if it had let him down. 'There is no column for breathing. The pickers from Larum come up as far as the booth, and the guide, but they never stay.' He looks down at the Field, and back at you. 'If you're going down there, go carefully. They've not seen a breather close in a long time, and they're frightened enough as it is.'" { Assert askedThisVisit(party). Increase cleeveAsked(party) by 1. }
  Rule cleeve_asks_second at snow_gate when at(party, snow_gate) and not askedThisVisit(party) and cleeveAsked(party) == 1
    says "Cleeve comes out of his booth with the ledger, and opens it, and dips his pen. 'Name and hour of—' He sees your breath. 'Oh, it's you,' he says. He shuts the ledger." { Assert askedThisVisit(party). Increase cleeveAsked(party) by 1. }
  Rule cleeve_asks_third at snow_gate when at(party, snow_gate) and not askedThisVisit(party) and cleeveAsked(party) == 2
    says "'Hour of—' says Cleeve, coming out with the ledger, out of nine hundred years of habit, and then he sees you and stops, and closes his eyes, and stands there a moment with his lips moving, like a man counting to ten." { Assert askedThisVisit(party). Increase cleeveAsked(party) by 1. }
  Rule cleeve_asks_more at snow_gate when at(party, snow_gate) and not askedThisVisit(party) and cleeveAsked(party) >= 3
    says "Cleeve looks out of his booth, sees your breath, and does not come out. 'You'll be wanting the brazier,' he says." { Assert askedThisVisit(party). Increase cleeveAsked(party) by 1. }
  Observe cleeve_knows at snow_gate as sign when deathCarrier(party) "Cleeve sees you, and goes back into his booth, and does not come out.".
  Rule cleeve_resets when askedThisVisit(party) and not inYsgard(party) { Retract askedThisVisit(party). }

  Topic cleeve_sorting with cleeve "Ask Cleeve how he sorts the dead" when true once {
    Says "'By the hour,' says Cleeve, and taps the rack of hourglasses. 'They come in out of the snow at the hour they died, and I ask, and they tell me, mostly; and before noon is east, to Morrowhall, and after noon is west, to Evenhall. Dawn raids and morning storms go to Morrow. Last stands and sunset charges go to Even.' He turns a page. 'Brothers come in an hour apart, sometimes, from the one field. One goes east and one goes west, and they've fought each other every day since. Hour-kin, the halls call it.' He rights an hourglass that had not fallen. 'There are men in Morrow who have not spoken to a brother in six hundred years, and could not tell you which of them started it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sorting_known). }
  }
  Discovery sorting_known "Cleeve sorts the dead who come in out of the snow by the hour they died: before noon to Morrowhall, after noon to Evenhall. It is not a law, only how it has always been done; brothers who died an hour apart have fought each other every day since, and the halls call them hour-kin.".
  Topic cleeve_ledger with cleeve "Ask Cleeve how far back his ledger goes" when knows(actor, sorting_known) once {
    Says "Cleeve turns the great ledger back, and back, and the hand changes, and changes again, and the ink goes brown, and then there is a page whose first line begins in the middle of a sentence: *—and so the dawn shall go to the east.* 'That is the first page there is,' says Cleeve. 'Whatever was before it, somebody tore out.' He smooths it. 'The halls each tell you why the war began. Morrow says Even refused the dawn its due. Even says Morrow struck first, at dawn, as it always does. They have had nine hundred years to get their stories straight and they have not managed it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, war_origin_disputed). }
  }
  Discovery war_origin_disputed "Cleeve's ledger begins in the middle of a sentence: '—and so the dawn shall go to the east.' Morrow says the war began when Even refused the dawn its due; Even says Morrow struck first, at dawn.".
  Topic cleeve_quiet with cleeve "Ask Cleeve about the quiet" when beforeTesting() once {
    Says "'They still come in,' says Cleeve. 'One or two an hour, the way they always have, still bloody, still shouting the battle they died in. And I tell them east or west, and they run down the hill to their hall with their swords out, and find a town.' He shakes his head. 'Forty days. I keep thinking I should tell them something else. But I only know the one thing to say.'".
  }
  // Now and then, while the company is there, someone comes in.
  Observe newcomer_morning at snow_gate as sign when hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 12 and dice(clock) <= 40 "Out of the curtain of snow behind you a man walks, in a leather jack with an arrow through the shoulder of it, his mouth open. Cleeve is out of the booth before he has taken three steps. 'Hour?' 'Morning. The ford. We had the ford at first light, we—' 'East,' says Cleeve, kindly, and points. The man looks down at the Field, and the hall on its eastern height, and goes, slowly, the arrow still in him.".
  Observe newcomer_evening at snow_gate as sign when hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 21 and dice(clock) <= 40 "Out of the curtain a woman walks, very young, in a bright surcoat cut half away, holding the stump of a lance. 'Hour?' says Cleeve. She says something about the sun being in their eyes. 'West,' says Cleeve, and points to the hall at the far end of the Field, where the low sun is. She goes down toward it, running.".

  // ── Ned Whitlock, who came in at noon ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Jory's son, killed by robbers at the Hob Bridge below the valley with his father's blackthorn in his hand, comes in
  // out of the snow at noon of the company's first day up: neither before noon nor after, and so neither east nor west.
  Person ned "Ned Whitlock" at limbo {
    Role "who came in at noon". Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Likeness "apprentice".
    Known as "a boy in a carter's smock" when not knows(party, ned_dead).
    Greets "A boy of sixteen or so is sitting on the edge of Cleeve's booth with a blackthorn stick across his knees, in a carter's smock with a dark stain down one side of it from the hair on that side of his head. He looks up at you, and sees your breath, and his face goes wild with hope. 'You're alive,' he says. 'Are you— is this— am I—' He stops. 'I am, aren't I,' he says. 'Dead.'".
    Greets again "Ned looks up, quick, and sees it is you, and something in his shoulders lets go.".
    Joins "'I'll come,' says Ned, and gets up with his father's stick. 'I'd rather. They keep looking at me down there like I'm a sum that won't come out.'".
    Remarks at the_ring "Ned stops at the ring of spears and looks at the dead man on the shields, and then at his own hands. 'He's like me,' he says. 'Isn't he. He's the only one here that's like me. Dead, I mean. Properly.' He swallows. 'Except I'm walking about.'".
    Remarks at oven "Ned stands in the Oven's warmth with his eyes shut. 'It smells like Nance's,' he says. 'Almost.'".
    Remarks at the_clear "Ned lies flat on the ice with his face to it like a boy at a pond, looking down at the swords. 'Dad'd give his eyes for this,' he says, and then remembers, and gets up.".
    Remarks at high_cairn "Ned looks out over the edge, at the lowland lying under glass a long way off, small and green. He shades his eyes with the stick. 'I can't see Larum,' he says. 'It'd be behind the fells. I can't see it.'".
  }
  Rule ned_comes at snow_gate when cameUp(party) and (day(clock) > upDay(clock) or hour(clock) >= 12) and at(ned, limbo) and not nedCame(ned)
    says "Out of the curtain of snow behind you, at noon by Cleeve's glasses, a boy walks, sixteen or so, in a carter's smock, with a blackthorn stick in his fist and blood all down one side of his head. He looks round at the sky and the snow and the Field below as if somebody had played a trick on him. Cleeve comes out with the ledger. 'Hour?' 'I don't know. Noon? The chapel at Hob was ringing noon when they—' He stops. Cleeve looks at his glasses, and at the boy, and at the ledger. 'Noon,' he says. 'Exactly noon.' He turns a page, and turns it back. 'There is no— before noon is east, and after noon is west, and at noon—' He looks up, helplessly, and the boy looks back at him, and neither of them knows what to do." { Assert at(ned, snow_gate). Assert nedCame(ned). }
  Relation nedCame(group).
  Discovery ned_dead "The boy who came in at noon is Ned Whitlock, Jory the guide's son, from Larum: robbers set on him on the road at the Hob Bridge and he hit one with his father's blackthorn before they killed him. Cleeve cannot sort him, and he cannot go home.".
  Topic ned_who with ned "Ask the boy who he is" when not knows(actor, ned_dead) once {
    Says "'Ned,' says the boy. 'Ned Whitlock. From Larum.' He says it the way you say the name of your village to a stranger, not expecting them to know it, and then sees your face. 'You know it? You've come up from Larum? Then you'll know my dad, Jory, he's the guide.' He grips the stick. 'He'll be waiting for me. I was to be home Thursday with the mule.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ned_dead). Assert acceptsEscort(ned, actor). }
  }
  Topic ned_how with ned "Ask Ned how he died" when knows(actor, ned_dead) once {
    Says "'At the Hob Bridge,' says Ned. 'Three men off the fells. They wanted the fleece money and the mule, and I'd Dad's stick, he always makes me take it, and I hit one, I hit him hard, I felt it go in his teeth.' He looks at the stick. 'Then the other one. I don't remember. And then I was walking in snow.' He looks up at you. 'Cleeve says it counts. Having the stick. Under arms, he says. Like a soldier.' He laughs, horribly. 'I'm a soldier.'".
  }
  Topic ned_wants with ned "Ask Ned what you can do for him" when knows(actor, ned_dead) once {
    Says "Ned thinks about it, with his whole face, the way boys do. 'Tell Dad,' he says. 'Somebody's got to. Better you than some carter.' He picks at the stick. 'Tell him the mule ran. It'll have gone home, it always goes home. Tell him I hit one.' He looks away. 'Tell him I'm sorry about the second cup. He'll know.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ned_message). }
  }
  Discovery ned_message "Ned asks you to tell his father: that the mule ran and will have gone home, that he hit one of them, and that he is sorry about the second cup. Jory will know what that means.".
  // The dead cannot go down into the White: they lie down in it.
  Rule ned_stops at snow_gate when following(ned, party) and at(party, the_white)
    says "At the edge of the curtain Ned stops, as if he had walked into a wall. 'I can't,' he says. He tries again, and his knees go, and he sits down in the snow. 'My legs won't. It's like stairs in a dream.' He gets up and backs away from the white. 'I'll be here,' he says. 'I'll wait by Cleeve's fire. Tell him. Tell him.'" { Retract following(ned, party). Assert at(ned, snow_gate). }
  // Left on the Field he goes back to the Coming-in, until somewhere else will have him.
  Rule ned_home_gate when at(ned, ?p) and not following(ned, party) and not at(ned, snow_gate) and not at(ned, limbo) and not nedHome(ned) and not at(ned, oven) and hour(clock) >= 21 { Assert at(ned, snow_gate). }
  Relation nedHome(group).
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/company:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  Company party "Your company" of 1 to 3 at march_road.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 14. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 2.
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/days.ky:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── Halt from day to day ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The town is forty days old and grows while the company is elsewhere; it answers what happens in it. Each line is a
  // sign of Trophy Row or the banner lanes, told while it holds.
  Query upFor(n: entity) means cameUp(party) and day(clock) - upDay(clock) >= dayCount(n).
  Measure dayCount(entity).
  Entity second_day: fact "the second day up". Entity third_day: fact "the third day up".
  Initially Set dayCount(second_day) to 1. Initially Set dayCount(third_day) to 2.
  Observe halt_grows_one at banner_lanes as sign when upFor(second_day) and not upFor(third_day) and haltStands() and beforeTesting() "There is a new lane since yesterday, at the north end, eleven tents long, and a dead man is going along it with a bucket of meltwater and a brush, painting a name on a shield and planting it at the end, as a street-sign. The name is WEDNESDAY. Nobody knows what it means; he says he remembered it.".
  Observe halt_grows_two at banner_lanes as sign when upFor(third_day) and haltStands() and beforeTesting() "The lanes have spread out past the shield-wall on the east side overnight, and somebody has started a second wall outside the first, as if the town meant to go on. On a pole at the crossing a list of names has been nailed up, in many hands, under a heading scratched with a knife: WHO HAS MADE WHAT. A spoon. A chair. A doll. A song, half. Bread, in another hand, with a question mark.".
  Observe halt_named at halt_cross as ambience when testingNamed(field_country) and beforeTesting() and not testingDay() and haltStands() and not truthSpoken(field_country) "Since Torold named the Testing, people on Trophy Row keep looking west at Evenhall in the middle of a sentence, and losing the end of it.".
  Observe halt_queue at halt_cross as sign when breadRisen(grimbold) and haltStands() and hour(clock) < 12 "A queue goes back from the Oven's mouth along the shield-wall, Morrow and Even and Runner in no order, a hundred long, waiting for bread, and nobody in it is pushing.".
  Observe halt_ribbons at banner_lanes as sign when wedded(mab) and haltStands() "Somebody has tied strips of red and white banner across the lane outside Mab Treloar and Ansel Haverlock's tent, Morrow's red and Even's white, plaited together. Half the lane has done the same since, without anyone saying why.".
  Observe halt_humming at halt_cross as ambience when songMade(wystan) and haltStands() "Somewhere along the Row someone is singing about a sheep, badly.".
  Observe halt_knows at banner_lanes as ambience when truthSpoken(field_country) and haltStands() and beforeTesting() "In the lanes people stand in twos and threes and talk low, the way people do after a death in a village: about what it means, and whether anything is different, and what they will do on the fourth morning, now they know they can.".
  Observe halt_sitters at halt_cross as sign when sittersDown(aulus) and haltStands() "Two very old men in bronze are going down the Row arm in arm, stopping at every blanket to tell its owner that whatever he has is wrong for the period.".
  Observe halt_buried at the_ring as sign when toroldMourned(torold) and haltStands() "People still lower their voices going past the ring, though there is nobody in it now; and they have started leaving things on the empty bier: a spoon, a crust, a ribbon, a little bronze pin.".

  // ── Ned, afterwards ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic ned_father with ned "Ask Ned how it was, seeing his father" when joryMet(jory) once {
    Says "Ned is quiet for so long that you think he will not answer. 'He brought my cap,' he says at last. 'I left it on the peg. He brought it all the way up through the white in his coat so it'd be warm.' He touches it; he is wearing it. 'It isn't warm now.' He looks at the floor. 'He asked was I hungry. I said no. Then I said yes, so he'd have something to do, and he went and asked Grimbold for bread, and stood over me while I ate it, like you do with a calf.' He swallows. 'He's coming every week. He said. I said he doesn't have to. He said, I know I don't.'".
  }
  Topic ned_noon with ned "Ask Ned whether he minds being neither one thing nor the other" when knows(actor, ned_dead) and nedHome(ned) once {
    Says "Ned thinks about it while he kneads, which he is getting better at. 'Cleeve says at noon the sun's not going up nor down,' he says. 'It's just there. Like it's thinking.' He slaps the dough over. 'I don't want to go to a hall and fight every day. I'd be rubbish. I'd be dead the first morning and get up and be dead again, and they'd all laugh.' He grins, suddenly sixteen. 'I'm a baker now. Grimbold says I'm the worst baker in two worlds. He says that's a start.'".
  }

  // ── Ansel ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic ansel_death with ansel "Ask Ansel Haverlock how he died" when true once {
    Says "'In the rearguard at Haverlock Water,' says Ansel, 'which was my father's ford, in the evening, holding it while the household got away.' He says it lightly, as an old story. 'I was eighteen. I had been knighted that morning, in a hurry, in the rain, because there was nobody older left.' He looks at his hands. 'I held it until the sun was in my eyes, and then I didn't. Cleeve said west, and I came here, and I have held fords ever since. It is the only thing I was ever taught to do well.' A pause. 'And sing, a little. My mother taught me the forms of courtesy and a great many songs, and I was killed before I could use either on anybody.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ansel_young). }
  }
  Discovery ansel_young "Ansel Haverlock died at eighteen in the evening rearguard at his father's ford, knighted that morning in the rain because there was nobody older left. He was taught courtesy and songs, and killed before he could use either on anybody.".
  Topic ansel_after with ansel "Ask Ansel Haverlock whether he is happy" when wedded(mab) once {
    Says "Ansel considers the question with great seriousness, as if it were a point of courtesy he had not been taught. 'I think so,' he says. 'I do not know the form.' He watches Mab across the lane arguing with a crossbowwoman about a spoon. 'She snores,' he says, wonderingly. 'Nobody told me that people snore. We never slept, on the Field; we got up.' He bows slightly to nobody, out of habit. 'I am going to have to learn everything,' he says, 'from the beginning,' and he does not sound sorry about it at all.".
  }

  Topic mab_ansel_young with mab "Tell Mab Treloar how Ansel Haverlock died" when knows(actor, ansel_young) and paired(mab) once {
    Says "Mab listens with her arms folded. 'Knighted that morning,' she says. 'In the rain.' She snorts, and then does not. 'Two hundred year I've been sticking a boy.' She looks away down the lane to where he is, bowing to somebody who has not noticed. 'Well,' she says. 'He's not getting any older. Somebody'll have to teach him.'".
  }

  // ── Torold, after Edith ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic torold_edith_after with torold "Ask Torold Hame why he let Edith Marl go" when edithSpared(edith) once {
    Says "Torold is a long time answering. 'Because he laughed,' he says. 'The first night. Telling me. He laughed about the vats.' He looks at the frost on his friend's face. 'Up here I could forget that, because up here nothing stayed. You kill a man and he gets up and you drink with him that night.' He shakes his head slowly. 'She's carried it twenty years. Down there, where things stay. I'd no right to take it from her. And I'd have been doing it for him.' He breathes out. 'He'd have laughed at that too.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/endings:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The Morning After ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At first light after the Testing day the horns sound, or they do not. Then the book closes on what the forty days
  // made, and on the Field; and the Field goes on.
  Query accounting() means outcomeDecided(field_country) and morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7.
  Chapter ch_after_field "The Morning After" when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 6 and inYsgard(party) "First light on the Field. Everyone on it, the living and the dead, is listening for the same thing.".
  Chapter ch_after_larum "The Morning After" when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 6 and not inYsgard(party) "First light in Larum. Everyone in the street is standing with their heads on one side, looking up at the Pass.".
  Rule horns_sound within field_country when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7 and outcomeDaily(field_country) and not spoke(horns_told)
    says "At the third horn they come down off both heights, Morrow from the east and Even from the west, as they have every morning for nine hundred years, and meet on the ford, and the noise goes up off the Field like a flock of birds. It goes over Halt. Halt does not slow it. By noon the shield-walls are down and the banner lanes are trodden into the snow, and the Oven's mantlet is on its side, and the Daily goes on over the place where the town was as if it had never been there." { Assert spoke(horns_told). }
  Rule horns_half_even within field_country when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7 and outcomeHalf(field_country) and halfByEven(field_country) and not spoke(horns_told)
    says "At the third horn Evenhall comes down the stone stair to the ford, and turns on itself, and begins: Even against Even, the Daily with one side. On the eastern height Morrowhall's doors stay shut. And in Halt, a mile from the ford, the dead of Morrow stand in their lanes listening to it, and go on with what they were doing, and the sound of it goes over them every day after that, like weather." { Assert spoke(horns_told). }
  Rule horns_half_morrow within field_country when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7 and outcomeHalf(field_country) and halfByMorrow(field_country) and not spoke(horns_told)
    says "At the third horn the doors of Morrowhall open, and Morrow comes down off the eastern height to the ford, because Hild Varley knows now that there is nothing to be afraid of, and does not know what else Morrow is for; and finds no Even there, and turns on itself, and begins. Even stays at its benches and in Halt, and listens to it, every day after, like weather." { Assert spoke(horns_told). }
  Rule horns_silent within field_country when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7 and (outcomeHalt(field_country) or outcomeQuiet(field_country) or outcomeFear(field_country)) and not spoke(horns_told)
    says "The third horn does not sound. Nor the first. The sun stands low in the white where it always stands, and the Field lies under it with nobody on it but a few Runners with a sledge, and in Halt the smoke goes up from the Oven, and somebody is laughing in the banner lanes." { Assert spoke(horns_told). }
  Entity horns_told: fact "the morning after".
  Rule larum_hears_loud within larum when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7 and skyLoud() and not spoke(larum_told)
    says "Down off the Pass, out of the standing cloud, faint as bells three valleys off, it comes: iron on iron, thousands of it. Larum stops in the street. A woman puts her hand to her mouth. Then somebody laughs, and somebody else, and the shepherd with the walnut face says, 'There. There, now,' as if to a ewe; and by noon nobody is listening to it, and that night Bet Garside sleeps until ten." { Assert spoke(larum_told). }
  Rule larum_hears_quiet within larum when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7 and not skyLoud() and outcomeDecided(field_country) and not spoke(larum_told)
    says "Nothing comes down off the Pass. Larum stands in the street with its head on one side and listens to nothing, as it has for forty-five days. Then Bet Garside comes out of the Hark with her two dented pans, and looks at them, and hangs them up on a nail by the door." { Assert spoke(larum_told). }
  Entity larum_told: fact "Larum's morning".

  // ── What the forty days made ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule fate_bread when accounting() and breadRisen(grimbold) and not spoke(fate_bread_told) says "Grimbold Ure bakes every morning at three, as his father did, and the Runners carry flour up from Larum a sack at a time, and Nance Pellett's Mother lives in a crock on a shelf above an oven built out of a broken bell, two hundred and some years old, in heaven. On the Field they still say nothing rises but the dead; and then they say, and Grimbold's bread." { Assert spoke(fate_bread_told). }
  Rule fate_bread_daily when accounting() and breadRisen(grimbold) and outcomeDaily(field_country) and not spoke(fate_bread_daily_told) says "When the Daily trampled Halt the Oven went over with it. Grimbold carried the crock up to Morrowhall inside his shirt, against his chest, where it is cold, and it died there before the Hour. He goes down to the Field every morning by the third horn with the rest of Morrow. He does not go mad any more. He is not much good." { Assert spoke(fate_bread_daily_told). }
  Rule fate_wedding when accounting() and wedded(mab) and not spoke(fate_wedding_told) says "Mab Treloar and Ansel Haverlock keep a tent in the banner lanes, of a black bird on gold that somebody picked off the Field. He bows to her every morning, the little bow. She has never once spat." { Assert spoke(fate_wedding_told). }
  Rule fate_wedding_daily when accounting() and wedded(mab) and outcomeDaily(field_country) and not spoke(fate_wedding_daily_told) says "On the first morning of the Daily, Mab Treloar and Ansel Haverlock did not go down to the ford. They went north, up the stair on the Old Ice, to sit with the Sitters and learn to play stones; and they are there still, and the halls have forgotten them, which they say is very restful." { Assert spoke(fate_wedding_daily_told). }
  Rule fate_paired_only when accounting() and paired(mab) and not wedded(mab) and not spoke(fate_wedding_told) says "Mab Treloar and Ansel Haverlock meet at the ford at noon, every day, with nothing in their hands, and talk. Nobody has married them. There is no form for it." { Assert spoke(fate_wedding_told). }
  Rule fate_song when accounting() and songMade(wystan) and not spoke(fate_song_told) says "Wystan Hollins's song about the sheep is sung in Halt by people who have forgotten who made it, which is how he says he likes it. He has made two more since, both bad. He is working on a third." { Assert spoke(fate_song_told). }
  Rule fate_elegy when accounting() and elegyMade(wystan) and not spoke(fate_song_told) says "Wystan Hollins's elegy for Halvard Eld is the best thing he ever made. Larum has it in print within the month, at a penny a sheet, and it sells in three countries; and wherever there is a war in Imbar, men sing it going in." { Assert spoke(fate_song_told). }
  Rule fate_runners when accounting() and runnersSeated(cuddy) and not spoke(fate_runners_told) says "There is a bench in Morrowhall, the low one by the door, where the Runners sit with horn cups while the hall eats. Cuddy Wardle sits at the end and swings her legs. Morrow hates it. Hild Varley says, good." { Assert spoke(fate_runners_told). }
  Rule fate_strike when accounting() and runnersStrike(cuddy) and not runnersSeated(cuddy) and not spoke(fate_runners_told) says "The Runners did not go out with the sledges that night, nor the next, and nobody on the heights knew what to do about it. Cuddy Wardle has been to both halls since, in a clean smock, by the front door." { Assert spoke(fate_runners_told). }
  Rule fate_sitters when accounting() and sittersDown(aulus) and not spoke(fate_sitters_told) says "The Sitters play stones on the floor of the Truce every evening, surrounded by the dead of both halls arguing about the rules. Aulus has found Cassian, in Morrow, after seven hundred years. They are not speaking. They play every night." { Assert spoke(fate_sitters_told). }
  Rule fate_plough when accounting() and ploughMade(gorm) and haltStands() and not spoke(fate_plough_told) says "On the southern Field, where the battle-lines never quite reached, there is a strip of ground scraped clean of iron and turned over with a plough of four swords, and something has been sown in it from a sack carried up from Larum. Nobody knows yet whether anything will come up in Ysgard. Gorm Hallett goes out every morning to look." { Assert spoke(fate_plough_told). }
  Rule fate_ned_halt when accounting() and haltStands() and knows(party, ned_dead) and not spoke(fate_ned_told) says "In Cleeve's ledger, after nine hundred years of EAST and WEST, there is a third column now, ruled in fresh ink: HALT, for those who come in with no hour. The first name in it is Ned Whitlock's." { Assert spoke(fate_ned_told). }
  Rule fate_ned_daily when accounting() and outcomeDaily(field_country) and knows(party, ned_dead) and not spoke(fate_ned_told) says "Ned Whitlock, who came in at noon, went to the Runners in the end, because there was nowhere else; Cuddy Wardle took him on the sledges. Every night after the Hour he drags the broken off the ford, a boy with a blackthorn stick tucked in his belt." { Assert spoke(fate_ned_told). }
  Entity fate_bread_told: fact "the bread". Entity fate_bread_daily_told: fact "the bread under the Daily". Entity fate_wedding_told: fact "the marriage".
  Entity fate_wedding_daily_told: fact "the marriage under the Daily". Entity fate_song_told: fact "the song". Entity fate_runners_told: fact "the Runners".
  Entity fate_sitters_told: fact "the Sitters". Entity fate_plough_told: fact "the plough". Entity fate_ned_told: fact "Ned".
  Rule fate_jory when accounting() and joryMet(jory) and not spoke(fate_jory_told) says "Jory Whitlock goes up through the White every seventh day, in his good coat, and sits with his son a few hours, and comes down before the cold. He does not say much about it in Larum. He has stopped laying the second cup." { Assert spoke(fate_jory_told). }
  Rule fate_jory_untold when accounting() and knows(party, ned_dead) and not joryTold(jory) and not spoke(fate_jory_told) says "In Larum Jory Whitlock still lays two cups, and the mule is in the byre, and nobody has told him." { Assert spoke(fate_jory_told). }
  Entity fate_jory_told: fact "Jory".
  Rule fate_edith_home_shaken when accounting() and edithHome(edith) and edithShaken(edith) and not spoke(fate_edith_told) says "Edith Marl went down the valley road on foot. A chapman says a woman with fuller's hands keeps a stall at Wendham market, selling cloth; and that once a year, in the summer of the bad wool, she shuts it and walks to where Wendmere was, and stands there." { Assert spoke(fate_edith_told). }
  Rule fate_edith_home when accounting() and edithHome(edith) and not spoke(fate_edith_told) says "Edith Marl went down the valley road on foot and was not heard of again in Larum, except that a chapman said a woman with fuller's hands had taken a stall at Wendham market, selling cloth, and would not have the ballad sung within earshot." { Assert spoke(fate_edith_told). }
  Rule fate_edith_killed when accounting() and edithDead(edith) and toroldKilledEdith(torold) and not spoke(fate_edith_told) says "Edith Marl came in out of the snow an hour after Torold Hame's sword, and Cleeve sent her west, into Evenhall. Torold was waiting at the foot of the stone stair. He has not lifted a sword since. He brings her a cup of mead every evening, at the end of the lowest bench, and she drinks it, and neither of them has said a word to the other, and they sit there." { Assert spoke(fate_edith_told). }
  Rule fate_edith_dead when accounting() and edithDead(edith) and not spoke(fate_edith_told) says "Edith Marl came in out of the snow in the afternoon, and Cleeve sent her west, into Evenhall, where Halvard Eld's name runs up the Tally from the floor to the roof. She sits at the end of a bench and does not fight and does not speak, and Torold Hame brings her a cup of mead every evening, and she drinks it, and neither of them says anything at all." { Assert spoke(fate_edith_told). }
  Rule fate_edith_unknown when accounting() and at(edith, edith_nook) and not knows(party, edith_named) and visitedBefore(warren) and not spoke(fate_edith_told) says "In the Scrapes, behind a banner, there is a woman in three Runners' smocks whose breath goes up white in the lamplight. She has learned the sledges. Nobody on the Field has asked her name." { Assert spoke(fate_edith_told). }
  Rule fate_edith_hidden when accounting() and at(edith, edith_nook) and knows(party, edith_named) and not spoke(fate_edith_told) says "Edith Marl is still in the Scrapes, in three Runners' smocks, shivering. She has learned the sledges. The Runners say she is better at them than most of the dead." { Assert spoke(fate_edith_told). }
  Entity fate_edith_told: fact "Edith".
  Rule fate_torold_ice when accounting() and buriedIce(torold) and not spoke(fate_torold_told) says "Torold Hame goes up to the Old Ice every evening at the Hour, and stands with his hand flat on the clear ice over his friend's face while the blue comes over, and then comes down." { Assert spoke(fate_torold_told). }
  Rule fate_torold_larum when accounting() and buriedLarum(torold) and not spoke(fate_torold_told) says "Torold Hame stands at the Coming-in every evening at the Hour, at the edge of the snow, and listens; and down in Larum the parson rings the Mending Bell, three times, and now he knows for whom." { Assert spoke(fate_torold_told). }
  Rule fate_torold_knows when accounting() and state(halvard, lying) and toroldKnows(torold) and knows(party, halvard_fell) and not spoke(fate_torold_told) says "Halvard Eld lies in the ring of spears under his frost, and Torold Hame stands over him still, though he knows now that the blue will never come over that face. He says somebody has to. People bring him things to hold while he stands there, a cup, a loaf, and he holds them." { Assert spoke(fate_torold_told). }
  Rule fate_torold_none when accounting() and state(halvard, lying) and knows(party, halvard_fell) and not spoke(fate_torold_told) says "Halvard Eld lies in the ring of spears in the middle of the Field under his frost. Torold Hame stands over him. At the Hour, every evening, he watches the face for it, and it does not come." { Assert spoke(fate_torold_told). }
  Entity fate_torold_told: fact "Torold".

  // ── The endings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Ending ending_halt "Halt" when accounting() and outcomeHalt(field_country) "They know now. Nothing came back to the Field but what came up the Pass, and they could go down to the ford by the third horn tomorrow and every day after and get up at the Hour every evening until the stars go out. They do not. They stay at their benches and their ovens and their swapping-blankets, Morrow and Even and Runner and noon, because forty days have given them something they would rather do. It is not safe, and it is not finished. It is only chosen. In Larum, below, it is quiet, and the Mending Bell rings at dusk, and everybody knows why.".
  Ending ending_quiet_known "The Long Quiet" over ending_quiet when accounting() and outcomeQuiet(field_country) and knows(party, living_kills) "Nobody on the Field knows what killed Halvard Eld. They believe death has come back to Ysgard, for all of them, and so the horns stay silent, and Halt grows, a tent at a time. It is a peace. It stands on not knowing. A breather knows what it stands on, and has not said, and goes down through the White to Larum, where it is quiet, carrying it.".
  Ending ending_quiet "The Long Quiet" when accounting() and outcomeQuiet(field_country) "Nobody on the Field knows what killed Halvard Eld, and nor, quite, do you. They believe death has come back to Ysgard, for all of them, and so the horns stay silent, and Halt grows, a tent at a time. It is a gentle peace, made of fear and spoons, and nobody knows how long it will last, and nobody asks.".
  Ending ending_fear "The Kept Fear" when accounting() and outcomeFear(field_country) "They saw a man of Even lie on the ford at the Hour and not get up, and they know now that death has come back to Ysgard, and the horns will never sound again. Halt will grow into a city. They will make bread and songs and marriages in it, and teach their children, if the dead ever have children, that the Field is death. It is a good peace, and it will last. You are the only person in either world who knows what it is made of. When you go down through the White your breath goes up in front of you, and you watch it, and do not look back.".
  Ending ending_half "Half a Field" when accounting() and outcomeHalf(field_country) "The Field is a war with one side now. Every morning one hall comes down and fights itself on the ford, and every evening gets up, and the other hall sits in Halt a mile away and bakes and swaps and listens to it, the way you listen to rain. Nobody can say whether this is better. Larum, below, hears the sky again, a little fainter than before, and says it is not the same noise.".
  Ending ending_daily_unseen "The Daily" over ending_daily when accounting() and outcomeDaily(field_country) and not visitedBefore(halt_cross) "Somewhere over the Pass, on the fourth morning, the men of Even went down to the ford and fought each other, and at the Hour every one of them got up, and so nothing had come back; and the next morning the horns sounded on both heights. Whatever the quiet was, it is over. In Larum the shepherds do not look up any more. You stood once at the head of the Pass, in a light like the inside of a knife, and looked down at a huddle of coloured tents in the middle of a white plain, and did not go down to see what they were.".
  Ending ending_daily "The Daily" when accounting() and outcomeDaily(field_country) "Every man of Even got up at the Hour, and so nothing had come back, and in the morning the horns sounded at the third hour on both heights, and the Field was what it had always been. Halt is snow and rags. The Oven is on its side. In Larum the noise is back, faint as bells three valleys off, and Bet Garside sleeps, and the shepherds do not look up any more, and nobody but you remembers that for forty-five days there was a town on the Field where people learned to make spoons.".
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/fellows:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The Account, kept: what each of a company sees at Larum and on the Field, and the one grave that must be chosen ───
  // The count is the Daily, kept by two halls and a bell; the first page is the Quarrel over whether noon moves first
  // or last, which the Sitters hold and nobody has asked for; the price of reading it is a man who stays dead. Nine
  // hundred, seven hundred and three hundred years are all said on this Field, and none of what follows reconciles them.

  // ── Voices ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation heardBellOffice(group). Relation heardHarness(group). Relation heardLocks(group). Relation heardWatch(group). Relation heardBallads(group).

  Rule voice_bell_office at larum_chapel when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, larum_chapel) and not heardBellOffice(party)
    says "{?m} takes the rope in both hands without ringing it, and feels the weight of the bell come down it. 'Three and three,' {?m} says, to the board over the door. 'That is not a mending bell. That is a passing bell: three for the one, three for the road. We ring it for the dying, in the parishes I know, and for nobody else.' {?m} lets the rope go up. 'Somebody changed one word in the founder's will, and was kind about it. It was never for the living.'" teaches bell_is_passing {
    Assert heardBellOffice(party).
  }
  Discovery bell_is_passing "The Mending Bell of Larum rings three and three, which is the form of a passing bell, rung for the dying and not for the living; someone long ago changed its name to something kinder.".
  Rule voice_harness at ice_stair when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and awake(?m) and at(party, ice_stair) and not heardHarness(party)
    says "{?m} stays where {?m} is, and looks at the white shape on the shelf for a long time before looking at anything else. 'A war-bear,' {?m} says, very low. 'Dwarvish. That is a bridle-ring on the harness, and those are brass studs where the girths went. It was trained to guard a stair and to be fed by one hand.' {?m} lets out a breath. 'It is not angry. It is on duty. It has been on duty for nine hundred years and has not once been relieved. Do not run. Do not throw anything but food. I can talk to it, if you let me, and it may let us by on the strength of that.'" {
    Assert heardHarness(party).
  }
  Rule voice_locks at halt_cross when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, halt_cross) and not heardLocks(party)
    says "{?m} walks the length of Trophy Row with a hand trailing along the pegs, and slows, and goes back. 'There isn't a lock,' {?m} says. 'Not on a door, not on a chest, not on a purse. Nine hundred years of the dead and nobody has ever needed one.' {?m} takes a bronze cup off a peg, looks at it, and puts it back exactly where it was. 'I find that harder to be in than a street full of thieves,' {?m} says." {
    Assert heardLocks(party).
  }
  Rule voice_watch at the_ring when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_warrior) and awake(?m) and at(party, the_ring) and state(halvard, lying) and not heardWatch(party)
    says "{?m} stands at the edge of the ring and watches the watch for a quarter of an hour, the way a sergeant would. 'Forty days,' {?m} says. 'Nobody has sat down. They changed the guard four times a night for the first week, and then stopped changing, and just stood. That is a watch that has forgotten what it is watching for.' {?m} nods at Torold Hame, whose hands have not left the sword-hilt. 'Do not give that man an order. Give him a reason to put it down. A man who has stood that long wants relieving, and does not know it.'" {
    Assert heardWatch(party).
  }
  Rule voice_ballads at hark when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, hark) and not heardBallads(party)
    says "{?m} runs an eye along the beams, lips moving, and stops under the woodcut of Halvard Eld. 'Look,' {?m} says. 'Every ballad on the wall is in the same metre, the penny-press metre, because old Habakkuk sets them all himself. Except this one. The first verse and the last are one man's work, and the middle is a patch by another, with a worse ear. Somebody put a middle in a ballad that did not have one.' {?m} taps the beam." {
    Assert heardBallads(party).
  }

  // ── A ranger's way through: the bear on the Sitters' stair ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Meat will do, and a climb will do; a ranger has a third thing, which asks for nothing the bear does not already want.
  Action calm_bear(actor: group, site: place, r: member) "Have {r} speak to the bear, low, from where {r} stands, as to a guard on duty" {
    Description "It has been on watch nine hundred years. It may be glad to be spoken to by someone who knows what a watch is.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bear, site) and able(bear) and not tolerates(bear, actor)
      and memberOf(r, actor) and hasCalling(r, calling_ranger).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert tolerates(bear, actor). Retract warned(bear, actor). }
    Result "{r} goes down on one knee in the trodden snow, palms out, and talks, in the flat even voice of someone reporting to a superior: no names, no hurry, a list of who is on the stair and why and when they will go. The bear listens with its head on one side, and its breath, which does not steam, goes in and out. At the end {r} says, quietly, 'Relieved.' The great head dips. It lies down on the shelf, crosswise, so that you may pass behind it, and puts its chin on its paws like a dog in a doorway.".
  }

  // A company with no ranger has a poorer road: a soldier knows what a sentry is owed, if not what this one is owed.
  // Standing to, giving the countersign of the wrong army and asking to relieve the post is a gamble, and a bear that
  // is not relieved takes it out of whoever asked.
  Hazard bear_cuff "a blow from the war-bear" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  Relation saluteFailed(group).
  Action salute_bear(actor: group, site: place, w: member) "Have {w} stand to, give the sentry's countersign, and ask to relieve the post" {
    Description "Not the bear's army, and not the bear's tongue. A soldier's voice, and a soldier's back.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bear, site) and able(bear) and not tolerates(bear, actor) and not saluteFailed(actor)
      and memberOf(w, actor) and hasCalling(w, calling_warrior) and not companyHasRanger(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert tolerates(bear, actor). Retract warned(bear, actor). }
    On failure { Assert saluteFailed(actor). Assert strikes(bear_cuff, actor). }
    Result "{w} comes to attention in the trodden snow, heels together, and says it in the voice that carries across a parade-ground: who is relieved, and by whom, and at what hour. It is not the right army. The bear listens with its head on one side and the breath not steaming, and then goes down on all fours, slowly, and turns its flank to you, and the shelf is clear. It does not lie down. It watches you the whole way past.".
    Otherwise "{w} says it, loud and correct, and it is the wrong army. The bear lets the word finish, and then reaches out almost gently and sets one paw across {w}'s chest and leans, and you are in the snow at the foot of the steps with the wind out of you and your ribs in a new order.".
  }
  Rule company_has_ranger when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and not companyHasRanger(party) { Assert companyHasRanger(party). }
  Relation companyHasRanger(group).

  // ── Where the grave is: the warrior and the cleric disagree, and are both right ───────────────────────────────────────
  // Torold Hame will bury Halvard up in the Old Ice among his own, or down at Larum under the bell. A company that has a
  // warrior and a cleric and has learned of both graves hears each of them say so; siding with one chooses the grave, and
  // the other keeps their silence all the way to the end of the carrying.
  Relation quarrelledGrave(group). Relation sidedUp(group). Relation sidedDown(group).
  Rule grave_quarrel at the_ring when memberOf(?w, party) and hasCalling(?w, calling_warrior) and awake(?w)
    and memberOf(?c, party) and hasCalling(?c, calling_cleric) and awake(?c) and at(party, the_ring) and state(halvard, lying) and toroldConsents(torold)
    and knows(party, ice_burial) and knows(party, bell_heard) and not iceChosen(torold) and not larumChosen(torold) and not quarrelledGrave(party)
    says "{?w} says it first, because somebody must. 'Up. The Hour is up there; the Sitters are up there; it is the only grave in Ysgard, and he is a man of the Field. You bury a soldier in his own country.' {?c} does not raise a voice. 'He cut WENDMERE into a cairn for twelve years,' {?c} says. 'There is a bell down there that rings three and three. I would put him where somebody rings for him, and has ever since the founder, and did not know whom.' Neither of them looks at you, and Torold Hame, who is listening to both, is waiting to be told." {
    Assert quarrelledGrave(party).
  }
  Action side_up(actor: group, site: place, w: member, c: member) "Tell {c} that {w} is right, and carry Halvard up to the Old Ice" {
    Description "Among his own, under the blue, beside the one grave there has ever been. {c} will say the office all the same.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_ring) and quarrelledGrave(party) and not sidedUp(party) and not sidedDown(party) and not iceChosen(torold) and not larumChosen(torold)
      and memberOf(w, actor) and hasCalling(w, calling_warrior) and memberOf(c, actor) and hasCalling(c, calling_cleric).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert sidedUp(party). Assert iceChosen(torold). Increase toroldTrust(torold) by 1. }
    Result "{c} says nothing for a long moment, and then inclines the head, and goes and stands at the foot of the bier with a hand on the shields. 'Then I will say it there,' {c} says. {w} lets out a breath and goes to take a pole. Torold looks from one to the other, and takes his hands from the sword at last, and says to the watch, not loudly, 'Up. We carry him up.'".
  }
  Action side_down(actor: group, site: place, w: member, c: member) "Tell {w} that {c} is right, and carry Halvard down to Larum churchyard" {
    Description "Under the bell, in ground with a name. {w} will take the front pole all the way down through the White.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_ring) and quarrelledGrave(party) and not sidedUp(party) and not sidedDown(party) and not iceChosen(torold) and not larumChosen(torold)
      and memberOf(w, actor) and hasCalling(w, calling_warrior) and memberOf(c, actor) and hasCalling(c, calling_cleric).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert sidedDown(party). Assert larumChosen(torold). Increase toroldTrust(torold) by 1. }
    Result "{w} says nothing against it, which is not agreeing, and takes up the front pole as if it were a spear, and shifts the weight of it onto a shoulder. 'Down, then,' {w} says, to nobody, in the voice of a soldier giving up a hill. {c} puts a hand on the dead man's chest, briefly. Torold watches them both, and takes his hands from the sword at last, and says, 'Down. To the white. We carry him as far as we can.'".
  }
  Observe grave_up_after at ice_foot as feature when buriedIce(torold) and sidedUp(party) "At the foot of the Old Ice, by the two cairns, a pair of footprints go up to the new grave and stop, and a third pair, smaller, are drawn up beside them, side by side. Whoever stood here at the Hour said the lowland office over a man of the Field, in the Field's own snow, and it is the first time in nine hundred years that the sound of it has carried there.".
  Observe grave_down_after at larum_chapel as feature when buriedLarum(torold) and sidedDown(party) "In the corner of the chapel yard, by the new grave, someone has laid a soldier's spear flat on the turf, point to the Pass, where a mourner would put a stone. The parson rings the bell at dusk, three and three, and Bet Garside says it is the first time in forty days it has sounded like it was for somebody.".

  Observe grave_up_unsaid at ice_foot as feature when buriedIce(torold) and not sidedUp(party) "At the foot of the Old Ice, by the two cairns, the Sitters stand with their picks grounded. Nobody says the lowland office over him. Torold says what he has: Halvard Eld, of Wendmere, of the Evenhall; his number; the day he came in at noon. The Sitters take their hats off, which they have not done for anything in three hundred years, and put them on again.".
  Observe grave_down_unsaid at larum_chapel as feature when buriedLarum(torold) and not sidedDown(party) "In the corner of the chapel yard the new grave has no stone. The parson has said what the book says, and the company has stood by with its hats off, and Bet Garside, afterwards, has rung it three and three on her own account.".

  // ── The guide's table ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A foreshadow for anyone who looks, and its payoff when Jory has found his son: a cup.
  Observe guide_cups at guide_house as feature when not joryMet(jory) "The table is laid for two and one cup has been used. The other is turned the right way up, as a cup is that is expected to be wanted. Jory does not look at it going out.".
  Observe guide_cups_drunk at guide_house as feature when joryMet(jory) "The table is laid for two and both cups have been drunk from. Jory has left the second one where it was, and washed it.".

  // ── Material culture and the kept light ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe chapel_hollows at larum_chapel as feature when true "The hollows worn in the stone floor are not a crowd's, which would be shallow and wide. They are two, a left foot and a right, deep as a bowl, side by side, in front of the rope, and a third pair behind them for a second ringer. Whoever stood there stood the way a smith stands at an anvil, with the left foot forward and the weight on the heel, for three hundred years. Every parson since has put his feet in them without knowing why.".
  Observe chapel_candles at larum_chapel as feature when true "On the ledge under the window stands a bundle of tall white fluted candles tied with red wool, and a ticket in the sexton's hand: HUME CART, NINE, FOR THE VIGIL, UNLIT. The parson burns one at the Hour and one at dawn when someone is dying, and says they last three nights and nobody in Larum has ever made one that would.".
  Observe booth_cloth at snow_gate as feature when true "On a nail in the Teller's booth hangs a grey-gold curtain-cloth that does not frost, a carter's gift from the north. Cleeve says it is the only thing in the booth that keeps its heat, and that he has stopped asking what it is made of.".
  Observe larum_cloth at larum_street as feature when not dark() "The doors of the better houses have a curtain of grey-gold cloth hung with the right edge turned in. It comes up the west road from Sixways for winter wool and lamp-oil, and must be given, never bought.".
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/field.k:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The Field ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe south_scene at field_south when haltStands() "The southern Field: snow, wind-scoured in long ripples, and out of it, everywhere, things. A sword standing up on its point. A shield-boss like a little iron hill. A gauntlet, palm up, with snow in it. The Field goes away north to Halt's smoke, and east and west to the two heights. To the south the ice of the Field's edge overhangs a long shadow where the Runners live; to the south-west, the black crags of the Teeth.".
  Observe south_daily at field_south when outcomeDaily(field_country) "The southern Field, and the Daily far off to the north of it, by the ford: a great dark smudge of people on the white, moving, and a noise like surf.".
  Observe ford_scene at lathe_ford when true "The ford of the Lathe, where for nine hundred years the Daily began, both hosts racing for it by the third horn: a frozen river crossing the Field between low banks, its ice grey and scarred and gouged. The banks are trodden into terraces.".
  Observe ford_uncleared at lathe_ford as feature when not fordCleared() "On both banks, in the snow, iron: the whole last day's worth of it, broken and frozen in where it fell. Nobody has cleared it.".
  Query fordCleared() means not runnersStrike(cuddy) and testingNamed(field_country) and day(clock) >= testDay(clock).
  Observe ford_iron at lathe_ford as feature when fordCleared() "The banks have been cleared overnight, scraped down to the ice: long sledge-tracks go away south toward the Scrapes.".
  Observe clear_scene at the_clear when true "Here the Field is clear ice, and you look down into it as into deep still water at nine hundred years of dropped arms, layer under layer, with bronze at the bottom. There is no bottom you can see: only things, hanging. Near the top, crossbow-bolts and pikes and a helmet with a plume frozen upright. Lower, mail, long-hafted axes, a horse's skull in a chanfron. Lower still, bronze: round shields, leaf-shaped blades, gone green. And lower than that, so deep they are only shadows in the green, shapes nobody could name. It is like looking down through history. Nobody is under the ice: only what they dropped. Everyone who dropped it got up.".
  Observe east_slope_scene at east_slope when true "The foot of the Morrow height, where the eastern host came down every morning: the snow trodden into a broad road going up, and at the top, black against the dawn side of the sky, Morrowhall. Along the road at intervals stand spears planted upright with rags of red on them, where somebody marked a line once, and nobody took them up.".
  Observe west_slope_scene at west_slope when true "The foot of the Even height, where the western host came down: a stair of flat stones laid in the snow by somebody's long patience, going up to Evenhall, grey against the sunset side of the sky. At the foot of the stair a great slab of stone is painted with a list of names in faded red that goes on down out of sight under the snow.".

  // ── Picking ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Heaven-iron for Master Ambler: what a day's picking turns up on the battle-line, and, under the Clear, the bronze.
  Item crossbow_one "a crossbow of the last century" is crossbow_find at limbo.
  Item mail_one "a shirt of rusted mail" is mail_find at limbo.
  Item banner_one "a frozen banner" is banner_find at limbo.
  Item bronze_one "a bronze blade from the bottom of the Clear" is bronze_find at limbo.
  Relation pickedSouth(group). Relation pickedFord(group). Relation pickedEast(group).
  Action pick_south(actor: group, site: place) "Pick over the southern Field for heaven-iron" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, field_south) and not pickedSouth(actor) and at(crossbow_one, limbo).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert pickedSouth(actor). Give crossbow_one to actor. }
    Result "You go along the ripples of snow kicking at things, and most of it is junk, rust and splinters, but under a drift there is a crossbow with a running fox carved on the stock and a row of notches, and you dig it out with numb fingers.".
  }
  Action pick_ford(actor: group, site: place) "Pick over the banks of the ford for heaven-iron" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lathe_ford) and not pickedFord(actor) and at(mail_one, limbo).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert pickedFord(actor). Give mail_one to actor. }
    Result "The banks of the ford are thick with the last day's iron, frozen in. You lever out a shirt of mail rusted into one stiff sheet, and stand holding it, and realise the last man who wore it took it off at the Hour and walked away.".
  }
  Action pick_east(actor: group, site: place) "Pick along the marked line under the Morrow height" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, east_slope) and not pickedEast(actor) and at(banner_one, limbo).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert pickedEast(actor). Give banner_one to actor. }
    Result "By one of the rag-hung spears you find a banner trodden into the snow, and pull it out stiff as a board: a black bird on what was once gold.".
  }
  Action cut_clear(actor: group, site: place) "Cut down through the Clear to the bronze" {
    Description "A long day's work with whatever you have, down through the clear ice to the nearest green.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_clear) and at(bronze_one, limbo) and not cutToday(actor).
    Time 12.
    Resolve check(actor, digging, dc_hard).
    On success { Give bronze_one to actor. }
    On failure { Assert cutToday(actor). }
    Result "You cut, and cut, and the chips fly blue and the hole goes down and the cold comes up out of it, and the green shape below you grows slowly from a shadow into a thing, until at last, lying on your belly with your arm down the shaft to the shoulder, you close numb fingers on a hilt bound in leather a thousand years old and draw up a sword of bronze, green as a leaf.".
    Otherwise "You cut until your arms will not lift, and the hole is a yard deep and the green shape at the bottom is as far off as ever. The ice is very old, and very hard, and does not care.".
  }
  Relation cutToday(group).
  Rule cut_resets when hour(clock) == 0 and cutToday(?g) { Retract cutToday(?g). }
  // What the finds have seen: told by the dead who were there.
  Topic saltash_crossbow with saltash "Show Old Saltash the crossbow with the running fox" when holding(actor, crossbow_find) once {
    Says "Saltash takes it and runs his thumb down the notches. 'Fox of Harrowby,' he says. 'Even's crossbows, a hundred year back. That's Wat Fenner's, I'd know it anywhere: forty-one notches and every one of them got up and came after him the next morning.' He hands it back. 'He's in the Truce most nights. Show him. He'll cry.'".
  }

  // ── The Teeth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe teeth_path_scene at teeth_path when true "Under the Teeth the snow is deep and soft and there is no iron in it at all: nobody fought here. The crags go up black above you, sharp as their name, and between two of them a scramble of broken rock goes up to a ledge. Wolf-tracks go up it.".
  Observe ledge_scene at wolf_ledge when true "A ledge under the black crags, littered with bones: old bones, ox and horse and something bigger, gnawed white. From it a last climb goes up to the highest Tooth, where a cairn stands against the sky.".
  Observe cairn_scene at high_cairn when true "On the highest Tooth a cairn cut all over with names, and past it, impossibly far down, as through glass, the living world. There is nothing else up here but the wind. Past the cairn, past the edge of the Field and the edge of Ysgard, impossibly far down and far off, as if through a thickness of glass, there is a green country with rivers in it, small and clear as a map: Imbar, the living world, with its roads and its smoke. The dead who come up here, Cleeve says, come to look at it. The cairn's stones are cut all over with names, hundreds of them, and some with a word or two after: a town, a woman's name, a child's.".
  Observe cairn_fresh at high_cairn as feature when not knows(party, halvard_cut) "On a stone near the top, newer than the rest, two letters, H. E., and after them a word cut deep and gone over more than once.".
  Discovery halvard_cut "On the cairn on the highest Tooth, where the dead come to look down at the living world, Halvard Eld cut his letters, H. E., and after them a word, deep, gone over more than once: WENDMERE.".
  Action read_cairn(actor: group, site: place) "Read the newest name on the cairn" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, high_cairn) and not knows(actor, halvard_cut).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, halvard_cut). }
    Result "You brush the rime off with your sleeve. H. E., it says, and after it, cut deep with a knife and gone over again and again until the letters are worn into grooves: WENDMERE.".
  }
  Topic torold_cairn with torold "Tell Torold Hame what Halvard cut into the cairn on the highest Tooth" when knows(actor, halvard_cut) and state(halvard, lying) once {
    Says "Torold's face does not change. 'He went up the Tooth,' he says. 'Every week, on the rest-day after the Hour. I asked him once what for, and he laughed and said for the view.' He turns the sword a quarter-turn in the snow. 'Wendmere.' His hands tighten on the pommel. 'He never said it again after the first night. Not once in twelve years. I thought he'd—' He stops. He looks down at the face under the frost; his hand goes out and stops an inch above it. 'You'd not think a man could go up a hill every week for twelve years to look at a thing and never say,' he says. 'And I stood beside him at the Hour every night, and never knew.' He breathes out. 'I'd like to bury him,' he says. 'Somewhere he can't see it.'".
    On discuss { Increase toroldTrust(torold) by 2. Assert toroldReady(torold). }
  }
  Relation toroldReady(group).
  // The wolves of the Teeth: dead wolves, who mend like anything else; they fear flame.
  Person wolves "the frost wolves" at wolf_ledge {
    Role "a pack of dead white wolves". Species frost_wolf. Numbers 3. Temperament territorial.
    Lair wolf_ledge. Fears flame.
    Warns "Three white wolves come out from among the crags onto the ledge, lean, silent, their breath not steaming, and stand between you and the climb with their heads low. They have been dead a long time, and have nothing to lose. A brand held up would drive them back; so would going back down.".
    Comes "The wolves come at you all together, low and silent, the way wolves do.".
    Flinches "The wolves shy from the fire, and slink back in among the crags, and watch you from there with their eyes like pale coins.".
    Refuge limbo.
  }
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/funeral:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── A grave for Halvard ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Nobody on the Field knows what to do with a dead man. There has been one grave in Ysgard, in the Old Ice. And below
  // the Pass there is a churchyard, and a bell. Torold consents once he knows Halvard will not rise, or has come to
  // trust the company and is ready, and once there is somewhere to take him.
  Query graveKnown() means knows(party, ice_burial) or knows(party, bell_heard).
  Topic offer_grave with torold "Offer to help Torold Hame bury Halvard" when state(halvard, lying) and graveKnown() and (toroldKnows(torold) or toroldReady(torold) or toroldTrust(torold) >= 3) and not toroldConsents(torold) once {
    Says "Torold looks at you as if you had spoken in a language he once knew. 'Bury him,' he says. 'Up here.' He looks at the face under the frost. 'There's no burying up here. There's never been anything to bury.' Then, slowly, the words coming out of him like stones out of a field: 'He's lain on these shields forty days. I've stood here forty days. Every Hour I watch his face for it, the blue coming over, and it never comes.' He takes his hands off the sword. 'Where would we take him?'".
    On discuss { Assert toroldConsents(torold). }
  }
  Topic grave_ice with torold "Tell Torold Hame of the grave the Sitters cut in the Old Ice" answering offer_grave when knows(actor, ice_burial) {
    Says "'In the ice,' says Torold. 'There's a grave in the ice.' He looks north, at the blue wall on the far side of the Field. 'All this time.' He nods slowly. 'Up here, then, among his own. Where I can go and stand.' He calls the watch with a jerk of his head. 'We'll carry him.'".
    On discuss { Assert iceChosen(torold). }
  }
  Topic grave_larum with torold "Tell Torold Hame of Larum churchyard below the Pass, and its bell" answering offer_grave when knows(actor, bell_heard) {
    Says "Torold is quiet a long while. 'Down there,' he says. 'In the ground. Where he came from.' He looks south, toward the Coming-in and the white beyond it. 'I can't go down. None of us can. We lie down in the white.' He swallows. 'I'd carry him as far as the snow, and you'd take him on. And I'd stand at the top and hear the bell.' He looks at the face under the frost. 'He'd be where Wendmere is. Under the same sky.' He nods, once. 'Yes. Down.'".
    On discuss { Assert larumChosen(torold). }
  }
  Relation iceChosen(group). Relation larumChosen(group).
  Relation buriedIce(group). Relation buriedLarum(group).
  // The carrying: up the Field to the Old Ice, Torold and the watch on the bier-poles and the company beside it.
  Action bury_ice(actor: group, site: place) "Carry Halvard Eld to the Old Ice with Torold and the watch, and bury him there" {
    Description "Up the length of the Field to the stair, and a grave cut in the blue: most of a day.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_ring) and iceChosen(torold) and state(halvard, lying) and not testingUnder().
    Time 24.
    Grave "Once he is under the ice, Torold's Testing has nothing to wait for.".
    On success { Assert state(halvard, gone_ice). Assert buriedIce(torold). Assert toroldMourned(torold). Assert at(actor, ice_foot). Assert at(torold, ice_foot). Assert at(even_watch, the_ring). Assert hourToday(field_country). }
    Result "Torold and the watch lift the bier of shields on spear-shafts and carry it out of the ring and up the length of Halt, and the lanes empty to watch it go, and then follow it, Morrow and Even and Runner, not in any order, out across the Field and up the long white swells to the north. Nobody says anything. At the foot of the Old Ice, by the little cairn, the Sitters are waiting, nine of them and Aulus, who has brought his own pick. They cut the grave into the blue beside the old one, the way they did three hundred years ago, and lay him in it with his hands on his chest and his eyes shut, and Torold puts his sword in with him, and they fill it with ice chips and pour meltwater over, and it freezes clear, so that he lies there under the ice like a man under deep water, looking up. At the Hour the light comes blue over him, and he does not move, and Torold stands with his hand flat on the ice above his face, and it is the first time anyone on the Field has seen Torold Hame weep.".
  }
  Rule ice_mended at ice_foot when buriedIce(torold) and at(torold, ice_foot) and hour(clock) >= 21 { Assert at(torold, the_ring). }
  // The carrying down: Torold to the edge of the white; Jory and the company on through it, if Jory has been told.
  Action bury_larum_jory(actor: group, site: place) "Carry Halvard Eld to the Coming-in with Torold, and down through the White to Larum churchyard" {
    Description "Torold and the watch as far as the white; after that it is you, and whoever will help you, through the cairns and down: most of a day.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_ring) and larumChosen(torold) and state(halvard, lying) and knows(actor, white_known) and joryTold(jory) and not testingUnder().
    Time 30.
    Grave "Once he is in the ground below the Pass, Torold's Testing has nothing to wait for.".
    On success { Assert state(halvard, gone_larum). Assert buriedLarum(torold). Assert toroldMourned(torold). Assert at(actor, larum_chapel). }
    Result "Torold and the watch carry the bier out of the ring and down the length of Halt, and the dead come out of the lanes and follow, all the way across the Field and up the track to the Coming-in, and stand there at the edge of the snow-curtain, hundreds of them, as far as they can come. Cleeve takes off his hat. Torold puts his hand on Halvard's chest once, and then gives the poles into your hands. Jory Whitlock is waiting at the edge of the white in his good coat, with a Runners' sledge; you go down into the white with him between you, Jory on the front trace, through the cairns one after another, and the dead man's frost does not melt the whole way down. In Larum the parson will not have him, and Bet Garside tells the parson what she thinks of that in front of the whole street, and they dig him a grave in the corner of the churchyard by the wall. At the Hour the parson rings the Mending Bell, three times, for him, and it goes up the Pass into the cloud; and somewhere at the top, at the edge of the snow, a man in blackened mail who cannot come down is listening.".
  }
  Action bury_larum_alone(actor: group, site: place) "Carry Halvard Eld to the Coming-in with Torold, and haul him down through the White alone to Larum churchyard" {
    Description "Torold and the watch as far as the white; after that it is you, and whoever will help you, through the cairns and down: most of a day.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_ring) and larumChosen(torold) and state(halvard, lying) and knows(actor, white_known) and capable(actor, brawn) and not joryTold(jory) and not testingUnder().
    Time 30.
    Grave "Once he is in the ground below the Pass, Torold's Testing has nothing to wait for.".
    On success { Assert state(halvard, gone_larum). Assert buriedLarum(torold). Assert toroldMourned(torold). Assert at(actor, larum_chapel). }
    Result "Torold and the watch carry the bier out of the ring and down the length of Halt, and the dead come out of the lanes and follow, all the way across the Field and up the track to the Coming-in, and stand there at the edge of the snow-curtain, hundreds of them, as far as they can come. Cleeve takes off his hat. Torold puts his hand on Halvard's chest once, and then gives the poles into your hands. You go down into the white alone with him on a Runners' sledge, hauling on the trace with your whole back, through the cairns one after another, and the dead man's frost does not melt the whole way down. In Larum the parson will not have him, and Bet Garside tells the parson what she thinks of that in front of the whole street, and they dig him a grave in the corner of the churchyard by the wall. At the Hour the parson rings the Mending Bell, three times, for him, and it goes up the Pass into the cloud; and somewhere at the top, at the edge of the snow, a man in blackened mail who cannot come down is listening.".
  }
  Observe larum_grave at larum_chapel as feature when buriedLarum(torold) "Through the chapel's little window you can see the new grave in the corner of the yard by the wall, with no name on it yet, and frost on it that does not melt.".
  Observe ice_grave at ice_foot as feature when buriedIce(torold) "Beside the little cairn, under clear new ice, Halvard Eld lies with his eyes shut and his sword on his chest, like a man under deep water.".
  // Torold, afterwards.
  Topic torold_after_grave with torold "Ask Torold Hame how he does" when toroldMourned(torold) once {
    Says "Torold is sitting on the empty bier, which nobody has taken away, with his hands hanging between his knees. 'I don't know,' he says. 'I've never done this.' He looks at the spears. 'None of us has. Two hundred years I've watched men go down, and got up beside them at the Hour.' He is quiet. 'Is this what it's like for you? Down there? All the time?' You tell him yes. He nods slowly. 'Then I don't know how you stand it,' he says. 'Or how you'd stand it any other way.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/halls.k:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── Morrowhall ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Black timber, roofed with shields, its back to the dawn and its doors to the Field. Morrow's dead fell before noon:
  // dawn raids, morning storms, first light. Brisk, loud, practical; they think Even gives itself airs.
  Observe morrow_yard_scene at morrow_yard when true "The yard of Morrowhall: trodden snow on the brow of the eastern height, the whole Field spread out below to the west, and Halt's smoke in the middle of it. The hall itself is black timber, very long, roofed with shields laid like scales. In the yard people are sparring with blunted spears, out of nine hundred years' habit and boredom, and arguing about it, and a great brindled ox stands by the doors chewing, and watches them with an expression of long experience.".
  Observe morrow_hall_scene at morrow_hall when true "Inside Morrowhall a fire runs the length of the hall in a trench, warm as the Oven, and over the benches, up into the smoke, hang the Tally-boards: planks, thousands of them, every one cut with notches, one notch for every man of Even killed by a man of Morrow, every day for nine hundred years, with the killers' names burned in at the ends. People sit on the benches mending things that do not need mending. It smells of nine hundred years of ox.".
  Observe morrow_hall_night at morrow_hall as sign when hour(clock) >= 19 or hour(clock) < 5 "The hall is eating. Down the length of the fire-trench the great ox Brindle turns on a spit, and the benches roar, and somebody is standing on a table telling a boast that everybody knows the end of and shouts with him.".
  Observe marshal_scene at marshal_room when true "A small square room behind the high seat, with a window looking west down the Field, a chair, a table and a map. The map is of the Field, drawn and redrawn over centuries, with the positions of nine hundred years of battle-lines rubbed out and drawn in again until the parchment is furred. In the middle of it somebody has drawn, quite recently, in a careful small hand, a little town.".

  // The halls let a breather sleep by their fires.
  Initially Assert restful(morrow_hall). Initially Assert restful(even_hall). Initially Assert restful(warren).
  Person brindle "Brindle" at morrow_yard {
    Role "Morrowhall's ox". Species cow. Peaceable. Pronouns he.
    Greets "The great ox swings his head round and looks at you with one wet brown eye, and breathes on you, and the breath does not steam. He goes back to chewing.".
  }
  Topic hall_brindle with mab "Ask Mab Treloar about the ox" when true once {
    Says "'Brindle,' says Mab. 'Siege-ox. Died hauling a ram at the Gate of Thorns, six hundred year back, with a bolt in his neck, so he come in under arms, technically, and Cleeve sent him east.' She grins. 'We eat him every night. He's in the yard again every morning, chewing, and he looks at you. Every morning. You get so you can't meet his eye.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, brindle_known). }
  }
  Discovery brindle_known "Brindle, Morrowhall's ox, died hauling a siege-ram six hundred years ago and came in under arms; the hall eats him every night, and every morning he is in the yard again, chewing.".
  Item brindle_slab "a slab of roast Brindle" is brindle_kind at limbo.
  Relation fedAtTrench(group).
  Action beg_brindle(actor: group, site: place) "Eat at the fire-trench with Morrow" {
    Description "Morrow eats Brindle every night; a breather is welcome to a share, and to a slab for the road.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, morrow_hall) and (hour(clock) >= 19 or hour(clock) < 5) and not fedAtTrench(actor).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert fedAtTrench(actor). Increase quantity(actor, rations) by 2. }
    Result "A big man at the spit carves you a slab the size of a book without being asked twice, and another for your pack, and watches you eat with an odd tender interest. 'Warm, is it?' he says. 'You can taste it warm?' He shakes his head. 'We taste it. But it's never warm.'".
  }
  Rule trench_resets when hour(clock) == 12 and fedAtTrench(?g) { Retract fedAtTrench(?g). }
  Action take_slab(actor: group, site: place) "Ask for a slab of Brindle wrapped in a cloth, to carry" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, morrow_hall) and (hour(clock) >= 19 or hour(clock) < 5) and at(brindle_slab, limbo).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Give brindle_slab to actor. }
    Result "The carver wraps a slab of the ox in a clean rag for you. 'For the road,' he says. 'Or for the bear,' says somebody down the bench, and they all laugh, as if it were an old joke.".
  }

  // ── Hild Varley, Marshal of Morrow ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // She blew the Halt because she was afraid. She has come to love the peace. She does not want to know what killed
  // Halvard, because if it can be known it can be done again.
  Person hild "Hild Varley" at marshal_room {
    Role "the Marshal of Morrowhall". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 8. Trait strong_willed. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    Likeness "prioress".
    Greets "A spare grey woman in a brown jack with a bridge-captain's chain on it looks up from the map. She sees your breath, and her eyes go very still, the way an animal's do. Then she puts the pen down. 'Breather,' she says. 'Cleeve sent word. Sit. Don't go near the fire, you'll scorch, you're not used to it.' She almost smiles. 'Nor are we.'".
    Greets again "Hild Varley looks up from the map, and at your breath, and puts the pen down.".
  }
  Rule hild_walks when hour(clock) >= 13 and hour(clock) < 17 and at(hild, marshal_room) and haltStands() and not hildHardened(hild) { Assert at(hild, banner_lanes). }
  Rule hild_returns when (hour(clock) >= 17 or hour(clock) < 13) and at(hild, banner_lanes) { Assert at(hild, marshal_room). }
  Observe hild_in_lanes at banner_lanes as sign when at(hild, banner_lanes) "Hild Varley walks the banner lanes slowly with her hands behind her back, like a farmer walking a field of something growing, stopping at every tent-mouth to look in.".
  Measure hildTrust(group).
  Relation hildKnows(group). Relation hildAsked(group). Relation hildRefused(group). Relation hildPromised(group). Relation hildResolved(group). Relation hildHardened(group).
  Topic hild_halt with hild "Ask Hild Varley why she blew the Halt" when true once {
    Says "'Because I was nearest,' says Hild. 'He was lying there at the Hour with his eyes open and everyone getting up round him, and somebody had to do something, and the call was in the horn.' She turns her hands over and looks at them, as if the horn might still be in them. 'Every horn on the Field has the Halt in it. It's the first call a horn-boy learns. Nobody ever blew it, because nobody ever wanted to stop.' She looks out over Halt. 'I blew it. And they stopped. Both hosts, the whole Field, mid-blow. Like a breath held.' Her hands go behind her back. 'That's all.'".
    On discuss { Increase hildTrust(hild) by 1. }
  }
  Topic hild_town with hild "Ask Hild Varley about the town on her map" when true once {
    Says "Hild looks at the tents, or out of her window at them, as though they were a thing she had drawn and was not sure of. 'Halt,' she says. 'Forty days old. I walk it every afternoon. I count the tents.' She says it as if confessing to drink. 'Four hundred years I held this hall. I know how many spears Even can put on the ford by the third horn. I don't know what a market is for. I go and stand in theirs and watch them swap spoons.' She is quiet. 'Do you know what it sounds like, the Field, with nobody dying on it? It sounds like a lot of people talking. I'd forgotten.'".
    On discuss { Increase hildTrust(hild) by 1. Assert knows(actor, hild_loves). }
  }
  Discovery hild_loves "Hild Varley walks Halt every afternoon and counts its tents. She has come to love the peace: the sound of a lot of people talking on the Field instead of dying on it.".
  Topic hild_secret with hild "Ask Hild Varley what she was afraid of" when hildTrust(hild) >= 2 and knows(actor, hild_loves) once {
    Says "Hild looks at the window. 'You'll not tell Morrow,' she says. It is not a request. 'I held the bridge at Wrenning at dawn four hundred years ago with sixty men, against two thousand, till they cut us all down. They sing it. Morrow made me Marshal for it.' Her hands are flat on the map. 'I was not brave at Wrenning. I could not run, there was nowhere to run. And I came in out of the snow and found that here you cannot die, and I have been brave every day since, because it costs nothing.' She breathes. 'Then I saw a man stay down. And I blew the Halt because I was afraid, breather. Because if death had come back I did not want to meet it. That is the bravest thing Morrow thinks I ever did.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hild_fear). Increase hildTrust(hild) by 1. }
  }
  Discovery hild_fear "Hild Varley blew the Halt out of fear: she was never brave where death was real, and in Ysgard bravery cost nothing until the day a man stayed down. Morrow thinks it the bravest thing she ever did.".
  // Told the law, her first thought is that it can be done again.
  Topic tell_hild with hild "Tell Hild Varley that only a living hand kills truly here" when knows(actor, living_kills) and not hildKnows(hild) once {
    Says "Hild hears you out with her hands folded on the map, and her face does not move, except that all the colour goes out of it, which in the dead is very little colour. Then she looks at your hands, and at your breath, and you see her think it, all the way to the end, quickly, the way a general thinks. 'Then it was a breather that killed him,' she says. 'And the Testing will prove nothing has come back, because nothing has. Even fights, and at the Hour they all get up, and the next morning Morrow and Even are on the Field again by the third horn.' She looks at the little town drawn on the map. 'Unless one of them does not get up.' She does not say anything else. She does not need to.".
    On discuss { Assert hildKnows(hild). }
  }
  // She asks.
  Topic hild_asks with hild "Ask Hild Varley what she is thinking" when hildKnows(hild) and not truthSpoken(field_country) and beforeTesting() and not hildAsked(hild) once {
    Says "'I am thinking,' says Hild, 'that on the Testing day Even will come down onto the Field by the ford and fight itself, a few hundred of them, in a great press, all morning. And that anyone could walk in among them. And that one man of Even, struck down in that press by a living hand, would not get up at the Hour, and every soul on this Field would see it.' She looks straight at you. 'And then the fear would hold, and the peace with it, for another nine hundred years. One man. One. There are thousands on the Field who would give one for this.' She waits. 'I am asking you, breather. Torold would be best. Torold, who will not let it be.'".
    On discuss { Assert hildAsked(hild). }
  }
  Topic hild_yes with hild "Say you will do it" answering hild_asks when true {
    Grave "A promise to kill, made to the Marshal of Morrow.".
    Says "Hild nods once, as if you had agreed to carry a message. 'By the ford,' she says. 'On the Testing morning. Nobody will know but you and I.' Then she turns to the window, and stays turned until you go.".
    On discuss { Assert hildPromised(hild). Assert promiseMade(hild_promise). }
  }
  Topic hild_no with hild "Say you will not" answering hild_asks when true {
    Says "Hild's mouth thins. 'No,' she says. 'No, of course not.' She looks down at the map, at the little town, and puts her finger on it, gently, as though it might be warm. 'Then the Testing will come, and they will all get up, and the town will go under the third horn like a stubble field.' She takes her finger away. 'Go away now, breather. I have to think how a Marshal does a thing like that without a breather.'".
    On discuss { Assert hildRefused(hild). }
  }
  Promise hild_promise "to strike down one of Even at the Testing, so the fear holds" to hild
    kept when trueDeathAtTesting(field_country) "Somewhere on the eastern height Hild Varley stands at her window with her hands behind her back, and does not turn round."
    broken when afterTesting() and not trueDeathAtTesting(field_country) "Somewhere on the eastern height a woman at a window turns away from it." { Assert hildHardened(hild). }.
  // What resolves her: refused, she is shown a reason to choose the peace without the fear.
  Query haltSigns() means breadRisen(grimbold) or wedded(mab) or songMade(wystan) or runnersSeated(cuddy) or sittersDown(aulus).
  Action resolve_hild(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Hild Varley she can choose the peace without the fear: that Halt is reason enough" {
    Speaker hild.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hild, site) and (hildRefused(hild) or truthSpoken(field_country) and hildKnows(hild)) and haltSigns() and not hildResolved(hild) and not hildTriedToday(hild) and beforeTesting().
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert hildResolved(hild). Retract hildHardened(hild). }
    On failure { Assert hildTriedToday(hild). }
    Result "You tell her what you have seen in her town. Hild listens with her back to you, looking down the Field at it through the window, and does not interrupt. When you have finished she folds the map in half, and unfolds it. 'Four hundred years brave for nothing,' she says. 'And now you want me brave for something.' She turns round. 'If they all get up, and Even comes down by the third horn the morning after, Morrow will not go to meet it. Morrow will be in Halt. I will see to it.' She looks at her own hands. 'I don't know if I can. I'll find out, won't I. That's what it's like for you lot, I suppose. All the time.'".
    Otherwise "Hild hears you out, looking down the Field. 'Words,' she says, not unkindly. 'Breathers have plenty. Come back tomorrow, when I've slept, and say it again.'".
  }
  Relation hildTriedToday(group).
  Observe hild_promised at marshal_room as sign when hildPromised(hild) and not afterTesting() "Hild Varley stands at the window with her back to the room, and does not turn round. She knows who it is by the breath.".
  // Heard, not argued with: told that what she does now, afraid, is what brave is.
  Topic hild_brave with hild "Tell Hild Varley that choosing the peace now, afraid, would be the first brave thing she has done" when knows(actor, hild_fear) and (hildRefused(hild) or truthSpoken(field_country) and hildKnows(hild)) and haltSigns() and not hildResolved(hild) and beforeTesting() once {
    Says "Hild does not answer. She stands at the window with her back to you and her hands behind her, the way she walks the banner lanes. 'Wrenning was nothing,' she says at last. 'There was nowhere to run.' Then: 'And here there is. There is the third horn, and the ford, and four hundred years of knowing exactly what to do.' She turns round. Her face is wet, which in the dead you did not know could happen. 'If they all get up, and Even comes down by the third horn the morning after, Morrow will not go to meet it. Morrow will be in Halt. I will see to it.' She almost laughs. 'Afraid. Yes. Well. I am told that's how it's done.'".
    On discuss { Assert hildResolved(hild). Retract hildHardened(hild). }
  }
  Rule hild_try_resets when hour(clock) == 0 and hildTriedToday(hild) { Retract hildTriedToday(hild). }
  // A bench for the Runners: the first in nine hundred years.
  Topic hild_bench with hild "Ask Hild Varley to give the Runners a bench in Morrowhall" when knows(actor, cuddy_wants) and not runnersSeated(cuddy) and hildTrust(hild) >= 1 once {
    Says "Hild's eyebrows go up. 'The Runners. At a bench.' She considers it, as she would consider a position. 'They clear the Field. They carry for us. They've done it nine hundred years and we spit at them.' She turns the pen over. 'If the Runners strike, there's no Testing; Torold can't fight on nine hundred years of iron. Did you think of that?' She looks at you narrowly. 'And if I seat them, they'll clear it for him out of gratitude, that Cuddy is honest to the bone.' She puts the pen down. 'Very well. A bench. The low one, by the door. Morrow will hate it.' She almost smiles. 'Good.'".
    On discuss { Assert runnersSeated(cuddy). Retract runnersStrike(cuddy). }
  }

  // ── Evenhall ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Grey stone on the western height, with the sunset in its windows. Even's dead fell after noon: last stands, sunset
  // charges, rearguards. Formal, melancholy, proud of its manners; they think Morrow eats with its mouth open.
  Observe even_court_scene at even_court when true "Evenhall's court: flagstones swept clean of snow every morning by somebody's habit, a well with a stone lid, and the hall standing grey and tall against the sky, its long windows facing east down the Field so that it gets the evening, all of it. Everything here is a little straighter than it needs to be. A man is sitting on the well-lid polishing a helm he will not need, very slowly, as if he would like it to last.".
  Observe even_hall_scene at even_hall when true "Evenhall is stone, and its fire is in a great hearth at the far end instead of down the middle, so that the hall is dim and cold at the door end and warm at the hearth, and the benches are arranged by rank. The Tally-boards here are painted, not cut: every kill of nine hundred years in a fine hand, in columns, with the killer's device beside it. Halvard Eld's column runs from the floor to the roof-beam in five years. At the top of it somebody has hung a black ribbon.".
  Observe forge_scene at forge when true "The forge of Evenhall: a long low smithy off the hall, its hearth the warmest place on the Field, and round the walls on racks, mail, hundreds of shirts of it, every one mended, every one oiled, ready for a morning that has not come in forty days.".

  // ── Gorm Hallett, the armourer ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person gorm "Gorm Hallett" at forge {
    Role "the armourer of Evenhall". Ancestry dwarf. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
    Likeness "blacksmith".
    Greets "A dwarf with forearms like hams and a leather apron burnt through in a dozen places looks up from an anvil where he is beating out a ring of mail that does not need it. 'Breather,' he says. 'Come for a look at the war-gear, have you? Look all you like. It's all I've got left to do, polish it.' He hits the ring, hard.".
    Greets again "Gorm Hallett grunts at you over the anvil.".
  }
  Topic gorm_trade with gorm "Ask Gorm Hallett how his trade goes" when beforeTesting() once {
    Says "'Four hundred year,' says Gorm, 'I've mended Even's mail every night. They come in off the Field at the Hour with it hanging off them in rags, and their bodies mend and their mail doesn't, and I sit up all night with the rings and by the third horn they've each a shirt again.' He waves the hammer at the racks. 'Forty nights, nothing. Hundreds of shirts. All mended. Nothing to mend.' He weighs the hammer in his hand, and puts it down. 'Torold's Testing, that's work. I'll have them all to do again by morning after.' He grins, horribly. 'Can't come soon enough.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, gorm_wants_war). }
  }
  Discovery gorm_wants_war "Gorm Hallett has mended Evenhall's mail every night for four hundred years, and has had nothing to mend for forty; he wants the Testing for the work.".
  Topic gorm_plough with gorm "Ask Gorm Hallett whether he could make a plough" when breadRisen(grimbold) and knows(actor, gorm_wants_war) and not ploughMade(gorm) once {
    Says "'A what?' says Gorm. You tell him: Grimbold's loaves, and the grain for them carried up from Larum a sack at a time, and the Field, five miles of it, flat. Gorm stares at you. Then he goes over to the racks and takes down a sword, an old long one, and holds it across his two hands and looks at it the way a man looks at a plank to see what's in it. 'Nine hundred years of swords on that Field,' he says slowly. 'Nobody's ever wanted them back.' He sets it on the anvil. 'Come back tomorrow. And don't tell Torold.'".
    On discuss { Assert ploughAsked(gorm). Set ploughDay(gorm) to day(clock). }
  }
  Relation ploughAsked(group). Relation ploughMade(group). Measure ploughDay(group).
  Rule plough_done when ploughAsked(gorm) and day(clock) > ploughDay(gorm) and not ploughMade(gorm) { Assert ploughMade(gorm). }
  Observe plough_seen at forge as sign when ploughMade(gorm) "Leaning against the anvil is a plough: a share beaten out of four sword-blades welded together, still with a fuller running down the middle of it, on a beam that was a spear-shaft. Gorm keeps looking at it and looking away, like a man with a new baby.".
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/halt.ky:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── Halt ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A town forty days old in the middle of the Field, where Halvard Eld fell: walls of shields stuck rim-down in the
  // snow, tents of the banners of a hundred dead wars, an alehouse in a siege-tower on its side, a bakehouse in a
  // war-mantlet, and in the middle the ring of spears.
  Query haltStands() means not outcomeDaily(field_country).
  Observe cross_first at halt_cross when not visitedBefore(halt_cross) and haltStands() "Between walls of shields stuck rim-down in the snow, hundreds of the dead, in every harness there has ever been, are standing about in the lanes in their shirtsleeves in the cold, talking. The shields are painted with every device there is: suns, wolves, hands, towers, a woman's face, a fish. Behind them, tents of banners on spear-poles, faded, frozen stiff, of wars nobody remembers. And people. Dead people, hundreds, in every harness there has ever been: mail and leather and plate and quilted linen and bronze, standing about in the lanes in the cold in their shirtsleeves, talking. Talking. Somebody is laughing. Somebody is carrying a chair. Nobody has a weapon in their hand, and they keep putting their hands where a hilt would be, and taking them away again.".
  Observe cross_scene at halt_cross when visitedBefore(halt_cross) and haltStands() "Trophy Row, where Halt's two lanes cross: dead men and women from every century squatting by blankets laid out on the snow, swapping what they carried. Nothing can be bought, because nothing they have is worth anything; so everything is swapped: a helm for a song, a ring for a story, a dagger for a go on somebody's chair. The Oven's mouth glows on one side of the crossing; on the other, the Truce lies on its side, a siege-tower with a door cut in its floor.".
  Observe cross_trampled at halt_cross when outcomeDaily(field_country) "Trophy Row is churned snow, and shields lying flat, and banners trodden into the ice. The Oven's mantlet is on its side with the oven cold in it. The Truce has been dragged off somewhere for timber. Nobody is here.".
  Observe cross_daily_sound at halt_cross as sound when outcomeDaily(field_country) and hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 18 "The Daily goes on all round: iron on iron, and shouting, and the long noise of a great many people doing the only thing they know.".
  Observe lanes_scene at banner_lanes when haltStands() "The banner lanes: tents of banners on spear-poles in crooked rows, a hundred dead wars' colours faded to the same tired pink and blue. Through a gap you see a dead woman sitting on a camp-stool in a tent-mouth, sewing two banners together, frowning, as if nobody had ever shown her how. Somebody has made a chair out of shields and is sitting in it with enormous pride.".
  Observe lanes_trampled at banner_lanes when outcomeDaily(field_country) "The banner lanes, trampled flat, a field of rags in the snow.".

  Person halt_folk "the dead of Halt" at halt_cross {
    Role "warriors of every century, in their shirtsleeves in the snow". Ancestry human. Numbers 6. Peaceable.
    Greets "A dozen dead faces turn to you, and to the white of your breath, and the talk along the Row stops. A woman in bronze scale with a hole in her throat that has long since closed says, carefully, 'Breather.' Then a man in a quilted jack spits, and somebody laughs, and the talk starts again, a little louder than before.".
  }
  Topic folk_what with halt_folk "Ask the dead of Halt what they do all day" when haltStands() once {
    Says "They think about it. 'Talk,' says one. 'Swap.' 'Sit.' 'Sleep, I've slept,' says a man in a mailed hood, with wonder, 'I'd forgot sleep.' A woman with a crossbowman's shoulders says, 'I made a spoon.' She shows you. It is a bad spoon, cut out of a shield-board with a dagger. 'It's still there in the morning,' she says. 'Everything we make is. Nine hundred years and I never made anything.' She puts it away inside her jack, next to her skin, as if it might get cold.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, makings_last). }
  }
  Discovery makings_last "On the Field what is done to a body is mended at dusk, but what is made is not: a spoon, a chair, a broken sword. The dead of Halt have started making things, badly, because the things stay.".
  Topic folk_halvard with halt_folk "Ask the dead of Halt about the man in the ring" when haltStands() once {
    Says "Voices drop. 'Halvard Eld,' says the man in the mailed hood. 'Even's champion. Fell in the Daily forty-one days back, up by the ford, and at the Hour he didn't get up. Everyone else did. He just lay there.' 'With his eyes open,' says the crossbowwoman. 'Hild Varley of Morrow was nearest, and she put the horn to her mouth and blew a call nobody'd ever heard, and everybody stopped.' 'The Halt,' says somebody. 'It was in the horns all along. Nobody'd ever blown it.' They look at each other. 'Death's come back,' says the man in the hood, very low. 'That's what they say. It's come back to Ysgard, for all of us.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, halvard_fell). }
  }
  Discovery halvard_fell "Forty-one days ago Halvard Eld, Evenhall's champion, fell in the Daily near the ford and did not get up at the Hour when everyone else did. Hild Varley of Morrow blew the Halt, a horn-call nobody had ever sounded, and the Daily stopped. Halt says death has come back to Ysgard.".

  // Trophy Row's swapper takes Larum tobacco, which is the only thing up here worth anything.
  Person saltash "Old Saltash" at halt_cross {
    Role "who swaps on Trophy Row". Ancestry dwarf. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Likeness "trader".
    Wants tobacco_kind.
    Greets "A dwarf in a coat of rings so old they have gone black sits behind a blanket covered in things: buckles, a horn, a helm with a swan on it, a crossbow with no string. 'Swap?' he says. 'Not coin, coin's for the living. Have you any Larum leaf? A twist of leaf and you can have the horn, and I'll throw in what it's seen.'".
    Greets again "Old Saltash pats his blanket. 'Leaf?' he says hopefully.".
  }
  Event saltash_swaps near saltash when keeps(saltash, ?t) and itemKind(?t, tobacco_kind) "Old Saltash puts the twist to his nose with his eyes shut and breathes it in, the way a man smells a woman's hair. Then he pushes the horn across the blanket at you. 'Blown at the Rout of Anvers, two hundred year back, to call the Morrow foot off the bridge, and they never came, and the man who blew it went on blowing till they killed him. He told me so. He's in Even now, he can't stand the sound of it.'" then { Give horn_found to party. }
  Item horn_found "a dented war-horn" is horn_find at limbo.
  Topic bet_tobacco with bet "Ask Bet Garside for a twist of tobacco" when true once {
    Says "'Leaf? For the Field?' Bet reaches behind the bar without looking. 'The Runners'll trade a helm for a twist. Here. Two for a penny, and if you're giving it to a dead man, tell him it's from Larum.'".
    On discuss { Give tobacco_one to actor. Give tobacco_two to actor. Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1 or to nothing. }
  }
  Item tobacco_one "a twist of Larum leaf" is tobacco_kind at limbo.
  Item tobacco_two "a twist of Larum leaf" is tobacco_kind at limbo.
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/larum.k:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The valley road and the hamlet ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Query skyLoud() means outcomeDaily(field_country) or outcomeHalf(field_country).
  Observe march_scene at march_road when not visitedBefore(march_road) "At the head of a long bare valley, a hamlet of turf-roofed houses, and above it a high pass full of a white cloud that does not move. It is very quiet. The road comes up beside a beck going white over stones and stops being a road at the first wall, as if it had set the hamlet down there and gone back. Above the roofs two shoulders of black rock stand up into the cloud, and between them a snowfield goes up into it and does not come out. Sheep. A chapel tower. Smoke going straight up.".
  Observe march_again at march_road when visitedBefore(march_road) "The valley road below Larum, the beck beside it, the turf roofs ahead, and above them the Pass going up into its standing cloud.".
  Observe street_scene at larum_street when true "Larum's one street, under the Pass: an inn with a hand cupped to an ear on its sign, a bakehouse breathing warmth out of its door, a squat chapel, and at the top a house with a rope and a long pole hung by the door, which is the guide's. Nobody goes up into the cloud but the guide, and Larum would very much like somebody to go and find out why the noise stopped. The houses are stone, turf-roofed, with their backs to the weather. Above everything, the Pass goes up into its cloud.".
  Observe street_quiet at larum_street as ambience when not skyLoud() and not dark() "Everyone in Larum, sooner or later, stops in the street and looks up at the Pass and listens. There is nothing to hear. People stand like that for a while with their heads on one side, and then go on.".
  Observe street_loud at larum_street as ambience when skyLoud() and not dark() "Down off the Pass, faint as bells three valleys off, comes the clangour: iron on iron, thousands of it, like a smithy the size of the sky. Nobody in the street looks up. A woman beating a rug on a wall is beating it in time.".
  Observe street_pans at larum_street as ambience when dark() and not skyLoud() "From an upper window of the Hark comes a slow steady clanging, two pans struck together and struck together again. Bet Garside, who has not slept properly in forty nights, is trying to.".
  Observe street_sleep at larum_street as ambience when dark() and skyLoud() "Larum is asleep. Down off the Pass in the dark comes the far iron noise of the Field, and the hamlet sleeps to it like a child to rain on a roof.".

  Person larum_folk "the folk of Larum" at larum_street {
    Role "shepherds and their wives, standing in the street". Ancestry human. Numbers 3. Peaceable.
    Greets "A shepherd with a crook and a face like a walnut nods to you. 'You'll have come about the quiet,' he says, as if it were a sick cow. 'Everyone does, now.'".
  }
  Topic folk_quiet with larum_folk "Ask the folk of Larum about the quiet" when not skyLoud() once {
    Says "'Nine hundred year,' says the shepherd, 'that noise has come down off the Pass, on still days. My granddad said it was the dead fighting in the snow, and his granddad said it, and it's true, Jory Whitlock's been up and seen them. You get so you don't hear it. Then forty days ago it stopped.' He looks up at the cloud. 'The ewes won't settle. Bet at the Hark bangs pans all night. The parson says it's a judgement. I don't know what on.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, quiet_heard). }
  }
  Discovery quiet_heard "For nine hundred years Larum heard the warrior dead fighting in the snow over the Pass, on still days, like a far smithy; forty days ago the noise stopped, and has not started since. Jory Whitlock, the guide, has been up and seen them.".

  // ── The Hark ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe hark_scene at hark when true "A low smoky taproom with a peat fire, and over the fire, newest and biggest of a hundred penny ballads pinned to the beams, a woodcut of a man with a sword in each fist and a town burning behind him: THE BALLAD OF HALVARD ELD, CHAMPION OF EVENHALL. The others curl along the beams, armoured men with their names in big letters underneath: BRAND OF THE RED HAND. MAB TRELOAR AND THE SIX FROM EVEN. A shelf of old iron by the door, ticketed for sale. Two pans hang by the stair with their bottoms dented.".
  Observe loft_scene at hark_loft when true "A loft under the turf with a bed, a stool, a window the size of a book looking at the Pass. On the beam over the bed somebody has cut a word, carefully, with a small knife, and gone over it more than once: WENDMERE.".

  Person bet "Bet Garside" at hark {
    Role "who keeps the Hark". Ancestry human. Profession innkeeper. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Likeness "laundress".
    Sells rations for 1 coin from 20. Sells halvard_ballad_kind for 1 coin from 6.
    Greets "A big fair woman with grey under her eyes looks up from the fire. 'Come in and shut that, the cold's not paying.' She looks at you properly. 'You're not a collector. You've not got the hands. You've come about the quiet, or you've come to go up.' She yawns enormously and is not sorry. 'Either way, you'll want feeding first.'".
    Greets again "Bet Garside looks up from the fire with her chin on her fist. 'Back down,' she says. 'Sit by the fire. You've got that blue look.'".
  }
  Topic bet_quiet with bet "Ask Bet Garside why she cannot sleep" when not skyLoud() once {
    Says "'Forty years I slept to it,' says Bet. 'Came up here a bride and lay awake the first month for the noise, and then never heard it again, the way you don't hear your own heart. And now it's stopped and I can hear everything. The beck. The sheep. The parson snoring two doors down. Myself.' She picks up a pan from the hearth and looks at it. 'I bang these. It doesn't help. It's not the noise I miss, it's that it was always going on, up there, and now I lie and wonder what they're doing instead.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, quiet_heard). Increase betTrust(bet) by 1. }
  }
  Measure betTrust(group).
  Topic bet_ballads with bet "Ask Bet Garside about the ballads on the beams" when true once {
    Says "'Larum's trade,' says Bet, and is proud of it. 'The pickers bring the news down from the Field, who's champion, who killed who how many times, and old Habakkuk at the press in the back makes it rhyme, and the chapmen carry it all over three countries at a penny a sheet. That's Brand, he was champion when I was a girl. That's Mab Treloar of Morrow, she's a favourite.' She jerks her chin at the fire. 'That's Halvard Eld. Twelve years dead and champion of Evenhall in five, the fastest there's ever been. That one's sold more than all the rest together.' She sells you a copy, if you like, for a penny. 'Lovely fighter,' she says. 'Horrible man, alive. It's in the song. They like that, down in the towns.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, halvard_heard). }
  }
  Discovery halvard_heard "Halvard Eld was champion of Evenhall in Ysgard, the fastest champion there has ever been; Larum's ballad of him has sold more than all the others together.".
  Topic bet_woman with bet "Ask Bet Garside about the word cut in the loft beam" when visitedBefore(hark_loft) or knows(actor, halvard_heard) and betTrust(bet) >= 1 once {
    Says "Bet is quiet a moment. 'Two months back,' she says, 'a woman came up the valley on foot, with a fuller's hands, red and cracked, a widow by her coat. Stayed in the loft a week. Bought a ballad of Halvard Eld, first thing, and read it at that table every night, and never sang it.' She rubs her eyes. 'She asked me how a body gets up the Pass without Jory, and I told her: you go up with the Runners' sledges when they come to trade, and dress like a picker. And one morning she'd gone, and left her rent on the bed.' Bet looks at the fire. 'Wendmere's the town in the ballad. The one he burned. I looked it up after.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, widow_heard). }
  }
  Discovery widow_heard "Two months ago a fuller's widow stayed a week in the Hark's loft, read the ballad of Halvard Eld every night, cut WENDMERE into the beam (the town Halvard burned, in the ballad), asked how to get up the Pass dressed as a picker with the Runners' sledges, and was gone.".
  Topic bet_jory with bet "Ask Bet Garside about the guide" when true once {
    Says "'Jory Whitlock,' says Bet. 'Top of the street, the house with the pole. He's the only one takes the living up through the White, and he'll not set foot on the Field himself, never has. Six coin and he'll see you to the Coming-in.' She lowers her voice. 'He's out of sorts. His lad Ned took the mule down to Wendham market four days back and should've been home Thursday. Jory says he'll have stopped for a girl.' She does not look as if she thinks so.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ned_overdue). }
  }
  Discovery ned_overdue "Jory Whitlock's son Ned took the mule down to Wendham market four days ago and is overdue; Jory says he will have stopped for a girl.".
  Topic bet_bell with bet "Ask Bet Garside about the chapel bell at dusk" when true once {
    Says "'The Mending Bell,' says Bet. 'Rung at dusk, when the noise stops for the day. Always has been. Parson says it was the founder's will and nobody's to ask. Since the quiet, he rings it anyway, at dusk, to nothing, and it's the worst sound in Larum.' She shivers. 'Like ringing for someone who isn't coming.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bell_heard). }
  }
  Discovery bell_heard "Larum chapel rings the Mending Bell at dusk, when the noise from the Pass stops for the day; nobody remembers why. Since the quiet the parson rings it anyway.".

  // The ballad of Halvard Eld.
  Item ballad "the Ballad of Halvard Eld" is halvard_ballad_kind at limbo.
  Action read_ballad(actor: group, site: place) "Read the Ballad of Halvard Eld" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and holding(actor, halvard_ballad_kind) and not knows(actor, ballad_read).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ballad_read). Assert knows(actor, halvard_heard). }
    Result "You read it through. It jogs along cheerfully: Wendmere of the fullers put to the torch, man, wife and child, and Halvard laughing, and the fullers' vats boiling over red. Then Coldharbour, nine men round him, and the snow, and glory. It is a good tune. It is a very bad thing to have a good tune.".
  }
  Discovery ballad_read "In the ballad, Halvard Eld in life was captain of the Free Company of the Hook, who burned Wendmere of the fullers, man, wife and child, and laughed; he died at the siege of Coldharbour twelve years ago and went to glory in Evenhall.".

  // ── Ambler, who buys the Field's iron ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person ambler "Master Ambler" at hark {
    Role "a collector of heaven-iron, from the lowlands". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Likeness "collector".
    Buys crossbow_find for 6 coin. Buys mail_find for 8 coin. Buys horn_find for 10 coin. Buys banner_find for 5 coin. Buys bronze_find for 30 coin.
    Greets "A round pink man in a good coat with a lens on a ribbon round his neck is turning a rusted helm over in his hands by the fire. 'Heaven-iron,' he says, without looking up. 'From the Field. Every dent in this was put there by a man who got up afterwards. Do you know what a duke pays for that?' He looks up. 'Have you been up? Are you going? Bring me anything. I buy anything.'".
    Greets again "Master Ambler puts his lens in his eye and looks hopefully at your pack.".
  }
  Topic ambler_trade with ambler "Ask Master Ambler about the trade in heaven-iron" when true once {
    Says "'The Runners pick it,' says Ambler, 'the ones up there who died running away; they clear the Field every night and bring the broken down to the Coming-in, and trade it to Larum for needles and salt and tobacco, and Larum sells it to me.' He polishes the helm on his sleeve. 'Nine hundred years of it. A crossbow of the last century, six coin. Mail, eight. A war-horn, ten, if it still sounds. But what I want,' and his voice changes, 'is bronze. Under the Field there is clear ice, the pickers say, and you can look down through it to the bottom of history, and at the bottom there is bronze. Nobody has ever brought me a piece. I would give thirty coin.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, clear_heard). }
  }
  Discovery clear_heard "Under the Field in Ysgard there is clear ice, the Clear, through which you can look down at nine centuries of broken arms in layers; at the bottom, the pickers say, there is bronze, and Master Ambler would give thirty coin for a piece.".

  // ── Nance Pellett's bakehouse ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe bakehouse_scene at bakehouse when true "A low hot room that smells of bread, and on a shelf above the glowing oven, wrapped in a shawl like an infant, a brown crock with a plate on top. Loaves on boards. Woodsmoke.".
  Person nance "Nance Pellett" at bakehouse {
    Role "Larum's baker". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Likeness "kitchenmaid".
    Sells rations for 1 coin from 30.
    Greets "A small woman with flour to the elbows and a face red from the oven looks round. 'Shut the door, you'll chill the Mother.' She nods at the crock on the shelf, wrapped in its shawl. 'Two hundred years she's been going, that one. My great-great-grandmother's. Bread?'".
    Greets again "Nance Pellett waves a floury hand without turning from the oven.".
  }
  Topic nance_mother with nance "Ask Nance Pellett about the crock in the shawl" when true once {
    Says "'The Mother,' says Nance. 'Sourdough. Flour and water and the air of this kitchen, kept going since before the road was cobbled: you feed her every day and take a cup out for the bread and she makes it rise. She's alive, you see. That's what rises a loaf, something alive in it, working.' She touches the shawl. 'Let her get cold and she dies, and then your bread's a brick. In a hard winter my gran used to sleep with her in the bed.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mother_alive). }
  }
  Discovery mother_alive "Nance Pellett's sourdough Mother is alive: it is what makes bread rise. Let it get cold and it dies, and the bread is a brick; in a hard winter Nance's grandmother slept with it in the bed.".
  Topic nance_grimbold with nance "Tell Nance Pellett about a baker on the Field whose bread will not rise" when knows(actor, grimbold_flat) and not crockGiven(nance) once {
    Says "Nance stares at you. Then she laughs, a great surprised bark, and puts her hands on her hips and leaves two white prints. 'Bread,' she says. 'Up there. The dead making bread.' She stops laughing. 'Of course it won't rise. Nothing alive lasts five minutes in that cold, Jory says. His yeast's dead before it's in the bowl.' She looks up at the crock, and then she takes it down, and spoons a great grey dollop of the Mother into a little crock of its own, and ties a cloth over it, and gives it you. 'Inside your shirt,' she says, 'against your skin, the whole way up, like a lamb. You're the only warm thing he's got.' She wipes her hands. 'Tell him: feed her every morning. Tell him she's two hundred years old and he's to be civil to her.'".
    On discuss { Give mother_crock to actor. Assert crockGiven(nance). Assert knows(actor, mother_alive). }
  }
  Relation crockGiven(group).
  Item mother_crock "a little crock of Nance's Mother" is mother_kind at limbo.
  // Carried against the skin, it lives through the White; carried in a pack, it dies.
  Relation nursed(group). Relation motherDied(place).
  Action nurse_mother(actor: group, site: place) "Put the crock of the Mother inside your shirt, against your skin" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and holding(actor, mother_kind) and not nursed(actor) and not motherDied(larum_country).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert nursed(actor). }
    Result "You put the little crock inside your shirt, against your ribs, and button your coat over it. It is cold for a moment, and then it is not, and every so often, when you are still, you feel it sigh.".
  }
  Rule mother_dies when holding(party, mother_kind) and not nursed(party) and coldHere(party) and not motherDied(larum_country) and not breadRisen(grimbold)
    says "The little crock in your pack has gone cold as a stone. When you lift the cloth the Mother has sunk into a grey skin, and does not sigh any more." { Assert motherDied(larum_country). }
  Topic nance_again with nance "Ask Nance Pellett for another cup of the Mother" when motherDied(larum_country) and not breadRisen(grimbold) and crockGiven(nance) {
    Says "Nance looks at the dead crock you bring her, and sighs, and fills it again. 'Against your skin,' she says. 'I did say.'".
    On discuss { Retract motherDied(larum_country). }
  }

  // ── Larum chapel and the Mending Bell ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe chapel_scene at larum_chapel when true "A cold whitewashed chapel with a bell-rope hanging down through a hole in the ceiling, and on the door-frame, cut deep and old: I. S. MADE THIS BELL. The stone floor is worn into hollows. Under it, newer, on a board in a parson's hand: THE BELL TO BE RUNG AT DUSK WHEN THE NOISE FROM THE PASS STOPS FOR THE DAY. FOUNDER'S WILL. NO QUESTIONS.".
  Observe chapel_known at larum_chapel as feature when knows(party, ithel_told) "I. S.: Ithel the Smith. He made the bell for the man he killed on the Field, and for his son, and asked Larum to ring it at the Hour, when the dead get up. Larum did, for three hundred years, without knowing for whom.".
  Relation rangToday(place).
  Action ring_bell(actor: group, site: place) "Ring the Mending Bell" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, larum_chapel) and hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 20 and not rangToday(larum_chapel).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert rangToday(larum_chapel). }
    Result "You haul on the rope and the bell speaks over Larum, three times, a big plain iron note that goes up the Pass and into the cloud. In the street people stop with their heads on one side, the way they do. Nothing answers.".
  }
  Rule bell_unrung when hour(clock) == 0 and rangToday(larum_chapel) { Retract rangToday(larum_chapel). }
  // At the Hour, up at the Coming-in, Larum's bell can be heard, very faint.
  Rule bell_heard_up at snow_gate when theHour() and at(party, snow_gate) and not heardBellUp(party)
    says "From somewhere behind you, down in the White, very faint and very far, a bell strikes three times. Cleeve, in his booth, takes his hat off, and puts it on again." { Assert heardBellUp(party). }
  Relation heardBellUp(group).
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/law.kyr:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The law of the living hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What the company can learn by three roads: by what it does (Mab's lip), by what it reads (the wound, and Ithel), or
  // from Edith. And what Halt knows once someone says it at the ring of spears, with proof.
  Relation truthSpoken(place). Relation deathCarrier(group).
  // A short broad blade from behind, by someone small; a fuller's widow who asked the way up dressed as a picker.
  Discovery widow_suspected "The wound that killed Halvard was made by a short broad blade like a fuller's knife, from behind; the fuller's widow from Wendmere who stayed at the Hark asked how to get up the Pass dressed as a picker, with the Runners' sledges. The Runners would know where she went.".
  Rule widow_inferred when knows(party, widow_heard) and (knows(party, wound_read) or knows(party, halvard_wound)) and not knows(party, widow_suspected) and not knows(party, edith_named)
    says "A short blade from behind, close, by someone small who waited. A fuller's widow with red hands who read the ballad every night and asked the way up dressed as a picker. The Runners bring the sledges down to the Coming-in." teaches widow_suspected { }
  Discovery runner_girl "On the day Halvard fell, the Runners say, a new picker came out with the sledges whom nobody knew, a woman, and she did not come back to the Scrapes with the others at the Hour; or so they say to strangers.".
  Topic runners_newcomer with runners "Ask the Runners whether anyone new came out with the sledges the day Halvard fell" when (knows(actor, widow_suspected) or knows(actor, halvard_fell)) and not knows(actor, runner_girl) once {
    Says "The Runners look at each other. 'New?' says the scarred man. 'Nobody new.' A woman beside him says, too quickly, 'Nobody,' and the scarred man looks at her, and she looks at the lamp. 'There was a picker that day,' says a boy at the back, 'that didn't come back at the Hour with—' and somebody kicks him. 'Nobody new,' says the scarred man again, and gets up and goes out, and the warren is very quiet.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, runner_girl). }
  }
  // Told privately, with proof, Torold knows his friend will not get up.
  Query proofHeld() means mabScarred(mab) and knows(party, living_kills) or knows(party, edith_did_it) or knows(party, ithel_told).
  Topic tell_torold with torold "Tell Torold Hame that a living hand killed Halvard, and that he will not get up" when knows(actor, living_kills) and proofHeld() and not toroldKnows(torold) and state(halvard, lying) once {
    Grave "There is no Testing that can give Halvard back after this, and he will know it.".
    Says "You tell him, all of it, and what you know it by. Torold listens with his hands on the pommel of the sword stood in the snow, and his eyes on the frost on Halvard's face, and he does not interrupt, and he does not look at you. When you have finished he stands there, and the frost on Halvard's face does not change. The watch at the corners of the bier have heard; they are looking at each other. 'Not the Field,' says Torold at last. 'Not us stopping.' His voice is quite level. 'A breather's hand. And no Daily in the world will bring him up.' He takes his hands off the sword. It stays standing in the snow. He looks at his empty hands. 'Then I've been standing here forty days for nothing,' he says. 'Waiting for the blue.'".
    On discuss { Assert toroldKnows(torold). }
  }
  // Said to all Halt at the ring by the company itself: the dead are slow to believe a breather.
  Action declare_truth(actor: group, site: place) "Tell all Halt, at the ring of spears, what killed Halvard Eld" {
    Description "That nothing has come back to the Field but what came up the Pass. A breather saying it is not to be believed for the asking.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_ring) and knows(actor, living_kills) and proofHeld() and not truthSpoken(field_country) and beforeTesting() and not declaredToday(actor).
    Grave "Once Halt knows that only the living kill here, it cannot be made not to know.".
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert truthSpoken(field_country). Assert toroldKnows(torold). Assert hildKnows(hild). }
    On failure { Assert declaredToday(actor). }
    Result "You get up on a barrel by the ring of spears and tell them. A crowd comes, slowly, then all at once, as crowds do when a breather is shouting about Halvard. You tell them about the wound that has not begun to close, and the hand that made it, and Ithel the Smith, and you tell them nothing has come back to the Field. At first they jeer. Then they stop. A man in bronze scale at the front looks at his own forearm, at the place where a sword took his hand off yesterday nine hundred years ago, smooth and whole. 'Nothing,' he says. 'Nothing's come back.' The crowd goes quiet, and stays quiet, and one by one they turn and look north, and east, and west, at the Field, as though seeing it for the first time.".
    Otherwise "You get up on a barrel by the ring of spears and tell them, and a crowd comes, and listens, and jeers, and a man throws a frozen glove at you. 'A breather,' somebody says, 'telling us what's alive and what's dead.' They go back to their swapping. Tomorrow, perhaps, with more to show them.".
  }
  Relation declaredToday(group).
  Rule declared_resets when hour(clock) == 0 and declaredToday(?g) { Retract declaredToday(?g). }
  Observe truth_known at halt_cross as ambience when truthSpoken(field_country) and haltStands() and beforeTesting() "Everyone in Halt has heard. You can see it in the way they stand: not frightened any more, and not easy either; like people who have been told the river can be crossed, and are looking at it.".
  // Hild, told it by all Halt, thinks what she would have thought.
  Rule truth_reaches_hild when truthSpoken(field_country) and not hildKnows(hild) { Assert hildKnows(hild). }
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/lore.ky:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  Description "Links outward from Larum: a piece of sky reported fallen far away, and a surveyor who wants the Teeth.".

  // ── A world event, read: the sky is not as it was ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe lore_street_sky at larum_street when befell(cloudgate_fell) "Bet Garside has propped the Hark's door open, which she does not do in winter, and the whole street is standing in it looking up. 'A drover from the coast,' says Ambler, 'says a piece of the sky came down in a bay. A whole piece. With a house on it.' The street looks up. The sky above the Pass is quite as it was, grey and low and quiet. 'It is a comfort,' says Bet, 'to be told somebody else's has fallen.'".

  // ── The surveyor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_pym_larum "Orlando Pym of the Collegium of Measures was at Larum before the snow, and chained the street, and left a mark on the Hark's doorpost; he will come back for the Teeth when the White lifts.".
  Topic lore_bet_pym with bet "Ask Bet Garside about the mark on the doorpost" when true once {
    Says "'That,' says Bet, 'is a surveyor.' She wipes the chalk-mark on the Hark's doorpost with the back of a knuckle and thinks better of it. 'Pym, of the Measures. Came in off the south road with a chain and a boy and a wet cough, and was very sorry, and chained my street. Forty-one chains. He said, in the Lull they are nine short of the table and Larum is exact, and was so pleased he forgot his hat. I have it.' She puts a hat on the bar. 'He said he'd come back for the Teeth when the White lifts. If he does, I'll tell him what the Teeth are for. He'll write it down.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_pym_larum). }
  }
}

Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── Mab Treloar and Ansel Haverlock ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A pikewoman of Morrow, two hundred years dead, and a knight of Even, six hundred: old partners, the halls say, who
  // always found each other on the Field. They have killed each other something like three thousand times. In the Truce
  // they cannot be in the same lane. Each believes the other wants the war back, because it was the only way they had of
  // meeting.
  Person mab "Mab Treloar" at morrow_yard {
    Role "pikewoman of Morrowhall". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 6. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner jovial.
    Likeness "heroine".
    Greets "A broad freckled woman with a pike-butt in her fists and her sleeves rolled up over arms like a smith's looks round from the sparring and sees your breath, and her face splits into a grin. 'A breather!' she says. 'Well, there's something new, and Brindle be praised, because nothing else is. Mab Treloar, Morrow foot, two hundred and eleven years on the Field and bored to my back teeth.' She spins the pike. 'Can you fight? You've the look of somebody who's been taught.'".
    Greets again "Mab Treloar looks round at you, and the pike stops spinning.".
    Wants challenge_kind. Wants plain_kind.
  }
  Person ansel "Ansel Haverlock" at even_hall {
    Role "a knight of Evenhall". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 6. Trait knight. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Likeness "squire".
    Greets "A slender dark man in a surcoat so old its device has worn away rises from a bench as you come near, and bows, exactly as far as courtesy requires toward a stranger of unknown degree. 'Ansel Haverlock,' he says, 'of the household of Evenhall. You are the living guest. You are welcome to this hall.' He does not look at your breath. He is too well brought up.".
    Greets again "Ansel Haverlock rises and bows, a little less far than the first time, which in him is warmth.".
  }
  // Their days: Mab spars in Morrow's yard of a morning and haunts Trophy Row of an afternoon; Ansel keeps Even's hall of
  // a morning and walks down to the ford of the Lathe in the afternoon, where Morrow and Even always met.
  Relation paired(group). Relation wedded(group).
  Rule mab_afternoon when hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 18 and at(mab, morrow_yard) and haltStands() and not wedded(mab) and not paired(mab) { Assert at(mab, halt_cross). }
  Rule mab_to_ford when hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 17 and at(mab, morrow_yard) and paired(mab) and not wedded(mab) and not testingUnder() { Assert at(mab, lathe_ford). }
  Rule mab_evening when hour(clock) >= 18 and (at(mab, halt_cross) or at(mab, lathe_ford)) and not wedded(mab) { Assert at(mab, morrow_hall). }
  Rule mab_morning when hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 12 and at(mab, morrow_hall) and not wedded(mab) { Assert at(mab, morrow_yard). }
  Rule ansel_afternoon when hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 17 and at(ansel, even_hall) and haltStands() and not wedded(mab) and not testingUnder() { Assert at(ansel, lathe_ford). }
  Rule ansel_evening when hour(clock) >= 17 and at(ansel, lathe_ford) and not wedded(mab) { Assert at(ansel, even_hall). }
  // Married, they keep a tent in the banner lanes.
  Rule wedded_home when wedded(mab) and not at(mab, banner_lanes) and not testingUnder() { Assert at(mab, banner_lanes). Assert at(ansel, banner_lanes). }
  Observe ansel_at_ford at lathe_ford as sign when at(ansel, lathe_ford) and not paired(mab) "On the far bank of the frozen Lathe, where the ford is, a slender man in an old surcoat stands looking across the ice at the empty eastern bank, with his hands clasped behind him, very still, like a heron.".

  Topic mab_daily with mab "Ask Mab Treloar what she misses about the Daily" when beforeTesting() once {
    Says "Mab leans on the pike. 'Miss it? It was a job,' she says. 'You get up, you eat Brindle, you go down by the third horn, you kill some Even, they kill you, you get up. Two hundred year.' She looks down the Field, toward the ford. 'You get so you know them. The ones you always meet. Like the faces at market.' She spins the pike butt in the snow, a little circle. 'I don't miss it,' she says. 'I miss—' and stops. 'Nothing. Spar with me, breather, I'm going mad.'".
    On discuss { Increase mabTrust(mab) by 1. Assert knows(actor, mab_misses). }
  }
  Measure mabTrust(group).
  Discovery mab_misses "Mab Treloar does not miss the Daily, she says; she misses the ones you always meet on the Field, like faces at market. Something particular she does not say.".
  Topic folk_partners with halt_folk "Ask the dead of Halt who Mab Treloar always met on the Field" when knows(actor, mab_misses) once {
    Says "The crossbowwoman snorts. 'Ansel Haverlock,' she says, and three people round her laugh. 'Old partners, them two. Two hundred year, every day, they'd find each other in the press, if they had to go through fifty of us to do it. Mab and the knight. Larum did a ballad.' 'Three thousand times,' says somebody. 'More,' says somebody else. 'And now they won't stand in the same lane,' says the crossbowwoman. 'Mab goes left at the Row if she sees his colours. He walks down to the ford every afternoon and stands looking at our bank.' She shrugs. 'Pair of fools.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, old_partners). }
  }
  Discovery old_partners "Mab Treloar of Morrow and Ansel Haverlock of Even are old partners: for two hundred years they found each other in the press every day and killed each other, some three thousand times. Now they will not stand in the same lane; he walks down to the ford every afternoon and looks at Morrow's bank.".
  Topic mab_ansel with mab "Ask Mab Treloar about Ansel Haverlock" when knows(actor, old_partners) and mabTrust(mab) >= 1 once {
    Says "Mab's face shuts like a door. 'That Even prig,' she says. Then she looks at the pike in her hands for a while. 'Three thousand one hundred and six,' she says. 'I counted. His and mine together. He's got the better of it by forty, the prig, he's quick.' She is not looking at you. 'He used to bow. Before. Every morning, across the ford, before the horn: a little bow, like that, like we was at a dance. And I'd spit. And then we'd go at it.' She swallows. 'He'll want the war back. Course he will. It's all he had of me. It's all I had of him.'".
    On discuss { Increase mabTrust(mab) by 1. Assert knows(actor, mab_loves). }
  }
  Discovery mab_loves "Mab Treloar counted: three thousand one hundred and six times, his and hers together. Ansel used to bow to her across the ford every morning before the horn. She thinks he wants the war back, because it was all he had of her.".
  Topic ansel_mab with ansel "Ask Ansel Haverlock about Mab Treloar" when knows(actor, old_partners) once {
    Says "Ansel goes still. 'Mistress Treloar,' he says, 'is the finest pike in the Morrow foot. I have had the honour of her acquaintance on the Field for two hundred and eleven years.' He looks at his hands. 'I have not had the honour of a word with her in forty days. She avoids my colours.' He straightens. 'Which is her right. In the Truce we are nothing to one another; there is no form for it.' Then, lower, as if it were dragged out of him: 'I have been composing a challenge.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ansel_challenge_heard). }
  }
  Discovery ansel_challenge_heard "Ansel Haverlock has been composing a challenge to Mab Treloar.".
  Topic ansel_challenge with ansel "Ask Ansel Haverlock what kind of challenge" when knows(actor, ansel_challenge_heard) and not challengeGiven(ansel) once {
    Says "'A formal challenge,' says Ansel, colouring, 'to meet at the ford of the Lathe, at noon, without arms, in the presence of witnesses. In my century, when a knight wished to—' He stops. 'It is the only form I know. I was eighteen when I died. I had been taught the forms for everything except this.' He takes a folded paper from his surcoat, much handled. 'Would you carry it to her? I cannot go into Morrow's lanes. It would be taken as an act of war.' He holds it out, and his hand is not quite steady. 'Without arms,' he says. 'You will tell her, without arms.'".
    On discuss { Give challenge to actor. Assert challengeGiven(ansel). Assert knows(actor, ansel_means). }
  }
  Relation challengeGiven(group).
  Discovery ansel_means "Ansel Haverlock's challenge to Mab Treloar, to meet at the ford at noon without arms before witnesses, is the only form he knows for what he means: in his century it was how a knight asked.".
  Item challenge "Ansel Haverlock's challenge" is challenge_kind at limbo.
  // Ansel can be talked into saying it plainly, first.
  Action plain_ansel(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Ansel Haverlock to throw the challenge on the fire and write to her plainly" {
    Speaker ansel.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ansel, site) and challengeGiven(ansel) and not plainWritten(ansel) and not mabInsulted(mab) and holding(actor, challenge_kind) and not anselBalked(ansel).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert plainWritten(ansel). Spend challenge from actor. Give plain_letter to actor. }
    On failure { Assert anselBalked(ansel). }
    Result "Ansel looks at you as if you had suggested he go into battle naked. Then he looks at the challenge in your hand, and turns it over to see whether the back is any better, and takes it, and holds it over Evenhall's hearth until the corner catches, and lets it go. He sits down at the end of a bench with a scrap of lining and a stub of charcoal, and writes, with his tongue between his teeth like a schoolboy, and crosses out, and writes. When he gives it you he will not meet your eye.".
    Otherwise "'Plainly,' says Ansel, as though you had said barefoot. 'There is no plainly. There is the form, or there is nothing.' He turns away. 'Carry the challenge, if you will. Or don't.'".
  }
  Relation plainWritten(group). Relation anselBalked(group). Relation mabInsulted(group). Relation mabGoes(group). Measure mabGoesDay(group).
  Item plain_letter "Ansel Haverlock's letter" is plain_kind at limbo.
  Event mab_takes_challenge near mab when keeps(mab, challenge) and not mabInsulted(mab) and not mabGoes(mab) "Mab sees the folded lining in your hand, and the old upright writing on it, and goes white under her freckles. She takes it and reads it, and reads it again. 'A challenge,' she says. 'Without arms, before witnesses.' She crumples it in her fist. 'So that's it. He wants it back. Can't bear it, can he, forty days without his Morrow pike to stick. Wants to meet at the ford and start it all again.' Her voice cracks. 'Tell him no. Tell him if he wants Mab Treloar he can wait for the third horn like everybody else.' She turns her back." then { Assert mabInsulted(mab). }
  Event mab_takes_letter near mab when keeps(mab, plain_letter) and not mabGoes(mab) "Mab takes the scrap of lining as if it might go off in her hand. She reads it. Her lips move. She reads it again, and her face does something you have never seen a dead face do, which is go red. 'With nothing in his hands,' she says. 'The prig. The great courtly fool.' She folds it very small and puts it inside her jack against her skin, where the crossbowwoman keeps her spoon. 'Noon,' she says. 'Tomorrow.' And then, ferociously: 'Don't you dare come and watch.'" then { Assert mabGoes(mab). Set mabGoesDay(mab) to day(clock). }
  Topic mab_explain with mab "Tell Mab Treloar what Ansel's challenge means in his century" when mabInsulted(mab) and knows(actor, ansel_means) and not mabGoes(mab) once {
    Says "Mab stares at you. 'A what?' You tell her again: the form; eighteen when he died; the only form he knows; how a knight asked. Mab sits down on the snow, hard, with the pike across her knees, and laughs until she has to put her face in her hands, and you cannot tell after a while whether she is still laughing. 'Six hundred year,' she says into her hands. 'Six hundred year dead and he's still eighteen.' She wipes her face with her sleeve. 'Noon, it said. The ford.' She gets up. 'Tomorrow, then. And don't you dare come and watch.'".
    On discuss { Assert mabGoes(mab). Set mabGoesDay(mab) to day(clock). }
  }
  // The meeting at the ford, at noon of the next day.
  Rule lovers_meet when mabGoes(mab) and day(clock) > mabGoesDay(mab) and hour(clock) >= 12 and not paired(mab) and beforeTesting() { Assert at(mab, lathe_ford). Assert at(ansel, lathe_ford). Assert paired(mab). }
  Rule lovers_seen at lathe_ford when paired(mab) and at(party, lathe_ford) and not spoke(lovers_told)
    says "On the ice of the ford, halfway between the banks where for two hundred years the hosts met by the third horn, Mab Treloar and Ansel Haverlock are standing a yard apart with nothing in their hands. Neither of them knows what to do with the hands. Ansel bows, the little bow. Mab does not spit. She says something, and he says something, and then she reaches out, very slowly, the way you would reach for a weapon you were afraid of, and takes hold of his sleeve. On both banks, at a distance, a little crowd of the dead has come to watch, Morrow on the east and Even on the west, and nobody is saying anything at all." { Assert spoke(lovers_told). }
  Entity lovers_told: fact "the meeting at the ford".
  Topic mab_paired with mab "Ask Mab Treloar how it went at the ford" when paired(mab) and not wedded(mab) once {
    Says "Mab looks at the ground. 'We talked,' she says. 'Two hundred year, and we talked. He's got a dog's name for his horse. He's afraid of moths. He was eighteen.' She grins suddenly. 'He says he always let me have the better of the first blow. Lying prig.' Then the grin goes. 'He wants to marry. Properly. Nobody's ever married up here, there's no form, and the halls'll have us for deserters, and who'd stand up for us?' She kicks the snow. 'Morrow and Even don't stand up together. Not for anything.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lovers_wish). }
  }
  Discovery lovers_wish "Mab Treloar and Ansel Haverlock want to marry, the first marriage there has ever been on the Field; but there is no form for it, the halls will call it desertion, and nobody from Morrow and Even will stand up together for anything.".
  // A witness who stands for both halls: Grimbold, who bakes for everyone.
  Topic grimbold_witness with grimbold "Ask Grimbold Ure whether he would stand witness for Mab Treloar and Ansel Haverlock" when knows(actor, lovers_wish) and not weddingSet(mab) once {
    Says "Grimbold stops kneading. He looks at you, and down at his great hands in the dough, and his face goes slowly crimson from the beard up. 'Me,' he says. 'A Morrow man. For an Even knight.' He thinks about it with his whole body, like a hill thinking. 'I bake for Even. I baked for Even yesterday. They come to the Oven same as anyone.' He wipes his hands on his apron. 'Tomorrow at the Hour, in the banner lanes. I'll bring bread, if there's bread.' His eyes are wet. 'Nobody's ever asked me to stand for anything but the third horn.'".
    On discuss { Assert weddingSet(mab). Set weddingDay(mab) to day(clock). }
  }
  Relation weddingSet(group). Measure weddingDay(group).
  Rule wedding_happens when weddingSet(mab) and day(clock) > weddingDay(mab) and hour(clock) >= 18 and not wedded(mab) and haltStands() { Assert wedded(mab). Assert at(mab, banner_lanes). Assert at(ansel, banner_lanes). Assert at(grimbold, banner_lanes). }
  Rule wedding_seen at banner_lanes when wedded(mab) and at(party, banner_lanes) and theHour() and not spoke(wedding_told)
    says "At the Hour, when the light goes blue over the Field, they are married in the banner lanes, in front of half of Halt and a fair number of both halls who have come to look disapproving and stayed. Nobody knows how it is done, so they make it up. Grimbold stands between them with flour on his beard and says, 'Well,' and then, 'well,' and then nothing for so long that someone laughs, and then he takes Mab's hand and Ansel's hand and puts one in the other and holds them there in both of his, like a loaf. That is the wedding. Mab is crying. Ansel bows to her, the little bow, and she does not spit." { Assert spoke(wedding_told). }
  Entity wedding_told: fact "the wedding".
  Rule wedding_bread at banner_lanes when wedded(mab) and breadRisen(grimbold) and at(party, banner_lanes) and theHour() and not spoke(wedding_bread_told)
    says "Then Grimbold's loaves go round, risen and brown, the first wedding bread in Ysgard, and four hundred of the dead break it and smell it and do not know what to do with their faces." { Assert spoke(wedding_bread_told). }
  Entity wedding_bread_told: fact "the wedding bread".
  Rule wedding_song at banner_lanes when wedded(mab) and songMade(wystan) and at(party, banner_lanes) and theHour() and not spoke(wedding_song_told)
    says "And Wystan Hollins, drunk and furious, stands on a barrel and sings the new song, the one that is not about killing anybody, and gets halfway through the second verse before his voice goes, and the whole lane finishes it for him." { Assert spoke(wedding_song_told). }
  Entity wedding_song_told: fact "the wedding song".
  Topic hild_bless with hild "Ask Hild Varley to let Mab Treloar keep her bench, married to Even" when knows(actor, lovers_wish) and not hildBlessed(hild) and hildTrust(hild) >= 1 once {
    Says "Hild looks at you over the map. 'Mab Treloar,' she says, 'and the Haverlock boy.' She is quiet. 'There is no rule against it, because nobody ever thought of it.' She picks up the pen. 'She keeps her bench. If Torold takes the boy's from him, he can sit at hers.' She writes something on the edge of the map, small. 'Tell her I said so. Tell her not to make a fuss about it.'".
    On discuss { Assert hildBlessed(hild). Increase hildTrust(hild) by 1. }
  }
  Relation hildBlessed(group).

  // ── Sparring in Morrow's yard ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Morrow spars all day, out of habit. It asks the breather in. A cut a living hand gives here does not close at the
  // Hour; Mab carries the first scar in Ysgard, and the company learns what it is by what it has done.
  Relation mabCut(group). Relation mabScarred(group).
  Action spar_mab(actor: group, site: place) "Spar with Mab Treloar, with blunted pikes" {
    Description "Morrow spars all day. Blunted, it hurts and that is all; whatever it does mends at the Hour.".
    Speaker mab.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(mab, site) and at(actor, morrow_yard) and not mabCut(mab) and beforeTesting().
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, tumbling, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert mabCut(mab). Increase mabTrust(mab) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert mabCut(mab). Assert strikes(pike_butt, actor). Increase mabTrust(mab) by 1. }
    Result "She is very good, and very fast, and two hundred years bored, and for a while you only stay out of her way. Then she overreaches, laughing, and you get inside the pike and bring your own butt round, and it catches her across the mouth, hard, and she sits down in the snow with her lip split open. The yard cheers. Mab spits blood and grins up at you with red teeth. 'That's one,' she says. 'It'll mend at the Hour. Again?'".
    Otherwise "She puts you on your back in the snow three times in as many breaths, and the yard laughs, and the fourth time, flailing, the end of your staff catches her across the mouth, more by luck than anything, and splits her lip. She sits back on her heels and spits blood and laughs. 'Got one in,' she says. 'Lucky. It'll mend at the Hour.'".
  }
  Hazard pike_butt "a blunted pike-butt in the ribs" means "Deal (1d4) bludgeoning damage to ally.".
  Rule mab_scar near mab when mabCut(mab) and theHour() and not mabScarred(mab)
    says "The Hour comes over the Field: the light goes blue all at once, as if a glass had been put over the sun, and for a moment everyone near you stops what they are doing and closes their eyes, out of nine hundred years' habit. Mab Treloar opens hers and puts her fingers to her mouth, and takes them away, and looks at them. There is blood on them. Her lip is still split, exactly as you split it. She touches it again. All round her the dead are looking at her mouth, and then, one by one, at you." teaches living_kills { Assert mabScarred(mab). }
  // Not there at the Hour, the company finds it out from her.
  Rule mab_scar_unseen when mabCut(mab) and afterHour() and not mabScarred(mab) and not theHour() { Assert mabScarred(mab). }
  Topic mab_lip with mab "Ask Mab Treloar about her lip" when mabScarred(mab) and not knows(actor, living_kills) once {
    Says "Mab touches the split in her lip. It has scabbed, the way a living wound scabs. 'It didn't mend,' she says. 'At the Hour. Everything mends at the Hour. Two hundred years, I've had my head off, and it mended.' She looks at you, not angry, only very puzzled and a little frightened. 'You did that. With a blunt stick.' She swallows. 'What are you, breather?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, living_kills). }
  }
  Observe mab_lip_seen near mab as sign when mabScarred(mab) "Mab Treloar's lip is scabbed where you split it, and she keeps touching it with her tongue, the way you touch a tooth that has gone.".
  // She carries it to her Marshal that night.
  Rule mab_tells_hild when mabScarred(mab) and hour(clock) >= 20 and not hildKnows(hild) { Assert hildKnows(hild). }
  Topic mab_show with mab "Ask Mab Treloar to show her lip at the ring of spears, to all Halt" when mabScarred(mab) and knows(actor, living_kills) and not truthSpoken(field_country) and beforeTesting() once {
    Grave "Once Halt knows that a living hand ends what it strikes here, it cannot be made not to know.".
    Says "Mab is quiet a long while. 'If I show them,' she says, 'they'll know nothing's come back. Not for us. Only for what you lot do.' She touches her lip. 'And then there's nothing stopping the Daily but whether we want it.' She looks down the Field to Halt, and the ford beyond it. 'All right,' she says. 'Let them want it or not, then, knowing. I'm sick of being afraid of a thing that isn't there.' She goes down to the ring of spears in the middle of Halt and stands on a barrel and shows them all her mouth, and tells them how she got it, and who from, and by the time she is done there is nobody in Halt who does not know.".
    On discuss { Assert truthSpoken(field_country). Assert toroldKnows(torold). Assert hildKnows(hild). }
  }
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/old-ice:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The Old Ice ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // North, where the Field rises into a glacier, a stair cut by nobody knows whom goes up to a cave in the blue ice, and
  // in the cave sit the Sitters: ten of the oldest dead in Ysgard, from before the halls, who refused the Daily seven
  // hundred years ago and have played a game of stones ever since, forgotten. Their bear wanders the stair.
  Observe north_scene at field_north when true "The northern Field rises in long white swells toward a wall of ice that fills the north from side to side: the Old Ice, blue-green, cracked into towers, very slow. There is less iron here. The battle-lines never came this far. The snow is unmarked except for a line of very big footprints going up toward the ice, each one a yard across.".
  Observe ice_foot_scene at ice_foot when true "At the foot of the Old Ice the cold comes off the glacier like a draught from a door. Steps go up it, cut into the blue, old, worn hollow in the middle by feet. Beside the bottom step somebody has built a little cairn of stones, which is the only cairn on the Field, and on the top stone is cut a word in letters you cannot read.".
  Observe ice_stair_scene at ice_stair when true "Halfway up the ice the steps come out on a shelf, wide as a room, with the whole Field below you, the two halls tiny at its ends, Halt's smoke in the middle. Behind you the blue ice goes up into towers. The shelf is trodden all over by the same huge prints, and smells, faintly, of animal.".
  Observe cave_known_tell at ice_stair as feature when knows(party, sitters_known) "At the back of the shelf, where the ice is darkest, there is a low mouth, and from it, very faint, comes the click of stones on a board.".
  Discovery sitters_known "At the back of the shelf on the Old Ice's stair there is a mouth into the ice, and in it, the Runners say, old men who never come down.".
  Discovery sitters_rumour "The Runners say there are old ones under the Old Ice who never come down, who would know things.".
  Topic cuddy_sitters with cuddy "Ask Cuddy Wardle about the old ones under the ice" when (knows(actor, sitters_rumour) or cuddyTrust(cuddy) >= 2) and not knows(actor, sitters_known) once {
    Says "'The Sitters,' says Cuddy. 'Runners know. Nobody else. Up the steps on the Old Ice, there's a cave, and in it there's ten old men from before there were halls, playing stones. They stopped fighting before anyone can remember. Everyone forgot them.' She grins. 'We take them up honey and they tell us the old stories wrong on purpose to see if we notice. Mind the bear.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sitters_known). Assert knows(actor, sitters_rumour). }
  }
  Relation searchedStair(group).
  Action search_stair(actor: group, site: place) "Search the back of the ice shelf" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, ice_stair) and not knows(actor, sitters_known) and not searchedStair(actor).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, sitters_known). }
    On failure { Assert searchedStair(actor). }
    Result "At the back of the shelf, where the ice goes darkest, you find a low mouth in the blue, and stop, because from somewhere inside it comes a small dry sound, over and over: click. Click. Stones on a board.".
    Otherwise "You go along the back of the shelf, and find nothing but ice, and the bear's prints going everywhere.".
  }

  // A search that found nothing may be made again by a company that has gone away and come back: the latch had held
  // for good, so whether the Sitters were found at all came down to one roll (the Imbar authors' friction, M19-205).
  Rule stair_search_again when searchedStair(party) and not at(party, ice_stair) { Retract searchedStair(party). }

  // ── The bear ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A war-bear of a dwarven host, dead nine hundred years, who mends at the Hour like anyone. It is the Sitters', and
  // likes honey and roast ox, and does not like strangers on its stair.
  Person bear "a great white bear" at ice_stair {
    Role "who keeps the Sitters' stair". Species bear. Level 7. Temperament territorial.
    Lair ice_stair.
    Warns "On the shelf a white shape that you had taken for a heap of snow gets up, and goes on getting up, until it is twice the height of a man, a bear, white as the ice, with the rags of an iron harness still on its shoulders and its breath not steaming. It looks at you with small black eyes and opens its mouth and makes a sound like a door the size of a hall. It will not have you on its stair. A slab of something to eat would not come amiss; nor would going round it, if you are a climber.".
    Comes "The bear comes at you across the shelf faster than anything that big should move.".
    Pleads "The bear sits down suddenly in the snow, heavily, like a tired old dog, and licks its paw, and looks away from you. It is done.".
  }
  Relation bearKilled(group).
  Action feed_bear(actor: group, site: place) "Throw the bear the slab of roast Brindle" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bear, site) and able(bear) and holding(actor, brindle_kind) and not tolerates(bear, actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Spend brindle_slab from actor. Assert tolerates(bear, actor). Retract warned(bear, actor). }
    Result "The slab of ox lands in the snow at its feet. The bear looks at it, and at you, and puts its great head down and sniffs it, and then lies down on the shelf with the meat between its paws and eats it slowly, with its eyes half shut, and does not look at you again.".
  }
  Action climb_round_bear(actor: group, site: place) "Climb round the bear by the ice towers to the back of the shelf" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bear, site) and able(bear) and not tolerates(bear, actor) and not fellFromIce(actor).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, climbing, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert tolerates(bear, actor). Retract warned(bear, actor). }
    On failure { Assert fellFromIce(actor). Assert strikes(ice_fall, actor). Assert at(actor, ice_foot). }
    Result "You go up into the ice towers at the edge of the shelf, handhold by handhold in the blue, and along, and down again behind the bear, which turns its head and looks at you there, and seems to decide you are not worth turning the rest of itself round for.".
    Otherwise "A hold comes away in your hand, and you go down the face of the ice in a rush of blue chips, and fetch up at the foot of the steps in a heap.".
  }
  Relation fellFromIce(group).
  Rule fell_clears when fellFromIce(?c) and hour(clock) == 0 { Retract fellFromIce(?c). }
  Hazard ice_fall "a fall down the face of the Old Ice" means "Deal (2d4) bludgeoning damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  Rule bear_dies when dead(bear) and not bearKilled(bear) { Assert bearKilled(bear). }
  Rule bear_stays_dead near bear when bearKilled(bear) and theHour() and not spoke(bear_dead_told)
    says "The Hour comes over the Old Ice, blue, and the bear does not get up. It lies on the shelf in its rags of harness, white on the white, with its small eyes open. From the back of the shelf, from the mouth in the ice, somebody old is crying out in a language you do not know, the same word over and over." { Assert spoke(bear_dead_told). }
  Entity bear_dead_told: fact "the bear".

  // ── The Sitters ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe cave_scene at sitters_cave when true "In a cave of blue ice, in a cold green underwater light, ten very old men and women sit round a board of stones, in harness older than anything on the Field. They sit on stools of stone round a low table, in harness older than anything you have seen on the Field: bronze scale, leather, a cuirass of linen glued in layers. On the table is a board scratched into the stone, and on the board, stones, black and white. One of them is moving a stone. The others are watching as if it were the most important thing in the world. Nobody looks up.".
  Person sitters "the Sitters" at sitters_cave {
    Role "the oldest dead in Ysgard, round a board of stones". Ancestry human. Numbers 9. Peaceable.
    Greets "Nine very old faces turn to you, slowly, the way old trees would turn if they could, and look at your breath, and turn back to the board.".
  }
  Person aulus "Aulus" at sitters_cave {
    Role "the eldest of the Sitters". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 9. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Likeness "sage".
    Greets "The old man moving the stone finishes moving it, with enormous care, and sits back, and only then looks up. He has a face like a walnut and a legionary's bronze cuirass gone green, and his eyes are very bright and very malicious. He says something in a tongue that has been dead a thousand years, and then, in a strange heavy old Common, 'A breather. Ha. The last breather on this stair was Ithel, and he would not play either.' He gestures at the board. 'Do you play Tabula? You do not. Nobody plays Tabula now. Sit. Lose. I will tell you things while you lose.'".
    Greets again "Aulus looks up from the board. 'Again? Good. Sit.'".
  }
  Measure tabulaLost(group). Relation tabulaWon(group).
  Discovery ithel_told "Three hundred years ago Ithel the Smith, a living man from Larum, came up looking for his son among the dead, quarrelled with a man of Even and killed him with a hammer, and the Even man never rose at the Hour. The Sitters buried him in the Old Ice. A living hand ends what it strikes in Ysgard. Ithel went home, made a bell, and died of grief.".
  Discovery living_kills "In Ysgard a wound given by a living hand does not mend at the Hour: the living kill truly here, and nothing else does. Death has not come back to the Field. It came up the Pass.".
  Discovery ice_burial "The Sitters know the only burial there has ever been in Ysgard: a grave cut into the Old Ice, where the man Ithel killed lies with his eyes shut, under the little cairn at the foot of the steps.".
  Discovery quarrel_known "The Sitters say the war began over a game of Tabula: whether a man who came in at noon should play first or last. Nobody has asked them in seven hundred years.".
  Action play_tabula(actor: group, site: place) "Play Aulus a game of Tabula" {
    Description "Stones and a board, a game of the Aenean world. He talks while he plays.".
    Speaker aulus.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(aulus, site) and not tabulaWon(actor) and tabulaLost(actor) < 3.
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert tabulaWon(actor). Assert knows(actor, quarrel_known). Assert knows(actor, ithel_told). Assert knows(actor, living_kills). Assert knows(actor, ice_burial). }
    On failure { Increase tabulaLost(actor) by 1. Assert knows(actor, quarrel_known). }
    Result "You know the shape of the game from somewhere, a running game, stones racing round the board, and you play it carefully, and Aulus talks, and talks, and goes on talking more and more slowly as your stones come home, until he stops altogether and stares at the board. Then he laughs, a great cracked delighted bark that makes the other nine look up. 'Ithel,' he says. 'You play like Ithel. Ithel would not play, but he played like that in his head.' And because you have beaten him he tells it plainly, moving your winning stone back and forth while he does. 'A smith from Larum came up the stair three hundred years ago for his son. Found him in Morrow. Quarrelled with a man of Even at the ford over the boy, and hit him with his hammer.' The stone stops. 'At the Hour the Even man did not get up. The smith stood over him breathing white. A living hand ends what it strikes, up here. Nothing else does.' He sets the stone down. 'We cut the Even man a grave in the Old Ice, the only grave in Ysgard. The cairn at the foot of the steps is his. Ithel went home down the Pass and did not come again. He made a bell, we heard. For the Hour. Is it still rung?'".
    Otherwise "Aulus plays fast and dirty and talks all the time, mostly about a quarrel seven hundred years ago over this very game, over whether a man who came in at noon should move first or last, which he still thinks he was right about and which is, he says, how the whole war started, ha, the halls do not know that, nobody has asked the Sitters anything in seven hundred years. Your stones are still on the board when his are home. 'Again,' he says, sweeping them up. 'You are learning. Slowly.'".
  }
  // Losing, he tells it anyway, sideways, gloating.
  Rule aulus_gossips near aulus when tabulaLost(party) >= 2 and not knows(party, ithel_told) and at(party, sitters_cave)
    says "Sweeping the stones up after his second win, Aulus says, as if it did not matter: 'You breathers. The last one was Ithel, the smith. Killed an Even man at the ford three hundred years ago over his son, with a hammer, and the Even man never got up. Never. We buried him in the ice.' He sets the stones out again. 'A living hand ends what it strikes up here, did you not know? Nobody knows anything any more. Again?'" teaches ithel_told { }
  Rule ithel_teaches_law when knows(party, ithel_told) and not knows(party, living_kills)
    says "A living man struck a dead one on the Field with a hammer three hundred years ago, and the dead man never rose. Halvard Eld was killed by a short blade from behind, and has not risen. It was not the Field that would not mend them." teaches living_kills { }
  Rule ithel_teaches_burial when knows(party, ithel_told) and not knows(party, ice_burial)
    says "There is one grave in Ysgard: the Sitters cut it in the Old Ice for the man Ithel killed, under the little cairn at the foot of the steps." teaches ice_burial { }
  Topic aulus_who with aulus "Ask Aulus who the Sitters are" when true once {
    Says "'The First Host,' says Aulus. 'Before the halls. When the snow first let us in, there were few of us, and we built a fire and sat round it, and played.' He moves a stone. 'Then there were more, and the dawn-comers and the dusk-comers quarrelled over the board, and went off to build their halls at each end of the Field and fight about it, every day, forever.' He snorts. 'We sat. We are still sitting. They forgot us in a hundred years. It was very restful.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, quarrel_known). }
  }
  Topic aulus_why with aulus "Ask Aulus why the Sitters never fought" when knows(actor, quarrel_known) once {
    Says "Aulus stops with a stone in his fingers. For a moment the malice goes out of his face and he looks only very old. 'I was a soldier for twenty-six years,' he says, 'in the legions of a world that is under the sea now. I died on a wall. When I came in out of the snow I looked at the Field and I thought: no. Not forever. A man is entitled to stop.' He puts the stone down. 'They thought we were cowards. We let them. You cannot explain a thing like that to people who have just found out they cannot die.'".
    On discuss { Increase aulusTrust(aulus) by 1. }
  }
  Measure aulusTrust(group).
  Topic aulus_bronze with aulus "Show Aulus the bronze blade from the bottom of the Clear" when holding(actor, bronze_find) once {
    Says "Aulus takes the green blade in both hands and turns it over, and the other nine Sitters stand up off their stools, all at once, with a scrape of stone. 'Cassian's,' says Aulus. His voice has gone strange. 'That is Cassian's. He threw it at me across the board, at the Quarrel, when I said noon moves last, and it went into the snow, and we never found it.' He hands it back, quickly, as though it were hot. 'He is in Morrow, Cassian. Seven hundred years. I wonder if he still thinks he was right.' Then, almost shy: 'Does Morrow still eat that ox?'".
    On discuss { Increase aulusTrust(aulus) by 1. Assert knows(actor, cassian_known). }
  }
  Discovery cassian_known "The bronze blade from the bottom of the Clear was Cassian's, who threw it at Aulus across the board at the Quarrel that started the war; Cassian is in Morrow still.".
  // Brought down: for a burial, or because there is somewhere now worth coming down to.
  Relation sittersDown(group).
  Topic aulus_down with aulus "Ask Aulus whether the Sitters would come down to Halt" when (knows(actor, ithel_told) and aulusTrust(aulus) >= 1 or toroldMourned(torold) and state(halvard, gone_ice)) and haltStands() and not sittersDown(aulus) and not bearKilled(bear) once {
    Says "Aulus looks at the board for a long time. Then he looks round at the nine, and they look back at him. 'A town,' he says. 'On the Field. With no fighting in it.' He picks up a stone and puts it down. 'Seven hundred years we have sat here waiting for them to get bored.' He stands up, slowly, all of him creaking like a ship. 'Very well. We will come down and look. If it is no good we will come back up. Somebody bring the board.'".
    On discuss { Assert sittersDown(aulus). Assert at(aulus, truce). Assert at(sitters, truce). }
  }
  Observe sitters_in_truce at truce as sign when sittersDown(aulus) and at(aulus, truce) "In the middle of the Truce ten very old people in bronze and leather sit round a board on the floor, playing stones, surrounded by a ring of the dead of both halls who have never seen anyone play anything and are arguing about the rules. Aulus is winning, and saying so.".
  Topic aulus_speak with aulus "Ask Aulus to tell Halt at the ring of spears what a living hand does here" when sittersDown(aulus) and knows(actor, ithel_told) and not truthSpoken(field_country) and beforeTesting() once {
    Grave "Once Halt knows that only a living hand kills here, it cannot be made not to know.".
    Says "Aulus considers it, with a stone in his fingers. 'They will not like it,' he says. 'They will find out nothing came back but what came up the Pass. Then they must decide whether they want their war, with nothing to be afraid of.' He puts the stone down. 'Good. It is time they decided something.' He goes to the ring of spears with the nine behind him, and tells the whole of Halt, in his heavy old Common, about Ithel the Smith; and at the end he points at the cairn of shields where Halvard lies and says: 'A living hand. Not death. Death did not come back. It came up the stair.'".
    On discuss { Assert truthSpoken(field_country). Assert toroldKnows(torold). Assert hildKnows(hild). }
  }
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/oven.ky:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The Oven ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A war-mantlet set on its end and roofed with shields, round an oven Grimbold built out of a bell he found in the
  // snow and broke up, and siege-stones. The only warm room in Halt, and the only place on the Field that smells of
  // anything.
  Relation breadRisen(group). Relation crockTaken(group). Measure crockDay(group).
  Initially Assert restful(oven).
  Observe oven_scene at oven when not breadRisen(grimbold) "Inside the war-mantlet it is warm, and you could weep for it: an oven of siege-stones and broken bell-bronze, a long board of loaves flat and grey and hard as tiles, and a mountain of a man in an apron looking at them. A sack of Larum flour sags against the wall. The man stands over the board with his great arms folded, looking at the loaves the way a man looks at a field after hail.".
  Observe oven_risen at oven when breadRisen(grimbold) "Inside the war-mantlet it is warm, and it smells of bread: real bread, brown and sour and risen, so that your mouth runs. The loaves stand on the long board in rows, round as helms, split across the top where they have opened in the heat. Dead people keep putting their heads in at the mouth of the Oven just to smell it, and going away again with their eyes shut.".

  Person grimbold "Grimbold Ure" at oven {
    Role "a berserker of Morrowhall, who bakes". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 7. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Likeness "berserker".
    Wants mother_kind.
    Greets "The mountain of a man looks round from his flat loaves, and sees your breath, and his face goes soft all over, like dough. 'Oh,' he says. 'You're warm. Come in by the oven, then, you'll want it more than any of us.' He holds out a hand the size of a spade, covered in flour. 'Grimbold Ure. I was a berserker. I'm trying to be a baker. It isn't going well.'".
    Greets again "Grimbold Ure lifts a floury hand. 'In by the oven,' he says. 'You're blue.'".
  }
  Topic grimbold_bread with grimbold "Ask Grimbold Ure what is wrong with the bread" when not breadRisen(grimbold) once {
    Says "Grimbold picks up a loaf and taps it on the board. It sounds like a roof-slate. 'Flour from Larum,' he says. 'The Runners trade for it, a sack at a time. Water from the snow. Salt. And a cup of the old dough from yesterday's, to start it, the way my father did.' He puts it down. 'It won't rise. Forty mornings. I knead it, I set it by the oven, I wait, and it lies there like a dead thing.' He looks at his hands. 'They say up here nothing rises but the dead. I never thought that was a saying about bread.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, grimbold_flat). }
  }
  Discovery grimbold_flat "Grimbold Ure's bread will not rise: forty mornings of flat loaves, started from yesterday's dough as his father did. On the Field they say nothing rises but the dead.".
  Topic grimbold_past with grimbold "Ask Grimbold Ure how a berserker comes to bake" when true once {
    Says "Grimbold sits down on a sack of flour, which groans. 'My father had a bakehouse in Ostry,' he says. 'Five hundred years gone. I was in it from when I could stand. Up at three, the oven, the smell.' He smiles at nothing. 'The Margrave's men came through when I was fifteen and took every lad who could lift a sack, and gave us axes, and found I went mad in a fight, and was good at it. I died at twenty at the Morning of Ashes with my teeth in a man's neck.' He looks at his flat loaves. 'I've not touched dough in five hundred years. I don't believe it'll work. I do it every morning anyway.' He shrugs, enormously. 'Somebody has to try first.'".
  }
  Topic grimbold_why with grimbold "Tell Grimbold Ure why his bread will not rise" when knows(actor, mother_alive) and knows(actor, grimbold_flat) and not breadRisen(grimbold) and not crockTaken(grimbold) once {
    Says "Grimbold listens, very still, with his hands on his knees. 'Alive,' he says. 'The thing in the dough that does it. And nothing alive keeps up here.' He looks at the old dough in its bowl, grey and quiet. 'So I've been starting every loaf with a dead one.' He laughs, a big helpless laugh, and wipes his eyes with a floury wrist. 'Forty mornings. Of course. Of course it is.' Then he looks at you, and at your breath going up white, and slowly his face changes. 'Unless it came up with something warm.'".
  }
  Event grimbold_takes near grimbold when keeps(grimbold, ?m) and itemKind(?m, mother_kind) and not motherDied(larum_country) and not crockTaken(grimbold) "Grimbold takes the little crock in both hands as if it were a bird, and holds it to his ear, and his whole face opens. 'It's working,' he whispers. 'Listen. It's working.' He mixes it into the flour himself, slowly, talking to it under his breath, the way his father talked to the oven, and shapes the loaves, and sets them on the board by the warm stones under a cloth, and sits down on the sack beside them to wait, like a man sitting up with someone sick. 'In the morning,' he says. 'If it's going to, it'll be by the morning.'" then { Assert crockTaken(grimbold). Set crockDay(grimbold) to day(clock). }
  Event grimbold_dead_crock near grimbold when keeps(grimbold, ?m) and itemKind(?m, mother_kind) and motherDied(larum_country) and not crockTaken(grimbold) "Grimbold lifts the cloth and looks at the grey skin on the Mother, and sniffs it, and puts it down. 'Dead,' he says gently, as if telling you about a dog. 'The cold got it on the way up.' He gives it you back. 'Take it down to her, and say sorry. And carry the next one closer.'" then { Give mother_crock to party. }
  Rule bread_rises when crockTaken(grimbold) and day(clock) > crockDay(grimbold) and hour(clock) >= 6 and not breadRisen(grimbold) { Assert breadRisen(grimbold). }
  Rule bread_seen at oven when breadRisen(grimbold) and at(party, oven) and not spoke(bread_told)
    says "When you put your head in at the Oven's mouth Grimbold is standing at the long board with a cloth in his hands, not moving. Under the cloth the loaves have risen. They have risen like hills; they have pushed the cloth up off the board; they sit there round and pale and breathing a little, and when he slides the first one into the oven and brings it out brown, and breaks it, steam comes out of it, steam, in Ysgard, and the smell goes out of the mouth of the Oven and down the lanes of Halt, and people come. They come out of the tents and up the Row and stand outside the Oven in the snow, a hundred of them, two hundred, in mail and leather and bronze, not saying anything, smelling it. Grimbold gives them the first loaf in pieces, a piece each, until it is gone, and then the next. He is crying into his beard. 'Nothing rises in Ysgard but the dead,' he says to you, 'and Grimbold's bread.'" { Assert spoke(bread_told). }
  Entity bread_told: fact "the bread rising".
  // The Oven feeds the living, who need it.
  Relation fedAtOven(group).
  Topic grimbold_feeds with grimbold "Ask Grimbold Ure for something to eat" when not fedAtOven(actor) {
    Says "Grimbold gives you what he has, and stands over you while you eat it, and asks you what it tastes like. He wants to know very much what it tastes like.".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, rations) by 2. Assert fedAtOven(actor). }
  }
  Rule oven_feeds_daily when hour(clock) == 0 and fedAtOven(?g) { Retract fedAtOven(?g). }
  Observe halt_smells at halt_cross as ambience when breadRisen(grimbold) and haltStands() "Over everything in Halt, over the cold iron smell of the Field, there is a smell of bread.".
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/pass.ky:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The Pass and the White ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The way through the White is a line of old cairns, each out of sight of the last in the cloud. Jory Whitlock knows
  // it and will take the living through for six coin; a wayfinder can find the cairns alone; anyone else wanders in the
  // white until the cold sends them down.
  Observe pass_foot_scene at pass_foot when true "Above the last wall of the last field the path goes up between two shoulders of black rock, steep, through snow that is trodden in a line by sledge-runners. A little way above you it goes into the cloud, and the cloud is not grey, as cloud is, but white, bright, as if lit from inside. It does not move. A post stands at the edge of it with a bell on top and a board: LIVING, GO NO FURTHER WITHOUT THE GUIDE.".
  Observe white_scene at the_white when not knows(party, white_known) "White. White underfoot and white overhead and white in front of your face, so that you cannot tell how far off your own hand is. The cold has a smell, like iron. There is no sound at all. Somewhere there is a line of cairns, Jory says, each out of sight of the last. You cannot see a cairn. You cannot see anything.".
  Observe white_known_scene at the_white when knows(party, white_known) "White, and in the white, if you look for it, a darker shape a dozen yards on: a cairn, rimed thick, with a ram's skull on top. And beyond it, when you get there, the next.".
  Observe white_sound at the_white as sound when skyLoud() "Somewhere above you in the white, iron on iron, a long way off and all around.".

  Discovery white_known "The way through the White is a line of old cairns, each with a ram's skull on top and each out of sight of the last: keep the last at your back and walk until the next comes out of the white.".
  Action find_cairns(actor: group, site: place) "Search the White for the line of cairns" {
    Description "Alone in the white, by the feel of the ground and the set of the snow.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_white) and not knows(actor, white_known) and not lostInWhite(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, wayfinding, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, white_known). }
    On failure { Assert lostInWhite(actor). Assert strikes(frostbite, actor). }
    Result "You go slowly, keeping the slope of the ground under your left foot, and after a long time a darker shape comes out of the white: a cairn, with a ram's skull on it. You stand with your back to it and walk, and the next comes.".
    Otherwise "You walk, and the white walks with you, and after a long time your own footprints come out of the white in front of you, going the other way. Your hands have stopped hurting, which is worse. You had better go down and warm them and try again.".
  }
  Relation lostInWhite(group).
  Rule lost_clears when lostInWhite(?c) and not at(?c, the_white) { Retract lostInWhite(?c). }

  // ── Jory Whitlock, the guide ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe guide_house_scene at guide_house when true "A bare clean room with a table laid for two, and two cups on it, and only one of them used. Ropes coiled on pegs, ice-poles in a rack, a row of sheepskin coats hanging like a row of tired men.".
  Person jory "Jory Whitlock" at guide_house {
    Role "the guide, who takes the living up through the White". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Level 4. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Likeness "guide".
    Uses go. Plans 20 steps.
    Sells sheepskin_kind for 4 coin from 4.
    Greets "A lean grey man in a sheepskin coat looks up from mending a rope, and looks at you the way he would look at the weather on the Pass. 'Going up,' he says. It is not a question. 'Six coin to the Coming-in. I'll not set foot on the Field. Nobody living should. And you'll want a coat; you'll not like the cold up there. It's not weather. It's a place that doesn't keep heat.'".
    Greets again "Jory Whitlock looks up from his rope and nods, once.".
  }
  Topic jory_field with jory "Ask Jory Whitlock what is up there" when true once {
    Says "Jory goes on with his rope. 'The dead,' he says. 'Soldiers. Every soldier that ever died holding something, some of them. They come in out of the snow at the Coming-in and Cleeve sends them east or west by what hour they died, and they go to the halls and fight every day on the Field, and at dusk whatever was done to them mends and they get up.' He pulls a knot tight. 'Nine hundred years. And now they don't. I took a collector up a fortnight back. They were sitting about on the Field in the snow like men after a harvest, talking, and building a town out of their shields.' He looks at the rope. 'I've seen them a hundred times. They're people. That's the worst of it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, quiet_heard). Assert knows(actor, halt_heard). }
  }
  Discovery halt_heard "Since the quiet, the dead in Ysgard sit about on the Field building a town out of their shields, Jory Whitlock says.".
  Topic jory_ned with jory "Ask Jory Whitlock about his son" when knows(actor, ned_overdue) and not knows(actor, ned_dead) once {
    Says "Jory looks at the second cup on the table, and away. 'Ned took the mule to Wendham,' he says. 'Fleeces. Four days. Three to there and back, and a day for a lass, I'd say, he's sixteen.' He puts the rope down. 'The road's been bad by the Hob Bridge this spring. Men off the fells.' He picks the rope up again. 'He'll have stopped for a lass.'".
  }
  Action hire_jory(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Jory Whitlock six coin to take you up through the White" {
    Description "To the Coming-in, at the head of the Pass on the far side: about three hours, mostly in the white.".
    Speaker jory.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(jory, site) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 6 and not joryGrieving(jory).
    Time 16.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Increase quantity(jory, gold) by 6. Assert knows(actor, white_known). Assert at(actor, snow_gate). }
    Result "Jory takes a pole from the rack and a coil of rope, and you go up the street and up the path between the black shoulders, and into the white. He walks a yard ahead with the rope between you, and does not talk, and every so often he stops and puts his hand flat on a cairn with a ram's skull on top, the way a man touches a doorpost. 'Keep the last at your back,' he says, once, 'and walk till the next comes.' Then the white thins, and goes blue, and you are standing on a height in a light like the inside of a knife, and the cold has teeth. Jory looks out over it for a moment. Then he turns round without a word and goes back down into the white, and is gone.".
  }
  // Afterwards he will take you up again whenever you ask, for nothing, if you have brought him word.
  Action jory_again(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Jory Whitlock to see you up through the White again" {
    Speaker jory.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(jory, site) and joryTold(jory) and not joryGrieving(jory).
    Time 16.
    On success { Assert at(actor, snow_gate). }
    Result "Jory takes the pole and the rope without a word and you go up through the white together. At the top he does not turn back at once, this time. He stands looking down at the Field for a long while. Then he goes.".
  }
}

Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // The country beyond a march of a generated world: the company that comes up the valley road is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  // What is said of Larum in the country behind it: once the Morning After has come, it is old news there.
  Entity word: fact "What is said of Larum and the quiet in the country behind it.".
  Rule word_old when outcomeDecided(field_country) and morningAfter() and not stale(word) { Assert stale(word). }
  // And which way it went: the sky loud again over the Pass, or quiet still (the word of it in countries.json, by).
  Entity word_loud: fact "That the dead up the Larum Pass have started again.".
  Rule word_loud_old when skyLoud() and morningAfter() and not stale(word_loud) { Assert stale(word_loud). }
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/ring.ky:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The ring of spears ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Halvard Eld lies where he fell, on a bier of shields, under a frost that does not melt; four of Even stand over him
  // day and night, and Torold Hame, his sworn brother, has not left the ring in forty days.
  Observe ring_scene at the_ring when state(halvard, lying) "In the middle of Halt, inside a ring of planted spears, a big red-haired man lies on a bier of shields under a frost that does not melt, and four of Evenhall stand over him with their backs to him. He lies on his back with his hands on his chest and his eyes shut. The frost has grown over his red hair and his eyebrows and his beard, white and fine as fur. People going past the ring lower their voices, the way people do going past a church.".
  Observe ring_empty at the_ring when not state(halvard, lying) "The ring of spears stands in the middle of Halt as it did, but the bier of shields inside it is empty, and the snow on it is going over smooth. Somebody has hung a red-haired doll on one of the spears.".
  Thing halvard "Halvard Eld, on his bier" at the_ring {
    State lying "Halvard Eld lies on his bier under his frost.".
    State gone_ice "Halvard Eld lies in the Old Ice.".
    State gone_larum "Halvard Eld lies in Larum churchyard.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(halvard, lying).
  Observe halvard_looked near halvard when tried(halvard, looking) and state(halvard, lying) and not knows(party, halvard_wound) "From outside the spears you can see his face, quiet under the frost, and the place on his chest where his hands are folded over a hole in his jack. You cannot see more from here without going in, and the four of Even are watching you go round.".

  Person even_watch "the watch on Halvard" at the_ring {
    Role "four of Evenhall, standing over their champion". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 5. Numbers 4. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Greets "The nearest of the four looks at your breath, and at you, and moves his hand to where his sword is, and leaves it there. 'Stand back from the spears, breather.'".
  }
  Person torold "Torold Hame" at the_ring {
    Role "the Warden of Evenhall, Halvard's sworn brother". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 8. Trait brave. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
    Likeness "crusader".
    Greets "A big grey-bearded man in old blackened mail stands at the head of the bier with his hands folded on the pommel of a sword stood point-down in the snow, and does not look round when you come. When he does, it is at your breath, and for a moment something moves in his face, and then it is gone. 'You're the breather Cleeve sent down,' he says. 'Stand where you like. Don't touch him.'".
    Greets again "Torold Hame looks at you, and back at the bier.".
  }
  Measure toroldTrust(group).
  Relation toroldLeave(group). Relation toroldKnows(group). Relation toroldConsents(group). Relation toroldMourned(group).
  Topic torold_who with torold "Ask Torold Hame who lies on the shields" when state(halvard, lying) once {
    Says "'Halvard Eld,' says Torold. 'Champion of Evenhall. My brother, by oath.' He looks at the face under the frost. 'He came in out of the snow twelve years ago, at four in the afternoon, with nine men's blood on him, laughing. I took him into Even. He was champion in five years. There's never been anyone like him on the Field.' He is quiet. 'He'll get up,' he says. 'When the Daily comes back, he'll get up. You'll see.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, halvard_fell). Increase toroldTrust(torold) by 1. }
  }
  Topic torold_why with torold "Ask Torold Hame why he wants the Testing" when testingNamed(field_country) and state(halvard, lying) once {
    Says "Torold looks at you a long time, as if deciding whether you are worth an answer. 'The Mending came with the Daily,' he says. 'Nine hundred years: every day we fought, and every dusk the light came blue and we got up. Then Hild blew her call over his body, and we stopped, and he stayed down.' He turns the sword's pommel under his hands. 'We broke it. We stopped fighting and the Mending stopped for him. Start the Daily, and the Hour will come blue over the Field again, and he'll get up off those shields and laugh at me.' His jaw works. 'They think I want the war. I don't want the war. I want to stop standing here.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, torold_theory). Increase toroldTrust(torold) by 1. }
  }
  Discovery torold_theory "Torold Hame believes the Mending came with the Daily, and stopped for Halvard when the fighting stopped; start the Daily again and Halvard will rise at the Hour. He does not want the war. He wants his friend back.".
  Topic torold_what with torold "Ask Torold Hame what Halvard was" when toroldTrust(torold) >= 2 and state(halvard, lying) once {
    Says "'You've read the ballad,' says Torold. 'Everyone has. Larum makes it rhyme.' He does not look at you. 'I know what he was alive. He told me himself, the first night, laughing: Wendmere. The fullers. The vats.' He is silent so long that the watch shift their feet. 'Up here it didn't matter. That's what I told myself. Up here nothing you do to a man stays done. You kill him and he gets up. You could be anything you liked, up here, and the next morning it was gone.' He looks down at the frost on Halvard's face. 'He was good to me. He was the best friend I had in two hundred years. And he burned children.' Then, very low: 'And now it's stayed done. The one thing.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, torold_knows_what). Increase toroldTrust(torold) by 1. }
  }
  Discovery torold_knows_what "Torold Hame knows what Halvard was in life, from Halvard's own mouth: the burner of Wendmere. Up here, he told himself, nothing done stayed done. Halvard was his best friend in two hundred years, and burned children.".
  Topic torold_leave with torold "Ask Torold Hame's leave to look closely at the wound" when state(halvard, lying) and toroldTrust(torold) >= 1 and not toroldLeave(torold) once {
    Says "Torold considers you. 'You've a breather's eyes,' he says. 'Maybe you see different.' He jerks his head, and the watch step back from the bier. 'Look, then. Don't touch him.'".
    On discuss { Assert toroldLeave(torold). }
  }
  Action look_wound(actor: group, site: place) "Look closely at the wound that killed Halvard Eld" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_ring) and toroldLeave(torold) and state(halvard, lying) and not lookedWound(actor).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert lookedWound(actor). Assert knows(actor, halvard_wound). }
    Result "You go in among the spears. Close to, under the frost, his skin is smooth as a boy's: no scar anywhere on the face or the great forearms, though Torold says he fought every day for twelve years. The hole in his jack over the chest is only a tear, and there is nothing under it. Torold turns the head, gently, for you to see. At the back of the neck, at the top of the spine, there is a small wound, no wider than your thumb, clean, and its edges are exactly as they were the moment it was made. It is the only mark on him.".
  }
  Relation lookedWound(group).
  Discovery halvard_wound "Halvard Eld has no scar on him from twelve years of the Daily: every wound mended. The only mark on him is a small wound at the nape, no wider than a thumb, made by a short blade from behind, its edges exactly as they were the moment it was made.".
  Action read_wound(actor: group, site: place) "Read the wound as the dead are read" {
    Description "What made it, and how, and what it did.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_ring) and lookedWound(actor) and not knows(actor, wound_read) and state(halvard, lying).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, rites, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, wound_read). }
    Result "You know wounds. This one was made by a fuller's knife, or something like one, short and broad and very sharp, held low and driven up from behind by somebody small, somebody who stood close and waited for the moment; and he never saw it. And it is not like the others. Every other wound this man ever took up here has gone; this one has not even begun to close. It was not the Field that would not mend it. It was the hand.".
    Otherwise "You look a long time. A small blade, from behind, close: whoever did it was in the press beside him, where nobody looks at anybody but the man in front, and where the Runners go with their sledges. Beyond that it will not tell you anything.".
  }
  Discovery wound_read "The wound that killed Halvard was made by a short broad blade like a fuller's knife, driven up from behind by someone small who stood close and waited; and it has not begun to close, as though it were not the Field that would not mend it, but the hand.".
  // Slipping in at night, past the watch.
  Action creep_to_bier(actor: group, site: place) "Slip in among the spears in the dark, past the watch, and look at the body" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_ring) and dark() and state(halvard, lying) and not lookedWound(actor) and not toroldLeave(torold) and not caughtAtBier(actor).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert lookedWound(actor). Assert knows(actor, halvard_wound). }
    On failure { Assert caughtAtBier(actor). Decrease toroldTrust(torold) by 1 or to nothing. }
    Result "You go in low between two spears while the watch at the near corner looks at the stars. Torold is asleep on his feet, leaning on his sword. Close to, Halvard's skin is smooth: no scar anywhere, though he fought every day for twelve years. At the nape of his neck, when you ease the frozen hair aside, there is a small clean wound no wider than your thumb, its edges exactly as they were when it was made. It is the only mark on him. You are out between the spears again before anyone turns.".
    Otherwise "You are halfway between the spears when a hand takes you by the collar and lifts you off your feet and sets you down outside the ring. Torold Hame looks at you over the hand. 'I said don't touch him,' he says, and lets go.".
  }
  Relation caughtAtBier(group).
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/scrapes:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The Scrapes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Under the Field's southern lip, where the ice overhangs, the Runners have built a warren out of nine centuries of
  // what the Field leaves: shields for walls, banners for doors, a siege-ladder for a stair. Those who died running live
  // here, wear no arms, sit at no bench, and are owed nothing. They clear the broken off the battle-line every night so
  // the next day has footing; they keep the Picking, the trade with Larum.
  Observe mouth_scene at scrapes_mouth when true "Under the southern lip of the Field the ice overhangs like a wave about to break, green and blue, and under the wave, in its shadow, a wall of shields stuck edge to edge with a gap in it hung with a banner. Sledges stand outside piled with broken iron. A dead girl sits on one in a smock with no device on it, mending a sledge-trace with her teeth.".
  Observe warren_scene at warren when true "The Runners' warren: low rooms walled with shields and roofed with the ice itself, lit with fat-lamps that make it, against all sense, warm, and dead men and women in plain smocks looking up at your breath. Banners hang for doors. Everything here is something the Field threw away: a table that was a cart's tailboard, chairs that were saddles, a cradle that was a helm, though there are no children. No smock has a device on it.".
  Observe nook_scene at edith_nook when at(edith, edith_nook) "Behind the banners a nook no bigger than a cupboard, with a heap of sacking for a bed, a fat-lamp, a tin cup, and a woman sitting on the sacking with her knees drawn up, wrapped in three Runners' smocks one over the other, shivering. Her breath goes up white in the lamplight.".
  Observe nook_empty at edith_nook when not at(edith, edith_nook) "A nook behind the banners: sacking, a fat-lamp gone out, a tin cup. Nobody.".
  // Seen from the warren, by one who knows what a breath means here.
  Observe edith_breath at warren as sign when at(edith, edith_nook) and knows(party, breath_sign) and not knows(party, nook_known) "Far back in the warren, behind a hanging banner, a little white breath goes up in the lamplight, and stops, as if whoever it belongs to has seen you, and is holding it." teaches nook_known.
  Discovery nook_known "Behind a hanging banner far back in the Runners' warren there is a nook, and somebody in it who breathes white.".

  Person runners "the Runners" at warren {
    Role "the dead who died running, in smocks with no device". Ancestry human. Numbers 4. Peaceable.
    Greets "Nobody gets up. A man with a long scarred face says, not unkindly, 'Breather. You're in the wrong place. The halls are up the hill. This is where the Field puts what it doesn't want.'".
  }
  Topic runners_life with runners "Ask the Runners what they do" when true once {
    Says "'Carry,' says the scarred man. 'Every night, after the Hour, when they've all got up and gone home to their oxen, we go out on the Field with the sledges and drag off what's broken, so they've footing in the morning. Swords, shields, carts, a tower once.' He shrugs. 'Nine hundred years. They don't see us. You can walk through Morrow's yard with a sledge of their own broken spears and they'll look through you like a window.' A woman beside him says, 'We died running. That's all they need to know.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, runners_clear). }
  }
  Discovery runners_clear "The Runners, the dead who died fleeing, clear the broken off the battle-line every night so that the halls have footing in the morning. Nobody sees them. They died running; that is all the halls need to know.".

  // ── Cuddy Wardle, foreman of the Runners ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person cuddy "Cuddy Wardle" at scrapes_mouth {
    Role "the foreman of the Runners". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 4. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Likeness "goose-girl".
    Wants tobacco_kind.
    Greets "A thin sharp girl of sixteen or so, with a face that has been sixteen for a hundred and fifty years, looks you up and down from the sledge she is checking. 'Breather,' she says. 'You'll be wanting something. They always want something, the ones that come up. Iron for Larum, or the way to somewhere, or a look at the poor dead Runners.' She spits. 'What've you got?'".
    Greets again "Cuddy Wardle looks up from a sledge. 'You again.' It is not entirely unfriendly.".
  }
  Measure cuddyTrust(group).
  Relation runnersStrike(group). Relation runnersSeated(group). Relation edithShown(group).
  Event cuddy_leaf near cuddy when keeps(cuddy, ?t) and itemKind(?t, tobacco_kind) and cuddyTrust(cuddy) < 1 "Cuddy turns the twist over, and smells it, and puts it away inside her smock very fast. 'Larum leaf,' she says. 'Well.' For a moment she looks exactly sixteen. 'Nobody gives a Runner anything. They trade.' She looks at you differently. 'Sit, then, if you want. Ask.'" then { Increase cuddyTrust(cuddy) by 1. }
  Topic cuddy_self with cuddy "Ask Cuddy Wardle how she died" when true once {
    Says "'Running,' says Cuddy. 'Battle of Sallow Lane, a hundred and fifty year back. I was a drummer-girl, sixteen, I'd been hired the week before because I could keep time. First volley I dropped the drum and ran. Ball in the back.' She shrugs. 'Cleeve asked me the hour and I told him, and he looked at the hole, and wrote RUNNER, and that was that. No hall. No bench. Just the sledges.' She tugs a trace tight. 'I'm good at the sledges. I'm foreman. Nobody up the hill knows my name.'".
    On discuss { Increase cuddyTrust(cuddy) by 1. }
  }
  Topic cuddy_want with cuddy "Ask Cuddy Wardle what she wants" when cuddyTrust(cuddy) >= 1 once {
    Says "Cuddy laughs. Then she stops. 'A bench,' she says. 'In one of the halls. Not a good one. The low one by the door that the dogs sleep under, in the stories.' She is not looking at you. 'Just to sit at it, once, with a cup, while they eat their ox. Just to see what it's like, to sit at a bench.' She kicks the sledge. 'Stupid. Forget it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, cuddy_wants). Increase cuddyTrust(cuddy) by 1. }
  }
  Discovery cuddy_wants "Cuddy Wardle, foreman of the Runners, wants a bench in one of the halls: the low one by the door, just to sit at once, with a cup, while they eat.".
  // The lever: nobody has cleared the Field in forty days; a Testing on nine hundred years of iron cannot be fought.
  Topic cuddy_field with cuddy "Ask Cuddy Wardle who will clear the Field for the Testing" when testingNamed(field_country) and knows(actor, runners_clear) and beforeTesting() once {
    Says "Cuddy opens her mouth to say Runners, of course, and shuts it. 'Nobody's cleared it since the Halt,' she says slowly. 'Forty days. There's been nothing to clear. But the last day they fought, they fought to the Hour, and nobody went out after. It's all still there under the snow by the ford: the whole of that day's iron.' She looks at you, and you watch her see it. 'Torold can't fight on that. You can't hold a line on a floor of swords. They'll need us out there the night before, all night, with the sledges.' A slow grin. 'Nobody's asked us. They'll just expect it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, field_uncleared). Increase cuddyTrust(cuddy) by 1. }
  }
  Discovery field_uncleared "Nobody has cleared the Field since the Halt: the whole last day's iron lies under the snow by the ford, and Torold's Testing cannot be fought on it. The Runners will be expected to clear it the night before. Nobody has asked them.".
  Topic cuddy_strike with cuddy "Put it to Cuddy Wardle that the Runners need not clear the Field" when knows(actor, field_uncleared) and not runnersStrike(cuddy) and not runnersSeated(cuddy) and beforeTesting() and cuddyTrust(cuddy) >= 2 once {
    Says "Cuddy looks at you for a long time. 'Not clear it,' she says. 'Just. Not go out.' She looks back into the warren, at the dead in their smocks round the lamps. 'They'd come down here. Torold's men. They'd drag us out.' Then: 'And make us do what? We're dead. They can kill us all day, we get up at the Hour.' She starts to laugh, softly. 'Nine hundred years, and we never thought of it. Because nobody ever thought we could say no.' She gets up. 'I'll put it to them. They'll do it. They'll do it for the look on Torold's face.'".
    On discuss { Assert runnersStrike(cuddy). }
  }
  Topic cuddy_seated with cuddy "Tell Cuddy Wardle that Morrowhall will give the Runners a bench" when runnersSeated(cuddy) and not spoke(cuddy_bench_told) once {
    Says "Cuddy does not say anything for a long time. Then she wipes her nose on her sleeve, hard. 'The low one,' she says. 'By the door.' You nod. 'Well,' says Cuddy. 'Well.' She looks out of the mouth of the Scrapes, up the long white slope to the eastern height. 'Then we'll clear the Field for Torold, if he wants it. A bargain's a bargain. Somebody up there's treated us straight, and we'll not be the ones that don't.'".
    On discuss { Assert spoke(cuddy_bench_told). }
  }
  Entity cuddy_bench_told: fact "the bench".
  Observe runners_bench at morrow_hall as sign when runnersSeated(cuddy) and (hour(clock) >= 19 or hour(clock) < 5) "At the low bench by the door, where the dogs sleep in the stories, a row of Runners in plain smocks sit with horn cups, very upright, not eating, looking at everything. Cuddy Wardle is at the end, swinging her legs.".

  // ── Edith Marl ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Living, a fuller's widow from Wendmere, whose husband and daughter Halvard Eld's company burned in life. She came up
  // with the Runners' sledges dressed as a picker, and killed him in the Daily with a fuller's knife. Cuddy hides her,
  // because she is the first person in Ysgard who ever did a Runner's work and then did something else.
  Person edith "Edith Marl" at edith_nook {
    Role "who breathes white". Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    Likeness "seamstress".
    Known as "a woman wrapped in Runners' smocks" when not knows(party, edith_named).
    Greets "The woman on the sacking looks up at you, and at your breath, white like hers in the lamplight, and something goes out of her shoulders that has been holding them up for a long time. 'Oh,' she says. 'You're alive.' She does not get up. 'Have you come to take me to Torold Hame?'".
    Greets again "Edith Marl looks up from her sacking, and pulls the smocks closer.".
  }
  Measure edithTrust(group).
  Relation edithHome(group). Relation edithGivenUp(group). Relation edithConfessed(group). Relation edithDead(group). Relation edithSpared(group).
  Discovery edith_named "The woman hiding in the Scrapes is Edith Marl, a fuller's widow of Wendmere, living.".
  Topic edith_who with edith "Ask the woman who she is" when not knows(actor, edith_named) once {
    Says "'Edith Marl,' she says. 'Of Wendmere, that was.' She watches you to see if the name means anything. 'You'll have read the ballad. Everybody's read the ballad.' Her hands are red and cracked, a fuller's hands, wrapped round the tin cup. 'I killed him,' she says, quite flatly, as you might say you had shut a gate. 'Halvard Eld. With my fulling-knife, in the back of the neck, in the press by the ford. I'd been waiting a week for him to come near enough.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, edith_named). Assert knows(actor, edith_did_it). Increase edithTrust(edith) by 1. }
  }
  Discovery edith_did_it "Edith Marl killed Halvard Eld with her fulling-knife, in the back of the neck, in the press by the ford, having waited a week for him to come near enough.".
  Topic edith_why with edith "Ask Edith Marl why" when knows(actor, edith_did_it) once {
    Says "Edith looks at the lamp. 'Tom,' she says. 'My husband. And Alys, she was four. The Free Company of the Hook came through Wendmere the summer of the bad wool, twenty year back, and they wanted the fullers' silver and we hadn't any, and Halvard Eld laughed and fired the vats.' She is quite steady. 'I was at my sister's in Hob. I came home to the smoke.' She turns the cup. 'Twelve years ago he died in a siege. I thought that was the end of it. And then a chapman came through with a penny ballad, and they were singing it in the inn: Halvard Eld, champion of Evenhall, fighting on in glory till the stars go out.' Her voice does not change. 'Till the stars go out. Every day. Laughing. And getting up.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, edith_why_known). Increase edithTrust(edith) by 1. }
  }
  Discovery edith_why_known "Halvard Eld's Free Company burned Edith Marl's husband Tom and her four-year-old daughter Alys in the fullers' vats at Wendmere twenty years ago. When the ballad told her he was fighting on in glory in Ysgard, getting up every day, she came up the Pass to kill him.".
  Topic edith_knew with edith "Ask Edith Marl whether she knew a living hand would kill him for good" when knows(actor, edith_did_it) once {
    Says "'No,' says Edith. 'I thought he'd get up. I thought I'd do it and he'd get up at dusk and I'd have done it anyway, once, to his face, so he'd know somebody remembered.' She looks at her red hands. 'I wanted him to know. That was all I wanted. And he went down in the snow, and at dusk the blue came over, and they all got up, all round me, thousands of them, and he didn't.' She is silent. 'I stood there. I was the only one standing there breathing. And a girl in a smock took my arm and said, quiet, come on, and brought me here.' She pulls the smocks tighter. 'A living hand. That's what it is. Cuddy says the old ones under the ice would know.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, living_kills). Assert knows(actor, sitters_rumour). Increase edithTrust(edith) by 1. }
  }
  Topic edith_sorry with edith "Ask Edith Marl whether she is sorry" when knows(actor, edith_why_known) and edithTrust(edith) >= 2 once {
    Says "Edith thinks about it properly, which is worse than if she had answered at once. 'No,' she says. 'I've tried. I lie here and try.' She looks at you. 'I'm sorry he's the only one up here it stays done to. I'm sorry about Torold Hame; Cuddy says he stands there all day. I'm sorry the peace is made of me.' She pulls a smock up round her chin. 'But Tom's in the ground and Alys is in the ground and he was up here laughing. I'm not sorry about that.' Then, very low: 'I'd like to go home. I can't find the way down. I came up with the sledges, I never learned the cairns.'".
    On discuss { Assert acceptsEscort(edith, actor). Increase edithTrust(edith) by 1. }
  }
  Topic edith_cairn with edith "Tell Edith Marl that Halvard cut the name of Wendmere into the cairn on the highest Tooth" when knows(actor, halvard_cut) and knows(actor, edith_named) once {
    Says "Edith goes very still. 'Wendmere,' she says. You tell her: the cairn on the Tooth, from which the lowland can be seen, and the name cut fresh among the old ones, and Torold saying he went up there every week. Edith puts her cup down. Her hands are shaking for the first time, and not with cold. 'I cut it in the beam,' she says. 'At the Hark. Every night, over again.' She stares at the lamp. 'He remembered it.' She says it as if it were the worst thing you could have told her. 'I didn't want him to have remembered it. I don't want him to have been sorry. Then what was I—' She stops, and puts her face in her knees, and does not cry, and you sit with her a while.".
    On discuss { Increase edithTrust(edith) by 1. Assert edithShaken(edith). }
  }
  Relation edithShaken(group).
  // Cuddy shows the nook to one she trusts.
  Topic cuddy_edith with cuddy "Ask Cuddy Wardle about the breather in the Scrapes" when (knows(actor, widow_heard) or knows(actor, wound_read) or knows(actor, breath_sign)) and cuddyTrust(cuddy) >= 3 and not knows(actor, nook_known) once {
    Says "Cuddy looks at you a long time, chewing her lip. Then she jerks her head. 'Come on,' she says. 'She's the first one ever did a Runner's work up here and then did something else. If you hurt her, I'll know.' She takes you into the warren and holds a banner aside.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, nook_known). Assert at(actor, warren). }
  }
  // Given up to Even, without being brought: Even goes down into the Scrapes, and she is killed, and comes in out of the
  // snow at the hour she died, and Cleeve sends her west, into Evenhall, forever.
  Topic give_up_edith with torold "Tell Torold Hame where Halvard's killer is hiding" when knows(actor, edith_did_it) and at(edith, edith_nook) and state(halvard, lying) and not edithGivenUp(edith) once {
    Grave "Torold will go down into the Scrapes, and she is living.".
    Says "Torold hears you without a word. When you are done he takes his sword up out of the snow, and looks at it, and calls two of the watch with a jerk of his head, and goes, walking, not hurrying, south toward the lip of the Field. He does not look back at you or the bier.".
    On discuss { Assert edithGivenUp(edith). Set givenUpAt(edith) to watch(clock). Assert toroldKnows(torold). Assert at(torold, warren). }
  }
  Measure givenUpAt(group).
  Rule edith_taken when edithGivenUp(edith) and watch(clock) >= givenUpAt(edith) + 6 and not edithDead(edith) { Assert edithDead(edith). Assert at(edith, limbo). Set givenUpAt(edith) to watch(clock). Assert at(torold, the_ring). }
  Rule edith_comes_in when edithDead(edith) and at(edith, limbo) and watch(clock) >= givenUpAt(edith) + 1 { Assert at(edith, snow_gate). }
  Rule edith_comes_in_seen at snow_gate when edithDead(edith) and at(edith, snow_gate) and at(party, snow_gate) and not spoke(edith_in_told)
    says "Out of the curtain of snow a woman walks, in three Runners' smocks one over the other, with red cracked hands. She is not shivering. Her breath does not steam. She looks down at the Field, and at the hall on its western height, where the low sun is, and her face does nothing at all. 'Hour?' says Cleeve gently, coming out with the ledger. 'Afternoon,' says Edith Marl. Cleeve writes, and points west. She goes, down toward Evenhall, where Halvard Eld's name is painted on the Tally from the floor to the roof." { Assert spoke(edith_in_told). }
  Entity edith_in_told: fact "Edith coming in".
  Rule edith_to_evenhall when edithDead(edith) and at(edith, snow_gate) and not at(party, snow_gate) and (spoke(edith_in_told) or watch(clock) >= givenUpAt(edith) + 144) { Assert at(edith, even_hall). }
  // Brought to the ring, she confesses before Torold.
  Action bring_edith(actor: group, site: place) "Bring Edith Marl in among the spears, before Torold Hame" {
    Description "She will say what she did, aloud, to him and to all Halt. What he does then is his.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_ring) and following(edith, actor) and at(torold, site) and state(halvard, lying) and not edithConfessed(edith).
    Grave "Torold Hame is the best sword in Evenhall, and she is living.".
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert edithConfessed(edith). Assert truthSpoken(field_country). Assert toroldKnows(torold). }
    Result "Edith stops outside the spears. Torold Hame sees her breath, white, and her red hands, and lifts his head. For a long moment nobody moves. Then Edith goes in between the spears, past the watch, who do not stop her because they do not understand what they are seeing, and stands at the foot of the bier, and says, loud enough for the whole of Halt that is in earshot: 'I am Edith Marl of Wendmere. I killed him. With my fulling-knife. Because he burned my husband and my child in the vats, and laughed, and you made a song of him.' The lane goes silent from end to end.".
  }
  Rule torold_spares at the_ring when edithConfessed(edith) and following(edith, party) and at(party, the_ring) and (toroldTrust(torold) >= 2 or knows(party, torold_knows_what)) and not edithSpared(edith) and not edithDead(edith)
    says "Torold Hame looks at her for so long that the watch begin to shift. His hands are on the pommel of the sword stood in the snow, and they tighten, and loosen. 'I know what he was,' he says at last, to her, not loud. 'He told me. The first night.' He looks down at the frost on Halvard's face. 'I'll not take it from you. You've carried it twenty years. It's yours.' He turns his back on her, which in Even is the gravest courtesy there is. 'Go home, Edith Marl. Before the cold has you.'" { Assert edithSpared(edith). }
  Rule torold_kills at the_ring when edithConfessed(edith) and following(edith, party) and at(party, the_ring) and toroldTrust(torold) < 2 and not knows(party, torold_knows_what) and not edithSpared(edith) and not edithDead(edith)
    says "Torold Hame lifts the sword out of the snow. Nobody stops him. It is very quick. Edith Marl does not try to get out of the way. She lies in the snow at the foot of Halvard's bier with her breath going up white, once, twice, and then not. Torold stands over her with the sword, and looks at it, and at her, and at the bier, and puts his hand over his eyes." { Assert edithDead(edith). Retract following(edith, party). Assert at(edith, limbo). Set givenUpAt(edith) to watch(clock). Assert toroldKilledEdith(torold). }
  Relation toroldKilledEdith(group).
  // Brought down to Larum, she goes home.
  Rule edith_goes_home at larum_street when following(edith, party) and at(party, larum_street) and not edithHome(edith)
    says "In Larum street Edith Marl stands still a long while in the warmth coming out of the bakehouse door, with her eyes shut. Then she unwinds the three Runners' smocks one after another and folds them over her arm, and stands in her own widow's coat. Bet Garside has come out of the Hark and is looking at her. 'You'll want your rent back,' says Bet. 'No,' says Edith. 'Keep it. I'll want the road.' She looks at you once, and nods, the way you nod to someone across a market, and goes off down the valley road on foot, toward the lowlands and the town that is not there, not hurrying." { Assert edithHome(edith). Retract following(edith, party). Assert at(edith, limbo). }
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/song.ky:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The Truce ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A siege-tower lying on its side in the middle of Halt, with a door cut in its floor and benches nailed to its walls:
  // the alehouse, where they drink a mead whose honey the Runners trade for at the pass.
  Observe truce_scene at truce when true "An alehouse inside a siege-tower lying on its side, its floors become walls, lit by ox-fat lamps, with a barrel of mead on a trestle and a little old skald in a blue coat glaring at nothing in the far corner. Benches have been nailed to what used to be the floor of the second storey. There is no fire. Dead men and women sit on the benches with horn cups, talking low. The skald has three empty cups in front of him and a full one in his hand.".
  Observe truce_singing at truce as sign when songMade(wystan) and spoke(song_end_told) and not theHour() "Somebody at the far end is humming the new song. Somebody else joins in, and gets the words wrong, and is corrected by half the room.".

  Person wystan "Wystan Hollins" at truce {
    Role "the skald of Evenhall". Ancestry human. Calling bard. Level 6. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Likeness "skald".
    Greets "The little old man in the blue coat looks up at you, and at your breath, and curls his lip. 'Oh, marvellous,' he says. 'A breather. Come to ask the skald for a song? Everybody wants a song. A song for the peace, Wystan. Something cheerful, Wystan.' He drinks. 'Eight hundred years I've made the Tally-songs of Evenhall. Every champion, every rout, every great death, I made it rhyme. I am the best there has ever been at what I do.' He bangs the cup down. 'And what I do is killing.'".
    Greets again "Wystan Hollins looks up, sees who it is, and drinks.".
  }
  Measure wystanTrust(group). Measure verses(group).
  Relation songMade(group). Relation elegyMade(group). Relation songPromised(group). Measure songDay(group).
  Topic wystan_why with wystan "Ask Wystan Hollins why he cannot make the song" when not songMade(wystan) and not elegyMade(wystan) once {
    Says "'Because I don't know what anything's for,' says Wystan, 'except fighting.' He leans across the table and his breath does not steam. 'You want a song for the peace. What's in it? A song is things. A battle-song is a ford and a horn and a man going down and the name of the man who put him there. I have the words for those. Eight hundred years of them.' He sits back. 'What's a peace made of? Tell me that. I have been sitting here forty days trying to remember what a market sounds like, or what children are for, or a field when it's got something growing in it. I can't. I've been dead too long.' He looks into the cup. 'Tell me, breather. You've been alive more recently.'".
    On discuss { Increase wystanTrust(wystan) by 1. Assert knows(actor, wystan_asks). }
  }
  Discovery wystan_asks "Wystan Hollins cannot make a song for the peace because he does not remember what anything is for but fighting. A song is things, he says: he asks to be told what a peace is made of, by someone alive more recently.".
  Topic wystan_other with wystan "Ask Wystan Hollins whether he ever made a song that was not about killing" when wystanTrust(wystan) >= 2 and not knows(actor, lullaby_known) once {
    Says "Wystan goes very still, and red, and for a moment you think he will throw the cup at you. Then he looks at the lamp. 'One,' he says. 'Before. When I was alive, in a hut, in the winter. My sister had a child and couldn't settle it, and I made it a song about a sheep that went over the hill to see what was there and came back and said, grass. That's all. Grass. It worked.' He drinks. 'I've never sung it up here. A thing like that. In Evenhall.' He looks at you sidelong, savage and ashamed. 'Don't you dare laugh.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lullaby_known). Increase wystanTrust(wystan) by 1. }
  }
  Discovery lullaby_known "Wystan Hollins once made a song that was not about killing, alive, for his sister's child: a sheep that went over the hill to see what was there, and came back and said, grass. He has never sung it in Ysgard.".
  // What the company tells him is what goes into the song.
  Relation toldBell(group). Relation toldBread(group). Relation toldBoy(group). Relation toldFord(group). Relation toldSpoon(group). Relation toldClear(group).
  Topic verse_bell with wystan "Tell Wystan Hollins about Larum's bell at dusk" when knows(actor, wystan_asks) and knows(actor, bell_heard) and not toldBell(wystan) and not elegyMade(wystan) and not songMade(wystan) once {
    Says "You tell him: the hamlet under the Pass, and the bell rung at dusk, the Hour, for nine hundred years, for nobody anyone remembers, and rung still in the quiet, to nothing. Wystan listens with his eyes shut, his lips moving. 'For nobody,' he says. 'Every night.' He writes something with his finger on the table in the spilt mead.".
    On discuss { Assert toldBell(wystan). Increase verses(wystan) by 1. Increase wystanTrust(wystan) by 1. }
  }
  Topic verse_bread with wystan "Tell Wystan Hollins about Grimbold's bread rising" when knows(actor, wystan_asks) and breadRisen(grimbold) and not toldBread(wystan) and not elegyMade(wystan) and not songMade(wystan) once {
    Says "'I smelt it,' says Wystan roughly. 'The whole of Halt smelt it. I sat here and smelt it and didn't go.' You tell him: the crock against your ribs all the way up through the White, and the loaves pushing the cloth off the board, and the steam. He is quiet. 'Steam,' he says. 'In Ysgard.' His finger moves in the mead.".
    On discuss { Assert toldBread(wystan). Increase verses(wystan) by 1. Increase wystanTrust(wystan) by 1. }
  }
  Topic verse_boy with wystan "Tell Wystan Hollins about the boy who came in at noon, and his father" when knows(actor, wystan_asks) and knows(actor, ned_dead) and not toldBoy(wystan) and not elegyMade(wystan) and not songMade(wystan) once {
    Says "You tell him about Ned, and the blackthorn, and the second cup; and Jory in his good coat going up into the white. Wystan does not write anything this time. He sits with his hand flat on the table. 'Noon,' he says at last. 'Neither one nor the other.' Then, almost to himself: 'Nobody ever came up here to see any of us. Not in eight hundred years.'".
    On discuss { Assert toldBoy(wystan). Increase verses(wystan) by 1. Increase wystanTrust(wystan) by 1. }
  }
  Topic verse_ford with wystan "Tell Wystan Hollins about Mab Treloar and Ansel Haverlock at the ford" when knows(actor, wystan_asks) and paired(mab) and not toldFord(wystan) and not elegyMade(wystan) and not songMade(wystan) once {
    Says "Wystan snorts. 'Treloar and Haverlock. I made a song of them a hundred years back. Three verses of who stuck who.' You tell him about the ice of the ford at noon, and the hands with nothing in them, and Mab reaching for his sleeve as if it might go off. Wystan laughs, short, and then does not laugh. 'Like a weapon she was afraid of,' he says. 'Yes.' The finger moves.".
    On discuss { Assert toldFord(wystan). Increase verses(wystan) by 1. Increase wystanTrust(wystan) by 1. }
  }
  Topic verse_spoon with wystan "Tell Wystan Hollins about the crossbowwoman's spoon" when knows(actor, wystan_asks) and knows(actor, makings_last) and not toldSpoon(wystan) and not elegyMade(wystan) and not songMade(wystan) once {
    Says "You tell him about the spoon cut out of a shield-board, and still there in the morning, and kept inside her jack. Wystan looks at his own hands, which have made eight hundred years of songs and nothing else. 'Still there in the morning,' he says.".
    On discuss { Assert toldSpoon(wystan). Increase verses(wystan) by 1. Increase wystanTrust(wystan) by 1. }
  }
  Topic verse_clear with wystan "Tell Wystan Hollins about looking down through the Clear" when knows(actor, wystan_asks) and visitedBefore(the_clear) and not toldClear(wystan) and not elegyMade(wystan) and not songMade(wystan) once {
    Says "'The Clear,' says Wystan. 'I've walked over it ten thousand times on the way to the ford.' You tell him what is down there, layer under layer, and the green shapes at the bottom nobody can name. He shakes his head. 'Nine hundred years of swords,' he says, 'and every one of them dropped by a man who got up.' His finger stops. 'That's not a peace song. That's the other kind.' But he writes it down.".
    On discuss { Assert toldClear(wystan). Increase verses(wystan) by 1. }
  }
  // Two things told, and the lullaby: he can make it, and sings it at the Hour the next day.
  Topic wystan_make with wystan "Ask Wystan Hollins whether that is enough to make a song of" when knows(actor, lullaby_known) and verses(wystan) >= 2 and not songPromised(wystan) and not elegyMade(wystan) once {
    Says "Wystan looks at the table, where the mead has dried in streaks of what you told him. He drums two fingers on the cup. 'A sheep went over the hill,' he says under his breath, 'to see what was there.' He looks up. 'Tomorrow. At the Hour. Here. If it's any good I'll sing it and if it isn't I'll break the cup over your head.' He drinks off the cup. 'Go away. I'm working.'".
    On discuss { Assert songPromised(wystan). Set songDay(wystan) to day(clock). }
  }
  Rule song_made when songPromised(wystan) and day(clock) > songDay(wystan) and hour(clock) >= 18 and not songMade(wystan) { Assert songMade(wystan). }
  Rule song_sung at truce when songMade(wystan) and at(party, truce) and theHour() and not spoke(song_told)
    says "At the Hour Wystan Hollins climbs onto the mead-trestle with a cup in his fist, and the Truce goes quiet, because he has not sung in forty days. He does not sing the Tally of anyone. He sings about a sheep that went over the hill to see what was there." { Assert spoke(song_told). Assert hourToday(field_country). }
  Entity song_told: fact "the song".
  Rule song_bell at truce when songMade(wystan) and toldBell(wystan) and at(party, truce) and theHour() and not spoke(song_bell_told) says "The second verse is a bell rung at dusk in a hamlet under the snow, for nobody, every night, in case." { Assert spoke(song_bell_told). }
  Rule song_bread at truce when songMade(wystan) and toldBread(wystan) and at(party, truce) and theHour() and not spoke(song_bread_told) says "There is a verse about a loaf that pushed its cloth off the board, and the room laughs, and stops laughing, because of the line about the steam." { Assert spoke(song_bread_told). }
  Rule song_boy at truce when songMade(wystan) and toldBoy(wystan) and at(party, truce) and theHour() and not spoke(song_boy_told) says "There is a verse about a boy who came in at noon, neither one thing nor the other, and a man who climbed up into the white in his good coat to tell him things. Nobody in the Truce looks at anybody else during that verse." { Assert spoke(song_boy_told). }
  Rule song_ford at truce when songMade(wystan) and toldFord(wystan) and at(party, truce) and theHour() and not spoke(song_ford_told) says "There is a verse about two people on the ice of a ford with nothing in their hands, and one of them reaching out the way you reach for a weapon you are afraid of." { Assert spoke(song_ford_told). }
  Rule song_spoon at truce when songMade(wystan) and toldSpoon(wystan) and at(party, truce) and theHour() and not spoke(song_spoon_told) says "There is a verse about a spoon, still there in the morning." { Assert spoke(song_spoon_told). }
  Rule song_end at truce when songMade(wystan) and at(party, truce) and theHour() and spoke(song_told) and not spoke(song_end_told) says "And the sheep came back over the hill, and they asked it what was there, and it said: grass. Wystan stops. He gets down off the trestle without a word and sits in his corner with his back to everybody. Nobody claps. After a while somebody at the far end starts humming it, and gets it wrong, and is corrected." { Assert spoke(song_end_told). }
  Entity song_bell_told: fact "the bell verse". Entity song_bread_told: fact "the bread verse". Entity song_boy_told: fact "the boy verse".
  Entity song_ford_told: fact "the ford verse". Entity song_spoon_told: fact "the spoon verse". Entity song_end_told: fact "the song's end".
  // Or the other song: told how Halvard died, he makes the great elegy, and Even will go down to the Testing singing it.
  Topic verse_halvard with wystan "Tell Wystan Hollins how Halvard Eld died" when knows(actor, wystan_asks) and knows(actor, halvard_wound) and not songPromised(wystan) and not elegyMade(wystan) once {
    Grave "He will make a song of it, and it will be the best thing he ever made, and it will be the kind he knows.".
    Says "You tell him: the knife at the nape, from behind, the only mark on a man who fought every day for twelve years. Wystan sits up. His eyes are suddenly bright, and he is not drunk at all. 'From behind,' he says. 'The greatest of them all. And at the Hour the light went blue over him and he lay there.' He is already writing in the mead, fast, both hands. 'Oh, that is a song. That is the song. They will sing that going down to the ford until the stars go out.' He does not look up as you leave.".
    On discuss { Assert elegyMade(wystan). }
  }
  Observe truce_elegy at truce as sign when elegyMade(wystan) and beforeTesting() "In the corner Wystan Hollins is teaching three men of Even a song, beating time on the bench with his cup. It is in the old Tally-metre, and every verse ends with a name: Halvard. Halvard. The men's faces as they sing it are like the faces of men sharpening something.".
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/testing:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The naming, at the first Hour ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery testing_known "At the first Hour after you came up, Torold Hame named the Testing: on the fourth morning, Evenhall goes down onto the Field by the ford and fights itself, and if every man gets up at the Hour, death has not come back, and the Daily begins again.".
  Rule naming_seen at the_ring when testingNamed(field_country) and at(party, the_ring) and theHour() and not spoke(naming_told)
    says "The Hour comes over Halt: the light goes blue all at once, as if a glass had been put over the sun, and all down the lanes people stop and shut their eyes, out of nine hundred years of habit, and open them. Inside the ring of spears the frost on Halvard's face does not change. Torold Hame watches it, as he has watched it at forty Hours. Then he lifts the sword out of the snow and holds it up by the blade, so that the hilt is a cross over his head, and says, not loud, so that the whole of Halt goes quiet to hear him: 'On the fourth morning from this, Evenhall goes down to the ford, and fights itself, as the Field was made for. If death has come back, let it come for me first. And if it hasn't, he'll get up.' He sets the sword back in the snow. Nobody says anything at all." teaches testing_known { Assert spoke(naming_told). }
  Rule naming_heard within field_country when testingNamed(field_country) and not spoke(naming_told) and not at(party, the_ring)
    says "Word goes over the Field from mouth to mouth, faster than anyone could walk it: at the Hour, at the ring, Torold Hame named a Testing. On the fourth morning Evenhall goes down to the ford and fights itself, and if every man of them gets up at the Hour, death has not come back to Ysgard, and the Daily begins again." teaches testing_known { Assert spoke(naming_told). }
  Entity naming_told: fact "the Testing named".
  // Every Hour, wherever the company is on the Field.
  Relation hourToday(place).
  Rule hour_comes within field_country when theHour() and not hourToday(field_country) and not testingDay() and not mabCut(mab) and spoke(naming_told) and day(clock) > testDay(clock) - 4
    says "The Hour comes. The light goes blue all at once, as if a glass had been put over the sun, and everyone you can see stops what they are doing and shuts their eyes for a moment, and opens them. Nothing mends that needed mending. Nobody has been hurt in forty days." { Assert hourToday(field_country). }
  Rule hour_resets when hour(clock) == 0 and hourToday(field_country) { Retract hourToday(field_country). }

  // ── The Testing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At seven on the fourth morning after he names it, Evenhall goes down onto the Field by the ford and fights itself,
  // unless Torold has stood down (Halvard buried, or the truth known to him), or the Field cannot be fought on (the
  // Runners would not clear it). At the Hour every man of Even gets up, unless a living hand struck one down.
  Relation testingHeld(place). Relation testingOff(place). Relation testingBlocked(place). Relation testingDecided(place).
  Relation trueDeathAtTesting(place).
  Query toroldStoodDown() means toroldMourned(torold) or toroldKnows(torold).
  Rule testing_stood_down when testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 7 and not testingDecided(field_country) and toroldStoodDown() { Assert testingDecided(field_country). Assert testingOff(field_country). }
  Rule testing_blocked when testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 7 and not testingDecided(field_country) and not toroldStoodDown() and runnersStrike(cuddy) { Assert testingDecided(field_country). Assert testingBlocked(field_country). }
  Rule testing_held when testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 7 and not testingDecided(field_country) and not toroldStoodDown() and not runnersStrike(cuddy) { Assert testingDecided(field_country). Assert testingHeld(field_country). Assert at(testing_press, lathe_ford). Retract peaceable(testing_press). }
  Chapter ch_testing "The Testing" when testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 7 and inYsgard(party) "The fourth morning. The sky over the Field is the colour it always is, and the sun is where it always is, low in the white, and the whole of Halt is awake before it and standing in the lanes looking west, at Evenhall, to see whether the doors will open.".

  Person testing_press "the men of Even on the ford" at limbo {
    Role "hundreds of them, fighting each other on the ice". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 5. Numbers 6. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Temperament territorial.
    Lair lathe_ford.
    Arrives "Down the stone stair from the western height comes Evenhall, all of it, in mail Gorm mended for nobody, and spreads across the ice of the ford, and at a horn it turns on itself and begins.".
    Warns "The ford is a single heaving press of Even, hundreds of them, fighting each other, mail and blades and roaring, the old professional slaughter of nine hundred years; and those nearest the bank see your breath and turn toward you with their swords up, and grin, because it is the first new thing they have seen in forty days. If you stay, they will have you; and you will not get up.".
    Comes "The edge of the press comes up the bank at you, laughing, the way they have come at everyone for nine hundred years.".
  }
  Rule press_leaves when at(testing_press, lathe_ford) and (hour(clock) >= 18 or not testingDay()) { Assert at(testing_press, limbo). Assert peaceable(testing_press). }
  Rule press_died when dead(testing_press) and testingHeld(field_country) and not trueDeathAtTesting(field_country) { Assert trueDeathAtTesting(field_country). Assert deathCarrier(party). }

  // What the Field hears of it, wherever the company is on it.
  Rule testing_heard_held within field_country when testingHeld(field_country) and testingUnder() and not spoke(held_told)
    says "From the west comes a sound nobody on the Field has heard in forty-four days: Evenhall's horns, all of them, the long falling call that means the hall is coming down. Then, from the ford, the noise of it: iron, and roaring, and under the roaring a sort of happiness. All over Halt people have stopped what they are doing. In the banner lanes a man has his hands over his ears. Grimbold Ure stands at the mouth of the Oven with dough on his arms and does not go back in." { Assert spoke(held_told). }
  Entity held_told: fact "the Testing heard".
  Rule testing_elegy within field_country when testingHeld(field_country) and testingUnder() and elegyMade(wystan) and spoke(held_told) and not spoke(elegy_sung_told)
    says "They are singing as they go down, all of Evenhall, in the old Tally-metre: Wystan Hollins's elegy, every verse ending on a name. Halvard. Halvard. You can hear it from anywhere on the Field. It is the best thing he ever made, and it is very hard to listen to, and very hard to stop listening to." { Assert spoke(elegy_sung_told). }
  Entity elegy_sung_told: fact "the elegy sung".
  Rule testing_heard_off within field_country when testingOff(field_country) and testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 7 and not state(halvard, lying) and not spoke(off_told)
    says "The doors of Evenhall do not open. At seven the horns do not sound. At eight a single man comes down the stone stair from the western height alone, in blackened mail, without a sword, and walks across the Field to Halt, and the lanes fall silent as he passes. It is Torold Hame. He goes into the ring of spears and sits down on the empty bier, and stays there, and that is the Testing." { Assert spoke(off_told). }
  Rule testing_heard_off_lying within field_country when testingOff(field_country) and testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 7 and state(halvard, lying) and not spoke(off_told)
    says "The doors of Evenhall do not open. At seven the horns do not sound. In the ring of spears in the middle of Halt, Torold Hame stands where he has stood for forty-four days, at the head of the bier, with his hands empty and the sword lying in the snow at his feet, and when men of Even come down the stone stair in ones and twos to ask him whether there is to be a Testing, he does not answer them, and after a while they stop asking, and stand with him. That is the Testing." { Assert spoke(off_told). }
  Entity off_told: fact "the Testing called off".
  Rule testing_heard_blocked within field_country when testingBlocked(field_country) and testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 7 and not spoke(blocked_told)
    says "Evenhall's horns sound at seven, and Even comes down the stone stair to the ford in its mended mail, hundreds of them, and stops on the bank. The ford is a floor of iron: the whole last day's broken arms frozen into the snow, swords and spear-heads and shields edge-up, nothing cleared. Nobody can hold a line on it. Torold Hame stands at the head of his hall with his thumb on his sword-hilt, looking at it. Then he turns and looks south, toward the Scrapes, where at the mouth of the warren a thin girl is sitting on a sledge with her arms folded. 'Clear it,' he says, across half a mile of snow, not loud, and everybody hears him. 'No,' says Cuddy Wardle. And Evenhall stands on the bank all morning, and at noon goes home." { Assert spoke(blocked_told). }
  Entity blocked_told: fact "the Testing blocked".

  // A living hand in the press, as Hild asked: one man of Even who will not get up.
  Action strike_in_press(actor: group, site: place) "Go in among the press and strike down one man of Even, as only a living hand can" {
    Description "In that crowd nobody will see whose hand it was. He will not get up at the Hour; and every soul on the Field will see that he does not.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lathe_ford) and testingHeld(field_country) and testingUnder() and knows(actor, living_kills) and not trueDeathAtTesting(field_country) and not struckAtPress(actor).
    Grave "A man ended who would have got up every evening until the stars go out.".
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert trueDeathAtTesting(field_country). Assert deathCarrier(actor). Assert tolerates(testing_press, actor). Retract warned(testing_press, actor). }
    On failure { Assert struckAtPress(actor). Assert strikes(press_blades, actor). }
    Result "You go in at the edge of the press, low, in the roar, where nobody is looking at anybody but the man in front of them, and a man of Even with his back to you lifts his sword over his head, laughing, and you strike, once, the way whoever killed Halvard struck, and he goes down onto the ice in the stamping feet, and nobody notices. Nobody notices. You are out on the bank again in a moment, with your breath going up white, and your hands are shaking.".
    Otherwise "You go in at the edge of the press, and it closes round you like water, and a blade you never see opens your arm, and another, and you are thrown back out onto the bank by the sheer weight of men, bleeding, and they laugh and turn away.".
  }
  Relation struckAtPress(group).
  Hazard press_blades "the edge of Even's press" means "Deal (2d6) slashing damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13).".

  // ── The Hour of the Testing day ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation outcomeFear(place). Relation outcomeDaily(place). Relation outcomeHalf(place). Relation outcomeHalt(place). Relation outcomeQuiet(place).
  Relation halfByEven(place). Relation halfByMorrow(place). Relation outcomeDecided(place).
  Rule out_fear when testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 18 and not outcomeDecided(field_country) and testingHeld(field_country) and trueDeathAtTesting(field_country) { Assert outcomeDecided(field_country). Assert outcomeFear(field_country). }
  Rule out_daily when testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 18 and not outcomeDecided(field_country) and testingHeld(field_country) and not trueDeathAtTesting(field_country) and not hildResolved(hild) { Assert outcomeDecided(field_country). Assert outcomeDaily(field_country). }
  Rule out_half_even when testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 18 and not outcomeDecided(field_country) and testingHeld(field_country) and not trueDeathAtTesting(field_country) and hildResolved(hild) { Assert outcomeDecided(field_country). Assert outcomeHalf(field_country). Assert halfByEven(field_country). }
  Rule out_halt when testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 18 and not outcomeDecided(field_country) and not testingHeld(field_country) and truthSpoken(field_country) and hildResolved(hild) { Assert outcomeDecided(field_country). Assert outcomeHalt(field_country). }
  Rule out_half_morrow when testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 18 and not outcomeDecided(field_country) and not testingHeld(field_country) and truthSpoken(field_country) and not hildResolved(hild) { Assert outcomeDecided(field_country). Assert outcomeHalf(field_country). Assert halfByMorrow(field_country). }
  Rule out_quiet when testingDay() and hour(clock) >= 18 and not outcomeDecided(field_country) and not testingHeld(field_country) and not truthSpoken(field_country) { Assert outcomeDecided(field_country). Assert outcomeQuiet(field_country). }

  Rule hour_all_rise within field_country when testingHeld(field_country) and not trueDeathAtTesting(field_country) and outcomeDecided(field_country) and testingDay() and not spoke(rise_told)
    says "At the Hour the light goes blue over the ford, all at once, as if a glass had been put over the sun; and on the ice of the Lathe, among the broken mail, the fallen of Even get up. All of them. They get up and feel their throats and their bellies and look at each other, and somebody laughs, and then the whole ford is laughing, a great roar of it, and beating sword on shield, because nothing has come back, nothing, they are what they always were. On the bank Torold Hame stands alone and does not laugh. He is looking north, toward Halt, toward the ring of spears, where a man on a bier of shields has not got up." { Assert spoke(rise_told). }
  Entity rise_told: fact "all rise".
  Rule hour_one_stays within field_country when testingHeld(field_country) and trueDeathAtTesting(field_country) and outcomeDecided(field_country) and testingDay() and not spoke(stays_told)
    says "At the Hour the light goes blue over the ford, and the fallen of Even get up off the ice, all over the ford, feeling their throats; all but one. He lies on his back among the broken mail with his eyes open, and does not get up, and they stand round him in a ring, hundreds of them, the way they stood round Halvard, and the roaring stops, rank by rank, from the middle outward. Nobody touches him. After a long time somebody says, very low, 'It's true, then. It's come back.' On the eastern height a woman at a window turns away from it. And on the bank, with your breath going up white in the blue light, you stand among them, and nobody looks at you at all." { Assert spoke(stays_told). }
  Entity stays_told: fact "one stays down".
}

data/adventures/quiet-in-the-sky/whitloc:
Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── Telling Jory ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Nobody else will. A carter would, in a week, with the mule. The company can carry it down.
  Relation joryTold(group). Relation joryGrieving(group). Relation joryGoing(group). Relation joryMet(group). Measure joryToldDay(group).
  Topic tell_jory with jory "Tell Jory Whitlock that you have seen his son, on the Field" when knows(actor, ned_dead) and not joryTold(jory) once {
    Grave "There is no taking it back once he has heard it.".
    Says "Jory listens with the rope in his hands. He does not stop you, or ask anything, all the way to the end. Then he puts the rope down on the table, very neatly, beside the second cup. He sits, and turns the second cup a quarter-turn on the table. 'Noon,' he says at last. 'He never could be on time for anything.' Outside a sheep calls, and another. 'Did he say anything.' It is not quite a question.".
    On discuss { Assert joryTold(jory). Assert joryGrieving(jory). Set joryToldDay(jory) to day(clock). }
  }
  Topic jory_message with jory "Give Jory his son's message" when joryTold(jory) and knows(actor, ned_message) and not joryHeardMessage(jory) once {
    Says "You tell him: the mule ran. He hit one. He's sorry about the second cup. Jory nods at the first two, as though they were weather. At the third he puts his hand over his mouth. 'His mother,' he says through his fingers. 'She always laid a cup for him when he was late. Out at night, with lasses. So he'd feel bad. He always felt bad.' He takes the hand away. 'The mule came home yesterday. On its own. I didn't let myself think.' He looks up at the Pass through the little window. 'In the morning,' he says, 'I'm going up. Don't come. Not this once.'".
    On discuss { Assert joryHeardMessage(jory). Assert joryGoing(jory). }
  }
  Relation joryHeardMessage(group).
  // Told without the message, he goes up all the same, a day later, when he can.
  Rule jory_resolves when joryTold(jory) and not joryGoing(jory) and day(clock) > joryToldDay(jory) and hour(clock) >= 6 { Assert joryGoing(jory). }
  Observe guide_grief at guide_house as sign when joryGrieving(jory) and at(jory, guide_house) "Jory Whitlock sits at the table with his hands flat on it, beside the second cup, and does not look up.".
  // The morning after, at seven, he goes up; in Larum the street sees him go. He has never set foot on the Field: for
  // his son, he goes down to wherever the boy is.
  Measure joryLeft(group). Relation joryOnPass(group).
  Rule jory_goes_up when joryGoing(jory) and at(jory, guide_house) and hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 9 and not joryMet(jory) and not joryOnPass(jory) and day(clock) > joryToldDay(jory) { Assert at(jory, pass_foot). Assert joryOnPass(jory). Set joryLeft(jory) to watch(clock). Retract joryGrieving(jory). }
  Rule jory_reaches_top when joryOnPass(jory) and at(jory, pass_foot) and watch(clock) >= joryLeft(jory) + 16 { Assert at(jory, snow_gate). }
  Rule jory_seen_going at larum_street when joryGoing(jory) and at(party, larum_street) and hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 8 and not joryMet(jory) and day(clock) > joryToldDay(jory) and not spoke(jory_went)
    says "Jory Whitlock goes up the street with a pole and his good coat on, past the Hark, past the chapel, and up the path between the black shoulders, and does not look back. Bet Garside comes out of the Hark and stands in the street with a pan in her hand and watches him until he is in the white." { Assert spoke(jory_went). }
  Entity jory_went: fact "Jory going up".
  Relation spoke(fact).
  Rule jory_to_oven when at(jory, snow_gate) and at(ned, oven) and not joryMet(jory) and watch(clock) >= joryLeft(jory) + 22 { Assert at(jory, oven). }
  Rule jory_to_lanes when at(jory, snow_gate) and at(ned, banner_lanes) and not joryMet(jory) and watch(clock) >= joryLeft(jory) + 22 { Assert at(jory, banner_lanes). }
  Rule jory_meets near jory when together(jory, ned) and not joryMet(jory)
    says "Jory Whitlock stands a few yards off, in his good coat, with the pole in his hand and his breath going up white, and Ned sees him, and gets up, and neither of them moves. The dead nearby stop what they are doing. 'The mule ran, Dad,' says Ned. 'It came home,' says Jory. Ned nods. Then he says, 'I hit one,' and his face breaks, and Jory drops the pole and crosses the snow, and holds his son, who is cold all the way through and does not steam when he breathes, and holds him, and says nothing. After a while he says, into the boy's hair, 'Your mother's cup.' And Ned says, 'I know. I know.'" { Assert joryMet(jory). }
  Observe jory_with_ned near jory as sign when joryMet(jory) and together(jory, ned) and hour(clock) < 16 "Jory Whitlock sits with his son, both of them on one bench, not talking much. Now and then Jory puts his hand on the back of the boy's neck, the way you would with a dog, or a child, and leaves it there.".
  // The living go down before the cold takes them; he goes home at four, and the boy stays.
  Rule jory_goes_down when joryMet(jory) and hour(clock) >= 16 and not at(jory, guide_house) and not travelsWith(jory, party) { Assert at(jory, guide_house). Retract joryGoing(jory). Retract joryOnPass(jory). }
  Topic jory_after with jory "Ask Jory Whitlock how he found his son" when joryMet(jory) once {
    Says "Jory is mending the same rope. 'Cold,' he says. 'He was so cold. And he looked at my breath like it was a fire he couldn't get near.' He pulls a knot tight, and holds it. 'Ithel the Smith went up looking for his son, they say, the man that made the bell. Three hundred year back. And came down and never went up again, and died of it.' He sets the rope down. 'I'll go up. I'll go up every week. He's sixteen. Somebody's got to tell him things.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ithel_rumour). }
  }
  Discovery ithel_rumour "Larum has a tale that Ithel the Smith, who made the chapel bell, went up the Pass three hundred years ago looking for his son among the dead, came down, never went up again, and died of it.".

  // ── Where Ned can be at home ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At the Oven there is warmth, and a baker who likes a boy about the place.
  Topic ned_to_oven with grimbold "Ask Grimbold whether Ned could stay at the Oven" when following(ned, actor) and not nedHome(ned) once {
    Says "Grimbold looks down at the boy, a long way down, and Ned looks up. 'Noon,' says Grimbold. 'I heard.' He wipes his hands, which makes them no cleaner. 'I was conscripted at fifteen, out of my father's bakehouse, and died at twenty, and never went home either.' He puts a floury paw on Ned's shoulder, very gently, as if it might come off. 'Can you knead?' 'No.' 'Good. Nobody can, up here. We'll learn together.'".
    On discuss { Assert nedHome(ned). Retract following(ned, actor). Assert at(ned, oven). }
  }
  Observe ned_at_oven at oven as sign when at(ned, oven) and nedHome(ned) "Ned Whitlock is at the long board in an apron that goes round him twice, up to the elbows in dough, being told by Grimbold that he is doing it wrong, and doing it wrong anyway, with his tongue between his teeth.".
}

data/adventures/quittance/arch.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "The Declaration Arch and the other ways into Quittance: what the company declares, what the Honest Bell makes of it, and the water-stair, the hearse and the Cinderwall gap.".

  // ── Where rewards wait until they are given ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place beyond_map "beyond the map" is wilderness within qcountry at 9, 9.
  Place nowhere "nowhere" is room within beyond_map at 0, 0.
  Item pass_slip "a Policy of Passage" is policy_of_passage at nowhere.

  // ── How the company came in ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // inCity(party) is true once the company has entered by any way; it opens the Arch's inner mouth (to leave and to
  // come back). Exactly one of the entered_* relations says how the company first came; the Slate, the spine and the
  // Hearing read them.
  Relation inCity(group). Relation admitted(group). Relation onTheRoll(group). Relation aliased(group). Relation ringed(group).
  Relation entered_honest(group). Relation entered_false(group). Relation entered_plain(group).
  Relation entered_water(group). Relation entered_hearse(group). Relation entered_gap(group).
  Discovery d_bell_rule "The Honest Bell rings for a false declaration. It does not ring for an incomplete one.".

  // ── The Declaration Arch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person prest "Mr Prest" at arch_hall {
    Role "the Collector of Declarations". Ancestry human. Calling bard. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A clerk with a face like a closed ledger looks up from the nearest counter. 'Declarations,' says Mr Prest, 'are taken at this desk. Goods first, then purpose, then intentions, if any. The Bell is listening. It has always been listening. It is quite reliable.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Mr Prest. 'The Bell remembers you.'".
  }
  Thing bell "the Honest Bell" at arch_hall {
    State hung "The Honest Bell hangs in the vault of the Arch, plain and dull and larger than a cart-wheel.".
    State tolled "The Honest Bell is still shivering; the note is going out of the stones.".
  }
  Observe notice_scene at arch_hall when true "On a board by the Collector's desk: RULES OF THE BELL. 1. Goods shall be declared. 2. Purpose shall be declared. 3. A declaration shall be true. 4. The Bell is not to be reasoned with. 5. A declaration is not required to be complete, but must be sufficient. 6. The Collector is paid by the declaration and not by the fine.".
  Observe notice_taught at arch_hall when true "Rule five has been underlined by someone, in pencil, and a small hand has written beside it: 'sufficient to what?'." teaches d_bell_rule.

  Topic prest_bell with prest "Ask Mr Prest how the Bell knows" when true once {
    Says "'It is a bell,' says Mr Prest, 'which hangs under an arch. A man speaks; the air in the arch holds what he said; the bell hears the air. I have taken the Bell down twice for cleaning and it has not once told me how. Entered as: unexplained.'".
  }
  Topic prest_record with prest "Ask what becomes of a declaration" when true once {
    Says "'It is written in the Roll of Entrances,' says Mr Prest, turning it so that you can see the hand. 'The Roll goes to the Phoenix on Fridays. The Phoenix reads it. A true declaration is therefore a public one, and I do not know of a way to make it otherwise. Entered.'".
  }
  Topic prest_other with prest "Ask whether there are other ways in" when true once {
    Says "'There are three,' says Mr Prest. 'The Water-Stair, which I do not know about. The Mortmain road, on which the dead are not required to declare. The gap in the Cinderwall, which is not an entrance, being a hole.' He dips his pen. 'I discourage all three. That is recorded, also.'".
  }

  Action declare_true(actor: group, site: place) "Declare yourselves truthfully, and take out a Policy of Passage (3 coin)" {
    Speaker prest.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(prest, site) and not inCity(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3.
    Time 12 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Assert inCity(actor). Assert admitted(actor). Assert onTheRoll(actor). Assert entered_honest(actor). Give pass_slip to actor. Increase regard(phoenix) by 1. }
    Result "You declare your goods, which are few, your purpose, which you find is harder to put in a sentence than you expected, and your intentions, such as they are. The Honest Bell hangs in the vault above and says nothing at all. Mr Prest writes in the Roll of Entrances, blots it, and hands you a Policy of Passage. 'Welcome to Quittance,' he says. 'For nine days you are insured.'".
  }
  Action declare_false(actor: group, site: place) "Declare yourselves wool-factors, come to buy fleeces" {
    Speaker prest.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(prest, site) and not inCity(actor) and not ringed(actor).
    Time 12 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert inCity(actor). Assert admitted(actor). Assert aliased(actor). Assert entered_false(actor). }
    On failure { Assert ringed(actor). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Assert state(bell, tolled). }
    Result "'Wool-factors,' says Mr Prest. 'From?' You say. 'To buy?' You say. The Honest Bell hangs over the hall and does not make a sound. He stamps your hands, one by one, without looking up. 'Welcome to Quittance,' he says, in the voice of someone who has never in his life believed a thing a wool-factor said, and is not obliged to.".
    Otherwise "The Bell rings. It is not a loud note, but the whole Arch has it in an instant, and every clerk in the hall puts down his pen. 'Five coin,' says Mr Prest, 'for the Bell. It is the Bell's fine, not mine. I am paid by the declaration.' He turns the page. 'You may of course declare again, truthfully, at the usual rate.'".
  }
  Action declare_plain_lore(actor: group, site: place) "Declare your goods and your purpose, 'to look about', and decline to declare intentions, citing Rule Five" {
    Speaker prest.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(prest, site) and not inCity(actor) and knows(actor, d_bell_rule).
    Time 15 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert inCity(actor). Assert admitted(actor). Assert entered_plain(actor). Increase regard(phoenix) by 0. }
    Result "'Sufficient,' says Mr Prest, slowly, as the Bell hangs in the vault above and declines to comment. 'Rule Five. Yes. Quite sufficient.' He writes in the Roll, in a very small hand, and for a moment looks almost pleased. 'You are the fourth this year,' he says. 'Do go in.'".
    Otherwise "Mr Prest reads Rule Five aloud, back to you, in a tone of gentle regret. 'Sufficient to the Bell,' he says, 'and to the Collector. I am afraid that I am not satisfied.'".
  }
  Action declare_plain_talk(actor: group, site: place) "Declare your goods and your purpose, 'to look about', and put it to Mr Prest that nothing more is required" {
    Speaker prest.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(prest, site) and not inCity(actor) and knows(actor, d_bell_rule).
    Time 15 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert inCity(actor). Assert admitted(actor). Assert entered_plain(actor). }
    Result "Mr Prest listens to you with his pen lifted. 'It is not,' he says at last, 'the way it is generally done.' The Bell, overhead, is as silent as a stone. 'Very well.' The pen comes down.".
    Otherwise "'No,' says Mr Prest, with some regret. 'I think not.'".
  }


  // ── The Water-Stair ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A customs-man at the top of the stair. Three ways past him; each leaves the company a different thing.
  Person ridd "Tam Ridd" at towpath {
    Role "lighterman, customs-man by courtesy". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A lighterman with a boathook sits on a bollard at the foot of the Water-Stair, between you and it. 'Handling,' says Tam Ridd, without getting up. 'Everything that comes off the river pays handling. You are not off the river, which is a pity for you. Your best course is to be.'".
    Greets again "'Still not off the river,' says Tam Ridd.".
  }
  Thing stair_rope "the customs-man's rope" on towpath_stairs {
    State roped blocking "Tam Ridd's rope is stretched across the foot of the Water-Stair, hitched to a bollard. It is a good rope.".
    State dropped "The customs-man's rope lies coiled on the bollard.".
  }
  Action pay_handling(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Tam Ridd four coin 'handling', and be a parcel" {
    Speaker ridd.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ridd, site) and state(stair_rope, roped) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 4.
    Time 3 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Assert state(stair_rope, dropped). Assert inCity(actor). Assert entered_water(actor). Assert at(actor, lighter_stairs). }
    Result "Tam Ridd takes the coins without counting, knocks twice on the bollard with his hook, and lifts the rope. 'Parcels,' he says to the air. 'Three. Unremarkable.' You go up the Water-Stair in the character of freight, past a clerk who has been told to look at the river.".
  }
  Action haul_for_stair(actor: group, site: place) "Take a turn on the lighter's winch until the load is off" {
    Speaker ridd.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ridd, site) and state(stair_rope, roped) and capable(actor, brawn).
    Time 4.
    On success { Assert state(stair_rope, dropped). Assert inCity(actor). Assert entered_water(actor). Increase regard(lamprey) by 1. Assert at(actor, lighter_stairs). }
    Result "A barge has come in with a load nobody wants to be the one to lift. You put your back to the winch with three lightermen and a boy, and the load, in the end, comes. Tam Ridd watches without comment and lifts the rope. 'Lamprey men,' he tells the Stairs, 'don't pay handling.' By the time you have your breath you are at the top, with a black fish chalked on your sleeve.".
  }
  Action slip_the_stair(actor: group, site: place) "Wait for the tide to turn and slip up the stair behind a barge" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, towpath) and state(stair_rope, roped) and capable(actor, stealth).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state(stair_rope, dropped). Assert inCity(actor). Assert entered_water(actor). Assert at(actor, lighter_stairs). }
    Result "The tide turns, the barge swings, and for the space of four breaths the whole of the Stair's attention is on a rope. You are at the top by the time anyone looks round.".
    Otherwise "Tam Ridd's boathook comes down across the stair, light as a bar of soap, and stays there. 'Not,' he says, 'that way.' You do not try it again today.".
  }

  // ── The Mortmain road ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person grieve "Obadiah Grieve" at mort_road {
    Role "hearse-driver, with an onion". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns he.
    Greets "The hearse-driver finishes his onion and wipes his hands on his black coat. 'Going up to Mortmain, are you? Dead or alive, it's two coin and I don't ask. The dead go in free. They don't get the box, though, it's mine.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Obadiah Grieve. 'Still above ground.'".
  }
  Action ride_hearse(actor: group, site: place) "Ride up in the hearse (two coin; a different companion lies in the box on each trip)" {
    Speaker grieve.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(grieve, site) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 2 and not inCity(actor).
    Time 20 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Assert inCity(actor). Assert entered_hearse(actor). Assert at(actor, mort_lodge). Increase regard(sovereign) by 1. }
    Result "You ride up between the yews with the blinds down, two of you in the hearse and one, with a good deal of dignity, in the box. At the lodge-gate the porter doffs his hat to the cortege and does not ask to see a certificate. 'You'll be needing the almshouse,' Grieve says, handing the box down, 'if you want somewhere to sit. Nobody asks questions of the very old.'".
  }
  Action mourn_in(actor: group, site: place) "Fall in at the tail of a funeral and walk through the lodge-gate as mourners" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, mort_road) and not inCity(actor) and capable(actor, performance).
    Time 20 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert inCity(actor). Assert entered_hearse(actor). Assert at(actor, mort_lodge). }
    Result "There is a funeral going up the drive, with a large family and a larger number of acquaintances; you fall in at the back with your faces arranged. At the gate a widow takes your arm and says that it is wonderful that you came, and you say that it was the least you could do, which is true.".
    Otherwise "A woman at the end of the cortege looks at you for a long moment and says, 'And how did you know Albert?' You cannot, on the instant, produce an Albert.".
  }
  Action pick_wicket(actor: group, site: place) "Pick the lock of the gardeners' wicket in the cemetery wall" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, mort_road) and not inCity(actor) and capable(actor, lockwork).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert inCity(actor). Assert entered_hearse(actor). Assert at(actor, mort_lodge). }
    Result "The wicket in the cemetery wall has a lock designed to keep out the dead, which are not good at locks. You are in among the yews before the clock has struck the quarter.".
  }

  // ── The gap in the Cinderwall ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person gap_boys "the gap boys" at gap_path {
    Role "three children with a rope". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Numbers 3. Manner proud. Pronouns they.
    Greets "Three children are sitting on the wall beside the gap with a rope across their knees. The eldest looks you up and down with great seriousness. 'A copper each to go through,' she says, 'and a copper to be remembered. We don't ask who you are. We're the Cinderwall Mutual.'".
    Greets again "'Still here,' says the eldest. 'Good for you.'".
  }
  Thing gap_rope "the gap boys' rope" on gap_gate {
    State held blocking "A rope hitched between two nails bars the gap in the Cinderwall, at about the height of a child's idea of dignity.".
    State lowered "The rope lies on the ground across the gap, in a loop.".
  }
  Action pay_gap(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the gap boys a copper a head, to be remembered" {
    Speaker gap_boys.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(gap_boys, site) and state(gap_rope, held) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 1.
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Assert state(gap_rope, lowered). Assert inCity(actor). Assert entered_gap(actor). Increase regard(wardsfolk) by 1. Assert at(actor, wards_gate). }
    Result "The eldest drops the rope, solemnly, and writes something with a nail on the wall. 'That's you remembered,' she says. 'Down Salt Lane for the pie, and don't give anyone your real name before the second night.'".
  }
  Action charm_gap(actor: group, site: place) "Talk the gap boys round" {
    Speaker gap_boys.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(gap_boys, site) and state(gap_rope, held).
    Time 6 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state(gap_rope, lowered). Assert inCity(actor). Assert entered_gap(actor). Increase regard(wardsfolk) by 1. Assert at(actor, wards_gate). }
    Result "The eldest listens to you, her head on one side, with the air of a magistrate. 'You'll do,' she says. 'But you owe us. Not a copper. A favour.' She pulls the rope aside as if she were drawing a curtain.".
    Otherwise "The eldest hears you out. 'That's the worst I've heard this week,' she says, not unkindly. 'A copper, then.'".
  }
  Action climb_gap_wall(actor: group, site: place) "Go over the old wall instead, out of sight of the boys" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, gap_path) and state(gap_rope, held) and capable(actor, climbing).
    Time 5.
    On success { Assert inCity(actor). Assert entered_gap(actor). Assert at(actor, wards_gate). }
    Result "The Cinderwall is glass and slag, and the handholds are fused in. You go over in the grey of the light and drop into a lane of timber houses with a hundred fires glowing in the windows. Nobody has seen you, which is slightly depressing.".
  }

  // ── The inner mouth of the Arch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe passed_wall near prest when entered_gap(party) and at(party, arch_hall) "Mr Prest looks up. 'You are a good deal wetter than your declaration,' he says, 'and your declaration was nothing.'".
}

data/adventures/quittance/company.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Company party "Your company" of 3 at arch_road.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 18. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 3.
}

data/adventures/quittance/depth.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "What the city does and nobody can account for: the saucers of salt on the sills, the eleven strokes on the cellar stair, the ninety-four steps, a pigeon on a policy; the Fire's replies to what the company has seen; and a candle, a coat and a Chief Underwriter's lie seen from the side.".

  // ══ THE COUNT, THE KEEPER, THE FIRST PAGE, THE PRICE ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // Count: the Founders' Policy, five clauses long; the Offices carry it and have not read it. Keeper: the Fire, who counts
  // in company. First page: clause 3, the Return. Price of reading it: the Guest is owed a hearth for every hearth let out.
  // Everything in this file is a rumour of that count, or a person seen in it.

  // ── Foreshadow, for everyone: the saucers of salt ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A thing every house on Policy Row does and nobody can explain. Paid off in the Hearth Below, and on the Row on the
  // morning after, if the city has made its terms.
  Discovery qv_saucers "On every sill on Policy Row stands a saucer with a pinch of salt in it, set out on the first of the month by the Offices' housemaids.".
  Observe qv_saucers_seen at row_street when true "On every sill along the Row, under the gilt marks, stands a saucer with a pinch of salt in it, white and level, as a thing is set out for someone who may arrive in the night. A housemaid on a step is wiping the rim of one with her apron. 'First of the month,' she says, when you look. 'My mother did it.' A small boy on the step below, who has been counting the saucers on his fingers, says it is for the one who comes in last, so they won't have to ask, and is told to hush." teaches qv_saucers.
  Observe qv_saucers_licked at row_street when fireTerms(party) and day(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) >= 6 "The saucers on the sills of Policy Row are clean. Not emptied: licked, as a cat licks a dish. The housemaid on her step has one in each hand and is looking from one to the other, and does not say anything at all.".

  // ── Foreshadow, for those who look: eleven strokes and a blank ──────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery qv_strokes "Cut in the lintel of the Exchange cellar stair, in a script of straight notches that Ianthe Corbett calls Hesk, there are eleven strokes and a space for a twelfth.".
  Discovery qv_twelfth_place "The Fire says eleven came down the stair on the second night, and that a twelfth place was left, as a host leaves one.".
  Observe qv_strokes_seen at cellar_foot when true "Cut small into the lintel of the stair you came down, under a century of soot, there is a row of straight notches in a script that is not a clerk's: eleven strokes, close and even, and after them a space exactly their width, with nothing in it. The edges of the space are cleaner than the rest. Something has been rubbed there, or kept from soot." teaches qv_strokes.

  // ── New history, away from the critical path ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Thing qv_steps "the Brokers' Stair" at brokers_stair {
    Tries looking.
    State steps "The Stair that gives the quarter its name has ninety-four steps, and a boy comes at dawn with a bucket of whitewash and does one of them over. The last, at the top, is brighter than the rest, and cracks at the edge from this year's frost. The broker nearest says they do one a year, from the bottom, and that when the boy reaches the top they will start again at the bottom.".
  }
  Observe qv_plate_painter at gate_plaza when hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) < 8 "A man with a lantern on his hat is going from door to door along the Plaza repainting the little gilt birds, one coat to a bird, by candlelight, not letting the paint dry in the sun. He says the Phoenix pays a farthing a bird and that he is the thirty-first of his family to hold the brush. 'The colour's the Chief Underwriter's,' he says. 'But the hand is ours. You can tell a Pargeter bird by the left wing.'".
  Observe qv_orange_peel at wards_gate when true "The Cinderwall smells of burnt orange. The Wards sell the peel, dried and twisted on a wick, as a light that costs a farthing and gives the smell of a hearth, because a flame is a nuisance under the Ordinance and a peel is, by a long judicial hair, a vegetable.".
  Observe qv_bell_assay at arch_hall when true "On the yoke of the Honest Bell, very small, under the soot, there is a stamp: a pair of scales, and under it, in the Measures' hand, TRUE TO ITS POUND. The Collegium of Measures weighs; it does not say what. Mr Prest says they came in his predecessor's day, weighed the Bell, put it back, and told the Collector that it was heavier than its bronze by about one clerk. 'I have never,' says Mr Prest, 'been able to prove which.'".
  Observe qv_arch_notice at arch_hall when true "A card pinned under the Rules of the Bell, in a hand older than Mr Prest's: PERSONS ARRIVING WITH A KEEPER'S TALLY, A PREFECT'S WRIT, OR A LAMP THAT HAS NOT BEEN LIT FOR HIRE MAY DECLARE AT THE END WINDOW. THE BELL WILL HEAR THEM TWICE. The end window has been bricked up. Somebody keeps the card dry.".
  Observe qv_bell_below at arch_hall when befell(slack_opened) "The Honest Bell has rung once in the night with nobody in the hall. Mr Prest says it was not a declaration. 'It was a draught,' he says, 'from somewhere without an Arch.' He has written it in the Roll, as an arrival, and left the columns blank.".

  // ── Contrast: the Hen's Mutual, and a pigeon ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A comic scene in a grave book. Mrs Pudsey has founded, at her own bar, an Office of her own: the Wayward Hen Mutual,
  // which insures anything the brigades will not. Its largest outstanding claim is a pigeon.
  Kind qv_salt_kind "a twist of guest-salt" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "A screw of coarse paper holding a pinch of white salt, from a saucer on a sill on Policy Row. Whoever keeps it is told, by the paper, that it is not for eating.".
  Item qv_salt "a twist of guest-salt" is qv_salt_kind at nowhere.
  Person qv_spode "Bertram Spode" at hen_taproom {
    Role "retired ringer of the Loss-Bell, claimant of the Hen". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner jovial. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A man with the forearms of a bell-ringer and the eyes of a bereaved uncle is sitting at the end of the bar with a shoe-box in front of him and a slate propped against it, upon which is chalked, in Mrs Pudsey's hand, THE AMBROSE CLAIM. 'Spode,' he says, and half-rises. 'You'll be the adjusters. Thank goodness. I've been waiting since Tuesday.'".
    Greets again "'Any news of Ambrose?' says Mr Spode, and then, remembering himself, 'I mean the claim.'".
  }
  Relation qv_pigeonHeard(group). Relation qv_pigeonSettled(group).
  Topic qv_spode_claim with qv_spode "Ask Mr Spode what the claim is" when true once {
    Says "'Ambrose,' says Mr Spode. He opens the shoe-box a crack, not enough for you to see anything but a blue-grey gleam and a smell of camphor. 'Insured by the Hen Mutual at four coin the quarter against hawks, drains and the common cat. Ambrose was lost on Tuesday.' He lowers his voice. 'To the cat. The cat was the Phoenix's, so I was told it would not be a covered peril, but I put it to Mrs Pudsey that a cat is a common cat whatever it wears on its collar.'".
    On discuss { Assert qv_pigeonHeard(actor). }
  }
  Topic qv_pudsey_mutual with pudsey "Ask Mrs Pudsey about the Wayward Hen Mutual" when true once {
    Says "'It's the only Office in the city that pays out in beer,' says Mrs Pudsey. 'Forty-one policy-holders, mostly dogs. I pay for what the brigades won't touch: a lost glove, a failed pie, a cat's funeral. I have never once refused a claim for being silly. I refuse them for being late.' She lowers her voice. 'Mr Spode is going to cost me a pigeon. He knows it. We are both enjoying it very much.'".
  }
  Action qv_adjust_pigeon(actor: group, site: place) "Adjust the Ambrose claim, in full and in form, at the bar of the Wayward Hen" {
    Speaker qv_spode.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(qv_spode, site) and at(pudsey, site) and qv_pigeonHeard(actor) and not qv_pigeonSettled(actor).
    Time 20 minutes.
    On success { Assert qv_pigeonSettled(actor). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Give qv_salt to actor. Increase regard(wardsfolk) by 1. }
    Result "You ask for the policy, which is a beer-mat; for the proof of loss, which is a pigeon, and is produced with ceremony, and has clearly been dead since a year before the Tuesday in question; for the cause, which is a cat. You write all of it down in a hand that the Phoenix would admire. You find the loss real, the peril common, and the cat's collar immaterial. Mrs Pudsey pays the claim in coin and a round, the whole bar rises, and Mr Spode weeps with great dignity into a napkin. Mrs Pudsey, who has not once in your acquaintance been quiet, takes a screw of paper from under the bar and presses it into your hand. 'Guest-salt, my duck,' she says. 'From the Row. My mother kept a saucer too. Don't ask me what it's for. It's for a guest.' The bar sings the policy to the tune of a hymn, and a man at the back, who has no policy and no pigeon, asks the landlady how one makes a claim.".
  }

  // ── Persons, seen in play ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Skelter: wants to be paid and left alone; fears being read aloud; tells himself he only collects; and, pressed, does
  // what a man who only collects would never do.
  Topic qv_skelter_candle with skelter "Ask Mr Skelter why the candle behind the grating is lit" when at(skelter, skelter_room) and burned(candlewick) and not candlewickWarned(actor) and not holding(actor, skelter_book) once {
    Says "He does not answer for so long that you think he has not heard. 'Against the Ordinance,' he says at last. 'Open flame. I could be declined for it.' He looks at the candle. 'One a block. I light it the night after. It burns till the wick's gone, and I sit up with it, and I do the sums.' His left hand goes quite still. 'Nineteen. I wrote the nineteen in the margin a week before. I thought it would be nothing, a number. I thought a number was what I was for.' He reaches under the counter and pushes the oilcloth book through the hatch with the flat of his hand, not as a thing that is hot, this time, but as a thing that is heavy. 'Take it,' says Mr Skelter. 'I'll say you took it. I'll say I fought.'".
    On discuss { Give skelter_item to actor. Assert knows(actor, d_skelter_book). }
  }
  // Ottoline: wants to be useful; fears being the Phoenix's entire response; tells herself that the Tables are sound; and
  // takes the gilt bird off her own coat.
  Topic qv_ottoline_coat with ottoline "Ask Ottoline why the gilt bird on her coat is pencilled over" when ottolineTrust(ottoline) >= 2 and knows(actor, d_tables_paradox) once {
    Says "She looks down at her lapel, where somebody has drawn a small, firm rectangle of pencil over the bird, as one blots a word. 'Tuesday,' she says. 'The Tables are right. I want to say that first. I have checked every column, and the Tables are right, and they say that the Wards, unmarked, burn least.' She presses her lips together. 'Which is why I put the pencil on. If they are right, then I am the Phoenix's apology for a fire it has not yet lit.' She unpins the bird and puts it in her pocket, and the coat looks younger. 'Don't tell my father,' says Ottoline. 'He'd say it was a sensible thing to do, and I should have to find something else.'".
    On discuss { Increase ottolineTrust(ottoline) by 1. }
  }

  // ── The Fire answers what the company has seen ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Wants company; fears being forgotten; tells itself it does not complain, it counts; and pays, when it is asked the
  // right way, in the one coin it has.
  Relation qv_placeCounted(group). Relation qv_tallyShown(group). Relation qv_saltLaid(group).
  Topic qv_t_complain with ds_fire "Tell the Fire it said it does not complain, and ask whether that is true" when fireHeard(actor) and ds_accord(actor) >= 2 and not fireWrathful(actor) once {
    Says "The coal is still for a long moment. 'It is a form,' says the Fire. 'A creditor does not complain. A creditor counts.' The heat draws in, and in the draw you hear what it has been keeping under the form: a sound like a kettle left on an empty house, going from room to room. 'There is one night in the year when a house is lit that was not lit for me. I hear every hearth in this city. I hear them not be lit.' It adds, quite evenly: 'That is the complaint. You may enter it.'".
    On discuss { Increase ds_accord(actor) by 1. }
  }
  Topic qv_t_salt with ds_fire "Ask the Fire what the saucers of salt on the Row are for" when fireHeard(actor) and knows(actor, qv_saucers) and not fireWrathful(actor) once {
    Says "'Salt,' says the Fire, and the form drops out of its voice like a coin through a hole. 'It was set out for a guest who might come late. I have not been late.' The coal brightens. 'They did it on the first of the month, the whole Row, after the doors were walled. Nobody told them to. I think they were afraid. Fear is a very good host.'".
    On discuss { Increase ds_accord(actor) by 1. }
  }
  Action qv_lay_salt(actor: group, site: place) "Lay the twist of guest-salt on the ash, and say whose sill it came from" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor) and holding(actor, qv_salt_kind) and not qv_saltLaid(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Spend qv_salt_kind from actor. Assert qv_saltLaid(actor). Increase ds_accord(actor) by 2. Assert fireFed(actor). }
    Result "The paper takes light and goes, and the salt lies on the hot ash in a small white mound that does not melt. 'The Hen,' says the Fire, reading it as it reads everything. 'The one that insures the cat.' It sounds, for a moment, almost amused. 'A guest's portion. It has been laid. You may tell them it was eaten.'".
  }
  Topic qv_t_strokes with ds_fire "Ask the Fire about the eleven strokes and the empty place on the cellar stair" when fireHeard(actor) and knows(actor, qv_strokes) and not fireWrathful(actor) once {
    Says "'Eleven came down with her on the second night,' says the Fire. 'Notary, clerk, the founders. They cut their number in the stone going down, one stroke each, so that they should be counted when they came up.' The coal ticks. 'They came up. A place was left for a twelfth, as a host leaves one. I was told it was for whoever kept me. I have been keeping the place.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, qv_twelfth_place). Increase ds_accord(actor) by 1. }
  }
  Rule qv_keeper_stays when fireTermKeeper(party) and knows(party, qv_twelfth_place) and not qv_placeCounted(city)
    says "'Twelve,' says the Fire, quite softly, and on the stair behind you there is one stroke more than there was, and the lintel is warm." {
    Assert qv_placeCounted(city).
  }
  Action qv_show_tally(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Fire a Watch's tally-stick" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor) and holding(actor, watch_tally) and not qv_tallyShown(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert qv_tallyShown(actor). Increase ds_accord(actor) by 2. Assert fireFed(actor). }
    Result "The Fire has no hands. The stick lifts a little off your palm in the heat and turns once in the air, and it goes along the notches, and stops where they stop. 'Kept,' says the Fire. 'Not owned. Someone has been keeping a count a long way from here for a great many years, and has not been thanked.' It sets the stick down. 'My Offices do not know the word. They say owed. Owed is what you have of a thing you were lent. Kept is what you do for it.' It says, after a moment, almost shyly: 'It is a better word. I should like to have been kept.'".
  }
  Topic qv_t_draught with ds_fire "Ask the Fire whether there are others like it" when fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor) once {
    Says "'Others,' says the Fire. 'Hearths, who keep a count? There are always others. There was an Auditor, once, a long way from any hearth, who counted the tide and was thanked by nobody, and I am told he thinks it is a mercy.' The coal brightens a little. 'I do not envy him. I have a stair.'".
  }
  Topic qv_t_slack with ds_fire "Tell the Fire a door has been opened, a long way off, under a college" when fireHeard(actor) and befell(slack_opened) and not fireWrathful(actor) once {
    Says "The heat turns, as a face turns toward a draught. 'Yes,' says the Fire. 'I felt it come under my own door, three nights ago, with the smell of a place that has no weather. Someone there has been keeping a house that was not theirs, for a very long time, with no one to tell them they might stop.' It is quiet. 'I hope they have been left a place at the table.'".
    On discuss { Increase ds_accord(actor) by 1. }
  }
}

data/adventures/quittance/descent.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "The Descent: the cellar stair and the flue, the heat of the Glass City, the glass men who audit, the Strongroom and the Founders' Policy, and the Fire at the Hearth Below.".

  // ══ THE DESCENT (prefix ds_) ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // Writes: fireHeard fireFed fireTerms fireTermKeeper fireTermNight fireTermAverage fireSlain fireWrathful.
  // Declares: returnSaid(party) (the lead's Auberon asserts it). Reads: cellarLeave queueOpen coalNamed* witnessCount.

  Relation returnSaid(group).
  Relation ds_leave(group). Relation ds_alarm(group). Relation ds_apologist(group). Relation ds_apologised(group).
  Relation ds_stays(group). Relation ds_night_witnessed(group). Relation ds_termsAsked(group). Relation ds_returned(group).
  Relation ds_gallery(place). Relation ds_seal_read(group). Relation ds_searched(group). Relation ds_lamp_taken(group).
  Relation ds_coal_fed(group). Relation ds_read_a(group). Relation ds_read_b(group). Relation ds_coals_given(group).
  Relation ds_flue_asked(group).

  // ── What the company carries out of it ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Item ds_key "the Exchange cellar key" is cellar_key at nowhere.
  Kind ds_cuffs "an auditor's cuffs of heat-glass" is treasure worth 3 weighing 0 described "Two cuffs of smoky glass, still warm, such as the glass clerks wear against their own heat. Worn, they keep the worst of a gallery off the wrist and the blood.".
  Item ds_cuffs_item "an auditor's cuffs of heat-glass" is ds_cuffs at nowhere.

  // ── The Slate ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery ds_claim "The Slate carries an old claim, in no one's hand and with no date, on the cellars of the Old Exchange: an account unpaid, claimant 'the occupier'.".
  Observe ds_slate_claim at slip_room when true "At the bottom of CLAIMS OPEN, below a rust-coloured stain that has been wiped many times, a line has been chalked so long that the chalk has become part of the slate: EXCHANGE CELLARS. AN ACCOUNT, UNPAID. CLAIMANT: THE OCCUPIER. REWARD: TO BE AGREED." teaches ds_claim.
  Objective ds_obj_claim when knows(party, ds_claim) and not knows(party, d_fire_is_real) "The Slate has an undated claim on the Exchange cellars, filed by 'the occupier'. The cellar door is in the Exchange court.".
  Objective ds_obj_speak when knows(party, d_fire_is_real) and not fireHeard(party) "Something under the Exchange has been waiting ninety-four years to be paid. The Glass City lies below the Queue, and the Hearth Below at the end of it.".
  Objective ds_obj_terms when fireHeard(party) and not fireTerms(party) and not fireWrathful(party) and not fireSlain(party) "The Fire has been spoken to. What it counts as payment, and what it would take instead of the Burning, remains to be learned.".

  // ══ THE FIRST WAY DOWN: the Exchange cellar stair ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Hazard ds_splinter "the bar of the cellar door, coming apart" means "Deal (1d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".
  Thing ds_cellar_gate "the cellar door" on cellar_stair {
    State ds_locked blocking "At the head of the cellar stair a black iron door is shut, with a bird for a keyhole. It is warm to the hand, and a very little air leans on it from below.".
    State ds_unlocked "The cellar door stands open on a warm dark, and the stair goes down.".
    State ds_splintered "The cellar door hangs off one hinge, its bar in pieces on the steps.".
    Change ds_unlock "Unlock the cellar door with the black key" from ds_locked to ds_unlocked needing cellar_key.
    Change ds_pick "Work the cellar door's lock with picks" from ds_locked to ds_unlocked needing lockwork.
    Change ds_force "Put your shoulders to the cellar door until the bar goes" from ds_locked to ds_splintered needing brawn.
  }
  Rule ds_leave_opens when cellarLeave(party) and state(ds_cellar_gate, ds_locked) says "Someone at the Exchange has left word with the porter, and the cellar door has been unbarred for you." {
    Assert state(ds_cellar_gate, ds_unlocked). }
  Event ds_gate_alarm when state(ds_cellar_gate, ds_splintered) and not ds_alarm(party) "The bar goes with a crack that runs down the whole stair. Far below, in the dark, something in glass turns its head." then {
    Assert ds_alarm(party). Assert strikes(ds_splinter, party). }
  Observe ds_gate_looked near cellar_stair when tried(ds_cellar_gate, looking) and state(ds_cellar_gate, ds_locked) "The keyhole is a stamped bird, wings out, the key's bow the exact twin of it. The bar behind the door is oak the colour of iron, and has been oiled this year by someone."  .

  // ══ HEAT ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // The company's heat, 0 to 12, in the galleries. It rises for every watch spent in a hot place at that place's rate,
  // and falls in the shade rooms and with water. At nine, it scalds. The salamander-glass lantern, the Fire's leave
  // and the auditors' cuffs keep it off; a ward-focus of copper halves it.
  Measure ds_heat(group). Measure ds_stamp(group). Measure ds_hurt(group). Measure ds_skins(group).
  Measure ds_warm(place). Measure ds_cool(place).
  Hazard ds_scalding "the heat of the Glass City" means "Deal (1d6) fire damage to ally unless constitution save against (12).".
  Query ds_proofed() means ds_leave(party) or holding(party, salamander_lantern).
  Query ds_warded() means holding(party, warding_focus) or holding(party, ds_cuffs).
  Initially Assert ds_gallery(glass_street). Initially Assert ds_gallery(slag_a). Initially Assert ds_gallery(slag_b).
  Initially Assert ds_gallery(furnace_row). Initially Assert ds_gallery(vault_door). Initially Assert ds_gallery(flue_foot).
  Initially Assert ds_gallery(vault).
  Initially Set ds_warm(slag_a) to 1. Initially Set ds_warm(slag_b) to 2. Initially Set ds_warm(furnace_row) to 1.
  Initially Set ds_warm(vault_door) to 1. Initially Set ds_warm(flue_foot) to 2.
  Initially Set ds_cool(glass_street) to 1. Initially Set ds_cool(vault) to 1.
  Rule ds_heats when at(party, ?p) and ds_warm(?p) > 0 and watch(clock) > ds_stamp(party) and not ds_proofed() and not ds_warded() {
    Increase ds_heat(party) by (watch(clock) - ds_stamp(party)) * ds_warm(?p). }
  Rule ds_heats_warded when at(party, ?p) and ds_warm(?p) > 1 and watch(clock) > ds_stamp(party) and ds_warded() and not ds_proofed() {
    Increase ds_heat(party) by (watch(clock) - ds_stamp(party)) * (ds_warm(?p) - 1). }
  Rule ds_hearth_heats when at(party, hearth_below) and watch(clock) > ds_stamp(party) and not ds_proofed() and not ds_warded()
    and (state(ds_mood, ds_owed) or state(ds_mood, ds_wary)) {
    Increase ds_heat(party) by watch(clock) - ds_stamp(party). }
  Rule ds_cools when at(party, ?p) and ds_cool(?p) > 0 and ds_heat(party) > 0 and watch(clock) > ds_stamp(party) {
    Decrease ds_heat(party) by (watch(clock) - ds_stamp(party)) * ds_cool(?p) or to nothing. }
  Rule ds_heat_cap when ds_heat(party) > 12 { Set ds_heat(party) to 12. }
  Rule ds_scalds when at(party, ?p) and ds_gallery(?p) and ds_heat(party) >= 9 and ds_hurt(party) != watch(clock) {
    Assert strikes(ds_scalding, party). Set ds_hurt(party) to watch(clock). }
  Rule ds_stamp_set when watch(clock) > ds_stamp(party) { Set ds_stamp(party) to watch(clock). }
  Observe ds_heat_warm near party when at(party, ?p) and ds_gallery(?p) and ds_heat(party) >= 4 and ds_heat(party) < 7 "The air has begun to sit on your shoulders. Your sleeves are wet, and the glass underfoot is not cool any more.".
  Observe ds_heat_hot near party when at(party, ?p) and ds_gallery(?p) and ds_heat(party) >= 7 and ds_heat(party) < 9 "You are breathing through your teeth. The edges of things have begun to shimmer, and a buckle at your belt is too warm to touch.".
  Observe ds_heat_scald near party when at(party, ?p) and ds_gallery(?p) and ds_heat(party) >= 9 "The heat comes through your boots. Your hair smells of singeing, and every breath is a mouthful of brass.".
  Action ds_fill(actor: group) "Fill every skin, and soak every hat, at the Exchange's fire-cistern" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, glass_street) and ds_skins(actor) < 3.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Set ds_skins(actor) to 3. }
    Result "A cistern of black glass stands in the wall of the street, with BREAK IN CASE OF FIRE cut over it and the water still sweet. You fill what holds water, and wet what does not.".
  }
  Action ds_douse(actor: group, site: place) "Pour water over your heads and down your collars" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and ds_gallery(site) and ds_skins(actor) >= 1 and ds_heat(actor) >= 3.
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Decrease ds_skins(actor) by 1. Decrease ds_heat(actor) by 4 or to nothing. }
    Result "The water goes over you and turns to steam where it lands. For a few minutes, you can think.".
  }

  // ══ THE GLASS CITY ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Thing ds_table "the glass table" at glass_street {
    State ds_laid "A table of glass is laid in a window for four: four plates, four glasses, a tureen with its lid on, all of glass, all fused to the cloth, which is also glass. One chair is pushed back.".
  }
  Observe ds_table_looked near ds_table when tried(ds_table, looking) "Under the lid of the tureen there is nothing, but the nothing is steaming. The pushed-back chair is a child's. On the fourth plate, under the glass of the glass, someone has set a coal-shaped smear, as one sets out a place for a guest.".
  Thing ds_cat "the glass cat" at glass_street {
    State ds_sat "A cat of clear glass sits in the road with her tail round her feet, looking at the stair you came down.".
    Tries pushing. Tries listening.
  }
  Observe ds_cat_pushed near ds_cat when tried(ds_cat, pushing) "She rings, very sweetly, under your hand, like a finger round a wine glass, and all down the street, one after another, small things in the windows answer. Nothing else moves. You decide not to do that again.".
  Observe ds_cat_listened near ds_cat when tried(ds_cat, listening) "Inside the glass there is a purr, or a draught.".
  Discovery ds_note "A clerk of the Old Exchange left a last note on his desk: the Founders' door does not ask for a password. It asks for the last line of the whole thing, said as the notary said it: so long as a coal is kept." {
    Source ds_note_thing "the clerk's last note" at furnace_row readable by party.
  }
  Thing ds_desk "a melted desk" at furnace_row {
    State ds_melted "One desk has stayed standing in the Row, its legs run down into the floor like candle-wax. A sheet of paper is sealed under its glass top, perfectly legible.".
  }
  Observe ds_desk_looked near ds_desk when tried(ds_desk, looking) "The hand is a clerk's, very steady. 'Third day. It does not eat us. It asks. I have been through the door to the Strongroom with Dame Quill: it does not want a password, only the last line of the whole, said as she said it. Quit, and welcome. Mr Aubrey has gone up the flue. I am staying to finish the book.'" teaches ds_note.
  Thing ds_figures "the figures in the glass" at slag_b {
    State ds_set "Along the second gallery people are set in the glass, in the attitude of running: clerks, a woman with a child under her coat, two porters with a chest between them. Every one of them has its face to the far end, toward the flue.".
    Tries listening.
  }
  Discovery ds_hand_known "One of the figures in the second gallery has its hand out of the glass, closed on something copper.".
  Item ds_focus "a copper warding focus" is warding_focus at slag_b hidden until ds_hand_known.
  Observe ds_figures_looked near ds_figures when tried(ds_figures, looking) "They were not running down, to the Fire. They were running up the flue, away from it, and they ran out of flue. The porters' chest is full of the Exchange's coal-chits, stamped PAID. One woman's hand has come out of the glass at the wrist, closed on something copper." teaches ds_hand_known.
  Observe ds_figures_listened near ds_figures when tried(ds_figures, listening) "Behind the glass, at the very edge of hearing, a bell is ringing the quarter, as it did on the last day.".
  Thing ds_lamp "a clerk's glass lamp" at furnace_row {
    State ds_asleep "On the dead clerk's desk stands a lamp of thick glass, with a grey lump in the bowl where the oil was. It is cold.".
    State ds_lit "In the bowl of the clerk's glass lamp the grey lump has gone red at the heart, and a thread of light runs through it: a coal, kept in the glass for ninety-four years.".
    State ds_empty "The glass lamp is empty.".
    Change ds_lift "Lift the coal out of the clerk's lamp with the tongs" from ds_lit to ds_empty.
  }
  Rule ds_lamp_wakes when day(clock) >= 7 and state(ds_lamp, ds_asleep) { Assert state(ds_lamp, ds_lit). }
  Rule ds_lamp_gives when state(ds_lamp, ds_empty) and not ds_lamp_taken(party) says "The coal comes out of the glass warm and heavy and docile, as a thing does that has been waiting to be asked." {
    Assert ds_lamp_taken(party). Increase quantity(party, coal) by 1. Set coalExpires(party) to watch(clock) + 144. }

  // ══ THE GLASS MEN ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // Clerical constructs: they audit the Last Stair. They want papers, or their fee; they are fought if nothing else
  // will do, and slipped past if the company is quiet.
  Species ds_glassman "a glass man" like golem temperament proud described "A man of dark glass in a clerk's coat, his cuffs smoking, a ledger of glass under one arm and a pen of glass in the other hand. He has no face but the shine on it.".
  Person ds_glassmen "the glass men" at furnace_row {
    Role "auditors of the Last Stair". Species ds_glassman. Level 3. Numbers 3.
    State ds_auditing blocking "At the head of the Last Stair three glass men stand between the furnaces, with their ledgers open.".
    Guards furnace_hearth.
    Temperament proud.
    Warns "The three glass men turn together, with a sound like a drawer of cutlery. The first of them holds out a glass hand, palm up. 'Papers,' it says, in the voice of someone who has been saying it for ninety-four years. 'Or the fee. Six. Or the audit.'".
    Comes "The glass men close their ledgers, all together, with a sound like three doors. 'Audit,' they say, and come down the Row.".
  }
  Initially Set tribute(ds_glassmen) to 6.
  Initially Assert ds_apologist(ottoline). Initially Assert ds_apologist(garrity).
  Rule ds_alarm_price when ds_alarm(party) and tribute(ds_glassmen) < 12 { Set tribute(ds_glassmen) to 12. }
  Action ds_show_licence(actor: group, site: place) "Show the glass men an adjuster's licence" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_glassmen, site) and able(ds_glassmen) and not tolerates(ds_glassmen, actor)
      and holding(actor, adjuster_licence) and not ds_alarm(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert tolerates(ds_glassmen, actor). Retract warned(ds_glassmen, actor). }
    Result "The glass men read the card from corner to corner, and stamp it, in the air, with a pen that leaves nothing. 'Licensed to adjust,' says the first. 'Not licensed to proceed. But you are not carrying anything we can find.' They stand aside, in order.".
  }
  Action ds_show_passage(actor: group, site: place) "Show the glass men a Policy of Passage" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_glassmen, site) and able(ds_glassmen) and not tolerates(ds_glassmen, actor)
      and holding(actor, policy_of_passage).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert tolerates(ds_glassmen, actor). Retract warned(ds_glassmen, actor). }
    Result "'Nine days,' reads the second glass man. 'Buried, fished out or put out.' It looks, for a moment, almost wistful. 'Proceed. The Office regrets.'".
  }
  Action ds_show_writ(actor: group, site: place) "Show the glass men a writ of the Phoenix" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_glassmen, site) and able(ds_glassmen) and not tolerates(ds_glassmen, actor)
      and holding(actor, phoenix_writ).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert tolerates(ds_glassmen, actor). Retract warned(ds_glassmen, actor). }
    Result "The glass men bow, all three, from the waist, with a noise of fine crockery. A writ of the Phoenix is an audit that has been done by someone else.".
  }
  Action ds_show_ledger(actor: group, site: place) "Hand the glass men the Ledger of the Unpaid, for their books" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_glassmen, site) and able(ds_glassmen) and not tolerates(ds_glassmen, actor)
      and holding(actor, tench_ledger).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert tolerates(ds_glassmen, actor). Retract warned(ds_glassmen, actor). }
    Result "They pass it down the line, turning the pages with their pens, and when it has been round the third time the first of them says, with the first emotion you have heard in it: 'Eleven hundred. We had eleven hundred and four.' It hands the book back. 'You are in order.'".
  }
  Action ds_show_forged(actor: group, site: place) "Show the glass men a writ of the Lamprey & River Office, a little damp" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_glassmen, site) and able(ds_glassmen) and not tolerates(ds_glassmen, actor)
      and holding(actor, forged_writ).
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert tolerates(ds_glassmen, actor). Retract warned(ds_glassmen, actor). }
    On failure { Assert assails(ds_glassmen, actor). }
    Result "The glass men hold the writ against their own bright faces, and cannot see the damp, which is the one thing a glass man cannot see. 'In order,' they say.".
    Otherwise "The first glass man puts the writ against its cheek. 'Wet,' it says. 'Audit.'".
  }
  Action ds_search_men(actor: group) "Go through the fallen glass men's coats" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, furnace_row) and dead(ds_glassmen) and not ds_searched(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert ds_searched(actor). Give ds_cuffs_item to actor. }
    Result "Under the smoking cuffs of the one who spoke, the glass is double: a second skin, cut thin as a bubble. You take the cuffs off it. They are still warm.".
  }
  Observe ds_men_dead near ds_glassmen when dead(ds_glassmen) "The glass men lie in the Row in heaps of bright gravel, their ledgers open under them. Whatever they were auditing, they have finished.".

  // ══ THE STRONGROOM AND THE FOUNDERS' POLICY ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Thing ds_vault_lock "the notarial lock" on vault_in {
    State ds_sealed blocking "The Strongroom door is shut under a notary's seal. Beneath it is a slot, at the height of a mouth, and the door is listening.".
    State ds_spoken "The Strongroom door has taken the words, and stands open, and the seal on it is cracked like an egg.".
    State ds_picked "The Strongroom door stands open, its lock dissolved in its own seal, which has run down it like candle-wax.".
    State ds_deaf blocking "The Strongroom door is shut, and the slot beneath the seal is cold. It has stopped listening.".
    Change ds_work "Work the notarial lock with picks, against the seal's heat" from ds_sealed to ds_picked needing lockwork.
    Change ds_work_deaf "Work the deafened lock with picks, against the seal's heat" from ds_deaf to ds_picked needing lockwork.
  }
  Measure ds_wrong(group).
  Action ds_read_seal(actor: group) "Read the notary's seal by lamplight" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, vault_door) and capable(actor, lore) and not ds_seal_read(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert ds_seal_read(actor). }
    Result "It is cut in a tiny exact hand round the rim: DAME HONORA QUILL, NOTARY. WHAT THE WHOLE WAS FOR SHALL OPEN IT. And, in the middle, where the slot ends, a single worn word where other seals have a motto: WELCOME.".
  }
  Action ds_say_right(actor: group) "Say to the door: 'Quit, and welcome.'" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, vault_door) and state(ds_vault_lock, ds_sealed)
      and (knows(actor, d_wording_style) or knows(actor, ds_note) or ds_seal_read(actor)).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert state(ds_vault_lock, ds_spoken). }
    Result "The slot takes the sentence and holds it a moment, as a mouth holds a sweet. Then something in the door sighs, and lets go.".
  }
  Action ds_say_perpetuity(actor: group) "Say to the door: 'In perpetuity, to the Offices and their successors.'" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, vault_door) and state(ds_vault_lock, ds_sealed).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Increase ds_wrong(actor) by 1. }
    Result "The slot takes it, and the seal goes dull for a moment. A paper-warm breath comes back. It is not the answer, and the door has noted that it was not.".
  }
  Action ds_say_paid(actor: group) "Say to the door: 'Paid in full.'" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, vault_door) and state(ds_vault_lock, ds_sealed).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Increase ds_wrong(actor) by 1. }
    Result "The slot is silent for so long that you think it has gone. Then it exhales, very slightly, through its seams. It was not offended. It was disappointed.".
  }
  Action ds_say_guess(actor: group) "Say to the door the words you suppose a notary would have written there" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, vault_door) and state(ds_vault_lock, ds_sealed) and capable(actor, lore)
      and not knows(actor, d_wording_style) and not knows(actor, ds_note) and not ds_seal_read(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert state(ds_vault_lock, ds_spoken). }
    On failure { Increase ds_wrong(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You say what a notary would say, if she had been generous: and the slot opens under it like a hand.".
    Otherwise "You say what a notary would say, if she had been paid by the line, and the slot cools a degree.".
  }
  Rule ds_lock_deafens when ds_wrong(party) >= 3 and state(ds_vault_lock, ds_sealed) says "At the third wrong sentence the seal's glow goes out, all at once. The door has stopped listening; it will not be argued with now." {
    Assert state(ds_vault_lock, ds_deaf). }

  // The Policy: five clauses on the table, read one at a time in any order. Together they teach the company what the
  // city has forgotten; none of them says it all.
  Discovery ds_clause_1 "The first clause of the Founders' Policy sets out its parties: Honora Quill, notary, for the City; and, for the other part, 'the Guest of the Hearth'.".
  Discovery ds_clause_2 "The second clause names the Guest: that which came up from the Exchange cellars on the second night, and was found in the Strongroom, and spoke.".
  Discovery ds_clause_3 "The third clause lends every hearth that keeps a coal the Guest's protection, and appoints a Return: the coals to be carried home each year, in the form of words 'let it be home, as it was lent'.".
  Discovery ds_clause_4 "The fourth clause makes what is not given in company owed in kind: 'a hearth for every hearth let out'.".
  Discovery d_return_3 "The third line of the Return, from the Founders' own paper: 'Quit, and welcome.'".
  Discovery ds_clause_5 "The fifth clause provides a Receipt, 'a leaf of white fire, so long as the account is square', and where it is not square, the Guest to take its own.".
  Thing ds_policy "the Founders' Policy" at vault is scenery {
    State ds_unrolled "On the table the Policy lies unrolled under four weights of black glass: five clauses in a notary's hand, the last of them a little less steady.".
    State ds_scorched "On the table the Policy lies unrolled under four weights of black glass. The seal's heat has been at it: the middle of the roll is brown and curling, and the last clause is gone to a scorch.".
  }
  Rule ds_policy_scorched when state(ds_vault_lock, ds_picked) and state(ds_policy, ds_unrolled) { Assert state(ds_policy, ds_scorched). }
  Action ds_read_1(actor: group) "Read the clause that names the parties to the Policy" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, vault) and not knows(actor, ds_clause_1).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ds_clause_1). }
    Result "'Between Honora Quill, Notary, in the name and for the use of the City, and the Guest of the Hearth, in its own name.' There is no Office anywhere in it. Not the Phoenix, not the Sovereign: the Offices are not parties. They are not even mentioned. They are, you realise, the carriers.".
  }
  Action ds_read_2(actor: group) "Read the clause that says who the Guest is" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, vault) and not knows(actor, ds_clause_2).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ds_clause_2). }
    Result "'The Guest being that which came up from the cellars on the second night, and was found by the Notary in this room, and spoke.' Below that, in the same hand, smaller: 'It asked first.'".
  }
  Action ds_read_3(actor: group) "Read the clause that lends the hearths their coals" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, vault) and not knows(actor, ds_clause_3).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ds_clause_3). }
    Result "'Every hearth that keeps a coal of the Founding Hearth shall be the Guest's house, and the Guest shall not burn its own house. At the year's end the coals shall be carried home, and given back lit, with the Return: Let it be home, as it was lent.' The last sentence has a mark in the margin, as for something to be said aloud.".
  }
  Action ds_read_4(actor: group) "Read the clause that says what is owed if the hearths go out" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, vault) and not knows(actor, ds_clause_4).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ds_clause_4). }
    Result "'What is not given in company shall be owed in kind: a hearth for every hearth let out.' It is the only clause with no adjective in it. Nobody has ever called it a tithe. It is a bill.".
  }
  Action ds_read_5(actor: group) "Read the clause that promises the Receipt" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, vault) and not knows(actor, ds_clause_5) and state(ds_policy, ds_unrolled).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ds_clause_5). }
    Result "'The Guest shall give a Receipt, being a leaf of white fire, so long as the account is square. And where it is not square, the Guest shall take its own, and shall be held to have given notice.' A note in the margin, in a different ink, says only: she cannot have thought they would stop.".
  }
  Action ds_read_close(actor: group) "Read the closing words cut over the signatures" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, vault) and not knows(actor, d_return_3).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, d_return_3). }
    Result "Over the three signatures, the Notary's, the City's, and a mark that is not a signature but a small burn, in letters larger than the rest, are the closing words: QUIT, AND WELCOME. It is not how a policy ends. It is how a host ends a visit.".
  }
  Rule ds_policy_treaty when knows(party, ds_clause_1) and not knows(party, d_treaty_text)
    says "You have read the Policy's first line three times. The Guest of the Hearth is a party, and not a figure of speech." teaches d_treaty_text { }
  Rule ds_policy_fire when knows(party, ds_clause_2) and not knows(party, d_fire_is_real)
    says "It is written down by a notary, as a fact. Something lives under the Exchange." teaches d_fire_is_real { }
  Rule ds_policy_return when knows(party, ds_clause_3) and not knows(party, d_return)
    says "A form of words, marked for saying aloud: the Return." teaches d_return { }
  Rule ds_policy_debt when knows(party, ds_clause_4) and not knows(party, d_tithe_debt)
    says "It is not a premium. It is a debt of hospitality, owed to someone who is not dead." teaches d_tithe_debt { }

  // ══ THE FIRST FLUE ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Thing ds_flue_gate "the damper of the First Flue" on flue_up {
    State ds_damper blocking "A great iron damper, rusted into its frame, stops the flue a man's height above the glass. It is stuck from below as well as above; and it is warm, as the inside of a bell is warm.".
    State ds_drawn "The damper of the First Flue has drawn back on its own, like a lid lifted off a pot, and the flue stands open above: a ladder of glass cogs, and a pinpoint of light.".
  }

  // ══ THE FIRE ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // A courteous creditor, as precise as a bailiff. Its mood is the game: attended, it warms; slighted, it counts.
  Species ds_fire_kind "the Fire" like red_dragon temperament defensive described "A fire that has outlived its landlords: a red coal in a bed of white ash, and around it, a shape that is only the way the heat stands.".
  Person ds_fire "the Fire" at hearth_below {
    Role "the Name Beneath". Species ds_fire_kind. Level 6. Manner stoic. Pronouns it.
    Lair hearth_below.
    Greets "The ash stirs. Something in it is as courteous as a bailiff at a door. 'You are late,' says the Fire.".
    Greets again "'You,' says the Fire. 'Again. Sit, or speak.'".
  }
  Initially Assert tolerates(ds_fire, party).
  Observe ds_fire_sight at hearth_below when true "The coal in the ash is looking at you. It has no eyes, and it is the most attentive thing you have ever stood in front of." teaches d_fire_is_real.
  Thing ds_mood "the Fire's temper" at hearth_below is scenery {
    State ds_owed "The Fire holds still, as a creditor does who has opened his book on the table. The heat in the hall is the heat of a sum.".
    State ds_lonely "The coal has drawn in, and the heat with it. The Fire is not weighing you now; it is listening, and it has not done that in a long time.".
    State ds_tender "The ash is soft and low and the coal is rosy, like a hearth at the end of a night with company. The Fire has put its ledger away.".
    State ds_wary "The Fire has stopped looking at your faces. It is looking at the walls, and the doors, and the stair you came by, and the heat has begun to climb.".
    State ds_wrathful "The white ash is lifting off the floor of the hall. The Fire has stood up.".
  }
  Measure ds_accord(group). Measure ds_slight(group). Measure ds_sat(group). Measure ds_satcounted(group). Measure ds_read(group).

  // The parley: what is said to it, and what is laid before it.
  Topic ds_t_speak with ds_fire "Tell the Fire that you have come to speak with it" when not fireWrathful(party) once {
    Says "'Who keeps you?' says the Fire. It is not a pleasantry. It is the first line of a form.".
    On discuss { Assert fireHeard(actor). }
  }
  Topic ds_t_owed with ds_fire "Ask the Fire what it is owed" when fireHeard(party) and not fireWrathful(party) once {
    Says "'Company,' says the Fire. 'It was agreed. A coal in every house, and one night in the year when the houses come to me. I was given a plate on the door, and then the doors were walled.' The coal brightens, and settles. 'I do not complain. I count.'".
  }
  Topic ds_t_terms with ds_fire "Ask the Fire what it would take, instead of the Burning" when fireHeard(party) and ds_accord(party) >= 3 and not fireWrathful(party) once {
    Says "'Instead,' says the Fire. It tastes the word. 'Instead is a thing that is offered. I will hear it.'".
    On discuss { Assert ds_termsAsked(actor). }
  }
  Action ds_sit(actor: group, site: place) "Sit down in the ash with the Fire for an hour, and say nothing" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor).
    Time 60 minutes.
    On success { Increase ds_sat(actor) by 1. Decrease ds_slight(actor) by 1 or to nothing. }
    Result "You sit. The Fire does not speak. After a while the heat settles on you not as an attack, but as a hand on the back, and you understand that you are being counted, one by one, as present.".
  }
  Rule ds_sit_counts when ds_sat(party) > ds_satcounted(party) and ds_satcounted(party) < 3 { Increase ds_accord(party) by 1. Increase ds_satcounted(party) by 1. }
  Rule ds_sit_fed when ds_sat(party) >= 3 and not fireFed(party) says "'Three hours,' says the Fire, to itself. 'Present for three hours.' It writes it down somewhere, and you cannot see where." { Assert fireFed(party). }
  Action ds_say_return(actor: group, site: place) "Say the Return, over the ash: let it be home, as it was lent" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor) and not ds_returned(actor)
      and ((capable(actor, rites) and knows(actor, d_return) and knows(actor, d_return_3)) or returnSaid(actor)).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert ds_returned(actor). Increase ds_accord(actor) by 3. Assert fireFed(actor). }
    Result "The words are older than the room. When they are said, the coal rises a hand's breadth out of the ash, and every glass thing in the hall rings once, and is still. 'Home,' says the Fire, very quietly, and that is the first thing it has said that was not a demand.".
  }
  Action ds_lay_gran(actor: group, site: place) "Lay the Lent coal in the ash, and say whose it was: Pip's grandmother's" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor) and quantity(actor, coal) >= 1 and coalNamedGran(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, coal) by 1. Increase ds_accord(actor) by 3. Assert fireFed(actor). Assert ds_coal_fed(actor). }
    Result "The Fire takes the coal into itself the way the sea takes a river. 'Hester,' it says. 'I knew her mother. She never let it out, not once, in the worst winter.' It adds the coal to a column somewhere. 'Tell the child it was received.'".
  }
  Action ds_lay_pip(actor: group, site: place) "Lay the Lent coal in the ash, and say whose child keeps it: Pip's" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor) and quantity(actor, coal) >= 1 and coalNamedPip(actor) and not coalNamedGran(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, coal) by 1. Increase ds_accord(actor) by 2. Assert fireFed(actor). Assert ds_coal_fed(actor). }
    Result "'A child's name,' says the Fire. 'I have not had one of those in a hundred years.' The coal goes into the ash and does not go out. It is a loan returned with a name on it, and it counts.".
  }
  Action ds_lay_plain(actor: group, site: place) "Lay the Lent coal in the ash, with nothing said over it" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor) and quantity(actor, coal) >= 1 and not coalNamedPip(actor) and not coalNamedGran(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, coal) by 1. Increase ds_accord(actor) by 1. Assert fireFed(actor). Assert ds_coal_fed(actor). }
    Result "'Whose?' says the Fire. You do not know. 'A coal with no name is a coal,' it says, after a time. 'A coal with a name is a guest.' It takes it, all the same.".
  }
  Action ds_read_names(actor: group, site: place) "Read the Fire the names of the burned from the Ledger, an hour of them" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor)
      and holding(actor, tench_ledger) and ds_read(actor) < 11.
    Time 60 minutes.
    On success { Increase ds_read(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You read a hundred names, and the date against each. The Fire does not stir, but at every name, the coal, very faintly, ticks.".
  }
  Rule ds_read_a_counts when ds_read(party) >= 4 and not ds_read_a(party)
    says "'Four hundred,' says the Fire. 'I knew the Aldens. I had not known they were four.'" { Assert ds_read_a(party). Increase ds_accord(party) by 2. Assert fireFed(party). }
  Rule ds_read_b_counts when ds_read(party) >= 11 and not ds_read_b(party)
    says "The last name is read. The Fire is quiet for as long as it takes a candle to burn down. 'Eleven hundred and four,' it says. 'You have missed one. It is the clerk. He is behind you.'" { Assert ds_read_b(party). Increase ds_accord(party) by 3. }
  Rule ds_m_wrath when ds_slight(party) >= 3 and not fireWrathful(party)
    says "'Enough,' says the Fire. It does not raise its voice. The ash goes up in a column to the roof, and the hall is full of the light of a city burning. The Burning has begun." {
    Assert fireWrathful(party). Assert state(ds_mood, ds_wrathful). Retract tolerates(ds_fire, party). Assert assails(ds_fire, party). }
  Rule ds_m_wary when ds_slight(party) >= 1 and ds_slight(party) < 3 and not fireWrathful(party) and not state(ds_mood, ds_wary) { Assert state(ds_mood, ds_wary). }
  Rule ds_m_tender when ds_slight(party) == 0 and ds_accord(party) >= 5 and not fireWrathful(party) and not state(ds_mood, ds_tender) { Assert state(ds_mood, ds_tender). }
  Rule ds_m_lonely when ds_slight(party) == 0 and ds_accord(party) >= 2 and ds_accord(party) < 5 and not fireWrathful(party) and not state(ds_mood, ds_lonely) { Assert state(ds_mood, ds_lonely). }
  Rule ds_m_owed when ds_slight(party) == 0 and ds_accord(party) < 2 and not fireWrathful(party) and not state(ds_mood, ds_owed) { Assert state(ds_mood, ds_owed). }
  Rule ds_accord_cap when ds_accord(party) > 10 { Set ds_accord(party) to 10. }
  Observe ds_slight_one near ds_fire when ds_slight(party) == 1 and not fireWrathful(party) "'Careful,' says the Fire.".
  Observe ds_slight_two near ds_fire when ds_slight(party) == 2 and not fireWrathful(party) "'I am counting,' says the Fire. The hall is hot enough to hurt.".

  Action ds_apology_prewitt(actor: group, site: place) "Let Sedley Prewitt say what he has done in the Fire's name" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor) and following(prewitt, actor) and not ds_apologised(prewitt).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert ds_apologised(prewitt). Increase ds_accord(actor) by 3. Assert fireFed(actor). }
    Result "Prewitt stands in the ash with his hat in his hands. 'Six years of blocks,' he says. 'I put them in a table. I called it mercy. They were your hosts.' He does not ask to be forgiven. 'It is an apology,' he says, 'from the one who owes it.' The Fire looks at him while the coal ticks over twice. 'Yes,' it says. 'That is the right man.'".
  }
  Action ds_apology_tobias(actor: group, site: place) "Let Tobias Pargeter say what the brigade has done to the Fire" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor)
      and (following(tobias, actor) or travelsWith(tobias, actor)) and not ds_apologised(tobias).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert ds_apologised(tobias). Increase ds_accord(actor) by 1. Assert fireFed(actor). }
    Result "'I put out your fires,' says Tobias, to the coal. 'In houses where you were a guest. I didn't know. I'm sorry.' The Fire says nothing for a time. 'You were told it was your trade,' it says. 'Come back when it is not.'".
  }
  Action ds_apology_other(actor: group, who: group, site: place) "Let {who} say what they owe the Fire" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(who, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor)
      and ds_apologist(who) and following(who, actor) and distinct(who, prewitt) and distinct(who, tobias) and not ds_apologised(who).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert ds_apologised(who). Increase ds_accord(actor) by 2. Assert fireFed(actor). }
    Result "{who} says what they owe, and it is not a long speech. The Fire counts it as it was meant.".
  }
  Action ds_apology_company(actor: group, site: place) "Say, for the company, that you have worn the Offices' licence and taken their pay" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor)
      and holding(actor, adjuster_licence) and not ds_apologised(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert ds_apologised(actor). Increase ds_accord(actor) by 1. }
    Result "'You owe me a little,' says the Fire. 'You wear their card. You did not make the Ordinance.' It considers. 'It is something. It is the cheapest apology I have been offered, and it is true.'".
  }
  Action ds_bribe(actor: group, site: place) "Offer the Fire coin to let the matter drop" {
    Grave "The Fire is not a clerk. Offered a price for its patience, it will take the offer as the price of its patience.".
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 1.
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Increase ds_slight(actor) by 1. }
    Result "The coin goes into the ash, and does not melt. It lies there, bright and a little ridiculous. 'You have mistaken me,' says the Fire, 'for a trade.'".
  }
  Action ds_threaten(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Fire what the company will do to it if it does not stand down" {
    Grave "A threat to the Fire is not forgotten as a clerk forgets one.".
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Increase ds_slight(actor) by 1. }
    Result "The Fire hears you out. It has, you realise, heard this before, from better armed. 'You have a great deal to say,' it says, 'about an account that is not yours.'".
  }

  // Terms.
  Action ds_term_night(actor: group, site: place) "Promise the Fire a Night: once every year, the city to come to it, and bring its coals" {
    Grave "A promise made to the Fire is a debt to it. It will be collected from whoever lives in the city.".
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor)
      and ds_termsAsked(actor) and ds_accord(actor) >= 5 and not fireTermNight(actor) and witnessCount(city) < 2.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert fireTermNight(actor). Assert fireTerms(actor). }
    Result "'Every year,' says the Fire. 'The city to come to me, and bring its coals, and sit.' It looks at you. 'On your word. It is what I was given the last time, and I am a patient creditor.'".
  }
  Action ds_term_night_witnessed(actor: group, site: place) "Promise the Fire a Night, and give it the names of those who have said they will keep it" {
    Grave "A promise made to the Fire is a debt to it. It will be collected from whoever lives in the city.".
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor)
      and ds_termsAsked(actor) and ds_accord(actor) >= 5 and not fireTermNight(actor) and witnessCount(city) >= 2.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert fireTermNight(actor). Assert fireTerms(actor). Assert ds_night_witnessed(actor). }
    Result "'Names,' says the Fire. It takes them in, one by one, and you can see it turn them over. 'These I will remember. It is a great deal better than a word.'".
  }
  Action ds_term_average(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Fire the Cinder Ward will be emptied, and burned by daylight, and the Offices will pay" {
    Grave "What the Fire is promised here, it will take whether or not the Offices have agreed.".
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor)
      and ds_termsAsked(actor) and ds_accord(actor) >= 7 and knows(actor, d_decline_roll) and not fireTermAverage(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert fireTermAverage(actor). Assert fireTerms(actor). }
    Result "'A general average,' says the Fire, who has been reading the Offices' books since before there were Offices. 'The loss shared among all who are saved by it. It is the one thing they invented that I admire.' It considers. 'Empty. In the light. And paid for, by those who were saved. Yes.'".
  }
  Action ds_term_keeper_prewitt(actor: group, site: place) "Let Sedley Prewitt stay, as Hearthkeeper" {
    Grave "Whoever stays at the Hearth Below does not come up again.".
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor)
      and ds_termsAsked(actor) and ds_accord(actor) >= 5 and following(prewitt, actor) and ds_apologised(prewitt) and not fireTermKeeper(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert fireTermKeeper(actor). Assert fireTerms(actor). Assert ds_stays(prewitt). Retract following(prewitt, actor). Assert at(prewitt, hearth_below). }
    Result "'I would like to stay,' says Prewitt, as a man who has found, at the bottom of a long column, the one entry that balances. He does not look back at you. The Fire does not thank him. It makes room.".
  }
  Action ds_term_keeper_tobias(actor: group, site: place) "Let Tobias Pargeter stay, as Hearthkeeper" {
    Grave "Whoever stays at the Hearth Below does not come up again.".
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor)
      and ds_termsAsked(actor) and ds_accord(actor) >= 5 and tobiasWilling(actor) and (following(tobias, actor) or travelsWith(tobias, actor)) and not fireTermKeeper(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert fireTermKeeper(actor). Assert fireTerms(actor). Assert ds_stays(tobias). Retract following(tobias, actor). Retract travelsWith(tobias, actor). Assert at(tobias, hearth_below). }
    Result "'Somebody has to hold the poker,' says Tobias, and tries to grin. The Fire looks at him, and its heat drops away from him in a ring. 'Brave,' it says. 'Foolish. I will keep him warm.'".
  }
  Action ds_term_keeper_auberon(actor: group, site: place) "Let old Auberon Hearn stay, as Hearthkeeper, as he has always meant to" {
    Grave "Whoever stays at the Hearth Below does not come up again.".
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor)
      and ds_termsAsked(actor) and ds_accord(actor) >= 5 and following(auberon, actor) and not fireTermKeeper(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert fireTermKeeper(actor). Assert fireTerms(actor). Assert ds_stays(auberon). Retract following(auberon, actor). Assert at(auberon, hearth_below). }
    Result "'Honora?' says Auberon, and then, with the clarity that comes to him for a moment at a time, 'No. It is not Honora. It is the other one.' He sits down by the coal, and puts his hands to it. 'Here you are,' he says. 'I am so sorry we were so long.'".
  }
  // What the Fire gives, and lets.
  Action ds_ask_leave(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Fire for leave to go through its house unburned" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor)
      and ds_accord(actor) >= 3 and not ds_leave(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert ds_leave(actor). }
    Result "'You have sat in my house,' says the Fire. 'A guest does not burn in it.' The heat goes off your skin as though a door had been shut. It will not hurt you in the Glass City now.".
  }
  Action ds_ask_flue(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Fire to let you climb the First Flue" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor)
      and ds_accord(actor) >= 2 and not ds_flue_asked(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert ds_flue_asked(actor). Assert state(ds_flue_gate, ds_drawn). }
    Result "'Go up,' says the Fire. 'It is my flue. It was the way my guests came and went.' High above, in the flue, an iron damper that has been shut for ninety-four years draws back with a sound like a long breath let out.".
  }
  Action ds_ask_coals(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Fire for coals to carry home to the hearths" {
    Speaker ds_fire.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ds_fire, site) and fireHeard(actor) and not fireWrathful(actor) and day(clock) >= 7
      and (fireTerms(actor) or fireFed(actor)) and not ds_coals_given(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert ds_coals_given(actor). Increase quantity(actor, coal) by 2. Set coalExpires(actor) to watch(clock) + 144. }
    Result "The Fire draws two coals out of itself like a man taking coins from a purse. 'Lent,' it says. 'To be returned. Do not let them out. It will know, and it will mind.'".
  }
  Rule ds_slain when dead(ds_fire) and not fireSlain(party)
    says "The Fire goes out. It goes out as a hearth does at the end of a long day, patiently, the last coal last: and all through the city, in a thousand grates, a red eye closes." {
    Assert fireSlain(party). }
  Goal false.
}

data/adventures/quittance/hearing.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "The Hearing of the Five, at two on Reckoning day: the Tables, the Ordinance, the Appointed Losses and the motion; how each Office votes, and what carries it.".

  // The Five sit on Reckoning, day 8, at two (watch 1188). Four matters, a half-hour each. The company may take part
  // from the floor of the Hall; or be elsewhere, and the Hearing goes on without it and decides on what the Offices
  // already think of the company. Votes are decided by regard and by arcs, never by a document alone (02-review R4).
  Measure argued(group). Measure ayes(group). Relation decided(matter).
  Relation voted(group). Relation aye(group). Relation motionCarried(group). Relation motionLost(group).
  Relation aliasAmended(group). Relation prestTestified(group). Relation confessed(group). Relation bellRung(group).
  Relation gauntSwayed(group). Relation bookLaid(group). Relation witnessesCalled(group). Relation tablesRead(group).

  Person chairmen "the Chairmen" at hall_five {
    Role "one to each Office, on the dais". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Numbers 5. Pronouns they.
    Greets "Five chairs stand on the dais and five people sit in them, in the attitudes of a family that has been told it has to talk about money. The Phoenix's is empty, with a clerk's stool beside it; the Lamprey's is a wet-coated man looking at his hands; the Sovereign's is a sleepy figure in a black sun; the Providence's is plump, rosy and cheerful as a hot-water bottle; the Residuary's is a small bald gentleman who has brought sandwiches.".
    Greets again "The Five look up and then, with some relief, down again.".
  }
  Rule hall_gathers when watch(clock) >= 1182 and not at(prewitt, hall_five) and not appointedHalted(city) and arc(prewitt) < 3 { Assert at(prewitt, hall_five). Assert at(gaunt, hall_five). }
  Rule hall_gathers_turned when watch(clock) >= 1182 and arc(prewitt) >= 3 and not at(prewitt, hall_five) { Assert at(prewitt, hall_five). Assert at(gaunt, hall_five). }

  Occasion hearing "the Hearing of the Five" at hall_five when watch(clock) >= 1188 {
    Matter h_tables "The Tables are laid on the table, and the Keeper of the Tables is not in the Hall." for 30 minutes until decided(h_tables).
    Matter h_ordinance "Lord Gaunt-Halloran rises to speak to the Smokeless Ordinance." for 30 minutes until decided(h_ordinance).
    Matter h_losses "The Chairman of the Residuary reads, from a slip, a matter 'touching certain losses in the Wards'." for 30 minutes until decided(h_losses).
    Matter h_motion "The Five proceed to the motion: that the Ordinance be suspended for the Night, the Appointed Losses ended, and the City be called to its hearths." for 30 minutes until decided(h_motion).
    Closes "The Five rise. Chairs are pushed back. A clerk begins to blow out the candles on the dais, one at a time, and is told to stop.".
  }
  Rule hearing_over when occasionOver(hearing) and not hearingOver(city) { Assert hearingOver(city). }
  Rule hearing_over_unseen when watch(clock) >= 1230 and not hearingOver(city) { Assert hearingOver(city). Assert decided(h_motion). }

  // ── The Tables ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Action stand_with_pettifer(actor: group, site: place) "Stand beside Cornelia Pettifer while she says the numbers" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hall_five) and matterOpen(h_tables) and travelsWith(pettifer, actor) and arc(pettifer) >= 1 and not pettiferSpoke(city).
    Time 20 minutes.
    On success { Assert pettiferSpoke(city). Increase argued(city) by 2. Assert decided(h_tables). }
    Result "She has the page in both hands and it is shaking, and then she looks at the Phoenix's empty chair and, perhaps because it is empty, begins. 'Ninety-four years,' says Cornelia Pettifer. 'Four hundred and two fires in the marked wards in the last twelve. Eleven in the Bare Wards. The Wards are tinder and they burn eleven.' Her voice rises, and steadies, because it is only a number. She says them all. When she has said them she stops, and finds she is still standing, and that you are beside her, and that nobody has interrupted. 'That is all,' she says. 'Thank you.' The Chairman of the Providence begins, with great enthusiasm, to applaud, and is stopped.".
  }
  Action read_the_curves(actor: group, site: place) "Read the two curves from the Tables yourself, as well as you can" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hall_five) and matterOpen(h_tables) and knows(actor, d_tables_paradox) and not tablesRead(city) and not pettiferSpoke(city).
    Time 20 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert tablesRead(city). Increase argued(city) by 1. Assert decided(h_tables). }
    On failure { Assert tablesRead(city). Assert decided(h_tables). }
    Result "You do your best with someone else's pencil marks. The Chairman of the Sovereign wakes up enough to say 'Hear, hear,' and falls asleep again, but the small bald gentleman of the Residuary has taken out a pencil of his own.".
    Otherwise "You read it to the Five with every confidence. After a while the Chairman of the Providence asks, kindly, whether you might perhaps start again with the labels.".
  }

  // ── The Ordinance ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe gaunt_speaks at hall_five when matterOpen(h_ordinance) and arc(gaunt) == 0 "Lord Gaunt-Halloran is on his feet, and so is his chandelier. 'The future is a gas,' he is saying, 'and a gas does not go out.' He pauses for the cheering, which does not come.".
  Observe gaunt_speaks_bought at hall_five when matterOpen(h_ordinance) and arc(gaunt) >= 1 "Lord Gaunt-Halloran is on his feet, and in a quite different voice than he began with. 'The Company,' he is saying, 'has always been sensible of the public interest, and it may be that the public interest is, on the night in question, a warm one.' He looks, over the top of the paper, at you.".
  Action flatter_gaunt(actor: group, site: place) "Rise from the floor and propose that the Gas Company light the first hearth on Policy Row, in the Company's name" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hall_five) and matterOpen(h_ordinance) and not gauntSwayed(city) and arc(gaunt) < 2.
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert gauntSwayed(city). Increase arc(gaunt) by 1. Assert decided(h_ordinance). }
    On failure { Assert gauntSwayed(city). Assert decided(h_ordinance). }
    Result "Lord Gaunt-Halloran stops mid-sentence. 'The first hearth,' he says. 'In the Company's name.' His eye goes distant. 'On Policy Row.' He has the look of a man being measured for a statue. 'I confess,' he says, 'that I had not thought the Ordinance admitted of ceremony.' He sits, with a look of enormous private satisfaction.".
    Otherwise "'The Company,' says Lord Gaunt-Halloran, 'takes the suggestion as a kindness, and declines it as a precedent.' He sits down. He has a look of someone who has been right on principle and wrong on the facts.".
  }
  Action leave_ordinance(actor: group, site: place) "Let the Ordinance pass without a word from you" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hall_five) and matterOpen(h_ordinance).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert decided(h_ordinance). }
    Result "You let him finish. It does not take long, in the end; the chandelier has the best of it.".
  }

  // ── The Appointed Losses ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe prest_enters at hall_five when matterOpen(h_losses) and aliased(party) and not aliasAmended(party) "At the back of the Hall, in a dark coat, a clerk has appeared from the Arch with the Roll of Entrances under his arm. It is Mr Prest, and he is looking at the company with an expression of the deepest regret.".
  Rule prest_testifies when matterOpen(h_losses) and aliased(party) and not aliasAmended(party) and not prestTestified(city)
    says "'I am obliged to report,' says Mr Prest, to the Hall, 'that the persons addressing the Five are entered in the Roll as wool-factors, come to buy fleeces. The Bell was silent at the time. I draw no conclusion; the Bell is not to be reasoned with.' He sits down. The Chairman of the Providence has stopped smiling." {
    Assert prestTestified(city). Decrease argued(city) by 1 or to nothing. }
  Rule prewitt_confesses when matterOpen(h_losses) and prewittTurned(party) and not confessed(city)
    says "Sedley Prewitt rises before the Residuary can finish. 'There is a list,' he says, 'and it is mine. Six years of it. The Bare Wards, one block a year, at the Appointed Night. I have the dates. I have the sums. I have not, until this week, had the nerve to say what they were for.' He lays a thin ledger on the dais. 'Four hundred a year, I told myself, against eighty thousand.' He takes off his spectacles. 'I should like the Hall to know that I was wrong, and that I am quite certain that I was right.' And out in the city, a mile away, under the Arch, the Honest Bell tolls once, softly, like a sigh." {
    Assert confessed(city). Increase argued(city) by 4. Assert decided(h_losses). }
  Rule prewitt_denies when matterOpen(h_losses) and not prewittTurned(party) and not confessed(city) and not bellRung(city)
    says "'There is no such list,' says Sedley Prewitt, evenly. 'There is a prudent reserve against a catastrophe, of which the Five have been aware for six years and which I have audited myself.' And a mile away, under the Arch, the Honest Bell tolls once. Every head in the Hall turns toward the windows. The small bald gentleman of the Residuary writes something down. 'The Chairman asks,' he says mildly, 'whether the Bell may be entered as testimony.' 'The Bell,' says the Chairman of the Sovereign, waking, 'is not to be reasoned with.' 'No,' says the Residuary. 'But it is, I think, to be noted.'" {
    Assert bellRung(city). Increase argued(city) by 1. }
  Action lay_the_book(actor: group, site: place) "Lay Skelter's rent-book before the Five" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hall_five) and matterOpen(h_losses) and holding(actor, skelter_book) and not bookLaid(city).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert bookLaid(city). Increase argued(city) by 2. }
    Result "You put the oilcloth book on the dais. The small bald gentleman of the Residuary turns it round, finds the margin, turns two pages, and puts on a second pair of spectacles. 'It is a fine thing,' he murmurs, 'a second column.' The Chairman of the Lamprey reads over his shoulder and is seen to go the colour of a boiled fish.".
  }
  Action call_witnesses(actor: group, site: place) "Call everyone who will say what they saw" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hall_five) and matterOpen(h_losses) and witnessCount(city) >= 1 and not witnessesCalled(city).
    Time 30 minutes.
    On success { Assert witnessesCalled(city). Increase argued(city) by witnessCount(city). Assert decided(h_losses). }
    Result "They come in by ones and twos and are asked to stand at a rail, and they do. A clerk who has been taking things down for twenty years puts down his pen in the middle of a word; a woman says the name of a street; a child says nothing at all, with great force. By the time the last has sat down, the Hall has the look of a room in which a number has been said aloud and cannot be unsaid.".
  }
  Action rest_the_case(actor: group, site: place) "Rest your case" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hall_five) and matterOpen(h_losses).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert decided(h_losses). }
    Result "'That is the case,' you say. The Chairman of the Residuary nods and writes it down.".
  }

  // ── The motion ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule vote_phoenix when matterOpen(h_motion) and not voted(phoenix) says "The Phoenix's clerk, standing in for an empty chair, looks at the door of the Chief Underwriter's room and then at the floor." {
    Assert voted(phoenix). }
  Rule phoenix_aye when voted(phoenix) and not aye(phoenix) and (prewittTurned(party) or (arc(prewitt) >= 2 and not prewittHardened(party))) { Assert aye(phoenix). Increase ayes(city) by 1. }
  Rule vote_lamprey when matterOpen(h_motion) and not voted(lamprey) { Assert voted(lamprey). }
  Rule lamprey_aye when voted(lamprey) and not aye(lamprey) and (arc(dree) >= 1 or regard(lamprey) >= 2) { Assert aye(lamprey). Increase ayes(city) by 1. }
  Rule vote_sovereign when matterOpen(h_motion) and not voted(sovereign) { Assert voted(sovereign). }
  Rule sovereign_aye when voted(sovereign) and not aye(sovereign) and (arc(cray) >= 1 or regard(sovereign) >= 2) { Assert aye(sovereign). Increase ayes(city) by 1. }
  Rule vote_providence when matterOpen(h_motion) and not voted(providence) { Assert voted(providence). }
  Rule providence_aye when voted(providence) and not aye(providence) and (regard(providence) >= 1 or argued(city) >= 3) and not (prewittHardened(party) and regard(providence) < 2) { Assert aye(providence). Increase ayes(city) by 1. }
  Rule vote_residuary when matterOpen(h_motion) and not voted(residuary) { Assert voted(residuary). }
  Rule residuary_aye when voted(residuary) and not aye(residuary) and (witnessCount(city) >= 3 or argued(city) >= 4) { Assert aye(residuary). Increase ayes(city) by 1. }
  Rule motion_carried when voted(residuary) and voted(providence) and voted(sovereign) and voted(lamprey) and voted(phoenix) and not motionCarried(city) and not motionLost(city) and ((arc(gaunt) == 0 and ayes(city) >= 4) or (arc(gaunt) >= 1 and ayes(city) >= 3))
    says "The Chairman of the Residuary counts aloud, with a pencil, and reaches the number. 'Carried,' he says, rather surprised. 'I believe that is the first time.' The Hall has not yet decided whether to cheer. The Chairman of the Providence has, and does." {
    Assert motionCarried(city). Assert decided(h_motion). }
  Rule motion_lost when voted(residuary) and voted(providence) and voted(sovereign) and voted(lamprey) and voted(phoenix) and not motionCarried(city) and not motionLost(city) and ((arc(gaunt) == 0 and ayes(city) < 4) or (arc(gaunt) >= 1 and ayes(city) < 3))
    says "The Chairman of the Residuary counts, and counts again, and sets down his pencil. 'Lost,' he says. The Hall is quiet. 'The Five regret that the matter is not within the Five's competence.' Somebody laughs, once, without any amusement at all." {
    Assert motionLost(city). Assert decided(h_motion). }
  Observe hall_aftermath at hall_five when motionCarried(city) "The Hall empties slowly, in knots of clerks arguing about where to find a coal.".
  Observe hall_aftermath_lost at hall_five when motionLost(city) "The Hall empties quickly. Nobody is saying anything that could be quoted.".

  // ── What the small adventures lend the Hearing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation ruleCited(group). Relation marksCited(group).
  Rule mark_street_rule_cited when matterOpen(h_ordinance) and ms_rule(party) and not ruleCited(city)
    says "The Chairman of the Lamprey, to everyone's surprise, rises on a point of order. 'The Mark Street Rule,' he says, 'provides that where two brigades quarrel over a plate, a third certification stands. It was devised by these persons, on the day, in front of a burning house. I propose that it stand for the Night.' The Chairman of the Phoenix's clerk writes it down, rather than not." {
    Assert ruleCited(city). Increase argued(city) by 1. }
  Rule forged_doors_cited when matterOpen(h_losses) and fg_network(party) and not marksCited(city)
    says "The Chairman of the Providence has been handed a plate. It is a gilt bird, correct to the feather and not quite round. 'There are a dozen doors in the Wards,' he says, 'with one of these on them, and the brigades have been putting them out for a month. I cannot find that anybody has been defrauded.' He turns it over. 'I find that it is a rather good plate.'" {
    Assert marksCited(city). Increase argued(city) by 1. }

  // ── The Chairmen, a face each ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic chair_residuary with chairmen "Ask the Chairman of the Residuary what the sixth stool is for" when true once {
    Says "The small bald gentleman puts down his sandwich. 'The Residuary,' he says, 'is the Office for what the others will not cover. It was a joke. We have had it a hundred years.' He looks at the stool. 'Dame Honora left a seat for the Guest. We dust it on Thursdays. I am afraid it is the only part of my duties that I have ever understood.'".
  }
  Topic chair_lamprey with chairmen "Ask the Chairman of the Lamprey how his fish is" when true once {
    Says "The wet-coated man looks up from his hands. 'Dree says it is the best brigade in the city,' he says. 'Dree is wrong. It is the second best. The best is whichever one is not the Phoenix. It saves a great deal of arguing.'".
  }
  Topic chair_providence with chairmen "Ask the Chairman of the Providence whether he is ever frightened" when true once {
    Says "The plump rosy Chairman beams. 'I insure against falling off ladders,' he says. 'Every day. For people who then do not fall off them, because they are insured, and are careful, because they have paid.' The beam falters for a moment. 'Twice a week somebody falls off one anyway, and I pay, and the week after there are two more people on ladders.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/quittance/kernel.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "What every part of Quittance shares: the Offices and what they think of the company, the arcs of its principal people, what the company can come to know, and what a Lent coal is.".

  // ══ THE KERNEL CONTRACT ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // Every small adventure (q_*.kyr) is written against the names below and no others of the spine's. A quest may
  // declare as many names of its own as it wants, each beginning with its prefix; it may read any name here; it
  // may only WRITE the ones the contract says it writes.

  // ── The Offices, and what they think of the company ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // regard(x): how well the company stands with x. Starts at 0; a good turn is +1 or +2, a betrayal -1 or -2. The
  // Hearing counts them (hearing.kyr), a quest may spend them.
  Entity phoenix: group "the Phoenix Fire Office". Entity lamprey: group "the Lamprey & River Office".
  Entity sovereign: group "the Sovereign Mutual". Entity providence: group "the Providence". Entity residuary: group "the Residuary Office".
  Entity gasco: group "the Gas Company". Entity wardsfolk: group "the people of the Bare Wards". Entity brigades: group "the brigades".
  Entity city: group "Quittance".
  Measure regard(group).

  // ── How far a principal figure has come ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // arc(x): 0 where they begin. A figure moves one stage at a time, by a lever that suits them (02-review R4), and
  // the world remembers the stage, not a flag.
  //   Prewitt   0 hard . 1 shaken . 2 open . 3 turned          (and 4: hardened, the other way)
  //   Garrity   0 rival . 1 asked . 2 partner
  //   Dree      0 rival . 1 out-bargained . 2 willing
  //   Ianthe    0 deferring . 1 decided
  //   Pettifer     0 silent . 1 speaks
  //   Cray      0 bonus-minded . 1 remembers his mother . 2 an ally
  //   Gaunt     0 pompous . 1 flattered . 2 bought in
  //   Hearn     0 lost . 1 lucid for a time . 2 lucid
  Measure arc(group).

  // ── What the company comes to know ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A quest teaches these (Assert knows(actor, d_...)) when its play has earned it, never otherwise. The spine reads
  // them. Each is a fact a person could say in a sentence, and none is the whole truth.
  Discovery d_tables_paradox "The Tables are wrong: the unmarked Bare Wards, which should burn worst, burn least, and the marked Brickfields have been burning more every year since the Smokeless Ordinance.".
  Discovery d_appointed_notice "Rent-collectors in the Bare Wards give notice early, in a few blocks a year, a week before each is burned. The notice is stamped by someone with an Office's seal.".
  Discovery d_list_exists "There is a list. Certain blocks in the Bare Wards are chosen, and chosen from above, before they burn.".
  Discovery d_prewitt_appoints "The list is Sedley Prewitt's, kept by Mr Skelter of the rent-office in the Bare Wards.".
  Discovery d_pilots_step "The gas pilot-lights of the Glass Quarter go out and come back in step, as if one thing were breathing through all of them.".
  Discovery d_lent_coal "In the Bare Wards some households keep a coal that is never allowed to go out, and say it was lent. It is passed down, and it is called a Lent coal.".
  Discovery d_oven_coal "The oven in Tolliver's bakehouse keeps a Lent coal, and has since before the Burning; its draw is not the flue's.".
  Discovery d_wording_style "The Founders' papers are drafted in an exact and generous style: the wording does what it says, and says what it means, and leaves room for the poor.".
  Discovery d_unpaid_ledger "The dead of the Burning have a ledger of unpaid claims, eleven hundred of them, kept by a clerk in the Exchange cellars.".
  Discovery d_tithe_debt "The Founders' Policy was never a policy of insurance: it is a debt of hospitality, owed to someone who is not dead.".
  Discovery d_way_teague "A cellar-diver named Ambrose Teague knew a way down to the old city that is not by the Exchange stair.".
  Discovery d_decline_roll "The Surveyors' Roll has the Cinder Ward marked Declined: unfit for cover, and unfit to stand, as of the Reckoning.".
  Discovery d_marks_work "Forged fire-marks, nailed up by the poor, are respected by the brigades more often than they should be.".
  Discovery d_cold_lamp_bound "The cold-lamps do not give light by themselves: each holds a spark of something that is held there, against its will, in glass.".
  Discovery d_barge_girl "A girl was smuggled out of the Bare Wards on the Prudent Margaret before an Appointed block burned: someone had warned her, and then was bought off.".
  Discovery d_receipt_pale "The Receipt on the Hall of the Five is the Founders' Policy's quittance, and it is nearly blank.".
  Discovery d_treaty_text "The Founders' Policy, read whole, names a party who is not an Office, a city, or a person: 'the Guest of the Hearth'.".
  Discovery d_fire_is_real "Something lives under the Exchange, and has been waiting ninety-four years to be paid.".
  Discovery d_return "There is a form of words, the Return, by which the Lent coals are carried home at Reckoning. Auberon Hearn used to say it, and cannot say it alone.".
  Discovery d_candlewick_next "The next block on the list is Candlewick Court, in the Bare Wards; the notice there is stamped, and the date on it is the second night.".
  Discovery d_gasket_next "The second block on the list is Gasket Yard, in the Bare Wards, and the night written against it is the sixth.".
  Discovery d_skelter_book "Skelter's rent-book records the notices in advance, with the sum paid for each, and who signed.".

  // ── Witnesses: who will say it at the Hearing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A quest that wins a person's willingness to testify asserts witness(person). The Hearing reads the count.
  Relation witness(group).
  Measure witnessCount(group).
  Relation witnessCounted(group).
  Rule witness_counted when witness(?w) and not witnessCounted(?w) { Assert witnessCounted(?w). Increase witnessCount(city) by 1. }

  // ── Wards, coals, hearths ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The six wards are the settlements brick, reach, glass, hill, mort and wards. A ward is LIT on the Night when a
  // Lent coal is laid in one of its hearths (hearthAt), and somebody there will keep it (keeper(ward)). A coal is
  // carried as a good; it gutters a day after it is taken. A quest that gives a ward its keeper writes
  // keeper(ward); a quest that gives a coal writes quantity(party, coal) (via source_coal below).
  Entity coal: good "Lent coal".
  Relation keeper(place). Relation hearthAt(place, place). Relation coaled(place). Relation counted(place).
  Measure wardsLit(group). Measure coalExpires(group).
  Initially Assert hearthAt(tolliver_shop, brick). Initially Assert hearthAt(sluice_room, reach).
  Initially Assert hearthAt(lamplighters_hall, glass). Initially Assert hearthAt(hearn_hearth, hill).
  Initially Assert hearthAt(alms_room, mort). Initially Assert hearthAt(penny_hall, wards).
  Rule ward_counted when coaled(?w) and keeper(?w) and not counted(?w) { Assert counted(?w). Increase wardsLit(city) by 1. }
  Rule coal_gutters when quantity(party, coal) > 0 and watch(clock) >= coalExpires(party) says "The Lent coal in its tin has shrunk to a red thread, and then to ash. You were too slow with it." {
    Set quantity(party, coal) to 0. }
  Action take_coal_from_hearth(actor: group, site: place) "Take a Lent coal from the hearth here, in a tin" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and coalSource(site) and quantity(actor, coal) < 2 and day(clock) >= 7.
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Increase quantity(actor, coal) by 1. Set coalExpires(actor) to watch(clock) + 144. Assert coalTaken(site). }
    Result "You scoop a live coal into a tin and shut the lid. It is warm through the metal, and it ticks.".
  }
  Relation coalSource(place). Relation coalTaken(place).
  Action lay_coal(actor: group, site: place, dist: place) "Lay a Lent coal in the hearth here" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and hearthAt(site, dist) and quantity(actor, coal) >= 1 and not coaled(dist) and day(clock) >= 7.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, coal) by 1. Assert coaled(dist). }
    Result "You rake the hearth, lay the coal on the grate, and breathe it up. It takes slowly and then all at once, and the room, for a moment, seems to lean toward it.".
  }

  // ── The clock of the Night ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Day 0 is the first morning; Reckoning is the night of day 8. The days are named by the Slate.
  Entity reckoning: group "Reckoning".
  Relation reckoned(group).
  Relation lapsed(group).

  // ── The adjuster's licence, and what a company may certify ─────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind adjuster_licence "an adjuster's licence of the Bell & Slip" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "A card of buff pasteboard, signed by the Bell & Slip's Master of the Slate: the bearer is permitted to take claims, enter premises named in them, and certify a mark.".
  Kind policy_of_passage "a Policy of Passage" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "A stamped slip from the Declaration Arch. For nine days, the Office named on it will bury you, fish you out or put you out, as the case may be.".

  // ── Ordinary things sold in Quittance ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind chandlers_candle "a mark-insured candle" is gear worth 1 weighing 0 described "A tallow candle with a tiny Phoenix stamped in the base, guaranteeing it against its own flame.".

  // ── Things that pass between small adventures ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The kinds are declared here so that the adventure that gives one and the adventure that asks for it can be written
  // apart. The adventure that gives a thing declares its Item (at nowhere) and Gives it; the one that asks for it asks
  // holding(actor, kind).
  Kind forged_writ "a writ of the Lamprey & River Office, not quite" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "A sheet of Lamprey & River foolscap, correctly watermarked with a fish, correctly signed by a captain who did not sign it. The seal is excellent. The paper is very slightly the wrong shade of wet.".
  Kind tench_ledger "the Ledger of the Unpaid" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1 described "A long narrow account-book in a boy's careful hand: eleven hundred names, each with the date of the Burning against it and a sum claimed, and a column headed PAID that is empty from top to bottom.".
  Kind roll_extract "an extract of the Surveyors' Roll" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "A clean copy of one page of the Roll, with the Guild's stamp: the Cinder Ward, and against it, in the Roll's own hand, DECLINED. Beneath it is the date, which is Reckoning.".
  Kind cellar_key "the Exchange cellar key" like cell_key described "A black iron key with a stamped bird for a bow. It is warm to the hand, and does not seem to cool.".
  Kind skelter_book "Skelter's rent-book" is treasure worth 0 weighing 1 described "A thick rent-book bound in oilcloth. Down the margin of its pages, in a different ink from the rents, runs a second column of dates, each a week before a fire.".
  Kind salamander_lantern "a salamander-glass lantern" like lantern described "A lantern of dark green glass in which a small steady light burns without oil. It does not flicker, and it does not go out. It is warm to the hand like something asleep.".
  Kind phoenix_writ "a writ of the Phoenix" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "A sheet of Phoenix foolscap with a gilt bird, signed in a clear unhesitating hand: the bearer may enter any Phoenix premises, and certify any Phoenix mark, in the Office's name.".

  // ── Ways between the surface and the Sunk City ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Each way down is gated by a Thing on its passage, owned by one file:
  //   cellar_stair (the Exchange)      descent.kyr         key (cellar_key), lockwork, or leave from Prewitt/Pettifer
  //   catacomb_stair (Mortmain)        q_annuitant.kyr     the rite (rites), the sexton's leave, or the Oakes name
  //   bell_shaft_way (the Reach)       q_barge.kyr         Dree's leave, a forged_writ, the Teague combination, or force
  //   flue_up (the Cinder Ward)        descent.kyr         opened from below by the Fire only
  // The Queue (q_queue.kyr) stands on down_glass: every way down but the Flue meets it.
  Relation dree_leave(group). Relation queueOpen(group). Relation teagueCombination(group).
  Relation sextonLeave(group). Relation cellarLeave(group).

  // ── What the Descent hands the endings ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // descent.kyr writes these; endings.kyr reads them.
  Relation fireHeard(group). Relation fireFed(group). Relation fireTerms(group). Relation fireTermKeeper(group).
  Relation fireTermNight(group). Relation fireTermAverage(group). Relation fireSlain(group). Relation fireWrathful(group).
  Relation coalNamedGran(group). Relation coalNamedPip(group). Relation coalNamedNone(group).
  Relation tobiasWilling(group).
}

data/adventures/quittance/links.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "Links outward from the Arch: a ship left in the Slack, and a ship given a quay.".

  // ── World events, read: the Honest Bell and the Roll ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe lore_bell_ship at arch_hall when befell(remainder_harboured) and not befell(remainder_kept) "Mr Prest has a new column in the Roll, ruled that morning, headed ARRIVALS WITHOUT AN ARCH. There are forty-odd entries in it, in forty hands, none of them his. 'They came ashore,' he says, 'in the south, off a ship. A town found them a quay. They declared nothing. The Bell was not asked.' He looks at the Bell. 'I have never wished so much that it had been.'".
  Observe lore_bell_kept at arch_hall when befell(remainder_kept) "The Honest Bell has been wrapped, overnight, in a cloth that was not there at close. Mr Prest says he did not do it. 'A ship that was not harboured,' he says. 'Left. With her people. It has made the Bell shy.' He lifts the cloth and lets it drop. 'It does not like to hear of a declaration that nobody was there to make.'".

  // ── A road with no duty paid, and a debt of fourteen days ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Quittance reckons in what is owed. Two things that were settled in the west and kept no receipt come in as
  // entries Mr Prest does not know where to enter.
  Observe lore_prest_road at arch_hall when befell(calx_opened) "Mr Prest has ruled a new column in the Roll in red, headed ROADS WITH NO DUTY. There is one entry in it, in his own hand, and it is two miles long: the Aenean pavement under a ridge in the west, opened, they say, by strangers with a pot of lamp oil. 'Nobody has levied on it,' he says. 'I have looked. There is a toll-house on the hill and it faces the wrong way.' He taps the column. 'It is the first road I have ever wished were mine.'".
  Observe lore_prest_names at arch_hall when befell(tallow_names) "Mr Prest has found, folded into the back of the Roll where a debt would be, a sheet in a stranger's pencil: fourteen names, and against each a day's wage, and the word PAID in a different ink for each. 'Sixty years late,' he says, 'by a village.' He smooths it. 'The Office would say it is out of time. The Bell has not said anything.' The Honest Bell, over his head, does not.".
}

data/adventures/quittance/lore.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "What Quittance remembers and does not say: the Receipt that fades by the day, Dame Honora's small hand, the Burning in the glass, the children's counting-rhyme, the Reckoning pageant, and a hundred small things with a history behind them. Nothing here is needed; everything here is a rumour of the thing under the Exchange.".

  // ══ THE RECEIPT, DAY BY DAY ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // The Receipt on the front of the Hall of the Five is written in fire gone to white. It is read from the court of the
  // Exchange, and every morning there is less of it. (Foreshadowing for the whole book, and a clock a player can read.)
  Thing receipt "the Receipt on the Hall's front" at exchange_court {
    Tries looking.
    State full "The Receipt on the Hall's front is still legible if you stand where the clerks stand. RECEIVED OF THE CITY OF QUITTANCE, THE SUM OF ITS PREMIUM, IN FULL. The last three words have gone the colour of old teeth; the rest is white.".
    State fading "The Receipt has lost its last words since you came. RECEIVED OF THE CITY OF QUITTANCE, THE SUM OF ITS. Where PREMIUM was, the plaster shows through a pale smear, like a word breathed on a window.".
    State faint "The Receipt has dwindled to RECEIVED OF THE CITY, and under it a long faint stroke, such as a clerk makes with the side of the pen before he has decided what to write. The clerks pass it with their eyes down.".
    State bright "The Receipt is brighter. RECEIVED OF THE CITY OF QUITTANCE, and a word has come back that nobody has been able to read. There is a small crowd at the rail, and a clerk who has been told not to stand on the step is standing on it.".
  }
  Rule receipt_fades_a when day(clock) >= 4 and state(receipt, full) { Assert state(receipt, fading). }
  Rule receipt_fades_b when day(clock) >= 7 and state(receipt, fading) { Assert state(receipt, faint). }
  Rule receipt_brightens when wardsLit(city) >= 3 and not state(receipt, bright) { Assert state(receipt, bright). }
  Observe receipt_candle at exchange_court when burned(candlewick) and day(clock) >= 3 "Since the night of the fire in the Wards another letter has gone from the Receipt, and the clerks, who are exact, have written the date of its going in chalk on the step.".

  // ══ DAME HONORA ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Thing honora_statue "the statue of Dame Honora Hearn" at exchange_court {
    Tries looking.
    State standing "A bronze notary stands on a granite plinth in the middle of the court, a quill in her left hand and a sheaf under her arm. Her right hand is held out, palm up, a little cupped, as if to receive something small. No bird has ever settled in it.".
  }
  Observe honora_plinth near honora_statue when tried(honora_statue, looking) "The plinth says: DAME HONORA HEARN, NOTARY. SHE READ THE TERMS. Under it, on the lower course, in a different and later chisel: AND SIGNED. Under that, scratched with a nail by someone with a great deal of time: and was kind.".
  // Her handwriting, small and upright and in pencil, in the margin of everything she touched. Five places have it; the
  // sixth is in the Strongroom.
  Thing slip_first_slate "the first Slate, framed over the mantel" at slip_room {
    Tries looking.
    State framed "Over the mantel of the Bell & Slip, behind glass, hangs the first Slate ever chalked in Quittance, on a door taken off its hinges in the year of the Burning. It lists eleven claims. Nine are marked PAID. Two are marked, in pencil, in a small upright hand, HELD OVER, and against the second someone has written: until the claimant is able to attend.".
  }
  Thing mort_gate_plaque "the plaque on the Mortmain lodge-gate" at mort_lodge {
    Tries looking.
    State plaque "A brass plaque on the gatepost, worn nearly smooth by a century of widows: THE SOVEREIGN MUTUAL UNDERTAKES TO PAY WHILE THE LIFE SHALL LAST. Below it, a line engraved in a smaller hand than the rest, in very small capitals, as though it had been added after the plate was approved: A LIFE IS WHAT IT IS CALLED.".
  }
  Observe vault_margin at vault when knows(party, d_bell_rule) "In the margin of the closing clause, in pencil, in the same small upright hand as the Rules of the Bell at the Arch, someone has written: sufficient, my dear, to the guest. And beneath that, in a fainter hand that cannot be hers: she did not say whose.".
  Observe vault_margin_plain at vault when not knows(party, d_bell_rule) "There is a pencil note in the margin of the closing clause, in a small upright hand, nearly gone. You can make out only: sufficient to the.".

  // ══ THE BURNING, IN THE GLASS ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Thing founders_glass "the Founders' Glass" at exchange_court {
    Tries looking.
    State wall "On the south side of the court a wall of fused black glass, ten feet high, is all that is left of the Exchange's great window. In the day it shows your own face, a little darker than it is.".
  }
  Observe glass_dusk near founders_glass when tried(founders_glass, looking) and hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 20 "At dusk the glass changes. Behind your reflection, very small, a street runs in a long curve with its houses open like books, and every window is a colour you have no name for. A woman is walking down the middle of it. She carries a flat case under one arm and she is writing as she walks, without looking at the page, and the street is closing behind her like a mouth. She is not hurrying. She turns her head once, toward the glass, and you have the impression of a very tired person who has seen a thing she means to be civil to. Then the dusk goes, and there is only the court.".
  Observe glass_day near founders_glass when tried(founders_glass, looking) and (hour(clock) < 17 or hour(clock) >= 20) "In the glass there is your own face, and behind it the court, and a little lower than your shoulder, for an instant, a window of orange light that is not in the court. The clerks do not look at the wall. They have learned the hours when it is worth looking.".
  Observe court_warm at exchange_court when day(clock) >= 5 "The black glass paving is warm to the hand. Not hot: warm, as a stone is warm that a cat has just left. On the steps of the Hall the snow has melted in a clean shape like a footprint with no foot.".

  // ══ THINGS WITH A HISTORY ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Thing assize_placard "the Assize of Marks" at gate_plaza {
    Tries looking.
    State placard "A tarnished placard on the Arch wall, framed against pigeons: THE ASSIZE OF MARKS, YEAR THREE. A MARK IS THE POLICY. NO MARK, NO RESCUE. ORDERED AFTER BREWERS' ROW, WHERE BOTH BRIGADES ARRIVED AT ONE FIRE AND EACH WAITED FOR THE OTHER TO PASS ITS HOSE. THE LOSS WAS TWENTY-SIX HOUSES AND A BREWERY. THE BREWERY WAS INSURED.".
  }
  Thing loss_bell "the Loss-Bell" at slip_room {
    Tries looking.
    State hung "A small bell with a worn rope hangs by the Slate, struck once for each ship lost in the Reach, and not struck for houses. Underneath, a card says: BY CUSTOM OF THE HOUSE THE WAITER MAY BE ASKED TO STRIKE IT FOR A SUM, WHERE THE LOSS IS A PRIVATE ONE. There is a brass plate on the rope, rubbed to a shine at the height of a hand: the plate is the Founders' own mark, a coal in a nest, and the nest has been polished until it is almost a bird.".
  }
  Thing mean_obelisk "the obelisk of mean expectation" at annuity_row {
    Tries looking.
    State obelisk "At the head of Annuitants' Row stands a small obelisk of white stone, cut in rows: MEAN EXPECTATION OF LIFE, BY PARISH AND YEAR. Hands have been at it. Beside the Mortmain figure someone has scratched a tally of a hundred and three, and under it, fainter, as if ashamed: but not the Oakeses.".
  }
  Thing pattern_book "the pattern board of marks" at brick_lane {
    Tries looking.
    State board "A glazed board fixed to a wall at the corner of Brick Lane shows every mark a man might nail to his door, in colour: the Phoenix's gilt bird, the black fish, the sun, the open hand, the eye. At the bottom, a sixth, oldest, drawn in a different red and not described: a little nest of lines, and in it a point, as of a coal. The caption says: CEASED, 1224. NOT TO BE REISSUED.".
  }
  Thing ordinance_board "the board of the Smokeless Ordinance" at foundry_row {
    Tries looking.
    State ordinance "A board of black enamel on the end of the Row, in white: BY ORDINANCE OF THE OFFICES, THE LIGHTING OR KEEPING OF AN OPEN FIRE WITHIN THE INNER WARDS IS A NUISANCE. SECOND OFFENCE: THE FIRE TO BE EXTINGUISHED AT THE OFFENDER'S COST. THIRD: THE PREMISES DECLINED. Someone has chalked beneath it the number of premises declined so far this year, and then, in another hand, the number of fires.".
  }
  Thing hall_patch "the smooth patch where a hearth was" at hall_five {
    Tries looking.
    State patch "On the bare wall behind the dais, a hearth-shaped patch of plaster has been smoothed and lime-washed a shade whiter than the rest. It was done carefully, by a person who did not want the work noticed.".
  }
  Observe patch_warm near hall_patch when tried(hall_patch, looking) and day(clock) >= 5 "You lay a hand on the plaster. It is warm. Behind it, very faintly, like a pulse felt through a pillow, something ticks.".
  Observe patch_cold near hall_patch when tried(hall_patch, looking) and day(clock) < 5 "You lay a hand on the plaster. It is cool, and smooth, and slightly damp, like the wall of a cellar. You are not certain why you expected anything else.".
  Observe patch_red at hall_five when day(clock) >= 8 "Along the foot of the smooth patch, where the lime-wash meets the floor, there is a thin line of red light, steady, such as a door lets under it when there is a lamp lit in the next room.".

  // ══ THE CHILDREN'S RHYME ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // The children of the Brickfields skip to a rhyme that counts the days to Reckoning, and none of them knows what it
  // is counting. Whoever stands in Brick Lane in the day hears the line that belongs to the day.
  Observe rhyme_1 at brick_lane when day(clock) == 1 and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 18 "Two girls turn a rope across the Lane and a third skips in it, chanting: 'Nine for the Offices, nine for the door, / eight for the brigades that quarrel for more.'".
  Observe rhyme_2 at brick_lane when day(clock) == 2 and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 18 "The rope is turning again, and the girl in it chants: 'Seven for the Tables that never are wrong, / six for the fire that's a hundred years long.'".
  Observe rhyme_3 at brick_lane when day(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 18 "The children are skipping. 'Five for the premium paid in the hand, / four for the coal that was lent to the land.' The smallest stops to ask what a premium is, and is told by the others to jump.".
  Observe rhyme_4 at brick_lane when day(clock) == 4 and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 18 "'Three for the Receipt that goes white as a sheet,' the skipper chants, 'two for the guest that has nothing to eat.' Her mother, turning, has never been able to tell her what guest.".
  Observe rhyme_5 at brick_lane when day(clock) >= 5 and day(clock) <= 8 and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 18 "The rope turns, slower than it did. 'One for the Reckoning, who'll be the next? / Quit, and welcome, and out goes the—' and the girl in the middle misses her footing, on purpose, as the rhyme requires, and all the children shout.".

  // ══ THE RECKONING PAGEANT ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // Each Reckoning Day the Offices stage the Burning, in paper, for the children of the city, at the Exchange. It is the
  // most popular entertainment in Quittance.
  Observe pageant_row at row_street when day(clock) == 9 and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 14 "The Reckoning pageant is coming down Policy Row, and the whole street is let out to see it. Five floats, one to an Office: the Phoenix's a gilt bird on wheels, flapping; the Lamprey's a fish of papier-mâché with a boy in its mouth; the Sovereign's a sun carried by eight mourners in white; the Providence's an enormous open hand in which a very small girl sits and waves; and the Residuary's a cart containing a desk, and at the desk, with a pen, a little bald man who does not look up.".
  Observe pageant_court at exchange_court when day(clock) == 9 and hour(clock) >= 11 and hour(clock) < 14 "In the court a tank has been set out on trestles, and in it, on a scale of one to forty, stands a paper city. A cadet of the Phoenix in a gilt helmet reads the Burning from a scroll — 'and the fire took the Glassmakers' Row, and the Exchange, and the Hall of Weights' — and at each name a boy with a taper sets a paper house alight. The children are not allowed to clap until the end. At the end, when the tank is a bed of ash, a girl in a notary's gown is led out and made to stand in it, and the children cheer; she is Honora, and she has been told to hold up her hand.".
  Observe pageant_plaza at gate_plaza when day(clock) == 9 and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 18 "Paper birds hang from every doorway in Gate Plaza, gilt, blue and black, and the brokers have put down their trays to sell them. A man is selling a paper coal, a red twist of tissue in a nest of straw, at a farthing, and has sold forty; nobody can tell him why they buy it.".

  // ══ SOUNDS, SMELLS, HOURS ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Observe qv_carter at arch_road when day(clock) <= 1 and hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 18 "From under the Arch a bell rings once, flat and unhurried. The carter at the head of the queue takes off his hat to the sky and says, to the cart behind, that he did say turnips, he did say turnips, and the Collector's boy comes out and walks round the load with a long pin. The queue moves up a cart. Nobody in it appears to have enjoyed that as much as they will tell the story.".
  Observe amb_road at arch_road as ambience when true "Carts creak in the queue behind you. Someone is selling pies from a tray with a small gilt bird stamped on every crust.".
  Observe amb_plaza at gate_plaza as sound when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 18 "'Rates! Rates! Fire at ninepence, water at a groat!' The brokers cry them in a chant as old as the Arch, and no one is listening and everyone is.".
  Observe amb_row at row_street as sound when hour(clock) >= 18 or hour(clock) < 8 "Policy Row at night is the quietest street in Quittance. A single clerk is going down it with a lantern and a ladder, snuffing the Offices' lamps, one to a door, in an order that has not changed in a hundred years.".
  Observe amb_brick at brick_lane as sound when hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) < 8 "From the fire-house yards comes the dawn drill: forty buckets passed hand to hand along a whitewashed line, to a sergeant's count, and the sound of boots, and under it, steady, the brigades not looking at each other.".
  Observe amb_wharf at mere_wharf as sound when true "Winches, gulls, the tide-gun at the Lamprey's roof, and from somewhere under the planking the hollow knocking of the river against a hull that is not there.".
  Observe amb_foundry at foundry_row as ambience when true "The Row smells of hot brick and cold iron and, beneath it, faintly, of bread, for no reason that any baker in the Glass Quarter can give.".
  Observe amb_hill at hill_street as sound when true "Surety Hill is silent in the way a church is silent: a cart a long way off, a bell in the Row, and all about you a hush made of lawns and money.".
  Observe amb_salt at salt_lane as ambience when hour(clock) >= 17 or hour(clock) < 5 "Eel-pie, tallow, hot oil, wet wool, smoke from a hundred real hearths, and over it all a fiddle being played by someone with more love than skill.".
  Observe amb_mort at mort_lodge as sound when true "Rooks in the yews, gravel under the porter's boots, and from the almshouse, very faint, a kettle that has been on the boil since breakfast.".
  Observe amb_cellar at cellar_foot as sound when true "The draught in the cellars makes a sound, down the arcade, like someone breathing in to speak and then thinking better of it.".
  Observe amb_gulls at round_furnace as sound when true "The gulls along the wall do not cry. They sit with their feet to the warm bricks, facing the river, which is the wrong way to face if you are a gull.".
  Observe amb_stoves at brick_lane as ambience when day(clock) >= 4 and hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 20 "A kettle boils over on a sill two doors down before the woman has put it on the hob, and she stands and looks at it with her hand on her hip. Along the terrace a stove-door ticks, and ticks, like a thing cooling that has not been lit.".
}

data/adventures/quittance/people.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "The people the spine and more than one small adventure share. Each is declared here, once; the adventures that need them add Topics, Actions and Observations of their own beside the person, and never redeclare them.".

  // ── The Phoenix ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person prewitt "Sedley Prewitt" at prewitt_room {
    Role "Chief Underwriter of the Phoenix". Ancestry human. Calling mage. Level 4. Trait evoker. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns he.
    Known as "a grey man behind a desk" when not knows(party, d_prewitt_met).
    Greets "A grey man rises from behind the desk as you come in, and does not offer his hand. He is neither tall nor short, neither old nor young; he has the stillness of a clock that has been wound for the last time. 'Sedley Prewitt,' he says. 'You are the people the Arch sent up. Do sit. The chair on the left is mine.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Sedley Prewitt. 'The adjusters.'".
  }
  Discovery d_prewitt_met "You have met Sedley Prewitt, the Chief Underwriter of the Phoenix.".
  Person ottoline "Ottoline Prewitt" at phoenix_floor {
    Role "loss-adjuster of the Phoenix". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Level 3. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A young woman in a plain brown coat looks up from a ledger with a pencil behind her ear and another in her hair. 'You'll be the new adjusters,' says Ottoline Prewitt. 'Thank goodness. The Slate has been jammed for a week and I am, regrettably, the Phoenix's entire response to it.'".
    Greets again "'Oh good,' says Ottoline. 'Alive.'".
  }
  Person pettifer "Cornelia Pettifer" at tables_room {
    Role "Keeper of the Tables". Ancestry human. Calling mage. Level 3. Trait evoker. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A small woman at the far end of the room does not look up. She goes on writing, her lips moving, until she reaches the bottom of a column, and then she lifts her head and sees you with the expression of someone who has been surprised by a door. 'Oh,' says Cornelia Pettifer. 'You are not a clerk.'".
    Greets again "Cornelia Pettifer looks up and says, 'Four hundred and two,' and then, with some alarm, 'I beg your pardon. Hello.'".
    Joins "'I will come,' says Cornelia Pettifer, and then, as if someone had said it for her, 'Yes. Good. I will need my pencils.'".
    Leaves "'I think I had better,' says Cornelia Pettifer, 'be somewhere there are numbers.'".
  }
  Person garrity "Captain Garrity" at drill_yard {
    Role "captain of the Phoenix brigade". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 4. Trait toughness. Peaceable. Manner proud. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A broad woman in a blue coat the colour of a bruise is standing in the middle of the yard with a leather helmet under one arm and her hair tied up in a brass-buttoned ribbon. 'Garrity,' she says. 'Captain. If you've come about a mark, it's not mine. If you've come about the Lamprey, it's worse than you think.'".
    Greets again "'You,' says Captain Garrity. It is not clear whether it is a greeting.".
  }
  Person tobias "Tobias Pargeter" at pargeter_front {
    Role "young fireman of the Phoenix". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Trait brave. Uses go. Plans 14 steps. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A young man in a blue coat is standing at the sideboard, looking at a mark nailed on it upside down, with great seriousness. 'I know what it looks like,' says Tobias Pargeter. 'It was meant as a joke.'".
    Greets again "'You again,' says Tobias, brightening.".
    Joins "'Right,' says Tobias, and takes his helmet down from its peg. 'I haven't been told not to.'".
    Leaves "'I'd better go home,' says Tobias. 'My mother will have insured the dinner.'".
  }

  // ── The Lamprey ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person dree "Captain Dree" at dree_room {
    Role "captain of the Lamprey brigade". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 4. Trait toughness. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A small, spare, weathered man in an oilskin coat sits in a chair that is screwed to the floor, whittling a bung. 'Dree,' he says. 'Ezra Dree. Captain of the Lamprey and River brigade. I know what you've heard about me and it is all true except the parts about the dog.'".
    Greets again "'Well,' says Captain Dree. 'You haven't drowned.'".
  }

  // ── The Gas Company ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person gaunt "Lord Gaunt-Halloran" at board_room {
    Role "Chairman of the Gas Company". Ancestry human. Calling bard. Level 3. Peaceable. Manner jovial. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A very large man in a very large coat stands in front of the map of the city with his hands behind him, looking at it as a farmer looks at a field in June. 'Gaunt-Halloran,' he says, in a voice that has been trained to fill a hall. 'Of the Gas Company. We are the future. Do sit down. Do not touch the chandelier.'".
    Greets again "'Splendid,' says Lord Gaunt-Halloran, and means it, for the moment.".
  }

  // ── The Bare Wards ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person skelter "Mr Skelter" at skelter_room {
    Role "rent-collector for the Bare Wards". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 3. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "The grating has a candle behind it, lit, which is against the Ordinance, and a man behind the candle who writes with his left hand and holds a cooling dumpling in his right. He looks at you as one looks at a stain that has not decided whether to spread. 'Rent,' says Mr Skelter. It is not a question. His eyes go to the door you came by, and then, quickly, to a book on the shelf that is no different from the others. 'Nobody with business with me,' he says, 'ever comes by the front.'".
    Greets again "'Rent,' says Mr Skelter, and turns a page.".
  }

  // ── Mortmain and the cellars ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person cray "Pennington Cray" at sov_floor {
    Role "loss-adjuster of the Sovereign Mutual". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 3. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A neat man in a black coat is standing at a counter, tearing a form in two, with great precision, along its fold. 'Cray,' he says. 'Of the Sovereign. Adjuster of annuities. I find that nine in ten are not as alive as claimed. The tenth is usually worse.'".
    Greets again "'You are still here,' says Pennington Cray. 'I find that restful.'".
  }
  Person tench "Dobbin Tench" at cellar_arcade {
    Role "junior clerk of the Old Exchange". Ancestry human. Calling bard. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner compassionate. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A young man in sleeve-guards has set up a small desk between two melted pillars and is writing something down with a quick, apologetic scratch of the pen. 'Don't tread on the queue,' says Dobbin Tench, 'please. I mean, you can't; they're not quite there. But they do notice.'".
    Greets again "'Oh good,' says Dobbin Tench. 'Someone who can see them.'".
  }

  // ── The hill ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person auberon "Auberon Hearn" at hearn_hearth {
    Role "last Hearthkeeper of Quittance". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Level 4. Trait vitalist. Peaceable. Manner compassionate. Pronouns he.
    Greets "An old man sits close by the little hearth in a chair padded with cushions and old coats. He has his hands to the coal. At the sound of the door he looks round with a brilliant, vague, welcoming smile. 'Honora?' he says. 'No. No, of course. How very good of you to come. Are you the coal-men?'".
    Greets again "'Oh,' says Auberon Hearn, 'you've come back. How kind. I think we've met.'".
  }
  Person ianthe "Ianthe Corbett" at corbett_study {
    Role "surveyor of the Guild". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Level 3. Uses go. Plans 14 steps. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns she.
    Known as "a woman with a rope on her shoulder" when not knows(party, d_ianthe_met).
    Greets "A woman is sitting on the desk with her boots on a plan, eating an apple and examining the ceiling with the intensity of someone assessing a dead man's stairs. 'Ianthe Corbett,' she says. 'Surveyor. If it's about a mark, I'll say now that I don't do favours. If it's about a roof, I'll do it for nothing.'".
    Greets again "'Hello again,' says Ianthe Corbett. 'Have you brought me a roof?'".
  }
  Discovery d_ianthe_met "You have met Ianthe Corbett, who surveys the roofs of Quittance.".
}

data/adventures/quittance/placed.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  // The Assured City as a country beyond a march: the company that comes down the north road to the Declaration Arch is
  // the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  // What the country below says of the city (its keepers' rumour of the blank Receipt): once Reckoning has come, one way
  // or another, it is old news there, and they say so to whoever comes back down the north road.
  Entity word: fact "What is said of Quittance in the country below.".
  Rule word_old when (reached(end_burning) or reached(end_slaying) or reached(general_average) or reached(hospitality) or reached(quittance_best) or reached(quittance_contested) or reached(controlled_loss) or reached(evacuated_loss) or reached(end_lapse)) and not stale(word) { Assert stale(word). }
}

data/adventures/quittance/q_annuitant.ky:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "The Annuitant: Mortmain, an annuity paid for ninety-four years to a woman of a hundred and thirty-one, the adjuster who will stop it on Monday, the almshouse that lives on it, and the grate on the catacomb stair.".

  // ── What the matter is, as a number ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // an_status: 0 pending . 1 held (Cray sits on the stop) . 2 secured . 3 deferred (bought, shamed or forged: it
  // comes undone) . 4 stopped . 5 restored after the stop . 6 exposed (stopped for good).
  // The stop falls on Monday, day 2, at noon (watch 312). Cray reads it to the seven in the day-room from nine.
  Measure an_status(group).
  Relation an_win(group). Relation an_fed(group). Relation an_giving(group). Relation an_trust(group).
  Relation an_bought(group). Relation an_shamed(group). Relation an_forged(group). Relation an_exposed(group).
  Relation an_asked_badly(group). Relation an_shame_failed(group). Relation an_read_failed(group).
  Relation an_policy_had(group). Relation an_lawful(group). Relation an_grate_forced(group).
  Relation an_slighted_cray(group). Relation an_slighted_sovereign(group). Relation an_wragg_cross(group).
  Relation an_tea_taken(group).

  Discovery an_claim "The Sovereign Mutual means to stop Mrs Jessamy Oakes's annuity on Monday, at noon: a hundred and thirty-one is not an age, and seven people in the almshouse live on what she is paid.".
  Discovery an_truth "'Mrs Oakes' is a succession of women of one family. Each takes the name when the last has died, and the present one is nineteen.".
  Discovery an_wording "The policy pays 'so long as Jessamy Oakes shall be living in her name'. The family has kept it to the letter.".
  Discovery an_cray_mother "Pennington Cray's mother did the almshouse linen, and lies on the third terrace of Mortmain under a stone with no brass plate.".
  Discovery an_quill_annuity "The Sovereign's Life Office pays a second annuity, quarterly since the Burning, to 'the household of Honora Quill', on a named life that is left blank.".

  // ── The places I add ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place an_terrace "the third terrace" is room within mort at 0, 2 outdoors.
  Passage an_row_terrace "the lawn steps" is path between annuity_row and an_terrace taking 3 minutes.
  Observe an_terrace_scene at an_terrace when true "A lawn of old graves, all of them with their brass plates; the Sovereign's sun, the year and a number. Under a yew one stone has none. The sun on it has been scratched in with a nail, by someone small, and gone over with a nail since, now and then, by someone larger.".
  Observe an_terrace_grave at an_terrace when true "A pressed bunch of rosemary lies on the stone with no plate. It is not the season for rosemary. Somebody keeps it here, and somebody changes it." teaches an_cray_mother.

  // ── Things that pass ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind an_policy_k "the Oakes policy" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "A sheet gone the colour of weak tea, in a round clerk's hand that wastes no word and grudges none. The Sovereign's sun is at the head. The sum is to be paid 'to Jessamy Oakes, widow, and to no other, so long as Jessamy Oakes shall be living in her name; and the Mutual shall not ask of her what the poor are not asked, which is proof'.".
  Item an_policy "the Oakes policy" is an_policy_k at nowhere.
  Kind an_register_k "the sexton's register of the unclaimed" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "A narrow book of ruled paper, ninety-four years of Wragg's predecessors and Wragg, the names of the dead below the catacomb stair who were never called for. Each has a year, and a line left blank for the day somebody comes.".
  Item an_register "the sexton's register" is an_register_k at nowhere.
  Kind an_key_k "the Oakes vault key" like cell_key described "A small brass key on a black ribbon, worn smooth by women's thumbs. It is for the Oakes vault, and the vault is under the catacomb stair.".
  Item an_oakes_key "the Oakes vault key" is an_key_k at nowhere.

  // ── The Slate, and the lodge ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe an_slate at slip_room when day(clock) <= 2 and an_status(party) < 4 "CLAIMS OPEN: Sovereign Mutual v. a hundred and thirty-one years. Adjuster wanted to certify an annuitant at Mortmain before the stop on Monday. The fee is a third of nothing, and the hearse is on the Mutual." teaches an_claim.
  Observe an_slate_late at slip_room when an_status(party) >= 4 "TOTAL LOSSES: an annuity, stopped at Mortmain. The Sovereign regrets.".
  Observe an_notice at annuity_row when an_status(party) < 4 "A printed notice is pinned to the gate of the Oakes cottage with a drawing-pin through the Sovereign's sun: ANNUITY OF MRS J. OAKES, AGED 131, WILL BE REVIEWED ON MONDAY AT NOON. THE SOVEREIGN MUTUAL PAYS." teaches an_claim.
  Observe an_row_stopped at annuity_row when an_status(party) == 4 or an_status(party) == 6 "The shutters on the Oakes cottage are closed. The notice on the gate has been replaced by another, with the same sun: ANNUITY CEASED.".
  Observe an_alms_cold at alms_room when an_status(party) == 4 or an_status(party) == 6 "The stove has not been lit. Seven shawls sit in seven chairs with the particular patience of people who have been told to expect nothing in writing.".
  Observe an_alms_warm at alms_room when an_status(party) == 2 or an_status(party) == 5 "The stove is lit, and the kettle is on it, and on the wall beside the leaflets somebody has pinned a drawing of a coal.".

  // ── The clock ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule an_cray_visits when watch(clock) >= 294 and watch(clock) < 312 and an_status(party) == 0 and at(cray, sov_floor) { Assert at(cray, alms_room). }
  Rule an_cray_back when watch(clock) >= 312 and (at(cray, alms_room) or at(cray, oakes_room)) { Assert at(cray, sov_floor). }
  Rule an_monday when watch(clock) >= 312 and an_status(party) == 0 says "Somewhere in Mortmain a clerk's pen goes down on a form for the last time, and the Sovereign's sun is struck through." {
    Set an_status(party) to 4. }
  Rule an_relents when watch(clock) >= 744 and an_status(party) == 1 says "Pennington Cray signs the stop at last, with a hand that was not steady, and takes it to the Board himself." { Set an_status(party) to 4. }
  Rule an_undone when watch(clock) >= 864 and an_status(party) == 3 says "The deferment lapses at midnight, as deferments do. The Sovereign's sun is struck through at Mortmain." { Set an_status(party) to 4. }
  Rule an_forgery_found when watch(clock) >= 864 and an_status(party) == 4 and an_forged(party) and not an_slighted_sovereign(party) {
    Assert an_slighted_sovereign(party). Decrease regard(sovereign) by 2 or to nothing. }
  // Cray, remembering, sits on the stop; if it was already struck he reopens the file while the week is young.
  Rule an_held when arc(cray) >= 1 and an_status(party) == 0 and not an_bought(party) { Set an_status(party) to 1. }
  Rule an_reopened when arc(cray) >= 1 and an_status(party) == 4 and not an_bought(party) and not an_forged(party) and watch(clock) < 744 {
    Set an_status(party) to 1. }
  // A win: the stop is taken off (or put back to rights).
  Rule an_win_early when an_win(party) and an_status(party) < 4 { Set an_status(party) to 2. Retract an_win(party). }
  Rule an_win_late when an_win(party) and an_status(party) == 4 { Set an_status(party) to 5. Retract an_win(party). }

  Observe an_cray_ally at sov_floor when arc(cray) >= 2 "Pennington Cray is at his counter, tearing a form with no particular precision, and has put a second cup, which is chipped, on the sill for visitors.".
  Observe an_cray_held at sov_floor when arc(cray) == 1 and not an_bought(party) "Pennington Cray is at his counter with the Oakes file in front of him, closed, and a hand flat on it, as if it might get up.".

  // ── Pennington Cray, who is paid by the denied claim ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic an_cray_what with cray "Ask Cray what he makes of the Oakes annuity" when not an_shamed(party) once {
    Says "'A hundred and thirty-one,' says Pennington Cray, and tears a form in half along its fold. 'The oldest recorded Englishwoman was a hundred and sixty-nine, and she was a Welshwoman, and wrong. I am paid, you understand, by the denial. It is a cleaner arrangement than you would think. I intend to correct Mrs Oakes on Monday at noon, and I shall do it very gently, in the day-room, so that the seven can hear it at the same time.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, an_claim). }
  }
  Topic an_cray_knows with cray "Ask Cray whether he believes in Mrs Oakes" when knows(actor, an_claim) and not an_shamed(party) once {
    Says "'I believe,' says Cray, 'that someone is drinking her tea. I find that the proof of life is a second cup.' He looks at the form in his hand as if it had said it. 'No. You will not move me with evidence. I know what is in that cottage. I have known since my first quarter. The Sovereign does not pay me to know.'".
  }
  Action an_cray_ask(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Cray, quietly, with the form put down between you, where his mother is buried" {
    Speaker cray.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(cray, site) and knows(actor, an_cray_mother) and arc(cray) == 0 and not an_asked_badly(actor) and not an_shamed(actor) and an_status(party) < 6.
    Time 5 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Set arc(cray) to 1. }
    On failure { Assert an_asked_badly(actor). }
    Result "Cray puts the form down. He does not do it as a man puts down a form; he does it as a man puts down a child. 'The third terrace,' he says. 'Under the yew. They would not give her a plate, because she was linen and not an annuitant, and so I scratched the sun myself, with a nail, when I was nine, and I have gone over it since.' He looks at the form. 'I have been stopping other people's mothers for twenty-two years,' says Cray. 'It is not that I did not notice.'".
    Otherwise "Cray looks at you, and at the form, and picks the form up again. 'Ah,' he says. 'You have been to the third terrace.' It is said in the voice he uses to read a stop. 'Good day to you.' He does not tear anything; this is worse.".
  }

  // The kindness, witnessed: Cray reads the stop in the day-room on Monday morning. Rations given out while he is
  // there move him a step; the same rations given on another day only warm the seven.
  Action an_share(actor: group) "Share your rations out among the seven, there in the day-room" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, alms_room) and quantity(actor, rations) >= 1 and an_status(party) < 6.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, rations) by 1. Assert an_fed(actor). Assert an_giving(actor). }
    Result "There is no more than a day's bread between you, and you cut it into seven, which is not as easy as it sounds. Nobody thanks you. Seven people accept it at once and with great dignity, as though it had been owing, and Mr Tarbuck says 'WHAT?' and is told, and says 'GOOD', and eats his with his eyes shut.".
  }
  Rule an_kind_seen when an_giving(party) and at(party, alms_room) and at(cray, alms_room) and arc(cray) == 0 and not an_shamed(party)
    says "Pennington Cray watches the bread go round with the form held at his side. When it comes to the chair by the window, where the smallest of the seven has been given the larger half, he looks away at the leaflets on the wall, and says, to nobody, 'My mother cut it like that.' He does not read the stop." {
    Set arc(cray) to 1. }
  Rule an_giving_done when an_giving(party) { Retract an_giving(party). }

  // A better bonus: Cray is paid by the denial, and will take a larger one for a smaller trouble.
  Action an_bonus(actor: group, site: place) "Offer Cray ten coin, as a bonus in place of the denial, to leave the Oakes file shut for a quarter" {
    Speaker cray.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(cray, site) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 10 and arc(cray) == 0 and an_status(party) < 4 and not an_shamed(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Assert an_bought(actor). Set arc(cray) to 1. Set an_status(party) to 3. Assert an_slighted_sovereign(actor). Decrease regard(sovereign) by 1 or to nothing. }
    Result "Cray counts it with his thumb, the way a man counts who was taught by a nun. 'It is not a bribe,' he says. 'It is a bonus in a different currency. I am bound to take whichever is larger.' The ten coin goes into the black coat. 'A quarter,' he says. 'I shall be thinking of what to say to the Board at Michaelmas. You will think of something better. I find that restful.'".
  }

  // Shaming him: only on Monday morning, in the day-room, in front of the seven.
  Action an_shame(actor: group) "Ask Cray to read the stop aloud to the seven, one at a time, by name, and look at each" {
    Speaker cray.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, alms_room) and at(cray, alms_room) and arc(cray) == 0 and an_status(party) == 0 and not an_shame_failed(actor).
    Time 15 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert an_shamed(actor). Set an_status(party) to 3. Assert an_slighted_cray(actor). }
    On failure { Assert an_shame_failed(actor). }
    Result "Cray reads. He reads the first name, and the first shawl turns, and he reads the second, and the second shawl turns, and at the fourth, which is Mr Tarbuck, who cannot hear it, and looks up at him anyway with the trust of the deaf, he stops. 'I shall leave it with the Board,' he says, in a voice like a closing drawer, and folds the form and goes, and does not look at you, and will not look at you again.".
    Otherwise "Cray reads all seven, by name, and looks at each; he has done it before. When he reaches the end he turns the page, and the seven, who have been looked at by a good many men with forms, look at you, rather than him, as the cause.".
  }
  // A shamed Cray has no more to say to the company, and will not be asked.
  Observe an_cray_cold at sov_floor when an_shamed(party) "Pennington Cray is at his counter, tearing a form into very small pieces. He does not look up.".

  // The forged testimonial: the Sovereign asks each year for a physician's certificate that its annuitant is living.
  Action an_forge(actor: group) "Fill in a spoiled certificate of life for Mrs Oakes, in Dr Ibbotson's hand, and put it on the file" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, sov_floor) and an_status(party) < 4 and not an_forged(actor) and not an_shamed(actor).
    Time 20 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert an_forged(actor). Set an_status(party) to 3. }
    On failure { Assert an_forged(actor). Assert an_slighted_cray(actor). Set an_status(party) to 4. Decrease regard(sovereign) by 1 or to nothing. }
    Result "There is a stack of spoiled certificates under the counter, because the Sovereign's physicians cannot keep from beginning with 'I hereby'. You choose one, and a pen, and the hand of a man who has been signing the same form since the Burning, and put it on the Oakes file where a clerk will find it in the morning. It is a good hand. It is very slightly the wrong shade of doctor.".
    Otherwise "You have the certificate on the file for as long as it takes Cray to come back from the stairs. He reads it in the doorway without coming in. 'Dr Ibbotson,' he says, 'has been dead for four years. He does not sign with a flourish on the L.' He tears it along its fold, with great precision, and strikes the Oakes line through. 'Monday has been brought forward.'".
  }
  Rule an_forged_with_cray when an_forged(party) and an_status(party) == 3 and arc(cray) >= 1 and not an_bought(party) { Set an_status(party) to 2. }

  // The wording, read and laid before him.
  Action an_press_open(actor: group) "Look for the Oakes policy among the Life Office's deeds" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, sov_floor) and not an_policy_had(actor) and (holding(actor, adjuster_licence) or arc(cray) >= 1 or capable(actor, lockwork)).
    Time 20 minutes.
    On success { Give an_policy to actor. Assert an_policy_had(actor). }
    Result "The deeds are kept in a press with a lock the size of a snuff-box. You come at it as the company is able: by the licence that entitles you to see a policy you are certifying, or by a word from Cray, or by the thin wire. The Oakes policy is the fourth sheet, and is the only one in the press that has been unfolded in the last year.".
  }
  Action an_policy_ask(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Mrs Oakes, as one who has promised to keep her secret, for the family's copy of the policy" {
    Speaker an_oakes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(an_oakes, site) and an_trust(actor) and not an_policy_had(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Give an_policy to actor. Assert an_policy_had(actor). }
    Result "'It is in the Bible-box,' says Mrs Oakes, in a voice that has not been through an ear-trumpet in its life. 'The Sovereign has one in the press, but this is the one that was read aloud to each of us. You may keep it a day. It is not to go in the fire. Mother put it in the fire once, by mistake, and it came out of the kettle.'".
  }
  Action an_read(actor: group) "Read the Oakes policy through, clause by clause, on the bench by the rose" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, annuity_row) and holding(actor, an_policy_k) and not knows(actor, an_wording) and not an_read_failed(actor).
    Time 20 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, an_wording). Assert knows(actor, d_wording_style). }
    On failure { Assert an_read_failed(actor). }
    Result "You read it through, and it will not be a fraud however you look at it. It says what it means. It says it twice, once for the Sovereign and once for the woman, and the second time it says a little more than the first. 'So long as Jessamy Oakes shall be living in her name' means exactly what the family has taken it to mean, and could not have been written by anyone who did not intend it to. It is the most generous sentence you have read in this city, and it is in a clerk's hand.".
    Otherwise "You read it three times. It is a perfectly good annuity, in a perfectly good hand, and you can see that there is something in the sixth line and you cannot see what.".
  }
  Action an_wording_show(actor: group, site: place) "Lay the Oakes policy before Cray, and put your finger on 'in her name'" {
    Speaker cray.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(cray, site) and knows(actor, an_wording) and holding(actor, an_policy_k) and an_status(party) != 2 and an_status(party) != 5 and an_status(party) != 6 and not an_shamed(actor).
    Time 15 minutes.
    On success { Assert an_win(actor). Increase regard(sovereign) by 1. }
    Result "Cray reads it standing. He reads it again, with his lips moving, which nobody has seen. 'In her name,' he says. 'It is a very handsome clause. I could not have drafted it better, and I am paid to dislike drafting.' He puts the form he was holding into the stove. 'On my reading the instrument is satisfied. On the Board's reading it will be satisfied by Friday, once I have explained what satisfied means.' He gives the policy back by its corners. 'I should like to know,' he says, 'who wrote it. It has the air of someone who was not afraid of being taken advantage of.'".
  }
  Topic an_tarbuck_read with an_tarbuck "Hand Mr Tarbuck the policy, and ask whether he can make anything of the sixth line" when holding(actor, an_policy_k) and an_read_failed(actor) and not knows(actor, an_wording) once {
    Says "Mr Tarbuck holds it at arm's length, and then very close. 'IN HER NAME,' he says, to the room, which jumps. 'It's not a hundred and thirty-one, you fool, it's a NAME. My sister had a name for forty years and no one asked HER how old she was.' He hands it back, delighted. 'That's Miss Quill's writing, that is. She never wrote a sentence that wanted to catch you out.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, an_wording). Assert knows(actor, d_wording_style). }
  }

  // The proof, given to the man who does not need it.
  Action an_expose(actor: group, site: place) "Give Cray the proof he has been waiting for: the present Mrs Oakes is nineteen" {
    Speaker cray.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(cray, site) and knows(actor, an_truth) and an_status(party) < 6 and an_status(party) != 2 and an_status(party) != 5.
    Time 10 minutes.
    Grave "Told to Cray, it is told to the Sovereign; there is no taking it back, and the seven live on that annuity.".
    On success { Set an_status(party) to 6. Assert an_exposed(actor). Increase regard(sovereign) by 1. Retract an_trust(actor). Assert an_wragg_cross(actor). }
    Result "'Nineteen,' says Cray. He writes it on the form, which is a new one, and there is the particular silence of a man who has been handed what he already had. 'It is very kind. It makes the file shorter.' He seems about to say something else and does not. 'The stop will be effective from the quarter-day. I shall see that the girl is not prosecuted. I do not promise the rest.'".
  }
  Topic an_cray_books with cray "Ask Cray what the Life Office's books say of the Quills" when arc(cray) >= 2 once {
    Says "'You are not asking as the Sovereign's adjuster,' says Cray. 'I am not answering as one.' He takes you to a press that is not the one with the deeds, and turns the key with his back to the door. 'A second annuity. Quarterly, since the Burning, to the household of Honora Quill. The life named on it is blank. The sum is called for by a boy from the hill, who signs with a drawing of a coal.' He closes it. 'I have never been asked why we pay it. It is paid. I find that, on the whole, I like the Sovereign for it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, an_quill_annuity). }
  }

  // The tea: Cray comes to the parlour, and the girl takes off the shawls.
  Action an_bring_cray(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Cray if he will take tea with Mrs Oakes, as an annuitant's guest and not the Sovereign's man" {
    Speaker cray.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(cray, site) and arc(cray) == 1 and not an_bought(actor) and an_trust(actor) and an_status(party) != 6 and not an_tea_taken(actor).
    Time 20 minutes.
    On success { Assert at(cray, oakes_room). Retract at(cray, site). }
    Result "'Tea,' says Cray. 'I have been in that parlour fifty times and I have never once been offered the tea.' He puts his hat on, and takes it off again, and carries it in his hand the whole length of the Row.".
  }
  Topic an_shawls_off with an_oakes "Ask Mrs Oakes to put the ear-trumpet down, with Cray there to see" when at(cray, oakes_room) and arc(cray) == 1 and an_trust(actor) once {
    Says "Mrs Oakes puts down the ear-trumpet. She takes off the cap, and the first shawl, and the second, and the third, and she is nineteen, with a long plait and an expression of enormous steadiness. 'I am the sixth,' says Tamsin Oakes. 'I am sorry about the trumpet. It was my great-aunt's.' Cray looks at her over the top of a form he has not yet torn. Then he sits down in the chair that is not the great chair, and she pours him tea in the second cup, which is the one that has always been poured for whoever came before. 'Miss Oakes,' he says, 'the policy says living in her name.' 'Yes,' says Tamsin. 'We read it every quarter-day.' 'Then I do not see,' says Pennington Cray, 'that there is anything whatever to stop.'".
    On discuss { Set arc(cray) to 2. Assert an_win(actor). Assert witness(cray). Assert an_tea_taken(actor). Increase regard(sovereign) by 2. }
  }

  // ── Mrs Oakes, the sixth, who is nineteen ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person an_oakes "Mrs Jessamy Oakes" at oakes_room {
    Role "annuitant of the Sovereign Mutual, aged 131 on the policy". Ancestry human. Calling bard. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns she.
    Greets "An ear-trumpet rises out of the shawls, followed by a cap, and then, at some interval, by a voice that has been practised. 'EH?' says Mrs Jessamy Oakes. 'WHO IS IT? IS IT THE VICAR? I HAVE BEEN WAITING FOR THE VICAR SINCE THE REFORM BILL.'".
    Greets again "'EH?' says Mrs Oakes, and the second cup, at her elbow, rattles in its saucer.".
  }
  Topic an_shout with an_oakes "Shout a greeting into the ear-trumpet" when not an_trust(actor) once {
    Says "'THE EARL OF CHESTERFIELD DIED OF IT,' says Mrs Oakes, with great satisfaction, to a question you did not put. 'MY FATHER SAID SO. MY FATHER WAS A CHANDLER. I HAD HIM IN THE FIRE.' A pause. 'I MEAN THE FIRE HAD HIM. I AM VERY OLD.' This is delivered a little too quickly, as one says a line learnt.".
  }
  Topic an_cup with an_oakes "Ask whom the second cup is for" when not an_trust(actor) once {
    Says "'THE VICAR,' says Mrs Oakes. She moves the tray, a little, so that the cup is behind the teapot. It is not the movement of a woman of a hundred and thirty-one; it is the movement of a girl moving a cup.".
  }
  Action an_see(actor: group, site: place) "Look past the shawls at Mrs Oakes's hands, and at how the second cup is poured" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(an_oakes, site) and not knows(actor, an_truth).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, an_truth). }
    Result "The hands in the mittens are not a hundred and thirty-one. They are nineteen, and bitten at the nail. The second cup has been poured, as a cup is poured for a guest, and set a little to the side, with its handle turned toward the chair that nobody is in. You understand that you are being given tea by a girl in a cap, and that the second cup is for the one who had the name before her.".
    Otherwise "A very old lady looks at you out of her shawls with eyes that may be a little brighter than they ought to be. There is nothing you can put your finger on. She nods, deafly, to a question you did not ask.".
  }
  Topic an_tell_girl with an_oakes "Tell her you know, and that you mean her family no harm" when knows(actor, an_truth) and not an_trust(actor) and an_status(party) != 6 once {
    Says "The ear-trumpet goes down in her lap. 'Oh, thank God,' says the girl, in an entirely different voice, and rubs her back with both hands. 'Tamsin. Tamsin Oakes. I am the sixth. My great-aunt was the fifth, and she died in March, and Mother says that nobody in the Mutual has seen Mrs Oakes since the Jubilee but the doctor, and the doctor is a Quill's cousin.' She looks at the second cup. 'It is the policy. It says in her name. Mrs Oakes is a name, and we keep it. The Mutual pays the seven because we cannot eat a hundred and thirty-one years of it ourselves.'".
    On discuss { Assert an_trust(actor). }
  }
  Topic an_why_oakes with an_oakes "Ask Tamsin why the family did not simply say so" when an_trust(actor) once {
    Says "'And be asked for proof,' says Tamsin. 'It is a policy for a widow, whom the Mutual shall not ask for proof. I should be asked for proof of a thing I cannot prove. I would be a girl of nineteen asking for eleven pounds a quarter.' She takes the cap from the arm of the chair and puts it on, without looking, as one puts on a face. 'I am a very good Mrs Oakes. I have been practising since I was nine.'".
  }
  Topic an_key_ask with an_oakes "Ask whether the Oakes vault under the catacomb stair might be visited" when an_trust(actor) and not holding(actor, an_key_k) once {
    Says "'Mother and the aunts are down there,' says Tamsin. 'The five, and the first, who was the real one.' She gets up and goes to the Bible-box, and comes back with a brass key on a ribbon. 'It opens the grating, from the top, for the family. You will bring it back. Say my name, if you meet anyone, and tell them it is for the sixth Mrs Oakes, who sends her respects to the first.'".
    On discuss { Give an_oakes_key to actor. }
  }

  // ── The almshouse's seven ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person an_mawdsley "Mother Mawdsley" at alms_room {
    Role "eldest of the seven". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A woman in the chair nearest the stove does not get up. 'You'll be wanting the Row,' says Mother Mawdsley. 'We don't get visitors, in the day-room, unless they've come with a form. Have you come with a form?'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Mother Mawdsley. 'You haven't a form. Sit.'".
  }
  Person an_tarbuck "Mr Tarbuck" at alms_room {
    Role "the deafest of the seven". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner jovial. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A very old man with an ear-trumpet of his own, rather larger than anybody's, turns it toward you like a gun. 'WHAT?' says Mr Tarbuck.".
    Greets again "'WHAT?' says Mr Tarbuck, and beams.".
  }
  Topic an_mawd_seven with an_mawdsley "Ask Mother Mawdsley how the seven live" when true once {
    Says "'On Mrs Oakes,' says Mother Mawdsley. 'The Mutual pays the almshouse by way of her. She brings it in a pudding-basin, quarter-day, and we take it out with a spoon. It is not a thing we say. Where would we go? The Sovereign owns the roof.' She looks at the stove. 'Monday, they tell us. At noon. They have always been very punctual about the end of things.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, an_claim). }
  }
  Topic an_mawd_cup with an_mawdsley "Ask Mother Mawdsley who looks after Mrs Oakes, and for whom the second cup is" when an_fed(actor) and not knows(actor, an_truth) once {
    Says "She looks at the bread, and at the door, and then at you. 'You have been fair,' she says. 'It's the girl. It has always been a girl. When one dies the next one is told, and she puts on the cap, and the cup is for the one that went. Tamsin is the sixth.' She takes your wrist for a moment, with a hand like a clothes-peg. 'It's a name, you see. It's only ever been a name. They have been very careful of it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, an_truth). }
  }
  Topic an_tarbuck_cray with an_tarbuck "Ask Mr Tarbuck about the neat man in black who reads the stop" when true once {
    Says "'WHAT?' says Mr Tarbuck. You ask again. 'THAT'S LITTLE PEN CRAY,' he says. 'HIS MOTHER DID THE LINEN. SHE'S ON THE THIRD TERRACE, UNDER THE YEW, AND THEY WOULDN'T GIVE HER A PLATE.' He taps his chest. 'I CARRIED HER.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, an_cray_mother). }
  }
  Topic an_mawd_kin with an_mawdsley "Ask Mother Mawdsley if any of her people were in the Burning" when true once {
    Says "'My mother's mother's mother,' says Mother Mawdsley. 'Lettice Gorringe, a widow, who had a sideboard. She stood in a queue at the Exchange to be told what she was owed, and the Exchange fell on the queue. We never had a grave to take her to.' A pause. 'I believe the family has been waiting to be told what she was owed for rather longer than the Sovereign has been waiting to stop Mrs Oakes.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, qu_descendant). }
  }
  Topic an_mawd_hearth with an_mawdsley "Ask Mother Mawdsley whether the almshouse would keep a hearth lit for the Night" when an_status(party) == 2 or an_status(party) == 5 once {
    Says "'We have a coal,' says Mother Mawdsley, 'in the stove, which has not been let out since the Burning, and which we have never mentioned to the Sovereign, who would say it was a fire risk.' She looks round at the six. 'There's none of us can carry it far. But there's seven of us here, and we can keep a stove. Send us a coal on the night and we shall sit by it until it's done.'".
    On discuss { Assert keeper(mort). }
  }
  Topic an_mawd_refuse with an_mawdsley "Ask Mother Mawdsley whether the almshouse would keep a hearth lit for the Night" when an_status(party) != 2 and an_status(party) != 5 once {
    Says "'There'll be no hearth in this house,' says Mother Mawdsley, 'while we are waiting to be put out of it. Come and ask when you have done what you can.'".
  }

  // ── The sexton, and the grate on the catacomb stair ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person an_wragg "Josiah Wragg" at catacomb_head {
    Role "sexton of Mortmain". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A man in a clean smock is sitting on an upturned barrow by the grating, shelling peas into his hat. 'Wragg,' he says. 'Sexton. You'll be lost. Nobody comes down this end but the family, and they've a key.'".
    Greets again "'Still lost,' says Josiah Wragg, not unkindly.".
  }
  Topic an_wragg_stair with an_wragg "Ask the sexton about the stair" when true once {
    Says "'It goes where the unclaimed go,' says Wragg. 'Under the stair, there's a vault, and the vault's full of the Burning's dead that nobody called for, stacked by year. Ninety-four years, and every label says UNCLAIMED. I take them flowers on the day.' He looks at the grating. 'I'd sooner it stayed shut. I'd sooner still it was visited by somebody who'd say their names. There's a clerk at the bottom, so they tell me, with a book. I have a register. It has never gone down the stair.'".
  }
  Topic an_wragg_register with an_wragg "Promise Wragg you will carry his register of the unclaimed to the clerk below, and bring it back marked" when not an_wragg_cross(actor) and not promiseMade(an_wragg_promise) once {
    Says "Wragg wipes his hands on his smock, and reaches into the barrow, and brings out a narrow book wrapped in a Sovereign leaflet. 'Forty-one names with no claimant,' he says. 'He'll know them or he won't. Bring it back with a mark against the ones he knows. And mind the grating; it's older than the stair.' He turns the key on his belt in the lock, and does not look to see if you have gone down.".
    On discuss { Give an_register to actor. Assert promiseMade(an_wragg_promise). Assert sextonLeave(actor). }
  }
  Topic an_wragg_friend with an_wragg "Remind Wragg what you did for the seven" when (an_status(party) == 2 or an_status(party) == 5) and not sextonLeave(actor) and not an_wragg_cross(actor) once {
    Says "'The almshouse has been telling me,' says Wragg. 'Mother Mawdsley says there was a neat man in black who didn't stop it.' He stands up, and the peas go down in a hat. 'The stair is not mine to give, but the key is. Go down. Mind your lamp.'".
    On discuss { Assert sextonLeave(actor). }
  }
  Promise an_wragg_promise "to carry the sexton's register to the clerk below and bring it back marked" to an_wragg
    kept when qu_register_given(party) "Wragg has the register back across his knee, and turns the pages, and does not say anything for some time."
    broken when day(clock) >= 8 and not qu_register_given(party) "Somewhere in Mortmain a sexton looks at an empty barrow, and goes on shelling peas." { Assert an_wragg_cross(party). Retract sextonLeave(party). }.

  Rule an_register_thanks when qu_register_given(party) and not an_register_thanked(party) { Assert an_register_thanked(party). Increase regard(sovereign) by 1. }
  Relation an_register_thanked(group).

  Thing an_grate "the grating over the catacomb stair" on catacomb_stair {
    State locked blocking "A low iron grating shuts the stair under the worn sun, with a padlock that has been oiled and a hasp that has not.".
    State open "The grating stands open on its hinge, and the cold comes up out of the stair like a held breath.".
    Change pick "Pick the padlock" from locked to open needing lockwork at catacomb_head.
    Change wrench "Wrench the grating off its staples" from locked to open needing brawn at catacomb_head.
    Change family "Unlock the grating with the Oakes vault key" from locked to open needing an_oakes_key at catacomb_head.
  }
  Action an_rite(actor: group) "Say the burial office over the worn sun, and let the grating be a door" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, catacomb_head) and state(an_grate, locked) and capable(actor, rites).
    Time 15 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, rites, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state(an_grate, open). Assert an_lawful(actor). }
    Result "The sun over the grating is a funeral seal under the wear: the Sovereign buried its dead under it, and the office still answers. You say the words you would say over any of the unclaimed. The padlock opens, as though a hand on the other side had been waiting for the last word.".
    Otherwise "You say the office, and mean it, and the sun does not stir. A wren looks down at you from the wall.".
  }
  Action an_sexton_opens(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Wragg to unlock the grating for you" {
    Speaker an_wragg.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(an_wragg, site) and state(an_grate, locked) and sextonLeave(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert state(an_grate, open). Assert an_lawful(actor). }
    Result "Wragg unlocks the padlock and hangs it on the hasp, for show. 'It makes it a visit,' he says, 'and not a trespass.'".
  }
  Action an_key_lawful(actor: group) "Say the sixth Mrs Oakes's name at the grating, and unlock it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, catacomb_head) and state(an_grate, locked) and holding(actor, an_key_k).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert state(an_grate, open). Assert an_lawful(actor). }
    Result "'For the sixth Mrs Oakes,' you say, to the grating, 'who sends her respects to the first.' The key turns on its own warmth. It seems that is what the lock was waiting to be told.".
  }
  Rule an_grate_damage when state(an_grate, open) and not an_lawful(party) and not an_grate_forced(party) says "Behind you, as the grating gives, a man sets down a hat of peas." {
    Assert an_grate_forced(party). Assert an_wragg_cross(party). Assert an_slighted_sovereign(party). Decrease regard(sovereign) by 1 or to nothing. }
  Observe an_grate_scene at catacomb_head when true "The worn sun over the grating is a funeral seal, you can see now, under the wear: the Mutual put its dead under it, and a rim of lettering round it says IN LIFE AND AFTER.".
  Observe an_foot_scene at catacomb_foot when true "Against the wall by the slot a bronze plate has been set, so old it has gone to the colour of the bones: OAKES, with a row of five names under it, and above them, in a plainer hand, the first.".
}

data/adventures/quittance/q_bakery.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "Tolliver's bakery: an oven that fails the Smokeless Ordinance because it draws, and the reason it draws.".

  // ══ The survey, and the cover ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // The Phoenix's Inspector of Flues surveys Tolliver's oven at noon on the second day (watch 312). The cover lapses
  // at midnight the day after (watch 384) unless something has been satisfied. The oven keeps a Lent coal, and the
  // flue is not what draws it: fix the flue and the coal goes out.
  Entity bk_bakery: group "Tolliver's bakery".
  Relation bk_pass(group). Relation bk_judged(group). Relation bk_failed(group). Relation bk_lapsed(group).
  Relation bk_coal_dead(group). Relation bk_helped(group). Relation bk_bread(group). Relation bk_reprieved(group).
  Relation bk_flue_wrecked(group). Relation bk_ianthe_there(group). Relation bk_flash_told(group).
  // What the company did, said by name for the Hearing to read.
  Relation bk_flue_fixed(group). Relation bk_bribed_gudgeon(group). Relation bk_exempt(group). Relation bk_registered(group).
  Relation bk_trusted(group). Relation bk_by_bread(group). Relation bk_by_ianthe(group). Relation bk_own_mark(group).
  Relation bk_ianthe(group). Relation bk_g_asked(group). Relation bk_gwen_told(group). Relation bk_coal_known_dead(group).
  Query bk_lives() means not bk_coal_dead(bk_bakery).

  Discovery bk_survey "Tolliver's oven is to be surveyed under the Smokeless Ordinance at noon on the second day, and the bakery's cover lapses the day after unless it passes.".
  Discovery bk_claim "The Slate has a claim chalked on it: a bakery in Brick Lane, an oven, an Inspector, and a Monday.".
  Discovery bk_bread_hint "Mr Gudgeon of the Phoenix has not eaten a decent loaf since his mother died, and writes FAIL where he is hungry.".
  Discovery bk_clause "The Smokeless Ordinance has a clause for ancient hearths, number forty-four, by application to the Committee of Exceptions, with evidence of antiquity.".

  Thing bk_oven "Tolliver's oven" at bakehouse {
    State bk_breathing "The oven sits in the back wall with its mouth banked, a low red light under a skin of ash, drawing steadily through a flue that goes up behind the wall to a chimney which nobody has swept in living memory and which has never smoked.".
    State bk_cold "The oven sits in the back wall with its door shut. It draws exactly as the Ordinance requires, and it is warm, as an oven is warm that has been lit and not lived in. The red light under the ash is gone.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(bk_oven, bk_breathing).

  // ── The people ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person bk_gwen "Gwen Tolliver" at bakehouse {
    Role "baker, widow of Hal Tolliver". Ancestry human. Calling monk. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A tall woman in a floury apron is turning loaves out of the peel onto a rack with the speed of habit. She has a Brick Lane voice laid carefully over something older, and it slips on the vowels when she is tired. 'Gwen Tolliver,' she says, not stopping. 'If you're from the Phoenix the flue is in the back. If you're from the Lamprey, I haven't any ships.'".
    Greets again "'Mind the peel,' says Gwen Tolliver, and moves a tray out of your way without looking.".
  }
  Person bk_granny "Old Mother Tolliver" at bakehouse {
    Role "Hal Tolliver's mother, in the chimney-corner". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner compassionate. Pronouns she.
    Greets "In the chimney-corner beside the oven sits a very small old woman in four shawls, with her hands held out to the brick, as to a person. 'Mind,' she says, quite loud. 'It's resting.' Then, to the oven, 'They're nobody. They'll go.'".
    Greets again "'It's resting,' says Old Mother Tolliver, to you, not unkindly.".
  }
  Person bk_gudgeon "Mr Gudgeon" at phoenix_floor {
    Role "Inspector of Flues for the Phoenix". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A small round man with a ten-foot rule under one arm, a ledger under the other and a candle in his hat is writing something in the margin of a form with the gravity of a man signing a treaty. 'Gudgeon,' he says. 'Flues. Chimneys also, but flues chiefly. I have been in four hundred and eleven kitchens this year, and I have not been offered a seat in one.'".
    Greets again "'You,' says Mr Gudgeon, in a voice from which hope has been removed by degrees.".
  }
  Person bk_brundle "Mr Brundle" at phoenix_floor {
    Role "Secretary of the Committee of Exceptions". Ancestry human. Calling bard. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A very neat clerk at a small desk, under a brass plate that says EXCEPTIONS, has before him a form, a blotter and a single dried pea. 'Brundle,' he says. 'Secretary. The Committee sits on the last Thursday of each month, and has not sat since the Ordinance. I do, however, receive applications. It is the pleasure of my life.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Mr Brundle, and squares the pea.".
  }

  // ── What can be seen, said, and read ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe bk_smell at brick_lane when true "Under the smell of polish and coal-smoke, the warm bread smell of a real oven comes up Brick Lane from a shop with a bow window, and has done so since five.".
  Observe bk_shop_notice at tolliver_shop when true "A printed notice is pinned to the end of the counter with a hat-pin: THE SMOKELESS ORDINANCE. THESE PREMISES WILL BE SURVEYED, THE SECOND DAY, AT NOON. IN DEFAULT OF A SATISFACTORY FLUE THE COVER LAPSES AT MIDNIGHT THE DAY FOLLOWING. By order. An apprentice at the till, who is about eleven, tells you without being asked that Mrs Tolliver is in the back and that it is very bad." teaches bk_survey.
  Observe bk_bakehouse_cold at bakehouse when bk_coal_dead(bk_bakery) "The bakehouse is warm and quiet and has an air of being on its best behaviour. The loaves are good. Gwen Tolliver does not hum.".
  Observe bk_bakehouse_wrecked at bakehouse when bk_flue_wrecked(bk_bakery) "A drift of soot lies across the floor from the flue-door, and a brick has been laid out on the peel as if for burial.".
  Observe bk_slate at slip_room when watch(clock) < 312 "CLAIMS OPEN: TOLLIVER'S, Brick Lane. A survey: oven, flue, the Smokeless Ordinance. Noon, the second day. The client says it draws; the Inspector says it cannot. Fee: a loaf a week, and the thanks of the lane. An adjuster is wanted who is good with a flue or with a surveyor." teaches bk_claim.
  Observe bk_slate_lapsed at slip_room when bk_lapsed(bk_bakery) "PREMIUMS: the Phoenix withdraws its mark from a bakery in Brick Lane. FIXTURES: unscrewing, a.m.".
  Observe bk_door_lapsed at tolliver_shop when bk_lapsed(bk_bakery) and not bk_own_mark(party) "Over Tolliver's door there is a pale square where the Phoenix's bird was, and two screw-holes. The apprentice has stuck a paper bird in the window, which fools nobody and gives satisfaction.".
  Observe bk_door_own at tolliver_shop when bk_lapsed(bk_bakery) and bk_own_mark(party) "Over Tolliver's door a bird is nailed where the Phoenix's was, a little too high, a little too gilt, and correct to the last feather.".
  Observe bk_door_stands at brick_lane when bk_lapsed(bk_bakery) and bk_lives() "Tolliver's has no mark over its door, and its bow window is bright and its chimney is drawing, and every other house in the lane has glanced at it once and then not.".
  Observe bk_flash_scene at bakehouse when bk_flash_told(bk_bakery) "The ceiling above the flue is scorched in a long black tongue. A Phoenix certificate has been pinned beside it, clean and new: DAMAGE ASSESSED, PAID.".
  Observe bk_granny_dead near bk_granny when bk_coal_dead(bk_bakery) "Old Mother Tolliver has turned her chair to the wall.".
  Observe bk_gwen_dead near bk_gwen when bk_coal_dead(bk_bakery) "Gwen Tolliver stands with her hand flat on the oven door, as if listening for something that used to answer.".
  Observe bk_gwen_lives near bk_gwen when bk_trusted(party) and bk_lives() "Gwen Tolliver has put a loaf aside on the rack with a bit of paper on it. The paper says YOURS in a hand that is learning to be easy.".

  Action bk_read_lore(actor: group) "Wipe the soot from the line cut over the oven mouth, and read it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, bakehouse) and not knows(actor, d_oven_coal) and capable(actor, lore).
    Time 15 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, d_oven_coal). Assert knows(actor, d_lent_coal). }
    Result "The line is cut in the old square hand, worn to a groove, and with the soot off it you can read it by touch: LENT, NOT GIVEN; KEEP IT AND IT KEEPS THE HOUSE. Under it, smaller, in a different chisel: THE FOUNDING HEARTH. HAL'S GRANDFATHER'S GRANDFATHER BANKED HERE. You look at the oven. The oven is looking, you feel, at you.".
    Otherwise "You get as far as LENT, and a thing that might be a hearth, and the rest of it is a groove with a bird's nest of soot in it. The oven ticks, once, behind its ash.".
  }
  Action bk_read_rites(actor: group) "Lay a hand on the stone under the line over the oven mouth, and say what it says" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, bakehouse) and not knows(actor, d_oven_coal) and capable(actor, rites).
    Time 15 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, rites, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, d_oven_coal). Assert knows(actor, d_lent_coal). }
    Result "It is not a line to be read, you find; it is a line to be said, and the stone gives the words to the mouth: lent, not given; keep it and it keeps the house. The oven answers with a small settling in the ash, like a guest accepting a chair.".
    Otherwise "You say what you think it says. The ash does not settle, and Old Mother Tolliver says, from her corner, quite loud, 'No.'".
  }

  // ── Gwen, and the old woman ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic bk_g_trouble with bk_gwen "Ask Gwen Tolliver what the matter is" when true once {
    Says "'The Ordinance,' says Gwen Tolliver, and slaps a tray into the rack. 'No flue in the marked wards that isn't fitted to the pattern. Mine isn't. Hal had it passed in nineteen and nobody's been since; I put the date right on the certificate myself. Twice.' Another tray. 'The man comes the second day at noon. If he says no, I'm uncovered the day after, and a bakery with a fire in it and no bird on the door, nobody in this lane will stand next to.' She straightens, floury to the elbow. 'It draws, you see. That's what he'll say is wrong. It draws too well.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bk_survey). }
  }
  Topic bk_g_draws with bk_gwen "Ask Gwen Tolliver why the oven draws so well" when knows(actor, bk_survey) once {
    Says "'It was never taken out,' says Gwen Tolliver. 'That's the only answer I've had. Hal's gran said you don't take that oven out, the way you don't take a tooth out of a living mouth, and nobody ever has. I bank it at night. I don't rake it. My mother always banked hers, and I've never been able to do otherwise.'".
  }
  Topic bk_g_mother with bk_gwen "Ask Gwen Tolliver where she learned to bank a fire like that" when bk_helped(party) and not bk_g_asked(party) once {
    Says "Gwen Tolliver is quiet a moment. 'Salt Lane,' she says, in the older voice. 'In the Wards. We had a tin on the hearth, my mother and me, and I was told what was in it and I thought it was a story. She used to say it had been lent. Nobody in the Wards says anyone owns it.' She looks at the oven. 'I came up to the Brickfields at seventeen with a clean apron and my mouth shut. I don't tell the lane. The tin went out the winter she died, and I never found out what it was that went out of the room.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, d_lent_coal). Assert bk_g_asked(party). }
  }
  Topic bk_g_tell with bk_gwen "Tell Gwen Tolliver what the line over her oven says" when knows(actor, d_oven_coal) and bk_lives() and bk_helped(party) and not bk_gwen_told(party) once {
    Says "Gwen Tolliver listens with her hands in the flour. 'Lent,' she says, and then again, as if it were a word in a language she had been told she didn't speak. 'It's lent. It's not my oven. It's a guest.' She takes her hands out of the flour and wipes them, one at a time, slowly. 'Well. I knew that, didn't I,' she says. 'I knew. I didn't know I knew.' She turns the rack so a loaf faces you. 'If anyone wants it lit for them, on a night, they'd better ask me. I'd as soon not be the last person to be asked.'".
    On discuss { Assert bk_gwen_told(party). Assert bk_trusted(party). Assert coalSource(bakehouse). Assert keeper(brick). }
  }
  Topic bk_g_tell_cold with bk_gwen "Tell Gwen Tolliver what the line over her oven says" when knows(actor, d_oven_coal) and bk_lives() and not bk_helped(party) and not bk_gwen_told(party) once {
    Says "Gwen Tolliver looks at you for a long moment over the peel. 'Is that what it says,' she says. 'And what is it you'd like for telling me?' It is not a question she expects to be answered with a clear conscience, and you find you cannot supply one yet.".
  }
  Topic bk_g_tell_dead with bk_gwen "Tell Gwen Tolliver what the line over her oven says" when knows(actor, d_oven_coal) and bk_coal_dead(bk_bakery) and not bk_coal_known_dead(party) once {
    Says "Gwen Tolliver stands with the peel across her knees. She does not shout. 'Lent,' she says. 'It was lent.' She sits down on the flour-bin, which she has never done in front of anyone. 'And I let a man put a plate in it,' she says. 'For a certificate.' She looks at the oven. It is a good oven. It draws exactly as it should. 'Go on,' she says, gently. 'There's bread for you in the front.'".
    On discuss { Assert bk_coal_known_dead(party). }
  }
  Topic bk_g_cold with bk_gwen "Ask Gwen Tolliver how the oven is" when bk_coal_dead(bk_bakery) and watch(clock) >= 240 once {
    Says "'It draws,' says Gwen Tolliver, 'by the pattern. The Inspector sent a card. The bread's good. It's been good. I don't know that I can say what's different.' She presses her hand to the brick. 'It doesn't hold the night. I come down at four, and it's gone out, and I light it, and it takes the way a stove takes. I used to come down and it was waiting.'".
  }
  Topic bk_g_bread with bk_gwen "Ask Gwen Tolliver what the Inspector is like" when knows(actor, bk_survey) once {
    Says "'Small,' says Gwen Tolliver. 'Round. He's been in the lane twice this month and he's looked at the loaves the way a man looks at a house he can't afford. He asked my neighbour what she put in her crust. I think he's hungry.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bk_bread_hint). }
  }
  Topic bk_gr_share with bk_granny "Share a ration with Old Mother Tolliver in the chimney-corner" when quantity(actor, rations) >= 1 and not knows(actor, d_oven_coal) once {
    Says "You break a ration in half, and the old woman takes her half with both hands and eats it as slowly as a child. 'Not from here,' she says, 'the bread you've got. Sit.' You sit. For some time nothing is said. Then Old Mother Tolliver says, to the oven, in the sing-song of a lesson learned before reading: 'Lent, not given. Keep it, and it keeps the house. Who banks it eats; who rakes it, doesn't.' She looks at you. 'That's all it says, over the door. People always want it to say more.'".
    On discuss { Decrease quantity(actor, rations) by 1. Assert knows(actor, d_oven_coal). Assert knows(actor, d_lent_coal). Assert bk_helped(party). }
  }
  Topic bk_gr_dead with bk_granny "Ask Old Mother Tolliver what is wrong with the oven" when bk_coal_dead(bk_bakery) once {
    Says "'It's been told to go,' says Old Mother Tolliver, 'and it went. It's polite. They are.' She does not say who. 'My Hal would have known what to do. He never took anything out of that oven but bread.'".
  }

  // ── Mr Gudgeon, and the Committee ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic bk_gud_loaf with bk_gudgeon "Ask Mr Gudgeon what he has had for his breakfast" when true once {
    Says "'A roll,' says Mr Gudgeon. 'From the Hen. It is grey, and it is damp, and it has a hole in it that goes all the way through. My mother baked on Thursdays. It was always a Thursday, in my recollection; I believe that she baked on other days but I was not there to see.' He writes something in his ledger. 'I do not wish to be understood to complain.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bk_bread_hint). }
  }
  Topic bk_gud_clause with bk_gudgeon "Ask Mr Gudgeon whether the Ordinance excepts old hearths" when knows(actor, bk_survey) once {
    Says "'Clause forty-four,' says Mr Gudgeon, immediately and with great reluctance. 'Hearths of ancient standing. By application to the Committee of Exceptions, with evidence of antiquity. I have seen four hundred and eleven kitchens this year and not one application.' He looks unhappy. 'A person would have to know what the evidence was.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bk_clause). }
  }
  Topic bk_gud_bread with bk_gudgeon "Hand Mr Gudgeon a hot loaf from the morning's baking" when bk_bread(party) and not bk_pass(bk_bakery) and not bk_lapsed(bk_bakery) once {
    Says "Mr Gudgeon holds the loaf for some time. He does not eat it. He looks at it as a man looks at a letter he has been expecting from a place he does not go. Then he breaks the end off and eats it, standing, with his ledger under his arm and his ten-foot rule forgotten against his knee; and when it is gone he says, 'I have been over the flue in my mind. I find that the matter of the draw is a matter of the oven's age, and not of the flue's design, and the Ordinance is silent upon ages.' He writes. 'Pass,' he says, in the voice of a man who has been given leave. 'With a loaf a week, in kind, for the Office's convenience.'".
    On discuss { Assert bk_pass(bk_bakery). Assert bk_by_bread(party). Assert bk_helped(party). }
  }
  Action bk_gud_bribe(actor: group, site: place) "Slip Mr Gudgeon twelve coin in the margin of his ledger" {
    Speaker bk_gudgeon.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bk_gudgeon, site) and not bk_pass(bk_bakery) and not bk_lapsed(bk_bakery) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 12.
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 12. Assert bk_pass(bk_bakery). Assert bk_bribed_gudgeon(party). }
    Result "Mr Gudgeon looks at the coin and then at you with an expression of hurt professional surprise. He writes the sum, and the date, and your names, neatly, in the margin of a different page. 'For the record,' he says. 'In case I should ever be asked.' It passes. It passes in the way a thing does that will be remembered.".
  }
  Action bk_committee(actor: group, site: place) "Lodge Form 44-B for an ancient hearth, with the line and the morning's loaf as evidence" {
    Speaker bk_brundle.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bk_brundle, site) and holding(actor, adjuster_licence) and knows(actor, d_oven_coal) and bk_bread(party) and not bk_pass(bk_bakery) and not bk_lapsed(bk_bakery).
    Time 20 minutes.
    On success { Assert bk_pass(bk_bakery). Assert bk_exempt(party). Assert bk_registered(party). Assert bk_helped(party). Increase regard(phoenix) by 1. }
    Result "Mr Brundle takes Form 44-B, reads each line, and, when he reaches EVIDENCE OF ANTIQUITY, takes the loaf, turns it over, smells it, and enters it as an exhibit. 'Sufficient,' he says, with a catch in his voice. 'Quite sufficient. The oven will be entered in the Register of Excepted Hearths, which is a book I have been keeping for eleven years and have not been allowed to open.' He rubber-stamps something. The stamp is the colour of a good wine. 'It is a pleasure,' says Mr Brundle, 'to be of use.'".
  }
  Topic bk_brundle_register with bk_brundle "Ask Mr Brundle who reads the Register of Excepted Hearths" when bk_registered(party) once {
    Says "'The Chief Underwriter,' says Mr Brundle, 'has a copy sent up annually. He has not yet acknowledged it.' He squares the pea. 'He is, I think, a reader of lists.'".
  }
  Topic bk_ianthe_ask with ianthe "Ask Ianthe Corbett to look at the flue on a bakehouse roof, as a favour" when knows(actor, bk_survey) and not bk_ianthe(party) and watch(clock) < 312 once {
    Says "'A flue?' says Ianthe Corbett, dropping her boots off the plan. 'On a roof? Is it high?' She hears you out, eating the rest of her apple. 'The Guild's word beats an Inspector's, you know. It always has; nobody thinks of it. If it draws and the Ordinance can't say why, a Guild surveyor can put her name to why, if she's seen it, and she can't have seen it unless she's been up. I'll be there at eleven on the day. Don't tell the Inspector. He's very good at looking down.'".
    On discuss { Assert bk_ianthe(party). }
  }

  // ── Fixing the flue: the cost is hidden until the line is read ──────────────────────────────────────────
  Action bk_fix_trap(actor: group) "Take out the old damper and bring the flue to the Ordinance's pattern" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, bakehouse) and capable(actor, trapwork) and not knows(actor, d_oven_coal) and not bk_pass(bk_bakery) and not bk_flue_wrecked(bk_bakery) and watch(clock) < 384.
    Time 120 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, trapwork, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bk_pass(bk_bakery). Assert bk_coal_dead(bk_bakery). Assert bk_flue_fixed(party). Assert state(bk_oven, bk_cold). }
    On failure { Assert bk_flue_wrecked(bk_bakery). }
    Result "You draw the old damper, a plate of black iron older than the street, and fit a new one to the pattern in the Ordinance, with a throat and a baffle and a little door that opens one way. The oven goes quiet. It is a small thing, the quiet; you think about it later. Gwen Tolliver, standing at the bakehouse door, looks pleased, and then, somehow, less so.".
    Otherwise "A brick comes out of the throat that was holding three others. There is a moment of attentive stillness, and then soot. You spend the rest of the morning shovelling it out of the bakehouse, and the oven draws as it did before, which is to say perfectly and against the Ordinance.".
  }
  Action bk_fix_trap_k(actor: group) "Take out the old damper and bring the flue to the Ordinance's pattern, though the line says LENT" {
    Grave "The line over the oven says it is lent and not given. A new damper puts the Ordinance's draw in, and the old guest out, and what has gone from the oven will not be lit again.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, bakehouse) and capable(actor, trapwork) and knows(actor, d_oven_coal) and not bk_pass(bk_bakery) and not bk_flue_wrecked(bk_bakery) and watch(clock) < 384.
    Time 120 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, trapwork, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bk_pass(bk_bakery). Assert bk_coal_dead(bk_bakery). Assert bk_flue_fixed(party). Assert state(bk_oven, bk_cold). }
    On failure { Assert bk_flue_wrecked(bk_bakery). }
    Result "You draw the old damper and fit a new one to the pattern. The oven goes quiet, and Old Mother Tolliver, without a word, gets up out of her corner and goes into the shop.".
    Otherwise "A brick comes out of the throat that was holding three others, and there is soot. Perhaps, you think, it is as well.".
  }
  Action bk_fix_brawn(actor: group) "Break out the old throat with a sledge and lay the flue again to the Ordinance's pattern" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, bakehouse) and capable(actor, brawn) and not knows(actor, d_oven_coal) and not bk_pass(bk_bakery) and not bk_flue_wrecked(bk_bakery) and watch(clock) < 384.
    Time 120 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bk_pass(bk_bakery). Assert bk_coal_dead(bk_bakery). Assert bk_flue_fixed(party). Assert state(bk_oven, bk_cold). }
    On failure { Assert bk_flue_wrecked(bk_bakery). }
    Result "The old throat comes out in four swings, a hundred years of black brick in a drift on the floor, and you lay the new one to the pattern in the afternoon. The oven goes quiet. It is a small thing, the quiet; you think about it later.".
    Otherwise "The sledge rings off a stone that was set by someone who meant it. You take half a brick off your own boot, and the oven, behind its ash, draws as it did before.".
  }
  Action bk_fix_brawn_k(actor: group) "Break out the old throat with a sledge and lay the flue to the pattern, though the line says LENT" {
    Grave "The line over the oven says it is lent and not given. A new throat puts the Ordinance's draw in, and the old guest out, and what has gone from the oven will not be lit again.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, bakehouse) and capable(actor, brawn) and knows(actor, d_oven_coal) and not bk_pass(bk_bakery) and not bk_flue_wrecked(bk_bakery) and watch(clock) < 384.
    Time 120 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bk_pass(bk_bakery). Assert bk_coal_dead(bk_bakery). Assert bk_flue_fixed(party). Assert state(bk_oven, bk_cold). }
    On failure { Assert bk_flue_wrecked(bk_bakery). }
    Result "The old throat comes out in four swings, and you lay the new one to the pattern. The oven goes quiet, and the old woman in the corner puts her face in her shawls.".
    Otherwise "The sledge rings off a stone that was set by someone who meant it.".
  }

  // ── Cooking for the Inspector ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Action bk_bake(actor: group) "Spend the morning at the ovens with Gwen Tolliver, baking, and pay for the flour (3 coin)" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, bakehouse) and watch(clock) < 312 and not bk_bread(party) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3.
    Time 180 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Assert bk_bread(party). Assert bk_helped(party). }
    Result "You are given an apron and a bowl, and a place at the board where the floor is worn to the shape of a boot. You knead until you stop thinking about the kneading. The first batch comes out of the oven with the crust crackling and Gwen Tolliver, after a moment, tears a heel off one and gives it to you without a word. 'That,' she says, 'is what he wants. He doesn't know it. I'll tell you what I tell the lane: if you can't taste it, you can't mark it.' There are twelve loaves under a cloth, still warm, and you may carry one wherever it is needed.".
  }

  // ── The mark of one's own ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Action bk_nail_plate(actor: group) "Nail one of Ma Gedge's plates over Tolliver's door, where the Phoenix's was" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, tolliver_shop) and bk_lapsed(bk_bakery) and not bk_own_mark(party) and holding(actor, fg_plate_kind).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Spend fg_plate_kind from actor. Assert bk_own_mark(party). Assert bk_helped(party). }
    Result "You nail it up with the apprentice holding the ladder. It is a Phoenix bird, correct to the last feather, and the whole of Brick Lane is looking out of its windows and not looking at it. Gwen Tolliver, in the doorway, says 'It's lovely' in a voice that has not decided what it means.".
  }

  // ── The clock of the survey ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Event bk_gud_arrives when watch(clock) >= 306 and not bk_judged(bk_bakery) "At eleven on the second day Mr Gudgeon of the Phoenix goes into Tolliver's with a ten-foot rule, a ledger and a lit candle in his hat, and the bow window is, for a moment, entirely full of apprentice." then {
    Assert at(bk_gudgeon, bakehouse).
  }
  Rule bk_ianthe_stamps when watch(clock) >= 306 and watch(clock) < 384 and bk_ianthe(party) and not bk_ianthe_there(bk_bakery) and not bk_lapsed(bk_bakery) says "A shape comes over the roof opposite the bakehouse and down a rope, and a woman in a roped coat swings in at the flue-door with her boots first, eating an apple. 'Corbett,' says Ianthe, upside down, to the Inspector. 'Guild. Don't stop on my account.' She goes up the flue with a candle and comes back with soot to the elbow and the look of a person who has found something she hopes to be allowed to say. 'It draws by a cause outside the flue,' she announces. 'The Guild so certifies. The Ordinance is silent.' Mr Gudgeon, white as the loaf, writes it down." {
    Assert at(ianthe, bakehouse). Assert bk_ianthe_there(bk_bakery). Assert bk_pass(bk_bakery). Assert bk_by_ianthe(party). Assert bk_helped(party).
  }
  Rule bk_ianthe_home when bk_ianthe_there(bk_bakery) and watch(clock) >= 324 and at(ianthe, bakehouse) { Assert at(ianthe, corbett_study). }
  Rule bk_noon_pass when watch(clock) >= 312 and not bk_judged(bk_bakery) and bk_pass(bk_bakery) and at(bk_gudgeon, bakehouse) says "Mr Gudgeon closes his ledger, and stamps the cover with the Phoenix's bird, and says to the oven, in the sombre voice of a man making a note for posterity, 'Sufficient.' He goes out into Brick Lane and looks for a moment at the sky." {
    Assert bk_judged(bk_bakery). Assert at(bk_gudgeon, phoenix_floor).
  }
  Rule bk_noon_fail when watch(clock) >= 312 and not bk_judged(bk_bakery) and not bk_pass(bk_bakery) and at(bk_gudgeon, bakehouse) says "Mr Gudgeon holds a candle up the flue and watches the flame lean, steadily, toward the oven as though drawn by the sleeve. 'It draws,' he says, with satisfaction, 'in the face of the Ordinance.' He writes a word in the margin of the form, in capitals, and Gwen Tolliver closes her eyes. 'The cover lapses,' says Mr Gudgeon, 'the day after tomorrow, at midnight. Good day.' At the door, he looks over his shoulder at the loaves, and appears to find something there to forgive. He does not, however, forgive it." {
    Assert bk_judged(bk_bakery). Assert bk_failed(bk_bakery). Assert at(bk_gudgeon, phoenix_floor).
  }
  Rule bk_reprieve when bk_failed(bk_bakery) and bk_pass(bk_bakery) and not bk_reprieved(bk_bakery) and not bk_lapsed(bk_bakery) says "A boy from Phoenix House runs into Tolliver's with a slip for Gwen Tolliver, who reads it twice and puts it behind the till without a word, and then, to the apprentice's alarm, takes it out and kisses it." {
    Assert bk_reprieved(bk_bakery).
  }
  Rule bk_lapse when watch(clock) >= 384 and not bk_pass(bk_bakery) and not bk_lapsed(bk_bakery) says "Two men in blue come to Tolliver's at first light on the third day with a ladder and a screwdriver, and take the bird down from over the door, with great politeness, and leave." {
    Assert bk_lapsed(bk_bakery).
  }
  Rule bk_flash when watch(clock) >= 564 and bk_coal_dead(bk_bakery) and not bk_flash_told(bk_bakery) says "At six on the fourth morning a chimney goes up in Brick Lane: Tolliver's. The Phoenix comes with its engine, the crew sing out the street, and in twenty minutes the bakehouse is a black wet room and the loaves are in the road. The Office pays, with a cheque for the ceiling, and the Inspector of Flues, who is made to attend, writes in his ledger the single word UNAVOIDABLE." {
    Assert bk_flash_told(bk_bakery).
  }
  Objective bk_obj when (knows(party, bk_claim) or knows(party, bk_survey)) and watch(clock) < 312 and not bk_pass(bk_bakery) "Tolliver's oven is surveyed under the Smokeless Ordinance at noon on the second day; unless it passes, the bakery's cover lapses at midnight after. Its flue draws, and Gwen Tolliver does not know why.".
  Objective bk_obj_late when bk_failed(bk_bakery) and not bk_pass(bk_bakery) and not bk_lapsed(bk_bakery) "The oven failed its survey. The cover lapses at midnight on the third day unless it can still be satisfied.".
}

data/adventures/quittance/q_barge.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "The Scuttled Barge: the Prudent Margaret sunk at the Mere Wharf, two salvor crews, a calm owner, an adjuster who has been paid, a girl in a cellar; and the hatch of the diving-bell, the Reach's way down to the Sunk City.".

  // ══ THE SCUTTLED BARGE (prefix bg_) ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // Truth: the Margaret was holed from inside by her owner to hide a passenger, Kitty Spratling of the Bare Wards,
  // a girl of twelve sent out of the Wards in the hold the week before an Appointed block burned. Mr Orpwood of the
  // Lamprey, who had seen the Phoenix's stamped notice cross his counter and had told the girl's mother, was then
  // given a consideration to call the loss total and ask nothing. Josiah Skell dived the wreck by night and has
  // eighty-nine jars under a tarpaulin. The call is Orpwood's, at noon on day 2; the cargo is auctioned at noon on
  // day 4; Kitty is shipped to an aunt on the night of day 3. The company can change what is called until the bell.
  //   bg_ruling(lamprey):  0 not yet called . 1 Total Loss . 2 Salvage . 3 As agreed . 4 Fraud handed in . 5 General Average

  Measure bg_ruling(group).

  // ── Places of my own ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place skell_loft "Skell's bunkhouse" is room within reach at 3, 2.
  Place bg_cellar "the Sluice-tap's cellar" is room within sluice_b at 0, 2 underground.
  Passage bg_loft_door "the bunkhouse door" is door between skell_yard and skell_loft.
  Passage bg_trap "the trap under the sluice-wheel" is crawl between sluice_room and bg_cellar hidden until bg_cellar_known.

  // ── The tide ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Reach keeps its low water at five and at five, morning and evening: a bad tide-table and a good clock.
  Query bg_lowwater() means (hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) < 8) or (hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 20).
  Observe bg_tide_out at mere_wharf when bg_lowwater() "The tide is out. The Margaret's after-deck stands clear of the brown water, and her hatch-coamings show a hand's breadth above it.".
  Observe bg_tide_in at mere_wharf when not bg_lowwater() "The tide is in. Nothing of the Margaret shows but the top of her mast and a ring of oily bubbles where she breathes.".
  Observe bg_gauge at lighter_stairs when true "The tide-board painted by the Stair reads, in a lighterman's hand under the official figures, LOW WATER 5 AND 5. THE REST IS RIVER.".
  Observe bg_bell_dry at cradle when not bg_lowwater() "The diving-bell hangs dry in its gantry. A lighterman sitting under it says that nobody goes down to the Margaret except at low water, when her hatch is a fathom up and the bell can find it.".
  Observe bg_bell_ruined at cradle when state(bg_hatch, wrecked) "The diving-bell lies on its side on the quay in the wreck of its gantry, its chain parted a fathom above the ring. A lighterman is using it as a seat. He says the Lamprey has been told, and that the Lamprey has said nothing, which is worse.".
  Observe bg_bell_wet at cradle when bg_lowwater() and not state(bg_hatch, wrecked) "The tide is out, and the diving-bell hangs over the water with its crank slack. Below it, a long way down, is the Margaret's hatch, a fathom under.".

  // ── What the company can know ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery bg_claim "The Slate asks an adjuster to settle the Prudent Margaret: Total Loss or Salvage, the Lamprey & River to pay.".
  Discovery bg_manifest_read "The Prudent Margaret's manifest enters four hundred sealed jars of cold-lamps.".
  Discovery bg_counted "There are three hundred and eleven jars in the Margaret's hold, and a clear berth in the straw.".
  Discovery bg_tally_read "The Stairs tally-board chalked the Margaret past the Stair with three hundred and eleven jars.".
  Discovery bg_count_short "The Margaret's manifest enters eighty-nine more jars than she ever carried, or than lie in her hold.".
  Discovery bg_holed "The Margaret was holed from inside, with augers, and not by her anchor.".
  Discovery bg_berth "Somebody lay in the Margaret's hold in a berth made up in the straw: a child, by the length of it.".
  Discovery bg_skell_dived "Josiah Skell has eighty-nine of the Margaret's jars under a tarpaulin, wet: his crew dived her before anyone had claimed her.".
  Discovery bg_bought "Mr Orpwood of the Lamprey was given a sum to call the Margaret a Total Loss and ask nothing.".
  Discovery bg_owner_afraid "Mistress Veasey is not calm, but afraid for someone small.".
  Discovery bg_tariff_known "The Salvors' tariff board has a third clause nobody posts: AS AGREED is settled between the crews, the owner and the adjuster, and the Lamprey's captain must sign it.".
  Discovery bg_average_known "A hull given up to save a life is no one's loss but everyone's: the Lamprey calls it General Average and the owner, the insurer and the salvors bear it together, without naming whose life.".
  Discovery bg_cellar_known "Under the sluice-wheel in the Sluice-tap there is a trap, and a cellar below it with a child in it." {
    Found by searching sluice_room "Under the wheel, in the wet plank, a trap-ring with the rust worn off it by use. The trap is no bigger than a tea-tray. Below it somebody has set a candle on a barrel, and somebody has been sitting very still beside the candle.".
  }

  // ── The people ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person bg_orpwood "Mr Orpwood" at lamprey_floor {
    Role "adjuster of the Lamprey & River". Ancestry human. Calling bard. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A man in oilskin cuffs is writing at a high desk, and finishes his sentence before he looks up. 'Orpwood,' he says. 'Adjuster. If it is the Margaret, the answer is Total Loss, and I sign on the second day at noon. If it is anything else, it will keep.'".
    Greets again "'The Margaret,' says Mr Orpwood, without looking up. 'Still a Total Loss.'".
  }
  Person bg_veasey "Mistress Honor Veasey" at mere_wharf {
    Role "who owns the Prudent Margaret". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A woman in good grey wool sits on a folding stool at the wharf's edge with her back to the wind, knitting, and looking at her sunk barge as one looks at a kettle one has no reason to expect to boil. 'Veasey,' she says. 'Her owner. Yes, it is a pity. I am insured.'".
    Greets again "'Still there,' says Mistress Veasey, of the barge, and counts a row.".
  }
  Person bg_skell "Josiah Skell" at skell_yard {
    Role "who runs Skell & Sons, salvors". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner jovial. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A large man with a small hat is sitting on the hatch among his crew, dealing, and does not stop dealing. 'Skell,' he says. 'Skell and Sons. The sons are the ones who are winning.' He looks you over. 'If you are the Salvors' Yard's, you are lost. If you are the Lamprey's, you are late.'".
    Greets again "'Dealt you in,' says Josiah Skell, 'if you want.'".
  }
  Person bg_sons "Skell's sons" at skell_yard {
    Role "three of Skell's crew, not all of them his sons". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Numbers 3. Temperament territorial. Pronouns they.
    Warns "A bucket goes over with a sound like a bell, and the bunkhouse door opens. The cards stop. Three men are standing on the quay with boat-hooks and the slow, unhurried look of people who have been woken for the right reason. 'That is a private tarpaulin,' says the largest. 'Say a good reason before the watch is out, or say good night.'".
    Comes "'Over the side with them,' says the largest, and Skell's sons come at you across the yard with their boat-hooks low.".
    Pleads "The largest of Skell's sons lets his hook go on the stones. 'Enough,' he says. 'Enough. Take your jars. Take your look. Skell can pay for his own tarpaulin.'".
    Refuge skell_loft.
  }
  Person bg_grindle "Nan Grindle" at salvor_yard {
    Role "who keeps the Salvors' Yard". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 3. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A woman built like a bollard is mending a block-and-tackle with a marlinspike, and has the air of someone who has been right in public for thirty years. 'Grindle,' she says. 'Master of the Yard. You are here about the Margaret. Everybody is. Stand there; that is where they stand.'".
    Greets again "'The Margaret,' says Nan Grindle. 'Still ours.'".
  }
  Person bg_jessop "Cob Jessop" at sluice_room {
    Role "who keeps the Sluice-tap, and was a lighterman". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A man with forearms like mooring-posts is drawing a pot of brown beer with great care, as if it were a pot of something else. 'Jessop,' he says. 'The Sluice is mine. The beer is the river's. If you are the Lamprey's, you can stand; if you are anyone else, you can sit and be quiet.'".
    Greets again "'Brown or brown,' says Cob Jessop.".
  }
  Person bg_girl "Kitty Spratling" at bg_cellar {
    Role "a girl of twelve, in a lighterman's coat". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner proud. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A girl is sitting on an upturned bucket by a candle, in a coat that has been cut down from a bigger one, with her feet off the floor so that she does not have to feel the damp. She looks at the trap, and at you, and at the trap again. 'Cob said nobody comes down,' she says. 'So you are either nobody, or Cob said it wrong.'".
    Greets again "'Oh,' says Kitty Spratling. 'You.'".
  }

  // ── The Slate: the claim, and other doors in ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe bg_slate at slip_room when day(clock) <= 3 and not bg_settled() "CLAIMS OPEN: THE PRUDENT MARGARET, barge, sunk at the Mere Wharf with a cargo of cold-lamps. Total Loss or Salvage; two crews, one owner. The Lamprey & River will pay a fee of twelve coin to whoever settles it before the cargo is sold. TAKEN: no one."
    teaches bg_claim.
  Objective obj_bg when knows(party, bg_claim) and not bg_settled() and watch(clock) < 600 "The Prudent Margaret lies at the Mere Wharf, and Mr Orpwood of the Lamprey will call her a Total Loss at noon on the second day; the cargo is sold at noon on the fourth.".

  // ── The Water-Stair and the Wharf: what the lightermen think, before and after ─────────────────────────────
  Observe bg_wharf_crowd at mere_wharf when day(clock) <= 1 and bg_ruling(lamprey) == 0 "A crowd stands along the edge, divided by a rope into the Salvors' Yard on the left and Skell & Sons on the right, each telling the other which of them is going to be paid.".
  Observe bg_wharf_called at mere_wharf when bg_ruling(lamprey) == 1 and watch(clock) < 600 "A paper is nailed to the bollard nearest the wreck: TOTAL LOSS. Beneath it, in a smaller hand, THE CARGO IS TO BE SOLD ON THE FOURTH DAY, NOON.".

  // ── The Salvors' Yard ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Thing bg_board "the tariff board" at salvor_yard {
    State chalked "The tariff board hangs by the gate: ONE THIRD, ONE HALF, AS AGREED. Somebody has underlined the third clause twice, and somebody else has scratched the underlining out.".
  }
  Observe bg_board_read at salvor_yard when tried(bg_board, looking) and capable(party, lore) and not knows(party, bg_tariff_known) "You read the board as a clerk would, not as a salvor. The third clause is not a price. It is a procedure: where the crews, the owner and the adjuster agree, the Lamprey's captain signs, and the one third and the one half are whatever they have agreed. The sums it has produced are posted nowhere."
    teaches bg_tariff_known.
  Observe bg_board_plain at salvor_yard when tried(bg_board, looking) and not capable(party, lore) "The board is clear about the first two clauses and says of the third only AS AGREED, in the voice of a clause that does not want to be asked.".
  Topic bg_grindle_claim with bg_grindle "Ask Nan Grindle for the Yard's claim to the Margaret" when true once {
    Says "'We had a line on her within the hour,' says Nan Grindle. 'First on the wreck, first with a grapple, first at the Lamprey's door. A salvage, one half, to the Yard. If she is called a Total Loss, the Yard gets a third of nothing, because there is nothing to raise.' She takes a pull on her marlinspike, as other people take on a pipe. 'It is not a Total Loss. A Total Loss does not float her bow up at the turn of the tide.'".
  }
  Topic bg_grindle_skell with bg_grindle "Ask Grindle why Skell's crew sleeps by day" when true once {
    Says "'Because they work by night,' says Nan Grindle. 'Nobody sleeps like a man who has been under a barge. They think I do not hear the pump. I hear the pump.' She hammers the pin home. 'If you want to know what he has, ask it at night. If you want to ask it politely, bring a good reason.'".
  }
  Topic bg_grindle_after with bg_grindle "Ask Nan Grindle how the Yard is faring" when bg_settled() once {
    Says "'The Yard,' says Nan Grindle, and considers. 'Is paid as the Lamprey called it. I have asked the lightermen what they say. They say what lightermen say.' It is not clear that she is displeased.".
  }

  // ── Skell's yard, and the fight ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Initially Assert tolerates(bg_sons, party).
  Rule bg_sons_bunk when dark() and at(bg_sons, skell_yard) and not routed(bg_sons) and tolerates(bg_sons, party) {
    Retract at(bg_sons, skell_yard). Assert at(bg_sons, skell_loft). }
  Rule bg_sons_up when not dark() and at(bg_sons, skell_loft) and not routed(bg_sons) and tolerates(bg_sons, party) {
    Retract at(bg_sons, skell_loft). Assert at(bg_sons, skell_yard). }
  Observe bg_tarp at skell_yard when not knows(party, bg_skell_dived) "Something under the tarpaulin in the corner of the yard is dripping steadily into a bucket that has been emptied recently, and a fish has not been the cause.".
  Observe bg_yard_night at skell_yard when dark() "The yard is shut for the night. The crew has gone into the bunkhouse, and the cards lie where they were left, under a lantern turned low. The tarpaulin drips.".
  Observe bg_bunk_snore at skell_yard as sound when dark() "Behind the bunkhouse door, a good many men are asleep in a good many keys.".
  Kind bg_jar "a wet cold-lamp jar" like lantern described "A sealed glass jar the size of a loaf, ringed with weed and still wet to the bottom. A small light burns in it, a long way off.".
  Item bg_jar_one "a wet cold-lamp jar" is bg_jar at nowhere.
  Relation bg_searched(group). Relation bg_shown(group).
  Action bg_search_yard(actor: group) "Slip into Skell's yard after dark and lift the corner of the tarpaulin" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, skell_yard) and dark() and not bg_searched(actor) and at(bg_sons, skell_loft) and tolerates(bg_sons, actor).
    Time 4 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bg_searched(actor). Assert knows(actor, bg_skell_dived). Give bg_jar_one to actor. }
    On failure { Retract tolerates(bg_sons, actor). Retract at(bg_sons, skell_loft). Assert at(bg_sons, skell_yard). }
    Result "You lift the corner of the tarpaulin a hand's breadth and let it fall. Under it is a stack of cold-lamp jars, wet from the river, each with the black mark of the Margaret's lading burned in the straw it came out of: eighty-nine, by the stack. You take one, because a thing in the hand is what a Lamprey adjuster believes.".
    Otherwise "Your foot finds the bucket you had not seen.".
  }
  Action bg_pay_sons(actor: group) "Pay Skell's sons six coin to have been asleep" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, skell_yard) and warned(bg_sons, actor) and able(bg_sons) and not tolerates(bg_sons, actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 6.
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Assert tolerates(bg_sons, actor). Retract warned(bg_sons, actor). Retract halts(bg_sons, actor). }
    Result "The largest of Skell's sons weighs the coin in his palm, and then the company, and then the hour. 'We were asleep,' he says. 'Weren't we?' Three others agree that they were. The cards are picked up in a clatter.".
  }
  Action bg_show_licence(actor: group) "Show Skell's sons the Lamprey's licence, and say you are on the claim" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, skell_yard) and warned(bg_sons, actor) and able(bg_sons) and not tolerates(bg_sons, actor) and holding(actor, adjuster_licence) and not bg_shown(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert tolerates(bg_sons, actor). Retract warned(bg_sons, actor). Retract halts(bg_sons, actor). }
    On failure { Assert bg_shown(actor). }
    Result "You hold out the buff card and say, in the voice of a clerk, that premises named in a claim are open to the adjuster. The largest of Skell's sons reads the card twice, and then reads the claim, which is on the Slate and not in his hand. 'Named,' he says. 'Well. Named is named.' He steps back. The tarpaulin is not mentioned.".
    Otherwise "The largest of Skell's sons reads the card, and then reads it again to someone behind him. 'It says adjuster,' he says. 'It does not say at night.'".
  }
  Action bg_name_dree(actor: group) "Tell Skell's sons that Captain Dree knows where you are" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, skell_yard) and warned(bg_sons, actor) and able(bg_sons) and not tolerates(bg_sons, actor) and arc(dree) >= 1.
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert tolerates(bg_sons, actor). Retract warned(bg_sons, actor). Retract halts(bg_sons, actor). }
    Result "The name goes down the line of boat-hooks like a draught. 'Dree,' says the largest, and the hooks come down. 'He's a man who writes things in books.' Nobody wants to be in this one.".
  }
  // A fight won is a fight that kills: three of Skell's crew fall in the yard, and the Reach hears of it.
  Relation bg_killed_sons(group).
  Rule bg_sons_fallen when dead(bg_sons) and not bg_killed_sons(party)
    says "It is all along the Reach by the next tide that three of Skell's crew went down in his yard to a company with a licence to do no such thing. The Lamprey brigade is made to write it up." {
    Assert bg_killed_sons(party). Assert bg_skell_out(bg_skell). Decrease regard(lamprey) by 1 or to nothing. Assert bg_slighted_dree(party). }
  Observe bg_yard_fallen at skell_yard when dead(bg_sons) "The cards are where they were left. Josiah Skell sits on the hatch among his remaining crew with his small hat in his hands, and does not look up when you come.".
  Topic bg_skell_claim with bg_skell "Ask Josiah Skell about his claim to the Margaret" when true once {
    Says "'Total Loss,' says Josiah Skell. 'A third to the first crew with the nerve, and that's us: nine crates up before the Yard had its kettle on. Ask on the quay.' He deals a card face up. 'Evens they say we were first. Two to one they weren't looking.'".
  }
  Topic bg_skell_tarp with bg_skell "Ask Skell what is under the tarpaulin" when true once {
    Says "'Rain,' says Josiah Skell. 'Lay you a coin it's rain.' He does not wait to be taken up on it.".
  }
  Topic bg_skell_jars with bg_skell "Tell Skell you have seen what is under his tarpaulin, and counted it" when knows(actor, bg_skell_dived) and not bg_skell_out(bg_skell) once {
    Says "Josiah Skell puts down the deck. For some time he does not say anything, and the sons, behind him, find things to look at. 'Eighty-nine,' he says at last, in a different voice. 'It is eighty-nine. I will tell you what I did not do. I did not sink her.' He takes his small hat off. 'The Yard can have the claim. I will have my jars, and you will have the sense to leave Skell and Sons out of the Lamprey's book. My boys will not put a hook near you again.'".
    On discuss { Assert bg_skell_out(bg_skell). Assert tolerates(bg_sons, actor). }
  }
  Relation bg_skell_out(group).
  Topic bg_skell_after with bg_skell "Ask Skell how Skell and Sons are faring" when bg_settled() once {
    Says "'Faring,' says Josiah Skell. 'Five to four on, if you want the odds. We've been seen to fare.' He deals. 'I don't complain. Man who complains is a man who has jars.'".
  }

  // ── The Mere Wharf: Mistress Veasey ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation bg_veasey_cold(group). Relation bg_veasey_yielded(group). Relation bg_veasey_consents(group). Relation bg_veasey_read(group).
  Topic bg_veasey_ask with bg_veasey "Ask Mistress Veasey about the Margaret" when true once {
    Says "'She was a good barge,' says Mistress Veasey. 'Eleven years. A sound hull, a sound master, a sound cargo. Nothing in her was not sound.' The needles continue. 'She went down at her moorings on a still night, which is what barges do. I am insured. I am told it is in hand.'".
  }
  Topic bg_veasey_papers with bg_veasey "Lay the manifest and the count before Mistress Veasey" when knows(actor, bg_count_short) once {
    Says "Mistress Veasey looks at the figures as one looks at weather. 'I do not doubt your arithmetic,' she says. 'I have kept barges for twenty years. I know what is in my hold.' She counts a row. 'I do not understand why you have brought me numbers. Numbers are Mr Orpwood's.'".
  }
  Action bg_veasey_hands(actor: group) "Watch Mistress Veasey's needles while you ask who lay in the hold" {
    Speaker bg_veasey.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, mere_wharf) and at(bg_veasey, mere_wharf) and not bg_veasey_read(actor) and not bg_veasey_cold(actor).
    Time 3 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bg_veasey_read(actor). Assert knows(actor, bg_owner_afraid). }
    On failure { Assert bg_veasey_cold(actor). }
    Result "The needles do not stop; the wool does. For a count of four the working end hangs in the air, and then goes on, and the row is shorter than the last by one stitch. Mistress Veasey is not calm. She is holding herself very exactly still, as one does with a full cup. It is not her barge she is afraid for. It is somebody small.".
    Otherwise "Mistress Veasey looks at you over the wool. 'Who lay where?' she says, pleasantly, and the stool is a little further from you than it was. 'I think we have discussed the Margaret.'".
  }
  Action bg_veasey_press(actor: group) "Tell Mistress Veasey you know whose child it was, and that you will keep her out of every book" {
    Speaker bg_veasey.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, mere_wharf) and at(bg_veasey, mere_wharf) and bg_veasey_read(actor) and not bg_veasey_yielded(actor) and not bg_veasey_cold(actor).
    Time 6 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert bg_veasey_yielded(actor). Assert knows(actor, d_barge_girl). Assert knows(actor, d_list_exists). Assert knows(actor, bg_bought). Assert bg_veasey_word(actor). }
    On failure { Assert bg_veasey_cold(actor). }
    Result "Mistress Veasey puts the knitting in her lap. 'Annis Spratling washed my linen for nine years,' she says, 'and she came to me one night in a state I had not seen her in, and said that a man from the Lamprey had told her a thing, and that it was true, because he had a cuff with the Lamprey's fish on it and no reason to tell it. A notice had come, a week before the fact, on the Phoenix's paper with the bird on it. Their block was to burn on the Saturday. So I took the child out in my hold, and I put my own anchor through my own bottom, because a barge that is lost is a barge that has never carried anyone.' She does not look up. 'I paid Mr Orpwood to be of the opinion that a Total Loss is total. It is an expensive opinion.'".
    Otherwise "Mistress Veasey does not look up. 'I have no idea,' she says, 'what you mean.' She is still knitting. She will say it to the Lamprey exactly as she has said it to you.".
  }
  Relation bg_veasey_word(group).
  Topic bg_veasey_safe with bg_veasey "Tell Mistress Veasey that Kitty is alive, dry and has asked after her" when bg_girl_met(party) and not bg_veasey_yielded(party) once {
    Says "The needles stop and do not start. Mistress Veasey puts the knitting down on the stool, and the stool on the wharf, and herself on the stool. 'Dry,' she says. 'Is she dry.' It takes her some time. 'There was a notice,' she says at last. 'The bird on good paper, and APPOINTED across the top in a clerk's hand. Annis could not read it. She did not need to.' She looks at you for the first time. 'Whatever you want, you may have. Whatever it is. Is she dry?'".
    On discuss { Assert bg_veasey_yielded(actor). Assert bg_veasey_word(actor). Assert knows(actor, d_barge_girl). Assert knows(actor, d_list_exists). Assert knows(actor, bg_bought). }
  }
  Topic bg_veasey_jettison with bg_veasey "Ask Mistress Veasey to let the Margaret be called a jettison, made to save a life" when bg_veasey_yielded(actor) and knows(actor, bg_average_known) and not bg_veasey_consents(actor) once {
    Says "'A jettison,' says Mistress Veasey. She says it as if it were a word in another tongue and the right one. 'A barge given up for a child. In the Lamprey's book, in the Lamprey's hand.' The knitting goes to a bag. 'I will sign it. I will sign it whatever it costs me and whoever I must pay.'".
    On discuss { Assert bg_veasey_consents(actor). }
  }
  Topic bg_veasey_after with bg_veasey "Ask Mistress Veasey how she stands now" when bg_settled() once {
    Says "'I stand,' says Mistress Veasey. She has taken up the knitting again, and the stitches, for the first time, are even. 'A person may be said to stand at several prices.'".
  }

  // ── The Lamprey's counting-floor: Orpwood, the manifest, the table of Averages ─────────────────────────────
  Thing bg_manifest "the Margaret's manifest" at lamprey_floor {
    State filed "The Margaret's manifest is pinned to the claims-rail in a clerk's copperplate: a barge, a master, and a cargo of COLD-LAMPS, SEALED, 400 JARS.".
  }
  Observe bg_manifest_seen at lamprey_floor when tried(bg_manifest, looking) and not knows(party, bg_manifest_read) "You read it down. The master is Absalom Tuck, a name nobody on the floor is able to place. The cargo is entered at four hundred jars, in nine crates. The draught is entered at three feet four."
    teaches bg_manifest_read.
  Thing bg_tally "the Stairs tally-board" at lighter_stairs {
    State chalked "A tally-board hangs by the Stair, chalked with every barge that has come up past it this month and what each said she carried.".
  }
  Observe bg_tally_seen at lighter_stairs when tried(bg_tally, looking) and not knows(party, bg_tally_read) "Against the Margaret, eleven days back, in the lighterman's own hand: three hundred and eleven jars, nine crates. Beside it, in another hand, somebody has written a small neat question mark and then rubbed it out."
    teaches bg_tally_read.
  Relation bg_compared(group).
  Action bg_compare(actor: group) "Set the Margaret's manifest against the count of her jars" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, lamprey_floor) and knows(actor, bg_manifest_read) and (knows(actor, bg_counted) or knows(actor, bg_tally_read)) and not bg_compared(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bg_compared(actor). Assert knows(actor, bg_count_short). }
    On failure { Assert bg_compared(actor). }
    Result "You lay one figure under the other and go down the column. Four hundred entered; three hundred and eleven counted. The draught is entered for a full lading, and a full lading would have sunk her a hand deeper than she sank. Eighty-nine jars, and a barge lightened to carry something else. The loss is not total. It is arranged.".
    Otherwise "You go down the column twice and come to a different figure each time. It is possible that this is a clerk's error. It is possible that it is something else. You are not able to say which, and a Lamprey clerk looks at you, helpfully, and does not.".
  }
  Thing bg_averages "the Lamprey's table of Averages" at lamprey_floor {
    State hung "A framed table of Averages hangs by the stair: PARTICULAR AVERAGE, GENERAL AVERAGE, JETTISON. The glass is spotted, and the frame is the only part that has been cleaned.".
  }
  Relation bg_table_read(group).
  Action bg_read_averages(actor: group) "Read the Lamprey's table of Averages for a hull given up on purpose" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, lamprey_floor) and not knows(actor, bg_average_known) and not bg_table_read(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert bg_table_read(actor). Assert knows(actor, bg_average_known). }
    On failure { Assert bg_table_read(actor). }
    Result "The third head is the one that matters. GENERAL AVERAGE: where a hull or a cargo is sacrificed to save life or common property, the loss is the common loss of owner, insurer and salvors, in their proportions; and the cause need not be entered, only the saving. It was written for sailors who had thrown the cargo overboard in a gale. Nothing in it says the gale must be weather.".
    Otherwise "You read the three heads and take them all to mean that somebody has lost something. The glass reflects a woman of no great learning reading a table.".
  }
  Relation bg_orp_open(group). Relation bg_orp_set(group).
  Topic bg_orp_call with bg_orpwood "Ask Mr Orpwood how he will call the Margaret" when true once {
    Says "'A Total Loss,' says Mr Orpwood. 'Holed from within by her own anchor. Not an uncommon accident. The owner is a woman of unblemished record, and she has sat on that wharf for two days looking at her loss, which in my experience is what the unblemished do.' He dips a pen. 'I sign at noon on the second day. Before that it would be a guess, and after the fourth day, it is a sale.'".
  }
  Topic bg_orp_confide with bg_orpwood "Ask Mr Orpwood, as a colleague, what he would call a barge holed to save a child" when (knows(actor, bg_berth) or knows(actor, d_barge_girl)) and not bg_orp_open(party) once {
    Says "Mr Orpwood puts down the pen. It takes him some time. 'I have a cuff,' he says, 'with a fish on it. A woman came to my counter, once, to ask a thing of the Lamprey that had nothing to do with fish, and I saw a paper cross the floor with a bird on it that I was not meant to see. I said what I said to her. I did not say it to anyone else. And then someone was kind to me, in a way I could not afterwards explain.' He does not look up. 'General Average,' he says. 'If the master and the captain would sign it. The master is a woman who would, I think. The captain is Captain Dree, who would not unless he had been asked correctly. You ask me as a colleague. I have not been asked as a colleague since I took the cuffs.'".
    On discuss { Assert bg_orp_open(actor). Assert knows(actor, d_barge_girl). Assert knows(actor, bg_bought). Assert knows(actor, bg_average_known). }
  }
  Topic bg_orp_after with bg_orpwood "Ask Mr Orpwood how the Margaret stands" when bg_settled() once {
    Says "'As called,' says Mr Orpwood. He looks, for once, like a man whose handwriting has been the same size all day. 'It makes a difference, I am told, when it is the right size.'".
  }

  // The call itself. Each is said to Mr Orpwood, and each is done before the bell, or not at all.
  Query bg_open() means bg_ruling(lamprey) <= 1 and watch(clock) < 600.
  Rule bg_default_call when watch(clock) >= 312 and bg_ruling(lamprey) == 0 says "At noon on the second day Mr Orpwood signs a Total Loss on the Prudent Margaret, and the lightermen along the Reach read it from a distance and agree that it is a pity." { Set bg_ruling(lamprey) to 1. }
  Action bg_call_salvage(actor: group) "Put it to Mr Orpwood that she was not lost but laid down, and call her a Salvage" {
    Speaker bg_orpwood.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, lamprey_floor) and at(bg_orpwood, lamprey_floor) and bg_open() and not bg_orp_set(actor)
      and (knows(actor, bg_count_short) or knows(actor, bg_berth) or knows(actor, bg_holed) or knows(actor, bg_skell_dived)).
    Time 6 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Set bg_ruling(lamprey) to 2. Increase regard(lamprey) by 1. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 12. Assert bg_veasey_ruined(party). }
    On failure { Assert bg_orp_set(actor). }
    Result "Mr Orpwood goes down your figures with a ruler and gets to the bottom more slowly than he got to the top. 'A salvage,' he says. 'One half to the Yard. The owner to bear the hull. I shall want it in writing that I did not say why.' He crosses out a word and writes another above it. 'The Lamprey is obliged to you,' he says, in the voice of a man being obliged. You are paid the Slate's twelve coin.".
    Otherwise "Mr Orpwood hears you out and signs nothing. 'Total Loss,' he says. 'I have the owner's good name on one side and your arithmetic on the other, and a man with a cuff is paid to prefer the first.' He will not hear the same figures again from you; you will have to bring him something that is not a figure.".
  }
  Relation bg_veasey_ruined(group).
  Action bg_call_fraud(actor: group) "Lay the scuttling before Mr Orpwood as a fraud on the Lamprey" {
    Speaker bg_orpwood.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, lamprey_floor) and at(bg_orpwood, lamprey_floor) and bg_open()
      and (knows(actor, bg_count_short) or knows(actor, bg_berth) or knows(actor, bg_holed) or knows(actor, bg_skell_dived) or knows(actor, d_barge_girl)).
    Time 6 minutes.
    Grave "A fraud handed to the Lamprey is a fraud entered in the Lamprey's book, with the berth in it. The Lamprey sends its books to the Phoenix, and there is a list.".
    On success { Set bg_ruling(lamprey) to 4. Increase regard(lamprey) by 2. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 12. Assert bg_girl_listed(bg_girl). Decrease regard(wardsfolk) by 2 or to nothing. Assert bg_gave_up_girl(party). }
    Result "Mr Orpwood writes it down without a word, and then writes it down again for the file. 'Fraud on the Lamprey,' he says. 'A barge holed from within, a berth made up in the hold, a passenger.' He does not ask who. He does not need to; the berth has a length. 'The Lamprey is grateful,' he says, 'and the Lamprey sends its books to the Phoenix every evening.' You are paid the Slate's twelve coin. It feels exactly like twelve coin.".
  }
  Relation bg_girl_listed(group). Relation bg_gave_up_girl(group).
  Action bg_call_average(actor: group) "Put it to Mr Orpwood that the Margaret is a General Average, given up to save a life, with the owner's and Captain Dree's names to it" {
    Speaker bg_orpwood.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, lamprey_floor) and at(bg_orpwood, lamprey_floor) and bg_open()
      and knows(actor, bg_average_known) and bg_veasey_consents(actor) and arc(dree) >= 1.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Set bg_ruling(lamprey) to 5. Increase regard(lamprey) by 2. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Assert bg_staying(bg_girl). }
    Result "Mr Orpwood reads Mistress Veasey's mark, and Captain Dree's, which is a capital D like a man standing on one leg. He does not ask who. 'General Average,' he says, 'on account of the saving of life. Owner, insurer and salvors in their proportions.' He blots it. 'It is the only entry in this book I have made in eleven years,' he says, 'that I would show my mother.' The Yard has half of what it would have had and Skell and Sons nothing, and the owner pays for her barge and is still, in some sense, her own person. You are paid ten coin. The Lamprey writes you down as a friend.".
  }
