  // ══ THE DIVING-BELL (the Reach's way down) ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // The bell goes two places: down onto the Margaret's hatch (workable at low water, brawn on the crank or coin to the
  // lightermen who turn it, and Captain Dree's blessing or none), and down the shaft to the foot of the Sunk City, behind
  // the hatch on the passage. The hatch has four ways open: Dree's leave, a forged writ, the Teague combination, and force.
  // The first crossing of the opened shaft is bad air: it hurts, drives the company back to the cradle, and airs the shaft;
  // after that the way is twenty minutes of ladder (a plain cost; the Descent may read the state of bg_hatch).
  Hazard bg_foul "the foul air of the diving shaft" means "Deal (1d4) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (11).".
  Thing bg_hatch "the bell's hatch" on bell_shaft_way {
    State shut blocking "The bell's hatch is dogged shut at the bottom of the cradle's well, a round plate of black iron with the Lamprey's fish riveted on it and a number-plate below, six dials that do not belong to any clock.".
    State open dangerous "The hatch stands open on a round dark shaft, and the air that comes up it smells like a cellar that has been shut a hundred years and has just remembered you.".
    State aired "The shaft has been aired by the first of you down it, and the air that comes up it now is only cold. A hundred rungs of ladder go down into the dark.".
    State wrecked blocking "The bell's hatch hangs by one dog, its plate buckled, the chain that held the bell snapped off short. Nothing will come up this shaft, and nothing will go down it.".
    Hurts with bg_foul when open then aired.
  }
  Action bg_hatch_leave(actor: group) "Show the bellman Captain Dree's leave and have the hatch dogged back" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cradle) and state(bg_hatch, shut) and dree_leave(actor).
    Time 4.
    On success { Assert state(bg_hatch, open). }
    Result "The bellman reads the chit and puts it in his hat. 'Captain's mark,' he says. 'Mind the air on the way, and the way up, if you come up.' The dogs come back, one at a time, and the hatch falls open on the dark.".
  }
  Action bg_hatch_writ(actor: group) "Show the bellman a writ of the Lamprey & River, not quite" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cradle) and state(bg_hatch, shut) and holding(actor, forged_writ).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_fair).
    On success { Spend forged_writ from actor. Assert state(bg_hatch, open). }
    On failure { Spend forged_writ from actor. Decrease regard(lamprey) by 1 or to nothing. Assert bg_writ_caught(party). }
    Result "The bellman holds the writ to the light and turns it over. 'Wet,' he says, doubtfully. 'Everything's wet.' He puts the paper in his hat as if it had been the real one and swings the dogs. The paper is not seen again.".
    Otherwise "The bellman holds the writ to the light, and then to a lamp, and then he goes very quiet. 'A fish,' he says, 'that has never met a river.' The writ goes into his hat and, presumably, up the stairs to Captain Dree. The dogs stay as they were.".
  }
  Relation bg_writ_caught(group).
  Action bg_hatch_combination(actor: group) "Set the six dials of the hatch to the Teague combination" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cradle) and state(bg_hatch, shut) and teagueCombination(actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert state(bg_hatch, open). }
    Result "Six dials, none of them a number you would have put there, and the plate sighs and comes up on its hinge. Ambrose Teague knew a way, and had the manners not to change the lock.".
  }
  Action bg_hatch_force(actor: group) "Break the hatch with the bell's own chain, and go down it hand over hand" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cradle) and state(bg_hatch, shut) and capable(actor, brawn).
    Time 18.
    Grave "Three hours of chain, and at the end of it the bell is wrecked and the hatch is a ruin: you go down, and nothing comes up that way again. Captain Dree will hear of it.".
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state(bg_hatch, wrecked). Assert at(actor, bell_foot). Decrease regard(lamprey) by 1 or to nothing. Assert bg_slighted_dree(party). Assert bg_bell_wrecked(party). }
    Result "You put the bell's own chain through the hatch-dogs and take the strain, one at a time, and the dogs go with a noise like a very old tooth. The hatch comes down the shaft with a crack. The chain goes after it, and then so do you, hand over hand, three hours of black cold and bad air. The bell hangs above you, empty and broken, and it is the last time it will go anywhere.".
    Otherwise "The chain runs through your hands and takes the skin with it, and the dogs hold. It is an hour before you can close a fist.".
  }
  Relation bg_slighted_dree(group). Relation bg_bell_wrecked(group).
  Observe bg_shaft_up at bell_foot when state(bg_hatch, open) or state(bg_hatch, aired) "The ladder rises into the dark shaft, a hundred rungs, to a hatch you cannot see. A little bad air comes down it in breaths.".
  Observe bg_shaft_wrecked at bell_foot when state(bg_hatch, wrecked) "The shaft above is choked with the buckled plate of the hatch and a coil of snapped chain. The way you came is no way at all.".

  // The Margaret, and the way down to her.
  Relation bg_dived(group).
  Action bg_dive_crank(actor: group) "Crank the diving-bell down over the Margaret's hatch yourselves" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cradle) and bg_lowwater() and not state(bg_hatch, wrecked) and capable(actor, brawn).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert at(actor, margaret_hold). Assert bg_dived(actor). }
    Result "The crank is a wheel the height of a man and it wants three. You take it on your own: the bell comes off its pawls, swings, and goes down over the quay's edge with a sound like a church dropping its voice. The water takes the glass and goes black, and then green. The Margaret's hatch comes up to meet the bell's lip, and the bell fits it as a cup does a saucer.".
    Otherwise "The pawls slip. The bell drops a yard, hangs, and goes up again on a shout from the gantry. You lose the tide and your temper.".
  }
  Action bg_dive_hired(actor: group) "Pay the lightermen six coin to turn the crank, and go down in the bell" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cradle) and bg_lowwater() and not state(bg_hatch, wrecked) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 6.
    Time 3.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Assert at(actor, margaret_hold). Assert bg_dived(actor). }
    Result "Three lightermen take the crank without having to be told twice, and a fourth keeps the time. The bell goes down with you in it, sitting very still on the bench, and settles over the Margaret's hatch like a hand over a candle.".
  }
  Action bg_surface(actor: group) "Rap on the bell for the lightermen to wind you up" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, margaret_hold).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert at(actor, cradle). }
    Result "Three raps on the bell's iron, and a pause, and the crank takes up. You rise through the green and the black and into the afternoon with your ears ringing.".
  }
  Rule bg_hold_floods when at(party, margaret_hold) and not bg_lowwater()
    says "The tide has turned. Water comes in round the bell's lip in a grey sheet, and the lightermen up top, who have been counting, haul without being asked." {
    Assert at(party, cradle). }
  Rule bg_slight_charged when bg_dived(party) and not bg_bell_ok(party) and not bg_slighted_dree(party)
    says "Word of a company that took the Lamprey's bell down without so much as a chit goes up Policy Row with the morning rolls." {
    Assert bg_slighted_dree(party). Decrease regard(lamprey) by 1 or to nothing. }
  Observe bg_hold_light at margaret_hold when true "The jars that are still alight make a green dusk the size of a room. Their glow does not so much lighten the water as agree with it.".
  Thing bg_crates "the cold-lamp crates" at margaret_hold {
    State stowed "Nine crates are stacked in the waist, two of them burst and drifting, the rest tumbled against each other in their straw, each jar sealed with wax and a little stamp.".
  }
  Observe bg_crates_counted at margaret_hold when tried(bg_crates, looking) "You count them off by their own light, crate by crate: three hundred and eleven jars. The upper tiers of the straw are bone dry, where the crates have been moved, and then moved back by someone who was quick."
    teaches bg_counted.
  Thing bg_bunk "the berth in the straw" at margaret_hold {
    State made "In the lee of the cuddy bulkhead a berth has been made in the straw, lengthways, the length of a child: a blanket, a heel of bread gone to paste, and a candle-end in a saucer.".
  }
  Observe bg_berth_seen at margaret_hold when tried(bg_bunk, looking) "The blanket has been folded with a mother's corners. Near the saucer, scratched on a cask-end with a nail, are four tally-marks, a row of crooked letters that spell KITTY, and, underneath, a small drawing of a fish with legs."
    teaches bg_berth.
  Thing bg_hull "the Margaret's planking" at margaret_hold {
    State holed "The planking of the waist is split in a star, low on the starboard side, and the water comes through it in a slow brown braid.".
  }
  Observe bg_hull_seen at margaret_hold when tried(bg_hull, looking) "You put your lamp to the split. The planks are driven outwards, not in: the splinters stand away from the hull like the petals of a flower. A pair of ship's augers lies in the bilge below it, bright where the rust has been rubbed off by a hand."
    teaches bg_holed.
}

data/adventures/quittance/q_coldlamp.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "The Cold-Lamp Demonstration: Perpetua Wynne's lamps are to be shown to the Offices on the fourth day at three, each holds a spark that must be vented nightly, and the Gas Company needs them to fail.".

  // ── The clock of the Quarter: six and six ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Gasworks changes shift at the whistle at six in the morning and at six at night, and the two shifts
  // hand over in the yard for the hour before it: the retort-house stands empty then. The day foreman keeps
  // the yard by day; the steward lives on the Stokers' Steps, and on the fourth afternoon he is at the Gasworks
  // arguing the Company out of docking his men.
  Query cl_h_day() means hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 17.
  Query cl_h_foreman() means hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 18.
  Query cl_h_swap() means hour(clock) == 17 or hour(clock) == 5.
  Query cl_h_night() means hour(clock) >= 18 or hour(clock) < 5.
  Query cl_afternoon_four() means day(clock) == 4 and hour(clock) >= 13 and hour(clock) < 17.
  // The demonstration is at three on the fourth day, in the demonstration hall.
  Query cl_demo_due() means day(clock) == 4 and hour(clock) >= 16.

  Discovery cl_claim "On the Slate: the Philosophical Lamp-house shows its cold-lamps to the Offices on the fourth day at three, and has asked for steady hands.".
  Discovery cl_sickening "The cold-lamps in the demonstration hall are yellow and whining: they have not been vented for a week, and tomorrow night they will be sick.".
  Discovery cl_shed_shown "A free spark can stay of its own will where it is kept like a guest: there is one doing it in a glaziers' shed.".

  // ── People ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person wynne "Perpetua Wynne" at wynne_lab {
    Role "inventor of the cold-lamp". Ancestry human. Calling mage. Level 3. Trait evoker. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns she.
    Known as "a woman asleep on a stool" when not knows(party, cl_wynne_met).
    Greets "A woman in a canvas apron is asleep on a stool with her cheek on a notebook and a pencil still in her fist. She wakes the moment you come in, the way a woman wakes who has been sleeping with one eye on a door. 'Wynne,' she says. 'Perpetua. The Lamp-house. I was not asleep.' She looks at the shelf of jars. 'Nine days,' she says. 'It is nine days since I slept in a bed.'".
    Greets again "'You,' says Perpetua Wynne, and rubs her eyes. 'Good. I was just about to forget something.'".
  }
  Discovery cl_wynne_met "You have met Perpetua Wynne, who built the cold-lamp and has not slept properly since.".
  Person quarrell "Lemuel Quarrell" at lamp_front {
    Role "apprentice at the Lamp-house". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A young man is dusting a shelf of globes with a feather duster and an expression of ghastly cheerfulness. 'Mind the green ones,' says Lemuel Quarrell. 'They're the dear ones. The white ones are only expensive.'".
    Greets again "'Back!' says Lemuel Quarrell. 'Do mind the green ones.'".
  }
  Person threlfall "Amos Threlfall" at round_steps {
    Role "steward of the Gasworks stokers". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A stoker with arms like banisters is sitting on a step with a ledger on his knee, not reading it. 'Threlfall,' he says. 'I speak for the day men and the night men, which is to say for the half of them who are awake at any hour. If you've come to be kind, don't. If you've come to be of use, sit down.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Amos Threlfall. 'The useful ones.'".
  }
  Person mallow "Ned Mallow" at retort_house {
    Role "stoker of the Gasworks". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A stoker leans on a shovel in front of the great boiler, black to the elbow, with the face of a man who has been paid to watch a thing that has never once done anything. 'Mallow,' he says. 'Days. If it goes up, I go up. If it doesn't, nobody remembers my name.'".
    Greets again "'Mallow,' says Ned Mallow, as if you might have forgotten.".
  }
  Person hesketh "Old Hesketh" at nowhere {
    Role "stoker of the Gasworks". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "An old man with a lamp on his hat is sitting on an upturned bucket by the boiler, eating bread and dripping off a shovel. 'Hesketh,' he says. 'Nights. Mind the damper, the damper is a liar.'".
    Greets again "'Hesketh,' says Old Hesketh.".
  }

  // The day foreman minds the yard by day; the stokers go where the whistle puts them.
  Rule cl_gudgeon_in when cl_h_foreman() and at(gudgeon, ?p) and distinct(?p, gas_yard) { Retract at(gudgeon, ?p). Assert at(gudgeon, gas_yard). }
  Rule cl_gudgeon_out when not cl_h_foreman() and at(gudgeon, gas_yard) { Retract at(gudgeon, gas_yard). Assert at(gudgeon, nowhere). }
  Rule cl_mallow_in when cl_h_day() and at(mallow, ?p) and distinct(?p, retort_house) { Retract at(mallow, ?p). Assert at(mallow, retort_house). }
  Rule cl_mallow_swap when cl_h_swap() and at(mallow, ?p) and distinct(?p, gas_yard) { Retract at(mallow, ?p). Assert at(mallow, gas_yard). }
  Rule cl_mallow_off when cl_h_night() and at(mallow, ?p) and distinct(?p, nowhere) { Retract at(mallow, ?p). Assert at(mallow, nowhere). }
  Rule cl_dace_in when cl_h_night() and at(hesketh, ?p) and distinct(?p, retort_house) { Retract at(hesketh, ?p). Assert at(hesketh, retort_house). }
  Rule cl_dace_swap when cl_h_swap() and at(hesketh, ?p) and distinct(?p, gas_yard) { Retract at(hesketh, ?p). Assert at(hesketh, gas_yard). }
  Rule cl_dace_off when cl_h_day() and at(hesketh, ?p) and distinct(?p, nowhere) { Retract at(hesketh, ?p). Assert at(hesketh, nowhere). }
  Rule cl_threlfall_board when cl_afternoon_four() and at(threlfall, ?p) and distinct(?p, board_room) { Retract at(threlfall, ?p). Assert at(threlfall, board_room). }
  Rule cl_threlfall_steps when cl_h_day() and not cl_afternoon_four() and at(threlfall, ?p) and distinct(?p, round_steps) { Retract at(threlfall, ?p). Assert at(threlfall, round_steps). }
  Rule cl_threlfall_home when not cl_h_day() and hour(clock) != 17 and at(threlfall, ?p) and distinct(?p, nowhere) { Retract at(threlfall, ?p). Assert at(threlfall, nowhere). }
  Observe cl_whistle at gas_yard when cl_h_swap() "The shifts are handing over in the yard: two lots of men, one black from the day and one clean from the street, standing in lines passing a pot of tea between them, not speaking, and a long hand-bell is rung once on the gasometer stair. The retort-house doors have been left on the latch.".

  // ── The Slate, and the shopfront ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe cl_slate at slip_room when day(clock) >= 1 and day(clock) <= 4 "Chalked in a neat copper-plate by a clerk who did not enjoy it: THE PHILOSOPHICAL LAMP-HOUSE WILL SHEW ITS COLD-LAMPS TO THE OFFICES, FOURTH DAY, THREE O'CLOCK, DEMONSTRATION HALL, FOUNDRY ROW. THE GAS COMPANY WILL ATTEND. STEADY HANDS WANTED, AND A STRONG STOMACH FOR SPEECHES." teaches cl_claim.
  Objective cl_obj_demo when knows(party, cl_claim) and not cl_demoDone(wynne) "The Cold-Lamp Demonstration, the fourth day at three: see which of the Gas Company, the Phoenix and the inventor gets what it wants.".
  Relation cl_demoDone(group). Relation cl_crateGiven(group). Relation cl_jarred(group). Relation cl_boiled(group). Relation cl_freed(group).
  Relation cl_stewardSide(group). Relation cl_noticeUp(group). Relation cl_exposed(group). Relation cl_walkingWynne(group).
  Relation cl_adopted(group). Relation cl_adoptedOpen(group). Relation cl_gaswon(group). Relation cl_refused(group). Relation cl_confessed(group). Relation cl_ruined(group).
  Relation cl_ordinanceTight(group). Relation cl_lanternGiven(group). Relation cl_coalGiven(group). Relation cl_flattered(group). Relation cl_profitTried(group). Relation cl_keyBought(group).
  Relation cl_slighted_gasco(group). Relation cl_slighted_wynne(group). Relation cl_slighted_phoenix(group). Relation cl_tipTried(group). Relation cl_flatterTried1(group). Relation cl_flatterTried2(group).
  Measure cl_stage(group). Measure cl_ventedAt(group).
  Query cl_involved() means knows(party, cl_wynne_met) or arc(gaunt) > 0 or cl_boiled(wynne) or cl_freed(wynne) or cl_stewardSide(wynne) or cl_exposed(wynne).
  Query cl_stopped() means arc(gaunt) >= 2 or cl_boiled(wynne) or cl_stewardSide(wynne).

  Topic cl_t_quarrell with quarrell "Ask Lemuel Quarrell what the Lamp-house is showing, and to whom" when not knows(party, cl_claim) once {
    Says "'The cold-lamps,' says Lemuel Quarrell, 'to the Offices, in the hall behind me, the fourth day at three. A hundred of them, hung up on wires. Miss Wynne has not been to bed. She says it is the venting; I don't ask. I am only the apprentice and I am only to say that the Lamp-house is delighted.' He dusts a globe that did not need it. 'It is not delighted. She has not vented since Tuesday week. The lamps have gone a sort of colour.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, cl_claim). }
  }
  Topic cl_t_quarrell2 with quarrell "Ask Lemuel Quarrell what 'venting' is" when knows(party, cl_claim) once {
    Says "'Every night,' says Lemuel Quarrell, 'the glass has to be let off. There is something in each lamp, a sort of a spark, that sits there for the light, and it has to be let out into a jar for an hour and then taken back, or it sulks, or the lamp does. Dim, then yellow, then sick. Miss Wynne does it herself; she has never let me see. I am forbidden from the jars.' He lowers his voice. 'I am forbidden from them because I once said good night to one.'".
  }

  // ── The Demonstration Hall: the lamps themselves ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Thing cl_rack "the hundred cold-lamps" at demo_hall {
    State sickening "A hundred cold-lamps hang from the ceiling on wires. They are lit, if that is the word: a thick yellow light that comes and goes, and under it a whine at the edge of hearing like a kettle thinking. Two in the front row have gone out.".
    State bright "A hundred cold-lamps hang from the ceiling on wires, lit white and perfectly still, with a hum like a hive that has been told good news.".
    State empty "A hundred cold-lamps hang from the ceiling on wires, dark. They are glass and nothing else: when you put your hand near one it is the temperature of the room.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(cl_rack, sickening).
  Rule cl_dim when state(cl_rack, bright) and watch(clock) >= cl_ventedAt(wynne) + 156 { Assert state(cl_rack, sickening). }
  Observe cl_rack_sign at demo_hall when state(cl_rack, sickening) and not knows(party, cl_sickening) "Along the front row a lamp gutters, brightens, and goes out. The next one does the same, a little later, as if the dark were being passed down a line." teaches cl_sickening.
  Item cl_crate "a crate of empty catch-jars" is cl_crate_empty at nowhere.
  Item cl_full "a crate of catch-jars, each lit from within" is cl_crate_full at nowhere.
  Kind cl_crate_empty "a crate of empty catch-jars" is gear worth 0 weighing 1 described "A wooden crate of stoppered glass jars, each labelled NIGHT and a number in a quick, tired hand.".
  Kind cl_crate_full "a crate of catch-jars, each lit from within" is gear worth 0 weighing 1 described "A wooden crate of stoppered glass jars. In each a spark the colour of a bruise-yellow ember turns on its own axis and puts its face, if it has one, against the side facing you.".
  Item cl_lantern "a salamander-glass lantern" is salamander_lantern at nowhere.

  // ── Perpetua Wynne ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic cl_w_show with wynne "Ask Wynne about the demonstration" when not cl_demoDone(wynne) once {
    Says "'The fourth day, at three,' says Wynne. 'The Offices will sit on the benches and I will light a hundred lamps at one word, and they will look at the ceiling the way people look at a thing they would like to own and be told is cheap. The Phoenix wants fewer fires. The Gas Company wants me poor.' She pushes the notebook an inch away. 'Each lamp has to be vented. Every night. I can do it in six hours with the whole rack. I have not done it since Tuesday week, because I have been writing the speech.' She looks at the shelf. 'I am aware of what that means.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, cl_wynne_met). }
  }
  Topic cl_w_offer with wynne "Offer to vent the lamps for her, tonight, while she sleeps" when state(cl_rack, sickening) and not cl_crateGiven(wynne) and not cl_demoDone(wynne) {
    Says "Wynne looks at you for a long moment. 'It is six hours,' she says. 'You open each cock a quarter-turn, you catch what comes in the jar, you set the jar on the bench for an hour, you put it back. It is not skilled. It is only... You do not have to look at them.' She takes the crate down. 'I will not watch. I have found I cannot. Do not tell me how it goes.'".
    On discuss { Assert cl_crateGiven(wynne). Give cl_crate to actor. }
  }
  Topic cl_w_sparks with wynne "Ask Wynne where the sparks come from" when knows(party, cl_wynne_met) once {
    Says "'The furnaces,' says Wynne. 'The Foundry's own, when the Company bricked them. They came out of the chimneys in the first spring, small, like pollen. I caught them in jars. I thought they were a vapour.' A pause. 'I thought a good many things.'".
  }
  Topic cl_w_tell with wynne "Tell Wynne what the sparks did when you let them out" when knows(party, d_cold_lamp_bound) and cl_stage(wynne) == 0 and not cl_demoDone(wynne) {
    Says "You say it as plainly as you can: that when the cocks were opened they came out into the jars and turned, all together, and looked at you, and that when the stoppers were put in they did not look away. Wynne sits down on the stool. 'Of course they did,' she says, in a voice you would not like to be responsible for. 'Of course. I have written NIGHT FORTY-ONE on a jar. Forty-one nights.' She is silent. 'If there is another way to make light, I will not keep them. I will not. Show me another way and I will do it with my hands. I cannot do it with my reasons.'".
    On discuss { Set cl_stage(wynne) to 1. }
  }
  Topic cl_w_come with wynne "Ask Wynne to come and look at a flame in a glaziers' shed" when cl_stage(wynne) == 1 and not cl_walkingWynne(wynne) {
    Says "'A flame in a shed,' says Wynne. 'On what?' You tell her: on nothing; on a bench. She takes off her apron.".
    On discuss { Assert cl_walkingWynne(wynne). Assert following(wynne, actor). }
  }
  Action cl_show_shed(actor: group, site: place) "Show Wynne the flame that stays in the glaziers' shed" {
    Speaker wynne.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wynne, site) and at(ll_shed, site) and cl_walkingWynne(wynne) and cl_stage(wynne) == 1.
    Time 20 minutes.
    On success { Set cl_stage(wynne) to 2. Retract following(wynne, actor). Retract cl_walkingWynne(wynne). Assert at(wynne, wynne_lab). Assert knows(actor, cl_shed_shown). }
    Result "Wynne stands in the shed door with her apron half off one shoulder. The flame on the bench between the stacks of glass leans a very little toward her, as it leans toward anything that is not going to put a lid on it. 'It is not in anything,' she says. 'Nothing is holding it. It has a door, the whole of the passage is a door, and it stays.' Master Hune says it likes the cullet. 'It likes being fed,' says Wynne. 'It likes being asked.' She is gone before you notice, back up the Row at a trot, with the apron over her arm. When you reach the laboratory she is drawing a lamp with a hinged door in the side of it.".
  }
  Topic cl_w_lantern with wynne "Ask Wynne about the lamp with a door" when cl_stage(wynne) == 2 and not cl_lanternGiven(wynne) once {
    Says "'It is not a lamp,' says Wynne, 'it is a room. The glass is salamander-glass, the old Foundry kind, and the door is in the base. It has been out three times now, and come back three times. I have not caught it. It stays because the room is warm.' She puts it in your hands. It is warm like something asleep. 'Keep it lit. Open the door if it asks. It will ask.'".
    On discuss { Assert cl_lanternGiven(wynne). Give cl_lantern to actor. }
  }
  Topic cl_w_told_freed with wynne "Tell Wynne you let the sparks go, on the bricks of the Furnace Wharf" when cl_freed(wynne) and cl_stage(wynne) >= 1 and not cl_coalGiven(wynne) once {
    Says "Wynne does not move for some time. 'Where did they go?' she says. You tell her: into the warm bricks, the old furnace-mouths, one after another, like swallows into a barn. 'Home,' says Wynne, and takes off her glasses, and that is all she says for a minute. Then: 'One of them stayed. It is in the back jar, on the left. I did not put it there. It came out of the wall of the lab, and sat down.'".
    On discuss { Assert cl_coalPending(wynne). }
  }
  Relation cl_coalPending(group).
  Action cl_coal(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Wynne for the spark that stayed, lit" {
    Speaker wynne.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wynne, site) and cl_coalPending(wynne) and not cl_coalGiven(wynne) and day(clock) >= 7 and quantity(actor, coal) < 2.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Increase quantity(actor, coal) by 1. Set coalExpires(actor) to watch(clock) + 144. Assert cl_coalGiven(wynne). }
    Result "Wynne lifts the back jar down and unstoppers it. The spark comes out on to her palm, sits for a moment, and then climbs on to the ember she has banked in a tin, which takes it without remark. 'It is a coal,' she says. 'It is lit. It was lit when it came. Don't thank me, it did it on its own.' The tin is warm through your coat, and ticks.".
  }

  // What Wynne says afterwards: the world remembers how the afternoon went.
  Topic cl_a_ruined with wynne "Ask Wynne what she will do now" when cl_ruined(wynne) {
    Says "'Go back to my sister in the country,' says Wynne, folding a cloth over a jar, 'and light a candle. It will be very strange to have something burn that doesn't know me.'".
  }
  Topic cl_a_adopted with wynne "Ask Wynne how the order stands" when cl_adopted(wynne) and not cl_adoptedOpen(wynne) {
    Says "'Three hundred,' says Wynne. 'By Michaelmas. I have been told that it is a triumph. I have been awake for it.' She looks at the shelf of jars, and does not say what she is thinking, and neither do you.".
  }
  Topic cl_a_open with wynne "Ask Wynne how the order stands" when cl_adoptedOpen(wynne) {
    Says "'Three hundred, with doors,' says Wynne. 'The Phoenix wrote it into the order in its own hand, and then sent a man to ask what a door was.' She is very nearly smiling. 'I have told him it is a thing you can leave by.'".
  }
  Topic cl_a_refused with wynne "Ask Wynne how she feels about not showing them" when cl_refused(wynne) {
    Says "'The Gas Company showed them a chandelier,' says Wynne. 'It was a perfectly good chandelier.' She turns a jar to the wall. 'I am not sorry. I am only unemployed. Find me a way, if there is one, and I will make you something that does not need a lid.'".
  }
  Topic cl_a_confessed with wynne "Ask Wynne how the Offices took it" when cl_confessed(wynne) {
    Says "'Politely,' says Wynne. 'Ottoline Prewitt took notes. The Chairman asked whether they would be available in a smaller size.' She takes her glasses off. 'I do not know what I am now. I know I am not a keeper.'".
  }
  Topic cl_a_gaunt with gaunt "Ask Lord Gaunt-Halloran how the Company finds the cold-lamp business" when arc(gaunt) >= 2 and cl_demoDone(wynne) {
    Says "'A licence,' says Lord Gaunt-Halloran, 'is a lamp that burns for ever in a ledger.' He is looking at the chandelier without malice. 'One must move with the age. One has always said so, in the age before.'".
  }

  // ── The venting, and where the night's spark goes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Action cl_vent(actor: group, site: place) "Vent the hundred lamps into the catch-jars, a row at a time, through the night" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(cl_rack, site) and holding(actor, cl_crate_empty) and not cl_demoDone(wynne) and not state(cl_rack, empty).
    Time 36.
    On success { Spend cl_crate_empty from actor. Give cl_full to actor. Assert state(cl_rack, bright). Set cl_ventedAt(wynne) to watch(clock). Assert knows(actor, d_cold_lamp_bound). }
    Result "You open the cocks a quarter-turn each, and set a jar to every one, and wait. They come out slowly, one spark to a lamp, and you move along the row. Somewhere about the thirtieth they all turn together to look at you. It is not an expression. It is only that a hundred small lights, which had been turning as lights turn, all stop turning. When you stopper the last jar the lamps overhead glare white and settle, and the jars in the crate go on watching you. The hall hums like a hive that has been told good news.".
  }
  Action cl_return_jars(actor: group, site: place) "Carry the catch-jars back to Wynne's shelf" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wynne, site) and holding(actor, cl_crate_full).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Spend cl_crate_full from actor. Assert cl_jarred(wynne). }
    Result "You set the jars on the shelf where they were, by their numbers, and they turn to face the wall.".
  }
  Thing cl_firedoor "the boiler's fire-door" at retort_house {
    State chained "The great boiler's fire-door is chained shut with a company padlock, and a card tied to the chain says TO BE OPENED BY THE STOKER ON DUTY ONLY.".
    State open "The fire-door hangs open on the great boiler's white heart.".
  }
  Action cl_tip_pick(actor: group, site: place) "Slip the padlock on the boiler fire-door while the retort-house is empty, and tip the catch-jars in" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(cl_firedoor, site) and holding(actor, cl_crate_full) and not at(mallow, site) and not at(hesketh, site) and not cl_tipTried(wynne).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, lockwork, dc_fair).
    On success { Spend cl_crate_full from actor. Assert cl_boiled(wynne). Assert state(cl_firedoor, open). }
    On failure { Assert cl_tipTried(wynne). }
    Result "The padlock is the Company's best, and not good enough. You pour the jars through the door one at a time. The sparks go in like children into the sea, and the boiler's white heart goes blue, and a long way off in the yard a gauge begins to climb.".
    Otherwise "The padlock is the Company's best. It bites a thumb and holds, and somewhere in the yard a boot turns toward the door. You go out the way you came with the crate and the jars watching you.".
  }
  Action cl_tip_bribe(actor: group, site: place) "Give the stoker on duty five coin to look at his dinner while the catch-jars go into the boiler" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(cl_firedoor, site) and holding(actor, cl_crate_full) and (at(mallow, site) or at(hesketh, site)) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 5.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Spend cl_crate_full from actor. Assert cl_boiled(wynne). Assert state(cl_firedoor, open). }
    Result "The stoker takes the coin, sits down on the coal-bin with his back to you and his dinner on his knee, and eats it with great attention. The sparks go in like children into the sea. The boiler's white heart goes blue. He does not look up even when the gauge starts to climb. 'Nobody ever remembers the stoker,' he says, with his mouth full. 'It's the principle of the thing.'".
  }
  Action cl_tip_steward(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Threlfall's men to turn their backs while the catch-jars go into the boiler" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(cl_firedoor, site) and holding(actor, cl_crate_full) and cl_stewardSide(wynne) and (at(mallow, site) or at(hesketh, site) or hour(clock) == 17 or hour(clock) == 5).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Spend cl_crate_full from actor. Assert cl_boiled(wynne). Assert state(cl_firedoor, open). }
    Result "The stoker on duty has his instructions from his steward: for the next quarter of an hour he is a man with an excellent view of the coal-bin. The sparks go in like children into the sea. The boiler's white heart goes blue.".
  }
  Rule cl_boiler_roars when cl_boiled(wynne) and not cl_roared(wynne) says "A long way across the Gasworks yard the gasometer rides up its guides as if it had been given a key. The Company's engineer opens the relief, and a flame twenty feet high stands on the relief-stack for a quarter of an hour, with no smoke at all. Every pilot-light in the Quarter, for a moment, leans toward the retort-house." {
    Assert cl_roared(wynne). Assert cl_slighted_gasco(party). Decrease regard(gasco) by 1 or to nothing.
  }
  Relation cl_roared(group).
  Action cl_free(actor: group, site: place) "Open the catch-jars to the warm bricks of the old furnace-mouths, and let the sparks go" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ll_lamp_f, site) and holding(actor, cl_crate_full) and knows(actor, d_cold_lamp_bound).
    Time 15 minutes.
    Grave "Sparks let go do not come back to the lamps. A hundred cold-lamps will be glass.".
    On success { Spend cl_crate_full from actor. Assert cl_freed(wynne). Assert state(cl_rack, empty). }
    Result "You unstopper the jars one at a time and hold each to a crack in the bricks. They go in, one by one, the way water goes into sand, and the bricks that were warm are for a moment hot. A flicker runs along the bricked mouths of the furnaces, forty furnaces, forty bricks, and goes out. In the lamp-house above you, on the Wharf, the gulls stand up, and sit down again, and face the wall.".
  }
  Observe cl_wharf_freed at round_furnace when cl_freed(wynne) "The warm bricks of the furnace-mouths are warmer than they were, and one of them has a shine on it, like a chestnut.".

  // ── The Gas Company, and what moves it ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule cl_notice_up when day(clock) == 4 and hour(clock) >= 12 and not cl_noticeUp(wynne) and not cl_stopped() says "At noon a stoker in a Company cap nails a notice to the door of the demonstration hall: CLOSED PENDING EXAMINATION OF VAPOURS, BY ORDER OF THE GAS COMPANY'S INSPECTORATE. The stoker does not look at anyone while he does it." {
    Assert cl_noticeUp(wynne).
  }
  Topic cl_g_wynne with gaunt "Ask Lord Gaunt-Halloran what the Company thinks of the Lamp-house's demonstration" when not cl_demoDone(wynne) once {
    Says "'A toy,' says Lord Gaunt-Halloran. 'A very pretty toy. It makes no heat and no smoke and no revenue, which is, I need hardly say, three defects. We shall of course sit through it. We shall be very courteous.' He looks at the chandelier. 'The Inspectorate has been told to take an interest in the vapours.'".
  }
  Action cl_flatter1(actor: group, site: place) "Admire the gasometer to Lord Gaunt-Halloran, at some length, from the window" {
    Speaker gaunt.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(gaunt, site) and arc(gaunt) == 0 and not cl_flatterTried1(gaunt).
    Time 15 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Set arc(gaunt) to 1. Assert cl_flatterTried1(gaunt). }
    On failure { Assert cl_flatterTried1(gaunt). }
    Result "You describe the gasometer as the lung of a city, and then as its conscience, and then, for variety, as its mother. Lord Gaunt-Halloran, who has been looking at it for thirty years, turns from the window with wet eyes. 'You see it,' he says. 'You are the first who has said it without a figure.'".
    Otherwise "'Quite,' says Lord Gaunt-Halloran, who has been admired by experts.".
  }
  Action cl_flatter2(actor: group, site: place) "Notice aloud that the chandelier hisses in tune" {
    Speaker gaunt.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(gaunt, site) and arc(gaunt) == 0 and not cl_flatterTried2(gaunt).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Set arc(gaunt) to 1. Assert cl_flatterTried2(gaunt). }
    On failure { Assert cl_flatterTried2(gaunt). }
    Result "It does: a thin steady A, a little flat. Lord Gaunt-Halloran has had it tuned, he confesses, at some expense, by a man who tunes organs, and in nine years nobody has noticed. He puts a hand on your arm.".
    Otherwise "You say it hisses nicely. He says it ought to, for what it costs.".
  }
  Action cl_profit(actor: group, site: place) "Put it to Lord Gaunt-Halloran that the Company could hold the licence for the cold-lamps, and meter them" {
    Speaker gaunt.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(gaunt, site) and arc(gaunt) == 1 and not cl_profitTried(gaunt).
    Time 20 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Set arc(gaunt) to 2. Assert cl_profitTried(gaunt). }
    On failure { Assert cl_profitTried(gaunt). }
    Result "A lamp that makes no gas, you say, still wants a company to lay its wire and read its dial and send its quarterly bill. 'A meter,' says Lord Gaunt-Halloran slowly, as men say 'a daughter.' 'On a lamp that cannot be seen to burn.' By the end of the quarter-hour he is drafting terms for the inventor on the back of a gas-bill. The Inspectorate, he adds, will be told to lose interest in vapours.".
    Otherwise "'The Company,' says Lord Gaunt-Halloran, 'sells light by the foot. A lamp without a foot...' He makes a gesture of the hand that dismisses a river.".
  }
  Action cl_buy_key(actor: group, site: place) "Have a gilt first-lamp key struck at the Booths, for the Chairman to open the demonstration with (5 coin)" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(booth_clerk, site) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 5 and not cl_keyBought(gaunt).
    Time 30 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Assert cl_keyBought(gaunt). }
    Result "A booth clerk in a paper cap will strike you a gilt key in an hour: THE FIRST LIGHT, with a ribbon. 'It is only brass, of course,' she says brightly. 'But it is insured for gold.'".
  }
  Action cl_role(actor: group, site: place) "Offer Lord Gaunt-Halloran the honour of opening the demonstration with the first-lamp key" {
    Speaker gaunt.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(gaunt, site) and arc(gaunt) == 1 and cl_keyBought(gaunt).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Set arc(gaunt) to 2. }
    Result "You lay the gilt key on the table. Lord Gaunt-Halloran does not touch it. He stands and looks at it as a man looks at his own name carved in a door. 'The Chairman of the Gas Company,' he says, 'turning the first light of the age.' He puts it in his waistcoat. 'It is a beginning. One begins. One has always said so.' The Inspectorate, he adds, will be asked to take an interest in the ceremony and no longer in the vapours.".
  }
  Topic cl_g_poor with gaunt "Mention the stokers' docked half-days to Lord Gaunt-Halloran" when arc(gaunt) >= 0 and not cl_demoDone(wynne) once {
    Says "'The men,' says Lord Gaunt-Halloran, 'are a matter for Mr Gudgeon.' He turns the page of nothing. 'We were speaking of the future.'".
  }

  // ── The steward ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic cl_t_grievance with threlfall "Ask Threlfall what ails the stokers" when not cl_stewardSide(wynne) once {
    Says "'Half a day,' says Threlfall. 'Docked. A pilot goes out on a man's shift, it goes down against him. Pilot-neglect. Six a month, the Company reckons.' He holds up a thumb and finger a hair apart. 'They do go out. All the lamps, yard and street, in one breath, and back in the next, and the man minding them is down for neglect, because there has to be a man.' He taps the ledger. 'Six half-days a month, a man. I'll not make a speech. Prove it wasn't us and I'll buy the tea.'".
  }
  Topic cl_t_side with threlfall "Tell Threlfall the pilots go out in step across the whole Quarter, and you have seen it" when knows(party, d_pilots_step) and not cl_stewardSide(wynne) {
    Says "Threlfall lays down the ledger. 'The whole Quarter,' he says. 'Not the yard alone.' You tell him: the lamps on the Row, the Wharf, the Steps, every one, in one instant. 'Then it isn't a man's shift,' says Threlfall slowly. 'It can't be. I've a hundred and eleven men on the books who are not in a hundred and eleven places.' He gets up. 'I'll have that read into the Company's own minutes. And the Company can have an afternoon of its own stokers at its own door, and a notice that gets lost, because someone will carry the notice and I'm the one who tells them where the post is.'".
    On discuss { Assert cl_stewardSide(wynne). }
  }
  Topic cl_t_afternoon with threlfall "Ask Threlfall why he is up at the Gasworks this afternoon" when cl_afternoon_four() once {
    Says "'The hours,' says Threlfall. 'There is a meeting with the Chairman at two about the new rota, and it is the Chairman, so it will go on till four. I've told my men to say nothing to anyone and to stand where they're put.'".
  }

  // ── Exposing the flaw ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Action cl_expose(actor: group, site: place) "Show Ottoline Prewitt a sickened lamp, and tell her what is in it, for the Phoenix to decide" {
    Speaker ottoline.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ottoline, site) and knows(actor, d_cold_lamp_bound) and not cl_demoDone(wynne) and not cl_exposed(wynne).
    Time 20 minutes.
    Grave "The Phoenix will ask the Lamp-house for its books; and the Lamp-house is one inventor and a boy with a duster.".
    On success { Assert cl_exposed(wynne). Assert cl_regarded(wynne). Assert cl_slighted_wynne(party). Decrease regard(phoenix) by 1 or to nothing. Assert cl_slighted_phoenix(party). Increase regard(gasco) by 1. }
    Result "Ottoline Prewitt hears you out with the pencil behind her ear quite still. 'In glass,' she says. 'Against their will.' She writes it down. 'I will take it to my father,' she says, 'because I must. I am so sorry. I wish you had told me before you were sure.' By evening the Offices have asked the Lamp-house for its books.".
  }

  // ── The demonstration ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule cl_d_exposed when cl_demo_due() and not cl_demoDone(wynne) and cl_exposed(wynne) says "At three o'clock the Offices send word that they will not be attending. The hall is empty. The Gas Company, which does attend, is gracious about it. The Lamp-house's books are sealed; Perpetua Wynne is seen going out of the front door with a canvas apron over her arm." {
    Assert cl_demoDone(wynne). Assert cl_gaswon(wynne). Assert cl_ruined(wynne).
  }
  Rule cl_d_confess when cl_demo_due() and not cl_demoDone(wynne) and cl_freed(wynne) and cl_stage(wynne) >= 1 says "At three o'clock the Offices sit on the benches, and Perpetua Wynne walks to the platform and does not light a lamp. 'These are glass,' she says. 'They were lit by something I kept in a jar. It is not in them now. I will not light them again, and I will tell you what it was.' She tells them. Mr Prewitt's daughter, in the second row, writes it all down. The Gas Company's Chairman, who has been looking forward to this afternoon for a month, finds that he has no appetite for it. The Smokeless Ordinance is referred to a committee." {
    Assert cl_demoDone(wynne). Assert cl_confessed(wynne).
  }
  Rule cl_d_dark when cl_demo_due() and not cl_demoDone(wynne) and cl_freed(wynne) says "At three o'clock the Offices sit on the benches and Perpetua Wynne throws the word, and a hundred lamps do nothing at all. She looks at the ceiling, and then, which is worse, at the Offices. 'Someone has been in,' she says. The Gas Company sends her a basket of fruit." {
    Assert cl_demoDone(wynne). Assert cl_gaswon(wynne). Assert cl_ruined(wynne). Assert cl_slighted_wynne(party).
  }
  Rule cl_d_refuse when cl_demo_due() and not cl_demoDone(wynne) and cl_stage(wynne) == 1 says "At three o'clock the Offices sit on the benches, and Perpetua Wynne comes out on to the platform, and says that she is very sorry, and that she will not light them. She does not say why. She goes back to the laboratory and shuts the door, and the Gas Company, with great delicacy, shows the Offices a gas chandelier it happens to have brought." {
    Assert cl_demoDone(wynne). Assert cl_refused(wynne). 
  }
  Rule cl_d_blocked when cl_demo_due() and not cl_demoDone(wynne) and cl_noticeUp(wynne) and not cl_stopped() says "At three o'clock the Offices stand on the step reading a notice, and the Gas Company's Inspectorate regrets that the hall cannot be opened until the vapours have been examined, which will be some weeks. Lord Gaunt-Halloran, who has come in his best coat, is very sorry. Perpetua Wynne, behind the door, does not come out." {
    Assert cl_demoDone(wynne). Assert cl_gaswon(wynne). Assert cl_ruined(wynne). 
  }
  Rule cl_d_sick when cl_demo_due() and not cl_demoDone(wynne) and not state(cl_rack, bright) says "At three o'clock the Offices sit on the benches and Perpetua Wynne throws the word, and a hundred lamps come up the colour of weak tea, whine, and begin to go out along the front row, one after another, as if the dark were being passed down a line. The Gas Company applauds. It is a very short ovation, and perfectly sincere." {
    Assert cl_demoDone(wynne). Assert cl_gaswon(wynne). Assert cl_ruined(wynne). 
  }
  Rule cl_d_open when cl_demo_due() and not cl_demoDone(wynne) and cl_stage(wynne) == 2 says "At three o'clock Perpetua Wynne throws the word, and a hundred lamps come up white and still. The Offices applaud. 'These are the last I shall make like this,' says Wynne, over it. 'The next will have a door.' She holds up a drawing. The Phoenix's Chief Underwriter, in the front row, who has not smiled in six years, writes something and underlines it. The Smokeless Ordinance is read a fourth time, with a rider for the lamps." {
    Assert cl_demoDone(wynne). Assert cl_adopted(wynne). Assert cl_adoptedOpen(wynne). Assert cl_ordinanceTight(wynne).
  }
  Rule cl_d_adopt when cl_demo_due() and not cl_demoDone(wynne) says "At three o'clock Perpetua Wynne throws the word, and a hundred lamps come up white and still, and the Offices applaud as one applauds a thing that will save money. The Phoenix orders three hundred. The Smokeless Ordinance is read a fourth time, with a rider for the lamps. Perpetua Wynne, on the platform, takes her bow without looking at the ceiling." {
    Assert cl_demoDone(wynne). Assert cl_adopted(wynne). Assert cl_ordinanceTight(wynne).
  }

  // The Offices and the Gas Company think well or ill of a company that took a hand, not of one that was never there.
  Relation cl_regarded(group).
  Rule cl_regard_won when cl_adopted(wynne) and cl_involved() and not cl_regarded(wynne) { Assert cl_regarded(wynne). Increase regard(phoenix) by 2. Decrease regard(gasco) by 1 or to nothing. }
  Rule cl_regard_lost when (cl_gaswon(wynne) or cl_refused(wynne)) and cl_involved() and not cl_regarded(wynne) { Assert cl_regarded(wynne). Increase regard(gasco) by 1. Decrease regard(phoenix) by 1 or to nothing. }
  Rule cl_regard_confessed when cl_confessed(wynne) and cl_involved() and not cl_regarded(wynne) { Assert cl_regarded(wynne). Decrease regard(phoenix) by 1 or to nothing. }

  // ── What the demonstration leaves ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe cl_notice_door at lamp_front when cl_noticeUp(wynne) and not cl_demoDone(wynne) "A printed notice is nailed to the demonstration hall door: CLOSED PENDING EXAMINATION OF VAPOURS.".
  Observe cl_lab_ruined at wynne_lab when cl_ruined(wynne) "Perpetua Wynne is packing: the notebooks in one crate, the jars in another, with a cloth between them. She does not look up. 'The landlord,' she says, 'has been very understanding.'".
  Observe cl_lab_adopted at wynne_lab when cl_adopted(wynne) "The laboratory has been given an extra bench and two assistants and a case of Phoenix stationery, and Perpetua Wynne sits at the end of it with her chin on her hand, designing a door.".
  Observe cl_lab_refused at wynne_lab when cl_refused(wynne) "Perpetua Wynne sits with her back to the shelf of jars, which she has turned to face the wall, and her chin on her fists.".
  Observe cl_slate_tight at slip_room when cl_ordinanceTight(wynne) "On the Slate, under PREMIUMS, in a fresh hand: the Smokeless Ordinance read a fourth time. An amended clause: cold-lamps recommended in all inner wards, and open hearths in them to be struck from the Roll after Reckoning.".
  Observe cl_hall_after at demo_hall when cl_demoDone(wynne) and not state(cl_rack, empty) "The benches have been put back and a boy is sweeping up programmes.".
}

data/adventures/quittance/q_forger.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "Ma Gedge's back-shop in Dyers' Alley: counterfeit Phoenix plates for the unmarked poor, a mark-hunter with a sister, and the reason the plates work.".

  // ══ The hunt, and who is behind which plate ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // The Phoenix's hunter, Mr Dabney, finds the shop on the evening of the second day (watch 336) unless the company
  // has done something about him or her. Everything the company writes about it is by name for the Hearing and the
  // endings: fg_network (a web of marked doors in the Wards, fg_doors of them), fg_informed (reported), fg_turned
  // (the hunter turned), fg_extorted.
  Entity fg_shop: group "Ma Gedge's back-shop".
  Measure fg_doors(group).
  Relation fg_network(group). Relation fg_better(group). Relation fg_informed(group). Relation fg_turned(group).
  Relation fg_extorted(group). Relation fg_trusted(group). Relation fg_warned(group). Relation fg_bailed(group).
  Relation fg_raided(group). Relation fg_raid_done(group). Relation fg_protected(group). Relation fg_hostile(group).
  Relation fg_plate_taken(group). Relation fg_sister_asked(group). Relation fg_read_dabney(group).

  Discovery fg_claim "The Slate has a claim chalked on it: the Phoenix wants the founder of false plates.".
  Discovery fg_plates "False Phoenix plates, nailed up by the unmarked, are going up on doors in the Bare Wards, and a Phoenix hunter is looking for who casts them.".
  Discovery fg_forger "The plates are cast by Ma Gedge, in the back-shop in Dyers' Alley, who was die-sinker to the Phoenix itself for thirty-one years.".
  Discovery fg_sister "Mr Dabney, the Phoenix's hunter, has a sister in Salt Lane, and she has a bird over her door that Ma Gedge cast.".
  Discovery fg_hunter_known "A man called Dabney is hunting the founder of the false plates, and he is nearer than the founder knows.".

  Kind fg_plate_kind "a plate of Ma Gedge's" is treasure worth 2 weighing 0 described "A gilt bird on an iron backing with a nail-hole at each corner, correct to the last feather. It is not quite round. It looks, you think, very slightly more tired than the real ones.".
  Item fg_plate "a plate of Ma Gedge's" is fg_plate_kind at nowhere.
  Item fg_writ "a writ of the Lamprey & River Office, not quite" is forged_writ at nowhere.

  Thing fg_dies "the master dies" at gedge_back {
    State fg_dies_out "On the bench, wrapped in a chamois, lie three master dies, bird, fish and hand, each the size of a child's palm. They are the best-made things in Quittance.".
    State fg_dies_hidden "The bench is bare except for a tin of rivets and a half-made door-knocker, in the shape of a hand.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(fg_dies, fg_dies_out).

  // ── The people ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person fg_gedge "Ma Gedgewick" at gedge_back {
    Role "die-sinker, retired by the Phoenix". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 3. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A broad old woman in a leather apron looks up from a tray of sand with a face like a clenched fist that has been told a joke. She has a file in one hand and she does not put it down. 'Gedgewick,' she says. 'Nobody has called me that since the Works. It's Ma Gedge in the alley. The door's for customers, which you aren't. I make door-knockers.' A cough takes her, and she waits for it as for a tradesman. 'And the hundred on the wall are for the collection of a gentleman who has not yet been born.'".
    Greets again "'Door-knockers,' says Ma Gedge, to you, in the tone of a woman handing in her notice.".
  }
  Person fg_dabney "Mr Dabney" at dyers_alley {
    Role "mark-hunter, hired by the Phoenix". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Level 3. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A lean man in a brown coat is standing at the mouth of the alley with a plate in one hand and a magnifying glass in the other, examining the plate as though it had been rude. He has a very tidy beard and the stoop of a person who has spent a great many years looking at the bottoms of doors. 'Dabney,' he says. 'Mark Office. I am retained to find who is casting these.' He turns the plate. 'Do not trouble to say you have seen nothing. Nobody sees anything in the Wards, and the Wards are where they all are.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Mr Dabney, putting the glass in his pocket. 'The adjusters.'".
  }

  // ── The first sign, and the second ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe fg_notice at brick_lane when watch(clock) < 384 "A new notice is pasted over the old ones at the Lane's mouth: THE PHOENIX MARK OFFICE WILL PAY TWELVE COIN FOR THE NAME OF ANY PERSON CASTING OR SELLING FALSE PLATES. The word FALSE has been scratched out by someone and written in again by someone else." teaches fg_plates.
  Observe fg_slate at slip_room when watch(clock) < 384 and not fg_raided(fg_shop) "CLAIMS OPEN: PHOENIX MARK OFFICE. A plate cast in no foundry of the Office's has been seen nailed up in the Bare Wards, correct to the last feather. The Office will pay twelve coin to any adjuster who can name the founder." teaches fg_claim.
  Observe fg_wards_plate at salt_lane when true "Beside a doorway on the Lane a gilt bird is nailed up over a hearth-stone, and a small boy is polishing it with his sleeve. It is a very good bird. It is not quite round." teaches fg_plates.
  Observe fg_shop_scene at gedge_back when true "The bench is covered with moulds and sand and file-dust, and a fire-pot ticks at the back with the sound of a clock in a coffin. A tray of fresh-cast birds cools on a rack. One of them, you notice, is still wet." teaches fg_forger.
  Observe fg_network_scene at salt_lane when fg_network(party) "Over every fourth door in Salt Lane, now, a bird; over every fifth a hand. The woman at the pump touches two fingers to her forehead as you pass. Nobody says anything. It is a very quiet city.".
  Observe fg_dabney_after near fg_dabney when fg_turned(party) "Mr Dabney tips his hat to you and goes on turning the plate over and over, with his glass in his pocket.".
  Observe fg_shop_raided at gedge_back when fg_raided(fg_shop) and at(fg_gedge, engine_room) "The back-shop has been turned over by men with their boots on. The bench is bare, the rack is gone, and a Phoenix seal is pasted across the fire-pot.".

  // ── Ma Gedge ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic fg_g_wall with fg_gedge "Ask Ma Gedge about the plates on her wall" when true once {
    Says "'Samples,' says Ma Gedge. 'From my days.' She does not say which days. 'Thirty-one years I was die-sinker to the Mark Works. I cut the master of that bird, with my own hands, from a drawing by a man who had never seen a feather. Then they put in a steam press and a contractor, and I was told that a person of no registered mark can't draw a pension.' She files a rivet. 'So I make door-knockers.'".
  }
  Topic fg_g_hunter with fg_gedge "Warn Ma Gedge that a Phoenix hunter in Dyers' Alley is looking for her plates" when knows(actor, fg_hunter_known) and not fg_warned(party) and not fg_hostile(party) and not fg_raided(fg_shop) once {
    Says "Ma Gedge sets the file down. It is the first time, you think, in some while. 'Dabney,' she says. 'The one with the glass.' She looks at the rack, the bench, the dies, and then at you with an expression of intense, unwilling calculation. 'You could've had twelve coin from him this morning,' she says. 'Why didn't you?' When you do not answer she wraps the three dies in their chamois, one by one, and goes out with them through the back, and comes in again without. 'Sit down,' she says. 'There's tea. It's terrible.'".
    On discuss { Assert fg_warned(party). Assert fg_trusted(party). Assert state(fg_dies, fg_dies_hidden). }
  }
  Topic fg_g_past with fg_gedge "Ask Ma Gedge how she came to cast for the Wards" when fg_trusted(party) once {
    Says "'The Wards bought my doors,' says Ma Gedge. 'The Mark Works never did. Three winters ago a boy came to me with a tin of his mother's pewter. His house had burned the week before and the Phoenix had stood in the road and watched it, because it had no plate. I made him a bird. I thought: it's tin, and a nail. A bird's a bird.' She looks at her hands. 'He nailed it up, and the next fire in his street, the lads came.'".
  }
  Topic fg_g_why with fg_gedge "Ask Ma Gedge why a plate nobody cast should keep a house" when fg_trusted(party) once {
    Says "'Because of who's looking,' says Ma Gedge. 'Nine in ten of the lads in the Phoenix's blue were born within a mile of Salt Lane. They know what a bird is and what it isn't. A man in a Phoenix coat looks at a tin bird nailed up over a poor man's door and thinks: Mum's got one of those. He can't do much, you see. He's not allowed to put water on an unmarked house. But he's allowed to read a plate.' She wipes her face with a sooty wrist. 'Not every time. Not when a captain is by. But some. Enough that I keep working.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, d_marks_work). }
  }
  Topic fg_g_ledger with fg_gedge "Ask Ma Gedge who her best customers are" when fg_trusted(party) and not fg_sister_asked(party) once {
    Says "'There's a book,' says Ma Gedge, 'and nobody's to have it.' She opens it to the Ds. 'A Cissie Dabney, in Salt Lane. Four birds in a year; a girl who wanted the biggest bird I had. She said she had a brother in the Office, who'd never look at the bottom of a door he hadn't been told about.' Ma Gedge looks up. 'I thought it was funny.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, fg_sister). Assert fg_sister_asked(party). }
  }
  Action fg_join(actor: group) "Ask Ma Gedge to show you how a plate is cast, and how a writ is sealed" {
    Speaker fg_gedge.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, gedge_back) and at(fg_gedge, gedge_back) and fg_trusted(party) and not fg_network(party) and not fg_raided(fg_shop) and not fg_hostile(party).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert fg_network(party). Increase fg_doors(party) by 12. Give fg_writ to actor. Assert knows(actor, d_marks_work). }
    Result "Ma Gedge shows you the sand, the sprue, the pour and the file, in the order, she says, that they bite you. By dusk you can cast a bird that no one would call round. She takes a sheet of Lamprey foolscap from under the bench, signs a captain's name across it without looking, drops a blot on the corner and blots the blot, and slides it over. 'For the diving-bell,' she says. 'Dree's men never read what they sign. Don't use it on the Wharf, use it on the bell. And you don't know me.' It is, she explains, her pension.".
  }
  Action fg_buy_plate(actor: group) "Buy a finished bird from Ma Gedge's rack (3 coin)" {
    Speaker fg_gedge.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, gedge_back) and at(fg_gedge, gedge_back) and fg_trusted(party) and not fg_plate_taken(party) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3.
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Give fg_plate to actor. Assert fg_plate_taken(party). }
    Result "'For the tin,' says Ma Gedge, and gives you a bird with the wet still a little in the feathers. 'Nail it up. Don't polish it, they like it duller.'".
  }
  Action fg_improve_lore(actor: group) "Show Ma Gedge what is wrong with her feathers, from the true bird on the fire-house wall" {
    Speaker fg_gedge.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, gedge_back) and at(fg_gedge, gedge_back) and fg_trusted(party) and not fg_better(party) and not fg_hostile(party) and capable(actor, lore).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert fg_better(party). Increase fg_doors(party) by 8. }
    Result "You tell her, from the fire-house wall and your memory of the plate over Mark Street, that the true bird has seven tail-feathers and that she has cast eight, because the man who drew the original had never seen a bird. Ma Gedge says nothing for a full minute. Then she takes down the master, turns it in the light, and says a word that she does not repeat in front of company. 'Thirty-one years,' she says. 'Nobody told me.' The next tray comes out with seven.".
    Otherwise "You say that the feathers are wrong and cannot say how. Ma Gedge looks at you with great patience. 'Some of them,' she says. 'Do go on.'".
  }
  Action fg_improve_mend(actor: group) "Take the file from Ma Gedge and put right the crooked bevel on the master bird" {
    Speaker fg_gedge.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, gedge_back) and at(fg_gedge, gedge_back) and fg_trusted(party) and not fg_better(party) and not fg_hostile(party) and capable(actor, mending).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, mending, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert fg_better(party). Increase fg_doors(party) by 8. }
    Result "You take a quarter-inch off the left shoulder of the bird with a file the shape of a tongue, and the plate that comes out of the next pour sits flat against the wall for the first time in its life. Ma Gedge holds it to the lamp. 'I'd know that a mile off,' she says. 'It's better.' She does not sound entirely pleased.".
    Otherwise "The file skates and you take a corner off the mould. Ma Gedge looks at the corner and at you. 'It'll cast,' she says, 'with an air.'".
  }
  Action fg_extort(actor: group) "Tell Ma Gedge that Mr Dabney would pay twelve coin for her address, and that you could be talked out of it" {
    Speaker fg_gedge.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, gedge_back) and at(fg_gedge, gedge_back) and not fg_extorted(party) and not fg_trusted(party) and not fg_raided(fg_shop) and capable(actor, intimidation).
    Time 5 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert fg_extorted(party). Assert fg_hostile(party). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 15. Decrease regard(wardsfolk) by 1 or to nothing. }
    On failure { Assert fg_hostile(party). }
    Result "Ma Gedge listens, as she listens to a tradesman with a bill, and counts fifteen coin out of a tin on the shelf, slowly, onto the sand. She does not say anything. 'This is for knowing the shop,' she says finally, 'not for keeping the secret. I won't be using you again.' The coins are quite warm.".
    Otherwise "'Twelve coin,' says Ma Gedge. 'You'd get a better price for your boots.' She turns her back, and the file in her hand begins to move again, steadily, a quarter-inch from the table. 'Door-knockers,' she says. 'Next.'".
  }
  Topic fg_g_after with fg_gedge "Ask Ma Gedge how her pension is coming on" when fg_network(party) once {
    Says "'Forty-one doors by the end of next week,' says Ma Gedge, 'if nobody burns before then.' She nods, once, at the rack. 'There's a woman in Candlewick Court who's paid in advance for her fourth. I told her the lads would come. She said it's not the lads she's paying for. It's the nail.'".
  }
  Topic fg_g_paid with fg_gedge "Ask Ma Gedge what it was like in the fire-house cell" when fg_bailed(party) once {
    Says "'Quiet,' says Ma Gedge. 'They gave me a blanket with a mark on it. I looked at it a good while. It was a very bad bird.' She wipes her hands on her apron. 'I owe you ten coin and the use of my bench. Come when you need it.'".
  }
  Action fg_bail(actor: group) "Pay Ma Gedge's fine at the fire-house desk (10 coin)" {
    Speaker fg_gedge.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, engine_room) and at(fg_gedge, engine_room) and fg_raided(fg_shop) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 10.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Assert at(fg_gedge, gedge_back). Assert fg_bailed(party). Assert fg_trusted(party). Retract fg_raided(fg_shop). Assert state(fg_dies, fg_dies_hidden). }
    Result "The desk-sergeant, a Pargeter by the look of the chin, writes the sum in a book, rubs it out, and writes it again. 'Fined for a nuisance,' he says. 'Door-knockers.' Ma Gedge comes out of the back with her apron over her arm, and does not look at you until the street, where she says, with a rough, incomplete courtesy, 'I'll want my dies.'".
  }

  // ── Mr Dabney ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic fg_d_hunt with fg_dabney "Ask Mr Dabney what he is hunting" when true once {
    Says "'Plates,' says Mr Dabney. 'A bird with eight tail-feathers, where the Office's has seven, and a fish with a crooked eye. The same hand every time. I have forty-one in a drawer.' He turns the plate over. 'The Office pays me a farthing a door, and a bounty at the founder. I am told she is a woman.' He looks, briefly, down Dyers' Alley, at a hundred and fifty years of die-works. 'I expect to know by Wednesday.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, fg_hunter_known). Assert knows(actor, fg_plates). }
  }
  Topic fg_d_why with fg_dabney "Ask Mr Dabney why the Office minds, if nobody is hurt" when knows(actor, fg_plates) once {
    Says "'Because a plate is a promise,' says Mr Dabney, 'and the Office does not honour promises made by people it did not make them to. If a house with a false plate burns and the brigade turns out, the Office has been defrauded of a hose.' He pauses. 'Though I have never in my career seen the brigade refuse.'".
  }
  Action fg_read_dabney(actor: group, site: place) "Watch Mr Dabney's face while he talks about the Wards, and see what he is not saying" {
    Speaker fg_dabney.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(fg_dabney, site) and not knows(actor, fg_sister) and not fg_read_dabney(party) and knows(actor, fg_hunter_known).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, fg_sister). Assert fg_read_dabney(party). }
    On failure { Assert fg_read_dabney(party). }
    Result "He talks about the Wards the way a man talks about a country he left: very exactly. And when he reaches Salt Lane, he stops, and looks at his own thumb for a moment, and goes on; and you understand that somebody lives in Salt Lane, and that it matters what is nailed over her door.".
    Otherwise "Mr Dabney talks for ten minutes about plates and mouldings, and gives away precisely as much as a closed door.".
  }
  Action fg_report(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Mr Dabney where the plates are cast, and take the Office's twelve coin" {
    Speaker fg_dabney.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(fg_dabney, site) and knows(actor, fg_forger) and not fg_informed(party) and not fg_turned(party) and not fg_raid_done(fg_shop).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success {
      Assert fg_informed(party). Assert fg_raided(fg_shop). Assert fg_raid_done(fg_shop). Assert at(fg_gedge, engine_room).
      Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 12. Increase regard(phoenix) by 1. Decrease regard(wardsfolk) by 1 or to nothing. Assert at(fg_dabney, phoenix_floor).
    }
    Result "Mr Dabney writes the name in the small book. He does not look pleased. 'Gedge,' he says. 'Dyers' Alley. A woman I should think I walked past forty times.' He takes twelve coin out of an envelope and counts it into your palm like a man paying for something he has already eaten. By nightfall, the shop is shut, and a long row of Phoenix seals is across its door.".
  }
  Topic fg_d_sister with fg_dabney "Ask Mr Dabney whether the door of his sister's house in Salt Lane has a bird on it, and whose" when knows(actor, fg_sister) and not fg_turned(party) and not fg_informed(party) once {
    Says "Mr Dabney has stopped turning the plate. For some time he does not seem to be anywhere. 'Cissie,' he says. 'She put it up in the spring. She said it was a present.' His thumb moves over the eighth feather of the plate he has been holding for a month, and then, slowly, his glass goes into his pocket. 'I shall report,' says Mr Dabney, 'that the founder is a tinsmith, deceased. It's a very common trade. It has a very large list of deceased.' He puts the plate in his coat. 'I did not,' he says, 'ask who looked.'".
    On discuss { Assert fg_turned(party). Assert fg_protected(fg_shop). Assert witness(fg_dabney). }
  }
  Topic fg_d_after with fg_dabney "Ask Mr Dabney how the hunt is going" when fg_turned(party) once {
    Says "'Wednesday,' says Mr Dabney, 'has been postponed.' He considers. 'Indefinitely. I have found three new tinsmiths.'".
  }

  // ── The complication: why the marks work ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic fg_tob_plates with tobias "Ask Tobias Pargeter whether he has ever turned out for a plate he knew was false" when knows(actor, fg_plates) once {
    Says "Tobias Pargeter turns his helmet round once before he answers. 'Not knew,' he says. 'Wondered.' He looks at the black fish nailed backwards on his sideboard. 'There's a bird up in Candlewick that hasn't got the right feathers. We turned out for the house two years ago. Captain Garrity said nothing at all about it. She stood beside the pump and looked at the plate, and I thought, she knows, she knows, she's going to say it. And she said, Water.' He sets the fish straight, and then back. 'Half the lads are from the Wards. We don't look hard. It's a thing you can not-see, if you're brought up to it. You'd be surprised how often.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, d_marks_work). }
  }

  // ── The hunt's clock ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule fg_raid_empty when watch(clock) >= 336 and fg_warned(party) and not fg_protected(fg_shop) and not fg_raid_done(fg_shop) says "At four on the second afternoon Mr Dabney goes down Dyers' Alley with two men in blue and a warrant and comes out of the die-works twenty minutes later with a door-knocker, in the shape of a hand, and a face that suggests that he has been given something to think about." {
    Assert fg_raid_done(fg_shop).
  }
  Rule fg_raid_full when watch(clock) >= 336 and not fg_protected(fg_shop) and not fg_raid_done(fg_shop) says "At four on the second afternoon Mr Dabney goes down Dyers' Alley with two men in blue and a warrant. By five the shop is shut, the fire-pot has a seal on it, and an old woman in a leather apron is being walked up Brick Lane to the fire-house, still holding her file." {
    Assert fg_raid_done(fg_shop). Assert fg_raided(fg_shop). Assert at(fg_gedge, engine_room). Assert at(fg_dabney, phoenix_floor).
  }
  Objective fg_obj when (knows(party, fg_claim) or knows(party, fg_plates)) and not fg_raid_done(fg_shop) "Someone is casting false Phoenix plates for the doors of the Bare Wards, and a mark-hunter will have the founder by the evening of the second day.".
  Objective fg_obj_after when fg_raided(fg_shop) and not fg_bailed(party) and at(fg_gedge, engine_room) "Ma Gedge is in the fire-house cell for a nuisance, with her dies in a drawer. The fine is ten coin.".
}

Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "The Lamplighter's Round: Hob Tansy's last dusk in the Glass Quarter, four lamps each dark for a different reason, a way to retire an old man, and the pilot-flames that go out and come back together.".

  // ── Clocks ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The lamps are lit from five until nine. The gas-lamps of the Foundry come out of Hob's hands on the night of the fifth day,
  // whatever the Offices think of cold-lamps: the Gas Company's lease on the Row's brackets runs out, and the
  // brackets go to the mains. If the company is not there, Hob walks the Round alone, and the Stokers' Steps are
  // fifty steps long.
  Query ll_dusk() means hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 21.
  Query ll_lastNight() means (day(clock) == 5 and hour(clock) >= 21) or day(clock) >= 7.

  Discovery ll_claim "On the Slate: the Lamplighters' Hall asks for hands to walk the Foundry Round with Hob Tansy, who is retired when the cold-lamps come in.".
  Discovery ll_nan_hid "A child is hiding in the lamp-house on the Furnace Wharf: there is a boot-toe under its door.".
  Discovery ll_glow_seen "In a glaziers' shed off the Glaziers' Passage a flame stands on a slab with nothing to burn, and the lamp over the corner is out.".

  // ── People ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person hob "Hob Tansy" at lamplighters_hall {
    Role "lamplighter of the Foundry Round". Ancestry human. Calling ranger. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns he.
    Known as "an old man with a pole on his shoulder" when not knows(party, ll_hob_met).
    Greets "An old man is coming down Foundry Row at the pace of his own pole, a brass-tipped thing twice his height, and he is looking at the lamps he passes as one looks at the faces of the dead. His eyes are the white of boiled eggs. 'Tansy,' he says, to the air a little to your left. 'Hob. Forty-one years the Row's. You'll be the adjusters. I can hear a licence.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Hob Tansy, to your left. 'I know that boot.'".
  }
  Discovery ll_hob_met "You have met Hob Tansy, who has lit the lamps of Foundry Row for forty-one years.".
  Person quoyle "Warden Quoyle" at lamplighters_hall {
    Role "Warden of the Lamplighters' Hall". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A tall woman is polishing a tinder-box with the cuff of her sleeve, which has been polishing tinder-boxes for some time. 'Quoyle,' she says. 'Warden. The Hall is open to any lamplighter and to anyone who has come about one. There is a book by the door. It is not for signing.'".
    Greets again "'You again,' says Warden Quoyle, and goes on polishing.".
  }
  Person gudgeon "Foreman Gudgeon" at gas_yard {
    Role "day foreman of the Gasworks". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A man with a notice in one hand and a pencil in the other looks up from reading it. 'Gudgeon,' he says. 'Foreman. Days. If it's the stokers, the steward is Threlfall. If it's the Company, the Company is upstairs and does not come down.'".
    Greets again "'Still here,' says Foreman Gudgeon, without surprise.".
  }
  Person oddy "Mrs Oddy" at round_tinkers {
    Role "widow of a tinker, who sells what her husband did not". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A woman leans out of a shuttered shop-front, over a tray of small white bags like the fingers of gloves. 'Mantles,' says Mrs Oddy. 'Incandescent. Two coin, and I will tell you which of my husband's lamps they do not fit, which is all of them.'".
    Greets again "'Mantles,' says Mrs Oddy, in welcome.".
    Sells ll_mantle for 2 coin from 6.
  }
  Person strood "Mrs Strood" at round_steps {
    Role "a stoker's widow, who lives at the top of the Steps". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A woman in a shawl stands on the top step with her arms folded and her back to a shop. 'If you've come to take his side,' says Mrs Strood, 'you may say so now and save the stairs.'".
    Greets again "'Well,' says Mrs Strood.".
  }
  Person beadle "Mr Beadle" at round_steps {
    Role "a pawnbroker, who lives at the foot of the Steps". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A round man in a waistcoat is standing in a shop doorway at the foot of the Steps with a ring of keys, looking up at the top of the stairs as at a bad debt. 'Beadle,' he says. 'Pawnbroker. Whatever she has said of me is true in the particular and false in the whole.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Mr Beadle. 'Witnesses.'".
  }
  Person nan "Nan Rudge" at round_furnace {
    Role "the stoker Rudge's daughter, aged eight". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns she.
    Seen when knows(viewer, ll_nan_hid).
    Greets "A very small voice, from above and behind the glass of the lamp, says, 'He can't light it if I'm in it. It's the rule.'".
    Greets again "'I'm not coming down,' says Nan Rudge.".
  }
  Person hune "Master Hune" at round_glaziers {
    Role "glazier". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A man with a glazier's diamond on a string round his neck is eating his dinner off a window-sill. 'The lamp's out,' says Master Hune, before you can ask. 'Went out in the spring. We don't relight it. Not that it can't be.'".
    Greets again "'Still out,' says Master Hune, comfortably.".
  }

  // ── The Slate, and the way Hob is met ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe ll_slate at slip_room when day(clock) >= 1 and day(clock) <= 5 "Chalked low on the Slate, in a hand that is not the boy's: WANTED, TWO PAIRS OF EYES FOR AN OLD LAMPLIGHTER. LAST ROUND, FIFTH NIGHT, DUSK. APPLY LAMPLIGHTERS' HALL, FOUNDRY ROW. NO FEE; THE ROUND IS ITS OWN." teaches ll_claim.
  Objective ll_obj_round when knows(party, ll_claim) and not ll_ended(hob) "Walk Hob Tansy's last round with him at dusk: four lamps in the Glass Quarter, and then decide how an old lamplighter is to be retired.".
  Relation ll_walking(group). Relation ll_everWalked(group). Relation ll_handed(group). Relation ll_trusts(group). Relation ll_told(group). Relation ll_moved(group).
  Relation ll_ended(group). Relation ll_hurt(group). Relation ll_bitter(group). Relation ll_roundDone(group). Relation ll_breathing(group). Relation ll_breathed(group).
  Relation ll_pensionOffer(group). Relation ll_placeOffer(group). Relation ll_flueClear(group). Relation ll_hallClosed(group).
  Relation ll_howPension(group). Relation ll_howPlace(group). Relation ll_howFinish(group). Relation ll_howPlain(group). Relation ll_howHearth(group). Relation ll_howFell(group).
  Relation ll_sideSteps(group). Relation ll_sideShop(group). Relation ll_sideBoth(group). Relation ll_mantled(group). Relation ll_slighted_gasco(group). Relation ll_shedTaper(group).
  Measure ll_lit(group). Measure ll_breathAt(group).

  // Hob is on Foundry Row from five to eight, the rest of the day in the Hall; ended, in the Hall at all times but
  // for the one night, and not at all on a night the company has him by the arm.
  Rule ll_hob_to_row when ll_dusk() and at(hob, lamplighters_hall) and not ll_ended(hob) and not ll_hurt(hob) { Retract at(hob, lamplighters_hall). Assert at(hob, foundry_row). }
  Rule ll_hob_to_hall when not ll_dusk() and at(hob, foundry_row) and not following(hob, party) { Retract at(hob, foundry_row). Assert at(hob, lamplighters_hall). }
  Observe ll_hob_row at foundry_row when at(hob, foundry_row) and not ll_ended(hob) "The lamps along the Row are dark, and an old man stands at the corner with his pole upright in both hands, his face turned up toward each bracket in turn, as if reading.".

  // ── Hob's talk ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic ll_t_met with hob "Ask Hob what he is doing with that pole" when not ll_ended(hob) once {
    Says "'Lighting,' says Hob. 'Forty-one years at it. Tinkers' Court, the Stokers' Steps, the Glaziers' Passage, the Furnace Wharf. Four, at the end; there were thirty when I started and I knew them by their smell.' He lowers the pole. 'Friday the Company turns them off at the main, and puts a cold thing on the bracket, or a tap, or nothing. I don't ask which. I've the one more round.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ll_hob_met). Assert knows(actor, ll_claim). }
  }
  Topic ll_t_eyes with hob "Ask Hob about the four lamps" when knows(party, ll_hob_met) and not ll_ended(hob) once {
    Says "'The ones I can't see,' says Hob, simply. 'Tinkers' lamp wants a mantle and I can't find the bracket to put it on. The Steps are a quarrel, and I can't see who is standing where. The Wharf lamp has a child in it, I should say, or something with a child's breath. And the Passage lamp has been out since spring and I do not go in, because there is something in the shed that I do not care to be lit by.' He turns his face to you. 'Walk it with me. I would like to do the last one right, and I would like to be told where I am.'".
  }
  Topic ll_t_walk with hob "Offer to walk Hob's last round with him, tonight" when ll_dusk() and knows(party, ll_hob_met) and not ll_walking(hob) and not ll_ended(hob) and not ll_roundDone(hob) {
    Says "'Good,' says Hob. 'Take my elbow. Not that one. You'll find I steer.' He gives you the taper and the brass tinder-box, and keeps the pole.".
    On discuss { Assert ll_walking(hob). Assert ll_everWalked(hob). Assert following(hob, actor). Assert knows(actor, ll_hob_met). }
  }
  Topic ll_t_leave with hob "Tell Hob you'll bring the lamps back to the Round, and meet him again at dusk" when ll_walking(hob) and not ll_roundDone(hob) and not ll_ended(hob) {
    Says "'Tomorrow, then,' says Hob. 'If there is one,' and he takes his pole and goes up the Row with the sound of a man counting.".
    On discuss { Retract ll_walking(hob). Retract following(hob, actor). }
  }
  Topic ll_t_pilots_early with hob "Ask Hob whether the lamps ever do anything odd" when not ll_trusts(hob) and not ll_ended(hob) once {
    Says "'Lamps do what lamps do,' says Hob, too quickly. 'They hiss, they gutter, they go out in a wind. Ask me something about the poles.'".
  }
  Topic ll_t_pilots with hob "Ask Hob what it is he hasn't said about the pilot-flames" when ll_trusts(hob) and not ll_told(hob) {
    Says "Hob is quiet so long that you think he has not heard. 'Nobody asked,' he says. 'Forty-one years, nobody asked. They go out. All of them. The Gasworks pilots and the street pilots and the pilot in the bakehouse oven at the foot of the Brickfields, I'm told, in the one breath, and they come back in the next. Not a wind. A wind comes from somewhere. This comes from everywhere. Since the spring, twice a week; since the Ordinance's second reading, every night at the same minute.' He turns his white eyes to the Row. 'I've got it written down in the Hall: the nights. After the lamps are all lit, stand in the Quarter and wait for it. I'd as soon not be told what it is.'".
    On discuss { Assert ll_told(hob). }
  }
  Topic ll_t_after with hob "Tell Hob what you saw the lamps do" when knows(party, d_pilots_step) and ll_told(hob) and not ll_moved(hob) {
    Says "'There,' says Hob. 'I thought I'd imagined it. A man's eyes go and then he doesn't trust what's left.' He is not weeping, because he doesn't, but he finds his sleeve. 'It was something,' he says. 'Wasn't it. I wasn't lighting nothing, all those years.'".
    On discuss { Assert ll_moved(hob). }
  }
  Topic ll_t_witness with hob "Ask Hob whether he would say what he knows to the Five, in the Hall" when ll_moved(hob) and not witness(hob) {
    Says "'To the Five,' says Hob. 'With my eyes.' He considers it. 'I can say what I heard. I can say it in forty-one years of dusks. They can look at me and decide what that's worth.'".
    On discuss { Assert witness(hob). }
  }

  // ── What Hob says afterwards (the world remembers how he was retired) ───────────────────────────────────
  Topic ll_a_pension with hob "Ask Hob how he does" when ll_howPension(hob) {
    Says "'The time,' says Hob. 'What's the time?' You tell him. 'Ah,' he says, and nods, as if the answer had been a favour done him, and he does not ask again for a quarter of an hour.".
  }
  Topic ll_a_place with hob "Ask Hob how he does in the chair" when ll_howPlace(hob) {
    Says "'It's a good chair,' says Hob. 'The window does what a window can.' He passes a thumb along the brass of the pole. 'Keeper of the Tinder-boxes. Not one of them has been struck since Michaelmas.'".
  }
  Topic ll_a_finish with hob "Ask Hob how the wrist is" when ll_howFinish(hob) {
    Says "'It aches, as it ought,' says Hob. 'It was fifty steps, I was told, and I'd have said forty-nine. You get a thing wrong after forty-one years, you ought to know which thing.' He seems very pleased with himself.".
  }
  Topic ll_a_plain with hob "Ask Hob how it is to be told" when ll_howPlain(hob) {
    Says "'Cold,' says Hob. 'And I would not have had it any other way. Do you know I had been told for a year by people who meant well that I was only tired?'".
  }
  Topic ll_a_hearth with hob "Ask Hob how the hearth draws" when ll_howHearth(hob) {
    Says "'Like a good dog,' says Hob. 'Don't ask me what I do with it. I put on coke at six and I take off the ash at six. The Warden says it is a post. I say it is a lamp, with the pole shorter.'".
  }
  Topic ll_a_fell with hob "Ask Hob how he comes to be here" when ll_howFell(hob) {
    Says "'I fell off the Steps,' says Hob, 'and the lamp was lit, so I'll not be apologising to anybody.' He turns his white eyes to the door. 'Next time, I'd want somebody to tell me where the fiftieth step was. That is all a man wants.'".
  }
  Topic ll_a_drift with hob "Ask Hob what became of the Round" when ll_howDrift(hob) {
    Says "'The Company turned them off at the main on Friday,' says Hob, 'and I was told afterward, by a boy.' He thinks about it. 'It was a decent Round.'".
  }

  // ── The Warden, the foreman, the offers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic ll_t_hall with quoyle "Ask Warden Quoyle what the Hall will do for Hob when the Round ends" when knows(party, ll_hob_met) and not ll_placeOffer(hob) once {
    Says "'We will give him a chair,' says Warden Quoyle. 'By the window. A title: Keeper of the Tinder-boxes. He will be asked to show new men how to hold a pole, and there will be no new men, because there will be no poles.' She polishes. 'He will hate it. I would, in his place. I should add that I am very sorry.'".
    On discuss { Assert ll_placeOffer(hob). }
  }
  Topic ll_t_hearth with quoyle "Ask the Warden whether the Hall could keep its old hearth for the Night" when knows(party, ll_hob_met) and not ll_flueClear(hob) {
    Says "'There is a hearth,' says Warden Quoyle. 'The Hall's, the Founders' own, in the corner behind the ladders. Not lit since the Ordinance. Bricked at the chimney-throat by the Company, which put a stopper in it as a courtesy. A hearth cannot be kept lit that cannot draw. I would not stop anyone sweeping it. I would not help them, either; the Gasworks inspector counts chimneys.'".
  }
  Topic ll_t_hearth2 with quoyle "Tell the Warden the flue is clear, and Hob would keep the hearth" when ll_flueClear(hob) and ll_moved(hob) and not keeper(glass) {
    Says "Warden Quoyle puts down the tinder-box. 'Then it is not charity,' she says. 'It is a post. A Keeper of the Hearth is in the Hall's founding rules, line three, and no one has held it in sixty years.' She writes his name in the book by the door, which, you learn, is for signing after all.".
    On discuss { Assert ll_hearthWarden(hob). }
  }
  Relation ll_hearthWarden(group).
  Topic ll_t_pension with gudgeon "Ask Foreman Gudgeon whether the Company pays a lamplighter anything when he is turned off" when knows(party, ll_hob_met) and not ll_pensionOffer(hob) once {
    Says "'The Benevolent,' says Gudgeon. 'Six coin a quarter, to a man with forty years in the Company's books, on his own signature. Tansy's name is in them. I've sent the form to the Hall twice.' He looks at his pencil. 'He tore the second. He's a man who would rather be hungry in his own way.'".
    On discuss { Assert ll_pensionOffer(hob). }
  }

  // ── The four lamps ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind ll_mantle "a gas mantle" is gear worth 2 weighing 0 described "A little white bag of knitted ash, knotted at the neck, that glows when you put a flame to it and crumbles when you look at it hard.".
  Relation ll_lamp(thing).
  Thing ll_lamp_t "the Tinkers' Court lamp" at round_tinkers {
    State dead "The lamp on its bracket has no mantle; the ring where it should sit is a burnt ring, and the glass is clouded with soot.".
    State fitted "The lamp on its bracket has a new mantle, white as a clean glove, and is ready for the taper.".
    State lit "The lamp burns steady and white; the court looks, for the first time in a year, like a place where tinkers might have lived.".
    State breath "The lamp stands cold; its mantle still glows from within, with no flame to account for it.".
    Change fit "Knot a new mantle on the Tinkers' Court lamp" from dead to fitted consuming ll_mantle at round_tinkers.
  }
  Thing ll_lamp_s "the Stokers' Steps lamp" at round_steps {
    State quarrel "A lamp-arm juts from the middle of the stair wall, on a swivel, and it points at neither house. Two people are sure which it is for.".
    State ready "The lamp-arm is fixed and trimmed, its glass wiped, ready for the taper.".
    State lit "The lamp on the Steps burns steady, and shows every one of the fifty steps.".
    State breath "The lamp on the Steps stands cold; the mantle glows by itself.".
  }
  Thing ll_lamp_g "the Glaziers' Passage lamp" at round_glaziers {
    State out "The lamp on the corner is out. It has been out so long that the pigeons have given up on its ledge.".
    State ready "The lamp on the corner has a flame in its mantle, small and still, that was not lit by any taper, and it is waiting for the others.".
    State lit "The corner lamp burns clear; the passage is a long street of stacked windows, each with a lamp in it.".
    State breath "The lamp stands cold, and every pane in the passage has a light in it which is not a reflection.".
  }
  Thing ll_lamp_f "the Furnace Wharf lamp" at round_furnace {
    State occupied "An iron lamp-house stands at the head of the wharf, the size of a sentry-box, with a ladder bolted to it and a glazed lantern on top. There is a boot-toe under its door.".
    State ready "The Wharf's lamp-house stands empty and open, its lantern trimmed.".
    State lit "The Furnace Wharf lamp is lit; on the bricks below it the gulls have turned, all together, to face it.".
    State breath "The lamp-house stands cold. On the wall the gulls have all stood up.".
  }
  Initially Assert ll_lamp(ll_lamp_t). Initially Assert ll_lamp(ll_lamp_s). Initially Assert ll_lamp(ll_lamp_g). Initially Assert ll_lamp(ll_lamp_f).
  // The lamps are put out at dawn, as Hob always did.
  Rule ll_dawn when hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 17 and ll_lamp(?l) and state(?l, lit) { Assert state(?l, ready). Decrease ll_lit(hob) by 1 or to nothing. }
  Rule ll_late when not ll_dusk() and ll_lit(hob) < 4 and ll_walking(hob) and not ll_roundDone(hob) and not ll_ended(hob) says "The dusk is gone and the lamps that are lit will stand till morning. 'Tomorrow, then,' says Hob, and takes his pole back from you, and goes up the Row toward the Hall by the wall." { Retract ll_walking(hob). Retract following(hob, party). Assert at(hob, lamplighters_hall). }

  // Tinkers' Court: the mantle, bought from Mrs Oddy, or got from the Hall's locker, which is locked.
  Thing ll_locker "the lamplighters' locker" at lamplighters_hall {
    Holds.
    State locked closed "A tall locker of black tin, labelled in gold LAMPLIGHTERS' STORES, is locked.".
    State open "The locker stands open; the shelves are empty but for dust and a single tin.".
    Change pick "Pick the stores locker's lock" from locked to open needing lockwork.
  }
  Item ll_spare "a spare mantle" is ll_mantle in ll_locker.
  Observe ll_mantle_hint at round_tinkers when state(ll_lamp_t, dead) and not holding(party, ll_mantle) "From the shuttered shop-front opposite, a hand shakes out a tray of white bags like gloves and draws them in again.".

  // The Stokers' Steps: whose is the lamp?
  Topic ll_t_strood with strood "Ask Mrs Strood what the quarrel is" when state(ll_lamp_s, quarrel) once {
    Says "'My Joe went down these steps at six in the morning in the dark,' says Mrs Strood, 'because the lamp was swung to light that man's window, and he is on the cemetery side of Foundry Row now, and I have to climb them every day to look at him. Fifty steps. Turn it to the Steps. A lamp is for the street.'".
  }
  Topic ll_t_beadle with beadle "Ask Mr Beadle what the quarrel is" when state(ll_lamp_s, quarrel) once {
    Says "'I have had my window broken twice in a year,' says Mr Beadle, 'and the second time the thief stood under the lamp that she has turned to the Steps and was not seen, and I have eleven unredeemed fiddles in there that I am answerable for. A lamp is for the property. And I would add, madam, that I sympathise.'".
  }
  Action ll_swing_steps(actor: group, site: place) "Swing the Steps lamp to light the stair, for Mrs Strood" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ll_lamp_s, site) and state(ll_lamp_s, quarrel).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert state(ll_lamp_s, ready). Assert ll_sideSteps(hob). }
    Result "You set the lamp-arm square to the stair. Mrs Strood unfolds her arms, one at a time. Mr Beadle takes out a pocket-book and writes in it, which is how he cries.".
  }
  Action ll_swing_shop(actor: group, site: place) "Swing the Steps lamp to light the pawnbroker's window, for Mr Beadle" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ll_lamp_s, site) and state(ll_lamp_s, quarrel).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert state(ll_lamp_s, ready). Assert ll_sideShop(hob). }
    Result "You set the lamp-arm to the shop window. Mr Beadle shakes your hand with both of his. At the top of the stair Mrs Strood turns and goes in, and her door is not slammed, which is worse.".
  }
  Action ll_second(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the Company for a second bracket on the Steps (5 coin), so both may have a lamp" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ll_lamp_s, site) and state(ll_lamp_s, quarrel) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 5.
    Time 20 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Assert state(ll_lamp_s, ready). Assert ll_sideBoth(hob). Increase regard(gasco) by 1. }
    Result "Foreman Gudgeon's man comes down with a bracket under his arm and a receipt. The lamp-rate for a second arm is paid in advance to the Gas Company, which is delighted. The quarrel does not stop; it relocates, and is about whose bracket is the second.".
  }
  Action ll_share(actor: group, site: place) "Talk both of them into sharing the lamp-rate and the arm, turn and turn about" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ll_lamp_s, site) and state(ll_lamp_s, quarrel) and not ll_shareTried(hob).
    Time 20 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert state(ll_lamp_s, ready). Assert ll_sideBoth(hob). Assert ll_shareTried(hob). }
    On failure { Assert ll_shareTried(hob). }
    Result "You put it to them as a pair of creditors: the lamp is owed one night to the stair and the next to the window, and the Company is owed the rate between them. Mr Beadle says 'Mondays.' Mrs Strood says 'Mondays is mine.' It takes the better part of the hour, and at the end of it they are speaking to each other in the tone of people who will be disappointed in each other for decades.".
    Otherwise "They agree on one thing: that you are a stranger, and that it is none of your business. It is a sound agreement and they leave it there.".
  }
  Relation ll_shareTried(group).

  // The Glaziers' Passage: the shed, and what is in it.
  Thing ll_shed "the glaziers' shed" at round_glaziers {
    State glowing "A tarred shed with a ventilator in its roof. Through the ventilator comes the light of a flame the size of a thumbnail, standing on a bench between stacks of window-glass, with nothing under it.".
    State given "The shed is dim; a flame the size of a thumbnail stands on its bench, as before, and leans a very little toward the lamp on the corner.".
  }
  Observe ll_glow at round_glaziers when state(ll_shed, glowing) "A glow of some sort shows inside one of the sheds. It does not flicker." teaches ll_glow_seen.
  Action ll_taper(actor: group, site: place) "Hold Hob's taper to the flame in the glaziers' shed, and carry what it gives to the corner lamp" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ll_lamp_g, site) and state(ll_lamp_g, out) and state(ll_shed, glowing) and (ll_walking(hob) or ll_handed(hob)).
    Time 15 minutes.
    On success { Assert state(ll_lamp_g, ready). Assert state(ll_shed, given). Assert ll_shedTaper(hob). }
    Result "You hold the taper to the flame, and the flame, which has stood on its bench for five months, leans into it like a cat. It does not burn the wick. It takes the taper as one takes a hand. You carry the little light across the passage in your cupped palm, and the corner lamp's mantle, which was not touched by any other, takes it without a sound. Master Hune stops chewing.".
  }
  Action ll_glaze_tinder(actor: group, site: place) "Light the corner lamp from the tinder-box, and leave the shed alone" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ll_lamp_g, site) and state(ll_lamp_g, out) and (ll_walking(hob) or ll_handed(hob)).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert ll_tinderTried(hob). }
    Result "You strike the tinder-box and hold the flame to the mantle. It takes, glows, and goes out, three times, and the third time the glow in the shed brightens for a moment, as if looking up. The lamp does not light.".
  }
  Relation ll_tinderTried(group).

  // The Furnace Wharf: the child in the lamp.
  Observe ll_nan_sign at round_furnace when state(ll_lamp_f, occupied) and not knows(party, ll_nan_hid) "From the lamp-house comes the sound of someone breathing very carefully, and then of someone not breathing at all." teaches ll_nan_hid.
  Topic ll_t_nan with nan "Ask Nan why she is in the lamp" when state(ll_lamp_f, occupied) once {
    Says "'Mr Tansy said it's the last one,' says Nan. 'He told my father. If I'm in it he can't, and then it isn't. It's not a rule. It's just what happens.' She is silent for a moment. 'He taught me to hold the pole.'".
  }
  Action ll_coax(actor: group, site: place) "Coax Nan down with a story about a lamp that was not lit" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ll_lamp_f, site) and state(ll_lamp_f, occupied) and knows(actor, ll_nan_hid) and not ll_coaxTried(hob).
    Time 20 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state(ll_lamp_f, ready). Assert ll_childOut(hob). }
    On failure { Assert ll_coaxTried(hob). }
    Result "You tell her about a lamp that was never lit and a lamplighter who walked past it for forty years because he knew exactly what it was thinking. Nan comes down the ladder at the part about the cat, and sits on the bottom rung with her boots in her hands, and is not at all sorry.".
    Otherwise "Nan listens to the whole of it from the dark, and says, kindly, that she has heard better ones, and that they were all about lamps that were lit.".
  }
  Action ll_climb(actor: group, site: place) "Climb the ladder and lift Nan out of the lamp-house" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ll_lamp_f, site) and state(ll_lamp_f, occupied) and knows(actor, ll_nan_hid) and not ll_climbTried(hob).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, climbing, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state(ll_lamp_f, ready). Assert ll_childOut(hob). }
    On failure { Assert ll_climbTried(hob). }
    Result "The ladder is wet and the lantern-top is round, but you have her by the back of the coat before she has finished deciding. She says nothing at all all the way down, with great dignity, and then, 'You could have asked.'".
    Otherwise "A rung goes. You hang for a moment by one arm over the Furnace Wharf, and Nan, from inside, says 'Mind the gulls,' and that is all the help she gives.".
  }
  Action ll_wait(actor: group, site: place) "Sit by the lamp-house door with Nan until she is ready to come out" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ll_lamp_f, site) and state(ll_lamp_f, occupied) and knows(actor, ll_nan_hid).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert state(ll_lamp_f, ready). Assert ll_childOut(hob). }
    Result "You sit with your back to the iron and say nothing for an hour, which is a kind of rudeness she respects. At some point the gulls go quiet. At some point a boot-toe comes out from under the door, and then a boot, and Nan sits down beside you without a word and falls asleep on your arm.".
  }
  Action ll_hob_speaks(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Hob to tell Nan, himself, that it is over" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hob, site) and at(ll_lamp_f, site) and state(ll_lamp_f, occupied) and knows(actor, ll_nan_hid) and ll_walking(hob) and ll_trusts(hob).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert state(ll_lamp_f, ready). Assert ll_childOut(hob). Assert ll_moved(hob). }
    Result "Hob puts his face against the iron, where she is, and tells her in his flat voice that it is over, and that it is over whether she is in it or not, and that a lamplighter who has been prevented from lighting a lamp by a child has been paid the highest wage there is. A bolt slides. Nan comes out and takes the pole from him, and holds it, and he lets her.".
  }
  Relation ll_childOut(group). Relation ll_coaxTried(group). Relation ll_climbTried(group).

  // ── The lighting ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule ll_trust when ll_lit(hob) >= 2 and not ll_trusts(hob) { Assert ll_trusts(hob). }
  Action ll_light(actor: group, site: place, lamp: thing) "Light {lamp} with Hob's taper" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(lamp, site) and ll_lamp(lamp) and state(lamp, ready)
      and ll_dusk() and (ll_walking(hob) or ll_handed(hob)).
    Time 3 minutes.
    On success { Assert state(lamp, lit). Increase ll_lit(hob) by 1. }
    Result "The mantle takes, flares white, and settles. Hob, at your elbow, turns his face to it, and says 'There,' as one says it to a horse.".
  }
  Rule ll_tinkers_ready when state(ll_lamp_t, fitted) { Assert state(ll_lamp_t, ready). }
  Rule ll_round_done when ll_lit(hob) >= 4 and not ll_roundDone(hob) says "Behind you, at the end of the Row, the fourth lamp of the Round comes up white. Hob stops. 'That's the four,' he says. 'Stay where you are, if you want to see something.'" { Assert ll_roundDone(hob). Assert ll_breathing(hob). Set ll_breathAt(hob) to watch(clock) + 2. }

  // The Pilots' Breath: the watched event. Everything lit goes out together, and comes back together.
  Rule ll_breath_out when ll_breathing(hob) and not ll_breathed(hob) and watch(clock) >= ll_breathAt(hob) and within(party, glass)
    says "Every lamp in the Quarter goes out in the same instant. Not the flames; the glow in the mantles stays. The gulls on the Furnace Wharf stand up. In the Gasworks yard the gasometer, which was rising, stops. Nobody speaks. The pigeons come down off the roofs of the Row and walk about, which they never do at dusk."
    { Assert ll_breathed(hob). Set ll_breathAt(hob) to watch(clock) + 1. Assert state(ll_lamp_t, breath). Assert state(ll_lamp_s, breath). Assert state(ll_lamp_g, breath). Assert state(ll_lamp_f, breath). }
  Rule ll_breath_in when ll_breathed(hob) and ll_breathing(hob) and watch(clock) >= ll_breathAt(hob) and within(party, glass)
    says "And all of them are lit again, together, as if nothing had happened. The gulls sit down. The gasometer, which has been waiting, rises. Hob, beside you, lets out a long breath that he seems to have held for forty years."
    teaches d_pilots_step
    { Retract ll_breathing(hob). Assert state(ll_lamp_t, lit). Assert state(ll_lamp_s, lit). Assert state(ll_lamp_g, lit). Assert state(ll_lamp_f, lit). }

  // ── How the old man is retired ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Action ll_r_pension(actor: group, site: place) "Put the Gas Company's pension papers into Hob's hands" {
    Speaker hob.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hob, site) and ll_pensionOffer(hob) and not ll_ended(hob) and (ll_roundDone(hob) or ll_lastNight()).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert ll_ended(hob). Assert ll_howPension(hob). Retract following(hob, actor). Retract ll_walking(hob). Assert ll_bitter(hob). Increase regard(gasco) by 1. }
    Result "Hob feels the paper, with his thumbs, as a man reads a coin. 'The Benevolent,' he says. 'Six coin a quarter. For being turned off.' He folds it small. 'I'll keep it,' he says, 'as a thing that was offered,' and puts it in the tinder-box where the spare tapers go. The Company will pay him until he dies. He does not speak to you again except to ask the time.".
  }
  Action ll_r_place(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Warden to give Hob the chair by the Hall window and the title" {
    Speaker quoyle.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(quoyle, site) and ll_placeOffer(hob) and not ll_ended(hob) and (ll_roundDone(hob) or ll_lastNight()).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert ll_ended(hob). Assert ll_howPlace(hob). Retract following(hob, actor). Retract ll_walking(hob). Assert ll_bitter(hob). }
    Result "Hob is shown to the chair by the window and sits in it, because he has been taught to, with the pole across his knees like a man on a bench at a station. Warden Quoyle reads out the title. 'Keeper of the Tinder-boxes,' says Hob, to the dark where the window is. 'That's a good title.' He does not say the rest of it, and neither does anyone.".
  }
  Action ll_r_finish(actor: group, site: place) "Give Hob the taper, step back, and let him finish the Round himself" {
    Speaker hob.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hob, site) and ll_walking(hob) and not ll_roundDone(hob) and not ll_ended(hob) and ll_dusk() and ll_lit(hob) >= 1.
    Time 60 minutes.
    Grave "Hob will try the lamps that are left alone, by touch, in the dusk. He is not likely to find the Steps.".
    On success { Assert ll_ended(hob). Assert ll_howFinish(hob). Assert ll_hurt(hob). Assert ll_moved(hob). Retract ll_walking(hob). Retract following(hob, actor). Assert at(hob, lamplighters_hall). }
    Result "You stand back at the foot of the Steps and say nothing. Hob goes up them one at a time, his hand on the wall and the pole in the other, naming each step as he comes to it; he lights the lamp by smell, and lights it right. On the fortieth he puts his foot where the fiftieth should be. The sound he makes is not a cry. You carry him to the Hall between you, and he does not say thank you, and he does not ask you to put him down. 'That was the Round,' he says on the way. 'That was it, wasn't it? All of it.' He has broken his wrist, and finished.".
  }
  Action ll_r_plain(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Hob plainly that it is his eyes that have retired him, and give him the choice of the Round" {
    Speaker hob.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hob, site) and not ll_ended(hob) and not ll_handed(hob) and knows(actor, ll_hob_met).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Grave "Told plainly, it cannot be untold; the Warden, who does not like the word, will hear that it was you.".
    On success { Assert ll_handed(hob). Assert ll_howPlain(hob). Assert ll_hallClosed(hob). Assert ll_told(hob). Assert ll_trusts(hob). Retract ll_walking(hob). Retract following(hob, actor). Assert ll_slighted_gasco(party). }
    Result "'Your eyes have retired you, Mr Tansy,' you say, 'and not the Company. You can't see the mantle.' There is a long silence. 'No,' says Hob. 'I can't.' He puts the tinder-box in your hand and closes your fingers on it, one at a time. 'Then you'll do it,' he says, 'and I'll stand where I'm told. I would sooner be told that than carried.' He tells you, then, more than he meant to. At the Hall the Warden hears of it before you have got your boots off, and does not say a word, and puts the book away.".
  }
  Action ll_r_hearth(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Hob to light the Hall's old hearth, with the Warden watching, and keep it" {
    Speaker hob.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hob, site) and at(quoyle, site) and ll_flueClear(hob) and ll_moved(hob) and ll_hearthWarden(hob) and ll_roundDone(hob) and not ll_ended(hob) and not ll_hallClosed(hob).
    Time 20 minutes.
    On success { Assert ll_ended(hob). Assert ll_howHearth(hob). Retract following(hob, actor). Retract ll_walking(hob). Assert keeper(glass). Assert witness(hob). }
    Result "Hob kneels at the old grate with the tinder-box, and strikes it once, and it lights; he has lit nothing so well. The flue draws with a low steady note, and the Hall's old brickwork, which has not been warm in sixty years, begins to tick. Warden Quoyle stands with her hands behind her. 'Keeper,' she says, and her voice goes in the middle. 'Of the Hearth of the Lamplighters. For the Night, and for any other.' Hob lays the pole across the fender. 'I never could keep a thing alight,' he says, 'that wasn't on a pole.' He is lying; he does not stop kneeling.".
  }
  Action ll_sweep(actor: group, site: place) "Sweep the Lamplighters' Hall's old flue and unbrick the throat" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ll_locker, site) and not ll_flueClear(hob).
    Time 36.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert ll_flueClear(hob). }
    Result "You take down a century of soot, and forty years of ladders, and a Gas Company stopper stamped OUR COMFORT IS GUARANTEED, which you leave on the mantel. The hearth behind the ladders is a plain brick one with an iron fender. It draws. The sooty light that comes down the flue is, you notice, the first daylight to have reached that grate since the Ordinance.".
    Otherwise "The brick is the Company's, and the Company is thorough. You get an hour of soot and one stopper out and no further.".
  }
  Rule ll_broken when ll_lastNight() and ll_everWalked(hob) and not ll_roundDone(hob) and not ll_ended(hob) says "The night is gone and the Round is not done. At the Gasworks the lamp-rate is a day in arrears, and Foreman Gudgeon has a list of what is dark." {
    Decrease regard(gasco) by 1 or to nothing. Assert ll_slighted_gasco(party).
  }
  Rule ll_fell when ll_lastNight() and not ll_roundDone(hob) and not ll_ended(hob) says "In the Stokers' Steps, in the dark, an old man misses the fiftieth step. By the morning it is all over the Foundry: Hob Tansy lit his last lamp, and fell off the world with the pole in his hand. He is in the Hall with his wrist in a splint and nobody who was with him." {
    Assert ll_ended(hob). Assert ll_howFell(hob). Assert ll_hurt(hob). Assert at(hob, lamplighters_hall). Retract following(hob, party). Retract ll_walking(hob).
  }
  Rule ll_drift when ll_lastNight() and ll_roundDone(hob) and not ll_ended(hob) says "The Gas Company's notice runs out at the hour, with nobody to receive it. Hob Tansy hangs up the pole in the Hall, himself, and sits where the Warden puts him." { Assert ll_ended(hob). Assert ll_howDrift(hob). Assert ll_bitter(hob). Assert at(hob, lamplighters_hall). Retract following(hob, party). Retract ll_walking(hob). }
  Relation ll_howDrift(group).

  // ── What the Round leaves behind ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe ll_hall_bitter at lamplighters_hall when ll_bitter(hob) "Hob Tansy sits in the chair by the window, with his white eyes toward it, and does not move his head when you come in.".
  Observe ll_hall_hurt at lamplighters_hall when ll_hurt(hob) and not ll_bitter(hob) "Hob Tansy sits in the chair by the window, his arm splinted across his chest, with the brass pole upright against his shoulder, and a look on his face like a man who has stopped being afraid of something.".
  Observe ll_hall_hearth at lamplighters_hall when keeper(glass) "A hearth burns in the corner behind the ladders, and an old man sits by it with his hands out, his face turned a little to the heat.".
  Observe ll_hall_cold at lamplighters_hall when ll_hallClosed(hob) "Warden Quoyle has taken the book from beside the door, and put a small card there: THE HALL IS NOT OPEN TO VISITORS TONIGHT.".
  Observe ll_steps_after at round_steps when ll_sideSteps(hob) "A woman is sitting on the top step with her shawl off, in the light of the lamp, shelling peas.".
  Observe ll_steps_after2 at round_steps when ll_sideShop(hob) "The lamp lights the pawnbroker's window, and a row of fiddles hangs in it like hanged men.".
  Observe ll_steps_after3 at round_steps when ll_sideBoth(hob) "Two lamps on the Steps; two people on the Steps, not speaking, each in a separate light.".
  Observe ll_nan_after at round_furnace when ll_childOut(hob) "A very small girl sits on the bottom rung of the lamp-house ladder, being a child who is not in it.".
}

data/adventures/quittance/q_markstreet.k:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "Mark Street: a house on fire wearing the wrong Office's plate, two brigades arguing the mark, and a family in the road.".

  // ══ The fire, and what the house is worth while it burns ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // At ten on the first morning (watch 12) a chimney goes in Number Nine. The house is worth twelve watches of the
  // dispute; it falls by one a watch, and by about noon (watch 24) there is nothing to argue about. Whatever closes
  // the dispute sets the verdict (ms_v_*) and the house goes to "closing"; the rules below read what is left and
  // turn it into a house saved, half saved, a shell, or a heap.
  Entity ms_nine: group "Number Nine, Mark Street".
  Measure ms_worth(group). Measure ms_tier(group). Measure ms_pulled_at(group).
  Relation ms_v_buckets(group). Relation ms_v_phoenix(group). Relation ms_v_lamprey(group). Relation ms_v_third(group).
  Relation ms_v_salvors(group). Relation ms_v_none(group). Relation ms_ended(group). Relation ms_dispersed(group).
  Relation ms_contents(group). Relation ms_paid(group). Relation ms_book_taken(group).
  // What the company did, said by name for the Hearing and the Slate to read.
  Relation ms_rule(group). Relation ms_precedent_mark(group). Relation ms_slighted_lamprey(group).
  Relation ms_slighted_phoenix(group). Relation ms_slighted_brigades(group). Relation ms_swapped(group).
  Relation ms_garrity_shamed(group). Relation ms_caught(group). Relation ms_g_insulted(group). Relation ms_burned(group).
  Relation ms_asked(group). Relation ms_unpaid(group).

  Discovery ms_claim "The Slate has a claim chalked on it: a house on Mark Street, a mark disputed, a family in the road.".
  Discovery ms_alarm "A house is burning on Mark Street, and the two brigades are not putting it out.".
  Discovery ms_lamprey_cover "The Peascods' house wears the Phoenix's bird, but their cover is with the Lamprey, and the proof is in a book in their front room.".
  Discovery ms_nailed_wrong "A surveyor nailed the wrong plate on Number Nine, on the word of a bag he had mixed up in the dark.".
  Discovery ms_proof "You have read the Peascods' policy-book: the Lamprey & River Office, in ink, for the house at Number Nine.".

  Query ms_over() means not state(ms_house, ms_whole) and not state(ms_house, ms_alight) and not state(ms_house, ms_closing).
  Query ms_open() means state(ms_house, ms_whole) or state(ms_house, ms_alight).

  // ── Places: the house itself ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place ms_nine_b "Number Nine, Mark Street" is building within brick.
  Place ms_front "the front room of Number Nine" is room within ms_nine_b at 0, 0.
  Place ms_kitchen "the kitchen of Number Nine" is room within ms_nine_b at 0, 1.
  Passage ms_front_door "the front door of Number Nine" is door between mark_street and ms_front.
  Passage ms_kitchen_door "the kitchen door of Number Nine" is door between nine_yard and ms_kitchen.
  Passage ms_hall "the passage through the house" is passage between ms_kitchen and ms_front.

  Hazard ms_flame "the heat in the front doorway" means "Deal (1d6) fire damage to ally unless dexterity save against (12).".

  Thing ms_house "Number Nine" at mark_street {
    State ms_whole "Number Nine is a house like its neighbours, with a bird over the door where the others have a fish.".
    State ms_alight "Number Nine is burning at the back. Smoke the colour of a wet slate comes out of the kitchen chimney and the first-floor windows, and a long unlit hose lies across the cobbles from each side to the middle and stops, as if both had been told to.".
    State ms_closing "Number Nine is being seen to.".
    State ms_saved "Number Nine stands, black over the door and wet to the first floor, with its windows out and its roof on.".
    State ms_half "Number Nine stands in front and not behind: the front wall and the first-floor rooms are whole, and where the kitchen and the yard side were there is a wet black gap with the sky in it.".
    State ms_shell "Number Nine is a front wall with a house's idea behind it. The door still opens, onto daylight.".
    State ms_gutted "Where Number Nine stood there is a front wall without a door, and a warm heap, and a smell. The terrace has a tooth out.".
  }
  Thing ms_plate "the plate over Number Nine's door" at mark_street {
    State ms_bird "Over Number Nine's door a gilt bird is nailed, level with its neighbours' fish, and a good deal newer.".
    State ms_bare "Over Number Nine's door a pale square marks where a plate was, with two nail-holes and a drip of rust.".
    State ms_fish "Over Number Nine's door a black fish is nailed a little crooked, with the paint of a different door still on its tail.".
  }
  Thing ms_door "the front door of Number Nine" on ms_front_door {
    State ms_shutdoor "The front door of Number Nine is shut.".
    State ms_ablaze dangerous "The front door of Number Nine is open on a wall of heat and the front room beyond it is orange.".
    State ms_charred "The front door of Number Nine stands open on a black passage, still ticking.".
    Hurts with ms_flame when ms_ablaze then ms_charred.
  }
  Thing ms_kdoor "the kitchen door of Number Nine" on ms_kitchen_door {
    State ms_kshut "The kitchen door of Number Nine is shut, with a boot-scraper beside it.".
    State ms_jammed blocking "The kitchen door of Number Nine is swollen in its frame with the heat, and a thread of smoke is coming round the edge of it.".
    State ms_unjammed "The kitchen door of Number Nine hangs open.".
    Change ms_shoulder "Put your shoulder to the kitchen door until it gives" from ms_jammed to ms_unjammed needing brawn.
    Change ms_slip_bolt "Slip the swollen kitchen door's bolt with a wire" from ms_jammed to ms_unjammed needing lockwork.
  }

  Initially Assert state(ms_house, ms_whole). Initially Assert state(ms_plate, ms_bird). Initially Assert state(ms_door, ms_shutdoor).
  Initially Assert state(ms_kdoor, ms_kshut).

  Kind ms_book_kind "the Peascods' policy-book" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "A black oilcloth book, tied round with tape: Lamprey & River Office, Domestic and Household, Policy No. 4,117, the insured premises being No. 9, Mark Street, in the name of Aubrey Peascod, clerk. It smells of smoke and lavender.".
  Item ms_book "the Peascods' policy-book" is ms_book_kind at nowhere.

  Observe ms_front_scene at ms_front when state(ms_house, ms_whole) "A front room kept for company: a good clock, a horsehair sofa, and a bureau with a brass lock and a bird on the lid, which is the Peascods' idea of a joke on the Phoenix.".
  Observe ms_front_burning at ms_front when state(ms_house, ms_alight) "The front room is full of orange air. The sofa is smoking at one end. The bureau stands against the far wall with its brass lock too hot to look at, and the drawer under the lid is a tin-lined drawer, which has so far kept its counsel.".
  Observe ms_front_after at ms_front when ms_over() "What the fire left of the front room is a bureau with a tin-lined drawer, black outside, and a sofa's iron ghost.".
  Observe ms_kitchen_scene at ms_kitchen when state(ms_house, ms_whole) "A kitchen with a range, a table scrubbed white, and a canary, who has opinions.".
  Observe ms_kitchen_burning at ms_kitchen when state(ms_house, ms_alight) "The kitchen ceiling is alight along one beam and dropping sparks onto a scrubbed table. The range is roaring. The canary's cage is gone from its hook.".
  Observe ms_kitchen_after at ms_kitchen when ms_over() "A wet black kitchen, with the range standing in it like a bull in a ruin.".

  // ── The people in the street ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person ms_mrs "Ada Peascod" at ms_kitchen {
    Role "Aubrey Peascod's wife". Ancestry human. Calling bard. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A woman in an apron is wiping a table that is already clean. 'You'll be from the Offices,' says Ada Peascod. 'Everyone is. My husband is on the Wharf and has not been told, and I have been meaning to put the kettle on since seven.'".
    Greets again "'Oh,' says Ada Peascod, putting down the cloth. 'It's you.'".
  }
  Person ms_kids "the Peascod children" at ms_kitchen {
    Role "three children, one with a cat". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Numbers 3. Manner cheerful. Pronouns they.
    Greets "Three children are at the scrubbed table with a slate between them, doing sums on it. The smallest has a cat in her lap who is doing none. 'We're insured,' says the eldest, not looking up. 'It's on the door.'".
    Greets again "'The cat's called Premium,' says the smallest.".
  }
  Person ms_mate "Mate Marchbanks" at lamprey_floor {
    Role "mate of the Lamprey & River brigade, under Captain Dree". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Trait toughness. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A heavy man in an oilskin, with a black fish on his helmet and an expression of long unforced patience, is checking a coil of hose against a list. 'Marchbanks,' he says. 'Mate. The Captain's compliments, and he is at the Reach, and he says it is none of ours until the policy says it is, and the policy says it is, and I am not to mention it.'".
    Greets again "'It's the adjusters,' says Mate Marchbanks, to the hose.".
  }
  Person ms_tapley "Mr Tapley" at hen_taproom {
    Role "surveyor of the Guild, lately of the Brickfields marks". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner grim. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A man in a good coat that has been slept in has his head on the bar and a hammer by his elbow. 'The light,' says Mr Tapley, without lifting it, 'was very poor. Do not ask me about the light.'".
    Greets again "'I have a very clear memory of it,' says Mr Tapley. 'Of the nail.'".
  }
  Person ms_quennell "Master Voakes" at salvor_yard {
    Role "master of the Salvors' Yard". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 3. Peaceable. Manner jovial. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A man with a barrel chest and a boathook is directing six others in the loading of a handcart with hooks, ropes and a very large sack. 'Voakes,' he says. 'Salvage. If it is wet, burning or lost, we are already on our way to it.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Master Voakes. 'Mind the cart.'".
  }

  // ── The clock ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Event ms_ignite when watch(clock) >= 12 and state(ms_house, ms_whole) "Somewhere to the west the Phoenix bell begins, and then, a little late and a little out of time, a deeper note that is the Lamprey's. Over the roofs of the Brickfields a brown thumb of smoke goes up. The two bells go on, not together, for some time." teaches ms_alarm then {
    Assert state(ms_house, ms_alight). Assert state(ms_door, ms_ablaze). Assert state(ms_kdoor, ms_jammed). Set ms_worth(ms_nine) to 10.
    Assert at(garrity, mark_street). Assert at(tobias, mark_street). Assert at(ms_mate, mark_street). Assert at(ms_tapley, mark_street).
    Assert at(ms_mrs, mark_street). Assert at(ms_kids, mark_street).
  }
  Rule ms_burns when state(ms_house, ms_alight) and ms_worth(ms_nine) > 0 { Decrease ms_worth(ms_nine) by 1. }
  Rule ms_burnt when state(ms_house, ms_alight) and ms_worth(ms_nine) <= 0 says "The roof of Number Nine goes in with a long soft sound, like a sigh let out by something that has been holding it. Both captains take their hats off. Neither takes the other's." {
    Assert state(ms_house, ms_closing). Assert ms_v_none(ms_nine). Assert state(ms_door, ms_charred).
  }
  Rule ms_salvors_come when state(ms_house, ms_alight) and state(ms_plate, ms_bare) and watch(clock) >= ms_pulled_at(ms_nine) + 3 says "A handcart comes round the corner of Mark Street at a trot, with six men in leather aprons and a boathook in front. 'Unmarked!' cries Master Voakes, from a long way off, with the joy of a man who has heard a rumour confirmed. 'Salvage! Nobody touch it!' The two brigades, who have been standing at ease for some time, watch him go by with the expression of men who have been robbed of a thing they did not want." {
    Assert state(ms_house, ms_closing). Assert ms_v_salvors(ms_nine). Increase ms_worth(ms_nine) by 2. Assert at(ms_quennell, mark_street).
  }
  // What is left of the house when the dispute is closed. The rules run in order: the first that fits takes the house out of "closing".
  Rule ms_tier_saved when state(ms_house, ms_closing) and ms_worth(ms_nine) >= 8 { Set ms_tier(ms_nine) to 3. Assert state(ms_house, ms_saved). }
  Rule ms_tier_half when state(ms_house, ms_closing) and ms_worth(ms_nine) >= 4 { Set ms_tier(ms_nine) to 2. Assert state(ms_house, ms_half). }
  Rule ms_tier_shell when state(ms_house, ms_closing) and ms_worth(ms_nine) >= 1 { Set ms_tier(ms_nine) to 1. Assert state(ms_house, ms_shell). }
  Rule ms_tier_gutted when state(ms_house, ms_closing) { Set ms_tier(ms_nine) to 0. Assert state(ms_house, ms_gutted). }

  // The verdicts. Each says what the street makes of it, once, and writes what the Hearing and the people will read.
  Rule ms_end_buckets when ms_over() and ms_v_buckets(ms_nine) and not ms_ended(ms_nine) says "The line breaks up in the way a line does when it is over, with men sitting on the kerb and buckets everywhere. Captain Garrity walks the length of Mark Street with her helmet under her arm, and at the end of it says, loudly enough to be heard at the Lamprey's end, 'Phoenix mark. Phoenix house. Phoenix saved.' Mate Marchbanks writes something in a small book. Mrs Peascod, who has been holding a clock throughout, puts it on the step." {
    Assert ms_ended(ms_nine). Assert ms_precedent_mark(party). Assert ms_unpaid(party). Increase regard(phoenix) by 1. Increase regard(brigades) by 1.
  }
  Rule ms_end_phoenix when ms_over() and ms_v_phoenix(ms_nine) and not ms_ended(ms_nine) says "The Phoenix pump goes in with nothing across the road from it, which is what a pump is for. Captain Garrity does not ask what has become of the opposition. She puts the fire out as if it had been rude to her, and then she says, to the street at large, 'Phoenix mark. Phoenix house.' And nobody says otherwise." {
    Assert ms_ended(ms_nine). Assert ms_precedent_mark(party). Assert ms_unpaid(party). Assert ms_slighted_lamprey(party).
    Increase regard(phoenix) by 1. Decrease regard(lamprey) by 1 or to nothing.
  }
  Rule ms_end_lamprey when ms_over() and ms_v_lamprey(ms_nine) and not ms_swapped(party) and not ms_ended(ms_nine) says "Mate Marchbanks reads the number from the policy-book aloud, to the Lamprey, to the Phoenix and to Mark Street, and the Lamprey's hose goes in at the front door like a thing let off a lead. Captain Garrity stands where she is. She is looking at the plate, and then at you, and then at the ground; she says, finally, to nobody, 'It's what the Office says.' She puts her helmet on and she does not take it off again until she is back in the yard." {
    Assert ms_ended(ms_nine). Assert ms_paid(ms_nine). Assert ms_garrity_shamed(party). Assert ms_slighted_phoenix(party).
    Increase regard(lamprey) by 2. Decrease regard(phoenix) by 1 or to nothing.
  }
  Rule ms_end_swapped when ms_over() and ms_v_lamprey(ms_nine) and ms_swapped(party) and not ms_ended(ms_nine) says "Captain Garrity looks at the door with the face of a woman reading a bill. 'That's a fish,' she says. There is a silence in which a good many people decide not to remember a bird. 'A mark on the door is the policy,' says Captain Garrity, heavily, 'and that is a mark.' She steps back, and the Lamprey's hose goes in under Mate Marchbanks's astonished eye. Nobody says a word about the other side of the street, where Number Ten has a pale square over its own door." {
    Assert ms_ended(ms_nine). Assert ms_paid(ms_nine). Increase regard(lamprey) by 1.
  }
  Rule ms_end_third when ms_over() and ms_v_third(ms_nine) and not ms_ended(ms_nine) says "You write it out on the back of the Peascods' own policy-book, with your licence open beside it on the step: THIS HOUSE WEARS THE MARK OF THE PHOENIX AND HOLDS THE POLICY OF THE LAMPREY; THE BRIGADE OF THE MARK SHALL ATTEND, THE OFFICE OF THE POLICY SHALL PAY, AND THE SALVAGE BE SHARED. Mate Marchbanks reads it twice. Captain Garrity reads it once, holding it a little away, as a woman looks at a bill from a trade she did not know she had. Then she signs, slowly, beneath you, 'Garrity, for the mark', and Marchbanks 'Marchbanks, for the policy', and the two hoses go in together." {
    Assert ms_ended(ms_nine). Assert ms_rule(party). Assert ms_paid(ms_nine).
    Increase regard(phoenix) by 1. Increase regard(lamprey) by 1. Increase regard(brigades) by 2.
  }
  Rule ms_end_salvors when ms_over() and ms_v_salvors(ms_nine) and not ms_ended(ms_nine) says "Master Voakes sets his men at the house like a gang at a regatta and gets the better part of it out of the fire in a quarter of an hour, with a quarter of the better part going onto his cart. 'A third,' he tells Mrs Peascod, kindly, and writes it on his cuff. 'Of what is saved. Of what is not, a sixth, as agreed.' The Phoenix and the Lamprey stand side by side at the end of the street, in complete agreement, for the first time in their histories." {
    Assert ms_ended(ms_nine). Assert ms_unpaid(party). Assert ms_slighted_brigades(party). Decrease regard(brigades) by 1 or to nothing.
  }
  Rule ms_end_none when ms_over() and ms_v_none(ms_nine) and not ms_ended(ms_nine) {
    Assert ms_ended(ms_nine). Assert ms_unpaid(party). Assert ms_burned(party).
  }
  // Everyone goes home, one way or another.
  Rule ms_home_saved when ms_ended(ms_nine) and not ms_dispersed(ms_nine) and ms_tier(ms_nine) >= 2 {
    Assert ms_dispersed(ms_nine). Assert at(ms_mrs, ms_kitchen). Assert at(ms_kids, ms_kitchen). Assert at(garrity, drill_yard). Assert at(ms_mate, lamprey_floor).
    Assert at(ms_tapley, hen_taproom). Assert at(ms_quennell, salvor_yard). Assert state(ms_door, ms_charred).
  }
  Rule ms_home_lost when ms_ended(ms_nine) and not ms_dispersed(ms_nine) {
    Assert ms_dispersed(ms_nine). Assert at(ms_mrs, pargeter_front). Assert at(ms_kids, pargeter_front). Assert at(garrity, drill_yard). Assert at(ms_mate, lamprey_floor).
    Assert at(ms_tapley, hen_taproom). Assert at(ms_quennell, salvor_yard). Assert state(ms_door, ms_charred).
  }
  Rule ms_tobias_home when ms_dispersed(ms_nine) and not travelsWith(tobias, party) and at(tobias, mark_street) { Assert at(tobias, pargeter_front). }
  Rule ms_tobias_thanks when ms_ended(ms_nine) and (ms_tier(ms_nine) >= 2 or ms_contents(ms_nine)) and not ms_v_salvors(ms_nine) and not tobiasWilling(party) {
    Assert tobiasWilling(party).
  }

  // ── The Slate, and the street's other ways of telling ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe ms_slate_open at slip_room when watch(clock) >= 12 and ms_open() "CLAIMS OPEN, in a fresh chalk that has run in the corner: MARK STREET, No. 9. A house burning; a mark disputed between Phoenix and Lamprey; a family in the road. The Offices will pay on the report of an adjuster who can say whose house it is. Reward: a settlement, and the thanks of the street." teaches ms_claim.
  Observe ms_slate_burned at slip_room when ms_burned(party) and watch(clock) >= 96 "TOTAL LOSSES (Brickfields): a house, Mark Street, No. 9; the dispute is adjourned.".
  Observe ms_slate_done at slip_room when ms_ended(ms_nine) and not ms_burned(party) and watch(clock) >= 96 "CLAIMS CLOSED: Mark Street, No. 9; the Offices are in correspondence.".
  Observe ms_boy_plaza at gate_plaza when watch(clock) >= 12 and watch(clock) < 28 and state(ms_house, ms_alight) "A boy runs across the plaza with a bucket in each hand, shouting that it is a mark and they won't, and that Mark Street is going up. A man selling polish decides to walk that way too." teaches ms_alarm.
  Observe ms_boy_lane at brick_lane when state(ms_house, ms_alight) "Brick Lane has emptied toward Mark Street. A woman is sweeping her step as if the end of the world would at least be tidy.".
  Observe ms_lane_after at brick_lane when ms_over() and ms_tier(ms_nine) <= 1 "At the top of Mark Street the smell of wet char hangs in the lane. Someone has propped a board against a lamp-post: SALLOWS, NO. 9, STAYING AT THE PARGETERS'.".
  Observe ms_street_burning at mark_street when state(ms_house, ms_alight) "The two brigades stand on Mark Street with a house between them, each behind its own hose: the Phoenix in blue, with its engine at the hydrant, the Lamprey in oilskin, with a hand-pump dragged up from the Reach and a mate with a book. Captain Garrity and Mate Marchbanks are in the middle, nose to nose, and nobody is putting out the fire. A family stands in the cobbles with a clock.".
  Observe ms_street_after_lost at mark_street when ms_over() and ms_tier(ms_nine) <= 1 "On the cobbles opposite the heap a trestle has been set up with blankets, a kettle and a tin of buns, and a young man in a blue coat is handing them out with great gentleness and no discrimination.".
  Observe ms_street_ten at mark_street when state(ms_plate, ms_fish) "Over the door of Number Ten, where a black fish should be, there is a pale square with two nail-holes.".
  Observe ms_garrity_after near garrity when ms_ended(ms_nine) and ms_v_buckets(ms_nine) "Captain Garrity has the look of a woman who has won something and hopes nobody checks the receipt.".
  Observe ms_garrity_after_lamprey near garrity when ms_garrity_shamed(party) "Captain Garrity looks at a spot a little to one side of you, and goes on looking at it.".
  Observe ms_garrity_after_swap near garrity when ms_swapped(party) "Captain Garrity watches you for a moment with deep suspicion and, you think, something not far from respect.".
  Observe ms_garrity_after_rule near garrity when ms_rule(party) "Captain Garrity touches two fingers to her helmet when she sees you, which, from her, is a speech.".
  Observe ms_garrity_after_burned near garrity when ms_burned(party) "Captain Garrity is oiling a hose that does not need it.".
  Observe ms_mrs_after_paid near ms_mrs when ms_paid(ms_nine) and ms_tier(ms_nine) >= 2 "On the table in Mrs Peascod's kitchen a letter from the Lamprey lies open, flattened under the kettle, beside a slice of cake with your names on a paper pennant.".
  Observe ms_mrs_after_unpaid near ms_mrs when ms_unpaid(party) and ms_over() and not ms_paid(ms_nine) "Mrs Peascod does not look at you; she is folding a blanket that is not hers into a square.".

  // ── At the fire: what the company can ask, and who answers ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic ms_mrs_policy with ms_mrs "Ask Mrs Peascod whose cover the house is under" when ms_open() once {
    Says "'The Lamprey's,' says Ada Peascod, not taking her eyes off the front wall. 'Aubrey's firm takes it for all the clerks, the way they take the tea. It's in the policy-book, in the bureau in the front room, in the tin drawer; I could show you the page. And it's the Phoenix has come, with a bird the Guild's man put up on Monday, and I said at the time, I said, Mr Tapley, that's a bird. And he said it was a very good fish.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ms_lamprey_cover). }
  }
  Topic ms_mrs_clock with ms_mrs "Ask Mrs Peascod why she is holding the clock" when ms_open() once {
    Says "'Because it was the first thing to hand,' says Ada Peascod, 'and I thought if I put it down I should have to decide about the rest.'".
  }
  Topic ms_kids_what with ms_kids "Ask the children what they have saved" when ms_open() once {
    Says "'Premium,' says the smallest, holding the cat up. 'And the slate. And Papa's best hat, but only the box.' The eldest shows you the slate. On it, in careful chalk: IF A HOUSE IS INSURED AND IT BURNS, WHO.".
  }
  Topic ms_tapley_plate with ms_tapley "Ask Mr Tapley about the plate" when ms_open() once {
    Says "'There were two bags,' says Mr Tapley, to the cobbles. 'One of birds and one of fish. They were in the dark, by the door, and I was, I admit, a little merry. I took a bird. I took it with great confidence. Nobody has ever said that I lacked confidence.' He puts a hand to his eyes. 'The Lamprey's policy was on the schedule. I read the schedule. I simply did not let it detain me.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ms_nailed_wrong). }
  }
  Topic ms_tapley_swear with ms_tapley "Ask Mr Tapley to say so to the captains" when knows(actor, ms_nailed_wrong) and state(ms_house, ms_alight) once {
    Says "Mr Tapley rises, with dignity, goes four steps toward the captains, hears the word 'Guild' used in the sense of a pit, and sits down. 'Not,' he says, 'for any sum.'".
  }
  Topic ms_ruddle_cover with ms_mate "Ask Mate Marchbanks what the Lamprey says about the mark" when ms_open() once {
    Says "Mate Marchbanks opens his small book. 'Lamprey and River, Household, number four-one-one-seven. Peascod. No. 9. It was a fish in the schedule and it is a bird on the door, and the Captain's standing order is that we do not put the Office's water into a house that the plate says is the Phoenix's, for if the plate is right we are out the water and if the plate is wrong we are out the argument.' He looks at the house. 'I should very much like to be told I was wrong.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ms_lamprey_cover). }
  }
  Topic ms_ruddle_price with ms_mate "Ask Mate Marchbanks what would send the Lamprey home" when ms_open() once {
    Says "'Eight coin for the hose-boys' beer,' says Mate Marchbanks, 'would have the hose-boys convinced it was a Phoenix matter, and me convinced that I had not been asked. I am not saying that. I am saying what a hose-boy might say.'".
  }
  Topic ms_quennell_share with ms_quennell "Ask Master Voakes what the Salvors take" when true once {
    Says "'One third of a total loss,' says Master Voakes. 'One half of a salvage. Of a case you do not ask about, as agreed. The Reach does not hold with a house being nobody's, you understand. It is a waste of a house.'".
  }
  Topic ms_pudsey_fire with pudsey "Ask Mrs Pudsey if anything is happening in the Brickfields this morning" when watch(clock) < 28 once {
    Says "'There's always something happening in the Brickfields,' says Mrs Pudsey. 'It's what they have instead of weather. Go up Brick Lane toward ten. If there's a house on fire, it'll be Mark Street, and if there's two captains, it'll be Garrity and the Lamprey's man, and if there's a family in the road, ask them about the book.'".
  }

  // ── Captain Garrity: asked, and not argued with ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic ms_g_argue with garrity "Put it to Captain Garrity that a plate is only as good as the man who nailed it" when state(ms_house, ms_alight) once {
    Says "'A plate,' says Captain Garrity, 'is a plate. If it says Phoenix then the Phoenix has the house, and if I start taking the word of a householder over the word of the door, I shall be putting out fires by appointment for the rest of my life. I hear you. I have heard you. You can say it again if you like. It is not going to be any different.'".
  }
  Topic ms_g_bribe with garrity "Slip Captain Garrity ten coin to let the Lamprey's hose in" when state(ms_house, ms_alight) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 10 and not ms_g_insulted(party) once {
    Says "Captain Garrity looks at the hand and then at the coin and then at the hand. 'I have been offered money,' she says, 'by better men, and refused it at longer odds. You may take that back.' She puts it, with some precision, in the top of your coat.".
    On discuss { Assert ms_g_insulted(party). Decrease regard(phoenix) by 1 or to nothing. }
  }
  Topic ms_g_sorry with garrity "Beg Captain Garrity's pardon for the ten coin" when ms_g_insulted(party) once {
    Says "'I do not accept apologies,' says Captain Garrity, 'on duty. But I notice you have made one.'".
    On discuss { Retract ms_g_insulted(party). }
  }
  Topic ms_g_ask with garrity "Tell Captain Garrity that you are not here to order her; ask her, as a favour to you, to let Mate Marchbanks's hose lie beside hers" when state(ms_house, ms_alight) and arc(garrity) == 0 and not ms_g_insulted(party) once {
    Says "Captain Garrity opens her mouth, and shuts it. She is a woman who has been told things by a great many people in the last quarter of an hour. 'Nobody asks,' she says. 'They tell me. They send a boy, or a form.' She looks at the house. 'I'll not move my crew off the plate. A plate's a plate. But I'll let Marchbanks's hose lie alongside, and I'll not call it a trespass, and if the policy's his then I'll sign beneath whatever the Office says it is, if it's a thing a woman can sign.' She jerks her head at the Lamprey line. 'Go on, then. Do whatever you do.'".
    On discuss { Set arc(garrity) to 1. Increase ms_worth(ms_nine) by 2. Assert ms_asked(party). }
  }
  Topic ms_g_late with garrity "Ask Captain Garrity, as a favour, to put her name to a certification of the Peascods' house after the fact" when ms_over() and arc(garrity) == 0 and not ms_g_insulted(party) and not ms_rule(party) once {
    Says "Captain Garrity takes her time. 'After the fact,' she says. 'It was a house, and it's a heap, and you want me to say the heap had two owners.' She looks at the yard. 'Nobody asks, you know. I'll sign if the book's good. I'll not sign if it's only talk.'".
    On discuss { Set arc(garrity) to 1. Assert ms_asked(party). }
  }
  Topic ms_g_after_won with garrity "Ask Captain Garrity how Mark Street sits with the Office" when ms_v_buckets(ms_nine) or ms_v_phoenix(ms_nine) once {
    Says "'The Office is pleased,' says Captain Garrity. 'It says the plate held. I have been told twice. The Lamprey has not said anything, which is how I know they will.'".
  }
  Topic ms_g_after_lost with garrity "Ask Captain Garrity how Mark Street sits with the Office" when ms_garrity_shamed(party) once {
    Says "'It sits,' says Captain Garrity, 'on my desk, in writing, with your name beside it. A plate is a plate. Until a man with a book says it isn't.' She turns a hose over and over. 'You were right. I should like that to be a thing I could say with pleasure.'".
  }
  Topic ms_g_after_both with garrity "Ask Captain Garrity what the Office makes of the certification" when ms_rule(party) once {
    Says "'They call it the Mark Street Rule,' says Captain Garrity. 'The Lamprey say it was theirs. We say it was ours. It is on a card in both fire-houses. There's a clause I'd have put otherwise.' She does not say which.".
  }

  // ── The company's own doings at the fire ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Action ms_buckets(actor: group) "Form a bucket-line from the pump in the yard and pass until the fire is out" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, nine_yard) and state(ms_house, ms_alight) and state(ms_plate, ms_bird).
    Time 30 minutes.
    On success { Increase ms_worth(ms_nine) by 2. Assert state(ms_house, ms_closing). Assert ms_v_buckets(ms_nine). }
    Result "You find the pump, a coal-hole and every pail in the Brickfields, and put your backs into a line with the Peascods' neighbours and half the lane. It is a good line, and hot work. By the time the roof stops spitting nobody remembers who stood in the middle of the street.".
  }
  Action ms_buckets_strong(actor: group) "Take the head of the bucket-line yourselves, and carry the water to the kitchen window" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, nine_yard) and state(ms_house, ms_alight) and state(ms_plate, ms_bird) and capable(actor, brawn).
    Time 30 minutes.
    On success { Increase ms_worth(ms_nine) by 5. Assert state(ms_house, ms_closing). Assert ms_v_buckets(ms_nine). }
    Result "You take the head of the line, where the pails are heaviest and the heat is on your face, and a woman from number six calls the time in a voice that could stop a ship. It is the straightforward thing, and it works; you go over the sill of the kitchen window with the last pail and what is behind you is steaming, and standing.".
  }
  Action ms_furniture(actor: group) "Carry the Peascods' furniture out through the yard while the captains talk" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, nine_yard) and state(ms_house, ms_alight) and not ms_contents(ms_nine).
    Time 30 minutes.
    On success { Assert ms_contents(ms_nine). }
    Result "You carry out what there is: the table, the clock's spare weights, a sideboard through a window, a bed in four parts, the canary's spare cage, the kitchen chairs one at a time, and the bureau's contents in your arms, tied up in a sheet, in the confusion. The children make a line of themselves and the cat.".
  }
  Action ms_front_entry(actor: group) "Take the Peascods' policy-book from the bureau in the front room" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, ms_front) and not ms_book_taken(ms_nine) and not holding(actor, ms_book_kind).
    Time 4 minutes.
    On success { Give ms_book to actor. Assert ms_book_taken(ms_nine). }
    Result "The bureau's lid is too hot to touch, and you do not touch it; you break the brass lock with the butt of a knife and drag the tin-lined drawer out on its runners. Inside, tied in tape, lies a black oilcloth book, dry as a bone, with a fish stamped on its cover. You have it under your coat before your eyebrows have decided what to do.".
  }
  Action ms_read_book(actor: group) "Read the Peascods' policy-book through" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and holding(actor, ms_book_kind) and not knows(actor, ms_proof).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, ms_proof). Assert knows(actor, ms_lamprey_cover). }
    Result "Policy No. 4,117, Domestic and Household: the Lamprey & River Office insures the house at No. 9, Mark Street, in the name of Aubrey Peascod, against fire, flood, and the act of an enemy. In the margin, in the Lamprey's clerk's best hand: This house to be marked with the Fish. Beneath, in a different ink: Schedule received, plate not yet fixed. The Guild's surveyor is to be informed. He was.".
  }
  Action ms_certify_lamprey(actor: group) "Certify the mark false, on your licence, and the policy the Lamprey's" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, mark_street) and state(ms_house, ms_alight) and holding(actor, adjuster_licence) and holding(actor, ms_book_kind) and knows(actor, ms_proof).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert state(ms_house, ms_closing). Assert ms_v_lamprey(ms_nine). }
    Result "You open your licence in one hand and the Peascods' book in the other and read the number out to Mark Street.".
  }
  Action ms_certify_third(actor: group) "Certify a third thing on your licence: the Phoenix's mark, the Lamprey's policy, one fire, two hoses" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, mark_street) and state(ms_house, ms_alight) and holding(actor, adjuster_licence) and holding(actor, ms_book_kind) and knows(actor, ms_proof) and arc(garrity) >= 1.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert state(ms_house, ms_closing). Assert ms_v_third(ms_nine). }
    Result "It is not in any book you have read, and you make it up in the street, with a licence and a policy-book and two captains' attention. Garrity said she would sign if it was a thing a woman could sign. It is.".
  }
  Action ms_certify_after(actor: group) "Certify the dead house after the fact, with the Peascods' book, and the Phoenix's name beside the Lamprey's" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, drill_yard) and ms_over() and not ms_rule(party) and not ms_paid(ms_nine) and holding(actor, adjuster_licence) and holding(actor, ms_book_kind) and knows(actor, ms_proof) and arc(garrity) >= 1 and at(garrity, drill_yard).
    Time 20 minutes.
    On success { Assert ms_rule(party). Assert ms_paid(ms_nine). Retract ms_unpaid(party). Increase regard(phoenix) by 1. Increase regard(lamprey) by 1. Increase regard(brigades) by 1. }
    Result "You write it out on the lid of a water-butt: THE MARK WAS THE PHOENIX'S, THE POLICY WAS THE LAMPREY'S, THE LOSS IS SHARED. Garrity signs it standing, as though it were an oath. A boy takes it to the Reach at a run, and returns with a note in Dree's hand that says only, in capitals, ABOUT TIME.".
  }
  Action ms_pull_plate(actor: group) "Prise the gilt bird off Number Nine's door while both captains are looking at each other" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, mark_street) and state(ms_house, ms_alight) and state(ms_plate, ms_bird) and not ms_caught(party).
    Time 6 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state(ms_plate, ms_bare). Set ms_pulled_at(ms_nine) to watch(clock). }
    On failure { Assert ms_caught(party). Decrease ms_worth(ms_nine) by 2 or to nothing. Decrease regard(brigades) by 1 or to nothing. Assert ms_slighted_brigades(party). }
    Result "The nails come out of the new wood like teeth out of a child. You have the bird under your coat before Captain Garrity has finished her sentence. The house is, in a moment, nobody's; and the captains, who have both been given what each wanted, are stranded in it.".
    Otherwise "Captain Garrity's hand closes on your collar from behind. 'That,' she says, 'is the Office's bird.' For the first time that morning she and Mate Marchbanks are in complete agreement, and the thing they agree about is you.".
  }
  Action ms_swap_plate(actor: group) "Swap Number Ten's black fish for Number Nine's gilt bird, while both captains are looking at each other" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, mark_street) and state(ms_house, ms_alight) and state(ms_plate, ms_bird) and not ms_caught(party).
    Time 6 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert state(ms_plate, ms_fish). Assert ms_swapped(party). Assert state(ms_house, ms_closing). Assert ms_v_lamprey(ms_nine). }
    On failure { Assert ms_caught(party). Decrease ms_worth(ms_nine) by 2 or to nothing. Decrease regard(brigades) by 1 or to nothing. Assert ms_slighted_brigades(party). }
    Result "A fish is a good deal lighter than a bird, and Number Ten's neighbour is looking the other way. You are on the step, and off it, and a black fish is hanging a little crooked over Number Nine's door with the paint of a different house on its tail, before anyone has so much as drawn breath.".
    Otherwise "Mate Marchbanks, who is looking at you for the first time, says in a conversational voice, 'That is the Lamprey's fish,' and Captain Garrity says, 'That is the Phoenix's bird,' and the two of them take hold of an arm each. You have lost a quarter of an hour and a good deal of Mark Street's regard.".
  }
  Action ms_bribe_ruddle(actor: group) "Press eight coin into Mate Marchbanks's hand for the hose-boys' beer, and let the Phoenix have the house" {
    Speaker ms_mate.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, mark_street) and at(ms_mate, mark_street) and state(ms_house, ms_alight) and state(ms_plate, ms_bird) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 8.
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 8. Increase ms_worth(ms_nine) by 4. Assert state(ms_house, ms_closing). Assert ms_v_phoenix(ms_nine). }
    Result "Mate Marchbanks does not look at the coin. He looks at the sky, and says to the hose-boys that the Lamprey has no standing on a Phoenix mark and that anybody who thinks otherwise can say so to Captain Dree. It is, you realise, the position he has been maintaining all morning.".
  }
  Action ms_scare_ruddle(actor: group) "Tell Mate Marchbanks what the Lamprey's pump will look like at the bottom of the river" {
    Speaker ms_mate.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, mark_street) and at(ms_mate, mark_street) and state(ms_house, ms_alight) and state(ms_plate, ms_bird) and capable(actor, intimidation).
    Time 5 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_hard).
    On success { Increase ms_worth(ms_nine) by 4. Assert state(ms_house, ms_closing). Assert ms_v_phoenix(ms_nine). }
    On failure { Assert ms_slighted_lamprey(party). Decrease regard(lamprey) by 1 or to nothing. }
    Result "Mate Marchbanks listens to a description of his pump and the river with the patience of a man who has been threatened by experts, and then he tells his hose-boys, quietly, to go home. You do not like how little it cost.".
    Otherwise "'Captain Dree,' says Mate Marchbanks, in the tone of a man reading the weather, 'was threatened by a harbour-master once. The harbour-master has since retired.' He writes your description into the small book.".
  }
  Topic ms_tob_fetch with tobias "Ask Tobias Pargeter to run in at the front and bring out the Peascods' policy-book" when state(ms_house, ms_alight) and not ms_book_taken(ms_nine) once {
    Says "Tobias Pargeter looks at Captain Garrity, who is not looking at him, and at the front door, which is. 'Nobody told me not to,' he says, and goes in with his coat over his head. He comes out a long minute later with his eyebrows gone and a black oilcloth book held to his chest. 'It's got a fish on it,' he says, rather surprised, and gives it to you.".
    On discuss { Give ms_book to actor. Assert ms_book_taken(ms_nine). Decrease ms_worth(ms_nine) by 2 or to nothing. }
  }
  Topic ms_tob_blankets with tobias "Ask Tobias Pargeter how the Peascods are" when ms_over() and ms_tier(ms_nine) <= 1 once {
    Says "'My mother's coming with the broth,' says Tobias Pargeter. 'They'll have our back room. Mrs Peascod won't sit down, so I put the kettle where she can see it.' He looks at the heap, and does not say anything more.".
  }
  Topic ms_tob_thanks with tobias "Ask Tobias Pargeter what he made of Mark Street" when tobiasWilling(actor) and not ms_burned(party) once {
    Says "'I put out my share,' says Tobias Pargeter, 'and carried more than my share, and I'd not have had it done any other way. I think the Office had better learn what the Lamprey knew. I'd like to come with you, if you're going on with it. I've the evenings.'".
  }
  Topic ms_tob_join with tobias "Ask Tobias Pargeter to come along with the company" when tobiasWilling(actor) once {
    Says "Tobias Pargeter takes his helmet off its peg, puts it on, takes it off, and hangs it up again. 'Right,' he says. 'Mother will insure the dinner.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(tobias, actor). Set hire(tobias) to 0. }
  }
  Topic ms_mrs_witness with ms_mrs "Ask Mrs Peascod whether she would say what happened before the Five" when ms_paid(ms_nine) or ms_rule(party) once {
    Says "'I should think so,' says Ada Peascod. 'I've been waiting for someone to ask me something that was not whether I was covered.'".
    On discuss { Assert witness(ms_mrs). }
  }
  Objective ms_obj_fire when (knows(party, ms_claim) or knows(party, ms_alarm)) and state(ms_house, ms_alight) "A house burns on Mark Street under the wrong Office's plate, and the two brigades will not work a mark that is not theirs. It will be gone by noon.".
  Objective ms_obj_claim when knows(party, ms_claim) and ms_over() and ms_unpaid(party) and not ms_paid(ms_nine) "The Peascods' house is lost or saved by the wrong Office, and nobody is paying them: the policy-book is in the front room, and the Captains of both brigades are in their yards.".
}

Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "The Bare Wards: the Penny Mutual's empty box and its forgiven treasurer, the stamped notice she was paid to keep quiet about, and the Night Market, which sells second-hand marks, eel-pie and other people's hats, and says what it thinks of the Offices.".

  // ── What is mine ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // wards_gate, salt_lane, penny_hall, night_market, pip_stair (Pip's file) and one garret of my own. The fund is
  // fourteen coin. The nine names on the NEXT board die slowly, three at a time (days 3, 5 and 7), until the fund is
  // home. The treasurer takes the night boat at eight on the evening of day 2 (watch 216; day(clock) is 1 on the first morning, so
  // the fire of the second night is in the small hours of day 3, watch 240 to 300) unless she has been found.
  Place pm_garret "the garret over the oven-yard" is room within wards at 2, 0.
  Passage pm_garret_way "the oven-yard stair" is passage between salt_lane and pm_garret hidden until pm_garret_known.

  Measure pm_dying(group).
  Initially Set pm_dying(wardsfolk) to 9.
  Relation pm_fund_home(group). Relation pm_proud(group). Relation pm_ashamed(group). Relation pm_loan(group).
  Relation pm_found(group). Relation pm_purse(group). Relation pm_told_club(group). Relation pm_court_warned(group).
  Relation pm_disbelieved(group). Relation pm_resolved(group). Relation pm_neglected(group). Relation pm_rent_strike(group).
  Relation pm_gone(group). Relation pm_cowed(group). Relation pm_robbed(group). Relation pm_stamp_seen(group).
  Relation pm_garrowby_for(group). Relation pm_refused_loan(group). Relation pm_trail_cold(group). Relation pm_pie(group).
  Relation pm_deputy_warned(group). Relation pm_slighted_wards(group). Relation pm_keeper_asked(group). Relation pm_ouseley_speaks(group).

  Discovery pm_claim "The Penny Mutual of Salt Lane has lost its treasurer and its fund, and nine of its members are on the NEXT board.".
  Discovery pm_vote "The Penny Mutual has voted, forty-one to one, to forgive the treasurer who ran with its fund.".
  Discovery pm_garret_known "Prudence Ouseley, the Mutual's treasurer, is lodging as Mrs Ames in a garret over the oven-yard, off Salt Lane.".
  Discovery pm_bribed "Prudence Ouseley was paid by the rent-collector's man to say nothing of a notice, and ran when she understood what the notice was for.".

