    Greets again "'Marks,' says Old Ferrule, comfortably.".
    Sells pm_old_mark for 2 coin from 6.
  }
  Topic ferrule_marks with pm_ferrule "Ask Old Ferrule where the marks come from" when true once {
    Says "'Off burnt houses, off houses that got a better plate, off houses where the family moved,' says Old Ferrule. 'The Office never takes its own mark back. It would have to admit the fire. So the plates lie in the ashes till somebody with a barrow comes by, and then they hang in the Wards, where there's no Office to ask for them back.' He holds up a bird, the beak down. 'A Phoenix. The brigade will look at it, I find. About one time in three.'".
  }
  Topic ferrule_gas with pm_ferrule "Ask Old Ferrule about the Gas Company's men in the square" when true once {
    Says "'Lord Gaunt-Halloran,' says Old Ferrule, with the reverence of a man describing weather, 'has forbidden the open flame in the inner wards for the safety of the public. His men confiscate the lamps. They bring them here to be sold again, for a commission, to the people they were confiscated from. I'm the commission.' He polishes a hand-shaped plate with his sleeve. 'He doesn't know. Honest man. You'd be amazed how little that helps.'".
  }

  Person pm_pennifold "Hannah Pennifold" at night_market {
    Role "who sells other people's hats". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns she.
    Seen when hour(clock) >= 17 or hour(clock) < 5.
    Greets "A girl of sixteen, wearing three hats, stands behind a clothes-line hung with forty. 'Hats,' says Hannah Pennifold. 'Bowlers, caps, a bishop's. A clerk's, a captain's, a mourner's. If you want to be somebody for an evening I can have you somebody in a minute. If you want to be nobody, I'm afraid that's cheaper.'".
    Greets again "'Hats,' says Hannah Pennifold. 'Hello again.'".
    Sells pm_hat for 3 coin from 4.
  }
  Topic pennifold_hats with pm_pennifold "Ask Hannah Pennifold where she gets the hats" when true once {
    Says "'From the Hill, mostly,' says Hannah Pennifold. 'Gentlemen leave them in cabs. The Phoenix clerks are the best; they have a gilt bird in the band, and a man in a hat with a gilt bird in the band can walk in anywhere in the Wards and ask for any book, and nobody asks him for his name.' She straightens a bishop's. 'I only sell the hats. I don't say what they're for.'".
  }
  Topic pennifold_dree with pm_pennifold "Ask Hannah Pennifold which captains' hats she has had" when true once {
    Says "'Captain Dree's, four times,' says Hannah Pennifold. 'Somebody takes it off the peg in the Lamprey House and brings it here, and Mrs Dree buys it back the next day. I think it's a game. I think they're both rather proud of it.' She lowers her voice. 'Cray of the Sovereign tears up forms in a good coat and buys a new one when he's done. I've never seen his hat. I have a feeling that it's his mother's.'".
  }

  // ── The garret ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe pm_garret_scene at pm_garret when true "A slope-ceilinged room over a yard, warm from the oven below, with a bed made tight, a kettle that is much too new and a carpet-bag packed and standing by the door like a dog that has been told to wait. On the back of the door, at eye level, someone has pinned a half-sheet of grey paper, face in.".
  Person pm_ouseley "Prudence Ouseley" at pm_garret {
    Role "treasurer of the Penny Mutual, lodging as Mrs Ames". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A thin woman in a good grey dress is sitting upright on the end of the bed with her hands in her lap, as if she were waiting for a verdict. 'You'll be the Mutual,' says Prudence Ouseley. 'Or the Office. I'd rather you were the Mutual. I've a boat on the evening of the second day and I've packed.' She does not look at the bag. 'I'd as soon be told I was a thief by someone who loved me.'".
    Greets again "'You,' says Prudence Ouseley. 'Please sit.'".
  }
  Topic ouseley_why with pm_ouseley "Ask Prudence Ouseley why she ran" when true once {
    Says "'Because I was paid five coin to say nothing,' says Prudence Ouseley, 'by Mr Larkworth, on behalf of someone who signs with a bird. I was shown a paper. It was a notice, for a block in this ward, for the second night. I know what a notice is. They come a week early, and the block burns.' She looks at the wall. 'The Mutual would have buried them. I thought: if I take the box, I'll be gone, and Keturah will say I stole, and nobody will ask me about the paper. I thought I could buy a passage for Seth and me.' She laughs, shortly. 'And I find that I can't be bought with five coin. It's only that I can't be believed for less.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, pm_bribed). }
  }
  Action pm_ouseley_home(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Prudence Ouseley that the club has voted to forgive her, and ask her to come home" {
    Speaker pm_ouseley.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pm_ouseley, site) and knows(actor, pm_vote) and not pm_found(actor) and not pm_purse(actor).
    Time 20 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert pm_found(actor). Give pm_notice to actor. Retract at(pm_ouseley, pm_garret). Assert at(pm_ouseley, penny_hall). }
    Result "She does not believe you. You tell her again, and name the number, and tell her who voted the one, and why; and her face does what a face does that has not been forgiven in eleven years. 'Forty-one,' she says. 'And one.' She stands, and takes the grey paper from the back of the door, and puts it into your hand with the purse. 'I'll come,' says Prudence Ouseley. 'But I'll walk in front, and you'll not hold my arm.'".
    Otherwise "'A club can vote anything,' says Prudence Ouseley. 'It's a club.' She turns her face to the wall. 'Go away, please. You are being kind and it is making it worse.'".
  }
  Action pm_ouseley_press(actor: group, site: place) "Stand over Prudence Ouseley until she hands over the purse and the paper" {
    Speaker pm_ouseley.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pm_ouseley, site) and not pm_found(actor) and not pm_purse(actor) and capable(actor, intimidation).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert pm_purse(actor). Assert pm_cowed(actor). Give pm_notice to actor. }
    Result "She is not a woman who is easily frightened, but she has been frightened for a week, and that has taken the practice out of it. The purse comes out of the bag. The grey paper comes off the back of the door. 'There,' says Prudence Ouseley, and does not look at you, and does not say anything else, and for a long time afterward does not look at the door.".
    Otherwise "'You do not frighten me,' says Prudence Ouseley. 'I have been frightened by experts.' She does not move from the bed. You find that you have been, in some way you cannot place, rather rude.".
  }
  Action pm_ouseley_lift(actor: group, site: place) "While she is out on the stair with the kettle, take the purse and the paper" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, pm_garret) and at(pm_ouseley, pm_garret) and not pm_found(actor) and not pm_purse(actor) and capable(actor, stealth).
    Time 5 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert pm_purse(actor). Assert pm_robbed(actor). Give pm_notice to actor. }
    On failure { Assert pm_gone(actor). Retract at(pm_ouseley, pm_garret). Assert pm_cowed(actor). }
    Result "She goes down the stair with the kettle. You have, by the length of a shuffle and a pour, the time it takes to say a prayer. The purse is in the bag, the paper is on the door, face in. You are on the oven-yard stair before the kettle is full.".
    Otherwise "A board speaks. 'Fine,' says Prudence Ouseley, from the stair, without turning round. 'Fine. Take it, then.' By the time you have the bag open, she has gone down the stair, and out through the yard, and into the lane, at a pace that suggests that she is leaving more than a garret. It is a very good bag. It is empty.".
  }
  Action pm_lay_purse(actor: group, site: place) "Lay the recovered purse on the Mutual's table, and say a collector's man left it" {
    Speaker pm_trendle.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pm_trendle, site) and at(actor, penny_hall) and pm_purse(actor) and not pm_fund_home(actor).
    Time 8 minutes.
    On success { Assert pm_fund_home(actor). Assert pm_proud(actor). Assert pm_resolved(actor). Increase regard(wardsfolk) by 1. }
    Result "Keturah Trendle weighs the purse in her hand, and lays it in the box, and counts it, which takes some time. 'Fourteen,' she says. 'Less nothing.' She locks the three locks, one after the other, with three keys from three chains, and looks at you. 'A collector's man,' she says. 'Well. I have never heard that a collector's man left anything anywhere. But I am not going to ask, because we are a club.' She does not meet Garrowby's eye. 'Will you take a pie?'".
  }

  Rule pm_boat at pm_garret when watch(clock) >= 216 and at(pm_ouseley, pm_garret) says "The garret over the oven-yard is empty. The bed is stripped, the kettle gone, and the stair scrubbed within the hour. Down at the river a boat that was to go at eight has gone." { Retract at(pm_ouseley, pm_garret). Assert pm_gone(party). }

  // ── Home, and what is told ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic trendle_ouseley_q with pm_trendle "Tell Mrs Trendle that Prudence Ouseley is at the door, with what she carried off" when pm_found(party) and at(pm_ouseley, penny_hall) and not pm_resolved(party) once {
    Says "Prudence Ouseley has come in at the door behind you and stood just inside it, in her good grey dress, with her hands folded, like a woman at her own trial. The club has stopped. 'Prudence,' says Keturah Trendle. 'It is fourteen coin.' 'It is,' says Prudence Ouseley. 'Fourteen. I have not spent a farthing.' There is a pause. 'The club has forgiven you,' Mrs Trendle says. 'Forty-one to one. Is there something that the club does not know?'".
  }
  Topic trendle_tell with pm_trendle "Tell the club what she was paid to keep quiet about, and by whom, and put the notice on the table" answering trendle_ouseley_q when pm_stamp_seen(actor) and holding(actor, pm_paper) {
    Says "You lay the grey paper on the long table, under the lamp, with the seal to the room. Nobody in the Penny Mutual has ever seen a Phoenix seal on a notice to quit in the Wards, and a number of them read, with their lips moving, the name of a court that most of them have cousins in. Garrowby says 'Told you,' and no one hushes him. Mrs Trendle looks at the paper, and at Prudence Ouseley, who is white to the lips, and says, 'You were paid to say nothing of this.' 'Yes,' says Prudence. 'And you took the box.' 'Yes. To go. To not be asked.' A silence. 'Well,' says Keturah Trendle, and her voice has changed, 'that is not a club that does not ask any more.' She takes down the board that says WE DO NOT ASK, and turns it to the wall.".
    On discuss { Assert pm_told_club(actor). Assert pm_fund_home(actor). Assert pm_resolved(actor). Assert pm_rent_strike(wardsfolk). Increase regard(wardsfolk) by 2. }
  }
  Topic trendle_quiet with pm_trendle "Say only that she has come home, and let the vote stand" answering trendle_ouseley_q when true {
    Says "You say that she has come home, and with the fund, and that that is all the club asked for. Keturah Trendle looks at you for a moment, and at Prudence, and at the paper that you do not mention, and nods. 'Then that is that,' she says. She takes the purse from Prudence's hands, and puts her own hand over Prudence's for the length of a breath, and takes it away. The club sighs, and begins to breathe, and somebody puts a kettle on. It is a fine club. It does not ask.".
    On discuss { Assert pm_fund_home(actor). Assert pm_proud(actor). Assert pm_resolved(actor). Increase regard(wardsfolk) by 1. }
  }
  Topic ouseley_witness with pm_ouseley "Ask Prudence Ouseley whether she will say before the Five what she was paid" when pm_told_club(actor) and at(pm_ouseley, penny_hall) and not pm_ouseley_speaks(actor) once {
    Says "'In the Hall,' says Prudence Ouseley, 'with the five chairs.' She is quiet. Behind her the Mutual has gone silent, to a woman, and forty-one of them have looked up. 'Forty-one to one,' she says. 'I think I might.' She holds out her hands to the hall as if asking it to take them. 'But if I am to be believed by the Offices, I shall want the club in the room. And a hat of my own.'".
    On discuss { Assert witness(pm_ouseley). Assert pm_ouseley_speaks(actor). }
  }

  // The warning. It is believed as the company is trusted. The date is the second night.
  Topic trendle_warn_yes with pm_trendle "Tell Mrs Trendle that Candlewick Court has a stamped notice, for the second night" when knows(actor, d_candlewick_next) and not pm_court_warned(actor) and (entered_gap(actor) or pm_fund_home(actor) or regard(wardsfolk) >= 1) {
    Says "'Candlewick,' says Keturah Trendle, and she is across the room before you have finished, with her shawl, and two of the Mutual's men behind her, who have not been asked. 'Seven houses. My sister's boy lives at Number Four.' She turns at the door. 'We have a cart, and a lane, and a blanket for every shoulder in the Mutual. We will have them out by dusk and in our own halls by midnight, and they may curse us in the morning for waking them.' She looks at you. 'It is a great thing, to be believed,' she says. 'I would not have done it for the Phoenix.'".
    On discuss { Assert pm_court_warned(actor). Increase regard(wardsfolk) by 1. }
  }
  Topic trendle_warn_no with pm_trendle "Tell Mrs Trendle that Candlewick Court has a stamped notice, for the second night" when knows(actor, d_candlewick_next) and not pm_court_warned(actor) and not pm_disbelieved(actor) and not entered_gap(actor) and not pm_fund_home(actor) and regard(wardsfolk) < 1 once {
    Says "Keturah Trendle goes still. 'You know the date,' she says. 'You know the court, and the night. I have been in the Wards for sixty years, and the people who know the date of a fire beforehand are the people who set it.' She does not shout. 'I do not say that you did. I say that I do not know you, and that is not a night on which to learn. Do something for the club. Then say it again.'".
    On discuss { Assert pm_disbelieved(actor). }
  }
}

data/adventures/quittance/q_pip.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "Pip's Tin: a child on the top landing of a Salt Lane stair keeps a Lent coal that is going out; to sit up with it, or to carry it where a fire will love it, and what it is to be called.".

  // ── Pip's stair ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Everything happens on the top landing (pip_stair): the tin on the floor, the old woman in the chair across the
  // open door, the child on the boards. The coal's own clock is pt_dies_at(pt_pip), a watch: it is 384, the stroke
  // of midnight at the end of the third day (day(clock) is 1 on the first morning), and a rite can put it back a day.
  Measure pt_dies_at(group). Measure pt_carry_until(group).
  Initially Set pt_dies_at(pt_pip) to 384.
  Relation pt_lore(group). Relation pt_options_known(group). Relation pt_clock_known(group). Relation pt_named(group).
  Relation pt_consent(group). Relation pt_sat(group). Relation pt_rite_done(group). Relation pt_carried(group).
  Relation pt_saved(group). Relation pt_lost(group). Relation pt_wronged(group). Relation pt_trusted(group).
  Relation pt_kept_penny(group). Relation pt_kept_hearn(group). Relation pt_kept_glass(group). Relation pt_kept_gas(group).
  Relation pt_gifted(group). Relation pt_gift_asked(group). Relation pt_witnessing(group). Relation pt_gift_refused(group).
  Relation pt_told_pump(group). Relation pt_rite_failed(group). Relation pt_stair_bare(group).

  Discovery pt_claim "A child on the top of a Salt Lane stair keeps a coal in a tin and cannot keep it lit.".
  Discovery pt_pump_seen "Pip carries Mr Larkworth his dinner, and saw him chalk the pump in Candlewick Court.".

  Person pt_pip "Pip" at pip_stair {
    Role "nine years old, who keeps a coal in a tin". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner proud. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A child sits on the boards of the top landing with her knees up and her back against the doorpost, and a tin between her feet. She has the look of someone who has been told to guard a thing and has guarded it for a very long time. 'It's not for sale,' says Pip, 'and you can't have a look unless you say please.'".
    Greets again "'You,' says Pip, and moves her feet a little further round the tin.".
  }
  Person pt_gran "Hester Tamsett" at pip_stair {
    Role "Pip's grandmother, who has not left her chair in a month". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns she.
    Greets "An old woman sits in a kitchen chair set across the open door, wrapped to the chin in a blanket the colour of porridge. 'I am not dead,' says Hester Tamsett, 'though the stair has been told so. The child will not talk to you unless you say please. I mention it as a kindness.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Hester Tamsett, 'the polite ones.'".
  }

  Thing pt_tin "the tin" at pip_stair {
    State lit "A flat tin with a loose lid stands on the boards of the landing, and in it, under a skin of ash, a coal the size of a plum gives a dull red light that swells and shrinks as if it were being breathed. The tin is warm. The wood under it is not scorched.".
    State low "The tin on the boards has a coal in it the size of a thumb-joint. It is the colour of a plum, and when the draught moves it, it goes out of the corners of your eye and has to be looked for.".
    State steady "The tin on the landing holds a coal of a clear steady red, and a hand held over it feels warmth that does not come from fire alone. Pip has taken to sitting a little nearer to it.".
    State out "The tin on the boards holds a little grey ash, and a small black cinder that was a coal. There is no heat in it. Pip has not shut the lid.".
    State away "There is a pale square on the boards of the landing where a tin stood.".
  }
  Observe pt_tin_look near pt_tin when tried(pt_tin, looking) and (state(pt_tin, lit) or state(pt_tin, low) or state(pt_tin, steady)) "You get down beside the tin, with Pip's leave, which she gives like a coin she will want back. Under the ash the coal is not wood or coke or sea-coal. It has a grain in it, as of something that was once alive, and a faint glaze, and at the heart of it a seam of white that moves when you do not. Pip says: 'It listens.'".
  Observe pt_tin_ash near pt_tin when tried(pt_tin, looking) and state(pt_tin, out) "You get down beside the tin. In the ash is a cinder like a black bean, with a seam through it that was once white.".

  // ── The clock of the coal ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule pt_dims at pip_stair when watch(clock) + 96 >= pt_dies_at(pt_pip) and state(pt_tin, lit) says "The coal in the tin has shrunk to a plum-coloured thread, and Pip has stopped talking." {
    Assert state(pt_tin, low). }
  Rule pt_goes_out when watch(clock) >= pt_dies_at(pt_pip) and (state(pt_tin, low) or state(pt_tin, lit)) {
    Assert state(pt_tin, out). Assert pt_lost(party). }
  Observe pt_out_told at pip_stair when state(pt_tin, out) and not pt_gifted(party) "Pip sits with the tin in her lap and the lid off, and does not look up.".
  Rule pt_dies_carried when pt_carried(party) and watch(clock) >= pt_carry_until(party) says "The lid of the tin has stopped being warm. When you lift it the coal is a grey cinder, and the draught takes its ash. You were too slow with it." {
    Retract pt_carried(party). Assert pt_lost(party). }

  // ── The slate, and the stair ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe pt_slate at slip_room when day(clock) <= 3 and not pt_saved(party) and not pt_lost(party) "CLAIMS OPEN, in a child's capitals pasted over a corner of the Slate: WANTED. SOMEONE TO SIT WITH A FIRE. SALT LANE, TOP OF THE STAIR. PAYS NOTHING. ASK FOR PIP. Underneath, in the chalk boy's hand: 'Pays nothing' has been underlined twice, in admiration." teaches pt_claim.
  Objective pt_tin_obj when knows(party, pt_claim) and not pt_saved(party) and not pt_lost(party) "A coal in a tin at the top of a Salt Lane stair is going out, and a child will not let anyone but a polite person near it. It has until the end of the third day.".

  Topic pip_tin with pt_pip "Say please, and ask Pip about the tin" when true once {
    Says "Pip considers the please, and finds it genuine. 'It's Gran's,' she says. 'It was her mam's. I'm to keep it. It has to be kept in a tin because the stair is draughty, and you have to talk to it, only not much, because it gets embarrassed.' She looks at the tin. 'It's gone a bit small.'".
  }
  Topic pip_dinner with pt_pip "Ask Pip what she does when she is not minding the coal" when true once {
    Says "'I carry dinner,' says Pip. 'Mr Larkworth gives me a farthing a day to take him his pie at the rent-office and I'm not to look in the book. I don't. I look at the pump instead, in Candlewick, on the way. Somebody chalked a number on it on Tuesday, and Mr Larkworth was standing by it with the chalk. He said it was for the water-board.' She considers. 'There isn't a water-board.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, pt_pump_seen). }
  }
  Topic pip_part with pt_pip "Ask Pip whether the coal might be happier somewhere warmer" when knows(actor, d_lent_coal) and not pt_consent(actor) and not pt_carried(actor) and not state(pt_tin, away) once {
    Says "'It's happy here,' says Pip, in the voice of a person who has been told it is not. 'If it goes, it's not mine, and then it's nobody's, and Gran says a lent thing that's nobody's is the same as a stolen thing.' She holds the lid. 'Anyway, nobody here has one that's the same. It'd go off with strangers.'".
  }
  Action pt_talk_round(actor: group, site: place) "Sit down on the boards and talk Pip round to letting the coal go somewhere warmer" {
    Speaker pt_pip.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pt_pip, site) and at(actor, pip_stair) and knows(actor, d_lent_coal) and pt_options_known(actor) and not pt_consent(actor) and not pt_carried(actor) and not pt_wronged(actor) and (state(pt_tin, lit) or state(pt_tin, low)).
    Time 12 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert pt_consent(actor). }
    Result "You do not argue. You tell Pip what you saw in the tin, and what Gran said it would take, and you do not say that it will be all right, because it will not be, for her. Pip listens with her chin on her knees. 'I'd have to give it,' she says, at last. 'Not lose it.' She lifts the lid and looks, and shuts it. 'You can carry it. You hold it all the way, and you don't let it bump.'".
    Otherwise "Pip hears you out with the face of a magistrate. 'That's the worst I've heard this week,' she says, not unkindly, and sets the lid down, and sits on it.".
  }
  Action pt_promise_round(actor: group, site: place) "Promise Pip she shall be brought to see the coal wherever it is kept, if she will let it go" {
    Speaker pt_pip.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pt_pip, site) and at(actor, pip_stair) and knows(actor, d_lent_coal) and pt_options_known(actor) and not pt_consent(actor) and not pt_carried(actor) and not pt_wronged(actor) and (state(pt_tin, lit) or state(pt_tin, low)).
    Time 6 minutes.
    Grave "A promise to a child is a promise.".
    On success { Assert pt_consent(actor). Assert pt_promised(actor). }
    Result "'Properly brought?' says Pip. 'Not just told?' She puts out her hand, and you shake it, once. 'Then it can go,' she says. 'But it has to be somewhere I could walk to. I'm not allowed far.'".
  }
  Relation pt_promised(group).

  // ── Gran ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic gran_tin with pt_gran "Ask Hester Tamsett what is in the tin" when true once {
    Says "'What it looks like,' says Hester Tamsett. 'A coal. It came out of my mother's grate, and hers, and it goes back to a grate in a cellar I have never seen. We keep it in. That is the whole of the art: you do not sell it, and you do not let the Gas Company put a stove in the room.' She smiles, thinly. 'They have called twice. The second time they brought a man with a tape.'".
  }
  Topic gran_lent with pt_gran "Ask Hester Tamsett why she calls it a lent coal" when tried(pt_tin, looking) and not knows(actor, d_lent_coal) once {
    Says "'Because it is,' she says. 'Somebody lent it. You do not light a coal like that, child, you cannot; there is nothing in it you could light. It is given into a house to be kept, and a house that keeps it is not burned. That is what lent means. It means there is a lender.' She looks at the open door. 'My mother never said who. She said you were not to ask, it was rude, and that you were to be kind to it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, d_lent_coal). Assert pt_lore(actor). }
  }
  Topic gran_lent_again with pt_gran "Ask Hester Tamsett what a lent coal is" when knows(actor, d_lent_coal) and not pt_lore(actor) once {
    Says "'You have heard it said, I see,' says Hester Tamsett. 'In my mother's day it was said at every hearth in the Wards. A coal that is lent is not owned. It is kept, which is not the same, and it keeps you.'".
    On discuss { Assert pt_lore(actor). }
  }
  Topic gran_clock with pt_gran "Ask Hester Tamsett how long the coal has" when pt_lore(actor) once {
    Says "'Until the turn of the third day,' says Hester Tamsett, 'or so the way it has gone down this week tells me. Past that, it will not be a thing that can be asked of anyone. Somebody must sit with it; or it must be carried, and the child will not like that; or it will go out.' She is quite calm. 'I have buried a husband, a son and a daughter-in-law. I would like to bury nothing else this year.'".
    On discuss { Assert pt_clock_known(actor). }
  }
  Topic gran_carry with pt_gran "Ask Hester Tamsett where else it could be kept" when pt_clock_known(actor) once {
    Says "'Not by me, and not in this stair.' Hester Tamsett counts them off on the blanket with one bent finger, like a woman laying out cards. 'The Penny Mutual, in Salt Lane: poor and proud, which is the right sort. Old Hearn on the Hill, who knew about these things and has his own, if he still knows he has. The Wynne woman's glass, that does not let a thing go out. I do not say it lets it be.' The finger lifts. 'The Gas Company has furnaces that have not been out in thirty years, and no manners. I would not choose. Ask the coal.'".
    On discuss { Assert pt_options_known(actor). }
  }
  Topic gran_name_q with pt_gran "Ask Hester Tamsett what the coal wants" when pt_clock_known(actor) and not pt_named(actor) once {
    Says "'A name,' says Hester Tamsett. 'It has never had one, as we have never said one aloud; but it is dying, and a thing that is dying wants to be said. What is named is written down, somewhere, by someone. I do not know who. I would not like to choose.' She looks at you for some time. 'You are the ones who sat down. Will you?'".
  }
  Topic name_gran with pt_gran "Say that it is called for Hester, for the woman who kept it" answering gran_name_q when not pt_named(actor) {
    Says "'Hester,' says the old woman. For a moment she says nothing else. 'It is a plain name,' she says. 'I would have chosen worse.' The tin does not change; but Pip, on the boards, takes her thumb out of her mouth.".
    On discuss { Assert coalNamedGran(actor). Assert pt_named(actor). }
  }
  Topic name_pip with pt_gran "Say that it is called for Pip, who will keep it after" answering gran_name_q when not pt_named(actor) {
    Says "'Pip,' says the old woman. Pip, who has been pretending not to listen, goes the colour of the coal. 'Well,' says Hester Tamsett, 'that is a thing it will have to live up to.' In the tin, something shifts, with a small dry sound like a page turned.".
    On discuss { Assert coalNamedPip(actor). Assert pt_named(actor). }
  }
  Topic name_none with pt_gran "Say that it is not yours to name, and decline" answering gran_name_q when not pt_named(actor) {
    Says "The old woman looks at you for some time. 'No,' she says at last, 'it is not. I wondered if you would see that.' It is not clear whether she is pleased. 'It will do without. It has before.'".
    On discuss { Assert coalNamedNone(actor). Assert pt_named(actor). }
  }

  // ── Sitting with it ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Action pt_sit(actor: group, site: place) "Sit up with the coal through the night, until it takes" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, pip_stair) and (state(pt_tin, lit) or state(pt_tin, low)) and not pt_sat(actor) and not pt_carried(actor) and (hour(clock) >= 18 or hour(clock) < 3).
    Time 48.
    Grave "It will take the whole night, and you will not be anywhere else in it.".
    On success { Assert state(pt_tin, steady). Assert pt_sat(actor). Assert pt_saved(actor). Set pt_dies_at(pt_pip) to 9999. }
    Result "You sit on the boards with your backs to the wall and the tin between your feet. Hester Tamsett sleeps in her chair. Pip does not. Toward the second hour the coal is the colour of a plum, and you talk to it, as you were told, not much; toward the fourth, you hold your hands round it; at some time after the sixth you find that the room is warm, and the window has gone grey. The coal is a clear steady red. Pip is asleep against your arm with the lid in her fist.".
  }
  Action pt_rite(actor: group, site: place) "Say over the tin the old words for keeping a fire in" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, pip_stair) and (state(pt_tin, lit) or state(pt_tin, low)) and not pt_rite_done(actor) and not pt_rite_failed(actor) and knows(actor, d_lent_coal) and capable(actor, rites).
    Time 20 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, rites, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert pt_rite_done(actor). Increase pt_dies_at(pt_pip) by 144. Assert state(pt_tin, lit). }
    On failure { Assert pt_rite_failed(actor). }
    Result "You say what you know of a fire's keeping, which is the same in every country and no use at all in this one, and then you say it again more slowly, and leave out the parts that are for fires that are only fires. The coal goes red to the edges. It will not last. It has, you think, bought a day.".
    Otherwise "You say the words. The coal does nothing, courteously. 'It wants ours,' says Hester Tamsett from her chair. 'Not the words. The way of saying.'".
  }
  Topic gran_ways with pt_gran "Ask Hester Tamsett how the family says it" when pt_clock_known(actor) and not pt_rite_done(actor) once {
    Says "'We talk to it,' she says. 'Wipe your hands first. It likes a person who has wiped their hands. Tell it the day, and what the weather is, and who is dead.' She waves a hand. 'It is not liturgy. It is manners.'".
  }

  // ── Carrying it away ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Action pt_take_tin(actor: group, site: place) "Take up the tin with Pip's leave, to carry it where a fire will keep it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, pip_stair) and pt_consent(actor) and (state(pt_tin, lit) or state(pt_tin, low)) and not pt_carried(actor).
    Time 3 minutes.
    Grave "Pip's stair will have no fire on it.".
    On success { Assert state(pt_tin, away). Assert pt_carried(actor). Set pt_carry_until(actor) to watch(clock) + 36. Assert pt_stair_bare(actor). }
    Result "Pip puts the lid on, and holds it down with both hands, and then lets go. You lift the tin as you would lift a full cup. It is warm through the metal, and it ticks. 'Don't let it bump,' says Pip, from the doorpost.".
  }
  Action pt_lift_tin(actor: group, site: place) "While Pip is at the pump, lift the tin from the landing" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, pip_stair) and not pt_consent(actor) and not pt_carried(actor) and not pt_wronged(actor) and (state(pt_tin, lit) or state(pt_tin, low)) and capable(actor, stealth).
    Time 5 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On failure { Assert pt_wronged(actor). }
    On success { Assert state(pt_tin, away). Assert pt_carried(actor). Set pt_carry_until(actor) to watch(clock) + 36. Assert pt_wronged(actor). Assert pt_stair_bare(actor). Decrease regard(wardsfolk) by 1 or to nothing. Assert pm_slighted_wards(actor). }
    Result "Pip goes down for water, with the pail, and she is gone as long as it takes to count thirty-one stairs. You take the tin by its lid, which is the wrong end, and you are on the lane with it before the bucket has reached the pump. Behind you, from five floors up, a child's voice says the only word that she has, which is a name, and it is not yours.".
    Otherwise "A board speaks. 'I know what you are going to do,' says Hester Tamsett, from her chair, without opening her eyes. Pip, on the doorpost, has not taken her hand off the lid. Neither of them says anything more. They do not have to.".
  }


  // The places that will keep it: a coal laid on a grate that loves it. Each is a different thing to have done.
  Action pt_lay_penny(actor: group, site: place) "Lay Pip's coal on the Penny Mutual's grate" {
    Speaker pm_trendle.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pm_trendle, site) and at(actor, penny_hall) and pt_carried(actor) and (pm_proud(actor) or pm_loan(actor) or regard(wardsfolk) >= 2).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Retract pt_carried(actor). Assert pt_saved(actor). Assert pt_kept_penny(actor). Assert coalSource(penny_hall). Increase regard(wardsfolk) by 1. }
    Result "Keturah Trendle takes the tin in her two red hands and stands for a moment with it as a woman stands with a baby that is not hers. 'In Salt Lane,' she says. 'On our own grate. Let it be said that the Mutual kept it.' She rakes the ash, lays the coal, and the hearth takes it all at once, and the room leans toward it. 'The child may come,' she says, 'whenever she likes. She'll find the door open. We do not lock the fire.'".
  }
  Action pt_lay_hearn(actor: group, site: place) "Set Pip's tin in Auberon Hearn's hands, at the hearth-room" {
    Speaker auberon.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(auberon, site) and at(actor, hearn_hearth) and pt_carried(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Retract pt_carried(actor). Assert pt_saved(actor). Assert pt_kept_hearn(actor). Assert coalSource(hearn_hearth). }
    Result "The old man takes the lid off the tin and looks in, and for the length of three breaths his face is entirely his own. 'Oh,' says Auberon Hearn, 'from the Wards. It has that smell. They never stopped, you know, the poor.' He lays it, with his shaking fingers, in the bed of the little hearth beside the coal that is already there, and the two of them lean together like old friends in a doorway. 'Tell the child,' he says, 'that it is not alone.' Then he looks round, vaguely, and says, 'Honora?'".
  }
  Action pt_set_glass(actor: group, site: place) "Set Pip's tin among the green glass lamps in the Lamp-house shopfront" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, lamp_front) and pt_carried(actor).
    Time 8 minutes.
    Grave "The glass does not let a thing go out. It does not say it lets it be.".
    On success { Retract pt_carried(actor). Assert pt_saved(actor). Assert pt_kept_glass(actor). }
    Result "You set the coal in a spare globe of green glass at the end of a shelf, and shut the stopper, as the card beside it says. It does not go out. It will never now go out. It sits in its globe with its seam of white, perfectly steady, and a faint hum, in step with all the others on the shelf. After a while you realise it is the only thing in the room that is not humming in time.".
  }
  Action pt_lay_furnace(actor: group, site: place) "Feed Pip's coal into a retort-house furnace that has not been out in thirty years" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, retort_house) and pt_carried(actor).
    Time 8 minutes.
    On success { Retract pt_carried(actor). Assert pt_saved(actor). Assert pt_kept_gas(actor). Assert coalSource(retort_house). Increase regard(gasco) by 1. Decrease regard(wardsfolk) by 1 or to nothing. Assert pm_slighted_wards(actor). }
    Result "A stoker shows you the warmest oven, and does not ask. The cat on it gets up, looks into the tin, and goes out of the room with its tail very straight. The coal takes at once. It is a good fire, deep and fed, that nobody has ever let go out; and a stoker with a shovel says, with respect, 'That's old, that is,' and writes in the shift-book that a coal was received. It is on the Company's books now. Pip will not be able to walk here.".
  }
  Rule pt_promise_broken when pt_promised(party) and (pt_kept_hearn(party) or pt_kept_glass(party) or pt_kept_gas(party)) and not pt_wronged(party) { Assert pt_wronged(party). }
  Observe pt_reached_empty near pt_pip when pt_stair_bare(party) and (pt_kept_penny(party) or pt_kept_hearn(party) or pt_kept_glass(party) or pt_kept_gas(party)) "Pip is sitting by the pale square on the boards where the tin stood, drawing a tin on it with her finger. 'Is it warm?' she says. 'Where it is.'".

  // ── Afterwards ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule pt_trust_earned when pt_saved(party) and pt_named(party) and not pt_wronged(party) and not pt_trusted(party) { Assert pt_trusted(party). }
  Observe pt_trusted_greets near pt_pip when pt_trusted(party) and not pt_stair_bare(party) "Pip has moved her stool so that you can sit down. 'You can come in,' she says. 'You wiped your hands.'".
  Observe pt_wronged_greets near pt_pip when pt_wronged(party) "Pip looks past you, at a point on the wall. Her grandmother, from her chair, says 'The child is not at home.' The child is at home.".
  Observe pt_ash_greets near pt_gran when state(pt_tin, out) "Hester Tamsett has the tin in her lap, closed. She looks at you without any anger at all, which is worse.".
  Topic gran_ash with pt_gran "Say you are sorry about the coal" when state(pt_tin, out) once {
    Says "'It was never yours to be sorry for,' says Hester Tamsett. 'It was ours, and we kept it for ninety years, and a polite person is no use against ninety years of draught.' She is silent. 'There will be others in the Wards, I suppose. There always were. Tell them to wipe their hands.'".
    On discuss { Increase regard(wardsfolk) by 0. }
  }

  // The Night: Pip's coal, offered, or her word, offered, and not both. A child's hearth is bare after the one;
  // a child's day is gone after the other.
  Topic pip_gift_q with pt_pip "Ask Pip whether she would give her coal to the Return, if it is asked of her" when pt_trusted(party) and state(pt_tin, steady) and day(clock) >= 7 and not pt_gift_asked(actor) and not pt_witnessing(actor) once {
    Says "Pip thinks about it with her whole face. 'If I give it,' she says, 'I haven't got one. Gran says a house with no coal is a house with a door that anyone can open. And it doesn't come back; it goes home, with the rest.' She looks at her grandmother, who looks at the ceiling. 'But it asked for a name, and you gave it one. So it's yours a bit, as well.' She pulls the lid off. 'You can have it. But I'll have a cold hearth till it's back, and you're to say thank you properly.'".
    On discuss { Assert pt_gift_asked(actor). }
  }
  Action pt_accept_gift(actor: group, site: place) "Accept Pip's coal for the Night, and thank her properly" {
    Speaker pt_pip.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pt_pip, site) and at(actor, pip_stair) and pt_gift_asked(actor) and not pt_gifted(actor) and not pt_witnessing(actor) and quantity(actor, coal) < 2 and day(clock) >= 7.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Increase quantity(actor, coal) by 1. Set coalExpires(actor) to watch(clock) + 144. Assert pt_gifted(actor). Assert state(pt_tin, out). Increase regard(wardsfolk) by 1. }
    Result "You thank her, as you were told to, standing, with your hat in your hand, and you take the coal out of the tin into one of your own. She watches it go. The tin, with only ash in it, goes cold in her lap, and she holds it anyway. 'Say it's from me,' says Pip, 'when they ask.'".
  }
  Action pt_refuse_gift(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Pip to keep her coal; you will find another" {
    Speaker pt_pip.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pt_pip, site) and at(actor, pip_stair) and pt_gift_asked(actor) and not pt_gifted(actor) and not pt_gift_refused(actor).
    Time 3 minutes.
    On success { Assert pt_gift_refused(actor). Increase regard(wardsfolk) by 1. }
    Result "'Keep it,' you say. 'A house shouldn't be without.' Pip looks at you for some time, and puts the lid back with a small, formal click. 'That's the first time anyone's said so,' she says. 'Everyone says take it.'".
  }
  Topic pip_witness_q with pt_pip "Ask Pip whether she would tell the Five who chalked the pump" when pt_trusted(party) and knows(actor, pt_pump_seen) and not pt_witnessing(actor) and not pt_gifted(actor) once {
    Says "Pip looks at her grandmother. Her grandmother, who has not opened her eyes, says, 'It is not mine to say.' 'In the big hall?' says Pip. 'With the five chairs?' She has gone a bad colour. 'I'd have to sit in one. And say it, out loud, with people. And not be at the stair.' She picks at the lid. 'Who'd mind the coal?'".
  }
  Action pt_ask_witness(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Pip to say before the Five what she saw Mr Larkworth chalk" {
    Speaker pt_pip.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pt_pip, site) and at(actor, pip_stair) and pt_trusted(actor) and knows(actor, pt_pump_seen) and not pt_witnessing(actor) and not pt_gifted(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Grave "A child at the Five is a hard thing, and she will not be at her coal on the Night.".
    On success { Assert pt_witnessing(actor). Assert witness(pt_pip). }
    Result "Pip takes the lid off the tin, looks in, and puts it back before she answers. 'All right,' she says. 'But you sit next to me. And Gran has to be carried, she'll want to see.' She has gone very white, and very dignified. 'And you're to mind the coal,' she says, 'since I'll not be here to.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/quittance/q_queue.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "The Queue: the dead of the Burning, in line in the Exchange cellars to file claims ninety-four years late, the junior clerk who takes them down in secret, and the slag stair that every way down but the Flue must pass.".

  // qu_way: how the Queue was got by. 0 not yet . 1 a penny paid . 2 claims adjusted . 3 the office said (the dead sent home)
  // 4 a ticket and a wait . 5 pushed through.
  Measure qu_way(group). Measure qu_nerve(group). Measure qu_fairs(group). Measure qu_regard(group). Measure qu_called(group).
  Relation qu_ticket(group). Relation qu_pushed(group). Relation qu_released(group). Relation qu_hidden(group).
  Relation qu_ledger_stolen(group). Relation qu_register_given(group). Relation qu_rolled(group).
  Relation qu_asked(group). Relation qu_done(group). Relation qu_fair(group). Relation qu_fire_read(group).
  Relation qu_fire_receipted(group). Relation qu_slighted_fire(group). Relation qu_slighted_dead(group).
  Relation qu_penny(group).

  Discovery qu_claim "The dead of the Burning are queueing in the Exchange cellars to file claims, and a junior clerk is taking them down. A clerk is wanted who is not afraid of being thanked.".
  Discovery qu_descendant "Lettice Gorringe, a widow of the Burning, has a descendant: Mother Mawdsley, of the Mortmain almshouse.".

  Item qu_ledger "the Ledger of the Unpaid" is tench_ledger at nowhere.

  // ── The gate: the slag stair ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Thing qu_line "the Queue on the slag stair" on down_glass {
    State closed blocking "The dead stand on the head of the slag stair three abreast, politely, to the full width of it, and each holds out a scrap of paper. There is no pushing past them that does not go through someone.".
    State open "The dead have drawn aside to the walls of the stair, as people do for a funeral, and a gap runs down the middle of them to the glass.".
  }
  Rule qu_line_opens when queueOpen(party) and state(qu_line, closed) { Assert state(qu_line, open). }

  Observe qu_slate at slip_room when day(clock) <= 6 and not queueOpen(party) "CLAIMS OPEN: Exchange cellars. Persons unknown, in some numbers, standing. A clerk wanted who is not afraid of being thanked. The Exchange regrets that it has no record." teaches qu_claim.
  Objective qu_obj when knows(party, qu_claim) and not queueOpen(party) "The dead of the Burning are queueing in the Exchange cellars. Nobody goes down past them without answering them.".
  Objective an_obj when knows(party, an_claim) and an_status(party) < 2 "The Sovereign means to stop Mrs Oakes's annuity on Monday at noon, and seven people in the almshouse live on it.".
  Observe qu_arcade_note at cellar_arcade when not queueOpen(party) "Past the pillars the arch to the Queue's hall is open, and from it comes a sound you take for the draught, and which turns out, when you stop, to be several hundred people not coughing.".
  Observe qu_pushed_scene at queue_hall when qu_pushed(party) "The Queue has closed up behind you into a silence like a held breath. They are not hurt. They are offended, which is a great deal quieter.".
  Observe qu_released_scene at queue_hall when qu_released(party) "The hall is empty to the walls, and swept, as a church is after a funeral. The scraps of paper lie in a neat pile by the clerk's desk, tied, and a smell of candle-smoke goes slowly out through the arch.".
  Observe qu_settled_scene at queue_hall when qu_way(party) == 2 "The line is thinner than it was. The settled stand in a ring along the wall, tidy, in the manner of people who have had their affairs put in order and are not yet certain what to do with their hands.".
  Observe qu_desk at queue_hall when qu_nerve(party) >= 2 "The clerk's chair at the far end is not empty. Dobbin Tench sits in it, upright, with the ledger open, and a pen that he is no longer apologising with.".

  // ── Dobbin Tench, who grows a spine ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // qu_nerve: 0 apologetic . 1 asked, and answered . 2 sits in the chair, and will stand up in a Hall.
  Rule qu_tench_comes when qu_nerve(party) >= 1 and at(tench, cellar_arcade) { Assert at(tench, queue_hall). Retract at(tench, cellar_arcade). }
  Rule qu_register_nerve when qu_register_given(party) and qu_nerve(party) == 0 { Set qu_nerve(party) to 1. }

  Topic qu_tench_writing with tench "Ask Dobbin Tench what he is writing" when true once {
    Says "'Oh,' says Dobbin Tench, and puts a hand over the page, and then, seeing that this is the gesture of a man hiding something, takes it off again. 'Sums. A letter. It's nothing the Exchange would want to see, and I am sorry, I know that's the same as saying it is.' Behind him, in the hall beyond the arch, someone coughs politely, and several hundred people say 'Sh.'".
  }
  Topic qu_tench_cold with tench "Ask Tench whether he will speak to you" when qu_pushed(party) once {
    Says "'You went through them,' says Dobbin Tench, not looking up. 'I heard it from here. They said sorry, you know, all the way. They said sorry to you.' His pen goes on. 'I think you had better go on down. I don't think I can help you.'".
  }
  Topic qu_gor_cold with qu_gorringe "Ask Mrs Gorringe whether she holds the Queue's offence against you" when qu_pushed(party) once {
    Says "'I do not hold it,' says Mrs Gorringe. 'I have been holding things for ninety-four years; I have the habit. It is merely that I shall not now be able to say that the Phoenix's people were civil.' She does not look at you again.".
  }
  Action qu_tench_gently(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Tench, gently, what the book is that he keeps under his sleeve" {
    Speaker tench.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(tench, site) and not knows(actor, d_unpaid_ledger) and not qu_hidden(actor) and not qu_pushed(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, d_unpaid_ledger). }
    On failure { Assert qu_hidden(actor). }
    Result "Tench's shoulders come down by an inch. 'It's a ledger,' he says. 'It's the claims. They come to the desk when I'm at it and they say, would I mind, and I never have, and there are eleven hundred of them, and nobody has been paid. I put the date of the Burning against each one, and I leave the column that says PAID.' He turns the book so you can see it. 'It's empty. It's been empty the whole time.'".
    Otherwise "Tench goes pink, and tucks the book further up his sleeve, and says that it is nothing and that he is sorry, and you can see that he will go on saying so until you go away.".
  }
  Topic qu_tench_roll with tench "Ask Tench to call the roll aloud, as the first clerk of the Exchange would have" when knows(actor, d_unpaid_ledger) and qu_nerve(party) == 0 and not qu_pushed(party) and not qu_ledger_stolen(party) once {
    Says "'I couldn't,' says Tench. 'I'm only a junior.' He looks at you; you wait. He goes to the arch, and takes the book from his sleeve, and stands there with it for a time that is rather longer than you had expected. 'Abbott, Thomas,' he calls, in a small clear voice. 'Abbott, Mary. Abbott, Samuel.' And from the hall beyond, from eleven hundred throats, one after another, patient, a little hoarse with disuse, each in turn: 'Present.' It goes on past the first hundred, and the second. At the end of it Tench is standing a little straighter than at the start, though not, perhaps, as much as he thinks.".
    On discuss { Set qu_nerve(party) to 1. Assert qu_rolled(actor). }
  }
  Topic qu_tench_register with tench "Give Tench the sexton's register of the unclaimed" when holding(actor, an_register_k) once {
    Says "Tench opens the sexton's register on the desk and turns the pages with one finger. 'Forty-one,' he says. 'Forty-one with nobody to call them.' He gets out the ledger and, below the last name in it, he writes: And of the Unclaimed. 'Thank you,' he says. 'I'm sorry. I mean it. Nobody has ever brought me a name.' Then he writes a mark against each, for the sexton.".
    On discuss { Spend an_register from actor. Assert qu_register_given(actor). }
  }
  Action qu_tench_lift(actor: group) "Lift the book out of Tench's sleeve while he is writing" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, cellar_arcade) and at(tench, cellar_arcade) and not qu_hidden(actor) and not qu_ledger_stolen(actor) and qu_nerve(party) == 0 and not holding(actor, tench_ledger).
    Time 5 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Give qu_ledger to actor. Assert qu_ledger_stolen(actor). }
    On failure { Assert qu_hidden(actor). }
    Result "He is leaning to the next line with his tongue between his teeth. You have the ledger out of his sleeve like a letter out of a post-box. It is the weight of a short Bible. Tench does not look up until you are beyond the pillars, and then he does, and his hand goes slowly to the empty sleeve, and the whole of his face with it.".
    Otherwise "Tench turns at the wrong moment and puts his arm across the sleeve, in a movement so unlike him that he seems as startled as you are. 'No,' he says. 'No, I'm sorry. I don't think I can let you.' He sits with his back to you, and the ledger is not seen again.".
  }
  Topic qu_tench_ledger with tench "Ask Tench to let you carry the Ledger of the Unpaid up into the light" when qu_nerve(party) >= 2 and not holding(actor, tench_ledger) once {
    Says "Tench shuts the book. For a moment he holds it as if the answer were in it, and then he gets up from the chair, which he has not done in front of the Queue in ninety-four years, and holds it out. 'Take it,' he says. 'Eleven hundred. They are all in there, and some of them are children, and somebody ought to read it in a room where people can't say it's none of their business.' He draws a breath. 'I'll come. If it's a Hall, I'll stand up in it. I've had the practice.'".
    On discuss { Give qu_ledger to actor. Assert witness(tench). Assert knows(actor, d_unpaid_ledger). }
  }

  // ── The ways through ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Action qu_penny(actor: group) "Lay three coin on the nearest claim, a penny a head, and ask to be let by" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, queue_hall) and not queueOpen(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3.
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Assert queueOpen(actor). Set qu_way(actor) to 1. Assert qu_penny(actor). }
    Result "A woman in a Sunday bonnet looks at the three coins on her claim, and at you, and at the coins. 'Well,' she says, 'it is a penny.' There is a long, civil pause. 'Let them by, Mr Tench would say,' she says to the line, and the line, with great reluctance and perfect manners, draws in its skirts.".
  }
  Action qu_rite_known(actor: group) "Say the office for the dead over the Queue, and tell it that it has been heard, and may go home" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, queue_hall) and not queueOpen(actor) and capable(actor, rites) and knows(actor, d_unpaid_ledger).
    Time 30 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, rites, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert queueOpen(actor). Set qu_way(actor) to 3. Assert qu_released(actor). Increase qu_regard(actor) by 1. Assert at(qu_gorringe, nowhere). Assert at(qu_ned, nowhere). Assert at(qu_fluellen, nowhere). }
    Result "You say it, and you say that the claims are in a book, and that a clerk has them, and that it has been heard. The Queue listens with the deep attention of people who have been waiting for exactly this and cannot quite believe it is not a form. One by one, from the front, they say 'Thank you,' and put their scraps down at the clerk's desk, and are not there.".
    Otherwise "The Queue hears you out with great courtesy. 'That was very nice,' says a tall man at the front. 'Thank you. Will it be long?'".
  }
  Action qu_rite_blind(actor: group) "Say the office for the dead over the Queue, not knowing what it is waiting for" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, queue_hall) and not queueOpen(actor) and capable(actor, rites) and not knows(actor, d_unpaid_ledger).
    Time 30 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, rites, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert queueOpen(actor). Set qu_way(actor) to 3. Assert qu_released(actor). Assert at(qu_gorringe, nowhere). Assert at(qu_ned, nowhere). Assert at(qu_fluellen, nowhere). }
    Result "You say it without knowing what they are waiting for, and it is enough, narrowly. The Queue lets out a breath that is not a breath, and puts its scraps down in a heap. 'We were only waiting to be said to,' a small girl explains. The hall is empty.".
    Otherwise "The Queue says 'Amen' in a ragged mutter, the way people do who are polite to clergy, and does not move. 'We have a claim,' someone says, kindly, from the back. 'Is it that?'".
  }
  Action qu_ticket(actor: group) "Take a numbered ticket from the spike on the clerk's desk, and wait your turn" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, queue_hall) and not queueOpen(actor) and not qu_ticket(actor).
    Time 5 minutes.
    On success { Assert qu_ticket(actor). Set qu_called(actor) to watch(clock) + 144. }
    Result "The ticket is number 1,104 in a hand like a child's. 'Oh, you're very sensible,' says the man in front of you, who is 1,103. 'They'll call you in a day, or thereabouts. They always call, in the end.'".
  }
  Rule qu_called_rule when qu_ticket(party) and watch(clock) >= qu_called(party) and not queueOpen(party) says "At the far end of the hall, where the chair is empty, a voice that is nobody's calls: 'Eleven hundred and four.' The line parts as for a bride, and the dead, who have nothing in the world to do but wait, look at you with real affection." {
    Assert queueOpen(party). Set qu_way(party) to 4. Retract qu_ticket(party). }
  Action qu_push(actor: group) "Put your shoulder to the Queue, and go through it to the slag stair" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, queue_hall) and not queueOpen(actor).
    Grave "The dead are not hurt by it. They are offended, and they will remember, and so will whoever is waiting for them below.".
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert queueOpen(actor). Set qu_way(actor) to 5. Assert qu_pushed(actor). Assert qu_slighted_dead(actor). Assert qu_slighted_fire(actor). Decrease qu_regard(actor) by 2 or to nothing. }
    Result "You go through them. It is like walking into a cold wet sheet hung to dry, and a cold wet sheet that says 'Oh,' and 'I beg your pardon,' and 'There is a queue,' in small hurt voices, one after another, all the way to the stair. At the end you look back. Nobody has moved. They are all looking at you with the terrible patience of the wronged.".
  }
  Rule qu_adjusted when qu_fairs(party) >= 4 and qu_way(party) == 0 and not queueOpen(party) says "The line gives a sound like a page turning. 'Mr Tench,' says Mrs Gorringe, 'they have done it properly.' At the foot of the slag stair the dead step back to the wall." {
    Assert queueOpen(party). Set qu_way(party) to 2. Increase regard(sovereign) by 1. }

  // ── The claimants ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person qu_gorringe "Mrs Gorringe" at queue_hall {
    Role "a widow of the Burning, with a claim for furniture". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A woman in black bombazine, quite upright, holds out a long claim in a hand that does not shake because it has nothing in it to shake with. 'Gorringe,' she says. 'Lettice, relict of Josiah. Furniture. I have been waiting since the fourth of October.'".
    Greets again "'Still here,' says Mrs Gorringe, with some dignity.".
  }
  Person qu_ned "Ned Pounceby" at queue_hall {
    Role "a boy of seven, with a claim for boots". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A very small boy at the front of the line looks at you with enormous interest and holds up a piece of paper by one corner. 'I'm Ned,' he says. 'My mother says I'm to wait for the Phoenix. It's about my boots.'".
    Greets again "'Hello,' says Ned.".
  }
  Person qu_fluellen "Mr Fluellen" at queue_hall {
    Role "a claimant for a house". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner proud. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A broad man in a velvet collar says, without being asked, 'Fluellen. Freeholder. Number nine, Cutler's Row. I shall want the Phoenix's man, or the Phoenix's man's superior. Is that you?'".
    Greets again "'You again,' says Mr Fluellen. 'Have you the Phoenix's man?'".
  }
  Person qu_crumpe "Mr Crumpe" at queue_hall {
    Role "a claimant for his own death, in good health". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner acerbic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A thin, vigorous old man in a very good muffler is stamping his feet to keep warm. This is an eccentric thing to do in a line of the dead, and his breath is showing, which theirs does not. 'Crumpe,' he says. 'Policy forty-four seventeen. Death benefit. You'll be the Sovereign, I hope.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Mr Crumpe. 'The Sovereign, at last?'".
  }
  Person qu_creditor "the Creditor" at queue_hall {
    Role "a claimant from further down, who is last in the line". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns it.
    Seen when knows(viewer, d_unpaid_ledger).
    Greets "At the very end of the line, after the last of the dead, there is a figure that is not the colour of candle-smoke. It is the colour of the inside of a stove. It holds out a claim, with the same patience as the rest, and the paper in its hand is faintly brown at the corners.".
    Greets again "The figure at the end of the line holds out the claim again, with the same patience.".
  }

  // Mrs Gorringe, widow: the claim is for furniture, the grievance is for the name on the policy.
  Topic qu_gor_ask with qu_gorringe "Ask Mrs Gorringe what she is claiming" when true once {
    Says "'Forty pounds,' says Mrs Gorringe. 'A sideboard, six chairs, a clock, the table where I laid out my own dead.' She considers. 'I do not want the sideboard. It was my mother's and it was ugly. The policy was in Josiah's name, and when they came to pay, the Phoenix paid his brother, who had not sat at that table in ten years. I should like it written that it was my house.' She says it lightly, as one says the thing one has been practising for ninety-four years.".
    On discuss { Assert qu_asked(qu_gorringe). Assert knows(actor, d_unpaid_ledger). }
  }
  Topic qu_gor_full with qu_gorringe "Allow the claim in full: forty pounds, for the furniture" when qu_asked(qu_gorringe) and not qu_done(qu_gorringe) once {
    Says "'Forty pounds,' says Mrs Gorringe, in a voice of ice. 'For a sideboard I called ugly. I do not wish to be bought a sideboard. I wished to be believed about a table.' She withdraws the claim and folds it small. The line behind her says nothing, with great conviction.".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_gorringe). Assert qu_slighted_dead(actor). Decrease qu_regard(actor) by 1 or to nothing. }
  }
  Topic qu_gor_valued with qu_gorringe "Allow the furniture at the valuer's twelve pounds" when qu_asked(qu_gorringe) and not qu_done(qu_gorringe) once {
    Says "'The valuer,' says Mrs Gorringe, 'was a Phoenix man. I am happy to be told it is twelve pounds. I am not happy to be told by him.' She looks at you without expression. 'You have settled a claim, I see. It is the one I do not have.'".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_gorringe). Assert qu_slighted_dead(actor). Decrease qu_regard(actor) by 1 or to nothing. }
  }
  Topic qu_gor_name with qu_gorringe "Enter her as the householder of record, and allow the claim in her own name" when qu_asked(qu_gorringe) and not qu_done(qu_gorringe) once {
    Says "You write it, in the margin of her claim, in your own hand: LETTICE GORRINGE, HOUSEHOLDER. The ink takes. 'Ah,' says Mrs Gorringe. Her mouth moves, once, as a mouth does that has been shut on a word since the Burning. 'I shall not want the forty pounds,' she says. 'A shilling for the table, if you would. For the principle.' You pay it, and she folds the claim into her glove with a look of rather terrible satisfaction.".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_gorringe). Assert qu_fair(qu_gorringe). Increase qu_fairs(actor) by 1. Increase qu_regard(actor) by 1. }
  }
  Topic qu_gor_kin with qu_gorringe "Tell Mrs Gorringe that her great-granddaughter, Mother Mawdsley, keeps the almshouse day-room at Mortmain, and has not forgotten her" when knows(actor, qu_descendant) and not qu_done(qu_gorringe) once {
    Says "'Mawdsley,' says Mrs Gorringe. 'Which Mawdsley? Ah.' She sits down on nothing, in the way of the dead, with a movement that has a good deal of the ordinary in it. 'And she has a stove, and a day-room, and she tells people about me.' The claim comes out of her glove and is held a little away. 'Then it is paid,' she says. 'I wished to be told that I was somebody's. I have been told.'".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_gorringe). Assert qu_fair(qu_gorringe). Increase qu_fairs(actor) by 1. Increase qu_regard(actor) by 1. }
  }
  Topic qu_gor_tench with qu_gorringe "Ask Tench to settle Mrs Gorringe's claim himself" when qu_nerve(party) == 1 and not qu_done(qu_gorringe) and not qu_pushed(party) once {
    Says "Tench takes the claim in both hands. 'I couldn't,' he says. 'I'm only a junior.' Nobody tells him he isn't. He goes up the hall, past eleven hundred of the dead, and sits down in the clerk's chair at the far end, which has been empty since the fire, and picks up a pen. 'Mrs Gorringe,' he says, 'I have your claim. I find that the policy was in your husband's name, and that the house was yours.' His voice shakes on the last word and then does not. 'Lettice Gorringe, householder. It is allowed.' It goes through the Queue like a thaw.".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_gorringe). Assert qu_fair(qu_gorringe). Increase qu_fairs(actor) by 1. Increase qu_regard(actor) by 1. Set qu_nerve(party) to 2. }
  }

  // Ned Pounceby, seven, boots.
  Topic qu_ned_ask with qu_ned "Ask Ned about his boots" when true once {
    Says "'They were new,' says Ned. 'I had them on on the Saturday, for the first time, and my mother said not to go out in them, and I did, and then the fire came.' He looks down at his feet. They are bare, and the colour of candle-smoke. 'The Phoenix is going to give me some more. I've got a paper.' He holds it up by its corner. It has a number on it and a drawing of a boot.".
    On discuss { Assert qu_asked(qu_ned). Assert knows(actor, d_unpaid_ledger). }
  }
  Topic qu_ned_away with qu_ned "Tell him a claim is no matter for a child, and send him back to his mother" when qu_asked(qu_ned) and not qu_done(qu_ned) once {
    Says "'She's behind the lady in the green,' says Ned. 'She said I'm not to move.' He looks at the paper, and then at you, and goes back to the line with it folded very small, and his shoulders go in the way of a child who has been told that this is not a place for him.".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_ned). Assert qu_slighted_dead(actor). Decrease qu_regard(actor) by 1 or to nothing. }
  }
  Topic qu_ned_schedule with qu_ned "Allow the claim at the Phoenix's schedule for juvenile footwear, twelve shillings, to be paid to his mother" when qu_asked(qu_ned) and not qu_done(qu_ned) once {
    Says "'Twelve shillings,' says Ned, who does not know what they are. 'I don't want shillings. I want boots.' Behind the lady in the green, a woman's voice, thin with the effort of not interrupting, says, 'Ned, mind your manners,' and he says 'Thank you,' to you, and goes quiet.".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_ned). Assert qu_slighted_dead(actor). Decrease qu_regard(actor) by 1 or to nothing. }
  }
  Topic qu_ned_boots with qu_ned "Pay a coin for the boots, and set the pair down at his feet" when qu_asked(qu_ned) and not qu_done(qu_ned) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 1 once {
    Says "You put the coin on his paper, and say that it is for the boots, and the paper fills, quietly, with the drawing of a boot. And there they are on the floor: small, brown, a little scuffed at the toes, with the laces already done up. 'Oh,' says Ned. He sits down on the stone and puts them on, one at a time, with the concentration of a child, and stands up in them and stamps. 'They fit,' he says. Behind the lady in the green a woman is crying, slowly, in the manner of someone who has been waiting to.".
    On discuss { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Assert qu_done(qu_ned). Assert qu_fair(qu_ned). Increase qu_fairs(actor) by 1. Increase qu_regard(actor) by 1. }
  }

  // Mr Fluellen, who claims a house that was never his.
  Topic qu_flu_ask with qu_fluellen "Ask Mr Fluellen what he is claiming" when true once {
    Says "'Number nine, Cutler's Row,' says Mr Fluellen, 'freehold, four hundred pounds, with a view.' From further down the line, at about the volume of a remark not meant to be overheard, a stout woman in curl-papers says, 'He was my lodger.' 'The first floor,' Fluellen says, without turning, 'was in my keeping.' 'A pound a quarter,' the woman says. 'And a clock that was mine.'".
    On discuss { Assert qu_asked(qu_fluellen). Assert knows(actor, d_unpaid_ledger). }
  }
  Topic qu_flu_full with qu_fluellen "Allow the house at four hundred pounds, and let the landlady make what she can of it" when qu_asked(qu_fluellen) and not qu_done(qu_fluellen) once {
    Says "'Four hundred,' says Mr Fluellen, and takes a step back, and looks at the stout woman, who has stopped speaking. A sound goes through the line like a rustle in a hedge. 'I do not think,' he says, after a time, very quietly, 'that I could take that.' He leaves the claim on the floor, and walks to the wall, and stands there with his collar up.".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_fluellen). Assert qu_slighted_dead(actor). Decrease qu_regard(actor) by 1 or to nothing. }
  }
  Topic qu_flu_refuse with qu_fluellen "Refuse the claim, and tell him he is not the householder" when qu_asked(qu_fluellen) and not qu_done(qu_fluellen) once {
    Says "'I see,' says Mr Fluellen, and his chin goes up, and he looks past you at the arch, with the particular expression of a man who has lost a house for the second time. 'I had expected rather more of the Phoenix.'".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_fluellen). Assert qu_slighted_dead(actor). Decrease qu_regard(actor) by 1 or to nothing. }
  }
  Topic qu_flu_lease with qu_fluellen "Allow him the tenant's interest: a quarter's rent and the cost of removing a clock" when qu_asked(qu_fluellen) and not qu_done(qu_fluellen) once {
    Says "You write: FLUELLEN, O., TENANT OF THE FIRST FLOOR, ONE QUARTER, ONE CLOCK. Mr Fluellen reads it three times, with his lips moving. 'It was a good first floor,' he says at last. 'It had a view.' He folds the claim. 'I shall tell people that I had the freehold,' he says, 'in the proper place.' The stout woman, nine places down, says 'He was always a gentleman, mind,' with great warmth. 'The clock was a good clock.'".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_fluellen). Assert qu_fair(qu_fluellen). Increase qu_fairs(actor) by 1. Increase qu_regard(actor) by 1. }
  }

  // Mr Crumpe, who is not dead.
  Topic qu_cru_ask with qu_crumpe "Ask Mr Crumpe what he is claiming" when true once {
    Says "'Death benefit,' says Mr Crumpe. 'Policy forty-four seventeen, the Sovereign Mutual. I have paid the premium on the quarter-day since the year of the Jubilee. I came to the Exchange to inquire about the cover, and was told there was a queue, and joined it, and I will say this for the dead: they are the most civil people I have ever stood in a line with. No one has called my number.' He stops stamping. 'I believe,' he says, 'that I have a pulse.'".
    On discuss { Assert qu_asked(qu_crumpe). Assert knows(actor, d_unpaid_ledger). }
  }
  Topic qu_cru_pay with qu_crumpe "Allow the death benefit, and pay it" when qu_asked(qu_crumpe) and not qu_done(qu_crumpe) once {
    Says "'In the event of my decease,' reads Mr Crumpe, slowly. He looks at the sum. He looks at his hands, which are shaking with cold. The Queue behind him makes a sound like a pew full of people not saying anything. 'I do not think I can take it,' he says, 'while I am still using it.' He gives the claim back and goes to stand against the wall, with the air of a man who has been offered his own funeral.".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_crumpe). Assert qu_slighted_dead(actor). Decrease qu_regard(actor) by 1 or to nothing. }
  }
  Topic qu_cru_wait with qu_crumpe "Take his number from him, and tell him his turn will come" when qu_asked(qu_crumpe) and not qu_done(qu_crumpe) once {
    Says "'It has been forty years,' says Mr Crumpe, with great restraint, 'and my turn has not come, and I do not think it will, and I think you know that.' He gives you the number. It is still warm from his hand.".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_crumpe). Assert qu_slighted_dead(actor). Decrease qu_regard(actor) by 1 or to nothing. }
  }
  Topic qu_cru_home with qu_crumpe "Tell Mr Crumpe he is not dead, and show him the stair" when qu_asked(qu_crumpe) and not qu_done(qu_crumpe) once {
    Says "'Not,' says Mr Crumpe. He sits down. The Queue, to a man, has taken a half-step toward him, and the lady beside him puts a hand that is not there on his sleeve. 'Forty years,' he says. 'I have been thinking I was a very patient man.' He stands, and shakes your hand, and the dead shake it after him, one by one, some of them twice. 'I shall go to Mortmain,' says Mr Crumpe at the arch, 'and ask a Mr Cray what a living man is owed, on policy forty-four seventeen. I believe I shall enjoy it.'".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_crumpe). Assert qu_fair(qu_crumpe). Increase qu_fairs(actor) by 1. Increase qu_regard(actor) by 1. Assert at(qu_crumpe, cellar_arcade). }
  }

  // The Creditor: the Fire files a claim, as a creditor, for hospitality given and not repaid.
  Topic qu_fire_read with qu_creditor "Take the claim the Creditor holds out, and read it" when knows(actor, d_unpaid_ledger) once {
    Says "The paper is warm, and the hand is a clerk's hand, round and wasting nothing. FOR HOSPITALITY GIVEN AND NOT REPAID: ONE HEARTH, THROUGH NINETY-FOUR WINTERS; TO THE HOUSE OF THE FOUNDERS, AND THE CITY THAT WAS BUILT ON IT, AND THE POLICY THAT SAYS SO. THE SUM IS LEFT TO THE DEBTOR. A hot thumb-print, as for a seal, sits at the foot of it. It reads like a policy turned inside out: not what is owed to the burned, but by whom.".
    On discuss { Assert qu_fire_read(actor). Assert knows(actor, d_tithe_debt). }
  }
  Topic qu_fire_refuse with qu_creditor "Refuse the claim as ninety-four years out of time" when qu_fire_read(actor) and not qu_done(qu_creditor) once {
    Says "The Creditor takes the claim back. It does not argue. Where its thumb was, the paper has curled and blackened, and a smell of singed cloth goes down the line to the stair, and all the dead turn their heads, once, in the direction of the floor.".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_creditor). Assert qu_slighted_fire(actor). }
  }
  Topic qu_fire_penny with qu_creditor "Offer a penny on the claim, to be going on with" when qu_fire_read(actor) and not qu_done(qu_creditor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 1 once {
    Says "The Creditor looks at the coin, and then at you, and there is a long moment during which the nearest of the dead take a step back. The penny, when you look, has run flat on the stone, and is red, and cooling. 'It is noted,' says a voice from a long way under the floor, mildly. It does not sound pleased.".
    On discuss { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Assert qu_done(qu_creditor). Assert qu_slighted_fire(actor). }
  }
  Topic qu_fire_receipt with qu_creditor "Write a receipt: 'Received of the Hearth, one claim for hospitality; not refused; to be answered at the Night'" when qu_fire_read(actor) and not qu_done(qu_creditor) once {
    Says "You write it, and sign it, and the Creditor reads it with its head on one side. It is the first receipt anyone has given it. It folds the paper and holds it against its chest, and for a moment the whole hall is warm, and the dead, who have not felt the heat of anything in ninety-four years, make a sound like people who have just been let into the kitchen. 'It will be answered,' the Creditor says, in a voice like an oven door. It goes down the slag stair ahead of you, and its footprints, in the glass, are faintly lit.".
    On discuss { Assert qu_done(qu_creditor). Assert qu_fair(qu_creditor). Assert qu_fire_receipted(actor). Increase qu_fairs(actor) by 1. Increase qu_regard(actor) by 1. }
  }
}

data/adventures/quittance/q_surveyor.kyr:
Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "The Surveyor's Daughter: Ianthe Corbett of the Lamprey's friends has measured the Pargeters' house in Dyers' Alley twice and has not written the Decline. Tobias Pargeter of the Phoenix's brigade has not been told. Three assignations are to be contrived, and a rule to be bent or kept.".

  // ══ The Surveyor's Daughter (prefix sd_) ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // The Corbetts are the Lamprey's friends (a fish over their door); the Pargeters are the Phoenix's (nine of them in blue).
  // Ianthe has measured 4 Dyers' Alley: the flue has cracked in the party wall it shares with the die-works. The Rule says
  // Decline; Declined, the Pargeters lose their cover, and a fireman whose own house is uninsured is struck off.
  // Ianthe and Tobias keep hours (rules below). Three assignations each warm her by one:
  //   1 the lantern gallery at dusk (a ladder, or a climber) . 2 the Guild's model by day (a fireman is not admitted)
  //   3 the householders' drill on the third day at ten (a ladder pin slipped, or a pump-handle wrenched).
  // How she comes to decide (arc(ianthe) 0 -> 1): an example (the Hargreave Rider), or Tobias's honesty on the roof, or time
  // (the Guild's list closes at noon on the fifth day and she writes the Decline alone). Never pressure.
  // Writes: arc(ianthe), d_decline_roll, roll_extract (Give), witness(ianthe), tobiasWilling(party), keeper(hill),
  //   regard(brigades), regard(city) (down on a forgery).
  // Names for the Hearing: sd_end_honest, sd_end_declined, sd_end_exiled, sd_end_forged, sd_end_apart, sd_slighted_guild.
  // Needs (asked of the lead): `Uses go. Plans 14 steps.` on ianthe and tobias in people.kyr, so that these hours can be
  // Pursuits that the company meets on the road; as it stands they are rules (friction/sd.md).

  Place sd_lantern "the lantern gallery" is room within hill at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place sd_roof "the Corbetts' roof" is room within hill at 3, 1 outdoors.
  Kind sd_ladder_k "a surveyor's folding ladder" is gear worth 3 weighing 2 described "Twelve feet of ash, on hinges, with the Guild's stamp on the stile and a card tied to the top: NOT TO BE USED FOR LOVE.".
  Item sd_ladder "the Guild's folding ladder" is sd_ladder_k at nowhere.
  Item sd_extract "an extract of the Surveyors' Roll" is roll_extract at nowhere.
  Thing sd_rungs "the way up to the lantern gallery" at belvedere {
    State drawn_up "A drainpipe, a ledge, and above them the lantern gallery with its rail, ten feet over the parapet. There are no rungs on the pipe.".
    State set "A ladder stands against the lantern gallery's rail.".
    Change climb "Go up the drainpipe to the lantern gallery and let a line down" from drawn_up to set needing climbing.
    Change ladder "Set the Guild's ladder against the lantern gallery" from drawn_up to set needing sd_ladder_k.
  }
  Passage sd_up "the way up to the lantern gallery" is steps between belvedere and sd_lantern opening when state(sd_rungs, set) "The lantern gallery is ten feet over the parapet and nothing reaches it.".
  Passage sd_drill_ladder "the drill ladder against the Corbetts' roof" is steps between hill_street and sd_roof opening when sd_drill() "The Corbetts' roof is a long way up." opening when not sd_stranded(party) "The drill ladder has gone down in the street, and is not going up again.".
  Thing sd_pin "the drill ladder's foot-pin" at hill_street {
    State fast "A long drill ladder lies along the Corbetts' railing, its foot pinned to an iron shoe with a pin no thicker than a cork.".
    State slipped "The ladder has been taken from its shoe: the pin lies in the gutter where it was dropped.".
    Change slip "Draw the pin from the drill ladder's shoe, while the sergeant looks at the sky" from fast to slipped needing stealth.
  }
  Thing sd_pump "the drill engine's pump-handle" at hill_street {
    State steady "The Phoenix pump stands at the kerb with its handle chained to a stanchion, and a hose, as thick as a man's leg, coiled at its foot. A notice on the Corbetts' railing: HOUSEHOLDERS' DRILL, THE THIRD DAY, AT TEN. NOT TO BE TOUCHED.".
    State burst "The hose has split from end to end, and the street is wet to the Corbetts' step.".
    Change wrench "Throw your weight on the pump-handle against the sergeant's count" from steady to burst needing brawn.
  }
  Thing sd_flue "the Pargeters' flue" at dyers_alley {
    State cracked "Along the party wall of 4 Dyers' Alley, where the die-works fire-pot stands against it, the brick has cracked from cornice to coping, and a pencil line has been run alongside it by someone who has measured it twice.".
    State mended "The Pargeters' flue has been relined in firebrick, with new mortar still green. A pencilled date has been added by the old line: MENDED.".
    Change rebuild "Take down the cracked course of the party wall and rebuild it in firebrick" from cracked to mended needing brawn.
    Change reline "Re-line the flue with a sleeve of sheet iron and lute it with clay" from cracked to mended needing trapwork.
  }
  Thing sd_survey "the Pargeters' survey" at corbett_study {
    State blank "On the plan-chest lies the survey of 4 Dyers' Alley, in a clean hand, measured twice, with one line in the verdict left blank, and a pencil laid across it.".
    State declined "The Pargeters' survey lies on the plan-chest, the verdict written: DECLINED, and signed.".
    State rider "The Pargeters' survey lies on the plan-chest: PASSED, subject to repair, on the Hargreave Rider, and signed.".
    State forged "The Pargeters' survey lies on the plan-chest: PASSED, in a hand that is very nearly hers.".
  }

  Measure sd_warmth(group). Relation sd_beat1(group). Relation sd_beat2(group). Relation sd_beat3(group). Relation sd_cleared(group).
  Relation sd_t_invited(group). Relation sd_t_out(group). Relation sd_tobias_knows(group). Relation sd_stranded(group).
  Relation sd_public(group). Relation sd_rider_offered(group). Relation sd_elope_plan(group). Relation sd_gone(group).
  Relation sd_caught(group). Relation sd_end_honest(group). Relation sd_end_declined(group). Relation sd_end_exiled(group).
  Relation sd_end_forged(group). Relation sd_end_apart(group). Relation sd_slighted_guild(group). Relation sd_pargeters_uncovered(group).
  Relation sd_roof_honest(group). Relation sd_ladder_lent(group). Relation sd_sent_on(group).
  Query sd_drill_morning() means day(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 12.
  Query sd_drill() means day(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) < 12 and not at(ianthe, bakehouse).
