  Observe bethan_tired near bethan when not bethanAtPeace(bethan) and not dark() "Old Bethan's eyes are red at the rims, and twice while you watch she starts to nod over the eels and jerks awake.".
  Topic bethan_bell with bethan "Ask Old Bethan about the bell under the water" when true once {
    Says "'The bell.' She kills an eel, neatly, with the back of a knife. 'They'll tell you it's the drowned. Lir's church went down with the lower town the night the hill went up, and the sexton with it, and he's been at his rope two hundred years.' Another eel. 'My Ned went out after mackerel in the January blow and the sea kept him. Never come ashore. Not a button.' She wipes the knife. 'And twice a day, at the turn, that bell. And every time I think it's for him. And it isn't. It's for nobody. And I've to go on thinking it, twice a day, morning and night, and I haven't slept since Candlemas.' She looks at you. 'Eel pie?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bell_grief). }
  }
  Discovery bell_grief "Old Bethan's husband, Ned Saltash, was lost at sea in January and never came ashore. Twice a day, at the turn of the tide, the bell under the bay rings, and every time she thinks it rings for him; she has not slept since Candlemas.".
  Topic peg_bell with peg "Ask Peg Arklow who rings the bell under the water" when true once {
    Says "'The drowned.' She says it the way you'd say the post. 'Lir's sexton, still at his rope. My gran said so, and hers did.' She leans on the bar. 'Mind, my gran also said the merfolk ate children, and there's one of theirs comes up the Fish Stairs every morning and sells cockles to the children, so.'".
  }
  // Ha'penny tells it plainly, being the one who rings it.
  Topic hapenny_bell with hapenny "Ask Ha'penny about the bell in the drowned church" when true once {
    Says "'The bell!' Ha'penny's whole face lights up, gills and all. 'We ring it. Me and Shutters and Cash Only and all of us. You swim up the tower and you get hold of the rope and you hang off it, and it goes BONG and you go up with it, and it goes BONG again and you come down.' She demonstrates, with her whole body, on the step. 'At the turn, when the water swings. It's the best noise in the Whelm.' She stops. 'Can you hear it up here?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bell_ringers). }
  }
  Discovery bell_ringers "The bell under the bay is rung by the merfolk children, Ha'penny among them, who hang off its rope at the turn of the tide for the noise.".
  Relation hapennySorry(group).
  Topic hapenny_told_bethan with hapenny "Tell Ha'penny about Old Bethan, who cannot sleep for the bell" when knows(actor, bell_grief) and knows(actor, bell_ringers) and not hapennySorry(hapenny) once {
    Says "Ha'penny goes very still on the step, and then she puts her cockles down. 'We didn't know,' she says. 'Nobody told us anybody heard.' Her gills open and shut. 'Is she the little one with the eels? She gives me the heads.' She looks at the water, as if the bell were looking back. 'We could stop.' A pause. 'Or we could ring it for him. Properly. Once. So he'd know.' She looks up at you. 'Which would she want?'".
    On discuss { Assert hapennySorry(hapenny). }
  }
  Topic hapenny_stop with hapenny "Ask Ha'penny to stop ringing the bell" answering hapenny_told_bethan when hapennySorry(hapenny) and not bellStopped(sennet_bay) and not bellForNed(sennet_bay) once {
    Says "'All right.' She says it sadly, the way a child gives up a stick. 'I'll tell the others. Cash Only will cry. He always cries.' She slides off the step into the water up to her chin. 'Tell her sorry. From the bell.'".
    On discuss { Assert bellStopped(sennet_bay). }
  }
  Topic hapenny_ring with hapenny "Ask Ha'penny to ring the bell once, at the evening tide, for Ned Saltash" answering hapenny_told_bethan when hapennySorry(hapenny) and not bellStopped(sennet_bay) and not bellForNed(sennet_bay) once {
    Says "'Once.' She nods hard. 'Ned Saltash. Once, at the turn, and slow, and then nobody touches it.' She says the name over to herself twice, to keep it. 'You tell her to be on the Quay. You tell her it's for him.'".
    On discuss { Assert bellForNed(sennet_bay). }
  }
  Relation bethanWaiting(group).
  Topic bethan_told_ring with bethan "Tell Old Bethan the bell will be rung once at the evening tide, for Ned, and then not again" when bellForNed(sennet_bay) and not bellRungForNed(sennet_bay) and not bethanWaiting(bethan) once {
    Says "She does not say anything for a while. She covers the eels with a wet sack. 'Who by?' You tell her. 'A merfolk child.' She laughs, once, short. 'Ned would like that. He used to throw them his crusts.' She takes off one of the shawls and folds it and puts it back on. 'The evening tide. On the Quay.' She nods at nothing. 'I'll be there.'".
    On discuss { Assert bethanWaiting(bethan). }
  }
  Rule bethan_waits when bethanWaiting(bethan) and hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 19 and not bellRungForNed(sennet_bay) and not at(bethan, quay) { Assert at(bethan, quay). }
  Rule bell_for_ned at quay when bellForNed(sennet_bay) and bethanWaiting(bethan) and hour(clock) == 18 and not bellRungForNed(sennet_bay)
    says "At the turn of the evening tide the harbour goes quiet, the way it does, and out in the bay under the water the bell rings once: slow, and deep, and a long time dying. Then nothing. Old Bethan is standing at the edge of the Quay in her three shawls with her hands folded. 'Ned Saltash,' she says, not loud, to the water. Then she turns round and goes home, with the barrow, at six in the evening, which nobody on the Quay has seen her do since January." {
    Assert bellRungForNed(sennet_bay). Assert bethanAtPeace(bethan). Assert bethanFriend(bethan). Assert bellStopped(sennet_bay). Retract at(bethan, quay). Assert at(bethan, offstage). }
  Rule bell_rung_away when bellForNed(sennet_bay) and hour(clock) == 18 and not bethanWaiting(bethan) and not bellRungForNed(sennet_bay) { Assert bellRungForNed(sennet_bay). Assert bellStopped(sennet_bay). }
  Topic bethan_stopped with bethan "Tell Old Bethan the bell will not ring again" when bellStopped(sennet_bay) and not bellRungForNed(sennet_bay) and not bethanFriend(bethan) once {
    Says "'Won't it.' She listens, as if it might. 'Well.' She kills an eel. 'Well, that's something.' And then, not looking at you: 'Who'll I think of, at the turn, then?' She doesn't wait for an answer.".
    On discuss { Assert bethanFriend(bethan). }
  }
  // Muffled by hand, with a rope round the clapper, down in the drowned tower (whelm.kyr).
  Topic bethan_muffled with bethan "Tell Old Bethan you have tied up the clapper of the bell under the water" when bellMuffled(sennet_bay) and not bethanFriend(bethan) once {
    Says "She stares at you. 'You went down there? Into the lower town?' She looks at your hair, which is still wet. Then she gives you an eel pie, for nothing, which on the Quay is a declaration. 'Mad,' she says. 'Ned was mad. Eat that.'".
    On discuss { Assert bethanFriend(bethan). }
  }
  // One of the cloth, or anyone who knows the rites of the dead, can say them for a man the sea kept.
  Action bethan_rite(actor: group, site: place) "Say the words for the drowned with Old Bethan, for Ned Saltash, at the edge of the Quay" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bethan, site) and at(actor, quay) and knows(actor, bell_grief) and not bethanAtPeace(bethan)
      and (capable(actor, rites) or craft(actor, craft_faith)).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert bethanAtPeace(bethan). Assert bethanFriend(bethan). Assert bethanRite(bethan). }
    Result "You take her to the edge of the Quay, where the steps go down, and say the words for those the sea keeps: the old ones, that the harbour has half forgotten, about the deep and the returning path and a light left in the window. She says them after you, the bits she knows, with her eyes on the water. When you have finished she stands a while. 'He'll hear that,' she says. 'Better than any bell.' And then, at the turn of the tide, as if it had been waiting for her, the bell under the bay rings, slow and deep, and Old Bethan laughs out loud for the first time since January. 'There,' she says. 'That's him saying goodnight.'".
  }
  Relation bethanRite(group).
  Observe bethan_asleep_after at quay when bethanAtPeace(bethan) and at(bethan, quay) "Old Bethan is asleep on an upturned crate behind her barrow, with her mouth open, in the sun. The harbour is stepping round her.".
  // What the words on the drowned church door are: the harbour remembers, Bethan's family above all.
  Topic bethan_mercy with bethan "Ask Old Bethan about the words cut on the drowned church door" when bethanFriend(bethan) and knows(actor, door_words) once {
    Says "'Mercy on us.' She says it straight away, the way you'd say your own address. 'Jinny Saltash cut that. My gran's gran's sister. The sexton's girl. They were in Lir's church when the water came, because the church was highest, and it came up the nave anyway, and she got up on the porch and cut that in the door with a fish-knife while it came. They found the knife on the Quay in the morning and nothing else.' She looks at the water. 'It's what you say, on the Quay, when the sea's up. Mercy on us. We say it without thinking.' She looks at you. 'Why?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mercy_meaning). }
  }
  Discovery mercy_meaning "MERCY ON US, cut in the drowned church door, was cut by Jinny Saltash, the sexton's girl, with a fish-knife, as the sea came up the nave on the night of the Whelming. It is what the harbour still says when the sea is up.".

  // ── Peg Arklow and the Sounding Line ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person peg "Peg Arklow" at taproom {
    Role "the landlady of the Sounding Line". Profession innkeeper. Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner jovial.
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 8.
    Greets "A broad woman with her sleeves rolled pulls you a pint before you ask for it. 'There. You've the look of the coast road.' She jerks her head at the window and Cloudgate in it. 'Not going up there, are you? Nobody goes up there but the laundry and the Tourists, and the laundry comes back.'".
    Greets again "'There you are,' says Peg Arklow, and pulls you a pint, and pushes a folded paper along the bar under the glass without looking at it. 'Left by a man in a good coat. He said you would know. I said I did not hold with notes. I held it anyway.'".
  }
  Topic peg_tour with peg "Ask Peg Arklow about the Grand Tour" when true once {
    Says "'Oh, the Tour.' She polishes a glass with great contempt. 'The Rector's proclaimed it. First in two hundred years. Whoever brings her the four petals of the Rose gets to go first through the Door of Doors, up in her tower, which opens on anywhere.' She holds the glass to the light. 'Anywhere. The town's full of rich boys from up there with bear-leaders, and boys from three countries off with fathers' money, buying fire-cloaks off Ollerenshaw.' She puts the glass down. 'You enter at the House, on the headland. She sees you herself, they say. Charming woman. Makes you feel you've been waiting all your life to be talked to.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, tour_known). }
  }
  Discovery tour_known "The Rector of the House of Doors has proclaimed the Grand Tour: whoever brings her the four petals of the Rose of the Winds, from the courts of the elemental planes, will go first through the Door of Doors, in her tower, which opens on anywhere. The Tour is entered at the House of Doors, on the headland.".
  Topic peg_perrin with peg "Ask Peg Arklow about the young man who fell" when true once {
    Says "'Perrin Halyard.' She crosses herself, the harbour way, a little circle like a porthole. 'The Halyards' younger boy. He was a Doorward at the House, a nice lad, used to come in here in his gown and drink with the fishermen, which his mother never knew. Went off the Balustrade the night the Tour was proclaimed. Fog. They say he'd been drinking with his brother, and quarrelling.' She lowers her voice. 'They say a lot, up there. They never found him. The bay doesn't give back what comes off that rock.' She glances up at the window. 'They're dropping the coffin anyway. Third day, noon. You'll see it from the Quay.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, perrin_fell). }
  }
  Discovery perrin_fell "Perrin Halyard, younger son of the Halyards of Cloudgate and a Doorward of the House of Doors, went over the Balustrade of Cloudgate in fog on the night the Grand Tour was proclaimed, twelve days before you came; he had been drinking and quarrelling with his brother. He was never found. His empty coffin is to be let down off the Balustrade at noon on the third day.".
  Topic peg_lifting with peg "Ask Peg Arklow about Cloudgate" when true once {
    Says "'Cloudgate.' She says it like a debt. 'That was the top of the town once. Halyard Hill. Two hundred years ago Lady Ysabeau Halyard came home from the Air Door with something in her pocket and lifted the whole hill into the sky, houses and all, and the sea came into the hole where it had been, and the lower town went under in an hour.' She wipes the bar. 'They call it the Lifting, up there. Ascension Day, they keep it, with lanterns. We call it the Whelming, down here, and we keep it with candles on the water. Same night.' She shrugs. 'You can see both from the Quay. Very pretty.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lifting_known). }
  }
  Discovery lifting_known "Two hundred years ago Lady Ysabeau Halyard came back through the Air Door with something that lifted Halyard Hill, the top of old Sennet, into the sky with its houses: Cloudgate. The sea came into the hole it left, and the lower town drowned in an hour. Cloudgate keeps the night as the Lifting, with lanterns; the harbour keeps it as the Whelming, with candles on the water.".

  // ── Ha'penny and the third step ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A merfolk child comes up the Fish Stairs at the morning and evening tides to sell cockles to the harbour children,
  // to the third step, which is as far as the Bylaw lets her. She wants to go to the Glass Market and buy a present.
  Person hapenny "Ha'penny" at drowned_street {
    Role "a merfolk child with a basket of cockles" when not hapennyUp(hapenny).
    Role "a merfolk child in a fish-basket, delighted with everything" when hapennyUp(hapenny).
    Ancestry undine. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "A merfolk child is sitting on the third step from the bottom of the dry ones, with her tail in the sea and a basket of cockles in her lap: green-skinned, freckled with silver, with gills under her ears like the gills of a fish, which open and shut when she is interested, which is always. 'Cockles,' she says. 'Ha'penny a scoop. That's my name too. Ha'penny. What's yours?'".
    Greets again "'It's you!' says Ha'penny, and her gills go.".
    Joins "Ha'penny grips the rim of the basket with both hands, like a queen in a carriage. 'Go on, then,' she says. 'Before the fat man looks.'".
    Leaves "Ha'penny flicks her tail once and is gone into the green, the way the merfolk go: not leaving, just not there." to drowned_street.
  }
  Relation hapennyUp(group). Relation hapennyWish(group). Relation hapennyShopped(group). Relation hapennyInvites(group).
  Query stairsTide() means (hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 10) or (hour(clock) >= 16 and hour(clock) < 18).
  Rule hapenny_up_stairs when stairsTide() and begun() and not hapennyUp(hapenny) and not following(hapenny, party) and not at(hapenny, fish_stairs) { Assert at(hapenny, fish_stairs). }
  Rule hapenny_down when not stairsTide() and not hapennyUp(hapenny) and not following(hapenny, party) and not at(hapenny, drowned_street) { Assert at(hapenny, drowned_street). }
  Observe hapenny_on_step at fish_stairs when at(hapenny, fish_stairs) and not hapennyUp(hapenny) "On the third step from the bottom, exactly on the brass plate, as if to make a point, a merfolk child sits with a basket of cockles and her tail in the water.".
  Topic hapenny_wish with hapenny "Ask Ha'penny what is up the stairs that she wants" when true once {
    Says "'The market.' She says it the way other children say Midsummer. 'The glass one. Where everything's glass and the light's in the bottles.' She looks up the stairs, all the way up, to where they turn the corner onto the Quay. 'I want to buy a present. With my own pearl.' She shows you: a pearl the size of a pea, in her fist. 'For Mercy. She's gone funny. She smiles at nothing all day and won't come to the shoals.' Her gills shut, offended. 'But it's above the plate. The fat man with the telescope says five coin to anybody who brings me.' She considers you. 'Have you got five coin?'".
    On discuss { Assert hapennyWish(hapenny). Assert knows(actor, third_step). }
  }
  Discovery third_step "By the Harbour Bylaw of 1109 no merfolk may come above the third step of the Fish Stairs, on pain of five coin to whoever brings them. Ha'penny, a merfolk child, wants to go up to the Glass Market and buy a present for Mercy with her own pearl.".

  // ── Mr. Pumphrey, the Harbourmaster ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person pumphrey "Mr. Josiah Pumphrey" at pumphrey_office {
    Role "the Harbourmaster of Sennet, with a brass telescope and the Bylaws under his arm". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Greets "A stout man in a blue coat with brass buttons, a brass telescope and a bound copy of the Harbour Bylaws, looks at you through the telescope from four feet away, and then lowers it. 'Josiah Pumphrey,' he says. 'Harbourmaster. If you have business on the Quay, I am the Quay.'".
    Greets again "'Ah,' says Mr. Pumphrey, and consults the Bylaws, in case. 'There is a new bylaw,' he says, with pride and a hint of dread. 'About boats that arrive from nowhere. It was drafted on your account, in a sense. I have not been able to find the clause that says what to do about you.'".
  }
  Rule pumphrey_office_hours when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 12 and not at(pumphrey, pumphrey_office) { Assert at(pumphrey, pumphrey_office). }
  Rule pumphrey_patrol when hour(clock) >= 13 and hour(clock) < 18 and not at(pumphrey, fish_stairs) { Assert at(pumphrey, fish_stairs). }
  Rule pumphrey_dines when ((hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 13) or (hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 21)) and not at(pumphrey, taproom) { Assert at(pumphrey, taproom). }
  Rule pumphrey_bed when (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 8) and not at(pumphrey, offstage) { Assert at(pumphrey, offstage). }
  Topic pumphrey_bylaw with pumphrey "Ask Mr. Pumphrey about the brass plate on the third step" when true once {
    Says "'Bylaw Eleven-oh-Nine.' He opens the book without looking, at the page, which is worn grey. 'No person of the sea above the third step of the Fish Stairs, on pain of five coin to whoever brings them.' He closes it. 'Since the Whelming. The sea came up into the town once, and the town decided it would be the one to say how far, after.' He polishes the telescope. 'They trade at the third step. Proper. Orderly. Nobody on the Quay has a word against them. Below the plate.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, third_step). }
  }
  Relation pumphreyRelents(group). Relation pumphreyDeposit(group).
  Topic pumphrey_bethan with pumphrey "Have Old Bethan tell Mr. Pumphrey about his grandmother" when bethanFriend(bethan) and hapennyWish(hapenny) and at(bethan, ?p) and at(pumphrey, ?p) and not pumphreyRelents(pumphrey) once {
    Says "Old Bethan puts her hands on her hips. 'Josiah Pumphrey,' she says, loud enough for the Quay. 'Your gran, Hester Pumphrey, sold cockles to the sea-folk on those stairs before you were breeched, and sat on the top step to do it, and nobody fined her, and you used to sit in her lap and pull their hair.' The Quay has gone very quiet. The Harbourmaster has gone the colour of a boiled crab. 'That,' he says, 'is neither here nor there.' He looks at the Bylaws. He looks at the plate. 'An hour,' he says. 'Under my eye. For the child. And if she bites anyone it is on your heads.'".
    On discuss { Assert pumphreyRelents(pumphrey). }
  }
  Action argue_pumphrey(actor: group, site: place) "Argue with Mr. Pumphrey, in front of the whole Quay, that a child going shopping is not a person of the sea" {
    Speaker pumphrey.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pumphrey, site) and hapennyWish(hapenny) and not pumphreyRelents(pumphrey) and not argued(pumphrey).
    Time 1 minute.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert pumphreyRelents(pumphrey). Assert argued(pumphrey). }
    On failure { Assert argued(pumphrey). }
    Result "You put it to him that a child is a person of the sea only in the sense that a cod is a person, and that the Bylaw says person, and the Quay starts laughing at about the word cod and does not stop. The Harbourmaster holds out against it as long as a man can. 'An hour,' he says, at last, with dignity. 'Under my eye. As an exception. Which proves the rule.'".
    Otherwise "You put it to him, and he hears you out, and then reads you the Bylaw again, slowly, with the stresses in different places, until the Quay gets bored and goes back to work.".
  }
  Relation argued(group).
  Action pumphrey_deposit(actor: group, site: place) "Offer Mr. Pumphrey the five coin in advance" {
    Speaker pumphrey.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pumphrey, site) and hapennyWish(hapenny) and not pumphreyRelents(pumphrey) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 5.
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Increase quantity(pumphrey, gold) by 5. Assert pumphreyRelents(pumphrey). Assert pumphreyDeposit(pumphrey). }
    Result "'There is no provision,' says Mr. Pumphrey, 'for paying in advance.' He looks at the coins. He looks at the Bylaws, which have nothing to say. 'I will accept it,' he says, 'as a deposit,' and writes you a receipt in a beautiful hand.".
  }
  // Brought up the stairs: by leave, or unseen while the Harbourmaster is at his dinner, or anyway, and fined.
  Query pumphreyWatching() means at(pumphrey, fish_stairs) or at(pumphrey, quay).
  Action carry_hapenny(actor: group, site: place) "Lift Ha'penny into a fish-basket and carry her up the Fish Stairs to the Glass Market" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, fish_stairs) and at(hapenny, site) and hapennyWish(hapenny) and not hapennyShopped(hapenny) and not hapennyUp(hapenny).
    Time 1.
    On success {
      Assert hapennyUp(hapenny). Assert following(hapenny, party). Retract at(actor, fish_stairs). Assert at(actor, glass_market).
    }
    Result "She weighs about as much as a wet dog, and she is in the fish-basket before you have finished lifting it, with her tail curled round under her and her arms over the rim, and her gills going like bellows. Up the stairs, past the brass plate (she leans out to spit on it), along the Quay, where every head turns, up the Haul, and into the Glass Market, where she sees the bottles with the light moving in them and says nothing at all for the first time since you met her.".
  }
  Rule hapenny_fined when hapennyUp(hapenny) and not pumphreyRelents(pumphrey) and not fined(party) and pumphreyWatching()
    says "Behind you on the Quay a whistle goes, and Mr. Pumphrey comes along it at a pace he has not used in years, with the Bylaws open. 'Bylaw Eleven-oh-Nine!' he says. 'Five coin!' And he holds out his hand, and the Quay, which loves a fine as it loves a wedding, watches you pay." {
    Assert fined(party). Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 5 or to nothing. }
  Relation fined(group).
  Observe hapenny_market at glass_market when hapennyUp(hapenny) and following(hapenny, party) and not hapennyShopped(hapenny) "In her fish-basket Ha'penny is looking at everything at once: the bottles with the light in them, the glass floats, a stall of hand-mirrors, the crier's board, a dog. The stallholders have stopped crying their wares to look at her, and she at them.".
  // At Prue Quickly's she buys her present with her pearl (lamp.kyr), and on the way back says what it is for.
  Topic hapenny_gossip with hapenny "Ask Ha'penny why Mercy needs a present" when hapennyShopped(hapenny) and not knows(actor, sky_man) once {
    Says "'Because she's gone soft.' Ha'penny holds the mirror up and looks at herself in it and makes a face. 'She caught a man. Out of the sky. He came down through the cloud in the fog like a gannet, twelve nights ago, and she caught him before the bottom got him, and took him to the air-bell, and she keeps him there, and feeds him, and he's broken his leg, and he reads books, and she won't come to the shoals.' She puts the mirror against her chest. 'Gran says he's a dry man and no good. I've seen him. He's all right. He talks to me.' She looks at you sideways. 'Don't tell. It's a secret. Everybody knows.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sky_man). }
  }
  Discovery sky_man "Twelve nights ago, in the fog, a man came down out of the sky into the bay, and Mercy, a merfolk girl, caught him before the bottom did, and keeps him in an air-bell in the Whelm. He has broken his leg, and reads books. The merfolk all know.".
  Topic hapenny_home with hapenny "Take Ha'penny back down to the Fish Stairs" when hapennyUp(hapenny) and hapennyShopped(hapenny) once {
    Says "She is quiet on the way back, holding the mirror. At the third step she slides out of the basket and into the water to the shoulders and turns round. 'You can come to supper,' she says. 'In the Guildhall. Gran won't mind. She will, but she won't.' She looks at the stairs going down into the dark. 'You need breath to come. I can give you some. Mine doesn't last long. I'm little.' And she ducks, and is gone, and the mirror flashes once, going down.".
    On discuss { Retract hapennyUp(hapenny). Retract following(hapenny, party). Assert at(hapenny, drowned_street). Assert hapennyInvites(hapenny). Retract at(actor, glass_market). Assert at(actor, fish_stairs). Assert knows(actor, supper_asked). }
  }
  Discovery supper_asked "Ha'penny has asked the company to supper in the drowned Guildhall, at the table of her grandmother, the merfolk matriarch.".
}

data/adventures/the-grand-tour/history.k:
Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  // ── What Sennet remembers, and what it has painted over ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Roll of the Grand Tour in the Hall of Doors; the labels of the Museum; the register on the lectern of the
  // drowned church; where the merfolk got their English; why there is no weather on Cloudgate; the Rector's keys.
  // None of it is needed. All of it is true, and some of it is the story told early by people who did not know they
  // were telling it.

  // The Roll: five Tours in three hundred years, and the last one was Ysabeau's.
  Observe roll_board at hall_of_doors as sign when not knows(party, roll_known) "Between the two doors, above Mr. Threlkeld's desk, a board painted black, with names in gilt: THE ROLL OF THE GRAND TOUR. 1012, proclaimed by Rector Aenhild Brack: WON, by Odo Sare, Doorward, who went through first and came back and would not say where. 1047: NOT WON. 1088: NOT WON. Under 1088, in smaller gilt, the entered Tourists, and among them: Ysabeau Halyard, aged seventeen, through the Air Door, DECLARED NOTHING. And under that, in different gilt, much newer: the Court of the Air reports its petal lost, the same year. Then two hundred years of black board, and at the bottom, still tacky: 1290, proclaimed by Rector I. Quance." teaches roll_known.
  Discovery roll_known "The Roll of the Grand Tour says the last Tour, in 1088, was not won; Ysabeau Halyard went through the Air Door in it, at seventeen, and declared nothing; and the Court of the Air reported its petal lost that year.".
  Observe roll_again at hall_of_doors as sign when knows(party, roll_known) "Between the doors, the Roll of the Grand Tour: 1088, Ysabeau Halyard, DECLARED NOTHING.".

  // The Museum's labels, read along the cabinets.
  Observe museum_labels at museum as sign when not visitedBefore(museum) "The labels, in a dozen hands over two hundred years. CABINET ONE: the cast skin of a salamander, brought home by the first Tourist, 1012. CABINET SIX: A SIGH OF THE AIR, IN A STOPPERED BOTTLE. DO NOT UNSTOP. CABINET NINE: a minute of the Slow Assembly, a slab of banded stone, translated underneath: RESOLVED, THAT THE ASSEMBLY IS AWARE (1146). CABINET TWELVE: Dame P. Murrey's snowball jar, empty, MELTED, 1231. CABINET THIRTEEN: a comb of green shell, A PERSON OF THE SEA'S, TAKEN ON THE FISH STAIRS, MCCXI. Nobody has written down from whom, or why.".
  Observe museum_comb at museum as sign when visitedBefore(museum) and knows(party, plate_known) "In Cabinet Thirteen, the green shell comb: TAKEN ON THE FISH STAIRS, MCCXI. The year on the brass plate.".
  Entity plate_known: fact "The brass plate on the third step of the Fish Stairs is dated MCCXI.".
  Observe plate_seen at fish_stairs when not knows(party, plate_known) "The plate is brass, green at the screws; its letters have been polished smooth by eighty years of people sitting on them." teaches plate_known.

  // Lir's church: the sexton's register, and the last name in it.
  Observe church_register at drowned_church when not knows(party, register_known) "On the lectern, chained, a book swollen to three times its size, its pages fused into a block except the last, which the current lifts and lets fall. On it, in a hand that gets worse down the page, a column of names without dates: the sexton's list of who was in the church when the water came up the nave, written as it came. Forty-one names. The last, in letters the size of a child's, is JINNY SALTASH." teaches register_known.
  Discovery register_known "The register on the lectern of the drowned church lists forty-one people who were in Lir's when the water came, the night Cloudgate was lifted; the last of them is Jinny Saltash.".
  Topic bethan_register with bethan "Tell Old Bethan about the names in the register on the drowned lectern" when knows(actor, register_known) and bethanFriend(bethan) once {
    Says "'Forty-one.' She does not ask whether Jinny is among them. 'Saltash is Ned's name. They say there was a Saltash in the church that night, and that's why we've always been on the water and never up the chain, any of us.' She is quiet. 'They put a plaque up in Cloudgate for the Lifting. To the Glory of God and the House of Halyard. Nobody put one up for the church.'".
  }

  // Where the merfolk got their English: off the drowned shop-signs, and Lir's hymn-books.
  Topic perrin_signs with perrin "Ask Perrin Halyard where the merfolk learned to speak Common" when true once {
    Says "'Off the signs!' He is delighted to be asked. 'They came through the Water Door two lifetimes after the Whelming and found a town with its signs still up and nobody to read them. So the old woman is No Admittance, and the boys are Cash Only and Shutters, and Ha'penny's mother is called Rooms To Let.' He grins. 'They got the rest out of the hymn-books in Lir's. So they all talk like the Book of Common Prayer in a hurry. Listen to the old woman some time. Keeping is the whole of it. That's a collect, very nearly.'".
  }

  // Why there is never any weather on Cloudgate.
  Observe no_weather at balustrade when aloft() and not dark() and not knows(party, keel_petal) "There is never any weather on Cloudgate. The wind that should come in off the sea parts round the hill like water round a stone, and goes on, and the cloud lies under the rail like a floor. In Cloudgate they say it is breeding. Down on the Quay they say it is not natural, and spit.".

  // The Rector's keys: heard before they mean anything, and listened to after.
  Observe keys_first at rector_study as sound when at(quance, rector_study) and not visitedBefore(rector_study) "Whenever the Rector moves, the keys on her chain of office chime, a small bright sound, like a purse shaken.".
  Observe keys_eulogy at balustrade as sound when matterOpen(eulogy) "When the Rector puts her hand on the rail to speak, the keys on her chain chime against the stone.".
  Observe keys_after near quance as sound when knows(party, keys_heard) and rectorFree() and not knows(party, quance_pushed) "The Rector's keys chime when she moves. You find that you are listening to them.".

  // The Nexus floor: a square of black metal nobody has opened (the top of the Aenean shaft; undertow.kyr).
  Observe nexus_hatch at nexus when not openedBelow(sennet_bay) "Set into the boards beside the Door of Doors is a square of black metal the size of a trapdoor, flush with the floor, with no handle and no hinge. It is cold, and if you lay your hand on it, very faintly, it hums, the way the chain hums in the Ascent yard.".
  // The cold in the cellar, before anyone tells you why.
  Observe cellar_cold at wine_cellar when not knows(party, keel_petal) and not knows(party, keel_ladder_known) "The bottles nearest the end of the racks are frosted, in June. A draught comes from somewhere behind them that smells, for no reason anyone has given, of snow.".
}

data/adventures/the-grand-tour/hours.kyr:
Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  Description "The black square in the Nexus floor, which three keys open; the shaft under it; the Slack, where the count has a pause; and the ship that lies in the pause.".

  // ── What this is ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Aeneans' House of Doors was built over the top of something they found: a square of black metal, flush with the
  // Nexus floor, that hums, and has no handle. Nobody in the House has opened it, and the House has had no wish to ask
  // what is under it. It opens to three things, none of which the House has: a reading, a measure, and a standing. Each
  // is a thing a company can have got elsewhere, in more than one form; and each has a costly form for a company that
  // has not.
  Thing black_square "the black square" at nexus {
    State sealed "A square of black metal, flush with the Nexus floor, humming faintly under the sole of the foot. It is cold. Along its four edges are tiny notches, and across its face a line of marks.".
    State unsealed "The black square has swung down on a hinge nobody saw, and under it a stair of the same black metal goes down into a light the colour of old paper.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(black_square, sealed).
  Relation squareRead(group). Relation squareMeasured(group). Relation squareVouched(group).
  Relation squareTalk(place). Measure inkDay(place).

  // 1. The reading. A line of Aenean capitals, cut in later, and under it a longer row of marks that are not Aenean.
  Action read_by_lore(actor: group, site: place) "Read the line cut on the black square" {
    Description "Aenean capitals, much worn, and under them a row of marks older than the Aeneans' letters.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nexus) and state(black_square, sealed) and not squareRead(actor) and capable(actor, lore).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert squareRead(actor). }
    Result "The Aenean is easy: HORARIUM, it says, and under it QUOD RESTAT CUSTODITUR. The hour-place. What remains is kept. It is an Aenean's gloss, a clerk's: it does not say who made the plate, only what the Aeneans thought it was for. The row beneath it is longer, and you cannot read it; you can only see that it is cut very evenly, by a hand that did not hurry.".
  }
  Action read_by_rubbings(actor: group, site: place) "Lay a keeper's tally and a Prefect's table against the black square" {
    Description "Two rubbings of two notations. A bilingual is a bilingual wherever it is laid.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nexus) and state(black_square, sealed) and not squareRead(actor) and holding(actor, tally_rubbing) and holding(actor, pharos_rubbing).
    Time 8.
    On success { Assert squareRead(actor). }
    Result "You spread them on the floor of the Nexus, one beside the other, the cloth from a stone bench on a headland and the paper from a bronze table on an island, and lay the black square's row of marks beside them. They are three copies of one thing. The keepers' strokes on the cloth are the marks on the square. The Prefect's numerals on the paper are the numerals the keepers used where they had them. Between them a person who has neither lore nor luck can read the square: HORARIUM, says the third notation; and what it says after is the number twelve, in a way you did not know a number could be said.".
  }
  Action hire_scribes(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the Collegium of Measures' scribes to copy and read the square" {
    Description "Thirty coin, a day, and the Collegium of Measures knowing that something in the Nexus floor can be read.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nexus) and state(black_square, sealed) and not squareRead(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 30.
    Time 144.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 30. Assert squareRead(actor). Assert squareTalk(sennet_bay). }
    Result "Two young Fellows with ink on their cuffs and a manner of enormous tact copy the plate on their knees for a day and a night, and read it out to you at dawn in a way that shows they have read it to each other all night. HORARIUM. They do not say what they think it is. They look at you as people look at the person who has just told them that a door in their own house leads somewhere.".
  }
  Observe fellows_at_square at nexus when squareTalk(sennet_bay) and state(black_square, sealed) "Two Fellows of the Collegium of Measures are sitting on the floor of the Nexus a respectful distance from the black square, not touching it, and not leaving.".

  // 2. The measure. The square is cut with a scale along its edges: a unit the House has never used.
  Action measure_by_rod(actor: group, site: place) "Lay the dyke-reeve's rod along the edge of the black square" {
    Description "A rod of black wood shod in notched bronze, from a dale in the north.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nexus) and state(black_square, sealed) and not squareMeasured(actor) and holding(actor, sluice_rod).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert squareMeasured(actor). }
    Result "The rod's bronze shoe fits the notches along the square's edge as a key fits a lock. You did not expect that it would, and what you feel is not triumph, it is a kind of vertigo: that a reeve's rod in a village with a lime tree and a lake behind it is a measure in use on this floor, in this room, two hundred miles from the dale. The notches match to the last. Whoever cut them did not stop at a dale.".
  }
  Action measure_by_table(actor: group, site: place) "Read the black square's scale against the Prefect's table" {
    Description "The Aeneans wrote the unit down, in numerals, in a lamp-room on an island.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nexus) and state(black_square, sealed) and not squareMeasured(actor) and holding(actor, pharos_rubbing).
    Time 4.
    On success { Assert squareMeasured(actor). }
    Result "The Prefect's numerals are the unit's length in the Aeneans' own foot, to nine places, and you divide, carefully, by the notches along the square's edge, and the answer is a whole number, and the whole number is twelve. You check it twice. A measure like this exists for one reason: so that two people who have never met can build the same thing.".
  }
  Hazard plate_cold "The cold of the black square" means "Deal (1d6) cold damage to ally unless constitution save against (12).".
  Action measure_by_pacing(actor: group, site: place) "Pace out the notches and trust your hands" {
    Description "No rod, no table: only a patient eye and a steady hand, and a plate that is cold enough to bite.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nexus) and state(black_square, sealed) and not squareMeasured(actor).
    Time 36.
    Resolve check(actor, wayfinding, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert squareMeasured(actor). }
    On failure { Assert strikes(plate_cold, party). }
    Result "You go along the edge a notch at a time, with your fingers, and your breath smoking, for the better part of a day, and come at the end to a number you can trust.".
    Otherwise "The plate bites. You come away with your hands white to the wrist and a number you do not believe.".
  }

  // 3. The standing. The square will open to a keeper, or to anyone a keeper's House vouches for. It does not care which House.
  Action vouch_by_writ(actor: group, site: place) "Say the keeper's formula over the black square, from the Prefect's writ" {
    Description "NON DOMINIUM SED CUSTODIA. A keeping is not an ownership; whoever claims one in the formula is heard.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nexus) and state(black_square, sealed) and not squareVouched(actor) and holding(actor, prefects_writ).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert squareVouched(actor). }
    Result "You read it aloud from the monk's copy, in the dead tongue, in the voice of someone who does not believe in what they are doing: NON DOMINIUM SED CUSTODIA. NE QUIS CUSTODEM IMPEDIAT. The black square hums on, and then the hum changes pitch, once, as if it had been addressed correctly by someone it had given up expecting.".
  }
  Action vouch_by_mask(actor: group, site: place) "Hold a keeper's grey face to the black square" {
    Description "A face of fired clay without eyes or mouth, which rings when it is struck.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nexus) and state(black_square, sealed) and not squareVouched(actor) and holding(actor, keeper_mask).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert squareVouched(actor). }
    Result "The grey face rings against the black metal like a bell struck underwater. The square answers it, a note lower, and then the two notes beat together and are one, and the note it sets up under your feet is the same note, a size larger.".
  }
  Action vouch_by_letter(actor: group, site: place) "Show the black square a Fellow's letter of introduction" {
    Description "A folded letter with a seal on it, from a man who believes it will open fewer doors than it does.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nexus) and state(black_square, sealed) and not squareVouched(actor) and holding(actor, collegium_letter).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert squareVouched(actor). }
    Result "It is a ridiculous thing to do, and you do it with a straight face: you unfold the letter and read it out to a plate of black metal. 'To all who keep working things,' it says, 'greeting.' The square listens with its whole cold weight, and the hum drops by a tone, and stays.".
    Otherwise "You read it out. The square does not care. Somewhere in the House a door slams.".
  }
  Action vouch_by_perrin(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Perrin Halyard to speak for the House" {
    Description "A student of the House, who has read the Aenean plaque more often than anyone alive.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nexus) and state(black_square, sealed) and not squareVouched(actor) and perrinHere().
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert squareVouched(actor). }
    Result "Perrin Halyard kneels by the black square on his one good knee and lays his hand flat on it, and says in the tone of someone introducing a friend: 'It's all right. They're with me.' The hum changes, so that for a moment you hear it as music. 'I've been saying that to the plaque in the Undercroft for a week,' Perrin says. 'I think it's the right grammar.'".
  }

  Action open_the_square(actor: group, site: place) "Open the black square" {
    Description "A reading, a measure, and a standing. All three, and the plate will turn.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nexus) and state(black_square, sealed) and squareRead(actor) and squareMeasured(actor) and squareVouched(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert state(black_square, unsealed). Assert befell(slack_opened). }
    Result "You lay your hands on the square where the notches meet. It does not open as a door opens. It stops being a floor. A line of light runs round its four edges like the line round a page when the page is held up to a lamp, and the square swings down and away, and under it a black stair goes down into a pale and level light. The hum has stopped. In the quiet you can hear, from a very long way below, the sound of a ship's bell being struck, once, and then again, exactly eleven times.".
  }
  Passage square_way "the black stair" is shaft between nexus and shaft_head opening when state(black_square, unsealed) "".
  Observe nexus_open at nexus when state(black_square, unsealed) "The black square stands open in the Nexus floor, and a pale light comes up out of it onto the Door of Doors, which does not seem to mind.".

  // ── The Slack ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place slack "the Slack" is plane.
  Place slack_region "the Slack" is region within slack.
  Place descent "the black stair" is wilderness within slack_region at 0, 0.
  Place berth "the Quay of Hours" is site within slack_region at 1, 0.
  Place remainder_site "the Remainder" is site within slack_region at 2, 0.
  Place shaft_head "the foot of the black stair" is room within descent at 0, 0.
  Place hours_quay "the Quay of Hours" is room within berth at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place rem_deck "the Remainder's deck" is room within remainder_site at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place rem_count "the count-room" is room within remainder_site at 1, 0 indoors.
  Place rem_watch "the watch-room" is room within remainder_site at 0, 1 indoors.
  Place rem_hold "the hold of remainders" is room within remainder_site at 1, 1 indoors.
  Passage slack_descend "the way down to the quay" is steps between shaft_head and hours_quay taking 20 minutes.
  Passage rem_stair "the count-room stair" is passage between rem_deck and rem_count.
  Passage rem_hatch "the watch-room hatch" is door between rem_deck and rem_watch.
  Passage rem_hold_way "the hold hatch" is ladder between rem_deck and rem_hold.
  Passage rem_gangway "the Remainder's gangway" is steps between rem_deck and hours_quay opening when at(remainder, hours_quay) "".
  Passage rem_gangway_out "the Remainder's gangway on Mechanus" is steps between rem_deck and outer_mechanus_threshold opening when at(remainder, outer_mechanus_threshold) "".

  Observe slack_shaft_scene at shaft_head when true "The foot of a very long stair. The light here has no source: it is level, pale and shadowless, like the light inside a page. The walls are the black metal of the square, ruled with fine lines at a spacing that your eye keeps trying to read as writing, and above, a great way up, a square of ordinary gold lamplight.".
  Observe slack_quay_scene at hours_quay when true "A quay of black metal under a ruled sky: not stars, lines, pale on pale, ruling the dome from edge to edge and very slowly sliding. There is no water. Where the water should be there is a level surface of something like slack tide, still, bright and without depth, in which the ruled sky is reflected exactly, so that you seem to stand on the lip of a second sky.".
  Observe quay_ship at hours_quay when at(remainder, hours_quay) "A ship lies against the quay. She is long and low and the colour of old paper, with a single mast and sails that are not cloth; and along her side, in marks no one reads, and under them in Aenean capitals, a name: RELIQUA.".
  Observe quay_gone at hours_quay when not at(remainder, hours_quay) "The quay is bare. A ring in it, big as a wheel, has had a rope on it recently.".
  Observe rem_deck_scene at rem_deck when true "The deck is level metal, scoured, with a round-edged mast rising from the middle of it and a deck-bell hanging from the mast by a cord of something that is not rope. The rail is waist high and warm. There are marks on it, notches, rows and rows, and the rows are in elevens.".
  Observe rem_count_scene at rem_count when true "A round room, low, with a table in the middle of it, and on the table a set of rods and beads and slates, arranged by hand and re-arranged, with the drudged patience of something that is always being corrected. On the wall a great ruled chart, and on the chart a single pin, and the pin is not moving.".
  Observe rem_watch_scene at rem_watch when true "The crew live here: twenty-odd bunks in tiers, the bedding patched and patched, a long table, a stove that does not burn anything, a slate on which each day's tally is chalked and then wiped to chalk again. There are children's drawings pinned over one bunk, of people on a shore. Nobody in the drawings has a face.".
  Observe rem_hold_scene at rem_hold when true "The hold is lit from the floor. It is not a large hold, and it is not full: it is, you think, the right size for what is in it. Racks and cages and sealed jars and long locked chests, each with a card. The cards are in a hand that has been copied and copied. REMAINDER, each says, and a number.".
}

data/adventures/the-grand-tour/lamp.kyr:
Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  // ── Lamp Street ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The glass-houses of Sennet burn on heat piped from the Fire Door, by the hour, by the House's licence. Prue Quickly
  // makes floats and bottles and mirrors, and, for the Tourists, "genuine petals of the Rose" at a coin each, stamped on
  // the back A PRESENT FROM SENNET. One of them has got her into trouble with the Watch.
  Observe lamp_scene at lamp_street when true "Lamp Street climbs toward the headland between glass-houses, every one of them with its doors open and its furnace roaring, so that walking up it is like walking past a row of opened ovens. Over each furnace a copper pipe comes down out of the street's great main, which runs up the hill on iron legs to the House of Doors, and hums.".
  Observe lamp_shops at lamp_street when true "Between the glass-houses, two shops: MURREY'S, under a sign of a gilt key, with a window full of the same red book; and PARGETER'S, OUTFITTERS TO THE GRAND TOUR, with a dummy in the window wearing a fire-cloak, a brine-glass helm and an expression of great confidence.".
  Observe glasshouse_scene at glasshouse when true "Prue Quickly's glass-house: one long hot room, a furnace at the end of it like an open mouth, and on every shelf and hook and windowsill glass: floats, bottles, rods, hand-mirrors, a chandelier half-made hanging from a beam, and a tray of red glass petals, each the length of your hand, under a card: GENUINE PETALS OF THE ROSE. ONE COIN.".
  Observe glasshouse_cold at glasshouse when furnaceCold(glasshouse) "The furnace is out. The pipe over it is cold, and someone has tied a cardboard label to it: HEAT WITHDRAWN BY ORDER OF THE HOUSE.".

  Kind mirror_kind "a hand-mirror" is gear worth 2 weighing 0 described "A hand-mirror of Prue Quickly's glass, round, in a frame of bent copper.".
  Kind glass_petal_kind "a glass petal" is gear worth 1 weighing 0 described "A petal of red glass the length of your hand, very like the pictures of the Fire petal of the Rose, and stamped on the back in small capitals: A PRESENT FROM SENNET.".

  Person prue "Prue Quickly" at glasshouse {
    Role "a glass-blower, with forearms like a stevedore's and no eyebrows". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Sells mirror_kind for 2 coin from 4.
    Sells glass_petal_kind for 1 coin from 9.
    Greets "A woman with no eyebrows and a blowpipe over her shoulder like a musket turns round from the furnace. 'Mind the floor, it's hot. Everything's hot.' She looks you over. 'Tourist? You'll want a petal. Everybody wants a petal. One coin, and I'll tell you a secret: it isn't real.'".
    Greets again "'Mind the floor,' says Prue Quickly.".
  }
  Relation furnaceCold(place). Relation prueSaved(group). Relation watchCame(group). Relation prueTrouble(group).
  Rule prue_works when openHours() and not at(prue, glasshouse) { Assert at(prue, glasshouse). }
  Rule prue_evening when hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 22 and not at(prue, taproom) { Assert at(prue, taproom). }
  Rule prue_bed when (hour(clock) >= 22 or hour(clock) < 8) and not at(prue, offstage) and not making(prue) { Assert at(prue, offstage). }

  // Ha'penny's present: a mirror, for a pearl (harbour.kyr). Prue gives change in glass fish.
  Kind glass_fish_kind "a glass fish" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "A little fish of blue glass with a bubble in its belly, made by Prue Quickly for a merfolk child who had never seen a fish that would not swim away.".
  Action hapenny_shops(actor: group, site: place) "Let Ha'penny choose her present" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, glasshouse) and at(prue, site) and following(hapenny, party) and not hapennyShopped(hapenny).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert hapennyShopped(hapenny). }
    Result "Ha'penny goes along Prue's shelves in her fish-basket like a duchess at a sale, touching nothing, looking at everything, while Prue Quickly watches her with her arms folded and something happening to her face. In the end Ha'penny chooses a hand-mirror in a copper frame, the plainest, and holds out her pearl for it on her flat palm. Prue looks at the pearl, which would buy the shop, and closes Ha'penny's fingers back over it. 'Keep that,' she says. 'Mirrors are a ha'penny today. For people called Ha'penny.' And she gives her a little blue glass fish as well, for change, and Ha'penny holds it up to the furnace light and sees the bubble in it and makes a sound like a kettle.".
  }

  // ── The Watch, and a petal that was not a forgery ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person bassett "Sergeant Bassett" at offstage {
    Role "a sergeant of the Watch, in a leather hat". Ancestry dwarf. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "The sergeant takes off his leather hat to you, and puts it back on. 'Bassett, of the Watch. Lamp Street is my beat, and I'll thank you not to buy anything off it that's pretending to be something else.'".
  }
  // His beat, by day, when the glass-blower is not his business: Lamp Street, as he says.
  Rule bassett_beat when openHours() and not at(bassett, glasshouse) and not at(bassett, lamp_street) and not bassettGoes(bassett) and not watchAtPrue() { Assert at(bassett, lamp_street). }
  Rule bassett_off when not openHours() and at(bassett, lamp_street) { Retract at(bassett, lamp_street). Assert at(bassett, offstage). }
  Query watchAtPrue() means prueTrouble(prue) and not prueSaved(prue) and hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) < 13 and (day(clock) == 2 or day(clock) == 3).
  Rule watch_comes when day(clock) == 2 and hour(clock) >= 10 and not watchCame(party) {
    Assert watchCame(party). Assert prueTrouble(prue). Assert at(bassett, glasshouse). }
  Observe bassett_here at glasshouse when at(bassett, glasshouse) and prueTrouble(prue) and not prueSaved(prue) "Sergeant Bassett of the Watch stands just inside the door with his leather hat in his hands and a notebook open on it, and Prue Quickly stands at the furnace with her arms folded, and neither of them is enjoying it.".
  Rule watch_goes when at(bassett, glasshouse) and hour(clock) >= 13 { Retract at(bassett, glasshouse). Assert at(bassett, offstage). }
  Rule watch_returns when day(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) < 13 and prueTrouble(prue) and not prueSaved(prue) and not at(bassett, glasshouse) { Assert at(bassett, glasshouse). }
  // Unless somebody speaks for her by noon on the third day, the House takes back her heat.
  Rule heat_withdrawn when day(clock) == 3 and hour(clock) >= 12 and prueTrouble(prue) and not prueSaved(prue) and not furnaceCold(glasshouse) {
    Assert furnaceCold(glasshouse). }
  Topic prue_trouble with prue "Ask Prue Quickly what the Watch wants with her" when prueTrouble(prue) and not prueSaved(prue) once {
    Says "'Forgery.' She spits on the floor and it hisses. 'A boy from up there, a Mottram, bought one of my petals yesterday and took it straight up the headland and laid it on the Rector's desk as the Fire petal of the Rose. Without turning it over.' She turns one over for you: A PRESENT FROM SENNET. 'The Rector laughed, they say. Then her Bursar put in a complaint, forgery of the Rose, and if it isn't settled the House takes back my heat. Off the main.' She jerks her chin at the copper pipe. 'Ten years I've had that heat. You can't blow glass on wanting to.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, prue_complaint). }
  }
  Discovery prue_complaint "The Honourable Florian Mottram laid one of Prue Quickly's souvenir petals on the Rector's desk as the Fire petal without turning it over; the House's Bursar has complained of forgery, and unless it is settled by noon on the third day the House will take back the heat that runs Prue's furnace.".
  Topic bassett_stamp with bassett "Show Sergeant Bassett what is stamped on the back of the petals" when prueTrouble(prue) and not prueSaved(prue) and at(bassett, glasshouse) once {
    Says "The sergeant puts his spectacles on and turns the petal to the furnace light, and reads A PRESENT FROM SENNET aloud, in a voice that makes it sound like a confession. He turns it over again. 'It's not my place to say what's a forgery and what's a present,' he says. 'It's the House's complaint. If the House takes it back, I've nothing to do.' He puts his hat on. 'Get the House to take it back, or get the young gentleman to say it was his mistake. Either will do me.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bassett_terms). }
  }
  Discovery bassett_terms "Sergeant Bassett will let the forgery complaint against Prue Quickly drop if the House withdraws it, or if Florian Mottram says it was his own mistake.".
  // Settled by the Rector (collegium.kyr), who likes to be generous, and remembers it; or by Florian (rivals.kyr).
  Rule prue_saved_told at glasshouse when prueSaved(prue) and at(bassett, glasshouse) says "Sergeant Bassett closes his notebook, and puts on his hat, and says to the furnace, 'Complaint withdrawn,' and goes." {
    Retract at(bassett, glasshouse). Assert at(bassett, offstage). }
  Topic prue_thanks with prue "Tell Prue Quickly the complaint is withdrawn" when prueSaved(prue) and not prueFriend(prue) once {
    Says "She looks at you with her bald, scorched face for a moment, and then she puts down her blowpipe and shakes your hand hard enough to hurt. 'Right,' she says. 'Right. You want glass, you come to me. Anything. I'll make you a chandelier.' She thinks. 'Don't ask for a chandelier.'".
    On discuss { Assert prueFriend(prue). }
  }
  Relation prueFriend(group).
  Rule heat_restored when prueSaved(prue) and furnaceCold(glasshouse) says "In Lamp Street the copper main hums again, and Prue Quickly's furnace roars up like a lion let out." { Retract furnaceCold(glasshouse). }

  // ── A petal of the North Wind ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What Prue could make, given the things to make it with: a jar of the Air plane's own wind, a real petal to copy,
  // and her furnace. Made, it holds up whatever it is set in, as the true one does (door.kyr).
  Topic prue_could with prue "Ask Prue Quickly whether she could make a petal that was not a present" when true once {
    Says "She snorts. Then she looks at the tray of red glass, and stops. 'A real one, you mean. One that does what they do.' She picks up a rod and turns it in the furnace mouth. 'Glass is only sand that's been told what to be by fire. The Rose's petals are glass that's been told by something else: the Fire one by the Fire, the Air one by the wind.' She draws out the rod, glowing. 'Give me a jar of the Air plane's own wind, the real wind, not Cloudgate's, and let me have one of the real petals in my hand an hour to see how it's made, and my heat, and a night.' She looks at you. 'I could make you one that would hold up a hat. Or a house, if it were a big enough hat.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, made_possible). }
  }
  Discovery made_possible "Prue Quickly says that, given a jar of the Air plane's own wind, a real petal of the Rose to copy for an hour, her furnace's heat and a night, she could make a petal of the Rose that does what a real one does.".
  Kind wind_jar_kind "an empty wind-jar" is gear worth 2 weighing 1 described "A stoppered jar of thick green glass, Ollerenshaw's best, sold to Tourists for bringing home a breath of the Plane of Air. It is empty, which is to say full of Sennet.".
  Kind north_wind_kind "a jar of the North Wind" is gear worth 0 weighing -1 described "A stoppered jar of green glass, very cold to hold, that pulls a little upward out of your hand. Inside, something moves that is not anything; frost is growing on the inside of the glass in ferns.".
  Kind made_petal_kind "the petal Prue Quickly made" is treasure worth 0 weighing -6 described "A petal of clear glass the length of your hand, made in Lamp Street, with a fern of frost inside it that never melts, that pulls upward out of your fingers like a kite on a string. On the back, very small, Prue has stamped: A PRESENT FROM SENNET.".
  Item made_petal "the made petal" is made_petal_kind at offstage.
  Relation making(group). Relation madeReady(group). Measure madeSince(group).
  Query seenPetal() means carries(party, fire_petal) or carries(party, earth_petal) or carries(party, water_petal) or carries(party, air_petal).
  Action prue_make(actor: group, site: place) "Give Prue Quickly the jar of the North Wind, and lend her a petal of the Rose for the night, to make one" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(prue, site) and holding(actor, north_wind_kind) and seenPetal()
      and knows(actor, made_possible) and not furnaceCold(glasshouse) and not making(prue) and not madeReady(prue).
    Time 1.
    On success { Spend north_wind_kind from actor. Assert making(prue). Set madeSince(prue) to watch(clock). }
    Result "Prue takes the jar in both hands, and the frost on the inside of it ferns up toward her fingers, and she sucks in her breath. She holds the real petal to the furnace light and turns it, once, twice, the way a jeweller turns a stone she wants to be wrong about. 'Right,' she says, and bars the door. 'Go away. Come back in the morning. Don't let anybody in this street open a window.'".
  }
  Rule made_done when making(prue) and watch(clock) >= madeSince(prue) + 60 and hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 19 {
    Retract making(prue). Assert madeReady(prue). }
  Rule prue_makes_at_night when making(prue) and not at(prue, glasshouse) { Assert at(prue, glasshouse). }
  Observe making_seen at glasshouse when making(prue) "Prue Quickly's door is barred and her shutters are up, and through the cracks of them comes a light that is not furnace-light: white, and cold, like moonlight on snow. The street outside is full of frost in June.".
  Topic prue_made with prue "Ask Prue Quickly whether the petal is made" when madeReady(prue) and at(made_petal, offstage) once {
    Says "She has not slept. Her hands are wrapped in wet rag and she is grinning like a fool. She unwraps something on the bench, carefully, and it lifts off the cloth and stands on its point in the air, turning, a hand's breadth up, until she catches it. 'There,' says Prue Quickly. 'Hold on to it. It wants to go up.' She gives it you, and gives you back the true one. 'It's as good. I'd swear to it in front of the Rector.' She turns it over to show you. 'I stamped it. Old habits.'".
    On discuss { Give made_petal to actor. }
  }

  // ── Ollerenshaw's, outfitters to the Grand Tour ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind fire_cloak_kind "a fire-cloak" like cloak worth 6 weighing 2 described "A long hooded cloak of grey stuff woven with asbestos and soaked in alum, very stiff, smelling of a blacksmith's apron: Ollerenshaw's patent, for the Plane of Fire. In it the heat of the Fire is only very hot.".
  Kind brine_helm_kind "a brine-glass helm" is gear worth 12 weighing 3 described "A bowl of thick glass for the head, with a collar of oiled leather and a bladder on the back that hisses. Ollerenshaw's patent, for the Whelm. Inside it you breathe, of a kind, with your ears full of your own heart.".
  Observe outfitter_scene at outfitter when true "Ollerenshaw's: a long shop like a ship's chandlery for a voyage to nowhere, hung from the beams with fire-cloaks stiff as boards, glass helms in rows on wooden heads, coils of rope, lamps, and green wind-jars in pyramids. Everything has a ticket, and every ticket has been crossed out and written again higher.".
  Person pargeter "Mr. Ollerenshaw" at outfitter {
    Role "an outfitter to the Grand Tour, in a waistcoat of many pockets". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Sells fire_cloak_kind for 6 coin from 4.
    Sells brine_helm_kind for 12 coin from 2.
    Sells wind_jar_kind for 2 coin from 6.
    Sells rope for 1 coin from 5.
    Sells lantern for 7 coin from 3.
    Sells lamp_oil for 1 coin from 8.
    Greets "'Ah!' A thin man in a waistcoat of a great many pockets comes round the counter with both hands out. 'A Tourist! I can always tell. The look of a person who has not yet been anywhere.' He sweeps an arm. 'Fire-cloaks, brine-glass helms, wind-jars, a Tourist's complete necessaire in a calf case at eleven guineas, which I do not recommend to you, as you are clearly a person of sense.'".
    Greets again "'Back!' says Mr. Ollerenshaw, delighted. 'They always come back.'".
  }
  Rule pargeter_hours when openHours() and not at(pargeter, outfitter) { Assert at(pargeter, outfitter). }
  Rule pargeter_home when not openHours() and not at(pargeter, offstage) { Assert at(pargeter, offstage). }
  // The Dowager was born over this shop; he is her brother's son. She has been in it once since she married.
  Topic pargeter_imogen with pargeter "Ask Mr. Ollerenshaw whether he has ever sold to Halyard House" when met(imogen) once {
    Says "'Once.' He straightens a helm on its wooden head that does not need straightening. 'Her Ladyship came in herself, last spring, for a fire-cloak for Mr. Perrin, the best I had. Paid the ticket without looking at it. Didn't look at me, either.' He moves the helm back. 'She was born upstairs. Imogen Ollerenshaw. My father's sister. She went up the chain at nineteen to be a lady's maid, and came down a Halyard, and has not come down since.' He smiles at you with all his teeth. 'I keep her room as it was. In case. You never know, with the Tour, who'll want outfitting.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, imogen_pargeter). }
  }
  Discovery imogen_pargeter "Lady Imogen Halyard was born Imogen Ollerenshaw, over the outfitter's shop in Lamp Street; she went up the chain at nineteen as a lady's maid and married the heir. Mr. Ollerenshaw is her nephew, and keeps her room as it was.".
  Topic pargeter_advice with pargeter "Ask Mr. Ollerenshaw what a Tourist needs" when true once {
    Says "'For the Fire, a cloak. Without one you will be cooked in an hour, a little at a time, like a ham.' He shows you one. 'For the Whelm, a helm, unless you can get one of the sea-folk to kiss you, which I am told lasts three hours and costs nothing, but I could not say, not having been asked.' He sniffs. 'For the Earth, a lamp: it is dark in there, and slow. For the Air, nothing: the sylphs will hold you up out of politeness, but they will talk about you after.' He taps a green jar. 'And a wind-jar, to bring home a breath of it. Very popular with aunts.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, tour_needs). }
  }
  Discovery tour_needs "What a Tourist needs, by Mr. Ollerenshaw: a fire-cloak for the Plane of Fire, or be cooked; a brine-glass helm for the Whelm, or a merfolk kiss, which lasts three hours; a lamp for the Plane of Earth, which is dark; nothing for the Plane of Air. And a wind-jar, to bring home a breath of the Air.".
  // What is worn: a helm while it is held gives breath, a cloak proof against the Fire (W1 of 02-adaptation.md: an
  // item of the module's own cannot yet grant a capability of the module's own).
  Entity heatproof: capability "Proof against the heat of the Fire".
  Rule helm_breath when holding(party, brine_helm_kind) and not granted(party, breath) { Assert granted(party, breath). Set grantedUntil(party, breath) to 0. }
  Rule cloak_proof when holding(party, fire_cloak_kind) and not granted(party, heatproof) { Assert granted(party, heatproof). Set grantedUntil(party, heatproof) to 0. }
  Rule cloak_gone when not holding(party, fire_cloak_kind) and granted(party, heatproof) and grantedUntil(party, heatproof) == 0 { Retract granted(party, heatproof). }
}

Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  // ── The Night of Lanterns ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Ascension Day: the fourth night. On the Promenade, Cloudgate keeps the Lifting: a band, the Dowager's toast, the
  // dancing, and at half past nine a thousand paper lanterns loosed off the rim into the dark. Below, on the black water
  // of the bay, the harbour keeps the Whelming with candles. From the Balustrade, if you look down through the hole in
  // the cloud, you can see both at once.
  Occasion lanterns "the Night of Lanterns" at promenade when lanternNight() and not cloudgateFell(sennet_bay) {
    Matter guests "Cloudgate's guests come up through the cloud in basket after basket, in pale silk, and walk along the Promenade under strings of paper lanterns not yet lit." for 30 minutes.
    Matter toast "The band stops. The Dowager Lady Halyard stands on the steps of Halyard House in black, with a glass, and Cloudgate falls silent for the toast to the Lifting." for 30 minutes.
    Matter dancing "The band strikes up a reel, and Cloudgate dances on the gravel of the Promenade under the stars, which up here are enormous." for 90 minutes.
    Matter loosing "Half past nine. Every house in Cloudgate brings out its lanterns, a thousand of them, paper, lit, and at a sign they are let go off the rim of the Promenade into the dark, all at once, and go up." for 30 minutes.
    Matter supper "Supper is laid in the drawing room of Halyard House, under the portraits." for 60 minutes.
    Closes "The band packs up. The last lanterns are very small and very high. Cloudgate goes to bed in the starlight.".
  }
  Observe lantern_toast at promenade when matterOpen(toast) "The Dowager raises her glass. 'To Ysabeau,' she says, 'who lifted us up out of the damp.' Cloudgate drinks. The Rector of the House of Doors, among the guests in her gown of four colours, drinks too, and catches your eye over the rim of the glass, and smiles.".
  Observe lantern_dancing at promenade when matterOpen(dancing) "Couples go by on the gravel, turning. Aubrey Halyard dances with nobody and drinks with everybody. Florian Mottram dances very badly with Miss Sone, who leads.".
  Observe lantern_loosing at promenade when matterOpen(loosing) "The lanterns go up off the rim of Cloudgate in a single breath, a thousand, gold, turning slowly, rising into a sky so black and full of stars that it looks like the inside of a bell; and the whole of Cloudgate stands with its face turned up, silent, while they go.".
  Observe candles_below at balustrade when lanternNight() "Far below, through a hole in the cloud, on the black water of the bay, there is another field of lights: small, steady, low, a thousand of them, drifting. The harbour's candles for the Whelming, set on the water for the lower town.".
  Observe candles_quay at quay when lanternNight() and aloft() "The harbour is on the Quay with candles, every one of them, in jars and in eggshells and in hollowed loaves, and is setting them on the water one at a time, saying names, so that the bay below Cloudgate is covered with small lights going out with the tide. Overhead, in the black above the cloud, Cloudgate's lanterns are going up.".
  Observe candles_quay_fallen at quay when lanternNight() and not aloft() "The harbour is on the Quay with candles, as it is every year, setting them on the water one at a time and saying names. This year the candles drift out on the tide and fetch up, one after another, against the wet stone of a hill a hundred yards off, and burn there, along its foot, in a ring.".
  Observe candle_bethan at quay when lanternNight() and bethanAtPeace(bethan) "Old Bethan sets one candle on the water, in an eggshell, and says 'Ned Saltash,' and goes home to bed.".
  Relation danced(group). Relation candlesTold(group).

  // ── A dance ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic dance_fabian with fabian "Ask Fabian Murrey to dance" when matterOpen(dancing) and fondness(fabian) >= 3 and not danced(fabian) once {
    Says "He looks at you as if you had asked him to step off the Balustrade. 'I don't. I can't. I've never.' Then he puts his notebook in his pocket, and his pencil behind his ear, where there is one already, and takes your hand. He is a very bad dancer and does not tread on you once. Halfway down the Promenade, under the paper lanterns, he says, not looking at you, 'I've written down every place I've been with you. I haven't written down this.' And you go round again.".
    On discuss { Assert danced(fabian). Increase fondness(fabian) by 1. Increase talk(party) by 1. }
  }
  Topic fabian_beloved with fabian "Tell Fabian Murrey what he is to you" when fondness(fabian) >= 5 and danced(fabian) and not beloved(fabian) once {
    Says "He hears you out, standing very still, with the pencil stopped over his notebook; and when you have finished he puts the pencil down. 'I have written,' says Fabian Murrey, 'four hundred pages about places, and not one line about a person, because Grandmother said people were not what a guidebook is for.' He looks at you. 'She was wrong about the Hour Court. She was wrong about the keel.' He takes your hand, as he did on the Promenade, quite formally, as if he had been taught it out of a book. 'I think she may have been wrong about that too.'".
    On discuss { Assert beloved(fabian). }
  }

  // ── Mercy sees them go up ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule mercy_lanterns at promenade when mercyAloft(mercy) and following(mercy, party) and at(party, promenade) and matterOpen(loosing) and not mercySawLanterns(mercy)
    says "Mercy, in her water-butt on its barrow at the rim of the Promenade, with her chin on the edge and her hair in wet ropes down the staves, watches the lanterns go up. A thousand of them, alive, gold, turning. She does not make a sound. Her gills are quite still. Round her the whole of Cloudgate has turned from the lanterns to look at her, a mermaid on the Promenade on the Night of Lanterns, and she does not notice any of it. When the last of them is only a star she says, to nobody, 'They go up.' And then, louder, and you realise she is speaking to the Dowager, who is standing three feet from the barrow in her black lace with a glass in her hand: 'I caught your son. Out of the sky. He's in my air-bell with his leg broke, eating fish. He says to say he isn't coming home, and he says to say he's sorry about the coffin.' Across the Promenade, among the guests, the Rector of the House of Doors sets her glass down on the rim of the Balustrade, very carefully, and goes to find her cloak." {
    Assert mercySawLanterns(mercy). Increase talk(party) by 3. Assert imogenMetMercy(imogen). Assert heardOf(imogen, perrin_alive). Assert heardOf(quance, perrin_alive). Assert heardOf(florian, perrin_alive). Assert toldAlive(party). }
  // A ring, to show she is telling the truth: his signet, which she wears on her thumb.
  Rule imogen_ring at promenade when mercySawLanterns(mercy) and imogenMetMercy(imogen) and not imogenBelieves(imogen) and at(imogen, promenade)
    says "The Dowager does not move. Then Mercy holds up her hand out of the water, and on her thumb, too big for any finger, is a ring: gold, with a hill on a hand cut in the stone. Lady Imogen Halyard looks at it. The glass goes out of her fingers and breaks on the gravel, and she does not look down at it. She looks at the girl in the butt without blinking, and then, as if every bone in her had been told to, she kneels on the gravel of the Promenade in her black lace, in front of Cloudgate, so that her face is level with the mermaid's, and takes the wet hand with the ring on it in both of hers. 'Thank you,' she says. That is all. Nobody on the Promenade has ever seen her kneel." {
    Assert imogenBelieves(imogen). }
  Rule mercy_home_after when mercySawLanterns(mercy) and following(mercy, party) and (day(clock) >= 5 or hour(clock) < 5) {
    Retract following(mercy, party). Retract mercyUp(mercy). Assert at(mercy, air_bell). Retract mercyAloft(mercy). }

  // ── What the Dowager comes to ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Her son alive, and the girl who saved him, and the candles on the water for the people her family drowned.
  Topic imogen_candles with imogen "Tell Lady Halyard what the harbour is setting on the water tonight, and for whom" when knows(actor, lifting_known) and lanternNight() and not imogenShamed(imogen) once {
    Says "'Candles,' she says. 'I know.' She does not look toward the Balustrade. 'We have always known. We say that it is very pretty, from up here.' She says nothing until the gravel has stopped crunching under someone's boots on the Promenade. 'The street below hers,' she says, very low. 'Chandlers' Row. Her own nurse lived on it. They drowned in their beds so that she could be above the smell of fish. And every year they light candles for them, and we stand up here and drink to her.' She puts her glass down on the rim of the Balustrade, untouched. 'I was born on Lamp Street,' says Lady Halyard. 'Over a shop. I have never once in my life gone down to the Quay on this night.'".
    On discuss { Assert imogenShamed(imogen). }
  }
  Topic imogen_alive_shown with imogen "Tell Lady Halyard that her son is alive, and show her his letter in his own hand" when knows(actor, perrin_alive) and carries(actor, mother_letter) and not imogenBelieves(imogen) once {
    Says "She reads the first line and her face does not change, and she reads the rest, and her face does not change, and she folds it up very small and holds it in her fist against her chest, and stands like that, quite still, in the middle of her drawing room under all the portraits. 'He writes like his father,' she says. 'Abominably.' She does not cry. She says, when the clock on the mantel has struck the quarter, 'Where?' and when you tell her, 'Under the sea,' she shuts her eyes. 'With a girl of the sea-folk. Who caught him.' She opens them. 'Then I owe a girl of the sea-folk my son.'".
    On discuss { Assert imogenBelieves(imogen). Assert heardOf(imogen, perrin_alive). Assert toldAlive(actor). }
  }
  Kind mother_letter_kind "Perrin's letter to his mother" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "A page torn from a drowned book, written over in pencil in a quick, untidy hand: Mother, I am alive, I am sorry about the coffin, it was not Aubrey, I am very happy, please do not come. A girl caught me. Her name is Mercy. Be kind to her if you ever meet her, which you won't. P.".
  Item mother_letter "Perrin's letter to his mother" is mother_letter_kind at offstage.
  Topic perrin_mother with perrin "Ask Perrin Halyard to write to his mother" when perrinWrote(perrin) and not carries(actor, mother_letter) and at(mother_letter, offstage) once {
    Says "He groans. 'Must I?' But he is already tearing out another page. He writes it quickly and badly, crosses out a line, writes it again. 'Tell her not to come down,' he says, giving it you. 'She'd bring a footman.'".
    On discuss { Give mother_letter to actor. }
  }
  Rule imogen_turns when imogenBelieves(imogen) and (imogenMetMercy(imogen) or imogenShamed(imogen)) and not imogenSorry(imogen) { Assert imogenSorry(imogen). }
  Topic imogen_go_up with imogen "Ask Lady Halyard to come up through the Air Door with you, and say it to the North Wind herself" when imogenSorry(imogen) and (knows(actor, tramontane_story) or knows(actor, ysabeau_letters)) and not giftRenewed(sennet_bay) and not following(imogen, party) once {
    Says "'To the North Wind.' She looks at the portrait of the lady in green. 'To say that we are sorry. Two hundred and thirty years late.' Her mouth moves, very slightly. 'Halyards are always late; it is a mark of breeding.' She gets her shawl. 'Very well. Now, before I think better of it. And you will not tell anyone that I was frightened on the stair.'".
    On discuss { Assert following(imogen, party). }
  }
  // She opens the Air Door herself, who keeps its seal.
  Rule imogen_opens when following(imogen, party) and not keyholder(party, air_bar) { Assert keyholder(party, air_bar). }
}

data/adventures/the-grand-tour/lore.kyr:
Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  Description "What Sennet says of itself once the black square has been opened: the Roll in the Hall of Doors, the Remainder's name, and the lamp-keeper's name.".

  // ── World events, read from the House's own Hall ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe lore_roll_chalk at hall_of_doors when befell(remainder_harboured) "Under the last gilt line of the Roll of the Grand Tour someone has chalked, not very straight: RELIQUA, OF THE SLACK. HARBOURED. Mr Threlkeld says it was not him, and that the House does not chalk. The chalk is rubbed off every morning and is back by noon.".
  Observe lore_roll_gone at hall_of_doors when befell(remainder_kept) "Under the last gilt line of the Roll someone has pencilled: RELIQUA, NOT HARBOURED. SAILING. Mr Threlkeld rubs it out each morning. It does not come back, but a smear stays, in the shape of a ship.".

  // ── A name, and where it goes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_sabe_title "Sabe, among the Watch of the Remainder, is what the keeper of the lamp is called; Orrel is the keeper's own name, and has been for eleven generations.".
  Topic lore_sabe_name with sabe "Ask Orrel Sabe why his name is the wrong way round" when true once {
    Says "'It isn't,' says Sabe, mildly. 'The Orrels keep the lamp. The one who keeps it is called Sabe, as the one who keeps the log is called Pursey and the one who rings the bell is called Tolly. It is a post.' He looks at his hands. 'I have heard it said that there is another Orrel somewhere, a woman, who keeps a lamp on a stair, a long way up and a long way off, and is called Sabe by her mother. If there is, I would like her to know that the post was not meant to be hereditary. It is only that there has never been anyone to hand it on to.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_sabe_title). }
  }
  Discovery lore_ship_name "The ship is called the Remainder, in the old marks and in Aenean capitals RELIQUA, after the ninth column of a count whose other eight were filled long ago.".
  Topic lore_tamsin_name with tamsin "Ask Tamsin Quaye how the ship came by her name" when true once {
    Says "'Remainder?' says Tamsin. 'What is left when the sum is done.' She puts her pen behind her ear. 'Eleven generations ago the Watch were told to count something. They counted. When they had counted everything they could, there was a remainder, and the remainder was the ship. It is not a name so much as an entry.' She smiles, a little crookedly. 'There is a place somewhere with a wheel for each kind of being that is counted, and a ninth that is empty. My grandmother used to say that was ours.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_ship_name). }
  }
}

data/adventures/the-grand-tour/murrey.ky:
Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  // ── Fabian Murrey ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Grandson of Dame Philippa Murrey, who did the Tour nine times and wrote the Handbook. Thirty-four. He has written
  // four hundred pages of the seventh edition out of the sixth, in the room over the shop, and has never been through
  // a door: at twelve his grandmother took him to the Fire Door and he fainted in the heat, and she said he had the
  // soul of an index. Frightened, funny, warm; he notices everything and believes none of it is worth writing down
  // unless somebody more important saw it first. If he comes on the Tour he writes the seventh edition as he goes,
  // and what it says depends on what he was shown.
  Person fabian "Fabian Murrey" at murrey_shop {
    Role "a bookseller, long and thin, with ink on his cuffs and a pencil behind each ear" when not travelsWith(fabian, party).
    Role "a guidebook man, with a pencil behind each ear" when travelsWith(fabian, party).
    Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Background scholar. Level 2. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "A long thin man unfolds himself from behind a counter stacked with the same red book, knocks a pile of them over, catches two, and says, 'Murrey's. Handbook for Travellers through the Doors. Sixth edition. Three coin.' He looks at the pile on the floor. 'It's a bit out of date. Forty years. But the planes don't change much, do they?' A pause. 'I wouldn't know.'".
    Greets again "'Oh! You,' says Fabian Murrey, and drops a pencil, and gets down on all fours after it and talks from under the counter. 'Seventh edition. In preparation. I wondered if I might have your account of the Fire. I would give you a credit on the title-page. In very small type. Smaller than Murrey's.'".
    Joins "Fabian Murrey puts on his hat, and takes it off, and puts it on again, and puts a second pencil behind his other ear. 'I'll come,' he says. 'I've a notebook. I'll be no use at all in a fight, I want that understood.' He turns the sign on the shop door to CLOSED, and then, after a moment, turns it back to OPEN. 'Somebody might want a book.'".
    Leaves "'I'll be at the shop,' says Fabian Murrey. 'Writing it down. Come and tell me the rest.'".
  }
  Measure fondness(group).
  Relation fabianAsked(group). Relation fabianDefended(group). Relation fabianShamed(group). Relation fabianWilling(group).
  Relation fabianHome(group). Relation fabianLost(group). Relation beloved(group). Relation fabianTold(group).
  Rule fabian_shop when openHours() and not travelsWith(fabian, party) and not at(fabian, murrey_shop) { Assert at(fabian, murrey_shop). }
  Rule fabian_upstairs when not openHours() and not travelsWith(fabian, party) and not at(fabian, offstage) { Assert at(fabian, offstage). }
  Observe murrey_scene at murrey_shop when true "Murrey's: a narrow shop with a gilt key over the door, every wall shelved to the ceiling with the same red book, MURREY'S HANDBOOK FOR TRAVELLERS THROUGH THE DOORS, and over the counter a portrait of a formidable old woman in a fire-cloak, with one foot on a stone that is plainly from somewhere else.".

  Kind handbook_kind "Murrey's Handbook, sixth edition" is gear worth 3 weighing 1 described "MURREY'S HANDBOOK FOR TRAVELLERS THROUGH THE DOORS, BY DAME PHILIPPA MURREY. SIXTH EDITION. A fat red book on thin paper, with folding maps of planes that do not hold still, and a great many opinions. This copy is a new printing, of last spring, of the edition of forty years ago.".
  Kind philippa_kind "Dame Philippa's own Handbook" is gear worth 0 weighing 1 described "A red book gone brown, swollen, scorched at one corner and stained with salt, that has been through the Doors nine times in a fire-cloak's pocket: the sixth edition, forty years old, the first copy ever printed, with Dame Philippa's own corrections in the margins in green ink, and a pressed flower from the Plane of Air that crumbles if you breathe on it.".
  Item philippa_copy "Dame Philippa's own Handbook" is philippa_kind at offstage.
  Item shop_copy "a Handbook from the pile" is handbook_kind at murrey_shop owned by fabian.
  Action buy_handbook(actor: group, site: place) "Buy a copy of Murrey's Handbook for three coin" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(fabian, site) and at(shop_copy, murrey_shop) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3.
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Increase quantity(fabian, gold) by 3. Assert lends(fabian, shop_copy, actor). Give shop_copy to actor. }
    Result "He wraps it in brown paper, though you are going to carry it under your arm, and ties the string in a bow, and then unties it again to show you the folding map of the Plane of Fire, which does not hold still.".
  }

  Topic fabian_book with fabian "Ask Fabian Murrey about the Handbook" when true once {
    Says "'My grandmother's.' He glances up at the portrait. 'Dame Philippa Murrey. She did the Tour nine times, when it was the fashion, before the fashion went to the spas. She wrote the sixth edition in a single winter, after her ninth, and it's never been out of print.' He touches a copy. 'I'm doing the seventh. I've done four hundred pages.' He clears his throat. 'Out of the sixth. Correcting the commas. I've not been through a door myself, as such.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, handbook_known). }
  }
  Discovery handbook_known "Fabian Murrey is writing the seventh edition of his grandmother's Handbook for Travellers through the Doors, out of the sixth, which is forty years old, without ever having been through a door himself.".
  Topic fabian_doors with fabian "Ask Fabian Murrey why he has never been through a door" when knows(actor, handbook_known) once {
    Says "He takes off his spectacles and cleans them on his tie, which makes them worse. 'When I was twelve she took me to the Fire Door, to start me. It was open. I could see the Hour Court through it, all red. And the heat came out of it like a hand.' He puts them back on. 'I fainted. Into a Doorward. She picked me up off the floor by my collar and said, in front of the whole Hall, Fabian, you have the soul of an index.' He smiles, very slightly. 'She wasn't wrong. I'm a very good index. Guidebook men don't go. They write down where other people went.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, fabian_fear). }
  }
  Discovery fabian_fear "Fabian Murrey fainted at the Fire Door when he was twelve, and his grandmother told the whole Hall he had the soul of an index. He has never been through a door since.".
  Topic fabian_grandmother with fabian "Ask Fabian Murrey what his grandmother was like" when knows(actor, fabian_fear) once {
    Says "'Magnificent.' He says it at once. 'She wore a fire-cloak to dinner. She was crowned in the Hour Court twice, once for showing them a snowball and once for being rude to them, which they'd never had. She called the sylphs a pack of fishwives to their faces and they loved her.' He looks at the portrait. 'She never once in her life asked anybody what they thought of anything. I used to bring her my essays and she'd correct the commas.' He laughs. 'I do the commas now. In her book.' And then, as if he had not meant to say it: 'I'd like to write one sentence she didn't.'".
    On discuss { Increase fondness(fabian) by 1. Assert knows(actor, fabian_wish). }
  }
  Discovery fabian_wish "Fabian Murrey would like to write one sentence of the Handbook that his grandmother did not.".

  // ── Florian at Murrey's ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // On the first afternoon the Honourable Florian Mottram comes into the shop with Miss Sone to buy the Handbook, and
  // finds out what its author's grandson has not done (rivals.kyr has them).
  Query florianInShop() means day(clock) == 1 and hour(clock) >= 15 and hour(clock) < 16.
  Event florian_mocks at murrey_shop when florianInShop() and at(party, murrey_shop) and at(florian, murrey_shop) "The shop bell goes, and a young man in a coat the colour of a sunset comes in with a grey, square woman behind him, and buys four copies of the Handbook without looking at them. 'Murrey,' he says. 'Murrey! You're the grandson. Grandmother was a legend, Papa says. Crowned in the Fire twice.' He beams. 'And you? How many times have you been through, then? Ten? Twenty?' Fabian Murrey says nothing. 'None?' The young man laughs, delightedly, not unkindly, as you would laugh at a dog in a hat. 'You've written a book about it and you've never been! Sone, did you hear? Never been!' Miss Sone, behind him, closes her eyes." then { Assert fabianShamed(fabian). }
  Topic defend_fabian with florian "Tell the Honourable Florian Mottram that Fabian Murrey knows more about the planes than he will learn on the Tour" when fabianShamed(fabian) and at(fabian, ?p) and at(florian, ?p) and not fabianDefended(fabian) once {
    Says "Florian Mottram stops laughing, with his mouth still open. He looks at you, and at Fabian, and at the four red books in his arms. 'Oh,' he says. 'Oh, I say. I didn't mean.' He goes pink to the ears. 'I'm sure he does. I haven't read it. Sone reads it.' Behind him Miss Sone opens her eyes and looks at you with something like interest. When they have gone Fabian Murrey picks a pencil up off the floor that he did not drop, and puts it behind his ear, where there is one already. 'Nobody,' he says, carefully, 'has said anything like that about me in my life.'".
    On discuss { Assert fabianDefended(fabian). Increase fondness(fabian) by 1. }
  }
  Observe fabian_crushed at murrey_shop when fabianShamed(fabian) and not fabianDefended(fabian) and not travelsWith(fabian, party) and at(fabian, murrey_shop) "Fabian Murrey is correcting commas in a proof with great concentration, and does not look up.".

  // ── Asked to come ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // He will not go through a door for a stranger's asking. For someone who has been through one, and promises to
  // bring him back, he will.
  Query beenThrough() means been(party, fire_threshold) or been(party, earth_threshold) or been(party, air_threshold) or been(party, drowned_stair).
  Topic fabian_ask with fabian "Ask Fabian Murrey to come with you on the Tour" when knows(actor, handbook_known) and not fabianAsked(fabian) and not travelsWith(fabian, party) once {
    Says "He drops the book he is holding, and picks it up, and sees that you mean it. 'Me? I'd faint. I'd faint and you'd have to carry me, and I'm all elbows.' He picks up a book and puts it down. 'Have you been through? Any of them?' He looks at your face. 'No. Then you don't know either.' He shakes his head. 'Go through one. Come back and tell me what it was really like, and not what she says it's like.' He taps the red book. 'Then ask me again.'".
    On discuss { Assert fabianAsked(fabian). }
  }
  Topic fabian_told_through with fabian "Tell Fabian Murrey what it was really like, through the door" when fabianAsked(fabian) and beenThrough() and not fabianTold(fabian) once {
    Says "He listens to all of it with his pencil stopped over his notebook and does not write a word. When you have finished he looks at the portrait until the lamp needs trimming. 'She never said it smelt like that,' he says. 'She never said anything was frightening. She said the Hour Court was vulgar.' He puts the pencil down. 'If I came,' he says, very quietly, 'would you bring me back? Not her way. Your way. Would you promise?'".
    On discuss { Assert fabianTold(fabian). Increase fondness(fabian) by 1. }
  }
  Topic fabian_promise with fabian "Promise Fabian Murrey you will bring him home" answering fabian_told_through when fabianTold(fabian) and not fabianWilling(fabian) once {
    Says "'All right,' says Fabian Murrey, and swallows. 'All right. I'll hold you to it, mind. I'll write it down.' He does: you watch him write it in the notebook, in a small careful hand, and underline it. Then he goes up the stairs at the back of the shop two at a time, and comes down with a red book gone brown, scorched at one corner, and holds it out to you. 'Hers,' he says. 'The first copy. She took it through nine times. You carry it. My hands shake.'".
    On discuss { Assert fabianWilling(fabian). Increase fondness(fabian) by 1. Assert willing(fabian, actor). Set hire(fabian) to 0. Assert promiseMade(fabian_home). Give philippa_copy to actor. Assert lends(fabian, philippa_copy, actor). Increase fondness(fabian) by 1. }
  }
  Promise fabian_home "to bring Fabian Murrey home from the Tour" to fabian
    kept when fabianHome(party) "Fabian Murrey sits down on his own stool behind his own counter, and puts both hands flat on it, as if it might go somewhere."
    broken when fabianLost(party) "Somewhere a line is drawn through a promise you wrote in a notebook." { }.
  // Home: back in the shop from wherever the Tour took him, with the Tour behind him.
  Rule fabian_home_again when fabianWilling(fabian) and beenWith() and at(party, murrey_shop) and not travelsWith(fabian, party) and at(fabian, murrey_shop) and not fabianHome(party) { Assert fabianHome(party). }
  Rule fabian_back_through when fabianWilling(fabian) and travelsWith(fabian, party) and beenWith() and at(party, murrey_shop) and not fabianHome(party) and doorOpen(sennet_bay) { Assert fabianHome(party). }
  Relation wentWith(group).
  Query beenWith() means wentWith(fabian).
  Rule fabian_went when travelsWith(fabian, party) and inPlanes() and not wentWith(fabian) { Assert wentWith(fabian). }
  // A member slain leaves the company, and is a member of their own again (memberOf), not joinedAs: either holds.
  Rule fabian_falls when (joinedAs(?m, fabian) or memberOf(?m, fabian)) and slain(?m) and not fabianLost(party) { Assert fabianLost(party). }

  // ── On the road ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic fabian_how with fabian travelling "Ask Fabian how he is bearing up" when inPlanes() once {
    Says "'I haven't fainted.' He sounds astonished. 'I keep waiting to. I've been holding the notebook ready, in case.' He looks round him at the place, at all of it, with his mouth a little open. 'She said vulgar,' he says. 'It's not vulgar. It's the least vulgar thing I've ever seen.' And he writes that down.".
    On discuss { Increase fondness(fabian) by 1. }
  }
  Topic fabian_notebook with fabian travelling "Ask Fabian what he has written so far" when wentWith(fabian) once {
    Says "He shows you. It is not like the Handbook at all. It is short, and written in pencil, and crossed out, and some of it is about the places and a good deal of it is about the people, including, you notice, you. He takes it back before you can read that part. 'It's not ready,' he says. 'It's only true.'".
  }

  // His fondness, shown where he shows everything: in what he writes.
  Relation fabianWe(group). Relation fabianSigned(group).
  Rule fabian_we when travelsWith(fabian, party) and fondness(fabian) >= 3 and not fabianWe(fabian)
    says "Fabian is writing in his notebook as you walk, and you see over his shoulder that he has stopped writing 'the traveller', as his grandmother did, in every line for four hundred pages. He has started writing 'we'." { Assert fabianWe(fabian). }
  Rule fabian_signed when travelsWith(fabian, party) and fondness(fabian) >= 5 and not fabianSigned(fabian)
    says "At the foot of a page, under 'we', Fabian has written your name, and crossed it out, and written it again." { Assert fabianSigned(fabian). }
}

data/adventures/the-grand-tour/placed.ky:
Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  // A province of a generated world's first country: the company that comes down the coast road is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  // What the country's towns say of Sennet (the Rector's proclamation, nailed up where travellers are kept): once
  // the Tour is settled, one way or another, it is old news there, and they say so to whoever comes back.
  Entity word: fact "What is said of Sennet and its Grand Tour in the towns of the country.".
  Rule word_old when (doorOpen(sennet_bay) or cloudgateFell(sennet_bay) or closingDay()) and not stale(word) { Assert stale(word). }
}

data/adventures/the-grand-tour/rector.ky:
Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  // ── What the Rector does, if nobody stops her ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // She has proclaimed the Tour so that others will bring her the three petals the courts still keep. Florian and
  // Miss Sone bring her the Fire (second day) and the Earth (fourth). On the fourth day she buys six brine-glass helms
  // and six harpoons on the House's account, and at dawn on the sixth her divers go down into the Whelm for the Water
  // petal, among people who have never been attacked. On the seventh night, with three, she goes down the keel
  // ladder for the fourth, and the hill falls into its hole on the Whelm, and she sets the Rose and goes through the
  // Door of Doors and is not seen again. Every step is her own; each can be stopped.
  Relation raided(group). Relation raidRepulsed(group). Relation divers(group). Relation huntTried(group).
  Relation rectorHunted(group). Relation rectorSawCompany(group). Relation keelTried(group).
  Query rectorThree() means rectorHas(fire_petal) and rectorHas(earth_petal) and rectorHas(water_petal).
  Query rectorAll() means rectorThree() and rectorHas(air_petal).
  // ── The divers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule divers_ordered when day(clock) >= 4 and rectorFree() and not petalTaken(water_petal) and not divers(quance) { Assert divers(quance). }
  Topic pargeter_trade with pargeter "Ask Mr. Ollerenshaw how trade is, with the Tour on" when divers(quance) once {
    Says "'Marvellous! The House bought six brine-glass helms yesterday, on the Rector's own account.' He rubs his hands. 'And six harpoons. Whaling, I said to the clerk, ha ha.' He stops rubbing them. 'He didn't laugh. Nobody in the House laughs, this week.' He looks at you over his spectacles. 'What does a college want with harpoons, under the water? There's nothing down there but the sea-folk.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, rector_divers). }
  }
  Discovery rector_divers "On the fourth day the House of Doors bought six brine-glass helms and six harpoons from Ollerenshaw's, on the Rector's own account. There is nothing under the bay to use them on but the merfolk.".
  Topic warn_admittance with admittance "Warn No Admittance that dry men are coming down with harpoons for the Water petal" when knows(actor, rector_divers) and not whelmWarned(admittance) and not raided(quance) once {
    Says "She does not ask how you know. 'Harpoons.' She looks at her people at their supper, the children, the old man in the drowned armchair. 'In my Guildhall.' Her hand goes up to the crown. 'We have never been hunted. We came through the Door to a town already drowned; nobody was left to hunt us.' She stands up out of the mayor's chair. 'Then we will be awake.' She gives orders, in bubbles, low and quick, and the merfolk get up from the table and go, and you hear, through the water, all down Chandlers' Row, doors being shut.".
    On discuss { Assert whelmWarned(admittance). }
  }
  Person house_divers "the House's divers" at offstage {
    Role "six men in brine-glass helms with harpoons". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 3. Numbers 3. Pronouns they.
    Arrives "Down the drowned street, out of the green, come men in brine-glass helms with harpoons, walking along the bottom in lead boots, slow, with the bladders on their backs hissing.".
  }
  Rule raid_down when day(clock) == 6 and hour(clock) >= 5 and rectorFree() and not petalTaken(water_petal) and not raided(quance) and at(party, guildhall) and not whelmWarned(admittance) {
    Assert at(house_divers, guildhall). Assert assails(house_divers, party). Assert raided(quance). Assert raidFought(party). }
  Relation raidFought(group).
  Rule raid_beaten when raidFought(party) and not able(house_divers) and not raidRepulsed(quance) says "The last of the divers goes up toward the light kicking, without his harpoon. The merfolk come out of the doors of Chandlers' Row, slowly, and look at you." {
    Assert raidRepulsed(quance). Assert admittanceTrusts(admittance). Assert at(house_divers, offstage). }
  Rule raid_won when raidFought(party) and not able(party) and able(house_divers) and not petalTaken(water_petal) {
    Assert petalTaken(water_petal). Assert rectorHas(water_petal). Assert keeps(quance, water_petal). Increase rectorPetals(sennet_bay) by 1. Assert whelmRaided(admittance). }
  Rule raid_unseen when day(clock) == 6 and hour(clock) >= 5 and rectorFree() and not petalTaken(water_petal) and not raided(quance) and not at(party, guildhall) {
    Assert raided(quance). }
  Rule raid_repulsed when raided(quance) and whelmWarned(admittance) and not raidFought(party) and not raidRepulsed(quance) { Assert raidRepulsed(quance). }
  Rule raid_takes when raided(quance) and not whelmWarned(admittance) and not raidFought(party) and not petalTaken(water_petal) {
    Assert petalTaken(water_petal). Assert rectorHas(water_petal). Assert keeps(quance, water_petal). Increase rectorPetals(sennet_bay) by 1. Assert whelmRaided(admittance). }
  Relation whelmRaided(group).
  Rule raid_news within sennet_town when whelmRaided(admittance) and not raidNews(party)
    says "On the Quay they are saying that men in helms came up the Fish Stairs at six this morning with harpoons, and one of the harpoons had blood on it that was not red, and that they went up the headland to the House without a word to anybody." { Assert raidNews(party). }
  Rule repulse_news within sennet_town when raidRepulsed(quance) and not raidNews(party)
    says "On the Quay they are saying that men in helms came up the Fish Stairs at six this morning without their harpoons, and one of them bitten through the leg, and would not say what by." { Assert raidNews(party). }
  Relation raidNews(group).
  Observe whelm_after_raid at guildhall when whelmRaided(admittance) and at(admittance, guildhall) "No Admittance sits in the mayor's chair with her arm bound up in weed, and no crown. The Guildhall is very quiet. Nobody looks at you.".
  Rule raided_hostile when whelmRaided(admittance) and not admittanceTrusts(admittance) and not whelmHostile(party) { Assert whelmHostile(party). Retract tolerates(guard, party). Retract admitted(party). }

  // ── What she does when she hears Perrin Halyard is alive ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At two in the morning after she hears it, she goes down into the Whelm in the House's helm, to the air-bell.
  Query perrinGuarded() means perrinUp(party) or perrinMoved(party) or whelmWarned(admittance) or at(party, air_bell) or not at(perrin, air_bell).
  Rule rector_hunts when heardOf(quance, perrin_alive) and rectorFree() and hour(clock) == 2 and not huntTried(quance) and not perrinDead(party) and perrinGuarded() and at(party, air_bell)
    says "Something comes up through the hole in the floor of the air-bell, slowly: a bowl of glass, a collar of leather, a gown of four colours gone dark with the sea. The Rector stands up in the air of the bell in a brine-glass helm, with her keys on their chain, dripping, and takes the helm off, and sees you. She looks at you, and the water runs off her chin onto the boards, and she lets it. Then she looks at Perrin Halyard, who is awake now, and white. 'Another night,' she says, quite pleasantly, and puts the helm back on, and goes down through the floor again." teaches rector_came {
    Assert huntTried(quance). Assert rectorSawCompany(quance). }
  Discovery rector_came "At two in the morning the Rector came up into the air-bell in a brine-glass helm, found the company there with Perrin Halyard, said 'Another night,' and went.".
  Rule rector_hunt_balked when heardOf(quance, perrin_alive) and rectorFree() and hour(clock) == 2 and not huntTried(quance) and not perrinDead(party) and perrinGuarded() and not at(party, air_bell) {
    Assert huntTried(quance). }
  Rule rector_kills when heardOf(quance, perrin_alive) and rectorFree() and hour(clock) == 2 and not huntTried(quance) and not perrinDead(party) and not perrinGuarded() {
    Assert huntTried(quance). Assert perrinDead(party). Assert rectorHunted(quance). Retract at(perrin, air_bell). Assert at(perrin, offstage). }
  Rule perrin_found_dead at fish_stairs when rectorHunted(quance) and perrinDead(party) and not deathNews(party) and hour(clock) >= 7 and at(party, fish_stairs)
    says "A merfolk child is sitting on the third step of the Fish Stairs, not selling anything, with her face in her hands. When you come near, Ha'penny looks up. 'Somebody came into the air-bell in the night,' she says. 'Mercy's sky-man. He's on the bottom now. She won't come out.'" { Assert deathNews(party). }
  Relation deathNews(group).

  // ── The keel, on the seventh night, or as soon as she knows she is known ─────────────────────────────────────────
  Query keelNight() means (day(clock) == 7 and hour(clock) >= 22) or (heardOf(quance, quance_pushed) and hour(clock) >= 22).
  // A keepsake renewed does not come out for her: she goes down the ladder with her case and comes up with it empty.
  Rule rector_balked when keelNight() and rectorFree() and rectorThree() and giftRenewed(sennet_bay) and not keelTried(quance) {
    Assert keelTried(quance). Assert rectorBalked(quance). }
  Relation rectorBalked(group).
  Rule rector_to_keel when keelNight() and rectorFree() and rectorThree() and state(keel_rose, set) and not giftRenewed(sennet_bay) and not keelTried(quance) {
    Assert keelTried(quance). Assert rectorAbout(quance). Assert at(quance, keel). Set keelAt(quance) to watch(clock). }
  Measure keelAt(group).
  Event rector_at_keel at keel when at(party, keel) and at(quance, keel) and keelTried(quance) and state(keel_rose, set) "The keel ladder rings, and someone comes down it, slow and sure, in a gown of four colours with the sleeves tied back, and a chain of keys that chimes at every rung; and steps off onto the ledge, and sees you, and stops. The Rector has a black case under her arm. 'Oh, my dear,' says Isadora Quance. 'Oh, I am sorry it's you.' She looks past you at the petal in the rock, pouring its cold wind down into the cloud. 'Come with me,' she says. 'I mean it. Stand aside, and come up the tower with me tonight, and we'll go through it together, both of us, first. Nobody else alive will ever have done it.' She smiles at you, and it is the same smile, the one that makes you feel you have been waiting all your life to be talked to. 'Well?'" then { Assert rectorOffers(party). }
  Relation rectorOffers(group).
  // Before the choice, she will answer two questions, and the answers are the whole of her.
  Topic rector_why with quance "Ask the Rector why she pushed Perrin Halyard" when rectorOffers(party) and at(party, keel) and state(keel_rose, set) once {
    Says "'I didn't push him.' She says it reasonably, as she says everything. 'I put my hands on his back. It is not the same, though I don't expect a court to see it.' The keys chime; she stills them with her other hand. 'He came to my study with it, so pleased. The Air petal in the keel of Cloudgate. And he was going to give it back to the wind. To the wind, my dear, which has never once wanted anything but to be talked about.' She looks along the ledge at the petal. 'I have been second through every door of my life. I was not going to be second to weather.'".
  }
  Topic rector_under with quance "Ask the Rector what is under the hill, where it will come down" when rectorOffers(party) and at(party, keel) and state(keel_rose, set) once {
    Says "'Under it?' For a moment she genuinely does not understand you. 'The bay. Chandlers' Row, what's left of it. Fish.' Then she does understand, and her face does a thing you have seen on the Promenade, on the faces of people looking at the view. 'The sea-folk. Yes. I suppose so.' She shrugs, very slightly, in her gown of four colours. 'I was born under that hill, you know, on Fish Street. Nobody up here ever came down to tell us anything. I don't see why I should go down to tell them.'".
  }
  Topic join_rector with quance "Stand aside, and go with the Rector" when rectorOffers(party) and at(party, keel) and state(keel_rose, set) once {
    Grave "Cloudgate stands on that petal. Taken out, the hill will come down where it came from, on the Whelm.".
    Says "You stand aside. She goes past you along the ledge, and puts her hand to the petal in the rock, and takes it out. The wind stops. Above you the hill settles, the way a sleeper turns over. 'Come,' she says, and takes your arm.".
    On discuss { Assert state(keel_rose, taken). Assert rectorHas(air_petal). Assert petalTaken(air_petal). Assert descending(sennet_bay). Set descent(sennet_bay) to 0. Assert rectorTookKeel(quance). Assert accomplice(party). Assert at(quance, nexus). Assert at(party, nexus). }
  }
  Relation accomplice(group).
  Topic refuse_rector with quance "Tell the Rector no, and stand between her and the petal" when rectorOffers(party) and at(party, keel) and state(keel_rose, set) and not refusedRector(party) once {
    Says "'No?' She looks genuinely surprised, and then, oddly, pleased, as a teacher is when a student says something unexpected. 'No. Well.' She sets the black case down on the ledge, carefully. 'I had so hoped,' says the Rector, and takes off her rings.".
    On discuss { Assert refusedRector(party). Retract peaceable(quance). Assert assails(quance, party). }
  }
  Relation refusedRector(group).
  Topic over_rector with quance "Tell the Rector it is over: Perrin Halyard is alive, and up, and Cloudgate knows" when rectorOffers(party) and at(party, keel) and perrinUp(party) and not rectorFled(quance) once {
    Says "For a long moment she does not move at all. Then she laughs, very quietly, a real laugh, at herself. 'Up,' she says. 'Of course he is. He always did come back up, that boy, whatever you threw him into.' She looks at the petal in the rock, and at the black case under her arm, and at you. 'Say it where it can't be unsaid,' she says. 'I taught him that.' She sets the case down on the ledge at your feet, very gently, as if it might wake. 'Mind the petals. They're the only things I ever earned.' And she goes back up the keel ladder, rung by rung, with her keys chiming, and you do not see her again.".
    On discuss { Assert rectorFled(quance). Retract rectorHas(fire_petal). Retract rectorHas(earth_petal). Retract rectorHas(water_petal). Give fire_petal to actor. Give earth_petal to actor. Give water_petal to actor. Assert at(quance, offstage). }
  }
  // Nobody there to stop her, or nobody who did in time: she takes it, and the hill comes down.
  Rule rector_takes_keel at keel when keelTried(quance) and at(quance, keel) and state(keel_rose, set) and rectorFree() and able(quance) and watch(clock) >= keelAt(quance) + 2 and not refusedRector(party)
    says "'Well,' says the Rector gently, when you have neither come nor stood in her way, 'I did ask.' She goes past you along the ledge, close enough that her sleeve brushes your face, and puts her hand to the petal in the rock, and takes it out. The wind stops. Above you the hill settles, the way a sleeper turns over. She is up the ladder before you have moved, quick and sure, with the case under her arm, and the chain of keys chiming at every rung." {
    Assert state(keel_rose, taken). Assert rectorHas(air_petal). Assert petalTaken(air_petal). Assert descending(sennet_bay). Set descent(sennet_bay) to 0. Assert rectorTookKeel(quance). Assert at(quance, nexus). }
  Rule rector_beaten when refusedRector(party) and not able(quance) and not rectorTaken(quance)
    says "The Rector lies on the ledge with her gown spread round her and her keys under her hand, breathing, looking up at the underside of Cloudgate. 'I was very good,' she says. 'I was very, very good, you know.' Footsteps on the ladder: Halyard footmen, and behind them, for some reason, Sergeant Bassett of the Watch, who has never been up the chain in his life and is green." {
    Assert rectorTaken(quance). Retract rectorHas(fire_petal). Retract rectorHas(earth_petal). Retract rectorHas(water_petal). Give fire_petal to party. Give earth_petal to party. Give water_petal to party. Assert at(quance, offstage). }

  // ── The Rector with four petals sets the Rose and goes through ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule rector_sets_rose when rectorAll() and rectorFree() and at(quance, nexus) and not doorOpen(sennet_bay) {
    Assert doorOpen(sennet_bay). Assert roseMade(sennet_bay). Set openedAt(sennet_bay) to watch(clock). Assert socketed(fire_petal). Assert socketed(earth_petal). Assert socketed(water_petal). Assert socketed(air_petal). Set socketCount(nexus) to 4. }
  // Given the fourth, by a student who did as she was told: she does not wait for night.
  Event rector_climbs near quance when rectorAll() and rectorFree() and not doorOpen(sennet_bay) and not at(quance, nexus) and not keelTried(quance) and not rectorClimbing(quance)
    "The Rector closes the black case on the four petals and stands up. 'You have done everything I asked,' she says, 'and done it beautifully, and I shall say so in the Courant.' She takes her chain of keys off the hook. 'Come up and watch, if you like. Someone ought to.' And she goes out, and up the tower stair, not hurrying, with the case under her arm, and leaves the tower door open behind her." then {
    Assert rectorClimbing(quance). Assert rectorAbout(quance). Set climbAt(quance) to watch(clock). Assert state(tower_lock, open). }
  // (A moment later: an event that moved her at once would not be told, nor would the petal given with it.)
  Relation rectorClimbing(group). Measure climbAt(group).
  Rule rector_at_top when rectorClimbing(quance) and rectorFree() and not doorOpen(sennet_bay) and not at(quance, nexus) and watch(clock) >= climbAt(quance) + 1 {
    Assert at(quance, nexus). Assert rectorAbout(quance). }
  Rule rector_opens_seen at nexus when rectorAll() and at(quance, nexus) and doorOpen(sennet_bay) and at(party, nexus) and not rectorSeenOpen(party)
    says "The Rector sets the four petals in the rose of the Door of Doors one after another, quickly, without looking, as if she had done it in her sleep a thousand times; and turns the Rose, and the Door opens on everywhere, and the wind of everywhere comes into the Nexus and lifts the hair off her forehead. She stands looking at it with her hands at her sides. 'Oh,' says Isadora Quance, very softly, like a girl." { Assert rectorSeenOpen(party). }
  Relation rectorSeenOpen(group).
  Rule rector_goes_through when doorOpen(sennet_bay) and at(quance, nexus) and rectorFree() and not firstThrough(party) and watch(clock) >= openedAt(sennet_bay) + 2 and not accomplice(party) and not rectorBarred(quance) {
    Assert rectorThrough(quance). Retract at(quance, nexus). Assert at(quance, offstage). }
  Rule rector_follows when doorOpen(sennet_bay) and at(quance, nexus) and rectorFree() and firstThrough(party) and not rectorThrough(quance) and not rectorBarred(quance) and watch(clock) >= firstAt(party) + 1
    says "The Rector steps through the Door of Doors after you, into everywhere, without looking back; and does not come out again on this side, whatever you think of." {
    Assert rectorThrough(quance). Retract at(quance, nexus). Assert at(quance, offstage). }
  // An accomplice is let go first, as she promised: she keeps her word, being vain.
  Rule accomplice_first when accomplice(party) and doorOpen(sennet_bay) and at(party, nexus) and not firstThrough(party)
    says "'You first,' says the Rector. 'You won. I said so.' She is laughing. Behind you, over the bay, a whole hill is coming down out of the sky." { Assert firstThrough(party). Assert doorward(party). }
  // Opened from below or by the company's Rose, the door brings her running up the tower stair.
  Rule rector_comes_running when doorOpen(sennet_bay) and rectorFree() and not rectorAll() and not at(quance, nexus) and not rectorThrough(quance) and within(quance, sennet_town) {
    Assert at(quance, nexus). Assert rectorAbout(quance). Assert rectorCame(quance). }
  Relation rectorCame(group). Relation rectorBarred(group).
  Rule rector_arrives_seen at nexus when rectorCame(quance) and at(quance, nexus) and at(party, nexus) and not rectorArrivalTold(party)
    says "Feet on the tower stair, running, and the tower door bangs back: the Rector of the House of Doors, with her gown of four colours flying and her chain of keys in her fist, stops in the doorway of the Nexus and sees the Door of Doors standing open on everywhere, and you beside it. She does not say anything at all. She looks past you, at it, the way a woman looks at a sea she has walked a long way to see." { Assert rectorArrivalTold(party). }
  Relation rectorArrivalTold(group).
  Action bar_rector(actor: group, site: place) "Stand in the doorway of the Door of Doors, and bar the Rector's way" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, nexus) and at(quance, site) and doorOpen(sennet_bay) and rectorFree() and not rectorBarred(quance).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert rectorBarred(quance). }
    Result "You step into the doorway, with everywhere at your back, and she stops a yard from you. For a moment you think she will try; she is taller than you, and has her keys in her fist, and you have seen what is in her face. Then she laughs, a little, and sits down on the floor of the Nexus in her gown of four colours, with her back against the wall, and looks at the Door over your shoulder. 'I shall sit here, then,' says Isadora Quance, 'and look at it. Nobody can stop me looking.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/the-grand-tour/remainder:
Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  Description "The Remainder: a ship that lies in the pause between counts, her Watch, her hold of things that did not divide, and a choice about what is to be done with her.".

  Thing remainder "the Remainder" at hours_quay {
    State berthed "The Remainder lies at the Quay of Hours.".
    State out "The Remainder is away from the quay.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(remainder, berthed).
  Measure slackWatches(group). Measure interestOwed(group). Measure mechAt(entity). Measure trust(group). Measure boardedAt(group). Measure pinned(group).
  Relation allowed(group). Relation counted(group). Relation tariffed(group). Relation surety(group). Relation faceGiven(group).
  Relation harboured(entity). Relation keptInSlack(entity). Relation mechanusSeen(entity). Relation boarded(group).

  // ── The Slack keeps its own interest ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Hours spent below are paid twice: once as they pass, and again, as long on the stair, when the company climbs
  // it. The Count keeps its books. (The world's clock goes on all the while.)
  Query inSlack(g: group) means at(g, shaft_head) or at(g, hours_quay) or at(g, rem_deck) or at(g, rem_count) or at(g, rem_watch) or at(g, rem_hold).
  Rule slack_tick when company(party) and inSlack(party) { Increase slackWatches(party) by 1. }
  // The interest is charged for real: the climb takes as many watches as were spent below, to a ceiling of a day.
  Rule slack_interest_accrues when company(party) and inSlack(party) and interestOwed(party) < 144 { Increase interestOwed(party) by 1. }
  Action climb_out(actor: group, site: place) "Climb the black stair back to the Nexus" {
    Description "A long stair, and the light at the top growing gold. The Count will have its interest.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, shaft_head).
    Time interestOwed(actor).
    On success { Retract at(actor, shaft_head). Assert at(actor, nexus). Assert tariffed(actor). Set interestOwed(actor) to 0. }
    Result "You climb. It is a very long stair and it takes the whole of the afternoon, and when you come out into the Nexus there are lamps lit that were not lit when you went down, and Mr Threlkeld is sitting on the stair of the tower with his hat in his lap, looking at the black square as if it had been rude to him.".
  }
  Rule slack_interest when tariffed(party) and at(party, nexus) and slackWatches(party) > 0 and not interestPaid(party)
    says "The lamps are lit in the House, and the porter says it is the third morning since you went in. He is not entirely sure what he means by it. In the Nexus the cold of the black square comes up through your boots, and you have the feeling of having been tallied." {
    Assert interestPaid(party).
  }
  Relation interestPaid(group).

  // ── The Watch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person sabe "Orrel Sabe" at rem_deck {
    Role "Captain of the Slow Watch of the Remainder". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Level 6. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Likeness "abbess".
    Greets "A very old man is seated on a coil of something at the foot of the mast with a slate on his knee, counting under his breath. He counts to eleven, and stops, and begins again. 'The eleventh,' he says, finishing, and does not look up. 'The Watch does not speak to a stranger before the second bell. There is a bench.'".
  }
  Person tamsin "Tamsin Quaye" at rem_count {
    Role "Reckoner of the Second Watch". Ancestry human. Calling mage. Level 4. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner jovial.
    Likeness "scholar".
    Greets "A young woman with ink to the elbows has the rods and beads of the count-room spread across the table in a pattern she is plainly trying to break. 'Don't touch,' she says. 'No. Do touch. Touch something else. I need the table to be wrong.' She looks up properly, and is silent for a moment. 'You are real,' she says. 'Good. I had decided to be disappointed.'".
  }
  Person quartermaster "the Quartermaster" at hours_quay {
    Role "a tall grey figure at the foot of the gangway, with a smooth blank face". Species automaton. Level 8.
    Wants keeper_face.
  }
  Person watch "the Watch of the Remainder" at rem_watch {
    Role "the Watch". Ancestry human. Numbers 22. Peaceable.
  }
  Initially Assert allowed(sabe).
  Observe quartermaster_scene at hours_quay when not faceGiven(party) "At the head of the gangway stands a tall grey figure with its long arms at its sides and a smooth blank oval where a face should be. It does not move. It has been waiting a very long time and gives no sign of having minded.".
  Topic sabe_slack with sabe "Ask Captain Sabe where the ship is" when secondBell(actor) once {
    Says "Sabe does not answer at once. He gets up, which takes him a while, and walks you to the lee rail, and stands with you looking at the low place in the sky where the ruling thins. At the dishes the old woman draws her line a third time in the first heap. 'She carries what would not divide,' he says at last. 'That is all of it that can be said in a sentence.' He nods at the sky, and lets you look.".
    On discuss { Assert counted(actor). }
  }
  Topic sabe_roll with sabe "Ask Captain Sabe about the names on the ship's roll" when counted(actor) once {
    Says "'Two rolls,' says Sabe. 'One. Two.' He lifts a finger for each, as if you might lose count. 'The first is in the marks we do not read. We copy it out every Watch, and each copy is a little less like the one before, and no one can say now what it was a copy of. The second was never in the Watch's hand. Forty names. Thirty-eight with a line through.' He lays the slate face down on his knee. 'Tamsin says the Watch wrote it to account for the names painted on the bulkhead. I say someone was here. We have agreed to count it either way.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, roll_two). }
  }
  Discovery roll_two "The Remainder keeps two rolls: one in marks nobody reads, one in a hand that is not the Watch's, forty names, thirty-eight struck through. The Captain believes it was written by someone who was there. The Reckoner thinks the Watch wrote it to explain the names on the bulkhead.".
  Topic sabe_want with sabe "Ask Captain Sabe what the Watch wants" when counted(actor) once {
    Says "'Nothing,' says Sabe. 'One. We keep the hours. Two. We keep the remainders. Three.' He seems to look for a third, and to be content without it. 'My mother said it to me by that rail, and her mother to her: nothing is required but that the count be kept.' His hands are folded on the slate. 'My Reckoner thinks otherwise. She is young, and the pin has moved.'".
  }
  Topic tamsin_count with tamsin "Ask Tamsin Quaye what she is trying to break" when secondBell(actor) once {
    Says "'The count,' she says. 'Ours. The ship's.' She puts down a bead. 'For nine hundred of our years the pin on that chart has been in the same place. Last year it moved. A hair.' She looks at it. 'The Captain says it is a cold week. When the slack ends the count has us, and everything in the hold, and it will not be unkind about it.'".
    On discuss { Assert counted(actor). Assert knows(actor, slack_thin). }
  }
  Discovery slack_thin "The Reckoner of the Remainder says the Slack is thinning: the pin on the chart has moved by a hair, and when the slack ends the count will take the ship and everything in her hold, and her Watch.".
  Topic tamsin_harbour with tamsin "Ask Tamsin Quaye what she wants done" when knows(actor, slack_thin) once {
    Says "'Harbour,' says Tamsin. 'A real one, with a quay that stays where you tie to it.' She taps the ceiling with the end of a rod, twice, as you knock on a neighbour's wall. 'There's a stair over our heads and a House with a lamp at the top. The log says the Prefect's household went up it eleven generations ago and did not come down. I mean to go up it myself, with twenty-two people and seven years' bedding, and I won't take them into a dark I haven't seen.' She sets the rod down. 'A harbour wants a surety. Somebody to say these are ours to keep, and sign. I'd thought: whoever comes down the stair. And here you are, with wet boots.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, surety_asked). }
  }
  Discovery surety_asked "Tamsin Quaye asks the company to stand surety for the Remainder's Watch and her hold, so that they may be harboured in the House above.".

  // ── The hold of remainders ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Thing jar_bend "a stoppered jar the size of a boat" at rem_hold {
    Tries looking.
    State standing "A big stoppered jar on a rack. Its card says REMAINDER 4, and under it a name in the old marks, and under that in a later hand, in Aenean letters: LUNAE FLEXUS. A bend of the Lune. Through the glass something moves, slowly, wet.".
  }
  Observe bend_looked near jar_bend when tried(jar_bend, looking) "It is a river's bend. Not water: a bend, the shape of a bend, with the willows still on the outside of it and a heron standing on one leg in the shallows, every detail present, nothing for it to be attached to. The heron turns its head. The card says that the Lune was straightened, in a year the card does not give, and that this is what the straightening left.".
  Thing winter_chest "a long locked chest, white with frost" at rem_hold {
    Tries looking.
    State shut "A long iron chest with frost on its lid and frost on the floor round it, in a warm hold.".
    State opened dangerous "The lid of the iron chest stands open, and out of it comes a cold like a hand on the back of the neck.".
    Change lift "Lift the lid of the frosted chest" from shut to opened at rem_hold.
  }
  Observe chest_looked near winter_chest when tried(winter_chest, looking) "REMAINDER 7, says the card. A winter. Not weather, not a season: the last week of a winter in a year when winter did not end, boxed and sealed. The Watch have never opened it. Orrel Sabe says it is the only remainder he has ever been afraid of.".
  Rule chest_bites at rem_hold when state(winter_chest, opened) and not chestBit(party) says "The cold goes through you like a thought. You smell snow that fell nine hundred years ago, and hear a bell, and a dog barking at a door, and then the lid is down and somebody has put a knee on it, and your hands are blue to the wrist." {
    Assert strikes(chest_cold, party). Assert chestBit(party).
  }
  Hazard chest_cold "The cold of a boxed winter" means "Deal (2d6) cold damage to ally unless constitution save against (14).".
  Relation chestBit(group).
  Person tern "a grey tern in a wicker cage" at rem_hold {
    Role "a bird that speaks a dead language". Species raven. Level 1. Peaceable.
    Greets "The tern puts its head on one side, and says, clearly, in a human voice, a short sentence in a tongue you do not know, in the manner of a bird that has said it a hundred thousand times and has never once been answered.".
  }
  Topic tern_listen with tern "Listen to the tern, and write down what it says" when true once {
    Says "The tern says it again. And again. It says: a word, a space, the same word, a space, over and over, and then a sentence of eight syllables, which ends in a rising sound that is, in every language you have ever heard, a question. Odile Quint, if she were here, would weep. You write it down phonetically on the back of your hand. It is the only remainder on the ship that can be taken away by a person with a pen.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, tern_sentence). }
  }
  Discovery tern_sentence "The tern in the hold speaks a dead tongue, a word said over and over and then a question, which you have written down by sound.".

  // ── The Quartermaster ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind keeper_face "a keeper's face" like keeper_mask described "A smooth face of grey fired clay, without eyes or mouth, with a single notch where a brow would be.".
  Action fit_face(actor: group, site: place, carrier: member) "Fit {carrier}'s grey face to the Quartermaster" {
    Description "A keeper wakes when it is given its face, and stops when it loses it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hours_quay) and at(quartermaster, site) and memberOf(carrier, actor) and awake(carrier) and (holding(actor, keeper_mask) or holding(actor, keeper_face)) and not faceGiven(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert faceGiven(actor). Assert at(quartermaster, rem_deck). Increase trust(actor) by 3. }
    Result "The Quartermaster does not move as you lift the grey face to it. Then it takes the face in both hands as one takes a sleeping child, and sets it where a face goes, and there is a sound like a very small bell, and the figure straightens by an inch, and turns its head, and sees the ship it has been standing at the foot of since before there was a Watch. Orrel Sabe, who has come down the gangway without being noticed, says: 'Ah.' He says it again. 'I had forgotten that sound.' The Quartermaster goes up the gangway and takes the deck.".
  }

  // ── The surety ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Whoever stands surety is binding the House above, or a House, to keep. There are three kinds a company may have, and
  // a fourth that is not to stand surety at all.
  Action surety_collegium(actor: group, site: place) "Stand surety for the Remainder in the name of the Collegium of Lesser Instruments" {
    Description "The Collegium collects working things, and has a letter that says it keeps them. It will be delighted, and it will not be gentle.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rem_count) and knows(actor, surety_asked) and holding(actor, collegium_letter) and not surety(actor) and not boarded(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert surety(actor). Assert harboured(remainder). Assert befell(remainder_harboured). }
    Result "You read Halm's letter aloud to the Reckoner of the Remainder, and she listens with her chin on her hands, and at the end says: 'It says a friend of working things. It does not say he can feed twenty-two people for a winter.' 'No,' you say. 'But it says he will try.' Tamsin Quaye laughs, once, and picks up a bead, and puts it down in a different place. The pin on the chart moves.".
  }
  Action surety_writ(actor: group, site: place) "Stand surety for the Remainder in the Prefect's formula: custodia, not dominium" {
    Description "A keeping and not an ownership: the House above will keep what the Watch keeps, and not claim it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rem_count) and knows(actor, surety_asked) and holding(actor, prefects_writ) and not surety(actor) and not boarded(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert surety(actor). Assert harboured(remainder). Assert befell(remainder_harboured). }
    Result "You unfold the monk's copy on the table of the count-room and read the Latin aloud, and then your own plain English, line for line, as Mother Ysolt wrote it. 'To keep and not to own,' you say. 'Whoever is given it is a keeper, and may not sell. The House that stands behind it may be replaced if it neglects the keeping.' Tamsin Quaye has gone very still. 'That is a law,' she says. 'Somebody made that for exactly this.' She looks at Orrel Sabe, who has not said anything. 'Captain,' she says. 'It is not a harbour. It is a custody.'".
  }
  Action surety_none(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Tamsin Quaye you cannot stand surety for what you cannot count" {
    Description "It is a hard thing to say to a young woman who has waited her whole life for someone to come down the stair.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rem_count) and knows(actor, surety_asked) and not surety(actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert surety(actor). Assert keptInSlack(remainder). Assert befell(remainder_kept). }
    Result "'I understand,' says Tamsin Quaye, in the voice of someone who has understood nothing. She puts down the rod. 'Captain Sabe was right. He generally is. It is a terrible habit.' She looks at the pin on the chart for a long time. 'I will tell him he may count the day a success,' she says. 'Go up your stair. I would take it as a kindness if you did not say what we looked like.'".
  }
  Observe harbour_scene at rem_count when harboured(remainder) "The count-room is full of the Watch, packing: twenty-two people with seven years' bedding apiece, and children asking whether it is true that there is a sky. The pin on the chart has moved a hand's breadth and nobody has said so.".
  Observe kept_scene at rem_count when keptInSlack(remainder) "Tamsin Quaye has taken the pin off the chart and is holding it in her fist. She does not turn round. 'It'll see me out,' she says. 'It won't see out the children.'".

  // ── Putting out ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Remainder is a ship, and ships go. In the slack her one voyage is to the berth of Mechanus (the set square,
  // turning in its time, like the inside of a great clock), which she has visited since before the Watch, because the
  // pin on the chart has always pointed that way. She lies there twelve watches, by her own hours, and goes back to the
  // Quay; a company that is ashore when she casts off is on the threshold of Mechanus until she comes again, which she
  // does every forty-eight. Her Captain will take a company who asks, once he is sure what it has come down for.
  Measure leftAt(entity).
  Action put_to_mechanus(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Captain Sabe to put out for Mechanus" {
    Description "Twelve watches at the berth, by the ship's reckoning, and not a minute longer. The ship will come again in forty-eight. Whoever is ashore when she goes waits for her.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rem_deck) and at(sabe, rem_deck) and at(remainder, hours_quay) and counted(actor) and not boarded(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Retract at(remainder, hours_quay). Assert at(remainder, outer_mechanus_threshold). Assert state(remainder, out). Set mechAt(remainder) to watch(clock). }
    Result "'It is a long time since anyone asked me that,' says Orrel Sabe. He puts the stylus down. 'The Watch has been telling the story of the other berth for eleven generations. None of us has set a foot on it. We keep the ship at the oar.' He gets to his feet, which takes him time. 'Hands to the lines,' he says, in a voice that has not been used for orders, and twenty-two people come out of the watch-room, one at a time, blinking. The Remainder leaves the Quay of Hours the way a ship leaves a slip with its keel greased, without a sound. The ruled sky slides. Ahead, where the level surface meets the ruled sky, a vertical line of light appears, and widens, and is a place.".
  }
  Rule mechanus_arrives when at(remainder, outer_mechanus_threshold) and not mechanusSeen(remainder) and at(party, rem_deck)
    says "She slides into a berth she has been to a thousand times and never landed at. The air smells of oil and brass. Beyond the rail is a floor ruled in squares each the size of a cottage, and, as far as the eye goes, wheels: set square, turning in their time, each with its tooth in the next. Somewhere very far away something strikes the hour. It is a different hour from the one you were in, and it is in no hurry." {
    Assert mechanusSeen(remainder). Assert befell(mechanus_seen).
  }
  Rule remainder_returns when state(remainder, out) and at(remainder, outer_mechanus_threshold) and watch(clock) >= mechAt(remainder) + 12
    says "Orrel Sabe takes the bell-cord in his hand and rings the deck-bell. The lines come in. The Remainder goes off the berth like a leaf off a stone." {
    Retract at(remainder, outer_mechanus_threshold). Assert at(remainder, hours_quay). Set leftAt(remainder) to watch(clock).
  }
  Rule remainder_comes_again when state(remainder, out) and at(remainder, hours_quay) and watch(clock) >= leftAt(remainder) + 48 and at(party, outer_mechanus_threshold)
    says "A long way off, across the squares, a bell is struck, and a ship is coming in over a floor that has no water, at the speed of a thought being remembered." {
    Retract at(remainder, hours_quay). Assert at(remainder, outer_mechanus_threshold). Set mechAt(remainder) to watch(clock).
  }
  Observe stranded_mech at outer_mechanus_threshold when not at(remainder, outer_mechanus_threshold) and mechanusSeen(remainder) and at(party, outer_mechanus_threshold) "The Remainder is gone. The quay she lay at is a square of black metal in a floor of squares, and on it a short row of marks has been cut with a knife, fresh, the way you mark a place you mean to come back to.".

  // The cost of a harbour. A surety named in the Prefect's formula or in the Collegium's keeping is bounded by it, if the
  // company has taken the trouble to learn what a surety is: a clerk of the Balance wrote it down for anyone who asked.
  // A company that stood surety blind answers for everything the Watch holds, and the Watch holds a good deal, and eats.
  Relation liable(group). Relation calledToday(group).
  Rule surety_binds when harboured(remainder) and surety(party) and not holding(party, surety_terms) and not liable(party)
    says "Orrel Sabe has set down his slate, and is looking at you with an apology that is entirely sincere. 'I have to tell you,' he says, 'what our roll says about a surety who does not name the keeping. It says they answer for all of it.'" {
    Assert liable(party).
  }
  Rule watch_calls when liable(party) and hour(clock) == 9 and not calledToday(party) and harboured(remainder)
    says "A boy from the House comes at nine with a slate: the Watch's bread, the Watch's lamp-oil, the Watch's winter coats. The account is in your name, in a hand as exact as the Valuer's. It is not large. It is every day." {
    Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 3 or to nothing. Assert calledToday(party).
  }
  Rule watch_calls_resets when hour(clock) != 9 and calledToday(party) { Retract calledToday(party). }
  Observe note_pinned at rem_count when harboured(remainder) and holding(party, surety_terms) "Over the great chart, held with a pin from the old count, a strip of ruled paper has been fixed: A SURETY ANSWERS FOR THE KEEPING NAMED. Tamsin has underlined KEEPING twice.".

  // ── The second bell ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Watch does not speak to a stranger before the second bell, an hour after the stranger is aboard. A company
  // that comes up the gangway has an hour of the ship with nobody to ask.
  Rule boarded_note when at(party, rem_deck) and boardedAt(party) == 0 { Set boardedAt(party) to watch(clock). Assert onboard(party). }
  Relation onboard(group).
  Query secondBell(g: group) means boardedAt(g) > 0 and watch(clock) >= boardedAt(g) + 6.
  Observe first_hour at rem_deck when onboard(party) and not secondBell(party) "Nobody speaks. Twenty-odd people stand along the rail and in the hatches and watch you with an unhurried courtesy, as a congregation watches someone who has come in late to a funeral and sat down, and is not sure whether it is theirs. The old man counts. The deck-bell hangs from the mast on its cord and does not move, and you realise that you have been listening for it since the stair.".
  // The hour with nobody to ask: the Watch is at its work, and the company sees something of the ship and is not told.
  Relation railSeen(group).
  Rule rail_unasked at rem_deck when onboard(party) and not secondBell(party) and watch(clock) >= boardedAt(party) + 2 and not railSeen(party)
    says "Along the lee rail someone has set out a row of shallow dishes, and in each a heap of something grey and fine as flour. A woman goes down the row with a feather, drawing in every heap a short straight line, and when she has done the last she stands back to wait. The first heap is smoothing itself flat again, slowly, from the edges in. She draws her line in it a second time. You say 'Excuse me,' and then, 'What is it for?' She glances at you as one glances at a child who has spoken in church, and bends to the third dish. At the hatch a man has a hand lifted to his brow, as if for a sail, and is looking at the low place in the sky where the ruling thins. You look where he looks. There is a colour there, faint, for which you have no name, and something in your chest does what it does at the first line of a hymn you were never taught. You ask him. He lowers his hand and goes below. Whatever it is, you will have to look at it without being told." {
    Assert railSeen(party).
  }
  Rule second_bell at rem_deck when onboard(party) and secondBell(party) and not belled(party)
    says "The deck-bell is struck, once. It is not a loud sound, and it goes on. Along the rail the Watch lets out a breath it has been holding for an hour, and several people sit down, and a child who has been watching you from behind a hatch-cover comes out and stands in front of you and says, with enormous dignity, 'You may speak now.'" {
    Assert belled(party).
  }
  Relation belled(group).

  // ── What hangs on the mast ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe bracket_scene at rem_deck when not steadied(remainder) "At the masthead, above the bell, there is a bracket: an iron ring, as wide as a dinner plate, with nothing in it. It has been polished. Cut small on the inside of the ring, where only someone looking for it would look, is a fish, and over the fish a flame." teaches bracket_seen.
  Discovery bracket_seen "At the masthead of the Remainder there is an empty iron ring, polished and waiting, cut on the inside with a fish and a flame.".
  Relation steadied(entity).
  Topic tamsin_bracket with tamsin "Ask Tamsin Quaye about the empty ring on the mast" when knows(actor, bracket_seen) once {
    Says "'The masthead lamp,' says Tamsin, not looking up from the rods. 'It was taken ashore to be mended. That is what the roll says, in the second hand.' She sets a bead. 'One name on it isn't struck through. It has a question mark.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lamp_lent). }
  }
  Discovery lamp_lent "The Remainder's masthead lamp was taken ashore to be mended, the second roll says; one name on that roll has a question mark where the others have a line. Tamsin thinks the ship's pin is slow because she has no light.".
  Item tally_stick "a Watch's tally-stick" is watch_tally at offstage owned by tamsin.
  Relation tallyCut(group).
  Topic tamsin_tally with tamsin "Ask Tamsin Quaye whether someone could carry the Watch's asking" when knows(actor, lamp_lent) and not tallyCut(tamsin) once {
    Says "'Asking,' says Tamsin Quaye, and puts down the rod, and for the first time since you came aboard is not doing anything with her hands. 'We have said for generations that it would be asked for when the man with the question mark came back. I think he did not come back. I think the island has the lamp.' She takes a stick of grey wood from the table and a knife and cuts a row of notches in it, steady, and stops in the middle of a stroke. 'This is how the Watch asks. They will know. They have the other half of it on the wall.' She puts it in your hand. It is warm. 'Do not,' she says, 'tell them it is urgent. They have kept it a long time, and they will be afraid.'".
    On discuss { Give tally_stick to actor. Assert tallyCut(tamsin). }
  }
  Place nowhere_slack "nowhere" is room within descent at 9, 9.
  Action fit_lens(actor: group, site: place) "Fit the green lens of the Pharos into the ring at the masthead" {
    Description "A lens lent to an island, and kept. A ring that has been polished for as long as anyone has had a hand to polish it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rem_deck) and holding(actor, pharos_lens) and not steadied(remainder).
    Time 6.
    On success { Spend pharos_lens from actor. Assert steadied(remainder). Assert befell(remainder_steadied). Retract at(divider, rem_deck). Assert at(divider, nowhere_slack). }
    Result "You go up the mast. It is a long way, and the deck below goes small, and the Watch has come out on the deck and is looking up. The ring takes the lens as a hand takes a hand: there is no sound, only a settling. A moment after, the green glass catches a light that has no source, and the whole of the ruled sky turns, very slowly, and finds a point in it to be arranged about. On the count-room's chart, a hundred feet below, a pin stops. Orrel Sabe lays down his slate. He does not count. For the first time in his life he stands on his own deck, in the light, and has nothing to do.".
  }
  Observe steadied_scene at rem_deck when steadied(remainder) "The Remainder has a light at her masthead: a steady green, round and warm, and the ruled sky is arranged about it. The Watch go about the deck softly, looking up. Nobody has said what it means.".

  // ── The Divider ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The slack is thin and thinning, and a company that lingers in it is a thing the count has not yet divided. After
  // two days' worth of watches below, the count sends something to see. It is not malicious. It is exact. It comes up
  // the gangway at the second night-bell, a tall figure ruled in fine lines like a page of accounts, and it begins to
  // divide whatever is nearest: the cage of the tern, the Quartermaster's hand, a child's name. It can be fought, with
  // difficulty; it can be turned by something that does not divide; it can be answered with a complete count; it can
  // be stood between by someone who would rather not be counted either; and it can be left behind up the stair.
  Species divider_kind "a thing the count sends" like spirit temperament ambush described "A figure a head taller than a tall man, drawn in lines as fine as hairs, ruled and ruled again, so that the eye keeps trying to read its face and finds a column of figures.".
  Person divider "the Divider" at nowhere_slack {
    Role "a ruled figure that divides what it is near". Species divider_kind. Level 5. Pronouns it.
    Warns "A tall figure stands at the head of the gangway, ruled all over in fine lines. Along the rail the Watch has gone entirely silent. A child has been taken below. The figure is looking at the deck-bell, and the bell, you notice, is slightly smaller than it was.".
    Comes "It comes along the deck with a tread like a quill on paper, and the lines on it are moving.".
  }
  Relation dividerCame(group). Relation turned(group). Relation thin(entity). Relation divHurt(group). Measure dividedAt(entity).
  Rule divider_comes when slackWatches(party) >= 48 and not dividerCame(party) and not steadied(remainder) and at(party, rem_deck)
    says "At the second night-bell, which is struck once and then, hesitantly, not at all, a tall shape is on the gangway. It is ruled all over in lines as fine as hairs. It stops at the head of the gangway and tilts its head, as a clerk tilts it at a sum, and begins to come aboard." {
    Assert dividerCame(party). Retract at(divider, nowhere_slack). Assert at(divider, rem_deck). Set dividedAt(divider) to watch(clock).
  }
  Rule divider_divides when at(divider, rem_deck) and at(party, rem_deck) and watch(clock) >= dividedAt(divider) + 12 and not turned(party) and not dead(divider)
    says "The Divider lays one ruled hand on the nearest thing, and the thing is less. A cage, a hand, a child's name, a rope: it takes a half of it and, with unhurried courtesy, a half of what is left. Somebody on the deck cries out in a voice that has lost a syllable." {
    Assert strikes(division, party). Set dividedAt(divider) to watch(clock).
  }
  Hazard division "The count dividing" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless wisdom save against (14).".
  Action ring_the_twelfth(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Captain Sabe for the bell-cord, and ring the twelfth" {
    Description "The Remainder has struck eleven for as long as there has been a Watch. A complete count is a thing that a divider does not know how to take.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rem_deck) and at(divider, site) and counted(actor) and not turned(actor) and not thin(remainder).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert turned(actor). Retract at(divider, rem_deck). Assert at(divider, nowhere_slack). Assert thin(remainder). }
    Result "Orrel Sabe looks at the cord for some time. 'It was not rung in my mother's time,' he says. 'Or her mother's.' Then he puts it into your hand, and the rest of the Watch makes a sound like a held breath leaving. You pull it: eleven, as it has always been, and then, with the whole of your weight, a twelfth. The Divider stands where it is. The lines on it slow. It looks at the bell, at the cord, at you, as a clerk looks at a sum that has come out even, and it folds, from the top down, like a ledger being closed. The sound of the twelfth goes on in the ruled sky a long time. 'We have used something,' says Sabe, quietly. 'I do not know what.'".
    Otherwise "'No,' says Sabe, very gently, and takes the cord out of your hand. 'Not by one who has not yet learned what it is for.'".
  }
  Action speak_the_sentence(actor: group, site: place) "Say the tern's sentence to the Divider" {
    Description "A remainder is a thing that does not divide. A sentence in a dead tongue, said as it has been said for a hundred thousand years, is a thing that does not.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, rem_deck) and at(divider, site) and knows(actor, tern_sentence) and not turned(actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert turned(actor). Retract at(divider, rem_deck). Assert at(divider, nowhere_slack). Retract at(tern, rem_hold). Assert at(tern, nowhere_slack). }
    Result "You say it. You say it as you wrote it down, by sound, with the tern's rise at the end like a question, again and again, in a voice that is not yours. The Divider listens with its head on one side. Its lines begin to slow; at the last it opens its hands. You say the question. It takes the sentence out of the air as a priest takes a wafer, and goes down the gangway with it carefully, as if carrying water. Below, in the hold, a grey tern in a wicker cage opens its beak and nothing comes out of it at all.".
  }
  Rule quartermaster_stands when faceGiven(party) and at(divider, rem_deck) and not turned(party) and not stilled(quartermaster)
    says "The Quartermaster steps between. It does not hurry. It has had a face for a very short time and is not sure what to do with it, but it knows what a gangway is for. It puts both long arms out. The Divider lays a ruled hand on its chest, and the Quartermaster takes the hand, and holds it, and the lines on the Divider go slack, and stop. Both figures stand quite still at the head of the gangway. Neither moves again. The grey face has not changed expression, having none." {
    Assert turned(party). Assert stilled(quartermaster). Retract at(divider, rem_deck). Assert at(divider, nowhere_slack).
  }
  Relation stilled(entity).
  Observe quartermaster_still at hours_quay when stilled(quartermaster) "At the head of the gangway the Quartermaster stands with its arms out and its face on, not moving. Someone has laid a coat over one of its shoulders, as one does for a person who is only sleeping.".
  Observe dividerHere at rem_deck when at(divider, rem_deck) and not dead(divider) "The Divider stands at the head of the gangway, ruled over, patient. A rope near it is a hand's breadth shorter than it was.".
}

data/adventures/the-grand-tour/rivals.ky:
Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  // ── Florian Mottram and Miss Sone ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Honourable Florian Mottram, nineteen, of Cloudgate, has bought everything, read nothing, and is an idiot of
  // great sweetness. His bear-leader, Miss Agatha Sone, a retired sergeant of fifty, has done the Tour eleven times
  // with eleven idiots and would like to do something else before she dies. She is competent: left alone they take
  // the Fire petal at noon on the second day, and the Earth petal on the fourth morning (Florian, being incapable of
  // patience, digs), and give each to the Rector at five the same evening. They cannot get into the Whelm: Florian
  // called the merfolk at the third step "fish", and the whole Whelm heard.
  Person florian "the Honourable Florian Mottram" at glass_market {
    Role "a Tourist from Cloudgate, in a coat the colour of a sunset" when not florianChanged(florian).
    Role "a traveller from Cloudgate, in a coat the colour of a sunset, rather singed" when florianChanged(florian).
    Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "A young man in a coat the colour of a sunset, with a parcel under each arm and another on his head, beams at you. 'Florian Mottram,' he says. 'I'd shake hands, but. Are you on the Tour? Isn't it marvellous? I've bought a fire-cloak, a brine-helm, two wind-jars, and a stuffed salamander, though Sone says that's cheating.' He lowers his voice. 'Sone's my bear-leader. She's been eleven times. She knows everything. It's frightfully restful.'".
    Greets again "'Hullo!' says Florian Mottram, and drops a parcel, and Miss Sone picks it up without breaking step. 'We are ahead of you,' he says. 'Or we were. There is a fair chance we are behind. Sone says it depends on the sort of woods one counts.'".
  }
  Person sone "Miss Agatha Sone" at glass_market {
    Role "a bear-leader, square and grey, with a sergeant's moustache of eyebrow". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Trait strong_willed. Level 5. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    Greets "A square grey woman with an umbrella like a pike looks at you, and at Florian, and back, with the expression of a sheepdog that has been asked to mind a swan. 'Sone,' she says. 'Bear-leader. If he asks you to hold anything, don't.'".
    Greets again "Miss Sone nods to you, once, like a sergeant to another sergeant, and holds the umbrella a degree more upright. 'He has not been out of my sight since the harbour,' she says. 'Do not tell him I said so. It would make him feel watched, and he is quite right.'".
  }
  Initially Assert passesTo(florian, quance).
  Relation florianChanged(group). Relation soneAsked(group). Relation soneWithholds(group). Relation soneKnows(group).
  Relation florianReclaims(group). Relation florianConfessed(group). Relation florianStopped(group).
  // ── Where they are ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Query rivalsFree() means not florianChanged(florian) or not soneWithholds(sone).
  Query rivalsFire() means day(clock) == 2 and hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) < 13.
  Query rivalsEarth() means day(clock) == 4 and hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 11.
  Rule rivals_market when day(clock) == 1 and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 15 and not at(florian, glass_market) { Assert at(florian, glass_market). Assert at(sone, glass_market). }
  Rule rivals_murreys when florianInShop() and not at(florian, murrey_shop) { Assert at(florian, murrey_shop). Assert at(sone, murrey_shop). }
  Rule rivals_quad when ((day(clock) == 1 and hour(clock) >= 16 and hour(clock) < 19) or (hour(clock) >= 14 and hour(clock) < 19 and day(clock) >= 2 and not funeralHour())) and not at(florian, quad) { Assert at(florian, quad). Assert at(sone, quad). }
  Rule rivals_fire when rivalsFire() and not at(florian, hour_court) { Assert at(florian, hour_court). Assert at(sone, hour_court). }
  Rule rivals_earth when rivalsEarth() and not at(florian, assembly) { Assert at(florian, assembly). Assert at(sone, assembly). }
  Rule rivals_funeral when funeralHour() and not at(florian, balustrade) { Assert at(florian, balustrade). Assert at(sone, balustrade). }
  Rule rivals_morning when hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 14 and day(clock) >= 2 and not rivalsFire() and not rivalsEarth() and not funeralHour() and not at(florian, glass_market) { Assert at(florian, glass_market). Assert at(sone, glass_market). }
  Rule rivals_evening when hour(clock) >= 19 and not at(florian, promenade) { Assert at(florian, promenade). Assert at(sone, promenade). }
  Rule rivals_night when (hour(clock) < 9 and not rivalsEarth()) and not at(florian, offstage) { Assert at(florian, offstage). Assert at(sone, offstage). }

  // ── The Fire, at noon on the second day ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Miss Sone brings a block of Cloudgate ice up from the Halyards' ice-house in a box of sawdust, which is four.
  Rule florian_crowned at hour_court when day(clock) == 2 and hour(clock) >= 12 and not petalTaken(fire_petal) and not crowned(party) and not emberCrowned(fire_land) and reign(fire_land) < 4 and not florianStopped(florian)
    says "Miss Sone opens a box of sawdust and lifts out of it a block of ice from the Halyards' ice-house, clear as glass, sweating. The Hour Court has never seen cold that you can hold. It crowns Florian Mottram, who is so pleased he takes his hat off, and his hair catches fire, and Miss Sone puts it out with her hand. Florian decrees that the petal is his, being a quick study, and an ifrit gives it him." {
    Assert rivalHas(fire_petal). Assert petalTaken(fire_petal). Assert rivalCrowned(fire_land). Assert keeps(florian, fire_petal). }
  // ── The Earth, on the fourth morning: Florian cannot bear the Assembly either ─────────────────────────────────────
  Event florian_digs at assembly when day(clock) == 4 and hour(clock) >= 10 and not petalTaken(earth_petal) and not florianStopped(florian) and at(party, assembly) "Florian Mottram comes down the long tunnel with a lamp in one hand and a pick in the other, saying 'Sorry, sorry, frightfully sorry,' to the Assembly, which does not hear him, and kneels by the petal in the chamber floor and starts to dig. Miss Sone, behind him, looks at the ceiling." then { Assert florianDigging(florian). }
  Relation florianDigging(group).
  Topic florian_vote with florian "Tell Florian Mottram that the Assembly is two words from granting the petal, and he is digging up a vote" when florianDigging(florian) and at(party, assembly) and sat(actor) and not florianStopped(florian) once {
    Says "Florian stops, with the pick in the air. He looks round at the Assembly, at the hundred still shapes on their tiers, at the Speaker, all of them listening to a word you can feel in the floor. 'Oh,' he says. 'Oh, I say. Is it a vote? In the middle of a vote?' He puts the pick down, very carefully, as if it might go off. 'One doesn't,' he says, going red. 'Papa would. One doesn't.' Behind him Miss Sone looks at him, for a moment, as if she had never seen him before.".
    On discuss { Assert florianStopped(florian). }
  }
  Rule florian_digs_out when day(clock) == 4 and hour(clock) >= 11 and not petalTaken(earth_petal) and not florianStopped(florian) {
    Assert rivalHas(earth_petal). Assert petalTaken(earth_petal). Assert keeps(florian, earth_petal). Retract florianDigging(florian). }
  // At five on the evening of a win, Florian takes it up the headland to the Rector, unless Miss Sone will not let him.
  Rule rivals_deliver when rivalHas(?p) and keeps(florian, ?p) and hour(clock) >= 17 and not soneWithholds(sone) and rectorFree() {
    Retract rivalHas(?p). Retract keeps(florian, ?p). Assert keeps(quance, ?p). Assert rectorHas(?p). Increase rectorPetals(sennet_bay) by 1. }
  Observe florian_petal near florian when rivalHas(fire_petal) and keeps(florian, fire_petal) "Florian Mottram has a petal of red glass in his breast pocket, warm, with the light moving in it, and keeps taking it out to look at it.".

  // ── Talking with them ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic sone_opinion with sone "Ask Miss Sone what she thinks of the Grand Tour" when true once {
    Says "She looks at you for a long time, as if nobody had asked her that in twenty years, which, you gather, nobody has. 'I think it's a Rector wanting her name over a door,' she says. 'I think the courts gave those petals to keep, and every boy with a Papa now wants to bring one home and put it on the mantelpiece.' She looks at Florian, who is buying a glass float. 'I think I've done eleven Tours with eleven boys, and brought eleven boys home, and not one of them has ever looked at anything but the label.' She folds her hands on her umbrella. 'Since you ask.'".
    On discuss { Assert soneAsked(sone). }
  }
  // An entered Tourist on Miss Sone's account, as her assistant, for nothing.
  Topic sone_assistant with sone "Ask Miss Sone whether she could put you down as her assistant, for the Tour" when soneAsked(sone) and not enrolled(actor) once {
    Says "'Assistant bear-leader.' She almost smiles. 'The Mottrams will pay for it without noticing. They pay for everything without noticing.' She takes a card from her reticule and writes on it in a square hand, and gives it you, and it is a licence of the Grand Tour with the Rector's violet signature already on it, the bottom half blank. 'I keep a few,' says Miss Sone. 'In case of idiots. You're not one. Go through the doors. Look at something.'".
    On discuss { Assert enrolled(actor). Give licence to actor. }
  }
  Topic florian_collection with florian "Ask Florian Mottram what he means to bring home from the Tour" when true once {
    Says "'Oh, everything!' He beams. 'I've a cabinet. Papa's got two. Great-grandpapa had a whole room, he brought home an ember from the Fire that's still burning, it's in the Museum with his name on it, Hon. Thos. Mottram, I go and look at it on Sundays.' He stops beaming, a little. 'It's only, you know. Sone says I look at the labels.' He looks at a parcel. 'I'd like to bring home something I'd actually, you know. Seen. Once. Myself.' He laughs. 'Silly.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, florian_wish). }
  }
  Discovery florian_wish "Florian Mottram's great-grandfather brought home the ember in Cabinet Fourteen; Florian goes to look at it on Sundays. He would like, once, to bring home something he had actually seen himself.".
  Topic florian_ember with florian "Tell Florian Mottram that his great-grandfather's ember is alive, and asks to go home, and that a Mottram could take it back" when knows(actor, ember_alive) and knows(actor, florian_wish) and not emberFreed(museum) and not florianReclaims(florian) once {
    Says "He goes white, and then red. 'Alive?' He looks at the headland, toward the Museum. 'I've been going to look at it. On Sundays. For years. It does sparks when I talk to it.' He swallows. 'I thought that was. I thought it liked me.' He stands up, and drops all his parcels, and does not pick them up. 'A Mottram could take it back? It's ours? Then I'm taking it back.' He looks at Miss Sone. Miss Sone looks at him. 'Sone,' he says. 'Sone, I'm going to take it home. Myself. Through the door. Will you come?' 'Yes,' says Miss Sone.".
    On discuss { Assert florianReclaims(florian). }
  }
  // He goes to the Museum and reclaims it, and gives it to the company to carry, being afraid he will drop it.
  Rule florian_reclaims when florianReclaims(florian) and not emberFreed(museum) and openHours() and not carries(party, ember)
    says "Word comes along Lamp Street, by way of several students, that the Honourable Florian Mottram has walked into the Museum of the Tour and asked Dr. Cole, as a Mottram, for his great-grandfather's ember back, and that Dr. Cole sat down on the floor." {
    Assert emberFreed(museum). Assert florianChanged(florian). Give ember to party. }
  Topic florian_bassett with florian "Ask Florian Mottram to tell Sergeant Bassett it was his own mistake about the glass petal" when knows(actor, prue_complaint) and prueTrouble(prue) and not prueSaved(prue) and not florianConfessed(florian) once {
    Says "'The petal! The Rector's desk!' He claps his hand to his forehead. 'I didn't turn it over. Who turns things over? It said Genuine on the card.' He looks stricken. 'Has she got into trouble? Prue? The glass woman with no eyebrows? She gave me a float for nothing.' He is already putting on his hat. 'I'll go and tell the sergeant. I'll tell him I'm an ass. Sone, I'm going to go and tell a sergeant I'm an ass.' Miss Sone says that it will be a novelty for the sergeant.".
    On discuss { Assert florianConfessed(florian). Assert prueSaved(prue). }
  }
  // Told what the Rector did, Miss Sone will not carry another petal up the headland.
  Topic sone_told with sone "Tell Miss Sone who pushed Perrin Halyard, and what the Rector means to do with the petals" when knows(actor, quance_pushed) and soneAsked(sone) and not soneWithholds(sone) once {
    Says "She hears you out with her face like a wall. When you have finished she is quiet a moment. 'I carried a boy home from the Tour once with his neck broken,' she says. 'Fell off a stair in the Air, showing off. I carried him home to his mother.' She looks at Florian. 'Nothing more goes up that headland in my charge,' she says. 'Not one petal. If you want what we have, ask me for it.'".
    On discuss { Assert soneWithholds(sone). Assert soneKnows(sone). }
  }
  Topic sone_petals with sone "Ask Miss Sone for the petals she is keeping back from the Rector" when soneWithholds(sone) and (keeps(florian, fire_petal) or keeps(florian, earth_petal)) once {
    Says "She takes them out of Florian's breast pocket herself, while he watches, and gives them you. 'There,' she says. 'Do something with them a Rector wouldn't.'".
    On discuss { Retract rivalHas(fire_petal). Retract rivalHas(earth_petal). Give fire_petal to actor. Give earth_petal to actor. }
  }
  // Florian trades a petal, once, for a thing he has never seen and nobody else has.
  Topic florian_trade with florian "Offer Florian Mottram the geode from the Minutes, which nobody in Cloudgate has, for the petal in his pocket" when rivalHas(fire_petal) and keeps(florian, fire_petal) and holding(actor, geode_kind) once {
    Says "You crack it open for him. His eyes go perfectly round at the purple inside. 'Oh,' he says. 'Oh. Nobody's got one of those. Papa hasn't got one of those.' He looks at the petal in his hand, warm, with its light moving, and at the thing in yours. He is not a clever young man; but he is, you discover, an honest one, and he does not haggle. 'Done,' he says, and gives you the petal, and holds the two halves of the stone against his chest. 'Done. Sone, look. A million years. I've got a million years.'".
    On discuss { Retract rivalHas(fire_petal). Retract keeps(florian, fire_petal). Spend geode_kind from actor. Give fire_petal to actor. Assert florianTraded(florian). Assert florianChanged(florian). }
  }
  Relation florianTraded(group).
}

data/adventures/the-grand-tour/sexton.ky:
Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  // ── The Sexton ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The harbour says the drowned sexton of Lir's has been at his rope two hundred years. The Whelm says the Sexton is
  // the conger that has lived in the belfry since the water came in, grown on two centuries of what the bay lets fall,
  // and that the bell rung at the turn of the tide is what keeps it up there: it hates the noise, and lies in the
  // hollow of the beam with its head under its tail until it stops. The grandmothers knew. The children ring it for
  // the joy of the noise, and have forgotten why; that is what keeping becomes. Stop the bell for Old Bethan's sake,
  // or muffle it, and at the next turn the Sexton comes down into Chandlers' Row.
  Query bellSilent() means bellStopped(sennet_bay) or bellMuffled(sennet_bay).
  Species conger_kind "a conger of the old harbour" like great_pike temperament ambush described "A conger eel as long as a fishing boat and as thick as a man, grey-black, with a head like a shut fist and a mouth that does not quite close on its teeth. Its skin is scarred white where two hundred years of the bay's leavings have gone down it the wrong way: anchors, a mooring chain, a bishop's crozier, they say on the Quay, though nobody on the Quay has seen it.".
  Person sexton "the Sexton" at belfry {
    Role "a conger as long as a boat, coiled round the bell-beam" when at(sexton, belfry).
    Role "a conger as long as a boat, loose in the drowned street" when not at(sexton, belfry).
    Species conger_kind. Level 5. Pronouns it.
  }
  Relation sextonCowed(group). Relation sextonFed(group). Relation sextonDown(group). Relation sextonKilled(group).
  Discovery sexton_known "The bell under the bay is not rung only for the noise. At the turn of the tide it keeps the Sexton, a conger as long as a boat, coiled in the belfry of Lir's church; stop the bell, and the Sexton comes down into Chandlers' Row. The grandmothers knew. The children have forgotten.".
  Observe belfry_scene at belfry when at(sexton, belfry) "The belfry of Lir's church: a square stone room at the top of the drowned tower, its louvres long gone, green light coming in sideways. The bell hangs on its beam in the middle, as big as a cart, and round the beam, round and round, so that at first you take it for the beam's own shadow, lies something grey-black and thick as a man, with a head like a shut fist, resting on the lip of the bell.".
  Observe belfry_empty at belfry when not at(sexton, belfry) "The belfry of Lir's church: the bell on its beam, and the beam rubbed smooth and pale all the way round, as a rope rubs a bollard.".
  Observe tower_rubbed at drowned_church when true "Inside the tower, where the floors fell in, the stone has been rubbed smooth from the inside in a long slow spiral going up into the dark, as if something very large went round and round it, often.".

  // While it rings, at the turn, the Sexton lies still: the safe hour to be in the belfry. Fed, it lets you be.
  Rule sexton_cowed when tideTurn() and not bellSilent() and at(sexton, belfry) and not sextonCowed(party) { Assert sextonCowed(party). Assert tolerates(sexton, party). }
  Rule sexton_rouses when sextonCowed(party) and not tideTurn() { Retract sextonCowed(party). }
  Rule sexton_angry when not sextonCowed(party) and not sextonFed(party) and tolerates(sexton, party) { Retract tolerates(sexton, party). }
  Observe sexton_still at belfry when sextonCowed(party) and at(sexton, belfry) "The bell is ringing. You feel it in your teeth and your ribs and the roots of your hair, and on the beam the great grey shape has drawn itself in tight, head under its tail, and lies like a coil of hawser, shuddering at every stroke.".
  Action feed_sexton(actor: group, site: place) "Tip Old Bethan's eels into the water for the Sexton" {
    Description "It has eaten what fell for two hundred years. Nobody has ever given it anything.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(sexton, site) and holding(actor, eel_basket_kind) and not sextonFed(actor) and able(sexton).
    Time 1.
    On success { Spend eel_basket_kind from actor. Assert sextonFed(actor). Assert tolerates(sexton, actor). }
    Result "You pull the sack off the creel and the eels go out into the green in a long bright rope, and the Sexton's head comes round faster than anything that size should move, and takes them, the whole rope, in three bites, and swallows; and then it lies looking at you with one round eye the size of a plate, as a dog looks at whoever has fed it, and does not move again while you are there.".
  }

  // Ha'penny knows the rule, though not the reason; her grandmother knows both.
  Topic hapenny_why_turn with hapenny "Ask Ha'penny why the children ring the bell at the turn, and never between" when knows(actor, bell_ringers) once {
    Says "She frowns, as if you had asked why the sea is wet. 'Because you do. At the turn.' She thinks. 'Gran says if you don't, the Sexton comes down.' She says it in a voice that does not believe in the Sexton, and then she looks down the stairs into the green and her gills shut. 'Shutters's grandad has one arm,' she says. 'He says it was a shark.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sexton_hint). }
  }
  Discovery sexton_hint "The merfolk children ring the bell at the turn of the tide because their grandmothers told them to, or 'the Sexton comes down'. They think it is a story.".
  Topic admittance_sexton with admittance "Ask No Admittance what the Sexton is" when knows(actor, sexton_hint) or knows(actor, bell_ringers) once {
    Says "'Keeping.' She says it as if it were the answer to everything, and for her it is. 'When we came through, there was a thing in the tower already. Old. It had eaten the sexton, and his bell-ropes, and anything that came down. Our grandmothers rang the bell at the turn, and it went up into the beam and stayed. Two lifetimes.' She turns the crown in her hands. 'The children ring it now for the noise. They do not know. That is what keeping is, when it works: nobody knows what it is for.' She looks at you. 'Do not stop the bell, dry one. Whoever asks you to.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sexton_known). }
  }

  // What Bethan comes to, told: it was never ringing for Ned.
  Topic bethan_why with bethan "Tell Old Bethan why the merfolk ring the bell at the turn of the tide" when (knows(actor, sexton_known) or knows(actor, sexton_hint)) and knows(actor, bell_grief) and not bethanAtPeace(bethan) and not bellSilent() once {
    Says "She listens with the knife in her hand and an eel in the other, and does not kill it. 'A thing in the tower,' she says. 'And their bairns ringing it down, twice a day, so it won't come out and take the rest of them.' She puts the eel back in the barrow, alive, which you have not seen her do. 'Then it was never ringing for Ned.' She is quiet. 'It's ringing so nobody else's goes.' She covers the barrow with the wet sack. 'He'd want it rung. He threw them his crusts.' And at the next turn of the tide, they tell you on the Quay, Old Bethan slept through it.".
    On discuss { Assert bethanAtPeace(bethan). Assert bethanFriend(bethan). }
  }

  // Silenced, it comes down at the next turn into Chandlers' Row, and the Whelm shuts its doors.
  Rule sexton_descends when bellSilent() and tideTurn() and at(sexton, belfry) and not sextonFed(party) and able(sexton) {
    Retract at(sexton, belfry). Assert at(sexton, drowned_street). Assert sextonDown(party). }
  Rule sexton_descends_told within whelm when sextonDown(party) and at(sexton, drowned_street) and not sextonDownTold(party)
    says "The merfolk tell it you in the Guildhall's voice, low: at the turn of the tide there was no bell. There was a silence where the bell should be, and the whole Whelm heard it; and in the silence something came down out of the tower of Lir's church, slowly, the way a rope pays out, and into Chandlers' Row. Every door in the Row was shut on it. A child was calling a name, and stopped." { Assert sextonDownTold(party). }
  Relation sextonDownTold(group).
  Rule sexton_descends_heard within sennet_town when sextonDown(party) and at(sexton, drowned_street) and not sextonDownHeard(party) and tideTurn()
    says "At the turn of the tide the bell under the bay does not ring. On the Quay the harbour, which has always said it hated that bell, stands and listens to it not ringing, and nobody goes home." { Assert sextonDownHeard(party). }
  Relation sextonDownHeard(group).
  Observe row_shut at drowned_street when at(sexton, drowned_street) "Chandlers' Row is shut: every door, every shutter of every drowned shop pulled to, and the white lamps out in half the windows. Nobody is in the street. Something is: it lies along the middle of the Row from CASH ONLY to the Guildhall steps, grey-black, thick as a man, its head lifted a little off the cobbles, waiting.".
  // Rung again, it goes back up at the turn: by Ha'penny, if she is asked, or by the company cutting its own muffle.
  Topic hapenny_ring_again with hapenny "Ask Ha'penny and the others to ring the bell again at the turn, the way their grandmothers did" when bellSilent() and knows(actor, sexton_hint) and not bellMuffled(sennet_bay) and able(sexton) once {
    Says "'Again?' She looks at you, and you see her decide not to ask why; she has heard the silence too. 'At the turn. All of us. Cash Only can hang on my tail.' She is gone down the stairs before you have finished.".
    On discuss { Retract bellStopped(sennet_bay). }
  }
  Action cut_muffle(actor: group, site: place) "Cut the rope off the bell's clapper" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, belfry) and bellMuffled(sennet_bay).
    Time 1.
    On success { Retract bellMuffled(sennet_bay). }
    Result "You saw through your own knots with a knife, and the clapper swings free, and touches the bell, very lightly; and the whole tower hums.".
  }
  Rule sexton_returns when not bellSilent() and tideTurn() and at(sexton, drowned_street) and able(sexton) {
    Retract at(sexton, drowned_street). Assert at(sexton, belfry). Retract sextonDown(party).  Assert sextonWentUp(party). }
  Relation sextonWentUp(group).
  Rule sexton_returns_told within whelm when sextonWentUp(party) and not sextonUpTold(party)
    says "Chandlers' Row is open again, and the merfolk tell you how it went, all talking at once: at the turn the bell rang, and the great grey shape in the Row lifted its head as if it had been struck, and went back up the street and into the church and up the tower the way it came, paying itself out backward into the dark." { Assert sextonUpTold(party). }
  Relation sextonUpTold(group).

  // Killed: the Whelm is safe, and the bell is only a bell; the children lose their reason and keep the noise.
  Rule sexton_slain when not able(sexton) and not sextonKilled(party)
    says "The Sexton goes slack all at once, two hundred years of it, and lies along the cobbles; and after a while the doors of Chandlers' Row open, one, and then another, and the merfolk come out and stand round it, not close, the way the harbour stands round a wreck. No Admittance comes down the Guildhall steps and looks at it a long while. 'It was old,' she says. 'It kept the tower. We kept it.' She touches its scarred head with her foot. 'Now nobody keeps anything.'" {
    Assert sextonKilled(party). Retract sextonDown(party). }
  // With it dead, the bell may stop for Bethan and nothing will come of it.
  Observe church_after at drowned_church when sextonKilled(party) "The tower is empty. Up in the belfry the bell hangs on its pale-rubbed beam with nothing round it.".
}

data/adventures/the-grand-tour/state.kyr:
Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  // ── The Rose of the Winds ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The key of the Door of Doors, broken in four and given to the four courts so that nobody could open it alone. Each
  // petal is in one place until somebody has it: the company (in its packs), Florian and Miss Sone (the rivals, who
  // give what they win to the Rector the evening they win it), or the Rector.
  Kind fire_petal_kind "the Fire petal of the Rose" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "A petal of red glass the length of your hand, warm as a cup of tea, with a light moving in it like a coal breathing. It does not burn anything it touches.".
  Kind earth_petal_kind "the Earth petal of the Rose" is treasure worth 0 weighing 2 described "A petal of dark stone the length of your hand, much heavier than it should be, cool, with a grain in it like the rings of a tree.".
  Kind water_petal_kind "the Water petal of the Rose" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "A petal of green glass the length of your hand, always a little wet, with a sound in it, if you hold it to your ear, like the sea in a shell.".
  Kind air_petal_kind "the Air petal of the Rose" is treasure worth 0 weighing -6 described "A petal of clear glass the length of your hand, with nothing in it at all that you can see, that pulls upward out of your fingers like a kite on a string. Wind comes out of it, steady, cold, smelling of snow.".
  Item fire_petal "the Fire petal" is fire_petal_kind at offstage.
  Item earth_petal "the Earth petal" is earth_petal_kind at offstage.
  Item water_petal "the Water petal" is water_petal_kind at offstage.
  Item air_petal "the Air petal" is air_petal_kind at offstage.
  Relation rivalHas(entity). Relation rectorHas(entity). Relation petalTaken(entity).
  // Who has won each petal, whoever holds it now.
  Query companyHas(p: entity) means carries(party, p).
  Measure rectorPetals(place). Measure companyPetals(place).

  // ── What the week turns on ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Perrin Halyard, the Rector, Cloudgate, the Door: the large facts every part of the city reads.
  Relation perrinDead(group). Relation perrinUp(group). Relation perrinMoved(group).
  Relation rectorExposed(group). Relation rectorTaken(group). Relation rectorThrough(group). Relation rectorFled(group).
  Relation cloudgateFell(place). Relation descending(place). Measure descent(place). Relation whelmEmptied(place).
  Relation madeSet(place). Relation giftRenewed(place).
  Relation doorOpen(place). Relation openedBelow(place). Relation roseMade(place). Relation firstThrough(group).
  Measure openedAt(place).
  Relation enrolled(group).
  // Cloudgate's talk of the company: what the Gallery of Winds listens for (air.kyr).
  Measure talk(group).
}

Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  // ── The Undertow ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Under the drowned Guildhall, the Aenean Undercroft, and in it the tide-engine. The merfolk know what it is: their
  // grandmothers read the plaque, and never needed it. The House of Doors was built over the Aeneans' own; the engine
  // drives a shaft up through the rock of the headland to the Nexus, and started, it pushes the Door of Doors open
  // from below without the Rose. It runs on the whole tide of the Whelm: while it turns, a day and a night, the
  // Whelm's lamps go out and its air-bells empty. Nobody may start it without No Admittance's leave who wants to be
  // welcome in the Whelm after; and nobody should start it with anybody still in an air-bell.
  Relation engineRunning(place). Measure engineSince(place). Relation engineLeave(group). Relation leaveTerms(group).
  Relation engineSeen(group).
  Topic perrin_engine with perrin "Ask Perrin Halyard about the Aenean books he is drying" when true once {
    Says "'Oh!' His whole face changes, the way Mercy's does about the lanterns. 'You won't believe it. The House of Doors, the Collegium, was built on top of the Aeneans' own. Ours is a copy. Theirs is down there, under the Guildhall.' He points at the floor of the bell. 'The tide-engine. It drives a shaft that goes up through the headland to the Nexus, and if you start it, it opens the Door of Doors from below. No Rose. No petals. The Aeneans never needed a key; they had the sea.' He frowns. 'Though I don't think they built the engine. The plaque says this wheel turns, not we turned it, and the stone is wrong for them: too true. I think they found it, and learned to start it, and wrote that down.' He laughs. 'Isadora says that is a pedant's distinction. Isadora has not read the plaque as often as I have.' 'Isadora would sell her soul for it. I haven't told her. I've been rather busy being dead.' He sobers. 'It runs on the whole tide of the Whelm, though. Start it, and every lamp down here goes out for a day, and the air-bells empty.' He looks round at the bell he is lying in. 'Including this one.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, undertow_known). }
  }
  Discovery undertow_known "The tide-engine in the Aenean Undercroft drives a shaft up through the headland to the Nexus; started, it opens the Door of Doors from below, without the Rose. It runs on the whole tide of the Whelm: for a day the lamps go out and the air-bells empty.".
  Action read_plaque(actor: group, site: place) "Read the plaque on the tide-engine" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, engine_room) and not knows(actor, undertow_known)
      and (capable(actor, lore) or craft(actor, craft_learning) or carries(actor, perrin_notebook)).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, undertow_known). }
    Result "It is Aenean, square and plain, and says what it is with the dreadful simplicity of a people who had never needed to explain anything twice: that this wheel turns on the tide of the whole harbour, and turning, raises the cage of the shaft to the Hall of All Doors above, and sets that door open; and that while it turns, all lamps below, and all air held below, are given to it. Underneath, in a later hand, someone has scratched in Common: PERRIN WAS HERE.".
  }
  Topic admittance_engine with admittance "Ask No Admittance for leave to start the tide-engine" when admittanceTrusts(admittance) and knows(actor, undertow_known) and not engineLeave(actor) once {
    Says "She takes off her crown and holds it in her lap, which in the Whelm is how you think. 'A day without lamps,' she says. 'A day without the bells. The children will be frightened. The old ones will not come out of their houses.' She looks at you. 'We have never started it. Our grandmothers read what it does, and decided they had no door they wanted that much.' She turns her crown in her hands. 'You want a door that much?' And then, before you can answer: 'If you do it, do it with us. With every hand of the Whelm on the wheel, so it is ours that did it, not yours. And not with anyone left in a bell. Move the dry man first.'".
    On discuss { Assert leaveTerms(actor). }
  }
  Topic mercy_moves with mercy "Ask Mercy to take Perrin out of the air-bell for the day, while the engine runs" when leaveTerms(party) and not perrinMoved(party) and not perrinUp(party) and not perrinDead(party) once {
    Says "'Out of the bell?' She looks at you, and at the floor, through which, somewhere, the great wheel is waiting. Then she nods. 'To the Guildhall. With me. I'll breathe for him all day; he won't like it, he says I breathe like a seal.' She goes down through the floor of the water like a dropped stone, and you hear, faintly, up through the green, Perrin Halyard objecting.".
    On discuss { Assert perrinMoved(party). Assert at(perrin, guildhall). }
  }
  Rule leave_given when leaveTerms(party) and (perrinMoved(party) or perrinUp(party) or perrinDead(party)) and not engineLeave(party) { Assert engineLeave(party). }
  Observe engine_waiting at engine_room when engineLeave(party) and not engineRunning(sennet_bay) "The merfolk are here, all of them, the whole Whelm, holding the paddles of the great wheel in silence, waiting for you.".
  // With every hand of the Whelm on it: anyone can, given leave.
  Action start_engine_together(actor: group, site: place) "Put your hands on the great wheel beside the merfolk, and turn the tide-engine over" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, engine_room) and engineLeave(actor) and not engineRunning(sennet_bay) and not openedBelow(sennet_bay).
    Grave "While the engine runs, a day and a night, the Whelm's lamps are out and its air-bells empty.".
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert engineRunning(sennet_bay). Set engineSince(sennet_bay) to watch(clock). }
    Result "No Admittance says a word in bubbles, and the whole Whelm leans on the wheel, and so do you, and nothing happens, and nothing happens, and then the sea moves. You feel it: the whole weight of the bay, swinging, the way the tide swings at the turn, and the wheel goes over with it, slowly, enormously, and the paddles come up out of the pit streaming, and somewhere far above in the rock a chain begins to run. All down the Undercroft the white lamps go out, row by row, as if somebody were walking along them with a snuffer. In the dark, under your hands, the wheel turns.".
  }
  // Alone, with skill, and without leave if need be: the Whelm will know who did it.
  Action start_engine_alone(actor: group, site: place) "Find the engine's catch, and let the tide take the wheel" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, engine_room) and knows(actor, undertow_known) and not engineRunning(sennet_bay) and not openedBelow(sennet_bay) and not engineFailed(actor)
      and (capable(actor, lockwork) or capable(actor, mending) or craft(actor, craft_mechanisms)).
    Grave "While the engine runs, a day and a night, the Whelm's lamps are out and its air-bells empty.".
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, lockwork, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert engineRunning(sennet_bay). Set engineSince(sennet_bay) to watch(clock). Assert startedAlone(actor). }
    On failure { Assert engineFailed(actor). }
    Result "It takes you an hour, in the green light, along the black shafts with your hands, before you find it: a pawl, as long as your arm, holding the whole wheel against the tide, as a finger holds a door. You lift it. The sea takes the wheel. It goes over with a sound you feel in your teeth, and the paddles come up out of the pit streaming, and the white lamps of the Undercroft go out, row by row, all the way along, as if somebody were walking along them with a snuffer.".
    Otherwise "You find a dozen things that might be the catch, and none of them is, and the wheel stands in its pit, enormous and patient, and does not turn.".
  }
  Relation startedAlone(group). Relation engineFailed(group).
  Rule engine_unwelcome when startedAlone(party) and not engineLeave(party) and not whelmHostile(party) { Assert whelmHostile(party). Retract tolerates(guard, party). Retract admitted(party). }
  // Everyone in an air-bell when it empties drowns, unless they have breath of their own.
  Rule bell_empties when engineRunning(sennet_bay) and at(perrin, air_bell) and not perrinDead(party) and not perrinMoved(party) { Assert perrinDead(party). Assert drownedByEngine(party). }
  Relation drownedByEngine(group).
  Rule bell_empties_told at air_bell when engineRunning(sennet_bay) and drownedByEngine(party) and not drownTold(party)
    says "Somewhere above you, through the rock, the air-bells are emptying: you hear them, one after another, a long gulp and a rush of bubbles. One of them is the bell off the Guildhall where Mercy keeps what she caught." { Assert drownTold(party). }
  Relation drownTold(group).
  Observe whelm_dark at drowned_street when engineRunning(sennet_bay) "The lamps of the Whelm are out. Chandlers' Row is black, and full of the sound of the merfolk calling to each other in the dark.".
  Rule engine_stops when engineRunning(sennet_bay) and watch(clock) >= engineSince(sennet_bay) + 144 { Retract engineRunning(sennet_bay). }
  // The cage, at the foot of the shaft, goes up while the wheel turns, into the Nexus.
  Action ride_cage(actor: group, site: place) "Step into the Aenean cage, and ride it up the shaft" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, shaft_foot) and engineRunning(sennet_bay).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert at(actor, nexus). Assert openedBelow(sennet_bay). Assert doorOpen(sennet_bay). Set openedAt(sennet_bay) to watch(clock). }
    Result "The cage goes up. It goes up through black rock for a long time, out of the water and into air, cold, then dry, rattling, with the chain running somewhere beside you and the tide working the whole of it from below like a heart; and stops; and the roof of the cage opens like a hatch, and you climb out of the floor of a round room at the top of a tower, beside a door standing by itself with nothing behind it. As you watch, the Door of Doors swings open on its own, pushed from below by the whole weight of the sea, and on the other side of it there is everywhere.".
  }
  Observe shaft_waiting at shaft_foot when engineRunning(sennet_bay) "The cage at the foot of the shaft is humming, and its door stands open.".
}

data/adventures/the-grand-tour/whelm.kyr:
Module sennet "The Grand Tour" {
  // ── The Whelm ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The lower town of old Sennet, two hundred years under the bay: Chandlers' Row, Lir's church with its bell, the
  // Guildhall. The merfolk came through the Water Door three generations ago and live in it, by the light of Aenean
  // lamps they found burning in the Undercroft below, and take their names from the signs over the drowned shops,
  // which they think are old words of power. They are ruled, or kept, by an old woman called No Admittance.
  Relation wet(place).
  Initially Assert wet(drowned_stair). Initially Assert wet(drowned_street). Initially Assert wet(drowned_church). Initially Assert wet(belfry).
  Initially Assert wet(guildhall). Initially Assert wet(undercroft). Initially Assert wet(engine_room). Initially Assert wet(shaft_foot).
  Hazard drowning "Water in the lungs" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (12).".
  Rule drowns when at(party, ?p) and wet(?p) and not capable(party, breath)
    says "Your breath is gone. The green goes black at the edges; you kick, and kick, and the stairs are somewhere above you in the dark, and then a hand that is not yours has you by the collar and is hauling, and you come up out of the bay onto the Fish Stairs on your face, coughing up half of it." {
    Assert strikes(drowning, party). Assert at(party, fish_stairs). }
  Rule breath_going when at(party, ?p) and wet(?p) and granted(party, breath) and breathUntil(party) >= 1 and breathUntil(party) - watch(clock) == 1 and not warnedBreath(party)
    says "There is a tightness coming in your chest, very gentle, like a hand. What breath you were given is running out." { Assert warnedBreath(party). }
  Relation warnedBreath(group).
  Rule breath_renewed when warnedBreath(party) and breathUntil(party) - watch(clock) > 1 { Retract warnedBreath(party). }

  Observe dstair_scene at drowned_stair when not visitedBefore(drowned_stair) "Green. Everything is green, and slow, and the light comes down from above in long wavering ropes. The Fish Stairs go down out of the sky into a street: a real street, cobbled, with houses on both sides of it with their doors open and their windows open and weed growing out of their chimneys, and lamps lit in some of the windows, white lamps, burning steady under the sea. A shoal of little silver fish goes up the street like a crowd going home.".
  Observe dstair_again at drowned_stair when visitedBefore(drowned_stair) "The foot of the Fish Stairs, in the green, where the stairs come down out of the light into the drowned street.".
  Observe dstreet_scene at drowned_street when true "Chandlers' Row, under the water: shopfronts with their glass long gone and their signs still up, the gilt letters furred with weed, CHANDLER, TALLOW AND WAX, ROOMS TO LET, CASH ONLY, SHUTTERS, HA'PENNY A SCOOP. The merfolk live in the shops. Through the open doors you see them at their lives: a woman combing a child's hair, an old man asleep in a drowned armchair, two boys fighting over a teapot.".
  Observe dchurch_scene at drowned_church when true "Lir's church stands at the bottom of the street with its tower going up into the green and its door open. The nave is full of fish. On the porch, cut deep into the oak of the door with something sharp and in a great hurry, letters you can still read: MERCY ON US.".
  Discovery door_words "On the door of Lir's church, under the water, someone cut MERCY ON US with something sharp, in a hurry.".
  Observe dchurch_words at drowned_church when not knows(party, door_words) "The letters on the door are cut deep and badly, and the last one runs off down the grain, as if whoever cut it had not had time to finish." teaches door_words.
  Observe dchurch_bell at drowned_church when true "High in the tower, if you look up the shaft of it through the water, the bell hangs on its beam, green, with a rope going down from it that sways in the current like a weed.".
  Action muffle_bell(actor: group, site: place) "Swim up the drowned tower and tie up the bell's clapper with your rope" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, belfry) and holding(actor, rope) and not bellMuffled(sennet_bay) and not bellStopped(sennet_bay).
    Time 3.
    On success { Spend rope from actor. Assert bellMuffled(sennet_bay). }
    Result "The bell is green and enormous and nearer than you wanted, and its clapper as big as a man. You lash it to the frame with every turn of rope you have, and knot it, and it hangs there trussed like a ham. Below you, at the foot of the tower, three merfolk children are watching with their mouths open, and one of them, who has a sign over his house that says CASH ONLY, begins to cry.".
  }
  Observe guild_scene at guildhall when true "The Guildhall of old Sennet: a great room with a hammer-beam roof, where the merchants met, full now of the merfolk. White Aenean lamps hang from the beams on chains. At the far end, in the drowned mayor's chair, sits an old woman with a crown of shells.".
  Observe guild_sign at guildhall when true "Over the small door at the back of the Guildhall, in old gilt letters furred with weed, a sign: NO ADMITTANCE.".
  Observe bell_scene at air_bell when true "You come up out of the water through a round hole in a floor, into air. Real air, cool and stale and smelling of copper. You are inside a dome of something like glass, as big as a room, set on the bottom of the sea, with the green light outside it on every side and fish looking in. An Aenean lamp burns on a hook. On the floor: a mattress of weed, a heap of books drying in a row, a broken chair, and a young man with his leg in splints made of an oar.".
  Observe undercroft_scene at undercroft when true "Below the Guildhall the merfolk's town stops and something much older begins: walls of black stone fitted without mortar, tall arches, everything square and plain and cut with a precision that hurts the eye. The Aeneans called it theirs, and cut their plaque on it, and put their lamps in it. The lamps here are the same white lamps, but there are hundreds of them, in rows, and they hum.".
  Observe engine_scene at engine_room when true "The tide-engine fills a hall the size of a church: a great wheel of black metal, standing on its edge, half in a pit, with paddles on it the size of doors, and round it a confusion of shafts and chains and copper, all green, all still. A plaque in the wall is cut in letters you half know.".
  Observe shaft_scene at shaft_foot when true "The passage ends at the foot of a shaft, square, black, going straight up into the rock, with a cage of black metal standing at the bottom of it on rails, like a lift in a mine, waiting.".

  // ── No Admittance ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person admittance "No Admittance" at guildhall {
    Role "the merfolk's matriarch, in a crown of shells with something green in it". Ancestry undine. Level 5. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner proud.
    Greets "The old woman in the drowned mayor's chair looks at you a long time out of eyes like two wet stones. Her crown is shells, and in the front of it is a petal of green glass, and the water round it moves like water round a spring. 'Dry,' she says at last. 'You are dry. In my Guildhall.' She considers this. 'I am No Admittance. I keep who comes and goes. Who let you come?'".
    Greets again "No Admittance considers you from the mayor's chair.".
  }
  Relation admitted(group). Relation ateWith(group). Relation admittanceLaughed(group). Relation admittanceTrusts(group).
  Relation whelmWarned(group). Relation whelmHostile(group). Relation blessed(group). Relation waterGiven(group).
  Rule admittance_trusts when (admittanceLaughed(admittance) or blessed(admittance)) and ateWith(party) and not admittanceTrusts(admittance) { Assert admittanceTrusts(admittance). }
  Person guard "the Admittance's guard" at drowned_street {
    Role "two merfolk with eel-spears, at the foot of the Guildhall steps". Ancestry undine. Numbers 2. Calling cleric. Trait oceanist. Level 2. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    State posted blocking "Two merfolk with eel-spears keep the Guildhall steps, floating, watching who comes.".
    Guards guild_way.
  }
  Rule guard_admits when admitted(party) and not tolerates(guard, party) and not whelmHostile(party) { Assert tolerates(guard, party). }
  Topic guard_invited with guard "Tell the guards Ha'penny asked you to supper" when hapennyInvites(hapenny) and not admitted(actor) once {
    Says "The two guards look at each other. One of them says something to the other in bubbles, and the other laughs, also in bubbles. 'Ha'penny,' the first says. 'She brings us everything. Last week a cat.' He moves his spear aside. 'Supper is at the turn of the evening.' He leans close and breathes on you, which is how the Whelm says come in; the water in your chest goes soft and easy. 'Go up. Eat what you are given.'".
    On discuss { Assert admitted(actor). Assert granted(actor, breath). Set grantedUntil(actor, breath) to 0. Set breathUntil(actor) to watch(clock) + 18. }
  }
  // A sailor knows the greeting the merfolk give at the third step, and gives it back.
  Topic guard_greeting with guard "Touch your forehead to the water and say Salt and welcome, as the fishermen do" when craft(actor, craft_water) and not admitted(actor) once {
    Says "The guards stare. Then the older one touches his own forehead, slowly, and says back, in a voice like water going down a drain, 'Salt and welcome, dry one,' and grins with a great many teeth. 'A boatman. You smell of tar.' He leans in and breathes on you, which is how the Whelm says come in, and the water in your chest goes easy. 'Go up.'".
    On discuss { Assert admitted(actor). Assert granted(actor, breath). Set grantedUntil(actor, breath) to 0. Set breathUntil(actor) to watch(clock) + 18. }
  }
  Kind candle_gift_kind "a beeswax candle" is gear worth 1 weighing 0 described "A good beeswax candle, the kind the House uses in Veyra's chapel.".
  Topic guard_gift with guard "Show the guards something dry they have never seen" when not admitted(actor) and (holding(actor, mirror_kind) or holding(actor, glass_petal_kind) or holding(actor, handbook_kind) or holding(actor, wind_jar_kind)) once {
    Says "They come close, the both of them, and look at it with their gills going, and touch it with the ends of their spears. 'Dry,' one says, reverently. 'Dry, and down here.' They hand it back to you, which you did not expect. 'Gran will want to see you,' the other says, and breathes on you, which is how the Whelm says come in. 'Go up. Bring it.'".
    On discuss { Assert admitted(actor). Assert granted(actor, breath). Set grantedUntil(actor, breath) to 0. Set breathUntil(actor) to watch(clock) + 18. }
  }
  Action table(actor: group, site: place) "Sit down at No Admittance's table, and eat what you are given" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, guildhall) and at(admittance, site) and admitted(actor) and not ateWith(actor) and hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 22.
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert ateWith(actor). }
    Result "Supper in the Whelm is laid on the old merchants' table, under the white lamps: raw things, in brine, on drowned plates with the arms of the Glovers' Company on them. Eels. Something with too many legs that is still deciding whether to be dead. Weed in long green ribbons. A soup of nothing you can name that tastes of the inside of a shell. The merfolk watch you eat it, every mouthful, in a silence like a theatre. No Admittance watches longest. When you have eaten it all she picks something off her own plate, a little white thing like a pearl, and holds it out to you on her palm. You eat that too. The Guildhall breathes out. 'Well,' says No Admittance. 'Well. That is how it is done.'".
  }
  Observe sailor_supper at guildhall when ateWith(party) and craft(party, craft_water) and not visitedBefore(guildhall) "One of the merfolk at table says, loudly, that you eat like a fisherman, and the table laughs, and you understand it is the highest compliment the Whelm has.".
  Topic admittance_crown with admittance "Ask No Admittance about the green petal in her crown" when true once {
    Says "'The Court of Waters gave it my grandmother when we came through, to keep.' She does not touch it. 'Not to give, not to use. To keep. They gave keeping to us because we are good at it. We kept the street. We kept the lamps lit. We kept the dry men's bell.' She looks at you. 'Now every dry child in Sennet with a bear-leader comes to the third step and shouts down that they want it. For a door.' She snorts a stream of bubbles. 'Keeping is the whole of it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, water_kept). }
  }
  Discovery water_kept "No Admittance wears the Water petal of the Rose in her crown of shells. The Court of Waters gave it her grandmother when the merfolk came through, to keep: not to give or to use.".
  Topic admittance_dry with admittance "Ask No Admittance what she thinks of the dry folk of Sennet" when true once {
    Says "'They let the sea into their own houses.' She sweeps a hand at the Guildhall, the street outside, the church. 'Their great ones went up into the sky and the sea came into the hole, and their little ones drowned in their beds, and we came through two lifetimes after and found the lamps still lit and the tables laid.' She leans forward. 'And then the dry men set a brass plate on the third step and told the sea how far it may come up their stairs.' She sits back. 'No admittance. Above the third step, no admittance.' She does not seem to hear what she has said.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, admittance_grievance). }
  }
  Discovery admittance_grievance "No Admittance resents the Harbour Bylaw that keeps the merfolk below the third step of the Fish Stairs: the dry folk let the sea into their own houses, and then told it how far it might come up their stairs.".
  Topic admittance_name with admittance "Tell No Admittance what the sign over the back door of her Guildhall says, and what it means in Sennet" when knows(actor, admittance_grievance) and not admittanceLaughed(admittance) once {
    Says "You tell her. In Sennet, over a door, NO ADMITTANCE means keep out. It is what they put up on the door to the cellar. The Guildhall goes so still you can hear the lamps hum. No Admittance looks at you. She looks over her shoulder at the little door at the back of the hall, and the gilt letters over it, for a long time. Then her shoulders begin to shake, and her crown slips, and she puts up a hand to it, and the sound that comes out of her is so loud and so long that the fish go out of the windows. She laughs until she weeps, and the merfolk laugh with her because she is laughing, and then because they understand. 'Keep out!' she says, wiping her eyes. 'Sixty years. Sixty years I have been keep out, and so proud of it.' She looks at you with her wet-stone eyes and they are not stones at all. 'Well. We are the same, then, the plate and I. The plate and I should meet.'".
    On discuss { Assert admittanceLaughed(admittance). }
  }
  Topic admittance_step with admittance "Tell No Admittance that the Harbourmaster let Ha'penny up the stairs to the Glass Market" when hapennyShopped(hapenny) and pumphreyRelents(pumphrey) and not stepTold(admittance) once {
    Says "'He did.' She knows, of course; Ha'penny has told the whole Whelm, twice. 'With his own leave, the brass man.' She thinks about it. 'Then he is not all brass.' She looks at you. 'And you asked him. A dry one asked a dry one, for one of ours.' She inclines her head, a little, the way a queen does when nobody is watching. 'That is noted.'".
    On discuss { Assert stepTold(admittance). Assert blessed(admittance). }
  }
  Relation stepTold(group).

  // ── The Water petal ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Keeping is the whole of it. She gives it, in the end, for a reason that is not a door: because a dry one asked a
  // dry one for one of hers, at the third step; or as the gift of the house to the guest who stood with her
  // granddaughter when Mercy asked her blessing on the dry man she caught.
  Relation matchBlessed(group). Relation mercyAsks(group).
  Topic admittance_petal with admittance "Ask No Admittance for the Water petal of the Rose" when admittanceTrusts(admittance) and not petalTaken(water_petal) and not stepTold(admittance) and not matchBlessed(admittance) once {
    Says "'For a door.' She does not raise her voice. 'Every dry child with a bear-leader wants it for a door. Keeping is the whole of it.' She breathes out a thread of bubbles that goes straight up and does not break. 'Bring me a reason that is not a door, and I will think about it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, admittance_reason). }
  }
  Discovery admittance_reason "No Admittance will not give the Water petal for a door. She asks for a reason that is not a door.".
  Topic admittance_gives with admittance "Ask No Admittance again for the Water petal" when admittanceTrusts(admittance) and not petalTaken(water_petal) and (stepTold(admittance) or matchBlessed(admittance)) once {
    Says "She takes off the crown of shells and looks at the green petal in it, and the water round it moves like water round a spring. 'Keeping,' she says. 'My grandmother kept it, and my mother, and I, sixty years. For the Court of Waters, that never once came to see whether we had.' She works it free of the shells with her old fingers. 'A dry one asked for one of ours, and was given. Now one of ours gives a dry one.' She holds it out to you on her palm, wet. 'Not for a door. For the asking.'".
    On discuss { Give water_petal to actor. Assert petalTaken(water_petal). Assert waterGiven(admittance). }
  }
  Topic mercy_ask_blessing with mercy "Tell Mercy she should ask her grandmother's blessing herself, and that you will stand with her" when mercyTrusts(mercy) and knows(actor, perrin_alive) and admittanceTrusts(admittance) and not matchBlessed(admittance) and not mercyAsks(mercy) once {
    Says "She goes very still in the water. 'Ask Gran.' She says it as if you had told her to ask the tide. 'For a dry man.' Then her chin comes up, exactly like a crown. 'At supper. In front of everyone. Then she can't pretend she didn't hear.' She looks at you. 'You'll be there. You said.'".
    On discuss { Assert mercyAsks(mercy). }
  }
  Event mercy_blessing at guildhall when mercyAsks(mercy) and at(party, guildhall) and at(mercy, guildhall) and at(admittance, guildhall) and hour(clock) >= 17 and not matchBlessed(admittance) "Mercy swims up the length of the merchants' table with the whole Whelm watching, and stops in front of the drowned mayor's chair, and says, loud enough for the bell to hear, that she has caught a dry man out of the sky and means to keep him, and asks her grandmother's blessing on it. Nobody breathes, if that is the word. No Admittance looks at her granddaughter for a long time; and then, for longer, at you, standing beside her. 'A dry man,' she says. 'Under my roof. Eating my fish.' She turns the crown in her hands. 'Who reads books to the children, Ha'penny says, and lets them sit on his bad leg.' A very long pause. 'Keep him, then,' says No Admittance. 'Keeping is the whole of it.' The Guildhall goes up like a fountain." then { Assert matchBlessed(admittance). Assert admittanceTrusts(admittance). }

  // ── Mercy ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Named from the words on the church door; caught a man falling out of the sky twelve nights ago, and has kept him.
  // She wants to go up and see the lanterns of Cloudgate go up alive, which she has only ever seen come down dead.
  Person mercy "Mercy" at air_bell {
    Role "a merfolk girl with silver in her hair" when not following(mercy, party).
    Role "a merfolk girl in a water-butt on a barrow, astonished" when following(mercy, party).
    Ancestry undine. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "A merfolk girl comes up through the water as if she had been poured, and stops a foot from your face, and looks at you with enormous curiosity and no fear at all. She is perhaps twenty. There is silver in her hair like the scales of a fish. 'You came down the stairs,' she says. 'Nobody comes down the stairs. Are you looking for something? Everybody up there is looking for something.' She tilts her head. 'I am Mercy.'".
    Greets again "'You again,' says Mercy, pleased.".
    Joins "Mercy settles her chin on the rim of the butt. 'Push,' she says.".
    Leaves "Mercy goes home to the Whelm before the tide turns, as merfolk must.".
  }
  Relation mercyTrusts(group). Relation mercyKissed(group). Relation mercyNamed(group). Relation mercyWish(group). Relation mercySawLanterns(group).
  Rule mercy_supper when hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 21 and not following(mercy, party) and not at(mercy, guildhall) and not perrinDead(party) and not mercyUp(mercy) { Assert at(mercy, guildhall). }
  Rule mercy_bell when (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 17) and not following(mercy, party) and not at(mercy, air_bell) and not mercyUp(mercy) and not perrinUp(party) { Assert at(mercy, air_bell). }
  Relation mercyUp(group).
  Rule mercy_trusts when (ateWith(party) or admittanceTrusts(admittance) or following(aubrey, party)) and not mercyTrusts(mercy) { Assert mercyTrusts(mercy). }
  Action mercy_breath(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Mercy for breath" {
    Speaker mercy.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(mercy, site) and mercyTrusts(mercy) and not perrinDead(party) and not (granted(actor, breath) and breathUntil(actor) - watch(clock) > 6).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert granted(actor, breath). Set grantedUntil(actor, breath) to 0. Set breathUntil(actor) to watch(clock) + 18. Assert mercyKissed(actor). }
    Result "She laughs, and takes your face in her two cold hands and kisses you on the mouth, and it tastes of salt and something green, and the water you are breathing goes soft and easy in your chest, like air in a warm room. 'There. Three hours. Then come up, or come back.' She lets go. 'Dry ones always ask so politely.'".
  }
  Action hapenny_breath(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Ha'penny for some of her breath" {
    Speaker hapenny.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hapenny, site) and hapennyInvites(hapenny) and not (granted(actor, breath) and breathUntil(actor) - watch(clock) > 3).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert granted(actor, breath). Set grantedUntil(actor, breath) to 0. Set breathUntil(actor) to watch(clock) + 6. }
    Result "She puts her arms round your neck and kisses you on the nose, very loud. 'There. An hour. I'm little.' She considers. 'If it runs out, come up. Don't be brave. The brave ones are the ones on the bottom.'".
  }
  Topic mercy_catch with mercy "Ask Mercy about the man she caught" when knows(actor, sky_man) and not mercyTrusts(mercy) once {
    Says "Her face closes like a shell. 'Who told you that?' And then, before you can answer: 'Ha'penny. Ha'penny tells the fish.' She looks at you hard. 'He is mine. I caught him. If you are from up there, from the sky-island, come to take him back up where they threw him, you can go up the stairs again, and you will not get breath from me.' She turns to go, and turns back. 'Come to Gran's table, if you want to talk to me. Eat what you are given. Then I'll know.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mercy_wary). }
  }
  Discovery mercy_wary "Mercy will not speak of the man she caught to anyone from the sky-island come to take him back. She will talk to someone who has eaten at No Admittance's table.".
  Topic mercy_catch_trusted with mercy "Ask Mercy how she caught the man who fell out of the sky" when mercyTrusts(mercy) once {
    Says "'In the fog.' She says it with her whole face, the way Ha'penny talks about the bell. 'I was at the top, at the cloud, where the light is, the night of the first fog. And something came down through it. A man, all arms, with his coat open like wings, falling.' She holds out her arms. 'I went up under him and caught him in the water before the bottom got him, and his leg broke on me, and he was drowning, so I gave him breath and took him down to the air-bell, the one the guests sleep in, and he woke up and saw me and said, I'm dead, aren't I.' She laughs. 'And I said no, you're in the Whelm. And he said, that's worse, my mother would die.' She looks at you. 'His name is Perrin. He's mine. Do you want to see him?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, perrin_alive). Assert knows(actor, air_bell_known). }
  }
  Discovery perrin_alive "Perrin Halyard is alive. Mercy caught him in the bay the night he fell, and keeps him in an air-bell in the Whelm with a broken leg.".
  Topic mercy_wish_asked with mercy "Ask Mercy what she would like, if she could have anything" when mercyTrusts(mercy) once {
    Says "She does not have to think. 'The lanterns.' She points up, through the green, toward a light you cannot see. 'Every year, on the long night, lights go up from the sky-island, a thousand, and in the morning they come down into the sea, black and dead, all over the Whelm, and the children collect them.' She looks up. 'I have never seen one alive. I want to see one go up. Burning. From the sky-island, with my own eyes, on the night.' She looks at you as if it were obvious. 'And Perrin wants to stay down here for ever. So we are going to have to work something out.'".
    On discuss { Assert mercyWish(mercy). Assert knows(actor, mercy_wants_lanterns). }
  }
  Discovery mercy_wants_lanterns "Mercy wants to see the lanterns of Cloudgate go up, alive, on the Night of Lanterns, from Cloudgate itself; she has only ever seen them come down dead into the sea. Perrin wants to stay in the Whelm for ever.".
  Topic mercy_name with mercy "Tell Mercy what her name means, and who cut it on the church door" when knows(actor, mercy_meaning) and not mercyNamed(mercy) once {
    Says "She listens without moving at all, the way the merfolk listen, with her gills still. 'A prayer,' she says. 'Somebody's prayer. A girl's, with a fish-knife, while the water came.' She puts her hand flat against her own chest. 'And it worked.' She looks at you, astonished. 'It worked, didn't it. I was mercy on him. Nobody up there had any, and I was.' She is quiet for a while. 'Is her family still up there? On the Quay?' You tell her about Old Bethan, and the eels. 'I'd like to meet her,' says Mercy. 'I'd like to tell her it worked.'".
    On discuss { Assert mercyNamed(mercy). }
  }

  // ── Perrin Halyard ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Pushed in the fog, by hands he did not see, with keys ringing. He has decided it was his brother, whom he can
  // forgive, rather than either of the two people who wear keys; and would rather stay dead than accuse him. He has
  // never been so happy in his life.
  Person perrin "Perrin Halyard" at air_bell {
    Role "a young man with his leg in splints made of an oar" when not perrinUp(party) and not legSet(perrin).
    Role "a young man with his leg properly splinted" when legSet(perrin) and not perrinUp(party).
    Role "Perrin Halyard, come up out of the sea" when perrinUp(party).
    Ancestry human. Calling mage. Trait diviner. Level 4. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "The young man on the weed mattress looks up from a drowned book he is drying page by page against the lamp, and sees you, and goes white, and then, seeing your face, laughs. 'Oh, God. A Tourist. Of course. The bay's full of them.' He has a quick, clever, sunburnt face and his mother's nose. 'I'm dead, you know. Officially. They're letting me down on the third day. I'd come, but I've broken my leg.'".
    Greets again "'You again,' says Perrin Halyard, and shuts his book on his finger.".
    Joins "Perrin Halyard gets the oar under his arm and stands, white to the lips, and grins at you. 'Lead on. Slowly. I'm a dead man; we don't hurry.'".
    Leaves "Perrin Halyard lets go of your shoulder, and stands on his own, on the oar, and nods to you, as one Doorward to another.".
  }
  Entity aubrey_did: claim "Aubrey pushed Perrin off the Balustrade".
  Initially Assert believes(perrin, aubrey_did). Initially Set conviction(perrin, aubrey_did) to 2.
  Relation legSet(group). Relation perrinKnows(group). Relation perrinForgives(group). Relation perrinPromised(group).
  Relation perrinWrote(group). Relation perrinWantsUp(group).
  Topic perrin_fall with perrin "Ask Perrin Halyard what happened at the Balustrade" when true once {
    Says "He stops smiling. 'I was pushed.' He says it quite plainly. 'I'd quarrelled with my brother, on the Promenade, and gone off to the Balustrade to cool down, and the fog came up over the rail, the way it does at night, thick as wool. I was leaning on the rail. And there were hands in my back, two of them, hard, and I went over.' He looks at his hands. 'I didn't see. I heard keys, ringing, a lot of keys, as if somebody had shaken a chain. And then I was falling through the cloud for a very long time and then I was in the sea and there was a girl.' He shrugs. 'Aubrey. It must have been Aubrey. He'd told me to jump. He was drunk. He didn't mean it.' He looks at you. 'I'm not going back up there to put my brother in the dock for being drunk. I'd rather be dead. I'm very good at it; I've had practice.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, keys_heard). }
  }
  Discovery keys_heard "Perrin Halyard was pushed off the Balustrade from behind, in the fog, by two hands he did not see; he heard keys ringing, a great many, as if someone had shaken a chain. He has decided it was his brother Aubrey, drunk, and will not go back up to accuse him.".
  Topic perrin_found with perrin "Ask Perrin Halyard what he found out, that he quarrelled over" when knows(actor, keys_heard) once {
    Says "He looks at you, deciding, and picks at the splint on his leg. 'You'll find out anyway, if you're on the Tour.' He pulls himself up against the glass. 'Ysabeau, my great-great-whatever, the one with the hill on her hand. She didn't lift Cloudgate by magic. She lifted it with a petal. The Air petal of the Rose, that the North Wind gave her because he loved her, and she took it home and set it in the keel of Halyard Hill, and up it went, and the sea came in.' He rubs his face. 'It's still there. Under the cellars. I climbed down and saw it, the week before the Tour was proclaimed. Every petal the Rector is sending people after is in a court somewhere, and the fourth is holding up my mother's house.' He laughs, shortly. 'I said the Air should have it back. Aubrey said the house would fall down. Well, it would.' He hesitates. 'I told the Rector. Before anyone. She was my teacher. She said she'd think about what to do.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, keel_petal). Assert knows(actor, perrin_told_rector). }
  }
  Discovery keel_petal "The Air petal of the Rose is not in the Plane of Air. The North Wind gave it to Ysabeau Halyard for love; she set it in the keel of Halyard Hill and lifted it into the sky. It is still there, in the keel under the cellars of Halyard House, holding Cloudgate up. Taken out, Cloudgate would fall.".
  Discovery perrin_told_rector "Perrin Halyard told the Rector what holds Cloudgate up, before anyone else, the week before the Grand Tour was proclaimed; he told her the Air should have its petal back, and she said she would think about what to do.".
  Kind perrin_notebook_kind "Perrin's notebook" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "A red notebook with the key of the House of Doors stamped on the cover, swollen with salt: Perrin Halyard's. Pages of Aenean, copied off plaques and drowned books; a drawing of a great wheel. The last pages are dated after the night he fell.".
  Item perrin_notebook "Perrin's notebook" is perrin_notebook_kind at air_bell owned by perrin.
  Topic perrin_notebook_asked with perrin "Ask Perrin Halyard for his notebook, which the Rector wants" when commissioned(actor) and not carries(actor, perrin_notebook) once {
    Says "'Isadora wants it?' He looks pleased, and then puzzled. 'It's only the Aenean. And the wheel. Nothing she couldn't read off the plaque herself.' He hands it over. 'Tell her I'm sorry about the coffin.' Then he stops, with his hand still out. 'No. Don't tell her anything. Don't tell anybody I'm here. Will you promise me?'".
    On discuss { Give perrin_notebook to actor. Assert lends(perrin, perrin_notebook, actor). }
  }
  Topic perrin_promise with perrin "Promise Perrin Halyard you will tell nobody he is alive" when knows(actor, perrin_alive) and not perrinPromised(perrin) once {
    Says "'Thank you.' He means it; he looks younger. 'It's only that if I'm alive, somebody pushed me, and if somebody pushed me it was Aubrey, and if it was Aubrey he hangs, or worse, he lives with it.' He picks up his book. 'Dead is so much simpler. You'd be surprised.'".
    On discuss { Assert perrinPromised(perrin). Assert promiseMade(perrin_secret). }
  }
  Relation toldAlive(group).
  Promise perrin_secret "to tell nobody that Perrin Halyard is alive" to perrin
    kept when closingDay() and not toldAlive(party) and not perrinDead(party) "Somewhere under the bay a young man who is officially dead goes on being so, as he asked."
    broken when toldAlive(party) "Somewhere a secret you promised to keep is out in the world, and running." { }.
  Topic perrin_aubrey with perrin "Tell Perrin Halyard that his brother believes he pushed him, and is drinking himself to death over it" when knows(actor, aubrey_quarrel) and not perrinWrote(perrin) once {
    Says "He stares at you. 'He thinks.' He puts the book down. 'Oh, the idiot. Oh, the great fool.' He laughs, and it goes wrong halfway. 'It wasn't Aubrey. I said it was, because. It wasn't. He was on the gravel, being sick. I heard him. I heard him being sick while somebody else came up behind me.' He puts his face in his hands. 'I let him think it. I lay down here and let him think it, so I wouldn't have to think who.' He looks up. 'Give me a pen. Have you got a pen? No, of course, there's no ink in the sea. Pencil.' He tears a page out of a drowned book and writes on it, fast, against his knee, and folds it, and holds it out. 'Take him that. Please. Today.'".
    On discuss { Assert perrinWrote(perrin). Give brother_letter to actor. Set conviction(perrin, aubrey_did) to 0. }
  }
  // Told what the winch-gang, the footman or the amanuensis know, he sees whose keys they were.
  Topic perrin_told_who with perrin "Tell Perrin Halyard what you have learned of who was at the Balustrade" when (knows(actor, late_basket) or knows(actor, bishop_sleeves) or knows(actor, chapter_rewritten)) and knows(actor, keys_heard) and not perrinKnows(perrin) once {
    Says "He listens, and as he listens his face changes, the way a face changes when someone you love walks into the room behind you and you see them in a mirror. 'Keys,' he says. 'A chain of keys. Sleeves like a bishop's.' He looks at the lamp. 'The eleven o'clock basket.' He is quiet for a long time. 'I told her. I told her, and I went to the Balustrade, and she came after me to talk, and I didn't turn round because I thought it was Aubrey come to say sorry.' He closes his eyes. 'Isadora. She taught me Aenean. She lent me her own books.' When he opens his eyes they are perfectly dry and much older. 'She'll go for the keel. She'll take the Tour's three and go down for the fourth, and the house will fall, and Mother, and the Whelm under it.' He takes hold of the oar on his leg. 'I have to go up.'".
    On discuss { Assert perrinKnows(perrin). Assert perrinWantsUp(perrin). Assert knows(actor, quance_pushed). Set conviction(perrin, aubrey_did) to 0. }
  }
  Discovery quance_pushed "It was the Rector, Isadora Quance, who pushed Perrin Halyard off the Balustrade in the fog: he had told her what holds Cloudgate up, and that the Air should have its petal back. Her chain of keys rang; her sleeves hung like a bishop's; she came down alone on the eleven o'clock basket.".
  // A leg set by someone who knows how can carry him up the stairs on his own; otherwise Mercy carries him.
  Action set_leg(actor: group, site: place) "Take the oar off Perrin Halyard's leg and set it properly" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(perrin, site) and not legSet(perrin) and (capable(actor, mending) or craft(actor, craft_healing)).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert legSet(perrin). }
    Result "Mercy set it as you would set a fin, which is to say with great love and in the wrong place. You take the oar off, and feel along the bone while he swears in three languages, one of them Aenean, and pull it straight, and splint it with two of the drowned books, which is the best thing anybody has done with that edition. 'There,' you say. He looks at it, white and sweating. 'I could walk on that,' he says. 'In a week. I could swim on it now.'".
  }
  Topic perrin_up_asked with perrin "Ask Perrin Halyard to come up out of the Whelm with you" when perrinWantsUp(perrin) and not perrinUp(party) and not following(perrin, party) once {
    Says "'Yes.' He is already pulling himself toward the hole in the floor. 'Mercy will bring me, she'll have to, I'm a stone in the water with this leg.' He looks at you over his shoulder. 'Where? Not Mother's. Not yet. Somewhere she'd come to.' He thinks. 'Somewhere very public, Isadora would say. She always said, if you've something to say, say it where it can't be unsaid.'".
    On discuss { Assert following(perrin, party). Assert perrinMoved(party). }
  }
  // Once he is up the Fish Stairs and on dry stone, he is up: the city will know him.
  Rule perrin_surfaces when following(perrin, party) and inSennet() and not perrinUp(party)
    says "Perrin Halyard comes up the Fish Stairs out of the bay on Mercy's shoulder, dripping, with his leg out stiff in front of him, a dead man in a wet shirt in the middle of the Quay, and the Quay stops. Somebody drops a lobster. Old Bethan, if she is anywhere about, says Mercy on us, and means it." {
    Assert perrinUp(party). }

  // ── The brothers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Aubrey brought to the Fish Stairs after dark; Mercy brings Perrin up to the third step to meet him.
  Event brothers_meet at fish_stairs when at(party, fish_stairs) and following(aubrey, party) and dark() and not perrinDead(party) and not perrinUp(party) and not brothersMet(party) "Aubrey Halyard goes down the Fish Stairs in the dark, past the brass plate, and down, until he is standing in the bay up to his waist in his good coat, and stands there. For a while nothing. Then the water by the third step bulges, and a merfolk girl comes up out of it with a young man on her shoulder, and the young man says, 'You great fool, you're ruining Father's coat.' Aubrey makes a noise like nothing you have heard a man make. He gets hold of his brother, coat, splints, merfolk girl and all, and holds on. 'I thought I'd,' he says. 'I thought.' 'You were being sick on the gravel,' says Perrin, into his shoulder. 'I heard you. You've always been sick on gravel. Mother despairs.' It is some time before either of them lets go." then {
    Assert brothersMet(party). Assert perrinForgives(perrin). Assert aubreyFreed(aubrey). Set conviction(aubrey, aubrey_guilt) to 0. Assert aubreyFriend(aubrey). Retract following(aubrey, party). }

  // ── The water-butt ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // How to take a mermaid up to Cloudgate for the Night of Lanterns: a water-butt, a barrow, the basket, and nerve.
  Relation buttGot(group). Relation mercyComing(group).
  Topic peg_butt with peg "Ask Peg Arklow to lend you the rain-butt off the Sounding Line's yard, and a barrow" when knows(actor, mercy_wants_lanterns) and not buttGot(actor) once {
    Says "'My rain-butt.' She looks at you. 'What for?' You tell her. Peg Arklow puts both hands flat on the bar and laughs until the sounding-lead swings. 'A mermaid. Up the chain. To the Lanterns.' She wipes her eyes. 'Take it. Take the barrow. Take my blessing. I'll stand on the Quay and watch you go up.' She points a finger at you. 'You bring my butt back.'".
    On discuss { Assert buttGot(actor). }
  }
  Topic kittiwake_butt with kittiwake "Ask Mother Kittiwake for the loan of the winch-house's fire-butt, and a barrow" when knows(actor, mercy_wants_lanterns) and gangFriend(actor) and not buttGot(actor) once {
    Says "'The fire-butt.' She looks at you. 'If the winch-house catches light while it's gone it's on your head.' She hears what it is for, and her face goes through several things. 'NO DOGS, the slate says,' she says at last. 'It doesn't say a word about mermaids.' She whistles up two of the gang to carry it.".
    On discuss { Assert buttGot(actor). }
  }
  Topic mercy_lanterns_offer with mercy "Tell Mercy you will take her up to Cloudgate to see the lanterns go up, in a water-butt" when mercyWish(mercy) and buttGot(actor) and day(clock) == 4 and not mercyComing(mercy) once {
    Says "She stares at you, and then she shrieks, a sound like a gull, and turns over in the water three times. 'In a butt! Like a herring!' She comes up again with her hair over her face. 'Perrin will say no. Perrin will say I'll be seen.' She pushes her hair back. 'I want to be seen. Let the sky-island see me. Let them see who caught their boy.' She looks at you. 'Tonight? The long night? You'll have to carry me up the stairs, and up the chain, and I'll need to be wet the whole time, and I'll want to see everything.'".
    On discuss { Assert mercyComing(mercy). }
  }
  Action fetch_mercy(actor: group, site: place) "Bring the water-butt and the barrow down to the Fish Stairs, and help Mercy into it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, fish_stairs) and mercyComing(mercy) and buttGot(actor) and not following(mercy, party) and not mercySawLanterns(mercy) and day(clock) == 4.
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert following(mercy, party). Assert mercyUp(mercy). }
    Result "It takes four fishermen, the butt, the barrow, a great deal of advice from the Quay and a bucket chain of the harbour's children to fill it, and then Mercy comes up the Fish Stairs past the brass plate on your arm, flopping, laughing, and goes into the butt with a splash that soaks everybody in reach, and comes up with her chin on the rim. 'Go on,' she says. 'Go on, go on.' The Quay pushes the barrow.".
  }
  Action ride_up_mercy(actor: group, site: place) "Wheel the barrow with Mercy in it onto the basket, and go up" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, winch_floor) and following(mercy, party) and basketRuns() and (gangFriend(actor) or quantity(actor, gold) >= 10).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert at(actor, landing_stage). Assert mercyAloft(mercy). }
    Result "Mother Kittiwake looks at the barrow for a long time. Then she blows her whistle, and the gang, which has heard, puts its backs into the bars and sings, and you go up through the cloud with a mermaid in a water-butt with her chin on the rim, saying 'Oh. Oh. Oh,' all the way, at every turn of the chain, and when you come up out of the top of the cloud she stops saying anything at all.".
  }
  Relation mercyAloft(group).
  // If she cannot be paid for, the gang will take her up free once it knows the company; else ten coin, for two.
  Rule mercy_fare when mercyAloft(mercy) and not gangFriend(party) and not mercyPaid(party) { Assert mercyPaid(party). Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 10 or to nothing. }
  Relation mercyPaid(group).
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/charter.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "What the Hall was given the Long Wall to do, and what the parish was told it owned: the charter over the steward's fire, the sheaf in forty, the reeve's office, and the bell.".

  // ── The Hall's charter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A monk's copy of a much older writ of the Prefect of the Marches (the Aeneans, who found the wall and did not
  // build it; they fenced the culvert, wrote the keeping into law and let the law outlast them). The copy is in the
  // old imperial tongue; under it, pinned, a card in a later hand gives the Hall's own understanding of it. The two
  // differ by one word, custodia, which is a keeping and which three centuries of lords have read as a holding.
  Discovery charter_seen "A framed charter hangs over the steward's fire: close lines in the old imperial tongue, much copied, and pinned under it in a later hand a card that reads THE HOUSE HOLDS THE LONG WALL AND ALL IN IT." {
    Source charter "the framed charter over the study fire" at study readable by party.
    Known by venn.
  }
  Discovery charter_read "The charter is a writ of the Prefect of the Marches: the House on the water is given the KEEPING of the Long Wall of the Hesci and of the waters behind it, to keep and not to own; the dale renders one sheaf in forty for so long as the wall stands; none shall hinder the Keeper of the Wall in its work; the House shall neither take from the wall nor sell nor suffer it to be taken, and what is found in the wall is the dale's; and if the keeping fail, the dale shall choose another House. The reeve of the waters holds the rod to watch the keeping." {
    Found by searching study with lore "The old imperial tongue is a lawyer's Latin, and the first lines are not hard. CUSTODIA MURI LONGI HESCORUM: the keeping of the Long Wall of the Hesci. NON DOMINIUM SED CUSTODIA: not lordship but keeping. Under those, a long list of clauses in a clerk's abbreviations, which you can follow only as far as a sheaf, a rod and a reeve before the hand gets away from you. The card pinned under it says only that the House holds the wall and all in it. Mother Ysolt will read the rest.".
  }
  Relation reeveRoused(group). Relation valeTold(group). Relation bellGone().
  Relation wardenChosen(group). Relation sheafWithheld(group).

  // Mother Ysolt reads the copy as she reads the register: slowly, and as someone who learned her letters from nuns
  // who copied this sort of thing for their bread. What she finds is not what she has preached.
  Topic ysolt_charter with ysolt "Show Mother Ysolt the charter over the steward's fire" when knows(actor, charter_seen) and not valeTold(ysolt) {
    Says "She reads it standing, with her lips moving, and then once more with her finger under the line. 'Murus Longus,' she says. 'The Long Wall. Say it quickly, in the mouth of a dale that never spoke Latin, and where do you come to?' She almost smiles. 'And Merrow is murus with the stone worn off it. I have been christening children on the Wall for twenty years and calling it a king.' She reads the third line again and does not like it. 'Custodia. Keeping. It does not say the House holds the wall. It says the House keeps it, and is paid a sheaf in forty to do so, and may be replaced if it does not. The card under it has had that wrong since before the Hall's grandfather.' She puts the copy down. 'And Hesci. I took it for a surname in the register. There was a Hesk, reeve of the waters, buried in the year the Long Man wept.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, charter_read). Assert valeTold(ysolt). }
  }
  Observe hesk_register at vestry when knows(party, charter_read) and knows(party, wept_known) "Turning back through the register with the charter's word in your head, you find them: Hesk, Alys, dyke-reeve, buried in the year after the water; and before her, Hesk, Wat, and Hesk, Brid, and a column of Hesks at the foot of the old pages, thinning to one. Nobody of the name since. The reeve's office went to the Collers by marriage, and the rod with it.".

  // Gammer Coller reads the same lines as an office, not a history.
  Topic nell_office with nell "Tell Gammer Coller what the charter says of the reeve of the waters" when knows(actor, charter_read) and not reeveRoused(nell) {
    Says "Gammer Coller says nothing for the length of a pipe she does not smoke. 'To watch the keeping,' she says. 'I thought I was to keep the ditches. Forty years I have kept the ditches and been thanked for it with a pot of lard at Michaelmas.' She takes the rod down from its pegs and sets it across her knees. 'It was never the Mower I ought to have been watching on the crest. It was the Hall.' She looks at you sharply. 'Does it say what the reeve does if the Hall will not be watched?'".
    On discuss { Assert reeveRoused(nell). }
  }
  Topic nell_remedy with nell "Tell Gammer Coller the charter lets the dale choose another House" when reeveRoused(nell) and knows(actor, charter_read) once {
    Says "'Another House,' she says, tasting it. 'There is no other House. There is Dunnet, who has not been paid since Lammas and is the only man at the Hall who goes into the hill when the Mower walks, and there is me, and I am seventy-one.' She turns the rod over. 'A reeve may not choose a House. A parish may choose a man to hold the key.' She sniffs. 'It would want Mother Ysolt to say so from the font, and Hob Teller to put his name under it, and Hob Teller has a good deal to put his name under, I should think.'".
  }
  Topic dunnet_warden with dunnet "Ask Dunnet whether he would keep the wall, if the parish asked" when reeveRoused(nell) and valeTold(ysolt) and not wardenChosen(dunnet) {
    Says "Dunnet looks at his hands for a good while. 'Keep it,' he says. 'Not own it. Not sell it.' He turns the words over like a man trying a step. 'A sheaf in forty. That would be a wage, near enough, if it were all brought to the one barn.' He looks up at the hill, and for the first time the look is not afraid. 'Somebody ought to learn what the Mower knows, before it tires. I'd want Gammer Coller to show me the rod. And I'd want it said at the font, where I can be held to it.'".
    On discuss { Assert wardenChosen(dunnet). Retract serves(dunnet, venn). }
  }

  // Venn reads, or is read to. He is no thief by temper: he is a man who was given a card.
  Topic venn_lord with venn "Ask Aldous Venn about the Lord, whom he writes to every week" when not exposed(venn) and not hostile(venn, actor) once {
    Says "'Dame Isolde,' says Venn, and for once the smile does not arrive first. 'The Lord's widow. She has a house at Marlow at her sister's charge, and a suit in the Chancery of the March against her late husband's brother, who says the Hall is his.' He straightens a ledger that is already straight. 'The suit costs eleven crowns a month. The Hall brings in less. I did not sell the old metal because I thought the hill was a quarry, friend. I sold it because it was the one thing at the Hall that nobody was using.'".
  }
  Topic venn_charter with venn "Read Aldous Venn his own charter, line by line" when knows(actor, charter_read) and not exposed(venn) and not hostile(venn, actor) and not reeveRoused(nell) {
    Says "He takes the card down from under the frame, and reads it aloud, and then you read him the Latin above it. He does not interrupt. At custodia his mouth moves, and at the sheaf in forty he sits down. 'Every Michaelmas,' he says. 'Thirty years the dale has brought it to the Hall barn, and the late Lord said it was the Hall's due, and I said it was the Hall's due.' He looks at the key at his belt. 'It is a wage. We have been taking a wage for a job nobody told us we had.' He unhooks the key. 'If this goes to the Chancery, the suit is lost, and the Hall with it. And if I do not do something with it, the water takes the dale.' He hangs the key on the hook and does not look at it. 'Do what you must. I will write to Dame Isolde tonight, and tell her I have been a fool in her service.'".
    On discuss { Assert exposed(venn). Give key to actor. Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  }
  Topic venn_charter_reeve with venn "Tell Aldous Venn the reeve of the waters has read his charter" when knows(actor, charter_read) and not exposed(venn) and not hostile(venn, actor) and reeveRoused(nell) {
    Says "Venn is still reading the card when Gammer Coller comes in behind you with the rod across her arm and her good shawl on. She does not sit. 'Mr Venn,' she says. 'I am to watch the keeping. I am come to watch it.' He starts to say something about the estate, and she lifts the rod an inch, not high, and he does not say it. 'Give the key to this company,' she says. 'And give Dunnet his wages out of the sheaf in forty, which is the dale's, as I read it, and has been since the Prefect.' Venn looks from the rod to the card to the old woman, and unhooks the key with fingers that are almost steady. 'Dame Isolde will be ruined,' he says. 'Mistress Coller, she will be ruined, and she did not know.' 'No,' says Gammer Coller, not unkindly. 'None of you did.'".
    On discuss { Assert exposed(venn). Give key to actor. Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  }

  // ── The bell ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The old register's next leaf: how the parish answered the year the Long Man wept. The bronze of the dale's bell was
  // the same bronze as the wall's teeth: the Hesci's founders' pour. It was given to the Mower, and the parish bought
  // the thin bell that hangs there now with pennies.
  Discovery bell_given_before "The parish register, the leaf after the weeping: 'The Hall's men having sold the teeth, the water was stopped by the gift of the bell of the Ford, which the Keeper took in at the south door and fitted. The parish bought another with pennies, and it is not so good.' In the margin, in a later hand: 'Alys Hesk gave the word to give it.'" {
    Source register_leaf "the parish register, the leaf after the weeping" at vestry readable by party.
    Known by ysolt.
  }
  Observe bell_scene at nave when not bellGone() "By the font a bell-rope hangs up through the roof, worn pale where hands take it. The bell is not large, and its voice is thin; the sexton says it was bought by the penny.".
  Observe bell_gone_scene at nave when bellGone() "The bell-rope hangs by the font with nothing on the end of it. The sexton has tied a rag round the end, to remember where it was.".
  Topic ysolt_bell with ysolt "Ask Mother Ysolt whether the parish would give its bell again" when knows(actor, bell_given_before) and knows(actor, teeth_taken) and not state(leak_gate, mended) and not bellGone() {
    Says "Mother Ysolt does not answer at once. She looks up the rope into the dark of the roof. 'That bell was bought with the pennies of children,' she says. 'Most of Merrow's dead were christened and buried to it.' She puts her hand flat on the font. 'And another bell was given, once, by a parish that had decided what a bell was for. If I ask it of them from the font, they will say yes, and then they will not forgive me for a year.' She goes up the rope hand over hand, with a sexton's boy to hold the ladder, and the bell comes down in an hour on a hay-cart: green-bronze under the black, as heavy as a man.".
    On discuss { Assert bellGone(). Assert knows(actor, bell_gift_made). }
  }
  Discovery bell_gift_made "Mother Ysolt has had the parish bell taken down for the Mower; the bronze of it is the old pour, and will serve as the teeth did.".
  Item bell_bronze "the bell of the Chapel of the Ford" is bell_teeth at nave hidden until bell_gift_made.
  Event mower_mends_bell near party when keeps(mower, bell_bronze) and not state(leak_gate, mended) "The Mower takes the bell from you in both arms as a man takes a sleeping child, and stands a moment with its blank face bent over the green bronze. Then it turns and carries it into the hill, and you hear it ring once, a long way down, in a note a good deal deeper than the one the parish has been using; and after it something heavy closing, as it closed at the weeping: one low note that you feel in the soles of your feet." then {
    Assert state(leak_gate, mended). Assert at(mower, leak). Assert bellSpent().
  }
  Relation bellSpent().
  Rule bell_unrung when storming() and bellGone() and convinced(ysolt) and at(folk, green) and not at(folk, yard)
    says "There is no bell to ring. Mother Ysolt goes from door to door in the rain with the porch lantern and a sexton's boy, calling the houses by name, and it takes three times as long, and Merrow comes up the Hall lane in ones and twos with its feet in the water." {
    Assert at(folk, yard). Assert at(ysolt, yard).
  }

  // ── What the dale does with it, afterwards ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Each reads only what the company left in the dale. None of them is the only right ending: the dale has a wall, a
  // wage and a quarrel, and which it sorts out first is its own business.
  Observe after_warden at green when calm(long_man) and wardenChosen(dunnet) and not broke(long_man) "On the green a board has been nailed to the lime tree. It is headed THE KEEPING, and under it, in two hands, Mother Ysolt's and Gammer Coller's, the dale's sheaf in forty is entered against a name: Dunnet, warden. Hob Teller has put his name under it. Dunnet goes by the well with the reeve's rod across his shoulder and Gammer Coller three steps behind correcting how he carries it.".
  Observe after_bell at green when calm(long_man) and bellSpent() and not broke(long_man) "Nobody has hung another bell. At the hours a boy goes round the green with a pan and a spoon, and the children follow, banging, and Mother Ysolt says in a year or two the dale will find the pennies.".
  Observe after_hall_cold at yard when calm(long_man) and exposed(venn) and not wardenChosen(dunnet) "The Hall is quiet. Venn's study door stands open on a table with one long letter on it, half written, to Marlow.".

  // A fair copy of the writ, for a parish that has learnt to want one. Mother Ysolt writes it out in the vestry, in the
  // clerkly hand of her nuns, the Latin above and her own plain English below; it is hers to give or to keep.
  Place beyond_map "beyond the map" is wilderness within dale at 9, 9.
  Place nowhere "nowhere" is room within beyond_map at 0, 0.
  Item writ_copy "a fair copy of the Prefect's writ" is prefects_writ at nowhere owned by ysolt.
  Topic ysolt_copy with ysolt "Ask Mother Ysolt for a fair copy of the charter" when knows(actor, charter_read) and valeTold(ysolt) and not copied(ysolt) once {
    Says "She looks at you for a while, over the top of the register. 'It is the Hall's,' she says. 'It is also the dale's, which is what it says. I would sooner it were in two houses than one.' She takes a clean leaf from the back of the register, and ink, and writes it out in the vestry without sitting down, the Latin above and her own plain English under, line for line, in the hand the nuns gave her. When she has sanded it she folds it in three. 'Do not let anyone burn it,' she says, 'in either house.'".
    On discuss { Give writ_copy to actor. Assert copied(ysolt). }
  }
  Relation copied(group).
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/company.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Company party "Your company" of 3 at road_end.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 12. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 2.
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/dale.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "Merrowdale: a dry dale under a long straight ridge the village calls the Long Man, a lake behind it, and three days before the autumn storm.".

  // The dale, north to south: Hollow Water, the Long Man across the dale's throat, the low fields, Merrow.
  Place dale "Merrowdale" is region.
  Place hollow "Hollow Water" is wilderness within dale at 1, 0.
  Place long_man "the Long Man" is site within dale at 1, 1.
  Place fields "the low fields" is wilderness within dale at 1, 2.
  Place merrow "Merrow" is settlement within dale at 0, 2.
  Place south "the south road" is wilderness within dale at 0, 3.

  Place inn "the Drowned Ox" is building within merrow.
  Place chapel "the Chapel of the Ford" is building within merrow.
  Place mill "Teller's mill" is building within merrow.
  Place cottage "Gammer Coller's cottage" is building within merrow.
  Place hall "the Hall" is building within merrow.

  Place road_end "the end of the south road" is room within south at 0, 0.
  Place green "Merrow green" is room within merrow at 1, 2.
  Place taproom "the Drowned Ox" is room within inn at 1, 3.
  Place nave "the chapel" is room within chapel at 0, 2.
  Place vestry "the vestry" is room within chapel at 0, 3.
  Place millhouse "the millhouse" is room within mill at 2, 2.
  Place reeve_room "Gammer Coller's kitchen" is room within cottage at 0, 1.
  Place hall_floor "the Hall" is level within hall.
  Place undercroft "the Hall's undercroft" is level within hall.
  Place yard "the Hall yard" is room within merrow at 1, 0.
  Place study "the steward's study" is room within hall_floor at 0, 0.
  Place chamber "the steward's bedchamber" is room within hall_floor at 1, 0.
  Place cellar "the Hall cellar" is room within undercroft at 2, 0.
  Place race "the mill race" is room within merrow at 2, 1.
  Place low_field "the low field" is room within fields at 0, 1.
  Place springs "the Weeping Springs" is room within fields at 0, 0.
  Place landing "the mill landing" is room within fields at 1, 1.
  Place hollow_door "the Hollow Door" is room within fields at 1, 0.
  // Where people go who have left the dale: downriver on the barge.
  Place downriver "downriver" is room within south at 1, 0.

  Passage south_road "the south road" is road between road_end and green taking 30 minutes.
  Passage ox_door "the Ox's door" is door between green and taproom.
  Passage chapel_porch "the chapel porch" is doorway between green and nave.
  Passage vestry_door "the vestry door" is door between nave and vestry.
  Passage mill_lane "the mill lane" is path between green and race taking 10 minutes.
  Passage mill_door "the mill door" is door between race and millhouse.
  Passage reeve_door "Gammer Coller's door" is door between green and reeve_room.
  Passage hall_lane "the Hall lane" is road between green and yard taking 30 minutes.
  Passage study_door "the study door" is door between yard and study.
  Passage chamber_door "the bedchamber door" is door between study and chamber.
  Passage cellar_stair "the cellar stair" is stair between yard and cellar.
  Passage dyke_path "the dyke path" is path between green and low_field taking 20 minutes.
  Passage spring_path "the spring path" is path between low_field and springs taking 20 minutes.
  Passage beck_path "the beck path" is path between low_field and landing taking 20 minutes.
  Passage mill_steps "the mill steps" is steps between millhouse and landing.
  Passage wall_foot "the foot of the wall" is path between springs and hollow_door taking 20 minutes.
  Passage door_path "the beck side" is path between landing and hollow_door taking 20 minutes.

  // Who comes up the south road: a company of its own (company.kyr) when the dale is a campaign, the world's company
  // when it is a country reached across a march (placed.kyr).

  Observe road_scene at road_end when true "The south road comes up out of the willows into a dale of black, wet-smelling earth. At its head a long green ridge lies across the valley, dead straight, like a sleeper under a blanket. A village of grey stone sits below it with its back to the hill.".
  Observe green_scene at green when not drowned(green) "A green with a well and a lime tree, and grey houses with their backs to the hill. The chapel stands at the low end by the beck; the Drowned Ox faces it across the grass. Up the lane, the Hall's roofs show at the north end of the Long Man.".
  Observe green_drowned at green when drowned(green) "Brown water stands over the green to the height of a man's waist, and moves. The lime tree is full of thatch.".
  Observe taproom_scene at taproom when true "A low taproom smelling of peat and wet wool. A sign over the hearth shows an ox up to its horns in water, which the landlord says is a joke.".
  Observe nave_scene at nave when true "A plain chapel with a floor of flagstones worn into hollows. By the door stands the font: a square grey pillar, smooth as soap, notched all the way up one edge. The highest notch is level with the roof-beam.".
  Observe vestry_scene at vestry when true "A cupboard of a room that smells of candle-ends and damp wool. The parish register is chained to a shelf by a chain too long for it, so that it lies on the floor between visits like a tired dog. A basin of cold water; a surplice on a nail, mended in a thread of a different white.".
  Observe millhouse_scene at millhouse when not drowned(millhouse) "The whole millhouse shakes with the wheel, and the shake gets into your teeth. Flour hangs so thick that the lamp has a halo, and the cat asleep on the sacks is white to the whiskers.".
  Observe race_scene at race when true "The mill race runs full and loud along its stone channel to the wheel, fuller than a beck this size has any right to.".
  Observe reeve_scene at reeve_room when true "A kitchen with a peat fire and a cat, and on pegs by the door the tools of forty years of ditching: spades, a slasher, a long hook, every handle worn to the dent of one pair of hands. The room smells of wet dog and boiled onions, and the clock is eleven minutes slow and always has been.".
  Observe yard_scene at yard when true "A cobbled yard under the north end of the Long Man, where the ridge rises behind the Hall like a wall behind a house. The hill is so close that the sun leaves the yard an hour before it leaves the green. A pump with a rag tied round its handle; a mounting-block; a kennel with no dog.".
  Observe yard_smashed at yard when state(cart, smashed) "Something walked through the yard gate without opening it.".
  Observe study_scene at study when true "A steward's study: a fire banked to last the night, and a desk heaped with bills, each weighted down with a different thing from the Hall, a pestle, a horse-brass, a stone egg. The accounts stand in a row of ledgers whose spines have been re-lettered so often that the leather has gone to felt.".
  Observe chamber_scene at chamber when true "A narrow bedchamber over the yard. The grate is cold, the jug on the washstand has a crack mended with wax, and the bed-curtains are the green of a pond in October. The window looks straight up at the hill, so that whoever sleeps here wakes to it.".
  Observe cellar_scene at cellar when true "The Hall cellar is old at the back, older than the Hall: walls of smooth grey stone, fitted without mortar. Barrels stand along them, and the air at the back is colder than a cellar's should be.".
  Item bar "an iron bar" is crowbar at cellar.
  Observe bar_seen at cellar when at(bar, cellar) "An iron bar leans against the barrels, one end bright with scraped bronze.".
  Observe field_scene at low_field when not drowned(low_field) "A low field of black earth under the Long Man. The furrows hold water, and the grass is the bright green of a meadow that is turning into a bog.".
  Observe field_drowned at low_field when drowned(low_field) "The low field is under a hand's depth of water. The furrows are gone; reeds are coming up through it.".
  Observe springs_scene at springs when true "At the foot of the Long Man a row of small springs comes out of the turf, clear and very cold. They run into a ditch that runs to the mill.".
  Observe landing_scene at landing when true "A stone landing where the beck widens below the mill, with iron rings for mooring, worn bright on the downstream side only, where every rope that was ever tied here has pulled to be gone.".
  Observe hollow_door_scene at hollow_door when true "At the south end of the Long Man the beck comes out of the hill through a great round arch, smooth and pale as a tooth, glazed blue-green where the water runs. An iron grate closes it, newer than the arch by a thousand years.".
  Observe downriver_scene at downriver when true "Below the landing the beck slides away south between pollard willows, their heads cut off for firewood, toward the river and the towns.".

  // The people of Merrow, and what they want.
  Person venn "Aldous Venn" at study {
    Role "steward of the Hall". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "Aldous Venn gets up from his bills with a smile that arrives a moment before the rest of him. 'A traveller, and armed,' he says. 'You will have seen my notice.'".
    Greets again "Aldous Venn gets up from his bills with the smile arriving ahead of him again, but a little thinner at the edges. 'You have been in the dale,' he says, 'and you have been asked questions, and you have come to tell me the answers. Do sit.'".
    Objects "Venn sees {?i} in your hands, and his face changes. 'That belongs to the Hall,' he says. 'Give it here.'".
  }
  Person dunnet "Dunnet" at yard {
    Role "foreman at the Hall". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "Dunnet, a big man with a slow face, is lifting a cart-shaft that two men could manage, and sets it down gently when he sees you, as though it might wake. His eyes go past you to the hill, to see what you have brought down off it.".
    Greets again "Dunnet has put the cart-shaft down and is rubbing his palm along the grain of it, over and over. 'It has not gone away,' he says, to the wood. 'Whatever you think I saw. I would like to be wrong. I have said so to nobody.'".
    Wants bandages. Wants tin_lantern.
    Objects "Dunnet looks at {?i}, and at you, and goes in to the steward without a word. The study door bangs.".
  }
  Initially Assert serves(dunnet, venn).
  Person ysolt "Mother Ysolt" at nave {
    Role "priest of the Chapel of the Ford". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Likeness "abbess".
    Greets "Mother Ysolt closes the parish register on one finger, in the manner of a woman who has buried half the parish and christened the rest. 'You'll be after the steward's forty crowns,' she says. 'Sit down first.'".
    Greets again "Mother Ysolt has not moved from the font. 'You have been up the hill,' she says, 'or you would not stand like that. Tell me when you can say it without saying the word king.'".
    Wants keeper_mask.
  }
  Event mask_buried near ysolt when keeps(ysolt, ?face) and itemKind(?face, keeper_mask) "Mother Ysolt takes the grey face in both hands and looks at it a long time. That evening she buries it in the chapel yard with the words for the dead, and rings the bell once." then {
    Assert buried(?face).
  }
  Relation buried(item).
  Person hob "Hob Teller" at millhouse {
    Role "the miller". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Likeness "potter".
    Greets "'Mill's not grinding today,' says Hob Teller, over the noise of the wheel, and the flour settles on his shoulders as he says it. He has put himself, you notice, between you and the window that gives on the dyke path.".
    Greets again "Hob Teller says nothing, over the noise of the wheel, in a way that carries across the room. The flour has fallen on his shoulders again and he has not brushed it off.".
  }
  Person nell "Gammer Coller" at reeve_room {
    Role "the dyke-reeve". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "Gammer Coller does not get up from her chair by the fire. 'Well,' she says. 'Shut the door, or the cat will be out.' The cat, which is on her knee, has not moved since Lammas.".
    Greets again "Gammer Coller does not get up. 'Shut the door,' she says, 'or the cat will be out.' The cat is on the fender now, and has plainly made her own arrangement with the door.".
    Objects "'That is the reeve's rod,' says Gammer Coller, very quietly. 'It is not yours, and it is not mine to lose. Put it back.'".
  }
  Person martin "Martin Pask" at taproom {
    Role "landlord of the Drowned Ox". Profession innkeeper. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "'A traveller!' says Martin Pask, loud enough for half the place to hear. 'Sit, sit. Or stand. What'll it be?'".
    Greets again "Martin Pask has your drink before you have asked, and a story to go with it, and the story is about someone else's drink. 'Storm coming,' he says. 'Gammer Coller says. It is the one thing in Merrow I have ever heard her say twice.'".
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 6.
    Sells torch for 1 coin from 6.
  }
  Person folk "the people of Merrow" at green {
    Role "villagers". Ancestry human. Numbers 4. Peaceable.
  }
  Observe folk_here at green when at(folk, green) and not storming() and not dark() "A few people are at the well, and stop talking to watch you come.".
  Topic folk_long_man with folk "Ask the people at the well about the Long Man" when true once {
    Says "'The Long Man's barrow,' says a woman with a basket of eggs. 'There's a giant king under it, that the Long Folk buried with his gold. You don't go up there after dark.' She nods at the ridge. 'The Mower walks.'".
  }
  Topic folk_mower with folk "Ask the people at the well about the Mower" when true once {
    Says "'Grey,' says a boy, before anyone can stop him, 'and taller than the chapel door. It came down onto the green last week and stood looking at the springs half the night, and Hob Teller hid in his own millpond.' His mother cuffs him, not hard.".
  }
  Topic folk_venn with folk "Ask the people at the well about the steward" when true once {
    Says "They look at one another. 'Owes money downriver, they say,' says the woman with the eggs. 'The barge comes up for his old metal. He'll have put that notice up because the Mower knocked his cart about.'".
  }
  Topic martin_news with martin "Ask Martin Pask what is new in Merrow" when true once {
    Says "'Storm coming,' says Martin, wiping a pot. 'Three days, Gammer Coller says, and she's never been wrong in my life. And the Heron's due up the beck tomorrow noon for the steward's cart. Cass Rowell drinks here.' He sets the pot down. 'If you're going after the Mower, the steward's your man. I'd want paying first.'".
  }

  // The steward's notice, the steward's bronze, and the steward's key.
  Discovery bounty_known "The notice on the Ox's door, in a clerk's hand: WHOEVER LAYS THE MOWER THAT WALKS THE LONG MAN SHALL HAVE FORTY CROWNS OF THE STEWARD. A. VENN, FOR THE LORD." {
    Source notice "the steward's notice on the Ox's door" at green readable by party.
    Known by venn.
  }
  Thing cart "the cart under the tarpaulin" at yard {
    Holds.
    State covered closed "A cart stands under a tarpaulin with its shafts down, the tarpaulin roped tight.".
    State uncovered "The cart's tarpaulin is thrown back.".
    State smashed "The cart lies on its side with its wheels smashed and its tarpaulin torn.".
    Change uncover "Untie the tarpaulin on the cart" from covered to uncovered.
  }
  // The bronze is the steward's, he says, and his foreman says so first.
  Rule dunnet_sees_cart when state(cart, uncovered) and together(dunnet, party) and serves(dunnet, venn) and not noticedCart(dunnet) says "'That's the steward's,' says Dunnet, and comes over, not quickly. 'You'll want to ask him before you go in there.'" { Assert noticedCart(dunnet). }
  Relation noticedCart(group).
  Item teeth "a sack of bell-teeth" is bell_teeth in cart owned by venn.
  Thing cellar_chest "a barrel by the cellar's back wall" at cellar {
    Holds.
  }
  // The grate key is on the steward's belt by day, and on its hook by the study door while he sleeps; he lends it
  // to whoever takes his forty crowns. He sleeps after supper, in the room behind the study.
  Rule venn_retires when dark() and at(venn, study) and able(venn) { Assert at(venn, chamber). }
  Rule venn_rises when not dark() and at(venn, chamber) and able(venn) { Assert at(venn, study). }
  Thing key_hook "the hook by the study door" at study {
    Holds.
    State worn closed "The steward wears a big iron key on his belt.".
    State hung "A big iron key hangs on the hook by the study door.".
    State empty "Nothing hangs on the hook by the study door.".
  }
  Item key "the steward's iron key" is cell_key in key_hook owned by venn.
  // What a close look finds, of the things in the dale and the Hall (no try of them goes unanswered).
  Observe cart_looked near cart when tried(cart, looking) "The cart is built for more than wool: its axle would carry a millstone. Under the edge of the tarpaulin the bed is gouged pale, where something heavy and hard has been dragged in and out.".
  Observe chest_looked near cellar_chest when tried(cellar_chest, looking) "An old wine-barrel with its head set back loose. The top staves are bright where hands have been at them lately, and one is smeared with green, like the green on old bronze.".
  Observe hook_looked near key_hook when tried(key_hook, looking) "A plain iron hook by the study door, worn bright where a ring has hung from it for years.".
  Rule venn_sleeps when dark() and state(key_hook, worn) and not lends(venn, key, ?c) { Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  Rule venn_wakes when not dark() and state(key_hook, hung) and not lends(venn, key, ?c) and inside(key, key_hook) { Assert state(key_hook, worn). }
  // The hook says what hangs on it: once the key is gone, nothing does.
  Rule hook_emptied when state(key_hook, hung) and not inside(key, key_hook) { Assert state(key_hook, empty). }
  Rule hook_filled when state(key_hook, empty) and inside(key, key_hook) { Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  Discovery ledger_known "Venn's ledger: twelve bronze teeth sold to Cass Rowell of the barge Heron this year, at eight crowns the tooth, against a debt of sixty crowns, with more to come." {
    Source ledger "the steward's ledger" at study readable by party.
    Known by venn.
  }
  Discovery cellar_known "Behind a barrel in the Hall cellar, a door has been set into a hole broken through the old grey wall, into the inside of the Long Man." {
    Found by searching cellar "Behind the last barrel the old wall has been broken through, and a heavy new door set into the hole. Cold, dry air comes round its edges.".
    Found by searching gallery "Low in the gallery wall an old breach has been fitted with a heavy new door. It does not give: it is barred from the other side.".
    Known by venn, dunnet.
  }

  // Venn hides the bronze in the cellar at nightfall on the first day, and loads it onto the barge when it comes.
  Rule teeth_hidden when watch(clock) >= 60 and inside(teeth, cart) { Retract inside(teeth, cart). Assert inside(teeth, cellar_chest). }
  // Loaded, the teeth are Cass's: on her deck at the landing, hers to sell back, and gone downriver when she goes.
  Rule teeth_loaded when at(cass, landing) and inside(teeth, cellar_chest) { Retract inside(teeth, cellar_chest). Retract owns(venn, teeth). Assert at(teeth, landing). Assert aboard(teeth). }
  Relation aboard(item).
  Rule cass_wants when aboard(teeth) and at(teeth, landing) and not forSale(teeth) { Assert forSale(teeth). Assert soldBy(teeth, cass). Set price(teeth) to 12. }
  Rule teeth_sail when aboard(teeth) and at(teeth, landing) and at(cass, downriver) { Assert at(teeth, downriver). }
  // Told what the bronze held shut, Cass will not carry it: she leaves it on the landing and has the Hall's plate instead.
  Topic cass_weir with cass "Tell Cass Rowell what the bronze was holding shut" when knows(actor, wall_known) and knows(actor, teeth_taken) and aboard(teeth) {
    Says "Cass hears you out without a word, looking past you at the hill. 'My father was under a weir on the Lune when it went,' she says. 'I'll not carry one downriver in a sack.' She whistles, and one of her hands sets the sack down on the landing stones. 'The steward owes me sixty crowns. I'll have them in silver before dusk, or I'll have his plate.'".
    On discuss { Retract aboard(teeth). Retract forSale(teeth). Retract soldBy(teeth, cass). Assert dunned(venn). }
  }
  Relation dunned(group). Relation ruined(group).
  Rule venn_ruined when dunned(venn) and at(cass, downriver) and not ruined(venn) { Assert ruined(venn). }
  Observe study_stripped at study when ruined(venn) "The dresser by the fire is bare: the Hall's plate has gone downriver on the Heron.".
  // Cass drinks at the Ox for an hour while her hands load.
  Rule cass_drinks when watch(clock) >= 186 and watch(clock) < 192 and at(cass, landing) { Assert at(cass, taproom). }
  Rule cass_back when watch(clock) >= 192 and at(cass, taproom) { Assert at(cass, landing). }
  // The Ox's cellar is the lowest in Merrow but the mill's: when the low field goes under, Martin bails.
  Observe ox_bailing at taproom when drowned(low_field) and not drawn(hollow) and not broke(long_man) "Martin Pask is bailing his cellar by the bucket and swearing at the hill. 'Never in my life,' he says. 'Not once, not in a wet year.'".
  Observe cass_at_ox at taproom when at(cass, taproom) "Cass Rowell sits alone by the fire with her boots on the fender, reading a letter and moving her lips.".
  // Merrow's evenings are spent in the Ox, and its nights in its own beds.
  Rule folk_evening when dark() and untilLight(clock) > 42 and at(folk, green) and not storming() and not lostToWater(folk) { Assert at(folk, taproom). }
  Rule folk_bed when at(folk, taproom) and untilLight(clock) <= 42 { Assert at(folk, green). }
  Observe green_night at green when dark() and not drowned(green) "The green is dark. Somebody's dog barks once.".
  Observe ox_evening_first at taproom when at(folk, taproom) and watch(clock) < 144 "The taproom is full and loud. Everybody has an opinion about the steward's notice, and nobody means to go up the hill after dark to earn it.".
  Observe ox_evening_second at taproom when at(folk, taproom) and watch(clock) >= 144 and not state(leak_gate, mended) and not drawn(hollow) "The talk in the Ox is of the barge, and of the low field, where Ned Rook went in over his boots this afternoon by the springs, on ground that was dry at Lammas.".
  // Once the leak is shut or the lake is down, the low field is not the talk (the Bushweald play heard Ned Rook go in
  // over his boots the evening after the wall was mended).
  Observe ox_evening_eased at taproom when at(folk, taproom) and watch(clock) >= 144 and (state(leak_gate, mended) or drawn(hollow)) "The talk in the Ox is of the barge, and of the springs at the foot of the Long Man, which ran clear this morning for the first time since Lammas.".
  // Hob walks up to the springs at dusk with his spade, and stands looking at the water.
  Rule hob_walks when dark() and untilLight(clock) > 48 and at(hob, millhouse) and not confessed(hob) { Assert at(hob, springs). }
  Rule hob_home when at(hob, springs) and untilLight(clock) <= 48 { Assert at(hob, millhouse). }
  Observe hob_watching at springs when at(hob, springs) "Hob Teller stands at the springs in the dusk with a spade over his shoulder, looking at the water as a man looks at a debt.".


  // Dunnet hurt: an arm bound properly buys what wages would.
  Observe dunnet_sling at yard when hurt(dunnet) and at(dunnet, yard) "Dunnet sits on the mounting-block with his arm in a sling of sacking and his jaw set.".
  Event dunnet_bound near dunnet when keeps(dunnet, ?b) and itemKind(?b, bandages) and hurt(dunnet) "Dunnet lets you set the arm and bind it, and only swears once. 'The bar comes off the cellar door at dark,' he says. 'For you. Not for him.'" then {
    Retract hurt(dunnet). Assert promisedDoor(dunnet). Retract serves(dunnet, venn).
  }
  // Pell's lantern brought back: Dunnet tells it all, and then tells Mother Ysolt.
  Event pell_told near dunnet when keeps(dunnet, lantern) "Dunnet turns the lantern over and over in his hands and wipes the glass with his thumb. 'Pell's,' he says. 'The steward told them Pell went down the river in the spring. He never. The clay stood up and took him while we had the teeth out, and I ran.' He gets up. 'I'm going to tell Mother Ysolt. Then they can all know.'" then {
    Assert confessedPell(dunnet). Retract serves(dunnet, venn).
  }
  Relation confessedPell(group). Relation pellKnown().
  // He goes down to the chapel at dusk, and by morning the whole parish has it.
  Rule dunnet_to_chapel when confessedPell(dunnet) and dark() and at(dunnet, yard) { Assert at(dunnet, nave). }
  Rule pell_known when confessedPell(dunnet) and at(dunnet, nave) and not pellKnown() { Assert pellKnown(). Assert exposed(venn). }
  Observe dunnet_at_chapel at nave when at(dunnet, nave) "Dunnet sits on the bench by the font with Pell's lantern on his knees.".
  Observe pell_mourned at green when pellKnown() and at(folk, green) and not dark() "At the well they are talking low about Pell, and nobody says the steward's name, and everyone means it.".
  // Dunnet is owed his wages, and is frightened of what is behind the cellar door.
  Relation promisedDoor(group).
  Topic dunnet_fear with dunnet "Ask Dunnet about the Mower" when true once {
    Says "Dunnet looks at the hill. 'It's not the Mower I mind,' he says. 'It's what's in the wet tunnel. It stood up out of the floor at Pell and me, all mud, and came after us. I'm not going back through that door, not for the steward, not for anyone.'".
  }
  Topic dunnet_door with dunnet "Ask Dunnet what is behind the cellar door" when knows(actor, cellar_known) or state(cellar_door, barred) {
    Says "'The inside of the Long Man,' says Dunnet. 'Tunnels, dry as a church, all that grey stone. And the wheels. We had the teeth out of the big wheel in the wet tunnel, twelve of them, before the mud stood up.' He looks at his boots. 'The steward keeps it barred now.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, cellar_known). }
  }
  Action pay_dunnet(actor: group, site: place) "Give Dunnet three coin toward the wages he is owed" {
    Description "He is owed three months, and the steward will not pay.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(dunnet, site) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3
      and not promisedDoor(dunnet).
    On success {
      Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Increase quantity(dunnet, gold) by 3. Assert promisedDoor(dunnet).
      Retract serves(dunnet, venn).
    }
    Result "Dunnet counts the coins twice. 'The steward sleeps after supper,' he says, low. 'The bar comes off the cellar door at dark, and goes back on at cockcrow. That's all. I never saw you.'".
  }
  // Dunnet takes the bar off at dark and puts it back at cockcrow; a bar the company lifted itself is its own affair.
  Rule door_unbarred when promisedDoor(dunnet) and dark() and state(cellar_door, barred) { Assert state(cellar_door, unbarred). Assert dunnetsBar(cellar_door). }
  Rule door_rebarred when dunnetsBar(cellar_door) and not dark() and state(cellar_door, unbarred) and not at(party, cellar) { Assert state(cellar_door, barred). Retract dunnetsBar(cellar_door). }
  Relation dunnetsBar(entity).

  // Venn: what he says, and what he pays.
  Topic venn_bounty with venn "Ask Aldous Venn about the Mower" when not exposed(venn) and not hostile(venn, actor) {
    Says "'The Mower,' says Venn, and smiles as if it were a joke between gentlemen. 'The Long Man's ghost. It walks the crest at night and frightens the parish, and now it has taken to coming down into my yard. Forty crowns, and you may keep the mask it wears to show for it; Mother Ysolt will want to bury it.' He unhooks a big iron key from his belt and hangs it by the door. 'It lies up inside the hill by day, the men say. That key opens the grate at the Hollow Door.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bounty_known). Assert lends(venn, key, actor). Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  }
  Topic venn_bronze with venn "Ask Aldous Venn what was in the cart" when knows(actor, ledger_known) and not exposed(venn) and not hostile(venn, actor) {
    Says "Venn's smile stays where it is, but his eyes go to the ledgers. 'Old metal,' he says. 'Lumber from the Long Folk's mill under the hill. The estate has debts, and the hill is the estate's.' He spreads his hands. 'Nobody in Merrow ever had a use for it.'".
  }
  // Shown his own ledger beside what the bronze held shut, he gives up the key, and then the dale.
  Topic venn_shown with venn "Show Aldous Venn his own ledger, and tell him what the bronze held shut" when knows(actor, ledger_known) and knows(actor, teeth_taken) and not exposed(venn) {
    Says "Venn reads his own hand as if a stranger had written it. 'A sluice,' he says. 'Old metal off a sluice.' He sits down. 'Sixty crowns, and a letter from the Lord every week asking where they are.' He unhooks the iron key from his belt and hangs it by the door, and does not look at it. 'Take it. Do what you like with the hill.' When you go out he is writing, fast, to Cass Rowell.".
    On discuss { Assert exposed(venn). Assert lends(venn, key, actor). Assert state(key_hook, hung). }
  }
  Relation exposed(group).
  Rule venn_flees when exposed(venn) and at(cass, landing) and able(venn) and not at(venn, landing) and not at(venn, downriver) { Assert at(venn, landing). }
  Rule venn_sails when exposed(venn) and at(venn, landing) and at(cass, downriver) { Assert at(venn, downriver). }
  Observe venn_waits at landing when exposed(venn) and at(venn, landing) "Aldous Venn sits on the Heron's hatch with a valise on his knees, and does not look up at the hill.".
  Action claim_bounty(actor: group, carrier: member, face: item, site: place) "Show Aldous Venn {face}" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(venn, site) and memberOf(carrier, actor)
      and ownedItem(face, carrier) and itemKind(face, keeper_mask) and not paidBounty(venn).
    On success { Decrease quantity(venn, gold) by 40. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 40. Assert paidBounty(venn). }
    Result "Venn turns the grey face over in his hands, and for a moment he looks old. Then he counts out forty crowns, most of them in silver he has clearly borrowed. 'Merrow will sleep tonight,' he says.".
  }
  Relation paidBounty(group).
  Initially Set quantity(venn, gold) to 40.

  // Mother Ysolt and the font.
  Topic ysolt_mower with ysolt "Ask Mother Ysolt about the Mower" when not convinced(ysolt) {
    Says "'The Long Man is restless,' says Mother Ysolt. 'He was a king, and a cruel one; the font is his tally, a notch for every sin, and the parish has prayed him down for two hundred years. Now he walks again. Bring me his mask and I will put it in the ground with the proper words, and he will lie still.'".
  }
  Relation convinced(group).
  Topic ysolt_notches with ysolt "Tell Mother Ysolt what the notches on the font are" when knows(actor, notches_known) and not convinced(ysolt) {
    Says "Mother Ysolt stands a long time at the font with her hand flat on the stone, looking up at the highest notch and the roof-beam beside it. 'The chapel step,' she says at last. 'The register says the water came to the chapel step.' She turns. 'If it comes again, it will not stop at the step. I will ring the bell, and Merrow will go up the hill to the Hall, and the steward can say what he likes.'".
    On discuss { Assert convinced(ysolt). }
  }
  Discovery wept_known "The parish register, two hundred years back: 'In the year the Long Man wept, the water came over the low field to the chapel step. The Mower walked by day as well as night, and in seven days the water went back. The lord's men had dug into the Barrow for its gold.'" {
    Source register "the parish register" at vestry readable by party.
    Known by ysolt.
  }

  // Hob Teller and the springs.
  Topic hob_springs with hob "Ask Hob Teller about the springs" when not confessed(hob) {
    Says "'Blessed springs,' says Hob. 'My father's wheel stood still every dry summer. This one turns day and night.' He does not look toward the hill.".
  }
  Relation confessed(group).
  Topic hob_cuts with hob "Show Hob Teller the spade-cuts at the springs" when knows(actor, cuts_known) and not confessed(hob) {
    Says "Hob goes white, then red. 'It was the drought,' he says. 'A few spits with the spade, in the spring, to let them run. They've run harder every week since.' He looks at his mill, the lowest house in Merrow. 'I'll stake them and clay them over tomorrow, before light. God help me, I'll do it.'".
    On discuss { Assert confessed(hob). }
  }
  Rule hob_staunches when confessed(hob) and state(cuts, open) and untilLight(clock) == 1 { Assert state(cuts, staunched). }
  // What the springs are is not in their name: looking closely, or searching the place, finds the spade-cuts.
  Thing cuts "the spring-heads" at springs {
    State open "The springs pour out of the turf, cold and clear, more water than a few springs ought to give.".
    State staunched "The cuts at the springs have been staked and packed with clay. The water seeps instead of pouring.".
    Change staunch "Stake the spade-cuts and pack them with clay" from open to staunched needing digging or shovel after learning cuts_known.
  }
  Discovery cuts_known "Someone has cut the Weeping Springs wider with a spade, this year: the edges are still square." {
    Found by searching springs "Under the water the turf is cut in clean square bites, too regular for water to have made. A spade did this, not long ago.".
  }
  Observe cuts_looked near cuts when tried(cuts, looking) "Under the water the turf is cut in clean square bites, too regular for water to have made. A spade did this, not long ago." teaches cuts_known.

  // Gammer Coller and her rod.
  Topic nell_rhyme with nell "Ask Gammer Coller about the Mower" when true once {
    Says "'There's a rhyme,' says Gammer Coller. 'When the Mower walks the crown, keep the willow-roots cut down. When the Mower walks the green, the water's coming in between. When the Mower walks by day, Merrow, take your bed away.' She pokes the fire. 'It's been walking the green this month. Nobody asked me.'".
  }
  Topic nell_rod with nell "Ask Gammer Coller about the rod by her door" when true once {
    Says "'The dyke-reeve's rod,' she says, and takes it down: black wood, with notched bronze on both ends. 'Every reeve has had it since there were reeves. You measure a ditch with it.' She runs her thumb along the notches. 'Not that the notches match any measure I know.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, rod_seen). }
  }
  Topic nell_lend with nell "Ask Gammer Coller for the loan of her rod" when knows(actor, mower_keeps) and at(rod, reeve_room) {
    Says "She listens without a word while you tell her what the Mower does. Then she lays the rod on the table. 'I always thought it walked like a reeve,' she says. 'Bring it back.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(nell, rod, actor). }
  }
  Item rod "the dyke-reeve's rod" is sluice_rod at reeve_room hidden until rod_seen owned by nell.
  Discovery rod_seen "Gammer Coller keeps an old rod shod in notched bronze, the dyke-reeve's rod, by her door.".

  // Cass Rowell's barge, the Heron: up the beck at noon on the second day, away at dusk.
  Person cass "Cass Rowell" at downriver {
    Role "master of the barge Heron". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
    Likeness "butcher".
    Greets "Cass Rowell has her back to the bank and her eye on it, which she manages by watching it in the water of a tin cup. 'If it's passage, I'm full,' she says. 'If it's business, say it.'".
    Greets again "Cass Rowell does not turn round. 'You are back,' she says, to the tin cup. 'On any other river I would say you were following me. On this one there is only one way to go.'".
    Buys bell_teeth for 8 coin.
  }
  Person hands "the Heron's hands" at downriver {
    Role "bargemen". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Numbers 2.
  }
  Initially Assert serves(hands, cass). Initially Set quantity(cass, gold) to 60.
  Thing hold "the Heron's hold" at downriver {
    Holds.
  }
  Observe hold_looked near hold when tried(hold, looking) "The Heron's hold is open to the sky and wet underfoot. There is room in it for a good deal more than wool, and the boards are scored where something heavy was stowed and taken out again.".
  Rule cass_comes when watch(clock) >= 168 and watch(clock) < 204 and at(cass, downriver) { Assert at(cass, landing). Assert at(hands, landing). Assert at(hold, landing). }
  Rule cass_goes when watch(clock) >= 204 and at(cass, landing) and able(cass) { Assert at(cass, downriver). Assert at(hands, downriver). Assert at(hold, downriver). }
  Observe heron_scene at landing when at(cass, landing) "The barge Heron lies at the landing, low in the water, with a brown sail furled and two bargemen sitting on the hatch.".
  Topic cass_trade with cass "Ask Cass Rowell what she is carrying" when true once {
    Says "'Whatever pays,' says Cass. 'Wool down, iron up. Bronze, when the steward has it. He owes me sixty crowns and pays me in old teeth.' She looks you over. 'If you've teeth to sell, I buy at eight. If you want them back, they cost twelve. That's trade.'".
  }

  // The steward's grate, and the key that opens it.
  Thing grate "the iron grate" on culvert {
    State locked blocking "The iron grate is locked with a padlock the size of a loaf.".
    State open "The iron grate stands open on its hinges.".
    Change unlock "Unlock the grate with the steward's key" from locked to open needing key.
  }
  Observe grate_looked beside culvert as event when tried(grate, looking) "New iron in old stone, a thousand years apart. The hinges are greased, and the mud at the foot of the grate has been walked through, lately, in boots.".
  Initially Assert keyholder(venn, grate).
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/kin.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "What the company can do by what it is, and a little of what Merrow does when nobody is asking it: the ranger's drain, the priest's sermon, the reeve's rod given away, two clocks that disagree, and what two strangers' papers mean here.".

  // ── The ranger's way ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Hall keeps the grate, and the key to it, and the steward's temper with the key. A company with a ranger need
  // none of the three: the springs run into a ditch, and a ditch that has run for three hundred years has a history
  // in the grass. Nobody else in the company would look at the grass.
  Discovery drain_known "A reeve's drain, older than the Hall's grate, takes some of the springs' water down into the hill: a way into the sluice chamber that does not pass the Hollow Door.".
  Action read_the_ground(actor: group, site: place, r: member) "Walk the ditch at the springs, and read where the water goes" {
    Description "A ditch is dug by someone, for something. This one has been dug twice.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, springs) and memberOf(r, actor)
      and hasCalling(r, calling_ranger) and awake(r) and not knows(actor, drain_known).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, drain_known). }
    Result "{r} walks the spring-ditch end to end with the flat of a hand on the turf, and stops where the grass turns from bent to straight. 'Two cuts,' {r} says. 'This one is the Mower's: clean, the same width as its blade. And under it, older, laid with stone by somebody with a line.' A flag has been lifted and set back so well that you would have gone past it. Under the flag a drain goes down into the dark, dry, and wide enough for a man bent double, and the air that comes up it smells of wet iron and the inside of a bell.".
  }
  Passage reeve_drain "the reeve's old drain" is passage between springs and sluice taking 30 minutes hidden until drain_known.
  Observe drain_came at sluice when knows(party, drain_known) and not state(grate, open) "The drain comes up under the floor of the chamber through a hole no wider than a pail, and the grate over the culvert is still locked. Nobody at the Hall knows you are inside the hill.".

  // ── The priest's sermon, and what it was for ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Mother Ysolt wants the parish safe and the dead laid; she is afraid that if the king is taken from them they will
  // have nothing to be careful of; the lie is the sermon. Told what the notches measure, she does not argue.
  Relation sermonChanged(group).
  Topic ysolt_sermon with ysolt "Ask Mother Ysolt what she will preach on Sunday, now" when convinced(ysolt) and knows(actor, notches_known) and not sermonChanged(ysolt) once {
    Says "She takes a long time to answer, and does not look at the font. 'I have told them for forty years that he was a king and cruel, and that the notches were sins,' she says. 'A king can be prayed at. A frightened parish will do a great deal for a king.' She folds her hands. 'A wall can only be mended, and nobody is afraid of a wall until it is down.' She looks at last at the highest notch. 'Sunday I shall say it is a measure. They will hate it for a year, and then the children will stand against it to see how tall they are.'".
    On discuss { Assert sermonChanged(ysolt). }
  }
  Observe font_measured at nave when sermonChanged(ysolt) "A line has been chalked across the font at the height of the chapel step, and beside it, in a child's capitals, HERE. Below it a row of smaller marks, each with a name.".

  // ── The reeve's rod ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Gammer Coller wants a reeve after her; she is afraid there will not be one; her lie is that the notches on the rod
  // are a mystery she has never tried to read. Shown that the rod fits the wheel, she says she has read them for years.
  Relation rodGiven(group).
  Topic nell_last with nell "Tell Gammer Coller the rod fits a wheel in the Water-House, and ask her what it is for" when knows(actor, rod_fits) and not rodGiven(nell) {
    Says "'Fits,' says Gammer Coller. She sits very still. 'I have measured that lake at Lammas for forty years, off the lakeshore, with this, and written the figure in the back of my mother's psalter, and never once said to anyone what the figure was a figure of.' She does not look at you. 'I said I did not know what the notches measured. That was not so. I knew they measured it and I did not want to be the one who knew.' She lays the rod across your hands, and her own are not quite steady. 'Take it up there and leave it where it belongs. I am seventy-one. There is nobody after me who would know which end to hold.'".
    On discuss { Assert rodGiven(nell). Give rod to actor. }
  }

  // ── Off the road: a hum, a smell, a quarrel about the time ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe springs_hum at springs when not dark() "Standing still by the springs, you can feel the Long Man in your back teeth. A note too low to hear comes up through the soles of your feet and goes on; the water in the ditch is shivering very slightly at its edges. The cold that comes off the turf smells of a cellar that has had a bell in it.".
  Observe ox_clocks at taproom when true "Two clocks hang in the Ox: one over the hearth, which has one hand and agrees with nothing; and a slate by the door on which Martin Pask chalks, each noon, what the chapel bell has said, so that he can tell the hearth-clock how wrong it is.".
  Topic martin_clocks with martin "Ask Martin Pask about the two clocks" when true once {
    Says "'The chapel keeps a bell, and the Ox keeps a clock, and in the year of the big frost they fell out about which was the time,' says Pask, with enormous satisfaction. 'Every Lammas the parish votes to set the clock by the bell. Every Lammas it is found that the clock was set by the bell the Lammas before, and that the bell has been rung by Mother Ysolt's sexton's boy, who cannot tell the time, off the Ox's clock.' He taps the slate. 'Round and round. There is a wager on the beam. Four people in this room are owed money by a dead man.'".
  }

  // ── Papers from elsewhere ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery kin_letter_read "The Collegium of Lesser Instruments counts the instruments of a place: a letter of the Collegium, shown to Gammer Coller, makes the reeve's rod a working thing of a kind the Collegium asks after, and she is plainly more frightened by that than flattered.".
  Topic nell_letter with nell "Show Gammer Coller the letter of the Collegium of Lesser Instruments" when holding(actor, collegium_letter) once {
    Says "She holds it at arm's length, then close. 'Working things,' she reads. 'They collect them.' She looks at the rod on its pegs. 'They are welcome to write it down. They are not welcome to take it. There is a difference, and I had it from the Hall's own charter.' She gives the letter back, and straightens the rod on its pegs a quarter-inch, as if it had been looked at.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, kin_letter_read). }
  }
  Discovery kin_surety_read "A surety answers for the keeping named, and where none is named, for all: shown the Ninth Valuer's note, Mother Ysolt thinks of the bell the parish gave as a surety, and of who was never asked to give it back.".
  Topic ysolt_surety with ysolt "Show Mother Ysolt the Ninth Valuer's note on a surety" when holding(actor, surety_terms) once {
    Says "'A surety.' Mother Ysolt reads the strip twice. 'Answers for the keeping named, and where none is named, for all.' She sets it on the register. 'The year the water wept, this parish gave its bell to the Keeper on those terms, I think, though nobody wrote them. We named no keeping. So we answered for all of it.' She almost laughs. 'And now a man with the bell-teeth in his cellar thinks the account is his to close.' She gives it back, carefully, by the edge, and for a moment the register in front of her seems heavier than it was.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, kin_surety_read). }
  }
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/lore.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "Links outward from Merrowdale: news from the south that has come up the drove roads, a rubbing of a keeper's bench brought to the chapel, and the almanack woman, passing through.".

  // ── World events, read: what the carters say at the Drowned Ox ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe lore_ox_south at taproom when befell(slack_opened) "Martin Pask has a new subject, which he is giving to the whole room, and it is not sheep. 'A black square,' he says, 'in the floor of a college, and a stair under it. And the college did not open it, mark you, a company did. And now every mason from here to the coast says he always knew.' Somebody asks him what a mason would know. 'That's what I asked,' says Pask. 'They said: where the stone is not the same stone.' He drinks. 'I told them we have a wall like that up the dale, and they were very polite.'".
  Observe lore_ox_ship at taproom when befell(remainder_harboured) "The talk at the Drowned Ox has moved from the Long Man to a ship. 'Out of a cellar,' a drover is saying, 'and her people came ashore in the wrong clothes, and some old fellow gave them a bed in his own house.' Hob Teller's cousin, who has come over from the mill for the beer, says he would not give a bed to anyone who had not asked for one. The drover says that is exactly what the old fellow said.".

  // ── A visitor from elsewhere: a keeper's bench in wax ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_rubbing_notches "A wax rubbing of a keeper's bench, brought from a church by the sea, has the same count as the notches in the keeper's niche under the Long Man: eleven, and a space where a twelfth would go.".
  Topic lore_ysolt_rubbing with ysolt "Show Mother Ysolt the wax rubbing of a keeper's bench" when holding(actor, tally_rubbing) once {
    Says "Mother Ysolt takes the wax in both hands, and for a time she does not look at it; she looks at you. 'From a church, you said? By the sea?' She carries it to the chapel window. 'Three notations. A hand I cannot read. A hand that counted like a customs house. And these.' Her thumb finds the last rows, a stroke and a ring. 'This is the way Hob's grandmother counted sheep. I did not know it was a way. I thought it was a family.' She gives it back with great care. 'I will say what I told the steward when he asked what the niche was for. A bench is for sitting. A tally is for the one who sits after.' She looks at the wall of the chapel, towards the hill, as if it might answer, and then at the rubbing, and then back at you.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_rubbing_notches). }
  }

  // ── The almanack woman ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_cattermole_merrow "Jessamy Cattermole, the almanack woman, came through Merrowdale from the Bowl of Ammerlin and has gone south for the Season at Hessel, where, Martin Pask says, they buy anything with a date in it.".
  Topic lore_pask_cattermole with martin "Ask Martin Pask whether any pedlars come up the dale" when true once {
    Says "'One,' says Pask. 'Cattermole. A woman with an almanack for every year there ever was and a different one for each town.' He pours. 'She was here a month ago on her way down from a place in the north called the Bowl. She told me the steward's notice had been put up in the Bowl's market, and read it aloud to a man who laughed and paid her twopence to see the original. I told her there was no giant. She said that was a pity, there was a season in a giant.' He shakes his head. 'Off down the drove road to Hessel, for the Season. She said they will buy anything with a date in it. They would not buy mine. Mine says it is a hundred and seventy years later than hers.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_cattermole_merrow). }
  }
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/merrow.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "Merrow's talk as the three days go on: what the well says when the low field goes under, what is said of Pell once it is known, the miller's grandmother, and where the bronze goes when the Heron leaves.".

  // ── The well, as the water rises ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The people at the well have one thing to say on the first day (the giant, the Mower, the steward). They have
  // other things to say by the third, and they say them differently: nobody tells a joke about the hill once the
  // low field is under.
  Topic folk_water with folk "Ask the people at the well about the low field" when drowned(low_field) and not broke(long_man) once {
    Says "'It was a furrow yesterday,' says the woman with the eggs, and looks at her own boots, which are dry. 'Ned Rook went in over his boots by the springs on ground that was dry at Lammas, and Ned has never been afraid of a puddle in his life.' Behind her a man says the Gammer's rhyme under his breath, the second verse, and then, because it is the second verse, stops.".
  }
  Topic folk_pell with folk "Ask the people at the well about Pell" when pellKnown() once {
    Says "'Pell,' says the woman with the eggs, and stops, and begins again. 'We were told he went down the river in the spring. His mother kept his boots by the door till Michaelmas.' Nobody says the steward's name. A boy is sent off to the yard with a loaf for Dunnet, and carries it as if it were something else.".
  }
  Topic folk_eased with folk "Ask the people at the well how the springs are running" when (state(leak_gate, mended) or drawn(hollow)) and not broke(long_man) once {
    Says "'Clear,' says the boy who told you about the Mower, and then, before his mother can cuff him: 'Not like before. Before they were loud.' The woman with the eggs says she has lived beside those springs all her life and never once listened to them, and now she cannot stop.".
  }

  // ── The miller, and his grandmother's sheep ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The wax rubbing from the sea-church has a hand the chapel cannot read; the miller's family can, and does not know
  // that it can. (Told in Mother Ysolt's version at the chapel; this is the other end of the same thread.)
  Topic hob_grandmother with hob "Show Hob Teller the stroke-and-ring on the wax rubbing" when knows(actor, lore_rubbing_notches) once {
    Says "Hob holds the wax to the window with a floury thumb and a forefinger, the way you hold a coin you suspect. 'That's sheep,' he says. 'That's how my gran counted sheep: a stroke each, and a ring when you'd done a score. She'd do it on the gate with a nail.' He turns it over, and his voice has gone a little hoarse. 'She said she had it from her gran. I thought everyone did.' He gives it back as if it had got heavier. 'Don't say that to Ysolt. She'll make a sermon of it.'".
  }
  Topic hob_after with hob "Ask Hob Teller how the mill is running" when confessed(hob) once {
    Says "'Slower,' says Hob, and for the first time since you met him it sounds like a boast. 'Ran dry every August till I put the spade to the springs, and I told myself the Lord had meant it for the mill. He hadn't.' He wipes his hands. 'I have staked what I cut. I'll not stake what I never cut, and there's a hundred other springs in that dale that were doing it long before me.' He does not say what he means by that. He looks at the hill.".
  }

  // ── Where the Heron goes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The dale knows the barge only as the Heron; the country below knows what the bronze is sold to. A rumour that
  // leaves the dale, and does not say what it is: there is a buyer on the coast road who pays by the pound.
  Discovery heron_road "The Heron goes down the beck to the river, and the river to the coast road, where a Founders' Exchange factor pays by the pound for old bronze and signs a receipt that is worse than none.".
  Topic martin_heron with martin "Ask Martin Pask where the Heron goes when it leaves Merrow" when true once {
    Says "'Down,' says Pask. 'Down the beck to the river, down the river to where it meets the coast road, and there's a hall there that buys what the steward sells. The Founders' Exchange, they call it, which I took for a chapel till Cass told me.' He wipes the bar slowly. 'They pay by the pound for green bronze and old bells and ask no questions, and they give you a receipt, which is a good deal worse than none, because it has your name on.' He puts the cloth down. 'She says they are very fond of the Hall's metal. I'd like to know what they want it for. I have never been asked to sell them anything.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, heron_road). }
  }
  Topic cass_receipt with cass "Ask Cass Rowell about the receipts the Exchange gives" when knows(actor, heron_road) once {
    Says "Cass turns her cup a quarter-turn on the hatch. 'Numbered,' she says. 'On thick paper, with a seal like two hands shaking. You'd think it a courtesy.' She looks at the sack of teeth, or the place where it was. 'I asked a clerk once what number I was. He said I was the thirty-first. He said it in the voice of a man who had been told not to say.' She drinks. 'That's every bargeman from here to the sea, with a number. I've never wanted to ask what they do with the numbers.'".
  }

  // ── Mother Ysolt, once the steward is exposed ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic ysolt_letter with ysolt "Ask Mother Ysolt what she will do about the steward" when exposed(venn) once {
    Says "'Write,' says Mother Ysolt. 'I have written to the bishop's registry in the cathedral town every Michaelmas for twenty years about the state of the chapel roof, and had no answer.' She smooths the register under her hand. 'This once, I think, there will be an answer. A steward who sells a parish's bell is a thing a bishop notices.' She is almost smiling. 'I shall write it on the thick paper. They do read the thick paper.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/placed.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  // The dale as a country beyond a march: the company that comes up the south road is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  // What the country below says of the dale (its innkeepers' rumour of the forty crowns): once Merrow is safe from its
  // wall, it is old news there, and they say so to whoever comes back down the north road.
  Entity word: fact "What is said of Merrowdale in the country below.".
  Rule word_old when (state(leak_gate, mended) or drawn(hollow) or (broke(long_man) and calm(long_man) and not lostToWater(folk))) and not stale(word) { Assert stale(word). }
  // The factor of the Founders' Exchange in the country below, when the world holds one (the herald on the roads to
  // this dale): bell-teeth that go downriver on the barge are sold to her, and become hers to hold and send. The dale
  // does not write what she does with them. Standing alone, the dale has no such factor, and the barge carries them
  // off as it always has.
  Entity factor: group "The factor who buys old bronze in the country below.".
  Rule teeth_to_factor when aboard(teeth) and at(teeth, downriver) and not consigned(teeth) says "Cass Rowell touches her cap to the landing as the Heron goes out of sight round the first bend, with the sack of bronze under the tarpaulin forward, bound for whoever pays by the pound." {
    Retract at(teeth, downriver). Retract aboard(teeth). Assert consigned(teeth). Assert keeps(factor, teeth).
  }
  Relation consigned(item).
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/trimmer.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "A lamp-trimmer who keeps the ford lamp in the Chapel of the Ford, which is lit for no one living, and what he has heard on the roads about other lamps like it.".

  // ── Osmund Wethered, who trims the ford lamp ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The lamp hangs by the font and has been lit every dusk since the winter the ford took the carriers. Nobody in the
  // dale is left who crossed with them. He wants to be told whom it is for; he fears it is for nobody and that, if he
  // were to stop, nothing would happen; the lie he tells himself is that he does it for the oil-money. In two beats:
  // the gossip, and (told what the notches count) a second wick that he trims for no reason he will give.
  Person wethered "Osmund Wethered" at nave {
    Role "the lamp-trimmer of the Chapel of the Ford, who comes in at dusk with a pair of snuffers and a can". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "A bent man in a leather apron is on a stool by the font with a lamp in his lap, taking the char off its wick with a small pair of brass scissors. He does not stop. 'There is a charge for the oil,' says Osmund Wethered. 'There is no charge for the looking. Do not stand in the light.'".
    Greets again "Osmund Wethered holds the wick up to the window, squints, and lets it down again. 'Not yet,' he says. 'It is never yet.'".
    Sells lamp_oil for 1 coin from 4.
  }
  Relation wethereldTold(group). Relation twoWicks(group).
  Discovery wethered_gossip "Osmund Wethered, the lamp-trimmer, gets his wicks from a chandler's loft at Skeel by the coast carriers, and has a brother's tale of a lamp on the rock at Skerrow that is lit for no one living either, by men who do not say why.".
  Observe wethered_lamp at nave when not twoWicks(party) "By the font a small lamp hangs from a bracket in the wall, with a glass black on the weather side and clean on the other. It is lit. Under it, on a ledge worn smooth, a can, a pair of scissors and a stub of candle.".
  Observe wethered_lamp_two at nave when twoWicks(party) "By the font the small lamp burns with two flames, not one, side by side in the same dish, and the glass is clean all round. Under it, on the worn ledge, there is a second pair of scissors, newer than the first.".

  Topic wethered_lamp_ask with wethered "Ask Osmund Wethered whom the lamp by the font is lit for" when true once {
    Says "'Ask the parish,' he says, 'and it will tell you the carriers who drowned at the ford, the winter of the hard frost, eleven of them, and a boy.' The scissors do not stop. 'Ask the register, and it says nothing. Ask my mother, who had the trimming before me, and she said do not ask. I have asked everyone who comes through. Pedlars. Carters.' He lays the wick straight. 'A chandler's man from Skeel, once, came up with the wicks, a great river of rope-walk grey in his bag, and he said there was a lantern on the Holm at Skeel kept by a lass who took the log of an empty sea, and that she had asked the same, and written it down, and had no better. And my brother, God keep him, went to be lamp-boy on a rock off the south, Skerrow, where the Pharos is, and he sent a letter once that said they lit it there for the same reason. Nobody living. No one will say who.' He sniffs. 'It is a good business, lamps. Nobody asks for their money back.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, wethered_gossip). Assert wethereldTold(wethered). }
  }
  Topic wethered_notches with wethered "Tell Osmund Wethered what the notches under the Long Man count" when knows(actor, wethered_gossip) and knows(actor, notches_known) and not twoWicks(party) once {
    Says "He puts down the scissors for the first time. 'Eleven,' he says. 'And a space.' He looks at the lamp, and at the font beneath it, and the high-water mark on the wall that somebody kept level with the roof-beam. 'I have trimmed this thing forty winters,' he says, 'and I had it in my head that it was for the dead. For the drowned.' He is quiet. 'It has eleven drowned and a boy. Twelve.' He gets up, with his hand on the font, and takes a second stub of wick out of his apron, and lays it in the dish beside the first without asking you or anyone. 'The twelfth is not lost,' he says. 'Somebody knows where the twelfth is. Light it for him until he does.' He does not thank you. He goes back to the stool and begins on the second wick, as if it had always been there, and does not look up for the rest of the hour.".
    On discuss { Assert twoWicks(party). }
  }
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/voices.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "What each member of the company makes of the dale, by what they are: the cleric at the font, the ranger on the crest, the warrior at the cart, the thief at the door.".

  // The preset party is not a set of declared people, so it has no Remarks of its own. What a rule can ask of a member
  // is their calling, and print their name. Said once for the company, by whoever it has of the calling; a company
  // without a ranger has nobody to notice the cut saplings, and must notice them itself.
  Relation heardFont(group). Relation heardCrest(group). Relation heardCart(group). Relation heardDoor(group).
  Relation heardOx(group). Relation heardWheel(group).
  Relation quarrelled(group).

  Rule voice_font at nave when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, nave) and not heardFont(party)
    says "{?m} lays a hand flat on the font and keeps it there. 'Nobody tallies sins on a floor,' {?m} says, low. 'A tally has no use for a floor. This one has a high-water mark that somebody kept level with the roof-beam.'" {
    Assert heardFont(party).
  }
  Rule voice_crest at crest when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and awake(?m) and at(party, crest) and not heardCrest(party)
    says "{?m} goes down on one knee by a stump and runs a finger across the cut. 'Same height, same angle, every one, all the way along,' {?m} says. 'That is not a man's hook, and it is not a deer. It is a thing with a very long reach and no hurry at all.'" {
    Assert heardCrest(party).
  }
  Rule voice_cart at yard when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_warrior) and awake(?m) and at(party, yard) and state(cart, covered) and not heardCart(party)
    says "{?m} walks round the cart once, looking at the axle and the gouged bed. 'That is not wool,' {?m} says. 'Something that weighs more than a man has been dragged in and out of there, and somebody has been at pains to hang a tarpaulin over the marks. Ask the foreman about his arm before you ask anyone about the hill.'" {
    Assert heardCart(party).
  }
  Rule voice_door at cellar when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, cellar) and not heardDoor(party)
    says "{?m} runs a thumb round the hinge of the new door in the old wall. 'Greased this week,' {?m} says. 'Somebody goes in and out of here, and not to roll barrels.'" {
    Assert heardDoor(party).
  }
  Rule voice_ox at taproom when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, taproom) and not heardOx(party)
    says "{?m} sits a while with an ear turned to the room. 'Everyone has a different story of the Mower and the same one of the steward,' {?m} says at last. 'When a village agrees about a man and not about a ghost, I know which one it has seen.'" {
    Assert heardOx(party).
  }
  Rule voice_wheel at sluice when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_mage) and awake(?m) and at(party, sluice) and not heardWheel(party)
    says "{?m} stands with a palm held an inch from the nearest tooth of green bronze. 'No working in it,' {?m} says, puzzled. 'Nothing I could name. It does not do a thing. It counts, and the counting does the thing.'" {
    Assert heardWheel(party).
  }

  // A disagreement the company has with itself: only a company with both a warrior and a cleric has it, and each is right.
  // The money is forty crowns; the Hall owes the warrior's trade nothing; the cleric has seen the font.
  Rule quarrel_over_bounty at green when memberOf(?w, party) and hasCalling(?w, calling_warrior) and awake(?w)
    and memberOf(?c, party) and hasCalling(?c, calling_cleric) and awake(?c) and at(party, green) and knows(party, bounty_known) and knows(party, notches_known)
    and not paidBounty(venn) and not quarrelled(party)
    says "{?w} says it first, because somebody must. 'Forty crowns is forty crowns. It walks the crest at night and it has hit a man; lay it and be paid.' {?c} does not raise a voice. 'It keeps the wall that keeps the lake that keeps the chapel dry,' says {?c}. 'I would like to be certain what it is before I put a bar under its chin.' Neither looks at you, and both are waiting for you to say which of them is right." {
    Assert quarrelled(party).
  }

  // Taking a side is a choice with a cost: the warrior's way buys a man, the cleric's way wakes a priest, and neither
  // does the other's work. One answer closes the other.
  Relation sidedWarrior(group). Relation sidedCleric(group).
  Action side_warrior(actor: group, site: place, w: member, c: member) "Tell {c} that {w} is right about the forty crowns, and go to the foreman" {
    Description "Forty crowns and a man at the Hall who will not be paid. {w} will go in with the first of the money.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, green) and quarrelled(party) and not sidedWarrior(party) and not sidedCleric(party)
      and memberOf(w, actor) and hasCalling(w, calling_warrior) and memberOf(c, actor) and hasCalling(c, calling_cleric) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3.
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert sidedWarrior(party). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Increase quantity(dunnet, gold) by 3. Assert promisedDoor(dunnet). Retract serves(dunnet, venn). }
    Result "{c} says nothing, and goes on saying nothing all the way up the Hall lane. {w} finds Dunnet in the yard and puts three coin in his hand without a word of explanation, as a man pays a debt to his own trade. Dunnet counts them twice. 'The bar comes off the cellar door at dark,' he says, low. 'For you.' Behind you {c} has stopped at the gate and is looking at the hill with an expression you will remember at the wrong moment.".
  }
  Action side_cleric(actor: group, site: place, w: member, c: member) "Tell {w} that {c} is right, and take the font to Mother Ysolt" {
    Description "{c} will say what the notches are, in the chapel, before the parish; {w} will hold the door.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, green) and quarrelled(party) and not sidedWarrior(party) and not sidedCleric(party)
      and memberOf(w, actor) and hasCalling(w, calling_warrior) and memberOf(c, actor) and hasCalling(c, calling_cleric) and knows(actor, notches_known).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert sidedCleric(party). Assert convinced(ysolt). }
    Result "{w} says nothing against it, which is not the same as agreeing, and stands at the chapel door with arms folded while {c} puts a hand on the font and says what the notches are, in the plain voice of someone who has done it before. Mother Ysolt listens to the end. When {c} has finished she looks up at the roof-beam, and then at {w}, and says: 'Ring the bell, if it comes. I will see it rung.' {w} unfolds arms. 'Forty crowns,' {w} says, to the doorpost, and goes out to see to the weather.".
  }
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/wall.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "The Long Man: the crest a figure walks at night, and the grey galleries inside the hill.".

  Place inside "the galleries" is level within long_man.
  Place crest "the crest of the Long Man" is room within long_man at 1, 0.
  Place gauge_head "the gauge stone" is room within long_man at 2, 0.
  Place gallery "the grey gallery" is room within inside at 1, 1.
  Place sluice "the sluice chamber" is room within inside at 2, 2.
  Place rest "the keeper's niche" is room within inside at 0, 1.
  Place leak "the wet gallery" is room within inside at 1, 2.
  Place shaft_foot "the foot of the gauge shaft" is room within inside at 2, 1.
  // The clay core, where what the leak made of the clay goes when the leak is shut.
  Place core "the clay core" is room within inside at 0, 2.
  Initially Assert unlit(gallery). Initially Assert unlit(sluice). Initially Assert unlit(rest). Initially Assert unlit(leak).
  Initially Assert unlit(shaft_foot).

  Passage crest_steps "the steps up the Long Man" is steps between yard and crest taking 20 minutes.
  Passage valley_face "the valley face" is path between crest and springs taking 20 minutes.
  Passage crest_walk "the crest" is path between crest and gauge_head taking 10 minutes.
  Passage culvert "the culvert" is culvert between hollow_door and sluice taking 10 minutes.
  Passage broken_wall "the broken wall" is doorway between cellar and gallery hidden until cellar_known.
  Passage sluice_way "the sluice passage" is passage between gallery and sluice.
  Passage niche_way "the keeper's passage" is passage between gallery and rest.
  Passage wet_way "the wet passage" is passage between gallery and leak.
  Passage shaft_way "the shaft passage" is passage between gallery and shaft_foot.
  Passage gauge_shaft "the gauge shaft" is shaft between shaft_foot and gauge_head taking 30 minutes needing climbing or rope.
  Passage sinkhole "the sinkhole" is climb between crest and leak taking 20 minutes needing rope.

  // The bar is on the cellar side: only someone in the cellar can lift it.
  Thing cellar_door "the door in the broken wall" on broken_wall {
    State barred blocking "A heavy door closes the hole broken through the wall, barred on the cellar side.".
    State unbarred "The bar is off the door in the broken wall, and it stands a hand's width open on the dark.".
    Change lift "Lift the oak bar off the door in the broken wall" from barred to unbarred at cellar.
  }
  Observe door_looked beside broken_wall as event when tried(cellar_door, looking) "New planks, hung in a hole knocked through grey stone that was never meant to be broken: the stone is cracked for a yard round the hole, the way ice cracks.".
  Initially Assert keyholder(venn, cellar_door).
  // Shut in behind a barred door, a company can always make itself heard: at a price.
  Action hammer_door(actor: group, site: place) "Hammer on the door until someone in the cellar hears" {
    Description "Somebody will come in the end. Everybody at the Hall will know who it was.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, gallery) and state(cellar_door, barred)
      and knows(actor, cellar_known).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert state(cellar_door, unbarred). Assert hostile(venn, actor). }
    Result "You hammer on the oak until your hands ache. At last the bar scrapes off its brackets, and Dunnet's face looks in at you, white. 'The steward will hear of this,' he says, and he is right.".
  }

  Observe crest_scene at crest when not dark() "The crest of the Long Man is a dead-level walk of turf, wide as a lane. On one hand the dale falls away to Merrow's roofs; on the other, a long way down, lies Hollow Water, black and still, filling the valley to the hills. Nothing grows on the crest higher than a hand: every sapling has been cut off at the root, clean.".
  Observe crest_night at crest when dark() "By night the crest is a pale road between two darks: the dale's, with a few lights in it, and the lake's, with none.".
  Observe sinkhole_scene at crest when true "Halfway along, the turf has fallen into a raw hole a cart wide. Water drips somewhere far down in it.".
  Observe gauge_scene at gauge_head when true "At the north end of the crest a square grey stone stands over a square shaft going down into the hill. Notches are cut down every edge of the shaft, deeper than the light goes.".
  Observe gallery_scene at gallery when true "A tunnel lined with smooth grey stone, tall and narrow, as if cut for something taller than a man. The air is dry and still. Ways go off to either hand.".
  Observe sluice_scene at sluice when true "A chamber over the culvert, where the beck runs loud below an iron grating. Two great wheels, pale as old tallow, stand on their edges, set round with teeth of green bronze, and a third, smaller, works the shutter of the bottom sluice.".
  Observe rest_scene at rest when true "A niche in the gallery wall, taller than two men, with a ledge at the back and tools laid on it in order: blades, hooks, a stone trowel, each lying exactly where a hand would put it down. Notches run in close rows up the walls.".
  Observe leak_scene at leak when not state(leak_gate, mended) "Water comes through a crack in the inner face of the gallery, a sheet of it, and runs away under the floor.".
  Observe leak_mended at leak when state(leak_gate, mended) "The wall of the gallery is wet, and no more.".
  Observe shaft_scene at shaft_foot when true "The bottom of a square shaft. Notches climb its four edges up into the dark, and the stone of the shaft-side toward the lake sweats.".

  // The Mower: it stands in its niche by day and walks the crest by night, and goes after its bronze.
  Person mower "the Mower" at rest {
    Role "the tall grey figure that walks the Long Man". Species automaton. Level 12.
    Wants bell_teeth.
  }
  Rule mower_rises when dark() and at(mower, rest) and able(mower) and not hunting(mower) { Assert at(mower, crest). }
  Rule mower_returns when not dark() and not at(mower, rest) and able(mower) { Assert at(mower, rest). Retract hunting(mower). }
  Relation hunting(group).
  // At midnight on the first night it comes down for the bronze that was in the cart, and finds the cart empty.
  Rule mower_hunts at yard when dark() and watch(clock) >= 96 and watch(clock) < 132 and state(cart, covered) and able(mower)
    says "Something tall comes over the yard wall without climbing it. The Mower goes to the cart, tears the tarpaulin away, finds nothing, and turns the cart over as if it were a barrow. A shaft flies. Dunnet, who came out with a lantern, goes down with a cry." {
    Assert state(cart, smashed). Assert hunting(mower). Assert at(mower, yard). Assert hurt(dunnet).
  }
  Relation hurt(group).
  Observe mower_crest at crest when dark() and at(mower, crest) "The Mower walks the crest, slowly, the length of it and back. Every few paces it stoops, and a long blade flicks, and something small falls." teaches mower_keeps.
  Observe count_matched at rest when knows(party, last_count) "The last row of notches on the niche wall is a count of days, and it stops at forty-one.".
  Observe mower_resting at rest when at(mower, rest) and able(mower) "The Mower stands in its niche: a figure taller than two men, grey and too smooth, with its long arms at its sides and a face like a blank mask. It does not move. On its breastplate, in the light, a row of notches." .
  Observe mower_yard at yard when at(mower, yard) "The Mower stands in the yard by the overturned cart, its blank face turned toward the cellar." .
  Discovery keeper_named "The notches on the Mower's breastplate, read: KEEPER OF THE WALL." {
    Found by searching rest with lore "The notches on the Mower's breastplate are writing, the same writing as on the walls. It says, as near as it can be read: KEEPER OF THE WALL.".
  }
  Discovery mower_keeps "The Mower keeps the Long Man: it cuts every sapling on the crest before its roots can crack the wall, and it goes after bronze taken from its wheels.".
  // Given back its bronze, it fits the teeth to the leak gate's wheel that night, and closes the gate. The company
  // that gave them sees it go into the hill (near the company, since it is the Mower that goes).
  Event mower_mends near party when keeps(mower, teeth) and not state(leak_gate, mended) "The Mower takes the sack of teeth in both hands, turns, and walks away into the hill. Some time later, deep inside the Long Man, something heavy closes, and the note comes up through the dale, and every dog in Merrow lifts its head." then {
    Assert state(leak_gate, mended). Assert at(mower, leak).
  }
  Item mask "the Mower's mask" is keeper_mask at core.
  Rule mower_falls when dead(mower) and at(mower, ?p) and at(mask, core) { Assert at(mask, ?p). }
  // By day it stands still in its niche, and its face is a mask that a bar can lever off. That lays it, as Venn wants
  // and Ysolt prays for; and then nobody keeps the wall.
  Hazard unmasking "The mask levered off" means "Kill ally.".
  Action unmask_mower(actor: group, site: place) "Get the bar under the Mower's face and lever it off" {
    Description "By day it does not move. Whatever it is, its face is a mask, and a mask comes off.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(mower, site) and at(mower, rest) and able(mower)
      and not dark() and holding(actor, crowbar) and not benighted(actor).
    On success { Assert strikes(unmasking, mower). Retract at(mask, core). Assert at(mask, rest). }
    Result "The bar goes in under the grey chin, and you lean on it. The mask comes away with a sound like a cracked bell, and the Mower folds down onto its ledge like a dropped coat, and is still.".
  }

  // The leak gate, and what the leak has made of the clay.
  Thing leak_gate "the bronze shutter" at leak {
    State jammed "A shutter of bronze teeth hangs half across the crack, on a wheel with twelve empty sockets.".
    State fitted "The bronze teeth are back in the shutter's wheel; it hangs open, ready to be turned.".
    State mended "The bronze shutter is closed across the crack, every socket of its wheel filled.".
    Change heave "Heave the shutter's wheel round and close it" from fitted to mended needing brawn.
  }
  Observe shutter_looked near leak_gate when tried(leak_gate, looking) and state(leak_gate, jammed) "Each of the twelve sockets is shaped for one of the bell-teeth, and each is bright at its edges where a bar went in and levered the tooth out. Water beads along the crack behind the shutter and runs down into the clay.".
  Observe shutter_seen near leak_gate when tried(leak_gate, looking) and not state(leak_gate, jammed) "Bronze, green with age, on a wheel of twelve sockets; behind it, the crack in the clay core, darker than the clay round it.".
  Action fit_teeth(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Fit the bell-teeth back into the shutter's wheel" {
    Description "Twelve sockets, twelve teeth. Each seats a little lower in pitch than the one before.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(leak_gate, site) and state(leak_gate, jammed)
      and memberOf(carrier, actor) and awake(carrier) and ownedItem(teeth, carrier).
    Time 6.
    Resolve drop(teeth, carrier).
    On success { Assert at(teeth, core). Assert state(leak_gate, fitted). }
    Result "One by one the teeth go into their sockets, and each one rings as it seats. When the twelfth is in, the wheel turns a finger's width under your hand.".
  }
  Person wet "the Wet" at leak {
    Role "a heaving mass of wet clay". Species slump. Level 5.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "At the far end of the wet gallery the floor heaves, and a shape stands up out of the clay, streaming, as tall as a door.".
    Comes "The Wet comes down the gallery at you, faster than mud should.".
  }
  // What the Wet took: the man who went in with Dunnet for the teeth.
  Item lantern "a miner's lantern" is tin_lantern at leak.
  Observe pell_seen at leak when at(lantern, leak) "At the far end of the gallery, half sunk in the clay, a man's lantern lies on its side, its glass packed with mud.".
  Rule wet_slumps at leak when state(leak_gate, mended) and at(wet, leak) says "The Wet sags, and sags, and is a heap of clay on the floor, and then is only floor." { Assert at(wet, core). }

  // The sluice: the bottom gate under the chamber. Opened, it fills the culvert and runs the beck high.
  Thing bottom_sluice "the bottom sluice" at sluice {
    State shut "The small wheel is turned home; the bottom sluice is shut.".
    State open dangerous "The small wheel is turned out, and below the grating the water roars.".
    Change open_it "Turn the small wheel and open the bottom sluice" from shut to open needing brawn.
    Change shut_it "Turn the small wheel home and shut the bottom sluice" from open to shut needing brawn.
  }
  Observe sluice_looked near bottom_sluice when tried(bottom_sluice, looking) "A shutter of grey stone in a groove, worked by the small wheel. The groove is worn as smooth as the font: it has gone up and down ten thousand times, and the last time not long ago.".
  Thing culvert_water "the water in the culvert" on culvert is scenery {
    State low "The beck runs ankle-deep along the culvert floor.".
    State high blocking dangerous "The culvert is full to the roof with fast brown water.".
  }
  Rule culvert_fills when state(bottom_sluice, open) and state(culvert_water, low) says "Somewhere below, the water changes its voice." { Assert state(culvert_water, high). }
  Rule culvert_drains when state(bottom_sluice, shut) and state(culvert_water, high) { Assert state(culvert_water, low). }
  Rule mower_guards_sluice when state(bottom_sluice, open) and together(mower, party) and able(mower) says "The Mower turns its blank face toward the open sluice, and then toward you." { Assert assails(mower, party). }

  // The gauge shaft and its notches.
  Discovery notches_known "The notches on the font are water heights, like the notches down the gauge shaft: the same cuts, the same spacing. The highest notch on the font is level with the chapel's roof-beam." {
    Source shaft_notches "the notches down the gauge shaft" at shaft_foot readable by party.
  }
  Discovery wall_known "The Long Man is a wall: it holds Hollow Water back from the dale, and the beck comes through it by a culvert.".
  // What the Long Man is, come to at last: told as a revelation, set apart from the run of the page (NAR-14).
  Observe sluice_teaches at sluice as revelation when true "Above the grating the wheels and the culvert make plain what the Long Man is: not a barrow, a wall, with a lake behind it and a sluice through it." teaches wall_known.
  Observe teeth_missing at leak when not state(leak_gate, mended) "Fresh bright scars on the stone by the crack show where a bar has been used, and lately." teaches teeth_taken.
  Discovery teeth_taken "Twelve bronze teeth have been prised out of the wheel of the shutter that should close the leak in the Long Man.".

  // The storm comes on the third day; two hours after midnight the Long Man breaks, unless its leak is shut or the
  // lake is drawn down.
  Relation storming(). Relation broke(place). Relation drowned(place). Relation drawn(place).
  Rule storm_comes when watch(clock) >= 312 and not storming() and not calm(long_man) says "The wind goes round to the north, and the rain comes in over the fell in grey ropes." { Assert storming(). }
  Observe storm_scene at crest when storming() "Rain drives across the crest. Hollow Water has come up the lake face of the Long Man, grey and heaving, nearer than it was.".
  Rule field_wets when watch(clock) >= 240 and not state(leak_gate, mended) and not drowned(low_field) { Assert drowned(low_field). }
  Rule long_man_breaks when watch(clock) >= 396 and not state(leak_gate, mended) and not drawn(hollow) and not broke(long_man)
    says "In the dark, under the noise of the rain, there is another noise, very deep, like a wall falling a long way off. Then the sound of water." {
    Assert broke(long_man). Assert drowned(low_field). Assert drowned(green).
  }
  Hazard flood_waters "The flood" means "Deal (4d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Rule flood_takes when broke(long_man) and (at(party, green) or at(party, low_field) or at(party, landing) or at(party, millhouse) or at(party, nave) or at(party, taproom) or at(party, hollow_door) or at(party, springs))
    and not swept(party) { Assert strikes(flood_waters, party). Assert swept(party). }
  Relation swept(group).
  // Merrow on the hill, if Mother Ysolt rang the bell; otherwise Merrow in the low town when the water came.
  Rule bell_rung at green when storming() and convinced(ysolt) and at(folk, green)
    says "The chapel bell rings and rings, and doors open all over Merrow, and people go up the Hall lane in the rain with what they can carry." {
    Assert at(folk, yard). Assert at(ysolt, yard).
  }
  Relation lostToWater(group).
  Rule folk_lost when broke(long_man) and (at(folk, green) or at(folk, taproom)) { Assert lostToWater(folk). Assert at(folk, core). }
  Observe folk_saved at yard when at(folk, yard) and broke(long_man) "Merrow stands in the Hall yard in the rain, and looks down the lane at where it lived.".
  // The morning after the third night: the storm passes, and the dale is what the three days made it.
  Relation calm(place).
  Rule storm_passes when watch(clock) >= 432 and storming() says "The rain stops before dawn. The wind drops, and the dale lies under a washed, colourless sky." { Retract storming(). Assert calm(long_man). }
  Observe after_mended at green when calm(long_man) and not broke(long_man) and not drawn(hollow) "The beck runs brown but low between its banks, and nobody on the green is talking about the Long Man. The springs at its foot, people say, have nearly stopped.".
  Observe after_drawn at green when calm(long_man) and drawn(hollow) "Children stand on the dyke looking north, where the roofs of a grey town show above Hollow Water for the first time in a thousand years.".
  Observe after_broken at yard when calm(long_man) and broke(long_man) "Below the Hall the dale is one brown water from the ridge to the willows. The Long Man has a gap in it a hundred yards wide, and the lake is going out through it.".
  // Merrow safe from its wall: the leak shut, by the Mower or by the company; the lake drawn down; or the wall broken
  // with Merrow up the hill. Seen through, it is the company's experience (module.json, placed.json).
  Goal state(leak_gate, mended) or drawn(hollow) or (broke(long_man) and calm(long_man) and not lostToWater(folk)).
}

data/adventures/the-long-man/water.kyr:
Module longman "The Long Man" {
  Description "Hollow Water: the lake behind the Long Man, the Water-House on its island, and the town under it.".

  Place lakeshore "the lakeshore" is room within hollow at 0, 1.
  Place deep "the deep water" is room within hollow at 1, 1.
  Place water_house "the Water-House" is room within hollow at 2, 0.
  Place drowned_street "the drowned street" is room within hollow at 2, 1.
  Place face_house "the face-house" is room within hollow at 3, 1.
  Place last_house "the last house" is room within hollow at 2, 2.

  Passage lake_face "the lake face of the Long Man" is path between crest and lakeshore taking 20 minutes.
  Passage punt_way "out on Hollow Water" is ferry between lakeshore and deep taking 30 minutes.
  Passage island_way "the island landing" is ferry between deep and water_house taking 30 minutes.
  Passage house_steps "the steps below the Water-House" is steps between water_house and drowned_street.
  Passage face_door "a tall narrow door" is doorway between drowned_street and face_house.
  Passage last_door "a barred door" is door between drowned_street and last_house.

  Thing punt "an old punt" on punt_way {
    State beached blocking "An old punt lies drawn up in the reeds, grey with weather, its pole across the thwarts.".
    State afloat "The punt rides at the edge of the reeds.".
    Change launch "Push the punt off the reeds" from beached to afloat needing brawn.
  }
  Observe punt_looked beside punt_way as event when tried(punt, looking) "She is old and grey with weather, but somebody keeps her: her seams are fresh-tarred, and the pole across the thwarts is new ash.".
  Thing steps_water "the water over the steps" on house_steps is scenery {
    State under blocking "Below the Water-House door, steps go down into the lake, and the lake closes over them.".
    State drawn "The steps go down from the Water-House door into a street of grey houses, wet and shining.".
  }

  Observe shore_scene at lakeshore when not drawn(hollow) "Reeds, and black water going away to the hills, so still it holds the sky. The cold comes off it like a cellar's. Far out, a square tower stands up out of the lake on an island no bigger than a barn.".
  Observe shore_drawn at lakeshore when drawn(hollow) "The lake has drawn back from the reeds a long stone's throw, leaving mud, and the stumps of trees older than any in the dale.".
  Observe deep_scene at deep when true "Out on the water the punt pole finds no bottom. The water is cold enough to ache, and too clear: far down, something pale, like a roof.".
  Observe house_scene at water_house when true "One room, square and tall, of the same grey stone as the Long Man. In the middle of the floor stands a wheel of the same stone on an axle as thick as a man, and round the walls, in rows from floor to ceiling, notches.".
  // The wheel's socket notched to the shoe of Gammer Coller's rod: what she has been keeping, set apart (NAR-14).
  Observe socket_seen at water_house as revelation when knows(party, rod_seen) "In the hub of the great wheel is a socket, square, its edges notched in a close pattern: the pattern on the shoe of Gammer Coller's rod." teaches rod_fits.
  Observe street_scene at drowned_street when true "A street of dressed-stone houses with their roofs on, silted to the sills and shining with water. The doors are tall and narrow, and over each one a short row of notches, a little higher or lower from door to door, as if each house had measured the water for itself.".
  Observe face_house_scene at face_house when true "A long low room with a kiln at the far end, its mouth stopped with clay. Shelves run the length of both walls, and on them stand moulds of grey clay, each the hollow of a long, smooth face with no eyes.".
  Discovery moulds_read "The keepers' faces were fired here in moulds and set on last. A keeper wakes when it is given its face, and stops when it loses it." {
    Found by searching face_house "In the last mould on the last shelf lies a face already fired: grey, smooth, blind, never fitted to anything. Round the mould's rim runs a count of days in notches, the time it took to make.".
  }
  Item spare_face "a grey face, fired and never fitted" is keeper_mask at face_house hidden until moulds_read.
  Thing last_bar "the bar across the last house's door" on last_door {
    State barred blocking "A bar of black oak lies across the door in iron brackets, on the street side.".
    State lifted "The oak bar leans against the wall beside the open door.".
    Change lift "Lift the bar from the door" from barred to lifted at drowned_street.
  }
  Observe bar_looked beside last_door as event when tried(last_bar, looking) "The oak is black with the water, not with age, and the brackets are on the street side: whoever barred this door meant it to stay shut from outside.".
  Observe last_house_scene at last_house when true "One room. A table is laid for four, with bowls, a jug, and bread gone to grey stone. Nothing has been moved but by the water.".
  Observe tally_seen at last_house when true "Down the door-post runs a tally of days, cut neat and even. It stops at forty-one." teaches last_count.
  Discovery last_count "The last house of the drowned town was barred from outside, with its table laid for a meal. The tally of days on its door-post stops at forty-one, the same count as the last notches in the keeper's niche. The Hesk meant to come back.".
  Thing toy_bell "a child's bell of weirstone" at last_house {
    State still "On the sill sits a child's toy, a little bell of grey weirstone no bigger than a fist.".
    Tries pushing.
  }
  Observe bell_looked near toy_bell when tried(toy_bell, looking) "A little bell of grey weirstone, cut, not cast. Its clapper is a pebble of bronze on a thread of gut gone as hard as wire.".
  Event bell_answered near toy_bell when tried(toy_bell, pushing) "It rings, clear and long. Far off, under the hill, something rings back, once." then {
    Assert rung(toy_bell).
  }
  Relation rung(entity).

  Discovery rod_fits "The square socket in the hub of the Water-House wheel is notched to the pattern of the dyke-reeve's rod: the rod is a key to it.".
  Discovery hesk_known "The words cut round the Water-House wall, read: WE GAVE THE LOW HOUSES TO THE WATER, SO THAT THE FIELDS WOULD BE DRY. WE WILL KEEP THE WALL AS WE KEPT THE HOUSES." {
    Found by searching water_house with lore "The notches round the walls are writing, the writing of the Mower's breastplate. Round and round the room, as near as it can be read: WE GAVE THE LOW HOUSES TO THE WATER, SO THAT THE FIELDS WOULD BE DRY. WE WILL KEEP THE WALL AS WE KEPT THE HOUSES.".
  }
  Discovery town_known "Under Hollow Water stands a town of the people who built the Long Man, drowned by its own builders.".
  Observe street_teaches at drowned_street when true "Whoever lived here walked out of these doors uphill, and let the water in after them." teaches town_known.

  // The master wheel: worked with the rod, it draws the lake down by a man's height in two hours.
  Thing wheel "the great wheel" at water_house {
    State set "The great wheel stands with its square socket uppermost.".
    State turned "The great wheel has been turned its full round; somewhere below, water is going out with a long sigh.".
    Change turn "Set the rod in the socket and turn the great wheel" from set to turned needing sluice_rod.
  }
  Observe wheel_looked near wheel when tried(wheel, looking) "The great wheel is grey as the wall and taller than a man. In its hub is a square socket, its edges notched in a close pattern, made for something that is not here.".
  Measure drawsAt(place).
  Rule draw_begins when state(wheel, turned) and drawsAt(hollow) == 0 { Set drawsAt(hollow) to watch(clock). Increase drawsAt(hollow) by 12. }
  Rule lake_drawn when state(wheel, turned) and drawsAt(hollow) > 0 and watch(clock) >= drawsAt(hollow) and not drawn(hollow)
    says "Hollow Water goes down. It goes down the lake face of the Long Man a man's height, and the beck below the wall goes up the dale brown and roaring." {
    Assert drawn(hollow). Assert state(steps_water, drawn). Assert drowned(low_field). Assert drowned(millhouse).
  }
  Observe mill_drowned at millhouse when drowned(millhouse) "The beck has come in through the millhouse door. The wheel has stopped, jammed with branches, and Hob Teller is standing in his own millpond to the knees.".

  // The Old Jack keeps the deep water.
  Person jack "the Old Jack" at deep {
    Role "a pike as long as the punt". Species great_pike. Level 4.
    Temperament ambush.
    Warns "A shadow longer than the punt turns under the water, slowly, and comes up beneath you. It has seen you see it.".
    Comes "The water opens beside the punt, and the Old Jack comes up out of it with its mouth wide.".
  }

  // What the company is asked, and what it comes to see it must do.
  Objective lay_mower when knows(party, bounty_known) and not paidBounty(venn) and able(mower) and not knows(party, mower_keeps) "Aldous Venn will pay forty crowns for the Mower's mask.".
  Objective keep_wall when knows(party, teeth_taken) and knows(party, wall_known) and not state(leak_gate, mended) and not drawn(hollow) and not broke(long_man) "The Long Man is leaking where its bronze was taken, and the storm is coming.".
  Objective warn_merrow when knows(party, notches_known) and not convinced(ysolt) and not broke(long_man) "If the Long Man goes, the water will come over the chapel roof. Someone should tell Mother Ysolt.".
}

data/adventures/the-lull/acts.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── The chapters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Sixways, while the company waits; the first Lullday it spends in the valley; the next; the Working Day. Each opens
  // on the first page that finds the company where it is told.
  Relation sixwaysRoom(place).
  Initially Assert sixwaysRoom(march_road). Initially Assert sixwaysRoom(sx_street). Initially Assert sixwaysRoom(sx_taproom).
  Initially Assert sixwaysRoom(rooke_yard). Initially Assert sixwaysRoom(coll_kitchen). Initially Assert sixwaysRoom(haskett_loft).
  Initially Assert sixwaysRoom(exiles_row). Initially Assert sixwaysRoom(simeon_room). Initially Assert sixwaysRoom(sx_spring).
  Chapter ch_sixways "Sixways" when at(party, ?p) and sixwaysRoom(?p) and not cameIn(party) "Six days of the week Sixways is a hamlet on the march with too many carts for its size, and the seventh it is a door. Everyone here lives by the Lull: they cart for it, buy its cloth, sell it what it will not make, marry into it, wait for it. They count its days on a board by the pump and a stone on the rise. They say of someone who has gone in and not come out for a long while that they are lingering, and they do not say it unkindly.".
  Objective obj_wait_for_lull when not cameIn(party) and not lullday() "The valley opens one day in seven, at six in the morning, at the Fold-stone; the board by the pump counts the days. Ask at the Waiting Woman what it is like inside, then sit by the stone until the road changes.".
  Chapter ch_first "The First Lullday" when cameIn(party) and dayOne() "It is the holy day. It has been the holy day in this valley for fifty-seven years, which is four hundred of the world's, and nobody you meet here has done anything today that they did not mean to. The road you came in by will be there until midnight.".
  Chapter ch_second "The Second Lullday" when dayTwo() and inLull(party) and not hesterDead(hester) "For the Lull it is the next morning. For you it is a week on, and you can see it in the way people look at you: the Lull-born notice a week on a face the way other people notice a haircut. The Long Table is being laid. The Weekday Club is on the broken bridge, talking low. The Working Day is the next Lullday.".
  Chapter ch_second_mourning "The Second Lullday" when dayTwo() and inLull(party) and hesterDead(hester) and not chapterOpened(ch_second) "For the Lull it is the next morning; for you, a week on. Somebody has tied a black thread to the top of the Strike Post. In the Gardens, people talk low over the beans. Hester Lindsell died in the night, and tonight is her Watching; the town says the wasting took her at last, and that it was a mercy, and some of them look at the Lindsells' door while they say it. The Working Day is the next Lullday.".
  Chapter ch_working "The Working Day" when dayThree() and inLull(party) and workingBegun(lull_country) and not chapterOpened(ch_working_off) "It is the Lullday. It is also, for the first time in fifty-seven years, something else. Before six the young of Linger went down to the Shift Bridge in their oldest clothes with ropes and timbers and a cart of stone, and when the town came out to lay the Long Table it found them working: in public, in daylight, with their sleeves rolled. Nobody is laying the Table. Everybody is going down to the leat.".
  Chapter ch_working_off "The Lullday After" when dayThree() and inLull(party) and hour(clock) >= 7 and not workingBegun(lull_country) and not chapterOpened(ch_working) "It is Lullday, as it always is. The Shift Bridge is broken, as it always has been, and nobody is on it. The Long Table is being laid.".
}

data/adventures/the-lull/after.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── Afterwards: the valley, come back to ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The book closes on the Working Day, and the valley goes on: a company that comes back finds it as the day left it.
  Chapter ch_after_seventh "Monday, and After" when pastThree() and inLull(party) and outcomeSeventh(lull_country) "The road goes down from the stone every day now, and on six of them Linger works, badly and with enormous interest, like a town that has been given a new toy; and on the seventh it rests, and the law holds, and at the Watching some things come apart and most do not. There are people in Linger under fifty-seven who have now seen a Tuesday, and talk about it.".
  Chapter ch_after_monday "A Valley Like Any Other" when pastThree() and inLull(party) and outcomeMonday(lull_country) "The road goes down from the stone every day now, and nothing in the valley comes apart at sunset any more, and nothing holds better than it would anywhere else. There is a sound from the Mill, by day, that the Old Shift do not talk about.".
  Chapter ch_after_sunday "Still Lullday" when pastThree() and inLull(party) and (outcomeSunday(lull_country) or outcomeBroken(lull_country) or outcomeMeant(lull_country)) "It is Lullday. It is always Lullday. The town is a week older than the last time you saw it, which is to say a day.".

  Observe bridge_built at mill_bridge when lullOpen() and bridgeBuilt(club) "The Shift Bridge goes over the mill-leat again: new oak on the old piers, a little crooked in the middle where Davy Mote set it, and worn already on the boards where people walk out to the middle to stand and look at the Mill.".
  Observe bridge_built_seventh at mill_bridge as feature when lullOpen() and outcomeSeventh(lull_country) "At the Mill end an old weighbridge house has a new door, and a clock over it, and a board: C. LINDSELL, CLOCKS, FOR WAGES SIX DAYS IN SEVEN.".
  Observe yard_monday at mill_yard when lullOpen() and lawGone(lull_country) and not dark() "The great doors of the Mill stand open on the yard. Inside, on the ground floor, Haskett's men are taking the warps off the old looms and stringing new ones, and a few Lull-born are watching them, and one or two are helping, carefully, the way you help with something you might be blamed for.".
  Observe stone_after at fold_stone as feature when weekReturned(lull_country) "Under all the rows of seven on the Fold-stone somebody has carved, deep: AND THEN MONDAY.".
  Observe board_week at sx_street as feature when weekReturned(lull_country) and not lawGone(lull_country) and not dark() "Somebody has rubbed the count off the board by the pump and chalked instead: LULL EVERY DAY. LULLDAY: MIND WHAT YOU MEAN.".
  Observe board_monday at sx_street as feature when lawGone(lull_country) and not dark() "The board by the pump says, in fresh chalk: LINGER, CARTING WANTED, APPLY HASKETT.".
  Observe green_week_evening at green when lullOpen() and not lawDay() and weekReturned(lull_country) and hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 21 "The Long Table is laid, the way it always was, and the town eats at it, the way it always did; and nobody sets anything out on the grass, because nothing is going to come apart tonight, and the starlings go over the Tump as they always have, and nobody watches them.".
  // Where people are, afterwards.
  Rule after_tobias when outcomeSeventh(lull_country) and pastThree() and dayAt(tobias, hester_room) { Retract dayAt(tobias, hester_room). Assert dayAt(tobias, mill_bridge). Retract held(tobias). }
  Rule after_corin when (outcomeSeventh(lull_country) or outcomeSunday(lull_country)) and pastThree() and held(corin) { Retract held(corin). Retract held(club). Retract held(davy). Retract held(kezia). Retract held(piran). Retract held(aldith). Retract held(linnet). Retract held(folk). Retract held(wardens). Retract held(hobday). }
  Rule after_release when (outcomeMonday(lull_country) or outcomeBroken(lull_country)) and pastThree() and held(corin) { Retract held(corin). Retract held(club). Retract held(davy). Retract held(kezia). Retract held(piran). Retract held(aldith). Retract held(linnet). Retract held(folk). Retract held(wardens). Retract held(hobday). Retract held(tobias). }
  Observe tobias_at_bridge at mill_bridge as sign when lullOpen() and at(tobias, mill_bridge) and pastThree() "Tobias Lindsell sits on a kitchen chair at the Mill end of the bridge with a little clock ticking in his waistcoat pocket, telling the strike to a child, from the inside of the window.".
  Topic tobias_after with tobias "Ask Tobias Lindsell how he finds Monday" when pastThree() and outcomeSeventh(lull_country) and lullOpen() once {
    Says "Tobias considers it, the way he considers everything, as if it might be a trick question. 'Loud,' he says. 'Corin's hammering from six. Davy Mote has joined the Wardens, the new ones, that keep the peace on the six days and leave it alone on the seventh; he has a hat.' He takes out the little clock and looks at it. 'I am two days older than I was last Lullday. I can feel both of them.' He puts the clock away. 'Hester would have liked it. Or she'll like it, I should say, if you're asking her; she's on the bank most afternoons, telling them they're doing it wrong.'".
  }
  Topic corin_after with corin "Ask Corin Lindsell what she is making" when pastThree() and lullOpen() and (outcomeSeventh(lull_country) or outcomeSunday(lull_country)) once {
    Says "Corin holds up something small and brass, and squints at you through it. 'A clock that keeps both,' she says. 'The world's days, and the Lull's. For the stone. So Sixways can stop notching.' She turns it in the light. 'It'll come apart at sunset, I expect, the first time. I'm making it for wages, Haskett's paying.' She grins. 'And then I'll make it again for nobody, for the stone, and that one'll hold.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/the-lull/ashbys.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── The Lindsells' house ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Tobias Lindsell, of the Old Shift, who tells the strike best; Hester, his wife, who has been dying for six years of the
  // world's time; Corin, their granddaughter, whose clocks come apart every dusk. Tobias was not a striker. On the
  // seventh day of the strike he went into the Mill to work, alone, for his mother's physic, and was inside when the
  // Hallowing came; he climbed out of the window after the others had barred the doors from within. His name is not
  // on the beam. He has never bought anything across the Tump since.
  Observe kitchen_scene at lindsell_kitchen when lullOpen() "A weaver's kitchen with the loom long gone and a clockmaker's bench in the loom's place under the long window: a vice, a lens on a stalk, trays of tiny wheels sorted by size, and a litter of brass shavings. There is no clock anywhere in the room. On the dresser, plates with starlings painted on them; on the settle, a blanket folded by somebody who folds things when they are worried.".
  Observe kitchen_dark at lindsell_kitchen when folded() "The Lindsells' kitchen in the dark. At the bench under the window someone has fallen asleep with her head on her arms among the trays of little wheels.".
  Observe hester_scene at hester_room when lullOpen() and not hesterDead(hester) "A small room with a big bed, and in the bed a very small old woman, propped up, with a face like a walnut and eyes like a bird's. The window is open on the Gardens. There is a chair by the bed with the shape of a man worn into it, and a cup on the sill that nobody has drunk from.".
  Observe hester_gone at hester_room when lullOpen() and hesterDead(hester) "The small room with the big bed, and the bed made, very smooth, and nobody in it. The window is open. On the chair by the bed somebody has left a folded weaver's shirt.".
  Observe hester_dark at hester_room when folded() and not hesterDead(hester) "Hester Lindsell's room in the dark. The old woman is asleep, or something like it, with her hands open on the sheet; her breath is very slow, and in the chair beside her, sleeping too, an old man holds one of them.".
  Observe hester_dark_gone at hester_room when folded() and hesterDead(hester) "Hester Lindsell's room in the dark, the bed empty, and in the chair beside it an old man asleep, holding nothing.".

  // ── Hester ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person hester "Hester Lindsell" at hester_room {
    Role "an old weaver of the Old Shift, who is dying". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Likeness "abbess".
    Greets "The old woman in the bed looks at you for a while before she says anything, the way you might look at weather. 'A Sixer,' she says. 'Come in, then. Shut the door; Tobias'll fuss. Sit on the end of the bed; the chair's his.' She closes her eyes, opens them. 'I'm dying. You'll have heard. Everybody's heard. I've been at it six of your years, which is ten months of mine, and it's very dull, and nobody will talk to me about anything else.'".
    Greets again "Hester Lindsell opens one eye. 'You. Good. Talk to me about something.'".
    Wants poppy_kind. Wants nightshade_kind. Wants keepsake_kind.
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(hester). Initially Assert held(hester). Initially Assert bedAt(hester, hester_room).
  Relation hesterDead(group). Relation hesterEased(group). Relation diedBy(group, group). Measure hesterTrust(group).
  Discovery hester_sick "Hester Lindsell, of the Old Shift, is dying of a wasting sickness. In the Lull nobody dies quickly: she has been at it six years of the world's time, ten months of hers.".
  Observe hester_teaches at hester_room when lullOpen() and at(hester, hester_room) and not hesterDead(hester) and not knows(party, hester_sick) "When she moves, her face goes white round the mouth and comes back, and she does not stop talking while it does." teaches hester_sick.
  Topic hester_else with hester "Talk to Hester Lindsell about something else" when lullOpen() and not hesterDead(hester) once {
    Says "So you tell her about the world: the road you came by, the march, the price of things, a fight you saw, a fair. She listens with her eyes shut and her mouth twitching. 'Thirty years since I went out,' she says. 'Their thirty. I went to Sixways to see the sea, because somebody told me you could see the sea from the stone, and you can't.' She opens her eyes. 'It was the noise. Everyone in such a hurry. Doing things they didn't mean.' Pause. 'I liked it.' She laughs, and it hurts her, and she laughs anyway.".
    On discuss { Increase hesterTrust(hester) by 1. }
  }
  Topic hester_monday_ask with hester "Ask Hester Lindsell what she wants" when lullOpen() and not hesterDead(hester) and hesterTrust(hester) >= 1 and not knows(actor, hester_monday) {
    Says "Hester looks at you with her head on one side. 'A Monday,' she says. 'Do you know what that means, here? It means a day that never comes. When a child says they'll tidy their room, you say, on Monday. When a man says he'll forgive his brother: Monday.' She moves her hand on the sheet. 'I want mine. I've had the Lull fifty-seven years and I've loved every day of it and I want it to stop now, and it won't, not for years.' She is quite calm. 'There's a woman in Sixways, Ruth Coll, keeps a phial with a black thread round its neck. Tobias won't fetch it. He'd sooner do it with his own two hands, and he would, God help him, and then he'd carry it, the rest of his life, which here is a very long time.' She looks at you. 'You'd not carry it so far. You'd be out of here by midnight.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hester_monday). Increase hesterTrust(hester) by 1. }
  }
  Discovery hester_monday "Hester Lindsell has asked for her Monday: the phial with the black thread that Ruth Coll keeps in Sixways. Tobias will not fetch it, and she is afraid that he will do it himself, and carry it.".
  Topic hester_tobias with hester "Ask Hester Lindsell about Tobias" when lullOpen() and not hesterDead(hester) once {
    Says "'Tobias Lindsell,' says Hester, 'tells the Strike better than anyone alive, because he was at the window when we came out.' She smiles at the ceiling. 'He always says that. At the window.' The smile goes somewhere private. 'Ask him, one day, which side of the window. Not today. He's tired.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, which_side). Increase hesterTrust(hester) by 1. }
  }
  Discovery which_side "Hester Lindsell says to ask Tobias, one day, which side of the Mill window he was on.".
  Topic hester_simeon with hester "Tell Hester Lindsell that Simeon Eddowes is in Sixways, and old" when lullOpen() and not hesterDead(hester) and knows(actor, simeon_banned) and not following(simeon, party) once {
    Says "Hester's eyes come open all the way. 'Simeon.' She laughs, and coughs, and laughs. 'Old? He was old at twenty. He wrote me a Gloss once, number forty, that a girl who walks up a hill with one man is not thereby walking away from another. The Reeve made him paint over it.' She lies back. 'Old,' she says again, differently. 'Of course he is. He went out.' She is quiet. 'Tell him I'd like to see him. Tell him I said Gloss forty.'".
    On discuss { Assert hesterAsksSimeon(hester). }
  }
  Relation hesterAsksSimeon(group).

  // Poppy: she sleeps, and is eased, and lives on into the Working Day. Tobias minds that it was bought.
  Event hester_poppy near hester when keeps(hester, ?p) and itemKind(?p, poppy_kind) and not hesterEased(hester) "Hester turns the twist of paper over and reads Ruth Coll's writing on it, and snorts. 'Don't boil it,' she says. 'As if I'd boil it.' She has you steep it in the cup on the sill, and drinks it, and makes a face, and in a little while her face loosens, all of it, like a fist let go. 'Oh,' she says. 'Oh, that's.' She sleeps. When Tobias comes in he looks at her, and at the twist of paper, and at you, and takes the cup off the sill and rinses it in the basin without a word." then {
    Assert hesterEased(hester). Assert tobiasSawPoppy(tobias).
  }
  Relation tobiasSawPoppy(group).
  Observe hester_eased at hester_room when lullOpen() and hesterEased(hester) and not hesterDead(hester) "Hester is asleep, or nearly; her face is smooth, and her hands are easy on the sheet. The cup on the sill has been drunk from.".
  // The phial: she drinks it that evening, and dies before midnight, and it holds.
  Event hester_phial near hester when keeps(hester, ?p) and itemKind(?p, nightshade_kind) and not hesterDead(hester) "Hester holds the phial up to the window and looks at the black thread. 'Ruth Coll,' she says. 'She always did know what people meant.' She puts it under her pillow. 'Not now. At the Watching, when they're all out at the Table. Tobias too: I'll send him.' She takes your hand, which surprises you; her hand is very light and very hot. 'Thank you,' she says. 'Now go and eat something. You'll not want to be here.'" then {
    Assert hesterHasPhial(hester).
  }
  Relation hesterHasPhial(group).
  // Simeon, there when she has it, gives it her himself.
  Rule simeon_gives at hester_room when hesterHasPhial(hester) and following(simeon, party) and at(party, hester_room) and not hesterDead(hester) and not simeonWith(hester)
    says "Simeon has not said a word since he came in. He sits on the end of the bed, where Hester pats, and they look at each other, and she says, 'Gloss forty,' and he says, 'Held,' and his voice goes. Then she shows him what is under her pillow, and he looks at it, and at her, and he says, 'I'll stay. I'll sit with you. Tobias can have the Table.' She says, 'You always did want to be in at the end of things.' He says, 'Only yours.'" {
    Assert simeonWith(hester). Retract following(simeon, party). Assert at(simeon, hester_room). Assert simeonHome(simeon).
  }
  Relation simeonWith(group).
  Rule hester_drinks when hesterHasPhial(hester) and lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 20 and not hesterDead(hester) { Assert hesterDead(hester). Assert diedBy(hester, party). Assert at(hester, limbo). }
  Rule hester_drinks_told at green when hesterDead(hester) and diedBy(hester, party) and at(party, green) and not spreadFact(hester_death_told)
    says "In the middle of the Watching Tobias Lindsell comes out of his house and stands at the end of the Long Table, and the table goes quiet from that end to the other, the way a field goes quiet when a hawk goes over. Somebody gets up and gives him their place, and he sits in it, and puts his hands on the table, open." { Assert spreadFact(hester_death_told). }
  Entity hester_death_told: fact "Hester's death, told".
  Relation spreadFact(fact).

  // Unless something else has been done, Tobias does it himself, on the night of the company's first Lullday, after
  // the Watching. He tells nobody.
  Rule tobias_does_it when dayOne() and lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 22 and not hesterDead(hester) and not hesterEased(hester) and not hesterSat(hester) and not hesterHasPhial(hester) { Assert hesterDead(hester). Assert diedBy(hester, tobias). Assert at(hester, limbo). Assert tobiasCarries(tobias). }
  Relation tobiasCarries(group).
  // Her Watching, on the next Lullday: the town believes the wasting took her at last.
  Observe hester_watching at green when dayTwo() and lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 21 and hesterDead(hester) "Tonight there is a space at the top of the Long Table, by the Old Shift, with a cup set at it and a weaver's shirt folded on the bench. It is Hester Lindsell's Watching. They set her shirt out on the grass with the day's makings, and they watch it with the rest, and it holds, because it was always going to: it was woven fifty-seven years ago by a woman who meant it.".

  // ── Tobias ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person tobias "Tobias Lindsell" at hester_room {
    Role "an old weaver of the Old Shift, who tells the strike best". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Likeness "abbot".
    Greets "A tall stooped old man gets up out of the chair by the bed, slowly, and looks at you with very mild blue eyes. 'You'll be the Sixer that's been talking to my wife,' he says. 'She likes a new face. Come in the kitchen, and don't tire her.'".
    Greets again "Tobias Lindsell nods to you, mildly, as if you had been there yesterday, which for him perhaps you were.".
    Wants keepsake_kind.
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(tobias). Initially Assert dayAt(tobias, hester_room). Initially Assert bedAt(tobias, hester_room).
  Measure tobiasTrust(group).
  Topic tobias_strike with tobias "Ask Tobias Lindsell to tell you the strike" when lullOpen() once {
    Says "Tobias sits down on the settle and puts his hands on his knees and tells it, and he tells it well: the Long Shift, the war that wanted cloth, which war nobody now remembers; the seven-day weeks; Agnes Crane's sister falling asleep at her loom and the shuttle taking her eye; the morning the weavers did not go in. Seven days on the Tump in the rain, with the bailiffs' men at the foot of it. 'And on the seventh day,' he says, 'they came down off the hill and went into the Mill, all fifty-one, and barred the doors behind them from the inside with the big beam, and wrote their names on it, and then they climbed out of the windows one by one, and I was at the window.' He stops. 'And they walked up the Tump, and they asked. And when the sun went down, it was still the holy day, and in the morning it was the holy day, and it has been the holy day ever since.' He looks at his hands. 'That's the strike.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, strike_told). Increase tobiasTrust(tobias) by 1. }
  }
  Topic tobias_hester_ask with tobias "Tell Tobias Lindsell what Hester has asked you for" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, hester_monday) and not hesterDead(hester) once {
    Says "Tobias does not look surprised. He looks very tired. 'She's asked me every day for a month,' he says. 'Every day. That's four months of yours.' He turns his cup round. 'I'll not fetch it. I'll not buy anything over the Tump; I bought physic once, for my mother, and I'll not do that again.' He is quiet. 'If it comes to it,' he says, 'I'll not need anything bought.' Then he looks at you, and you see that he has frightened himself.".
    On discuss { Increase tobiasTrust(tobias) by 1. Assert knows(actor, tobias_will). }
  }
  Discovery tobias_will "Tobias Lindsell will not buy physic across the Tump, because he bought it once for his mother; and if it comes to it, he says, he will not need anything bought to give Hester her Monday.".
  // What he will tell, and to whom: which side of the window.
  Topic tobias_window with tobias "Ask Tobias Lindsell which side of the window he was on" when lullOpen() and not dayOne() and (knows(actor, which_side) or knows(actor, beam_names)) and tobiasTrust(tobias) >= 2 and not tobiasConfessed(tobias) {
    Says "Tobias is still for so long that you think he has not heard. Then he gets up and shuts the kitchen door, and sits down again. 'The inside,' he says. 'My mother was dying, and the bailiffs said a shilling a day to anyone who'd come in on the seventh day and keep a loom going, and nobody would, and I did.' His hands are open on his knees. 'I was alone in there at a loom when they came in and barred the doors. They didn't see me. I heard them say their names and cut them. I heard them go out of the windows, one by one. Then I went out of the window, last, and up the Tump after them, at the back, in the rain.' He looks at you. 'And it was the holy day ever after, and my mother died anyway, on the Monday that never came, and the shilling was back in the bailiff's purse by sunset. I never told. Hester knew. Hester always knew.' He breathes. 'You'll want to know why I'll not have the week back. That's why. I know what I'd do for wages. I did it.'".
    On discuss { Assert tobiasConfessed(tobias). Assert knows(actor, tobias_inside). Increase tobiasTrust(tobias) by 1. }
  }
  Relation tobiasConfessed(group).
  Discovery tobias_inside "Tobias Lindsell was not a striker. On the seventh day he was inside the Mill working at a loom for a shilling, for his mother's physic, when the strikers barred the doors; he climbed out of the window last. His name is not on the beam. He fears the week's return because he knows what he would do for wages.".
  Topic tobias_how_died with tobias "Ask Tobias Lindsell how Hester died" when lullOpen() and hesterDead(hester) and diedBy(hester, tobias) and tobiasTrust(tobias) >= 1 and not tobiasToldDeath(tobias) {
    Says "Tobias looks at the chair by the bed, and then at you. 'She asked me,' he says. 'Every day for a month. And on the night you were here she asked me again, and I said yes.' He holds his hands out in front of him and looks at them as if they belonged to someone in the street. 'I held the pillow. I meant it. That's the thing about this place: I meant it, and it held.' He puts the hands away. 'They think the wasting took her. Let them.'".
    On discuss { Assert tobiasToldDeath(tobias). Assert knows(actor, tobias_killed). }
  }
  Relation tobiasToldDeath(group).
  Discovery tobias_killed "Hester Lindsell did not die of the wasting. Tobias gave her her Monday himself, with a pillow, on the night she asked him again. The town does not know.".
  Topic tobias_poppy with tobias "Ask Tobias Lindsell about the poppy" when lullOpen() and hesterEased(hester) and not hesterDead(hester) and dayTwo() once {
    Says "Tobias sits by the bed and does not look at you for a while. 'Bought,' he says at last. 'Over the Tump. In my house.' Then: 'She knew my face this morning. She said, You've not shaved, Tobias Lindsell. She's not said my name in a month.' He rubs his jaw. 'I'll not thank you. I don't know how to. Sit down.'".
    On discuss { Increase tobiasTrust(tobias) by 1. Assert tobiasSoftened(tobias). }
  }
  Relation tobiasSoftened(group).

  // ── Corin ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person corin "Corin Lindsell" at mill_bridge {
    Role "who makes clocks that do not last". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Likeness "apprentice".
    Greets "A young woman with brass dust on her hands and her hair tied up with a bootlace is sitting on the broken end of the bridge, swinging her heels over the leat. 'You're a Sixer,' she says. 'You've got that look. Like you've somewhere to be.' She looks at you properly. 'I'd give anything for somewhere to be.'".
    Greets again "Corin Lindsell looks up, quick, as if she had been expecting someone else, and then decides you will do.".
    Wants purse_kind. Wants keepsake_kind.
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(corin). Initially Assert dayAt(corin, mill_bridge). Initially Assert bedAt(corin, lindsell_kitchen).
  Measure corinTrust(group).
  Topic corin_clocks with corin "Ask Corin Lindsell about her clocks" when lullOpen() once {
    Says "'I make clocks,' says Corin. 'Good ones. I've made forty-one. Every one of them falls to bits at sunset, at the Watching, in front of everybody.' She holds up her brass-dusty hands. 'Wheels, springs, pins, in the grass. Forty-one times.' She laughs, not nicely. 'The Glossers say it's because I'm not making them for anybody. Aunt Lettice says it's because I don't love clockmaking. I love clockmaking more than I love anything in this valley.' She looks at the dark mill. 'I make them because a clock is the one thing in here that knows something's supposed to happen next.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, clock_ravels). Increase corinTrust(corin) by 1. }
  }
  Discovery clock_ravels "Corin Lindsell's clocks come apart at every Watching: forty-one of them. She makes them, she says, because a clock knows something is supposed to happen next.".
  Topic corin_want with corin "Ask Corin Lindsell what she wants" when lullOpen() and corinTrust(corin) >= 1 once {
    Says "Corin swings her heels. 'Everybody asks the Lull-born that like we want to leave. I don't want to leave. If I go out over the Tump for a year I come back a year older and Davy's a week older and Grandad's a week older and I'm a stranger in my own house.' She kicks the bridge. 'I want all of us to go on. I want Monday. I want to make a thing on Monday and come back on Tuesday and find it a day old.' She looks at you. 'Two hundred and thirty-one of us have never seen a day that wasn't this one. We're not resting. We're stopped.'".
    On discuss { Increase corinTrust(corin) by 1. Assert knows(actor, corin_stopped). }
  }
  Discovery corin_stopped "Corin Lindsell does not want to leave the Lull: she wants it to go on, all of it, into a week. 'We're not resting,' she says. 'We're stopped.'".
  // Making a clock for someone: suggested once she has said why she makes them.
  Topic corin_for_someone with corin "Ask Corin Lindsell whether she has ever made a clock for someone" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, clock_ravels) and corinTrust(corin) >= 2 and not corinMaking(corin) and not corinClockHeld(corin) {
    Says "'For someone,' says Corin, and makes a face. 'Who would I make a clock for? Nobody here needs to know the time. It's always the same time.' She is quiet. Then, not looking at you: 'Grandad used to time the strike. He had a watch, a big turnip of a thing, he said he timed the seven days on it. It stopped, the day of the Hallowing. Never went again.' She picks at the brass on her fingers. 'I could make him one that goes.' She gets up. 'I'll make it for the next Lullday. It'll fall to bits like all the rest. But I'll make it.'".
    On discuss { Assert corinMaking(corin). Set corinStarted(corin) to lullCount(clock). }
  }
  Relation corinMaking(group). Relation corinClockHeld(group). Measure corinStarted(group).
  Thing corin_clock "Corin's clock for her grandfather" at limbo {
    State ticking "A small clock in a case of pale wood stands on the grass before the Long Table, ticking, with a card propped against it: FOR GRANDAD, WHO TIMED THE STRIKE.".
    State held "Corin's clock for her grandfather is still ticking.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(corin_clock, ticking).
  Rule clock_set_out when corinMaking(corin) and lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 19 and lullCount(clock) > corinStarted(corin) and at(corin_clock, limbo) and not corinClockHeld(corin) { Assert at(corin_clock, green). }
  Rule clock_holds at green when at(corin_clock, green) and lullDusk() and state(corin_clock, ticking)
    says "Among the makings, Corin's little clock goes on ticking. A basket beside it comes apart into withies with a dry rustle, and someone at the Table groans and is laughed at. The clock goes on ticking. Corin is standing up. She has not noticed she is standing. The clock ticks. The starlings come over. The clock ticks. Somebody starts to clap, and is hushed, because it is not a thing you clap; and then the whole Table is clapping anyway, and Corin sits down on the grass in front of her clock with her hands over her face." {
    Assert state(corin_clock, held). Assert corinClockHeld(corin). Retract corinMaking(corin).
  }
  // Given, it changes Tobias.
  Rule clock_given at green when corinClockHeld(corin) and lullDusk() and at(tobias, green) and not hesterDeadByHim() and not clockGiven(tobias)
    says "Corin picks the clock up off the grass and walks the length of the Long Table with it, to the top, where the Old Shift sit, and puts it into her grandfather's hands. Tobias holds it to his ear. Then he holds it against his chest, under his coat, the way you would hold a bird. He says something to her that nobody else hears, and Corin's face changes, and she sits down beside him, very close, and they talk with their heads together until the lanterns are out." {
    Assert clockGiven(tobias). Assert tobiasConfessed(tobias). Assert corinKnowsWindow(corin). Assert tobiasLovePath(tobias). Retract at(corin_clock, green). Assert at(corin_clock, hester_room).
  }
  Rule clock_given_grief at green when corinClockHeld(corin) and lullDusk() and at(tobias, green) and hesterDeadByHim() and not clockGiven(tobias)
    says "Corin picks the clock up off the grass and walks the length of the Long Table with it, to the top, and puts it into her grandfather's hands. Tobias holds it to his ear. Then he gives it back to her, very gently, and gets up, and goes home without a word, and the Table watches him go." {
    Assert clockGiven(tobias). Retract at(corin_clock, green). Assert at(corin_clock, lindsell_kitchen).
  }
  Query hesterDeadByHim() means diedBy(hester, tobias) and not tobiasForgiven(tobias).
  Relation clockGiven(group). Relation corinKnowsWindow(group). Relation tobiasLovePath(group). Relation tobiasForgiven(group).
  // What Corin hears from the company, of what it learned.
  Topic corin_window with corin "Tell Corin Lindsell which side of the window her grandfather was on" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, tobias_inside) and not corinKnowsWindow(corin) once {
    Grave "This is Tobias's to tell, and he has not told her.".
    Says "Corin listens with her jaw set. When you have finished she winds a loose thread from her cuff round one finger, tighter and tighter. Then: 'He timed the strike,' she says. 'On his watch. He told me he timed it from the Tump.' She stands up. 'He was inside.' And she goes to the very end of the broken pier and stands there with her back to you, looking across the leat at the dark mill, so still that people on the green stop to look.".
    On discuss { Assert corinKnowsWindow(corin). Assert corinBetrayed(corin). }
  }
  Relation corinBetrayed(group).
  Topic corin_forgive with corin "Ask Corin Lindsell to hear it from her grandfather" when lullOpen() and corinBetrayed(corin) and not tobiasLovePath(tobias) and tobiasConfessed(tobias) and not hesterDeadByHim() once {
    Says "Corin is on the bridge with her back to you. 'Why should I?' she says. Then, after a while, because you wait: 'Because it's him.' She gets up and goes to find him, slowly this time. At the Watching you see them at the top of the Table, the old man talking, the girl listening, his hands open on the boards.".
    On discuss { Assert tobiasLovePath(tobias). Retract corinBetrayed(corin). }
  }
}

data/adventures/the-lull/bride.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── The Bride-Gift: Abel Rooke and Wenna Spurling ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Abel thinks that to marry into the Lull he must become a Lull man and give up the road; so he makes Wenna a chair,
  // the most settling thing there is, meaning to give himself up. He does not mean it, and it comes apart. Wenna wants
  // to go on the road with him, and has never said, because he talks so much about how restful the Lull is.
  Person wenna "Wenna Spurling" at spurling_shop {
    Role "the chandler's daughter, who dips candles". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Likeness "apprentice".
    Greets "The girl at the candle-bench looks up with her tongue still between her teeth, and takes it in. 'Sorry. If I talk I get them lumpy.' She hangs a pair of wet candles on the rack by their wick. 'Wenna Spurling. You're a Sixer. Do you know Abel Rooke? Everybody out there knows Abel, he says.' She goes pink. 'He says that about everybody.'".
    Greets again "Wenna Spurling lifts a dripping candle to you in greeting, and a bead of wax runs down her wrist, and she lets it. 'Back before sunset,' she says. 'A good habit. Whatever you do here without meaning it goes with the light, and I mean this candle, so mind it.'".
    Wants keepsake_kind.
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(wenna). Initially Assert dayAt(wenna, spurling_shop). Initially Assert bedAt(wenna, spurling_shop).
  // Abel comes in on Lulldays, to her; and goes home before midnight.
  Rule abel_in when lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 19 and not at(abel, spurling_shop) and not abelHeld(abel) { Assert at(abel, spurling_shop). }
  Rule abel_table when lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 21 and not at(abel, green) and not abelHeld(abel) { Assert at(abel, green). }
  Rule abel_out when (folded() or hour(clock) >= 21) and not at(abel, rooke_yard) and not abelHeld(abel) and not travelsWith(abel, party) { Assert at(abel, rooke_yard). }
  Relation abelHeld(group).
  Observe abel_at_wenna at spurling_shop when lullOpen() and at(abel, spurling_shop) "Abel Rooke is sitting on a stool much too small for him in the corner of the chandlery, holding a skein of wicks for Wenna, and talking, mostly about how restful it is in here.".
  Relation abelLoves(group). Relation wennaWants(group). Relation abelTold(group). Relation wennaTold(group). Relation abelMeans(group). Relation wedded(group). Relation abelPaidHelp(group).
  Topic abel_likes with abel "Ask Abel Rooke what he likes best in the world" when not lullOpen() and knows(actor, chair_ravels) once {
    Says "'Wenna,' says Abel at once. Then, because you wait: 'And Dulcie. And the road. You'd not think it, a road, but in the morning when you've got the cart loaded and you come up over Sixways rise and the whole march is in front of you and Dulcie's leaning into the collar and you've got a pipe going, and you don't know who you'll meet, and it's just a road, going to somewhere, and you're on it.' He stops. He looks at the thing under the sack. 'In the Lull you don't go anywhere. That's the beauty of it.' He does not sound as if it is.".
    On discuss { Assert abelLoves(abel). Assert knows(actor, abel_road). }
  }
  Discovery abel_road "Abel Rooke loves the road more than he knows: the cart, the mare, the march in the morning. He means to give it up to marry into the Lull.".
  Topic wenna_wants with wenna "Ask Wenna Spurling what she wants of Abel" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, chair_ravels) once {
    Says "Wenna puts down the wicks. 'Don't tell him,' she says. 'He loves it here. He's always saying how restful it is.' She dips a candle, slowly, and draws it out. 'I want to go on the cart. I want to see the mill towns, and the downs, and the sea if there is one, and sleep under a cart in the rain and get up in the morning and not know who we'll meet.' She hangs the candle up. 'I've dipped candles in this shop since I was six and it's always the same afternoon. He brings the road in on his boots. I can smell it.' She looks at you, fierce. 'Don't tell him. He'd give it up for me, and then he'd hate me, at sunset, every day.'".
    On discuss { Assert wennaWants(wenna). Assert knows(actor, wenna_road). }
  }
  Discovery wenna_road "Wenna Spurling wants to leave the Lull and go on the road with Abel Rooke. She has never told him, because he talks so much about how restful the Lull is.".
  Topic abel_told with abel "Tell Abel Rooke what Wenna Spurling wants" when knows(actor, wenna_road) and not abelTold(abel) once {
    Says "Abel stares at you. 'The road,' he says. 'Wenna.' He sits down on the mounting-block, slowly, the way a man sits who has been carrying something very heavy and has just been told he can put it down. 'I thought she'd want me to stop,' he says. 'Everyone in there stops.' Then he is up again and pulling the sack off the chair and looking at it with something like hatred, and then something like laughter. 'A chair,' he says. 'I made her a chair.' He pushes it over with his boot. 'I'll make her a seat. A cart-seat. Two wide, with a back, and a box under it for her candles.' He is already measuring. 'That I'd mean.'".
    On discuss { Assert abelTold(abel). Assert abelMeans(abel). }
  }
  Topic wenna_told with wenna "Tell Wenna Spurling what Abel Rooke loves" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, abel_road) and not wennaTold(wenna) once {
    Says "Wenna listens with a candle forgotten in her hand, dripping. 'He loves it,' she says. 'The road.' She starts to laugh. 'And he's been making me chairs.' She puts the candle down. 'Then I'll tell him. Today. I'll tell him I want the road and see if he can say no to that.' She takes off her apron. 'If the next chair comes apart, it'll be because he's a fool, not because I am.'".
    On discuss { Assert wennaTold(wenna). Assert abelMeans(abel). }
  }
  // Paid help with the chair: the company's work for wages comes apart with it.
  Action help_chair(actor: group, site: place) "Help Abel Rooke with the chair's joints, for three coin" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(abel, site) and at(actor, rooke_yard) and knows(actor, chair_ravels) and not abelPaidHelp(abel) and not abelMeans(abel) and not lullday().
    Time 18.
    On success { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Assert abelPaidHelp(abel). }
    Result "You spend the afternoon with Abel at the chair, paring tenons and driving pegs, and it is a good chair when you have done, square and sound. Abel pays you, gratefully. 'Next Lullday,' he says. 'Fourth time lucky.'".
  }
  // The gift set out at the Watching on the second Lullday: the chair again, unless he means something else.
  Thing abel_gift "Abel's wedding gift" at limbo {
    State chair "Before the Long Table stands a plain ash chair with a card on it: FOR WENNA, FROM ABEL. People are already smiling.".
    State seat "Before the Long Table stands a cart-seat, two wide, with a back, and a box under it that smells of beeswax, and a card: FOR WENNA, FOR THE ROAD, FROM ABEL.".
    State ravelled "Where Abel's chair stood before the Long Table there is a little heap of pegs and shavings.".
    State held "Abel's cart-seat stands before the Long Table, and Wenna Spurling is sitting on it.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(abel_gift, chair).
  Rule gift_out when dayTwo() and lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 19 and at(abel_gift, limbo) and not wedded(wenna) { Assert at(abel_gift, green). }
  Rule gift_is_seat when abelMeans(abel) and state(abel_gift, chair) and not at(abel_gift, green) { Assert state(abel_gift, seat). }
  Rule chair_ravels at green when lullDusk() and at(abel_gift, green) and state(abel_gift, chair)
    says "At sunset Abel's chair comes apart for the fourth time, in front of the whole Long Table: legs, rails, seat, a little heap of pegs and shavings. Wenna Spurling's aunt does not laugh this time. Nobody laughs. Abel stands looking at it with his big hands hanging, and then he goes off up the Tump road in the dusk, alone, without his supper, and Wenna watches him go." {
    Assert state(abel_gift, ravelled). Assert abelGaveUp(abel). Assert at(abel_gift, limbo).
  }
  Relation abelGaveUp(group).
  Rule seat_holds at green when lullDusk() and at(abel_gift, green) and state(abel_gift, seat)
    says "The sun goes off the Tump. The cart-seat stands in the grass. Abel Rooke, who has been standing beside it rigid as a gatepost, sees that it has not moved and makes a noise nobody in Linger has heard a man make before, and Wenna Spurling walks out from the Table and sits down on it, on her side, and pats his. The Long Table stands up. Somebody starts the wedding-song, which is old and goes 'Rest you, rest you', and somebody else changes it to 'Go you, go you', and by the second verse the whole of Linger is singing it that way. In the music room over the Open Hand a fiddle takes it up. They are married by the Glosser at the top of the Table, with the seat as the witness." {
    Assert state(abel_gift, held). Assert wedded(wenna). Assert spreadFact(wedding_told).
  }
  Entity wedding_told: fact "the wedding".
  // Married, they go out over the Tump before midnight in the cart; they come back for the Working Day.
  Rule newlyweds_out when wedded(wenna) and lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 22 and lullFolk(wenna) and dayTwo() { Retract lullFolk(wenna). Assert at(wenna, rooke_yard). Assert wennaOut(wenna). }
  Relation wennaOut(group).
  Observe wenna_in_yard at rooke_yard when wennaOut(wenna) and at(wenna, rooke_yard) and not dark() "Wenna Rooke, who was Wenna Spurling, is sitting on the cart-seat in the yard in a borrowed coat, watching the road, with Dulcie's nose on her shoulder.".
  Rule wenna_with_abel when wennaOut(wenna) and at(abel, ?p) and not at(wenna, ?p) and not wennaHand(wenna) { Assert at(wenna, ?p). }
  Relation wennaHand(group).
  Topic wenna_out_talk with wenna "Ask Wenna Rooke how she finds the world" when wennaOut(wenna) and not lullOpen() once {
    Says "'Loud,' says Wenna happily. 'Everybody's in such a hurry. A man shouted at Dulcie this morning, at nothing, and Abel shouted back, and they both laughed.' She looks at her hands. 'It's Third already. Third! I've never had a Third. Tomorrow's Fourth.' She hugs her knees. 'Mother's had one day. One day, and I've had three. I'll be older than her soon, the way it goes, in my heart.' She does not stop smiling while she says it, but she says it.".
  }
  Event wenna_keepsake near wenna when keeps(wenna, keepsake) and madeFor(keepsake, wenna) "Wenna turns the little carving over and over, and then wraps it in a twist of wick and puts it in her apron pocket. 'For the cart,' she says. 'For the box under the seat.'" then { Assert keepsakeKept(keepsake). }

  // ── The Waiting Woman: Dorcas and Piran ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Piran carves his wife every Lullday, and has for four years of his: two hundred heads, and she ages along the shelf.
  // He knows; she does not know he knows. She is ill, and has not told him. His mother is of the Old Shift.
  Person piran "Piran Trewin" at piran_shop {
    Role "a carver of Linger". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Likeness "craftsman".
    Greets "A quiet man in his thirties with shavings in his beard looks up from a block of limewood. He is shaping, you see, a woman's head. 'Sixer,' he says, not unkindly, and goes on shaping. 'If you're from the Waiting Woman, she's not here yet. She comes at nine.'".
    Greets again "Piran Trewin nods, and goes on carving, and the thing under the knife is a little nearer to a face than it was. 'It does not matter what it is,' he says. 'It will come apart at sunset if I mean it. I am working very hard not to mean it.'".
    Wants keepsake_kind.
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(piran). Initially Assert dayAt(piran, piran_shop). Initially Assert bedAt(piran, piran_shop).
  Rule dorcas_in when lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 19 and not at(dorcas, piran_shop) and not dorcasStays(dorcas) { Assert at(dorcas, piran_shop). }
  Rule dorcas_table when lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 21 and not at(dorcas, green) { Assert at(dorcas, green). }
  Rule dorcas_home when (folded() or hour(clock) >= 21) and not at(dorcas, sx_taproom) and not dorcasStays(dorcas) { Assert at(dorcas, sx_taproom). }
  Relation dorcasStays(group). Relation piranOut(group). Relation piranKnowsIll(group). Relation dorcasKnowsHeads(group).
  Observe dorcas_with_piran at piran_shop when lullOpen() and at(dorcas, piran_shop) "Dorcas Trewin is sitting for her husband on a stool by the window, very straight, in her good blue gown, turning her face a little away from the light without seeming to.".
  Topic piran_heads with piran "Ask Piran Trewin about the heads on his shelves" when lullOpen() once {
    Says "Piran looks along the shelves: the same woman, again and again, a little apart from each other. 'One every Lullday,' he says. 'Four years of mine. Two hundred and some.' He takes one down from the near end, a young woman, and one from the far end, and puts them side by side on the bench. He leaves them there side by side for the length of a breath. 'She thinks I can't see it,' he says. 'She says the walk tires her. I let her say it.' He puts the young one back. 'I'm a carver. I see faces. I see hers every morning.' He picks up his knife. 'Don't tell her.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, piran_sees). }
  }
  Discovery piran_sees "Piran Trewin has carved his wife's head every Lullday for four years of his: two hundred heads, and she ages along the shelf. He knows. He lets her say it is the walk.".
  Topic piran_ill with piran "Tell Piran Trewin that Dorcas is ill" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, dorcas_ill) and not piranKnowsIll(piran) once {
    Grave "She has not told him.".
    Says "Piran's knife stops. He sets it down, and the block, and sits with his hands on his knees while the light moves along the shelf. 'A year,' he says. 'Two. Her count.' He looks along the shelf. 'Fifteen Lulldays. Twenty.' Then he gets up and takes his coat off the peg. 'My mother's in the Almshouse,' he says. 'Agnes Crane, that sang it on the Tump. If I go out, she'll see me once a week and I'll see her once a year, and when I come back she'll still be there and I'll be old.' He puts the coat on. 'I'm going out. Tonight. With Dorcas. For the year, or the two.' He looks at you. 'Don't say anything kind. I'll not manage it.'".
    On discuss { Assert piranKnowsIll(piran). Assert piranOut(piran). }
  }
  Topic dorcas_heads with dorcas "Tell Dorcas Trewin about the heads on Piran's shelves" when knows(actor, piran_sees) and not dorcasKnowsHeads(dorcas) once {
    Says "Dorcas has her back to you, at the barrel. She does not turn round. 'Two hundred,' she says. 'Every week.' Her shoulders move. 'And I've been turning my face from the window.' She does turn, then, and she is laughing, and crying, and she does not care which. 'The fool. The fool. Four years.' She wipes her face with the bar-cloth. 'Then he knows I'm old, and I can stop pretending I'm not.' She takes off her apron. 'I've been thinking. If I went in. Lived in. I'd be ill there a day a week instead of seven. Ruth says a year or two: that's ten years of the Lull, with him.' She folds the apron. 'Ten years of Lulldays. Like Hester Lindsell.' She is quiet. 'I'd take that. I'd take that and say thank you.'".
    On discuss { Assert dorcasKnowsHeads(dorcas). Assert dorcasWouldStay(dorcas). }
  }
  Relation dorcasWouldStay(group).
  Rule piran_goes_out when piranOut(piran) and lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 21 and lullFolk(piran) and not dorcasStays(dorcas) { Retract lullFolk(piran). Assert at(piran, sx_taproom). }
  Rule dorcas_moves_in when dorcasWouldStay(dorcas) and not piranOut(piran) and lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 21 and not dorcasStays(dorcas) { Assert dorcasStays(dorcas). Assert lullFolk(dorcas). Assert bedAt(dorcas, piran_shop). Assert dayAt(dorcas, piran_shop). }
  Observe piran_out at sx_taproom when at(piran, sx_taproom) and not lullday() "Behind the bar of the Waiting Woman a quiet man in his thirties with a carver's hands is drawing ale, badly, and Dorcas Trewin is teaching him, and they keep stopping to look at each other.".
  Observe piran_shop_shut at piran_shop when lullOpen() and piranOut(piran) and not at(piran, piran_shop) "Piran's workshop is shut up, the shavings swept. The heads are gone from the shelves: all but one, the youngest, which faces the door.".
  Observe dorcas_lives_in at piran_shop when lullOpen() and dorcasStays(dorcas) "Dorcas Trewin sits by the window of the workshop in her blue gown, not turning her face from the light any more, while Piran carves her.".
  Event piran_keepsake near piran when keeps(piran, keepsake) and madeFor(keepsake, piran) "Piran turns the little carving to the light and looks at it as a carver does, critically, and then not critically at all. He puts it on the shelf with the heads." then { Assert keepsakeKept(keepsake). }
  Event dorcas_keepsake near dorcas when keeps(dorcas, keepsake) and madeFor(keepsake, dorcas) "Dorcas puts the little carving on the shelf behind the bar, beside the old sign, facing the window and the stone." then { Assert keepsakeKept(keepsake). }
}

data/adventures/the-lull/builds.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── What different hands can do here ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Ways into the valley's stories for those who have the craft for them: a priest's words for the dying, which are
  // not bought; a watchful eye on an old man's hands; a thief's way round the wardens; a scholar's way into the
  // Glossary's back room; a woodsman's way to the Brock; a climber's way into the Mill; a bonesetter's way with a hand.

  // A priest's words for the dying: Hester eased, and nothing bought across the Tump.
  Action rites_for_hester(actor: group, site: place) "Sit with Hester Lindsell and say the words for the dying over her" {
    Description "Not to hasten anything: the words that let the dying stop holding on so hard.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hester_room) and at(hester, hester_room) and lullOpen() and capable(actor, rites) and knows(actor, hester_sick) and not hesterEased(hester) and not hesterDead(hester).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert hesterEased(hester). Assert hesterBlessed(hester). Assert tobiasSoftened(tobias). Increase tobiasTrust(tobias) by 1. }
    Result "You sit on the end of the bed and say them, the old words, the ones every priest in Imbar knows in some tongue or other, about rest and about letting go and about the birds. Hester listens with her eyes shut. Halfway through she says, 'Again, that bit,' and you say it again. When you have finished her hands are lying open on the sheet and her face has gone smooth as a plate, and she is asleep, properly asleep, for the first time, Tobias says afterwards, in a month. He does not thank you. He brings you a cup of something, and sits with you, and that is the same thing.".
  }
  Relation hesterBlessed(group).

  // A watchful eye: the old man's hands, while he tells it.
  Action watch_tobias(actor: group, site: place) "Watch Tobias Lindsell's hands while he tells the strike" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(tobias, site) and lullOpen() and capable(actor, insight) and knows(actor, strike_told) and not knows(actor, which_side).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, which_side). Increase tobiasTrust(tobias) by 1. }
    Result "He tells it with his hands, the way weavers do, and you watch them. When the strikers barred the doors, his hands do not bar anything: they throw a shuttle, left to right, right to left, and stop, the way hands stop at a loom when somebody comes in. Every time he says 'I was at the window', his thumb goes to his waistcoat pocket, where a man keeps a coin. He does not know he does it.".
  }

  // A thief's way round: the sheep-walk on the Tump's far side, out of the wardens' sight.
  Action sheep_walk(actor: group, site: place) "Take Simeon round the Tump by the sheep-walk, out of the wardens' sight" {
    Description "A way a shepherd or a thief would see: up the back of the hill and down through the gorse.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, fold_stone) and lullOpen() and capable(actor, stealth) and following(simeon, actor) and not simeonHome(simeon).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert at(actor, strike_post). }
    Result "You leave the road at the stone and go up the back of the Tump through the gorse, bent double, with the old man puffing behind you and laughing under his breath, and come out on the top among the ribbons with the wardens below you on the shoulder looking the other way.".
  }

  // A scholar's way into the Glossary's back room: the boards painted over.
  Discovery gloss_forty "In the Glossary's back room, among the boards the Reeves have had painted over, the old lettering of one still shows through the white under a lamp: GLOSS 40. THAT A GIRL WHO WALKS UP A HILL WITH ONE MAN IS NOT THEREBY WALKING AWAY FROM ANOTHER. And in the corner, very small: S.E.".
  Action read_boards(actor: group, site: place) "Read the old boards in the Glossary's back room, under the paint" {
    Description "Painted-over glosses still show through, to someone who knows the old hands.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, glossary) and lullOpen() and capable(actor, lore) and not knows(actor, gloss_forty).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, gloss_forty). }
    Result "In the back room the boards stand in stacks against the walls, painted over white by order of one Reeve or another, and with a lamp held low and slantwise the old letters come up through the paint like fish under ice. There is a gloss on whether a sigh is speech; one on whether a dog can be thanked; the famous nine hundred and twelve, which somebody has painted over three times. And one very old board, much smaller than the rest, that you read twice.".
  }
  Topic hester_gloss with hester "Tell Hester Lindsell you found Gloss forty in the Glossary's back room" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, gloss_forty) and not hesterDead(hester) once {
    Says "Hester laughs until she has to hold her side, and then lies back. 'Under the paint,' she says. 'They never could get rid of anything in that place, only cover it.' She is quiet. 'He was right, you know. I went up the hill with Tobias and I never walked away from Simeon. I just never went anywhere with him.' She turns her head on the pillow. 'If you see him, tell him I said held.'".
    On discuss { Increase hesterTrust(hester) by 1. Assert hesterAsksSimeon(hester). }
  }

  // A woodsman's way to the Brock: his drinking place, where he can be met without coming to his door.
  Action track_brock(actor: group, site: place) "Follow the Old Brock's road down to where he drinks, and leave the comb there" {
    Description "A badger keeps to his own roads. Find the one to water, and you need not face him at his door.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hanger_path) and capable(actor, woodcraft) and carries(actor, comb) and able(brock) and not brockTruce(brock).
    Time 6.
    On success { Spend comb_kind from actor. Assert at(comb, limbo). Assert brockTruce(brock). Assert tolerates(brock, actor). }
    Result "His road is easy to find once you see it: a groove in the leaf-litter worn hand-deep, going down through the beeches to a spring under a root. You leave the comb on a stone there and go back up the slope and wait. He comes at dusk, as big as a pony, scarred, slow, and finds it, and eats it, and lifts his long grey head and looks straight up the slope at where you are sitting, for a long time. Then he goes back up his road, and the next time you meet him he only looks.".
  }

  // A climber's way into the Mill: the hoist-beam over the loading door, up the outside to the bell loft.
  Passage hoist "the old hoist-beam, up the outside of the Mill" is passage between mill_yard and bell_loft taking 20 minutes needing climbing or rope.
  Observe hoist_seen at mill_yard as feature when true "High on the Mill's end wall a hoist-beam sticks out over a loading door at the top floor, with a stub of chain still hanging from it.".

  // A bonesetter's hands: Corin's broken hand set straight on the bank.
  Relation corinMended(group).
  Action set_corin_hand(actor: group, site: place) "Set Corin Lindsell's broken hand properly, here on the bank" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(corin, site) and corinHurt(corin) and capable(actor, mending) and not corinMended(corin).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert corinMended(corin). }
    Result "You kneel on the bank and take her hand, and she lets you, white to the lips, and you feel for the broken ends and draw them true and splint the hand with two straight pieces of the new oak and a strip of somebody's apron. 'Will it,' she says, and stops. 'Yes,' you say. You mean it, and in the Lull that is worth something.".
  }
  Rule fate_corin_mended when accounting() and corinHurt(corin) and corinMended(corin) and not spreadFact(fate_corin) says "Corin Lindsell's hand was set on the bank of the leat by a Sixer, and mended straight. She has made a clock since for whoever it was, and it is waiting on the bench in her window, with no card, ticking, for whenever they come back." { Assert spreadFact(fate_corin). }
}

data/adventures/the-lull/clock.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── The Lull-count ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Imbar counts thirty days to a month and no weeks. The Lull keeps a sennight of its own, counted from the Hallowing,
  // and Sixways keeps it for the Lull, notched on the Fold-stone. lullCycle is the day of that sennight (0 to 6) and
  // turns at midnight; the seventh, 6, is the Lullday. The valley is open from six in the morning of its day until
  // midnight; the rest of the week it is folded.
  Measure lullCycle(clock). Relation midnightTurned(clock).
  Initially Set lullCycle(clock) to 4.
  Rule lull_midnight when hour(clock) == 0 and not midnightTurned(clock) { Assert midnightTurned(clock). Increase lullCycle(clock) by 1. }
  Rule lull_wraps when lullCycle(clock) >= 7 { Set lullCycle(clock) to 0. }
  Rule lull_unturn when hour(clock) != 0 and midnightTurned(clock) { Retract midnightTurned(clock). }
  Query lullday() means lullCycle(clock) == 6.
  // Once the week has come back to the valley (weekReturned), it is open every day; its law keeps the Lullday, or
  // nothing, as the Working Day went (lawGone).
  Relation weekReturned(place). Relation lawGone(place).
  Query lullOpen() means lullCycle(clock) == 6 and hour(clock) >= 6 or weekReturned(lull_country).
  Query folded() means not lullOpen().
  Query lawDay() means lullCycle(clock) == 6 and not lawGone(lull_country).
  // The Lull's dusk: eight in the evening, when the starlings go over the Tump and what was not meant comes apart.
  Query lullDusk() means lawDay() and lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 20.
  Query lullEvening() means lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 19.

  // How many Lulldays have dawned (lullCount), the watch of the next dawn (lullNextDawn), and the watches until it
  // (untilLull), which is how long a night in the Lull lasts, or a wait at the stone. The first is reckoned from the
  // hour the country is first reached, and set exactly at each midnight that begins a Lullday; at each dawn the next is
  // a week on. (A country placed in a world counts its watches from its own first morning; only differences of watches
  // are read here, never a watch of the world's.)
  Measure lullCount(clock). Measure lullNextDawn(clock). Measure untilLull(clock). Relation dawnReckoned(clock).
  Rule lull_reckons when not dawnReckoned(clock) { Set lullNextDawn(clock) to watch(clock) + (24 - hour(clock)) * 6 + (5 - lullCycle(clock)) * 144 + 36. Assert dawnReckoned(clock). }
  Rule lull_eve when lullCycle(clock) == 6 and hour(clock) == 0 and not eveReckoned(clock) { Set lullNextDawn(clock) to watch(clock) + 36. Assert eveReckoned(clock). }
  Rule lull_eve_ends when hour(clock) != 0 and eveReckoned(clock) { Retract eveReckoned(clock). }
  Relation eveReckoned(clock).
  Rule lull_dawns when lullCycle(clock) == 6 and hour(clock) >= 6 and lullNextDawn(clock) <= watch(clock) { Set lullNextDawn(clock) to watch(clock) + 1008. Increase lullCount(clock) by 1. }
  Rule lull_counts_down when untilLull(clock) != lullNextDawn(clock) - watch(clock) { Set untilLull(clock) to lullNextDawn(clock) - watch(clock). }

  // ── The story's Lulldays ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The story is told in Lulldays counted from the first the company spends inside: the first (I), the next (II), and
  // the Working Day (III), which Corin names on the first evening for the Lullday after next. Nothing in the valley
  // waits for the company after that.
  Relation cameIn(group). Measure firstLull(clock).
  Rule came_in_first when lullOpen() and within(party, lull_country) and inLull(party) and not cameIn(party) { Assert cameIn(party). Set firstLull(clock) to lullCount(clock). }
  Query storyDay(n: entity) means cameIn(party) and lullCount(clock) - firstLull(clock) + 1 == lullDayNumber(n).
  Measure lullDayNumber(entity).
  Entity day_one: fact "the first Lullday". Entity day_two: fact "the second Lullday". Entity day_three: fact "the Working Day".
  Initially Set lullDayNumber(day_one) to 1. Initially Set lullDayNumber(day_two) to 2. Initially Set lullDayNumber(day_three) to 3.
  Query dayOne() means cameIn(party) and lullCount(clock) == firstLull(clock).
  Query dayTwo() means cameIn(party) and lullCount(clock) == firstLull(clock) + 1.
  Query dayThree() means cameIn(party) and lullCount(clock) == firstLull(clock) + 2.
  Query pastThree() means cameIn(party) and lullCount(clock) >= firstLull(clock) + 3.
  // Whether the company is in the valley (not Sixways, which is the world's).
  Relation lullRoom(place).
  Query inLull(g: group) means at(g, ?p) and lullRoom(?p).
  Query inSixnight() means folded() and inLull(party).

  // ── The fold ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Folded, the valley is dark and its people asleep where they lie down at night, and cannot be woken. Whoever is in
  // the fold does not hunger: nobody eats in a day that is not kept.
  Rule fold_darkens when folded() and lullRoom(?p) and not unlit(?p) { Assert unlit(?p). }
  Rule fold_lightens when lullOpen() and lullRoom(?p) and unlit(?p) and not alwaysDark(?p) { Retract unlit(?p). }
  Relation alwaysDark(place).
  Relation lullFolk(group). Relation bedAt(group, place). Relation dayAt(group, place). Relation held(group).
  Query routine(x: group) means lullFolk(x) and able(x) and not held(x) and not travelsWith(x, party) and not following(x, party).
  Rule folk_sleep when folded() and lullFolk(?x) and able(?x) and not asleep(?x) and not travelsWith(?x, party) { Assert asleep(?x). }
  Rule folk_to_bed when folded() and routine(?x) and bedAt(?x, ?p) and not at(?x, ?p) { Assert at(?x, ?p). }
  Rule folk_wake when lullOpen() and lullFolk(?x) and asleep(?x) { Retract asleep(?x). }
  Rule folk_day when lullOpen() and hour(clock) < 19 and routine(?x) and dayAt(?x, ?p) and not at(?x, ?p) { Assert at(?x, ?p). }
  Rule folk_table when lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 21 and routine(?x) and dayAt(?x, ?d) and not at(?x, green) { Assert at(?x, green). }
  Rule folk_home when lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 21 and routine(?x) and bedAt(?x, ?p) and not at(?x, ?p) { Assert at(?x, ?p). }

  Relation foldFast(group).
  Rule fold_fast when inSixnight() and eats(party) { Retract eats(party). Assert foldFast(party). }
  Rule fold_fast_ends when foldFast(party) and not inSixnight() { Assert eats(party). Retract foldFast(party). }

  // ── Sleeping Lull-fashion ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Lie down in the Lull after dusk with your hands open, and the Lull's night takes you through the six days it does
  // not keep, and you wake on its next morning, a week older outside. A bed bought or a camp made is a night like any
  // other, and ends in the morning, in the dark.
  Relation sleptLull(group). Measure weeksAsleep(group).
  Action lull_sleep(actor: group, site: place) "Lie down Lull-fashion, hands open, and let the Lull's night take you" {
    Description "You will wake on the Lull's next morning. Outside, a week will have gone by.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and lullRoom(site) and lullEvening() and not alwaysDark(site) and not weekReturned(lull_country).
    Time untilLull(clock).
    On success { Assert sleptLull(actor). Increase weeksAsleep(actor) by 1. Increase lastSlept(actor) by 1008. Retract weary(actor). }
    Result "Last night you lay down with your hands open, as they showed you, and the starlings' noise went over and away, and you did not hear it stop. You woke to the same light, birds again, and the smell of bread from the Long Table. Nothing had moved. Your beard, or your nails, or a cut on your hand that has healed, says otherwise: outside, it has been a week.".
  }
  // In the Sixnight, open hands are the strikers' sign: lie down so and the six days take you out the other side.
  Action sixnight_sleep(actor: group, site: place) "Lie down with your hands open, and wait for the Lull's morning" {
    Description "The six days will go over you, as over everyone else in the valley.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and lullRoom(site) and inSixnight() and knows(actor, open_hands) and not threatened(actor).
    Time untilLull(clock).
    Interrupted when threatened(actor).
    On success { Assert sleptLull(actor). Increase lastSlept(actor) by 1008. Retract weary(actor). }
    Result "You lie down in the dark with your hands open, palms up, the way the strikers lay down on the Tump, and the dark is very long and does not touch you, and then the starlings are going over and it is morning.".
  }
  Discovery open_hands "In the Lull you lie down to sleep with your hands open, palms up, as the strikers lay on the Tump: then the Lull's night takes you through to its next morning. Whoever lies down otherwise, or not at all, is awake in the six days it does not keep.".

  // ── Waiting at the stone ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // How long the wait was, for the sleep it stood for: the longest wait ahead seen at the stone.
  Measure stoneMark(group).
  Rule stone_marks when at(party, fold_stone) and folded() and stoneMark(party) < untilLull(clock) { Set stoneMark(party) to untilLull(clock). }
  Rule stone_unmarks when not at(party, fold_stone) and stoneMark(party) > 0 { Set stoneMark(party) to 0. }
  Action stone_wait(actor: group, site: place) "Sit down by the Fold-stone and wait for the Lull" {
    Description "Until the road goes down into the valley, at six on its morning.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, fold_stone) and folded() and not inLull(actor).
    Time untilLull(clock).
    Interrupted when threatened(actor).
    On success { Increase lastSlept(actor) by stoneMark(actor). Retract weary(actor). Set stoneMark(actor) to 0. }
    Result "You sit with your back to the stone and watch the road go round the bare hill and come back, all day, and sleep in your coat against the stone, and wake, and watch it again; people come and go past you from Sixways and do not remark it, because people do. Then one morning at six the light changes, the way it does, and there is another road, going down.".
  }
}

data/adventures/the-lull/company.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  Company party "Your company" of 1 to 3 at march_road.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 14. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 2.
}

data/adventures/the-lull/endings.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── The Watching of the Working Day ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At the Working Day's dusk the town watches the bridge, and every Hand's work stands or falls in front of it. The
  // Lull ends if one of those who asked for it means it to, with enough of the young who mean it beside him; whether
  // its law goes with it depends on why he came.
  Rule working_hands when working() and hour(clock) >= 6 and not joins(corin) and not wardensBroke(club) { Assert joins(corin). Assert means(corin). Assert joins(davy). Assert means(davy). Assert joins(club). Assert means(club). }
  Relation counted(group).
  Rule count_hand when working() and hour(clock) >= 19 and joins(?x) and means(?x) and not counted(?x) and not wardensBroke(club) { Assert counted(?x). Increase handsMeaning(lull_country) by 1. }
  Measure handsMeaning(place).
  Relation outcomeMonday(place). Relation outcomeSeventh(place). Relation outcomeSunday(place). Relation outcomeMeant(place). Relation outcomeBroken(place).
  Query lullEnds() means joins(tobias) and handsMeaning(lull_country) >= 5 and not wardensBroke(club) and not killedMeant(party).
  Rule working_meant when dayThree() and workingBegun(lull_country) and lullDusk() and killedMeant(party) and not workingOver(lull_country) { Assert workingOver(lull_country). Assert outcomeMeant(lull_country). }
  Rule working_broken when dayThree() and workingBegun(lull_country) and lullDusk() and wardensBroke(club) and not killedMeant(party) and not workingOver(lull_country) { Assert workingOver(lull_country). Assert outcomeBroken(lull_country). }
  Rule working_holds_seventh when dayThree() and workingBegun(lull_country) and lullDusk() and lullEnds() and not tobiasGrief(tobias) and not workingOver(lull_country) { Assert workingOver(lull_country). Assert outcomeSeventh(lull_country). Assert bridgeBuilt(club). Assert state(bridge_gap, mended). }
  Rule working_holds_monday when dayThree() and workingBegun(lull_country) and lullDusk() and lullEnds() and tobiasGrief(tobias) and not workingOver(lull_country) { Assert workingOver(lull_country). Assert outcomeMonday(lull_country). Assert bridgeBuilt(club). Assert state(bridge_gap, mended). }
  Rule working_sunday when dayThree() and workingBegun(lull_country) and lullDusk() and not lullEnds() and not wardensBroke(club) and not killedMeant(party) and not workingOver(lull_country) { Assert workingOver(lull_country). Assert outcomeSunday(lull_country). Assert bridgeBuilt(club). Assert state(bridge_gap, mended). }
  Rule working_called_off when dayThree() and lullDusk() and clubDisbanded(club) and not workingOver(lull_country) { Assert workingOver(lull_country). Assert outcomeSunday(lull_country). }
  Query watchingWorking() means (at(party, green) or at(party, mill_bridge)).
  // What the Watching sees, told to whoever is there.
  Rule watched_paid when workingOver(lull_country) and joins(folk) and lullDusk() and dayThree() and watchingWorking() and not spreadFact(paid_told) and not wardensBroke(club)
    says "The sun goes off the Tump, and the Long Table, which has been carried down to the leat bank, holds its breath. At the stone-end of the bridge, where the townsfolk worked for Haskett's wages, the stone comes apart from the stone and slides into the leat, a course at a time, with a sound like a cart tipping; and from a dozen aprons the coins rise and go away up the Tump road in the dusk like starlings, home to Sixways. The people who were paid stand looking at their hands." { Assert spreadFact(paid_told). }
  Entity paid_told: fact "the paid work".
  Rule watched_stands when workingOver(lull_country) and bridgeBuilt(club) and lullDusk() and dayThree() and watchingWorking() and not spreadFact(stands_told)
    says "And the rest stands. The new oak lies across the leat from pier to pier, rough, and a little crooked where Davy Mote set it, and the stones at the Mill end are the stones the young carried meaning it, and they do not move. Corin Lindsell walks out onto the middle of it, slowly, and stamps, once, and it holds her. Behind her the Mill stands dark across the water, and for the first time in fifty-seven years there is a way to its door." { Assert spreadFact(stands_told). }
  Entity stands_told: fact "the bridge stands".
  Rule watched_seventh when outcomeSeventh(lull_country) and lullDusk() and dayThree() and watchingWorking() and not spreadFact(seventh_told)
    says "Then the starlings come over, as they do every dusk, and go over the Tump, and come back. They come back. They come down onto the new bridge in hundreds, onto the rails and the stones and Tobias Lindsell's shoulders, and stay there, talking. Up at the Mill there is a sound like a door taking a breath. Nobody moves. Tobias says, so that only Corin and the birds can hear it: 'Monday, then.' And Corin says: 'Tuesday too.' Midnight will come, and go, and something tells everyone at that table that tomorrow will be tomorrow." { Assert spreadFact(seventh_told). Assert weekReturned(lull_country). }
  Rule watched_hester when outcomeSeventh(lull_country) and lullDusk() and dayThree() and at(hester, mill_bridge) and watchingWorking() and not spreadFact(hester_watched_told)
    says "On the bank Hester Lindsell, in her quilt of strikers' shirts, has her eyes open, and is laughing without any sound, and has one hand out of the quilt, open, palm up, on her knee." { Assert spreadFact(hester_watched_told). }
  Entity hester_watched_told: fact "Hester watched".
  Rule watched_monday when outcomeMonday(lull_country) and lullDusk() and dayThree() and not spreadFact(monday_told)
    says "Then the starlings come over, as they do every dusk, and go over the Tump, and do not come back. The sky over the valley is empty of them, all at once, the way a room is empty when someone has left it. Up at the Mill the great doors open, by themselves, outward, and in the dusk across the new bridge come the Hands: a hundred shapes of grey lint in the shape of weavers, walking, not hurrying, and they go past the Long Table without turning their no-faces to it, up the Tump road, over the shoulder, and away out of the valley into the world, where the work is. Tobias Lindsell watches them go with his hands open on his knees. 'Let it end,' he said. It has." { Assert spreadFact(monday_told). Assert weekReturned(lull_country). Assert lawGone(lull_country). }
  Rule watched_sunday when outcomeSunday(lull_country) and lullDusk() and dayThree() and not clubDisbanded(club) and watchingWorking() and not spreadFact(sunday_told)
    says "Then the starlings come over, and go over the Tump, and the sun goes, and the bridge stands, and the night comes down on Linger the way it always has, and at the Long Table people start, a little sheepishly, to eat. Corin sits on the middle of her bridge with her feet over the water. 'It holds,' she says. 'It holds, and it's still Lullday.' She does not say it bitterly. She says it as if she were trying it for size." { Assert spreadFact(sunday_told). }
  Rule watched_broken when outcomeBroken(lull_country) and lullDusk() and dayThree() and watchingWorking() and not spreadFact(broken_told)
    says "There is nothing on the leat to watch. The timbers have gone down toward the Swallow. The Long Table is quiet, and eats, and does not look at the young of Linger, who sit at the bottom with the children, or at Corin Lindsell, whose right hand is bound in a cloth and will not, the bonesetter says, ever be quite a clockmaker's hand again." { Assert spreadFact(broken_told). }
  Rule watched_meant when outcomeMeant(lull_country) and lullDusk() and dayThree() and watchingWorking() and not spreadFact(meant_told)
    says "Nobody sets anything out on the grass tonight. They have carried the dead to the chapel, and laid them under the rafters full of starlings, and at the Watching the Long Table sits with the dusk coming down and watches the chapel arch instead, the whole town, the way it watches what was made that day, to see whether it will hold. It holds. In the Lull it always does, when it was meant." { Assert spreadFact(meant_told). }
  Entity seventh_told: fact "the Seventh Day". Entity monday_told: fact "Monday". Entity sunday_told: fact "the long Sunday". Entity broken_told: fact "the broken bridge". Entity meant_told: fact "what was meant".

  // ── Afterwards ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At midnight after the Working Day the book closes on what became of each person, and then on the valley. The
  // valley goes on: its road open every day if the week came back, one in seven if not.
  Query accounting() means workingOver(lull_country) and cameIn(party) and (pastThree() or dayThree() and hour(clock) >= 23).
  Rule fate_corin_seventh when accounting() and outcomeSeventh(lull_country) and not spreadFact(fate_corin) says "Corin Lindsell has a workshop at the end of the Shift Bridge, in the old weighbridge house, with a clock over the door that is right twice a day, which is more than any clock in the Lull managed for fifty-seven years. On Lulldays the clocks she makes for wages come apart at sunset, and she does not mind, and the ones she makes for people do not." { Assert spreadFact(fate_corin). }
  Rule fate_corin_monday when accounting() and outcomeMonday(lull_country) and not spreadFact(fate_corin) says "Corin Lindsell sells clocks in Sixways and in the mill towns, good ones, at a good price, and they keep time. She does not go to the Watching; there is no Watching now. Some evenings she stands on the Shift Bridge and listens for the starlings." { Assert spreadFact(fate_corin). }
  Rule fate_corin_held when accounting() and outcomeSunday(lull_country) and corinClockHeld(corin) and not spreadFact(fate_corin) says "Corin Lindsell still makes clocks, in the Lull, for people; they hold. She is making one for every member of the Old Shift, in order of age, and says she will start on the Club when she has finished, and then on everybody else, and that it should take her about fifty-seven years." { Assert spreadFact(fate_corin). }
  Rule fate_corin_hurt when accounting() and corinHurt(corin) and not spreadFact(fate_corin) says "Corin Lindsell's hand mended crooked. She has taught Davy Mote to cut the wheels, and sits beside him at the bench and tells him what he is doing wrong, and the clocks still come apart at sunset, both of theirs." { Assert spreadFact(fate_corin). }
  Rule fate_corin_sunday when accounting() and not spreadFact(fate_corin) says "Corin Lindsell went out over the Tump a Lullday after the Working Day with a bag of tools, to make clocks in the world. She comes back for the Watching once a year, her count, and every time Linger is a week older and she is a year, and every time her grandfather says, You look tired." { Assert spreadFact(fate_corin). }
  Entity fate_corin: fact "Corin".
  Rule fate_tobias_love when accounting() and joins(tobias) and bridgeBuilt(club) and not tobiasGrief(tobias) and not spreadFact(fate_tobias) says "Tobias Lindsell keeps the Shift Bridge. He sits on a chair at the Mill end with Corin's clock in his waistcoat, and tells the strike to anyone who crosses, and tells it, now, from the right side of the window." { Assert spreadFact(fate_tobias). }
  Rule fate_tobias_broken when accounting() and joins(tobias) and wardensBroke(club) and not spreadFact(fate_tobias) says "Tobias Lindsell went into the leat after the timbers, at eighty-two, and brought one out, and set it on the bank, and sat on it. He sits on it still, most Lulldays, with Corin's clock in his waistcoat, and tells the strike from the right side of the window, to whoever will listen." { Assert spreadFact(fate_tobias). }
  Rule fate_tobias_grief when accounting() and tobiasGrief(tobias) and not spreadFact(fate_tobias) says "Tobias Lindsell died in the autumn, of being eighty-two in a valley where time had started again, quite quickly, in his chair by the empty bed. They found his hands open." { Assert spreadFact(fate_tobias). }
  Rule fate_tobias_none when accounting() and not spreadFact(fate_tobias) says "Tobias Lindsell sits by his window in the Lull and tells the strike to whoever asks, always from the window, and does not say which side." { Assert spreadFact(fate_tobias). }
  Entity fate_tobias: fact "Tobias".
  Rule fate_hester_eased when accounting() and hesterEased(hester) and not hesterDead(hester) and not spreadFact(fate_hester) says "Hester Lindsell has her poppy from Ruth Coll every Lullday, carried in by whoever is going, and is dying as slowly as ever, and minds it less, and says so." { Assert spreadFact(fate_hester). }
  Rule fate_hester_sat when accounting() and hesterSat(hester) and not hesterDead(hester) and not spreadFact(fate_hester) says "Hester Lindsell lived through the first night because a stranger had taken Tobias's chair, and has not forgotten whose. She is dying as slowly as ever. She asks for her Monday when the visitors are fewer, and Tobias leaves the chair empty now, in case." { Assert spreadFact(fate_hester). }
  Rule fate_hester_you when accounting() and diedBy(hester, party) and not spreadFact(fate_hester) says "Hester Lindsell had her Monday from a Sixer's hand, and the Lull never asked whose. Tobias knows. On your account he says nothing at all, which in him is a kind of thanks." { Assert spreadFact(fate_hester). }
  Rule fate_hester_tobias when accounting() and diedBy(hester, tobias) and not spreadFact(fate_hester) says "Hester Lindsell is buried on the Tump under the Strike Post, by the striker's grave of Nell Lumb, her little sister. The Lull believes the wasting took her." { Assert spreadFact(fate_hester). }
  Entity fate_hester: fact "Hester".
  Rule fate_simeon_with when accounting() and simeonWith(hester) and not spreadFact(fate_simeon) says "Simeon Eddowes sat with Hester Lumb at the end, as she drank what she had asked for, and held her hand, and told her a gloss he had been keeping sixty years, and she laughed at it. He lives at the Glossary now, and paints, very slowly, and every board he paints holds." { Assert spreadFact(fate_simeon). }
  Rule fate_simeon_home when accounting() and simeonHome(simeon) and not spreadFact(fate_simeon) says "Simeon Eddowes lives at the Glossary, unbanned by nobody in particular, and argues every day with Aldith Mote, and loses." { Assert spreadFact(fate_simeon). }
  Rule fate_simeon_out when accounting() and not simeonHome(simeon) and not spreadFact(fate_simeon) says "Simeon Eddowes writes his glosses in Exiles' Row, facing the stone." { Assert spreadFact(fate_simeon). }
  Entity fate_simeon: fact "Simeon".
  Rule fate_abel_wed when accounting() and wedded(wenna) and not spreadFact(fate_abel) says "Abel and Wenna Rooke are on the march road with Dulcie and the cart, with a box of green candles under the seat, going somewhere. Wenna has seen the sea. It was, she says, too big, and she has made Abel take her back twice." { Assert spreadFact(fate_abel). }
  Rule fate_abel_week when accounting() and weekReturned(lull_country) and not wedded(wenna) and not spreadFact(fate_abel) says "Abel Rooke carts for Linger now, six days in seven, and Wenna Spurling rides beside him on the seat to Sixways and back, which is not the sea, she says, but it is a road." { Assert spreadFact(fate_abel). }
  Rule fate_abel_not when accounting() and not spreadFact(fate_abel) says "Abel Rooke has stopped making chairs. Wenna Spurling dips candles in the chandlery in the Lull, and smells the road on every Sixer's boots, and says nothing." { Assert spreadFact(fate_abel). }
  Entity fate_abel: fact "Abel and Wenna".
  Rule fate_dorcas_week when accounting() and weekReturned(lull_country) and not dorcasStays(dorcas) and not piranOut(piran) and not spreadFact(fate_dorcas) says "Piran Trewin walks out over the Tump to the Waiting Woman every evening now, because there is an every evening; and he is getting older at the same pace as his wife, at last, and says it is the best thing that ever happened to him, and she says he is a fool." { Assert spreadFact(fate_dorcas). }
  Rule fate_dorcas_out when accounting() and piranOut(piran) and not spreadFact(fate_dorcas) says "Piran Trewin keeps the bar of the Waiting Woman beside his wife, and draws a poor pint, and has carved a new sign for the inn: a woman at a window, sixty, in a blue gown, looking out." { Assert spreadFact(fate_dorcas). }
  Rule fate_dorcas_in when accounting() and dorcasStays(dorcas) and not spreadFact(fate_dorcas) says "Dorcas Trewin lives in the Lull now, at her husband's workshop, and is ill a day a week instead of seven, and sits for him at the window, not turning her face from the light." { Assert spreadFact(fate_dorcas). }
  Rule fate_dorcas_none when accounting() and not spreadFact(fate_dorcas) says "Dorcas Trewin walks in over the Tump every Lullday, and Piran tells her she looks tired, and she tells him it is the walk." { Assert spreadFact(fate_dorcas). }
  Entity fate_dorcas: fact "Dorcas and Piran".
  Rule fate_houses_dead when accounting() and dead(hobday) and not spreadFact(fate_houses) says "Lettice Pryce gives nothing to anybody now. She sits in the parlour with the cabinets and the carpet, and Mabyn Gale comes over every Lullday and sits with her, and neither of them says a word about generosity, and it holds." { Assert spreadFact(fate_houses). }
  Rule fate_houses_peace when accounting() and housesAtPeace(mabyn) and not spreadFact(fate_houses) says "The Pryces and the Gales keep one open house between them, on alternate Lulldays, and the guests of both are fed half as much and twice as well." { Assert spreadFact(fate_houses). }
  Rule fate_houses_given when accounting() and pryceHouseGiven(lettice) and not spreadFact(fate_houses) says "Mabyn Gale gave the Pryces' house back to Lettice Pryce at the next Watching, and it held, because Mabyn meant it; and Lettice has not forgiven her for that either." { Assert spreadFact(fate_houses). }
  Rule fate_houses_none when accounting() and not spreadFact(fate_houses) says "Lettice Pryce gave the Glossary a weathercock in the spring. Mabyn Gale gave it a wind." { Assert spreadFact(fate_houses). }
  Entity fate_houses: fact "the Open Houses".
  Rule fate_nan_out when accounting() and (nanExposed(nan) or nanBanned(nan)) and not spreadFact(fate_nan) says "Quick Nan sells pasties on Sixways street and not over the Tump. The bright ribbons on the Strike Post have all gone; the Lull blue is back, ugly and holding." { Assert spreadFact(fate_nan). }
  Rule fate_nan_reformed when accounting() and nanReformed(nan) and not spreadFact(fate_nan) says "Quick Nan sells pasties on the Green on Lulldays, eaten before sunset, and nothing else; and she put six coin in the chapel basin for the mothers, and the Glosser says it held." { Assert spreadFact(fate_nan). }
  Rule fate_nan_partner when accounting() and nanPartner(nan) and not spreadFact(fate_nan) says "Quick Nan's ribbons still go off the Strike Post at sunset, and the mothers of Linger still sit in the chapel afterwards, and the Glossers still say it is a hard year." { Assert spreadFact(fate_nan). }
  Rule fate_nan_week when accounting() and weekReturned(lull_country) and not spreadFact(fate_nan) says "Quick Nan has a stall on Linger green every day of the week now, and sells what she sells, and it stays sold, and she finds she misses the race against the sunset more than she can say." { Assert spreadFact(fate_nan). }
  Rule fate_nan_none when accounting() and not spreadFact(fate_nan) says "Quick Nan still goes in at six and out by four." { Assert spreadFact(fate_nan). }
  Entity fate_nan: fact "Nan".
  Rule fate_linnet_stay when accounting() and stayPromised(party) and not spreadFact(fate_linnet) says "In the music room over the Open Hand there is a tune that everybody in Linger knows, that has a next bit. Linnet Gale plays it at every Watching, and looks down the Long Table to where you sit." { Assert spreadFact(fate_linnet). }
  Rule fate_linnet_come when accounting() and linnetWillCome(linnet) and not spreadFact(fate_linnet) says "Linnet Gale has her fiddle and her boots and a pack Mabyn filled, and is waiting at the stone for you to ask her again, on the road, so that she knows you meant it." { Assert spreadFact(fate_linnet). }
  Rule fate_linnet_tune when accounting() and linnetTune(linnet) and not spreadFact(fate_linnet) says "Linnet Gale's tune with the next bit is sung at the Watching every Lullday, by people who do not know who it was made for." { Assert spreadFact(fate_linnet). }
  Rule fate_linnet_week when accounting() and weekReturned(lull_country) and not spreadFact(fate_linnet) says "Linnet Gale's tunes are remembered now, because there is a tomorrow to remember them in. She plays Monday's on Tuesday, and people know it, and sing it back to her wrong." { Assert spreadFact(fate_linnet). }
  Rule fate_linnet_none when accounting() and not spreadFact(fate_linnet) says "Linnet Gale makes a tune a day in the music room over the Open Hand, and in the morning it is gone." { Assert spreadFact(fate_linnet). }
  Entity fate_linnet: fact "Linnet".

  Ending seventh_day "The Seventh Day" when accounting() and outcomeSeventh(lull_country) "Midnight came to the Lull and went, and the starlings did not stop, and in the morning it was Monday. Nobody in Linger under fifty-seven had ever seen one. They did not know what to do with it, and mostly they rested, out of habit, and some of them went down to the Shift Bridge and stood on it. The week came back to the valley, and the Lullday stayed in it: one day in seven the law still holds there, and whatever is done without meaning it comes apart at sunset, and people walk in from Sixways on that day, now, to rest, and to see what holds. The road is open every day. The Fold-stone has stopped being notched. Somebody has carved on it, under all the rows of seven: AND THEN MONDAY.".
  Ending monday "Monday" when accounting() and outcomeMonday(lull_country) "Midnight came to the Lull and went, and it was Monday, and then Tuesday, and then it was a valley like any other, with a mill in it that Mercer Haskett has bought from nobody in particular and set going. Things made there for wages hold, now, and so does everything else. The Old Shift began to age at the world's pace, and are going, one by one; the young are learning to hurry. On the Tump the ribbons on the Strike Post fade, and no new ones are tied. In the mill towns, they say, there are grey workers on the roads who will do any work at all, without faces, and nobody asks where they came from.".
  Ending long_sunday "The Long Sunday" when accounting() and outcomeSunday(lull_country) "Midnight came to the Lull, and the starlings stopped in the middle of a note, and the lanterns went out, and it was the six days it does not keep. The Shift Bridge stands across the leat, made meaning it, to a mill nobody goes into. The next Lullday was Lullday, and the one after. The road goes down from the Fold-stone one day in seven, and Sixways notches the stone, and in the valley it is the holy day, still, as it was asked, and nobody can say whether the asking is still meant, or only still kept.".
  Ending broken_bridge "The Bridge in the Leat" when accounting() and outcomeBroken(lull_country) "Midnight came, and the starlings stopped, and the Lull folded up its six days as it always has. The timbers of the Shift Bridge went down the Idle into the Swallow and under the hill and came out, they say, in Sixways, in the spring behind the Waiting Woman. Nobody in the Lull speaks of the Working Day. The Rest-wardens fine nobody for anything for a long time afterwards. The warden who broke Corin Lindsell's hand goes to the Watching every Lullday and sits at the bottom of the Table, with the children.".
  Ending what_was_meant "What Was Meant" when accounting() and outcomeMeant(lull_country) "In the Lull you can only be killed by somebody who means it. On the Working Day somebody was. The bridge was not finished; the work came to nothing either way, and the Lull is the Lull, and the dead are buried on the Tump under the Strike Post among the ribbons. The town does not speak of whose hand it was. At the Watching, every Lullday, there is a place left at the Long Table, and something set out on the grass in front of it, and it holds.".

  // ── What the company grows by ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Milestone m_first_lull "walked into the Lull" worth 50 when cameIn(party).
  Milestone m_watching "sat through a Watching" worth 25 when sawWatching(party).
  Relation sawWatching(group).
  Rule watching_seen when lullDusk() and at(party, green) and not sawWatching(party) { Assert sawWatching(party). }
  Milestone m_law "found what holds in the Lull" worth 150 when knows(party, meaning_law).
  Milestone m_sixnight "lived through the Sixnight" worth 100 when sixnightLived(party).
  Milestone m_beam "read the strikers' beam" worth 50 when knows(party, beam_names).
  Milestone m_window "heard which side of the window" worth 100 when knows(party, tobias_inside).
  Milestone m_wedding "saw Abel and Wenna wed" worth 100 when wedded(wenna).
  Milestone m_heads "told Dorcas and Piran the truth" worth 75 when piranKnowsIll(piran) or dorcasKnowsHeads(dorcas).
  Milestone m_ribbons "set the mothers of Linger right" worth 100 when jenetHealed(jenet).
  Milestone m_brock "settled the Old Brock" worth 100 when brockFed(brock) or brockGone(brock) or dead(brock) and not bountyTaken(party).
  Milestone m_clock "saw Corin's clock hold" worth 150 when corinClockHeld(corin).
  Milestone m_overseer "faced the Overseer" worth 150 when overseerBroken(overseer) or state(pay_chest, open).
  Milestone m_hester "answered Hester Lindsell" worth 100 when hesterEased(hester) or hesterSat(hester) or diedBy(hester, party).
  Milestone m_houses "ended the war of the Open Houses" worth 75 when housesAtPeace(mabyn) or pryceHouseGiven(lettice).
  Milestone m_bridge "worked on the Shift Bridge" worth 100 when workedBridge(party).
  Milestone m_working "saw the Working Day through" worth 200 when workingOver(lull_country) and cameIn(party).
}

data/adventures/the-lull/fellowship.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── The Account, kept: what each of a company sees in the Lull, and what a cleric can do that nobody else can ───────
  // The count is the sennight; its keeper is the Fold-stone and, inside the valley, the Old Shift; its first page is the
  // war that wanted cloth, which nobody can now name and which this file does not try to. What a company of several
  // callings finds is the cost of the count: who was inside the Mill, who sits with the dying, who is not asked.

  // ── Voices ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation heardPiers(group). Relation heardBrock(group). Relation heardBeam(group). Relation heardWasting(group). Relation heardBirds(group).

  Rule voice_piers at mill_bridge when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_warrior) and awake(?m) and at(party, mill_bridge) and not bridgeBuilt(club) and not heardPiers(party)
    says "{?m} walks to the edge of the leat and looks at the two piers for a long time, and then at the eight young people on the near end, who are watching {?m} with the hope of the very bored. 'The piers are sound,' {?m} says. 'Dressed stone, laid dry, and not a course moved in fifty-seven years. It wants oak, forty feet of it, and ropes, and a day's honest hauling from people who know which end of a timber is which.' {?m} glances at them. 'They do not. They would be glad to learn.'" {
    Assert heardPiers(party).
  }
  Rule voice_sett at hanger_path when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and awake(?m) and at(party, hanger_path) and not heardBrock(party)
    says "{?m} crouches by a spoil-heap with the leaf-litter scraped back, and does not touch the paw-print in the black earth, which is wider than a hand and a half. 'Old,' {?m} says. 'He is old and he has been hurt, and he is not hungry, which is the odd part. See the dung? Honey and beech-mast. Somebody has been feeding him, years back, and stopped, and he has not forgotten.' {?m} gets up slowly, looking at the trees and not the hole. 'He is not wicked. He remembers being killed. Give him what he wants, and keep your hands where he can see them.'" {
    Assert heardBrock(party).
  }
  Rule voice_beam at mill_floor when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, mill_floor) and not heardBeam(party)
    says "{?m} runs a bare palm along the strikers' beam from the near bracket, reading the cut letters with the fingertips as {?m} would a lock. 'Fifty-one names,' {?m} says. 'Fifty-one hands. Good, honest, hacked-out work, standing up, on the outside face.' The hand stops at the far end, at the bracket, where the beam goes into the iron, and turns the wrist to feel the underside. 'And here is one stroke more. A T. Begun and not finished. It is cut from the wrong side, from underneath and behind, by somebody crouching in the dark who did not have the nerve or the time. The others signed in the light.' {?m} takes the hand away. 'I would not mention it to anyone who loved him.'" teaches beam_stroke {
    Assert heardBeam(party).
  }
  Discovery beam_stroke "On the underside of the strikers' beam, at the iron bracket, there is a single stroke of a T, begun from behind by someone crouching and never finished: the fifty-second name, not cut.".
  Rule voice_wasting at hester_room when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, hester_room) and at(hester, hester_room) and not hesterDead(hester) and not heardWasting(party)
    says "{?m} stands at the foot of the bed a moment without speaking, taking in the old woman and the worn chair and the cup on the sill, and then sits on the edge of the bed where Hester pats it. 'She is well nursed,' {?m} says to the room, quietly. 'No sores. Clean linen, turned every morning. Whoever sits in that chair has not been out of it for weeks.' {?m} looks at the cup. 'What she lacks is not physic. It is leave. She has been told for ten months that she is dying, and nobody has said the other half, that it may be done gently, and that she may stop. There is an office for that. It does not need anything bought.'" {
    Assert heardWasting(party).
  }
  Rule voice_birds at chapel when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, chapel) and not heardBirds(party)
    says "{?m} stands in the arch and listens to the starlings in the basin without trying to name them. 'They are not copying anything,' {?m} says, and tips an ear. 'Starlings borrow. This one has a car-door in it, and a kettle, and the smith's third hammer. These are only doing the one tune, and it is the hymn the Old Shift taught me, with the end taken off, going up where you expect it to go down.' {?m} sings the first line back under the breath, and a starling answers from the rim, exactly. 'Somebody taught them and they never forgot,' {?m} says." {
    Assert heardBirds(party).
  }

  // ── A cleric's way through: the Office for the Easing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Hester has asked for her Monday. Tobias will not buy physic across the Tump and, left alone, does it himself on the
  // first night. Ruth Coll's poppy and the phial are bought; a cleric has a third thing, which is not. It eases and does
  // not end; she asks for the end again at the Watching, and the company must live with having been asked.
  Relation easedByOffice(group). Relation hesterAsksAgain(group).
  Action ease_hester_office(actor: group, site: place, c: member) "Have {c} say the Office for the Easing over Hester Lindsell" {
    Speaker hester.
    Description "Nothing is bought and nothing is carried in. {c} sits with her, and says the words for a bed like hers.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hester_room) and at(hester, hester_room) and lullOpen() and not hesterDead(hester) and not hesterEased(hester)
      and hesterTrust(hester) >= 1 and memberOf(c, actor) and hasCalling(c, calling_cleric).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert hesterEased(hester). Assert easedByOffice(hester). Assert hesterAsksAgain(hester). }
    Result "{c} says it in the plain low voice for it, with a hand on the sheet, not hurrying: the three parts of it, the naming, the laying down of the burden, and the letting go of the day. It does nothing you can see. Hester listens with her eyes shut and her mouth twitching, as she listens to the world. Somewhere in the second part her whole face changes, the way a field changes when the cloud goes off it. 'Oh,' she says. 'Somebody's said it.' Then she sleeps, deeply, with her hands open on the sheet, and in the doorway Tobias Lindsell has stood for the whole of it with his own hands hanging empty at his sides.".
  }
  // A company with no priest in it can only sit. It is a lesser thing: she sleeps for the first part of the night and
  // not for the rest, nothing is taken from her and nothing is given, and Tobias, who would have done it at ten,
  // finds a stranger in his chair and cannot. It costs the whole evening, and it does not last.
  Relation hesterSat(group).
  Action sit_up_with_hester(actor: group, site: place) "Sit up with Hester Lindsell through the evening, and tell her where you have been" {
    Speaker hester.
    Description "You are not a priest, and you have nothing to give her. You can sit in the chair.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hester_room) and at(hester, hester_room) and lullOpen() and dayOne() and not hesterDead(hester) and not hesterEased(hester) and not hesterSat(hester)
      and hesterTrust(hester) >= 1 and not capable(actor, rites).
    Time 300 minutes.
    On success { Assert hesterSat(hester). Assert hesterAsksAgain(hester). }
    Result "You take the chair that is Tobias's and tell her where you have been, the road and the weather and the bad inn, in no order, and she corrects the distances. About ten she stops correcting and her breath goes long. Tobias comes to the door with the cup in his hand, and sees the chair is taken, and stands there, and goes back to the kitchen. You sit on. She wakes twice and each time looks for the other chair, and finds you. Near dawn she says, quite clearly, 'You are not who I asked,' and holds on to your sleeve until she is asleep again.".
  }
  Observe hester_sat_asks at hester_room when hesterSat(hester) and not hesterDead(hester) and dayTwo() "Hester is awake and looking at the chair. 'I did not die,' she says. 'It was kind of you. It was not what I asked for.' She is not angry, and she is looking past you at the other chair.".
  Topic tobias_office with tobias "Ask Tobias Lindsell about the Office" when easedByOffice(hester) and not hesterDead(hester) once {
    Says "Tobias is sitting on the settle with the cup in both hands. 'Nothing bought,' he says. 'Nothing carried over the Tump.' He turns the cup. 'I stood in that door and I thought, there is a way that is not mine and not Ruth Coll's. There is a thing that is just said.' He looks up. 'She knew my name this morning. She said, You've not shaved.' His mouth works. 'I'll not thank you. I will do your washing for a year.'".
    On discuss { Increase tobiasTrust(tobias) by 2. Assert tobiasSoftened(tobias). }
  }
  Observe hester_asks_again at hester_room when hesterAsksAgain(hester) and hesterEased(hester) and not hesterDead(hester) and dayTwo() "Hester is awake, and clear, and looking at you. 'I am much better,' she says. 'I may last till the Working Day, and watch it, and be told about it afterwards. That is not what I asked you for.' She is quite calm. 'You have given me a good deal. I am going to keep asking. I thought you should know.'".

  // ── The bolt of the Long Shift ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A company that wove the six days in the dark carries a bolt of grey cloth that will never wear out, worth twenty
  // coin to Mercer Haskett. It is also exactly what Tobias Lindsell did not do: work a day because it was owed, and
  // keep what he made. Given to him, it opens what he has not said; sold, it buys a good deal in Sixways.
  Relation tobiasHasBolt(group).
  Topic tobias_bolt with tobias "Give Tobias Lindsell the bolt of cloth you wove in the Mill" when lullOpen() and carries(party, shift_bolt) and not tobiasHasBolt(tobias) once {
    Says "Tobias takes the end of it in his fingers, and rubs the weave between thumb and forefinger without looking at it, the way he found the notch on the shilling. His whole face goes still. 'Mill weave,' he says. 'Seven-and-a-half to the inch, and the selvedge turned in. Nobody has woven that since the Hallowing.' He looks at you. 'You were in there. In the dark. Working.' He does not ask. He sits down on the settle with the cloth across his knees. 'I worked one day for a shilling,' he says. 'And it was gone at sunset, every thread. You worked six, and it stayed.' He folds a corner over, carefully, as if it might not like it. 'Then that is what holds. Not the wage. The leaving off. Ask me what you came to ask. You came by the cloth honestly.'".
    On discuss { Spend long_shift_cloth from actor. Assert tobiasHasBolt(tobias). Increase tobiasTrust(tobias) by 2. }
  }
  Observe bolt_on_the_chair at hester_room when tobiasHasBolt(tobias) and lullOpen() and not hesterDead(hester) "Across the foot of Hester Lindsell's bed lies a bolt of grey cloth the colour of nothing at all, folded in thirds, and the old woman has her feet on it.".
  Observe bolt_at_the_table at green when tobiasHasBolt(tobias) and hesterDead(hester) and lullOpen() and dayTwo() and hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 21 "By the cup at the top of the Long Table, under Hester's folded shirt, someone has laid a bolt of grey cloth, and the Old Shift keep stopping to touch the edge of it, one at a time, as they pass.".

  // ── Things nobody can explain ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Nell Lumb's lantern is the Lull's kept light: lit on every Lullday dusk by whichever child of Linger has most lately
  // lost a tooth, at the Strike Post, and carried down at dawn. Nell was the child who said, can't it just stay Sunday.
  Observe nells_lantern at strike_post as feature when lullOpen() "On a hook driven into the top of the Strike Post hangs a tin lantern with a stub of candle in it, and a card tied to the handle in a child's hand: NELL. The children of Linger take it in turns to light it at dusk, and the rota is whoever lost a tooth last. Ask a child why and the answer is, 'Because it is Nell's.' Ask a grown man and he looks at the ground. The Old Shift say she is dead, and that it makes no difference.".
  Observe sixways_curtains at sx_street as feature when not dark() "Every door in Sixways has its curtain of grey-gold Lull-cloth, hung with the right edge turned in. The carters say it is never bought, only given: a woman who bought hers in the market town hung it one night, and in the morning it was the colour of ditchwater.".
  Observe haskett_oldest at haskett_loft as feature when true "On the lowest rack, wrapped in paper gone brown, hangs the oldest bolt in the loft. Its ticket is in a hand nobody now writes, and says, in full: FOR THE WAR. NOT TO BE SOLD. Haskett's father would not say which war. Haskett says he has never asked, and that this is the whole of what he is proud of.".

  // ── Outward: Sixways, the candle trade, and the news by the north road ─────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe spurling_candles at spurling_shop as feature when lullOpen() "On the rack above the bench, apart from the Lull's own spurling and beeswax dips, hangs one bundle of tall white fluted candles, tied with a bit of red wool and a ticket: HASKETT CART, FROM THE WOLD OF HUME, ASKED UNLIT. Wenna says they burn three nights each and smell of summer, and that nothing she dips will do it; and that they came from a place where half a town walks away behind a swarm, which she thinks is the most Lull-like thing she has ever heard of outside the Lull.".
  Topic dorcas_carters with dorcas "Ask Dorcas Trewin where the carters come from" when true once {
    Says "'Everywhere that wants cloth.' Dorcas counts on her fingers, not unkindly. 'Larum, up the west road, for the winter wool, and they pay in lamp-oil and say the quiet up there wants warm things. The Hume carts, from the south, for the grey-gold, and bring back candles to be lit unlit.' She smiles at that. 'The Wold of Hume sends us wax and takes cloth, and neither of them has ever once asked what the other does with it. If a Sixer wanted to see the sea, they could go with the Hume cart, but I would not say the sea is any better for it.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/the-lull/houses.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── The Open Houses ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Pryces and the Gales keep open house, and are at war in generosity. On the first Lullday Lettice Pryce gives
  // the guest something magnificent, to beat Mabyn Gale; a gift given to win comes apart at dusk, and at the Watching
  // everybody sees it. On the next, humiliated, she gives Mabyn her house, out of pure spite; spite is meant, and holds;
  // the Pryces are homeless by their own gift, and the Chief Rest-warden sleeps in his enemy's spare room. What that
  // does to Hobday decides whether the wardens come to the Green on the Working Day.
  Observe pryce_scene at pryce_parlour when lullOpen() and not pryceHouseGiven(lettice) "The best parlour in Linger, and it knows it: a carpet, a clock that does not go (on the mantel, as an ornament), a glass-fronted cabinet of gifts received with each card turned outward, and a second cabinet, larger, of gifts given, represented by the receivers' thank-you letters, framed. Everything smells of beeswax and of being looked at.".
  Observe pryce_given at pryce_parlour when lullOpen() and pryceHouseGiven(lettice) "The Pryces' parlour, which is now Mabyn Gale's, and which Mabyn has not come into. The cabinets are there, and the carpet. The ornamental clock has been turned to face the wall.".
  Observe pryce_dark at pryce_parlour when folded() "The best parlour in Linger in the dark, with the glass of its cabinets catching what little light there is.".

  Person lettice "Lettice Pryce" at pryce_parlour {
    Role "who keeps the Pryces' open house, and is the most generous woman in the Lull". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner proud.
    Likeness "noblewoman".
    Greets "A tall woman with a great deal of grey hair piled up like a loaf sweeps across the parlour to you with both hands out. 'A guest. And nobody has given you anything yet, I can see it in your face. Sit. Sit! Lettice Pryce. You'll have been to the Gales'.' The smile does not move. 'Lovely people. Simple.'".
    Greets again "'My dear,' says Lettice Pryce, and looks at once at what you are carrying.".
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(lettice). Initially Assert dayAt(lettice, pryce_parlour). Initially Assert bedAt(lettice, pryce_parlour).
  Person hobday "Hobday Pryce" at green {
    Role "the Chief Rest-warden of the Lull". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Likeness "constable".
    Greets "A big pink man with a staff and a sash of the grey-gold cloth stops you with a raised hand. 'Slowly,' he says. 'Slowly, friend. You're in the Lull. Nobody here is late for anything.' He looks you up and down. 'Hobday Pryce. Chief Rest-warden. You'll find us very easy to get on with, provided you're easy.'".
    Greets again "Hobday Pryce raises his staff to you, slowly, as a lesson, and holds it there until you have understood that it is the lesson. 'The first time,' he says, 'you came as a guest. This time you have come as a question. Both are welcome, but one of them eats less.'".
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(hobday). Initially Assert dayAt(hobday, green). Initially Assert bedAt(hobday, pryce_parlour).
  Person kezia "Kezia Pryce" at gardens {
    Role "the Pryces' daughter, with mud to the elbow". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "A girl of seventeen in an expensive dress with mud on it to the elbow looks up from a strip of leeks. 'If Mother sent you, I'm not here,' she says. 'If she didn't, hello. I'm Kezia. Don't tell her you saw me digging. Digging's fine. It's that I'm digging leeks, and leeks are the Gales'.'".
    Greets again "Kezia Pryce waves a trowel at you, and a clod of earth goes with it, and hits the wall. 'Sorry!' she says. 'It was meant. I think. Isn't that odd? I have been meaning things all morning and none of them will stay put.'".
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(kezia). Initially Assert dayAt(kezia, gardens). Initially Assert bedAt(kezia, pryce_parlour).
  Person wardens "the Rest-wardens" at tump_shoulder {
    Role "in grey-gold sashes, with staves". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Numbers 3. Peaceable.
    Greets "Three wardens in grey-gold sashes lean on their staves and look at you with the patience of men who are paid in nothing and like it. 'Slowly,' says one, out of habit.".
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(wardens). Initially Assert dayAt(wardens, tump_shoulder). Initially Assert bedAt(wardens, weavers_row).
  // The wardens keep the shoulder in the morning, and the green after.
  Rule wardens_to_green when lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 11 and hour(clock) < 19 and routine(wardens) and not at(wardens, green) { Assert at(wardens, green). }
  Initially Assert serves(wardens, hobday).
  // The wardens turn Simeon Eddowes back at the shoulder, by the old Chief Warden's word, while they keep it.
  Relation simeonTurned(group). Relation simeonHome(group).
  Rule simeon_turned at tump_shoulder when following(simeon, party) and at(party, tump_shoulder) and at(wardens, tump_shoulder) and lullOpen() and not simeonHome(simeon) and not hobdayGrateful(hobday)
    says "The wardens on the shoulder look at the old man in the white apron, and at each other, and one of them steps into the road with his staff across it. 'Simeon Eddowes,' he says, not unkindly, as if reading it off something. 'Put out by the Chief Warden's word. You'll go back to the stone, sir.' Simeon stands in the road, looking past them at the valley. Then he turns round and walks back up toward the Fold-stone, very straight, without a word, and the wardens watch him go, and look at their boots." {
    Retract following(simeon, party). Assert at(simeon, fold_stone). Assert simeonTurned(simeon).
  }
  Rule simeon_waits when at(simeon, fold_stone) and simeonTurned(simeon) and not lullOpen() { Assert at(simeon, simeon_room). }
  Rule simeon_comes_home when following(simeon, party) and inLull(party) and lullOpen() and not simeonHome(simeon) and not (at(party, tump_shoulder) and at(wardens, tump_shoulder))
    says "Simeon stops in the road below the shoulder with the whole valley in front of him, the woods and the tarn and the town and the dark mill, and for a moment he does not move. Then he says, 'They've painted the Glossary,' in a voice you have not heard him use." { Assert simeonHome(simeon). }

  // The war in generosity.
  Topic hobday_fines with hobday "Ask Hobday Pryce what the Rest-wardens do" when lullOpen() once {
    Says "'Keep the peace,' says Hobday. 'The rest, I should say. A man runs, we stop him. A woman haggles, we have a word. Somebody's seen to be trying too hard at a thing, we remind them.' He leans on his staff. 'Fines are in gifts. You give the Lull something: a loaf to the Table, a morning in the Gardens. Freely.' He frowns slightly, as if at an old splinter. 'It holds, mostly. You'd be surprised how many people give a fine freely.'".
  }
  Topic lettice_gift with lettice "Accept what Lettice Pryce wants to give you" when lullOpen() and dayOne() and not letticeGave(lettice) and not letticeHumbled(lettice) once {
    Says "Lettice opens the larger cabinet and takes out a cloak: grey-gold Lull-cloth, lined with red, with a silver clasp in the shape of a starling, and puts it round your shoulders herself. 'There,' she says. 'Now you can tell the Gales you've been given something.' She stands back. 'Wear it to the Watching. They'll all see.'".
    On discuss { Assert letticeGave(lettice). Give pryce_cloak to actor. }
  }
  Relation letticeGave(group). Relation letticeHumbled(group). Relation letticeShamed(group). Relation pryceHouseGiven(group).
  Kind pryce_cloak_kind "a cloak from Lettice Pryce" is gear worth 6 weighing 1 described "A cloak of grey-gold Lull-cloth lined with red, with a silver clasp in the shape of a starling, given to you by Lettice Pryce to show the Gales.".
  Item pryce_cloak "a cloak from Lettice Pryce" is pryce_cloak_kind at limbo.
  Initially Assert unmeant(pryce_cloak).
  // At the Watching, in front of everybody, it comes apart; if the company is elsewhere, it comes apart elsewhere.
  Rule cloak_ravels_public at green when lullDusk() and carries(party, pryce_cloak) and at(party, green) and at(lettice, green)
    says "The cloak Lettice Pryce gave you begins to come apart on your back: first the lining, a red thread at a time, then the grey-gold, the way a cobweb goes in a draught, until the silver clasp drops into your lap on its own and there is a little heap of loose wool at your feet. Along the Table nobody says anything, very loudly. Lettice Pryce sits perfectly upright with her face like a plate. At the far end, Mabyn Gale gets up, and comes down the Table, and picks the clasp out of your lap, and gives it back to Lettice, and goes back to her seat; and that is the worst thing that has happened to Lettice Pryce in fifty years." teaches given_to_win {
    Spend pryce_cloak_kind from party. Assert at(pryce_cloak, limbo). Assert letticeShamed(lettice).
  }
  Rule cloak_ravels_private when lullDusk() and carries(party, pryce_cloak) and not (at(party, green) and at(lettice, green))
    says "Somewhere about sunset, the cloak Lettice Pryce gave you comes apart: lining first, then the grey-gold, until the silver starling clasp drops on its own into a little heap of loose wool. Nobody sees it but you." teaches given_to_win {
    Spend pryce_cloak_kind from party. Assert at(pryce_cloak, limbo).
  }
  Discovery given_to_win "A gift given to win comes apart at sunset in the Lull: Lettice Pryce's cloak, given to beat the Gales, ravelled to loose wool.".
  // Told beforehand what will happen, she is shaken, and gives something else instead.
  Topic lettice_warned with lettice "Tell Lettice Pryce that a gift given to beat Mabyn Gale will not hold" when lullOpen() and dayOne() and letticeGave(lettice) and not letticeShamed(lettice) and not letticeHumbled(lettice) and (knows(actor, glosser_doctrine) or knows(actor, simeon_doctrine) or knows(actor, chair_ravels)) once {
    Says "Lettice looks at you as if you had slapped her. Then at the cloak. Then at the cabinet of framed letters, and for a moment you see her read them, all of them, at once. 'Take it off,' she says, quite quietly. She folds the cloak over her arm. 'I am sixty-one,' she says. 'I have given away a great deal. I suppose I should like to know how much of it held.' She sits down. 'Mabyn's girl has the croup every winter. Every winter Mabyn sits up with her. I have a recipe of my mother's for it.' She looks at the cloak. 'I could give her that. I don't know if I'd mean it.' A pause. 'I'd like to try.'".
    On discuss { Assert letticeHumbled(lettice). Spend pryce_cloak_kind from actor. Assert at(pryce_cloak, limbo). }
  }
  Rule lettice_recipe at green when letticeHumbled(lettice) and lullDusk() and at(lettice, green) and at(mabyn, green) and not spreadFact(recipe_told)
    says "At the Watching Lettice Pryce sets a folded paper on the grass with the day's makings, and the town reads the card on it, FOR MABYN GALE, A RECEIPT FOR THE CROUP, and looks at Mabyn, and Mabyn looks at Lettice. The sun goes. The paper stays. Mabyn Gale comes down the Table and picks it up and reads it, and says, 'Your mother's,' and Lettice says, 'Yes,' and that is all anybody says, and it is the talk of the Lull for a week of Lulldays." { Assert spreadFact(recipe_told). Assert housesAtPeace(mabyn). }
  Entity recipe_told: fact "the receipt for the croup".
  Item mabyn_cloth "a length of Lull-cloth from Mabyn Gale" is lull_cloth at limbo.
  Rule mabyn_thanks at green when housesAtPeace(mabyn) and at(party, green) and lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 20 and at(mabyn_cloth, limbo) and not spreadFact(mabyn_thanked)
    says "Later, when the lanterns are going out, Mabyn Gale finds you at the bottom of the Table and puts something soft into your arms without a word: a length of grey-gold Lull-cloth, folded small, that smells of her linen-press. 'My mother wove that,' she says. 'For whoever made Lettice Pryce give me something she meant.' She pats it. 'It'll outlast you. Don't sell it to that Haskett for less than fifteen.'" { Assert spreadFact(mabyn_thanked). Give mabyn_cloth to party. }
  Entity mabyn_thanked: fact "Mabyn's thanks".
  Relation housesAtPeace(group).
  // Shamed, on the next Lullday she gives Mabyn her house. Spite is meant. It holds.
  Rule house_given at green when letticeShamed(lettice) and dayTwo() and lullDusk() and not pryceHouseGiven(lettice)
    says "At the Watching Lettice Pryce stands up at her place at the Long Table, which nobody does, and says in a clear voice that she gives her house, her parlour and her cabinets and her carpets, to Mabyn Gale of the Open Hand, freely, as a courtesy for the clasp. Then she sits down. Nobody breathes. The sun goes off the Tump. The Pryces' house does not come apart, or go anywhere; it stands there across the green, as a house does, and it is not the Pryces' any more, because she meant it. She meant it with every bone in her body. Hobday Pryce puts his face in his hands. Mabyn Gale says, to nobody, 'Oh, Lettice, you fool,' and goes to make up the spare room." teaches spite_holds {
    Assert pryceHouseGiven(lettice).
  }
  Rule house_given_quiet when letticeShamed(lettice) and dayTwo() and lullDusk() and not pryceHouseGiven(lettice) and not at(party, green) { Assert pryceHouseGiven(lettice). }
  Discovery spite_holds "Spite holds in the Lull. Lettice Pryce gave her house to Mabyn Gale out of pure spite at the Watching, and it held: the Pryces are homeless by their own gift.".
  // Homeless, the Pryces lodge at the Open Hand.
  Rule pryces_lodge when pryceHouseGiven(lettice) and bedAt(lettice, pryce_parlour) { Retract bedAt(lettice, pryce_parlour). Assert bedAt(lettice, open_hand). Retract bedAt(hobday, pryce_parlour). Assert bedAt(hobday, open_hand). Retract bedAt(kezia, pryce_parlour). Assert bedAt(kezia, linnet_loft). Retract dayAt(lettice, pryce_parlour). Assert dayAt(lettice, open_hand). }
  Observe hobday_lodging at open_hand when lullOpen() and pryceHouseGiven(lettice) and at(hobday, open_hand) "Hobday Pryce is sitting in the corner of the Open Hand in his sash, with a cup of something, being looked after by Matthias Gale with a tenderness that is clearly agony to both of them.".
  Rule hobday_mornings when pryceHouseGiven(lettice) and lullOpen() and hour(clock) < 11 and routine(hobday) and dayAt(hobday, green) { Retract dayAt(hobday, green). Assert dayAt(hobday, open_hand). }
  // Under Mabyn's roof he softens, if anyone speaks to him kindly about it; or he hardens, if nobody does.
  Topic hobday_lodged with hobday "Ask Hobday Pryce how he finds the Open Hand" when lullOpen() and pryceHouseGiven(lettice) and not hobdaySoftened(hobday) once {
    Says "Hobday looks into his cup for a long time. 'He brought me cocoa,' he says. 'At two in the morning. I was sitting on the end of the bed in my sash because I couldn't think how to take it off in somebody else's house, and Matthias Gale knocked and brought me cocoa and a hot brick for my feet and said he'd always wanted to look after a warden.' He sets the cup down. 'Forty years I've fined people for trying too hard. That man tries harder than anyone in the Lull. And it holds.' He looks at you. 'I don't know what to do with that.'".
    On discuss { Assert hobdaySoftened(hobday). }
  }
  Relation hobdaySoftened(group).
  Observe pryces_dark at open_hand as feature when folded() and pryceHouseGiven(lettice) "In the corner, the Chief Rest-warden is asleep upright in a chair by the dead fire, with his sash on and a cocoa cup in his open hand.".

  // Kezia, who is in the Weekday Club because her mother would hate it.
  Topic kezia_club with kezia "Ask Kezia Pryce whether she knows Corin Lindsell" when lullOpen() and (knows(actor, club_rumour) or knows(actor, working_day_plan)) once {
    Says "Kezia sits back on her heels and looks at you sideways. 'Everybody knows Corin.' Then, lower: 'If you mean, am I in the Club: yes. Don't tell Father. He'd have to arrest me, and he'd cry.' She stabs a leek. 'Why? Because Mother would hate it. Because if I have to spend my whole life being a Pryce at a table, I'd like it to be a table where something happens.' She grins. 'And you needn't look like that. Aldith says spite's as good as love, at sunset. Better, some days.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, kezia_club). }
  }
  Discovery kezia_club "Kezia Pryce, the Chief Rest-warden's daughter, is in the Weekday Club, because her mother would hate it.".
  // Hobday will give something for the names of the Club. A gift given to buy a name comes undone at sunset.
  Topic hobday_names with hobday "Ask Hobday Pryce what he knows of the Weekday Club" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, working_day_plan) and not hobdayKnows(hobday) once {
    Says "Hobday's face closes. 'Young people with nothing to do,' he says. 'Talking. They'll grow out of it, or we'll grow them out of it.' He lowers his voice. 'I'd take it kindly if anybody told me who. I'd give them something for it. A gift.' He looks at your purse. 'A handsome one.'".
    On discuss { Assert hobdayAsks(hobday). }
  }
  Relation hobdayAsks(group). Relation hobdayKnows(group).
  Action tell_names(actor: group, site: place) "Give Hobday Pryce the names of the Weekday Club, for his gift of ten coin" {
    Grave "The Club will know who told.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hobday, site) and hobdayAsks(hobday) and lullOpen() and not hobdayKnows(hobday).
    On success { Assert hobdayKnows(hobday). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Assert informerPaid(actor). }
    Result "You give him the names, Corin's first. Hobday writes them down on his cuff with a pencil, slowly, and his face gets pinker at one of them, and he does not say which. He counts ten coins into your hand. 'A gift,' he says. 'Freely given.' He does not look at you while he says it.".
  }
  Relation informerPaid(group).
  Rule informer_ravels when lullDusk() and informerPaid(party) and not informerRavelled(party)
    says "At sunset the ten coins Hobday Pryce gave you for the names go out of your purse like water out of a cupped hand, and are gone, back to his, you suppose. A gift given to buy something is not a gift. The names stay told." {
    Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 10 or to nothing. Increase quantity(hobday, gold) by 10. Assert informerRavelled(party).
  }
  Relation informerRavelled(group).
}

data/adventures/the-lull/law.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── The Ravel ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What is done in the Lull without meaning it comes apart at its dusk. What the company carries of such a thing goes
  // from its hands; each that has words of its own (ownRavel) says them, the rest are told plainly.
  Relation unmeant(item). Relation ravelled(item). Relation ownRavel(item).
  Rule ravel_carried when lullDusk() and unmeant(?i) and carries(party, ?i) and itemKind(?i, ?k) and not ownRavel(?i)
    says "At sunset {?i} comes apart in your pack, the way frost goes off a pane: it is there, and then it is a little loose stuff, and then it is not even that." {
    Spend ?k from party. Assert at(?i, limbo). Assert ravelled(?i).
  }

  // ── On What Holds ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Aldith Mote, the junior Glosser, suspects the twelfth Gloss. With a Sixer's help she tries it: a cairn stacked for
  // a coin; a skep set for a coin by a man who loves bees; and what the company sees of gifts given to win, and of
  // spite. The law is meaning it: wages are beside the point.
  Relation aldithTesting(group). Relation lawFound(group).
  Topic aldith_test with aldith "Offer to help Aldith Mote test the twelfth Gloss" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, glosser_doctrine) and not aldithTesting(aldith) once {
    Says "Aldith goes pink to the ears. 'Would you? Nobody in the Lull can, you see; we can't do anything for wages without meaning to see if it holds, and then we mean it, and it's spoiled.' She is already writing. 'Two things. First: I give you a coin, and you stack me a cairn on the Glossary step, for the coin. Second: there's Hob Linsey at the tarn, who loves his bees more than his life. If he'd take a coin to set a skep in the Gardens, he'd be working for wages at a thing he loves. Gloss twelve says it ravels.' She bites the pencil. 'I don't think it will.' She gives you two coins. 'And anything else you see at sunset, tell me. Anything that holds that shouldn't, or goes that shouldn't.'".
    On discuss { Assert aldithTesting(aldith). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 2. }
  }
  Thing cairn "a cairn on the Glossary step" at limbo {
    State stacked "On the Glossary step stands a neat cairn of river stones, stacked for a coin.".
    State scattered "On the Glossary step lie a few river stones, scattered, where a cairn stood.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(cairn, stacked).
  Action stack_cairn(actor: group, site: place) "Stack a cairn of river stones on the Glossary step, for Aldith Mote's coin" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, green) and aldithTesting(aldith) and lullOpen() and hour(clock) < 19 and at(cairn, limbo) and not knows(actor, wage_ravels).
    Time 3.
    On success { Retract at(cairn, limbo). Assert at(cairn, green). Assert state(cairn, stacked). }
    Result "You fetch stones up from the Idle, flat ones, and stack them on the Glossary step to the height of your knee, carefully, because she is watching and because it is the kind of thing you find you want to do properly. It is the first thing you have done in the Lull for wages.".
  }
  Rule cairn_falls at green when lullDusk() and at(cairn, green) and state(cairn, stacked)
    says "The cairn on the Glossary step comes down, not as if pushed but as if each stone had remembered, at the same moment, where in the river it was lying this morning; the stones roll down the step and lie there. Aldith Mote, at the Table, writes it down without looking surprised." teaches wage_ravels {
    Assert state(cairn, scattered).
  }
  Observe cairn_seen at green when at(cairn, green) and state(cairn, scattered) and lullOpen() and not knows(party, wage_ravels) "On the Glossary step, river stones lie scattered where your cairn stood." teaches wage_ravels.
  Discovery wage_ravels "Work done in the Lull for wages, by someone who does not care for it, comes undone at sunset: the cairn you stacked for Aldith Mote's coin fell back into the river's order.".
  Rule cairn_cleared when lullOpen() and hour(clock) == 7 and at(cairn, green) and state(cairn, scattered) { Assert at(cairn, limbo). }
  // Hob Linsey and the skep.
  Thing skep "a new skep in the Gardens" at limbo {
    State set "A new straw skep stands on a plank in the Gardens, with bees already finding it.".
    State held "The skep Hob Linsey set for a coin stands in the Gardens, and the bees are in and out of it.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(skep, set).
  Rule skep_holds when lullDusk() and at(skep, gardens) and state(skep, set) { Assert state(skep, held). }
  Observe skep_seen at gardens when lullOpen() and at(skep, gardens) and state(skep, held) and not knows(party, loved_wage_holds) "Hob Linsey's skep, set for a coin, is still standing in the Gardens, bees and all." teaches loved_wage_holds.
  Rule skep_told at green when lullDusk() and at(skep, gardens) and at(party, green) and not knows(party, loved_wage_holds)
    says "Aldith Mote comes running down the Table, which nobody does, with her apron flying. 'The skep held,' she says, to you, low and fierce. 'He took the coin. He set it for the coin. It held.'" teaches loved_wage_holds { }
  Discovery loved_wage_holds "Work done in the Lull for wages by someone who loves the work holds: Hob Linsey set a skep in the Gardens for a coin, and it stood at sunset.".
  Rule davy_stone at green when dayTwo() and lullDusk() and not pryceHouseGiven(lettice) and at(party, green) and not knows(party, spite_holds)
    says "Among the makings on the grass tonight is a stone with a face cut on it, a big pink face with a mouth like a purse, which everybody recognises and nobody mentions. The card says BY DAVY MOTE, FOR THE CHIEF WARDEN, and it is not a kind card. The sun goes. The stone stays. Hobday Pryce looks at it, and at the pink face, and then laughs, which nobody expected, least of all Davy." teaches spite_holds { }
  Topic aldith_found with aldith "Tell Aldith Mote what you have seen hold, and come undone" when lullOpen() and aldithTesting(aldith) and knows(actor, wage_ravels) and knows(actor, loved_wage_holds) and (knows(actor, given_to_win) or knows(actor, spite_holds) or knows(actor, chair_ravels)) and not lawFound(aldith) {
    Says "Aldith writes while you talk, fast, and stops you twice, and when you have finished she sits for a while with the pencil against her teeth. 'The cairn went, and you didn't care for it. The skep held, and he did, and he was paid.' She writes. 'Mrs Pryce's gifts were free, and given to win, and went. And spite holds.' She looks up. 'It isn't wages. It isn't love, either, Simeon Eddowes, wherever you are. It's meaning it. Whatever you do in the Lull, if you mean it, all of you, all the way down, it holds.' She gets up on the ladder with a new white board and starts to paint, very carefully, and you read it as it comes: GLOSS 2,214: THAT WHAT HOLDS IS WHAT IS MEANT. She stops. 'They'll make me paint over it,' she says. 'I don't care.' And then, quite differently: 'Corin should know this. If it isn't wages, her Working Day isn't what she thinks it is.'".
    On discuss { Assert lawFound(aldith). Assert knows(actor, meaning_law). }
  }
  Discovery meaning_law "What holds in the Lull is what is meant: not what is unpaid, not what is loved, but what is done meaning it, all the way down. Wages are beside the point; so is love; spite holds, and grief.".
  Topic simeon_wrong with simeon "Tell Simeon what Aldith Mote found the law to be" when knows(actor, meaning_law) and following(simeon, party) and not simeonWrong(simeon) once {
    Says "Simeon stops dead in the road. 'Meaning,' he says. 'Not love.' He thinks about it with his whole face, which works like a loom. 'Spite holds. Yes. It would. God help us, of course it would.' Then he laughs, a great bark that sends birds up. 'Held: I was wrong. Twenty years. Wonderful. Oh, that is wonderful.' He wipes his eyes. 'Who found it? The little Mote girl? Good. Good. They'll make her paint over it. They made me.'".
    On discuss { Assert simeonWrong(simeon). }
  }
  Relation simeonWrong(group).
  Topic simeon_wrong_here with simeon "Tell Simeon what Aldith Mote found the law to be" when knows(actor, meaning_law) and not following(simeon, party) and not simeonWrong(simeon) once {
    Says "Simeon puts down his pen. 'Meaning,' he says. 'Not love.' He sits back. 'Spite holds,' he says slowly, and you see his shoulders begin to shake, and it is a moment before you understand that he is laughing. 'Twenty years I kept the gloss that love is the law, and a Pryce boy has proved it with a rude stone.' He wipes his spectacles on the apron. 'I was wrong. I should like to see that board before they paint it out.'".
    On discuss { Assert simeonWrong(simeon). Assert acceptsEscort(simeon, actor). }
  }

  // ── The Gift Hall bench ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Piran Trewin leaves limewood offcuts on the bench for anyone. Make something there for someone; at sunset it
  // holds if you meant it, which is to say if you have come to care for them, and comes apart if you were only being
  // polite.
  Relation cares(group, group). Relation canMakeFor(group). Relation madeFor(item, group). Relation benchUsed(group).
  Initially Assert canMakeFor(linnet). Initially Assert canMakeFor(hester). Initially Assert canMakeFor(corin). Initially Assert canMakeFor(tobias).
  Initially Assert canMakeFor(wenna). Initially Assert canMakeFor(dorcas). Initially Assert canMakeFor(piran).
  Relation met(group, group).
  Rule meeting when addressed(?p, ?c) and not met(?p, ?c) { Assert met(?p, ?c). }
  Rule cares_hester when hesterTrust(hester) >= 2 and not cares(party, hester) { Assert cares(party, hester). }
  Rule cares_corin when corinTrust(corin) >= 2 and not cares(party, corin) { Assert cares(party, corin). }
  Rule cares_tobias when tobiasConfessed(tobias) and not cares(party, tobias) { Assert cares(party, tobias). }
  Rule cares_wenna when (wennaTold(wenna) or abelTold(abel)) and not cares(party, wenna) { Assert cares(party, wenna). }
  Rule cares_dorcas when dorcasKnowsHeads(dorcas) and not cares(party, dorcas) { Assert cares(party, dorcas). }
  Rule cares_piran when piranKnowsIll(piran) and not cares(party, piran) { Assert cares(party, piran). }
  Kind keepsake_kind "a little limewood carving you made" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "A small thing of pale limewood, whittled at the Gift Hall bench from one of Piran Trewin's offcuts: not very good, and yours.".
  Item keepsake "a little limewood carving you made" is keepsake_kind at limbo.
  Observe bench_scene at gift_hall as feature when lullOpen() "Under the window at the end is a long bench with a box of limewood offcuts on it, and knives, and a card: FROM PIRAN, FOR ANYBODY.".
  Action make_keepsake(actor: group, who: group, site: place) "Sit at the Gift Hall bench and carve something for {who}" {
    Description "Whether it lasts the sunset depends on whether you meant it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, gift_hall) and lullOpen() and hour(clock) < 19 and canMakeFor(who) and met(who, actor) and at(keepsake, limbo) and not benchUsed(actor).
    Time 12.
    On success { Retract at(keepsake, limbo). Give keepsake to actor. Assert madeFor(keepsake, who). Assert benchUsed(actor). }
    Result "You sit at the bench for two hours with a knife and a lump of limewood, and the light moves across the floor, and a child comes and watches and goes away again, and what comes out of the wood is small and lopsided and, you think, recognisably what you meant. You put it in your pack for sunset.".
  }
  Rule bench_resets when hour(clock) == 0 and benchUsed(?g) and at(keepsake, limbo) { Retract benchUsed(?g). }
  Rule keepsake_meant when madeFor(keepsake, ?w) and not cares(party, ?w) and not unmeant(keepsake) and not keepsakeKept(keepsake) { Assert unmeant(keepsake). Assert ownRavel(keepsake). }
  Rule keepsake_cared when madeFor(keepsake, ?w) and cares(party, ?w) and unmeant(keepsake) { Retract unmeant(keepsake). }
  Relation keepsakeKept(item).
  Rule keepsake_ravels when lullDusk() and unmeant(keepsake) and carries(party, keepsake) and madeFor(keepsake, ?w)
    says "At sunset the little carving in your pack comes apart into shavings, curl by curl, until there is only a pinch of pale dust. You were being kind. Kind is not the same." {
    Spend keepsake_kind from party. Assert at(keepsake, limbo). Retract madeFor(keepsake, ?w). Retract unmeant(keepsake).
  }
  Rule keepsake_ravels_given when lullDusk() and unmeant(keepsake) and keeps(?w, keepsake) and madeFor(keepsake, ?w)
    says "Somewhere in Linger, at sunset, a little limewood carving comes apart in somebody's hand into shavings." {
    Retract keeps(?w, keepsake). Assert at(keepsake, limbo). Retract madeFor(keepsake, ?w). Retract unmeant(keepsake).
  }
  Rule keepsake_holds when lullDusk() and madeFor(keepsake, ?w) and not unmeant(keepsake) and not keepsakeKept(keepsake) { Assert keepsakeKept(keepsake). }
}

data/adventures/the-lull/linnet.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── Linnet ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Linnet Gale plays the Watching in. Nothing she makes can come apart, because a tune is not a thing; and every tune
  // she makes is sung once and forgotten, because in the Lull nothing ever happens that a tune could be about. For her
  // the company is there every day. She notices what a week does to someone.
  Observe loft_scene at linnet_loft when lullOpen() "A long room under the roof of the Open Hand, all window on one side, the old loom-light: a fiddle on a nail, a bench, music written on the whitewashed wall in charcoal and rubbed out and written again until the wall is grey with it, and a young woman sitting in the window with her feet up, playing something and stopping and playing it differently.".
  Observe loft_dark at linnet_loft when folded() "The music room in the dark. The young woman is asleep on the window-seat with the fiddle across her knees and her hands open on it. You could touch her shoulder. She would not wake.".
  Observe linnet_plays at green as sound when lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 21 and at(linnet, green) "At the top of the Long Table Linnet Gale is playing, standing on the bench: a dance, then a slow air, then something new that nobody knows, which the Table listens to with its spoons held still.".
  Person linnet "Linnet Gale" at linnet_loft {
    Role "who plays the Watching in". Ancestry human. Calling bard. Level 2. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Likeness "minstrel".
    Greets "The young woman in the window stops playing and looks at you over the fiddle. 'Oh, you're new,' she says, delighted. 'Nobody's new. Sit down. No: stand there, where the light is.' She plays four notes, looking at you, and nods. 'Linnet. That's you, that bit. I'll use it.'".
    Greets again "Linnet looks up from the fiddle and plays your four notes at you, by way of hello.".
    Joins "Linnet takes the fiddle off its nail and puts it under her arm, and looks round the music room as if she were memorising it, and then does not look back.".
    Wants keepsake_kind.
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(linnet). Initially Assert dayAt(linnet, linnet_loft). Initially Assert bedAt(linnet, linnet_loft).
  Initially Set hire(linnet) to 0.
  Measure linnetWarm(group). Relation linnetLoves(group). Relation linnetTune(group). Relation linnetSawDay(group). Measure linnetLast(group).
  Rule linnet_remembers when addressed(linnet, party) and linnetLast(linnet) != lullCount(clock) { Set linnetLast(linnet) to lullCount(clock). Increase linnetWarm(linnet) by 1. }
  Topic linnet_tunes with linnet "Ask Linnet Gale about her tunes" when lullOpen() once {
    Says "'I make one a day,' says Linnet. 'Every day. A Lull's worth of tunes. Fifty-seven years of Lulldays, and my mother says there were fiddlers before me making one a day too.' She plucks a string. 'They can't ravel. A tune's not a thing. But nobody keeps them. Nothing happens here for a tune to be about, so they sing it once at the Watching and in the morning it's gone, like a dream, and I make another.' She looks at the charcoal on the wall. 'I'd like to make one that everybody sings next week. Next year. One that's about something.' She laughs. 'I'd need something to happen.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, linnet_wants). }
  }
  Discovery linnet_wants "Linnet Gale makes a tune every Lullday, and every one is sung once and forgotten. She wants to make one that is about something, and kept; and for that something would have to happen.".
  Topic linnet_sixways with linnet "Ask Linnet Gale whether she has been out over the Tump" when lullOpen() once {
    Says "'Once.' Linnet makes a face. 'I was sixteen. I went to Sixways for a day to hear their fiddler, and it was so loud. Not him: everything. Carts and hammers and people saying hurry, hurry, and a dog that barked at nothing all afternoon, and I couldn't hear anything I was playing.' She tunes a peg. 'I came back by the evening road and I cried at the stone. Not because it was horrible. Because I liked it, and I couldn't bear it.' She looks at you sideways. 'You came through all that to get here. Is it like that everywhere?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, linnet_afraid). }
  }
  Discovery linnet_afraid "Linnet Gale went out to Sixways once, at sixteen, and liked the noise of the world, and could not bear it, and cried at the Fold-stone.".
  // The second day she sees you: for her it is the next morning; for you, a week.
  Topic linnet_yesterday with linnet "Let Linnet Gale look at you" when lullOpen() and linnetWarm(linnet) >= 2 and not linnetSawDay(linnet) {
    Says "Linnet puts the fiddle down and looks at you properly, head on one side, the way she looks at a tune that is not right yet. 'You were here yesterday,' she says. 'And you're not the same.' She reaches out and turns your hand over. 'You had a scratch there. It's gone. Healed.' She lets go. 'You've been out there a week. Seven days of things happening to you, and I've been asleep.' She picks the fiddle up, and puts it down again. 'I'll count them,' she says. 'Your weeks. If you keep coming. Somebody ought to.'".
    On discuss { Assert linnetSawDay(linnet). Assert knows(actor, linnet_counts). }
  }
  Discovery linnet_counts "Linnet Gale sees what a week has done to you, every time you come back, and says she will count your weeks.".
  Topic linnet_came_back with linnet "Tell Linnet Gale that you came back to see her" when lullOpen() and linnetSawDay(linnet) and not linnetLoves(linnet) once {
    Says "Linnet does not say anything for a while. She plays four notes, the ones that are you, slowly, and then four more after them that you have not heard before, that answer them. 'There,' she says. 'Now it's about something.' She does not look at you. 'Don't say it again till you mean it at sunset. I couldn't stand it if it ravelled.' Then she does look at you, and laughs, because she cannot help it. 'Oh, I'm so glad. I'm so glad you came back.'".
    On discuss { Assert linnetLoves(linnet). Assert cares(party, linnet). }
  }
  Topic linnet_play with linnet "Ask Linnet Gale to play you something" when lullOpen() and not linnetLoves(linnet) once {
    Says "She plays you yesterday's tune, she says, from memory, which she is not sure of: a slow thing like water going over a weir, that turns at the end into a dance and stops before the dance is finished. 'That's the trouble with them,' she says. 'They stop. There's never a next bit.'".
  }
  Topic linnet_play_love with linnet "Ask Linnet Gale to play you something" when lullOpen() and linnetLoves(linnet) and not linnetTune(linnet) {
    Says "She plays the four notes that are you, and the four that answer them, and then goes on, and it is a tune, a whole one, that goes somewhere and comes back changed. When she stops she sits looking at the fiddle. 'That's the first one with a next bit,' she says.".
  }
  Event linnet_keepsake near linnet when keeps(linnet, keepsake) and madeFor(keepsake, linnet) "Linnet holds the little carving in both hands and looks at it, and then at the window, where the sun is going. 'Stay till the Watching,' she says. 'Stay and see if it holds.' At sunset it is still in her hands, and she says nothing; she takes up the fiddle and plays, there in the window over the green, and down at the Long Table they stop talking to listen, and before she is done the children have the tune, and are singing it, wrong, under the table." then {
    Assert keepsakeKept(keepsake). Assert linnetTune(linnet). Assert spreadFact(tune_told).
  }
  Entity tune_told: fact "Linnet's tune".
  // What she asks, on the Working Day or after.
  Relation stayPromised(group). Relation linnetWillCome(group).
  Topic linnet_tomorrow with linnet "Linnet Gale asks whether you will be here tomorrow" when lullOpen() and linnetLoves(linnet) and (dayThree() or pastThree()) and not stayPromised(party) and not linnetWillCome(linnet) {
    Says "Linnet is sitting on the window-seat with her arms round her knees. 'Tomorrow,' she says. 'Will you be here tomorrow?' She means it the Lull's way: the next Lullday, which for you is a week. She means it the other way too, and you both know it. 'Don't answer now,' she says. 'Answer before midnight. I want to hear what you mean.'".
  }
  Topic linnet_stay with linnet "Tell Linnet Gale that you will stay in the Lull" when lullOpen() and linnetLoves(linnet) and (dayThree() or pastThree()) and not stayPromised(party) and not linnetWillCome(linnet) once {
    Grave "Every night you sleep in the Lull is a week gone in the world outside.".
    Says "Linnet looks at you for a long time. 'Every night a week,' she says. 'Everything out there, going on without you. All the people.' She puts her hand flat on your chest. 'You mean it,' she says, surprised, as if she could feel it there. 'All right. All right, then.' She takes up the fiddle, and does not play, and holds it.".
    On discuss { Assert stayPromised(party). }
  }
  Topic linnet_come with linnet "Ask Linnet Gale to come out over the Tump with you" when lullOpen() and linnetLoves(linnet) and (dayThree() or pastThree()) and not stayPromised(party) and not linnetWillCome(linnet) once {
    Says "Linnet's face goes white, and then very bright. 'Out,' she says. 'Into all that.' She looks round the music room, the charcoal on the walls. 'Mother would have one day for every seven of mine. I'd come back for the Watching and she'd say, You look tired.' She swallows. 'I'd be loud. I'd be in a hurry. I'd have tomorrows.' She stands up. 'Yes. Ask me again in the road, so I know you meant it.'".
    On discuss { Assert linnetWillCome(linnet). Assert willing(linnet, actor). }
  }
  Promise stay_promise "to stay in the Lull, with Linnet" to linnet kept when stayPromised(party) and lullCount(clock) >= firstLull(clock) + 5 and inLull(party) "Linnet has counted five of your weeks on the window-frame of the music room, in charcoal, and stopped counting." broken when stayPromised(party) and lullEvening() and not inLull(party) "Somewhere in Linger, in the music room over the Open Hand, a tune is going round and round without a next bit." .
  Topic linnet_travel with linnet travelling "Ask Linnet what she makes of the world" when travelsWith(linnet, party) and not inLull(party) once {
    Says "'It's so loud,' says Linnet, delighted, with her fiddle under her arm, looking at everything. 'Everything's going somewhere. Do you hear that? That man's late. He's late! For something!' She plays four notes at a passing cart, and the carter looks round. 'I'm going to make a tune about him,' she says. 'And tomorrow I'm going to make one about tomorrow.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/the-lull/lore.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  Description "Links outward from Linger: a shift that is still being worked somewhere else, the Glossary shown a Collegium book, and a surveyor with a chain.".

  // ── A world event, read: the Old Shift hears of a ship ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe lore_shift_ship at almshouse when befell(remainder_kept) "One of the Old Shift has been moved to the window and sits looking out at nothing, with her hands going. 'There is a ship,' she says, to no one, 'that has been left on the other side of a door, and they are sailing on, and nobody has relieved the watch.' The warden says she has said it since Tuesday. 'It is only the Shift,' he says. 'They do get a feeling when somebody else is still on.'".

  // ── A visitor from elsewhere: the Collegium's glossary ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_glossary_kin "The Collegium's glossary of the old script, shown to the Glossary's keeper, has a column of marks that the Glossary of Linger has in the margin of its own Rule, a hundred years apart in the same hand.".
  Topic lore_aldith_glossary with aldith "Show Aldith Mote the Collegium's glossary" when holding(actor, old_glossary) once {
    Says "Aldith turns the book over, weighs it in her palm like a loaf, and says nothing for long enough that you wonder whether she heard. Then she crosses to the shelf behind her and takes down a thin volume, bound in the grey of the almshouse, and lays the two side by side. 'The marks in the margin of our Rule,' she says, 'and the marks in your column. The same. Not the same words. The same hand: look how it makes the descender.' Her mouth works. 'Somebody carried a column of marks from wherever this came from, and copied it into the Rule of a house for tired people. We have said the Rule aloud for two hundred years.' She closes the almshouse book on her finger. 'I think we have been reading someone else's letter.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_glossary_kin). }
  }

  // ── The surveyor, and the almanack woman ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_pym_lull "Orlando Pym of the Collegium of Measures chained the march road at Sixways and found the Lull nine chains shorter at the Fold than it is on the Collegium's table. He has gone on to the Pass at Larum before the White comes down.".
  Topic lore_dorcas_pym with dorcas "Ask Dorcas Trewin about the man with a chain" when true once {
    Says "'He sat there,' says Dorcas, pointing with her chin at the window-seat, 'and ate a pie with one hand and wrote in a book with the other, and did not spill. Pym. From the Measures. He had a boy to hold the stake.' She leans on the bar. 'He said the Lull is nine chains shorter at the Fold than it is in the Collegium. I said, perhaps it has been shortened. He wrote that down. Went on up toward Larum and the Pass, before the snow, he said, to get the Teeth.' She considers. 'He never asked once whether anyone here was asleep. Everyone else asks.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_pym_lull). }
  }
}

data/adventures/the-lull/market.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── The Dusk Market: Quick Nan and the ribbons ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Nan sells on the Green from six until four on Lulldays, and is home over the Tump before sunset. What she sold
  // goes back to her tray at sunset, wherever she is; the coin she took is out of the Lull and stays hers. Mothers of
  // Linger buy her bright ribbons for their newborns to tie on the Strike Post; at the Watching the ribbons go, and
  // the Glossers say a ribbon that ravels was not meant.
  Rule nan_in when lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 16 and not nanBanned(nan) and not nanDelayed(nan) and able(nan) and not at(nan, green) { Assert at(nan, green). Assert at(gurney, green). }
  Rule nan_out when (folded() or hour(clock) >= 16) and not nanDelayed(nan) and able(nan) and not at(nan, sx_street) { Assert at(nan, sx_street). Assert at(gurney, sx_street). }
  Relation nanBanned(group). Relation nanDelayed(group). Relation nanExposed(group). Relation nanReformed(group). Relation nanPartner(group).
  Observe nan_on_green at green when lullOpen() and at(nan, green) and hour(clock) < 16 "By the Gift Hall steps Quick Nan has her tray open on a trestle, with Gurney behind her like a wall: pasties, tin whistles, and ribbons, red and blue and a yellow like nothing that grows in the Lull. Lull women are buying the ribbons, two and three at a time.".
  Observe post_nan_ribbons at strike_post as feature when lullOpen() and not nanExposed(nan) and not nanReformed(nan) and not nanBanned(nan) "Among the faded ribbons at the bottom of the Post, a few are new and very bright: a red, a yellow like nothing that grows in the Lull.".

  Person jenet "Jenet Hollis" at chapel {
    Role "a young mother of Linger, with a baby in a shawl". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
    Greets "A young woman is sitting on the bench round the wall of the chapel with a baby asleep in a shawl on her chest, watching the starlings in the basin. She has been crying, and has stopped, and is waiting to start again.".
    Greets again "Jenet Hollis glances up from the baby and down again, and has already begun to hum. 'Quiet today,' she says, to the child, or to you. 'It is always quiet today. That is the whole of what a Lull is, and I have never once got tired of it.'".
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(jenet). Initially Assert dayAt(jenet, chapel). Initially Assert bedAt(jenet, weavers_row).
  Relation jenetHealed(group).
  Topic jenet_ribbon with jenet "Ask Jenet Hollis what is the matter" when lullOpen() and not jenetHealed(jenet) once {
    Says "'Robin's ribbon,' says Jenet. 'My boy. He came last Lullday and I tied his ribbon on the Post in the morning, like everyone, and at the Watching it was gone. Just gone. Off the Post.' She looks down at the baby. 'Glosser Fenn says a ribbon that ravels wasn't meant. He was very kind about it.' Her mouth goes wrong. 'I love him. I'm sure I love him. I sit here and I look at him and I'm sure. But it ravelled. And the Glosser says you can't fool the sunset.' The baby wakes, and she rocks him, and he sleeps.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ribbon_ravelled). }
  }
  Discovery ribbon_ravelled "Jenet Hollis's newborn's ribbon came off the Strike Post at the Watching. The Glosser told her a ribbon that ravels was not meant, and she is afraid she does not love her child.".
  Topic jenet_where with jenet "Ask Jenet Hollis where the ribbon came from" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, ribbon_ravelled) and not jenetHealed(jenet) once {
    Says "'Off Quick Nan's tray,' says Jenet, surprised. 'On the Green. Everybody has hers now. They're so bright. We've nothing in the Lull that dyes like that yellow.' She frowns. 'Moll Lacey's girl's went too. And the Tolley twins'. Glosser Fenn says it's a hard year.' She looks at you. 'Why?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ribbon_from_nan). }
  }
  Discovery ribbon_from_nan "Jenet Hollis bought her son's ribbon from Quick Nan's tray on the Green. Other mothers' ribbons from Nan have gone from the Post too.".
  // Buying one, to see.
  Kind lull_ribbon_kind "one of Quick Nan's ribbons, bought in the Lull" is gear worth 1 weighing 0 described "A length of bright red ribbon off Quick Nan's tray, the kind a Lull child ties to the Strike Post; bought on the Green.".
  Item nan_ribbon "one of Quick Nan's ribbons, bought in the Lull" is lull_ribbon_kind at limbo.
  Initially Assert unmeant(nan_ribbon). Initially Assert ownRavel(nan_ribbon).
  Action buy_lull_ribbon(actor: group, site: place) "Buy a ribbon off Quick Nan's tray for a coin" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, green) and at(nan, green) and lullOpen() and quantity(actor, gold) >= 1 and at(nan_ribbon, limbo) and not ravelled(nan_ribbon).
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Increase quantity(nan, gold) by 1. Retract at(nan_ribbon, limbo). Give nan_ribbon to actor. }
    Result "'Lovely choice,' says Nan, and the coin is gone into her apron before the ribbon is in your hand.".
  }
  Rule nan_ribbon_ravels when lullDusk() and carries(party, nan_ribbon)
    says "The ribbon you bought off Quick Nan's tray slides out of your pack like a snake out of a basket and is gone, off toward the Tump, quick as a swift. The coin does not come back. Nan is over the hill with it." teaches nan_ribbons_ravel {
    Spend lull_ribbon_kind from party. Assert at(nan_ribbon, limbo). Assert ravelled(nan_ribbon).
  }
  Discovery nan_ribbons_ravel "What Quick Nan sells in the Lull goes back to her at sunset, as any sale there does; but she is over the Tump by then, with the coin, which stays hers. The mothers' ribbons were never theirs to mean.".
  Topic jenet_told with jenet "Tell Jenet Hollis that the ribbon was sold, and that a sale comes undone, whoever loves whom" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, ribbon_from_nan) and (knows(actor, nan_ribbons_ravel) or knows(actor, wage_ravels) or knows(actor, meaning_law)) and not jenetHealed(jenet) once {
    Says "Jenet looks at you without understanding, and then all at once she does, and her whole face comes undone. 'Sold,' she says. 'It was sold.' She holds the baby so tight that he wakes and complains. 'It wasn't him. It wasn't me. It was Nan's.' She is laughing. 'I'll weave him one. Tonight. Off my own loom, blue, the ugly blue we have, and I'll tie it on myself.' She stands up. 'Glosser Fenn,' she says, in quite a different voice, 'is going to hear about this.'".
    On discuss { Assert jenetHealed(jenet). }
  }
  Observe post_jenet at strike_post as feature when lullOpen() and jenetHealed(jenet) "At the bottom of the Post there is a new ribbon in the ugly Lull blue, tied in a fierce knot: ROBIN HOLLIS, says the label.".
  // Nan, confronted on the Green.
  Topic nan_confronted with nan "Tell Quick Nan you know what happens to her ribbons at sunset" when lullOpen() and inLull(party) and knows(actor, nan_ribbons_ravel) and not nanReformed(nan) and not nanExposed(nan) and not nanPartner(nan) once {
    Says "Nan's smile does not move at all. 'Everything I sell's good till sunset, love,' she says. 'They know the law. It's their law.' She straightens a whistle on the tray. 'Nobody makes them buy. And I'll tell you what: a Lull ribbon's a dull thing. Mine are pretty. Pretty for a day's better than dull for ever, ask anybody.' Gurney, behind her, has stopped looking at the Green and is looking at you.".
    On discuss { Assert nanConfronted(nan). }
  }
  Relation nanConfronted(group).
  Action shame_nan(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Quick Nan what the mothers think it means when the ribbon goes" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(nan, site) and nanConfronted(nan) and not nanReformed(nan) and not nanExposed(nan) and lullOpen().
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert nanReformed(nan). Decrease quantity(nan, gold) by 6 or to nothing. }
    On failure { Assert nanShrugged(nan). }
    Result "You tell her about Jenet Hollis in the chapel with her baby, and what the Glosser said, and what Jenet has been sitting there believing. Nan listens with her head on one side. When you have done she is quiet a moment. Then she takes the ribbons off her tray, all of them, and stuffs them in her apron. 'I've a girl myself,' she says, not to you. 'In the mill towns. With her gran.' She counts six coins out of her apron and puts them in your hand. 'For the mothers. Tell them it was the dye.' She shuts the tray. 'Pasties only, from now. Pasties they eat before sunset.'".
    Otherwise "Nan hears you out with her bright smile, and says, 'Sad, love, sad,' and sells a ribbon over your shoulder to the next woman.".
  }
  Relation nanShrugged(group).
  Action threaten_nan(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Quick Nan that if she sells another ribbon in the Lull, you will see to it she regrets it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(nan, site) and nanConfronted(nan) and not nanReformed(nan) and not nanExposed(nan) and lullOpen().
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert nanReformed(nan). }
    On failure { Retract peaceable(gurney). Assert hostile(gurney, actor). Assert assails(gurney, actor). }
    Result "Nan looks at you, and at Gurney, and at the Green full of Lull folk who would not lift a hand, and back at you, and decides. 'No more ribbons,' she says. 'There. Happy?' She is not frightened. She is doing sums.".
    Otherwise "Nan laughs, and says, 'Gurney,' and the big man comes round the trestle with his hands open, and they do not stay open.".
  }
  // The clever way: keep her talking past four, and let the sunset catch her in the Lull.
  Action delay_nan(actor: group, site: place) "Keep Quick Nan talking until it is too late for her to leave before sunset" {
    Description "She will want to be over the Tump by sunset. Talk well enough, and she will not notice the shadows.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(nan, site) and at(actor, green) and knows(actor, nan_ribbons_ravel) and lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 14 and hour(clock) < 16 and not nanDelayed(nan) and not nanReformed(nan) and not nanExposed(nan).
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_fair).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert nanDelayed(nan). }
    Result "You ask Nan about her pasties, and her girl in the mill towns, and the price of tin, and you admire her whistles, and you buy a pasty and ask how she crimps it, and she shows you, and tells you about her mother's, and Gurney sits down on the grass, and the shadow of the Tump comes across the Green and nobody remarks it.".
    Otherwise "Nan answers you with half her mind and keeps one eye on the shadow of the Tump, and at four she shuts her tray in the middle of your sentence. 'Lovely talking, love,' she says, and goes.".
  }
  Rule nan_caught at green when lullDusk() and nanDelayed(nan) and at(nan, green) and not nanExposed(nan)
    says "The sun goes off the Tump, and Quick Nan, who has just looked up and seen where the shadow is, says a word that stops the Long Table. Then it happens: from every pocket and pack along the Table, from the children's hands and the necks of the cats, Nan's day comes back to her: pasties, whistles, and from the top of the Tump a stream of bright ribbons that pours down the hill in the dusk like a flock of finches and into her tray. And out of her apron, the coins: up, and out, and away down the Long Table to the purses they came from, ringing on the boards. Nobody speaks. Then Jenet Hollis stands up with her baby and says, very clearly, 'It was sold,' and the Long Table understands all at once, and the noise it makes is not a kind one. Hobday Pryce walks Nan and Gurney to the Tump road himself, and tells them not to come back." {
    Assert nanExposed(nan). Assert nanBanned(nan). Assert jenetHealed(jenet). Retract nanDelayed(nan). Assert at(nan, sx_street). Assert at(gurney, sx_street).
  }
  Topic hobday_nan with hobday "Tell Hobday Pryce what Quick Nan's ribbons are" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, nan_ribbons_ravel) and not nanBanned(nan) and not nanReformed(nan) and not nanPartner(nan) once {
    Says "Hobday goes from pink to purple, slowly, like a sky. 'The mothers,' he says. 'The mothers have been coming to me. Asking if they're bad mothers.' He takes up his staff. 'She'll not come over the Tump again. Not while I'm Chief Warden.' He looks at you. 'Thank you. That was well done. That was meant.'".
    On discuss { Assert nanBanned(nan). Assert hobdayGrateful(hobday). }
  }
  Relation hobdayGrateful(group).
  // Or go in with her.
  Topic nan_partner with nan "Offer to carry Quick Nan's tray in the Lull for a share of the take" when knows(actor, nan_hours) and not nanReformed(nan) and not nanBanned(nan) and not nanExposed(nan) and not nanPartner(nan) once {
    Says "Nan looks you up and down. 'Not a bad idea,' she says. 'Gurney frightens them. You look like someone they'd buy a ribbon from.' She spits on her palm and holds it out. 'A third of the morning's take, and out by four, and if anyone asks, the ribbons are for luck.'".
    On discuss { Assert nanPartner(nan). }
  }
  Relation nanCarried(group).
  Action carry_tray(actor: group, site: place) "Carry Quick Nan's tray through the morning on the Green, for a third of the take" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, green) and at(nan, green) and nanPartner(nan) and lullOpen() and hour(clock) < 14 and not nanCarried(actor).
    Time 24.
    On success { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Assert nanCarried(actor). }
    Result "You stand on the Green with the tray round your neck and smile, and the Lull women come, and buy, ribbons mostly, for babies; and at two Nan counts the take on the trestle and pushes your third across. Four coin. It stays in your hand, because you will be over the Tump with it before sunset. You find you do not look at the Post on your way out.".
  }
  Rule tray_resets when hour(clock) == 0 and nanCarried(?g) { Retract nanCarried(?g). }
}

data/adventures/the-lull/placed.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // The country beyond a march of a generated world: the company that comes in by the march road is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  // What is said of the Lull in the country behind it: once the Working Day is over, it is old news there.
  Entity word: fact "What is said of the Lull in the country behind it.".
  Rule word_old when workingOver(lull_country) and not stale(word) { Assert stale(word). }
}

data/adventures/the-lull/sixnight.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── The Wrought Mill, by day ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe bridge_scene at mill_bridge when lullOpen() and not bridgeBuilt(club) "Here the Shift Bridge went over the mill-leat to the Mill yard, and does not now: two stone piers, a few black timbers hanging from the far one, and the leat running deep and quick between. The young of Linger sit on the near end with their legs over the water. Across the leat the Mill stands up seven storeys, with its windows dark.".
  Observe bridge_dark at mill_bridge when folded() and not bridgeBuilt(club) "The broken end of the Shift Bridge in the dark. The leat is loud. Across it, the Mill is not dark. In every one of its seven storeys of windows there is a faint grey light, like dawn seen through cloth, and it is moving.".
  Thing bridge_gap "the gap in the Shift Bridge" on shift_bridge is scenery {
    State broken blocking "The Shift Bridge is down: two old piers, and the leat running deep and quick between them.".
    State mended "The Shift Bridge is whole again, new oak over old stone.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(bridge_gap, broken).
  Observe yard_mill at mill_yard when lullOpen() "The Mill yard: setts with grass between, a mounting-block, the great double doors of the Mill, iron-studded, shut. Over the doors is a stone shield with a hammer and a fleece on it and a name cut away. Along the ground floor the windows are boarded; one of them, low down, has its boards painted white and lettered: GLOSS 3. THAT THE MILL IS STOPPED.".
  Observe yard_mill_dark at mill_yard when folded() "The Mill yard in the dark, and the Mill above it lit grey from within, every window, all seven storeys, and the whole building faintly shaking. From inside comes a sound like heavy rain on a roof that does not stop: looms, hundreds of them, going. The boarded window low down is not boarded. It is open, the way it was the night the strikers climbed out of it.".
  Observe floor_scene at mill_floor when lullOpen() "The ground floor of the Mill: a long room of iron pillars and dust, the light coming grey through the boarded windows. The great doors are barred on the inside with a beam of black oak as thick as a man, set in iron brackets, and the beam is cut all over with letters.".
  Observe floor_dark at mill_floor when folded() "The Mill's ground floor in the grey light that comes down the stairwell from above, where the noise is. The lint of the Ravel lies on the floor like snow and drifts in the draught from the stair. The great doors are barred on the inside with a beam of black oak cut all over with letters, and they are moving: outward, a finger's breadth, against the beam, and back, and again, very slowly, though there is nobody at them, as if the whole Mill were leaning on them from inside, breathing.".
  Thing beam "the beam across the Mill doors" at mill_floor {
    State barring "Across the Mill doors, on the inside, lies the strikers' beam.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(beam, barring).
  Observe beam_read at mill_floor as feature when not knows(party, beam_names) and tried(beam, looking) "Cut deep along the beam, in capitals: WE HAVE STOPPED. And under it, names, fifty-one of them, in fifty-one hands, some cut neat and some hacked, some barely letters: AGNES CRANE. AMOS TOLLEY. HESTER LUMB. NELL LUMB, in a child's hand, a little crooked, very deep. SIMEON'S FATHER, OSWY EDDOWES. You read them all. There is no Tobias Lindsell." teaches beam_names.
  Discovery beam_names "On the beam that bars the Mill doors from inside are cut WE HAVE STOPPED and the fifty-one strikers' names: Agnes Crane, Amos Tolley, Hester Lumb, Nell Lumb, Oswy Eddowes and the rest. Tobias Lindsell's name is not among them.".
  Observe loom_scene at loom_floor when lullOpen() "The loom floor: a hall the length of the Mill, and in it looms, row on row, a hundred of them, with warps still on them gone grey as cobweb, and every shuttle lying where it was dropped fifty-seven years ago. It is completely silent. Dust lies on the dust.".
  Observe loom_dark at loom_floor when folded() "The loom floor, lit grey from nowhere, and every loom going: a hundred of them, the shuttles flying, the beaters coming down, the noise like a mill-race. At each loom something is working it. They have the shape of weavers, and are made of grey lint, the Ravel packed into the shape of a woman, a boy, a man, and they have no faces, and they do not stop. The cloth comes off the looms grey and endless and goes away into the dark at the end of the hall.".
  Observe loft_scene_bell at bell_loft when lullOpen() "The bell loft under the Mill's roof: rafters, pigeons, a bell on a beam with its rope hanging down the well to the floors below, and in a corner an iron-bound chest under a heap of sacking.".
  Observe loft_bell_dark at bell_loft when folded() "The bell loft, grey-lit and shaking with the looms below. The bell on its beam swings a little, by itself.".
  Observe gap_scene at gap when true "A long low tunnel the river once took: the old tail-race, cut square in the rock, half full of black water running toward the hill's heart. Grey lint is caught along the waterline like scum, and the walls are scored with tally-marks in sevens, very old, as if somebody once counted days down here.".
  Observe pit_scene at wheel_pit when true "The wheel-pit under the Mill: the great wheel standing still in a slot of black water, its buckets furred with weed, and beyond it, low, the tail-race going away into the hill, wet-walled and breathing cold.".

  // The strikers' window: open in the dark, boarded in the day.
  Thing strikers_boards "the boards on the strikers' window" on strikers_window is scenery {
    State boarded blocking "The low window the strikers climbed out of is boarded, and the boards are painted: GLOSS 3. THAT THE MILL IS STOPPED.".
    State open "The strikers' window stands open.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(strikers_boards, boarded).
  Rule window_opens_dark when folded() and state(strikers_boards, boarded) { Assert state(strikers_boards, open). }
  Rule window_boarded_day when lullOpen() and state(strikers_boards, open) { Assert state(strikers_boards, boarded). }

  // ── The Sixnight ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Whoever is awake in the Lull at midnight on its day is in the six days it does not keep. The valley is unlit, its
  // people asleep and not to be woken, the Ravel drifting, the Mill working. It explains nothing.
  // Told as the company first sees the dark, wherever in the valley it is; never to a company that slept through.
  Observe sixnight_tump within tump as felt when inSixnight() and at(party, ?here) and sixnightBegan(?here) "It is past midnight. There was no sound to it: the starlings stopped, all at once, in the middle of a note, and the lights went out together as if a door had shut on them, and the stars went. Not behind cloud. Out. You are standing in the Lull in a dark with no top to it, and nobody else in the valley is awake.".
  Observe sixnight_linger within linger as felt when inSixnight() and at(party, ?here) and sixnightBegan(?here) "It is past midnight. There was no sound to it: the starlings stopped, all at once, in the middle of a note, and the lanterns along the Long Table went out together as if a door had shut on them, and the stars went. Not behind cloud. Out. You are standing in the Lull in a dark with no top to it, and nobody else in the valley is awake.".
  Observe sixnight_mill within mill as felt when inSixnight() and at(party, ?here) and sixnightBegan(?here) "It is past midnight. There was no sound to it, except that the starlings stopped, and the stars went out, and the Mill began.".
  Observe sixnight_wild within hangers as felt when inSixnight() and at(party, ?here) and sixnightBegan(?here) "It is past midnight. The birds stopped all at once in the middle of a note, and the stars went out, and nobody else in the valley is awake.".
  Observe sixnight_tarn within tarn as felt when inSixnight() and at(party, ?here) and sixnightBegan(?here) "It is past midnight. The birds stopped all at once in the middle of a note, and the stars went out of the tarn, and nobody else in the valley is awake.".
  Observe sixnight_swallow within swallow as felt when inSixnight() and at(party, ?here) and sixnightBegan(?here) "It is past midnight. The birds stopped all at once, and the stars went out, and the river goes on into the hill in the dark.".
  Rule sixnight_now when inSixnight() and not inSixnightNow(party) and at(party, ?p) { Assert inSixnightNow(party). Assert sixnightBegan(?p). }
  Rule sixnight_moved when sixnightBegan(?p) and not at(party, ?p) { Retract sixnightBegan(?p). Assert sixnightToldDone(party). }
  Relation sixnightBegan(place). Relation sixnightToldDone(group). Relation sixnightLived(group).
  Relation inSixnightNow(group).
  Rule sixnight_lifts when inSixnightNow(party) and lullOpen() and inLull(party) and not sixnightLived(party)
    says "The six days are over. The dark has gone the way it came, all at once, and there are starlings, and the smell of the Long Table, and it is Lullday; and you have been where nobody in the Lull has been but Hob Linsey and his bees." teaches sixnight_known { Retract inSixnightNow(party). Retract sixnightToldDone(party). Assert sixnightLived(party). }
  Rule sixnight_escaped when inSixnightNow(party) and at(party, sx_spring) and not sixnightLived(party)
    says "You come up out of the hill on your hands and knees beside a spring, into an ordinary night with stars in it and a dog barking somewhere and the Waiting Woman's back window lit. It is the world's night, the ordinary kind, that ends in the morning. Behind you the Gap breathes wool." teaches sixnight_known { Retract inSixnightNow(party). Retract sixnightToldDone(party). Assert sixnightLived(party). }
  Rule sixnight_over when inSixnightNow(party) and sixnightLived(party) and (lullOpen() or at(party, sx_spring)) { Retract inSixnightNow(party). Retract sixnightToldDone(party). }
  Discovery sixnight_known "Whoever is awake in the Lull at its midnight is in the six days it does not keep: a dark without stars, the people asleep and not to be woken, and the Mill working.".
  Observe green_sound at green as sound when folded() "From up the leat, very faint, comes a sound like rain on a roof that does not stop.".
  Observe sixnight_shoulder at tump_shoulder as feature when folded() and inSixnightNow(party) "The road you came by goes up into the dark and does not come down anywhere. There is no stone at the end of it. There is no end of it.".
  Topic sleeper_wake with folk "Try to wake the people of Linger" when folded() once {
    Says "You shake a shoulder; you shout; you hold a light to a face. They sleep on with their hands open, breathing very slowly, a breath to your ten, and do not wake.".
  }

  // The Hands.
  Species hands_kind "a shape of grey lint, working" like spirit temperament seizing described "The shape of a weaver, made of the Ravel: grey lint packed close into a body, with hands that are very exact and no face at all.".
  Person hands "the Hands" at limbo {
    Role "shapes of grey lint in the shape of weavers, with no faces, working". Species hands_kind. Numbers 12. Pronouns it.
    Temperament seizing.
    Warns "Along the nearest row the Hands stop. All of them, at once, the shuttles hanging. They turn toward you the places where their faces are not, and the looms behind them go on by themselves. The nearest holds out a shuttle to you. There is no fighting a whole floor of this. Lie down, or take it, or go.".
    Comes "The Hands come down the rows to you without hurry, and take you by the arms with fingers like wet wool, very gently, and put you at a loom, and put the shuttle in your hand.".
  }
  Rule hands_wake when folded() and not at(hands, loom_floor) and able(hands) { Assert at(hands, loom_floor). }
  Rule hands_sleep when lullOpen() and not at(hands, limbo) { Assert at(hands, limbo). Retract tolerates(hands, party). }
  // Set to work: the company is kept at the loom, and can only work until the Lull's morning, or lie down open-handed.
  Relation atLoom(group).
  Rule hands_take when captured(hands, party) and not atLoom(party)
    says "There is a loom in front of you and a shuttle in your hand, and your hands are working it. They are quite good at it. They seem to know how. Around you the Hands work without looking at you, and if you stop, the nearest turns toward you, and waits." {
    Assert atLoom(party). Retract captured(hands, party). Assert tolerates(hands, party).
  }
  Rule hands_return when atLoom(party) and inSixnight() and not at(party, loom_floor) and not sleptLull(party)
    says "On the stair, gently, wet-wool hands take you by the arms, and turn you round, and bring you back to your loom." { Assert at(party, loom_floor). }
  Rule loom_freed when atLoom(party) and lullOpen() { Retract atLoom(party). }
  Item shift_bolt "a bolt of the Long Shift's cloth" is long_shift_cloth at limbo.
  Action work_loom(actor: group, site: place) "Work the loom, as they want, until the Lull's morning" {
    Description "Six days, less what has gone. There is nothing else.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, loom_floor) and atLoom(actor) and inSixnight().
    Time untilLull(clock).
    On success { Retract atLoom(actor). Assert at(actor, mill_yard). Retract at(shift_bolt, limbo). Give shift_bolt to actor. Assert weary(actor). Assert sleptLull(actor). Assert knows(actor, wove_shift). }
    Result "You work. There is no other word for it, and no other thing. The shuttle goes, the beater comes down, the cloth comes, and the grey light does not change, and you do not get hungry or thirsty or sleep, and you do not stop, because there is nothing to stop for, and the Hands beside you do not stop. Somewhere in it you look up for a window, and there is none, and you go on. Then the bell above you rings once, and you are standing in the Mill yard in the morning with starlings going over and a bolt of grey cloth in your arms that you wove, and your hands ache to the shoulder, and it is Lullday.".
  }
  // Lying down open-handed, as the strikers did: neither the Hands nor the Overseer touch the resting.
  Action lie_open(actor: group, site: place) "Lie down where you are with your hands open, palms up, as the strikers did" {
    Description "Whatever works the Mill does not touch the resting. Or so Hob Linsey says.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and inSixnight() and knows(actor, open_hands) and (warned(hands, actor) or warned(overseer, actor) or assails(overseer, actor)) and not atLoom(actor).
    On success { Retract warned(hands, actor). Retract warned(overseer, actor). Retract assails(overseer, actor). Retract assails(hands, actor). Assert tolerates(hands, actor). Assert tolerates(overseer, actor). Assert restingBefore(actor). }
    Result "You lie down on the boards with your hands open, palms up, and the noise of the looms goes on over you. Something tall comes and stands over you, and looks, if it is looking, a long time. Then it goes away. When you get up, nothing turns toward you. You are, as far as the Mill is concerned, on strike.".
  }
  Relation restingBefore(group).
  Rule chest_noticed when state(pay_chest, open) and at(overseer, bell_loft) and able(overseer) and tolerates(overseer, party) and at(party, bell_loft) and not overseerBroken(overseer)
    says "The lid of the pay-chest goes back, and the bell rings by itself, once, and the tall thing by the bell turns its hat toward you. Resting is one thing. This is another." { Retract tolerates(overseer, party). Assert assails(overseer, party). }
  Discovery wove_shift "You worked the six days at a loom of the Wrought Mill in the dark, beside the Hands, and came out on the Lull's morning with a bolt of grey cloth that you wove.".

  // The Overseer, in the bell loft, over the pay-chest.
  Species overseer_kind "a tall shape of iron and lint" like golem temperament territorial described "Taller than a door, a coat of grey lint over a frame of iron, a hand like a bell-clapper, and where the face should be a bailiff's iron hat with nothing under it.".
  Person overseer "the Overseer" at limbo {
    Role "a tall shape of iron and lint with a bailiff's hat for a face, beside the bell". Species overseer_kind. Level 6. Pronouns it.
    Temperament territorial.
    Lair bell_loft. Refuge loom_floor. Fears performance.
    Warns "By the bell, in the grey light, something unfolds that you took for a heap of sacking: tall, iron under lint, a bailiff's hat where a face should be. It lifts one long arm toward the bell-rope. It does not care that you are here; it cares that you are idle here. It will ring, and come, unless you take up work, or lie down like a striker, or are gone. Someone who could sing the strikers' hymn at it might make it remember what it lost.".
    Comes "The Overseer comes across the loft at you in three long strides with the bell ringing behind it, and the floor below goes silent to listen.".
    Flinches "You sing it, the hymn they sang on the Tump, Rest and be thankful, badly, and the tall thing stops with its arm up, and the hat turns as if to listen, and then it goes down the ladder backwards into the noise of the looms and is lost among the Hands.".
    Pleads "The Overseer goes down on its iron knees with a sound like a dropped anvil, and the bailiff's hat rolls off, and there is nothing under it at all.".
  }
  Rule overseer_wakes when folded() and at(overseer, limbo) and able(overseer) and not overseerBroken(overseer) { Assert at(overseer, bell_loft). }
  Rule overseer_sleeps when lullOpen() and not at(overseer, limbo) { Assert at(overseer, limbo). }
  Relation overseerBroken(group).
  Rule overseer_down when dead(overseer) and not overseerBroken(overseer) { Assert overseerBroken(overseer). }
  Thing pay_chest "the Wroughts' pay-chest" at bell_loft {
    Holds.
    State locked closed "In the corner, under sacking, stands an iron-bound chest with a hammer and a fleece painted on its lid.".
    State open "The Wroughts' pay-chest stands open, and the smell that comes out of it is of old coin.".
    Change pick "Pick the lock of the pay-chest" from locked to open needing lockwork.
    Change force "Lever the lid of the pay-chest off its hinges" from locked to open needing crowbar.
    Change smash "Break the pay-chest's lock with a blow" from locked to open needing brawn.
  }
  Initially Assert state(pay_chest, locked).
  Kind shilling_kind "one shilling, notched" is gear worth 1 weighing 0 described "A single old silver shilling, worn, with a notch filed in its edge by somebody who meant to know it again.".
  Item shillings "a bag of the Wroughts' shillings" is wrought_shillings_kind in pay_chest.
  Item notched_shilling "one shilling, notched" is shilling_kind in pay_chest.
  Observe chest_looked near pay_chest when tried(pay_chest, looking) "The lid is painted with the Wroughts' hammer and fleece. Chalked inside the lid, very faint: SEVENTH DAY. 1 TAKER.".
  // The notched shilling, given to Tobias.
  Topic tobias_shilling with tobias "Give Tobias Lindsell the notched shilling from the Wroughts' pay-chest" when lullOpen() and carries(party, notched_shilling) and tobiasConfessed(tobias) and not tobiasForgiven(tobias) once {
    Says "Tobias turns the shilling over and finds the notch with his thumbnail without looking, the way you find a key in your own pocket. 'I filed that,' he says. 'With a nail. In the Mill, at the loom, on the seventh day, so I'd know it. A shilling a day.' He holds it up to the window. 'It was gone from my pocket at sunset. Back to the bailiff. I've thought of it every day since. Every day.' He closes his hand on it. 'Fifty-seven years in a box.' He laughs, which you have not heard him do. 'In a box, in the dark, with the rest. Not even spent.' He puts it in his waistcoat pocket and pats it. 'I'll keep it. Not for the shame of it. For the joke.'".
    On discuss { Spend shilling_kind from actor. Assert tobiasForgiven(tobias). }
  }
}

data/adventures/the-lull/sixways.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  Description "Sixways, a hamlet on the march that lives by a valley you can walk into one day in seven; and the Lull, that valley, where it has been the holy day for fifty-seven years and whatever is done without meaning it comes apart at sunset.".

  // ── The country ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // West to east: the march road comes into Sixways; the Fold-stone stands on the rise beyond it; one day in seven the
  // Lull road goes down from the stone over the Tump's shoulder into the valley. The valley runs north to south: Lammas
  // Tarn at its head, the Wrought Mill on its leat, Linger on the Idle, the Swallow at its foot where the river goes
  // under the hill. The Hangers are the beech woods of its western side.
  Place lull_country "the Lull country" is region.
  Place sixways "Sixways" is settlement within lull_country at 5, 3.
  Place fold "the Fold" is wilderness within lull_country at 4, 3.
  Place tump "the Tump" is wilderness within lull_country at 3, 2.
  Place linger "Linger" is settlement within lull_country at 2, 2.
  Place mill "the Wrought Mill" is site within lull_country at 2, 1.
  Place tarn "Lammas Tarn" is wilderness within lull_country at 2, 0.
  Place hangers "the Hangers" is wilderness within lull_country at 1, 1.
  Place swallow "the Swallow" is wilderness within lull_country at 2, 3.

  Initially Assert terrain(lull_country, forest).
  Initially Assert landform(tarn, land_lake). Initially Assert landform(hangers, land_wood).
  Place waiting_woman "the Waiting Woman" is building within sixways.
  Place coll_house "Ruth Coll's" is building within sixways.
  Place haskett_house "Haskett's" is building within sixways.
  Place simeon_house "Simeon Eddowes's cottage" is building within sixways.

  Place march_road "the march road at Sixways" is room within sixways at 0, 1.
  Place sx_street "Sixways street" is room within sixways at 1, 1.
  Place sx_taproom "the Waiting Woman's taproom" is room within waiting_woman at 1, 0.
  Place rooke_yard "Rooke's yard" is room within sixways at 2, 1.
  Place coll_kitchen "Ruth Coll's kitchen" is room within coll_house at 1, 2.
  Place haskett_loft "Haskett's cloth-loft" is room within haskett_house at 2, 0.
  Place exiles_row "Exiles' Row" is room within sixways at 2, 2.
  Place simeon_room "Simeon Eddowes's room" is room within simeon_house at 3, 2.
  Place sx_spring "the spring behind the Waiting Woman" is room within sixways at 0, 0.
  Place fold_stone "the Fold-stone" is room within fold at 0, 0.
  Place limbo "nowhere" is room within fold at 9, 9.

  Passage march_way "Sixways street" is road between march_road and sx_street taking 5 minutes.
  Passage taproom_door "the Waiting Woman's door" is door between sx_street and sx_taproom.
  Passage yard_gate "Rooke's yard gate" is gate between sx_street and rooke_yard.
  Passage coll_door "Ruth Coll's door" is door between sx_street and coll_kitchen.
  Passage haskett_stair "the outside stair to Haskett's loft" is steps between rooke_yard and haskett_loft.
  Passage row_lane "the lane to Exiles' Row" is path between sx_street and exiles_row taking 5 minutes.
  Passage simeon_door "Simeon Eddowes's door" is door between exiles_row and simeon_room.
  Passage spring_path "the path round the back of the inn" is path between sx_street and sx_spring taking 5 minutes.
  Passage stone_road "the road up to the Fold-stone" is road between sx_street and fold_stone taking 20 minutes.

  // ── What Sixways is ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe march_scene at march_road when true "The march road comes over the last rise and down into a hamlet of one street: flint walls, low thatch, a pump, and more carts than so few houses need. At every door there hangs a curtain of the same grey-gold cloth, and every one of them looks new. Beyond the roofs the road climbs on to a standing stone on a bare green rise, and stops.".
  Observe street_scene at sx_street when not dark() "Sixways street: the pump, the inn, a carter's yard, a herbwife's door with bunches hung in the porch, and the lane to a row of three cottages that stand a little apart. Everybody here seems to know what day it is in a way that people elsewhere do not. The road up the rise to the Fold-stone is where the Lull opens, when it opens; the Waiting Woman has a window on it.".
  Observe street_night at sx_street when dark() "Sixways street at night: the pump, the inn's lit window, and up on the rise the Fold-stone against the sky.".
  Observe street_count at sx_street when lullCycle(clock) < 6 and not weekReturned(lull_country) and not dark() "The board by the pump says, in chalk: LULL IN {lullDaysAway(clock)}.".
  Observe street_lullday at sx_street when lullday() and not weekReturned(lull_country) and not dark() "The board by the pump says, in chalk, LULLDAY, and underneath, in another hand, BACK BY MIDNIGHT.".
  Observe taproom_scene at sx_taproom when true "The Waiting Woman's taproom is low and long, with a settle by the fire and a window at the end that looks up the road to the stone. Everybody who sits down sits facing that window. On the wall is the inn's old sign, taken down and kept indoors: a young woman at a window, in fresh paint, her face very carefully done.".
  Observe yard_scene at rooke_yard when true "A carter's yard: two carts, a heap of harness, a grey mare in a stall with her head over the door, and against the wall, under a sack, something with four legs that somebody has been making and unmaking.".
  Observe coll_scene at coll_kitchen when true "Ruth Coll's kitchen smells of rue and boiled linen. Bunches hang from every beam, the jars on the dresser are labelled in a sharp hand, and a pestle stands in a mortar on the table, mid-sentence.".
  Observe haskett_loft_scene at haskett_loft when true "A long loft over the yard, smelling of wool. On racks along the walls hang bolts of the grey-gold cloth, some of them, by their tickets, older than the inn, and every one of them unworn and unfaded. A desk at the end has samples pinned along its edge like butterflies.".
  Observe exiles_scene at exiles_row when true "Three cottages in a row on the slope behind the street, set a little apart from Sixways, with their windows facing up the rise to the stone. The people of Sixways call them the Outlived: Lull-born who came out, and stayed out, and got old.".
  Observe simeon_room_scene at simeon_room when true "A room full of paper. Sheets pinned to the walls, stacked on the chair, weighted on the table with stones; every sheet headed GLOSS and a number, in a fine old hand, and some of the numbers in the thousands.".
  Observe spring_scene at sx_spring when true "Behind the inn a spring comes out of the hillside under a lip of rock, cold and very clear, with a draught breathing out of the dark above the water. It smells of wet stone, and, faintly, of wool.".
  Observe stone_scene at fold_stone when true "The Fold-stone is a grey stone, waist-high, on the bare top of the rise, notched along both edges with seven notches to a row, row on row, so many that the lower ones are worn to dimples. Nothing hangs on it but the weather. From it the road goes on round a bare green hill, and comes back to the stone.".
  Observe stone_open at fold_stone when lullOpen() "There is another road from the stone this morning: down, through a gap in the turf that was not there, into a valley full of beech trees and smoke and birds, with a town in it, and a mill.".
  Observe stone_count at fold_stone when lullCycle(clock) < 6 and not weekReturned(lull_country) "The newest notches on the stone say that the Lull is {lullDaysAway(clock) in words} days off.".

  // The days to the Lull, as Sixways chalks them.
  Measure lullDaysAway(clock).
  Rule days_away when lullDaysAway(clock) != 6 - lullCycle(clock) { Set lullDaysAway(clock) to 6 - lullCycle(clock). }


  // ── Dorcas Trewin, the Waiting Woman ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person dorcas "Dorcas Trewin" at sx_taproom {
    Role "who keeps the Waiting Woman". Profession innkeeper. Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Likeness "innkeeper".
    Greets "A handsome woman of sixty or so, in a good blue gown that is a little young for her, looks up from the barrel she is tapping. 'Come in, come in, shut it, the wind comes straight down off the stone.' She looks at your boots. 'Come for the Lull, have you? Everyone has. Sit where you can see the road; everyone does.'".
    Greets again "Dorcas Trewin looks up, and then, before she looks back at you, out of the window at the stone.".
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 8.
    Sells torch for 1 coin from 6.
    Sells rope for 2 coin from 2.
  }
  Topic dorcas_lull with dorcas "Ask Dorcas Trewin about the Lull" when true once {
    Says "'One day in seven,' says Dorcas, wiping the tap. 'On the other six the road goes round the hill and back to the stone, and you can walk it all day if you like; people do, the first time. On the seventh, at six in the morning, there's another road, and down you go.' She leans on the bar. 'They don't work in there. Anything you do in the Lull you don't mean comes to bits at sunset. Bread, chairs, money.' She smiles. 'And mind the night. Be on the road back by midnight, or lie down the way they do and sleep it out. Sleep a night in the Lull and you wake up a week on.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lull_heard). }
  }
  Discovery lull_heard "Over the Fold-stone, one day in seven, a road goes down into the Lull. Inside, what is done without meaning it comes undone at sunset; a night slept there is a week gone outside; whoever is not on the road out by midnight must lie down the Lull's way, or be awake in the dark.".
  Topic dorcas_sign with dorcas "Ask Dorcas Trewin about the sign on the wall" when true once {
    Says "'That's me,' says Dorcas, not looking at it. 'At twenty-eight. My husband painted it, the week we married, before the old sign blew down. I touch her up every spring.' She does look at it, then. 'He's in there. Piran. In the Lull. Thirty years we've been married, my count, and four of his.' She turns back to the barrel. 'I go in on Lulldays. He says I look tired. I tell him it's the walk.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, dorcas_piran). }
  }
  Discovery dorcas_piran "Dorcas Trewin of the Waiting Woman is married to Piran, a Lull man. Thirty years have passed for her and four for him. She walks in every Lullday, and he tells her she looks tired.".
  Topic dorcas_week with dorcas "Ask Dorcas Trewin what a week is like, waiting" when knows(actor, dorcas_piran) once {
    Says "Dorcas puts down the cloth. 'Six days,' she says. 'You keep busy. Carters, the factor's people, folk come to look at the stone. The first day after is the worst: you've just seen him, and he's just seen you, and for him it was this morning.' She laughs, short. 'For him I come every day. Can you think of it? Every single morning, there's his wife at the door, a bit older. He told me once he can see me age if he looks hard. He was being kind. He meant it was hard to see.' She picks the cloth back up. 'He doesn't know I'm poorly. Ruth Coll says a year, two. That's three months to him, three and a half.' Then, briskly: 'What'll you have?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, dorcas_ill). }
  }
  Discovery dorcas_ill "Dorcas Trewin is ill: Ruth Coll gives her a year or two, which is three months of Piran's. He does not know.".

  // ── Ruth Coll, herbwife ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind poppy_kind "a twist of poppy" is gear worth 3 weighing 0 described "Dried poppy-heads and a little wild lettuce in a twist of brown paper, with RUTH COLL — FOR PAIN — STEEP, DON'T BOIL written on it in a sharp hand.".
  Kind nightshade_kind "a phial of nightshade" is gear worth 4 weighing 0 described "A small corked phial of something dark, with a black thread tied round its neck, which is how Ruth Coll marks what she does not want mistaken for anything else.".
  Person ruth "Ruth Coll" at coll_kitchen {
    Role "herbwife of Sixways". Profession herbalist. Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Likeness "herbalist".
    Greets "A thin woman with her sleeves rolled to the elbow is grinding something in a mortar and does not stop. 'If you're bleeding, sit there. If you're not, tell me what you want. If you want to ask about the Lull, I've a pestle in my hand.'".
    Greets again "Ruth Coll goes on grinding. 'Well?'".
    Sells bandages for 1 coin from 6.
    Sells herbs for 2 coin from 4.
    Sells antidote for 3 coin from 2.
    Offers healing "stitching and a poultice" for 2 coin.
  }
  Item poppy "a twist of poppy" is poppy_kind at limbo.
  Item nightshade "a phial of nightshade" is nightshade_kind at limbo.
  Topic ruth_lull with ruth "Ask Ruth Coll about physic in the Lull" when true once {
    Says "Ruth puts the pestle down, which is a sign of something. 'Physic I make out here and carry in, holds; it's made here, and I mean it. What they mix in there for sale, if anybody did, which they don't, would be weeds again by supper.' She wipes her hands. 'They don't buy physic. That's their custom, not their law; their law doesn't care. The old ones won't have anything bought across the Tump. Pride.' She picks the pestle back up. 'Tobias Lindsell came out to me once, years ago their time, for his wife. Stood just where you're standing, with the money in his fist. Went away without buying. Pride, or something worse.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, tobias_came_out). }
  }
  Discovery tobias_came_out "Tobias Lindsell, of the Lull, came out to Ruth Coll in Sixways once for physic for his wife, with the money in his hand, and went away without buying.".
  Topic ruth_hester with ruth "Ask Ruth Coll what she would send in for Hester Lindsell" when knows(actor, hester_sick) and not ruthAsked(ruth) {
    Says "'Poppy,' says Ruth at once. 'Steeped, not boiled. It won't mend her; nothing mends what she's got. It'll let her sleep, and stop the worst of it, and she'll know her husband's face.' She takes down a jar. 'Three coin. I'd give it, but then it would be a gift from me, and they'd want to know what I meant by it.' She looks at you over the jar. 'And if what she's asked you for is the other thing, I keep that too. Black thread on the neck. Four coin. I don't ask, and you'll not tell me.'".
    On discuss { Assert ruthAsked(ruth). }
  }
  Relation ruthAsked(group).
  Action buy_poppy(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Ruth Coll three coin for a twist of poppy" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ruth, site) and ruthAsked(ruth) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 3 and at(poppy, limbo).
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Increase quantity(ruth, gold) by 3. Retract at(poppy, limbo). Give poppy to actor. }
    Result "Ruth weighs out the poppy, twists the paper, and writes on it. 'Steep it. Don't boil it. If she sleeps a long while, let her.'".
  }
  Action buy_nightshade(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Ruth Coll four coin for the phial with the black thread" {
    Grave "This is for Hester Lindsell to die by. It cannot be undone.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ruth, site) and ruthAsked(ruth) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 4 and at(nightshade, limbo).
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Increase quantity(ruth, gold) by 4. Retract at(nightshade, limbo). Give nightshade to actor. }
    Result "Ruth takes the phial down from the top shelf without looking at you, and puts it in your hand, and closes your fingers on it with hers. 'All of it, in something sweet,' she says. 'She'll sleep first.' Then she goes back to her mortar, and grinds, and does not look up again until you have gone.".
  }

  // ── Mercer Haskett, cloth-factor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind lull_cloth "a length of Lull-cloth" is gear worth 12 weighing 1 described "A length of grey-gold woollen cloth, close-woven and soft, with no wear on it anywhere and none to come: it was woven by someone who meant it, in the Lull, and it does not fray, fade, or felt.".
  Kind long_shift_cloth "a bolt of the Long Shift's cloth" is gear worth 20 weighing 2 described "A bolt of grey cloth from the looms of the Wrought Mill in the dark: close, even, perfect, and the colour of nothing at all. You wove it. It will never wear out.".
  Kind wrought_shillings_kind "a bag of the Wroughts' shillings" is gear worth 15 weighing 1 described "Old silver shillings in a canvas bag, struck with a hammer and a fleece: the Long Shift's wages for the seventh day, paid out to whoever would work it, and come back to the bailiff's chest at sunset.".
  Person haskett "Mercer Haskett" at haskett_loft {
    Role "cloth-factor of Sixways, who buys Lull-cloth". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Likeness "merchant".
    Greets "A stout pleasant man in a waistcoat of the grey-gold cloth gets up from the desk with his hand already out. 'Haskett. Cloth. You'll have come about the Lull; everyone comes about the Lull. Sit down, sit down. Feel that.' He puts a corner of a bolt into your hand. 'Forty years old, that piece. Not a thread gone. You can't buy it in there for love or money: only for love.' He laughs at his own joke, which he has clearly made before, and means.".
    Greets again "'Ah!' says Haskett, delighted. 'Back from the Lull, or going?'".
    Buys lull_cloth for 12 coin.
    Buys long_shift_cloth for 20 coin.
    Buys wrought_shillings_kind for 15 coin.
  }
  Topic haskett_shift with haskett "Show Mercer Haskett the grey cloth you wove in the Mill" when carries(party, shift_bolt) once {
    Says "Haskett takes the bolt to the window and says nothing for as long as it takes to count to twenty, which for him is a great deal of not saying. He rubs it, smells it, holds it to the light. 'Perfect,' he says at last. 'Perfect, and the colour of nothing.' He gives it back to you, not quite at once. 'I'll give you twenty for it. I'll give you twenty and I'll put it at the back of the rack where I don't have to look at it.' He wipes his hands on his waistcoat. 'Who wove that? No. Don't tell me.'".
  }
  Topic haskett_trade with haskett "Ask Mercer Haskett how he comes by Lull-cloth" when true once {
    Says "'Gifts,' says Haskett. 'Every scrap of it. A Lull weaver weaves a length for her sister in Sixways because she loves her sister and loves the loom, and the sister, who has a roof to mend, brings it to me. Forty years my father did it and thirty I have.' He strokes the bolt. 'Do you know what it would be worth, if they wove for wages and it held? They have four hundred people in there who have done nothing for fifty years but get good at things they love.' He sighs like a man looking at an orchard over a wall. 'And they won't take a penny. Their law, they say. Their custom, I say.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, haskett_wants). }
  }
  Discovery haskett_wants "Mercer Haskett, cloth-factor of Sixways, would give a great deal to hire the Lull's weavers for wages, if the Lull ever let him.".

  // ── Abel Rooke, carter ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person abel "Abel Rooke" at rooke_yard {
    Role "carter of Sixways". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Likeness "farmer".
    Greets "A big young man with sawdust in his hair is standing in front of something under a sack, looking at it as if it owed him money. 'Don't look,' he says. 'It's a chair. Well, it's a chair till sunset.' He wipes his hands down his front and holds one out. 'Abel Rooke. Carts. If you want a load taken, I'm your man; if you want a chair made, I'm not.'".
    Greets again "Abel Rooke looks up from the thing under the sack, and grins in spite of himself.".
  }
  Species mare_kind "a grey mare" like horse tame described "A big grey cart-mare with feathered feet and a patient, sceptical eye, who leans on whoever stands next to her.".
  Person bess "Dulcie" at rooke_yard {
    Role "Abel Rooke's mare". Species mare_kind. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
  }
  Topic abel_chair with abel "Ask Abel Rooke about the chair" when true once {
    Says "'Wedding gift,' says Abel. 'In the Lull you give each other a thing you made, at the Long Table, the evening before, and if it's still there at sunset you're as good as wed.' He lifts the sack: a plain good chair, well-jointed, in ash. 'Wenna Spurling. She's a chandler's daughter in Linger. Sixty days I've been courting her, her count, and sixty weeks mine.' He drops the sack. 'Three times I've carried a chair in there and set it down by the Table and three times it's come to bits at sundown in front of the whole town. Pegs, legs, shavings. Her aunt laughed so hard she had to be helped home.' He looks at the chair. 'I don't know what I'm doing wrong. I mean it. I swear I mean it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, chair_ravels). }
  }
  Discovery chair_ravels "Abel Rooke's wedding chair for Wenna Spurling has come apart at sunset in the Lull three times, in front of the whole town.".
  // A run with the cart: work that holds, because it is done in the world.
  Relation carted(group). Measure runs(group).
  Action cart_run(actor: group, site: place) "Take a load to the mill towns with Abel Rooke, for four coin" {
    Description "Out along the march road and back: most of a day.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(abel, site) and not lullday() and not dark() and hour(clock) <= 10 and not cartedToday(actor).
    Time 54.
    On success { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Assert cartedToday(actor). Increase runs(actor) by 1. Assert carted(actor). }
    Result "You load bales and barrels with Abel in the yard, and walk beside the cart behind Dulcie all day along the march road to the mill towns and back, while Abel talks: about Dulcie, about the road, about the price of hay and the way the light goes on the downs in the evening, and about Wenna, and then about the road again. He pays you at the yard gate. The money stays in your hand. It is the most ordinary thing in the world.".
  }
  Relation cartedToday(group).
  Rule carted_resets when hour(clock) == 0 and cartedToday(?g) { Retract cartedToday(?g). }

  // ── Simeon Eddowes, the Outlived ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person simeon "Simeon Eddowes" at simeon_room {
    Role "a Glosser of the Lull, put out of it" when not following(simeon, party).
    Role "a Glosser of the Lull, going back" when following(simeon, party).
    Ancestry human. Calling mage. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Likeness "scholar".
    Greets "An old man in a white apron with no pockets looks up from his writing as though you had interrupted a sentence of some length. 'Gloss two thousand and ninety,' he says. 'Whether a visitor who knocks meaning to be let in is welcome, if he does not mean to stay. Held: he is.' He puts down the pen. 'Simeon Eddowes. I used to be a Glosser. I'm told I still am, by the apron, which I haven't taken off in twenty years. Sit, if you can find a chair under the law.'".
    Greets again "Simeon Eddowes looks up. 'Ah. The visitor. Held: welcome.'".
  }
  Topic simeon_who with simeon "Ask Simeon Eddowes why he was put out of the Lull" when true once {
    Says "'For a gloss,' says Simeon, with relish. 'Number nine hundred and twelve. A weaver's lad wanted to pay the woman he loved for sitting to him while he drew her, because he was poor and proud and she was poorer and prouder, and the Rest-wardens said a wage was a wage. I held that a wage paid in love is not a wage.' He spreads his hands. 'They said I'd opened the door to the week. Hobday Pryce's father was Chief Warden then. I was walked to the stone and told not to come back.' He smiles. 'The lad and the woman were married. The drawing held. Hobday's father did not.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, simeon_banned). }
  }
  Discovery simeon_banned "Simeon Eddowes was put out of the Lull by the Rest-wardens twenty years ago, his time, for ruling that a wage paid in love is not a wage. The wardens will turn him back at the Tump.".
  Topic simeon_law with simeon "Ask Simeon Eddowes what the Lull's law really is" when true once {
    Says "'The Glossers will tell you: what is done for wages, or under compulsion, comes undone. That is wrong at the edges, and I lost my place saying so.' He holds up a finger. 'The law is love. What is done for love holds; what is not, ravels. A wage changes nothing if the hand that takes it loves the work. A gift given without love comes apart in your hand.' He taps the table. 'I have had twenty years out here to doubt it and I have not managed to. Go and see. Bring me back what you see, and I'll tell you how it proves me right.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, simeon_doctrine). }
  }
  Discovery simeon_doctrine "Simeon Eddowes holds that the Lull's law is love: what is done for love holds, and what is not comes undone, wages or no wages.".
  Topic simeon_hester with simeon "Tell Simeon Eddowes that Hester Lindsell is dying" when knows(actor, hester_sick) and not simeonToldHester(simeon) {
    Says "Simeon is still for a long moment. Then he takes off his spectacles and folds them, very carefully, as if they might break. 'Hester Lumb,' he says. 'Lindsell. Yes.' He puts the spectacles down on a gloss. 'When we were twenty, her count and mine, I asked her to walk up the Tump with me, and she went up it with Tobias Lindsell instead. He was the better man. I have held that for sixty years and it has never once ravelled.' He looks at the window, at the stone. 'Dying. In there, nobody dies quick. She'll have been dying for years of mine.' He gets up. 'I should like to see her. I should very much like to see her. And I can't get past the Tump.'".
    On discuss { Assert simeonToldHester(simeon). Assert acceptsEscort(simeon, actor). }
  }
  Relation simeonToldHester(group).
  Topic simeon_join_offer with simeon "Ask Simeon Eddowes to come into the Lull with you" when knows(actor, simeon_banned) and not simeonToldHester(simeon) and not acceptsEscort(simeon, actor) once {
    Says "Simeon looks at you over his spectacles. 'The wardens would turn me back at the Tump,' he says. 'And I would stand there and let them, because I am old and I have nothing in there worth the shame of it.' He goes back to his pen. 'Ask me again if that changes.'".
  }
  // He will come with the company once there is something in the Lull worth the shame of being turned back.
  Rule simeon_sets_out when following(simeon, party) and not simeonSetOut(simeon)
    says "Simeon takes off the white apron, folds it, looks at it, and puts it back on. 'If I am going to be turned back at the Tump,' he says, 'I should like them to see what they are turning back. They keep the shoulder in the mornings, the wardens. After eleven they go down to the Green to fine people for enjoying themselves.'" { Assert simeonSetOut(simeon). }
  Relation simeonSetOut(group).
  Topic simeon_travel_lull with simeon "Ask Simeon what he makes of the Lull, now he is back" when inLull(party) and lullOpen() and following(simeon, party) once {
    Says "Simeon has stopped in the road and is looking at the Strike Post on the Tump with his mouth a little open. 'It's the same,' he says. 'It's the same morning. The same birds.' He wipes his eyes, without embarrassment. 'Twenty years out there, and in here they've had three. The Pryce boy will be Chief Warden. The Lindsell girl will be grown.' He sniffs. 'I am going to be very rude to a great many people.'".
  }

  // ── Quick Nan Fossick and Gurney ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind pasty_kind "a Sixways pasty" is gear worth 1 weighing 0 described "A big pasty, still warm, crimped along the top, with N.F. pricked into the crust.".
  Kind lull_ribbon "a ribbon of Nan's" is gear worth 1 weighing 0 described "A length of bright red ribbon, the kind a Lull child ties to the Strike Post.".
  Person nan "Quick Nan Fossick" at sx_street {
    Role "a pedlar with a tray". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Likeness "merchant".
    Greets "A small quick woman with a tray of pasties, ribbons and tin whistles slung from her neck darts over to you. 'There's a face that wants a pasty,' she says. 'Nan Fossick, Quick Nan, everybody knows me. Pasties a coin, ribbons a coin, whistles two, and if you're going in on Lullday, love, I'm the only one sells anything in there at all.'".
    Greets again "'Back again!' says Quick Nan. 'I knew you'd be back. They all come back.'".
    Sells pasty_kind for 1 coin from 6.
    Sells lull_ribbon for 1 coin from 6.
  }
  Person gurney "Gurney" at sx_street {
    Role "a big silent man who carries Quick Nan's baskets". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "The big man with the baskets looks at you and does not say anything. After a while he nods, which seems to be the whole of it.".
  }
  Initially Assert serves(gurney, nan).
  Topic nan_lull with nan "Ask Quick Nan how she can sell in the Lull" when true once {
    Says "Nan laughs and taps her nose. 'Early bird, love. In at six, out by four. What they buy off me stays bought till sunset, and by sunset I'm home with my feet up.' She winks. 'There's no harm in it. They like a pasty, same as anyone.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, nan_hours). }
  }
  Discovery nan_hours "Quick Nan goes into the Lull at six on Lullday mornings and sells on the Green, and is back out over the Tump by four, before sunset.".
}

data/adventures/the-lull/wild.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── Lammas Tarn and Hob Linsey ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Hob Linsey keeps bees by the tarn and does not always lie down at night, because bees don't. He knows the dark.
  Observe tarn_scene at tarn_shore when lullOpen() "Lammas Tarn lies at the head of the valley in a bowl of beeches, black and still, so clear at the edge you can count the stones. The Idle comes out of it over a lip of rock. Along the shore on a bank of thyme stand skeps, dozens of them, straw domes on planks, and the air over the bank is loud and gold. There is a hut, and a boat drawn up, and a man asleep in the boat.".
  Observe tarn_dark at tarn_shore when folded() "Lammas Tarn in the dark, without a star in it. The skeps are silent. Out on the water, so faint you might be imagining it, someone is rowing.".
  Person hob "Hob Linsey" at tarn_shore {
    Role "who keeps bees at the tarn". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Likeness "hermit".
    Greets "The man in the boat sits up with bees in his beard and looks at you without hurry. 'Don't flap,' he says. 'They don't mind you. They mind flapping.' He climbs out. 'Hob Linsey. These are mine, or I'm theirs; it's been argued both ways.'".
    Greets again "Hob Linsey lifts a hand, slowly, so as not to annoy the bees, and the bees, who are annoyed anyway, go on with it. 'They know you,' he says. 'That is a compliment, or a warning. In the Lull, I find, they are generally the same.'".
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(hob). Initially Assert dayAt(hob, tarn_shore). Initially Assert bedAt(hob, tarn_shore).
  Topic hob_skep with hob "Ask Hob Linsey to set a skep in the Gardens for one of Aldith Mote's coins" when lullOpen() and aldithTesting(aldith) and at(skep, limbo) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 1 once {
    Says "Hob looks at the coin as if it were a wasp. 'Money,' he says. 'For bees.' He looks at it longer. 'For the Mote girl.' He sighs through his beard. 'She wants to see if it ravels.' He takes the coin and puts it in his cheek, which is apparently where he keeps things, and picks up a skep from the bank, and a smoker, and walks off down the leat path without another word. When you see him next, in the Gardens, there is a new skep on a plank by the bean-rows, and bees going in and out of it, and Hob Linsey is sitting beside it with the face of a man watching his child's first day at school.".
    On discuss { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Increase quantity(hob, gold) by 1. Assert at(skep, gardens). Assert state(skep, set). }
  }
  Topic hob_dark with hob "Ask Hob Linsey what the Lull is like at night" when lullOpen() once {
    Says "Hob is quiet for a while. 'There isn't a night,' he says. 'Not like yours. You lie down Lull-fashion, hands open, and you wake up and it's Lullday. That's the night.' He turns a skep to the light. 'Bees don't lie down. So some nights I don't.' He does not look at you. 'Then it's dark. Six days of it. Everybody asleep, and you can't wake them; I've tried. And the Mill going.' He sets the skep down. 'If you're ever in it, keep away from the Mill. If they see you, lie down with your hands open, like the strikers did on the Tump; they don't touch the resting. And if you want out, there's the Gap, under the Swallow, where the Idle goes into the hill. It comes out behind the Waiting Woman. I've been out that way. It's a long crawl and it smells of wool.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, open_hands). Assert knows(actor, gap_known). Assert knows(actor, mill_works). }
  }
  Discovery mill_works "Hob Linsey says that in the dark between Lulldays, the six days the Lull does not keep, the Wrought Mill is working; and that whatever works it does not touch those who lie with open hands.".
  Kind comb_kind "a comb of Hob Linsey's honey" is gear worth 2 weighing 0 described "A slab of honeycomb wrapped in a dock leaf, dripping, smelling of thyme.".
  Item comb "a comb of Hob Linsey's honey" is comb_kind at limbo.
  Topic hob_brock with hob "Ask Hob Linsey about the Old Brock" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, brock_known) once {
    Says "'Poor old devil,' says Hob. 'He's been in the Hangers longer than me. Last Lullday Hobday paid a Sixer trapper to lay him, and the fool did, and took the coin, and at sunset the Brock got up.' He shakes his head. 'Hired harm. It doesn't hold, here. You can only hurt something in the Lull if you mean it. Well, he's been hurt and got up, and now he means it.' He goes into the hut and comes out with something wrapped in a dock leaf. 'He's a honey-badger at heart, like all of them. Leave him that at the sett and he'll be your friend for an hour. Leave him that every Lullday and he'll keep out of the Gardens.' He gives it to you. 'Freely. Don't thank me, it'll go to my head.'".
    On discuss { Retract at(comb, limbo). Give comb to actor. Assert knows(actor, brock_honey). }
  }
  Discovery brock_honey "Hob Linsey says the Old Brock will take honey at his sett and be peaceable for it; and that if he is given it every Lullday he will keep out of the Gardens.".
  Topic hob_feed with hob "Ask Hob Linsey to leave comb at the Old Brock's sett every Lullday" when lullOpen() and brockTruce(brock) and not brockFed(brock) once {
    Says "Hob grunts. 'He took it, then. Good.' He looks at the skeps. 'I've comb enough. I'll take him a piece on my way round. He's a neighbour.' He considers. 'I never thought to. Forty years. Nobody asked.'".
    On discuss { Assert brockFed(brock). }
  }

  // ── The Hangers and the Old Brock ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe hangers_scene at hanger_path when lullOpen() "A path along the valley side under tall beeches, their trunks grey as elephants, the floor deep in copper leaves. Old charcoal hearths, round and black, stand in the clearings, cold for fifty-seven years, with ferns in them. Here and there a beech has been carved with initials and a date, the date always a Lullday.".
  Observe hangers_dark at hanger_path when folded() "The Hangers in the dark: the grey trunks, a smell of leaf-mould, and the lint of the Ravel caught in the low branches like old-man's-beard.".
  Observe sett_scene at brock_sett when lullOpen() "A bank under the beeches torn open in a dozen places: the Old Brock's sett, generations deep, with spoil-heaps the size of carts and paths beaten through the leaves to every hole. It smells of earth and musk. In the mouth of the biggest hole the soil has been dug out fresh, and there are hairs on the roots, grey, and very long.".
  Observe sett_dark at brock_sett when folded() "The sett in the dark. From deep in the bank, something breathes.".
  Species lull_brock "a badger the size of a pony" like badger temperament territorial described "A badger, grey and black and white, as big as a pony, with a head like a ram's and claws like garden forks.".
  Person brock "the Old Brock" at brock_sett {
    Role "a badger the size of a pony, grey with age, scarred across the shoulders". Species lull_brock. Level 5. Pronouns he.
    Temperament territorial.
    Lair brock_sett. Refuge brock_sett. Fears flame.
    Warns "Something comes up out of the biggest hole and stands in the leaves, and it is a badger, and it is as big as a pony, and there is a long bare scar across its shoulders where something went in and came out again. It does not run. It has been killed once already, and it remembers. It will not have you at its sett; it will give you the time it takes to back away, or to show it something it wants more than you.".
    Comes "The Old Brock comes at you low and fast, the way badgers do, as if the ground were throwing it.".
    Flinches "The Old Brock shies from the flame with a cough of rage and goes down into the bank.".
    Pleads "The Old Brock backs into the mouth of the sett with its head low, grunting, and will not come out again.".
  }
  Discovery brock_known "The Old Brock, a badger as big as a pony, comes down out of the Hangers into the Pleasure Gardens at dusk and roots up the strips. Hobday Pryce gives a bounty for him.".
  Relation brockTruce(group). Relation brockFed(group). Relation brockGone(group). Relation bountyTaken(group). Relation brockRose(group).
  // At dusk he comes down into the Gardens, unless he is fed, or gone.
  Rule brock_raids when lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 21 and able(brock) and not brockFed(brock) and not brockGone(brock) and at(brock, brock_sett) and not at(party, brock_sett) { Assert at(brock, gardens). }
  Rule brock_home when lullOpen() and (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 19) and able(brock) and at(brock, gardens) { Assert at(brock, brock_sett). }
  Observe brock_in_gardens at gardens when lullOpen() and at(brock, gardens) "At the top of the Gardens the Old Brock is tearing up a strip of potatoes, as big as a pony in the dusk, and the children who were racing barrows have all gone indoors.".
  Observe brock_met near brock when not knows(party, brock_known) "The grass and the leaf-litter all about are torn as if with forks." teaches brock_known.
  Topic hobday_bounty with hobday "Ask Hobday Pryce about the Old Brock" when lullOpen() and not bountyTaken(party) once {
    Says "'A nuisance,' says Hobday. 'He has the Gardens every dusk. Nobody here will lay him; they say you can't, not meaning it, and nobody means it, he's a badger.' He looks at your weapons with interest. 'A Sixer could. I'd make it worth your while. Ten coin, freely given, to whoever brings me word he's laid.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, brock_known). Assert bountyOffered(hobday). }
  }
  Relation bountyOffered(group).
  Topic hobday_bounty_take with hobday "Take Hobday Pryce's bounty on the Old Brock" when lullOpen() and bountyOffered(hobday) and not bountyTaken(party) and able(brock) once {
    Says "'Good,' says Hobday, and shakes your hand. 'Freely given, mind. When you've done it.'".
    On discuss { Assert bountyTaken(party). }
  }
  // Honey at the sett: a truce.
  Action leave_comb(actor: group, site: place) "Set Hob Linsey's honeycomb down in the mouth of the sett, and back off" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, brock_sett) and carries(actor, comb) and able(brock) and not brockTruce(brock).
    On success { Spend comb_kind from actor. Assert at(comb, limbo). Assert brockTruce(brock). Assert tolerates(brock, actor). Retract warned(brock, actor). Retract assails(brock, actor). }
    Result "You put the comb down in the leaves at the mouth of the big hole and step back, and back again. The Old Brock comes up out of the bank and stands over the comb, and looks at you, and you look at it. Then it eats, the whole comb, leaf and all, with its eyes half shut, and when it has finished it licks its claws one by one and lies down in the mouth of the sett with its chin on its paws, and lets you be.".
  }
  // Smoked out with flame, he goes over the Hangers and does not come back.
  Action smoke_sett(actor: group, site: place) "Fill the sett with smoke from a brand, and drive him out of the valley" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, brock_sett) and capable(actor, flame) and able(brock) and not brockGone(brock) and not brockTruce(brock).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert brockGone(brock). Assert at(brock, limbo). }
    Result "You pile leaves and green beech in the mouths of the holes and set the brand to them, and the smoke goes in, and in, and out of holes you had not seen, all along the bank. A long time later, far up the slope, something big breaks out of the ground coughing and goes away over the top of the Hangers, crashing, into the next valley, and does not come back. The sett smokes for an hour. You find you are not proud of it.".
  }
  // Laid for the bounty, he gets up at sunset. Laid meaning it, he does not.
  Person brock_risen "the Old Brock, up again" at limbo {
    Role "a badger the size of a pony, with two scars now, and his eyes red". Species lull_brock. Level 6. Pronouns he.
    Temperament savage.
    Lair brock_sett.
    Comes "The Old Brock comes up out of the leaves at you, the second scar open and dry across his ribs where your blow went in, and he does not stop to warn you this time; he has been killed for hire twice, and he means it.".
  }
  Rule brock_rises when dead(brock) and bountyTaken(party) and lullDusk() and not brockRose(brock)
    says "At sunset, somewhere up in the Hangers, there is a sound like a sack of earth being dropped and picked up again; and then a long, low, furious cough. The Old Brock was laid for a bounty. In the Lull, that does not hold." teaches hired_harm {
    Assert brockRose(brock). Assert at(brock, limbo). Assert at(brock_risen, brock_sett).
  }
  Discovery hired_harm "Harm done in the Lull for hire does not hold: the Old Brock, laid for Hobday Pryce's bounty, got up again at sunset.".
  Topic hobday_bounty_paid with hobday "Tell Hobday Pryce that the Old Brock is laid" when lullOpen() and dead(brock) and bountyTaken(party) and not bountyPaid(party) once {
    Says "Hobday counts out ten coins into your hand, beaming. 'Freely given,' he says. Then he looks at the sky, at where the sun is, and his beam goes thoughtful. 'You'll want to be over the Tump with that before sunset,' he says. 'Just to be safe.'".
    On discuss { Assert bountyPaid(party). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Decrease quantity(hobday, gold) by 10 or to nothing. }
  }
  Relation bountyPaid(group).
  Rule bounty_ravels when lullDusk() and bountyPaid(party) and inLull(party) and not bountyRavelled(party)
    says "At sunset the ten coins of Hobday's bounty go out of your purse like water out of a cupped hand, back to his, and are gone. A wage comes undone in the Lull with the work it paid for." {
    Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 10 or to nothing. Increase quantity(hobday, gold) by 10. Assert bountyRavelled(party).
  }
  Relation bountyRavelled(group).
}

data/adventures/the-lull/working.kyr:
Module lull "The Lull" {
  // ── The Weekday Club ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Corin's plan: on the Working Day, from dawn to dusk, the Club will work in public for wages: mend the Shift Bridge
  // to the Mill, which nobody has crossed since the strike. They think a day's wage-work will break the Hallowing. They
  // are wrong about the wages and right about the day: the Lull holds while the valley wants it, and the Working Day
  // shows, at the Watching, whose work was meant.
  Person club "the Weekday Club" at mill_bridge {
    Role "the young of Linger, sitting on the broken bridge with their legs over the leat". Ancestry human. Numbers 8. Peaceable.
    Greets "Eight young people on the broken end of the bridge stop talking all at once and look at you, then at each other, then at you again, the way people do who have been talking about the very thing.".
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(club). Initially Assert dayAt(club, mill_bridge). Initially Assert bedAt(club, weavers_row).
  Topic club_monday with club "Ask the Weekday Club what they would do with a Monday" when lullOpen() once {
    Says "They all talk at once, and then, because Corin glares, one at a time. A boy wants to be bored, properly, for a whole day, the way the Sixers say they are. A girl wants to start a thing and not finish it and come back to it. Tam Hollis wants to apprentice to the smith in Sixways and come home every evening with burnt hands. Kezia Pryce, if she is there, wants to be late for something. The smallest of them, a girl of fifteen with a squint, says she would like to have a birthday that was a different day from everybody else's, and the others go quiet.".
  }
  Topic club_mean with club "Ask the Weekday Club whether they mean it" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, working_day_plan) once {
    Says "They look at each other. 'Mean what?' says the boy who wants to be bored. 'To end it,' you say. 'All of it. Your grandparents' Lull.' Nobody says anything for a while. Then the girl with the squint says, 'We don't mean to end it. We mean to start something,' and Corin, without turning round, says, 'Same thing,' and the girl says, 'It isn't, though,' and nobody answers her.".
  }
  Person davy "Davy Mote" at mill_bridge {
    Role "Aldith's brother, who wants to be a soldier". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "A gangling boy of seventeen with a stick he holds like a pike jumps down off the pier. 'Davy Mote. Are you a soldier? You look like a soldier. Have you been in a war?' He does not wait. 'I'm going to be a soldier. As soon as there's a Monday.'".
    Greets again "Davy Mote salutes you with his stick, and the salute turns, halfway, into an attempt to straighten the stick, which is bent. 'Mended it twice,' he says. 'It is bent the same way both times. I think it has an opinion.'".
  }
  Initially Assert lullFolk(davy). Initially Assert dayAt(davy, mill_bridge). Initially Assert bedAt(davy, glossary).
  Topic davy_why with davy "Ask Davy Mote why he wants to be a soldier" when lullOpen() once {
    Says "Davy considers it, seriously, which he does not do with much. 'Because they go places,' he says. 'And things happen to them, and then they come home and the things have happened. Here nothing's happened to anybody since Grandad's time.' He swings the stick. 'Aldith says I'd hate it. Aldith says soldiers are what the Long Shift was for.' He looks at the dark mill. 'Maybe. But I'd have hated it on a Tuesday.'".
  }
  Relation clockKicked(group). Relation workingNamed(group).
  // The first Watching: a clock comes apart, and is kicked across the Green.
  Rule first_clock at green when dayOne() and lullDusk() and at(party, green) and not clockKicked(corin) and not corinMaking(corin)
    says "Among the makings on the grass, a little apart, stands a clock in a case of brass and walnut, very fine, ticking, with no card. It comes apart with the light. It does it neatly, almost politely: the case opens, the wheels lift out one by one and lie down in the grass in order of size, the spring uncoils with a small sigh. A young woman with brass dust on her hands gets up from the Table and walks out and kicks the whole lot, wheels and case and all, across the Green into the dark, and walks off after it. Nobody says anything. An old woman near you says, 'That's forty-two,' without looking up from her knitting." teaches clock_ravels {
    Assert clockKicked(corin).
  }
  Rule first_clock_quiet when dayOne() and lullDusk() and not at(party, green) and not clockKicked(corin) { Assert clockKicked(corin). }
  Topic corin_club with corin "Ask Corin Lindsell about the Weekday Club" when lullOpen() and (knows(actor, club_rumour) or clockKicked(corin) or corinTrust(corin) >= 1) and not workingNamed(corin) {
    Says "Corin looks at you for a long moment, deciding. Then she jerks her head, and you sit beside her on the end of the broken bridge. 'There's eight of us. More who'd come.' She talks fast and low. 'The Glossers say: what's done for wages, ravels. So we'll do it. A whole day, dawn to dusk, in front of everybody: we'll mend the Shift Bridge, for wages, real coin, all of us. A whole valley's day of wage-work. Not one thing done for love.' She grips the stone. 'Either it all ravels at sunset and we're laughed at for ever, or it doesn't and the Hallowing's broken and tomorrow is Monday.' She looks at you. 'The Lullday after next. We need coin, a Sixer's coin, for wages: there's a factor in Sixways would give it, he'd give anything to see the Lull open. We can't go out for it; we'd come back a week older than everyone. You can.'".
    On discuss { Assert workingNamed(corin). Assert knows(actor, working_day_plan). Increase corinTrust(corin) by 1. }
  }
  Discovery working_day_plan "Corin Lindsell and the Weekday Club mean to work for wages, in public, from dawn to dusk on the Working Day (the Lullday after the one when she told you of it), mending the Shift Bridge to the Mill; they believe a day of wage-work will break the Hallowing. They need coin for wages from Mercer Haskett in Sixways.".
  Objective obj_working when knows(party, working_day_plan) and not workingOver(lull_country) "On the Working Day the Weekday Club will mend the Shift Bridge for wages, from dawn to dusk, to break the Hallowing; at the Watching the town will see what holds.".
  // The wages, from Haskett.
  Kind purse_kind "a purse of Haskett's wages" is gear worth 30 weighing 0 described "A heavy leather purse with M.H. stamped on it: thirty coin, for the wages of the Working Day.".
  Item wages "a purse of Haskett's wages" is purse_kind at limbo.
  Relation wagesGiven(group). Relation clubPaid(group). Relation corinRefusesWages(group).
  Topic haskett_wages with haskett "Tell Mercer Haskett that Corin Lindsell wants wages for a Working Day in the Lull" when knows(actor, working_day_plan) and not wagesGiven(haskett) once {
    Says "Haskett is quite still. Then he gets up and shuts the loft door. 'A day's wage-work,' he says. 'In the Lull. In public.' He goes to the strongbox under the desk and counts thirty coin into a purse without, you think, entirely meaning to. 'Thirty. Wages for a day for twenty hands, Lull rates, which is to say whatever I like.' He gives it to you, and then five more, separately. 'And that's for carrying it. If it holds, I'll want first refusal on every loom in the valley.' He shakes your hand too hard. 'If it ravels, tell them it was a gift from an admirer. It'll go back to my strongbox at sunset in any case, I suppose.'".
    On discuss { Assert wagesGiven(haskett). Retract at(wages, limbo). Give wages to actor. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 5. }
  }
  Event corin_wages near corin when keeps(corin, wages) and not clubPaid(club) "Corin weighs the purse in her hand and laughs, a short hard laugh. 'Wages,' she says. 'Real ones.' She ties it to her belt. 'Now we'll see.'" then {
    Assert clubPaid(club).
  }
  // What the company learned of the law, told to Corin, changes her Working Day.
  Topic corin_meaning with corin "Tell Corin Lindsell what Aldith Mote found: that what holds is what is meant, wages or no" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, meaning_law) and workingNamed(corin) and not corinKnowsMeaning(corin) once {
    Says "Corin stares at you. 'Then the wages don't matter.' She gets up and walks to the end of the broken pier and back. 'It's not whether we're paid. It's whether we mean it. Whether we want it.' She stops. 'Whether the valley wants it.' She sits down again, hard. 'That's worse. That's much worse. You can pay people.' After a while she says, quietly: 'Grandad and the others asked for it, on the Tump. They meant it. If the Lull's going to end, it'll be because somebody who asked for it means it to.' She looks up at the Almshouse. 'And none of them will.'".
    On discuss { Assert corinKnowsMeaning(corin). Assert knows(actor, old_shift_key). }
  }
  Relation corinKnowsMeaning(group).
  Discovery old_shift_key "Corin Lindsell thinks the Lull can end only if someone of the Old Shift, who asked for it, means it to.".
  Event corin_wages_refused near corin when keeps(corin, wages) and corinKnowsMeaning(corin) and not corinRefusesWages(corin) "Corin pushes the purse back at you. 'Give it back to Haskett. We'll not pay anybody. Whoever comes, comes because they want to.'" then {
    Assert corinRefusesWages(corin). Retract keeps(corin, wages). Give wages to party.
  }
  Rule wages_refused_after when clubPaid(club) and corinKnowsMeaning(corin) and not corinRefusesWages(corin) { Assert corinRefusesWages(corin). }
  Topic haskett_return with haskett "Give Mercer Haskett his purse back" when carries(party, wages) once {
    Says "Haskett takes the purse and weighs it, and looks at you. 'Unspent,' he says. 'In my experience that means somebody had a better idea.' He puts it back in the strongbox. 'I hope it was a good one. I hope it costs me a great deal of money.'".
    On discuss { Spend purse_kind from actor. Assert at(wages, limbo). Assert wagesReturned(haskett). }
  }
  Relation wagesReturned(group).
  // Talking Corin out of it.
  Topic corin_calloff with corin "Ask Corin Lindsell to call off the Working Day" when lullOpen() and workingNamed(corin) and corinClockHeld(corin) and not tobiasLovePath(tobias) and not clubDisbanded(club) once {
    Says "Corin looks at the little clock in her hands, ticking. 'It held,' she says. 'I made a thing that held. In here.' She is quiet. 'I could stay. I could make things.' She puts the clock to her ear. 'Grandad's not coming down. Without him it's just us, working, and laughing, and it won't do anything.' She stands up. 'All right. Not this Lullday.' She looks at the Mill. 'Not never. Not this Lullday.'".
    On discuss { Assert clubDisbanded(club). }
  }
  Relation clubDisbanded(group).

  // ── Who will come down to the Green ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Each Hand on the Working Day either means it or does not; the Lull ends only if one of those who asked for it comes.
  Relation joins(group). Relation means(group).
  Topic linnet_hand with linnet "Ask Linnet Gale to work beside you on the Working Day" when lullOpen() and linnetLoves(linnet) and knows(actor, working_day_plan) and not joins(linnet) and not workingOver(lull_country) once {
    Says "Linnet is quiet a long time. 'If it works,' she says, 'there'll be a Monday. And I'll have to wait for things. And so will you; for me.' She looks at you. 'And you'd not lose a week every time you slept.' She puts the fiddle down. 'I've never worked. I don't know how.' Then she laughs. 'I'll carry stones. I'll carry them meaning it. I'll make a tune about carrying stones.'".
    On discuss { Assert joins(linnet). Assert means(linnet). }
  }
  Topic aldith_hand with aldith "Ask Aldith Mote whether she will come to the Working Day" when lullOpen() and lawFound(aldith) and knows(actor, working_day_plan) and not joins(aldith) and not workingOver(lull_country) once {
    Says "'Come?' says Aldith. 'I'll work. I want to see. All my life I've painted what other people found out.' She takes off the white apron, and looks at it, and puts it back on. 'I'll work in it. Let them see a Glosser carrying stones. Gloss two thousand two hundred and fourteen.' She grins. 'If the Reeve wants me to paint over that one he can come and find me on the bridge.'".
    On discuss { Assert joins(aldith). Assert means(aldith). }
  }
  Topic kezia_father with kezia "Ask Kezia Pryce whether she can keep her father off the bridge" when lullOpen() and knows(actor, kezia_club) and knows(actor, working_day_plan) and not keziaAsked(kezia) and not workingOver(lull_country) once {
    Says "Kezia sits back on her heels. 'Father,' she says. 'Father will come down at noon with the wardens and his staff and tell us all to rest, and then he'll take hold of somebody, and it'll be me, and he'll cry.' She thinks. 'I could tell him. Before. That I'll be there. He'd have to come and drag his own daughter off a bridge in front of the Lull.' She rubs her nose with a muddy wrist. 'He mightn't. He might just not come. He's soft, Father. Mother's the one with the staff, really.'".
    On discuss { Assert keziaAsked(kezia). Assert keziaTells(hobday). }
  }
  Relation keziaAsked(group). Relation keziaTells(group).
  // Tobias, for love of his granddaughter, or in grief for what he did.
  Relation tobiasComes(group). Relation tobiasGrief(group).
  Topic tobias_come_love with tobias "Ask Tobias Lindsell to come down to the Shift Bridge on the Working Day, for Corin" when lullOpen() and tobiasLovePath(tobias) and knows(actor, working_day_plan) and not tobiasComes(tobias) and not workingOver(lull_country) once {
    Says "Tobias turns the shilling, or the clock, or nothing, in his hands. 'I asked for it,' he says. 'Up there, at the back, in the rain, with the shilling gone out of my pocket. I asked as hard as any of them.' He looks at you. 'And it was good. Fifty-seven years. I'd not give one of them back.' He gets up, slowly, the way he does everything. 'But it's hers now, not mine. The Lull. And she wants it to go on.' He takes his coat off the peg. 'I'll carry a stone for her. I know how to work. That's the one thing I do know.'".
    On discuss { Assert tobiasComes(tobias). }
  }
  Topic tobias_come_grief with tobias "Ask Tobias Lindsell to come down to the Shift Bridge on the Working Day, for Hester" when lullOpen() and diedBy(hester, tobias) and tobiasToldDeath(tobias) and not tobiasLovePath(tobias) and knows(actor, working_day_plan) and not tobiasComes(tobias) and not workingOver(lull_country) once {
    Grave "He will mean it. Not as Corin means it.".
    Says "Tobias looks at the made bed, and the folded shirt on the chair. 'Six years she was dying,' he says. 'Ten months of it hers. In a valley where nothing ever comes.' He gets up. 'Aye. I'll come down. I'll put my hands to it. Let it end. Let it all end, and let the old die when they're old, and the sick when they're sick.' His mild blue eyes are not mild. 'I mean it,' he says. 'God help me, I mean that more than anything I ever said on the Tump.'".
    On discuss { Assert tobiasComes(tobias). Assert tobiasGrief(tobias). }
  }
  // Hester, eased, asks to be carried down to see it; and Tobias comes with her.
  Topic hester_come with hester "Ask Hester Lindsell whether she would like to see the Working Day" when lullOpen() and hesterEased(hester) and not hesterDead(hester) and knows(actor, working_day_plan) and not hesterWatches(hester) and not workingOver(lull_country) once {
    Says "Hester opens her eyes. 'Corin's day?' She smiles. 'Carry me down. In the chair. I want to see the bridge mended. I was on it the morning we stopped.' She closes her eyes again. 'Tobias will carry me. He'll grumble. He'll stay. He always stays where I am.' A pause. 'And if he puts his hand to a stone while he's there, I'll not stop him.'".
    On discuss { Assert hesterWatches(hester). Assert tobiasLovePath(tobias). }
  }
  Relation hesterWatches(group).

  // ── The Working Day ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation workingBegun(place). Relation workingOver(place). Relation wardensCame(group). Relation wardensBroke(group).
  Relation wardensAside(group). Relation killedMeant(group). Relation bridgeBuilt(group). Relation corinHurt(group).
  Query working() means dayThree() and lullOpen() and workingBegun(lull_country) and not workingOver(lull_country).
  Rule working_begins when dayThree() and lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 6 and not workingBegun(lull_country) and not clubDisbanded(club) and workingNamed(corin) { Assert workingBegun(lull_country). Assert held(corin). Assert held(club). Assert held(davy). Assert at(corin, mill_bridge). Assert at(club, mill_bridge). Assert at(davy, mill_bridge). }
  Rule working_unnamed when dayThree() and lullOpen() and hour(clock) >= 6 and not workingBegun(lull_country) and not workingNamed(corin) and not clubDisbanded(club) { Assert workingNamed(corin). }
  Observe work_dawn at mill_bridge when working() and hour(clock) < 12 and not wardensBroke(club) "The Working Day. The young of Linger are on the broken bridge at the leat in their oldest clothes, with ropes and timbers and a cart of stone from the old wall of the Gardens, working: actually working, in the Lull, in daylight, sweating, with their sleeves rolled up. They are not very good at it. Davy Mote has fallen in the leat twice. Up on the Green the town has come out and stands along the bank to watch, the way it might watch a fire.".
  Observe work_afternoon at mill_bridge when working() and hour(clock) >= 12 and not wardensBroke(club) "The Shift Bridge is half across the leat: new oak on the old piers, stone at the ends, and the young of Linger on it like ants, and others now among them.".
  Observe work_broken at mill_bridge when working() and wardensBroke(club) "The new timbers of the Shift Bridge are in the leat. The Club sit on the bank in a row, wet, saying nothing. Corin Lindsell is holding her right hand in her left.".
  Observe work_green at green as sign when working() "Everybody in Linger is at the leat bank by the Shift Bridge, watching the young work. Nobody is laying the Long Table.".
  // The Hands come down, as the morning goes.
  Rule hand_kezia when working() and hour(clock) >= 8 and not joins(kezia) and not hobdayKnows(hobday) { Assert joins(kezia). Assert means(kezia). Assert held(kezia). Assert at(kezia, mill_bridge). }
  Rule hand_wenna when working() and hour(clock) >= 8 and wedded(wenna) and not joins(wenna) { Assert joins(wenna). Assert means(wenna). Assert wennaHand(wenna). Assert at(wenna, mill_bridge). Assert abelHeld(abel). Assert at(abel, mill_bridge). }
  Rule hand_piran when working() and hour(clock) >= 8 and piranKnowsIll(piran) and not joins(piran) { Assert joins(piran). Assert means(piran). Assert held(piran). Assert at(piran, mill_bridge). }
  Rule hand_linnet when working() and hour(clock) >= 9 and joins(linnet) and not at(linnet, mill_bridge) and not travelsWith(linnet, party) { Assert held(linnet). Assert at(linnet, mill_bridge). }
  Rule hand_aldith when working() and hour(clock) >= 9 and joins(aldith) and not at(aldith, mill_bridge) { Assert held(aldith). Assert at(aldith, mill_bridge). }
  Rule hand_paid when working() and hour(clock) >= 9 and clubPaid(club) and not corinRefusesWages(corin) and not joins(folk) { Assert joins(folk). Assert held(folk). Assert at(folk, mill_bridge). }
  Rule hand_tobias when working() and hour(clock) >= 10 and tobiasComes(tobias) and not joins(tobias) { Assert joins(tobias). Assert means(tobias). Assert held(tobias). Assert at(tobias, mill_bridge). }
  Rule hand_hester when working() and hour(clock) >= 10 and hesterWatches(hester) and not hesterDead(hester) and not at(hester, mill_bridge) { Assert at(hester, mill_bridge). }
  Rule tobias_follows_hester when working() and hour(clock) >= 10 and hesterWatches(hester) and not joins(tobias) { Assert tobiasComes(tobias). }
  Observe kezia_on_bridge at mill_bridge as sign when working() and joins(kezia) and not wardensBroke(club) "Kezia Pryce, in her best dress, is carrying stone, very badly, very fast, with a face like a lit lamp.".
  Observe paid_on_bridge at mill_bridge as sign when working() and joins(folk) and not wardensBroke(club) "A dozen of the townsfolk have come down for Haskett's wages and are working at the stone-end, cheerfully, with their pay in their aprons.".
  Observe hester_at_bridge at mill_bridge as sign when working() and at(hester, mill_bridge) "Hester Lindsell is sitting in a chair on the bank, wrapped in a quilt of strikers' shirts, watching with her bird's eyes, and telling everybody what they are doing wrong.".
  Rule tobias_arrives at mill_bridge when working() and joins(tobias) and at(party, mill_bridge) and not spreadFact(tobias_came_told)
    says "At ten o'clock, the bank goes quiet from the top. Tobias Lindsell is coming down the path from the Green, slowly, in his weaver's coat, with his sleeves already turned back. The Club stop working. Corin stops with a timber on her shoulder. He does not look at anyone. He goes to the stone-cart and takes a stone out of it in both hands, and walks out onto the new timbers with it, and sets it where it goes, and stands up, and looks at the Mill. Then he goes back for another. Along the bank, one of the Old Shift begins to cry, and another to laugh, and no one can tell which is which." { Assert spreadFact(tobias_came_told). }
  Entity tobias_came_told: fact "Tobias came down".
  // The company's own hands.
  Relation workedBridge(group).
  Action work_bridge(actor: group, site: place) "Take off your coat and work on the Shift Bridge with them" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, mill_bridge) and working() and not wardensBroke(club) and not workedBridge(actor) and hour(clock) < 18.
    Time 18.
    Interrupted when wardensCame(wardens) and not wardensAside(wardens) and not wardensBroke(club) and not wardensWarned(party).
    On success { Assert workedBridge(actor). }
    Result "You work. You carry stone from the cart and pass timbers and hold ropes, and someone hands you a mallet, and the sun goes round, and nobody is in a hurry and nobody stops. The young of Linger work beside you the way you might dance a dance you have only seen done: with great seriousness, getting it wrong, getting it right. Somewhere in the afternoon you see Corin Lindsell on the middle of the bridge, filthy, with her hands on her hips, looking at what they have made, mud to the eyebrows, with her mouth open.".
  }

  // On the bridge, while the day goes on.
  Topic corin_working with corin "Ask Corin Lindsell how it is going" when working() and not wardensBroke(club) once {
    Says "Corin wipes her forehead with the back of a wrist and leaves a stripe of mud on it. 'Badly,' she says, delighted. 'Davy's been in the leat three times. Kezia dropped a stone on my foot. We put the first timber in upside down.' She looks along the bridge at the others, at the town on the bank. 'I've never been tired before,' she says. 'Not like this. Tired from something.' Then: 'Don't tell anyone I said it was good. It's supposed to be wages.'".
  }
  Topic tobias_working with tobias "Ask Tobias Lindsell what it is like, working again" when working() and joins(tobias) and not wardensBroke(club) once {
    Says "Tobias sets a stone down and straightens, slowly, with a hand in the small of his back. 'My hands know it,' he says. 'Fifty-seven years, and they knew it before I did. That's the worst of it.' He looks at Corin on the timbers. 'And the best.' He goes back for another stone. Over his shoulder: 'Don't tell her I'm enjoying it. She'll think it's the wages.'".
  }
  Topic davy_working with davy "Ask Davy Mote whether this is like a war" when working() and not wardensBroke(club) once {
    Says "Davy considers, wet to the waist, with a rope over his shoulder. 'No,' he says. 'Nobody's trying to stop us.' He looks up at the top of the bank. 'Yet.' He grins. 'I'd still rather this. Don't tell Aldith.'".
  }
  Topic linnet_working with linnet "Ask Linnet Gale to play while they work" when working() and at(linnet, mill_bridge) and not wardensBroke(club) once {
    Says "Linnet puts down the stone she is carrying, very carefully, as if it might ravel, and gets her fiddle off a bush where she hung it, and stands on the pier and plays: a working tune, which nobody in the Lull has ever heard, with a beat you could lift a timber to; and they do. By the third time round the bank is clapping on the beat. 'There,' she says to you, out of the side of her mouth. 'A tune about something.'".
    On discuss { Assert linnetTune(linnet). }
  }
  Topic hester_working with hester "Ask Hester Lindsell how they are doing" when working() and at(hester, mill_bridge) once {
    Says "'Terribly,' says Hester, from inside her quilt. 'They've no idea. The boy's put that beam in like a man putting on a hat in a gale.' She watches Tobias carry a stone out along the timbers, slow and sure. 'He hasn't,' she says, differently. 'Look at him. He hasn't forgotten anything.' She closes her eyes, and opens them again, quickly, as if she might miss something.".
  }

  // ── The wardens ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At noon Hobday brings the wardens down to stop it, unless he has been softened, or will not drag his daughter off a
  // bridge, or the Glossary has a ruling on the bank in a white apron.
  Query wardensStay() means hobdaySoftened(hobday) or keziaTells(hobday) or lawFound(aldith) and joins(aldith) or housesAtPeace(mabyn).
  Rule wardens_come when working() and hour(clock) >= 12 and not wardensCame(wardens) and not wardensStay() { Assert wardensCame(wardens). Assert held(wardens). Assert held(hobday). Assert at(wardens, mill_bridge). Assert at(hobday, mill_bridge). }
  Relation wardensWarned(group).
  Rule wardens_arrive at mill_bridge when working() and wardensCame(wardens) and not wardensAside(wardens) and not wardensBroke(club) and at(party, mill_bridge) and not wardensWarned(party)
    says "At noon Hobday Pryce comes down the path from the Green with three wardens behind him, staves on their shoulders, and stops at the top of the bank. He is very red. 'That's enough,' he says. 'That's enough now. Down off it, all of you. It's the holy day.' Nobody moves. 'I'll give you till one o'clock,' says Hobday, 'and then we'll take you down.' And he stands there, with the town watching him, and waits." { Assert wardensWarned(party). }
  Rule wardens_stay_told at mill_bridge when working() and hour(clock) >= 12 and wardensStay() and at(party, mill_bridge) and not spreadFact(wardens_stayed_told)
    says "At noon Hobday Pryce comes down to the top of the bank with his staff and his sash and the wardens behind him, and stands there. He looks at the bridge, and at the young on it, and at his daughter, if she is there, and at Aldith Mote on the timbers in her white apron, if she is. He stands there while the shadow of the Mill crosses the water and reaches the bank. Then he plants his staff in the turf, and sits down on the bank beside it, and the wardens, after a moment, sit down beside him; and they watch, like everybody else." { Assert spreadFact(wardens_stayed_told). Assert wardensAside(wardens). }
  Entity wardens_stayed_told: fact "the wardens sat down".
  Rule wardens_stay_quiet when working() and hour(clock) >= 12 and wardensStay() and not at(party, mill_bridge) and not wardensAside(wardens) { Assert wardensAside(wardens). }
  Observe wardens_here at mill_bridge as sign when working() and wardensCame(wardens) and not wardensAside(wardens) and not wardensBroke(club) and able(wardens) "Hobday Pryce stands at the top of the bank with three wardens and their staves, red in the face, telling the young of Linger to rest, in a voice that is not resting. 'Down off it,' he says. 'Down off it, all of you, or we'll take you down. I'll give you till one.'".
  Rule wardens_break when working() and wardensCame(wardens) and hour(clock) >= 13 and not wardensAside(wardens) and not wardensBroke(club) and able(wardens) and not routed(wardens)
    says "At one o'clock the wardens go out onto the bridge. It is not a fight; the young of Linger do not know how to fight, and the wardens do not quite mean to. The new timbers go into the leat. The stone goes in after them. Davy Mote stands in their way with his stick and is knocked into the water. Corin Lindsell holds onto a timber, and a warden's staff comes down on her hand, and there is a sound, and she lets go. The warden, a Tolley, stands looking at his staff. He meant it. He did not know he did until it was done. It holds." {
    Assert wardensBroke(club). Assert corinHurt(corin). Retract means(corin).
  }
  Action talk_down(actor: group, site: place) "Talk Hobday Pryce down off the bank" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hobday, site) and working() and wardensCame(wardens) and not wardensAside(wardens) and not wardensBroke(club).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert wardensAside(wardens). }
    Result "You go up the bank to him and talk, not loud: about his daughter, about what a bridge is for, about what the Lull is for, about what he will look like to the Long Table tonight if he puts his staff through a mended bridge. Hobday listens with his jaw going. Then he plants the staff, and sits down on the bank by it, heavily, and the wardens sit down with him.".
    Otherwise "Hobday hears you out, and shakes his head. 'Rest,' he says, 'is the law of the Lull. I'm sorry for it. Off the bank.'".
  }
  Action talk_down_easy(actor: group, site: place) "Remind Hobday Pryce what you did for the mothers of Linger, and ask him to sit down" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hobday, site) and working() and wardensCame(wardens) and not wardensAside(wardens) and not wardensBroke(club) and hobdayGrateful(hobday).
    On success { Assert wardensAside(wardens). }
    Result "Hobday looks at you, and remembers, and his face does several things. 'That was meant,' he says at last. 'I said so.' He plants his staff in the turf and sits down on the bank beside it, and after a moment the wardens sit down too.".
  }
  Action stand_against(actor: group, site: place) "Stand on the bridge-end between the wardens and the Club" {
    Grave "Whatever you do to them here, you will mean.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wardens, site) and working() and wardensCame(wardens) and not wardensAside(wardens) and not wardensBroke(club).
    On success { Retract peaceable(wardens). Retract peaceable(hobday). Assert hostile(wardens, actor). Assert hostile(hobday, actor). Assert assails(wardens, actor). Assert assails(hobday, actor). }
    Result "You go and stand on the end of the new timbers with your hands where they can see them, and Hobday comes down the bank at you with the wardens, and nobody in the Lull has seen this in fifty-seven years.".
  }
  Rule wardens_routed when working() and wardensCame(wardens) and (routed(wardens) or dead(wardens)) and not wardensAside(wardens) { Assert wardensAside(wardens). }
  Rule warden_killed when (dead(wardens) or dead(hobday)) and dayThree() and not killedMeant(party) { Assert killedMeant(party). }
}

data/adventures/thrume/clocks.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "Thrume: a salt town where people pay to sleep, a giants' hold on the ridge, a mountain that is a body, a city that farms dreams, a tomb built to kill, a palace in a sky a thousand years gone, and what lies under every sleep.".

  // The country. The fells are the titan's body; everything but the dream and the Between is inside them or on them.
  Place fells "the Thrume country" is region.
  Place lowroad "the salt road" is wilderness within fells at 0, 3.
  Place saltgrave "Saltgrave" is settlement within fells at 1, 3.
  Place fellside "the fellside" is wilderness within fells at 1, 2.

  // Three clocks run under everything.
  // Thrume's stirring: two now; one more each morning the Margravine's overseer cuts; at six the ground shakes, at
  // ten he wakes.
  Measure stirring(place). Measure nextCut(place). Relation woken(place). Relation shaken(place).
  Initially Set stirring(fells) to 2. Initially Set nextCut(fells) to 144.
  Rule cut_stirs when cutting(brannoc) and watch(clock) >= nextCut(fells) and not woken(fells) {
    Increase stirring(fells) by 1. Set nextCut(fells) to nextCut(fells) + 144.
  }
  Rule ground_shakes when stirring(fells) >= 6 and not shaken(fells)
    says "The ground moves. Not a tremor: a slow, enormous shifting, like a sleeper turning over. Dust comes down from every roof-beam in the country, and then it is still." {
    Assert shaken(fells).
  }
  Rule thrume_wakes when stirring(fells) >= 10 and not woken(fells) and not sealed(fells) and not sungClean(fells)
    says "Thrume wakes. There is a sound under everything, deeper than sound, and then the fells stand up. Rivers run backwards off their shoulders. Somewhere to the south, where the Ebb is, the land is lifted and set down again in another place." {
    Assert woken(fells).
  }

  // Thrume's breath: an hour in, an hour out, for ever. The Lungs, the Room of Three Breaths and the cloud-stair keep
  // its time.
  Relation exhaling(place). Measure nextBreath(place).
  Initially Assert exhaling(fells). Initially Set nextBreath(fells) to 6.
  Rule breath_in when exhaling(fells) and watch(clock) >= nextBreath(fells) { Retract exhaling(fells). Set nextBreath(fells) to watch(clock) + 6. }
  Rule breath_out when not exhaling(fells) and watch(clock) >= nextBreath(fells) { Assert exhaling(fells). Set nextBreath(fells) to watch(clock) + 6. }

  // The host of Harle crosses the Ebb at the start of the tenth day. What stands on the Shoulder road that morning is
  // what the company left there.
  Relation crossed(place).
  Rule harle_crosses when watch(clock) >= 1296 and not crossed(fells) says "Word comes up the salt road at a gallop: the Duke of Harle's host is over the Ebb." { Assert crossed(fells). }

  // How it ends. These hold for ever once true; the epilogue observations below read them.
  Relation sealed(place). Relation sungClean(place). Relation cutOut(place).
  Observe end_woken at market when woken(fells) "Saltgrave is gone. Where the town was, a slope of new scree runs down into a valley that was not there yesterday, and the fells to the north are not where they were. Something vast is walking away into the west, taking its time.".
  Observe end_sung at market when sungClean(fells) and not woken(fells) "The fells are quiet, the right kind of quiet. The red salt in the Salt Office's cellar has gone grey and crumbles at a touch. People who never slept well in Saltgrave sleep now.".
  Observe end_sealed at market when sealed(fells) and not sungClean(fells) "The fells are still. Nobody in Saltgrave sleeps well, and the dream-houses stay shut.".
  Observe end_cut at market when cutOut(fells) "The Salt Office is loading wagons of red salt for the river, under guard, day and night. The springs above the town are running low, though it has rained.".
}

data/adventures/thrume/company.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Company party "Your company" of 3 at salt_road.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 30. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 3.
}

data/adventures/thrume/faces.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "The faces of Thrume that do not stand on the road to the Mouth: a clerk, a child who is a giant, a provost with a daughter, a young blood with a thane he carried to bed; and what the country does and no one can say why.".

  // ── Saltgrave: the clerk, the provost, the sister, the landlord ────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person pell "Maud Quarrow" at office_floor {
    Role "clerk of the Salt Office, who crossed out CLOSED and was told to cross it back". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "A woman of forty behind the long counter, with ink to the second knuckle, who has been weighing salt for the Office for nineteen years and has not been thanked for it once. 'If it is the Number Four,' she says, 'it is open. If it is a complaint, it is the provost. If it is a funeral, it is Sister Agathe.'".
  }
  Discovery orsett_buys "A factor of the Founders' Exchange at Orsett sends a carter to the Salt Office every spring, asking for unmarked red salt at three times the Margravine's price, and has been refused every year by an Office that did not know what it was refusing.".
  Topic pell_closed with pell "Ask Maud Quarrow who crossed out CLOSED on the Number Four" when true once {
    Says "'I wrote it,' says Quarrow. 'In red, the morning the roof came down on Brannoc's predecessor. The provost crossed it out that afternoon, on a rider's word from Ebb. I wrote it again. He crossed it out. We did it nine times.' She shows you the map, where the red has been scraped to a pink bruise. 'The tenth time I did not write it. Put that down somewhere for me. I was right nine times and I gave up on the tenth.'".
  }
  Topic pell_orsett with pell "Ask Maud Quarrow who else buys the red salt" when true once {
    Says "'Everyone has a use for salt that is red,' says Quarrow. 'The Margravine for the silver. The Hearth-Mother for the pinch on the doorstep. And once a spring a carter with a good coat comes up the road from Orsett on the river, from a Founders' Exchange, with a purse and no questions, and asks for it unmarked, unweighed, and unrecorded.' She sniffs. 'I say no. I say no in writing. I should like to know what a river factor wants with a thing that is warm.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, orsett_buys). }
  }
  Relation hauksTurned(group).
  Topic hauk_turn with hauk "Tell Provost Hauk that one of the carts' sleepers is Col Dunmore, who is sixteen" when knows(actor, carts_known) and knows(actor, col_gone) and not hauksTurned(hauk) once {
    Says "Hauk does not say that he has not asked. He opens his mouth to, and he looks at the open ledger, and at the three entries in his own hand, and shuts it. He gets up. He unlocks the strongbox, which makes a noise like a small door, and counts out twenty crowns on to the blotter, in coin the colour of the Lantern's salt. 'The Lantern's quiet,' he says. 'For the weeks I have kept it. It is the one thing in this room that I did not earn.' He pushes it across. 'Buy him back. I have a daughter in Ebb who is fourteen, and I would not like to be told what I did to a boy of sixteen with the price in my desk.'".
    On discuss { Assert hauksTurned(hauk). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 20. }
  }
  Topic agathe_tithe with agathe "Ask Sister Agathe why the Salt Office leaves a pinch at her door" when true once {
    Says "'The first salt out of every cart,' says Agathe. 'A pinch of white for the sill, older than the Office or the town. The carters will tell you it is a toll for the road-saint, paid so the axle holds. There is no road-saint. I have looked.' She smiles. 'Twice the Office has tried to end it, and twice a cart has broken an axle on the road up, so the carters think they were right. I do not say it is the Hearth-Mother. I say that Sorrow at the Saltcellar lost a wagon of hams the week the provost drew up the paper, and that the paper was burnt.'".
  }
  Topic agathe_fire with agathe "Ask Sister Agathe about the fire that never goes out" when true once {
    Says "'Nobody lit it,' says Agathe, and then, at the way you look: 'Somebody lit it. Nobody in this town knows who, and the Office has no record, and I have not asked the fire.' She turns a splinter over in her fingers. 'Pilgrims come through in summer from the west with ash on their sleeves, and sit by it, and go home.'".
  }
  Topic sorrow_ham with landlord "Ask Gil Sorrow about the hams on the beams" when true once {
    Says "'Cured in red,' says Gil Sorrow. 'You can't hang a ham in a town with salt like ours and not. It keeps forever, and it is the only ham I know of that you cannot eat a second time.' He cuts you a curl of it. It is dark, and sweet, and tastes of something you cannot quite put a name to: a summer, perhaps, not one of yours. 'The first slice, it's pork,' he says. 'The second, it's the pig's own last dream. Nobody orders it twice.'".
  }

  // ── The workings: the boots, and the man who lies badly ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe adit_boots at adit_head when true "Hung from the props at head height, boot after boot, pairs knotted by the laces: a hundred and twelve, by the count of anyone who counts. A boot for every man the Number Four has taken, in the way of the miners. A boy of about nine is sitting under them eating an apple, and says, without being asked, that you hang the boots up so the man has something to come back for.".
  Relation brannocLies(group).
  Topic brannoc_after with brannoc "Ask Overseer Brannoc what he will tell the Margravine" when stopped(brannoc) and not brannocLies(brannoc) once {
    Says "Brannoc chews the answer over like a man with a bad tooth; he has built his life on the ground being where the chalk says it is. 'That the Number Four has run dry,' he says. 'That the red was a pocket, and the roof is bad, and I will lose no more men to it.' He looks at the clean board. 'My brother was under the Ebb roof in the spring. I told the Margravine it would hold.' He spits to one side. 'I will tell it badly. You will find I am no use at it.'".
    On discuss { Assert brannocLies(brannoc). }
  }
  Observe brannoc_lying at market when brannocLies(brannoc) and not dark() "Overseer Brannoc has come up from the adit with six men in a file behind him, each with his own pick, and is standing at the Salt Office door telling the clerk that the Number Four has run dry. He is explaining it with his hands, and he is quite plainly the worst liar in the Margravine's service.".

  // ── The Shoulder Hall: the wolves, the child, the young blood, the thane ───────────────────────────────────────
  Kind thrume_whistle "Skarn's wolf-whistle, a pipe of yellow bone" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "A whistle of bone as long as your finger, bored with three holes, yellow with handling. The frost wolves of the Shoulder Hall come to it, and lie down.".
  Observe kennel_lamps at kennels when true "Hung on the wall of the wolf-pens, forty miners' lanterns, tin and horn, each with a twist of black wool through the handle where the giants' fingers could not manage the knot. They have been carried up the scree road with care and hung where the wolves cannot reach them, at the height of a miner's hand.".
  Item kennel_lantern "a miner's lantern from the wolf-pens" is lantern at kennels.
  Relation wolvesCalmed(group). Relation wolvesWhistled(group).
  Action calm_wolves(actor: group, site: place, r: member) "Let the ranger go in among the wolves, hands open" {
    Description "{r} has never been afraid of a thing in its own country. The wolves of the Shoulder Hall are in theirs.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, kennels) and at(wolves, kennels) and memberOf(r, actor) and hasCalling(r, calling_ranger) and awake(r) and not wolvesCalmed(actor) and not wolvesWhistled(actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert wolvesCalmed(actor). Assert tolerates(wolves, actor). }
    Result "{r} goes in alone, slowly, with the hands low and the eyes down and a noise in the throat that is not a word. The nearer wolf puts its head over {r}'s shoulder as a horse does, and breathes. 'They were pups when they came up the scree,' {r} says quietly, with the wolf's weight against one hip. 'Orphans. Nobody has touched one of them in a year but the girl.' The other wolf sits. The straw settles.".
  }
  Action whistle_wolves(actor: group, site: place) "Blow Skarn's bone whistle at the wolves" {
    Description "Skarn gave it for the asking of an honest question. The wolves know the sound better than the name.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, kennels) and at(wolves, kennels) and holding(actor, thrume_whistle) and not wolvesCalmed(actor) and not wolvesWhistled(actor).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert wolvesWhistled(actor). Assert tolerates(wolves, actor). }
    Result "Three notes, falling. The wolves look at one another, and then at you, with an expression of deep and personal betrayal, and lie down in the straw with their chins on their paws to be scratched.".
  }

  Person wenna "Wenna" at hearth {
    Role "the thane's granddaughter, who is eight, which is about the height of a barn door". Species shoulder_giant. Level 1. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner jovial.
    Greets "A very large child with a very small braid sits in the ashes of the mothers' hearth with a wooden hall in her lap, as long as a coffin, with doors that open. She looks at the company the way a cat looks at a mouse that has just walked in on its own. 'You are the right size,' she says, with deep satisfaction.".
  }
  Discovery wenna_rhyme "The giants' skipping rhyme, as an eight-year-old counts it out on the hearth-stones: 'Hollin, Orrab, Gur-and-Gwen, Bellow walks and will not stop, Marl lies down and Thrume lies last: count it, count it, count it fast.'".
  Discovery morrach_weeps "Thane Mórrach sits the high seat after the hall has gone to bed with a hand on the stone, and the stone hums back, and he weeps. Wenna has watched him from under a bench every night for a year.".
  Relation wennaPlayed(group).
  Action play_house(actor: group, site: place) "Let Wenna put the company to bed in her wooden hall" {
    Description "It is not a request.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hearth) and at(wenna, hearth) and guest(actor) and not wennaPlayed(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert wennaPlayed(actor). Assert knows(actor, wenna_rhyme). Assert knows(actor, morrach_weeps). }
    Result "You are lifted, one at a time, by the belt, and set down in a wooden hall that smells of resin, and put to bed on a pillow stuffed with sheepswool. Wenna sits over you like a roof. 'You are the guests,' she says. 'You have to be quiet and not be eaten. Grandfather is the thane and he sits in the chair and cries.' A pause. 'Not really. He pretends he is looking at the ceiling.' She counts you off on one finger the size of a loaf, singing under her breath, and gets it wrong, and begins again: 'Hollin, Orrab, Gur-and-Gwen, Bellow walks and will not stop, Marl lies down and Thrume lies last: count it, count it, count it fast.' The Rememberer, at the pillar, says without turning, in a voice like wind in a flue: 'Wenna. Put them down.' You are put down. Wenna is not sorry. 'Come back tomorrow,' she says. 'You can be the dragon.'".
  }
  Topic morrach_seat with morrach "Tell Thane Mórrach that Wenna says the seat hums back" when knows(actor, morrach_weeps) and state(morrach, presiding) once {
    Says "For a long time he does not answer. The great hand on his knee opens and closes once. 'She is eight,' he says at last. 'She tells everything. It is the best thing about her.' He looks at the stone arm of the seat. 'It hums when he turns over. It has hummed since the red salt came up. I sit here at night because it is the only place in the hold where I can hear whether he is still asleep.' A pause as long as a tide. 'Do not say so to Skarn.'".
  }
  Relation skarnAsked(group).
  Topic skarn_why with skarn "Ask Skarn why the young bloods want a war" when tolerates(skarn, actor) and not skarnAsked(skarn) once {
    Says "'Honour,' says Skarn. He says it at once, and loudly, and looks at the young bloods behind him to see that they heard. 'The old women keep the song. We keep the doors. A door that has been cut into, that is not a thing you talk about with a ring and a cup.' The great jaw works. 'The Margravine took a hand's breadth of the thane's belly and the thane has asked us to be patient. I have been patient for a year.'".
    On discuss { Assert skarnAsked(skarn). }
  }
  Topic skarn_pressed with skarn "Tell Skarn that his thane weeps at the high seat, and that Wenna told you" when knows(actor, morrach_weeps) and tolerates(skarn, actor) and skarnAsked(skarn) once {
    Says "Skarn goes quite still. The young bloods behind him, who have been playing at not listening, stop. 'The child,' he says. It is not a question. He sits down on a bench like a man sitting down on his own hand. 'I carry him to bed,' he says, very low. 'Every night, after. Eleven winters now he has been too heavy for the stair, and I have carried him, and I am the only one he lets. That is why I want the war. Because when the old ones go there is no one to carry me.' He takes a pipe of yellow bone from his belt and puts it on the floor in front of you. 'For the wolves,' he says. 'They are not mine to give, and they are the only thing in this hold that likes you. Do not say I gave you anything.'".
    On discuss { Give thrume_whistle to actor. }
  }
  Observe hearth_pebbles at hearth when true "At the foot of each pillar, in sockets cut in the floor-stone, a row of small round pebbles: grey for the most part, a few white, three of them red. The last socket in the row nearest the Rememberer's hand is empty, and has been kept clean.".
  Topic rememberer_stones with rememberer "Ask the Rememberer why every pillar has a row of pebbles at its foot" when true once {
    Says "'A pebble for each of us who has died,' says the Rememberer. 'The size of the life, not the person. Grey for the quiet ones, white for the angry, and red for the three who were cut down by smiths.' Her long hand goes over the lowest hand's breadth of the pillar, where the sockets run like a row of teeth. 'There is one socket that is empty. It is for the one the song has not named yet. We are the only people I know who set a place at the table for the dead we have not met.'".
  }

  // ── Outward: what Thrume reads of the world ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe gauge_slack at gauge_room when befell(slack_opened) "The brass hand of the dial, which has stood at the same mark since the smiths went, has moved. A hair's breadth, backward, as though a count somewhere very far away had paused and this one had stopped to listen.".
  Observe landing_cloudgate at cloud_landing when befell(cloudgate_fell) "The cloud is thinner at one edge than it was, as if a great piece of the sky had been taken from the dream. Far off, in the white, something the size of a city has come down out of the weather and is lying on the water with its lamps on, and Thrume has noticed it, and cannot decide whether to dream it.".

  // ── Where the story is read, once it is over ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation smithsSung(place). Relation rhymeSung(place).
  Rule smiths_sung when sungClean(fells) and at(party, mouth_edge) and knows(party, smith_names) and not smithsSung(fells)
    says "Between the names of the old ones the song takes in a smaller list, one you did not know you were singing: Ysolt Fenn, and a hundred and six more, the Hollow Smiths of the delving, who climbed the hill and wept and died in dozens. The Mouth cannot swallow them either. Somewhere above, in a low cold room that smells of tallow, a hundred and seven pegs creak, as if every hammer had been set down at once." {
    Assert smithsSung(fells).
  }
  Rule rhyme_sung when sungClean(fells) and at(party, mouth_edge) and knows(party, wenna_rhyme) and not rhymeSung(fells)
    says "As you reach the last name, a child's voice, a long way off and very high, takes the line out of your mouth and finishes it, too fast and a little flat, the way it is done on the hearth-stones: 'Thrume lies last: count it, count it, count it fast.' The grey does not know what to do with a child counting. It goes very still, and listens." {
    Assert rhymeSung(fells).
  }

  Objective settle_wage when knows(party, gods_wage) and not paidSettled(paid) and not paidLaid(paid) "The Paid stand at the pay-window in the Delving, waiting for a wage that was never handed over.".
}

data/adventures/thrume/hush.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "Hush: the city of the Quiet Court, grown in the hollow of the titan's skull, where nobody speaks aloud.".

  Place hushc "Hush" is settlement within fells at 2, 0.
  Place lull_house "House Lull" is building within hushc.
  Place pallor_house "House Pallor" is building within hushc.
  Place spire "the Abbess's spire" is building within hushc.
  Place grey_library "the Silent Library" is building within hushc.

  Place hush_gate "the gate of Hush" is room within hushc at 0, 1.
  Place hand_street "the Street of Hands" is room within hushc at 1, 1.
  Place thrall_market "the Thrall-Market" is room within hushc at 1, 2.
  Place lull_hall "the hall of House Lull" is room within lull_house at 2, 2.
  Place pallor_hall "the hall of House Pallor" is room within pallor_house at 0, 2.
  Place library_hall "the Silent Library" is room within grey_library at 0, 0.
  Place choir "the Choir" is room within hushc at 2, 1.
  Place spire_foot "the foot of the spire" is room within spire at 1, 0.
  Place spire_top "the Abbess's room" is room within spire at 2, 0.
  Place throat_head "the head of the long throat" is room within hushc at 3, 1.

  Passage hush_in "the gate of Hush" is arch between hush_approach and hush_gate taking 10 minutes.
  Passage hand_way "the Street of Hands" is path between hush_gate and hand_street taking 10 minutes.
  Passage market_way "the market steps" is path between hand_street and thrall_market taking 10 minutes.
  Passage lull_door "the door of House Lull" is door between thrall_market and lull_hall.
  Passage pallor_door "the door of House Pallor" is door between thrall_market and pallor_hall.
  Passage library_door "the library door" is door between hand_street and library_hall.
  Passage choir_way "the choir walk" is path between hand_street and choir taking 10 minutes.
  Passage spire_door "the spire door" is door between choir and spire_foot.
  Passage spire_stair "the spire stair" is steps between spire_foot and spire_top taking 10 minutes.
  Passage throat_way "the far street" is path between choir and throat_head taking 20 minutes.

  Observe hgate_scene at hush_gate when true "A city of grey stone grown rather than built, like coral, under a roof of bone so high it might be sky. Grey light comes from nowhere. There is no sound at all. People move in the streets, tall and soft-faced, and talk to each other with their long hands.".
  Observe street_scene at hand_street when true "The Street of Hands. The Court's people pass you without looking, their fingers moving. Here and there a human thrall walks behind one of them, eyes still and smiling, carrying something.".
  Observe tmarket_scene at thrall_market when true "A square of niches cut in the grey stone, like a dovecote for people. In each niche someone sleeps, propped up, with a crust of red salt on their lips. Their eyes are moving. Some of the Court stand before the niches with their faces very close to the sleepers' faces, not touching, and the sleepers' faces go slack, and the Court's faces grow pink.".
  Observe lull_scene at lull_hall when true "A soft room, warm, hung with grey stuffs that drink the light. It smells of milk and sleep. The people of House Lull lie on low couches like cats.".
  Observe pallor_scene at pallor_hall when true "A hard bright room. Spears of grey crystal racked on the walls. On a table, a sleeper is laid out, and he is having a nightmare, and three of House Pallor are standing over him, very close.".
  Observe glibrary_scene at library_hall when true "Shelves of grey scrolls, and the readers read them with their fingertips, eyes shut.".
  Observe choir_scene at choir when exhaling(fells) "The Choir: a round amphitheatre, full. The whole Court sits in rows with their faces turned up to the bone roof, and the roof is humming. Above them, through the bone, you can feel something enormous dreaming, and the Court is drinking it.".
  Observe choir_empty at choir when not exhaling(fells) "The amphitheatre stands empty and humming faintly, like a bell after it is struck.".
  Observe spirefoot_scene at spire_foot when true "The foot of a spire of grey crystal. Steps go up round the inside of it.".
  Observe spiretop_scene at spire_top when true "A small round room at the top of the spire, open to the bone roof. On a pedestal of grey crystal rests something like a great closed eyelid of red stone, as big as a shield, and it is warm.".
  Observe throat_scene at throat_head when true "At the edge of the city, where the grey coral stops, a great shaft goes down: smooth, ribbed, red at the bottom. The long throat. Warm air comes up it, and the slow sound of a heart.".

  Species court_kin "one of the Quiet Court" like mind_destroyer.
  Person weigher "the Weigher" at thrall_market {
    Role "master of the Thrall-Market". Species court_kin. Level 8. Peaceable.
  }
  Person col "Col Dunmore" at thrall_market {
    Role "a boy asleep in a niche, with salt on his lips". Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Peaceable.
  }
  Thing col_niche "Col's niche" at thrall_market {
    State held "In a low niche at the end of a row, a boy of sixteen sleeps with his head against the stone and salt on his lips. He is very thin.".
    State broken "Col's niche is broken open, and empty.".
    Change smash_niche "Break Col's niche open" from held to broken needing brawn.
  }
  Topic weigher_col with weigher "Ask the Weigher the price of the boy in the end niche" when not freed(col) and state(col_niche, held) once {
    Says "The Weigher's long fingers move, and a thrall standing beside it speaks for it in a pleasant, empty voice. 'That one dreams of his father. Very rich. Ten coin.' The fingers move again. 'There are four hundred and twelve in the market. Do you want them all?'".
  }
  Action buy_col(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the Weigher ten coin for Col Dunmore" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, thrall_market) and at(weigher, thrall_market) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 10 and not freed(col).
    Time 1.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Increase quantity(weigher, gold) by 10. Assert freed(col). Assert state(col_niche, broken). Assert at(col, chandlery_shop). }
    Result "The Weigher takes the coins without looking at them. A thrall lifts Col out of the niche like a sack, and he wakes, and does not know you, and then he does. He walks up the long way out without speaking. 'His mother,' he says once, at the gate, and that is all. Behind you, someone else is put in his niche.".
  }
  Rule col_snatched when state(col_niche, broken) and not freed(col)
    says "Col falls out of the broken niche into your arms, awake and screaming. Every face in the market turns. Across the square the door of House Pallor opens." {
    Assert freed(col). Assert at(col, chandlery_shop). Assert roused(hushc).
  }
  Observe col_home at chandlery_shop when freed(col) "Col Dunmore sits by the stove wrapped in a blanket, and his mother has not let go of his hand.".
  Topic col_thanks with col "Ask Col Dunmore what he saw below" when freed(col) and at(col, chandlery_shop) once {
    Says "Col looks at the stove. 'There's a palace,' he says. 'Up in the sky, inside the mountain. In the dream. They take you there and you walk about and it's beautiful. And she's there, the Abbess, at the top of a tower, at the end of a bridge. And under the bridge there's nothing.' He holds his mother's hand harder. 'Not nothing. Something that's hungry.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, mouth_rumoured). }
  }
  Discovery mouth_rumoured "Under the bridge from the Abbess's tower in the dreamed palace there is something hungry.".

  // The Houses.
  Person lady_lull "the Lady of Lull" at lull_hall {
    Role "head of House Lull". Species court_kin. Level 10. Peaceable.
  }
  Relation lullPact(group).
  Topic lull_bargain with lady_lull "Ask the Lady of Lull what House Lull wants" when not lullPact(actor) {
    Says "A thrall at the couch's foot speaks for her. 'Sleep,' says the empty voice. 'Long, soft, sweet, for ever. The Abbess and House Pallor want him stirred, nearly woken, so the dreams are strong. Strong dreams are bitter. And if he wakes, there are no dreams at all.' The Lady's fingers move, slow. 'You want the Abbess's Eye. The Abbess sits with the Choir when he breathes out; her spire is empty then. Go with my sign and her guard will not see you, and leave by the servants' bone stair at the spire's foot; it goes down to the throat. Promise me he will sleep.'".
    On discuss { Assert lullPact(actor). Assert tolerates(spire_guard, actor). Assert knows(actor, choir_time). Assert knows(actor, bone_stair_known). }
  }
  Discovery bone_stair_known "From the foot of the Abbess's spire, a servants' stair of bone goes down to the head of the long throat." {
    Found by searching spire_foot "Behind the curve of the spire wall, a narrow stair of yellowed bone goes down, worn by small feet.".
  }
  Passage bone_stair "the servants' bone stair" is passage between spire_foot and throat_head taking 20 minutes hidden until bone_stair_known.
  Discovery choir_time "The Abbess goes down from her spire to sit with the Choir while Thrume breathes out.".
  Person pallor_guards "House Pallor" at pallor_hall {
    Role "the soldiers of House Pallor". Species court_kin. Level 9. Numbers 3. Temperament obedient.
    Uses go, assail. Plans 8 steps.
  }
  Pursuit pallor_hunt for pallor_guards "hunting the intruders through Hush" priority 20 when roused(hushc) and able(pallor_guards) seeks assails(pallor_guards, party).
  Rule pallor_sees when at(party, pallor_hall) and not roused(hushc)
    says "Three soft faces turn from the nightmare on the table toward you, all at once, like flowers to the sun." { Assert roused(hushc). }

  // The Silent Library.
  Discovery mouth_known "The grey scrolls of the Silent Library, read with the fingers: under every sleeping thing is the Between, where forgotten dreams fall, and in it the Mouth, which eats them. The Court is a seed of the Mouth. The Abbess serves it. In the Heart-Tomb below, the Keeper's Chair beside the heart opens on Thrume's dream, and from the dream a bridge goes down to the Between." {
    Source grey_scrolls "the grey scrolls" at library_hall readable by party.
  }

  // The Abbess and her Eye.
  Person abbess "the Abbess of Hush" at spire_top {
    Role "the Abbess of Hush". Species court_kin. Level 14. Peaceable.
    Objects "The Abbess's long hands go still. Every thrall in Hush turns, at once, toward you. Then the soft grey people come.".
  }
  Rule abbess_to_choir when exhaling(fells) and at(abbess, spire_top) { Assert at(abbess, choir). }
  Rule abbess_to_spire when not exhaling(fells) and at(abbess, choir) { Assert at(abbess, spire_top). }
  Rule abbess_angered when hostile(abbess, party) and not roused(hushc) { Assert roused(hushc). }
  Rule eye_missed when at(abbess, spire_top) and not inside(the_eye, pedestal) and not roused(hushc) and not sungClean(fells)
    says "Far off, at the top of the spire, something without a mouth screams, and every thrall in Hush screams with it, all at once, and then is silent. In the silence, doors open." {
    Assert roused(hushc).
  }
  Person spire_guard "the spire's guard" at spire_foot {
    Role "a tall one of the Court with a spear of grey crystal". Species court_kin. Level 9. Temperament obedient.
    Guards spire_stair.
    State watching blocking "A tall one of the Court stands at the foot of the spire stair with a spear of grey crystal, and its soft face follows you.".
  }
  Kind abbess_eye "the Abbess's Eye, a closed lid of warm red stone the size of a shield" is treasure worth 0 weighing 3.
  Thing pedestal "the grey pedestal" at spire_top {
    Holds.
  }
  Item the_eye "the Abbess's Eye" is abbess_eye in pedestal owned by abbess.

  Objective free_col when knows(party, col_gone) and knows(party, hush_named) and not freed(col) "Col Dunmore is in Hush.".
  Objective take_eye when knows(party, mouth_known) and inside(the_eye, pedestal) "The Abbess keeps the Eye; the Heart-Tomb's door needs it.".
}

data/adventures/thrume/placed.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  // Thrume as a country beyond a march: the company that comes in by the salt road is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  // What is said of Thrume in the country behind it: once it is seen through, it is old news there.
  Entity word: fact "What is said of Thrume and Saltgrave in the country behind it.".
  Rule word_old when (woken(fells) or sungClean(fells) or sealed(fells) or cutOut(fells) or crossed(fells)) and not stale(word) { Assert stale(word). }
}

data/adventures/thrume/saltgrave.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "Saltgrave: the Salt Office, the dream-houses, the night carts.".

  Place salt_office "the Salt Office" is building within saltgrave.
  Place saltcellar "the Saltcellar" is building within saltgrave.
  Place red_lantern "the Red Lantern" is building within saltgrave.
  Place shrine "the Hearth-Mother's shrine" is building within saltgrave.
  Place chandlery "Dunmore's chandlery" is building within saltgrave.

  Place salt_road "the salt road below the town" is room within lowroad at 0, 0.
  Place market "the market square" is room within saltgrave at 1, 1.
  Place office_floor "the Salt Office" is room within salt_office at 2, 1.
  Place provost_room "the provost's room" is room within salt_office at 2, 0.
  Place inn_room "the Saltcellar's taproom" is room within saltcellar at 0, 1.
  Place lantern_front "the Red Lantern's front room" is room within red_lantern at 1, 2.
  Place smoke_room "the smoke-room" is room within red_lantern at 2, 2.
  Place lantern_back "the back room of the Red Lantern" is room within red_lantern at 2, 3.
  Place shrine_room "the shrine" is room within shrine at 0, 0.
  Place chandlery_shop "Dunmore's chandlery" is room within chandlery at 0, 2.
  Place miners_row "the miners' row" is room within saltgrave at 1, 0.
  Place carters_yard "the carters' yard" is room within saltgrave at 1, 3.
  Place cart_road "the cart road" is room within fellside at 1, 1.
  Place scree_foot "the foot of the scree road" is room within fellside at 0, 0.

  Passage salt_gate "the town gate" is road between salt_road and market taking 20 minutes.
  Passage office_door "the Salt Office door" is door between market and office_floor.
  Passage provost_door "the provost's door" is door between office_floor and provost_room.
  Passage inn_door "the Saltcellar's door" is door between market and inn_room.
  Passage lantern_door "the Red Lantern's door" is door between market and lantern_front.
  Passage smoke_curtain "the smoke-room curtain" is doorway between lantern_front and smoke_room.
  Passage lantern_back_door "the Lantern's back door" is door between smoke_room and lantern_back.
  Passage back_yard_gate "the yard gate behind the Lantern" is gate between lantern_back and carters_yard.
  Passage shrine_door "the shrine door" is door between market and shrine_room.
  Passage chandlery_door "Dunmore's door" is door between market and chandlery_shop.
  Passage row_lane "the row lane" is path between market and miners_row taking 10 minutes.
  Passage yard_lane "the yard lane" is path between market and carters_yard taking 10 minutes.
  Passage cart_track "the cart road" is road between carters_yard and cart_road taking 1 hour.
  Passage scree_lane "the north lane" is path between miners_row and scree_foot taking 30 minutes.

  Observe road_scene at salt_road when not dark() "The salt road comes up out of the river country between fields gone white at the edges, as if salted. Ahead, Saltgrave sits under the fells in its own dust: new timber, white roofs, a church tower with no church yet. Beyond the town the fells go up and up, brown and long and oddly smooth, like something lying under a blanket.".
  Observe road_night at salt_road when dark() "The town's lights are few and yellow. One lantern, red, burns later than the rest.".
  Observe market_scene at market when not dark() and not woken(fells) "A square of trodden white dust. Carts, salt-dust on everything, a dry pump, a notice on a post, and on one side a narrow house with a red lantern over its door, unlit by day. Everyone who crosses the square looks north to the fells, and then at the notice. The Margravine's envoy eats at the Saltcellar; the families of the men the giants took are in the miners' row; and the Red Lantern is where people go to pay to sleep, and some of them do not come back.".
  Observe market_night at market when dark() and not woken(fells) "The square is empty but for a dog. Over the narrow house on the south side, the red lantern is lit.".
  Observe office_scene at office_floor when true "Scales, sacks, a long counter and a clerk behind it. On the wall a map of the workings, Number One to Number Four, and on Number Four someone has written CLOSED in red, and someone else has crossed it out.".
  Observe provost_scene at provost_room when true "A good room for a raw town: a carpet, a decanter, a strongbox. A ledger lies open on the desk.".
  Observe inn_scene at inn_room when true "Low beams, salt-cured hams, and miners drinking without talking. In the best corner a man in the Margravine's blue and silver eats alone, with a sword across the bench beside him.".
  Observe front_scene at lantern_front when true "A dim room hung with red cloth, warm and sweet as a bakery. The rushes have been swept to the walls so that no boot will scrape. A little table, a bell with its clapper bound in wool, and a chair behind them.".
  Observe smoke_scene at smoke_room when true "Pallets in a row, and on them people asleep with their eyes moving under the lids: miners, a girl in a good dress, an old man. A brazier burns something red that smells of iron and rain. Every sleeper's lips are moving, and they are all saying the same thing.".
  Observe back_scene at lantern_back when true "A storeroom: sacks of red salt, blankets, rope. A row of pegs by the yard gate, and on them the coats of people who are not wearing them.".
  Observe shrine_scene at shrine_room when true "A whitewashed room with a hearth for an altar. The fire on it is the only one in Saltgrave that never goes out. Prayers are nailed on the wall on scraps: for the men in the Number Four, for a son, for sleep.".
  Observe chandlery_scene at chandlery_shop when true "Candles, rope, lamp-oil, picks, stacked to the rafters for a mine that is shut. Candles are sold singly now, each in a twist of paper, and the men who buy them say they are for sleeping by.".
  Observe row_scene at miners_row when true "A double row of salt-white cottages. Forty doors have a twist of black wool on the latch: the families of the men the giants took.".
  Observe yard_scene at carters_yard when not dark() "A yard of salt-carts with their shafts down, and the stable smell. The carts have stood idle since the mine was shut; their axles are freshly greased.".
  Observe cart_road_scene at cart_road when true "The cart road climbs the fellside in long loops toward the black mouths of the workings. The turf on either side is warm to the hand.".
  Observe scree_foot_scene at scree_foot when true "The north lane gives out into scree. A path goes up it, very steep, toward the shoulder of the fells and a smudge of smoke under the glacier.".
  Passage scree_climb_long "the scree road" is path between scree_foot and scree_road taking 2 hours.

  // The Margravine's envoy, and the price on the thane.
  Person varne "Sir Odo Varne" at inn_room {
    Role "the Margravine's envoy". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 6. Peaceable.
    Greets "Sir Odo Varne has the Margravine's notice in a leather tube on the table and his sword across his knees, and has evidently decided that a visitor is either a witness or a rival. 'Varne,' he says. 'Envoy. Sit, and tell me if you are going up the fell. I should like to know whether to be sorry for you.'".
    Greets again "Sir Odo Varne has not moved the sword, but he has moved the notice, so that you can read it upside down. 'Harrowby is a good lordship,' he says. 'Eighteen hundred acres and a mill. I should like to be a man who had earned it with a better thing than a head.'".
  }
  Discovery bounty_known "The Margravine's notice: FOR THE HEAD OF THE GIANT MÓRRACH, THAT CALLS HIMSELF THANE, THE LORDSHIP OF HARROWBY AND ITS RENTS. SIR O. VARNE, FOR IDONY VASK, MARGRAVINE OF EBB." {
    Source notice "the notice on the market post" at market readable by party.
    Known by varne.
  }
  Topic varne_bounty with varne "Ask Sir Odo Varne about the giants" when true once {
    Says "'Four months back they came off the fells,' says Varne. 'Smashed every mine-head. Took forty men. Burned the overseer in his house.' He wipes his knife and does not look up. 'The Margravine wants salt by the new moon. Harle's host is at the Ebb by then, and the companies she means to hire want something heavier than promises. Bring me the thane's head and you are lords.' The knife goes home in its sheath. 'Brannoc is down the old adit with a crew to keep the salt coming. He does not stop. Do not ask him to.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bounty_known). Assert knows(actor, brannoc_below). }
  }
  Discovery brannoc_below "Overseer Brannoc has gone down the old adit of the Number Four with a crew, to keep cutting red salt for the Margravine.".
  Topic varne_truth with varne "Tell Sir Odo Varne what the red salt is" when knows(actor, thrume_known) and knows(actor, salt_is_blood) once {
    Says "Varne hears you out without interrupting, which is a courtesy you did not expect. At the end he is quiet a long time. 'If you are lying, you are the best liars I ever met,' he says. 'If you are not, the Margravine is cutting the throat of the ground she stands on.' He takes a folded paper from his coat, sealed in blue wax, writes on it, and holds it out. 'Brannoc obeys the seal. Not me. The seal. Give him this.'".
    On discuss { Assert lends(varne, seal_letter, actor). Assert at(seal_letter, inn_room). }
  }
  Kind margrave_seal "a letter under the Margravine's blue seal" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0.
  Item seal_letter "an order under the Margravine's seal" is margrave_seal at limbo owned by varne.
  Place limbo "nowhere" is room within lowroad at 1, 0.

  // The provost and his ledger.
  Person hauk "Provost Lisle Hauk" at provost_room {
    Role "provost of the Salt Office". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
    Greets "Provost Lisle Hauk rises behind a desk so tidy it looks swept, and takes a half-step to keep the ledger between you and the door. 'The Salt Office is open,' he says, though the board outside says closed. 'For you, it is open. I have always held that a visitor is a matter of principle.'".
    Greets again "Provost Hauk has shut the ledger before you are through the door, and laid a paperweight of red salt on it. 'You have been in the town,' he says, 'and in the town things are said. I would ask you to remember that the Office does not say them. The Office only weighs.'".
    Objects "Hauk sees {?i} in your hands and goes the colour of tallow. 'That is the Office's,' he says. 'I will have the watch on you.'".
  }
  Discovery ledger_known "The Salt Office ledger: every week since spring, forty crowns in salt-silver from 'the Lantern, for quiet', in the provost's own hand. Beside the last three entries, a tally of carts: four, six, nine." {
    Source office_ledger "the Salt Office ledger" at provost_room readable by party.
    Known by hauk.
  }
  Topic hauk_lantern with hauk "Ask Provost Hauk about the Red Lantern" when not knows(actor, ledger_known) once {
    Says "'A respectable house,' says Hauk. 'Miners need their rest. The Office licenses it.' He moves the ledger an inch further from you without looking at it.".
  }
  Topic hauk_ledger with hauk "Ask Provost Hauk what the carts in his ledger carry" when knows(actor, ledger_known) once {
    Says "Hauk sits down. 'Sleepers,' he says, very low. 'The ones who sleep too deep to wake. She says they are taken up to the hot springs above the workings, to be cured. She pays for the carts. She pays for my not asking.' He looks at his hands. 'I have not asked. I have a daughter in Ebb.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, carts_known). }
  }

  // The dream-house.
  Person quietly "Mother Quietly" at lantern_front {
    Role "keeper of the Red Lantern". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
    State smiling "Mother Quietly sits behind her little table with her hands folded, smiling. Her eyes do not move when she looks at you; her head does.".
    State emptied "Mother Quietly sits behind her little table with her hands folded. There is nobody behind her eyes at all.".
  }
  Person dreamers "the dreamers" at smoke_room {
    Role "sleepers on the pallets". Ancestry human. Numbers 4. Peaceable.
  }
  Discovery dream_shared "Everyone who sleeps on the red salt dreams the same dream: a palace in a sky too close to the ground, and a great slow heart beating under the floor.".
  Topic dreamers_dream with dreamers "Listen to what the sleepers are saying" when true once {
    Says "You lean close. They are all saying it, the girl in the good dress and the old man and the miners, in the same breath: 'The sky is so close. The floor is beating. The sky is so close. The floor is beating.' One of the miners opens his eyes, looks at you without seeing you, and says, quite clearly, 'He is turning over,' and sleeps again.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, dream_shared). }
  }
  Topic quietly_col with quietly "Ask Mother Quietly about Col Dunmore" when knows(actor, col_gone) and state(quietly, smiling) once {
    Says "'Such a sad boy,' says Mother Quietly. 'His father in the mine. He slept so beautifully.' Her head tilts; her eyes stay where they were. 'He has gone up to the springs, to be cured. They all go up, the deep sleepers. Would you like to rest a little? You look so tired.'".
  }
  Action rest_on_salt(actor: group, site: place) "Lie down on a pallet and breathe the red smoke" {
    Description "Mother Quietly says it is the best sleep in the world. The dreamers' faces say she may be right.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, smoke_room) and not dreamt(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert dreamt(actor). }
    Result "You sleep, and you are standing in a palace of white stone with the sky so close above it you could touch the clouds. Under the floor something vast is beating, very slowly, and the whole palace rises and falls with it like a chest. Far away, at the end of a long hall, someone grey with no mouth turns to look at you, and you wake on the pallet with your heart going like a bird's.".
  }
  Relation dreamt(group).
  // Seen only by those who have dreamt on the salt: what the Court's thralls look like to the dreaming.
  Person watcher "the grey thing behind Mother Quietly" at lantern_front {
    Role "something grey and soft-faced, standing where her shadow should be". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
    Seen when dreamt(viewer).
  }
  Topic watcher_speaks with watcher "Look the grey thing in its soft face" when true once {
    Says "It has no mouth. It speaks anyway, inside your head, in a voice as warm as a bed: 'You slept so well. Come down and sleep with us. It is so quiet in Hush.' Mother Quietly, in front of it, smiles a little wider, as if she had said it.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hush_named). }
  }
  Topic watcher_hush with watcher "Ask the grey thing what Hush is" when knows(actor, hush_named) once {
    Says "'Quiet,' it says, inside your head, in that kind voice. 'Nobody is afraid in Hush. Nobody is cold, or sorry, or anything at all. You would like it so much.' It does not move. Its soft face stays turned to you the whole time you are in the room, the way a sunflower stays turned to the sun.".
  }

  // The night carts.
  Person hushed "the night carters" at lantern_back {
    Role "two men with still eyes, who do not speak". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Numbers 2. Peaceable.
  }
  Topic hushed_asked with hushed "Ask the two men with still eyes what they do here" when true once {
    Says "Neither of them answers. The nearer one looks at you the way a man looks at rain on a window, and then past you at the Lantern's back gate, and waits, quite patiently, for you to stop being there. Their eyes do not blink as often as eyes should. When you step back, both of them, at the same moment, breathe out.".
  }
  Relation carting(group). Relation ringBroken(group).
  Rule carters_out when dark() and at(hushed, lantern_back) and not ringBroken(hushed) and untilLight(clock) > 36 { Assert at(hushed, carters_yard). Assert carting(hushed). }
  Rule carters_back when at(hushed, carters_yard) and (untilLight(clock) <= 36 or ringBroken(hushed)) { Assert at(hushed, lantern_back). Retract carting(hushed). }
  Observe carts_by_night at carters_yard when carting(hushed) "Two men with still eyes are lifting sleepers out of the Lantern's back gate, wrapped in blankets, and laying them in a salt-cart like sacks. Nobody sleeping wakes. When the cart is full they lead the horse out on the cart road toward the workings, without a lantern." teaches carts_known.
  Discovery carts_known "By night the Red Lantern's carters carry the deepest sleepers up the cart road to the workings, in salt-carts.".

  // Breaking the ring: Mother Quietly cornered.
  Topic quietly_carts with quietly "Ask Mother Quietly where the carts go" when knows(actor, carts_known) and state(quietly, smiling) once {
    Says "Mother Quietly's smile does not change. Then it does not change for too long. Her hands come apart on the table, slowly, as if someone else were unfolding them, and she sits back. Her mouth opens. 'Down,' she says, in a voice with no breath behind it. 'Down to Hush, where it is quiet.' Then nothing is behind her eyes at all. Something drops from her fingers and rolls across the table: a grey pebble, humming.".
    On discuss { Assert state(quietly, emptied). Assert ringBroken(hushed). Assert knows(actor, hush_named). Assert knows(actor, quietly_emptied). }
  }
  Discovery hush_named "The sleepers carried from the Red Lantern go 'down to Hush, where it is quiet'.".
  Discovery quietly_emptied "Cornered, Mother Quietly was emptied like a cup by whatever was behind her, and dropped a grey humming stone.".
  Kind hush_stone "a grey pebble that hums at the edge of hearing" is treasure worth 1 weighing 0.
  Item hush_pebble "a grey humming pebble" is hush_stone at lantern_front hidden until quietly_emptied.

  // Hesper Dunmore and her son.
  Person hesper "Hesper Dunmore" at chandlery_shop {
    Role "chandler, whose son has not come home". Ancestry human. Peaceable.
    Greets "Hesper Dunmore is trimming a candle that does not need trimming, one wick after another along the shelf, working steadily from left to right, and has to start again at the left when you speak. 'Rope, torches, rations,' she says. 'The boy used to keep the counter. Forgive me. I have been three nights at this shelf.'".
    Greets again "Hesper Dunmore has trimmed the whole shelf and begun again from the left. 'You have been to the Lantern,' she says, not as a question. 'I can tell by how you stand. People who have been there stand as if they were listening for something they have not got.'".
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 8. Sells torch for 1 coin from 12. Sells rope for 1 coin from 4.
  }
  Discovery col_gone "Col Dunmore, sixteen, started sleeping at the Red Lantern after his father died in the Number Four, and has not come home in three nights.".
  Topic hesper_col with hesper "Ask Hesper Dunmore what is wrong" when true once {
    Says "'My boy,' says Hesper, and puts down the candle she was trimming. 'Col. His father died in the Number Four in the spring, and Col couldn't sleep, and someone told him about the Red Lantern. He slept there every night after. Three nights ago he didn't come home.' She looks at you. 'The watch says he's gone off to the giants for the bounty. He's sixteen and he's frightened of dogs. Will you look?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, col_gone). }
  }
  Topic hesper_news with hesper "Tell Hesper Dunmore where Col was taken" when knows(actor, hush_named) and knows(actor, col_gone) once {
    Says "Hesper listens with both hands flat on her counter. 'Down,' she says. 'Down where?' Then: 'No. Don't tell me. Bring him up.' She pushes a cloth of bread and cheese across the counter and will not take money for it.".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, rations) by 2. }
  }

  // The shrine: rest, healing, and a priest who knows the old stories.
  Person agathe "Sister Agathe" at shrine_room {
    Role "keeper of the Hearth-Mother's fire". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Level 4. Peaceable.
    Greets "Sister Agathe is on her knees at the hearth-shrine with a brush and a pan, taking up the ash as carefully as another woman would take up a baby. 'The fire has not gone out in two hundred years,' she says. 'I mean to keep that true another night. Mind where you put your feet.'".
    Greets again "Sister Agathe sets down the brush and rubs the ash into the lines of her palms, which is her way of putting on a clean face. 'Another prayer for sleep,' she says. 'You are not asking, I see. You are the first this week who is not asking. Sit.'".
    Offers healing "the Hearth-Mother's blessing and clean linen" for 2 coin.
  }
  Topic agathe_fells with agathe "Ask Sister Agathe about the fells" when true once {
    Says "'The old shepherds had a saying,' says Agathe. 'Walk soft on Thrume, he's only sleeping.' She smiles. 'They meant the giant in the stories. The one the hills were made from.' She looks at the prayers on the wall. 'Since the Number Four broke through, I have had more prayers for sleep than for anything else. People here cannot sleep, and when they do they all dream the same.'".
  }

  // The Saltcellar.
  Person landlord "Gil Sorrow" at inn_room {
    Role "landlord of the Saltcellar". Profession innkeeper. Peaceable.
    Greets "Gil Sorrow is wiping a tankard with a cloth that has not been white since the old Margrave, and holding it to the light for a flaw that is in the cloth. 'The Saltcellar,' he says. 'Beds, beer, bread, and an opinion if you want one. The opinion is free, which is why nobody does.'".
    Greets again "Gil Sorrow has put your name on the slate behind the bar, and rubbed it out, and put it on again. 'I never know,' he says, 'whether it is bad luck to write a traveller down. The last three who were written down went up the fell.'".
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 8. Sells torch for 1 coin from 6.
  }

  // The miners' row: the families, and the way to the giants.
  Person wives "the miners' wives" at miners_row {
    Role "women of the miners' row". Ancestry human. Numbers 3. Peaceable.
  }
  Topic wives_giants with wives "Ask the miners' wives about the giants" when true once {
    Says "'They didn't kill anyone that night,' says a woman with a baby on her hip. 'Only the overseer, and that was the fire. They took the men out of the Number Four like you'd take kittens out of a well, and carried them up the scree road.' Another says: 'Aud Brenning's with them. Aud doesn't die easy.' The first: 'If you go up there for the Margravine's money, you can bring ours home while you're about it.'".
  }

  Objective find_col when knows(party, col_gone) and not freed(col) "Hesper Dunmore's son Col did not come home from the Red Lantern.".
  Objective lay_thane when knows(party, bounty_known) and not knows(party, thrume_known) "The Margravine will pay a lordship for Thane Mórrach's head.".
}

data/adventures/thrume/shoulder.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "The Shoulder Hall: the giants' hold on the ridge, forty miners held in it, and the keepers' way down into the body.".

  Place scree "the scree road" is wilderness within fells at 0, 1.
  Place hold "the Shoulder Hall" is site within fells at 1, 1.
  Place glacier "the Shoulder glacier" is wilderness within fells at 1, 0.
  Place cellars "the glacier cellars" is level within hold.

  Place scree_road "the top of the scree road" is room within scree at 0, 0.
  Place gate_yard "the gate-yard" is room within hold at 1, 2.
  Place kennels "the wolf-pens" is room within hold at 0, 2.
  Place long_hall "the long hall" is room within hold at 1, 1.
  Place thane_seat "the high seat" is room within hold at 1, 0.
  Place hearth "the mothers' hearth" is room within hold at 0, 1.
  Place barracks "the young bloods' house" is room within hold at 2, 1.
  Place pens "the thrall-pens" is room within hold at 2, 2.
  Place midden "the midden under the pens" is room within glacier at 2, 1.
  Place glacier_foot "the glacier's foot" is room within glacier at 1, 1.
  Place ice_cellar "the ice cellar" is room within cellars at 1, 0.
  Place cage_room "the cage of ice" is room within cellars at 2, 0.
  Place stair_head "the head of the Keepers' Stair" is room within cellars at 0, 0.
  Initially Assert unlit(ice_cellar). Initially Assert unlit(cage_room). Initially Assert unlit(stair_head).

  Passage scree_climb "the last of the scree" is path between scree_road and gate_yard taking 30 minutes.
  Passage kennel_gate "the wolf-pen gate" is gate between gate_yard and kennels.
  Passage hall_doors "the hall doors" is door between gate_yard and long_hall.
  Passage seat_steps "the steps to the high seat" is steps between long_hall and thane_seat.
  Passage hearth_way "the hearth passage" is doorway between long_hall and hearth.
  Passage bloods_door "the young bloods' door" is door between gate_yard and barracks.
  Passage pens_gate "the pens gate" is gate between gate_yard and pens.
  Passage midden_chute "the midden chute" is crawl between pens and midden taking 10 minutes needing climbing or rope.
  Passage midden_path "the ice under the midden" is path between midden and glacier_foot taking 20 minutes.
  Passage glacier_track "the edge of the glacier" is track between scree_road and glacier_foot taking 1 hour.
  Passage crevasse "the blue crevasse" is tunnel between glacier_foot and ice_cellar taking 20 minutes hidden until crevasse_known.
  Passage cellar_stair "the cellar stair" is stair between ice_cellar and long_hall.
  Passage cage_way "the cold passage" is passage between ice_cellar and cage_room.
  Passage keepers_arch "the keepers' arch" is arch between ice_cellar and stair_head.

  Observe sroad_scene at scree_road when not dark() "The scree gives out under a hold of black timber and grey stone that sits on the shoulder of the fells under a glacier, like a hut under a wave. Its doors are three times the height of a man.".
  Observe sroad_night at scree_road when dark() "Above you the hold's smoke-holes glow red. Somebody up there is singing, very low; you feel it in the stones before you hear it.".
  Observe gyard_scene at gate_yard when true "A yard of trodden snow and bones. The gate-posts are whole pine trunks. A pole of grey wood stands by the hall doors, hung with a hammer the size of a child.".
  Observe hall_scene at long_hall when not dark() "A hall long enough to race horses in, smoky, roofed with whole trees. Benches you would need a ladder for run down both sides of a fire-trench.".
  Observe hall_night at long_hall when dark() "The fire-trench is down to embers. Along both walls, on the benches and under them, giants sleep in their furs like a range of low hills, breathing slow. One of them is talking in its sleep.".
  Observe seat_scene at thane_seat when true "The high seat is a block of the mountain itself, left where it stood when the hall was built round it, polished by a thousand years of sitting. It is warm.".
  Observe hearth_scene at hearth when true "A round room, warm, smelling of milk and smoke. Four great pillars hold up the roof, and every one is carved from floor to rafters in lines too small for the hands that must have cut them.".
  Observe barracks_scene at barracks when true "Sleeping platforms, war-gear, and a table scored with a map of the dale below: Saltgrave, the mine-heads, the road. Someone has driven a knife through the town.".
  Observe pens_scene at pens when not freed(aud) and not razed(scree) "Forty miners in a pen of stakes, under a roof of hides. They are cold and filthy and alive, which they did not expect.".
  Observe pens_empty at pens when freed(aud) "The pen of stakes is empty, and the hides flap.".
  Observe pens_razed at pens when razed(scree) and not freed(aud) "Do not look at the pens.".
  Observe midden_scene at midden when true "The midden spills out from under the pens onto the ice. Above you a square chute goes up into the dark; there are hand-holds in it, worn.".
  Observe foot_scene at glacier_foot when not dark() "The glacier ends here in a wall of blue ice, cracked, sweating, groaning to itself in the sun.".
  Observe foot_night at glacier_foot when dark() "The glacier ends here in a wall of ice that is faintly blue even in the dark. It ticks and groans as the cold takes hold of it.".
  Observe icecellar_scene at ice_cellar when true "A cellar cut in the glacier. The walls are blue and give back no light. Joints of meat hang from hooks. A cold passage goes off to one side; on the other, an arch of old grey stone, older than the hall, opens on a stair going down.".
  Observe stairhead_scene at stair_head when true "A stair as wide as a road goes down into the mountain in long flights, the treads worn into dips by enormous feet. The air coming up it is warm, and smells faintly of blood and salt.".

  Discovery crevasse_known "A crevasse at the glacier's foot runs back under the hold, into its ice cellar." {
    Found by searching glacier_foot "Behind a slab of fallen ice a blue crevasse runs back into the glacier, and the air in it smells of smoke and meat.".
    Known by aud.
  }

  // The giants. Nothing in the hold is scaled to the company.
  Species shoulder_giant "a giant of the Shoulder" like colossus.
  Person morrach "Thane Mórrach" at thane_seat {
    Role "thane of the Shoulder Hall". Species shoulder_giant. Level 12. Peaceable.
    State presiding "Thane Mórrach sits the high seat with his hands on his knees: grey-bearded, heavy, very still, and twice as tall as the door you came in by.".
    State deposed "Thane Mórrach sits on the floor beside the high seat with his hands bound in front of him in a ship's cable. Skarn sits the seat.".
  }
  Person skarn "Skarn" at barracks {
    Role "first of the young bloods". Species shoulder_giant. Level 9. Temperament obedient.
    Uses go, assail. Plans 6 steps.
  }
  Person bloods "the young bloods" at barracks {
    Role "young giants spoiling for a war". Species shoulder_giant. Level 7. Numbers 3. Temperament obedient.
    Uses go, assail. Plans 6 steps.
  }
  Initially Assert serves(bloods, skarn).
  Person rememberer "the Rememberer" at hearth {
    Role "the thane's mother, keeper of the song". Species shoulder_giant. Level 10. Peaceable.
    Greets "The Rememberer sits at the long hearth with her hands on her knees, as large and still as a standing stone, and the fire throws her shadow up the wall to the rafters. When she speaks the whole hall seems to lean in. 'A small one,' she says, 'who walked up the road. I have not spoken to a small one since the song was shorter.'".
    Greets again "The Rememberer has not moved, and the shadow has moved for her. 'You came back,' she says. 'It takes the small ones a very long time to come back. I counted. It was less time than I had been told it would be.'".
    Wants heart_salt.
  }
  Person wolves "the hold's wolves" at kennels {
    Role "frost wolves the size of ponies". Species frost_wolf. Numbers 2.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "Two white wolves the size of ponies get up out of the straw, without hurry, and stand between you and everything else.".
  }

  // The hostages.
  Person aud "Aud Brenning" at pens {
    Role "foreman of the Saltgrave miners". Ancestry dwarf. Calling warrior. Level 3. Peaceable.
    Greets "Aud Brenning stands at the front of the pens with his arms crossed over a barrel of a chest, between you and the miners, and does not lower them. 'Foreman,' he says. 'Forty men and nine days of short rations, and a hall that treats us like guests. I would rather be treated like prisoners. A prisoner knows where he is.'".
    Greets again "Aud Brenning moves a half-pace to one side, to let you see the men behind him, and does not pretend this is not what he is doing. 'Forty,' he says. 'Counted this morning. Counted again at noon. I do not intend to lose one by being careless of my sums.'".
  }
  Person kell "Tobias Kell" at pens {
    Role "a miner who will not meet your eye". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 2. Peaceable.
    Greets "Tobias Kell is sitting with his back to the pen rail, facing the wall, and manages to talk to you without turning his head. 'Nothing to say,' he says. 'Nothing to hear. I am a miner. I dig. Ask Brenning about anything else.'".
    Greets again "Tobias Kell has moved a hand's breadth along the rail, away from the others, and is working a splinter out of his palm with his teeth. 'You are going to ask me again,' he says. 'I will tell you I have nothing to say again, and we shall both feel the worse.'".
  }

  // The alarm. By day a stranger in the yard is challenged and has a little while to answer at the guest-pole; by
  // night the hold sleeps, and the long hall can be crept through by the light-footed.
  Relation roused(place). Relation guest(group). Relation freed(group). Relation gagged(group). Relation sawUs(group).
  Relation challenged(group). Measure answerBy(group).
  Rule seen_in_yard when at(party, gate_yard) and not dark() and not guest(party) and not roused(hold) and not challenged(party) and not sworn(morrach)
    says "A giant crossing the yard with a bucket stops, and looks down at you, and sets the bucket down. He says one word, a question, in a voice like a rockfall, and his eyes go to the pole by the hall doors and back to you." {
    Assert challenged(party). Set answerBy(party) to watch(clock) + 2.
  }
  Rule challenge_unanswered when challenged(party) and not guest(party) and not roused(hold) and watch(clock) >= answerBy(party)
    says "The giant with the bucket stops waiting. He shouts, and the hall doors bang open." { Assert roused(hold). }
  Rule seen_in_hall when (at(party, long_hall) or at(party, barracks)) and not dark() and not guest(party) and not roused(hold) and not sworn(morrach)
    says "A roar goes up from the benches, and then the sound of a great many people getting to their feet, one bench at a time, like a landslide arriving in order." { Assert roused(hold). }
  // Crossing the sleeping hall: the light-footed pass; others may not.
  Relation crept(group).
  Rule hall_wakes when at(party, long_hall) and dark() and not guest(party) and not sworn(morrach) and not capable(party, stealth) and not roused(hold) and dice(long_hall) <= 35
    says "Your boot finds a bone in the dark. It cracks like a branch. Along the wall a shape the size of a hayrick sits up, and says something, and then shouts it." { Assert roused(hold). }
  Pursuit hunt for skarn "hunting the intruders" priority 20 when roused(hold) and able(skarn) seeks assails(skarn, party).
  Pursuit hunt_with for bloods "hunting the intruders with Skarn" priority 20 when roused(hold) and able(bloods) seeks assails(bloods, party).

  // Guest-right.
  Action ask_guest_right(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the guest-pole and ask for hall-right" {
    Description "The old law of the hills: whoever asks hall-right at the pole is under the thane's roof until they leave it, and may not lift a hand there.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, gate_yard) and not guest(actor) and not roused(hold).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert guest(actor). Assert tolerates(morrach, actor). Assert tolerates(skarn, actor). Assert tolerates(bloods, actor). }
    Result "The hammer is almost too heavy to lift. The pole rings like a bell. The hall doors open, and a giant looks down at you for a long moment, and stands aside. 'Hall, and hearth, and high seat,' he says, slowly, as to children. 'Not the pens. Not the cellars. Not the young ones' house.'".
  }
  // Where a guest may not go: told when hall-right is given, and once more, the first time, by whoever sees; a guest
  // still there an hour later, or come back after that, has broken it (a curious company went down the cellar stair,
  // was hunted by Skarn and died on the first day: Mission 18's reach audit, M18-09).
  Relation guestBarred(place). Relation trespassed(group, place). Measure leaveBy(group).
  Initially Assert guestBarred(pens). Initially Assert guestBarred(ice_cellar). Initially Assert guestBarred(barracks).
  Rule trespass_warned when guest(party) and not sworn(morrach) and at(party, ?p) and guestBarred(?p) and not trespassed(party, ?p)
    says "Somewhere behind you a giant says one word, flat and heavy, the way you would speak to a dog at a gate. Guests do not come here. Be gone, and do not come back." {
    Assert trespassed(party, ?p). Set leaveBy(party) to watch(clock) + 6.
  }
  Rule guest_broken when guest(party) and not sworn(morrach) and at(party, ?p) and guestBarred(?p) and trespassed(party, ?p) and watch(clock) >= leaveBy(party)
    says "Skarn's voice, from across the yard: 'Guests. Look where the guests are.' And then, louder, to the whole hold." {
    Retract guest(party). Retract tolerates(skarn, party). Retract tolerates(bloods, party). Retract tolerates(morrach, party). Assert roused(hold).
  }

  // Kell sells whoever comes to the pens, as soon as their backs are turned, unless Aud has him held.
  Rule kell_sees when at(party, pens) and not guest(party) and not sawUs(kell) { Assert sawUs(kell). }
  Rule kell_sells when sawUs(kell) and not at(party, pens) and not gagged(kell) and not roused(hold) and not freed(aud) and not sworn(morrach)
    says "From the pens behind you a man's voice goes up, high and clear, calling for Skarn by name." { Assert roused(hold). }
  Topic aud_kell with aud "Ask Aud Brenning about the man who won't look at you" when sawUs(kell) and not gagged(kell) once {
    Says "'Tobias Kell,' says Aud, not quietly. 'He showed them where we slept. He'll be shouting before you're over the stakes.' She looks at Kell, and two of her miners get up and sit down either side of him. 'Not today, Tobias.'".
    On discuss { Assert gagged(kell). }
  }
  Topic aud_deep with aud "Ask Aud Brenning why the giants came" when true once {
    Says "'We broke into something at the bottom of the Number Four,' says Aud. 'Red salt, a whole wall of it, and warm. Warm, under a mountain. The next week they came.' She lowers her voice. 'I kept a piece back. It's in the midden under us, wrapped in my shirt. I don't know why I did that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, salt_hidden). }
  }
  Discovery salt_hidden "Aud Brenning hid a lump of the red salt from the bottom of the Number Four in the midden under the pens.".
  Kind heart_salt "a lump of red heart-salt, warm to the touch" is treasure worth 40 weighing 1.
  Item salt_lump "a shirt wrapped round something warm" is heart_salt at midden hidden until salt_hidden.

  // The Rememberer.
  Discovery song_seen "The carvings on the hearth pillars are a song in the giants' writing, and it is about something they keep.".
  Observe pillars_teach at hearth when true "Close to, the lines on the pillars are writing, tiny and endless, the same few signs over and over: a mountain, a heart, a closed eye." teaches song_seen.
  Topic rememberer_keeps with rememberer "Ask the old giantess by the hearth what she keeps" when not saltReturned(rememberer) once {
    Says "The Rememberer turns her blind face down toward your voice, from very high up. 'Small ones,' she says, in a voice like wind in a chimney. 'I keep the song. Somebody must. The young ones would rather keep a war.' Her hand, as long as you are, moves over the pillar beside her, over the tiny endless writing. 'Your miners cut deep at the bottom of their hole, and found something red, and warm. If any of it has come up into the light, bring it to me. Then I will tell you whose it is.'".
  }
  Discovery thrume_known "Thrume is not a mountain. It is a titan, sleeping, and the range is its body; the red salt is its blood. The giants of the Shoulder are its keepers, and the mine is a wound.".
  Relation saltReturned(group).
  Event salt_given near rememberer when keeps(rememberer, ?s) and itemKind(?s, heart_salt)
    "The Rememberer holds the red salt against her blind eyes, then against her cheek, as you would a sick child's forehead. 'Warm,' she says. 'He is warm. They have cut him to the blood.'" then {
    Assert saltReturned(rememberer).
  }
  Topic rememberer_truth with rememberer "Ask the Rememberer who is warm" when saltReturned(rememberer) once {
    Says "She turns her face to you and takes her hand from the pillar for the first time. 'Sit, small ones. Your Margravine thinks she is mining a mountain. There is no mountain. Thrume is the last of the old ones, and he is asleep, and the hills are the shape he sleeps in. We keep him. Your miners have cut him to the blood, and he is beginning to dream.' Her hand finds the pillar beside her. 'When he dreams, things walk. You have one in our cellar.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, thrume_known). }
  }
  Discovery song_known "The keepers' song, as the Rememberer sang it: the names of the old ones, one by one, and Thrume's last. A song is a thing remembered by the living; nothing that eats forgetting can eat it.".
  Topic rememberer_song with rememberer "Ask the Rememberer to teach you the song" when knows(actor, thrume_known) and (dreamt(actor) or knows(actor, mouth_known)) once {
    Says "She is silent while the fire settles twice. Then she leans close and breathes in, as if smelling your hair. 'You have been in his dream,' she says. 'I can smell the sky on you.' A pause. 'The song is not for small ones. But the small ones are going where we cannot.' She sings. It is long, and very low, and your teeth ache with it, and it is only names: the old ones, one by one, the hills that walked, and last of all Thrume's. When she stops, you find you can sing it back to her, every name. 'Do not lose it,' she says. 'Down there it is the one thing that cannot be eaten, while one of us remembers.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, song_known). }
  }
  Topic rememberer_cage with rememberer "Ask the Rememberer about the thing in the cellar" when knows(actor, thrume_known) once {
    Says "'The first of his dreams to walk,' she says. 'A dream of salt. We caught it in the snow below the workings, killing sheep, and the ice holds it. When he dreams harder, they will come out of the hills by dozens.' Her face turns toward the floor. 'Do not let it out. It is not wicked. It is only what he is dreaming, and he is dreaming badly.'".
  }

  // The thane: his terms, his ring, and the miners.
  Relation sworn(group).
  Topic morrach_why with morrach "Ask Thane Mórrach why he took the miners" when state(morrach, presiding) once {
    Says "The thane looks down at you for a long moment. 'Because they were cutting,' he says. His voice is very quiet for a voice that big. 'Your Margravine wants a war. My young bloods want a war. I want the cutting to stop. Forty of them in my pens and the cutting stops.' He opens one hand. 'And then she sent another down the old hole, with more men, and the cutting goes on.'".
  }
  Topic morrach_oath with morrach "Swear to Thane Mórrach that you will close the wound" when knows(actor, thrume_known) and state(morrach, presiding) and not sworn(morrach) {
    Says "The thane gets up. You had not seen him stand; it takes some time. He takes a ring from his finger, a ring of grey stone the size of a cart-wheel's hub, and puts it down on the floor in front of you. 'The keepers' ring,' he says. 'The arch in my cellar opens to it, and the stair below goes down into him, a long way down. Close the wound, small ones. Stop the cutting. And take your miners home; I have no more use for them.' Behind you, across the yard, someone throws a cup against a wall.".
    On discuss { Assert sworn(morrach). Assert guest(actor). Assert tolerates(morrach, actor). Assert tolerates(skarn, actor). Assert tolerates(bloods, actor). Assert at(thane_ring, thane_seat). Assert freed(aud). Assert at(aud, miners_row). Assert at(kell, miners_row). Retract roused(hold). }
  }
  Kind keepers_ring "the keepers' ring, a band of grey stone the size of a hub" is treasure worth 0 weighing 2.
  Item thane_ring "the keepers' ring" is keepers_ring at limbo.
  Thing keepers_door "the keepers' arch" on keepers_arch {
    State shut blocking "The arch of grey stone is closed by a slab with a round socket in it, as big as a hub, and worn smooth.".
    State open "The slab has gone down into the floor of the arch. Warm air comes up the stair beyond.".
    Change open_arch "Set the keepers' ring in the socket of the arch" from shut to open needing keepers_ring.
  }
  Observe miners_home at miners_row when freed(aud) "The twists of black wool are gone from the latches. Aud Brenning is going from door to door with a list in her hand, crossing names off.".
  Topic aud_home with aud "Ask Aud Brenning about the Number Four" when freed(aud) and at(aud, miners_row) once {
    Says "'The old adit,' she says. 'Brannoc went down it with twelve men and a quota. Below the old workings it comes out in the red, and below the red, I don't know. We never went past the warm face.' She folds the list. 'If you go down there, there's a rope ladder at the Number Four sump that goes further than we ever did. We found it there. We didn't put it there.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sump_ladder). }
  }
  Discovery sump_ladder "At the sump of the Number Four hangs a ladder that goes deeper than the miners ever went. They did not put it there." {
    Found by searching sump "Behind a fall of salt beside the sump a hole goes down, and a ladder of fine grey rope hangs into it.".
    Found by searching vein_foot "A ladder of fine grey rope hangs out of a hole in the cave roof, swaying in the warm air. It goes up toward the workings.".
  }

  // Skarn throws down the thane if the hold is roused and blood is spilled; the young bloods go to war.
  Relation razed(place). Relation coup(place).
  Rule skarn_rises when roused(hold) and (dead(bloods) or hurt(skarn)) and not coup(hold) and able(skarn)
    says "Somewhere in the hold a voice roars, and another answers it, and then the whole hall is shouting one name, and it is not the thane's." {
    Assert coup(hold). Assert state(morrach, deposed). Assert at(skarn, thane_seat).
  }
  Relation hurt(group).
  // The young bloods' clock: at dark on the second night they kill the miners and go down on Saltgrave, unless the
  // thane has given the miners up.
  Rule massacre when watch(clock) >= 216 and dark() and not freed(aud) and able(skarn) and not razed(scree)
    says "In the dark the hold wakes all at once: torches, a horn, and then from the pens a sound the wolves answer. Then the young bloods go out of the gate and down the scree road toward Saltgrave, singing." {
    Assert razed(scree). Assert at(skarn, market). Assert at(bloods, market). Increase stirring(fells) by 1.
  }
  Observe market_raided at market when razed(scree) "Half the square is burnt. The pump is a stump. A giant's footprint is pressed into the dust in front of the Salt Office, deep enough to stand in.".

  // The thing in the ice.
  Thing ice_cage "the cage of ice" at cage_room {
    State frozen "In a cage of blue ice something white turns and turns like salt poured slowly into water. It has no face, and it is looking at you.".
    State melted "A pool of meltwater, and an empty cage, and a white crust like frost all across the floor.".
    Change melt "Melt the cage of ice with fire" from frozen to melted needing flame.
  }
  Person salt_dream "the salt-dream" at limbo {
    Role "a walking dream of salt". Species salt_elemental. Level 6.
    Temperament savage.
    Comes "The white thing pours out of the broken ice and comes at you, hissing like a struck match.".
  }
  Rule dream_loose when state(ice_cage, melted) and at(salt_dream, limbo) { Assert at(salt_dream, cage_room). }

  Objective free_miners when not freed(aud) and not razed(scree) "Forty miners are held in the Shoulder Hall, and the young bloods mean to kill them on the second night.".
  Objective learn_why when knows(party, song_seen) and not knows(party, thrume_known) "The giants keep something, and their song says what.".
  Objective close_wound when sworn(morrach) and cutting(brannoc) "You swore to Thane Mórrach to stop the cutting.".
}

data/adventures/thrume/tomb.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "The Heart-Tomb: the Hollow Smiths' killing gauntlet around the heart of Thrume. Every trap is an argument for their doctrine: what wakes, kills; what kills, wakes.".

  Place tomb "the Heart-Tomb" is site within fells at 3, 1.
  Place tomb_outer "the outer tomb" is level within tomb.
  Place tomb_halls "the halls of the tomb" is level within tomb.
  Place tomb_pit "the oubliette" is level within tomb.
  Place tomb_core "the core of the tomb" is level within tomb.

  Place tomb_mouth "the foot of the long throat" is room within tomb_outer at 0, 0.
  Place salt_landing "the head of the salt stair" is room within tomb_outer at 1, 0.
  Place hammer_hall "the hall of the hammers" is room within tomb_halls at 0, 0.
  Place doctrine_hall "the Hall of Doctrine" is room within tomb_halls at 1, 0.
  Place face_room "the Sleeper's Face" is room within tomb_halls at 2, 0.
  Place door_hall "the Hall of Doors" is room within tomb_halls at 2, 1.
  Place breaths_room "the Room of Three Breaths" is room within tomb_halls at 3, 1.
  Place gearworks "the Gearworks" is room within tomb_halls at 3, 0.
  Place warder_gallery "the gallery over the Warder" is room within tomb_halls at 4, 0.
  Place oubliette "the oubliette" is room within tomb_pit at 2, 1.
  Place false_heart "the Chamber of the Heart" is room within tomb_core at 0, 0.
  Place warder_hall "the Warder's corridor" is room within tomb_core at 1, 0.
  Place locks_room "the hall of the locks" is room within tomb_core at 2, 0.
  Place heart_chamber "the Keeper's Chair" is room within tomb_core at 3, 0.
  Initially Assert unlit(tomb_mouth). Initially Assert unlit(salt_landing). Initially Assert unlit(hammer_hall).
  Initially Assert unlit(face_room). Initially Assert unlit(door_hall). Initially Assert unlit(oubliette). Initially Assert unlit(warder_hall).
  Initially Assert unlit(locks_room).

  Passage long_throat "the long throat" is tunnel between throat_head and tomb_mouth taking 2 hours needing climbing or rope.
  Passage landing_way "the outer passage" is passage between tomb_mouth and salt_landing.
  Passage salt_stair "the salt stair" is stair between salt_landing and hammer_hall.
  Passage hammer_gate "the Gate of Three Hammers" is gate between hammer_hall and doctrine_hall.
  Passage doctrine_way "the end of the painted hall" is doorway between doctrine_hall and face_room.
  Passage behind_eye "the way behind the left eye" is crawl between face_room and door_hall hidden until eye_way_known.
  Passage true_door "the door that is not there" is doorway between door_hall and breaths_room hidden until true_door_known.
  Passage pit_climb "the oubliette shaft" is shaft between oubliette and door_hall one way taking 1 hour needing climbing or rope.
  Passage breath_way "the far side of the Room of Three Breaths" is passage between breaths_room and gearworks
    opening when exhaling(fells) "Between the Room of Three Breaths and the Gearworks the salt-dust is up in a roaring white wall, drawn in toward a grating as if into a mouth. Nobody crosses it on the in-breath.".
  Passage gallery_walk "the gallery walk" is passage between gearworks and warder_gallery.
  Passage core_stair "the core stair" is stair between gearworks and false_heart taking 10 minutes.
  Passage plinth_way "the way behind the plinth" is passage between false_heart and warder_hall hidden until plinth_known.
  Passage warder_end "the end of the Warder's corridor" is passage between warder_hall and locks_room.
  Passage heart_door "the Door of Three Locks" is door between locks_room and heart_chamber.
  Passage keepers_rise "the keepers' road" is passage between heart_chamber and stair_foot taking 3 hours
    opening when sungClean(fells) or sealed(fells) "A road goes up from the Keeper's Chair, closed by a slab carved with giants' signs; it opens only to keepers.".

  // What it costs.
  Hazard unmaking "Unmade" means "Kill ally.".
  Hazard tread_fall "The false tread" means "Deal (2d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13).".
  Hazard bronze_blow "The bronze hammer's answer" means "Deal (3d6) necrotic damage to ally unless constitution save against (14).".
  Hazard lid_needle "The right lid's needle" means "Deal (1d6) poison damage to ally unless dexterity save against (13). Apply poisoned to ally for 3 turns unless constitution save against (12).".
  Hazard blades "The scything door" means "Deal (4d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (15).".
  Hazard brine_spray "The brine door" means "Deal (3d6) poison damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Hazard crushing "The falling door" means "Deal (4d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Hazard burning_salt "The burning door" means "Deal (3d6) fire damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Hazard salt_choke "The in-breath's dust" means "Deal (1d6) poison damage to ally unless constitution save against (13).".
  Hazard scald "The Gearworks' steam" means "Deal (3d6) fire damage to ally unless dexterity save against (14).".
  Hazard ceiling_fall "The roof of the false heart" means "Deal (4d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (15).".
  Hazard stays_behind "The one who stays" means "Kill ally.".

  Observe tmouth_scene at tomb_mouth when true "The long throat ends on a floor of red stone, smooth as the inside of a cheek. Ahead, a passage. Cut over it, very small, in the smiths' square hand: TURN BACK. HE IS ONLY SLEEPING.".
  Observe landing_scene at salt_landing when true "A stair of white salt goes down into the dark, each tread cut sharp and unworn. There is no footprint in the dust on the treads, not even a mouse's.".

  // 1. The salt stair: the third tread is no tread.
  Thing false_tread "the third tread of the salt stair" on salt_stair {
    State whole dangerous "The treads of the salt stair are cut sharp and white, every one alike.".
    State found "The third tread of the salt stair has fallen away on a hinge of salt into a black slot. There is room to step over it.".
    Hurts with tread_fall when whole then found.
  }
  Rule tread_shown when tried(false_tread, prodding) and state(false_tread, whole)
    says "The pole goes down on the third tread and the tread goes down with it, swinging away on a hinge of salt into a slot that goes down further than you can hear." {
    Assert state(false_tread, found).
  }

  // 2. The Gate of Three Hammers: iron wakes the sleeper; bronze wakes the dead; salt sleeps.
  Observe hammer_scene at hammer_hall when true "A gate of grey iron fills the hall's end. Three hammers hang before it on chains: one of iron, one of bronze, one of red salt. Cut over the gate: IRON WAKES THE SLEEPER. BRONZE WAKES THE DEAD. STRIKE WITH WHAT IS SLEEPING, AND PASS INSTEAD.".
  Thing gate_bar "the Gate of Three Hammers" on hammer_gate {
    State shut blocking "The grey gate is shut. It has no lock, no handle and no hinges you can see.".
    State open "The grey gate has swung inward, silent, on hinges that were not there before.".
  }
  Action strike_iron(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the gate with the iron hammer" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hammer_hall) and state(gate_bar, shut).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert strikes(unmaking, actor). Increase stirring(fells) by 1. }
    Result "The iron rings on the iron, and the ring goes on and on, down into the floor, and under your feet the whole mountain flinches. The one who swung the hammer is standing very still. Then they are not standing at all.".
  }
  Action strike_bronze(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the gate with the bronze hammer" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hammer_hall) and state(gate_bar, shut).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert strikes(bronze_blow, actor). Increase stirring(fells) by 1. }
    Result "The bronze booms. Something cold comes up out of the floor like water out of a sponge, and through whoever is nearest, and away.".
  }
  Action strike_salt(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the gate with the hammer of salt" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hammer_hall) and state(gate_bar, shut).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert state(gate_bar, open). }
    Result "The salt hammer makes no sound at all against the iron. It crumbles in your hand to red dust. The gate swings open.".
  }

  // 3. The Hall of Doctrine: it teaches, and it lies once, at the Smith-Master's order.
  Observe doctrine_scene at doctrine_hall when true "A long gallery, painted from floor to vault in colours a thousand years old. Panel after panel shows the smiths at their work in this tomb, as a lesson: a smith prodding a stair with a pole; a smith with a red hammer at a gate; a smith creeping past a great face by its left eye; a smith searching a wall between painted doors; a smith crossing a dusty room while a giant breathes out; three wheels, with a smith setting them. The last panel shows a smith kneeling to a figure in a crown, saying words.".
  Discovery panels_read "The Hall of Doctrine's last panels, read close: the wheels of the Gearworks set iron at rest, salt at rest, bone awake; and, under the kneeling smith, the doctrine, which the crowned figure answers.".
  Observe panels_teach at doctrine_hall when true "Close to, the panel of the wheels has words painted under each: IRON, REST. SALT, REST. BONE, WAKE. Under the kneeling smith: WHAT WAKES, KILLS." teaches panels_read.

  // 4. The Sleeper's Face: never go where he is awake.
  Observe sface_scene at face_room when true "The end of the hall is a face. A titan's face, cut in red stone, as tall as a house: eyes closed, mouth open. The mouth is perfectly black. Nothing in it reflects your light. It makes no sound, and the air does not move in it.".
  Action enter_mouth(actor: group, site: place) "Walk into the Sleeper's open mouth" {
    Description "It is wide enough for a cart. Beyond it there is only black.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, face_room).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert strikes(unmaking, actor). }
    Result "The first of you steps into the black, and is not anywhere. No sound. No sign. The black is just as it was.".
  }
  Thing left_lid "the Sleeper's left eyelid" at face_room {
    State lidded "The left eyelid of the face, on your left as you face it, is a slab of red stone as big as a door.".
    State pressed "The left eyelid has sunk into the stone, and behind it a low way runs back into the dark.".
    Tries pushing.
  }
  Thing right_lid "the Sleeper's right eyelid" at face_room {
    State lidded "The right eyelid of the face is a slab of red stone as big as a door, with a crack at its edge.".
    State sprung "A needle as long as a finger stands out of the crack at the right eyelid's edge.".
    Tries pushing.
  }
  Discovery eye_way_known "Behind the Sleeper's left eyelid, a low way runs on into the dark.".
  Observe eye_opens at face_room when state(left_lid, pressed) "Where the left eyelid was, a low way runs back into the dark." teaches eye_way_known.
  Rule left_gives when tried(left_lid, pushing) and state(left_lid, lidded)
    says "The left eyelid sinks under your hands with a sigh of air, like a sleeper's breath, and the stone behind it slides away." {
    Assert state(left_lid, pressed).
  }
  Rule right_bites when tried(right_lid, pushing) and state(right_lid, lidded)
    says "Something in the crack at the right lid's edge goes snick." {
    Assert state(right_lid, sprung). Assert strikes(lid_needle, party).
  }

  // 5. The Hall of Doors: every door you can see is a death; the door is the one that is not there.
  Observe doors_scene at door_hall when true "A long hall with six doors along its walls, three to a side, each of a different wood, each with a different handle: bone, bronze, iron, salt, glass, horn. The end wall is bare red stone.".
  Thing door_bone "the door with the bone handle" at door_hall { State shut "A door of pale ash with a handle of bone.". State open "The ash door hangs open on a blank wall.". Change open_bone "Open the door with the bone handle" from shut to open. }
  Thing door_bronze "the door with the bronze handle" at door_hall { State shut "A door of oak with a handle of bronze.". State open "The oak door hangs open on a blank wall, scored with blade-marks.". Change open_bronze "Open the door with the bronze handle" from shut to open. }
  Thing door_iron "the door with the iron handle" at door_hall { State shut "A door of black yew with a handle of iron.". State open "The yew door hangs open on nothing; the floor beyond it was never there.". Change open_iron "Open the door with the iron handle" from shut to open. }
  Thing door_salt "the door with the salt handle" at door_hall { State shut "A door of pine with a handle of white salt.". State open "The pine door hangs open on a wall of crumbled salt.". Change open_salt "Open the door with the salt handle" from shut to open. }
  Thing door_glass "the door with the glass handle" at door_hall { State shut "A door of pear-wood with a handle of glass.". State open "The pear-wood door hangs open on a blackened wall.". Change open_glass "Open the door with the glass handle" from shut to open. }
  Thing door_horn "the door with the horn handle" at door_hall { State shut "A door of elm with a handle of horn.". State open "The elm door hangs open on a slab of fallen stone.". Change open_horn "Open the door with the horn handle" from shut to open. }
  Relation sprungDoor(entity).
  Rule bone_door when state(door_bone, open) and not sprungDoor(door_bone) says "Behind the ash door is a wall, and the wall breathes out a fine white salt that burns the eyes and throat." { Assert sprungDoor(door_bone). Assert strikes(brine_spray, party). }
  Rule bronze_door when state(door_bronze, open) and not sprungDoor(door_bronze) says "The oak door opens on a wall, and out of a slot in the wall a blade the length of a man comes round at waist height." { Assert sprungDoor(door_bronze). Assert strikes(blades, party). }
  Rule iron_door when state(door_iron, open) and not sprungDoor(door_iron) says "The yew door swings outward and the floor under you swings with it, down." { Assert sprungDoor(door_iron). Assert at(party, oubliette). }
  Rule salt_door when state(door_salt, open) and not sprungDoor(door_salt) says "The salt handle crumbles. So does the wall behind the door, and the roof above it, all at once." { Assert sprungDoor(door_salt). Assert strikes(crushing, party). }
  Rule glass_door when state(door_glass, open) and not sprungDoor(door_glass) says "Behind the pear-wood door the air catches fire." { Assert sprungDoor(door_glass). Assert strikes(burning_salt, party). }
  Rule horn_door when state(door_horn, open) and not sprungDoor(door_horn) says "The elm door opens and the slab above it, which you had not noticed, comes down." { Assert sprungDoor(door_horn). Assert strikes(crushing, party). Increase stirring(fells) by 1. }
  Discovery true_door_known "In the bare end wall of the Hall of Doors, a door with no frame and no handle, cut so fine its edges are a hair." {
    Found by searching door_hall "You go over the bare end wall a hand's breadth at a time. Low down, a hair-fine line; then another, upright; then the shape of a door with no frame and no handle, which swings when you lean on it.".
  }
  Discovery iron_drop_known "Behind the door with the iron handle, the floor of the Hall of Doors swings down into a pit.".
  Observe iron_drop_seen at door_hall when state(door_iron, open) "Beyond the yew door the floor hangs down on a hinge over a black drop." teaches iron_drop_known.
  Passage iron_drop "the drop behind the yew door" is shaft between door_hall and oubliette one way hidden until iron_drop_known.
  Observe oubliette_scene at oubliette when true "A round pit of red stone, smooth, very deep. Far above, a square of less dark. On the floor, the bones of three people who were not patient, and scratched on the wall by one who was: THE SHAFT HAS HOLDS. FEEL FOR THEM.".

  // 6. The Room of Three Breaths: out is open.
  Observe breaths_scene at breaths_room when exhaling(fells) "A long room of red stone. A warm wind blows gently from a grating in the far wall, and the floor is drifted with salt-dust like snow, rippled. The far door stands clear.".
  Observe breaths_in at breaths_room when not exhaling(fells) "The wind in the long room has turned, and the salt-dust is up off the floor in a roaring white wall, pouring toward the grating in the far wall. You cannot see your hand.".
  Rule dust_chokes when at(party, breaths_room) and not exhaling(fells)
    says "The salt-dust is in your mouth, your nose, your eyes." { Assert strikes(salt_choke, party). }

  // 7. The Gearworks: iron at rest, salt awake, bone at rest. The painted panel lies.
  Observe gear_scene at gearworks when true "A chamber full of machinery: three great wheels standing on their edges, one of iron, one of red salt, one of bone, each as tall as a mill-wheel and each marked round its rim REST and WAKE. A lever as long as a spear stands up out of the floor. A stair goes down beyond a grating; a gallery goes off along the wall.".
  Thing iron_wheel "the iron wheel" at gearworks {
    State awake "The iron wheel stands with WAKE uppermost.". State rest "The iron wheel stands with REST uppermost.".
    Change iron_rest "Turn the iron wheel to REST" from awake to rest. Change iron_wake "Turn the iron wheel to WAKE" from rest to awake.
  }
  Thing salt_wheel "the salt wheel" at gearworks {
    State rest "The salt wheel stands with REST uppermost.". State awake "The salt wheel stands with WAKE uppermost.".
    Change salt_rest "Turn the salt wheel to REST" from awake to rest. Change salt_wake "Turn the salt wheel to WAKE" from rest to awake.
  }
  Thing bone_wheel "the bone wheel" at gearworks {
    State awake "The bone wheel stands with WAKE uppermost.". State rest "The bone wheel stands with REST uppermost.".
    Change bone_rest "Turn the bone wheel to REST" from awake to rest. Change bone_wake "Turn the bone wheel to WAKE" from rest to awake.
  }
  Thing great_lever "the great lever" at gearworks {
    State up "The great lever stands upright.". State down "The great lever is thrown down.".
    Change throw "Throw the great lever" from up to down.
  }
  Thing core_grating "the grating over the core stair" on core_stair {
    State shut blocking "A grating of grey iron closes the stair going down.".
    State open "The grating over the core stair stands open.".
  }
  Rule gears_right when state(great_lever, down) and state(iron_wheel, rest) and state(salt_wheel, awake) and state(bone_wheel, rest) and state(core_grating, shut)
    says "Somewhere in the walls a long chain runs, and the grating over the stair rises into the roof." { Assert state(core_grating, open). }
  Rule gears_wrong when state(great_lever, down) and state(core_grating, shut) and not (state(iron_wheel, rest) and state(salt_wheel, awake) and state(bone_wheel, rest))
    says "The lever goes down, and the wheels shudder, and every joint in the machinery blows white steam at once." { Assert strikes(scald, party). Assert state(great_lever, up). Increase stirring(fells) by 1. }

  // 8. The Warder: kills what moves while it is wound; it can be unwound only from the gallery above.
  Observe wgallery_scene at warder_gallery when true "A narrow gallery high in the wall over a long corridor. Below, a figure of grey iron stands in the middle of the corridor. Beside you, in the gallery wall, a great key is set in a spring-case, like a clock's.".
  Thing warder_spring "the Warder's spring" at warder_gallery {
    State wound "The great key stands in its spring-case, the spring tight.".
    State unwound "The great key has been turned back; the spring lies slack in its case.".
    Change unwind "Turn the great key back and let the Warder's spring run down" from wound to unwound needing brawn or lockwork.
  }
  Person warder "the Warder" at warder_hall {
    Role "a figure of grey iron, twice a man's height, with blades for hands". Species automaton. Level 14. Temperament obedient.
    Comes "The Warder moves. It is very fast for something so heavy.".
  }
  Rule warder_strikes when at(party, warder_hall) and state(warder_spring, wound) and able(warder) { Assert assails(warder, party). }
  Observe warder_still at warder_hall when state(warder_spring, unwound) "The Warder stands in the middle of the corridor with its blade-hands at its sides, run down, like a clock nobody wound.".

  // 9. The false heart, and the last of the Hollow Smiths.
  Observe fheart_scene at false_heart when not state(decoy, taken) "A chamber like the inside of a crown. On a plinth in the middle, a heart of red crystal as big as a cart, glowing, beating slowly, beautifully. Before it stands a tall figure in a smith's leather apron gone black with age, with a crown of iron on its skull, quite still.".
  Thing decoy "the great red heart" at false_heart {
    State resting "The heart of red crystal glows on its plinth.".
    State taken "The plinth is bare and cracked. Red crystal lies in shards across the floor.".
    Change pry "Prise the great red heart from its plinth" from resting to taken needing brawn.
  }
  Person ardath "the crowned figure" at false_heart {
    Role "a tall figure in a smith's apron, crowned with iron". Species lich. Level 13. Peaceable.
    State keeping "The crowned figure stands before the heart with its hands folded on a smith's hammer. It watches you with nothing in its eye-sockets.".
  }
  Rule ardath_rises when state(decoy, taken) and not hostile(ardath, party)
    says "The roof of the chamber comes down in red slabs. Through the dust the crowned figure lifts its hammer, and its voice is a forge-bellows: 'THIEF.'" {
    Assert strikes(ceiling_fall, party). Assert hostile(ardath, party). Assert assails(ardath, party). Increase stirring(fells) by 1.
  }
  Discovery plinth_known "Behind the plinth of the false heart, a way goes on, for those the crowned figure lets pass.".
  Topic ardath_doctrine with ardath "Say the doctrine of the Hollow Smiths to the crowned figure" when knows(actor, doctrine_known) and not hostile(ardath, actor) once {
    Says "'What wakes, kills,' you say. The crowned figure answers, in a voice like old iron: 'What kills, wakes.' Its jaw works on nothing. 'You are not ours. But you have our words.' It turns, and lays a hand on the plinth. 'This is a lie. I keep it so that thieves stop here. I have kept it since the roof was new, and I do not remember who told me to.' The plinth slides aside. 'The true heart is beyond. He is sleeping. Do not wake him. Do not kill him.' Its hand stays on the plinth. 'I was paid to kill him, once. We all were. Tell him I am sorry.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, plinth_known). }
  }

  // 10. The Door of Three Locks: the keepers' ring, the Smith-Master's hammer, the Abbess's Eye.
  Observe locks_scene at locks_room when true "A door of red stone, round, like a great closed eye. In it, three sockets: a round one the size of a hub; a narrow one the shape of a little hammer's head; and a broad shallow one, lid-shaped.".
  Thing ring_lock "the round socket" on heart_door {
    State empty blocking "The round socket in the door is empty.". State filled "The keepers' ring sits in the round socket.".
    Change set_ring "Set the keepers' ring in the round socket" from empty to filled needing keepers_ring.
  }
  Thing token_lock "the narrow socket" on heart_door {
    State empty blocking "The narrow socket is empty.". State filled "The Smith-Master's hammer sits in the narrow socket.".
    Change set_token "Set the Smith-Master's hammer in the narrow socket" from empty to filled needing smith_token.
  }
  Thing eye_lock "the lid-shaped socket" on heart_door {
    State empty blocking "The lid-shaped socket is empty.". State filled "The Abbess's Eye lies in the lid-shaped socket, and is open.".
    Change set_eye "Lay the Abbess's Eye in the lid-shaped socket" from empty to filled needing abbess_eye.
  }

  // 11. The Keeper's Chair.
  Observe chair_scene at heart_chamber when true "A small chamber, plain, round, warm. In the floor, in a basin of grey stone, the heart of Thrume: not crystal, flesh, dark red, the size of a cottage, beating once in a long while. The whole room moves with it. Beside the basin, a chair of grey stone, carved with the giants' signs, empty.".
  Relation seated(group).
  Passage into_dream "the dream beyond the Chair" is passage between heart_chamber and cloud_landing taking 1 hour
    opening when seated(party) "The Chair is empty. Whoever sits in it, the keepers say, sits in his dream.".
  Action sit_chair(actor: group, site: place) "Sit in the Keeper's Chair, and go into his dream" {
    Description "The stone is warm. The giants' signs on it are the same three, over and over: a mountain, a heart, a closed eye.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart_chamber) and not seated(actor) and not woken(fells).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert seated(actor). }
    Result "You sit. The heart beats, once, and the room goes away. You are standing on a cloud, and the cloud holds you, and above you a palace of white stone floats in a sky so close you could touch it.".
  }
  Action stay_keeper(actor: group, site: place) "One of you stays in the Chair, and keeps him sleeping" {
    Description "The keepers say someone must sit by the heart and sing, for ever, or he will stir again. Nobody who stays comes back.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart_chamber) and not sealed(fells) and not woken(fells) and not sungClean(fells).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert sealed(fells). Assert strikes(stays_behind, actor). Set stirring(fells) to 0. }
    Result "One of you sits down in the Chair, and puts a hand on the warm stone of the basin, and begins, very low, to hum. The heart slows. When the rest of you go, the one in the Chair does not look up.".
  }
  Action cut_heart(actor: group, site: place) "Cut into the heart of Thrume for the Margravine's salt" {
    Description "The heart is blood, and the blood is the red salt, and there is more of it here than in all the workings. Ebb would win its war.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart_chamber) and capable(actor, digging) and not cutOut(fells) and not woken(fells).
    Time 12.
    On success { Assert cutOut(fells). Set stirring(fells) to 0. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 400. }
    Result "It takes the rest of the day. The heart does not wake. It beats slower, and slower, and the red that comes out of it goes hard and glittering in the air as it runs, and you fill sack after sack. At the end it beats once more, and then it does not, and the whole mountain is very still, and very cold.".
  }
  Action wake_heart(actor: group, site: place) "Strike the heart of Thrume, and wake him" {
    Description "What kills, wakes.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heart_chamber) and not woken(fells).
    Time 1.
    On success { Set stirring(fells) to 10. }
    Result "You strike. The heart stops. Then it beats, once, so hard you are thrown off your feet, and again, and again, faster, and the floor tilts, and does not tilt back.".
  }

  Objective cross_tomb when at(party, tomb_mouth) and not seated(party) "The heart of Thrume lies at the bottom of the Hollow Smiths' tomb.".
}

data/adventures/thrume/voices.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "What each of the company makes of the country, by what they are: the ranger on the snow of the hold-yard, the cleric among the sleepers and over the Smith-Master's bones, the warrior in a hall that was never built for war.".

  // The preset party is not a set of declared people, so it has no Remarks of its own. What a rule can ask of a member is
  // their calling, and print their name (doc/imbar/11-technical-report.md, 11.6). Each is said once, by whoever the
  // company has of the calling; a company without one has nobody to notice, and must notice it itself.
  Relation heardTracks(group). Relation heardBreath(group). Relation heardWalls(group). Relation heardPulse(group).
  Relation heardTongs(group). Relation heardBones(group). Relation heardMeadow(group). Relation heardInn(group).
  Relation heardPegs(group). Relation heardDial(group). Relation heardStreet(group). Relation heardNiches(group). Relation heardHammers(group).
  Relation quarrelPaid(group).

  // Act II: the Shoulder. The ranger reads the ground the giants left.
  Rule voice_tracks at gate_yard when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and awake(?m) and at(party, gate_yard) and not heardTracks(party)
    says "{?m} crouches at the edge of the trodden snow and lays two fingers in a print the size of a bread-board. 'Forty men went up this road,' {?m} says. 'Walking. Not one dragged.' The big prints beside them are slow and wide, set down like feet carrying a full bowl. Further on {?m} lifts a bone out of the snow, meat still on it, split down the middle to be shared. 'Nobody feeds hostages off their own plate,' {?m} says, and puts it back where it lay. 'Whatever these people are, they did not think they were stealing.'" {
    Assert heardTracks(party).
  }
  Rule voice_walls at long_hall when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_warrior) and awake(?m) and at(party, long_hall) and not heardWalls(party)
    says "{?m} walks the length of the hall with a hand on the nearest bench, which is level with {?m}'s chin, and counts the doors. There is one. 'No wall-walk. No loft for a bowman, no bar to drop.' {?m} kicks a roof-post, which does not notice. 'I have held halls and I have taken them, and you build a hall for the day you lose it. This was built to sit in, by people who never once expected company they did not want.' {?m} lowers the voice without knowing it. 'Whatever they want of the Margravine, it is not a fight they planned.'" {
    Assert heardWalls(party).
  }

  // Act I: the Red Lantern. The cleric among the sleepers.
  Rule voice_breath at smoke_room when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, smoke_room) and not heardBreath(party)
    says "{?m} kneels by the nearest pallet, a hand light on a sleeper's chest and two fingers on the wrist, and says the short form for a bedside before saying anything else. 'A sleeper's breath wanders,' {?m} says. 'These do not. Every one is breathing in the same time, six hours in and six out, if I have it right, and I cannot have it right, because nobody breathes so.' {?m} takes the hand away and does not stand at once. 'I would very much like to know whose breath they are keeping.'" {
    Assert heardBreath(party).
  }

  // Act III: the inward roads. The cleric at the Wound; the warrior at the cold forge; the thief at the shut Lantern.
  Rule voice_pulse at red_gallery when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, red_gallery) and not heardPulse(party)
    says "{?m} stops in the middle of the gallery with a hand flat to the red crystal and a face gone quite still. 'That is the beat I counted in the Lantern,' {?m} says. 'The same, to the breath.' The hand comes away slowly. 'I have sat by a great many wounds. I did not expect to be standing in one.'" {
    Assert heardPulse(party).
  }
  Rule voice_tongs at cold_forge when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_warrior) and awake(?m) and at(party, cold_forge) and not heardTongs(party)
    says "{?m} takes down the nearest hammer, turns it in the torchlight and puts a thumb to the face. 'Worn on the heel, not the face. Whoever swung this flinched at the top of every stroke, for years, and kept swinging.' {?m} hangs it back on its peg and wipes the hand on a coat, though the hand is clean. 'That is how you wear a hammer when you are paid to do a thing you are sorry for. Smiths. Not soldiers.'" {
    Assert heardTongs(party).
  }
  Rule voice_bones at master_cell when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, master_cell) and not heardBones(party)
    says "{?m} stands in the doorway of the cell a good while before coming in, and says under the breath the form for entering a room where someone sleeps. 'He died sitting up,' {?m} says. 'Hands folded on a hammer, back to the wall, facing the door. That is how a man waits.' {?m} looks at the bare floor, the unscorched shelf, the cot never slept in. 'And nobody has said a word over him. There is an office for the unpaid, and one for the unburied, and a short one for the dead who are still on duty.' A pause. 'I know the third by heart. It is very short.'" {
    Assert heardBones(party).
  }
  Rule voice_pegs at wage_hall when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, wage_hall) and not heardPegs(party)
    says "{?m} runs a finger down the pegs, lips moving, and counts again from the other end, because the sum was not the one wanted. 'A hundred and eight pegs,' {?m} says, 'and a hundred and seven names. One peg with no name and no hammer, and swept clean.' The finger taps it. 'That is the peg for the man who is paid and is not on the roll. Every house has one. It is always the best-kept thing in the house.'" {
    Assert heardPegs(party).
  }

  // Act IV: the Hush and the Tomb. The ranger in the Street of Hands, the cleric at the Thrall-Market, the warrior among the hammers.
  Rule voice_street at hand_street when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and awake(?m) and at(party, hand_street) and not heardStreet(party)
    says "{?m} looks down before looking along the street. There is dust on the grey stone and nobody has left a print in it: the Court's feet do not touch it, or do not weigh. The only tracks are small, round and shallow, always at a Court-walker's heel, and they stop at every doorway and begin again on the far side. 'Thralls walk where they are walked,' {?m} says. 'Not one has turned left on his own.'" {
    Assert heardStreet(party).
  }
  Rule voice_niches at thrall_market when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, thrall_market) and not heardNiches(party)
    says "{?m} goes along the niches with a thumb on one eyelid after another and does not find what was looked for. 'Not sick,' {?m} says. 'Not dying.' The thumb comes away from the last lid as if burned. 'They are being drunk, a sip at a time, and fed so that there will be more. I have sat with the dying and I know what is asked of them. This is the other thing, and there is no office for it.'" {
    Assert heardNiches(party).
  }
  Rule voice_hammers at hammer_hall when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_warrior) and awake(?m) and at(party, hammer_hall) and not heardHammers(party)
    says "{?m} stops under the first of the hammers and measures the swing of it with an arm held out, then the height of the door. 'Door cut to a man's shoulders, not an inch to spare,' {?m} says. 'Hammers hung where one man can reach them, and only one man at a time.' A grunt. 'Whoever built this knew how big the visitor would be, and that it would come alone. I do not like being expected.'" {
    Assert heardHammers(party).
  }

  // Act V: the Dream. The ranger in a meadow with no shadows.
  Rule voice_meadow at dream_field when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and awake(?m) and at(party, dream_field) and not heardMeadow(party)
    says "{?m} stands in the middle of the grass, turning slowly. 'No wind,' {?m} says. 'The grass leans anyway.' {?m} crouches. 'No shadow under a single sheep. Every blade has a different light on it, each from a different afternoon.' A hand goes to a stem, and stops short of it. 'Not made. Kept. I would sooner take nothing out of here.'" {
    Assert heardMeadow(party).
  }

  // Act I: any company with a bard has an ear for the inn; any with a mage, for the dial.
  Rule voice_inn at inn_room when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, inn_room) and not heardInn(party)
    says "{?m} listens to the room for a minute with eyes half shut, the way one listens to a lute being tuned. 'Forty miners and not a word about the giants,' {?m} says. 'Hear it? Sleep. The man by the door, the pair at the fire, the boy with the pot. Every table has the same song, and not one of them knows he is singing it.'" {
    Assert heardInn(party).
  }
  Rule voice_dial at gauge_room when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_mage) and awake(?m) and at(party, gauge_room) and not heardDial(party)
    says "{?m} puts a palm an inch from the brass of the dial and takes it away quickly. 'I would say this is not a machine,' {?m} says, 'though I would not swear to it. There is a working in it, and the working has a tide. Whatever it measures is alive, and a long way off, and the needle is going the wrong way.' A glance at the glass tube. 'One tick, in the time I have stood here. I should like to be wrong.'" {
    Assert heardDial(party).
  }

  // A disagreement the company has with itself, in the Paymasters' hall: only a company with both a warrior and a cleric
  // has it, and each is right. One answer closes the other (wages.kyr).
  Rule quarrel_over_wage at wage_hall when memberOf(?w, party) and hasCalling(?w, calling_warrior) and awake(?w)
    and memberOf(?c, party) and hasCalling(?c, calling_cleric) and awake(?c) and at(party, wage_hall) and knows(party, gods_wage) and not paidSettled(paid) and not paidLaid(paid) and not quarrelPaid(party)
    says "{?w} says it first, because somebody must. 'It is a wage, owed, and it was never paid. Pay it. They are only standing here to be paid, and twelve crowns is cheap against a fight in a room with no back door.' {?c} does not raise a voice. 'A thousand years of wages is not paid in crowns,' says {?c}. 'It is read out. Every name, over the roll, in the office for those who died at their work. It takes the afternoon, and it is the only thing that has ever closed an account like this.' Neither looks at you. Both are waiting for you to say whose way it is." {
    Assert quarrelPaid(party).
  }
}

data/adventures/thrume/wages.kyr:
Module thrume "Thrume" {
  Description "The Paymasters' hall: a low room off the cold forge where the Hollow Smiths drew their wages from the young gods, and where two of them are standing in line still.".

  // ── The first page of the account ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Hollow Smiths were paid by the young gods to kill the titans. They were to be paid daily, in starmetal, and the
  // last day's wage on the day the hill was down. The hill is not down; it is asleep. The last day's wage has stood on
  // the counter ever since. Nobody has been owed it, and nobody has been paid, and two of them have not gone home.
  Place wage_hall "the Paymasters' hall" is room within delving at 0, 1.
  Initially Assert unlit(wage_hall).
  Passage tally_door "the tally door" is door between cold_forge and wage_hall.

  Observe wage_scene at wage_hall when true "A low room, cold, long as a barracks, with a pay-window at the far end: a slot in a wall of grey stone, a counter, and on the counter a row of wooden trays. In the trays lie bars of dull pale metal, seven to a tray, each stamped with a star, light as cork to look at. Along the wall a hundred and eight pegs, and on each peg a hammer, and under each hammer a name scratched in the stone. Over the window, a tallow dip burns a finger high, steady in dead air. It is the only flame under the mountain that nobody lit.".
  Observe wage_lintel at wage_hall when true "Cut over the window, in the square hand of the delving, in letters that have been gone over with a knife many times: YSOLT FENN, PAYMASTER, MADE THIS WINDOW AND WAS PAID BY IT. Someone, long after, has added in a rougher hand: SHE WAS NOT.".
  Observe wage_dip at wage_hall when true "The tallow dip over the window has not burned down. Beside it on the sill is a flint, a snuffer, and a scrap of leaf with one word on it, written seven times down the page: stay.".

  Discovery gods_wage "The Hollow Smiths' contract with the Young Court of the Sky: a hundred and eight hands, paid daily in starmetal, seven bars a day, and the last day's wage on the day the hill was down. The hill was never brought down; the last wage stands in the trays at the pay-window, kept and not owed, and has stood there a thousand years." {
    Source wage_roll "the pay-roll of the delving" at wage_hall readable by party.
  }

  Kind thrume_starbar "a bar of starmetal, dull and pale, light as cork" is treasure worth 30 weighing 1 described "A bar of metal fallen from the sky, stamped with a small star. It is the last day's wage of a Hollow Smith, laid out a thousand years and never handed over.".
  Item star_bar "a bar of starmetal from the tray" is thrume_starbar at wage_hall hidden until gods_wage.

  // ── The Paid ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Species thrume_paid "one of the Paid" like revenant temperament territorial described "A Hollow Smith in a leather apron gone to black leather, hands like tongs, who has stood at the window waiting to be handed what he is owed, and will not have anyone else take it.".
  Relation paidSettled(group). Relation paidLaid(group). Relation ringsOut(place).
  Person paid "the Paid" at wage_hall {
    Role "two Hollow Smiths, standing in line at the pay-window since the day the hill did not fall". Species thrume_paid. Level 3. Numbers 2.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "Two men in leather aprons stand in line at the window with their backs to you. They do not turn. One by one the hammers on the pegs beside them lift a hand's breadth off the wall and settle again, the way a man settles his feet before a blow.".
    Comes "The nearest of the two turns at last. His face is a smith's face, grey, and patient, and quite without a quarrel. 'Not on the roll,' he says, and the hammer comes down off its peg.".
    Pleads "The two put down their hammers, side by side, and go back to the window, and stand.".
  }

  // They are not hasty. A smith at a pay-window has all the day, and the company has an hour to say its business before
  // the line decides it is not on the roll (the shared rules give a warned company one watch; a pay-roll to be read
  // and a quarrel to be settled want more).
  Relation paidWaited(group).
  Rule paid_give_an_hour when warned(paid, party) and not paidWaited(paid) {
    Assert paidWaited(paid). Set patience(paid) to watch(clock) + 6.
  }

  // What the Paid do to the mountain when they are broken: what wakes, kills; what kills, wakes. A fight in the Delving
  // rings along the iron of it, and Thrume feels every blow.
  Rule paid_ring when dead(paid) and not ringsOut(delving)
    says "The last of the Paid falls against the counter, and the sound goes out of the room along the iron of the delving and the stone of the stair, and does not stop. Somewhere above, very far, the needle of the Gauge ticks toward WAKING." {
    Assert ringsOut(delving). Increase stirring(fells) by 1.
  }

  // ── Four ways round ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // They are paid; they are shown the Master's hammer; they are given the last day's wage out of the tray; or the
  // office for the dead at their work is said over them, by someone with the form. The first three let them stand; only
  // the fourth lets them go, and only the fourth teaches the names (the Mouth).
  Action pay_the_paid(actor: group, site: place) "Pay the Paid their last day's wage in crowns at the window" {
    Description "Twelve crowns, counted into the slot. It is not what they are owed; it is what a stranger has.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wage_hall) and at(paid, wage_hall) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 12 and not paidSettled(paid) and not paidLaid(paid) and not dead(paid).
    Time 2.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 12. Assert paidSettled(paid). Assert tolerates(paid, actor). }
    Result "You count the coin into the slot one crown at a time, aloud, and the taller of the two bends his head to listen to it as to a clock. At twelve he straightens. He counts it again with his lips. 'Short,' he says, with no quarrel in it, the way a carter says a load is short. 'Short, and in a coin I do not know. It will do for tonight.' He takes his hammer from the wall and hangs it back on its peg, and they stand again at the window with their backs to you, and are only men in a queue.".
  }
  Action hand_over_bars(actor: group, site: place) "Hand the Paid the bars from the tray, which are their own last wage" {
    Description "It was laid out for them a thousand years ago and has not been touched.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wage_hall) and at(paid, wage_hall) and holding(actor, thrume_starbar) and not paidSettled(paid) and not paidLaid(paid) and not dead(paid).
    Time 2.
    On success { Spend thrume_starbar from actor. Assert paidSettled(paid). Assert tolerates(paid, actor). }
    Result "You put the bar into the taller one's hand. His fingers close on it, and he stands for some time looking at the star on its face. 'Seven a day,' he says. 'This is one.' Then, almost kindly: 'The rest is on the counter. It was always on the counter. I could not take it; it was not mine to take until it was handed to me.' He does not thank you. He goes back to the window with the bar held in both hands like a candle.".
  }
  Action show_master_hammer(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Paid the Smith-Master's little hammer" {
    Description "A man who has waited for a thousand years for his master's word will stand for his master's hammer.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wage_hall) and at(paid, wage_hall) and holding(actor, smith_token) and not paidSettled(paid) and not paidLaid(paid) and not dead(paid).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert tolerates(paid, actor). Assert paidSettled(paid). }
    Result "The two turn, and look at the grey iron hammer no longer than your hand, and the line comes to attention as one man. The taller touches his brow. 'Master,' he says, to whoever is holding it, and the word has no surprise in it at all. 'We kept the window. We were not told to stop.' You put the hammer away. It is some time before they turn back to the wall, and when they do their shoulders are lower than they were.".
  }
  Action read_the_office(actor: group, site: place, c: member) "Say the office for the dead at their work over the Paid, and read them out of the roll" {
    Grave "It will take the rest of the afternoon, every name must be said aloud, and two men will go.".
    Description "{c} knows the form: the office for those who died at their work and are still on duty.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wage_hall) and at(paid, wage_hall) and memberOf(c, actor) and hasCalling(c, calling_cleric) and awake(c) and knows(actor, gods_wage) and not paidSettled(paid) and not paidLaid(paid) and not dead(paid).
    Time 18.
    On success { Assert paidLaid(paid). Retract at(paid, wage_hall). Assert at(paid, limbo). Assert knows(actor, smith_names). }
    Result "{c} takes the roll from the counter and reads it out. Not the contract: the names. A hundred and seven, one after the other, in the plain voice of someone who has said the office over a good many beds and never once for so many. At each name the taller of the Paid says, quietly, 'Here,' and then, after a while, 'Paid.' At the hundred and seventh the line is thin, the hammers are still on their pegs, and the tallow dip over the window gutters, which it has not done since it was lit. {c} does not read the hundred and eighth. There is no name against it; {c} puts a hand on the empty peg instead, and says nothing. When you look up, the window is empty, and the dip is burning again, and the bars lie in their trays, and nobody is waiting for them.".
  }
  Discovery smith_names "The names of the Hollow Smiths of the delving, a hundred and seven of them, read out in full over the roll; and a hundred and eighth peg with no name against it.".
  Observe wage_empty at wage_hall when paidLaid(paid) "The window is empty. The hammers hang on their pegs under their names. The dip burns on the sill. It is quite a warm room, now.".

  // The Paid are not a trap; they are a debt. A company that has been round the whole delving can know where the wage
  // is, and what they are, before it opens the door.
  Observe tally_hint at cold_forge when carries(party, smith_token) "From a door in the wall of the forge, a draught that smells of tallow, and, very faintly, of a queue.".
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/afterm:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── After the Settlement ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // In a world that goes on (a generated world holding Tessary as one country among others), the city is still there
  // after its story ends, and shows what became of it.
  Query homecoming() means matured(ossel) and (discharged(ossel) or saultWarden(ossel) and saultHoldsNote(ossel)).
  Query factorRules() means matured(ossel) and saultHoldsNote(ossel) and not saultWarden(ossel).

  Observe after_withies at withies when homecoming() "Boots stand on the mats inside the stilt-house doors now, pairs and pairs of them, put there the way the army taught. Somebody has taken the red coats in off the rails. Somebody else is teaching a soldier who has been asleep for three months how to mend an eel-trap again, and laughing at him.".
  Observe after_withies_held at withies when matured(ossel) and foreclosed(ossel) "From the eaves of the stilt-houses, all along the boardwalks, boots hang by their laces, pair by pair, turning a little in the wind off the sea. Nobody takes them down.".
  Observe after_withies_factor at withies when factorRules() "Half the men of the Withies are in the Factor's coats now, grey with a salt-white collar, and go out to Panhythe at dawn in step without being told. Their wives watch them go from the doors.".
  Observe after_landgate_kept at landgate when matured(ossel) and keptPromise(ossel) "On the board: a surveyor's notice, and a list of the strips upriver, and names against them in a clerk's hand, and against some of the names a cross where a man who cannot write has made his mark. Someone has written THEY KEPT IT across the top in charcoal, and someone else has written ABOUT TIME.".
  Observe after_landgate_release at landgate when matured(ossel) and released(ossel) "On the board, the Board's notice of a medal for the Long Muster, to be presented on the steps of the Council House. Under it, in pencil, in a great many hands: NO THANK YOU.".
  Observe after_landgate_factor at landgate when factorRules() "On the board, a single printed bill on good paper, with the Great Seal at the foot and a pair of crossed rakes beside it: THE WARDEN OF THE CITY GIVES NOTICE. The rest is about curfews and the price of bread, which has gone down.".
  Observe after_landgate_void at landgate when matured(ossel) and (noteVoid(ossel) or noteTorn(ossel)) "On the board: THE BOARD OF MOIETIES WILL HEAR THE QUESTION OF THE VETERANS' SETTLEMENT AGAIN AT THE SPRING SITTING. Someone has written under it, very neatly, AND WE WILL BE THERE.".
  Observe after_yard_release at legion_yard when matured(ossel) and released(ossel) "There are things on the Oath Stone's plinth now: a cap badge, a child's drawing of a soldier, a pair of boots, a stub of candle. People keep bringing them. Nobody has told anyone to.".
  Observe after_yard_factor at legion_yard when factorRules() "The Yard is full again: the Long Muster drilling in the Factor's grey under her own sergeants, very smartly, and very quietly. The Oath Stone stands in the middle of the parade ground and the files wheel round it without looking at it.".
  Observe after_tidewall_factor at tidewall when factorRules() "Soldiers in grey stand along the Tidewall at intervals, facing the city, not the sea.".
  Observe after_drum at drum_taproom when matured(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) and homecoming() "The Third Company's drum hangs over the bar with its head bare. The Drum is full, every bench, and the noise is the noise of people who have somewhere to go in the morning.".
  Observe after_steps_foreclosed at tideline_steps when matured(ossel) and foreclosed(ossel) and dark() "Far out past the bar, the sea is showing stars that are not the stars over Tessary: a great many, very close and very bright, in no shapes you know. Then a wave goes over them and they are gone.".
  Observe after_bath_torn at bath_hall when matured(ossel) and noteTorn(ossel) "In the arch of the plunge-room a hollow man in a grey coat stands a little apart from the others, very still, with one hand held out, palm up, ruled like paper. It does not come any nearer.".
  Observe after_chamber_void at weighing_chamber when matured(ossel) and noteVoid(ossel) "The pan where the black glass lay is empty. The pointer of the Balance stands off the level by the width of a city, and a Scruple sits on a stool at the foot of it with a ledger, writing down, very carefully, how far.".
  Observe after_countinghouse_warden at sault_office when matured(ossel) and saultWarden(ossel) and saultHoldsNote(ossel) "The War Note hangs on the wall behind the Factor's desk in a plain frame, a sheet of black glass that does not reflect anything. Under it, pinned, a letter from the King of Hethra about the working of brine, much annotated.".

  // The Valuer, freed, keeps a stall on Scriveners' Row.
  Person tally_freed "the scrivener in grey" at scriveners_row {
    Role "who keeps a stall at the end of the Row: CONTRACTS READ, DISPUTES WEIGHED, NO LIES TOLD (NONE)". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns they. Manner stoic.
    Seen when matured(ossel) and tallyFreed(ossel).
  }
  Topic tally_freed_asked with tally_freed "Ask the scrivener in grey how they are" when true once {
    Says "The scrivener in grey looks up from a lease, and the ruled lines on their face move in a way that, on anyone else, would be a smile. 'I have a name,' they say, 'and a stall, and three disputes about fences, and a mudlark who brings me an eel on Fourth-day, which I have learned to eat.' They consider. 'I said a great many things to you that were exact. I will say one that is not: I am happy. I cannot measure it. I note it all the same.'".
  }
  Rule tally_goes_up when matured(ossel) and tallyFreed(ossel) and at(tally, ?p) { Retract at(tally, ?p). Assert tallyBelow(ossel). }
  Rule tally_parts when matured(ossel) and tallyFreed(ossel) and travelsWith(tally, party) { Retract travelsWith(tally, party). Assert tallyBelow(ossel). }
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/callin:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  Description "What a thief hears in a city of seals and queues, and the one thing a thief can do on the ebb-runners' quay that costs neither five coin nor a lie: read the slate, and answer it in chalk.".

  // ── The thief's ear ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Said once for the company, by whoever it has of the calling. A company without a thief walks through all of it.
  Relation heardStrongbox(group). Relation heardQueue(group). Relation heardStilts(group). Relation heardQuay(group).
  Rule thief_strongbox at sault_office when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, sault_office) and not heardStrongbox(party)
    says "{?m} looks once at the strongbox behind the Factor's desk and then not again, which is how a thief looks at a thing. 'Iron outside, oak inside, and a lock a child could shim,' {?m} says, very low. 'She did not buy that to keep anything in it. She bought it to be seen to own something that locks.'" {
    Assert heardStrongbox(party).
  }
  Rule thief_queue at seals_hall when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, seals_hall) and not heardQueue(party)
    says "{?m} stands at the end of the Office of Seals' queue for the length of one slow breath and is bored beyond bearing. 'Seven hundred people, and not a purse out of place,' {?m} says. 'They are too frightened of the clerks to be robbed. The only living in this hall is for whoever sells the places in the line.'" {
    Assert heardQueue(party).
  }
  Rule thief_stilts at withies when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, withies) and not heardStilts(party)
    says "{?m} walks the length of one gangway with a hand on the rail, and counts the doors. 'Not one bolt on the outside of any door,' {?m} says. 'Not one in the whole ward. Either they have nothing worth the taking, or everyone here has agreed on a thing they will not tell a stranger.'" {
    Assert heardStilts(party).
  }
  Rule thief_quay at landing when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, landing) and not heardQuay(party)
    says "{?m} looks at the board of notches by the tunnel mouth, and does not look at the woman with the cutlass at all. 'A tally, in cant,' {?m} says. 'It is not for counting. It says who has paid, and who may come and go, and who is not to be touched. If that were mine, I would want to know it by heart.'" {
    Assert heardQuay(party).
  }

  // ── The thief's way on the quay ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Bettany Slake will let a company use her quay for five coin, or if it works for the Factor. She has a third rule that
  // she does not say aloud, because it is a rule of her old trade: whoever can read the board and chalk the right sign
  // on it is one of the quay's, and is let by without a word. Anyone may stand and look at the slate. It is a thief who
  // can read what it is for.
  Relation chalkedSign(group).
  Action chalk_the_sign(actor: group, site: place, c: member) "Chalk the quay's own sign on the board by the tunnel mouth" {
    Description "Read the slate for what it is, a tally of who may pass, and answer it in the same cant.".
    Speaker slake.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(slake, site) and able(slake) and memberOf(c, actor)
      and hasCalling(c, calling_thief) and awake(c) and not tolerates(slake, actor) and not hostile(slake, actor) and not chalkedSign(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert chalkedSign(actor). Assert tolerates(slake, actor). Assert tolerates(runners, actor). Assert slakeLetsPass(actor). }
    Result "{c} takes the chalk from its string, thumbs out a stroke at the end of the bottom row, a crossed stroke through it, and a small round mark that is not a number. It takes four seconds. Bettany Slake's eyes come up from her crate, and go to the board, and to {c}'s hand, and stay on it. She says nothing at all for as long as it takes to breathe in and out. 'Quay's yours,' she says. 'Not the crates. And if anyone asks you where you learned that, you learned it from nobody, and I never saw it.'".
  }

  // ── Off the road ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Something to smell, and something carved that nobody can explain.
  Observe row_smell at scriveners_row when not dark() "Scriveners' Row smells of reed-paper drying on every sill, a flat green smell like wet hay, and of the iron-gall ink that comes off the pens in the hot afternoon. Under it all runs a sound you take at first for rain: three hundred nibs, all going.".
  Observe drum_lintel at drum_taproom when true "Cut into the lintel over the Muffled Drum's door, one under another, are a dozen sets of initials, each with a year, and under every set the same two words in the Row's formal hand: HELD. QUIT. Hannelore Rackham says it is the way the Third Company's old sergeants signed out of the house, and that she has never known which of the two words they meant.".
}

Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── The fortnight ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Tessary keeps its days by the ebbs. Low water comes twice a day, about the eleventh hour and about the eleventh of
  // the night, and lasts some five hours each time; while it lasts the outer basin drains through the Swatch and
  // Lowtide stands out of the water. The night ebb at two in the morning is the one the city counts: each is a night of
  // the fortnight. On the first, the eighth and the fifteenth it is a spring ebb, the lowest of all, and on those
  // nights the Balance takes its interest. The fifteenth is the Feast of Settlement, when the war note falls due.
  Query lowWater() means hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) <= 14 or hour(clock) >= 22 or hour(clock) <= 2.
  // The hour the water turns, when anyone still down in Lowtide had better be on a roof.
  Query turning() means hour(clock) == 14 or hour(clock) == 2.
  Measure night(place). Relation counted(place).
  // The first night counted is the first two o'clock at least five hours after the company comes.
  Rule night_turns when hour(clock) == 2 and not counted(ossel) and watch(clock) >= 30 {
    Increase night(ossel) by 1. Assert counted(ossel). }
  Rule night_passes when hour(clock) != 2 and counted(ossel) { Retract counted(ossel). }
  Query springNight() means night(ossel) == 1 or night(ossel) == 8 or night(ossel) == 15.
  // From the evening of the fourteenth night's day the city is keeping the Feast.
  Query feastEve() means night(ossel) >= 14.

  // Where word of the city's doings reaches the company: anywhere in Tessary, not under the sea. A company that has
  // been below hears what happened when it comes up.
  Relation cityRoom(place).
  // News already gone round, so it is not told twice.
  Relation spread(fact).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(throat_head).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(tidewall).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(legion_yard).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(tideline_steps).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(scriveners_row).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(terraces).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(withies).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(landgate).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(saltgate).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(pans).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(teazle_room).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(drum_taproom).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(sault_office).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(warehouse_floor).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(cistern).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(muster_hall).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(seals_hall).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(seals_inner).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(exchequer_room).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(pounce_stall).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(council_chamber).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(kings_rooms).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(marrable_room).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(chapel).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(chandlery).
  Initially Assert cityRoom(causeway_end).
  Query inTessary() means at(party, ?p) and cityRoom(?p).

  // A place the company has left and come back to is told shortly: what changed, not the whole of it again.
  Relation visitedNow(place). Relation visitedBefore(place).
  Rule arrives_at when at(party, ?p) and not visitedNow(?p) { Assert visitedNow(?p). }
  Rule leaves_from when visitedNow(?p) and not at(party, ?p) { Retract visitedNow(?p). Assert visitedBefore(?p). }

  // ── The calling ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At a spring ebb the Balance calls a dozen of the collateral, in the order of the Muster's roll. They come down
  // through the Withies in step, barefoot, set their boots together on the top step and walk out over the wet sand
  // toward the Hall of Oaths. In the morning their families find the boots.
  Measure held(place). Measure callings(place). Relation bootsOnSteps(place). Relation callingDue(place).
  Initially Set held(ossel) to 138. Initially Set callings(ossel) to 0.
  Rule calling_due when counted(ossel) and springNight() and night(ossel) < 15 and callings(ossel) < night(ossel) and not interestPaid(ossel) {
    Assert callingDue(ossel). Set callings(ossel) to night(ossel). }
  Relation interestPaid(place).
  Rule interest_waived when counted(ossel) and springNight() and callings(ossel) < night(ossel) and interestPaid(ossel) {
    Set callings(ossel) to night(ossel). Retract interestPaid(ossel). }
  Rule calling_happens when callingDue(ossel) {
    Retract callingDue(ossel). Increase held(ossel) by 12. Assert bootsOnSteps(ossel). Assert calledLast(ossel). }
  Relation calledLast(place).
  Rule boots_taken when bootsOnSteps(ossel) and hour(clock) == 9 { Retract bootsOnSteps(ossel). }
  Rule calling_told at tideline_steps when calledLast(ossel) says "They come down through the Withies a little after two, twelve of them, in step, though nobody is calling the step. Barefoot. Their eyes are open. At the top of the Watersteps each of them stops, and stoops, and sets his boots side by side on the stone, toes to the water, and straightens, and walks down into the sea. The water is very low. They walk out over the sand toward the walls in the basin, getting smaller, keeping step, until the dark has them." teaches calling_witnessed { Retract calledLast(ossel). }
  Rule calling_unseen when calledLast(ossel) { Retract calledLast(ossel). }
  Discovery calling_witnessed "At the spring ebb, twelve veterans of the Long Muster walked barefoot and in step down the Watersteps and out across the drained basin toward the drowned city, as if called, and left their boots paired on the top step.".
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/compan:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // The company of the campaign played alone: one traveller come down the marsh road with a little coin (placed.kyr is
  // the world's own company, come in by the Causeway).
  Company party "You" of 1 to 3 at causeway_end.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 12. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 2.
}

Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── The Valuer about the city ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // By day the inventory in the Withies; by night the Watersteps, watching the water.
  Rule tally_to_steps when hour(clock) >= 21 and at(tally, withies) and not travelsWith(tally, party) and not tallyBelow(ossel) {
    Retract at(tally, withies). Assert at(tally, tideline_steps). }
  Rule tally_to_withies when hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 21 and at(tally, tideline_steps) and not travelsWith(tally, party) and not tallyBelow(ossel) {
    Retract at(tally, tideline_steps). Assert at(tally, withies). }
  Relation tallyBelow(place).
  // What the Valuer does with a contradiction: a filing.
  Relation tallyHeardPrior(place). Relation tallyKnowsDominion(place).
  Topic tell_tally_prior with tally "Tell the Valuer that the city promised its soldiers land and a pension before it pledged them" when knows(actor, enlist_promise) and knows(actor, promise_weight) and not tallyHeardPrior(ossel) once {
    Says "The Valuer stops writing. 'The recruiting bill,' they say. 'Eleven years old. The Muster was raised when the war began; the note was drawn when the war was a year old, and going badly.' They are silent for a while. 'The promise to the soldiers was made first.' They look at the ledger as if it had said something rude. 'A prior promise, of the same weight, to the same persons, unkept. And the city pledged those persons to us as if they were its own.' A long pause. 'That is not on my inventory. I find I cannot stop thinking about it.'".
    On discuss { Assert tallyHeardPrior(ossel). }
  }
  Topic tell_tally_dominion with tally "Tell the Valuer that the Factor means to buy the note in order to govern the city" when knows(actor, sault_bid) and not tallyKnowsDominion(ossel) once {
    Says "'To govern,' says the Valuer. 'With the collateral.' Their voice does not change; the ruled lines on their face do. 'A note may be taken up at foreclosure by whoever pledges its weight. It may not be taken up for dominion. That is the ninth chapter.' They write for some time. 'I will file an objection to the Factor's bid with the Broker's superiors. It will be heard. Whether it is heard in time I cannot say.'".
    On discuss { Assert tallyKnowsDominion(ossel). }
  }
  Relation objectionFiled(place).
  Rule objection_heard when tallyKnowsDominion(ossel) and night(ossel) >= 12 and not objectionFiled(ossel) and not tallyUnravelled(ossel) { Assert objectionFiled(ossel). Assert brokerSuspended(ossel). }

  // The indictment: only a Valuer who has seen the Room of Defaults, and kept faith with the company that showed
  // it to them, will bring it.
  Action ask_indictment(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Valuer to indict the Comptroller before the Assembly" {
    Speaker tally. Time 1.
    Grave "If the Assembly finds against him, the Comptroller will unravel, or at best be put down from his office; and the Valuer will have done the gravest thing a Scruple can do.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and travelsWith(tally, actor) and tallySawDefaults(ossel)
      and not brokeFaith(actor) and not indictmentFiled(ossel) and not tallyUnravelled(ossel) and not caughtCopying(actor)
      and (tallyHeardPrior(ossel) or keptFaith(actor) or tallyKnowsDominion(ossel)).
    On success { Assert indictmentFiled(ossel). Retract travelsWith(tally, actor). Assert tallyBelow(ossel). Assert at(tally, clerks_hall).
      Assert holdingAdmits(actor). }
    Result "The Valuer is quiet for a long time. 'Yes,' they say. 'It must be one of us, and it must be someone who has read the entry, and I have read it.' They take out a fresh sheet and write on it, standing, in a hand that does not shake. When they have done they fold it once. 'The Assembly will sit in the Weighing Chamber on the night of the Settlement, from midnight, and the Notary will come out of the Holding to sit with it. I will be there. You should be there; you read it with me.' They look at you. 'I am leaving you here. I have a great deal to prepare and I find I would rather be alone.'".
  }
  Rule indictment_spoken when indictmentFiled(ossel) and swornSilence(party) and not forswornParty(party)
    says "Somewhere under the sea a promise of silence you made to the Comptroller breaks, and you feel it go, a cold hand laid flat between your shoulders." {
    Assert forswornParty(party). }

  // ── The Release ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Durrance, if she is free and has thought it through, can call the Muster to the Oath Stone on the night of the
  // Feast to release the city from its promise to them; the Factor's men will try to break it up.
  Relation releaseCalled(place). Relation releaseGathered(place). Relation releaseBroken(place). Relation releaseHeld(place).
  Query cityPaying() means votePassed(ossel) and not sealStolen(ossel).
  Topic ask_release with durrance "Ask Durrance to call the Muster to the Oath Stone on the night of the Feast, to release the city" when durranceKnowsRelease(durrance) and not heldNow(durrance) and not releaseCalled(ossel) and not cityPaying() and night(ossel) <= 14 and not serves(durrance, sault) once {
    Says "Durrance has had her days to think, and she has thought. 'Eleven years,' she says. 'And the Board votes no, or yes and then lets the Factor walk off with the Seal, and either way the lads stay under the sea.' She stands up. 'So we do it. The Muster on the Stone at the Feast, as many as I can get, and we say it: we hold you quit. Keep your land. Keep your pension. Give us back our own.' She laughs, short. 'I'll have to tell them it was my idea. They'll never stand for it if it was a stranger's.' She looks at you. 'The Factor will send her lightermen. Be there.'".
    On discuss { Assert releaseCalled(ossel). }
  }
  Rule release_gathers when releaseCalled(ossel) and night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) == 22 and not releaseGathered(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) and at(durrance, ?p) {
    Assert releaseGathered(ossel). Retract at(durrance, ?p). Assert at(durrance, legion_yard). }
  Rule release_gathers_with when releaseCalled(ossel) and night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) == 22 and not releaseGathered(ossel) and travelsWith(durrance, party) {
    Assert releaseGathered(ossel). }
  Observe release_scene at legion_yard when releaseGathered(ossel) and not released(ossel) and not releaseBroken(ossel) "The Legion Yard is full of soldiers. Not in step, not in ranks: a crowd of men and women in old red coats and whatever else they have, with lanterns, thousands of them, filling the Yard and the wall-walk and the lane, and more coming. Durrance stands on the Oath Stone's plinth with one hand on the Stone. It is very quiet for so many people. Out on the Tidewall the Feast's bonfires are burning, and the city's year of contracts is going up in sparks.".
  Event release_crowd at legion_yard when releaseGathered(ossel) and not released(ossel) and not releaseBroken(ossel) "They come in through the Yard gate in ones and twos at first, and then in files, and then in a crowd that does not stop: soldiers of the Long Muster in their old red coats and in their working clothes, with lanterns, with their wives and husbands and children, filling the parade ground and the wall-walk and the lane behind. Nobody gives an order. Durrance climbs up onto the plinth and lays her hand on the Oath Stone and waits, and the Yard goes quiet round her a rank at a time.".
  Event lightermen_turned_back at legion_yard when releaseGathered(ossel) and fiskTurned(fisk) and night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) == 23 and not released(ossel) "There is a stir at the Yard gate. A dozen men in salt-stiff jerkins have come up the lane with cudgels, and found the gate full of the Third Company, with Benno Fisk in front of them in his old red coat. Nobody raises a hand. The lightermen look at the crowd behind Fisk for a long moment, and then they go back down the lane the way they came, and the crowd lets them.".
  Rule lightermen_come when releaseGathered(ossel) and hour(clock) == 23 and night(ossel) == 14 and able(lightermen) and not saultStopped(ossel) and at(lightermen, ?p) and not at(lightermen, legion_yard) and not fiskTurned(fisk) {
    Retract at(lightermen, ?p). Assert at(lightermen, legion_yard). }
  Rule lightermen_at_yard at legion_yard when at(lightermen, legion_yard) and releaseGathered(ossel) and at(party, legion_yard) and not assails(lightermen, party) and able(lightermen) and not released(ossel)
    says "There is a shout from the gate. Sault's lightermen are coming through the crowd with cudgels, shoving, a dozen of them, making for the plinth." {
    Assert assails(lightermen, party). }
  Rule release_broken when releaseGathered(ossel) and at(lightermen, legion_yard) and able(lightermen) and hour(clock) == 0 and not at(party, legion_yard) and not released(ossel) and not releaseBroken(ossel) {
    Assert releaseBroken(ossel). }
  Rule release_broken_told when releaseBroken(ossel) and not spread(release_broken_known)
    and inTessary() says "Word comes from the Legion Yard: the Factor's lightermen broke up the Muster at the Oath Stone with cudgels, and the Watch stood by, and Durrance was carried off the plinth with a broken head." { Assert spread(release_broken_known). }
  Discovery release_broken_known "The Factor's lightermen broke up the Muster's gathering at the Oath Stone on the Feast night.".
  Relation saultStopped(place).
  Action stand_release(actor: group, site: place) "Stand with the Muster at the Oath Stone while they say it" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, legion_yard) and releaseGathered(ossel)
      and not released(ossel) and not releaseBroken(ossel) and night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) >= 23
      and not (at(lightermen, legion_yard) and able(lightermen)).
    On success { Assert released(ossel). }
    Result "Durrance says it first, alone, with her hand on the Stone, in a voice that carries to the back of the Yard without being raised: 'The city of Tessary promised me land and a pension if I came home. I came home. I hold it quit.' Then the Third Company says it, ragged, and then the Yard, all of it, eight thousand voices or near enough, not together, a long rolling noise like surf: I hold it quit. And under your feet, under the Yard, under the Tidewall and the drowned streets, something very large and very far down settles by a hair's breadth, like a pan of a scale coming level.".
  }
  Rule release_by_itself when releaseGathered(ossel) and hour(clock) == 1 and night(ossel) == 14 and not released(ossel) and not releaseBroken(ossel)
    and not (at(lightermen, legion_yard) and able(lightermen)) { Assert released(ossel). }

  // ── The Assembly ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation assemblySits(place). Relation assemblyHeard(place). Relation mercyAsked(place). Relation comptrollerUnravelled(place).
  Relation comptrollerDeposed(place).
  Rule assembly_convenes when indictmentFiled(ossel) and night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) == 0 and not assemblySits(ossel) {
    Assert assemblySits(ossel). Retract at(tally, clerks_hall). Assert at(tally, weighing_chamber).
    Retract at(comptroller, comptroller_office). Assert at(comptroller, weighing_chamber). }
  Event assembly_comes at weighing_chamber when assemblySits(ossel) "At midnight they come down the Counting Stair, all of them: the Scruples in their grey coats, in silence, in rows, more of them than you have seen in all the halls together, and fill the floor of the nave under the Balance. The Comptroller comes last and stands alone. Then the Door of the Holding brightens, and something steps out of it that is made of fine ruled lines of light, as a drawing of a clerk is made of lines, and takes its place at the foot of the Balance. The Valuer steps forward with one folded sheet. Nobody has said a word.".
  Observe assembly_scene at weighing_chamber when assemblySits(ossel) and not noteVoid(ossel) "The Assembly of the Scruples is sitting. They stand in rows on the floor of the nave under the Balance, all of them, grey and pale and silent, with their ruled hands folded. At the foot of the Balance the Notary stands, come out of the Holding for the first time in five hundred years, a figure drawn in lines of light. The Comptroller stands alone before it. The Valuer stands alone before him, with one folded sheet.".
  Action testify(actor: group, site: place) "Testify before the Assembly to what you read in the Room of Defaults" {
    Time 2.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, weighing_chamber) and assemblySits(ossel)
      and knows(actor, note_designed) and not assemblyHeard(ossel).
    On success { Assert assemblyHeard(ossel). }
    Result "You tell them what you read, and where, and when, and who was with you. The floor of the nave registers every word; the ruled lines along the walls brighten and hold. Nobody interrupts. When you have finished the Notary turns its face of lines to the Comptroller. He does not deny it. He cannot. 'I would draw it again,' he says, to the Assembly, to the Balance, to the Door with the white floor beyond it. 'There was no other way to close it. There is still none.'".
  }
  Action ask_mercy(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Assembly to put the Comptroller down from his office, and spare him unravelling" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, weighing_chamber) and assemblyHeard(ossel)
      and not mercyAsked(ossel) and not noteVoid(ossel).
    On success { Assert mercyAsked(ossel). }
    Result "There is a long silence in the nave. Then the Notary speaks. 'A promise made to be broken is no promise,' it says. 'That is the law. What becomes of the one who made it is the Assembly's.' It looks at the Valuer. The Valuer looks at the Comptroller for a long time. 'He has kept the ledger for eleven hundred years,' they say. 'Let him keep the archive. Under supervision. Without the black glass.' And the rows of grey figures bow, all together, which is apparently how the Scruples vote.".
  }
  Rule note_voided when assemblySits(ossel) and hour(clock) == 1 and night(ossel) == 14 and not noteVoid(ossel) and not tallyUnravelled(ossel)
    says "In the Weighing Chamber the Notary lays a line of light through the sheet of black glass in the pan, end to end, and the glass goes grey, and then clear, and then is nothing. 'Void,' it says. 'A promise made to be broken is no promise. The collateral is released.' The pointer of the Balance swings, a long slow arc, and stops where it stops: not level. There is still a hole in the ledger the size of a city. But it is the Comptroller's, now, and not the Muster's." {
    Assert noteVoid(ossel). }
  Rule comptroller_unravels when noteVoid(ossel) and not mercyAsked(ossel) and not comptrollerUnravelled(ossel)
    says "The Comptroller does not cry out. The ruled lines of his face begin to come apart, very slowly, like a page left in rain, and then less slowly, and then he is a coat with nobody in it, standing at the foot of the Balance with its hands out, as if it wanted to be given something. Two of the Weights come and lead it away toward the stair, quite gently. Nobody watches it go except the Valuer." {
    Assert comptrollerUnravelled(ossel). Retract at(comptroller, weighing_chamber). }
  Rule comptroller_put_down when noteVoid(ossel) and mercyAsked(ossel) and not comptrollerDeposed(ossel) { Assert comptrollerDeposed(ossel). }

  // ── The Factor on the night ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // If her broker is suspended she comes to the Weighing Chamber herself, with lightermen, by the cistern and the
  // drowned streets, to pledge in person at foreclosure; if he is not, her bid is lodged on the fourteenth day.
  Relation saultBidLodged(place). Relation saultInChamber(place). Relation saultWarden(place).
  Rule bid_lodged when night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) == 12 and not brokerSuspended(ossel) and able(sault) and not saultBidLodged(ossel) {
    Assert saultBidLodged(ossel). }
  Rule sault_goes_down when night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) == 23 and brokerSuspended(ossel) and able(sault) and not saultInChamber(ossel) and at(sault, ?p) and not saultStopped(ossel) {
    Assert saultInChamber(ossel). Retract at(sault, ?p). Assert at(sault, weighing_chamber). Retract peaceable(sault). }
  Observe sault_in_chamber at weighing_chamber when saultInChamber(ossel) and at(sault, weighing_chamber) and not matured(ossel) "Factor Sault is here, in the nave of the Weighing Chamber, in a sea-cloak still wet from the Hall of Oaths, with a lantern and two lightermen and a paper in her hand. She is looking up at the Balance with her mouth slightly open, like anyone. Then she sees you, and puts the look away. 'Of course,' she says. 'Of course it's you.'".
  Topic sault_terms with sault "Put terms to the Factor: take up the note and call the Muster out only to send them home to their land" when (saultInChamber(ossel) or saultExposed(ossel) or brokerSuspended(ossel) or saultShaken(ossel)) and knows(actor, sault_bid) and knows(actor, salt_springs) and not saultWarden(ossel) and not matured(ossel) and able(sault) once {
    Says "Factor Sault hears you out with her head on one side. 'Warden of the Settlement,' she says. 'Hold the note and never use it but to send them home. And for that?' You tell her: the salt springs of Hethra, which the war was fought for, and which nobody else in Tessary knows how to work. She laughs. 'You've been talking to Amaury.' She turns the paper cone over, point down. 'They'd still owe me,' she says. 'The city. For ever.' She looks at the Balance. 'All right. Write it down, whatever you people write it on. I'll swear it. I'd rather be owed than hated, and I'd rather be either than beaten.'".
    On discuss { Assert saultWarden(ossel). }
  }
  Action stop_sault(actor: group, site: place) "Stand between the Factor and the Balance" {
    Time 0.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(sault, site) and saultInChamber(ossel) and able(sault)
      and not saultWarden(ossel) and not matured(ossel) and not assails(sault, actor).
    On success { Assert assails(sault, actor). Assert assails(lightermen, actor). }
    Result "'Don't,' says Factor Sault, almost kindly, and draws.".
  }
  Rule lightermen_with_sault when saultInChamber(ossel) and at(lightermen, ?p) and not at(lightermen, weighing_chamber) and able(lightermen) {
    Retract at(lightermen, ?p). Assert at(lightermen, weighing_chamber). }
  Rule sault_beaten when saultInChamber(ossel) and not able(sault) and not saultStopped(ossel) { Assert saultStopped(ossel). }
  Rule sault_captured when captured(sault, party) and at(party, ?p)
    says "You come round on the floor of the nave with your head ringing. Factor Sault is standing over you, wiping her hands. 'Stay down,' she says. 'It's nearly two.'" {
    Retract captured(sault, party). }
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(sault).

  // The Valuer's last resort: in the chamber at the Settlement, with nothing else left, they can take the black
  // glass out of the pan and break it. A Scruple who breaks the note breaks a promise held by the Balance.
  Action ask_tear(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Valuer to take the War Note out of the pan and break it" {
    Speaker tally. Time 1 minute.
    Grave "The Valuer will be breaking a promise the Balance holds. You know what happens to a Scruple who does.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, weighing_chamber) and at(tally, weighing_chamber)
      and tallySawDefaults(ossel) and not indictmentFiled(ossel) and not brokeFaith(actor) and night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) >= 0
      and hour(clock) < 2 and not released(ossel) and not deedsDelivered(ossel) and not noteTorn(ossel).
    On success { Assert noteTorn(ossel). Assert tallyUnravelled(ossel). Retract travelsWith(tally, actor). Retract willing(tally, actor). Assert tallyBelow(ossel). }
    Result "The Valuer looks at you, and then up at the Balance, for a long moment. 'Yes,' they say. 'Somebody should break it who knows what it is.' They climb the side of the pan like a child climbing into a boat, and walk across the bottom of it to the sheet of black glass, and pick it up in both ruled hands, and break it over their knee. It breaks like ice. The pointer of the Balance swings, slowly, all the way across the dial. And the ruled lines on the Valuer's face begin, very gently, to come undone. 'Oh,' they say, looking at their hands. 'That is what it feels like.' They sit down in the bottom of the pan. 'Tell the child,' they say, 'that the eel was very kind,' and then there is nobody in the grey coat at all.".
  }
  Rule tally_with_party_down when travelsWith(tally, party) and at(party, weighing_chamber) and not at(tally, weighing_chamber) { Assert at(tally, weighing_chamber). }
  Rule tally_off_floor when at(tally, weighing_chamber) and travelsWith(tally, party) and not at(party, weighing_chamber) { Retract at(tally, weighing_chamber). }

  // ── The Settlement ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At the fifteenth spring ebb the note matures. What is true of the city at that moment decides what follows.
  Rule maturity when night(ossel) == 15 and not matured(ossel) { Assert matured(ossel). Assert settling(ossel). }
  Relation settling(place).
  Rule settle_kept when settling(ossel) and deedsDelivered(ossel) { Retract settling(ossel). Assert keptPromise(ossel). Assert discharged(ossel). }
  Rule settle_released when settling(ossel) and released(ossel) { Retract settling(ossel). Assert discharged(ossel). }
  Rule settle_void when settling(ossel) and noteVoid(ossel) { Retract settling(ossel). Assert discharged(ossel). }
  Rule settle_torn when settling(ossel) and noteTorn(ossel) { Retract settling(ossel). Assert discharged(ossel). }
  // A bid for dominion, objected to by a Valuer, fails; a Warden's bid, sworn to send the Muster home, does not.
  Rule settle_taken when settling(ossel) and (saultBidLodged(ossel) or (saultInChamber(ossel) and able(sault) and not saultStopped(ossel)))
    and (not objectionFiled(ossel) or saultWarden(ossel)) {
    Retract settling(ossel). Assert saultHoldsNote(ossel). }
  Rule settle_foreclosed when settling(ossel) { Retract settling(ossel). Assert foreclosed(ossel). }
  // Discharged: every oath in the pan goes home.
  Rule held_wake when discharged(ossel) and heldNow(?s) { Retract heldNow(?s). Retract asleep(?s). Assert cameHome(?s). Assert wokeHome(?s). }
  Rule held_warden when saultHoldsNote(ossel) and saultWarden(ossel) and heldNow(?s) { Retract heldNow(?s). Retract asleep(?s). Assert cameHome(?s). Assert wokeHome(?s). }
  Rule held_count when (discharged(ossel) or saultWarden(ossel) and saultHoldsNote(ossel)) and held(ossel) > 0 { Set held(ossel) to 0. }
  Rule settlement_heard at ranks when discharged(ossel) and not spread(held_woke)
    says "All down the Ranks the sleepers open their eyes, together, as if a drum had beaten the stand-down. They look at their hands. They look at each other. Somebody laughs. Somebody starts to cry. Then, without anyone giving the order, they turn, all of them, and begin to walk back across the white floor toward the Door, in step, because they do not know how not to." { Assert spread(held_woke). }
  Rule settlement_seen when discharged(ossel) and not at(party, ranks) and not spread(held_woke)
    and inTessary() says "At two in the morning, all over the Withies, people wake for no reason and go out onto the boardwalks. The basin is out, lower than anyone has ever seen it. And out in the drowned city, very small, coming up the steps of the Hall of Oaths and across the Forum in the starlight, barefoot and in their shirts and in step, a hundred and sixty soldiers of the Long Muster are walking home." { Assert spread(held_woke). }
  Discovery held_woke "At the Settlement the note was discharged, and the called of the Long Muster woke and walked home.".
  Rule muster_called when saultHoldsNote(ossel) and not saultWarden(ossel) and not spread(muster_called_known)
    says "At two in the morning, all over Tessary, the soldiers of the Long Muster get up out of their beds, the old ones and the young ones and the one-armed ones, and dress, and go out into the streets, and walk in step through the dark to Panhythe, where Factor Sault is waiting for them on the steps of her countinghouse with a lantern. Her voice carries a long way in the quiet. 'Good morning, lads,' she says. 'You're paid from today.'" { Assert spread(muster_called_known). }
  Discovery muster_called_known "At the Settlement Factor Sault took up the War Note and called the Long Muster to Panhythe.".
  Rule muster_warden when saultHoldsNote(ossel) and saultWarden(ossel) and not spread(muster_called_known)
    says "At two in the morning the soldiers of the Long Muster wake in their beds all over the city, every one of them, for no reason, and lie listening. Nothing calls them. Out in the drowned city, in the starlight, a hundred and sixty more are walking home across the Forum, and at the head of them, in a wet sea-cloak with a lantern, the Factor of the Salt Moiety is picking her way over the weed and swearing." { Assert spread(muster_called_known). }
  Rule foreclosure_told when foreclosed(ossel) and not spread(foreclosed_known)
    and inTessary() says "At two in the morning nothing happens. The basin is out, lower than anyone remembers; the Tidewall bonfires have burned down to red; the last contracts of the year are ash. Nobody walks into the sea. Nobody walks out of it. Only, a long way out past the Hall of Oaths, where the outer bar meets the open water, the sea for a moment shows a sky full of stars that are not the stars over Tessary, bright and close, and then is the sea again." { Assert spread(foreclosed_known). }
  Discovery foreclosed_known "At the Settlement the War Note fell in and nobody took it up. The called stay where they are, and the ledger is uneven at Tessary.".

  // ── What became of them ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Told in the morning after the Settlement, before the book closes.
  Query morning() means night(ossel) >= 15 and hour(clock) >= 7.
  Relation toldFates(place).
  Rule fate_tally_reformer when morning() and noteVoid(ossel) and not tallyFreed(ossel) and not told_tally(ossel) says "The Ninth Valuer sits now at the Comptroller's desk, which they have had moved into the Hall of Clerks where everyone can see it. They have begun to go through the ledger from the first page, with the old city's hole in it, and to write in the margin, for each entry, whether it was honest. It will take them, they estimate, four hundred years. They seem, as far as anyone can tell with a Scruple, happy." { Assert told_tally(ossel). }
  Rule fate_tally_freed when morning() and tallyFreed(ossel) and not told_tally(ossel) says "There is a new stall on Scriveners' Row: CONTRACTS READ, DISPUTES WEIGHED, NO LIES TOLD (NONE). The scrivener behind it has a grey coat and ruled hands and a name nobody in Tessary has heard before, which by the end of the winter nobody finds strange. Pounce says it is unfair competition. Brother Ancel says it is the saint come home. Wick brings them an eel every Fourth-day, and they eat it." { Assert told_tally(ossel). }
  Rule fate_tally_unravelled when morning() and tallyUnravelled(ossel) and not told_tally(ossel) says "Wick Teazle sits on the Watersteps every evening at the ebb, with an eel in a paper cone, and watches the doorways of Lowtide where the hollow men stand, looking for one in a grey coat. He has not seen it yet. He does not know what he would do if he did. He thinks he would give it the eel." { Assert told_tally(ossel). }
  Rule fate_tally_plain when morning() and not tallyFreed(ossel) and not tallyUnravelled(ossel) and not noteVoid(ossel) and not told_tally(ossel) says "The Ninth Valuer went below at the Settlement with the inventory complete. The children of the Withies still call the stair at the end of the boardwalk Docket's Step, though none of them can say why." { Assert told_tally(ossel). }
  Relation told_tally(place). Relation told_durrance(place). Relation told_quire(place). Relation told_sault(place).
  Rule fate_durrance_release when morning() and released(ossel) and not told_durrance(ossel) says "Thomasin Durrance never takes a penny of the pension she released. She runs the Muffled Drum with Hannelore now, and the Third Company's drum hangs over the bar with its head bare, and on the night of every spring ebb she beats the stand-down on it, at two in the morning, for anyone who might be listening." { Assert told_durrance(ossel). }
  Rule fate_durrance_sault when morning() and serves(durrance, sault) and not told_durrance(ossel) says "Sergeant Durrance sergeants the Factor's Muster, in a good coat, and is fair to them, and is paid, and does not go into the Muffled Drum any more." { Assert told_durrance(ossel). }
  Rule fate_durrance_held when morning() and heldNow(durrance) and not told_durrance(ossel) says "Sergeant Durrance is still standing in the Ranks of the Holding, asleep, with her hands at her sides. At the Muffled Drum her boots stand on the bar under the covered drum, and nobody touches them." { Assert told_durrance(ossel). }
  Rule fate_durrance_home when morning() and not heldNow(durrance) and not serves(durrance, sault) and not released(ossel) and not told_durrance(ossel) says "Sergeant Durrance goes back to the Muffled Drum and drinks one pot, standing, and then goes down to the Watersteps to meet the ones coming home, and calls the roll for them on the top step, every name, in order, until her voice goes." { Assert told_durrance(ossel). }
  Rule fate_quire_confessed when morning() and quireConfessed(ossel) and not told_quire(ossel) says "Josiah Quire is put out of the Exchequer by the Board in a vote of seven to nothing, and goes to live in two rooms in the Lettered Quarter, and writes letters for people who cannot, at Pounce's old rates, which annoys Pounce. He is sleeping again." { Assert told_quire(ossel). }
  Rule fate_quire_dead when morning() and quireDrowned(ossel) and not told_quire(ossel) says "Brother Ancel hangs a weight in Saint Evenhand's for Josiah Quire: lead, for a debt. It is the only one in the chapel nobody paid for." { Assert told_quire(ossel). }
  Rule fate_sault_exposed when morning() and saultExposed(ossel) and not saultHoldsNote(ossel) and not told_sault(ossel) says "Factor Sault keeps her pans and her ships and loses her chair on the Board, and is seen every evening on the Tidewall eating eels out of a paper cone, as cheerful as ever, and doing sums." { Assert told_sault(ossel). }
  Rule fate_sault_warden when morning() and saultWarden(ossel) and saultHoldsNote(ossel) and not told_sault(ossel) says "Factor Sault holds the War Note in a frame on the wall of her countinghouse, and never calls on it, and works the salt springs of Hethra by treaty with a king who finds her very amusing. The city owes her everything. She reminds it daily." { Assert told_sault(ossel). }
  Rule fate_sault_foreclosed when morning() and foreclosed(ossel) and not saultHoldsNote(ossel) and not told_sault(ossel) says "Factor Sault came up the Long Stair on the morning of the Settlement with nothing in her hands, and has not said a word about it since, to anyone. In the spring she pays, out of her own purse, for another course of stone along the Tidewall, a foot higher than the Moieties' and the Aenean ones under it, and has nothing cut on it at all." { Assert told_sault(ossel). }
  Rule fate_sault_thwarted when morning() and not foreclosed(ossel) and not saultExposed(ossel) and not saultHoldsNote(ossel) and not told_sault(ossel) says "Factor Sault's bid was never opened: at the Settlement there was nothing owing to bid for. She keeps her chair and her pans and her ships. One by one, over the winter, the coats she gave the Muster's men come back to her hiring hall, folded, and she has them hung on pegs along the wall, in rows, and does not give them out again." { Assert told_sault(ossel). }
  Relation told_comptroller(place).
  Rule fate_comptroller_foreclosed when morning() and foreclosed(ossel) and not told_comptroller(ossel) says "Under the sea the Comptroller has his eight thousand oaths, and the hole in his ledger is filled, to the last line, as he drew it. The Copyist says he has not been seen to write since." { Assert told_comptroller(ossel). }
  Rule fate_comptroller_outbid when morning() and saultHoldsNote(ossel) and not told_comptroller(ossel) says "Under the sea the Comptroller enters the War Note transferred to a woman of the Salt Moiety, in his own hand, which does not shake. The hole in the Room of Defaults is eleven hundred years wide and stays so. He has the Copyist read the entry back to him twice." { Assert told_comptroller(ossel). }
  Rule fate_comptroller_discharged when morning() and (keptPromise(ossel) or released(ossel) or noteTorn(ossel)) and not told_comptroller(ossel) says "Under the sea the Comptroller enters the War Note discharged and closes the ledger. The hole in the Room of Defaults is still there. The Copyist says he has taken to sitting in that room in the evenings, with the door open, which the Scruples find more frightening than anything he has done in eleven hundred years." { Assert told_comptroller(ossel). }

  // ── Endings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Ending kept "The Kept Promise" when morning() and keptPromise(ossel) "In the spring the old estates of the Moieties along the Ossel are surveyed into strips, and eight thousand soldiers and their families go upriver with ploughs bought on the city's credit, which is now bad, because the city has nothing; but the city kept its word, and the Balance under the sea is level, and the Scruples go back to writing down the small promises of fishwives. The Board meets in a Council House with boarded windows. On the twelfth of Haying there is no procession for the Kneeling. Instead, in the Withies, somebody's mother puts a recruiting bill in the fire, and everyone stands round and watches it burn.".
  Ending release "The Release" when morning() and released(ossel) "The Muster saved the city twice. The second time it paid for the privilege with every penny the city had promised it, and the city knows it, and does not know what to do with the knowledge. The Board votes the Muster a medal. The Muster does not come to collect it. Instead, the veterans of Tessary go to work, on the pans and the boats and in the Lettered Quarter, owing nobody anything, and when the Board next wants a war it finds that nobody in the Withies will answer a drum, and has to think of something else.".
  Ending void "The Void Note" when morning() and noteVoid(ossel) "The note is void and the Muster is home, and the city owes nothing to the Balance and its soldiers everything, as before; the Board will hear the question of the Settlement again in the spring, and this time the public bench will be full. Under the sea the Scruples have a new Comptroller who keeps a hole in the ledger the size of a city in plain sight, and on certain nights, far out past the bar, the sea at Tessary shows other stars. The fishermen have stopped being frightened of it. They say it is good for the eels.".
  Ending torn "The Broken Note" when morning() and noteTorn(ossel) "The note is broken, and the Muster is home, and nobody in Tessary but you knows exactly how. The Scruples enter it as a default by an officer of the Balance, and say nothing more; the Board says nothing at all. In Lowtide the mudlarks say there is a new hollow man in the doorways of the bath-house, in a grey coat, who stands very still and does not come out, and who once, at the turn of the tide, held out a hand ruled like paper to a child, palm up, as if to show it was empty.".
  Ending warden "The Warden of the Settlement" when morning() and saultHoldsNote(ossel) and saultWarden(ossel) "The called come home, and the Muster belongs to Factor Sault, who will never call it; the city's debt has become a debt to one woman, who can count, and does, out loud, at every meeting of the Board. The veterans go upriver to land that is theirs in all but law, under the Warden of the Settlement, who visits every autumn with seed-corn and a ledger. It is not justice. It is something people can live in, which in Tessary is often the best on offer.".
  Ending factor "The Factor's Tessary" when morning() and saultHoldsNote(ossel) and not saultWarden(ossel) "The Muster belongs to Factor Sault. Within the week the Board, which has no army and no money and no more chairs than it has frightened councillors, gives her the Great Seal and the title of Warden of the City. Tessary is better run than it has been in a century. The soldiers are fed and paid and housed, and stand on the Tidewall in her coats, and nobody in the city is sure any more what they would do if they were told to do something terrible, and the soldiers least of all.".
  Ending foreclosure "Foreclosure" when morning() and foreclosed(ossel) "Nothing happens, which is the worst of it. The called stay where they are. The Board says nothing; there is no money to say anything with. The rest of the Muster goes back to the boardwalks and the pans and waits for the next spring ebb, which does not come, because there is nothing left owing, only something forfeit. In the Withies they hang the boots from the eaves of the stilt-houses, pair by pair. And out past the bar, on more nights every month, the sea shows stars that are not Tessary's, very close, and once in the winter something comes up the Swatch on the flood and is found dead on the Pans in the morning, pale and many-jointed and the size of a calf, and not one book in the Lettered Quarter has a word for it; and the Scruples, who might have, have closed the black wall and do not answer.".

  // ── Objectives ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Objective find_davy when knows(party, notice_read) and not knows(party, davy_went) and heldNow(davy) "Nan Teazle of the Withies wants to know where her son Davy went when he walked into the sea.".
  Objective follow_davy when knows(party, davy_went) and not knows(party, held_alive) and heldNow(davy) "Davy Teazle walked into the sea at the spring ebb. Where did he go, and why do the soldiers keep step as they go?".
  Objective why_held when knows(party, held_alive) and not knows(party, collateral) and not matured(ossel) "The soldiers who walk into the sea are held, not dead. Who is holding them, and for what?".
  Objective what_owed when knows(party, collateral) and not knows(party, promise_weight) and not matured(ossel) "The city pledged its soldiers' oaths against a debt. What does it owe, and how can it be paid?".
  Objective pay_it when knows(party, promise_weight) and not voted(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "The War Note is paid if the city keeps its promise of land and a pension to every soldier who came home. The Board votes on the thirteenth day, and has no money.".
  Objective save_durrance when knows(party, durrance_next) and night(ossel) < 8 and not durranceSafe() and not heldNow(durrance) "Sergeant Durrance is on the next page of the roll, and will walk into the sea at the eighth night's spring ebb.".
  Objective carry_deeds when knows(party, deeds_for_held) and not deedsDelivered(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "The deeds of the called must be put into their hands in the Holding before the note falls due at two in the morning after the Feast.".
  Objective feast_release when releaseCalled(ossel) and not released(ossel) and not releaseBroken(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "Durrance will call the Muster to the Oath Stone on the night of the Feast, to release the city. The Factor's lightermen will come.".
  Objective feast_assembly when indictmentFiled(ossel) and not noteVoid(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "The Assembly of the Scruples sits in the Weighing Chamber from midnight on the night of the Feast. The Valuer asked you to be there.".
  Objective sault_bid_known when knows(party, sault_bid) and not matured(ossel) and not saultWarden(ossel) and not saultStopped(ossel) "Factor Sault means to take up the War Note when it falls in, and govern Tessary with the Muster.".

  // The module is seen through when the note is discharged, or held by a Warden sworn to send the Muster home.
  Goal discharged(ossel) or saultWarden(ossel) and saultHoldsNote(ossel).
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/histor:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── What the city remembers, and what it has forgotten ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Tessary counts its years from the Drowning: it is the year 1144 of the Drowning. Four hundred years of mud-huts on
  // the ridge before anyone dared build a wall on the old one; the Oath Stone hauled up out of the basin in the 942nd
  // year; and forty years ago the Salt War, against the fen-reeves of Carrabay, for which the city raised its First
  // Muster and promised it land on the south bank of the Ossel. It gave the First Muster a plaque, and the right to
  // rake the pans in perpetuity. Factor Sault's father raked salt.

  Observe tidewall_datestone at tidewall when not visitedBefore(tidewall) "Where the city's courses begin on the Aenean ones, the parapet is painted with a ladder of white bars, each with a year of the Drowning beside it: the Grey Water of 711, the Long Spring of 902, the Salt Flood of 1104, each bar higher than the one before. The fishermen touch the top bar for luck going out. Below the lowest, where the old city's stone begins, there is a bar in another paint, very faded, older than all of them, with no year.".
  Observe tidewall_stars at tidewall when dark() "Lanterns along the parapet, and fishermen under them, talking low. One of them says, not to you, that the stars past the bar were wrong again last night, the whole sky of them, close as lamps. The man next to him tells him to shut his mouth and mind his line.".
  Observe terraces_plaque at terraces when not visitedBefore(terraces) "By the Council House steps a bronze plaque, green with salt, is set into the wall at knee height, where nobody reads it: TO THE FIRST MUSTER OF THE SALT WAR, WHO KEPT THE CITY. THE CITY WILL NEVER FORGET. IN THE 1104th YEAR OF THE DROWNING.".
  Observe terraces_plaque_again at terraces when visitedBefore(terraces) and knows(party, first_muster) "The First Muster's plaque by the Council House steps, at knee height, green with salt.".
  Observe pans_rakers at pans when not dark() "The rakers are old, most of them, and stoop the same way. One has a soldier's cap badge pinned to his hat, so green you can hardly see the crossed keys on it: the badge of a regiment nobody under fifty remembers.".
  Discovery first_muster "Forty years ago, for the Salt War against the fen-reeves of Carrabay, Tessary raised a First Muster and promised it land on the south bank of the Ossel. It gave the First Muster a bronze plaque and the right to rake the city's salt-pans in perpetuity. Factor Sault's father was one of them." {
    Known by sault, tolley.
  }
  Topic tolley_first with tolley "Ask Brother Ancel about the old rakers on the Pans" when true once {
    Says "'The First Muster,' says Ancel. 'What is left of it. The Salt War, forty years back. They were promised land on the south bank, and the Board voted them a plaque instead, and the rakes, and called it generous.' He looks up at the hanging weights. 'Half the brass up there is theirs. Their wives hung them. Factor Sault's mother hung one, I'm told, the year Imma was born. It is still there. They dust round it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, first_muster). }
  }

  // The saint's sayings: the oldest thing in the chapel, and the first word anyone in Tessary spoke of a default.
  Discovery evenhand_saying "Saint Evenhand used to say that the sea did not drown the old city: a promise did. Asked whose, he wept, which is the only time his book says he wept." {
    Known by tolley.
  }
  Topic tolley_saying with tolley "Ask Brother Ancel what the saint said about the Drowning" when knows(actor, evenhand_tale) once {
    Says "Ancel takes a small book from the altar, so old the boards have gone soft as cloth. 'His sayings,' he says. 'Taken down by the first brothers. Most of them are about weights and measures.' He turns to a page he does not have to look for. 'Not the sea. A promise drowned the old city.' He closes the book. 'They asked him whose promise, and he wept. Seven hundred years of brothers have argued about what he meant. I think he meant exactly what he said. He could not do otherwise.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, evenhand_saying). }
  }
  // The worn letters on the Watersteps, which are the beginning of the formula on the Hall's wall.
  Discovery steps_letters "The worn letters on the Watersteps are Aenean: WHO COMES TO THE LEDGER, and the rest worn away. The Steps were an instrument of the Balance once, like the Oath Stone, and a little of them still is: what is sworn on them is held.".
  Topic tally_steps with tally "Ask the Valuer what the letters on the Steps say" when at(tally, tideline_steps) or travelsWith(tally, actor) and at(actor, tideline_steps) once {
    Says "The Valuer does not need to bend. 'Who comes to the ledger,' they say. 'The rest is worn away by feet. These steps were an instrument once, as the Stone in your Yard was. They are a very old one, and very tired, but they still hold a little.' They look down at the water. 'It is why the called come this way. The calling goes by the old roads. And it is why, when a ferryman swears on these steps that he will not drink, we write it down.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, steps_letters). }
  }

  // ── The city under the city ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // New Tessary was built on the old one's plan, street over street, because the old walls were the only stone on the
  // ridge to build on. From Lowtide, looking up, you see it.
  Observe forum_under at forum when lowWater() and not dark() and not visitedBefore(forum) "You know this square. It takes a moment to see why: it is the Landgate's square, its three corners, its slope, exactly, laid out down here in stone eleven hundred years older, with the sky where the bill-board should be. Up over the Tidewall's edge you can see the Landgate's own roofs, standing where these roofs stood.".
  Observe forum_pool at forum when lowWater() and not dark() "In the fountain's broken basin a sheet of standing water holds the sky, and in it, upside down and perfectly still, the Tidewall and the roofs of Tessary. The mudlark children walk round it, never across. The city in the pool, they say, has people of its own, who walk with their feet on the sky and keep every promise they make, and want you to come down and live with them.".
  Observe scales_under at scales_street when not visitedBefore(scales_street) "It runs where Scriveners' Row runs above, and bends where the Row bends, by the width of a cart. Scales here, on every counter; seals there, on every desk.".
  Observe court_hollow at oath_court when not benighted(party) "In the end wall, at the height of a man, there is a hollow cut into the black stone: square-edged and clean, a slab's breadth and a man's height and a hand deep, the shape of something that was cut out of this wall and taken away. You have seen that shape. It stands on a plinth in the Legion Yard, directly over your head, with eleven thousand handprints worn into it.".
  Topic pounce_copies with pounce "Ask Pounce why every contract in Tessary is drawn twice" when true once {
    Says "'Two parties, two copies,' says Pounce. 'One each. Every child knows that.' He sands a line. 'The old people said the ledger under the sea keeps a third, which is why a Tessarine will swear on his mother's grave and then look at the floor.' He sets the pen down. 'This whole city is a second copy, you know. Drawn on the old one, street for street. The original is filed under four fathoms of water at the bottom of the basin.' He snorts. 'And we still argue about the boundaries.'".
  }

  // ── The bell of the old city ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The mudlarks have looked for the drowned city's bell for a thousand years. It is not in Lowtide. On storm nights
  // the Withies hear it under the basin. It is on the white floor, with a tag.
  Observe forum_tower at forum when not visitedBefore(forum) "At the Forum's east side stands the stump of a bell-tower, roofless, its bell-frame empty. Every mudlark in Tessary has dug under it at one time or another. There is nothing there.".
  Thing old_bell "the bell of the old city" at far_edge {
    State hanging "On a frame of black timber at the very edge of the floor hangs a bell taller than a man, green with the sea that never touched it, with a tag on its rope the size of a shield: the bell of the Aenean city, pledged by its magistrates as surety for the compact, forfeit in the year of the Drowning.".
    State humming "The old city's bell is still humming on its frame at the edge of the floor.".
    Change ring "Haul on the bell-rope" from hanging to humming.
  }
  Relation bellHeard(place).
  Event bell_rings at far_edge when state(old_bell, humming) "The bell swings, slowly, and speaks: a note so low it is more a pressure than a sound, and it goes out across the white floor and past the edge into the dark where the nine lights hang, and does not come back. Far behind you, through the Door, faintly, you think you hear water move." then {
    Assert bellHeard(ossel). }
  Rule bell_heard_above when bellHeard(ossel) and inTessary() and not spread(bell_news)
    says "They are talking about it in the Withies: the bell under the basin rang last night, with no storm and no wind, and every dog on the boardwalks howled. Wick is unbearable about it." { Assert spread(bell_news). }
  Entity bell_news: fact "the bell under the basin".
  Rule bell_resets when state(old_bell, humming) and not at(party, far_edge) { Assert state(old_bell, hanging). }
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/holdin:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── The Holding ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Where pledged things are kept against their promises, and forfeit things for ever: beyond the Balance, a white
  // floor under no sky. Everything here has a tag. (A contribution to Imbar's cosmology for canon review: the Kept's
  // tradition, not a narrator's fact. See doc/adventures/what-tessary-owes/03-revised-design.md.)
  Place holding_plane "the Holding" is plane.
  Place white_floor "the white floor" is region within holding_plane.
  Place holding "the Holding" is site within white_floor at 0, 0.
  Place threshold "the threshold of the Holding" is room within holding at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place sheaves "the field of sheaves" is room within holding at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place folded_lake "the folded lake" is room within holding at 2, 0 outdoors.
  Place notary_desk "the Notary's desk" is room within holding at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place tags "the avenue of tags" is room within holding at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place ranks "the Ranks" is room within holding at 1, 2 outdoors.
  Place far_edge "the far edge" is room within holding at 2, 2 outdoors.

  // The Door stands open on the night of the Settlement; at other times only to the Valuer and whoever goes with
  // them, or to whomever the Comptroller admits.
  Relation holdingAdmits(group).
  Query doorOpen() means feastEve() and hour(clock) >= 18 or night(ossel) >= 15 or travelsWith(tally, party) or holdingAdmits(party).
  Passage holding_door "the Door of the Holding" is passage between weighing_chamber and threshold
    opening when doorOpen() "The Door of the Holding stands at the end of the nave with the white floor showing through it, and when you walk toward it you do not come any nearer.".
  Passage floor_n "the white floor" is passage between threshold and sheaves taking 10 minutes.
  Passage floor_lake "the white floor" is passage between sheaves and folded_lake taking 10 minutes.
  Passage floor_desk "the white floor" is passage between threshold and notary_desk taking 10 minutes.
  Passage floor_tags "the white floor" is passage between notary_desk and tags taking 10 minutes.
  Passage floor_sheaves_tags "the white floor" is passage between sheaves and tags taking 10 minutes.
  Passage floor_ranks "the white floor" is passage between tags and ranks taking 10 minutes.
  Passage floor_edge "the white floor" is passage between ranks and far_edge taking 30 minutes.
  Passage floor_lake_edge "the white floor" is passage between folded_lake and far_edge taking 30 minutes.

  Observe threshold_scene at threshold when true "You step through and there is no sky. There is a floor, white, faintly ruled, going on in every direction until it is too far to see, and there is a light that comes from nowhere and casts no shadows. Behind you the Door stands on its own, with the nave of the Weighing Chamber dim inside it like a room seen through a window at night. Ahead, in rows that go on past seeing, things stand on the floor with tags tied to them.".
  Observe sheaves_scene at sheaves when true "A field of sheaves, standing in stooks on the white floor, gold and dry and smelling of August: a harvest, a whole country's harvest, acres of it. The tag on the nearest stook is old leather, and the writing on it says, in a script like the Scruples', a king's word that his people would not starve, given in a year of famine, and broken.".
  Observe lake_scene at folded_lake when true "A lake, folded. That is the only way to say it: a lake has been folded like linen, in squares, and laid on the floor in a stack higher than a house, and you can see through the folds the reeds and the fish and a little boat, very small and perfectly still, caught between two layers of water. Its tag is the size of a door.".
  Observe tags_scene at tags when true "An avenue of tags with nothing tied to them: little white tags on cords, hanging from a rail at the height of your eyes, thousands of them, stirring though there is no wind. Each has a name on it in the ruled script. These are the names of the Scruples, pledged at their births. Some are very old. Some are new, and the ink still wet.".
  Observe ranks_scene at ranks when true "The Ranks. Soldiers of the Long Muster, standing in files on the white floor as if on parade, barefoot, in their shirts, their eyes closed, their hands at their sides. They are breathing, very slowly, all together. There are a hundred and fifty of them, and more; there are faces you have seen on the boardwalks of the Withies, and faces you have seen only on the Valuer's pages. Nobody has tied tags to them. Their tags are in the Weighing Chamber, in the pan.".
  Observe desk_scene at notary_desk when true "A white desk stands on the white floor with nothing round it for a long way in any direction: a clerk's desk, sloped, with an inkwell, and a rail behind it hung with keys that have no doors. There is no chair. Whoever works here does not sit.".
  Observe durrance_held near durrance when heldNow(durrance) and at(durrance, ranks) and asleep(durrance) "At the end of the Third Company's file, a little apart, as a sergeant stands, Thomasin Durrance is asleep on her feet, barefoot, with her chin up as if on parade.".
  Observe davy_held near davy when heldNow(davy) and asleep(davy) "In the Third Company's file, between a big man with a burned hand and a boy who cannot be more than seventeen, Davy Teazle is asleep in his shirt. His feet are bare and very white. He looks cold.".
  Observe edge_scene at far_edge when true "The floor ends. It does not drop away; it stops, and beyond it is dark that is not night, and in the dark, very far off, there are nine points of black light, arranged in no shape you know, perfectly still. They do not twinkle. The cold comes off them the way cold comes off a cellar door, and it smells of iron. You find you have counted them three times.".
  Observe ranks_count at ranks when held(ossel) > 150 "The files are longer than they were. New faces at the ends of them, in their shirts, with their eyes closed.".

  // The Notary: the Balance's own clerk, who keeps the Holding and sits with the Assembly at a Settlement.
  Person notary "the Notary" at notary_desk {
    Role "a figure at a white desk, made of fine ruled lines of light, as a drawing of a clerk is made of lines". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns it. Manner stoic.
    Greets "The figure at the desk looks up. It has no face, only the lines where a face would be drawn, very close together, and when it speaks the lines move. 'Weighed,' it says, in a voice like a page turning. 'Come in. Everything here is accounted for.'".
    Greets again "The Notary's lines draw closer together, which is its way of attending. 'Weighed,' it says again, and on the white desk a page you did not see it write lies face down. 'What you owe is smaller than when you left. It will be larger when you return. That is not a threat. It is interest.'".
  }
  Topic notary_place with notary "Ask the Notary what this place is" when true once {
    Says "'The Holding,' says the Notary. 'Where what is pledged is kept against the promise it was pledged for, until the promise is kept or released, and where what is forfeit is kept for ever.' Its lines move. 'A harvest. A lake. A singer's voice, in a jar, over there; she pledged it against her lover's return, and he came home, and she has never come for it. I do not know why. People are not always in a hurry for what is theirs.'".
  }
  Topic notary_lights with notary "Ask the Notary about the nine black lights at the far edge" when true once {
    Says "The Notary's lines draw close together, and one of them goes out. 'Security,' it says. 'For the oldest promise this floor holds.' It puts the line back. 'I do not discuss the terms. They are being kept. At one place the keeping is slack, and I think you have walked on it.'".
  }
  Topic notary_redeem with notary "Ask the Notary how the called may be redeemed" when true once {
    Says "'Three ways,' says the Notary. 'The debt is paid, and all that was pledged for it goes home. The debt is released, by the one it is owed to, and all goes home. Or a single thing is redeemed by another pledge of its weight, laid on this desk.' It turns a page that is not there. 'A soldier's oath weighs about what a person's name weighs, and everything they carry of worth. I make that observation to everyone who asks. Very few people ask twice.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, redeem_by_pledge). }
  }
  Discovery redeem_by_pledge "In the Holding a single held thing may be redeemed by laying another pledge of its weight on the Notary's desk: a soldier's oath weighs about what a person's name weighs, and everything they carry of worth.".
  Topic notary_comptroller with notary "Ask the Notary about the Comptroller's default" when knows(actor, note_designed) once {
    Says "'Entered in his hand eleven hundred years ago,' says the Notary. 'An honest entry.' The lines of its face do not move at all. 'The note he drew for your city was not honest. I hold what I am given. I do not choose what I am given. If the Assembly sits at the Settlement and finds the note drawn to be broken, I will hold that too.' A pause. 'He has been very unhappy. I make that observation as well.'".
  }
  // A goose, pledged in a wager three hundred years ago and forfeit, who has views.
  Person old_goose "a goose" at sheaves {
    Role "a grey goose with a tag round its neck, three hundred years forfeit". Species goose_kind. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
  }
  Observe old_goose_scene near old_goose when at(old_goose, sheaves) "Among the sheaves a grey goose is eating a king's harvest, one grain at a time, with the air of someone who has been doing it for a very long while and intends to go on. The tag round her neck says she was wagered on a horse-race in the Ossel country three hundred and four years ago, by a miller, who lost. When she sees you she hisses, on principle.".
  Topic notary_goose with notary "Ask the Notary about the goose" when true once {
    Says "'Forfeit,' says the Notary. 'A miller wagered her on a horse and the horse lost. She is the property of the Balance. She has eaten approximately a third of the harvest of Old Ennelmark.' Its lines move in a way that might be a sigh. 'Nothing forfeit to the Holding ages. Nothing in the Holding can be made to leave it. I have tried.'".
  }

  // ── The called ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person held_files "the called of the Long Muster" at ranks {
    Role "soldiers asleep on their feet, in files". Ancestry human. Numbers 1. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
  }
  Initially Assert asleep(held_files).
  Person davy "Davy Teazle" at ranks {
    Role "a private of the Long Muster, nineteen, the youngest of the Third". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "Davy Teazle is standing very straight with his boots wet to the ankle and his eyes on the middle distance, and it takes him the length of a breath to bring them to you. He seems to be trying to remember whether you are someone he dreamed.".
    Greets again "Davy Teazle has turned his face to the sea, and it takes a hand on his shoulder to bring it round. 'It is you,' he says, relieved, like a man finding his own door in the dark. 'Don't leave me alone with the tide. It talks when it thinks I am asleep.'".
  }
  Initially Assert asleep(davy). Initially Assert heldNow(davy).
  Relation davyWoke(place).
  Action wake_davy(actor: group, site: place) "Lay Davy's coat over his shoulders" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(davy, site) and carries(actor, davy_coat)
      and heldNow(davy) and not davyWoke(ossel).
    On success { Assert davyWoke(ossel). Retract asleep(davy). }
    Result "You put the red coat round his shoulders, the darned elbow and all, and he shivers once, the whole length of him, and opens his eyes. 'Mam?' he says. Then he sees you, and the white floor, and the files of sleepers going away on either side of him, and his face does the thing a face does when a dream turns out not to be one. 'I put my boots together,' he says. 'Didn't I? She'll never believe it.'".
  }
  Topic davy_talk with davy "Ask Davy what it is like here" when davyWoke(ossel) and heldNow(davy) once {
    Says "'Like standing guard,' says Davy. 'Only nobody comes to relieve you.' He pulls the coat round himself. 'I can't move my feet. I've tried. I can hear the others breathing. Sometimes somebody talks in his sleep, the Lucey twins mostly, they always did.' He looks at you. 'Are we coming home? Tell me straight. The army never told anyone anything straight.'".
  }
  Rule davy_sleeps_again when davyWoke(ossel) and heldNow(davy) and not at(party, ranks) { Assert asleep(davy). }
  Rule davy_wakes_again when davyWoke(ossel) and heldNow(davy) and at(party, ranks) and asleep(davy) { Retract asleep(davy). }

  // Durrance, if she was taken: her own oath, said to her to its last words, wakes her.
  Relation durranceWoke(place).
  Action wake_durrance(actor: group, site: place) "Say the Muster's oath to Durrance, to the very end: 'until it release me'" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(durrance, site) and heldNow(durrance)
      and knows(actor, oath_words) and not durranceWoke(ossel).
    On success { Assert durranceWoke(ossel). Retract asleep(durrance). }
    Result "You say it into her face, the way she said it to you in the Drum: I swear to keep the city of Tessary, its walls and its people, while I live or until it release me. At release her eyes open. She looks at you for a long moment without knowing you, and then knowing you. 'Until it release me,' she says. 'Nobody ever listens to that part.' She tries to move her feet, and cannot. 'Well,' she says. 'Here I am, then. Where's the one doing the calling? I said I'd like to look at them.'".
  }
  Rule durrance_sleeps_again when durranceWoke(ossel) and heldNow(durrance) and not at(party, ranks) { Assert asleep(durrance). }
  Rule durrance_wakes_again when durranceWoke(ossel) and heldNow(durrance) and at(party, ranks) and asleep(durrance) { Retract asleep(durrance). }

  // The deeds of the called, put into their hands before the Settlement: the city's promise, kept to every soldier.
  Action deliver_deeds(actor: group, site: place) "Go down the files putting a sealed deed into every hand" {
    Description "A hundred and sixty-odd deeds, name by name. It will take a while.".
    Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, ranks) and carries(actor, held_deeds)
      and not deedsDelivered(ossel) and not matured(ossel).
    On success { Assert deedsDelivered(ossel). }
    Result "You go down the files with the casket open, reading the names off the deeds, finding the faces. Pargeter. Haskett. Moll Bryer. The Lucey twins, side by side. Teazle, D. Every hand takes the paper as you put it there, the way a sleeping hand will close on whatever is put in it, and holds it. When you come to the end of the last file the casket is empty, and all down the Ranks, very faintly, there is a sound like a great many people breathing out.".
  }

  // ── The pledge ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // One pledge to a person, for there is one name to a person: laid on the Notary's desk, it redeems one held thing.
  Relation pledgedSelf(group). Relation redeemedBy(group, group). Relation tallyFreed(place). Relation tallyNameFound(group).
  Observe tally_tag at tags when knows(party, tally_name_known) and not tallyFreed(ossel) "In the ninth row, near the end, a tag hangs whose ink is twenty-nine years old. You know it is the Valuer's before you read it. It is a short name. It would sound strange in Tessary, and then, after a while, it would not.".
  Discovery tally_name_known "The Valuer's name hangs in the avenue of tags in the Holding, pledged at their birth.".
  Topic tally_name with tally "Ask the Valuer what their name is" when tallySawDefaults(ossel) and not knows(actor, tally_name_known) once {
    Says "The Valuer looks at you for a long time. 'It is held,' they say. 'In the ninth row of the avenue of tags. I have never seen it. One is not shown one's name.' A pause. 'I find, since the Room of Defaults, that I would like to know what it is. I note that. I do not know what to do with it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, tally_name_known). }
  }
  Action pledge_for_davy(actor: group, site: place) "Lay your name and everything you carry of worth on the Notary's desk, to redeem Davy Teazle" {
    Speaker notary. Time 1 minute.
    Grave "A name pledged to the Holding is held. It is not given back.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(notary, site) and knows(actor, redeem_by_pledge)
      and heldNow(davy) and not pledgedSelf(actor) and not discharged(ossel).
    On success { Assert pledgedSelf(actor). Assert redeemedBy(davy, actor). Set quantity(actor, gold) to 0. Assert registered(actor). }
    Result "You say your name, the whole of it, and the Notary writes it on a tag, and ties the tag to the rail with the others, and it hangs there stirring. 'Held,' it says. 'Teazle, D., redeemed.' Your purse is empty; you did not see it go. When you try to think of your own name it is there, still, but at a distance, like a word in a language you used to speak. 'You will be called something,' says the Notary. 'People always are.'".
  }
  Action pledge_for_durrance(actor: group, site: place) "Lay your name and everything you carry of worth on the Notary's desk, to redeem Thomasin Durrance" {
    Speaker notary. Time 1 minute.
    Grave "A name pledged to the Holding is held. It is not given back.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(notary, site) and knows(actor, redeem_by_pledge)
      and heldNow(durrance) and not pledgedSelf(actor) and not discharged(ossel).
    On success { Assert pledgedSelf(actor). Assert redeemedBy(durrance, actor). Set quantity(actor, gold) to 0. Assert registered(actor). }
    Result "You say your name, the whole of it, and the Notary writes it on a tag and ties it to the rail. 'Held,' it says. 'Durrance, A., redeemed.' Your purse is empty. Your own name, when you reach for it, is there, but at a distance, like the name of a town you passed through once.".
  }
  Action pledge_for_tally(actor: group, site: place) "Lay your name and everything you carry of worth on the Notary's desk, to redeem the Valuer's name" {
    Speaker notary. Time 1 minute.
    Grave "A name pledged to the Holding is held. It is not given back. The Valuer's, redeemed, is theirs.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(notary, site) and knows(actor, redeem_by_pledge)
      and knows(actor, tally_name_known) and not tallyFreed(ossel) and not pledgedSelf(actor) and not tallyUnravelled(ossel).
    On success { Assert pledgedSelf(actor). Assert tallyFreed(ossel). Set quantity(actor, gold) to 0. Assert registered(actor). }
    Result "The Notary goes down the avenue of tags without seeming to walk, and comes back with one small white tag in the lines of its hand, and lays it on the desk, and ties yours in its place. 'A Scruple's name, redeemed,' it says. 'That has not happened before.' Its lines move. 'They will not be able to lie any more easily than they could. But they will be able to leave.'".
  }
  Relation tallyUnravelled(place).
  Rule redeemed_go_home when redeemedBy(?s, ?c) and heldNow(?s) {
    Retract heldNow(?s). Retract asleep(?s). Assert cameHome(?s). Assert wokeHome(?s). }
  Relation wokeHome(group).
  Rule davy_home when wokeHome(davy) and at(davy, ranks) { Retract at(davy, ranks). Assert at(davy, teazle_room). }
  Rule durrance_home when wokeHome(durrance) and at(durrance, ranks) { Retract at(durrance, ranks). Assert at(durrance, drum_taproom). }
  Rule comptroller_redeems when redeemedByComptroller(davy) and heldNow(davy) and lowWater() and dark() {
    Retract heldNow(davy). Retract asleep(davy). Assert cameHome(davy). Assert wokeHome(davy). }
  Rule davy_back_told when wokeHome(davy) and not knows(party, davy_back) and inTessary()
    says "Word runs along the Withies faster than the tide: Davy Teazle woke up on the Watersteps in his shirt with his boots beside him, and walked home, and put his boots on the mat inside his mother's door, side by side." teaches davy_back { }
  Discovery davy_back "Davy Teazle has come home to the Withies.".
  Event nan_pays near nan when knows(party, davy_back) and nanOffer(party) and not nanPaid(party) "Nan Teazle puts a tin in your hands without a word. Nine coin in it. Davy is asleep in the cupboard bed behind her, in his coat, with his boots on." then {
    Increase quantity(party, gold) by 9. Assert nanPaid(party). }
  Event nan_pays_knowing near nan when toldNan(party) and nanOffer(party) and heldNow(davy) "Before you go, Nan Teazle puts a tin in your hands. 'Nine coin,' she says. 'You told me where he is. That was the bargain.'" then {
    Increase quantity(party, gold) by 9. Assert nanPaid(party). }
  Relation nanPaid(group).
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/lore.k:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  Description "Links outward from the Ossel: a ship's people with no papers, the Valuer shown a writ that says kept, a Factor's packet for the Tolleth packet, and a Collegium surveyor with a chain.".

  // ── A world event, read: the queue at the Office of Seals ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe lore_queue_ship at seals_hall when befell(remainder_harboured) "The queue has a new rumour, which it is passing back along itself like a bucket: a ship's company, given harbour in the south, who have kept their own accounts for eleven generations and cannot say to whom they owe the first page. The queue's view is that this is the most terrible thing it has ever heard, and the queue would like to know whether they have a number.".

  // ── A visitor from elsewhere: a writ that says kept ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_valuer_kept "The Ninth Valuer, shown a fair copy of a writ that says KEPT, says that the Balance has no column for it, and that a column for it would ruin the Balance.".
  Topic lore_valuer_writ with tally "Show the Ninth Valuer the fair copy of the Prefect's writ" when holding(actor, prefects_writ) once {
    Says "The Valuer reads with a finger, as the faintly ruled do. 'Servandam,' they say, 'to be kept. Not oath-bound, not collateral. There is no mark for this in my book.' They turn a page and show you the columns, owed and paid and in arrears, each ruled to the edge. 'Centuries of Tessarine accounting and this word is not in it. An oath may be pledged, bought, sold, discounted. A thing that is kept may not be.' A pause like a ruler laid down. 'I will not copy this. I will remember it. It is the first thing in a long time I have not known how to enter.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_valuer_kept). }
  }

  // ── An entry point: Factor Sault waits on a shipment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind exchange_ledger "The Exchange's black ledger" is treasure worth 2 described "A slim ledger bound in black calf, in a clerk's hand: sums paid out of the Salt Exchange's strongroom to 'O.N., at the Gap', every month since the spring.".
  Item lore_sault_packet "Factor Sault's sealed packet of accounts" is exchange_ledger at nowhere owned by sault.
  Relation lore_saultPacket(group).
  Topic lore_sault_tolleth with sault "Ask Factor Sault whether anything is wanted carried overseas" when true once {
    Says "'You have a face for a courier,' says Sault, not kindly, and shoves a ledger aside. 'Salt I can sell. What I cannot do is get an answer out of the Orsett factors at Tolleth, who have had my money since the spring and sent me one letter, in which they say a ship is delayed. The ship is the Dorothea, Captain Bascom, and she is delayed in the way a ship is delayed that has been paid twice by two houses.' She seals a packet with a thumb of black wax. 'Take it to Tolleth. There is a board on the quay with her sailings chalked up; if Bascom is not there, the harbour woman will know. Put it in Bascom's hand and in no one else's, least of all the Orsett man's. Tell her the Salt Moiety remembers what is owed.' She considers. 'Say it as a threat. It is not one.'".
    On discuss { Give lore_sault_packet to actor. Assert lore_saultPacket(actor). }
  }

  // ── The Collegium's surveyor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_pym_tessary "A surveyor of the Collegium of Measures, Orlando Pym, found the Causeway four feet longer at low water than the Collegium's tables, and has gone north up the drove road with his chain to the Lull and the Pass at Larum.".
  Topic lore_sedge_pym with sedge "Ask Hannelore Rackham about the man with the chain on the Causeway" when true once {
    Says "'Pym,' says Sedge. 'Surveyor, Collegium of Measures, which weighs things and will tell you so before you ask. He set his chain along the Causeway at low water and found it four feet longer than it was in his tables, and wrote it down, and said the tables were wrong. I said, the tide was wrong. He said the tide is never wrong, it is merely early.' She almost smiles. 'He has gone north with a boy to carry the stake. He wants the Lull, and the Pass beyond it, he says. A man who measures things for his bread will measure anything that holds still.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_pym_tessary). }
  }

  // ── Three things from elsewhere ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_rubbing_valuer "The Ninth Valuer, shown a keeper's tally rubbed from a bench by the sea, has no column for the oldest rows, and enters them as 'unruled'.".
  Topic lore_valuer_rubbing with tally "Show the Ninth Valuer the rubbing of a keeper's tally" when holding(actor, tally_rubbing) once {
    Says "The Valuer follows the rows with one ruled finger, top to bottom, as the faintly ruled do. 'A stroke for a ship, a mark for whatever the sea gave back,' they say. 'And here, nothing owed.' They stop at the oldest rows and do not go on. 'I have no category for these. They are not receipts. They are not debts. They are the other thing, the one that is not in the ledger.' They take out their pen. 'May I enter them as unruled? It is not an honour I give lightly.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_rubbing_valuer). }
  }
  Discovery lore_letter_deckle "Ulric Deckle, Keeper of the Great Seal, shown a letter bearing the seal of the Collegium of Lesser Instruments, says nobody forges it, because nobody wishes to be a friend of working things.".
  Topic lore_deckle_letter with deckle "Show the Keeper the letter of the Collegium of Lesser Instruments" when holding(actor, collegium_letter) once {
    Says "Deckle takes the letter and does not read a word of it. He looks at the seal, a cog in a ring, for a long, professional minute. 'Pressed from the left,' he says. 'Wax too cool when it was struck, so the ring has a seam. A good seal, honestly made, by a hand that does not care how it looks.' 'Nobody has ever forged a seal as plain as that; there is nothing to be got by it.' He gives the letter back the way one hands back a child, and wipes his fingers.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_letter_deckle). }
  }
  Discovery lore_teeth_pitch "Lemuel Pitch, shown a sack of green bronze teeth, says they are not chandler's metal and not ship's metal, and that the grain in them is a clock's.".
  Topic lore_pitch_teeth with pitch "Show Lemuel Pitch the bell-teeth" when holding(actor, bell_teeth) once {
    Says "Pitch takes one tooth between a thumb and a finger and holds it to the lamp, and then bites it, which he never does. 'Bronze,' he says. 'But not tin and copper as my father mixed it. This has something in it besides, and it has been struck, not cast.' He rings it on the counter. The note goes on a very long time. 'I sell old bronze by the pound to a man who does not ask. I would not sell these to him.' He pushes them back across the counter with one finger, and does not look at them again, and from the back of the shop a clock he has never wound seems to tick a little louder.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_teeth_pitch). }
  }
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/lowtid:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── Lowtide ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Eleven hundred years ago the sea came over the Aenean city in a night and kept it. Its streets lie in the outer
  // basin under four fathoms at high water; at low water they drain through the Swatch and stand out for a few hours,
  // weeded, wet, picked over by mudlarks, used by smugglers, and haunted. The Hall of Oaths, the old city's court, is
  // at the bottom of the basin, and the wall at the back of it is the way down to the Strongrooms.
  Place throat_foot "the foot of the Swatch Stair" is room within lowtide at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place colonnade "the Weed Colonnade" is room within lowtide at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place forum "the Drowned Forum" is room within lowtide at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place scales_street "the Street of Scales" is room within lowtide at 2, 1 outdoors.
  Place aqueduct_foot "the foot of the Aqueduct" is room within lowtide at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place aqueduct_top "the top of the Aqueduct" is room within lowtide at 0, 2 outdoors.
  Place landing "the ebb-runners' landing" is room within lowtide at 3, 1 outdoors.
  Place bath_house "the bath-house" is building within lowtide.
  Place bath_hall "the bath-house hall" is room within bath_house at 2, 2.
  Place plunge "the plunge-room" is room within bath_house at 3, 2.
  Place bath_dome "the top of the bath-house dome" is room within lowtide at 2, 3 outdoors.
  Place oath_house "the Hall of Oaths" is building within lowtide.
  Place oath_court "the Hall of Oaths" is room within oath_house at 1, 2.

  Passage throat_stair "the Swatch Stair" is steps between throat_head and throat_foot
    opening when lowWater() "The Swatch Stair goes down into green water and does not come up. The basin is full.".
  Passage colonnade_way "the colonnade" is arch between throat_foot and colonnade.
  Passage forum_steps "the forum steps" is steps between colonnade and forum.
  Passage scales_way "the Street of Scales" is path between forum and scales_street taking 5 minutes.
  Passage aqueduct_way "the lane to the aqueduct" is path between forum and aqueduct_foot taking 5 minutes.
  Passage pier "the broken pier" is passage between aqueduct_foot and aqueduct_top needing climbing or rope
    opening when lowWater() "The broken pier stands up out of the sea. The water is over everything below it.".
  // A company come through the runners' tunnel at high water had walked down the quay steps into the drowned street
  // and been rolled out through the Swatch, three times in an afternoon, until it died (M18-09).
  Passage landing_way "the quay steps" is steps between scales_street and landing
    opening when lowWater() "The quay steps go down into the sea. The Street of Scales is under it, and so is everything else.".
  Passage bath_door "the bath-house door" is doorway between scales_street and bath_hall.
  Passage plunge_arch "the plunge-room arch" is arch between bath_hall and plunge.
  Passage dome_stair "the dome stair" is passage between bath_hall and bath_dome
    opening when lowWater() "The dome stair goes down into black water.".
  Passage hall_steps "the Hall steps" is steps between forum and oath_court.
  Passage runners_tunnel "the ebb-runners' tunnel" is tunnel between landing and cistern taking 20 minutes.
  Initially Assert unlit(plunge). Initially Assert unlit(oath_court).

  // What floods, and what does not: the landing is a raised quay at the tunnel's mouth; the aqueduct and the dome
  // stand above the highest water.
  Relation floods(place).
  Initially Assert floods(throat_foot). Initially Assert floods(colonnade). Initially Assert floods(forum).
  Initially Assert floods(scales_street). Initially Assert floods(aqueduct_foot). Initially Assert floods(bath_hall).
  Initially Assert floods(plunge). Initially Assert floods(oath_court).
  Relation lowtideRoom(place).
  Initially Assert lowtideRoom(throat_foot). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(colonnade). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(forum).
  Initially Assert lowtideRoom(scales_street). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(aqueduct_foot). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(aqueduct_top).
  Initially Assert lowtideRoom(landing). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(bath_hall). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(plunge).
  Initially Assert lowtideRoom(bath_dome). Initially Assert lowtideRoom(oath_court).

  // ── The water ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe water_low near party when at(party, ?p) and floods(?p) and lowWater() and not turning() "Water stands in the low places and runs in the gutters, going out. Somewhere far off, toward the Swatch, the sea is a long way away.".
  Observe water_turning near party when at(party, ?p) and floods(?p) and turning() "The water in the gutters has stopped running out. Now it is running back. A wet line is creeping up the steps of the nearest house, and from the direction of the Swatch comes a sound like a mill-race opening.".
  Observe table_says near party when at(party, ?p) and floods(?p) and turning() and carries(party, ?t) and itemKind(?t, tide_table) "By Wick's table the basin fills on the hour. The drawing of the wave with teeth is underlined twice.".
  Observe refuge_high near party when at(party, ?p) and lowtideRoom(?p) and not floods(?p) and not lowWater() "The sea is in. Green water lies over Lowtide from the Tidewall to the outer bar, with the tops of colonnades standing up out of it, and gulls on them. You are above it, and will be until the ebb.".
  Hazard drowning "Rolled through the Swatch by the flood" means "Deal (2d4) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (12).".
  Rule swept when at(party, ?p) and floods(?p) and not lowWater()
    says "The flood comes back through the Swatch all at once, a brown wall of it shouldering down the streets. It takes your feet. It takes everything. You are rolled, and dragged, and something hits you, and there is no up; and then there is, and air, and you are being carried out along the pan-dykes with the weed and the timber, and you crawl out at last onto the salt crust east of the city and lie there, coughing up the sea. Your purse is lighter." {
    Retract at(party, ?p). Assert at(party, pans). Assert strikes(drowning, party). Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 3. Assert sweptOnce(party). }
  Relation sweptOnce(group).

  // ── The places ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe throat_foot_scene at throat_foot when not visitedBefore(throat_foot) "The stair comes down the face of the Tidewall into a gully of wet stone and kelp. The noise of the Swatch fills the gully: the basin draining past you through the one deep channel, brown and quick. Ahead, through a gap in the old sea-wall, a street begins.".
  Observe throat_foot_scene_again at throat_foot when visitedBefore(throat_foot) "The foot of the Swatch Stair, loud with the channel.".
  Observe colonnade_scene at colonnade when not visitedBefore(colonnade) "A street of columns, their tops lost, their shafts furred with weed that lies flat in the direction the water went. Between the columns, doorways, full of sand to the lintel. Anemones the colour of raw meat have opened in the wet, and close if you go near.".
  Observe colonnade_scene_again at colonnade when visitedBefore(colonnade) "The Weed Colonnade, its columns furred with weed, anemones in the doorways.".
  Observe forum_scene at forum when not visitedBefore(forum) "The old city's market square, a hundred paces across, paved in great slabs, most of them still there. The fountain in the middle is a heap of stone with a crab on it. On every side the fronts of buildings stand roofless, their windows full of sky. At the south end, broad steps go down to a building with no windows at all.".
  Observe forum_scene_again at forum when visitedBefore(forum) "The Drowned Forum, wide and wet, with the windowless Hall at the bottom of its south steps.".
  Observe forum_larks at forum when lowWater() and not dark() "Mudlarks are working the square with buckets and rakes, children mostly, and a few old men who have been children here for sixty years. They lift their heads to look at you, and go back to work.".
  Observe forum_dark at forum when dark() "In the dark the square is a pale floor, and the buildings round it are holes. Things move in the wet places. There is no sound but the Swatch.".
  Observe scales_scene at scales_street when not visitedBefore(scales_street) "A street of shops, by the look of it: every doorway has a stone counter, and every counter a pair of carved scales. Eleven hundred years have not worn the scales off. At the far end, a quay stands up out of the sand, higher than the street, with steps.".
  Observe scales_scene_again at scales_street when visitedBefore(scales_street) "The Street of Scales, a pair of carved scales on every counter, and the quay at the far end.".
  Observe aqueduct_foot_scene at aqueduct_foot when true "The aqueduct comes in over the basin on three arches from somewhere that is now open sea, and stops in mid-air above a heap of its own fallen stones. One pier still stands to the top. Its stones are stepped and broken; there is a rusted ring set in it, high up, where somebody has knotted rope before.".
  Observe aqueduct_top_scene at aqueduct_top when true "The water-channel along the aqueduct's top is a yard wide and dry, and you can lie in it out of the wind. From here the whole of Lowtide is laid out like a plan: the colonnade, the forum, the dome of the bath-house, the windowless Hall at the bottom of everything, and beyond it all the outer bar, and the sea.".
  Observe bath_hall_scene at bath_hall when true "A hall of benches round a dry basin, under a dome that has kept its roof. Light comes down through the hole at the top of the dome in a white post. Against one wall, a stair winds up inside the dome's thickness. On the other side an arch opens on darkness, and the air that comes out of it is cold and smells of nothing at all.".
  Observe plunge_scene at plunge when true "The plunge-room: a deep square pool, dry, its floor a bed of silt. Round its edge, against the walls, things are standing that look at first like coats hung on pegs, and then do not.".
  Observe dome_scene at bath_dome when true "The dome's top is a broad shallow cap of stone with the light-hole in the middle of it, crusted with gull-lime. It stands above the highest water. People have sat out tides here before: there are names scratched in the stone, and a tally of days.".
  Observe court_scene at oath_court when true "The Hall of Oaths has no windows. It is a long room of black stone, the same black as the Oath Stone in the Legion Yard, dry, except for the sea's tidemark half way up the walls, as if the water had come in and thought better of it. The walls are carved from floor to tidemark with ruled lines, ledger on ledger, and on the end wall, where a judge's seat would be, there is no seat, only an inscription in Aenean letters a foot high, and under it a plain black wall.".

  // ── The ebb-runners ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Factor Sault's people in Lowtide. They work the old city for bronze and dressed stone, run untaxed salt through the
  // cistern, and for ten years carried the city's interest silver down to the Hall of Oaths. They take prisoners:
  // whoever they beat wakes on the Pans.
  Person slake "Bettany Slake" at landing {
    Role "who runs the ebb-runners, in a fisherman's smock with a cutlass through the belt". Ancestry human. Calling thief. Level 3. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "A woman in a smock stands up off a crate with a cutlass in her hand and puts her other hand up, palm out. 'That's far enough,' she says. 'This is a working quay. Five coin for the use of it, or back up the street the way you came, and don't stand there thinking about it.'".
    Comes "'Right,' says Bettany Slake, almost sorry, and the ebb-runners come off the crates.".
    Pleads "Bettany Slake puts her cutlass down on the stones. 'All right,' she says. 'All right. You've made your point.'".
  }
  Person runners "the ebb-runners" at landing {
    Role "three of Bettany Slake's people, with hooks and short clubs". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Numbers 3. Pronouns they.
    Temperament territorial.
  }
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(slake). Initially Assert takesPrisoners(runners).
  Initially Assert serves(runners, slake). Initially Assert serves(slake, sault).
  Observe landing_scene at landing when true "A stone quay at the end of the Street of Scales, high enough that the flood laps its top and goes no further. Crates, coils of rope, a brazier, a long boat drawn up on rollers. A low tunnel goes back into the quay wall, toward the city, with lamps on hooks along it. On a post by the tunnel mouth hangs a board scored with notches.".
  Rule runners_captured when captured(slake, party) or captured(runners, party)
    says "You come round on the salt crust east of the city at the edge of a pan, with a headache and an empty feeling at your belt. Someone has carried you up the tunnel and dumped you here. Someone has also been through your purse." {
    Retract captured(slake, party). Retract captured(runners, party). Retract at(party, landing). Assert at(party, pans).
    Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 5. }
  Topic slake_quay with slake "Ask Bettany Slake what the ebb-runners do" when true once {
    Says "'Salvage,' says Bettany. 'Bronze, dressed stone, whatever the sea's been keeping. All above board, in the Factor's name.' She spits over the edge of the quay. 'And what goes up and down that tunnel is the Factor's business and mine, and not a thing a stranger wants to be curious about, if the stranger likes the shape of his head.'".
  }
  Topic slake_silver with slake "Ask Bettany Slake what she carried to the Hall of Oaths" when knows(actor, collateral) or knows(actor, note_terms) once {
    Says "Bettany looks at you a long moment. 'Silver,' she says. 'Every month for ten years. The city's, in the Factor's boats, down the tunnel and across at the ebb and into the Hall, and left in the niche by the wall, and the next ebb it was gone.' She shrugs. 'Then in the summer there wasn't any silver, and we stopped. And at the next spring ebb the first of them walked past us across the Forum with their eyes open.' She looks away. 'I don't carry anything to that Hall any more. Only the Factor's letters.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sault_courier). }
  }
  Discovery sault_courier "For ten years the ebb-runners carried the city's interest silver, in Factor Sault's boats, down to the Hall of Oaths. The slate on the post is chalked with a month to a stroke, twelve to a row, ten rows, the oldest rubbed nearly away and chalked over again; across the top someone has painted the crossed rakes of the Salt Moiety and the words HALL. NICHE. BY THE MONTH. The Factor has known the whole arrangement from the beginning." {
    Source runners_board "the chalked slate on the post by the tunnel" at landing readable by party.
  }
  Relation slakeLetsPass(group).
  Action pay_slake(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Bettany Slake five coin for the use of her quay" {
    Speaker slake. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(slake, site) and able(slake)
      and not tolerates(slake, actor) and not hostile(slake, actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 5.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Increase quantity(slake, gold) by 5. Assert tolerates(slake, actor). Assert tolerates(runners, actor). Assert slakeLetsPass(actor). }
    Result "Bettany weighs the coins in her palm, and bites one, and pockets them. 'Quay's yours,' she says. 'Don't touch the crates.'".
  }
  Topic slake_factor with slake "Tell Bettany Slake you work for the Factor" when hiredBySault(actor) and not tolerates(slake, actor) once {
    Says "'Do you,' says Bettany. She looks you up and down. 'She said she'd hired someone to go asking. All right. Mind yourself on the quay.' She sits back down on her crate.".
    On discuss { Assert tolerates(slake, actor). Assert tolerates(runners, actor). Assert slakeLetsPass(actor). }
  }
  Thing runners_box "the ebb-runners' lockbox" at landing {
    Holds.
    State locked closed "An iron-bound lockbox is chained to the boat's thwart.".
    State open "The lockbox stands open.".
    Change pick "Pick the lockbox" from locked to open needing lockwork.
    Change smash "Smash the lockbox open" from locked to open needing brawn.
  }
  Item sault_letter "a letter in the Factor's hand" is letter_kind in runners_box.
  Kind letter_kind "a sealed letter" is gear worth 0 weighing 0
    described "A letter folded small and sealed with salt-white wax, stamped with a pair of crossed rakes.".
  // What is seen taken, by those who keep the quay.
  Rule box_watched when state(runners_box, open) and perceives(slake, party) and able(slake) and not hostile(slake, party) and not slakeGaveLetter(ossel)
    says "'Oi,' says Bettany Slake, and her cutlass comes out." { Assert hostile(slake, party). Assert assails(runners, party). }
  Discovery sault_bid "Factor Sault has written to a broker of the Scruples offering to bid for the War Note at its foreclosure, and to pledge her own house to the Balance as surety: 'The Board will not pay. When the Feast passes, I will take up the note, and with it the Muster, and Tessary will be governed by someone who can count.'".
  Action read_letter(actor: group, site: place) "Break the wax and read the Factor's letter" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and carries(actor, sault_letter) and not benighted(actor)
      and not knows(actor, sault_bid).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, sault_bid). }
    Result "It is addressed to the Broker of the Fourth Pan, the Strongrooms, by hand of B. Slake. 'Sir. You will have had my earlier. I repeat my offer: when the city's note falls in at the Feast and is offered at foreclosure, I bid for it, and I will pledge House Sault entire as surety, which your Comptroller will find to weigh what it needs to. The Board will not pay; I have seen to that, and if I had not, the treasury would. I will take up the note and with it the Muster. They will be fed and paid and housed. Tessary will be governed by someone who can count. Burn this. I. Sault, Factor.'".
  }

  // Councillor Haverick's goose, taken off the Terraces by the ebb-runners for their Feast.
  Species goose_kind "a goose" like hen tame described "A big white goose with an orange bill and an opinion of everyone.".
  Person plum "Mistress Plum" at landing {
    Role "a large white goose of the old Paper strain, very much offended". Species goose_kind. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
  }
  Observe plum_crate near plum when at(plum, landing) and not plumLoose(ossel) "In a crate by the brazier a big white goose is hissing steadily at the ebb-runners, who are ignoring it. A ribbon round its neck says PLUM in gold thread.".
  Relation plumLoose(place). Measure distractedUntil(place).
  Action release_plum(actor: group, site: place) "Knock the peg out of the goose's crate" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, landing) and at(plum, landing) and not plumLoose(ossel).
    On success { Assert plumLoose(ossel). Assert acceptsEscort(plum, actor). Assert unseen(actor, slake). Assert unseen(actor, runners).
      Assert tolerates(slake, actor). Assert tolerates(runners, actor). Retract assails(slake, actor). Retract assails(runners, actor).
      Set distractedUntil(ossel) to watch(clock) + 3. }
    Result "The peg comes out and the crate door falls open and Mistress Plum comes out of it like a cannonball, wings out, neck out, screaming, and goes straight for the nearest ebb-runner's ankles. In a moment the whole quay is chasing a goose round the brazier and the goose is winning. Nobody is looking at you at all.".
  }
  Rule distraction_ends when plumLoose(ossel) and watch(clock) >= distractedUntil(ossel) and unseen(party, slake) {
    Retract unseen(party, slake). Retract unseen(party, runners). }
  Rule distraction_over when plumLoose(ossel) and watch(clock) >= distractedUntil(ossel) and tolerates(slake, party) and not slakeLetsPass(party) and not hostile(slake, party) {
    Retract tolerates(slake, party). Retract tolerates(runners, party). }
  Observe plum_loose near plum when plumLoose(ossel) and not following(plum, party) and not plumHome(ossel) "Mistress Plum stands on a bollard with her wings half open, daring anyone to try it.".

  // ── The Forsworn ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Aenean oath-breakers whose bindings unravelled when they broke a promise the Balance held. What is left of them
  // stands in the plunge-room and comes to the sound of swearing, and to whoever has broken a promise held below.
  Species forsworn_kind "a Forsworn" like revenant temperament savage
    described "A thing like a person-shaped hollow, wearing the rags of an Aenean robe. Where its face should be there is a darkness with the texture of torn paper.".
  Person forsworn "the Forsworn" at plunge {
    Role "hollow people in the rags of Aenean robes". Species forsworn_kind. Level 3. Numbers 3. Pronouns they.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "All round the dry pool the things like coats on pegs turn toward your light, without any sound, and hold out their hands, palm up, as if they wanted to be given something. They do not come any nearer. Not yet.".
    Comes "The coats on the pegs come off the walls. They come round the dry pool toward you without any sound at all, with their hands out, as if they wanted to be given something.".
    Lair plunge.
  }
  // A company that has broken a promise held below is followed through Lowtide by the Forsworn, as the tide turns.
  Relation forswornParty(group).
  Rule forsworn_follow when forswornParty(party) and at(party, ?p) and floods(?p) and turning() and able(forsworn) and not at(forsworn, ?p) and not dark()
    says "Something is standing in the nearest doorway that was not there a moment ago: a coat with nobody in it, turned toward you." {
    Retract at(forsworn, plunge). Assert at(forsworn, ?p). Assert assails(forsworn, party). }

  // ── The Hall of Oaths ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery compact_read "The inscription in the Hall of Oaths is the drowned city's compact with the keepers of the Balance: 'THE SEA SHALL NOT HAVE THIS CITY WHILE THE LEDGER KEEPS. WHO COMES TO THE LEDGER COMES TO BE WEIGHED.' The sea had the city all the same.".
  Action read_compact(actor: group, site: place) "Puzzle out the Aenean inscription on the end wall" {
    Time 3.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, oath_court) and not benighted(actor)
      and not knows(actor, compact_read) and not travelsWith(tally, actor).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, compact_read). }
    Result "Letter by letter, with the ruled walls watching. The Aenean is formal, legal, very old, and plain once you have the first word: THE SEA SHALL NOT HAVE THIS CITY WHILE THE LEDGER KEEPS. And under it, smaller, over the black wall: WHO COMES TO THE LEDGER COMES TO BE WEIGHED. You look up at the tidemark half way up the walls, and think about the sea, and what it had.".
    Otherwise "You can make out a word here and there, CITY and SEA and something that might be LEDGER or might be SCALES, but the sense of it slides away from you in the dark.".
  }
  Observe tally_reads at oath_court when travelsWith(tally, party) and not knows(party, compact_read) and not benighted(party) "The Valuer stops in front of the end wall and reads it aloud, in a flat clear voice, as a clerk reads a clause. 'The sea shall not have this city while the ledger keeps. Who comes to the ledger comes to be weighed.' They are quiet a moment. 'That is the compact of the old city with the Balance. It is a famous text. I have never seen it.' Another pause. 'The sea had the city. I had not thought about that before.'" teaches compact_read.
  // The black wall: open to the Scruples, to the called, and to whoever says the words on it and means them.
  Relation weighedAt(group, place).
  Action say_words(actor: group, site: place) "Put your hand on the black wall and say 'I come to the ledger to be weighed'" {
    Grave "The words are written on a wall that hears them. Below, what you say is held to.".
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, oath_court) and knows(actor, compact_read)
      and not weighedAt(actor, oath_court) and not barredBelow(actor).
    On success { Assert weighedAt(actor, oath_court). Assert registered(actor). }
    Result "The stone is warm under your hand, warm as a sleeping animal. You say the words, and for a moment you feel it: a weighing, as if you were standing in one pan of a scale with something enormous in the other, and the beam lifting, considering. Then the wall under your hand is not there.".
  }
  Relation registered(group).
  Passage black_wall "the black wall" is passage between oath_court and long_stair
    opening when (travelsWith(tally, party) or weighedAt(party, oath_court) or registered(party)) and not barredBelow(party) "A plain wall of black stone, warm to the touch, with no door in it.".
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/people:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── What can be known ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The facts of the adventure, in the order a company is likely to come by them. Each is a step in what the
  // vanishings turn out to be.
  Discovery notice_read "Nan Teazle of the Withies will give her savings for news of her son, who walked into the sea. The notice is in a careful, laboured hand, pressed hard into cheap paper: 'MY SON PRIVATE DAVY TEAZLE OF THE LONG MUSTER WENT DOWN THE TIDELINE STEPS INTO THE SEA AT THE LAST SPRING EBB. HE SET HIS BOOTS ON THE TOP STEP. WHO CAN TELL ME WHERE HE WENT I WILL GIVE MY SAVINGS. NOT A BODY. WHERE HE WENT. NAN TEAZLE, THE WITHIES, BY THE DRUM.'" {
    Source notice "a notice on the Landgate board" at landgate readable by party.
  }
  Discovery enlist_promise "Eleven years ago, raising the Long Muster, the city of Tessary promised land and a pension to every soldier who came home. It was cried in every square and printed on every bill." {
    Known by nan, durrance, marrable, quire, sault.
  }
  Discovery hall_of_oaths_way "The called walk out across the drained basin to the Hall of Oaths in Lowtide and go in at a wall where there is no door." {
    Known by wick.
  }
  Discovery roll_order "The called go in the order of the Long Muster's roll, Third Company first, a dozen at each spring ebb." {
    Known by durrance, tally.
  }
  Discovery durrance_next "Sergeant Thomasin Durrance is on the next page of the roll. Unless something changes she will be called at the eighth night's spring ebb." {
    Known by durrance, tally.
  }
  Discovery council_knows "Treasurer Quire keeps a list, in his own hand, of every veteran called since the summer, a hundred and thirty-eight names, each with an address in the Withies or the Eel quarter, and against each a column of sums: four marks, four marks, four marks, every month since the summer. Nobody sends money to the mothers of deserters." {
    Source quire_list "a list in the Treasurer's hand, under a paperweight" at exchequer_room readable by party.
  }
  Discovery collateral "The Muster's oaths, sworn on the Oath Stone, were pledged as security on a debt the city owes to the keepers of an engine under the sea. At each spring ebb a dozen are taken as interest." {
    Known by tally, quire, sault, comptroller.
  }
  Discovery note_terms "The War Note: ten years ago, when the war was a year old, Tessary borrowed, from the Scruples who keep the Balance under the sea, the right to call an oath King Amaury's ancestor swore to the Aenean emperors at Aen-Vessaly. The Long Muster's oaths were pledged as collateral; interest was paid in silver each month; the principal falls due at the Feast of Settlement in the twelfth year, and may be paid only in a kept promise of equal weight." {
    Known by tally, quire, sault, comptroller.
  }
  Discovery promise_weight "In the Scruples' reckoning only a promise of a whole people to a whole people weighs as much as the War Note, and Tessary has made one such promise: land and a pension for every soldier who came home. If the city keeps it, the debt is paid." {
    Known by tally, comptroller.
  }
  Discovery held_alive "The called are not dead. They are held in the Holding, beyond the Balance, standing asleep, until their oaths are redeemed." {
    Known by tally, comptroller.
  }
  Discovery kneeling_felt "King Amaury did not kneel at Sedge Ford of his own will. He felt a hand on the back of his neck, he says, nine hundred years old, and his knees went into the river." {
    Known by amaury.
  }
  Discovery kneeling_bought "The Kneeling at Sedge Ford was bought: Tessary called in an oath Amaury's ancestor swore to the Aenean emperors, borrowed from under the sea, and the king's body kept his ancestor's word.".
  Discovery oath_words "The Muster's oath, sworn hand on the Oath Stone: 'I swear to keep the city of Tessary, its walls and its people, while I live or until it release me.'" {
    Known by durrance, marrable, fisk.
  }
  Discovery evenhand_tale "Saint Evenhand, say the brothers of his chapel, was a clerk who came up out of the sea when the old city drowned, with ruled lines on his skin, and lived among the people of the new city weighing their quarrels, and never once told a lie.".

  // What a company that knows two things comes to see for itself.
  Observe kneeling_seen near party when knows(party, kneeling_felt) and knows(party, note_terms) and not knows(party, kneeling_bought) "You put them side by side: the old oath of Amaury's line in the War Note, and the hand Amaury felt on his neck at the ford. The miracle the city keeps a saint's day for was paid for, by the month, in silver and then in soldiers." teaches kneeling_bought.

  // ── The Landgate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person tolley "Brother Ancel" at chapel {
    Role "the brother who keeps Saint Evenhand's". Ancestry human. Profession priest. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Offers healing "a dressing, a prayer and a weight hung for you" for 2 coin.
  }
  Topic tolley_weights with tolley "Ask Brother Ancel about the hanging weights" when true once {
    Says "'Promises,' says Brother Ancel, and touches one so that it turns on its cord. 'A man who wants a thing kept hangs its weight here. Brass for a marriage. Lead for a debt. This one, a stone off the beach, a girl hung for her sweetheart in the Muster.' He looks up at them, hundreds, turning. 'Eleven years of war, and the cords are getting thin. The saint holds the scales, you see. He doesn't put his thumb on them.'".
  }
  Topic tolley_saint with tolley "Ask Brother Ancel who Saint Evenhand was" when true once {
    Says "'A clerk of the drowned city,' says Ancel, 'who came up out of the sea the night it went down. That is the old story. He had lines on his skin like a ledger, and he could not tell a lie, and he lived among the first people of Tessary weighing their quarrels for them, and they trusted him because he could not be bought or frightened or flattered. He never went back.' He smiles. 'The scholars say he is a story about a set of scales.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, evenhand_tale). }
  }
  Topic tolley_calling with tolley "Ask Brother Ancel about the soldiers walking into the sea" when knows(actor, notice_read) or knows(actor, calling_witnessed) once {
    Says "Ancel's hand finds the nearest weight and holds it still. 'Nan Teazle's boy was the first I buried with no body,' he says. 'I have said the office over eleven pairs of boots since. The Board says they are deserters. A deserter takes his boots.' He lets the weight go. 'Talk to the clerk in grey, if you can make him answer. He was in here yesterday, reading the cords. He said they were all of them accurate.'".
  }

  Person pitch "Lemuel Pitch" at chandlery {
    Role "a ship's chandler". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "Lemuel Pitch goes on splicing a line as thick as his wrist. 'If it's rope, it's on the left,' he says. 'If it's the tides, everyone asks. Ask. I have a sheet of them pinned up and nobody reads it.'".
    Greets again "Lemuel Pitch has moved on to the next fathom of the same line, and the same remark. 'If it's rope,' he says, 'it's on the left. If it's the tide table, I have changed it, because the sea has. Ask me again at slack water.'".
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 8.
    Sells rope for 1 coin from 4.
    Sells torch for 1 coin from 6.
    Sells lantern for 3 coin from 2.
    Sells lamp_oil for 1 coin from 6.
    Sells oilskin for 2 coin from 3.
    Sells bandages for 1 coin from 4.
    Sells chapbook for 1 coin from 2.
  }
  Kind chapbook "a chapbook of ballads" is gear worth 1 weighing 0
    described "Twenty pages of cheap reed-paper, badly printed: 'The Drowned Bell', 'Sally of the Withies', 'The Soldier's Return' and nine more, with a woodcut of a ship on the cover.".
  Kind oilskin "an oilskin" like cloak worth 2 weighing 2
    described "A fisherman's coat of oiled canvas, stiff as a board and smelling of linseed. Water runs off it.".
  Topic pitch_tide with pitch "Ask Lemuel Pitch about the tides" when true once {
    Says "'Twice a day it goes out and twice it comes back, same as anywhere,' says Pitch, 'only here when it goes out it goes out properly. The basin's out from ten in the morning till two, and from ten at night till two, give or take a little: four hours of streets, and then it turns. Then it turns. And when it turns in the basin it doesn't come in, it comes back, all at once through the Swatch like it's been sent for.' He taps the counter. 'Rope. Anyone going down into Lowtide wants rope, and something to stand on.' And then, lower, because it is not the kind of thing a chandler says to strangers: 'And don't take a boat out past the bar at night. Some nights the stars out there are wrong. My father saw it, and I've seen it twice, and I don't care who laughs.'".
  }

  // ── The Withies: Nan and Wick Teazle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person nan "Nan Teazle" at teazle_room {
    Role "an eel-wife of the Withies". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
    Greets "Nan Teazle does not get up. She is mending an eel-trap on her knee, in withies the colour of old bone, and the needle goes in and out of the same hole three times before she notices. 'If you've news,' she says, 'sit where I can hear it. If you've not, the trap is ready on Thursday.'".
    Greets again "Nan Teazle has the eel-trap off her knee and a second one on it, begun. 'Davy came by,' she says, to the withies. 'He ate. He did not say where he had been. I'll not ask a boy who is home what he thinks the sea did to him.'".
  }
  Person wick "Wick Teazle" at withies {
    Role "a mudlark, about ten, with a tray on a string". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Sells tide_table for 1 coin from 3.
    Sells aenean_coin for 1 coin from 9.
  }
  Kind tide_table "a tide-table" is gear worth 1 weighing 0
    described "A square of reed-paper ruled in a child's careful hand: the hours of low water for the fortnight, the turn marked each time with a drawing of a wave with teeth.".
  Kind aenean_coin "a genuine Aenean coin" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0
    described "A disc of greenish metal with a face on it, stamped, rather recently, by someone who had seen an Aenean coin once and liked it.".
  Discovery davy_went "Davy Teazle came home with the Muster, sat on his mother's step for a week without saying much, and at the last spring ebb got up in his sleep, went down the Watersteps barefoot and walked into the sea." {
    Known by nan, wick.
  }
  Topic nan_davy with nan "Ask Nan about Davy" when not cameHome(davy) once {
    Says "'He came home on the Tuesday with the rest of them,' says Nan, 'and he sat on that step out there for a week. Didn't say much. Ate what I put down. Then the spring ebb, the night after the new moon, I wake up and he's going down the ladder in his shirt. I called him. He didn't turn round.' Her needle goes in and out of the net. 'He set his boots on the top step. Side by side. I had to tell him every night of his life to put his boots together and he never once did it, and he set them on the step like a gentleman's valet. They taught him that.' She bites the cord. 'Then he walked into the sea.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, davy_went). }
  }
  Relation nanOffer(group).
  Topic nan_reward with nan "Ask Nan what she is offering" when not cameHome(davy) and not nanOffer(actor) once {
    Says "'Nine coin,' says Nan. 'It's in a tin. And all the eels you can eat for a twelvemonth, which you'll be sick of in a week.' She looks at you properly for the first time. 'I don't need him back. I'm not a fool. I need to know where he went. If he's down there drowned, I need to know where, so I can say so to the brother at the chapel and have him say the office over something that isn't a pair of boots.'".
    On discuss { Assert nanOffer(actor). }
  }
  Topic nan_bill with nan "Ask Nan about the recruiting bill on her shelf" when true once {
    Says "'LAND AND A PENSION FOR EVERY MAN WHO COMES HOME,' says Nan, without looking at it. 'They cried that in the Withies with a drum. Davy was seventeen. He came home Tuesday with a red coat and a paper that says he's owed eleven years' pay, and the Exchequer has no money to pay it with, and the Board's to hear the question of the land on the thirteenth day. The question.' She snorts. 'Eleven years they've had to think of an answer.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, enlist_promise). }
  }
  Topic nan_alive with nan "Tell Nan that Davy is alive" when knows(actor, held_alive) and knows(actor, davy_went) and not toldNan(actor) once {
    Says "Nan Teazle puts the net down. She sits very still for a long time with her hands in her lap. 'Asleep,' she says at last. 'Standing up. Under the sea.' She gets up and takes Davy's red coat off its peg and holds it, and then holds it out to you. 'If you're going where he is, take him this. He'll be cold. He was always cold.' Her voice does not change at all. 'And tell him to put his boots on.'".
    On discuss { Assert toldNan(actor). }
  }
  Relation toldNan(group).
  Item davy_coat "Davy Teazle's red coat" is soldier_coat at teazle_room hidden until coat_given.
  Kind soldier_coat "a red coat of the Long Muster" like cloak worth 0 weighing 2
    described "A soldier's coat, red gone brown at the shoulders, with the Muster's brass buttons and a darn at the elbow in someone's careful wool.".
  Discovery coat_given "Nan Teazle has given you Davy's coat to take to him.".
  Action take_coat(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Take Davy's coat from Nan" {
    Speaker nan. Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(nan, site) and toldNan(actor)
      and memberOf(recipient, actor) and awake(recipient) and not knows(actor, coat_given).
    Resolve acquire(davy_coat, soldier_coat, recipient).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, coat_given). Retract at(davy_coat, teazle_room). }
    Result "Nan lays the coat over your arm, and smooths the darn at the elbow once with her thumb, and lets go.".
  }
  Initially Give davy_coat to party.

  Topic wick_night with wick "Ask Wick about the night Davy went" when not cameHome(davy) once {
    Says "'I followed him,' says Wick, fast, as if he has been waiting to be asked. 'All the way down the Steps and out on the sand, it was a spring ebb, you can walk right out. There were twelve of them and they kept step and nobody was calling it. Out past the colonnade, across the Forum. Into the Hall of Oaths.' He lowers his voice. 'There's no door in the Hall of Oaths. It's a wall at the back. I've felt it. They walked into the wall and it let them, and then it was a wall again.' He considers. 'I'll show you, if you like. A coin. Two if you want the tide-table too, which you do.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hall_of_oaths_way). }
  }
  Topic wick_lowtide with wick "Ask Wick about Lowtide" when true once {
    Says "'It's the old city,' says Wick. 'You go down the Swatch Stair at low water and it's all streets, with weed in, and you can find things. Coins.' He rattles his tray. 'You've got five hours, about. When the tide turns you get up high, the aqueduct or the top of the bath-house dome, and you sit there till it goes out again, and you don't go in the bath-house, not ever, because the hollow men are in the bath-house.' He thinks. 'And keep out of the way of the ebb-runners at the landing. They don't like being looked at.'".
  }
  Topic wick_hollow with wick "Ask Wick about the hollow men" when true once {
    Says "Wick stops grinning. 'They were people,' he says. 'Old ones, from when the city was up. Mudlarks see them sometimes in the doorways when the water's coming. They're like coats with nobody in. They come if you swear. My nan says they come for anyone who's broke a promise, so I never promise anything.' He holds out a coin. 'Genuine Aenean. One coin. I'm not promising it's genuine.'".
  }
  Topic wick_grey with wick "Ask Wick about the clerk in grey" when true once {
    Says "'That's Docket,' says Wick. 'I called him that because he's always counting. He asked me my name and wrote it down and asked was I sure. He knows everyone's name in the Withies now. He knows Davy's. He said Davy was on page four.' Wick scuffs the boards. 'He doesn't eat anything. I gave him an eel and he thanked me and wrote it down and put it in his pocket.'".
  }

  // ── The Muffled Drum: Sergeant Durrance and the Muster ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person sedge "Hannelore Rackham" at drum_taproom {
    Role "who keeps the Muffled Drum". Ancestry human. Profession innkeeper. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner jovial.
    Greets "Hannelore Rackham has hung a muffled drum over her bar, its skin stuffed with a rag, and she glances at it every time the door goes, the way she has glanced at it for every customer since the summer. 'Drink or news?' she says. 'The drink is paid for. The news is the other way about.'".
    Greets again "Hannelore Rackham has a cup poured before you reach the bar, as she has for the regulars, and for no one else, since summer. 'You're one of ours now,' she says. 'It's not an honour. It's a tab.'".
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 6.
  }
  Topic sedge_drum with sedge "Ask Hannelore Rackham about the drum over the bar" when true once {
    Says "'The Third Company's,' says Hannelore. 'Thomasin brought it home. She tied the cloth over it herself. Nobody plays it till the last of the Third comes home, she says, and since the summer that's been looking like never.' She wipes the bar. 'Don't touch it. I mean that kindly.'".
  }
  Person durrance "Thomasin Durrance" at drum_taproom {
    Role "a sergeant of the Long Muster, out of uniform". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 4. Trait brave. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "Sergeant Durrance is out of uniform and cannot get her shoulders to know it. She puts her pot down in line with the table's edge before she speaks. 'Nineteen years I have been telling lads what is in front of them,' she says. 'I'm out of practice at telling it to anyone who is not afraid of me.'".
    Greets again "Sergeant Durrance has moved her pot an inch to the left, out of line, as a test, and watches you notice. 'Good,' she says. 'You see things. I could have used you at Hethra. They told me you were not enlisting. I was told many things at Hethra.'".
    Joins "Durrance finishes her pot and stands, and is suddenly a sergeant again. 'Right,' she says. 'Let's go and look at where I'm going.'".
    Leaves "'I'll be at the Drum,' says Durrance. 'Where else.'".
  }
  Topic durrance_vanished with durrance "Ask Durrance about the soldiers who have gone into the sea" when true once {
    Says "'Third Company,' says Durrance. 'All of them. Pargeter, Haskett, Moll Bryer, the Lucey twins, Davy Teazle. And in order. You know what order? Roll order. Alphabet by platoon, the way the paymaster calls it.' She drinks. 'I've had nineteen years of roll calls. Somebody is calling the roll, and it isn't anybody in this city. Next spring ebb it's Ruddock, Saye, Tamsett, Oddie, Amsel. And then it's a page turn, and the top of the next page is me.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, roll_order). Assert knows(actor, durrance_next). }
  }
  Topic durrance_will with durrance "Ask Durrance what she means to do when it is her turn" when knows(actor, durrance_next) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "'Go,' says Durrance. 'What do you think?' She puts her hand flat on the table. 'I put this hand on the Stone in the Yard nineteen years ago and swore. Nobody made me. I swore to keep the city, and I've kept it, through two sieges and Sedge Ford and the winter at Galt. If the city's calling me in, I go in.' She looks at her hand. 'I'd like to know who's doing the calling, mind. That's all. I'd like to look at them.'".
  }
  Topic durrance_oath with durrance "Ask Durrance what the oath on the Stone says" when true once {
    Says "Durrance doesn't have to think. ''I swear to keep the city of Tessary, its walls and its people, while I live or until it release me.'' She shrugs. 'Hand on the Stone, say it once, the recruiting sergeant slaps your back and you're the city's. Nobody listens to the words. I listened. I was that kind of recruit.' A short laugh. 'Until it release me. It never has. I've never heard of anyone it did.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, oath_words). }
  }
  Topic durrance_ford with durrance "Ask Durrance about Sedge Ford" when true once {
    Says "'I was ten yards off,' says Durrance. 'Their king came down the bank on a grey horse with his whole household round him. We were finished. We knew it, they knew it. And in the middle of the river he gets off his horse, and goes down on his knees in the water, and holds out his sword to Captain Ancrum hilt first.' She turns her pot. 'People say he looked like a man praying. He didn't. He looked like a man being pushed down by a hand on the back of his neck. And there wasn't anybody behind him.'".
  }
  Topic durrance_join with durrance "Ask Durrance whether she would come with you into Lowtide" when knows(actor, hall_of_oaths_way) and knows(actor, durrance_next) and not willing(durrance, actor) and not travelsWith(durrance, actor) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "Durrance looks at you a long moment. 'To the Hall of Oaths,' she says. 'Where they go in.' She pushes her pot away. 'Yes. I'd like to see the door before I walk through it. And you'll want someone who can hold a line when the tide comes, and that's me. Say the word and I'll get my coat.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(durrance, actor). }
  }
  Initially Set hire(durrance) to 0.

  Person fisk "Benno Fisk" at drum_taproom {
    Role "a corporal of the Long Muster". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "Benno Fisk lifts his pot to you with one hand and smooths the front of a new grey coat with a salt-white collar with the other.".
    Greets again "Benno Fisk has taken the grey coat off and put it on the back of the bench, where he can see it, and not on him. 'Don't tell the Sergeant,' he says. 'I just wanted to see what I looked like without being in it.'".
  }
  Initially Assert serves(fisk, sault).
  Topic fisk_work with fisk "Ask Fisk where he got the new coat" when true once {
    Says "'Factor Sault,' says Fisk, and smooths it. 'Best employer in Tessary. Day's pay for a day's work, and she knows your name. She knew my name before I knew hers.' He winks. 'Night work too, for them as don't ask questions. Carrying. Down Panhythe way, under the warehouse. Pays double.' He drinks. 'I don't ask questions.'".
  }
  Topic fisk_board with fisk "Ask Fisk what the Muster thinks of the Board" when true once {
    Says "'The Board?' says Fisk. 'The Board sent us to Hethra for eleven years and now it's going to hold a meeting about whether it owes us. A meeting.' He laughs, not pleasantly. 'There's lads at the Muster hall say if the Board votes no, they'll go up the Terraces and ask again, louder. The Factor says not to. The Factor says leave it to her.'".
  }

  // ── Panhythe: Factor Sault ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person sault "Imma Sault" at sault_office {
    Role "Factor of the Salt Moiety". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 5. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "Factor Sault wipes her fingers on a cloth, salt and ink together, and holds out her hand across the ledgers before you have crossed the room. It is a dry, short, businesslike grip, and she lets go at the right time. 'You've come about the Muster,' she says. 'Everyone has. I'm the only person in Tessary who is not sorry about it.'".
    Greets again "Factor Sault finishes the line she was on before she gives you her hand, and the hand is saltier than before. 'You have been to see the Balance,' she says. 'I can smell the ink on you. They never get it off.'".
  }
  Relation hiredBySault(group).
  Topic sault_work with sault "Ask the Factor about the veterans who have gone into the sea" when not hiredBySault(actor) once {
    Says "'My lads,' says Factor Sault. 'Forty of them on my books at the Muster hall, and six of the forty gone into the water since the summer, and the Board says deserters.' She snorts. 'Deserters. Men who'd come to me for work at dawn every day for a month. You're a stranger here, which is useful: nobody's paying you to see nothing. Find out who's taking them, and how, and bring it to me. Twenty coin.' She holds your eye. 'And if the grey clerk who goes about writing down their names is any part of it, I want to know what he writes.'".
    On discuss { Assert hiredBySault(actor). }
  }
  Topic sault_board with sault "Ask the Factor what she thinks of the Board" when true once {
    Says "'The furniture?' Factor Sault laughs. 'Eight chairs, five of them inherited. They started a war over salt springs they could have bought for a tenth of what it cost, borrowed to fight it, and now the bill's come in, they want to send it to the men who did the fighting.' She spreads her hands, salt-cracked. 'I came up off the pans. I could tell you the name of every rake in my yards. Half of them were soldiers once, before your time, and the city promised them something too.' She does not say what. 'Somebody in this city has to be able to count.'".
  }
  Topic sault_muster with sault "Ask the Factor about her hiring hall" when true once {
    Says "'No man turned away who wore the coat,' says Sault. 'It costs me. The Board was supposed to look after them and didn't, so I do.' She shrugs. 'And they work, and they're grateful, and in a city that's about to have eight thousand angry soldiers in it, I would rather they were grateful to me than to anyone else. I don't pretend it's charity.'".
  }
  // What she pays for: what is taking her lads, told; or the grey clerk's inventory, copied. Either brings her plans on.
  Topic sault_report with sault "Tell the Factor what is taking her lads" when hiredBySault(actor) and knows(actor, collateral) and not saultInformed(sault) once {
    Says "Factor Sault listens with her chin on her fist and does not interrupt once. When you have done she counts twenty coin onto the ledger and pushes them across. 'Pledged,' she says. 'Their oaths. As collateral.' She is not surprised, you notice; she is checking it against something. 'Well. You've earned it.' She looks out of the window toward the Muster hall. 'Ten years I've carried—' She stops. 'Never mind what I've carried. Go and have your supper.'".
    On discuss { Assert saultInformed(sault). Decrease quantity(sault, gold) by 20. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 20. }
  }
  Topic sault_confronted with sault "Tell the Factor you have read her letter to the Broker of the Fourth Pan" when knows(actor, sault_bid) and not saultExposed(ossel) and not voted(ossel) once {
    Says "Factor Sault puts her pen down. 'Bettany,' she says, not as a question. 'Well. Every word of it's true.' She leans back. 'So what will you do with it? Take it to the Board, and they'll read it, and be frightened of me, and vote no anyway because there's no money, and I'll have the note at the Feast and you'll have been right. Or take it under the sea to the old man, and he'll stop my broker, and I'll go down and bid in person.' She shrugs. 'Or put me terms, if you can find anything I want more than the Muster. Nobody has yet.' She picks up the pen. 'I'm not your enemy. Ask the Board who has been paying attention.'".
  }
  // The grey clerk's inventory, copied.
  Item inventory_copy "a copy of the Valuer's inventory" is ledger_copy at tideline_steps hidden until inventory_copied.
  Kind ledger_copy "a copied page of an inventory" is gear worth 1 weighing 0
