      and dark() and not travelsWith(tally, actor) and not knows(actor, inventory_copied) and not caughtCopying(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, inventory_copied). Assert knows(actor, roll_order). Assert knows(actor, durrance_next). }
    On failure { Assert caughtCopying(actor). }
    Result "The Valuer stands at the water's edge with their back to you, quite still, and the ledger lies open on the step in the lamplight. You copy two pages by its light, names in roll order and columns of marks you cannot read, and the Valuer does not turn round. Third Company. Page four: Teazle, D. Page five, near the top: Durrance, A.".
    Otherwise "You have copied half a page when the Valuer says, without turning round, 'That is the property of the Balance.' They come and close the ledger, and take it up, and look at you with no expression at all. 'I note it,' they say.".
  }
  Event sault_paid near sault when keeps(sault, inventory_copy) "Factor Sault reads the pages through twice, running a salt-cracked finger down the names, stopping at some. 'Roll order,' she says. 'Well, well.' She counts twenty coin onto the ledger without looking at them. 'You've earned it. I'll not forget it.' She folds the pages away into her coat." then {
    Assert saultInformed(sault). Decrease quantity(sault, gold) by 20. Increase quantity(party, gold) by 20. }
  Initially Set quantity(sault, gold) to 60.

  // ── The Lettered Quarter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person quire "Josiah Quire" at exchequer_room {
    Role "Treasurer of Tessary". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "The Treasurer blinks at the door as it opens, as though it had let in someone other than he had been expecting, or everyone. His chain of office has been turned round so that the clasp is at the front, and he has not noticed. 'Yes,' says Josiah Quire. 'Come in. Come in before anyone sees you.'".
    Greets again "Josiah Quire has turned his chain the right way round, and is looking at it as if someone else had done it. 'Thank you for coming back,' he says. 'No one else has. I have begun to think I am a thing that people only visit once.'".
  }
  Topic quire_vanished with quire "Ask the Treasurer about the soldiers who have gone into the sea" when not knows(actor, council_knows) once {
    Says "'Deserters,' says Quire, too quickly. 'That is the Board's finding. Men who have been away eleven years do not always want to come home to what they left.' He moves a paperweight on his desk from one stack to another and back. 'I'm sorry. I am very tired. Is there anything else?'".
  }
  Relation quireConfided(group).
  Topic quire_list_asked with quire "Ask the Treasurer about his list of names" when knows(actor, council_knows) and not quireConfided(actor) once {
    Says "Quire looks at the list for a long time. 'A hundred and thirty-eight,' he says. 'I send their mothers something every month. Out of my own salary, which the city also does not pay.' He takes off his spectacles. 'I signed it. Ten years ago. We went down under the sea, six of us, and they showed us a thing like a ledger the size of a ship, and an old man who could not lie read us the terms, and we signed, because we were going to lose the war, and we won.' His hands are shaking. 'The Muster's oaths. As collateral. I put my name to eight thousand men like a farmer putting up his cows.'".
    On discuss { Assert quireConfided(actor). Assert knows(actor, collateral). }
  }
  Topic quire_terms with quire "Ask the Treasurer what the city must do to pay" when quireConfided(actor) and not knows(actor, promise_weight) once {
    Says "'Keep a promise,' says Quire. 'Of equal weight. Their words.' He laughs, horribly. 'And there is exactly one of those in the city's books, and I have it by heart: land and a pension for every man who comes home. Two hundred thousand marks. The treasury has nothing. The Board will vote no on the thirteenth day, because there is no money, and on the fifteenth the note falls due, and then...' He doesn't finish.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, promise_weight). Assert knows(actor, enlist_promise). }
  }

  Person pounce "Hesketh Pounce" at pounce_stall {
    Role "a scrivener of the Row". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
  }
  Topic pounce_trade with pounce "Ask Pounce about his trade" when true once {
    Says "'Contracts drawn, contracts read, contracts explained,' says Pounce. 'The first is easy, the second is a skill, the third is extra because nobody likes what I tell them.' He sands a page. 'Tessary is a city where a fishwife will sue a gull. I have made a good living out of it for thirty years. I keep every draft I ever wrote, you know. A scrivener who burns his drafts is a scrivener who gets sued.'".
  }
  Topic pounce_council with pounce "Ask Pounce whether he has ever drawn a contract for the Board" when true once {
    Says "Pounce's pen stops. 'Once,' he says. 'Ten years ago. A fair copy of an instrument, done at night in the Council House with a councillor at my elbow and sworn to silence after. Strangest thing I ever copied. Half of it was in a hand I had never seen and had to copy by shape.' He looks at you sideways. 'I kept my draft. Of course I kept my draft. I am sworn to silence, mind. But a scrivener's drafts are his own property, and his property is for sale, and it is no breach of silence to sell a man a piece of paper he will read for himself.' He names the price: 'Six coin.'".
    On discuss { Assert pounceOffered(actor). }
  }
  Relation pounceOffered(group).
  Item pounce_draft "Pounce's draft of the War Note" is draft_kind at pounce_stall hidden until draft_bought.
  Kind draft_kind "a scrivener's draft" is gear worth 1 weighing 0
    described "Six closely written pages of reed-paper, foxed and folded, the draft of a fair copy: a contract between the city of Tessary and a party named only as the Ledger Below.".
  Discovery draft_bought "Pounce has sold you his twelve-year-old draft of the Board's secret instrument.".
  Action buy_draft(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Pay Pounce six coin for his old draft" {
    Speaker pounce. Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pounce, site) and pounceOffered(actor)
      and memberOf(recipient, actor) and awake(recipient)
      and not knows(actor, draft_bought) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 6.
    Resolve acquire(pounce_draft, draft_kind, recipient).
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Increase quantity(pounce, gold) by 6. Assert knows(actor, draft_bought). Retract at(pounce_draft, pounce_stall). }
    Result "Pounce goes to a chest and comes back with six pages folded small, and counts your coins before he lets go of them. 'You did not get these from me,' he says. 'You got them from a man you met in a tavern who resembled me.'".
  }
  Action read_draft(actor: group, site: place) "Read Pounce's draft of the War Note" {
    Time 2.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and carries(actor, pounce_draft) and not benighted(actor)
      and not knows(actor, note_terms).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, note_terms). }
    Result "You read it through twice. The city's half is plain Tessarine legal hand: the city of Tessary, as heir to the Aenean emperors in the matter of oaths, borrows the calling of an oath sworn by the house of Hethra, &c. The other half is in a script Pounce copied by shape, ruled like a ledger; but the terms are restated in the city's hand at the foot, as terms are. The Long Muster's oaths as surety. Silver monthly. And at the Feast of Settlement in the twelfth year, the principal, to be paid in a kept promise of equal weight. The Treasurer's signature. Five councillors'. And a sixth mark that is not a signature at all, only a set of ruled lines.".
  }
  Action explain_draft(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Pounce two coin to explain the clause about equal weight" {
    Speaker pounce. Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pounce, site) and carries(actor, pounce_draft)
      and knows(actor, note_terms) and not knows(actor, promise_weight) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 2.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Increase quantity(pounce, gold) by 2. Assert knows(actor, promise_weight). Assert knows(actor, enlist_promise). }
    Result "Pounce puts on a second pair of spectacles over the first. 'Equal weight,' he says. 'Weight of what? Not silver, or it would say silver. A promise of equal weight to an oath that bound a royal house for nine hundred years.' He taps the page. 'A people's promise, then, to a people. Has this city ever made one?' He answers himself before you can. 'Land and a pension for every man who comes home. I drew the recruiting bills. So if the city keeps that, it pays this.' He takes off both pairs of spectacles. 'And if it doesn't, it doesn't. That will be two coin. I did say nobody likes what I tell them.'".
  }

  // The Office of Seals: the queue, and the Keeper of the Seal.
  Person queue "the queue" at seals_hall {
    Role "who have been waiting since breakfast, or Tuesday, or longer, each with a document". Ancestry human. Numbers 1. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Greets "Every face in the queue turns to see whether you mean to push in, and, satisfied, turns back.".
    Greets again "The queue shuffles up one place without turning, as one body, as you pass the end of it. Nobody shouts. A woman at the back says, to nobody, 'They never go to the front,' and nobody answers her.".
  }
  Topic queue_asked with queue "Ask the queue how long they have been waiting" when true once {
    Says "Several people answer at once. A man with a deed: 'Since breakfast.' A woman with a marriage contract: 'Since Tuesday.' An old man near the front, without turning round: 'My father held this place in the queue before me. I am sealing the lease he came to seal. It has run out, but it is the principle.'".
  }
  Person deckle "Ulric Deckle" at seals_inner {
    Role "Keeper of the Great Seal". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Wants seal_kind.
  }
  Relation reachedKeeper(group).
  Action wait_in_queue(actor: group, site: place) "Take your place in the queue" {
    Description "It moves. Slowly, but it moves.".
    Time 18.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(queue, site) and not reachedKeeper(actor)
      and hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 15.
    On success { Assert reachedKeeper(actor). }
    Interrupted when threatened(actor).
    Result "Three hours later, having learned the life history of a rope-maker's widow and the full grounds of a dispute about a fence, you reach the grille. A clerk looks at you over it. 'Business?' And, since you have none he recognises: 'The Keeper will see you. The Keeper sees everyone who reaches the grille. It is the law.' He opens the door.".
  }
  Thing grille "the grille" on seals_grille {
    State shut blocking "A clerk behind the grille admits whoever reaches the head of the queue, and nobody else.".
    State open "The clerk has opened the grille for you.".
  }
  Query keeperSends() means deedsSealed(ossel) or sealStolen(ossel) or votePassed(ossel) and night(ossel) == 13 and hour(clock) >= 15.
  Rule grille_opens when (reachedKeeper(party) or keeperSends()) and state(grille, shut) { Assert state(grille, open). }
  Rule grille_shuts when state(grille, open) and not reachedKeeper(party) and not keeperSends() { Assert state(grille, shut). }
  Rule grille_closes_at_night when dark() and reachedKeeper(party) and not at(party, seals_inner) and not keeperSends() { Retract reachedKeeper(party). }
  Topic deckle_seal with deckle "Ask the Keeper about the Great Seal" when true once {
    Says "'The Seal of Tessary,' says Deckle, and lifts the glass bell an inch as if letting it breathe. 'What it seals, the city has done. A deed sealed here is land given. A treaty sealed here is peace made. If the Board were to vote the Veterans' Settlement' (he says it the way one says the name of a disease) 'every one of eight thousand deeds would have to pass under this hand. My clerks could do it in a night and a day, if they did nothing else.' He lowers the bell. 'Nobody has asked them to.'".
  }

  // ── The Terraces ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person marrable "Ysbel Marrable" at marrable_room {
    Role "who sits for the Eel Moiety on the Board, a veteran with one sleeve pinned up". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
  }
  Topic marrable_vote with marrable "Ask Councillor Marrable how the vote will go" when not voted(ossel) once {
    Says "'Badly,' says Marrable. 'Eight chairs. Mine is yes. Old Hallam has buried two sons in Hethra; he's yes, if he's awake. Salt is Sault's and Sault says no, there's no money, which is true. Rope is Dauntry and Dauntry votes the way Sault tells him. Greaves and Vantage are the furniture and will not give an inch of their land. Paper is Haverick, who cares about nothing but his goose, and Ship is Orme, who will vote for whatever he thinks will be paid for.' She counts on one hand, which takes no time. 'I need five. I have two.'".
  }
  Topic marrable_sway with marrable "Ask Councillor Marrable what would change their minds" when not voted(ossel) once {
    Says "'Proof,' says Marrable. 'They call the vanished deserters because if they're not deserters, something worse is happening and somebody on the Board knows what. Show them the Treasurer knows. Show them why. Bring them someone they can't call a liar.' She looks at the pinned sleeve. 'And keep the Muster off the Terraces. If soldiers come up that hill shouting the night before, Orme and Hallam will vote no out of fright and I won't blame them.' She looks at you. 'We sit on the thirteenth day, from ten in the morning till the bell at two. The public bench is open. Anyone with something to say can stand up and say it, until two. After two it's a count.'".
  }
  Person amaury "Amaury of Hethra" at kings_rooms {
    Role "King of Hethra, a hostage in Tessary". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 6. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "The King of Hethra is playing both sides of a draughts board and winning neither. 'A visitor,' he says. 'How unusual. Sit, sit. I am allowed visitors. I am allowed everything except the door.'".
    Greets again "The King of Hethra turns the draughts board so that you will be playing the white pieces, which have more men. 'You have been out in the weather,' he says. 'Sit. I am allowed visitors. I am hoping you are the one who is going to disappoint me.'".
  }
  Topic amaury_kneeling with amaury "Ask the King about the Kneeling at Sedge Ford" when true once {
    Says "'Ah,' says the King. 'The famous kneeling.' He moves a draught. 'I had won. You understand that? I had your city's Muster pinned against the river and I rode down to accept its surrender. And in the middle of the ford I felt a hand. Here.' He touches the back of his neck. 'Old. Patient. Quite certain of its rights. Nine hundred years old, I would say, if a hand can be old. And my knees went into the water and my sword went out hilt first and I heard my own voice yielding the kingdom.' He looks at the board. 'Your saint's day for it is the twelfth of Haying. I watch the procession from this window. It is the only day of the year I drink before noon.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, kneeling_felt). }
  }
  Relation amauryPlayed(group).
  Action play_amaury(actor: group, site: place) "Play the King a game of Hethran draughts" {
    Speaker amaury. Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(amaury, site) and not amauryPlayed(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert amauryPlayed(actor). Assert amauryWon(actor). }
    On failure { Assert amauryPlayed(actor). }
    Result "It is a long game, and the King talks all through it, about his horses, the weather in the hills, the absurdity of a city that keeps its prisoner in better rooms than its Treasurer. Somewhere in the second hour you see the trap he has been building on the left side of the board, and walk round it, and he sits back. 'You see what's in front of you,' he says. 'That is rarer than it should be. Come again.'".
    Otherwise "It is a long game, and the King talks all through it, and in the second hour springs a trap on the left side of the board that he has been building since the first move. 'Hethran draughts,' he says kindly, sweeping up your pieces, 'is a game for people who expect to lose a war. Come again.'".
  }
  Relation amauryWon(group).
  Relation amauryWillTestify(group).
  Topic amaury_told with amaury "Tell the King how Sedge Ford was won" when knows(actor, note_terms) and not amauryWillTestify(actor) once {
    Says "The King hears you out without moving a piece. When you have done, he laughs, quite quietly, for a long time. 'An oath of my house,' he says, 'to the Aenean emperors. Bought back off a shelf under the sea by a city of paper-makers, for silver, on the never-never.' He wipes his eyes. 'And then paid for in their own soldiers when the silver ran out. Oh, that is good. That is the best thing I have heard in a year.' He stops laughing. 'If you want this told to the Board in a voice they cannot dismiss as a stranger's, I will tell it. They will have to let me out of these rooms to hear it, and I should like to see the inside of their chamber, and the painting.' He moves a draught at last. 'I should like very much to see their faces.'".
    On discuss { Assert amauryWillTestify(actor). Assert knows(actor, kneeling_felt). }
  }
  Topic amaury_wants with amaury "Ask the King what he wants" when true once {
    Says "'To go home,' says the King. 'My ransom is a sum your Board cannot ask for and my people cannot pay, which suits both of them. And to know what happened to me in that river.' He sets a piece down very precisely. 'A man can lose a kingdom and live. I find it is harder to have been made to give it away.'".
  }

  // ── The Ninth Valuer ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A clerk of the Scruples, sent up to inventory the collateral before the note falls due. Exact; unable to lie;
  // answers what it is asked and nothing it is not.
  Person tally "the Ninth Valuer" at withies {
    Role "a clerk in a grey coat with a ledger, whose skin is faintly ruled like paper". Ancestry human. Calling cleric. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns they. Manner stoic.
    Called "Docket".
    Seen when not tallyUnravelled(ossel).
    Greets "The clerk in grey turns a page of the ledger without lifting a hand to it. Close to, the skin of their face and hands is very faintly ruled, like a page, in lines as fine as hairs. 'Good day,' they say. 'You are not on my inventory.'".
    Greets again "The clerk in grey makes a mark in the ledger, so fine you can scarcely see it. 'You were not on the inventory,' they say. 'You are now. It is not a promotion. It is a form of attention.'".
    Joins "'Our inquiries coincide,' says the Valuer, and closes the ledger on a ribbon. 'I will accompany you. I will note anything you do that bears on the collateral.'".
    Leaves "The Valuer inclines their head, very exactly, and closes the ledger on its ribbon, and goes.".
  }
  Initially Set hire(tally) to 0.
  Topic tally_who with tally "Ask the clerk in grey who they are" when true once {
    Says "'I am the Ninth Valuer of the Scruples,' says the clerk. 'I am taking an inventory.' A pause, which seems to be for you to say something, and when you do not: 'The children call me Docket. It is not my name. My name is held. Docket is accurate as a description, and I do not object to it.'".
  }
  Topic tally_counting with tally "Ask the Valuer what they are counting" when true once {
    Says "'The Long Muster,' says the Valuer, 'page by page, in the order of its roll.' They make a small mark. 'I am not at liberty to say why. The affairs of a debtor are not discussed with a third party. You are a third party.' A pause, quite friendly. 'You may ask me anything. I will not lie to you. I will decline a great deal.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, roll_order). }
  }
  Topic tally_where with tally "Ask the Valuer where the soldiers you saw walk into the sea have gone" when knows(actor, calling_witnessed) and not knows(actor, held_alive) once {
    Says "The Valuer considers whether this is the affair of a debtor, and decides, visibly, that what you saw with your own eyes is your own affair. 'Into the Holding,' they say, 'where pledged things are kept. They are not harmed. They are held. They stand asleep with the rest of what has been pledged and forfeit, and they do not age.' A pause. 'You are distressed. I am sorry. It is a lawful collection.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, held_alive). }
  }
  Topic tally_discharge with tally "Ask the Valuer what would bring the called home" when knows(actor, held_alive) and not knows(actor, release_law) once {
    Says "'The discharge of the debt they stand surety for,' says the Valuer, as if reading it. 'A debt is discharged in two ways. It is kept, or it is released: if the one to whom a promise was made says freely to the one who made it, I hold you quit, that weighs in the Balance exactly as the keeping does.' A pause. 'People forget the second.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, release_law). }
  }
  Topic tally_confirm with tally "Ask the Valuer whether the city pledged its soldiers' oaths" when (knows(actor, council_knows) or quireConfided(actor)) and not knows(actor, collateral) once {
    Says "'You have seen the Treasurer's list,' says the Valuer. 'Then you have it from the debtor's own officer, and I may confirm what he has let you see.' They open the ledger flat. 'The oaths of the Long Muster, sworn on the instrument the city calls the Oath Stone, are pledged as security on a debt the city owes to the Balance. Since the silver stopped in the summer, interest has been taken in oaths at each spring ebb, in the order of the roll.' They close it. 'Some of the collateral has died since it was pledged, of wounds and of drink. I am noting that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, collateral). }
  }
  Topic tally_debt with tally "Ask the Valuer what the city borrowed" when knows(actor, collateral) and not knows(actor, note_terms) once {
    Says "'The terms are the debtor's affair,' says the Valuer. And then, with great exactness: 'The city made a fair copy of the instrument in its own hand, as a debtor must. Its Board had it made at night by a scrivener of the Row, under an oath of silence.' They look at you. 'In my experience of this city, a scrivener keeps his drafts. I say so as an observation about scriveners.'".
  }
  Topic tally_how with tally "Ask the Valuer what promise would weigh as much as the War Note" when knows(actor, note_terms) and not knows(actor, promise_weight) once {
    Says "'I am not permitted to advise the debtor,' says the Valuer. 'You are not the debtor.' They consider this for some time. 'A promise is weighed by who makes it and to whom, and what it binds. An oath of a royal house to an empire is very heavy. Only a promise of a whole people to a whole people would balance it. I have read the city's books. It has made one.' They look, for the first time, faintly uncomfortable. 'I cannot tell you which. I can tell you that it is printed on a bill on the shelf of a house in this ward, and that I have read it there.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, promise_weight). }
  }
  Topic tally_next with tally "Ask the Valuer whose names are on the next page" when knows(actor, roll_order) and night(ossel) < 8 once {
    Says "The Valuer opens the ledger at a ribbon. 'Ruddock, J., private. Saye, W., private. Tamsett, M., private. Oddie, F., drummer. Amsel, K., private. Then the page turns. Durrance, A., sergeant, Third Company, nineteen years' service.' They look up. 'Then Elcock, Fane, Garrow, Hobb, Ince and Jessup. Twelve.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, durrance_next). }
  }
  Topic tally_join with tally "Ask the Valuer to come with you to the Hall of Oaths" when knows(actor, hall_of_oaths_way) and knows(actor, held_alive) and not willing(tally, actor) and not travelsWith(tally, actor) once {
    Says "'The Hall of Oaths,' says the Valuer. 'The way down.' They are quiet, and you have the impression of a calculation being done. 'I am to return below before the Feast in any case, to report. If you are going that way, I will take you through the wall, and note what you do on the other side of it.' They hold out a hand, ruled like a page. 'I must ask you to promise not to lie to me. It is a small thing, for you. You will find it is not small below.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(tally, actor). Assert promisedTally(actor). }
  }
  Relation promisedTally(group).

  // The Valuer cannot lie and will not volunteer. Asked what a surety owes, it writes the answer down, which is the
  // only way it knows to be of use to a stranger.
  Place beyond_ledger "beyond the ledger" is wilderness within ossel at 9, 9.
  Place nowhere "nowhere" is room within beyond_ledger at 0, 0.
  Item surety_note "the Valuer's note on the terms of a surety" is surety_terms at nowhere owned by tally.
  Topic tally_surety with tally "Ask the Valuer what a surety owes" when knows(actor, release_law) and not suretyNoted(tally) once {
    Says "'A surety answers for the keeping named,' says the Valuer, 'and for no more. Where the keeping is named, the surety is bounded. Where it is not named, the surety answers for everything the principal holds, to the last coin and the last day.' A small pause. 'This is the whole of the law, and it is why I am so seldom asked. People sign what they are given.' The pen is moving. The strip of paper that comes away is ruled in lines as fine as hairs, and says in a hand like type what the Valuer has just said. 'Receipt,' says the Valuer. 'I never give a thing without one.'".
    On discuss { Give surety_note to actor. Assert suretyNoted(tally). }
  }
  Relation suretyNoted(group).
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/placed:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // The Ossel delta as a country beyond a march: the company that comes in along the Causeway is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  // What is said of the Ossel delta in the country behind it: once it is seen through, it is old news there.
  Entity word: fact "What is said of Tessary and the Ossel in the country behind it.".
  Rule word_old when (keptPromise(ossel) or released(ossel) or noteVoid(ossel) or noteTorn(ossel) or saultHoldsNote(ossel) or foreclosed(ossel)) and not stale(word) { Assert stale(word). }
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/plot.k:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── The state of the city's affairs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Relations shared by every movement: who is held, whether the Board has voted, how the note stands.
  Relation heldNow(group). Relation voted(place). Relation votePassed(place).
  // At the Settlement the note is discharged (kept, released or voided), or it falls in: foreclosed, or taken up.
  Relation discharged(place). Relation foreclosed(place). Relation saultHoldsNote(place).
  Relation keptPromise(place). Relation released(place). Relation noteVoid(place). Relation noteTorn(place).
  Relation matured(place).

  // ── Factor Sault's undertakings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What she does whether or not anyone interferes: makes the vanished out to be deserters; buys what she can of the
  // Muster; leans on the Treasurer; keeps the Board from voting the Settlement by whatever it takes; and, when the
  // Feast passes, takes up the note. Her lightermen do the heavy work and take prisoners rather than kill.
  Person lightermen "Sault's lightermen" at warehouse_floor {
    Role "three big men in salt-stiff jerkins, with cudgels". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Numbers 3. Pronouns they.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "Three big men in salt-stiff jerkins step out from between the stacks. 'Warehouse is shut,' says the biggest.".
    Comes "Sault's lightermen come at you with their cudgels up, not hurrying, the way men do who have done this before.".
    Pleads "The last of the lightermen backs off with his hands open. 'Not paid enough,' he says. 'Not for this.'".
  }
  Topic lightermen_whose with lightermen "Ask the lightermen whose warehouse this is" when true once {
    Says "'The Factor's,' says the biggest, as if that settled it, which in Panhythe it does. 'And the Factor's not here, and the warehouse is shut.' He taps his cudgel against his palm, gently, in no particular time. 'You've asked. Now go and ask somebody who's paid to answer.'".
  }
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(lightermen). Initially Assert serves(lightermen, sault).
  Rule lightermen_captured when captured(lightermen, party) and at(party, ?p)
    says "You wake on the salt crust out on the Pans, at dawn, with a split lip and your purse lighter. Somebody has left you a cup of water, which is the Factor all over." {
    Retract captured(lightermen, party). Retract at(party, ?p). Assert at(party, pans). Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 4. }

  // What the Factor says, seeing her letter in a stranger's hand: nothing.
  Event sault_sees_letter near sault when carries(party, sault_letter) "The Factor's eyes go to the letter in your hand, with her own wax on it, and come back to your face. She says nothing about it at all. She goes on talking about the price of peat.".
  Discovery sault_saw_letter "Factor Sault has seen her letter in your hands.".

  // What the city shows a company that comes back to it, of what was done while it was away.
  Event drum_boots at drum_taproom when durranceCalled(ossel) and heldNow(durrance) "Thomasin Durrance's boots stand on the bar of the Muffled Drum, side by side, toes to the door, under the drum with the cloth over it. Nobody drinks at that end of the bar.".
  Observe exchequer_shut at exchequer_room when quireDrowned(ossel) "The Treasurer's room has been shut up. The cot is stripped, the ledgers stacked, and someone has tied a black ribbon round the empty bottle and left it on the desk.".
  Observe terraces_riot at terraces when riotHappened(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "Glass glitters in the gutters of the Terraces. The Council House windows are boarded, and men of the Watch stand on its portico with pikes, looking anxious.".
  Observe marrable_abed at marrable_room when marrableHurt(ossel) "Ysbel Marrable is sitting up in a chair by the window with her head bandaged and one eye closed. 'They didn't take the other arm,' she says. 'Considerate of them.'".
  Observe landgate_lost at landgate when voted(ossel) and not votePassed(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "On the board, the Speaker's notice: the question of the Veterans' Settlement is lost, the city having no money. Pasted over half of it, the old recruiting bill: LAND AND A PENSION FOR EVERY MAN WHO COMES HOME.".
  Observe landgate_carried at landgate when votePassed(ossel) and not matured(ossel) "On the board, in fresh print: THE VETERANS' SETTLEMENT IS CARRIED. Someone has drawn a pair of scales on it in charcoal, and someone else a goose.".

  // 1. The whisper: from the second day, bills on the Landgate board and talk in the Withies.
  Relation whispered(place).
  Rule whisper_starts when night(ossel) >= 2 and not whispered(ossel) { Assert whispered(ossel). }
  Observe whisper_bill at landgate when whispered(ossel) and not voted(ossel) "A new bill on the board, printed, not handwritten, on good paper: DESERTERS. Those who have left their homes by night since the summer are absconders from the city's service and from their just debts. Information to the Watch. Beneath it, in pencil, someone has written: MY BOY NEVER OWED ANYONE A PENNY.".
  Observe whisper_withies at withies when whispered(ossel) and not dark() and not voted(ossel) "Two women on the boardwalk stop talking as you pass. You catch the word deserter, and the other one saying, quite loudly, that she'd like to see the man who printed it come and say it here.".

  // 2. The Sergeant's silver: on the fifth day she offers to pay the next spring ebb's interest herself, in silver, if
  // Durrance will sergeant her Muster. Durrance takes it only if she has learned what the city did with her oath and
  // nothing yet of what Sault means to do with it.
  Relation durranceKnowsSold(group). Relation durranceKnowsFraud(group). Relation durranceKnowsRelease(group).
  Relation durranceKnowsSault(group). Relation saultOffered(place). Relation durranceSaults(place).
  Rule silver_offered when night(ossel) >= 5 and hour(clock) == 12 and not saultOffered(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) {
    Assert saultOffered(ossel). }
  Rule silver_taken when saultOffered(ossel) and durranceKnowsSold(durrance) and not durranceKnowsSault(durrance)
    and not durranceSaults(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) and night(ossel) < 8 {
    Assert durranceSaults(ossel). Assert interestPaid(ossel). Assert serves(durrance, sault). }
  Observe durrance_refused near durrance when saultOffered(ossel) and not durranceSaults(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) and night(ossel) < 8 "'The Factor sent for me,' says Durrance. 'Offered to pay the silver for the next ebb out of her own pocket, all twelve of us, if I'd sergeant her Muster after.' She turns her pot. 'I told her I'd sworn already. Once is enough for anyone.'".
  Event durrance_took near durrance when durranceSaults(ossel) "Durrance has a new coat on, a good one, and does not meet your eye. 'The Factor's paying the next ebb's silver,' she says. 'All twelve. Out of her own pocket. And I'm her sergeant after.' She drinks. 'The city sold my oath. The Factor bought it back. I don't see the difference, and nor will Ruddock's mother.'".
  Discovery sault_offer_known "Factor Sault offered to pay the next spring ebb's interest in silver from her own purse if Sergeant Durrance would sergeant her Muster.".
  Topic tell_durrance_sold with durrance "Tell Durrance what the city did with the Muster's oaths" when knows(actor, collateral) and not durranceKnowsSold(durrance) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "Durrance hears you out. Then she sits for a long time looking at the drum over the bar with the cloth on it. 'Collateral,' she says at last. 'Like a cow.' She laughs, once. 'Nineteen years. I buried the whole of the Second Platoon at Galt in one trench. And the Board had us in a pawnshop the whole time.' She finishes her pot. 'Well. It's still my oath. They sold it. I didn't.'".
    On discuss { Assert durranceKnowsSold(durrance). }
  }
  Topic tell_durrance_sault with durrance "Tell Durrance what the Factor means to do with the note" when knows(actor, sault_bid) and not durranceKnowsSault(durrance) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "'Govern,' says Durrance. 'With us.' She is very still. 'Not pay us. Own us. Call us out of wherever we are and stand us on the Tidewall in her coats.' Her face does not change. 'She'd feed us. She'd be better than the Board. I'd still be a cow.'".
    On discuss { Assert durranceKnowsSault(durrance). }
  }
  Rule durrance_quits_sault when durranceSaults(ossel) and durranceKnowsSault(durrance) and serves(durrance, sault)
    says "Durrance takes off the Factor's coat and folds it and leaves it on the bench." { Retract serves(durrance, sault). }
  Topic tell_durrance_fraud with durrance "Tell Durrance that the note was drawn to fail" when knows(actor, note_designed) and not durranceKnowsFraud(durrance) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "Durrance listens with her hands at her sides. When you have finished she is quiet so long that you think she has not heard. 'A promise made to be broken,' she says. 'By them. The ones who keep the books.' She looks at her right hand, the one she laid on the Stone. 'Then what did I swear to? A trap?' She stands up. 'An oath sworn into a fraud is no oath. My grandmother could have told them that. I'm not going in when the drum goes. And I'm not going to let anyone else go either.'".
    On discuss { Assert durranceKnowsFraud(durrance). }
  }
  Topic tell_durrance_release with durrance "Tell Durrance that a promise can be discharged by release" when knows(actor, release_law) and not durranceKnowsRelease(durrance) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "'Released,' says Durrance slowly. 'If the one it was made to says, I hold you quit.' She is looking at the drum. 'The city promised us land and pension. That's the promise in their scales. And it's ours. It was made to us.' Her hand closes. 'So if we let them off it. If the Muster stood on the Stone and said, we hold you quit, keep your land...' She stops. 'Then the debt's paid. With our pensions. And the lads come home.' She laughs, not happily. 'Eleven years, and we save the city twice, and the second time we pay for it. Let me think. Don't ask me today. Let me think.'".
    On discuss { Assert durranceKnowsRelease(durrance). }
  }

  // 3. The eighth night: Durrance walks. A company with her an hour before the ebb can hold her back; the drum over
  // the Drum's bar, uncovered and beaten to the stand-down, breaks the step of any soldier of the Third who hears it.
  Relation durranceWalking(place). Relation heldBack(group). Relation drumBeaten(place). Relation elcockTaken(place).
  Relation durranceCalled(place).
  Query durranceSafe() means durranceSpared(ossel) or interestPaid(ossel) or heldBack(durrance) or durranceKnowsFraud(durrance).
  Rule durrance_walks when night(ossel) == 7 and hour(clock) == 1 and not durranceWalking(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance)
    and not durranceSafe() { Assert durranceWalking(ossel). }
  Event durrance_walks_seen near durrance when durranceWalking(ossel) and not heldBack(durrance) and not heldNow(durrance) and hour(clock) == 1
    "Durrance stops. She goes still all at once, the way a soldier comes to attention when an officer walks in, and what she had in her hand falls and she does not look at it. Her eyes are open. She is listening to something. Then she bends and begins, very neatly, to unlace her boots.".
  Action hold_durrance(actor: group, site: place) "Get hold of Durrance and keep her from the Steps" {
    Description "She is a sergeant of nineteen years and she is not awake.".
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(durrance, site) or travelsWith(durrance, actor))
      and durranceWalking(ossel) and not heldBack(durrance) and not triedHolding(actor) and hour(clock) == 1.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert heldBack(durrance). }
    On failure { Assert triedHolding(actor). }
    Result "You get your arms round her from behind and she throws you off as if you were a coat, and you get them round her again, and this time you hang on, and go down with her, and lie on her on the boards while she fights in perfect silence with her eyes open. It goes on a long time. Then, all at once, she goes slack, and blinks, and says in her own voice, 'Get off me, you great lump.'".
    Otherwise "You get hold of her and she simply walks on, and takes you with her a step, and puts you down against the wall with one hand, quite gently, as if you were in her way. Then she goes out barefoot into the night.".
  }
  Relation triedHolding(group).
  Thing third_drum "the Third Company's drum" at drum_taproom {
    State muffled "Over the bar hangs a regimental drum with a black cloth tied over its head.".
    State bare "The Third Company's drum hangs over the bar with its head bare.".
    Change uncover "Pull the cloth off the Third Company's drum and beat the stand-down" from muffled to bare.
  }
  Rule drum_breaks when state(third_drum, bare) and durranceWalking(ossel) and not heldBack(durrance) and hour(clock) == 1
    says "The drum fills the low room. Rap, rap, and the long roll, and rap: the stand-down, that every soldier of the Muster has heard at the end of every day for eleven years. Durrance stops with one boot off. All over the Withies, in the stilt-houses, you hear other things stop: a door, a ladder, someone on the boardwalk. Durrance sits down, hard, on the floor, and looks at the boot in her hand as if she has never seen it." {
    Assert heldBack(durrance). Assert drumBeaten(ossel). }
  Rule drum_offends when state(third_drum, bare) and not drumBeaten(ossel) and at(party, drum_taproom)
    says "Hannelore Rackham comes round the bar and puts the cloth back over the drum's head, and ties it, and looks at you. 'I said don't,' she says. 'I said it kindly.'" {
    Assert state(third_drum, muffled). }
  Rule durrance_goes when night(ossel) == 8 and callings(ossel) == 8 and not durranceCalled(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance)
    and not durranceSafe() {
    Assert durranceCalled(ossel). Assert heldNow(durrance). Assert asleep(durrance). Retract travelsWith(durrance, party).
    Retract willing(durrance, party). Assert at(durrance, ranks). Retract serves(durrance, sault). }
  Relation heldRoom(place). Initially Assert heldRoom(ranks).
  Rule durrance_leaves_place when heldNow(durrance) and at(durrance, ?p) and not heldRoom(?p) { Retract at(durrance, ?p). }
  Rule durrance_gone_told when durranceCalled(ossel) and not spread(durrance_gone)
    and inTessary() says "In the morning Hannelore Rackham stands Thomasin Durrance's boots on the bar of the Muffled Drum, side by side, toes to the door, under the drum with the cloth over it. Nobody drinks there all day." { Assert spread(durrance_gone). }
  Discovery durrance_gone "Sergeant Durrance answered the drum at the eighth night's spring ebb, and walked into the sea.".
  // Whoever is passed over, the weight is the weight: another goes in their place.
  Rule elcock_goes when night(ossel) == 8 and callings(ossel) == 8 and not elcockTaken(ossel) and not interestPaid(ossel)
    and (durranceSpared(ossel) or heldBack(durrance) or durranceKnowsFraud(durrance)) and not heldNow(durrance) {
    Assert elcockTaken(ossel). }
  Rule elcock_told when elcockTaken(ossel) and not knows(party, elcock_known)
    and inTessary() says "In the morning there are twelve pairs of boots on the Watersteps. The eleventh pair is small, and very new, and belongs to Robin Elcock, who was a drummer, and was nineteen." teaches elcock_known { }
  Discovery elcock_known "Durrance was not taken at the eighth night's ebb. Robin Elcock, a drummer of nineteen, was taken in her place.".
  Topic durrance_elcock with durrance "Tell Durrance who went in her place" when knows(actor, elcock_known) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "'Elcock,' says Durrance. 'Robin Elcock. He couldn't keep time. I used to make him march at the back so the step wouldn't go to pieces.' She looks at her hands. 'He went in my place.' A long silence. 'Right. Then I owe him. And I pay what I owe, which is more than this city does.'".
    On discuss { Assert durranceOwes(durrance). }
  }
  Relation durranceOwes(group).

  // 4. The Treasurer: on the ninth day the Factor goes to see him. Unless someone has given him a reason to live, on
  // the tenth night he walks down the Swatch Stair into the full basin.
  Relation quirePressed(place). Relation quireHope(group). Relation quireDrowned(place). Relation quireWillConfess(group).
  Rule quire_pressed when night(ossel) >= 9 and hour(clock) == 11 and not quirePressed(ossel) { Assert quirePressed(ossel). }
  Observe quire_after at exchequer_room when quirePressed(ossel) and not quireDrowned(ossel) and not quireHope(quire) "Quire has not slept. The bottle is empty. 'The Factor came,' he says to you, or to the room. 'She sat in that chair and told me what would happen to me when the Board learns what I signed. Very kindly. She brought eels.'".
  Topic quire_hope with quire "Tell the Treasurer that the called are alive, and that the debt can still be paid" when knows(actor, held_alive) and knows(actor, promise_weight) and quireConfided(actor) and not quireHope(quire) and not quireDrowned(ossel) once {
    Says "Quire stares at you. 'Alive,' he says. 'Asleep. All of them.' He takes his spectacles off, and puts them on, and takes them off. 'And if the Board keeps the promise, they come home.' He stands up, too fast, and holds the desk. 'Then somebody has to tell the Board why. And it has to be the man who signed.' He looks at the empty strongboxes along the wall. 'I'll do it. On the thirteenth day, in front of all of them. It will finish me. Good.'".
    On discuss { Assert quireHope(quire). Assert quireWillConfess(quire). }
  }
  Rule quire_walks when night(ossel) == 10 and hour(clock) == 4 and quirePressed(ossel) and not quireHope(quire) and not quireDrowned(ossel) {
    Assert quireDrowned(ossel). Retract at(quire, exchequer_room). }
  Rule quire_found when quireDrowned(ossel) and not spread(quire_dead)
    and inTessary() says "Word goes along the Tidewall in the morning: the Treasurer went down the Swatch Stair before dawn, into the full basin, with his coat buttoned. The fishermen brought him up at the ebb. In his coat was a list of a hundred and thirty-eight names." { Assert spread(quire_dead). }
  Discovery quire_dead "Treasurer Quire drowned himself at the Swatch on the tenth night, with the list of the called in his coat.".

  // 5. the chairs: the Board as it stands, and what can move it on the thirteenth day.
  // 6. The attempt on Marrable, the night before the eleventh ebb, if the vote looks as if it might pass.
  Measure support(place). Relation marrableHurt(place). Relation marrableGuarded(place). Relation attemptMade(place).
  Query looksLikely() means quireWillConfess(quire) or amauryWillTestify(party) or carries(party, sault_letter) or at(plum, terraces) or plumHome(ossel).
  Rule attempt_on_marrable when night(ossel) == 10 and hour(clock) == 23 and looksLikely() and not attemptMade(ossel) and at(lightermen, ?p) {
    Assert attemptMade(ossel). Retract at(lightermen, ?p). Assert at(lightermen, marrable_room). }
  Rule attempt_succeeds when attemptMade(ossel) and at(lightermen, marrable_room) and hour(clock) == 0 and not at(party, marrable_room)
    and not marrableGuarded(ossel) and not marrableHurt(ossel) and able(lightermen) {
    Assert marrableHurt(ossel). Retract at(lightermen, marrable_room). Assert at(lightermen, warehouse_floor). }
  Rule attempt_guarded when attemptMade(ossel) and at(lightermen, marrable_room) and hour(clock) == 0 and marrableGuarded(ossel) and not at(party, marrable_room) {
    Retract at(lightermen, marrable_room). Assert at(lightermen, warehouse_floor). Assert attemptFoiled(ossel). }
  Relation attemptFoiled(place).
  Rule attempt_foiled_told when attemptFoiled(ossel) and inTessary() and not spread(attempt_foiled_known)
    says "Word in the morning: three men came to Councillor Marrable's door in the night, and found four veterans of the Third on her step, and went away again." { Assert spread(attempt_foiled_known). }
  Discovery attempt_foiled_known "The Factor's lightermen came for Councillor Marrable in the night and found her step guarded.".
  Rule attempt_met at marrable_room when attemptMade(ossel) and at(lightermen, marrable_room) and at(party, marrable_room) and not assails(lightermen, party) and able(lightermen)
    says "Boots on the step, and the door goes in. Three big men in salt-stiff jerkins, with cudgels, who stop when they see that Marrable is not alone." {
    Assert assails(lightermen, party). }
  Rule marrable_hurt_told when marrableHurt(ossel) and not knows(party, marrable_beaten)
    and inTessary() says "Word comes up from the Terraces in the morning: Councillor Marrable was beaten in her own house in the night, by men nobody saw the faces of. She is alive. She will not be at the Board on the thirteenth day." teaches marrable_beaten { }
  Discovery marrable_beaten "Councillor Marrable was beaten in her house the night before the eleventh ebb, and will not be able to speak at the Board.".
  Topic ask_guard with durrance "Ask Durrance to put some of the Third on Councillor Marrable's step" when not heldNow(durrance) and not marrableGuarded(ossel) and night(ossel) < 11 and (knows(actor, sault_bid) or knows(actor, note_designed) or durranceKnowsSold(durrance)) once {
    Says "'Ysbel Marrable?' says Durrance. 'She carried me off the field at Galt with one arm.' She turns on the bench and whistles, and four of the Third look up from four pots. 'Councillor Marrable's step,' she says. 'Nights. Till the Board sits. Nobody goes in that isn't asked.' They go.".
    On discuss { Assert marrableGuarded(ossel). }
  }

  // 7. The riot: the night before the vote, the Factor's men among the veterans at the Exchequer and up the Terrace
  // Steps, unless Fisk will not lead them, or someone the Muster listens to stands them down.
  Relation fiskTurned(group). Relation riotHappened(place). Relation riotCalmed(place). Relation riotGathering(place).
  Topic turn_fisk with fisk "Tell Fisk what the Factor means to do with the Muster" when knows(actor, sault_bid) and not fiskTurned(fisk) once {
    Says "Fisk's grin goes. He reads it twice in your face. 'Own us,' he says. 'With a note. Like a debt.' He takes the new coat off and looks at it. 'She knew my name before I knew hers.' He drops the coat on the floor. 'There's a thing she wants done the night before the Board sits. Lads up the Terrace Steps with torches, shouting. She said it'd show the Board what eight thousand angry soldiers look like.' He shakes his head. 'Not me. Not now. And I'll tell the others why.'".
    On discuss { Assert fiskTurned(fisk). Retract serves(fisk, sault). }
  }
  Rule riot_gathers when night(ossel) == 12 and hour(clock) == 20 and not fiskTurned(fisk) and not riotGathering(ossel) and not voted(ossel) and at(fisk, ?p) {
    Assert riotGathering(ossel). Retract at(fisk, ?p). Assert at(fisk, scriveners_row). }
  Observe riot_scene at scriveners_row when riotGathering(ossel) and not riotHappened(ossel) and not riotCalmed(ossel) "The Row is full of soldiers. Two hundred of them, more, in red coats, with torches, and more coming up from the Withies. Fisk is on a scrivener's desk shouting about the Board. The crowd is not quite a mob yet. It is waiting for something to make it one.".
  Action calm_riot(actor: group, site: place) "Get up on a desk beside Fisk and talk the Muster down" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, scriveners_row) and riotGathering(ossel)
      and not riotHappened(ossel) and not riotCalmed(ossel) and not triedCalming(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert riotCalmed(ossel). }
    On failure { Assert triedCalming(actor). }
    Result "You tell them what is true: that the Board will vote tomorrow, and that if soldiers go up the Terraces tonight with torches, Orme and old Hallam will vote no out of fright, and the Factor knows it, and that is why they are here. It takes a long time, and some of them shout you down, and then one of them says, 'That's right,' and then a lot of them say it. By midnight the Row is empty, and the torches are going home through the Withies in twos and threes.".
    Otherwise "You get up on the desk and they shout you off it.".
  }
  Relation triedCalming(group).
  Action durrance_stands_down(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Durrance to stand the Muster down" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, scriveners_row) and riotGathering(ossel)
      and not riotHappened(ossel) and not riotCalmed(ossel) and travelsWith(durrance, actor) and not serves(durrance, sault).
    On success { Assert riotCalmed(ossel). }
    Result "Durrance does not get up on anything. She walks into the middle of the Row and says, not very loudly, 'Third Company. Fall in.' And they do, the ones who were Third, from all over the crowd, and the ones who were not stop to watch. She looks at them for a long time. 'Go home,' she says. 'The Board sits tomorrow. Let them do their own dirty work.' And they go.".
  }
  Rule riot_breaks when riotGathering(ossel) and hour(clock) == 23 and not riotCalmed(ossel) and not riotHappened(ossel) {
    Assert riotHappened(ossel). }
  Rule riot_told when riotHappened(ossel) and not knows(party, riot_known)
    and inTessary() says "In the night the soldiers went up the Terrace Steps with torches, two hundred of them, shouting for the Board. Somebody threw a stone through the Council House window. Nobody was killed. By morning the Terraces are full of the Watch, and the Board is frightened, which is what somebody wanted." teaches riot_known { }
  Discovery riot_known "On the night before the vote soldiers went up the Terrace Steps with torches and broke the Council House windows. The Board is frightened.".
  Rule riot_ends when riotCalmed(ossel) and at(fisk, scriveners_row) { Retract at(fisk, scriveners_row). Assert at(fisk, drum_taproom). }
  Rule riot_over when riotHappened(ossel) and at(fisk, scriveners_row) and night(ossel) >= 13 { Retract at(fisk, scriveners_row). Assert at(fisk, muster_hall). }

  // ── The Board sits ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // On the thirteenth day, from ten in the morning to two in the afternoon, the Board of Moieties hears the question of
  // the Veterans' Settlement. Whoever is in the chamber may lay before it what they have.
  Person board "the Board of Moieties" at council_chamber {
    Role "the councillors in their carved seats". Ancestry human. Numbers 1. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Seen when inSession().
  }
  Query inSession() means night(ossel) == 13 and hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) < 14 and not voted(ossel).
  Rule sault_sits when inSession() and at(sault, sault_office) { Retract at(sault, sault_office). Assert at(sault, council_chamber). }
  Rule sault_leaves when not inSession() and at(sault, council_chamber) { Retract at(sault, council_chamber). Assert at(sault, sault_office). }
  Rule marrable_sits when inSession() and at(marrable, marrable_room) and not marrableHurt(ossel) { Retract at(marrable, marrable_room). Assert at(marrable, council_chamber). }
  Rule marrable_home when not inSession() and at(marrable, council_chamber) { Retract at(marrable, council_chamber). Assert at(marrable, marrable_room). }
  Observe session_scene at council_chamber when inSession() "The Board of Moieties is sitting. Seven of the eight carved seats are full; the Salt chair is Factor Sault's, and she sits in it with her arms folded, eating nothing for once. Councillors Greaves and Vantage, the furniture, in velvet. Old Hallam asleep or nearly. Haverick of Paper, red-eyed. Orme of Ship, doing sums on his cuff. Dauntry of Rope, looking at Sault. The public bench is full of red coats. The Speaker is reading the question aloud, slowly, as if hoping it will go away.".
  Observe session_marrable at council_chamber when inSession() and at(marrable, council_chamber) "Ysbel Marrable stands at the Eel chair with her pinned sleeve, waiting her turn to speak, and when it comes she speaks for a quarter of an hour without notes, and does not raise her voice once.".
  Observe session_empty_eel at council_chamber when inSession() and marrableHurt(ossel) "The Eel chair is empty. Everybody looks at it and nobody mentions it.".
  Relation boardSawList(place). Relation boardSawTerms(place). Relation boardSawBid(place). Relation amauryTestified(place).
  Relation quireConfessed(place). Relation plumHome(place). Relation saultExposed(place).
  Action lay_list(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Board what is on the Treasurer's list" {
    Time 1. Speaker board.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(board, site) and inSession() and knows(actor, council_knows)
      and not boardSawList(ossel).
    On success { Assert boardSawList(ossel). }
    Result "You tell them: a hundred and thirty-eight names, in the Treasurer's own hand, each with an address and a sum of money sent to the family every month since the summer. Nobody sends money to the mothers of deserters. Orme stops doing sums on his cuff. Haverick looks at Greaves. Greaves looks at the ceiling.".
  }
  Action lay_terms(actor: group, site: place) "Read the Board the terms of the War Note" {
    Time 1. Speaker board.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(board, site) and inSession() and knows(actor, note_terms)
      and not boardSawTerms(ossel).
    On success { Assert boardSawTerms(ossel). }
    Result "You read them the terms. The calling of the oath of Hethra. The Muster as surety. Silver monthly. The principal at the Feast, in a kept promise of equal weight. When you come to the signatures, three of the councillors in the room are on it, and they know it, and the public bench knows it by the time you have finished the sentence. The noise from the red coats is like surf.".
  }
  Action lay_bid(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Board the Factor's letter" {
    Time 1. Speaker board.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(board, site) and inSession() and carries(actor, sault_letter)
      and not boardSawBid(ossel).
    On success { Assert boardSawBid(ossel). Assert saultExposed(ossel). }
    Result "You read them the Factor's letter: I will take up the note and with it the Muster, and Tessary will be governed by someone who can count. Factor Sault does not interrupt. When you have finished she stands up, quite unhurried, and looks round the chamber at each of them, and at the public bench. 'Every word,' she says. 'Somebody should.' And walks out. Dauntry of Rope sits for a moment, and then, very slowly, as if testing whether it is allowed, takes his eyes off her empty chair.".
  }
  // Someone they cannot call a liar: the Board is the debtor, and the Valuer may state a debtor's affairs to it.
  Relation boardHeardTally(place).
  Action lay_tally(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Valuer to tell the Board what the city pledged" {
    Time 1. Speaker tally.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(board, site) and inSession() and travelsWith(tally, actor)
      and not boardHeardTally(ossel) and not tallyUnravelled(ossel).
    On success { Assert boardHeardTally(ossel). }
    Result "The Valuer walks out into the middle of the floor, under the painting of the Kneeling, and opens the ledger. 'You are the debtor,' they say to the Board, 'so I may state your affairs to you. I am the Ninth Valuer of the Balance. I cannot lie; you may ask anyone below.' Then they read out, in the voice of someone reading a bill of lading, what the city pledged, and when, and how many have been taken, by name, in roll order. Somewhere about the fortieth name Councillor Greaves stops pretending to read his papers. Nobody calls the Valuer a liar. Nobody can think how.".
  }
  Event amaury_testifies at council_chamber when inSession() and amauryWillTestify(party) and not amauryTestified(ossel) "The doors open and the King of Hethra comes in between two guards, in a plain coat, and walks up to the painting of the Kneeling and stands under it. 'I am told,' he says to the Board, pleasantly, 'that this city has been paying for my knees.' And he tells them about the hand on the back of his neck, and the oath of his house, and the silver, and when he has done the Speaker has to call for order three times." then {
    Assert amauryTestified(ossel). }
  Event quire_confesses at council_chamber when inSession() and quireWillConfess(quire) and not quireConfessed(ossel) and not quireDrowned(ossel) "Treasurer Quire gets up from the officers' bench, where he is not supposed to speak, and speaks. 'I signed it,' he says. 'Ten years ago. So did you, Greaves, and you, Vantage, and Dauntry. We put the Muster up as surety for a miracle, and the miracle came, and the bill has come after it.' He puts his list on the Speaker's table. 'Those men are not deserters. They are asleep under the sea, and if this Board keeps its promise to them, they come home. If it does not, the rest follow them.' He sits down. He is shaking. Nobody looks at him." then {
    Assert quireConfessed(ossel). Assert boardSawList(ossel). }
  Rule quire_at_board when inSession() and quireWillConfess(quire) and at(quire, exchequer_room) { Retract at(quire, exchequer_room). Assert at(quire, council_chamber). }
  Rule quire_back when not inSession() and at(quire, council_chamber) { Retract at(quire, council_chamber). Assert at(quire, exchequer_room). }
  Rule amaury_comes when inSession() and amauryWillTestify(party) and at(amaury, kings_rooms) { Retract at(amaury, kings_rooms). Assert at(amaury, council_chamber). }
  Rule amaury_back when not inSession() and at(amaury, council_chamber) { Retract at(amaury, council_chamber). Assert at(amaury, kings_rooms). }

  // Haverick's goose, home.
  Person haverick "Lucius Haverick" at terraces {
    Role "who sits for the Paper Moiety on the Board". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "Councillor Haverick has been weeping at a window for some minutes and does not hide it. He turns to you with a printed bill in each hand, the one ruled in red, the other in black, and holds them both out as if you might be about to tell him which was the true one.".
    Greets again "Councillor Haverick has dried his eyes and wept anew in the time it took you to cross the room. He holds out both bills again, the red and the black. 'Which one,' he says, 'did you say was true? I have written it down, and I have written it down both ways.'".
  }
  Topic haverick_goose with haverick "Ask Councillor Haverick what the matter is" when not plumHome(ossel) once {
    Says "'Plum,' says Councillor Haverick. 'Mistress Plum. A goose, sir, a white goose of the old Paper strain, the last of her line. Taken off my lawn on the night of the Muster's homecoming, by persons. I have posted a reward. I have posted three.' He wipes his eyes. 'People think it absurd. A goose. I have no children, sir. I have a goose.'".
  }
  Event plum_home near haverick when following(plum, party) and at(party, terraces) and at(haverick, terraces) and at(plum, ?p) "Mistress Plum sees Councillor Haverick across the Terraces and goes for him at a run, wings out, honking like a wagon with a bad axle, and he goes down on his knees in his good stockings and gathers her up, and she bites him on the ear, and he weeps. 'Anything,' he says to you, over her. 'Anything at all. Name it.' And then, before you can: 'The Settlement? The Paper chair will vote for it. Plum would want me to. She has a great respect for soldiers.' He presses a purse on you as well, without looking at it, and goes back to Plum." then {
    Increase quantity(party, gold) by 10.
    Assert plumHome(ossel). Retract following(plum, party). Retract at(plum, ?p). Assert at(plum, terraces). }

  // The count, at two in the afternoon, in one breath.
  Relation counting(place).
  Rule vote_begins when night(ossel) == 13 and hour(clock) == 14 and not voted(ossel) and not counting(ossel) {
    Assert counting(ossel). Set support(ossel) to 2. }
  Rule vote_marrable when counting(ossel) and marrableHurt(ossel) { Decrease support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_marrable(ossel). }
  Rule vote_plum when counting(ossel) and plumHome(ossel) { Increase support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_plum(ossel). }
  Rule vote_list when counting(ossel) and boardSawList(ossel) { Increase support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_list(ossel). }
  Rule vote_terms when counting(ossel) and boardSawTerms(ossel) { Increase support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_terms(ossel). }
  Rule vote_quire when counting(ossel) and quireConfessed(ossel) { Increase support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_quire(ossel). }
  Rule vote_amaury when counting(ossel) and amauryTestified(ossel) { Increase support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_amaury(ossel). }
  Rule vote_bid when counting(ossel) and boardSawBid(ossel) { Increase support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_bid(ossel). }
  Rule vote_tally when counting(ossel) and boardHeardTally(ossel) { Increase support(ossel) by 1. Assert counted_tally(ossel). }
  Relation counted_tally(place).
  Rule vote_riot when counting(ossel) and riotHappened(ossel) { Decrease support(ossel) by 2. Assert counted_riot(ossel). }
  Relation counted_marrable(place). Relation counted_plum(place). Relation counted_list(place). Relation counted_terms(place).
  Relation counted_quire(place). Relation counted_amaury(place). Relation counted_bid(place). Relation counted_riot(place).
  Rule vote_carried when counting(ossel) and support(ossel) >= 5 {
    Retract counting(ossel). Assert voted(ossel). Assert votePassed(ossel). }
  Rule vote_lost when counting(ossel) and support(ossel) < 5 {
    Retract counting(ossel). Assert voted(ossel). }
  Rule vote_carried_told when votePassed(ossel) and inTessary() and not spread(vote_known)
    says "At two in the afternoon the Board of Moieties votes on the Veterans' Settlement. The bell on the Council House rings, and goes on ringing, and down in the Withies people come out onto the boardwalks to listen, and somebody shouts, and then everybody does. Land and a pension for every soldier who came home. Carried." { Assert spread(vote_known). }
  Rule vote_lost_told when voted(ossel) and not votePassed(ossel) and inTessary() and not spread(vote_known)
    says "At two in the afternoon the Board of Moieties votes on the Veterans' Settlement, and the Council House bell does not ring. The question is lost. There is no money, says the Speaker's notice on the Landgate board, and the city will not make promises it cannot keep. Under it, by evening, someone has pasted the old recruiting bill: LAND AND A PENSION FOR EVERY MAN WHO COMES HOME." { Assert spread(vote_known). }
  Discovery vote_known "The Board of Moieties has voted on the Veterans' Settlement.".

  // ── The Seal ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A Settlement voted is not a Settlement kept: eight thousand deeds must pass under the Great Seal. The night the
  // vote is carried, the Factor's men come for it.
  Relation sealStolen(place). Relation sealGuarded(place). Relation sealTried(place).
  Item great_seal "the Great Seal of Tessary" is seal_kind at seals_inner.
  Kind seal_kind "a disc of dark bronze the size of a plate" is treasure worth 0 weighing 4
    described "The Great Seal of Tessary: a pair of scales over a wave, and round the rim, in old letters, WHAT IS SEALED IS DONE.".
  Initially Assert owns(deckle, great_seal).
  Topic deckle_warned with deckle "Warn the Keeper that the Factor's men will come for the Seal tonight" when votePassed(ossel) and not sealGuarded(ossel) and not sealTried(ossel) and (knows(actor, sault_bid) or knows(actor, riot_known) or knows(actor, marrable_beaten)) once {
    Says "Deckle looks at you as if you had suggested the sea might come in. 'The Seal,' he says, 'has not left this room in three hundred years.' Then he looks at the bell glass, and at the door, which has a lock a child could open. 'The Watch is the Factor's,' he says slowly. 'Everybody knows that.' He sits down. 'I shall sit up with it. I shall sit up with it myself. And if you know anyone who would sit up with me, who carries something heavier than a pen...'".
    On discuss { Assert deckleWarned(deckle). }
  }
  Relation deckleWarned(group).
  Topic ask_guard_seal with durrance "Ask Durrance to put a guard on the Office of Seals tonight" when votePassed(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) and not sealGuarded(ossel) and not sealTried(ossel) and not serves(durrance, sault) once {
    Says "'The Seal,' says Durrance. 'Of course. She'll not let a vote stop her.' She is already on her feet. 'Six of the Third, inside the Office, round the Keeper's table. They can sleep in the morning. They've slept in worse.'".
    On discuss { Assert sealGuarded(ossel). }
  }
  Topic fisk_guard_seal with fisk "Ask Fisk to get some of the lads round the Office of Seals tonight" when votePassed(ossel) and fiskTurned(fisk) and not sealGuarded(ossel) and not sealTried(ossel) once {
    Says "'The Seal,' says Fisk, and laughs. 'That's where she'll go, isn't it. Course it is. Eight thousand deeds and not one of them worth the paper without it.' He is already pulling on his old coat, the red one. 'I know every lad she's paying. I'll have the ones she isn't in the Keeper's room by dark, and the ones she is can come and try it.'".
    On discuss { Assert sealGuarded(ossel). }
  }
  Topic marrable_guard_seal with marrable "Ask Councillor Marrable to put a guard on the Seal tonight" when votePassed(ossel) and not marrableHurt(ossel) and not sealGuarded(ossel) and not sealTried(ossel) and (knows(actor, sault_bid) or knows(actor, riot_known) or knows(actor, marrable_beaten)) once {
    Says "Marrable looks at you for a moment, and then at her one hand. 'She'll go for it tonight,' she says. 'Of course she will.' She stands. 'The Eel Moiety has boatmen who have never once in their lives done what the Watch told them. I'll have six of them in the Keeper's room by dark, with oars.'".
    On discuss { Assert sealGuarded(ossel). }
  }
  Rule seal_raid when votePassed(ossel) and night(ossel) == 13 and hour(clock) == 23 and not sealTried(ossel) and able(lightermen) and at(lightermen, ?p) {
    Assert sealTried(ossel). Retract at(lightermen, ?p). Assert at(lightermen, seals_inner). }
  Rule seal_raid_met at seals_inner when sealTried(ossel) and at(lightermen, seals_inner) and at(party, seals_inner) and not assails(lightermen, party) and able(lightermen) and not sealStolen(ossel)
    says "The door of the Keeper's room is forced from the hall side. Three lightermen, cudgels out, who had expected an old man." {
    Assert assails(lightermen, party). }
  Rule seal_taken when sealTried(ossel) and at(lightermen, seals_inner) and hour(clock) == 0 and not at(party, seals_inner)
    and not sealGuarded(ossel) and not sealHidden(ossel) and able(lightermen) and at(great_seal, seals_inner) {
    Assert sealStolen(ossel). Retract at(great_seal, seals_inner). Assert inside(great_seal, sault_strongbox).
    Retract at(lightermen, seals_inner). Assert at(lightermen, warehouse_floor). }
  Rule seal_bed when sealTried(ossel) and at(lightermen, seals_inner) and hour(clock) == 0 and sealHidden(ossel) and not sealGuarded(ossel) and not at(party, seals_inner) {
    Retract at(lightermen, seals_inner). Assert at(lightermen, warehouse_floor). Assert sealRaidFoiled(ossel). }
  Rule seal_kept when sealTried(ossel) and at(lightermen, seals_inner) and hour(clock) == 0 and sealGuarded(ossel) and not at(party, seals_inner) {
    Retract at(lightermen, seals_inner). Assert at(lightermen, warehouse_floor). Assert sealRaidFoiled(ossel). }
  Relation sealRaidFoiled(place).
  Rule seal_kept_told when sealRaidFoiled(ossel) and inTessary() and not spread(seal_kept_known)
    says "In the night three lightermen broke into the Office of Seals and found the Keeper's room full of people who had been waiting up for them, and left faster than they came." { Assert spread(seal_kept_known). }
  Discovery seal_kept_known "The Factor's lightermen tried for the Great Seal in the night and were driven off.".
  Rule seal_stolen_told when sealStolen(ossel) and not spread(seal_gone)
    and inTessary() says "The Office of Seals does not open in the morning. The Keeper is sitting on the step in his nightshirt with his head in his hands: the Great Seal was taken in the night, and without it not one deed of the Settlement can be sealed." { Assert spread(seal_gone). }
  Discovery seal_gone "The Great Seal of Tessary was stolen the night after the vote. Without it the Settlement's deeds cannot be sealed.".
  Thing sault_strongbox "the Factor's strongbox" at sault_office {
    Holds.
    State locked closed "Behind the Factor's desk stands an iron strongbox the size of a dog kennel.".
    State open "The Factor's strongbox stands open.".
    Change pick "Pick the strongbox" from locked to open needing lockwork at sault_office.
  }
  // Picked in front of her: she lets you, and says what is in it, which is nothing yet.
  Event strongbox_seen near sault when state(sault_strongbox, open) and at(sault, sault_office) and at(party, sault_office) and not sealStolen(ossel)
    "Factor Sault watches you do it, with her chin on her fist. 'Empty,' she says, before the lid is up. 'I keep the money at the pans, where there are forty men who'd notice.' She reaches over and pushes the lid shut with one finger, and the lock goes home. 'Come back after the thirteenth day if you want to see something worth the trouble.'" then {
    Assert state(sault_strongbox, locked). }
  Rule seal_back when sealStolen(ossel) and (keeps(deckle, great_seal) or at(great_seal, seals_inner)) { Retract sealStolen(ossel). Retract inside(great_seal, sault_strongbox). }
  Event seal_returned near deckle when keeps(deckle, great_seal) "The Keeper takes the Seal from you in both hands and holds it against his chest like a child that was lost in a market. Then he puts it under its glass, and rings for his clerks, and they come running, all of them, with their sleeves rolled up." then {
    Retract keeps(deckle, great_seal). Assert at(great_seal, seals_inner). }

  // The deeds: sealed through the fourteenth day if the vote passed and the Seal is under its glass. The deeds for the
  // held cannot be put into their hands in Tessary.
  Relation deedsSealed(place). Relation deedsDelivered(place).
  Rule deeds_sealed when votePassed(ossel) and night(ossel) == 14 and hour(clock) == 16 and not sealStolen(ossel) and at(great_seal, seals_inner) and not deedsSealed(ossel) {
    Assert deedsSealed(ossel). }
  Rule deeds_sealed_told when deedsSealed(ossel) and inTessary() and not spread(deeds_sealed_known)
    says "All day the Office of Seals has worked with its doors shut and every clerk in the Lettered Quarter borrowed; by four in the afternoon the last deed has passed under the Seal, and they begin carrying them out to the Withies in baskets, with the Muster's own sergeants calling the names. Land and a pension. A deed to every hand." { Assert spread(deeds_sealed_known). }
  Discovery deeds_sealed_known "The deeds of the Settlement have been sealed and given out.".
  Item held_deeds "the deeds of the called" is deeds_kind at seals_inner hidden until deeds_for_held.
  Kind deeds_kind "a casket of sealed deeds" is gear worth 0 weighing 3
    described "A cedar casket with a hundred and sixty-odd deeds in it, each sealed with the scales and the wave: land and a pension, made out to soldiers of the Long Muster who are not in Tessary to receive them.".
  Discovery deeds_for_held "The deeds made out to the called cannot be put into their hands in Tessary. They wait in a casket at the Office of Seals for whoever will carry them down.".
  Rule deeds_casket at seals_inner when deedsSealed(ossel) and not knows(party, deeds_for_held)
    says "On the Keeper's table, apart from the rest, stands a cedar casket. 'The deeds of the ones who are not here,' says Deckle. 'The Settlement says every hand. I cannot put these into a hand.' He looks at you. 'I am told that somebody may know where those hands are.'" teaches deeds_for_held { }
  Initially Assert lends(deckle, held_deeds, party).
  Action take_deeds(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Take the casket of the deeds of the called from the Keeper" {
    Speaker deckle. Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(deckle, site) and knows(actor, deeds_for_held)
      and memberOf(recipient, actor) and awake(recipient) and at(held_deeds, site).
    Resolve acquire(held_deeds, deeds_kind, recipient).
    On success { Retract at(held_deeds, site). }
    Result "Deckle puts the casket in your arms. It is heavier than paper should be. 'Every hand,' he says. 'That is what it says. Every hand.'".
  }
  Rule deeds_word when deedsSealed(ossel) and not spread(deeds_word_known) and not at(party, seals_inner)
    and inTessary() says "A boy from the Office of Seals finds you: the Keeper asks for you. There is a casket of deeds that nobody in Tessary can deliver." { Assert spread(deeds_word_known). }
  Discovery deeds_word_known "The Keeper of the Seal has a casket of deeds for the called, and asks for you.".
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/strong:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── The Strongrooms ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Under the Hall of Oaths, cut in the bedrock of the delta by people of the Mathematical Age: white stone that hums,
  // rooms that weigh whoever stands in them, and at the bottom the Balance, which makes a sworn promise binding in the
  // prima materium. The Scruples keep it. They were the drowned city's clerks; a thousand years beside the Balance have
  // made them pale, long-lived, unable to lie, and ruled like paper. Each pledged their name to it at birth.
  Place strongrooms "the Strongrooms" is site within ossel at 2, 0.
  Place sr_head "the stair-head" is level within strongrooms.
  Place sr_halls "the halls of the Scruples" is level within strongrooms.
  Place sr_deep "the deep rooms" is level within strongrooms.
  Place long_stair "the head of the Long Stair" is room within sr_head at 1, 0 underground.
  Place antechamber "the Antechamber of Weights" is room within sr_halls at 1, 0 underground.
  Place clerks_hall "the Hall of Clerks" is room within sr_halls at 1, 1 underground.
  Place archive "the Archive of Instruments" is room within sr_halls at 0, 1 underground.
  Place defaults_room "the Room of Defaults" is room within sr_halls at 0, 2 underground.
  Place dormitory "the standing dormitory" is room within sr_halls at 2, 1 underground.
  Place comptroller_office "the Comptroller's office" is room within sr_halls at 1, 2 underground.
  Place gallery "the Gallery of Pans" is room within sr_deep at 1, 0 underground.
  Place weighing_chamber "the Weighing Chamber" is room within sr_deep at 1, 1 underground.

  Passage long_stair_way "the Long Stair" is stair between long_stair and antechamber taking 20 minutes.
  Passage ante_door "the inner door of the Antechamber" is doorway between antechamber and clerks_hall.
  Passage archive_arch "the archive arch" is arch between clerks_hall and archive.
  Passage defaults_door "the door of the Room of Defaults" is door between archive and defaults_room.
  Passage dorm_way "the dormitory passage" is doorway between clerks_hall and dormitory.
  Passage office_door "the Comptroller's door" is door between clerks_hall and comptroller_office.
  Passage counting_stair "the Counting Stair" is stair between clerks_hall and gallery.
  Passage chamber_door "the pan door" is door between gallery and weighing_chamber.

  Observe long_stair_scene at long_stair when true "Behind the black wall the dark is dry and smells of stone dust and, faintly, of hot metal. A stair goes down, straight and steep and very long, cut in white rock that gives back a little light of its own. You can hear a hum, below the edge of hearing, in your teeth. The steps are worn in the middle, but not by feet: by something that went up and down them on a groove for a very long time, before the Scruples, before the old city, when whoever cut this place was still here to need it.".
  Observe ante_scene at antechamber when true "A square white room with a floor of a single slab, smooth as a pond. When you step onto it the slab gives, very slightly, as a pan of a balance gives, and steadies. Around the walls ruled lines run at the height of a man's mouth, and as you speak they brighten along their length, and fade, as if writing down what was said. A notice in three scripts, one of them Tessarine: WHAT IS SAID HERE IS HELD.".
  Observe hall_scene at clerks_hall when true "A long white hall full of desks, and at the desks the Scruples, writing: forty or fifty of them in grey, pale as candles, the ruled lines on their hands and faces moving a little as they move. Nobody speaks above a murmur. The pens make a sound like rain. At the end of the hall a stair goes down; beside it, a door with the word COMPTROLLER cut over it, and nothing else.".
  Observe archive_scene at archive when true "Shelves to the ceiling, and the ceiling out of sight. On them, not books, but instruments: slabs, rolls, tablets, sheets of something like black glass, each with a tag. Every promise the Balance has ever held is here, the Scruples say, from the oath of a king to the bet of a fishwife. In the far wall, a door bound in iron with a single word on it in the ruled script, which you cannot read, and which nobody here looks at.".
  Observe defaults_scene at defaults_room when true "A small room, which is the surprise. After the archive's endless shelves, this is a cupboard: one table, one lamp that lights when you come in, one ledger. The ledger is thin. The Scruples do not record many defaults.".
  Observe dorm_scene at dormitory when true "The Scruples sleep standing. Rows of them along the walls in a dim room, eyes closed, hands folded, breathing very slowly and all together. Some have tags at their wrists, like the instruments in the archive. A very young Scruple at the end of a row has a book open under her folded hands.".
  Observe office_scene_c at comptroller_office when true "A white room with nothing in it but a desk, a chair that has never been sat in, and the Comptroller standing behind the desk. On the desk lies one sheet of black glass, ruled, which he has been reading for a very long time.".
  Observe gallery_scene at gallery when true "A gallery cut through the rock with the hum much louder here, a sound you feel in your breastbone. At the far end a door of white metal with no handle stands between two great pans hung on chains from the roof. One pan holds a block of lead cut with nine ruled lines. The other is empty, and the door does not open. Along the wall, on a rack, a set of brass weights, each with its number of lines. Over the door: NINE AGAINST NINE.".
  Observe chamber_scene_w at weighing_chamber when true "The Weighing Chamber is a nave cut so deep into the bedrock that the hum is the only sound left in it. The Balance hangs in it from a beam lost in the dark overhead: two pans each the size of a fishing boat, and a pointer as tall as a mast at rest against a dial of ruled lines. In one pan, very small at the bottom of it, lies a single sheet of black glass. In the other are oaths: not things but the shapes of things, eight thousand faint warm shapes like breath on a cold window, each the size of a hand laid flat. Beyond the Balance, at the end of the nave, is a door with no frame, standing on its own, through which you can see a white floor going on for ever.".
  Observe chamber_level at weighing_chamber when not discharged(ossel) "The pointer leans a hair's breadth toward the black glass, and the oaths in the other pan stir now and then, like sleepers.".

  // ── The Scruples ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person scruples "the Scruples at their desks" at clerks_hall {
    Role "who keep the Balance's books". Ancestry human. Numbers 1. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Greets "The nearest of the clerks lifts their pen from the page and waits, without looking up, as if for dictation.".
    Greets again "The nearest of the clerks does not look up, but the pen has already moved to the line beneath, ready to put you down. 'Name,' says a voice, 'and what you owe. Everyone owes. We are only interested in how much more than they think.'".
  }
  Topic scruples_asked with scruples "Ask the clerks at the desks what they are writing" when true once {
    Says "The nearest clerk finishes the line before looking up. 'Promises,' she says. 'As they are kept. A fishwife in the Withies has paid her rent. A ferryman has sworn to his wife on the Watersteps that he will not drink, and has drunk, and it is a small thing and the Balance has noted it. A great deal of the city stands on the old instruments without knowing it, you see. We write what is kept and what is not.' She dips her pen. 'Mostly it is not.'".
  }
  Topic scruples_names with scruples "Ask the clerks what they are called" when true once {
    Says "Three or four of the nearest clerks look up at once, which they evidently find embarrassing. 'By our offices,' says one. 'I am the Third Copyist of Settlements. He is the Clerk of Small Wagers. She has been the Second Tare-Clerk for two hundred years and will be for two hundred more.' He touches his wrist, where there is a pale band like the mark of a ring long worn. 'Our names are on the white floor beyond the Balance. One gives it at birth, as surety for a lifetime's exactness. One does not miss it. One cannot miss what one has never had.' The others go back to their pens, a little too quickly.".
  }
  Topic scruples_defaults with scruples "Ask the clerks about the iron door in the archive" when true once {
    Says "The pens stop, all of them, all down the hall, and then start again a beat later, as if nothing had happened. The Clerk of Small Wagers does not look up. 'The Room of Defaults,' he says, very quietly. 'It is the Comptroller's room. Nobody else goes in.' He dips his pen. 'He goes in once a year, on the anniversary of the Drowning, and stays the night, and comes out in the morning, and nobody asks.' The Second Tare-Clerk says his office, not loudly, and he says nothing more.".
  }
  Topic scruples_surface with scruples "Ask the clerks what they think of the city above" when true once {
    Says "'Tessary?' The Clerk of Small Wagers puts down his pen. 'We write it down. We are very fond of it, in the way one is fond of weather.' He turns back a page. 'This morning a woman in the Withies swore on the Watersteps that she would never speak to her sister again, and at noon she spoke to her sister. The Balance holds the steps; we entered it.' He shakes his head. 'They do it all day. They do not know they are doing it. Sometimes I think the whole of the drowned city went down because nobody up there ever once meant what they said, and sometimes I think that is what I would like most to try.' The Second Tare-Clerk looks at him, and he picks up his pen.".
  }
  Topic scruples_sleep with scruples "Ask the clerks why they sleep standing" when true once {
    Says "'One sleeps as one stands before the Balance,' says the Second Tare-Clerk, without looking up. 'Upright, and ready to be weighed.' A pause. 'Also, there is not room for beds. The Mathematical people built for a thousand clerks and there are eleven thousand of us. The archive takes precedence.'".
  }
  Person copyist "the Fourteenth Copyist" at clerks_hall {
    Role "a very young Scruple with ink on her ruled fingers and a bad habit of looking at the stair". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Wants chapbook.
  }
  Topic copyist_surface with copyist "Ask the Copyist about the surface" when true once {
    Says "The Copyist puts her pen down with enormous care. 'Is it true,' she says, very low, 'that up there people say things they do not mean? All the time? And nothing happens?' Before you can answer: 'Someone left a book in the Hall of Oaths with the silver once. Poems. In Tessarine. I have read it two hundred and eleven times.' She looks at the stair. 'There is one about a woman who promises to wait for a sailor and does not. And it is sad. And nobody unravels. I have never understood anything so well.'".
  }
  Relation copyistFriend(group).
  Event copyist_book near copyist when keeps(copyist, ?b) and itemKind(?b, chapbook) "The Copyist takes the chapbook in both hands and does not open it, as if it might go off. 'Twelve new ones,' she says. 'Twelve.' She puts it inside her coat, against her ruled skin. 'I am in your debt. I know exactly how much. If there is a door down here you need opened, I can file for it. I am very good at forms.'" then {
    Assert copyistFriend(party). }
  Discovery release_law "In the Scruples' law a promise is discharged in two ways: when it is kept, and when the one it was made to holds the promisor quit. A release freely given weighs as much as the keeping." {
    Known by copyist, comptroller, tally.
  }
  Topic copyist_release with copyist "Ask the Copyist how a promise can be discharged" when true once {
    Says "'Two ways,' says the Copyist promptly, as if reciting. 'Kept, or released. If I promise you a thing, and give it, it is kept. If I promise you a thing and you say to me, freely, I hold you quit of it, that is a release, and in the Balance it weighs the same as the keeping.' She frowns. 'People forget the second. It is in the first chapter. I think people stop reading after the first page.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, release_law). }
  }
  Discovery assembly_law "Any Scruple may indict another before the Assembly of the Scruples. The Assembly meets in the Weighing Chamber at the Settlement, and the Notary sits with it. It has happened twice in a thousand years.".
  Topic copyist_assembly with copyist "Ask the Copyist whether a Scruple can be called to account" when knows(actor, compact_read) once {
    Says "The Copyist goes quite still. 'An indictment,' she says. 'Before the Assembly. Any of us may bring one against any other, even the least against the greatest. It is in the second chapter.' She swallows. 'It has happened twice. The Assembly sits in the Weighing Chamber at a Settlement, and the Notary comes out of the Holding to sit with it, and what is found is found. Both times, the one indicted...' She stops, and makes a small gesture of something coming apart. 'Why do you ask?'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, assembly_law). }
  }
  Action copyist_files(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Copyist to file for the Room of Defaults to be opened to you" {
    Speaker copyist. Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(copyist, site) and copyistFriend(actor)
      and state(defaults_lock, locked).
    On success { Assert state(defaults_lock, open). }
    Result "The Copyist fills out a form requesting the form for a request, and then the request, and takes them up the hall to a desk, and from that desk to another, and comes back an hour later with the iron key on a ribbon. 'An inspection of records in the course of an inventory,' she says. 'The Ninth Valuer's inventory. They will not mind. They are very thorough.' She looks at the key. 'Nobody has asked to see that room in my lifetime.'".
  }

  // ── The weighing floor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What is said on the Antechamber's floor is held. A company that comes down from Tessary, where people swear about
  // everything, may say something it will have to keep.
  Relation sworeToFind(group).
  Action swear_find(actor: group, site: place) "Say, 'I'll find Davy Teazle if it kills me'" {
    Description "It is the kind of thing anyone says.".
    Time 0.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, antechamber) and knows(actor, davy_went)
      and not sworeToFind(actor) and heldNow(davy).
    On success { Assert sworeToFind(actor). Assert registered(actor). }
    Result "The ruled lines round the walls brighten all along their length, and hold, and fade. The floor under you dips a hair, and steadies. Somewhere far below, something has written it down.".
  }
  Observe swore_noted at antechamber when sworeToFind(party) and travelsWith(tally, party) and at(party, antechamber) "'That was held,' says the Valuer, looking at the walls. 'I would not have said if it kills me.'".

  // ── Lies to the Valuer ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Valuer asked a promise of honesty at the Hall of Oaths; below, it is held.
  Relation askedEmployer(group). Relation keptFaith(group). Relation brokeFaith(group).
  Observe tally_asks at antechamber when travelsWith(tally, party) and at(party, antechamber) and hiredBySault(party) and not askedEmployer(party) "On the weighing floor the Valuer stops and turns to you. 'A question,' they say, 'which I should have asked above. Are you in anyone's employ in this matter?'".
  Action tell_tally_truth(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Valuer that Factor Sault hired you to find out who takes the veterans" {
    Speaker tally. Time 0.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, antechamber) and travelsWith(tally, actor)
      and hiredBySault(actor) and not askedEmployer(actor).
    On success { Assert askedEmployer(actor). Assert keptFaith(actor). }
    Result "The lines on the walls brighten and fade. 'The Factor of the Salt Moiety,' says the Valuer. 'Who carried the silver.' They write it down. 'Thank you. That cannot have been comfortable to say. I will remember that you said it here.'".
  }
  Action lie_to_tally(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the Valuer that you are in no one's employ" {
    Speaker tally. Time 0.
    Grave "You promised the Valuer not to lie to them, and here what is said is held.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, antechamber) and travelsWith(tally, actor)
      and hiredBySault(actor) and not askedEmployer(actor).
    On success { Assert askedEmployer(actor). Assert brokeFaith(actor). Assert forswornParty(actor). }
    Result "The ruled lines round the walls go dark, all of them at once, and the floor under you drops a finger's breadth and does not come up. The Valuer looks at the walls, and at you. They do not say anything. They write something down, and close the ledger, and do not open it again for a long while.".
  }

  // ── The Room of Defaults ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Thing defaults_lock "the iron door" on defaults_door {
    State locked blocking "The door of the Room of Defaults is bound in iron and locked.".
    State open "The iron door of the Room of Defaults stands open.".
    Change pick "Pick the lock of the iron door" from locked to open needing lockwork at archive.
  }
  Action tally_opens(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Valuer to open the Room of Defaults in the course of the inventory" {
    Speaker tally. Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, archive) and travelsWith(tally, actor)
      and knows(actor, compact_read) and state(defaults_lock, locked) and not brokeFaith(actor).
    On success { Assert state(defaults_lock, open). }
    Result "The Valuer looks at the iron door for some time. 'The compact of the old city is not on my inventory,' they say. 'But the city of Tessary claims the old city's oaths as its heir, and so its defaults are the city's defaults, and so they bear on the collateral.' They lay a ruled hand flat on the iron, and the lock turns over inside the door with a sound like a slow bell. 'I find that I want to see it,' they say. 'I note that I want to.'".
  }
  Discovery default_record "The Room of Defaults records the drowned city's compact as broken eleven hundred years ago, in the Comptroller's own hand: 'The sea had the city. The ledger did not keep. Default entered by the clerk who swore it.' Beside the entry, in the same hand, a reckoning runs down the margin for a thousand years, and ends in fresh ink: 'Tessary, heir. War note drawn. Repayment at the weight of a people's promise. At foreclosure, eight thousand oaths.' And under it, a single word: 'Balanced.'" {
    Source defaults_ledger "the thin ledger on the table" at defaults_room readable by party.
  }
  Discovery note_designed "The War Note was drawn to fail. The Comptroller swore the drowned city's compact eleven hundred years ago and could not keep it; his default left a hole in the Balance's ledger. He set Tessary's repayment at a weight its heir could never meet, so that at foreclosure the Muster's oaths would fall into the Holding and fill the hole he made.".
  Observe designed_seen near party when knows(party, default_record) and knows(party, note_terms) and knows(party, promise_weight) and not knows(party, note_designed) "You read the margin again with the War Note's terms in your head. The weight of a people's promise, and a city with exactly one such promise in its books and no money to keep it. Eight thousand oaths at foreclosure. Balanced. The repayment was never meant to be made." teaches note_designed.
  Relation tallySawDefaults(place).
  Event tally_reads_defaults at defaults_room when travelsWith(tally, party) and knows(party, default_record) "The Valuer reads the ledger over your shoulder, and then reads it again, alone, with their finger on the lines, the way a child reads. When they straighten, the ruled lines on their face have gone faint, as if something had rubbed at them. 'He swore the compact,' they say. 'He did not keep it. And he has drawn the city's note so that it cannot be paid, so that the Muster will fall in and cover it.' A long pause. 'A promise made in order to be broken is not a promise. It is the first thing we are taught. It is the gravest thing one of us can do.' They close the ledger very gently. 'I do not know what I am going to do.'" then {
    Assert tallySawDefaults(ossel). }

  // ── The Gallery of Pans ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The door to the Weighing Chamber opens when the empty pan is made to balance the nine-line lead: a test every
  // Scruple passes as a child. The brass on the rack is two, three, four and five.
  Thing door_pan "the empty pan" at gallery {
    Holds.
    State hanging "The empty pan hangs high on its chains, the lead's pan low.".
  }
  Initially Assert receptacle(door_pan).
  Kind brass_two "a brass weight of two lines" is gear worth 1 weighing 2 described "A flat brass weight with two ruled lines cut across it.".
  Kind brass_three "a brass weight of three lines" is gear worth 1 weighing 3 described "A flat brass weight with three ruled lines cut across it.".
  Kind brass_four "a brass weight of four lines" is gear worth 1 weighing 4 described "A flat brass weight with four ruled lines cut across it.".
  Kind brass_five "a brass weight of five lines" is gear worth 1 weighing 5 described "A flat brass weight with five ruled lines cut across it.".
  Item w_two "a brass weight of two lines" is brass_two at gallery.
  Item w_three "a brass weight of three lines" is brass_three at gallery.
  Item w_four "a brass weight of four lines" is brass_four at gallery.
  Item w_five "a brass weight of five lines" is brass_five at gallery.
  Query panBalanced() means (inside(w_four, door_pan) and inside(w_five, door_pan) and not inside(w_two, door_pan) and not inside(w_three, door_pan))
    or (inside(w_two, door_pan) and inside(w_three, door_pan) and inside(w_four, door_pan) and not inside(w_five, door_pan)).
  Thing counter_door "the white door" on chamber_door {
    State shut blocking "The white door between the pans has no handle, and does not open.".
    State open "The white door stands open, the pans level on their chains.".
  }
  Rule door_balances at gallery when panBalanced() and state(counter_door, shut)
    says "The empty pan sinks, slowly, and the lead rises to meet it, and the two hang level. The pointer between them settles on its mark. Without any sound, the white door opens." { Assert state(counter_door, open). }
  Rule door_unbalances when not panBalanced() and state(counter_door, open) and not chamberOpened(ossel) { Assert state(counter_door, shut). }
  Relation chamberOpened(place).
  Observe pan_wrong at gallery when not panBalanced() and inside(?w, door_pan) "The pan has something in it, and has moved, but the pointer between the pans has not come to its mark.".

  // The Weights: bailiffs of stone and bronze, who seize the forsworn and those in default.
  Species weight_kind "a Weight" like bronze_construct temperament obedient
    described "A figure of bronze and white stone twice the height of a man, with a pair of scales cast into its chest where a heart would be. It does not move unless something is owed.".
  Person weights "the Weights" at gallery {
    Role "two bailiffs of bronze and white stone, standing either side of the door". Species weight_kind. Level 8. Numbers 2. Pronouns they.
    Comes "The Weights come down the gallery toward you, not fast, with their bronze hands open: not to strike, to take hold.".
  }
  // Bailiffs seize; they do not kill. Whoever they take is carried up the Long Stair and put out through the black wall,
  // which does not open to them again.
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(weights).
  Relation barredBelow(group).

  Initially Assert tolerates(weights, party).
  Initially Assert peaceable(weights).
  // The Weights do not fight. They take hold, the way the tide does, and nobody has ever made them let go.
  Rule weights_seize when forswornParty(party) and at(party, ?p) and at(weights, ?p) and not barredBelow(party)
    says "The Weights turn their heads, both together, with a grinding of bronze. The scales in their chests have tipped. They come down the gallery toward you, not fast, with their bronze hands open, and there is nothing to be done about it at all: you might as well fight the sea. The hands close on you very gently, the way a careful man picks up something that might break. You are carried, a long way, up the Long Stair in the dark, and set down on the floor of the Hall of Oaths, and when you turn round there is only the black wall, and it is cold." {
    Retract at(party, ?p). Assert at(party, oath_court). Assert barredBelow(party). }

  // ── The Comptroller ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Eldest of the Scruples. He swore the drowned city's compact, and has kept the ledger for eleven hundred years
  // since he failed to keep his word. He cannot lie. He can choose what to say.
  Person comptroller "the Comptroller" at comptroller_office {
    Role "eldest of the Scruples, tall and thin as a rule, the ruled lines on his face so close they look like shading". Ancestry human. Calling mage. Level 9. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Greets "The Comptroller lifts his face from the black glass, slowly, as though out of water. His eyes are the colour of old paper. 'You have come down,' he says, 'from the debtor's city. Very well. You may ask.'".
    Greets again "The Comptroller does not come up out of the black glass this time, but speaks to it, and the glass speaks to you. 'You have come back,' says his reflection. 'In the debtor's city they would call that a second instalment.'".
  }
  Topic comptroller_note with comptroller "Ask the Comptroller about the War Note" when true once {
    Says "'A loan,' says the Comptroller. 'The city wished to call an oath its predecessors were owed, and could not pay for the calling. We lent it, against security, as is our office.' He touches the black glass. 'When an oath is called, the ledger is drawn down by its weight, and the weight must be restored. That is all the Balance is: a pan that must come level.' He looks at the glass a while longer than the sentence needs. 'It has not been level for some time. I am not concerned with your city's poverty. I am concerned with that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, note_terms). }
  }
  Relation comptrollerAlly(group). Relation brokerSuspended(place).
  Topic comptroller_bid with comptroller "Tell the Comptroller that the Factor means to buy the note" when knows(actor, sault_bid) and not comptrollerAlly(actor) once {
    Says "For the first time the Comptroller looks at you directly. 'Buy it,' he says. 'At foreclosure.' The ruled lines on his face tighten. 'It is lawful. A note in default may be taken up by whoever pledges its weight. And then the holder may call the collateral out, to service as sworn, and the oaths leave the Holding, and the weight with them.' He is silent a while. 'That must not happen. Bring me what she has written, in her hand, and I will suspend the broker she has suborned. Whatever else she does, she will have to do in person, in this chamber, on the night.' He bows very slightly. 'In this, we want the same thing.'".
    On discuss { Assert comptrollerAlly(actor). }
  }
  Event broker_suspended near comptroller when keeps(comptroller, sault_letter) "The Comptroller reads the Factor's letter once, and lays it on the black glass, and the glass takes it, the way still water takes a dropped page. 'The Broker of the Fourth Pan is suspended,' he says. 'If the Factor wants the note, she will come to the Weighing Chamber on the night of the Settlement and pledge in person.' He looks at you. 'Thank you. The ledger is in your debt. I do not say that often.'" then {
    Assert brokerSuspended(ossel). }
  Relation durranceSpared(place). Relation promisedLetter(group).
  Topic comptroller_spare with comptroller "Ask the Comptroller to strike Sergeant Durrance from the next page" when knows(actor, durrance_next) and night(ossel) < 8 and not durranceSpared(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "'The page will be read,' says the Comptroller. 'Twelve oaths. The weight is the weight.' He considers you. 'But the order of the roll is a convenience, not a term. I can have the sergeant passed over. Elcock, who is next, will go in her place, and the one after Jessup in his.' He lets that sit. 'I will do it for a promise, made here, where it is held: that you will bring me, before the Settlement, the Factor's bid in her own hand.'".
  }
  Action promise_comptroller(actor: group, site: place) "Promise the Comptroller the Factor's letter before the Settlement, so that Durrance is passed over" {
    Speaker comptroller. Time 1 minute.
    Grave "A promise made to the Comptroller is held by the Balance. If it is not kept by the Feast, it is broken; and Elcock goes into the sea in Durrance's place.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(comptroller, site) and knows(actor, durrance_next)
      and night(ossel) < 8 and not durranceSpared(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) and not keeps(comptroller, sault_letter).
    On success { Assert durranceSpared(ossel). Assert promisedLetter(actor). Assert registered(actor). }
    Result "The Comptroller takes a pen and writes one line on the black glass, and the glass takes the ink. 'Durrance, A., passed over,' he says. 'Elcock, R., to be called in her place.' He does not look up. 'Elcock is nineteen. He was a drummer. I mention it because you will want to know what you have done, and I do not say things that are not so.'".
  }
  Rule letter_promise_kept when promisedLetter(party) and keeps(comptroller, sault_letter) { Retract promisedLetter(party). Assert keptFaith(party). }
  Rule letter_promise_broken when promisedLetter(party) and feastEve() and hour(clock) >= 18
    says "Somewhere under the sea a line is drawn through a promise you made, and you feel it, exactly as if a cold hand had been laid flat between your shoulders and then taken away. The Comptroller's letter was not brought." {
    Retract promisedLetter(party). Assert forswornParty(party). }
  Topic comptroller_drowned with comptroller "Ask the Comptroller about the drowned city's compact" when knows(actor, compact_read) and not knows(actor, note_designed) once {
    Says "The Comptroller does not move at all. 'That is not a matter of the note,' he says. 'You will not find me willing to discuss it.' And then, because he cannot leave a false impression standing, and you see him know it: 'I do not say that there is nothing to discuss. I say that I will not discuss it.' He looks back down at the black glass. 'You may go.'".
  }
  Relation comptrollerConfronted(group). Relation silenceOffered(group). Relation swornSilence(group).
  Topic comptroller_confronted with comptroller "Put the reckoning in the Room of Defaults to the Comptroller" when knows(actor, note_designed) and not comptrollerConfronted(actor) once {
    Says "The Comptroller listens to the end. He cannot say it is not so, and he does not try. 'I swore the compact,' he says. 'I was younger than your Valuer. The sea came over the old city in one night and the ledger did not keep, and I wrote the default in my own hand, as one must.' He lays his ruled hand flat on the glass, as if keeping something down. 'I have been filling the hole honestly ever since. One cannot. Nobody owes that much.' He looks up. 'Then your city came down the stair, poor and frightened, with six signatures and no silver. I drew the note so that it would fail. Eight thousand sleepers, unharmed, against a hole I made.' A pause, exact. 'I would draw it again.'".
    On discuss { Assert comptrollerConfronted(actor). Assert silenceOffered(actor). }
  }
  Action swear_silence(actor: group, site: place) "Promise the Comptroller your silence, and take Davy Teazle out of the Holding for it" {
    Speaker comptroller. Time 1 minute.
    Grave "A promise of silence made here is held. If you speak of the reckoning to anyone after, you are forsworn.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(comptroller, site) and silenceOffered(actor)
      and not swornSilence(actor) and heldNow(davy) and not indictmentFiled(ossel).
    On success { Assert swornSilence(actor). Assert registered(actor). Assert redeemedByComptroller(davy). }
    Result "'Then it is held,' says the Comptroller, and writes on the black glass. 'Teazle, D., private, redeemed from the Holding by order of the Comptroller.' He does not look up. 'He will wake on the Watersteps at the night ebb, with his boots beside him. Go home. You have done a good thing for one family, and nothing at all for the rest, and you knew that when you chose.'".
  }
  Relation redeemedByComptroller(group). Relation indictmentFiled(place).

}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/voices:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── Where people are in the day ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Factor eats her supper on the Tidewall every evening, from a paper cone, standing up; Wick works Lowtide at the
  // day's ebb with the other mudlarks.
  Rule sault_to_wall when hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 21 and at(sault, sault_office) and not inSession() and not feastEve() {
    Retract at(sault, sault_office). Assert at(sault, tidewall). }
  Rule sault_from_wall when (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 18) and at(sault, tidewall) {
    Retract at(sault, tidewall). Assert at(sault, sault_office). }
  Event sault_eels near sault when at(sault, tidewall) "Factor Sault is leaning on the parapet with a paper cone of hot eels, watching her ships come in on the evening tide, and nodding to every second person who passes. Most of them nod back.".
  Rule wick_to_forum when hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) < 14 and at(wick, withies) { Retract at(wick, withies). Assert at(wick, forum). }
  Rule wick_from_forum when (hour(clock) >= 14 or hour(clock) < 10) and at(wick, forum) { Retract at(wick, forum). Assert at(wick, withies). }
  Observe wick_digging near wick when at(wick, forum) "Wick is up to his knees in a drain at the edge of the square with a rake, a bucket and an expression of total professional absorption.".
  Observe wick_swept near wick when sweptOnce(party) "Wick looks you up and down. 'You got rolled,' he says, delighted. 'Didn't you. Out through the Swatch. Everybody does once.' He considers. 'Most people only once.'".
  Discovery wick_teased "Wick knows you were caught by the flood.".

  // ── Sergeant Durrance, on the way ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Event durrance_forum at forum when travelsWith(durrance, party) "Durrance stands at the edge of the Forum and looks across it, the way she would look at a field before crossing it under fire. 'Out past the colonnade,' she says, 'across the Forum, into the Hall. Wick's route.' She sets off across the slabs in a straight line, not hurrying, as if she were walking it for someone.".
  Event durrance_hall at oath_court when travelsWith(durrance, party) and not benighted(party) "Durrance goes to the end wall and puts her hand flat on the black stone, the way she put it on the Stone in the Yard nineteen years ago, and takes it away again quickly, as if it were hot. 'Same stone,' she says. 'Same as the Yard.' She wipes her hand on her coat. 'Well. Now I know what I swore on.'".
  Event durrance_landing at landing when travelsWith(durrance, party) and at(slake, landing) "Durrance and Bettany Slake look at each other across the quay, two people who have each run something hard for a long time, and something like respect passes between them without either of them saying anything.".
  Event durrance_floor at antechamber when travelsWith(durrance, party) "Durrance looks at the ruled lines round the walls, and at the notice, and closes her mouth with a snap. 'Not a word,' she says under her breath, and the lines brighten along their length at every syllable of it. She glares at them. After that she doesn't speak at all until you are off the floor.".
  Event durrance_chamber at weighing_chamber when travelsWith(durrance, party) "Durrance stands with her thumbs in her belt, looking up into the second pan, at the faint warm shapes of the oaths. 'That's us,' she says at last. 'Eight thousand.' She shakes her head. 'You'd think we'd weigh more.'".
  Event durrance_ranks at ranks when travelsWith(durrance, party) "Durrance walks slowly down the Third Company's file, saying the names under her breath as she passes each face. Pargeter. Haskett. Moll Bryer. The Lucey twins. She stops in front of a boy at the end, and straightens his collar, and goes on.".
  Event durrance_ranks_elcock at ranks when travelsWith(durrance, party) and elcockTaken(ossel) "At the end of the file Durrance stops in front of a thin boy with a drummer's calluses on his hands. 'Elcock,' she says. 'You never could keep time.' She stands there a while. Then she comes back, and does not say anything for some time.".
  Event durrance_yard at legion_yard when travelsWith(durrance, party) and not feastEve() "Durrance stops at the Yard gate and does not go any further. She looks at the Oath Stone across the empty parade ground. 'Nineteen years,' she says. 'Come on. I don't like it here.'".

  // ── The Valuer, on the way ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Event tally_drum at drum_taproom when (travelsWith(tally, party) or at(tally, drum_taproom)) and not durranceCalled(ossel) and not heldBack(durrance) "The Valuer stands looking up at the drum over the bar with the black cloth tied over its head. 'That drum beat the Third Company's muster on the day it swore,' they say. 'The calling speaks to what an oath was sworn by: the stone, and the drum. I note that a cloth does not stop it.' A pause. 'I would not be surprised if it answered to the drum in other ways. I make no recommendation.'".
  Event tally_forum at forum when travelsWith(tally, party) "The Valuer stands in the middle of the Forum and turns slowly round, looking at everything. 'It is smaller than in the records,' they say. 'Everything is.' They bend and touch a paving slab with one ruled finger, very gently, as if it might mind.".
  Event tally_landing at landing when travelsWith(tally, party) "The Valuer looks at the ebb-runners' boat, and makes a mark. 'The niche by the black wall,' they say. 'Where the silver was left. Every month for ten years I took it out and weighed it and entered it. I did not think about who carried it.' They write something down.".
  Event tally_stone at legion_yard when travelsWith(tally, party) "The Valuer goes straight to the Oath Stone and lays a hand on it, and the fine ruled lines cut in its face brighten for a moment under their palm, and fade. 'An instrument of the Balance,' they say. 'Salvaged. The city does not know what it has. It swears its soldiers on it the way a child plays with a sword.'".
  Event tally_chapel at chapel when travelsWith(tally, party) "The Valuer walks slowly under the hanging weights, reading them. 'All accurate,' they say. Then they look up at the saint over the altar, holding his scales level, and stand quite still. 'There was a clerk who went up,' they say at last, 'when the old city drowned. We are told about him in the nursery. As a warning.' They look at the scales a while longer. 'I had not known he was a saint.'".
  Event tally_tags at tags when travelsWith(tally, party) "The Valuer walks down the avenue of tags with their eyes fixed straight ahead. 'I will not look for mine,' they say, before you can ask. 'One is not shown one's name.' They walk a little faster.".
  Event tally_ranks at ranks when travelsWith(tally, party) "The Valuer goes along the files with the ledger open, checking the faces against the names, as they have done in the Withies every day. Every one is there. When they reach the end they close the ledger and stand for a moment with their hand on it, and their face does something you have not seen it do before.".
  // "Wait here a minute."
  Relation tallyWaiting(place). Measure tallyWaitFrom(place). Measure tallyWaited(place).
  Action tally_wait(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Valuer to wait here a minute" {
    Speaker tally. Time 0.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and travelsWith(tally, actor) and not tallyWaiting(ossel).
    On success { Retract travelsWith(tally, actor). Assert at(tally, site). Assert willing(tally, actor). Assert tallyWaiting(ossel).
      Set tallyWaitFrom(ossel) to watch(clock) * 10. }
    Result "'A minute,' says the Valuer, and opens the ledger.".
  }
  Rule tally_rejoined when tallyWaiting(ossel) and travelsWith(tally, party) { Retract tallyWaiting(ossel). }
  Rule tally_counts when tallyWaiting(ossel) and perceives(party, tally) and watch(clock) * 10 - tallyWaitFrom(ossel) > 30 and tallyWaited(ossel) == 0 {
    Set tallyWaited(ossel) to watch(clock) * 10 - tallyWaitFrom(ossel). }
  Rule tally_says_minutes near tally when tallyWaiting(ossel) and tallyWaited(ossel) > 0
    says "'You said a minute,' says the Valuer, closing the ledger on their finger. 'It has been {tallyWaited(ossel)} minutes. I have noted it.' A pause. 'I do not mind. I note it because it is so.'" {
    Retract tallyWaiting(ossel). Set tallyWaited(ossel) to 0. }
  Rule tally_waits_quietly when tallyWaiting(ossel) and perceives(party, tally) and watch(clock) * 10 - tallyWaitFrom(ossel) <= 30 and tallyWaited(ossel) == 0 { Retract tallyWaiting(ossel). }

  // ── What the careless swear on the weighing floor costs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation foundDavy(group).
  Rule found_davy when sworeToFind(party) and at(party, ranks) and not foundDavy(party) { Assert foundDavy(party). Assert keptFaith(party). }
  Rule swear_unkept when sworeToFind(party) and matured(ossel) and not foundDavy(party) and heldNow(davy) and not forswornParty(party)
    says "Somewhere under the sea a line is drawn through something you said once on a white floor without thinking: I'll find Davy Teazle if it kills me. You did not find him. It did not kill you. The Balance does not care which part you meant." {
    Assert forswornParty(party). }

  // ── What the Factor does with what she is given ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // With the Valuer's pages she knows the roll order, and goes to Durrance two days sooner.
  Rule silver_offered_early when saultInformed(sault) and night(ossel) >= 3 and hour(clock) == 12 and not saultOffered(ossel) and not heldNow(durrance) {
    Assert saultOffered(ossel). }
  // A Keeper warned takes the Seal to bed with him.
  Relation sealHidden(place).
  Rule seal_hidden when deckleWarned(deckle) and votePassed(ossel) and night(ossel) == 13 and hour(clock) == 22 and not sealHidden(ossel) and not sealGuarded(ossel) {
    Assert sealHidden(ossel). }

  // ── What the King knows of the war ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery salt_springs "What the war was fought for: the salt springs of Hethra on the upper Ossel, which make a white salt finer than anything from the Pans. Nobody in Tessary knows how to work them except, the King says, one person who has asked him about them twice.".
  Topic amaury_springs with amaury "Ask the King what the war was really for" when amauryPlayed(actor) or amauryWillTestify(actor) once {
    Says "'Salt,' says the King, as if it were obvious. 'The springs at Hethra-under-Fell. White salt, fine as flour; your Pans make grey. Your Board wanted them because they are worth more than the Pans. Your Factor wanted them because she understood that.' He moves a piece. 'She has written to me. Twice. Very civil letters, about the working of brine. She is the only person in this city who has asked me a sensible question in a year.' He smiles. 'If I were your Board I would be frightened of her. I am not your Board. I find her rather good company.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, salt_springs). }
  }

  // ── Quiet ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Supper at the Teazles', once, of an evening: eels, and the peg with the coat on it.
  Relation suppedWithTeazles(group).
  Action sup_with_teazles(actor: group, site: place) "Stay for supper with the Teazles" {
    Speaker nan. Time 6.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, teazle_room) and at(nan, teazle_room)
      and hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 22 and knows(actor, davy_went) and not suppedWithTeazles(actor).
    On success { Assert suppedWithTeazles(actor). Increase quantity(actor, rations) by 1. }
    Result "Nan does not ask you to stay; she puts a third bowl on the table and that is that. Eels, stewed with onions, and bread, and a jug of something brown. Wick talks the whole time, about the bell that rings under the basin on stormy nights (he has heard it; his nan has heard it; nobody believes either of them), about a coin he nearly found, about the clerk in grey, who he has decided is lonely. Nan says almost nothing. Once, without seeming to notice she is doing it, she reaches out and straightens the red coat on its peg. When you go she gives you the end of the loaf wrapped in a cloth, for tomorrow.".
  }
  // Dawn at the Oath Stone, with Durrance, before the Feast.
  Event durrance_dawn at legion_yard when travelsWith(durrance, party) and hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) < 8 and not feastEve() "In the first grey light the Yard is empty and the shell is wet. Durrance walks out to the Oath Stone and stands in front of it with her hands behind her back, the way she would stand in front of an officer. 'I was sixteen,' she says. 'I lied about it. The sergeant knew; he slapped my back anyway. My mother cried all the way home and then made me a cake.' She looks at the ruled lines on the Stone. 'I'd do it again. That's the trouble with me. Come on, before somebody sees us and thinks I'm sentimental.'".
  // In the Holding, a singer's voice in a jar: pledged against her sweetheart's coming home, and never collected.
  Thing voice_jar "a stoppered jar with a tag" at folded_lake {
    State stoppered "On the white floor by the folded lake stands a plain stoppered jar of brown glaze with a tag on its neck: a voice, pledged by a woman of the Withies a hundred and ninety years ago against her sweetheart's return from the sea. He came home. The tag says she never came for it.".
    State unstoppered "The jar by the folded lake stands unstoppered, and very faintly, if you bend close, someone is still singing in it.".
    Change listen "Take the stopper out of the jar and listen" from stoppered to unstoppered.
  }
  Event jar_sings at folded_lake when state(voice_jar, unstoppered) "Out of the jar comes a woman's voice, small and clear and far away, singing to nobody in particular, the way people sing over washing. It is 'Sally of the Withies', the old ballad of the girl who waited for a sailor, that Pitch sells in a penny chapbook and that the Copyist under the sea has read until she stopped counting. In the jar she has got to the third verse, where he comes home. She sings it twice. Then she starts again from the beginning.".
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/ways.k:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── The Factor at dusk ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // She seeks out whoever she has hired, once, on the Tidewall, with eels; and if she has not hired them, she looks
  // them over anyway. What she says depends on what they have done to her.
  Event sault_dusk near sault when at(sault, tidewall) and night(ossel) >= 2 and hiredBySault(party) and not saultExposed(ossel) and not voted(ossel) "Factor Sault sees you before you see her, and holds out the paper cone. 'Eel,' she says. 'Go on. You look like someone who's been under the sea.' She watches her ships come in for a while. 'I know what you've found, roughly. I know what the Board did ten years ago, exactly; I carried the silver. I'll tell you what I think, and then you can tell me I'm a monster.' She eats an eel. 'The Board will vote no. Not because they're wicked. Because they've never once had to pay for anything. And when they vote no, those lads go under the sea, all of them, and stay there, unless someone with the weight to do it takes up the note.' She licks salt off her thumb. 'When the Feast's done I'll need someone who's been down there and isn't afraid of clerks. Think about it. I'll be here every evening. I like the light.'".
  Event sault_dusk_letter near sault when at(sault, tidewall) and carries(party, sault_letter) and not saultExposed(ossel) and not voted(ossel) "Factor Sault looks at the letter in your hand, with her own wax on it, broken. 'Ah,' she says. 'Bettany never could keep a box shut.' She doesn't ask for it back. 'Well, you've read it. Every word's true, which is more than the Board can say for anything it ever signed.' She offers you the cone of eels. 'Keep it. Show it to whoever you like. I'd rather be hated for what I mean than liked for what I don't.'".
  Relation saultShaken(place).
  Topic sault_father with sault "Ask the Factor about the First Muster's plaque" when knows(actor, first_muster) and not saultShaken(ossel) once {
    Says "For the first time the Factor doesn't answer straight away. 'My father,' she says. 'Third rank, First Muster, the Salt War. They promised them the south bank. Good land, the south bank. They gave them that plaque, at knee height so you'd have to kneel to read it, and the right to rake salt for the Board at the Board's price, for ever.' She turns the paper cone in her hands. 'He raked for twenty-two years and died owing the company store four marks. I was fourteen. I raked it off. Then I bought the store. Then I bought the pans.' She looks out at the Pans steaming in the dusk. 'So when you tell me the city will keep its promise to the Long Muster, I'll laugh, and you'll forgive me. I've seen this city keep a promise. It's green, and it's at knee height.'".
  }
  Topic sault_designed with sault "Tell the Factor that the War Note was drawn to fail" when knows(actor, note_designed) and not saultShaken(ossel) once {
    Says "Factor Sault hears you out without eating anything. Then she laughs, once, a short bark that makes the fishermen along the parapet look round. 'Rigged,' she says. 'From the start. The Board too stupid to see it, and me too clever by half.' She picks a crust of salt off her sleeve. 'Ten years I carried that silver down a tunnel and never once asked what the other side wanted with it.' She turns to you. 'It changes nothing. A rigged game is still the only game in town, and I'll still be at the table when the note falls in.' And then, much lower: 'It changes what I'd be buying. Tell me what you'd have me do instead, and I'll listen. Once.'".
    On discuss { Assert saultShaken(ossel). }
  }

  // ── The drowned city's own way down ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Under the plunge-pool a drain runs down through the bedrock into the cistern the Scruples draw their water from,
  // behind the standing dormitory: the old city's clerks went down to the Balance by it before the black wall was
  // sealed. The Forsworn stand over it. There are three ways past them: through them; round them, quietly; or by
  // giving them what they hold out their hands for, which is the weight of a promise that was kept.
  Place scruples_cistern "the Scruples' cistern" is room within sr_halls at 3, 1 underground.
  Passage plunge_drain "the drain under the plunge-pool" is crawl between plunge and scruples_cistern taking 20 minutes.
  Passage cistern_way "the cistern steps" is steps between scruples_cistern and dormitory.
  Observe scruples_cistern_scene at scruples_cistern when true "A round cistern of white stone, half full of black water so still that the lamp-light lies on it like a coin. A crawl comes in high up on one side, from the dark, cut by hands much older than the Scruples'; steps on the other side go up toward the sound of very slow breathing.".
  Observe plunge_drain_seen at plunge when not benighted(party) "In the floor of the dry pool, under the silt the Forsworn stand in, there is a square drain-mouth, cut with ruled lines like everything the old city's clerks made, and a draught comes up out of it that smells of stone dust and, faintly, of hot metal.".
  Relation forswornAppeased(place).
  Thing forsworn_watch "the Forsworn over the drain" on plunge_drain is scenery {
    State standing blocking "The Forsworn stand over the drain-mouth, close as reeds, with their hands out.".
    State parted "The Forsworn have drawn back from the drain-mouth, against the walls.".
  }
  Rule forsworn_part when (forswornAppeased(ossel) or not able(forsworn)) and state(forsworn_watch, standing) { Assert state(forsworn_watch, parted). }
  Rule forsworn_close when able(forsworn) and not forswornAppeased(ossel) and state(forsworn_watch, parted) and not at(party, plunge) and not at(party, scruples_cistern) { Assert state(forsworn_watch, standing). }
  // A weight of a kept promise, from Saint Evenhand's.
  Kind votive_weight "a votive weight of a kept promise" is gear worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A small lead weight on a cord, rubbed smooth, from the chapel ceiling: hung forty years ago by a woman whose husband promised to come home from the sea, and did. Brother Ancel says it has been kept a long time, and can be spared.".
  Item kept_weight "a votive weight of a kept promise" is votive_weight at chapel hidden until weight_given.
  Discovery weight_given "Brother Ancel has given you the weight of a kept promise.".
  Topic tolley_hollow with tolley "Ask Brother Ancel what the hollow men in Lowtide want" when true once {
    Says "Ancel does not laugh. 'The forsworn,' he says. 'The old city's oath-breakers, the book calls them. The saint pitied them. He said they hold out their hands because they want to be given back what they broke, and there is no giving it.' He looks up at the weights. 'He used to take a weight down from here, one of the old ones, a promise that had been kept, and go down at the ebb and give it to one. The book says it stood aside for him, and let him go where he was going. I have never tried it. I am a coward, and they are not mine to pity.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hollow_want). }
  }
  Discovery hollow_want "Saint Evenhand used to give the Forsworn the weight of a kept promise from his chapel, and they would stand aside for him.".
  Action ask_weight(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Ask Brother Ancel for the weight of a kept promise" {
    Speaker tolley. Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(tolley, site) and knows(actor, hollow_want)
      and memberOf(recipient, actor) and awake(recipient) and at(kept_weight, chapel).
    Resolve acquire(kept_weight, votive_weight, recipient).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, weight_given). Retract at(kept_weight, chapel). }
    Result "Ancel stands on the altar-step and reaches up among the weights, turning the little paper tags to the light, and comes down with a lead one rubbed smooth as a pebble. 'Forty years,' he says. 'A sailor's wife. He came home. She died last winter, and he the winter before, and it has hung here kept all that while.' He puts it in your hand and closes your fingers over it. 'Bring the cord back, if you can. I like to know where they go.'".
  }
  Action give_weight(actor: group, giver: member, site: place) "Hold out the weight of a kept promise to the Forsworn" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, plunge) and at(forsworn, plunge) and able(forsworn)
      and memberOf(giver, actor) and carries(actor, kept_weight) and not forswornAppeased(ossel) and not benighted(actor).
    Resolve drop(kept_weight, giver).
    On success { Assert forswornAppeased(ossel). Retract assails(forsworn, actor). Assert tolerates(forsworn, actor). Retract at(kept_weight, plunge). }
    Result "You hold it out on its cord, and they stop. All of them, all at once, the way the soldiers stopped on the Steps. The nearest puts out a hand that is not quite a hand and takes the weight, and holds it, and for a moment, in the torn dark where its face should be, something is almost there: a mouth, an old man's mouth, about to say a name. Then it is gone. They draw back against the walls of the plunge-room, all of them, with the weight passed from hand to hand among them like something warm, and leave the drain-mouth clear.".
  }
  Action slip_forsworn(actor: group, site: place) "Slip along the pool's edge to the drain while the Forsworn face the arch" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, plunge) and at(forsworn, plunge) and able(forsworn)
      and not forswornAppeased(ossel) and not triedSlipping(actor) and state(forsworn_watch, standing).
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert state(forsworn_watch, parted). Assert unseen(actor, forsworn). }
    On failure { Assert triedSlipping(actor). Assert assails(forsworn, actor). }
    Result "You go along the very edge of the dry pool with your back to the wall and your light shaded in your hand, so close to the nearest of them that you could touch its sleeve. It does not turn. Nothing turns. The drain-mouth is at your feet, and then you are in it.".
    Otherwise "Your foot finds a loose tile at the pool's edge, and every empty face in the room turns to you at once.".
  }
  Relation triedSlipping(group).
  Rule slip_done when unseen(party, forsworn) and not at(party, plunge) { Retract unseen(party, forsworn). }

  // ── Other keys ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A Scruple balances the weighing pans as a child of seven does.
  Action tally_balances(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Valuer to balance the pans" {
    Speaker tally. Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, gallery) and travelsWith(tally, actor)
      and state(counter_door, shut) and not brokeFaith(actor).
    On success { Assert state(counter_door, open). Assert chamberOpened(ossel). }
    Result "The Valuer does not look at the brass on the rack. They step into the empty pan themselves, and stand quite still, and the pan sinks under them, a little, and stops a hair short; and they take a pen out of their coat and hold it out at arm's length, and the pointer creeps to its mark, and the white door opens. 'Every one of us does that at seven years old,' they say, stepping out. 'It is how we are taught what we weigh. A pen is about the weight of an untold lie.'".
  }
  // Bettany Slake carries the Factor's letters. Shown what they are for, she will not carry another.
  Topic slake_letters with slake "Tell Bettany Slake what the Factor's letters to the Hall are for" when knows(actor, collateral) and knows(actor, sault_courier) and tolerates(slake, actor) and not state(runners_box, open) once {
    Says "Bettany listens with her arms folded, and when you get to the soldiers walking past the quay with their eyes open she unfolds them. 'Buying them,' she says. 'The Factor. With a letter in my box.' She spits over the edge of the quay, a long way. 'I run untaxed salt. I've run worse. I never yet carried a man.' She takes a key off her belt and opens the lockbox and holds out the letter on two fingers, as if it were wet. 'Take it. Tell her Bettany Slake said so. And then don't come back to my quay, because I'll have to say you robbed me.'".
    On discuss { Assert state(runners_box, open). Assert slakeGaveLetter(ossel). }
  }
  Relation slakeGaveLetter(place).
  Rule slake_lets_box when slakeGaveLetter(ossel) and not tolerates(slake, party) { Assert tolerates(slake, party). }
  // The Factor's lightermen let anyone on the Factor's books go about her warehouse, until she has reason not to.
  Rule lightermen_know_you when hiredBySault(party) and not saultExposed(ossel) and not tolerates(lightermen, party) and not hostile(sault, party) {
    Assert tolerates(lightermen, party). }
  Rule lightermen_forget_you when saultExposed(ossel) and tolerates(lightermen, party) { Retract tolerates(lightermen, party). }
  Action bribe_lightermen(actor: group, site: place) "Give the lightermen two coin each to finish their game somewhere else" {
    Time 2 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(lightermen, site) and able(lightermen)
      and not tolerates(lightermen, actor) and not assails(lightermen, actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 6.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Increase quantity(lightermen, gold) by 6. Assert tolerates(lightermen, actor). }
    Result "The biggest of them looks at the coins, and at his mates, and at the door to Panhythe, where the Factor is not. 'Never saw you,' he says, and they go and sit on the salt-sacks by the far wall with their backs to the trap-door.".
  }

  // ── The Treasurer and the Comptroller ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Two men who put their names to a promise they knew could not be kept.
  Topic quire_designed with quire "Tell the Treasurer that the War Note was drawn to fail" when knows(actor, note_designed) and quireConfided(actor) and not quireDrowned(ossel) once {
    Says "Quire takes his spectacles off. 'Drawn to fail,' he says. 'Then we were cheated.' He sits with that for a moment, and you watch him want it, the relief of it, and then watch him put it down. 'No,' he says. 'We read it. We knew the treasury. We knew what land and a pension for eight thousand would cost, and we signed it anyway, because the other side wanted it signed and we wanted to win.' He puts the spectacles back on. 'A man who signs a promise he cannot keep, because the man across the table would like it broken, is still the man who signed it. Your clerk under the sea and I are the same kind of fool. He has only been one longer.'".
  }
  // ── The Teazles, after ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe teazles_home at teazle_room when cameHome(davy) and at(davy, teazle_room) "The red coat is not on its peg. Davy Teazle is asleep in the cupboard bed in it, with his boots on, which his mother has not mentioned. Nan is mending a net by the brazier and has stopped pretending she is not looking at him. The recruiting bill is gone from the shelf; there is a pale square where it was.".
  Topic davy_home_talk with davy "Ask Davy what he remembers" when cameHome(davy) and at(davy, teazle_room) and not asleep(davy) once {
    Says "'Standing,' says Davy. 'In a line. White, everywhere, like snow with no cold in it.' He looks at his hands. 'And a voice somewhere singing the Sally song over and over, a woman, very far off. I kept trying to remember the last verse and I couldn't.' He looks up at his mother. 'He comes home,' he says. 'In the last verse. I remember now.'".
  }
  Rule davy_wakes_home when cameHome(davy) and at(davy, teazle_room) and asleep(davy) and hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 20 { Retract asleep(davy). }

  // ── The eel-mother ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A conger as long as a boat that comes up the Swatch at the night ebb to hunt the drained streets, and lies at the
  // foot of the stair. By day she is out in the deep channel. Ways past her: by day; by the Factor's cistern; quietly,
  // while she is turned to the channel; or with what the Withies always give her, hot eels with vinegar, which she
  // likes better than anyone has ever been able to explain.
  Species tessary_conger "a great conger" like great_snake temperament territorial
    described "An eel as long as a boat and as thick as a horse, grey-black, with a head like a ram and a mouth full of back-curved teeth. The Withies call her the eel-mother and say she was old when their grandmothers were girls.".
  Person eelmother "the eel-mother" at throat_foot {
    Role "a conger as long as a boat, lying in the channel at the stair-foot". Species tessary_conger. Level 5. Pronouns she.
    Seen when dark() and lowWater().
    Warns "The black water at the foot of the stair humps up, and a head as big as a ram's comes out of it on a neck that keeps coming, and turns, slowly, toward your light. Her mouth is open. She does not want you on her stair.".
    Comes "The eel-mother comes up out of the channel all at once, the whole grey length of her, faster than anything that size should move.".
  }
  Kind hot_eels "a paper cone of hot eels" is gear worth 1 weighing 0
    described "Eels, stewed and sliced, hot, in a cone of the city's own paper, with too much vinegar. The paper is going soft.".
  Person eel_seller "Old Gudrun" at tidewall {
    Role "who sells hot eels in paper cones on the Tidewall, from a brazier on a barrow". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner jovial.
    Greets "Old Gudrun holds up a paper cone before you have asked for one. 'Hot,' she says. 'One coin. Mind the vinegar.'".
    Greets again "Old Gudrun has the cone held out before you can draw breath. 'Hot,' she says. 'One coin. Same as yesterday, and the day before, and the day the soldiers came. The price of an eel is the one honest thing in Tessary.'".
    Sells hot_eels for 1 coin from 6.
    Seen when not dark().
  }
  Topic gudrun_eelmother with eel_seller "Ask Old Gudrun about the eel-mother" when true once {
    Says "'Her?' Old Gudrun laughs, and stirs the pot. 'She's been coming up the Swatch at the night ebb since my gran was a girl. Takes a dog now and then. Took a mudlark in my mother's time, and they say the mudlark had it coming.' She fills a cone and holds it out to you, steaming. 'You want to go down there of a night, you take her a cone of these. Vinegar. Lots. Throw it in the channel and she'll stop to eat it, and while she's eating you go by. She's been eating my eels sixty years. She knows the smell of my pot better than my husband does.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, eelmother_known). }
  }
  Discovery eelmother_known "A great conger, the eel-mother, comes up the Swatch at the night ebb and lies at the foot of the stair; a cone of hot eels thrown into the channel stops her long enough to get past.".
  Topic wick_night_ebb with wick "Ask Wick about going down at the night ebb" when true once {
    Says "'Don't,' says Wick at once. 'Not at the night ebb. The eel-mother comes up.' He holds his hands as far apart as they go, and then looks at them as if they were not nearly far enough. 'She lies at the bottom of the stair with her head out. You take her Gudrun's eels, from the barrow on the Wall. Everybody knows that.' He considers. 'Or you go round by the Factor's tunnel, but they'll break your head. Or you don't go.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, eelmother_known). }
  }
  Relation eelmotherFed(place).
  Action feed_eelmother(actor: group, giver: member, cone: item, site: place) "Throw {cone} into the channel" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, throat_foot) and at(eelmother, throat_foot)
      and able(eelmother) and dark() and lowWater() and memberOf(giver, actor) and ownedItem(cone, giver) and itemKind(cone, hot_eels)
      and not eelmotherFed(ossel).
    Resolve drop(cone, giver).
    On success { Assert eelmotherFed(ossel). Assert tolerates(eelmother, actor). Retract assails(eelmother, actor). }
    Result "The cone hits the black water and opens, and the smell of vinegar goes up, and the great head turns away from you toward it with something you would swear was pleasure. She takes the whole thing, paper and all, in one movement, and slides back down into the channel to see if there is any more. You go past the end of her while she looks.".
  }
  Rule eelmother_full when eelmotherFed(ossel) and not dark() { Retract eelmotherFed(ossel). Retract tolerates(eelmother, party). }
  Action slip_eelmother(actor: group, site: place) "Wait for her to turn to the channel, and go by along the wall" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, throat_foot) and at(eelmother, throat_foot)
      and able(eelmother) and dark() and lowWater() and not tolerates(eelmother, actor) and not triedEel(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert tolerates(eelmother, actor). }
    On failure { Assert triedEel(actor). Assert assails(eelmother, actor). }
    Result "You stand pressed against the wet wall of the stair-foot for the count of a hundred, while the great head swings slowly back and forth over the channel, and when it is turned away you go, along the wall, one step and then another, close enough to smell her. She does not turn.".
    Otherwise "A stone turns under your boot. The head comes round.".
  }
  Relation triedEel(group).
  Rule eel_forgets when tolerates(eelmother, party) and not dark() and not eelmotherFed(ossel) { Retract tolerates(eelmother, party). }
}

data/adventures/what-tessary-owes/week.k:
Module tessary "What Tessary Owes" {
  // ── The middle of the fortnight ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What happens between the first week's findings and the Feast happens somewhere, at an hour, whether or not anyone
  // is there: Durrance's night, the Treasurer at the Swatch, the lightermen at Marrable's door, the Muster on the Row,
  // the Board, the Seal. The Muffled Drum hears of each a day or two before, and Hannelore says what it hears.
  Topic gossip_deserters with sedge "Ask Hannelore what they are saying in the Drum" when night(ossel) >= 2 and night(ossel) <= 4 once {
    Says "'Deserters,' says Hannelore, and empties a pot into the slop-bucket as if it had said it. 'That bill on the Landgate. Printed, on good paper. The Board hasn't paper like that; it came off the Factor's press, and the whole Withies knows it.' She wipes the bar. 'And Benno Fisk is buying rounds, which he never did in his life. And nobody says a word to Thomasin about her page, so she sits there and says it to herself.'".
  }
  Topic gossip_coats with sedge "Ask Hannelore what they are saying in the Drum" when night(ossel) >= 5 and night(ossel) <= 6 once {
    Says "'Coats,' says Hannelore. 'Lads go down to the Factor's hall in the morning in red and come back in grey with a salt-white collar. And they say she's offered to pay the next ebb's silver herself, all twelve, if the right sergeant asks her nicely.' She looks up at the drum. 'The spring ebb's the night after next. Two in the morning. If you've anything to do for Thomasin, do it before then.'".
  }
  Topic gossip_tonight with sedge "Ask Hannelore what they are saying in the Drum" when night(ossel) == 7 and not heldNow(durrance) once {
    Says "'Nothing,' says Hannelore. 'Nobody's saying anything tonight.' She is polishing the same pot she was polishing when you came in. 'Spring ebb's at two. Thomasin's at the top of the page. She's said she'll sit up here with her boots on, like a soldier.' She puts the pot down. 'Rap, rap, and the long roll. My husband used to beat it. I've not touched it since.'".
  }
  Topic gossip_treasurer with sedge "Ask Hannelore what they are saying in the Drum" when night(ossel) >= 8 and night(ossel) <= 10 and not quireDrowned(ossel) once {
    Says "'The Treasurer,' says Hannelore. 'Twice now the eel-men have seen him at the head of the Swatch Stair before dawn, in his good coat, buttoned up, looking down at the water. Not doing anything. Just looking.' She frowns. 'Somebody ought to say something to him. Somebody he'd listen to.' And then, lower: 'And the Factor's lightermen were in the Eel quarter yesterday asking which door is Councillor Marrable's. Asking nicely.'".
  }
  Topic gossip_terraces with sedge "Ask Hannelore what they are saying in the Drum" when night(ossel) >= 11 and night(ossel) <= 12 and not fiskTurned(fisk) and not riotHappened(ossel) and not riotCalmed(ossel) once {
    Says "'Torches,' says Hannelore. 'The lads at the Factor's hall say if the Board's going to vote no, they'll go up the Terraces the night before and ask it again, louder. Fisk's getting them together on Scriveners' Row after dark, the night before the sitting.' She shakes her head. 'And the Factor says leave it to her, and pays for the torches. Work that out.'".
  }
  Topic gossip_coats_back with sedge "Ask Hannelore what they are saying in the Drum" when night(ossel) >= 11 and night(ossel) <= 12 and fiskTurned(fisk) once {
    Says "Hannelore has a grey coat hanging off the end of the bar, dripping into a bucket, and she is not hiding it. 'Out of the canal,' she says. 'Fisk's been telling the lads at the Factor's hall what she wants them for, and some of them believed him. Half the Withies went fishing for coats this morning.' She wrings the sleeve out over the bucket. 'The Board sits the day after tomorrow. Ten in the morning. I've never been on the public bench in my life. I might go.'".
  }
  Topic gossip_board with sedge "Ask Hannelore what they are saying in the Drum" when night(ossel) == 13 and not voted(ossel) once {
    Says "'The Board's sitting,' says Hannelore. 'Ten till two, and then the count. Public bench is open to anyone who'll stand, and anyone with anything to say can stand up and say it, before two.' She unties her apron. 'Half the Withies is going. Mind, if the Board votes yes, the Factor's lost, and she doesn't like losing. I'd watch the Office of Seals tonight, if I were the Keeper. He sleeps in there with it.'".
  }
  Topic gossip_carried with sedge "Ask Hannelore what they are saying in the Drum" when votePassed(ossel) and night(ossel) == 13 and not sealTried(ossel) once {
    Says "'Carried!' says Hannelore, and kisses you on both cheeks before you can stop her. Then she sobers. 'It's not done till the Seal's on the deeds tomorrow, mind. The Factor's lightermen were on Scriveners' Row this afternoon looking at the Keeper's windows. Somebody ought to sit up with him tonight.'".
  }
  Topic gossip_feast with sedge "Ask Hannelore what they are saying in the Drum" when night(ossel) == 14 once {
    Says "'Feast tomorrow,' says Hannelore. 'Feast of Settlement, and the spring ebb with it. Fifteenth night.' She rubs a clean place on the drum-skin with her apron, where it wants no rubbing. 'There's people in the Withies hanging their sons' boots on the door. I don't know if it's for luck or the other thing.'".
  }

  // The tenth night: an hour before he goes down the stair, the Treasurer goes to the head of it and stands there.
  // Anyone at the head of the Swatch Stair can speak to him. Who knows what to tell him can give him a reason; anyone
  // can try to give him a smaller one.
  Rule quire_to_throat when night(ossel) == 10 and hour(clock) == 3 and quirePressed(ossel) and not quireHope(quire)
    and not quireDrowned(ossel) and at(quire, exchequer_room) {
    Retract at(quire, exchequer_room). Assert at(quire, throat_head). }
  Rule quire_off_throat when quireDrowned(ossel) and at(quire, throat_head) { Retract at(quire, throat_head). }
  Rule quire_back_home when quireHope(quire) and at(quire, throat_head) and hour(clock) != 3 {
    Retract at(quire, throat_head). Assert at(quire, exchequer_room). }
  Observe quire_at_throat near quire when at(quire, throat_head) and not quireHope(quire) "At the head of the Swatch Stair, in the dark, a man is standing with his coat buttoned to the neck, looking down at the full basin. It is the Treasurer. He has taken his spectacles off and holds them folded in one hand, as if he did not expect to need them again.".
  Relation triedQuire(group).
  Action stay_quire(actor: group, site: place) "Ask the Treasurer who will send the money to the mothers on the first of the month" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, throat_head) and at(quire, throat_head)
      and not quireHope(quire) and not quireDrowned(ossel) and not triedQuire(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert quireHope(quire). }
    On failure { Assert triedQuire(actor). }
    Result "He looks at you as if you had asked him the time. 'Four marks,' he says. 'Each. A hundred and thirty-eight of them, and twelve more after the Feast.' He thinks about it. 'Nobody,' he says. 'Nobody would. The Board would stop it in a week.' He puts his spectacles back on, and stands there a while longer, and then he turns round and walks back up toward the Lettered Quarter, slowly, like a man who has remembered an appointment.".
    Otherwise "He hears you out politely, and thanks you, and says you should go home to bed. He does not move from the top step.".
  }
  Rule quire_saved_told when quireHope(quire) and night(ossel) == 10 and not quireDrowned(ossel) and not spread(quire_lived)
    and inTessary() and not at(party, throat_head) says "Word goes along the Tidewall in the morning that the Treasurer was seen at the head of the Swatch Stair before dawn, and that he went home." { Assert spread(quire_lived). }
  Discovery quire_lived "The Treasurer stood at the head of the Swatch Stair on the tenth night, and went home.".

  // The thirteenth day: the Council House bell.
  Discovery board_sits "The Board of Moieties sits on the thirteenth day, from ten in the morning until the count at two in the afternoon. The public bench is open, and anyone with something to say may stand up and say it before two.".
  Rule board_bell when night(ossel) == 13 and hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 10 and inTessary() and not spread(board_sits)
    says "The Council House bell rings over the city, nine strokes and then nine more: the Board of Moieties sits at ten to hear the question of the Veterans' Settlement, and the public bench is open." teaches board_sits {
    Assert spread(board_sits). }
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/carth.ky:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── A Winter in Carth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Scaifes are tenants of the Minster's Fabric, two years behind with the rent. At Candlemas the Penitentiary
  // offered them the Cold Vigil Ninian Hern had refused: forty nights of no fire in the house, two shillings a night,
  // half paid in advance. They took it for the rent. It is the twenty-third night. Ralph Scaife, the grandfather, died
  // on the fourteenth, of the cold or of being eighty, and lies on a hurdle in the byre because the ground will not take
  // a spade before the thaw; his wife sits up with him. Dowsie, who is nine, has a cough. The house is dark, because a
  // flame is a fire.
  Entity carth_vigil: group "the Carth vigil".
  Relation vigilEnded(group). Relation vigilBroken(group). Relation vigilReleased(group). Relation vigilKept(group).
  Query vigilOn() means not vigilEnded(carth_vigil).
  Measure vigilNight(group).
  Initially Set vigilNight(carth_vigil) to 23.

  // The hearth: what the vigil is, and what the Ash-reeve tests.
  Thing hearth "the hearth at Carth" at house_place {
    State cold "The hearth is dead: a bed of grey ash swept flat, and over it on the chain an empty pot. Beside it, on a cloth on the floor, a bowl and a spoon laid for somebody.".
    State ablaze "A fire burns on the hearth, peat and thorn, and the room has come up out of the dark: the black beams, the dresser, the box-bed in the wall with its doors open, the faces.".
    State snowed "The hearth is packed with snow, grey with ash, melting into a black slush that steams a little and then stops.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(hearth, cold).
  // With a fire on the hearth or in the byre, the house is lit; else it is dark.
  Relation byreFire(group).
  // By day a little grey comes in at the one window; by night, without a fire, nothing does.
  Rule house_lit when (state(hearth, ablaze) or not nightfall()) and unlit(house_place) { Retract unlit(house_place). }
  Rule house_dark when not state(hearth, ablaze) and nightfall() and not unlit(house_place) { Assert unlit(house_place). }
  // A light with no fire in it (a mage's conjuring) is no breach of a cold vigil, and the house knows it at once.
  Rule cold_light at house_place when nightfall() and capable(party, light) and not capable(party, flame) and not state(hearth, ablaze)
    and vigilOn() and stayingAtCarth(party) and not spread(cold_light)
    says "The light that comes off your hand is white, and gives no heat, and makes no smoke, and the whole house-place stands up out of the dark at once: the beams, the dresser, the box-bed, five faces turned toward you. Annis Scaife looks at it without blinking. 'Is that a fire?' she says. Nobody can say it is. Old Mother Scaife leans over and holds her hands to it, out of habit, and takes them back. 'Cold,' she says, satisfied. 'He'll not mind that.' In the box-bed the child sits up to look at it, and for a while forgets to cough; and then remembers." { Assert spread(cold_light). }
  Entity cold_light: fact "a cold light at Carth".
  Rule byre_lit when (byreFire(carth_vigil) or not nightfall()) and unlit(carth_byre) { Retract unlit(carth_byre). }
  Rule byre_dark when not byreFire(carth_vigil) and nightfall() and not unlit(carth_byre) { Assert unlit(carth_byre). }

  // ── The household ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person will "Will Scaife" at house_place {
    Role "a big silent man sitting on the settle in the dark with a billhook across his knees, because he has to hold something" when nightfall() and not state(hearth, ablaze).
    Role "a big silent man on the settle, with his hands open on his knees and his face to the fire" when state(hearth, ablaze).
    Role "a big silent man with a shovel, grey-faced, who does not look at anyone" when not nightfall() and not state(hearth, ablaze).
    Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
    Greets "A man's voice, out of the dark, low: 'Sit down where you are. Don't walk about. There's a child.'".
    Greets again "Will Scaife says nothing, and shifts the shovel to his other hand so that the blade is behind him. You can hear him breathing: the breath of a man who has kept a vigil one day longer than a man can, and has not been told whether to stop.".
  }
  Person annis "Annis Scaife" at house_place {
    Role "the farmer's wife, a sharp voice in the dark, never still" when nightfall() and not state(hearth, ablaze).
    Role "the farmer's wife, thin as a lath, with her sleeves rolled and her mouth set" when state(hearth, ablaze) or not nightfall().
    Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "'You'll be the ones the snow brought,' says a woman's voice. 'There's oatmeal in water and there's a turnip, and you're welcome to your share of both, and of the dark. Sit on the floor by the wall. Don't touch the hearth.'".
    Greets again "'Well?' says Annis Scaife, not turning from the pot. 'Is there news from the road? I do not ask for good news. I ask whether the road is still there.'".
  }
  Person granny "Old Mother Scaife" at house_place {
    Role "an old woman in a shawl, a shape by the dead hearth that rocks a little" when not at(granny, carth_byre).
    Role "an old woman in the byre in the dark, sitting on a milking-stool by the hurdle, talking to someone" when at(granny, carth_byre).
    Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "'Is that the Guest?' says an old voice by the hearth, quite calmly. Then: 'No. The Guest doesn't talk. Sit down, love. Ralph's in the byre. He'll not mind you.'".
    Greets again "'Is that you, love?' says Old Mother Scaife, to the dark by the hearth. 'You were quiet on the stair. You were always quiet on the stair. Ralph never was.' She has the habit of speaking to whoever has just come in as though it were someone she had been waiting for since before the snow.".
  }
  Person dowsie "Dowsie Scaife" at house_place {
    Role "a child in the box-bed, under every blanket in the house, coughing" when not dowsieDead(dowsie) and not nightOver(party).
    Role "a thin child in the box-bed with her hair stuck to her forehead, cool now, and very interested in you" when not dowsieDead(dowsie) and nightOver(party).
    Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "A small hoarse voice from the wall: 'Are you from Gaunt? Is it true the Minster's so tall you can't see the top? Is it true they've a man there that's all stone, carrying another man?' A cough. 'Grandad walks at night. I've heard him. Mam says I haven't.'".
    Greets again "'You didn't go,' says Dowsie, pleased, and coughs, and counts the cough on her fingers as it passes. 'That's the third today. Mam says three is good. I think three is just three.'".
    Seen when not dowsieDead(dowsie).
  }
  Person fly "Fly" at house_place {
    Role "the Scaifes' collie bitch, thin, who presses against your legs in the dark and shivers". Species dog. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
    Greets "Fly stays where she is, against your legs, and goes on shivering, which is as much welcome as you are going to get.".
    Greets again "Fly's tail goes once against the floor, and then, because she is a collie, she gets up and puts herself between you and the door, to be sure you will not leave without telling her where.".
  }
  Relation dowsieSafe(group). Relation dowsieBurning(group). Relation dowsieDead(group).
  Relation grannyIn(group). Relation grannyCold(group). Relation ralphLaid(group).
  Relation beastsIn(group). Relation sharedBed(group). Relation nursed(group). Relation hernCoat(group).
  Relation scaifesConsent(group). Relation hernConfessed(group). Relation litWithoutLeave(group).
  Relation brokeVigil(group). Relation reeveDeceived(group).

  // ── Coming in out of the snow ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation stayingAtCarth(group). Relation nightOver(group).
  Measure carthArrived(group). Measure carthDay(group).
  Rule carth_arrival at house_place when at(party, house_place) and snowing() and not stayingAtCarth(party)
    says "THE FIRST NIGHT. The door shuts behind you, and the dark is complete. Not the dark of a night outdoors, which has a sky in it; the dark of a shut room with no fire, which has nothing. Somebody takes your arm, a hard small hand, and puts you down on the floor against a wall, which is stone, and cold through your clothes in a moment. You hear: a child coughing, close; someone breathing slow by where the hearth must be; a clock; the cow, through the wall; a dog, which comes and presses itself against your legs. And the cold. Not the cold outside, which moves. A cold that has been sitting in this room for twenty-three days, and has settled." {
    Assert stayingAtCarth(party). Set carthArrived(party) to watch(clock). Set carthDay(party) to dayN(gaunt_town). }
  Query carthNight() means stayingAtCarth(party) and not nightOver(party).

  // ── Talk in the dark ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic annis_why with annis "Ask Annis Scaife why there is no fire" when vigilOn() once {
    Says "'Because we're keeping a vigil,' says Annis. 'A cold one. Forty nights. For somebody in Gaunt that's done something, and is sorry, and paid the Penitentiary to have it kept.' A pause. 'Two shillings a night. Half in advance. It's the rent. We're two years behind with the Fabric and they'd have had us out at Lady Day.' Another pause, longer. 'It's the twenty-third. Seventeen to go. Ralph died on the fourteenth. He's in the byre. The ground won't take a spade.' She says it all in the same voice, the voice of someone reading out a list.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, vigil_kept). }
  }
  Discovery vigil_kept "The Scaifes of Carth are keeping the Cold Vigil for wages, forty nights of no fire, two shillings a night, half paid in advance, to pay two years' rent owed to the Minster's Fabric. It is the twenty-third night. The grandfather died on the fourteenth.".
  Topic annis_how with annis "Ask Annis how anyone would know if the fire were lit" when knows(actor, vigil_kept) and not knows(actor, ash_test) once {
    Says "'He'd know.' Annis says it flat. 'The Ash-reeve. Raistrick. He comes in the night, any hour, no knock, and kneels down and puts his hand in the hearth. Warm, it's broken, and we've nothing, and we owe the twenty back.' You hear her move. 'He's never once looked anywhere but the hearth. Twenty-two nights. Just the hearth. Then he gets up and goes.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ash_test). }
  }
  Topic annis_coin with annis "Ask Annis who paid them" when knows(actor, vigil_kept) once {
    Says "'The Penitentiary,' says Annis. 'That's who pays. That's who always pays. Whoever owes pays the Penitentiary, and it pays you.' A box is opened, and something put into your hand: a shilling, cold, with a mark struck on its face that you can feel with your thumb: a little raised oblong, like a cut log. 'It never came out of the Penitentiary's chest,' she says. 'All twenty of them have that mark. Somebody's own shillings, marked for their own counting-house.' She takes the coin back. 'I'm not a fool. I know whose mark that is. I've known since Candlemas.' And she will say nothing more about it tonight.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, billet_coin). }
  }
  Discovery billet_coin "The Scaifes' advance for the Carth vigil was paid in shillings countermarked with a little cut log, somebody's own coin marked for their own counting-house. Annis Scaife knows whose mark it is, and will not say.".
  // Why Annis took the vigil: not only the rent.
  Topic annis_ellen with annis "Ask Annis whether she knows whose sorrow she is keeping" when knows(actor, billet_coin) and not knows(actor, ellen_wray) once {
    Says "Annis is quiet so long you think she has gone to sleep. Then: 'My sister Ellen went down to the Row at Martinmas twelvemonth, to proxy for the winter. She was good at it. She could kneel all night on the Steps and get up laughing.' Somewhere the rocking-chair creaks. 'She was in the frost. They've a peg for her in the Barefoot Hall. The thirtieth. I walked down and looked at it.' Another silence. 'So when the Penitentiary's clerk came up the fell with forty nights for sale, and a bag of shillings with that mark on them, I knew whose they were, and what they were for.' Her voice does not change at all. 'And I took them. Two shillings a night to sit in the cold for the man that froze her. Will said I was mad. It's the rent, I said.' You hear her turn over. 'It's not the rent. I want him forgiven by somebody who knows what it cost. A night at a time. I've not decided yet whether I'll finish.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ellen_wray). }
  }
  Discovery ellen_wray "Annis Scaife's sister, Ellen Wray, was one of the forty-one who froze in the Row last winter. Annis knew whose penance the Carth vigil was when she took it, and took it for that: to be the one who forgives him, a night at a time, or does not.".
  Topic will_billhook with will "Ask Will Scaife why he holds the billhook" when knows(actor, vigil_kept) and not state(hearth, ablaze) once {
    Says "For a long time nothing. Then, out of the dark, low: 'Because if anybody lights that hearth, it's twenty shillings back, and Lady Day, and the road.' The billhook shifts on his knees. A long time after that, so long that you have stopped waiting, he says: 'And Ellen's for nothing.' He does not say anything else all night.".
  }
  Topic granny_guest with granny "Ask Old Mother Scaife who the Guest is" when not at(granny, carth_byre) once {
    Says "'The Cold Guest.' She is pleased to be asked. 'When a house lets its fire go out for a debt, the Guest comes and sits at the hearth. You lay him a place, so he knows he's expected and doesn't take offence. My grandmother laid one in the bad winter, and he came, and he sat, and in the spring there were three fewer of them.' The rocking goes on. 'I've laid his place. It's by the hearth. Don't sit in it.' A pause. 'In my mother's day, of course, the beasts were in with us all winter, and nobody had to lay anything. You can't let a fire go out that's a cow.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, beasts_old). }
  }
  Discovery beasts_old "In Old Mother Scaife's mother's day the beasts wintered in the house-place with the family, for the warmth of them.".
  Topic granny_ralph with granny "Ask Old Mother Scaife about Ralph" when true once {
    Says "'Sixty-one years.' Her voice is warm. 'He's in the byre. I sit with him at night, because it's cold in there and he never could abide being cold, and Will won't have him in here with the child.' The rocking stops. 'They say he's dead. He's eighty and he's cold and he doesn't answer, but he never did answer, Ralph.' She laughs, a dry small sound. 'I'll go through to him soon.'".
  }
  Topic dowsie_rhyme with dowsie "Ask Dowsie about the stone man carrying the other man" when not dowsieDead(dowsie) once {
    Says "'Saint Oswy.' Dowsie is hoarse but glad. 'There's a rhyme. The Row children sing it on the ice, Mam says, when we went to market. Oswy, Oswy, up the hill, carry me and carry me still.' She coughs. 'There's more. I don't know the more. The Row children know it.'".
  }
  Topic dowsie_grandad with dowsie "Ask Dowsie what she has heard at night" when not dowsieDead(dowsie) once {
    Says "'Grandad.' A whisper. 'In the byre. Talking, like he did. And somebody comes in in the night, every night, and kneels down by the fire that isn't, and goes out again. Mam says it's the man from the Penitentiary. I've never seen him.' The cough. 'I think it's the Guest.'".
  }

  // ── The night ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation coughHeard(group). Relation grannyGone(group). Relation feverTold(group). Relation hernGave(group).
  Rule night_cough at house_place when carthNight() and at(party, house_place) and hour(clock) >= 21 and not coughHeard(party) and not state(hearth, ablaze)
    says "In the box-bed the child's cough changes. It has been a dry cough, a little bark, like a fox. Now it has something in it that rattles, and after each one there is a breath that goes in too high. Annis Scaife gets up in the dark and you hear her sit down on the bed. Nobody says anything." { Assert coughHeard(party). }
  Rule night_cough_lit at house_place when carthNight() and at(party, house_place) and hour(clock) >= 21 and not coughHeard(party) and state(hearth, ablaze)
    says "In the box-bed the child coughs, a dry little bark like a fox, and then, in the warmth, stops, and sleeps." { Assert coughHeard(party). }
  Rule granny_byre when carthNight() and hour(clock) >= 23 and at(granny, house_place) and not grannyIn(carth_vigil) and not grannyGone(carth_vigil) {
    Assert grannyGone(carth_vigil). Retract at(granny, house_place). Assert at(granny, carth_byre). }
  Rule granny_told at house_place when grannyGone(carth_vigil) and at(party, house_place) and carthNight() and not spread(granny_told)
    says "The rocking-chair creaks, and stops. The old woman gets up, and you hear her feel her way along the wall, and the byre door, and her voice through it, quite ordinary: 'There you are, Ralph. It's cold. Shift up.'" { Assert spread(granny_told). }
  Entity granny_told: fact "the old woman to the byre".
  Rule fever_comes when carthNight() and hour(clock) >= 0 and hour(clock) < 6 and not dowsieSafe(dowsie) and not dowsieBurning(dowsie) { Assert dowsieBurning(dowsie). }
  Rule fever_told at house_place when dowsieBurning(dowsie) and at(party, house_place) and carthNight() and not feverTold(party)
    says "Past midnight the child stops coughing, which is worse. Annis says her name, sharply, and the child answers, but in a voice that is somewhere else, talking about the Minster and a stone man, and laughing. You can feel the heat of her from where you sit against the wall. Will Scaife stands up in the dark. You hear the billhook laid down on the settle, very carefully, as if it might wake somebody." { Assert feverTold(party). }
  // At two, if nothing has been done for the child, Hern does it: he takes off his coat, which is the only warm thing he
  // has, and gets into the box-bed with her, and holds her, and is cold all night.
  Rule hern_gives at house_place when carthNight() and hour(clock) >= 2 and hour(clock) < 6 and not dowsieSafe(dowsie) and at(hern, house_place) and not hernGave(hern)
    says "In the dark Hern gets up. You hear him take off his coat, the frieze coat that is the only warm thing he has, and you hear Annis begin to say something and Hern say, 'Hush. I've done forty nights cold for worse people than her.' The box-bed creaks. 'Shift up, chick. I've done this before. I'm the best there is at it, ask anybody in the Row.' The child laughs, a cracked small laugh, and then coughs, and then is quiet; and for the rest of the night you hear his breathing, and hers, and his is the worse." {
    Assert hernGave(hern). Assert dowsieSafe(dowsie). Assert hernFailing(hern). Assert hernCoat(hern). Retract dowsieBurning(dowsie). }

  // What can be done. In the dark a hearth is felt for, not looked at; what is done here is done by hand.
  Action light_hearth(actor: group, site: place) "Strike a light from the tinderbox on the mantel and light the peat on the hearth" {
    Description "There is peat by the hearth, dry, and thorn; and a tinderbox on the mantel. Twenty-three nights' cold would go out of the room in an hour.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, house_place) and state(hearth, cold) and vigilOn() and not scaifesConsent(carth_vigil).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert state(hearth, ablaze). Assert dowsieSafe(dowsie). Retract dowsieBurning(dowsie). Assert litWithoutLeave(actor). Assert grannyIn(carth_vigil). Retract at(granny, carth_byre). Assert at(granny, house_place). }
    Result "Your hands find the tinderbox on the mantel by memory of where tinderboxes are. Flint, steel, a spark that is the first light in this house in twenty-three nights, so bright it hurts; the tinder; a curl of thorn; the peat. The room comes up out of the dark around you: black beams, a dresser with three plates, a box-bed in the wall full of faces, a settle, a man getting up off it with a billhook in his hand. Will Scaife looks at the fire, and at you. He takes one step. Then Annis has him by the arm. 'It's done,' she says. 'It's done now. Let it burn for her.' He stands there a long time with the billhook, and then he sits down, and puts his hands over his face, and the light comes through his fingers.".
  }
  Rule granny_to_fire at house_place when state(hearth, ablaze) and grannyGone(carth_vigil) and grannyIn(carth_vigil) and carthNight() and not spread(granny_to_fire)
    says "Through the byre door the old woman comes in, feeling along the wall toward the warmth, saying 'Ralph? Ralph, there's a fire.'" { Assert spread(granny_to_fire). }
  Entity granny_to_fire: fact "the old woman comes to the fire".
  Action ask_will_light(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Will Scaife to light the hearth himself, for the child" {
    Description "It is his house, and his vigil, and his child.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, house_place) and at(will, house_place) and state(hearth, cold) and vigilOn()
      and dowsieBurning(dowsie) and not scaifesConsent(carth_vigil) and not triedWill(actor).
    Time 2.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert scaifesConsent(carth_vigil). }
    On failure { Assert triedWill(actor). }
    Result "You say it into the dark: the child, the heat of her, what a fever does at that age in a cold house by morning. Will Scaife says nothing for so long you think he has not heard. Then he gets up, and you hear him at the mantel, and the tinderbox, and the spark. He kneels at the hearth and lights the peat himself, and does not look round. 'There,' he says to the fire, and that is all he says.".
    Otherwise "Will Scaife hears you out in the dark. Then he says, 'Seventeen nights,' and nothing else; and the child mutters about the stone man, and he does not move.".
  }
  Relation triedWill(group).
  Rule will_lights_for_annis at house_place when scaifesConsent(carth_vigil) and annisOrdered(carth_vigil) and state(hearth, cold) and vigilOn() and carthNight()
    says "For a long moment nothing. Then Will Scaife gets up off the settle, and you hear the billhook laid down, and his hands on the mantel, and the tinderbox. The spark is so bright in the dark that it hurts. He kneels and lights the peat, and blows on it, and the room comes up round you out of the black: beams, a dresser, a box-bed full of faces, and Hern sitting against the wall with his eyes shut. Nobody looks at Hern. Annis sits on the bed and watches the fire take, and says, to the fire, 'There. Now we're nothing. Now we owe.'" {
    Assert state(hearth, ablaze). Assert dowsieSafe(dowsie). Retract dowsieBurning(dowsie). Assert grannyIn(carth_vigil). Retract at(granny, carth_byre). Assert at(granny, house_place). }
  Relation annisOrdered(group).
  Rule will_lights when scaifesConsent(carth_vigil) and not annisOrdered(carth_vigil) and state(hearth, cold) and vigilOn() and carthNight() {
    Assert state(hearth, ablaze). Assert dowsieSafe(dowsie). Retract dowsieBurning(dowsie). Assert grannyIn(carth_vigil). Retract at(granny, carth_byre). Assert at(granny, house_place). }
  // Hern's own refusal, told to the house that is keeping what he would not.
  Action hern_confesses(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Hern to tell the Scaifes what penance he refused last winter" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, house_place) and at(hern, house_place) and knows(actor, vigil_refused)
      and knows(actor, vigil_kept) and not hernConfessed(hern) and not hernDead(hern).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert hernConfessed(hern). }
    Result "Hern tells them, into the dark, plainly: the Cold Vigil, Candlemas, forty nights for a blood-fault, offered to him first; and that he said no. Nobody speaks. Then Annis Scaife says, very quietly, 'You. You've kept three. Everybody knows you've kept three.' 'Yes.' 'You could have kept this.' 'Yes.' 'And so it came to us.' 'Yes,' says Hern. 'I didn't think who it would come to. I thought about the man who paid.' A long silence. Then Annis says: 'Will. Light it.' And when he does not move: 'Light it, Will. Let him see what it costs. Let him sit in it.'".
  }
  Rule annis_consents when hernConfessed(hern) and vigilOn() and carthNight() and not scaifesConsent(carth_vigil) and state(hearth, cold) { Assert scaifesConsent(carth_vigil). Assert annisOrdered(carth_vigil). }
  // The letter of it: Raistrick tests the hearth. Rake the fire out and pack the hearth with snow before he comes, and
  // light it again when he has gone.
  Action quench_hearth(actor: group, site: place) "Rake the fire off the hearth and pack the hearth with snow from the door" {
    Description "So that when a hand is put into the ash, it is cold.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, house_place) and state(hearth, ablaze) and vigilOn() and knows(actor, ash_test).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert state(hearth, snowed). Assert quenched(carth_vigil). }
    Result "You rake the burning peat off the hearth onto the shovel and out of the door into the snow, where it hisses and dies, and you bring in snow in your hands, armful after armful, and pack it down on the hot stone, which spits. Steam goes up in the last of the light. Then the dark again, and the cold coming back into the room like water into a footprint. Annis Scaife says nothing at all, and you can feel her not saying it.".
  }
  Relation quenched(group).
  Action relight_hearth(actor: group, site: place) "Rake the wet off the hearth and light it again" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, house_place) and state(hearth, snowed) and reeveDone(carth_vigil).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert state(hearth, ablaze). }
    Result "Dry peat from the stack, the tinderbox, the spark. The fire comes up again, smokier for the wet, and the faces in the box-bed come back out of the dark one by one.".
  }
  // The byre: a fire there is not a fire on the hearth.
  Action byre_fire(actor: group, site: place) "Make a fire of straw and thorn in the old fire-pit in the byre, and bring the household through to it" {
    Description "Raistrick puts his hand in the hearth. He has never once looked anywhere else.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and inHouse() and vigilOn() and knows(actor, ash_test) and not byreFire(carth_vigil) and not state(hearth, ablaze) and nightfall().
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert byreFire(carth_vigil). Assert dowsieSafe(dowsie). Retract dowsieBurning(dowsie). Assert grannyIn(carth_vigil). Retract at(party, house_place). Assert at(party, carth_byre). }
    Result "In the byre wall there is an old fire-pit, from before the house had a chimney: a ring of blackened stones. You lay straw in it, and thorn, and strike a light, and the byre comes up out of the dark: the cow, turning her head; the calf; the old woman on her stool by a long shape under a sheet, blinking. Will Scaife comes to the byre door and looks at the fire for a long time. He says nothing. Then he goes back and lifts the child out of the box-bed in her blankets and brings her through, and lays her in the straw by the fire, and sits down beside her; and Annis comes after them with every blanket in the house; and nobody says the word vigil, or the word hearth, all night.".
  }
  Action beasts_in(actor: group, site: place) "Bring the cow and the calf through from the byre into the house-place" {
    Description "The old way: a beast is a fire nobody can call one.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, house_place) and vigilOn() and (capable(actor, woodcraft) or knows(actor, beasts_old)) and not beastsIn(carth_vigil) and not state(hearth, ablaze) and nightfall().
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert beastsIn(carth_vigil). Assert dowsieSafe(dowsie). Retract dowsieBurning(dowsie). }
    Result "Through the byre door in the dark, a hand on the cow's warm flank, a word, a push; she comes, as cows will, at last, all at once, and the calf after her bawling. You stand them by the box-bed with their great breathing sides to it, and the smell of them fills the house-place, hay and dung and milk and warmth, and the cold goes back from the bed a yard, and then another. Old Mother Scaife laughs out loud in the dark. 'That's how it was,' she says. 'That's how it was.' The child's breathing eases. It is not much warmer. It is enough.".
  }
  Action share_bed(actor: group, site: place) "Get into the box-bed with the household, everyone together, under every blanket in the house" {
    Description "Heat is heat, and you have some.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, house_place) and vigilOn() and not sharedBed(carth_vigil) and not state(hearth, ablaze) and nightfall()
      and (coughHeard(actor) or dowsieBurning(dowsie)).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert sharedBed(carth_vigil). Assert dowsieSafe(dowsie). Retract dowsieBurning(dowsie). Assert strikes(carth_cold, actor). }
    Result "Annis Scaife says 'What—' and then, 'Aye. All right. Aye.' You get into the box-bed in the dark with your boots off, against the wall, with the child between you and her mother, and Will on the other side of his wife like a wall, and a dog across all your feet, and every blanket and coat and sack in the house over the lot of you. The child is so hot it is like holding a loaf. Her breathing goes on against your neck all night, and some time before morning it changes, and eases; and you are colder than you have ever been, on the outside of all that warmth, and you do not move.".
  }
  Hazard carth_cold "a night on the cold side of the bed" means "Deal (1d3) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (11).".
  Action nurse_child(actor: group, site: place) "Sit up with Dowsie through the fever" {
    Description "Cold cloths and warm hands, and water a sip at a time, and somebody who knows what the breathing means.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, house_place) and capable(actor, mending) and dowsieBurning(dowsie) and not nursed(dowsie).
    Time 12.
    On success { Assert nursed(dowsie). Assert dowsieSafe(dowsie). Retract dowsieBurning(dowsie). }
    Result "You sit on the edge of the box-bed in the dark with your hand on her forehead and a wet cloth, and you count her breaths, and when they go wrong you sit her up, and when she burns you cool her, and when she shivers you hold her. Annis holds the cup. Neither of you says anything for two hours. Some time after that, the child sighs, and turns over, and sleeps; and her forehead under your hand is only warm.".
  }
  // The old woman in the byre: sat with, she is watched over; laid out with the rites, he is let go, and she comes in.
  Relation sawGranny(group).
  Action sit_with_granny(actor: group, site: place) "Sit up in the byre with Old Mother Scaife" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, carth_byre) and at(granny, carth_byre) and not sawGranny(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert sawGranny(actor). Assert grannyWatched(carth_vigil). }
    Result "You sit on the straw in the dark by the cow's warm side, and the old woman talks to Ralph: about a dance at Martinmas in a year with no name, about a pig, about how cold it is. After a while she stops talking, and you hear her get up off the stool, and the hurdle creak, and the sheet move. She has lain down beside him, under the sheet, against him, with her arms round him; to warm him. 'There,' she says, quite content. 'There.' You understand, then, how the dead man comes to have moved in the night.".
  }
  Discovery granny_lies "Each night Old Mother Scaife lies down beside her dead husband in the byre, under his sheet, to warm him.".
  Rule granny_seen when sawGranny(party) and not knows(party, granny_lies) says "Old Mother Scaife lies down by her husband in the dark, every night, to warm him." teaches granny_lies { }
  Relation grannyWatched(group).
  Action lay_out_ralph(actor: group, site: place) "Lay Ralph Scaife out properly on his hurdle, and say the words for the dead over him" {
    Description "The words for one who is going, said by someone who has the right to say them.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, carth_byre) and capable(actor, rites) and not ralphLaid(carth_vigil).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert ralphLaid(carth_vigil). Assert grannyIn(carth_vigil). Retract at(granny, carth_byre). Assert at(granny, house_place). }
    Result "You straighten him on the hurdle: his hands, which have been folded two ways and slept with, folded once more; his jaw bound; his eyes, which someone has been opening, closed and weighted with two of his own buttons. Then you say the words, in the dark, the ones for a man who is going. The old woman listens with her hand on his chest. At the end she says, 'Going. Aye. He always was slow,' and lets you take her hand, and stands up off the stool, and comes back through into the house-place to sit by the child; and does not go into the byre again that night.".
  }
  Topic granny_come_in with granny "Ask Old Mother Scaife to come through and sit with the child" when at(granny, carth_byre) and dowsieBurning(dowsie) and not grannyIn(carth_vigil) once {
    Says "The old woman is quiet a moment. 'The child?' Then the stool scrapes. 'Ralph,' she says, 'I'll be back. Don't you go anywhere.' She comes through with her hand on your arm, and sits on the edge of the box-bed and takes the child's hot hand in her two cold ones, and begins to sing under her breath, a song with no tune; and stays there.".
    On discuss { Assert grannyIn(carth_vigil). Retract at(granny, carth_byre). Assert at(granny, house_place). }
  }

  // ── The Ash-reeve ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At three, unannounced, he comes in, kneels, and puts his bare hand into the ash of the hearth. He holds it there a
  // watch; in that time the company, if it is awake and there, can speak to him.
  Relation reeveKneeling(group). Relation reeveDone(group). Measure reeveAt(group).
  Rule reeve_comes when carthNight() and hour(clock) >= 3 and hour(clock) < 6 and not reeveDone(carth_vigil) and not reeveKneeling(raistrick) and vigilOn() {
    Assert reeveKneeling(raistrick). Assert at(raistrick, house_place). Set reeveAt(raistrick) to watch(clock). }
  Rule reeve_told_byre within carth_house when reeveKneeling(raistrick) and byreFire(carth_vigil) and inHouse() and not spread(reeve_told)
    says "Through the byre wall you hear the house door: the latch, and nobody knocking, and boots on the flagstones, exact and unhurried, crossing to the hearth. The cow turns her head toward the sound. In the straw by the fire-pit nobody moves." { Assert spread(reeve_told). }
  Rule reeve_told_lit within carth_house when reeveKneeling(raistrick) and state(hearth, ablaze) and inHouse() and not spread(reeve_told)
    says "The latch lifts. Nobody knocked. A long man in a sheepskin comes in out of the snow and shuts the door behind him, and in the firelight he does not look at any of you, or at the child, or at the fire. He kneels at the hearth and puts his bare hand into the ash at the fire's edge, under the burning peat, and holds it there; and his face does not change at all." { Assert spread(reeve_told). }
  Rule reeve_told within carth_house when reeveKneeling(raistrick) and not byreFire(carth_vigil) and not state(hearth, ablaze) and inHouse() and not spread(reeve_told)
    says "The latch lifts. Nobody knocked. Cold air comes in along the floor and finds your ankles, and the door shuts, and someone is in the room: you hear the snow fall off him, and his breathing, slow, and his boots cross the flagstones, exactly, without feeling for anything, as a man crosses his own kitchen. He kneels at the hearth. You hear the ash move. He is holding his hand in it. Nobody in the house breathes. In the box-bed even the child is still." { Assert spread(reeve_told). }
  Entity reeve_told: fact "the Ash-reeve kneels".
  Action deceive_reeve(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the man at the hearth the warmth is the child's: she burned with fever, and was laid on the hearthstone to cool" {
    Description "It is a lie. It may be the kind he cannot afford to check.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, house_place) and reeveKneeling(raistrick) and state(hearth, ablaze) and not reeveDeceived(raistrick) and not triedReeve(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert reeveDeceived(raistrick). }
    On failure { Assert triedReeve(actor). }
    Result "The man at the hearth is quite still. Then, in the firelight, he turns his head and looks at the child in the box-bed, flushed, asleep, and at the hearthstone, and at you. 'A fever,' he says. He takes his hand out of the ash and wipes it on his sheepskin, slowly. 'I've known a fever warm a stone.' He stands. 'Kept,' he says, to nobody, and goes out; and you understand that he has decided to believe you, and that he will not do it twice.".
    Otherwise "Raistrick does not look at you. 'The ash is warm,' he says, 'not the stone. A child's fever doesn't make a fire.' He takes his hand out of the hearth.".
  }
  Relation triedReeve(group).
  // What he finds is decided when he takes his hand out, by the hearth as it is then; a fire lit again after he has gone
  // is not his business until tomorrow night.
  Relation reeveFoundWarm(group). Relation reeveFoundCold(group). Relation reeveFoundWet(group).
  Query reeveRising() means reeveKneeling(raistrick) and watch(clock) >= reeveAt(raistrick) + 1.
  Rule reeve_finds_warm when reeveRising() and state(hearth, ablaze) and not reeveDeceived(raistrick) and vigilOn() {
    Assert reeveFoundWarm(carth_vigil). Assert vigilBroken(carth_vigil). Assert vigilEnded(carth_vigil). }
  Rule reeve_finds_wet when reeveRising() and state(hearth, snowed) and vigilOn() { Assert reeveFoundWet(carth_vigil). }
  Rule reeve_finds_cold when reeveRising() and (state(hearth, cold) or reeveDeceived(raistrick)) and vigilOn() { Assert reeveFoundCold(carth_vigil). }
  Rule reeve_judges when reeveRising() {
    Retract reeveKneeling(raistrick). Assert reeveDone(carth_vigil). Assert at(raistrick, reeve_hut). }
  Rule reeve_broken within carth_house when reeveFoundWarm(carth_vigil) and inHouse() and not spread(reeve_kept)
    says "Raistrick takes his hand out of the warm ash and looks at it in the firelight as if it had told him something about himself. 'Broken,' he says. He does not say it unkindly. He takes a stick out of his coat and a knife, and cuts a mark on it, and goes out into the snow, and the door shuts." { Assert spread(reeve_kept). }
  Rule reeve_kept_cold within carth_house when reeveFoundCold(carth_vigil) and not byreFire(carth_vigil) and not reeveDeceived(raistrick) and inHouse() and not spread(reeve_kept)
    says "He takes his hand out of the ash. He stands, and you hear him wipe it on his coat. 'Kept,' he says, and goes out, and the cold air goes along the floor after him." { Assert spread(reeve_kept). }
  Rule reeve_kept_wet within carth_house when reeveFoundWet(carth_vigil) and inHouse() and not spread(reeve_kept)
    says "He takes his hand out of the hearth and holds it up. It drips. He says nothing; you can hear him thinking, a sound like a stone being turned over in a field. 'Wet,' he says. 'Cold.' He wipes his hand. 'Kept,' he says, and goes out." { Assert spread(reeve_kept). }
  Rule reeve_kept_byre within carth_house when reeveFoundCold(carth_vigil) and byreFire(carth_vigil) and inHouse() and not spread(reeve_kept)
    says "From the byre, where the whole household lies in the straw by the fire-pit, you can hear him kneeling at the dead hearth, and nothing else but the cow shifting her feet. Then he sniffs. Smoke: the whole house smells of it. You hear him stand up. Then you hear him kneel down again, and put his hand back in the ash, and hold it there; and stand; and say 'Kept,' in a voice like a man putting down something heavy; and go." { Assert spread(reeve_kept). }
  Entity reeve_kept: fact "kept".

  // ── Morning ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The first six o'clock after the night: what happened is told plainly.
  Rule morning_comes when carthNight() and hour(clock) >= 7 and dayN(gaunt_town) > carthDay(party) { Assert nightOver(party). Assert morningDue(carth_vigil). Set morningAt(carth_vigil) to watch(clock). }
  Measure morningAt(group).
  Relation morningDue(group).
  Rule child_dies when morningDue(carth_vigil) and not dowsieSafe(dowsie) and not dowsieDead(dowsie) { Assert dowsieDead(dowsie). }
  Rule granny_cold when morningDue(carth_vigil) and not grannyIn(carth_vigil) and not grannyCold(carth_vigil) { Assert grannyCold(carth_vigil). }
  Rule kept_tonight when morningDue(carth_vigil) and vigilOn() and not vigilKept(carth_vigil) { Assert vigilKept(carth_vigil). Increase vigilNight(carth_vigil) by 1. }
  Rule morning_byre within carth when morningDue(carth_vigil) and atCarth() and dowsieSafe(dowsie) and byreFire(carth_vigil) and not hernCoat(hern) and not spread(morning_told)
    says "Morning comes grey through the cracks of the byre door. The fire in the old pit is down to one red eye. The child is asleep in the straw between the calf and her father, cool, with her mouth open; Annis asleep sitting up against the hurdle; the old woman asleep on her stool with her hand on the sheet. Will is the first up. He scatters the ash of the fire-pit with his boot, and goes out to dig. Snow has stopped in the night; it lies to the knee in the yard, and the light off it is so white after the dark that it hurts." { Assert spread(morning_told). }
  Rule morning_child_well within carth when morningDue(carth_vigil) and atCarth() and dowsieSafe(dowsie) and not byreFire(carth_vigil) and not hernCoat(hern) and not spread(morning_told)
    says "Morning comes grey through the one window. The child is asleep, and cool, with her mouth open, and her mother asleep sitting up beside her. Will Scaife is at the door, digging. Snow has stopped in the night; it lies to the knee in the yard and to the eaves on the north side, and the light off it is so white after the dark that it hurts." { Assert spread(morning_told). }
  Rule morning_hern_coat within carth when morningDue(carth_vigil) and atCarth() and hernCoat(hern) and not spread(morning_told)
    says "Morning comes grey through the one window. The child is asleep and cool in the box-bed, wrapped in a frieze coat that is not hers. Beside her, on the outside, is Hern, in his shirt, grey as the ash, with his lips blue, awake. He sees you looking and grins. 'Kept her warm,' he says, and it comes out in a whisper, with the cough under it like a stone under a sheet. 'Professional.'" { Assert spread(morning_told). }
  Rule morning_child_dead within carth when morningDue(carth_vigil) and atCarth() and dowsieDead(dowsie) and not spread(morning_told)
    says "Morning comes grey through the one window. Annis Scaife is sitting on the edge of the box-bed with the child in her lap, and she is not rocking her. Nobody has said anything yet, and nobody does. After a while Will gets up, and goes out to the byre, and you hear him moving the hurdle along to make room." { Assert spread(morning_told). }
  Entity morning_told: fact "the morning at Carth".
  Rule morning_granny within carth when morningDue(carth_vigil) and grannyCold(carth_vigil) and atCarth() and spread(morning_told) and watch(clock) > morningAt(carth_vigil) and not spread(morning_granny)
    says "In the byre the old woman is asleep under the sheet against her husband, with her arms round him. Her hands, when Annis takes them, are white to the wrist, and she does not feel it. She wakes, and is cross to be woken. 'He was cold,' she explains, and lets herself be brought in to sit by the dead hearth, and by night she will go through to him again." { Assert spread(morning_granny). }
  Entity morning_granny: fact "the old woman in the morning".
  // Morning's verdict on the company, from the household: who lit what without asking is told to go when the road opens.
  Rule morning_go within carth when morningDue(carth_vigil) and atCarth() and litWithoutLeave(party) and vigilBroken(carth_vigil) and spread(morning_told) and watch(clock) > morningAt(carth_vigil) and not spread(morning_go)
    says "Will Scaife does not look at you all morning. When he has dug the yard gate clear he stands by it, and waits, and you understand that he is waiting for you to go through it. Annis puts a heel of bread in your hand at the door, without a word, and shuts it." { Assert spread(morning_go). }
  Entity morning_go: fact "told to go".
  Rule morning_relit within carth when morningDue(carth_vigil) and atCarth() and quenched(carth_vigil) and state(hearth, ablaze) and vigilOn() and spread(morning_told) and watch(clock) > morningAt(carth_vigil) and not spread(morning_wet)
    says "Will Scaife sits with his boots to the fire that was lit again after the Ash-reeve went, smoking still for the wet. 'Kept,' he says, as if trying the word for weight. 'He had his hand in it. Kept.' He puts on another peat, and goes out to dig." { Assert spread(morning_wet). }
  Rule morning_wet within carth when morningDue(carth_vigil) and atCarth() and quenched(carth_vigil) and state(hearth, snowed) and vigilOn() and spread(morning_told) and watch(clock) > morningAt(carth_vigil) and not spread(morning_wet)
    says "Will Scaife looks at the hearth, black and wet, with the ash in it gone to a paste. Then he looks at you. 'Kept,' he says; and says it again, to see whether it will hold; and goes out to dig." { Assert spread(morning_wet). }
  Entity morning_wet: fact "the wet hearth".
  // Whoever lit the hearth without leave and broke the vigil has taken its debt: seventeen nights, in the Register.
  Rule debt_taken when vigilBroken(carth_vigil) and litWithoutLeave(party) and not brokeVigil(party) { Assert brokeVigil(party). }

  // ── After: the vigil goes on, a night at a time ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Each morning after the first, while it is kept, another night is counted. The old woman who sleeps in the byre
  // with no one to stop her does not see the twenty-sixth morning.
  Relation nightCounted(group).
  Rule vigil_counts when vigilOn() and morningDue(carth_vigil) and hour(clock) == 6 and not nightCounted(carth_vigil) and dayN(gaunt_town) >= 3 { Increase vigilNight(carth_vigil) by 1. Assert nightCounted(carth_vigil). }
  Rule vigil_count_resets when nightCounted(carth_vigil) and hour(clock) != 6 { Retract nightCounted(carth_vigil). }
  Relation grannyDead(group).
  Rule granny_dies when vigilOn() and grannyCold(carth_vigil) and not grannyWatched(carth_vigil) and not ralphLaid(carth_vigil) and vigilNight(carth_vigil) >= 26 and not grannyDead(granny) { Assert grannyDead(granny). Assert at(granny, limbo). }
  // Raistrick keeps every night of it: at three, in the house, whether anyone is there or not.
  Rule reeve_again when vigilOn() and hour(clock) == 3 and morningDue(carth_vigil) and not at(raistrick, house_place) and not reeveKneeling(raistrick) { Assert at(raistrick, house_place). }
  Rule reeve_again_goes when hour(clock) == 4 and at(raistrick, house_place) and not reeveKneeling(raistrick) { Assert at(raistrick, reeve_hut). }
  // Released, the vigil ends: the fire is lit, and stays lit.
  Rule released_lit when vigilReleased(carth_vigil) and not state(hearth, ablaze) { Assert state(hearth, ablaze). Assert vigilEnded(carth_vigil). Assert grannyIn(carth_vigil). }
  Rule granny_comes_home when vigilEnded(carth_vigil) and at(granny, carth_byre) and not grannyDead(granny) { Assert at(granny, house_place). }
  Observe house_after at house_place when morningDue(carth_vigil) and vigilOn() and not state(hearth, ablaze) and nightfall() "The house-place at Carth, dark again for the night: the cold has come back into it and sat down.".
  Observe granny_gone_scene at carth_byre when grannyDead(granny) "The byre at Carth, and along the far wall two long shapes on two hurdles under two sheets.".
  Observe released_scene at house_place when vigilReleased(carth_vigil) "There is a fire on the hearth at Carth that nobody is afraid of, and a pot on it, and steam; and by the hearth, on the cloth, the place laid for the Guest has been taken up, and the bowl put back on the dresser.".

  // ── People at Carth by day ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic annis_morning with annis "Ask Annis what will happen to them now" when morningDue(carth_vigil) and vigilBroken(carth_vigil) once {
    Says "'Nothing,' says Annis. 'Nothing happens. That's what happens.' She is cutting bread very thin. 'We give back the twenty. We haven't got it; it went to the Fabric for the rent. So the Fabric has us out at Lady Day anyway, and the Penitentiary has us for twenty shillings, and we go to the Row and do penances for the people that paid for this one.' She puts the knife down. 'You'd think somebody had arranged it.'".
  }
  Topic annis_kept with annis "Ask Annis whether the vigil was kept" when morningDue(carth_vigil) and vigilOn() once {
    Says "'Kept,' says Annis. 'Twenty-four. Sixteen to go.' She does not thank you or blame you. She is cutting bread very thin. 'He'll be back tonight. And the next. You've a city to go to.' Then, not looking up: 'If you see the man that's sorry, in Gaunt, you might tell him it's cold.'".
  }
  Topic will_morning with will "Speak to Will Scaife" when morningDue(carth_vigil) once {
    Says "Will Scaife leans on his shovel in the yard and looks at the fell, where the road is, under the snow. 'Two years behind,' he says, to the fell. 'My father farmed it fifty years and never was behind. Then the Fabric put the rent up for the tower.' He looks at you. 'They're building a tower,' he says, as if it were the strangest thing he knew. 'Two hundred years.' He goes back to digging.".
  }
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/clock.ky:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── Four days to the Fast ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Gaunt's days are counted from the company's coming, at each six o'clock after its first hour in the country: the
  // day it comes is the first (Saturday). Shrove Monday is the second, Fastens' Eve the third, Ash Day the fourth. The
  // Consistory sits at noon on Ash Day; the Gate of Ash is opened at dusk; the book closes at six that evening.
  Measure dayN(place). Relation dawned(place).
  Initially Set dayN(gaunt_town) to 1.
  Rule dawn_counts when hour(clock) == 6 and not dawned(gaunt_town) and watch(clock) >= 6 { Increase dayN(gaunt_town) by 1. Assert dawned(gaunt_town). }
  Rule dawn_passes when hour(clock) != 6 and dawned(gaunt_town) { Retract dawned(gaunt_town). }
  Query firstDay() means dayN(gaunt_town) == 1.
  Query mondayN() means dayN(gaunt_town) == 2.
  Query eveDay() means dayN(gaunt_town) == 3.
  Query ashDay() means dayN(gaunt_town) == 4.
  Query afterAsh() means dayN(gaunt_town) >= 5.
  Query daytime() means hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 18.
  // The dark of a February night: the world's own dark comes at nine and goes at six whatever the month, so Gaunt keeps
  // its own, from five in the afternoon to seven in the morning.
  Query nightfall() means hour(clock) >= 17 or hour(clock) < 7.
  Query evening() means hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 23.
  Query smallHours() means hour(clock) >= 0 and hour(clock) < 6.
  // Fastens' Eve: the licence, from seven until the Fast is rung in at midnight.
  Query licence() means eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 19.
  // The Consistory: in the Chapter House from noon on Ash Day until it rises at two.
  Query sitting() means ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 14.
  Query sentenced() means ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 14 or afterAsh().
  // The book closes at six on Ash Day; for a company that is elsewhere, the next morning all the same.
  Query accounting() means cameToGaunt(party) and (ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 18 or afterAsh()).

  // ── The chapters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Each day opens on the first page after six on which the company is in the country, in the city's own voice: what
  // the city is doing, and what the day is for.
  Rule chapter_monday when mondayN() and hour(clock) >= 6 and inCountry() and not spread(chapter_monday)
    says "SHROVE MONDAY. In Gaunt the bells of the Minster ring the hour, and the Stand opens at eight, and the Ladder of Merit is read by more people than read anything else in the city. Today the bakers have two days left to sell what the Fast will forbid, and the Consistory has two days to make up its mind about a man whose mind is made up." { Assert spread(chapter_monday). }
  Rule chapter_eve when eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 6 and inCountry() and not spread(chapter_eve)
    says "FASTENS' EVE. The last day before the Fast. At two the Doctors dispute in the Schools; at seven the masks come out, and the Fat King is carried round the Middle Town on a door, to be burnt at midnight outside the Wood Exchange, where wood is dearest; and at midnight the tenor bell of the Minster rings the Fast in, and whatever was said under a mask was never said." { Assert spread(chapter_eve). }
  Rule chapter_ash when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 6 and inCountry() and not spread(chapter_ash)
    says "ASH DAY. At nine every forehead in Gaunt is marked with ash at the Minster door, and the Ladder of Merit is gilded for the year. At noon the Consistory sits in the Chapter House on the matter of Ninian Hern. At dusk, for the first time in nineteen years, the Gate of Ash may be opened." { Assert spread(chapter_ash). }
  Entity chapter_monday: fact "Shrove Monday". Entity chapter_eve: fact "Fastens' Eve". Entity chapter_ash: fact "Ash Day".

  // ── Where the company is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A company that has come into Gaunt's country at all: every ending and every fate asks it.
  Relation cameToGaunt(group).
  // The rooms of the city, and of the country round it (the road, Carth, the Levels, the wood): country.kyr marks each.
  Relation townRoom(place). Relation countryRoom(place).
  Rule came_in when at(party, ?p) and countryRoom(?p) and not cameToGaunt(party) { Assert cameToGaunt(party). }
  Query inTown() means at(party, ?p) and townRoom(?p).
  Query inCountry() means at(party, ?p) and countryRoom(?p).
  // A place the company has left and come back to is told shortly.
  Relation visitedNow(place). Relation visitedBefore(place).
  Rule arrives_at when at(party, ?p) and not visitedNow(?p) { Assert visitedNow(?p). }
  Rule leaves_from when visitedNow(?p) and not at(party, ?p) { Retract visitedNow(?p). Assert visitedBefore(?p). }
  // What a place shows the company the first time, it shows until the company has learned it and gone away (a line held
  // only until it is known would be gone before the page that shows it is drawn: Hessel's friction 4).
  Relation teachesAt(entity, place). Relation seenOnce(entity).
  Rule seen_once_at when knows(party, ?f) and teachesAt(?f, ?p) and not at(party, ?p) and not seenOnce(?f) { Assert seenOnce(?f). }
  // Whoever is going along with the company keeps up with it.
  Rule keep_up when following(?x, party) and at(party, ?p) and not at(?x, ?p) and not hernTesting(?x) { Assert at(?x, ?p). }
  // News already told, so it is not told twice.
  Relation spread(fact).

  // Fastens' Eve in the streets, for whoever is in the city and not already where it is told (the Shambles, the Fat Lamb).
  Rule eve_masks when eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 23 and inTown() and not at(party, shambles) and not at(party, fat_lamb) and not spread(eve_masks)
    says "At seven the masks come out. All over the Middle Town the shutters go up again and the torches are lit, and from the Shambles comes a drum, and a roar, and over the roofs, on a door, a wooden giant with a pig's head and a barrel for a belly goes by on the shoulders of eight apprentices: the Fat King, on his way to be burnt. Everybody you pass is somebody else until midnight." { Assert spread(eve_masks). }
  Entity eve_masks: fact "the masks come out".
  Rule fast_bell when ashDay() and hour(clock) < 6 and inTown() and not hernDead(hern) and not spread(fast_bell)
    says "At midnight the tenor bell of the Minster rings the Fast in, one stroke, and then another, slow, over the whole city; outside the Wood Exchange the Fat King goes up in a sheet of flame; and all over the Middle Town the masks come off at once, as if somebody had said a word. Whatever was said tonight was never said." { Assert spread(fast_bell). }
  Entity fast_bell: fact "the Fast rung in".
  // The city's own hours, told to whoever is in its streets.
  Rule stand_hiring when mondayN() and hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 11 and inTown() and not at(party, the_stand) and not spread(stand_hiring)
    says "The Stand is hiring, in the old sheep-market, and you can hear it from streets away: a clerk calling names, and burgesses' men calling rates, FASTS THREEPENCE, BAREFOOT A SHILLING THE MILE, and a sound under it like a fair, which is two hundred people waiting to be hired to be sorry." { Assert spread(stand_hiring). }
  Entity stand_hiring: fact "the Stand opens".
  Rule proxies_home when mondayN() and hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 20 and inTown() and not spread(proxies_home)
    says "At dusk the proxies come home through Bow Gate to the Row: the day's fasters walking carefully, the barefoot ones with their boots slung round their necks, a woman with a board still on her back saying somebody else's fault in somebody else's name, which she has forgotten to take off. Nobody talks much. In the Middle Town, behind them, the lamps go on in the houses of the forgiven." { Assert spread(proxies_home). }
  Entity proxies_home: fact "the proxies home".
  Rule ashing when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 11 and inTown() and not inChapter() and not spread(ashing)
    says "At nine the Minster's west door is opened and the city goes past it in a line that reaches down the Bearer's Steps and into the Shambles, and a canon with a bowl of ash puts his thumb to every forehead, the brewster's and the barefoot man's alike, and says the same four words to each. For an hour everyone in Gaunt has the same mark on them. Then they go and look at the Ladder." { Assert spread(ashing). }
  Entity ashing: fact "the ashing".

  // ── Aims the page can lead with ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Objective who_paid_for_carth when knows(party, vigil_kept) and not knows(party, thackray_vigil)
    "Someone paid the Scaifes of Carth to sit forty nights without a fire. The coin carries a little cut log.".
  Objective under_the_window when knows(party, hal_plan) and not hernFreed(hern) and not verdictGiven(consistory)
    "Hal Metcalfe means to be under the gaol window at eleven on Fastens' Eve with a ladder and a file.".
  Objective ash_day_sitting when knows(party, beadle_offer) and not verdictGiven(consistory)
    "The Consistory of Gaunt sits on Ninian Hern on Ash Day.".
  Objective north_tower when knows(party, unbuilding) and not knows(party, lodge_under)
    "By night Canon Laverock's men take down the course of stone Joby Thwaite's masons set on the north tower by day.".
}

Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // The campaign played alone: a traveller come up the march road to the Penitent's Cross at nine in the morning, three
  // days before the Fast, with a little money and nowhere in particular to be. (placed.kyr is the world's own company,
  // come over the march by the same road.)
  Company party "You" of 1 to 3 at cross_road.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 10. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 2.
}

Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── The account ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At six on Ash Day the book closes on an account: each strand's morning after, told plainly, then one ending, by what
  // the Consistory did. No custom, no ever-after; the next morning, and stop.
  Rule fate_carth_released when accounting() and vigilReleased(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_carth) says "At Carth there is a fire on the hearth and a cart of oak in the yard, and the forty nights are paid in full by the man who bought them, and the rent with them. Ralph Scaife is still in the byre, because the ground is still iron; but there is a lamp by him now, and nobody has to lie down with him to keep him warm. Annis Scaife has walked down to the Barefoot Hall and painted her sister's name on the thirtieth peg herself, in white, and rubbed out the little mark beside it." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_paid when accounting() and vigilBroken(carth_vigil) and scaifesPaid(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_carth) says "The Carth vigil was broken, and paid for in full all the same by the man who bought it, with a cart of oak besides; and the Scaifes owe nothing to anyone, which Will Scaife says he does not know how to feel about, and sits by his fire feeling it." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_forgiven when accounting() and vigilBroken(carth_vigil) and arrearsForgiven(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_carth) says "The Carth vigil was broken, and the Scaifes owe the Penitentiary twenty shillings they have not got; but the Fabric has forgiven them two years' rent, for reasons the Master of the Fabric describes as charity, and they keep the farm, and a fire, and the debt, which in Gaunt is the same as owning a cow." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_ruined when accounting() and vigilBroken(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_carth) says "The Carth vigil was broken, and the Scaifes owe the twenty shillings back, and the rent besides. At Lady Day the Fabric will have them off the fell. Annis Scaife has already been down to the Stand to ask the rates for a fast." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_kept_forgiven when accounting() and vigilOn() and arrearsForgiven(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_carth) says "The Carth vigil goes on, a night at a time, and Raistrick comes at three to put his hand in the ash. The Fabric has forgiven the arrears, so the Scaifes will be paid forty shillings for nothing they owe, at the thaw, and do not know what to do with that either." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_kept_struck when accounting() and vigilOn() and putOut(party) and not spread(fate_carth) says "The Carth vigil goes on, a night at a time, with more people in the house to keep it than there were, and so more warmth in the box-bed, which Raistrick cannot put his hand in." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_kept when accounting() and vigilOn() and not spread(fate_carth) says "The Carth vigil goes on: night twenty-six tonight, fourteen to go. Raistrick will come at three and kneel and put his hand in the ash, and say 'Kept', and go. At the thaw the Scaifes will be paid, and pay the Fabric, and be square, and it will be spring." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Entity fate_carth: fact "Carth".
  Rule fate_child_dead when accounting() and dowsieDead(dowsie) and not spread(fate_child) says "Dowsie Scaife lies in the byre at Carth beside her grandfather, under a clean sheet, until the ground will take a spade." { Assert spread(fate_child). }
  Rule fate_child when accounting() and not dowsieDead(dowsie) and stayingAtCarth(party) and not spread(fate_child) says "Dowsie Scaife is up and about in her mother's shawl, with a cough she is proud of, telling the hens about the stone man in the Minster, who she has never seen." { Assert spread(fate_child). }
  Entity fate_child: fact "Dowsie".
  Rule fate_granny_dead when accounting() and grannyDead(granny) and not spread(fate_granny) says "On the twenty-sixth morning of the vigil Old Mother Scaife did not come in from the byre. She had gone through to Ralph in the night, as she did every night, and lain down under the sheet with him to keep him warm; and this time nobody brought her back. There are two hurdles in the byre at Carth now." { Assert spread(fate_granny). }
  Rule fate_granny_laid when accounting() and ralphLaid(carth_vigil) and not grannyDead(granny) and not spread(fate_granny) says "Old Mother Scaife sits by the hearth at Carth in the rocking-chair and does not go into the byre at night. Ralph, she tells the hens, is going; he always was slow." { Assert spread(fate_granny). }
  Entity fate_granny: fact "the old woman".
  Rule fate_thackray_bore_warm when accounting() and thackrayBears(thackray) and vigilReleased(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_thackray) says "Hugh Thackray is struck from the Register of Gaunt and from the Ladder of Merit, where a mason has chiselled his name out of the gold, leaving a long pale scar at the top of the board that nobody will paint over. He walked to Carth in a pair of borrowed boots and knocked, and Annis Scaife let him in, and gave him the axe, and he is splitting the oak he sent up the fell, very badly, in the yard, in the snow, and will not come in to the fire until it is all done." { Assert spread(fate_thackray). }
  Rule fate_thackray_bore when accounting() and thackrayBears(thackray) and not spread(fate_thackray) says "Hugh Thackray is struck from the Register of Gaunt and from the Ladder of Merit, where a mason has chiselled his name out of the gold, leaving a long pale scar at the top of the board that nobody will paint over. He walked to Carth in a pair of borrowed boots and knocked, and Annis Scaife let him in, and he is sitting at a cold hearth he paid for, keeping the last of his own forty nights himself." { Assert spread(fate_thackray). }
  Rule fate_thackray_changed when accounting() and thackrayChanged() and not spread(fate_thackray) says "Alderman Thackray is still top of the Ladder, and cannot be got off it, because the Wood Exchange has given away more this week than the Ladder can count. Oak is twenty shillings the cord and the Row has the dead-wood right again. He looks ten years older and sleeps at night." { Assert spread(fate_thackray). }
  Rule fate_thackray_known when accounting() and knows(party, thackray_vigil) and not spread(fate_thackray) says "Alderman Thackray has his name re-gilded at the top of the Ladder, and rides up the fell road some mornings on a grey cob to look at a chimney, and weeps, and rides back, and the price of oak is thirty-one shillings the cord." { Assert spread(fate_thackray). }
  Rule fate_thackray_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_thackray) says "The Ladder of Merit is gilded for the year with HUGH THACKRAY, WOOD-REEVE at the top of it, and the price of oak is thirty-one shillings the cord." { Assert spread(fate_thackray). }
  Entity fate_thackray: fact "Thackray".
  Rule fate_widow when accounting() and betrothed(joan) and not spread(fate_widow) says "The banns of Joan Pickersgill, widow, and Abel Lumb, proxy, will be read in the Minster on the first Sunday after the Fast. Abel has eaten every day this week and has stopped being able to see through his hands. Mistress Pickersgill has stopped paying anyone to fast for her thoughts, on the grounds that she means to act on them." { Assert spread(fate_widow). }
  Rule fate_widow_fed when accounting() and abelFed(abel) and not betrothed(joan) and not spread(fate_widow) says "Abel Lumb eats, and does not fast for anybody, and goes past Tanners' Row every day the long way round, and Mistress Pickersgill pays fourteen fasts a week for her thoughts to somebody else, and goes down on Mondays to watch, and comes home cross." { Assert spread(fate_widow). }
  Rule fate_widow_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_widow) says "Abel Lumb fasts for Mistress Pickersgill's thoughts, eleven a week, and she goes down on Mondays to watch him not eat; and neither of them has said anything to anyone." { Assert spread(fate_widow). }
  Entity fate_widow: fact "the widow".
  Rule fate_ladder_exposed when accounting() and ladderExposed(dinsdale) and not spread(fate_ladder) says "Mistress Dinsdale and Master Sowerby are both a rung down the Ladder this year, by order of the Lady Penitentiary, for buying penance in advance; their advances went to the Barefoot Hall, which bought a stove with them." { Assert spread(fate_ladder). }
  Rule fate_ladder_both when accounting() and sowerbyWalked(sowerby) and dinsdaleWalked(dinsdale) and not spread(fate_ladder) says "Nobody is gilded second on the Ladder of Merit this year. On Ash Day there was nobody at the Stand to hire, so Mistress Dinsdale and Master Sowerby walked their own miles barefoot, and were not clean by the canons in time for the gilding. Mistress Dinsdale minds very much. Master Sowerby does not seem to; he has given a widow her money back for a bolt of black cloth, seven years late, with interest." { Assert spread(fate_ladder). }
  Rule fate_ladder_dinsdale when accounting() and dinsdaleWalked(dinsdale) and not sowerbyWalked(sowerby) and not spread(fate_ladder) says "Mistress Dinsdale is not gilded second on the Ladder this year: on Ash Day the Row would not be hired, and she walked her own mile barefoot in her velvet bonnet, and was not clean by the canons in time for the gilding. She has had her feet bound in velvet, and is suing the Row." { Assert spread(fate_ladder). }
  Rule fate_ladder_walked when accounting() and sowerbyWalked(sowerby) and not spread(fate_ladder) says "Master Sowerby is not gilded second on the Ladder this year, because he did not hire a proxy for Ash Day and so was not clean by the canons in time for the gilding; and he does not seem to mind. He has given a widow her money back for a bolt of black cloth, seven years late, with interest." { Assert spread(fate_ladder). }
  Rule fate_ladder_scar when accounting() and thackrayBears(thackray) and not spread(fate_ladder) says "Under the scar at the top of the Ladder, DINSDALE is gilded first this year and SOWERBY second, or the other way about; the city has stopped being able to tell, and the scar is above them both." { Assert spread(fate_ladder). }
  Rule fate_ladder_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_ladder) says "Under the top of the Ladder, DINSDALE is gilded second and SOWERBY third, or the other way about; the city has stopped being able to tell." { Assert spread(fate_ladder). }
  Entity fate_ladder: fact "the Ladder".
  Rule fate_tower_set when accounting() and courseSet(joby) and not spread(fate_tower) says "The north tower of the Minster of Gaunt has a new course of white stone on it, the first in two hundred and eleven years that stayed, and Joby Thwaite goes up the scaffold every morning to look at it, and comes down, and sets another." { Assert spread(fate_tower). }
  Rule fate_tower_pellow when accounting() and pellowExposed(pellow) and not spread(fate_tower) says "Canon Laverock is no longer Master of the Fabric. He has been given a stall in the Minster to sing in, and sings, very sweetly, and the north tower is in the hands of a committee, which is the next best thing to frost." { Assert spread(fate_tower). }
  Rule fate_tower_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_tower) says "On the north tower Joby Thwaite's masons set a course of white stone today, and tonight the frost will get into it." { Assert spread(fate_tower). }
  Entity fate_tower: fact "the tower".
  Rule fate_row_struck when accounting() and struck(barefoot) and not spread(fate_row) says "The Stand reopened on the Thursday, at the old rates. Nobody in the Row has stopped talking about Ash Day, and nobody in the Middle Town has started." { Assert spread(fate_row). }
  Rule fate_row_wood when accounting() and woodOpened(thackray) and not spread(fate_row) says "The dead-wood right is open in the Bishop's Wood, and every child in the Row is out there with a sledge, and the Barefoot Hall's stove is lit, and on the wall the forty-one pegs have the forty-one names on them, painted, in white." { Assert spread(fate_row). }
  Rule fate_row_sledge when accounting() and rowWarmed(barefoot) and not spread(fate_row) says "The Barefoot Hall's stove is lit, on stolen wood, by right; and the woodmen have been told to watch the Bishop's Wood harder; and the Row is warm for a week." { Assert spread(fate_row). }
  Rule fate_row_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_row) says "In the Row the Barefoot sit in their doorways with their feet in bowls, and the stove in the Hall is not lit." { Assert spread(fate_row). }
  Entity fate_row: fact "the Row".
  Rule fate_hal_taken when accounting() and halTaken(hal) and not spread(fate_hal) says "Hal Metcalfe is in the Consistory gaol, in the warm room, for Fastens' Eve and a ladder, and will be heard after the Fast. Prudence Garth's mother has paid her pains and can buy in the Shambles, and Prudence has not been seen on the Steps since." { Assert spread(fate_hal). }
  Rule fate_hal_out when accounting() and escapedWindow(hern) and not spread(fate_hal) says "Hal Metcalfe came back through the Fell Gate on Ash Day morning without his ladder and has not said where he left it." { Assert spread(fate_hal). }
  Rule fate_pru when accounting() and prudenceTurned(prudence) and not spread(fate_hal) says "Prudence Garth is on the Minster steps on Sundays, listening to whoever is preaching there; her mother is on the Register as a defaulter for a hen, or is not, and either way buys her bread in the Row." { Assert spread(fate_hal). }
  Rule fate_hal_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_hal) says "Hal Metcalfe never came to Gaol Lane with his ladder; and Prudence Garth never had to tell." { Assert spread(fate_hal). }
  Entity fate_hal: fact "Hal".
  Rule fate_tib when accounting() and tibBears(party) and not spread(fate_tib) says "Tib Ackroyd is keeping the seventeen nights of cold hearth you broke at Carth, at a shilling a night, in a room in the Row with the window open; he is on the fourth." { Assert spread(fate_tib). }
  Rule fate_owing when accounting() and pains(party) > 0 and not putOut(party) and not spread(fate_tib) says "Your tally is still notched. In the Register of Gaunt you owe what you owe, and it will be there when you come back, doubled." { Assert spread(fate_tib). }
  Rule fate_struck_warm when accounting() and putOut(party) and vigilReleased(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_tib) says "Your name is struck from the Register of Gaunt. You walked south across the Levels in the dark with a barefoot old man in a new grey coat, and at first light you came up the fell to Carth, where there was smoke going up from the chimney at last; and Annis Scaife opened the door to the pair of you and looked at you both, up and down, and said, 'Well, you'd better come in, the both of you, and shut that door, it's cold.'" { Assert spread(fate_tib). }
  Rule fate_struck when accounting() and putOut(party) and not spread(fate_tib) says "Your name is struck from the Register of Gaunt. You walked south across the Levels in the dark with a barefoot old man in a new grey coat, and at first light you came up the fell to Carth, where no smoke goes up, and knocked; and Annis Scaife opened the door, and looked at the pair of you, and stood aside. There are fourteen nights of the vigil left. You are keeping them, with the Scaifes, in the dark, the whole house in one bed, and Hern telling the child stories about Gaunt that are mostly true." { Assert spread(fate_tib). }
  Rule fate_shriven when accounting() and shriven() and not putOut(party) and not spread(fate_tib) says "Your tally is clean. Gaunt has nothing against you, which in Gaunt is the most anybody ever has." { Assert spread(fate_tib). }
  Entity fate_tib: fact "the shrift".
  Rule fate_fold_joby when accounting() and jobyToFold(joby) and not spread(fate_fold) says "On Ash Day, when the course had stood a night and a day, Joby Thwaite walked out of Gaunt across the Levels with a mason's lantern, to a sheepfold with a thread of smoke going up from it, and sat down by the fire there beside his son; and neither of them said much, and neither of them needed to." { Assert spread(fate_fold). }
  Rule fate_fold_known when accounting() and cuthbertKnows(cuthbert) and not spread(fate_fold) says "In the put-outs' fold on the Levels, Cuthbert Thwaite watches the lantern on the north tower every night, and knows now that he was not wrong, which after nineteen years is not nothing, and is not much." { Assert spread(fate_fold). }
  Rule fate_hern_fold when accounting() and verdictPutOut(consistory) and not putOutDead(hern) and hernHeardFold(hern) and not wentWithHern(party) and not spread(fate_hern) says "At the put-outs' fold on the Levels they made room by the fire for an old man in a grey coat, who arrived after dark with his feet bleeding and his cough worse, and has been telling them every evening since, at length, that not one of them is sorry for anything. They agree with him, and give him the warm side." { Assert spread(fate_hern). }
  Entity fate_fold: fact "the fold". Entity fate_hern: fact "Hern after".
  Rule fate_fly when accounting() and following(fly, party) and not spread(fate_fly) says "Fly the collie is at your heels, and will not be sent back." { Assert spread(fate_fly). }
  Entity fate_fly: fact "Fly".
  // The account is told, and a watch later the book closes on the ending, so that the morning after comes first.
  Relation accountClosed(group). Measure accountAt(group).
  Rule account_closes when accounting() and not accountClosed(party) { Assert accountClosed(party). Set accountAt(party) to watch(clock). }
  Query bookClosed() means accountClosed(party) and watch(clock) > accountAt(party).

  // ── The endings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Ending the_fast "The Fast" when bookClosed() and verdictFast(consistory) "The Consistory of Gaunt never sat on the matter of Ninian Hern. On Ash Day the burgesses of the city walked their own penances barefoot through the snow in front of the Row, and the Lady Penitentiary adjourned until the Commerce of Merit should resume, which it did, on the Thursday, at the old rates. Hern was let out of the gaol on Lady Day with no charge against him that anybody could remember. He went back to his room in the Row and sat on the step of the Barefoot Hall with his feet in a bowl. The next morning was cold and clear, and the Stand was full.".
  Ending the_flight "The Flight" when bookClosed() and verdictFlight(consistory) "Ninian Hern was put out of Gaunt in his absence, from a city he had already left. Nobody knows where he went. In the spring a drover coming in by the Fell Gate said there was an old man barefoot on the drovers' road west of Carth Fell, preaching to cattle; but drovers will say anything. The next morning the Stand was full, and the Ladder was gilded, and on the Minster steps, where Hern used to stand, nobody stood.".
  Ending the_recantation "The Recantation" when bookClosed() and verdictRecant(consistory) "Ninian Hern recanted in the Chapter House on Ash Day, and went home to the Row that evening, and slept in his own room with somebody's coat over his feet. The Commerce of Merit stands; the Row eats; the Ladder is gilded. On the morning after, very early, someone saw the Lady Penitentiary in the Row without a mask, at the Barefoot copper, tasting the soup, and adding water.".
  Ending the_bearer "The Bearer" when bookClosed() and verdictBearer(consistory) "On Ash Day the Consistory of Gaunt accepted, for the first time in two hundred and eleven years, that a man's sentence could be borne by another, and put out an innocent person for a guilty one in front of the whole city, and wrote it down. The Commerce of Merit has not fallen; it has only been seen. The next morning, at the Stand, the clerk could not find anyone who would be hired for anything, all morning; by afternoon it was business as usual, and by evening it was not quite.".
  Ending put_out_dead "Put Out" when bookClosed() and putOutDead(hern) "Ninian Hern was put out of Gaunt at dusk on Ash Day in a deal coffin, through the Gate of Ash, and left on the Levels in the snow, struck from the Register. In the night someone came out from the Row with a sledge and took him away, and nobody in Gaunt will say where he is buried, though the children on the ditch know, and sing about it, and get it wrong.".
  Ending put_out "Put Out" when bookClosed() and verdictPutOut(consistory) and not putOutDead(hern) "Ninian Hern was put out of Gaunt at dusk on Ash Day, through the Gate of Ash, into the Levels, in what he stood in, struck from the Register; and the gate was shut and chained and sealed, and the city went in to its supper, which was fish. The next morning the snow had covered whatever footprints there were.".
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/eve.kyr:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── Dame Hawise Strake, the Lady Penitentiary ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Born in the Row, a proxy at twelve beside Hern; rose by being better at it than anyone. Warm, worldly, funny,
  // partial, a politician; she bends small rules for the Row every day and is proud of it. She believes, with reason,
  // that the Commerce feeds the Row in winter: "I have turned vanity into bread." Her exactness is about one thing: the
  // sentence. She will put out the man she loved, fairly. By day at her desk she is the Penitentiary; on Fastens' Eve,
  // masked, she ladles soup at the Barefoot copper in the Row, as she has for thirty years, and is no one.
  Person hawise "Dame Hawise Strake" at penitentiary {
    Role "the Lady Penitentiary, a broad handsome woman of sixty in grey, with a pen behind her ear and the Row still in her voice" when not masked(hawise).
    Role "a masked woman in a grey shawl ladling soup at the Barefoot copper, with a voice from the Row" when masked(hawise).
    Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "The woman at the desk by the fire takes the pen from behind her ear, and points it at the chair. 'Sit. You're the stranger who brought Ninian in, or the one who didn't. Either way you've walked with him, so you'll have opinions. Everybody who walks with Ninian comes away with opinions.' She smiles: a Row smile, all at once and gone, that has not been taught any manners by forty books. 'Mine are on the wall.' The forty books of the Register stand behind her on their lecterns.".
    Greets again "Dame Hawise has a slip of paper in her teeth and the Register open at a page she does not seem to like. She takes the slip out. 'Good,' she says, 'you are back. I have the proofs of Ninian's pardon, and the proofs of his sentence, both fair-copied, and I am not at all sure which of them I shall have to read out.'".
  }
  Relation masked(group). Measure hawiseReasons(group). Query hawiseMoved() means hawiseReasons(hawise) >= 2.
  Relation hawiseHeardCarth(group). Relation hawiseHeardHern(group). Relation hawiseHeardVerse(group).
  Relation carryingHern(group). Relation carryingHawise(group). Relation hernHeardHawise(group).
  Relation ringGiven(group). Relation metMasked(group).
  // Her days: the Penitentiary from eight to five; Fastens' Eve, masked, at the Barefoot copper from nine to eleven;
  // Ash Day, the Chapter House.
  Rule hawise_desk when daytime() and not masked(hawise) and not at(hawise, penitentiary) and not sitting() and not afterTrial(hawise) { Assert at(hawise, penitentiary). }
  Rule hawise_home when not daytime() and at(hawise, penitentiary) and not masked(hawise) { Assert at(hawise, limbo). }
  Rule hawise_masks when eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 21 and hour(clock) < 23 and not masked(hawise) and not spread(hawise_masked_done) { Assert masked(hawise). Assert at(hawise, limbo). }
  Rule hawise_unmasks when masked(hawise) and (hour(clock) >= 23 or not eveDay()) { Retract masked(hawise). Assert at(hawise, limbo). Assert spread(hawise_masked_done). }
  Entity hawise_masked_done: fact "the Lady at the copper".
  Relation afterTrial(group).
  // Under the mask she is nobody: written as a person of her own, there only while the mask is on, so that nobody in
  // the Row (and nothing on the page) calls her by her name.
  Person masked "the masked woman at the copper" at limbo {
    Role "a broad woman in a grey shawl and a black half-mask, ladling soup, with a voice from the Row". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
    Greets "The masked woman holds out a bowl to you without looking, then looks. 'You're not Row,' she says. 'Have some anyway. It's Fastens' Eve.'".
    Seen when masked(hawise).
  }
  Rule mask_on when masked(hawise) and not at(masked, row_lane) { Assert at(masked, row_lane). }
  Rule mask_off when not masked(hawise) and at(masked, row_lane) { Assert at(masked, limbo). }
  Observe copper_masked at row_lane when masked(hawise) "At the Barefoot copper by the Hall door a masked woman in a grey shawl is ladling soup into the bowls held out to her, a ladle a bowl, never spilling, talking to everyone in the queue by name, and the queue talking back. Some of them call her Duchess. Nobody calls her anything else.".

  // ── At her desk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic hawise_commerce with hawise "Ask the Lady Penitentiary whether the Commerce of Merit does anyone any good" when not masked(hawise) once {
    Says "'Good!' She laughs. 'It feeds the Row through the winter. Do you know what the Row was before the Commerce? I do. I was in it. A burgess has a sin on his conscience; before, he'd buy a candle and forget it. Now he buys a fast, and a woman in the Row eats for a week.' She taps the nearest book. 'Vanity, into bread. I've done that every day for thirty years. Ninian says nobody's sorry. He's right. Nobody's fed by sorrow either.' She puts the pen back behind her ear. 'He was always better at being right than at being useful. I was always the other.'".
  }
  Topic hawise_hern with hawise "Ask the Lady Penitentiary what will happen to Ninian Hern" when not masked(hawise) once {
    Says "Her face does not change at all, which is how you know. 'He'll be heard,' she says. 'Ash Day, noon, the Chapter House. Canon Laverock will prosecute, gently; the Faculty will determine, expensively; and I will ask him whether he recants. If he does, he goes home to the Row and does three years' penance by proxy, which the Barefoot will do for him for nothing, and that's the end of it.' She dips her pen. 'If he doesn't, I will put him out at the Gate of Ash at dusk, in what he stands in.' She writes a line. 'He never had a coat worth the name. I've had one made. It's in that cupboard. Don't tell him.'".
  }
  Topic hawise_law with hawise "Ask the Lady Penitentiary whether a sentence of putting-out may be borne by another" when not masked(hawise) once {
    Says "She puts down her pen. 'Who's been reading the canons to you?' She looks at you, hard, for the first time. 'Yes. It's a penance; the greatest. Any penance may be borne. It's never been tried. A Lady Penitentiary who had it offered in the Chapter House would have to decide whether the law means what it says.' She picks up the pen again. 'I'd sooner not be that Lady Penitentiary,' she says, lightly. 'But I would decide.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sentence_borne). }
  }
  Topic hawise_pellow with hawise "Tell the Lady Penitentiary what Canon Laverock's men do on the north tower at night" when knows(actor, unbuilding) and not pellowExposed(pellow) and not pellowBargain(pellow) once {
    Says "Dame Hawise listens without a word, writing nothing. When you have done she sits back. 'The frost,' she says. 'Fifty-three years of frost.' Then she laughs, quite helplessly, with her hand over her eyes. 'Oh, Hamo. Oh, the Fabric.' She stops laughing. 'He'll not prosecute anybody on Ash Day for saying the Commerce is a fraud. Not in my Chapter House. I'll have the precentor do it, who believes in nothing and reads beautifully.' She is still for a moment. Then she gets up and goes along the lecterns to the last of the forty books, and turns it back nineteen years, and puts her finger on a line, and keeps it there. 'Cuthbert Thwaite,' she says, to the book. 'Slander.' She closes it gently, as if it might wake. 'Thank you,' she says, and does not turn round.".
    On discuss { Assert pellowExposed(pellow). Increase hawiseReasons(hawise) by 1. }
  }
  Topic hawise_last with hawise "Ask the Lady Penitentiary who was last put out at the Gate of Ash" when not masked(hawise) once {
    Says "She does not need to look it up. 'Cuthbert Thwaite, journeyman mason, nineteen years ago this Ash Day. Slander of the Fabric.' She dips her pen. 'My first sitting in the stone chair. Hamo Laverock prosecuted, gently. The boy said he'd seen men take the tower down by night. I asked him did he recant, and he said he'd seen what he'd seen.' She writes a line, and blots it. 'So I put him out. Fairly. I've not put anyone out since.' She does not look up. 'Ninian will be the second.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, last_put_out). }
  }
  Topic hawise_ladder with hawise "Tell the Lady Penitentiary that Mistress Dinsdale and Master Sowerby are buying penance in advance to race each other up the Ladder" when knows(actor, dinsdale_hiring) and not ladderExposed(dinsdale) and not masked(hawise) once {
    Says "'In advance.' Dame Hawise closes her eyes. 'For faults they haven't done.' She opens them. 'That's not penance, that's a subscription.' She writes. 'Both of them down a rung on Ash Day, and the advances forfeit to the Barefoot Hall.' She looks up. 'Don't look so pleased. They'll be back up next year. People always are. That's what the Ladder's for.'".
    On discuss { Assert ladderExposed(dinsdale). }
  }

  // ── Under the mask ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic masked_who with masked "Ask the masked woman at the copper who she is" when masked(hawise) and not metMasked(actor) once {
    Says "'Nobody,' says the masked woman. 'It's Fastens' Eve. Nobody's anybody.' She ladles. 'I came out of this Row at twelve. Fasted for a fishmonger's wife with a boy who ate her cat's dinner on the fourth day and made me eat half. Every Fastens' Eve since I've come down and ladled, because on Fastens' Eve you can.' She looks at you through the eyeholes. 'You've walked with Ninian Hern,' she says. 'It's all over you. Opinions.' The ladle stops. 'Go on, then. It's Fastens' Eve. Say what you like to nobody.'".
    On discuss { Assert metMasked(actor). }
  }
  Topic masked_carth with masked "Tell the masked woman about the night at Carth" when masked(hawise) and metMasked(actor) and stayingAtCarth(actor) and not hawiseHeardCarth(hawise) once {
    Says "You tell her: the dark, the hearth, the hand in the ash; the child's cough, the old man in the byre, the old woman lying down with him. She goes on ladling the whole time, a ladle a bowl, never spilling. When you get to the old woman, she misses a bowl. The man holding it says nothing; he waits. She fills it. 'Forty nights,' she says. 'I set it. It's the penance for blood. I set it on a farm.' The next bowl. 'I've never seen a vigil kept. In thirty years. I've the Register. I've Raistrick's sticks.' She ladles. 'Go on,' she says. 'The old woman. Go on.'".
    On discuss { Assert hawiseHeardCarth(hawise). Increase hawiseReasons(hawise) by 1. }
  }
  Topic masked_hern_word with masked "Give the masked woman Hern's word: the soup was always too salt" when masked(hawise) and metMasked(actor) and carryingHern(actor) and not hawiseHeardHern(hawise) once {
    Says "The ladle stops. The masked woman stands quite still with it held over the copper, dripping, and the queue waits, and nobody says anything, because it is the Row. Then she puts the ladle down and lifts her mask a little, just to wipe her eyes, and puts it back. 'We made it,' she says. 'When we were fifteen. The Hall's first soup. I salted it, and he said it was too salt, and I said he could fast, then. Forty-five years.' She picks up the ladle. 'It's still too salt,' she says. 'I've never changed it. Tell him—' She stops. 'No. I'll tell him.'".
    On discuss { Assert hawiseHeardHern(hawise). Increase hawiseReasons(hawise) by 1. }
  }
  Topic masked_verse with masked "Sing the masked woman the end of the children's sliding rhyme" when masked(hawise) and metMasked(actor) and knows(actor, second_verse) and not hawiseHeardVerse(hawise) once {
    Says "You sing it, badly, the end the Row's children sing on the ditch: at the top he set him down: NOW WALK, said Oswy, into town. The masked woman laughs out loud. 'We sang that,' she says. 'Ninian and me, on the ditch, when it froze. I'd forgotten there was an end to it. It's not on the plinth.' She ladles. 'Now walk.' She stops. 'He carried him up, and set him down, and said, now walk. Not, I've done it for you. Now walk.' She looks up at the Close wall, over the Row, where the Penitentiary's forty windows are dark. 'I've been carrying the whole city for thirty years,' she says, 'and never once set it down.'".
    On discuss { Assert hawiseHeardVerse(hawise). Increase hawiseReasons(hawise) by 1. }
  }
  Topic masked_save with masked "Ask the masked woman what would save Ninian Hern" when masked(hawise) and metMasked(actor) and hawiseReasons(hawise) >= 1 and not carryingHawise(actor) once {
    Says "'Nothing,' she says at once. 'He won't let it.' She ladles. Then, quietly: 'He could say he was sorry once. Not that he's wrong. Not that the Commerce is good. Just that once, in thirty years, for one of them, he was sorry: really sorry, his own sorrow, not bought. It would be true. I know it's true. I was there.' She fills a bowl. 'That's a recantation. In the canons, that's enough; the heresy is that nobody's sorry. One man sorry, once, and the proposition's false, and I can let him go home.' She does not look at you. 'He won't say it. He'll think it's giving in. Tell him it's giving me the words.'".
    On discuss { Assert carryingHawise(actor). }
  }
  Kind gaunt_ring "Dame Hawise's ring, a plain silver ring with the Penitentiary's billet of keys on it" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0.
  Item ring "Dame Hawise's ring" is gaunt_ring at limbo.
  Topic masked_ring with masked "Ask the masked woman for remission of your pains" when masked(hawise) and metMasked(actor) and hawiseMoved() and not ringGiven(hawise) once {
    Says "She laughs, and holds the ladle out to the next bowl, and while she fills it she works a ring off her finger with her thumb and drops it on the step beside the copper. 'Remission,' she says. 'Show that at the Close Gate. It's no good anywhere else in the world, but in Gaunt it's the Lady Penitentiary's ring, and you owe nothing.' She does not look at you. 'Nobody gave it to you. It's Fastens' Eve.'".
    On discuss { Assert ringGiven(hawise). Assert at(ring, row_lane). }
  }
  Rule ring_taken when carries(party, ring) and not spread(ring_taken) says "You pick the ring up off the step by the copper. It is still warm from her hand." { Assert spread(ring_taken). }
  Entity ring_taken: fact "the ring taken up".
  Action show_ring(actor: group, site: place) "Show the porter of the Close Gate the Lady Penitentiary's ring" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, close_gate_street) and carries(actor, ring) and not shriven() and tallied(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Set pains(actor) to 0. Retract forgedTally(actor). }
    Result "The porter looks at the ring through the grille for a long moment. Then he takes your tally, and with his knife he shaves every notch off it, slowly, one by one, until it is a smooth white stick, and gives it back. 'Remitted,' he says. He does not ask how.".
  }
  // Moved, she does the one thing in her gift that is not the sentence: she sends her own physician to the gaol.
  Rule hawise_sends_physician when hawiseMoved() and hernFailing(hern) and hernGaoled(hern) and not hernTended(hern) and not hernDead(hern) { Assert hernTended(hern). }
  Relation hernTended(group).
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/fold.kyr:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── The put-outs' fold ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Where the Gate of Ash leads. Nineteen years ago the gate was opened for Cuthbert Thwaite, journeyman mason, Joby's
  // son, who said the Fabric's men took the north tower down by night. Canon Laverock prosecuted; Dame Hawise, in her
  // first year in the stone chair, put him out; Hern was hired by the Fabric to fast three days in thanksgiving for a
  // slander stopped. Cuthbert did not walk away. He lives in a ruined sheepfold on the Levels with the others the gate
  // was opened for, owing nobody, within sight of the tower, and watches the lantern go up it every night. He is the
  // answer to the question Hern cannot answer: what comes after.
  Person cuthbert "Cuthbert Thwaite" at fold {
    Role "a put-out mason of fifty, with his father's shoulders and a turf-spade, who looks at the city before he looks at you". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "'Lost?' says the man with the turf-spade. 'Nobody comes out here that isn't lost or put out, and you've boots on.' He looks past you at Gaunt, the way everyone here does. 'Sit by the fire. It's peat we cut ourselves, so nobody owes anybody for it.'".
    Greets again "Cuthbert Thwaite nods, and his eyes go back to the walls of Gaunt, as to a window in a house he was put out of. 'I counted the bells at noon,' he says. 'You can count them from here. I got to forty before I lost it. There are not forty bells. I do not know what I was counting.'".
  }
  Relation cuthbertKnows(group). Relation cuthbertTold(group). Relation jobyToFold(group). Relation hernHeardFold(group).
  Discovery last_put_out "Nineteen years ago a young mason, Thwaite, was put out of Gaunt at the Gate of Ash for saying that the Fabric's men took the north tower down at night. Nobody has seen him since; nobody has looked.".
  Discovery cuthbert_story "Cuthbert Thwaite, Joby Thwaite's son, was put out of Gaunt nineteen years ago for saying the Fabric's men took the north tower down by night. Canon Laverock prosecuted; Dame Hawise, in her first year as Lady Penitentiary, put him out. He lives in the put-outs' fold on the Levels.".
  Discovery fold_after "There is an after to being put out of Gaunt: a turf-roofed fold on the Levels where the put-out live, owing nothing, keeping nobody's penance but their own.".
  Topic cuthbert_who with cuthbert "Ask the man with the turf-spade why he was put out" when true once {
    Says "'Cuthbert Thwaite. Mason. Nineteen years this Ash Day.' He leans on the spade. 'I was a journeyman on the north tower. One night I'd left my level up top and went back for it, and there were men on the scaffold by lantern taking down what we'd set that day, block by block, and a canon below with his hands in his sleeves.' He shrugs. 'I said so. In the Fat Lamb, drunk, which was a mistake; and then sober, at the Penitentiary, which was a worse one. Slander of the Fabric. Canon Laverock prosecuted, very gently.' He spits into the fire. 'The new Lady Penitentiary asked me did I recant. I said I'd seen what I'd seen. She was very fair about it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, cuthbert_story). Assert knows(actor, last_put_out). }
  }
  Topic cuthbert_after with cuthbert "Ask Cuthbert Thwaite what comes after the Gate of Ash" when knows(actor, cuthbert_story) once {
    Says "'This,' he says, and means all of it: the fold, the turf roof, the fire, the seven of them. 'Nobody in the Register. Nobody owes anybody anything, and nobody's paid to be sorry for us. We cut turves. We herd for the drovers when they come through at Lammas. We bury our own, in the soft ground by the dyke where the frost doesn't reach.' He looks at the city. 'It's a hard life. It's mine. It's the first thing in my life that was.' A pause. 'They never put that in the stories, do they. The after.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, fold_after). }
  }
  Topic cuthbert_father with cuthbert "Ask Cuthbert Thwaite about his father" when knows(actor, cuthbert_story) once {
    Says "'Joby.' He turns a turf over with the spade, and another. 'He came to the Gate of Ash when they put me out. Stood in the lane with his cap in his hands, and never looked at me. He'd set that course himself that day, and as far as he was concerned I'd called him a liar about his own frost.' He straightens. 'He's set it every day since. I can see the scaffold from here. Every night I watch the lantern go up it.'".
  }
  Topic cuthbert_tower with cuthbert "Tell Cuthbert Thwaite you have seen the Fabric's men take the tower down" when knows(actor, unbuilding) and knows(actor, cuthbert_story) and not cuthbertKnows(cuthbert) once {
    Says "He puts the spade down, carefully, as if it might break. 'Still,' he says. 'Nineteen years.' He sits down on the wall of the fold. For a while he does not say anything at all. Then he laughs, once. 'I was drunk,' he says. 'But I wasn't wrong.'".
    On discuss { Assert cuthbertKnows(cuthbert). }
  }
  Topic cuthbert_joby with cuthbert "Tell Cuthbert Thwaite that his father knows the truth now" when jobyKnows(joby) and knows(actor, cuthbert_story) and not cuthbertTold(cuthbert) once {
    Says "Cuthbert Thwaite does not say anything. He goes to the gap in the wall of the fold and stands in it with his back to the fold, looking at the city. When he comes back he has been crying and is not ashamed of it. 'Don't tell him where I am,' he says. 'If he wants to know, the lantern's on the tower every night, and I'm at the other end of it.'".
    On discuss { Assert cuthbertTold(cuthbert). Assert cuthbertKnows(cuthbert). }
  }
  // Hern brought to the fold himself, on the way in to his trial: the after, seen.
  Rule hern_at_fold at fold when following(hern, party) and at(party, fold) and at(cuthbert, fold) and not hernHeardFold(hern)
    says "Hern stops in the gap of the fold wall and does not come in. The man with the turf-spade looks up and sees him, and goes on looking. 'Barefoot Hern,' says Cuthbert Thwaite at last. 'You fasted for my going.' 'I did,' says Hern. 'Three days. A shilling a day. The Fabric paid.' 'Was it a good fast?' 'It was the best I ever kept,' says Hern, 'and I never meant a minute of it.' Cuthbert considers this, and nods, as if it were a fair answer to a fair question, and moves up on the turf bench by the fire. 'There's room,' he says, 'if they put you out.' Hern does not sit down. But he stands in the gap a long time, looking at the seven faces and the fire, the way a man looks at a road he had not known was there." teaches fold_after {
    Assert hernHeardFold(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. }
  // Told to Hern, in his cell or at the bars, the after is a reason to live: there is somewhere to walk to.
  Topic hern_fold_cell with hern "Tell Hern what Cuthbert Thwaite says comes after the Gate of Ash" when hernGaoled(hern) and knows(actor, fold_after) and not hernHeardFold(hern) once {
    Says "Hern listens with his feet to the fire. 'Young Thwaite,' he says, and you can see him remember a shilling a day. He looks at the fire. 'And he's been out there all this time. Cutting turves. Owing nobody.' He laughs, and it turns into the cough, and the cough goes on. 'An after,' he says, when he can. 'Well. I'd not thought there was anywhere to walk to.'".
    On discuss { Assert hernHeardFold(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. }
  }
  Topic hern_fold_window with hern_window "Tell Hern what Cuthbert Thwaite says comes after the Gate of Ash" when knows(actor, fold_after) and not hernHeardFold(hern) once {
    Says "The face at the bars is quiet a long time. 'Young Thwaite,' says Hern. 'Out there all this while, owing nobody.' The hands on the bars tighten and loosen. 'An after. I'd not thought there was anywhere to walk to.'".
    On discuss { Assert hernHeardFold(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. }
  }
  Milestone m_fold "found where the Gate of Ash leads" worth 100 when knows(party, fold_after).
  Milestone m_cuthbert "carried word between a mason and his son" worth 150 when cuthbertTold(cuthbert) and jobyToFold(joby).
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/gaol.kyr:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── Hern in the gaol ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A warm cell in the Close, visited by day from the Close side (for a company that may enter the Close), and talked
  // to at any hour through the barred window from Gaol Lane, below. A person is talked to where they are; the voice at
  // the window is written as its own person, seen from the lane only while Hern is in the cell.
  Person hern_window "Ninian Hern" at gaol_lane {
    Role "a voice and two hands and a bit of a face at the barred window over Gaol Lane, the hands holding the bars". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "'Is that my custodian?' says the face at the bars. 'Or a stranger? Either is welcome; I've had the precentor in all day, explaining my heresy to me. He's very good at it. I'm thinking of taking it up.' A cough. 'Stand where I can see you. I'm on the bed on tiptoe.'".
    Greets again "Hern's hands come round the bars, and then his forehead, and then his grin. 'Visitors twice,' he says. 'They'll say I have friends. It will go against me at the Consistory. Tell me what the weather's doing; the precentor won't, he says weather is a distraction from sin.'".
    Seen when hernAtBars().
  }
  Query hernAtBars() means hernGaoled(hern) and at(hern, gaol_cell) and not hernFled(hern) and not hernDead(hern).
  Relation toldToLive(group). Relation hernRecants(group). Relation hernWillLive(group).
  Rule will_live when hernReasons(hern) >= 2 and not hernWillLive(hern) and not hernDead(hern) { Assert hernWillLive(hern). }
  // Each reason to live is counted once: the child saved by someone else's warmth than his; Bess heard; Hawise's words;
  // being told to, by someone who said on the road that one man can be sorry for another, or that what we owe is to
  // finish, or who kept a promise anyway.
  Rule reason_dowsie when nightOver(party) and dowsieSafe(dowsie) and not hernCoat(hern) and at(hern, house_place) and not spread(reason_dowsie) { Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. Assert spread(reason_dowsie). }
  Entity reason_dowsie: fact "the child saved".
  Topic gaol_word with hern "Ask Hern if there is anything he would say to the Lady Penitentiary" when hernGaoled(hern) and not carryingHern(actor) once {
    Says "Hern thinks, with his feet to the fire, and scratches one. 'Tell her,' he says, 'the soup was always too salt.' He grins at the fire. 'She'll know. Nobody else in Gaunt would.' Then, not grinning: 'Don't tell her anything else. Not that I'm ill. She'd send a physician and I'd have to be polite to him.'".
    On discuss { Assert carryingHern(actor). }
  }
  Topic window_word with hern_window "Ask Hern if there is anything he would say to the Lady Penitentiary" when not carryingHern(actor) once {
    Says "The hands on the bars tighten and loosen. 'Tell her,' says Hern's voice, 'the soup was always too salt.' A laugh, and a cough. 'She'll know. Nobody else in Gaunt would. Don't tell her I'm coughing.'".
    On discuss { Assert carryingHern(actor). }
  }
  Topic gaol_bess with hern "Give Hern Bess Ackroyd's word: you don't kneel on your knees" when hernGaoled(hern) and carryingBess(actor) and not hernHeardBess(hern) once {
    Says "You tell him all of it: you can be right in heaven; down here we eat; recant, Ninian; next winter come and sit by the stove and tell us it's worth nothing, and we'll feed you while you say it. Hern listens with his eyes shut. At the end he laughs, a small dry laugh. 'You don't kneel on your knees,' he says. 'You kneel on your mind. I told her that when she was nine.' He opens his eyes. 'She's right. She's always right too. That's the trouble with Bess.'".
    On discuss { Assert hernHeardBess(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. }
  }
  Topic window_bess with hern_window "Give Hern Bess Ackroyd's word: you don't kneel on your knees" when carryingBess(actor) and not hernHeardBess(hern) once {
    Says "You tell it up to the bars: you can be right in heaven; down here we eat; recant, Ninian. For a long while there is nothing at the window but his hands. Then his voice: 'You kneel on your mind. I taught her that.' A cough. 'She's right too. That's the trouble with Bess. Everybody's right but the Penitentiary, and the Penitentiary's useful.'".
    On discuss { Assert hernHeardBess(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. }
  }
  Topic gaol_hawise with hern "Give Hern the Lady Penitentiary's words: that he was sorry once, really, for one of them" when hernGaoled(hern) and carryingHawise(actor) and not hernHeardHawise(hern) once {
    Says "Hern sits up on the bed. 'She said that.' He looks at the fire. 'Once,' he says. 'Aye. A fishmonger's wife. Her husband beat her, and she put rat-bane in his ale, and he lived, and she came to the Penitentiary shaking, and they set it at a week's fast, and I fasted it. Fifteen, I was.' He rubs his face. 'I was sorry. All week. For her. It was the only time.' He laughs, and it hurts him. 'Hawise was in the next pen eating the cat's dinner. She'd remember that.' He looks at you. 'It's not giving in, then?' he says. 'If it's true?'".
    On discuss { Assert hernHeardHawise(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. }
  }
  Topic window_hawise with hern_window "Give Hern the Lady Penitentiary's words: that he was sorry once, really, for one of them" when carryingHawise(actor) and not hernHeardHawise(hern) once {
    Says "The hands go still on the bars. 'She said that,' says Hern's voice. Then, a long while after: 'Once. Aye. A fishmonger's wife, and a week's fast, when I was fifteen. I was sorry all week. For her.' A cough. 'She was in the next pen. She'd remember.' Then, very quietly: 'If it's true, it's not giving in. Is it.'".
    On discuss { Assert hernHeardHawise(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. }
  }
  Topic gaol_live_love with hern "Tell Hern you would rather he lived, because one man can be sorry for another, and you are" when hernGaoled(hern) and saidLove(actor) and not toldToLive(hern) once {
    Says "Hern looks at you over his knees. 'You said on the road that one man being sorry for another is what love is,' he says. 'I've had that in my head ever since, and I can't get it out, and I've tried.' 'Well,' he says, when he has done, 'you're a dangerous person to walk forty miles with.' He scratches his foot. 'I'd thought I'd go out of the Gate of Ash like a man in a story. I'd thought that was the end of it.' He coughs. 'I've not thought about after. There's never been an after, for a proxy. You finish, you're paid, you go and stand in the next pen.'".
    On discuss { Assert toldToLive(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. }
  }
  Topic gaol_live_finish with hern "Tell Hern you would rather he lived, and finish what he was doing, as the dead would" when hernGaoled(hern) and saidFinish(actor) and not saidLove(actor) and not toldToLive(hern) once {
    Says "Hern looks at you over his knees. 'You said on the road we owe the dead the finishing of what they were doing,' he says. 'Kell was kneeling. I'm walking. You'd have me finish walking, would you, and not stop at a gate.' 'Well,' he says, when he has done, 'you're a dangerous person to walk forty miles with.' He scratches his foot. 'I'd thought I'd go out of the Gate of Ash like a man in a story. I'd thought that was the end of it.' He coughs. 'I've not thought about after. There's never been an after, for a proxy. You finish, you're paid, you go and stand in the next pen.'".
    On discuss { Assert toldToLive(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. }
  }
  Topic gaol_live_chosen with hern "Tell Hern you would rather he lived, since neither of you is who you were on the road" when hernGaoled(hern) and saidChosen(actor) and not saidLove(actor) and not saidFinish(actor) and not toldToLive(hern) once {
    Says "Hern looks at you over his knees. 'Not who I was that morning, you said, at the Fork,' he says. 'And keep it anyway. I've been turning that over on this bed like a stone in my pocket.' 'Well,' he says, when he has done, 'you're a dangerous person to walk forty miles with.' He scratches his foot. 'I'd thought I'd go out of the Gate of Ash like a man in a story. I'd thought that was the end of it.' He coughs. 'I've not thought about after. There's never been an after, for a proxy. You finish, you're paid, you go and stand in the next pen.'".
    On discuss { Assert toldToLive(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. }
  }
  Topic window_live_love with hern_window "Tell Hern you would rather he lived, because one man can be sorry for another, and you are" when saidLove(actor) and not toldToLive(hern) once {
    Says "'You said on the road that one man being sorry for another is what love is,' says the voice at the bars. 'I've had that in my head ever since, and I can't get it out, and I've tried.' Then: 'You're a dangerous person to walk with.' A long cough. 'I'd thought the Gate of Ash was the end of the story. Proxies don't get an after. I'll think about it. I'll think about it on the bed, on tiptoe.'".
    On discuss { Assert toldToLive(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. }
  }
  Topic window_live_finish with hern_window "Tell Hern you would rather he lived, and finish what he was doing, as the dead would" when saidFinish(actor) and not saidLove(actor) and not toldToLive(hern) once {
    Says "'You said on the road we owe the dead the finishing of what they were doing,' says the voice at the bars. 'Kell was kneeling. I'm walking. You'd have me finish walking, would you, and not stop at a gate.' Then: 'You're a dangerous person to walk with.' A long cough. 'I'd thought the Gate of Ash was the end of the story. Proxies don't get an after. I'll think about it. I'll think about it on the bed, on tiptoe.'".
    On discuss { Assert toldToLive(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. }
  }
  Topic window_live_chosen with hern_window "Tell Hern you would rather he lived, since neither of you is who you were on the road" when saidChosen(actor) and not saidLove(actor) and not saidFinish(actor) and not toldToLive(hern) once {
    Says "'Not who I was that morning, you said, at the Fork,' says the voice at the bars. 'And keep it anyway. I've been turning that over on this bed like a stone in my pocket.' Then: 'You're a dangerous person to walk with.' A long cough. 'I'd thought the Gate of Ash was the end of the story. Proxies don't get an after. I'll think about it. I'll think about it on the bed, on tiptoe.'".
    On discuss { Assert toldToLive(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. }
  }
  Topic gaol_law with hern "Ask Hern whether anybody could bear his sentence for him" when hernGaoled(hern) and not knows(actor, sentence_borne) once {
    Says "Hern laughs so hard he has to hold the bedpost. 'By the canons? Yes. Putting-out's a penance; any penance may be borne by another.' He wipes his eyes. 'Nobody ever has. Nobody who's put out has friends.' He sobers, and points a finger like a root at you. 'Don't you get ideas.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sentence_borne). }
  }
  Topic gaol_carth with hern "Ask Hern what he thinks about now, in the warm" when hernGaoled(hern) and stayingAtCarth(actor) once {
    Says "'Carth.' He holds his feet to the fire. 'Twenty-three nights. The child. The old woman in the byre.' He is quiet. 'I refused it to spite a man in a warm house. And it went to a cold one.' He looks at the fire. 'I'm in a warm room. I'm the heretic and I'm in the warmest room I've slept in since I was a boy.' He laughs. 'Gaunt,' he says, as if it were a swear-word, and also a prayer.".
  }
  // His chest: a cold night given away and not tended kills him by the Fast. Tended, by someone with the skill, or by
  // the Lady's physician, he mends enough to stand on Ash Day.
  Action tend_hern(actor: group, site: place) "Tend Hern's chest" {
    Description "Steam, and a mustard plaster, and making him lie still, which is the hard part.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, gaol_cell) and at(hern, gaol_cell) and capable(actor, mending) and hernFailing(hern) and not hernTended(hern).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert hernTended(hern). }
    Result "You make him lie down, which takes most of the hour, and steam his chest with a kettle and a towel, and put a plaster on him that makes him swear in the language of the Row, which is extensive. By the end of it the rattle in his breath has gone back down to somewhere you can bear to listen to. 'I'll live till Wednesday,' he says, accusingly, 'thanks to you.'".
  }
  Rule hern_dies when hernFailing(hern) and not hernTended(hern) and not hernDead(hern) and not hernFled(hern) and eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 23 { Assert hernDead(hern). Assert at(hern, limbo). }
  Rule hern_dies_told when hernDead(hern) and inTown() and not spread(hern_dies_told)
    says "At midnight the tenor bell of the Minster rings the Fast in over the city, one stroke, and then another, and the masks come off all over the Middle Town. In the Consistory gaol, in the warmest room he had slept in since he was a boy, Ninian Hern is dead, of the night he gave a child at Carth, with his feet to the fire. The serjeant who finds him says he looked pleased." { Assert spread(hern_dies_told). }
  Entity hern_dies_told: fact "Hern dead".

  // ── The rescue ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Hal Metcalfe, a printer's apprentice and Hern's loudest follower, means to be under the gaol window at eleven on
  // Fastens' Eve with a ladder and a file. Prudence Garth, who listens to Hern on the Steps and believes him, has been
  // offered the informer's fee, six shillings, which is her mother's three years of unpaid pains; at eight she will tell
  // the gaol's serjeants.
  Person hal "Hal Metcalfe" at gaol_lane {
    Role "a printer's apprentice of eighteen with ink to the elbow, loitering under the gaol window with his hands in his pockets, very obviously not loitering". Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Level 1. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "The young man under the window peels himself off the wall. 'You're the one that came down the fell with him,' he says. Everybody in Gaunt has heard. He lowers his voice to a whisper that carries the length of Gaol Lane. 'Fastens' Eve. Eleven. A ladder and a file. Are you with us?'".
    Greets again "Hal Metcalfe winks at you, enormously, with his whole face, and glances at the window above in case anyone has failed to notice that he is being discreet. 'Fastens' Eve,' he whispers, in a whisper that carries to the Minster. 'Eleven. Bring a file, or bring a friend with one.'".
  }
  Person prudence "Prudence Garth" at row_lane {
    Role "a pale serious girl of seventeen with a student's satchel and darned gloves, who does not meet anyone's eye". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    Greets "The girl with the satchel starts when you speak to her. 'I listen to him,' she says, before you have asked anything. 'On the Steps. Everybody knows I do. I believe him.' She looks at her gloves. 'I do believe him.'".
    Greets again "Prudence Garth looks at her gloves, which have been darned since you saw them, in a thread of a slightly different grey. 'I was on the Steps this morning,' she says. 'Someone else read his sermon, and it was not the same. It was a good sermon. That is what I could not forgive.'".
  }
  Relation informs(group). Relation informed(group). Relation prudenceTurned(group). Relation rescueOff(group). Relation halTaken(group).
  Relation barsOut(group). Relation hernRefusedWindow(group).
  Discovery hal_plan "Hal Metcalfe means to be under the gaol window at eleven on Fastens' Eve with a ladder and a file, to get Hern out.".
  Discovery prudence_informs "Prudence Garth has been offered the informer's fee, six shillings, the price of her mother's three years of unpaid pains, to tell the gaol's serjeants when Hal Metcalfe comes for Hern; she will tell them at eight on Fastens' Eve.".
  Initially Assert informs(prudence).
  Topic hal_plan_topic with hal "Ask Hal Metcalfe what he means to do" when true once {
    Says "'Get him out.' Hal is delighted to be asked. 'Fastens' Eve, eleven, everyone drunk and masked and the serjeants at the Fat Lamb. I've a ladder at the printer's, and a file, and Pru's to keep watch at the lane end.' He beams. 'Pru's one of us. She's at every sermon. She cried when he said nobody's sorry.' He leans in. 'I've not told anyone but Pru.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hal_plan). }
  }
  Topic pru_mother with prudence "Ask Prudence Garth about her mother" when knows(actor, hal_plan) and not prudenceTurned(prudence) once {
    Says "Prudence Garth goes white, and then, because you are a stranger and she has been waiting a week to tell somebody, she tells you. Her mother is three years behind in her pains: a lie to an Assessor about a hen, assessed, never paid, doubled, doubled again. Next Lady Day they'll put her on the Register as a defaulter, and a defaulter can't be served in the Shambles. And a canon of the Fabric, a pleasant round man, said there was an informer's fee for the night Hern's friends came for him; six shillings; exactly. She looks at her darned gloves. 'I do believe him,' she says. 'I believe every word. And I'm going to tell them at eight.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, prudence_informs). }
  }
  Action pay_pru(actor: group, site: place) "Give Prudence Garth six shillings for her mother's pains, and ask her to tell nobody anything" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(prudence, site) and knows(actor, prudence_informs) and not prudenceTurned(prudence) and not informed(prudence) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 6.
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Assert prudenceTurned(prudence). Retract informs(prudence). }
    Result "Prudence Garth looks at the shillings in her palm as if they were something she had dropped long ago and stopped looking for. 'It's the same money,' she says. 'It's exactly the same money.' Then she closes her hand on it and goes off up the Row toward a door with a hen-coop beside it, running, which you have not seen her do, and does not come back to thank you, which you understand.".
  }
  Topic pru_turned with prudence "Tell Prudence Garth what Hern said on the road about being sorry for another" when knows(actor, prudence_informs) and not prudenceTurned(prudence) and not informed(prudence) and answeredSorry(actor) once {
    Says "You tell her what Hern asked on the fell, and what you answered, and what he said. Prudence listens with her satchel against her chest. 'One man sorry for another,' she says. 'He asked that?' She is quiet. 'My mother lied about a hen.' She laughs, and it turns into something else. 'I'll not go to them,' she says. 'Let them have her on the Register. She'd sooner, if she knew. She'd sooner be a defaulter than have me do that.' She goes, fast, up the Row.".
    On discuss { Assert prudenceTurned(prudence). Retract informs(prudence). }
  }
  Topic hal_warned with hal "Tell Hal Metcalfe that Prudence means to sell the night to the serjeants" when knows(actor, prudence_informs) and not rescueOff(hal) and not prudenceTurned(prudence) once {
    Says "Hal Metcalfe's face falls apart and puts itself back together as something older. 'Pru,' he says. 'Pru did?' He looks up at the window. 'Then they'll be waiting.' He takes his hands out of his pockets. 'Then I'll not come. I'll not get him taken worse for my ladder.' He goes away down Gaol Lane, kicking the snow.".
    On discuss { Assert rescueOff(hal). }
  }
  Rule pru_informs when informs(prudence) and eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 20 and not informed(prudence) and not rescueOff(hal) and not hernFled(hern) and hernGaoled(hern) { Assert informed(prudence). Retract informs(prudence). }
  // The serjeants: at the window from half past ten, if they were told.
  Person serjeants "the Consistory's serjeants" at limbo {
    Role "two serjeants of the Consistory in grey, with staves, waiting in the shadow of the lane". Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Level 1. Numbers 2. Pronouns they.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "Two men in the Consistory's grey step out of a doorway in Gaol Lane with staves. 'In the Consistory's name,' says the elder, without much interest. 'Whoever's for the window, go home. It's Fastens' Eve. Nobody wants this.'".
    Pleads "The serjeants back off down the lane, one helping the other. 'Fastens' Eve,' says the elder. 'We never saw a thing.'".
  }
  Rule serjeants_wait when informed(prudence) and eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 22 and at(serjeants, limbo) and able(serjeants) and not routed(serjeants) { Assert at(serjeants, gaol_lane). }
  Rule serjeants_go when (not eveDay() or hour(clock) < 22) and at(serjeants, gaol_lane) { Assert at(serjeants, limbo). }
  Rule hal_comes when eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 23 and not rescueOff(hal) and not halTaken(hal) and hernGaoled(hern) and not hernFled(hern) and not hernDead(hern) { Assert halHere(hal). Assert at(hal, gaol_lane). }
  Relation halHere(group).
  Rule hal_routine when not halHere(hal) and not halTaken(hal) and daytime() and not at(hal, gaol_lane) { Assert at(hal, gaol_lane). }
  Rule hal_taken at gaol_lane when halHere(hal) and at(serjeants, gaol_lane) and able(serjeants) and not tolerates(serjeants, party) and not halTaken(hal) and not barsOut(hern)
    says "Hal Metcalfe comes down Gaol Lane at eleven with a ladder on his shoulder, masked, whistling, and the serjeants step out and take him by both arms, ladder and all, quite gently, and walk him away up the Bearer's Steps. 'Pru,' he says, over his shoulder. 'Pru?'" {
    Assert halTaken(hal). Retract halHere(hal). Assert at(hal, limbo). }
  Action file_bars(actor: group, site: place) "Help Hal Metcalfe up the ladder and get the bars out of the gaol window" {
    Description "Two bars, set in lead; a file and a strong arm, or a lockworker's patience.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, gaol_lane) and halHere(hal) and at(hal, gaol_lane) and hernAtBars() and not barsOut(hern)
      and (capable(actor, lockwork) or capable(actor, brawn)) and not threatened(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert barsOut(hern). }
    Result "Up the ladder with the file, the lane below full of masks going by who see nothing because it is Fastens' Eve: lead dug out of the stone, a bar bent back, and another, until there is a hole a thin old man could go through. Inside, by the fire, Hern is sitting on the bed with his hands on his knees, looking at the hole.".
  }
  Rule hern_comes_out when barsOut(hern) and hernWillLive(hern) and not hernHeardHawise(hern) and not hernFled(hern)
    says "Hern looks at the hole for a long time. Then he gets up, and buttons the Penitentiary's grey coat up to the neck, and comes to the window, and puts one bare foot through it, and then the other. 'I'd thought I'd go out of the Gate of Ash,' he says, on the ladder, 'like a man in a story.' He comes down into Gaol Lane among the masks. 'This is a better story. Nobody'll believe it.' Hal Metcalfe takes one arm and you take the other, and the three of you go down to Bow Gate and out through the Row, and nobody stops anybody, because it is Fastens' Eve; and at the Fell Gate, which is never shut, he stops, and shakes your hand for the last time, and goes off into the Levels on his bare feet in the dark, toward the fell and the drovers' road, with Hal beside him carrying the ladder for no reason." {
    Assert hernFled(hern). Assert escapedWindow(hern). Retract hernGaoled(hern). Assert at(hern, limbo). Assert at(hal, limbo). Retract halHere(hal).
    Assert at(party, fell_gate). }
  Relation escapedWindow(group).
  Rule hern_stays_in when barsOut(hern) and not hernFled(hern) and not hernRefusedWindow(hern) and (not hernWillLive(hern) or hernHeardHawise(hern))
    says "Hern looks at the hole, and at the night through it, and does not get up. 'No,' he says. 'Thank you, Hal. Thank you.' He comes to the window and puts his hand through and pats Hal's face, on the ladder. 'I didn't walk forty miles to go out of a window. Put the bars back, if you can, and go home, and be at the Minster on Wednesday.'" {
    Assert hernRefusedWindow(hern). Retract halHere(hal). Assert at(hal, limbo). }
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/gate.kyr:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── The Commerce of Merit ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Every fault in Gaunt has its price in pains, set by the Penitentiary; every pain may be paid by doing a penance, or
  // by paying another to do it. A company carries its shrift on a tally-stick cut at the gate: the pains it owes. Owing
  // anything, it may not pass into the Close, nor be heard at the Consistory. The shrift is never a number on the page;
  // it is told in the city's words where the city reads it.
  Measure pains(group).
  Relation tallied(group). Relation forgedTally(group). Relation porterPassed(group). Relation porterCaught(group).
  Query shriven() means tallied(party) and pains(party) < 1.
  // Gaunt gives no credit: a night on the Steps for one pain clears the one, and the other five are the Fabric's.
  Rule no_credit when pains(party) < 0 { Set pains(party) to 0. }
  Query closeAdmits() means shriven() or porterPassed(party) or ashOpen().
  Relation putOut(group).

  // ── The Fell Gate ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person assessor "the Assessor of the Fell Gate" at fell_gate {
    Role "a canon of the Penitentiary in a black gown, at a table under the arch, with a box of tally-sticks and a knife". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Greets "The Assessor does not look up from the tally he is cutting. 'Faults of the road,' he says. 'Name them. What you do not name, and is known, is assessed double.'".
    Greets again "The Assessor does not stop cutting, but the knife slows. 'Faults,' he says. 'You have had a day in Gaunt since last, and a day in Gaunt is a day of faults. Name them, or I assess you for the ones I find.'".
  }
  Relation assessed(group). Relation assessing(group).
  // The first time the company comes through, it is assessed for the road: what it did, and whom it kept company with.
  Rule assess_begins at fell_gate when at(party, fell_gate) and not assessed(party) and not assessing(party)
    says "You are moved up the queue by the queue, and come to the table under the arch. The Assessor dips his pen. 'Faults of the road,' he says, without looking up, and then he does look up, and sees what you have brought with you, or have not, and his pen stops." {
    Assert assessing(party). Set pains(party) to 0. }
  Rule assess_association at fell_gate when assessing(party) and following(hern, party) and not spread(assess_association)
    says "'Association,' says the Assessor, and cuts one notch. 'With the accused, Ninian Hern. One pain. Everyone who walks with him pays it; you are the first who has.'" { Increase pains(party) by 1. Assert spread(assess_association). }
  Rule assess_board at fell_gate when assessing(party) and keptBoard(party) and not spread(assess_board)
    says "'Interference with a penance in progress, at the Proxy's Stone,' says the Assessor, who has had it from the road already, and cuts two. 'Two pains. The proxy was dead, which is a mitigation, and the board was the Common Council's, which is not.'" { Increase pains(party) by 2. Assert spread(assess_board). }
  Rule assess_vigil at fell_gate when assessing(party) and brokeVigil(party) and not spread(assess_vigil)
    says "The Assessor has a paper, come down off the fell before you on a pair of snowshoes. He reads it. Then he takes a fresh stick and cuts it a long time. 'A vigil broken at Carth, by fire, by a stranger,' he says. 'Whoever breaks a penance takes its debt. Seventeen nights of a cold hearth.' He holds up the stick, which is notched along a third of its length. 'Seventeen pains.'" { Increase pains(party) by 17. Assert spread(assess_vigil). }
  Entity assess_association: fact "Association". Entity assess_board: fact "Interference". Entity assess_vigil: fact "the vigil".
  Rule assess_done at fell_gate when assessing(party) and pains(party) > 0 and not assessed(party)
    says "He splits the tally down its length, gives you one half and drops the other into a box marked F for Fell. 'Your shrift,' he says. 'Owing that, you are welcome in the Row and the Middle Town and you will not pass the Close Gate, nor be heard by the Consistory, until you have paid it. The Stand is in the old sheep-market. Next.'" {
    Assert assessed(party). Retract assessing(party). Assert tallied(party). }
  Rule assess_clean at fell_gate when assessing(party) and pains(party) < 1 and not assessed(party)
    says "He cuts no notches. He splits the blank tally and gives you half. 'Clean,' he says, faintly surprised, as if he had seen a white crow. 'Welcome to Gaunt. Keep it so.' Next." {
    Assert assessed(party). Retract assessing(party). Assert tallied(party). }
  Topic assessor_hern with assessor "Ask the Assessor what is to be done with Ninian Hern" when following(hern, actor) and not hernGaoled(hern) once {
    Says "'Delivered,' says the Assessor, 'to the Consistory gaol in the Close, by his custodian, by noon on Fastens' Eve. The custodian is admitted to the Close for that errand and that only, and paid on delivery.' He looks at Hern, who is looking at the box of tallies with professional interest. 'Until then he is in your keeping, and his faults are yours.' Hern beams at you.".
  }
  Topic assessor_law with assessor "Ask the Assessor how a debt of pains is paid" when tallied(actor) once {
    Says "The Assessor sighs, as at a child. 'By penance. Done by yourself, at the Stand or on the Steps: a fast, two pains a day; a barefoot mile round the walls, one; stripes at the post, three; a night's vigil on the Bearer's Steps, six. Or by another: any penance may be borne by another. The Stand will find you one, a shilling a pain. Or by remission, which is the Lady Penitentiary's, and which you will not get.' He returns to his tally. 'It is very simple. That is its beauty.'".
  }

  // ── Delivering the accused ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation delivered(group).
  Action deliver_hern(actor: group, site: place) "Bring Ninian Hern up the Bearer's Steps and in at the Close Gate to the Consistory gaol" {
    Description "The custodian is admitted to the Close for that errand, and paid eight shillings on delivery.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, close_gate_street) and following(hern, actor) and custody(actor) and not hernGaoled(hern) and not delivered(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert delivered(actor). Assert hernGaoled(hern). Retract following(hern, actor). Assert at(hern, gaol_cell). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 8.
      Retract at(actor, site). Assert at(actor, close_green). }
    Result "The porter of the Close Gate looks at Hern for a long moment through the grille, and then opens it without a word. Inside, the Close is warm, swept, quiet, and smells of woodsmoke. Two serjeants in the Consistory's grey come across the lawn for him. Hern shakes your hand once more. 'Thank you for having me,' he says, as if leaving a dinner. 'Come and see me. They allow visitors. They're merciful.' The serjeants take him across the Close to a low door, and he goes in under it without ducking, being short, and the door shuts. A clerk counts eight shillings into your hand. You are standing in the Close of Gaunt, where nobody owes anything.".
  }
  Action deliver_uncustodied(actor: group, site: place) "Walk Ninian Hern up the Bearer's Steps to the Close Gate, and leave him at it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, close_gate_street) and following(hern, actor) and not custody(actor) and not hernGaoled(hern).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert hernGaoled(hern). Retract following(hern, actor). Assert at(hern, gaol_cell). }
    Result "At the top of the Bearer's Steps Hern knocks on the porter's grille himself. 'Ninian Hern,' he says, 'come in on his own feet, for the Consistory.' The gate opens a crack, and he goes in, and turns in the gap. 'Come and see me,' he says. 'They allow visitors.' The gate shuts.".
  }
  // He keeps his appointment whatever his custodian does: by noon on Fastens' Eve he is in the gaol.
  Rule hern_gives_himself_up when eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 12 and not hernGaoled(hern) and not hernFled(hern) and not hernDead(hern)
    and following(hern, party) and at(party, ?p) and townRoom(?p) says "Hern looks up at the sun and says, 'Noon on Fastens' Eve. I've an appointment,' and goes off up the Bearer's Steps by himself, and is let in at the Close Gate, and does not look back." {
    Assert hernGaoled(hern). Retract following(hern, party). Assert at(hern, gaol_cell). }
  Rule hern_leaves_you when eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 12 and not hernGaoled(hern) and not hernFled(hern) and not hernDead(hern)
    and at(hern, ?p) and at(party, ?p) says "Hern gets up and looks at the sun. 'Noon on Fastens' Eve,' he says. 'I've an appointment in Gaunt, and I'll keep it on my own feet.' He goes off north, barefoot, at a walk, and does not look back." {
    Assert hernGaoled(hern). Retract following(hern, party). Assert at(hern, gaol_cell). }
  Rule hern_keeps_appointment when eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 12 and not hernGaoled(hern) and not hernFled(hern) and not hernDead(hern) {
    Assert hernGaoled(hern). Retract following(hern, party). Assert at(hern, gaol_cell). }
  // Refused at the Cross, he walks down from Carth when the snow stops, and is in the gaol by Shrove Monday noon.
  Rule hern_walks_in when hernAhead(hern) and mondayN() and hour(clock) >= 12 and not hernGaoled(hern) and not hernFled(hern) and not following(hern, party) and not hernDead(hern) {
    Assert hernGaoled(hern). Assert at(hern, gaol_cell). }
  // Left anywhere on the road by a company that goes on without him, he goes on without it.
  Rule hern_strays when following(hern, party) and nightfall() and at(party, ?p) and townRoom(?p) and not inClose() and not custody(party) and not spread(hern_strays)
    says "Hern stops at a corner. 'I've a room in the Row,' he says, 'nobody's let it; I'll sleep there, and save you the custody of me.' He goes off into the dark." { Assert spread(hern_strays). }
  Entity hern_strays: fact "Hern goes his way".

  // ── Paying: by doing it ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation fastToday(group). Measure fastedOn(group).
  Action own_fast(actor: group, site: place) "Keep a day's fast at the Stand for two of your pains" {
    Description "Nothing to eat until tomorrow. A clerk notes it on your tally.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_stand) and daytime() and tallied(actor) and pains(actor) >= 1 and not fastToday(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert fastToday(actor). Set fastedOn(actor) to dayN(gaunt_town). Assert hungry(actor). Set nextMeal(actor) to watch(clock) + 144. Set pains(actor) to pains(actor) - 2. }
    Result "The Stand's clerk cuts a fast on your tally with a small curved mark like a crescent moon. 'Two,' he says. 'Don't eat. People will be watching. They always are, in the Fast; it's the main amusement.'".
  }
  Rule fast_ends when fastToday(party) and dayN(gaunt_town) > fastedOn(party) { Retract fastToday(party). }
  Hazard barefoot_mile "a mile barefoot on the frozen setts" means "Deal (1d2) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (10).".
  Action own_mile(actor: group, site: place) "Walk a barefoot mile round the walls for one of your pains" {
    Description "Boots off, round the inside of the new wall, with a board on your back saying what for.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_stand) and daytime() and tallied(actor) and pains(actor) >= 1.
    Time 3.
    On success { Decrease pains(actor) by 1. Assert strikes(barefoot_mile, actor). Assert walkedBarefoot(actor). }
    Result "Boots off, a board on your back saying your own fault in your own name, which nobody in the Stand has seen in years and several of them come out to look at, and once round the inside of the new wall on the frozen setts, a mile, past the Row and the Fell Gate and the Gate of Ash and back. Your feet stop hurting after the first quarter, which is worse. Children follow you. At the end the clerk cuts a notch off your tally with a flourish.".
  }
  Relation walkedBarefoot(group).
  Hazard stripes "stripes at the Stand's post" means "Deal (1d3) physical damage to ally.".
  Action own_stripes(actor: group, site: place) "Take stripes at the Stand's post for three of your pains" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_stand) and daytime() and tallied(actor) and pains(actor) >= 1.
    Time 1.
    On success { Set pains(actor) to pains(actor) - 3. Assert strikes(stripes, actor). }
    Result "The post is in the middle of the Stand and the man who lays them on is a proxy himself, between jobs, and apologises. Six with a leather strap, counted aloud by the clerk. It is over quicker than you expected and hurts for longer. 'Three,' says the clerk, and cuts.".
  }
  Hazard steps_cold "a night on the Bearer's Steps" means "Deal (1d4) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (11).".
  Action own_vigil(actor: group, site: place) "Kneel the night on the Bearer's Steps yourself, for six of your pains" {
    Description "From dusk to first light, on the stone, in the open.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, close_gate_street) and nightfall() and tallied(actor) and pains(actor) >= 1 and not licence().
    Time 36.
    On success { Set pains(actor) to pains(actor) - 6. Assert strikes(steps_cold, actor). Assert keptStepVigil(actor). }
    Result "You kneel on the Bearer's Steps all night with the Close Gate shut above you and the Shambles shut below. Twice the porter opens his grille and looks at you and shuts it. Once a woman from the Row brings you a hot stone wrapped in a rag and goes away again without a word. The Minster bells give you every hour, so that you know exactly how much of it there is. At first light the porter comes out with a knife and cuts six notches off your tally and gives it back. 'Six,' he says. 'You did it properly. Nobody does it properly.'".
  }
  Relation keptStepVigil(group).

  // ── Paying: by another ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A shilling a pain at the Stand. The page says who takes the work.
  Action hire_proxy(actor: group, site: place) "Hire a proxy at the Stand to bear your pains, a shilling a pain" {
    Description "Your shrift paid, today, by somebody else's back.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_stand) and daytime() and tallied(actor) and pains(actor) >= 1 and pains(actor) < 10
      and quantity(actor, gold) >= pains(actor) and not struck(barefoot).
    Time 3 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by pains(actor). Set pains(actor) to 0. Assert hiredProxy(actor). }
    Result "The Stand's clerk takes your tally and your shillings, and calls a name, and a woman in a grey shawl comes out of a pen and takes the tally from him, and reads it, and nods, and puts on a board with your fault on it in your name, and goes off to do it. She does not look at you. Why would she? It is not personal. The clerk gives you back a clean tally. 'Shriven,' he says. 'Next.'".
  }
  Action hire_proxy_heavy(actor: group, site: place) "Hire a proxy at the Stand to bear your pains, a shilling a pain" {
    Description "Your shrift paid, today, by somebody else's back.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_stand) and daytime() and tallied(actor) and pains(actor) >= 10
      and quantity(actor, gold) >= pains(actor) and not struck(barefoot).
    Time 3 minutes.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by pains(actor). Set pains(actor) to 0. Assert hiredProxy(actor). Assert tibBears(actor). }
    Result "Seventeen nights of cold hearth is a lot of pains to find a back for, and the Stand's clerk has to go along the pens asking. In the end it is a boy, twelve or so, thin, with his feet in rags, who says he can do cold, he's done cold before, his gran's the Prior. 'Tib Ackroyd,' the clerk writes, and gives him your tally, and the boy reads it slowly with his finger, and nods, and goes off to find a cold room to sit in for seventeen nights at a shilling a night, which in the Row is good money. The clerk gives you back a clean tally. 'Shriven,' he says.".
  }
  Relation hiredProxy(group). Relation tibBears(group).

  // ── Paying: by forgery ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person heb "Heb" at heb_cellar {
    Role "a small sharp woman with spectacles pushed up into grey hair and a tally-knife, a Penitentiary clerk's widow". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "'Shut the door,' says the woman at the table. 'There. Now. You've a tally you don't like the look of.' She holds out her hand for it without looking. 'Everybody has. Show.'".
    Greets again "Heb pushes her spectacles up into her hair, and takes them down again, which is her way of indicating that she has read your face. 'Back again,' she says. 'Whatever the tally says today, do not tell me how it came to say it. I should have to enter it.'".
  }
  Action buy_forgery(actor: group, site: place) "Buy a clean tally of Heb, four shillings" {
    Description "It will look like a clean one. Whether it passes for one depends on who looks.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, heb_cellar) and tallied(actor) and pains(actor) >= 1 and not forgedTally(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 4.
    Time 2.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Assert forgedTally(actor). }
    Result "Heb turns your tally over in her fingers like a jeweller, splits a blank stick of the same willow from her bundle, ages it over the brazier, rubs it in ash and spit and her own sleeve, and cuts the Fell Gate's mark in the end with three flicks. 'There,' she says. 'Clean as a nun. It'll pass any porter that's been on the gate more than a year and less than ten; the new ones look too hard and the old ones know my hand.' She drops your real one in a drawer full of real ones. 'You still owe it, mind. That's between you and Saint Oswy.'".
  }
  Topic heb_law with heb "Ask Heb about the law of penance" when true once {
    Says "'The law.' Heb snorts. 'I copied it out for thirty years, for him upstairs.' She means her husband, and the Penitentiary. 'It's all one sentence: every fault has a price, and anyone can pay it. All the rest is arithmetic.' She cuts a notch for emphasis. 'Putting-out's a penance too, did you know? The greatest. It's in the canons. So by the law anyone could be put out for anyone.' She looks at you over the spectacles. 'Nobody ever has. People with friends don't get put out.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sentence_borne). }
  }
  Action show_forgery(actor: group, site: place) "Show the porter of the Close Gate Heb's clean tally" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, close_gate_street) and forgedTally(actor) and not porterPassed(actor) and not porterCaught(actor) and not shriven().
    Time 1 minute.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert porterPassed(actor). }
    On failure { Assert porterCaught(actor). Retract forgedTally(actor). Increase pains(actor) by 3. }
    Result "The porter takes the stick through the grille and turns it in the lamplight, and runs his thumb along it, and hands it back. 'Clean,' he says, and the grille shuts, and the gate opens.".
    Otherwise "The porter takes the stick through the grille and turns it in the lamplight, and smiles for the first time. 'Heb,' he says, fondly, and snaps it in two. 'She does a lovely job. Forgery's three more.' He cuts them on your real tally, which he seems to have had all along, and pushes it back through the grille.".
  }
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/placed.k:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // The country beyond a march of a generated world: the company that comes in at the Penitent's Cross is the world's own.
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  // What is said of the Levels of Gaunt in the country behind it: once it is seen through, it is old news there.
  Entity word: fact "What is said of Gaunt and the Ash Day trial in the country behind it.".
  Rule word_old when bookClosed() and not stale(word) { Assert stale(word). }
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/road.kyr:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── Ninian Hern ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Sixty. For thirty years the most sought-after proxy in Gaunt: he has fasted, knelt, walked and kept vigil for half
  // the Guildhall. Last winter he was offered the Cold Vigil, forty nights of no fire, for a blood-fault, and refused it;
  // and then he began to say on the Minster steps that he had repented for a hundred men and been sorry for none of
  // them, and neither had they, so who had been forgiven? He is walking to his trial of his own will, because he wants to
  // say it in the Minster. He is funny, coarse, vain of his feet, generous, ill, and sometimes wrong.
  Person hern "Ninian Hern" at cross_road {
    Role "a barefoot old man in a frieze coat, ignoring a cough" when not hernGaoled(hern) and not hernCoat(hern) and not hernKersey(hern) and not at(hern, chapter_house).
    Role "a barefoot old man in his shirt, grey as ash, with a cough that has stopped being ignorable" when not hernGaoled(hern) and hernCoat(hern) and not hernKersey(hern) and not at(hern, chapter_house).
    Role "a barefoot old man in a new grey coat, coughing, and pleased with the world" when not hernGaoled(hern) and hernKersey(hern) and not at(hern, chapter_house).
    Role "a barefoot old man in a warm cell, in a new grey coat of the Penitentiary's kersey, sitting on the end of the bed with his feet to the fire" when hernGaoled(hern) and not at(hern, chapter_house).
    Role "a barefoot old man in a new grey coat, standing on a square of different stone with his hands behind his back" when at(hern, chapter_house).
    Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "Hern is interested in you enormously, as he is interested in everything, as if you were a new kind of weather. 'Ninian Hern,' he says, as he says to everybody every time, in case they have forgotten, and holds out a hand like a root. 'Heretic. I'm expected.'".
    Greets again "Hern is pleased to see you, in the unspecific way he is pleased by doors and weather, which he would be the first to tell you is not saying much. 'Ninian Hern,' he says again, in case you have forgotten. 'Heretic. Still expected.'".
    Joins "Hern picks up his stick and falls in at your shoulder, barefoot, as if he had been waiting all morning to be asked.".
    Leaves "For now, that is the last of Hern.".
  }
  // In the gaol he is given the Penitentiary's grey kersey, and wears it ever after.
  Relation hernKersey(group). Rule hern_kersey when hernGaoled(hern) and not hernKersey(hern) { Assert hernKersey(hern). }
  Relation hernGaoled(group). Relation hernFled(group). Relation hernDead(group). Relation hernFailing(group).
  Relation custody(group). Relation refusedCustody(group). Relation hernAhead(group).
  // The beadle sent to fetch him, who has frozen his foot on the march.
  Person beadle "Beadle Clem Sutcliffe" at cross_road {
    Role "a beadle of the Penitentiary in a black gown, sitting on the ledge of the Cross with one boot off and his foot in his hat". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
    Greets "The man in the beadle's gown does not get up. 'You'll be going north,' he says. 'Everybody's going north. It's the Fast.' He looks at his foot, which is the colour of a candle. 'I'm not. I've a commission for whoever is.'".
    Greets again "Beadle Sutcliffe nods at you over his foot, which is no better, and has gone from the colour of a candle to the colour of a church window. 'The commission still stands,' he says. 'I will not trouble you with it again. I will merely say that the offer remains, and so does the foot.'".
  }
  Discovery beadle_offer "Beadle Sutcliffe was sent from the Penitentiary to bring Ninian Hern in to the Consistory at Gaunt, which sits on him on Ash Day; he has frozen his foot on the march and cannot walk. He will pay two shillings now and promise eight more at the Fell Gate to whoever takes Hern in.".
  Topic beadle_why with beadle "Ask the beadle what the commission is" when not custody(actor) and not refusedCustody(actor) once {
    Says "'Him,' says the beadle, and nods at the old man on the step. 'Ninian Hern. Barefoot Hern, they call him in the Row. The Consistory sits on him on Ash Day, for heresy, and I was sent to fetch him in, and I've fetched him this far, and here's my foot.' He takes it out of the hat and looks at it and puts it back. 'He's not chained. He'd go by himself, he says. But the law says he's to be brought, and brought means somebody brings him, and the somebody's paid. Two shillings now. Eight at the Fell Gate, from the Assessor, when you hand him over.' He sniffs. 'It's three days' walk for a beadle. It's one for anybody with two feet.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, beadle_offer). }
  }
  Topic beadle_heresy with beadle "Ask the beadle what Hern's heresy is" when knows(actor, beadle_offer) once {
    Says "The beadle lowers his voice, though there is nobody on the fell but the three of you and a crow. 'He says penance can't be borne by another. Or he says it can, but it does no good. Or he says nobody's sorry. It depends which day you hear him.' He shakes his head. 'Thirty years he bore it for half the Guildhall, and the best at it there ever was. Forty nights on the Minster steps for the old Wood-reeve, and never moved. And then last winter he wouldn't, and now he won't stop talking.' He looks at Hern with something like love. 'He's the only man I ever saw do a penance properly. That's the joke of it.'".
  }
  Action take_custody(actor: group, site: place) "Take Ninian Hern into your custody, for the beadle's two shillings now and eight at the Fell Gate" {
    Description "He will walk with you to Gaunt, and you will answer for him there.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, cross_road) and at(hern, cross_road) and knows(actor, beadle_offer)
      and not custody(actor) and not refusedCustody(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert custody(actor). Assert acceptsEscort(hern, actor). Assert following(hern, actor). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 2. }
    Result "The beadle counts two shillings into your palm out of a purse that is mostly string. 'He's yours,' he says. 'Eight more at the Fell Gate. Don't lose him. And don't listen to him: he's very persuasive and he's always wrong.' Hern has finished not-mending his sandal. He throws it into the snow, stands up on his bare feet, and shakes your hand, solemnly, as if a bargain had been struck. 'My custodian,' he says. 'I've never had one. I've been one, often. It's very restful, being had.'".
  }
  Action refuse_custody(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the beadle you will not take the old man in" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, cross_road) and at(hern, cross_road) and knows(actor, beadle_offer)
      and not custody(actor) and not refusedCustody(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert refusedCustody(actor). Assert hernAhead(hern). Assert at(hern, limbo). }
    Result "The beadle shrugs as if he had expected nothing else of the world. Hern stands up, barefoot in the snow, and stretches, and picks up his stick. 'Then I'll bring myself,' he says. 'I've done it before. I'll go on up; you'll catch me up, or you won't.' He goes off up the fell road at an old man's pace that is faster than it looks, and does not look back, and in a while the road has him.".
  }
  // A beadle's foot bound is a beadle grateful, and a beadle knows the canons better than the canons.
  Relation footBound(group).
  Action bind_foot(actor: group, site: place) "Bind up the beadle's frozen foot" {
    Description "Snow first, not fire; then warm hands, and wool.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(beadle, site) and capable(actor, mending) and not footBound(beadle).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert footBound(beadle). Assert knows(actor, sentence_borne). }
    Result "You rub the foot with snow until he swears, and then with your hands until he weeps, and then wrap it in a stocking of your own and his hat. 'I'll keep it,' he says, surprised. He watches you a while. Then he says, low, so that Hern will not hear: 'There's a thing in the canons nobody reads. Putting-out's a penance. The greatest there is, but a penance. And any penance may be borne by another.' He looks at Hern on the step. 'I've always wondered if anybody would. Nobody ever has, because nobody who was put out ever had a friend.'".
  }
  Discovery sentence_borne "In the canons of Gaunt, putting-out is a penance, the greatest; and any penance may be borne by another. A man sentenced to be put out may, by the city's own law, have the sentence borne for him.".
  // Raistrick, met by day at the Cross: the vigils' warden, in his own house, polite.
  Person raistrick "Raistrick" at reeve_hut {
    Role "the Ash-reeve, a long quiet man in a sheepskin, the Penitentiary's warden of vigils". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 3. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "The man at the table closes his book on one finger, and waits. He is perfectly polite. 'Raistrick,' he says. 'I keep the vigils on this side of the Levels.'".
    Greets again "Raistrick has not opened the book, and waits, as he waited the first time, with a courtesy that gives away nothing at all. 'You have come again to the vigil,' he says. 'You will find nothing has altered, Mistress. It is our principal merit.'".
  }
  Topic raistrick_warm with raistrick "Ask Raistrick whether he has ever found a hearth warm" when knows(actor, ash_test) once {
    Says "Raistrick considers the question as if it were a hearth. 'Often,' he says. 'Most vigils break. The cold is longer than people think.' He turns his book round on the table, and back. 'The first I found warm was my mother's. Forty nights, for a miller's lie, on a farm the other side of the Levels. I was nine. My sister had the croup on the twentieth night, and I lit it. The reeve that year came at three and put his hand in it and said Broken, and we were off the farm by Lady Day.' He opens the book. 'I took the post when he died. I thought the hand in the ash should be a hand that knows.' He finds his place, and makes a small neat mark. 'It doesn't change what the ash says.'".
  }
  Discovery ash_test "Raistrick, the Ash-reeve, comes to every vigil house in the night, unannounced, and puts his bare hand into the ash of the hearth. If it is warm the vigil is broken. That is the whole of the test: the hearth.".
  Topic raistrick_what with raistrick "Ask Raistrick what he keeps" when true once {
    Says "'Vigils,' says Raistrick. 'Cold vigils. A house that takes one keeps no fire, for so many nights; I see that it does.' He holds up his right hand, and turns it over, as if it were a tool he were showing you. 'Once a night, at an hour I choose, I go in, and I put my hand in the ash of the hearth. Cold, it is kept. Warm, it is broken.' He lowers the hand. 'I don't knock. A vigil isn't a thing you're told about before.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ash_test). }
  }
  Topic raistrick_whose with raistrick "Ask Raistrick whose vigils they are" when knows(actor, ash_test) once {
    Says "'The Penitentiary's.' He opens his book again, and finds his place. 'Bought, of the Penitentiary, by those who owe; kept, for wages, by those who need them. I keep the count.' He makes a small neat C against a name. 'I report each morning at ten to the one who pays, at his own yard, so he knows his nights are being kept. That's his right.' He looks up. 'I'm not to say who. You'll know the yard by the billet over the gate.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, reeve_reports). }
  }
  Discovery reeve_reports "Raistrick reports each morning at ten to whoever paid for the Carth vigil, at his own yard in Gaunt, which has a carved billet of wood over its gate.".

  // ── The road: three questions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Each station has a question; each answer is kept, and turned on the company later: at Carth, at the gaol, at the
  // trial.
  Relation askedSorry(group). Relation saidLove(group). Relation saidOwn(group). Relation saidTrade(group).
  Query answeredSorry(a: group) means saidLove(a) or saidOwn(a) or saidTrade(a).
  Event cross_question at proxy_stone when at(party, proxy_stone) and following(hern, party) and not askedSorry(party) "All the way up the fell road Hern has walked beside you, bare feet in the snow, not hurrying, and you notice he puts each foot down flat and whole, like a man laying something on a table. Just below the stone he says: 'Thirty years I did other people's sorrow for them. Fasts, vigils, the stairs on my knees. I was the best in Gaunt.' He coughs, and spits, and goes on. 'So here's a question for you to walk on. Can one man be sorry for another?'" then { Assert askedSorry(party). }
  Topic say_love with hern "Tell him: yes. That is what love is" when askedSorry(actor) and not answeredSorry(actor) once {
    Says "'Love!' says Hern, delighted, as if you had shown him a coin he had never seen. 'Now that's a better answer than the Penitentiary's, and they've had two hundred years.' He thinks about it. 'But love's not for hire at a shilling a night, is it? Or is it?' He laughs, and coughs, and laughs. 'I'll think about that. I'll think about that all the way.'".
    On discuss { Assert saidLove(actor). }
  }
  Topic say_own with hern "Tell him: no. Sorrow is your own, or it is nothing" when askedSorry(actor) and not answeredSorry(actor) once {
    Says "Hern looks at you with great affection. 'That's my heresy,' he says. 'You've just said my heresy, on the king's highway, to a man in custody. They'll have you for that.' He looks away up the road. 'It's true, mind. I'm only not sure it's all that's true.'".
    On discuss { Assert saidOwn(actor). }
  }
  Topic say_trade with hern "Tell him: it is a trade like any other, and he was good at it" when askedSorry(actor) and not answeredSorry(actor) once {
    Says "'A trade.' Hern considers his feet. 'I was good at it. I was very good at it. I could kneel eleven hours on a stone stair and think about dinner the whole time, and the Minster bells counted it as eleven hours of contrition for a draper.' He is quiet. 'That's what I couldn't stand, in the end. Not that it didn't work. That it did.'".
    On discuss { Assert saidTrade(actor). }
  }
  // The Proxy's Stone: a proxy who froze kneeling, last winter, for a councillor's adultery.
  Relation askedDead(group). Relation saidNames(group). Relation saidNothing(group). Relation saidFinish(group). Relation keptBoard(group).
  Query answeredDead(a: group) means saidNames(a) or saidNothing(a) or saidFinish(a).
  Event stone_question at proxy_stone when at(party, proxy_stone) and following(hern, party) and answeredSorry(party) and not askedDead(party) "Hern stops at the stone. He looks at the kneeling man, and then he goes down on his own knees in the snow beside him, easily, as a man sits in his own chair, and looks into his face. 'Tobias Kell,' he says. 'He was a good proxy. Steady. He'd have finished the forty, too, if it hadn't been the winter it was.' He puts out a hand and does not quite touch the board. 'Here's your second question, then. What do we owe the dead?'" then { Assert askedDead(party). }
  Topic say_names with hern "Tell him: their names" when askedDead(actor) and not answeredDead(actor) once {
    Says "Hern nods slowly. 'Their names.' He turns the board round on its cord. On the back, in chalk gone grey, a different hand has written: GIDEON ROPER, OF THE COMMON COUNCIL. 'He wrote it himself,' says Hern. 'Kell. Whose it was. So somebody would know.' He looks up at you. 'Shall we give him his own, then, instead of Roper's?'".
    On discuss { Assert saidNames(actor). }
  }
  Topic say_nothing with hern "Tell him: nothing. The dead are past owing" when askedDead(actor) and not answeredDead(actor) once {
    Says "'Past owing.' Hern sits back on his heels. 'That's the Penitentiary's view, near enough. A proxy dies on the job, the job's void, and the Councillor buys another forty from somebody else.' He looks at the board. 'I'm sixty. I'll be past owing myself soon. I'd like to think somebody'd at least take this off me.'".
    On discuss { Assert saidNothing(actor). }
  }
  Topic say_finish with hern "Tell him: to finish what they were doing" when askedDead(actor) and not answeredDead(actor) once {
    Says "Hern laughs, a short bark that turns into a cough. 'Finish Tobias's forty nights for Gideon Roper? Kneel here till the thaw?' Then he stops laughing. 'No. You don't mean that. You mean finish what he was doing, which was feeding his sister's boys.' He looks at you sideways. 'That's a harder thing. That's a thing a man could spend his life on.'".
    On discuss { Assert saidFinish(actor). }
  }
  Action take_board(actor: group, site: place) "Help Hern take the board from Tobias Kell's neck, and cut the proxy's own name in the stone" {
    Description "The cord is frozen, and so is he.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, proxy_stone) and following(hern, actor) and askedDead(actor) and not keptBoard(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert keptBoard(actor). }
    Result "The cord will not untie; you cut it. The board comes away with a sound like a page. Hern lays it face down in the snow, GIDEON ROPER uppermost, and takes out a knife and cuts into the stone above the kneeling man, slowly, in capitals that are not very straight, TOBIAS KELL, and under it, after thought, HIS OWN. 'There,' he says. 'Now he's kneeling for himself.' He gets up, with your arm. 'They'll assess us for that. Interference with a penance in progress. Two pains each, if I know the Fell Gate.' He seems pleased.".
  }
  // The Drove Fork: the third question, and the test.
  Relation askedPromise(group). Relation hernTesting(group). Relation saidBinds(group). Relation saidChosen(group).
  Event fork_question at drove_fork when at(party, drove_fork) and following(hern, party) and not askedPromise(party) "At the Drove Fork Hern stops, and leans on his stick, and looks west down the drovers' road, green under the snow, going away round the fell to country where nobody has heard of Gaunt. 'Third question,' he says. 'You promised Clem this morning you'd bring me in. Are you the one who promised?' And before you can answer he turns off the fell road and walks away down the drovers' road, not fast, without looking back, to see what you will do." then {
    Assert askedPromise(party). Assert hernTesting(hern). Assert at(hern, drovers_way). }
  Action call_binds(actor: group, site: place) "Call after him: a promise binds the one who made it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, drove_fork) or at(actor, drovers_way)) and hernTesting(hern) and not hernFled(hern).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract hernTesting(hern). Assert saidBinds(actor). }
    Result "Hern stops. He stands in the drovers' road with his back to you for a while, and then he turns round and comes back up, slowly, and when he is close enough you see he is grinning. 'It binds the one who made it,' he says. 'So it binds you, and you're the same one, are you, as this morning? Every bit of you that was there?' He falls in beside you. 'Then I'll hold you to it. Whatever it turns out to mean.'".
  }
  Action call_chosen(actor: group, site: place) "Call after him: neither of you is who you were this morning, and you will keep it anyway" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, drove_fork) or at(actor, drovers_way)) and hernTesting(hern) and not hernFled(hern).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract hernTesting(hern). Assert saidChosen(actor). }
    Result "Hern laughs out loud, there on the drovers' road, and the sound goes away over the snow. He comes back. 'Not who I was,' he says. 'No. I'm a man who's been called after on a road, which I wasn't when I set out.' He falls in beside you. 'Keep it anyway. That's not the Flow, and it's not the One. I don't know what it is. It's better than both.'".
  }
  Action bring_him_back(actor: group, site: place) "Go after him and take him by the arm" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, drovers_way) and at(hern, drovers_way) and hernTesting(hern) and not hernFled(hern).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract hernTesting(hern). }
    Result "You take him by the arm, which is like taking hold of a bundle of sticks in a coat. He does not resist. 'Well,' he says, and looks at your hand on his sleeve. 'That's an answer. It's the beadle's answer, mind.' He turns round and comes, quite cheerfully. 'You'll find that a lot of people will give you the beadle's answer, in Gaunt. It's the one that doesn't need saying.'".
  }
  Action let_hern_go(actor: group, site: place) "Let him go down the drovers' road" {
    Grave "He will not come to Gaunt. The Consistory will sit to an empty floor.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, drove_fork) or at(actor, drovers_way)) and hernTesting(hern) and not hernFled(hern).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract hernTesting(hern). Assert hernFled(hern). Assert at(hern, limbo). Retract acceptsEscort(hern, actor). Retract following(hern, actor). }
    Result "You do not call. He does not look back. You watch him go away round the shoulder of Carth Fell on the drovers' road, an old man in a frieze coat with his bare feet going down flat and whole in the snow, getting smaller, until the fell takes him; and you do not know, and never will, whether he wanted you to call.".
  }
  // A company that leaves him on the drovers' road and goes on up the fell has let him go.
  Rule hern_left when hernTesting(hern) and (at(party, fell_top) or at(party, proxy_stone)) says "Behind you, nobody calls, and nobody comes back up the drovers' road." {
    Retract hernTesting(hern). Assert hernFled(hern). Assert at(hern, limbo). Retract acceptsEscort(hern, party). Retract following(hern, party). }

  // Left at the Cross with nothing said, he comes along anyway: if nobody is bringing him, he will come with whoever is going.
  Rule hern_tags_along when at(party, proxy_stone) and at(hern, cross_road) and not custody(party) and not refusedCustody(party)
    says "Behind you on the road there is someone singing, badly, in a cracked old voice; and in a while the barefoot old man from the Cross comes up level with you, and nods, as if you had arranged it. 'Clem's still sitting there,' he says. 'If nobody's bringing me I'll come with whoever's going. It's the same road.'" {
    Assert acceptsEscort(hern, party). Assert following(hern, party). Assert at(hern, proxy_stone). }
  // Told to make his own way, he does: on up the fell ahead of the company.
  Rule hern_sent_ahead when dismissed(hern, party) and not hernGaoled(hern) and not hernFled(hern) and not hernAhead(hern) and not following(hern, party) { Assert hernAhead(hern). Assert at(hern, limbo). }
  // Refused at the Cross, he walks on alone, and is at Carth before you, because he means to be.
  Rule hern_at_carth when hernAhead(hern) and snowing() and not at(hern, house_place) and not hernGaoled(hern) { Assert at(hern, house_place). }

  // ── Talk on the road, and anywhere he can be talked to ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic hern_why_walk with hern "Ask Hern why he is walking to his own trial" when not hernGaoled(hern) once {
    Says "'Because it's in the Minster,' says Hern. 'Ash Day, the whole city in the nave with the ash on its foreheads. I've said it on the steps for a year, to whoever went past. I want to say it once inside, where they can't walk past.' He coughs. 'And then they'll put me out at the Gate of Ash, I expect, and I'll walk off into the Levels like a man in a story.' He grins at you with three teeth. 'I've always wanted to be a man in a story. Proxies never are. We're in other people's.'".
  }
  Topic hern_refused with hern "Ask Hern what penance it was that he refused" when not hernGaoled(hern) once {
    Says "Hern is quiet for a while. 'The Cold Vigil,' he says. 'Forty nights. No fire in the house, not a spark, from Candlemas on. It's the penance for blood. Somebody in Gaunt has blood on him, and was sorry, and went to the Penitentiary, and they set it at forty nights cold, and he paid for it, and they offered it to me.' He spits. 'I've kept cold vigils. Three. I'm the best there is. And I thought, I'll freeze forty nights so some man in a warm house needn't, and he'll be forgiven, and the blood won't be any less on the floor. And I said no.' He looks at his feet. 'So somebody else is keeping it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, vigil_refused). }
  }
  Discovery vigil_refused "Last winter Ninian Hern refused to keep the Cold Vigil, forty nights of no fire, the penance for a blood-fault, bought by someone in Gaunt; so somebody else is keeping it.".
  Topic hern_gate with hern "Ask Hern what becomes of a man put out of Gaunt" when not hernGaoled(hern) once {
    Says "'He walks,' says Hern. 'Out of the Gate of Ash at dusk, into the Levels, in what he stands in, and they seal the gate behind him, and that's the end of the story.' He thinks about it. 'Last one was nineteen years since. A mason, young Thwaite, for saying the Fabric's men took the tower down at night. I fasted three days for the Fabric the week he went: a thanksgiving, for a slander stopped. A shilling a day.' He coughs. 'Best-paid fast I ever kept. Nobody's seen him since. Nobody's looked.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, last_put_out). }
  }
  Topic hern_hawise with hern "Ask Hern who will judge him" when not hernGaoled(hern) once {
    Says "'The Lady Penitentiary,' says Hern, as if it were a joke he had made long ago. 'Hawise Strake. We were proxies together in the Row when we were twelve: we fasted for a fishmonger's wife, the pair of us, a week, and ate her cat's dinner on the fourth day. She went up. I stayed down. She'll put me out.' He looks at the snow. 'She'll be very fair about it. She always was. That was the trouble.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hern_and_hawise). }
  }
  Discovery hern_and_hawise "Hawise Strake, the Lady Penitentiary who will judge Hern, was a proxy beside him in the Row when they were twelve.".
  Topic hern_law with hern "Ask Hern whether anybody could bear his sentence for him" when not hernGaoled(hern) and not knows(actor, sentence_borne) once {
    Says "Hern stops dead in the road. Then he laughs so hard he has to hold the snow-post. 'Oh,' he says, 'oh, you've read the canons, or you've a mind like a proxy's. Yes. Putting-out's a penance. Any penance may be borne by another.' He wipes his eyes. 'Nobody ever has. Nobody who's put out has friends; that's why they're put out.' He sobers. 'Don't you get ideas. I didn't walk all this way to have a stranger walk out of the Gate of Ash in my coat.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sentence_borne). }
  }
  // His cough: he says nothing of it unless asked.
  Topic hern_cough with hern "Ask Hern about his cough" when not hernGaoled(hern) and not hernFailing(hern) once {
    Says "'What cough?' says Hern, and coughs. 'Thirty winters on the Minster steps. It's not the cough you want to worry about; it's the thing the cough's about.' He thumps his chest. 'It'll do till Ash Day. After that it can do what it likes.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/row.kyr:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── The Barefoot ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The proxies' fellowship in the Row, and its Prior, Bess Ackroyd: Hern's oldest friend and his enemy now, because
  // if his teaching takes the Row loses its winter wage. She will call the Row out on Ash Day, the year's best day for
  // wages, if the Wood Exchange will not open the dead-wood right; but the Row will not come out for her unless it can
  // afford to, or has a reason better than its stomach.
  Entity barefoot: group "the Barefoot".
  Relation struck(group). Relation strikeCalled(group). Relation rowWorked(group). Relation broughtWood(group).
  Relation tibHelped(group). Relation carryingBess(group). Relation hernHeardBess(group).
  Person bess "Bess Ackroyd" at barefoot_hall {
    Role "the Prior of the Barefoot, a square grey woman with her feet in a bowl and a ledger on her knee, who looks at everyone's feet first". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner grim.
    Greets "The woman with her feet in the bowl looks at your feet, and then at your face. 'Not a proxy,' she says. 'Not a burgess. A stranger with boots.' She turns a page of her ledger. 'If you've come to look at the poor, the pegs are along that wall. Forty-one. Everybody looks at the pegs.'".
    Greets again "Bess Ackroyd looks at your feet, and nods, and moves the bowl an inch so that the water does not splash them. 'You are still shod,' she says. 'It is a condition, not a fault. In the Row we have a long list of conditions that are not faults. It is what keeps us.'".
    Wants gaunt_sledge.
  }
  Discovery strike_threat "Bess Ackroyd, Prior of the Barefoot, has threatened to call the Row out on Ash Day, the year's best day for proxies' wages, unless the Wood Exchange opens the Row's old right to the dead wood in the Bishop's Wood; but the Row cannot afford to lose Ash Day's wage, and will not come out for her.".
  Discovery bess_view "Bess Ackroyd thinks Ninian Hern is right, and that if he wins, the Row starves: the Commerce of Merit is its winter's bread.".
  Topic bess_barefoot with bess "Ask Bess Ackroyd about the Barefoot" when true once {
    Says "'We're the backs,' says Bess. 'Every fast in Gaunt, every vigil, every mile on the setts, every stripe at the post that some burgess earned, one of us does it, and gets paid, and eats.' She nods at the pegs. 'Last winter the Wood-reeve held the oak back for a fortnight in the frost, and shut the dead-wood right, which was always ours, in the Bishop's Wood. Forty-one.' She turns a page. 'I've said I'll call the Row out on Ash Day if he doesn't open the right. Ash Day, when every burgess wants to be clean for the gilding. Best wage of the year.' She looks at her ledger. 'They'll not come out. They can't afford to. I can't afford to. But I've said it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, strike_threat). }
  }
  Topic bess_hern with bess "Ask Bess Ackroyd about Ninian Hern" when true once {
    Says "Bess takes her feet out of the bowl and dries them, one, then the other, slowly, with great care, as you would dry a tool. 'Ninian Hern was the best back in this Hall for thirty years,' she says. 'He taught me to kneel. You don't kneel on your knees, he said, you kneel on your mind.' She puts her stockings on. 'And now he stands on the Minster steps and tells the burgesses it does them no good. And he's right. And if they believe him, there's no Stand, and no wage, and next winter there's eighty pegs on that wall instead of forty.' She stands up. 'He can afford to be right. He's sixty and he's got a cough. We've got children.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bess_view). }
  }
  // Work for the Hall: an unpaid vigil, for a proxy too sick to keep it, and the Hall remembers.
  Action keep_hall_vigil(actor: group, site: place) "Keep tonight's vigil for a sick proxy of the Hall, unpaid" {
    Description "Old Nell Firth is booked for a night on the Bearer's Steps for a tallow-chandler, and she is coughing blood. Someone has to, or she loses the booking and the next one.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, barefoot_hall) and evening() and not licence() and not rowWorked(actor) and knows(actor, strike_threat).
    Time 36.
    On success { Assert rowWorked(actor). Assert strikes(steps_cold, actor). Assert keptStepVigil(actor). }
    Result "You kneel on the Bearer's Steps all night with Nell Firth's board round your neck and the chandler's fault on it, for no pay, and in the morning Bess Ackroyd comes up the Steps herself with a can of tea and stands while you drink it, and says nothing, and takes the board back, and cuts Nell's notch in the Hall's book with her own knife. 'Nell's kept her booking,' she says. 'That's next week's bread.' At the bottom of the Steps she turns. 'You've knees,' she says. It is the highest praise in the Row.".
  }
  // The strike: with Dinsdale's every back bought, the Row has leverage, and Bess sees it at once.
  Topic bess_cornered with bess "Tell Bess Ackroyd that Mistress Dinsdale has hired every back in the Stand for Ash Day" when knows(actor, stand_cornered) and knows(actor, strike_threat) and not strikeCalled(barefoot) and not woodOpened(thackray) once {
    Says "Bess Ackroyd sits quite still. Then she laughs, which you have not heard her do; it is a short dry sound like a stick breaking. 'Every back,' she says. 'Paid in advance, I'll be bound; Grizel Dinsdale always pays in advance.' She shuts the ledger. 'So we're paid for Ash Day already, every one of us. And if we stay at home, there's not a proxy to be had in Gaunt for love nor money, and every burgess that wants to be clean for the gilding will have to—' She stops, and looks at the pegs. 'Will have to do it themselves,' she says. 'Barefoot. In the snow. In front of the Row.' She stands up. 'I'll call them out. They'll come, for that. They'd pay to see that.'".
    On discuss { Assert strikeCalled(barefoot). }
  }
  Action persuade_strike(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Bess Ackroyd the Row should come out on Ash Day, and you will stand with it" {
    Description "Without the Stand bought out, the Row would lose the year's best wage. She will want a reason she can say to them.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, barefoot_hall) and at(bess, barefoot_hall) and knows(actor, strike_threat)
      and (rowWorked(actor) or broughtWood(actor)) and not strikeCalled(barefoot) and not woodOpened(thackray) and not triedStrike(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert strikeCalled(barefoot). }
    On failure { Assert triedStrike(actor). }
    Result "You say it to the Hall, in the end, not to Bess: to forty proxies on the benches with their feet in bowls. That the Wood-reeve shut the right and they froze; that the burgesses buy their way clean on their backs; that on one day in the year, the day the Ladder is gilded, the backs could stay at home. Nobody says anything. Then an old man at the back says, 'I'd give a week's wage to see Grizel Dinsdale's feet,' and the Hall laughs, and that is the vote.".
    Otherwise "The Hall hears you out, politely, with their feet in their bowls. Then Bess says, 'Ash Day's three days' bread. You've not got children,' and that is the end of it.".
  }
  Relation triedStrike(group).
  // At six on Ash Day the Row stays home, unless the right was opened, in which case Bess calls it off: they asked for
  // the wood and got it.
  Rule row_stays_home when strikeCalled(barefoot) and ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 6 and not woodOpened(thackray) and not struck(barefoot) { Assert struck(barefoot). }
  Rule row_struck_told when struck(barefoot) and inTown() and ashDay() and not spread(row_struck)
    says "On Ash Day morning the Stand is empty. Every pen, every board rubbed out, and the clerk sitting at his desk at the gate with his ledger open and his pen up and nobody to write. In the Row, every doorstep has someone sitting on it with their feet in a bowl, watching the Middle Town, as if waiting for a procession. At half past eight it begins: the burgesses of Gaunt, who must be clean for the gilding, coming down the Shambles barefoot in the snow to do their own penance, one by one, white-faced, in their shirts, with their boards round their necks in their own hands. The Row watches from its doorsteps with its feet in its bowls. Somebody begins to count the burgesses aloud, and gets to forty before the counting stops being funny." { Assert spread(row_struck). }
  Entity row_struck: fact "the Barefoot out".
  Observe stand_struck at the_stand when struck(barefoot) and ashDay() "The Stand on Ash Day: empty pens, rubbed-out boards, and the clerk at his desk with nobody to write.".
  // Bess's word for Hern, carried by someone the Row trusts.
  Topic bess_plea with bess "Ask Bess Ackroyd what she would say to Ninian Hern, if she could" when knows(actor, bess_view) and not strikeCalled(barefoot) and not hernHeardBess(hern) and (rowWorked(actor) or broughtWood(actor) or tibHelped(actor)) once {
    Says "Bess looks at the pegs, and then at her hands. 'Tell him,' she says, 'he can be right in heaven. Down here we eat.' She rubs her eyes with the heel of her hand. 'Tell him: recant, Ninian. Say it was the cough talking. Let them gild their Ladder. And next winter, when the Row's eating, he can come and sit by the stove and tell us all over again how none of it's worth anything, and we'll feed him while he says it.' She turns back to the ledger. 'Tell him I said, you don't kneel on your knees. He'll know.'".
    On discuss { Assert carryingBess(actor). }
  }
  // Met face to face, while he is still out and walking with the company.
  Action hern_meets_bess(actor: group, site: place) "Bring Ninian Hern and Bess Ackroyd face to face" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, barefoot_hall) and following(hern, actor) and at(bess, barefoot_hall) and not hernHeardBess(hern) and not strikeCalled(barefoot).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert hernHeardBess(hern). Increase hernReasons(hern) by 1. Assert knows(actor, bess_view). }
    Result "Hern stands in the doorway of the Barefoot Hall with his bare feet on the sill and looks at the pegs, and then at Bess. Neither says anything. Then he goes and puts his hand flat on Tobias Kell's peg, which is the newest. 'I passed him on the fell,' he says. 'Kneeling yet, for Roper.' Bess says, 'Did you.' 'I knelt down with him a while.' 'Did you.' He turns round. 'Bess.' 'You can be right in heaven, Ninian,' Bess says. 'Down here we eat.' And they argue then, for an hour, the way old friends argue, not to win, with the whole Hall listening; and at the end of it Hern sits down on the bench with his feet in somebody's bowl, and coughs, and says to you, not to her: 'She's right, too. That's the devil of it. She's always been right too.'".
  }
  Measure hernReasons(group).

  // ── The Bishop's Wood ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind gaunt_sledge "a sledge of dead wood from the Bishop's Wood" is treasure worth 4 weighing 4.
  Item sledge "a sledge of dead wood" is gaunt_sledge at limbo.
  Kind gaunt_faggot "a faggot of thorn from the Wood Exchange" is treasure worth 2 weighing 1.
  Relation sledgeLoaded(group).
  Person woodmen "the Wood-reeve's woodmen" at wood_edge {
    Role "three woodmen in leather with billhooks, keeping the Bishop's Wood". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Numbers 3. Pronouns they.
    Temperament proud.
    Warns "Three woodmen step out from the holly with billhooks on their shoulders. 'Dead-wood right's suspended,' says the biggest, quite pleasantly. 'By order. Four shillings and we never saw you, for an hour; or back to the Levels; or we can be assessed together, all four of us, for a brawl, which is two pains each and worth it on a cold day.'".
    Pleads "The woodmen back off into the holly with their hands up. 'All right,' says the biggest. 'All right. Take your sticks. It's not our wood either.'".
  }
  Initially Set tribute(woodmen) to 4.
  Rule woodmen_gone when woodOpened(thackray) and at(woodmen, wood_edge) { Assert at(woodmen, limbo). }
  Observe wood_open at wood_edge when woodOpened(thackray) "Someone has taken down the board at the edge of the Bishop's Wood and leant it against the post face inward. Along the woodmen's path there are sledge-runners, many, and children's footprints.".
  Person wolves "the wolves of the Bishop's Wood" at limbo {
    Role "five grey wolves, thin from the winter, at the edge of the clearing". Species wolf. Numbers 5.
    Temperament territorial.
    Warns "At the edge of the clearing five grey wolves stand up out of the snow, one after another, as if the snow had made them, and look at you, and the biggest drops its head. It is dusk. It is their wood at dusk.".
  }
  Rule wolves_come when (hour(clock) >= 16 or hour(clock) < 7) and at(wolves, limbo) and able(wolves) and not routed(wolves) and not wolvesTurned(deadfall) { Assert at(wolves, deadfall). }
  Rule wolves_go when hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 16 and at(wolves, deadfall) { Assert at(wolves, limbo). }
  Action load_sledge(actor: group, site: place) "Cut and load a sledge with dead wood from the deadfall" {
    Description "Three hours' work with an axe borrowed from nobody, and a sledge made of two boughs and your belt.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, deadfall) and not sledgeLoaded(actor) and not at(wolves, deadfall).
    Time 18. Interrupted when threatened(actor).
    On success { Assert sledgeLoaded(actor). Assert at(sledge, deadfall). }
    Result "Dead oak, dry as bone, grey; it breaks under a boot in lengths a child could carry, and you load it on a sledge of two boughs lashed with your belt until the sledge groans. It is enough to keep a household a fortnight, or an oven a week, or a cold farm till the thaw. It is the Row's, by right, and nobody in Gaunt can buy it this winter.".
  }
  Event bess_gets_wood near bess when keeps(bess, sledge) "Bess Ackroyd stands in the Hall door and looks at the sledge, and at you, and at the sledge. 'From the Bishop's Wood,' she says. 'By right.' She calls over her shoulder, and in a minute the Row is round the sledge, and the wood is going away into every doorway an armful at a time, and somebody is lighting the stove in the Hall for the first time this winter. Bess does not touch it. 'They'll say we stole it,' she says. 'Let them say it at the Consistory.'" then { Assert broughtWood(party). Assert rowWarmed(barefoot). }
  Relation rowWarmed(group).

  // ── The slide ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Purely the Row's: a boy who has lost his skate-bones, cut by his dead father, under the ice by the culvert.
  Person tib "Tib Ackroyd" at row_ditch {
    Role "a boy of twelve with his feet in rags, sitting on the ditch bank watching the others slide". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
    Greets "The boy on the bank does not look round. 'They're under the ice,' he says. 'By the grating. My skates. They went through yesterday where it's black.' He looks at the slide. 'Dad cut them. Out of a cow.'".
    Greets again "Tib Ackroyd looks round, and back at the ice, and says that his skates have not come up. 'Dad says they will in the thaw. He says that about most things. He has been right about two of them.'".
    Wants gaunt_skates.
    Seen when not tibBears(party).
  }
  Kind gaunt_skates "a pair of skate-bones, cut from a cow's shins, with leather thongs" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0.
  Item skates "Tib Ackroyd's skate-bones" is gaunt_skates at limbo.
  Relation skatesFound(group).
  Hazard ditch_water "the black water under the ditch ice" means "Deal (1d2) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (10).".
  Action find_skates(actor: group, site: place) "Break the black ice by the culvert grating and reach in for the boy's skate-bones" {
    Description "The water under it is black, and the ice round the hole will not hold a man.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, row_ditch) and not nightfall() and not skatesFound(actor) and not tibBears(actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert skatesFound(actor). Assert at(skates, row_ditch). Assert strikes(ditch_water, actor). }
    Result "You lie flat on the ice with the whole slide watching, and break the black skin by the grating with your heel, and reach in to the shoulder. The cold of it is so complete that for a moment you cannot tell whether you have a hand at all. Then your fingers close on something knobbled, bone and thong, and you draw it out streaming, and roll back onto the bank, and the children cheer as if you had pulled out a drowned man alive.".
  }
  Event tib_skates near tib when keeps(tib, skates) "Tib Ackroyd takes the skate-bones and turns them over and wipes them on his sleeve and does not say thank you, which in the Row means thank you. He ties them on. Then he goes out onto the slide, and the line of children makes room, and as he goes they all begin to sing, the way they do, the sliding song, and for the first time you hear the end of it: Oswy, Oswy, up the hill, carry me and carry me still; at the top he set him down: NOW WALK, said Oswy, into town! And on NOW WALK whoever is at the front of the line has to get off the slide and walk, and everybody shrieks." teaches second_verse then { Assert tibHelped(party). }
  Discovery second_verse "The Row's children sing the end of Saint Oswy's rhyme, which is cut on no stone: at the top of the hill, Oswy set the sinner down, and said, Now walk.".
  Observe ditch_tib_gone at row_ditch when tibBears(party) and not nightfall() "The children slide on the ditch in a line, singing. On the bank, where a boy was sitting yesterday, there is nobody: the boy is keeping somebody's seventeen cold nights, at a shilling a night, in a room in the Row with the window open.".

  // ── The Shrove baker ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person tunstall "Mother Sugden" at bakehouse {
    Role "a baker as round and floury as her own loaves, with her arms crossed, glaring at her oven". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "'Two days,' says Mother Sugden, 'two days to Ash Day, three hundred shrove-cakes risen, a pig's worth of crackling, and the oven stone cold, because the Wood-reeve wants thirty shillings the cord for oak and I'd as soon put my own feet in it.' She glares at you. 'If you've wood, I'll love you. If you haven't, mind the dough.'".
    Greets again "Mother Sugden glares at you with great warmth, and it is a warmth she has not got to spare, because the oven is cold and the dough is rising regardless. 'Have you seen the Wood-reeve?' she says. 'No. You would have said. It is the first thing a sensible person tells me.'".
    Wants gaunt_faggot. Wants gaunt_sledge.
  }
  Thing oven "Mother Sugden's oven" at bakehouse is scenery {
    State cold "The oven's mouth is black and cold.".
    State hot "The oven roars.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(oven, cold).
  Event oven_lit near tunstall when (keeps(tunstall, ?w) and itemKind(?w, gaunt_faggot) or keeps(tunstall, sledge)) and state(oven, cold) "Mother Sugden has the wood in the oven before you have let go of it, and the flint struck, and the bellows going; and in a quarter of an hour the bakehouse is roaring and she is sliding trays in on the peel two at a time, singing something rude. 'Come back on Ash Day morning,' she says over her shoulder. 'Not before. You'll not get anything before.'" then { Assert state(oven, hot). Assert bakerHelped(party). }
  Relation bakerHelped(group).
  Observe baker_cake at bakehouse when bakerHelped(party) and ashDay() "On the bakehouse step, wrapped in a cloth with your name chalked on it, there is a shrove-cake, still faintly warm. It is Ash Day. You may not eat it. Mother Sugden, through the window, is watching to see whether you will.".
  Person exchange_clerk "the Wood Exchange clerk" at wood_exchange {
    Role "a clerk with chalk held between two fingers, putting prices up". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "'Wood?' says the clerk, chalk poised. 'Oak's thirty the cord. Faggots, a hundred, nine shillings; or one, for the poor, two shillings, which is cheaper by the faggot and dearer by the hundred.' He smiles. 'Arithmetic.'".
    Sells gaunt_faggot for 2 coin from 6.
  }

  // ── Fly ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Scaifes' dog follows a company that was good to the house and to her, down the fell; and goes home the next time
  // it is at Carth, if there is a child there to go home to.
  Rule fly_follows when petted(fly, party) and dowsieSafe(dowsie) and morningDue(carth_vigil) and at(party, levels_road) and not following(fly, party) and not flyHome(fly) { Assert following(fly, party). Assert acceptsEscort(fly, party). Assert at(fly, levels_road). }
  Relation flyHome(group).
  Rule fly_goes_home at carth_yard when following(fly, party) and at(party, carth_yard) and not dowsieDead(dowsie) and not flyHome(fly)
    says "Fly goes off across the yard without looking back, and scratches at the door, and it opens, and a small voice inside says 'Fly!' and the door shuts." { Retract following(fly, party). Assert flyHome(fly). Assert at(fly, house_place). }
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/seam.kyr:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  Description "The seam in Gaunt's history, kept open: an empty lantern-hook on the north tower, a tower drawn under a tower, five lines planed off a plinth, a lintel worn smooth where a hand goes, a thirty-second loop on a ring of keys; and the trades and customs round it: the Last Inch, the chestnut man who sells indulgences, the Fat King stuck in Bow Gate, a Doctor who tells of the Veyran with the notebook.".

  // The count here is the Register of Gaunt: forty books on forty lecterns, two hundred and eleven years of every fault
  // in the city and who paid for it. Its keeper is the Lady Penitentiary, who holds thirty-one keys. Its first page is
  // the one the clerks copy and no one reads: nine lines in a rubric nobody teaches (voices.kyr, `first_leaf`). What
  // reading it costs is that the Lady must decide what her keys are for. Nothing here says where the Bishop went, who
  // is to ask for the keys, or what a second tower was to carry: those stay open on purpose, and every new piece below
  // is a thing a person has seen and not understood.

  // ── The lantern-hook, the early detail whose last act is Ash Day's dusk ───────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe hook_seen at tower_foot when not nightfall() "High on the stump of the north tower, on the face that looks out over the Levels, an iron bracket stands a yard out of the stone with a lantern-hook at its end: the only ironwork on all the scaffold that is not rusted red. Nothing hangs from it. The masons walk under it every day and nobody looks up.".
  Observe lantern_hung at tower_foot when courseSet(joby) and ashDay() and nightfall() "Somebody has hung a horn lantern from the bracket at the head of the north tower, and nobody has taken it down. It burns there steady, high over the Close, in the first dark since the Commerce began in which no Fabric man has put it out. Joby Thwaite stands under it with his hat in his hands. He does not know why he did it, he says. The hook was there.".
  Rule fate_lantern when accounting() and courseSet(joby) and not spread(fate_lantern_told)
    says "Of the lantern: it was still burning at dawn on the north tower. The lodge has taken to trimming it. From the fold on the Levels, they say, it can be seen all the way, a small yellow point at the head of a tower and a half, and the put-out sit facing it when they are not at work." {
    Assert spread(fate_lantern_told).
  }
  Entity fate_lantern_told: fact "the lantern".
  Observe lantern_hung_under at tower_foot when courseSet(joby) and ashDay() and nightfall() and knows(party, lodge_under) "You have seen the other drawing, under the finished tower, on the lodge floor: slimmer, with a small room at its head and a flame in a box in every window. The lantern on the bracket sits just where that room would stand.".

  // ── The lodge: a tower under a tower, and a mark struck out ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lodge_under "Under the finished north tower drawn on the lodge's tracing floor, much fainter and much older, another tower is scratched full size: slimmer, with no bell-chamber, and a small room at its head with a window on every face and a flame in a box in each. The masons walk on it. Joby says it is a prentice's sketch." {
    Found by searching masons_lodge with lore "You go down on your knees on the tracing floor and put a lamp low to it, and the finished tower stands up out of the scratches in the plaster as it has for two hundred years. Under it, where the plaster has worn to the lath, is another set of lines, thinner, not a mason's: a tower with no bell-chamber and a small room at the head of it, with windows. In each window a little drawn thing like a flame inside a box.".
  }
  Observe lodge_lintel at masons_lodge when true "Over the lodge door, cut into the lintel in a row, are the marks of every master since the Commerce: a square, a fork, a pair of compasses, an arrow. One place in the row has been chiselled out clean, nineteen years ago by the look of the edges.".

  // ── The gate: a custom nobody can explain ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe gate_lintel at close_gate_street when true "Everyone who climbs the Bearer's Steps to the Close Gate puts a hand up at the top, without looking, and touches the lintel on the right-hand side, where a place a hand's breadth wide is worn pale and smooth as a pebble. Canons do it. The porter does it as he opens the grille. A child sitting on the top step, asked, says it is so the stone will not be lonely, and goes on eating her bread.".

  // ── The Last Inch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery last_inch "The candles sold in the Minster to be burned for another's sins are bought back by the chandler's boy at a halfpenny when they are an inch from the end, and sold again whole: the same wax, forty times, so that a grandfather is prayed for with what a stranger was prayed for yesterday. The trade is called the Last Inch.".
  Topic dent_inch with landlord "Ask Matthias Dent why every candle in the Fat Lamb is burned down to the same inch and no further" when true once {
    Says "'The Last Inch.' He wipes the knife on his apron with a kind of professional pride. 'A burgess buys a candle in the Minster to burn for his grandfather. It burns. At the last inch, a chandler's boy comes round with a basket and buys the stub for a halfpenny, and it goes back to the seller, and the seller sells it whole.' He holds up a candle: an inch of stump in a dish. 'Same wax. Forty times, they say. I light one at every table, and I take it back at the inch, and it is the lawfullest thing in the Fat Lamb.' He sets the dish down gently, and wipes the knife again, though it is clean.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, last_inch). }
  }

  // ── Doctor Ploughwright and the Veyran ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic ploughwright_veyra with ploughwright "Ask Doctor Ploughwright where the Faculty had its Determinations from" when true once {
    Says "'From Veyra, in the north, which teaches.' He says it as a man names a poor relation. 'A chapel and a school, and a Grand Tour of its own that goes round the whole country asking to be told things.' He stiffens by a degree. 'We do not need to be taught in Gaunt. We are told. Once a generation a Veyran comes down the fell road with a notebook and asks to see the Register's first book. The Lady Penitentiary shows him the first line. He asks to see the second. The Lady Penitentiary tells him that there is no second.' Doctor Ploughwright smooths his hood. 'He goes home, I understand, very thoughtful.'".
  }

  // ── The contrast: the chestnut man, the indulgence, and the Fat King in Bow Gate ──────────────────────────────────
  // A grave adventure, one scene of plain comedy. It is also the satire in one image: a man selling hot chestnuts and
  // indulgences from the same brazier, and a paper that is good in exactly the street he stands in.
  Person hodge "Hodge Peasegood" at shambles {
    Role "a man with a brazier of chestnuts in one hand and a stack of printed indulgences under the other arm". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "'Hot!' cries Hodge Peasegood, to nobody, to everybody. 'Hot chestnuts! Hot indulgences! A penny the pair!' He lowers his voice to the pitch of a confidence. 'You'll be wanting both. Everybody wants both. It is the Shambles. We have a feeling for it.'".
    Greets again "Hodge Peasegood waves a chestnut at you like a man blessing a crowd, and then, seeing who you are, hides the indulgences under his arm and offers you only the chestnut. 'The other business is a two-time price,' he says. 'First sin, full rate. Second sin, loyalty discount.'".
  }
  Kind gaunt_chestnuts "a paper of hot chestnuts" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "Twelve chestnuts in a twist of printed paper, hot enough to hold in a pocket against the cold.".
  Item chestnuts "a paper of hot chestnuts" is gaunt_chestnuts at limbo.
  Kind gaunt_indulgence "a printed indulgence" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 described "A handbill, thumb-black, in two colours: GOOD FOR ONE PAIN. SEE OVERLEAF. On the back, in smaller type: VALID IN THE SHAMBLES, BETWEEN BOW GATE AND THE BEARER'S STEPS, FOR THE DAY OF PURCHASE. NOT TO BE PRESENTED AT THE CLOSE.".
  Item indulgence "a printed indulgence" is gaunt_indulgence at limbo.
  Topic hodge_trade with hodge "Ask Hodge Peasegood how an indulgence differs from a chestnut" when true once {
    Says "'The chestnut,' says Hodge, with the patience of a man explaining the sea, 'you eat. The indulgence you hold. They are both warm when you buy them.' He turns a handbill in the brazier's light. 'The Penitentiary has a price for the pain, a shilling. The Stand has a price for the proxy, a shilling. I have a price for the paper, a halfpenny, and I do not pretend it is a pain. It is a feeling. It is the feeling of having done something at the right end of the street.' He eats a chestnut. 'It is the only honest article in the Commerce. I have never once been assessed.'".
  }
  Topic hodge_buy with hodge "Buy a paper of hot chestnuts and an indulgence, a penny the pair" when quantity(actor, gold) >= 1 and not hodgeSold(hodge) once {
    Says "He fishes the penny out of your palm as if it were a coal. 'There.' He puts the chestnuts in your hands and the handbill on top of them. 'Read the back,' says Hodge Peasegood.".
    On discuss { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Give chestnuts to actor. Give indulgence to actor. Assert hodgeSold(hodge). }
  }
  Relation hodgeSold(group).
  Observe fat_king_stuck at shambles when licence() "At the foot of Bow Gate the Fat King has stuck. The giant's belly, being a barrel, has jammed in the arch, and eight apprentices on the door beneath him are conducting an argument about whether to take his head off or put his belly on a diet. The crowd is giving advice. The Fat King, from above, with his pig's face fixed in a smile, is saying nothing at all.".

  // ── The Rector at Sennet ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Read only in a world where the Watch of the House of Doors has taken up its Rector.
  Observe rector_letter at penitentiary when befell(rector_taken) and not masked(hawise) "On the corner of the Lady Penitentiary's desk, under an ink-pot in the shape of a key, lies a letter from a brother house on the coast, opened and not flattened, that a clerk has been told not to read aloud: that at Sennet the Watch has taken up the Rector of the House of Doors, and that his keys, every one of them, are being counted before a magistrate. Dame Hawise has read it twice. She has put the ink-pot on it, and she is not looking at it.".

  // ── The Gate of Ash, for those who went looking ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe ash_loop at gate_of_ash when gateOfAshOpen() and knows(party, first_leaf) "A serjeant works the old lock with the Penitentiary's billet of keys, and as the ring swings in his hand you count them without meaning to: thirty-one. At the end of the ring, where a thirty-second would hang, there is a bare loop of iron, worn bright by a thumb.".
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/stand.ky:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── The Fat Lamb ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person landlord "Matthias Dent" at fat_lamb {
    Role "the landlord of the Fat Lamb, in a leather apron, carving". Profession innkeeper. Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "The landlord points his carving knife at the ox. 'Eat,' he says. 'Eat now. On Wednesday it's fish and the Fast till Easter, and the Penitentiary sends a man round to look in the pots.'".
    Sells rations for 2 coin from 12.
  }
  // ── The Stand ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The old sheep-market, where proxies are hired. Nobody here is sorry for anything, and all of them are working.
  Person clerk "the Stand's clerk" at the_stand {
    Role "a clerk in fingerless gloves at a high desk at the Stand's gate, with a ledger of backs and a box of tallies". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "'Bearing or buying?' says the clerk, pen up. 'If buying, what is it and how many; if bearing, show me your feet.'".
    Greets again "'Bearing or buying?' says the clerk, pen up, and then, recognising you, writes your name in the margin, where it will be mistaken for a correction. 'Rates have changed since you were in. They go up on Ash Eve. I would buy today.'".
  }
  Topic clerk_rates with clerk "Ask the clerk how the Stand works" when true once {
    Says "'Simplest thing in Gaunt.' He taps the board. 'Somebody does a fault. The Penitentiary prices it. They come here with the tally. I find them a back; the back does it; the back gets paid; the Penitentiary gets its tithe; the Fabric gets a tithe of the tithe; the tower goes up.' He considers. 'The tower doesn't go up, as it happens. But that's the masons.' He leans down. 'Busiest week of the year, this. Everybody wants to be clean for Ash Day, when the Ladder's gilded. If you've a back to sell, I can sell it twice before Wednesday.'".
  }

  // ── Bearing for others: proxy work, paid in coin ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation boreFor(group, group).
  Action bear_dinsdale(actor: group, site: place) "Bear a day's fast for Mistress Dinsdale, the brewster, three shillings" {
    Description "Nothing to eat until tomorrow, for a brewster's sins, which are mostly in her measures.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_stand) and daytime() and not fastToday(actor) and not boreFor(actor, dinsdale) and not struck(barefoot).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert boreFor(actor, dinsdale). Assert fastToday(actor). Set fastedOn(actor) to dayN(gaunt_town). Assert hungry(actor). Set nextMeal(actor) to watch(clock) + 144.
      Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Assert knows(actor, dinsdale_hiring). }
    Result "The clerk writes you down against DINSDALE, G., BREWSTER, SHORT MEASURE (4 PAINS), and gives you three shillings and a little lead token stamped with a barrel to show anyone who offers you a pie. 'She's hiring,' he says. 'Hiring and hiring. She wants to be clean for the gilding, and to be cleaner than Sowerby. Between you and me there's not enough sin in that brewhouse to keep a dozen proxies busy, so she's started paying us to fast for things she means to do next week.'".
  }
  Discovery dinsdale_hiring "Mistress Grizel Dinsdale, the brewster, is hiring proxies by the dozen to be clean for the gilding of the Ladder on Ash Day, and cleaner than Master Sowerby; she is paying in advance for faults she has not yet done.".
  Action bear_sowerby(actor: group, site: place) "Walk a barefoot mile round the walls for Master Sowerby, the draper, two shillings" {
    Description "Boots off, and a board on your back with his fault on it.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_stand) and daytime() and not boreFor(actor, sowerby) and not struck(barefoot).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert boreFor(actor, sowerby). Assert strikes(barefoot_mile, actor). Assert walkedBarefoot(actor). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 2. }
    Result "The board says SOWERBY, P., DRAPER, A FALSE ELL (1 PAIN), and you carry it barefoot once round the inside of the new wall on the frozen setts, past the Row, where the people in the doorways with their feet in bowls watch you go by with the professional interest of carpenters watching a man saw. At the Gate of Ash an old woman calls out, 'Lift your feet, love, you're not ploughing,' and the whole Row laughs, kindly. Two shillings, at the end, and your feet are somebody else's.".
  }
  Action bear_alderman(actor: group, site: place) "Kneel a night's vigil on the Bearer's Steps for an alderman's son, five shillings" {
    Description "From dusk to first light, on the stone. The son was sick in the font at a christening.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, close_gate_street) and nightfall() and not licence() and not boreFor(actor, clerk) and not struck(barefoot).
    Time 36.
    On success { Assert boreFor(actor, clerk). Assert strikes(steps_cold, actor). Assert keptStepVigil(actor). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 5. }
    Result "The board round your neck says ROPER, G. (THE YOUNGER), PROFANATION OF A FONT, and you kneel all night on the Bearer's Steps under it in the cold. At two in the morning a young man in a good cloak comes up the Shambles from the Fat Lamb, singing, and stops, and reads the board, and laughs until he has to hold the rail, and goes on up and in at the Close Gate, where the porter lets him through without a tally. At first light the clerk comes with five shillings. 'Gideon Roper's boy,' he says. 'Good family.'".
  }

  // ── The Ladder ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Mistress Grizel Dinsdale and Master Pentecost Sowerby are level on the second rung, and the Ladder is gilded at nine
  // on Ash Day for the year. A company carrying news between them can raise the stakes until one of them hires the
  // whole Stand for Ash Day, which leaves no back in Gaunt for anybody else.
  Person dinsdale "Mistress Grizel Dinsdale" at dinsdale_brewhouse {
    Role "a brewster in a velvet bonnet at a high desk, doing sums of penance and of beer in two columns" when not dinsdaleWalked(dinsdale).
    Role "a brewster in a velvet bonnet and no shoes, with her chin up" when dinsdaleWalked(dinsdale). Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner proud.
    Greets "Mistress Dinsdale sizes you up as if estimating your capacity in gallons. 'If it's about the measures,' she says, 'they're paid for. Forty fasts, in advance. I could give short measure till Michaelmas and still be owed.'".
    Greets again "'Well?' says Mistress Dinsdale, not looking up from her columns. 'Have you come to tell me the measures are short, or to tell me they are long? Either way, I will say it was the cooper.'".
  }
  Person sowerby "Master Pentecost Sowerby" at sowerby_shop {
    Role "a draper with a measuring-rod he holds like a sceptre, and the look of a man who has been second for eleven years" when not sowerbyWalked(sowerby).
    Role "a draper with his feet in a bowl of warm water, looking surprised at himself" when sowerbyWalked(sowerby). Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "Master Sowerby comes round the counter with both hands out. 'A customer! Or a proxy? Either is welcome; the second more so, this week.' He lowers his voice. 'Eleven years second. Eleven. Behind Thackray I don't mind, Thackray's a saint. Behind a brewster.'".
    Greets again "Master Sowerby beams at you over the broadcloth, and then, with the air of a man trying a new phrase, says, 'Eleven years second.' He tries it again. 'I said it aloud and nothing fell. I think I am a little different.'".
  }
  Relation sowerbyRaised(group). Relation standCornered(group). Relation ladderExposed(group).
  Relation sowerbyWalked(group). Relation dinsdaleWalked(group).
  Topic dinsdale_ladder with dinsdale "Ask Mistress Dinsdale about the Ladder" when true once {
    Says "'Second rung,' says Mistress Dinsdale, 'and on Ash Day it'll be gilded, and it'll stay gilded the year, and it'll say DINSDALE, and not that draper.' She turns a page of her columns. 'He hires by the day. I hire by the dozen. He's a man who thinks penance is a matter of feeling.' She makes a note. 'It's a matter of volume.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, dinsdale_hiring). }
  }
  Topic sowerby_told with sowerby "Tell Master Sowerby that Mistress Dinsdale is hiring proxies by the dozen for the gilding" when knows(actor, dinsdale_hiring) and not sowerbyRaised(sowerby) once {
    Says "Master Sowerby goes the colour of one of his own bolts, a good scarlet. 'By the dozen.' He lays the measuring-rod down very gently on the counter. 'Then I shall hire by the score.' He takes a purse out of the till and shakes it. 'Two to fast, and two to walk, every day until Wednesday. And a vigil every night on the Steps.' He looks at you. 'You'd not want work? No? I'd pay double. I'd pay you to tell her.'".
    On discuss { Assert sowerbyRaised(sowerby). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 2. }
  }
  Topic dinsdale_told with dinsdale "Tell Mistress Dinsdale that Master Sowerby has hired by the score" when sowerbyRaised(sowerby) and not standCornered(dinsdale) once {
    Says "Mistress Dinsdale puts down her pen. For a moment she does nothing at all. Then she rings a bell, and a boy comes, and she writes a note and blots it and folds it. 'To the Stand's clerk,' she says. 'Every back he has, for Ash Day, from first light. Every one. At his price.' The boy goes. She picks up her pen again. 'Let the draper do his own penance,' she says, 'if he can find anybody to do it.'".
    On discuss { Assert standCornered(dinsdale). }
  }
  Discovery stand_cornered "Mistress Dinsdale has hired every proxy at the Stand for Ash Day, from first light, so that no one else in Gaunt can hire one.".
  Rule cornered_known when standCornered(dinsdale) and not knows(party, stand_cornered) says "By evening the whole Middle Town knows: Mistress Dinsdale has bought every back at the Stand for Ash Day." teaches stand_cornered { }
  // Ash Day morning: with no back to be had, the loser walks; if the Row is out, both do.
  Rule sowerby_walks when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 8 and standCornered(dinsdale) and not sowerbyWalked(sowerby) { Assert sowerbyWalked(sowerby). Assert at(sowerby, minster_porch). }
  Rule dinsdale_walks when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 8 and struck(barefoot) and not dinsdaleWalked(dinsdale) { Assert dinsdaleWalked(dinsdale). Assert at(dinsdale, minster_porch). }
  Rule sowerby_told_walking when sowerbyWalked(sowerby) and not struck(barefoot) and inTown() and ashDay() and hour(clock) < 12 and not spread(sowerby_walking)
    says "At eight on Ash Day morning the Middle Town comes out of its doors to see a thing nobody has seen in eleven years: a burgess of Gaunt doing his own penance. Master Pentecost Sowerby, draper, second on the Ladder, comes up the Shambles barefoot on the frozen setts in his shirt, with a board round his neck in his own hand, A FALSE ELL, and his measuring-rod for a staff, very slowly, and white, and weeping a little with the cold. Nobody laughs. Somebody, after a while, takes off their hat. By the time he gets to the Bearer's Steps there are two hundred people walking behind him, quietly, as if it were a funeral, or a wedding." { Assert spread(sowerby_walking). }
  Entity sowerby_walking: fact "Sowerby walks".
  Topic sowerby_after with sowerby "Ask Master Sowerby how it was" when sowerbyWalked(sowerby) once {
    Says "Master Sowerby sits on the step of the Minster porch with his feet in a bowl that somebody has brought him, and his face is a strange colour, and he is smiling. 'Cold,' he says. 'Very cold. A false ell, it was. Seven years ago. A widow's bolt of black.' He looks at his feet in the water. 'I'd forgotten it. I'd paid for it, so I'd forgotten it.' He looks up at you. 'It was mine,' he says, wonderingly. 'Do you see? It was mine. It's the first time it was.'".
    On discuss { Assert sowerbyChanged(sowerby). }
  }
  Relation sowerbyChanged(group).
  Observe sowerby_porch at minster_porch when sowerbyWalked(sowerby) and ashDay() "Master Sowerby sits on the step of the porch under the Ladder, barefoot, with his feet in a bowl of warm water, and people keep stopping to look at him as if he were a relic.".
  Observe dinsdale_porch at minster_porch when dinsdaleWalked(dinsdale) and ashDay() "Mistress Dinsdale, in her velvet bonnet and no shoes, stands in the porch under the Ladder with her chin up, daring anyone to say anything, and nobody does.".

  // ── Abel Lumb ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A young proxy who has fasted eleven days for a widow's impure thoughts, and is fainting at the Stand.
  Person abel "Abel Lumb" at the_stand {
    Role "a long, gangly young proxy, very pale, in a pen with a board that says FASTS" when not abelFed(abel).
    Role "a long, gangly young man with colour in his face for the first time in a fortnight" when abelFed(abel).
    Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "The young man in the pen says, 'Fasts, threepence a day, I'm the best in the Stand for fasts, I don't feel it any more,' all in one breath, and sways a little.".
    Greets again "Abel Lumb smiles at you weakly over the hurdle. He has been fed, you can see, but not for long enough to believe it. 'Threepence a day,' he says. 'Best in the Stand. I do not feel it. I would like to feel it. Is that a thing one asks for?'".
  }
  Relation abelFainted(group). Relation abelFed(group).
  Rule abel_routine_stand when daytime() and not at(abel, the_stand) and not abelAway(abel) and not licence() and not following(abel, party) { Assert at(abel, the_stand). }
  Rule abel_routine_hall when not daytime() and not at(abel, barefoot_hall) and not abelAway(abel) and not licence() and not following(abel, party) { Assert at(abel, barefoot_hall). }
  Relation abelAway(group).
  Rule abel_faints at the_stand when mondayN() and hour(clock) >= 16 and not abelFainted(abel) and not abelFed(abel) and at(party, the_stand)
    says "In his pen Abel Lumb sits down quite suddenly in the straw, as if someone had cut his strings, and lies there looking at the sky with a puzzled expression. The clerk says 'Oh, not again,' and two proxies lift him up and pour broth into him, which he tries to refuse. 'I'm fasting,' he says. 'It's paid.'" { Assert abelFainted(abel). }
  Rule abel_faints_away when mondayN() and hour(clock) >= 16 and not abelFainted(abel) and not abelFed(abel) and not at(party, the_stand) { Assert abelFainted(abel). }
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/thackray:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── Whose forty nights ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Hugh Thackray, Wood-reeve, holds the Bishop's licence for firewood and sits for the Guildhall on the Consistory. In
  // the great frost last winter he held back wood to raise the price, and forty-one people froze in the Row. No law calls
  // that a crime. He went to the Penitentiary and confessed it as blood; they set it at forty nights cold; he paid,
  // and Hern refused it, and the Scaifes took it. He is genuinely sorry. He has not lowered the price. Knowing who he is
  // opens a door to him; it does not move him. He is moved by people: by Annis Scaife to his face, by one night of his
  // own vigil, by his cousin's laughter, by a children's rhyme.
  Person thackray "Alderman Hugh Thackray" at wood_exchange {
    Role "the Wood-reeve: a big soft man in a fur-lined gown, with a kind face and the look of someone who has not slept in a year" when not nightAtCarth(thackray).
    Role "the Wood-reeve, a big soft man in a fur-lined gown, grey in the face, who has not been warm since yesterday" when nightAtCarth(thackray).
    Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "The big man in the fur-lined gown turns to you with real pleasure. 'A stranger! Welcome to Gaunt. Have you somewhere warm? You must have somewhere warm.' He presses your hand. 'Wood is dear this winter, I'm afraid. Wood is always dear in a hard winter. It's a law of nature,' he says, and then looks as if he wished he had not.".
    Greets again "Alderman Thackray turns from the scales and smiles at you, kindly, tiredly, and, for once, says nothing about wood. He weighs a billet in his hand and sets it down. 'I am told the city talks of me,' he says. 'It is being done very courteously. I find I admire that, which I did not expect.'".
  }
  Discovery thackray_vigil "Alderman Hugh Thackray, the Wood-reeve, bought the Cold Vigil at Carth: forty nights, one for each of the forty-one who froze in the Row last winter when he held back wood to raise its price. He is sorry. He has not lowered the price.".
  Discovery reeve_to_thackray "Raistrick, the Ash-reeve, reports each morning at ten at the Wood Exchange, to Alderman Thackray.".
  Measure thackrayMoved(group).
  Relation annisSaid(group). Relation nightAtCarth(group). Relation verseToThackray(group). Relation thackrayNightDue(group).
  Query thackrayChanged() means thackrayMoved(thackray) >= 2.
  Relation woodOpened(group). Relation thackrayWillBear(group). Relation scaifesPaid(group).

  // His day: the Exchange from nine; on Shrove Monday morning, the fell road, alone, to look at a chimney.
  Relation onFell(group).
  Rule thackray_rides when mondayN() and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 11 and not snowing() and not onFell(thackray) and not nightAtCarth(thackray) and not spread(thackray_rode) { Assert onFell(thackray). Assert at(thackray, carth_yard). Assert spread(thackray_rode). }
  Entity thackray_rode: fact "Thackray on the fell".
  Rule thackray_back when onFell(thackray) and hour(clock) >= 11 { Retract onFell(thackray). Assert at(thackray, wood_exchange). }
  Rule thackray_exchange when daytime() and not onFell(thackray) and not at(thackray, wood_exchange) and not thackrayAway(thackray) and not sitting() { Assert at(thackray, wood_exchange). }
  Rule thackray_evening when not daytime() and at(thackray, wood_exchange) and not thackrayAway(thackray) { Assert at(thackray, limbo). }
  Relation thackrayAway(group).
  Observe thackray_on_fell at carth_yard when onFell(thackray) "At the yard gate, on a grey cob up to its hocks in the snow, sits a big man in a fur-lined gown, looking at the chimney of the house. Just looking at it. He has a face like a kind uncle's, and he has been crying.".
  Topic thackray_fell with thackray "Ask the man on the grey cob what brings him up the fell" when onFell(thackray) and not knows(actor, thackray_vigil) once {
    Says "The big man starts, and wipes his face with a fur cuff. 'Riding,' he says. 'For my health. The physicians say riding.' He looks at the chimney again. 'Nobody's smoke,' he says, to himself. Then, to you, too brightly: 'A hard winter. A very hard winter. One does what one can.' He turns the cob's head for Gaunt.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, thackray_rides_out). }
  }
  Discovery thackray_rides_out "A big man in a fur-lined gown rode up the fell on Shrove Monday morning to look at the chimney at Carth, and wept.".
  // Raistrick's report at ten, seen.
  Rule reeve_reports_in when (mondayN() or eveDay() or ashDay()) and hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) < 11 and vigilOn() and morningDue(carth_vigil) and not at(raistrick, wood_exchange) and not reeveKneeling(raistrick) { Assert at(raistrick, wood_exchange). }
  Rule reeve_reports_out when hour(clock) >= 11 and at(raistrick, wood_exchange) { Assert at(raistrick, reeve_hut). }
  Observe reeve_seen at wood_exchange when at(raistrick, wood_exchange) and at(thackray, wood_exchange) "Through the door behind the scales you see the Ash-reeve, Raistrick, snow on his sheepskin, standing in front of Alderman Thackray's desk, saying one word, which you do not hear; and the big man nodding, and nodding, and putting his face in his hands." teaches reeve_to_thackray.
  Observe vigil_book at wood_exchange when vigilBroken(carth_vigil) and at(thackray, wood_exchange) and not vigilReleased(carth_vigil) "On the Wood-reeve's desk, behind the scales, a short notched stick lies by itself, cut through.".
  Topic thackray_ask with thackray "Ask Alderman Thackray whose forty nights are being kept at Carth" when not knows(actor, thackray_vigil)
    and (knows(actor, reeve_to_thackray) or knows(actor, billet_known) or knows(actor, thackray_rides_out) and knows(actor, thackray_strange)) once {
    Says "Alderman Thackray does not pretend. That is the first surprising thing about him. He sits down on a sack of charcoal, in his fur gown, and looks at his hands. 'Mine,' he says. 'Last winter, in the great frost, I held the oak back from the Exchange a fortnight to bring the price up. Everybody does. It's the market.' He turns his hands over. 'Forty-one in the Row. The Barefoot Hall has their pegs on the wall. I went to see them, the pegs.' He looks up. 'I went to the Penitentiary and confessed it as blood, which it isn't, in law. Dame Hawise set it at forty nights cold. I paid. Barefoot Hern wouldn't keep it. A farm took it.' He is quiet. 'I'm sorry. I'm sorrier than I have ever been. I'd give anything.' Then, because he is an honest man: 'I haven't lowered the price. You can't, in a hard winter. The market won't bear it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, thackray_vigil). }
  }
  // Annis Scaife to his face, at her own gate.
  Action fetch_annis(actor: group, site: place) "Fetch Annis Scaife out to the man at the gate" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, carth_yard) and onFell(thackray) and at(annis, house_place)
      and (knows(actor, billet_coin) or knows(actor, thackray_vigil)) and not annisSaid(thackray).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert annisSaid(thackray). Increase thackrayMoved(thackray) by 1. Assert knows(actor, thackray_vigil). Assert knows(actor, ellen_wray). }
    Result "Annis Scaife comes out into the yard in her shawl, and looks at the man on the grey cob, and at his gown, and his gloves, and his face; and you see her know him. She has known his mark since Candlemas. She does not shout. She walks up to the cob's shoulder, in the snow to her knees, and says, up to him: 'It's cold.' That is all. He looks down at her. 'I know,' he says. 'No,' says Annis Scaife, 'you don't. It's cold. In there. Twenty-four nights. My father-in-law's in the byre in his Sunday coat waiting for the ground. My girl's got a cough. My sister's on your wall in the Row: Ellen Wray, the thirtieth peg. It's cold.' She turns round and goes back into the house and shuts the door, and the big man sits his horse in the yard with the tears running into his fur collar until the dog loses interest, and then rides away down the fell without a word.".
  }
  Topic thackray_annis_city with thackray "Tell Alderman Thackray what Annis Scaife said: it's cold" when knows(actor, thackray_vigil) and stayingAtCarth(actor) and not annisSaid(thackray) and not onFell(thackray) once {
    Says "You tell him: the dark, the hearth, the child's cough, the old man in the byre, the old woman lying down with him. He listens with his eyes shut. When you have finished he says, 'Thank you,' as if you had handed him a bill, and pays it.".
    On discuss { Assert annisSaid(thackray). Increase thackrayMoved(thackray) by 1. }
  }
  // The thirtieth peg: whose penance it is, and who is keeping it.
  Relation ellenToThackray(group).
  Topic thackray_ellen with thackray "Tell Alderman Thackray whose sister hangs on the thirtieth peg" when knows(actor, ellen_wray) and knows(actor, thackray_vigil) and not annisSaid(thackray) and not ellenToThackray(thackray) and not onFell(thackray) once {
    Says "'The thirtieth,' he says. He knows the pegs; he went to look at them. 'Wray. Ellen Wray, from the fell.' Then he understands it, and you watch it go into him the way the cold goes into a house, from the floor up. 'Her sister,' he says. 'And she took my forty nights.' He puts his soft hands over his face. 'She's keeping my penance for her own sister's death, at two shillings a night, and I paid it.' After a while: 'Why would she do that?' And then, before you can answer, because he is not a stupid man: 'So that it's kept by somebody who knows.'".
    On discuss { Assert ellenToThackray(thackray). Increase thackrayMoved(thackray) by 1. }
  }
  // One night of his own.
  Topic thackray_night with thackray "Ask Alderman Thackray to keep one night of his forty himself, at Carth, at the cold hearth" when knows(actor, thackray_vigil) and vigilOn() and not nightAtCarth(thackray) and not thackrayNightDue(thackray) and not onFell(thackray) once {
    Says "He looks at you as if you had suggested he fly. 'Myself,' he says. 'It's bought. It's paid. It's—' He stops. He looks at his fur cuffs. 'They'd let me in? The Scaifes?' Then, slowly: 'Nobody ever does it themselves. It isn't done. That's the whole—' He stops again. He takes off his gloves, and looks at his hands, which are soft. 'Tonight,' he says. 'Tonight. Before I think about it.'".
    On discuss { Assert thackrayNightDue(thackray). }
  }
  Rule thackray_to_carth when thackrayNightDue(thackray) and hour(clock) >= 20 and not nightAtCarth(thackray) and not at(thackray, house_place) { Assert thackrayAway(thackray). Assert at(thackray, house_place). }
  Rule thackray_kept_night at house_place when thackrayNightDue(thackray) and at(thackray, house_place) and hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 12 and not nightAtCarth(thackray) {
    Assert nightAtCarth(thackray). Increase thackrayMoved(thackray) by 1. Retract thackrayAway(thackray). Assert at(thackray, wood_exchange). Retract thackrayNightDue(thackray). }
  Rule thackray_night_seen at house_place when thackrayNightDue(thackray) and at(thackray, house_place) and at(party, house_place) and smallHours() and not spread(thackray_night_seen)
    says "In the dark, by the dead hearth, someone large is sitting on the floor with his back to the wall where you sat, breathing in short hard breaths through his nose. At three the latch lifts and the Ash-reeve comes in and kneels and puts his hand in the ash, and the large man by the wall makes a small sound, and Raistrick turns his head toward it and says, very quietly, 'Alderman,' and nothing else, and goes." { Assert spread(thackray_night_seen). }
  Entity thackray_night_seen: fact "Thackray at Carth by night".
  Topic thackray_after_night with thackray "Ask Alderman Thackray about his night at Carth" when nightAtCarth(thackray) once {
    Says "He is grey, and his voice has gone, and he has not taken off his gloves. 'I couldn't feel my feet by midnight,' he says. 'By two I couldn't think. There's a child coughs all night. There's a man in the byre.' He holds his hands to the brazier and they shake. 'Forty-one,' he says. 'One night, and I thought I'd die of it, and I've a fur gown.' He looks at you. 'I'm not sorry any more. I don't know what I am. Sorry was warm.'".
  }
  Topic thackray_verse with thackray "Tell Alderman Thackray the second verse of the children's rhyme" when knows(actor, second_verse) and knows(actor, thackray_vigil) and not verseToThackray(thackray) once {
    Says "You say it to him, the children's rhyme off the Row ditch: Oswy, Oswy, up the hill, carry me and carry me still. At the top he set him down: NOW WALK, said Oswy. Thackray says it after you, under his breath, twice. 'Now walk,' he says. 'He carried him all the way up, and then put him down, and said, now walk.' He sits very still. 'I've been carried,' he says. 'I've been carried all my life.'".
    On discuss { Assert verseToThackray(thackray). Increase thackrayMoved(thackray) by 1. }
  }
  Rule joan_moves_him when joanLaughed(thackray) and not spread(joan_moved) { Increase thackrayMoved(thackray) by 1. Assert spread(joan_moved). }
  Entity joan_moved: fact "Joan laughed".
  Observe joan_at_exchange at wood_exchange when joanLaughed(thackray) and at(thackray, wood_exchange) "Mistress Pickersgill has been to the Wood Exchange. The whole of the Middle Town knows it, because she laughed at her cousin in front of the scales for a quarter of an hour, with a young man from the Stand standing behind her eating a pie; and at the end of it, the clerks say, the Wood-reeve laughed too, and then sat down on the charcoal and cried.".

  // Moved, he acts.
  Topic thackray_release with thackray "Ask Alderman Thackray to release the Carth vigil, and pay the Scaifes in full" when thackrayChanged() and not vigilReleased(carth_vigil) and not scaifesPaid(carth_vigil) once {
    Says "'Yes,' he says at once, as if he had been waiting all winter for somebody to ask. He writes, on the Exchange's paper, in a big untidy hand: the Carth vigil released by the purchaser, the forty nights paid in full to the keepers, and a cart of oak to go up the fell today. He sands it, and seals it with the billet. 'Raistrick will take it up,' he says. 'He'll be glad. He never liked that one.'".
    On discuss { Assert vigilReleased(carth_vigil). Assert scaifesPaid(carth_vigil). }
  }
  Topic thackray_wood with thackray "Ask Alderman Thackray to open the dead-wood right in the Bishop's Wood" when thackrayChanged() and not woodOpened(thackray) once {
    Says "Thackray looks at the price-board for a long time, and at the clerk writing it up a shilling with his chalk held between two fingers. 'The dead wood,' he says. 'That was always theirs, the Row's. I shut it because it brought the price down.' He gets up, and takes the chalk out of the clerk's fingers, and goes and rubs out OAK, THE CORD, 30S with his sleeve, which is fur, and writes nothing in its place. 'Open the right,' he tells the clerk. 'Today. Send to the woodmen. And send to the Barefoot Hall, to Bess Ackroyd, and tell her it's open, and tell her—' he stops. 'Tell her nothing. Tell her it's open.'".
    On discuss { Assert woodOpened(thackray). }
  }
  Topic thackray_bear with thackray "Ask Alderman Thackray whether he would bear Ninian Hern's sentence" when thackrayChanged() and knows(actor, sentence_borne) and not thackrayWillBear(thackray) and not hernFled(hern) and not hernDead(hern) once {
    Says "He does not answer for so long that you think he has not understood. Then he says, 'Put out. Walked through the Gate of Ash at dusk with nothing.' He looks at his gown. 'He refused my forty nights, Hern. He was the only man in Gaunt who told me what they were for.' He stands up. 'If the Consistory will have it,' he says, 'yes. I'll walk.' He smiles, a little, for the first time. 'Now walk,' he says. 'I'll tell them at the trial. I sit on it, after all.'".
    On discuss { Assert thackrayWillBear(thackray). }
  }
  // Released, the vigil's coin reaches Carth, and the fire is lit there; told to a company that is there or comes.
  Observe released_yard at carth_yard when vigilReleased(carth_vigil) "There is a cart in the yard at Carth with a load of oak on it, half unloaded, and a woodman eating his dinner on the shafts.".
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/tower.ky:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── The unfinished tower ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The north tower has stood unfinished since the year the Commerce began, because the Fabric's fees are the
  // Commerce's tithe, and the day the tower is finished the Fabric has no reason to take them. Old Joby Thwaite, master
  // mason, seventy-one, sets its last course by day; by night Canon Hamo Laverock, Master of the Fabric, has his men take
  // it down. Joby does not know why it never rises. Laverock is also the Scaifes' landlord, and the Consistory's
  // prosecutor.
  Person joby "Old Joby Thwaite" at fat_lamb {
    Role "a master mason of seventy-one with stone-dust in his eyebrows and hands like two mallets, eating a pie with great concentration". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "The old man with the stone-dust eyebrows points at the bench opposite with his pie. 'Sit,' he says. 'You've a look of somebody who's seen the north tower. Everybody gets that look.' He chews. 'Fifty-three years I've been setting the last course on it. Fifty-three. I'm the only man alive who's seen it with all four corners level.' He chews. 'Tuesday week, that was.'".
    Greets again "Joby Thwaite waves the pie, which is a different pie, but held at the same angle. 'The north tower,' he says. 'Fifty-two years I have been on it, and I've never been up it. That is the sort of thing you can say in a pie shop and be thought modest.'".
  }
  // His day: the tower by day, the Fat Lamb at noon and in the evening.
  Rule joby_tower when daytime() and not (hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 13) and not at(joby, tower_foot) and not jobyGuards(joby) { Assert at(joby, tower_foot). }
  Rule joby_dinner when hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 13 and not at(joby, fat_lamb) and not jobyGuards(joby) { Assert at(joby, fat_lamb). }
  Rule joby_evening when hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 22 and not at(joby, fat_lamb) and not jobyGuards(joby) { Assert at(joby, fat_lamb). }
  Rule joby_bed when (hour(clock) >= 22 or hour(clock) < 7) and not at(joby, masons_lodge) and not jobyGuards(joby) { Assert at(joby, masons_lodge). }
  Relation jobyKnows(group). Relation jobyLeave(group). Relation jobyGuards(group). Relation courseSet(group).
  Topic joby_tower with joby "Ask Joby Thwaite why the north tower is never finished" when not jobyKnows(joby) once {
    Says "'Frost,' says Joby. 'The Master of the Fabric says frost. You set a course, and the frost gets in the mortar overnight, and in the morning it's spalled, and you've to take it down and set it again.' He finishes his pie and looks at the crust. 'Fifty-three years I've been a mason, and I never saw frost do it in a night anywhere but here.' He brushes his hands. 'I'd a lad once who said it wasn't frost. Said it in here, drunk, at that table. They put him out of the Gate of Ash for it.' He turns the crust over. 'Laverock says it's the tower. It's a holy tower. It's humble. It doesn't want to be finished.' He looks at you. 'I'd like to see it finished,' he says, simply, 'before I'm humble.'".
  }
  Initially Assert teachesAt(unbuilding, gaol_lane). Initially Assert teachesAt(unbuilding, tower_foot).
  Discovery unbuilding "By night, by lantern, Canon Laverock's men take down the course of stone Joby Thwaite's masons set on the north tower by day: the tower is kept unfinished on purpose.".
  Observe unbuilt_seen at tower_foot when (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 4) and not seenOnce(unbuilding) "Up on the scaffold, at the top platform, by the light of a horn lantern, three men in the Fabric's brown are taking today's course of white stone down, one block at a time, with a crowbar and a rope and a great deal of care, and lowering it on the pulley to the ground, where a fourth man stacks it with the others, quietly, under a tarpaulin. One of them says something and another laughs, softly. Below them, in the shadow of the lodge door, a canon in a fur tippet is watching, with his hands in his sleeves." teaches unbuilding.
  Observe unbuilt_lane at gaol_lane when (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 4) and not seenOnce(unbuilding) "Over the Close wall you can see the top of the north tower's scaffold, and on the top platform, by the light of a horn lantern, men in brown taking the day's new stone down, block by block, very carefully, and lowering it on a rope; a canon in a fur tippet watching from below with his hands in his sleeves." teaches unbuilding.
  Topic joby_told with joby "Tell Joby Thwaite what you have seen on the scaffold at night" when knows(actor, unbuilding) and not jobyKnows(joby) once {
    Says "Joby Thwaite puts down his pie. He sits with his big hands flat on the table until the pie goes cold. 'Frost,' he says at last. 'Fifty-three years.' And then, much more quietly: 'Cuthbert.' He does not shout; masons do not. He stands up, very slowly, as a wall stands up. 'Fastens' Eve,' he says. 'We'll set it in the morning, and we'll sit up with it at night, the lodge, all of us, with our mallets. Let them come with their crowbar.' He looks at you. 'You'll come and sit with us. The lodge door's open to you, now, the yard door off the Steps. Any time. Tell the lads Joby said.'".
    On discuss { Assert jobyKnows(joby). Assert jobyLeave(party). }
  }
  Topic joby_fold with joby "Tell Joby Thwaite that his son is alive, in the put-outs' fold on the Levels" when jobyKnows(joby) and knows(actor, cuthbert_story) and not jobyToFold(joby) once {
    Says "Joby Thwaite holds the last of his pie and does not eat it. 'Alive,' he says. 'Out there.' He turns his head as if he could see through the wall of the Fat Lamb and both the walls of the city to the Levels. 'Nineteen years. I could have walked it in an hour.' He puts the pie down. 'Ash Day,' he says. 'When the course is set and stood. I'll take him a lantern. He'll know what it means.'".
    On discuss { Assert jobyToFold(joby). }
  }
  // Fastens' Eve: the masons sit up with the stone; whoever sits with them sees the Fabric's men come and go away.
  Rule masons_guard when jobyKnows(joby) and eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 20 and not jobyGuards(joby) { Assert jobyGuards(joby). Assert at(joby, tower_foot). }
  Rule masons_stand when jobyGuards(joby) and ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 6 and not courseSet(joby) { Assert courseSet(joby). Retract jobyGuards(joby). }
  Rule masons_seen at tower_foot when jobyGuards(joby) and at(party, tower_foot) and hour(clock) >= 22 and not spread(masons_seen)
    says "At ten the Fabric's men come round the lodge corner with their lantern and their crowbar, and stop. On the scaffold, on every platform, in the dark, there is a mason sitting with his mallet across his knees: eleven of them, and Joby at the top, with his legs over the edge. Nobody says a word. After a while the Fabric's men go away. Somebody on the second platform begins to sing, quietly, a masons' song about a wall, and the others take it up, and at midnight, when the tenor bell rings the Fast in over their heads, they are still singing." { Assert spread(masons_seen). }
  Entity masons_seen: fact "the masons on the scaffold".
  Observe course_stands at tower_foot when courseSet(joby) and not nightfall() "On the top platform of the north tower the new course of white stone is still there in the morning, all four corners level, and Joby Thwaite is sitting on it with his legs over the edge, asleep.".

  // The Fabric's night-men: from nine till four they hold the scaffold-yard, and nobody who sees them there is meant to
  // say so. They warn once, and then they are four men with crowbars in the dark. Ways round them: watch from Gaol Lane
  // over the wall; come into the yard at dusk, before they do; sit up with Joby's masons on Fastens' Eve, when they do
  // not come; or have their canon silenced.
  Person nightmen "the Fabric's night-men" at limbo {
    Role "four labourers in the Fabric's brown, with crowbars, and a horn lantern held low". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 1. Numbers 4. Pronouns they.
    Temperament territorial. Refuge limbo.
    Warns "Four men in the Fabric's brown come out of the dark under the scaffold with crowbars, and one of them lifts a horn lantern to look at you, and lowers it. 'Fabric's business,' he says, quite low. 'There's nobody in the scaffold-yard at night. There never has been. Go back over the wall the way you came, and in the morning you'll not have seen anything; or stop, and in the morning they'll find you at the foot of it, and say it was the frost.'".
    Comes "They come at you all together and without a word, the way they take the stone down: carefully, and for wages.".
    Pleads "The night-men back off into the dark of the lodge corner with their crowbars held out in front of them, and the one with the lantern says, 'All right. All right. We were never here,' and blows it out.".
  }
  Rule nightmen_come when (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 4) and at(nightmen, limbo) and able(nightmen) and not routed(nightmen) and not jobyGuards(joby) and not pellowGone(pellow) { Assert at(nightmen, tower_foot). }
  Rule nightmen_go when hour(clock) >= 4 and hour(clock) < 21 and at(nightmen, tower_foot) { Assert at(nightmen, limbo). }
  Rule nightmen_stand_down when (jobyGuards(joby) or pellowGone(pellow)) and at(nightmen, tower_foot) { Assert at(nightmen, limbo). }

  // ── Canon Hamo Laverock ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person pellow "Canon Hamo Laverock" at close_green {
    Role "the Master of the Fabric, in a fur tippet, a pleasant round man with very clean hands". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "'Welcome to the Close,' says the round canon, warmly. 'You'll have seen the tower. Everybody looks at the tower. Two hundred and eleven years.' He beams up at it. 'A great work of faith is never finished. That is how you know it is a great work of faith.'".
    Greets again "Canon Laverock beams at you, and at the tower behind you, and cannot decide which to look at. 'It is a joy to see you again,' he says, 'but I must ask: have you a thought on scaffolding? It is the one thing about which the Fabric has no opinion at all.'".
  }
  Rule pellow_day when daytime() and not sitting() and not at(pellow, close_green) and not pellowGone(pellow) { Assert at(pellow, close_green). }
  Rule pellow_night when not daytime() and at(pellow, close_green) { Assert at(pellow, limbo). }
  Relation pellowGone(group). Relation pellowExposed(group). Relation arrearsForgiven(group). Relation pellowBargain(group).
  Topic pellow_hern with pellow "Ask Canon Laverock about Ninian Hern" when true once {
    Says "The canon's face does something complicated and kindly. 'Poor Hern. A great penitent, once. Thirty years on the Steps.' He shakes his head. 'And now he says the Commerce of Merit is a fraud, on the Minster steps, to the Fabric's own congregation. Do you know what the Commerce of Merit builds?' He points at the tower. 'That. Faith made stone. If nobody pays for penance, nobody pays for the tower.' He lowers his voice. 'I shall prosecute him myself. Very gently. And he will be put out, gently, at the Gate of Ash, and the tower will go on.'".
  }
  Topic pellow_tell with pellow "Tell Canon Laverock you have seen his men take the tower down by night" when knows(actor, unbuilding) and not pellowExposed(pellow) and not pellowBargain(pellow) once {
    Says "Canon Laverock does not stop smiling, which is a terrible thing to watch. He takes your arm and walks you across the lawn, out of anyone's hearing. 'The frost,' he says. 'And if it were not the frost, what then? A finished tower is a finished tithe. Two hundred clerks, sixty masons, the Stand, the Row: it all hangs on the north tower not being finished.' He pats your arm. 'You've come down the fell. You'll know the Scaifes at Carth: the Fabric's tenants, two years behind. Lady Day, they go.' He lets that sit. 'Or they don't. Their arrears could be forgiven. Today. If you'd the goodness to have seen nothing on the scaffold.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, pellow_offer). }
  }
  Discovery pellow_offer "Canon Laverock will forgive the Scaifes' arrears to the Fabric, if the company keeps quiet about the unbuilding of the north tower.".
  Action take_pellow_bargain(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Canon Laverock you saw nothing on the scaffold, if the Scaifes' arrears are forgiven" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pellow, site) and knows(actor, pellow_offer) and not pellowBargain(pellow) and not pellowExposed(pellow).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert pellowBargain(pellow). Assert arrearsForgiven(carth_vigil). }
    Result "'Saw nothing,' says Canon Laverock, delighted. 'Nothing at all. The frost.' He writes a note on a leaf of his pocket-book and tears it out: the arrears of the tenement of Carth forgiven by the Master of the Fabric, for a work of charity. He gives it to a passing servitor. 'There,' he says. 'Mercy. That's what the Fabric is for.' He goes off across the Close humming. Up on the scaffold a mason is setting a white stone that will not be there in the morning.".
  }
  // Told to the Lady Penitentiary, at her desk or under her mask, Laverock is silenced: she does not let a canon who unbuilds
  // the Minster prosecute a man for saying the Commerce is a fraud.
  Rule pellow_silenced when pellowExposed(pellow) and not pellowGone(pellow) { Assert pellowGone(pellow). Assert at(pellow, limbo). }
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/trial.ky:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── The Schools ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Consistory asks the Faculty whether a proposition is heresy, and the Faculty answers for a fee. Canon Laverock has
  // paid Doctor Ploughwright, the Irrefragable, for a Determination that Hern's is. Doctor Quist, the Seraphic, will sell
  // a contrary one to anybody. On Fastens' Eve at two they dispute in the Schools.
  Person ploughwright "Doctor Ploughwright" at schools {
    Role "the Irrefragable Doctor, a tall grey scholar in a fur hood, who has never been refuted because he has never been understood". Ancestry human. Calling mage. Level 4. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Greets "The tall doctor inclines his head a quarter of an inch. 'If you have come to dispute,' he says, 'the fee is a shilling, and you will lose. If you have come to purchase, the list is on the wall.'".
    Greets again "Doctor Ploughwright inclines his head a quarter of an inch, which, from him, is a bow. 'The fee for a dispute is a shilling,' he says, 'and I should tell you I have not lost since the Feast of the Holy Cross. I am confident you have it in you to end the streak.'".
  }
  Person quist "Doctor Quist" at schools {
    Role "the Seraphic Doctor, a small round woman in an inky gown who argues with her hands and her feet and her whole small body". Ancestry human. Calling bard. Level 4. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "The small round doctor bounces up from a bench. 'A stranger! Do you want a Determination? I've some very good ones going cheap: whether the Fast includes eels; whether a penance done in a dream counts; whether Saint Oswy was tall.' She leans in. 'Or are you here about Barefoot Hern? Everybody's here about Barefoot Hern. Ploughwright's sold his. Mine's still on the shelf.'".
    Greets again "Doctor Quist waves at you with both hands, and a pamphlet in each. 'More!' she says. 'I've more! Whether the Fast includes eels is settled, but there is a rider, and the rider is whether the rider is in the Fast. Will you hear it?'".
  }
  Relation quistBought(group). Relation crossed(group).
  Topic ploughwright_hern with ploughwright "Ask Doctor Ploughwright what he has determined about Ninian Hern" when true once {
    Says "'That the proposition, Nobody is sorry for another, therefore nobody is forgiven, is heresy,' says Doctor Ploughwright, 'on three grounds, each irrefragable.' He tells you the three grounds. The first is about Saint Oswy, the second is about arithmetic, and the third you do not understand at all, and suspect he does not either. 'Determined,' he says, 'at the request of the Master of the Fabric. The fee was considerable. Truth is expensive. That is how you know it is truth.'".
  }
  Topic quist_hern with quist "Ask Doctor Quist what she would determine about Ninian Hern" when true once {
    Says "'Oh, that it's not heresy at all.' Doctor Quist is delighted. 'The proposition's a matter of fact, not of faith: whether anybody in Gaunt is sorry. You can't determine a fact, you have to go and look.' She waves at the window. 'Nobody in the Faculty's been to look in two hundred years. That's what Ploughwright's paid for.' She sobers. 'And there's an old Life of Saint Oswy in the library nobody reads, with the end of the story in it. He didn't carry the sinner in. He put him down at the door and told him to walk.' She holds out a hand. 'Five shillings, and I'll write it all down, sealed, and it'll be read at the Consistory beside his. Two Determinations, contrary. They hate that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, quist_offer). Assert knows(actor, second_verse). }
  }
  Discovery quist_offer "Doctor Quist will write a contrary Determination on Hern's proposition, for five shillings, to be read at the Consistory beside Doctor Ploughwright's.".
  Action buy_quist(actor: group, site: place) "Buy Doctor Quist's contrary Determination, five shillings" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, schools) and at(quist, schools) and knows(actor, quist_offer) and not quistBought(quist) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 5.
    Time 3.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Assert quistBought(quist). }
    Result "Doctor Quist writes it standing up, at the pulpit, very fast, with her tongue out, and reads it aloud as she writes, to the students on the benches, who cheer the good bits. It is two pages. It says that the proposition is a matter of fact, that the Faculty has not looked, and that Saint Oswy, by the oldest account, put the sinner down at the door. She seals it with a seal that is mostly ink. 'There,' she says. 'Ploughwright will have to dispute it on Fastens' Eve, and he hates disputing; he might lose.' She gives you back a shilling. 'For the pleasure.'".
  }
  Rule schools_dispute at schools when quistBought(quist) and eveDay() and hour(clock) >= 14 and hour(clock) < 16 and at(party, schools) and not spread(schools_dispute)
    says "At two the Doctors dispute. Ploughwright in one pulpit, Quist in the other, the benches full and the doors open and the students hanging on the windows. Ploughwright gives his three grounds, irrefragably. Quist answers the first with Saint Oswy, the second with the price of a fast at the Stand, and the third with a long pause and then the words 'Neither do you,' at which the benches rise. By three the students are fighting, cheerfully, with the benches. By four the Faculty has determined nothing, and both Determinations will be read on Ash Day, contrary, which nobody can remember happening before." { Assert spread(schools_dispute). }
  Entity schools_dispute: fact "the Doctors dispute".

  // ── Ash Day: the Consistory ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At nine the Close is open to the whole city for the ashes, and stays open until dusk: on Ash Day anybody may stand in
  // the nave, and in the Chapter House from eleven, tallied or not. Only a shriven witness is heard.
  Query ashOpen() means ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 18.
  Relation trialOpen(group). Relation hernAnswered(group). Relation verdictGiven(group).
  Relation companyOffered(group). Relation thackrayOffered(group). Relation testifiedCarth(group). Relation testifiedRoad(group).
  Relation shouted(group). Relation sowerbyStood(group).
  Relation verdictFast(group). Relation verdictFlight(group). Relation verdictRecant(group). Relation verdictBearer(group). Relation verdictPutOut(group).
  Relation proxyRefused(group). Relation companyBears(group). Relation thackrayBears(group).
  Entity consistory: group "the Consistory".
  // Into the Chapter House at eleven.
  Rule hern_to_chapter when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 11 and hernGaoled(hern) and not hernFled(hern) and not hernDead(hern) and not verdictGiven(consistory) and not at(hern, chapter_house) { Assert at(hern, chapter_house). }
  Rule hawise_to_chapter when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 11 and hour(clock) < 14 and not at(hawise, chapter_house) and not verdictGiven(consistory) { Assert at(hawise, chapter_house). }
  Rule thackray_to_chapter when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 11 and hour(clock) < 14 and not at(thackray, chapter_house) and not verdictGiven(consistory) and not thackrayAway(thackray) { Assert at(thackray, chapter_house). }
  Rule pellow_to_chapter when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 11 and hour(clock) < 14 and not pellowGone(pellow) and not at(pellow, chapter_house) and not verdictGiven(consistory) { Assert at(pellow, chapter_house). }
  Query inChapter() means at(party, chapter_house).
  Observe chapter_sitting at chapter_house when sitting() and not verdictGiven(consistory) "The Chapter House on Ash Day: the stone bench full of canons with ash on their foreheads, the Lady Penitentiary in the stone chair, the Wood-reeve beside her for the Guildhall, and every inch of floor behind the rope packed with the city, standing, with ash on its forehead too. In the little square of different stone in the middle of the floor stands a barefoot old man in a new grey coat, coughing into his fist.".
  // Noon: the Consistory sits, or does not.
  Rule trial_struck when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 12 and struck(barefoot) and not verdictGiven(consistory) {
    Assert verdictGiven(consistory). Assert verdictFast(consistory). }
  Rule trial_struck_told when verdictFast(consistory) and inTown() and not spread(trial_struck_told)
    says "At noon the Consistory does not sit. It cannot: of its seven members, five are on the Bearer's Steps, barefoot, in their shirts, with boards round their necks, doing their own penance for the gilding because there is not a proxy to be had in Gaunt; and the sixth, the Wood-reeve, is sitting on the bottom step with his shoes in his hand, weeping, for reasons nobody can get out of him. The Lady Penitentiary comes out of the Chapter House at a quarter past twelve, looks down the Steps at her Consistory, and says, quite loudly, to the whole of the Close: 'Adjourned. Until the Commerce of Merit resumes.' In the nave the Row, which has been on its feet since six, sits down on the flagstones where it stands." { Assert spread(trial_struck_told). }
  Entity trial_struck_told: fact "adjourned".
  Rule trial_empty when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 12 and hernFled(hern) and not verdictGiven(consistory) {
    Assert verdictGiven(consistory). Assert verdictFlight(consistory). }
  Rule trial_empty_told when verdictFlight(consistory) and inTown() and not spread(trial_empty_told)
    says "At noon the Consistory sits in the Chapter House on the matter of Ninian Hern, and the little square of different stone in the middle of the floor is empty. The charge is read to it. The Determination is read to it. The Lady Penitentiary asks it whether it recants, and waits, with great courtesy, the proper time for an answer. Then she pronounces him put out, in his absence, from a city he is no longer in; and the precentor, who believes in nothing, has to turn away to the wall." { Assert spread(trial_empty_told). }
  Entity trial_empty_told: fact "the empty floor".
  Rule trial_opens when sitting() and not trialOpen(consistory) and not verdictGiven(consistory) { Assert trialOpen(consistory). }
  Rule trial_opens_told at chapter_house when trialOpen(consistory) and inChapter() and not spread(trial_opens_told)
    says "The Consistory sits. The charge is read by Canon Laverock, gently: that Ninian Hern, proxy, of the Row, has taught on the Minster steps that no man is sorry for another, therefore that no penance borne by another is of any effect, therefore that the Commerce of Merit is a fraud upon the faithful and the Fabric. Then the Determination of the Faculty, by Doctor Ploughwright, the Irrefragable, on three grounds. You do not understand the third. Hern, on his square of stone, is listening to it with professional appreciation." { Assert spread(trial_opens_told). }
  Rule trial_opens_precentor at chapter_house when trialOpen(consistory) and inChapter() and pellowGone(pellow) and not spread(trial_precentor)
    says "Canon Laverock is not on the bench. The precentor reads the charge instead, beautifully, as he reads everything, as if it were a lesson about somebody long dead." { Assert spread(trial_precentor). }
  Entity trial_opens_told: fact "the charge". Entity trial_precentor: fact "the precentor".
  Rule trial_crossed at chapter_house when trialOpen(consistory) and quistBought(quist) and not crossed(consistory)
    says "Then a second Determination, which the bench was not expecting, sealed with ink: Doctor Quist's, the Seraphic, contrary. It is read in full. It says that the proposition is a matter of fact, that the Faculty has not looked, and that Saint Oswy put the sinner down at the door and told him to walk. The canons look at each other. Two Determinations, contrary. In the stone chair the Lady Penitentiary has put her hand over her mouth, and you cannot see what it is doing." {
    Assert crossed(consistory). Increase hawiseReasons(hawise) by 1. }
  Rule sowerby_stands at chapter_house when trialOpen(consistory) and sowerbyChanged(sowerby) and not sowerbyStood(sowerby) and hour(clock) >= 12
    says "Behind the rope, barefoot still, Master Pentecost Sowerby, draper, puts up his hand like a boy at a dame-school, and when nobody stops him, says: 'I walked this morning. My own. A false ell, seven years ago. It was mine.' He looks round at the city. 'It was the first time it was mine,' he says, 'and I was sorry. I was. Nobody bought it.' He sits down on the floor, because there is nowhere else. Nobody tells him to be quiet." {
    Assert sowerbyStood(sowerby). Increase hawiseReasons(hawise) by 1. }
  // What a shriven witness may do while the Consistory sits.
  Action testify_carth(actor: group, site: place) "Stand as a witness, and tell the Consistory what you saw at Carth" {
    Description "A shriven witness is heard.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter_house) and sitting() and trialOpen(consistory) and not verdictGiven(consistory) and shriven()
      and stayingAtCarth(actor) and not testifiedCarth(actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert testifiedCarth(actor). Increase hawiseReasons(hawise) by 1. }
    Result "You stand up behind the rope and give your name and show your clean tally, and the Lady Penitentiary says, 'Speak,' and you tell the Consistory of Gaunt about Carth: the house with no fire in it; the dark; the hand in the ash; the child's cough, and what was done for her, and by whom; the old man in the byre on his hurdle, and the old woman who goes through to him at night. The Chapter House is very quiet. Beside the stone chair the Wood-reeve has gone grey. When you have done, the Lady Penitentiary says, 'Thank you,' in a voice you have not heard her use, and writes nothing.".
  }
  Action testify_road(actor: group, site: place) "Stand as a witness, and tell the Consistory what Hern said on the road" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter_house) and sitting() and trialOpen(consistory) and not verdictGiven(consistory) and shriven()
      and askedSorry(actor) and not testifiedRoad(actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert testifiedRoad(actor). }
    Result "You tell them: the fell road, the old man barefoot in the snow asking whether one man can be sorry for another; the kneeling proxy at the stone, and the board, and what is owed the dead; the Drove Fork. The canons write. Hern listens with his head on one side, as if hearing a story about someone he once knew, and when you get to what you yourself answered he grins at you across the floor, and the Lady Penitentiary sees him do it.".
  }
  Action offer_to_bear(actor: group, site: place) "Stand, and offer to bear Ninian Hern's sentence yourself" {
    Grave "If the Lady Penitentiary accepts it, it is you who will be put out of Gaunt at dusk, in what you stand in, struck from its Register for good.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter_house) and sitting() and trialOpen(consistory) and not verdictGiven(consistory) and shriven()
      and knows(actor, sentence_borne) and hernAnswered(consistory) and not hernRecants(hern) and not companyOffered(actor) and not hernDead(hern).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert companyOffered(actor). Set proxyAt(consistory) to watch(clock). }
    Result "You stand up behind the rope with your clean tally in your hand and say it: that putting-out is a penance, by the canons, and any penance may be borne by another; and that you will bear his. Nobody moves. Then everybody does. The canons turn to each other on the bench; the city behind the rope makes a long sound like a wave going back down a beach; Hern, on his square of stone, says 'No—' and starts to cough and cannot finish. In the stone chair the Lady Penitentiary looks at you without any expression at all, which in a Lady Penitentiary is an expression. 'The canons,' she says at last, 'allow it.' She looks at Hern. 'The canons have never been asked.'".
  }
  Action shout(actor: group, site: place) "Shout for him from behind the rope" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, chapter_house) and sitting() and trialOpen(consistory) and not verdictGiven(consistory) and not shriven() and not shouted(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert shouted(actor). Increase pains(actor) by 1. }
    Result "You shout it, whatever it is, over the rope, and the city round you takes it up for a moment, a ragged roar, and the serjeants come along the rope and look at you, and a clerk writes something down, and the Lady Penitentiary says, without looking up, 'Contempt. One pain,' and the trial goes on. Hern, on his square of stone, has turned round to see who it was, and is beaming.".
  }
  // One o'clock: she asks him.
  Rule hern_asked when sitting() and hour(clock) >= 13 and trialOpen(consistory) and not hernAnswered(consistory) and not verdictGiven(consistory) and at(hern, chapter_house) {
    Assert hernAnswered(consistory). Set answeredAt(consistory) to watch(clock). }
  Measure answeredAt(group). Measure proxyAt(group).
  Query afterAnswer() means hernAnswered(consistory) and watch(clock) > answeredAt(consistory).
  Rule hern_recants_rule when hernAnswered(consistory) and hernWillLive(hern) and (hernHeardHawise(hern) or hernHeardBess(hern)) and not hernRecants(hern) and not hernDead(hern) { Assert hernRecants(hern). }
  Rule hern_recants_true at chapter_house when hernRecants(hern) and hernHeardHawise(hern) and inChapter() and not spread(hern_answer)
    says "At one the Lady Penitentiary asks him: 'Ninian Hern, do you recant?' Hern looks at her a long time across the floor. Then he says: 'I said nobody's sorry for another. It's not so. I was, once. For a fishmonger's wife, the week I was fifteen, and I fasted for her, and I was sorry all week, for her, and you were in the next pen eating the cat's dinner.' The bench is baffled. The Lady Penitentiary is not. 'Then the proposition is false,' she says, 'by the witness of the accused, and the accused recants it.' She looks at him. 'Go home, Ninian.' And very quietly, so that perhaps only the front of the crowd hears it: 'It's still too salt.'" { Assert spread(hern_answer). }
  Rule hern_recants_bess at chapter_house when hernRecants(hern) and not hernHeardHawise(hern) and inChapter() and not spread(hern_answer)
    says "At one the Lady Penitentiary asks him: 'Ninian Hern, do you recant?' Hern stands on his square of stone a long while. 'Aye,' he says. 'For the Row. Bess Ackroyd says they eat, and I've never been right enough to be worth that.' He looks at the bench. 'I recant. Gild your Ladder.' It is the most bitter thing you have heard said in Gaunt, and it is said quite gently. The Lady Penitentiary writes it down, and does not look up while she does it." { Assert spread(hern_answer). }
  Rule hern_stands_love at chapter_house when hernAnswered(consistory) and not hernRecants(hern) and saidLove(party) and inChapter() and not spread(hern_answer)
    says "At one the Lady Penitentiary asks him: 'Ninian Hern, do you recant?' And Hern says no, and then he says it: what he came forty miles barefoot to say inside the Minster where nobody could walk past. Thirty years of other men's fasts. The stairs on his knees. Eleven hours of contrition for a draper, thinking about dinner. 'I was the best there was,' he says, 'and I was never sorry once, and nor were they, and the bells counted it.' He coughs. 'You can buy anything in Gaunt but that.' He looks round at the city behind the rope, at the ash on its foreheads. 'A man asked me on the road—' and he turns, and finds you behind the rope. 'Can one man be sorry for another, I said. And this one said: yes, that's what love is.' He lets the Chapter House hear it. 'Which you can't hire at a shilling a night. Not even from me. I was the best there was.' Then he stops, because he has said it, and stands on his square of stone looking pleased and frightened and old." { Assert spread(hern_answer). }
  Rule hern_stands_own at chapter_house when hernAnswered(consistory) and not hernRecants(hern) and saidOwn(party) and not saidLove(party) and inChapter() and not spread(hern_answer)
    says "At one the Lady Penitentiary asks him: 'Ninian Hern, do you recant?' And Hern says no, and then he says it: what he came forty miles barefoot to say inside the Minster where nobody could walk past. Thirty years of other men's fasts. The stairs on his knees. Eleven hours of contrition for a draper, thinking about dinner. 'I was the best there was,' he says, 'and I was never sorry once, and nor were they, and the bells counted it.' He coughs. 'You can buy anything in Gaunt but that.' He looks round at the city behind the rope, at the ash on its foreheads. 'A man asked me on the road—' and he turns, and finds you behind the rope. 'Can one man be sorry for another, I said. And this one said: no; sorrow is your own, or it is nothing.' He grins. 'My heresy, from a stranger's mouth, on the king's highway, for nothing. You'll want to try them too.' Then he stops, because he has said it, and stands on his square of stone looking pleased and frightened and old." { Assert spread(hern_answer). }
  Rule hern_stands_trade at chapter_house when hernAnswered(consistory) and not hernRecants(hern) and saidTrade(party) and not saidLove(party) and not saidOwn(party) and inChapter() and not spread(hern_answer)
    says "At one the Lady Penitentiary asks him: 'Ninian Hern, do you recant?' And Hern says no, and then he says it: what he came forty miles barefoot to say inside the Minster where nobody could walk past. Thirty years of other men's fasts. The stairs on his knees. Eleven hours of contrition for a draper, thinking about dinner. 'I was the best there was,' he says, 'and I was never sorry once, and nor were they, and the bells counted it.' He coughs. 'You can buy anything in Gaunt but that.' He looks round at the city behind the rope, at the ash on its foreheads. 'A man asked me on the road—' and he turns, and finds you behind the rope. 'Can one man be sorry for another, I said. And this one said: it's a trade like any other, and you were good at it.' He bows to you, a little. 'Which is true. Which is my whole case.' Then he stops, because he has said it, and stands on his square of stone looking pleased and frightened and old." { Assert spread(hern_answer). }
  Rule hern_stands_alone at chapter_house when hernAnswered(consistory) and not hernRecants(hern) and not saidLove(party) and not saidOwn(party) and not saidTrade(party) and inChapter() and not spread(hern_answer)
    says "At one the Lady Penitentiary asks him: 'Ninian Hern, do you recant?' And Hern says no, and then he says it: what he came forty miles barefoot to say inside the Minster where nobody could walk past. Thirty years of other men's fasts. The stairs on his knees. Eleven hours of contrition for a draper, thinking about dinner. 'I was the best there was,' he says, 'and I was never sorry once, and nor were they, and the bells counted it.' He coughs. 'You can buy anything in Gaunt but that.' He looks round at the city behind the rope, at the ash on its foreheads. 'I asked myself on the road, coming here,' he says, 'all forty miles, by myself, whether one man can be sorry for another; and I've answered.' Then he stops, because he has said it, and stands on his square of stone looking pleased and frightened and old." { Assert spread(hern_answer). }
  Entity hern_answer: fact "Hern's answer".
  // The Wood-reeve: moved, and asked, he offers at once when Hern has refused.
  Rule thackray_offers at chapter_house when afterAnswer() and not hernRecants(hern) and thackrayWillBear(thackray) and not thackrayOffered(thackray) and not verdictGiven(consistory)
    says "Beside the stone chair the Wood-reeve stands up. He is a big soft man in a fur gown and he has to put a hand on the Lady Penitentiary's chair to do it. 'I'll bear it,' he says. 'By the canons. Putting-out is a penance; any penance may be borne.' His voice shakes and then does not. 'I bought forty nights cold of the Penitentiary last winter for the forty-one I froze in the Row by holding back the oak, and Ninian Hern wouldn't keep them, and a farm on the fell has kept them for me ever since.' He takes off the fur gown and lays it on the bench. 'Now walk,' he says, to the room, and then, to the Lady Penitentiary: 'Let me walk.'" {
    Assert thackrayOffered(thackray). Set proxyAt(consistory) to watch(clock). }
  // Two o'clock: the verdict, from what has been made true.
  Rule verdict_recant when sitting() and afterAnswer() and hernRecants(hern) and not verdictGiven(consistory) {
    Assert verdictGiven(consistory). Assert verdictRecant(consistory). }
  Rule verdict_dead when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 12 and hernDead(hern) and not verdictGiven(consistory) {
    Assert verdictGiven(consistory). Assert verdictPutOut(consistory). Assert putOutDead(hern). }
  Relation putOutDead(group).
  Rule verdict_dead_told when putOutDead(hern) and inTown() and not spread(verdict_dead_told)
    says "At noon the Consistory sits in the Chapter House on the matter of Ninian Hern, deceased, who is present in a deal coffin on trestles on his square of stone, because the canons are clear that death does not discharge a penance, only interrupts it. The charge is read. The Determination is read. The Lady Penitentiary asks the coffin whether it recants, and waits the proper time, and pronounces it put out, in a voice like a door closing. At dusk four serjeants carry it through the Gate of Ash and set it down in the snow outside, on the Levels, and come back in, and the gate is shut and sealed." { Assert spread(verdict_dead_told). }
  Entity verdict_dead_told: fact "the coffin put out".
  Rule verdict_bearer when sitting() and afterAnswer() and watch(clock) > proxyAt(consistory) and (companyOffered(party) or thackrayOffered(thackray)) and hawiseMoved() and not hernRecants(hern) and not verdictGiven(consistory) {
    Assert verdictGiven(consistory). Assert verdictBearer(consistory). }
  Rule bearer_thackray when verdictBearer(consistory) and thackrayOffered(thackray) and not thackrayBears(thackray) and not companyBears(party) { Assert thackrayBears(thackray). }
  Rule bearer_company when verdictBearer(consistory) and companyOffered(party) and not thackrayOffered(thackray) and not companyBears(party) { Assert companyBears(party). }
  Rule verdict_bearer_told at chapter_house when verdictBearer(consistory) and inChapter() and not spread(verdict_told)
    says "The Lady Penitentiary stands up out of the stone chair, which nobody has seen a Lady Penitentiary do during a sitting. 'The canons allow it,' she says. 'Nobody has ever asked them. I've been asked.' She looks at Hern on his stone, and at the one who offered, and for a moment you see the girl from the Row who ate the cat's dinner. 'The sentence of putting-out on Ninian Hern is borne by another, who has offered it freely, and it is accepted, and it will be carried out at dusk at the Gate of Ash.' The Chapter House breaks into noise. Under it, if you are near enough, you hear her say to the precentor: 'And the Commerce of Merit has just put out an innocent person for a guilty one in front of the whole city, and called it law, which is what Ninian has been saying for a year. Write that down too.'" { Assert spread(verdict_told). }
  Entity verdict_told: fact "the verdict".
  Rule verdict_out when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 14 and not verdictGiven(consistory) and not hernDead(hern) and not hernFled(hern) and not struck(barefoot) {
    Assert verdictGiven(consistory). Assert verdictPutOut(consistory). }
  Rule proxy_was_refused when verdictPutOut(consistory) and (companyOffered(party) or thackrayOffered(thackray)) and not putOutDead(hern) and not proxyRefused(consistory) { Assert proxyRefused(consistory). }
  Rule verdict_out_told at chapter_house when verdictPutOut(consistory) and not putOutDead(hern) and inChapter() and not proxyRefused(consistory) and not spread(verdict_told)
    says "At two the Lady Penitentiary pronounces sentence, in the stone chair, in a level voice: that Ninian Hern, proxy, of the Row, having taught that no man is sorry for another and refused to recant it, is struck from the Register of Gaunt, and put out of the city at the Gate of Ash at dusk this day, in what he stands in, and no door in Gaunt to be opened to him after. She does not look at him while she says it. When she has said it, she does. Hern bows to her, a proxy's bow, from the waist, the way they bow at the Stand when they are hired." { Assert spread(verdict_told). }
  Rule verdict_refused_told at chapter_house when verdictPutOut(consistory) and inChapter() and proxyRefused(consistory) and not spread(verdict_told)
    says "At two the Lady Penitentiary pronounces. She says, first, that the offer to bear the sentence is refused: that a putting-out is a judgment upon a man's own mind, and cannot be borne by another. She says it clearly, so that the whole Chapter House hears, and the whole Chapter House hears what it means; somewhere behind the rope someone laughs once, a sound like a slate breaking. Hern, on his stone, closes his eyes as if he had been given a present. Then she pronounces him put out at the Gate of Ash at dusk." { Assert spread(verdict_told). }
  // Whoever is in the city and not in the Chapter House hears the verdict as the city does.
  Rule recant_news when verdictRecant(consistory) and inTown() and not inChapter() and not spread(verdict_news)
    says "At two the news comes down the Bearer's Steps faster than anyone can walk it: Barefoot Hern has recanted, in the Chapter House, in front of everybody. Nobody in the Row believes it, and then everybody does. By three he is walking down Bow Gate in a grey coat, slowly, coughing, with a crowd behind him that does not know whether to cheer, and so does not; and at the door of the Barefoot Hall somebody puts the copper on again, at three in the afternoon on Ash Day, which is not allowed." { Assert spread(verdict_news). }
  Rule out_news when verdictPutOut(consistory) and not putOutDead(hern) and inTown() and not inChapter() and not spread(verdict_news)
    says "At two the news comes down from the Close and goes through the city like cold through a coat: Barefoot Hern would not recant. He said it in the Chapter House, all of it, and he is to be put out at the Gate of Ash at dusk. In the Row people come out of their doors and stand in the snow, and do not go back in." { Assert spread(verdict_news). }
  Rule bearer_news when verdictBearer(consistory) and inTown() and not inChapter() and not spread(verdict_news)
    says "At two the news comes down from the Close, and nobody at first can say it straight: Barefoot Hern would not recant, and somebody stood up in the Chapter House and offered to be put out in his place, and the Lady Penitentiary accepted it. By the canons. In front of everybody. In the Shambles a butcher puts down his cleaver and says to his block, 'Well, then what have I been paying for?'" { Assert spread(verdict_news). }
  Entity verdict_news: fact "the verdict in the city".
  Rule verdict_recant_done when verdictRecant(consistory) and not spread(recant_done) { Assert spread(recant_done). Assert at(hern, row_lane). Retract hernGaoled(hern). }
  Entity recant_done: fact "Hern home".
  Rule consistory_rises when verdictGiven(consistory) and ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 14 and not afterTrial(hawise) { Assert afterTrial(hawise). Assert at(hawise, minster_porch). Assert at(thackray, minster_porch). }
  // ── Dusk: the Gate of Ash ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Query gateOfAshOpen() means ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 16 and hour(clock) < 18 and (verdictPutOut(consistory) and not putOutDead(hern) or verdictBearer(consistory)).
  Rule hern_to_gate when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 16 and verdictPutOut(consistory) and not putOutDead(hern) and not hernOut(hern) { Assert at(hern, gate_of_ash). Retract hernGaoled(hern). }
  Rule thackray_to_gate when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 16 and thackrayBears(thackray) and not thackrayOut(thackray) { Assert at(thackray, gate_of_ash). Assert thackrayAway(thackray). }
  Rule hern_free when verdictBearer(consistory) and not hernFreed(hern) { Assert hernFreed(hern). Retract hernGaoled(hern). Assert at(hern, close_green). }
  Relation hernOut(group). Relation thackrayOut(group). Relation hernFreed(group). Relation wentWithHern(group).
  Observe gate_dusk_hern at gate_of_ash when at(hern, gate_of_ash) and gateOfAshOpen() "At the Gate of Ash the chain hangs broken and the gate stands open on the Levels, white and blue in the dusk, and the whole Row is in the lane, silent. Two serjeants stand with Hern between them, in his new grey coat, barefoot. He looks out at the Levels the way a man looks at a road he is glad to be on at last.".
  Action go_out_with_hern(actor: group, site: place) "Go out of the Gate of Ash with him" {
    Description "You are not put out. You can come back in at the Fell Gate. He cannot.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, gate_of_ash) and at(hern, gate_of_ash) and gateOfAshOpen() and not hernOut(hern).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert wentWithHern(actor). Assert hernOut(hern). Retract at(actor, site). Assert at(actor, levels_road). Assert at(hern, levels_road). Assert willing(hern, actor). Set hire(hern) to 0. }
    Result "You walk out of the Gate of Ash beside him, and the serjeants let you, because nobody ever told them not to. Behind you the gate is shut, and you hear the chain, and the seal pressed. Hern stands in the snow of the Levels and looks back at Gaunt, its three walls, its one tower and a half, the lamps coming on in the Close. Then he looks at you. 'Well,' he says. 'I've been put out. I'm in a story.' He coughs, and spits, and laughs. 'They never say, in the stories, where the man goes after.' He looks south, toward the fell, where Carth is. 'There's a farm up there keeping a vigil I wouldn't,' he says. He sets off, barefoot, flat-footed, in the snow. 'Fourteen nights,' he says. 'I've done worse. Are you coming?'".
  }
  Rule hern_goes_alone when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 17 and at(hern, gate_of_ash) and not hernOut(hern) says "At five the serjeants walk Ninian Hern out of the Gate of Ash into the Levels, and come back in without him, and the gate is shut and chained and sealed; and through the grating, for a while, the Row watches a barefoot man in a grey coat walking away south across the snow toward the fell, not fast, not looking back, until the dark has him." {
    Assert hernOut(hern). Assert at(hern, limbo). }
  Rule thackray_goes when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 17 and thackrayBears(thackray) and not thackrayOut(thackray) says "At five the Gate of Ash is opened, and Hugh Thackray, Wood-reeve, who has been top of the Ladder of Merit for eleven years, walks out of it into the Levels in his shirt, without his gown, barefoot, carrying nothing, and the gate is shut behind him. The Row is at the grating. Nobody jeers. Someone pushes a pair of old boots through the bars after him, and he comes back for them, and puts them on, sitting in the snow, and gets up, and goes away south, toward the fell, where there is a farm keeping a vigil he bought." {
    Assert thackrayOut(thackray). Assert at(thackray, limbo). }
  // The company that bears it is walked out of the gate at dusk, struck from the Register for good; Hern, freed, follows,
  // because a free man can walk out of any gate he likes.
  Rule company_put_out when ashDay() and hour(clock) >= 17 and companyBears(party) and not putOut(party)
    says "At five the serjeants come for you wherever you are, politely, and walk you to the Gate of Ash through a Row that is standing in its doorways to see, and through the gate, which is open on the Levels and the dusk, and leave you outside in the snow in what you stand in. The gate is shut. You hear the chain, and the seal. Your name is struck from the Register of Gaunt; no door in it will open to you again. Then, behind you, the wicket in the gate opens, which nobody has seen opened in nineteen years, and a barefoot old man in a new grey coat comes through it and shuts it after him. 'Free man,' says Hern. 'I can go out of any gate I like.' He looks at you. 'You fool,' he says. 'You lovely fool.' He looks south, to the fell. 'Fourteen nights at Carth,' he says. 'Shall we? We're the only people in the world who know how.'" {
    Assert putOut(party). Assert at(party, levels_road). Assert at(hern, levels_road). Assert willing(hern, party). Set hire(hern) to 0. Assert wentWithHern(party). }
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/voices.k:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  Description "What each member of the company makes of Carth and Gaunt by what they are: the cleric at the dead man's hands, the ranger in the Bishop's Wood, the thief in Heb's cellar, the mage at the planed-off plinth, the bard at the Fat Lamb. And the things only a particular calling can do: read the first leaf of the Register in the old rubric, and decide who to tell; face the Bishop's Wood at dusk.".

  // The preset party is not a set of declared people, so it has no Remarks of its own. What a rule can ask of a member
  // is their calling, and print their name. Said once for the company, by whoever it has of the calling.
  Relation heardByre(group). Relation heardDeadfall(group). Relation heardHeb(group). Relation heardPlinth(group). Relation heardLamb(group).

  // ── Act II, Carth: the cleric at the byre ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule voice_byre at carth_byre when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, carth_byre) and not ralphLaid(carth_vigil) and not heardByre(party)
    says "{?m} stands over the hurdle and looks, for a long time, at the dead man's hands. 'Folded two ways,' {?m} says, very low, 'and slept with, and folded again. Somebody has been keeping him from going.' A pause. 'A man who is kept is not at peace. He is waiting. I have seen what that does to the one who keeps him.' {?m} does not look at the old woman on the stool. 'I could say the words. It would be a kindness to somebody. I do not know which of them it would be a kindness to.'" {
    Assert heardByre(party).
  }

  // ── Act III, the Bishop's Wood: the ranger ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule voice_deadfall at deadfall when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and awake(?m) and at(party, deadfall) and not heardDeadfall(party)
    says "{?m} goes along the edge of the clearing with a hand out, not touching. 'All in the same prints,' {?m} says. 'Five of them, and not one has put a foot down on its own.' {?m} straightens. 'They have a road, in a wood where no wolf has been given one. I should be out of here by four.'" {
    Assert heardDeadfall(party).
  }

  // ── Act III, the Row: the thief in Heb's cellar ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule voice_heb at heb_cellar when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, heb_cellar) and not heardHeb(party)
    says "{?m} takes a tally from the nearest bundle and tilts it to the lamp. 'Cut yesterday, smoked, rubbed with ash and mutton fat,' {?m} says. 'Whoever sold you one of these knew the Assessor looks at the ends and not at the notches.' A shrug. 'It's good work. It would be better if it were not the same work for the Fabric's accounts.'" {
    Assert heardHeb(party).
  }

  // ── Act IV, the Minster: the mage and the plinth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery plinth_lines "Five lines were dressed off the plinth of Saint Oswy's shrine by a different hand than cut the three that remain, perhaps a hundred years after them; the stone has not forgotten the depth of the letters.".
  Rule voice_plinth at minster_nave when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_mage) and awake(?m) and at(party, minster_nave) and not ashDay() and not heardPlinth(party)
    says "{?m} runs two fingers across the dressed-back place on Oswy's plinth with the grain of the chisel. 'Five lines,' {?m} says. 'Not three. A stone remembers the depth of a letter the way a bruise remembers a hand.' The fingers come away. 'This was done later than the cutting by a hundred years, and by someone who was careful. It was not defaced. It was edited.'" teaches plinth_lines {
    Assert heardPlinth(party).
  }

  // ── Act IV, Fastens' Eve: the bard and the missing verse ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule voice_lamb at fat_lamb when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, fat_lamb) and licence() and not heardLamb(party)
    says "{?m} sits with a cup untouched and an ear turned to the fiddle and the drum. 'Listen to the fiddler,' {?m} says. 'Eight bars into every tune he takes a breath, and the drum takes it with him, and not one of these people has noticed that all four tunes stopped at the same place.' {?m} taps the table at the gap, once, and the man across the table taps it too, looking puzzled. 'Somebody asked the whole city to stop singing the same eight bars. It did, and then it forgot it had been asked.'" {
    Assert heardLamb(party).
  }

  // ── The first leaf of the Register: the calling-unique reading ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Register's first book opens with a line every clerk in the Penitentiary can read. Under it, the original goes on
  // for nine lines in the rubric the Minster stopped teaching two hundred years ago, which every clerk copies, letter by
  // letter, at the head of each new book, and not one has read. A cleric can read it. Nobody else in Gaunt can, and no
  // one will have asked.
  Discovery first_leaf "Under the first line of the Register, the original goes on for nine lines in the old rubric: In the year the Bishop went away, the Penitentiary took up his keys, to keep and not to have, until they be asked for. Thirty-two keys are named; thirty-one were received. The Minster is of two towers, whereof the one shall carry the bell and the other the light, when it is asked for. To the poor of Gaunt the fallen wood, for ever.".
  Action read_first_leaf(actor: group, site: place, m: member) "Have {m} read the first leaf of the Register in the old rubric, under the clerks' copy" {
    Description "The clerks copy it at the head of every new book and not one of them has read it. It is nine lines. It will take an hour at the lectern with the Lady Penitentiary looking up from her desk.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, penitentiary) and daytime() and memberOf(m, actor) and hasCalling(m, calling_cleric) and awake(m) and not knows(actor, first_leaf).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, first_leaf). }
    Result "{m} stands at the first lectern with a finger under the rubric, and reads it a line at a time, under the breath, the way one reads a thing one has been taught as a boy and never needed. At her desk by the fire Dame Hawise has stopped writing. Nine lines. The year the Bishop went away: the keys, taken up to keep and not to have, until they be asked for. Thirty-two named; thirty-one received. A Minster of two towers, the one to carry the bell and the other the light, when it is asked for. To the poor of Gaunt the fallen wood, for ever. {m} reads the last word aloud, and nobody in the room moves. 'It does not say where he went,' {m} says. 'It does not say who is to ask.'".
  }
  // The lone company's way: a bard cannot read the rubric, but a bard has an ear. The clerks mutter it as they copy, and
  // an ear can hold nine lines of sound it does not understand. What comes out is the grant, with the words not quite right,
  // and the keys and the towers lost; the woodmen stand down for the winter, not for ever. The cleric's reading stays whole.
  Discovery first_leaf_ear "A bard's version of the first leaf, taken by ear from the clerks' muttering: the Bishop went away, the Penitentiary took up his keys, and to the poor of Gaunt the fallen wood, for a year and a day. The rest was lost in the sound of the pens.".
  Relation grantYear(group).
  Action recite_first_leaf(actor: group, site: place, m: member) "Have {m} sit with the clerks and take the old rubric down by ear, as they mutter it" {
    Description "The clerks copy the first leaf at the head of every new book, mouthing as they go. It will take an hour of sitting where the Lady Penitentiary can see you, and what is got is a tune, not a text.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, penitentiary) and daytime() and memberOf(m, actor) and hasCalling(m, calling_bard) and awake(m) and not knows(actor, first_leaf) and not knows(actor, first_leaf_ear).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, first_leaf_ear). }
    Result "{m} takes a stool at the end of the long bench and shuts both eyes, and the clerks go on mouthing at their lecterns, a murmur like a mill-race. After an hour {m} has a run of sounds that scan and mean nothing, and under them, twice, three words that do: the keys, and the wood, and a year. 'For ever, or for a year and a day,' {m} says, quietly, at the door. 'It does not carry. I have the grant, as a song has a grant.' At her desk by the fire Dame Hawise has watched all of it, and has not looked down once.".
  }
  Action grant_to_woodmen_ear(actor: group, site: place) "Sing the Wood-reeve's woodmen the grant as you took it down: the fallen wood to the poor of Gaunt, for a year and a day" {
    Description "It opens the wood by right, but a right you cannot swear to, and only as long as the winter. It tells the Lady Penitentiary nothing.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wood_edge) and at(woodmen, site) and able(woodmen) and knows(actor, first_leaf_ear) and not knows(actor, first_leaf) and not leafUsed(actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert leafUsed(actor). Assert grantShown(actor). Assert grantYear(actor). Assert at(woodmen, limbo). }
    Result "You give them what you have, as it came to you, in the tune it came in. The biggest woodman listens with his billhook on his shoulder, and at 'a year and a day' he shakes his head. 'Ever, my father said,' he says. 'Not a year.' He looks at the board on its post for some time. 'But you've the right of it, near enough, and I'll not be the one to say the Reeve's is better.' The three go back into the holly. In the morning, you suppose, they will be cutting.".
  }
  Rule leaf_known at penitentiary when at(party, penitentiary) and knows(party, first_leaf) and not leafHeard(party)
    says "The clerks have stopped copying. Nobody in the Penitentiary has ever heard the rubric read aloud. In the long room a pen is put down, and then another, and a young clerk at the back lays both hands flat on his desk and leaves them there." {
    Assert leafHeard(party).
  }
  Relation leafHeard(group). Relation leafUsed(group). Relation grantShown(group). Relation hawiseReadLeaf(group).

  // The choice. The cleric has read the leaf once. It can be used one way: it cannot be spent twice.
  Action grant_to_woodmen(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Wood-reeve's woodmen the Bishop's grant, as read in the Register: to the poor of Gaunt the fallen wood, for ever" {
    Description "It opens the wood by right and not by leave. It tells the Lady Penitentiary nothing.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wood_edge) and at(woodmen, site) and able(woodmen) and knows(actor, first_leaf) and not leafUsed(actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert leafUsed(actor). Assert grantShown(actor). Assert at(woodmen, limbo). }
    Result "You give them the nine lines as you read them, the rubric and then the plain, standing in the snow before the board on its post. The biggest of the woodmen listens with his billhook on his shoulder, and when you have finished he goes to the post and puts his hand on the old cut letters under the Wood-reeve's board, TO THE POOR OF GAUNT, THE FALLEN WOOD, FOR EVER, as if they had just that moment appeared. 'I knew that,' he says, in an odd voice. 'My father said. I never knew it was wrote.' The three of them go back into the holly without another word, and do not come out. Thackray has not been told.".
  }
  Action leaf_to_hawise(actor: group, site: place) "Lay the nine lines of the first leaf before Dame Hawise, as the Bishop wrote them" {
    Description "It tells the Lady Penitentiary what her keys are for. It opens nothing at the Wood.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, penitentiary) and at(hawise, penitentiary) and not masked(hawise) and knows(actor, first_leaf) and not leafUsed(actor) and not hawiseReadLeaf(hawise).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert leafUsed(actor). Assert hawiseReadLeaf(hawise). Increase hawiseReasons(hawise) by 1. }
    Result "Dame Hawise listens with her pen laid across the page. When you have finished she gets up, and unhooks the billet of keys from her belt, and counts them aloud on the desk, one by one, in the voice of the Row, which she uses when she is frightened. 'Thirty-one,' she says. 'I have counted them every Michaelmas for eleven years, and never once asked why a Lady carries thirty-one of a thing whose first line is a number.' She puts them in your hand. 'Try them,' says the Lady Penitentiary, 'if you can think where.' You cannot. She takes them back. 'To keep and not to have,' she says. 'I have been had, by these, for eleven years.' She sits down.".
  }
  Rule fate_grant_year when accounting() and grantYear(party) and not spread(fate_grant)
    says "Of the Bishop's Wood: the woodmen have stopped asking for four shillings for this winter, on the word of a stranger who sang it wrong. The board is back on its post face outward by Lady Day, and the Row's children are told it was a year and a day." {
    Assert spread(fate_grant).
  }
  Rule fate_grant when accounting() and grantShown(party) and not grantYear(party) and not spread(fate_grant)
    says "Of the Bishop's Wood: nobody knows who told the woodmen. They have stopped asking for four shillings, and keep the board on its post face inward, and the Row's children go out with their sledges on any afternoon they like, singing, and come back with the dead oak a sled at a time." {
    Assert spread(fate_grant).
  }
  Entity fate_grant: fact "the grant".
  Rule fate_leaf_hawise when accounting() and hawiseReadLeaf(hawise) and not spread(fate_leaf)
    says "Dame Hawise has had the nine lines copied out, in the plain, and hung beside the first lectern in the Penitentiary, where the clerks read them going past and do not know what to do with them. She has not decided what the thirty-second key is for. She says she is in no hurry to be asked." {
    Assert spread(fate_leaf).
  }
  Entity fate_leaf: fact "the leaf".

  // ── The Bishop's Wood at dusk: danger, and two ways that are not a fight ──────────────────────────────────────────
  // Five wolves, in the same prints, at the deadfall from four until seven. They can be fought, and it will cost. They can
  // be gone round, downwind, by someone who knows how; or sung at, in the Row's children's way, loud and slow, by
  // someone who has the end of the rhyme.
  Relation wolvesTurned(place).
  Rule wolves_rest when hour(clock) == 7 and wolvesTurned(deadfall) { Retract wolvesTurned(deadfall). }
  Relation wolvesRounded(group). Relation wolvesSung(group).
  Action round_deadfall(actor: group, site: place) "Take the company and the sledge wide round the wolves, downwind, along the bank of the beck" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, deadfall) and at(wolves, site) and able(wolves) and capable(actor, woodcraft) and not wolvesRounded(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert wolvesRounded(actor). Assert wolvesTurned(deadfall). Assert at(wolves, limbo). Retract assails(wolves, actor). Retract warned(wolves, actor). }
    On failure { Assert wolvesRounded(actor). }
    Result "You go off the woodmen's path onto the bank of the beck, where the hazel stands up through the snow, and keep the wind on your cheek so that it carries your smell away from them and not to them; theirs comes down on you, rank and warm. You go slowly. The biggest lifts her head as you pass, and holds it there, and you do not look at her. Half a mile on you come out on the track with the sledge and everyone you started with, and behind you in the dusk five grey shapes are going in single file along the other bank, in the same prints, toward Gaunt, and then not toward it.".
    Otherwise "Halfway round, the wind goes round, as it does in a wood at dusk, and the biggest lifts her head, and stands, and turns to look at you; and the rest stand up one after another, as if the snow had made them.".
  }
  Action sing_the_wolves(actor: group, site: place) "Sing the Row's sliding rhyme at them, to the end: loud, slow, and walking out" {
    Description "The Row's children go into the Bishop's Wood singing, because their mothers told them wolves do not care for a tune that has an end.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, deadfall) and at(wolves, site) and able(wolves) and knows(actor, second_verse) and not wolvesSung(actor).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert wolvesSung(actor). Assert wolvesTurned(deadfall). Assert at(wolves, limbo). Retract assails(wolves, actor). Retract warned(wolves, actor). }
    On failure { Assert wolvesSung(actor). }
    Result "Oswy, Oswy, up the hill, you sing, loud and slow and a little flat, walking toward them with the sledge-rope in your fist; carry me and carry me still. The biggest tilts her head. At the top he set him down, you sing, and the wolves, one by one, sit, like dogs outside a butcher's; and on NOW WALK, said Oswy, into town the leader gets up, and turns her back on you, and goes, and the others after her, in the same prints, unhurried, as if it had been their idea.".
    Otherwise "You sing it, and your voice breaks on the second line, and the biggest of them hears the break and lowers her head.".
  }
}

data/adventures/winter-in-carth/widow.ky:
Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── The widow's thoughts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Mistress Joan Pickersgill, a tanner's widow, rich, fifty, hires Abel Lumb every week to fast for her impure
  // thoughts. Her thoughts are about Abel Lumb. Abel Lumb is starving. Neither can say it. She is Hugh Thackray's
  // cousin, and the only person in Gaunt who laughs at him.
  Person joan "Mistress Joan Pickersgill" at pickersgill_parlour {
    Role "a tanner's widow of fifty in plum silk, with a laugh like a dropped tray and a book of devotion on her knee that is not a book of devotion". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner jovial.
    Greets "Mistress Pickersgill peers at you over the top of her book and closes it on her thumb. 'Oh, good,' she says. 'A stranger. Sit down. Strangers don't count. Have a fig.'".
    Greets again "'You again!' says Mistress Pickersgill, delighted, and has the fig on the table before you have sat. 'Strangers don't count, I said, and you have been twice, and I am beginning to wonder if I have been miscounting strangers. Have another.'".
  }
  Relation joanKnows(group). Relation abelKnows(group). Relation abelBearing(group). Relation joanThinksHarder(group).
  Relation betrothed(group). Relation joanLaughed(group).
  Discovery joan_thinks "Mistress Joan Pickersgill pays a proxy at the Stand to fast every week for her impure thoughts, which are about a young man at the Stand.".
  Discovery abel_fasts "Abel Lumb has fasted eleven days running at the Stand for Mistress Pickersgill's impure thoughts, at threepence a day, and is fainting.".
  Discovery abel_loves "Abel Lumb is in love with Mistress Pickersgill, and would sooner starve than stop fasting for her.".
  Topic joan_penance with joan "Ask Mistress Pickersgill about her penances" when true once {
    Says "'Oh, my penances.' She is enchanted to be asked. 'Impure thoughts, my dear, by the week. The Penitentiary has me at one pain a thought, and a fast a pain, and I am paying for eleven a week.' She eats a fig. 'I've a young man at the Stand who does them for me. Long, thin, very serious. He's so good at them. I go down on a Monday and watch him not eat.' A pause. 'That's not one of the thoughts. That's just devotion.' Another pause. 'Some of it is the thoughts.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, joan_thinks). }
  }
  Topic abel_who with abel "Ask Abel Lumb whose fast he is keeping" when not abelFed(abel) once {
    Says "'Mistress Pickersgill's,' says Abel, with a sort of shy pride. 'Impure thoughts. Eleven a week. I've not eaten since the Monday before last.' He sways. 'She comes and watches. To see it's done properly. She's very exact.' He looks at his feet. 'She's very kind. She brought me a fig once, and then she remembered, and took it back.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, abel_fasts). }
  }
  Topic abel_feelings with abel "Ask Abel Lumb why he does not stop" when knows(actor, abel_fasts) and not abelFed(abel) once {
    Says "Abel goes a red that shows how white he was. 'Because then somebody else would do them,' he says. 'Her thoughts. Somebody else would be fasting for them, and she'd go and watch him.' He grips the hurdle. 'I couldn't bear it. I'd sooner starve.' He hears himself. 'I am starving,' he says, surprised.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, abel_loves). }
  }
  Topic tell_joan with joan "Tell Mistress Pickersgill what her thoughts are costing the young man who fasts for them" when knows(actor, abel_fasts) and knows(actor, joan_thinks) and not joanKnows(joan) once {
    Says "Mistress Pickersgill hears you out with a fig halfway to her mouth, and it stays there. 'Eleven days,' she says. 'He's eaten nothing. For my—' She puts the fig down. She goes very pink, then very white, then pink again, which in plum silk is a remarkable sight. 'I thought he was just good at it,' she says. And then, quite differently: 'Does he know? What they're about?' She does not wait to be answered. She rings for her maid. 'My cloak,' she says, 'and a basket, and in the basket everything in the larder.' She stops. 'No. Not today. He'd not take it, from me, today; he'd think it was charity.' She sits down. 'Fastens' Eve,' she says. 'At the Fat Lamb. Everybody says everything on Fastens' Eve and nobody minds. Tell him to come.'".
    On discuss { Assert joanKnows(joan). }
  }
  Topic tell_abel with abel "Tell Abel Lumb who Mistress Pickersgill's thoughts are about" when knows(actor, joan_thinks) and knows(actor, abel_fasts) and not abelKnows(abel) and not abelFed(abel) once {
    Says "Abel Lumb looks at you for a long time. Then he laughs, carefully, as if laughing might use something up. 'No,' he says. 'No. She's a tanner's widow with a house on Tanners' Row and I'm a back at the Stand.' But he has gone pink to the ears. 'You're having me on.' He grips the hurdle. 'Are you having me on?' And then, before you can answer, he faints again, this time with an expression of great happiness.".
    On discuss { Assert abelKnows(abel). }
  }
  // Taking over his fasts: the complication. Joan, told her proxy is changed, thinks harder.
  Action take_abels_fast(actor: group, site: place) "Take Abel Lumb's fast for Mistress Pickersgill on yourself, so he can eat" {
    Description "Threepence a day, and her thoughts on your account.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, the_stand) and at(abel, the_stand) and knows(actor, abel_fasts) and not abelBearing(actor) and not abelFed(abel) and not fastToday(actor) and daytime().
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert abelBearing(actor). Assert abelFed(abel). Assert fastToday(actor). Set fastedOn(actor) to dayN(gaunt_town). Assert hungry(actor). Set nextMeal(actor) to watch(clock) + 144. Assert joanThinksHarder(joan). }
    Result "The clerk crosses out LUMB, A. and writes you in against PICKERSGILL, J., IMPURE THOUGHTS, and Abel is lifted out of his pen and taken off to the Fat Lamb by two proxies for a bowl of mutton, protesting, looking back at you over his shoulder like a dog being taken to a different house. By evening the clerk has news for you, with a straight face: Mistress Pickersgill came down to watch, and found her fasts being kept by a stranger, and went home, and has sent word that she will need fourteen this week.".
  }
  Topic joan_harder with joan "Ask Mistress Pickersgill why she needs fourteen fasts this week" when joanThinksHarder(joan) and not joanKnows(joan) once {
    Says "'Because my young man's gone,' says Mistress Pickersgill, crossly, 'and somebody else is doing my thoughts, and I don't know where he is, and so naturally I can't stop thinking about him, can I, and it all has to be paid for.' She takes a fig, looks at it, and puts it back. 'Is he eating? Somebody said he was eating. At the Fat Lamb.' She looks at the fire. 'Good,' she says, in a small voice. 'That's good.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, joan_thinks). Assert knows(actor, joan_misses). }
  }
  Discovery joan_misses "Mistress Pickersgill misses Abel Lumb.".
  // Fastens' Eve at the Fat Lamb, under masks: she says it.
  Action bring_abel(actor: group, site: place) "Bring Abel Lumb to Mistress Pickersgill's table at the Fat Lamb" {
    Description "Masks on, licence until midnight, and everyone saying everything.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, fat_lamb) and licence() and at(joan, fat_lamb) and at(abel, fat_lamb)
      and (joanKnows(joan) or abelKnows(abel) or knows(actor, joan_misses)) and not betrothed(joan).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert betrothed(joan). Assert abelFed(abel). }
    Result "You put Abel Lumb down in the chair opposite Mistress Pickersgill's, masked, and stand back. Neither of them says anything while the fiddle goes once round, and the landlord comes by with his jug and says 'Midnight, mind,' and goes away. Then Mistress Pickersgill pushes her mask up on her forehead and says, quite loudly, because it is Fastens' Eve: 'They're about you. All of them. Every week. Eleven. I've been paying you to starve for wanting you, and I'm a wicked old woman and I want you to eat this pie.' Abel Lumb looks at the pie, and at her, and takes his own mask off. 'I'd sooner eat it,' he says, 'than anything,' which does not quite make sense, and then he does. The whole of the Fat Lamb applauds, because the whole of the Fat Lamb has been listening.".
  }
  Rule joan_to_lamb when licence() and hour(clock) < 23 and not at(joan, fat_lamb) and (joanKnows(joan) or joanThinksHarder(joan)) { Assert at(joan, fat_lamb). }
  Rule abel_to_lamb when licence() and hour(clock) < 23 and not at(abel, fat_lamb) and (abelKnows(abel) or abelFed(abel) or joanKnows(joan)) { Assert at(abel, fat_lamb). Assert abelAway(abel). }
  Rule joan_home when (not licence() or hour(clock) >= 23) and at(joan, fat_lamb) { Assert at(joan, pickersgill_parlour). }
  Rule abel_home when (not licence() or hour(clock) >= 23) and abelAway(abel) and not betrothed(joan) { Retract abelAway(abel). }
  Rule abel_wed when betrothed(joan) and not licence() and at(abel, fat_lamb) { Assert abelAway(abel). Assert at(abel, pickersgill_parlour). }
  Topic joan_cousin with joan "Ask Mistress Pickersgill about her cousin Hugh Thackray" when true once {
    Says "'Hugh!' She laughs her dropped-tray laugh. 'Top of the Ladder. Holiest man in Gaunt, by the gold. He was a fat little boy who cried when he trod on a beetle, and he grew into a fat big man who cries when he puts the price of wood up.' She stops laughing. 'He's been strange all winter. Since the frost. He comes to dinner and doesn't eat and doesn't say anything. I thought it was his liver.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, thackray_strange). }
  }
  Discovery thackray_strange "Hugh Thackray, the Wood-reeve, has been strange all winter, since the great frost, his cousin says: silent at dinner, eating nothing.".
  // Betrothed, she has a good deal of courage to spare, and spends some of it on her cousin.
  Topic joan_tell_hugh with joan "Ask Mistress Pickersgill to tell her cousin Hugh to do his own penance" when betrothed(joan) and knows(actor, thackray_vigil) and not joanLaughed(thackray) once {
    Says "'Forty nights,' says Joan Pickersgill, when you have told her, 'of a cold farm, for the Row he froze. Bought. By Hugh.' She stands up. Abel stands up too, because she has. 'I shall go round,' she says, 'and laugh at him. I've not laughed at Hugh since he was nine and it did him good then.' She puts on her cloak. At the door she turns. 'Abel. Come and watch. You're good at watching penance.'".
    On discuss { Assert joanLaughed(thackray). }
  }
}

data/adventures/wrayford/aftermath.kyr:
Module wrayford "The Third Night" {
  // ── After the verdict ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // In a world that goes on, Wrayford is still there after its story, and shows what became of it.
  Rule captain_leaves when verdictGiven(wray) and hour(clock) >= 12 and not captainGone(wray) and fourthDay() {
    Assert captainGone(wray). Assert at(sefton, limbo). Assert at(troop, limbo). Assert at(gault, limbo). Assert at(riders, limbo). }
  Relation captainGone(place).
  Rule captain_gone_told when captainGone(wray) and inWrayford() and not spread(gone_fact) says "At noon the captain rides out over the drawbridge with her riders and Gault's four behind her, and the lord's toll money in a strongbox on a led horse, and does not look back at the gatehouse, and Wrayford watches her all the way up the south road until the hedges have her." { Assert spread(gone_fact). }
  Entity gone_fact: fact "The captain gone".
  // Whatever of the dead is not in the ground at the verdict goes to the lord's lime.
  Rule unburied_to_lime when verdictGiven(wray) and deadBody(?b) and not buried(?b) and not at(?b, limbo) { Assert at(?b, limbo). }
  Rule maudie_after when maudieHanged(maudie) and not at(maudie, limbo) { Assert at(maudie, limbo). }
  Rule maudie_home_after when verdictGiven(wray) and not maudieHanged(maudie) and maudieTaken(maudie) and not at(maudie, pardoe_kitchen) { Assert at(maudie, pardoe_kitchen). }

  Observe after_gate_fire at gate_road when verdictRebellion(wray) and not dark() "The gatehouse rail is crowded now. Nobody in the Bridge End looks up. Nobody stands about. People cross the bridge with their eyes on their feet and do not pay the farthing and nobody asks them to.".
  Observe after_gate_maudie at gate_road when verdictGiven(wray) and maudieHanged(maudie) and not verdictRebellion(wray) and not dark() "Four cut ends of rope hang from the hooks on the gatehouse rail. Somebody has tied a twist of black wool round the fourth, and nobody has taken it off.".
  Observe after_gate_mothers at gate_road when verdictGiven(wray) and mothersWalked(wray) and not dark() "On the coping of the gatehouse rail, where the hooks were, there are flowers: field scabious and corn-cockle and a bunch of mint, tied with carters' twine, renewed every morning by somebody nobody sees.".
  Observe after_gate_down at gate_road when verdictGiven(wray) and buried(wat_dead) and not mothersWalked(wray) and not maudieHanged(maudie) and not verdictRebellion(wray) and not dark() "The hooks on the gatehouse rail are empty, and the cut ends of rope have been taken down by someone, and people do not look up as they pass, or they do, briefly, the way you look at a place where a tooth was.".
  Observe after_gate_lime at gate_road when verdictGiven(wray) and not buried(wat_dead) and not verdictRebellion(wray) and not dark() "The hooks on the gatehouse rail are empty. The drovers say there is a new place at the crossroads on the south road where the lime has burned the grass white, and they take their beasts round it.".
  Observe after_row_fire at wain_row when verdictRebellion(wray) "Wain Row is gone: a lane of black chimneys and fallen roofs, cart-sheds open to the sky, the painted doors burned down to their hinges. The red one too.".
  Observe after_kitchen_empty at pardoe_kitchen when maudieHanged(maudie) and not verdictRebellion(wray) "The kitchen is cold. On every surface the loaves she made are going stale under their cloths, and nobody has the heart to throw them out, and nobody can eat them.".
  Observe after_kitchen at pardoe_kitchen when verdictGiven(wray) and not maudieHanged(maudie) and buried(wat_dead) "The kitchen smells of bread. There is one loaf on the table, not twenty. Somebody has wound the clock on the dresser.".
  Observe after_kitchen_lime at pardoe_kitchen when verdictGiven(wray) and not maudieHanged(maudie) and not buried(wat_dead) and not verdictRebellion(wray) "Maudie Pardoe sits at the table with her hands flat on it. She is not baking. The coat is gone from the hook by the door.".
  Observe after_hobday at hobday_room when verdictGiven(wray) and nedBuried(jennet) "The shutters are open. The bed is made. On the windowsill, in a jar, a boy's fishing line wound round a cork.".
  Observe after_hall_reeve at guild_hall when verdictGiven(wray) and (hulmeResigned(hulme) or reeveRelease(wray) or tooLate(wray)) "At the end of the long hall the reeve's chair stands empty, with his chain of office laid across its arms, and nobody has sat in it.".
  Rule hulme_dismissed when verdictGiven(wray) and (reeveRelease(wray) or tooLate(wray)) and not hulmeResigned(hulme) { Assert hulmeResigned(hulme). }
  Rule hulme_retires when hulmeResigned(hulme) and not at(hulme, hulme_study) { Assert hulmeAway(hulme). Assert at(hulme, hulme_study). }
  Observe after_acre at wades_acre when verdictGiven(wray) and reconciled(wray) and evening() "At dusk Dorcas Mudd rows across to the Acre steps, and Corbin comes down the steps to meet her, and they sit in the boat together not talking, and then they start to quarrel, comfortably, the way people do who have all the time in the world.".

  // ── What is given ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Bench, entering its charity in the minutes, enters its benefactor too: the freedom of the bridge.
  Relation tokenGiven(group). Relation ferryTokenGiven(group).
  Rule bench_token when verdictGiven(wray) and releasedBy(wray, by_charity) and inWrayford() and not tokenGiven(party) and at(party, ?p) says "Lancelot Inchbold finds you in the crowd with a brass token on a ribbon and a paper to sign. 'The freedom of the bridge,' he says. 'By the Bench's resolution of this morning, in recognition of your services to the Company's charity.' He does not smile. 'It is entered in the minutes. Everything is.'" {
    Assert tokenGiven(party). Assert at(bridge_token, ?p). }
  // Dorcas, for a crossing the bridge never saw: her own token, a penny with a hole in it, good at any hour.
  Kind ferry_token_kind "Dorcas Mudd's penny" is gear worth 0 weighing 0
    described "A penny with a hole bored through it, on a twist of tarred twine, and MUDD scratched on the back: good for the ferry at any hour, for life, with no questions and no farthings.".
  Item ferry_token "Dorcas Mudd's penny" is ferry_token_kind at limbo.
  Rule dorcas_token when verdictGiven(wray) and (boatCrossed(wray) or reconciled(wray)) and inWrayford() and not ferryTokenGiven(party) and at(party, ?p) says "A boy from the Wharf finds you with something wrapped in a bit of sacking: a penny with a hole bored through it, on tarred twine. 'From Mistress Mudd,' he says. 'She says it's good for the ferry any hour, and she says don't thank her, and she says she means it.'" {
    Assert ferryTokenGiven(party). Assert at(ferry_token, ?p). }

  // ── The Bridge Feast ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // On the fifth day at eleven the Company processes over the bridge in its blue gowns, and at the gatehouse the Abbess
  // receives the bridge penny that the city has paid the Liberty since the bridge was built.
  Relation feastHeld(place).
  Rule feast_none when fifthDay() and hour(clock) == 11 and verdictRebellion(wray) and not feastHeld(wray) and inWrayford() says "There is no Bridge Feast this year. The Company's blue gowns stay in their presses. At eleven, when the procession should have crossed, the bell of Saint Wade's rings once, by itself, someone says, though everyone knows the Abbess rang it." { Assert feastHeld(wray). }
  Rule feast_mothers when fifthDay() and hour(clock) == 11 and mothersWalked(wray) and not feastHeld(wray) and inWrayford() says "At eleven the Worshipful Company of the Bridge processes over the bridge in its blue gowns, with Gidley at the head and a band, and at the gatehouse the Abbess is waiting to receive the bridge penny, as the Liberty has since the bridge was built. Gidley holds it out. The Abbess looks at it, and at him, and at the flowers on the rail above, and does not take it. 'The city paid this year,' she says, loud enough for the Bridge End. 'Twice.' And goes back to Overbridge, and the procession does not know whether to go on, and does, very slowly, and the band stops." { Assert feastHeld(wray). }
  Rule feast_plain when fifthDay() and hour(clock) == 11 and not verdictRebellion(wray) and not mothersWalked(wray) and not feastHeld(wray) and inWrayford() says "At eleven the Worshipful Company of the Bridge processes over the bridge in its blue gowns, with a band, and at the gatehouse, from habit, Alderman Gidley stops under the empty rail and takes his hat off and weeps a little, beautifully, while the band waits. The Abbess takes the bridge penny from him at the drawbridge without a word, and bites it." { Assert feastHeld(wray). }
  Observe feast_portrait at guild_hall when fifthDay() and portraitHung(wray) "For the Feast the Guildhall is hung with blue, and at the end of the row of Masters the new portrait of the Bench is lit with candles, and every carter in Wrayford has found a reason to come in and stand in front of it.".
  Observe feast_banner at carters_yards when dayN(wray) >= 4 and portraitBanner(wray) "Against the yard wall, on its cart-shafts, Tom Lumley's portrait of the Bench, a little rained on, with somebody's pipe stuck in Gidley's mouth.".
}

data/adventures/wrayford/bridge.kyr:
Module wrayford "The Third Night" {
  // ── The Bridge End ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The lord's gatehouse spans the north end of the bridge. The toll is taken at a booth under its arch, where the
  // toll-house stood until four nights ago. Above, on the leads, the river rail; on the rail, the three.
  Measure crowd(place). Measure temper(place).
  Initially Set crowd(wray) to 1. Initially Set temper(wray) to 0.
  // The crowd grows every morning the dead are still up.
  Rule crowd_grows when hour(clock) == 7 and not crowdCounted(wray) and stillHanging() { Increase crowd(wray) by 1. Assert crowdCounted(wray). }
  Rule crowd_count_ends when hour(clock) == 8 and crowdCounted(wray) { Retract crowdCounted(wray). }
  Relation crowdCounted(place).
  Query stillHanging() means state(rail, hanging).

  Observe gate_scene at gate_road when not dark() and not visitedBefore(gate_road) "The road comes out of the Market into the shadow of the gatehouse, a square tower of red stone over the bridge's first arch, with the lord's arms over the arch and the lord's chain across it, new, the links still bright. Beside the arch, where a house stood, a heap of black timbers. In front of the chain, a booth of planks with a board nailed up beside it, very freshly painted. And up on the tower's river side, along the parapet of the leads, three shapes in sacking hang against the sky on short ropes, and turn a little when the wind comes up the river, and turn back.".
  Observe gate_scene_again at gate_road when not dark() and visitedBefore(gate_road) and stillHanging() "The Bridge End, under the gatehouse: the bright chain, the booth and its board, the black heap of the toll-house, and up on the leads the three in their sacking.".
  Observe gate_scene_down at gate_road when not dark() and not stillHanging() "The Bridge End, under the gatehouse: the chain, the booth and its board, the black heap of the toll-house. There is nothing on the rail now. People still look up as they pass, out of habit.".
  Observe gate_night at gate_road when dark() "The Bridge End at night. A lantern hangs under the gatehouse arch. Up on the leads the riders' brazier makes a red smudge, and against it, the three.".
  Observe crowd_small at gate_road when not dark() and stillHanging() and crowd(wray) <= 2 "A few people stand about at the Bridge End looking up, the way people stop to look at a fire, and then go on.".
  Observe crowd_large at gate_road when not dark() and stillHanging() and crowd(wray) >= 3 and temper(wray) < 2 "There is a crowd at the Bridge End now, fifty or sixty people, more at noon: drovers in for the market, apprentices, a man selling ballads, children on their fathers' shoulders. Someone has thrown a cabbage at the sacking. Someone else has said that's enough of that, and there was nearly a fight.".
  Observe crowd_quiet at gate_road when not dark() and stillHanging() and crowd(wray) >= 3 and temper(wray) >= 2 "There is a crowd at the Bridge End, a big one, and it is quiet. Nobody is selling anything. People come and stand and look up, and take their hats off, and go.".
  // The decree on the door.
  Observe decree_scene at gate_road when stillHanging() and not knows(party, decree_known) "A paper is nailed to the gate-ward's door in the tower, in a clerk's round hand with the reeve's seal at the foot.".

  // ── The toll ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery toll_schedule "The Bridge Company's new toll-board, by the booth: A CART, ONE PENNY. A BEAST, ONE PENNY THE HEAD. A CARCASS, THREE PENCE THE HUNDREDWEIGHT. GOODS OF A FELON: FORFEIT TO THE LORD, NOT TO PASS. A PILGRIM TO SAINT WADE'S ON HIS OWN FEET: FREE. THE ABBESS'S TITHE AND THE LIBERTY'S OFFAL TO THE TAN-YARDS: FREE, BY ANCIENT PRIVILEGE. A FOOT-PASSENGER: ONE FARTHING (SINCE THE RIOT). BY ORDER OF THE WORSHIPFUL COMPANY OF THE BRIDGE, FARMERS OF THE LORD'S TOLL." {
    Source toll_board "the Company's new toll-board" at gate_road readable by party.
    Known by pinch, gidley, inchbold.
  }
  Person pinch "Amos Pinch" at gate_road {
    Role "the Bridge Company's collector, in a new black coat". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "Amos Pinch has chalked the new rate on the gatehouse door and stands under it with his tally-stick, guarding a very small treasure. 'A farthing, foot-passengers,' he says, before you have put your hand to a purse. 'Since the riot.' He does not say whose riot it was, or why it should cost the foot-passenger.".
    Greets again "Amos Pinch has already got the farthing out of his own pocket, to save you the trouble of producing yours. 'Lower on the way back,' he says. 'No, it is not. But I always say so.'".
  }
  // The farthing, taken at the chain from everyone who goes on to the bridge while Pinch keeps the booth: once a day,
  // since he gives a tally-stick for it, and nobody but the Bench's freemen goes free.
  Measure tollDay(group). Initially Set tollDay(party) to 0.
  Relation owesToll(group).
  Rule toll_taken when at(party, bridge_street) and at(pinch, gate_road) and not asleep(pinch) and tollDay(party) < dayN(wray)
    and not carries(party, bridge_token) and quantity(party, gold) >= 1 says "At the chain Amos Pinch takes your farthing. There being no farthings left in Wrayford since the riot, he takes a penny, and writes you a tally-stick for the three farthings he owes you, which he says the Company will honour at Michaelmas." {
    Set tollDay(party) to dayN(wray). Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 1. }
  Rule toll_owed when at(party, bridge_street) and at(pinch, gate_road) and not asleep(pinch) and tollDay(party) < dayN(wray)
    and not carries(party, bridge_token) and quantity(party, gold) < 1 says "At the chain Amos Pinch holds out his hand, and looks at your empty one, and writes your name in the day-book as owing the Worshipful Company of the Bridge one farthing, and lets you by." {
    Set tollDay(party) to dayN(wray). Assert owesToll(party). }
  // The freedom of the bridge: a brass token, the Bench's, which the Bench gives to almost nobody.
  Kind bridge_token_kind "a bridge token" is gear worth 0 weighing 0
    described "A brass token stamped with the gold bridge and WE BEAR THE CROSSING: the freedom of the bridge at Wrayford, toll-free, by the Bench's leave, for life.".
  Item bridge_token "the freedom of the bridge" is bridge_token_kind at limbo.
  // He keeps the booth from eight until the curfew, and sleeps behind the counting-house.
  Rule pinch_opens when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 20 and not at(pinch, gate_road) and not pinchGone(pinch) { Assert at(pinch, gate_road). }
  Rule pinch_shuts when (hour(clock) >= 20 or hour(clock) < 8) and not at(pinch, pinch_room) and not pinchGone(pinch) { Assert at(pinch, pinch_room). }
  Rule pinch_sleeps when (hour(clock) >= 22 or hour(clock) < 6) and at(pinch, pinch_room) and not asleep(pinch) { Assert asleep(pinch). }
  Rule pinch_wakes when hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 22 and asleep(pinch) { Retract asleep(pinch). }
  Relation pinchGone(group).
  // The rulings: how a dead man crosses the bridge, by the board.
  Relation ruling(entity). Relation pinchFlustered(group). Relation pinchCowed(group).
  Discovery ruled_felon "Pinch has ruled, in writing, at the chain, that the dead on the rail are goods of a felon: forfeit to the lord, not to pass. Whatever else they were, they are now a ruling.".
  Discovery ruled_carcass "Pinch rules that the dead may cross as carcasses, at three pence the hundredweight.".
  Discovery ruled_tithe "Pinch rules that the dead, claimed by the Abbess, cross free as her tithe.".
  Topic pinch_dead with pinch "Ask Pinch what it costs to carry a dead man over the bridge" when not pinchFlustered(pinch) once {
    Says "Pinch's pen stops. 'A dead man,' he says. 'A dead man is not on the board.' He looks at the board as if it might have changed while his back was turned. 'The board is complete. The Company drew it up with great care. Everything that crosses is on the board, and a dead man is not, and therefore,' and he stops, because he does not know what therefore. 'Read the board,' he says. 'What it is depends on what it is.'".
  }
  Topic pinch_felon with pinch "Put it to Pinch that the dead are goods of a felon" when knows(actor, toll_schedule) and not pinchFlustered(pinch) once {
    Says "'Goods of a felon,' says Pinch, with relief, as if you had handed him something he had dropped. 'Forfeit to the lord. Not to pass. Yes.' He writes it down. 'That is very clear. Thank you.' Then he looks up at the rail, and at you, and for the first time something crosses his face that is not arithmetic. 'Was that what you wanted?'".
    On discuss { Assert ruling(ruled_felon). Assert knows(actor, ruled_felon). Increase temper(wray) by 1. }
  }
  Topic pinch_carcass with pinch "Put it to Pinch that a dead man is a carcass, by the hundredweight" when knows(actor, toll_schedule) and not pinchFlustered(pinch) and not ruling(ruled_carcass) and not ruling(ruled_felon) once {
    Says "Pinch considers this with his whole face. 'A carcass,' he says. 'Three pence the hundredweight. A carcass is a dead beast. A man is not a beast. But the board does not say beast, it says carcass, and a dead man,' and he closes his eyes, and opens them, 'is a carcass. Wat Pardoe was a big man. Call it twelve stone, with the rope. One hundredweight and a half: four pence ha'penny. Dunstan Fenner, ten stone. Joss Wilder, a boy, nine.' He writes it all down in a small exact hand. 'One and a penny farthing for the three. In coin, at the chain.' The crowd has gone very quiet. Annis Pye, at her pitch, puts down the pie she was holding.".
    On discuss { Assert ruling(ruled_carcass). Assert knows(actor, ruled_carcass). }
  }
  Topic pinch_pilgrim with pinch "Put it to Pinch that Wat Pardoe is a pilgrim to Saint Wade's" when knows(actor, toll_schedule) and not pinchFlustered(pinch) once {
    Says "'On his own feet,' says Pinch at once. 'It says on his own feet. A pilgrim to Saint Wade's on his own feet: free. Wat Pardoe is not,' he looks up at the rail, and down again quickly, 'on his own feet. In the relevant sense.' Somebody in the crowd laughs, and then somebody else, and it is not a kind laugh, and it is not at the dead. Pinch goes red to the ears.".
    On discuss { Increase temper(wray) by 1. }
  }
  Topic pinch_tithe with pinch "Put it to Pinch that the dead are the Abbess's tithe, and she has claimed them" when knows(actor, toll_schedule) and abbessClaims(abbess) and not pinchFlustered(pinch) and not ruling(ruled_tithe) once {
    Says "Pinch reads the Abbess's letter twice, holding it at arm's length as if it might bite. 'The Abbess's tithe,' he says. 'Free. By ancient privilege.' He looks at the board, which says so, in his own paint. 'The Company has always respected the Liberty's privilege,' he says, in the voice of a man repeating something he was told to say, and writes it down, and does not look up at the rail at all.".
    On discuss { Assert ruling(ruled_tithe). Assert knows(actor, ruled_tithe). }
  }
  Action press_pinch(actor: group, site: place) "Press Pinch for a ruling, here, now, in front of the crowd" {
    Description "Loudly. He has been asked the same question all morning and has no answer.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(pinch, site) and at(actor, gate_road)
      and not pinchFlustered(pinch) and not dark().
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert pinchFlustered(pinch). Increase temper(wray) by 1. }
    Result "Pinch stands up in his booth. 'A cart, one penny,' he says. 'A beast, one penny the head. A carcass, three pence the hundredweight.' The crowd turns to listen. He goes faster. 'Goods of a felon, forfeit, not to pass. A pilgrim to Saint Wade's on his own feet, free. The Abbess's tithe and the Liberty's offal to the tan-yards, free by ancient privilege. A foot-passenger, one farthing, since the riot.' He takes a breath. 'Everything else is forbidden!' The crowd cheers him as if he had sung. He sits down, white, and pulls the shutter of the booth to, and will not open it again today.".
  }
  Rule pinch_recovers when hour(clock) == 8 and pinchFlustered(pinch) { Retract pinchFlustered(pinch). }

  // ── The leads, the rail and the three ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe leads_scene at gate_leads when not dark() "The leads of the gatehouse: grey lead sheet, a parapet, a brazier, the riders' saddlebags. The river is a long way down, brown and quick, and the whole city is laid out from here: Northgate's smoke, the Hill's gardens, the bridge running out on its arches to Overbridge and the church tower on the far bank.".
  Observe leads_night at gate_leads when dark() "The leads at night: the brazier's red glow, the parapet a black line, the river loud below.".
  Thing rail "the river rail" at gate_leads {
    State hanging "Along the river parapet three men hang on short ropes from iron hooks driven into the coping, under sacking the reeve allowed. Their boots show below the sacking: a carter's big boots, a pair mended with wire, a boy's.".
    State cut "The iron hooks in the coping are empty. Three cut ends of rope hang from them.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(rail, hanging).
  // The three, once they are down: carried, laid down, buried. A body borne slows whoever bears it to half pace.
  Relation deadBody(entity). Relation bearing(member, entity). Relation buried(entity).
  Thing wat_dead "Wat Pardoe" at limbo is scenery {
    State lying "Wat Pardoe lies wrapped in his sacking, a big man, his boots showing.".
  }
  Thing dunstan_dead "Dunstan Fenner" at limbo is scenery {
    State lying "Dunstan Fenner lies wrapped in his sacking, his mended boots showing.".
  }
  Thing joss_dead "Joss Wilder" at limbo is scenery {
    State lying "Joss Wilder lies wrapped in his sacking. He was not very old.".
  }
  Place limbo "nowhere" is room within fells_edge at 9, 9.
  Initially Assert deadBody(wat_dead). Initially Assert deadBody(dunstan_dead). Initially Assert deadBody(joss_dead).
  Initially Assert state(wat_dead, lying). Initially Assert state(dunstan_dead, lying). Initially Assert state(joss_dead, lying).
  // Who bears a body takes it wherever they go, and goes at half pace.
  Rule body_carried when bearing(?m, ?b) and memberOf(?m, ?c) and at(?c, ?p) and not at(?b, ?p) { Assert at(?b, ?p). }
  Rule bearer_slowed when bearing(?m, ?b) and speed(?m) != 50 { Set speed(?m) to 50. }
  Rule bearer_eased when speed(?m) == 50 and not bearing(?m, ?b) and memberOf(?m, ?c) and company(?c) { Set speed(?m) to 0. }
  Query borne(b: entity) means bearing(?m, b).
  Query bearingAny(a: group) means memberOf(?m, a) and bearing(?m, ?b).

  // The watch: Sergeant Gault and four of the lord's riders, who keep the gatehouse until the captain comes.
  Person gault "Sergeant Gault" at gate_leads {
    Role "the riders' sergeant, a square man with a broken nose". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 4. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "Sergeant Gault is oiling a stirrup-leather six feet from the rail, and goes on oiling it. 'They stay where they are till the captain says,' he tells the leather. 'If it is the dead you have business with, it is her you wait for. If it is the living, mind the chain.'".
    Greets again "Sergeant Gault has moved his stool two feet to put the rail out of the corner of his eye, and sits there as if it were somebody else's idea. 'Captain's not in,' he says. 'Nor tonight. Ask again tomorrow, and I will say the same, but later.'".
  }
  Person riders "the lord's riders on the gate" at gate_leads {
    Role "four of the lord's riders, in buff coats, with the lord's badge". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Numbers 4. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Greets "Four buff coats have dealt a hand of cards on a drum-head under the rail. One lays down a knave and says something low, and the others laugh a little too long. None of them looks up at what hangs over the cards, and none of them would sit with his back to it.".
    Greets again "The cards are on the drum-head still, the same hand, the pot a little bigger. 'Another round of questions?' says the knave-layer. 'We have answers. They are all the same one.'".
  }
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(gault). Initially Assert takesPrisoners(riders). Initially Assert serves(riders, gault).
  // They sleep in the small hours, on the nights before the captain comes; after, her own riders keep the bridge too,
  // and nobody sleeps.
  Rule riders_sleep when smallHours() and hour(clock) >= 1 and hour(clock) < 4 and not captainCome() and not asleep(riders) and not ridersRoused(riders) { Assert asleep(riders). }
  Rule riders_wake when (hour(clock) >= 4 or hour(clock) < 1 or captainCome()) and asleep(riders) { Retract asleep(riders). }
  Relation ridersRoused(group).
  Rule roused_ends when hour(clock) == 12 and ridersRoused(riders) { Retract ridersRoused(riders). }
  // Gault drinks at the Nine Wheels from seven until ten, because nobody else will serve him.
  Relation gaultAway(group).
  Rule gault_drinks when hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 22 and not at(gault, wheels_taproom) and not gaultAway(gault) and able(gault) { Assert at(gault, wheels_taproom). }
  Rule gault_back when (hour(clock) >= 22 or hour(clock) < 19) and not at(gault, gate_leads) and not gaultAway(gault) and able(gault) { Assert at(gault, gate_leads). }
  Observe leads_asleep at gate_leads when asleep(riders) and at(riders, gate_leads) "The riders are asleep round the brazier, rolled in their cloaks with their boots to the coals, and one of them is snoring. Sergeant Gault sits against the parapet with his chin on his chest and his hand on his sword-hilt, asleep or near it.".
  Observe leads_turned at gate_leads when dark() and not asleep(riders) and riderPeaceBought(riders) and at(riders, gate_leads) "The riders sit round the brazier with their backs to the river parapet, all of them, very deliberately, eating bread and dicing, and none of them looks round.".
  Observe leads_awake at gate_leads when dark() and not asleep(riders) and not riderPeaceBought(riders) and at(riders, gate_leads) "The riders are awake round the brazier, dicing for farthings on a cloak, and every so often one of them looks along the parapet at the three.".
  Rule gault_sleeps when smallHours() and hour(clock) >= 1 and hour(clock) < 4 and not captainCome() and at(gault, gate_leads) and not asleep(gault) { Assert asleep(gault). }
  Rule gault_wakes when (hour(clock) >= 4 or hour(clock) < 1 or captainCome()) and asleep(gault) { Retract asleep(gault). }
  Topic gault_hanged with gault "Ask Sergeant Gault why he hanged them on the road" when true once {
    Says "'Warrant.' He holds his hands out to the brazier. 'Lord's warrant for the ringleaders of any rising against the lord's toll, to be taken and hanged where taken. We took them on the fell road with a dead lad in the back of the cart. Rising, a dead lad. That's the warrant.' He shrugs. 'The big one said he'd been driving. Said it twice. I don't hang a man twice.' He looks at the sacking, without anything in his face. 'Your reeve wanted them brought in for the court. I said: warrant. He went white. Clerks do.'".
  }
  Topic gault_road with gault "Ask Gault how he knew which road they'd take" when true once {
    Says "'Word came.' He does not look at you. 'Midnight, a lad with a letter. Back road to the fells, the cart with the red wheels, before light.' He shrugs. 'Somebody in this town wanted it done quiet. They all want it done quiet. Then they all come and stand at the gate and look.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, word_came). }
  }
  Discovery word_came "Someone in Wrayford sent Sergeant Gault a letter at midnight on the night of the rising, saying which road the carters would take to the fells, and that the cart had red wheels.".

  // Taking them down: the act the decree hangs a man for.
  Relation cutBy(group). Relation seenAtRail(group). Relation takenDown(place).
  Action cut_down(actor: group, site: place) "Cut the three down from the rail" {
    Grave "The decree is on the gatehouse door: whoever touches them shall hang beside them. Cut down, they cannot be put back.".
    Description "A knife to each rope, and a hand under each, so they do not fall.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, gate_leads) and state(rail, hanging) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert state(rail, cut). Assert cutBy(actor). Assert takenDown(wray).
      Retract at(wat_dead, limbo). Assert at(wat_dead, gate_leads). Retract at(dunstan_dead, limbo). Assert at(dunstan_dead, gate_leads).
      Retract at(joss_dead, limbo). Assert at(joss_dead, gate_leads). }
    Result "You cut them down one by one, and take each one's weight as the rope goes, and lay them on the leads. They are lighter than you thought, and heavier. The sacking has set stiff in the sun, like board.".
  }
  // Whoever is seen at it by an awake rider is seized. The riders take prisoners.
  Rule seen_at_rail when cutBy(?c) and perceives(riders, ?c) and not seenAtRail(?c) and not riderPeace(riders) says "A rider is on his feet by the brazier. 'Sergeant! Sergeant, they're at the rail!' Then they are all up, and coming." {
    Assert seenAtRail(?c). Retract peaceable(riders). Retract peaceable(gault). Assert assails(riders, ?c). Assert ridersRoused(riders). }
  Rule seen_bearing when bearingAny(?c) and perceives(riders, ?c) and not seenAtRail(?c) and not riderPeace(riders) says "Someone on the leads shouts. A rider is looking straight at you, and at what you carry." {
    Assert seenAtRail(?c). Retract peaceable(riders). Retract peaceable(gault). Assert assails(riders, ?c). Assert ridersRoused(riders). }
  Relation riderPeace(group).
  // Taken: a night in the Guildhall cellar, and the dead back on the rail by morning.
  Relation heldInCellar(group).
  Rule taken_at_rail when (captured(riders, party) or captured(gault, party)) and not (fireFought(wray) and at(party, counting_room)) says "You come round in the dark on cold stone, with your hands tied. The Guildhall cellar. Up the stair, through the door, somebody is saying your name to the reeve." {
    Retract captured(riders, party). Retract captured(gault, party). Assert at(party, guild_cellar). Assert heldInCellar(party).
    Assert peaceable(riders). Assert peaceable(gault). }
  Rule cellar_unburdens when heldInCellar(party) and bearing(?m, ?b) { Retract bearing(?m, ?b). }
  Rule dead_put_back when heldInCellar(party) and state(rail, cut) and not buried(wat_dead) { Assert state(rail, hanging).
    Assert at(wat_dead, limbo). Assert at(dunstan_dead, limbo).
    Assert at(joss_dead, limbo). }

  // ── Bridge Street ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe street_scene at bridge_street when not dark() and not visitedBefore(bridge_street) "Bridge Street runs out over the river on the arches, three storeys of shops leaning toward each other across a lane so narrow the upper floors nearly meet: a glover, a cook-shop, a seller of spectacles, a seller of Saint Wade's badges, a tooth-drawer. Between the houses you see the river below through gaps, going by brown and fast. Halfway along, a chapel is built into the middle pier, and beyond it the drawbridge, and beyond that Overbridge and its church.".
  Observe street_again at bridge_street when not dark() and visitedBefore(bridge_street) "Bridge Street on the arches: the leaning shops, the gaps with the river in them, the chapel on the middle pier.".
  Observe street_night at bridge_street when dark() "Bridge Street at night: shutters, a cat, the sound of the river much louder than by day.".
  Observe hobday_outside at bridge_street when not jennetOpen(jennet) and not visitedBefore(bridge_street) "The first house past the gatehouse is the toll-keeper's, narrow, with a shut door. Its shutters are closed in the middle of the day.".

  // The bridge chapel, and under it, the starling: the cutwater ledge round the middle pier, reached by a ladder
  // through the undercroft, where boys fish.
  Observe chapel_scene at chapel when true "A small chapel of grey stone built into the pier, so that the river is loud through the floor. Candles. A trapdoor in the floor, propped open, with a ladder going down into the dark and the noise of water.".
  Observe starling_scene at starling when not dark() "The starling: a ledge of stone round the foot of the middle pier where it breaks the river, wet, green, wide enough for two to sit with their legs over. Under the arch the light is green and moving. On the stone someone, a long time ago, has cut two sets of initials with a knife.".
  Observe starling_night at starling when dark() "The starling at night: only the sound of the river, very close, and the arch overhead blacker than the sky.".

  // ── Jennet Hobday ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person jennet "Jennet Hobday" at hobday_room {
    Role "the toll-keeper's widow". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner proud.
    Greets "Jennet Hobday does not look up from the bed.".
    Greets again "Jennet Hobday has not moved the chair, and has not moved her hands. 'You came back,' she says, to the boy on the bed, and then, to you, correcting it without hurry, 'You came back.'".
  }
  Thing hobday_shut "Jennet Hobday's door" on hobday_door {
    State kept_shut blocking "The toll-keeper's door is shut. Knock, and a woman's voice inside says, 'Go away,' without anger, the way you would say it to the rain.".
    State on_latch "The toll-keeper's door is on the latch.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(hobday_shut, kept_shut).
  Measure jennetTrust(group). Initially Set jennetTrust(jennet) to 0.
  Relation jennetOpen(group). Relation jennetSat(group). Relation jennetIced(group).
  Rule jennet_opens when jennetOpen(jennet) and state(hobday_shut, kept_shut) { Assert state(hobday_shut, on_latch). }
  Observe hobday_scene at hobday_room when true "A front room with the shutters closed and a smell under the smell of lavender. On the bed, under a sheet, a boy. A woman sits by him on a hard chair, upright, with her hands in her lap. ".
  Observe hobday_hot at hobday_room when not jennetIced(jennet) "The room is very hot, and the shutters keep the heat in.".
  Observe hobday_iced at hobday_room when jennetIced(jennet) "Under the bed, in a tin bath, a block of ice wrapped in sacking is sweating into the tin. The room is a little cooler. The smell is a little less.".
  Kind ice_kind "a block of ice in sacking" is gear worth 1 weighing 6
    described "A block of grey ice the size of a loaf, wrapped in wet sacking, dripping. It will not keep long out of the dark.".
  Action bring_ice(actor: group, giver: member, cake: item, site: place) "Knock at Jennet Hobday's door, and say you have brought {cake}" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, bridge_street) and state(hobday_shut, kept_shut)
      and memberOf(giver, actor) and ownedItem(cake, giver) and itemKind(cake, ice_kind).
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve drop(cake, giver).
    On success { Assert jennetOpen(jennet). Assert jennetIced(jennet). Increase jennetTrust(jennet) by 1. }
    Result "There is a long silence on the other side of the door. Then the bolt goes back. Jennet Hobday looks at the ice in your arms, and at you, and stands aside, and you carry it in and put it in the tin bath under the bed, where he is, and she watches you do it.".
  }
  Action sit_jennet(actor: group, site: place) "Sit with Jennet Hobday by the bed, and say nothing" {
    Description "An hour. She does not want talking to.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hobday_room) and at(jennet, hobday_room) and not jennetSat(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert jennetSat(actor). Increase jennetTrust(jennet) by 1. }
    Result "You sit. She does not tell you to go. After an hour she says, 'He took his father's place at the booth for the Company. A penny a day. He was proud of the penny.' That is all she says.".
  }
  Topic jennet_ned with jennet "Ask Jennet about Ned" when jennetTrust(jennet) >= 1 once {
    Says "'Fourteen.' She looks at the sheet. 'His father kept the lord's toll eleven years and died of his chest in the winter, and when the Company took the farm they said the boy could have the booth, a penny a day, since he knew the work. He'd stand at the chain in his father's hat.' Her hands stay still in her lap. 'He was at the chain when they came. He tried to keep it shut. A boy of fourteen, with his father's hat, holding the lord's chain against a hundred carters.' She looks at you for the first time. 'Wat Pardoe's cart. Everybody says so. And they've hung him for it, and I'm glad. I'm glad. Let the crows have him. Let the crows have him till the crows are sick.' She does not raise her voice at all.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, jennet_hates). }
  }
  Discovery jennet_hates "Jennet Hobday believes Wat Pardoe's cart killed her son, and is glad he hangs, and wants him left to the crows.".
  Topic jennet_custom with jennet "Ask Jennet why Ned is not buried" when jennetTrust(jennet) >= 1 once {
    Says "'Corbin won't dig.' Flat. 'Old Corbin, at Wade's Acre. He's dug every grave in Wrayford forty years and he says he'll dig none while there's a Wrayford man on that rail, and he means the carters, not my boy. So my boy waits for Wat Pardoe.' Her mouth moves. 'The third day is tomorrow. The day after. I don't know what day it is. He'll go looking. That's what they say. I'd like to see him look. I'd like to see him get up.' And then, for the first time, her face goes, and she puts her hand over it, and keeps it there.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, corbin_strike). }
  }
  Discovery corbin_strike "Corbin, sexton of Saint Wade's for forty years, will dig no grave in Wade's Acre while a Wrayford man hangs on the bridge. Nobody in the city can be buried until the carters come down: not the toll-keeper's boy, not Alderman Gidley's aunt.".
  // The truth, told by the one who drove, or by someone else.
  Relation kitToldJennet(group). Relation jennetTold(group). Relation jennetInformed(group).
  Action kit_tells_jennet(actor: group, site: place) "Stand by Kit while he tells Jennet Hobday who was driving" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hobday_room) and at(jennet, hobday_room)
      and travelsWith(kit, actor) and kitConfessed(actor) and not kitToldJennet(jennet).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert kitToldJennet(jennet). Increase jennetTrust(jennet) by 2. Assert knows(actor, jennet_knows). }
    Result "Kit stands in the doorway with his cap in his hands, and tells her. All of it: the horse, the press, the wheel, his father lifting Ned into the cart like something precious, the bone-setter at Scar Top, the riders on the fell road. He does not cry until he gets to the part where his father said get away home. Jennet Hobday listens without moving. When he has finished she sits a long time. Then she says, 'You used to fish with him. Off the starling.' Kit nods. She looks at the sheet on the bed. 'He said you were the only one of the carters' lot who wasn't a lout.' She does not forgive him. She does not tell him to go, either.".
  }
  Discovery jennet_knows "Jennet Hobday knows who was driving, and why Wat Pardoe said he was.".
  Action tell_jennet(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Jennet Hobday that Kit Pardoe was driving, and Wat took the blame" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hobday_room) and at(jennet, hobday_room)
      and knows(actor, kit_driving) and not kitToldJennet(jennet) and not jennetTold(jennet).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert jennetTold(jennet). Assert jennetInformed(jennet). }
    Result "She hears you out without moving. Then she gets up, and puts on her shawl, and goes past you out of the door without a word, and down Bridge Street toward the Guildhall, walking very fast.".
  }
}

data/adventures/wrayford/captain.kyr:
Module wrayford "The Third Night" {
  // ── The captain ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Lys Sefton, the lord's captain, comes up the south road at dusk on the third day with her riders, sups with the
  // Bench in the Guildhall, and gives her verdict on the fourth morning: is Wrayford in rebellion?
  Person sefton "Captain Lys Sefton" at limbo {
    Role "the lord's captain, in a grey riding-coat with the lord's badge". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 6. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner stoic.
    Greets "Captain Sefton looks at you as if you were a road she had to decide whether to take.".
  }
  Person troop "the captain's riders" at limbo {
    Role "a dozen of the lord's riders, dusty from the road". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 3. Numbers 6. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
  }
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(sefton). Initially Assert takesPrisoners(troop).
  Rule riders_sighted when thirdDay() and hour(clock) >= 12 and not spread(sighted_fact) and inWrayford() says "At noon a boy comes running over the drawbridge from Overbridge shouting that there are riders on the south road, a long way off, a dozen of them and a woman in grey, and the whole of the Bridge End turns to look south." { Assert spread(sighted_fact). }
  Entity sighted_fact: fact "Riders sighted".
  // On the south road in the late afternoon, ahead of her own arrival.
  Rule captain_on_road when thirdDay() and hour(clock) >= 15 and hour(clock) < 19 and at(sefton, limbo) { Assert at(sefton, south_road). Assert at(troop, south_road). }
  Rule captain_arrives when captainCome() and not captainHere(wray) { Assert captainHere(wray). Assert at(sefton, guild_hall). Assert at(troop, gate_road). }
  Relation captainHere(place).
  Rule captain_told when captainHere(wray) and inWrayford() and not spread(arrived_fact) says "At dusk the captain rides in over the drawbridge with her riders behind her, and does not look up at the gatehouse as she passes under it, and goes to the Guildhall, where the Bench has laid supper." { Assert spread(arrived_fact). }
  Entity arrived_fact: fact "The captain arrived".
  Rule captain_sups when captainHere(wray) and hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 23 and not at(sefton, guild_hall) and not verdictGiven(wray) { Assert at(sefton, guild_hall). }
  Rule captain_retires when captainHere(wray) and (hour(clock) >= 23 or hour(clock) < 7) and not at(sefton, hulme_study) and not verdictGiven(wray) { Assert at(sefton, hulme_study). }
  Rule captain_court when fourthDay() and hour(clock) >= 7 and not at(sefton, guild_hall) and not verdictGiven(wray) { Assert at(sefton, guild_hall). }
  Observe supper_scene at guild_hall when captainHere(wray) and hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 23 "The Bench's supper for the captain: candles down the long table, the aldermen in their best gowns, a swan nobody is eating, and at the head of the table a woman in a grey riding-coat with the road's dust still on it, eating bread and cheese and listening to Gidley with no expression at all. The reeve sits at her right hand and does not eat.".
  Measure captainView(group). Initially Set captainView(sefton) to 0.
  Relation captainMet(group). Relation captainPinch(group). Relation captainFuneral(group). Relation companyOffersKit(place).
  Discovery captain_question "Captain Sefton has one question for Wrayford: is it in rebellion? Ten hanged for every rider hurt, and the carters' row burned, if it is; the toll money taken and her riders home if it is not.".
  Topic sefton_road with sefton "Ask the captain what she means to do in Wrayford" when not verdictGiven(wray) once {
    Says "'Find out whether Wrayford is in rebellion.' She does not slow her horse, or her voice. 'If it is, I have a warrant for ten for every rider hurt and the carters' row burned to the stones, and I will do it. If it is not, I will take the lord's toll money and go home, and be glad.' She looks at you for the first time. 'I would rather go home. People think a captain likes a burning. Nobody likes a burning.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, captain_question). Assert captainMet(actor). }
  }
  Action meet_captain(actor: group, site: place) "Walk beside the captain's horse and tell her what Wrayford is, before the Bench does" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, south_road) and at(sefton, south_road) and captainMet(actor) and not triedCaptain(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Increase captainView(sefton) by 1. Assert triedCaptain(actor). }
    On failure { Assert triedCaptain(actor). }
    Result "You walk at her stirrup for a mile and tell her: the carters broke a chain and threw a board in the river; a boy died under a cart in the press; three men hanged on the road without a court; a widow who means to bury her husband; a city that would rather bury its dead than burn. She does not say anything. At the last milestone she says, 'Thank you. I'll see for myself,' and you understand that you have been listened to.".
    Otherwise "She listens to the first sentence and then says, 'I'll see for myself,' and touches her horse, and you are walking alone.".
  }
  Relation triedCaptain(group).
  Action tell_captain_fire(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the captain at supper that there was no rising: a riot, and a thief" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, guild_hall) and at(sefton, guild_hall) and knows(actor, fire_pinch)
      and (carries(actor, daybook) or pinchExposed(wray)) and not captainPinch(actor).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert captainPinch(actor). Increase captainView(sefton) by 2. Assert pinchExposed(wray). }
    Result "You tell her about the flask in the ash, and the shirt, and the day-book, and what is in it, and when you have finished she turns, slowly, to look down the table at Alderman Gidley, who has gone the colour of the swan. 'So the carters broke a chain,' she says, 'and threw your board in the river, and your collector burned your toll-house to hide that he was robbing you.' She puts her bread down. 'That is not a rising, Alderman. That is a riot, and a thief.' Nobody at the table says anything at all.".
  }
  Action tell_captain_funeral(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the captain that Wrayford will bury its dead, not burn" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, guild_hall) and at(sefton, guild_hall) and not captainFuneral(actor)
      and (buried(wat_dead) or mothersMet(wray) or releaseUnderway(wray)).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert captainFuneral(actor). Increase captainView(sefton) by 1. }
    Result "She hears you, and looks at the reeve, who nods without lifting his eyes. 'A funeral,' she says. 'Not a rising.' She seems to think about it. 'I've seen both. I know the difference.'".
  }
  // A drover who owes you something, and who has driven through every rising in the north, says so where it counts.
  Relation hamSpoke(group).
  Rule ham_speaks when captainHere(wray) and hamGrateful(party) and not hamSpoke(ham) and not verdictGiven(wray) says "At the Bridge End, as the captain's riders water their horses, Ham Ostler leans on his crook and tells the nearest of them, loud enough for the captain, that he has driven beasts through every rising in the north these thirty years, and this is not one, it is a city with a toothache. The captain looks at him from the saddle. Drovers, it seems, are people she listens to." {
    Assert hamSpoke(ham). Increase captainView(sefton) by 1. }
  // She asks the company one question, the first time it speaks to her in the city: the only one at the table she has
  // not been told what to think of. What it may answer depends on who it is.
  Relation captainAsked(group). Relation captainAnswered(group).
  Event captain_asks near sefton when captainHere(wray) and addressed(sefton, party) and not captainAsked(party) and not verdictGiven(wray) "Captain Sefton looks at you down the length of the table, past the aldermen. 'You,' she says. 'You are the only person in this hall I have not been told what to think of. Is Wrayford in rebellion?' The table goes quiet. Gidley opens his mouth, and she lifts one finger without looking at him, and he shuts it." then { Assert captainAsked(party). }
  Topic answer_captain_kin with sefton "Tell her: my father is on that rail, and I have not burned anything" when captainAsked(actor) and homecomer(actor) and not captainAnswered(actor) once {
    Says "She puts down her knife. 'Pardoe,' she says. 'The big one, who sang.' She turns her cup round on the cloth. 'A rebel's child who comes to supper with the Bench instead of to the gate with a torch.' She does not say what she makes of it. But she does not look at Gidley again for the rest of the meal.".
    On discuss { Assert captainAnswered(actor). Increase captainView(sefton) by 1. }
  }
  Topic answer_captain_stranger with sefton "Tell her: I am a stranger here, with nobody on the rail; it is grief, not rebellion" when captainAsked(actor) and stranger(actor) and not captainAnswered(actor) once {
    Says "'A stranger.' She considers you as if you were a horse somebody else was selling. 'Then you've no reason to lie to me, and no reason to tell me the truth, which is the best a captain ever gets.' She nods, once. 'Grief. I have seen grief. It does not usually set fire to things.' She looks down the table at the aldermen. 'Usually.'".
    On discuss { Assert captainAnswered(actor). Increase captainView(sefton) by 1. }
  }
  Topic answer_captain_carters with sefton "Tell her to ask the carters, not the Bench" when captainAsked(actor) and not captainAnswered(actor) once {
    Says "'The carters.' She almost smiles. 'Yes. I'll go to the yards tonight, without my riders, and see what they are.' She does. Word comes back before midnight: she stood in the carters' yards for an hour with a pot of the Nine Wheels' ale, and they told her about the board in the river, and the chain, and nobody drew a knife.".
    On discuss { Assert captainAnswered(actor). Assert captainSawYards(sefton). }
  }
  Relation captainSawYards(group).
  // What she finds in the yards depends on what the carters did.
  Rule captain_yards_quiet when captainSawYards(sefton) and not fireTried(wray) and not countingBurned(wray) and not yardsCounted(sefton) { Assert yardsCounted(sefton). Increase captainView(sefton) by 1. }
  Rule captain_yards_laughing when captainSawYards(sefton) and boardSunk(wray) and not countingBurned(wray) and not yardsCounted(sefton) { Assert yardsCounted(sefton). Increase captainView(sefton) by 1. }
  Relation yardsCounted(group).
  // The Company, at supper, offers the captain a live ringleader for the lord's justice: the boy, if it knows of him.
  Rule company_offers when captainHere(wray) and hour(clock) >= 20 and (bargainMade(party) or kitExposed(wray)) and not companyOffersKit(wray) and not kitTaken(kit) and not travelsWith(kit, party) says "A pot-boy comes out of the Guildhall kitchen with a tray on his shoulder and tells the yard: Alderman Gidley has told the captain, with tears, that the true driver of the cart was Wat Pardoe's son, and that the Company would think it a great mercy to the city if the lord's justice took the boy alive. The riders go to the yards for Kit Pardoe." {
    Assert companyOffersKit(wray). Assert kitTaken(kit). Assert at(kit, guild_cellar). }
  // The Company keeps its word, such as it is: a live ringleader bought, it asks mercy for the dead, before the third night.
  Rule company_mercy when captainHere(wray) and hour(clock) >= 20 and kitSold(kit) and stillHanging() and not releaseUnderway(wray) says "Word comes out of the Guildhall supper: the Company, having given the lord's justice a live ringleader, has asked the captain's mercy for the dead, as a kindness to the city, and she has granted it, with a look at Alderman Gidley that goes on a little too long. The three come down from the rail by torchlight and are carried over the bridge to Wade's Acre, to wait for morning." {
    Assert releaseUnderway(wray). Assert releasedBy(wray, by_captain). }

  // ── The third night: the reeve, too late; the carters, rising ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation reeveLate(place). Relation tooLate(place). Relation riseNight(place).
  Rule reeve_goes_late when hulmeMoved(hulme) >= 3 and captainCome() and stillHanging() and thirdDay() and hour(clock) >= 3 and hour(clock) < 6 and not reeveLate(wray) and not releaseUnderway(wray) {
    Assert reeveLate(wray). }
  Rule reeve_late_finds when reeveLate(wray) and maudieTaken(maudie) and not tooLate(wray) says "In the small hours Simon Hulme comes down the Cartway to the Bridge End alone, without a lantern, with a knife in his hand, to cut his cousin's husband down from the rail against the captain's word and answer for it. He is a quarter of an hour behind Maudie Pardoe. He stands under the gatehouse arch and looks at the empty step where the riders took her, and the riders look down at him from the leads, and nobody says anything at all." { Assert tooLate(wray). }
  Rule reeve_late_cuts when reeveLate(wray) and not maudieTaken(maudie) and stillHanging() says "In the small hours Simon Hulme comes down the Cartway to the Bridge End alone with a knife in his hand, and goes up the gate-ward's stair past the captain's riders, who do not stop the reeve, and cuts the three down himself, against the captain's word, and has them carried over the bridge at first light." {
    Assert releaseUnderway(wray). Assert reeveRelease(wray). Assert releasedBy(wray, by_reeve). }
  // With his mother in the cellar and his father on the rail, Kit takes the young carters to the gatehouse, unless he
  // is held, or with you, or has given his word.
  Rule carters_rise when maudieTaken(maudie) and stillHanging() and not kitTaken(kit) and not travelsWith(kit, party) and not kitStoodDown(kit) and thirdDay() and hour(clock) >= 4 and hour(clock) < 6 and not riseNight(wray) says "Before dawn the carters' yards empty. Kit Pardoe goes down the Cartway at the head of thirty men with cart-staves and torches, to the gatehouse where his mother was taken, and the captain's riders meet them at the Bridge End. By first light it is over, and Kit is in the Guildhall cellar with his arm broken, and two of the riders are being carried into the Bridge End inn." {
    Assert riseNight(wray). Assert kitTaken(kit). Assert at(kit, guild_cellar). }

  // ── The verdict ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At nine on the fourth morning, in the Guildhall. Rebellion is fire raised, or riders beaten, or a rising at the gate.
  Relation verdictGiven(place). Relation verdictRebellion(place). Relation verdictOrder(place).
  Relation countingBurned(place). Relation ridersBeaten(place). Relation kitHanged(group). Relation maudieHanged(group).
  Rule riders_beaten when (routed(riders) or not able(riders) or not able(gault)) and not ridersBeaten(wray) { Assert ridersBeaten(wray). }
  Query rebellion() means countingBurned(wray) or ridersBeaten(wray) or riseNight(wray).
  Rule verdict_rebellion when fourthDay() and hour(clock) >= 9 and not verdictGiven(wray) and rebellion() {
    Assert verdictGiven(wray). Assert verdictRebellion(wray). }
  Rule verdict_order when fourthDay() and hour(clock) >= 9 and not verdictGiven(wray) and not rebellion() {
    Assert verdictGiven(wray). Assert verdictOrder(wray). }
  // An example: whoever she holds for the decree, she hangs; whoever she holds for the cart, she takes to the lord.
  Rule maudie_hanged when verdictGiven(wray) and maudieTaken(maudie) and not maudieHanged(maudie) and captainView(sefton) < 3 { Assert maudieHanged(maudie). }
  Rule kit_hanged when verdictGiven(wray) and kitTaken(kit) and (kitSold(kit) or companyOffersKit(wray) or verdictRebellion(wray) or fireTried(wray) and not kitStoodDown(kit) and not kitTurned(kit) and not boardSunk(wray) or kitBlamed(kit)) and not kitHanged(kit) { Assert kitHanged(kit). }
  // The company is let out of the cellar at the verdict, fined, and told to be gone by the south road; the captain
  // has what she came for.
  Rule cellar_released when verdictGiven(wray) and heldInCellar(party) says "At nine the cellar door opens and a rider takes you up into the long hall, where the captain is sitting in the reeve's chair. She goes on peeling an apple, one long curl. 'You did what you did,' she says. 'I have what I came for.' A fine is taken from your purse. 'Be on the south road by noon, and do not come back to the lord's bridge this year.' The riders walk you to the drawbridge." {
    Retract heldInCellar(party). Assert at(party, overbridge_street). Assert banished(party). }
  Relation banished(group).
  Rule cellar_fine when banished(party) and not fined(party) { Assert fined(party). Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 5. }
  Relation fined(group).
  Rule halt_banished when banished(party) and at(party, gate_road) says "The captain's rider at the Bridge End shakes his head. 'Not this year,' he says." { Assert at(party, bridge_street). }
}

data/adventures/wrayford/clock.kyr:
Module wrayford "The Third Night" {
  // ── The three days ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Wrayford's days are counted from the company's coming, at each dawn after the first hour it is here: the day it
  // comes is the first. The dead were hanged four nights before. The captain comes at dusk on the third day; the third
  // night is the night after it, and in the small hours of the fourth day Maudie Pardoe goes to the gatehouse.
  Measure dayN(place). Relation dawned(place).
  Initially Set dayN(wray) to 1.
  Rule dawn_counts when hour(clock) == 6 and not dawned(wray) and watch(clock) >= 6 { Increase dayN(wray) by 1. Assert dawned(wray). }
  Rule dawn_passes when hour(clock) != 6 and dawned(wray) { Retract dawned(wray). }
  Query dayIs(n: place) means dayN(wray) == dayN(n).
  // Days by name, for rules that read like the city's own talk.
  Query firstDay() means dayN(wray) == 1.
  Query secondDay() means dayN(wray) == 2.
  Query thirdDay() means dayN(wray) == 3.
  Query fourthDay() means dayN(wray) == 4.
  Query fifthDay() means dayN(wray) == 5.
  Query morning() means hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 12.
  Query evening() means hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 22.
  Query smallHours() means hour(clock) >= 0 and hour(clock) < 5.
  // The third night: after the captain's coming, until the fourth day's dawn.
  Query thirdNight() means thirdDay() and (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 6).
  Query captainCome() means thirdDay() and (hour(clock) >= 19 or hour(clock) < 6) or dayN(wray) >= 4.

  // ── The river ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The mills above the weir grind by day and pen the river by night: from one in the morning until five the Wray
  // runs low below the bridge, and the old ford-stones are under a foot of water instead of six.
  Query lowWater() means hour(clock) >= 1 and hour(clock) < 5.
  // Dorcas runs her ferry from six in the morning until the curfew bell, and at night for those she has agreed to.
  Relation ferriesAtNight(group).
  Query ferryRunning() means hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 22 and at(dorcas, ferry_stage) or ferriesAtNight(party).

  // The drawbridge goes up at the curfew bell, for the night barges and against the night, and comes down at dawn.
  Thing drawbridge "the drawbridge" on drawbridge_span is scenery {
    State down "The drawbridge is down.".
    State raised blocking "The drawbridge stands up against the sky on its chains. Nobody crosses the river by it until it comes down at dawn.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(drawbridge, down).
  Rule curfew_raises when hour(clock) >= 22 and state(drawbridge, down) { Assert state(drawbridge, raised). }
  Rule small_hours_raised when hour(clock) < 5 and state(drawbridge, down) { Assert state(drawbridge, raised). }
  Rule dawn_lowers when hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) < 22 and state(drawbridge, raised) { Assert state(drawbridge, down). }
  Rule curfew_bell at gate_road when hour(clock) == 22 and not knows(party, curfew_known) says "Saint Wade's rings the curfew across the water, and on the bridge the drawbridge chains begin to grind." teaches curfew_known { }
  Discovery curfew_known "At the curfew bell, ten at night, the drawbridge goes up, and nobody crosses the bridge until it comes down at dawn.".

  // ── Where word reaches the company ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // News of the city is heard anywhere in Wrayford, on the bridge or in Overbridge; not out on the roads.
  Query inWrayford() means at(party, ?p) and not at(party, drove_road) and not at(party, south_road).
  // News already gone round, so it is not told twice.
  Relation spread(fact).
  // A place the company has left and come back to is told shortly.
  Relation visitedNow(place). Relation visitedBefore(place).
  Rule arrives_at when at(party, ?p) and not visitedNow(?p) { Assert visitedNow(?p). }
  Rule leaves_from when visitedNow(?p) and not at(party, ?p) { Retract visitedNow(?p). Assert visitedBefore(?p). }

  // ── Who the company is, here ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Wat Pardoe's elder child, come home (the campaign played alone: company.kyr); or a traveller, come down the drove
  // road with the world's own company. Everything said to kin is said only to kin.
  Relation homecomer(group).
  Query stranger(g: group) means not homecomer(g).

  // ── Aims the page can lead with ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Each is true while its question is open and says only what the company has learned; none names a way to answer it.
  Objective bury_the_dead when knows(party, third_night_custom) and stillHanging() and not buriedByNight(wray)
    "Wrayford buries its dead on the third day, or they do not rest. Three men have hung on the gatehouse rail since the night of the rising.".
  Objective kit_at_midnight when knows(party, kit_plan) and not cartersOut(carters) and not cartersTaken(carters)
    "At midnight on the second night Kit Pardoe and the young carters mean to burn the Bridge Company's counting-house.".
  Objective answer_the_captain when knows(party, captain_question) and not verdictGiven(wray)
    "The lord's captain comes at dusk on the third day, to ask Wrayford one question: is it in rebellion?".
  Objective who_wrote_the_letter when knows(party, letter_read) and not knows(party, hand_match)
    "Someone in Wrayford wrote to the riders at midnight, naming the road the carters took. The hand has not been matched.".
  Objective ice_for_the_boy when knows(party, ice_seen) and not jennetIced(jennet)
    "In the Hill's ice-house the blocks lie in the straw. In a front room on the bridge a boy has lain under a sheet for four days.".
}

data/adventures/wrayford/company.kyr:
Module wrayford "The Third Night" {
  // The campaign played alone: Wat Pardoe's elder child, three years away with the droves on the far side of the fells,
  // coming home on their mother's letter, a week after it was written. (placed.kyr is the world's own company, come in
  // by the drove road with no kin here.)
  Company party "You" of 1 to 3 at drove_road.
  Initially Set quantity(party, gold) to 9. Initially Set quantity(party, rations) to 2.
  Initially Assert homecomer(party).
  Initially Assert kin(party, maudie). Initially Assert kin(party, kit).
  Initially Assert kinship(maudie, called_mother). Initially Assert kinship(kit, called_brother).
  Entity called_mother: fact "your mother". Entity called_brother: fact "your brother".
}

data/adventures/wrayford/day.kyr:
Module wrayford "The Third Night" {
  // ── The Remonstrance ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Noon to two on the second day, in the Guildhall: the Bench of the Bridge Company moves a Remonstrance to the lord
  // against the toll it farms, and any citizen may move a clause. The Bench passes whatever costs it nothing it can be
  // seen to lose. If nobody moves anything, the clerk's own clause passes.
  Query benchSitting() means secondDay() and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 14 and not benchRose(wray).
  Relation benchRose(place). Relation moved(entity).
  Relation clauseCharity(place). Relation clauseRelease(place). Relation clauseWorse(place). Relation clauseAudit(place).
  Entity motion_release: fact "that the dead be released".
  Entity motion_charity: fact "that the dead be commended to the Liberty's charity".
  Entity motion_toll: fact "that the toll be lifted".
  Entity motion_audit: fact "that the Company's accounts be laid open".
  Person bench "the Bench of the Bridge Company" at guild_hall {
    Role "five aldermen in blue gowns at the long table". Ancestry human. Numbers 1. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
    Seen when benchSitting().
  }
  Observe bench_scene at guild_hall when benchSitting() "The Bench is sitting: five aldermen in blue gowns along the dais, Gidley in the middle, the clerk Inchbold at a little desk below with the Remonstrance before him, and the public benches full of carters with their caps on their knees, and the Hill's wives in the gallery with their fans. Gidley is reading the Remonstrance aloud. It is very long, and it is against the toll in every particular, and it ends: the Company remaining, notwithstanding, the lord's loyal farmers of the same.".
  Query canMove(a: group) means benchSitting() and at(a, guild_hall).
  Action move_release(actor: group, site: place) "Rise, and move that the dead be released from the rail" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and canMove(actor) and not moved(motion_release).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert moved(motion_release). }
    Result "There is a silence on the dais, and then a great deal of shuffling. Alderman Pocock says that it would be very unwise, at such a time, for the Company to be seen to dictate to the lord's officers. Alderman Dunch says the lord might take it amiss. Gidley says, with real tears, that his heart is with you, wholly, and the motion is put, and fails, four to one, the one being nobody: Gidley abstains, from emotion.".
  }
  // Or the Alderman has seen his own face that morning, painted as it is, and taken it for a portrait of his burden.
  Rule release_carried_portrait when moved(motion_release) and portraitHung(wray) and not honoriaLobbies(honoria) and not clauseRelease(wray) says "Gidley has been looking all the while past the speakers to the easel at the end of the hall, where Tom Lumley's Bench sits round its model bridge with his own face in the middle of it. Now he stands, and wipes his eyes, and says that a Company which bears the crossing can bear this, and that he votes for the motion; and Alderman Pocock, who owes him money, votes with him, and so does Alderman Dunch, who owes Pocock. It passes, three to two. At the easel, Tom Lumley puts his brushes away very carefully, so as not to be seen laughing." { Assert clauseRelease(wray). }
  Rule release_carried when moved(motion_release) and honoriaLobbies(honoria) and not clauseRelease(wray) says "And then, from the gallery, a woman's voice, quite clear: 'Prosper.' Alderman Gidley looks up at his wife among the fans. He looks for a long time. Then he stands, and says that on reflection he will vote, and that he votes for the motion, and Alderman Pocock, who owes him money, votes with him, and so does Alderman Dunch, who owes Pocock. It passes, three to two. The carters' benches do not cheer. They do not know what to do." { Assert clauseRelease(wray). }
  Action move_charity(actor: group, site: place) "Rise, and move that the dead be commended to the Liberty's charity, at the Liberty's charge, the Company's rights being reserved" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and canMove(actor) and knows(actor, bench_rule) and not moved(motion_charity).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert moved(motion_charity). Assert clauseCharity(wray). }
    Result "You put it as Inchbold would: the dead commended to the Liberty's charity, at the Liberty's charge, the Company's rights in all things being reserved and its loyalty to the lord unquestioned. There is a pause while the Bench looks for what it costs. It costs nothing. Gidley's face lights up. 'Charity,' he says, 'at the Liberty's charge,' and the motion is carried by acclamation, and the Bench congratulates itself at some length on its humanity. Inchbold writes it in. He looks up at you once, with something like professional respect.".
  }
  Action move_toll(actor: group, site: place) "Rise, and move that the toll be lifted" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and canMove(actor) and not moved(motion_toll).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert moved(motion_toll). }
    Result "The Bench laughs. Not unkindly: the way you laugh at a child who has asked why the sea is salt. Alderman Pocock wipes his eyes. 'The Company,' says Gidley, 'is the city's shield against the toll,' and the motion is not put. On the carters' benches a man says something very short, and is not hushed.".
  }
  Action move_audit(actor: group, site: place) "Rise, and move that the Company's accounts of the toll be laid open to the city" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and canMove(actor) and knows(actor, fire_pinch) and not moved(motion_audit).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert moved(motion_audit). Assert clauseAudit(wray). Assert pinchExposed(wray). Increase temper(wray) by 1. }
    Result "You say why: the oil flask in the ash, the shirt, the day-book. The hall goes so quiet you can hear the clock. Gidley stands up, purple, and says that the Company has nothing to hide, nothing, and that if its servant has robbed it the Company will be the first to know, and the motion is carried, and only afterwards, in the arcade, does he seem to understand what he has voted for. The carters' benches empty into the Market shouting PINCH.".
  }
  // At two, the Bench rises; if nobody moved anything of use, the clerk's clause is read in.
  Rule bench_rises when secondDay() and hour(clock) >= 14 and not benchRose(wray) { Assert benchRose(wray). }
  Rule worse_clause when benchRose(wray) and stillHanging() and not clauseCharity(wray) and not clauseRelease(wray) and not clauseWorse(wray) and inWrayford() says "At two the Bench rises. The Remonstrance goes to the lord with one clause added at the end, which the clerk read in and nobody opposed: that the dead remain upon the rail until the Company's loss in the riot shall have been reckoned by the lord's captain, the Company's claims being thereby secured. The reeve, it is said, read it in his court with his face like a shut door." { Assert clauseWorse(wray). }
  // A measure cannot go below nothing: an effect that would take it there makes the whole rule impossible.
  Rule worse_clause_hardens when clauseWorse(wray) and hulmeMoved(hulme) >= 1 and not clauseHardened(wray) { Assert clauseHardened(wray). Decrease hulmeMoved(hulme) by 1. }
  Relation clauseHardened(place).

  // ── The Liberty's charity: the dead released lawfully, before the captain ────────────────────────────────────────
  Query crossingLawful() means ruling(ruled_tithe) or pinchExposed(wray) or pinchGone(pinch) or ruling(ruled_carcass).
  Query benchLeave() means clauseCharity(wray) or clauseRelease(wray).
  Relation releaseUnderway(place). Relation reeveRelease(place). Relation releasedBy(place, entity).
  Entity by_charity: fact "the Liberty's charity". Entity by_reeve: fact "the reeve's own word". Entity by_captain: fact "the captain's leave". Entity by_city: fact "the city itself".
  Action lay_before_reeve(actor: group, site: place) "Lay before the reeve the Bench's leave, the Abbess's claim, and the ruling at the chain" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(hulme, site) and stillHanging() and not captainCome()
      and benchLeave() and abbessClaims(abbess) and crossingLawful() and not releaseUnderway(wray).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert releaseUnderway(wray). Assert lawfulRelease(wray). Assert releasedBy(wray, by_charity). }
    Result "He reads the Abbess's letter, and the Bench's clause in Inchbold's copperplate, and the line in Pinch's tally, slowly, all three, twice. Then he puts them square on the desk, edge to edge, the way a clerk does. 'Cover,' he says. 'There it is.' He does not look pleased. He looks like a man who has been let off something and knows it. He calls his constable. 'Cut them down,' he says. 'Give them to the Abbess's brothers at the chain. They cross as the Liberty's tithe, by the Bench's leave.' And then, to you, so low you barely hear it: 'Thank you.'".
  }
  // The reeve's own word, moved far enough by people and not by papers: he does it himself, by day, and will answer
  // for it to the captain.
  Rule reeve_relents when hulmeMoved(hulme) >= 3 and stillHanging() and not captainCome() and not releaseUnderway(wray)
    and hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 18 and inWrayford() says "In the middle of the day Simon Hulme comes out of the Guildhall alone, without his chain of office, and walks down to the Bridge End, and the crowd parts for him. He goes up the gate-ward's stair. Gault meets him at the top and says something, and the reeve says something back, and Gault stands aside. And the reeve of Wrayford cuts the three down from the rail with his own knife, one by one, and hands them down to the carters below, and comes down after them, and goes back up the Cartway to the Guildhall, and shuts the door." {
    Assert releaseUnderway(wray). Assert reeveRelease(wray). Assert releasedBy(wray, by_reeve). }
  // Once released, by day: carried over, graves dug, buried.
  Rule release_takes_down when releaseUnderway(wray) and stillHanging() { Assert state(rail, cut). Assert takenDown(wray).
    Assert at(wat_dead, wades_acre). Assert at(dunstan_dead, wades_acre). Assert at(joss_dead, wades_acre). Assert corbinWillDig(wray). }
  Rule release_graves when releaseUnderway(wray) and state(graves, marked) and corbinResigned(corbin) { Assert state(graves, dug). }
  Rule release_buries when releaseUnderway(wray) and state(graves, dug) and not buried(wat_dead) says "In Wade's Acre, in the afternoon, the three are buried by the church door, with Wrayford standing round the wall and on the wall and on the roofs of the tan-yards. The Abbess says the office herself." {
    Assert buried(wat_dead). Assert buried(dunstan_dead). Assert buried(joss_dead). Assert buriedLawfully(wray).
    Assert at(wat_dead, limbo). Assert at(dunstan_dead, limbo). Assert at(joss_dead, limbo). }

  // ── The two mothers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation jennetKnowsTruth(group). Relation mothersMet(place). Relation mothersWalk(place). Relation mothersWalked(place).
  Relation mothersTurnedBack(place). Measure walkDay(place).
  Rule jennet_learns_from_kit when kitToldJennet(jennet) and not jennetKnowsTruth(jennet) { Assert jennetKnowsTruth(jennet). }
  // Told by someone she trusts, she keeps it; by someone she does not, she goes to the reeve.
  Rule jennet_keeps when jennetTold(jennet) and jennetTrust(jennet) >= 3 and not jennetKnowsTruth(jennet) and not kitInformedOn(kit) { Assert jennetKnowsTruth(jennet). }
  Rule jennet_goes_to_reeve when jennetTold(jennet) and jennetTrust(jennet) < 3 and not kitInformedOn(kit) and not jennetKnowsTruth(jennet) says "Jennet Hobday walks up the Cartway to the Guildhall and asks for the reeve, and is with him an hour. In the evening the riders take Kit Pardoe from the yards." {
    Assert kitInformedOn(kit). Assert kitTaken(kit). Assert at(kit, guild_cellar). Set kitTrust(kit) to 0. }
  Relation kitInformedOn(group).
  Observe jennet_after_tell at hobday_room when jennetTold(jennet) and jennetTrust(jennet) >= 3 and not kitToldJennet(jennet) "Jennet Hobday sits by the bed with her hands in her lap. 'He lifted him in,' she says, not to you. 'He lifted him in like something precious and drove for the bone-setter.' She says it again, as if learning it. 'You've sat with me,' she says. 'I'll not hang a boy for this. I've had enough of hanging.'".
  Action bring_jennet(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Jennet Hobday to come with you to Wain Row, and sit with Maudie Pardoe" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hobday_room) and at(jennet, hobday_room)
      and jennetKnowsTruth(jennet) and jennetTrust(jennet) >= 3 and stillHanging() and not mothersMet(wray) and not captainCome().
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert mothersMet(wray). Set walkDay(wray) to dayN(wray) + 1. Assert at(actor, wain_row). Assert at(jennet, pardoe_kitchen). }
    Result "She looks at the bed for a long time. Then she puts on her shawl. You walk with her the length of Bridge Street and up the Cartway and down Wain Row, and people stop in their doorways to watch the toll-keeper's widow go to the carter's widow's door. Maudie Pardoe opens it with flour on her hands. The two women look at each other. Then Maudie stands aside, and Jennet goes in, and the door shuts, and you are not asked in, and you do not ask. After an hour Maudie comes to the door and says to you, quite briskly, as if arranging a wash-day: 'In the morning. Both of them. Over the bridge, in the light, with the city behind us. And let them stop us.'".
  }
  // The morning after: if the city is behind them, nobody stops them.
  Rule mothers_set_out when mothersMet(wray) and dayN(wray) >= walkDay(wray) and hour(clock) >= 8 and stillHanging() and not mothersWalk(wray) and not captainCome() and temper(wray) >= 2 {
    Assert mothersWalk(wray). Assert releaseUnderway(wray). Assert releasedBy(wray, by_city). Assert mothersWalked(wray). Assert corbinWillDig(wray). }
  Rule mothers_turned when mothersMet(wray) and dayN(wray) >= walkDay(wray) and hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 9 and stillHanging() and not mothersWalk(wray) and temper(wray) < 2 and not mothersTurnedBack(wray) says "In the morning the two widows walk down the Cartway together to the Bridge End with a handful of neighbours behind them, and at the gate-ward's door Sergeant Gault meets them and says, not unkindly, 'Not on my watch, mothers. Go home.' There are not enough of them. They go home. But by noon the whole of Wrayford has heard of it." {
    Assert mothersTurnedBack(wray). Increase temper(wray) by 1. Set walkDay(wray) to dayN(wray) + 1. }
  Rule mothers_walk_told when mothersWalk(wray) and inWrayford() and not spread(mothers_fact) says "In the morning Maudie Pardoe and Jennet Hobday walk down the Cartway together to the Bridge End, arm in arm, in black, and behind them comes Wrayford: Wain Row and Northgate, the yards, the Shambles, the fish-wives from the Wharf, Annis Pye with her fist shut, Win Fenner with four children, people from the Hill with their hats in their hands, so many that the Bridge End will not hold them and they stand back up the Cartway to the Cross. At the gate-ward's door Sergeant Gault looks at them for a long time. Then he takes his key off his belt and unlocks the door himself, and stands aside, and says to his riders, 'Let them be.' The toll-keeper's widow goes up first. When the three come down from the rail it is into the arms of the city, and they cross the bridge on carters' shoulders, and Amos Pinch, at the chain, lifts it without a word, and does not write anything down. Behind them, carried on a hurdle, comes Ned Hobday. Halfway over, by the chapel on the middle pier, somebody starts the carters' hymn, and then the whole bridge is singing it, badly, in the heat: carry me over, Wade, carry me over." { Assert spread(mothers_fact). }
  Entity mothers_fact: fact "The two mothers walked".
  Rule ned_buried when mothersWalked(wray) and buried(wat_dead) and not nedBuried(jennet) { Assert nedBuried(jennet). }
  Relation nedBuried(group).
  Rule ned_buried_lawful when buriedLawfully(wray) and not nedBuried(jennet) and corbinWillDig(wray) { Assert nedBuried(jennet). }
  Rule hulme_resigns when mothersWalked(wray) and buried(wat_dead) and not hulmeResigned(hulme) and hour(clock) >= 18 says "In the evening the reeve of Wrayford takes off his chain of office in the Guildhall before the Bench, and lays it on the long table, and goes home." { Assert hulmeResigned(hulme). }
  Relation hulmeResigned(group).
  Rule jennet_goes_home when mothersWalked(wray) and buried(wat_dead) and not at(jennet, hobday_room) { Assert at(jennet, hobday_room). }
}

data/adventures/wrayford/endings.kyr:
Module wrayford "The Third Night" {
  // ── Endings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Reached at the captain's verdict on the fourth morning, by what the three days prepared. The first that holds is
  // the one told. None of them is a custom kept for ever after: each is the morning after, told plainly.
  Ending fire "The Fire" when verdictRebellion(wray) "The captain gives her verdict at nine in the Guildhall, and it takes one sentence. By noon the carters' row is burning, Wain Row and the yards behind it, and the captain's riders stand at the end of every lane to see that nobody puts it out. Ten men are hanged from the gatehouse rail beside the three, which is the lord's law for a rising, and the rail is not long enough, and they use the drawbridge chains, as her father did at the Michaelmas fair, and she watches it done from the same place at the Bridge End where she held his horses. In the evening the riders go home down the south road with the toll money and the lord's thanks, and Wrayford stands in its own smoke and does not speak to itself for a generation. The Company rebuilds its counting-house in stone.".
  Ending too_late "Too Late" when verdictGiven(wray) and tooLate(wray) "The captain hangs Maudie Pardoe from the gatehouse rail at nine in the morning, beside her husband, under the reeve's own decree, which is on the door in his son's best hand. Simon Hulme stands below with his hat in his hands and his knife still in his coat, where it was when he came down the Cartway a quarter of an hour behind her. He resigns that afternoon. In a week he is gone from Wrayford, nobody knows where. The three are taken down at noon and buried with her in Wade's Acre, four graves by the church door, and old Corbin digs them, and says nothing at all, and the reeve's house on the Hill stands empty, and nobody in the city will buy it.".
  Ending away "Away" when verdictGiven(wray) and maudieHanged(maudie) and not inWrayford() "You are not in Wrayford when it happens, and you hear it weeks later, in another country, from a drover in an inn, the way news of a place you have left always comes: badly told, by someone who does not know they are telling it to you. A carter's widow went up to the gatehouse in the night with her bread knife to cut her husband down, and the captain hanged her beside him in the morning, under the reeve's own decree. The drover shakes his head and says it was a hard thing, and drinks, and talks about the price of cattle.".
  Ending third_night "The Third Night" when verdictGiven(wray) and maudieHanged(maudie) "At nine in the morning Captain Sefton gives her verdict in the Guildhall: Wrayford is in order, its ringleaders on the rail, and one more, taken in the act against the lord's dead, under the reeve's decree. She hangs Maudie Pardoe from the gatehouse rail beside her husband before ten. The reeve watches from the Bridge End and does not look away, because he wrote it, or his son did. The captain takes the toll money and goes home down the south road, and at dusk on the fourth day the reeve has all four cut down and given to the Abbess, and Corbin digs, and Wrayford buries them by the church door; and every year after, on the third night, nobody in Northgate goes out of doors; and the eel-men on the night barges say that someone wades at Wade's Step, singing, with something heavy on her back.".
  Ending bargain "The Company's Bargain" when verdictGiven(wray) and kitSold(kit) "The captain takes Kit Pardoe south with her at noon, tied to a rider's saddle, for the lord's justice at Harbury, which is a rope. The Company, as it promised, asks the captain's mercy for the dead, justice having been done, and she grants it with a look at Alderman Gidley that he will not forget, and the three are buried that afternoon in Wade's Acre. Maudie Pardoe stands at the graveside and does not look at you once. You have forty crowns. The Company prints a ballad of the son who let his father die for him, at a penny, and it sells well.".
  Ending mothers "The Two Mothers" when verdictGiven(wray) and mothersWalked(wray) "When the captain comes up the south road at dusk on the third day there is nothing on the rail. There is a funeral: four new graves by the church door in Wade's Acre, the toll-keeper's boy among them, carried over the bridge on the city's shoulders, the way Wade carried the child, and the whole of Wrayford still standing about in the Liberty in its black, not going home. She looks at it a long time from her horse. In the morning she gives her verdict in one line: that the city is in order. She takes the toll money and goes home. The toll stands; the Company keeps its farm; Simon Hulme is not reeve any more. On Bridge Street, in the toll-keeper's house, Jennet Hobday has opened her shutters, and Maudie Pardoe comes on Sundays, with bread.".
  Ending charity "The Liberty's Charity" when verdictGiven(wray) and releasedBy(wray, by_charity) "The captain finds nothing on the rail but three cut ropes, and a letter from the Abbess claiming her dead, and the Bench's clause in Inchbold's copperplate, and the collector's ruling, and three new graves in Wade's Acre, dug square by old Corbin, who says it is the best work he has done in forty years. She reads the papers at supper with an expression nobody can read. In the morning she gives her verdict, that Wrayford is in order, and goes home with the toll money. The reeve keeps his office. The Company keeps its farm, and has its charity entered in its minutes, at the Liberty's charge. Everyone in Wrayford is a little ashamed, and the rail is empty, and the Company's minutes record the charity twice, in two hands, because the second clerk did not trust the first.".
  Ending reeve "The Reeve's Release" when verdictGiven(wray) and reeveRelease(wray) "The captain hears at supper that the reeve of Wrayford cut the rebels down from the lord's rail with his own hands. In the morning she gives her verdict: that the city is in order, and its reeve is not. Simon Hulme hands her his chain of office on the Guildhall steps, and she takes it, not unkindly, and rides home with it and the toll money. He goes on living in the house on the Hill, and keeps a garden, and on the third night of every month walks down to the Bridge End and stands under the gatehouse for an hour, and nobody asks him why.".
  Ending earth "Earth on Him" when verdictGiven(wray) and buriedByNight(wray) "When the captain comes up the south road there is nothing on the rail but three cut ropes, and in Wade's Acre there are three graves nobody will admit to digging. The reeve has his answer for her, because he had to have one. She takes it, and the toll money, and gives her verdict that Wrayford is in order, and goes. They were carried over, the old way, in the dark, by someone's back. In Wain Row Maudie Pardoe bakes bread for three days and gives it all away. Nobody in the city ever says, out loud, who climbed the gatehouse in the small hours, and everybody knows.".
  Ending third_man "The Third Man" when verdictGiven(wray) and (buried(wat_dead) or buried(dunstan_dead) or buried(joss_dead)) and not buriedByNight(wray) and not buriedLawfully(wray) "When the captain comes up the south road there is nothing on the rail but three cut ropes, and in Wade's Acre there are new graves that nobody will admit to digging, and not enough of them. The one who could not be got over the water before the river rose was found by the reeve's men at first light, where he was left, and the captain has him put in the lord's lime at the crossroads on the south road, alone, which is the lord's law for a rebel's body. Then she gives her verdict that Wrayford is in order, and goes. Ever after, in the alehouses of Northgate, Wrayford argues about which of the three it was, and whether it matters; and it does.".
  Ending lime "The Lime" when verdictGiven(wray) and not buried(wat_dead) and not buried(dunstan_dead) and not buried(joss_dead) and not maudieHanged(maudie) "The captain gives her verdict that Wrayford is in order, and orders the ringleaders taken down and put in the lord's lime at the crossroads on the south road, which is the lord's law for rebels' bodies. It is done at noon. There is no grave, and nobody carried them over; the cart did, which is not the same. Maudie Pardoe stands in her doorway in Wain Row while the cart goes past to the south road with the three in it, and does not go in until it is out of sight, and does not speak to you, or to anyone, for a long time; and Corbin, at the Acre, picks up his spade and digs for Ned Hobday and for Gidley's aunt, very slowly, because there is no reason now not to.".

  // ── What became of them, told at the verdict ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule fate_kit_hanged when verdictGiven(wray) and kitHanged(kit) and not kitSold(kit) and not spread(fate_kit) says "Kit Pardoe goes south with the captain, tied to a rider's saddle, for the lord's justice at Harbury. He looks back once, at the bridge." { Assert spread(fate_kit). }
  Entity fate_kit: fact "Kit's fate".
  Rule fate_maudie_fire when verdictGiven(wray) and verdictRebellion(wray) and maudieHanged(maudie) and not spread(fate_maudie) says "Maudie Pardoe is the first of the ten. She goes up the gate-ward's stair on her own feet, and does not look for anyone in the crowd." { Assert spread(fate_maudie). }
  Entity fate_maudie: fact "Maudie's fate".
  Rule fate_kit_free when verdictGiven(wray) and not kitTaken(kit) and not spread(fate_kit) and kitTrust(kit) >= 2 says "Kit Pardoe goes back to the yards, and to his father's place on the box, and the horse that went forward in the press, which he will not let anyone else drive." { Assert spread(fate_kit). }
  Rule fate_kit_cellar when verdictGiven(wray) and kitTaken(kit) and not kitHanged(kit) and not spread(fate_kit) says "The captain, having what she came for, has Kit Pardoe let out of the cellar with a cuff and a warning, and he walks home up the Cartway in the sun with his hands in his pockets." { Assert spread(fate_kit). Retract kitTaken(kit). Assert at(kit, carters_yards). }
  Rule fate_hal when verdictGiven(wray) and halTakesBlame(hal) and not spread(fate_hal) says "Hal Hulme comes out of the cellar when the captain has gone, and stands blinking in the Market, and his father is waiting for him at the Guildhall door, and they go home together up the Mercer Steps, very slowly, not talking." { Assert spread(fate_hal). }
  Entity fate_hal: fact "Hal's fate".
  Rule fate_hal_told_cut when verdictGiven(wray) and halToldFather(hal) and reeveRelease(wray) and not halTakesBlame(hal) and not spread(fate_hal) says "Hal Hulme, it is said, told his father what he did on the night of the rising, and his father sat with his head in his hands until dawn; and it was the next day that the reeve went down to the Bridge End with his knife." { Assert spread(fate_hal). }
  Rule fate_hal_told when verdictGiven(wray) and halToldFather(hal) and not reeveRelease(wray) and not halTakesBlame(hal) and not spread(fate_hal) says "Hal Hulme, it is said, told his father what he did on the night of the rising, before supper, and his father sat with his head in his hands until dawn, and in the morning went to his court as usual." { Assert spread(fate_hal). }
  Rule fate_corbin when verdictGiven(wray) and reconciled(wray) and not spread(fate_corbin) says "At the end of the week the banns are read at Saint Wade's for Corbin, sexton, of this parish, and Dorcas Mudd, ferry-woman, of the city, and the whole Liberty laughs, and so does the whole Wharf, and neither of them minds at all." { Assert spread(fate_corbin). }
  Entity fate_corbin: fact "Corbin and Dorcas".
  Rule fate_annis when verdictGiven(wray) and annisRing(annis) and not spread(fate_annis) says "Annis Pye wears Joss Wilder's ring on a string round her neck, and does not set up her pitch at the Bridge End again, but on the Wharf, where nobody ever hanged anybody." { Assert spread(fate_annis). }
  Entity fate_annis: fact "Annis".
  Rule fate_robin when verdictGiven(wray) and (robinHome(robin) or robinStays(robin)) and buried(wat_dead) and not spread(fate_robin) says "At the burying, somebody's boy beat a drum, slow, a bear-ward's drum with a bear painted on it: Robin Tull, who had nobody to bury, and came anyway." { Assert spread(fate_robin). }
  Entity fate_robin: fact "Robin".
  Rule fate_win when verdictGiven(wray) and winHelped(party) and buried(dunstan_dead) and not spread(fate_win) says "Win Fenner stood at Dunstan's grave with her four children in a row by height, and the chisels in the eldest's hands." { Assert spread(fate_win). }
  Entity fate_win: fact "Win".
  Rule fate_pinch when verdictGiven(wray) and (captainPinch(party) or pinchExposed(wray)) and not pinchGone(pinch) and not spread(fate_pinch) says "Amos Pinch goes south with the captain's baggage, for the lord's court at Harbury, on foot behind the led horse, with the day-book under his arm. He asked to carry it himself." { Assert spread(fate_pinch). Assert pinchGone(pinch). Assert at(pinch, limbo). }
  Entity fate_pinch: fact "Pinch".
}

data/adventures/wrayford/fire.kyr:
Module wrayford "The Third Night" {
  // ── Kit's night ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At midnight on the second night Kit and the young carters go for the Company's counting-house with lamp-oil.
  // The Company's clerk hears everything at the Nine Wheels: Gault and two riders are waiting in the dark of the
  // arcade. Unless Kit has been talked down, or turned to sinking the board, or is held, or is walking with you.
  Query kitMeansFire() means not kitStoodDown(kit) and not kitTurned(kit) and not kitTaken(kit) and not travelsWith(kit, party).
  Query fireHour() means secondDay() and hour(clock) < 2.
  Person ambush "two of the lord's riders" at limbo {
    Role "two of Gault's riders, waiting in the dark of the arcade". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 2. Numbers 2. Peaceable. Pronouns they.
  }
  Initially Assert takesPrisoners(ambush). Initially Assert serves(ambush, gault).
  Relation ambushLaid(place). Relation fireTried(place). Relation boardSunk(place). Relation fireFought(place).
  Rule ambush_laid when secondDay() and hour(clock) >= 23 and not ambushLaid(wray) and (kitMeansFire() or kitJoined(kit)) and not kitTurned(kit) and not kitStoodDown(kit) {
    Assert ambushLaid(wray). Assert gaultAway(gault). Assert at(gault, counting_room). Assert at(ambush, counting_room). }
  Observe ambush_seen at counting_room when ambushLaid(wray) and not fireTried(wray) and not fireFought(wray) "In the dark of the counting-house, behind the counter, something shifts: a buff coat, the gleam of a drawn blade. Sergeant Gault and two of his riders are waiting here in the dark.".
  // They come at midnight.
  Rule carters_go when fireHour() and (kitMeansFire() or kitJoined(kit)) and not kitTurned(kit) and not kitStoodDown(kit) and not cartersOut(carters) and not fireTried(wray) {
    Assert cartersOut(carters). Assert kitOut(kit). Assert at(carters, counting_room). Assert at(kit, counting_room). }
  // With the company there beside them: Gault comes out of the dark at them.
  Rule ambush_springs when cartersOut(carters) and at(party, counting_room) and ambushLaid(wray) and not fireFought(wray) says "The young carters come into the counting-house with the oil, and Kit with a lantern, and Sergeant Gault stands up from behind the counter. 'Evening,' he says, and two of the lord's riders step out of the dark either side of the door." {
    Assert fireFought(wray). Retract peaceable(gault). Retract peaceable(ambush). Assert assails(gault, party). Assert assails(ambush, party). }
  // Without the company: Gault takes them in the act.
  Rule ambush_takes when cartersOut(carters) and not at(party, counting_room) and ambushLaid(wray) and not fireTried(wray) and not fireFought(wray) says "The milk-boy brings it before dawn, hammering on doors: the young carters went for the Company's counting-house at midnight with lamp-oil, and Sergeant Gault was waiting in the dark for them, and the fire was out before it was lit, and Kit Pardoe and two others are in the Guildhall cellar." {
    Assert fireTried(wray). Assert kitTaken(kit). Assert cartersTaken(carters). Assert at(kit, guild_cellar). Assert at(carters, guild_cellar).
    Retract cartersOut(carters). Retract kitOut(kit). Retract gaultAway(gault). Assert at(ambush, limbo). }
  // Won: the counting-house burns.
  Rule counting_burns when fireFought(wray) and (not able(gault) or routed(gault)) and (not able(ambush) or routed(ambush)) and not countingBurned(wray) says "The oil goes on the ledgers and the lantern after it, and the counting-house of the Worshipful Company of the Bridge goes up with a sound like a great breath. The gold bridge over the door melts and runs. By the time the Market is awake the whole of it is burning, and the bells are ringing, and nobody in Wrayford will ever again be able to say there was no rising." {
    Assert countingBurned(wray). Assert fireTried(wray). Retract cartersOut(carters). Retract kitOut(kit). Retract gaultAway(gault). }
  Rule fire_lost when fireFought(wray) and at(party, counting_room) and (captured(gault, party) or captured(ambush, party)) says "You come round in the Guildhall cellar on the straw, with Kit beside you with his face cut, and the young carters, and the smell of lamp-oil on your hands." {
    Retract captured(gault, party). Retract captured(ambush, party). Assert at(party, guild_cellar). Assert heldInCellar(party). Assert kitTaken(kit). Assert at(kit, guild_cellar).
    Assert cartersTaken(carters). Assert at(carters, guild_cellar). Assert fireTried(wray). Retract cartersOut(carters). Retract kitOut(kit). Retract gaultAway(gault).
    Assert peaceable(gault). Assert peaceable(ambush). Assert at(ambush, limbo). }
  // And the proof of the first fire goes in the second: Pinch's day-book, under his mattress behind the counter.
  Rule daybook_burns when countingBurned(wray) and at(daybook, pinch_room) { Retract at(daybook, pinch_room). }
  Observe counting_burned at counting_room when countingBurned(wray) "The counting-house is a shell: black walls, the counter charcoal, a smell that will be in the Market for a year. Over the doorway a lump of gold metal hangs where the bridge was.".
  // Turned: the new toll-board goes into the river instead, and nobody hangs for a board.
  Rule board_sinks when fireHour() and kitTurned(kit) and not boardSunk(wray) and not kitTaken(kit) {
    Assert boardSunk(wray). Increase temper(wray) by 2. }
  Rule board_told when boardSunk(wray) and inWrayford() and hour(clock) >= 6 and not spread(board_fact) says "All Wrayford is laughing by breakfast. In the night somebody unbolted the Company's new toll-board from beside the booth, all eight feet of it, freshly painted, and carried it down Bridge End and threw it in the Wray, for the second time in a week, and the sergeant and two riders sat in the dark of the counting-house all night waiting for a fire that never came. Amos Pinch stood at the booth this morning and ruled from memory, and got the price of a beast wrong, and the drovers cheered him." { Assert spread(board_fact). }
  Entity board_fact: fact "The board in the river".
  Rule ambush_stands_down when dayN(wray) >= 3 and ambushLaid(wray) and not fireTried(wray) and not fireFought(wray) { Retract gaultAway(gault). Assert at(ambush, limbo). Assert fireTried(wray). }
  Rule fire_carters_home when (fireTried(wray) or boardSunk(wray)) and cartersOut(carters) and not cartersTaken(carters) { Retract cartersOut(carters). Retract kitOut(kit). }
  // Standing in the door at the last moment, with a brother who trusts you.
  Action stand_in_door(actor: group, site: place) "Stand in the counting-house door, and tell Kit no" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, counting_room) and at(kit, counting_room) and cartersOut(carters)
      and kitTrusts(actor) and not fireFought(wray) and not kitStoodDown(kit).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert kitStoodDown(kit). Retract cartersOut(carters). Retract kitOut(kit). Assert at(kit, wheels_taproom). Assert at(carters, wheels_taproom). }
    Result "You stand in the door with your back to Gault's dark and say no, and Kit looks at you over the lantern, and at the oil in the others' hands, and something goes out of his face. 'Home,' he says to them. 'Home.' They go, and behind you in the dark of the counting-house someone lets out a long breath, and a blade goes back into its scabbard.".
  }
}

data/adventures/wrayford/hill.kyr:
Module wrayford "The Third Night" {
  // ── Mercer Hill ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe hill_scene at mercer_hill when not dark() and not visitedBefore(mercer_hill) "Mercer Hill: the houses of people who no longer have to live near what they sell. Gardens with walls, a view down over the roofs to the river and the bridge, a row of young limes. From up here you can see the gatehouse square and small at the end of the bridge, and what hangs from it, and somebody on this hill has planted the limes so that one day, when they are grown, nobody will have to.".
  Observe hill_again at mercer_hill when not dark() and visitedBefore(mercer_hill) "Mercer Hill: walled gardens, the young limes, the view of the bridge.".
  Observe hill_night at mercer_hill when dark() "Mercer Hill at night: lit windows behind garden walls, and the river below, and the brazier on the gatehouse leads, very small.".

  // ── The reeve ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe study_scene at hulme_study when true "The reeve's study: books of the city's statutes, a map of the bridge with every arch numbered, a fire, two chairs, and a desk with the reeve's seal on it in a dish, and a stack of papers in a round careful clerk's hand.".
  Person hulme "Simon Hulme" at guild_hall {
    Role "the Reeve of Wrayford, grey and careful". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "Simon Hulme stops signing, caps the ink, and you watch him decide, in the space of a breath, to be the reeve and not anything else. 'You have come about Tuesday,' he says. 'Everyone has. I will tell you what I tell everyone, and you may judge what it costs me.'".
    Greets again "Simon Hulme puts the pen down at once this time, which costs him something. 'You will have heard more by now than I have,' he says. 'Sit, and tell me the worst of it first. I would rather not be surprised on the stairs.'".
  }
  Rule hulme_court when hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 17 and not at(hulme, guild_hall) and not hulmeAway(hulme) { Assert at(hulme, guild_hall). }
  Rule hulme_home when (hour(clock) >= 17 or hour(clock) < 9) and not at(hulme, hulme_study) and not hulmeAway(hulme) { Assert at(hulme, hulme_study). }
  Relation hulmeAway(group).
  Measure hulmeMoved(group). Initially Set hulmeMoved(hulme) to 0.
  Relation hulmeAsked(group). Relation hulmeAnswered(group).
  Discovery hulme_reasons "The reeve keeps the dead on the rail because the captain comes at dusk on the third day to see whether Wrayford is in rebellion. If she finds the city in order, she takes the toll money and goes. If she finds it in rebellion, the lord's law is ten hangings and the carters' row burned.".
  Discovery charity_path "The reeve would release the dead before the captain comes, if he were given cover: the Bench's leave, which the Company will not give for nothing, and someone to take them who is beyond the reeve's writ, such as the Abbess of Overbridge, if she claimed them, and their crossing ruled lawful at the bridge.".
  Topic hulme_why with hulme "Ask the reeve why the dead must stay on the rail" when true once {
    Says "'Because the captain comes at dusk on the third day,' says Simon Hulme, 'and asks one question: is Wrayford in rebellion. If she finds the city quiet and its ringleaders on the rail, she takes the toll money and goes home. If she finds it in rebellion, the lord's law is ten hanged for every rider hurt and the carters' row burned to the stones.' He says it as if he had said it many times, to himself. 'Three men on a rail, or thirty. I have kept this city twenty years.' His hand is flat on the desk. 'I did not hang them. I would have brought them to the lord's court. The riders carried a warrant I was not shown.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hulme_reasons). }
  }
  // Kin: he stood godfather to Kit. He asks his question once.
  Event hulme_question near hulme when homecomer(party) and knows(party, hulme_reasons) and addressed(hulme, party) and not hulmeAsked(party) "He squares the papers on the desk, edge to edge. 'You were in my house every day of your childhood,' he says. 'You and Hal. Tell me, then. You've come home and found your father on the rail, and you're the only one in this city who can say anything to me I'd listen to.' His voice does not rise. 'What would you have me do?'" then { Assert hulmeAsked(party). }
  Topic answer_cut with hulme "Tell him: cut them down, and let the captain find a city that buries its dead" when hulmeAsked(actor) and not hulmeAnswered(actor) once {
    Says "He shuts his eyes. 'A city that buries its dead,' he says. 'That's a thing to say. That's a fine thing.' He opens them. 'And when she asks who cut them down against the lord's warrant?' He waits. You do not have an answer, and he sees it. 'No,' he says, gently. 'Neither have I.' But he does not look away from you.".
    On discuss { Assert hulmeAnswered(actor). Increase hulmeMoved(hulme) by 1. }
  }
  Topic answer_liberty with hulme "Tell him: give them to the Liberty, and let the Abbess's charity be the city's cover" when hulmeAsked(actor) and not hulmeAnswered(actor) once {
    Says "That makes him look up properly. 'The Liberty,' he says slowly. 'If the Abbess claimed them. If the Bench gave me leave, which they won't, for nothing. If the crossing were ruled lawful at the chain, so it's not a felon's goods going over the bridge.' He is counting on his fingers like a clerk. 'Then it's not the city releasing rebels. It's the Liberty taking up its dead, as it has the right, and the city standing aside, as it must.' He looks at you. 'Get me those three things, and I'll give them up before the captain's in sight.'".
    On discuss { Assert hulmeAnswered(actor). Assert knows(actor, charity_path). }
  }
  Topic answer_hang with hulme "Tell him: then hang me beside him" when hulmeAsked(actor) and not hulmeAnswered(actor) once {
    Says "He flinches. It is the first thing that has touched him, and he cannot hide it. 'Don't,' he says. 'Don't say that to me.' He gets up and goes to the window and stands with his back to you for a long time. 'Get out,' he says at last, quite gently. 'Go home to your mother.'".
    On discuss { Assert hulmeAnswered(actor). Increase hulmeMoved(hulme) by 1. }
  }
  // After the Bench's clause: its dead are now the Company's surety, and the reeve its bailiff. Anyone may say so.
  Topic hulme_clause with hulme "Put it to the reeve that the Bench has made his dead the Company's surety, and him its bailiff" when clauseWorse(wray) and stillHanging() once {
    Says "He has the Remonstrance on his desk; he has read it more than once. 'Its surety,' he says. 'Yes.' He turns it face down. 'I kept them on the rail for the city. Three men, so that it should not be thirty. And the Company has written under my seal that they stay there till its riot-money is counted.' He looks at the decree on the wall, in his son's hand. 'I did not hang men to be a debt-collector's pledge.' He does not say anything else, but he has not turned the paper back over.".
    On discuss { Increase hulmeMoved(hulme) by 1. }
  }
  Topic hulme_release with hulme "Ask the reeve what would let him release the dead" when stranger(actor) and knows(actor, hulme_reasons) once {
    Says "He considers you: a stranger, who has no stake, and is asking anyway. 'Cover,' he says. 'If the Abbess of Overbridge claimed them, they'd be the Liberty's, not the city's rebels. If the Bench gave me leave. If the crossing at the chain were ruled lawful, so it's not a felon's goods going over the bridge. Three things.' He shakes his head. 'The Bench will give nothing for nothing, and the Abbess gives nothing at all.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, charity_path). }
  }
  Topic hulme_kit with hulme "Tell the reeve what Kit Pardoe means to do tomorrow night" when knows(actor, kit_plan) and not kitStoodDown(kit) and not kitTurned(kit) and not kitTaken(kit) and not kitBetrayed(kit) once {
    Says "The reeve listens with his hand over his eyes. 'The counting-house,' he says. 'He'd hang. They'd hang him with his father.' He takes his hand away. 'I'll have him taken up tonight, before. The cellar's dry. It's better than the rope.' He looks at you. 'He'll not forgive you.'".
    On discuss { Assert kitBetrayed(kit). Assert kitTaken(kit). Set kitTrust(kit) to 0. }
  }
  Rule kit_taken_up when kitBetrayed(kit) and not at(kit, guild_cellar) and not travelsWith(kit, party) { Assert at(kit, guild_cellar). Assert kitTaken(kit). }

  // ── Hal ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person hal "Hal Hulme" at guild_hall {
    Role "the reeve's son, who writes his father's papers". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "Hal Hulme is copying a fair hand out of his father's rough one, and has a second sheet at his elbow that he lays face down, unhurriedly, before he stands. For a moment he is twelve years old and caught at it; then he is not. 'Father's papers,' he says. 'I write them. I do not decide them.'".
    Greets again "Hal Hulme has the second sheet face up this time, and does not trouble to cover it. 'I decided,' he says, 'that if you were going to tell my father, you would have done it by now.'".
  }
  // His father's clerk by day; at dusk he goes down to the starling under the middle arch, where he always went; home.
  Relation halAway(group).
  Rule hal_clerk when hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 18 and not at(hal, guild_hall) and not halAway(hal) { Assert at(hal, guild_hall). }
  Rule hal_starling when hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 21 and not at(hal, starling) and not halAway(hal) { Assert at(hal, starling). }
  Rule hal_home when (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 9) and not at(hal, hulme_study) and not halAway(hal) { Assert at(hal, hulme_study). }
  Relation halSat(group). Relation halConfessed(group). Relation halKept(group). Relation halToldFather(group). Relation halTold(group).
  Topic hal_hello with hal "Ask Hal how he has been" when homecomer(actor) once {
    Says "He does not get up. 'You've got thin,' he says, as if you were a word he had been trying to remember for three years. 'I wrote to you. Three times. I didn't send them. I've been writing my father's letters instead.' A breath. 'His decrees.' He looks down at the paper under his hand. 'I wrote that one. On the gatehouse door. In my best hand.' His face does something, and stops. 'I'm glad you've come. I'm sorry it's now.'".
  }
  Observe starling_hal at starling when at(hal, starling) "Hal Hulme is sitting on the starling with his legs over the water and his back to the pier, where the two sets of initials are cut, as if he had been there every evening for three years.".
  Action sit_hal(actor: group, site: place) "Sit down by Hal on the starling, the way you used to" {
    Description "Half an hour, with the river under your feet.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, starling) and at(hal, starling) and homecomer(actor) and not halSat(actor).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert halSat(actor). }
    Result "You sit. He moves over without looking, the way he always did, to give you the dry bit. After a while his shoulder is against yours, and neither of you moves it. 'You went away,' he says to the river. 'I know why. I'd have gone with you if I'd had any sense.' The river goes under you, brown and fast and loud. 'I haven't any sense,' he says. 'I've done something.' And then he does not say what.".
  }
  Discovery hand_match "The letter that sent the riders to the fell road is in the same round careful hand as the reeve's decree on the gatehouse door: Hal Hulme's, who writes his father's papers.".
  Rule hand_known when knows(party, letter_read) and knows(party, decree_known) and homecomer(party) and not knows(party, hand_match) says "You knew the hand the moment you saw it. You learned your letters beside it at the same bench. Hal's." teaches hand_match { }
  Action compare_hands(actor: group, site: place) "Hold the riders' letter in your mind against the decree on the gatehouse door" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, gate_road) and knows(actor, letter_read) and stillHanging()
      and not knows(actor, hand_match) and not benighted(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, hand_match). }
    Result "You read the decree again, slowly, the shapes of the letters and not the words: the round careful clerk's hand, the long tail on the y, the way the d leans back. It is the same hand. The reeve's papers are written by his son.".
  }
  Topic hal_confess with hal "Tell Hal you have read his letter in Gault's coat" when knows(actor, hand_match) and not halConfessed(actor) once {
    Says "He goes white, and then he goes very still, the way his father does. 'Yes,' he says. 'I wrote it.' He does not look away. 'My father said the riders would take them for the lord's court. That's what he believed; he hadn't seen the warrant. The young ones were going to burn the counting-house, and the chain was already gone, and I thought: if the old ones are taken quietly on the road there'll be no more fire, and they'll be fined at the court, and that will be all.' His hands are shaking and he puts them flat on his knees. 'They hanged them on the road at sunrise. I have not slept. I have written the decree that keeps them there, in my best hand, because my father told me to and I had already done the other thing.' He looks at you. 'Do what you like with it. I'd tell Kit myself if I thought he'd let me finish.'".
    On discuss { Assert halConfessed(actor). Assert knows(actor, hal_wrote). }
  }
  Discovery hal_wrote "Hal Hulme, the reeve's son, wrote to the riders at midnight on the night of the rising, believing they would only take the old carters for the lord's court and spare the city another night of fire. They hanged them on the road. He has told no one.".
  Topic hal_tell_father with hal "Tell Hal he must tell his father" when halConfessed(actor) and not halToldFather(hal) and not halKept(hal) once {
    Says "He nods, slowly, as if you had told him the time. 'Yes.' He gets up. 'Tonight. When he comes in.' At the door he stops. 'He'll resign,' he says. 'Or he won't, and that'll be worse.'".
    On discuss { Assert halToldFather(hal). Increase hulmeMoved(hulme) by 2. }
  }
  Topic hal_keep with hal "Tell Hal you'll keep it between the two of you" when halConfessed(actor) and not halToldFather(hal) and not halKept(hal) once {
    Says "Hal laughs, once, without any sound. 'That's worse,' he says. 'You know that. That's worse than telling.' But he takes your hand, on the stone between you, where the initials are, and holds on to it as if the river might take one of you.".
    On discuss { Assert halKept(hal). }
  }
  Topic kit_told_hal with kit "Tell Kit who sent the riders to the fell road" when knows(actor, hal_wrote) and not halTold(kit) and not kitTaken(kit) once {
    Says "Kit hears you out without a sound. Then he stands up. 'Hal,' he says. 'Hal Hulme.' He looks at his hands as if they were somebody else's. 'He used to fish with us. Off the starling.' He goes, without another word, toward the bridge.".
    On discuss { Assert halTold(kit). Assert kitHunting(kit). }
  }
  Relation kitHunting(group). Relation halHurt(group).
  // Kit goes for Hal at the starling at dusk, unless someone is there to stop it.
  Rule kit_finds_hal when kitHunting(kit) and at(hal, starling) and not kitTaken(kit) and not halHurt(hal) and not at(party, starling) says "Word comes along Bridge Street at dusk: Kit Pardoe went down through the bridge chapel to the starling where Hal Hulme sits of an evening, and there was shouting under the arch, and Hal Hulme was pulled out of the river below the bridge by the fish-wives with his head cut open, alive, and Kit is in the Guildhall cellar." {
    Assert halHurt(hal). Assert kitTaken(kit). Retract kitHunting(kit). Assert at(kit, guild_cellar). Assert halAway(hal). Assert at(hal, hulme_study). }
  Action stop_kit_hal(actor: group, site: place) "Put yourself between Kit and Hal" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, starling) and kitHunting(kit) and at(hal, starling).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Retract kitHunting(kit). }
    Result "Kit comes down the ladder fast and stops on the last rung when he sees you between them. For a moment nobody moves. Then Hal says, 'Let him,' and Kit says, 'Get out of the way,' and you do not, and after a long time Kit sits down on the wet stone where he is and puts his head in his hands and Hal, very slowly, sits down too.".
  }
  Rule kit_finds_hal_watched at starling when kitHunting(kit) and at(hal, starling) and at(kit, starling) and at(party, starling) and not halHurt(hal) says "Kit comes down the ladder from the chapel with his face white and his fists shut." { }
  Rule kit_comes_down when kitHunting(kit) and at(hal, starling) and at(party, starling) and not at(kit, starling) and not kitTaken(kit) { Assert at(kit, starling). }

  // ── Alderman Gidley ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe parlour_scene at gidley_parlour when true "A parlour of the best kind: a Turkey carpet, a harpsichord nobody plays, a view of the river through good glass, and over the fire a sampler: WE BEAR THE CROSSING. The blinds of the room above are drawn, for the aunt.".
  Person gidley "Alderman Prosper Gidley" at gidley_parlour {
    Role "the Master of the Worshipful Company of the Bridge, in a blue gown". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "Alderman Gidley takes your hand in both of his, which are warm and soft, and holds it. 'Terrible days,' he says. 'Terrible. Sit down.'".
    Greets again "Alderman Gidley takes your hand in both of his, again, and the grip is a little less warm than before and a little longer. 'Friend,' he says. 'You are in Wrayford yet. How very good of you. How very kind.'".
  }
  // Breakfast at home; at nine to the gatehouse, where he weeps; the Guildhall; home to dine.
  Rule gidley_weeps when hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 10 and stillHanging() and not at(gidley, gate_road) { Assert at(gidley, gate_road). }
  Rule gidley_hall when hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) < 17 and not at(gidley, guild_hall) { Assert at(gidley, guild_hall). }
  Rule gidley_dines when (hour(clock) >= 17 or hour(clock) < 9) and not at(gidley, gidley_parlour) { Assert at(gidley, gidley_parlour). }
  Rule gidley_weeping at gate_road when hour(clock) == 9 and stillHanging() and at(gidley, gate_road) and not weptToday(gidley) says "Alderman Gidley arrives at the Bridge End in his blue gown, as he has every morning, and stands below the rail with his hat in his hand and weeps, beautifully, for some minutes, while the crowd watches. Then he wipes his eyes, and asks Pinch for the morning's takings, and goes up the Cartway to the Guildhall." { Assert weptToday(gidley). }
  Relation weptToday(group).
  Rule weeping_ends when hour(clock) == 10 and weptToday(gidley) { Retract weptToday(gidley). }
  Topic gidley_toll with gidley "Ask Alderman Gidley about the toll" when true once {
    Says "'A scandal.' He sits back. 'An imposition. The lord has no more right to tax that bridge than to tax the river.' He shakes his head. 'The Company opposed it with every fibre. And when it came, we took the farm of it ourselves, at great expense, so that it should at least be collected by Wrayford men, with Wrayford hearts, and not by some stranger.' He pats your hand. 'We are drawing up a Remonstrance. Tomorrow, at noon. You must come and speak, if you like. All are welcome. It costs nothing.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, remonstrance_called). }
  }
  Topic gidley_aunt with gidley "Ask the Alderman about his aunt" when knows(actor, corbin_strike) once {
    Says "Gidley's face falls into its folds. 'Aunt Letitia. Since Tuesday. In the blue room, with the blinds drawn and Mistress Gidley not able to go up.' He takes out his handkerchief. 'That old man at the Acre will not dig, because of the carters. The Company has offered him double fees. Treble.' He blows his nose. 'He laughed at the Company's clerk. Laughed.'".
  }
  // The bargain: forty crowns for the boy who drove.
  Relation bargainMade(group). Relation purseTaken(group).
  Topic gidley_bargain with gidley "Tell Alderman Gidley who was really driving Wat Pardoe's cart" when knows(actor, kit_driving) and not bargainMade(actor) once {
    Says "Gidley listens with his mouth a little open. Then he seizes your hand in both of his. 'The son,' he says. 'And the father died for him. Oh, that is beautiful. That is a ballad.' His eyes are wet. Then they are not. 'The captain will want a ringleader alive to take back to the lord. A live one is worth three on a rail. Give us the boy, and the Company will ask the captain to let the dead be buried, as a mercy, justice having been done.' He takes a purse from his desk and puts it on the table between you. 'Forty crowns, for your trouble. For the city's sake.'".
    On discuss { Assert bargainMade(actor). }
  }
  Action take_purse(actor: group, site: place) "Take the Company's forty crowns, and give them Kit" {
    Grave "Kit will be taken to the captain, alive, for the lord's justice.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(gidley, site) and bargainMade(actor) and not purseTaken(actor)
      and not kitTaken(kit).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 40. Assert purseTaken(actor). Assert kitTaken(kit). Assert kitSold(kit). Set kitTrust(kit) to 0. }
    Result "The purse is heavy. Gidley sends a boy running for the reeve's men, and pours you a glass of something, and toasts the city. You do not drink it.".
  }
  Relation kitSold(group).
  Rule kit_sold_taken when kitSold(kit) and not at(kit, guild_cellar) { Assert at(kit, guild_cellar). Retract travelsWith(kit, party). }
  // The flask shown to the Alderman: the Company has been robbed, by its own collector.
  Relation audited(group).
  Topic gidley_flask with gidley "Show Alderman Gidley the Company's oil flask from the ash of the toll-house" when carries(actor, company_flask) and not audited(gidley) once {
    Says "Gidley turns the flask over in his soft hands and sees the gold bridge stamped on it, and goes slowly purple. 'Ours,' he says. 'Our oil. In the toll-house.' He stands up. 'Pinch.' He rings a bell. 'If that man has been at the Company's takings,' and his voice shakes with a grief more real than any you have heard from him, 'then the Company has been robbed. Robbed! By its own servant!' He sends for Pinch's room to be opened. When the clerk comes back he is carrying the toll day-book, and Gidley reads three pages and closes it and puts it on the fire, and watches it burn, and turns to you with tears in his eyes. 'For the Company's good name,' he says. 'Pinch leaves Wrayford at dawn. Not a word of this, I beg of you.'".
    On discuss { Assert audited(gidley). Assert pinchDismissed(pinch). Assert knows(actor, gidley_burned_book). }
  }
  Relation pinchDismissed(group).
  Discovery gidley_burned_book "Shown the Company's oil flask, Alderman Gidley had Pinch's room opened, read three pages of the toll day-book, burned it, and dismissed Pinch from the Company's service for robbing the Company; and begged that nothing be said, for the Company's good name.".
  Rule daybook_burned when audited(gidley) and not carries(party, daybook) { Retract at(daybook, pinch_room). }
  Rule pinch_leaves when pinchDismissed(pinch) and hour(clock) == 6 and not pinchGone(pinch) { Assert pinchGone(pinch). Assert at(pinch, limbo). }

  // Mistress Gidley, and the ice.
  Person honoria "Honoria Gidley" at gidley_parlour {
    Role "the Alderman's wife, in black for the aunt". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner compassionate.
    Greets "Mistress Gidley is working a sampler of the Bridge in black silk on black linen, which can be read only by tilting it to the window. She takes the needle from her mouth. 'Oh,' she says. 'Visitors. Prosper will be so glad. He has been so low.'".
    Greets again "Mistress Gidley has finished a leaf of the black bridge and started on another, and cannot tell you which arch it is. 'Prosper is out,' she says, 'being low somewhere. He will be so sorry.'".
  }
  Relation honoriaLobbies(group). Relation iceGiven(group).
  Topic honoria_aunt with honoria "Ask Mistress Gidley about her aunt" when true once {
    Says "'Aunt Letitia.' She puts the sampler down. 'Ninety-one. Upstairs, in the blue room, since Tuesday, with the ice-man going up and down the back stairs four times a day with blocks, and the whole house smelling of lilies, and I cannot go up.' She looks at the window, where the river is. 'Because an old man at the Acre will not dig while those poor men are on the bridge. And Prosper says the bridge is the lord's business and the Company cannot interfere.' She pricks herself, and does not notice. 'I do think a Company that can farm a toll could manage a funeral.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, corbin_strike). }
  }
  Topic honoria_ice with honoria "Ask Mistress Gidley for a block of ice for the toll-keeper's boy" when knows(actor, corbin_strike) and not iceGiven(actor) once {
    Says "'The Hobday boy.' Her hand goes to her mouth. 'In this heat. Oh, that poor woman.' She is already on her feet. 'Tobias! Tobias, a block for the toll-keeper's house, the biggest, and don't tell the Alderman.' To you, low: 'He'll say it's the Company's ice. It's my ice. I married it.'".
    On discuss { Assert iceGiven(actor). Assert at(ice_gift, ice_house). Assert knows(actor, ice_waiting). }
  }
  Discovery ice_waiting "Mistress Gidley has had a block of ice set out for you in the ice-house on the Hill, for the toll-keeper's boy.".
  Item ice_gift "a block of ice" is ice_kind at limbo.
  Topic honoria_lobby with honoria "Tell Mistress Gidley that if the carters come down, Corbin will dig for her aunt" when knows(actor, corbin_strike) and knows(actor, remonstrance_called) and not honoriaLobbies(honoria) once {
    Says "She sits very still. 'If the carters come down.' She looks at the ceiling, through which is the blue room. 'The Remonstrance is tomorrow at noon.' Her mouth goes thin. 'Prosper will do as I tell him, for once. He'll speak for whatever lets that old man dig. You tell me what to make him say, and he'll say it.'".
    On discuss { Assert honoriaLobbies(honoria). }
  }
  // The ice-house: Tobias Wren by day, who sells to the Hill and to nobody else; locked at night.
  Observe icehouse_scene at ice_house when true "Down a stair into the hill: a brick dome, cold enough to make your breath smoke, and straw, and under the straw, blocks of last winter's river, grey and sweating.".
  Person tobias "Tobias Wren" at ice_house {
    Role "the Alderman's ice-man, in a sacking cape". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner stoic.
    Greets "Tobias Wren straightens up from the straw with a pair of tongs. 'Hill houses only,' he says. 'Alderman's orders.'".
    Greets again "Tobias Wren has put the straw back over the block by the time you are through the door. 'Hill houses only,' he says, with less conviction. 'I will not say what the ice is for, and you will not ask, and we will both have a cooler evening.'".
  }
  Topic tobias_blue_room with tobias "Ask Tobias Wren who the ice is for" when true once {
    Says "'The blue room, mostly.' Tobias leans on the tongs. 'Four blocks a day up the back stairs since Tuesday, and lilies, and the window kept shut.' He looks at the straw. 'Ninety-one, she was. And the old man at the Acre won't dig.' He turns a block over to its cold side. 'There's ice in here for a fortnight, if the weather holds. After that I'd not want to be the one carrying it up.'".
  }
  Rule tobias_day when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 18 and not at(tobias, ice_house) { Assert at(tobias, ice_house). }
  Rule tobias_night when (hour(clock) >= 18 or hour(clock) < 8) and at(tobias, ice_house) { Retract at(tobias, ice_house). Assert at(tobias, limbo). }
  Thing ice_lock "the ice-house door" on ice_door {
    State locked blocking "The ice-house door is padlocked for the night.".
    State open "The ice-house door is unlocked.".
    Change pick "Pick the padlock on the ice-house door" from locked to open needing lockwork.
    Change wrench "Wrench the padlock's hasp off the ice-house door" from locked to open needing brawn.
  }
  Initially Assert state(ice_lock, open).
  Rule ice_locked when (hour(clock) >= 18 or hour(clock) < 8) and state(ice_lock, open) and not iceForced(wray) { Assert state(ice_lock, locked). }
  Rule ice_unlocked when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 18 and state(ice_lock, locked) { Assert state(ice_lock, open). Retract iceForced(wray). }
  Relation iceForced(place).
  Rule ice_forced when state(ice_lock, open) and (hour(clock) >= 18 or hour(clock) < 8) and not iceForced(wray) { Assert iceForced(wray). }
  // Taken at night, unseen: anyone can lift a block, once in.
  Item ice_night "a block of ice" is ice_kind at ice_house hidden until ice_seen.
  Discovery ice_seen "In the straw of the ice-house lie blocks of grey river ice, and nobody watches them at night." { Found by searching ice_house. }
  Topic tobias_sell with tobias "Ask Tobias Wren to sell you a block of ice" when not iceGiven(actor) once {
    Says "'Hill houses only.' He looks at you. 'What for?' You tell him. He goes on looking. Then he takes a block out of the straw with his tongs and wraps it in sacking and puts it in your arms, and holds out his hand. 'Two coin,' he says. 'For the Hobday lad. And it fell off the cart.'".
    On discuss { Assert iceGiven(actor). Assert at(ice_gift, ice_house). Assert knows(actor, ice_waiting). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. }
  }
}

data/adventures/wrayford/liberty.kyr:
Module wrayford "The Third Night" {
  // ── Overbridge ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Liberty of Saint Wade's: the reeve's writ ends at the foot of the drawbridge.
  Observe over_scene at overbridge_street when not dark() and not visitedBefore(overbridge_street) "Overbridge Street comes off the drawbridge into another town: older, lower, poorer and louder, timber houses with their upper floors leaning on their neighbours, the tan-yards stinking at one end and the bear-garden roaring at the other, and in the middle Saint Wade's, a squat old church with a tower, and the Abbess's lodging behind a wall. A painted post at the bridge foot says THE LIBERTY OF SAINT WADE. The reeve's writ ends here, and everybody walks a little differently.".
  Observe over_again at overbridge_street when not dark() and visitedBefore(overbridge_street) "Overbridge Street: leaning houses, the church, the post that says THE LIBERTY OF SAINT WADE.".
  Observe over_night at overbridge_street when dark() "Overbridge at night: the Ferry Inn lit and loud, and every other door shut.".
  Observe stair_scene at south_stair when true "The south ferry-stair: worn steps going down into the river, a post for tying up, and the Acre wall above, with the tops of the gravestones showing over it.".
  Observe tanyards_scene at tanyards when not dark() "The tan-yards: pits of lime and bark and worse, hides on frames, men with their arms stained to the elbow, and a smell that takes the breath out of you. Nobody comes here who need not.".
  Observe tanyards_night at tanyards when dark() "The tan-yards at night: the pits black, the hides on their frames like people standing.".
  Observe ferry_inn_scene at ferry_taproom when true "The Ferry Inn: a low room that smells of wet wool and pipe-ash, with the floor sloping to the river so that every pot has to be put down on purpose. Watermen at one table, tanners at another, and by the window two men in good coats drinking slowly, who have business in the Liberty that they would not have in the city.".
  Observe south_road_scene at south_road when not dark() "The south road leaves Overbridge between hedges, already white with dust, toward the lord's country. A drover's dog is asleep in the only shade. A milestone: HARBURY XII.".

  // ── Saint Wade's and the Acre ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe nave_again at nave when visitedBefore(nave) "Saint Wade's: whitewash, the cheerful saint, the carved wheels on the pews.".
  Observe nave_scene at nave when not visitedBefore(nave) "Saint Wade's: a low, old, whitewashed church, cold even in this heat, smelling of damp stone and tallow. Every pew has a carved wheel on its end, for the carters, and on the oldest pews the wheels have been touched smooth.".
  Observe acre_scene at wades_acre when not dark() "Wade's Acre: the burying ground of Wrayford since there was a Wrayford, between the church and the river, gravestones leaning every way like a crowd looking at something.".
  Observe acre_night at wades_acre when dark() "The Acre at night: the stones pale, the river loud beyond the wall, the tower black.".
  Person corbin "Corbin" at wades_acre {
    Role "the sexton of Saint Wade's, old as his spade". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "Corbin sits on the Acre wall with a spade across his knees and the look of a man who has dug for this parish for fifty years and been told, this week, to stop. 'Not dead, are you,' he says. 'No business of mine, then.'".
    Greets again "Corbin has taken the spade off his knees and laid it on the wall beside him, where he can see it. 'You again,' he says. 'Not dead. It is becoming a habit with you, and I do not hold with habits in the living.'".
  }
  Rule corbin_wall when hour(clock) >= 7 and hour(clock) < 21 and not at(corbin, wades_acre) { Assert at(corbin, wades_acre). }
  Rule corbin_bed when (hour(clock) >= 21 or hour(clock) < 7) and not at(corbin, nave) { Assert at(corbin, nave). }
  Rule corbin_sleeps when (hour(clock) >= 22 or hour(clock) < 6) and not asleep(corbin) { Assert asleep(corbin). }
  Rule corbin_wakes when hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 22 and asleep(corbin) { Retract asleep(corbin). }
  Topic corbin_strike_talk with corbin "Ask Corbin why he will not dig" when true once {
    Says "'Forty years I've dug for Wrayford. Every one of them.' He points with his pipe at the stones. 'There's not a soul in this Acre I didn't put there, bar the old ones. Wat Pardoe's father. Dunstan Fenner's mother. Joss Wilder's sister, when she was three.' He puts the pipe back. 'I'll not dig a hole in this Acre while there's a Wrayford man hanging on that bridge for the crows. Not for the toll-keeper's boy, God rest him. Not for Gidley's aunt, God rest her, at treble fees.' He looks at you. 'Let them feel it. Let the Hill smell it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, corbin_strike). }
  }
  Topic corbin_terms_talk with corbin "Ask Corbin what would make him dig" when knows(actor, corbin_strike) once {
    Says "'When they're down.' He considers. 'Or,' and his face does something sour, 'or when that woman over the water asks me. Dorcas Mudd.' He takes his pipe out and looks into the bowl. 'She's not asked me for anything in forty years. She'll not start now.'".
    On discuss { Assert corbinTerms(actor). }
  }
  Action tell_corbin_lie(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Corbin that Dorcas Mudd asked after him" {
    Description "She did not.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wades_acre) and at(corbin, wades_acre)
      and dorcasTerms(actor) and corbinTerms(actor) and not corbinLied(actor) and not reconciled(wray) and not triedCorbinLie(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert corbinLied(actor). }
    On failure { Assert triedCorbinLie(actor). }
    Result "'Asked after me.' He takes his pipe out. 'What did she ask?' You tell him something. He looks across the water at the ferry-stage until the pipe has gone cold in his hand, and puts it back without lighting it. 'Did she,' he says.".
    Otherwise "Corbin laughs until he coughs. 'Dorcas Mudd,' he says, 'would ask after the Devil's health before mine. Go on with you.'".
  }
  // The graves: three, by the church door. Corbin digs them by the next morning once he has a reason; or anyone can.
  Thing graves "the three graves by the church door" at wades_acre {
    State marked "By the church door, three graves' worth of turf marked out with string and pegs, uncut.".
    State dug "By the church door, three graves, dug clean and square, with the earth heaped neatly beside each.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(graves, marked).
  Relation corbinWillDig(place). Relation corbinFinished(group).
  Rule corbin_reason when (corbinDigs(party) or takenDown(wray) and stillDownOrBuried()) and not corbinWillDig(wray) and not corbinResigned(corbin) { Assert corbinWillDig(wray). }
  Query stillDownOrBuried() means not stillHanging().
  Rule corbin_digs when corbinWillDig(wray) and state(graves, marked) and hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) < 21 says "In Wade's Acre old Corbin has taken his coat off and is cutting turf by the church door, and the sound of the spade carries over the water." { Assert state(graves, dug). }
  Action dig_graves(actor: group, site: place) "Dig the three graves yourself" {
    Description "Three graves, square and deep, in heavy ground: half a day for a digger.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wades_acre) and state(graves, marked) and capable(actor, digging)
      and not dark().
    Time 18.
    On success { Assert state(graves, dug). Assert dugOwn(actor). }
    Result "You cut the turf back and stack it, and dig. It is heavy river clay under a foot of black earth, and the sun is on your back. Some time in the second grave Corbin gets down off the wall and stands over you with his pipe, and in the third he takes the spade out of your hands without a word and squares off the sides himself. 'Crooked,' he says. 'Every one.' But he does not stop.".
  }
  Relation dugOwn(group).
  Kind spade_kind "the sexton's spade" like crowbar worth 1 weighing 4
    described "A long-handled spade with a narrow blade worn bright and a T-handle black with forty years of one man's hands.".
  Item sexton_spade "the sexton's spade" is spade_kind at nave owned by corbin.
  Action dig_graves_spade(actor: group, digger: member, site: place) "Dig the three graves with the sexton's spade" {
    Description "Without a digger's knack it takes all night, and you will not do it well.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wades_acre) and state(graves, marked)
      and memberOf(digger, actor) and ownedItem(sexton_spade, digger) and not capable(actor, digging).
    Time 30.
    On success { Assert state(graves, dug). Assert dugOwn(actor). }
    Result "It takes five hours, and your hands are raw by the first, and the graves are not square and not quite deep enough. But they are graves.".
  }
  // The Abbess may order him to dig, and he will, and then he will put his spade down for good.
  Relation corbinOrdered(group). Relation corbinResigned(group).

  // ── The Abbess ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe court_scene at abbess_court when true "The Abbess's court-room: a long room with a dais, a chair under a canopy, a table with a green cloth, and on the walls the charters of the Liberty, framed, all of them, from the oldest, which is a scrap of vellum with a seal like a biscuit, to the newest, which is a letter from the lord's steward that she has had framed upside down.".
  Person abbess "Dame Isobel Crane" at abbess_court {
    Role "the Lady Abbess of Saint Wade's, who holds the Liberty of Overbridge". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "The Abbess has a pair of spectacles on her nose and another pair pushed up into her wimple, and takes up a pen in your honour, as if you were a charter. 'Sit,' she says. 'Or stand. Only be brief, and be accurate: I am keeping two records of today, and one of them is for the Bishop.'".
    Greets again "The Abbess has put one pair of spectacles up and brought the other down, which means you have been entered in the second record. 'Be brief,' she says. 'I have already forgiven you for the first visit. I should like not to have to forgive the second.'".
  }
  Measure abbessRegard(group). Initially Set abbessRegard(abbess) to 0.
  Relation abbessClaims(group). Relation sanctuary(group). Relation ritesOffered(group).
  Discovery abbess_terms "The Abbess holds that whatever of Wrayford's dead reaches the Liberty is the Liberty's to bury. She will not fetch the three across the city's bridge herself, since to do so would admit the bridge is the city's; but she will claim them, in writing, for someone she has cause to trust, so that they cross as the Liberty's tithe.".
  Topic abbess_dead with abbess "Ask the Abbess about the dead on the bridge" when true once {
    Says "'A question of jurisdiction,' says the Abbess, 'first, and of charity second, and I am honest enough to say so in that order.' She takes her spectacles off. 'Wrayford has buried its dead in Wade's Acre since before the bridge, and every one of them crossed the river to get here, and not one paid the lord a penny. If those three reach the Liberty, they are mine, and I will bury them, and the reeve can write to the lord.' She folds the spectacles. 'I will not fetch them. If I send my brothers over that bridge for them I have admitted that the bridge is the city's road and not the Liberty's, and my predecessors have not admitted it for three hundred years.' She looks at you. 'I might put my claim in writing. For someone I had cause to trust.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, abbess_terms). }
  }
  Topic abbess_bench with abbess "Ask the Abbess about the Bridge Company" when true once {
    Says "'The Worshipful Company of the Bridge.' Very dry. 'I have known Prosper Gidley since he sang in my predecessor's choir. He sang very sweetly, and he was the boy who carried the collection. He has not changed. He has only grown.' She turns a page. 'They will vote for anything that costs them nothing they can be seen to lose. Remember that, if you have business with them. It is the only thing about them worth knowing.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bench_rule). }
  }
  Kind claim_kind "the Abbess's letter" is gear worth 0 weighing 0
    described "A folded sheet sealed in green wax with the Liberty's seal: THE LIBERTY OF SAINT WADE CLAIMS ITS DEAD, WAT PARDOE, DUNSTAN FENNER AND JOSS WILDER, TO BE BURIED IN WADE'S ACRE AS IT HAS ALWAYS BURIED WRAYFORD, AND THEY ARE TO CROSS AS THE LIBERTY'S TITHE. I. CRANE, ABBESS.".
  Item claim_letter "the Abbess's letter" is claim_kind at limbo.
  Action ask_claim(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Ask the Abbess to put her claim to the dead in writing" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, abbess_court) and at(abbess, abbess_court)
      and knows(actor, abbess_terms) and abbessRegard(abbess) >= 1 and not abbessClaims(abbess) and memberOf(recipient, actor).
    Time 1.
    Resolve acquire(claim_letter, claim_kind, recipient).
    On success { Assert abbessClaims(abbess). }
    Result "She writes it herself, without a draft, in a hand like a row of pikes, and seals it in green, and gives it to you. 'If the city stands aside,' she says, 'they are mine. Show that to the collector. Show it to the reeve. Show it to the captain, if it comes to that. And then go away and let me get on.'".
  }
  Action argue_claim(actor: group, site: place) "Argue to the Abbess that charity cannot wait on jurisdiction" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, abbess_court) and at(abbess, abbess_court)
      and knows(actor, abbess_terms) and abbessRegard(abbess) < 1 and not triedAbbess(actor).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Increase abbessRegard(abbess) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert triedAbbess(actor). }
    Result "She hears you out without interrupting, which you are given to understand is a compliment. 'You are quite wrong,' she says. 'Jurisdiction is charity, over three hundred years.' A pause. 'But you put it well, and you were brief.'".
    Otherwise "'Charity,' says the Abbess, 'is a word people use when they would like someone else to pay for something.' She returns to her papers.".
  }
  Relation triedAbbess(group).
  // A cleric's office for the dead: the thing she cannot do herself, since to say it on the bridge is to cross it.
  Action offer_rites(actor: group, site: place) "Offer to say the office of the dead for the three, on the bridge, as a priest of no parish" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, abbess_court) and at(abbess, abbess_court)
      and capable(actor, rites) and not ritesOffered(actor).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert ritesOffered(actor). Increase abbessRegard(abbess) by 1. }
    Result "The Abbess takes off her spectacles. 'A priest of no parish,' she says. 'Who can stand on the lord's bridge and say the words over Wrayford's dead without it meaning that the Liberty crossed it.' For the first time she looks at you as if you were of use. 'Yes. Do. Tonight, at the curfew, under the rail. And come back to me after.'".
  }
  Rule rites_said at gate_road when ritesOffered(party) and hour(clock) == 22 and stillHanging() and at(party, gate_road) and not spread(rites_fact) says "At the curfew bell you stand under the rail and say the office of the dead for Wat Pardoe, Dunstan Fenner and Joss Wilder, aloud, in the old words. The riders on the leads stop talking. In the doorways of Bridge Street people come out and stand. When you have finished there is no sound at all but the river, and then, from somewhere behind the shutters, someone says Amen, and then a great many people do." { Assert spread(rites_fact). Increase temper(wray) by 1. }
  Entity rites_fact: fact "The office said under the rail".
  Topic abbess_after_rites with abbess "Tell the Abbess the office is said" when spread(rites_fact) once {
    Says "'I heard.' She does not look up. 'The whole of Overbridge heard. Half of it came out on to the drawbridge to listen, and the riders let them stand there, which they have not let anyone do in four days.' She writes something, and sands it. 'You did what I could not, and you did it properly. The old words, not the new ones.' She looks up. 'The Liberty is obliged to you. It does not say that often.'".
    On discuss { Increase abbessRegard(abbess) by 1. }
  }
  Topic abbess_sanctuary with abbess "Ask the Abbess whether the Liberty would shelter you, if it came to that" when abbessRegard(abbess) >= 2 and not sanctuary(actor) once {
    Says "'It has sheltered worse.' She does not look up. 'Whoever is in the Liberty is beyond the reeve's writ. If you have done something in the city you would rather not answer for to Simon Hulme, be on this side of the drawbridge at dawn, and he may send me a letter.' She signs something. 'I shall frame it.'".
    On discuss { Assert sanctuary(actor). }
  }
  Topic abbess_order with abbess "Ask the Abbess to order Corbin to dig" when knows(actor, corbin_strike) and abbessRegard(abbess) >= 1 and not corbinOrdered(actor) and not corbinWillDig(wray) once {
    Says "She considers. 'I can,' she says. 'He is my sexton. He will dig, because I tell him to.' She looks at you over the spectacles. 'And then he will put down his spade, after forty years, and never pick it up again, because I made him dig against his conscience. Shall I?' You do not answer, and she rings the bell anyway, and sends for him.".
    On discuss { Assert corbinOrdered(actor). Assert corbinResigned(corbin). Assert corbinWillDigOrdered(wray). }
  }
  Relation corbinWillDigOrdered(place).
  Rule corbin_digs_ordered when corbinWillDigOrdered(wray) and state(graves, marked) and hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) < 21 says "In Wade's Acre old Corbin is digging three graves by the church door, very slowly and very well, and when he has finished he cleans his spade and lays it on the Abbess's step and walks away up the south road without his coat." { Assert state(graves, dug). Assert at(corbin, limbo). }
  Rule corbin_stays_gone when corbinResigned(corbin) and state(graves, dug) and not at(corbin, limbo) { Assert at(corbin, limbo). }

  // The hide: a case before the Liberty's court, which the Abbess hands to you on the morning of the second day.
  Relation courtSitting(place). Relation hideJudged(place). Relation hideFor(group). Relation hideSplit(place).
  Query courtHours() means secondDay() and hour(clock) >= 10 and hour(clock) < 12 and not hideJudged(wray).
  Person crouch "Barnaby Crouch" at tanyards {
    Role "a tanner, stained to the elbow". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "Barnaby Crouch wipes his hands, which makes them worse. 'If it's about the hide,' he says, 'it's mine.'".
    Greets again "Barnaby Crouch rubs his hands on his apron, which makes them worse. 'It is about the hide,' he says. 'I told you. I tell everybody. It is the one thing in Wrayford I am certain of.'".
  }
  Rule crouch_court when courtHours() and not at(crouch, abbess_court) { Assert at(crouch, abbess_court). }
  Rule kemp_court when courtHours() and not at(kemp, abbess_court) { Assert at(kemp, abbess_court). }
  Rule crouch_home when not courtHours() and at(crouch, abbess_court) { Retract at(crouch, abbess_court). Assert at(crouch, tanyards). }
  Rule kemp_home when not courtHours() and at(kemp, abbess_court) { Retract at(kemp, abbess_court). Assert at(kemp, shambles). }
  Thing hide "the disputed hide" at abbess_court {
    State disputed "On the green cloth, rolled and tied: a raw cowhide, red side out, with a ticket on it in the Abbess's hand: KEMP v. CROUCH.".
    State awarded "The hide has gone from the table.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(hide, disputed).
  Observe hide_court at abbess_court when courtHours() "The Abbess's court is sitting. Saul Kemp the butcher and Barnaby Crouch the tanner stand before the table, not looking at each other, and on the green cloth between them lies a rolled cowhide. The Abbess looks at you as you come in and says, 'You have a face like a juryman. I have a jurisdiction to defend this morning and no time for cows. Judge it.' And sits back.".
  Topic kemp_claim with kemp "Ask Saul Kemp why the hide is his" when courtHours() and at(kemp, abbess_court) once {
    Says "'Beast died in my pens, in the Shambles, in the city,' says Kemp. 'I skinned it. It's mine.'".
  }
  Topic crouch_claim with crouch "Ask Barnaby Crouch why the hide is his" when courtHours() and at(crouch, abbess_court) once {
    Says "'Came over in the offal cart,' says Crouch. 'Anything in the offal cart is the tan-yards' by the Liberty's privilege. It's mine.'".
  }
  Observe hide_brands near hide when tried(hide, looking) and (capable(party, woodcraft) or capable(party, lore)) and not knows(party, hide_brand) "Unrolled, the hide has two marks on the flank: a fresh nick in the ear, the Shambles' tally-mark for a beast sold, and under it, older, a drover's brand burned into the hair: H.O., and a little curlew. Ham Ostler's. The beast was never sold. It died in the pens and somebody skinned it." teaches hide_brand.
  Observe hide_brands_plain near hide when tried(hide, looking) and not capable(party, woodcraft) and not capable(party, lore) "Unrolled, the hide has a nick in the ear, and under the hair on the flank some older mark you cannot make out.".
  Discovery hide_brand "The disputed hide carries Ham Ostler's drover's brand, the curlew: the beast was his, never sold, and died in the Shambles pens before market. It is neither the butcher's nor the tanner's.".
  Action judge_kemp(actor: group, site: place) "Give the hide to the butcher" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, abbess_court) and courtHours().
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert hideJudged(wray). Assert hideFor(kemp). Assert state(hide, awarded). }
    Result "Kemp takes it under his arm with a grin. Crouch says something about the city that the Abbess pretends not to hear. 'So,' she says. 'The Liberty yields a hide to the Shambles.' She writes it down. She does not look pleased.".
  }
  Action judge_crouch(actor: group, site: place) "Give the hide to the tanner, by the Liberty's privilege" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, abbess_court) and courtHours().
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert hideJudged(wray). Assert hideFor(crouch). Assert state(hide, awarded). Increase abbessRegard(abbess) by 1. }
    Result "Crouch takes it as if it were a sword of state. 'The Liberty's privilege upheld,' says the Abbess, and writes it down with some satisfaction. Kemp goes out without a word, and the door bangs.".
  }
  Action judge_split(actor: group, site: place) "Cut the hide in two, and give each of them half" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, abbess_court) and courtHours().
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert hideJudged(wray). Assert hideSplit(wray). Assert state(hide, awarded). }
    Result "There is a knife on the table for the purpose, it seems. You cut the hide down the backbone and give each of them a half. Both look at their halves, which are now worth nothing to anybody, with the same expression. The Abbess laughs out loud, once, like a door slamming. 'Solomon,' she says, 'and nobody's baby. Very good. Get out, both of you.'".
  }
  Action judge_ham(actor: group, site: place) "Give the hide to neither: it is Ham Ostler's, by his brand" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, abbess_court) and courtHours() and knows(actor, hide_brand).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert hideJudged(wray). Assert hideFor(ham). Assert state(hide, awarded). Increase abbessRegard(abbess) by 1. Assert hamGrateful(actor). }
    Result "You show her the curlew. The Abbess takes her spectacles off and looks at it for a long time, and then at the butcher, who is looking at the floor, and at the tanner, who is looking at the butcher. 'A beast that died in the pens before market,' she says, 'and was skinned, and sent over the bridge in the offal cart, and argued over by two men who both knew whose it was.' She puts her spectacles back on. 'The hide is Ham Ostler's, and the Liberty is obliged to whoever noticed.' She writes. 'That is the first sensible thing anyone has said to me this week.'".
  }
  Rule hide_regard_split when hideSplit(wray) and abbessRegard(abbess) < 1 { Increase abbessRegard(abbess) by 1. }

  // ── The bear-garden ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe bear_scene at bear_garden when not dark() "The bear-garden: a ring of raised benches round a sanded pit, a post in the middle with a chain, and on the chain an old brown she-bear, sitting on her haunches with her forepaws in her lap like a farmer's wife. A boy of twelve or so is combing the burrs out of her coat, and she lets him.".
  Person robin "Robin Tull" at bear_garden {
    Role "a cutler's boy of twelve, with bear-hair on his sleeves". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Greets "The boy looks up from the bear's coat. 'She's called Margery,' he says, before you can ask anything else.".
    Greets again "The bear's head is in the boy's lap this time, and he is combing a burr out of her ear with a cutler's pick. 'Margery likes you,' he says. 'She likes anybody who does not come with a rope.'".
  }
  Person clout "Sim Clout" at bear_garden {
    Role "the bear-ward, with a strap at his belt". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner grim.
    Greets "Sim Clout sits on a bucket outside the bear's pen with a strap across his knees and the chain looped three times round his wrist. 'Show's at four,' he says. 'Penny. Not before, whatever the boy tells you. She has her mornings.'".
    Greets again "Sim Clout has put the strap through his belt and is mending the chain's third link with a pair of pliers and a great deal of breath. 'It is not four yet,' he says. 'But you are very welcome to wait with us until it is.'".
  }
  Person margery "Margery" at bear_garden {
    Role "an old brown she-bear on a chain". Species bear. Peaceable. Pronouns she.
  }
  Relation clouted(group). Relation margeryBought(group). Relation margerySettled(group).
  Topic robin_why with robin "Ask Robin Tull why he will not go home" when knows(actor, robin_gone) and not robinHome(robin) and not robinStays(robin) once {
    Says "'Because Margery won't dance for anyone else.' He goes on combing. 'Not for him. Only me. And if she won't dance he'll sell her to the baiting at Harbury at Michaelmas, he says so, and they'll set dogs on her.' He looks at the strap on Clout's belt, and away. 'So I can't go home. Can I.' He combs. 'I like knives,' he says, as if it were a confession. 'I do. I'd rather bears.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, margery_fate). }
  }
  Discovery margery_fate "The bear, Margery, dances only for Robin Tull. If she will not dance, Sim Clout will sell her to the baiting at Harbury at Michaelmas.".
  Action persuade_robin(actor: group, site: place) "Talk Robin Tull into going home to his mother" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, bear_garden) and at(robin, bear_garden)
      and knows(actor, robin_gone) and not robinHome(robin) and not robinStays(robin) and not triedRobin(actor).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert robinHome(robin). Retract at(robin, bear_garden). Assert at(robin, tull_shop). }
    On failure { Assert triedRobin(actor). }
    Result "It takes a while, and it is mostly about his mother, and how she grinds the cleavers when she is frightened. In the end he puts the comb down and says goodbye to Margery, which takes longer, and comes.".
    Otherwise "'No,' he says, and goes on combing, and the bear looks at you over his head.".
  }
  Relation triedRobin(group).
  Action buy_margery(actor: group, site: place) "Buy Margery from Sim Clout for ten coin, and give her to the Liberty" {
    Description "The Abbess has a walled garden. Nobody has told her yet.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, bear_garden) and at(clout, bear_garden)
      and knows(actor, margery_fate) and not margeryBought(actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 10.
    Time 1.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Assert margeryBought(actor). Assert robinHome(robin). Increase abbessRegard(abbess) by 1.
      Retract at(robin, bear_garden). Assert at(robin, tull_shop). Retract at(margery, bear_garden). Assert at(margery, abbess_court). }
    Result "Clout counts the coins twice and unhooks the chain. You walk Margery down Overbridge Street on it with Robin at her other side, and all the Liberty comes to its doors to watch, and the Abbess comes to her gate, and looks at the bear, and at you, and says, 'I see,' and has the gate opened. Robin goes home to his mother after that without being asked, because he can come and visit on Sundays.".
  }
  Action settle_margery(actor: group, site: place) "Show Robin how a drover settles a beast with a low whistle, so anyone can work her" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, bear_garden) and at(robin, bear_garden)
      and capable(actor, woodcraft) and knows(actor, margery_fate) and not margerySettled(actor) and not robinHome(robin).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert margerySettled(actor). Assert robinHome(robin). Retract at(robin, bear_garden). Assert at(robin, tull_shop). }
    Result "It is the whistle a drover uses for a nervous cow, low and two notes, and the old bear lifts her head at it. You have Robin teach it to Sim Clout, who is bad at it, and then Clout does it, badly, and Margery gets up on her hind legs and turns round once, as if humouring him. Robin watches with his mouth open. 'She'll do it for him now,' he says. 'She'll do it for anyone.' He sounds, for a moment, bereft. Then he goes home.".
  }
  Action face_clout(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Sim Clout that if he lays that strap on the boy again, you will have his ears" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, bear_garden) and at(clout, bear_garden)
      and knows(actor, robin_gone) and not clouted(actor) and not robinHome(robin).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert clouted(actor). Assert robinStays(robin). }
    Result "Clout looks at you, and at the strap, and takes it off his belt and hangs it on the post, and does not look at it again. Robin watches it all. 'I can stay, then,' he says. 'With Margery.' And then, carefully: 'Will you tell my mother I'm well. And that I'm sorry. And not where I am, because she knows.'".
    Otherwise "Clout puts his hand on the strap and smiles at you with very few teeth. 'Liberty,' he says. 'No reeve here. Go home.'".
  }
}

data/adventures/wrayford/lore.kyr:
Module wrayford "The Third Night" {
  Description "Links outward from the vale of the Wray: Corbin shown a lamplighter's seal from another town, a rumour of the Tolleth coast, and the almanack woman, who paid the penny twice.".

  // ── A visitor from elsewhere: a seal of the lamplighters ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_corbin_seal "Corbin, who lights a lamp for the drowned each night as his father did, has seen a seal like a lamp with a hand closed round it before: his father's was the same, and was lost in the flood.".
  Topic lore_corbin_seal_show with corbin "Show Corbin the lamplighters' seal" when holding(actor, lamplighter_seal) once {
    Says "Corbin turns the seal over on its chain, brass, a lamp with a hand closed around it, and the hand shakes. 'My father had one,' he says. 'Went in the flood. I thought it was ours.' He gives it back as if it were hot. 'It is not ours. It is somebody's who does what I do, and is not known to me.' He looks at the water. 'There is a town, you say. With a Charter. Where the lamps are lit by Order.' He is silent. 'Mine is lit by nobody. I have been very proud of that.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_corbin_seal). }
  }

  // ── An entry point: the coast ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_pell_coast "A carter says raiders are taking salt-boats on the western coast beyond the Orsett shore, and that the Dorothea, a packet out of Tolleth, is late with the Orsett factors' money.".
  Topic lore_pell_coast_ask with pell "Ask Pell what the carters from the coast are saying" when true once {
    Says "'Salt,' says Pell. 'It is always salt with the coast carters, and this year it is raiders in it. Boats taken off the Orsett shore and the crews sent home in their shirts.' She draws a pint. 'And a packet out of Tolleth, the Dorothea, that is late with the factors' money, and a captain who is a woman and a temper. They say she has not missed a tide in her life. They say the notice board on the quay at Tolleth has her sailings in chalk, and that they are always right and always an hour earlier than anybody expects.' She puts the pint down. 'If you are going that way, take your own bread.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_pell_coast). }
  }

  // ── The almanack woman ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_cattermole_wray "Jessamy Cattermole crossed the Wray bridge and paid the penny twice, to see if the Company would notice; they did not. She has gone on to the sea, to Skeel, for the wreck.".
  Topic lore_pell_cattermole with pell "Ask Pell whether a pedlar has crossed the bridge lately" when true once {
    Says "'The almanack woman,' says Pell. 'Cattermole. She paid the penny twice at the bridge, once for herself and once for her satchel, which she says has a right to cross. The Bench noted it and said nothing. They did not know what to enter.' She laughs. 'She told me it is 1312 on the coast, or 1290 at Sennet, or 1121 where the Bishop went away, or 612 here, and the Third Night falls on the same night anyway. She went off south and west, to Skeel, for the wreck. She says a wreck is good for business: everyone wants to know what year it is when it went.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_cattermole_wray). }
  }
}

data/adventures/wrayford/market.kyr:
Module wrayford "The Third Night" {
  // ── The Market Cross ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe cross_scene at market_cross when not dark() and not visitedBefore(market_cross) "The Market is a sloping square with a stone cross in the middle where the hiring is done, the Guildhall along the top side with its clock and its arcade, and the Bridge Company's counting-house next to it, newly painted blue, with a bridge in gold over the door. The Mercer Steps go up behind to the Hill. Down Shambles Lane you can hear cattle, and smell them. On the Cross itself, on every post of the arcade, and on the counting-house door, the same printed sheet is pasted.".
  Observe cross_again at market_cross when not dark() and visitedBefore(market_cross) "The Market Cross: the Guildhall clock, the blue counting-house, the sheets on every post.".
  Observe cross_night at market_cross when dark() "The Market at night: the Guildhall clock lit, and a watchman sitting on the steps of the Cross.".
  Observe cross_market_day at market_cross when not dark() and hour(clock) < 12 and (secondDay() or fifthDay()) "It is market day: farm carts, egg-women, a man selling eels live out of a barrel, and at the Cross the hiring, labourers standing with a tuft of wool or a whip in their hats for what they do.".
  // The broadside on every post.
  Discovery confession_read "Pasted on every post in the Market: THE TRUE AND LAST CONFESSION OF WAT PARDOE, CARTER, TAKEN ON THE FELL ROAD. 'I, Wat Pardoe, being led astray by Drink and the Devil and the Wicked Counsel of Others, did conspire against the Lord's Toll, which is a Just and Godly Toll, and did with my Cart run down an Innocent Youth, for which I am Heartily Sorry, and I Bless the Worshipful Company of the Bridge, who have been Ever Kind to Carters.' Printed by E. Quoin, Cutler's Lane. Price One Penny." {
    Source broadside "the printed sheet on the Market Cross" at market_cross readable by party.
  }
  Relation confessionDown(place).
  Observe sheets_down at market_cross when confessionDown(wray) and not dark() "The posts of the arcade are bare where the Confession was. Someone has scraped the last of it off the Cross with a knife.".

  // ── The Guildhall ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe hall_scene at guild_hall when not visitedBefore(guild_hall) "The Guildhall's long hall: a hammer-beam roof, the city's arms in plaster, a long table on a dais where the Bench sits, and at the far end the reeve's chair and his clerk's desk, where he keeps court. Along one wall hang the portraits of fifty years of the Bridge Company, Masters and Wardens, in blue gowns, each more prosperous than the last. An easel stands at the end of the row.".
  Observe hall_again at guild_hall when visitedBefore(guild_hall) "The Guildhall's long hall: the Bench's table, the reeve's chair, the row of blue-gowned portraits and the easel at the end.".
  Observe cellar_scene at guild_cellar when true "The Guildhall cellar, which is the city's lockup: stone, straw, a bucket, a grating at the top of the wall that lets in the feet of people crossing the Market.".

  // Tom Lumley's portrait of the present Bench, for the Bridge Feast.
  Person lumley "Tom Lumley" at guild_hall {
    Role "a painter, in a coat with paint on the elbows". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner acerbic.
    Greets "Tom Lumley does not take his eyes off the canvas. 'If you're from the Company, I've not finished. If you're not, have you a shilling?'".
    Greets again "Tom Lumley has moved the canvas an inch to the left and is calling it composition. 'If you are from the Company,' he says, 'I have found the third hanged man a hat. If not, I have nothing to say that is not in the picture.'".
  }
  Rule lumley_drinks when hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 23 and not at(lumley, wheels_taproom) { Assert at(lumley, wheels_taproom). }
  Rule lumley_paints when hour(clock) >= 9 and hour(clock) < 18 and not at(lumley, guild_hall) { Assert at(lumley, guild_hall). }
  Thing portrait "the Company's portrait" at guild_hall {
    State sketched "On the easel, the present Bench of the Bridge Company, five aldermen in blue gowns round a table with a model of the bridge on it, blocked in and half painted. It is extremely good. Alderman Gidley is in the middle, with one hand on the model bridge as if blessing it and the other, which the painter has not finished, very near the money-box.".
    State true_likeness "On the easel, the Bench of the Bridge Company, finished: five aldermen in blue gowns round the model bridge, each exactly himself, the soft hands, the good dinners, the small eyes and the large purses, and Gidley in the middle with one hand blessing the bridge and the other on the money-box, and on all their faces the same expression of men who have just been told something sad about other people.".
    State flattering "On the easel, the Bench of the Bridge Company, finished: five noble aldermen, rather thinner than life, gazing into the distance over the model bridge with the look of men contemplating Sacrifice. The money-box has been painted out. There is a dove.".
    State carried_off "The easel at the end of the row is empty.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(portrait, sketched).
  Relation lumleyPaid(group). Relation gidleySat(group). Relation portraitBanner(place). Relation portraitHung(place).
  Topic lumley_portrait with lumley "Ask Tom Lumley about the portrait" when state(portrait, sketched) once {
    Says "'The Worshipful Company of the Bridge, for their new hall.' He mixes something on a plate. 'Ten crowns, on delivery, if they like it, by the Feast.' He looks at the canvas with dislike. 'They won't sit. They sat once, all together, for an hour, and talked about the carters, and I got all I need.' He adds a touch of red to Gidley's nose. 'I'm painting what I saw. What I saw is not what they'll pay for. I have the rent to find.' He looks at you sidelong. 'They'll vote for anything that costs them nothing, you know. I've watched them do it for three weeks. You could get the Bench to pass a vote of thanks to the Devil if he waived the fee.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bench_rule). }
  }
  Discovery bench_rule "The Bench of the Bridge Company will pass any motion that costs them nothing they can be seen to lose: not money, not face with the lord, not the toll. Phrased so, they will pass anything." {
    Known by lumley, inchbold, abbess, pell.
  }
  Action sit_gidley(actor: group, site: place) "Keep Alderman Gidley talking by the easel while Tom Lumley paints him" {
    Description "An hour of the Company's sacrifices, while the painter works.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, guild_hall) and at(gidley, guild_hall)
      and at(lumley, guild_hall) and state(portrait, sketched) and not gidleySat(actor).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert gidleySat(actor). Assert state(portrait, true_likeness). }
    Result "You ask the Alderman about the Company's burdens, and he tells you, for an hour, standing by the easel, about the cost of the bridge's upkeep, the ingratitude of carters, the lord's unreasonable rent, and his own sleepless nights, with his hand on his heart. Behind him Tom Lumley paints without once looking at his own hand. When Gidley at last goes off to his dinner, Lumley steps back from the canvas and looks at it and says, quite quietly, 'There. There he is.'".
  }
  Topic lumley_flatter with lumley "Tell Tom Lumley to paint them what they'll pay for" when state(portrait, sketched) once {
    Says "The brush stays in the air. 'The rent,' he says. 'Yes.' He picks up a rag and wipes out the money-box, and Gidley's nose, and everyone's chins, with a long sigh, very carefully, the way a man takes out a splinter. 'I'll put a dove in,' he says. 'They like a dove.'".
    On discuss { Assert state(portrait, flattering). Assert lumleyPaid(lumley). }
  }
  Action carry_portrait(actor: group, site: place) "Carry the true portrait out to the carters' yards for a banner" {
    Description "Lumley says it's his to sell, and he'll sell it for a pint to anyone who'll carry it where it'll be looked at.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, guild_hall) and state(portrait, true_likeness)
      and not portraitHung(wray) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 1.
    Time 2.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Assert state(portrait, carried_off). Assert portraitBanner(wray). Increase temper(wray) by 1. }
    Result "Lumley takes your coin, and laughs, and helps you get it off the easel. You carry it down the Cartway with the paint still tacky and set it up against the wall of the carters' yards. Within the hour there is a crowd round it, and within two hours somebody has nailed it to a pair of cart-shafts so that it can be carried, and the carters are standing in front of it doing Gidley's face.".
  }
  // Gidley comes to see it before the Remonstrance, and weeps.
  Rule gidley_sees_true at guild_hall when secondDay() and hour(clock) == 11 and state(portrait, true_likeness) and not portraitHung(wray) says "Alderman Gidley comes in to see the portrait before the Bench sits. He stands in front of it for a long time with his hands behind his back, and then his face begins to work, and he takes out a handkerchief. 'He has caught it,' he says, thickly. 'Our burden. Look at us. Look at our faces.' He blows his nose. 'It shall hang in the Guildhall at the Feast, where every carter in Wrayford can see what the Company has given.' He pays Lumley on the spot. Lumley takes the money as if it might go off." { Assert portraitHung(wray). Assert lumleyPaid(lumley). Increase temper(wray) by 1. }
  Observe portrait_hung at guild_hall when portraitHung(wray) and state(portrait, true_likeness) "The true portrait of the Bench hangs at the end of the row now, framed in gilt, with a little brass plate: THE WORSHIPFUL COMPANY OF THE BRIDGE IN THE YEAR OF THE RIOT. Carters come into the hall on any excuse and stand in front of it with their caps off, very respectfully, shaking.".

  // ── The Guildhall yard: the impounded carts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe reeve_yard_scene at reeve_yard when not dark() "The Guildhall yard, behind the hall: the city's fire-cart, a stack of hurdles, and along the wall three carts drawn up with their shafts down and a chalked notice on each: IMPOUNDED. GOODS OF A FELON. Wilder's is a light cart. Fenner's is old.".
  Thing pardoe_cart "Wat Pardoe's cart" at reeve_yard {
    State impounded "A big four-wheeled carter's wagon with red wheels and PARDOE, WAIN ROW painted on the board, impounded.".
    State reclaimed "Wat Pardoe's cart, with the IMPOUNDED notice rubbed off.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(pardoe_cart, impounded).
  Observe tailboard_told near pardoe_cart when tried(pardoe_cart, looking) "You go over it: the wheels first, because that is what everyone says. The wheels are clean. A wheel that had gone over a boy would not be clean, and nobody has washed these; there is the fell road's red mud dried on every spoke. Then the tailboard, and the bed of the cart behind it. There is blood there, a good deal of it, dried brown into the boards, along the length of the bed, where something was laid down and lay a long while. Not where a wheel goes. Where a boy is lifted in, and held." teaches tailboard_seen.
  Discovery tailboard_seen "Wat Pardoe's cart was not washed, and its wheels are clean. The blood is in the bed of the cart, behind the tailboard: where a hurt boy was lifted in and laid down, not where a wheel went over one.".

  // ── The Bridge Company's counting-house ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe counting_scene at counting_room when true "A long counter, high desks, a smell of new paint and new ledgers, and over the inner door a painted board: WE BEAR THE CROSSING. The Company's motto. A strongbox with the bridge in gold on the lid. Behind the counter, a door to the collector's room.".
  Person inchbold "Lancelot Inchbold" at counting_room {
    Role "the Bridge Company's clerk, with ink to the second knuckle". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner proud.
    Greets "Lancelot Inchbold finishes his line, sands it, and only then looks up, as if you were a sum he had been expecting.".
    Greets again "Lancelot Inchbold wipes his pen and sands the line he has just finished, and only then acknowledges you, as one acknowledges a sum that has come out the same twice. 'The books are not open,' he says. 'But I will tell you they are balanced. It is the only thing about them I can tell you.'".
  }
  // The clerk keeps the Company's hours, and spends his evenings in the Nine Wheels, where he hears everything.
  Rule inchbold_works when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 18 and not countingBurned(wray) and not at(inchbold, counting_room) { Assert at(inchbold, counting_room). }
  Rule inchbold_works_burned when hour(clock) >= 8 and hour(clock) < 18 and countingBurned(wray) and not at(inchbold, guild_hall) { Assert at(inchbold, guild_hall). }
  Rule inchbold_drinks when hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 23 and not at(inchbold, wheels_taproom) { Assert at(inchbold, wheels_taproom). }
  Rule inchbold_home when (hour(clock) >= 23 or hour(clock) < 8) and not at(inchbold, limbo) { Assert at(inchbold, limbo). }
  Topic inchbold_bench with inchbold "Ask the Company's clerk how the Bench decides things" when true once {
    Says "'Gracefully.' He dips his pen. 'The Bench is a body of gentlemen of the greatest goodwill, who will agree to any proposal that does not cost them anything. I draft the proposals.' He does not smile, quite. 'You would be surprised what does not cost anything, phrased well. The Remonstrance against the toll is being moved tomorrow at noon in the hall. It costs nothing: the lord will not read it.' He writes. 'I wrote it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bench_rule). Assert knows(actor, remonstrance_called). }
  }
  Discovery remonstrance_called "At noon on the second day the Bench of the Bridge Company meets in the Guildhall to move a Remonstrance to the lord against the bridge toll, which the Company itself farms. Citizens may attend, and move clauses." {
    Known by inchbold, gidley, lumley, hulme, hal, pell.
  }
  Topic inchbold_confession with inchbold "Ask the clerk who wrote Wat Pardoe's confession" when knows(actor, confession_read) and knows(actor, quoin_named) once {
    Says "Inchbold sands a line. 'A confession is a public document,' he says, 'and the public has a right to the consolation of it. Wat Pardoe was not in a position to write it himself.' He blots. 'I find the public is consoled by Drink and the Devil, and by gratitude to the Company. It is a penny. It has sold four hundred.' He looks up at last. 'It was not a lie. It was an improvement.'".
  }
  // The collector's room: Pinch's bed, and under the mattress what he could not bring himself to burn.
  Observe pinch_room_scene at pinch_room when true "A narrow room behind the counting-house: a bed made with corners like a box, a washstand, a candle-end in a saucer, a shelf with the toll schedule copied out fair and pinned up as if it were a prayer.".
  Thing pinch_lock "the lock on the collector's door" on pinch_door {
    State locked blocking "The door behind the counter is locked. Pinch keeps the key on a string round his neck.".
    State open "The door to the collector's room stands open.".
    Change pick "Pick the lock on the collector's door" from locked to open needing lockwork.
  }
  Initially Assert state(pinch_lock, locked).
  // The clerk sees everything, and writes it down, and that is all he does with it.
  Relation inchboldNoted(group).
  Rule inchbold_notes when state(pinch_lock, open) and at(inchbold, counting_room) and at(party, counting_room) and not pinchGone(pinch) and not inchboldNoted(party) says "Lancelot Inchbold watches you open the collector's door. He dips his pen, and writes something in the margin of his ledger, and blots it, and goes back to his figures. Whatever it is, it is minuted." {
    Assert inchboldNoted(party). }
  Rule pinch_locks when hour(clock) == 8 and state(pinch_lock, open) and not pinchGone(pinch) { Assert state(pinch_lock, locked). }
  Discovery daybook_found "Under Pinch's mattress, wrapped in a clean shirt: the toll day-book from the burned toll-house, its covers scorched and its pages whole." { Found by searching pinch_room. }
  Kind daybook_kind "the toll day-book" is gear worth 0 weighing 1
    described "A day-book bound in calf, scorched on the outside, every page within ruled and filled in a small exact hand: four months of the bridge toll, cart by cart, beast by beast, and a second column, very faint, in pencil.".
  Item daybook "the toll day-book" is daybook_kind at pinch_room hidden until daybook_found.
  Action read_daybook(actor: group, reader: member, site: place) "Read the toll day-book" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and memberOf(reader, actor) and ownedItem(daybook, reader) and not benighted(actor) and not knows(actor, daybook_read).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, daybook_read). }
    Result "It is very clear, which is the terrible thing about it. Every cart, every beast, every farthing, entered in ink. And beside every fifth entry, in pencil, faint as a breath, a mark: a penny for the Company, and a penny for Amos Pinch. Four months of it. The last page is the night of the rising, the entries stopping at the hour the chain went, and under them, in pencil, as if he could not help it, a sum: what the fire would save him.".
  }
  Discovery daybook_read "Pinch's day-book shows that for four months he took a penny in five of the bridge toll for himself, marked in pencil. The last page is the night of the rising, and under it a sum: what a fire would save him.".
  Discovery fire_pinch "The carters broke the chain and threw the board in the river; they did not burn the toll-house. Amos Pinch, the Company's collector, set it alight in the confusion, to burn the tally of what he had been taking. Then he could not bring himself to burn the day-book, and kept it.".
  Rule fire_put_together when knows(party, daybook_read) and (knows(party, flask_found) or knows(party, pinch_shirt)) and not knows(party, fire_pinch) says "It goes together all at once: the Company's oil flask in the ash where no carter went, the collector's shirt stinking of lamp-oil the morning after, and the day-book under his mattress with the sum on the last page. The carters broke the chain. Amos Pinch burned the toll-house." teaches fire_pinch { }
  Topic pinch_cornered with pinch "Show Pinch the Company's flask from the ash of the toll-house" when knows(actor, flask_found) and carries(actor, company_flask) and not pinchCowed(pinch) once {
    Says "Pinch looks at the flask and his lips begin to move. 'A cart, one penny,' he whispers. 'A beast, one penny the head. A carcass,' and stops, and puts his face in his hands. 'I couldn't burn the book,' he says through his fingers. 'I had the oil on it and the light in my hand and I couldn't. Four months of figures. It's the best book I ever kept.' He looks up, grey. 'What do you want? I'll rule anything. Anything on the board. Only don't show the Alderman.'".
    On discuss { Assert pinchCowed(pinch). Assert knows(actor, fire_pinch). }
  }
  Topic pinch_rules_any with pinch "Tell Pinch he will rule that the dead cross free, as the Liberty's tithe" when pinchCowed(pinch) and not ruling(ruled_tithe) once {
    Says "'The Liberty's tithe.' He writes it in his tally with a hand that shakes. 'Free. By ancient privilege.' He does not look at you. He does not look at anyone, for the rest of the day.".
    On discuss { Assert ruling(ruled_tithe). Assert knows(actor, ruled_tithe). }
  }

  // ── Cutler's Lane: the printer, the pawnshop, the cutler ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe lane_scene at cutlers_lane when not dark() "Cutler's Lane: a narrow street behind the Market where every door has a knife hung out for its sign, so that the whole lane seems to be pointing at you. Sparks from a grinder's wheel, the clatter of a press from one door, and three gilt balls over another.".
  Observe quoin_scene at quoin_shop when true "A print shop: the press like a great wooden mangle, cases of type, wet sheets pegged up on lines to dry like washing, and the smell of ink and lamp-black. On the lines: The True and Last Confession of Wat Pardoe, forty times over.".
  Person quoin "Ezra Quoin" at quoin_shop {
    Role "a printer, inky to the elbow". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner jovial.
    Greets "Ezra Quoin straightens up from the press with a sheet in each hand. 'Ballads, bills, confessions, almanacs, notices of sale,' he says. 'Three coin the hundred and I'll set it while you wait.'".
    Greets again "Ezra Quoin has pulled a fresh sheet off the press and holds it out wet by the corners, as a man shows a baby. 'You are in it,' he says. 'Not by name. By description. Whether it is a compliment depends on who reads it.'".
  }
  Topic quoin_lines with quoin "Ask Quoin what is drying on his lines" when not knows(actor, confession_read) once {
    Says "'The True and Last Confession of Wat Pardoe,' says Quoin, with a craftsman's pride. 'Forty on the lines and three hundred posted. Best thing I've sold in years.' He pats a damp sheet as if it were a horse. 'There's one on every post in the Market, if you'd rather read it dry. Everybody else has.'".
  }
  Discovery quoin_named "The Confession was printed by Ezra Quoin of Cutler's Lane, who prints anything paid for.".
  Rule confession_printer when knows(party, confession_read) and not knows(party, quoin_named) and at(party, quoin_shop) says "You know that black letter; you read it on every post in the Market." teaches quoin_named { }
  Topic quoin_who with quoin "Ask Quoin who brought him Wat Pardoe's confession to print" when knows(actor, confession_read) once {
    Says "'A gentleman of the Company,' says Quoin cheerfully. 'Mr Inchbold, the clerk. Brought it in fair copy, paid in advance, very generous.' He hangs up a sheet. 'I print what I'm brought. That's the trade. If you want to say something else, bring it me and three coin, and I'll print that too.' 'I'm a great believer in both sides.' He says it as if it were a creed, and perhaps it is.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, quoin_named). Assert knows(actor, quoin_prints). }
  }
  Discovery quoin_prints "Ezra Quoin will print anything for three coin, set while you wait, and post it in the Market by evening.".
  Action buy_confessions(actor: group, site: place) "Buy up Quoin's whole stock of the Confession, and have the sheets in the Market taken down" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, quoin_shop) and at(quoin, quoin_shop)
      and knows(actor, confession_read) and not confessionDown(wray) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 5.
    Time 1.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Assert confessionDown(wray). Increase temper(wray) by 1. }
    Result "'The lot?' Quoin is delighted. 'Five coin, and my boy'll scrape the Market for nothing, he likes scraping.' He bundles the drying sheets off the lines and gives them to you to burn, which you do, in the alley, and his boy goes off with a bucket.".
  }
  Action smash_forme(actor: group, site: place) "Knock the type of the Confession out of Quoin's press" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, quoin_shop) and capable(actor, brawn)
      and not confessionDown(wray).
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert confessionDown(wray). Assert hostile(quoin, actor). }
    Result "You put your shoulder to the forme and it comes out of the bed of the press and goes over, and four hundred letters go across the floor like hail. Quoin stands looking at them. 'That,' he says, 'was three hours' work,' and then, quite calmly, 'Get out of my shop.'".
  }
  // A broadside of your own: what it says is what you know, and what you choose to say.
  Relation printed(entity).
  Entity sheet_trial: fact "THREE CARTERS HANGED ON THE ROAD WITHOUT A TRIAL".
  Entity sheet_fire: fact "WHO BURNED THE TOLL-HOUSE?".
  Entity sheet_elegy: fact "AN ELEGY FOR NED HOBDAY, AGED FOURTEEN".
  Entity sheet_kit: fact "THE TRUE ACCOUNT OF THE CART".
  Query printReady(a: group) means at(a, quoin_shop) and at(quoin, quoin_shop) and knows(a, quoin_prints) and not hostile(quoin, a) and quantity(a, gold) >= 3.
  Action print_trial(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Quoin to print: THREE CARTERS HANGED ON THE ROAD WITHOUT A TRIAL" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and printReady(actor) and not printed(sheet_trial).
    Time 2.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Assert printed(sheet_trial). Increase temper(wray) by 1. }
    Result "You write it at his bench in the plainest words you have: the warrant, the fell road, the rope before light, no court, no trial, a dead boy in the cart. Quoin sets it in the big black letter. By evening it is pasted on every post the Confession was on, and over half of them.".
  }
  Action print_fire(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Quoin to print: WHO BURNED THE TOLL-HOUSE?" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and printReady(actor) and knows(actor, fire_pinch) and not printed(sheet_fire).
    Time 2.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Assert printed(sheet_fire). Assert pinchExposed(wray). Increase temper(wray) by 1. }
    Result "You write it as a question, which is how Quoin says the best ones go: an oil flask of the Company's in the ash where no carter went, a collector's shirt sent to the wash stinking of lamp-oil, a day-book that did not burn. Quoin reads it over twice and whistles. 'Both sides,' he says. 'I did say.' By evening a crowd is reading it aloud at the Cross, and somebody has written PINCH under it in charcoal.".
  }
  Relation pinchExposed(place).
  Action print_elegy(actor: group, site: place) "Write an elegy for Ned Hobday, and pay Quoin to print it" {
    Description "Not about the carters. About the boy.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and printReady(actor) and knows(actor, jennet_hates) and not printed(sheet_elegy).
    Time 3.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Assert printed(sheet_elegy). Increase temper(wray) by 1. Increase jennetTrust(jennet) by 1. }
    Result "It takes you longer than you thought, at Quoin's bench, crossing out. In the end it is short: a boy of fourteen in his father's hat, a penny a day, holding the lord's chain because it was his to hold. Nothing about who drove. Quoin reads it, and does not make a joke, and sets it in a small plain letter with a black border, and does not charge for the border. By evening it is on the door of the toll-keeper's house, and somebody has put a flower under it.".
  }
  Action print_kit(actor: group, site: place) "Pay Quoin to print the true account of the cart: that Kit Pardoe was driving, and his father took the blame" {
    Grave "Printed, it cannot be unprinted. Every rider and constable in Wrayford can read.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and printReady(actor) and knows(actor, kit_driving) and not printed(sheet_kit).
    Time 2.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Assert printed(sheet_kit). Assert kitExposed(wray). }
    Result "Quoin sets it without a word, and pastes it up at dusk. It is true. Wat Pardoe did not run down the toll-keeper's boy; he lifted him into the cart and drove for the bone-setter, and said he had been driving so that his son would not hang. Everyone in the Market reads it. Sergeant Gault reads it at the Cross, slowly, moving his lips, and then goes off up the Cartway toward Northgate.".
  }
  Relation kitExposed(place).
  Rule kit_taken_exposed when kitExposed(wray) and not kitTaken(kit) and not travelsWith(kit, party) and hour(clock) >= 20 says "In the evening the riders go into the carters' yards and take Kit Pardoe, who does not fight them, and walk him to the Guildhall cellar through a crowd that does not know whether to cheer or curse." {
    Assert kitTaken(kit). Assert at(kit, guild_cellar). Set kitTrust(kit) to 0. }

  // The pawnshop, kept by Alderman Gidley's cousin.
  Observe pawn_scene at pawnshop when true "A dark shop full of other people's things: clocks, Sunday coats, a fiddle, a trayful of rings under glass, a cradle. Each has a ticket on a string.".
  Person pratt "Dorothea Pratt" at pawnshop {
    Role "who keeps the pawnshop, Alderman Gidley's cousin". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner proud.
    Greets "Mistress Pratt reads your hands before she reads your face: what you carry, what you have lately stopped carrying, the pale band where a ring was. 'Pledge or redeem?' she says. 'Either way, the ticket is the thing, not the goods, and I do not discuss the goods.'".
    Greets again "Mistress Pratt does not read your hands this time. She reads your pockets, and is satisfied that she has not mistaken the trade. 'Nothing today,' she says. 'Then it is a call, and I do not take calls.'".
  }
  Relation ringFreed(group). Relation chiselsBought(group).
  Topic pratt_ring with pratt "Ask Mistress Pratt about Joss Wilder's betrothal ring" when knows(actor, ring_missing) once {
    Says "'Wilder.' She turns a ledger and runs her finger down it. 'A gold ring, plain, a heart cut inside. Pawned for four shillings a fortnight ago, to pay the new toll on his cart.' She closes the ledger. 'It's not for sale. Mr Inchbold of the Company has been round. A felon's goods are forfeit to the lord, and the Company is making the inventory for the lord's steward. I'm to hold it.' She looks at you without much interest. 'Unless the redemption were paid twice over, for my trouble. Which I would have to account for. Eight coin.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ring_pawned). }
  }
  Discovery ring_pawned "Joss Wilder pawned his betrothal ring a fortnight ago to pay the new toll on his cart. Mistress Pratt holds it for the Company's inventory of a felon's goods, and will sell it back for eight coin.".
  Kind ring_kind "Joss Wilder's ring" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0
    described "A plain gold ring, thin with being worn, with a heart cut on the inside.".
  Item joss_ring "Joss Wilder's ring" is ring_kind at limbo.
  Action buy_ring(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Pay Mistress Pratt eight coin for Joss Wilder's ring" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, pawnshop) and at(pratt, pawnshop)
      and knows(actor, ring_pawned) and not ringFreed(actor) and memberOf(recipient, actor) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 8.
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve acquire(joss_ring, ring_kind, recipient).
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 8. Assert ringFreed(actor). }
    Result "She counts the coins twice and puts the ring in your palm without a word, and writes something in the ledger, and you see that it is: lost.".
  }
  Action argue_ring(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Tell Mistress Pratt that the ring was pawned before Joss was any felon, and is the pawn's, not the lord's" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, pawnshop) and at(pratt, pawnshop)
      and knows(actor, ring_pawned) and not ringFreed(actor) and not triedPratt(actor) and not ruling(ruled_felon) and memberOf(recipient, actor)
      and quantity(actor, gold) >= 4.
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Assert ringFreed(actor). Assert acquireRing(recipient). }
    On failure { Assert triedPratt(actor). }
    Result "She opens her mouth, and shuts it, and looks at the ledger. 'A fortnight ago,' she says. 'He was a carter a fortnight ago.' She sniffs. 'The four shillings, then. And the Company can take it up with me.' She puts the ring in your hand.".
    Otherwise "'Mr Inchbold says otherwise,' she says. 'Eight coin, or good day.'".
  }
  Relation triedPratt(group). Relation acquireRing(member).
  Action take_ring(actor: group, recipient: member, site: place) "Take the ring that is owed" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and memberOf(recipient, actor) and acquireRing(recipient).
    Time 0.
    Resolve acquire(joss_ring, ring_kind, recipient).
    On success { Retract acquireRing(recipient). }
    Result "{recipient} takes Joss Wilder's ring.".
  }
  // What is pledged is hers until it is redeemed, and she says so.
  Entity pratt_objects: fact "'Those are pledged,' says Mistress Pratt, very loud, with her hand on the bell for the reeve's man. 'Pledged, and in my ledger, and not yours.'".
