    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, revels_hall) and mishapOn(wapshotts) and not mishapDone(wapshotts) and (echoLearned(actor) or reversalLearned(actor))
      and (mishapCloud(wapshotts) or mishapColonel(wapshotts)).
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert mishapDone(wapshotts). Increase revelsScore(wapshotts) by 3. }
    On failure { Assert mishapDone(wapshotts). }
    Result "You go out and stand under him, and become him: the Colonel stuck, the Colonel silent, the Colonel with his crown over one eye, exactly, his mirror; and then you move first, and he, without meaning to, follows you, and the mirror-door of Pell and Fell is suddenly happening in front of the Household with the Colonel as its other half. Mother Pell, in the gallery, shrieks. The Dowager laughs before anyone. It is, everyone afterwards agrees, the best thing in either masque.".
    Otherwise "You go out and give the moment back, and it is only you copying a man in trouble, and the court looks away, politely.".
  }
  Action call_tom_down(actor: group, site: place) "Cup your hands and call, in Jabez's voice: 'Tom! Supper!'" {
    Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, revels_hall) and mishapRaven(wapshotts) and not mishapDone(wapshotts) and (echoLearned(actor) or knows(actor, tom_call)).
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert mishapDone(wapshotts). Increase revelsScore(wapshotts) by 3. }
    On failure { Assert mishapDone(wapshotts). Decrease revelsScore(wapshotts) by 1 or to nothing. }
    Result "You call him the old way, high and thin, 'Tom! Supper!', in a voice that is Jabez's near enough; and Old Tom comes down out of the rigging in a long black slant and lands on the arm of the Dowager's chair and gives her back her tiara, carefully, as a present, and waits for supper. The Dowager looks at the raven. The raven looks at the Dowager. 'MAKE WAY FOR THE KING,' he says to her, kindly. She laughs till she has to be held.".
    Otherwise "You call, and it is your voice, and in the rigging Old Tom says, in your voice, 'Tom! Supper!' and keeps the tiara.".
  }
  Action carry_on(actor: group, site: place) "Carry on exactly as if nothing had happened, as the forms of a court require" {
    Time 1.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, revels_hall) and mishapOn(wapshotts) and not mishapDone(wapshotts) and courtTaught(actor).
    On success { Assert mishapDone(wapshotts). Increase revelsScore(wapshotts) by 1. }
    Result "You step forward and carry on as Hench taught you: as if a court had never in its history seen anything amiss, which is what courts are for. You finish the Colonel's speech for him from memory, word for word, with a bow. The hall, which has been given permission to have seen nothing, gratefully sees nothing.".
  }
  Rule mishap_saved at revels_hall when mishapOn(wapshotts) and not mishapDone(wapshotts) and watch(clock) >= masqueAt(wapshotts) + 2 and regard(mumchance) >= 5
    says "Before anyone else can move, Mumchance walks out onto the stage, in his white face, without hurry, and looks up at whatever has gone wrong; and then he looks at the court, with the look, the one he gives the ladder; and the court, who did not know they were allowed to, laugh." {
    Assert mishapDone(wapshotts). Increase revelsScore(wapshotts) by 1. }
  Rule mishap_left at revels_hall when mishapOn(wapshotts) and not mishapDone(wapshotts) and watch(clock) >= masqueAt(wapshotts) + 3
    says "Nobody does anything. In the end Tobias Quarrendon, scarlet, goes up a ladder, and the thing is put right after a fashion, and the Triumph of Wonder limps to an end with the court looking at its hands." {
    Assert mishapDone(wapshotts). Decrease revelsScore(wapshotts) by 2 or to nothing. }

  // ── 6. The verdict ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule m7_rest_unroofed at revels_hall when revelsOn(wapshotts) and masque(wapshotts) == 7 and not hallRoofed(wapshotts) and not masqueTold(rest_gate)
    says "The Steward rises. 'The Rest,' she says first, as the charter requires. 'I have sat three hours under the open sky in a hall the Household roofed in lead four hundred years ago. It is a fine sky. It is not a roof.'" { Assert masqueTold(rest_gate). Decrease revelsScore(wapshotts) by 2 or to nothing. }
  Rule m7_rest_roofed at revels_hall when revelsOn(wapshotts) and masque(wapshotts) == 7 and hallRoofed(wapshotts) and not masqueTold(rest_gate)
    says "The Steward rises. 'The Rest,' she says first, as the charter requires. 'It has a roof over its Revels again, and its dens are fit for beasts, or nearly, and its Warm-House stands, or nearly. Somebody has done in twelve days what the Household could not do in three hundred years, which is not a great compliment to the Household.'" {
    Assert masqueTold(rest_gate). Increase revelsScore(wapshotts) by 2. }
  Rule m7_dens when masqueTold(rest_gate) and densFit(wapshotts) and not masqueTold(beast_yard) { Assert masqueTold(beast_yard). Increase revelsScore(wapshotts) by 1. }
  Rule m7_warm when masqueTold(rest_gate) and warmGlazed(wapshotts) and not masqueTold(warm_house) { Assert masqueTold(warm_house). Increase revelsScore(wapshotts) by 1. }
  Rule m7_cloud when masqueTold(rest_gate) and cloudMended(wapshotts) and not masqueTold(revels_hall) { Assert masqueTold(revels_hall). Increase revelsScore(wapshotts) by 1. }
  Rule m7_sold at revels_hall when masqueTold(rest_gate) and bishopSold(methuselah) and not masqueTold(keepers_book)
    says "'The Bishop,' says the Steward, and her voice goes cold, 'is at Coldharbour, in a heated pen, being measured daily. I am told he was sold. I am told it was for forty coin.' She does not look at Sir Gervase, who has gone pink to the ears." {
    Assert masqueTold(keepers_book). Decrease revelsScore(wapshotts) by 3 or to nothing. }
  Rule m7_shilling at revels_hall when masqueTold(rest_gate) and sealLost(tobias) and knows(party, jabez_shilling) and not masqueTold(tom)
    says "'The seal,' says the Steward, and Tobias goes white, 'is lost; my great-nephew lost it on this hill. A warrant cannot be given without a seal.' Silence. Then, at the door, Jabez Orme lifts the ribbon from round his neck and holds out a silver coin worn as thin as a fingernail. 'The last King's shilling,' he says. 'He gave it at the gate. Keep it, Orme, we shall come again.' The Steward looks at it for a long time. 'That,' she says, 'will do better than a seal.'" {
    Assert masqueTold(tom). Retract sealLost(tobias). Assert sealBack(tobias). }
  Rule m7_judge at revels_hall when masqueTold(rest_gate) and masque(wapshotts) == 7 and not revelsDone(wapshotts) and not masqueTold(dowager) {
    Assert masqueTold(dowager). }
  // Wapshott's, or the United Circus, wins.
  Rule warrant_won at revels_hall when masqueTold(dowager) and not revelsDone(wapshotts) and revelsScore(wapshotts) > pellScore(wapshotts)
    and (merged(wapshotts) or revelsScore(wapshotts) > sallowScore(wapshotts)) and not (fenwickSigned(wapshotts) and clauseBeasts(wapshotts))
    says "The Steward turns to the Dowager, who has been laughing on and off since the cockerel and has not entirely stopped. The Dowager nods. The Steward raises her staff with its little gilt wheel. 'By the Crown's leave,' she says, 'and the Household's seal, the office of MASTER OF THE REVELS AND KEEPER OF THE MENAGERIE ROYAL, vacant these three hundred years, is given to,' and she looks down at the paper, and then at the Colonel, 'Colonel Florian Wapshott and his company. With the King's Rest for its winter seat, and the Inventory for its charge, and God help them all.' The Colonel does not roar. He kneels on the green boards of the Revels Hall in his gold crown, and bows his head, and when he lifts it his face is wet; and at the door Jabez Orme is sweeping the step, as hard as he can, so as not to be seen crying." {
    Assert warrantOurs(wapshotts). Assert revelsDone(wapshotts). Retract revelsOn(wapshotts). }
  Rule warrant_fenwick at revels_hall when masqueTold(dowager) and not revelsDone(wapshotts) and revelsScore(wapshotts) > pellScore(wapshotts)
    and (merged(wapshotts) or revelsScore(wapshotts) > sallowScore(wapshotts)) and fenwickSigned(wapshotts) and clauseBeasts(wapshotts)
    says "The Steward raises her staff. 'The office of Master of the Revels is given to Colonel Wapshott and his company.' The hall rises. The Steward lifts a hand, and it sits again. 'And since the Colonel's contract, which Sir Gervase has very properly laid before me, gives Sir Gervase the first right in every beast of the Inventory, the Keepership of the Menagerie Royal goes with that right. To Sir Gervase Fenwick, of Coldharbour.' Sir Gervase stands up, delighted, and then sees Billie Ostrander's face, and sits down again, less so. The Colonel bows, beautifully, to everyone, and looks, for the first time since you have known him, his age." {
    Assert warrantOurs(wapshotts). Assert warrantFenwick(wapshotts). Assert revelsDone(wapshotts). Retract revelsOn(wapshotts). }
  // Or a rival does.
  Rule warrant_pell at revels_hall when masqueTold(dowager) and not revelsDone(wapshotts) and pellScore(wapshotts) >= revelsScore(wapshotts) and (merged(wapshotts) or pellScore(wapshotts) >= sallowScore(wapshotts))
    says "The Steward raises her staff. 'The office of Master of the Revels, being in its first nature an office of plays and masques, is given to Mr Augustus Pell and the Comedians of the Theatre Royal.' Augustus bows to the dais, magnificently, with real tears. The Steward turns. 'And Her Serene Highness, who will be obeyed, wishes it known that she has laughed more tonight than in thirty years, and not at the Virtues.' The Dowager holds out a parchment, already signed: BY APPOINTMENT TO HER SERENE HIGHNESS THE DOWAGER ARCHDUCHESS, WAPSHOTT'S CIRCUS, PURVEYORS OF WONDER. The Colonel takes it in both hands. It is everything he has wanted all his life. He looks at it for a long time, and then up at the green ceiling of the Revels Hall, and you can see him find out that it is not, now, what he wants." {
    Assert warrantPell(wapshotts). Assert revelsDone(wapshotts). Retract revelsOn(wapshotts). }
  Rule warrant_sallow at revels_hall when masqueTold(dowager) and not revelsDone(wapshotts) and rivalSallow() and sallowScore(wapshotts) > pellScore(wapshotts) and sallowScore(wapshotts) >= revelsScore(wapshotts)
    says "The Steward raises her staff. 'The office of Master of the Revels and Keeper of the Menagerie Royal is given to Madame Cordelia Sallow and the Imperial Hippodrome, who can add.' Madame Sallow rises and curtseys, not deeply. Then she turns, across the whole hall, to the Colonel. 'Florian,' she says. 'I shall want someone to tell me what the Inventory is for.' The Dowager, meanwhile, holds out a parchment to the Colonel: BY APPOINTMENT TO HER SERENE HIGHNESS, WAPSHOTT'S CIRCUS, PURVEYORS OF WONDER. 'For the cockerel,' she says." {
    Assert warrantSallow(wapshotts). Assert revelsDone(wapshotts). Retract revelsOn(wapshotts). }
  // The Long Court becomes the circus's stand on that round, for good, if the Rest is theirs.
  Rule rest_kept when warrantOurs(wapshotts) and revelsDone(wapshotts) and nextGround(tober_a, tober_b) and current(wapshotts, tober_c) { Retract nextGround(tober_a, tober_b). Assert nextGround(tober_a, tober_r). }
  Rule court_goes when revelsDone(wapshotts) and day(clock) > revelsDay(wapshotts) and hour(clock) >= 9 and not offstage(dowager) {
    Assert offstage(dowager). Assert offstage(steward). Retract away(fenwick). Retract jabezBusy(jabez). }
  Rule fenwick_home when revelsDone(wapshotts) and day(clock) > revelsDay(wapshotts) + 1 and not warrantFenwick(wapshotts) and travels(fenwick) and (not crateCome(wapshotts) or backFromSarn(wapshotts)) { Retract travels(fenwick). Assert offstage(fenwick). }
  Rule hench_leaves near hench when henchGoes(hench) and revelsDone(wapshotts) and day(clock) > revelsDay(wapshotts) and travels(hench)
    says "Hench leaves with the Dowager's household in the morning, his trunk on the back of her carriage, in a new black coat. He shakes hands with everyone in the backyard, formally, and with Bucephalus, and goes. The wardrobe wagon is very quiet. On its steps, folded, is the Margravine's green spangle, on a note: FOR THE RAVEN." {
    Retract travels(hench). Assert offstage(hench). }
  Rule sallow_goes_after when revelsDone(wapshotts) and rivalSallow() and day(clock) > revelsDay(wapshotts) and sallowAtRevels(sallow) and not offstage(sallow) { Assert offstage(sallow). }
  Rule neb_goes_after when revelsDone(wapshotts) and rivalSallow() and day(clock) > revelsDay(wapshotts) and not exhibit(neb) and not offstage(neb) { Assert offstage(neb). }
  Rule hob_to_rest near jabez when revelsDone(wapshotts) and hobInvited(ninepence) and warrantOurs(wapshotts) and not hobAtRest(ninepence) and day(clock) > revelsDay(wapshotts)
    says "Ninepence does not come down the hill with the wagons. In the Keeper's Lodge at the King's Rest the porridge, from this morning, is very good." {
    Assert hobAtRest(ninepence). Retract travels(ninepence). Assert at(ninepence, keeper_lodge). Retract hobJoined(ninepence). Retract hobAtInn(ninepence). }

  // ── After: what each says ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic wap_after_revels with wapshott "Ask the Colonel what the Revels have made of Wapshott's" when revelsDone(wapshotts) and warrantOurs(wapshotts) once {
    Says "The Colonel is sitting on the mounting-block at the end of the Long Court in his shirt, with the warrant on his knee and Jabez's broom against his shoulder, looking at the ruin. 'A royal seat,' he says. 'With no roof but Lusk's. A menagerie royal, consisting of a tortoise, a cockerel and an owlbear. An Inventory of beasts three hundred years dead or gone to the fen. And a warrant to hold a Progress every year, at my own expense, before the Household of the Progress, which is two people.' He looks at you, and he is happier than you have ever seen him, and more frightened. 'I have never in my life been given anything I could not afford. I find it very much worse than being poor.' A pause. 'Sir Gervase says the rest of the Worm is under that field. He says the Royal Society would pay to see it dug.' The light comes into his eye. 'Ada says if I so much as look at a spade she'll have my pen again.'".
  }
  Topic wap_after_pell with wapshott "Ask the Colonel how he bears losing the Revels to Pell" when revelsDone(wapshotts) and (warrantPell(wapshotts) or warrantSallow(wapshotts)) once {
    Says "The Colonel has hung the Dowager's parchment in his wagon, in place of the portrait, which is now on the other wall, facing the room. 'By appointment,' he says. 'Nineteen years I wanted that.' He looks at it with great affection and no longer quite seeing it. 'And now I find I want a hill with a ruin on it, and a raven, and an old man with a broom.' He shrugs. 'Pell will make the Rest a theatre, and it will be very good, and very indoors.' Then he grins. 'He has asked me to lend him the Bishop for his masque next spring. I said yes. I said: at a cabbage an hour.'".
  }
  Topic steward_after with steward "Ask the Steward what the Household will do now" when revelsDone(wapshotts) once {
    Says "Dame Honorine leans on her staff. 'Hold a Progress,' she says. 'Every year, as the warrant says. A little one: a hill, a ruin, a circus.' She looks round the Long Court, at the wagons, the swept setts, the raven on the gatehouse. 'For fifty-one years I have been Steward of nothing. I had begun to think that the Household was a joke the Crown had forgotten to stop telling.' She taps the staff. 'It may still be. But it is a better joke now.' And then, as she is carried off down the hill: 'Tell your Colonel the Treasury's wagon is not to be found. Tell him not to look for it. He will look for it.'".
  }
  Topic jabez_after with jabez "Ask Jabez how it feels, now the Progress has come" when revelsDone(wapshotts) once {
    Says "Jabez is sitting on his step in the green velvet coat, with his broom across his knees. 'It came,' he says. 'Next spring, the King said, and it came. A bit late.' He laughs his dry bird's laugh. 'Three hundred years. Six brooms.' He looks up at the seventh hook. 'I swept the court this morning anyway. Somebody has to be ready. It would be a terrible thing if they came back and found it dirty.'".
  }
  Milestone m_letter "carried the Revels round from the letter to the Rest" worth 100 when knows(party, letter_known) and revelsDone(wapshotts).
  Milestone m_book "read the Keepers' Book with Jabez Orme" worth 100 when knows(party, margins_known).
  Milestone m_bishop "brought the Bishop home to the King's Rest" worth 300 when bishopAtRest(methuselah).
  Milestone m_seal "found the Household's seal" worth 100 when sealBack(tobias) and knows(party, seal_lost_known).
  Milestone m_pit "went down to the floor of the marl-pit" worth 200 when knows(party, worm_stone).
  Milestone m_pike "carried the great pike to the river alive" worth 100 when pikeSaved(pike).
  Milestone m_riposte "learned the Riposte from Mumchance" worth 100 when riposteLearned(party).
  Milestone m_echo "learned the Echo from Mother Pell" worth 100 when echoLearned(party).
  Milestone m_reversal "learned the mirror-door from Pell and Fell" worth 250 when reversalLearned(party).
  Milestone m_ladder "played the ladder for two before the Household of the Progress" worth 250 when masqueTold(mumchance) and partnered(party) and partnerRehearsed(party).
  Milestone m_wedding "stood for Honoria and Mumchance in the chapel of the Rest" worth 100 when weddingDone(honoria) and witness(party).
  Milestone m_ascension "rigged the Sylph's Ascension" worth 150 when ascensionRigged(wapshotts) and masqueTold(zephyrine).
  Milestone m_warrant "saw the office of the Revels given to Wapshott's" worth 400 when warrantOurs(wapshotts) and knows(party, letter_known).
}

data/goings-on/circus/sarn_keeping.kyr:
Module circus "Wapshott's Peregrine Circus" {
  // ── What the Keepership is for ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Three things said of the Leg and the Great Worm in Phase II meet here. The Leg in the shrine was a calf of three
  // summers, sent north as a gift for a king who wanted a wonder, and buried by his diggers in the marl while it was
  // still breathing: HE IS NOT DEAD ENOUGH. The Colonel has been calling himself a Keeper for a year. Sarn tells him
  // what the word meant to the people who had it first.
  Relation legKnown(concern). Relation colonelGrieved(concern). Relation legPromised(concern). Relation widowLetter(concern).

  Topic jabez_sarn with jabez "Ask Jabez what is written in the Southern column of the Book" when knows(actor, margins_known) once {
    Says "Jabez Orme turns the Book to a column the others have skipped. 'The Southern Preserve,' he says. 'Nobody reads it. The Wardens' hand, not the Keepers'. My grandfather's grandfather swept these cages because the last Warden wrote, and I have it by heart: SOMEONE MUST KEEP THE DOORS FOR WHEN THEY ARE ASKED FOR. We have been keeping them.' He closes the Book. 'Nobody has asked.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sarn_known). }
  }
  Observe tortoise_knows near methuselah when exhibit(methuselah) and crateCome(wapshotts) and not voyaged(wapshotts) "In his pen the Bishop has raised his head, which he does for cabbages, and is holding it up towards the yard, towards the crate, with his old eyes shut, as if he were smelling the sea.".
  Observe ada_crate near ada when crateCome(wapshotts) and not voyaged(wapshotts) "Ada Thripp has stopped writing the Brigand's Bride and is writing, in the book of the circus's accounts, a column headed SARN, in which every figure is a question.".

  Topic wap_great_beast with wapshott "Show the Colonel the page of the Warden's journal about the Great Beast" when voyaged(wapshotts) and knows(actor, journal_read) and not legKnown(wapshotts) once {
    Says "The Colonel reads it standing. At the line about the calf of three summers he stops. 'The Leg,' he says. He walks to the end of the quay and back, twice. 'HE WAS NOT DEAD ENOUGH,' he says to the sea, in his ring voice: it is what the stone said. Then, in nobody's: 'Oh, the beggars.'".
    On discuss { Assert legKnown(wapshotts). Assert colonelGrieved(wapshotts). }
  }
  Topic wap_leg_promise with wapshott "Ask the Colonel what he will do about the Leg in the shrine" when legKnown(wapshotts) and voyaged(wapshotts) and not legPromised(wapshotts) once {
    Says "'The calf comes home,' says the Colonel. 'Not the bones: the bones are the town's, they have prayed over them. The name. I shall have it cut on the shrine's step, and the Rest's, and over the beast tent: that his name was asked, and that he was brought a long way, and that he was a child.' He looks up the jungle. 'Billie,' he says, 'what was he called?' Billie says: 'Nobody knows.'".
    On discuss { Assert legPromised(wapshotts). }
  }
  Observe leg_promise_home near wapshott when backFromSarn(wapshotts) and legPromised(wapshotts) "On the step of the third town's shrine, new-cut: HE WAS ASKED FOR, AND BROUGHT, AND HE WAS A CHILD. The children have put flowers on it. The Colonel will not talk about it, and goes round by the other door.".

  // The Colonel on the cliff-top, with the colony launching: the other kind of audience.
  Topic wap_widow with wapshott "Ask the Colonel who he is writing to on the cliff-top" when voyaged(wapshotts) and at(party, cliff_top) and not widowLetter(wapshotts) once {
    Says "He folds the page before you can see it. 'A woman at Dunmere,' he says, 'to whom I owe a coin a week.' The colony goes off the edge, wing on wing. 'I have written to say I have seen it. He would have liked the house.'".
    On discuss { Assert widowLetter(wapshotts). }
  }
  Milestone m_leg "learned what the Leg in the shrine was" worth 300 when legKnown(wapshotts).
  Milestone m_widow "stood with the Colonel on the cliff-top" worth 100 when widowLetter(wapshotts).
}

data/goings-on/circus/sarn_people.kyr:
Module circus "Wapshott's Peregrine Circus" {
  // ── Companions with arcs, and four side stories that belong to no one's plot ────────────────────────────────────
  // Each companion wants something, has a fault, is asked one question by the company or asks it, and moves on at
  // least three times. A question put to the player (a `once` topic) is answered by one of several topics that
  // `answer` it, and each answer leaves a different fact. The side stories (a grave, a bottle, a camp, a boy in the
  // hold) lead nowhere; they only make the island and the voyage older than the circus.
  Relation billieCage(concern). Relation billieField(concern). Relation billieNeither(concern). Relation mumRead(group).
  Relation mumYes(concern). Relation mumNo(concern). Relation mumMatters(concern). Relation scopeNone(concern). Relation scopeSmall(concern).
  Relation scopeAll(concern). Relation crewePardoned(concern). Relation creweBlamed(concern). Relation creweAsked(concern).
  Relation dabFound(concern). Relation dabTold(concern). Relation dabHidden(concern). Relation dabColonel(concern).
  Relation epitaphDone(group). Relation thorneBuried(group). Relation thorneRead(group). Relation fenwickYielded(concern).
  Relation harrowStory(concern). Relation crewLeft(concern). Relation crewHired(concern). Relation crewStranded(concern).
  Relation bottleRead(group). Relation bottleCast(group). Relation bottleKept(group).

  // ── Billie: a woman who has kept cages all her life and has come to see what they were for ─────────────────────
  Topic billie_asks with billie "Ask Billie what she makes of the cages in the hold" when billieSat(wapshotts) and atSea(wapshotts) and not billieCage(wapshotts) and not billieField(wapshotts) and not billieNeither(wapshotts) once {
    Says "'You've seen both,' says Billie. 'I've only seen the one.' She does not look round. 'Which is worse. A cage that is kept well, or a field where nobody keeps anything?'".
  }
  Topic billie_a1 with billie "Say a kind cage is worse, because the animal learns to be glad of it" answering billie_asks when true {
    Says "'Seen that,' says Billie. She says nothing else for an hour.".
    On discuss { Assert billieCage(wapshotts). Increase regard(billie) by 1. }
  }
  Topic billie_a2 with billie "Say the field is worse, because nothing in it is answerable" answering billie_asks when true {
    Says "'The Rule says the Keeper is answerable to the beast,' says Billie. 'I've been wondering who a field is answerable to.' She looks pleased, for a moment, and annoyed to be.".
    On discuss { Assert billieField(wapshotts). Increase regard(billie) by 1. }
  }
  Topic billie_a3 with billie "Say neither, and that it depends on who is looking" answering billie_asks when true {
    Says "'That's what the Colonel would say,' says Billie. 'It isn't wrong. It's what you say when you don't want to be asked again.'".
    On discuss { Assert billieNeither(wapshotts). }
  }
  Topic billie_cage_asks with billie "Ask Billie what she would do with the Preserve-house if it were hers" when at(party, cage_row) and (billieCage(wapshotts) or billieField(wapshotts) or billieNeither(wapshotts)) and not billieCageSaid(wapshotts) once {
    Says "Billie stands in front of the ninth cage with her hands in her coat. 'If it were mine I'd open every door and sweep them all anyway,' she says. 'I'd keep the doors for when they were asked for. I'd never shut one.' She frowns at it. 'The Colonel would never shut one either. He'd hang a bill on it.'".
    On discuss { Assert billieCageSaid(wapshotts). }
  }
  Relation billieCageSaid(concern).
  Action read_billie(actor: group, site: place) "Look at what Billie does with her hands while the Colonel talks of the egg" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(billie, site) and at(party, landing) and not billieRead(party).
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert billieRead(party). Increase regard(billie) by 1. }
    Result "She is counting, on the inside of her coat, with her thumb against her fingers. It is the number of days she has left to say yes to him. She sees you see it, and does not put her hand away.".
    Otherwise "Billie is looking at the sea, and gives you nothing.".
  }
  Relation billieRead(group).

  // ── Mumchance: a man who has been silent for forty years and has never been asked to speak by anyone he trusted ──
  Action read_mumchance(actor: group, site: place) "Watch Mumchance's face while the Colonel talks" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(mumchance, site) and atSea(wapshotts) and not mumRead(party).
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert mumRead(party). }
    Result "He is listening to the Colonel the way a man listens to the sea. The Colonel says a great thing, and Mumchance's mouth moves a hair's breadth. He is saying it with him, for the tenth thousand time, with no sound. He would, you think, give a year of his life to hear someone say something to him that he had not already known.".
    Otherwise "Mumchance meets your eye with the look he keeps for the house, which gives away nothing, and is kind.".
  }
  Topic mum_slate with mumchance "Take the slate Mumchance holds out to you" when herdSeen(party) and not mumYes(wapshotts) and not mumNo(wapshotts) and not mumMatters(wapshotts) once {
    Says "He has written, in a clerk's round hand: DO THEY KNOW WE ARE HERE. He holds the slate up, and the herd goes on drinking behind him.".
  }
  Topic mum_a1 with mumchance "Write: yes, and they do not mind" answering mum_slate when true {
    Says "He reads it twice. He wipes the slate with his sleeve, and writes: GOOD. THEN I NEED NOT WORRY ABOUT THE HOUSE. He puts his chalk away and does not take it out again.".
    On discuss { Assert mumYes(wapshotts). }
  }
  Topic mum_a2 with mumchance "Write: no, they have never heard of us" answering mum_slate when true {
    Says "He nods. He writes: THAT IS WHAT I THOUGHT. He smiles.".
    On discuss { Assert mumNo(wapshotts). Increase regard(mumchance) by 1. }
  }
  Topic mum_a3 with mumchance "Write: it makes no difference" answering mum_slate when true {
    Says "He looks at it a good while. Then he writes, small, in the corner: IT DOES TO ME. He wipes it before you can read it twice.".
    On discuss { Assert mumMatters(wapshotts). Increase regard(mumchance) by 2. }
  }

  // ── Sir Gervase: kind, and blind in one place ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic fenwick_scope with fenwick "Ask Sir Gervase which kinds he will take" when at(party, landing) and voyaged(wapshotts) and clausesRead(wapshotts) and not scopeNone(wapshotts) and not scopeSmall(wapshotts) and not scopeAll(wapshotts) once {
    Says "Sir Gervase has his list on his knee. 'Which would you let me take?' he says. He is asking. It is the first time he has asked anyone.".
  }
  Topic fenwick_a1 with fenwick "Say none, and let the Society have your drawings instead" answering fenwick_scope when true {
    Says "He is silent some time. 'I should have to explain to the committee,' he says, 'that I went to the end of the world and drew a picture.' He laughs. 'I find I should like that much.' He crosses out the whole page.".
    On discuss { Assert scopeNone(wapshotts). Assert fenwickYielded(wapshotts). }
  }
  Topic fenwick_a2 with fenwick "Say only the small and plentiful: the runners, the skimmers, the lizards" answering fenwick_scope when true {
    Says "'Plentiful,' he says. 'Yes. Yes, that is a principle.' He writes it down as though it were. 'A pair of each of the small. I can defend that to any committee in England.' He looks, you think, as though he had been let off.".
    On discuss { Assert scopeSmall(wapshotts). Assert fenwickWants(wapshotts). }
  }
  Topic fenwick_a3 with fenwick "Say all of them, if it keeps the Colonel in the Society's good books" answering fenwick_scope when not thorneBuried(party) {
    Says "He takes his pencil out. He does not write anything. 'You are kind,' he says, 'and you have not understood me at all.' He puts the pencil away. 'But it is what I wrote in the contract.'".
    On discuss { Assert scopeAll(wapshotts). Assert fenwickWants(wapshotts). }
  }

  // ── Mate Crewe: a man who has been asked to be master of a dead man's ship ──────────────────────────────────────
  Topic crewe_asks with crewe "Ask Crewe what weighs on him" when vanceKnown(wapshotts) and atSea(wapshotts) and not creweAsked(wapshotts) once {
    Says "Crewe turns the hat. 'It was my idea to answer the letter,' he says. 'Vance would have let it lie. I said a Keeper's a Keeper. He took the clutch off the beds himself, with the fever on him, and died off the Cape.' He does not look at you. 'Was it right? To ask him?'".
    On discuss { Assert creweAsked(wapshotts). }
  }
  Topic crewe_a1 with crewe "Say it was right, and that the Captain wanted to go" answering crewe_asks when true {
    Says "'I know he did,' says Crewe. 'Was it right, I said.' He puts the hat on. 'But I thank you for the answer.' He sets the course a point to starboard for no reason.".
    On discuss { Assert crewePardoned(wapshotts). }
  }
  Topic crewe_a2 with crewe "Say it was not, and that a dying man should not have been asked" answering crewe_asks when true {
    Says "'No,' says Crewe. 'That's what I think.' He is quiet. 'I have been waiting a long while for someone to say it. It is less than I hoped, and more than I could have said myself.'".
    On discuss { Assert creweBlamed(wapshotts). }
  }
  Topic crewe_a3 with crewe "Say you cannot know, and that the clutch is alive" answering crewe_asks when true {
    Says "He looks at the hold, where the sound of something small is coming up through the hatch. 'That's so,' he says. 'There's that.'".
    On discuss { Assert crewePardoned(wapshotts). }
  }

  // ── The boy in the hold ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Person dab "Dab" at hold {
    Role "a boy of eleven, stowed away among the cages". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
    Seen when dabFound(wapshotts).
    Greets "A boy comes out of the straw with a biscuit in each hand. 'Inspecting,' he says.".
  }
  Initially Assert offstage(dab).
  Rule dab_aboard when voyaged(wapshotts) and offstage(dab) { Retract offstage(dab). Assert at(dab, hold). }
  Action listen_hold(actor: group, site: place) "Listen in the hold among the empty cages" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hold) and voyaged(wapshotts) and not dabFound(wapshotts).
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert dabFound(wapshotts). }
    Result "One of the cages is breathing. A boy is asleep in the straw of the third, with a biscuit-bag for a pillow and his boots on the wrong feet.".
    Otherwise "The hold creaks and knocks. Nothing in it is anybody.".
  }
  Topic dab_asks with dab "Ask the boy what he is doing in the hold" when dabFound(wapshotts) and not dabTold(wapshotts) and not dabHidden(wapshotts) and not dabColonel(wapshotts) once {
    Says "'Mam's cook at Port Dree,' says Dab. 'I'm bound at twelve. I'm eleven.' He looks at you. 'Tell?'".
  }
  Topic dab_a1 with dab "Say you will tell Mr Crewe, and stand beside him when you do" answering dab_asks when true {
    Says "Crewe cuffs him, as the law requires, and then gives him a tin plate and a place at the galley. 'I was eleven once,' says Crewe. Dab eats his biscuit with a face like a saint's.".
    On discuss { Assert dabTold(wapshotts). }
  }
  Topic dab_a2 with dab "Say nothing, and tell him to stay out of the way" answering dab_asks when true {
    Says "'I will,' says Dab, and vanishes into the straw with the dignity of a great man. For the rest of the voyage things go missing: a biscuit, a candle, one of the Colonel's gloves.".
    On discuss { Assert dabHidden(wapshotts). Decrease quantity(party, rations) by 2 or to nothing. }
  }
  Topic dab_a3 with dab "Take him to the Colonel" answering dab_asks when true {
    Says "The Colonel hears it standing, with his hat on. 'A boy,' he says, 'who has stowed away to see the unseen.' He looks round for something grand to say, and says it. 'Master Dab, you are appointed Assistant Zoologist to the Menagerie Royal, at a salary of nothing, with all the privileges.' Dab salutes with both hands.".
    On discuss { Assert dabColonel(wapshotts). }
  }
  Topic dab_glide with dab "Ask Dab what he has seen from the foretop" when dabColonel(wapshotts) and at(party, cycad_aisle) and not knows(actor, hollow_way_known) once {
    Says "'Them lizards,' says Dab, who has climbed a cycad without being asked. 'They all go the same road at supper. Look. There.' He points. 'All to the notch in the trees.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hollow_way_known). }
  }

  // ── Captain Harrow, his men, and a debt ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Place wreck_camp "the Coldharbour camp" is room within s_delta at 1, 2 outdoors.
  Passage delta_wreck "the tide-line track" is path between delta_edge and wreck_camp taking 20 minutes.
  Topic harrow_story with harrow "Ask Captain Harrow how he came to Sarn" when knows(actor, harrow_known) and not harrowStory(wapshotts) once {
    Says "'I kept lions for Cordelia Sallow for twelve years,' says Harrow. 'I lost one. Not to a bite; to a draught. She dismissed me with a month's wages and a reference, and the reference was true, which is worse.' He nods at the four men at their mugs. 'They were my stable lads. They came with me because they are owed. I shall pay them out of the first calf.' He does not look at them. 'Tell me honestly. Would you leave four men on a beach for a principle?'".
    On discuss { Assert harrowStory(wapshotts). }
  }
  Topic harrow_a1 with harrow "Say yes, if the principle is theirs to keep" answering harrow_story when true {
    Says "'Then you will not mind,' says Harrow, 'if I hold you to it,' and he laughs, and he has a good laugh, and you understand he has no idea what he will do.".
    On discuss { Assert crewStranded(wapshotts). }
  }
  Topic harrow_a2 with harrow "Say no, and that you will make good what they are owed" answering harrow_story when true {
    Says "'That is handsome,' says Harrow. 'Handsome. I would have settled for yes.' He sends for the men. 'Lads. These people will stand your wages in the fair town if you come aboard with them.' There is a long silence, and then a net-man puts down his mug.".
    On discuss { Assert crewLeft(wapshotts). Assert harrowBeaten(party). Retract at(harrow_men, harrow_camp). }
  }
  Topic harrow_a3 with harrow "Say they might do well in a circus, and that you can ask the Colonel" answering harrow_story when true {
    Says "'In a circus,' says Harrow. 'Four net-men.' He thinks about it. 'There is a Hippodrome rule that a net-man is a net-man. I should like to see it broken.' He raises his voice. 'Lads! Mr Wapshott's offering places.' The net-men look at the Colonel, and at one another. It is, you think, the most dignified resignation in the history of the trade.".
    On discuss { Assert crewHired(wapshotts). Assert harrowBeaten(party). Retract at(harrow_men, harrow_camp). }
  }
  Observe crew_hired_home near honoria when crewHired(wapshotts) and backFromSarn(wapshotts) "Four men in oilskins are mucking out the horse lines, cheerfully and with a good deal of method. Honoria has told them where the tea is.".

  // ── The grave-garden: an unfinished epitaph ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe grave_seventh at cage_row when holding(party, preserve_key) "The seventh Warden has no stone. The plate in the earth is cut for a key, and below it, half-worked, an epitaph: WARDEN ANSEL THE YOUNGER, WHO KEPT THE DOORS FOR WHEN THEY WERE ASKED FOR, AND. The mason, whoever he was, stopped there.".
  Action finish_epitaph(actor: group, site: place) "Set the Preserve's key in the seventh grave and read the last word" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, cage_row) and holding(actor, preserve_key) and not epitaphDone(party).
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert epitaphDone(party). Spend preserve_key from actor. }
    Result "The key goes into the plate like a tongue into a groove. Under the unfinished line the old cut comes up in the bronze, one letter at a time: WERE ASKED. That is all. That is the whole of the sentence, and it is the same sentence.".
    Otherwise "The key sticks. The script on the plate is older than you can read, and you cannot tell if the last word is a name or an order.".
  }
  Observe crewe_grave near crewe when epitaphDone(party) and at(party, cage_row) "Crewe has taken off his hat and not put it on. He is standing at the foot of the seventh grave reading a line that is not for him.".

  // ── The bottle from the Hasty Mary ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Kind mary_bottle "a green glass bottle with a letter in it" is document teaching bottle_read described "A thick green bottle, stopped with wax and a wheel-seal, with a sheet of paper rolled inside.".
  Discovery bottle_read "The Hasty Mary's master wrote that the Great Beast refused to eat for nine days, sang to the stars all night, and would take his food only from the boy who sang back; that he put this bottle over the side to say so; that they were four days from the King's port.".
  Item bottle_item "a green glass bottle in the wrack" is mary_bottle at cliff_foot.
  Action cast_bottle(actor: group, site: place) "Reseal the bottle and throw it back from the quay" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, landing) and holding(actor, mary_bottle) and not bottleCast(party).
    Time 0.
    On success { Spend mary_bottle from actor. Assert bottleCast(party). }
    Result "It falls in a long arc and floats, green and bright, and the ebb takes it out of the bay. It will go where the Hasty Mary went, sooner or later, or nowhere.".
  }
  Topic jabez_bottle with jabez "Give Jabez the letter from the Hasty Mary's bottle" when holding(actor, mary_bottle) and not bottleKept(party) once {
    Says "Jabez Orme reads it standing, and then sits down on the step with the paper on his knee. 'It sang,' he says. 'We swept the cage three hundred years and nobody said it sang.' He lays the sheet in the Book at the page for the Great Worm, and does not close it. 'He was a boy of three summers. Somebody sang back.'".
    On discuss { Assert bottleKept(party). Spend mary_bottle from actor. }
  }
  Milestone m_bottle "carried the Hasty Mary's letter to the Keepers' Book" worth 200 when bottleKept(party).

  // ── The Coldharbour camp ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe wreck_camp_scene at wreck_camp when true "A camp thirty years old, on the sand above the tide-line: three tents rotted to ribs, a table with a chart nailed to it, and a row of specimen-cases burst and emptied by weather. Three skeletons lie in the shade of the largest tent, side by side, with their boots still on. Someone has put a tarpaulin over one, and the tarpaulin has been eaten to lace.".
  Kind thorne_journal "Dr Thorne's field-book" is document teaching thorne_read described "A salt-stained field-book in a small neat hand, the last entry dated nine days before the others. The drawings are good.".
  Discovery thorne_read "Dr Edmund Thorne of Coldharbour came to Sarn with two companions in the year of the old king's death; they took fever from the delta water; he drew the lantern-necks at the lake, and wrote that he had never been so happy.".
  Item thorne_item "Dr Thorne's field-book" is thorne_journal at wreck_camp.
  Item thorne_glass "a brass spyglass, green with age" is spyglass at wreck_camp.
  Action bury_thorne(actor: group, site: place) "Bury the three dead of the Coldharbour camp" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wreck_camp) and not thorneBuried(party).
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, rites, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert thorneBuried(party). }
    Result "You dig in the sand above the tide-line, three graves in a row, and say what you know. The tarpaulin goes in with the one it covered. It is not a funeral. It is thirty years late and it is all you have.".
    Otherwise "You say the words, and cannot find the end of them. The dead are as they were.".
  }
  Topic fenwick_thorne with fenwick "Give Sir Gervase Dr Thorne's field-book" when holding(actor, thorne_journal) and not thorneRead(party) once {
    Says "Sir Gervase opens it, and reads a line, and puts his hand over his mouth. 'He was my master,' he says. 'He went to the South in the year of my first paper. They told us fever and the sea.' He turns the pages, and his hands shake, and he finds the drawing of the herd at the lake. 'Look at it,' he says. 'He drew them as I should. As large as that. He did not take one.' He closes the book. 'I have been following him all my life and did not know where.' After a minute he says, in a different voice: 'He did not take one. Did he.'".
    On discuss { Assert thorneRead(party). Spend thorne_journal from actor. Increase regard(fenwick) by 2. }
  }
  Milestone m_thorne "found what became of Dr Thorne" worth 250 when thorneRead(party).

  Rule epitaph_pardons when epitaphDone(party) and not creweBlamed(wapshotts) and not crewePardoned(wapshotts) { Assert crewePardoned(wapshotts). }
  Observe bottle_afloat at deck when calmDone(wapshotts) and atSea(wapshotts) and bottleCast(party) "A green bottle rides past on the swell, a long way off, with its wax glinting. Nobody remarks on it. Crewe watches it out of sight.".
  Observe stranded_men at landing when crewStranded(wapshotts) and berthS(wapshotts) "Four net-men sit on the strand by the delta path in a row with their boots off, drinking, and singing a song about a woman at Dunmere with a hundred names.".
  Rule fenwick_thorne_soft when thorneRead(party) and thorneBuried(party) and not fenwickYielded(wapshotts) { Assert fenwickYielded(wapshotts). }
  Topic crewe_bottle with crewe "Give Crewe the letter from the Hasty Mary's bottle" when holding(actor, mary_bottle) once {
    Says "Crewe reads it with his lips. 'The boy who sang back,' he says. 'There'll have been a boy.' He folds it into his hat.".
    On discuss { Spend mary_bottle from actor. Assert bottleKept(party). }
  }
}

data/goings-on/circus/show.kyr:
Module circus "Wapshott's Peregrine Circus" {
  // ── The show: every night of a stand at seven, in seven parts of twenty minutes ───────────────────────────────
  // How full the benches are (the house, in coin) is the town's regard for the circus, the bills and the parade, the
  // menagerie and the weather; how well it goes (its quality) is what has been put right or let go wrong behind the
  // canvas. The takings go into the strongbox when it is over, and a good night raises the town's regard.
  Relation showOn(concern). Measure act(concern). Measure actAt(concern). Measure showDay(concern).
  Relation raining(concern). Relation strikeOn(concern). Relation admitted(group). Measure ticketDay(group).
  Relation hand(group).
  Kind actpart. Entity part_entry: actpart "the Grand Entry". Entity part_horse: actpart "Bucephalus". Entity part_quincey: actpart "the Brothers Quincey".
  Entity part_ox: actpart "the Ox of Abernant". Entity part_clown: actpart "Mumchance". Entity part_wire: actpart "the Sylph". Entity part_close: actpart "the close".
  Relation told(actpart). Relation sawAct(actpart). Measure incident(concern).
  // An act told in full the first time the company sees it, and in brief after; and every night one thing that
  // happens only that night.
  Rule saw_act when told(?p) and at(party, ?r) and ringHere(?r) and not sawAct(?p) { Assert sawAct(?p). }
  Query tonightGround(g: place) means pitched(wapshotts) and current(wapshotts, g).
  Rule admit_ticket when ticketDay(party) == day(clock) and not admitted(party) { Assert admitted(party). }
  Rule admit_hand when (hand(party) or booked(party, ?t)) and not admitted(party) { Assert admitted(party). }
  Rule admit_ends when admitted(party) and not hand(party) and not booked(party, ?t) and ticketDay(party) < day(clock) { Retract admitted(party). }

  Action buy_ticket(actor: group, site: place) "Buy a ticket for tonight's show from Ada, one coin" {
    Speaker ada. Time 1 minute.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(ada, site) and pitched(wapshotts) and not admitted(actor)
      and quantity(actor, gold) >= 1 and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 21.
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Increase strongbox(wapshotts) by 1. Set ticketDay(actor) to day(clock). Assert admitted(actor). }
    Result "Ada takes your coin, bites it, which is a joke, and tears a ticket off a roll: a square of pink card that says WAPSHOTT'S. ADMIT ONE. NO REFUNDS IN CASE OF ACTS OF GOD, FIRE, OR THE COLONEL. 'Doors at seven,' she says. 'Find a bench by the ring and stay put; it runs two hours, a turn every twenty minutes, and the wire's last.'".
  }

  // A rotten canvas, thrown at six: on a big top worn to one seam in three, a seam may go in the night wind.
  Rule rain_falls when pitched(wapshotts) and hour(clock) == 18 and showDay(wapshotts) < day(clock) and not rainThrown(wapshotts) {
    Assert rainThrown(wapshotts). }
  Rule rain_wet when rainThrown(wapshotts) and not raining(wapshotts) and not rainSettled(wapshotts) and canvas(wapshotts) <= 1 and dice(wapshotts) <= 40 { Assert raining(wapshotts). Assert rainSettled(wapshotts). }
  Rule rain_dry when rainThrown(wapshotts) and not rainSettled(wapshotts) { Assert rainSettled(wapshotts). }
  Relation rainThrown(concern). Relation rainSettled(concern).
  Rule seam_goes near ringpost when showOn(wapshotts) and act(wapshotts) == 3 and raining(wapshotts) and not seamTold(wapshotts)
    says "Above the gallery a rotten seam of the big top gives way with a noise like a sail going, and the night wind comes in through the gap and blows half the lamps out; people under it get up, and some of them go home." { Assert seamTold(wapshotts). }
  Relation seamTold(concern).

  // ── The doors at seven ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule show_begins when tonightGround(?g) and hour(clock) >= 19 and hour(clock) < 20 and showDay(wapshotts) < day(clock) and not strikeOn(wapshotts) and not revelsNight() {
    Assert showOn(wapshotts). Set showDay(wapshotts) to day(clock). Set act(wapshotts) to 1. Set actAt(wapshotts) to watch(clock).
    Set house(wapshotts) to 2 + standing(?g) * 2. Set quality(wapshotts) to 0. Set incident(wapshotts) to dice(wapshotts). Retract told(part_entry). Retract told(part_horse). Retract told(part_quincey). Retract told(part_ox). Retract told(part_clown). Retract told(part_wire). Retract told(part_close). }
  Rule show_struck near pole when tonightGround(?g) and hour(clock) >= 19 and showDay(wapshotts) < day(clock) and strikeOn(wapshotts) and not revelsNight()
    says "There is no show tonight. The canvasmen are sitting on the grass with their arms folded, and the big top stands dark, and people come to the field gate and look at it and go away." {
    Set showDay(wapshotts) to day(clock). Decrease standing(?g) by 1 or to nothing. }
  Rule show_next when showOn(wapshotts) and watch(clock) >= actAt(wapshotts) + 2 and act(wapshotts) < 7 and not onTurn(party) {
    Increase act(wapshotts) by 1. Set actAt(wapshotts) to watch(clock). }
  // What brings people, or keeps them away, counted as the doors open.
  Rule house_menagerie when showOn(wapshotts) and act(wapshotts) == 1 and not told(part_entry) and menagerieOpen(wapshotts) {
    Increase house(wapshotts) by draw(wapshotts). }
  Rule house_wet when showOn(wapshotts) and act(wapshotts) == 1 and not told(part_entry) and raining(wapshotts) and canvas(wapshotts) <= 1 {
    Decrease house(wapshotts) by 4 or to nothing. Decrease quality(wapshotts) by 2. }
  Rule house_rival when showOn(wapshotts) and act(wapshotts) == 1 and not told(part_entry) and sallowPlaying(?g) and current(wapshotts, ?g) {
    Decrease house(wapshotts) by 3 or to nothing. }
  Rule house_bills_down when showOn(wapshotts) and act(wapshotts) == 1 and not told(part_entry) and current(wapshotts, ?g) and billOf(?g, ?b) and state(?b, defaced) {
    Decrease house(wapshotts) by 2 or to nothing. }
  Rule ticket_collected near ada when showOn(wapshotts) and act(wapshotts) == 1 and at(party, ?r) and ringHere(?r) and not admitted(party) and quantity(party, gold) >= 1
    says "Ada Thripp comes along the bench with her cash-box before the band has finished, and stops in front of you, and holds out her hand, and waits, and you find you have given her a coin." {
    Decrease quantity(party, gold) by 1. Increase strongbox(wapshotts) by 1. Set ticketDay(party) to day(clock). Assert admitted(party). }

  Observe house_full near ringpost when showOn(wapshotts) and at(ringpost, ?r) and house(wapshotts) >= 10 "Every bench is full, and people are standing at the back and sitting on the ring boards' edge, and children are being passed along the rows over heads like parcels.".
  Observe house_fair near ringpost when showOn(wapshotts) and at(ringpost, ?r) and house(wapshotts) >= 6 and house(wapshotts) < 10 "The benches are well filled: farmers in their good coats, girls in threes, a row of boys who have got in under the side-wall and are pretending they paid.".
  Observe house_thin near ringpost when showOn(wapshotts) and at(ringpost, ?r) and house(wapshotts) < 6 "The house is thin tonight: a few families on the front benches, a courting couple at the back, and a great deal of bare planking that the Colonel plays to as if it were full.".
  // ── 1. The Grand Entry ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule entry_told near ringpost when showOn(wapshotts) and act(wapshotts) == 1 and not told(part_entry) and not musicSwapped(wapshotts) and not sawAct(part_entry)
    says "The band crashes into the Grand Entry. The flap flies back and in they all come, at a canter, at a walk, on their hands: the Brothers Quincey turning cartwheels, Pip with a banner, the Ox of Abernant with a pony under each arm, the Sylph in silver standing on Bucephalus's back as if he were a floor, and last of all the Colonel, enormous in crimson, cracking a whip at nothing. 'LADIES,' he roars, 'AND GENTLEMEN, AND THOSE OF YOU WHO ARE NEITHER!' The benches roar back. It is impossible not to roar back." {
    Assert told(part_entry). Increase quality(wapshotts) by 1. }
  Rule entry_hymn near ringpost when showOn(wapshotts) and act(wapshotts) == 1 and not told(part_entry) and musicSwapped(wapshotts)
    says "The band crashes into the Grand Entry, and it is a hymn. Fipps stares at the book on his stand, which is not his book, and goes on, because the band always goes on, and the whole company comes cantering into the ring to THE PENITENT'S LAMENT, slow, in a minor key, so that the Brothers Quincey cartwheel in like mourners and Bucephalus stops dead in the ring, swings his great head round, and looks at Fipps. The benches do not know whether to laugh. Some of them take their hats off." {
