  // ── The life of the place: what is going on, by the hour and the day of the stand ─────────────────────────────
  Query standDay(n: concern) means pitched(n).
  Observe yard_morning near cookfire when pitched(wapshotts) and at(cookfire, ?r) and hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 9 "Honoria Bulstrode is frying bacon by the hundredweight in a pan like a cartwheel, and the whole circus is queuing for it in its nightshirts, in order of precedence: the Colonel first, then Bucephalus, then everyone else.".
  Observe yard_noon near cookfire when pitched(wapshotts) and at(cookfire, ?r) and hour(clock) >= 12 and hour(clock) < 14 "It is the dead hour after dinner. Somebody is asleep under every wagon. A dog has stolen a sausage and is being chased, without much conviction, by a man in a sequinned jacket.".
  Observe yard_afternoon near cookfire when pitched(wapshotts) and at(cookfire, ?r) and hour(clock) >= 14 and hour(clock) < 18 and day(clock) == arrivedDay(wapshotts) "The backyard is all hammering: the seat-scaffolding going up inside, the ring boards being knocked together, Lusk's lads singing a heaving song with only one verse, which is mostly the word HEAVE.".
  Observe yard_afternoon2 near cookfire when pitched(wapshotts) and at(cookfire, ?r) and hour(clock) >= 14 and hour(clock) < 18 and day(clock) == arrivedDay(wapshotts) + 1 "Washing day: every guy-rope round the backyard is hung with tights, spangled bodices, a clown's white smock and a vast flowered apron, and the big top looks as if it had been dressed for a wedding by someone who had never been to one.".
  Observe yard_afternoon3 near cookfire when pitched(wapshotts) and at(cookfire, ?r) and hour(clock) >= 14 and hour(clock) < 18 and day(clock) >= arrivedDay(wapshotts) + 2 "Last day of the stand: the circus is already half-packed in its head. Crates are being nailed. The Colonel is walking round and round the wagons with a list, adding things to it.".
  Observe yard_evening near cookfire when pitched(wapshotts) and at(cookfire, ?r) and hour(clock) >= 18 and hour(clock) < 19 "The half-hour before the show: everyone in the backyard is in costume and in a temper. Somebody cannot find a shoe. Somebody else is being sick behind the canvas wagon, as they are every night, and then goes on and is wonderful.".
  Observe yard_night near cookfire when pitched(wapshotts) and at(cookfire, ?r) and hour(clock) >= 21 "After the show the backyard is lamplight and steam: performers in their shirts eating stew off their knees, telling each other what went wrong. Somebody has a fiddle. The Colonel is counting the takings aloud to Ada Thripp, who is counting them silently and getting a different number.".
  Observe yard_good_night near cookfire when pitched(wapshotts) and at(cookfire, ?r) and hour(clock) >= 21 and lastNightGood(wapshotts) "It was a good house tonight, and the whole backyard knows it: everybody is talking at once, the Quinceys' quarrel is forgotten for ten minutes, and the Colonel has given Bucephalus a whole loaf.".
  Observe ring_rehearsal near ringpost when rehearsal() and at(ringpost, ?r) "It is rehearsal. The Brothers Quincey are tumbling, one at each end of the ring, not looking at each other. Pip is holding a hoop for nobody. Up on the wire the Sylph is walking very slowly back and forth, back and forth, in a grey practice dress, like somebody pacing a landing at night.".
  Observe tober_front near pole when pitched(wapshotts) and at(pole, ?r) and hour(clock) >= 17 and hour(clock) < 19 "In front of the big top the band is playing the people in: a cornet, a drum and the serpent, which goes BUMP, BUMP under everything like a cow in a cellar. A crowd is gathering at the flap, and Ada Thripp, in the hatch of the ticket wagon, is taking their coins with a face like a tax.".

  // ── Colonel Florian Wapshott ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic wap_circus with wapshott "Ask the Colonel about his circus" when true once {
    Says "'The Grand Peregrine Circus and Hippodrama,' says the Colonel, 'founded by myself in a field, with one horse and a borrowed ladder, nineteen years ago this Lammas. We have played before the crowned heads of nowhere I can name for legal reasons, and the uncrowned heads of everywhere.' He spreads his arms to take in the big top, the wagons, a goose. 'Eleven wagons. Thirty souls. One horse of genius. We go round {town_a}, {town_b} and {town_c} like the hand of a clock, and the clock, my friend, is going to strike.' He lowers his voice to a mere bellow. 'Wapshott's is going to be a household word. I have not yet decided which word.'".
    On discuss { Increase regard(wapshott) by 1. }
  }
  Topic wap_colonel with wapshott "Ask the Colonel what he was a colonel of" when true once {
    Says "'The Ninth Volunteers,' says the Colonel, without hesitation. Then, with a little: 'Fusiliers.' Then: 'Of a sort.' He strokes his moustache. 'I bought the commission from a man in the Waggoner at Dunmere for a meat pie and my second-best hat. He was a colonel, there is no doubt of it. He had the paper. That he was a colonel of something that existed I will not swear to, but nor, my friend, will you swear that it didn't.' He beams. 'Never ask a showman for his papers. Ask him for his show.'".
  }
  Topic wap_ambition with wapshott "Ask the Colonel what he wants" when regard(wapshott) >= 1 once {
    Says "The Colonel is silent, which is so rare that a canvasman looks round. 'A roof,' he says at last. 'Not a canvas one. A building. An amphitheatre, with a ring of oak and a gallery and gas, in a city, with WAPSHOTT'S cut in stone over the door, where a horse could be stabled in winter and a clown could grow old in a chair by a stove. And a warrant. A Royal Warrant, framed, on the wall of the ticket office: BY APPOINTMENT.' He clears his throat enormously. 'And in the meantime, a menagerie. One must start somewhere. Madame Sallow has a menagerie. Madame Sallow has a camel. A camel!' He looks at you as if you had personally failed to provide one.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, wapshott_dreams). }
  }
  Entity wapshott_dreams: fact "Colonel Wapshott wants a building, a Royal Warrant, and in the meantime a menagerie, because his rival Madame Sallow has a camel.".
  Topic wap_sallow with wapshott "Ask the Colonel who Madame Sallow is" when knows(actor, wapshott_dreams) once {
    Says "'Cordelia Sallow,' says the Colonel, and for once in his life he says something quietly. 'We were partners, once. Wapshott and Sallow's Royal Circus. She had the head for figures and I had the head for everything else, and we were to be married at the Fair at Dunmere, in the lion's cage, for the publicity.' He looks at his boots. 'She went off with the lion, the elephant and the ledger, and started the Imperial Hippodrome, and has done very well, and I wish her every success, in a distant country, with damp.' He brightens with an effort. 'She has a camel. It is not a very good camel.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, sallow_known). }
  }
  Entity sallow_known: fact "Madame Cordelia Sallow, of Sallow's Imperial Hippodrome, was once the Colonel's partner and his betrothed; she left him at the altar, in a lion's cage, with the ledger.".
  Topic wap_money with wapshott "Ask the Colonel how the circus is doing for money" when true once {
    Says "'Splendidly,' says the Colonel. 'Brilliantly. The houses are full, the public is enraptured, and the money comes in like the tide.' A pause. 'And goes out like it. Ask Ada. No, don't ask Ada; she will show you the book, and the book is a pessimist.'".
  }
  Topic wap_honest with wapshott "Tell the Colonel that some of his bills are not true" when knows(actor, wapshott_dreams) once {
    Says "The Colonel looks genuinely hurt. 'Not true? My friend. A bill is not a sworn statement. A bill is a promise of wonder. If I put THE SYLPH OF THE WIRE, A LADY OF THE AIR FROM THE COURTS OF THE EAST, I promise you a lady of the air, and she is one, I have seen her up there, and as for the courts of the East, everybody comes from the east of somewhere.' He puts a hand on your shoulder. 'Nobody ever came out of Wapshott's feeling they had been cheated. Some of them came out feeling they had been magnificently cheated. That is a different thing. That is art.'".
  }

  // ── Ada Thripp ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic ada_book with ada "Ask Ada to show you how the books stand" when true {
    Says "Ada turns the ledger round so you can read it, and taps the bottom of the page with her pencil. 'In the strongbox: {strongbox(wapshotts)} coin. In the larder: {larder(wapshotts)} days' food for thirty people and a horse who eats for six. The canvas: {canvas(wapshotts)}, out of three, which is my own measure, and means Lusk is worried. Wages owed and unpaid: {arrears(wapshotts)} stands.' She closes it. 'Every three days we strike, and every strike the wages are due, ten coin for the company, and every day the larder wants three. The houses pay it, when they come. When they don't, the Colonel has an idea, and the ideas cost money.'".
  }
  Topic ada_how with ada "Ask Ada how you could help the circus pay its way" when true once {
    Says "Ada counts it off on inky fingers. 'Fill the benches: the bills, the parade, a town that likes us, a show that goes right. Keep the larder full, and buy it cheaper than the Colonel does, which is any price at all. Keep the canvas sound, or the rain comes in and the house goes home. Keep the wages paid, or Lusk's lads sit down. And if you can do anything at all, do it in the ring, because a new face in the ring is worth a cartload of bills.' She looks at you. 'Or sign the book and be a hand. Two coin a stand, when I've got it, and all the stew you can eat.'".
  }
  Topic ada_self with ada "Ask Ada how she came to keep the circus's books" when true once {
    Says "'The Colonel bought forty yards of rope from my father's chandlery in Marlow with an IOU,' says Ada. 'I came after it. I found him in this wagon eating sardines off a playbill with the ledger propping up the table, and I opened it, and I couldn't leave. It was like finding a beautiful house with no roof.' She sniffs. 'That was four years ago. I'm going to own a quarter-share in this circus by the time I'm thirty, and when I do, the first thing I'm going to do is take away his pen.'".
    On discuss { Increase regard(ada) by 1. }
  }
  Topic ada_secret with ada "Ask Ada what she is always writing in the back of the ledger" when regard(ada) >= 1 once {
    Says "Ada goes red to the bonnet. 'Accounts,' she says. You wait. 'Oh, very well.' She turns the ledger over and opens it from the back, where the pages are close-written in a different, wilder hand. 'THE BRIGAND'S BRIDE, OR, THE FATAL CONVENT. A Romance in Forty Parts, by A Lady of the Road. They print it in Dunmere at a penny a part and they've sold eleven hundred.' She shuts it. 'If you tell the Colonel I will put you in it, and something will happen to you in a crypt.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ada_writes). Increase regard(ada) by 1. }
  }
  Entity ada_writes: fact "Ada Thripp, who keeps Wapshott's books, secretly writes a penny romance, THE BRIGAND'S BRIDE, as A Lady of the Road.".
  Topic ada_pension with ada "Ask Ada why there is a coin a week written against Mrs Gale" when regard(ada) >= 2 once {
    Says "Ada is quiet a moment. 'Tom Gale's father was a flyer. He came off the bar at Wakeham six years ago and the Colonel has paid his widow a coin a week ever since, out of his own share, in a week when there is no share, and he made me promise not to put it in the book.' She looks at the line. 'I put it in the book. I put it in very small. He's a vain, idle, ridiculous man and he'd sell his own grandmother for a camel.' She dips her pen. 'And he's never once missed that coin.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, wapshott_pension). Increase regard(ada) by 1. }
  }
  Entity wapshott_pension: fact "Colonel Wapshott has paid the widow of a flyer killed in his ring a coin a week for six years, out of his own share, and told nobody.".

  // ── Mumchance ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic mum_silence with mumchance "Ask Mumchance why he never speaks in the ring" when true once {
    Says "'Because a laugh,' says Mumchance, 'is a thing the audience does, not a thing I do. If I talk, I tell them what is funny. If I don't, they have to find it themselves, and what you find yourself you keep.' He considers the white of his face in the mirror. 'Also when I was young I had a voice like a gate and they threw things.'".
    On discuss { Increase regard(mumchance) by 1. }
  }
  Topic mum_past with mumchance "Ask Mumchance where he learned to fall" when true once {
    Says "'My father was a fencing-master,' says Mumchance. 'Augustin Fell, of the Salle Fell in Dunmere. He meant me for the sword. He taught me the feint and the parry and the lunge, and where to put my feet, and I learned that the whole art of the sword is making the other fellow sure you are somewhere you are not.' He smiles, very slightly. 'Then I saw a clown fall down a flight of stairs at the Midsummer Fair, all twelve, and get up, and look at the stairs as if they had insulted his mother. And I thought: that is the same art. That is the same art done better. I ran off with the circus the next morning. My father never forgave me, and he came to see me every year, at the back, where he thought I couldn't see.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, gentle_art_heard). Increase regard(mumchance) by 1. }
  }
  Entity gentle_art_heard: fact "Mumchance, the old clown, was a fencing-master's son: he holds that clowning and fencing are the same art, making the other fellow sure you are somewhere you are not.".
  Topic mum_pip with mumchance "Ask Mumchance about Pip" when true once {
    Says "'Pip,' says Mumchance, and something in the white face moves. 'She falls well. She has learned the fall. She has not learned the get-up, which is the hard part, and the funny part.' He looks across at the ring, where Pip is falling off a barrel on purpose. 'She wants to be famous. That's all right. I wanted to be famous. Then I wanted to be good. Then I wanted to be kind, and that's when I got funny.' He blots his lip. 'She'll go, one day. Somebody ought to take her and show her the world. Somebody who'll bring her back.'".
  }
  Topic mum_knees with mumchance "Ask Mumchance how he does, at his age, in the ring" when true once {
    Says "Mumchance rubs his knee. 'The knees,' he says, 'are seventy. The rest of me is forty, and the face is nine.' He is quiet. 'The Colonel has been looking at clowns. Young ones, at other circuses. He thinks I don't know. He put my name smaller on the bills this year: MUMCHANCE THE SILENT, under THE BROTHERS QUINCEY, in the size of type they use for the price of children.' He goes back to his mirror. 'Honoria makes me a liniment. It smells of a horse's funeral. It works, if somebody will buy the camphor.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, knees_known). }
  }
  Entity knees_known: fact "Mumchance's knees are bad; Honoria Bulstrode makes him a liniment, if somebody will buy the camphor for it.".

  // ── Pip Gallant ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic pip_dream with pip "Ask Pip what kind of clown she means to be" when true once {
    Says "'A loud one,' says Pip at once. 'A loud, big, enormous one, with a trick bicycle and a goose. Mumchance says the silence is the thing, and I believe him, I do, only I can't do it. I open my mouth and things come out of it.' She juggles three oranges, drops two and catches the third on her nose. 'He says I'll find my own way. I'd like to find it somewhere else than {town_c}, that's all. I've been to {town_c} eleven times and the cross has never once done anything.'".
    On discuss { Increase regard(pip) by 1. }
  }
  Topic pip_quinceys with pip "Ask Pip why the Brothers Quincey are not speaking" when true once {
    Says "'The Quincey Turn,' says Pip, rolling her eyes so hard she nearly falls over. 'Their famous somersault: two of you, back to back, over each other, at the same time, like a wheel. They both say they invented it. Hal says he dreamed it, Dunstan says he worked it out on paper. They've not said a word to each other for three weeks, they send messages through me, and now their pyramid falls down every night. Hal says tell Dunstan his left foot's late. Dunstan says tell Hal his left foot can go to the devil.' She sighs. 'I'm a ring-girl, not a post office.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, feud_known). }
  }
  Entity feud_known: fact "The Brothers Quincey have not spoken for three weeks: each claims to have invented the Quincey Turn, and their act falls apart nightly.".
  Topic mum_pip_go with mumchance "Ask Mumchance whether Pip might come with you for a while, and see the world" when fallLearned(actor) and regard(pip) >= 2 and not willing(pip, actor) and not travelsWith(pip, actor) once {
    Says "Mumchance does not answer at once. He finishes the line of his eyebrow, and looks at it, and wipes it off, and does it again. 'I said somebody ought to take her,' he says. 'Somebody who'd bring her back.' He puts the brush down. 'She can fall. She can't get up yet. The world's where you learn to get up.' He turns on his bucket and looks at you, the whole white face. 'Bring her back funnier. And bring her back.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(pip, actor). Set hire(pip) to 0. }
  }
  Topic pip_road with pip travelling "Ask Pip what she makes of the road" when travelsWith(pip, actor) {
    Says "'It's bigger than I thought,' says Pip. 'It just keeps going. In the circus the world's always forty-two feet across.' She practises a fall off a stile, lands, and gets up thinking. 'Mumchance said the get-up's the funny part. I think I see. You fall, and the world waits to see what you'll do about it, and what you do about it is the joke.'".
  }

  // ── Zéphyrine ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic zeph_wire with zephyrine "Ask Zéphyrine what it is like on the wire" when knows(actor, zephyrine_named) once {
    Says "'Quiet,' says Zéphyrine. 'Everything below is noise and smell and people eating oranges, and up there is a line as wide as your finger and nothing else in the world. One does not walk the wire. One agrees with it.' She tightens the linen round her ankle. 'I am going to walk across a river one day, from a steeple to a field, with all the town underneath with their mouths open. The Ascension, they will call it. I have the rope ordered. I do not have the steeple.'".
    On discuss { Increase regard(zephyrine) by 1. Assert knows(actor, ascension_known). }
  }
  Entity ascension_known: fact "Zéphyrine dreams of the Ascension: a wire from a steeple to a field, over the heads of a whole town.".
  Topic zeph_where with zephyrine "Ask Zéphyrine where she comes from" when knows(actor, zephyrine_named) once {
    Says "'From the East,' says Zéphyrine. A pause. 'From a long way east.' Another pause. 'The east of somewhere.' She looks away from you, toward the road, and her accent for a moment goes somewhere else entirely, somewhere with tripe in it. 'Excuse me. I must warm up.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, zeph_evasive). }
  }
  Entity zeph_evasive: fact "Zéphyrine will not say where she comes from, and when she is pressed her accent slips toward somewhere much nearer than the East.".

  // ── The Brothers Quincey ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic hal_turn with hal "Ask Hal about the Quincey Turn" when true once {
    Says "'I dreamed it,' says Hal. 'Eleven years old, in the loft of the Waggoner at Dunmere: two of us, back to back, over and over, like the spokes of a wheel. I woke up and I knew how. I showed him in the morning, and he got out a slate and drew a picture of it, and now he says the picture came first.' He does a furious back-flip. 'You can't draw a somersault. You can't draw a dream. Tell him that. No, don't tell him that. Don't tell him anything. I'm not speaking to him.'".
  }
  Topic dun_turn with dunstan "Ask Dunstan about the Quincey Turn" when true once {
    Says "'I worked it out,' says Dunstan. 'On the slate, in the loft of the Waggoner at Dunmere. Angles. Where the weight goes, where the hands go, which foot leaves first. You can't dream a thing like that, you'd break your neck. He'd been dreaming about it, that's true; he'd been dreaming about it for a year and falling on his head.' He stretches. 'Our father used to say we'd fight over the last breath in the room. He'd know what to do. He'd bang our heads together.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, father_quincey). }
  }
  Entity father_quincey: fact "The Brothers Quincey's late father would have known how to settle their quarrel over the Quincey Turn.".

  // ── Honoria Bulstrode ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic hon_strength with honoria "Ask Honoria how she came to be the Ox of Abernant" when true once {
    Says "'Abernant's a quarry town,' says Honoria. 'My father cut slate. When I was fourteen the slate-cart went over on the quarry road with my brother under it, and I lifted it. That's all. I didn't know I could till I did.' She stirs the pot. 'The Colonel heard about it in a tavern and came to Abernant with a contract and a bunch of violets. I lift Bucephalus now, every night, on a platform, and he hates it, and he lets me, because I give him the end of the bread.'".
    On discuss { Increase regard(honoria) by 1. }
  }
  Topic hon_teashop with honoria "Ask Honoria what she is saving for" when regard(honoria) >= 1 once {
    Says "Honoria lifts the lid of a tea-caddy on the shelf of the cookhouse wagon and shows you, very shyly, the coins in it. 'A tea-shop,' she says. 'With a bow window, and a bell on the door, and little cakes in rows. Somewhere I never have to lift anything heavier than a pot.' She puts the lid back. 'Another eight years, at this rate. Mumchance says he'll come and sit in the window and frighten off the customers.' She goes pink. 'He's an old fool. We were nearly married once, you know. In Wakeham. Then the bridge washed out, and the circus went round by Marlow, and somehow we never got back to it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, honoria_mumchance). }
  }
  Entity honoria_mumchance: fact "Honoria Bulstrode and Mumchance were nearly married once, at Wakeham, and somehow never got back to it.".
  // What the larder wants is learned of her, before anyone talks a merchant down for it (the owner, 3 November: the
  // circus's bill was haggled before anything was known of it).
  Entity larder_known: fact "Honoria Bulstrode keeps Wapshott's larder, and pays whatever price the Colonel agreed to: somebody could talk the merchants down for her.".
  Topic hon_larder with honoria "Ask Honoria how the larder stands" when true {
    Says "'{larder(wapshotts)} days,' says Honoria, 'if nobody has seconds, and everybody has seconds.' She tips her head at the town. 'I buy what I can off {merchant_a} and the rest, at whatever price the Colonel has agreed to, which is always the first one they say. If somebody could talk them down, I'd cook them a pie in the shape of their own head.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, larder_known). }
  }

  // ── Signor Fipps ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic fipps_overture with fipps "Ask Fipps what he is writing on the backs of the playbills" when true once {
    Says "'The Grand Circus Overture,' says Fipps reverently, 'in four movements, for a band of twenty. The Entry of the Horses. The Ascent. The Fall of the Clown. The Apotheosis.' He sighs. 'We are a band of three. I have arranged it for three. The Apotheosis is mostly drum.' He polishes the serpent. 'And she won't play the low G, which is the note the whole Apotheosis turns on. A new serpent, from a proper maker, is twenty coin. I have asked the Colonel for a serpent eleven times.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, fipps_serpent). }
  }
  Entity fipps_serpent: fact "Signor Fipps, the bandmaster, needs a new serpent, a bass horn, because his old one will not play the low G; he has asked the Colonel for one eleven times.".

  // ── Lucius Hench ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic hench_court with hench "Ask Hench about his years with the Margravine" when true once {
    Says "'Eleven years,' says Hench, threading a needle without looking at it. 'Her Grace of Oster. I dressed her for two weddings, three funerals, a christening and a war. I know the order of precedence of every coronet from here to the sea, how to bow to a margrave, an archduke and a dowager who is all three, and which fork.' He bites the thread. 'Then she married a man who liked his own valet, and I went for a walk, and the walk ended here. I now dress a horse.' A pause. 'He has better posture than the Margrave.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, hench_court). }
  }
  Topic hench_progress with hench "Ask Hench whether the old courts ever went travelling" when knows(actor, hench_court) once {
    Says "'The old kings did nothing else,' says Hench. 'The Household of the Progress: the whole court on the roads from spring to Michaelmas, two hundred wagons, a chapel on wheels, the Treasury in an iron cart, and the Menagerie Royal behind it all in cages, so that the country could see what the king owned. A crowned wheel on every wagon.' He bites a thread. 'They went round, my dear, exactly as we go round, only with archbishops instead of Quinceys. The last Progress was three hundred years ago. The Household still exists, on paper, in a house near the sea, with a Steward and no wagons.' He smooths the bodice on his knee. 'I have sometimes thought the Colonel was born three hundred years too late, and on the wrong side of the wheel.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, progress_known). }
  }
  Entity progress_known: fact "The old kings' Household of the Progress went round the country with two hundred wagons and the Menagerie Royal, under a crowned wheel; it still exists, on paper, with a Steward and no wagons.".
  Entity hench_court: fact "Lucius Hench, Wapshott's wardrobe-master, was eleven years valet to the Margravine of Oster, and knows the forms of every court.".
  Topic hench_owed with hench "Ask Hench how the wardrobe does" when true once {
    Says "'Spangles,' says Hench, 'are the curse of my life. They come off in the ring, and the ring eats them, and I sew them back, and the Colonel does not pay for the gold braid, which I bought in {town_a} on my own account last spring and have not been paid for since.' He holds up a tumbler's jersey with a rent in it from collar to hip. 'One of the Quinceys. They tear each other's costumes now, on the turn, out of spite, and pretend it is the other's fault, and I am to make them whole by seven.'".
  }

  Topic mum_slee with mumchance "Ask Mumchance what he makes of Varney Slee" when knows(actor, slee_named) once {
    Says "'He makes things easy,' says Mumchance. 'He told me so. He told Hal he could make the Turn easy for him, at the Hippodrome, with a net.' He is quiet. 'Everything worth doing in this tent is hard. The fall's easy. Anybody falls. The get-up's hard. A man who makes things easy is a man who has never got up.' He looks at his knee. 'Mind, I've known some very nice men with nets.'".
  }

  // ── Gideon Lusk ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic lusk_canvas with lusk "Ask Lusk how the canvas is" when true {
    Says "Lusk looks up at the big top for a long time. 'Old,' he says. Then: 'Rotten at the seams, two places.' Then, because you are still there: '{canvas(wapshotts)} of three. Every strike takes it down a bit. Rain on a bad seam, and the house gets wet, and a wet house goes home.' He picks up a palm and needle as big as a dagger. 'Somebody who can mend could help. Somebody who'd sit up here with me an hour.'".
  }
  Topic lusk_lads with lusk "Ask Lusk about his canvasmen" when true once {
    Says "'Eight lads,' says Lusk. 'Good lads.' A long silence. 'Owed.' He drives a stake in with one blow. 'Ten coin a stand, for all of us, at the strike. If it's not paid, they'll put the big top up, because they're good lads. If it's not paid twice, they won't, because they're not fools.'".
  }
  Topic lusk_nell with lusk "Ask Lusk whether he has family" when regard(lusk) >= 1 once {
    Says "Lusk stops working, which you have not seen him do. 'Nell,' he says. 'Eight. Lives with her gran in {town_b}.' He takes a folded paper out of his shirt: a child's drawing of a very large man and a very small tent. 'I see her three days every round. She wants to come with the wagons. Her gran says no circus. Her gran's right.' He folds it up again, carefully, along the same old creases. 'Her gran's always right. It's a terrible thing in a woman.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, nell_known). }
  }
  Entity nell_known: fact "Gideon Lusk's daughter Nell, eight, lives with her grandmother in {town_b} and longs to go with the wagons; her grandmother says no circus.".

  // ── Nance Tibbet ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic nance_fortune with nance "Ask Nance to tell your fortune, for a coin" when quantity(actor, gold) >= 1 and not toldFortune(actor) once {
    Says "Nance takes your coin, and your hand, and does not look at the hand at all; she looks at your face, the way a horse-coper looks at teeth. 'You'll go a long way,' she says, 'and most of it on foot. You'll meet a tall man who talks too much, and a quiet one who doesn't talk enough, and you'll have to choose which to believe, and you'll be wrong, and it'll come out right.' She lets go. 'That's the fortune. Here's the free part: the brothers in tights want their heads knocked together, the girl on the wire wants her mother, and the Colonel wants a camel. Everybody in this circus wants something, dearie, except the horse. The horse has everything.'".
    On discuss { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 1. Increase quantity(nance, gold) by 1. Assert toldFortune(actor). }
  }
  Relation toldFortune(group).
  Topic nance_zeph with nance "Ask Nance what she meant about the girl on the wire" when toldFortune(actor) once {
    Says "Nance puffs her pipe. 'Susan Pruett,' she says. 'Don't look like that, I've known since the first night; she sat on my steps and cried and I held her hand and the hand told me nothing and the crying told me everything. Ran away from {town_c} at fifteen with a rope over her shoulder and her mother's tripe-knife, to be something nobody in {town_c} had ever seen. She's never once been home. Every time we come round to {town_c} she has a headache.' She taps out the pipe. 'Her mother's still there. Dresses tripe in the lane behind the green. Never says a word about a daughter. Never misses a night of the circus, either. Sits at the back.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, susan_pruett). }
  }
  Entity susan_pruett: fact "The Sylph of the Wire is really Susan Pruett of {town_c}, who ran away at fifteen; her mother, a tripe-dresser in {town_c}, still lives there and comes to every show, at the back.".
  Topic nance_trouble with nance "Ask Nance what she sees coming for the circus" when metCircus(actor) once {
    Says "'Money,' says Nance, 'which is what I always see coming, and it never does.' Then she looks at you properly. 'There's a woman who owns the Colonel's debts. Not yet. She will. I've seen her man about the place in a grey hat asking what the canvas is worth. You don't ask what a thing is worth unless you mean to own it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, grey_hat). }
  }
  Entity grey_hat: fact "A man in a grey hat has been about Wapshott's, asking what its canvas is worth.".

  // ── Billie Ostrander and Bucephalus ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic billie_horse with billie "Ask Billie about Bucephalus" when true once {
    Says "'Twenty-six,' says Billie. 'Bought from a knacker's yard at nine for the price of his hide, and he has never forgiven anybody. He knows every cue in the show. He knows them better than the Colonel. If the band plays wrong, he stops dead in the ring and looks at Fipps until Fipps plays right.' She runs a hand down his neck. 'He's the only one in this circus that's never been paid and never once complained. That's breeding.'".
  }
  Topic billie_beasts with billie "Ask Billie what she thinks of the Colonel's menagerie" when knows(actor, wapshott_dreams) once {
    Says "Billie's jaw sets. 'I think,' she says, 'that a beast in a box is a sad thing and a beast in a dirty box is a wicked one, and that the Colonel has never in his life cleaned out a box.' She goes on grooming. 'If he does it, I'll keep them. Somebody has to. They'll be kept right, or I'll go. And anything that talks back,' she says, 'talks to me first.'".
    On discuss { Increase regard(billie) by 1. }
  }
  Action pat_bucephalus(actor: group, site: place) "Offer Bucephalus the heel of a loaf" {
    Time 0.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(bucephalus, site) and not patted(bucephalus).
    On success { Assert patted(bucephalus). Increase regard(billie) by 1. }
    Result "Bucephalus considers the bread for a long time, as if it were a petition. Then he takes it, with lips like a velvet purse, and lets you stand beside him while he eats it, which Billie says afterwards is more than he lets the Colonel do.".
  }
  Relation patted(group).

  // ── Sidney Quirk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Topic quirk_bills with quirk "Ask Quirk about his bills" when true once {
    Says "'A bill,' says Quirk, pasting as he talks, 'is the circus before the circus. People see it on Tuesday and they've been to the show in their heads by Thursday, and on Friday they come to see if it's as good as the one they had.' He slaps one onto a gatepost. 'Every bill I put up's a coin at the flap. Every one somebody tears down is a coin I'll never see.' He lowers his voice. 'Somebody's been tearing them down. Ahead of me, behind me. Pasting over them with gold and blue.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bills_torn). }
  }
  Entity bills_torn: fact "Somebody has been pasting over Wapshott's bills with Sallow's Imperial Hippodrome's, gold and blue.".

  // Talk among them, as the company stands by: what one says of another.
  Rule overheard_hench near hench when at(party, ?r) and at(hench, ?r) and at(hal, ?r) and not overheardHench(party)
    says "'Your knee's out again,' Hench says to Hal Quincey, without looking up from his needle. 'Not your knee, your costume. Though now I look, your knee as well.'" { Assert overheardHench(party). }
  Relation overheardHench(group).
  Rule overheard_cook near honoria when at(party, ?r) and at(honoria, ?r) and at(mumchance, ?r) and not overheardCook(party)
    says "'You've not eaten,' Honoria says to Mumchance. 'I've eaten,' says Mumchance. 'You've not eaten properly,' says Honoria, and gives him a bowl, and he eats it, and neither of them says anything else, and it is the most married thing you have ever seen." { Assert overheardCook(party). }
  Relation overheardCook(group).
  Rule overheard_ada near ada when at(party, ?r) and at(ada, ?r) and at(wapshott, ?r) and not overheardAda(party)
    says "'Ada,' says the Colonel, 'I have had an idea.' 'No,' says Ada. 'You haven't heard it.' 'I don't need to hear it, I can see its shadow.'" { Assert overheardAda(party). }
  Relation overheardAda(group).
}

data/goings-on/circus/voyage.kyr:
Module circus "Wapshott's Peregrine Circus" {
  // ── Act IV.iii: the Sundial ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Eleven days each way, the longest the circus has ever been off its wagons. A brig of ninety tons with a dead
  // captain's name still on her papers; a mate made master by a fever; a crew who think the voyage is mad and are
  // paid enough not to say so; a naturalist with a contract; a showman who cannot be seen to be afraid. The days are
  // told in three scenes: the clauses read aloud, the storm, the calm.
  Place sundial "The brig Sundial" is region.
  Place ship "the brig Sundial" is wilderness within sundial at 0, 0.
  Place deck "the Sundial's deck" is room within ship at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place hold "the Sundial's hold" is room within ship at 1, 0.
  Place great_cabin "the great cabin" is room within ship at 2, 0.
  Relation berthA(concern). Relation berthS(concern). Relation atSea(concern). Relation outward(concern). Relation homeward(concern).
  Relation stormOn(concern). Relation stormDone(concern). Relation calmDone(concern). Relation lashed(group). Relation clausesRead(concern).
  Relation colonelCovered(concern). Relation colonelNamedFear(concern). Relation vanceKnown(concern). Relation billieSat(concern).
  Measure sailDay(concern). Measure stormAt(concern).

  Rule berth_set when voyageReady(wapshotts) and not berthA(wapshotts) and not berthS(wapshotts) and not atSea(wapshotts) and not voyaged(wapshotts) { Assert berthA(wapshotts). }
  Passage gangway_a "the Sundial's gangway" is passage between green_a and deck
    opening when berthA(wapshotts) "The gangway is drawn in.".
  Passage gangway_s "the gangway to the Progress's quay" is passage between deck and landing
    opening when berthS(wapshotts) "The gangway is drawn in.".

  Observe deck_scene at deck when true "The Sundial is a brig of ninety tons, tarred, patched and spotless, with SUNDIAL cut over her taffrail and under it the name of a captain who is dead. Her crew of nine go about their work in a silence that is not hostile. The mate, who is her master now, keeps one hand on the rail as if it were someone's shoulder.".
  Observe hold_scene at hold when true "The hold smells of tar and bilge and the biscuit of a long voyage. Cages are stowed along both sides, empty, with fresh straw, built to Billie's measure in the fair town in a week; at the after end, lashed down, a big case of lamp-black and spirit that Sir Gervase calls his apparatus.".
  Observe great_cabin_scene at great_cabin when true "A low cabin lit by a stern window, with a table nailed to the floor, a chart of the Southern Sea pinned over it, and a litter of Sir Gervase's papers weighted with a beetle in a box. The chart stops, at its bottom edge, in a drawn hand that points off the paper.".
  Passage deck_hold "the hatch to the hold" is passage between deck and hold.
  Passage deck_cabin "the cabin door" is door between deck and great_cabin.

  Rule aboard at deck when at(party, deck) and voyageReady(wapshotts) and not voyaged(wapshotts) and wapshottAboard(wapshotts)
    says "The gangway comes in with a thump. The Colonel stands on the deck of the Sundial in his best coat with his hat held in front of him like a plate, and Ada Thripp, on the quay, with her pen behind her ear, lifts one hand and lets it drop. The mate says, to nobody, 'Mind your heads in the hatch.' You are, for the first time since the Fair, not on the circus's ground. Nobody has told the wagons." {
    Assert voyaged(wapshotts). Assert away(wapshott). Assert at(wapshott, deck). Assert following(wapshott, party).
    Assert away(fenwick). Assert at(fenwick, deck). Assert following(fenwick, party). Assert away(crewe). Assert at(crewe, deck).

    Increase quantity(party, rations) by 12. }
  Rule aboard_billie when at(party, deck) and voyaged(wapshotts) and billieAboard(wapshotts) and not away(billie) { Assert away(billie). Assert at(billie, deck). Assert following(billie, party). }
  Rule aboard_mumchance when at(party, deck) and voyaged(wapshotts) and mumchanceAboard(wapshotts) and not away(mumchance) { Assert away(mumchance). Assert at(mumchance, deck). Assert following(mumchance, party). }
  Rule circus_lies_up when voyaged(wapshotts) and not backFromSarn(wapshotts) and moveDay(wapshotts) < day(clock) + 2 { Set moveDay(wapshotts) to day(clock) + 3. }

  Action cast_off_out(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Mate Crewe to cast off for Sarn on the morning ebb" {
    Speaker crewe.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, deck) and voyaged(wapshotts) and berthA(wapshotts) and not homeward(wapshotts) and not outward(wapshotts).
    Time 0.
    On success { Retract berthA(wapshotts). Assert atSea(wapshotts). Assert outward(wapshotts). Set sailDay(wapshotts) to day(clock). }
    Result "'Let go for'ard,' says Crewe, in a voice you have not heard from him, and the quay slides away: Ada, the heap of rope, the gull, the fair town's roofs with the Hippodrome's flag at the far end of them, going down one by one behind the Sundial's wake. The Colonel does not wave. He stands with his hat on and his chin up, like a man going on in the ring.".
  }
  Rule landfall_out when atSea(wapshotts) and outward(wapshotts) and day(clock) >= sailDay(wapshotts) + 11 and hour(clock) >= 6 {
    Retract atSea(wapshotts). Assert berthS(wapshotts). }
  Rule landfall_home when atSea(wapshotts) and homeward(wapshotts) and day(clock) >= sailDay(wapshotts) + 11 and hour(clock) >= 6 {
    Retract atSea(wapshotts). Assert berthA(wapshotts). }
  Observe at_sea_out at deck when atSea(wapshotts) and outward(wapshotts) and not stormDone(wapshotts) "Nothing but water in every direction. The log says eleven days. The wind says it will do as it likes.".
  Observe at_sea_after at deck when atSea(wapshotts) and outward(wapshotts) and stormDone(wapshotts) "The sea has gone the colour of slate, and the sky has been wrung out. Somewhere under the keel the bottom falls away to a depth that has no number.".
  Observe land_out at deck when berthS(wapshotts) "Land at last, a green line on the south horizon that does not move like a cloud. The smell comes out to meet you before the sight: wet earth, eggs, rot, hot stone, and the sweetness of an enormous number of flowers. A quay of cut stone stands at the mouth of a bay, with a post on it, and a wheel on the post.".
  Observe land_home at deck when berthA(wapshotts) and homeward(wapshotts) "The fair town's roofs, and the flag of the Hippodrome, and on the quay a heap of rope and a gull. Ada is not there. Ada, you will learn, has not left the ticket wagon in eleven days.".

  // The contract, as the cabin has it.
  Topic fenwick_clauses with fenwick "Ask Sir Gervase what he has signed the Colonel to" when atSea(wapshotts) and outward(wapshotts) and not clausesRead(wapshotts) once {
    Says "'A pair of everything,' says Sir Gervase, 'living where possible, in spirits where not, and the Colonel's name on the title page, in capitals.' He pats the beetle-box. 'He asked for the capitals.'".
    On discuss { Assert clausesRead(wapshotts). Assert clauseBeasts(wapshotts). }
  }

  // The storm: the Colonel's hands on the rail.
  Rule storm_comes when atSea(wapshotts) and outward(wapshotts) and day(clock) >= sailDay(wapshotts) + 4 and hour(clock) >= 18 and not stormDone(wapshotts) and not stormOn(wapshotts) {
    Assert stormOn(wapshotts). Set stormAt(wapshotts) to watch(clock). }
  Observe storm_scene at deck when stormOn(wapshotts) "The sky to windward has come down to the sea. Crewe is on the quarterdeck with a speaking-trumpet: 'BELOW, OR LASH! BELOW, OR LASH!' The Sundial lies over until her yards are in the water. Rain like thrown gravel. In the dark, at the lee rail, the Colonel is singing the Galop from the Grand Entry at the top of his voice, with both hands clamped white on the wood.".
  Action lash_down(actor: group, site: place) "Lash yourselves to the main-mast with a rope" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, deck) and stormOn(wapshotts) and holding(actor, rope) and not lashed(party).
    Time 0.
    On success { Assert lashed(party). }
    Result "You pass the line round the mast and round each other, and the sea comes over the rail.".
  }
  Item hold_rope "a coil of the Sundial's lashing" is rope at hold.
  Item hold_rope_b "a second coil of lashing" is rope at hold.
  Item hold_oil "a flask of the Sundial's lamp oil" is lamp_oil at hold.
  Item hold_oil_b "a second flask of lamp oil" is lamp_oil at hold.
  Action go_below(actor: group, site: place) "Go below and wedge yourselves among the cages" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, deck) and stormOn(wapshotts) and not lashed(party).
    Time 0.
    On success { Assert lashed(party). }
    Result "The hatch slams over the storm. In the hold the cages bang like a bell-foundry, and Mr Mudge sings the whole time, and is quite wrong about the words.".
  }
  Hazard storm_wave "A sea over the rail" means "Deal (1d8) physical damage to ally unless strength save against (12).".
  Rule storm_breaks when stormOn(wapshotts) and watch(clock) >= stormAt(wapshotts) + 6 {
    Retract stormOn(wapshotts). Assert stormDone(wapshotts). Retract lashed(party). }
  Rule storm_strikes at deck when stormOn(wapshotts) and watch(clock) >= stormAt(wapshotts) + 3 and at(party, deck) and not lashed(party) and not stormHit(party)
    says "A green sea comes aboard abeam and takes the deck from end to end." { Assert strikes(storm_wave, party). Assert stormHit(party). }
  Relation stormHit(group).
  Rule storm_clear when stormDone(wapshotts) and stormHit(party) { Retract stormHit(party). }
  Topic wap_fear_cover with wapshott "Say nothing of his hands on the rail, and sing the second verse with him" when stormDone(wapshotts) and not colonelCovered(wapshotts) and not colonelNamedFear(wapshotts) once {
    Says "You pick up the Galop at the second verse, flat, and the Colonel looks at you with a face of such naked gratitude that you have to look at the sea. He does not say one word of the storm. He tells Crewe, loudly and at length, that it was a capital blow, and that in the Peninsula he had seen worse. He has never been to the Peninsula.".
    On discuss { Assert colonelCovered(wapshotts). }
  }
  Topic wap_fear_name with wapshott "Tell the Colonel you saw his hands on the rail, and that it was well done to sing" when stormDone(wapshotts) and not colonelCovered(wapshotts) and not colonelNamedFear(wapshotts) once {
    Says "The Colonel goes still. Then he puts his hat on, straight, and says, 'I was extremely frightened.' It is the first thing you have heard him say in an ordinary voice. 'I have been frightened every night of my life,' he says, 'and it has not once been the right night.' He looks at his hands. 'Do not tell Ada.' He does not speak to you again for a day, and the next morning he brings you tea himself, in the wrong cup, and spills it.".
    On discuss { Assert colonelNamedFear(wapshotts). Increase regard(billie) by 1. }
  }

  // The calm, and the dead captain.
  Rule calm_comes when atSea(wapshotts) and outward(wapshotts) and day(clock) >= sailDay(wapshotts) + 7 and hour(clock) >= 10 and not calmDone(wapshotts) { Assert calmDone(wapshotts). }
  Observe calm_scene at deck when calmDone(wapshotts) and atSea(wapshotts) and outward(wapshotts) "The wind has simply stopped. The sea is a sheet of hot lead; the sails hang like washing. The crew lie in the shade of the boat with their hats over their faces. A turtle, enormous, rides past on the surface with an air of having been invited.".
  Topic crewe_vance with crewe "Ask Mate Crewe about Captain Vance" when calmDone(wapshotts) and atSea(wapshotts) and not vanceKnown(wapshotts) once {
    Says "'Born on Sarn,' says Crewe, after a time. 'His line held the Preserve's key since the Wardens, and the eldest son was put to sea at nine with it round his neck and told to keep it. That was Vance. He kept it forty years. He never went back, because there was nothing to go back to but a rule and a lot of animals. He read your letter at Port Dree. He said, a Keeper, and sat down on a bollard.' Crewe turns his hat. 'He took the last clutch off the beds himself. He said the Keeper had asked, and somebody ought to answer.' He puts the hat on. 'He has the key, the Captain. It's in the cabin. It opens a door that isn't there any more.'".
    On discuss { Assert vanceKnown(wapshotts). Give preserve_key to actor. }
  }
  Kind preserve_key "the Preserve's key" is gear worth 0 weighing 1 described "A bronze key as long as a hand with a crowned wheel for a bow, worn smooth by a boy's chest and a man's. It is the key of the Preserve-house door.".
  Topic billie_rail with billie "Sit with Billie at the rail in the calm" when calmDone(wapshotts) and atSea(wapshotts) and billieAboard(wapshotts) and not billieSat(wapshotts) once {
    Says "'I kept a lion once,' says Billie, to the water. 'At Dunmere. His name was Nebuchadnezzar and I was nineteen, and I used to sit with him in the cage because it was warm. He was blind by then.' She says nothing for some time. 'Every cage I ever kept, I knew the day it would be the last. This is the first time I have gone to a place to see what the cages were for.' She turns her cup. 'I'll tell you what I'm afraid of. That it'll be better than the Colonel's tent, and he'll never forgive it.'".
    On discuss { Assert billieSat(wapshotts). Increase regard(billie) by 1. }
  }

  // Homeward: what was put in the hold.
  Observe hold_specimens at hold when homeward(wapshotts) and takeSpecimens(wapshotts) "The cages along both sides of the hold are full, and nobody has said so. A pair of fern-runners sit pressed together in one, as like two people on a coach as animals can be. The hook-claw's cage is the quiet one.".
  Observe hold_egg at hold when homeward(wapshotts) and takeEgg(wapshotts) "In a basket by the galley stove, wrapped in the Colonel's best coat and a damp cloth, a grey loaf-big egg. Somebody turns it every hour on the hour. It is, for the whole of the crew, a ship's pet.".
  Observe hold_empty at hold when homeward(wapshotts) and takeLeave(wapshotts) "The cages along both sides of the hold are empty, with the straw as fresh as it was. The Colonel, who is sitting among them with his back against a bar, says it is the best hold he has ever been in.".

  Rule hatchlings_aboard when voyaged(wapshotts) and not backFromSarn(wapshotts) and hatchlingsPenned(wapshotts) and not hatchlingsHome(party) and at(hatchlings, ?r) and distinct(?r, hold) {
    Retract travels(hatchlings). Retract post(hatchlings, rk_beasts). Retract at(hatchlings, ?r). Assert at(hatchlings, hold). }
  Rule crew_aboard_home when homeward(wapshotts) and not dead(mudge) and away(mudge) { Retract away(mudge). Assert at(mudge, deck). }
  Rule cook_aboard_home when homeward(wapshotts) and away(nunn) { Retract away(nunn). Assert at(nunn, deck). }
  Rule hull_leaks when homeward(wapshotts) and atSea(wapshotts) and hullHoled(wapshotts) and hour(clock) == 6 and bailedDay(wapshotts) < day(clock) { Set bailedDay(wapshotts) to day(clock). Decrease quantity(party, rations) by 2 or to nothing. Decrease waterCasks(wapshotts) by 1 or to nothing. }
  Measure bailedDay(concern).
  Observe hull_water at hold when homeward(wapshotts) and hullHoled(wapshotts) "Water slops over the hold floor at every roll, and Mr Mudge is bailing with a cage-bucket, singing.".
  Topic nunn_home with nunn "Ask Aggie what was in the stew" when homeward(wapshotts) and atSea(wapshotts) once {
    Says "'Mr Mudge,' says Aggie, and stirs. 'Mostly.'".
  }
  Rule hatchlings_back when backFromSarn(wapshotts) and hatchlingsPenned(wapshotts) and not hatchlingsHome(party) and not youngAshore(party) and at(hatchlings, hold) { Retract at(hatchlings, hold). Assert travels(hatchlings). Assert post(hatchlings, rk_beasts). }
  Action carry_young_ashore(actor: group, site: place) "Take the young hook-claws ashore in a sack" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hold) and at(hatchlings, hold) and hatchlingsPenned(wapshotts) and not youngAshore(party) and not backFromSarn(wapshotts).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert youngAshore(party). Retract at(hatchlings, hold). }
    Result "They go into the sack in a heap and a good deal of complaint. It is a sack that breathes.".
  }
  Relation youngAshore(group).
  Rule home_from_sarn at green_a when voyaged(wapshotts) and homeward(wapshotts) and not backFromSarn(wapshotts) and not atSea(wapshotts) and at(party, green_a) {
    Assert backFromSarn(wapshotts). Retract away(wapshott). Retract away(fenwick). Retract away(billie). Retract away(mumchance). Retract away(crewe). Retract away(mudge). Retract away(nunn).
    Retract following(wapshott, party). Retract following(fenwick, party). Retract following(billie, party). Retract following(mumchance, party).
    Set moveDay(wapshotts) to day(clock) + 1. }
  Chapter ch_voyage "The Sundial" when within(party, sundial) "Eleven days out, with a naturalist, a showman and a dead man's crew. The wagons are a long way behind.".
  Milestone m_clauses "had the contract read at sea" worth 100 when clausesRead(wapshotts).
  Milestone m_storm "rode out the storm with the Colonel" worth 150 when colonelCovered(wapshotts) or colonelNamedFear(wapshotts).
  Milestone m_vance "learned who Captain Vance was" worth 200 when vanceKnown(wapshotts).
}

data/goings-on/disputation/situation.kyr:
Module disputation "The disputation on the green" {
  Description "On market days two philosophers dispute on the green, and the town stands round to listen and take sides: one of the One, who teaches that all things are one thing and change is only seeming, and one of the Flow, who teaches that nothing stays. A sophist leans between them, and will argue either side for whoever pays. What the country's own history says would settle it, for whoever has found it.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place green "The green" is room.
  // The country's own history, for whoever has found it: who the first makers were, by their own marks, which still
  // read after them; how they ended; and the kingdom after them, and how it fell.
  Entity making: fact "Who the first makers were". Entity ending: fact "How the first makers ended".
  Entity successors: fact "The kingdom after them".
  Entity oneness: claim "that all things are one, and change is only seeming".
  Entity flux: claim "that nothing stays, and nothing made outlasts its making".
  Initially Assert refutes(making, flux). Initially Assert refutes(ending, oneness). Initially Assert refutes(successors, oneness).
  Entity dispute: fact "Two philosophers dispute at {green} on market days, one of the One and one of the Flow, and the town takes sides.".
  Initially Assert established(dispute).

  Person one "The philosopher of the One" at green { Role "a philosopher of the One". Peaceable. }
  Person flow "The philosopher of the Flow" at green { Role "a philosopher of the Flow". Peaceable. }
  Person sophist "The sophist" at green { Role "a sophist". Peaceable. }
  Initially Assert believes(one, oneness). Initially Set conviction(one, oneness) to 2. Initially Assert disputant(one).
  Initially Assert believes(flow, flux). Initially Set conviction(flow, flux) to 2. Initially Assert disputant(flow).
  Initially Set hire(one) to 0. Initially Set hire(flow) to 0.
  Relation heard(group). Relation answered(group, entity). Relation glanced(group).
  // A reason told badly is not lost: what the country's history says is still so, and it can be told again the next
  // day (a reason that failed its roll was gone for good: the play-structure investigation's PT-05).
  Relation faltered(group, entity).
  Rule told_again when faltered(?p, ?m) and untilLight(clock) == 1 { Retract faltered(?p, ?m). }
  Entity move_reason: fact "a reason". Entity move_after: fact "the kingdom after". Entity move_argue: fact "an argument".
  Entity move_sophist: fact "the sophist". Entity move_glance: fact "the old stones".

  Observe crowd at green when believes(one, oneness) and believes(flow, flux) "Two philosophers are disputing here, and a crowd stands round them: {one}, who holds that all things are one and change is only seeming, and {flow}, who holds that nothing stays. {sophist} leans between them with folded arms, and laughs at both.".
  Observe one_beaten at green when doubts(one, oneness) and not reasoned(one, oneness) "The crowd has gone over from {one} today, and laughs when {one} tries to speak.".
  Observe flow_beaten at green when doubts(flow, flux) and not reasoned(flow, flux) "The crowd has gone over from {flow} today, and laughs when {flow} tries to speak.".
  Observe one_recanted at green when reasoned(one, oneness) and doubts(one, oneness) "{one} no longer teaches the One: things end, {one} tells whoever will listen, and the end of them is not seeming.".
  Observe flow_recanted at green when reasoned(flow, flux) and doubts(flow, flux) "{flow} no longer teaches the Flow: some things stay, {flow} tells whoever will listen, longer than the hands that made them.".
  Observe one_cold near one when scorns(one, party) "{one} turns away from you.".
  Observe flow_cold near flow when scorns(flow, party) "{flow} turns away from you.".
  // Someone in the company who reads people sees it without being asked (a passive check: no roll): the philosopher
  // of the Flow keeps looking at the oldest stones in the town while saying that nothing stays.
  Entity glance: fact "The philosopher of the Flow looks at the oldest stones in the town every time the Flow is taught.".
  Initially Assert refutes(glance, flux).
  Observe flow_looks at green as sign when capable(party, insight) and believes(flow, flux) and not knows(party, glance) "Watching {flow} argue, you see where {flow}'s eyes go at each 'nothing stays': to the oldest stones in the town, which were old when the town was new." teaches glance.

  Topic one_doctrine with one "Ask {one} what the One is" when true once {
    Says "'There is one thing,' says {one}, 'and it does not change. The river, the hill, you and I and the dead: one thing, seen in pieces by eyes that see in pieces. What seems to end does not end. Nothing is lost, because nothing is apart.' The crowd murmurs; some of them nod.".
    On discuss { Assert heard(one). }
  }
  Topic flow_doctrine with flow "Ask {flow} what the Flow is" when true once {
    Says "'Nothing stays,' says {flow}. 'Not the river, not the hill, not the stones you stand on. What is made is unmade in the making; your house is already falling down. Hold on to nothing, and nothing will be taken from you.' The other half of the crowd laughs and claps.".
    On discuss { Assert heard(flow). }
  }
  Topic sophist_holds with sophist "Ask {sophist} what a sophist holds" when true once {
    Says "'Nothing at all,' says {sophist}, cheerfully. 'The truth is whatever is left standing when the arguing stops, and I can see to it that it is yours. Two coin, and I will argue either of them into the ground.'".
  }

  // A reason shakes a philosopher, and does not turn one: each has an answer to it, and lets the claim go only when
  // that answer is met in turn, or another reason is put. Whoever is shaken can no longer be argued down or bought
  // off: the dispute has become a real one. The follow-up independent review saw one example convert a philosopher
  // and finish the dispute.
  Relation gave(group, entity).
  Entity move_meaning: fact "whose words". Entity move_going: fact "which goes first".
  Entity move_lost: fact "what was lost". Entity move_names: fact "the names".

  // Against the Flow: the makers' own marks, which still read though the makers are long gone.
  Action answer_flow(actor: group, site: place) "Answer {flow} with the makers' own marks, which still read though they are gone" {
    Speaker flow. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(flow, site) and heard(flow) and believes(flow, flux)
      and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_reason) and not faltered(flow, move_reason) and knows(actor, making).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_reason). Assert gave(flow, move_reason). Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 1. Assert reasoned(flow, flux). }
    On failure { Assert faltered(flow, move_reason). }
    Result "You tell {flow} what the first makers cut in their stones, and that it still reads, when no one alive has seen a maker. {flow} is quiet a long time, and the crowd with {flow}.".
    Otherwise "You tell {flow} of the makers' marks, but you tell it badly, and {flow} turns it into a joke about stones that the crowd likes better. The marks say what they say: another day, you might tell it better.".
  }
  Observe flow_grants_stones at green when believes(flow, flux) and gave(flow, move_reason) "{flow} has granted you the stones, and not what was meant by them. 'That went with the hands that cut them,' {flow} tells the crowd. 'What you read in old scratches is your own.'".
  Action answer_flow_meaning(actor: group, site: place) "Read {flow} the makers' marks as they stand, and ask whose words they are" {
    Speaker flow. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(flow, site) and believes(flow, flux) and gave(flow, move_reason)
      and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_meaning) and not faltered(flow, move_meaning) and knows(actor, making).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_meaning). Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert faltered(flow, move_meaning). }
    Result "You give the crowd the marks as they stand, the makers' own name for themselves and the order they put things in, and nothing of yours in it. {flow} hears them through. 'Not yours,' {flow} says. 'Theirs. Then what they meant has stayed as well.'".
    Otherwise "What you remember of the marks comes out in your own words, and {flow} only nods: 'You see? Yours.' The crowd laughs. Another day, with the marks fresher in mind, you might read them better.".
  }
  Action answer_flow_glance(actor: group, site: place) "Ask {flow} why the old stones draw the eye of one who says that nothing stays" {
    Speaker flow. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(flow, site) and heard(flow) and believes(flow, flux)
      and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_glance) and not faltered(flow, move_glance) and knows(actor, glance).
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_glance). Assert gave(flow, move_glance). Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 1. Assert reasoned(flow, flux). }
    On failure { Assert faltered(flow, move_glance). }
    Result "{flow} looks at the shrine's stones, and then at you. 'Because they are still there,' {flow} says. 'I have looked at them every market day for twenty years, and said that nothing stays.'".
    Otherwise "{flow} only smiles. 'I look at them,' {flow} says, 'to see them going.' The crowd likes it. You saw what you saw: another day, you might put it better.".
  }
  Observe flow_holds_going at green when believes(flow, flux) and gave(flow, move_glance) "{flow} has owned to looking at the old stones, and says now that it is to watch them go: 'Look at the weather on them. Slowly is still going.'".
  Action answer_flow_going(actor: group, site: place) "Ask {flow} which will go first, the town or its old stones" {
    Speaker flow. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(flow, site) and believes(flow, flux) and gave(flow, move_glance)
      and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_going).
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_going). Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert answered(flow, move_going). }
    Result "'The town,' says {flow}, too quickly. 'The town, and me, and everyone here. They will still be standing.' {flow} looks at the stones a long while.".
    Otherwise "'Both,' says {flow} easily, 'each in its time,' and the crowd is satisfied.".
  }
  Event flow_comes_round near flow when doubts(flow, flux) and reasoned(flow, flux) "{flow} is quiet a long while, and then says it to the crowd, loud enough for all of them to hear: 'I have taught wrong.' Afterwards {flow} comes to you: 'If you are going where the old words are, I would read them with you.'" then {
    Assert willing(flow, party).
  }
  // Against the One: how the first makers ended, and the kingdom after them, which also ended.
  Action answer_one(actor: group, site: place) "Tell {one} how the first makers ended" {
    Speaker one. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(one, site) and heard(one) and believes(one, oneness)
      and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_reason) and not faltered(one, move_reason) and knows(actor, ending).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_reason). Assert gave(one, move_reason). Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 1. Assert reasoned(one, oneness). }
    On failure { Assert faltered(one, move_reason). }
    Result "You tell {one} how the first makers ended, as their own stones tell it. {one} listens to the end, and the crowd with {one}. 'A people,' {one} says, 'and then not.'".
    Otherwise "You tell {one} how the makers ended, but {one} hears it out and smiles: 'They are here still, in the One, as you are.' The crowd nods along. It is still how they ended: another day, you might tell it better.".
  }
  Observe one_holds_wave at green when believes(one, oneness) and gave(one, move_reason) "{one} has granted that the makers ended, and not that anything ended with them. 'A wave goes back into the sea,' {one} tells the crowd. 'You have told me that they ended. You have not told me that anything was lost.'".
  Action answer_one_lost(actor: group, site: place) "Ask {one} why the makers cut their own end in stone, if nothing was lost" {
    Speaker one. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(one, site) and believes(one, oneness) and gave(one, move_reason)
      and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_lost) and not faltered(one, move_lost) and knows(actor, ending).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_lost). Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert faltered(one, move_lost). }
    Result "'Because they were there,' you say, 'and did not think it seeming.' {one} starts to answer, and stops. 'They grieved,' {one} says at last. 'Nobody grieves a wave.'".
    Otherwise "'To show us what seeming looks like,' says {one}, gently, and the crowd nods. Another day, you might find the words.".
  }
  Action answer_one_after(actor: group, site: place) "Tell {one} of the kingdom that came after the makers, and how it fell" {
    Speaker one. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(one, site) and heard(one) and believes(one, oneness)
      and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_after) and not faltered(one, move_after) and knows(actor, successors).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_after). Assert gave(one, move_after). Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 1. Assert reasoned(one, oneness). }
    On failure { Assert faltered(one, move_after). }
    Result "You tell {one} of the kingdom that came after the makers, what it was and how it fell, with the names in it. 'Twice, then,' {one} says. 'Twice in this one country, a whole people ended.'".
    Otherwise "{one} lets you finish. 'Kingdoms are seeming,' {one} says, 'like the clouds,' and the crowd is with {one} again. The kingdom fell all the same: another day, you might tell it better.".
  }
  Observe one_holds_breath at green when believes(one, oneness) and gave(one, move_after) "{one} has heard the kingdom out, and says now that it was once, seen twice: 'Peoples come and go as the breath goes in and out. The breathing is one.'".
  Action answer_one_names(actor: group, site: place) "Ask {one} to say the fallen kingdom's names to the crowd, and tell it they are here still" {
    Speaker one. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(one, site) and believes(one, oneness) and gave(one, move_after)
      and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_names).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_names). Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 1. }
    On failure { Assert answered(one, move_names). }
    Result "{one} begins, and stops at the second name. Nobody in the crowd knows it. 'They are not here,' {one} says quietly. 'Nobody here has ever heard of them.'".
    Otherwise "{one} says the names, calm as a prayer, and the crowd hears them as a prayer.".
  }
  Event one_comes_round near one when doubts(one, oneness) and reasoned(one, oneness) "{one} sits down heavily. 'I will have to think again from the beginning,' {one} says. Then, to you: 'You know where the old things are. Let me come with you, and see them end for myself.'" then {
    Assert willing(one, party).
  }
  // Argument without a reason: it wins the day and is gone by morning, and is not forgiven.
  Action argue_flow(actor: group, site: place) "Argue {flow} down: some things stay" {
    Speaker flow. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(flow, site) and heard(flow) and believes(flow, flux)
      and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_argue)
      and not reasoned(flow, flux).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_argue). Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 2. Assert swayedBy(flow, flux, actor). }
    On failure { Assert answered(flow, move_argue). }
    Result "You turn {flow}'s own words on {flow}, faster than {flow} can answer, until the crowd is laughing and {flow} has nothing to say. It is a victory. It is not a reason.".
    Otherwise "{flow} lets you talk yourself out, and then says one thing, and the crowd laughs at you instead.".
  }
  Action argue_one(actor: group, site: place) "Argue {one} down: things change" {
    Speaker one. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(one, site) and heard(one) and believes(one, oneness)
      and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_argue)
      and not reasoned(one, oneness).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_argue). Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 2. Assert swayedBy(one, oneness, actor). }
    On failure { Assert answered(one, move_argue). }
    Result "You tie {one} in {one}'s own knots, one after another, until the crowd is jeering and {one} stops trying to answer. It is a victory. It is not a reason.".
    Otherwise "{one} answers every point with the same calm, and the crowd tires of you first.".
  }
  // The sophist argues for whoever pays: the day is won, and nothing else.
  Action hire_sophist_flow(actor: group, site: place) "Pay {sophist} two coin to argue {flow} into the ground" {
    Speaker sophist. Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(sophist, site) and at(flow, site) and heard(flow)
      and believes(flow, flux) and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_sophist) and not reasoned(flow, flux)
      and quantity(actor, gold) >= 2.
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_sophist). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Increase quantity(sophist, gold) by 2.
      Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 2. Assert swayedBy(flow, flux, actor). }
    Result "{sophist} pockets the coin, steps up beside {flow}, and takes {flow} apart in a quarter of an hour, cheerfully, to the delight of the green. Then {sophist} winks at you. 'By tomorrow,' {sophist} says, 'it will all be believed again. It always is.'".
  }
  Action hire_sophist_one(actor: group, site: place) "Pay {sophist} two coin to argue {one} into the ground" {
    Speaker sophist. Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(sophist, site) and at(one, site) and heard(one)
      and believes(one, oneness) and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_sophist) and not reasoned(one, oneness)
      and quantity(actor, gold) >= 2.
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_sophist). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Increase quantity(sophist, gold) by 2.
      Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 2. Assert swayedBy(one, oneness, actor). }
    Result "{sophist} pockets the coin, steps up beside {one}, and takes {one} apart in a quarter of an hour, cheerfully, to the delight of the green. Then {sophist} winks at you. 'By tomorrow,' {sophist} says, 'it will all be believed again. It always is.'".
  }

  // Unfinished until it is settled (arguing one down for the day had taken it out of the company's notes: the
  // play-structure investigation's PT-25); and said so when neither will hear the company.
  Query disputeSettled() means (reasoned(one, oneness) and doubts(one, oneness)) or (reasoned(flow, flux) and doubts(flow, flux)).
  Query shunned() means scorns(one, party) and scorns(flow, party).
  Objective disputed when knows(party, dispute) and not disputeSettled() and not shunned() "Two philosophers dispute at {green}: the One against the Flow. What the country's own history says could settle it.".
  Objective disputed_shut when knows(party, dispute) and not disputeSettled() and shunned() "Neither philosopher at {green} will hear you now: you had them argued down without a reason, and it is not forgiven.".
  Goal (reasoned(one, oneness) and doubts(one, oneness)) or (reasoned(flow, flux) and doubts(flow, flux)).
}

data/goings-on/drover/oxen/situation.kyr:
Module oxen "The thing that took the oxen" {
  Description "Whatever had the drover's oxen dragged them off from the ditch to a den in the wild. The trail is there to be read from the road, the son wants to see the end of it, and the yoke was his grandfather's.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place road "The road" is room.
  Place lair "The den" is room. Entity track: passage "The track to the den".
  Entity wife: group "The drover's wife". Entity son: group "The drover's son". Entity beasts: group "the beasts".
  Entity found_cart: fact "The drover's cart went off the road in the night.".
  // The trail from the ditch to the den nearest the drover's town (see the drover's scenario), told by the son, who
  // read it, once the cart is found; and a way there for whoever has heard it.
  Entity trail: fact "From the ditch below {road}, two furrows and a line of great prints go up the bank and away toward {lair}.".
  Initially Assert leadsTo(trail, lair). Initially Assert leadsVia(trail, track).
  Initially Assert revealedBy(track, trail).
  // Dealt with as the den is: dead, or driven off or laid to rest.
  Query dealt() means dead(beasts) or peaceable(beasts).
  Topic son_after with son "Ask {son} what he means to do now" when knows(actor, found_cart) and not dealt()
    and not knows(actor, trail) once {
    Says "'Whatever took them is up at {lair},' says {son}. 'I saw the marks from the ditch: two furrows, and prints too big for any dog.' He turns the spear in his hands. 'I want to see it. And I want the yoke back. It was Grandfather's.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, trail). }
  }
  // With the company, once the cart is behind it, he says it unasked: play 10's thread seemed to end with the burying
  // and the telling, the trail a question nobody thought to put to him.
  Rule son_speaks when knows(party, found_cart) and travelsWith(son, party) and not at(party, road)
    and not knows(party, trail) and not dealt() says "{son} has said nothing since the ditch. Now he says, to nobody in particular, 'Whatever took the oxen is up at {lair}. I saw the marks: two furrows, and prints too big for any dog.' He turns the spear in his hands. 'I want to see it. And I want the yoke back. It was Grandfather's.'" teaches trail { }
  Objective oxen when knows(party, trail) and not dealt() "Whatever took the drover's oxen dens at {lair}.".
  // The yoke, among the bones once the den is dealt with; carried home, it hangs over the hearth where it always hung.
  Kind ox_yoke "an ox-yoke" is treasure worth 2 weighing 8 described "An old ox-yoke of ash, carved along the bow with oak leaves, and worn smooth where the necks went.".
  Entity yoke_seen: fact "The drover's ox-yoke lies among the bones at {lair}.".
  Item yoke "the drover's ox-yoke" is ox_yoke at lair hidden until yoke_seen.
  Observe yoke_glimpse at lair when dealt() and not knows(party, yoke_seen) "Among the bones at the back an ox-yoke lies where it was dragged, carved along the bow with oak leaves." teaches yoke_seen.
  Relation hung(group).
  Event yoke_seen_home near wife when carries(party, yoke) and not hung(party) "{wife} sees it before you say anything, and puts down what is in her hands. 'You brought it back,' she says. 'Hang it where it was.'".
  Action hang_yoke(actor: group, carrier: member, site: place) "Hang the yoke over the hearth, where it always hung" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(wife, site) and memberOf(carrier, actor) and ownedItem(yoke, carrier)
      and not hung(actor).
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve drop(yoke, carrier).
    On success { Assert at(yoke, site). Assert hung(actor). }
    Result "It goes up on its two pegs over the hearth as if it had never been down. {wife} looks at it a long time, and does not say anything else, and does not need to.".
  }
  Goal hung(party).
}

data/goings-on/drover/situation.kyr:
Module drover "The drover who did not come home" {
  Description "A drover went out on the road three days ago with a cart and two oxen and did not come home. His dog did, alone, in the night. His wife cooks at the inn and will not talk about it; his son talks of nothing else.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place green "The green" is room.
  Place taproom "The taproom" is room.
  Place road "The road" is room.
  Relation told(group). Relation gone(group).
  Entity missing: fact "A drover went out on the road from {green} three days ago and did not come home. His dog did.".
  Initially Assert established(missing). Initially Assert staged(road, missing).

  Person wife "The drover's wife" at taproom { Role "the drover's wife, who cooks at the inn". Pronouns she. Peaceable. }
  // Someone outside the family who saw him go, and has a thought about what took the oxen: nobody but the family could
  // be asked about the father or the cart, not the wagoner who knows the road nor anyone at the inn (Mission 20's third
  // round, C §6).
  Person hedger "the hedger" at taproom { Role "a hedger who drinks his supper at the inn". Pronouns he. Peaceable. Manner stoic. }
  Topic hedger_saw with hedger "Ask the hedger whether he saw the drover go" when not knows(party, found_cart) once {
    Says "'Three nights back, at dusk,' says the hedger. 'Out on {road}, cart up high, the oxen going well. Said he'd be home by full dark.' He turns his cup round. 'He wasn't singing. He always sings on that road.'".
  }
  Topic hedger_oxen with hedger "Ask the hedger what would take two oxen and leave the man" when knows(party, found_cart) once {
    Says "The hedger puts his cup down. 'Wolves would take one and tear it where it fell. Whatever took both took them uphill, alive, and wanted them whole.' He looks at the window. 'There's an old drove road over the tops nobody uses now. My father wouldn't. Ask him why, he'd say: because of what minds it.'".
  }
  Person son "The drover's son" at green { Role "the drover's son, who wants to go after his father". Pronouns he. Peaceable. }
  // The dog that came home: a real dog, lame in the off forefoot, who lets anyone who is kind to her look at her; and
  // whoever does sees where she has been.
  Person dog "the grey dog" at green { Role "the drover's dog". Species dog. Pronouns she. Peaceable. }
  Observe dog_waits near dog of dog as sign when not told(wife) and at(dog, green) "A grey dog lies by the door of {taproom} with her head on her paws, watching the road. She holds one forefoot off the ground.".
  Observe dog_in near dog of dog when told(wife) and at(dog, taproom) "The grey dog lies by the kitchen fire with her chin on her paws.".
  Rule dog_goes_in when told(wife) and at(dog, green) { Assert at(dog, taproom). }
  Entity dog_mud: fact "The grey dog came home caked in black ditch-mud, the off forefoot cut as if on iron.".
  Observe dog_tells near dog as sign when petted(dog, party) and not knows(party, dog_mud) "Under your hand her coat is stiff with dried black mud to the belly: ditch-mud, not road dust, as if she had lain a long time somewhere low and wet. The pad of the off forefoot is cut clean across, the way iron cuts." teaches dog_mud.
  Observe dog_muddy near dog of dog as sign when knows(party, dog_mud) and not knows(party, found_cart) "Her coat is stiff with black ditch-mud to the belly.".
  // The ruts the road speaks of are a thing to follow, not only to search for: the cart was found only by the
  // generic "Search here" (the play-structure investigation's PT-08).
  Thing ruts "the fresh ruts" at road {
    State fresh "Fresh ruts run off the edge of the road here, where the bank drops away.".
    State followed "The ruts go over the edge of the road and down the bank, to the ditch.".
    Change follow "Follow the ruts over the edge" from fresh to followed.
  }
  Rule ruts_followed when state(ruts, followed) and not knows(party, found_cart) says "Below the road, where the bank drops away, a cart lies on its side in the ditch with a man under it, a day or more dead. The oxen are gone; something had them, and dragged them off toward the hills." teaches found_cart { }
  Rule ruts_read when knows(party, found_cart) and state(ruts, fresh) { Assert state(ruts, followed). }

  Discovery found_cart "The drover's cart went off the road in the night. He is under it, a day or more dead, and whatever had the oxen dragged them off toward the hills." {
    Found by searching road "Below the road, where the bank drops away, a cart lies on its side in the ditch with a man under it, a day or more dead. The oxen are gone; something had them, and dragged them off toward the hills.".
  }
  // To the drover's own child the man under the cart is their father, known before the face is (the M16 free play
  // found him "a man" to his child, in the words a stranger would find him in). Seen once: what it teaches is a mark
  // with no words, never told as something known.
  Entity father_known: fact "".
  Observe father_seen at road as event when kin(party, wife) and knows(party, found_cart) and not knows(party, father_known) "It is your father. You know the coat first, and the hands, before you will let yourself know the face." teaches father_known.
  Item knife "a drover's knife with a horn handle" is dagger at road hidden until found_cart.
  // Said while it is so: taken, the knife is no longer in his belt (the follow-up review took it and it stayed).
  Observe knife_belt at road when knows(party, found_cart) and at(knife, road) and not buried(party) and not fetched(party) "His knife is still in his belt.".

  // What becomes of him is the company's to choose, and the family's to hear: covered where he lies, for the village
  // to fetch home in the morning, or buried by the road with the words said; and either way somewhere to stand a
  // while, later (the follow-up review found nothing to do for him but read that he was there).
  Relation covered(group). Relation buried(group). Relation fetched(group). Relation stood(group).
  Action cover_drover(actor: group, site: place) "Cover him with the cart's sheet, and stand his whip up to mark the place" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, road) and knows(actor, found_cart) and not covered(actor)
      and not buried(actor).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert covered(actor). }
    Result "You get the sheet off the load and over him, and weigh its corners down with stones, and stand his whip up in the bank where anyone coming along the road will see it.".
  }
  Action bury_drover(actor: group, site: place) "Bury him by the road, and say the words over him" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, road) and knows(actor, found_cart) and not buried(actor)
      and not fetched(actor) and not capable(actor, rites).
    Time 120 minutes.
    On success { Assert buried(actor). Retract covered(actor). }
    Result "It takes the best part of two hours, with what you have to dig with. You lay him in the bank above the ditch, facing the road, and heap the ditch-stones over him, and say what words you have.".
  }
  // One who knows the rites of the dead says them, not what words come (journey 2 of Mission 19, 7 November: a
  // cleric who had laid the dead under the churchyard by the rite of rest buried a father with "what words you
  // have", as anyone would); and the family hears that it was done properly.
  Relation rited(group).
  Action bury_drover_rite(actor: group, site: place) "Bury him by the road, and say the rite of the dead over him" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, road) and knows(actor, found_cart) and not buried(actor)
      and not fetched(actor) and capable(actor, rites).
    Time 120 minutes.
    On success { Assert buried(actor). Assert rited(actor). Retract covered(actor). }
    Result "It takes the best part of two hours, with what you have to dig with. You lay him in the bank above the ditch, facing the road, and heap the ditch-stones over him; then you say the rite, all of it, the way the shrines keep it, with his name in the places for a name, and pour a little of the road's dust over the stones at the end.".
  }
  Observe drover_covered at road when covered(party) and not fetched(party) "The cart's sheet lies over him, weighted with stones, and his whip stands up in the bank.".
  Observe drover_cairn at road when buried(party) "Above the ditch a cairn of ditch-stones stands new by the road, facing it.".
  Observe knife_cairn at road when buried(party) and at(knife, road) "His knife lies on the cairn: nobody could bring themselves to bury it, or to take it.".
  // Told, the wife says what will be done: fetched home in the morning, or let lie where he is.
  Event wife_will_fetch near wife when told(wife) and covered(party) "'You covered him,' she says. 'Then we will go for him in the morning, with the reed-cutters' cart, and bring him home.'".
  Event wife_hears_cairn near wife when told(wife) and buried(party) and not rited(party) "'You buried him,' she says. 'By the road?' She is quiet a while. 'He would like that. He could never stand to be under a roof.'".
  Event wife_hears_rite near wife when told(wife) and rited(party) "'You buried him,' she says. 'By the road, with the rite said?' She is quiet a while. 'He would like that. And laid properly: nobody can say he was put in a ditch.' She looks at you as if you were someone she had not met. 'He could never stand to be under a roof.'".
  Rule drover_fetched when told(wife) and covered(party) and not buried(party) and untilLight(clock) == 1 {
    Assert fetched(party).
  }
  Observe drover_grave at green when fetched(party) "At the edge of {green} there is a new grave, with a drover's whip laid along it.".
  Action stand_at_grave(actor: group, site: place) "Stand a while at the grave" {
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and told(wife) and not stood(actor)
      and ((buried(actor) and at(actor, road)) or (fetched(actor) and at(actor, green))).
    Time 10 minutes.
    On success { Assert stood(actor). }
    Result "You stand a while. Nobody says anything, and nothing needs saying.".
  }
  Event son_at_grave near party when stood(party) and travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) "'Somebody should sing him something terrible,' says {son}. Nobody does; but you all think of it, and it helps.".

  // To one of the family the drover is a father, his wife a mother, his son a brother: they say other things.
  Observe wife_kin near wife when kin(party, wife) and not told(wife) "Your mother is at the hearth with her back to the room.".
  Observe son_kin near son when kin(party, son) and not told(son) and at(son, green) "Your brother is sitting on a rail with your father's old spear across his knees, watching the road. He is taller by a head than when you went away.".
  Observe son_kin_in near son when kin(party, son) and not told(son) and at(son, taproom) "Your brother sits by the kitchen fire with your father's old spear across his knees, not drinking. He is taller by a head than when you went away.".
  // Until he has somewhere to go, the son keeps the green by day and comes in to his mother after dark.
  Rule son_goes_in when dark() and at(son, green) and not willing(son, party) { Assert at(son, taproom). }
  Rule son_comes_out when not dark() and at(son, taproom) and not willing(son, party) { Assert at(son, green). }
  // At the rail, not wherever he is: come along with the company, he had been "waiting by the rail" two storeys under
  // the town (Mission 20's third round, C).
  Observe son_kin_ready near son when kin(party, son) and told(son) and not knows(party, found_cart) and not travelsWith(son, party) "Your brother is waiting by the rail with the spear, ready when you are.".
  // Told, she knows he is not coming: she had still looked up at the door (play 10).
  Observe wife_kin_told near wife when kin(party, wife) and told(wife) "Your mother is at the hearth, at her work. She has stopped looking at the door.".
  Topic wife_where with wife "Ask your mother where he was going" when kin(actor, wife) and not told(wife) once {
    Says "'Out by {road}, with the salt for the reed-cutters,' says your mother, and keeps her eyes on the pot. 'Three days there and back, the way he goes. The dog came home on the fourth, lame in the off foot.' She wipes her hands, though they are dry. 'Nobody will go and look. I am glad you came.'".
  }
  Topic wife_told_kin with wife "Tell your mother what you found on the road" when knows(actor, found_cart) and kin(actor, wife) and not told(wife) once {
    Says "Your mother does not sit down. She takes your face in her hands and looks at it for a long time. 'I knew,' she says. 'The dog knew.' Then she goes back to the pot, because there are people to feed.".
    On discuss { Assert told(wife). }
  }
  Topic son_plan with son "Ask {son} what he means to do" when kin(actor, son) and not knows(actor, found_cart) and not told(son) once {
    Says "'Go after him,' says {son}. 'Mother says wait. I have waited three days.' He looks at you, and at the road. 'If you are going, I am coming with you. If you are not, I am going anyway.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(son, actor). Assert told(son). }
  }
  // Not to one who knelt by the cart himself: he was there.
  Topic son_found_kin with son "Tell {son} what you found" when knows(actor, found_cart) and kin(actor, son)
    and not knows(actor, son_knelt) once {
    Says "{son} hears it out, and is quiet for a long time. 'Then whatever had the oxen is still out there,' he says. 'I want to see it.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(son, actor). Assert told(son). }
  }
  Topic wife_husband with wife "Ask {wife} about her husband" when not told(wife) and not kin(actor, wife) once {
    Says "'He went out with the cart three days back,' says {wife}, and keeps her eyes on the pot. 'The dog came home. He didn't.'".
  }
  Topic wife_told with wife "Tell {wife} what you found on the road" when knows(actor, found_cart) and not told(wife) and not kin(actor, wife) once {
    Says "{wife} puts down the ladle and sits. After a while she says, 'I knew. The dog knew.' She takes coin from her apron and puts it in your hand without counting it. 'For going.'".
    On discuss { Assert told(wife). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 6. }
  }
  // To one of the family, she is their mother, and it is their father's knife.
  Topic wife_knife_kin with wife "Show your mother his knife" when carries(actor, knife) and told(wife) and kin(actor, wife) once {
    Says "She turns the knife over in her hands, and gives it back. 'Keep it. He would want it used, not hung on a wall.'".
  }
  Topic wife_knife with wife "Show {wife} her husband's knife" when carries(actor, knife) and told(wife)
    and not kin(actor, wife) once {
    Says "She turns the knife over in her hands, and gives it back. 'Keep it. He would want it used, not hung on a wall.'".
  }
  Topic son_father with son "Ask {son} about his father" when not knows(actor, found_cart) and not kin(actor, son) once {
    Says "'Three days,' says {son}. 'Mother says wait. I have waited.' He looks at the road. 'If you are going that way, I will come.'".
  }
  Topic son_found with son "Tell {son} what you found" when knows(actor, found_cart) and not kin(actor, son)
    and not knows(actor, son_knelt) once {
    Says "{son} hears it out. 'Then whatever had the oxen is still out there,' he says. 'I am coming with you. No hire. I want to see it.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(son, actor). Assert told(son). }
  }
  // Once he has come with you, the son talks on the way: he knows the road his father took, and the cart.
  Topic son_road with son travelling "Ask {son} about the road your father took" when kin(actor, son) and awake(member_son_person) and not knows(actor, found_cart) once {
    Says "'By {road}, to market. He knew every rut of it.' {son} kicks at a stone. 'He had the left wheel out of true all spring and would not see to it. If the cart went off the road, look for where a wheel like that would take it.'".
  }
  Topic son_road_stranger with son travelling "Ask {son} about the road his father took" when not kin(actor, son) and awake(member_son_person) and not knows(actor, found_cart) once {
    Says "'By {road}, to market,' says {son}. 'He knew it in the dark. The left wheel of the cart was out of true. If it went off the road, that is why.'".
  }
  Topic son_night with son travelling "Sit up late with {son}" when awake(member_son_person) and dark() once {
    Says "'He used to sing to the oxen,' says {son}. 'Terrible songs. He made them up as he went, and they liked them better than anything.' He is quiet a while. 'Mother would not have him sing in the house.'".
  }
  Event son_wheel at road when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and at(party, road) and not knows(party, found_cart) "{son} stops where the ruts go off the road and stands looking at them. 'That is the left wheel,' he says. 'That is his.'".
  // He kneels there once, before the company's eyes: something seen, not something learned, so what it teaches has no
  // words (the M16 free play found his kneeling filed among what it knew).
  Entity son_knelt: fact "".
  Observe son_kneels at road as event when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and knows(party, found_cart) and not knows(party, son_knelt) "{son} goes down the bank to the cart before anyone can stop him, and kneels there a long time. When he comes back up he has nothing to say, and nobody asks him to." teaches son_knelt.
  // On the road with you he is himself, after the cart as before it: what he makes of where you take him, what he
  // remembers, and who he sits with (M16's deepening asked for one companion with a perspective, a memory and people
  // of his own). Said where the company is: one who has joined it stands nowhere of his own (his words at the grave,
  // said where he stood, were never heard while he went with you).
  Event son_under near party when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and at(party, ?p) and unlit(?p) and not benighted(party) "{son} keeps to the middle of the light and does not look behind him. 'Father would never go under a roof he could not see the end of,' he says. 'I used to think it was because he was a coward. I think now it was because he had sense.'".
  Event son_binds near party when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and memberOf(?m, party) and needsCare(?m) and not joinedAs(?m, son) "{son} binds the hurt fast and badly, the way Father bound the oxen when they went lame. 'Hold still,' he says, in Father's voice, and then stops, surprised at himself.".
  Event son_purse near party when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and quantity(party, gold) >= 60 "{son} weighs the purse in his hand. 'More than Father had in a year of droves,' he says. 'Mother is not to know how we came by it.' He thinks. 'Or she is, and we will not tell her.'".
  Event son_with_mother near party when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and told(wife) and at(party, taproom) and at(wife, taproom) and kin(party, son) "{son} sits down by your mother without a word, and she puts a hand on his arm without looking at him. That is all either of them will say about it, tonight.".
  Event son_and_fellow near party when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and travelsWith(?f, party) and distinct(?f, son) "{son} watches {?f} a while, when {?f} is not looking. 'Father would have liked {?f},' he says. 'He would have said so twice, and then given {?f} the worst ox.'".
  Topic son_after with son travelling "Ask {son} what he will do now" when kin(actor, son) and awake(member_son_person) and knows(actor, found_cart) once {
    Says "'Take Father's road to market, I suppose,' says {son}, 'if anything comes back of the oxen. Somebody has to.' He looks along the road a while. 'You will go back over the hills.' He does not ask you to stay, which is how you know he wants you to.".
  }
  Topic son_after_stranger with son travelling "Ask {son} what he will do now" when not kin(actor, son) and awake(member_son_person) and knows(actor, found_cart) once {
    Says "'See Mother right,' says {son}. 'Then I don't know. Father would have known.' He shoulders the spear. 'Till then I'm with you, if you'll have me.'".
  }
  Topic son_home with son travelling "Ask {son} about home" when kin(actor, son) and awake(member_son_person) once {
    Says "'You remember the flood year?' says {son}. 'You carried me over the ford on your back and told me there were eels in it the size of oxen. I did not go near water again until I was ten.' He grins for the first time. 'There were not, were there.'".
  }
  // Left alone too long, the son goes out after his father himself.
  Rule son_goes at green when watch(clock) >= 204 and not told(son) and at(son, green) says "{son} has taken his father's old spear and gone out on the road alone. Nobody stopped him." { Retract at(son, green). Assert gone(son). }

  Objective road when knows(party, missing) and not knows(party, found_cart) and not kin(party, wife) toward road "A drover from {green} went out on the road and did not come home.".
  Objective tell when knows(party, found_cart) and not told(wife) and not kin(party, wife) toward wife "The drover's wife, at the inn, does not know what you found.".
  // {road} is a place on the road he took (a ford, a bank), not the road itself: he went out by it, not on it (play
  // 10 read "Your father went out on the ford of the Nûrnellë").
  Objective road_kin when kin(party, wife) and not knows(party, found_cart) toward road "Your father went out by {road} with the cart, and did not come home.".
  Objective tell_kin when kin(party, wife) and knows(party, found_cart) and not told(wife) toward wife "Your mother, at the inn, does not know what you found.".
  Goal told(wife).
}

