data/origins/order/origin.kyr:
Module origin "The brothers' errand" {
  Kind chapter. Entity title: chapter "The brothers' errand".
  Entity party: group "You".
  Place shrine "The shrine" is room. Place delving "The old writing's place" is room.
  Entity priest: group "The priest". Entity named: fact "Where it is". Entity history: fact "Who made it".
  Entity fate: fact "How they ended".
  Entity found: fact "The way there".
  Relation delivered(group). Relation copied(group).
  // The bed the priest gives, once the letter is read: lodging for nothing, for as long as the errand lasts.
  Entity bed: service "the bed in the back". Initially Assert serviceOf(bed, lodging). Initially Set fee(bed) to 0.
  Initially Assert expects(priest, party). Initially Assert knows(party, named).
  Observe letter at shrine as feature when expects(priest, party) "You have the letter inside your coat: from the brothers of your order, over the hills, to the priest of {cult} at {homename}, asking that {protagonist}, who reads the old script, be given a bed and shown the way to {work}. There is writing there that the order has heard of for a hundred years and never seen copied.".
  // Come in off the road, the town named: the opening had told the letter and never where (its critique).
  Observe arrival at shrine as feature when watch(clock) < 1 "{homename} is smaller than the brothers made it sound, after so many days on the road. The first person you ask points the way to the priest of {cult}, and you go in.".
  Topic give_letter with priest "Give {priest} the brothers' letter" when expects(priest, actor) once {
    Says "{priest} reads it by the door, where the light is, and then reads it again. 'Brother Anselm's hand,' {priest} says. 'I did not know he was still living.' A pause. 'There is a bed in the back, such as it is. As for {work}: it is out in {where}, and I will tell you the way, since he asks it. People go out there and come back with their sheep missing. Go in daylight, and take the shrine's rope: the old places were not built to be walked into.'".
    On discuss { Retract expects(priest, actor). Assert delivered(actor). Assert knows(actor, found). Assert offers(priest, bed).
      Assert knows(actor, rope_handed). Give shrine_rope to actor. }
  }
  // The old places were not built to be walked into, and the brothers know it: their priest sends a rope with the way
  // (play 11's thief and drover walked sixteen hours to a door high in a tower wall, and could not reach it).
  // Kept out of sight until it is handed over, by a mark of its own: hidden until the way was known, it had made the
  // way told seem borne out.
  Entity rope_handed: fact "".
  Item shrine_rope "the shrine's coil of rope" is rope at shrine hidden until rope_handed.
  Topic show_copies with priest "Show {priest} what you copied at {work}" when (knows(actor, history) or knows(actor, fate)) and delivered(actor) and not copied(actor) once {
    Says "{priest} turns the pages slowly, and is a long time saying anything. 'So that is who they were,' {priest} says at last. 'The brothers will want this.' Coin is pressed into your hand for the road: the order pays its debts, even through other people's purses.".
    On discuss { Assert copied(actor). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 40. }
  }
  // Whatever the makers cut there of themselves is the old writing: how they lived, or how they ended.
  // Until the letter is given, the first thing to do is here, and said so: the priest, who will show the way (the owner,
  // 7 November: every origin's first goal names a place the company can go to).
  Objective errand_letter when expects(priest, party) and not copied(party) toward priest "The brothers want the old writing at {delving} copied. Their letter is for {priest}, who will show you the way.".
  Objective errand when not expects(priest, party) and not copied(party) and not knows(party, history) and not knows(party, fate) toward delving "The brothers want the old writing at {delving} copied.".
  Objective errand_home when not copied(party) and (knows(party, history) or knows(party, fate)) toward priest "You have copied the old writing at {delving}. {priest} at {homename} should see it.".
  Goal copied(party).
}

