data/situations/arcology/deeps.kyr:
Module arcology "The Numbered House" {
  // The deeps: the Drowned Level, the valve gallery and its three wheels, the sluice-race, the Roots, the pool, and the
  // seed-vault. Water is a wheel here, and each wheel is one thing with a consequence outside the walls.

  // --- the Drowned Level ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe drowned_scene at drowned when state(waterlevel, full) "Pillars stand in clear black water to their shoulders, row on row into the dark, each with a numeral at the height of a man's eye. Shafts of light come down through gratings in the vault from the Great Void above, and the water takes them and turns them green. A walkway on iron brackets runs out along the pillars to a gallery. There is no sound but dripping, and the occasional soft collision of something under the surface with the wall.".
  Observe drowned_dry at drowned when state(waterlevel, low) "The pillars stand in a floor of black silt, drying to a cracked crust. Shafts of light come down through gratings from the Great Void, and shine on the silt, and on the things that have been under the water for a thousand years: a boat of reeds, a row of buckets, the white curve of a bone. A walkway on iron brackets still runs out along the pillars to a gallery.".
  Thing waterlevel "the water in the Drowned Level" at drowned {
    State full "The water stands to the shoulders of the pillars, black and perfectly clear.".
    State low "The water has drained to a skin on the silt.".
  }
  Rule dry_country when water(house, wet_low) and state(waterlevel, full) once { Assert state(waterlevel, low). }
  Person eels "the eels" at drowned {
    Role "long pale eels, thick as a leg". Species eel. Numbers 3. Level 1. Temperament territorial.
    Warns "The water shivers about your legs, and then there are three long pale shapes in it, circling, thick as a leg and as quiet as thought. They have no eyes you can see. They know exactly where you are.".
    Comes "The eels come in all at once from three sides.".
    State circling "Something long and pale turns in the clear black water between the pillars.".
    State stranded "The eels lie in the silt among the pillars, thrashing weakly, out of their element. They have lost interest in you.".
  }
  Rule eels_stranded when state(waterlevel, low) and state(eels, circling) says "As the last of the water goes, the eels are left on the silt in the shafts of light, rolling and gasping. They will not trouble anyone now." { Assert state(eels, stranded). Assert peaceable(eels). }
  Rule eels_gone when water(house, wet_low) and state(eels, circling) { Assert state(eels, stranded). Assert peaceable(eels). }
  Thing roots_lock "the garden door" on roots_door {
    State under blocking "The garden door is a green-bronze valve in the wall, under water to its lintel; it will not be opened while the Level stands full.".
    State clear "The garden door stands above the water, a green-bronze leaf with a bar across it that lifts.".
  }
  Rule garden_door_clear when state(waterlevel, low) and state(roots_lock, under) { Assert state(roots_lock, clear). }
  Observe drowned_numbers at drowned as feature when true "The numerals on the pillars count down from the entrance end, so that each pillar names how many more there are before the gallery. Someone has counted them all before you, on the lowest pillar's foot, in a scratched tally that stops at the last and then says, in a different hand, YES.".

  // --- the valve gallery, and its wheels -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe valves_scene at valves when true "A gallery of iron grating hung over the water, hot with the smell of oil, and on it three great wheels as tall as a man, set in the wall above a bank of pipes as thick as a rib-cage. Each has a plate beside it with a picture. The pipes run away into the rock, and one of them hums.".
  Observe valves_plan at valves as feature when true "The plates beside the wheels have no words, only pictures: a bell-lily; a small roofed house with a lamp in it and a road going out of it a very long way; a bucket tipped over.".
  Thing wheel_garden "the wheel with the bell-lily" at valves {
    State open "The wheel with the bell-lily is turned wide. Water goes up the pipe above it with a sound like a held breath, toward the fourth ring.".
    State stopped "The wheel with the bell-lily is shut tight, and the pipe above it is cold.".
    Change shut_garden "Shut the wheel with the bell-lily" from open to stopped needing brawn.
    Change open_garden "Open the wheel with the bell-lily" from stopped to open needing brawn.
  }
  Thing wheel_town "the wheel with the roofed house" at valves {
    State stopped "The wheel with the little roofed house and the long road is shut. The pipe beside it is silent, and the other end of it must be a very long way off.".
    State open "The wheel with the roofed house is wide, and the pipe beside it is humming with water, going away under the hills.".
    Change open_town "Open the wheel with the roofed house" from stopped to open needing brawn.
    Change shut_town "Shut the wheel with the roofed house" from open to stopped needing brawn.
  }
  Thing wheel_drain "the wheel with the tipped bucket" at valves {
    State stopped "The wheel with the tipped bucket is shut.".
    State open "The wheel with the tipped bucket is open, and a deep, throaty gurgle goes down the pipe beside it.".
    Change open_drain "Open the wheel with the tipped bucket" from stopped to open needing brawn.
    Change shut_drain "Shut the wheel with the tipped bucket" from open to stopped needing brawn.
  }
  Initially Assert state(wheel_garden, open). Initially Assert state(wheel_town, stopped). Initially Assert state(wheel_drain, stopped).
  Rule drain_runs when state(wheel_drain, open) and state(waterlevel, full) says "Under the grating, the black water begins to move. It runs down between the pillars with a long sound like the world breathing out, and the numerals on the pillars stand up out of it one after another." { Assert state(waterlevel, low). }
  Observe wheels_read at valves of wheel_town as reading when capable(party, lore) "The plate beside the wheel names the pipe: THE HOUSE'S EXCESS GOES TO THE SHRINE, WHICH WAS BUILT OVER THE WELL. A later hand has scratched under it: THE HOUSE'S EXCESS IS ALL THE HOUSE'S WATER.".
  Rule spring_runs when state(wheel_town, open) and state(spring, failing) says "Under the hills, a very long way off, there is a sound like a drawn breath, and then a sound like a river." { Assert state(spring, running). }
  Rule spring_fails when state(wheel_town, stopped) and state(spring, running) says "Under the hills, a very long way off, a sound that had begun stops." { Assert state(spring, failing). }
  Thing culvert_water "the water in the culvert" on culvert {
    State shallow "The brook runs ankle-deep under the road-wall, clear and cold, and the culvert is a crawl through silt.".
    State flowing dangerous "The brook is running full and fast through the culvert, brown with silt, and it will take anyone that goes in.".
    Hurts with race_cold when flowing then flowing.
  }
  Hazard race_cold "The cold fast water of the race" means "Deal (1d6) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (12).".
  Rule race_floods when state(wheel_drain, open) and state(culvert_water, shallow) says "Far below, the drain roars, and the water that was in the Drowned Level comes out into the race, and into the brook." { Assert state(culvert_water, flowing). }
  Rule race_ebbs when state(wheel_drain, stopped) and state(culvert_water, flowing) { Assert state(culvert_water, shallow). }

  // --- the sluice-race ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe race_scene at race when true "A brick channel the width of a cart-track, roofed, running along a slope; the brook runs in from the daylight at one end and a grating takes it into the Drowned Level at the other. The air is cold, the sound of the water filling the whole length of it. In the roof, at intervals, a lamp-niche is cut, with the stub of something in it.".
  Observe race_wheel at race as sign when true "On the wall beside the grating, a small iron plate: the figure of a roofed house with a lamp in it, and an arrow going away. Under it, in the survey's chalk, a drawing of a bucket, with a question-mark.".

  // --- the Roots ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe roots_scene at roots when true "Terraced beds go down in tiers as far as the light does, black with the soil of a thousand harvests and run to green wilderness: wheat gone tall as a man, vines through the rafters, fruit-trees lying where they fell with new trees standing up out of them. A pale light comes from below, from a pool the colour of milk, and in it everything that grows throws a shadow upward.".
  Observe roots_air at roots as sign when true "The air is warm and wet and smells of leaf-mould, and a faint high note comes from everywhere at once: a thousand insects tuning. Overhead, a vent in the vault turns slowly in a draught.".
  Discovery stair_found "Behind a bed of tall wheat, a narrow stair of worn brick climbs into the wall." { Found by searching roots "Behind a bed of tall wheat, where the stalks lean away from the wall in a pattern that is not wind, there is a low arch, and inside it a narrow stair going up.". }
  Person beetles "the beetles" at roots {
    Role "great black beetles, as long as a dog". Species beetle. Variant great. Numbers 3. Level 2. Temperament territorial.
    Warns "The wheat rustles, and three great beetles come out of it on slow glittering legs: each as long as a dog, each with a pair of mandibles that can be heard opening. They have been fed here a long time, on what the beds let fall, and they do not know you from what the beds let fall.".
    Comes "The beetles come all at once, clicking.".
  }
  Thing vent_wheel "the vent-wheel by the vault door" at roots {
    State stopped "A bronze wheel on a spindle stands by the vault door, linked by a rod to the vent in the vault above. It is shut.".
    State open "The vent-wheel is turned wide; overhead the vent stands open and the draught runs past you, into the vault.".
    Change turn_vent "Turn the vent-wheel" from stopped to open needing brawn.
  }
  Thing vault_air "the air in the vault door" on vault_door {
    State foul dangerous "The air behind the vault door is dead; there is a smell of old fruit and of nothing, and the lamp flame leans away from it.".
    State clean "The air behind the vault door moves, and smells only of dry seed.".
    Hurts with dead_air when foul then foul.
  }
  Hazard dead_air "Air with nothing in it" means "Deal (1d8) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (13).".
  Rule vault_vents when state(vent_wheel, open) and state(vault_air, foul) says "The draught from the vent runs into the vault; there is a sigh, a long rush, as the air in it changes." { Assert state(vault_air, clean). }
  Observe vault_scene at vault when true "A dry vault of iron shelves, each with a hundred cells, and each cell with a screw-top jar of green glass in it, and each jar with a numeral and a leaf pressed behind its glass. A sealed room, kept cool and dry for something to come back to.".
  Item seed_a "a jar of seed" is seed_kind at vault.
  Item seed_b "a jar of seed" is seed_kind at vault.
  Kind seed_kind "a jar of the House's seed" is treasure worth 35 weighing 1 described "A jar of green glass with a screw top, a leaf pressed behind the glass, and a numeral. The seed inside is dry, grey, and heavier than it ought to be. The numeral is a count of how many years it has been kept; the number is not one the Empire could have written.".

  // --- the pool ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe pool_scene at pool when true "A round pool, twenty paces across, lit from within, white as milk, and the light that comes out of it lays the shadow of everything that grows upward on the walls. Crystals as thick as a thigh stand round its rim, glowing faintly. The surface is perfectly still, and there is a sweetness in the air that has nothing to do with the bell-lilies.".
  Item shard "a shard of living crystal" is shard_kind at pool.
  Kind shard_kind "a shard of living crystal" like lantern described "A shaft of clear crystal the length of a hand, that gives a soft steady light without flame or oil, and is cool to the touch. In the dark it casts a shadow upward.".
  Person slump "the slump" at pool {
    Role "a pale mass, drifting in the pool's shallows". Species slump. Level 2. Temperament territorial.
    Warns "Something in the shallows of the pool shifts. It is the colour of the pool and almost its shape, and it draws itself up out of the water in a slow glistening column, and leans toward you.".
    Comes "The slump comes out of the pool at you, in a rush like a wave.".
  }
}

data/situations/arcology/entry.kyr:
Module arcology "The Numbered House" {
  // Three parties have been here before the company, and none of them agrees about the stair: the Empire's surveyors
  // (who chalked what they were told and wrote a tablet that the road must go round), a monastic party (who cut a
  // ladder to the Ledge and then cut it down again), and someone this decade, who left a lantern-tin. Each of them
  // wrote down the order of the stair's plates; only one of them wrote it down right, and which one depends on the
  // country (Deem draws it).
  Kind seqpat. Entity pat_a: seqpat "the surveyors' order". Entity pat_b: seqpat "the monks' order". Entity pat_c: seqpat "the tin's order".
  Relation pattern(thing, seqpat). Relation stepOne(seqpat, thing). Relation stepTwo(seqpat, thing). Relation stepThree(seqpat, thing).
  Relation plate(thing). Measure progress(thing). Measure offered(group). Measure errors(group).
  Kind voicekind. Entity voice_chime: voicekind "a chime". Entity voice_rasp: voicekind "a rasp". Entity voice_hush: voicekind "a hush".
  Relation voiced(group, voicekind).

  // --- the Bend ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe bend_green at outside when true "What the folk call the fallen walls are the lips of terraces sunk under turf: course on course of dressed stone, each set a little back from the one below, climbing the hillside until the hill takes them. The old road comes up out of the country straight as a rule for a mile, and here it bends once, hard, round all that green, as if round a sleeper.".
  Observe bend_hum at outside as felt when true "Lay a palm on the kerb and the stone is not quite still. It is a hum too low to hear, like a cart passing a mile off on a road that has no cart on it.".
  Thing bend_stone "the milestone at the Bend" at outside {
    State unread "A milestone stands at the kerb with two counts cut on it, one beneath the other. The upper count has been struck through with a chisel; the lower is eight miles more.".
    State read "The upper count is the road as the Posts laid it, straight; the lower is the road as they were made to lay it, and the difference is the Bend. Under both, in a smaller and later hand: NOT TO BE STRAIGHTENED.".
    Change read "Read the figures on the milestone" from unread to read needing lore.
  }
  Observe bend_felt at outside as sign when state(bend_stone, unread) "Someone has been at the milestone with a chisel who meant it, and has cut a third line beneath the two, and a fourth over that, and then given up.".

  // --- the Landing ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe landing_scene at landing when true "A broad shelf of dressed stone runs along the foot of the terraces, wide enough to turn a post-wagon, and behind it stand doors three times the height of a man, the colour of old brass. One has swung a hand's breadth open. Warm air comes out of the gap, smelling of oil and rain-wet metal.".
  Observe landing_gone at landing as sign when true "Three parties have stood here before you. Chalk covers the wall by the doors; the stumps of a ladder lean against the face; a flat tin lies under the lintel with its lid sprung.".
  Thing survey_chalk "the survey party's chalk" at landing {
    State unread "Chalk covers the wall by the doors in a clerk's tidy hand, gone pale with weather. Near the top, nine upright strokes with a tenth laid across them, and beside the tenth a little loop of cord. Lower down, a row of three marks, bar-bar, bar-bar-bar, bar, and beside them the drawing of a flight of steps with three discs set in its lowest tread, each carrying bars of its own.".
    State read "The chalk reads, in the Empire's numerals: NINE ENTERED, ONE LED. TEN COUNTED. THE ASS REMAINS WITHOUT. Under it: THE THREE DISCS OF THE FIRST TREAD STRUCK IN THE ORDER OF THE FIGURES, TWO, ONE, THREE; AND BY THE SMALL DISC, HIGH; BY THE GREAT, LOW. And lower: DO NOT STAND ON THE DECK WITH MORE THAN THE POSTED LIMIT. WE WERE TOLD TO COUNT AND TO GO ROUND. WE COUNTED.".
    Change read "Read the survey party's chalk" from unread to read needing lore.
  }
  Discovery cairn_here "The survey party left things under the cairn by the doors." { Found by searching landing "Under the top stone of the survey's cairn there is a bronze tablet, and a plate of polished metal on a hinge.". }
  Item prefect_tablet "the Prefect's tablet" is prefect_kind at landing hidden until cairn_here.
  Item mirror "the surveyors' signal-plate" is arcology_mirror_kind at landing hidden until cairn_here.
  Item chalk_stub "a stub of the survey's chalk" is chalk at landing hidden until cairn_here.
  Kind prefect_kind "the Prefect's tablet" is document teaching detour_order worth 30 weighing 2 described "A bronze tablet the size of a hand, closed with a seal of lead stamped with a wheel and a wing. It orders the road round the Works, forbids a stage to be built within nine miles, and enjoins that no officer of the Posts enter or number what is within. It is signed with the Office of the Road's mark and no name.".
  Discovery detour_order "The Office of the Road ordered the Posts to carry the road round the Works and to build no stage near it; whether to keep people out, or something in, the tablet does not say.".
  Kind arcology_mirror_kind "the surveyors' signal-plate" is gear worth 4 weighing 1 described "A hinged plate of polished bronze, bright still, with a sighting-slot cut through its middle. The Posts used them to send a word down the road by sunlight; held to a lantern, one throws a hard small spot a long way.".

  Thing ledge_way "the goat-path" on ledge_up {
    State plain "A goat-path zigzags up the face from the shelf: ledges the width of a boot, and a few iron staples hammered into the rock by someone who wanted to get up without passing under the doors.".
  }

  // --- the Goat Ledge ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe ledge_scene at ledge when true "The Ledge is the width of a cart-track, cut along the cliff by something that never meant it for walking, and ravens use it. Below, the shelf and the road; ahead, the green flank of the hill running away to the north, and in the flank, where the turf has slipped, a curved wall of dark metal pitted red, rising out of the hillside for the length of a village.".
  Observe ledge_hull at ledge as feature when true "The wall is rust and old paint, riveted in courses as high as a house, and it does not stop where the turf does: it goes on under the hill. Scratched into the rock beside it in the Empire's hand: HVLL, struck through; HILL, written over; and beneath, too faint to read, a third attempt." teaches hull_seen.
  Discovery hull_seen "Under the green flank of the hill, a curved wall of riveted metal runs on for the length of a village; the Empire's surveyors argued over whether to call it a hull or a hill.".
  Person goats "the ledge-goats" at ledge {
    Role "wild goats, sure-footed". Species goat. Numbers 3. Peaceable.
    State grazing "Three goats graze the Ledge, as unconcerned as if it were a meadow, and one stands on the lip of the third balcony with all four feet on it, chewing, looking at you.".
  }
  Observe goats_tracks at ledge as sign noticed by woodcraft when true "The droppings on the Ledge are old and new together, and the hoof-marks go up and down the Narrow Stair in two lines, one deep, one light: the goats are carrying nothing, and something heavier than a goat goes up it every few days, and comes down. The deep prints are not a man's.".
  Observe goats_sign at ledge as sign when true "Where the Ledge stairs go on to the terraces, the goats go up and down them without looking at their feet. Whatever else is wrong with the Narrow Stair, it carries a goat's weight, and a heavy one.".

  // --- the Lodge, and the Count --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe lodge_scene at lodge when true "Behind the brass doors a long hall runs back into the dark, its floor worn into a shallow trough by the feet of people who queued here. A rail of brass posts, the height of a waist, makes a lane down the middle of it. At the end of the lane stands a taller post with a dial in its face, and beyond it a stair rises out of the floor.".
  Person usher "the Usher" at lodge {
    Role "the keeper of the Lodge". Species automaton. Level 2. Temperament obedient. Lair lodge. Guards counting_stair.
    Warns "At the end of the lane a figure of riveted brass plates turns its lamp-glass eyes on you. It stands across the stair and does not move. A voice comes out of the dial in the post, and the chime goes through you like a bell struck under a bowl: ARE YOU COUNTED?" when voiced(usher, voice_chime).
    Warns "At the end of the lane a figure of riveted brass plates turns its lamp-glass eyes on you. It stands across the stair and does not move. A rasp comes out of the dial, like a file drawn along a saw, and makes a word of itself: ARE YOU COUNTED?" when voiced(usher, voice_rasp).
    Warns "At the end of the lane a figure of riveted brass plates turns its lamp-glass eyes on you. It stands across the stair and does not move. The word comes as a hush, very close, as if someone had leaned out of the dark and said it into your ear: ARE YOU COUNTED?" when voiced(usher, voice_hush).
    Comes "The Usher steps off the stair and comes down the lane at you, as it was made to, the brass of its joints shrieking.".
    State posted blocking "The Usher stands across the foot of the stair with its hands at its sides.".
    State stood_aside "The Usher has stepped back from the stair and stands with its head a little bowed, in the attitude of a servant whose master has come.".
  }
  Thing post "the counting-post" at lodge {
    State waiting "The tall post at the end of the lane has a dial in its face, a brass tray under it, and a plate of numerals; its needle rests at nothing.".
    State counted "The needle of the dial stands at the figure it was given, and the post is warm to the touch, as if it had thought about it.".
  }
  Observe post_plate at lodge of post as reading when state(post, waiting) "The plate under the dial has one line cut on it, and it is a question: HOW MANY ARE YOU, AND HOW MANY LED? It does not say which hand to count with.".
  Action give_one(actor: group, site: place) "Give the post your number: one" {
    Description "The post asks how many you are, and how many you lead.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(usher, site) and not counted(actor) and not dead(usher) and state(post, waiting).
    Time 1 minute. On success { Set offered(actor) to 1. }
    Result "You give the post your number. The needle swings and waits.".
  }
  Action give_two(actor: group, site: place) "Give the post your number: two" {
    Description "The post asks how many you are, and how many you lead.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(usher, site) and not counted(actor) and not dead(usher) and state(post, waiting).
    Time 1 minute. On success { Set offered(actor) to 2. }
    Result "You give the post your number. The needle swings and waits.".
  }
  Action give_three(actor: group, site: place) "Give the post your number: three" {
    Description "The post asks how many you are, and how many you lead.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(usher, site) and not counted(actor) and not dead(usher) and state(post, waiting).
    Time 1 minute. On success { Set offered(actor) to 3. }
    Result "You give the post your number. The needle swings and waits.".
  }
  Action give_four(actor: group, site: place) "Give the post your number: four" {
    Description "The post asks how many you are, and how many you lead.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(usher, site) and not counted(actor) and not dead(usher) and state(post, waiting).
    Time 1 minute. On success { Set offered(actor) to 4. }
    Result "You give the post your number. The needle swings and waits.".
  }
  Action give_five(actor: group, site: place) "Give the post your number: five" {
    Description "The post asks how many you are, and how many you lead.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(usher, site) and not counted(actor) and not dead(usher) and state(post, waiting).
    Time 1 minute. On success { Set offered(actor) to 5. }
    Result "You give the post your number. The needle swings and waits.".
  }
  Action give_six(actor: group, site: place) "Give the post your number: six" {
    Description "The post asks how many you are, and how many you lead.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(usher, site) and not counted(actor) and not dead(usher) and state(post, waiting).
    Time 1 minute. On success { Set offered(actor) to 6. }
    Result "You give the post your number. The needle swings and waits.".
  }
  Rule count_right when offered(party) >= 1 and not counted(party)
    and offered(party) == count(memberOf(?m, party)) + count(following(?f, party))
    says "The needle settles on the figure and the dial gives a single soft note. The Usher lifts its head. COUNTED, says the voice, and the figure steps aside from the stair with a sound of springs. Somewhere above you, very far up, a lamp that has been out for longer than the Empire has been in becomes a little less out." {
    Assert counted(party). Assert tolerates(usher, party). Assert state(usher, stood_aside). Assert state(post, counted).
    Retract warned(usher, party). Retract halts(usher, party). Set offered(party) to 0. Set errors(party) to 0.
  }
  Rule count_wrong when offered(party) >= 1 and not counted(party) and errors(party) == 0
    says "The needle jerks and falls back to nothing, and the dial gives a flat note that is somehow worse than a shout. The Usher takes one step forward. THE NUMBER IS NOT THE NUMBER, says the voice. Count again." {
    Set offered(party) to 0. Set errors(party) to 1. Increase hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock).
  }
  Rule count_wrong_twice when offered(party) >= 1 and not counted(party) and errors(party) >= 1
    says "The dial gives the flat note a second time. The Usher does not wait for a third: it comes off the stair with its arms rising, saying only COUNT, COUNT, COUNT." {
    Set offered(party) to 0. Increase hum(house) by 2. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock). Assert assails(usher, party).
  }
  Topic usher_who with usher "Ask the Usher who is permitted" when state(usher, posted) once {
    Says "The voice comes from the dial, not the figure. THE PERMITTED ARE THE COUNTED. A pause, as of a clerk finding a line. THE COUNTED ARE THOSE WHO PASS UNDER THE ARCH, AND THOSE LED. THE ASS IS NOT A HEAD. ANYTHING THAT TALKS IS.".
  }
  Topic usher_queue with usher "Ask the Usher what happens to those who are not counted" when state(usher, posted) once {
    Says "THEY WAIT, says the voice. It says nothing more for long enough that you begin to turn away. THEY WAIT FOR THEIR NUMBER. The needle turns a little, and stops. NO NUMBER HAS BEEN CALLED SINCE THE LAST ONE.".
  }

  // --- the Stair That Counts -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe stair_scene at lodge when state(treads, sounding) "The stair rises from the floor in treads of grey stone, thirty of them, each as wide as the hall. In the face of the lowest tread three bronze discs are set in a row like the heads of nails, one small, one larger, one larger still, and each is marked with bars.".
  Thing treads "the treads of the Stair That Counts" on counting_stair {
    State sounding dangerous "Each tread of the stair gives a note under the foot, and the notes are not the same from one tread to the next. Climb it as it is and the treads let go under you one by one, so that you go up it as a man goes up a landslide.".
    State stilled "The stair stands quiet, and its treads are only stone.".
    Change wedge "Wedge the discs still with the bar" from sounding to stilled needing crowbar.
    Hurts with tread_fall when sounding then sounding.
  }
  Hazard tread_fall "The treads give way underfoot" means "Deal (1d6) physical damage to ally unless dexterity save against (11).".
  Thing plate_low "the great disc in the first tread" at lodge {
    State ready "The largest of the three discs is set in the face of the first tread, marked with three bars. Struck, it would sound low.".
    State rung "The great disc is still ringing, low and long.".
    Change strike_low "Strike the great disc" from ready to rung when state(treads, sounding) "The stair is quiet already.".
  }
  Thing plate_mid "the middle disc in the first tread" at lodge {
    State ready "The middle disc of the three is set in the face of the first tread, marked with two bars.".
    State rung "The middle disc is still ringing.".
    Change strike_mid "Strike the middle disc" from ready to rung when state(treads, sounding) "The stair is quiet already.".
  }
  Thing plate_high "the small disc in the first tread" at lodge {
    State ready "The smallest of the three discs is set in the face of the first tread, marked with one bar. Struck, it would sound high.".
    State rung "The small disc is still ringing, thin and high.".
    Change strike_high "Strike the small disc" from ready to rung when state(treads, sounding) "The stair is quiet already.".
  }
  Initially Assert plate(plate_low). Initially Assert plate(plate_mid). Initially Assert plate(plate_high).
  Initially Assert stepOne(pat_a, plate_mid). Initially Assert stepTwo(pat_a, plate_high). Initially Assert stepThree(pat_a, plate_low).
  Initially Assert stepOne(pat_b, plate_low). Initially Assert stepTwo(pat_b, plate_high). Initially Assert stepThree(pat_b, plate_mid).
  Initially Assert stepOne(pat_c, plate_high). Initially Assert stepTwo(pat_c, plate_mid). Initially Assert stepThree(pat_c, plate_low).
  Rule seq_one when plate(?p) and state(?p, rung) and pattern(treads, ?q) and stepOne(?q, ?p) and progress(treads) == 0
    says "A true note, and the stair holds its breath." { Set progress(treads) to 1. Assert state(?p, ready). }
  Rule seq_two when plate(?p) and state(?p, rung) and pattern(treads, ?q) and stepTwo(?q, ?p) and progress(treads) == 1
    says "A second note answers the first, a fifth above it." { Set progress(treads) to 2. Assert state(?p, ready). }
  Rule seq_three when plate(?p) and state(?p, rung) and pattern(treads, ?q) and stepThree(?q, ?p) and progress(treads) == 2
    says "The third note goes down through the floor and comes back up the stair as a chord, and the treads settle one after another like a long sigh." {
    Set progress(treads) to 3. Assert state(?p, ready). Assert state(treads, stilled).
  }
  Rule seq_wrong when plate(?p) and state(?p, rung)
    says "The disc rings wrong. The note goes up the stair and does not come back, and through the whole hall the brass posts take it up a little, and drop it." {
    Set progress(treads) to 0. Assert state(?p, ready). Increase hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock).
  }
  Observe wear_a at lodge as sign noticed by perception when pattern(treads, pat_a) and state(treads, sounding) "Round the three discs the stone is worn in an arc, the way it is round a latch that is lifted every day. The wear is deepest by the middle disc, and the arc runs from there to the small one, and ends at the great.".
  Observe wear_b at lodge as sign noticed by perception when pattern(treads, pat_b) and state(treads, sounding) "Round the three discs the stone is worn in an arc, the way it is round a latch that is lifted every day. The wear is deepest by the great disc, and the arc runs from there to the small one, and ends at the middle.".
  Observe wear_c at lodge as sign noticed by perception when pattern(treads, pat_c) and state(treads, sounding) "Round the three discs the stone is worn in an arc, the way it is round a latch that is lifted every day. The wear is deepest by the small disc, and the arc runs from there to the middle one, and ends at the great.".
}

data/situations/arcology/halls.kyr:
Module arcology "The Numbered House" {
  // The halls of the answering: the Question Hall and its hum, the Drawer Gallery's ring, the Keepers' Bay and its
  // Marshal, the Reckoning Room at noon, the Ring-walk, and the disc.

  // --- the Question Hall ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe hall_scene at hall when true "A long hall lined from floor to vault with niches, hundreds of them, and in each niche a tablet of brass the size of a hand, with a lamp-hollow beside it, a little bowl of stone for oil. Rolling ladders stand at intervals along the walls. The floor is a plain mosaic of black and white squares laid in a pattern you almost recognise.".
  Observe hall_hum_0 at hall as sound when hum(house) == 0 "The hum is steady and low, the sound a held note makes when it is waiting for the next one.".
  Observe hall_hum_1 at hall as sound when hum(house) >= 1 and hum(house) <= 2 "The hum has risen a little, and the lamp-hollows ring faintly to it, one after another, like a row of glasses.".
  Observe hall_hum_3 at hall as sound when hum(house) == 3 "The hum has climbed a step. In the niches along the wall, the oil in the lamp-hollows stands trembling in its bowls.".
  Observe hall_hum_5 at hall as sound when hum(house) >= 5 and hum(house) <= 7 "The hum is loud enough now to feel in the teeth. Down the hall, beyond the arch, there is the dry rattle of something very large winding itself.".
  Observe hall_hum_8 at hall as sound when hum(house) >= 8 "A bell with a cracked voice strikes somewhere under the floor, and goes on striking.".
  Observe hall_tablets at hall as feature when true "Six of the tablets are not like the others. Each stands in its own niche at eye height, and each is engraved with a device: a flight of steps; a disc with a hand held under it; a notched ring; a row of dots; a door with a second door behind it; and a closed eye over a lifted hand.".
  Thing tab_steps "the tablet engraved with steps" at hall {
    State silent "The tablet engraved with a flight of steps stands in its niche, the lamp-hollow beside it dry.".
    State answered_a "The tablet with the steps has given its answer: the stair of the Lodge is struck MIDDLE, HIGH, LOW. The surveyors had it right.".
    State answered_b "The tablet with the steps has given its answer: the stair of the Lodge is struck LOW, HIGH, MIDDLE. The monks had it right.".
    State answered_c "The tablet with the steps has given its answer: the stair of the Lodge is struck HIGH, MIDDLE, LOW. The man with the lantern-tin had it right.".
    Change ask_steps "Ask the tablet marked with steps" from silent to answered_a when pattern(treads, pat_a) "The tablet is silent.".
    Change ask_steps_b "Ask the tablet marked with steps" from silent to answered_b when pattern(treads, pat_b) "The tablet is silent.".
    Change ask_steps_c "Ask the tablet marked with steps" from silent to answered_c when pattern(treads, pat_c) "The tablet is silent.".
  }
  Thing tab_disc "the tablet engraved with a disc and a hand" at hall {
    State silent "The tablet engraved with a disc and a hand stands in its niche, dry.".
    State answered "The tablet with the disc and the hand has answered: THE DISC RISES FOR THE COUNTED, WHEN THE RING IS SET TO THE LIGHT AT NOON, OR TO ANY LIGHT THROWN BY THE SURVEYORS' PLATE.".
    Change ask_disc "Ask the tablet marked with a disc and a hand" from silent to answered.
  }
  Thing tab_ring "the tablet engraved with a notched ring" at hall {
    State silent "The tablet engraved with a notched ring stands in its niche, dry.".
    State answered "The tablet with the ring has answered: THE RING OF THE DRAWERS STANDS AT {target(ring) in words}.".
    Change ask_ring "Ask the tablet marked with a notched ring" from silent to answered.
  }
  Thing tab_dots "the tablet engraved with a row of dots" at hall {
    State silent "The tablet engraved with a row of dots stands in its niche, dry.".
    State answered "The tablet with the dots has answered: THE COUNTED ARE A NUMBER, AND ONE PLACE MORE IS KEPT THAN THEY.".
    Change ask_dots "Ask the tablet marked with a row of dots" from silent to answered.
  }
  Thing tab_doors "the tablet engraved with a door and a second door" at hall {
    State silent "The tablet engraved with a door behind a door stands in its niche, dry.".
    State answered "The tablet with the doors has answered: THE HOUSE IS FOR TWO THINGS. TO HOUSE, AND TO ANSWER. WHICH WAS FIRST IS NOT ON THE ROLL.".
    Change ask_doors "Ask the tablet marked with a door behind a door" from silent to answered.
  }
  Thing tab_eye "the tablet engraved with a closed eye" at hall {
    State silent "The tablet engraved with a closed eye over a lifted hand stands in its niche. Its lamp-hollow is dry, and the stone under the niche is rubbed smooth by hands that thought better of it.".
    State answered "The closed eye has opened, a little, on a bright small light, and closed again.".
    Change ask_eye "Ask the tablet marked with a closed eye" from silent to answered.
  }
  Observe eye_read at hall of tab_eye as reading when state(tab_eye, silent) and capable(party, lore) "Under the eye, in the Empire's numerals, a gloss in a later hand: THE QUESTION OF THE LAST COUNT IS NOT TO BE ASKED. THE HOUSE DOES NOT KNOW THE ANSWER AND CANNOT BEAR NOT TO.".
  Relation heard(thing).
  Rule steps_a when state(tab_steps, answered_a) and not heard(tab_steps) says "The lamp-hollow beside the tablet fills with a pale oil that was not there, and the brass hums an order of three notes: middle, high, low." { Assert heard(tab_steps). Increase hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock). }
  Rule steps_b when state(tab_steps, answered_b) and not heard(tab_steps) says "The lamp-hollow beside the tablet fills with a pale oil that was not there, and the brass hums an order of three notes: low, high, middle." { Assert heard(tab_steps). Increase hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock). }
  Rule steps_c when state(tab_steps, answered_c) and not heard(tab_steps) says "The lamp-hollow beside the tablet fills with a pale oil that was not there, and the brass hums an order of three notes: high, middle, low." { Assert heard(tab_steps). Increase hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock). }
  Rule disc_heard when state(tab_disc, answered) and not heard(tab_disc) says "The tablet's lamp-hollow brightens, and a pale oil fills it, and the brass says its answer once, in a voice like a bell heard through a wall." { Assert heard(tab_disc). Increase hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock). }
  Rule ring_heard when state(tab_ring, answered) and not heard(tab_ring) says "The tablet's lamp-hollow brightens, and a pale oil fills it; the brass says its answer, and on the last word hums for a moment out of tune, as if the number were an effort." { Assert heard(tab_ring). Increase hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock). }
  Rule dots_heard when state(tab_dots, answered) and not heard(tab_dots) says "The row of dots on the tablet brightens one by one, counting, and stops one dot beyond what you would have said." { Assert heard(tab_dots). Increase hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock). }
  Rule doors_heard when state(tab_doors, answered) and not heard(tab_doors) says "The brass says its answer in two voices, slightly apart, as if two people had been asked and had agreed on nothing else." { Assert heard(tab_doors). Increase hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock). }
  Rule eye_heard when state(tab_eye, answered) and not heard(tab_eye) says "For one moment the whole hall goes still. Then the hum comes up out of the floor all at once, like a held breath let go, and in the niches, every lamp-hollow fills with oil and burns." { Assert heard(tab_eye). Increase hum(house) by 4. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock). }
  Observe steps_taught at hall as reading when state(tab_steps, answered_a) or state(tab_steps, answered_b) or state(tab_steps, answered_c) "There is no ambiguity in it. The tablet has settled the matter of the stair.".
  Observe heads_taught at hall of tab_dots as reading when state(tab_dots, answered) "The dots stand in their row, and there is one more than your party and the House together can account for." teaches place_kept.
  Discovery place_kept "The tablets say that one place more is kept than the counted number.".
  Observe doors_taught at hall of tab_doors as reading when state(tab_doors, answered) "Two answers, each given as the whole truth: the House is a dwelling, and the House is an engine of answers, and the record does not say which it was made to be first." teaches purpose_known.
  Discovery purpose_known "The tablets say the House was made to house and to answer, and that which came first is not recorded.".

  // The hum falls an hour at a time; what is asked, and what is rung wrongly, raises it.
  Rule hum_falls when hum(house) >= 1 and humAt(house) + 6 <= watch(clock) { Decrease hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock). }

  Person keepers "the keepers" at hall {
    Role "bookkeepers who outlived their books". Species automaton. Level 2. Numbers 3. Lair hall. Peaceable.
    Warns "Three figures of brass plate have stepped out of their niches and stand across the hall, shoulder to shoulder. Their lamp-glass eyes are lit. One of them says, quite gently, in the voice of the Lodge: YOU ARE NOT YET COUNTED, OR YOU HAVE SPOKEN TOO LOUD. LEAVE THE HALL.".
    Comes "The keepers come at you down the hall in step, as they were made to.".
    State niched "In the niches along the wall, three tall figures of brass plate stand among the tablets, their lamp-glass eyes dark, so still that you took them for statuary.".
    State posted "The keepers stand across the arches in a line, their eyes lit, their hands at their sides.".
  }
  Rule keepers_post when hum(house) >= 4 and peaceable(keepers) and state(keepers, niched) and not tolerates(keepers, party)
    says "Down the hall, the lamp-glass of three pairs of eyes comes alight. The figures in the niches step out of them, in step, and take their places across the arches, with their hands at their sides. They have not been told to attack anyone yet." {
    Assert state(keepers, posted).
  }
  Rule keepers_turn when hum(house) >= 6 and peaceable(keepers) and state(keepers, posted) and not tolerates(keepers, party) {
    Retract peaceable(keepers). Assert temperament(keepers, temper_obedient).
  }
  Rule keepers_stand_down when hum(house) <= 2 and state(keepers, posted) and not assails(keepers, party)
    says "The hum falls, and with it the lights in the keepers' eyes. They turn, one after another, and go back to their niches." {
    Assert peaceable(keepers). Retract temperament(keepers, temper_obedient). Assert state(keepers, niched). Retract warned(keepers, party).
  }
  Rule keepers_key when holding(party, winding_key_kind) and not tolerates(keepers, party) { Assert tolerates(keepers, party). Assert tolerates(usher, party). Assert tolerates(marshal, party). }
  Rule counted_keepers when counted(party) and not tolerates(keepers, party) { Assert tolerates(keepers, party). Assert tolerates(marshal, party). }

  // --- the Drawer Gallery --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe drawers_scene at drawers when true "A gallery of drawers, floor to roof, each with a brass face and a number, and rolling ladders on rails to reach the high ones. A reading-desk stands in the middle of it with a book chained open on the slope. One bank of drawers has a notched ring fixed in the middle of its face, as big as a dinner-plate.".
  Observe drawers_wet at drawers when water(house, wet_high) "The lowest rows stand a hand in water, and the brass has gone green; damp has got into the numbering, and a few of the drawers have swelled shut.".
  Observe drawers_dry at drawers when water(house, wet_low) "The air is as dry as a held breath. The brass faces of the drawers are bright, and the paper in the open ones has gone brittle at the edges, and curled.".
  Measure notch(entity). Measure target(entity). Relation pressed(thing).
  Initially Set notch(ring) to 1. Initially Set target(ring) to (1d5+1).
  Thing ring "the notched ring on the drawer-face" at drawers {
    State fixed "A ring of bronze is set in the middle of the drawer-face, cut with six notches round its rim and a mark on the face that the notches pass under. It stands at {notch(ring) in words}.".
  }
  Thing drawer "the drawer of the ring" at drawers {
    Holds.
    State locked closed "The drawer behind the ring is shut. The ring can be turned a notch at a time, and pressed home.".
    State jammed closed "The ring has been pressed home wrong, and the drawer has jammed with a click like a tongue.".
    State open "The drawer has slid open on its runners.".
    Change force_drawer "Prise the jammed drawer" from jammed to open needing crowbar.
  }
  Item governor "the lift's governor" is governor_kind in drawer.
  Kind governor_kind "a brass governor" is gear worth 20 weighing 3 described "A drum of bronze the size of a pumpkin, geared at its rim, with a spindle in its middle and a spring inside. The ring on its housing is stamped with a figure, and the figure is the number of the lift.".
  Action turn_ring(actor: group, site: place) "Turn the ring one notch" {
    Description "The ring clicks round a notch at a time.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(drawer, site) and state(drawer, locked).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Increase notch(ring) by 1. }
    Result "The ring clicks round one notch.".
  }
  Rule ring_wraps when notch(ring) >= 7 { Set notch(ring) to 1. }
  Action press_ring(actor: group, site: place) "Press the ring home" {
    Description "Press on the ring at whatever notch it stands.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(drawer, site) and state(drawer, locked).
    Time 1 minute.
    On success { Assert pressed(drawer). }
    Result "You lean on the ring.".
  }
  Rule ring_opens when pressed(drawer) and notch(ring) == target(ring)
    says "The ring goes home with a sound like a latch lifting, and the drawer slides out on its runners, smooth as milk." { Assert state(drawer, open). Retract pressed(drawer). }
  Rule ring_jams when pressed(drawer) and notch(ring) != target(ring)
    says "The ring goes home with a flat clank, and every drawer in the gallery shudders in its bank. The one before you jams. The hum climbs." {
    Assert state(drawer, jammed). Retract pressed(drawer). Increase hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock). Set jamAt(drawer) to watch(clock).
  }
  Measure jamAt(entity).
  Rule ring_unjams when state(drawer, jammed) and jamAt(drawer) + 6 <= watch(clock) says "The drawer's jam lets go with a click, and the ring stands free again." { Assert state(drawer, locked). }
  Observe monks_2 at drawers as sign when target(ring) == 2 "Scratched on the brass beside the ring, in a rough hand, a column of figures with a line through each: THREE, FOUR, SIX. They tried them in order, and the drawer jammed, and a monk wrote the next beside it.".
  Observe monks_3 at drawers as sign when target(ring) == 3 "Scratched on the brass beside the ring, in a rough hand, a column of figures with a line through each: TWO, FIVE, SIX. They tried them in order, and the drawer jammed, and a monk wrote the next beside it.".
  Observe monks_4 at drawers as sign when target(ring) == 4 "Scratched on the brass beside the ring, in a rough hand, a column of figures with a line through each: TWO, THREE, SIX. They tried them in order, and the drawer jammed, and a monk wrote the next beside it.".
  Observe monks_5 at drawers as sign when target(ring) == 5 "Scratched on the brass beside the ring, in a rough hand, a column of figures with a line through each: TWO, THREE, FOUR. They tried them in order, and the drawer jammed, and a monk wrote the next beside it.".
  Observe monks_6 at drawers as sign when target(ring) == 6 "Scratched on the brass beside the ring, in a rough hand, a column of figures with a line through each: TWO, FOUR, FIVE. They tried them in order, and the drawer jammed, and a monk wrote the next beside it.".
  Thing roll "the Roll" at drawers {
    State open "A book as long as a man is tall is chained open on the slope of the desk. Its pages are ruled in columns of names, in a hundred hands, and the last page written is a name in no script and a number. The next line is ruled, and empty, and the chain that holds the book has a loop of chalk-dust at its end, as if chalk had been kept there.".
    State entered "The Roll has your names in it, in your own hands, in chalk. It is the first thing in the gallery that has changed in a long time, and the ruled line below yours is waiting.".
    Change enter "Write the company's names in the Roll, in chalk" from open to entered needing chalk.
  }
  Rule roll_counts when state(roll, entered) and not counted(party) says "The chalk takes. The page drinks it, and a thin bright line goes down the column and out of the book and into the floor, and somewhere a long way off a catch drops. A bell, so far below that it has to be a thought, strikes once." {
    Assert counted(party). Assert rolled(house). Assert tolerates(keepers, party). Assert tolerates(marshal, party). Assert tolerates(usher, party). Increase hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock).
  }
  Observe drawers_ladder at drawers when true "A rolling ladder on its rail stands at the foot of a stair that goes up to the rim of the Great Void, a hundred feet of light and air above, to which it is joined by a long unrailed catwalk.".

  // --- the Keepers' Bay ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe bay_scene at bay when true "A long low vault, floored in iron plate, with bays along both walls like stalls in a stable. Each is empty but one. In the last, a figure the height of a door and twice as wide stands with a spear at the slope, perfectly still, in a coat of riveted plate. A key the length of an arm projects from its back.".
  Person marshal "the Marshal" at bay {
    Role "a soldier of springs". Species clockwork_soldier. Level 1. Lair bay. Peaceable.
    Warns "The Marshal has turned, and it is wound. The spear comes down from the slope to the guard with a ratcheting sound like a hundred clocks all being struck at once, and the key in its back turns, slowly, once. It stands across the way. Whatever speaks in it speaks with the voice of the Lodge, but very close, like a second breath behind your own: NOT COUNTED. NOT COUNTED. NOT COUNTED.".
    Comes "The Marshal comes. It does not run, and nothing in the hall is as fast as it.".
    State dormant "The Marshal stands in the last bay of the vault, unmoving, its spear at the slope, its coat of plate stained red at the joints. A great winding-key projects from its back, a hand's breadth from the plate, and turns, now and then, a few degrees, as if the thing were breathing.".
    State roused "The Marshal stands in the way with its spear levelled.".
    State wound_down "The Marshal stands as it did, but the key is out of its back, and the stillness is a different thing: not waiting, only done.".
  }
  Action pull_key(actor: group, site: place) "Draw the winding-key out of the Marshal's back" {
    Description "A slow, quiet, close thing to do; the Marshal is still enough to be mistaken for a statue, and is not.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(marshal, site) and state(marshal, dormant) and capable(actor, stealth).
    Time 10 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert state(marshal, wound_down). Assert peaceable(marshal). Give winding_key_kind to actor. }
    On failure { Increase hum(house) by 3. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock). }
    Result "You draw the key out of the Marshal's back, a quarter-turn at a time, between its breaths. It comes free with a small sound like a tooth, and the thing's spring runs down with a long soft shudder, and then you are only holding a key.".
    Otherwise "Your hand slips, and the key chatters in its socket. The whole vault answers it. The Marshal does not move, but a long way off the hum comes up another note.".
  }
  Kind winding_key_kind "the Marshal's winding-key" is gear worth 30 weighing 4 described "A key as long as your arm, of black iron worn bright along its shank, with a bit like a tiny tower. The bow is a plain ring, worn thin by one hand, and cut on its inner edge with a single numeral that the Lodge's post also uses.".
  Rule marshal_wakes when hum(house) >= 8 and peaceable(marshal) and not tolerates(marshal, party) and state(marshal, dormant)
    says "A bell with a cracked voice strikes once, far down the vault, and the key in the Marshal's back begins to turn in a hard, quick, deliberate ratchet. The spear comes down." {
    Retract peaceable(marshal). Assert temperament(marshal, temper_savage). Assert state(marshal, roused).
  }
  Rule marshal_hunts when state(marshal, roused) and able(marshal) and not tolerates(marshal, party)
    and (at(party, hall) or at(party, drawers) or at(party, bay) or at(party, reckoning)) { Assert assails(marshal, party). Bring marshal to party. }
  Rule marshal_rests when state(marshal, roused) and hum(house) == 0 and not together(marshal, party)
    says "Far off, a spring runs down, and the Marshal's key goes still." { Assert peaceable(marshal). Retract temperament(marshal, temper_savage). Retract assails(marshal, party). Assert state(marshal, dormant). Assert at(marshal, bay). }

  // --- the Reckoning Room, and the disc -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe reckoning_scene at reckoning when true "A dome, a hundred feet across, painted inside with a night sky: seven bright bodies in a belt, and a field of fainter ones, each with its numeral. In the middle of the floor, set into the stone, a ring of bronze as broad as a cart-wheel lies flat, its rim cut with a scale and a single mark. Round it, at the cardinal points, four pillars hold up a lintel on which shafts of light fall from slits in the dome.".
  Observe reckoning_morning at reckoning when hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 11 "The light comes in at a long slant from the east, and lies in bars across the floor, short of the bronze ring by a man's length and creeping toward it.".
  Observe reckoning_noon at reckoning when hour(clock) >= 11 and hour(clock) < 14 "A single shaft of light has come down from the slit in the crown of the dome, narrow as a sword, and stands upon the bronze ring, exactly on its one mark.".
  Observe reckoning_late at reckoning when hour(clock) >= 14 and hour(clock) < 21 "The light slants in from the west now, and the bars of it lie across the floor past the bronze ring, creeping away.".
  Observe reckoning_night at reckoning when dark() "No light comes down the slits. The painted sky overhead is the only sky in the room, and it is lit, faintly, from within.".
  Thing bronze_ring "the bronze ring in the floor" at reckoning {
    State unset "The bronze ring lies flat in the floor, its single mark pointing at the north pillar. A scale runs round its rim.".
    State set "The bronze ring has been turned till its mark lies where the light falls. Beneath it, something in the floor has started to hum on a single note.".
    Change set_noon "Turn the ring until its mark meets the shaft of light" from unset to set when hour(clock) >= 11 and hour(clock) < 14 "The light does not lie on the mark. There is nothing for the ring to meet.".
    Change set_mirror "Throw lamplight onto the ring's mark with the surveyors' plate" from unset to set needing arcology_mirror_kind when capable(party, light) "The plate has nothing to throw without a light.".
  }
  Thing disc "the floating disc" on disc_way {
    State resting blocking "A disc of pale stone as wide as a table lies on the floor of a round well in the middle of the room, level with it, like a lid.".
    State risen "The disc of pale stone floats a hand above the lip of its well, perfectly level, with nothing under it, and the light of the dome slides across its face as across water. Cut round its rim, in the Empire's numerals: TAKE ONLY WHAT WAS COUNTED.".
  }
  Rule disc_rises when state(bronze_ring, set) and state(disc, resting) says "The hum under the floor falls into step with the light, and the disc comes up out of its well and hangs a hand above it, quite still." { Assert state(disc, risen). }
  Observe disc_cut at reckoning of disc as reading when state(disc, risen) and capable(party, lore) "The cut letters round the disc are in the Empire's numerals: TAKE ONLY WHAT WAS COUNTED, and under them, smaller, in the later hand: THE HOUSE LIKES THE NUMBER TO COME OUT.".

  // --- the Ring-walk ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe ring_scene at ring_walk when true "The roof of the House is a broad flat walk with a parapet, a hundred feet above the road. Above and ahead, so close that it seems to lean on the sky, a great ring stands on edge in the air, broad as a river and the colour of pewter, tilted against the cloud as if it were a coin dropped on a table. It does not turn. It does not seem to have anything to turn on.".
  Observe ring_city at ring_walk when not dark() "Beneath the ring, in a drowned plain, a city of spires and domes stands in clear water to its windows: broken viaducts over waterfalls, ivy on the slabs, mist, golden cloud. It is perhaps two days away. It is the colour of a place nobody has been to for a long time, and you have a distinct feeling that somebody has looked at you from it." teaches ring_seen.
  Discovery ring_seen "Beyond the roof of the House, a great ring stands on edge in the sky over a drowned city of spires and domes.".
  Observe ring_dark at ring_walk when dark() "In the dark the ring has a pale thin light of its own, and a few of the towers beneath it are lit.".
}

data/situations/arcology/kept.kyr:
Module arcology "The Numbered House" {
  // The kept floor: the one place in the House where nothing is wrong, and the long way home.

  Observe quiet_scene at quiet when true "A long hall with a floor of pale wood, swept. The lamps in their brackets are trimmed and lit, and burn with the steady unflinching light of a flame that has never been moved by a draught. There is no dust. Along both walls are doors with numbers on them, each door painted, each with a mat, and the mats are straight.".
  Observe quiet_air at quiet as sign when true "It smells of beeswax and bread and clean linen, and of something under them that is very faint and very sweet. Nobody else is here. Everything is ready for somebody.".
  Observe quiet_doors at quiet as feature when true "The doors are not locked. Behind each is a room with a bed made up, a lamp trimmed, a basin filled and a towel folded over the rail; behind the last, the bed has been slept in once, and made again.".
  Person steward "the Host" at quiet {
    Role "the steward of the kept floor". Species automaton. Level 1. Peaceable. Pronouns it.
    Greets "A figure of white enamel and brass, in a folded apron, comes down the hall to meet you with the unhurried walk of someone who has done it every day. It bows from the middle. 'You are expected,' it says. 'There is a table laid.'" when counted(party).
    Greets "A figure of white enamel and brass, in a folded apron, comes down the hall to meet you with the unhurried walk of someone who has done it every day. It bows from the middle. 'You are not on the Roll,' it says, without reproach. 'There is a place kept. Come and sit down.'" when not counted(party).
    Greets again "The Host bows from the middle. 'Welcome back,' it says. 'Your places are as you left them.'".
    State serving "The Host stands in the hall with its hands folded, waiting to be of use.".
  }
  Topic host_what with steward "Ask the Host what this floor is for" when true once {
    Says "'It is kept,' says the Host, as one would say the sky is up. 'Each one that is counted has a place here, and the place is laid. If they do not come, the place is laid again.' It looks at you with its lamp-glass eyes, mild as milk. 'No one has come for a long time. I am very glad you are here.'".
  }
  Topic host_who with steward "Ask the Host who it is keeping the places for" when true once {
    Says "'For the counted,' it says. And then, after a pause that is the length of a held breath: 'There is one more place than there are counted. I have kept it too. I do not know whose it is.' It folds its hands the other way. 'I have been asked not to ask.'".
  }
  Topic host_last with steward "Ask the Host when the last count was made" when true once {
    Says "The Host does not answer. It stands perfectly still. A lamp in the hall gutters, for no reason, and goes on; then another. 'That question is not permitted,' it says, and its voice has something in it that was not in it before, a kind of fear that has been polished down for a very long time. 'Will you sit down?'".
    On discuss { Increase hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock). }
  }
  Observe laid_scene at table_room when true "A round table laid for a meal, in a room with no corners. The cloth is white; the plates are white; the lamps are lit, and the bread on the board is warm, and steam rises from a bowl at the head. Chairs stand round it, each with a folded napkin, and each napkin has a number embroidered on it in thread the colour of the lamp.".
  Observe laid_extra at table_room as sign when true "One chair stands a little apart from the rest, at the foot, with a napkin folded over its back instead of laid. The plate in front of it is as clean as the others, and has never had a crumb on it.".
  Thing table "the laid table" at table_room {
    State laid "The table is laid and the food is hot.".
    State eaten "You have eaten at the table, and it has not changed. The bread on the board is whole.".
    Change eat "Sit down and eat what is laid" from laid to eaten when counted(party) "The Host stands at your shoulder. 'You are not on the Roll,' it says, kindly. 'I cannot seat you. Not yet.'".
  }
  Rule table_feeds when state(table, eaten) and not tenant(party) says "The food is good. It is the first meal you have eaten in a long while that did not have to be paid for. A warmth goes through you, and an ease you had forgotten you were missing, and when you rise the napkin by your plate has your name on it in thread." {
    Assert tenant(party). Set seatedFor(party) to count(memberOf(?m, party)). Restore party.
  }
  Observe laid_return_same at table_room when tenant(party) and seatedFor(party) == count(memberOf(?m, party)) "The table is laid for exactly as many as you are, and each napkin has a name in it that you know.".
  Observe laid_return_fewer at table_room when tenant(party) and seatedFor(party) > count(memberOf(?m, party)) "The table is laid for one more than you are. A napkin lies folded at a place no one sits at, with a name in it you know. The Host, in the doorway, does not look at it.".
  Observe laid_return_more at table_room when tenant(party) and seatedFor(party) < count(memberOf(?m, party)) "A place is missing at the table. As you watch, the Host comes from the doorway and lays another, with a napkin from a drawer, and works a name into it in thread, quickly and exactly.".
  Item spoons "the laid silver spoons" is spoon_kind at table_room.
  Kind spoon_kind "a spoon of the House" is treasure worth 15 weighing 1 described "A spoon of dull white metal, light as an eggshell, with a numeral on the handle. It does not tarnish. It has never been used, though it has been washed every day.".
  Rule spoon_owed when holding(party, spoon_kind) and not owed(party) says "The Host does not say a word. It looks at the spoon in your pack, and then at the bare place in the table where it was, and a lamp in the hall goes out and relights. A small bright coin of dread settles in you. You have taken something that was counted." {
    Assert owed(party). Increase hum(house) by 1. Set humAt(house) to watch(clock).
  }
  Relation squared(group).
  Rule spoon_squared when squared(party) { Retract owed(party). Retract squared(party). }
  Topic host_account with steward "Settle the account for the spoon" when owed(party) and holding(party, spoon_kind) once {
    Says "You put the spoon on the Host's palm. It closes its fingers over it, and bows, and carries it away, and returns with its hands empty, and the table at your back is, somehow, laid again. 'The account is settled,' says the Host. 'Thank you.'".
    On discuss { Spend spoons from party. Assert squared(party). }
  }

  // --- the Service Way ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Observe service_scene at serviceway when true "A narrow passage of brick, arched, running away into the dark. Lamp-niches are cut in the wall at every ten paces, and in every niche is a lamp trimmed and unlit, in rows, away and away. The floor is worn into a shallow channel down the middle by the feet of people who carried things, and there is a draught from the far end that smells of rain.".
  Observe service_plan at serviceway as feature when capable(party, lore) "On the wall beside the door, a plan cut into a bronze plate: a line of tunnel, a house at one end, and at the other end a fork. One branch ends at a cliff, and a door. The other goes under hills a very long way to a small square marked with the figure of a roofed house with a lamp in it. The lamp-niches along it are numbered, one to a mile, and the last is eleven." teaches slab_known_plan.
  Discovery slab_known_plan "The Service Way forks at the cliff door: one branch to the far side of the hill, and one under the hills for eleven miles to a roofed house with a lamp.".
  Discovery slab_known "At the end of the Service Way, a slab bars the passage to a place with a lamp in it." { Found by searching cliff "At the very end of the passage, behind the cliff door, a second, narrower tunnel goes off under a slab of pale stone, with a barred hatch.". }
  Observe cliff_scene at cliff when true "The Service Way comes to an end in a broad brick chamber with a bronze door in one wall, barred from the inside with a beam of black oak as thick as a thigh, and in the floor, a slab of pale stone with a bar of its own across it. A thin cold light comes in under the door, and the smell of rain, and of fern. Water runs in a shallow channel along one wall, and goes away under the slab.".
  Thing far_bar "the beam across the cliff door" at cliff {
    State fastened "The great beam of black oak lies across the bronze door in its iron brackets, barred from the inside.".
    State lifted "The beam leans against the wall. The bronze door stands ready to open on the hillside, and the light comes in.".
    Change lift_far "Lift the beam from the bronze door" from fastened to lifted needing brawn.
  }
  Thing slab "the slab in the floor of the cliff chamber" on shrine_way {
    State fastened blocking "A slab of pale stone with a bar of its own across it lies in the floor of the chamber. Under it, by the cold draught, there is a passage going down.".
    State open "The bar is drawn and the slab stands on its edge, and a draught comes up from the passage under it, smelling of tallow, and stone, and a very small cold, far-off warmth.".
    Change lift_slab "Draw the bar and heave the slab on its edge" from fastened to open needing brawn at cliff.
  }
  Observe shrine_slab at shrine when state(slab, open) "Behind the altar, a slab in the floor that has lain level for longer than the shrine has stood is on its edge, and a draught comes up from the hole under it, warm, smelling of oil and brass.".
  Passage far_door "the bronze door onto the far side of the hill" is door between cliff and outside taking 2 hours
    opening when state(far_bar, lifted) "The bronze door will not move: it is barred from within.".
  Observe bend_door at outside as sign when true "Round the shoulder of the hill, half hidden by hazel, a door of dark bronze stands in the rock with no handle on this side, and no latch, and no keyhole. Whoever made it did not mean it to be opened from here.".
}

