data/situations/silent-lord/below.kyr:
Module silent_lord "The silent lord" {
  // ---- The way under the wall: a culvert with bad air, a crawl, and a vault older than the keep.
  Hazard bad_air "Foul air" means "Deal (1d6) physical damage to ally unless constitution save against (11).".
  Thing foul_air "the air in the culvert" on culvert {
    State foul dangerous "The air in the culvert is thick and sweetish. A flame held up in it burns blue and leans back toward the outfall.".
    State clear "The air in the culvert moves, cold and clean, from the grating toward the ditch.".
    Change prop "Prop the old grating open and let the draught through" from foul to clear needing brawn or crowbar.
    Hurts with bad_air when foul then foul.
  }
  Observe culvert_tell at drain as sign when state(foul_air, foul) "A pale stain on the roof marks where the lamp-black has been drawn, and the walls are slick and shining past the second bend. At the far end the old grating hangs half open on one hinge, and a bar would hold it.".
  Person drain_rats "the drain's rats" at drain {
    Role "rats the length of a forearm, which live in the black water". Species rat. Numbers 3. Level 1. Variant great. Temperament territorial. Lair drain.
    Warns "In the black water at the bottom of the drain, something turns over, and then three of them come up the pipe with their teeth bared, in no hurry.".
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp(drain_rats) to 40.
  Observe vault_office at vault when vault_built(office_made) "Shelves of tally-sticks run down the walls in bundles, each tied with a tag, and over the lintel is cut a wheel with a wing. The Empire kept some things below ground, and counted all of them." teaches vault_known.
  Observe vault_founders at vault when vault_built(founders_made) "Racks of spear-heads rusted solid fill the walls, and at the far end is a stone chair, its arms cut with a tower and a star. The first lords of the keep came down here to be sworn, and to count what they had." teaches vault_known.
  Observe vault_makers at vault when vault_built(makers_made) "A ring of low niches runs round a floor of pale stone inlaid with a circle of bronze studs, and each stud has a hollow worn in it. Someone sat in each niche a very long time, and moved a counter from stud to stud." teaches vault_known.
  Observe vault_door at vault as feature when true "Behind you, the old door stands open on its counterweight. It is shut from this side by a ring on a chain.".

  // ---- The solar, the chancery shelf, the sentries.
  Thing solar_letters "the letters in the tray" at solar {
    State heaped "Letters lie in a tray on the lord's table, sealed and addressed, waiting to go.".
    State read "To the court, to an abbey, to a salt-factor: each begins as the lord would begin it, each is dated since the lord was last seen at table, each is in the lord's own hand. The hand is a little better than the lord's. The ink is fresh.".
    Change read "Read the letters in the tray" from heaped to read.
  }
  Observe solar_letters_learned at solar of solar_letters as reading when state(solar_letters, read) "Somebody has been writing the lord's letters with great care, for eleven days." teaches clerk_forges.
  Thing shelf_letters "the letters on the chancery shelf" at chancery {
    State filed "A bundle of letters is tied in tape on the shelf above the table, the most recent kept on top.".
    State read "Three letters. An abbess writes that the lord's ward is well, grown, learning her letters, and eager to see her uncle at Michaelmas. A salt-factor writes that prices in the lord's march have fallen by a third since a certain lord there was liked, and might the lord care to meet him? A captain of the March writes, in a tired hand, that the ford holds and he needs two hundred men by the first frosts, and begs the lord not to ask what for.".
    Change read "Untie the letters and read them" from filed to read.
  }
  Observe shelf_learned at chancery of shelf_letters as reading when state(shelf_letters, read) "The ward is alive and at an abbey, and nobody has told her." teaches heir_sought.
  Topic sentry_watch with sentries "Ask the sentries when the watch changes" when true once {
    Says "'Dusk, midnight and dawn,' says the elder, 'and an hour in the small hours when the brazier wants seeing to. Two till three, we go down and warm our hands. The lord has never minded. The castellan has never been told.' He studies you. 'If you are going to ask me what the wall looks like in that hour, I am going to say I do not know.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, dead_watch). }
  }
  Rule watch_turns when hunted(house) and (at(party, gatehouse) or at(party, ward)) and peaceable(gatewatch)
    says "A bell begins to ring in the gatehouse. The men of the watch come out of the guardroom with their spears levelled, and they are not smiling." { Retract peaceable(gatewatch). Assert assails(gatewatch, party). Bring gatewatch to party. }
  Rule herald_catches when (state(trunk, open) or state(purse, taken)) and at(party, guest) and at(herald, guest) and peaceable(bravos)
    says "The herald comes in from the stair and stops, and looks at the trunk, and then at you. He does not say anything. The two men behind him do not need him to." { Retract peaceable(bravos). Assert assails(bravos, party). Bring bravos to party. }
  Rule trunk_noticed when state(trunk, open) and at(herald, guest) and not at(party, guest) and not trunk_seen(house) and not unmasked(house) { Assert trunk_seen(house). }
  Relation trunk_seen(group).
}

data/situations/silent-lord/court.kyr:
Module silent_lord "The silent lord" {
  // ---- The clerk. He has been writing the lord's hand for eleven days, and wants the bailiff stopped.
  Topic clerk_hay with clerk "Ask {clerk} about the hay" when true once {
    Says "{clerk} puts down his pen with the air of a man who has been waiting a week for the question. 'A woman with a lead seal,' he says, 'has been collecting what she calls dues for the keeping of the road, in the castellan's name, from three hearths-worth of the march. The castellan has not granted any such thing. Her men took a rick of the keep's hay, last Sunday, against the dues, and I have written to her three times, and she writes back that the seal is good.' His mouth is a line. 'Show me a seal that is better than hers and I will have her stopped by Thursday.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bailiff_dues). }
  }
  Topic clerk_reading with clerk "Ask {clerk} what became of the Empire" when true once {
    Says "'Nothing became of it,' says {clerk}. 'It closed. Papers were sealed, and no order calling them out was ever written, so they are, in law, still sealed.' He looks very pleased with this. 'Everyone prefers a battle. A battle you can be sorry about. A closing, you have to read.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, reading_chancery). Assert heard_out(clerk, actor). }
  }
  Thing practice "the spoiled sheets under the table" at chancery {
    State heaped "A drift of spoiled sheets lies under the end of the long table, as if someone had been tidying badly.".
    State read "Each sheet is a signature, written over and over: the lord's name, in the lord's slanting hand. The first are wild. By the bottom of the heap they are a perfect likeness.".
    Change read "Pick through the spoiled sheets" from heaped to read.
  }
  Discovery clerk_forges "The clerk has been writing the lord's signature for eleven days; the sheets under his table show him learning it.".
  Observe practice_learned at chancery of practice as reading when state(practice, read) "The same name, forty times, until it is the lord's own." teaches clerk_forges.
  Topic clerk_practice with clerk "Put the spoiled sheets to {clerk}: the lord's name, written over and over" when knows(actor, clerk_forges) and not befriended(clerk, actor) once {
    Says "{clerk} goes the colour of the paper. 'Eleven days,' he says. 'I did it because she asked, and because the alternative was to be the man who said the lord was dead and had no proof of anything.' He sits very straight. 'If you mean to take this to the herald, I will deny it to his face. If you mean to do something else, I am listening. I can write a good deal in his hand, and I know where the press key is.'".
    On discuss { Assert befriended(clerk, actor). }
  }
  Topic clerk_key with clerk "Ask {clerk} for the press key" when befriended(clerk, actor) and not holding(actor, press_key_kind) once {
    Says "He takes it from his sleeve and puts it in your hand without looking at it. 'The will and the court's spring letter are in the first shelf. The seals are in the chest by the window. Do not touch the seals.'".
    On discuss { Give press_key_kind to actor. }
  }
  Topic clerk_remission with clerk "Ask {clerk} to write a remission of the levy of men, in the lord's hand" when befriended(clerk, actor) and not holding(actor, remission_kind) once {
    Says "'On account of the winter,' says {clerk}, 'which is true in a sense nobody will check.' He writes it in one stroke, the lord's long-tailed g and all, and presses the keep's seal into the wax with the flat of his thumb. 'It will do for a crier. It would not do for a king.'".
    On discuss { Give remission_kind to actor. }
  }
  Topic clerk_order with clerk "Ask {clerk} to write a pay-order for the garrison, in the lord's hand" when befriended(clerk, actor) and not holding(actor, order_kind) and not paid_off(house) once {
    Says "'The steward is to pay the garrison its arrears,' says {clerk}, writing, 'from the strongbox, forthwith. The strongbox has forty crowns in it, the marshal can count, and it will not do for long.' He seals it. 'Better than nothing, which is what they have had.'".
    On discuss { Give order_kind to actor. }
  }
  Topic clerk_rider with clerk "Ask {clerk} to send the writ against the bailiff by his own rider" when befriended(clerk, actor) and knows(actor, bailiff_dues) and holding(actor, die_kind) and vault_built(office_made) and not rider_sent(house) once {
    Says "{clerk} turns the bronze die over in his fingers, and for a moment is no longer afraid. 'It is the right shape,' he says. 'Whatever she is using is a copy of a copy. I can seal a writ with this that the whole march will believe, and she will not believe it, and that is the difference.' He is already cutting a pen. 'There is a boy in the stable who rides like a bird. It will be at the next green before the week is out.'".
    On discuss { Assert rider_sent(house). Set riderDay(house) to day(clock) + 2. }
  }
  Topic clerk_rider_plain with clerk "Ask {clerk} to send the writ against the bailiff by his own rider, under the keep's seal" when befriended(clerk, actor) and knows(actor, bailiff_dues) and not vault_built(office_made) and not rider_sent(house) once {
    Says "{clerk} considers. 'The keep's seal is only the keep's,' he says. 'She has a seal that claims to be the Office's, and ours claims nothing but the keep. It is the weaker paper.' He is already cutting a pen. 'But she cannot read, and her men can, and I would like to see what they do with it.' A shrug. 'It will be at the next green before the week is out.'".
    On discuss { Assert rider_sent(house). Set riderDay(house) to day(clock) + 2. }
  }
  Topic clerk_die with clerk "Sell {clerk} the bronze die" when holding(actor, die_kind) and not rider_sent(house) once {
    Says "{clerk} will not touch it until he has washed his hands. 'Forty crowns,' he says, 'from the chancery's own account, which has the right to buy such things, and which I am the only man to read.' He counts it into your palm. 'I would keep it, if I were you. But I am not you, and I would not be able to sleep.'".
    On discuss { Spend die_kind from actor. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 40. }
  }

  // ---- The herald, and the court he claims to speak for.
  Topic herald_writ with herald "Ask {herald} to show you the king's writ" when true once {
    Says "{herald} unrolls it with the air of a man who has done it forty times and enjoys it every one. 'The king's hand,' he says, 'and the king's seal.' A plain crown in red wax, struck from a good die. 'Twenty spears and a hundred bushels by the twelfth, or the heir in person, and the lord at court for the feast. The lord is unwell, I am told. That is a pity. The king will hear of it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, seal_plain). }
  }
  Topic herald_court with herald "Ask {herald} what news the court has" when true once {
    Says "'A new king in his second year,' says {herald}, 'and a court that has not quite learned to sit still. The marshal of the household has the king's ear, and the queen-mother's party has the rest of him.' He drinks, delicately. 'There is a matter in the March which wants men, and nobody on the council will say what it is, which is how you know it is serious. The levy is for that. I carry it. I do not read what I carry.'".
  }
  Action put_seals(actor: group, site: place) "Lay the court's spring letter beside the herald's writ, and ask which seal is the king's" {
    Speaker herald.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(herald, site) and knows(actor, herald_false) and not unmasked(house)
      and not now(p_feast).
    Time 3 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert unmasked(house). Assert herald_goes(house). }
    On failure { Retract peaceable(bravos). Assert assails(bravos, actor). Assert hunted(house). }
    Result "{herald} looks at the two seals for a long time. 'I carry what I am given,' he says at last, quite softly. 'Whoever gave it me did not mean me to read it.' He folds his writ, and the colour has gone from his tabard. 'I will be on the road at first light.'".
    Otherwise "'My dear sir,' says {herald}, smiling, 'you have been talking to a prisoner.' He does not raise his voice. The men behind him do not need him to.".
  }
  Action buy_off(actor: group, site: place) "Offer {herald} forty crowns to ride on without reading the writ" {
    Speaker herald.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(herald, site) and not unmasked(house) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 40
      and not now(p_feast).
    Time 3 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_fair).
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 40. Increase quantity(herald, gold) by 40. Assert unmasked(house). Assert herald_goes(house). Assert herald_bought(house). }
    On failure { Assert hunted(house). Retract peaceable(bravos). Assert assails(bravos, actor). }
    Result "{herald} counts it with his eyes, and then with his fingers. 'I am a man of the court,' he says. 'I would not dream of it.' He turns away to the window. 'But I do not read well in a bad light. I shall be on the road at first light, and my master will hear the keep was most hospitable.'".
    Otherwise "{herald} sets down his cup. 'Did you mean that for a bribe?' he says, very gently, and nods once to the men by the door.".
  }
  Relation herald_goes(group). Relation herald_bought(group). Relation read_out(group). Relation poison_deed(group).
  Rule herald_leaves when herald_goes(house) and at(herald, ?p) and at(bravos, ?q) and distinct(?p, outside) and not dead(herald)
    says "The herald's baggage is carried down and out of the keep, and the herald after it, and the two men after him, with the household watching." {
    Assert occupied(herald). Assert occupied(bravos). Retract at(herald, ?p). Assert at(herald, outside). Retract at(bravos, ?q). Assert at(bravos, outside).
  }
  Rule herald_dies_unmasks when dead(herald) and not unmasked(house) { Assert unmasked(house). }

  // ---- The prisoner. The hatch is barred from above, and the marshal has the key.
  Thing hatch_bar "the bar across the oubliette hatch" on hatch {
    State barred blocking "An oak bar lies across the hatch in two iron brackets. It has been dropped with care, by someone who did not want it done twice.".
    State lifted "The bar lies on the floor, and the hatch is open.".
    Change lift "Lift the bar off the hatch" from barred to lifted needing brawn.
    Change unbar "Unbar the hatch with the oubliette key" from barred to lifted needing hatch_key_kind.
  }
  Topic captive_who with captive "Ask the prisoner who he is" when true once {
    Says "'{captive}, rider of the king's household,' he says, 'though I have not had a coat to prove it for nine days.' His voice is steady; his hands are not. 'I rode from the court with the king's writ for the lord of this keep. I was met at the ford by three men in a blue tabard who said they were going the same way. The herald's. They took my satchel and brought me in tied across a horse, and told the castellan I was a thief. She locked me in on his word.' He looks at you. 'The seal on my writ is the king's. It is a crown between two ears of wheat. His is a crown, plain. Ask the groom whose horse is whose.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, captive_story). }
  }
  Topic captive_court with captive "Ask the rider what the king is like" when knows(actor, captive_story) once {
    Says "The rider thinks. 'Younger than his portrait,' he says. 'He signs with his left hand and is ashamed of it. He listens to whoever spoke last. He sends for the lord of this keep because his father did, and because there is a war in the March he has not been told the whole of.' A bleak smile. 'I carried a great many papers from that court. I did not read one.'".
  }
  Topic captive_come with captive "Ask the rider to come out with you" when knows(actor, captive_story) and not following(captive, party) once {
    Says "{captive} gets to his feet, which takes some time. 'Where to?' he says. 'The hall, I should think. I would like to be in it when the herald next speaks.'".
    On discuss { Assert following(captive, actor). Assert freed(captive). }
  }
  Relation freed(group).

  // ---- The castellan. She is a good soldier who has been lying for eleven days.
  Topic cast_lord with castellan "Ask {castellan} when the lord will receive you" when not knows(actor, lord_dead) once {
    Says "'His lordship is unwell,' says {castellan}, 'and sees no one but his physician.' She says it very smoothly, and has plainly said it a good many times, to a good many people, and each time a little more of the skin has come off her voice. 'I sign what he cannot. The keep is in good hands.'".
  }
  Topic cast_levy with castellan "Ask {castellan} what the king's levy means for the keep" when true once {
    Says "'Twenty spears,' says {castellan}, 'of thirty-one. A hundred bushels, of what the steward tells me is a good deal more than a hundred. And the lord at court for the feast, or his heir, which I am told the herald does not think a joke.' She is looking at the window. 'I will raise what I can. I will not strip the march to fill the king's ditch in a war he cannot name.'".
  }
  Topic cast_confront with castellan "Tell {castellan} you have seen the lord on his bier" when knows(actor, lord_dead) and not heard_out(castellan, actor) and not hunted(house) once {
    Grave "What you say now, the household hears. There is no unsaying it.".
    Says "{castellan} sets her letter down and looks at you for a long time. 'Eleven days,' she says. 'The herald arrived the morning after. I thought: if I say it, the keep is his. The king's writ says the lord or the heir, and the heir is a child at an abbey, and the will has not been read by anyone with the right to read it.' Her voice is level. 'I have thirty-one men, and a steward who cannot add, and a clerk who writes better than I do. What do you want?'".
    On discuss { Assert heard_out(castellan, actor). }
  }
  Topic cast_help with castellan "Offer to help her hold the keep until the heir comes" answering cast_confront when true {
    Says "'Help,' says {castellan}, trying the word. 'No one has said it in this house for eleven days.' She takes a slender steel key from her belt and puts it in your hand. 'The second lock of the strong-room. The doorward will let you up to the solar, when you wish. Tell me what you find. I have been alone with this for a long time.'".
    On discuss { Assert befriended(castellan, actor). Give castellan_key_kind to actor. Assert tolerates(doorward, actor). }
  }
  Topic cast_price with castellan "Say you will keep quiet, for a price" answering cast_confront when true {
    Says "{castellan} does not look surprised. 'Thirty,' she says, and counts it from her own purse. 'And you will have forgotten the way down to the crypt. I would not like to find you on it twice.' She holds your eye. 'You were never here.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 30. Assert bought(castellan). }
  }
  Topic cast_hall with castellan "Say the hall must be told" answering cast_confront when true {
    Says "{castellan} stands. 'Then you are a danger to the household,' she says, without heat, and calls a name, and the doorward is there before she has finished. 'You will be shown out.'".
    On discuss { Assert hunted(house). Retract peaceable(doorward). Assert assails(doorward, actor). }
  }
  Relation bought(group).
  Topic cast_ready with castellan "Tell {castellan} the hall should hear it from her, at the feast" when befriended(castellan, actor) and knows(actor, will_read) and not castellan_ready(house) once {
    Says "She is silent a long time. 'From me,' she says. 'In front of him.' Her hand has closed on the sword-belt. 'Yes. When the second cup is poured. If the will is what the chaplain says it is, I will not need to lie again.'".
    On discuss { Assert castellan_ready(house). }
  }

  // ---- The feast. The whole household is in the hall, and so is the herald.
  Action stand_and_tell(actor: group, site: place) "Rise at the high table and tell the hall the lord is dead" {
    Grave "Said before the hall, it cannot be taken back.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hall) and now(p_feast) and knows(actor, lord_dead) and not proclaimed(house) and hour(clock) >= 21.
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert proclaimed(house). }
    On failure { Assert hunted(house). }
    Result "The hall goes quiet in rings, as water does. You say it once and plainly. Nobody moves. Then the chaplain stands, and the castellan stands, and the room breathes out.".
    Otherwise "'A stranger,' says someone, loudly, and the hall takes it up. 'A stranger at the lord's table, calling him dead.' The doorward is already coming round the dais.".
  }
  Action present_writ(actor: group, site: place) "Lay the king's own writ before the hall, beside the herald's" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hall) and now(p_feast) and (holding(actor, true_writ_kind) or holding(actor, spring_kind))
      and knows(actor, herald_false) and not unmasked(house) and hour(clock) >= 21.
    Time 2 minutes.
    On success { Assert unmasked(house). Assert herald_goes(house). }
    Result "The two seals lie side by side on the board in the torchlight, a crown and a crown between two ears of wheat, and the castellan leans over them and puts one finger on the plain one. 'This was struck before the coronation,' she says. 'Where did you have it from, sir?' The herald, who has been smiling, goes on smiling a moment longer than it can be done.".
  }
  Action name_forgery(actor: group, site: place) "Name the herald's seal a forgery before the hall, with nothing to lay beside it" {
    Grave "A man named a liar before a hall can only answer with the sword.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, hall) and now(p_feast) and knows(actor, herald_false) and not holding(actor, true_writ_kind) and not holding(actor, spring_kind)
      and not unmasked(house) and hour(clock) >= 21.
    Time 2 minutes.
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert unmasked(house). Assert herald_goes(house). }
    On failure { Assert hunted(house). Retract peaceable(bravos). Assert assails(bravos, actor). }
    Result "Your words go down the hall like a dropped plate. The herald laughs, and nobody laughs with him, and the marshal says, loudly, 'Let him show the seal,' and the herald cannot.".
    Otherwise "'Insolence,' says the herald, standing, and the hall, which has no reason to love you, does not stop him.".
  }
}

data/situations/silent-lord/feast.kyr:
Module silent_lord "The silent lord" {
  // ---- Locks the rest of the module leans on: the armoury, the crypt, and the dead lord himself.
  Thing armoury_lock "the armoury door's lock" on armoury_door {
    State locked blocking "The armoury door is locked. The marshal wears the key.".
    State open "The armoury door stands unlocked.".
    Change key "Unlock the armoury door" from locked to open needing armoury_key_kind.
    Change pick "Pick the armoury door's lock" from locked to open needing lockwork.
    Change force "Force the armoury door with a crowbar" from locked to open needing crowbar.
  }
  Initially Assert state(armoury_lock, open).
  Rule armoury_locked_at_night when state(armoury_lock, open) and (now(p_night) or now(p_dead)) and not at(party, armoury) and at(marshal, armoury) { Assert state(armoury_lock, locked). }
  Thing crypt_door "the iron door to the crypt stair" on crypt_stair {
    State locked blocking "An iron door shuts the crypt stair. It has a chapel lock, and the chaplain wears the key.".
    State open "The iron door stands open on the crypt stair.".
    Change key "Unlock the crypt door" from locked to open needing chaplain_key_kind.
    Change pick "Pick the crypt door's lock" from locked to open needing lockwork.
    Change force "Force the crypt door with a crowbar" from locked to open needing crowbar.
  }
  Observe crypt_bier at crypt as feature when true "The cloth over the bier is lifted at one corner, as by someone who comes to look and cannot stay. Under it, a man of sixty, laid out in his good coat, with his hands folded on a sword and a cord of keys across his chest. He has been dead some days, and has been kept cold, and is not at all changed." teaches lord_dead.
  Observe crypt_fall at crypt as sign when death(fall) "His collar has been undone, and the whole length of his left side is one bruise, from hip to shoulder. A man who went off a horse at a gallop, and was a long while dying of it." teaches lord_dead.
  Observe crypt_fever at crypt as sign when death(fever) "His face has fallen in, and the lips are cracked and black. There is no mark on him. It was the winter fever that took the last of three households in the march, and it took him in nine days, the way it takes the old." teaches lord_dead.
  Observe crypt_seizure at crypt as sign when death(seizure) "The mouth is drawn down on one side and the left hand is closed on nothing. He was struck at table, sitting up, and did not speak again." teaches lord_dead.
  Observe crypt_candles at crypt as sound when true "The candles gutter in a draught that has no source.".

  // ---- The deductions the company makes for itself, once it has the facts to make them with.
  Rule seals_matched when knows(party, seal_plain) and knows(party, seal_ears) and not knows(party, herald_false)
    says "The two seals do not agree: a plain crown on the herald's writ, a crown between two ears of wheat on the king's own. The court changed its seal at the coronation. The herald's paper was sealed before it, and he is carrying it as if it were new." teaches herald_false { }
  Rule hand_s when knows(party, letter_marks_steward) and knows(party, quirk_tally) and not knows(party, hand_steward)
    says "The bar through the sevens in the herald's letter is the steward's. It is his hand." teaches hand_steward { }
  Rule hand_m when knows(party, letter_marks_marshal) and knows(party, quirk_roll) and not knows(party, hand_marshal)
    says "The tens counted in fives and strokes in the herald's letter are the marshal's. It is his hand." teaches hand_marshal { }
  Rule hand_c when knows(party, letter_marks_clerk) and knows(party, quirk_index) and not knows(party, hand_clerk)
    says "The blots and the long-tailed d in the herald's letter are the clerk's. It is his hand." teaches hand_clerk { }

  // ---- The muster day: set when the company first comes in at the gate, never earlier than the twelfth day.
  Rule entering when within(party, hold) and not entered(house) { Assert entered(house). Set feastDay(house) to max(12, day(clock) + 2). }
  Rule feast_opens heard at hall when now(p_feast) and hour(clock) < 21 and not read_out(house) and not unmasked(house) and not dead(herald)
    says "The doors of the hall stand open, and the feast is laid: the long tables loaded, the high seat's cup filled, the herald placed at the castellan's right hand, where the lord's heir would sit. The household takes its seats in order of rank and watches the door." { }
  Rule herald_reads heard at hall when now(p_feast) and hour(clock) >= 21 and not read_out(house) and not unmasked(house) and not dead(herald)
    says "When the second cup is poured, the herald rises, unrolls his writ, and reads it. The hall listens as men listen to weather. When he has done, the castellan says that the lord is unwell, and the herald says that the king will be sorry to hear it, and the marshal puts down his knife." { Assert read_out(house). }
  Rule herald_poisoned heard at hall when dosed(house) and now(p_feast) and hour(clock) >= 21 and at(herald, hall) and not dead(herald)
    says "The herald lifts his cup to the castellan, drinks, and puts his hand to his throat. It is some moments before the hall understands what it is watching, and the marshal is on his feet before it has understood. By the time the chaplain has crossed the dais the herald is dead." { Slay herald. Assert poison_deed(house). }
  Rule proclaims heard at hall when now(p_feast) and hour(clock) >= 21 and not proclaimed(house) and (chaplain_ready(house) or castellan_ready(house))
    says "The chaplain stands with a folded vellum in her hand, and the castellan stands beside her. 'The lord of this keep died eleven days ago at his own table,' says the chaplain, 'and lies in the crypt, and his will names his ward, and I have not been able to say it until now.' Nobody speaks. The marshal takes off his cap." { Assert proclaimed(house). }

  // A feast is a feast: for its hours the door-ward lets the whole hall pass, strangers included.
  Rule doorward_feasts when now(p_feast) and not tolerates(doorward, party) { Assert tolerates(doorward, party). }
  // ---- The reckoning, at the feast's height. What the keep is after it, it stays.
  Relation decided(group). Relation aftermath(group).
  Rule reckoning heard at hall when day(clock) == feastDay(house) and hour(clock) >= 22 and not reckoned(house)
    says "At the feast's height the keep makes up its mind, as a household does: without a vote, and all at once." { Assert reckoned(house). }
  Rule reckon_herald_dead_castellan when reckoned(house) and not decided(house) and dead(castellan) and unmasked(house) { Assert decided(house). Assert state(banner, mutinous). }
  Rule reckon_castellan_dead when reckoned(house) and not decided(house) and dead(castellan) { Assert decided(house). Assert state(banner, usurped). }
  Rule reckon_regency when reckoned(house) and not decided(house) and unmasked(house) and proclaimed(house) and paid_off(house) { Assert decided(house). Assert state(banner, regency). }
  Rule reckon_mutiny_a when reckoned(house) and not decided(house) and unmasked(house) and proclaimed(house) and not paid_off(house) { Assert decided(house). Assert state(banner, mutinous). }
  Rule reckon_hushed when reckoned(house) and not decided(house) and unmasked(house) and paid_off(house) { Assert decided(house). Assert state(banner, hushed). }
  Rule reckon_mutiny_b when reckoned(house) and not decided(house) and unmasked(house) { Assert decided(house). Assert state(banner, mutinous). }
  Rule reckon_usurped when reckoned(house) and not decided(house) { Assert decided(house). Assert state(banner, usurped). }

  // ---- What the keep becomes. The people of it move; the gate keeps the company's memory; the weeks go on.
  Rule after_regency when decided(house) and state(banner, regency) and not aftermath(house)
    says "By morning the banner is at half its staff, and the chaplain has begun to toll the bell. The castellan signs her own name at the foot of the lord's last letter." {
    Assert aftermath(house).
  }
  Rule after_hushed when decided(house) and state(banner, hushed) and not aftermath(house)
    says "The herald is gone, and the household sits down to breakfast as if nothing had been said. The lord's cup is filled at the high seat, and cleared untouched." {
    Assert aftermath(house).
  }
  Rule after_usurped when decided(house) and state(banner, usurped) and not aftermath(house) and at(castellan, ?p)
    says "In the morning the keep's banner is down. A steward in the herald's master's livery has the castellan's keys, and the castellan is in her own solar with two men outside the door." {
    Assert aftermath(house). Assert occupied(castellan). Retract at(castellan, ?p). Assert at(castellan, solar). Assert at(patron_man, hall).
  }
  Rule after_mutinous when decided(house) and state(banner, mutinous) and not aftermath(house) and at(marshal, ?p) and at(castellan, ?q)
    says "By morning the garrison has the hall. The marshal sits in the lord's chair, and not one of the thirty-one will look at the castellan, who has been put in the oubliette with her own bar across it." {
    Assert aftermath(house). Assert occupied(marshal). Retract at(marshal, ?p). Assert at(marshal, hall).
    Assert occupied(castellan). Retract at(castellan, ?q). Assert at(castellan, oubliette).
  }
  Person patron_man "the new steward" nowhere {
    Role "a steward in the herald's master's colours". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Level 3. Peaceable. Manner stoic. Pronouns he.
    Greets "A hard-faced man in unfamiliar livery sits at the high table with the keep's keys in front of him. 'The keep is held for {patron},' he says, 'by the king's writ. Your business?'".
  }
  Person deserters "unpaid spearmen" nowhere {
    Role "men of the garrison who would not stay for the mutiny and have not been paid in three months". Ancestry human. Calling warrior. Numbers 3. Level 1. Temperament territorial.
    Warns "Three men in the keep's old colours stand across the road with their spears grounded. 'A toll,' says the one in front, and does not look as though he has said it before. 'For the king's roads.'".
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp(deserters) to 70.
  Person heir "the young heiress" nowhere {
    Role "a girl of fourteen in a travelling cloak, the lord's ward". Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Level 1. Peaceable. Manner cheerful. Pronouns she.
    Greets "A girl in a travelling cloak, whose hands are red with the cold, looks round the ward as if she had known it all her life and had been told it was smaller. 'I am {heir},' she says. 'Where is my uncle? They said the chaplain wrote.'".
  }
  Rule heir_arrives when state(banner, regency) and aftermath(house) and day(clock) >= feastDay(house) + 7 and not at(heir, ward) and not dead(castellan) says "A girl in a travelling cloak rides in at the gate on a borrowed pony, with a nun on a mule behind her." {
    Assert at(heir, ward).
  }

  // ---- The aims.
  Objective keep_rumoured when knows(party, levy_called) and not entered(house) toward outside "A crier in the castellan's colours has read a levy on the green. The keep it comes from is {outside}, in {land}, a day or so along the roads from here, and its lord has not been seen in eleven days.".
  Objective keep_lord when entered(house) and not knows(party, lord_dead) and not reckoned(house) toward chaplain "The lord is unseen, his cup is filled and cleared untouched, and the old dog howls toward the chapel. Find where he is.".
  Objective keep_writs when entered(house) and knows(party, lord_dead) and not knows(party, herald_false) and not reckoned(house) toward herald "The lord is dead, and a herald with a levy-writ has not been told. His seal is a plain crown; the king's, someone says, is not.".
  Objective keep_feast when entered(house) and not reckoned(house) toward hall "The feast is in the hall on the evening of the {feastDay(house)}th day. The household will all be there, and so will the herald.".
  Objective keep_prisoner when knows(party, captive_story) and not freed(captive) and not reckoned(house) toward undercroft "A man in the oubliette says he is the king's rider. The steward's key, the marshal's, or a strong back will lift the bar.".
  Objective keep_pay when knows(party, arrears) and not paid_off(house) and not reckoned(house) toward marshal "The garrison is owed eighty crowns. A garrison that has not been paid will not stand for anyone.".
  Objective keep_will when knows(party, heir_sought) and not knows(party, will_read) and not reckoned(house) toward clerk "The lord's will is in the muniment press in the chancery, and the clerk holds the key.".
  Objective keep_leaguer when knows(party, letter_marks_steward) or knows(party, letter_marks_marshal) or knows(party, letter_marks_clerk) toward chancery "Someone in the household wrote to the herald's master. The hand in the letter has a tell, and the keep's papers have the same tells.".
}

